    ["AOTMatchTip"]="War of Freedom Matchmaking",
    ["AOTMatchTip_02"]="Party not available in matchmaking. Please exit party and try again.",
    ["AOTMatchTip_03"]="Other Adventurers",
    ["AOTMatchTip_04"]="Lv. ???",
    ["AOTMatchTip_05"]="Not in matchmaking period. Cannot proceed with matchmaking.",
    ["AOTMatchTip_06"]="If you leave now, you will not be able to enter <color=#ff5d5d>War of Freedom</color> matchmaking in the next <color=#ff5d5d>%s</color>. Are you sure?",
    ["AOTMatchTip_07"]="As you left the previous War of Freedom battle early, you will not be able to enter <color=#ff5d5d>War of Freedom</color> matchmaking for <color=#ff5d5d>%s</color>.",
    ["AOTPVPTips_001"]="●Rules\n1. War of Freedom is available daily for 1 hour at 12:00 and 20:00 respectively. 6 Adventurers can activate the War of Freedom exercise. 5 Human players and 1 Titan player will be randomly distributed during the matchmaking phase.\n2. Humans achieve victory by slaying the Titan. The Titan will win if all Humans are devoured.\n3. The match lasts for up to 10 minutes. The match is a tie if both sides remain standing when time is up. If the Titan exits the match after a given period of time, the Humans win.\n●Human Gameplay\n1. Humans can’t deal damage to the Titan.\n2. When the Human's HP is reduced to 1, they enter the Fallen State and cannot use skills. They can be revived by other Humans.\n3. Upon maxing out the Fear, Humans will enter the Panic State. Their movement, skills, and revival are disabled. The Fear will gradually go down, and Humans can resume normal functions once the Fear reaches 0.\n4. Humans can acquire skill items from Armories that randomly spawn on the map, which can be used to obtain corresponding skills.\n5. There are 5 Alarm Bells and 2 Wall-mounted Cannons. The cannons will be available after 4 bells are activated.\n6. Humans can attack the Titan with Wall-mounted Cannons. Upon impact, the Titan will enter the Fallen State, and cannot move nor use skills.\n7. The Titan that is almost in a Fallen State can be executed via QTE. Humans can get the Titan executed and win if successfully performing all QTE. If not, the Human that performs it will fall into the Panic State.\n●Titan Gameplay\n1. Three different Titans with distinct Movement Speed and Skills are available in this event. Each can deal various damage to Humans and increase their Fear.\n2. Minion Titans will randomly spawn on the map to assist the Titan in hunting down Humans.\n3. When the Human accumulates enough Fear, the Titan can close in and devour the Human. Devour all Humans to achieve victory.\n4. The Titan can attack Humans who operate Alarm Bells and Wall-mounted Cannons. When knocked down by the attacks from these cannons, the Titan will recover in a period.\n5. The Titan cannot pass some of the narrow terrain. Accordingly, some obstacles that Humans cannot pass can be passed by the Titan.\n●Rewards\n1. By the end of the match, all players receive Memory Fragments to unlock exclusive character incidents. The winning side receives 5 Battle Secret Notes and has a slight chance to receive Advanced Battle Secret Note. A draw or a failure grants players 2 Battle Secret Notes which can be exchanged for exclusive rewards in the Event Store.\n2. Players can obtain no more than 60 Battle Secret Notes and 2 Memory Fragments from the War of Freedom daily.",
