    ["AccessDesc_Title_1608"]="Obtained from the external event.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_1"]="The supreme rulers, the royal family of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom.\nTheir ancestor Tristan I led six other adventurers on an attack on the giant serpent Jormungandr.\nHe put an end to the Age of Gods, bringing salvation to the continent.\nHe established the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom, and was crowned its first King.\nHe founded the capital at the plains where Jormungandr fell, naming it Prontera.\nThe Gaebolg Family ruled over the other six adventurers' families,\nand they were collectively known to the world as the seven royal families.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_10"]="The ancient magical family that holds all of the political power in Geffen.\nWith their close relations with the Wizard Guild, their family has produced many talented Wizards.\nThey place emphasis on aptitude when choosing their patriarch,\nand one of their former patriarchs was even one of the few existing Great Sages in the world!\nWith their profound knowledge and excellent performance in subduing the rivals of blood in the past, \nthe Heines have the utmost trust of the royal family.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_11"]="The family that has taken charge of the Kingdom Defense Force since the founding of the country.\nApart from Gaebolg, they are the royal family with the largest influence.\nTheir family philosophy is that the kingdom always comes first.\nThey are overtly calm and apathetic when dealing with problems.\nThis alienated and distanced the Richard family from the other royal families\nand caused the royals to be wary of them.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_12"]="A family of chivalry,\nevery generation of their patriarch has come from the Royal Chivalry.\nThe Walter family has always had respectful manners and been of virtuous character.\nThey are well respected amongst the Prontera knights.\nTheir commitment to courtesy is even near perfect,\nwinning the praise and respect of the royal family.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_13"]="A fighting clan with supreme combat prowess.\nAfter Morroc merged into the Rune Kingdom, he actively moved to relocate his whole clan here.\nMorroc attempted to manage the chaos by ruling with an iron fist.\nEven though there may be anti-war dissidents in the clan occasionally,\nthey aren't able to change the deeply rooted reverence towards martial strength.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_14"]="The royal family has been merchants for generations,\nand they chose Alberta, the port city most suitable for foreign trade, as their home base.\nWith control of Libra and Serpentrod, the two major merchants groups, they are prominent across the seas.\nHowever, due to their love of freedom and the sea...\nor perhaps it is their love for riches,\nthey have yet to show any political ambition towards the throne.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_15"]="The hedonistic family based in Comodo.\nDue to their ancestor being a dancer, the clan has a rare matriarchal system.\nThey would rather exchange their rights of nobility for complete autonomy in a corner of the continent.\nThey have no interest in politics and are only passionate about the beautiful arts.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_2"]="The ancient magical family that holds all of the political power in Geffen.\nWith their close relations with the Wizard Guild, their family has produced many talented Wizards.\nThey place emphasis on aptitude when choosing their patriarch,\nand one of their former patriarchs was even one of the few existing Great Sages in the world!\nWith their profound knowledge and excellent performance in subduing the blood races in the past,\nthe Heines have the utmost trust of the royal family.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_3"]="The family that has taken charge of the Kingdom Defense Force since the founding of the country.\nApart from Gaebolg, they are the royal family with the largest influence.\nTheir family philosophy is that the kingdom always comes first.\nThey are overtly calm and apathetic when dealing with problems.\nThis alienated and distanced the Richard family from the other royal families\nand caused the royals to be wary of them.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_4"]="A family of chivalry,\nevery generation of their patriarch has come from the Royal Chivalry.\nThe Walter family has always had respectful manners and been of virtuous character.\nThey are well respected amongst the Prontera knights.\nTheir commitment to courtesy is even near perfect,\nwinning the praise and respect of the royal family.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_5"]="A fighting clan with supreme combat prowess.\nAfter Morroc merged into the Rune Kingdom, he actively moved to relocate his whole clan here.\nMorroc attempted to manage the chaos by ruling with an iron fist.\nEven though there may be anti-war dissidents in the clan occasionally,\nthey aren't able to change the deeply rooted reverence towards martial strength.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_6"]="The royal family has been merchants for generations,\nand they chose Alberta, the port city most suitable for foreign trade, as their home base.\nWith control of Libra and Serpentrod, the two major merchants groups, they are prominent across the seas.\nHowever, due to their love of freedom and the sea...\nor perhaps it is their love for riches,\nthey have yet to show any political ambition towards the throne.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_7"]="The hedonistic family based in Comodo.\nDue to their ancestor being a dancer, the clan has a rare matriarchal system.\nThey would rather exchange their rights of nobility for complete autonomy in a corner of the continent.\nThey have no interest in politics and are only passionate about the beautiful arts.",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_8"]="Day %s",
    ["AccumulativeLogin_9"]="The supreme rulers, the royal family of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom.\nTheir ancestor Tristan I led six other adventurers on an attack on the giant serpent Jormungandr.\nHe put an end to the Age of Gods, bringing salvation to the continent.\nHe established the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom, and was crowned its first King.\nHe declared the capital at the plains where Jormungandr fell, naming it Prontera.\nThe Gaebolg Family ruled over the other six adventurers' families,\nand they were collectively known to the world as the seven royal families.",
