    ["ActivityRule_100001"]="Mission Board\n\n1. Adventurers who have reached Adventurer Lv.22 can accept quests at the Mission Board in various main cities.\n2. Adventurers can obtain a small amount of Base EXP, Job EXP, and Zeny upon completing Mission Board Quests.\n3. Mission Board Quests are refreshed at 05:00 (UTC+7) daily. Adventurers can complete up to 10 Mission Board Quests daily.",
    ["ActivityRule_100004"]="OX Quiz Rules\n\n1. Adventurers at Adventurer Lv.20 or higher can participate in the OX Quiz event once daily.\n2. OX Quiz is available three times daily at 11:00 - 13:00, 17:30 - 20:00, and 21:00 - 23:00 (UTC+7).\n3. Each OX Quiz has 12 questions. Adventurers answering at least 3 questions correctly can obtain a Quiz Gift Pack. The more questions answered correctly, the better the rewards.\n4. After the question is revealed, move to the area of your chosen answer. The system will verify and announce the correct answer after locking the areas.\n5. Adventurers who answered correctly can continue the quiz, while Adventurers who answered incorrectly are moved to join the audience. The audience can select answers to help the Adventurers still in the quiz.",
    ["ActivityRule_100005"]="Daily Instance\n\n1. Daily Instance will be available after completing Main Story Quests and unlocking Fragment of Ymir's Heart.\n2. The Instance has two levels of difficulty: Normal and Hard. Adventurers can form parties of up to 5 Adventurers to challenge the Daily Instance.\n3. Defeat the boss to obtain instance exclusive equipment, cards, equipment materials, and other rewards. An overall rating will be given based on each Adventurer's damage dealt, healing, and damage taken. The Adventurer with the highest rating is the MVP.\n4. Daily Instance reward chances refresh at 05:00 (UTC+7) daily. Adventurers can obtain instance rewards up to 3 times daily.\n5. There is a wide variety of instance rewards available, with lots of EXP, Zeny, equipment, and rare materials up for grabs.\n\nBonus Rewards\n1. Adventurers who are 30 levels or more below the World Level can trigger an exclusive bonus.\n2. Party up with bonus Adventurers, and every time the bonus Adventurer uses 1 Instance reward chance, non-bonus Adventurers get rewards.\n3. Party up with bonus Adventurers, and every time the bonus Adventurer uses 1 MVP / MINI reward chance, non-bonus Adventurers get rewards.\n4. Party up with bonus Adventurers, and every time the bonus Adventurer uses 500 Odin's Blessings, nearby non-bonus Adventurers get rewards.\n5. Exclusive Odin EXP Multiplier\n10x for Lv.1-49 Adventurers\n9x for Lv.50-69 Adventurers\n8x for Lv.70-89 Adventurers\n7x for Lv.90-99 Adventurers\n6x for Lv.100-160",
    ["ActivityRule_100006"]="COC Mission\n\n1. Adventurers who have reached Adventurer Lv.25 can accept COC Missions from Chamber of Commerce Workers in various main cities.\n2. Adventurers can only select one out of the three merchant groups—Cool Event Corporation, Kafra Corporation, and Cat Hand Corporation—and complete the corresponding quest each time.\n3. Adventurers can obtain a small amount of Base EXP, Job EXP, Zeny, and Coins from the corresponding merchant groups upon completing COC Missions.\n4. Coins can be used at Prontera's Vending Machine to draw for gacha.\n5. The number of COC Mission attempts refreshes at 05:00 every Monday. One COC Mission attempt is added at 05:00 (UTC+7) daily, and can accumulate up to 7 attempts.",
    ["ActivityRule_100009"]="Guild Order Rules\n\nEligibility:\nOnly guild members can participate.\n\nOrder Submission:\n1. Guild Order resets at 05:00 (UTC+7) daily. For each reset, there are 8 Common Orders that will be refreshed for players, each corresponding to different materials. Submit the specified amount of materials to obtain Guild Contribution, Guild Pass EXP, and Guild Funds.\n2. Completing 8 Common Orders will allow you to spend crystals to refresh 8 Advanced Orders each time. After refreshing Advanced Orders 4 times, the Super Order feature will be unlocked. Super Orders will need 10 times the goods and grant 10 times the rewards of usual Advanced Orders.\n3. Guild Contribution can be used for Guild Blessings and in the Guild Store. Guild Funds are used for upgrading the guild.\n4. When Guild Level reaches Lv.2, submissions of orders additionally grant Otherworld Energy, for use in activating the Otherworld Gate event.\n5. The order submission limit and the types of orders refresh at 05:00 (UTC+7) daily.\n\nGuild Leaving Measures:\nAfter leaving and joining a new guild, orders can only be submitted after the 05:00 (UTC+7) refresh on the second day.",
    ["ActivityRule_100010"]="Endless Tower\n\n1. Adventurers who have reached Adventurer Lv.35 can enter the Endless Tower. Entering consumes 1 Tower Key.\n2. Adventurers can form parties of up to 5 Adventurers to challenge the Endless Tower.\n3. Upon entering the Endless Tower, Adventurers will be affected by Deviling's Curse, and they will have reduced regen abilities and be unable to use normal Regeneration Potion, Yggdrasil Berry, Seed of Yggdrasil, and Panacea\n4. A resting floor will appear every 20 floors. On a rest floor, there will be a fountain regenerating HP, a mysterious merchant to exchange blessings from, and a merchant selling consumables. Adventurers entering the Endless Tower again within the week can enter from the highest resting floor reached.\n5. Adventurers can obtain Tower Stones in the tower. Tower Stones can be exchanged for blessing buffs from the Mysterious Endless Merchant on a resting floor.\n6. Soul of God Portals will randomly appear after Adventurers defeat bosses. Adventurers can choose which portal they want to enter. Completing the battle within the portal will give Adventurers the corresponding Soul of God item.\n7. Adventurers can select one Blessing of God after completing certain floors. Only one of each type of blessing can be active at any time. Selecting blessings of the same type will upgrade the blessing effect of that type.\n8. There is a Soul Exchange right outside the Endless Tower. Adventurers can exchange for other items using soul items obtained from the tower.\n9. The Endless Tower resets at 5:00 (UTC+7) every Monday, when Adventurers will be moved to a designated resting floor. Adventurers can claim rewards from chests after reaching the next resting floor.",
    ["ActivityRule_100014"]="Free Arena\n\nAvailable Time:\nAll Day\n\nFree Arena Rules:\n1. Exclusive area for PVP. No restrictions on fights. Adventurers may participate individually or as a party.\n2. Normal potions and items cannot be used in the Free Arena. Only PVP exclusive potions and items can be used.\n3. Auto Medicine is prohibited in the Free Arena. Please use potions to recover manually.\n4. When players are killed, they will be revived in the preparation room after 10 seconds.\n\nRoom Creation Rules:\n1. Players can create rooms themselves and enjoy a private Training Course.\n2. Room conditions for individual rooms can be customized according to player needs.\n3. The rules for individual rooms and the public arena are the same.\n4. A room exists for 30 minutes, by the end of which the room will be removed.\n5. If there are no players in the room during that period, the room will be removed.\n\nMode Rules:\n1. Players can choose to enter the Free Arena in either Participate mode or Spectate mode.\n2. In the Participate mode, players can battle freely.\n3. In the Spectate mode, players cannot battle and are invisible to others.",
    ["ActivityRule_100015"]="Infinite Showdown\n\nIt's recommended not to engage in events in a party of 6 other than Infinite Showdown.\nFor other events, relevant effects won't be applied to the 6th member.\n\nAvailable Time:\nAll Day\n\nInfinite Showdown Rules:\n1. Solo or Party participation is allowed.\n2. Modes and maps are randomized.\n3. Upon a successful matching, you can ban a mode. Banned mode will have a reduced chance of being selected.\n4. Each map comes with its own set of unique mechanisms.\n5. Fulfill the winning conditions of each mode to secure a victory.\n\n\nRoom Creation Rules:\n1. Adventurers can create rooms and choose party members and opponents.\n2. Room rules are the same as those of Infinite Showdown.\n3. Adventurers can only invite their friends to the room or use the Shoutout feature to notice other Adventurers; matchmaking is disabled in the room. The match only starts when the room has enough players.\n\nMode Rules:\n1. Adventurers can choose from 2 vs 2, 3 vs 3, or 6 vs 6.\n\n\nFree Arena\n\nAvailable Time:\nAll Day\n\nFree Arena Rules:\n1. Exclusive area for PVP. No restrictions on fights. Adventurers may participate individually or as a party.\n2. Normal potions and items cannot be used in the Free Arena. Only PVP-exclusive potions and items can be used.\n3. Auto Medicine is prohibited in the Free Arena. Please use potions to recover manually.\n4. When Adventurers are killed, they will be revived in the preparation room after 10 seconds.\n\nRoom Creation Rules:\n1. Adventurers can create rooms themselves and enjoy a private Training Course.\n2. Room conditions for individual rooms can be customized according to the Adventurer's needs.\n3. The rules for individual rooms and the public arena are the same.\n4. A room exists for 30 minutes, by the end of which the room will be removed.\n5. If there are no Adventurers in the room during that period, the room will be removed.\n\nMode Rules:\n1. Adventurers can choose to enter the Free Arena via Participate Mode or Spectate Mode.\n2. Under Participate Mode, Adventurers can battle freely.\n3. Under Spectate Mode, Adventurers cannot battle and are invisible to others.",
    ["ActivityRule_100030"]="Trial Illusion\n\nEntry Requirements:\n1. Adventurers can enter the Trial Illusion after completing the tutorial quest: The Prophesized Hero. A corresponding Realm Key is required.\n2. Each time the Illusion Trial is cleared, a Realm Key will be consumed. Every Monday at 05:00 (UTC+7), the Illusion Keys obtained last week will be destroyed.\n3. Visit the Exchange Shop at the Geffen Library with librarian Winry to purchase or exchange for Realm Keys and other Illusion Trial related items.\n4. Adventurers can form a party to challenge the Trial Illusion. The team will be divided into 3 parties, with a maximum of 5 people per party.\n5. There's a crystal ball at the entrance to the Trial Illusion for summoning party members. However, it won't work in instances or special scenes.\n6. New party members joining the Trial Illusion during a run will automatically sync with the existing instance progress.\n\nReward Rules:\n1. Individual Reward: Obtained by clearing the Illusion Trial.\n2. Party Reward: Adventurers can tap the items they need in the Ornate Chest dropped by the boss and roll the dice. Adventurers with the highest number of dice in the party will get the item. The rewards of each chest differ and can only be shared by the party members.\n3. Team Reward: After clearing the Illusion Trial, there is a chance that the Black Market Merchant will appear and issue rewards. The rewards will be unlocked by using the Realm Voucher, and the rewards will be assigned according to the number of the Realm Vouchers given. Adventurers who do not get the rewards will reclaim the Realm Vouchers given by them previously.\n4. Reward chances in the Trial Illusion reset every Monday at 05:00 (UTC+7). Adventurers can earn up to 1 Individual Reward, 2 Party Rewards, and 1 Team Reward per week.\n\nBattle Rules:\n1. When fewer than 15 Adventurers enter the Illusion Trial, the attributes and stats of the monsters will be increased. The fewer Adventurers enter the Illusion, the stronger the monsters will be!\n2. The Adventurer's attack and defense abilities will be adjusted according to the Trial Illusion's standard level.\n3. Adventurers cannot resurrect instantly after dying in combat. They must wait until the entire party is wiped for the resurrection button to light up.\n4. Adventurers who die more than 2 times will face restricted resurrection, preventing them from resurrecting by using skills or items. The restriction resets after the resurrection.\n5. Using the skill Play Dead is not allowed in the Trial Illusion.",
    ["ActivityRule_100034"]="Trial Illusion\n\nRules:\n1. Entrance: You can challenge the instance directly via the Carnival entrance.\n2. Difficulty: The Trial Illusion is divided into 3 stages per chapter, with 4 difficulty options: Normal, Hard, Nightmare, and Master.\n3. Unlock Conditions: To unlock Normal, Hard, and Nightmare difficulties, specific conditions must be met, which reset every Monday at 05:00. Master difficulty is available for a limited time and allows for repeated attempts during the period.\n4. Party Size: Adventurers can form a party to challenge the Trial Illusion. Up to 5 participants can enter Normal, Hard, and Nightmare difficulties, and up to 10 participants can enter Master difficulty.\n5. Trial Illusion Exchange Shop: Visit the Exchange Shop at the Geffen Library with librarian Winry to exchange items.\n6. Master Leaderboard: Master difficulty instances come with their own rankings, ranking Adventurers by score. Each chapter also features overall rankings, summing up scores across all Master stages within the chapter.\n7. New Raid: Raid access requires reaching a certain world level and waiting 60 days after the previous raid leaderboard concludes. After fulfilling both requirements, the new raid will open at 5:00 AM on Monday.\n\nReward Rules:\n1. Individual Reward: Adventurers will get rewards every time they clear the Trial Illusion in Normal, Hard, or Nightmare difficulties.\n2. Party Reward: Upon clearing the Trial Illusion in Normal, Hard, or Nightmare difficulties, a Black Market Merchant may appear by chance, offering rewards that need to be unlocked with the Realm Voucher. The more Realm Vouchers Adventurers offer, the higher the chance of unlocking the rewards. Adventurers who do not receive the reward will get back all the Realm Vouchers offered by them without consuming reward chances.\n3. Reward Chance: Reward chances in the Trial Illusion reset every Monday at 05:00 (UTC+7). Adventurers can earn up to 2 Individual Rewards and 2 Party Rewards per week, with any leftover chances only carrying over for one week.\n4. Leaderboard Reward: In the Master difficulty of the Trail Illusion, corresponding rewards are given out to those with higher rankings. These rewards are sent via mail after the Master Challenge concludes.\n\nBattle Rules:\n1. Entering the Trial Illusion with fewer than the required number of Adventurers increases the monster's stat. The fewer the Adventurers, the stronger the monsters become.\n2. The Adventurer's attack and defense abilities will be adjusted according to the Trial Illusion's standard level.\n3. In Normal, Hard, and Nightmare difficulty instances within the Trial Illusion, Adventurers cannot resurrect instantly after dying in combat. They must wait until the entire party is wiped for the resurrection button to light up. In Master difficulty, Adventurers will be automatically resurrected with a temporary invincibility after the countdown ends.\n4. In Normal, Hard, and Nightmare difficulty instances within the Trial Illusion, Adventurers who die more than 8/4/2 times will face restricted resurrection, preventing them from resurrecting by using skills or items. The chances reset after the resurrection. In Master difficulty, the restriction occurs after 10 deaths, preventing resurrection by skills or items.\n5. Berserk: The berserk duration in stage 1/2/3 are 300/480/600 seconds, respectively.\n6. Using the skill Play Dead is not allowed in the Trial Illusion.\n\nLeaderboard Record Attempt Description\n1. While the leaderboard is active, Adventurers have ten attempts to record their Master Challenge's clearing scores on the leaderboard per week.\n2. If all party members have remaining leaderboard record attempts, an attempt is used automatically upon entering the Master Challenge, and the score is recorded after completing the Master Challenge.\n3. If any party member runs out of leaderboard record attempts, the score won't be recorded, and no rewards are given. In this case, it won't consume the other party members' leader record attempts.\n4. If a party member quits the Master Challenge midway and the remaining party members still complete the Master Challenge, the quitter's score won't be recorded, and their leaderboard record attempt won't be refunded.\n5. If a record attempt is used in a party, the party will become a fixed party and stay that way as long as no members change. Any member leaving, joining, or the party disbanding will render the status invalid.\n6. Entering the Master Challenge with a fixed party does not consume leaderboard record attempts, and the score still counts toward the leaderboard.\n7. Solo Adventurers cannot trigger the fixed party effect.",
    ["ActivityRule_100035"]="Challenge Time\n1. Every day from 01:00 to 05:00 (UTC+7) is the break period; Oblivion Realm is inaccessible during this time.\nUnlock Description\n1. Reach 3 stars to unlock the next difficulty.\n2. When partying up, the leader's difficulty unlocking progress is shared across the party.\n3. If a party earns a 3-star rating in a cross-difficulty challenge, all members will unlock all difficulties that were locked previously.\nReward Details\n1. Rewards can be claimed once per week at most.\n2. Upon Oblivion Realm settlement, you may either claim the reward or skip it. Skipping a reward doesn't consume your chance of claiming rewards.\n3. The reward tier is determined by the total stars earned from each floor of the challenge.\n4. The rating is determined by the party's clear time and death count.\n5. All premium rewards are dropped by chance, with higher difficulties offering better odds.\nFloor Rating Standards Description\n- 1 Star: Clear the stage in no more than 300 seconds.\n- 2 Stars: Clear the stage in no more than 180 seconds.\n- 3 Stars: Clear the stage in no more than 180 seconds and also fulfill:\nDifficulty 1-3: No more than 10 deaths.\nDifficulty 4-7: No more than 6 deaths.\nDifficulty 8-10: No more than 3 deaths.\nLeaderboard Record Attempt Description\n1. Each week, Adventurers have five attempts to record their Oblivion Realm's clearing scores on the leaderboard.\n2. If all party members have remaining leaderboard record attempts, an attempt is used automatically upon entering Oblivion Realm, and the score is recorded after defeating any boss of any floor.\n3. If any party member runs out of leaderboard record attempts, the score won't be recorded, and no rewards are given. In this case, it won't consume the other party members' leader record attempts.\n4. If a party member quits Oblivion Realm midway and the remaining party members defeat any boss of any floor, the quitter's score won't be recorded, and their leaderboard record attempt won't be refunded.\n5. If a record attempt is used in a party, the party will become a fixed party and stay that way as long as no members change. Any member leaving, joining, or the party disbanding will render the status invalid.\n6. Entering Oblivion Realm with a fixed party does not consume leaderboard record attempts.\n7. Solo Adventurers cannot trigger the fixed party effect.\nReset Description\n1. The leaderboard resets every Monday during the Oblivion Realm period, retaining the unlocked difficulty progress.\n2. Upon reset, all leaderboard ranking records and record attempts are reset, and rewards are distributed based on the rankings.\n3. Upon reset, all boss affixes across difficulties will be randomized.",
