    ["CollegeText_016"]="End Relationship",
    ["CollegeText_017"]="Terminate the mentorship relationship between yourself and <color=#7ACEFF>%s</color>? (After terminating a relationship you cannot establish another for 24 hours)",
    ["CollegeText_018"]="Confirm",
    ["CollegeText_019"]="Cancel",
    ["CollegeText_020"]="You can establish a relationship with someone in <color=#7ACEFF>%s</color>.",
    ["CollegeText_021"]="You don't currently have a master.",
    ["CollegeText_022"]="You don't currently have a student.",
    ["CollegeText_023"]="There are currently no players who meet the requirements.",
    ["CollegeText_024"]="Taught a total of <color=#7ACEFF>%s</color> adventurers to date.",
    ["CollegeText_025"]="Students can choose to graduate once they've completed all of the Study Level challenges. They will receive rewards corresponding to the number of Mentorship Points that they earned during the study period. The specific rewards are as follows:\n3000——3499 Reward = 1500 Academy Points\n3500——3999 Reward = 1750 Academy Points\n4000——4499 Reward = 2000 Academy Points\n4500——4999 Reward = 2250 Academy Points\n5000——5500 Reward = 2500 Academy Points\nYou can't claim this after graduation, so please think carefully, Adventurer!",
    ["CollegeText_026"]="[Messages]\nYou can view info on Instructors and Students on the information tab. Instructor players can set students as \"Star Pupils\" on this tab. Players who become Star Pupils gain a buff. Instructors can only change their Star Pupil once per day.\n[Quests]\nStudents and Instructors can complete quests on this to obtain Academy Points and Mentorship Point Rewards. Student players have three quests refreshed each day. After completion, they can increase their Mentorship Points, which determine the rewards they get when they graduate. Instructors can improve their Instructor Grade by completing quests and obtain Titles, Decorations, Academy Points and other rewards.\n[Store]\nStore goods will be different depending on players Academy identity. Goods are divided into permanent and rotated goods. Permanent goods have a purchase limit, while rotating goods type and quantity will refresh each day. Players can also refresh manually by spending Academy Points.\n[Rank]\nYou can view outstanding Instructors here by viewing the rankings based on player Influence. The Influence rankings will be locked from 5:00 a.m. on the second-to-last day of each month to 5:00 a.m. on the first day of the following month, and rewards will be issued to players according to their rankings via mail at 5:00 a.m. on the first day of the following month. Instructors are required to ensure their teaching efficiency and need to instruct at least one Student to graduate each month, otherwise they will be considered inactive Instructors and their Influence will be reduced for that month. On top of that, each additional Student (maximum of 4) Instructors guide to graduation will give them certain bonus in Influence for the month. Increases and decreases in Influence can be stacked until the player’s active status changes.\n[Recruitment]\nYou can find the right Instructor or Student here by setting the search criteria.\n[Study Network]\nCheck your Instructor or Student info, and make friends with more Adventurers.",
