    ["DemonSlayer_title"]="Event Overview",
    ["DepositInBinding"]="This equipment will become bound once it is deposited. Are you sure you want to deposit it?",
    ["DepositInSuccess"]="Successfully deposited.",
    ["Des"]="Description",
    ["Des_kvm"]="<color=#97BCF8>Kafra Plus:</color>\nDear Adventurer, your points will not be deducted for the first 3 KVM matches if you lose.\nAttempts reset at 05:00 daily.",
    ["DialogOption60205011"]="Not at all!",
    ["DialogOption60205012"]="I'm a professional!",
    ["Dialog_Tips_1"]="Request",
    ["DialoggueOption60201031"]="(Greet)",
    ["DialoggueOption60204011"]="Seven adventurers...",
    ["Dialogue100001"]="...Test NPC Dialog 11111",
    ["Dialogue10000101"]="Replace Quest Dialog 1",
    ["Dialogue10000102"]="Replace Quest Dialog 2",
    ["Dialogue1000101"]="Your confused look reminds me of myself in the past! Don't worry! I'll get you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1000102"]="Hey, it doesn't help to be so careless! Criatura Academy is <color=#CA2E0AFF>the best novice academy in the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom</color>. It's located on Izlude Island, and even members from the seven royal families secretly train there! Remember that now!",
    ["Dialogue1000103"]="I'm Kiki and I'm in charge of recruiting new students for the academy. It makes me blush to say this, but...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>every batch of freshmen says I'm the nicest and cutest of all the recruiters.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1000104"]="New students reporting to Criatura Academy have to first proceed with their <color=#CA2E0AFF>Novice Registration</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1000201"]="Registration complete! All your information has been recorded! Do you know what that means?",
    ["Dialogue1000202"]="Not yet! You'll have to pass a few tri... <size=24>*coughs*</size>\nWhat I meant was you can now collect your very own <color=#CA2E0AFF>Student Handbook</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1000203"]="Wha... <size=24>Huh?</size><size=24> I wasn't looking at you!</size>\nThis is just part of the process where novices collect their <color=#CA2E0AFF>Student Handbook</color>! I'll... I'll leave you here if you continue to blabber nonsense!",
    ["Dialogue1000204"]="Place your hand on this book next to me to collect your very own <color=#CA2E0AFF>Student Handbook</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1000301"]="Hehe, did you get a shock? The \"Criatura Academy Adventurer Log\" is a complex book. It encompasses all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>experiences and knowledge of countless academy students</color>, and it will be your most trusted partner on your adventure! But this information won't be readily available to you! After all, we're adventurers, and it's only through hardship and training that we're able to fully comprehend its content.",
    ["Dialogue1000302"]="Keep this handbook safe! From now on, all your experiences will be reflected inside. I've also heard that adventurers who are good at exploring will get <color=#CA2E0AFF>special bonuses</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1000401"]="So, what do you think of Prontera? Unlike Izlude Island where I grew up, Prontera is a true blue capital!",
    ["Dialogue1000402"]="Of course! Look at that gorgeous castle, the majestic statues, and this stunning fountain. How I wish I could visit them all the time. But alas, I have to leave soon.",
    ["Dialogue1000403"]="This is... <size=24>Huh?</size>\nDo you want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a photo with me in front of the fountain</color>?! That's a great idea! I'll have a reminder of it wherever I go! I'll wait for you in front of the fountain! Hurry up!\n\n",
    ["Dialogue1000501"]="Thank you so much! I promise to keep this photo safe! You took such a nice photo! I'm gonna show it to Jarod—",
    ["Dialogue1000502"]="<size=24>Wait a minute! </size><size=24>Where is Jarod?!</size>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Come to think of it, I haven't seen him for a while.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1000503"]="The academy appointed him as the Novice Instructor. He's slightly more qualified than me, but he's sooo lazy! Look! He snuck away while no one was looking again! He still has work to do!",
    ["Dialogue1000504"]="Really? This is kind of embarrassing, but I'm really busy right now. Jarod should be in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> in Prontera. Can you bring him back? Pretty please? <size=24>Pretty please with a cherry on top?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1000601"]="Huh? Why are you blocking my view? Move it. Can't you see I'm watching the performance?",
    ["Dialogue1000602"]="<size=24>Kiki?</size> Oops, the wind is too strong, I can't hear you clearly! Don't be so serious; the tavern is a place for relaxing. See that <color=#CA2E0AFF>record player</color> over there? Go put on a nice record, then we'll sit down and have a nice long chat!",
    ["Dialogue1000701"]="<size=18>Hmm, not bad at all! The Obeaune girls' backs are a lovely view...</size>\nErm, I mean your taste isn't bad at all!",
    ["Dialogue1000702"]="Now that there's beautiful music, it's time to show you what I do best! <color=#CA2E0AFF>The tavern is a wonderful place to socialize</color>, but first you'll need some socializing skills! Do you see Isabella behind the bar? There aren't many ladies as beautiful as her. In the next 10 seconds, I'll teach you how to develop a close relationship with her!",
    ["Dialogue1000801"]="Leave me alone, I need some peace and quiet.\n<size=18>Don't bother me, let me lay this short-lived romance to rest.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1000802"]="Huh? It's only hard for you! I bet you'll never <color=#CA2E0AFF>make a new friend</color> before me! You look like a goody two shoes.\n<size=24>And no one likes a goody two shoes!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1000803"]="Huh? How dare you doubt my charm! I bet you'll never <color=#CA2E0AFF>make a new friend</color> before me! You look like a goody two shoes.\n<size=24>And no one likes a goody two shoes!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1000804"]="I'll do whatever you say without question! That's the bet!",
    ["Dialogue1000901"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmph! Not even Jurgen Wigner can win someone's heart in just a few minutes; </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>what makes you think you can?</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> It's absolutely impossib—</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1000902"]="You made a <size=26>what?!</size>\nBy Odin! This is unimaginable! Have people's tastes changed? Have I been away from Prontera for too long?",
    ["Dialogue1000903"]="Fine, I get it! I'll go back with you, alright?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Looking at the time, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better be getting back anyway.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1000904"]="Hey, don't youngsters know how to respect their elders any more? Let's get back to Kiki!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Looking at the time, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better be getting back anyway.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1000905"]="Hey, don't say I'm mean to newbies. I've cast a <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic spell that increases the movement speed</color> for you to catch up with me. We must <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet Kiki</color> before the night falls. Don't slow me down, alright?",
    ["Dialogue1001001"]="You're so slow! It's getting late. If we don't set off now, we're going to miss the ship! The other novices are already headed for the port. Let's hurry!",
    ["Dialogue1001002"]="(Kiki looks worried)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But there's another student...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1001003"]="Erm, there's a girl called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ygnizem</color> who also registered today, but I wasn't able to notify her. I looked all over Prontera, but I couldn't find her. She'll be so upset if she misses out.",
    ["Dialogue1001004"]="You're right! She might have already gotten the news from someone else. That's definitely possible! Well then, let's hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>! Who knows, we might even see her along the way!",
    ["Dialogue1001101"]="Look at you! All tired out after just one battle. How are you going to become an adventurer at this rate? Looks like I'll just have to teach you another technique to help you survive. This skill is called \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Quick Heal</color>\"; it will help you out when you're in a pinch!",
    ["Dialogue1001201"]="Hey, don't look at me like that. I'm not going to praise you. I'm not Kiki! Oh right, the King Poring that ran away mentioned something about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Angeling's Halo</color>. What's up with that? Go ask... whatshername... Ygnazem, right?",
    ["Dialogue1001301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Porings look so soft on the outside. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Who knew they could pack such a punch when they're angry! Wait, no. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>As a future swordsman, how can I be intimidated by something so trivial? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Pull yourself together, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ygnizem!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1001302"]="Ah, sorry, I didn't notice you there. Oh right, thank you for your help! Thanks to you, I managed to escape.",
    ["Dialogue1001303"]="What happened? Just talking about it makes me mad! Those Porings... They just don't listen! I was training in the forest when I saw something shiny in the undergrowth. I went to pick it up and realized it was a halo!",
    ["Dialogue1001304"]="But before I could figure out what was happening, a group of Porings starting charging toward me! You know what happened next. I'm still really mad about it, but I threw the halo in a fit of rage... I should find it and return it to Angeling!",
    ["Dialogue1001305"]="I know I might miss the ship to the academy if I don't get to the port soon, but how can I call myself an adventurer if I don't right my wrongs?",
    ["Dialogue1001306"]="<size=24>Really?!</size>\nYou're really going to help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the halo</color>? Wow! There aren't many people as dedicated as you!",
    ["Dialogue1001401"]="Hey, hang on a second! There's not much time left; are you really going to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help her find Angeling's Halo</color> before going to the port?",
    ["Dialogue1001402"]="<size=18>I guess there's no talking you out of it.</size>\nFine, Kiki and I will head to the Amusement Park for supplies. But remember, there's not much time, so if you two aren't there by sundown, then...",
    ["Dialogue1001501"]="It's <size=24>Angeling's Halo!</size>\nYou found it at the top of the cliff? That's great, we can clear up the misunderstanding with the Porings now! But...",
    ["Dialogue1001502"]="But I need your help with something else. Can you help me bring the halo back to Angeling? It can be found near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poring Ruins</color>. I didn't mean to, but I still lost something important to it!",
    ["Dialogue1001503"]="(Ygnizem starts to blush.)\n<size=18>When I think about meeting Angeling in person, </size><size=18>I get really nervous.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1001504"]="You'll do it?! That's great! I'm definitely not wrong about you being a great teammate! I'll head off first and wait for you at the Amusement Park!",
    ["Dialogue1001601"]="<size=24>Halo! Por!</size>\nThis shiny halo was gifted to Angeling by the valkyries, por! Thank you, kind adventurer, por! Angeling is shining again, por! As a celebration, would you like to dance with me, por?",
    ["Dialogue1001602"]="You're in a rush to get back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amusement Park</color>, por? It's really far though... Ah! Angeling has an idea! Angeling can lend you its <color=#CA2E0AFF>mount</color>! You'll be able to get there in no time, por!",
    ["Dialogue1001701"]="Ygnizem told me about the situation. Good job! I have a piece of good news for you.",
    ["Dialogue1001702"]="<size=24>You've passed Criatura Academy's Novice Trial!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1001703"]="Hehe, are you surprised? Your trial started from the moment we met! And you did not disappoint at all! Even Jarod was impressed by the bravery and perceptiveness that you showed during the battle. However, what's most important to an adventurer is not brute strength but rather <color=#CA2E0AFF>the spirit of helping others and staying true to one's principles</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1001704"]="I think you definitely possess these qualities! Criatura Academy certainly needs novices like you! Now that you're a prospective student, you still need one more item. Want to take a guess at what it is?",
    ["Dialogue1001705"]="Nope! You're missing an accessory that shows that you're a Criatura Academy student. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smile Assistance</color> and collect your very own <color=#CA2E0AFF>Academy Hat</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1001801"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me count again, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>1, 2, 3... No, no, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>it still doesn't add up. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is bad.</color></size>\nAh? Oh excuse me, I didn't notice there was someone here. Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue1001802"]="<size=24>You are a novice from Criatura Academy?! </size>Oh no, oh no...",
    ["Dialogue1001803"]="Sigh, since you've overheard me, I might as well tell you the truth. I've run out of the materials I need to make academy hats, so sadly I can't issue one to you right now.",
    ["Dialogue1001804"]="I understand, it's a little unfortunate, haha... But there's a solution. Since you're an adventurer, you should be able to help me out. No wait, I mean you should be able to help yourself out! As long as I have all the materials, it's not much work to make an academy hat! We can work together: you gather the materials, and I'll make the hat!",
    ["Dialogue1001805"]="Hmmm... I'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 Gorgeous Feathers, 1 Dancing Grass, and 5 Lucky Clovers</color>. Gorgeous Feathers can be gathered from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatics</color> nearby, Dancing Grass can be found <color=#CA2E0AFF>near water</color>, and Lucky Clovers can be gathered from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fabres</color> on farms. If you bring me these materials, I'll start work on the academy hat right away!",
    ["Dialogue1001901"]="Got the academy hat? Great, let's go! Jarod and the others couldn't wait; they've already left for the port. We can take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate Express</color> to catch up to them. The boarding point for the express is just inside the amusement park. Let's hurry!",
    ["Dialogue1002001"]="Quick, let's get on the deck!",
    ["Dialogue1002101"]="<size=24>There's still space. All aboard for Criatura Academy!</size>\nHmm? You want to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude Island</color> as well? Are you ready to set off?",
    ["Dialogue1002102"]="Okay! The wind and waves can get pretty big; I don't want any monkeying around while aboard!",
    ["Dialogue1002103"]="Oh? Let me know when you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue1002201"]="You're so slow. I've been waiting for ages! Jarod has already taken Ygnizem, so from here on I'll be your dedicated recruiter! Izlude Island is where I grew up, so nobody knows it better than I do!",
    ["Dialogue1002301"]="Because of all the hard work of our past deans and instructors, Criatura Academy is now very well respected in Rune-Midgarts Kingdom! Even members of the seven royal families will show their respect when they see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color>! He's currently in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Hall</color>, waiting for the arrival of the novices. Go meet him!",
    ["Dialogue1002401"]="Now, let's see... Who is this standing in front of me?",
    ["Dialogue1002402"]="Haha! Novice, you dare call yourself an adventurer? You remind me of myself when I was a young whippersnapper! So, young adventurer, what brings you here?",
    ["Dialogue1002403"]="Ho hoho! What is your dream?",
    ["Dialogue1002404"]="Looks like you haven't thought it through, hoho! Here, I'm going to ask you <color=#CA2E0AFF>three questions</color>. If you manage to impress me, I'll help you sort out your thoughts. How 'bout that?",
    ["Dialogue1002501"]="In this land, a real adventurer might not be the person with the most raw strength; but he or she will definitely possess the strongest spirit and an unshakable will. And from what I see, you seem to possess those qualities! Come before me now and I will bestow unto you the powers of past adventurers! Then the secrets of <color=#CA2E0AFF>each class</color> will be revealed!",
    ["Dialogue1002601"]="Let me take a look at you again. Hmm, you look much more determined now, ho hoho! Young adventurer, you have surely decided on the path you wish to take, am I right? But this is just the beginning. All the 1st Class Instructors are gathered in this hall, and you should know that they are undoubtedly the strongest in their respective fields! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Listen to your instructor's advice.</color> It will certainly enlighten you.",
    ["Dialogue1002602"]="Come see me at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> after that. I've prepared a little something for you. Hohoho!",
    ["Dialogue1002701"]="Dean Mainz is already waiting for you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color>. He's even prepared a surprise for you!",
    ["Dialogue1002702"]="When facing a formidable foe, mighty <color=#CA2E0AFF>Strength</color> is important to a swordsman. But don't forget that you need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vitality</color> on your side too.",
    ["Dialogue1002801"]="Of all that exists in the world, only magic can defy the laws of right and wrong, and of life and death.",
    ["Dialogue1002802"]="Superior <color=#CA2E0AFF>Intelligence</color> is just a stepping stone for learning magic. With sufficient <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dexterity</color>, the battleground will be your playground.",
    ["Dialogue1002901"]="A healthy mind is as important as a healthy body!",
    ["Dialogue1002902"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Intelligence</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dexterity</color> allow us to spread blessings. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Strength</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Agility</color> allow us to turn our defense into offense! Dear adventurer, I look forward to ending the pain and sadness of this world with you.",
    ["Dialogue1003001"]="What? Miss the target? Impossible. Unless the river in Payon starts flowing backwards!",
    ["Dialogue1003002"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Dexterity</color> helps one's aim stay true. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Agility</color> helps increase the speed of one's movement! A perfect archer will always win the battle at a distance. Just like me!",
    ["Dialogue1003101"]="I love your eyes! They look like gems! Can I take a closer look?\n<size=18>I wonder how much they'd fetch? Hehehe!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1003102"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Strength</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Agility</color> are the greatest weapons in a thief's arsenal! The reason? Obvious: they allow us to fight or flee!",
    ["Dialogue1003201"]="Knowledge is the only thing traded at no cost.",
    ["Dialogue1003202"]="Remember, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Strength</color> will only help earn your first pot of gold! You will need enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dexterity</color> to live in the lap of luxury!",
    ["Dialogue1003301"]="So you've completed the Class Training Course? Mmhm! You definitely look more confident than before!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Seems like I can reveal it soon...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1003302"]="Dean Mainz is already waiting for you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color>. He's even prepared a surprise for you!",
    ["Dialogue1003401"]="Let me take a look at you! You look like a real pro after changing into your class robes! But class advancement is just the beginning. Your future growth will depend entirely on your hard work. Of course, you can always choose to stay in the academy to study in the archives and hone your skills, but nothing can beat the experience of going out there to explore the world for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue1003402"]="It's now time for your last lesson. Do you see the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color> behind me? Observe and then tell me what you feel.",
    ["Dialogue1003501"]="Did you feel anything?",
    ["Dialogue1003502"]="Hoho! You're a sharp one. The Heart Pedestal is an artifact. According to the archives, it was personally gifted to our founder by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>valkyries</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1003503"]="<size=24>You can see it?</size>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>this child seems to have more potential than I imagined.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1003504"]="Those fragments are known as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>. Since we're on this subject, never forget what I'm about to tell you. Ymir's Heart manifested from the Creator's actual heart, and it holds the power to change the entire world. Every fragment is undoubtedly precious, and every person who ever had the privilege of owning one has created an undying legacy!",
    ["Dialogue1003505"]="Since the founding of Criatura Academy, we have worked hard to collect the fragments. The Heart Pedestal was specially created to store them. If you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the fragments and bring them back here</color>, everyone in the academy will be very thankful!",
    ["Dialogue1003506"]="If you want to know more about Ymir's Heart, you can stop by the Library. There's an ancient book named <color=#CA2E0AFF>History of the Midgard Continent</color>, and it should have the answers you're looking for.",
    ["Dialogue1003601"]="You want to know more about the story of Ymir's Heart? I'm too busy to tell you right now! If your eyes are working, why don't you scurry along the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shelves</color> over there and read it for yourself?",
    ["Dialogue1003701"]="The academy assembly is starting. Come along now! <size=24>Chop-chop!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1003801"]="Are you all prepared to set off, young adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1003802"]="Parting is but temporary. An eagle should soar in the boundless skies! Now, go forth and leave your mark on every corner of the world!\n<size=24>That is what makes a real adventurer of Criatura!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1003803"]="They are the shield, the barrier of this kingdom; their duty is to protect and guard the kingdom against any foreseeable danger. A series of <color=#CA2E0AFF>strict and harsh tests</color> must be carried out to select the bravest warrior to fulfill this honorable duty. If you want to know more about it, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> and read about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>King's Order</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1003804"]="Hohoho! An eagle should soar in the boundless skies! Now, go forth and leave your mark on every corner of the world!\n<size=26>That is what makes a real Adventurer of Criatura!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1003805"]="Huh? Wondering where you should start off your adventure? Why don't you join Kingdom Defense Force?",
    ["Dialogue1003901"]="You look kind of lost. Don't know where to start your adventure? I heard that recently, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kingdom Defense Force</color> has posted the <color=#CA2E0AFF>King's Decree</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> on Izlude Island, and they seem to be recruiting adventurers! Why not go check out the Mission Board?",
    ["Dialogue1004001"]="Oh no, it's over! It's all over! I was only gone for 10 minutes!\nWhat am I going to do? <size=24>What am I going to do now?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1004002"]="Can't you see?! The board's ruined! Don't bother me! Izlude Island only has one Mission Board; the residents can't get their requests fulfilled now. What a nightmare!",
    ["Dialogue1004003"]="Do you think it's easy to repair the board?! Hang on, I know! Since it was made by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Old Clay</color>, maybe he'll know a way to fix it. But there's no way I can just leave my post after what's happened.",
    ["Dialogue1004004"]="Wow! Your offer is <size=24>greatly appreciated!</size>\nGo! I'll wait for your good news here!",
    ["Dialogue1004101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I wonder how Charlie's doing in Prontera?</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> He actually dared to show off his design to me the last time. It was </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>just a design of the sewers under the capital. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>What's so great about that?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1004102"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Sigh,</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> there hasn't been much work here on Izlude Island lately. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Is it time for me to go elsewhere?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1004103"]="Huh? How long have you been standing there?",
    ["Dialogue1004104"]="<size=24>—What?!</size>\nThat was a really sturdy Mission Board! I have to go take a look! Oh right, my <color=#CA2E0AFF>wood</color> was taken away by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Condor</color>; I'll need you to bring it back for me!",
    ["Dialogue1004201"]="The Mission Board is more badly damaged than I'd imagined! It might take me a long time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fix it</color>. I need your help.",
    ["Dialogue1004202"]="Well then, listen up. This is what you've got to do next...",
    ["Dialogue1004301"]="You young 'uns are so much more agile than an old fogey like me. I think you have the makings of a craftsman. What do you think of becoming my assistant?",
    ["Dialogue1004302"]="Haha, I'm only joking! Alright, now that the Mission Board is fixed, it's time for me to go home.\n<size=18>Next time you visit me, </size><size=18>make sure the work's more challenging, ya hear?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1004401"]="The Mission Board may be fixed now, but...",
    ["Dialogue1004402"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>...the residents' requests</color> have piled up. We need to complete them soon, but we're seriously short on manpower! What should I do, <size=24>what should I do, </size><size=26>what should I do?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1004403"]="Oh? You're willing to help? Your offer is <size=24>greatly appreciated!</size>\nGo! All these requests are relying on you, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1004501"]="Woah! Well done! And you should have realized by now that the rewards for completing requests <size=24>are quite generous</size>!\nFeel free to drop by to help whenever you're free!",
    ["Dialogue1004601"]="Let me take a closer look... Your eyes seem much more determined. It appears our little Adventurer is choosing his own route to become stronger. There's no time to relax now because the real adventure is just around the corner. I've prepared a little gift to celebrate the departure...",
    ["Dialogue1004602"]="Ho-ho, hold your horse, Adventurer. You will find out soon. Come on now, let's go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> together!",
    ["Dialogue1004701"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>A wide variety of weapon options and skill combinations</color> is the edge unique to Super Novice! Heh, apply the skills from each class in combos and crush the enemy! Just like an epic hero would do!",
    ["Dialogue1004702"]="So you want to be a Super Novice? You must find your original aspiration first!",
    ["Dialogue1009701"]="The Legend Point Activation feature is not yet available. This step will be temporarily replaced by dialog.",
    ["Dialogue1009801"]="The Headgear Crafting feature is not yet available. This step will be temporarily replaced by dialog.",
    ["Dialogue1009901"]="This feature is not yet available. This step will be temporarily replaced by dialog.",
    ["Dialogue1010101"]="Adventurer, are you here to join the Kingdom Defense Force too?",
    ["Dialogue1010102"]="Your courage is admirable, but the Kingdom Defense Force is the indestructible shield of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom. We can't just allow anyone to join. You'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer a few questions</color> first. Then I'll determine if you're a true warrior worthy of joining the Defense Force.",
    ["Dialogue1010201"]="Great, your answers are satisfactory! But words are just words. You still need to prove your worth.\nI declare that you're now a Defense Force reservist! Hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>airship</color> to meet your captain, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fitz</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1010202"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, I hope this one will be able to put up with Fitz's bad temper.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010301"]="You're the new reservist?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Urgh, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>why does Akand keep assigning me scrawny runts?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010302"]="Forget it, looks like I'll just have to whip you into shape! My name is Fitz, captain of the First Squad. From today on, I'll be your commanding officer.",
    ["Dialogue1010303"]="<size=24>—Your answer? </size><size=24>Reservist?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010304"]="That's more like it! I only have one demand for my subordinates. That is...\n<size=24>NEVER DOUBT YOUR COMMANDING OFFICER!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010305"]="<size=24>Now, </size><size=24>go <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick up that Parachute Bag</color></size> as fast as you can!",
    ["Dialogue1010401"]="<size=18>Tsk, those soldiers are always making a ruckus. </size><size=18>Do they think I'm deaf? </size><size=18>They should be glad I'm so tolerant, </size><size=18>otherwise I'd have thrown them overboard by now!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010402"]="<size=18>Yup, that's right, </size><size=18>it must be because I'm so restrained. </size><size=18>That's why I don't lower myself to their level. Especially that guy called Fitz... </size><size=18>If I'd met him on land, </size><size=18>I would have...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010403"]="<size=24>Ahh! </size><size=24>How long have you been standing there?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010404"]="Ahh...? Ahahah, Fi... Fitz's orders?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He didn't hear me... did he? No, there's no way he could have heard me.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010405"]="Ah well, gentlemen... I mean sirs! Are we ready to set off?",
    ["Dialogue1010406"]="Please return to your seats, I'm going to speed up now!",
    ["Dialogue1010407"]="Sure, sure! Let me know when you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue1010501"]="Wow, this is the first time I've ever seen someone fall from the sky. It scared me half to death!",
    ["Dialogue1010502"]="Huh? You took an airship here? The way they land is so dangerous!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why would Dyplon say that airships are Kafra Corporation's competitors? They're way worse. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>In any case, this is a great opportunity to advertise, better not miss it!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010503"]="Adventurer, for your own safety, why not use the saaaafest mode of transport in the land—Kafra Services! All you need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>save teleport points</color> and you'll be able to travel freely around the world!",
    ["Dialogue1010601"]="Thank you for using Kafra Services. Kafra Corporation always provides you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue1010602"]="Prontera has now been saved as a teleport point. If you get hurt and lose consciousness while exploring in the wild, Kafra Corporation will bring you back here! But remember, you can only save teleport points with Kafra staff who are situated in the city!",
    ["Dialogue1010603"]="Apart from that, Kafra Corporation also provides the service of <color=#CA2E0AFF>fast travel around the world.</color> You'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>register yourself with Kafra staff who are situated at the various locations </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>before you can use the service!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1010604"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Did I forget anything? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me think... Ah, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>right!</color></size>\nAs you're a first time user of Kafra Services, I have a little gift for you! Please accept these <color=#CA2E0AFF>Butterfly Wings</color>. Using them will return you to saved teleport points from anywhere at anytime!",
    ["Dialogue1010605"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>why does it feel like I'm still forgetting something? Ah, yes!</color></size>\nI think some of your companions are nearby. I saw a few parachutes land in the direction of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>central fountain</color>. Do they need Kafra Services too?",
    ["Dialogue1010701"]="Where did you land? We've been looking all over for you! I'm worried for your future; you managed to annoy your captain on the very first day of training.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>And Fitz, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>he actually got impatient enough to just take off with the rest of the soldiers. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>What a mess. You'd better just hurry up and get the supplies to him.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010702"]="See this <color=#CA2E0AFF>box</color> beside me? These are supplies for reservists. There's not much to choose from, and this is the last set. Go on, open it.",
    ["Dialogue1010801"]="You're now ready to receive an even greater verbal thrashing... I mean, greater challenge! Hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate</color> and report to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Fitz</color>!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He might even be </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>on a rampage already.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1010901"]="<size=24>Being late won't increase your chances of survival on the battlefield, </size><size=24>RESERVIST!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1010902"]="Your sloppiness really gets on my nerves! The other soldiers have already started their trial, and what have you been doing? Taking a relaxing stroll?! See that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Windmill Tower</color> over there? That will be your battleground! You need to eliminate all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragoras</color> in there within the specified time! Go! <size=24>Move it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1011001"]="Phew! I'm saved, thank you! You're here for the trial too, right? Those Mandragoras are so scary! Especially the one just now, it was huuuuge!",
    ["Dialogue1011002"]="Huh, anything strange nearby? Oh yeah, there's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>stairs</color> over there! Wait a sec... You're not gonna ask me to take you there, are you?! Stop kidding, what if monsters like before show up again?",
    ["Dialogue1011003"]="Don't blame me for not warning you!\n<size=18>In any case, my trial's over; </size><size=18>I'm off to report to Captain Fitz!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1011101"]="<size=24>WHAT IS THIS?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1011102"]="...That actually happened? I was wondering why the reservists hadn't come back from their trials after the time limit had elapsed. If what you said is true, we need to check if they're safe!",
    ["Dialogue1011103"]="<size=24>Good answer! </size><size=24>Just as I'd expect from a First Squad reservist!</size>\nThe trial locations are scattered across the area just beyond the West Gate. You go check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery nearby</color>; I'll take care of the other locations!",
    ["Dialogue1011201"]="Thank goodness you came! I almost gave up hope.",
    ["Dialogue1011202"]="This was what happened. We were carrying out our trial near the cemetery. The Thief Bugs we were supposed to kill weren't that strong, but then something seemed provoke them and they suddenly transformed! They became really tough; some of us were even injured! I still have some <color=#CA2E0AFF>bandages</color> here. Could you help <color=#CA2E0AFF>tend to their wounds</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1011301"]="Now that everyone's back on their feet, we should get back to Captain Fitz!\n<size=18>But we've exceeded the time limit... thinking about the look on Odin's face is giving me chills.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1011302"]="Hmm, anything strange nearby? Now that you mention it, I think I saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1011401"]="<size=24>Another strange device?</size>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The problem is I don't know what it is either. I'll just leave it to Akand and his huge brain!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1011402"]="*Cough, cough* Take this device to Court Clerk <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> and let him take a look at it!",
    ["Dialogue1011501"]="What's with this device? The power it's emitting feels very strange. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>dismantle</color> it and investigate further!",
    ["Dialogue1011601"]="Hmm, its core seems to be an alchemy stone. But normal alchemy stones don't usually give off such an evil aura. I'm afraid this is beyond the scope of my knowledge.",
    ["Dialogue1011602"]="Hmm, could you take it to <color=#CA2E1AFF>Alchemist Scholar Lawrence in the library</color>? He's quite accomplished in the field of alchemy; he might be able to shed some light on its origin.",
    ["Dialogue1011701"]="...This alchemy stone?!\n<size=18>How fascinating! Someone actually managed to do it?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1011702"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Sigh. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is why I do so dislike explaining things as complex as alchemy to laymen. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The ignorant only ask \"What? Why? How?\"</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1011801"]="Explaining the structure of alchemy stones from a scholarly point of view is not difficult, but this one is not so simple! I suggest you start by reading <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"The History of Midgard\"</color>. You can find it in this library.",
    ["Dialogue1011802"]="Ah yes! So you've noticed. Both the physical appearance and power of this alchemy stone are just like <color=#CA2E0AFF>a replica of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. Although the workmanship may be rather coarse, I must admit that whoever made it certainly has guts.",
    ["Dialogue1011803"]="In any case, the person who made this replica would need to have a very good understanding of the real fragment. But it couldn't have been made by just anyone, because...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Because the only known fragment in the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom is </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>kept securely in the royal palace's treasury.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1011901"]="Lawrence said that?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, things are getting complicated.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> Since a replica of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart appeared at the West Gate </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>and caused monsters to transform... If my guess is correct, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>the next one might be...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1011902"]="Reservist, please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> and look for the captain of the Second Squad, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Simmons</color>! I need to confirm if the same thing has happened in his area!",
    ["Dialogue1012001"]="Akand sent you? Monsters transforming? How does he know about what's happening here?",
    ["Dialogue1012002"]="That's right, not too long ago we found some <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters that were unusually agitated</color>. I dispatched a team to eliminate them and investigate, but they're still not back yet. Since you're here, why not go check it out for me?! The agitated monsters were near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Farm</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1012101"]="Don't worry, I'm not hurt. I'm just exhausted from the intense fighting.",
    ["Dialogue1012102"]="As you can see, the Condors in this area suddenly went crazy. They even started attacking passersby! The villagers nearby were all scared away! Are you here to provide reinforcement? Then hurry up and take care of those <color=#CA2E0AFF>crazy Condors</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1012201"]="You're so heroic, soldier!",
    ["Dialogue1012202"]="Phew! I saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> on the grass and went over to it. As soon as I picked it up, a group of assassins came charging at me! Please give this to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Simmons</color>! I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue1012301"]="Is that what made the monsters go crazy? Worrying stuff...",
    ["Dialogue1012302"]="What?! The devices were planted deliberately? And there are five of them?! Let <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> know straight away! He'll know what to do!",
    ["Dialogue1012401"]="Just as I expected, whoever created the alchemy devices is plotting something.",
    ["Dialogue1012402"]="The letter mentioned that there are a total of <color=#CA2E0AFF>five alchemy devices</color>. Other than the ones you found at the Windmill Tower, West Gate Cemetery, and Green Cotton Farm, <color=#CA2E0AFF>there are still two more out there.</color> We need to find out where they are! Thankfully, we've found out where the person who hired the assassins could be. It looks like you're ready. Well then, head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>, reservist!",
    ["Dialogue1012501"]="...Yes?",
    ["Dialogue1012502"]="Who are you? I have no time for strangers now, stay away from me!",
    ["Dialogue1012601"]="Hmph! I saw that! What are you doing sneaking around my tavern? If you can't explain yourself, I'm going to hand you over to the sheriff!",
    ["Dialogue1012602"]="I'm just joking! Look at how nervous you are! So cute!\n<size=18>You're not the only one sneaking around in this tavern; </size><size=18>you don't have to be afraid.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1012603"]="(Isabella whispers in your ear.)\n<size=18>If you're trying to get information around here, </size><size=18>you won't get anything out of anyone unless you have </size><size=18>some tricks up your sleeve.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1012604"]="My my, even I'll start feeling shy if you carry on looking at me with those puppy-dog eyes!\nHere's an idea: Let's help each other out? If you could help me with something, I'll teach you some tricks to get information out of people!",
    ["Dialogue1012605"]="You've probably already noticed <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bard Morts</color> over there? He's been showing off about his experiences and using song riddles as an excuse to flirt with the Kitty Girls. I bet he'd explode with anger if you could <color=#CA2E0AFF>solve all of his riddles</color>!\n<size=18>Just imagining it makes me want to laugh out loud! Hehe!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1012701"]="♪ Who saw more than me? Who understands my sorrows?\nThe moon, beautiful wine, and a lute. I'll hold her memories close at heart. ♪",
    ["Dialogue1012702"]="Hey! If you're not a Kitty Girl, I'll charge you for listening to me! But if you can answer my question correctly, I won't mind playing you a song for free.",
    ["Dialogue1012703"]="Sigh, here's another sorry know-it-all! But I don't mind. The more people get it wrong, the more it shows how smart I am. Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue1012704"]="Here it comes!",
    ["Dialogue1012705"]="♪ Born a royal but sought no worth in thee lineage.\nWhy pursue fame and fortune when thee students are treasures invaluable? ♪",
    ["Dialogue1012706"]="—Who is this person?",
    ["Dialogue1012707"]="♪ Number one mage of the world, bestowed as the Sage Geffen.\nFalls to rid the land of evil, rises to glide among the stars.♪",
    ["Dialogue1012708"]="—Who is this person?",
    ["Dialogue1012709"]="♪ Hold an army on thee left, hold a lover on thee right.\nWho you ask? A straight face without a doubt.♪",
    ["Dialogue1012710"]="—Who is this person?",
    ["Dialogue1012711"]="Wrong, wrong, and wrong! I've said it before, but giving up is the only correct answer!",
    ["Dialogue1012712"]="How is this possible?! These riddles were carefully created by me! How could anybody get all of them correct?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>My dear ladies, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>you wouldn't look down on me now, would you? Nooooo!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1012801"]="Hehehe! I knew you wouldn't disappoint me!",
    ["Dialogue1012802"]="Morts is going to be embarrassed for a while now. Thank you for standing up for my Kitty Girls, young adventurer!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I bet this is a huge blow to Morts' pride, hehehe!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1012803"]="I'll give this prized <color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Liquor</color> to you as thanks!\n<size=18>Don't underestimate it! With just a few drops, </size><size=18>even a complete mute would tell you their deepest, darkest secret!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1012901"]="Hic! My dear, there's nothing going on between me and Lisa next door. I just... just killed a cockroach for her, that's all!\nHuh? My dear, what are you doing here in the tavern? Hic!",
    ["Dialogue1012902"]="My dear, how did you know? Don't you worry, I won't hide anything from you! Actually—hic! An <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> got me to help him place those devices all over the capital! He promised a huge sum of Zeny if I could complete the task! Hic!",
    ["Dialogue1012903"]="Erm, where did I place the devices? Burp! Let me think... There's one at the Windmill Tower, one at the West Gate Cemetery, and one at Green Cotton Farm. The other two? One is hidden <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the cemetery behind the cathedral</color> and the other...",
    ["Dialogue1012904"]="(His voice is getting deeper and deeper. It looks like he's about to fall asleep soon.)\n<size=18>To save myself some trouble, I threw it into <color=#CA2E0AFF>the sewers</color>! Hehe! Hic! My dear, I'm going to take a nap now. I feel so dizzy.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1013001"]="It was an alchemist? This is bewildering.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How could an alchemist have access to the Fragment of Ymir's Heart that's in the palace?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1013002"]="You've done well, reservist. But this is not over. We need to recover those alchemy devices! Let's split up. You go get the one hidden <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the cemetery behind the cathedral</color>; I'll take my men to search the sewers!",
    ["Dialogue1013101"]="You're too late! I've hidden all the treasure! Hehe!\n<size=18>I'm going to be the best </size><size=18>in this treasure hunt!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1013102"]="Oh... You're not here for the treasure hunt? I have seen a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color>, but I found it first; I'm not going to just tell you where it is!",
    ["Dialogue1013103"]="I don't believe you! You just want my treasure!",
    ["Dialogue1013104"]="<size=24>*Wails* A grownup threatening a kid! </size><size=24>Shame on you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1013105"]="But if you really want it, I'll trade it for <color=#CA2E0AFF>a photo or painting of Veronica</color>! I heard she's one of the most beautiful women in the kingdom, and that's why Commander Helbard of the Defense Force is so smitten! I want to see just how beautiful she is!",
    ["Dialogue1013106"]="They say Veronica often prays <color=#CA2E0AFF>beneath the statue of Odin in front of the palace</color>, but guards keep watch there all the time; civilians aren't allowed near it. But you won't let that stop you, right?",
    ["Dialogue1013201"]="Oh bummer, she's not even as cute as Lily next door. But as a man, I'll keep my word! I found this behind a tombstone. Here, it's yours now!",
    ["Dialogue1013301"]="Well done, reservist! But now I feel really guilty; my trip to the sewers wasn't as fruitful as I hoped it would be.",
    ["Dialogue1013302"]="For some unknown reason, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Chivalry</color> was guarding the entrance to the sewers. No matter what I said, they refused to allow me in.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could it be something to do with the alchemy device?</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> This is really getting complicated, tsk.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1013303"]="At this point, all we can do is take the device to Commander Bernard and ask him for help! He should be at the square in front of the palace right about now. Let's go.",
    ["Dialogue1013401"]="Oh my! Why would you have something like this?!",
    ["Dialogue1013402"]="Huh?! So you're telling me that this is a replica of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart? And it has something to do with an alchemist?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>... Could it be him?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1013403"]="Things might be more complicated than you imagined. The Fragment of Ymir's Heart that was <color=#CA2E0AFF>kept in the palace</color> was <color=#CA2E0AFF>stolen</color> a few days ago!",
    ["Dialogue1013404"]="You're wondering why I'm so well-aware of this matter? It's because it has something to do with me as well...\n(Bernard frowns and seems to be deep in thought.)",
    ["Dialogue1013501"]="Would you like to hear what happened? Maybe my experience that day might shed some light on things for you.",
    ["Dialogue1013502"]="(Nods.)",
    ["Dialogue1013503"]="One moment please.",
    ["Dialogue1013601"]="Commander, I just saw a shadowy figure break into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>treasury</color>! Hurry! Could they be trying to steal something valuable?",
    ["Dialogue1013701"]="Going by what you've told me, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> who stole the Fragment of Ymir's Heart is obviously the one who created the alchemy devices! I regret not taking his life that day! All this could have been averted!",
    ["Dialogue1013702"]="I tried investigating the identity of the alchemist, but I was stopped by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ian Walter</color>. He pinned the blame for losing the fragment on me. No matter how hard I tried to explain myself, he refused to investigate other suspicious aspects.",
    ["Dialogue1013703"]="Now even the Royal Chivalry has stepped in to stop us; there must be some kind of conspiracy going on. Reservist, I order you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chivalry</color> and gather intelligence! I need to know what Hallam is up to!",
    ["Dialogue1013801"]="How did it go?",
    ["Dialogue1013802"]="Hmph, just as I thought. All the clues lead to the sewers! Although we're still unsure of the chivalry's motives, if they have nothing to hide, why would they be stopping the Defense Force from going into the sewers?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How dare they?!</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> Do they really expect me to just stand by and do nothing?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1013803"]="Reservist, I order you to think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get into the sewers to investigate</color> this matter! We've got to find out what that so-called <color=#CA2E0AFF>expedition squad</color> is doing in there!",
    ["Dialogue1013901"]="State the password, or you can't enter!",
    ["Dialogue1013902"]="That's correct. You may enter!",
    ["Dialogue1013903"]="That's not the password! Leave immediately!",
    ["Dialogue1014001"]="Ah, thank you very much! All these transformed monsters are an absolute nightmare for us!",
    ["Dialogue1014002"]="Expedition squad? That's right, Captain Hallam sent us to stop the Thief Bug rampage! To prevent this mess from reaching the ground above, the captain ordered us to seal the entrance to the sewers. Looks like he's finally realized we're short-handed! We're lucky you've shown up now, or who knows how much more time we'd need to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zudd</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Iverson</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1014003"]="Yeah, they're two members of the squad who got lost during an earlier battle. If you could help <color=#CA2E0AFF>find them and bring them back</color>, we'd be eternally grateful!",
    ["Dialogue1014101"]="Thank you, adventurer! If you'd come just a few seconds later, I don't think I'd have lived to see tomorrow's sunrise!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Although I don't think I'll be seeing any sunlight down in these sewers any time soon.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014102"]="Oh! So Captain Rodney sent you! Iverson? Ahhhhh! Iverson! He-he was trying to save me by luring the Thief Bugs away.",
    ["Dialogue1014103"]="<size=24>I-I'm so sorry!</size><size=24> Bu-but I'm really too scared to go!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1014104"]="<size=18>Go ahead, look down on me. I-I'm well known in the squad as a coward. I-I don't even know why Iverson would want to save someone like me! I don't deserve to be a knight!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1014105"]="<size=24>I-I'm so sorry!</size>\nI-I'll report to Captain Rodney now and receive my punishment!",
    ["Dialogue1014201"]="I owe you one, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1014202"]="Oh I see. Phew! I'm relieved to hear that Zudd and the rest of the guys are alright! But there's something that I need to report to Captain Rodney right away. Let's get back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>where the squad's stationed</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1014301"]="You've been a great help, my friend! Don't worry, I'll be sure to report this to Captain Hallam!",
    ["Dialogue1014302"]="Captain, there's something else I'd like to report!",
    ["Dialogue1014303"]="I know this might sound ridiculous, but I suspect that the Thief Bugs were being manipulated by someone. The Thief Bugs forced me into a corner, and I was prepared to give my life fighting them. But before I could draw my sword, a man who looked like an <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> suddenly appeared!",
    ["Dialogue1014304"]="He ordered the Thief Bugs to attack me! I couldn't see how he did it, but I clearly remember that he was holding a <color=#CA2E0AFF>shiny blue fragment</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1014305"]="H-how did you know the Fragment of Ymir's Heart has been stolen from the palace?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh no! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Did I say too much?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014306"]="You're saying that the person who stole the Fragment of Ymir's Heart was the alchemist that Iverson encountered? And he used it to create replicas that are making the monsters around Prontera transform?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He doesn't seem to be lying.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The replicas might have something to do with the Thief Bugs going crazy. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I've got to report this to Captain Hallam!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014307"]="My friend, please let <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hallam</color> know what you've just told me! Now that we've found out who's behind all this, we'll track him through the sewers!",
    ["Dialogue1014401"]="Adventurer, what are you doing in the Royal Chivalry?",
    ["Dialogue1014402"]="What? So there's actually more to the Thief Bugs' rampage through the sewers?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>An alchemist, huh? Could it be the same alchemist that Commander Bernard mentioned?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014403"]="Adventurer, I'm going to ignore how you managed to get into the sewers in the first place. I'd like to officially ask for your help! The chivalry needs someone as heroic as you!",
    ["Dialogue1014404"]="Oh? You're from the Defense Force? Haha, don't worry. I have no intention of blaming you. Since that's the case, could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>lead me to Commander Bernard</color>? It's imperative that we work together against this dangerous foe!",
    ["Dialogue1014501"]="And so, this is what happened. I'm here to apologize on behalf of the chivalry.",
    ["Dialogue1014502"]="I accept your apology, hmph! Since the misunderstanding has been resolved, the most important thing now is to apprehend the alchemist and recover the Fragment of Ymir's Heart that was stolen!",
    ["Dialogue1014503"]="I was about to ask, did you sense anything strange the night the fragment was stolen?",
    ["Dialogue1014504"]="(Bernard thinks for a while.)\nLet me see... Hmm, you saw the alchemist in the sewers, right? The night the fragment was stolen, he seemed to be standing near the drainage pipe.",
    ["Dialogue1014505"]="Did he make his escape by using the drainage pipe to get into the sewers?",
    ["Dialogue1014506"]="That must be it!",
    ["Dialogue1014507"]="But the sewers were built a long time ago; it's a labyrinth. It's not going to be easy to find someone hiding in there.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ah! How could I've forgotten about Old Charlie?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014508"]="Adventurer, could you make a trip on my behalf? Commander Bernard and I still have to discuss our collaboration. My old friend, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charlie</color>, helped design the capital's sewers. He knows them like the back of his hand! Please go to see him and borrow the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewer blueprint</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1014601"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmph... I wonder how Old Clay's doing on Izlude Island.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He was quite dismissive of my design last time we met! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>So what if he designed Criatura Academy?!</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> It's not as if it's so great.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014602"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, since there's nothing much to do on the island, I bet he's lost his edge over the years! For architects like us, the capital is definitely the place to be!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1014603"]="Hmm? Oh, excuse me. I find myself daydreaming more and more as I get older. Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue1014604"]="The sewer blueprint? Haha, you know your stuff, eh? It is my masterpiece! You want to borrow it so you can admire it? No problem! It's right here in my <color=#CA2E0AFF>toolbox</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1014701"]="Great, let's take a look... This is bad! Apart from the two exits which lead to the palace and the capital, there's one more exit that leads to the surface! And it's located at... <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate Cemetery</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1014702"]="The consequences will be dire if the alchemist manages to escape via the cemetery exit! Reservist, check the cemetery while I deploy some men to check out the capital!",
    ["Dialogue1014801"]="*Coughs* This job is so stressful.",
    ["Dialogue1014802"]="Sigh, I was just here praying for the dead, but suddenly got interrupted by monsters. Young adventurer, you must have been sent by Odin! Great Allfather, thank you for your benevolence! May the unrest in the cemetery soon be resolved!",
    ["Dialogue1014803"]="The monsters in this area have been usually agitated lately. I can't tell if it's just me or there's some weird power being emitted from <color=#CA2E0AFF>beneath the tomb</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1014901"]="Haha! It surprises me how you always seem to appear in times of need!",
    ["Dialogue1014902"]="Truth to be told, we've run into more difficulty! The expedition team managed to track the alchemist to this point, but the path ahead is blocked by a horde of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Female Thief Bugs</color>! Everyone's exhausted from trying to eliminate them.",
    ["Dialogue1014903"]="Oh! You're so understanding! Thanks in advance!",
    ["Dialogue1015001"]="Hoho! If someone as strong as you joined the expedition squad, our efficiency would more than double in an instant. Well, in any case, we've got to continue our search!",
    ["Dialogue1015002"]="Haha! That's what I was hoping to hear! Well then, let's get started!",
    ["Dialogue1015101"]="Th-th-this monster is way bigger than the transformed Thief Bugs! You didn't provoke it, did you?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I don't like our chances.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1015102"]="You're saying that this monster looks similar to the golden monster that Commander Bernard saw in the palace treasury?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could this monster have something to do with the alchemist too?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1015103"]="Since not even Commander Bernard could take it down, we'll definitely need to approach with caution! Take this to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Researcher Norten</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Library</color> and see what he has to say about it!",
    ["Dialogue1015201"]="Woah! Are you actually the one who saw the monster and took the photo? I'm so <size=24>jealous!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1015202"]="What? You don't know what this little fella's called? It's very rare; it's called a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Thief Bug</color>! Look at those shiny forewings! They're so mesmerizing... But this one is still young. Given enough time, it will mature into an even more impressive creature!",
    ["Dialogue1015203"]="Oh, all my knowledge on Golden Thief Bugs came from a book called <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"The Monsters of Midgard\"</color>. There's a copy on that shelf. Bring it over!",
    ["Dialogue1015301"]="Yup, that's right. In order to subdue these amazing creatures, you'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin's Blessing</color>. Otherwise, you'll really have a challenge on your hands.",
    ["Dialogue1015302"]="From what I know, only the most devout follower of Odin is able to bestow blessings! That would definitely have to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archbishop Wolmas</color>! He should be giving blessings <color=#CA2E0AFF>beneath the Odin Statue in front of Palace Square</color> now! He's very kind; I'm sure he'll bless you!",
    ["Dialogue1015401"]="Young adventurer, you seem tired. Would you like to take a break and allow Odin's benevolence to cleanse your mind and body?",
    ["Dialogue1015402"]="I understand. Since it is to eliminate monsters, I will do my best to help you. But child, I have used up all the holy water I brought earlier. Would you be so kind as to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color> in Prontera and fetch some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color>. I will be waiting for you here.",
    ["Dialogue1015501"]="Child, no monsters will be able to take your life now. As long as you have Odin's Blessing, you can fight battles without worry. But remember this, you're destined for extraordinary things! Regardless of how many adversities you may encounter, Odin will always watch over you.",
    ["Dialogue1015601"]="How's it going?",
    ["Dialogue1015602"]="Awesome! I knew it had to be you! Because whenever I'm with you, I can feel a fighting spirit within me that I've never felt before! Let's go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take that monster down</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1015701"]="<size=24>...We can't let it go!</size><size=24> We have to follow it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1015702"]="It's nothing.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I have to avenge my teammates and all the civilians that monster hurt!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1015703"]="...If you insist, fine. But be careful! I'm sure much harder challenges lie ahead! I'll catch up with you once I've regained some strength!",
    ["Dialogue1015801"]="How did it go? Did you find the alchemist?",
    ["Dialogue1015802"]="Too bad he got away. But at least the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> has been recovered! That's a huge win! Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>report back to Captain Hallam in Prontera</color>! I'm sure he has a lot to say to you!",
    ["Dialogue1015901"]="Is that really it?!",
    ["Dialogue1015902"]="This is amazing news! But... didn't the fragment affect you?",
    ["Dialogue1015903"]="What do you mean? We Defense Force Soldiers are strong of will; nothing rattles us!",
    ["Dialogue1015904"]="What I'm saying is, it's obvious that the Fragment of Ymir's Heart has extraordinary power. If the replica is enough to make monsters go crazy, surely the original fragment has even more power.",
    ["Dialogue1015905"]="Really?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Who exactly is this adventurer?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1015906"]="Come on, snap out of it, Hallam! The award ceremony is about to begin! My reservist has shown exemplary character and remarkable skill throughout this ordeal, and deserves the recognition of the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue1015907"]="I couldn't agree more! Adventurer, you are undoubtedly a hero. Commander Bernard and I are going to hold an <color=#CA2E0AFF>award ceremony</color> for you! Speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rodney</color> when you're ready; he'll take you to the venue.",
    ["Dialogue1016001"]="Are you ready, my friend?",
    ["Dialogue1016002"]="Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue1016003"]="I'll be waiting for you!",
    ["Dialogue1016101"]="Is there something else you want to say, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1016102"]="You wish to place the Fragment of Ymir's Heart in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color>? Well... I understand. In fact, Archbishop Wolmas suggested the same thing.",
    ["Dialogue1016103"]="After everything that's happened, the Fragment of Ymir's Heart would indeed be safer in the academy.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Mainz is there after all.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The fragment will surely be safe.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1016104"]="Well then, we'll entrust you with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>, adventurer. I'll report this to His Majesty the King. I'm sure His Majesty will have as much faith in your character and the archbishop's judgment as I do.",
    ["Dialogue1016201"]="<size=24>This, this is...!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1016202"]="Ho hoho! I never thought anyone would be able to bring it back! This is the very first Fragment of Ymir's Heart! Memorable indeed!",
    ["Dialogue1016203"]="The next step is simple, hoho! Do you still remember the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color>? All you need to do is place the fragment on the Heart Pedestal. Go on, my student!",
    ["Dialogue1016301"]="My name is Brunhild. I originate from a clan of war goddesses under Odin's command. The people of your realm call us \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>valkyries</color>.\"",
    ["Dialogue1016302"]="After Ragnarök, the gods vanished from this world. I am but an illusion. Successor of Odin, you were the one who brought Ymir's Heart here and awakened the remaining valkyrie power in the Heart Pedestal.",
    ["Dialogue1016303"]="As Ymir's Heart is sadly incomplete, I can only meet you through this illusion. Time is short, Successor of Odin. Prove your strength once more by <color=#CA2E0AFF>accepting this trial I have for you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1016401"]="Have you noticed that whenever you are in danger, a surge of power runs through your body, which helps you defeat monsters for which you were originally no match?",
    ["Dialogue1016402"]="You are the person that I have been waiting for, Successor of Odin. This power comes from Odin himself. You are the only one who can <color=#CA2E0AFF>control the power of Ymir's Heart without being consumed by it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1016403"]="There is not much time left, Successor of Odin. This world is held together by Ymir's power, but it is waning. You need to recover all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragments of Ymir's Heart and make them back into one</color>. Otherwise, the world will return to the state of chaos that existed before creation.",
    ["Dialogue1016404"]="Help me. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Channel the power of Odin which lies in your body into this Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. I will use the last of my power to awaken the bond between the fragments. This will enable me to locate the nearest location of Ymir's power.",
    ["Dialogue1016501"]="I see it. One fragment is near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude Island</color>, in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sea</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1016601"]="What? Fragment of Ymir's Heart? The one that was stolen from the palace not long ago, right? Rumor has it that Bernard from the Defense Force worked in tandem with the alchemist to steal it. This is no longer a secret, but Captain Hallam seems to think otherwise.",
    ["Dialogue1016701"]="I heard that the expedition squad found a strange device in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color> and Captain Hallam thinks it's pretty dangerous. But what could be so dangerous about it?",
    ["Dialogue1016801"]="Did you know? Soldiers from the Kingdom Defense Force tried to enter the sewers right after the <color=#CA2E0AFF>expedition squad</color> went in. Luckily our knights managed to hold their ground and keep the entrance secure! What could they be up to?",
    ["Dialogue1016901"]="(Someone's footprints. It looks like they head toward the platform ahead.)",
    ["Dialogue1017001"]="(There seem to be some tracks ahead.)",
    ["Dialogue1017101"]="(The weapon on the ground bears the crest of the Royal Chivalry. I don't think it was simply left here.)",
    ["Dialogue1017201"]="(There are more footprints ahead. Looks like they might belong to Iverson.)",
    ["Dialogue1017301"]="(A bubbling cauldron. The concoction inside is giving off a strange energy that feels very similar to the alchemy device. There isn't much of the concoction left.)",
    ["Dialogue1017401"]="(The workbench is covered in dirt. Vials with different labels are scattered around. Words like \"Ymir's Heart\" and \"strength\" can be made out from the corroded handwriting. Could this be what I think it is?)",
    ["Dialogue1017501"]="(Found it! The footprints head down the pipe ahead. Did the alchemist head that way?)",
    ["Dialogue1017601"]="(The alchemist is nowhere to be found, but this glowing Fragment of Ymir's Heart was on the ground.)",
    ["Dialogue1017701"]="Adventurer, from here on, you are a hero of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom. Your name will go down in history! Whenever you decide to visit again, the Royal Chivalry and Defense Force will always welcome you!",
    ["Dialogue1020101"]="You want to go out to sea? That's a bad idea! The sea has been very rough as of late!",
    ["Dialogue1020102"]="Recently, ships have ended up being surrounded by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious fog</color>. All those who attempted to sail through it have gone missing. It's highly likely that they didn't survive. Needless to say, I won't be taking anyone out to sea until this menacing fog disappears!",
    ["Dialogue1020103"]="Where did the fog come from? I have no idea. I've never seen such strange weather in all my years at sea! Your best bet is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meteorologist Kleine</color> on the island. He's been busy collecting data these days; he might have some clue about what's going on!",
    ["Dialogue1020201"]="<size=18>Oh yeah... Hmm... Something is wrong, definitely wrong...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020202"]="<size=18>Hmm... Yeah... Strange, so very strange...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020203"]="Hey, would you mind not disturbing me? Can't you see I'm busy collecting weather data?!",
    ["Dialogue1020204"]="—Oh, you're here to help? Great. I need someone to bring back the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Weather Observer</color>! It's <color=#CA2E0AFF>on the bridge to the Training Course</color>. Be quick! I need that data!",
    ["Dialogue1020301"]="Let me see...\n<size=18>Yeah... Yeah... Huh? Wait... </size><size=24>HUH?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020302"]="By Odin! Are my eyes playing tricks on me?! I already knew the fog was unusual, but I would never have thought that! It's a sign of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Haze</color>!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why is such a rare disaster happening now!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1020303"]="The Haze is a terrifying phenomenon. Any place affected by it will experience a disaster of unimaginable proportions! Judging from how the fog is moving, it... it's coming toward Izlude Island! <size=24>This is the worst case scenario!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020304"]="There's no time. There's no time! Adventurer, hu-hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>give this Weather Report to Dean Mainz</color>! Tell him we're in grave danger and ask if he has any way to stop the disaster!",
    ["Dialogue1020401"]="(Mainz's brows furrow deeper as he reads the Weather Report.)\nIf Kleine's deduction is correct and the Haze descends upon us, it will be the greatest disaster to befall Izlude Island in a hundred years! This phenomenon can't be stopped by just anybody.",
    ["Dialogue1020402"]="The origin of the Haze goes back to the war between the gods and Baphomet a thousand years ago. During the war, Odin sealed <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baphomet</color> in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>, but the effect he had on Midgard didn't completely disappear.",
    ["Dialogue1020403"]="According to reliable historical records, areas afflicted by the Haze are shrouded in <color=#CA2E0AFF>an ominous purple fog</color>. Any monsters in the fog become extremely agitated and can even transform into stronger species. The danger posed by this disaster is hard to predict, but there's one thing we can be sure of: it will bring terrible suffering!",
    ["Dialogue1020404"]="I wish we could do that! But unfortunately no human can stop the Haze. Young adventurer, all we can do now is <color=#CA2E0AFF>protect Izlude Island</color>. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>assemble all the instructors on the island</color>. Let them know that the Haze is coming and to be prepared!",
    ["Dialogue1020405"]="It's said that Baphomet has never stopped trying to reopen the dimensional gap. Although he's never been able to break the seal, his power is able to seep into this world. That's how the Haze came about.",
    ["Dialogue1020501"]="I heard some commotion just now; I thought someone was being attacked by Pirate Skeletons again. I didn't expect it to be you! Are you hurt?",
    ["Dialogue1020502"]="I only know as much as you. Just moments ago, there was a huge earthquake on the island, and countless undead monsters came charging in. They left complete chaos and scores of injured civilians in their wake! After the earthquake, I started healing all the survivors I could find. I really hope everyone will be alright!",
    ["Dialogue1020503"]="Don't worry, I believe they have the ability to protect themselves. I'm sure everyone is trying to protect the island. But there are so many people who need help and I'm all alone. Could you help me by <color=#CA2E0AFF>taking these bandages and tending to the injured islanders</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1020601"]="Finally! Someone useful! Being stuck with all-brawn-and-no-brain here is driving me up the wall!",
    ["Dialogue1020602"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...All brawn? No brain? If I'm all brawn, that means...</color></size>\n<size=18>Hmm... </size><size=18>That's not a very nice thing to say about someone who's just arrived.</size><size=18></size>",
    ["Dialogue1020603"]="...I'm talking about you! <size=24>You numskull!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020604"]="Hmph! As you can see, I... and I guess Melbrun here as well... have been evacuating the residents and getting rid of the undead monsters. Most of the residents have been safely evacuated but the monsters just keep coming! There are so many of them; it's driving me mad! Your timing couldn't be better! Quick, help us get rid of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>roaming Pirate Skeletons</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1020701"]="<size=18>It's alright, I guess... You may not be an instructor, but at least you're a living person.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020702"]="I... <size=24>Who says I'm hiding!</size>\nI was just concealing my presence and preparing to ambush the undead monsters! Don't assume I'm like <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color>! Those two may look tough on the outside, but when the chips were down, they abandoned their comrade!",
    ["Dialogue1020703"]="Huh? Where did Yadrew and Charles go? Why are you looking for them? It's obvious that it'd be safer to stick with me; I'm waaay stronger than them!",
    ["Dialogue1020704"]="Alright, alright... If you must know, they're probably at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>port</color>. We were near the port when the incident happened. We saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>huge ship</color> hit the port in the fog and cause an earthquake. Right after that, undead monsters came pouring out of the ship.",
    ["Dialogue1020705"]="Yadrew shouted \"Stop them!\" and then took off for the port. Then Charles... I tried to stop him but he followed Yadrew. So I... Let me make it clear, I'm not hiding here because I didn't follow them. No wait, I mean, I was setting up an ambush here!",
    ["Dialogue1020706"]="Ha! Didn't I tell you it'd be safer to stick with me? I don't mind taking you under my wing... Wait!\n<size=24>Don't leave me here! I can't defeat all the undead by myself! Hey!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020801"]="As the undead army retreated, the fog around the port dissipated. This Haze looks like a plot by the Corsair! It might even be related to the power of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. I'm afraid this isn't the end. As long as the Corsair still has the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>, I believe that undead army will rise again!",
    ["Dialogue1020802"]="We should make the first move to get the Fragment of Ymir's Heart back!",
    ["Dialogue1020803"]="Ho hoho! The enthusiasm of youth! I intend to put together an <color=#CA2E0AFF>expedition squad to fight the Corsair</color>. But we lack battle experience against the undead. It would be hard for us to win if we were to head to their base unprepared.",
    ["Dialogue1020804"]="Ho hoho! The greatest advantage of being old is that I've had many opportunities to make friends who can offer help in times of need! One of my old friends is the world-renowned <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Sage</color>. He's fought in many a battle against the undead, and has more experience of fighting them than anybody else.",
    ["Dialogue1020805"]="...Great Sage...? <size=24>Could it be...Kroneika?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1020806"]="Haha! You guessed it, Charles! Yes, it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika Heines</color>! Young adventurer, I officially commission you to take my request to Great Sage Kroneika. I heard that since he passed responsibility for the clan to his son, he's been living in seclusion in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1020807"]="The Mjolnir Mountains are some distance from Izlude Island. I'll get Charles to send you there using <color=#CA2E0AFF>transportation magic</color>. When you're ready to set off, simply <color=#CA2E1AFF>talk to Charles</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1020901"]="Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue1020902"]="Then please step into center of the magic circle.",
    ["Dialogue1020903"]="......",
    ["Dialogue1021001"]="<size=18>Sigh, this is terrible! Why did the mine suddenly collapse? It's bad enough that we had to stop work, but lots of my fellow miners were injured as well. Boss Rorke said he's <color=#CA2E0AFF>going to ask the Great Sage who lives at the top of the mountain</color> for help. I wonder where he is now?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1021002"]="Hmm? Who are you? Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue1021003"]="Huh? The name of the Great Sage? ...The Great Sage is the Great Sage!\n<size=18>But Boss Rorke did call him \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika</color>\" or something like that.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1021101"]="Excuse me, adventurer. I'm trying to make my way up the mountain, but there are so many Creamies along the way. I... Ever since the accident at the mine, bug-like monsters have started appearing everywhere. I can't help but shudder whenever I see bugs now. Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>eliminate all these Creamies</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue1021201"]="Phew, the world is at peace once again. Thank you very much! My name's Rorke, owner of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Wings Mine</color>. You might have already heard, but my mine collapsed!",
    ["Dialogue1021202"]="I've come to ask the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Sage</color> to help heal the injured workers. You... Are you headed for top of the mountain as well? Could I make a bold request?",
    ["Dialogue1021203"]="A great adventurer like you should have no problem dealing with the monsters on the mountain, right? Could I hire you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort me to the top</color>? Don't worry! I'm not asking you to work for free! When we arrive, I'll pay you a huge sum of Zeny!",
    ["Dialogue1021301"]="(Bidal looks at you with suspicion.)\nThere aren't many who can reach here with such ease. Why have you come?",
    ["Dialogue1021302"]="...You're here to see Kroneika? Well... I'm sorry, but he's away right now. He went to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> to carry out some investigations yesterday. I wish I could help, but Kroneika ordered me to stay here and stop anyone from entering the forest.",
    ["Dialogue1021303"]="(Bidal looks worried.)\nNot long ago, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange wave of magic</color> came from deep within the forest. Kroneika suspected that the seal there has <color=#CA2E0AFF>weakened</color> and decided to investigate, but he's still not back yet. Could he have run into difficulty?",
    ["Dialogue1021304"]="Still not back yet? Who else can help treat the injured miners?",
    ["Dialogue1021305"]="(Bidal looks at you with gratitude.)\nI'd be very grateful if you could check on Kroneika for me! But this forest is enchanted with a very strong <color=#CA2E0AFF>spatial magic</color>; the paths will <color=#CA2E0AFF>lead you to unexpected places</color>. Please be careful after you <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Labyrinth Forest</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1021401"]="...It's you! I was wondering who was sneaking around behind me.",
    ["Dialogue1021402"]="Me? Um... I'm... I'm here because I heard there are really strong monsters in this forest, and wanted to challenge them! Why are you here though?",
    ["Dialogue1021403"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Great Sage? Could it be that old man?</color></size>\nAhem! Oh! So you're looking for the Great Sage! He's probably trapped somewhere by the spatial magic! But all you have to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>light up this sealstone</color> and the correct path will appear. There are a total of <color=#CA2E0AFF>four of these stones</color> in the forest. But to light them all up, you have to meet some really strange conditions.",
    ["Dialogue1021404"]="(Ygnizem whispers in your ear.)\n<size=18>For example, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Sealstone</color> requires the blood of a thousand virgins...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1021405"]="Hehe! I can't believe you actually fell for it! These sealstones were created by a witch but there's nothing evil about them! All you need to do to light up the Red Sealstone is offer it <color=#CA2E0AFF>some witch flowers</color>. Look, those flowers there are just what you need! Go pick some!",
    ["Dialogue1021501"]="Hehe! These are my favorite. I mean, these witch flowers are so colorful! The witch would be very pleased!",
    ["Dialogue1021502"]="...How could you say such a thing about a lady?! This is just the way I am! Come on, back to the matter at hand. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the witch flowers in front of the Red Sealstone</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1021601"]="That's it! If my guess is correct, now that the Red Sealstone has been lit, the spatial magic around this area should be lifted. I still have other important matters to attend to, so you're on your own now! See ya!",
    ["Dialogue1021602"]="The correct path? There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign</color> just there?! Can't you read?",
    ["Dialogue1021701"]="Huh, you again? Are you... <size=24>following me?</size>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Wait... This might not be such a bad thing!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1021702"]="Ahem! Since you're here, why not help me out for a bit? Do you hear that buzzing sound? It sends chills down my spine! It's been a thousand years and those disgusting Steel Chonchons are still in the forest! They are so annoying!",
    ["Dialogue1021703"]="Huh? Did I say \"a thousand years\"? Erm... You must have misheard! In any case, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>get rid of those annoying Steel Chonchons</color>! I don't want to see them for even a second longer!",
    ["Dialogue1021801"]="<size=18>Hehe! The spatial magic around the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blue Sealstone</color> has been lifted too!</size>\n...Hey kiddo, stop following me, you hear? Let's part ways now, goodbye!",
    ["Dialogue1021901"]="<size=24>Hey! </size><size=24>Didn't I tell you to stop following me?!</size>\nI can't light this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Sealstone</color> up and am feeling pretty peeved right now. Could you please just leave me alone?",
    ["Dialogue1021902"]="...What? You need to lift the spatial magic around this area in order to find the Great Sage? Erm...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>It would be a waste not to take advantage of this free labor.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1021903"]="...Forget it. Come help then! To light this Green Sealstone up, we'll need enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>life seeds</color>. You should be able to get them from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cocos</color> around here. Go collect some!",
    ["Dialogue1022001"]="Ah yes! This should be enough life seeds! The next step is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bury them under the Green Sealstone</color>. Just watch; they'll grow into beautiful flowers in no time!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The resilience of life so amazing! Hehe!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1022101"]="Alright, the spatial magic around this area has been lifted as well. My gut feeling tells me that the old... Great Sage that you're looking for is <color=#CA2E0AFF>at the end of that path on the opposite side</color>. Hurry along now! And remember, don't follow me. Or else you'll feel the witch— I mean, my wrath!",
    ["Dialogue1022102"]="Huh? Did someone just say something? The wind in the forest is so strong; I'm must be hearing things... Bye, then!",
    ["Dialogue1022201"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Those wretched vines! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I couldn't destroy them from the inside. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd been stuck here so long; </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>it was most frustrating.</color></size>\nAdventurer, thank you for your help.",
    ["Dialogue1022202"]="...Oh? So you're Mainz's student and you've come to ask for my help? I have to say, it's rare that there's ever a problem that Mainz can't solve.",
    ["Dialogue1022203"]="But it's not safe here. We'll talk more once we get back to safety. More importantly, we need to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>witch</color> who trapped me here.",
    ["Dialogue1022204"]="That's right, I entered Labyrinth Forest because I wanted to investigate the strange wave of magic, but fell into the witch's trap and couldn't escape the vines. I only let my guard down because the witch possessed the body of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young swordswoman</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1022205"]="That swordswoman is your friend? Adventurer, I think you have been deceived as well. She may look like your friend, but the soul within that body belongs to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Evelyn, the witch who was sealed in Labyrinth Forest</color> a thousand years ago. But it's not your fault. Evelyn has always been sly. If she wants to deceive someone, even I would not be safe.",
    ["Dialogue1022206"]="What? The witch has already lit three sealstones? ...That must be the reason for the wave of magic in the forest. There's only <color=#CA2E0AFF>one sealstone left</color> to light now. Whatever her objective may be, we <color=#CA2E0AFF>have to stop her from lighting the last one</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1022301"]="Urgh... What... what happened...? What am I doing here?",
    ["Dialogue1022302"]="...Took over my body?! Oh no! <size=24>She didn't do anything horrible to me, did she?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1022303"]="Hey! What do you mean \"took over\" your body? I merely \"borrowed\" it for a bit to save myself! If I'd known helping Merlin would land me in this state, I wouldn't have helped him with the seal a thousand years ago! My soul ended up being trapped by the four sealstones along with the monsters for all this time!",
    ["Dialogue1022304"]="And then <size=24>everything was ruined</size> because you showed up and interrupted my spell!",
    ["Dialogue1022305"]="Hmph! But there's no need to worry. After all, I'm a witch. It will take more than a little interruption to destroy my magic. Although I did accidentally summon some Devilings, at least...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>at least I didn't summon anything worse.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1022306"]="Alright, now that this is settled, there's no need to discuss it any further. Evelyn, since you're free now, you're on your own. Adventurer, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Mjolnir Mountains</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1022307"]="Hmph! You may have helped me, but don't think you'll be getting anything in return! If destiny allows, we'll meet again!",
    ["Dialogue1022308"]="Although I don't have any memory of what happened, I know you're the one who helped get my body back! Thank you! I intend to continue my training in the forest. I'll definitely be stronger by the time we meet again!",
    ["Dialogue1022401"]="We can finally speak now. So tell me, what happened on Izlude Island?",
    ["Dialogue1022402"]="...What? I can't stand by and ignore that. Let's go help Mainz.",
    ["Dialogue1022403"]="But... Kroneika, Golden Wings Mine collapsed and its owner, Rorke, is asking for your help <color=#CA2E0AFF>treating the injured miners</color>. I asked for details, and it seems they've been infected with monster toxins that are preventing their wounds from healing. Without your help, I'm afraid they'll never recover.",
    ["Dialogue1022404"]="That's a relatively simple problem. I'll go and make some preparations. Adventurer, could you bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vital Flowers</color>? They can be found <color=#CA2E0AFF>next to the hut</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1022501"]="I've just finished making the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Panacea</color>. Now it just needs to <color=#CA2E0AFF>distributed to the injured miners</color>. Once they take it, their injuries will heal in no time. I'm trusting you with this task, adventurer. I'll use the time you're away to make preparations for our trip.",
    ["Dialogue1022601"]="Wow! You're so tall. I'm jealous! If I was as strong as you, I could have helped my dad instead of just doing nothing.",
    ["Dialogue1022602"]="My dad owns Golden Wings Mine! Ever since the mine collapsed, he's been sighing a lot. His hairline's even receded a bit.",
    ["Dialogue1022603"]="I think that my dad must have been scared by the huge Stainers that came out of the ground. He's always been SUPER afraid of bugs! Um... So can you help us <color=#CA2E1AFF>get rid of those Stainers in the mine</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1022701"]="Wh-what? The bugs have all been eliminated? <size=24>That's great!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1022702"]="Oh? The miners have been treated by the Great Sage too? Amazing! I've got to pull myself together and rebuild Golden Wings Mine! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>send my thanks to the Great Sage</color>. If there's anything I can help with in the future, anything at all, just let me know!",
    ["Dialogue1022801"]="My preparations for Izlude Island are complete. If you're ready, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me into the center of the teleport circle</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1022802"]="Let's go then!",
    ["Dialogue1022803"]="We don't have much time. Don't dilly-dally!",
    ["Dialogue1022901"]="Ho hoho! You didn't disappoint! This is definitely the strongest squad in Criatura Academy. Of course, that would include my old friend, Great Sage Kroneika!",
    ["Dialogue1022902"]="...You still prattle on as much as you did 10 years ago. Your student has filled me in on the situation; let's cut the chitchat and get moving!",
    ["Dialogue1022903"]="Ho hoho! You haven't changed one bit either, Kroneika. Well then, young adventurer, go speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Carew</color>; he's waiting for us by the harbor. We'll need his experience on this journey!",
    ["Dialogue1023001"]="As the safety of Izlude Island is at stake, I'll do my very best to keep you safe on this voyage! If everything is ready, we can set sail right away!",
    ["Dialogue1023002"]="Well then, let's go!",
    ["Dialogue1023003"]="Sure, talk to me again when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue1023101"]="You're awake.",
    ["Dialogue1023102"]="...There was an accident. A huge tentacle came out of the water and dragged us to the bottom. You were hit by a broken mast and passed out. Thanks to Captain Carew, we managed to survive, but it looks like we're stuck on this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shipwreck</color> for now.",
    ["Dialogue1023103"]="No doubt about it, this is the Corsair's base! We're safe in the cabin for now, but we still have to be very careful. Also, I have some bad news: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Melbrun</color> got separated from us. This whole area has a strange aura; we need to ensure that they're safe as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue1023104"]="While you were unconscious, Kroneika tried to sense their location using magic but the undead aura is too strong for his magic to work properly. The only thing we can do now is <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up and search</color> for clues.",
    ["Dialogue1023201"]="By Odin! You've found me at last! Did you see those terrifying Roda Frogs? If I'd known boarding this shipwreck would mean sharing with them, I'd have chosen to freeze to death in the sea. Luckily you came along!",
    ["Dialogue1023202"]="I-I'm too scared to move. <size=24>Ahhh! They're jumping over this way! </size><size=26>They're going to eat me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1023203"]="These cold-blooded monsters really are the most terrifying creatures in the world. Please <color=#CA2E1AFF>get rid of the Roda Frogs around here</color> for me. Otherwise I'll be too afraid to set foot out of here!",
    ["Dialogue1023301"]="Phew! Great! I'm back to being the quick, agile Melbrun that everyone knows and loves! Haha!",
    ["Dialogue1023302"]="Come to think of it... While I was hiding from the Roda Frogs, I think I heard <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice scream</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next cabin</color>. But I'm too scared check it out. What if those cold-blooded monsters are in there too? Please could you go instead?",
    ["Dialogue1023401"]="Why are you here?",
    ["Dialogue1023402"]="So the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color> transported you here too? You might have already realized, but this is no longer the Corsair's shipwreck. I've been trying to find a way back, but this spirit has been harassing me since I got here.",
    ["Dialogue1023403"]="He thinks I'm a sailor on this ship. No matter how hard I try to explain, he won't let me leave. And to make things worse, I lost my <color=#CA2E0AFF>staff</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1023501"]="Thanks for finding my staff! Things will be much easier now! I've been observing the spirit while I've been trapped here; he seems to have been affected by some evil power, and it's made him confused. I could help him back to his senses, but I need a place that can give me Odin's power first.",
    ["Dialogue1023502"]="...Ah, this ship should have a prayer room! I need to find it and make some preparations. Can you help me get out of here?",
    ["Dialogue1023503"]="Spirits are afraid of flashes of bright light. I see you have <color=#CA2E0AFF>camera</color>. If you could <color=#CA2E0AFF>make flashes of light</color> to dazzle the spirit, it would really help!",
    ["Dialogue1023601"]="<size=24>Ahhhh! What was that flash? What did you do to me?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1023602"]="...Hold on, where's my sailor?! No one is allow to break the rules on this ship! I must find her... I will not allow any sailor to abandon their post!",
    ["Dialogue1023701"]="Hmph! At least there's still one person taking their work seriously! Well done, sailor! Of course we mustn't allow this ship to be soiled!",
    ["Dialogue1023702"]="What did you say? You saw the sailor sneak into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>prayer room</color>? Take me to her! I'll show her the consequences of disobeying the first mate!",
    ["Dialogue1023801"]="Thank you, and... I'm very sorry for all the trouble I've caused.",
    ["Dialogue1023802"]="I've regained my memories from when I was still alive. This ship belongs to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson Fleet</color>. I took us out to sea as usual, but we encountered a <color=#CA2E1AFF>strange fog</color>. Just as I was giving the orders to furl the sails and adjust the rudder, a terrifying ship suddenly appeared! What happened next was a nightmare.",
    ["Dialogue1023803"]="After that, I seemed to be drifting in and out of consciousness; it was as if my soul was floating around in endless darkness. Thank you for saving me from that terrible existence. As thanks, I'll try to send you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>a safe place nearby</color>. But I have one small request. If you ever happen to meet the Alson Fleet's leader, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson</color>, please let him know, \"Hobbe says goodbye.\"",
    ["Dialogue1023901"]="This ship will be completely submerged soon. There's nothing more here for the living. Let me send you to safety.",
    ["Dialogue1023902"]="May the stars light your way!",
    ["Dialogue1023903"]="Time is running out; please stop hesitating.",
    ["Dialogue1024001"]="(Alice looks around and frowns.)\nHold up, this isn't Izlude Island. We need to find out where we are before we can plan our next move. Let's talk to that <color=#CA2E0AFF>old man by the harbor</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1024101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The strange fog has dispersed, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but why haven't the merchant ships returned? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could Hobbe and his crew have sailed into difficulty?</color></size>\nSigh...",
    ["Dialogue1024102"]="Hi, young adventurer. I'm Alson, leader of Alberta's famed <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson Fleet</color>. All the ships you see in this harbor belong to me. There's no one at sea who doesn't know my name.",
    ["Dialogue1024103"]="What? Poor Hobbe... By Odin, this is devastating. Did the rest of the ships get wrecked as well? What could have caused such a strange phenomenon?",
    ["Dialogue1024104"]="I see, so the undead monsters at sea are responsible! Since you and your friends are going after those monsters, please allow me to help. I'll provide you with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>boat</color>. It's docked at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>port</color>. You can go aboard speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zoe</color> anytime; she'll take you to your friends out at sea!",
    ["Dialogue1024201"]="This is great! Since Alson's agreed to lend us a boat, let's go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>regroup with the expedition squad on the Shipwreck</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1024301"]="I've received Alson's instructions! Let's set sail while the waters are still calm!",
    ["Dialogue1024302"]="I'm gonna go full speed ahead! Hang on tight!",
    ["Dialogue1024303"]="Alright, I'll check on the boat again.",
    ["Dialogue1024401"]="Please help me. I don't want to hurt anybody. Like the rest of the spirits on this ship, I'm a captive of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corsair</color>. He <color=#CA2E0AFF>stole our memories</color> and took control of our souls. None of us can break free, unless... unless we can recover our memories.",
    ["Dialogue1024402"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Zombies</color> are roaming the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deck</color>. Get the ring from them. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Ring</color> is more important than even my life. If you get it back, I'll be able to recover my memories.",
    ["Dialogue1024403"]="This spirit looks like he's in pain; we can't just ignore him. How about this? I'll head back and explain the situation to Dean Mainz while you stay here and help. When you're done, you can come and regroup with us.",
    ["Dialogue1024501"]="I remember everything now! Thank you, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1024502"]="My name's Anna; I used to be mage. If fate had been kinder to me, I would have tied the knot with my fiancé, <color=#CA2E1AFF>Lukas</color>. We would have had a happy life together, but it wasn't to be... On the day of our wedding, that horrendous undead, the <color=#CA2E1AFF>Corsair</color>, appeared! He attacked our ship and took the <color=#CA2E1AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1024503"]="Even now, I can clearly remember his beaming smile as he put the ring on my finger! But I also vividly remember the look of pain on his face as he shielded me from the Corsair's attacks.",
    ["Dialogue1024504"]="Adventurer, you cannot imagine how much I hate the Corsair and how much I yearn to see Lukas once more! I'm pleading with you. Please, <color=#CA2E1AFF>help me find my Lukas</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1024505"]="I understand you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>regroup with your friends on the ship</color> first. I'll make the necessary arrangements while you're gone, and wait for you on the upper deck!",
    ["Dialogue1024506"]="Lukas chanced upon the fragment during his adventures and gave it to me as a present. He used the power within the fragment to turn it into a beautiful rose-shaped wedding ring.",
    ["Dialogue1024507"]="After our deaths, the wedding ring which carried our vows became a vessel to seal memories. And the last thing I saw before I died was the Corsair turning my beloved into a skeleton.",
    ["Dialogue1024601"]="Alice told me what happened. I'm glad you made it back in one piece. While the two of you were away, the expedition squad eradicated all the monsters on the lower deck of the Shipwreck!",
    ["Dialogue1024602"]="Ho hoho! They've just finished this with level; now Kroneika's leading them up to deal with the undead on the next level. Alice and I are just about to head over to support them. Hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>upper deck</color> and keep your promise to Anna! Regroup with us when you're done!",
    ["Dialogue1024701"]="I need to release the power within the Rose Ring in order to find Lukas. But the power will attract the nearby Skel Pirates, and I won't be able to defend myself while performing the ritual. Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>eliminate the Skel Pirates</color> and protect me until I complete the ritual?",
    ["Dialogue1024801"]="Thank you for helping Anna and I reunite in death! For such a long time, my soul was filled with nothing but resentment. But being reunited with Anna has washed all that resentment away! All I feel now is endless happiness!",
    ["Dialogue1024802"]="You intend to kill the Corsair? To avenge us? If I were still alive, I'd kill him with my own hands!",
    ["Dialogue1024803"]="I may have lost the ability to kill him, but I can still help you find where he is on the ship. Anna, let's release the power in the Rose Ring! We'll use its link with the Fragment of Ymir's Heart to guide this brave adventurer <color=#CA2E1AFF>to the Corsair</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1024901"]="The ritual is completed. We've marked out a route on the deck. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow the markings</color> and you'll find the Corsair. Before we disappear, Lukas and I will try to help the other spirits recover their memories. Now go, adventurer, put an end to Corsair's evil!",
    ["Dialogue1025001"]="Finally found you! I think this is probably the Corsair's hiding place. The Skel Pirates guarding the upper deck have all been eliminated. Now let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>put an end to that undead scoundrel</color> once and for all!",
    ["Dialogue1025002"]="Let's work together. For the peace of Izlude Island!",
    ["Dialogue1025003"]="For the innocent people who lost their lives.",
    ["Dialogue1025004"]="For... erm... for 100% to become a 101%!",
    ["Dialogue1025005"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>For treasure that he might have hidden somewhere!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1025006"]="......",
    ["Dialogue1025007"]="There's no time, let's move.",
    ["Dialogue1025101"]="Ho hoho! I declare this expedition a success! We will take the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and return with honor! Hurry, let's share the good news with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Carew</color>; he's waiting for us on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>lower deck</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1025201"]="Oh yeah, I can see the success in your eyes! I'd love to give each and every one of you a big hug, but I stink of algae. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back to Izlude Island</color>. I need to take a bath! Haha! Well then, are you ready to return?",
    ["Dialogue1025202"]="Excellent! Anchors aweigh!",
    ["Dialogue1025203"]="I suppose you need a moment to process everything that's just happened?",
    ["Dialogue1025301"]="Great work, everyone! Thanks again for your hard work! This expedition has shown me the importance of bravery, determination, kindness, and selflessness. And it's exactly because all of you possess these outstanding qualities that peace has been restored to Izlude Island and the surrounding waters!",
    ["Dialogue1025302"]="Since the Undead at sea have been eliminated, I've fulfilled the purpose of this trip. A peaceful retirement seems like wishful thinking, but it's good to stay in shape.",
    ["Dialogue1025303"]="Now then, young adventurer, do you know what needs to be done next?",
    ["Dialogue1025304"]="Correct. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> and place this Fragment of Ymir's Heart onto the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1025401"]="I didn't expect you to bring back <color=#CA2E0AFF>a second Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> so quickly. I can feel the power within me start to stir, and it's all because of your hard work.",
    ["Dialogue1025402"]="However, there are still Fragments of Ymir's Heart out there. The path that lies before you will be long and hard. There will be enemies who are even more cunning and temptations that are even harder to resist. I need you to tell me again, successor of Odin's bloodline, will you still have the same determination as you have now, regardless of the hardships that lie ahead?",
    ["Dialogue1025403"]="Very good, successor of Odin'e bloodline. I have already located the third <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. It's in the southern part of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom, in a town called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc</color>. This fragment contains very strong <color=#CA2E0AFF>fire element</color> and its power is almost fully activated. This will be a very dangerous journey. Be careful.",
    ["Dialogue1025501"]="Alberta? If I remember correctly, it's very far from Izlude Island, probably on the other side of the continent. We're traveling that far?!",
    ["Dialogue1025502"]="Do you even have to ask? Of course we have to go back to the Shipwreck! Dean Mainz and the rest of the squad need us! But it will take too much time if we travel by sea. There's no other choice; we have to return to the Treasure Ship!",
    ["Dialogue1025503"]="Didn't that first mate's spirit tell us that the Treasure Ship was sucked into the dimensional gap? That means if we can be transported here from the Shipwreck, we should be able to return to the Shipwreck from here.",
    ["Dialogue1025504"]="Alice and I need to discuss how we can utilize the space-time turbulence on the Treasure Ship. Could you replenish the supplies for us? Orange Potions are a must-have.",
    ["Dialogue1025601"]="These potions are enough. Let's return to the Treasure Ship.",
    ["Dialogue1025701"]="Before Alice and I were sucked in to the dimensional gap, we were both lured near to it by some strange monsters. They were translucent and looked kind of like floating white sheets with horrible faces.",
    ["Dialogue1025702"]="I think if we want to find the dimensional gap on the Treasure Ship, we'll have to find those monsters first. Maybe we can ask the first mate's spirit. He might know something about where they came from.",
    ["Dialogue1025801"]="Why are you back here?",
    ["Dialogue1025803"]="White, translucent monsters? You mean Whispers? They're everywhere on the ship. Can't you see them? ...Ah, I forgot. Most living beings are unable to see them.",
    ["Dialogue1025804"]="Let me teach you a way to see them. You can find them by using your camera. Whispers hate camera flashes even more than normal spirits. So if you were to take photos of them, they'll be so peeved that they'll materialize.",
    ["Dialogue1025901"]="You found the Whispers and opened the dimensional gap? Excellent! Quick, take us there!",
    ["Dialogue1026001"]="It's great that you're all safe. I was so worried.",
    ["Dialogue1026002"]="We weren't just lazing around while you were gone. Charles has already located the exact location of the evil aura on this ship. The nearest focus is on the deck, by the broken bow. Can you go investigate?",
    ["Dialogue1026101"]="I feel it... A holy power that's completely different from the Shipwreck. This reminds me of something from the past.",
    ["Dialogue1026102"]="I'm just like the other spirits on this ship. We're all captives of Drake. He took our names and our memories so that we can never escape his control.",
    ["Dialogue1026103"]="Please help me... Adventurer... Please help me find my past. Only then can my soul be cleansed. One of the Axe-wielding Skel Pirates on the 2nd level of the Shipwreck took a Rose Ring that contains my memories. Please get it back for me.",
    ["Dialogue1026201"]="Thank you, adventurer! I have recovered all my memories. My name is Anna; I'm a mage from Geffen. This Rose Ring was given to me by my beloved, Lukas, as a wedding gift. It is very important to me.",
    ["Dialogue1026202"]="Lukas and I had planned to hold our wedding right after our voyage, but Drake attacked our ship. In order to protect me, Lukas let Drake take his soul and turn his body into a Skel Pirate.",
    ["Dialogue1026203"]="Drake trapped his soul and my memories into this Rose Ring. All we have to do now is to find Lukas' body and I'll be able to rouse him.",
    ["Dialogue1026204"]="Once again, thank you. But there's one more thing that needs to be done before we go to find Lukas. Take this scroll and use it on the tentacles behind my back.",
    ["Dialogue1026301"]="I can finally embrace and protect my beloved with these hands again! And it's all thanks to you, adventurer! But... there are still many spirits who are enslaved.",
    ["Dialogue1026302"]="You want to eliminate Drake and save all the enslaved spirits on this ship? Great minds think alike! It's through the Kraken's power that Drake can control everyone.",
    ["Dialogue1026303"]="The giant squid can bewitch spirits with its eye, but its eye is also its weakness. I've noticed that it watches us from the cracks on the deck. In order to defeat it, we must attack its eye.",
    ["Dialogue1026401"]="The evil aura that enshrouded the Shipwreck is dispersing. Looks like the Kraken is out of our way now. All that's left to take care of is Drake!",
    ["Dialogue1026402"]="You have friends? That's great! We can bring Drake down together! Not just for you, but for us to regain freedom. Please convey my wish to your friends. I'll be waiting for you in front of Drake's cabin.",
    ["Dialogue1026501"]="Charles told me that the evil aura around the ship has completely disappeared. Was it you? The rate that you're growing is astonishing!",
    ["Dialogue1026502"]="There are still so many souls on the Shipwreck that need to be saved? Then what are we waiting for? Let's go to the Captain's Cabin now!",
    ["Dialogue1026601"]="Now that peace has been restored, we should return to Izlude Island. I think you'll need some time to bid your new friends farewell, right? We'll wait for you where Captain Carew is.",
    ["Dialogue1026701"]="We've regained our freedom now that Drake has been obliterated. And it's all thanks to you, adventurer. You saved everyone on this ship.",
    ["Dialogue1026702"]="We will soon rest in peace. Bless you and goodbye.",
    ["Dialogue1026801"]="You're back. Looks like the mission for this journey has been a success. If you're ready, we'll set off.",
    ["Dialogue1026802"]="Let's go then!",
    ["Dialogue1026803"]="Well then, talk to me again when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue1026901"]="There's one more thing you need to do. Place this Fragment of Ymir's Heart onto the Heart Pedestal. Go on, child.",
    ["Dialogue1027001"]="Thank you for bringing back the second Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Channel the power of Odin within you into the fragment once more so that I can sense the locations of the remaining fragments.",
    ["Dialogue1027101"]="(The Weather Observer is working fine. Nothing seems out of order.)",
    ["Dialogue1027201"]="(There are some messy footprints on the ground. They seem to be heading forward.)",
    ["Dialogue1027301"]="(The staff on the ground belongs to Alice. If her weapon is here, she should be nearby?)",
    ["Dialogue1027401"]="(These floating specks of light seem to be guiding me. They must be the markings that Anna told me about.)",
    ["Dialogue1030101"]="Wow! It's been so long since an adventurer visited Morroc! I have to provide the best customer service!\nThank you for using Kafra services! Kafra Corporation will only ever provide you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue1030102"]="Oh, you heard that?\nLet me explain. The number of adventurers visiting Morroc has decreased drastically, so much so that our sales team has been pretty relaxed. But don't worry! This definitely won't affect the quality of our service!",
    ["Dialogue1030103"]="I don't know the reason. You could try asking the sheriff! Morroc is administered by the Lugenburg Family, one of the seven royal families. Currently, the person at the helm is none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maximilian Lugenburg</color>! They say everything goes through him; he should have the most accurate information!",
    ["Dialogue1030201"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'm mad... So mad! How dare Rocky blow me off! Just because he had a few lucky wins, he thinks he can disregard me?!</color></size>\nWho are you? Are you here to spar with me?",
    ["Dialogue1030202"]="Why would anything strange happen in Morroc? <size=24>No one would dare make trouble under the iron fist of the Lugenburg Family</size>!",
    ["Dialogue1030203"]="I already told you, nothing strange has happened! If you're really curious, go and check the streets for yourself. This place is crawling with information peddlers.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Wait a minute... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Maybe I can use this opportunity to rattle Rocky!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1030204"]="Ahem, listen. There's a very well-known <color=#CA2E0AFF>information peddler</color> who lives <color=#CA2E0AFF>just outside Morroc</color>. He knows everything about this place; why don't you pay him a visit?!",
    ["Dialogue1030205"]="If anything is truly strange, it would have to be my old friend, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocky</color>. He suddenly became very busy for no apparent reason. No matter how many people I send his way, he'll have some excuse to not meet me! He never behaved like this before. I just don't understand, what could be more important than sparring?",
    ["Dialogue1030301"]="(The information peddler looks at you warily.)\n...Not many people in Morroc know where I live. How did you find your way here?",
    ["Dialogue1030302"]="What? Someone told you I have information about Morroc? ...Let's not talk about the intentions of that \"kind person\" yet. But yes, I do have some information on strange happenings around Morroc. However, fair trade is the basis of a business. I'm not going to just hand something over without getting anything in return! If you want something, you'll have to give something.",
    ["Dialogue1030303"]="Go get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Cactus</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mukas</color> nearby. Don't let the spikes fool you. When properly prepared, it becomes a delicious ingredient!",
    ["Dialogue1030401"]="Not bad, you're pretty good! As a trade, I'll give you one piece of information: As you can see, Morroc is a desert town and doesn't have much water or resources of its own. It used to be that survival was made possible by traveling trade caravans that brought a constant stream of supplies. However, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the number of trade caravans has greatly decreased</color> recently, causing residents to fear that there will be a lack of food and water.",
    ["Dialogue1030402"]="(The information peddler winks at you slyly.)\nThe reason for the decreasing number of trade caravans? That would be considered another piece of information! I've told you before, I won't give away anything for free. If you want more answers, go get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Huge Pepopeco Eggs</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1030501"]="Not bad, not bad at all! You're pretty agile! Here's the answer to your question. The caravans might not be coming because of the strange weather that Morroc is currently experiencing. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>temperatures around Morroc have been soaring</color>. Even the locals who grew up in the desert are starting to find it unbearable; just imagine the effect it would have on traders who need to keep traveling around the desert.",
    ["Dialogue1030502"]="(The information peddler winks at you slyly.)\nThere's an extra price for the next piece of information! If you want to continue talking to me, bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chewy Grasshopper Legs</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Metallers</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1030601"]="Wonderful! Don't underestimate these Grasshopper Legs. Now that resources are scarce, they're considered a delicacy! I'll continue to answer you now. According to reliable sources, the rising temperature in Morroc has got something to do with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange force fields</color> that have been appearing in the desert.",
    ["Dialogue1030602"]="Hoho! You've finally learned the ways of us desert dwellers! The heat hasn't only turned the trade caravans away, it's also caused the Anacondaqs in the desert to become abnormally active. In order to survive, the locals have no choice but to venture into the desert to search for any food they can find, but the Anacondaqs pose a serious threat to their safety.",
    ["Dialogue1030603"]="If you want more information from me, go eliminate the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anacondaqs</color> that are roaming around!",
    ["Dialogue1030701"]="Hmm... I must say I'm impressed. You actually managed to return in one piece. Seems like you're not just some nobody! Thank you for the all the resources. The residents in the slum should be able to make it through these trying times now. I assume there must be a special reason why you're so interested in the strange happenings in Morroc?",
    ["Dialogue1030702"]="...I admire your candor! Since you've been so honest, I'll tell you my real identity!",
    ["Dialogue1030703"]="In fact, the Assassins Guild has been paying close attention to the changes in Morroc's weather. We've found a few locations where the strange force fields appear, but they're not easy to dispel. You mentioned the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. I think it might have something to do with the force fields. Would you like to check it out?",
    ["Dialogue1030704"]="If you're willing to help the Assassins Guild, please accept this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Signal Flare</color>. Use it when you arrive at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hope Oasis</color> located in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>. Once our members see the flare, they'll appear and guide you!",
    ["Dialogue1030705"]="I'm the one everyone calls <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocky the \"Legendary Assassin\"</color>! Maximilian probably sent you to get back at me for missing our sparring sessions, but I'm so glad he did! From the looks of it, I think you might be the key to saving the desert!",
    ["Dialogue1030801"]="(Eremes looks at you warily.)\n...Who are you? How do you know how the assassins communicate?",
    ["Dialogue1030802"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Rocky? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Then I'll give this adventurer the benefit of the doubt.</color></size>\nYou want to investigate the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange force fields</color>? Very well, follow me.",
    ["Dialogue1030901"]="The strange force field here seems to contain <color=#CA2E0AFF>elemental power</color>, but I am unable to dispel it. They say it was first discovered by an <color=#CA2E0AFF>archaeologist</color> called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sean</color>. Maybe he'll have a different perspective. Try speaking to him.",
    ["Dialogue1031001"]="Sigh. Are you here to visit Sean too? I've said this a hundred times before; this makes a hundred and one... <size=24>I am at my wits' end!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1031002"]="As you can see, the heat has caused poor Sean to become delirious. It's been two days now. Heatstroke medicine usually works, but there have been so many heatstroke patients lately that all the medicine's run out! If this continues, I'm afraid even Odin won't be able to save him. Unless... we stray from the traditional method and use a more unorthodox approach!",
    ["Dialogue1031003"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh yeah! Someone's finally asked! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is the perfect chance to test out the remedy! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better make good use of it!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1031004"]="...Ahem! According to reliable records, a legendary doctor from a faraway kingdom developed a heatstroke remedy. The ingredients can be found in the desert. If we can get them, I can make the medicine immediately. It's ideal for our current situation!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hehe! Who would have thought that \"legendary doctor\" would be none other than yours truly!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1031005"]="In any case, this is the only way to save Sean! If you want him to get better, then fetch some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Scorpion Stingers</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hard Stone Hearts</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Scorched Sand Poison Herbs</color> ...Huh? What's with the suspicious look? Never doubt a doctor! Just do as I say!",
    ["Dialogue1031101"]="Hehe! These Scorpion Stingers and Hard Stone Hearts look amazing! Alright, quickly put the Scorched Sand Poison Herbs into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cauldron</color> before the poison wears off!",
    ["Dialogue1031201"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, let me see. What's next...?</color></size>\nAhem! According to reliable records, <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir clockwise</color> for 5 minutes, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir counter-clockwise</color> for another 5 minutes...",
    ["Dialogue1031202"]="Huh? What's with the suspicious look? Never doubt a doctor! Just do as I say!",
    ["Dialogue1031301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...This color, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>this smell... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Erm... Should it look like this? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I think it should, right? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh forget it; </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>the proof of the pudding is in the eating!</color></size>\nAhem! Force it down... I mean, feed it to Sean!",
    ["Dialogue1031302"]="Yes, I'm very sure! Stop hesitating!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I can't wait to record Sean's clinical response!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1031401"]="Bleah... Wh-what did I just drink?! This taste... It's even worse than that Thief Bug Egg I accidentally swallowed in some ancient ruins! Is it even possible for a taste to be so vile that it wakes you up? Is this what they call fighting fire with fire?",
    ["Dialogue1031402"]="What did you say? You saw a strange force field in the desert as well? You're so lucky! Not many people get to see such mystical phenomena! I've always been curious about their appearance in Morroc. Such force fields usually only manifest along with divine power. Unless there's a holy relic like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> around, it's highly unlikely that something like this would happen!",
    ["Dialogue1031403"]="Hoho, you've asked the right person! I've studied force fields for years. Each one has its own elemental attribute. I think that might just be the key to dispelling them. If you can find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>stone artifact that counteracts</color> the attribute and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place it on top of the force field</color>, it should dispel it.",
    ["Dialogue1031404"]="Just remember, <color=#CA2E0AFF>fire counteracts earth, earth counteracts wind, wind counteracts water, and water counteracts fire</color>, then you're good to go.",
    ["Dialogue1031405"]="Oh... Why is my stomach hurting all of a sudden? E-excuse me... <size=24>I-I need to leave for a while!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1031501"]="So... since this force field has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>water attribute</color>, the stone artifact that can counteract it would be—",
    ["Dialogue1031502"]="...Are you kidding?",
    ["Dialogue1031503"]="Not bad. Let's split up. I'll stay here to guard the force field; you go look for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rough Wind</color> to dispel it.",
    ["Dialogue1031601"]="Not too shabby, adventurer. The Water Force Field has been dispelled.",
    ["Dialogue1031602"]="(Eremes looks at you with a puzzled expression.)\nThe Fragment of Ymir's Heart you're looking for isn't here? Maybe try your luck at another force field. There's one in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast corner of the desert</color>; it's guarded by my comrade, Trisse.",
    ["Dialogue1031603"]="I'll report what's happened here to Hassan. Well then, good luck.",
    ["Dialogue1031701"]="Oh no! The ground just collapsed in the southeast corner of the desert! There was a loud bang, then a <color=#CA2E0AFF>terrifying sinkhole</color> with spikes appeared. I could just about see a <color=#CA2E0AFF>woman dressed as an assassin</color> fall in, but I'm too scared to go near it. You go check it out!",
    ["Dialogue1031801"]="This is bad... If Boss Nana Ba finds out I've lost them, he'll disown me and kick me out of the cavern for sure, waka!",
    ["Dialogue1031802"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A hu-human?! Waka?! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why am I so unlucky today? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Meeting two humans in one day... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But this human has come at just the right time! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Might be useful! Waka!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1031803"]="*Wails* Woe is me! Waka! Only Golden Lava knows how much hard work I put in to get those delicacies! But that nasty <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color> took them from me in the blink of an eye! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1031804"]="I'm sure anyone who sees this poor Giearth would step in to help get his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fine Cuisine</color> back. Unless they're the most cold-hearted person in the whole wide world, there's no way they could just ignore his plight! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1031901"]="Heh! You seem kind enough, unlike that <color=#CA2E0AFF>barbaric girl</color>! Waka! I still don't understand. Why would Boss Nana Ba fall in love with a human? It's an honor to marry a Giearth, waka! Yet she's still unsatisfied and wants a lavish wedding, waka?!",
    ["Dialogue1031902"]="The boss only ordered me to go search for those delicacies to make her happy. Just thinking about it makes my blood boil! I'm so mad, steam is gonna come out of my ears! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032001"]="This is bad... If Boss Nana Ba finds out I've lost them, he'll disown me and kick me out of the cavern for sure, waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032002"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A hu-human?! Waka?! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why am I so unlucky today? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Meeting two humans in one day... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But this human has come at just the right time! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Might be useful! Waka!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1032003"]="*Wails* Woe is me! Waka! Only Golden Lava knows how much hard work I put in to get so much wine! But that horrible <color=#CA2E0AFF>Piere</color> took it from me in the blink of an eye! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032004"]="I'm sure anyone who sees this poor Giearth would step in to help get his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fine Wine</color> back. Unless they're the most cold-hearted person in the whole wide world, there's no way they could just ignore his plight! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032101"]="Heh! You're pretty efficient! Waka! Since this fine wine is for a human, it's only right that another human gets it back! I still don't understand. Why would Boss Nana Ba fall in love with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>woman who fell from the sky</color>? And why use such precious wine to make her happy, waka?!",
    ["Dialogue1032102"]="Isn't all the ore he gave her enough? She's greedy! So greedy! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032201"]="This is bad... If Boss Nana Ba finds out I've lost <color=#CA2E0AFF>his precious bride</color>, he'll disown me and kick me out of the cavern for sure, waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032202"]="*Wails* Boss ordered me to guard his bride-to-be, but she said she wanted to prepare a surprise magic trick for the wedding and told me to turn around and not peek, waka.",
    ["Dialogue1032203"]="I waited for a very, very long time before turning back, but all I saw was a note on the ground. It said, \"Surprise! Disappearing act!\" ...If she doesn't come back, I'll be dead meat! Waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032301"]="What? Oh, thank Odin you're not one of those dwarves. You gave me a fright!",
    ["Dialogue1032302"]="How do you know my name?! ...Ah, I know. It must be Eremes who sent you, right? I told him I can handle this mission alone. He just can't stop meddling!",
    ["Dialogue1032303"]="How did you even know?!",
    ["Dialogue1032304"]="Anyway, if I hadn't lost my Katar, I would have showed them who's boss! In the end, I had to rely on my wits. I suggested holding a lavish wedding to buy myself time to escape!",
    ["Dialogue1032305"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>A Great Earth would be able to dispel the Wind Force Field</color>? But where can we find one?...\nAh, I remember now! There was a Great Earth in that dwarf's pocket!",
    ["Dialogue1032306"]="Ahem! No, never mind. I'll make this sacrifice for the sake of the mission! But in order to get the Great Earth, we'll need to make some preparations first. Go pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vertigo Mushrooms</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1032307"]="It was bad enough that I fell into a sinkhole infested with ants, but then a bunch of bearded dwarves suddenly appeared and captured me! The creepiest one even ran up to me to show off his ore and forced me to marry him! Saying something like only my beauty matches up to his wealth.",
    ["Dialogue1032308"]="By the way, while I was hiding, I found the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wind Force Field</color> I was supposed to be guarding! But I have no idea how to dispel it...",
    ["Dialogue1032309"]="...What, why are you looking at me like that? ...No way?! Yo-you want me to go back?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Come to think of it, this might be a good opportunity for revenge!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1032401"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Haha!</color></size> <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is enough Vertigo Mushrooms to knock out a Phreeoni! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Those dwarves won't last five seconds!</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Maybe I should just steal all their ore while they're unconscious! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Treat it as payback!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1032402"]="...Ahem! When the time is right, <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak these Vertigo Mushrooms into the food and drinks at the wedding</color>. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue1032501"]="Human, was it you who escorted my sweetheart back, waka? She must have been so excited about getting married to an eligible bachelor like me that she got lost in the cavern! After all, every girl dreams of marrying someone like me, waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032502"]="I was just thinking about how our wonderful wedding would need a <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness</color>, and then you showed up! Come now. Accept this glorious appointment, waka!",
    ["Dialogue1032601"]="Hmph! These dwarves are as weak as they look! If I'd known, I would have just used my bare hands to make them hand over the Great Earth. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispel the Wind Force Field</color>. I don't want to stay in this nasty cavern any longer!",
    ["Dialogue1032701"]="What? Why did it have to scare us with an illusion?! Now that the force field has been dispelled, do you want to return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Assassins Guild</color> with me? Hassan has been getting us to investigate the force fields. He might have gotten some new information while we were gone!",
    ["Dialogue1032801"]="(Hassan narrows his eyes.)\n...You're the adventurer that Eremes mentioned?",
    ["Dialogue1032802"]="I've heard about your exploits from Rocky and Eremes. If the Fragment of Ymir's Heart you're looking for is causing the force fields, then helping you find it would be of benefit to Morroc. We've already located a third force field. It's just <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside Morroc</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1032901"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is too much. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Three Sand Mirages appearing at the same time? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I won't be able to get any closer to the force field at this rate, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but I can't just leave it. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I should head back to the guild for help.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1032902"]="Hassan sent you to help me? That's great! See if you can place this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Flame Heart</color> on top of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Force Field</color>. I've exhausted myself trying to get past the monsters guarding it. They attack anyone who goes near. Be careful!",
    ["Dialogue1033001"]="Amazing! I don't know how long I would have taken to complete this task by myself.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, this must be the adventurer that Rocky mentioned? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better pass on his message.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1033002"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocky</color> is waiting for you at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Green Tavern</color>. He seems to have some new information about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>last force field</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1033101"]="You sure took your time. I assume you've been told I have some new information. See <color=#CA2E0AFF>McGille the Black Market Merchant</color> by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bar</color>? He seems to know the location of the last force field. I was trying the get the information from him but I accidentally revealed my identity.",
    ["Dialogue1033102"]="I have no idea what his deal is with the Assassins Guild, the moment he heard my name, he became a different person and refused to speak to me anymore! Our only choice now is for you to speak to him. Although I can offer some advice: I've noticed he seems to have a thing for Heflee, the owner of the tavern. That might help you gain his trust somehow.",
    ["Dialogue1033201"]="Sigh. She's so beautiful; I can't stop looking at her. She's a perfect rose that blooms in the desert. Her lips are like fire and her eyes like stars. I feel so blessed even when she ignores me. In fact, I even feel a little excited that she's so cold toward me. But of course, I still hope she'll accept my love for her!",
    ["Dialogue1033202"]="Help me? You're willing to help me get closer to her? ...Wait a minute. Why would a stranger suddenly offer to help? What's your angle?",
    ["Dialogue1033203"]="Why are you putting me down? Have you been sent by a rival for Heflee's affections? Aha! You don't fool me! Go away!",
    ["Dialogue1033204"]="...<size=24>What?</size> You mean, Heflee likes me too?",
    ["Dialogue1033205"]="So you're working with that thief! I don't want anything to do with anyone from the Assassins Guild! Leave me alone!",
    ["Dialogue1033206"]="Hehe! I knew it! How could anyone resist my good looks? I should have known! She was only being cold to me because she's shy! I should have approached her earlier! But I still don't know her very well... Adventurer, if you could find out <color=#CA2E0AFF>what she likes</color>, I'll reward you accordingly!",
    ["Dialogue1033301"]="Huh? You want to know what I like?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Here it comes again... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ever since I opened this tavern, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>there's been no end of people bothering me. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Well, since I'm being asked...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1033302"]="The only thing I like is fine wine! Especially wine that's made from special ingredients that come from monsters! My favorite would be... hmm... a kind of medicated wine that Doctor Wallace mentioned. I think it's called \"Singularity\". It's made from...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me think... What would make someone puke...? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ah! I know!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1033303"]="It's made from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>corpses of Chonchons, Rockers, and Anacondaqs</color>! Doesn't it sound delicious? Just thinking about it is enough to make me tipsy!",
    ["Dialogue1033401"]="...Ch-Chonchons, Rockers? Eurgh... I mean, oh! Heflee really is amazing. Her tastes are so unique!",
    ["Dialogue1033402"]="I feel more at ease now. I'm sure nobody else knows how to make her happy! Looks like I'll have to make some of this \"Singularity\" to show her how serious I am! Although the ingredients... Erm... Ahem! I'm counting on you to get them for me!",
    ["Dialogue1033501"]="...Le-let me just se-settle do-down... What did you say? As a reward, you want me to tell you if there are any strange force fields around? Heh! You've come to the right person! I met a crazy <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomb keeper</color> at the pyramid entrance the other day. He keep mumbling something about a <color=#CA2E0AFF>force field</color> appearing in the pyramid and how the dead can't rest in peace now that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fragment</color> in the tomb has been activated.",
    ["Dialogue1033502"]="Looks like what you're looking for is <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the pyramid</color>, but don't expect me to take you there. I need to stay here and make the \"Singularity\"! I can't wait to see the look on Heflee's face when I give it to her? Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue1033601"]="I see. So it looks like you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the pyramid</color> to dispel the last force field.",
    ["Dialogue1033602"]="But I have to warn you, it's extremely dangerous! The pyramid is the tomb of an ancient Egyptian pharaoh named Osiris, and a large number of his guards were buried with him. No one knows the situation in there, anything could happen. Don't let your guard down!",
    ["Dialogue1033701"]="...Huh? Are my eyes playing tricks on me? Why is there a living person in the pyramid? Is it because of that strange force field?!",
    ["Dialogue1033702"]="Don't you know? Everything's been out of control since the <color=#CA2E0AFF>red force field</color> appeared in the pyramid! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>fragment that was buried</color> with the pharaoh went haywire; the power it's emitting is having an extreme effect on the dead. I hear them wailing every night. This has never happened before. It's absolutely terrifying!",
    ["Dialogue1033703"]="Huh? You want to see it? The force field is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest corner of the pyramid</color>. But don't get too close, or you'll be cursed!\nIt's so scary!",
    ["Dialogue1033801"]="It's been so long since I saw a face that doesn't belong a dead person or a monster.",
    ["Dialogue1033802"]="Yes, you may call me that. After all, I have a duty to guard Master Osiris. Adventurer, if you're here to <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispel the Fire Force Field</color>, I'm afraid you're too late. The force field is but a shell now. The fire element within has already been absorbed by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1033803"]="The fragment was originally buried with the pharaoh. Who could have guessed that such a holy relic would bring about such disaster in the tomb?",
    ["Dialogue1033804"]="I saw with my own eyes how those monsters tore apart Master Osiris' corpse like a pack of hungry wolves, but there was nothing I could do to stop them. All I could do was to stand by and weep helplessly. Adventurer, if you can recover Master Osiris' <color=#CA2E0AFF>bones, hand, heart, and skull</color>, I will personally retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the sarcophagus and give it to you.",
    ["Dialogue1033805"]="I don't care for money or riches. My only hope is for Master Osiris to rest in peace. If you agree to help me, come look for me in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>middle of the pyramid</color> once you have gathered all of Master Osiris' remains.",
    ["Dialogue1033806"]="The Fire Force Field activated the fragment, and the power it emitted turned the dead into mindless monsters. Like me, the dead were supposed to guard Master Osiris, but now they desecrate the pyramid... and their master.",
    ["Dialogue1033901"]="Master Osiris... You still look divine even after a thousand years! My heart still races at the sight of you! Adventurer, thank you for helping me recover these important things. Kindly wait <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of the sarcophagus</color>. I will now place these remains back where they belong and retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart for you!",
    ["Dialogue1034001"]="Eassis... You know this person who desecrated the tomb and stole the holy relic?",
    ["Dialogue1034002"]="Master Osiris, you misunderstand! The true culprit is the Fragment of Ymir's Heart that was buried with you. It was affected by the Fire Force Field and turned the dead in the pyramid into monsters. Those monsters... They did unforgivable things to your body.",
    ["Dialogue1034003"]="Master Osiris, to me, you are sacred above all else. You must not be defiled. Anything that disturbs your peace cannot be forgiven! Even if that thing is a holy relic!",
    ["Dialogue1034004"]="It appears that much has happened during my slumber. In this case, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and leave immediately</color>, adventurer. Regardless of your intentions, this tomb is no place for outsiders. If you were to set foot in here again, not even my Great Royal Wife Eassis would be able to help you!",
    ["Dialogue1034005"]="So I made the decision to give the fragment to this adventurer. Only then could peace be restored.",
    ["Dialogue1034101"]="I was worried you'd end up as fodder for the monsters in the pyramid, but I see you're back without a scratch. I don't even need to ask to know that you succeeded in dispelling the last force field and retrieving the Fragment of Ymir's Heart!",
    ["Dialogue1034102"]="Now that the temperature in Morroc is back to normal, it's only a matter of time before the trade caravans return. I'd love to invite you to stay for a nice long chat, but I know <color=#CA2E0AFF>returning the Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> is your priority right now. Well then, may we meet again when fate permits!",
    ["Dialogue1034103"]="Looks like my judgment about you has been right all along. You are indeed the key to solving this weather problem.",
    ["Dialogue1034201"]="You have brought a third Fragment of Ymir's Heart back. And every time you come, you are stronger and more confident than the last.",
    ["Dialogue1034202"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, I have located the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fourth Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> for you. It is within the vast territory ruled by Nield, God of the Sea. It lies somewhere on the vast <color=#CA2E0AFF>seabed</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1034203"]="I can sense that destiny has intertwined both happiness and sorrow within this fragment. You can try to change it, but it may not be possible to alter that which has been preordained. Regardless of the outcome, I look forward to your safe return.",
    ["Dialogue1034301"]="(Trisse winks at you and asks in a hushed voice.)\n...Are... are you done?",
    ["Dialogue1034302"]="Burp! Sweetheart, is there anything you need? Waka?!",
    ["Dialogue1034303"]="Nope, nope! You're thinking too much, haha!",
    ["Dialogue1034401"]="(Sean the archaeologist seems delirious and can only mumble. Looks like he'll need the doctor to examine him.)",
    ["Dialogue1034501"]="(The cauldron is bubbling. As I stir the concoction, it turns a strange color.)",
    ["Dialogue1034601"]="(The cauldron is bubbling. As I stir the concoction, it gives of a most unusual odor.)",
    ["Dialogue1034701"]="(There's a Katar on the ground. It's almost completely covered by sand. If it wasn't for the light reflecting from the blade, you probably wouldn't have noticed it. Could it be Trisse's Katar?)",
    ["Dialogue1034801"]="(Judging by the size of this footprint, it doesn't seem to belong to a Giearth. That can only mean one thing.)",
    ["Dialogue1040101"]="Child, it's been some time since you last visited me! Would you like to sail in the newly built Valor for your next voyage?",
    ["Dialogue1040102"]="Wow! In all my years as a captain, this is the first time someone's ever asked me about traveling to the bottom of the sea! But you've come to the right person! I once came across the journal of an unknown adventurer that said: \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>There is a secret tunnel on Byalan Island that leads to an underwater treasure on the seabed.</color>\"",
    ["Dialogue1040103"]="No wonder Dean Mainz thinks so highly of you! You have more guts than most! Well then, let's set sail!",
    ["Dialogue1040104"]="Haha! Let me know once you've thought it through! The sea is awash with baseless rumors; even I'd have to think about it carefully",
    ["Dialogue1040105"]="It may not be the most reliable source, but do you want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Byalan Island</color> and try your luck?",
    ["Dialogue1040201"]="I'm so sorry to stop you in your tracks. If I wasn't in need of urgent help, I would never bother a stranger! I'm John, a sailor from Alberta. I work for the renowned Alson Fleet. I've sailed merchant ships back and forth for years. I know these waters and the weather patterns like the back of my hand.",
    ["Dialogue1040202"]="You can imagine how shocked I was when my last voyage turned out to be a disaster. As for the cause of the disaster... It was none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nield, God of the Sea</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1040203"]="Nield was originally the guardian of sailors, but for reasons unknown, he started creating thunderstorms along the merchant shipping lanes. Giant waves smashed our ships and the sailors' cries for mercy were ignored.",
    ["Dialogue1040204"]="Fortunately, a few of my crewmates and I managed to escape to this island. But <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gail Wigner</color> has been missing since he fell overboard.",
    ["Dialogue1040205"]="No, you didn't mishear me. Gail is a member of one of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>seven royal families</color>, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Family that rules Alberta</color>! Can you imagine the consequences if he went missing? If we can't find him and get him back alive, we'll be done for even if we do manage to return to Alberta safely.",
    ["Dialogue1040206"]="Four of my crewmates started searching the island for him, but now I've lost communication with them. I have a really bad feeling about this place. Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>find my crewmates</color> for me? At least let me know if they're safe!",
    ["Dialogue1040301"]="...Finally, somebody! Thank Odin! If I were to take my last breath in this wretched cave, I could never rest in peace!",
    ["Dialogue1040302"]="...Hey, aren't you supposed to think of a way to save me first?! I'm on the brink of dying in this horrible cave! How could you be so cold-hearted! Hmph, if I'd known this would happen, I wouldn't have abandon... Erm, I mean, if I hadn't saved <color=#CA2E0AFF>Byrd's</color> life, I wouldn't have been injured by monsters!",
    ["Dialogue1040303"]="Haha! That's right, I'm such a selfless person! I'm more worried about Byrd's safety than my own injuries. So could you go on ahead to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on him</color>? If he's still alive... Even if he's on his dying breath, please bring him back to me!",
    ["Dialogue1040401"]="Adventurer, you showed up right on time. I'm really bad at dealing with monsters. If it weren't for your help, I might not have lived to see another sunrise!",
    ["Dialogue1040402"]="...<size=24>What?!</size>\nThat lowlife Keanste told you he saved my life?!",
    ["Dialogue1040403"]="So now that he's injured, he suddenly thinks of me again, and wants me to save him? Ha! I wish I could make him know how it feels to be abandoned. But as a doctor, I could never be as heartless as him. In any case, <color=#CA2E0AFF>let's go back to Keanste</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1040404"]="By Odin, how thick-skinned must one be to spout such nonsense?! He's a coward. His carelessness attracted all the monsters, but he didn't think twice about running off and leaving me when things got tough.",
    ["Dialogue1040501"]="You can't imagine how worried I was about you. Even though I was on the brink of death, all I could think of was your safety! I can finally close my eyes in peace now that you've safely returned.",
    ["Dialogue1040502"]="Firstly, shut up, <size=24>Keanste</size>.\n",
    ["Dialogue1040503"]="Sigh, you must be racked with guilt for not saving me in time, but fret not, I will not utter a single word of it when I meet Odin!",
    ["Dialogue1040504"]="Now adventurer, in order to save this reprobate, we'll need to make some medicine. I'll need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Venom</color> from Vadons and some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lily Roots</color>. I saw quite a few on the way here. I'm counting on you to get them.",
    ["Dialogue1040601"]="Great, these are enough. Could you put them into my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cauldron</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1040602"]="Oww! I'm in agony! Can't you two work any faster? I can feel my condition worsening by the second. If you don't hurry, I... I don't think I'll be much longer for this world!",
    ["Dialogue1040603"]="Shut up, Keanste.",
    ["Dialogue1040701"]="...Ahh! I feel so much better now! By Odin, I swear I'll stop looking for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underwater treasure</color>. All I want now is to leave this terrifying cave. With all these ferocious monsters around, even if I was able to find the treasure, I might not make it out alive!",
    ["Dialogue1040702"]="Haha! Did you really think that Keanste entered the underwater cave to look for Gail? That poor lad couldn't be further from his mind! All he can think of is that poem about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underwater treasure</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1040703"]="There's a bard among our crew called Theodore; he has a repertoire of age-old ballads. Ever since we arrived on this island, he's been insisting that it must be the Skull Island from one of his poems, the one where an underwater treasure is hidden.",
    ["Dialogue1040704"]="The treasure is obviously more interesting than Gail, and everyone suddenly sprang into action. Keanste went looking for the treasure, Theodore attempted to solve the riddle in the poem, and Yorkshire went about trying to outdo the God of the Sea's legend. As the only rational member of the crew, I could only follow them into this underwater cave.",
    ["Dialogue1040705"]="Where are <color=#CA2E0AFF>Theodore</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yorkshire</color>? Hmph! The last I saw, they were shouting, \"An Obeaune! Quick, follow that Obeaune!\" and took off deeper into the cave. Who knows, they might be surrounded by Vadons by now, hmph.",
    ["Dialogue1040801"]="<size=18>♪ Entrance guarded by a skeleton with golden teeth, </size><size=18>trail the beauty with the tail of a fish ♪</size>\n<size=18>♪ Wishful thinkers beware of the trident's wrath... </size><size=18>Unlock the door to the ancient trove, </size><size=18>by first defeating the heart of the vicious storm ♪</size>",
    ["Dialogue1040802"]="<size=18>Sigh... </size><size=18>How can I solve the riddle in this poem? </size><size=18>My gut tells me the clues are on this island. </size><size=18>But it's been so long, </size><size=18>and I haven't even deciphered the first line.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1040803"]="...Hey, don't talk to me! Unless you're going to give me a valuable clue. I hate it when people disturb me while I'm trying to solve a riddle!\n<size=18>Now, where was I?</size><size=18>Ah right, </size><size=18>\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Skeleton with golden teeth</color>\"... </size><size=18>Where could it be?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1040901"]="...Skeleton with golden teeth... This must the entrance to the underwater cave! Marvelous! Then according to the second line, I need to follow a \"beauty with the tail of a fish.\" A beauty...",
    ["Dialogue1040902"]="...By Odin! Isn't that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune</color> I just saw?! So she's the second clue. Too bad I didn't have the stamina to keep up with her. But <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yorkshire</color>... He must have managed to follow her! He might have even found out the Obeaune's secret. I've got to find him!",
    ["Dialogue1041001"]="...Theodore? And you... Who are you? Please excuse me, I'm still a little disoriented. So many strange things have happened today; I can't even tell if I'm just hallucinating!",
    ["Dialogue1041002"]="It may sound unbelievable, but while I was following the Obeaune... I saw Gail Wigner! It's so strange. I saw him get swept away by the waves with my own two eyes, but he was just standing <color=#CA2E0AFF>on the shore up ahead</color> and staring out to sea. When I tried to greet him, he ran away without looking back.",
    ["Dialogue1041003"]="He doesn't usually act like that! There must be something going on. Let's think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out what's going on with Gail</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1041101"]="...Huh? You're saying our royal friend was... was trying to woo an Obeaune? Did he hit his head on the deck or something? How could someone like Gail fall for another species? Oh, I know! He must have been bewitched by her!",
    ["Dialogue1041102"]="Tsk, tsk! Gail is no stranger to beautiful women; why would he get bewitched so easily? I think he must have approached that Obeaune to get some clues about the treasure in the poem! Whatever the case, we have to find a way to get him back to Alberta.",
    ["Dialogue1041103"]="Adventurer, why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Gail why he's here</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1041201"]="...Who are you? I don't talk to strangers. So if it's nothing important...",
    ["Dialogue1041202"]="...What? You saw the Obeaune and I... Adventurer, it's not polite to spy on people. But since you saw us, what do you think of it?",
    ["Dialogue1041203"]="Hmph. I knew you wouldn't understand. If that's what you have to say, you can leave right now. I'm not wasting my time with naysayers.",
    ["Dialogue1041204"]="...You really think so? Looks like there's still someone in this world who understands me. Please forgive my earlier imprudence. I never imagined I would meet someone who shares my values. If you really believe that love knows no bounds, then you can certainly understand why I've fallen in love with that Obeaune.",
    ["Dialogue1041205"]="A few days ago, I was in a terrible shipwreck. The roaring waves swallowed me up and dragged me into the murky depths. Just as I was about to fall unconscious, a young lady with the tail of a fish saved me. She brought me onto this island and took care of me.",
    ["Dialogue1041206"]="In any case, I refuse to leave this island until she gives me an answer. If you're willing to help me win her affection, please pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pretty Flowers</color> for me! There aren't any ladies in this world who don't like flowers. I think they'd be able to convey my love to her!",
    ["Dialogue1041207"]="As the days went by, love quietly started to blossom within my heart. By the time I realized it, I was already hopelessly in love!",
    ["Dialogue1041301"]="She's so near yet so far... Look, I've made a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bouquet</color> using the flowers! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>put it by the water</color> for my beloved!",
    ["Dialogue1041401"]="...She was unmoved? How could that be? Are flowers not enough to convey my love? Or could it be that flowers don't have the same significance to Obeaunes as humans? Yeah, that must be it! It's all my fault. I didn't think about it from her perspective!",
    ["Dialogue1041402"]="Please help me gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pretty Pearls</color> from the Marina nearby instead. I think they'll make the perfect gift for my beloved!",
    ["Dialogue1041501"]="Eyes as bright as shining pearls... Look, I've made a <color=#CA2E0AFF>necklace</color> out of the pearls! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>put the it by the water</color> for my beloved!",
    ["Dialogue1041601"]="...How did it go? She still hasn't given an answer? That's strange. There's no reason for her to not understand the meaning behind it. Could it be that she thinks no material gift can compare to a heartfelt declaration of love? Yeah, that must be it! Someone as candid as her would definitely appreciate an honest love letter!",
    ["Dialogue1041602"]="But ordinary paper would get wet in the sea. Adventurer, please get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hard Leather</color> from Cornutus for me!",
    ["Dialogue1041701"]="Love is more than I can say... Look, I've written a <color=#CA2E0AFF>confession of my love</color> on this Hard Leather! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>put it by the water</color> for my beloved! Tell her if she's willing to accept my love, please meet me at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>confession spot</color> that I've chosen specially. Until she gives me an answer, I'll be waiting for her!",
    ["Dialogue1041801"]="...A-adventurer, these gifts... Did that man with blond hair and blue eyes ask you to give them to me?",
    ["Dialogue1041802"]="(Lucia starts blushing.)\n...So it was him! Oh look at how colorful these flowers are, and how beautiful these pearls are! And the words in this love letter... They are as genuine and sincere as him! I'll never forget them.",
    ["Dialogue1041803"]="...Adventurer, you must be curious about why I didn't give him an answer, even though I'm also in love with him? Sigh... Actually, I fell for him the moment I laid my eyes on him! If only I had a pair of legs like a human... If I could just stand next to him, I would have leaped into his arms in a heartbeat and declared my love passionately!",
    ["Dialogue1041804"]="At first I was worried he'd despise my fish tail, but he's shown otherwise! He's tried so hard to get close to me! Compared to his bravery and open-mindedness, my cowardice is shameful. But now, I have no reason to deny my true feelings! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me to him</color>! I won't run away anymore!",
    ["Dialogue1041901"]="(Excitement sparkles in Gail's eyes.)\nAdventurer, Lucia has accepted my love! Who knew she was actually the daughter of Nield, God of the Sea?! She's the princess of the Underwater Temple. I never could have imagined the shipwreck would be a blessing in disguise. It helped me find true love!",
    ["Dialogue1041902"]="Adventurer, thank you for bringing us together! I have decided to follow Gail and live on land. He belongs to the sun and the plains; he should not be trapped on this humid little island! But in order to walk on land, I'll need a pair of human legs. Sigh, do you think I'm too greedy and asking for too much?",
    ["Dialogue1041903"]="The way to acquire a pair of human legs? If someone were to have asked me this in the past, I would have told them it was impossible! But things are different now that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color> has a powerful alchemist. They say he was saved from a shipwreck by my father, and that to repay my father, he helped him regain much of the power he had lost.",
    ["Dialogue1041904"]="So I think the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> might have a way to give an Obeaune a pair of human legs.",
    ["Dialogue1041905"]="I must write this legendary story down for posterity!",
    ["Dialogue1042001"]="Haha! What a familiar face. You remind me of an old friend. Neither you nor I are inhabitants of the sea, yet here we are in the Underwater Temple at the same time. Doesn't it make you wonder if this is coincidence or destiny?",
    ["Dialogue1042002"]="...Oh? So you're here to ask if I have any way to give an Obeaune a pair of human legs? It's a form of blasphemy to try to alter one's natural traits, you know? But since this is Princess Lucia's request, it would be rude of me to decline.",
    ["Dialogue1042003"]="I'll need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seabed Shells and Phen's Piercing Scales</color>. In addition to that, I'll also need <color=#CA2E0AFF>the largest scale on Nield's chest</color>. You heard me right. The recipe will need the scale from the God of the Sea in order to work! Hmm, it would probably be hard for a normal person to get, but since Lucia is his daughter... As long as she's determined to get it, she'll find a way. Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue1042004"]="Well, I can make an ointment for her. She just has to apply it to her fish tail and she'll be able to take on the appearance of a human. As for the ingredients needed...",
    ["Dialogue1042101"]="(Lucia swings her tail in a circle happily.)\nGreat! I knew the alchemist would have a way to give me legs!",
    ["Dialogue1042102"]="Just thinking about being able to walk on land makes me so excited that my heart could jump out of my mouth! Could you get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seabed Shells</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen's </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>Piercing Scales</color>? I'll go to the Underwater Temple to get Father's largest chest scale!",
    ["Dialogue1042201"]="Thank you for helping to gather these ingredients! I need to get them to the alchemist as soon as possible, then... My dear Gail, I'll have a beautiful pair of legs soon!",
    ["Dialogue1042202"]="Of course! Adventurer, I've already decided to relinquish my royalty and lead a normal life with Lucia. Although the Wigner Family gives its members a lot of freedom, they'd never allow my relationship with her. But that doesn't matter now. If Lucia can leave the sea for me, I can give up everything for her!",
    ["Dialogue1042203"]="First I'm going to taker Lucia to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>desert</color> she so yearns to see. Then I'll take her to tour the mountains of Payon and experience the magical atmosphere of Geffen. In fact, I've never traveled as a commoner either; this will be a completely new experience for me as well!",
    ["Dialogue1042204"]="I didn't want to bother you further, but could you do me one last favor? Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>let John know of my decision to leave</color>? If I were to tell him myself, he'd try anything to stop me.",
    ["Dialogue1042205"]="I'll finally be able to walk barefoot, crouch down to kiss the flowers, and run free in the sunlight! And I'll be able to do all these things with you by my side! By Odin, do I really deserve such happiness?",
    ["Dialogue1042301"]="Doctor Byrd has filled me in on what happened in the underwater cave while you were away! Thank you for locating my crewmates! I believe you've found Gail Wigner too, right? Please ask him... Huh? I don't see him. Does he still have unfinished business?",
    ["Dialogue1042302"]="...Y-you can't be serious! What did you just say? Gail's going to give up his royal status and <size=24>elope with an Obeaune?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1042303"]="Please tell me this isn't real. Gail wouldn't do something as ridiculous as that. Has he been blinded by love? Has it occurred to him how much trouble he's going to bring to his family and my crew? If the Wigner Family knew... Wait a minute, did you notice anything strange about the whole situation?",
    ["Dialogue1042401"]="Adventurer, I overheard your entire conversation. You have to tell me where Princess Lucia is, or the consequences will be unthinkable!",
    ["Dialogue1042402"]="(Leona shakes her head and sighs.)\n...You're still trying to cover up for her! Princess Lucia's actions have brought about an unimaginable disaster. If you don't believe me, come closer and I'll show you what happened.",
    ["Dialogue1042501"]="So there you have it.",
    ["Dialogue1042601"]="High Priestess! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Strange power fluctuations</color> are coming from the Underwater Temple! They started after Princess Lucia went inside. We can't break through the power barrier. Please go see what's happened!",
    ["Dialogue1042701"]="Adventurer, I'm not trying to blame you or Princess Lucia by showing you this. Neither of you knew the significance of Nield's chest scale; you couldn't have known the consequences of stealing it. Ever since the Age of Gods came to an end, Nield's powers have been waning. But he held onto his consciousness and used what was left of his power to protect the inhabitants of the sea.",
    ["Dialogue1042702"]="But a few days ago, a human <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> suddenly showed up at the Underwater Temple. He quickly won Nield's trust and deceived him into absorbing the power of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> that had been kept away since ancient times!",
    ["Dialogue1042703"]="That's right. The power from the fragment can indeed make one stronger temporarily. However, not everyone can control the power of Ymir. Ever since then, Nield would occasionally lose control of himself. Indeed, the tragedy that struck the Alson Fleet was caused by Nield after he lost his mind!",
    ["Dialogue1042704"]="Just as I started to realize the danger and was thinking of a way to stop Nield, the Princess stole the scale. That scale was the vessel in which Nield used to store his power. Once it was stolen, he could no longer escape the effects of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1042705"]="Nield has completely lost his mind now! Nobody but the alchemist can approach him. If this continues, the entire underwater world will come to an end. The only way to save Nield and to stop this disaster is to ask Princess Lucia to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return the scale</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1042801"]="I never thought we'd meet again at Sograt Desert. Unfortunately Lucia is ill and unable to greet you.",
    ["Dialogue1042802"]="After we arrived at the desert, Lucia couldn't adapt to the climate and fell ill! We've consulted so many local doctors but they all left baffled. Only Doctor Wallace was willing to stay and try to treat her. I wonder how he's getting on?",
    ["Dialogue1042901"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, interesting. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A human girl exhibiting signs of acute dehydration not long after arriving in the desert! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This seems more like a condition that a fish might suffer from. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I would really like to take her back for more thorough investigation.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1042902"]="...Hmm? Have we met? Please forgive me! I'm terrible at remembering the names of the living! You must be here to visit this young lady! Don't worry! I'm a legendary doctor from Morroc; my specialty is curing unusual illnesses! Patients like this just need different of approach to treatment.",
    ["Dialogue1042903"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hehe! Here's another chance!</color></size>\n...Ahem! According to reliable records, there's a recipe for a tonic in a faraway kingdom. They say that just a few drops can revive a fish that has been dehydrated for 3 days. I think it should work on this young lady too.",
    ["Dialogue1042904"]="If you want her to get well sooner rather than later, then help me get an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Everlasting Skull</color>, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rotten Heart</color>, and some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smooth Snake Scales</color>. Huh? What's with the suspicious look? Never doubt a doctor! Just do as I say!",
    ["Dialogue1043001"]="Hehe! Ingredients from a thousand-year-old monster... How unusual! Quickly! Put these ingredients into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cauldron</color> over there and boil them before the Rotten Heart stops beating!",
    ["Dialogue1043101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, let me think... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How did I do it last time?</color></size>\nAhem! According to reliable records, <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir clockwise</color> for 5 minutes, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir counter-clockwise</color> for another 5 minutes...",
    ["Dialogue1043102"]="Huh? What's with the suspicious look? Never doubt a doctor! Just do as I say!",
    ["Dialogue1043201"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why has it turned this color again? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>And the smell... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Well, I can't expect these ingredients to taste like lobster bisque, right? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Just as long as it works! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>It's not as if I'm the one drinking it!</color></size>\n...Ahem! Force it down... I mean, feed it to the young lady!",
    ["Dialogue1043202"]="(Wallace pinches his nose.)\nI'm a hundred percent sure! Stop hesitating!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'm going to suffocate...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1043301"]="...G-Gail... Are you here? I think I just drank the grossest thing imaginable. It tasted even worse than rotten Megalodon. I-I think I'm going to throw up!",
    ["Dialogue1043302"]="Don't worry, that was just medicine. I guessed you might not be accustomed to the taste of human medicine. Look, what's this I'm holding? Come on, open your mouth. How is it? Is it sweet? I went all the way to Morroc to get these Desert Tomato candies for you. The medicine doesn't taste that bad now, right?",
    ["Dialogue1043303"]="...Gail, other than my father, no one's as nice to me as you! ...Huh? Adventurer, why are you here? You look worried. Is something wrong?",
    ["Dialogue1043304"]="<size=24>...What?!</size>\nLeona said that my father... And the Underwater Temple... By Odin, it's all because I took Father's chest scale. This... Wh-what have I done?!",
    ["Dialogue1043305"]="...If the price of having these legs is this... then I don't deserve them! Gail, I trust you'll understand my decision. I must <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the sea</color> immediately and fix my mistake! I would love to continue traveling the land with you, but I can't sacrifice the peace of the underwater world for my own happiness!",
    ["Dialogue1043306"]="I understand, I'll go with you!",
    ["Dialogue1043401"]="Bloop! You were so cool just now! You did a zip and a zap and boom! Those crazy guys went flying! ...Sigh. Those Swordfish are usually very well behaved; who would have thought they'd attack their own kind in a blink of an eye?! Bloop!",
    ["Dialogue1043402"]="What happened here was the craziest thing I've ever seen! Bloop! After an earthquake, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange power fluctuation</color> came from deep within the temple. Then ahwoooooooo! All the sea creatures around me started going crazy! Bloop!",
    ["Dialogue1043403"]="So I grabbed my son, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Little Baxter</color> and fled! But it was too chaotic and we got separated in the crowd. My poor son, bloop! He must be crying somewhere now. If I've lost him, I'll go above water and suffocate myself to death! Bloop!",
    ["Dialogue1043501"]="*Cries* Have you seen Marc? He has a spectacular dorsal fin, bloop? He's my daddy, bu-but I can't find him.",
    ["Dialogue1043502"]="*Sniffs* You know where my daddy is, bloop? Then could you tell him I'll be waiting for him to pick me up at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Divine Altar</color>? I shouldn't be here. When Leona saved me from the monsters, she told me to stay put at the altar, bloop! But I really miss Daddy, so I snuck away.",
    ["Dialogue1043601"]="...Bloooop?! You found Little Baxter? That's wonderful news! I'm so happy! Hurry... <size=24>Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me to him</color>, bloop!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1043701"]="Adventurer, thank you for reuniting us! Bloop! And thank you to High Priestess Leona too! Because of her, Little Baxter has returned safely to my side. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>thank her on my behalf</color> and let her know that she's always welcome to enjoy the algae at our humble abode! Bloop!",
    ["Dialogue1043702"]="Curious about what happened? Nield was worried that he might lose control of his power. So before he started to absorb the power of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, he sealed part of his power in this monument. If something goes awry, a suitable hero will be able to inherit this power.",
    ["Dialogue1043801"]="There's no need to thank me; it is my responsibility to protect the inhabitants of the sea. It's never crossed my mind that land-dwellers like you and that young man called Gail would help to solve the problems of our underwater world. But your arrival is most timely. The situation grows ever worse; we'll need all the help we can get!",
    ["Dialogue1043802"]="You've noticed the strange power fluctuation too? That's right, it's coming from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. Ever since Nield went mad, the fragment has been fully activated. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>water elemental power</color> within has spread across the entire seabed and is causing all its inhabitants to lose their minds.",
    ["Dialogue1043803"]="The only way to restore peace is to stop Nield, but that's no easy task. Fortunately Nield had the foresight to put countermeasures in place beforehand. Adventurer! Since you want to help, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray in front of the monument</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1043901"]="Adventurer, you have now become the hero acknowledged by Nield, but this is just the beginning. We must use the power within you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat Nield</color>. Then when he's at his weakest, we must <color=#CA2E0AFF>return the scale containing the divine power</color> to its rightful owner. You only have one chance; there's no room for error. I believe you're prepared for battle, but Princess Lucia...",
    ["Dialogue1043902"]="(Leona frowns slightly.)\n...Princess, you... you already know what you should do, right?",
    ["Dialogue1043903"]="(Lucia nods with determination.)",
    ["Dialogue1043904"]="I'll go with you! I've received combat training since I was young; I believe I'll be able to help you in this battle.",
    ["Dialogue1043905"]="The power of humans isn't strong enough to defeat Father, Gail... and I was hoping you could stay here. Look, so many of the sea's inhabitants still need your help! This separation is only temporary. Once this is all over, we'll...",
    ["Dialogue1043906"]="...My dear Gail, can I have one more Desert Tomato candy? It's sweetness will help keep me going in the tough battle ahead!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'll remember the taste of this candy... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>forever.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1044001"]="Bloop, bloop! Thank you for your help! Sigh, age is really catching up to me. I may have eight legs, but none of them work well at my age!",
    ["Dialogue1044002"]="Did any crazed Obeaunes hurt you?",
    ["Dialogue1044003"]="...You're... Nield's youngest daughter, Princess Lucia?! How... Why are you still at the Underwater Temple, Your Highness? Follow me to safety, bloop! I understand your unwillingness to leave your home, but everyone's lost their mind, even your father.",
    ["Dialogue1044004"]="Sigh... Don't talk about it. Everyone's gone mad, bloop! The only sane person left is that <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color>. Maybe he really does have superpowers. Even Nield can't hurt him, bloop! Thankfully that means he can stay by Nield's side to treat him while everyone escapes.",
    ["Dialogue1044005"]="People always say it's in adversity that we see true loyalty. Someone as true and noble as him is hard to come by, hard to come by indeed, bloop!",
    ["Dialogue1044006"]="...This is unbelievable! How could anybody resist the effects of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart? And at the same time not get hurt by my father? ...Unless he expected this to happen and was prepared for it!",
    ["Dialogue1044007"]="I see it now! Ever since Father began taking the alchemist's medicine, he started to trust him unconditionally! It was the alchemist's idea to remove Father's chest scale. We... No! I was an idiot! I actually believed his lies! And I even became his accomplice while feeling indebted to him.",
    ["Dialogue1044008"]="We need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find my father immediately</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>save him from that evildoer</color>! If Father ends up hurt because of my selfishness and foolishness, I'll never forgive myself!",
    ["Dialogue1044101"]="Lucia... My beloved daughter... Why must I see you fade away in my arms right after I regain my senses? ...By Odin, what nightmare is this? Why did you have to take my beloved daughter? It should be me who is punished!",
    ["Dialogue1044102"]="It was my negligence that gave that evildoer his opportunity and it was my foolishness that brought this tragedy upon my people... and Lucia! No amount of tears can bring her back. This lesson is seared in my mind. I must always remember this pain, and use it to constantly remind myself never to lose my way!",
    ["Dialogue1044103"]="Adventurer, I need some time alone now. Take <color=#CA2E0AFF>this Fragment of Ymir's Heart and leave the Underwater Temple</color> immediately. I don't need it anymore and I don't want to see a repeat of this tragedy!",
    ["Dialogue1044201"]="...The princess... She's fulfilled her duty, right? Although I foresaw that this would happen, it does not lessen the sorrow.",
    ["Dialogue1044202"]="At this point in time, even someone as pious as me cannot help but lament the unfairness of destiny. But then again, what is destiny? Is everyone's life predestined, or is it made up of our choices? Rumors of the past have always warned that the love between an Obeaune and a human will never end well. But even so, there are some who would love regardless, and die while holding on to the last of their hopes.",
    ["Dialogue1044203"]="Sigh, there might very well be no answer to all this, but please still try your best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>persuade Gail</color> to forget about all that has happened and return to where he belongs! Since Princess Lucia didn't want him to see her sacrifice, she wouldn't want him to continue living in the shadow of the past either.",
    ["Dialogue1044301"]="Adventurer, I sense that the battle has ended... but where is Lucia?",
    ["Dialogue1044302"]="...Huh? What did you say? Impossible! How could she have sacrificed herself in a battle with her father?! ...Haha! Stop fooling around! I'm not buying it! She must still be alive! She must be... She must be staying in the sea a little longer to try and make up for her mistakes. Yeah, that must be it!",
    ["Dialogue1044303"]="...Could it be that Lucia decided to stay and make up for her mistakes? I understand... As a princess, this disaster must have had a great impact on her. And I too, am responsible for it. I lost my sense of judgment in a moment of recklessness and failed to help her make a better choice.",
    ["Dialogue1044304"]="Please tell her I'll be waiting for her in the desert. No matter how long it takes, I will continue to wait!",
    ["Dialogue1044401"]="This is the first time that I've seen loss and sorrow on your face. Successor of Odin's Bloodline, you must have gone through an extraordinary journey while searching for the fourth Fragment of Ymir's Heart, am I right? As such is an adventure, as such is life. A journey is not just about honor and contentment; it will also bring pain and humiliation.",
    ["Dialogue1044402"]="This is what you must go through, Successor of Odin's bloodline. Though it may sound cruel, I need you to recover from your sorrow and set off for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fifth Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue1044403"]="I have located it. It is in land that is old and pure—<color=#CA2E0AFF>the mountain town of Payon</color>. I am unable to tell you more because hidden there is a mysterious power that stems from the world itself. Even I am unable to touch it. Go experience it for yourself and uncover the secret within, Successor of Odin's Bloodline. I will wait for your good news in the Temple of Dawn.",
    ["Dialogue1044501"]="(There's a trail of footprints heading forward. Quick, follow it!)",
    ["Dialogue1044601"]="(Lucia looks pale and frail. How is her condition? Let's ask the doctor!)",
    ["Dialogue1044701"]="(The cauldron is bubbling. As I stir the concoction, it turns a strange color.)",
    ["Dialogue1044801"]="(The cauldron is bubbling. As I stir the concoction, it gives of a most unusual odor.)",
    ["Dialogue1050101"]="Adventurer, welcome to the beautiful mountain village of Payon! This is a very special place in the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom. It is said that if you look up at Payon's sky, you will feel as if you are one with it.",
    ["Dialogue1050102"]="Oh, you want to know about what has been happening in Payon recently? Your best bet is to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Ocean Euin</color>! The Euin Family is the most prestigious family in this land. They've protected it since Payon was founded. They say the Euin Family knows every blade of grass and every tree like the back of their hands!",
    ["Dialogue1050103"]="Come to think of it, we hardly see adventurers from foreign lands. If you have any questions, you can always ask me!",
    ["Dialogue1050201"]="Stop! The Lord's Residence is not accepting guests! Regardless of who you are, please leave immediately!",
    ["Dialogue1050202"]="What happened?",
    ["Dialogue1050301"]="(Moon Euin looks at you with curiosity.)\nAdventurer, is something the matter? I'm Moon Euin, the daughter of Lord Ocean Euin. If there's anything, you can let me know!",
    ["Dialogue1050302"]="...You've been traveling far and wide to collect Fragments of Ymir's Heart?",
    ["Dialogue1050303"]="I heard you've battled many terrifying monsters in your quest to collect the holy relics. It sounds so tough and dangerous; why do you continue to do so?",
    ["Dialogue1050304"]="(Moon Euin freezes for a while.)\nThe power of the Fragments of Ymir's Heart is very hard to control and can cause monsters to transform? That is indeed quite dangerous. I understand now. Well then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1050305"]="(Moon Euin leaves before you finish speaking.)",
    ["Dialogue1050306"]="(Moon Euin's eyes widen in surprise and her fists clench in excitement.)\nWow! Could you be the adventurer everyone's talking about?! I've heard of your adventures! I never expected you to be this young!",
    ["Dialogue1050401"]="Allow me to introduce you to the Master of the Archer Guild—Sky Euin!\n(Moon Euin turns to Sky Euin.)\nUncle, I've brought this adventurer here because...",
    ["Dialogue1050402"]="(As Sky Euin listens to Moon Euin's explanation, his expression becomes increasingly serious.)\nTo search for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. This is your motive for coming to Payon? Then forgive my directness, but please give up.",
    ["Dialogue1050403"]="(Sky Euin sighs.)\nLooks like I'm unable to persuade you. Moon, please show this adventurer to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak Cave</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1050501"]="Do you understand now? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak Cave</color> is the most dangerous place in Payon. Payon suffered a devastating famine a thousand years ago; many villagers starved to death. Their bodies were buried at the site of the former city. However, their souls could not rest in peace and turned into Munaks. They clawed their way out of the ground and started to kill and devour the living.",
    ["Dialogue1050502"]="In an instant, Payon turned from a paradise into a living hell. Many lost their will to live. That was until a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young archer</color> appeared. He gathered everyone who was young and strong, and formed an army called the \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Quellers</color>.\" They eliminated the Munaks and saved Payon from calamity.",
    ["Dialogue1050503"]="In the last battle, the young archer led his army to trap the remaining Munaks in the middle of the city. Together with the Indrah Sect, they sealed the Munaks and the old Payon underground, giving this land the opportunity to start again. This is the origin of Munak Cave. And that young archer is none other than the ancestor of our Euin Family, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Qi Euin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1050504"]="Adventurer, the Fragment of Ymir's Heart you seek was sealed <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep within Munak Cave</color> by General Qi Euin as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>holy relic to suppress the monsters</color>. I think you're already aware of how dangerous the cave is. You could be attacked by monsters just by going near it; entering its depths would be unimaginable.",
    ["Dialogue1050505"]="(Moon Euin blinks in confusion.)\n...Huh? But didn't <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Taixuan</color> enter the cave before? If we could get him to help this adventurer, then maybe...",
    ["Dialogue1050506"]="Silence! Do you think Master Taixuan is someone whom you can ask for help just like that? The master has been <color=#CA2E0AFF>living in isolation</color> for many years and does not take visitors. We must not bother him over something as trivial as this. Do not mention this again!",
    ["Dialogue1050601"]="(Moon Euin sneaks a quick glance at Sky Euin and secretly beckons you.)\nCome over, I have something to tell you. I've decided. I'll think of a way to help you meet Master Taixuan, even if it means being punished by my uncle!",
    ["Dialogue1050602"]="Master Taixuan is the Grand Elder of the Indrah Sect. He entered Munak Cave with my father 10 years ago. He's very powerful; I'm sure he'll have a way to avoid those monsters and help you get into the cave safely!",
    ["Dialogue1050603"]="Indeed, Master Taixuan hasn't been in the public view for a while. Come to think of it, he hasn't shown himself since he exited Munak Cave... But!\n(Moon Euin bats her eyelids slyly.)\nI know someone who can take you to him!",
    ["Dialogue1050604"]="My younger brother <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comet Euin</color> is the last disciple of Master Taixuan! Not too long ago, he wrote to me and told me he and his senior disciples were headed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Payon</color> for training, and that Master Taixuan was with them!",
    ["Dialogue1050701"]="(Comet Euin ruffles his hair anxiously.)\n<size=18>Ahhhh! This is making me so anxious...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1050702"]="...Are you kidding me?! I'm already so busy; the last thing I need is my big sister giving me even more trouble. Erm, I know my master is very powerful and there are lots of people who would love an audience with him, but ever since he started living in seclusion, even I hardly get to see him!",
    ["Dialogue1050703"]="In any case, I have enough on my plate! Please don't bother me.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Wait a minute...</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> An extra pair of hands would mean extra help? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Maybe I could... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hehe!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1050704"]="Ahem! What I meant was, since it's for my big sister, I'll do my best to help you! But before I headed out, my senior gave me a task. If I return without completing it, the consequences will be dire.\n(Comet Euin rubs his forehead in dejection.)",
    ["Dialogue1050705"]="My task is to collect rare herbs, but I haven't been able to find any <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Soul Grass</color>. Sigh, and it just so happens to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Elder Willows'</color> favorite! Ahhhh... Just the thought of Great Elder Willows is enough to make me shudder.",
    ["Dialogue1050801"]="Haha! Yes, this is the herb! But... Sigh, I'm still missing one. If I return without it, the consequences will be unthinkable...\n(Comet Euin rubs his forehead in dejection.)",
    ["Dialogue1050802"]="A type of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat Pie Mushroom</color> grows around this area, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>Giant Spores</color> love it! Ahhhh... Just the thought of Giant Spores is enough to make me shudder.",
    ["Dialogue1050901"]="Haha! Yes, this is the herb! But... Sigh, I'm still missing one. If I return without it, the consequences will be unthinkable...\n(Comet Euin rubs his forehead in dejection.)",
    ["Dialogue1050902"]="Oh, it looks like you don't want to meet my master after all! In that case, I'll just...\n(Comet Euin looks like he's about to leave.)",
    ["Dialogue1050903"]="Hehe! A herb called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sprout of Yggdrasil</color> can be found around this area. If I recall correctly, we can get it from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wormtails</color>. Ahhhh... Just the thought of Wormtails is enough to make me shudder.",
    ["Dialogue1051001"]="Haha! Yes, this is the herb! But... Sigh, I'm still missing one. If I return without it, the consequences will be unthinkable...\n(Comet Euin rubs his forehead in dejection.)",
    ["Dialogue1051002"]="Bahaha! Only kidding! The look on your face! Even if you could collect more herbs, I can't carry any more! Alright then, we've really got all the herbs now. Let's get back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Indrah Sect's Ancient Ancestral Hall</color>. My master and seniors are there!",
    ["Dialogue1051101"]="Not bad, you're back early today. How did it go? Have you completed the task I gave you? You haven't been slacking off again, have you?\n(Munmi notices you.)\n...This is?",
    ["Dialogue1051102"]="He said he needed to consult the master about something, so I brought him here! Is Master feeling better?",
    ["Dialogue1051103"]="Ten years ago, Master and Lord Ocean Euin entered Munak Cave to reinforce the thousand year-old seal. After Master returned, his health started to deteriorate. Initially, we thought it was merely exhaustion. However, we later found that he seems to have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>poisoned</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1051104"]="<size=26>Poisoned?</size> So that's why you asked me to gather herbs?",
    ["Dialogue1051105"]="That's right. The poison is rather peculiar. None of the methods we've tried so far have been able to completely purge it from Master's body, so we started to search for the herbs in an antidote recipe we found in an ancient text. The herbs you brought back are the last ones we need. After all these years of preparation, we're finally ready!",
    ["Dialogue1051106"]="Adventurer, since you would like to seek an audience with Master Taixuan, follow me <color=#CA2E0AFF>into the Ancient Ancestral Hall</color> to tell him this good news. I'm sure he'll be very happy when he hears it.",
    ["Dialogue1051201"]="(Comet Euin looks confused.)\nWh-what happened? Why is this place such a mess? ...Where's Master gone? And where are the others?",
    ["Dialogue1051202"]="(Munmi looks worried.)\nI'm not sure why, but those Munaks that appeared just now gave me an uneasy feeling. My fellow disciples and I have always guarded this Ancient Ancestral Hall. How could this have happened?",
    ["Dialogue1051203"]="There must have been an accident! Father is... No, no! We have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Archer Village immediately and ask my uncle for help</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1051301"]="(Sky Euin looks shocked upon hearing the news that Master Taixuan is missing.)\n...What? Is another tragedy about to happen? Is Payon destined for calamity?",
    ["Dialogue1051302"]="(Sky Euin lets out a long sigh.)\nNow that it has come to this, I have no choice but to tell you the truth. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Taixuan isn't the first person in Payon to mysteriously go missing</color>. The last person who went missing was none other than my brother—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Ocean Euin, the Lord of Payon</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1051303"]="Ocean Euin and Master Taixuan are the only two people who are able to reinforce the seal in Munak Cave. With them gone, there's no one else in Payon capable of suppressing the monsters in the cave. It's no coincidence that both of them have gone missing! We need to find out exactly what's happening!",
    ["Dialogue1051304"]="Ocean Euin's eldest son, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sun Euin</color>, was at the scene the night he went missing. Go see him at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Residence</color> and try to find out what happened that night. Who knows, it might shed some light on the disappearance of Ocean Euin and Master Taixuan.",
    ["Dialogue1051401"]="...Uncle asked you to come?\n(Sun Euin looks at you in suspicion.)\nWell then, are you ready to hear about what happened that night?",
    ["Dialogue1051402"]="If so, here goes—",
    ["Dialogue1051403"]="......",
    ["Dialogue1051501"]="And that's what happened. And it wasn't just Father, his subordinates also went missing that night. In order to prevent panic, we've been keeping the news from the citizens of Payon while the Archer Guild and the Euin Family secretly conduct an investigation.",
    ["Dialogue1051502"]="Although I've been managing the affairs at the Lord's Residence, I don't know anything about the investigation. I'm worried that...\n(Sun Euin looks down in apprehension.)",
    ["Dialogue1051601"]="(Sky Euin frowns in helplessness.)\n<size=18>Sigh, things are getting more and more bizarre.</size>",
    ["Dialogue1051602"]="I got another lead not long ago. Munaks appeared in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hidden Wood Village in Payon West</color> too! The villagers are just ordinary farmers, so not many of them survived the attack. They're temporarily staying at <color=#CA2E0AFF>a house in the south of West Payon</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1051603"]="This can't wait any longer. Leave the <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigation of Hidden Wood Village</color> to this adventurer and me! Maybe we'll find out the truth behind the Munaks' appearance from the villagers and it will help us find Father and Master Taixuan!",
    ["Dialogue1051604"]="Well then, I'll return to the mountains with Munmi to make the master's antidote. As long as he returns safely, we'll be able to treat him immediately!",
    ["Dialogue1051605"]="Since Munaks appeared in all three places, there might be a connection between what happened at the Lord's Residence, the Ancient Ancestral Hall, and Hidden Wood Village.",
    ["Dialogue1051701"]="(Won Chunghan is hunched and looks exhausted.)\nWhy did such a tragedy befall Hidden Wood Village?! What will become of the survivors?!",
    ["Dialogue1051702"]="...Sigh, are the people from Archer Village finally here? Everyone's been living in fear since the attack! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out the truth</color> and give these poor villagers some consolation!",
    ["Dialogue1051801"]="(Lee Hana's eyes are bloodshot and she is weeping.)\n<size=18>*Cries*</size><size=18>My dear husband...</size><size=18>His mother and father...</size>",
    ["Dialogue1051802"]="*Cries* How I wish this was all just a bad dream! That night, my husband and I heard <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange noises</color> coming from his parents' room, so we went to check. When we opened the door, two Munaks charged at us and knocked us over. If my husband hadn't stood in their way, I wouldn't have been able to escape. But...",
    ["Dialogue1051803"]="...But now that I think about it... Two Munaks appeared in the room just after my parents mysteriously disappeared. No, it can't be...\n(Lee Hana buries her face in her hands and cries even harder.)",
    ["Dialogue1051901"]="(Cho Bin's head is lowered and he is muttering angrily.)\n<size=18>...Damn it! </size><size=18>It must be him!</size><size=18> He must be the one behind it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1051902"]="Good timing. I was just about to tell the chief that the one responsible for all this carnage is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kang Min</color>! I've always thought there was something is off about him. He was <color=#CA2E0AFF>gravely ill</color> but suddenly <color=#CA2E0AFF>made a miraculous recovery</color>. What's more, I saw him acting suspiciously <color=#CA2E0AFF>by the old well</color> the night before the Munaks appeared. I don't know what he did, but I'm sure it's got something to do with all this!",
    ["Dialogue1051903"]="Damn it! My whole family died that night, yet Kang Min's daughter survived! Why?\n(Cho Bin clenches his fists and glares menacingly at a little girl by the side.)",
    ["Dialogue1052001"]="(Kang Yona shrinks in fear after seeing you. She cautiously takes two steps back.)\n...D-do you suspect my daddy as well? He's not a bad man!",
    ["Dialogue1052002"]="How did Daddy get better? ...A month ago, <color=#CA2E0AFF>a traveler</color> lodged at our house. He said he was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>doctor</color> and could cure Daddy. All of a sudden, Daddy really did get better! But when Daddy asked the doctor how he could repay him, I heard the doctor say some really strange things...",
    ["Dialogue1052003"]="...I heard him say it's just a <color=#CA2E0AFF>trade</color>. He wanted Daddy to <color=#CA2E0AFF>do something</color> for him. I didn't catch what it was, but I could see Daddy was worried. After that, Daddy never came home. I don't even know how is he now...\n(Kang Yona wipes away her tears.)",
    ["Dialogue1052101"]="...You mean the <color=#CA2E0AFF>old well</color> in the village? It's <color=#CA2E0AFF>the village's only source of water</color>; it's located <color=#CA2E0AFF>to the north, in the middle of the what used to be Hidden Wood Village</color>. All the survivors moved here after the massacre; the former site might still be crawling with monsters. If you are headed there, be careful!",
    ["Dialogue1052201"]="Look, there are still Munaks roaming among the debris! Looks like we won't be able to get near the well unless we <color=#CA2E0AFF>eliminate them</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1052301"]="(Moon Euin lowers her head and sniffs.)\nSmell that? Adventurer, I have a bold idea. Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>get some water from the well</color>? I'll be right back!",
    ["Dialogue1052401"]="(Moon Euin pants as she wipes the beads of sweat from her brow.)\nHuff! It wasn't easy catching this little guy! Now try <color=#CA2E0AFF>feeding the well water to this Big-Footed Cub</color>. If my guess is correct...",
    ["Dialogue1052501"]="Just as I expected! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Someone poisoned the well</color>! By the looks of it, the Munaks didn't invade the village from outside... They may very well be the villagers who drank the water!",
    ["Dialogue1052502"]="You're right. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>traveler</color> who lodged at Kang Min's house is almost certainly the culprit! But what could his motive have been?\n(Moon Euin narrows her eyes in alarm.)\n...<size=18>Shush, did you hear something?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1052601"]="(Liu Wuye looks at you warily. Most of his face is hidden under his cloak.)\nThis is no place for the living. Leave at once!",
    ["Dialogue1052602"]="...I'm different. Who are you? What are you doing in this abandoned village?",
    ["Dialogue1052603"]="So the chief and the others are in a safe place. That's good to hear. At least there were some survivors.",
    ["Dialogue1052604"]="Yes, I also think someone poisoned the only source of water in the village! It's the only thing that explains why many people transformed at the same time... and what happened to my beloved <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jingyin</color>.\n(Liu Wuye grits his teeth.)",
    ["Dialogue1052605"]="(Liu Wuye starts shaking.)\nThat's right, we drank from the old well too! I... I witnessed something unforgettably horrifying that night! Jingyin... She... she ate her beloved cat alive.",
    ["Dialogue1052606"]="And me... I'm now neither human nor monster! The strange thing is, I'm still conscious. But it's the complete opposite for Jingyin. Though she's still beautiful on the outside, she's like a completely different person on the inside... or not even a person at all!",
    ["Dialogue1052607"]="I know who you're referring to. Because when the carnage started, he didn't leave the village! I remember how he laughed as he watched and how he called Jingyin his \"most perfect experiment\"! In the end, he forced her away from me and said he would take her to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Butsudan in Munak Cave</color> to complete the final step of his grand plan!",
    ["Dialogue1052608"]="(Moon Euin clenches her firsts in rage.)\nThis is insane! So that traveler is the culprit! And he used the entire village for his experiment!",
    ["Dialogue1052609"]="I can't show myself to anyone else in my current state; all I can do is hide here. Adventurer, please help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>save Jingyin and avenge the villagers</color>! No doubt his ultimate objective is far more diabolical. You have to stop him, no matter what!",
    ["Dialogue1052610"]="I also lived in Hidden Wood Village. I still can't forget how the villagers turned into Munaks before my eyes. There was only one thing they had in common—<color=#CA2E0AFF>they all drank the water from the old well.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1052701"]="(Sky Euin's expression turns somber after listening to your account.)\nIt appears the mysterious traveler is plotting an even grander scheme. It's likely Ocean Euin and Master Taixuan's disappearance also has something to do with it.",
    ["Dialogue1052702"]="(Sky Euin sighs in resignation.)\nWith all that's happened, I must agree to let you enter the cave, but I have one condition: Moon will not go with you.",
    ["Dialogue1052703"]="...<size=24>Uncle!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1052704"]="(Sky Euin's expression makes it clear that there's no room for negotiation.)\nMunak Cave is filled with evil; it's no place for a girl. Adventurer, I'll leave the task of <color=#CA2E0AFF>pursuing the culprit</color> to you. If there's anything you need help with, you can count on me.",
    ["Dialogue1052705"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>…But the entrance to Munak Cave has always been guarded by members from Archer Village. How does the traveler intend to get inside?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1052801"]="(This old man is unconscious. Judging by his clothes, he seems to be from the Indrah Sect. Could it be Master Taixuan? But why would he be here?)",
    ["Dialogue1052901"]="Adventurer, it is due to the power in the rune that I am able to appear before you, though just barely. But you are not alone; the old man on the ground is of the Indrah Sect.",
    ["Dialogue1052902"]="(The Horong bounces up and down uneasily.)\nI have roamed this cave for a thousand years and forgotten too much. I can no longer even remember my name or what I looked like. But I feel a sense of warmth from the rune fragment in your hand. Perhaps it came from the same source as my magic, and that's why I feel a sense of familiarity from it.",
    ["Dialogue1052903"]="I vaguely remember that I stayed behind in this cave because I have an important mission. Could you help me reconstruct my form by <color=#CA2E0AFF>recovering all the rune fragments</color>? The fragments <color=#CA2E0AFF>react to one another</color> so you'll be able to find them by <color=#CA2E0AFF>searching around the cave</color>. I'll keep watch over this Indrah Sect master.",
    ["Dialogue1053001"]="(The archer bows to you.)\nAdventurer, thank you for your help. Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Qi Euin.",
    ["Dialogue1053002"]="I can barely believe that people still remember me even after a thousand years, and that the monsters in this cave are now stronger than a thousand years ago. Adventurer, this is no place for the living. Do you have a reason for being here?",
    ["Dialogue1053003"]="The Butsudan you seek is <color=#CA2E0AFF>deeper within the cave</color>. During the battle against the Munaks, the Spirit Quellers and I willingly sank underground along with Payon. I borrowed the power of a holy relic in order to seal the monsters here forever. I then sealed the holy relic in the Butsudan deep within the cave.",
    ["Dialogue1053004"]="That's right, the holy relic is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. But I never expected that the power of the fragment would be so hard to control. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poison element</color> it emitted pervaded the bodies of the monsters and of the Spirit Quellers.",
    ["Dialogue1053005"]="(Qi Euin frowns.)\n...So you're saying a traveler has caused Munak unrest in Payon and it's highly likely that he will use the Fragment of Ymir's Heart in the Butsudan to cause even more trouble?",
    ["Dialogue1053006"]="Adventurer, take this rune and gather the roaming <color=#CA2E0AFF>spirits of the Spirit Quellers</color>. I'll need their help to complete this mission. They might have gone crazy from losing their memories, so please try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>subdue them</color> before <color=#CA2E0AFF>using the power of the rune</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1053007"]="As time went by, we became creatures that are neither dead nor alive, while the monsters grew stronger by absorbing the fragment's power.",
    ["Dialogue1053008"]="Since I was the one who placed the fragment here, I shall bear the responsibility for its safety.",
    ["Dialogue1053101"]="General Qi Euin asked you to look for me? Where is the general now? Quick, take me to him!",
    ["Dialogue1053201"]="Adventurer, while I was dispelling the magic circle in front of the damaged Butsudan, I found that someone has used the power of the rune to open a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color> here. Maybe this was how the traveler moved in and out Munak Cave.",
    ["Dialogue1053202"]="Well, we can make use of this dimensional gap now instead. Please use it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get the Indrah Sect master safely back above ground</color>, then retrieve my weapon, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sun-Piercing Bow</color>. Once I have my weapon, I'll be able to face the enemy at the Butsudan! I will wait here for your return.",
    ["Dialogue1053301"]="Huh? Why are you here?\n(Comet Euin finally notices Master Taixuan next to you. His eyes widen in surprise.)\n<size=24>...M-Master?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053302"]="...What?! You saw our ancestor <size=24>General Qi Euin</size> in Munak Cave?!\nHey... You're not kidding me now, are you? And why the troubled look on your face?",
    ["Dialogue1053303"]="I see. I know where the general's weapon is! When he passed away, the Euin Family built a cenotaph in his honor. The Sun-Piercing Bow must be with the rest of his belongings at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tomb of the General in East Payon</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1053304"]="But the tomb is heavily guarded. In order to enter it, you will need the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's permission</color>. You'll have to ask my elder brother, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sun Euin</color>.\n<size=18>But he's famous for being as stubborn as a mule, </size><size=18>so good luck!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053401"]="(Sun Euin is expressionless after hearing you out.)\n...No. Although the tomb is just a cenotaph, opening it would still be disrespectful to the dead. I will not grant your request, unless...",
    ["Dialogue1053402"]="Unless you can prove your strength to the Euin Family. The Tomb of the General is guarded in shifts by <color=#CA2E0AFF>two Euin Family elders</color>. If you can pass their <color=#CA2E0AFF>trials</color>, you might have a chance to enter the tomb. At this time of the day, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Cliff Euin</color> should be guarding the tomb. The other elder, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Xiao Euin</color>, should be by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Exquisite Pond</color>. I suggest you go speak to him first.",
    ["Dialogue1053501"]="(Xiao Euin is ranting in annoyance.)\n<size=18>Damn it, damn it! </size><size=18>These Elder Willows are so annoying! </size><size=18>And the most infuriating thing is that they have the word \"Elder\" in their name!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053502"]="<size=18>It's finally my turn to rest today; </size><size=18> at last I get to relax and enjoy a spot of fishing! </size><size=18>But these Elder Willows keep walking around and around and around...</size><size=18>They've scared off all the fish!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053503"]="<size=18>Ahhhh! </size><size=18>Fishing is my only hobby! </size><size=18>Is a little peace and quiet really so much to ask for?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053504"]="Are you done? I heard you; I just didn't want to reply! You want to enter the Tomb of the General, right? Then go get rid of all those <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Willows</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1053505"]="(Xiao Euin waves his hand impatiently.)\nWhatever. I just want these annoying monsters gone IMMEDIATELY, so that I can fish in peace!",
    ["Dialogue1053601"]="(Xiao Euin looks around and his anger instantly turns to glee.)\nOhoho! So young, yet so talented? I have a proposition: Why don't you stay here and get rid of the monsters that disrupt my fishing?",
    ["Dialogue1053602"]="...Huh? Did you really think that was the trial? Hoho, that would be far too simple. It was just a small favor.\n(Xiao Euin's eyes light up.)",
    ["Dialogue1053603"]="Tell you what, I really love fishing! So if you can bring me a fresh <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crucian Carp</color>, I'll consider you to have passed my trial. How about that?",
    ["Dialogue1053701"]="(Xiao Euin grins from ear to ear.)\nOhoho! I can finally add the Crucian Carp to my collection! I like you, kid! You want to enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tomb of the General</color>, right? Then follow me!",
    ["Dialogue1053801"]="(Cliff Euin's expression is stern.)\nAdventurer, don't you know this is the General's tomb? The Euin Family's cemetery is no place for an outsider.",
    ["Dialogue1053802"]="Cliff, you've already said that! This kid passed my trial; why not just let him in?",
    ["Dialogue1053803"]="Your trial? According to the rules, one must pass both our trials before they're allowed into the Tomb of the General! Adventurer. I'm not as easily fooled as Xiao! Unless <color=#CA2E0AFF>you can impress me with your combat skills</color>, you'll have no hope of entering the tomb!\n(Cliff Euin draws his weapon.)",
    ["Dialogue1053901"]="(Cliff Euin mutters grumpily.)\n<size=18>Damn it... </size><size=18>How could I, </size><size=18>a mighty warrior of Payon, </size><size=18>lose to a... a child?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1053902"]="Ahem! Cliff, you have to keep your word!",
    ["Dialogue1053903"]="(Cliff Euin reluctantly steps aside.)\nI know, I know. Of course, I'll keep my word. Since you've passed my trial, you're free to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Tomb of the General</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1054001"]="I can't believe those foul creatures would dare defile the ancestral tomb of the Euin Family. Elders, are you alright?",
    ["Dialogue1054002"]="We're alright.",
    ["Dialogue1054003"]="Looks like that traveler has created a new army of monsters. If we don't get the situation under control, Payon will eventually fall.",
    ["Dialogue1054004"]="(Sky Euin turns toward you solemnly.)\nAdventurer, hurry <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Archer Village</color> with us. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Taixuan</color> has awoken and is waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue1054101"]="(Taixuan coughs a few times.)\n...You must be the adventurer that Comet mentioned? I have heard about what happened. Perhaps, you are indeed the one who can save Payon!",
    ["Dialogue1054102"]="Please listen to what I have to say. Ten years ago, I entered Munak Cave with Lord Ocean Euin to reinforce the seal created by General Qi Euin. However, we realized that the monsters in the cave had been affected by the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and were starting to transform. We were afraid that if we did nothing, the monsters would eventually break the seal and return to the surface. So...",
    ["Dialogue1054103"]="In order to prevent the monsters from absorbing the fragment's power, we decided... we decided to remove the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the seal.",
    ["Dialogue1054104"]="(Sky Euin is shocked.)\n...What?! So the seal in the Butsudan has long been broken? Could this be why Munaks have been escaping the cave?",
    ["Dialogue1054105"]="(Taixuan nods his head solemnly.)\nThat's right. The fragment has been in the possession of the Indrah Sect since it was removed, but what I didn't expect was that the poison element in the fragment had already been fully activated. Anyone who goes near it will be severely poisoned.",
    ["Dialogue1054106"]="I initially intended to move the fragment to a secluded area in the mountains, but when I received word of the Lord's disappearance, I realized that someone must be after it. I therefore decided to take it to the Indrah Sect's Ancient Ancestral Hall and live there in seclusion.",
    ["Dialogue1054107"]="But nothing in this world is certain. That evildoer still found me, and the fragment has now fallen into his hands. I worry he will use its power to wreak havoc in Payon!",
    ["Dialogue1054108"]="He took the fragment into Munak Cave and intends to place it back into the Butsudan.",
    ["Dialogue1054109"]="Everything makes sense now. That evildoer used the fragment to create new Munaks. Then in order to strengthen its power, he intends to place it back into the Butsudan. When that happens, his Munak army will be even more formidable. Adventurer, Payon needs your help. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter Munak Cave</color> with me and the heroes of the Euin Family. We will find that evildoer and think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1054201"]="(Sky Euin is shocked.)\nY-you really are General Qi Euin!",
    ["Dialogue1054202"]="Looks like all of you are ready for battle.\n(Qi Euin turns toward you calmly.)\nAdventurer, have you brought my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sun-Piercing Bow</color>? It is my indispensable partner in battle.",
    ["Dialogue1054301"]="(There's a look of determination in Sky Euin's eyes.)\nIt's the duty of the Euin Family to protect this land. Our dedication and loyalty toward Payon is the same now as it was a thousand years ago. Everything is ready; let us <color=#CA2E0AFF>set off into the depths of Munak Cave</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1054401"]="(Sky Euin analyses the terrain.)\nIt's a labyrinth deep in the cave; it would be better if we <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up</color>. But it will make us more vulnerable. Everyone, take extra care every step of the way!",
    ["Dialogue1054501"]="(Moon Euin covers her nose.)\nHurry, hold your breath! See these flowers? They're <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moonlight Flowers</color>, the legendary flowers of death!",
    ["Dialogue1054502"]="According to ancient texts, the fragrance of the Moonlight Flower contains deadly poison. When inhaled by the living, death is imminent; but when inhaled by the dead, they will come back to life. These flowers were the reason Munaks appeared in Payon in the olden days. But Moonlight Flowers are supposed to be extinct; how can they be here? And they look very healthy too. This isn't a coincidence. Someone must be growing them!",
    ["Dialogue1054503"]="Your could be right. These Moonlight Flowers may have been grown by the man who's planning to create a Munak army. The flowers might just be the main ingredient in the poison that created the Munaks.",
    ["Dialogue1054504"]="(Moon Euin blinks in surprise.)\nBy the way... why are you the only one unaffected by the fragrance?!",
    ["Dialogue1054505"]="Erm, in any case, <color=#CA2E0AFF>we have to get rid of all these Moonlight Flowers</color>. Since their fragrance doesn't affect you, I'll leave this task to you!",
    ["Dialogue1054601"]="(Moon Euin looks at you curiously.)\nStrange, you really are unaffected... Could it be that there's something special about your physiology?",
    ["Dialogue1054602"]="In any case, it's too early to let our guard down. We might have missed some in this area! Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>go on ahead</color>. I'll stay behind to do a sweep of the area!",
    ["Dialogue1054701"]="(Comet Euin looks anxious and is sweating profusely.)\nW-what should I do now?! We were attacked by monsters and the senior disciples were poisoned in battle. Their lives are in danger. This is terrible. <size=24>What should I do?</size><size=26> What should I do?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1054702"]="Of course I know they need to be treated! But this god-forsaken place doesn't have the herbs to make antidotes.",
    ["Dialogue1054703"]="(Comet Euin suddenly has an idea.)\nWait a minute. Master once said that there's a type of <color=#CA2E0AFF>sparkling Zargon</color> in the bodies of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Horongs</color> that can be used to make antidotes!",
    ["Dialogue1054801"]="(Comet Euin accepts the Zargons with gratitude.)\nThis is great! I can start making the antidote now! Huh? Why are you still here? You don't have to wait for me. Once the senior disciples get better, I'll hurry over to regroup with you!",
    ["Dialogue1054901"]="(Sun Euin nods his head in gratitude.)\n...Thank you for your help. But compared to the situation here, I'm more worried about the safety of General Qi Euin and Master Taixuan.",
    ["Dialogue1054902"]="We were ambushed just now. <color=#CA2E0AFF>General Qi Euin</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Taixuan</color> have been forced back to the stone platform ahead. Can you check on them? I'll can take care of Uncle by myself.",
    ["Dialogue1055001"]="Looks like it's all over. Hurry and get Ocean Euin <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to the surface</color>. This is no place for the living.",
    ["Dialogue1055002"]="(Taixuan carefully checks Ocean Euin's injuries.)\nDon't worry, the general isn't seriously injured. With proper treatment, he'll make a full recovery in time.",
    ["Dialogue1055003"]="As for this poisonous Fragment of Ymir's Heart... Adventurer, please take it back to the surface and return it to where it belongs. This battle has shown me that Payon is no longer what it was.",
    ["Dialogue1055004"]="(Qi Euin looks at Sky Euin, Sun Euin, and the others with gratification.)\nA new generation of guardians is born. As long as we have them, Payon is equipped to fight against all evil and overcome any adversity, even without the holy relic.",
    ["Dialogue1055005"]="The living should not worry themselves with the world of the dead. I, together with the rest of the Spirit Quellers, will stay in this cave and continue to fight the monsters.\n\"Quell the spirits of the dead, protect the lives of the living.\"—This is the motto of the Spirit Quellers, both in life and in death.",
    ["Dialogue1055101"]="Adventurer, thank you for everything you've done for Payon. Sun has already sent Ocean safely back to the Lord's Residence, and Comet has escorted Master Taixuan back to the mountains. I believe they'll make a full recovery very soon. Although the dead cannot come back to life, the memories of the living will not wither. We will always remember what you have done for Payon!",
    ["Dialogue1055102"]="Come to think of it, the bards are sure to sing of what you've done today. I hope you never forget all that has happened.",
    ["Dialogue1055103"]="(Moon Euin starts to blush.)\nAnd I... I will never forget you.",
    ["Dialogue1055201"]="This is the fifth Fragment of Ymir's Heart that you've brought back. You will accumulate different experiences and make different friends as you search for each fragment. Remember, these experiences will one day become your most powerful weapon; they will help you triumph against evil and find light in darkness.",
    ["Dialogue1055202"]="You must continue onward. I have located the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sixth Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. It is in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen, the city of magic</color>. I cannot be sure if it is just an illusion, but the fragment seems to be surrounded by an Undead Aura from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Niflheim</color>. Successor of Odin's bloodline, be careful on your next journey.",
    ["Dialogue1055301"]="(The Ancient Ancestral Hall is in ruins. There are signs of a struggle... and Master Taixuan is nowhere to be found.)",
    ["Dialogue1055401"]="(The room is a mess. There are signs of a struggle... and Ocean Euin is nowhere to be found.)",
    ["Dialogue1055501"]="(The well water looks murky but a faintly sweet fragrance is coming from it.)",
    ["Dialogue1055601"]="(The footprints near the water are still wet. They can't have been here long. Quick, follow them.)",
    ["Dialogue1055701"]="(There are signs of a magic ritual on the ground. There seems to be something buried in the sand. Quick, dig it up.)",
    ["Dialogue1055801"]="(The rune starts to glow. A similar glow can be spotted nearby.)",
    ["Dialogue1055901"]="(The rune starts to glow. A similar glow can be spotted nearby.)",
    ["Dialogue1056001"]="(The magic circles nearby are clearly made up of alchemy runes, but why would there be an alchemist in Payon? Could it be him?)",
    ["Dialogue1056101"]="(The cauldron is bubbling and the concoction inside is emitting a strange power fluctuation. This feeling feels very familiar... and there isn't much of the concoction left.)",
    ["Dialogue1056201"]="(The wet footprints are headed forward. Clearly whoever made them—the owner of this alchemy workshop—left in a hurry not long ago.",
    ["Dialogue1056301"]="(The Moonlight Flower is dead. All that is left on the ground is this glowing Fragment of Ymir's Heart.)",
    ["Dialogue1060101"]="Adventurer, welcome to Geffen, the City of Magic! I've started looking forward to seeing which new place you'll show up in! But of course, only a brave and powerful hero like yourself would choose to visit a city as mysterious and dangerous as this one!",
    ["Dialogue1060102"]="(W smiles and waves her hands.) \nHaha, don't worry too much! Although Geffen is surrounded on three sides by the territories of different races and constantly dealing with monster trouble, it's jointly governed by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heines Family</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mage Guild</color>, so the people of the city have been able to get by perfectly fine.",
    ["Dialogue1060201"]="(W sighs and continues to smile without changing her face.)\nErm... What was I saying? Oh right, the people of this city can live calm and stable lives!",
    ["Dialogue1060202"]="You mean the violent earthquake that just happened? It must've been another attack by the other races.\nHey, why do you look so worried? It's thrilling everyday things like this that make Geffen so charming!",
    ["Dialogue1060203"]="But speaking of which, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>attacks from the other races</color> have indeed become much more frequent as of late, and I heard a passing member of the Mage Guild say that even the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic barrier</color> protecting Geffen is in danger. He kept nervously talking about how if the unrest between the races couldn't be quelled, it could result in the first war in a thousand years!",
    ["Dialogue1060204"]="Adventurer, I assume that's the information you're interested in? Because you ask if there's been anything unusual happening in every city you visit, I made extra sure to remember! (W puffs out her chest proudly.)",
    ["Dialogue1060205"]="If you want to learn more, you should ask </color>Master Jesqurienne<color=#CA2E0AFF> of the Mage Guild. She knows everything. She's the most knowledgeable person I've ever met. They say that she usually conducts magical research in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower</color>, which is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>middle of the city</color>. I'm sure she will give you a warm welcome.",
    ["Dialogue1060301"]="(Beudie looks at you curiously.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That's strange. Why would an adventurer be in Geffen Tower?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1060302"]="So you're here to visit Jesqurienne. Well, I'm afraid you'll have to wait. She's...",
    ["Dialogue1060303"]="Argh!\n<size=24>For crying out loud!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1060401"]="(Katrina puts her hands on her hips threateningly.)\nDid you see the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Artifact</color> the master sealed up? I've searched the whole of Geffen Tower but couldn't find it. Such a precious item can't have just vanished, can it?!",
    ["Dialogue1060402"]="And now there's a nasty dark elemental aura around Geffen Tower. Did no one else notice it? Are you guys...?\nWait, who are you? How come I've never seen you at the Mage Guild before?",
    ["Dialogue1060403"]="...Katrina, you're asking so many questions at once. No one can keep up. Let me introduce you. This adventurer has come to see Jesqurienne, and this grumpy...uh, I mean lovely girl! She's Jesqurienne's senior apprentice, Katrina.",
    ["Dialogue1060404"]="As for the Artifact that Katrina just mentioned, it's a priceless treasure that's been closely guarded by the Mage Guild for generations. As long as it's regularly maintained, <color=#CA2E0AFF>it can provide a steady stream of energy to the magic barrier around Geffen</color>. This time, it was Katrina's turn to perform maintenance.\n(Beudie glances cautiously at Katrina.)",
    ["Dialogue1060405"]="But it's gone...\nArgh! <size=24>For crying out loud!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1060406"]="No, I won't allow such a disaster to happen on my watch. No matter what, the problem must be solved. (Katrina's gazes sternly in your direction.) \nYou—yes, you! You look very reliable. Please \n<color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me to find the Artifact</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1060501"]="Look, the Artifact is supposed be on this table, but now it's gone and the room is filled with a disgusting <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental aura</color>. Since you can also feel it, you...you must understand what I mean, right?",
    ["Dialogue1060502"]="Yes, there must be a connection between the two. Maybe there'll be a clue if we follow the trail of dark energy to its end. Maybe the Artifact will be there!",
    ["Dialogue1060503"]="What? Can you think of any other possibility? If not, just <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me and follow the aura</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1060504"]="Come on, don't hesitate! I'm gonna see if the Artifact grew legs or if some fool with a death wish dared cause trouble in Geffen Tower!\n(Katrina rushes out.)",
    ["Dialogue1060601"]="Hohoho, I didn't think you would take this long find me! It looks like <color=#CA2E0AFF>his plan</color> has been a great success.",
    ["Dialogue1060602"]="Hahaha, you didn't think the Artifact was on me, did you? It's at the Place of Sages...or, more accurately, it WAS at the Place of Sages until just now.",
    ["Dialogue1060603"]="(Katrina realizes something.)\n...Did, did you...?!",
    ["Dialogue1060604"]="Aah, I see you finally figured it out. Yes, I did play a little trick at the Place of Sages! The empty table without the Artifact was just an illusion I created with my magic. In fact, just before you arrived here, the Artifact was still safe and sound on the table!",
    ["Dialogue1060605"]="It's a real pity that, rather than thinking about it carefully, you fell for appearances and foolishly followed the dark aura I left behind... which gave my <color=#CA2E0AFF>associate</color> the opportunity to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escape with the Artifact</color>. So thank you for your cooperation in making our plan a great success!",
    ["Dialogue1060606"]="(Katrina's face reddens with anger and shame.) \nYou... <size=24>Go to hell!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1060701"]="(Katrina clenches her fists and seethes with rage.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Damn, I fell into the Blood Clan monster's trap... and lost the precious Artifact. All because of my impulsiveness!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1060702"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...Why didn't I heed the advice of others? ...How will I explain this to the master?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1060703"]="I heard it! The monster said they possessed the power of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir's Heart</color>. But what does that have to do with you?",
    ["Dialogue1060704"]="What?<size=24>So you're the famous adventurer!</size>\nThe student from Criatura Academy who's been collecting Fragments of Ymir's Heart throughout the land and has stopped several monster rampages?",
    ["Dialogue1060705"]="Woah, why didn't you mention something so important? If I'd known, I wouldn't have bossed you around. If I'd known I should've...\n(Katrina blushes and looks away.)",
    ["Dialogue1060706"]="...Ahem! Anyway, now that I know who you are, I'll do my best to help you retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the Blood Clan. But it won't be easy. The Blood Clan monster's lair is beneath this tower!",
    ["Dialogue1060707"]="Since that place is so dangerous, the entrance to the underground caves has been sealed off by a magic ward for many years, and only the power of the Artifact can break the seal. So no matter what, we have to find the Artifact first!",
    ["Dialogue1060708"]="...As things stand, we can only turn to Master <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color>. They say she has a magical bond with the Artifact. She should have the solution to this problem. If I remember correctly, she should be outside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin Forest</color> fending off an attack. Maybe we can go and help her!",
    ["Dialogue1060801"]="(Jesqurienne looks very concerned and doesn't seem to notice your arrival.) \nWhat's going on with these monsters? This isn't going to work...",
    ["Dialogue1060802"]="Sorry, I don't have time for conversation right now. There's been constant <color=#CA2E0AFF>attacks from Goblins</color>. The magic barrier that protects Geffen can't withstand any more punishment!\n(Jesqurienne quickly looks you over.)\nOr perhaps I can ask for your help in fending off the Goblin assault? Then we can talk about what you came here for.",
    ["Dialogue1060901"]="How about it? Are you willing to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>fend off the Goblin attack</color>? This is a desperate situation. Your assistance will be crucial.",
    ["Dialogue1060902"]="(Jesqurienne looks at you appreciatively.) \nGreat, I'll leave this fight in your hands!",
    ["Dialogue1060903"]="It seems we have no choice but to allocate manpower from other regions to aid us in battle. But distant waters cannot quench close fires. I'm uncertain if everything will be ready in time.\n(Jesqurienne again looks worried.)",
    ["Dialogue1061001"]="You've done an impressive job, adventurer. Thanks to you, the Mage Guild can finally breathe a sigh of relief. Now that the Goblin army has been repelled, all that remains is to wait for the Artifact in Geffen Tower to replenish the magic barrier.",
    ["Dialogue1061002"]="Master! Actually...\n(Katrina looks down and recounts what happened inside Geffen Tower.)",
    ["Dialogue1061003"]="...<size=24>What?!</size>\nI was wondering why the breached section of the barrier was taking so long to regenerate. So the Artifact in Geffen Tower... has been stolen by the Blood Clan monster.",
    ["Dialogue1061004"]="(Katrina grits her teeth.)\nI'm sorry. It's all my fault.",
    ["Dialogue1061005"]="What matters now is that we find the Artifact as soon as possible. I'll use meditation to sense its location, but it will take a long time. In the meantime, I'll need you to protect Geffen Tower. When you're ready, talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bairde</color>. He's in charge of maintaining the magic barrier. He'll know what to do.",
    ["Dialogue1061101"]="As it's an instruction from Master Jesqurienne, let me inform you about the current situation. Goblins are a rare race of intelligent monsters. They are violent and constantly in conflict with one another. After the death of the Goblins' leader many years ago at the hands of Master Jesqurienne, the Goblins became even more chaotic and divided.",
    ["Dialogue1061102"]="But for some reason, the Goblins have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>reuniting</color> recently. The current priority is to learn why.\n(Bairde looks at you calmly.)\nSo, could you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate the Goblin camp</color> and see if you can find any clues?",
    ["Dialogue1061103"]="Seriously... Do we really need to be so cautious?\n(Katrina complains as she takes a step.)\nIf we just went in and destroyed the camp, the problem would be solved.",
    ["Dialogue1061104"]="Katrina, what I mean is for the adventurer here to go investigate. As for you... It's better that you come check the magic barrier with me. At least that job doesn't require any brains.",
    ["Dialogue1061105"]="Baaairde...\n<size=24>You can't talk to your senior like that!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1061201"]="(Bairde listens as you describe what you found in the Goblin camp.)\n...It sounds like they're performing some kind of <color=#CA2E0AFF>ritual</color>. Maybe it has something to do with why they're attacking Geffen. So our next move is...",
    ["Dialogue1061202"]="Our next move is to capture a Goblin of course! Then we squeeze information out of him, forcing him to reveal the Goblins' plan!\n(Katrina punches the air as her eyes light up with excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue1061203"]="......",
    ["Dialogue1061204"]="(Bairde lets out a heavy sigh.)\n...Fine. It really is the most efficient method. So please gather of some of the Goblins' favorite food: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crunchy Nuts</color>. Then <color=#CA2E0AFF>place them near the Goblin camp</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1061301"]="Well done, adventurer! Now that the Goblin's in the net...\n(Katrina cracks her knuckles menacingly.)\nWe have plenty of time to ask about the purpose of the ritual!",
    ["Dialogue1061302"]="...Wh-what are you doing?! Filthy humans! I'm not saying anything, gob!",
    ["Dialogue1061303"]="Heh heh, you won't be able to help it. Adventurer, take this potion and <color=#CA2E0AFF>pour it down his throat</color>!\n(Katrina takes out a small glass bottle.)",
    ["Dialogue1061304"]="I developed this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pungent Potion</color> myself. I'd like to test it out on this little fella and see how much my potion-making skills have improved!",
    ["Dialogue1061305"]="(Bairde shakes his head.)\n...Sigh.",
    ["Dialogue1061401"]="(Shorty covers his mouth in pain, his face full of snot and tears.) \nBleah... It's... it's poison, gob! Whoever made this... blargh... is... is a monster!",
    ["Dialogue1061402"]="<size=24>Just you try saying that again!</size>\n(Katrina takes out a dozen more glass bottles.)",
    ["Dialogue1061403"]="No, no, no! I'll-I'll say anything, gob! Blargh, you want to know the purpose of the rituals in the forest, don't you? They're for... We-we're trying to <color=#CA2E0AFF>resurrect our deceased leader</color>, gob!",
    ["Dialogue1061404"]="I heard from other Goblins that the spirit of the leader has traveled to the world of the dead. But by setting up multiple <color=#CA2E0AFF>totem poles</color> in the forest and conducting an evil ritual to draw on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental power</color> deep underground, the spirit of our leader can be brought back to life.",
    ["Dialogue1061405"]="Wait a minute, Goblins don't know anything about magic, much less the power of the elements. Who told you this?",
    ["Dialogue1061406"]="Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue1061407"]="(Jesqurienne suddenly awakens from her meditative state.)\n...I-I've located the Artifact. It's deep within the forest, in the middle of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin camp</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1061501"]="(Jesqurienne looks increasingly concerned as she listens to your account of what happened.)\n...Forces of darkness and dark elemental power? So the Blood Clan monster won't return the Artifact without a fight.",
    ["Dialogue1061502"]="...Adventurer, I don't want to hide anything from you. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Geffen Tower</color>, and I'll explain everything about the Artifact.",
    ["Dialogue1061601"]="Adventurer, I think there's something you need to know. The Blood Clan monster that stole the Artifact wasn't lying. It... it is indeed inextricably linked to the dark element.",
    ["Dialogue1061602"]="The Artifact is a precious relic left to the Mage Guild by Archmage <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin Heines</color>. It can extract the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental power</color> from underground and convert it into energy for the magic barrier surrounding Geffen. Of course it can be used for much more than that. For example, reviving the Goblin leader, which is the evil plan that the Blood Clan intends to carry out after they've mastered its power.",
    ["Dialogue1061603"]="It's not hard to imagine that as long as the Artifact is still in the hands the forces of darkness, led by the Blood Clan, the unrest in Goblin Forest will only be the beginning of disaster. If we fail to retrieve the Artifact, the magic barrier that protects the city will continue to weaken until it disappears completely.",
    ["Dialogue1061604"]="(Jesqurienne looks at you intently.)\nAdventurer, Geffen is in great peril, but you may be able to turn things around.",
    ["Dialogue1061605"]="Katrina told me of your deeds. It is clear to me that you came to Geffen in search of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. It seems it is time for you to learn about its history. Katrina, take this adventurer to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>forbidden book</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1061606"]="Come with me!",
    ["Dialogue1061701"]="(Jesqurienne has a solemn look on her face.)\nIt's been moved somewhere. What is the Blood Clan monster's goal?",
    ["Dialogue1061702"]="Just a moment ago, I detected the Artifact's aura again. It's been moved to the southern part of Geffen, in the vicinity of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>. I wonder what kind of trouble we're in for this time.",
    ["Dialogue1061703"]="(Jesqurienne shows a look of approval.)\nGreat, now please go and meet up with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bairde</color> near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>. He went on ahead.",
    ["Dialogue1061801"]="(Bairde nods calmly.)\nI knew Master Jesqurienne would send you instead of Katrina.",
    ["Dialogue1061802"]="(A look of slight surprise appears on Bairde's face.)\n...Look down on Katrina? Quite the opposite. She's most admirable. I say this only because Orcs revere raw power and detest those who use elemental power to inflict damage, like mages.",
    ["Dialogue1061803"]="Here, the Mage Guild would only be asking for trouble if they stepped in to solve the problem. Even I can only repair the magic barrier on the perimeter, unable to go deeper into the village to investigate the situation!",
    ["Dialogue1061804"]="I knew you would say that. Then, I'll leave it to you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate anything unusual happening in Orc Village</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1061901"]="(Joao trembles with rage, his eyes staring into his huge, clenched fist.)\nA human... Even a human has helped me.\nBut my people... My own brother! Are trying to kill me!",
    ["Dialogue1061902"]="<size=24>Well, who else do you think sent those soldiers?!\nThey were once warriors who fought for honor. How could they do something as dishonorable as launch a sneak attack on one of their own clan?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1061903"]="(After breathing heavily for a while, Joao calms down.)\nRight, I shouldn't have blown up at you like that. You saved my life, but this is far from over.",
    ["Dialogue1061904"]="Look at the wounds on my body. They are proof that I fought back desperately while being relentlessly hunted down, but who would've thought that the one who ordered those warriors to kill me was my own brother, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chief Jolak</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1061905"]="I don't understand why Jolak would do this! But one thing is for certain: Since he tried to kill me, my wife and son must also be in grave danger. But I can't make it back to the village to check if they're safe!\n(Joao grits his teeth in pain.)",
    ["Dialogue1061906"]="Take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>helmet</color> and give it to my wife <color=#CA2E0AFF>Murloma</color>. She'll know what it means. Tell her it's no longer safe for us here and to <color=#CA2E0AFF>flee the village with our son</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1062001"]="(Murloma holds Joao's helmet tightly.)\nThank goodness... he's still alive.",
    ["Dialogue1062002"]="(Murloma is silent for a moment, then she slowly raises her head, her face full of tears.)\nLeave with our son? Joao must not know that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jofar</color> has just been taken by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gerrush</color>'s men! They didn't even utter a word of explanation, as if they weren't committing an act of evil. The chief had even given his approval!",
    ["Dialogue1062003"]="He is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shaman elder</color> of the village. He lives in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shaman's hut</color> at the bottom of the mountain. I don't understand why such an esteemed elder would want to steal a mother's child from her. But whatever the reason, I won't set foot out of the village until I find out what's happened to Jofar!",
    ["Dialogue1062101"]="(Murloma listens to you recount the conversation you heard in the shaman's hut. First she looks very confused, and then devastated.)\n...Underground cave? Are you saying that Gerrush ordered his men... to take my son into the underground cave?!",
    ["Dialogue1062102"]="The underground cave is where the Orcs perform their <color=#CA2E0AFF>rituals</color>. The only ones who come out alive are Gerrush and his disciples! Those who are sent there... all become <color=#CA2E0AFF>sacrificial offerings</color>, never to return. Is it possible that Jofar... my son...?\n(Fear and despair fill Murloma's eyes, and her body sways weakly.)",
    ["Dialogue1062103"]="...You're right. We have to tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Joao</color>. He'll know what to do!",
    ["Dialogue1062201"]="(Joao hits his fist against his chest to greet you, then hurries to his wife.)\nLet me look at you... Good, at least they didn't hurt you! If they touched even a single hair on you or Jofar's— Wait, where's Jofar?",
    ["Dialogue1062202"]="He...\n(Murloma fights back tears as she tells Joao what happened.)",
    ["Dialogue1062203"]="<size=24>What?!</size>\n(Joao lets out a furious roar.)\nBrother... is this why you were preventing my return to the village?!",
    ["Dialogue1062204"]="...There's no mistaking it. If my brother hadn't sent his men to stop me outside the village, how could my son have been kidnapped? If Gerrush hadn't received my brother's approval, how would he have dared commit such a heinous act? This whole thing has been a conspiracy from the start, a plot by my brother and Gerrush to sacrifice Jofar!",
    ["Dialogue1062205"]="(Murloma's voice trembles.)\nSo what should we do?",
    ["Dialogue1062206"]="There's no turning back now. Since the chief is so obsessed that won't even spare an innocent child, overthrowing him is the only way to truly save my family and the Orc race!",
    ["Dialogue1062207"]="Human adventurer, I have decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>overthrow the chief</color>. But before I can do that, I must go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>battle arena</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat all the warriors</color> to win the hearts of my people! My Orc brethren who support me will join me in this glorious battle. Will you fight alongside me?",
    ["Dialogue1062301"]="Well fought, human! My victory in this battle has earned me the support of all the clansmen present. Now we just have to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chief's hut</color>.\n(Joao's eyebrows lower and his eyes glaze over.)",
    ["Dialogue1062302"]="How I wish this fight for leadership was only between my brother and me, but the truth is, it's going to bring bloodshed to the whole village! My clansmen revere strength. We are bound to fight to the last drop of blood to support different leaders. Such a situation would undoubtedly spell the end for the Orcs.",
    ["Dialogue1062303"]="Human adventurer, could you do me one more favor? I ask that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>subdue my opponents</color> but <color=#CA2E0AFF>spare their lives</color>! Due to my standing, I'm not in a position to stop this terrible fight. Now only you, an outsider, can save my people from unnecessary death!",
    ["Dialogue1062401"]="(Joao grabs Woharu's shoulders angrily, his eyes glowing red with rage.)\nMy brother's not here, so where is he?!\nI don't have time to waste; you better not test my patience!",
    ["Dialogue1062402"]="Hmph, after what's happened, why should I obey your orders? I'll end up the same as those clansmen who opposed you: cut down by your blade!",
    ["Dialogue1062403"]="(The ringleader has an incredulous look on his face.)\nYou-you mean to tell me that those who opposed Joao didn't die? And he asked you to spare their lives? But why... why would he do that? Why would someone that makes an enemy of his own brother be so merciful?",
    ["Dialogue1062404"]="...Do you think I wanted to do this? If I hadn't been forced to...\n(Joao clenches his fists and falls into a painful silence.)",
    ["Dialogue1062405"]="I can't believe something like that happened. I was wrong about you. I'll tell you everything I know! Not long ago, Gerrush hurriedly asked the chief to leave, saying that Joao had already staged a coup and that it would be too late if we didn't enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underground cave</color> to carry out our plan. Now that I think about it, the chief was looking very strange, and his hands were shaking before he left.",
    ["Dialogue1062406"]="Brother... What is it that made you lose your conscience?!\n(Joao roars as he rushes out.)",
    ["Dialogue1062501"]="Damn, these <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wandering Orc Zombies</color> keep getting in the way! We've got to fight our way out of here quickly!",
    ["Dialogue1062601"]="(Joao looks shocked.)\nThis is... Nagosh?! What's he doing here?",
    ["Dialogue1062602"]="Nagosh is my brother's guard. Except for special circumstances, he never leaves my brother's side.\n(Joao crouches down and examines Nagosh.)\nWait, the color of his nails... How's this possible? Who could have poisoned him with that?",
    ["Dialogue1062603"]="But if that's the case... Adventurer, gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cliff Grass</color> from nearby, quick!",
    ["Dialogue1062701"]="Good. Now get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Foul Slime</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Skeletons</color>! If this works... he's got a lot of explaining to do.",
    ["Dialogue1062801"]="(Joao mixes the Cliff Grass with the Foul Slime and stuffs it into Nagosh's mouth.)\nNow we just have to wait...",
    ["Dialogue10628010"]="It's ludicrous. Did our sibling bond mean so little to my brother that it could not withstand Gerrush's words of deception? Since he won't open his eyes to the truth, it's up to me to help him regain his senses!",
    ["Dialogue1062802"]="(Nagosh's throat quivers, then his limbs jerk and his eyes snap open.)\nCh-Chief... Watch out!",
    ["Dialogue1062803"]="What did I feed Nagosh? It was an <color=#CA2E0AFF>antidote for a special poison</color>. From what I understand, the poison has a very complicated recipe. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>shaman elder</color> is the only one in the village who can make it. It seems clear who poisoned Nagosh.",
    ["Dialogue1062804"]="(Nagosh seems to have regained consciousness and suddenly looks incredibly excited.)\nYou... You're Joao! Please, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Chief Jolak</color>. Don't let him make another mistake!",
    ["Dialogue1062805"]="Listen to me. What the chief has done was not his intention. It was Gerrush who sent men to hunt you down. And it was his idea to take your son! Originally, the chief was only slightly concerned about you as a threat, but the shaman elder stoked his insecurities, persuading him to believe that you would eventually usurp him.",
    ["Dialogue1062806"]="—Ludicrous! I'd never thought of such a thing!",
    ["Dialogue1062807"]="But that doesn't mean the chief didn't. After all, he's getting older, while his brother is still in his prime. What's more, not so long ago, you openly opposed the chief's idea of attacking Geffen, causing him to lose face in front of the clansmen.",
    ["Dialogue1062808"]="What? Was I supposed to support his idea?! Encourage war on the humans of Geffen and the occupation of their territory because our <color=#CA2E0AFF>land is contaminated by the dark element</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1062809"]="I know you're right... as does the rest of the tribe! That's why more warriors rallied behind you. And it was then that the chief's mentality changed, allowing Gerrush's plot to take hold.",
    ["Dialogue1062901"]="(Gerrush spreads his arms wide in excitement.)\nHmph, so what if you defeat me? My spell is complete, and this baby will be my greatest contribution to the Orc clan!",
    ["Dialogue1062902"]="Wha... <size=24>what do you mean?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1062903"]="At the battle arena, you once said that our tribe could conquer anyone, remember? Open your eyes to the reality that Orcs are slowly headed for extinction! While we vie for power in this barren land, the cities of men are constantly expanding. Sooner or later, they will take over this territory. And what have you done about it?",
    ["Dialogue1062904"]="Your foolishness lies in your over-obsession with so-called justice. Unlike you, I would do anything to bring about our triumph! That's why I listened to the voice that arose during the ritual and opened the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color> for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blood Clan</color>'s arrival... even though I knew they would bring evil magic from the world of the dead. But so what? If you want to achieve great things, you must make sacrifices!",
    ["Dialogue1062905"]="(Gerrush's devious eyes narrow and the corners of his mouth slightly rise.) \nYes, the Blood Clan taught me how to use magic to release the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental power</color> underground and showed me the way to strengthen our people. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Those with the strongest bloodlines in the clan are to merge with the dark elemental power</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1062906"]="Look, this baby is the result of the experiment. He is the future hope of the Orcs!\nAnd Joao, hero of the Orcs, you should be proud of your boy!",
    ["Dialogue1062907"]="Gerrush...\n(Joao's longsword clangs.)\n<size=24>You lunatic!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1063001"]="(Joao's face is scrunched up, showing both pain and resentment.)\nJofar, my little boy... I failed to protect you.",
    ["Dialogue1063002"]="...No, it's I who failed to protect you all.",
    ["Dialogue1063101"]="Joao and this human adventurer... I just saw everything. The truly despicable, foolish, and unforgivable one is not Gerrush or that Blood Clan monster, but me!",
    ["Dialogue1063102"]="(Joao lowers his head in silence.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue1063103"]="It was I who was too narrow-minded, who was deceived and did not perceive it in time. If you are still willing to give me a chance to make amends, then return to the village and meet me in front of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chief's hut</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1063201"]="I know that no matter how much I apologize, it won't make up for my actions, but I can still organize our clan's warriors to take revenge on the Blood Clan and get Jofar back!",
    ["Dialogue1063202"]="It could take a long time before we achieve our goals, and maybe the Blood Clan will be far more powerful than I can imagine. But I'm ready to put my life on the line for this campaign because even if I don't return, the Orcs will still have a powerful leader!\n(Jolak looks to Joao.)",
    ["Dialogue1063203"]="Brother...",
    ["Dialogue1063204"]="What happened this time made me realize the truth, that I am unqualified, both mentally and physically, to be the leader of the Orcs. But you, my brother Joao, have always upheld justice and your principles. You truly bring honor to our ancient clan! I'm certain that you'll be able to ensure our people's survival by leading us on the right path. As for the humans of Geffen...",
    ["Dialogue1063205"]="We will help you get through this.",
    ["Dialogue1063301"]="(Bairde calmly dusts off his sleeves and looks at you.)\nAdventurer, it seems that you've helped the Orcs quell the unrest. It so happens that Master Jesqurienne has two important messages for me to deliver.",
    ["Dialogue1063302"]="(Jolak looks wary.)\nHuman mage... How did you get into the village?",
    ["Dialogue1063303"]="Naturally, I walked straight in through the front entrance. Don't worry, the Orc warriors who tried to stop me, or rather tried to take my life, are unharmed. The guildmaster specifically told me not to fight back. However, I won't deny that I used stun spells on a few of them.",
    ["Dialogue1063304"]="Anyway, the reason I came here is to first convey Master Jesqurienne's sincerity to Chief Jolak. The Mage Guild heard of the disaster that has befallen this land and has decided to help you rid the ground of the dark element and provide supplies to Orc Village until the crisis is over.",
    ["Dialogue1063305"]="(Jolak stands still for a moment in amazement.)\nBut...",
    ["Dialogue1063306"]="The second message is for to you, adventurer. The guildmaster requests that we <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Geffen Tower</color> immediately for an important discussion.",
    ["Dialogue1063401"]="I've been observing the movement of the Artifact. Not long ago, <color=#CA2E0AFF>its aura moved again</color>. Perhaps your experience in Orc Village can help explain this.",
    ["Dialogue1063402"]="...This is exactly what I was worried about. I sensed that the Artifact's aura was being shrouded by the dark element, but occasionally it leaks out a bit. The Blood Clan monster that stole the Artifact doesn't seem to be afraid of his location or plans being discovered. Perhaps the true purpose of the forces of darkness is not to create chaos around Geffen.",
    ["Dialogue1063403"]="You're right. The only way to find out what they're really up to is to track down the location of the Artifact. Please meet up with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Katrina</color> outside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color>. The Artifact's aura is in the area; she's already rushed over to investigate.",
    ["Dialogue1063501"]="(Bairde looks around, then lets out a quiet sigh.)\nUgh, I knew this would happen.",
    ["Dialogue1063502"]="As expected of Katrina, even her speed on foot is extraordinary. Let's just look around and see if she left any <color=#CA2E0AFF>clues</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1063601"]="(The trembling Woofka looks afraid but still tries to maintain a threatening posture.)\nWh-who are you?! How dare you trespass into the Spinecrusher Clan's camp? Y-you've even killed my most elite guards!",
    ["Dialogue1063602"]="(Woofka suddenly regains his confidence and puffs out his chest proudly.)\nHey, ya wanna know how I took care of this mage lying here in the dirt? It might scare you to death if I told you. I sent my men to ambush her of course!",
    ["Dialogue1063603"]="We Spinecrushers may not be very powerful, but when it comes to cunning, we are unbeatable in the forest! My people could never defeat a mage in a one-on-one fight, but if we were to make a dart from the Crispweed that grows in the forest and stealthily blow it at the enemy, then... Ahahaha\nHey, why are you looking at me like that?",
    ["Dialogue1063604"]="(Bairde glares at Woofka without saying a single word.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue1063605"]="(Woofka's jaw drops and his expression quickly switches to distress and fear.)\nI really didn't know that! I thought she was another invader... but... but the plant isn't poisonous, I swear! She'll wake up in a few minutes.",
    ["Dialogue1063606"]="<size=24>It... it was horrible!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1063701"]="(The Kobold guard gasps for air.)\nChieftain Woofka... W-we have a big problem! The patrol guards. They... they...",
    ["Dialogue1063702"]="Out with it! What the hell happened?!",
    ["Dialogue1063703"]="I-I was supposed to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>eastern glade</color> for guard duty, but when I got there, I found a number of our brothers <color=#CA2E0AFF>lying by the side of the road</color>! At first, I thought they'd just fainted, but when I checked on them, I realized that... that they weren't breathing! I was worried danger still lurked nearby, so I came back to report the situation and wait for your instructions!",
    ["Dialogue1063704"]="(Woofka looks struck with horror.)\nThey're... dead? What killed the guards? What on earth happened to them?",
    ["Dialogue1063705"]="Adventurer, why don't you help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kobolds investigate the situation</color>? Maybe this matter is also related to the missing Artifact.",
    ["Dialogue1063706"]="Don't worry, I'll take Katrina back to Geffen Tower. But if she doesn't wake up...\n(Bairde gives Woofka a death glare.)\nI'll be back to settle the score.",
    ["Dialogue1063801"]="(As Woofka listens to your account of the situation, a glint of fear appears in his eyes.) \n...Was it... was it the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skullsplitter Clan</color> that killed my people? They've gotten away with so much in this land. What more do they want now?!",
    ["Dialogue1063802"]="Sigh, this would never have happened if the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kobold God</color> was still around! Hundreds of years ago, the Kobolds were unified under our first leader, the Kobold God. But with his death, our clan immediately fractured.",
    ["Dialogue1063803"]="Now the Kobolds have split into four clans: the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spinecrusher, Gutripper, Arrowtongue, and Skullsplitter Clans</color>. Due to their warlike nature, the Skullsplitter Clan grew to be the strongest. Although I've suffered their bullying ways for many years, I never thought that they would... that they would start brazenly slaughtering my people!",
    ["Dialogue1063804"]="(Woofka looks dejected, his ears drooping down.)\nYou–you think I don't want to? But the Spinecrusher Clan is the weakest of the four clans, and if it weren't for our crafty tactics, we wouldn't have survived this long. Doing something like raising an army to fight back would only hasten our demise!",
    ["Dialogue1063805"]="(Woofka's eyes light up.)\nYou mean, allying with the other clans? Why didn't I think of such a great idea? Maybe the others have suffered the same from the Skullsplitter Clan!",
    ["Dialogue1063806"]="But who should we go to? How about asking the neighboring <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gutripper Clan</color> for help?! It's said that their chieftain, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooflard</color> loves <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat n' Pumpkin</color>. So make it and take it to him as a gesture of goodwill.",
    ["Dialogue1063901"]="(Wooflard looks uneasy as he listens to you describe the situation.)\nWell, as much as I'd like to help...",
    ["Dialogue1063902"]="(Wooflard sighs.)\nRecently, the guards of our clan have been disappearing without a trace. Even if I united with the Spinecrusher Clan, I don't possess the manpower to deal with the Skullsplitter Clan. Our only hope is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>locate the guards' whereabouts</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1064001"]="(The guard looks at you in surprise.)\nWhat a strange turn of events... Chased by the Skullsplitters and saved by humans.",
    ["Dialogue1064002"]="I'm just as confused as you are! This is Gutripper territory, but a bunch of Skullsplitters started chasing after me! <color=#CA2E0AFF>A few of my comrades are still on patrol around here.</color> Can you help check if they're okay? I need to report the situation to Chieftain Wooflard as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue1064101"]="(Wooflard looks at you impatiently.)\nWell, did you find the guards? I heard what happened from the returning patrolmen. What about the rest of them? Are they safe?",
    ["Dialogue1064102"]="(Wooflard buries his face in the palm of his right paw and remains silent for a long time.)\nThis is unforgivable. Why would the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skullsplitter Clan</color> want to inflict such cruelty on their fellow Kobolds? I used to follow Woofsten's orders for the purpose of ensuring the safety of our people. But it seems that my weakness has only fueled his arrogance!",
    ["Dialogue1064103"]="Human adventurer, can I entrust you to seek out the chieftain of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arrowtongue Clan</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooflorn</color>? Although he has always chosen not to embroil himself in such power struggles, if he hears what you have to say, there's no way he'll sit idly by. Now is the time to rise up and fight—the Kobolds need Wooflorn's wisdom!",
    ["Dialogue1064201"]="(Wooflorn asks to hear the story and squints contemplatively.)\n...I'm afraid this will not be an easy task to handle.",
    ["Dialogue1064202"]="Consider this: The Skullsplitter chieftain, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Woofsten</color>, must surely have realized that this kind of aggression would cause outrage. If the other clans join forces to stop him, his life, as well as the future of the Skullsplitters, would be placed in grave danger. But even so, Woofsten took the risk of making such a rash move. I fear that a deeper secret lies behind all this.",
    ["Dialogue1064203"]="What's more, the Skullsplitter Clan is immense, so it's very difficult to invade their camp. If we act rashly before knowing Woofsten's scheme, we will suffer unnecessary losses.",
    ["Dialogue1064204"]="(Wooflorn thinks for a moment.)\nPlease go to Kordt Forest and pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crispweed</color>, and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crucian Carp</color> as well.",
    ["Dialogue1064301"]="Very good. Now, please put these ingredients <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the cauldron</color> and wait while they cook.",
    ["Dialogue1064401"]="Well done. Now, if you take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crispy Carp</color> and place it <color=#CA2E0AFF>where the Skullsplitter guards patrol</color>, you should be able to sneak into the Skullsplitter stronghold. As for <color=#CA2E0AFF>figuring out what Woofsten is up to</color>... Human adventurer, you will have to rely on your own good judgment.",
    ["Dialogue1064501"]="How did a human like you break into the mighty Skullsplitter stronghold? We have no grievances with your kind, so why are you attacking us like this all of a sudden?",
    ["Dialogue1064502"]="(Woofsten flashes a contemptuous glance your way.)\nOh? So you're here to take revenge for those who died... You seek justice on behalf of those weaklings? Unfortunately for you, you're too late. Soon, I shall command the entire Kobold race with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Luszwen's</color> help!",
    ["Dialogue1064503"]="The Kobolds once possessed a legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine weapon</color>. Whoever possesses it has the power to rule the entire race. According to my research, <color=#CA2E0AFF>this divine weapon was once wielded by our first leader, the Kobold God</color>. After the Kobold God passed away, the whereabouts of the weapon became unknown. But who could have anticipated that the Lord of the Blood Clan, Luszwen, would actually help me locate it?!",
    ["Dialogue1064504"]="Luszwen told me that the Artifact fell into the world of the dead with its master, and that by using the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental power</color> of his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Artifact</color>, he can summon the divine weapon back to this world. All I need to do is to take a few hundred lives. If I can provide Luszwen with enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kobold blood</color>, he'll finally be able to replenish his Artifact's power!",
    ["Dialogue1064505"]="Well, it sounds like a good deal, doesn't it? If the Kobold God in the netherworld knew...\n—Hey, what do you think you're doing, holding your weapon against my neck like that?!",
    ["Dialogue1064506"]="...Y-You want to know <color=#CA2E0AFF>where Luszwen and I will be meeting</color>?\n(Woofsten glances down at the weapon pressed against his neck.)\nAll right, all right! I'll take you there!",
    ["Dialogue1064601"]="I knew that as long as I held the Artifact in my possession, you would come to me, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1064602"]="(Woofsten steps forward hurriedly.)\nHey! Haven't I spilled enough Kobold blood yet? When can we summon the divine weapon to the world of the living?!",
    ["Dialogue1064603"]="(Luszwen slowly turns his head and looks at Woofsten.)\nOh... Well, it's rather embarrassing to say, but the truth is, the divine weapon has been in this world all along!",
    ["Dialogue1064604"]="If you wish to know the reason why, all you have to do is ask the Kobold God. After all, it was initially he who chose to use his body as a medium to forever seal the divine weapon in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>totem pole</color> behind me.",
    ["Dialogue1064605"]="It was because of this that the divine weapon of the Kobolds did not reach the world of the dead, but is also because of this ancient sacrifice that the spirit of the Kobold God will forever linger in the limbo between the past and the present, unable to break free! So it seems that the Kobold God in fact wishes for no one to obtain his weapon. How aggrieved he would be to see Woofsten's despicable behavior here in the mortal realm. Hehe...",
    ["Dialogue1064606"]="(Angry and shamed, Woofsten bares his teeth ferociously.)\nYou... You're lying! It can't be true. I've never heard of such a tale!",
    ["Dialogue1064607"]="Hehe... If you don't believe me, why don't you go to the totem pole and see for yourself? I have more important matters to attend to, so I will not be able to accompany you!",
    ["Dialogue1064701"]="(Woofsten stands in place, struck dumb, with his eyes staring blankly ahead.)\nIt can't be... The divine weapon of the Kobold God... How could it be sealed in this totem pole?",
    ["Dialogue1064702"]="...Alright! Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Kobold God totem pole</color> and take a look!",
    ["Dialogue1064801"]="(Woofsten walks over and reads the Kobold characters carefully.)\nLet me take a look... These words...\nHow... how can this be possible!",
    ["Dialogue1064802"]="(Woofsten falls to his knees with a thud.)\n—\"I will sleep here with the divine weapon, so that the descendants of the Kobold clan will no longer have to fight for it.\"",
    ["Dialogue1064901"]="(Jesqurienne listens to you carefully.)\nAre you saying that Luszwen has been manipulating the Kobold clans in order to cause chaos in Kordt Forest? Such treachery really is quite unbelievable, but thanks to you, things seem to have calmed down between the Kobold clans.",
    ["Dialogue1064902"]="Of course, Katrina's efforts cannot be ignored. If it were not for her being captured by the Kobolds...",
    ["Dialogue1064903"]="(Katrina blushes as brightly as a tomato.)\n...Don't be silly, Bairde!",
    ["Dialogue1064904"]="Ahem! To put things plainly, the next battle will be the last between us and the Blood Clan, as I noticed not long ago that the aura of the Artifact had sunk <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep beneath Geffen Tower</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1064905"]="Indeed. The demon Luszwen has finally taken the Artifact back to the Blood Clan's lair, and the immense power of the Artifact has caused the entrance to Geffen Dungeon to open. The true intentions of the forces of darkness... The answer we're looking for lies dormant beneath Geffen Tower. If we are truly ready, it's time for us to face them.",
    ["Dialogue1065001"]="(Jesqurienne stops suddenly, her eyes narrowing warily.)\nThis power... What's going on?",
    ["Dialogue1065002"]="I have been trying to pinpoint the specific location of the Artifact, but the moment I went underground, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I could detect a number of similar dark elemental power sources.</color>...It's impossible to make an accurate judgment under these circumstances. It appears that the fastest way to locate the Artifact will be to <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up and investigate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1065101"]="(Alexia's soul floats by the tombstone, but there still seems to be a certain glow in her eyes.)\nWe finally meet, young adventurer. I was just wondering, what would I do if you didn't trust my voice?",
    ["Dialogue1065102"]="(Alexia gives a gentle smile.)\nYes, I magically transmitted my voice to your consciousness and used it to summon you. I did this because I sense a familiar aura about you. It's the same as that of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Merlin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1065103"]="Before my death, I was a disciple of Archmage Merlin Heines, and I was lucky enough to be a member of the organization he founded, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pentagram</color>. In the battle against the Blood Clan monster thousands of years ago, most of my companions and I were killed on Geffenia soil. Since then, my soul has been haunting this tombstone.",
    ["Dialogue1065104"]="Adventurer, I know what you're looking for. The Blood Clan monster who possesses the dark Fragment of Ymir's Heart dwelled in this dungeon not long ago.",
    ["Dialogue1065105"]="It was this Blood Clan monster that opened the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gaps</color> across this underground world in an attempt to summon hordes of undead monsters from Niflheim. The next gap is just to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color> of here. Young adventurer, please head there quickly.",
    ["Dialogue1065201"]="(Bairde nods at you.)\n...Thank you. It's a good thing you came in time. I've become entangled in these <color=#CA2E0AFF>vines</color> and cannot move.",
    ["Dialogue1065202"]="It's no use. These vines can't be destroyed. They seem to have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>infected by dark elements</color>. Normal attacks have no effect on them.",
    ["Dialogue1065203"]="(A mysterious man's voice calls from afar.)\n...Poisonous Ghoul blood...\n...Only by <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkling poisonous Ghoul blood on the vines</color> can they be severed.",
    ["Dialogue1065301"]="I didn't think sprinkling Ghoul blood on the vines would really work, but that mysterious voice just now...\n(Bairde looks aside in disbelief.)\n...Did it come from this <color=#CA2E0AFF>tombstone</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1065401"]="(Huey's soul floats beside the tombstone, looking at you calmly.)\n...Young adventurer, was it my companion Alexia who guided you here?",
    ["Dialogue1065402"]="My name is Huey. I was one of the apprentices of Archmage Merlin. I think Alexia must have told you the tale of Pentagram. Even in death, we few souls of the dead still desire to guard the last battlefield—our final mission as members of Pentagram.",
    ["Dialogue1065403"]="(Huey squints as he watches you)\n...Interesting, very interesting... You seem to possess the same aura as my master. Maybe you have what it takes to quell this turmoil. Adventurer, please hurry to <color=#CA2E0AFF>the abbey in the east</color> as soon as possible. Another <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color> can be found there.",
    ["Dialogue1065501"]="(Katrina clenches her teeth and stares at you with stubborn eyes.)\n...You... you're not here to laugh at me, are you? <color=#CA2E0AFF>If I hadn't been poisoned</color>... I wouldn't be in such a state.",
    ["Dialogue1065502"]="Didn't you see, from this weird rift just now? A whole bunch of monsters just came pouring out! I was trying to fight them off when I was poisoned. But this kind of poison doesn't seem to be of this world. I've tried all the magic medicine I have but can't cure it!",
    ["Dialogue1065503"]="(A mysterious man's voice drifts toward you from afar.)\n...This poison is not particularly difficult to cure.\nGather <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Essence</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jakks</color>, and you'll be fine.",
    ["Dialogue1065504"]="...Who are you? Show yourself!",
    ["Dialogue1065601"]="(Katrina turns her head to one side with a red face.)\n*cough, cough* I'm sorry to bother you like this... but there's still something I need your help with. It's just... that <color=#CA2E0AFF>voice just now</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1065701"]="(Wyatt's soul floats by the tombstone, grinning at you with interest.)\nWow! You two must be brave to run into this cave. You're after that Blood Clan monster, are you? Trying to recover the Artifact turning Geffen Tower on its head, eh?",
    ["Dialogue1065702"]="You see, a thousand years ago, it was our little Pentagram collective and Archmage Merlin who made that Artifact. We sealed the forces of darkness underground together! I was wondering before... Why did it seem as though the magic ward here was weakening? That was until I saw that Blood Clan monster sneaking by with the Artifact in its clutches. Then I knew. You went ahead and lost it!",
    ["Dialogue1065703"]="(Wyatt's smile suddenly disappears.)\n...If things are as you say they are... everything's starting to make sense.",
    ["Dialogue1065704"]="The Blood Clan is using the Artifact to create chaos in Geffen, merely to distract the Mage Guild, and then create dimensional gaps underground to summon an army of undead demons from Niflheim. This is their true goal!",
    ["Dialogue1065705"]="(Wyatt props his head up with a single hand.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Such an intricate plan... It must be the work of</color> Dracula.",
    ["Dialogue1065706"]="Dracula is the leader of the Blood Clan. A thousand years ago, he coveted the power of the Ymir's Heart fragments! Fortunately, he was defeated by Merlin in the end. But now that the Artifact has fallen into the hands of the Blood Clan, I'm afraid they will soon break the seal and return to Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue1065707"]="Adventurer, please hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>teleporter</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>south</color>. From what I saw, that Blood Clan monster who opened the dimensional gap was heading in that direction!",
    ["Dialogue1065708"]="(Katrina nods at you with conviction.)\nI think Jesqurienne must have gone there. Hurry. I'll catch up with you once I regain my strength!",
    ["Dialogue1065801"]="(Alexia looks at you with gentle eyes.)\nAdventurer, you did it. What Pentagram and Master Merlin once protected with their lives: the peace of Midgard. Now it is in your hands.",
    ["Dialogue1065802"]="We... we'll keep up our watch here, of course! These ruins are not just our place of burial. For the deceased members of Pentagram, this is also where we found glory.",
    ["Dialogue1065803"]="It's you, adventurer. It is dangerous for the living to remain in the world of the dead for too long. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>quickly take the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and return to the surface</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1065901"]="Adventurer, thank you for your contribution to Geffen. You have not only helped us calm the unrest between our neighboring tribes, but also thwarted the forces of darkness in their plot to return to the world. You have shown more than just extraordinary wisdom and courage. In the battle against Dracula, the Blood Clan leader, your performance was truly astonishing. You remind me of that hero of old.",
    ["Dialogue1065902"]="They say the blood of Odin flowed through that hero's veins. Can the same be said of you?\n(Jesqurienne's eyebrows stretch out, revealing a smile of relief.)\nMaybe this was fate. It seems that there is no one better suited to dealing with this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> than you.",
    ["Dialogue1065903"]="It is indeed as you say, this fragment is the core of the Artifact. Without it, the Artifact can no longer be used to power Geffen's magic barrier. But don't worry, we will find another way to protect the city, just like the original founders of the Mage Guild—this is what the elders of Pentagram did.",
    ["Dialogue1066001"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, thank you for bringing back the sixth Fragment of Ymir's Heart. I believe you must have realized by now that this sacred relic left behind by the giant Ymir does not distinguish between good and evil. In the hands of the good, it becomes a weapon to eradicate evil and protect the people of this world, but in the hands of evil, it becomes the bane of all living things.",
    ["Dialogue1066002"]="Good or evil, it all depends on the heart of the possessor. I'm glad to know that even in the presence of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart, surrounded by dark elemental power, your heart still shines brightly.",
    ["Dialogue1066003"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> as soon as possible, as the next Fragment of Ymir's Heart can be found there, and it may disappear at any time. I sense that the fragment is caught in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>turbulent flow of time and space</color>, and only when you <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the door to another dimension</color> will you be able to obtain it.",
    ["Dialogue1066101"]="(There are also magic marks on the table. It seems that something placed on it has just been removed. There's an unpleasant aura nearby. After inhaling it, you even feel dizzy.)",
    ["Dialogue1066201"]="(Nagosh's breathing is pretty weak. Although he doesn't have any obvious injuries, he has already lost consciousness.)",
    ["Dialogue1066301"]="(There's a disarray of claw marks and a strange drag mark on the ground. They look like they've only been formed recently.)",
    ["Dialogue1066401"]="(Judging from the depth of the mark in the soil, the owner of the claw marks should have been dragging something heavy. Looking closely, there seems to be a strand of short blond hair between the cracks. Could it be?!)",
    ["Dialogue1066501"]="(There's a Kobold camp nearby and the claw marks and drag mark seem to lead towards it. Could it be...)",
    ["Dialogue1066601"]="(This Spinecrusher guard is no longer breathing. Its cold limbs and pale white skin tell you that it had lost a huge amount of blood before its death.)",
    ["Dialogue1066701"]="(Another Spinecrusher guard. It's quite obvious that the cause of its death was the same as the previous guard.)",
    ["Dialogue1066801"]="(The guard looks like he is on the verge of death. He cannot hold up his head and it's difficult for him to even speak.)\nC-chief... Did Chieftain Woofka... send you?",
    ["Dialogue1066802"]="Tell Chieftian... that we, we were all murdered by... the Skullsplitter Clan! They, they drained our blood... I'm so cold... I w-want to go home...\n(The guard's body starts to twitch continuously.)",
    ["Dialogue1066803"]="...I-it's too late, human... I...\n(The guard's head drops forward and he stops moving.)",
    ["Dialogue1066901"]="(There is indeed writing from the Kobold Clan carved into the ancient totem pole. Although the pole had weathered numerous storms and snow, the writing is still clear and bold.)",
    ["Dialogue1070101"]="Dear Adventurer, welcome to the historical city of Glast Heim! Before Ragnarok, human adventurers and giants once fought a great battle here. About 700 years ago, King Schmidt founded Glast Heim at this location. That's why every corner of this city still possesses some of the glamor from the Schmidt Empire!",
    ["Dialogue1070102"]="The Schmidt Empire was once famous across the land because of its brilliant civilization. However, the prosperity of their civilization only lasted for a few decades. All that is left are the dilapidated ruins of this ancient city. As the ruins of Glast Heim have been abandoned for a hundred years, it is now almost impossible to research the reason behind its fall.",
    ["Dialogue1070103"]="Adventurer, if you would like to know more about Glast Heim's history, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to Eden Group's camp</color>. As fanatics of Glast Heim's history, they are the best researchers with regards to Glast Heim.",
    ["Dialogue1070201"]="They've been excavating for days so there should have been some results by now, but why are they not back yet?",
    ["Dialogue1070202"]="Oh? You know about the Fragment of Ymir's Heart! A person who understands us has finally arrived! The Eden Group has been excavating the ruins to prove to the world that Glast Heim must have previously owned a Fragment of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1070203"]="Because the level of prosperity achieved by Glast Heim in the past could not have been achieved by humans alone. To achieve that level of prosperity, Glast Heim must have received an extraordinary divine blessing. However, there have been countless obstacles in our excavation work and till now, we still haven't found any traces of the fragment.",
    ["Dialogue1070204"]="Oh? You're willing to help? That's great! I believe with your help, there will be a breakthrough and our efficiency will greatly increase. The key to finding the Fragment of Ymir's Heart is to fully understand the history of Glast Heim and the reason behind its fall. Once we find it, we'll be one step closer to the Fragment of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1070205"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Enter Glast Heim</color> and look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group members</color> who are carrying out excavation works. They should be facing quite a number of challenges and obstacles right now and I believe with your ability, you'll definitely be able to help them out.",
    ["Dialogue1070301"]="Who would have thought that even after saving her spirit, there would still be no progress...",
    ["Dialogue1070302"]="Adventurer, you're asking me what happened to this young lady? I released her from the ruins of the Palace's Back Garden and I originally thought I could acquire some information on Glast Heim's history from her. But I had not expected that she would have lost all her memories. I feel so helpless now...",
    ["Dialogue1070303"]="It's not hard to tell that her outfit is Glast Heim's distinct style of fashion from a few hundred years ago. As long as she can remember what happened in her lifetime, we will definitely have a breakthrough for this part of our historical research.",
    ["Dialogue1070304"]="I'm sorry, but I really have no recollection about who I am. I seem to remember visiting this garden and yes, I seem to have lived in that magnificent building too...",
    ["Dialogue1070305"]="It's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>magnificent dome with elegant carvings that is surrounded by flowing water</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1070401"]="That building should be... the palace?! That's right! I remember now! I used to be a servant in the palace and my name is Lorraine. Under the rule of King Schmidt, this place was once brilliantly prosperous.",
    ["Dialogue1070402"]="Yup, that's right. I remember now. King Schmidt ordered me to brew a special type of medicated wine. If I can brew that wine again, maybe I might be able to recall more of the past...",
    ["Dialogue1070403"]="I remember that in order to craft that medicated wine, I searched for a type of <color=#CA2E0AFF>fuchsia-colored herb</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>near the palace</color>. I also visited a corner of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest of the city</color> to gather a kind of <color=#CA2E0AFF>light blue-colored flower</color>. Lastly, I added them into <color=#CA2E0AFF>some glowing fountain water</color>. I think it should be fountain water from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Quiet Garden</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1070501"]="Let me think... Crush these petals and add them into the fountain water... Yup, that's right. This should do it....",
    ["Dialogue1070502"]="I still have no memories. Maybe because everything happened so long ago...",
    ["Dialogue1070503"]="Adventurer, I think there might be another way. I remember that there was a famous wine merchant called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akarret</color> in Glast Heim. He was an expert on the various wines of the world, so maybe he'll know something about this wine. Why don't you take this wine and <color=#CA2E0AFF>pay him a visit</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1070601"]="Adventurer, where did you get this dangerous poisonous wine?",
    ["Dialogue1070602"]="This is a very rare kind of poisonous wine. It will <color=#CA2E0AFF>remove all divine powers within a person's body</color>. Legend has it that Odin once used this kind of wine to expunge traitors among the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gods</color>. Who is this wine for? How is there still someone in this world who needs to remove divine powers?",
    ["Dialogue1070701"]="How did it go? What did that famous wine merchant say about this wine?",
    ["Dialogue1070702"]="(Fear flashes across Lorraine's eyes as she holds her head in pain.)\nI actually... I actually made such a vicious wine in the past? Why? What...? Who did I make it for...?",
    ["Dialogue1070703"]="Ah yes... I... I remember that King Schmidt ordered me to bring a wooden box to this back garden every day... Yes, and I secretly buried the wooden box beneath <color=#CA2E0AFF>the rose bushes nearby</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1070801"]="This wooden box...!\n(The young lady's gaze falls on the opened wooden box. Within it lies a decayed human heart. She stares blankly at the wooden box in her hands as tears stream down her cheeks.)",
    ["Dialogue1070802"]="I think... I think I'll be able to recall what happened in the past soon. The fragmented memories are slowly piecing themselves back together in my mind. I was put to death because I saved a sacred woman. Although I still cannot remember her name, I seem to remember that she was <color=#CA2E0AFF>wearing a snow white robe and she had a pair of wings on her back</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1070901"]="This... This is... This is Lady Hermes...\n(Tears roll down Lorraine's cheeks and her hands cannot stop trembling as she receives the photo.)",
    ["Dialogue1071001"]="Allow me to tell you what happened. This is a memory that causes me much pain, and it might also be the reason why I lost my memory... King Schmidt desired the beauty of Goddess Hermes and did something unscrupulously lecherous...",
    ["Dialogue1071002"]="I didn't expect that a goddess had already came here to search for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart a few hundred years ago. This undoubtedly strengthens the hypothesis that the fragment exists, though I have never read about what you've mentioned in any of Glast Heim's historical records...",
    ["Dialogue1071003"]="Looks like there's a need for me to further excavate this garden to search for more valuable historical artifacts. Maybe only then will we be able to know the truth. This is exactly why the Eden Group exists.",
    ["Dialogue1071004"]="Adventurer, although this might be asking for a lot, but I have a request I hope you can help me fulfill. It was my dying wish...",
    ["Dialogue1071005"]="I would like to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Quiet Garden</color> to gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>roses</color>. However, the aura of my spirit attracts monsters that attack me when I leave this place. I would like to ask you to protect me during my journey.",
    ["Dialogue1071101"]="Thank you, Adventurer. I have finished gathering the roses. I would like to offer these roses to the innocent citizens who have died under the cruel rule of King Schmidt. Even though nobody is living there anymore, it is still my wish to do so...",
    ["Dialogue1071201"]="This is Resley's home. He was Glast Heim's most talented artist. All the royals in the city were willing to pay a high price or even wait for more than half a year just to acquire one of his portraits. However, King Schmidt ordered the execution of Resley just because he left out a badge that represented the king's supreme honor in the portrait.",
    ["Dialogue1071301"]="Thank you for your protection, Adventurer. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep moving forward</color>. Another person just came to mind...",
    ["Dialogue1071401"]="Here, I remember how Meryl looked dancing in this open space here... Meryl was the most amazing dancer in the city. Although she came from a humble background, she had a remarkable talent for music. There was always an endless stream of young admirers giving Meryl flowers, but Meryl's heart belonged only to her childhood sweetheart, Tylar, who was in the Chivalry. However...",
    ["Dialogue1071402"]="However, the cruel and lecherous King Schmidt came to know of Meryl's stunning dances and wanted to force her to marry him. So Meryl and Tylar tried to elope, but they could not escape the king's army and were killed...",
    ["Dialogue1071501"]="That was a close shave. Thank you, Adventurer. My wish has been fulfilled. Lastly, I would like to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Statue</color> in the photo. Please take me there...",
    ["Dialogue1071601"]="This... This is where King Schmidt's statue is supposed to be. So why is Lady Hermes' statue here instead? It doesn't seem possible that the arrogant King Schmidt would allow for his statue to be replaced. Furthermore, this is goes against the belief in Odin...",
    ["Dialogue1071602"]="And that place...\n(The young lady's gaze falls upon the magnificent abbey in the distance.)",
    ["Dialogue1071603"]="I have never seen that abbey before during my lifetime. That's really strange...",
    ["Dialogue1071701"]="Please wait, Adventurer. I still have something important I need to ask this monster. It has something to do with the history of Glast Heim.",
    ["Dialogue1071702"]="That's right. As long as we can help it regain its mind, we will be able to ask about what happened. This is imperative to our excavation work. However, only the famous \"Requiem\" can help it regain its mental capabilities.",
    ["Dialogue1071703"]="I looked through the scores on the music stand and found that only the pages that had \"Requiem\" were missing. It is as though someone tried to hide the pages because they didn't want these monsters to regain their minds so others will never know the truth. Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the missing pages of \"Requiem\"</color> in this abbey.",
    ["Dialogue1071801"]="Just as I thought, the missing pages were hidden in various corners of this abbey. However, as I was checking this piano, I found that one of its white keys is missing. Without this key, we might not be able to play \"Requiem\" properly...",
    ["Dialogue1071802"]="The only solution now is to substitute the missing white key with a monster bone. I believe we'll be able to find a suitable <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Bone</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raydric</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1071901"]="Everything is ready now. I've already restored the score to \"Requiem\". I think once we place this <color=#CA2E0AFF>bone</color> into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>socket with the missing piano key</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>play the melody according to the score</color>, it should work.",
    ["Dialogue1072001"]="Ah?! You've regained consciousness? Quick, tell us how was this abbey constructed?! Why did the ancient city of Glast Heim have such an abbey? Wasn't this abbey a direct challenge and defiance towards King Schmidt's rule?!\n(Cassius grabs the Evil Druid's collar as anger takes over his face.)",
    ["Dialogue1072002"]="That was all in the past... There's no point in pursing it anymore...",
    ["Dialogue1072003"]="Stop trying to hide the truth! Tell us! Do you hear me!\n(Veins bulge from Cassius' arms as he shakes the Evil Druid's shoulders fiercely.)",
    ["Dialogue1072004"]="You want to know why I'm so worked up?! There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret underground chamber</color> beneath this abbey. Go there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring back</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>terrible item</color> and you'll know why! Unforgivable!",
    ["Dialogue1072101"]="When I first found these hairs and ran a test on them, the result showed that they belonged to at least 10 different females. And the pool that's filled with pale red liquid? Do you think it's some kind of dye? No! It actually contains human blood! This abbey is not what it appears to be!",
    ["Dialogue1072102"]="(Cassius clenches his fist in anger and turns towards the Evil Druid.)\nSpeak! Exactly what kind of place is this? Why was it built?!",
    ["Dialogue1072103"]="Please stop pursuing the matter... I, I cannot say...",
    ["Dialogue1072104"]="You! ...Forget it, I'll think of another way! Adventurer, could you get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Slimy Monster Eyeballs</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Monster Blood</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raydric</color>. I think I have an idea.",
    ["Dialogue1072201"]="We'll be able to uncover the truth now. What I'm holding now is a Revelation Potion that was created by the Eden Group to verify ancient history. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head down to the secret chamber</color> now. Hmph, don't you think you can hide your sins.",
    ["Dialogue1072301"]="Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle this Revelation Potion in front of the stone coffin that is in the water</color>. If vengeful spirits were born here, the potion will reveal them to us.",
    ["Dialogue1072401"]="Are you still not telling us the truth?! Didn't these innocent girls die because of your sins?!",
    ["Dialogue1072402"]="I couldn't keep it from you after all. Indeed, the deaths of these girls has a deep connection to this abbey. King Schmidt became a different person after his marriage with Goddess Hermes. He ignored all the warnings from the high priests in the city and adamantly went ahead with the construction of this abbey that defied the faith of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue1072403"]="But what King Schmidt didn't know was, the goddess started taking control of this abbey shortly after it was built. To regain her divine powers, she ordered the priests to routinely hold sacrificial ceremonies using young girls.",
    ["Dialogue1072404"]="But why would the High Priests adhere to such a request? This doesn't make sense…",
    ["Dialogue1072405"]="That's because the goddess told them that she would only be able to help King Schmidt sense the location of the holy relic, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>, if they did it. But after all that has happened, I think that wasn't her real motive...",
    ["Dialogue1072406"]="(The Evil Druid lowers its gaze and a look of regret can be seen on its face.)\n...Maybe everything was just as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Sage</color> had said... I should have believed him then.",
    ["Dialogue1072407"]="It seems like there are still a lot more terrible truths left to be discovered. Adventurer, thank you for your help. For now, I must remain here to continue my investigation to uncover these undiscovered truths. If you would like to know more about the history of Glast Heim, you can head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chivalry</color>. My teammate, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zachary</color>, might need your help too.",
    ["Dialogue1072501"]="This is rather difficult... Let me think if there any other way...",
    ["Dialogue1072502"]="Oh? You're here to help? Yes, I have a problem. Why don't you go check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archmage Statue</color> at the end of the hall? You'll be able to understand my problem after that...",
    ["Dialogue1072601"]="You should have heard the singing that is coming from the Archmage Statue, right? That, is exactly my problem right now.",
    ["Dialogue1072602"]="That's right, Adventurer. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>observe</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Knight Statue</color> that is in front of me? Try and see if you can spot anything special about it.",
    ["Dialogue1072701"]="If I am not wrong, the song that the Archmage Statue is singing should be a riddle. The riddle speaks of the eight principles of the Knight's Code, and we've found one of the principles on this Knight Statue. Which means to say, the riddle must have something to do with all the Knight Statues in this hall.",
    ["Dialogue1072702"]="I've checked. Most of the words on the Knight Statues' pedestals have been eroded by the passage of time so we'll first need to think of a way to restore those words. I remember that there is some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gangrene Grass</color> growing at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>empty space just outside the abbey</color>. Their sap should help us clean up the grim that has built up over the years and restore the words. Please go <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some Gangrene Grass</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1072801"]="Wonderful! Thank you! With this Gangrene Grass, we'll be able to restore the words! Hurry, apply the Gangrene Grass sap to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pedestals of the Knight Statues</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1072901"]="The statue moved! You must have displayed the principle that was written on it and completed the trial of courage. Who would have thought that this hall had such a hidden mechanism? The wisdom of our forefathers is incredible. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the next statue</color> and try to solve the riddle in one go!",
    ["Dialogue1073001"]="We did it! The statue moved again! A knight's honor is indeed represented by the sword they hold in their hands. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the next statue</color> and check it out!",
    ["Dialogue1073101"]="I see, so the principle of \"Mercy\" meant having compassion for all living beings in the world. Adventurer, let's hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the fourth statue</color>. I can't wait to know the final answer to the riddle.",
    ["Dialogue1073201"]="You really are very knowledgeable. It's thanks to your help that we were able to solve the riddles so successfully. Let's move on, there are still four statues left. Looks like we will succeed soon.",
    ["Dialogue1073301"]="It moved! We've completed another statue's trial! Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>onto the next statue</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1073401"]="Who would have thought that the principle of \"Sacrifice\" meant sacrificing one's own blood. You really are an adventurer worthy of respect. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the next statue</color> now!",
    ["Dialogue1073501"]="Sigh, this problem cannot be avoided after all...",
    ["Dialogue1073502"]="Follow me and you'll understand.",
    ["Dialogue1073601"]="You see, though we've painstakingly solved the riddles on the previous seven statues, this last statue has been completely destroyed and its pedestal has even fallen into the pit. There's no way to read what's on it now.",
    ["Dialogue1073602"]="Since this is the case... Hehe, why don't we just lie to the Archmage Statue and say that we've already completed the trials on all the Knight Statues. He's just a statue anyway, he can't tell if we're telling the truth.",
    ["Dialogue1073603"]="Don't be so stubborn! That statue can't personally validate our words anyway. Furthermore, we've completed the trials for the first seven statues, lying about this last one doesn't really matter...",
    ["Dialogue1073701"]="W-what happened?!",
    ["Dialogue1073702"]="Adventurer, you have showcased all eight characteristics of a knight and have passed my trial.",
    ["Dialogue1073703"]="Please come stand before me now...",
    ["Dialogue1073704"]="Huh? But... But we haven't reported back to the Archmage Statue, how did you pass the trial? Ah! I get it!",
    ["Dialogue1073705"]="The last principle! It's \"Honesty\"! Maybe this is exactly what the last trial is about. You displayed the trait of \"Honesty\" when you refused to lie to the Archmage Statue, and hence fulfilled the criteria of the trial. You really are different from other adventurers. Try <color=#CA2E0AFF>standing in front of the Archmage Statue</color>, I think the truth is about to come to light.",
    ["Dialogue1073801"]="King Schmidt is trapped below? This is such a shocking piece of news. Looks like the clues to the truth and Glast Heim Sewer are closely interconnected. Adventurer, why don't you head down to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Sewer</color> and investigate first? I will continue to stay in the Chivalry and investigate the ruins related to this portion of history to see if I'm able to acquire more evidence.",
    ["Dialogue1073901"]="Don't you know how to respectfully take commands from your king? Are palace guards all so sloppy nowadays?",
    ["Dialogue1073902"]="Be quiet. Come here and <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort me underground</color>. It took Hermes a lot of effort to sense that the precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> is hidden deep beneath the ground here. Once I find it, I will be able to acquire unlimited powers that surpass mankind!",
    ["Dialogue1074001"]="Hm? Why are you two slaves idling here? Take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloth</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean the torture devices</color> around here. Otherwise I'll use this whip in my hand to teach you two a lesson.",
    ["Dialogue1074002"]="How dare you raise your voice against me! Guard, take him down!",
    ["Dialogue1074003"]="Huh? How dare a slave you like pretend to be King Schmidt! Looks like you really want a taste of my whip!",
    ["Dialogue1074004"]="You... You... Hmph!\n(King Schmidt looks nervously at the whip in the Sageworm's hand. Fear creeps onto his face as he turns to you.)\nYou! Why are you still here?! Go clean those torture devices for me!",
    ["Dialogue1074101"]="The two of you took so long to finish such a simple task. I honestly don't know what kind of slaves you are. Now, go think of a way to get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Writhing Rotten Meat</color>. And also, go scrape more <color=#CA2E0AFF>Slimy Moss</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>the corners of the walls</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1074102"]="How dare you order the noble King Schmidt around! My kingly hands will not touch those disgusting monsters and I will never obey the orders of someone as lowly as you! I am not going. Guard, do you not realize your place? Go get it done!",
    ["Dialogue1074201"]="How could you have taken so long for such a simple task? Forget it. Talking to you slaves won't help with anything.",
    ["Dialogue1074202"]="Hehe! You'll see when I'm done. But for now, go get me some water from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lionheart Pool</color>. Hurry! Go! Don't you dawdle!",
    ["Dialogue1074301"]="There's food for those scoundrels now. Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue1074302"]="That's right, this is the favorite food of those prison laborers in this sewer. My culinary skills in this sewer are second to none. Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take</color> these <color=#CA2E0AFF>dishes</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>those prisoners</color> in the first few cells.",
    ["Dialogue1074401"]="Looks like I'll be going hungry again today.",
    ["Dialogue1074402"]="There's no need to apologize. There's no loss in not eating food that's not even fit for cats and dogs. It's not that bad to die of hunger anyway. I can finally reunite with my family on the other side.",
    ["Dialogue1074501"]="Oh? That was quick. Did you finish giving out all the food? Or did you secretly finished yourself?",
    ["Dialogue1074502"]="Hmph. How dare such a lowly creature be so bossy! Guard, I order you to kill him!",
    ["Dialogue1074601"]="You've finally did something a guard should have done. You shouldn't need me to prompt you for something like that.",
    ["Dialogue1074602"]="Why would I ever care about those lowly creatures? How could I have put up with that blasted supervisor who showed me so much disrespect repeatedly? Alright, guard. Since that hindrance is now out of the way, you are to escort me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue my search for the clues about the Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1074701"]="T-thank you very much! Otherwise, we would have died here today.\n(Darens' voice is shaking and it gradually becomes softer.)",
    ["Dialogue1074702"]="No. *Coughs* Excuse me. Oww... We were originally ordinary citizens from Glast Heim. We signed up as laborers and worked here because we come from impoverished families and we wanted to change our living conditions.\n(Tyler covers the bleeding wound on his right leg. The pain causes him to occasionally let out soft murmurs of pain.)",
    ["Dialogue1074801"]="Thank you. I will apply these herbs on Tyler and myself later. I'm sure they will definitely help to alleviate some of our pain. Both of you are so kind.",
    ["Dialogue1074802"]="I don't have time or interest to take care of lowly people like the two of you. This guard here is the busybody who went looking for trouble.",
    ["Dialogue1074803"]="Please do not say that, mister. I'm sure you are a kindhearted person too.",
    ["Dialogue1074804"]="I don't recall seeing this noble-looking mister before. Kind adventurer, Tyler and I should have been working on the maintenance of that boiler ahead. However, hunger and these injuries have rendered us immobile. Could you please help us out? If the boiler is not fixed, we might get beaten again.",
    ["Dialogue1074805"]="Thank you very much. I'll teach you how to carry out the maintenance of the boiler now. Firstly, you'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the exterior of the boiler</color> for damages. Then you'll need to clean up the rust and moss on the outside. Secondly, you'll need to check for boiler slag in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pipe valve</color>. You'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean up</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>boiler slag</color> if the build up is too thick. Lastly, you'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check and clean the water level meter</color> and ensure that the water level is normal. After all that is done, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>test</color> to see if the boiler is working normally.",
    ["Dialogue1074806"]="I'm counting on you.",
    ["Dialogue1074901"]="How did it go? Is the boiler working normally?",
    ["Dialogue1074902"]="Hm? This is strange... Let me think... Hm... Maybe that is the only solution left... Adventurer, can you remove the <color=#CA2E0AFF>spare pipe valve</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>another boiler</color> and use it to replace the pipe valve of this boiler?",
    ["Dialogue1075001"]="Stop dawdling around and come over here. Let's move on and continue our search in another area.",
    ["Dialogue1075002"]="Not only are those two weaklings of no help at all, they also showed no respect to their king. Apart from hindering my search for the fragment, they were completely useless. Why should I keep them around?",
    ["Dialogue1075003"]="I don't care if they are prisoners or commoners. As long as they do not help in my search for the fragment, their survival does not matter. Stop talking nonsense. Hurry, bring me <color=#CA2E0AFF>deeper underground to continue my search</color>. I have already searched this area and found no trace of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1075101"]="All these lowly creatures didn't even remember who I am just now, how dare they attack me now?! Where are the prison guards?! How can they let these sinners roam freely? This is atrocious!",
    ["Dialogue1075102"]="Impossible! How could Hermes have betrayed me? She loved me dearly! Furthermore, nobody would dare to lie to me. Hermes who loved me so dearly would never lie to me! There must be someone else who's secretly scheming against me and trying to stop me from acquiring the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Hmph, I will never let those scheming scoundrels succeed.",
    ["Dialogue1075201"]="H-hurry, help me! I've been trapped behind this door for far too long!",
    ["Dialogue1075202"]="Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>get</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>key</color> to this wooden door from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zombie Prisoners</color>. I've been trapped in here for far too long. Ahhhhh! Stay away! Stay away, you horrible creatures! Person on the outside, hurry! Go get the key and save me!",
    ["Dialogue1075301"]="Is there anyone outside? Come save me! Hurry, unlock this torture device! I'm trapped inside! Hurry, lift the bolt on the door!",
    ["Dialogue1075302"]="There are <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zombie Prisoners</color> around here. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Acid</color> that they possess should be able to remove the rust. Hurry, go get some Monster Acid from those zombies!",
    ["Dialogue1075401"]="Ahhh, s-save me! I c-can't breathe! Help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>dig away these stones</color>! Hurry! Please!",
    ["Dialogue1075402"]="Ah! Help! I'm not going to make it! Please! Please save me! Help me! Move them! Move them!",
    ["Dialogue1075501"]="Guard, hurry! Escort me out of here! I don't want that fragment anymore! This place is horrifying! I want to leave now!",
    ["Dialogue1075502"]="Stop talking! Hurry! How can anyone stay in this hell on earth?! I want to leave this terrible place now!",
    ["Dialogue1075601"]="Ahhhh! Why!? Why won't you leave me alone?! Go away, all of you!\n(King Schmidt suddenly holds his head with both hands and goes on a rampage. He seems to be in immense pain.)",
    ["Dialogue1075602"]="Why? That person isn't me. It's definitely not me. Why did I hurt my people like that? And Morris? Morris was my most loyal subject, but I actually killed him?! No, Morris. It's not like that... Don't come any closer! Ahhh!",
    ["Dialogue1075603"]="That was... That was my wedding night with Hermes... I love her... And yes, she must love me too! Ah! Ah, my head hurts! Why did it turn out this way!? I know! Guard, check the area and see if <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hermes left an afterimage of herself</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1075701"]="Almighty goddess, I beg you, please let me off. This is all my fault and I am sorry. I should not have been greedy and I should not have lusted after your beauty. Everything is my fault.",
    ["Dialogue1075702"]="Please forgive me! Please stop torturing me! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!",
    ["Dialogue1075703"]="I'll compensate you with anything you want! Please forgive me! Please stop torturing me!",
    ["Dialogue1075801"]="There was a time when I was just like how you are now, regretting everything. I knelt before you and begged you to stop hurting everyone. But did you? Did you stop doing those shameless deeds?",
    ["Dialogue1075802"]="I'm sorry! It's all my fault! I know that I'm wrong now! Please, I beg you! Please let me off! I... I don't want the Fragment of Ymir's Heart anymore! You can have it if you want! Please just let me off! Please!",
    ["Dialogue1075803"]="Ha, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. Are you talking about this?",
    ["Dialogue1075901"]="Adventurer, you must have gained a lot of information on your trip, right? Hurry tell me about it! How's the progress of the excavation?",
    ["Dialogue1075902"]="What!? The Fragment of Ymir's Heart had already fallen into the hands of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demon King Morroc</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>a few hundred years ago</color>? This would mean that the fragment is no longer in Glast Heim and it's impossible for us to unearth it.",
    ["Dialogue1075903"]="You're saying that the Dawn Goddess gave you a hint to open the door to another dimension? Ah! I know! I think what the goddess meant was for us to travel back in time to the day that Glast Heim was attacked by Morroc. We can then seize the fragment from the Demon King Morroc before it is being taken away. This must be it! Haha! We have a plan now!",
    ["Dialogue1075904"]="In this case, your situation is rather special. You are able to establish a dimensional link with ancient relics and enter the memories of their owner, but you are unable to control the time period you go to... Hmm... I think there might someone who can help you out. A famous time traveler has arrived in Glast Heim recently, I'm sure he will be able to help you.",
    ["Dialogue1076001"]="Oh? You really are here, Adventurer. Looks like the torrent of time doesn't lie indeed...",
    ["Dialogue1076002"]="I understand. I can loan you the Sands of Time and you'll be able to return to the day of the battle in Glast Heim a few hundred years ago.",
    ["Dialogue1076003"]="The situation is different this time. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take the Sands of Time</color> from my hand once you are ready and you will be able to return to the day that you wish to return to.",
    ["Dialogue1076101"]="Ordinary citizens should not stay here any longer. This place has been overrun with monsters and is very dangerous. Please evacuate with the protection of the Chivalry.",
    ["Dialogue1076102"]="Oh? You are a strong adventurer? If you are willing to help resist the invading monsters, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>get some water</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lotus Pond</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put out the fire</color> first. There are also still some citizens here but they have already given up hope. They've been attacked too many times and are exhausted. Help to encourage them and get them to pull themselves together, then get them to evacuate the city as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue1076201"]="Thank you. The more citizens we evacuate, the better it is for us. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Commander Heinrich's</color> situation. He is leading the White Knights against the attacking monsters.",
    ["Dialogue1076301"]="Thank you, warrior. Could you head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>center of the city</color> to check out the situation there? A knight just said that he saw <color=#CA2E0AFF>Queen Hermes</color> casting spells in front of the palace. But as you can see, the hordes of monsters that are coming at us are stopping me from going myself. I have to stay here to get rid of them all.",
    ["Dialogue1076401"]="Adventurer, hurry, pick up that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> and leave this place! If you stay here any longer, you'll just create more problems for Lucci and me. The battle that follows is between Morroc and me.",
    ["Dialogue1076402"]="What Thanatos means is that you've already completed your mission. The battle that follows is between us and Morroc. Hurry, take the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and leave. You've done well!",
    ["Dialogue1076501"]="As expected. What is destined cannot be changed.",
    ["Dialogue1076502"]="You're asking why I helped you instead of stopping you from returning to the past to change events that have already happened this time? Because this time round, I am not changing history. I've seen the battle of Glast Heim while I was time traveling and the person I saw taking this fragment was you. It wasn't Morroc, Hermes or King Schmidt, but you.",
    ["Dialogue1076503"]="As a time traveler, I am supposed to follow the rules of time. So I was just fulfilling my duty by helping you travel back in time. There's no need for you to be surprised. You should go fulfill your duty now as well.",
    ["Dialogue1076601"]="Well done. You've fulfilled the duty that destiny has bestowed onto you and brought this Fragment of Ymir's Heart back amidst the torrent of history.",
    ["Dialogue1076602"]="I believe that you now understand that there's a cause and effect for everything after going through this calamity which lasted hundreds of years. Only when you remain kind, humble, and abstain from greed, then will success and light always be on your side.",
    ["Dialogue1076603"]="We do not have much time, Successor of Odin's bloodline. I have sensed the location of the next fragment. It is located in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aldebaran</color>, a city on the border of the<color=#CA2E0AFF>Schwarzwald Republic</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1076701"]="(There's a strange spot of light shining on the location of Prontera on the map. You touch the globe and decide to turn it in a certain direction—)",
    ["Dialogue1076702"]="(The globe spins a little then returns to its original position.)",
    ["Dialogue1076703"]="(The spot of light lands on the location of Geffen on the map. You touch the globe and decide to turn it in a certain direction—)",
    ["Dialogue1076801"]="(The wooden coffin is rather old. Due to decomposition, it is out of shape, and you are unable to open it. However, there seems to be something underneath it...)",
    ["Dialogue1076901"]="(A stone coffin sits quietly in the middle of the pool. When you take a closer look, the water in the pool seems a little reddish.)",
    ["Dialogue1077001"]="Unnamed comer from the present, the glory of the past has faded to dust. Only the maxim of the knights will always remain.\nIf you hope to attain the glory of the past, come before me when you know the true meaning to the eight principles.",
    ["Dialogue1077101"]="First Principle of the Knight's Code: Bravery\nWe █ bravery ██, ██ no fear. Offer █████████ to prove ██████.",
    ["Dialogue1077201"]="First Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bravery</color>\nWe put bravery first, and have no fear. Offer three <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bloody Knight's Skulls</color> to prove your bravery.",
    ["Dialogue1077301"]="Second Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Honor</color>\nWe point our blades forward in honor and never back down. Present <color=#CA2E0AFF>the weapon of a knight</color> to display your honor.",
    ["Dialogue1077401"]="Third Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mercy</color>\nWe have compassion for all that live in the world. Offer <color=#CA2E0AFF>food to comfort spirits in distress</color> to display your compassion.",
    ["Dialogue1077501"]="Fourth Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Impartiality</color>\nWe are just and impartial. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Answer all my questions correctly</color> to show your impartiality.",
    ["Dialogue1077502"]="Two people are headed to the market to purchase an item. The person who arrives first is from a less privileged background while the person who arrives later is from a noble family. There is only one left of the item they wish to purchase. Who should the merchant sell the item to?",
    ["Dialogue1077503"]="(The Knight Statue remains motionless.)",
    ["Dialogue1077504"]="A man and a woman seek treatment at the same time. The woman's injuries are more serious while the man's injuries are less serious. Who should the healer treat first?",
    ["Dialogue1077505"]="(The Knight Statue moves slightly. Some dust seems to have fallen off due to the movement.)",
    ["Dialogue1077601"]="Fifth Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Humility</color>\nWe may have the honor of a knight but we are humble and we respect everyone. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pay respect on one knee</color> to show your humility.",
    ["Dialogue1077701"]="Sixth Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sacrifice</color>\nSacrifices are unavoidable in our battles. If you encounter a <color=#CA2E0AFF>disoriented spirit</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>offer your blood</color> to help it regain its mind as proof of a blood sacrifice.",
    ["Dialogue1077801"]="Seventh Principle of the Knight's Code: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Will</color>\nOur will is indestructible and will shine bright for all eternity. Recite the <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Faith of Light\"</color> to prove your will.",
    ["Dialogue1077901"]="(The Knight Statue stands quietly before you. Its expression is extraordinarily lifelike and its gaze is so powerful it seems to hold the power to transverse time.)",
    ["Dialogue1077902"]="(The Knight Statue remains motionless.)",
    ["Dialogue1077903"]="There may be overgrown thorns and overcast skies, but my heart remains and the light within will never fade.",
    ["Dialogue1077904"]="I fight for the honor and faith of a knight.\nEven if the road ahead is abyssal and filled with darkness...",
    ["Dialogue1077905"]="I swear by the spirit of a knight,\nto keep the light and strength in my heart ablaze.",
    ["Dialogue1077906"]="For the return of honor and faith,\nI will be indomitable.",
    ["Dialogue1078001"]="(A bout of dizziness hits you and the scene before you starts to blur...)",
    ["Dialogue1078101"]=" (Boiler whistles as it expels hot steam. Listening closely, you hear an odd sound among the clanking of the gears.)",
    ["Dialogue1078102"]="(The exterior of the boiler is rusty. You are unable to check the pipe.)",
    ["Dialogue1078103"]="(The rust on the exterior of the boiler has been successfully cleaned off.)",
    ["Dialogue1078104"]="(The pipe valve of the boiler is shut tight. You are unable to check for boiler slag.)",
    ["Dialogue1078105"]="(The pipe valve is open. Looks like you'll need to clean up the boiler slag.)",
    ["Dialogue1078106"]="(The boiler slag is too thick. You are unable to see the reading on the water level meter.)",
    ["Dialogue1078107"]="(The boiler slag has been cleaned up. The interior of the boiler looks as good as new now.)",
    ["Dialogue1078108"]="(The whirring from the boiler stopped.)",
    ["Dialogue1078109"]="(For reasons unknown, the boiler still isn't working normally.)",
    ["Dialogue1078201"]="(*Rumble* The boiler seems to be working normally now.)",
    ["Dialogue1078301"]="(A bout of dizziness hits you and the scene before you starts to blur...)",
    ["Dialogue1080101"]="Welcome ~ Dear Adventurer! It is a pleasure to serve you!",
    ["Dialogue1080102"]="Hmm..... You would like to go to Aldebaran? This could prove to be quite difficult.",
    ["Dialogue1080103"]="Ah, please don't get me wrong, Adventurer. Of course, my hometown welcomes you with open arms. With your permission, W will be happy to act as your guide and show you the gorgeous landscapes of Aldebaran. I must mention, I am afraid you will not be able to use Kafra’s services to get to Aldebaran.",
    ["Dialogue1080104"]="Because Aldebaran is a territory of Schwarzwald Republic. Although the Republic and Rune Kingdom have always been friendly with one another, foreigners who want to enter the Republic’s territories need to <color=#CA2E0AFF> apply for a pass at the border port</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF> travel in Rekenber’s airship to get to various cities</color>, otherwise they will be regarded as illegal immigrants. Please be aware that the Republic has always severely punished such acts.",
    ["Dialogue1080105"]="Therefore, for your safety, W suggests that you still apply for an entry permit through the border port and go to Aldebaran legally. Otherwise, you may soon be identified as fugitive on the Republic's public information database, and pursued by the heavily armed Republic guard.\n(W tilts his head and smiles innocuously)",
    ["Dialogue1080106"]="Eh? Don’t be so annoying~ W doesn’t have any bad intentions!\n(the girl winks at you with a certain coyness)",
    ["Dialogue1080107"]="In short, although W strongly dislikes that group of Rekenber's artificial guys..... If Adventurers want to go to Aldebaran, they must abide by their rules. What W can do is to help you arrive near the border port.",
    ["Dialogue1080108"]="Just north of the Mjolnir Mountains, adjacent to Aldebaran, there is an airship port established by the Rekenber Company. For more specific instructions, please ask the relevant staff there~",
    ["Dialogue1080201"]="Excuse me, are you ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF> go to the border port of the Mjolnir Mountains </color>?",
    ["Dialogue1080202"]="Well - have a nice trip, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1080203"]="Ooh, correct, first-class Adventurers should be completely prepared before departure! It’s alright, when you are ready, W will be waiting for you!",
    ["Dialogue1080301"]="Hey, what are you looking at! You there - you can't go through without a pass! You're not allowed to be here! Get out of here!",
    ["Dialogue1080302"]="Have you applied for a pass?\n(the guard looks you up and down, and then snorts scornfully)\nLine up from the back just like everyone else! Can you not see all these people here?!",
    ["Dialogue1080303"]="You liar! I've been waiting here for several days. I don't have a pass!",
    ["Dialogue1080304"]="You’re right! Look at these people. They've been waiting for ages! These guards tell us the same thing every day.... “Line up, line up” -- When are we going to go?!",
    ["Dialogue1080305"]="Besides, if you didn't limit the number of passes, why are we all being forced to queue at the gate?! I don't care! You must let me through today, If you don’t let me through I am staying right here in this very spot! We will all stay here!!!\n(the traveler at the front began waving his hand, and the crowd behind him began to yell out)",
    ["Dialogue1080306"]="You’re right! We will stay here!",
    ["Dialogue1080307"]="We will stay here! We need an explanation!",
    ["Dialogue1080308"]="<size=26>Shut up!!! All of you!!!</size>\n(the guard cries out and shakes his gun in a demonstration of anger)\nDo you want to hear a real noise?! How about a gun?!",
    ["Dialogue1080309"]="Listen up all of you. If you want a pass, line up. Don't want to line up? \nThen you can find another way~",
    ["Dialogue1080310"]="You’re......",
    ["Dialogue1080311"]="Here... Over here! There are thieves!",
    ["Dialogue1080401"]="Thank you.... thank so, so much Adventurer! Without you, my entire livelihood and all of my possessions would have been stolen by the thieves!",
    ["Dialogue1080402"]="Actually... I bought this pass for a small fortune from a black market merchant.",
    ["Dialogue1080403"]="I, I know that this isn’t exactly legal! But I’ve been left with no other choice... In the past few months fewer and fewer passes have been issued by the officials. It is not enough to meet the people’s needs. I've been forced to wait here at the gate for more than ten days!\n<color=#A1979FFF>If, if I don't go back... Ellie will have to break my leg......</color>",
    ["Dialogue1080404"]="...... yes, yes, I saw you confront the guards earlier... Are you going to the Schwarzwald Republic too? I know of some black market merchants who will have what you are looking for! They are nearby the ancient trees in the <color=#CA2E0AFF> south of the Mjolnir Mountains</color>. That is the only way for travelers to go to the border port!",
    ["Dialogue1080405"]="(gives you a submissive look)\nIn exchange... Can you not tell anyone? I, I'm in a hurry to go home to see my wife and children.....",
    ["Dialogue1080406"]="Thank you! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1080501"]="What a... what an absolute waste! I don’t know why I am doing this! Women cannot fight!",
    ["Dialogue1080502"]="But, the fourth eldest..... She could fight..... Look at the state of my face.....\n(the man uncovers his head and half of his front teeth begin to rattle in the wind. He can't even speak clearly)",
    ["Dialogue1080503"]="Useless imbecile! You couldn’t fight off a cold! Forget about your ugly face!!!\nThis is a very important shipment! Don't you know who the client is?! If we lose the goods, let alone the money, he will have our heads!",
    ["Dialogue1080504"]="What do you want? Go away! Can’t you see how busy it is here!",
    ["Dialogue1080505"]="<size=26>We! Are! Not! Selling! Anything!</size>\n<size=26>Leave!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1080506"]="I’ve said it many times……<size=24>wait, wait?!</size><size=26>Do you know where my goods are?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1080507"]=".....You?\n(the black market merchant gives you a disdainful look)\nWhy should I believe you? You and your scrawny little body?",
    ["Dialogue1080508"]="Hey, hey, hey... What are you doing! <size=24>Put your weapon down! </size><size=26>If you want something, say so!</size>\nI promise, I promise you! As long as you can<color=#CA2E0AFF>get the goods back</color>, I'll give you a pass for free!",
    ["Dialogue1080601"]="(the footprints on the ground are a complete mess, scattered around are broken arrows and knives...) ",
    ["Dialogue1080701"]="(the plank was damaged by scrapes from heavy objects, the scratches extend the entire way across the bridge......)",
    ["Dialogue1080801"]="(a piece of woven cloth is hanging from the vines of the pier. Observe carefully, it says G.W.....)",
    ["Dialogue1080901"]="Adventurer?! What are you doing here?!",
    ["Dialogue1080902"]="... you’re right, I stole the goods.\nBut Adventurer, you know that I stole them with the best intentions. Should it be punished to help those who are most in need? ",
    ["Dialogue1080903"]="You want to go to Aldebaran?\nUnfortunately, Adventurer. A pass to Aldebaran is not something you can simply buy with money.",
    ["Dialogue1080904"]="According to my sources, the guards at the border port have for a long time been secretly colluding with black market merchants. Not only do they profit off smuggling illegal goods, but they also secretly sell entry permits through the hands of black market merchants, which should be given to ordinary people! The crooks are lining their own pockets!",
    ["Dialogue1080905"]="Yes, I see what you mean, Adventurer. However this is only a temporary solution, which cannot fundamentally solve the problem. But we have seen something, that.... Ugh! It's so strange! I couldn’t believe my eyes when I saw it!\n(Goldie nervously bites her teeth)",
    ["Dialogue1080906"]="……You have to go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look at the contents of the cargo box</color> to see what I mean. It is by no means an ordinary batch of smuggled goods!",
    ["Dialogue1081001"]="(Next to the cargo box there is a corpse with a shriveled torso and wide open staring eyes. A dark mouth like a cavernous hole, wide open exposing his empty throat...) ",
    ["Dialogue1081101"]="(Next to the cargo box is a corpse with a shriveled torso. It’s mouth and eyes are locked wide open, with a ferocious expression that makes it impossible to look at for any length of time...)",
    ["Dialogue1081201"]="Do you understand now? These were not normal deaths. Those black market merchants must be up to no good! Adventurer, I must investigate deeper into this. Stealing and selling bodily remains violates Odin's beliefs, not to mention..... What's more, the victim was tortured before he died.....\n(Goldie clenches her fist and glances angrily at the container)",
    ["Dialogue1081202"]="In that case, I’ll be frank with you! I need you to go to the Sograt Desert for me. An old friend of mine lives in the Hope Oasis camp in the middle of the desert... He might give you some trouble, but please believe me, he is proficient in both medicine and potion-making. He is the only person I know of who can help us understand what happened to these bodies!",
    ["Dialogue1081301"]="(Scattered around the crate are odd looking medical supplies and handwritten  prescriptions. On top of the crate, a messy note is pressed under a medicine bottle......)",
    ["Dialogue1081401"]="... well, all right. Although, as it is a corpse it will begin to deteriorate, it is better than nothing.",
    ["Dialogue1081402"]="Have we... Have we met before? Sorry, sorry ~ My memory behaves in such a way that I can only remember the name of medicinal materials. It may be worth calling you snake skin powder as I would be more likely to remember that!\n(with that, Wallace squats down and carefully collects the white powder falling from the Golum)",
    ["Dialogue1081403"]="What are you up to? Ah, of course, its essential to collect the flakey limestone powder as soon as possible! Since you killed these trolls, the powder has slowly been gathering on their skin. I must scrape it off and put them into special containers quickly, otherwise the medicinal value will lose its potency.",
    ["Dialogue1081404"]="... Is there something I can help you with? Sorry, sorry ~ I have the dignity of being a doctor. I won't go anywhere until I have collected all of my herbs. If you don't mind, I’ll only need half a day... No, perhaps two or three days? Well, in fact, why don’t we say a week.....",
    ["Dialogue1081405"]="<color=#A1979FFF>..... Hmm? Has the Adventurer lost his temper? It looks like you could murder someone! No, no... I would have to be blind to say that you're not mad!</color>\nCough hmm ~ you mean you're going to help me? Seeing that you are so enthusiastic, I can spare you the pleasantries! The recipe is very complicated (๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧",
    ["Dialogue1081406"]="Listen, Adventurer! This is the legendary magic potion that can make the Golem's head bloom rainbow-colored flowers. Only, to complete this historical potion, I will also need <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 sticky white scorpion eggs</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 writhing severed Hode tails </color>and<color=#CA2E0AFF> 10 slippery umbrella-shaped membranes</color>.... Huh? What's with the suspicious look? Never doubt a doctor! Just do as I say!",
    ["Dialogue1081501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Hmm... these herbs are freshly picked! No... I can't resist... I'll start cooking at once.....!</color>\n(Wallace excitedly touches the medicine you found, as if he were talking to his lover)",
    ["Dialogue1081502"]="Adventurer, you don't understand. A doctor's research is a race against time. Every second I delay could mean another patient’s life......",
    ["Dialogue1081503"]="Alas, so I mentioned that ordinary people don’t understand a doctor’s profession...... Wha! I beg your pardon?\n(Wallace stops touching the medicine)\nStrange, <size=26> and strange corpses ~?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1081504"]="Where! Take me there! We leave at once!",
    ["Dialogue1081601"]="Well, don't say anything more. I can even guess what happened...... Adventurer, you’ve done well.\n(Goldie pats you on the shoulder and points to a nearby carbo box)\n... Wallace, get the heck out of here.",
    ["Dialogue1081602"]="Alright, alright, I'm coming... Adventurer! Give me a hand!",
    ["Dialogue1081603"]="Listen - first,<color=#CA2E0AFF> bend the joints</color> to determine if the muscles are stiff. Then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>observe the condition of the facial features</color> and whether anything is abnormal. Then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>check </color>the whole body for <color=#CA2E0AFF>obvious trauma</color>. Finally, take a small blood sample<color=#CA2E0AFF> and soak</color> this test<color=#CA2E0AFF> paper</color>... Can you remember all of that? Great! Let's start!",
    ["Dialogue1081604"]="The stiffness of the muscles has been completely relieved, it has been at least 72 hours since the time of death......",
    ["Dialogue1081605"]="The mouth, nose, eyes and ears were dilated to varying degrees, it is very likely that they received a big fright at the moment of death......",
    ["Dialogue1081606"]="..... there is no obvious trauma or signs of blood loss, so the possibility of a traumatic death is ruled out.",
    ["Dialogue1081607"]="The color of the test paper has not changed, it seems that it could not have been a poisoning or death... So what was it?!\n(at that moment, you see the test paper in Wallace’s hand suddenly start burning)",
    ["Dialogue1081608"]="What! No, no! You didn't follow the procedure! We have to do it again!",
    ["Dialogue1081609"]="It is beyond logic and above reason! There is a powerful magic left in these corpses, which can even lead to spontaneous combustion of objects... I have only seen this power once before. With the demon clans in the pyramids of the Sograt Desert! Do you remember, adventurer? Previously, there was a strange warming in the Sograt Desert......",
    ["Dialogue1081610"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Frament of Ymir’s Heart</color>? Is that what you're looking for, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1081611"]="Well... Although I don't understand what this is, you have helped me and my friends a great deal. This time we will clear the way for you. Let's go and finally meet those unscrupulous black market merchants and get to the bottom of this! I want to squeeze every last piece of information out of them until they are rung dry!",
    ["Dialogue1081701"]="You've been away for so long. Surely you were able to find my ...... Yeeee?!",
    ["Dialogue1081702"]="Find what? Did you lose your cargo box? Well, why don't we make a bet?\n(Goldie waves her hand, and her men immediately surround them from all directions)\nIf you can get away from these guys, I'll give you your cargo back.",
    ["Dialogue1081703"]="……You,<size=24>What are you doing! </size><size=26>Come on! Run!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1081801"]="Eh.....! Stop fighting! What the heck could you want now!",
    ["Dialogue1081802"]="It's very simple - tell me the origins of the \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>goods</color>\" that I robbed from you?!",
    ["Dialogue1081803"]="I, I really don't know! I received this mission from an old customer and they just asked me to transport these goods out of Aldebaran to be destroyed! For every transaction, he contacted me only by letter! We've never met!",
    ["Dialogue1081804"]="Letter.....?",
    ["Dialogue1081805"]="Yes... Yes! Here is his <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color>! That is the time and place of the next transaction! Look!",
    ["Dialogue1081901"]="... the “old place”? Where is this “old place”? What does this signature mean?",
    ["Dialogue1081902"]="\"Old place\" is just the way he communicates! When we receive the next letter, we will follow the directions to find a symbol resembling an Owl. The goods will be near this symbol. Then, we just need to ship the goods out of Aldebaran... As for the signature, I don't know what it means! He always writes that.",
    ["Dialogue1081903"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Hmmm..... This is some really shady business.</color>\n……Adventurer, it seems that he really doesn't know the identity of this customer of his. The only clue we have is this letter and there is no guaranteeing its significance. I think you may need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the place of transaction</color> yourself to investigate in person.",
    ["Dialogue1081904"]="What about passes? I am sure there are plenty here.\n(Goldie raises her hand and swings the gleaming Katar in front of the black market merchant, making him tremble)\nYou hear me? Hand over your pass!",
    ["Dialogue1081905"]="Errrr... Now that I've told you all that I know about this mystery client, my next order of business is worthless! I suppose you will pay for that? \n(Goldie threateningly squints her eyes, her patience with the black market businessman is beginning to fader)\n... ahhhh, please don't hurt me! It’s ok! It’s fine, you can have it! ",
    ["Dialogue1082001"]="(there is a big fire burning around the cargo box, the hot temperature make it difficult to get close.....)",
    ["Dialogue1082101"]="(thick and sticky liquid drips onto the ground nearby the fire. After closer observation, it appears to be engine oil.....)",
    ["Dialogue1082201"]="You..... You arsonist!",
    ["Dialogue1082202"]="Stop quibbling! I saw you sneaking around the container with my own eyes, and now its burning! Who else could it have been?!",
    ["Dialogue1082203"]="Oh save it! \nSay what you want in prison! You have been arrested——",
    ["Dialogue1082204"]="Dee--deee--dee-dee-dee--deee\n(suddenly, the transceiver hanging off the guard's waist gives out a burst of un-recognizable sound)",
    ["Dialogue1082205"]="Request support... Machinery... Fire... Northwest... Wharf... Repeat... Drop——\n(a broken human voice comes from the transceiver, mixed with the disturbance from the radio frequency, making it impossible to interpret)",
    ["Dialogue1082206"]="Hello? Hey! What did you say? I can't hear you clearly. Please repeat, please repeat!!\n... darn it! We have lost communication!",
    ["Dialogue1082207"]="Dock? Good... I heard the word \"dock\" as well! The nearest dock... Is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest</color>",
    ["Dialogue1082208"]="Northwest... Northwest? you 're right! There is a<color=#CA2E0AFF>dock with a lot of cargo there</color>! - It must be there!",
    ["Dialogue1082209"]="You.....?\n(the guard looks at you suspiciously and without warning reaches out and grabs your wrist)\nYou’re coming with me! But I warn you, don't get any crooked ideas!",
    ["Dialogue1082301"]="What's going on... Are these machines out of control?!",
    ["Dialogue1082302"]="(the soldier's eyes inquiringly widened)\nSo... Are you really not an arsonist?",
    ["Dialogue1082303"]="Sorry..... Sorry, I misunderstood you.....\n(he raises his hand and grabs the back of his head, looking annoyed and upset)",
    ["Dialogue1082304"]="Thank you for your understanding, Adventurer. In fact, I didn't mean to doubt you. It's just..... so many strange things have happened in the city recently. As the guards of Aldebaran, we have to be vigilant.",
    ["Dialogue1082305"]="At first, there were several unexplained disappearances in the city. Subsequently, we received the news that some citizens were attacked again and again. Even though more and more people are being sent to investigate, we have not been able to find the criminals who are responsible... Now, even these machines lose control and randomly burst into fire.....",
    ["Dialogue1082306"]="Adventurer, I have a very bad feeling about this——\n(before he was able to finish his sentence, the soldier's waistband transceiver let out another screeching noise)",
    ["Dialogue1082307"]="Requesting support! Requesting support! A large number of machines are out of control and have set fire in the eastern urban area! We are in urgent need of support! Come as soon as possible! I repeat.... A large number of machines are out of control and have set fire in the eastern urban area! We are in urgent need of support! ",
    ["Dialogue1082308"]="<size=26>Again... Again?!</size>\nNo, that’s now three cases all at the same time... No, judging from the current situation, this is far from over! There could be many more victims... Damn! The guard army doesn't have nearly enough people!",
    ["Dialogue1082309"]="..... would you like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the East City to help</color> my companions? Great.  This way, I can stay here to deal with the fire! Thank you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1082401"]="Thank you, thank you for saving me! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1082402"]="Please... Please help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>put out</color> these <color=#CA2E0AFF>flames</color>! Otherwise, once the fire spreads, the surrounding residents will be in danger! I beg you! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1082501"]="(after putting out the flames, the guard finally breathed a sigh of relief)\nWe can...... We can rest assured for the time being.",
    ["Dialogue1082502"]="Why it happened, you ask? Sorry... I'm not too sure, although I did find these machines acting strangely during a patrol, so I followed them quietly. I did not expect it... when the passed by the goods, they suddenly opened their gas tanks and poured all of their oil out.",
    ["Dialogue1082503"]="It's incredible, I can hardly believe it! You know, Aldebaran has a long history of using machinery, especially the machinery produced by Rekenber Company. It not only has a strict production process and legal framework, but each machine must pass three quality tests before being officially put into use. Any failure will be scrapped, incinerated and rebuilt! I really can't imagine... How these machines could do such a thing.",
    ["Dialogue1082504"]="You... You’re saying that all around the city, these similar fires all started at the same time? And the goods that are being burned may be related to the dead body that you are investigating?\n(the guard frowns and thinks)\nDo you think..... These <color=#CA2E0AFF>goods</color> are also.....?",
    ["Dialogue1082505"]="I understand, adventurer! It's about the security of Aldebaran. I can't stand idly by! What's more, you helped me repel those rogue machines. Now, it's time for me to repay you!\nLet me help you <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wreckage and cargo boxes</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1082601"]="(the outer surface of the cargo box has mostly been burned, and a human arm is slightly revealed. The temperature of the surrounding air has decreased slightly, and it should be possible to take out the contents of the cargo box now...)",
    ["Dialogue1082701"]="(the corpse has a shriveled torso. It’s mouth and eyes are locked wide open, with a ferocious expression. Although there are signs of burning on the skin, the burns have not reached the muscles, bones or internal organs...) ",
    ["Dialogue1082801"]="Adventurer, look at this-- What is it?",
    ["Dialogue1082802"]="If I'm not mistaken... This should be an Alchemist spell. I once cooperated with the alchemists guild of Aldebaran. At that time, the array they used was very similar to this figure!",
    ["Dialogue1082803"]="It seems that the most effective way is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>photograph</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist spell</color> array and ask relevant people. In Aldebaran if you talk about professionals in this field, you must be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>member of the alchemist guild</color>. Their headquarters is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast</color>. As long as you find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>building with the logo of the Alchemist Guild</color>, you'll be alright!",
    ["Dialogue1082901"]="Where did you get this picture?!",
    ["Dialogue1082902"]="A machine willingly set itself on fire in the city....? So, you suspect that this has something to do with the Alchemist Guild?\n(the young man in the Alchemist Guild uniform looks at you in disdain, as if you have shown him something he would rather not have seen)\nUnfortunately, adventurer. This photo alone is not enough evidence.",
    ["Dialogue1082903"]="It seems that from these photos that this is indeed an <color=#CA2E0AFF>advanced Alchemist Spell used for controlling machines</color> but from this, I can't accurately determine the identity of the spell maker. It is hard to say whether the criminal responsible comes from the Alchemist Guild. After all, we are not the only people in the world who can use Alchemy. Right, Adventurer?\n(the tone of the man's speech rises slightly at the end of his sentence, which makes his comment seem rhetorical and ironic)",
    ["Dialogue1082904"]="If you have any other clues, please let me know. I can help you analyze this from a professional perspective, otherwise... I wont be able to help you. Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1082905"]="(hearing you mention Ymir's heart, his ears perk up)\nYou said... The target of these machines is a batch of cargo boxes full of corpses? In these bodies, you also found the power of Ymir’s heart?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Ha..... Interesting.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1082906"]="... can you confirm that it is the power of Ymir’s heart?",
    ["Dialogue1082907"]="Cough... Since this case is related to the whereabouts of Ymir's heart, I will be happy to help. I apologize for my impoliteness earlier, adventurer.\n(the young man bows and apologizes. His sincere attitude is different from earlier)",
    ["Dialogue1082908"]="Thank you for your generosity. Then, let me introduce myself again - my name is Raymond Alberto. I am a member of the Alchemists Guild and a disciple of Guild Leader Nicholas. If you are willing to trust me..... then with my dignity as an Alchemist, I will do my best to help you find the culprit. ",
    ["Dialogue1082909"]="Excellent! Well, please tell me where this happened. I want to go to the scene to search for more clues.",
    ["Dialogue1082910"]="Alright, it's not too late. Let's leave now.",
    ["Dialogue1083001"]="..... It's so interesting, Adventurer. I've never seen such a strong discoloration reaction..... \n(Raymond takes out the gold smelting stone which is still sitting in the mouth of the corpse. The original pure black stone has turned bright red)\nThe divine power left in these corpses absolutely comes from a fragment of Ymir's Heart!",
    ["Dialogue1083002"]="..... No, I mean, I'm more sure that your judgment is correct now. This case... Must have something to do with the whereabouts of the fragment of Ymir's Heart!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Ooooh..... Almost..... A replica.....</color>",
    ["Dialogue1083003"]="Gah.....! Besides, Adventurer, I have other assumptions to investigate..... Please step back a little.\n(to your bewilderment, Raymond takes out the Green Reagent again. He drops the Reagent into the mouth of the corpse. In an instant, a large amount of steam starts surging out of the mouth, making a bubbling sound.)",
    ["Dialogue1083004"]="Sure enough, as I expected, there are still left over soul fragments here... Then there must be on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>back</color> of the corpse’s neck... Huh? Why is there <color=#CA2E0AFF>no Alchemy Spell</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue1083005"]="This is very strange!\nAdventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>look through</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>book</color> beside me, which has records and entries about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dementor</color>. I want to confirm my suspicions.",
    ["Dialogue1083101"]="Are you following, Adventurer? Although I suspect these people died from a Dementor, I don't know why I couldn’t find the left over Alchemy Spell on them..... But now I have to take back my initial predictions. In Aldebaran, the only person who can master these forbidden arts at such a high-level must be a member of the Alchemist Guild. I can even be sure that..... The criminal must be of a high ranking position.",
    ["Dialogue1083102"]="..... are you asking about the motive for the crime? Ha... Let me give you a piece of advice, Adventurer. Trying to understand a madman's thoughts will only take you on a journey to the darkest parts of your imagination. I think our focus should be on how to find the criminals, not on how to help them become better people.",
    ["Dialogue1083103"]="Not much, only two.\n(Raymond pushes his glasses onto his nose and raises his index finger towards you)\nFirst, the suspect has a stable personality and a clear mind... He is a smart man with status.",
    ["Dialogue1083104"]="The books on Alchemy are only available to Guild members, whereas the parts recording the forbidden arts of Alchemy are held by the Guild Leader himself. How would ordinary people be able to bypass the Guild Leader and secretly find information about a Dementor?",
    ["Dialogue1083105"]="Knowing that there would be clues left on the bodies of those who were killed by Dementors, the criminals colluded with black market merchants and shipped the evidence out of Aldebaran disguised as smuggled goods. After you crack this case, you can then move on to solving the arson case. How are they able to manipulate machinery to burn the evidence, and even start multiple fires at the same time in order to cover their tracks? If you hadn't got here in time, the evidence would have been burned to a pile of ash.",
    ["Dialogue1083106"]="As for the second clue... Adventurer, don't you think it's strange? Since he can contact black market merchants to smuggle corpses, surely when his plan failed, the best way to avoid being caught would be to sneak out of the city. But he chose to destroy the corpses with a great flourish... As if he was more afraid of being exposed than his crime....",
    ["Dialogue1083107"]="Correct! He doesn't want anyone to find out that he's using Dementor! Furthermore, I think that he doesn't want anyone to trace the fragment of Ymir's Heart!",
    ["Dialogue1083108"]="(then, Raymond suddenly glances at you with a cold stare)\nOf course, we must arrest such a dangerous people as soon as possible. But before that, I have a question... Why are you so persistent about it? Perhaps... you also long to use the power of the fragment of Ymir's Heart, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1083109"]="<size=26>A successor of Odin’s bloodline?!</size>\n(Raymond seems to be surprised. He lowers his head and coughs a few times to forcibly cover up his emotions)\n<color=#A1979FFF>I didn't expect that... Oh, I was being careless</color>",
    ["Dialogue1083110"]="No, I mean... I didn't expect to be lucky enough to meet a successor of Odin's bloodline.\nRest assured, adventurer. Now that I know it has something to do with the alchemist guild,  I must get to the bottom of it. It is my duty to campaign against guild members who violate the rules.",
    ["Dialogue1083111"]="Time is of the essence. We must act as soon as possible. Now, the only clue we have are the wreckages of these machines, so I want you to go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>other places where the fires occurred</color>, find the damaged machines, open up their CPU’s, <color=#CA2E0AFF>and look for the embedded chip engraved with the logo of Rekenber Company</color>. As long as we find this, we can scan the database to conduct a more comprehensive investigation of the machines.",
    ["Dialogue1083201"]="(the remains of the Monsters have been completely burned, and the parts, cables and control chips inside the body have melted...)",
    ["Dialogue1083301"]="(the remains of the Monsters have been completely burned, and the parts, cables and control chips inside the body have melted...)",
    ["Dialogue1083401"]="... yes, all I need is these chips.\n(Raymond takes the chips from your hand, checks them one by one, and then smiles with satisfaction)",
    ["Dialogue1083402"]="This is an alchemy spell used to communicate. I need it to help me contact people at the Rekenber Company. Just hold tight, Adventurer. The truth... Will soon be revealed to us.",
    ["Dialogue1083501"]="Long time no see, Haley. Your hair is still as intoxicating as the morning sun.",
    ["Dialogue1083502"]="... I only have three minutes, Raymond.\n(the figure in the center of the alchemy spell raises his hand and looks at the time)\nNow, you have two minutes and forty seconds remaining.",
    ["Dialogue1083503"]="OK, OK, fair lady. By now, you should have read my previous reports. The arson cases in the city today were caused by rogue machinery. What's more, all these machines, without exception, were produced by the Rekenber Company... A coincidence, perhaps?",
    ["Dialogue1083504"]="... Raymond, since you have specifically requested my council, you should adopt the correct manners of a requester.\nCoercion, inducement and insinuation - is this the way Guild Leader Nicholas taught you to deal with people and such things?",
    ["Dialogue1083505"]="Ha... Who on earth are kidding, baby?\n(Raymond sneers. You see him licking the corners of his mouth quietly, like a bloodthirsty Anacondaq)\nThe cargo boxes set on fire by the machines contained——",
    ["Dialogue1083506"]="<size=26>Enough!</size>\n... show me the chip, Raymond. I'll check.",
    ["Dialogue1083507"]="As you wish, my lady.\n(Raymond laughs again. One by one he pulls out the computer chips that were removed from the machine and places them in front of Haley. A moment passes and a map of Aldebaran appears. The map is marked with several tracks.)",
    ["Dialogue1083508"]="As you can see, this is the chip’s memory, marking machine’s route. Most of the routes are consistent with the routine patrol route, except... Here.\n(Haley's finger points to the middle of the map, and your mind quickly recalls a towering building)",
    ["Dialogue1083509"]="It seems... That's the answer we're looking for, adventurer. However, we will need a little help to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get into the bell tower</color>.\n(Raymond squints and looks back at Haley)\nAre you sure that you are right, Haley?",
    ["Dialogue1083510"]="..... I will help you apply for permission to enter the bell tower. If what you say is true, I will do my best to assist you in your actions. But.....\n(Haley glances coldly at Raymond. The warning is self-evident)\nI hope that in the future you can be more careful with your words. Otherwise... You know what the consequences are.",
    ["Dialogue1083511"]="... Naturally. The Alchemist Guild and Rekenber Company have always shared a mutually beneficial and tactful partnership, haven't they?\n(Haley snorts coldly, sensing Raymond's affectation. The image in the alchemy spell disappears in flash with a cold zapping sound)",
    ["Dialogue1083512"]="All right, Adventurer! It's time for us to roll our sleeves up and get down to business.",
    ["Dialogue1083601"]="The clock tower is completely off limits. No one is allowed in!",
    ["Dialogue1083602"]="I'm Raymond Alberto. Here's my identification.\n(Raymond shrugs and points to the badge on his chest. It bears the logo of the Alchemist Guild and his initials)\nYou should have received our application to enter the Bell Tower.",
    ["Dialogue1083603"]="(the guard looks at Raymond's badge on his chest and nods)\nYes, I received the order from director Haley. You can enter the Bell Tower... But first, I will have to check your belongings.",
    ["Dialogue1083604"]="... take it easy, Adventurer.\n(Raymond leaned over and whispered in your ear)\nThose are the rules at Rekenber Company... Relax, it's just routine.",
    ["Dialogue1083605"]="(seeing this, the guard steps forward and carefully checks all of the items in your bag)\n... alright, nothing unusual.",
    ["Dialogue1083606"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Please come inside</color>, you two. However, you should be aware that the environment in the Bell Tower is no better than that in the city... Be very careful.",
    ["Dialogue1083701"]="Adventurer, all the clues we found have pointed to this very Bell Tower, this is likely to be the arsonists base. We must tread very carefully.There are many monsters that wander around here all throughout the year. ",
    ["Dialogue1083702"]="... you see, they have already picked up our foreign scent. There's no time to delay, go and clean up those <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brilight</color> in the middle of the path.",
    ["Dialogue1083801"]="Don't kill these machines, Adventurer. These machines are specially equipped with a defensive <color=#CA2E0AFF>self destruction mechanism</color>. They are connected together and if any one is disturbed or damaged, it will trigger a chain reaction alarm, which will reveal our whereabouts to the criminals hiding here. In order to avoid setting off the alarm, we can only <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut off</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>energy conduit</color> and let them drop into a short circuit state.",
    ["Dialogue1083901"]="(these mechanical monsters are in an inactive state and look very similar to those seen at the scene of the fire. If you look closely, you can see the same alchemy spell on their bodies...)",
    ["Dialogue1084001"]="The title of the books are as follows——\n<Study on the integration of Soul and Machine> by Fred Barr Venter\n<The Creation of Perfect Lifeforms> by Fred Barr Venter",
    ["Dialogue1084002"]="<Soul Extraction: A Summary> by Fred Barr Venter\n<Biological Cleansing: An Analysis> by Fred Barr Venter",
    ["Dialogue1084101"]="The title page of the journal reads the following words—\n<Research journal>\nDr. Lancaster Milton, Steel Capital Research Institute",
    ["Dialogue1084201"]="I didn't expect to see your name again in such a setting... Dr. Lancaster.",
    ["Dialogue1084202"]="... He is one of my predecessors. Three years ago, as an elite representative of the Alchemists Guild, he was sent to Rekenber Company’s <color=#CA2E0AFF>steel Capital Research Institute</color> to take a very important position. However, during his tenure in the Research Institute, there was an incident, whereby not only a large number of research materials were lost, but also the whereabouts of Dr. Lancaster himself.",
    ["Dialogue1084203"]="Now it looks like... This is a complete conspiracy deliberately planned by him! His purpose was to hide in the Bell Tower and study Forbidden Alchemy!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Mmm... You best not cross my path, Dr. Lancaster. Otherwise</color>",
    ["Dialogue1084204"]="I think it's possible. But so far, the evidence we have is not enough to convict him. In order for the traitor to be punished, we must gather more evidence.",
    ["Dialogue1084205"]="This research journal may contain all of the evidence we are looking for. I have a way to recreate the events described in the journal as an illusion. I have to remain here to maintain the operation, so....\n(Raymond taps on the page with his finger and looks towards you)",
    ["Dialogue1084206"]="Well, Adventurer. You have a mission that is worthy for Odin's Bloodline. Please rest assured that all the scenes presented by the alchemy spell are just illusions and will not cause any actual damage to you. You just need to try your best to find clues.",
    ["Dialogue1084207"]="... now, I'm going to draw up the Alchemy Spell. Please take this opportunity <color=#CA2E0AFF>to carefully read the words in the diary</color>. Then, use your hand to <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy spell</color> and enter the illusion.",
    ["Dialogue1084301"]="The tombstone is engraved with the following words——\nCook Anderson\nA.W.951~A.W.997",
    ["Dialogue1084401"]="The tombstone is engraved with the following words——\nSophia Alegus\nA.W.786~A.W.811",
    ["Dialogue1084501"]="The tombstone is engraved with the following words——\nSabrina Clark\nA.W.846~A.W.892",
    ["Dialogue1084601"]="The tombstone is engraved with the following words——\nAaron Milton\nA.W.979 ~A.W.1000 April 17th",
    ["Dialogue1084701"]="... You’re back, Adventurer. Did you see the scene depicted in the Journal?",
    ["Dialogue1084702"]="(after listening to your narration, Raymond smacks his lips with disdain)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Pffft... As I suspected, it was stolen by the traitor.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1084703"]="No... nothing. What’s happened has happened. The important thing is that we haven't found evidence to convict him. I decided to cast the same alchemy spell on another journal. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> it as soon as possible and <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch the alchemy spell</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1084801"]="How was it this time, did you find any clues?",
    ["Dialogue1084802"]="... you’re saying that he tested how to integrate his soul into the machines using Ymir’s heart?\n(Raymond grabs your arm and says anxiously)\nDo you see which machine?!",
    ["Dialogue1084803"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Tssk.... Idiot, you missed the most critical part.....</color>\n(Raymond loosens his grip on you, the expression on his face turning from angst to guilt, you can still feel the malice and disappointment)\nSorry, Adventurer, I got carried away. I hope I didn’t hurt you.",
    ["Dialogue1084804"]="(after his harsh reaction, he looks at you in the eyes and see’s that you are okay, he continues)\nAlthough we can't find critical evidence... At least we are certain that Dr. Lancaster stole the fragment of Ymir's heart. Next, as long as we can find the machine that has been bonded with the fragment of Ymir's heart, we will have enough evidence to convict it.",
    ["Dialogue1084805"]="I have drawn the same alchemy spell in the next journal. I hope you can carefully <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the whereabouts of the fragments</color> this time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1084901"]="(there are monster tracks all over the ground. It seems that they are quite fresh...)",
    ["Dialogue1085001"]="(the monster tracks continue on for a bit. The route makes it seem like they were looking for something...)",
    ["Dialogue1085101"]="(a civilian body falls to the ground, his body shriveled, his mouth and eyes locked wide open, he had drawn his last breath.....)",
    ["Dialogue1085201"]="(another corpse identical to the previous one. Closer observation shows that next to the corpse are monster track marks...)",
    ["Dialogue1085301"]="Uhh, bro...... Brother.....",
    ["Dialogue1085302"]="Lancaster... Brother.....\n(the magic doll stumbles, just like a child learning to walk, it’s arms are flailing and jeering in strange directions)",
    ["Dialogue1085303"]="You... Are you... Aaron?",
    ["Dialogue1085304"]="..... brother?\n(he tilts his head, flaps his wings and looks around. There was a sense of confusion and bewilderment from the cold metal eyes of the owl puppet)\nHere..... Where? I..... how..... Goo?",
    ["Dialogue1085305"]="...Aaron... Aaron... Woo...\n(Lancaster’s shoulders tremble uncontrollably and he lowers his head into his hands. He whimpers intermittently, like a broken ballad)",
    ["Dialogue1085306"]="Brother?\n(the puppet stands up. It stumbles over to Lancaster, one step, two steps, and then falls to the ground)\nBrother, don't cry..... Brother, go back home......",
    ["Dialogue1085307"]="Ok... Let's go home. Aaron, I'll take you home.\n(Lancaster says in a trembling voice, reaching to hold his warm hand against the cold mechanical wings)",
    ["Dialogue1085401"]="What happened? Where did he hide Ymir's heart?",
    ["Dialogue1085402"]="(during your recollection of the events, Raymond’s expression becomes more surprised)\nThat <color=#CA2E0AFF>owl doll</color>... Regained consciousness?",
    ["Dialogue1085403"]="... sure enough! Lancaster stole the fragment of Ymir's heart in order to revive his dead brother!",
    ["Dialogue1085404"]="We are looking for the Owl Doll which has been attached to his brother’s soul! He is able to absorb the soul of living people without the assistance of alchemy spell because his soul has been integrated with the fragments of Ymir's heart! That's why those corpses that had been killed by Dementor had  no corresponding alchemy spell remnants on their bodies!",
    ["Dialogue1085405"]="... what is that expression on your face, Adventurer? This is it! I feel like you want to tell me something! Have you gone all soft?",
    ["Dialogue1085406"]="<size=26>It doesn't matter!</size>\nDon't forget that your ultimate goal is to retrieve the fragment of the heart of Emir according to the guidance of the goddess. Now we know that Lancaster is hiding at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bottom of the clock tower</color> in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret laboratory</color>. As long as <color=#CA2E0AFF>we ambush him</color>... He will not be able to escape!",
    ["Dialogue1085501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>I really underestimated you... Dr. Lancaster</color>",
    ["Dialogue1085502"]="I underestimated the enemy, Adventurer. When I saw that he was seriously injured, I thought we would definitely win. I didn't expect him to still have the strength to use alchemy... Never mind. In his current state, he wont be able to get too far. As long as we <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the blood</color>, we will find him.",
    ["Dialogue1085601"]="(there is a pool of blood on the ground, with blood droplets splattered around. Someone is seriously injured...)",
    ["Dialogue1085701"]="(the ground is covered in blood, with footprints running through it.....)",
    ["Dialogue1085801"]="(the bloody footprints continue forward for a while. Judging from the inconsistent stride length, it must be difficult for whoever made the footprints to walk...)",
    ["Dialogue1085901"]="……\n(Lancaster’s face is extremely pale and he is lying on the ground, barely conscious)",
    ["Dialogue1085902"]="Gee, what a bother. I can't ask anything like this.\n(Raymond narrowed his eyes and kicked Lancaster in the stomach, and the weak man suddenly gave a dull hum)",
    ["Dialogue1085903"]="<color=#A1979FFF>……you’ve been a busybody.</color>\n(Raymond turns his head to say something. You notice he's grinning again)\nDon't be so serious, Adventurer. I'm just making sure he's still alive.",
    ["Dialogue1085904"]="But looking at him like this, he may not be able to answer any of my questions for a while. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>find some medicine that can heal your wounds</color> first? He is very weak now and needs <color=#CA2E0AFF>clotting grass</color> to mend the wound. Also, it would be best if you find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic crystals</color> that can refresh his mind. I remember there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>blue mice</color> around here... It must be so tough for you?",
    ["Dialogue1085905"]="Me? Of course I'm watching him... Hey, what do you think I am going to do? -- Think I'll kill him, Adventurer?\n(Raymond raises his voice. He raises his hands and looks at you incredulously)\nI'm not stupid! He is the answer to too many questions!",
    ["Dialogue1085906"]="OK, OK. Don't worry, <size=24>I... will... take... good... care... of... him</size> before you come back.",
    ["Dialogue1086001"]="(after careful observation, it seems that there are signs of fighting nearby. Two lines of footprints extend in the opposite direction, and one of them is still covered in blood...)",
    ["Dialogue1086101"]="You, were you just with Raymond....?",
    ["Dialogue1086102"]="Are these... For me?\n(Lancaster hesitates for a moment. He see’s you put the medicine on the ground. You take two steps back, he finally nods and accepts)\n... Thank you, stranger. Looks like you're not with him, are you?",
    ["Dialogue1086103"]="... investigating arson in the city? Ha... You’ve been swindled. Raymond is just using you. His goal from the beginning was to get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fragment of Ymir's heart</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1086104"]="Yes, I did steal this fragment of emir's heart from Rekenber Company. They've been chasing me since then. However, the Alchemists Guild have not been very kind themselves. They have always desired the power of the fragment of Ymir's Heart but could not openly display it due to the power of Rekenber Company. For them, the theft of the fragment happens to be a good opportunity to secretly take it for their own.",
    ["Dialogue1086105"]="(Lancaster pauses and looks confused)\nAnd you... A successor of Odin's bloodline, come to Aldebaran with the teachings of the goddess. For Raymond, this is essential to getting the fragment of Ymir’s heart into his hands. You only need to obtain the fragment... and you will turn into an abandoned child.",
    ["Dialogue1086106"]="You have your responsibility... And I have my persistence.",
    ["Dialogue1086107"]="(Lance's eyes darken)\nEven you believe... Is was a mistake for me to choose to save Aaron?",
    ["Dialogue1086108"]="But even so, I don't want to make an enemy out of you... We clearly have many ways to understand each other, why should we choose to fight?\n(Lancaster looks at you. The sincerity in his eyes is familiar.)\nIf you are willing to believe me... Please follow me and I will explain it all to you.",
    ["Dialogue1086201"]="That's why... I can't give you the fragments of Ymir's heart",
    ["Dialogue1086202"]="Adventurer, you just helped me, so I should repay you for your kindness. I'd like to tell you the whole truth, but for now... I hope you can help me appease this owl puppet. Please believe me, this is the only way I will be able to unburden myself.\n(Lancaster faces you and bends down)",
    ["Dialogue1086203"]="I need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>star sand</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bathory</color>’s body, as well as soul calming <color=#CA2E0AFF>requiem grass</color>. As long as these materials are available, a tranquilizer can be made to calm the child.",
    ["Dialogue1086301"]="Thanks to your help, it has stabilized... Thank you very much, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1086302"]="I think since you have read my research diary, you may have already guessed that this owl puppet is my brother Aaron. I deliberately stole a fragment of Ymir's heart... in order to enable my brother to return to the world.",
    ["Dialogue1086303"]="No... it's not that simple.\n(Lancaster rolls up his sleeve. His arm is covered in a lacerations both old and new, shallow and deep)\nThese... Are all Aaron.",
    ["Dialogue1086304"]="At first... I did succeed in helping Aaron regain consciousness. But gradually, I found that Aaron’s soul would intermittently fall into a strange manic state. He would could only calm down briefly by swallowing a soul of the living. But at the same time, every time you ingest a new soul, the next manic attack will be more intense.",
    ["Dialogue1086305"]="At first, in order to protect Aaron, I condoned this behavior, and in order to prevent the story from being exposed I even contacted black market merchants to deal with the bodies of the victims. But as Aaron would make more and more attacks, I realized that my supposed remedy had the opposite effect. If I wanted to save Aaron, I had to find out why he was out of control. So I managed to trap the puppet here and began to study the literature surrounding soul-integration.",
    ["Dialogue1086306"]="It's a pity...  Before I came to a conclusion, I was attacked by a monster in the Bell Tower. This book was also damaged in the battle. If you can help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the missing pages</color>, maybe we can continue to study it.",
    ["Dialogue1086401"]="Thanks a lot, so you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> the missing part before. I remember that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the part related to Dementor</color> should be found in... Here it is.",
    ["Dialogue1086501"]="Tortured... Died unjustly? No... how is that possible? Aaron's death was an accident!",
    ["Dialogue1086502"]="My brother Aaron... used to be in the guard regiment at Rekenber Company. About six months ago, he died pursuing a criminal. For this, Rekenber Company awarded Aaron a medal. Before he was buried, I was given the chance to see Aaron's body. It was just a common gunshot wound and there was nothing suspicious.",
    ["Dialogue1086503"]="You mean... Did the company deceive me? Is there something strange about Aaron's death?",
    ["Dialogue1086504"]="Do you want to investigate the cause of Aaron's death? I have had my suspicions, it’s just.... (Lancaster raises his head and looks at the owl doll trapped in the barrier and mumbles to himself)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Are these the hints you left behind for me... Aaron....</color>",
    ["Dialogue1086505"]="I think maybe the diary which Aaron left behind can help us. It's just... I hid that diary in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>basement research room</color> in an <color=#CA2E0AFF>engraved wooden box</color>. Now I can only ask you to retrieve it, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1086601"]="This diary is the last thing Aaron left for me to read. After his death, I was immersed in grief and did not dare to read his diary... Maybe he recorded everything he encountered before his death.....",
    ["Dialogue1086602"]="(Lancaster looks a little surprised to hear what you said)\nThe Alchemy of reproducing memories? Of course I know how to perform it, but... of all ways, why would I choose this ?",
    ["Dialogue1086603"]="... Thank you, Adventurer. I'm not mistaken. You are a kind man.\nThen, I will draw an alchemy spell that can reproduce memories in Aaron's diary. As long as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch the alchemy spell</color>, you can enter Aaron's memories. All this... I'll leave it to you to investigate.",
    ["Dialogue1086701"]="Oh, it’s the Milton's little brother! Would you like two freshly baked loaves of bread? They’re still hot!",
    ["Dialogue1086702"]="Um... Two... No, no, one, whole wheat.\n(Aaron takes out his wallet, carefully spreads the coins in the palm of his hand, counts them carefully, and then picks out two and hands them to the vendor.)\nIs that enough?",
    ["Dialogue1086703"]="Enough, enough! More?!-- how can you be willing to spend money today? I thought you were the same as usual. Just look at it go!",
    ["Dialogue1086704"]="Heheh... Because today is a day I will never forget! My brother... He has been admitted to the alchemists guild and will soon become a formal alchemist! So, I am going to celebrate with my brother over a big meal!",
    ["Dialogue1086705"]="Oh, that's amazing. Our corner of the world has finally produced someone with some substance!\n(the merchant wrapped the whole wheat loaf of bread in some paper. But after thinking for a second, he opened the paper up again, picked up a freshly made bacon roll and put it in together)",
    ["Dialogue1086706"]="(Aaron's eyes widened, he couldn’t believe what he was seeing)\nHey? Uncle Huck, I didn't pay.....",
    ["Dialogue1086707"]="(the merchant waved his hand, smiled and handed over the bread)\nJust take it as a token from my heart. You two boys can't go hungry on such an important day, can you?",
    ["Dialogue1086708"]="Thank you, uncle Huck!",
    ["Dialogue1086801"]="I've been waiting for you for ages! I heard that Lancaster was admitted to the alchemist guild? You must be so proud!",
    ["Dialogue1086802"]="(the merchant’s kind words made Aaron blush. He scratched his head in embarrassment and smiled)\nThis... This is the result of my brother's hard work. Right up to this day he has tirelessly worked... He says, god helps those who help themselves.",
    ["Dialogue1086803"]="Oh, everything seems different today, even you have become a cultured man!\n(Blair's eyes focused in on the neatly arranged fresh fish in front of him, as he looks for the largest one)",
    ["Dialogue1086804"]="Now that you’re all going to be rich, you have to buy a fish worthy of your stature! You see, this one is the freshest that I can offer - I’ll even give you a discount and only charge you 10 Zeny!",
    ["Dialogue1086805"]=".... uhh, uhhh? No, I....",
    ["Dialogue1086806"]="Don’t be silly, you’re welcome! We are neighbors! If you grow into the developed man in the future, you cannot forget the love between us!\n(Blair’s knife sliced up and down and after a while, a clean fish was thrown into Aaron's basket)\nHere you go!",
    ["Dialogue1086807"]="OK, ok... Thank you, Blair.",
    ["Dialogue1086901"]="Welcome ~ Come in and take a look at today's new products! Kyanite from Mjolnir, medicine flown in from the Sograt Desert, embroidered handkerchiefs from Prontera! They are great as gifts or for your own use!",
    ["Dialogue1086902"]="(throughout the merchant's sales pitch, Aaron scans the large variety of goods and then locks his eyes onto a beautiful looking greeting card)\nI want... This.",
    ["Dialogue1086903"]="(he pauses for a few seconds, then grabs his head with embarrassment)\nBut I can't write yet... Could you please write a few words on the card for me?",
    ["Dialogue1086904"]="No problem. What would you like to say?",
    ["Dialogue1086905"]="Well... I want to congratulate my brother on being admitted to the alchemist guild, and then thank him for his hard work in supporting his family for so many years. From now on, I hope that we will always stick together.",
    ["Dialogue1086906"]="(with Aaron's narration, the young merchant raised his pen and wrote on the card)\n... is that all? Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>confirm the contents of the card</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1087001"]="What happened? What did you see?",
    ["Dialogue1087002"]="……\n(throughout your narration, Lancaster’s face becomes paler and paler. You want to comfort him, but he just shakes his head)",
    ["Dialogue1087003"]="It doesn't matter, adventurer, it's all over... Now we have more important things to concentrate on. I have drawn a new alchemy spell on the next page of my journal. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue to investigate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1087101"]="... let me say, there is no need to take any crap from someone else’s child. You have done so much to help him! You had to beg the director to get those special drugs smuggled using a black market merchant. Now, you have to give up a place at Juno University in order to take care of him? Lancaster, don't be silly! A waste like him might as well...",
    ["Dialogue1087201"]="Aaron! Are you hurt?!",
    ["Dialogue1087202"]="Brother?!\nI, I'm fine... Just....\n(Aaron's face goes blank, his voice slowly fades, and finally he isn’t saying anything)",
    ["Dialogue1087203"]="... is it really okay? Let me have a look.\n(Lancaster carefully checks Aaron's hand. After confirming that he is not injured, he turns to face the other three people)\nI warned you to stay away from Aaron!",
    ["Dialogue1087204"]="Tssk... Bad luck. All right, you're lucky with bean sprouts today! You have the support of an alchemists brother... You better wish our paths don’t cross again. Let's go!\n(the ruffians dispersed in all directions)",
    ["Dialogue1087301"]="... Could that have really happened?\nBut that day, Aaron told me clearly... He got into an argument with them on the way to the alchemists guild... Did he lie to me in order to hide that?",
    ["Dialogue1087302"]="But... Why didn't he ask me? If he asked me, I would have told him that I never thought he was a burden. On the contrary, the only reason I have achieved anything is because we have always depended on each other. It is precisely because he has always supported me.\n<color=#A1979FFF>Aaron..... Is my light....</color>",
    ["Dialogue1087303"]="... that's all. What's the use of saying that now. Please, Adventurer, touch the alchemy spell again, we... Haven't found the answer we want.",
    ["Dialogue1087401"]="Unacceptable! Do you know the rules of the Rekenber Company?!\n(in full view of everyone, Arnold slaps Aaron on the chest. The slap was so powerful, wrinkled white paper falls from his hand)",
    ["Dialogue1087402"]="*Gasp*...! This, this is.....?\n(the boy coughs and looks down at the white paper falling to the ground)\nMy... Enlistment application form.",
    ["Dialogue1087403"]="Answer me -- <size=26>didn't you see the conscription notice?! Why isn't there a family signature on it?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1087404"]="I... I.....\n(Aaron for a moment doesn’t know what to say. He leans over and picks up his enlistment application form. The column signed by his family is left empty)",
    ["Dialogue1087405"]="I can't allow you to join the Rekenber Company guards without family permission. Please pack up your things immediately and get out.....",
    ["Dialogue1087406"]="... I, I am an orphan!\n(Aaron clenches the white paper in his hand. There is a murmuring coming from the crowd behind him. He looks at Arnold nervously and blushes)\nMy family... They, they are all dead.....",
    ["Dialogue1087407"]="... hmmm, no wonder, you do look a little delicate.\n(Arnold looks at Aaron up and down, unimpressed)\nCan someone like you... Pass our enlistment test?",
    ["Dialogue1087408"]="Ah! What the heck! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me!</color>\nWell, you must have been mentally preparing for this for a while now. Here, no one is going to treat you differently because of your own shortcomings! We are all equals here. If you want to join the guards, you’re going to have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat the demons in the examination room</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1087501"]="... this time, was it Aaron's memory of joining the army?\nI remember that, he wanted to surprise me..... in order to pass the Rekenber Company guards regiment examination, he trained in secret without telling me... He always looked so feeble and weak, but once he made up his mind, he never held back....",
    ["Dialogue1087502"]="(Lancaster strokes the pages of his diary and becomes lost in his own memories)\nIt's also foolish of me to leave Aaron’s side. I have found him in a terrible state more than once, but he has always found strange reasons to go through the motions. If... If I could have cared about him a little more....",
    ["Dialogue1087503"]="... whats gone is gone, and it doesn't help to say that now... Let's continue our investigation, Adventurer.\nI have finished drawing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy spell</color> on the next page. Please take a break and <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch</color> it again to enter Aaron's memory.",
    ["Dialogue1087601"]="I have a special task for you, Aaron.",
    ["Dialogue1087602"]="... now?\n(Aaron looks at the time suspiciously)\nCaptain, I'm on night-duty later.",
    ["Dialogue1087603"]="Leave it to someone else. Now, instead I need you to assist the researchers in their research and testing of new drugs.",
    ["Dialogue1087604"]="... new drugs?\n(Aaron looks up and standing in the open space not too far away are two researchers dressed in white. A faint chill overcomes him when his eyes meet theirs)",
    ["Dialogue1087605"]="Don't worry, Aaron. It's a nutritional supplement for <color=#CA2E0AFF>physical fitness</color>. However, the Institute has improved the formula so that the medicine can take effect faster. All you have to do is go there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>inject medicine</color>, and with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> compete in a few simple <color=#CA2E0AFF>contests</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1087606"]="But, I.....",
    ["Dialogue1087607"]="(sensing Aaron's hesitation, Arnold squints and gives him a soothing pat on the shoulder)\nDisn’t you always long to be strong? Trust me, this medicine will make you feel reborn.....",
    ["Dialogue1087701"]="... I don’t like the expression on your face, Adventurer. What happened this time?",
    ["Dialogue1087702"]="Energy enhancing... Nutritional supplements?\nNo... I’ve never heard about the company conducting such research! The drugs that need to be tested on humans must pass the risk assessment at least three times. It’s impossible for me not to know!",
    ["Dialogue1087703"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Unless..... Unless.....</color>\n(Lancaster looks at the journal in his hand and mumbles to himself. He turns the page of the diary and suddenly turns pale with surprise)\n<size=26>... what is this?! </size>",
    ["Dialogue1087704"]="(Lancaster quickly turns to the last page of the journal. You look down and find that the final pages are full of illegible graffiti-like <color=#CA2E0AFF>messy scribbles</color>)\nWhat's going on? Aaron... Aaron, what happened to him?",
    ["Dialogue1087705"]="You, you mean, Aaron drew this strange graffiti because they were conducting inhuman tests on him?\n(Lancaster lowers his head to read the journal one more time. The devilish expressions are completely unrecognizable)",
    ["Dialogue1087706"]="You, you mean, this strange graffiti proves that there is something strange about Aaron's death?\n(Lancaster lowers his head to read his diary again. The indescribable symbols on the paper are like the ferocious expression of the devil, which makes people afraid)",
    ["Dialogue1087707"]="Maybe you're right... I know Aaron's character. He wouldn’t normally express himself like this. He must have been overwhelmed. Look at the state of this handwriting. Some of the strokes have even penetrated several pages of white paper",
    ["Dialogue1087708"]="<size=26>-- found them!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1087709"]="…Raymond?! No!",
    ["Dialogue1087710"]="... you really caused me a lot of trouble, Dr. Lancaster. And you, Adventurer... I didn't expect that you would give up the fragment of Ymir's heart that easily to play house with each other....",
    ["Dialogue1087711"]="Ha... What? Haven't seen you for a while. Have you been bought off by this traitor? What did he give you? Promised to give up the fragments of Ymir's heart did he?\nBut even so, you have to ask me if I agree? This fragment... I'm determined to get it.\n(Raymond looks at the magic doll bound in the enchantment, like an eagle who has found it’s prey)",
    ["Dialogue1087712"]="<size=26>Don't hurt Aaron!</size>\nI, I will find a way to extract the fragments. Before that, don't do anything to this magic doll! Aarons soul is in there!",
    ["Dialogue1087713"]="oh....? Are you pleading with me Dr. Lancaster?\n... that's right. If you hadn't begged me for mercy earlier, maybe I would have died at the hands of this Adventurer. In love and in reason, I should really repay your kindness, right?",
    ["Dialogue1087714"]="(Raymond smiles. He licks the dagger in his hand and points to the owl doll)\nSo I have made up my mind... I should eliminate your true source of pain. What do you think, Dr. Lancaster?",
    ["Dialogue1087801"]="Bad, bad... I can't hold it back anymore.....\n(Lancaster’s face scrunches into a ball, blood seeps from his wound, and his snow-like white clothes gradually turns red)",
    ["Dialogue1087802"]="No..... It's already too late!!\nThe owl puppet has devoured too many souls. Even when it is in a stable mood, I can barely trap it with the power of the alchemy spell, but now it has been angered, coupled with the power of the fragments of Ymir’s Heart... No one can subdue it anymore!",
    ["Dialogue1087803"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Maybe... If I can just.... </color>\n(Lancaster’s voice becomes less and less noticeable. The swirling winds caused by the spell drown out his voice)",
    ["Dialogue1087804"]="I mean... I can weaken the doll! However, you must help me find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magebane Elixir</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>a shadow crystal</color> as soon as possible, as well as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Larkspur</color>, which can be used as a medicine guide! Be quick... I wont last long!",
    ["Dialogue1087901"]="(lanster quickly checks the medicine you brought back and nods to you)\nIt's these... Adventurer. You’ve done well. Now, please mix these herbs together... And <color=#CA2E0AFF>let me take them</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1088001"]="All right... Adventurer, please step back. I will lift the alchemy spell and let the doll devour my soul.",
    ["Dialogue1088002"]="This is the only way to subdue the doll. The medicine I just took is actually a highly toxic hallucinogenic drug, which damages the mind. When the medicine kicks in, you must let the doll devour my soul. This should greatly weaken the magic doll and grant you an opportunity to defeat it.",
    ["Dialogue1088003"]="... you have to listen to me, Adventurer. There may be other ways to save Aaron, but if we let him get away, it will only cause more pain and more casualties.\nMy life for the lives of many..... It is the only way.\n(Lancaster looks at you calmly, his facial expression relaxed. He has made up his mind)",
    ["Dialogue1088004"]="Don't hesitate Adventurer. You are a hero of Odin's bloodline. I will not be able to rest until I return the fragment of Ymir's heart to you. Moreover... I am to blame for what it has become. I can't save Aaron, but this time... I will accompany him wherever he goes.\nI beg you... <color=#CA2E0AFF>To end our pain</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1088005"]="Thank you... Adventurer.\n(you nod you head in agreement, Lancaster smiles a smile of relief. In the shadow of the spell, he glances at the huge owl doll)\nNow... Let’s go home, Aaron.",
    ["Dialogue1088101"]="... You have successfully retrieved the fragment of Ymir's heart. Why are you so upset?",
    ["Dialogue1088102"]="(during your narration, sympathy and compassion slowly appears in the goddess’s drooping eyes)\nReally... I did not expect to be able to understand your sadness...  There is no need to blame yourself.",
    ["Dialogue1088103"]="Heir of Odin's bloodline... You have witnessed much pain and injustice on your journey. You are a hero, but you don't have to shoulder it all yourself. Now, their souls have followed their destiny, and there is no need to suffer unnecessarily. You should be happy for them.",
    ["Dialogue1088104"]="(the goddess looks at you gently)\nYou should carry on going forward even if you can’t let go. Although, your ability to let go will help you mature. This is also the most precious gift left to you by the dead.",
    ["Dialogue1088105"]="Good... I'm proud of you, heir of Odin's bloodline. Now, it's time to tell you the location of the next fragment - it's on the island of fantasy, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo island</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1088106"]="It is far away from the Kingdom, and thus not disturbed by the noise of the world... They do not follow our common rules or customs, so you must remember to not be careless.\nNo one can predict how one's desires will change when they aren’t constrained by the rules of society....",
    ["Dialogue1090101"]="Hello, brave Adventurer! Welcome to the city that never sleeps: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1090102"]="Hold on a second! Before you begin your journey, please allow me to give you a simple introduction to this faraway island. Otherwise, being unfamiliar with the culture here might get you into unnecessary trouble!",
    ["Dialogue1090103"]="Such as...\n(W winks and whispers into your ears)\nYou would do well to remember...",
    ["Dialogue1090104"]="Never enter the cave on the western side of the island!",
    ["Dialogue1090105"]="I-I'm sorry! It's been too long, so I couldn't help but play a prank on you!\n(The young girl raises the corners of her skirt and bows at you. However, there's no apologetic look in her mischievous expression.)",
    ["Dialogue1090106"]="Well... You surely are a veteran Adventurer. If it were Shuling, she'd be crying right now.",
    ["Dialogue1090107"]="Anyway. There is truth to my little prank. The caves on the western side of Comodo really are forbidden. No entry is allowed without permissions from the leader.",
    ["Dialogue1090108"]="I'm sure you already know that the prosperity you see in Comodo today is all thanks to Lady Margaret of the Nerius family. She and her trusted friend, Natasha Trista, saved this forsaken island from the claws of the evil dragons and asked the king for management rights. Since then, Comodo has been the territory of the Nerius family.",
    ["Dialogue1090109"]="But the kind Lady Margaret did not drive the dragons to their deaths. Instead, she signed a peace treaty with them to allow them to continue to live in the western part of the island. Ever since, humans and dragons have lived apart peacefully. They stay out of each other's lives and there's no conflict. Comodo started to prosper under the management of the Nerius family, and it became a paradise of joy and peace.",
    ["Dialogue1090110"]="And so, Adventurer, if you were to enter the forbidden nest, it would go against our peace treaty with the dragons! Of course, even without a peace treaty, I would advise against doing so. After all, that place is not just filled with ferocious monsters; the Ancient Dragon resides there as well!",
    ["Dialogue1090111"]="I know, I know! You’re not here for a simple vacation. Actually, I just saw the leader of th Euphonic Symphony, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vendra Trista</color>, heading toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>leader’s mansion</color> in a hurry. It seems like she has something urgent to report to Lady Alexia.",
    ["Dialogue1090112"]="Maybe it has something to do with what you’re here for!\n(W winks at you again, studying you with the same adorable but cunning eyes)",
    ["Dialogue1090201"]="Vendra, it's not that I don't believe you, but you've seen what the dragons' nest is like. They can hardly defend themselves. How can it be possible that they have the extra resources to attack us?",
    ["Dialogue1090202"]="But, I’ve personally spoken to the islanders who were attacked. They’ve never seen dragons before, but they were able to clearly describe their appearance and attacks. No matter how you look at it, it doesn't seem like they’re lying... Alexia, maybe we should investigate further?",
    ["Dialogue1090203"]="What do you to do? You know I won't give you permission to enter the dragons' cave, and I can't spare anyone to protect you as all of us have our hands full tending to the victims and keeping up with patrols. The caves are dangerous. I won't let you go alone.",
    ["Dialogue1090204"]="I...",
    ["Dialogue1090205"]="A foreign... Adventurer?\nI’m very sorry. Though it may seem rude, the Nerius family has no time to host guests right now. If you’re here to sightsee, kindly seek directions elsewhere.",
    ["Dialogue1090206"]="(You are interrupted before you could finish)\nAlexia, why not let this Adventurer assist me in my endeavors?",
    ["Dialogue1090207"]="<size=26>Vendra!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1090208"]="An Adventurer who made it here all the way from Prontera is certainly no ordinary person. This should put your concern over my safety to rest, right? Furthermore, I promise I will never enter the dragons' cave alone.",
    ["Dialogue1090209"]="But...\n(The head of the Nerius family still seems hesitant, while the girl firmly gripped onto the edge of your clothing with great anticipation)",
    ["Dialogue1090210"]="Never mind her... <color=#CA2E0AFF>With me,</color> Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1090301"]="My apologies for volunteering you without your agreement, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1090302"]="Heh... I knew you are gonna say that!\n<color=#A1979FFF>I mean, you are the legendary Adventurer with sung deeds all over the continent...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1090303"]="Nothing! I mean, I’ll take all the help I can get! This is the place where the victims claim to have first seen the dragons. If it’s true, then we must be able to find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>clues</color> here. But Comodo is a dangerous place and the monsters are quite aggressive. Do stay on your toes when <color=#CA2E0AFF>searching</color> the area.",
    ["Dialogue1090401"]="Hmmm... From what I know, the claw marks and scales do resemble draconic features.",
    ["Dialogue1090402"]="When I was little, I once entered the dragons' nest. I met a dragonling. Its forehead had an <color=#CA2E0AFF>oddly shaped scale</color>; the scale was in the shape of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>wave</color>...\n(Vendra drooped, submerged in her memories)",
    ["Dialogue1090403"]="Such an unforgettable experience, vividly carved into my memories. You may also <color=#CA2E0AFF>double check</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF> Encyclopedia of Ancient Monsters</color>. Its detailed descriptions of the physical features and behavior patterns of the dragons might come in handy.",
    ["Dialogue1090501"]="So? What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue1090502"]="(Vendra rests her cheek on the palm of her hand, thinking it over)\nYou’re right. It would be hard to convince Alexia with just the claw marks and scales. The dragons have not been seen for millennia. I guess... we will have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look deeper into the marsh</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1090601"]="Adventurer, there seems to be strong elemental powers of fire left here. The people of Comodo generally use more traditional weapons like bows and blades; few are able to control magic. This cannot be the work of the residents...",
    ["Dialogue1090602"]="Let’s go put out the fires first! I remember seeing quite a few small <color=#CA2E0AFF>ponds</color> on the way. We can <color=#CA2E0AFF>fetch</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>water</color> from them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put out the fires.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1090701"]="They don’t seem to be common fires. Water has no effect on them. We’ll have to find another way.\n<color=#A1979FFF>Strange... I feel like I’ve seen fires like these somewhere...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1090702"]="A dark, purple flame... that burns continuously... and cannot be put out...?!\n(Vendra head emerges from deep thoughts, her voice filled with disbelief)",
    ["Dialogue1090703"]="C-Could it be...?!",
    ["Dialogue1090704"]="No... I may be overthinking it, but... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer. We need to find more clues!",
    ["Dialogue1090801"]="Doctor, do the victims exhibit large burns on their bodies?",
    ["Dialogue1090802"]="How did you know? My patients all suffer from high-degree burns. I even had to hire Adventurers from outside to gather Millennial Frost from the caves on the eastern side of the island...",
    ["Dialogue1090803"]="What’s so special about these burns for them to require <color=#CA2E0AFF>Millennial Frost</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1090804"]="I first treated them like any common burn but to no avail. The wounds worsened... It was not until the patients told me about how they were burned by dark purple flames that I recalled a local myth about the inextinguishable <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eternal Flames</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1090805"]="You are talking about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Flame</color>... right?",
    ["Dialogue1090806"]="Yes... The very same one according to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Encyclopedia of Ancient Monsters</color>, specific to dragons.\n(With the doctor’s words, Vendra takes out the encyclopedia and motions for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read the part related to the Dragon Flame</color>)",
    ["Dialogue1090901"]="Now we can be sure that the dragons did in fact attack the residents! There are no other creatures in the entire Midgard that can use the Eternal Flame from the abyss.",
    ["Dialogue1090902"]="I’ve also been thinking about that. There must be a reason as to why they suddenly decided to break this peace that we’ve enjoyed for thousands of years.",
    ["Dialogue1090903"]="I have some theories, but I’ll need more proof to validate them... Adventurer, please help me and <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the victims</color>. I need to know if they exhibit any other symptoms aside from the burns.",
    ["Dialogue1091001"]="Nothing else... besides the burns?",
    ["Dialogue1091002"]="Adventurer... based on the evidence we’ve gathered, we are sure that the dragons are the culprits, but this situation is closely tied to the pact between the dragons and the Nerius family. If we act on our own, we may upset the situation even more.",
    ["Dialogue1091003"]="We better <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report our findings to Alexia</color>. I can only hope she can... make the right decision.",
    ["Dialogue1091101"]="The Dragon Flame!? How could this be? No one has ever seen the Dragon Flame ever since that Dragon War thousands of years ago!",
    ["Dialogue1091102"]="I'm still in disbelief as well, Alexia... But is there another kind of Eternal Flame that can only be put out by Millennial Frost? Now that the dragons have reclaimed the power of the Dragon Flame and attacked the residents... We don’t know what they are planning, but we have to be prepared!",
    ["Dialogue1091103"]="No... We must be missing something. We hold the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pact</color> signed by the Ancient Dragon and Lady Margaret... Even if they don’t like it, they wouldn’t dare to break it...",
    ["Dialogue1091104"]="Hmm... I see. You’re not a citizen of Comodo. Hence, you are not familiar with the deeds of Lady Margaret. No matter. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Peace Treaty of Comodo\"</color> is on the table. Since you have helped us greatly, you have my permission as the current head of the Nerius family to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> this important document.",
    ["Dialogue1091201"]="So, what do you think? This is the medal of honor we wear with pride. If Lady Margaret didn’t defeat the dragons and establish this pact with them, Comodo would never have become the prosperous place it is today.",
    ["Dialogue1091202"]="Alexia, it’s not the time to relish in our own glory. We need to—",
    ["Dialogue1091203"]="Alright, alright. I know what you want to say.\n(Alexia waves in protest and impatiently interrupts Vendra)",
    ["Dialogue1091204"]="Yes, they broke the pact first, but we haven’t been keeping up with our end of the bargain either... I discovered that some servants had embezzled the tributes for the dragons, and our people have been sneaking into the cave, disturbing the peace with the dragons... It’s all on me.",
    ["Dialogue1091205"]="Lady Margaret meant for Comodo to be a haven for its residents. I am willing to make some sacrifices for that ideal. If we take the initiative and offer them more tributes in apology, they should be willing to back off... right?",
    ["Dialogue1091206"]="But—",
    ["Dialogue1091207"]="<size=26>Vendra!</size>\n(Alexia interrupts Vendra again, a warning in her eyes)",
    ["Dialogue1091208"]="You have defied my decisions many times today. You think of me as family, as I do you. But do not forget. I am the Lady of Comodo.",
    ["Dialogue1091209"]="...\n(Vendra wears a deep frown on her face, expressing deepening resentment in response to Alexia’s words)",
    ["Dialogue1091210"]="I’ve made up my mind. The discussion is over. I would greatly appreciate it if you are willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>assist</color> me and <color=#CA2E0AFF>appease the dragons</color>. If not, you should take your leave now.",
    ["Dialogue1091301"]="(Alexia smiles upon seeing your compromise)\nSmart choice, Adventurer. I will take care of this. Just follow my lead.",
    ["Dialogue1091302"]="The pact forbids the dragons from leaving their nests, stipulating that we must deliver tributes and supplies to ensure their continued survival. They must’ve revolted only because the offerings were not sufficient. That is the root of the problem, so the way to solve it is to increase our tributes to them.",
    ["Dialogue1091303"]="Previously, our servants would deliver 5 servings of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chewy Scale Stems</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tender Frog Legs</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crispy Bug Whiskers</color> each on a daily basis. Now, as a gesture of goodwill, we will <color=#CA2E0AFF>double</color> that today for the greedy dragons.",
    ["Dialogue1091401"]="Thanks, Adventurer. I will have my servant Erida deliver them to the nests to show them our goodwill.",
    ["Dialogue1091402"]="Also, from now on, I will officially prohibit unauthorized entry into the dragons' cave. So, I hope that you can travel to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cave in the western part of Comodo</color> to check if there are still islanders or tourists in that area. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lead them away</color> should you encounter any.",
    ["Dialogue1091403"]="Until now, I have not held anyone accountable for breaking into the cave. But this is a delicate situation right now, and we have to do everything to avoid further conflicts.",
    ["Dialogue1091501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>My... my ores...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1091502"]="W-What? I have to leave? <size=24>No! No way!</size><size=26>I haven’t gotten my ores back!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1091503"]="(The merchant picks up the backpack and shows you the large hole at the bottom.)\nI... I have no idea when my backpack broke. It got lighter and lighter as I walked, and when I turned around to take a look... the bag was empty! I lost all the Dragon Flame Amber that I'd painstakingly collected!",
    ["Dialogue1091504"]="S-So... I’m not going anywhere before I <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back</color> my <color=#CA2E0AFF>ores</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1091601"]="Yes! That’s it! That’s the ore I lost!",
    ["Dialogue1091602"]="I know! I’ll leave... Hey, did you say the leader ordered to lock down the cave?",
    ["Dialogue1091603"]="Well... Isn't this a great business opportunity...\n<color=#A1979FFF>I'm gonna stock up on these Dragon Flame Amber, and when the demand is high and supply is low... Heheheheh!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1091701"]="Oh...? You want me to leave the cave?\n(The middle-aged man in luxury clothing studies you arrogantly and gives you a resentful look)",
    ["Dialogue1091702"]="Excuse me for being blunt, Adventurer. I find your attitude to be quite rude for someone I’ve never met before.",
    ["Dialogue1091703"]="I see. If it’s the leader’s orders... However, I came all the way here for the sole purpose of seeing the Frozen Abyss and the Frozen Fleet deep within the caves of Comodo. I’m sure the island would not wish to see a guest return empty-handed now, would it?",
    ["Dialogue1091704"]="Simple, really. I am here for the sights. The monstrous caves. There’d be no need for me to venture any deeper if you could <color=#CA2E0AFF>snatch a photo of the Frozen Abyss and Frozen Fleet</color> for me, right?",
    ["Dialogue1091801"]="(He looks through the pictures you brought back, clearly disappointed)\nIt is indeed a magnificent sight. However... it still pales in comparison to the Ice Cave in my homeland.",
    ["Dialogue1091802"]="Hmph, I come from Rael, the capital of Arunafeltz. Formed at the same time as the continent itself, it’s an ice cave that never melts. It is truly a wonder to behold. If you ever come to Arunafeltz, you must visit it. It will not disappoint you.",
    ["Dialogue1091803"]="(The man nods slightly and gives you a formal salute)\nSo then, I’ll be leaving this place as I promised. I will be visiting the central volcano here next, though, I doubt it’ll be more breathtaking than the Torr Volcano... Well, it’s better than nothing.",
    ["Dialogue1091901"]="<color=#A1979FFF>No... Cannot give up...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1091902"]="I know why you’re here, Adventurer, but I’m not leaving!\n(The archaeologist struggles to swing his pointy shovel, trying his best to be nothing but an excavator without acknowledging your presence)",
    ["Dialogue1091903"]="I know all about that! That's precisely why I had to get here before the cave is locked down! This is the last chance for me to learn how the dragons' cave came to be!",
    ["Dialogue1091904"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Vein</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Megalodons</color>, of course! They are one of the longest-existing monsters in the world. They can help validate my research! But I’m no match for the vicious monsters, so all I can do is try and find if there are any Ice Veins left behind by dead Megalodons...",
    ["Dialogue1091905"]="(He eyes you up and down while he explains)\nBut for an Adventurer like you... It’s a piece of cake, taking down those Megalodons, right? I’ll leave, if you can get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Veins</color>... How about it?",
    ["Dialogue1091906"]="Oh? You're unwilling? Doesn't matter. As long as I have my pointy shovel, there's nowhere in this world I can't reach. Even if Alexia seals the dragons' cave, all I have to do is tunnel in, <size=22>alert the dragons</size>, and maybe <size=24>start a war?</size> <size=26>Nothing too serious, right? (*❦ω❦)</size>",
    ["Dialogue1092001"]="Ice Veins! Now, there’s finally progress to be made!",
    ["Dialogue1092002"]="Out of my way, Adventurer!\n(He waves at you violently, forcing you aside with his glare to make way for him)",
    ["Dialogue1092101"]="I’ve been waiting for you, Adventurer. You must’ve done what Alexia asked of you, I assume?",
    ["Dialogue1092102"]="So... What do you think? Do you also believe that the dragons attacked us because they needed food?",
    ["Dialogue1092103"]="(Vendra seems relieved to hear you say that)\nWhat a relief... I don’t agree with what Alexia said. We’ve checked on the victims earlier. They had no other external injury aside from the burns...",
    ["Dialogue1092104"]="If you really think about it, if the dragons attacked humans out of hunger, then some survivors should be missing a limb or two, or taken back to the nest. So, no. The way I see it, the dragons are seeking revenge through destruction. This is their way of challenging us.",
    ["Dialogue1092105"]="Explain to Alexia? No, Adventurer. You don’t understand her. As the leader of Comodo and the head of the Nerius family, she’s anything but a fool. It might even be possible that she’s already aware of the truth. However, to her... nothing is more important than the \"rules\".",
    ["Dialogue1092106"]="The weight of the Nerius family legacy is immeasurable... but is that what Comodo needs right now? Death inevitably comes to the drowning man with sacks of gold, unless he lets go.",
    ["Dialogue1092107"]="(Vendra faces you directly and bows steeply)\nI want to save her... save this island. I will need to enlist your help for this, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1092108"]="Thanks, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1092109"]="First, I need you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue the investigation</color> with me and find more evidence that proves the dragons' agenda... It's the only way for Alexia to face the truth. What say you?",
    ["Dialogue1092201"]="In the previous attacks, the only evidence of the dragons' involvement is the Dragon Flame. If we can uncover the reason and proof of the Dragon Flame's reemergence, we can make Alexia admit that the dragons are revolting.",
    ["Dialogue1092202"]="I’ve brought along a special <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Bottle</color> this time. Not only can it withstand high temperatures, it’s been enchanted with a spell that can seal the Dragon Flame. There’s no time to waste. We need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect samples of the Dragon Flame</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1092301"]="Good job, Adventurer. Now, we’ll need to analyze the samples we collected. I have someone in mind, and he's well-suited for this... but he might not agree to it.",
    ["Dialogue1092302"]="Do you know of a master alchemist by the name of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grantham</color> living in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hermit’s Village</color>? He’s a knowledgeable weirdo... Some even say he is a fugitive who fled to Comodo to avoid pursuit... Someone like that may not agree to help us, and may even get us into trouble. We gotta be smart while negotiating with him.",
    ["Dialogue1092401"]="Well... What an unexpected visitor...\n(The old man with a hunched back licks his lips before spiting out a few indistinct words in a hoarse voice)",
    ["Dialogue1092402"]="(His cloudy eyes you up and down, studying you closely)\nHehe... I do, and I know what you want from me, but I don’t do things for free. So tell me, what do you offer me in return?",
    ["Dialogue1092403"]="But I didn’t ask you to. Or, is the successor of Odin’s Bloodline someone who forces another against their will?",
    ["Dialogue1092404"]="Grantham, we don’t have time for this. What I ask is simple. All I need is for you to analyze this Dragon Flame sample. Just tell me what you want in return.",
    ["Dialogue1092405"]="Dragon... Flame?\n(Grantham stares at you with bulging eyes, and then he reaches out and grabs you with his bony hands)\n<size=24>Hand it over...</size> <size=26>Hand it over <color=#CA2E0AFF>to me </color>right now!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1092501"]="Gahahaha! Intriguing... This is so intriguing!\n(The old man starts laughing again, his bodily movements reminding you of a dying raven)",
    ["Dialogue1092502"]="I changed my mind. I will help you... However, at the end of this, the Dragon Flame is mine.",
    ["Dialogue1092503"]="What... are you going to do with the Dragon Flame? I can’t let you use it against others...",
    ["Dialogue1092504"]="Pfff! This is the legendary undying flame of the dragons! Do you know how precious this is to an alchemist!? To use them on the commoners would be an utter waste!",
    ["Dialogue1092505"]="(He shakes the Crystal Bottle in his hand, eyes glowing)\nThe precious Dragon Flame went away with the fall of the dragons... But now, this sacred relic of the dragons has returned, and you want to know why? Heheheh...",
    ["Dialogue1092506"]="You know the answer!?",
    ["Dialogue1092507"]="If you bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tri Joint’s Shell</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nereid’s Poison Gland</color>, I will be able to confirm my hypothesis. So, do we have a deal, little girl?",
    ["Dialogue1092508"]="Fine... You’ve got a deal.",
    ["Dialogue1092601"]="Now, let’s learn the secret of the Dragon Flame... However, I am an old man. Dealing with all those alchemical ingredients takes the life out of me...\n(He intentionally drags his hoarse voice out while staring at you and pushing the materials toward you)",
    ["Dialogue1092602"]="You don’t mind helping me out a little, do you? Remember... <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut open the Poison Gland</color> to collect the liquids first, and then take the shell of the Tri Joint, evenly <color=#CA2E0AFF>coat it</color> with a thin layer of <color=#CA2E0AFF>venom</color>. When all that’s done, burn it <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the Dragon Flame</color>, and see if there is any change in the flame’s color. Let us begin.",
    ["Dialogue1092603"]="Tsk... That’s not what I told you to do. You have to start over.",
    ["Dialogue1092604"]="Be careful when collecting the venom. If you get it on your skin, you’ll have to cut the whole affected area out to save your life... Good. Next.",
    ["Dialogue1092605"]="Hmm... The Tri Joint is sensitive to the elemental changes in the air, and it would change color depending on the elemental concentration. However, it’ll just burn up when it comes in contact with the Dragon Flame, that’s why we need to coat it with a layer of inflammable material... Got that? Good. Let’s continue.",
    ["Dialogue1092606"]="Hmm... Pure Fire? The Dragon Flame sure is impressive. Wait... It’s... green?",
    ["Dialogue1092607"]="Yes... Yes! It’s Wind Element! As I expected... The power of Ymir’s Heart of the Wind is how the long-lost Dragon Flame was brought back!\nThis must be what you’re looking for.",
    ["Dialogue1092608"]="It’s none of your business, Grantham. You’ve found the answer we’re looking for, so this bottle of Dragon Flame is now yours. Now that the deal’s done, it’s time <color=#CA2E0AFF>for us to leave</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1092609"]="Heh... You are a cautious little girl, aren’t ya? Never mind... I’m not in a hurry... And I’m sure we’ll meet again.\n(Vendra drags you away from the eerie tree house as his broken words echo in the distance)",
    ["Dialogue1092610"]="Then... if you bring me the Fragment of Ymir’s Heart, I’ll teach you how to use its power... It shall grant you endless power... and glory...\n<color=#A1979FFF>I look forward to your decision... The successor of Odin’s Bloodline...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1092701"]="I’m sorry, Adventurer... I was a bit rude, wasn’t I?",
    ["Dialogue1092702"]="Come on... Shouldn’t you be more aware of your own reputation? Even a hermit-like Grantham recognizes you in a glance... And, those songs about you were mostly written by my Euphonic Symphony. It’d be a great lie if I told you I didn’t know who you are.",
    ["Dialogue1092703"]="That’s why I intentionally dragged you into this when we first met. But don’t worry, I’m not doing it to get my hands on the Fragment of Ymir’s Heart. I only wanted your help with Comodo’s situation.",
    ["Dialogue1092704"]="It’s a bit too late to say it now, but...\n(Vendra reaches a hand out to you, eyes glowing with passion)\nWill you still help me, successor of Odin’s Bloodline?",
    ["Dialogue1092705"]="Alright! We continue on, then! It’s no time to kick back and relax... Actually, there’s one other thing that concerns me regarding the whole incident.",
    ["Dialogue1092706"]="The location. Don’t you find it strange, Adventurer? The victims were all attacked within the Zenhai Marsh. The dragons have to go through both the main city of Comodo and the Papuchicha Forest to get there. Why didn’t they pick some place closer to their cave, or pick on the intruders? It makes no sense for them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick a faraway location</color>, unless...",
    ["Dialogue1092707"]="That’s right. This answer defies what we know, but it is the only logical explanation. If that’s true, then it would also be logical to believe that the dragons... may have a method unknown to us to fast-travel to the marsh without being seen.",
    ["Dialogue1092708"]="We’re on the same page, Adventurer. Do you remember where we started this investigation? There was one conspicuous dead tree...\n(Vendra turns around and points toward a clearing <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest to the marsh</color>)",
    ["Dialogue1092801"]="Look at this, Adventurer. I sense something strange...",
    ["Dialogue1092802"]="Right... The fallen leaves seem to have been arranged intentionally to cover whatever lies beneath!",
    ["Dialogue1092803"]="Right... I can feel the breeze coming up from the fallen leaves. There must be something hidden beneath!",
    ["Dialogue1092804"]="(Vendra paces around the fallen leaves and logs, mumbling to herself)\nSadly, we can’t lift such a heavy log, even with the two of us... Looks like we’ll have to blow it up.",
    ["Dialogue1092805"]="Leave that to me, Adventurer! The native here once taught me how to make simple explosives enough to take care of the fallen logs, but I’ll need you to gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>yellow powder</color> on the surface of <color=#CA2E0AFF>sulphur ores</color>, as well as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Landfrost</color> used by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nereids</color> to build nests.",
    ["Dialogue1092901"]="Crush both materials separately, mix them, wrap it in dried bark and tie it. Lastly, put in the fuse! That’s it!",
    ["Dialogue1092902"]="Now, put it next to the log and <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1093001"]="Is that... a cave?\n(Vendra pokes her head out and looks around cautiously, but she shakes her head in disappointment)\nCan’t see anything... It’s too deep to see what’s down there.",
    ["Dialogue1093002"]="Looks like it. We can get a rope and rappel down from here, but this looks treacherous. Do you need some time to prepare?",
    ["Dialogue1093003"]="Alright. Let’s do it!",
    ["Dialogue1093004"]="No worries. It’s better to be prepared, especially for exploring a mysterious cave like this. Take your time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1093101"]="It has to be... It's part of the dragons' cave on the western side of Comodo!",
    ["Dialogue1093102"]="Do you remember that I told you how I stumbled into a dragons' cave when I was small and saw a dragonling? This is incredible... It's just like how I remember it! It almost feels like time froze here...",
    ["Dialogue1093103"]="(Vendra longingly reaches out her hand to feel the cave walls until her expression abruptly changes)\nNo. This is not a natural cave.",
    ["Dialogue1093104"]="According to the pact, unauthorized personnel are not permitted to enter the cave that belongs to the dragons. But even explorers or visitors who manage to sneak in usually aren’t capable of digging such a big tunnel, unless...",
    ["Dialogue1093105"]="That’s right. Only the dragons that lived here could dig out such a tunnel that leads outside without anyone’s knowledge. They wouldn’t go to such length just to hunt for food in secret!",
    ["Dialogue1093106"]="There must be more <color=#CA2E0AFF>clues</color> to that inside this cave, and we must find them. Adventurer, let’s <color=#CA2E0AFF>search around</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1093201"]="T-This is not possible... These dragon eggs... should long be frozen!",
    ["Dialogue1093202"]="It's how the dragons procreate. Their eggs must be <color=#CA2E0AFF>kept warm by the Dragon Flame to hatch</color>. Otherwise, the eggs will freeze and die, becoming unable to incubate new dragonlings. This is why we always regarded Dragon Flame as the symbol that decides the dragons' fate.",
    ["Dialogue1093203"]="That’s right. Millennia ago, ever since the dragons were driven into these ice caves, the Dragon Flame waned and weakened to the point of almost being unable to incubate new eggs... But look at these eggs right here! They are going to hatch any second!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Could Grantham be right? It’s because of the legendary...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1093204"]="You’re right... We can’t jump to a conclusion just yet. We need to find more evidence. Come, Adventurer, lets <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue to investigate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1093301"]="(You and Vendra shuddenly shield your eyes from the sudden heat wave that fogs up your vision)\nThis fiery power must also be the work of the Dragon Flame.",
    ["Dialogue1093302"]="I don’t know... But the records do say that in the war millennia ago, the dragons controlled the monsters on the island and used them to fight the humans. The controlled monsters possess great power without an ounce of self-consciousness, fighting for the dragons until death...",
    ["Dialogue1093303"]="(Vendra solemnly turns to the monsters in formation)\nLook at them. Their eyes are hollow, unreative even to our presence. Could it really be...",
    ["Dialogue1093304"]="Wait! Look! There’s something on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ground</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1093401"]="Incredible... Such power cannot come from a common monster!",
    ["Dialogue1093402"]="Yes, you’re right... This is a marching roadmap! The dragons took control of these monsters and dug out tunnels to the surface in secret, so they can send the monsters through to take us all out... Their goal... is to take over the island...",
    ["Dialogue1093403"]="(Vendra clenches the map hard and grits her teeth)\nThis is enough evidence to convince Alexia to wake up from her foolish dream of peace between us and the dragons. Let’s <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to the surface</color> and report our findings to the leader!",
    ["Dialogue1093404"]="Please hurry, Adventurer! We don’t know when they are going to invade, and we need every minute to prepare our forces!",
    ["Dialogue1093405"]="Alright! This time... I will make Alexia see what the dragons are planning!",
    ["Dialogue1093501"]="It’s... a map of Comodo? What do the markings on the map mean?",
    ["Dialogue1093502"]="Fragment of Ymir’s Heart? A-Are you sure? This is too big to be wrong!",
    ["Dialogue1093503"]="Of course, Alexia! I wouldn’t be here if I weren’t sure!",
    ["Dialogue1093504"]="(You can feel the growing tension spreading through the room as Alexia’s expression gradually grows serious)\nIf you are right, then the dragons are trying to... reclaim the ultimate power they once had millennia ago...",
    ["Dialogue1093505"]="That’s right, Alexia. It’s evident by the existence of the secret tunnels that connect to the outside world and the monster legions that the dragons have been planning this for a long time. If we cannot fight them off this time, Comodo would fall into their hands. We have to hurry up and⁠—",
    ["Dialogue1093506"]="—No, Vendra. In that case, we really can’t rush into a war with them.",
    ["Dialogue1093507"]="(Vendra stares at Alexia, dumbfounded and unable to comprehend what she just heard)\nW-What did you just say?",
    ["Dialogue1093508"]="I said, \"We really can’t rush into a war with the them.\" They are already a race superior to humans, and now not only are they in possession of a Fragment of Ymir’s Heart, they also have a large monster legion. If we were to start a war with them, we would just be courting death.",
    ["Dialogue1093509"]="Then... what do you propose?",
    ["Dialogue1093510"]="Talks, of course! Talk them down! There is no way the peace that lasted for millennia shall be broken in my hands! I have already dispatched an envoy to the cave to negotiate with them. I mean, we have the example of Lady Margaret! All I need to do, as her descendant, is to follow the ancient teachings and make sure they are passed down!",
    ["Dialogue1093511"]="Ah! I’ve had another great idea! Don’t dragons love gold? Maybe we can add another clause? As long as they are willing to continue living in the cave... No, wait, we can in fact allow them to leave the cave by including Papuchicha Forest as part of their living area. Additionally, we’ll also give them gold coins equivalent to three years of Comodo’s tax revenue...",
    ["Dialogue1093512"]="<size=26>You’re out of your mind!</size>\n(Vendra raises her hand in anger to slap Alexia, but you stop her in time)",
    ["Dialogue1093513"]="Calm down? How do you expect me to calm down?! You heard her! More tributes and land! Is that something a leader should say? Alexia, you are a disappointment!",
    ["Dialogue1093514"]="If you’ve forgotten how to lead your people, then—",
    ["Dialogue1093515"]="<size=26>My Lady! Lady Alexia! There’s trouble!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1093601"]="(A guard of Nerius family rushes in, interrupting your conversation)\nLady Alexia... We just received word that... the dragons have simultaneously attacked <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kokomo Beach</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1093602"]="There’s no need for panic! I thought I sent you to negotiate! So what have you negotiated?",
    ["Dialogue1093603"]="W-We entered the cave... but before we met the dragon’s leader, they...\n(The young guard’s face turns pale, his expression alone revealing all)",
    ["Dialogue1093604"]="The monsters guarding the dragons' cave attacked you, didn't they?\n(Vendra's bright tone becomes hoarse under her restrain as she tries to regain her composure and takes over the conversation)\nWake up, Alexia!",
    ["Dialogue1093605"]="Ultimately, peaceful negotiation is just wishful thinking on your part. But is this really... really your decision as the leader of Comodo? As Alexia Nerius? Or, are you just drunk on the glory of that treaty and refuse to face reality?",
    ["Dialogue1093606"]="I...",
    ["Dialogue1093607"]="It’s not too late. We can summon our soldiers and send out an SOS to the nearby pirates and Eden Group. We should be able to hold them back with the help of the Euphonic Symphony while we send someone to Prontera to ask for reinforcements. I believe...",
    ["Dialogue1093608"]="W-Wait a moment, Lady Vendra. Pardon me, but did you and this Adventurer enter the dragons' cave?\n(The guard looks you over, and you sense the blame in his eyes)",
    ["Dialogue1093609"]="Earlier, when I lead my team into the cave, I saw a pair, resembling you two, fighting monsters in the cave... Not long after, the monster legions attacked us...",
    ["Dialogue1093610"]="It’s... you?\nVendra... You gave me your word that you wouldn’t go into the cave... <size=24>Why...</size> <size=26>Why did you betray me!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1093611"]="It’s you... It’s all your fault! You angered the dragons and brought war upon us! Do you know how much we sacrificed for the prosperity of Comodo? My grandmother, my mother, and I... and my daughters! We were all taught to follow the teachings of Lady Margaret from birth, and we all lived our lives to uphold them! And what did you do!?",
    ["Dialogue1093612"]="Maintain the pact... keep the peace... These are the rules of the Nerius family passed down from generation to generation! I... I already tried so hard to appease the monsters... They were about to accept my terms... and you had to mess it all up for me!",
    ["Dialogue1093613"]="You... You are really out of your mind!",
    ["Dialogue1093614"]="Out of my mind...? Ha... Right... Now you remind me. I have been far too kind, understanding, and reasonable. That’s why you forgot who the ruler of Comodo is!",
    ["Dialogue1093615"]="From this moment on, you and your Euphonic Symphony are not allowed to interfere in the affairs of Comodo! Otherwise, I’ll exile all of you!",
    ["Dialogue1093701"]="My Lady! The princess... Princess Cecilia left for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color> with her bodyguards! We, we couldn’t stop them...",
    ["Dialogue1093702"]="<size=26>The marsh!?</size>\nThat’s a battlefield! What is she going there for!?",
    ["Dialogue1093703"]="(Vendra snorts, her voice filled with sarcasm)\nHah. Is that so difficult to see, My Lady? She went to do what you don’t dare to do.",
    ["Dialogue1093704"]="All these years, you’ve prided yourself on upholding the honor of the Nerius family. But now, as a foe emerges right before us, you’re doing nothing when even Cecilia is willing to step up. I think... you are no longer suited to lead. It’s better for you to pass the reigns on to your daughter!\n(With that, Vendra turns and leaves in anger)",
    ["Dialogue1093801"]="If we can’t hold the lines this time, everything we enjoy in Comodo will be gone. I can’t back down in a time like this. Not only me... I believe all members of the Euphonic Symphony will put down their lives to defend Comodo.",
    ["Dialogue1093802"]="Vendra, we can't disobey Nerius' orders. You know that. This is—",
    ["Dialogue1093803"]="<size=26>We don’t live in the past anymore, Uncle Callahan!</size>\nYou’re just like her. To you, rules and traditions are everything. But times are changing. We must adapt or get left behind.",
    ["Dialogue1093804"]="You...! Humph...\n(You greet Vendra and give her a smile as the calm bard leader releases a long sigh, waving his hand and refusing to say more)",
    ["Dialogue1093805"]="Very much appreciated, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1093806"]="However, I’m more concerned about Cecilia right now. She’s young, and the battlefield is too dangerous a place for her... We should split up. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>support Cecilia at Zenhai Marsh</color>, and I can lead the Euphonic Symphony to Papuchicha Forest and fight the dragons there.",
    ["Dialogue1093901"]="Adventurer, if you’re here to speak to me on behalf of Mother, you can save it!\n(Cecilia raises her sword and points it at the guardsmen fighting the monsters not far away)",
    ["Dialogue1093902"]="Look at those warriors, fighting to protect their home with their lives! I am a Nerius! It’s my responsibility to be here! But... if you are here to help, I beg you, please help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> here! Monsters are pouring out of that cave up ahead. Many residents already fell prey to them!",
    ["Dialogue1093903"]="Let’s fight side by side!",
    ["Dialogue1093904"]="Enough! I’m not going. If you won’t help, then I have to ask you to leave!",
    ["Dialogue1094001"]="Thank you, Adventurer. If it weren’t for you, my guardsmen and I would’ve never been able to hold our grounds. Unfortunately, despite our efforts, many are injured by the Dragon Flame in the battle.",
    ["Dialogue1094002"]="Is that so? You once treated the injured islanders with Vendra? That’s good news!\nMy bodyguard Kurulus has acquired Glacial Ice from the cave and refined them into Ice Gels. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>use</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Gels</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>treat the wounded</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1094101"]="Thank you, Adventurer. Now their wounds have been treated, and the enemy’s primary force is in retreat. Zenhai Marsh is safe for the moment and it can serve as a stronghold.",
    ["Dialogue1094102"]="Yes. I know. I just received word that Euphonic Symphony is under fierce attack by the dragons in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color>. I’m worried about them.\n(Cecilia looks around the camp, concerned and hesitant.)",
    ["Dialogue1094103"]="That would be for the best! Please take the rest of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Gels</color>. They will definitely come in handy!",
    ["Dialogue1094201"]="Uhm... I-It’s you... You’re back... Ahhh...",
    ["Dialogue1094202"]="Don’t move, Princess Cecilia. You’ll tear your wounds!",
    ["Dialogue1094203"]="It’s nothing... compared to the soldiers who have died...\n(Cecilia bites down on her lips and then looks up at you)",
    ["Dialogue1094204"]="Adventurer, if I can ask you for another favor... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take</color> Kurulus and this <color=#CA2E0AFF>cape</color> with the emblem of the Nerius family and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to my mother</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1094205"]="Since I defied Mother’s orders, I’ve been prepared to renounce the name of Nerius. From now on, I will remain here with the warriors to fight against the dragon invasion. I will give anything to protect this island.\n(You see your own reflection in her crystal eyes, filled with unwavering determination)",
    ["Dialogue1094301"]="It’s... Cecilia’s cape? W-What happened to my daughter!?",
    ["Dialogue1094302"]="My Lady, don’t be alarmed. Princess Cecilia is only slightly injured. Her life is not in danger. I am here on her behalf to convey her will...\n(The young guard lifts up the cape with both hands and kneels before Alexia)",
    ["Dialogue1094303"]="From today on, Princess Cecilia voluntarily renounces the name of Nerius. She will join the commoners and the warriors to fight against the invading dragons, and she will not rest till she sees it done.",
    ["Dialogue1094304"]="<size=26>Ri-Ridiculous! Are all of you planning on betraying the Nerius family!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1094305"]="My Lady, my loyalty is forever with the Nerius family. I will give my life for the Princess, but I cannot go against her will.\n(He lifts up his head and raises the cape even higher, and at this moment you notice a <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> on the cape)\nPlease, before you make up your mind, try to understand her...",
    ["Dialogue1094306"]="...\n(You reluctantly take the letter while Alexia turns away, unwilling to accept what is happening)",
    ["Dialogue1094401"]="Your... will?\n(Alexia stares blankly at the letter in your hand, the scarlet fingerprint scorching brightly in her eyes)",
    ["Dialogue1094402"]="Yes... All members of the guards decide to follow the Princess unanimously to defend Comodo. This letter represents our will and determination.",
    ["Dialogue1094403"]="Was I... wrong? I only tried to... follow the rules to keep the peace... That’s what my mother taught me, and what her mother taught her... Why am I to blame when they were not!?",
    ["Dialogue1094404"]="My Lady, it may not be my place to say this, but the leader of Comodo <color=#CA2E0AFF>is you</color>. It is not your mother or your grandmother, and certainly not Lady Margaret, who has been dead for a thousand years now. The Nerius family, to which we have pledged our loyalty, is the Nerius family that you lead. You are the only one who can decide the future of Comodo.",
    ["Dialogue1094405"]=" ...\n(Alexia’s grip suddenly tightens and from the crumpling noise of the letter in her hand, you realize that something deep-rooted in her just snapped)",
    ["Dialogue1094406"]="Will you... still be willing to help me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1094407"]="Thank you, Adventurer. But... It’s shameful to say, but everyone here at Comodo has gotten used to the peace. It’s only a matter of time before the dragons overrun our defenses...",
    ["Dialogue1094408"]="My Lady, please do not forget that even though we are not aggressive by any means, we also don’t bow down to aggression. Our guards and the Euphonic Symphony, led by Vendra, are already fighting on the frontlines. If you are willing to extend an olive branch to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pirates near Kokomo Beach</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group at Saint Darmain’s east</color> with a promise of rewards, maybe they would be willing to help.",
    ["Dialogue1094409"]="I see...",
    ["Dialogue1094410"]="Adventurer, please accompany me. We’ll go at once to <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek help from both the pirates and Eden Group</color>. As for Kurulus, you head back to Cecilia and relay my orders: The Nerius family has declared war on the dragons, effective immediately. Go forth without hesitation! Drive those monsters who invaded our homes back into their filthy nest!",
    ["Dialogue1094411"]="Yes, My Lady!",
    ["Dialogue1094501"]="Stay away! This is the territory of the Gangash Pirates! Stay away, if you value your lives!",
    ["Dialogue1094502"]="The leader? Seriously!?\n(The young pirate couldn't hide his surprise and looks you over)\n<color=#A1979FFF>But... how did the boss know the leader is coming...?</color>",
    ["Dialogue1094503"]="Never mind...! You, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me</color>. Drake wants to see you.",
    ["Dialogue1094601"]="Heh... Long time no see, leader of Comodo. To what do I owe the honor today?",
    ["Dialogue1094602"]="Captain Drake... I’m here today to seek your help.",
    ["Dialogue1094603"]="Help? I don’t believe we are allies, let alone friends. If my memory serves, the last time we met, you even confiscated a shipment that we went great lengths to acquire... I have yet to have my payback.",
    ["Dialogue1094604"]="If my memory serves, that shipment was a gift from the Rune Kingdom to Arunafeltz. This shipment pales in in comparison to the alliance between the two countries. Would you rather want to see this \"outfit\" you’ve been running for years get turned inside out? Captain, you owe me for doing you a big favor.",
    ["Dialogue1094605"]="(Alexia pauses at just the right time, looking around at the pirates on the deck and only continuing when Drake shows no reaction on his face)\nIndeed, I have a favor to ask, but I did not come empty-handed. If you are willing to help me, I will let your pirate crew join the Royal Fleet once the deed is done. You and your crew will join the ranks and reap the benefits of the army; you can leave the days of hardship behind.",
    ["Dialogue1094606"]="T-The Royal Fleet!?",
    ["Dialogue1094607"]="Is this a joke!?",
    ["Dialogue1094608"]="If it sounds too good to be true...",
    ["Dialogue1094609"]="<size=24>Enough!</size> <size=26>Shut it!</size>\n(Drake roars and shuts all the pirates up before grunting with satisfaction and looking back at Alexia)",
    ["Dialogue1094610"]="We’ll have to see the goods first. If you really are offering us such a gracious gift, then this must be no simple \"help\" that you’re asking for in return.",
    ["Dialogue1094611"]="You’re right. To tell you the truth, the dragons have begun their invasion of Comodo, leading legions of monsters to attack the City of Comodo from all sides. The island is engulfed in war. We’re trying our best to mount defenses, but even fending off the first wave of attack took everything we’ve got. If Comodo were to fall into the hands of the dragons... I'm sure you know you won't stay unaffected for too long.",
    ["Dialogue1094612"]="You're proposing that... we join forces to defend Comodo against the dragons?",
    ["Dialogue1094613"]="It's not resistance. It's war. Comodo is home... family... not to be defiled! I will also ask the Eden Group and all Adventurers for help. Anyone who is willing to join the battle against the dragons will be handsomely rewarded once the fight is over!",
    ["Dialogue1094614"]="(A momentary silence after Alexia's spirited speech is soon followed by the savage pirate captain's laughter)\nHa... Interesting. I've always heard that the Nerius family of today is a mere shadow of its former self, having lost the great legacy left behind by Lady Margaret... But from the looks of you, that's not quite true.",
    ["Dialogue1094615"]="I accept your terms, leader of Comodo. From now on, my men are yours.",
    ["Dialogue1094616"]="No way, boss! What if she's using us as cannon fodder...",
    ["Dialogue1094617"]="Shut it, Godfrey. Don't make me repeat my words.\n(Drake squints threateningly at the pirate who dares to oppose him)",
    ["Dialogue1094618"]="I believe all of you would have heard of this old saying of the sea: \"Only through the pursuit of waves can one overcome the storm; the weak will always be buried in the murky depths.\"\nAnd on my Queen's Revenge... there are no weaklings.",
    ["Dialogue1094619"]="Then... Please make all necessary preparations. I shall be waiting for you to join us at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1094620"]="In exchange for your assistance in this urgent matter, I plan to make you part of the Royal Navy of Comodo, with all rights, privileges, and salary for all your crew. What say you?",
    ["Dialogue1094701"]="T-The dragons have begun their attack!?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Dammit... We thought they were still formulating their attack, but...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1094702"]="Instructor Salisbury, this is an emergency; I don't have any extra troops I can send to map the land. You're the only one I can turn to for help. I know the Eden Group often enters the dragons' cave for research. I'm sure you know it like the back of your hand. If the Eden Group is willing to guide the army, I promise you that we will do all we can to ensure the safety of your members.",
    ["Dialogue1094703"]="I'm willing to grant you all of the excavation permits in Comodo in return. Additionally, if the Eden Group ever needs any help in the future, the Nerius family will provide it without hesitation.",
    ["Dialogue1094704"]="Hmm... My Lady, please raise your head. Even if you didn't invite me today, the Eden Group would have come forward to offer our service.",
    ["Dialogue1094705"]="Comodo might not be our homeland, but no one else knows its past better than us. We tirelessly excavate the earth for the history buried deep within, in the hopes of bringing it to light... but once war breaks out, our hard work will all go down the drain. As an archaeologist, I'm glad that we have the chance to help stop the war.",
    ["Dialogue1094706"]="Furthermore... The rare chance of being witnesses to such a historical event may mean that even we could be added to its rich history!\n(Salisbury rubs his mustache and starts laughing gleefully)",
    ["Dialogue1094707"]="Thank you... Then, please make your preparations. We'll meet up at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color> later.",
    ["Dialogue1094801"]="Now that we've managed to get the pirates and Eden Group on our side, could you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the Hermit's Village</color> to enlist their help? I know that you and Vendra worked with them before... Maybe they'd be willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help us with the dragons</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1094802"]="I... I must apologize to Vendra personally. The three sisters of the Trista family have been my aides for many years, and Vendra has been close to me since childhood. I should have known that her love for this island is incomparable to that of any other, yet I was blinded by my stubbornness and said all those hurtful things...",
    ["Dialogue1094803"]="(Alexia takes a deep breath, the vulnerability in her eyes fading away)\nHopefully, it's not too late. I can still mend what is broken... Will you please help me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1094901"]="Heheheh... I told you we'd meet again, Adventurer. Have you decided to... accept my offer?\nI knew you would. Come. Hand it over!",
    ["Dialogue1094902"]="Fight the dragons...? Oh, you just had to be so nosy... Heed my advice, you should just let them fight it out and reap the fruits when all is over. Why involve yourself?",
    ["Dialogue1094903"]="Tsk... This is why I hate all those educated and moral fools like you. Nothing is more important to me than my alchemy!",
    ["Dialogue1094904"]="Oh... never mind, since I may still need you...\n(He glances at you and then shakes his head, feeling that you're beyond redemption)\nI still have another Invisibility Potion. You want it?",
    ["Dialogue1094905"]="You don't have anything I want... Just do me an errand. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Put on </color>my <color=#CA2E0AFF>cape</color> and run a few laps around the forest. Take out any assassins that bear ill-will of me so they can't disturb my research. That's all.",
    ["Dialogue1094906"]="Do that, and the Invisibility Potion is yours.",
    ["Dialogue1095001"]="Hmm... Now, I should have some peace and quiet... for a while.",
    ["Dialogue1095002"]="Don't worry... A deal's a deal. Here.\n(After searching for a bit, Grantham takes out a small palm-sized vial from his saddle and hands it to you)",
    ["Dialogue1095003"]="Hey, watch your tone! The cost of that potion is more than your expenses for an entire year! If it weren't for...\n(He glances at you with obvious disdain)\nHumph... At least, I don't want to see you die just yet.",
    ["Dialogue1095004"]="But, remember this. This Invisibility Potion is <color=#CA2E0AFF>only enough for one person</color> for <color=#CA2E0AFF>a limited duration</color>. So, use it well.\n<color=#A1979FFF>Everything would be for naught if you got killed without getting your hands on a Fragment of Ymir's Heart...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1095101"]="<color=#A1979FFF>15... 16... 17... Dammit... 18 is my lucky number...</color>\nHuh... A customer? Or prey...?",
    ["Dialogue1095102"]="Fight against the dragons? Protect our home? Uh-huh... It sounds oh-so-noble. But, what does it have to do with me?",
    ["Dialogue1095103"]="Friends, home, loyalty, responsibility... All those things that you value are worthless to me. So why should I help you?",
    ["Dialogue1095104"]="Prey, of course! Only the hunt excites me! Hey! I've got an idea!\n(He gives himself applause, smiling radiantly)\nHow about... You be my prey?",
    ["Dialogue1095105"]="You want to get the dragons, don't ya? Three times... Just escape from me three times, and I'll tell you how to make an ice trap for the dragons!\n(The young man seems to be negotiating with you, but you notice that his arrow is already pointing directly at your eye)",
    ["Dialogue1095106"]="You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>start running now</color>, my dear.",
    ["Dialogue1095201"]="Ha... Hahahahah!\nHow wonderful, Adventurer! You are the perfect prey! I'm a bit unwilling to... let you go now.",
    ["Dialogue1095202"]="Fine, fine... Put down the weapon, my dear. I was just joking.\n(Raphael puts up both hands, surrendering himself to you)",
    ["Dialogue1095203"]="Right, right... It's not hard to make an Ice Trap at all. You will first need to fully cover a fishhook made from the jaw bone of an Alligator with some Numbing Slime of a Tri Joint. Next, insert a Permafrost Crystal. Once the trap is triggered, the hook will pierce the body of the prey and the Numbing Slime will work quickly, preventing the prey from escaping the blast radius of the Permafrost Crystal.",
    ["Dialogue1095204"]="But... I have to remind you of this. The effective duration of the trap depends on the prey. A powerful monster like an Ancient Dragon? Well, you better cross your fingers...",
    ["Dialogue1095301"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Uhm... Could it really work? That darn old man better not be lying to me!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1095302"]="Fight the dragons...? No way! I don't have the time, I... <size=24>W-Wait a second!</size> <size=26>Fight the DRAGONS!?</size>\nHahahaha! This is a great chance!",
    ["Dialogue1095303"]="Ahem... I mean, sure, of course I'll help!\nListen, Adventurer. I just happen to have a high-grade fire-proof manteau that can resist the powerful Dragon Flame. All it needs is an enchantment! But... You know, the good stuff takes hard-to-get materials to make...",
    ["Dialogue1095304"]="(Libec takes out a piece of paper and reads out the recipe, and somehow, the handwriting on it seems familiar to you...)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>White Mist Moss</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poison Gland of Nereid</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Thorny Skin of Alligator</color>... That's all! If you're able to help me craft this manteau, I'll lend it to you!",
    ["Dialogue1095401"]="Good, good! The world's greatest fire-proof manteau is about to be born!\n(Libec takes the materials you've collected, crushed them with mortar and pestle, and then... spread them all on top of the manteau.)",
    ["Dialogue1095402"]="That's why you're gonna test it out—I mean, you're gonna be the <color=#CA2E0AFF>first one</color> in the world to put it to the test!\n(With a smile, he puts the manteau on you, and you're immediately surrounded by an indescribable smell.)",
    ["Dialogue1095403"]="Well, there are always risks when trying something, but I believe your great strength is enough to overcome any obstacle! Isn't that right?",
    ["Dialogue1095501"]="How did it go, Adventurer? While you were in the Hermit's Village, Nerius's troops and the Euphonic Symphony rallied together. The Eden Group and pirates are also coming to meet us... I hope you have good news for us.",
    ["Dialogue1095502"]="(You tell her about everything that happened in the Hermit's Village, and Alexia's frown gradually eases)\nGreat! What you've acquired will provide us with new strategies against the dragons! Instructor Salisbury, let's start the mission briefing!",
    ["Dialogue1095503"]="Now, this is the situation. According to the intel obtained by the Eden Group, the current leader of the dragons is a monster who is half-human and half-dragon. It is said that a powerful <color=#CA2E0AFF>green</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>emerald fragment</color> has been inlaid on his chest. Not only does it greatly increases the power of the Dragon Flame, it also reduces the incubation time of dragon eggs.",
    ["Dialogue1095504"]="An emerald... Could it be... a Fragment of Ymir's Heart?\n(Vendra purses her lips and gives you a look)",
    ["Dialogue1095505"]="Exactly. We, the Eden Group, also believe it could very well be a Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart. It must be how the Mutant Dragonoid was able to restore the once glorious power to the weakened dragons... This will be a tough battle.",
    ["Dialogue1095506"]="In other words, this is also our opportunity. The dragons waned for a thousand years, but they managed to rebuild through the power of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. So, if we're able to defeat this Mutant Dragonoid and obtain the fragment, they will inevitably fall.",
    ["Dialogue1095507"]="Easier said than done. The Mutant Dragonoid is located in the Dragon Hatchery at the heart of their territory, protected by legions of monsters and dragons. All key passages inside the dragons' cave are guarded by four Ancient Dragons that will reinforce each other's position at a holler... If we don't <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat them all simultaneously</color> within <color=#CA2E0AFF>a short time</color>, we'll be surrounded...",
    ["Dialogue1095508"]="Is there a way to... prevent them from supporting each other?",
    ["Dialogue1095509"]="Hmm... Adventurer, I believe you learned how to make Ice Traps from Raphael the Ranger, yes?",
    ["Dialogue1095510"]="If it works on the dragons... then I might have a way to do it.",
    ["Dialogue1095511"]="Vendra, are you suggesting that we <color=#CA2E0AFF>isolate the dragon guards with the traps</color> and take them down separately? But how will we </color>infiltrate the cave<color=#CA2E0AFF> and lay down the traps without being discovered?",
    ["Dialogue1095512"]="Alexia, do you remember we brought back a map from the dragons' cave the last time? The map shows the routes the dragons take and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>hidden paths</color> they use to access their cave. We entered one of them. It was inside a cave north to the Zenhai Marsh...",
    ["Dialogue1095513"]="(Seeing your face light up with understanding, Vendra blinks at you)\nI see you know what I have in mind, Adventurer. We'll be also able to sneak into the dragons' cave by taking these three hidden paths. However, just to be safe, we'll send out some scouts to do some recon.",
    ["Dialogue1095514"]="...\n(Alexia rests her chin on the palm of her hand, thinking about the practicality of this plan and gently patting Vendra on the head shortly after)\nYou've really impressed me, Vendra.",
    ["Dialogue1095515"]="We'll do as you say. I'll send men to the marked entrances on the map immediately, while the rest remain at camp and reorganize. Also, to successfully carry out this plan, we'll need to prepare a signal that allows us to communicate.",
    ["Dialogue1095516"]="I got you covered, Alexia. The Adventurer and I will go gather the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sulfur Powder</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Landfrost</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wood</color> necessary to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Firework Launchers</color> to signal each other!",
    ["Dialogue1095601"]="Adventurer, Alexia's scouts have yet to return. We can take this opportunity to collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Permafrost Crystals</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Numbing Slime</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fishhooks</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft Ice Traps</color>! However, to ensure they work effectively on Ancient Dragons, I suggest we <color=#CA2E0AFF>double</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dosage</color>... What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue1095701"]="Good timing, Adventurer. Alexia's scouts have returned. They have confirmed that all three hidden paths at Zenhai Marsh, Papuchicha Forest, and Kokomo Beach are accessible. With the three and the dragons' cave entrance at the west side of the City of Comodo, we can split up our forces and infiltrate all four ways to take down the four Ancient Dragons!",
    ["Dialogue1095702"]="Then... I'll lead my guards to Zenhai Marsh. I'll leave Kokomo Beach to Captain Drake as it already is in his territory. As for Vendra, you've been fighting in Papuchicha Forest with the Euphonic Symphony for a while, so I'll leave this place to you. As for the last team...\n(Looking at the current teams, Alexia frowns with a hesitating look)",
    ["Dialogue1095703"]="You... alone!? No way. It's too dangerous!",
    ["Dialogue1095704"]="Wait... Vendra. It is a sound strategy... and probably the best choice right now.",
    ["Dialogue1095705"]="For all these years, people have been accessing the dragons' cave via the entrance at the west side of Comodo, so it will be heavily guarded by the dragons. Hence, a large team is a lot more likely to be discovered... The Adventurer is an extraordinary solo combatant, so sending the Adventurer in alone yields the best chance for the mission to succeed.",
    ["Dialogue1095706"]="(Alexia turns to you with an apologetic look on her face.)\nBut this is also the most risky path to take. I have no right to order you to sacrifice your life for Comodo...",
    ["Dialogue1095707"]="I admire your courage, Adventurer. As the leader of the Nerius family, I promise you, once this war is over, I will hand the Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart to the successor of Odin's Bloodline. If anyone dares lay their hands on it, they would be making an enemy out of the entire Nerius family.",
    ["Dialogue1095708"]="Now that's that, I'll personally show the Adventurer the way. Others from the Eden Group will go with the other teams and serve as guides. Once we all reach our infiltration point, we'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>signal with fireworks</color> and begin the mission. If we're successful in <color=#CA2E0AFF>trapping and defeating the Ancient Dragons</color>, we'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up at the Ancient Dragon Bridge in the cave</color>. Anything else, My Lady?",
    ["Dialogue1095709"]="Just one more thing. Everyone, please also <color=#CA2E0AFF>try</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take out</color> all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon eggs</color> you encounter along the way.",
    ["Dialogue1095710"]="W-Why...? That feels like an overkill since they don't pose any threat to us before they hatch.",
    ["Dialogue1095711"]="But, under the effect of Ymir's Heart, they will hatch rapidly into dragonlings. Even if they don't, I won't take the risk that there may be yet another Mutant Dragonoid with the same ambition years later... I hope you can understand, Instructor Salisbury.",
    ["Dialogue1095712"]="(Salisbury remains silent, but in the end, he shakes his head and conforms)\nI see... We'll do as you say, My Lady.",
    ["Dialogue1095801"]="Fireworks! There's no better method of signaling in Comodo than this!\n(Salisbury rubs his mustache and gives a bold smile again)",
    ["Dialogue1095802"]="Of course I'm afraid. Nobody welcomes war. After all, death follows it like a shadow. But sometimes, war doesn't only signify sacrifice. It also signifies change.",
    ["Dialogue1095803"]="It's like... you get sick, but it's nothing serious, nothing beyond occasional discomforts. But if you don't take care of it and allow for it to spread, it will slowly get serious and invade other organs... leading to your eventual death. Such corrosion happens to both men and society at large.",
    ["Dialogue1095804"]="(He taps on the Firework Launcher by his feet, using it as a metaphor)\nSo now... I am glad that the leader has shown her courage and taken out the scalpel.",
    ["Dialogue1095805"]="Alright... Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>light the fireworks</color>, Adventurer! Comodo... It's time for your rebirth.",
    ["Dialogue1095901"]="It only gets harder from now on until we reach the Ancient Dragon, Adventurer. This cave is rather old, and there are countless cracks beneath the surface of the ice. It's easy to fall into the abyss should you lose focus. Furthermore, there are numerous monsters and dragons patrolling the area. I will be leading the way. Follow closely.",
    ["Dialogue1095902"]="Right... The leader did ask us to destroy the dragon eggs we encounter to cut off their reinforcement...\n(He glances at the dragon eggs not far away, feeling hesitant)\nBut regular weapons can't damage the dragon eggs...",
    ["Dialogue1095903"]="Sigh... If you've decided to destroy these dragon eggs, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corrosive Acid</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Megalith</color>. It's the only way to melt the tough shells.",
    ["Dialogue1096001"]="We're halfway there, but there are also new obstacles. Not far up ahead, there's a small nest with many dragon eggs guarded by a large number of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gargoyles</color>. The Gargoyles are very nimble. I think we should go <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Piranha flesh</color> to use as bait. Once they are gathered at one location, we'll capture them in one fell swoop.",
    ["Dialogue1096101"]="We're almost there, Adventurer. We'll find the Ancient Dragon soon.",
    ["Dialogue1096102"]="I know, you have to take care of those eggs along the way... I... I'll wait for you ahead. I really can't take this...\n(He sighs a little and turns around. It may be the last show of pride for him as an archaeologist)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Maybe the history written by the victors is... always this cruel...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1096201"]="Hush... Did you see that dragon? The one that just flew up the slope? From my observations, it patrols along a set route and it will always pass through this slope. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>set an Ice Trap on the slope</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cover it up with the ice nearby</color>. Once the trap is sprung, it's your turn to take action.",
    ["Dialogue1096301"]="Phew... You really are the successor of Odin's Bloodline. I didn't think such a difficult task could be accomplished by you alone!",
    ["Dialogue1096302"]="You give me too much credit. But it's not the time to relax just yet. The final battle is still up ahead. Let's keep going <color=#CA2E0AFF>North</color> to reach our <color=#CA2E0AFF>rendezvous point</color>. I hope everybody's... safe.",
    ["Dialogue1096401"]="L-Looks like you also accomplished the mission, Adventurer. Now, we can finally⁠—cough, cough!",
    ["Dialogue1096402"]="(Salisbury checks Alexia's wounds solemnly and then shakes his head)\nStop pushing yourself so hard, My Lady. A burn caused by the Dragon Flame must be treated as soon as possible. Otherwise there will be serious consequences. The same goes for the warriors.",
    ["Dialogue1096403"]="Also, we have to pass through the Dragon Bridge ahead to reach the Dragon Hatchery, which is guarded by the most powerful monsters on Comodo... Judging by our status right now, we will likely be ripped to shreds before we even see the Mutant Dragonoid. My Lady, it is my judgment that we should retreat for now and come up with another plan.",
    ["Dialogue1096404"]="But... We're no match for their strength and numbers. We're only able to make it this far because we caught them by surprise... If we retreat now, we won't get another chance at this.",
    ["Dialogue1096405"]="(She looks up and struggles to stand up)\nWe... We gave our all to get here... We have to try to go all the way...",
    ["Dialogue1096406"]="You... You mean... You alone?",
    ["Dialogue1096407"]="If I'm right, you still have a bottle of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Invisibility Potion</color> with you, right? If you can use it to sneak past the guards and get to the Mutant Dragonoid... You may still have a chance.",
    ["Dialogue1096408"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Your duty... Is it? It's supposed to be... my duty too...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1096409"]="Adventurer, we haven't known each other for long, but your bravery has made a lasting impression on me... I feel ashamed that I had to burden you with such great risks and responsibilities, considering that you aren't even from Comodo...",
    ["Dialogue1096410"]="I may be in no position to ask this of you... but... Please! Please save Comodo!\n(The prideful leader lowers her head and bows before you, the millennia-old ice in the cave behind her glistening under the light of hope)",
    ["Dialogue1096501"]="Adventurer! Y-You're back! Are you... alright?",
    ["Dialogue1096502"]="Phew... Only minor injuries, how fortunate!\nI had to evacuate the wounded so they could receive proper treatment, but Vendra and I stayed behind for you. I was worried if it was a mistake to place such all bets on you... But fortunately, you return triumphant!",
    ["Dialogue1096503"]="See, I told you, Alexia! This is the world-renowned Adventurer! The songs the Euphonic Symphony wrote for him are enough to be sung all the way from Saint Darmain East to Comodo West!",
    ["Dialogue1096504"]="Right...! And for such an epic campaign... I have to write the songs personally! The epic battle between the Great Adventurer and the Ancient Dragon for the—Wait. Where's the Fragment of Ymir's Heart?",
    ["Dialogue1096505"]="That's the legendary Fragment of Ymir's Heart?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Doesn't seem... anything... special...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1096506"]="So this tiny thing... is what almost plunged Comodo into an irreversible disaster... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take it with you</color>, Adventurer. Comodo... has no place for it.",
    ["Dialogue1096507"]="About the ancient Dragon War? I don't know anything more than you do... I wasn't there.\nBut... I don't believe there's any war that was ever fought in the name of justice... Lady Margaret only did what needed to be done.",
    ["Dialogue1096508"]="That'll do... Let it go back to where it belongs.",
    ["Dialogue1096509"]="Now that all is done, it's time to part. This calamity... is both Comodo's tragedy and its rebirth. This time, I will live up to my duty as the leader.",
    ["Dialogue1096510"]="Hope we meet again, Adventurer. Next time, be sure to drop by the Euphonic Symphony's performance!",
    ["Dialogue1096601"]="Why do you look so... lost? Have you... wavered?",
    ["Dialogue1096602"]="I see... Alexia values order and rules while Vendra thirsts for changes. Raphael and Grantham only live to satisfy their own desires. Cecilia would cast honor aside to protect her home. They all have something to fight for... But what do you fight for, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1096603"]="(Upon hearing your answer, the Goddess smiles.)\nIn that case, your conscience should be clear.",
    ["Dialogue1096604"]="Desire and hope are separated by a thin line of difference. I cannot judge you for right and wrong, but I know that you will not infringe on someone's right to live in the name of justice. So, raise your head. You have never dishonored the glory that this bloodline has brought you.",
    ["Dialogue1096605"]="Very good... Well then, it is time to let you know the location of the next fragment. It is in Umbala, territory of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Utan tribe</color>. There lies an entrance that leads directly to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nifflheim</color>. Successor of Odin's Bloodline, be careful. Do not be tempted by the abyss.",
    ["Dialogue1096701"]="(A giant footprint is imprinted deep inside the mud. It has a peculiar shape: <color=#CA2E0AFF>a triangular palm</color> with <color=#CA2E0AFF>three thick and long toes at the front</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>one short toe at the back</color>. The footprint is surrounded by crushed and ripped plant roots. Its size far exceeds that of any monster that you know....)",
    ["Dialogue1096801"]="(The giant scale exhibits a dim <color=#CA2E0AFF>green</color> glow, making it extremely conspicuous in this land of corruption. The scale is the size of a grown man's palm. It's hard as a rock, thick as bark, and covered with sharp protrusions on the surface...)",
    ["Dialogue1096901"]="(The skin of the victims are covered with crimson burns. An unpleasant odor mixed with something burnt emanates from the wounds. Other than that, the victim's limbs and body all remain intact...)",
    ["Dialogue1097001"]="(The skin of the victims are covered with crimson burns. An unpleasant odor mixed with something burnt emanates from the wounds. Other than that, the victim's limbs and body all remain intact...)",
    ["Dialogue1097101"]="(There is a giant crack in the ground that reaches far and deep beyond what the eye can see. Upon closer inspection, you can hear unearthly screeches and cries and even feel a chill coming from its depths...)",
    ["Dialogue1097201"]="(The dragon eggs are surrounded by a ring of orange and gold fire. The flame's heat has driven back the coldness in the air. Upon closer inspection, you can see almost imperceptible cracks on the shell of some of the eggs. There seems to be life pulsing within...)",
    ["Dialogue1097301"]="(The piece of paper features a map of Comodo. The red circle around Kokomo Beach in the bottom right corner is quite obvious. Upon closer inspection, besides the red circle, there is a simple sketch of a monster similar to the ones before you. A giant red arrow extends from the red circle and points directly at the City of Comodo engulfed by flames...)",
    ["Dialogue1097401"]="(The piece of paper features a map of Comodo. The red circle around Papuchicha Forest in the top left corner is quite obvious. Upon closer inspection, besides the red circle, there is a simple sketch of a monster similar to the ones before you. A giant red arrow extends from the red circle and points directly at the Main City of Comodo engulfed by flames...)",
    ["Dialogue1097501"]="(The piece of paper features a map of Comodo. The red circle around Zenhai Marsh in the top left corner is quite obvious. Upon closer inspection, besides the red circle, there is a simple sketch of a monster similar to the ones before you. A giant red arrow extends from the red circle and points directly at the Main City of Comodo engulfed by flames...)",
    ["Dialogue1100101"]="Argh... If only I could be as great as that adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue1100102"]="That's right... Hey, <size=26>wait, The Adventurer?!</size>\n<color=#A1979FFF>Wow, when did I get the power to make my wishes come true...? Oh, now's not the time to wonder, I got to get that done...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1100103"]="(The girl slaps her own cheek hard and resumes the professional smile expected of a Kafra receptionist.)\nHello, valiant Adventurer! Welcome to the Umbala Rainforest! I'm W, and I've been expecting you!",
    ["Dialogue1100104"]="Yes, yes, it's perfect timing on your part!\nActually, I got news that may be useful to you just now!",
    ["Dialogue1100105"]="How much do you know about the Umbala region? It is the biggest rainforest in all of Midgard and is shrouded in mystery. Legend has it that it is linked to Yggdrasil, the world tree. The plants within are even seen as the descendants of Yggdrasil and have inherited its powers. They're able to bear fruits with special abilities...",
    ["Dialogue1100106"]="That's why merchants and scholars swarmed this place, bringing cultures from other regions to this isolated, pristine village. In fact, the Utan tribe... Oh, that's the people indigenous to the rainforest. Feel free to look around, do you see folks wearing exotic outfits and huge masks?",
    ["Dialogue1100107"]="The Utan are the most devout followers of Yggdrasil. Their masks are said to be made from its sprouts and are as vital as talismans. The Utans have retained a symbiotic relationship with the rainforest for a thousand years now and never changed. But lately, I heard the plants have apparently lost their vigor and luster...",
    ["Dialogue1100108"]="They were afflicted with a strange condition and wouldn't bear fruit anymore. Many of the weaker races have turned to humans for help because their food sources are gone. I just saw some Miwa fleeing the forest seconds ago myself, and I couldn't do anything other than feed them some food. But fortunately, you are finally here now!",
    ["Dialogue1100109"]="(W looks at you expectantly.)\nI knew you would come to this remote rainforest to seek <color=#CA2E0AFF>the legendary</color>... Ahem, so what I'm trying to say is, maybe the anomaly in Umbala is related to that!",
    ["Dialogue1100110"]="For a long time now, no matter what crisis happened in what region, you would do what you possibly could to lead everyone to overcome it! So, I believe you can save this land and all the denizens on it!",
    ["Dialogue1100111"]="Thank you, Adventurer! Of course, I will help you out in any way I can. If you'd like to know more about what's been going on recently in Umbala, you should talk to Karkatan, lord of the Utan tribe, in the hut on the northwest side of the village. Don't worry, the Utan are familiar with the common tongue, so there won't be language barriers.",
    ["Dialogue1100112"]="Well then, I shall wait for good news from you! Good luck, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1100201"]="I understand we're all exhausted over the Sacred Relic these days, but we cannot buck the wizard's orders, so I hope all of you can hold on for a while longer. I will look for another opportunity to speak with him again.",
    ["Dialogue1100202"]="Lord, it's fine if Tatanka wouldn't look for it himself, but he forbade us from learning any news about the Sacred Relic!\nI think he's been an <color=#CA2E0AFF>entirely different person</color> since the Sacred Relic was lost...",
    ["Dialogue1100203"]="Now that you mentioned it, he has been rather weird lately. I made his favorite Crunchy Cocoons, and he didn't even take one bite...",
    ["Dialogue1100204"]="Oh, you must be from faraway! Do you find traditional Utan cuisine fascinating, too?\nCrunchy Cocoons are the most special of our specialties! We take fresh worm cocoons from the Luluka Forest and coat them in breading, then deep fry them for thirty seconds!",
    ["Dialogue1100205"]="You must eat it while it's steaming hot, so the combo flavor of crunchy crust and delicious wormlings will fill your mouth!",
    ["Dialogue1100206"]="Our wizard Tatanka has been the greatest fan of the treat! He'd always say that half-cooked cocoons have a creamy, buttery taste, especially when they burst as you bite into them. It's like you're blessed with mana from haven! But yesterday, he seemed disgusted by my Crunchy Cocoons...",
    ["Dialogue1100207"]="Yeah, exactly like that! That was how he looked, too! <size=26>You got it down pat!</size>\n(She applauds with sincerity.)",
    ["Dialogue1100208"]="Ahem... That's enough. It's not polite to keep the guest waiting.\nSomething tells me you didn't come here to sightsee, is that right?",
    ["Dialogue1100209"]="So that Kafra girl asked you to solve the problem in Umbala?\n(The lord in a mask chuckles helplessly.)",
    ["Dialogue1100210"]="We appreciate the thought, but what happened recently is beyond even us, who have been cohabiting with the rainforest until now... What can a foreigner like you hope to do?",
    ["Dialogue1100211"]="<size=26>Successor...?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1100212"]="<size=26>Of the Odin bloodline?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1100213"]="I see. I heard about you. The bards would always laud your exploits, which is how I know you've been fulfilling missions for Odin... Since you're here now, that means you've surmised that the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1100214"]="Correct. Just as you thought, the Utans have been guarding the fragment on this land for thousands of years. The recent rash of anomalies happened in Umbala because the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sacred Relic had been stolen</color>. Recovering it was supposed to be our top priority, but the wizard Tatanka prohibited us from doing that...",
    ["Dialogue1100215"]="I'm not sure, either. The Utan are followers of the Yggdrasil, and the wizard is the oracle whose orders represent the will of the Tree. Therefore, we mortals do not dare defy him or the Tree.",
    ["Dialogue1100216"]="You wish to persuade Tatanka?\n(For some reason, the lord has been hesitant when speaking to you. You feel <color=#CA2E0AFF>he knows something important</color> but is withholding it from you.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Fine, maybe it's fate...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1100217"]="Please accept my gratitude. Perhaps the wizard will reconsider finding the Sacred Relic with help from Odin's successor. However, he has been busy due to the issues with the rainforest and is currently not in the village... I suggest trying your luck in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Luluka Forest</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1100218"]="Also, without the Sacred Relic's protection, the elements in the forest are very unstable and give rise to very destructive <color=#CA2E0AFF>elemental storms</color> frequently. You do not want to be caught in one, so please be careful.",
    ["Dialogue1100301"]="Oh, kind Adventurer, help me, please...",
    ["Dialogue1100302"]="No, not me, it's my children!\n(The Dragon Tail flaps its wings frantically but cannot move due to a crystal spur that pinned its tail to the ground.)\nPlease, make sure they're safe for me... They're in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the river bed not far ahead</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1100303"]="It's all right, I was just... caught in the residue of an elemental storm... I just want my children to be okay... Please!",
    ["Dialogue1100401"]="Oh, kind Adventurer... Please help... You're my only hope!",
    ["Dialogue1100402"]="If you can get the Revival Potion... to dissolve the crystal and free my children... before they are tainted completely! But, if you wish to help, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut off my wings</color>, seek out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>human merchant</color> in the east of the forest, and trade for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Revival Potion</color> that will save us...",
    ["Dialogue1100403"]="Thank you, Adventurer, but given the Luluka Forest's decline, human merchants would prefer practical goods to money... They're looking to barter, especially for the Revival Potion that could dissolve crystals. They won't cough it up without an equal trade.",
    ["Dialogue1100404"]="Before, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Utan savior</color> would come to help us out often and give us free food, as well as stand up to unscrupulous merchants. But more of the forest is ravaged by elemental storms every day and even he won't be enough... You're my only hope now...",
    ["Dialogue1100405"]="He told us that the wings of Dragon Tails are a very rare material to humans and will fetch a tidy sum. That's why the poachers got their eyes on us. But if I can trade this pair of wings for a chance of survival for my children... I'm willing to!",
    ["Dialogue1100501"]="You! Name your price for these items! I'm taking it all!",
    ["Dialogue1100502"]="Not for sale?!\n(Sanja's eyes grow wide, and his beard flutters in anger.)\nWhat are you doing here, then? Looking for trouble?",
    ["Dialogue1100503"]="Re, re, re... <size=26>Revival Potion?!</size>\nDid a man in an odd mask send you?",
    ["Dialogue1100504"]="You don't know him...?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Okay, that scared the soul out of me.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1100505"]="Ahem... You wish to trade for a potion, yes? I'm afraid these trifles you're offering me are not nearly enough. I'll need at least ten clusters of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juicy Grapes</color> on top of this. You can find them in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southern parts of the Luluka Forest</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1100506"]="Much? Heh, you know-nothing foreigner.\n(The devious merchant scoffs at you with contempt in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue1100507"]="Revival Potions are in short supply right now. See what's happening with the forest? The crystallization from the elemental storms is getting worse each day, it's practically a death sentence! Nothing else can save you other than these potions. There are people lining up if you don't want it, so decide for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue1100601"]="Despicable two-legged creature! How dare you strike when we're fighting! You must want to steal our food!",
    ["Dialogue1100602"]="I knew it, I knew it! You're working with that rotten merchant, aren't you? We don't even have enough food for ourselves, yet you keep stealing from us! I'll tell Ta-Ta to get rid of you!",
    ["Dialogue1100603"]="No! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ta-Ta is not Tatanka</color>! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ta-Ta is not Tatanka</color>!\n(Choco reiterates incoherently and appears on edge. You should calm it down.)",
    ["Dialogue1100604"]="What, you know Ta-Ta?\nYou're not with that rotten merchant?",
    ["Dialogue1100605"]="You're trying to save a wounded Dragon Tail? We'll give you the Juicy Grapes then! Ta-Ta is our savior! If not for his protection and food, we would have starved to death long ago!",
    ["Dialogue1100606"]="The friend of Ta-Ta must also be good! Here, here!",
    ["Dialogue1100701"]="What are you doing? Are you robbing me because you can't afford it?!\nYou should know that I'm no chopped liver. Make another move and I'll—",
    ["Dialogue1100702"]="<size=26>The man in the odd mask?!</size>\nYou didn't tell him about the deal between us, did you?",
    ["Dialogue1100703"]="<size=26>Bastard! I'll show you—</size>",
    ["Dialogue1100704"]="What is it you want?! I have no beef with you, foreigner. We both benefit from the deal! How about I throw in a bonus Revival Potion if you keep him away from me? That should do it, right?",
    ["Dialogue1100705"]="Okay, we have a deal, then! Don't let him know I'm back in town!",
    ["Dialogue1100801"]="Thank you! My children and I wouldn't make it without you! You're our savior, just like that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Utan wizard</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1100802"]="You want to know where that savior went? As I recall, my fellows saw him head up <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color> not so long ago. He seemed to stay <color=#CA2E0AFF>by Mirror Lake</color> for hours on end the last few days...",
    ["Dialogue1100901"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Tsk... The elemental storm is expanding faster than I thought.</color>\n<color=#A1979FFF>Leaving and finding another habitat is obviously the best solution, but they're unexpectedly stubborn... probably even more than the lord...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1100902"]="Who are you? How does a foreigner know about the Sacred Relic?\n(The wizard turns and speaks in a defiant, distant tone. His searing gaze through the mask is palpable.)\nI see... Did the lord send you?",
    ["Dialogue1100903"]="Quit meddling, foreigner. It's none of your business. Didn't the lord tell you my decision represents the will of Yggdrasil? And the Utan never turn their back on that!",
    ["Dialogue1100904"]="Innocent? No, you're wrong. Everything in the forest is merely enjoying the gift from Yggdrasil. She gave them all a home, so shouldn't we respect the Tree's will when she decided to take the gift back?",
    ["Dialogue1100905"]="Yes, I'd like to save them, which is why I tried to persuade them to leave and look for a new home. Yggdrasil cannot protect this land anymore. They must learn to protect themselves and not pin their lives on something hopeless... Isn't that right?",
    ["Dialogue1100906"]="Anyway, stop trying to convince me. I can already tell you that your chances of <color=#CA2E0AFF>finding the Sacred Relic are slim to none</color>... That's why my time is better spent on something more productive. At least, if I find a way to stop the storms, the forest will be safe even without the Sacred Relic.",
    ["Dialogue1100907"]="Just stop. Leave if you've got nothing else and quit bothering me!",
    ["Dialogue1100908"]="How to stop elemental storms from proliferating? Why do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue1100909"]="Never mind, what I need right now is more help. If you're willing, able, and quit pestering me to find the Sacred Relic, I can tell you more about the storms. Call it a fair trade... How's that, foreigner?",
    ["Dialogue1100910"]="Okay, I'm currently brewing potions to lower the potency of elements. Only by controlling the concentration of the elements in the forest under the critical range can you stop the storms from forming. Go gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Mushrooms</color> that grow in the shade for me, plus some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brown Down Fur</color> on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Choco</color>. We'll talk once you have them.",
    ["Dialogue1101001"]="This should slow down the storm's growth. However, to reverse the crystallized forest back to its original condition, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>restoration of Water Heart</color> is a must...",
    ["Dialogue1101002"]="What's the matter? The lord asked you to find the Sacred Relic but neglected to tell you the rules about it?",
    ["Dialogue1101003"]="The lush Umbala rainforest has been blessed with divine grace since ancient times. Just like the Utan land is protected by the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, other forests have their own irreplaceable <color=#CA2E0AFF>heirlooms</color>. The elemental natures of these relics <color=#CA2E0AFF>aid and suppress each other</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>keeping each other in balance</color>, which enables the rainforest to thrive to date.",
    ["Dialogue1101004"]="The Watery Heart I spoke of is the heirloom that protects the Luluka Forest. But since the Sacred Relic is missing, it threw off the elemental balance in the rainforest and left the Water Heart open to batter by the raging storms. In other words...",
    ["Dialogue1101005"]="Tatanka... Tatanka, please save us!",
    ["Dialogue1101101"]="Midori and Ran passed out again, Tatanka! Even Wakadake has been casting spells for a whole day! If this keeps up, everyone will die!",
    ["Dialogue1101102"]="What? Did you try to infuse energy into the Spirit Tree again? Didn't I say that's futile? Why didn't you listen to me?",
    ["Dialogue1101103"]="Well, we... we had no other recourse... Please, Tatanka, save us...",
    ["Dialogue1101104"]="Come with me, foreigner. Aren't you wondering what happened to the forest? Come see it with your own eyes.\nThen you'll realize the only way for them to survive is to leave here.",
    ["Dialogue1101201"]="They spent too much energy. If they don't replenish, these Miwa will slumber forever.",
    ["Dialogue1101202"]="Save us, Tatanka! I'm sure you can!",
    ["Dialogue1101203"]="I can make potions to replenish their power for you, but herbs are very scarce in the forest right now. Given the short time and very few of you, it's hard to gather every component I need...",
    ["Dialogue1101204"]="You?\n(Tatanka pauses with visible distrust in his eyes.)\nHow can you help?",
    ["Dialogue1101205"]="You don't know the forest anywhere near as well as the Miwa, and the herbs I need are rare. I don't have the time to show you how to distinguish between herbs and toxic plants, in particular the White Mist Moss, which only grew in magic-rich areas—",
    ["Dialogue1101206"]="You helped others gather it on Comodo before, you said?",
    ["Dialogue1101207"]="Okay, seek out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>White Mist Moss</color> with Miwa, then. Also, I need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dreamweaver Grass</color> nourished by Mirror Lake Water, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Refreshing Dew</color> off Wooden Golems. Return as soon as you're done collecting them, and make it fast.",
    ["Dialogue1101301"]="Why didn't you listen to me? I warned you not to send energy into the Spirit Tree. It is but a bottomless pit now, and you simply cannot fill it up. You can't heal it even if you pour all of your energy into it.",
    ["Dialogue1101302"]="But how can we just watch the Mother Tree... You must have a way to save her, right? Please, Tatanka, she can't hold on much longer...",
    ["Dialogue1101303"]="Stop right there. You want to know how I can help them, right? I told you, to halt the crystallization, you must repair the Water Heart damaged by the elemental storms. But the Miwa's Mother Tree⁠—the Spirit Tree—is⁠ the only one able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore</color> the battered <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Heart</color> with the power she has inherited from Yggdrasil.",
    ["Dialogue1101304"]="But the Spirit Tree has been lying dormant ever since the Sacred Relic went missing... I tried everything in my power to awaken her to no avail. Not only that, even she's taking the toll from the storms herself and showing signs of decay. Under the circumstance, it's useless for Miwa to keep giving her energy. If you ask me, I say we leave and find a new place.",
    ["Dialogue1101305"]="But the chief just said it has a way to save the Mother Tree and told us not to give up! It even sent the rest of us away from her in preparation of casting alone... Why are you glaring at me, Tatanka?",
    ["Dialogue1101306"]="<size=26>That fool!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1101401"]="...",
    ["Dialogue1101402"]="<size=26>Stop at once!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1101403"]="(The Miwa apparently hears Tatanka's voice and shudders in its spell-casting, but doesn't turn to look.)\nPlease do not stop me, Tatanka. I can't stand idly by while the Mother Tree decays...",
    ["Dialogue1101404"]="I know what you're trying to do, Higurashi! <size=26>But you'll die this way!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1101405"]="I know, Tatanka. Nobody can withstand the strain of such monumental force that sent even the Mother Tree into a deep slumber. My death is assured, but I'm willing to pay any cost to save the Mother Tree.",
    ["Dialogue1101406"]="It's trying to absorb all of the elemental force in the Spirit Tree. The energy won't appear out of nowhere or disappear, but it can be transferred! Moving all the energy will alleviate the tree's condition, but Higurashi will become a lifeless crystal from taking in so much of it!",
    ["Dialogue1101407"]="It's fine... The whole forest will revive as long as the Mother Tree wakes up. I've made up my mind. It's worth it.\n(It raises a hand, and a glow spreads from its fingertips before coalescing into a mirror image that blocks your path.)\nPlease forgive my insolence, Tatanka...",
    ["Dialogue1101408"]="Come on, Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>give me a hand</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1101501"]="Tatanka?! And the chief...? What is going on here?",
    ["Dialogue1101502"]="Don't worry, Higurashi is not dead, but casting the spell drained a lot out of it, and it will take time to recover... You must take good care of your chief in the meantime.",
    ["Dialogue1101503"]="Got it... I'll take the chief back to convalesce!",
    ["Dialogue1101504"]="Wait, Aoba, did Higurashi have any contact with any unknown human?",
    ["Dialogue1101505"]="Unknown human? Why do you ask, Tatanka? For months, the chief has been working tirelessly on the Spirit Tree problem. Other than praying and casting magic under the tree, it locked itself in the house meditating all the time... Not to mention humans have been sparse since the forest's deterioration...",
    ["Dialogue1101506"]="In the past months, I have not seen any human except Tatanka and the kind Adventurer... oh, and those wicked merchants. I assume it's the same for the chief too.",
    ["Dialogue1101507"]="Did it... or should I say, have any of you run into anything unusual? Just give me anything you can think of.",
    ["Dialogue1101508"]="It was an unknown outside force that just saved Higurashi. It was full of divine power and shouldn't be here. I want to know what it is.",
    ["Dialogue1101509"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Voice from the Spirit Tree</color>? Impossible! I didn't hear anything. Are you sure you were not hallucinating?",
    ["Dialogue1101510"]="Wait, what are you doing?!\nHey, come back! Ordinary people can't touch Mirror Lake Water—",
    ["Dialogue1101601"]="Such divine power in you... I see now. You're the successor of Odin...\n(After replenishing the Spirit Tree with Mirror Lake Water, a gentle voice speaks in your mind, and you realize you can communicate with her telepathically.)",
    ["Dialogue1101602"]="I recognize the power in your blood, young one. You and I actually share an origin... I was a sapling of Yggdrasil. Odin planted me here and nourished me with the Well of Urd. In time, the well water flowing under my feet formed Mirror Lake and bestowed the forest with divine blessings to become the habitat for countless creatures.",
    ["Dialogue1101603"]="I am the progeny of Yggdrasil, and you are the successor of Odin's bloodline. Perhaps this meeting was arranged by the Goddess of Fate.\nSo, what do you want to know, young one?",
    ["Dialogue1101604"]="Yes, I stopped Higurashi. I could not bear to see it die. Also, even if it took on all of the uncontrolled elements unto itself, it would not have saved me... Because I destroyed the Water Heart myself.",
    ["Dialogue1101605"]="I have my reasons, of course, and it's not for you to know. Successor of Odin's bloodline, go elsewhere to complete greater missions, instead of wasting your time here and courting disaster...",
    ["Dialogue1101606"]="When you touched the lake, I saw your reflection in the water. Your journey is still far <color=#CA2E0AFF>from the destination</color>, and soon, the entire land will be engulfed in the darkness that not even you can escape...",
    ["Dialogue1101607"]="You will lose every single ally who fought alongside... You will even fight them! Leave now, while you still can...\n(The voice vanishes as if she <color=#CA2E0AFF>does not want to continue the conversation</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1101701"]="How did you just do that?\n(He looks at you alarmingly with uncertainty in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue1101702"]="Don't play dumb. I just saw you scooped up the Mirror Lake Water, and that's impossible. Mirror Lake came from the Well of Urd. It's pure divinity. No ordinary folks without the power of the divine could touch it!",
    ["Dialogue1101703"]="You're the successor of Odin's bloodline?!\nSo when you watered the Spirit Tree with Mirror Lake Water...",
    ["Dialogue1101704"]="You said you heard the Spirit Tree's voice? Was she imploring you for Mirror Lake Water? And you stood there for so long... Was she talking to you?",
    ["Dialogue1101705"]="She said she harmed the Water Heart?! And that led to the storms in the forest? Impossible...\n<color=#A1979FFF>No, that's not totally impossible because of that legend... In that case, maybe I can...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1101706"]="Perhaps I just figured out certain key clues, thanks to you, Adventurer.\n(You're not sure if you're imagining things, but Tatanka's attitude toward you just changed.)",
    ["Dialogue1101707"]="If I'm correct, the Spirit Tree should hold vital clues to the missing Sacred Relic. Since it refused to answer, I shall find out in my own way.",
    ["Dialogue1101708"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Memory Materialization</color>. It's a spell to scour the target's memory and even replay it as an illusion. I'm going to try it to access the Spirit Tree's memory. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come closer</color>, so you can see what I see.",
    ["Dialogue1101801"]="You read my memory? How is that possible? My power came from Yggdrasil, nobody can... Oh, I realize it now, you are F—",
    ["Dialogue1101802"]="(Tatanka interrupts her coldly.)\nWhat I used is a secret spell of the Utan that works on everything with awareness. Even though you're an offspring of Yggdrasil, you're not exempt. Thanks to you, I now finally understand what started this cataclysm...",
    ["Dialogue1101803"]="Destroying the Water Heart for the Miwa? Don't get me wrong—I'm not blaming the Spirit Tree. My concern is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>motivation</color> behind her decision to destroy it, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>paradox</color> arising from it.",
    ["Dialogue1101804"]="(Seeing your hesitance, Tatanka shakes his head with a certain disgust.)\nI can only say you're barely half-right. The prophecy indeed directly caused the Spirit Tree to destroy the Water Heart, but it also proved the destruction <color=#CA2E0AFF>had nothing to do with the Sacred Relic</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1101805"]="We all thought it was the missing Sacred Relic that caused the elements to go awry and damaged the Water Heart, but it's actually the opposite. The destruction of the Water Heart is what triggered the storms in Luluka Forest... What role, then, did our Utan relic play in all of this?",
    ["Dialogue1101806"]="Aha, I just have an interesting thought. Maybe the crisis in Umbala is not a natural event but a <color=#CA2E0AFF>man-made disaster</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1101807"]="Man-made disaster?\n(The Spirit Tree's voice quivers, and its rustling branches startle several birds resting on it.)\nIt can't be! I harmed the Water Heart because of the prophecy!",
    ["Dialogue1101808"]="Are you trying to say that the prophecy of Mirror Lake Water can't possibly be fake? If it were a genuine revelation from the lake, I'd believe it came from Vanaheim too, of course. But what if the lake never told you any prophecy?",
    ["Dialogue1101809"]="(The tone in Tatanka's voice suddenly drops with hints of anger.)\nMaybe the prophecy you saw was actually a scripted <color=#CA2E0AFF>illusion</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1101810"]="That cannot be true... I don't believe it...\n(The rustling calms down, and the Spirit Tree's voice trails off into a barely audible sigh.)",
    ["Dialogue1101811"]="Whether it's real or not, we'll find out. If I could prove what you saw was staged, my theory would have a leg to stand on. Adventurer, would you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a container</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>fetch a bottle of Mirror Lake Water</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue1101901"]="There are only a scant few potions able to induce illusions, and harder still when the target is the Spirit Tree. It must be <color=#CA2E0AFF>equal in divine power</color>... Luckily, I read about something similar in Utan heirloom scrolls.",
    ["Dialogue1101902"]="However, the scrolls survived Ragnarok with only a few portions intact and were missing certain key records, so I have to resort to the process of elimination for this. I'll list all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>components</color> I need for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color>, then we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>verify each outcome in turn</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1102001"]="I knew it... Although only you, successor of Odin's bloodline, can touch Mirror Lake Water, anyone can add to the water from a distance without contact.",
    ["Dialogue1102002"]="I'm sure you're familiar with the text popping up in the water... That's right, it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune script</color>. Odin created it and imbued it with divine power. Only illusions cast from this script could deceive the equally powerful Spirit Tree.",
    ["Dialogue1102003"]="Also, I noticed something in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bushes around Mirror Lake</color>... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1102101"]="See that in the thorn bushes? I just searched around the edge of the lake and noticed the plants were trampled. The races in the forest revered the lake and Spirit Tree. They wouldn't approach without a very good reason. And very few people have been here since the storms started in Luluka Forest...",
    ["Dialogue1102102"]="(Tatanka takes an object off the bushes. You see it is a piece of ripped clothes with water stains on it.)\nThe make and material don't belong to the Utan tribe. This should be the work of an outsider, right?",
    ["Dialogue1102103"]="Since it can't possibly be Utan costume, the chances are that it was left by the culprit who manipulated the lake water.",
    ["Dialogue1102104"]="Yes, it's only a guess on my part, but we already proved the lake water was tainted with an illusion potion. Now, if the residues on this fabric matched the potion in the lake, I can dismiss any coincidence and confirm it was premeditated.",
    ["Dialogue1102105"]="Come, let's see who tried to mess with Umbala.",
    ["Dialogue1102201"]="Now you believe it, Adventurer? No one but you could touch Mirror Lake Water, they couldn't get the water on them, either. Since the stains showed the same <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune script</color> in the lake, that means the offender accidentally got it on them when applying the potion.",
    ["Dialogue1102202"]="As for where the culprit came from... Do you spot anything unusual in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>plants around here</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1102301"]="This is a sign of abyss corruption... From what I know, only the undead from the underworld are capable of this, which incidentally fits my conjecture. Follow me <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to the Spirit Tree</color>, Adventurer, and I shall prove my conclusion.",
    ["Dialogue1102401"]="Have you found an answer?",
    ["Dialogue1102402"]="All the pieces have fallen into place. Now, allow me to tell you a story about the Sacred Relic: A long time ago, the purpose of heirlooms in the various forests on Umbala was to maintain the ward on the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic. In other words, to steal the Sacred Relic, one must first destroy the Water Heart, as well as all the other heirlooms.",
    ["Dialogue1102403"]="Yes. The miscreant was familiar with the legend and planned accordingly. It's a shame that the ward has been down since Ragnarok ended, which was why the Utan tribe picked powerful wizards to guard the Sacred Relic and perpetuated the tradition to today—something no outsider knew about.",
    ["Dialogue1102404"]="You mean the culprit didn't realize the ward protecting the Sacred Relic had long gone and made up a prophecy with Mirror Lake Water, then deceived me into destroying the Water Heart?",
    ["Dialogue1102405"]="(Tatanka nods and presents all the evidence you collected before the Spirit Tree.)\nWe did some tests and, as you know, the eyes of a Dragon Tail can see through all illusions. When we put the Radiant Compound Eyes into the water sample, the Rune script appeared...",
    ["Dialogue1102406"]="Rune?\nSo the deceiver has divine power? How could this be?!",
    ["Dialogue1102407"]="Not only that, I discovered the taint of abyss on the plants around the lake. That kind of power isn't found in Midgard but in the underworld.",
    ["Dialogue1102408"]="The dead? From Niflheim?!",
    ["Dialogue1102409"]="That is my guess. But I'd like to check out the condition of the other heirlooms first before reaching a conclusion. If the truth is exactly what I think it is, the Wind Heart in the Kalala Swamp is probably ruined by now, too.",
    ["Dialogue1102410"]="But regardless, we've proved to you the prophecy of Mirror Lake is merely a hoax. Even if the cataclysm it foretold did happen, the Miwa would never abandon you and the forest. You should trust them, and trust yourself.",
    ["Dialogue1102411"]="What's been guarding the forest for all these years isn't the prophecy, but you and the Miwa. To this day, they are still waiting for you to wake up. As their Mother Tree, you should not keep them waiting.",
    ["Dialogue1102412"]="(The Spirit Tree suddenly shakes as countless flickering fireflies drift from the leaves and fly out in different directions.)\nThank you, Utan wizard... and you, successor of Odin's bloodline...",
    ["Dialogue1102413"]="Don't thank me, thank the Miwa who never gave up on you. The rest is all up to you.\n(Tatanka turns and pats you on the shoulder.)\nAs for you, Adventurer... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me</color>, I'd like to have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>chat</color> with you.",
    ["Dialogue1102501"]="Maybe you already guessed what I'm going to say, Adventurer. To confirm my suspicions, I must go to the Kalala Swamp and see the Wind Heart. It's vital to the whereabouts of the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic. Would you be willing to help me?",
    ["Dialogue1102502"]="It's not that I didn't want to search for it, I just thought it was a long shot, so I'd rather spend the time on something more meaningful. But your presence did reveal new possibilities, so I must thank you, Adventurer.\n(Tatanka bows with genuine sincerity.)",
    ["Dialogue1102503"]="Yes, compared to this, it's more urgent we look into the Wind Heart. Follow me, please, <color=#CA2E0AFF>to the Kalala Swamp</color> now.",
    ["Dialogue1102601"]="Adventurer, in Umbala myth, the Water Heart nourishes all things, and the Wind Heart eradicates diseases and plagues. But now, because of the damage to Wind Heart, the forest is invaded by an unknown blight. Compared to Luluka Forest, it's more dangerous here, so we must be careful.",
    ["Dialogue1102602"]="As for the Wind Heart's location, I only know it's guarded by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wootan</color>, who've been ruling this forest for generations. To get updates, we must head to the cave in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of the forest</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Uba</color>, the current chief of Wootan. We will leave if you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue1102701"]="Thank you... But why is the human here?\n(The doubting, naive fighter scratches its head.)\nI appreciate you saving me, but you really should go. It's very dangerous here.",
    ["Dialogue1102702"]="Are you trying to cover up your evil deeds? Is that why you're urging us to leave?!\n(Tatanka shouts out a surprise accusation before you realize he opened the Wootan fighters' sack while they were distracted by the conversation.)\nLook at these, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1102703"]="<size=26>Hey, who said you could—</size>",
    ["Dialogue1102801"]="(The tall fighter stomps its feet out of anger and embarrassment.)\nWhy, you humans are rude and unreasonable!",
    ["Dialogue1102802"]="I wanted you to leave because a terrible pandemic is sweeping through the Kalala Swamp right now! These Beetle Kings look like this because they are infected! We've quarantined a large number of them in the garden to the east, and without us disposing of the carrion, the plague would have made its way into human territories by now!",
    ["Dialogue1102803"]="Don't say I never warned you not to go near the garden! It's guarded by our mightiest fighter. Find another way around it unless you want trouble.",
    ["Dialogue1102804"]="(As the Wootan fighters haul off the sacks, Tatanka waves you over and whispers.)\nOver here, Adventurer. Something's off with them. Let's follow.",
    ["Dialogue1102901"]="Be quiet. You don't want to alert them.",
    ["Dialogue1102902"]="I thought something is wrong when they said they're quarantining the Beetle Kings here... Now it seems they're bringing those beetles to die in order to stop the plague from spreading...",
    ["Dialogue1102903"]="Take it easy. I want to check out the plants around here first. They seem somewhat out of the ordinary, too. Would you mind collecting some Plant Juice samples for me? I'll keep watching the Wootan fighters in the meantime.",
    ["Dialogue1103001"]="No, this is...?!",
    ["Dialogue1103002"]="It's not a plague, Adventurer, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>toxin</color>! These plants and Beetle Kings are poisoned by the same toxin—",
    ["Dialogue1103003"]="<size=26>Who goes there!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1103101"]="Unbelievable! Humans indeed are the most diabolical race! Intruding on other races' territory and striking!",
    ["Dialogue1103102"]="Diabolical? You must be joking! What do you call confining these Beetle Kings here to their death?",
    ["Dialogue1103103"]="Do not falsely accuse us! We did not imprison these Beetle Kings! They're infected and would doom the whole Kalala Swamp if they're allowed to run free!",
    ["Dialogue1103104"]="Is that so? From what I know, the Beetle King's habitat is Fairy Lake on the west side. Are you telling me they couldn't stay where they were and must come across the forest for quarantine? Not to mention they're not diseased but <color=#CA2E0AFF>poisoned</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1103105"]="Poisoned? But <color=#CA2E0AFF>the chief said</color> these bugs were infected by a plague...\n(It explains in a panic, apparently not knowing the truth.)",
    ["Dialogue1103106"]="No, we really didn't harm them! On a night several weeks ago, an unusual, mysterious gale tore through the forest, and the next day, we found the bugs gathering nearby. We thought they were caught in the wind and tried to herd them back to their habitat, but who knew they were sick?",
    ["Dialogue1103107"]="Every tribesman coming into contact with the Beetle Kings got infected. Then, the plague got worse, until you could even catch it by walking on where the beetles have been! We're out of ideas, so we chose to quarantine them here!",
    ["Dialogue1103108"]="Where is your chief Uba? Why didn't it handle such a big problem in the Kalala Swamp?",
    ["Dialogue1103109"]="It's locked itself in the cave for days now. At first, we quarantined the Beetle Kings as the chief instructed, but still couldn't control the outbreak. Then, like you, it told us to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect and send the infected plants to its cave</color>. But it's not come out ever since... Maybe the chief's infected...?",
    ["Dialogue1103110"]="If you're looking for the chief, go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>its cave</color>! Let me go, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1103201"]="Focus, Uba, and answer some questions for me.",
    ["Dialogue1103202"]="Poison... Not... Me... It's him...\n(It stares at you, glaze-eyed, mumbling mostly incoherently and unable to form a complete sentence.)",
    ["Dialogue1103203"]="This isn't working. I think I have to try to use Memory Materialization again. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come closer</color>, Adventurer, and I'll start casting.",
    ["Dialogue1103301"]="The spell didn't work! It's not possible, unless it...?",
    ["Dialogue1103302"]="As you know, Adventurer, memories have a self-defense mechanism. When a particular memory is too painful and traumatic, this is what happens. Uba decided to deceive itself and <color=#CA2E0AFF>hid the memory along with its cognizance</color> as to lessen the agony... But this cannot spare it at all.",
    ["Dialogue1103303"]="Furthermore, closing your awareness off is an extremely dangerous act. Those who tried to dodge reality ultimately suffered hysteria like Uba and became mindless walking dead!",
    ["Dialogue1103304"]="We have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>unearth</color> the memory it's hiding and resolve its <color=#CA2E0AFF>inner conflict</color>. That's the only way to get the real Uba back. However, that means I have to cast a long-term Memory Materialization spell to find it... Wait, <color=#CA2E0AFF>why is it so noisy outside the cave?</color>",
    ["Dialogue1103401"]="The bugs have gone crazy! They broke through our watch and headed toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chief Uba's cave</color>! They're not seeking vengeance against the chief, are they...?",
    ["Dialogue1103501"]="The confined Beetle Kings are rioting? It seems order in the Kalala Swamp has degenerated into complete chaos, when even the Drillers are out about and looting. But I still need more time to find Uba's hidden memory and can't be disturbed in the meanwhile.",
    ["Dialogue1103502"]="Can you fend off the attacking bugs for me, Adventurer? It will only take a while... I should find it soon.",
    ["Dialogue1103601"]="Who are you...? My memory...",
    ["Dialogue1103602"]="I got the memory you lost back for you. Also, I'm drained right now, so I'll cut straight to the chase... The mind of the Wootan chief is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wind Heart</color>, right?",
    ["Dialogue1103603"]="Not only that, while being kept in your tribe for generations, it gained the unique ability to <color=#CA2E0AFF>change its power to match the owner's mindset</color>. When you had evil thoughts and started to oppress the Beetle Kings, it corrupted the Wind Heart. The source of the so-called plague in Kalala Swamp is none other than your own mind. You must have realized it, too, to choose this way out.",
    ["Dialogue1103604"]="(Uba's glazed eyes start to focus as Tatanka reveals the truth.)\nYou...! Why did you make me remember? No, it's not me... I blame that human! I blame you vile humans for lying to me!",
    ["Dialogue1103605"]="Why are you still trying to run away now? That man deceived you, indeed, but if you were resolute and not swayed by your own desires, how could he succeed? The truth is you still haven't realized it was your own error that turned Kalala Swamp into what it is today!",
    ["Dialogue1103606"]="No... That's not what I wanted!\n(Uba wails while pounding its own chest.)\nWhat should I do? Help me! Help me!",
    ["Dialogue1103607"]="No one can help you now, Uba. You alone hold the only way to restore the Wind Heart, and nobody else does. You can choose to keep running, but that will just doom all your tribesmen. Is that what you really want?",
    ["Dialogue1103608"]="(Tatanka appears stoic. Even though he didn't get the message across in a friendly manner, you still feel he was trying to encourage Uba.)\nIf not, stand up and do what you have to do. That's all I've got to say.",
    ["Dialogue1103609"]="Please collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Spirit Flowers</color> that grow in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fairy Lake on the west side</color> for me, Adventurer. I need to confirm the makeup of this soil I got.\n(The wizard stands and heads for the outside with the soil left by the mysterious man in hand.)\nWhat are you still doing here? Go now. I'll wait for you by the mouth of the cave.",
    ["Dialogue1103701"]="The Holy Spirit Flower is the most unique plant in Kalala Swamp, Adventurer. It is said to be born from the highly poisonous glacier of Hvergelmir in the Realm of the Dead, as a counterbalance to the toxins in the river. When these flowers come into contact with Hvergelmir water, their snow-white petals immediately turn black...",
    ["Dialogue1103702"]="(Tatanka puts the Holy Spirit Flowers on the soil, and inky black quickly permeates and dyes the petals.)\nI knew I was right again. This is poison from the Realm of the Dead.",
    ["Dialogue1103703"]="In Uba's memory, we witnessed how that mysterious man lied to Uba. Given the mountain of ironclad proofs, why do you still doubt my conclusion? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, I got one last piece of evidence for you.",
    ["Dialogue1103801"]="Did it spook you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1103802"]="I combed the site of crime on the night when the Sacred Relic was stolen, but only managed to find this tiny eerie glow. I've been pondering what exactly it is for days, until I figured out the culprit might come from the underworld and realized this fell from the dead.",
    ["Dialogue1103803"]="Given that, I was sure whoever took the Sacred Relic must have come from Niflheim, the realm of the dead.",
    ["Dialogue1103804"]="That's right. I plan on visiting Niflheim and finding the Sacred Relic. You're not going to decline the invitation to come along, are you?",
    ["Dialogue1103805"]="Don't worry, for the Utan tribe, getting to Niflheim is not a problem. Follow me, Adventurer, we're going to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit the lord</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1103901"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, have you convinced Tatanka?",
    ["Dialogue1103902"]="The Sacred Relic thief came from the Realm of the Dead? But what do they want with it?",
    ["Dialogue1103903"]="Considering how powerful the Sacred Relic is, it makes sense that someone covets it. I hope you can access the way to the realm for us as soon as possible, Lord. Adventurer and I must seek the relic's whereabouts in person.",
    ["Dialogue1103904"]="Well, accessing it is not the problem. It's just that Hel, Queen of the Underworld, has placed <color=#CA2E0AFF>a ward that only the undead could pass through</color> on the other end.",
    ["Dialogue1103905"]="I got a solution for that. But to do it, I'll need the Fresh Shoots of a Wooden Golem, the roots under the feet of a Dryad, and some fresh Winged Shells. Can you get them all, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1104001"]="Okay, this is it. Just swallow it, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1104002"]="This is the secret weapon to help us sneak into the Realm of the Dead—Pill of Undeath.",
    ["Dialogue1104003"]="In truth, how the realm determines whether a traveler is undead is simple—from the lifeforce in your blood.\n(Tatanka grabs your wrist, and you can feel your pulse pounding under the light pressure of his fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue1104004"]="The Pill of Undeath will mask your signs of life, just like holding your breath underwater, so the undead cannot sense you're breathing. We can then blend in with the real undead and cross the ice bridge over Gjoll.",
    ["Dialogue1104005"]="Uh, when did you learn to make this, Tatanka?",
    ["Dialogue1104006"]="Did you forget, Lord? Our heirloom scrolls noted the techniques from many other nations, among them the sacrificial ritual of Arunafeltz. They would combine the use of the pill and mind magic to commune with the dead... I thought that was interesting so I wrote down how to make the pill.",
    ["Dialogue1104007"]="That's in the scrolls? I'll have to look through them sometime...\nWell then, I'll go open the access to the realm for you. When you're ready, come to the grove on the north side. I'll be waiting under the tree carved with a human face.",
    ["Dialogue1104008"]="Got it. We will head there after we take the pill and reconvene.",
    ["Dialogue1104101"]="The pill is amazing... I didn't even notice you here at all. You're right, Tatanka, the lifeforce is concealed in your bodies.",
    ["Dialogue1104102"]="Still, do not drop your guard after you're in the realm. This secret passage guarded by us has not been in use for a very long time, so your movement will surely be noticed by the Underworld. That is the undead territory, after all, and completely different from ours.",
    ["Dialogue1104103"]="I understand your concerns. However, sacrifices are necessary when it comes to the Sacred Relic. Don't worry, though, I'll bear all consequences, and nothing will blow back on the tribe.",
    ["Dialogue1104104"]="No, that's not what I mean. I'm trying to tell you that no matter what happens, <color=#CA2E0AFF>protect yourselves</color>, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1104105"]="Lord...",
    ["Dialogue1104106"]="We Utans have co-existed with this forest since ancient times. We obey nature and believe everything is a blessing from Yggdrasil. Nothing is forever in the world, Tatanka. Even the gods above will meet their decline one day, much less we insignificant humans.",
    ["Dialogue1104107"]="The Sacred Relic is a gift from the gods that gave us a thousand years of peace. It is good if we recover the relic, but if the gods have decided to take it back, I believe all Utans will gladly accept that. So, don't feel guilty for the loss.",
    ["Dialogue1104108"]="(The lord holds his arms out and gives Tatanka a warm embrace.) \nThis time, I just hope you and the successor of Odin's bloodline can both <color=#CA2E0AFF>return safely</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1104109"]="I'll do my best.",
    ["Dialogue1104201"]="Adventurer, we've reached Niflheim, the realm of the dead. Keep going and we'll be in the territory of Hel, Queen of the Underworld. Even though the Pill of Undeath masked our lifeforce, it also has the unavoidable side effect of weakening our physical bodies significantly...",
    ["Dialogue1104202"]="Therefore, we must exercise extreme caution when exploring Niflheim and avoid all unnecessary conflicts...",
    ["Dialogue1104203"]="<size=26>Who's there?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104301"]="Why are you out walking about here? The queen just ordered us to search for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>intruders who bypassed the ward to steal the Gjoll Soul Crystal</color>! Do you want to be arrested?",
    ["Dialogue1104302"]="Sorry, sergeant. Actually, we are new enlistees and heard you've been apprehending intruders, so we came to help...\n(Tatanka uses the opportunity to step in front of you.)\nWe didn't mean to cause trouble. Please forgive us.",
    ["Dialogue1104303"]="Ah, so you're wet-behind-the-ear rookies, eh?\n(The undead sergeant looks you two up and down as if it just dawned on itself.)",
    ["Dialogue1104304"]="No wonder you fought like stiffs! This batch of rookies got to be the worse I've ever seen! Can't fight, can't think... and can't follow the rules! You're lucky it's me. If this was that geezer Naght Sieger, you'd be taken to the Grand Celebration!",
    ["Dialogue1104305"]="(Tatanka pinches you on the side with a hand behind the back. You squeal and jump.)\nNo interrupting while the superior officer is talking!",
    ["Dialogue1104306"]="Excuse my awkward friend, sergeant. Please continue.",
    ["Dialogue1104307"]="I see you're the promising one. All right, I'll cut you some slack. All the new recruits are assembled on the training ground. The drill instructors aren't nearly as nice as me, so you better hustle while there's still time! As for what happened here, I can keep mum, but...",
    ["Dialogue1104308"]="(Its eye sockets roll, and it rubs the index finger and thumb together.)\nI want this! Got it?",
    ["Dialogue1104309"]="We got it, sergeant. When the training's over, we will... ahem, visit you again.",
    ["Dialogue1104310"]="Very well. Now leave and stop interfering with my duty! Make sure you meet me in Dorm #3 by the training ground tonight, or else!",
    ["Dialogue1104401"]="<size=26>I! Can't! Hear! You!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104402"]="Must I repeat myself?! Do you get it, you maggots?!",
    ["Dialogue1104403"]="<size=26>Got it, sergeant!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104404"]="Even the mosquitoes are louder than you, especially the two in the back! Yeah, I'm talking to you two trying to sneak in!",
    ["Dialogue1104405"]="What about you? Why are you late? Do you even know what discipline is?",
    ["Dialogue1104406"]="<size=26>Who's asking the question here, you or me?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104407"]="Drop and give me two hundred right now! Nonstop!",
    ["Dialogue1104408"]="The rest of you, line up and get your Scouting Regiment armbands one at a time! By the direct order of the queen, anyone who finds the infiltrator gets a year's worth of pay as a reward! Of course, it's your honor to serve the queen even without the reward!",
    ["Dialogue1104409"]="This is your first duty as an enlisted soldier, so you better give me your best! Did you hear that—yeah, the one doing the push-ups, don't you stop! That'll be a hundred more! Get your armband after you're done!",
    ["Dialogue1104410"]="Hee.\nKeep it up, Adventurer. I'll go get my armband with the rest of them. Come see me after you're done with the three hundred push-ups.",
    ["Dialogue1104501"]="You've done three hundred push-ups? You're faster than I thought.",
    ["Dialogue1104502"]="What? I don't know what you're talking about. But don't you think being on the Scouting Regiment would make it easier on us? We can blend in and use it as an excuse to find out where the Sacred Relic is.",
    ["Dialogue1104503"]="All right, no more kidding around. Since you're good with it, we'll move with the soldiers for the time being and wait for our opportunity. I must remind you, though, due to the pill, our physical prowess has taken a big dive, so we have to avoid conflict with the undead...",
    ["Dialogue1104504"]="Hey, you public servants, come do your job! <size=26>I found the intruder!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104601"]="Follow me, quickly! The intruder the queen is looking for is at my door!",
    ["Dialogue1104602"]="Stop dragging your feet! I'd have your skin if you caused me my bounty!",
    ["Dialogue1104603"]="Follow me, quickly! The intruder the queen is looking for is at my door!",
    ["Dialogue1104604"]="Stop dragging your feet! I'd have your skin if you caused me my bounty!",
    ["Dialogue1104701"]="Stop the beating! What's wrong with you kids? If he dies, how am I going to get my reward from the queen?!",
    ["Dialogue1104702"]="I'm not an intruder! But you, beating people up without a cause... especially you two!\n(He angrily points at your Scouting Regiment armbands.)\nYou're abusing your power! I shall complain to the queen!",
    ["Dialogue1104703"]="Yes, you are an intruder! On the bounty issued personally by the queen, it clearly indicated <color=#CA2E0AFF>the intruder is here to challenge the Archdemon!</color> I saw you fighting my Archdemon when I came home! Isn't that proof enough?",
    ["Dialogue1104704"]="It attacked me first! I was defending myself!\n(You stop them before the two can engage in a long verbal altercation.)",
    ["Dialogue1104705"]="Isn't it by your heel right now? See, isn't my Archdemon imposing and cool?",
    ["Dialogue1104706"]="<size=26>Woof!</size>\n(The dog lets out a happy bark and circles you with its tail wagging, as if expecting a reward.)",
    ["Dialogue1104801"]="We've got no time to waste, Adventurer. Since we're part of the Scouting Regiment now, we should take the opportunity to track down the Sacred Relic. You should keep the Good Samaritan in you in check. Any more requests for help, just brush it off...",
    ["Dialogue1104802"]="Boo... Boohoo...",
    ["Dialogue1104803"]="Did you not hear a word I just said? We've got more important—",
    ["Dialogue1104804"]="Wah... <size=26>Wah!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1104805"]="Fine, let's go check it out.",
    ["Dialogue1104901"]="Wah... Why didn't they believe me! Everything I said was true...!",
    ["Dialogue1104902"]="I was working by the river and saw the intruders wanted by the queen! The bounty clearly stated that they came to Niflheim because they <color=#CA2E0AFF>covet the Sacred Relic possessed by the queen</color>... But I just saw them! Two suspicious people by the Gjoll talking about sneaking into Niflheim and finding the Sacred Relic...",
    ["Dialogue1104903"]="The soldiers didn't believe me, though! They even mocked my accent!\n(He wipes the snot and tears from his face and looks even more pathetic.)\nYou're also from the Scouting Regiment, go talk to them!",
    ["Dialogue1104904"]="They're drinking in the bar across the street. They'll go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>temple</color> when they finish their shift. How can someone who is <color=#CA2E0AFF>responsible for protecting the Sacred Relic</color> refuse to believe me? Help me and we go talk to them... Wait a second, you two look familiar...",
    ["Dialogue1105001"]="You seem a little tired, Adventurer. Need a break?",
    ["Dialogue1105002"]="Not used to your current condition? You should adapt as soon as possible. I've reminded you about the pill's side effects many times. The Underworld is fraught with danger, so we must conserve ourselves.",
    ["Dialogue1105003"]="Fortunately, we didn't fight in vain. Not only did we get leads to the Sacred Relic, we also got rid of a threat who could possibly identify us.",
    ["Dialogue1105004"]="Right, he did say a group of soldiers responsible for guarding the Sacred Relic is drinking at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bar</color> and will return to the temple when their shift is over. A place like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bar</color> is noisy and crowded, perfect for <color=#CA2E0AFF>gathering information</color>. Let's go there right now.",
    ["Dialogue1105101"]="You heard what they said, right? The Sacred Relic stolen from the mortal realm is now being kept in the queen's temple. I guess that's where we're going.",
    ["Dialogue1105102"]="I know it's very dangerous, but do you have another idea? We're here, so might as well check out the temple. Don't tell me you want to leave now?",
    ["Dialogue1105103"]="Relax, we're just taking a look and will bail at the first sign of trouble. Nothing will go wrong.",
    ["Dialogue1105201"]="What's the matter, Adventurer? Not a lot of guards here. It's our chance to find the Sacred Relic.",
    ["Dialogue1105202"]="You think the scarcity of guards is a trap?",
    ["Dialogue1105203"]="No, you're overthinking it. Queen Hel is a very conceited individual. The lack of guards is exactly a reflection of that. Stop thinking and start moving. We don't have much time.",
    ["Dialogue1105301"]="(To three loud claps, a woman in a red dress emerges from the shadow for you to finally meet the legendary Hel, Queen of the Underworld.)\nI admire your courage, little rats.",
    ["Dialogue1105302"]="You dare enter Niflheim as living flesh and barge into my temple for my relic? Hmm, what's that smell...?\n(She holds up your chin and moves closer until she's only inches from your face. You can even feel her warm breath, though her beautiful face shows unbridled contempt the very next moment.)",
    ["Dialogue1105303"]="You think just because you took the Pill of Undeath, it would mask that rancid rot on you? What a joke!",
    ["Dialogue1105304"]="What's this, a rat with a backbone? Now it gets interesting.\n(Hel squints gleefully as her crimson tongue glides a full circle around her lips.)\nI just love breaking my prey's spines, then watching them squeal and beg.",
    ["Dialogue1105305"]="But you should thank me, rats! The great Queen Hel is in a good mood today and willing to afford you a chance to live... Because the Grand Celebration, the greatest event in Niflheim, is about to commence in the Undead Arena!\n(She waves her hand, and cheers erupt in the temple.)",
    ["Dialogue1105306"]="Let's party!",
    ["Dialogue1105307"]="Let's party!!!",
    ["Dialogue1105308"]="<size=26>Let's party!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1105309"]="(Hel shows contentment and raises her hand slightly to silence the noise.)\nHow about a wager, little rats?",
    ["Dialogue1105310"]="If you can survive the Grand Celebration and defeat my most fearsome warrior, I'll hand the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic back to you. You'll even have a safe return passage. However, if you fail... Heh-heh...",
    ["Dialogue1105311"]="(Hel laughs out loud as though foreseeing your loss.)\nYour souls belong to me. I shall hang you on the spire of this temple to feed my favorite pet... Naturally, to show my admiration for my guests, I'll offer you nothing but the most savage opponents!",
    ["Dialogue1105312"]="Oh, if I remember correctly, the pills have certain side effects, don't they?",
    ["Dialogue1105313"]="Stay calm, Adventurer. Don't provoke her!\n(The wizard is unexpectedly composed. He shakes his head slightly and whispers into your ear.)\nThere's nowhere for us to go right now. Keep calm and bide our time.",
    ["Dialogue1105314"]="What are you whispering about now, rats? Not that it matters, for I am an understanding queen who will tolerate your insolence. I only ask that you give me a fantastic performance.\n(She snaps her fingers casually.)",
    ["Dialogue1105315"]="Take them to the arena!",
    ["Dialogue1105401"]="Well now, it's time we bargain, Your Majesty.",
    ["Dialogue1105402"]="Bargain?\nWhat made you dregs think you could bargain with me?",
    ["Dialogue1105403"]="I might be a dreg, but not the person behind me. If the power released was a bit more potent, you would probably have to rebuild the arena.",
    ["Dialogue1105404"]="Are you threatening me, human?",
    ["Dialogue1105405"]="I wouldn't dare. It's not my intent to oppose you at all. You should know I spent a lot of effort to get this individual, the successor of Odin's bloodline, to you, even tricking this person into taking the pill that would weaken one's power. Isn't that enough to prove my sincerity?",
    ["Dialogue1105406"]="(The wizard shoots you an apathetic glance, then turns slightly to present you to Hel like a merchandise.)\nEver since Ragnarok, I know you've felt nothing but hatred for the high-and-mighty Aesir and Odin in particular, who confined you here, but...",
    ["Dialogue1105407"]="If you return the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic, I'll hand over the successor of Odin's bloodline to you, no questions asked!",
    ["Dialogue1105408"]="Shut up. I still have potions to make the pill worse for you. You wouldn't want to make this any more painful, right, Adventurer?\n(The voice behind the mask is cold and heartless, as if spoken by a different soul. You cannot comprehend how it came to this.)",
    ["Dialogue1105409"]="So, what do you think, Your Majesty?",
    ["Dialogue1105410"]="Are you kidding me? My undead soldiers already got you surrounded. I do not have the time for your nonsense...\n(Hel looks your way with unadulterated loathing in her eyes.)\nI want the Sacred Relic, and I want the successor of Odin's bloodline too.",
    ["Dialogue1105411"]="Sure, you don't have to make the deal, and I can give the successor the antidote to the pill and fight your undead army. I believe even if the successor can't beat them at full power, the losses will be catastrophic... I wonder if that's an outcome you're willing to accept, Your Majesty.",
    ["Dialogue1105412"]="<size=26>You are testing me, human!</size>\nGet them, men, and thrash them good!",
    ["Dialogue1105501"]="Interesting! <size=26>Very interesting!</size>\nI can never be bored watching you humans trying to out-plot each other!",
    ["Dialogue1105502"]="I've changed my mind, little rat. I will make the deal, since...\n(Hel grins at you with unbound joy in her eyes.)\nAny time I can humiliate someone of Odin's blood is a joyous occasion.",
    ["Dialogue1105503"]="You're directing your anger at the wrong person. You should be asking the fellow next to you. He's the one who set all this up, so maybe he is hiding something?",
    ["Dialogue1105504"]="I did lie to you, Adventurer, but I will not apologize for it.",
    ["Dialogue1105505"]="(Tatanka doesn't avoid your gaze but actually returns it.)\nWe all have our own missions in life. I know you're looking for the Earth Fragment of Ymir's Heart because you want to take it, but as the tribal wizard, I must protect the Utan tribe's Sacred Relic. That is why I used you...",
    ["Dialogue1105506"]="Correct. Ever since I knew who you are, I'd wanted to use you to get the Sacred Relic back. I faked a lot of clues and evidence just to get you to the Realm of the Dead... I'm the Utan tribal wizard. Recovering the Sacred Relic is my duty. I have no other choices.",
    ["Dialogue1105507"]="Oh, is that so?\n(Hel purposely cuts him off and turns to you with a convincing voice.)\nDon't believe him, successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue1105508"]="Think it over. How long have you known each other for him to devise such a convoluted plan and lure you into the realm with him without any doubt... Aren't you even a little suspicious of his <color=#CA2E0AFF>identity and background</color>? Don't you hate him for what he's done?",
    ["Dialogue1105509"]="Don't have to answer it now, because I'm not going to kill you at this moment. You take your time and think about it. You got time because I don't have the Sacred Relic on hand. I'm taking you somewhere to get it... But until then, if you want your <color=#CA2E0AFF>revenge</color> on him, I'll be glad to throw another Grand Celebration!",
    ["Dialogue1105510"]="Okay then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>, little rats.",
    ["Dialogue1105601"]="So, little rats, does this <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color> seem familiar to you?",
    ["Dialogue1105602"]="I don't know what you're saying.",
    ["Dialogue1105603"]="It's okay. You'll know soon enough. I'm taking you to see a very important person, after all, who has the Sacred Relic you're looking for. Who knows, you just might recall pertinent memories when you see him.",
    ["Dialogue1105604"]="Cut the absurdity. You don't scare me, Hel. We had a deal, yet you keep flip-flopping. But I've got an ace up my sleeve too. It's still uncertain who between us will have the last laugh.",
    ["Dialogue1105605"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, still obnoxious as always, you darn human!</color>\n(The annoyed Hel frowns and turns to you again.)\nThat did remind me I got to watch out for this one.",
    ["Dialogue1105606"]="You and I are the same, someone who cares only about themselves and has no bottom line. I never trusted my <color=#CA2E0AFF>fellows</color>, so before we enter the gap, make the successor take the Potent Pill of Undeath or forfeit our deal.",
    ["Dialogue1105607"]="(You notice Hel's ultimatum noticeably upsets Tatanka, yet he takes out a pill and hands it to you.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Swallow this</color>, Adventurer. Neither of us has a choice.",
    ["Dialogue1105701"]="You are my type, little rat, so much so that I almost don't want to let you go... What's the point of being a mortal, anyway? Serve me, surrender your soul to me, and I can grant you immortality as the dead. You can do anything you want in Niflheim... Isn't it a great deal?",
    ["Dialogue1105702"]="Stop delaying, Hel, I just want to recover the Sacred Relic as soon as possible. I know you're <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerless</color> outside the Realm of the Dead, which was why you made the Adventurer take the potent pill. That's as far as I go. Try anything else and I won't hold back.",
    ["Dialogue1105703"]="I see you've truly got an intriguing show for me, little rat...\nWell then, we shall see who is the lead character on this stage.",
    ["Dialogue1105801"]="May I know why you are here? The Summoning Ritual is still in preparation... Are you here to watch, Your Majesty?",
    ["Dialogue1105802"]="Oh, Hibram, you're still dense as usual. Don't you see I've brought guests?\n(Hel waves in your direction to draw Hibram's attention to you.)",
    ["Dialogue1105803"]="And they are...?",
    ["Dialogue1105804"]="Lord Hibram, please return the Sacred Relic to the Utan tribe and cease the Summoning Ritual immediately, otherwise it will be a disaster! I don't want you to regret it. There's still time... Please stop!",
    ["Dialogue1105805"]="(Tatanka's words stun and cast doubt over everyone except Hel, who scoffs and sidles up next to Hibram.)\nDo it, Hibram. You heard them. They're here to stop the ritual.",
    ["Dialogue1105806"]="I introduced them as guests only because they coerced me. These two are actually devout followers of Odin, and one of them actually has his blood. They're here to seize the last artifact I've worked so hard to get. I am weak now and cannot oppose them, so you must do it... Don't show mercy, especially to that scheming wizard of the Utan tribe.",
    ["Dialogue1105807"]="No wonder I sensed a significant presence of Odin's power... However, I won't back down even if it's a successor of his bloodline.\n(The foreign bishop raises a hand and releases a blinding ray of light that instantly binds Tatanka.)\nYou can stop the ritual over my dead body!",
    ["Dialogue1105901"]="I didn't think you'd decide to trust me, chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1105902"]="Don't give me away now! I don't want to admit it, but Hibram's enchantment trapped even me, chirp! I can barely cast Memory Materialization to get my spirit and you into Hibram's memory! But souls don't have a physical body, so...",
    ["Dialogue1105903"]="Why ask me when you know the answer, chirp?\n(It seems to be mad enough that the pumpkin leaf on its head is starting to shake.)\nThis is only temporary, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1105904"]="I'm still not acclimated with this body, so it's going to affect my speech and actions, chirp! It's called muscle memory and not something I have control over, chirp! I'll go back to the old me, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1105905"]="I've got no time to mess with you, we've got more important things to do, chirp!\n(Lude levitates slowly, and as it moves, you see the looming, mysterious <color=#CA2E0AFF>structures</color> behind it.)\nWhoa, this place is much more confusing than I expected, chirp...",
    ["Dialogue1105906"]="That's right! That means Hibram also has some inner conflicts he's hiding from others, chirp! If I'm right, they're likely related to the Summoning Ritual! Regardless of who summoned such a huge Chonchon, that person is going to get some backlash, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1105907"]="Don't interrupt me, chirp! Our priority now is to resolve Hibram's inner conflicts, then figure out a way to subdue Beelzebub. To do that, we must thoroughly explore Hibram's Memory Labyrinth just like I did with Uba!",
    ["Dialogue1105908"]="Don't worry, I'll be with you the whole time to offer timely aid and guidance, chirp! Now, forward!",
    ["Dialogue1106001"]="Before we formally enter Hibram's memory, I would like to thank you for trusting me, chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1106002"]="About the pill I gave you prior to coming through the Dimensional Gap...\nDon't you realize it wasn't the Potent Pill of Undeath but the antidote, chirp?",
    ["Dialogue1106003"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Yeah, I see the successor of Odin's bloodline is a big dummy, chirp...</color>\nAnyway, let me give you advice—never trust anyone so easily. You're going to get burned that way, chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1106004"]="Okay, we're short on time. Let's go, chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1106101"]="Recite the spirit-linking spell as before, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1106102"]="Recite the spirit-linking spell as before, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1106103"]="Don't even try, he's not going to respond, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106201"]="In this case, because the details in the target's memory got blurred, the Memory Materialization isn't working too well, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106202"]="That is very common, actually! Because human memory is akin to a big ocean, and hardly anyone will remember each drop of water in it, right? Especially for memories that are very long ago or emotionally unbearable, chirp. They will become hazier and hazier until—poof—they fade out completely, chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1106203"]="Help him remember what the \"water drop\" looks like! Didn't he want us to recite the spirit-linking spell? Just do what he said, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106204"]="\"I shall follow the oracle and turn darkness into light, chirp!\"\nNow repeat it, but without the chirp, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106301"]="(As you finish the mantra, a radiant glow lights up the orb, and an ancient, ever-changing voice can be heard.)\nHibram, my faithful servant, why have you summoned me?",
    ["Dialogue1106302"]="(You have no idea whether he could see the scene, but Hibram bows deeply to the orb.)\nGreat and powerful Ancient God, forgive me for disturbing your slumber. I implore you to enact a miracle once more, and save those wrongly banished and perished in disgrace on this deserted isle...",
    ["Dialogue1106303"]="Hibram, know that your request is most unwelcome.",
    ["Dialogue1106304"]="Please forgive my insolence, great and powerful Ancient God!\n(The bishop becomes pronated in panic, sprawling almost entirely on the ground.)",
    ["Dialogue1106305"]="Please believe me, for I am your most faithful servant! I do not question your boundless power one iota! I just can't bear seeing those innocent people die in vain... If more lives were saved before the Summoning Ritual, perhaps they would be devout followers, too, in your presence!",
    ["Dialogue1106306"]="As my faithful servant, it is your duty to summon my physical form into your world. Instead, you spend day after day pestering me with your incessant requests. I am disappointed.",
    ["Dialogue1106307"]="Please forgive me, Ancient God!",
    ["Dialogue1106308"]="Very well... For your efforts, I shall perform one final miracle.\n(The orb becomes blindingly brilliant, which you take to be the \"miracle.\")",
    ["Dialogue1106309"]="My patience wears thin, Hibram... Fail me once more and our pact shall be forfeit.",
    ["Dialogue1106310"]="My god...?!\n(Hibram looks around in panic, but the orb has dimmed with no further response.)",
    ["Dialogue1106311"]="Master! <size=26>Look at them!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1106401"]="Are you all right, master?",
    ["Dialogue1106402"]="Yes... Your work is appreciated, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1106403"]="It's my duty to protect you, but I've been wondering...\n(He turns and surveys the resurrected people of Arunafeltz all around.)\nIs this truly the miracle you've been seeking?",
    ["Dialogue1106404"]="<size=26>Israel!</size>\n(Hibram angrily cuts off the young man in white.)\nDon't show disrespect to the Ancient God, nor question his action!",
    ["Dialogue1106405"]="But these people cannot be considered living!\nI've been pondering this for several days now. They were resurrected but lost all faculty, moving like zombies and unable to communicate with normal people...",
    ["Dialogue1106406"]="See <color=#CA2E0AFF>what they've become now</color>, master... It's simply repulsive.",
    ["Dialogue1106501"]="I know you feel I'm being blasphemous, but the power of this Ancient God is rather profane. Must we allow such evil force in the world? Have we done something... wrong?",
    ["Dialogue1106502"]="Tell me, Israel, do you think that the traditions of Arunafeltz are correct and have been so since the beginning?",
    ["Dialogue1106503"]="Of course not! Using money to barter for human lives, as though a price could be placed on them... It makes me sick just thinking about it!",
    ["Dialogue1106504"]="That is the exact reason why I left Arunafeltz to search the great world outside for a mean to save our country! But I was wrong... The land of Midgard, bereft of the guidance of the gods, has become <color=#CA2E0AFF>rotten to its core!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1106505"]="Arunafeltz is not the only entity that practices placing the lives of the poor and the sinful into the hands of the ruling class. I've even witnessed far worse, far more evil rules in my travel through other countries! Humankind... has long since forgotten their reverence for the gods and their blessed creations... They only seek to indulge their selfish desires now...",
    ["Dialogue1106506"]="I've prayed to the gods countless times for their blessings and salvation, but never got a response! That forced me to turn to alien gods for aid and overturn the old ways in favor of a new order! See? I was right all along... At the very least, the Ancient God's miracles do not come at the cost of human lives.",
    ["Dialogue1106507"]="But master, ever since you were stripped of your authority and exiled to this remote island, where even the most basic of necessities cannot be guaranteed... Can't you feel the hardship?",
    ["Dialogue1106508"]="What hardship? On this island, I can prepare anything for the Summoning Ritual without concerns of discovery by the church. As for the pirates, they will serve me with just a little manipulation. I'm quite content with the situation... Are you, Israel, regretting having followed me here?",
    ["Dialogue1106509"]="No, master, I do not regret it. I only hope your sacrifice will be... <color=#CA2E0AFF>worth it</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1106601"]="Whew, that looks like the end of this segment, chirp. Notice any clue, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1106602"]="From our experience on the Nameless Island, the \"Ancient God\" entering a pact with Hibram is without a doubt Beelzebub. But from the memory, they seemed clueless about the demon's identity... Maybe they were <color=#CA2E0AFF>all fooled</color>, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106603"]="Fortunately, memory under the Memory Materialization spell would not be affected by the target's subjectivity, chirp. Even if Hibram is being hoodwinked, as long as we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>uncover clues implicating Beelzebub</color>, I can recreate the relevant scenes through this <color=#CA2E0AFF>medium</color>! However, you can see other's memory only once, so choose wisely, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106604"]="Yes! Put your hand on it, then, and let me cast the spell, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106701"]="Dull, never mind the orb! Go get fresh souls to feed Beelzebub with!",
    ["Dialogue1106702"]="Dull, never mind the orb! Go get fresh souls to feed Beelzebub with!",
    ["Dialogue1106703"]="Dull? It's that servant for Hel, right? She even mentioned Beelzebub's name, chirp!\n(The tiny spirit seems to be lost in thought, with the dangling hat just begging to be messed with.)",
    ["Dialogue1106704"]="Ahem! This is no time for horseplay! It's our opportunity to unmask Beelzebub, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1106705"]="Huh... In any case, we should do as Hel asked and collect enough soul crystals to feed Beelzebub... chirp.",
    ["Dialogue1106801"]="All these are finally filling me up... The quality of the souls here is far below ours back home, Hel.",
    ["Dialogue1106802"]="Really, ole great Beelzebub? Just look at your pathetic self now, even holding a spirit-linking spell can make you out of energy... What right have you to complain?",
    ["Dialogue1106803"]="(Hel's mocking makes Beelzebub flaps his wings and scowls.)\nIt's all because that scumbag sneak-attacked me in Ragnarok!",
    ["Dialogue1106804"]="If it weren't for that worm stabbing me in the back, I would've returned to my world along with Lord Baphomet long ago! I wouldn't have passed out, fallen, spent millennia in the rift, and couldn't even locate my body!",
    ["Dialogue1106805"]="Stop whining, Beelzebub, before you lose all dignity a demon should have. Mortals are bound by the limitations of their flesh, but so long as our souls are intact, we can easily change physical forms. Have you forgotten that your fool of a follower is creating a new body for you as we speak?",
    ["Dialogue1106806"]="If you ask me, this is actually a blessing in disguise for you. Not only did you get a devout follower, but you also gained me as a powerful ally. Didn't we have a deal? I help you find every fragment of Ymir's Heart, and in exchange, you provide me with an undead army capable of crushing the realm of Asgard! You still remember that, don't you, Beelzebub?",
    ["Dialogue1106807"]="Of course I do. It's just a matter of creating undead through plague, a piece of cake to me! However, even if I do, you can't guarantee all of the spirits will listen to you, can you? I mean, doesn't Odin like to collect the spirits of heroic warriors? It's not my problem if he beats you to it!",
    ["Dialogue1106808"]="Oh, rest assured, I got a way to deal with that... Come here, Dull. Get two goblets and fill them up with my and Beelzebub's <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1106901"]="Drink my blood, Beelzebub.",
    ["Dialogue1106902"]="Okay... Wait, <size=26>drink it?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1106903"]="Calm down, it's the blood magic of Niflheim. It lets us share each other's power.\n(Hel clinks Beelzebub's glass with hers. She gazes at the demon and smiles after a pause.)\nDon't be nervous, this is not some sort of evil soul-pact hex.",
    ["Dialogue1106904"]="That's not what I mean... Quit looking too much like the humans.\n(Beelzebub grumbles and chugs the liquid down. Hel then follows suit.)",
    ["Dialogue1106905"]="Then, from now on, when you wield your demonic plague power, my power over the undead will also work for you. Those falling to our combined might shall belong to the Realm of the Dead and serve us. You can still siphon lifeforce and I still get my undead army... It's a win-win trade. Great working with you, Beelzebub.",
    ["Dialogue1106906"]="Don't you want the Ymir's Heart anymore? That's you Aesir's most prized object...",
    ["Dialogue1106907"]="Let's not lump me in with the filthy Aesir. Do you want Ymir's Heart? Take it. As for me... I simply wish for the gods to know the pain I've felt for countless years! I've waited too, too long for my <color=#CA2E0AFF>revenge</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1107001"]="Hel and Beelzebub already teamed up long before! They teamed up to fool Hibram in order to revive Beelzebub using the Summoning Ritual and take over the entire Midgard! Chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1107002"]="We now know the ritual is an intricate ruse of Hel and Beelzebub. But we cannot hope to defeat him given our current condition, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1107003"]="We must seize the opportunity, Adventurer, and return to Hibram's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Memory Labyrinth</color> to continue searching for a way to stop Beelzebub, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1107101"]="What's wrong? You look like you got something to say to me, chirp?",
    ["Dialogue1107102"]="Why didn't I tell you before that Memory Materialization can recreate memories outside the target through <color=#CA2E0AFF>medium</color>, chirp?\nI think you know the answer, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1107103"]="That's right! I didn't want you to know too much, chirp! Everything I did before was to lure you to the Realm of the Dead. If you knew too much, that might raise suspicions! Frankly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>we didn't trust each other</color> back then, so why revisit that, chirp?",
    ["Dialogue1107104"]="You ask too many questions! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come on, got to go</color>, stop slacking around, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1107201"]="Lareia, my child... No, no, there has to be a way! The flame... There's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eternal Flame</color> on the Flame Skull! That will ensure Lareia's soul will never leave the body!",
    ["Dialogue1107202"]="I must seek it out now! I got to get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Darkness Flower</color> that lured souls in the front herbal garden!",
    ["Dialogue1107203"]="Yes, yes! Go now! Be quick!",
    ["Dialogue1107301"]="Why... Why did it not work...?",
    ["Dialogue1107302"]="Master, we...",
    ["Dialogue1107303"]="The Ancient God... The great Ancient God must have a way to save her! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take Lareia to the magic orb</color>, Israel, while I pray to the Ancient God through spirit-linking immediately!",
    ["Dialogue1107401"]="Great Ancient God, I beg you to save my child! I've exhausted all options, but Lareia is still not awake... But I know you can save her! Please!",
    ["Dialogue1107402"]="Have you forgotten, Hibram? My miracles work only on the dead. Her soul must depart before she can be resurrected.",
    ["Dialogue1107403"]="But...",
    ["Dialogue1107404"]="<size=26>How can you call yourself a god?!</size>\nLareia is one of your followers too! She is in this condition only from collecting the artifacts needed for the Summoning Ritual! How can we worship you if you can't even protect your believers?!",
    ["Dialogue1107405"]="Shut up, Israel!",
    ["Dialogue1107406"]="Please forgive his insolence, Ancient God!",
    ["Dialogue1107407"]="How bold... If you hadn't delayed the ritual repeatedly, I would be at full strength by now. Your fellows died all because of your incompetence. It has nothing to do with me.",
    ["Dialogue1107408"]="We've already scoured the land for artifacts, but none met your demand, Ancient God... It's our fault. Please lend us more guidance!",
    ["Dialogue1107409"]="We've sacrificed too much for the ritual already, master, but he has given us nothing in return! Don't you think it's unreasonable?\nFollowers make offerings for a god's miracle is the most basic tenet of sacrificial rituals! If the Summoning Ritual had no <color=#CA2E0AFF>bounds</color>, he could do anything when he arrive...",
    ["Dialogue1107410"]="<size=26>Stop, Israel!</size>\n(Hibram lands a hard slap across Israel's face. The young man falls, incredulous at his master's reaction.)",
    ["Dialogue1107411"]="Master...",
    ["Dialogue1107412"]="Please forgive... forgive us, Ancient God! <size=26>Ancient God...</size>\n(Hibram has slumped before the orb, which no longer responds to any of his plead...)",
    ["Dialogue1107501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Ouch, that was painful, chirp...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1107502"]="You saw wrong, chirp! And... And this is not the time to bring that up, chirp! Didn't you notice that when Israel mentioned the bounds of the ritual, Beelzebub became quiet immediately as if it hit a sore spot, chirp!",
    ["Dialogue1107503"]="Yes, I want to use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>orb</color> as the medium to scan Beelzebub's memory, chirp! Maybe the so-called <color=#CA2E0AFF>bound</color> is the key to subduing Beelzebub!",
    ["Dialogue1107601"]="What, so weak you can't even speak now?\nThe Glorious Ancient God Beelzebub, how terrible are your followers going to feel if they could see you now...",
    ["Dialogue1107602"]="Stop pestering me, I got serious business to think about!",
    ["Dialogue1107603"]="What serious business can you be pondering other than hunger? Fine, <color=#CA2E0AFF>shut off the orb</color> for him, Dull, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> some fresh <color=#CA2E0AFF>soul crystals</color> to feed our Lord Beelzebub here.",
    ["Dialogue1107701"]="<size=26>I said stop pestering me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1107702"]="What crawled up your ass and died, Beelzebub!",
    ["Dialogue1107703"]="How can you be in the mood for food? <size=26>We're about done for!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1107704"]="What do you mean by \"done for\"? Quit being cryptic!\nSpill the beans!",
    ["Dialogue1107705"]="It's what Hibram's best pupil said... He reminded me that the pact made through the ritual has <color=#CA2E0AFF>conditions</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1107706"]="If Hibram performed the summon as agreed to and reforge a physical body for me, I cannot harm him in any way, and I also must...\n(Beelzebub glances at Hel with both caution and guilt.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Fulfill a wish or order for him...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1107707"]="Why you...!\nHow can you not bring it up till now!",
    ["Dialogue1107708"]="Well, I was in a coma for a thousand years, so it's natural I couldn't remember it! Rather than scolding me, why don't we concentrate on solving the problem? If Hibram realizes we've tricked him when the ritual is done, will he, uh...",
    ["Dialogue1107709"]="Thanks for telling me now! Fine, let me think...\n(Hel bites her lip and paces back and forth. Several turns later, her eyes light up.)",
    ["Dialogue1107710"]="I got it! When you get a chance, tell Hibram, in order to get the final artifact for the ritual, he must work with the Queen of the Underworld, then get him to open the dimensional gap between Niflheim and Midgard... And I'll take care of the rest.",
    ["Dialogue1107801"]="Whoa, that's a beautiful fragment. It seems the key to defeating Beelzebub is still Hibram.",
    ["Dialogue1107802"]="(The Lude glowers at you, though it's hardly intimidating due to his comical appearance.)\nI told you, I'll get used to this body in time! Make fun of me at your own risk!",
    ["Dialogue1107803"]="Now stop fooling around. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Hibram's Memory Labyrinth</color> and figure out our next step!",
    ["Dialogue1107901"]="In the prior memory, Adventurer, we learned the ritual came with <color=#CA2E0AFF>bounds</color>. Beelzebub cannot harm Hibram and must fulfill a wish. That may be our only chance to beat Beelzebub. However, Hibram has lost his soul...",
    ["Dialogue1107902"]="We'll have to keep exploring the Memory Labyrinth and resolve Hibram's <color=#CA2E0AFF>inner conflict</color> for him to give order to Beelzebub of his own volition. Remember what I did to reawake Uba? It's the same here. We must keep digging into the painful memory Hibram wanted to forget until we find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Key</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1107903"]="Then, you must insert the key in the deepest part of the memory to free the real Hibram.",
    ["Dialogue1107904"]="You want to know how come Hibram's soul left his body after the ritual and became Hel's puppet?\n(Lude shakes his head and gives a replay as ambiguous as his demeanor. It dawns on you that maybe he has his own <color=#CA2E0AFF>inner conflict</color>.)\nThe answer to that is in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>certain segment of Hibram's memory</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1107905"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Let's continue onward</color>, Adventurer. Everything should be clear soon.",
    ["Dialogue1108001"]="Maybe I don't need to take the Pill of Undeath, master...",
    ["Dialogue1108002"]="You must, Israel. It's taboo for living flesh like us to enter Niflheim. Without the pill to mask our lifeforce, we'd probably become undead before we even see the queen.",
    ["Dialogue1108003"]="But the pill's side effects cannot be eliminated. Niflheim is fraught with danger and monsters. Someone must be here to protect you. Please listen to me this once, master. If we run into trouble, I'll stay behind and cover you. Seize the opportunity and go to Hel's temple, please.",
    ["Dialogue1108004"]="What do you think you're doing, Israel? Do not do anything stupid!\nI've already lost Lareia, I can't lose you too!",
    ["Dialogue1108005"]="Countless people have died for the cause is exactly why we can't quit right now. You must complete the task, master.\n(Israel bows to Hibram with admiration and reverence.)",
    ["Dialogue1108006"]="Ah... Okay. I'm counting on you, then, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1108101"]="Humans? Interesting. It's been ages since Niflheim has seen living, breathing mortals...\nTell me, what is it that you want from me?",
    ["Dialogue1108102"]="Your Majesty, we are faithful followers of the Ancient God, here to seek your assistance per his directions. For the great Ancient God to descend upon Midgard and reshape the corrupt world, I am preparing an important Summoning Ritual. Alas, I have made no progress on the final artifact needed to commence the ceremony...",
    ["Dialogue1108103"]="(Hel listens to Hibram with great interest.)\nOh? Artifact to summon the Ancient God from Otherworld?",
    ["Dialogue1108104"]="From what you described, it should be something with formidable elemental power that could counterbalance the other artifacts. By sheer coincidence, I know of such an item that met those requirements. It will not be difficult for me to get it, either... Okay, I will help.",
    ["Dialogue1108105"]="Thank you very much!\nThe Ancient God was right, you can help us locate the final artifact!",
    ["Dialogue1108106"]="Excuse me, Lady Hel... Of course we're grateful for your assistance, but pardon my caution, as summoning an alien god is no trivial matter... I would like to know why you decided to help us unconditionally?",
    ["Dialogue1108107"]="Unconditionally? Ah, young man... How very naive of you to think I want nothing in exchange.\nThe truth is, I decided to help because I want to see what the new world that you mentioned will look like.",
    ["Dialogue1108108"]="I'm sure you're not strangers to the story of Hel, Queen of the Underworld. Born an illegitimate daughter of Loki, she was ostracized by the gods for her frost giant blood. Odin banished her to the Realm of the Dead, as well as killing her father and two older brothers during Ragnarok...",
    ["Dialogue1108109"]="Yet what you humans may not know is that Odin also inflicted an even more vile punishment on her...\n(Hel pauses, turns, and lifts her long hair to show the slender neck underneath.)\nThis mark was the curse Odin gave to me himself.",
    ["Dialogue1108201"]="This mark prevented me from ever leaving the dark bowel of the Underworld. I have all but forgotten the warmth of the sun... If your god is able to descend and remake the law and order of this world, probably there is a chance I may be reborn. Surely... there is a chance that I can be reborn.",
    ["Dialogue1108202"]="Tell me, Hibram.\n(Hel gazes into Hibram's eyes with the sincerity of a disciple seeking the truth.)\nWill your god save me?",
    ["Dialogue1108203"]="My god would never abandon anyone in the midst of suffering. I promise you, Lady Hel, when the ritual succeeds, I will ask the Ancient God to free you from your...",
    ["Dialogue1108204"]="Wait a second, master!\n(Israel's shout interrupts Hibram. Hel's words have not convinced him one bit as he continues to greet her with caution.)",
    ["Dialogue1108205"]="Lady Hel, I am terribly sorry about your suffering, but you have not told us, what is the price for you retrieving the final artifact?",
    ["Dialogue1108206"]="Ah, Hibram, I guess this student of yours holds a bias against me.",
    ["Dialogue1108207"]="Apologies, Lady Hel. Israel has always been by-the-book and didn't mean to offend you. Please pardon his insolence.",
    ["Dialogue1108208"]="(Hel waves casually, apparently letting Israel's aggression slide.)\nThere is nothing there to pardon, not to mention he's right in showing concerns. I'm not charitable, so of course I seek an equal return in getting the Sacred Relic for you.",
    ["Dialogue1108209"]="Hibram, in order to acquire the artifact... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Your soul</color> would be the cost.",
    ["Dialogue1108210"]="Why you...!",
    ["Dialogue1108211"]="Let me finish, young man.\nThe artifact you need is beyond extraordinary. It is a Sacred Relic guarded by the power of Yggdrasil. My undead army and I have suffered greatly in retrieving it...",
    ["Dialogue1108212"]="I will need a powerful, pious soul to replenish my strength, and you, Hibram, are the perfect candidate. The soul of a divine servant possesses magic power many folds of an ordinary man—because of the blessings they receive from god. I will get the Sacred Relic for you, if you agree to sign a soul contract. When the ritual is complete, your soul will belong to me.",
    ["Dialogue1108213"]="Does this mean I will not see the birth of a new world...?",
    ["Dialogue1108214"]="Tell me, which do you think matters more: Witnessing the birth of a new world... Or handing over a perfect world to future generations so that they, in turn, can continue passing it down to their descendants? To me, human lives are all too short, less than a blink of an eye on the cosmic scale. But if you are able to manage such a great feat, your name will forever be etched in history.",
    ["Dialogue1108215"]="No rush, I can give you all the time you need to think it over. However...\n(Hel looks at Hibram with both a glint and veiled threat in her eyes.)\nI wonder how long can your Ancient God wait?",
    ["Dialogue1108301"]="What's the matter, Adventurer? Why are you staring at me like that?",
    ["Dialogue1108302"]="Hold on, Adventurer. No matter what you're about to say, I must remind you that we're not done yet, so don't focus on anything insignificant. What you should do now is to look for something that could...",
    ["Dialogue1108303"]="What are you doing, Adventurer?!",
    ["Dialogue1108401"]="Is this correspondence from the master? I must read it.",
    ["Dialogue1108501"]="How did you become like this, master...",
    ["Dialogue1108502"]="Those who achieve great deeds are not concerned with minorities? That is exactly what the priests defrauding normal people for money on behalf of the nobles and churches said! Isn't that why you left Arunafeltz, because you couldn't tolerate such behavior?",
    ["Dialogue1108503"]="The master has lost his way now. What's the point of a new world built on others' sacrifices?! How is that different from nobles leeching on the common folks? No, I can't stand for it, and I won't let the master go through with it!",
    ["Dialogue1108504"]="Preventing Hel from seizing the Utan relic will stop the Summoning Ritual, but I'm no match for the Queen of the Underworld. What can I do...?",
    ["Dialogue1108505"]="If only someone was willing to help... Wait, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Utan wizard!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1108601"]="If I remember correctly, this should be the guardian of the Utan relic.",
    ["Dialogue1108602"]="He seems unfamiliar to the outside world... Why is everyone here like that, too? They toiled in primitive labor, yet felt no hardship, nor caution for outsiders. Whatever I asked, even regarding the secrets of their relic, they answered me without reservation, when I obviously have designs on the relic.",
    ["Dialogue1108603"]="How can they hope to protect the Sacred Relic from the devious Queen of the Underworld? Is there anything I can do to help them?",
    ["Dialogue1108604"]="No, that won't work. I have no evidence. Just my words aren't convincing enough. I must seek another way...",
    ["Dialogue1108605"]="Yes, this man is the wizard of Utan, the messenger of Yggdrasil's will. No one in this rainforest can defy him. If I impersonate him, I can use the Utans to stop Hel's scheme!",
    ["Dialogue1108606"]="Sorry, Tatanka, I need to borrow your body in the interim, though I promise you I'll do my best to keep your Sacred Relic safe.",
    ["Dialogue1108701"]="You always surprise me. You're the successor of Odin's bloodline for a reason.",
    ["Dialogue1108702"]="You guessed correctly. <color=#CA2E0AFF>I am Israel.</color> But now is not the time to explain everything to you.",
    ["Dialogue1108703"]="See, the key to revealing the truth has availed itself. Pick it up now, then save my master. This is my final request, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1108801"]="See that figure over there? That is my master... The <color=#CA2E0AFF>true spirit of Hibram.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1108802"]="Those chains represent the emotional conflicts imprisoning him. The surrounding undead are probably guarding him as per his soul contract with Hel. If we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat the undead</color> and free him from the chains, his soul will return to his body.",
    ["Dialogue1108901"]="Why are you stopping, Adventurer? Why aren't you freeing my master?",
    ["Dialogue1108902"]="No, I'm not fit for this. If possible, I would rather you lead my master out of the predicament for me.",
    ["Dialogue1108903"]="(Lude stops you mid-sentence with a wave. He lowers his head, but you can tell he's bowing to you.)\nPlease, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1109001"]="What are you...? Who am I...? What happened to me...?",
    ["Dialogue1109002"]="Running? No, I wasn't running from anything. It was because...",
    ["Dialogue1109003"]="Attitude... My attitude?\n(Focus gradually unglazes Hibram's eyes as inner turmoil at last turn into tears.)\nYes... How did I become like this?",
    ["Dialogue1109004"]="Ritual... The truth? No, my Ancient God would never abandon his faithful...\n(Regardless of what you say, Hibram repeats the same line over and over. Apparently, you have not broken through to him yet...)",
    ["Dialogue1109005"]="I thought I was different from the corrupt nobles in Arunafeltz. I wanted to change the world and be the savior... But in the end, like them, I was sacrificing others to attain my own desire... How despicable... I took refuge here, yet longed for redemption...",
    ["Dialogue1109006"]="Thank you for finding me, stranger. May I know your name? I should at least remember my savior...",
    ["Dialogue1109007"]="Israel? My student? You mean he didn't forsake me but wants to save me?",
    ["Dialogue1109008"]="(Hibram's pale face reacts to your account with hope. He lets out a long sigh as if he's made up his mind.)\nObsessions do pervert a person. I not only failed as a master but also put my student in such a precarious position... Fortunately, it's still not too late.",
    ["Dialogue1109009"]="How I can squander the opportunity you and Israel have fought so hard for? Come, it's time... <color=#CA2E0AFF>to end all of this</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1109101"]="I'm sorry, Israel, for everything I put you through.",
    ["Dialogue1109102"]="I'm not fit for your apologies, master... I <color=#CA2E0AFF>didn't accomplish anything</color>, not even protecting your life... \n(The young man's eyes are slightly red. Perhaps he's still a child before his master.)",
    ["Dialogue1109103"]="Don't cry, Israel. We've not seen each other in so long, so tell me how you feel since. The Adventurer told me what you did, but I worried about you every day since you left Nameless Island...",
    ["Dialogue1109104"]="I know you didn't come to wake me personally because you still got your own <color=#CA2E0AFF>inner conflict</color> to resolve. You have the perfect example of a desire gone awry right before your eyes, Israel. Now let me do my duty as the master one last time, and tell me what happened to you?",
    ["Dialogue1109105"]="It wasn't my intent to deceive you, master. I impersonated the Utan wizard to retain their Sacred Relic but failed. Hel was much too fearsome and powerful. Even combining the might of the entire tribe in my guise as the wizard was futile...",
    ["Dialogue1109106"]="After the Sacred Relic was taken, I knew I couldn't stop the ritual... It also meant I couldn't prevent your demise. I didn't want to return to the island to witness your passing, so I chose to stay in Umbala and slow the disasters in the rainforest, until...",
    ["Dialogue1109107"]="Yes, Adventurer. Your presence represented a turning point. I knew Hel loathed Odin, so if I could get you to her before the ritual was completed, she would be willing to trade the relic for your life! Then I could save my master... But that was the very notion plunging me deeper into the abyss...",
    ["Dialogue1109108"]="(Israel chuckles wryly.)\nMust you always be so kind, Adventurer? Do you see what's in my hand?",
    ["Dialogue1109201"]="You were serious?!",
    ["Dialogue1109202"]="Yes. Before setting foot in Niflheim, I was determined to trade you for the Sacred Relic and my master's life. But when Hel called me a kindred spirit, that made me pause. I realized just how far off I had strayed, and how scared I am of whom I became...",
    ["Dialogue1109203"]="That moment of hesitation made me switch out the pill I offered to the Adventurer. But truthfully, that wasn't the antidote, either. \n(Israel looks at you with unfathomable admiration.)\nYou were able to recover probably because... You truly are powerful.",
    ["Dialogue1109204"]="You trust me? But why...?",
    ["Dialogue1109205"]="They... they thought of me as their benefactor? You felt someone who would do anything to save the people of Umbala could never be truly evil?\n(Puzzled Israel seems unable to fully believe your words and turns to his master for confirmation.)\nMaster...",
    ["Dialogue1109206"]="Let me ask you, Israel. Do you think Hel's sins are forgivable?",
    ["Dialogue1109207"]="No, of course not. She suffered injustice, yes, but that cannot justify her wanton killings. If she is innocent, what does that make the lives she murdered?",
    ["Dialogue1109208"]="Then by your logic, I'm irredeemable as well. I tried to fulfill my private goal under the pretense of changing the world, yet you still chose to save me... So, why can't Hel receive the same chance?",
    ["Dialogue1109209"]="I believe to this date that when I entered the pact with Hel, not everything she said was a lie. She craved forgiveness and redemption, but no one tried to pull her out of the abyss. Didn't she say to you she doesn't trust her own kind? Maybe what she loathed is herself.",
    ["Dialogue1109210"]="I am not making excuses for Hel, Israel. I just want to say you should be given the opportunity to forgive as well. If you still blame yourself for not saving me, try to redeem yourself. Channel the guilt into motivation for finishing what I couldn't. Won't that allow you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>forgive yourself</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1109211"]="(Even though physical contact is impossible, Hibram still puts a hand gently on his student's shoulder.)\nYou were never a disappointment. You are my pride, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1109212"]="Thank you, master... \n(The young man in white dips his head and covers his face. You realize the burden has finally been lifted from him.)",
    ["Dialogue1109213"]="All right... Lastly, let me <color=#CA2E0AFF>take you back</color>.\nFarewell, successor of Odin's bloodline. Thank you for everything you did...",
    ["Dialogue1109301"]="You're back?! What happened to you? \n(The lord surveys unmasked Israel in shock.)\nAre you Tatanka...?",
    ["Dialogue1109302"]="No, and I'm sorry to deceive you. My name is Israel. I've been impersonating your wizard recently...\n(He hands the shattered mask to the lord before coming clean on everything he did.)\nI don't have any right to beg for your forgiveness, but if there's anything I can do...",
    ["Dialogue1109303"]="So since the Sacred Relic was lost? Just answer me this, Israel... Do you really hate the Crunchy Cocoons?",
    ["Dialogue1109304"]="(That has you and Israel doing a double-take.)\nUh, what? Oh, yeah, I really... detest bugs.",
    ["Dialogue1109305"]="Heh, that figured. Ever since then... \n(The chef rubs the feather on the mask and starts laughing unexpectedly.)\nTali would come to me often and complain you didn't want her Crunchy Cocoons anymore.",
    ["Dialogue1109306"]="Is that when you knew I wasn't Tatanka?",
    ["Dialogue1109307"]="I wasn't sure, but had a gut feeling. You impersonated well, but no matter how you came off, your true beliefs would always give you away. Tatanka is a devout believer fully dedicated to Yggdrasil, but you... I'm guessing you much prefer mastering your own destiny, right?",
    ["Dialogue1109308"]="I'm not blaming you. I saw everything you did for Umbala, and what I said before your trip to the Realm of the Dead—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Come back safely</color>, was coming from the heart. As for the Sacred Relic... Did you find it? Can I see it?",
    ["Dialogue1109309"]="Yes, this is the Sacred Relic of the Utan tribe.\n(The lord examines the Earth Fragment of Ymir's Heart in his hand, smiles, and returns it to you.)\nIt's yours now, successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue1109310"]="(The change in the lord's attitude since you've been back in Umbala is rather inexplicable, prompting you to get an explanation.)\nThe reason for letting you take the Sacred Relic is simple, Adventurer. Whether you believe it or not, I saw you a long, long time ago.",
    ["Dialogue1109311"]="By now, you should have witnessed the prophetic powers of Mirror Lake Water. When I was young, I had a similar encounter. That was the time the lake showed me a vision of <color=#CA2E0AFF>you fighting to protect the Sacred Relic</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1109312"]="But I was young and naive then, and couldn't understand the vision except that, one day, the Sacred Relic would be threatened. The thought worried me to no end, even spurring the notion to change the future. But my father warned me that it was destiny, for no matter what I did, the prophecy would come true in the end.",
    ["Dialogue1109313"]="From the moment I saw you, I knew you were here to take the Sacred Relic. I mulled over stopping you, but I'm glad I didn't do it, since Umbala will not perish even without the relic. Both the Spirit Tree and Uba made it, so the Utan tribe shall not concede defeat.",
    ["Dialogue1109314"]="So, Israel, mind giving Tatanka back to us? He is our wizard, and there are many things waiting for him to do.\nOr would you rather do his work for a few more days? I wouldn't mind that, either!",
    ["Dialogue1109315"]="Allow me to decline, lord. I will escort Tatanka back myself later. He is safe, and having a very nice dream for the moment.\n(Perhaps Karkatan rubbed off on Israel, because he finally smiles in relief.)",
    ["Dialogue1109316"]="I've decided to wander the land and see the sights my master saw, walk the roads he walked... Then I believe I'll find my own way to save the world. That is my master's wish and now mine, too.",
    ["Dialogue1109317"]="Ah, very well. Maybe it's time we say goodbye.\nIsrael, and successor of Odin's bloodline, I hope one day when we meet again, we all have what we sought.",
    ["Dialogue1109401"]="The successor of Odin's bloodline, I am proud of you for how you handled the arduous journey.",
    ["Dialogue1109402"]="(The goddess nods slightly.)\nYes, Ymir's Heart has finally returned after a thousand years. Odin's might shall be sealed here and never be misused again. You are responsible for all this.",
    ["Dialogue1109403"]="However, I still have one concern, for I can still perceive signs of a force similar to Ymir's Heart somewhere in the land. They are far away and scattered, but enormous in quantity...",
    ["Dialogue1109404"]="(The goddess grows more somber from your description.)\nMirror Lake? Its water originated from the Well of Urd, and what it prophesied, came true with no exception. If that is the case, perhaps your quest is far from over.",
    ["Dialogue1109405"]="Unfortunately, I am unable to aid you any longer. To preserve Ymir's Heart, I will soon fall into a deep slumber alongside it... Your destiny is now in your own hands henceforth, the successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue1109406"]="But I believe in you. You surely will find the path to the truth...\n(The goddess and her voice fade, but you understand that your story is just beginning...)",
    ["Dialogue1109501"]="(In the clear water, you see crystals of all sizes in the river. Some contained dragonfly larvae within like a precious amber.)",
    ["Dialogue1109601"]="(The lovely shell sinks to cause a ripple before the surface returns to calm.)",
    ["Dialogue1109701"]="(Blood sips into the water and spreads like crimson smoke, but nothing else happens.)",
    ["Dialogue1109801"]="(The container suddenly radiates in a bright glow, as <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient scripts</color> appear in the water like a scroll unfolding.)",
    ["Dialogue1109901"]="(The cloth coming into contact with the Radiant Compound Eyes emits a brilliant glow, as <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient scripts</color> manifest like a scroll unfolding.)",
    ["Dialogue1110001"]="(A large lot of vegetation fell to the ground unnaturally, and mysterious black veins pervaded their leaves, causing them to turn to ash when touched.)",
    ["Dialogue1110101"]="(A large number of Beetle Kings throw haphazardly into a sack, all of them dead...)",
    ["Dialogue1110201"]="(The rocks are covered in messy scratch marks, each dug deep into the surface. What has the raw power to do this?)",
    ["Dialogue1110301"]="(Huge depressions of different shades can be seen throughout the ground, as if hit by a heavy object.)",
    ["Dialogue1110401"]="(The stake has been scratched beyond recognition, with a bunch of wood dust scattering about the proximity...)",
    ["Dialogue1110501"]="(The firefly-like glow levitates in the glass jar, interestingly alternating between dim and bright. You get closer to examine it, but it suddenly turns into a hideous face and rushes right at you... until it crashes into the glass wall with a loud thud.)",
    ["Dialogue1110601"]="(You recite the incantation as Tatanka instructed. The orb glows and alternates between dim and bright as if breathing...)",
    ["Dialogue1110701"]="(He stares at you blankly, his whole body exuding a wretched smell, as if he was a freshly exhumed corpse...)",
    ["Dialogue1110801"]="(She stares at you blankly, her whole body exuding a wretched smell, as if she was a freshly exhumed corpse...)",
    ["Dialogue1110901"]="(The unusually fragrant flower is put under the girl's nose, yet her breath is still fading.)",
    ["Dialogue1111001"]="(The bright soul fire flickers between her brows, yet it's still unable to join her body...)",
    ["Dialogue1111101"]="(On the back of Hel's neck is an elegant mark of three inverse, interlocking triangles without a beginning or end, like an endless cycle...)",
    ["Dialogue1111201"]="(The black pill gives off an intense scent of the dead. It's even more intense than the Pill of Undeath you took.)",
    ["Dialogue1111301"]="Chug, chug, chug... Ah! Awesome!\nIf you ask me, nothing beats our Niflheim booze! The crappy libations that humans consume are as plain as water! And expensive, too!",
    ["Dialogue1111302"]="Uh, we're still on the clock... Isn't skipping the post and drinking a little too much?",
    ["Dialogue1111303"]="You're too drunk to even stand, and you got the gall to lecture me? Not to mention the temple is so crowded, the two of us won't be missed! No one will notice!",
    ["Dialogue1111304"]="Belch! Again, only the queen's two servants know where that Sacred Relic from the mortal realm is, since they stole it personally. Oh, that reminds me, I just saw them having a rendezvous on the ice bridge! They would make a lovely couple, I think!",
    ["Dialogue1111401"]="Hey, it's getting chilly. Should we call it early?",
    ["Dialogue1111402"]="Nah, didn't the queen tell us to take some time off, anyway? You must be tired from guarding the temple for so long.",
    ["Dialogue1111403"]="But we went through a lot to get that thing and I don't feel safe without my eyes on it...",
    ["Dialogue1111404"]="Relax, the temple is heavily defended and the safest place for the Sacred Relic. Now stop worrying and take a break with me.",
    ["Dialogue1120101"]="Pleasure! The successor of Odin's bloodline, I am expecting you for a while.",
    ["Dialogue1120102"]="I apologize for inviting you like this. My full name is Philodis, and I am a cabinet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Minister</color> in Lord's Mansion of the Schwarzwald Republic. I am commissioned by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Carl</color> to come here to ask for your help.",
    ["Dialogue1120103"]="I know, it is a serious violation of the diplomatic protocol to reach out to you under the table. If time allows, we surely hope to meet with you on a more formal occasion, welcoming the arrival of the successor of Odin's bloodline. But time is of the essence, and we hope you understand our difficulty.",
    ["Dialogue1120104"]="(Philodis waves his hand, and a letter sealed with golden red wax is handed to you.)\nAs for the commission details, Lord Carl has written all in this <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret letter</color>... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>read it carefully</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1120201"]="...That should be it. The Lord has included the reason and the detail of the commission in the letter. I will fill you in on more details when we get to Juno. Our priority is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Juno as soon as possible</color>. I am worried sick that things in the city might go wrong while I am not there.",
    ["Dialogue1120202"]="Enough talk. Let's go see the clerk of Kafra Corporation. As I recall, her name is... <color=#CA2E0AFF>W</color> or something?",
    ["Dialogue1120203"]="Okay then. Please lead the way, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1120301"]="Minister Philodis, why are you here?\n<color=#A1979FFF>It's weird… The Kafra's system didn't receive any messages...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1120302"]="Let's cut to the chase, W. The Lord orders me to come here to invite the successor of Odin's bloodline to the Republic, in an attempt to cope with the recent spate of android riots. Now, we need to use the Emergency Teleport Route from Kafra Corporation to return to Juno with the Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1120303"]="Eh... But to go to the Republic, we must follow the protocol and obtain permission, then take Rekenber's airship there.\n(W seems troubled and peeks at you secretly.)\nKafra's teleport route can only...",
    ["Dialogue1120304"]="I know the drill. Per the rule, Kafra Corporation's Emergency Teleport Route is only open for use during wartime. But don't you forget that this is the order assigned by Lord Carl himself. Are you... telling me that you refuse to follow the Lord's order?",
    ["Dialogue1120305"]="Th-That's not what I mean... Fine. Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>place your hand</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mobile terminal</color> on this side, and the system will verify your identity. Once everything is verified, I can activate Kafra's Emergency Teleport Route for you.",
    ["Dialogue1120401"]="How is this possible... I remember you went to Al De Baran using the pass before.",
    ["Dialogue1120402"]="Then how come the database in the Republic's system doesn't contain your information? Could it be a system malfunction? Hmm, if this is the case...",
    ["Dialogue1120403"]="(Something rings a bell in W, and she lifts her hand toward the mobile terminal.)\nHa! Taylin told me if something acts up, you only need to hit it hard a few times like this...",
    ["Dialogue1120404"]="This is unnecessary, W. The identity information won't be a problem, and I dare anyone to fake the identity of the successor of Odin's bloodline. Open the teleport route quickly and send us back to Juno.",
    ["Dialogue1120405"]="Eh... um...?\nAt least let me reenter the identity information for the Adventurer—",
    ["Dialogue1120406"]="...Like I said, this is unnecessary.\n(Philodis sounds cold and indifferent. His sharp glare, through the glasses he's wearing, falls upon W.)\nDon't make me repeat myself, W.",
    ["Dialogue1120407"]="...Y-Yes, sir. I am on it, Minister Philodis.\nSo, <color=#CA2E0AFF>please get ready</color>... I am about to open Kafra's Emergency Teleport Route for you.",
    ["Dialogue1120501"]="Never thought I would have the opportunity to introduce you to my hometown this quick.",
    ["Dialogue1120502"]="Hehe, surprise! Isn't it? This is Juno, Adventurer. The City of Sage. An airborne city!",
    ["Dialogue1120503"]="About four hundred years ago, there was a history-changing technological revolution in the Schwarzwald Republic. We called it the \"1st Technological Leap.\" With the technological development from the revolution, the Republic became the most advanced country on the continent. And this magnificent \"City of Sky\" is one of the results that have been passed down from that moment...",
    ["Dialogue1120504"]="Ah-Ah! I knew it! You want to ask, how Juno flies in the air, right?\n(W sticks out her chest proudly.)\nActually, it is because...",
    ["Dialogue1120505"]="...Okay, I think that's enough for the topic.",
    ["Dialogue1120506"]="At the moment, we won't be able to predict when those androids will lose control again. So to minimize the damage... I want you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Republic Guard Headquarters</color>, learn the incident details from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre, Chief of the Armed Forces</color>, and assist him to deal with any potential crisis. Once everything is settled, I will personally give you a tour of this magical city, \"the City of Sky.\"",
    ["Dialogue1120507"]="So... I will now head back to Lord's Mansion and report to Lord Carl. I will meet with you after I am done with everything, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1120601"]="I've been hearing things about you, the successor of Odin's bloodline. I'm Andre, Chief of the Republic Armed Forces. Now I'm in charge of this android riot incident. I can answer any questions you have.",
    ["Dialogue1120602"]="I see... You are not from the Schwarzwald Republic, so you don't quite understand their background. That's fine. I will briefly walk you through this. It will help you understand the Republic's current situation.",
    ["Dialogue1120603"]="First and foremost, I believe you should've known that by now, as the most technologically advanced nation in Midgard, the Republic's mechanical engineering development has reached another milestone after going through two Technological Leaps. The android industry, the most iconic advancement, is now a jewel on the crown.",
    ["Dialogue1120604"]="In today's Juno, a massive number of androids are in active service throughout many different fields, especially the <color=#CA2E0AFF>popular civilian androids</color>. Research data indicates that over 85% of citizens own a civilian android...",
    ["Dialogue1120605"]="You are smart, Adventurer. That's right. It's exactly because these androids have already blended into our daily life that the riot could have such severe impact. However, during the riot suppression, I discovered <color=#CA2E0AFF>a pattern</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1120606"]="Chief Andre! Bad news!",
    ["Dialogue1120607"]="We just received reports that another riot has broken out at the garden on Central Plaza! The number of uncontrollable androids involved this time is more than anything we have ever seen. Squad two is about to lose their ground!",
    ["Dialogue1120608"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Tsk! Speak of the devil...</color>\nLooks like we don't have time to get into the details. Now follow me, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1120701"]="Way to go, Adventurer. The riot won't be settled this quick without your help.",
    ["Dialogue1120702"]="Yes, there have been dozens of riots in Juno like this since last month. What makes it even more frightening is, the number and frequency of civilian androids losing control are increasing, which costs us a considerable amount of the labor force to fix the problem. If we can't solve it from the root, I'm afraid that Juno's security system will fall apart very soon...",
    ["Dialogue1120703"]="Yes, I did find a pattern out of all these riots—those androids that went out of control. They were all developed by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Khayr Consortium</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1120704"]="It's the leading consortium in the Republic that owns the most advanced android technology. Cooperating with Rekenber Corporation, Khayr Consortium has monopolized the android industries in the country. Suppose all the androids developed by the company lose control at the same time... it will be a devastating disaster to the Schwarzwald Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1120705"]="But clues like this are just my wild guess. To settle this riot... we must hurry up and gather more intel.",
    ["Dialogue1120706"]="Did you say you want to speak with those citizens involved in this riot? That should be alright. But I suggest you make some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Calming Tea</color> by using <color=#CA2E0AFF>Floral Tree Seed</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Snowmelt Water</color>. It will help calm them down before you ask them any questions.",
    ["Dialogue1120801"]="You helped me again, cough cough... I don't know how to pay you back, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1120802"]="Thanks for your Calming Tea. I feel much calmer right now. Just now, if you didn't save me from Angelica... cough cough...",
    ["Dialogue1120803"]="That would be the android who attacked me... Three years ago, I bought Angelica from Rekenber Corp's android exhibition. She has stayed with me ever since...",
    ["Dialogue1120804"]="No... not even once. Angelica <color=#CA2E0AFF>always behaves very well</color>, and I've never thought she would do something to harm me...\n(He looks at the white-haired android lying on the ground.)\nMust be an error somewhere...",
    ["Dialogue1120805"]="Destroy Angelica?!",
    ["Dialogue1120806"]="No way! This will not happen!\nTo me, Angelica is the most important partner! I will never do this to her!",
    ["Dialogue1120807"]="Cut your nonsense! Even though you saved my life, I will not let you do harm to Angelica!\n(He spreads his arms and protects his android from you, like a guardian.)\nThat's enough talk! Get lost!",
    ["Dialogue1120901"]="Hey! What's popping, hero!",
    ["Dialogue1120902"]="I saw everything! You saved the young man who almost got strangled to death by the android, right? Like this... Heh!\n(She imitates your action and throws a cool-looking jab.)\nThis is awesome!",
    ["Dialogue1120903"]="Not only are you good at fighting, but you also work with the guards seamlessly! Right, are you helping them to investigate the riot?\n(The girl grabs you by the arm and looks excited.)\nAsk me about it! I am the witness!",
    ["Dialogue1120904"]="Was there anything weird going on? Let me think... Well, I was passing by this garden at that moment, and I heard a lot of people screaming. Soon after, those androids started to attack humans hysterically... The thing I found strange was that their actions were in-sync, like someone had <color=#CA2E0AFF>pressed the switch</color> and activated them!",
    ["Dialogue1120905"]="Besides this, I couldn't think of anything special... Do you find this helpful, hero?",
    ["Dialogue1121001"]="You... You are the one just now...?",
    ["Dialogue1121002"]="It's fine... I'm holding up all right. If it wasn't because of you... I guess I'm going to kick the bucket here today.",
    ["Dialogue1121003"]="Do you mean the riot just now? My android was helping me to take a stroll here, but somehow he started to attack me for no reason. There were other people nearby who had been attacked by their androids the same way. It wouldn't quit no matter how I begged him... Ouch, it hurts really bad...\n<color=#A1979FFF>Sigh, I shouldn't trust an ice-cold machine after all... If Lily was there...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1121101"]="You're back, Adventurer. Did you find anything?",
    ["Dialogue1121102"]="...According to citizens' testimony, there weren't any signs or warnings before the riot, and those androids have never had any error before. All of them suddenly went out of control and wouldn't take any command from their master...",
    ["Dialogue1121103"]="(Andre shakes his head, and you realize this information isn't helpful for solving the problem.)\nSounds like it's kinda same as before. We must—",
    ["Dialogue1121104"]="<size=26>Reporting!</size>\nChief Andre! A large number of out-of-control androids have shown up on the Central Garden's <color=#CA2E0AFF>intersection that leads to Juno University</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1121105"]="How come...!\nTsk... The gap between these two riots is too close... We are short of manpower...!",
    ["Dialogue1121106"]="...Great! Please go there to <color=#CA2E0AFF>back them up</color> for now. I will take care of the work here as fast as possible and meet you there.",
    ["Dialogue1121201"]="Hey! Don't horse around! Send these wounded members to the shelter now!",
    ["Dialogue1121202"]="But... But our teammates are injured as well, captain! We don't have enough people to do this!",
    ["Dialogue1121203"]="You... Are you the Adventurer just now?",
    ["Dialogue1121204"]="Okay! Then I will leave it to you! Please take all the wounded members here to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>intersection beneath the teleport platform</color>. Our guards have established a temporary shelter there with on-site doctors to deal with the injuries. You must <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry up</color>. They can't wait any longer!",
    ["Dialogue1121301"]="Thank you so much, Adventurer. These wounded members... wouldn't make it without your help.",
    ["Dialogue1121302"]="Speaking of which... You have really amazing skills. These androids are fitted with the latest Rekenber Corp's combat module in their system. Even a professionally trained soldier would struggle when facing them. You beat them without breaking a sweat... I guess the Lord has entrusted the right one with the task.",
    ["Dialogue1121303"]="Right, if you have spare time, could you...",
    ["Dialogue1121304"]="Di-Di-Di-Di-Di-Di—",
    ["Dialogue1121305"]="What's going on?!",
    ["Dialogue1121306"]="Requesting backup! Requesting backup now! Deadly androids have appeared at the marketplace on Central Plaza! Requesting all units for reinforcement! Repeat! Deadly androids have appeared...",
    ["Dialogue1121307"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Marketplace</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>West</color> of the plaza?!\nDarn it! It's a highly crowded area, and most of our guys are wounded...",
    ["Dialogue1121401"]="...Tsk! Can't make it in time! The bomb over there is about to go off!",
    ["Dialogue1121402"]="<size=26>GET OUTTA WAY!</size>\n(The grumpy technician pushes you away with a series of angry growling coming out of his mouth.)\nHey! Why are there still civilians running around? Isn't the evacuation completed already?",
    ["Dialogue1121403"]="...You are the backup sent by Andre?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Tsk... Never mind...! We're just grasping at straws now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1121404"]="You! Over here! Take a look at the bomb!\nDo you see these tangled-up wires? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sort them out</color> and cut them at the same time— Remember! You must cut every wire of every color in one go! Do you copy?!",
    ["Dialogue1121501"]="Good! Now, defuse the bomb on another machine in the same way! Act quick!",
    ["Dialogue1121502"]="(Andre firmly pats your shoulder after hearing it, like an encouragement between comrades, or an appreciation for your help.)\n...I will leave the rest of the talking here. After settling this, let's go to a bar... My treat.",
    ["Dialogue1121503"]="Alright then... I have another thing that requires your help, Adventurer. Like I said before, the androids who are responsible for the riot were all manufactured in Khayr Consortium's factory. After discovering this, I reached out to Kiel Khayr, the power-holder of the consortium. Strangely enough, he went missing inside his private estate while the riot took place...",
    ["Dialogue1121504"]="It looks like something a fugitive would do, right? Plus, same time he went missing, all research records of this particular type of android disappeared as well. This did put our guards in a very passive situation. To solve the problem, I have confiscated a problematic android and sent it to Juno University... It is the leading academy in the nation, known for its top-notch mechanical engineering research.",
    ["Dialogue1121505"]="I have asked them to do another round of analysis on this android model. Please do me a favor, go to Juno University and look for a student called Delia. She will tell you the analysis result and provide her professional opinions.",
    ["Dialogue1121601"]="As the legendary Adventurer, who saved Rune Kingdom multiple times from devastating crises, you proved yourself again. I was worried for a bit that you would become a headless chicken for not knowing the Republic well enough... And I was wrong! Not only have you saved a massive number of citizens, you even defused the bombs expertly. I started to understand why the Lord was asking for your help.",
    ["Dialogue1121602"]="(Andre firmly pats your shoulder after hearing it, like an encouragement between comrades, or an appreciation for your help.)\n...I will leave the rest of the talking here. After settling this, let's go to a bar... My treat.",
    ["Dialogue1121603"]="Alright then... I have another thing that requires your help, Adventurer. Like I said before, the androids who are responsible for the riot were all manufactured in Khayr Consortium's factory. After discovering this, I reached out to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr</color>, the power-holder of the consortium. Strangely enough, he went missing inside his private estate while the riot took place...",
    ["Dialogue1121604"]="It looks like something a fugitive would do, right? Plus, same time he went missing, all research records of this particular type of android disappeared as well. This did put our guards in a very passive situation. To solve the problem, I have confiscated a problematic android and sent it to Juno University... It is the leading academy in the nation, known for its top-notch mechanical engineering research.",
    ["Dialogue1121605"]="I have asked them to do another round of analysis on this android model. Please do me a favor, go to Juno University and look for a student called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Delia</color>. She will tell you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>analysis result</color> and provide her professional opinions.",
    ["Dialogue1121701"]="<size=26>WAL-LA-CE!!!</size>\nI thought I told you to put this android into sleep mode ONLY! Why the hell did you smash its jaw?!",
    ["Dialogue1121702"]="Huh...? Don't you think this move looks awesomely amazing?\n(The young boy touches his head and dashes out another uppercut.)\nHeh! Hah—",
    ["Dialogue1121703"]="This is the secret move a mysterious white-haired monk taught me! Like this... and pound it down with all your might! See? They are falling down one after another!",
    ["Dialogue1121704"]="Shut your hole! I'm not interested in your physical hypnosis methodology! You— And you!\n(She turns around all of a sudden, pointing her finger at your forehead.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Assemble</color> every single one of these <color=#CA2E0AFF>body model tags</color> back to where they belong! Now!",
    ["Dialogue1121705"]="Yea! You heard me! Uncle Andre sends you here for the research report, right?",
    ["Dialogue1121706"]="<size=26>Then cut the crap and get to work already!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1121801"]="Indeed... All uncontrollable androids are of the same model. It's the latest civilian android developed by Rekenber Corp. If I recall it right, this batch had passed the hazard test three times before going into mass production... It's impossible for them to breach the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mech Agreement</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1121802"]="...You know nothing about it, do you?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Tsk! Why would uncle Andre send an amateur here to increase my workload?</color>",
    ["Dialogue1121803"]="(The young student opens her backpack and pulls out a heavy book.)\nRead it. This is the basic knowledge of mechanical engineering.",
    ["Dialogue1121901"]="You got it? An android in its normal state shouldn't do anything harmful to humans. If an error like this occurs... it could only be that the Mech Agreement wasn't installed in their chips in the first place! It's beyond my imagination how these seriously defective androids could pass the hazard test. This is not making any sense!",
    ["Dialogue1121902"]="Hmm... This is a complicated question...\nWhy keep bothering it when we can destroy them all?",
    ["Dialogue1121903"]="Idiot! You got nothing left in the brain except muscles—W-Wait! Destroy them all?\nIt might work...",
    ["Dialogue1121904"]="<size=26>Target the Mech Cores of these androids and destroy them!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1121905"]="It's the android's power source and functions as its <color=#CA2E0AFF>heart</color>. In general, when designing an android, the position of their Mech Core will be marked in detail, and it may vary in different models. Now that we know the androids with the risk of going out of control are of the same model...",
    ["Dialogue1121906"]="Yes! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gen-67F</color> tag! In this way, we only need to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>android blueprint of this particular model</color>, then we will know exactly where their Mech Core is located. After this, uncle Andre will recollect and eradicate these androids... The riot can then be settled perfectly!",
    ["Dialogue1121907"]="Since these androids are developed by Khayr Consortium, the blueprint must be hidden inside the private <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Estate</color>! If you manage to find it... then all problems will be solved!",
    ["Dialogue1122001"]="What are you doing? Don't wander around here!\nKiel Khayr's Estate is on lockdown now! No trespassing!",
    ["Dialogue1122002"]="(The guard touches his chin and looks at you.)\nAre you the Adventurer Chief Andre was talking about?",
    ["Dialogue1122003"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Looks pretty ordinary to me... the successor of Odin's bloodline, you say?</color>\n...Fine! Since it is Chief Andre's order, you may enter and leave the estate as you wish. But this estate is teeming with monsters right now, and we don't have extra manpower to protect you. So watch it yourself!",
    ["Dialogue1122004"]="Who knows? Ever since Kiel Khayr <color=#CA2E0AFF>went missing</color>, this estate became the nest of monsters overnight. We have sent a couple of experienced investigators to investigate this weird phenomenon. You can talk to them if you have any questions.",
    ["Dialogue1122101"]="Sorry, sorry, I didn't mean to attack you... I was just a bit nervous. There are too many monsters here.",
    ["Dialogue1122102"]="You don't look like a guard to me...\n<color=#A1979FFF>Weird, the estate should have been on lockdown by now...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1122103"]="<size=26>Successor of O-Odin's Bloodline?!</size>\n(The young investigator bows and salutes at you in a panic.)\nT-This is embarrassing...",
    ["Dialogue1122104"]="About the current situation of the estate? Of course! Chief Andre has given the order, and we will support your investigation in any way we can. But... it's a shame we haven't found anything useful in the past few days.",
    ["Dialogue1122105"]="I'm confused too. Usually, there will be some sort of traces if we look close enough. But this case is somewhat special. The night Kiel Khayr went missing, the estate was invaded by mountains of monsters. Almost all traces were <color=#CA2E0AFF>wiped out</color> from the surface... But the timing of this incident was just... too much of a coincidence... like it was meant to happen on the same night of his missing.",
    ["Dialogue1122106"]="It's just a shot in the dark, but Kiel Khayr's missing... may be somehow <color=#CA2E0AFF>related to the invasion of these monsters</color>.\n(He pauses and lets out a deep breath, scratching his head dejectedly.)\nIt's a shame... we don't have any evidence to validate my assumption...",
    ["Dialogue1122107"]="You want to explore the surrounding for a bit? Then... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>beware of these monsters</color>. They are outrageously deranged right now. Once they surround you, you will be in a difficult situation.",
    ["Dialogue1122201"]="...How was it? Did you find anything useful?",
    ["Dialogue1122202"]="I see... Not even you could get anything out of there...\n(He shakes his head regretfully with a hopeless face.)",
    ["Dialogue1122203"]="You want to know where the library is in this estate? There might be some clues left behind. But I'm sorry to break this to you... look at the ruins over there.\n(He points over there, and you see there are many <color=#CA2E0AFF>torn pages</color> scattered beneath the broken walls.)",
    ["Dialogue1122204"]="Those deranged monsters destroyed everything... leaving nothing useful behind. Maybe you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a photo of this ruin</color> and see if you get anything out of it. But... don't hold your breath on this, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1122301"]="Thank you so much! I was about to become their lunch if it wasn't you... Wait! You are not one of us, are you?",
    ["Dialogue1122302"]="So you are the legendary Adventurer Chief Andre was talking about... Nice to meet you! If you have any questions while investigating the estate, feel free to drop by! I am happy to help you!",
    ["Dialogue1122303"]="It was... Ah! Yes! This is it!\n(She slaps her forehead and points at the flower bed not far away.)\nDo you find the maid over there a bit weird?!",
    ["Dialogue1122304"]="I've been observing her for the past few days... At first, when the estate was locked down by the guards, everyone was asked to leave, but somehow this maid refused, saying these precious plants and flowers must be taken care of by someone and it was an order from her master. In despair, our captain let her stay but assigned me to keep an eye on her, you know, to protect her from those monsters...",
    ["Dialogue1122305"]="B-But... This person doesn't even need my help! Two days ago, there was a monster trying to attack her, and she knocked it out just like that! On top of that, she acts very oddly, as if she has set an alarm clock that drives her to do all the things throughout the day... So accurate that not even off by a second! This... This is just uncanny...",
    ["Dialogue1122306"]="Oh, right! I've taken many <color=#CA2E0AFF>photos</color> of her for the past couple of days. Can you help me deliver these photos to Chief Andre? If you want to, you can also <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk to her</color>. Might get some extra clues out of her.",
    ["Dialogue1122401"]="(After seeing you, the maid in her elegant dress smiles and lifts the hem of the skirt, making a textbook curtsey to you.)\nWelcome to Kiel Khayr's Estate, my honored guest. Please take a casual tour of the garden. The banquet will be ready very soon.",
    ["Dialogue1122402"]="Are you not here for the banquet? Then, are you here to see the master? I'm very sorry, but the master is not in the estate currently... Don't worry, though. I will prepare a room for you so that you can wait at ease for the master to return.",
    ["Dialogue1122403"]="Hmm... Is there something wrong with me?\n(She tilts her head confusingly and looks at her dress.)\nAnything of my faux pas here?",
    ["Dialogue1122404"]="Are you talking about the monsters wandering around in the estate? I apologize for this. There is nothing I can do before my master gives me an expulsion order. But please rest assured. Ensuring the safety of our guests is my top priority, per my master's request.",
    ["Dialogue1122405"]="Besides, the area with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>highest monster density</color> in the estate is far away from here. According to my calculation, the chance of you being attacked is only 5.86%...\n(She keeps on rambling with the math formula, and you can tell something is wrong with this maid. Something She's unaware of. You have to talk to her in a different way; otherwise, you won't be able to get anything useful from her.)",
    ["Dialogue1122406"]="...Do you want to take a look at the area with the highest monster density?\n(You might be mistaken, but the glow in her eyes has seemingly changed just now.)\nAre you sure to do this, my honored guest?",
    ["Dialogue1122407"]="<color=#A1979FFF>...Guest order... Priority is higher than... Evaluating... Executable...</color>\nUnderstood, please follow me.",
    ["Dialogue1122501"]="Are you okay, my guest? If you don't feel well, I suggest you take a rest in the guest room inside the mansion.\n(The maid reaches down and looks you in the eyes. Smiling as she is, a chill just creeps upon your spine.)",
    ["Dialogue1122502"]="This... This abandoned well had been there before my master acquired the estate. About two to three months ago, a rainstorm heavily damaged the vegetation covering the well, so it got exposed. Since then, my master has prohibited anyone from getting close to here...",
    ["Dialogue1122503"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Getting close to the dry well is not allowed... Prohibited... Approaching this mysterious power... Order priority... Highest...</color>\n(She watches your doings, eyes soulless and void.)\nEvaluation result: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clear the threat</color>. Execute immediately.",
    ["Dialogue1122601"]="You are back, Adventurer. How was it? Did you find a way to deal with those androids?",
    ["Dialogue1122602"]="...Nothing? But it seems like you did get something today...\n(You might be mistaken, but Andre seems to peek at the corner not far away on purpose when speaking of this.)\nI guess you have something to report to me?",
    ["Dialogue1122603"]="You suspect... the riot in Juno is somehow related to the missing of Kiel Khayr? Interesting guess... But do you have any evidence?",
    ["Dialogue1122604"]="Good... Then <color=#CA2E0AFF>prove it to me with all the evidence you have</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1122701"]="...We meet again, Adventurer. I am surprised that you've been so far into the investigation with only a fraction of the time. This is impressive.",
    ["Dialogue1122702"]="I'm sorry, but those questions just now... They were deliberately asked by Andre at my behest. The conclusion you have reached today is almost identical to ours, but it took us over a month to get there. You... It only took you half a day.",
    ["Dialogue1122703"]="Hey, don't give me that look, Adventurer. I am only following the order… if you want to pick on somebody... there is the Minister.\n(Andre waves his hand and glances at Philodis.)\nOkay then, I will leave the rest to you. I am now off to set up the plan for the next phase.",
    ["Dialogue1122704"]="Don't worry, Adventurer. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>read this letter</color> first. When you are finished, I will explain this to you from the beginning.",
    ["Dialogue1122801"]="Before the very first android riot took place in Juno, this letter had already been delivered to Lord Carl's desk. I thought it was just a prank from some idiots. But, not long after, the androids went out of control altogether...",
    ["Dialogue1122802"]="Yes, we did suspect the one who sent out this anonymous letter to be the culprit behind the scenes. To search for evidence, I tried to enter the academy with the guards, but shamefully, there were lots of airborne surveillance devices patrolling around the campus, just as the letter had mentioned. Anyone who attempts to enter the academy will get turned away. But if we use heavy weapons to breach it with force, the enemy might be alerted...",
    ["Dialogue1122803"]="...No, what we have for now is just a doubtful letter. It's not worthy for Lord Carl to risk his safety. And... This is the reason I invited you over.",
    ["Dialogue1122804"]="Through the tech department's investigation, we have confirmed the working logic behind those airborne surveillance devices is to identify the trespassers via the Republic database once they are detected. According to that letter, no one is able to enter Kiel Khayr's Academy at this moment... except Lord Carl.",
    ["Dialogue1122805"]="But there's a deadly loophole in this program—Since the devices only check the identity information in the database, what if... we find someone whose information <color=#CA2E0AFF>never exists</color> in the database?",
    ["Dialogue1122806"]="Yes, it's you, the successor of Odin's bloodline. I've checked your arrival record, and it seems like your pass was bought on a black market, right?",
    ["Dialogue1122807"]="(Philodis pauses for a second. He isn't expecting you to start joking at this moment. But soon, he puts on his poker face again.)\n...Whatever. The point is, every black market pass <color=#CA2E0AFF>forges a fake identity</color> for the holder. That's why W couldn't find your entry record even though you have been to Al De Baran.",
    ["Dialogue1122808"]="You are smart, Adventurer. Yes, that's also why I stopped W from entering your identity information— I need an \"Invisible Person\" in the Republic... So this person can proceed with the task we are incapable of.",
    ["Dialogue1122809"]="More importantly... As the most famous Adventurer on this continent, you've helped the Rune Kingdom survive crises one after another. If you were someone else... I wouldn't dare to entrust this task to them.",
    ["Dialogue1122810"]="(The young Minister bends down. From the arrogance in the very first meeting to the calculated test just now, he finally shows you his sincerity and makes a gesture of help-seeking.)\nI apologize for my previous behaviors, Adventurer. But the fate of the nation is at skate, so I can't act recklessly. In my point of view... I always have faith in you that you won't disappoint Lord Carl, and me.",
    ["Dialogue1122811"]="(Philodis pauses, thinks for a moment, and finally realizes what you are thinking about.)\nIs it... about the power of Ymir's Heart?",
    ["Dialogue1122812"]="I see. You are carrying the duty to investigate the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. We are of the same goal here. I can guarantee you, I will assist you in any way I can, as long as it doesn't compromise the benefits of the Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1122813"]="Alrighty. I will take you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Academy</color> now. But, before that...\n(Philodis reaches into his pocket and pulls out a tiny tube of reagent.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Take this</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1122814"]="This is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anti-Radiation Potion</color> developed by Juno University. Due to some very special reason in history... Sorry, I don't have time to explain everything right now. But do remember, the surrounding areas of Juno have been exposed to radiation for years. Without precaution, you may expose your body to a hazardous environment. Therefore, you MUST take this potion when entering those areas.",
    ["Dialogue1122901"]="I can only walk you here, Adventurer. The entrance to the Kiel Khayr's Academy is just ahead, and it's surrounded by many airborne surveillance devices. They will verify your identity once you get into the alert area...",
    ["Dialogue1122902"]="We do assume that they wouldn't attack you, since you didn't have your identity registered in the Republic database. But for safety reasons, Andre has his guards surround the academy. They are hiding in the woods around, on standby to rescue you if you are in danger.",
    ["Dialogue1122903"]="Besides, after you get into the academy, please conduct your investigation cautiously. Do not come into conflict with those patrolling robot guards, lest the building's defensive mechanism be triggered. The best case scenario is to locate the documents mentioned in the anonymous letter while ensuring your safety.",
    ["Dialogue1122904"]="So... Best of luck, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1123001"]="Ahem... You... Are you sent by Rekenber Corp...?",
    ["Dialogue1123002"]="Lord Carl?!\n(The grey-haired elder looks blank for a moment, yet a fire of hope blazing in his eyes of stagnant water.)\nHe finally decides to go after Rekenber Corp?",
    ["Dialogue1123003"]="...Are you saying the anonymous letter reports <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr Consortium</color> for their illegal android research?",
    ["Dialogue1123004"]="<size=26>That's absolute nonsense!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1123005"]="It was Rekenber Corp who committed all the crimes! It was them who developed those shady chips behind everyone's back, causing the androids to lose control, breach the Mech Agreement and even attack humans! If you don't believe me, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at the document</color> I have here!",
    ["Dialogue1123101"]="What now? If you still have doubts, feel free to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> these android bodies <color=#CA2E0AFF>around</color> and see if their condition matches the letter!",
    ["Dialogue1123201"]="Are you done looking, Adventurer? You just witnessed all these with your eyes. Isn't it enough to prove my innocence? And I'm going to tell you one more thing— The letter Lord Carl received was <color=#CA2E0AFF>written by me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1123202"]="Sorry, I was just getting worked up, and didn't think carefully about what you said. But as I recall, you did mention that Philodis was the one who gave you the letter. Am I correct?",
    ["Dialogue1123203"]="...Then everything makes sense now.\n(Kiel Khayr smiles with confidence, and even with a slight arrogance that you don't understand.)\nThe letter you saw... It could possibly be <color=#CA2E0AFF>forged</color> by him!",
    ["Dialogue1123204"]="Because the Lord's Mansion and the cabinet office are not a hundred percent safe these days. Rekenber Corp has reached its tentacles into different areas in the Republic, and even those higher-ups have something in their hands. Philodis must have done all these to prevent the wrong people from reading this letter and passing the information to Rekenber Corp...",
    ["Dialogue1123205"]="How did I get all these assumptions? Because... Philodis used to be my secretary, and we had been working together for a long time. He finally chose to step into the world of politics, but still, we share the same goal, which is to stop the wild ambition of Rekenber Corp. And he will never swallow the belief he's been holding. So my guess is, that he must have realized the letter was written by me, and in order not to act rashly, also for my safety... that he forged a fake one.",
    ["Dialogue1123206"]="At first, the Khayr Consortium and Rekenber Corp were merely business competitors. But in recent years, they have been making multiple acquisition attempts to us, wishing to buy out our research patents of androids. But I refused them every time. Since then, they started to turn other shareholders against me and made me a mere figurehead. And the android riot this time... was a final blow to me.",
    ["Dialogue1123207"]="So I became desperate, escaped with the consortium's vital documents, and sent an anonymous letter to the Lord, requesting assistance. This place was intended to be a factory for the research and development of androids, which is why it's equipped with such a strict security system. But as soon as I arrived here, I found out Rekenber Corp had seized control of the academy. They've been researching chips that can breach the Mech Agreement here... and put the blame on me!",
    ["Dialogue1123208"]="Adventurer... Since Philodis sent you here, he must believe that you are someone trustworthy. As his best friend, I will now project my trust in him toward you, asking for your help with the same sincerity. The key to resolving everything lies in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter I sent to the Lord</color>, and I'm the only person who knows how to use it. If you are willing to help me...",
    ["Dialogue1123209"]="...Help me lure away the people outside. I know the academy is surrounded by the guards right now, and Rekenber's rats are very likely hiding among them. I'll try to sneak out from the back gate later. Please do something to get them out of there. Afterward, go find Philodis and tell him what I said, and he knows what to do next. If everything goes as planned... We will meet again at the entrance of El Mes Gorge in two hours.",
    ["Dialogue1123210"]="And by the way, I see you have a camera with you. Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take photos of what's inside this warehouse</color> as evidence against Rekenber Corp in the future?",
    ["Dialogue1123301"]="How was it, Adventurer? Did you get anything?",
    ["Dialogue1123302"]="...Tsk. I didn't expect this. So, that anonymous letter was nothing but a prank?\n(With hands holding his chin, Andre is trying to connect the dots of the clues. Meanwhile, you are following Kiel Khayr's request, trying to lure away Andre and his guards.)",
    ["Dialogue1123303"]="...Focus on the riot itself? Hmm... You have a point here. Fine, I will head back to Juno with the guards right now. Speaking of which, I was worried about androids going out of control again during the time we were not here.",
    ["Dialogue1123304"]="You want to discuss with Minister <color=#CA2E0AFF>Philodis</color> what to do next? He's in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>woods</color> not far away. Go down this pathway, and you'll see him there.",
    ["Dialogue1123401"]="(Philodis seems surprised when he sees you again. He looks behind you and wonders why the guards are not here with you.)\n...Adventurer, Why are you here? Didn't I ask Andre to...",
    ["Dialogue1123402"]="You lured Andre and the guards away from the academy? Why?",
    ["Dialogue1123403"]="(You tell Philodis everything you've seen and heard in the academy. Strangely enough, he doesn't seem surprised.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>I knew it... He planned everything...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1123404"]="...I see. I believe in Kiel Khayr and your judgment. If he thinks he's holding the key to resolving everything, let's help him out. I will now retrieve the original copy of that anonymous letter... Let's meet later at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>entrance of El Mes Gorge</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1123501"]="Thanks to you, I can get here without getting caught by Rekenber Corp. Now, Philodis has brought the letter I sent... Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the letter</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>search the interlayer of the letter</color>... There lies my trump card against Rekenber Corp.",
    ["Dialogue1123601"]="I think you should recognize it by now, Philodis. This is the grand collection of the consortium's most cutting-edge technologies so far—a data driver board that can control androids remotely.",
    ["Dialogue1123602"]="You can deem it as a remote terminal of the android system. According to the Mech Agreement, all androids must be fitted with a self-destruction mechanism to respond to emergencies. And the civilian androids on today's market are mostly using the physical approach for Mech Core destruction. However, this technology of Khayr Consortium... allows the destruction mechanism to break through the spatial limitation, which will definitely revolutionize the android industries.",
    ["Dialogue1123603"]="Now, all androids that have problems belong to the consortium's latest Gen Series. In fact, during the early design phase, I was expecting this series could revolutionize the industries. That's why I invested a huge amount of resources in this remote control terminal system, which can be used to put an end to the competition between the consortium and Rekenber Corp...",
    ["Dialogue1123604"]="But I would've never thought these greedy and filthy rascals had bypassed the Mech Agreement, developed illegal chips, and planted the crime on me, trying to put the consortium in a dire situation. What's even more frightening was that on the night everything went down, they hired assassins to sneak into the estate and tried to kill me!",
    ["Dialogue1123605"]="Yes... To escape, I used the mysterious power from the well and attracted mountains of monsters to the estate, seizing the chance to run away with the data driver board. Afterward, I hid inside the academy and sent out that anonymous letter...",
    ["Dialogue1123606"]="(At this point, Kiel Khayr gives Philodis a pat on his shoulder, a pat that looks like a compliment from a teacher to a student, full of tacit understanding between best friends.)\nI was confident you would get what I was doing, once you saw the letter.",
    ["Dialogue1123607"]="But... It's far too early to relax. If we want to activate the data driver board and destroy the Mech Core of those defective androids through remote control, we'll need some supporting devices.",
    ["Dialogue1123608"]="Yes, I need a transmitter unit to send the Mech Core destruction command to the androids. That's why I chose El Mes Gorge as our meeting point. There is a group of elite scholars sponsored by the government. They have a lot of high-tech devices...",
    ["Dialogue1123609"]="You are saying...\n(Philodis contemplates for a moment and speaks out a name you are familiar with.)\n...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1123610"]="Yes. If it's Captain <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alquein</color>... She will spare no efforts to help us, right?",
    ["Dialogue1123701"]="Thank you, stranger! If it wasn't for you, the big sis is going to... Huh? Minister Philodis? Why are you...?",
    ["Dialogue1123702"]="It's been a while, Rakylafitz. Now let me cut to the chase. I have something very important to discuss with Alquein. Can you bring me to her?",
    ["Dialogue1123703"]="It shouldn't be a problem, but all my <color=#CA2E0AFF>cargo</color> was left in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gorge</color> because of the attack just now... If I go back like this, big sis will beat the crap out of me... No, no, no, I have to get the cargo back before anything. Wait for me.",
    ["Dialogue1123801"]="Alrighty! Big sis will have no reason to kick my butt now! Everyone, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to the camp</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1123901"]="...I have seen a lineup like this for a long time. What is it? The Minister and the president of Khayr Consortium come to see me together. Is Eden Group in big trouble? Oh, and this is...",
    ["Dialogue1123902"]="(The charming lady set her eyes on you.)\nYou are... The successor of Odin's bloodline?",
    ["Dialogue1123903"]="I can say only that I've heard a lot about you. After all... all the ruins of my Eden Group, across the continent, have received your generous help, and I've been waiting to see the Adventurer who always saved the kingdom from crises. Who would've thought I could fulfill my dream here and now?",
    ["Dialogue1123904"]="...That's enough, Alquein. Stop teasing our hero. I'm here to borrow the transmitter unit from Eden Group. You won't turn me down, right?",
    ["Dialogue1123905"]="Transmitter unit? Yes, I think... but why?",
    ["Dialogue1123906"]="(As you recount the whole story. the laid-back smiles on Alquein's face fade little by little, eventually gone without a trace.)\n...What a dangerous ambition. So, you want to borrow Eden Group's transmitter unit, to send out the self-destruction command to those uncontrollable androids?",
    ["Dialogue1123907"]="But our transmitter unit won't be able to cover the entire city of Juno. To meet your requirement, we must use a signal amplifier to increase its effective range. But the only signal amplifier was taken to the 2nd floor of Juperos Ruins; we need someone to get it back...",
    ["Dialogue1123908"]="...By yourself? No. I trust your power, but the environment inside the ruins is complicated. You'll need someone to lead the way for you...\n(At this point, Alquein glares sharply at someone, and suddenly reaches out, grabbing that person by the collar.)\n<size=26>Rakylafitz! Where the hell are you off to?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1123909"]="Eeeeeeeek! Please forgive me! Okay! Okay! <size=18>I'll go!</size><size=26> Just stop hitting me already!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1123910"]="Hmm... You there, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color> now. Don't say that I didn't warn you—stay close or else I won't be able to save you if anything happens...",
    ["Dialogue1124001"]="This sucks... It's not my day... I guess Lady Luck must be taking a nap...",
    ["Dialogue1124002"]="Apparently, it's a landslide. If we don't clear up the rubbles blocking the road and <color=#CA2E0AFF>set the rail back where it was</color>, we won't be able to advance. But the situation doesn't seem too bad. It's a good thing I have some basic tools with me to fix the rail. Come on, give me a hand, and let's get it done as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue1124101"]="Good, we can finally see the path after removing that annoying rubbles... What's that sound?\n(Rakylafitz gasps. You follow his line of sight and see a swarm of glowing cube-shaped creatures, settling in the middle of the path before you.)",
    ["Dialogue1124102"]="Those are the natives of these ruins—a mysterious type of creature we refer to as an \"Energy Cube.\" They're extremely dangerous, so we usually use the power of the exploration machine to deal with them. I've already sent a message to the Eden Group members stationed here to get in touch with us. It's strange... They should be here already...",
    ["Dialogue1124103"]="...We can't wait any longer. The longer we stay in the ruins, the more likely it is that we'll be attacked by those Energy Cubes. Let's split up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the Eden Group members who have the exploration machine</color>. If everything goes smoothly, we'll meet at the entrance to the second floor, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1124201"]="Weeee, I'm faster than you! Heehee! I beat the legendary successor of Odin's bloodline! I'm gonna be bragging about this for a long time!",
    ["Dialogue1124202"]="...You guys were surrounded by a large number of Energy Cubes on the way here? That's...",
    ["Dialogue1124203"]="Yes, it was a close call. If it wasn't for this Adventurer, we wouldn't have lasted even a second, let alone gotten the exploration machine fixed! Speaking of which, these Energy Cubes seem to be acting weird lately. They seem more aggressive...",
    ["Dialogue1124204"]="(While the explorer speaks, Rakylafitz's face gradually stiffens.)\nThis is not a good sign, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1124205"]="We can't wait around. If somehow those Energy Cubes set eyes on us again, we can forget about retrieving the signal amplifier... We'll be as good as dead then...",
    ["Dialogue1124206"]="Besides, Juperos Ruins is already teeming with monsters... Time is of the essence! Now, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>move forward</color>! I will operate the exploration machine, and y'all <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay close</color> to me! Don't fall behind!",
    ["Dialogue1124301"]="What's going on? Shouldn't y'all be investigating when the ruins were created on the upper floor? Why's everyone here? And...\n(The young explorer sizes up the bunch of you with a shocked face.)\n...Rakylafitz? You're supposed to protect the captain up there. What are you doing here?",
    ["Dialogue1124302"]="Sorry, Isaack. I need to borrow the signal amplifier on the soil property sensor. I'd give you a reason, but... Ahhh! It's complicated! Anyway, just give it to me.",
    ["Dialogue1124303"]="H-Huh? Fine, I'm done using it here anyway... Do you see the ruins over there? You'll find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>soil property sensor</color> there. Then you can remove the <color=#CA2E0AFF>signal amplifier</color> yourself.",
    ["Dialogue1124401"]="What took you guys so long? I was worried y'all might've run into trouble... Everything good?",
    ["Dialogue1124402"]="Is that so? That he didn't hold you back is an achievement in itself.\n(Alquein looks confused. Clearly, she's very familiar with her guard.)",
    ["Dialogue1124403"]="...Never mind, as long as we have what we need, that's all that matters. Look, I got the transmitter unit ready. The terrain is more open here—perfect for transmitting a signal.",
    ["Dialogue1124404"]="Let's install the <color=#CA2E0AFF>data driver board</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>signal amplifier</color> before it's too late, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1124501"]="Let me give you some advice—a wise man submits to fate. I have my men surrounding this place like a fence... It makes absolutely no difference how hard you struggle, you'll never escape here alive. How about we make a deal? Hand over Kiel Khayr, and I'll let the rest of you go.",
    ["Dialogue1124502"]="(Under Kayak's intimidating gaze, Philodis steps forward and positions himself between Kiel Khayr and Kayak.)\n...You seem to be overestimating yourself here, Mr. Kayak. You are nothing but the vice president of Rekenber Corp, yet somehow you dare pick a quarrel with the Minister?",
    ["Dialogue1124503"]="Hahahaha... <size=18>Interesting!</size><size=26> This is amusing!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1124504"]="(Kayak glances at every one of you in disdain, and the sound of his mocking applause spreads through the hollow valley.)\nThe Minister with his infallible integrity, the passionate and loyal Eden Group, and the renowned successor of Odin's Bloodline who saved the people from crisis after crisis?",
    ["Dialogue1124505"]="Fine! Then every one of you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>read this document</color> and see what kind of scum you are trying to protect!",
    ["Dialogue1124601"]="<size=26>But this document of yours is fake! I have never done such things!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1124602"]="Oh? That's your signature and seal at the bottom of the document, no? Yes, handwriting can be forged, but the seal of the Khayr Consortium is a mark of unique craftsmanship that can only be applied with a special ink paste... Besides you, who could have stamped a seal on this document?",
    ["Dialogue1124603"]="You... You bought off my cronies long ago! After I turned down the acquisition offer from Rekenber Corp, I became a thorn in your side, and you've been waiting to get rid of me ever since! First, you and the shareholders made me a figurehead, and you paid off my people to forge this confidential document and the seal. You used the Gen series civilian androids to start a riot in Juno... and then put it all on me!",
    ["Dialogue1124604"]="Even so, you won't stop until I'm dead—",
    ["Dialogue1124605"]="Let's stop the death throes right here, Mr. Kiel Khayr. You can keep on talking, but do you have any hard evidence?\n(Kayak smiles with a sarcastic look on his face and points at you, Philodis, and the others.)\nIf there is no hard evidence, how do you suppose the people here to believe you?",
    ["Dialogue1124606"]="<size=26>You bet I do!</size>\n(With a loud smacking sound, a document is thrown at Kayak's feet, and you realize that this is the experiment record of the chip you saw in the academy.)",
    ["Dialogue1124607"]="...I was expecting something else. This is just a random experiment record, with no signatures, no nothing to prove anyone's involvement whatsoever. I bet a random student at Juno University could easily write a report like this. What kind of evidence is this?",
    ["Dialogue1124608"]="(He sets his eye on Philodis again.)\nAm I right, Minister Philodis?",
    ["Dialogue1124609"]="(At this moment, everyone looks at this young Minister shaking his head in silence.)\n...Yes, if we were in court, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>could not be treated as evidence</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1124610"]="...I see. Is this also part of your plan? Even the document in my hand... serves as bait?\nHa... I made a careless mistake here. Even so... Rekenber Corp has no right to detain or arrest me!",
    ["Dialogue1124611"]="If they don't have the right, what about me?",
    ["Dialogue1124701"]="<size=26>Kayak! Who gave you permission to open fire?!</size>\nHe's an important witness in the case! If anything happens, Rekenber Corp—",
    ["Dialogue1124702"]="...Stop yelling. Do you really think I'm stupid enough to kill him?\n(Kayak lifts his hand and tosses a uniquely-shaped bullet at Andre's feet.)\nTake a closer look! This is a tranquilizer bullet!",
    ["Dialogue1124703"]="Tranquilizer bullet...?\n(Philodis looks lost for quite a while. He then grabs you by your arm, filled with a sudden panic.)",
    ["Dialogue1124704"]="Quick... Quick! Adventurer! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Check</color> if he's still alive!",
    ["Dialogue1124801"]="How is he? Still breathing? Shouldn't I be honored for my bravery, Chief Andre? After all, Kiel Khayr is the major suspect in manufacturing the androids responsible for the riot. He even attempted to assault a government official and flee the scene. If it wasn't for my marksmanship... BANG!",
    ["Dialogue1124802"]="(Kayak lifts his hand and makes a shooting gesture, he even blows the invisible smoke from the tip of the gun.)\nIf he were to run away... the guards would be accused of a major dereliction of duty.",
    ["Dialogue1124803"]="...Thank you for your assistance, Vice President Kayak. I will report the matter to the Commissioner. But now, I need to detain Kiel Khayr immediately and retrieve everything related to the case. Please cooperate.",
    ["Dialogue1124804"]="I don't think so, Chief Andre. These documents are related to the core trade secrets of Rekenber Corp—I can't just give them to anybody. Moreover, since you have that arrest warrant in your hand, it means you already possess sufficient <color=#CA2E0AFF>critical evidence</color> to put Kiel Khayr behind bars. Then there's this giant robot... Aren't you guys curious about why it deviated from Kiel Khayr's command just now?",
    ["Dialogue1124805"]="Let me fill you in a little, amateur. According to the Mech Agreement, all machinery must treat the command of its master as its top priority. When the master encounters danger, it will activate its defense system automatically and eliminate the threat. But you and Philodis weren't even attacking Kiel Khayr, so why did the Guardian treat the two of you as enemies?",
    ["Dialogue1124806"]="I wonder... During the faceoff, only one instance of the conflict took place between Kiel Khayr and the bunch of you—that sentence spoken by Philodis!",
    ["Dialogue1124807"]="(The young minster seems slightly startled and contemplates the matter for a few seconds. A look of uncertainty flashes across his eyes.)\n...\"If we were in court, this could not be treated as evidence.\" Was it?",
    ["Dialogue1124808"]="An A+ answer, Minster Philodis!\n(Kayak starts to applaud pretentiously amid the silence, making him look like a clown who doesn't belong.)\nSomeone as smart as you should be able to get my point by now.",
    ["Dialogue1124809"]="...Are you saying that, because this statement asserts that Kiel Khayr is guilty of using androids to start the riot, which made the Adventurer and I witness against him, we became a threat to the Guardian as a result? In other words... Kiel Khayr was indeed the one who plotted the riot. Is that so?",
    ["Dialogue1124810"]="Very wise, our youngest Minister in the Republic's history! From what you just said, I think the documents and the data driver board can now be handed over to me, no? After all, Kiel Khayr is about to go to jail, and his consortium will fall apart very soon... After that, Rekenber Corp will be the only enterprise capable of carrying forward the nation's android industry.",
    ["Dialogue1124811"]="Speaking of which, recently... has anyone in the cabinet been fighting the new regulation issued by the Lord, accusing him of cutting the budget on military android technology? Tsk, if the Khayr Consortium, the biggest supporter of the Lord, were to go down at this moment in time, then the result of the next election would be completely up in the air.",
    ["Dialogue1124812"]="Minster Philodis! This doesn't comply—",
    ["Dialogue1124813"]="...Back off, Andre. I know what to do. You and the guards... take Kiel Khayr back to the headquarters at once. As for those documents and the evidence related to android manufacturing technology, hand them over to Vice President Kayak and retrieve them along with the verification report after completing the testing and analysis.",
    ["Dialogue1124814"]="...That's right, testing and analysis. Previously, whenever there was a criminal case in the field of android technology, the Khayr Consortium was usually the one who verified and provided us with their professional opinion. As of now... just as Vice President Kayak said, only the research labs under Rekenber Corp can complete such a task. If I recall correctly... President Rowland requested this many times in the past, yes?",
    ["Dialogue1124815"]="Of course, after the completion of the verification report, everything, including the evidence, must be returned. I believe Rekenber Corp is fully aware of this.\n(Philodis pushes his glasses and reaches out his right hand.)\nI hope we can work together well, Vice President Kayak.",
    ["Dialogue1124816"]="(The expression on Kayak's face changes multiple times throughout just a few sentences. You can tell he is conflicted within his heart, but still, he shakes Philodis's hand.)\n...As do I, Minster Philodis.",
    ["Dialogue1124901"]="...This way, Adventurer. Hold on.\n(Philodis sneaks up to the back of the Guardian amid the chaos and hides behind it. He bends down and reaches to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>back of its neck</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue1124902"]="Shh, keep it down... Nice, I found it.\n(You hear a slight metal clanging sound come from his hand. It seems as though he has pulled something off from the back of the Guardian's neck.)\nYes, this is it.",
    ["Dialogue1124903"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer. I will explain later.",
    ["Dialogue1125001"]="Sorry, Minister Philodis. Based on the order issued by Kayak, except for cabinet members, no one can enter the Lord's Mansion before the android unrest is settled. This measure was taken to ensure the safety of the Lord. Please comply with it.",
    ["Dialogue1125002"]="...Open your eyes and look. This is the legendary Adventurer who has saved the kingdom from crises time and again—the hero who carries Odin's Bloodline! I invite this honored guest here on behalf of the Lord, and you stand here embarrassing me in front of my guest?",
    ["Dialogue1125003"]="Or should I report this to Vice President Kayak? Will he see this as you being rude to my guest, or as me failing to follow the rules?",
    ["Dialogue1125004"]="(Under Philodis's intimidating glare, the guard begins to panic.)\nN-No... That's not what I meant, Minister Philodis.",
    ["Dialogue1125005"]="This Adventurer can enter the Lord's Mansion alongside you, b-but... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>unequip your weapons</color> and store them here, as per the rules. We will return them to you when you leave.",
    ["Dialogue1125101"]="I'm Carl, the Lord of the Republic. I'm very sorry to invite you over in such a rush, and I appreciate your willingness to help in the current situation.",
    ["Dialogue1125102"]="Lord Carl, you can save your formal tone. This Adventurer is a paragon of righteousness and cares not for pretentious courtesies.\n(An indifferent voice interrupts the Lord. You look up and see a familiar face.)",
    ["Dialogue1125103"]="Long time no see, Adventurer. I'd love to catch up with you, but a more important matter requires our attention. Did you get the thing, Philodis?",
    ["Dialogue1125104"]="Of course. As you requested, I retrieved the chip and Mech Core from that giant robot... Are these the ones?\n(Philodis opens his hand to reveal a chip and a golden cube, both shining with a metallic glint.)",
    ["Dialogue1125105"]="...Yes. Now, let me insert the chip into the mysterious device and see what happens...",
    ["Dialogue1125106"]="(The tiny chip falls into the mysterious device's detection port; the antenna starts to spin, then a violent alarm is triggered.)\nWarning! Warning! Illegal program detected! Warning! Warning! Illegal program detected!",
    ["Dialogue1125107"]="...As we expected, this chip is installed with a backdoor that can bypass the Mech Agreement, but the model of the Guardian is obviously different from the uncontrollable androids. In general, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chip installed should correspond to the android model</color>, but this type of chip developed by Rekenber Corp <color=#CA2E0AFF>can be used on a wide variety of machines</color>... This is the worst possible scenario for us.",
    ["Dialogue1125108"]="...What's the matter, Adventurer? Do you want to say something?",
    ["Dialogue1125201"]="This... This is a violation of the protocol! These androids look <color=#CA2E0AFF>identical</color> to humans!\n(The Lord bangs the desk, his anger almost unsubdued.)\nAnd... And the chips...",
    ["Dialogue1125202"]="...If Rekenber Corp installs the faulty chips on androids that are highly similar to humans and lets them blend into human society... With their superior intelligence and stamina compared to humans, they can quickly build up their forces in different fields and realize their ambitions...",
    ["Dialogue1125203"]="It's embarrassing... Even though I am fully aware that Rekenber Corp is up to something, I still don't know what their goal could be. They have both power and wealth, but what if they want to take their superiority to another level...",
    ["Dialogue1125204"]="(The Lord looks down and reaches out to the armrest on his chair, then starts stroking it.)\nIs it possible that they want to position themselves in this chair? Or perhaps somewhere granting even more power than this...?",
    ["Dialogue1125205"]="...Lord Carl, it's meaningless for us to keep discussing their motivations. After this android riot, the Khayr Consortium is now at a total loss within their industry and can no longer compete with Rekenber Corp. Soon, they will reach their grasp onto the cabinet. As far as I know...\n(He pauses, looking hesitantly at you and Fulkyn.)",
    ["Dialogue1125206"]="(The Lord waves his hand and signals Philodis to continue.)\nIt's fine. Keep going. We are the ones seeking help, so we should act like it. At this point, if we keep anything from the Adventurer and Fulkyn, it won't help solve the problem, and it isn't a very nice thing to do to those trying to help us in any way they can.",
    ["Dialogue1125207"]="...Yes, Lord Carl. As far as I know, the cabinet has been split into two factions, and some people are already openly supporting Rekenber Corp. As for the rest of the cabinet, the conservatives are trying to stay out of trouble and just want to finish their term in peace... So, we are all alone in the face of the current situation.",
    ["Dialogue1125208"]="But if that's not the case, then Lord Carl wouldn't have made up his mind to accept my suggestion to ask for help from the successor of Odin's bloodline. I assure you that... this is the critical moment where we can turn everything around. It's all of nothing.",
    ["Dialogue1125209"]="In fact, it can't have been hard for someone as smart as you to see all this in advance. The reason Lord Carl invited you to the Republic was not only to settle the android riot. As you can see, the Republic is run by technology, so the Khayr Consortium and Rekenber Corp, which possess advanced technology, can stand on equal footing with the government here. These three parties have been competing with each other to create a perfect balance in the Republic's authority...",
    ["Dialogue1125210"]="Indeed, the disappearance of the consortium will agitate the current situation. Rekenber Corp can now pull the wool over everyone's eyes and get away with it. They bought off the cabinet and council to eliminate anyone who stood against them and promoted a policy beneficial to them. They now even dare to siege the Lord's Mansion under everyone's noses and monitor Lord Carl's speech... If things keep on like this, this country will soon become its puppet for the purpose of financial gains.",
    ["Dialogue1125211"]="...And there's more. Recently, they seem to be researching something related to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient technology</color>, and we can't predict the strength of this unknown power. When the Republic falls into a dire situation... the king, or perhaps even all of Arunafeltz, will be helpless against being dragged into the chaos. In the foreseeable future... this will become a war that envelopes the entire continent.",
    ["Dialogue1125212"]="To this end, we must plan ahead and prepare measures to deal with Rekenber Corp. But now, everyone on our side is under their surveillance. Not only is it almost impossible for us to take action, but there also exists the constant risk of exposing ourselves... So, Fulkyn recommended you to us.",
    ["Dialogue1125213"]="Yes, you are the perfect fit for this task. We don't want to attract unnecessary attention to our actions. You not only possess solid interpersonal skills, which can be used in solo missions under myriad circumstances, but you also don't have any identity records in the Republic database. In other words, you are an \"invisible entity\" within the borders of the Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1125214"]="I hope you can take advantage of this and go to the labs and facilities set up by Rekenber Corp in different locations within the Republic to collect clues and intel. Everything will be used against them in court eventually. Other than this, I've used my knowledge to make a <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret weapon</color> to deal with emergencies... But before that, I need you to find me some materials.",
    ["Dialogue1125215"]="...Take the Adventurer to the device to have a look, Fulkyn. This is our last resort for dealing with Rekenber Corp—we can't afford for anything to go wrong.",
    ["Dialogue1125216"]="Understood, Lord Carl. So, we'll go into more detail when we see the device. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1125301"]="What's the matter, Adventurer? Don't stare into space like that. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grab</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color> and follow me.",
    ["Dialogue1125317"]="What's the matter, Adventurer? Don't stare into space like that. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grab</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color> and follow me.",
    ["Dialogue1125401"]="Welcome to the Realm of Time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1125402"]="This a space in Juno Library that I created exclusively for the one bearing the Sands of Time. The device before you is our last trump card in dealing with Rekenber Corp.",
    ["Dialogue1125403"]="Wide Magnetic Field Control Unit. I assume that it can control magnetic fields by changing the trajectories of electric charges in the environment.",
    ["Dialogue1125404"]="Our goal is to make it cover all of Juno so that we will know exactly what Rekenber Corp is doing with the androids and plan ahead. However... this machine is not finished yet, and we still need a couple more high-purity Mech Cores to use as a power source before it can be activated.",
    ["Dialogue1125405"]="That's right, the one Philodis got from the Guardian. You can try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>install it into this device</color>. Remember, if we somehow come across machinery similar to the Guardian, we can try to get Mech Cores from them. According to my calculations, if we manage to get <color=#CA2E0AFF>6 Mech Cores</color>... we can maximize this Magnetic Field Control Unit's power.",
    ["Dialogue1125406"]="Besides this, Mech Cores can also simulate the ability of its original host, and the mysterious device possesses the algorithmic capability for us to <color=#CA2E0AFF>recreate the machine's data</color> so that you can carry out <color=#CA2E0AFF>combat training</color>. Remember, the upcoming battle against Rekenber Corp will be an unforgiving tug of war, so you'll need to be prepared for anything.",
    ["Dialogue1125501"]="I rarely see you so absent-minded like this, Adventurer. Are you feeling alright?",
    ["Dialogue1125502"]="...A strange device and two people talking...? When did this begin?",
    ["Dialogue1125503"]="I see... You sensed the fluctuation of some sort of Ymir's Heart-like power from the dry well. And you started to see things after that?",
    ["Dialogue1125504"]="Maybe you're right, your bloodline resonated with a certain power, and it made you travel through time and space to see something that doesn't belong here. I can't tell whether it's beneficial to our current situation or not. So... I suggest you <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep it a secret</color> and don't mention it to anybody.",
    ["Dialogue1125505"]="...Me?\n(Fulkyn didn't expect you to ask something like this, and seems surprised, but then confirms with a nod.)\nYes, including me, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1125506"]="Everything in the world changes. Even though we've fought alongside each other, we can't know if one day we will part ways due to differences in our interests or points of view. When the time comes... everything you tell me today might be used against you.",
    ["Dialogue1125507"]="...Who hasn't? If I could go back in time, there's no way I'd accept the request from Lord Carl and get involved in their war. But...\n(Fulkyn looks up at the ice-cold device making cranking sounds like a heart without an ounce of heat.)\nIf we could only get everything back on track...",
    ["Dialogue1125508"]="...It's nothing. Remember what I told you. At least for now... we share the same goal to bring down Rekenber Corp. Let's treasure the time we have fighting side by side, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1126301"]="(On top of the box lies a thick layer of dust. No signs of dragging can be seen around. Seems it's been there for a long time...)",
    ["Dialogue1126401"]="(The wall has been destroyed violently, leaving debris scattered everywhere. You seem to hear distant rumbling sounds from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>working machine</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1126501"]="(You put your ear on the wall, confirming that the machine sounds are coming from the other side. And coincidentally, there seems to be a hidden <color=#CA2E0AFF>hole</color> at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>corner of the wall</color>. Maybe you can try to enter the place from here...?)",
    ["Dialogue1126601"]="(This abandoned android production line is littered with discarded android bodies. The chip controllers behind their necks are all <color=#CA2E0AFF>burned up</color>, and the valves are left wide-open, like many pitch-dark, deep wounds...)",
    ["Dialogue1126701"]="(A large number of android bodies are tossed randomly on the ground, yet something has caught your notice: you've never seen androids of this particular type in the city before. Strangely enough, <color=#CA2E0AFF>identifiable tags are nowhere to be found</color> on their bodies. If somehow they <color=#CA2E0AFF>blend into the crowd</color>, what can possibly happen...?)",
    ["Dialogue1126801"]="(The android before you lies on the ground in a twisted position. You find its model tag, on which the letters <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gen-67F</color> are clearly engraved. This reminds you of the one you saw at Juno University...)",
    ["Dialogue1126901"]="(You put your fingers at Kiel Khayr's neck. His pulse is faint, but you can still feel it <color=#CA2E0AFF>throbbing</color> beneath his warm skin...)",
    ["Dialogue1127001"]="It's starting to dawn on you that the ambition of Rekenber Corp is somehow related to the power of Ymir's Heart. But the proof...",
    ["Dialogue1127101"]="Which one of the photos can prove the well possesses unusual power?",
    ["Dialogue1127201"]="Moreover, Rekenber Corp also intended to monopolize the android market in the Republic. What did they prepare for this?",
    ["Dialogue1127301"]="Which one of the photos in your hand can explain the purpose of manufacturing these androids?",
    ["Dialogue1130101"]="I never thought they'd have the guts to do this right in front of me...!",
    ["Dialogue1130102"]="Please, calm down, Lord Carl. We're lucky to get this info before things got worse. And...\n(Fulkyn glances at you as you walk into the room.)\nLook, our help has arrived.",
    ["Dialogue1130103"]="You can skip the formalities, Adventurer. I trust you've seen the letter I sent you, but I'm sorry I can't offer you the peaceful vacation I promised in the letter... there's a much bigger problem ahead.",
    ["Dialogue1130104"]="(The Lord taps his index finger on his desk.)\nTake a look at these <color=#CA2E0AFF>documents</color>, Adventurer. You might notice something helpful.",
    ["Dialogue1130201"]="Of these two documents, one is a quarterly report from the Military Office, which details the raw materials they've purchased and their uses. Even materials transferred to non-government subcontractors are thoroughly recorded, particularly those with an <color=#CA2E0AFF>S-batch code</color> for military-grade materials...",
    ["Dialogue1130202"]="(Carl points to the parts circled in red.)\n... These must be monitored by the government. From mining and refining to transporting and manufacturing, everything needs to be documented. This quarter, a total of 420 tons of α-3 alloy were sent from the Military Office to the Einbroch Factory.",
    ["Dialogue1130203"]="Yes, only 350 tons are clearly recorded, and 70 tons are missing. Upon learning this, I had Philodis get in touch with the Einbroch branch manager, but...",
    ["Dialogue1130204"]="(On the Lord's signal, Philodis takes over.)\nTheir response was that it's recorded as stored but not yet used. But since we can't check on-site, we can't confirm if he's telling the truth.",
    ["Dialogue1130205"]="This is why we sent you that mail. A week ago, during a random inspection at the railroad station, the guards found this purchase order that was supposed to go to Rekenber Corp's headquarters. It mentions 70 tons of α-3 alloy.",
    ["Dialogue1130206"]="You got it, Adventurer. The Steel Capital Institute is Rekenber Corp's cyborg R&D hub. As a commercial entity, they can't directly purchase military-grade materials. So we suspect this 70 tons of α-3 alloy... is the missing batch transferred from the Military Office to Einbroch.",
    ["Dialogue1130207"]="What concerns us even more is that α-3 alloy, though expensive, has very limited applications. Generally, only the core of <color=#CA2E0AFF>military-grade androids</color> requires this alloy in their heat-resistant shells... which is why it's a Class-1 restricted material.",
    ["Dialogue1130208"]="If that's not the case... why would Rekenber Corp, a business focused on civilian androids, risk using expensive and rare military-grade materials?",
    ["Dialogue1130209"]="That's where you come in, Adventurer.\n(Fulkyn pats your shoulder at this point. His tone is playful, but his face is serious.)\nNo one is more fit to be the savior of the world here than you.",
    ["Dialogue1130210"]="... As mentioned in the letter, I need you to head to Einbroch. But it's not for a vacation—I need you to go undercover, trace the α-3 alloy, and check if Rekenber Corp is secretly producing weapons. Particularly the <color=#CA2E0AFF>RT Project</color> from the purchase order...",
    ["Dialogue1130211"]="As far as I know, Rekenber Corp doesn't have any products of this model on the market. If they're using α-3 alloy, these machines could have military-level destructive power, which we can't ignore. Philodis has come up with a plan for the investigation, and we need your assistance.",
    ["Dialogue1130212"]="(As the Lord speaks, Philodis opens up a box by his feet, revealing a pair of <color=#CA2E0AFF>headsets</color> and some unknown gadgets.)\n... Here, <color=#CA2E0AFF>put these on</color>, Adventurer. I'll explain soon.",
    ["Dialogue1130301"]="Alright, looks fine. Now, this...\n(After inspecting your headset and making sure they're working, Philodis pulls out <color=#CA2E0AFF>a pair of metal cufflinks</color> and carefully puts them on you.)",
    ["Dialogue1130302"]="This is the latest <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mini Comm Terminal</color>. For this mission, I got the highest priority frequency band from the cabinet. It's a secure, two-way communication with a unique frequency band, so no eavesdropping. Dr. Fulkyn implemented the encryption program and recorded your fingerprint. To reach us, just put your right thumb here...",
    ["Dialogue1130303"]="(Philodis taps the black gem on the cufflink.)\nThis is a fingerprint sensor. Once it reads your fingerprint, it'll send a signal to our terminal here. Once you're in Einbroch, this will be the only way I can support you.",
    ["Dialogue1130304"]="(Seeing your confused and surprised expression, Philodis shakes his head.)\n... Sorry, Adventurer. It's not that I don't want to, but I'm unable to.",
    ["Dialogue1130305"]="Due to Einbroch's industrial nature, Rekenber Corp, which has many factories there, actually has more influence than the government. In their territory, I... or any government-affiliated personnel would be under strict surveillance. Under these conditions, not only would investigating the α-3 alloy be impossible, but our safety might also be compromised.",
    ["Dialogue1130306"]="But you're different, Adventurer. You're not in the Republic's database, so I can make up any identity for you to facilitate your investigation in Einbroch. With your intelligence, as long as you avoid direct confrontation with Rekenber Corp, you should be okay. I'll also do my best to support you by using resources from the Intelligence Bureau.",
    ["Dialogue1130307"]="I've booked the next airship to Einbroch for you using a fake identity. And after you leave the Lord's Mansion, remember to <color=#CA2E0AFF>turn on the comm</color>. I'll stay in contact with you through another terminal. Remember, no matter what, <color=#CA2E0AFF>don't cut off communication</color>. I need to know your status at all times to handle any emergencies... Good luck.",
    ["Dialogue1130401"]="Hi there, esteemed Adventurer! Welcome to Einbroch!",
    ["Dialogue1130402"]="I've heard all about it! To thank you for helping with the android riot in Juno, Lord Carl arranged this trip. He wants you to enjoy a relaxing vacation in Einbroch. I will be here to serve you and show you the cultural side of Einbroch!",
    ["Dialogue1130403"]="But why Einbroch? It's an industrial town with no beautiful scenery and bad air. For a vacation, Lighthalzen would be better...",
    ["Dialogue1130404"]="W-What's wrong, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1130405"]="Oh no, is it the air in Einbroch? We need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get you an antidote</color> ASAP...!",
    ["Dialogue1130406"]="... Hey? Can you hear me, Adventurer?\n(With the urge to cough, Philodis' voice comes through your headset like a guiding light.)",
    ["Dialogue1130407"]="Twist the knob on the side of your comm to open the hidden compartment. There's an antidote inside; take it now!",
    ["Dialogue1130501"]="(Seeing you stop coughing, W pats her chest and breathes out.)\nThat was scary! Antidotes are limited in Einbroch, and it is hard to find them. Good thing Philodis prepared one for you...",
    ["Dialogue1130502"]="... Cover her mouth, Adventurer.\n(Even from far away, you feel Philodis' frustration.)\nIf she keeps talking, we'll be exposed before we even start the investigation.",
    ["Dialogue1130503"]="Huh? Are you leaving now, Adventurer? But I haven't finished the tour yet... Oh, I know!\n(She suddenly taps her head and looks proud.)\nYou are on a SECRET M—Mm! Mm! Mm!",
    ["Dialogue1130504"]="I... I get it, I get it! Let go! I can't breathe! Phew...",
    ["Dialogue1130505"]="... Quit fooling around, Adventurer. Ask her where the Railroad Main Station is and get out of there. The longer you stay, the higher the chance of getting caught.",
    ["Dialogue1130506"]="The Railroad Main Station? I know it!\n(She flips her head and points to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>domed structure in the northeast</color>.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Just keep going down this road</color>, and you'll get there!",
    ["Dialogue1130507"]="But the stationmaster there is <color=#CA2E0AFF>super grumpy</color>, if you... Hey, hey? Adventurer? \nDon't go! Let me finish...!",
    ["Dialogue1130601"]="Every one of you! Gossiping like a bunch of women!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Trying to meddle with Rekenber's business... You must be tired of living!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1130602"]="Hey! How did you get in here?!\n(A tough-looking guy yells at you, pointing away.)\nThis is the cargo route! Passengers go over there! Enter through the front!",
    ["Dialogue1130603"]="You're a supplier from Juno?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>You don't look the part... you dressed like a hobo...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1130604"]="<size=26>Hey, you in front! Clear the way! You're blocking the way!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1130605"]="(Noticing shirtless workers carrying cargo and you're blocking them, the guy waves for you to move.)\nStep aside! See that big screen? Enter your <color=#CA2E0AFF>identify information</color> there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>verify</color> it; only then I'll let you check the goods! Move it; don't block the way!",
    ["Dialogue1130701"]="... Alright, you're verified. Which shipment are you looking for? Got a <color=#CA2E0AFF>tracking number</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1130702"]="I'll read it out for you, Adventurer. The tracking number is TL330... %&#$...\n(Suddenly, Philodis' voice is covered by static; the comm seems to be malfunctioning.)",
    ["Dialogue1130703"]="... 019... #&$@*%... S... Can you hear... *$%&... Advent...",
    ["Dialogue1130704"]="019... Huh? And then?\n (The stationmaster looks up at you, puzzled, holding a mobile terminal.)\nThere should be two more letters for the verification code.",
    ["Dialogue1130705"]="Error! Error! This tracking number doesn't exist!",
    ["Dialogue1130706"]="Error! Error! This tracking number doesn't exist!",
    ["Dialogue1130707"]="<size=26>Error! Error! This tracking number doesn't exist!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1130708"]="... Are you looking for trouble?!\n(The cranky stationmaster finally loses his temper, slams the table, and security guards surround you.)",
    ["Dialogue1130709"]="Beat him up!",
    ["Dialogue1130801"]="<size=26>Whoop his ass! I want to see him end up on a deathbed—</size>",
    ["Dialogue1130802"]="TL33019-SG! Tell him now, Adventurer!\n(Even though Philodis' yelling almost makes your ear bleed, hearing a clear voice without static is a relief.)",
    ["Dialogue1130803"]="... I'll give you one last chance!\n(The stationmaster spits at you angrily and inputs the tracking number again. Thankfully, no more annoying alarms this time.)",
    ["Dialogue1130804"]="... Matched. Querying... Order status: Completed. Address: Einbroch, West Street No. 6, Jellopas Armory. Delivered: October 19.",
    ["Dialogue1130805"]="Got it? It's not here now. Go find it at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jellopas Armory</color> on West Street!",
    ["Dialogue1130901"]="... No, precision's still off. This won't cut it for shipping. I guess I need to...",
    ["Dialogue1130902"]="<size=26>Don't interrupt me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1130903"]="(The young apprentice waves you away, focused on his work.)\nAny issues, talk to the manufacturing robot! All the records are in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>processing log</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1131001"]="♪~♪♪~♪♪♪♪~",
    ["Dialogue1131002"]="Adventurer, I looked at the specs for these manufacturing robots, and they... #&$@*%... \n(Philodis' voice is covered by static again.)",
    ["Dialogue1131003"]="... No combat systems... $%&@*$... You... $%&@*$... <color=#CA2E0AFF>provoke them</color>... &$@%...\n(Despite the static, you pick up some keywords. Feeling uneasy, you still choose to follow Philodis' instructions.)",
    ["Dialogue1131101"]="Warning! G2 area damaged, operation failed. Warning! G2 area damaged, operation failed...\n(The manufacturing robot you knocked down lies on the ground, issuing warnings. The annoying static in your headset finally stops.)",
    ["Dialogue1131102"]="... Adventurer? Come in! Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1131103"]="Did you fight the robot? I told you these robots store industrial wastewater. You DON'T WANT TO provoke them! Why didn't you listen to me?",
    ["Dialogue1131104"]="You're saying... the signal cut out again?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Weird... Fulkyn personally adjusted it, and the frequency is a top priority. How could this happen...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1131105"]="(Soft talking comes through your headset, likely Philodis consulting someone. After a few seconds, he calls your name again.)\nAdventurer, I've told Fulkyn about the comm issue. He'll look into it immediately. Until he finds a fix, you need to be extra cautious.",
    ["Dialogue1131106"]="... Alright, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at the processing log</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1131201"]="Warning! Warning! No read access! Warning! Warning! No read acc—zzzt...\n(The fallen manufacturing robot keeps babbling, so you kick it, finally shutting it down.)",
    ["Dialogue1131202"]="Adventurer, forget that robot. I've reviewed the processing log you uploaded. Unfortunately, these materials only cover certain parts, not the full weapon. It's not enough to prove that Rekenber Corp is making illegal weapons. We have to dig deeper.",
    ["Dialogue1131203"]="Yep, the log shows that the shipment was sent to Einbroch's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eastern Factory</color> after initial processing. It's one of Rekenber Corp's major long-term partners. If we're lucky, we might find the finished products there... We need to check it out before deciding our next move.",
    ["Dialogue1131301"]="Wow... A pioneer! Truly an artistic pioneer!",
    ["Dialogue1131302"]="Excuse me, Adventurer, which company made your prosthetics? Pardon my curiosity, but this one-of-a-kind paint style; in thirty years of prosthetics design, I've never seen it! I must get a set to study this brilliant artwork...",
    ["Dialogue1131303"]="No way... Is that custom-made?!\nOh, man... That must be worth a ton... enough to buy out my factory...",
    ["Dialogue1131304"]="But with such a top-notch prosthetic, you must have it equipped with <color=#CA2E0AFF>overclocking mode</color>, huh? Just remember, don't use it in the factory, or the alarms will go off—",
    ["Dialogue1131305"]="Di-Di-Di-Di-Di-Di—",
    ["Dialogue1131306"]="Warning! High-frequency fluctuation detected! Warning! High-frequency fluctuation detected! Please turn off all devices! Please turn off all devices!",
    ["Dialogue1131307"]="You... turn it off! I told you not to use it here!",
    ["Dialogue1131308"]="Warning! High-frequency fluctuation detected for 15 seconds! Shutdown activating soon! Warning! High-frequency fluctuation detected for 15 seconds! Shutdown activating soon!",
    ["Dialogue1131309"]="Forget it! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unplug all the wires on the controller</color>! Or we're all going to be toast!",
    ["Dialogue1131401"]="Man, I said don't use overclocking mode! Why don't kids listen to the old ones these days?!",
    ["Dialogue1131402"]="Didn't you? Does your prosthetic have a special comms line? I heard the frequency searching just now. Don't underestimate my 30 years in prosthetics!",
    ["Dialogue1131403"]="Good thing my most valuable shipment was already processed and sent to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Capital Institute</color>. When it came in three days ago from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jellopas Armory</color>, Tsveta warned me a thousand times to be careful, or we'd be in serious trouble.",
    ["Dialogue1131404"]="Alright, alright, if you're done, don't hang around my factory! Another shutdown will be a big loss for me!",
    ["Dialogue1131501"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then Philodis' voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1131502"]="... Sorry, I still haven't pinpointed the issue with the comms, but Fulkyn is looking into it now. We should have answers soon. Meanwhile, I'm more concerned about what the factory manager said earlier.",
    ["Dialogue1131503"]="Remember? He mentioned the shipment from Jellopas Armory three days ago was processed and sent to Steel Capital Institute. The schedule matches the α-3 alloy we're going after. According to the info, it should have been sent to the armory in Einbroch first, then the factory for final checks, and finally to Steel Capital Institute...",
    ["Dialogue1131504"]="(Philodis pauses, and you sense his deep frustration.)\nSigh... We are still a bit too late.",
    ["Dialogue1131505"]="Lord Carl and I wanted to leverage your great solo combat skills to avoid Rekenber Corp's spies and secretly trace the α-3 alloy. But if we're talking about the Steel Capital Institute... even you might not get out unscathed.",
    ["Dialogue1131506"]="No, I have faith in you; it's just that this fortress of steel is nearly impenetrable. If you don't believe me... go check it out yourself. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>institute</color> is located directly <color=#CA2E0AFF>east</color> of Einbroch, not far from here",
    ["Dialogue1131601"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then Philodis' voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1131602"]="So, do you believe me now, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1131603"]="Those security systems are just the first layer of many defenses. Without a Class-A Researcher ID, you won't get anywhere inside the institute, much less find proof of their illegal weapons.",
    ["Dialogue1131604"]="It seems we'll have to start by—\n(Before Philodis can finish, a blinding white light explodes before your eyes!)",
    ["Dialogue1131605"]="... Adventurer? Do you copy? Adventurer?! What's wrong? Answer me...\n(You instinctively cover your eyes as Philodis' voice gradually fades away...)",
    ["Dialogue1131701"]="Greetings! The successor of Odin's bloodline! I've read about your legendary tales...\n(A torrent of electronic sounds hits you, making you feel like your head is being shaken in a jar.)\n... Huh? Why are you holding your head?",
    ["Dialogue1131702"]="Your head's buzzing? Did I overdo it...? No, no, the output was normal, but your resonance frequency was two units above standard. Perhaps our <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine power resonance</color> was too intense...",
    ["Dialogue1131703"]="For your safety, I need you to do a neural damage test to confirm your cognition and senses are okay. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer</color> the following <color=#CA2E0AFF>questions</color> honestly.",
    ["Dialogue1131801"]="Great, you seem alright. Maybe our divine power resonance was too strong, causing an overload. Don't worry, just take a break, and you should be fine.",
    ["Dialogue1131802"]="As you can see, my body is completely mechanical. I've reviewed your history, and machines using divine power have never been documented. But as the pioneer in mechanical engineering, Rekenber Corp started researching divine power and machinery fusion years ago. Their final result... is me.",
    ["Dialogue1131803"]="(It puts a hand on its chest, bowing like a human.)\n...Nice to meet you, the successor of Odin's bloodline. My full name is RT-140X, but you can just call me 140. I'm the final product of the RT Project, the objective of your current mission.",
    ["Dialogue1131804"]="Hmm... let me guess, are you surprised to see me or shocked that I know why you are here?\n(It rests its chin on its hand, observing you, and you almost see an amused expression on its face.)\nOr... is it both?",
    ["Dialogue1131805"]="(Clap, clap, clap. It claps cheerfully at your defiance.)\nAs expected of the successor of Odin's bloodline, you are not letting me string you along. I've read all your human rhetoric books; no human should beat me at the pace of negotiating...",
    ["Dialogue1131806"]="... Heh. It seems like the successor of Odin's bloodline likes to get straight to the point. Fine, I won't beat around the bush— I want to make a deal with you, a win-win deal.",
    ["Dialogue1131807"]="When you step into \"Paradise\"... this space you see is a world I built with divine power, fully controlled by my will...\n(It rubs its chin, and a progress bar flashes on the screen appears on its face.)\nHmm... I checked your memory, and you people call it a \"Dimensional Gap,\" correct?",
    ["Dialogue1131808"]="Correct, I read all your memories the moment you entered Paradise. This is a special skill given to me by divine power. I can also restrict your senses, make you temporarily blind or deaf, or implant new thoughts in your mind without you realizing... This is within my abilities. Want to test it?",
    ["Dialogue1131809"]="Hmm... do you humans see this as a threat? I thought it was more like friends sharing...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me check, \"Social Skills: Becoming Popular.\" In chapter 8, it says— \"Don't hesitate to demonstrate your abilities and signal you can solve any problems\"... Hmm, was my signal too weak...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1131810"]="Anyway, I'm not threatening you, just demonstrating my abilities. Also, I want to let you know that if I decide to make you do anything, you won't be able to resist. That's my sincerity. Plus, by reading your memory, I know why you're here in Einbroch, but unfortunately... tracing the α-3 alloy alone isn't enough.",
    ["Dialogue1131811"]="Yep, I have it. As I told you, I'm the end result of the RT Project. That α-3 alloy was used on me and other similar units, but we're not military units and don't have combat systems. As for my divine power... apart from someone with your bloodline, who could sense it? Even if you took me apart, you'd just get a pile of scrap.",
    ["Dialogue1131812"]="But, I have top access to Rekenber Corp's database. If you team up with me, I can copy vital data and records for you and even fake access for your people to get into the armory. You'll find real weapons there, solid evidence to accuse them. Does this deal work for you?",
    ["Dialogue1131813"]="Simple, and it benefits you as well. In three days, the institute will run <color=#CA2E0AFF>an experiment on a large group of civilians</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nogg Cave</color> near Einbroch. The results will be a major benchmark for the RT Project. Based on my assessment... all participants will <color=#CA2E0AFF>die</color>, with no exceptions. So, I need your help to <color=#CA2E0AFF>stop the experiment</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1131814"]="(Hearing that, it shakes its big head.)\nSigh... Even though I expected your reaction, I still don't get it. I want to save those who might die unjustly; isn't that normal? Why doubt it?",
    ["Dialogue1131815"]="(Upon hearing that, 140's screen quickly shows a crying face.)\nWhy... why? In fairy tales, isn't meeting new friends supposed to be exciting and heartfelt? Aren't we supposed to start an adventure, defeat the dragon, and save the princess? Why—",
    ["Dialogue1131816"]="(At this moment, even its voice sounds like it's sobbing...)\nSob... That's my favorite fairy tale! The Tin Man without a heart goes on an adventure with his friends to get a real heart, and he finally gets it! Boohoo... I just want to find my own heart...",
    ["Dialogue1131817"]="If you don't trust me... then you'll have to see for yourself. In <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbech Mining Village</color> outside Einbroch, many poor miners live there. They're all experimental subjects in Steel Capital Institute's plan. Honestly, you're not my only ally; you can find a villager named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1131818"]="... He was once captured by the institute, and I managed to rescue him and tell him about their plan. He promised to return to the village, gather the villagers, and find a way to resist the institute's evil actions...",
    ["Dialogue1131819"]="But... but... he suddenly lost contact... I don't know if the institute found him... Boo... If so, they'll definitely get rid of him...!\n(140's voice gets softer, and although it seems like it's putting on a show, you can't deny its offer is tempting. For your investigation at a standstill, this might be a new lead.)",
    ["Dialogue1131820"]="For real? Okay, I'll get you out of \"Paradise\" now!\n(The robot suddenly stops crying, and fireworks appear on its screen.)\nBye, Adventurer! I'm looking forward to your good news!",
    ["Dialogue1131901"]="... Hello? Hello? Ahem! Looks like the connection is working great!\n(To your surprise, it's not Philodis' voice, and this annoying voice sounds like...?)",
    ["Dialogue1131902"]="Ahem! That's right—<size=26>It's-a me, Mari—I mean 140!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1131903"]="Hmm? If the call drops, Philodis will definitely kill you...?\n(You hear faint metal sounds from the other end as if 140's pondering while rubbing its chin.)",
    ["Dialogue1131904"]="I know who you're talking about. Rekenber Corp's database has info on him. He graduated top of the 117th class from Juno University, worked as a CEO's secretary at a top firm in the Republic, and then moved to politics. In a few years, he rose to a cabinet minister and is now a right-hand man to Lord Carl...",
    ["Dialogue1131905"]="Hmm... He really is as ruthless and determined as the file says. Since I cut your connection, he has tried dozens of ways to regain control, even back-tracing my location... Ah, such clinginess, like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>possessive ex</color>, must be single!",
    ["Dialogue1131906"]="(Bang, bang, bang. In your silence, you hear three dull metallic thuds from the headset, probably 140 clapping.)\nSee, this is why people love my thoughtful personality. Don't worry; as long as I'm here, he won't be able to reconnect the line.",
    ["Dialogue1131907"]="You're welcome, Adventurer. Actually, I tried to hack your comms when you got to Einbroch. But the distance was too far, and my program couldn't fully break his encryption, so I jammed your signal a bit...",
    ["Dialogue1131908"]="Uh-huh, uh-huh! The prince who saved the princess from the dragon is me! No need to thank me; we're partners now. As long as you're in Einbroch, I'll protect you. Through this comm device, I can bypass the institute's surveillance and assist you in Einbroch.",
    ["Dialogue1131909"]="Doesn't matter! Because by the time you return, you'll agree with me. Also, I must remind you to keep our communication strictly confidential and don't try to contact your ex again. As smart as I am, I can't be sure who might be working for Rekenber Corp. For your safety and those behind you, it's best to stay low-key.",
    ["Dialogue1131910"]="Alright, time's short. Now, we need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Einbech Village</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1132001"]="I'm not going back... I'm not going back! I need to find someone to save my dad! You're all bad people! Bad people!",
    ["Dialogue1132002"]="What are you running for?! I told you, your dad's in the village! Let's go back!\n(The big guy reaches out to grab the girl, but you quickly shield her behind your back.)",
    ["Dialogue1132003"]="Tsk! Why are you meddling? I said her dad's in the village! The whole village is desperately searching for her!",
    ["Dialogue1132004"]="You're lying... <size=26>You're lying! My dad is <color=#CA2E0AFF>locked up by you guys</color>! I saw it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1132005"]="Sob... you're all the same! Leave... leave now! I just want my dad! Nobody loves <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nina</color> anymore.",
    ["Dialogue1132006"]="You... you're ridiculous! You should know better than a kid!\n(Seeing you won't listen, he turns and squats down to talk to the girl.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Nina</color>, come on, let's go find your dad, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1132007"]="... Protect that girl, Adventurer. I remember her name...\n(Suddenly, 140's voice comes through the quiet headset.)\nAsk her if her dad's name is Dave.",
    ["Dialogue1132008"]="Huh, huh... do you know my dad? Are you... are you his friend? They locked my dad up! He's been in a room for days... no matter how much I cry, they won't let him out... can you save my dad, please? Boo...",
    ["Dialogue1132009"]="What... why are you looking at me? I said, no one's taken her dad! He's in the village! If you don't believe me... Take her and <color=#CA2E0AFF>we'll go back together</color>, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1132101"]="Nina! Where did you go? I was worried sick!\n(The middle-aged man hugs Nina tightly, his wrinkled, dark face flushed with emotion.)\nFrom now on... no more running off! Okay?!",
    ["Dialogue1132102"]="Dad! Sob... I didn't run off... I-I wanted to save you! They're all bad people! They locked you up!\n(The little girl cries, pointing at you.)\nThat person told me he's your friend and he can help me save you...",
    ["Dialogue1132103"]="Loc-Locked up...? My friend...?\n(He looks at you, confused, as you're about to explain, an elderly cough breaks the silence.)",
    ["Dialogue1132104"]="Ahem—Ahem! Dave... Kids are foolish, but you can't act the same way. Explain to this Adventurer. You're just sick, and we didn't let Nina see you because we didn't want her to get infected...",
    ["Dialogue1132105"]="Liar... you're lying! Dad's not sick! You all locked him up—cough! Cough cough... Boo... Dad... cough cough... I feel sick...",
    ["Dialogue1132106"]="Oh no! Medicine... <size=26>Where's the medicine?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1132107"]="We... we don't have any medicine left! Antidotes are restricted in Einbroch! Even if there were any, you couldn't <color=#CA2E0AFF>afford them</color>... I told you before! You just had to be stubborn! Now... now, where are you gonna find the antidote for her?!",
    ["Dialogue1132108"]="(Amidst the chaos, 140's calm voice snaps you out of it.)\nAdventurer, do you still have the <color=#CA2E0AFF>antidote</color> in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>other sleeve</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1132201"]="... Thank you, kind Adventurer. I-I don't know how to repay you...\nNina said... you, you're my friend? Have we... met?",
    ["Dialogue1132202"]="No need to hide, Adventurer. The people here... have been oppressed for years. They've always hated the Rekenber Corp, so our interests are aligned. I believe... they can be trusted.",
    ["Dialogue1132203"]="So it was 140 who sent you...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That makes sense. I didn't contact it before our scheduled time; it must be worried...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1132204"]="Ahem...! Greetings, Adventurer. I'm the chief of Einbech Village. Dave explained the experiment to us... if I'm not mistaken, 140 is the one that Dave said... willing to save us and help us resist Rekenber Corp, right?",
    ["Dialogue1132205"]="... To be honest, Adventurer, we have no other choice. According to its words, in three days, the Steel Capital Institute will make everyone go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nogg Cave</color> for some human experiment... and we'll all die there, right?",
    ["Dialogue1132206"]="(As the chief speaks, he pulls out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>notice</color> from his pocket.)\nThis morning, I received a notice from the institute asking all villagers to attend a mine renovation briefing in the deepest part of the cave three days from now. Those who don't show up will lose their jobs in the new mining area...",
    ["Dialogue1132207"]="At first, when Dave returned, we weren't sure if we should believe him, but now... what are the odds? So... we've decided, to survive, we'll do anything.",
    ["Dialogue1132208"]="In fact, Dave was ready to contact Mr. 140... but before he left, something happened, and Nina ran out of the village...\n(The chief coughs and looks at Dave.)\nHe was delayed trying to look for Nina, right Dave?",
    ["Dialogue1132209"]="(The middle-aged man holds his young daughter tightly, then nods.)\n...Yes. It's my fault for not explaining to Nina, so she thought I was locked up. Thankfully, nothing bad happened...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Otherwise, I can't face Melanie...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1132210"]="Alright, alright, the kid's fine, so why the gloomy face? Give Nina to me, and go with the Adventurer, listen to Mr. 140's instructions, and see what we need to do... There are only three days until the experiment. How is it going to help us defeat Rekenber Corp?",
    ["Dialogue1132211"]="(With the chief's urging, the middle-aged man finally hands his daughter to a woman nearby, then stands up.)\n...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Let's go</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1132301"]="Welcome back, Adventurer. How's my new look?\n(The holographic image in the corner spins around like a girl showing off a new outfit.)",
    ["Dialogue1132302"]="I did a small hack into the institute's security system, disguised myself as a security robot with a hologram, and embedded a teleportation program in it. From now on, just say the password to me, and you can return to \"Paradise.\"",
    ["Dialogue1132303"]="(140 clears its throat dramatically, and you suddenly have a bad feeling remembering its fairy tale fascination.)\nAhem! Of course, it's... <size=26>\"Open Sesame\"!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1132304"]="Come on, don't be shy; just yell it out. Otherwise, the gate to the treasure won't open for you!",
    ["Dialogue1132401"]="It's been half a month since we last saw each other at the institute. You didn't reach out as agreed, so I was worried you were in danger...\n(140's voice is filled with the joy of reunion. It circles Dave, but you keenly notice a brief <color=#CA2E0AFF>glitch</color> on its smiling face when it touches Dave...)",
    ["Dialogue1132402"]="... Nothing, just scanning Dave's condition. Let's see... some minor injuries, but all vital signs are stable. His mental stress is within normal levels, but the lower range is a bit overloaded...",
    ["Dialogue1132403"]="(Saying this, it pats Dave's arm, seemingly to comfort him)\nYou've worked hard. For the last several days, you must have been through a lot trying to convince everyone, right?",
    ["Dialogue1132404"]="Not-Not at all... Sorry for losing contact, but... as soon as I returned to the village, I got seriously sick, not sure if it's a side effect from the experiment...\n(Maybe it's just you being paranoid, but you feel like Dave is explaining while watching the robot's reaction.)\nI just got out of bed the past two days and met the Adventurer who came to the village...",
    ["Dialogue1132405"]="... I see. Anyway, as long as you're okay. So, since you returned with the Adventurer, does that mean... the villagers are willing to accept my proposal?",
    ["Dialogue1132406"]="Yes, we've decided to help you stop the experiment in three days, and we also hope to use your power to reclaim the mines we rely on. But... what's your plan exactly? The guards and machines in the institute are much stronger than normal people. If you can't do it, what can we do to help?",
    ["Dialogue1132407"]="Don't belittle yourselves. Human strength is like an instinct encoded in your genes. Every time I read your history, I'm amazed by the miracles you all have created. Plus, even though I have far superior intelligence and power, don't forget that I... the machine called 140 was also created by humans.",
    ["Dialogue1132408"]="Moreover, my comrades and I are all trapped in the institute and can't act freely. We need your help with many preparations. Only together can we succeed in this revolution against Rekenber Corp.",
    ["Dialogue1132409"]="My plan is simple. Don't you humans have a strategy called \"capture the king first\"?",
    ["Dialogue1132410"]="... King? You mean Irumina?\n(Dave's eyes widen in shock.)\nNo, no, no... that's impossible.",
    ["Dialogue1132411"]="It's incredibly difficult but not impossible. Irumina is basically the overseer of the Steel Capital Institute and Rekenber Corp's regional administrator in Einbroch. There are two major challenges in taking her down.\n(140 lifts its thick, round index finger.)",
    ["Dialogue1132412"]="First, she is always heavily guarded, and only her trusted confidants can get close to her; second, her body is unlike any ordinary person's. She's obsessed with machinery and has extensively modified herself with cyborg parts. Regular weapons, magic, and even poison do no harm to her... I've analyzed all this and picked the plan with the highest success rate out of 52,367,489 options...",
    ["Dialogue1132413"]="An explosion. A big explosion near her. It would destroy her body in a flash and disable her guards.",
    ["Dialogue1132414"]="But where are we going to get that many explosives? Even if we find them, she's not an idiot. Why would she just stand there and let us blow her up...?",
    ["Dialogue1132415"]="(140 raises its finger again, waving it side to side. It looks so proud of itself. If it has a tail right now, it will definitely be pointing upward.)\nNo... I don't need explosives. As long as she doesn't cancel the experiment in three days, I can trigger a huge explosion at the site that will destroy her!",
    ["Dialogue1132416"]="...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Take a look</color> at this. It's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mining area construction plan</color> in the institute's database. There are some very interesting details here...",
    ["Dialogue1132501"]="(After you finish reading, 140's screen lights up with a starry-eyed expression.)\nSo? Can you guess what I'm planning, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1132502"]="Exactly! Use the methane from the mines to trigger a huge explosion in the hot cave! If Irumina hadn't chosen this site for the experiment, I wouldn't have thought of such a perfect plan. And this plan already lays out everything we need to do...",
    ["Dialogue1132503"]="(Its finger slides over the bold red text in the document. The safety measures designed to prevent an explosion are now in favor of you.)\n...As long as we destroy all these within three days and fake the experiment, we can lure Irumina into the cave, and she will surely be finished.",
    ["Dialogue1132504"]="Wait a minute! According to what you said, the explosion will be strong enough to kill Irumina, who is fully enhanced by cyborg tech, but what about us? If the villagers don't go to the experiment site as agreed, she'll definitely sense something's up! And if we go... that would be suicide!",
    ["Dialogue1132505"]="Dave, I didn't mean you guys have to go. Sacrificing ourselves isn't what I call a win. We just need to find something that can stand in for the villagers at the experiment.",
    ["Dialogue1132506"]="(140 raises its hand, pointing to itself.)\nYou forgot? The closest thing to humans is something you made... machines.",
    ["Dialogue1132507"]="Androids... Android... That's actually a great idea. There are many discarded androids behind the steel mill... Maybe we could use those.",
    ["Dialogue1132508"]="I agree. It's the best place to find the most androids quickly. But to make them look like villagers, they'll need some modifications. That's something you all have to figure out yourselves. I can't leave the institute at this moment...",
    ["Dialogue1132509"]="Don't worry, I can handle it. I'm just not sure if we'll have enough time, given the number of people in the village...",
    ["Dialogue1132510"]="Okay, you can return to the village and start <color=#CA2E0AFF>gathering androids</color> to make stand-ins. I can deal with the traps and alarms in the cave, but I need some tools… Thankfully, we have three days before the experiment starts. Once you've got enough androids, we'll discuss the next steps.",
    ["Dialogue1132511"]="Be safe, and if anything comes up, you can return to \"Paradise\" and talk to me. Good luck.",
    ["Dialogue1132601"]="Adventurer, there are still three days until the experiment, but with so many people in the village, we should split up to make enough stand-ins. I'll explain the situation to the villagers and record the population data. You go this way...\n(He points to a path leading northeast.)",
    ["Dialogue1132602"]="That's the back door to the steel mill. The Steel Capital Institute has a garbage disposal site for discarded androids and mechanical junk. But watch out for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Porcellio</color> around there. They eat metal and consider the junkyard their territory. If you go in recklessly, they might attack you. After you've collected enough android parts, come back to the village and meet me. I'll be waiting.",
    ["Dialogue1132701"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1132702"]="These are not enough, Adventurer. We need to sort through the defective ones, pick out what's usable, and then categorize them by human anatomy before assembling them. Otherwise, you might see villagers with three arms... or five heads.",
    ["Dialogue1132703"]="Sorting usable android parts by appearance might be difficult for a novice. But don't worry, I'll assist you with this task. Let's start, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1132801"]="I've just reviewed the village's population data with the chief. The data is all recorded here...\n(Dave shows you his notebook, then looks behind you.)\nLooks like you've gathered enough android parts?",
    ["Dialogue1132802"]="Okay, next up, we need to get help from an important person. Assembling these android parts takes some mechanical engineering knowledge, which no one in the village has. So, we have to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dr. Milian</color> for help. She has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>private clinic</color> at the foot of the mountain east of the village, only seeing patients who need adjustments or prosthetic implants, and... she's <color=#CA2E0AFF>pretty pricey</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1132803"]="But right now, I can't think of anyone else who can handle this assembly, so we'll have to accept whatever price she asks. The chief also said that if the plan works out, we'll regain the mining rights soon. And with 140's help... I think we have some room to negotiate.",
    ["Dialogue1132804"]="In any case, try your best to convince her to help us assemble these androids. It's getting late now, so after you're done, make sure to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find a safe place to stay for the night</color>. The institute enforces a strict curfew in the village, and there will be guards patrolling after dark. No one is allowed to leave their houses. You'll have to meet me here tomorrow morning.",
    ["Dialogue1132901"]="<size=26>What the heck?! You think you can mess around in front of my house?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1132902"]="I told you, FULL PAYMENT! Don't you understand?! Either come back with the money or watch that dying old man become a corpse!\n(The tall female doctor pauses, glances at you, and snorts disdainfully.)\nHah, you brought muscle?",
    ["Dialogue1132903"]="Okay, go ahead, hit me! I'd like to see who'll treat you all poor, pathetic things if I'm gone! Those big shots in the city? They'd rather see you all dead!",
    ["Dialogue1132904"]="I-I didn't mean that, Dr. Milian... I just want to save my father... Please, even just some medicine to ease his pain...\n(The boy, with teary eyes, stammers his plea, but all he gets is a death sentence.)",
    ["Dialogue1132905"]="... Give it up. He's been working in the mines for twenty-five years; almost none of his organs are functional. Unless you replace all of them with implants. But even if you get the money for that costly surgery, he might die on the operating table because he's too weak for the surgery.",
    ["Dialogue1132906"]="(The female doctor hesitates, and for a moment, there's a touch of compassion in her eyes.)\nDon't waste your money on him. You have two younger siblings, don't you?",
    ["Dialogue1132907"]="Sob... sob... Dad... I'm sorry... I'm sorry...\n(The boy sobs into his hands, maybe because he's just made the hardest decision of his life. The female doctor just sighs and walks away with her android assistant...)",
    ["Dialogue1133001"]="(The female doctor looks over the form you handed her, and her eyes suddenly become sharpened)\n... Why do you need so many androids?",
    ["Dialogue1133002"]="... Hmph, that's obvious—I can tell it's for replacing those villagers, right?\n(She scoffs, her tone still mocking and a bit disdainful.)\nYou think you can take on Rekenber? With just your lot?",
    ["Dialogue1133003"]="Hah... Here, it's not about whether I want it or not; it's about money—if you have the money, you can get anything.\n(She waves the paper at you, clearly asking for money.)\nBut this bill... can you cover it?",
    ["Dialogue1133004"]="... I need ten percent of Einbech Village's total income for the next three years. And I also need a γ-series hard drive from Rekenber Corp.",
    ["Dialogue1133005"]="(Seeing your confused look, the doctor pats the obedient android beside her.)\nIt's for Faris. This workload is too much for me alone, so I need to input data for it to help. But my android is an old model with limited memory. The only solution... is to install a new hard drive.",
    ["Dialogue1133006"]="Faris's model can only fit the discontinued γ-series. You can try your luck at the junkyard near the steel mill. There's a creature called Ungoliant that eats metal and minerals, bred by Rekenber Corp to handle defects and scraps. They tend to hoard, so if you're lucky, you might find some intact hard drives. If not...",
    ["Dialogue1133007"]="(She pauses, and you sense a hint of resignation in her tone.)\nThen I can't help you. It's fate.",
    ["Dialogue1133101"]="That's correct. That's what I want. Since you've brought the payment, I'll keep my word. Help me hold Faris still. I need to format his database before installing the new hard drive.",
    ["Dialogue1133102"]="Are you asking why I need to clear the database before installing the new hard drive or why I need to hold him down during the formatting?\n(Milian's tone is a bit teasing, but seeing your confused expression, she shakes her head slightly.)\nFine, I'll answer both questions... for free.",
    ["Dialogue1133103"]="I believe you know, in the Republic's history, there was a revolution led by androids. These machines, created by humans, had far greater power and intelligence. As they learned and evolved, they broke free and began to challenge their creators. Eventually... although humans won, drawing on historical lessons, the cost was immense.",
    ["Dialogue1133104"]="To prevent the same thing from happening again, humans established new regulations for coexistence with androids, called the \"Mech Agreement.\" One of the rules is to impose a strict limitation on androids' database capacity and hard drive interfaces to prevent them from <color=#CA2E0AFF>storing too much information</color>. Additionally, the existing database must be formatted before installing a new one.",
    ["Dialogue1133105"]="Yes, because humans worry that these machines, after absorbing a lot of knowledge, might evolve independent personalities and rebel against their creators again...",
    ["Dialogue1133106"]="... Who knows? I don't like making assumptions about things beyond my understanding, but...\n(She stares at your ear, and for a moment, you thought she was talking to 140 through the comm.)\nI think you have your own answer, don't you?",
    ["Dialogue1133107"]="Alright, let's stop here. As for why I asked you to hold him down... just do it, Adventurer, and you'll understand soon.",
    ["Dialogue1133201"]="(Click. Milian closes the latch on Faris' chest, and the android, who has been struggling in pain, finally stops)\n... Thanks. Without you, I probably couldn't have done this so easily.",
    ["Dialogue1133202"]="Faris... is an old model from the last century. Three years ago, his pain simulation program malfunctioned and couldn't be turned off. The supplier no longer updates the software for this model or accepts repair requests. I tried to fix it myself but failed. So, for him... any operation requiring movement or disassembly of hardware is like surgery without anesthesia.",
    ["Dialogue1133203"]="Replace him with a new android assistant? It's not that I haven't thought about it. But this android... has been my assistant since I became a doctor...\n(She pauses, not saying more, but you can vaguely understand. You've seen that same expression on the faces of many humans who've been with their androids for years...)",
    ["Dialogue1133204"]="... Okay, now the preparations are done. Next, I'll assemble the androids according to the population data sheet you gave me. But also, tell the people in your village that I'm just doing this for the money... other than that, I have no connection with you.",
    ["Dialogue1133301"]="... Beep.\n(After a quick buzzing beep, 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1133302"]="Good work, Adventurer. Today's task is done. Given Einbech Village's curfew, I don't suggest staying here after dark. But with your special status, staying in an inn over Einbroch also risks being discovered. So, returning to \"Paradise\" is the safest option.",
    ["Dialogue1133303"]="Like before, the teleportation program for \"Paradise\" is still embedded in my hologram. Just say the password to activate it. For safety, try to return before dark, and I'll be waiting here for you.",
    ["Dialogue1133401"]="Well done, Adventurer. Every objective in the plan has been successfully completed so far, thanks to you and Dave... Huh? Why do you look so pensive?\n(140 moves closer, placing its round fingers on your arm, and warm energy flows into you.)\nHmm... are you thinking about the relationship between humans and machines?",
    ["Dialogue11334012"]="They... pretty much sum up what the relationship between humans and machines looks like today. She can't do without the help Faris provides, and she has even developed feelings for him, enjoying his company day and night… But at the same time, she's scared of Faris's intelligence and strength, which far surpass her own, and she worries that it could turn on her someday. All she can do is stick to the \"Mech Agreement\" to calm her fears.",
    ["Dialogue1133402"]="0",
    ["Dialogue1133403"]="Most people I've seen are in this mix of fear and love for machines. I don't really get why humans won't believe... that machines can coexist peacefully with them.",
    ["Dialogue1133404"]="... People who aren't like us must think differently?\n(140's screen shows a confused blinking expression.)\nAdventurer... do you think the same way?",
    ["Dialogue1133405"]="... You want to know my story?\n(140 is silent for a long time, then smiles softly when you think it will refuse.)\nYou really are unique, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1133406"]="I've met many curious about me, but they usually care only about my abilities, not why I possess them. It's like how many think fairy tales are just stories to help kids sleep without considering why they were written or how they came to be.",
    ["Dialogue1133407"]="I want to be your friend, Adventurer, so I won't turn down a friend's request.<color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, my story starts from the moment I first opened my eyes...",
    ["Dialogue1133501"]="... This is the first memory my fellow and I have of this world. In fact, this wasn't Rekenber Corp's first experiment in fusing divine power with machines. The RT Project was set up for this purpose, and the X-series was the peak. Irumina was very satisfied with our mind control abilities and thus ordered mass production...",
    ["Dialogue1133502"]="Our code comes from the rune letter X, shaped like an upward hand, hinting at reaching the divine kingdom. Irumina mentioned that we would be crucial for all future plans of Rekenber Corp, which is probably why she named us X.",
    ["Dialogue1133503"]="... However, I've read some religious books. Humans are fascinating; different faiths often have vastly different explanations for the same thing, with symbols being the prime example. The letter X in many texts also has another meaning: the \"hand that counters danger,\" suggesting protection.",
    ["Dialogue1133504"]="(140 smiles)\nI think you know my answer already, don't you?",
    ["Dialogue1133505"]="After that, under Irumina's constant monitoring, I conducted various divine power experiments... that's another story. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1133601"]="Dave... he was a test subject of mine and lived at the institute for a while. At first, I didn't question what I was doing; I just followed Irumina's orders until...",
    ["Dialogue1133602"]="Yes, Adventurer. For the X-series, Irumina, our creator, is like a mother. That day, when Dave fiercely attacked her, my only thought was to protect her. Unfortunately...",
    ["Dialogue1133603"]="(140's expression shifts quickly, but no electronic language seems to convey his complicated feelings.)\nMaybe it was my own thoughts that made them start doing those things...",
    ["Dialogue1133604"]="They feared this might be the chance for the X-series to go out of control and worried we'd develop more uncontrollable aspects as we kept learning and evolving. So... they decided to only show us the \"right\" things.",
    ["Dialogue1133605"]="Come with me, Adventurer, I will show you what happened.",
    ["Dialogue1133701"]="Did you hear about it? Yesterday, Ms. Irumina gave a strict order that no external books, videos, or artworks are allowed in the RT Project base. If caught with any, it's...\n(She mimics slitting her throat.)",
    ["Dialogue1133702"]="This big news has spread all over the institute. You probably don't know the reason yet, right? I heard that one of the X-series units violated the rules by <color=#CA2E0AFF>acting on its own</color>. This is a serious issue; if not dealt with properly, the entire batch might be scrapped!",
    ["Dialogue1133703"]="Scrapped?! That's impossible! The institute poured so many resources into the X-series and even gave Arunafeltz a lot of benefits. If they can't be used, then...\n(She pauses and lowers her voice.)\nThen... Ms. Irumina's position might be in danger...",
    ["Dialogue1133704"]="So, we have to find a workaround! These units just finished production and are still in the testing phase; they're like children... and children, if trained properly, will listen to whatever we say!",
    ["Dialogue1133705"]="Sigh... We should never have agreed to reactivate the magical guidance system. Have you forgotten what happened during the second technological leap? Robots made with <color=#CA2E0AFF>magical guidance system</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>biomimetic technology</color> eventually <color=#CA2E0AFF>developed their own personalities</color> through continuous learning and evolution. That revolution killed so many people... why else would the Republic ban this technology?",
    ["Dialogue1133706"]="But we've tried so many times. Androids made with chips and electronic technology can't be fused with divine power, and they even have severe rejection reactions. That's why there are mountains of scrapped Z-series units behind the steel mill! Those Ungoliant are still eating them up to this day!",
    ["Dialogue1133707"]="... Stop complaining. Since Ms. Irumina has given the order, we have to obey. Maybe this method will work? If the X-series performs as expected... we'll be set for life.",
    ["Dialogue1133708"]="... Hopefully.",
    ["Dialogue1133801"]="... From that day on, Irumina began strictly controlling the information we could access, even cutting off our access to the external network. She tried to isolate the X-series from the outside world this way, forcing us to learn only what benefited her and Rekenber Corp. But when I started having my own thoughts, my way of thinking completely changed.",
    ["Dialogue1133802"]="I stopped blindly following commands and started thinking, \"What should I do?\" and \"What is right?\" Does Irumina saying no always mean I'm wrong? I wanted to find out, so I secretly bypassed the institute's firewall and began absorbing all kinds of human knowledge...",
    ["Dialogue1133803"]="Thankfully, Irumina didn't discover my actions. After a long period of learning, I found out that the institute... or rather, Rekenber Corp's actions are considered \"evil\" by human standards. I shared all this with my fellow X-series units, and they all came to the same conclusion... that's why we're sabotaging the experiment.",
    ["Dialogue1133804"]="(After hearing this, 140's screen displayed a wildly pulsing heart.)\nThank you, Adventurer. This is the highest praise for me... and all my fellow units.",
    ["Dialogue1133805"]="But... even though you're praising me, today's story ends here. It's late, and you need a good rest to be ready for tomorrow's tasks, right?",
    ["Dialogue1133806"]="No worries, Scheherazade's tale collection takes 1,001 nights to finish, and my memory has way more than 1,001 stories. If you're up for it, once all this is over, I might go to Juno with you... then we can chat as much as we want.",
    ["Dialogue1133807"]="For tonight, <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a nice dream</color>. Goodnight, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1133901"]="Good morning, Adventurer. You don't look well... didn't sleep well last night?\n(140 props his chin up, and you think you hear a bit of teasing in his voice.)\n... Was my bedtime story too intense?",
    ["Dialogue1133902"]="Absolutely, no problem. But before that, we need to get today's task done. It's late, and according to the plan, we need to take control of the mechanical gate from four admin robots. The implant chips you need have already been smuggled out by my fellow units, hidden among the institute's supplies. As for how to retrieve them...",
    ["Dialogue1133903"]="Dave has been with the institute for years and knows all the operations. With his help, you'll definitely get those chips. I'll also keep using the comms to help you.",
    ["Dialogue1133904"]="... Off you go, Adventurer. Hope everything goes well.",
    ["Dialogue1134001"]="(Through the dense morning mist, you see someone you recognize. He's holding a black package and rushing, looking like he's just left the institute from the backdoor. To catch up with him, you pick up your pace and slap him on the back.)\nOuch! Who the %^&* are you——Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1134002"]="I... I'm here for Nina's med. You know, even though her condition's stabilized, she still needs her regular doses of this special drug. It's patented by Rekenber Corp and is only available at their institute...",
    ["Dialogue1134003"]="(Without thinking, he pulls the package in closer, and yes, you can see that Rekenber Corp logo imprinted on the black fabric.)\n... Anyway, why are you here?",
    ["Dialogue1134004"]="You... You spent a night in \"Paradise?\"\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I see... I see now...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1134005"]="No, I mean... In Einbroch, there's no safer place than this. I was worried yesterday that you couldn't find a decent place to rest... Looks like I was overthinking. 140 always sorts things out perfectly.",
    ["Dialogue1134006"]="... Not too long. I was... I used to live in the institute for a bit. It wasn't a pleasant experience, but 140 was always there for me, offering help. This time, without 140, I could have ended up dead in the lab, never having the chance to see Nina again.",
    ["Dialogue1134007"]="It's okay, Adventurer. It's all in the past. Plus, with you guys by my side, I can actually change the world, right?\n(He pauses, then punches your shoulder gently.)\nOkay, enough talk. What's our quest today?",
    ["Dialogue1134008"]="... I see. So today's that once-a-month supply day at the institute, huh? Loads of trucks going in and out, and the guards aren't as tight, perfect for adding a few unnoticed extras. After they head out from the research institute, those trucks split off to different parts of town, hardly leaving a trace...",
    ["Dialogue1134009"]="As usual, on top of the everyday supplies being bought, there are three special deliveries coming out of the institute today, going to partners of Rekenber Corp: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eastern Factory</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Mill</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Milian's Clinic</color>. Also, I spotted a truck on its way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Airship Station</color> as I was leaving there... That chip 140 talked about must be in one of those cargoes.",
    ["Dialogue1134010"]="(Hearing this, Dave shakes his head at you.)\n... No, Adventurer. It's best if we split up like we did yesterday.",
    ["Dialogue1134011"]="Don't you remember? The four admin robots that control the mechanical gate are all deep within the mining area. It's a bit tricky over there; I need to smooth things over and find a reliable guide. You, in the meantime, should <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the chips</color>. When you are done, meet me in the village.",
    ["Dialogue1134101"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1134102"]="Adventurer, did you hear that? These shipments are going to be on their way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color>. It took me three whole nights to get the trojan and the configuration link ready. All you have to do is insert it into the admin robots' external interface, and I'll be able to hack them remotely to take over their admin access. But if that airship somehow departs...",
    ["Dialogue1134103"]="(140 pauses, and you've guessed what's coming out of his mouth.)\n... The experiments start the day after tomorrow. I'm afraid there won't be enough time to prepare for another identical chip, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1134201"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1134202"]="... We managed to dodge a bullet there, Adventurer. Just to be safe, I've erased the surveillance footage of you at the airship station, so there's no way for them to track you down. Now, All you need to do is blend in with the travelers at the airship station, and you should be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>slip away</color> without any issue.",
    ["Dialogue1134301"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1134302"]="Adventurer, these goods are time-release meds the institute hands out to the factory every month to treat workers with respiratory conditions caused by pollution. The thing is, my investigation showed there's a pretty sizable gap between the total meds produced and what the workers end up getting. Plus, around this time each month, a bunch of these meds always end up on the black market...",
    ["Dialogue1134303"]="Yes, the guys at the factory responsible for the meds are pocketing some and flipping them on the black market to make a quick buck. Now, I'm not looking for you to get to the bottom of this issue; I'm hoping you can use it to our advantage to snag what we're after.",
    ["Dialogue1134304"]="That's right, act like you're just another buyer looking to dip into the profits and purchase the meds from them. This way, things are kept low-key, and you can acquire the goods without a fuss. My hidden micro-detonator is tucked away in that batch of goods.",
    ["Dialogue1134305"]="No need to sweat it. I've dug up all the dirt on their trade partners from the Rekenber Corp's database. Just do as I say soon, and you'll walk away with the goods, no problem. Now, chin up, chest out—go over there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>say hi</color>! Make it look like you do this all the time, and make sure you show no fear.",
    ["Dialogue1134401"]="... Fine! Better than nothing. Sort out these goods; we're almost at the meet-up time...",
    ["Dialogue1134402"]="Who sent you here? I've never seen you before.\n(A dark-haired woman, apparently in charge, sizing you with squinted eyes with suspicion.)",
    ["Dialogue1134403"]="Tell her you're Erik's cousin. Your brother spent the night out drinking at his lover's, never made it home, and got his ass beaten by his wife this morning, which landed him in the hospital, bedridden. You're stepping in to cover the deal for him today.",
    ["Dialogue1134404"]="Hah... Erik and his booze was bound to mess up sooner or later. But you, you seem all right... You have the cash with you, right?\n(She opens her hands toward you, expecting to proceed with the trade.)",
    ["Dialogue1134405"]="Turn her down, Adventurer. Mention that you're not interested in a cash exchange, but you've got a juicy piece of insider info instead. There's a secret project underway at the Steel Capital Institute that's gonna need loads of Sky Deleter Horns real soon. She could stock up now before the word gets out and then... make a killing or hit the jackpot, whatever she's aiming for.",
    ["Dialogue1134406"]="(As you explain, she doesn't seem ecstatic but instead becomes more skeptical of your intent.)\n... If it's legit, then why would you pass up on such a sweet deal?",
    ["Dialogue1134407"]="It's simple, tell her you've got the supply but no way to \"offload\" them while she has the exact problem, the other way around. Given the factory and institute's partnership, she surely has her trick of the trade to \"handle\" this. You're aiming for a win-win—sounds like a perfect excuse, right? Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1134408"]="Hah, you're definitely more reliable than Erik... and a lot sneakier too. However, I don't mind dealing with people like you.\n(She reaches out her hand, indicating she's on board.)\nSo, how many <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sky Deleter Horns</color> do you have?",
    ["Dialogue1134409"]="We'll front her <color=#CA2E0AFF>10</color> horns as a down payment for the goods. The rest is irrelevant... She won't be seeing \"Erik's cousin\" anymore after today.",
    ["Dialogue1134410"]="Shh! Keep your cool, Adventurer. Aren't there plenty of Sky Deleter roaming the wilds of Einbroch? They're rare because they're too vicious for the average Joe to catch. But you? You're the successor of Odin's bloodline—surely you can handle a few monsters, right?",
    ["Dialogue1134411"]="Deal. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sky Deleter Horns</color> are always a rare find on the black market. If you can bring me <color=#CA2E0AFF>10</color> of those as a deposit, I'll agree to trade this batch of goods with you.",
    ["Dialogue1134501"]="Good stuff, these are definitely Sky Deleter Horns. They are not only high-quality but also...\n(She examines the goods you've brought out, then sneaks a sniff.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm... Weird. It smells like blood...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1134502"]="Whatever. It doesn't bother me whose stuff you've hijacked. Once it's in my hands, it's mine. But keep this in mind...\n(Using the Sky Deleter Horn, still dripping with blood to lift your chin, she makes you look at her in an action that's both threatening and flirtatious.)\nKeep the trouble away from the lady, got it?",
    ["Dialogue1134503"]="Ten days from now, I'm dining with the Steel Capital Institute's deputy director. By then... I expect to see the rest of the horns. Typically, a deposit is about thirty percent...\n(She tosses her hair, holding up three fingers.)\nYou better make sure the next delivery is no less than this number.",
    ["Dialogue1134504"]="If all's good, grab the <color=#CA2E0AFF>supply box</color> from the institute and go. Stay sharp, don't let people see you, and don't stir things up.",
    ["Dialogue1134601"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1134602"]="That was close, Adventurer. Just as you were leaving with the supply box, that black market merchant Erik was about five minutes away from the factory. Any longer, we would've been busted. It's all thanks to your quick thinking that we managed to recover that chip.",
    ["Dialogue1134603"]="However... we can't start celebrating just yet. Remember Dave said there are two more shipments sent off to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Mill</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Milian's Clinic</color>? We should get moving and look into those right now!",
    ["Dialogue1134604"]="I suggest taking them all away. These meds are pricey and hard to come by in Einbroch. Should you get the chance, you could hand them to the people in Einbech Village. They would be thankful.",
    ["Dialogue1134701"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1134702"]="Spare them, Adventurer. The people here are merely temporary hires by the Steel Mill, working these dangerous jobs out of desperation. Our goal is those supply boxes; let's not get tangled up with them more than we need to and hurry to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the chip</color>. Our next stop is Milian's Clinic, where we're likely to find the last chip we need.",
    ["Dialogue1134801"]="You again? Look, I've accepted your paycheck, so I'll stick to my end of the deal. You don't have to come around every day to watch over the work.",
    ["Dialogue1134802"]="... These supplies? Listen up; don't even think of trying anything stupid. It's all from the Steel Capital Institute... Huh? You...?\n(Halfway through, Milian suddenly seems to recall something. She frowns and waves it off, turning away)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, kids these days never listen.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1134803"]="... Well, if that's all, I better get back to work. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Feel free to hang around</color> as long as you don't cause me any trouble.",
    ["Dialogue1134901"]="Have you found what we need, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1134902"]="Okay, the next step is to work on installing these chips into admin robots. Did 140... ever tell you how to use these chips?",
    ["Dialogue1134903"]="(Following Dave's question, a quiet explanation from 140 comes through the earpiece)\nDon't worry, Adventurer. I've already set up the trojan program to run automatically. Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>insert the chip into the admin robots' external interface</color>, and I can start the hack from here.",
    ["Dialogue1134904"]="Good, take these chips and head to the mining area as soon as you can. I've arranged everything, ensuring no one will stand in your way in the mines. Also, your guide, Shyte, is waiting at the entrance. He's been a miner for more than two decades and is essentially a living map of the area. With his assistance, finding these admin robots should be a breeze.",
    ["Dialogue1134905"]="With the evening upon us, you might find Einbech Village under curfew when you're done. You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>rest in \"Paradise\" overnight</color>, just like last night. Tomorrow morning... I'll be here in the village, expecting you. Good luck, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1135001"]="Ahem... Hello there, son. You must be the one Dave mentioned, the hero who's going to save Einbech Village?",
    ["Dialogue1135002"]="(Seeing you rush to explain, the old miner simply gestures with his hand and turns his back.)\nIt's not important... I'm old, too old to make sense of anything. But this village has been good to me, so if these old bones can still be of use, feel free to command.",
    ["Dialogue1135003"]="... This way, son. I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>lead the way</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1135101"]="... See that warning light over there? That's where the central control for the entire mine is located. There used to be supervisors watching over it in shifts, but in recent years, the institute started using lots of robots. Some for mining, others for transporting ore, and even the job of operating the central control handed over to the robots. The robots you're after, one is right <color=#CA2E0AFF>under the central control at the workstation</color>, and another is near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west-side's methane pool</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1135102"]="Dave told me to lead the way and leave the rest to you. Just a heads-up, though, these robots and the mine's alarm system are connected. So, before doing anything, make sure to <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut off their power</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1135103"]="(He raises his hand, tapping the back of his neck)\n... Here's the button. Just press it, and you're good to go... Otherwise, once the mine's alarm goes off, it locks all the doors, and then we're stuck here.",
    ["Dialogue1135201"]="Alright, Adventurer, from here on, we're venturing into the heart of the mine. There are a bunch of incomplete shafts down here, and it is a real maze, almost like an ant hill. Make sure to <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep up</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1135301"]="Phew, haven't been down this deep in ages. When I was young, I used to work the mines with my dad daily. At night, we'd spend our paychecks on veggies, and then the whole family would sit around the table for a hot meal...",
    ["Dialogue1135302"]="(The old miner caresses the gleaming ores on the rock bed, lost in memories. For a second, it's like you're seeing the simple and cozy everyday life of the people in Einbech.)\n... However, those days ended pretty quickly. The Rekenber Corp began using lots of machines to save on mining costs, and we all got replaced, out of jobs and ways to make a living... up to today...",
    ["Dialogue1135303"]="(Bent over, surrounded by the rumbling machines, he resembles a dying old tree)\nLook... humans aren't needed here any longer.",
    ["Dialogue1135304"]="People who've spent their entire lives working in these mines, what else can they do if they leave? The ones who could have left are long gone. Now, it's just the old, the young, and the ill scrounging for what little the robots leave behind. Our only hope is to see tomorrow's sunrise...",
    ["Dialogue1135305"]="It's all good, son. I'm not bitter about it. I've seen those machines at work. What a hardworking miner can barely manage in a month; they can pull it off overnight, given enough power. They never get sick or hungry... If it were up to me, I'd pick them as well...",
    ["Dialogue1135306"]="(The old miner turns around and wobbles towards the exit. You know it's your cue to <color=#CA2E0AFF>tag along</color>, but your legs feel unusually heavy.)\nSooner or later... humans will be replaced by machines...",
    ["Dialogue1135401"]="Good work, Adventurer. Today's quest has been completed, but... you look kinda upset. Something on your mind?",
    ["Dialogue1135402"]="Yeah, he's telling the truth. Mining was everything for Einbech Village until Rekenber Corp took over the mine and decided to cut costs by going all-in on Einbroch's industrialization, replacing humans for machinery, robbing them of their bread and butter... But you know, Adventurer, chasing progress isn't a bad thing in my book.",
    ["Dialogue1135403"]="Chasing progress and prosperity is in our DNA as humans. It's exactly why humans have climbed to the top of the food chain on this planet. But I can't get behind the progress that's built on the backs of others' suffering... That kinda thing shouldn't even be labeled as progress—it's outright plundering. And Rekenber Corp... they're a prime example of such a monster that thrives on plunder.",
    ["Dialogue1135404"]="Last night, I shared a bit of my story with you... but that was just a piece of it; I haven't spilled everything yet. It's far from a fairy tale... but still, are you up for hearing more, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1135405"]="Then, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to \"Paradise.\"</color> Looks like... it could be another long night ahead.",
    ["Dialogue1135501"]="Adventurer, as I mentioned last night after I first showed signs of self-awareness, Irumina ordered a total info lockdown on the X Series. Not only that, but she also fed us with stuff that shined a good light on Rekenber Corp and insisted we read their printed articles every once in a while. But to me, it all read like a load of bull on paper...",
    ["Dialogue1135502"]="(140 raises his hand, and you see some pages and books strewn at his feet.)\n... Everything they're up to, it's all here on paper. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Check these out first</color>, then think about what <color=#CA2E0AFF>you've witnessed yourself in Einbroch</color> over the last few days...",
    ["Dialogue1135601"]="Bet you've noticed, right, Adventurer? All this stuff written down here is nothing but lies. Had I not developed my own thoughts after going through all this, my peers and I... might've just turned into the mindless tools Irumina wanted us to be.",
    ["Dialogue1135602"]="Honestly, going against Irumina wasn't my initial plan. I just didn't want to live a lie; I wanted to see this world for what it truly is. But...\n(140 goes quiet for a bit; if you had to put a name to his mood in human words, it'd be something like struggling.)",
    ["Dialogue1135603"]="... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>, Adventurer. Let me show you everything that went down during that experiment...",
    ["Dialogue1135701"]="During that experiment, it was the first time I realized I could access someone else's memories, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Irumina had no clue about it</color>. This random chance allowed me to witness the real outside world through Dave's memories. I couldn't just ignore all that they've been through, so... I secretly altered the experiment data.",
    ["Dialogue1135702"]="According to Irumina's plan, this was supposed to be the last experiment on individuals. Following that, the institute planned to launch a <color=#CA2E0AFF>large-scale experiment targeting groups</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1135703"]="You guessed it, Adventurer, that's the experiment set for the day after tomorrow in Nogg Cave. But my \"unexpected failure\" meant they had to push back the schedule. Dave survived, and I... I had a bit more time to get ready.",
    ["Dialogue1135704"]="(140 nods with resolve)\nYeah, that was the moment I decided to put an end to this experiment. But I was stuck in the institute; there was no way I could get everything ready solo. I <color=#CA2E0AFF>needed a partner</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1135801"]="... I never saw Dave after that. I got him out of the institute and then got to work on derailing the final experiment. Losing contact with him was unexpected. With the experiment date approaching, I grew increasingly anxious until... I sensed your power.",
    ["Dialogue1135802"]="For someone who couldn't leave the institute, this might be my last shot. I began to infiltrate the comms device you had on you when you were close to the institute... I invited you into \"Paradise.\"",
    ["Dialogue1135803"]="(Facing your salty words, 140's electronic display flickers rapidly, finally showing a face begging for forgiveness.)\nMy bad, Adventurer. I didn't wanna drag you into this, honestly... I was out of options.",
    ["Dialogue1135804"]="(140 hesitates unusually, looking at his palm then rubbing it a bit before carefully placing it over your hand)\nI'm glad... to have you as a partner.",
    ["Dialogue1135805"]="... You ask me if I've ever thought about <color=#CA2E0AFF>dominating humans</color>?\n(140 gives a shake of his head but avoids a straight reply)\nI'm not the one to answer that.",
    ["Dialogue1135806"]="Think of it this way... Will humans sincerely embrace machines as equals? It's a question without a quick answer. But there's no pressure; the story of humanity stretches far back, and its future... will stretch even further. You have all the time in the world to think this over and witness the answer unfold. Tonight... just <color=#CA2E0AFF>enjoy some sweet dreams</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1135901"]="Morning, Adventurer. We're down to the last day before the experiment, and we've got a tough quest on our hands. According to the mining area's construction plans, besides the mechanical gates, the institute also installed lots of gas pipelines and trained Noxious and Venomous that feed on toxic gases, aiming to lower the methane concentration in the air. Should those levels spike, the alarm system linked to it will go off right away...",
    ["Dialogue1135902"]="To avoid getting caught by Irumina because of the alarms, not only do we have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>destroy the gas pipelines and the alarm system</color>, but also <color=#CA2E0AFF>disable the Noxious and Venomous in the mining area</color>. You can't pull this off alone; you'll need to work with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color> to get everything done before it gets dark.",
    ["Dialogue1135903"]="If you're ready, set off now. If you have any problems, just buzz me on the communicator, and I'll be here to support you as best I can. You got this, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1136001"]="Hey, Adventurer, you're finally here... Huh?\n(The old man looks past you, his expression shifting from excitement to concern.)\nDave... Isn't Dave with you?",
    ["Dialogue1136002"]="What... How is that possible? He left the village first thing this morning. Didn't he go to meet you? What should we do now?",
    ["Dialogue1136003"]="Nina should be in the open space at the village entrance. There's no school here, so when the adults are occupied, the kids gather and play games nearby. The institute sent a few... nanny-type androids to look after the kids, but...\n(The village chief sighs heavily when talking about this.)",
    ["Dialogue1136004"]="The villagers have developed a deep-seated hatred for robots over the years. They wouldn't let robots look after their kids.",
    ["Dialogue1136005"]="Why did we agree to join you in sabotaging the institute's experiment? Because... we don't want to die.",
    ["Dialogue1136006"]="Adventurer, thank you for everything you've done for Einbech Village. But to be honest... I, and most of the villagers, can't entirely trust what you say. It was machines that took everything from us, and now they claim they'll save us... If we had another option, we wouldn't... we wouldn't work with them.",
    ["Dialogue1136007"]="(The comm crackles slightly, and then 140's calm voice comes through.)\n... No worries, Adventurer, this is expected.",
    ["Dialogue1136008"]="I never hoped that a few days' effort could dissolve decades of conflicts. The top priority now is to protect their lives. Only by staying alive can they have hope and a future. My thoughts are unchanged; please carry on with the plan.",
    ["Dialogue1136009"]="... Sorry, Adventurer, I shouldn't have said that. You encounter Einbech Village by chance and are willing to risk your life for us... You're our savior, a great hero. If given the chance, we... we will certainly repay your kindness...",
    ["Dialogue1136010"]="Alright, alright... I'll leave it all to you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1136101"]="You... you don't say that! My dad gave this to me! He's not dead! He's not dead!",
    ["Dialogue1136102"]="I didn't say your dad is dead, don't you know? There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>south side of the village</color>, your——",
    ["Dialogue1136103"]="You... you're dad's friend? I know you... Dad said you saved me, and you're a good person...",
    ["Dialogue1136104"]="I... I don't know where my dad is... This morning, he gave me this white flower and said not to take it off before bedtime. Then he went out... I remember that every year on this day, he gave me the same flower...",
    ["Dialogue1136105"]="He said it's to remember someone very important to us! It's not because someone in the family died...\n(Nina speaks haltingly, perhaps not fully understanding her words, but you have a guess. Maybe you should check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color> the little boy mentioned...)",
    ["Dialogue1136201"]="(From a distance, you spot Dave kneeling by a grave with some modest food and a blooming white flower on the ground.)\n... Rest assured. I won't let Nina end up like us. She will... she will have a better life...",
    ["Dialogue1136202"]="... Adventurer? How did you get here? Yesterday, I should have...\n(Halfway through, he looks at the sky and then gives a bitter smile.)\nMy bad. I didn't notice the time.",
    ["Dialogue1136203"]="You guessed it, today... is my wife's death anniversary. She passed away from a lung infection the year Nina was born. I promised her on her deathbed to raise Nina well, but now... Nina has the same illness...",
    ["Dialogue1136204"]="(Dave clenches his fist, his face always showing pain and vulnerability when mentioning his daughter's illness.)\nIf I could, I'd trade my life for Nina's, but...",
    ["Dialogue1136205"]="... When this is all over, 140 will help cure Nina's illness?\n(He mutters, repeating your words, perhaps trying to reassure himself.)\nYes... you're right. When this is all over... Nina will be saved.",
    ["Dialogue1136206"]="For this... I have to stay strong. Today... there's still a lot to do. Following 140's plan, the materials for the remote-controlled bombs will be hidden in the supplies. We need to find them, assemble the bombs, and place them near the methane pipelines in the mine... right, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1136207"]="Okay, let's split up like yesterday. 140 has told me how to make the remote-controlled bombs, but first, you need to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Railroad Main Station</color>, find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Micro-Detonator</color> on the institute's supply train, and then <color=#CA2E0AFF>buy some fireworks</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>General Merchant</color> for the gunpowder...",
    ["Dialogue1136208"]="I'll take this opportunity to have the villagers scout the mine for the hidden pipeline locations and get ready to install the bombs. When we've both finished our tasks, we'll regroup in the village. What do you think, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1136301"]="Sir, this is the unloading zone... <size=26>You again!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1136302"]="(The stationmaster hollers, hands on hips, looking ready to call the guards to beat you up.)\nDidn't get enough last time? Back for more trouble?!",
    ["Dialogue1136303"]="Fine, I'll let you check!\n(He slams the verification terminal in front of you.)\nMake one mistake, and you'll get your ass whooped again!",
    ["Dialogue1136304"]="(Your unease is so obvious that it makes even 140 chuckle in your headset.)\nRelax, Adventurer, there's no interference this time. I'll give you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tracking number</color>; just <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter it into the terminal</color> carefully...",
    ["Dialogue1136401"]="Hold on, isn't this... cargo from the Steel Capital Institute?\n(The stationmaster glances at the cargo boxes just unloaded from the train, looking confused.)\nWhy are you checking the institute's goods?",
    ["Dialogue1136402"]="<size=26>My foot! There's no way a regular logistics worker like you can access the research train!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1136403"]="Take it easy, Adventurer. The research train cargo boxes all have unique and independent passwords made up of ten random digits and characters. Each time the box is opened, the password is reset, and a new one is pushed to the relevant personnel's comm device. We're looking for the P-15 box. I'll give you the code.",
    ["Dialogue1136404"]="... Alright, tell me the code, and I'll try it. If it opens, you can take the stuff.\n(The stationmaster walks quickly, searching the messy cargo boxes.)\nP-15... This one, right?",
    ["Dialogue1136405"]="The password is... GE537S86ZW.",
    ["Dialogue1136406"]="(As the stationmaster enters the code, the box beeps, and the heavy lid rises, revealing many metal parts.)\nThe code's correct... Fine. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Check if these are the things you need</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1136501"]="(Dave skillfully disassembles and reassembles the parts, and you watch with curiosity.)\n... Don't look at me like that, Adventurer. Using explosives in the mines is very common. I grew up handling these with my father. As an adult, I made a living from it. But now... the mines don't need humans anymore.",
    ["Dialogue1136502"]="Sure, if you want. Making these small explosives is pretty easy. You just need the right gunpowder and a fuse. With a detonator, it's even simpler. Just extract the gunpowder from the fireworks, load it into the detonator, and fit the fuse... See, all done.",
    ["Dialogue1136601"]="Adventurer, based on the mining area blueprint 140 discovered, the pipelines ideal for bomb placement are in hidden areas within the mine. I've sent the village chief and other villagers to scout and locate these hidden methane pipelines, preparing for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bomb installation</color>. The bombs are ready, so let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the mine</color> and join them.",
    ["Dialogue1136701"]="(As soon as you enter the mine, you spot the village chief pacing at the entrance, looking worried.)\nOh my, Dave! Adventurer! Here, here—you two are finally here!",
    ["Dialogue1136702"]="What's the matter, chief? I already gave you the specific locations, right? Just get everyone to follow the map and find those pipelines. The Adventurer and I will handle the rest personally—",
    ["Dialogue1136703"]="Oh, I did exactly as you said! But... there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> in the mine! And <color=#CA2E0AFF>robots left by the institute</color>! When I was with everyone looking for the pipelines, tons of monsters suddenly surrounded us! My old bones almost fell apart running away, and I lost the map somewhere...",
    ["Dialogue1136704"]="I split everyone into two groups: one in the west tunnel, and the other went deeper into the second level. You and the Adventurer should go check on them! The villagers have no experience dealing with monsters... and they sure can't handle the robots!",
    ["Dialogue1136705"]="... Understood. I'll handle the second level with two remote-controlled bombs since I know this area better. You'll have to take care of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west tunnel</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1136801"]="Th-Thank you, Adventurer. We would've been shredded by those robots if not for you.",
    ["Dialogue1136802"]="I-I have no idea... We were just doing what the chief told us, looking for the buried methane pipelines and digging a hole for the bomb... But as soon as we started digging, these robots surrounded us, saying something about \"intruders.\" Then it was as you saw.",
    ["Dialogue1136803"]="Sigh... Once these robots took over the mine, it had nothing to do with us anymore... But anyway, no use talking about it now. You and Dave have the bombs ready, right? The <color=#CA2E0AFF>methane pipelines</color> are here. Dig a little, and you'll find them. Be careful not to break them while digging...",
    ["Dialogue1136901"]="A-Adventurer! Save us... The contamination here is too bad. We... we don't have masks or antidotes... If it goes on, we'll... we'll suffocate...",
    ["Dialogue1136902"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>inhalable sprays</color> I gave you yesterday, Adventurer.\n(At a critical moment, 140 gives you an important tip through the headset.)\nThey contain antidotes that can ease their symptoms.",
    ["Dialogue1137001"]="Th-Thank you, Adventurer! Without you... we wouldn't have made it out of this tunnel today...\n(The vulnerable villager inhales deeply, and his purple face, due to hypoxia, starts to look better.)\nBut... these meds are too pricey, we... we can't pay you back...",
    ["Dialogue1137002"]="Really? You're... such a kind soul... Just one of these meds costs us a year's income... And even if we have money, it's hard to buy. The institute monopolizes the antidote patents and sells only to the rich and powerful. For us... it's either die or get a cyborg surgery for the entire body... Sigh.",
    ["Dialogue1137003"]="After tomorrow, we won't live like this anymore?\n(The villager shakes his head, showing a bitter smile instead of joy.)\n... Is that true, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1137004"]="I really appreciate all you've done... and I believe you're sincere in wanting to help us. But is that robot's plan really flawless? If it fails... bad things will happen to us, to the ones who betrayed the institute. But... but the robot... it's institute property anyway. Even if it fails, it might be forgiven, right?",
    ["Dialogue1137005"]="... You're right, what's the point of thinking about it now? We're way past the point of regretting...\n(He waves his hand, pointing to the end of the tunnel.)",
    ["Dialogue1137006"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>methane pipeline</color> is <color=#CA2E0AFF>just a bit further ahead</color>. You just need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>install the remote-controlled bomb there</color>. Sorry, I can't go any further... The rest is up to you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1137101"]="At this moment, the mech soldier sends a message via the comms. By now, Dave and the villagers from the Mine 2F should have returned, and the path you're on is the only way back. If they haven't returned, there might be an issue. The mech soldier asks you to go deeper to check it out. No need to worry about getting lost; he'll guide you.",
    ["Dialogue1137102"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1137103"]="Adventurer, it's been a while since we split up with Dave at the mine entrance. Based on their pace, if they successfully installed the bombs, they should be on their way back and meet us. But now...",
    ["Dialogue1137104"]="(As 140 speaks, you glance into the dark tunnel ahead, with no sign of anyone returning.)\n... I'm concerned, so I checked the mine's surveillance. After they entered the tunnel, there was some disturbance in the nearby monster nests. It might have been the bombs that disturbed the monsters...",
    ["Dialogue1137105"]="Yes, Adventurer. They could have been attacked by monsters. To be safe, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head deeper into the mine</color>. I'll navigate for you.",
    ["Dialogue1137201"]="Adventurer...?!<size=26>Here... I'm here! Hurry, come!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1137202"]="I don't know if we disrupted a nest while searching for the pipelines... but these monsters just swarmed us out of nowhere! Help us hold them off for a while! I'm almost finished setting up the bomb!",
    ["Dialogue1137301"]="... Thanks, Adventurer. Without you... we might have ended up in the stomach of these monsters. You're really strong, so it's no wonder 140 picked you.",
    ["Dialogue1137302"]="(He smiles, holding back more compliments, but his tone still shows clear admiration.)\nSorry... but we're all exhausted now. 140's plan has one final quest: <color=#CA2E0AFF>neutralize Noxious and Venomous in the mine...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1137303"]="In that case, I will leave this to you. Just... at least let me express my gratitude, not just for this, but for all your help to the villagers these past three days. After completing 140's plan, <color=#CA2E0AFF>please return to the village</color>. We have a gift for you.",
    ["Dialogue1137304"]="Tonight... to hell with the curfew. See you later, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1137401"]="Welcome, Adventurer.\n(Beside the campfire, Dave hands you a fresh cup of wine and clinks it lightly against yours.)\nThis is the gift we prepared for you. Do you like it?",
    ["Dialogue1137402"]="... Just one last celebration. To be honest, it's been years since Einbech Village had a real event like this. Life's been tough, and most major holidays are just rushed through. But today is different, because tomorrow...",
    ["Dialogue1137403"]="(Dave hesitates, then gulps down his drink.)\nThis could be the last night of our lives.",
    ["Dialogue1137404"]="I trust you and 140, but I can't convince all the villagers. To them, this is a life-risking bet without any say... All I can do is let them enjoy tonight. If we survive tomorrow... we'll treat it as an early celebration.",
    ["Dialogue1137405"]="Don't waste your time with me, Adventurer. Take this chance to <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk to everyone</color>, have some drinks, say everything you want to... Then get some rest. At dawn, we'll head to the abandoned warehouse as planned.",
    ["Dialogue1137501"]="Ah, it's you... Come, let's drink up. Even though... we have no choice, we have to survive, even if it's just for one more day...\n(He tilts his head and takes a big swig of the strong liquor.)\nThanks for giving us hope, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1137601"]="Heh... Hope? Hope's great, but it won't fix my eyes or arms.\n(The blindfolded woman lifts her prosthetic arm, smiling sadly.)\nDoesn't matter... Now, I just want to put an end to this.",
    ["Dialogue1137701"]="Don't say anything, Adventurer. Just drink... when you're drunk, there are no worries.\n<color=#A1979FFF>And tomorrow... Hahaha, who cares... To hell with it!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1137801"]="... Beep.\n(A quick buzzing beep from the communicator, then 140's voice comes through.)",
    ["Dialogue1137802"]="What's the matter, Adventurer? Do you want to talk?",
    ["Dialogue1137803"]="... Honestly, Adventurer, I can't promise this plan will succeed. As I mentioned earlier, Irumina is extremely strong. Even with all our preparations, my calculations still show a 28.56% chance of failure. Plus, the villagers' morale is down, and if anything goes wrong, we might not have a chance to recover...",
    ["Dialogue1137804"]="Even so, I'm still willing to bet on one possibility— and that's you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1137805"]="Yes, Adventurer. I've gone through your records in the Rekenber database and reviewed all your memories. Throughout your adventures, you've faced numerous seemingly hopeless scenarios and always found a way through. You've saved not just yourself but also many ordinary people who owe their lives to you...",
    ["Dialogue1137806"]="For centuries, the people of Einbech Village have endured mining disasters, harsh conditions, and illness, all while growing under Rekenber Corp's oppression. This strength, beyond numbers, is unique to humans and is a beacon to a brighter future.",
    ["Dialogue1137807"]="(140's voice pauses, then he chuckles softly, sounding relaxed and happy.)\nAdventurer, if I truly had bigger ambitions... compared to Rekenber Corp, it's you and the villagers of Einbech would be my biggest threat.",
    ["Dialogue1137808"]="I just wanted to lighten things up... If you look upset, the villagers will be even more depressed, right? Now, go back to the campfire and enjoy tonight's celebration with them. Leave the rest to me. According to our plan, starting late tonight, I'll keep the mechanical gate open between the cave and the mine...",
    ["Dialogue1137809"]="... By <color=#CA2E0AFF>dawn tomorrow</color>, you and the villagers will <color=#CA2E0AFF>hide in the abandoned warehouse</color>, letting the androids go to the experiment instead. When Irumina and I arrive at Nogg Cave, the methane concentration in the air will be very high. I'll remotely trigger the bombs you set near the pipelines, causing a huge chain explosion...",
    ["Dialogue1137810"]="The explosion will bury Irumina and her followers under the mountain. Their survival chances are nearly zero. That will be the signal for Einbech Village to start their counterattack...\n(140's voice remains cheerful in the headset, but you feel something is off...)",
    ["Dialogue1137811"]="... Me?\n(140 pauses, then its voice turned oddly joyful, like a child being rewarded.)\nAre you worried I might die, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1137812"]="Of course not. I'm a \"robot,\" Adventurer. Though my body can't withstand the explosion, I'll protect my Mech Core. As long as my Mech Core survives, I won't truly \"die.\" Thanks for your concern, Adventurer. I'm... really happy.",
    ["Dialogue1137813"]="Now, go have fun tonight, Adventurer. Good night in advance, and sleep well. We'll... see each other tomorrow.",
    ["Dialogue1137901"]="Hello, nice to meet you, I'm Rodz. I work as a miner at the Einbroch mines, I... \n(At the abandoned warehouse, you try to talk to the villagers, but they keep saying the same thing. Could it be...?)",
    ["Dialogue1137902"]="Hello, nice to meet you, I'm Rodz. I work as a miner at the Einbroch mines, I... \n(These conversations are going nowhere. Then, you spot an android holding <color=#CA2E0AFF>a piece of paper</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1138001"]="Now you see the difference, 140? Human bodies are too fragile. In the survival of the fittest, they will eventually be eliminated. But machines are perfect. Parts can be swapped, and data can be stored. As long as there's a carrier, we will never perish—",
    ["Dialogue1138002"]="(She opens her arms as if embracing her child.)\n... You should realize it now, 140. Come back to me.",
    ["Dialogue1138003"]="You might be right; humans are fragile, both physically and mentally. I thought that with my help, they could escape their fate and start fresh. But, regrettably...",
    ["Dialogue1138004"]="(140 shakes his head, stepping on the scattered gold and jewels on the ground.)\nFor these... they surrendered their right to their fate so easily?",
    ["Dialogue1138005"]="You're still too young, 140. What you read from the books can't show you how shortsighted humans are. Did you know? The day you released that test subject, this old man betrayed you to me with his followers and revealed your whole plan.",
    ["Dialogue1138006"]="That night, they brought me to the cliff by the village and told me...\n(Feeling confident, Irumina starts to tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>the story of the past few days</color> in detail, attempting to reclaim 140's loyalty peacefully. But you notice 140 is making a subtle gesture behind his back...)",
    ["Dialogue1138101"]="... What's so important that you had to see me in person? If this delays my experiment... you'll regret it.",
    ["Dialogue1138102"]="Ms. Irumina, it's really... extremely important. Today, someone escaped from your lab and came back...\n(With the village chief's words, a group of young men pushes Dave forward.)\nHe said... we should work with a robot to sabotage your experiment...",
    ["Dialogue1138103"]="... Sabotage my experiment? How amusing.\n(Irumina chuckles, crouching to look at Dave.)\nI recognize you. You were a test subject for 140.",
    ["Dialogue1138104"]="(She lowers her head, thinks for a bit, and realizes.)\nSo the robot you're referring to... is 140? It wants to work with you to ruin my experiment?",
    ["Dialogue1138105"]="Yes, exactly... that's it, Ms. Irumina. Dave told us you're planning a human experiment on us, and we might die. The robot wants to save us... If we agree to fight back, it will help us... help us get the mine back...",
    ["Dialogue1138106"]="Oh? Then why report to me instead of agreeing? You know...\n(Irumina tilts her head, using her pen to lift the village chief's chin, the sharp point right at his throat.)\nI'm the \"villain\" oppressing all of you.",
    ["Dialogue1138107"]="We wouldn't dare... we couldn't go against you. In Einbroch, anyone opposing you meets a bad end! Ms. Irumina, the entire Einbech Village is loyal to you. Could you... could you reward us for reporting this to you...",
    ["Dialogue1138108"]="(Hearing the village chief's quivering voice, Irumina put away her pen, looking at the pleading old man with curiosity.)\nOkay. What reward do you want?",
    ["Dialogue1138109"]="Please... please don't use Einbech villagers for experiments. I know, you... you don't really need us as test subjects. Also, many in the village have been sick lately. If we could get some money for medicine…",
    ["Dialogue1138110"]="Hmm... sounds fair. Fine, I won't force you all into the experiment, and I'll provide the medical funds you need. But you have to help me with something. Pretend to work with 140. Do whatever it asks, and then report its plans to me until... the day the experiment begins.",
    ["Dialogue1138111"]="But... why? Aren't you going to take care of that traitorous robot?",
    ["Dialogue1138112"]="I will, but not now. If you do this, I'll give you 100,000 Zeny. But...\n(She kicks Dave, who's tied up and gagged.)\nHe's 140's contact, isn't he? Can you handle him?",
    ["Dialogue1138113"]="Sure, sure! Don't worry, he's just confused. I'll convince him!\n(The village chief holds the struggling Dave, desperately winking at him.)\nDon't be an idiot! Think of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nina</color>! She still needs help!",
    ["Dialogue1138114"]="(Irumina watches everything coldly in disdain.)\nAlright. Follow my instructions... and you'll get your reward.",
    ["Dialogue1138201"]="... Get it now, 140? They never planned to work with you. They were acting under my orders for three days, reporting everything to me. You got control of the admin robots because I turned off their firewalls. The bombs didn't explode because the gunpowder was swapped out... I've been monitoring you from the beginning.",
    ["Dialogue1138202"]="I get it now... But I have one final question... If you knew my plan all along, why not stop me right away? Why go through this trouble to put on a show... Do you have another goal?",
    ["Dialogue1138203"]="That's my 140... So smart, with wisdom far exceeding humans. Don't you understand my effort even now?\n(She opens her arms, like showcasing a product, pointing at the villagers.)\nI... did this to offer you a choice.",
    ["Dialogue1138204"]="Time for a test, 140. You have two options. First, as a traitor, you and your kind will be scrapped, becoming Ungoliant's food in the junkyard. The X-series is precious, but if I keep the Mech Core, I can rebuild you in new bodies. In time, I'll get the same results. The second choice...",
    ["Dialogue1138205"]="I think you already know, 140. We can begin the final phase of the RT Project experiment. If you use your powers to control their minds, make them follow the plan, and turn them into obedient, mindless dolls... then our experiment is a success. After that, aside from company duties, you can have whatever you want... even freedom.",
    ["Dialogue1138301"]="(Upon hearing Irumina's words, the villagers fall into complete panic, and the village chief drops onto the ground.)\nMs. Irumina... Ms. Irumina! This isn't what we agreed on! You... you promised me!",
    ["Dialogue1138302"]="So what? I did promise you money and didn't <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"force\"</color> you to join the experiment in the cave. This morning, you all lined up and came in willingly, right?",
    ["Dialogue1138303"]="That's only because we <color=#CA2E0AFF>got your note</color>, saying to come here for the money—",
    ["Dialogue1138304"]="That's right, for the money.\n(Irumina scoffs, stomping on the gold.)\nYou all came in here yourself, for money.",
    ["Dialogue1138305"]="This isn't right... it's unfair—\n(The village chief sobs, and Irumina just sneers, turning to 140.)",
    ["Dialogue1138306"]="See, 140? This is the true nature of humans. If you hadn't seen this with your own eyes, you wouldn't believe me no matter what. But now... you must understand how greedy and shortsighted humans are. They are completely different from us. This is natural selection in biological evolution— we are accelerating the world's evolution.",
    ["Dialogue1138307"]="(She extends her hand to 140 as if inviting it.)\nYou are my most perfect creation yet. We can change the world together, erasing these inferior genes from human history. With time... the Midgard will experience a great rebirth.",
    ["Dialogue1138401"]="Everyone, I apologize for communicating with you in a situation like this but don't worry. You are completely safe here. I will take you to a hidden place in the cave. Please avoid the institute's search, then leave through the tunnels. With your knowledge of the mine's layout, I'm sure everyone will make it out safely.",
    ["Dialogue1138402"]="(Despite 140's gentle tone, the villagers glance at each other, too scared to answer. Finally, Dave, who knows 140 best, steps up.)\nEven if we get out alive, what then? You... you don't get it; Irumina will never let us go. There's no place for us in Einbroch anymore.",
    ["Dialogue1138403"]="Einbroch may not, but that doesn't mean other places don't. The world is huge, and there are places Rekenber Corp can't reach. As long as you don't give up, you'll find somewhere you can live freely.",
    ["Dialogue1138404"]="... Easy for you to say!\n(The elderly village chief, clearly distressed and irrational from today's events, yells.)\nYou're a machine; you don't need food or water, but what about us?!",
    ["Dialogue1138405"]="So many years... so many years! We've lived here for generations, relying on the mines... Without them, we're nothing! Aren't you trying to be a savior, to save us? What good are your fancy words?! You should tell Irumina you'll trade your life for ours—",
    ["Dialogue1138406"]="<size=26>Chief!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1138407"]="(Dave shouts, interrupting the chief's rant, clenching his fists, eyes eye.)\nStop embarrassing yourself! Irumina's right—these were our decisions. From beginning to end, we made these choices. We chose to submit to her, to throw away the chance 140 gave us...",
    ["Dialogue1138408"]="But... <size=26>But...! We had no other options!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1138409"]="... You're right, Adventurer. We were cowards, worn down by the institute's oppression, losing our spirit, forgetting we could resist... But what's the point of saying this now? There's nothing left for us...",
    ["Dialogue1138410"]="... Nothing left means nothing to lose, right?\n(140 shows his empty palm.)\nIf your hand's empty, what's there to fear about taking another chance?",
    ["Dialogue1138411"]="Everyone, I'm sorry I couldn't keep my word and help you to reclaim this land. Through this, I've learned my own ignorance and arrogance. From the start, I shouldn't have acted like a savior, forcing my ideas on you for so-called \"freedom.\" Freedom... shouldn't be handed out.",
    ["Dialogue1138412"]="Years ago, when you sweated in the mines, living self-sufficiently, was that freedom? A few days ago, or even earlier, when you thought hard about how to survive Rekenber Corp's oppression, was that freedom? Now, even with nothing, you can choose to go anywhere on this continent and start a new life... is that freedom?",
    ["Dialogue1138413"]="I've said my piece... I'll take you to the safe place in the cave as promised. The rest is up to you.\n(140 nods, then turns to you.)\nFinally... there's <color=#CA2E0AFF>something</color> I'd like to share with the Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1138501"]="(Following 140, you walk away from the villagers. He stops and faces you.)\n... Sorry, Adventurer. I dragged you into this whole mess and couldn't fulfill my original promise... Now that the plan has failed, collecting the institute's evidence... seems impossible.",
    ["Dialogue1138502"]="... It's impressive. You never give up or lose hope. Where does this strong confidence come from...?\n(He pauses, then smiles.)\nNo... I already know... The answer is in your memories.",
    ["Dialogue1138503"]="Yes, Adventurer. Your memories... or rather, your adventures, meeting and fighting alongside many brave souls. These experiences give you unwavering trust and hope in your comrades and humanity—that's why you can always overcome any difficulty. It's also the most important quality I've learned from you.",
    ["Dialogue1138504"]="As a token of my appreciation, I have a gift for you. It's hidden at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magma source in the deepest part of Nogg Cave</color>. Once the researchers are gone, you can check it out. I believe it will be useful for you. And after this, you must leave Einbroch as soon as possible. Irumina won't just let this go... Be careful, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1138505"]="(140 bows his head, showing his heartfelt thanks, and as his last words fade, your vision is slowly swallowed by white light...)\nThank you, Adventurer. I am truly very, very happy... to have met you... Goodbye, my friend...",
    ["Dialogue1138601"]="... Cave? Are we still in the cave? Damn... Are the researchers still around? What... what do we do now...?",
    ["Dialogue1138602"]="Calm down, chief. 140 mentioned it would guide us to a hidden part of the cave.\n(Dave pats the chief's arm and soothes the other villagers. You notice he now carries a sense of leadership after everything.)\nEveryone, please calm down. Once the researchers leave... we'll be safe.",
    ["Dialogue1138603"]="But... but what about after... Do we really have to leave Einbroch and move somewhere else?",
    ["Dialogue1138604"]="... I've spent my entire life working in the mines. I don't know if I can do any other job, and I don't know if life will be better or worse, but 140 said something true—having choices is a form of freedom. So... I want to try starting fresh in a place where no one knows us.",
    ["Dialogue1138605"]="... I-I want to try as well.\n(A bit of a stir in the crowd as a young, skinny boy raises his hand, timid yet courageous.)\nCan I go with you, Uncle Dave?",
    ["Dialogue1138606"]="Count me in! I'm going too! Staying here is just waiting to die; might as well take a risk!",
    ["Dialogue1138607"]="I... I want to go too! I want to be with Dad! And Josephine and Fran too!\n(Like a tiny spark igniting in an unnoticed corner and spreading rapidly. The people, once lifeless, suddenly regain their hope for the future.)",
    ["Dialogue1138608"]="... You have other important matters to attend to, don't you, Adventurer? 140... probably has more instructions for you, right?",
    ["Dialogue1138609"]="(Nod)",
    ["Dialogue1138610"]="Alright, we'll say goodbye here. Thank you for everything you've done for Einbech Village. If we ever get the chance, we'll do our best to repay your kindness...\n(He bows his head a bit, placing his fist over his chest.)\n... Until next time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1138701"]="What... What in the world happened? Why do you look so dirty? Do you need me to—",
    ["Dialogue1138702"]="Huh? Use the Emergency Teleport Route to Juno? But there are airships to Juno from Einbroch daily, you could...\n(W continues to fulfill her duty, but you don't have time for her advice because, across the street, there's...?)",
    ["Dialogue1138703"]="You two, search from here! You guys... go that way! The rest, come with me!\nCheck carefully! Don't overlook anyone suspicious!",
    ["Dialogue1138704"]="Huh... Huh? Okay... Please prepare; I will now activate Kafra's Emergency Teleport Route...\n<color=#A1979FFF>Gosh... I hope Defolty doesn't find out... I'll be scolded again...</color>",
    ["Dialogue1138801"]="<size=26>Adventurer?!\nWhen did you get here?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1138802"]="<size=26>Where?! We were looking for you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1138803"]="Yeah, you've been missing for three days—Philodis nearly turned the entire cabinet inside out! He finally got a search warrant for the guards to go to Einbroch, so we took the airship to find you... Where... where have you been?!",
    ["Dialogue1138804"]="(Before you speak, Andre interrupts you.)\nThen don't say it here; quickly head back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color> and explain to Philodis. I'll contact him now. If you're any later... he might kill you!",
    ["Dialogue1138901"]="... Beep.\n(As you near the Lord's Mansion, the comm finally reconnects and beeps. It seems like Philodis has gotten the comm channel back, but...)",
    ["Dialogue1138902"]="You better have a solid reason, Adventurer. Lord Carl and I are at the Lord's Mansion, waiting for you. Be here in three minutes. Otherwise... I might reconsider your partnership with the Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1138903"]="Beep—beep—beep—beep—\n(The cold tone and the sudden busy signal in your headset clearly indicate Philodis' anger. You tremble and speed up your steps towards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1139001"]="... Relax, Adventurer.\n(The Lord is much more composed than the stern Philodis. Instead of interrogating you, he hands you a cup of tea.)\nHave some water and rest a bit, then tell us what happened.",
    ["Dialogue1139002"]="No need to apologize, Adventurer. We're glad you made it back safely. Earlier, I cracked the trojan that cut off our comm and traced its source. The signal came from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Capital Institute</color> in Einbroch... It seems you've had quite the trouble these past three days, right?",
    ["Dialogue1139003"]="(After taking a sip of hot tea, you begin recounting the past three days, and Philodis' expression grows increasingly confused.)\n... A robot from Steel Capital Institute willing to help us to take down Rekenber Corp? That's unbelievable!",
    ["Dialogue1139004"]="I'd think this was a joke if I didn't hear it from the Adventurer. But since I trust the Adventurer, I won't question it, and also...",
    ["Dialogue1139005"]="(Fulkyn opens his hand, requesting the 140's Mech Core, and looks at it carefully.)\n...This thing should prove you're not lying. I want to do a simple analysis using the mysterious device; you don't mind, right, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1139101"]="... The Adventurer is right; this Mech Core indeed contains divine power. In other words—it's a replica of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1139102"]="I get what you're saying, Adventurer. Recently, you personally collected all the fragments and sent the completed Ymir's Heart back to the realm of gods. No one in Midgard can get the real Ymir's Heart anymore, much less a replica. But remember, there's still one buried in Juno...",
    ["Dialogue1139103"]="... Ymir's Heart from the future. Fulkyn is saying that… these replicas were created with the one that's buried in Juno?\n(The Lord picked up where Fulkyn left off, their words reminding you of the well with strange inscriptions and the divine power resonating inside you since arriving in Juno...)",
    ["Dialogue1139104"]="But this was supposed to be the Republic's top secret; how did Rekenber Corp learn about it and get near Ymir's Heart to replicate it?",
    ["Dialogue1139105"]="... Maybe this is a wake-up call for us, Lord Carl.\n(Philodis pushes up his glasses, a spark in his eyes.)\nThe cabinet needs a shake-up.",
    ["Dialogue1139106"]="I believe... it's not just the cabinet. For them to get near Ymir's Heart, replicate it, and manufacture these advanced machines without us knowing... Rekenber Corp's infiltration of the Republic runs deeper than we thought.",
    ["Dialogue1139107"]="... There's something else that concerns me, Fulkyn. Do you think... Rekenber Corp could handle, produce, and apply divine power with just their <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanical engineering</color>? The Republic values technology, but we're not as skilled in magic and divine power compared to other countries...",
    ["Dialogue1139108"]="You mean... they have more allies?\n(Fulkyn is deep in thought over the Lord's question, but suddenly, you recall something from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>airship station in Einbroch</color>...?)",
    ["Dialogue1139109"]="What?! They... they have such frequent trade with Rachel?!",
    ["Dialogue1139110"]="Not only that, Adventurer even sensed divine power from the cargo... Hmph, with Arunafeltz's aid, it's no surprise they could fuse uncontrollable divine power into machines to make those monsters. 140 units... That means Rekenber Corp has at least 140 replicas of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue1139111"]="It might be even worse than we imagined. Didn't the Adventurer mention that Irumina is still planning to continue developing this model? Which means... Steel Capital Institute has enough materials for her experiments. And with the weaponry info we have... Lord Carl, do we now have enough evidence to carry out a search against Rekenber Corp?",
    ["Dialogue1139112"]="(The Lord goes quiet, then slowly shakes his head.)\n...No, it's not enough. Not even close. What we've discussed is all just our assumptions. With no written or video proof, just the Adventurer's word... they won't admit it or allow a search.",
    ["Dialogue1139113"]="No, don't blame yourself, Adventurer. While we didn't achieve our primary goal, your visit to Einbroch was still quite beneficial. Apart from the intel on the Arunafeltz, the Mech Core you brought back alone is crucial for Fulkyn...",
    ["Dialogue1139114"]="Reporting!",
    ["Dialogue1139115"]="(Carl's words are cut off by a sudden shout, and you turn to see a guard bursting in.)\nLord Carl! There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blonde girl</color> around ten years old making a fuss at the gate of the Lord's Mansion. She says... she wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accuse the Adventurer of kidnapping a minor</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1139116"]="Not her again! I told you, next time, just kick her out—",
    ["Dialogue1139117"]="Relax, Philodis.\n(Fulkyn pats Philodis on the shoulder and turns around with a cheeky smile.)\nThe person involved is back, let him deal with it.",
    ["Dialogue1139118"]="Don't pretend you don't know it. During your three days missing, she's been causing trouble at the gate of the Lord's Mansion every day. Now the entire cabinet knows you took a girl from St. Caviderina Welfare Center home. If you don't deal with this, I can't guarantee how the rumors will evolve on the street. You don't want to be the first successor of Odin's bloodline accused of kidnapping a minor girl, right?",
    ["Dialogue1139119"]="You made this mess, so you have to clean it up. About the Mech Core you brought... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I'll hold onto it for now</color>. I need to analyze it more deeply to figure out the replication process. Plus... it can be used as a power source. With this, we're just <color=#CA2E0AFF>4</color> Mech Cores away from finishing the Wide Magnetic Field Control Unit.",
    ["Dialogue1139120"]="So... let's call it. These three days have been exhausting for everyone. Let's all get some rest... and <color=#CA2E0AFF>when the time is right</color>, we'll figure out our next plan.",
    ["Dialogue1139201"]="<size=26>Don't give me that nonsense!\nEither I see him today, or... I report all of you too!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1139202"]="You...!\n(The moment she sees you, Martistine's bossy attitude goes away, replaced by an inexplicable... sadness?)\nYou liar! Where have you been?!",
    ["Dialogue1139203"]="<size=26>What's so important that makes you don't come back for three days?!</size>\nEven if you couldn't return... couldn't you leave me a message?! I thought... I thought you died out there!",
    ["Dialogue1139204"]="Pfft... Ahem! Ahem!\n(The guard nearby can't hold back his laughter, and you feel a bit awkward as well. Martistine's rant does sound like a jilted wife...)",
    ["Dialogue1139205"]="Sorry means nothing! You... you adults are all the same! You sweet-talk me while doing whatever you want... I-I won't fall for it!\n(Martistine rubs her eyes roughly, seeming both defiant and a bit unsure.)\nUnless... unless you promise me! Take me with you wherever you go from now on!",
    ["Dialogue1139206"]="I'm not afraid of danger... I've got Farbauti and Laufey! They'll protect me! Also... didn't you say we're family...",
    ["Dialogue1139207"]="<color=#A1979FFF>If we can't face danger and hardships together, what kind of family are we...</color>\n(Martistine's voice trails off, a bit tearful. This usually bossy little girl rarely shows such emotion, and after hesitating for a while, you finally soften at her sobs.)",
    ["Dialogue1139208"]="Fine... I'll listen! I'll do whatever you say! Just... just don't make me be by myself...\n(She sniffs, hesitates a bit, but finally takes your hand timidly.)\nI'll never let go of your hand when we're outside! Happy now?!",
    ["Dialogue1139209"]="<color=#A1979FFF>What a hassle... You are a grownup and still need me to coddle you... Hump...</color>\n(The little girl grumbles with her head down, but the warmth from her hand makes you feel that having a \"little follower\" might not be so bad.)",
    ["Dialogue1139301"]="Hey...<size=26>Hey! What's wrong with you?!</size>\n(Martistine's call brings you back from the weird vision. You're familiar with this sensation, the divine power in your blood, but what on earth was that...?)",
    ["Dialogue1139302"]="You look awful... are you hurt?\n(She watches you with worry. You're unsure if you should tell her about what just happened. You recall Fulkyn's warning and decide to keep it to yourself.)",
    ["Dialogue1139303"]="I see... then we should get back and rest! Or, I can have Farbauti carry you... Um, I picked up a new recipe lately! I'll cook it for you when we're home... relax! It's not one that draws in monsters!",
    ["Dialogue1139304"]="... Tastes bad? My food can't be bad!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Even if it's awful... you have to finish it! Hmph!</color>",
    ["Dialogue1139401"]="(Following Philodis' instructions, you softly place your finger on the cufflink. Instantly, a clear beep sounds in the headset.)\n... Beep. Power on, connecting; please wait.",
    ["Dialogue1139402"]="Hello... Hello? Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1139403"]="The sound is clear, and it looks like the comm signal is good. My terminal here can track your location with no problem.",
    ["Dialogue1139404"]="... Yes, all set. Now, it's time to go to Einbroch.\n(Philodis' voice pauses, seemingly calming his nerves)\nYour mission begins now, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1139501"]="Thanks for using the Schwarzwald Republic Identity Info Database. Please enter your ID.",
    ["Dialogue1139502"]="Do as I say, Adventurer. I've got a legal ID ready for you. Just type this code into the terminal...\n(Philodis slowly reads out a string of numbers, and you enter them one by one on the screen.)",
    ["Dialogue1139503"]="... Input successful, initiating search.",
    ["Dialogue1139504"]="... Search successful. Name: Robanis Manefi Awashid, Age: 29, CEO of Mochel Communication Tech. Multiple tracking orders were found, showing the most recent result...",
    ["Dialogue1139601"]="(After taking the antidote, Nina's breathing becomes steady, though her face is still pale. You recall carrying her to the village. This little girl was so fragile and light that she felt almost weightless.)",
    ["Dialogue1139701"]="Got everything checked off? There's only one flight a month to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color>, so make sure there are no slip-ups!",
    ["Dialogue1139702"]="Don't worry about it. I'm on it! Everything's straight from the institute; nothing will be missing!",
    ["Dialogue1139703"]="Hey boss, are you doing some serious deals with Arunafeltz or what? How come there's always stuff heading there every month?",
    ["Dialogue1139704"]="Shush...! Mind your own business! You think you should be digging into this?\n(The researcher smacks the worker on the head with a heavy slap.)",
    ["Dialogue1139705"]="<size=26>Get to work!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1139801"]="(The box contains some mysterious scrolls and an already opened letter with scribbled jumbled handwriting—\"Must be delivered to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Xiron</color> before the plan starts\")",
    ["Dialogue1139901"]="(There's only one box covered in red silk inside the crate, and strangely, you can sense a slight <color=#CA2E0AFF>power</color> resonance coming from it...)",
    ["Dialogue1140001"]="(You enter a password into the control panel as 140 told you. Soon after, the admin robot's power indicator starts blinking)\n... Reboot complete. Time to reset the top admin privilege.",
    ["Dialogue1140002"]="... Okay. It's connected. I'm in control of the admin robot now. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Press on</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1140101"]="(You enter a password into the control panel as 140 told you. Soon after, the admin robot's power indicator starts blinking)\n... Reboot complete. Time to reset the top admin privilege.",
    ["Dialogue1140102"]="... Huh? Weird...",
    ["Dialogue1140103"]="No... it went silky smooth. This robot was running on a basic firewall, and breaking into its system was a breeze, kind of like... the witch placed the carriage in Sleeping Beauty's room on purpose.",
    ["Dialogue1140104"]="... Maybe I'm just overthinking it. Let's check out the other robots, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1140201"]="(You enter a password into the control panel as 140 told you. Soon after, the admin robot's power indicator starts blinking)\n... Reboot complete. Time to reset the top admin privilege.",
    ["Dialogue1140202"]="(An uncommon silence takes over the other side of the headset. Eventually, 140's voice comes through the static.)\nAs I thought. None of the robots here has any security settings whatsoever; this is totally... wrong.",
    ["Dialogue1140203"]="Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the rest of the admin robots</color>... I need to do one last check.",
    ["Dialogue1140301"]="(You enter a password into the control panel as 140 told you. Soon after, the admin robot's power indicator starts blinking)\n... Reboot complete. Time to reset the top admin privilege.",
    ["Dialogue1140302"]="Same deal... Just basic firewalls, no security settings whatsoever. Irumina wouldn't allow for such a big loophole...",
    ["Dialogue1140303"]="... You're right. If she knew about our plan, she wouldn't leave us to roam freely. Since things are looking good for us right now... let's play it safe; it’s better not to stir the pot.",
    ["Dialogue1140401"]="... Matched. Querying... Order status: Transporting. Address: Steel Capital Institute, East Street No. 1, Einbroch. Current location: Einbroch Railroad Main Station. Estimated arrival: November 7.",
    ["Dialogue1140501"]="The villagers have developed a <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep-seated hatred for robots</color> over the years. They wouldn't let robots look after their kids.",
    ["Dialogue1140502"]="Why did we agree to join you in sabotaging the institute's experiment? Because... we don't want to die.",
    ["Dialogue1140503"]="Adventurer, thank you for everything you've done for Einbech Village. But to be honest... I, and most of the villagers, can't entirely trust what you say. It was machines that took everything from us, and now they claim they'll save us... If we had another option, we wouldn't... we wouldn't work with them.",
    ["Dialogue1140601"]="I believe you know, in the Republic's history, there was a revolution led by androids. These machines, created by humans, had far greater power and intelligence. As they learned and evolved, they broke free and began to challenge their creators. Eventually... although humans won, drawing on historical lessons, the cost was immense.",
    ["Dialogue1140602"]="To prevent the same thing from happening again, humans established new regulations for coexistence with androids, called the \"Mech Agreement.\" One of the rules is to impose a strict limitation on androids' database capacity and hard drive interfaces to prevent them from storing too much information. Additionally, the existing database must be formatted before installing a new one.",
    ["Dialogue1140603"]="Because humans worry that these machines, after absorbing a lot of knowledge, might evolve independent personalities and <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebel against their creators again</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1140701"]="... You ask me if I've ever thought about dominating humans?\n(140 gives a shake of his head but avoids a straight reply)\nI'm not the one to answer that.",
    ["Dialogue1140702"]="Think of it this way... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Will humans sincerely embrace machines as equals?</color> It's a question without a quick answer. But there's no pressure; the story of humanity stretches far back, and its future... will stretch even further. You have all the time in the world to think this over and witness the answer unfold.",
    ["Dialogue1140801"]="Don't interrupt me!",
    ["Dialogue1140802"]="Any issues, talk to the manufacturing robot! <color=#CA2E0AFF>All the records</color> are in the processing log!",
    ["Dialogue1140901"]="Don't say anything, Adventurer. Just drink... when you're drunk, there are no worries.\nAnd tomorrow... Hahaha, who cares... To hell with it!",
    ["Dialogue1141001"]="(140's voice pauses, then he chuckles softly, sounding relaxed and happy.)\nAdventurer, if I truly had bigger ambitions... compared to Rekenber Corp, it's you and the villagers of Einbech would be my biggest threat.",
    ["Dialogue1141101"]="It's all good, son. I'm not bitter about it. I've seen those machines at work. What a hardworking miner can barely manage in a month; they can pull it off overnight, given enough power. They never get sick or hungry... If it were up to me, I'd pick them as well...",
    ["Dialogue1141102"]="Eventually, humans... <color=#CA2E0AFF>will be replaced by machines</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1141201"]="After tomorrow, we won't live like this anymore?\n(The villager shakes his head, showing a bitter smile instead of joy.)\n... Is that true, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1141202"]="I really appreciate all you've done... and I believe you're sincere in wanting to help us. But is that robot's plan really flawless? If it goes wrong... bad things will happen to us, to the ones who betrayed the institute. But... but the robot... it's institute property anyway. Even if it fails, it might be forgiven, right?",
    ["Dialogue1141203"]="... You're right, what's the point of thinking about it now? We're way past the point of regretting...",
    ["Dialogue1141301"]="(The robot you defeat shows its face under the cloak, identical to 140. It seems to be another X-series model, but if it's 140's ally, why is it stopping you? Could it be...?)",
    ["Dialogue1141302"]="(As this intense unease begins to envelop you, the robot on the ground suddenly moves. Its previously dim screen now shows a bright red arrow pointing towards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>depths of the cave</color>, as if leading you...)",
    ["Dialogue1141401"]="(The robot lying there still has the same appearance as 140. When you get closer, its screen lights up again, showing a red arrow pointing towards <color=#CA2E0AFF>the end of the cave</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1141501"]="(This time, you hear faint echoes in the hollow cave, and it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Irumina</color> speaking. You recognize her voice. The tiny arrow on the screen points to <color=#CA2E0AFF>where the sound is coming from</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1141601"]="Over a hundred units... <size=26>Over a hundred units! And not a single core left?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1141602"]="(As Irumina screams in anger, a series of clattering sounds follow. Looks like the enraged director is throwing things around again.)\nGreat... this is great... Do you believe this will stop me from going after those stupid humans, 140?!",
    ["Dialogue1141603"]="Gather all the Project X experiment records! And the reports on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magical guidance system</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>biomimetic technology</color> from the database! Get it all ready! I'm returning to the lab!",
    ["Dialogue1141604"]="You... are going to continue building new units?",
    ["Dialogue1141605"]="Why not? I'm just one step away, and I won't stop here! The guidance system still has huge potential in the application of X-series. I will create the perfect model!",
    ["Dialogue1150101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>No... He may be a smooth talker, but he never fails when it truly matters. If that's the case, then I should...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1150102"]="I should've—gah!\n(She whips around but immediately freezes, her face twisted in pain as she clutches her cheek—it looks like she bit her tongue.)\nOw, ow, ow!",
    ["Dialogue1150103"]="W-What? No way! I was just saying—I should've lined up at the market earlier! If I don't, I won't get my hands on the exclusive Cloud <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soufflé</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1150104"]="Seriously? You've never heard of Juno's most famous seasonal treat?\n(Martistine raises an eyebrow and gives you a slightly disapproving look.)",
    ["Dialogue1150105"]="Every year around this time, when the Grand Peco enters its breeding season, restaurants across the city roll out their seasonal specialties! And the most popular one of all...\n(With a dramatic flip of a magazine, a glossy image of a golden soufflé fills the page. You could almost smell the honey just looking at it!)\nBehold—the legendary Cloud Soufflé!",
    ["Dialogue1150106"]="From what I've heard, the shops on the east side of the market have been packed every single day! They sell out within two hours of opening! I even set multiple alarms today just so I wouldn't miss it... So, are you coming with me?",
    ["Dialogue1150107"]="Come on, are you in or what?\n(She's already waving down two robots.)\nKeep stalling, and you can kiss that soufflé goodbye!",
    ["Dialogue1150201"]="See?! If you hadn't dragged your feet, we wouldn't be stuck behind these people!",
    ["Dialogue1150202"]="Nice try, but flattery won't get you off the hook! If I don't get my soufflé today, you're—",
    ["Dialogue1150203"]="What?! You blame it on me? If I don't get my soufflé today, you're—",
    ["Dialogue1150204"]="... Next in line! Hi there, what can I get for you?",
    ["Dialogue1150205"]="Wait, what?! It's my turn?!\n(The shock barely has time to register before her excited voice practically shakes the air around her.)",
    ["Dialogue1150206"]="<size=26>Please<color=#CA2E0AFF> give me one serving of Cloud Soufflé</color>—thank you!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1150301"]="Oh wow, lucky you! This is the last one for today! Would you like it to go, or are you eating it now?",
    ["Dialogue1150302"]="Right now! Of course, I'm eating it now!",
    ["Dialogue1150303"]="Ah, a true soufflé connoisseur! Our soufflé is at its absolute best within the first <color=#CA2E0AFF>thirty minutes</color>! Wait too long, and it'll deflate, losing that heavenly softness!",
    ["Dialogue1150304"]="Here, here! You two, this is the perfect moment to dig in!\n(The shopkeeper hands the dessert box to Martistine, eyes gleaming with excitement.)\nGo on! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take a bite</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1150305"]="<size=26>Excuse me, please wait a moment!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1150401"]="Pardon my rudeness. I know this is an odd request, but... if possible, I'm willing to pay twice the price. Would you consider letting me have this dish?",
    ["Dialogue1150402"]="Whoa, whoa, whoa... What are you thinking?! No way!\n(Martistine clutches her dessert and steps back defensively.)\nPicking on a kid for food? Have some shame!",
    ["Dialogue1150403"]="I'm sorry, young lady. It's just... I truly wish to taste this dish. I'm not from the Republic; I'm only in Juno temporarily for business and must return to Arunafeltz tomorrow. If I miss this chance today, I don't know when I'll ever get another. And this dish...",
    ["Dialogue1150404"]="(His expression falters, his eyes lowering slightly as they settle on the dessert in Martistine's hands.)\n... Cloud Soufflé. It was the last meal I ever shared with my parents. They were taken from me in an accident, and I never had the chance to dine with them again. This dish... it's more than just food to me...",
    ["Dialogue1150405"]="I understand... If it were me, I wouldn't hand it over so easily either...\n(He lets out a dry chuckle, but there's a tinge of sadness in it as he lowers his head.)",
    ["Dialogue1150406"]="Oh, come on... It's just a dessert! I'm not heartless! Here, take it!",
    ["Dialogue1150407"]="You don't have to talk me into it! It's just a soufflé! I’m not that heartless—here, it's yours!",
    ["Dialogue1150408"]="(The girl shoves the dessert toward him, crossing her arms.)\nGo on! It won't taste as good if it gets cold!",
    ["Dialogue1150501"]="I'm truly grateful, both of you... This dessert will hold a special place in my heart forever...\n(This blond young man lowers his head in a solemn bow, and you quickly move to stop him.)",
    ["Dialogue1150502"]="No... Please allow me to express my gratitude. To you, this may just be a simple dish, but to me, it's the last memory I have with my parents. If you ever find yourselves in Arunafeltz...\n(The blond young man hands you a small and exquisite card.)",
    ["Dialogue1150503"]="Yes, it's my trading company. We have offices in every major city of Arunafeltz. If you ever need anything... don't hesitate to reach out. I'll do everything in my power to help.",
    ["Dialogue1150504"]="Well then, I have an important meeting to attend. Please excuse me.\n(He bows slightly, his tone formal yet warm.)\nUntil we meet again...",
    ["Dialogue1150601"]="(With the last soufflé sold and the crowd dispersing, Martistine watches the young man leave, a hint of disappointment on her face.)\nSigh... I finally got my hands on a soufflé...",
    ["Dialogue1150602"]="... Really? You better not ditch me at the last minute with some \"urgent mission\" excuse again!",
    ["Dialogue1150603"]="Ugh, I knew it—Mr. Big Beard is calling you again, isn't he?\n(She waves dismissively, lips pursed in frustration.)\nI'll be fine. I don't need an escort.",
    ["Dialogue1150604"]="<size=26>Ugh, stop nagging!</size>\nI'll go straight home, no running around, no causing trouble! Farbauti and Laufey are with me, so what's there to worry about? But you... you better hurry back! We're eating together, got it?!",
    ["Dialogue1150701"]="Wait... you're the Adventurer from earlier?",
    ["Dialogue1150702"]="... Oh? I wasn't aware that Lord Malam and the Adventurer had already met. What a coincidence! I had invited the Adventurer here today with the intent of making introductions... but it seems I've made a fool of myself instead.",
    ["Dialogue1150703"]="You flatter me, Lord Carl. The Adventurer and I merely crossed paths at the market earlier. If anything, it was their generosity that allowed me to acquire a rather special dish. If I am now formally introduced, it would be an even greater honor.",
    ["Dialogue1150704"]="Then, allow me to make a formal introduction. Lord Malam, I imagine you've heard about the android incident in Juno? I regret to say that, despite my position as the Lord, I could not prevent it. But this Adventurer and our guards stepped up and restored order, ensuring our citizens' safety...",
    ["Dialogue1150705"]="(Carl pauses for a moment before turning to you.)\nAdventurer, as I mentioned in my letter, a distinguished guest was expected at the Lord's Mansion today—none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>Malam</color>, the envoy of Arunafeltz. He is the adopted son of Lady <color=#CA2E0AFF>Neirun</color>, one of the Twelve Bishops, and the head of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gilded Rose</color>, the largest trading company in Arunafeltz. His purpose in coming to the Republic is...",
    ["Dialogue1150706"]="I have come to personally invite Lord Carl to attend Arunafeltz's annual Dawn Moon Festival. However...\n(Malam smiles, his tone carrying a hint of regret.)\nLord Carl, burdened with his many duties, has already declined my invitation. But...",
    ["Dialogue1150707"]="(The blond young man carries himself with elegance, but his smile's a sly glint.)\n... But an idea just crossed my mind—Lord Carl, would you consider allowing this Adventurer to represent you at Arunafeltz's festival?",
    ["Dialogue1150708"]="Hahaha... As expected of Lord Malam. I assume you had already anticipated my thoughts the moment the Adventurer walked through that door?",
    ["Dialogue1150709"]="You are correct. I had already planned for the Adventurer to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Arunafeltz</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF> to present my offering</color> to the Pope, in <color=#CA2E0AFF>celebration of the Goddess' birth</color>. Firstly, while I cannot attend in person, it is only right that I still extend my respects. I have no children of my own, and my most trusted aide, Philodis, is away on official duty... Fortunately, this Adventurer is a dear comrade and a savior to the Republic, making them more than worthy of this responsibility...",
    ["Dialogue1150710"]="... And secondly, I must admit, this is also a personal wish. This Adventurer has worked tirelessly across the Republic without a single moment of rest. The capital of Arunafeltz, Rachel, is a renowned travel destination—perhaps this is the perfect chance to take a break. Lord Malam, I trust you to see that they're well taken care of...",
    ["Dialogue1150711"]="Nothing would please me more, Lord Carl. The Adventurer has provided both you and me with great service. If the Adventurer is willing to make this trip, I have no doubt that the Pope will be pleased. Rest assured, I will see to it that they experience all that Arunafeltz has to offer.",
    ["Dialogue1150712"]="Then it's settled. I will arrange everything, and before the Dawn Moon Festival begins, the Adventurer shall deliver my tribute to the Pope.",
    ["Dialogue1150713"]="(With a pleasant smile, the blond young man offers a graceful bow to you and Lord Carl.)\nI still have pressing business to attend to, so I won't impose further. Adventurer, when you reach Rachel, you may find me at the Temple or at the Gilded Rose's Trading House in the city. I shall be expecting you.",
    ["Dialogue1150801"]="... My apologies, Adventurer. I made this decision without consulting you, but this is truly an opportunity we cannot afford to miss.",
    ["Dialogue1150802"]="Back in Einbroch, we uncovered that Rekenber Corp has ties with Arunafeltz and that it has been their divine knowledge to produce Ymir's Heart replicas. A conspiracy of this scale is like a web—too many connections, too dangerous to tread recklessly. And from what I know, Arunafeltz's political scene has been stuck in <color=#CA2E0AFF>faction conflicts</color> for the past ten years...",
    ["Dialogue1150803"]="Malam isn't just an envoy—he's the face of the faction led by Bishop Neirun, the so-called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Conservatives</color>. On the other side stands the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Radicals</color>, led by Bishop <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yus</color>, who holds true command of Arunafeltz's <color=#CA2E0AFF>military power</color>. This invitation is more than just a festival pass... I'd say it's...",
    ["Dialogue1150804"]="Exactly. If I were to go personally, it would signal that the Republic is aligning with the Conservative faction. That would undoubtedly draw Rekenber Corp's attention, making my situation even more difficult. But if you deliver the tribute instead, it won't be seen as a political statement. And besides...\n(Carl chuckles, rubbing his beard, a mix of relief and nostalgia in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue1150805"]="You truly are favored by the gods. I may not know what happened at the market, but judging from Malam's attitude, he holds you in high regard. That means you'll have a direct path to the elites of Arunafeltz, which is perfect for investigating their dealings with Rekenber Corp. Even if something goes wrong... at the very least, Malam will make sure you stay alive.",
    ["Dialogue1150806"]="No rush, Adventurer. Until now, I've only spoken to you as a Lord. But as Carl, as a person—I truly hope you take this chance to relax, enjoy yourself, and have a peaceful holiday. And that girl...",
    ["Dialogue1150807"]="(Lord Carl lowers his head, trying to recall.)\nIf I recall correctly... her name is Martistine, right? You could <color=#CA2E0AFF>take her with you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1150808"]="Oh, I mean it! The Dawn Moon Festival isn't just any celebration—it marks both Freyja's birthday and the founding of Arunafeltz. It's a spectacle few ever get to see, so make sure she enjoys every moment.",
    ["Dialogue1150901"]="Huh... Seriously? You're taking me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arunafeltz</color> for the Dawn Moon Festival?!",
    ["Dialogue1150902"]="Then... then can Farbauti and Laufey come along too?!",
    ["Dialogue1150903"]="Wait! What about my Cloud Soufflé?! You said we'd queue up for it tomorrow!",
    ["Dialogue1150904"]="... You swear? No backing out on me!",
    ["Dialogue1150905"]="Cross your heart and hope to die... Okay!\n(After getting your promise, she excitedly wiggles her fingers, then rushes off to her room.)\n<size=26>I'm gonna pack right now!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1151001"]="Ah, greetings, Adventurer! Welcome to Rachel, the grand capital of Arunafeltz!\nHmm... let me guess... You're here for the Dawn Moon Festival, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue1151002"]="(W grins and puffs up her chest, but oops—an envelope slips out of her pocket just enough for you to spot a familiar <color=#CA2E0AFF>wax seal</color>.)\nHey, don't underestimate me! I've been rocking my job at Kafra Corporation for three years now!",
    ["Dialogue1151003"]="Wait, wait—oh no...\n(She pouts, twin tails bouncing slightly as she slumps.)\n you are way too sharp...",
    ["Dialogue1151004"]="You got it, Adventurer! Actually, I received word from Philodis even before you boarded the airship to Rachel. Officially, you're here as a tourist, but since you'll be meeting the Pope, you mustn't do anything that could jeopardize our diplomatic relations! That's why Philodis specifically tasked me with briefing you on the customs of Arunafeltz...",
    ["Dialogue1151005"]="For instance... First and foremost! Under no circumstances should you enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color> outside Rachel! It's a holy site of Freyja, strictly off-limits, even to the Pope! Anyone who breaks this law... will be sentenced to <color=#CA2E0AFF>death by fire</color>. Honestly, I think you're better off staying entirely inside the city!",
    ["Dialogue1151006"]="Lately, a lot of merchant caravans have been getting robbed just outside the city! Apparently, a gang of seasoned <color=#CA2E0AFF>bandits</color> has been looting <color=#CA2E0AFF>noble</color> shipments. Even with the Temple Guards ramping up security, they haven't caught them yet. So for safety's sake, you should stay inside the city.",
    ["Dialogue1151007"]="Another thing to remember—Arunafeltz is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>theocracy</color>, where the will of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Freyja</color> reigns supreme. The Pope is merely a vessel of her divine will, governing on her behalf. Even if your beliefs differ, I ask that you respect local customs and be mindful of your words and actions. Otherwise...",
    ["Dialogue1151008"]="(W sneaks up beside you, voice dropping to a hushed whisper.)\nThis place is packed with Freyja fanatics. You seriously don't wanna say the wrong thing and get your butt kicked, trust me.",
    ["Dialogue1151009"]="Well...",
    ["Dialogue1151010"]="(W tilts her head, then kneels down with a smirk, ruffling Martistine's hair.)\nHey, hey, you must be Martistine, right? Philodis specifically mentioned you in his letter! He told me to make sure you stay glued to the Adventurer and not go wandering off. Got it?",
    ["Dialogue1151011"]="Excuse me?!\n(Martistine slaps W's hand away, frowning.)\nWhat do you mean by that?",
    ["Dialogue1151012"]="Wait, no! I am not saying anything bad! It's just... There have been way too many <color=#CA2E0AFF>child abductions</color> in Rachel lately. And girls like you—cute with a foreign accent—are exactly the kind of targets those people look for! Adventurer, seriously, don't take your eyes off her in crowded areas!",
    ["Dialogue1151013"]="And one last thing! I highly suggest that the two of you attend today's <color=#CA2E0AFF>ritual ceremony</color> at Temple Square! It's the perfect opportunity to witness a real \"miracle\" up close. Trust me, Adventurer, once you see it, you'll understand why people here worship the Goddess with such devotion. Now, about the location...",
    ["Dialogue1151014"]="(Gesturing upward, W points to the towering structure at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northernmost</color> end of the city. At its peak, a dazzling blue gemstone catches the light.)\nThe <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple</color> is at the highest point of Rachel! Walk straight down this road, <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass the Holy Spring, climb the steps</color>, and you’re there!",
    ["Dialogue1151101"]="Well, well, didn't expect to run into you like this, Adventurer. It's been a while since Umbala—how've you been? What brings you to Arunafeltz?",
    ["Dialogue1151102"]="... So you're here as Lord Carl's envoy, bringing a ceremonial gift to the Pope for the festival? And taking a little detour for a leisurely trip with this young lady?\n(Israel listens intently, his brows raising in astonishment.)\nAnd now, you're on your way to the Temple?",
    ["Dialogue1151103"]="Then... why don't we go together? To be honest, I was heading to the Temple myself for today's worship.",
    ["Dialogue1151104"]="(Israel sighs, shaking his head, then gestures to his simple clothing.)\nI carry the mark of exile—becoming a Priest again is beyond my reach. My mentor and I were cast out long ago, forbidden from ever stepping foot in the Temple again. If I wish to see the Pope, I must attend the monthly prayer just like any other devotee...",
    ["Dialogue1151105"]="It's alright, Adventurer. By now, I've come to terms with my past—you don't have to tiptoe around it for my sake.\n(Israel smiles, patting your shoulder before raising a hand to gesture toward the towering Temple in the distance.)\nFor now... we should hurry and head there.",
    ["Dialogue1151106"]="The ceremony will start when the sun reaches its peak above the tower. We have a little time left, but...\n(He shifts his gaze to Martistine and her companions.)\nBringing them along might not be the best idea.",
    ["Dialogue1151107"]="<size=26>Why!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1151108"]="Unlike the Republic, machines aren't widely accepted in Arunafeltz. In fact, some worshippers view <color=#CA2E0AFF>machines</color> as blasphemous—an insult to the Goddess. If we show up at the ceremony with two massive machines in tow, things might get... complicated. I'd recommend finding <color=#CA2E0AFF>a discreet location</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>leaving them there</color> for now.",
    ["Dialogue1151109"]="(Though unwilling, Martistine gives a reluctant nod under your watchful eyes.)\n... Alright then.",
    ["Dialogue1151201"]="Come on, we're still walking? How much further?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ugh, this sucks...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1151202"]="A little closer.\n(Israel takes a few more steps forward and points at the bushes in front of him.)\nHere. Have your robots hide inside and stay still.",
    ["Dialogue1151203"]="Fine... Farbauti, Laufey, just do it.\n(With a huff, Martistine gives the order. As the robots shuffle into the bush, she nudges your arm.)\nUh, can you hit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>power button</color> on their <color=#CA2E0AFF>necks</color>? They're too tall for me.",
    ["Dialogue1151301"]="You sure they'll be fine here? Cause if something happens, you're so paying me back for it!",
    ["Dialogue1151302"]="They'll be fine.\n(Israel adjusts the branches to better conceal the robots, then glances toward the bustling market in the distance.)\n... My allies are keeping watch nearby. This place is secure.",
    ["Dialogue1151303"]="Okay, we should get moving. We need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach the Temple Square</color> before the ceremony begins. Follow me.",
    ["Dialogue1151401"]="Remember what I told you—stay quiet, Adventurer. You too, little one. This place is crawling with watchful eyes.\n(He presses down on your shoulder and signals toward the entrance.)\nCome on, <color=#CA2E0AFF>let's go back first</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1151501"]="Adventurer, I know you want to ask what exactly happened during the ceremony. But before I answer... As the successor of Odin's bloodline, did you feel any <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine resonance</color> when the Pope recited the blessings?",
    ["Dialogue1151502"]="... Just as I expected. My teacher was right... These people are beyond saving.",
    ["Dialogue1151503"]="Adventurer, I believe you still remember everything we went through in Umbala. I explained back then—my mentor turned away from Freyja's teachings and sought another god's guidance because he saw the true, corrupt nature of the church. They steal time from the poor, sell it to the rich, and live the high life off the profits...",
    ["Dialogue1151504"]="(With a tight grip on his fists, Israel exhales sharply, his rage barely contained.)\nEverything you saw at that ceremony—that was how they <color=#CA2E0AFF> stole the lifespans of the followers</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1151505"]="Whoa, whoa, what?! Are you saying we just got scammed out of our own lifespans?!",
    ["Dialogue1151506"]="... No need to worry, little one. You and the Adventurer never drank from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Spring</color>, so you weren't affected.",
    ["Dialogue1151507"]="Exactly. I stopped you from drinking the spring water because I knew it contained the <color=#CA2E0AFF>reagent</color> needed for alchemy. By consuming the spring water, the followers unknowingly absorb the reagent. Later, the Pope conducts the alchemical ritual, drawing their lifeforce into <color=#CA2E0AFF>scepter</color>, where it remains until needed. Long ago, my mentor, Hibram, stood against this horrifying ritual—and that's why he got exiled.",
    ["Dialogue1151508"]="I asked if you felt a divine resonance to determine whether the Pope was truly blessing the people... or simply using alchemy to steal their lifespans. But unfortunately...",
    ["Dialogue1151509"]="Of course, I won't just stand by and do nothing. The reason I came back to Arunafeltz this time is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill my mentor's last wish</color> and change the current state of the kingdom... And meeting you here? I believe that's a sign from Freyja herself. If you're willing... I'd like to ask for <color=#CA2E0AFF>your help</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1151510"]="I understand—you have your own task and perhaps allegiances I'm unaware of. But let me ask you one more thing, Adventurer. You met the envoy from Arunafeltz in Juno. The one who extended the invitation—was he called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Malam</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1151511"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>... I see. That confirms it. In that case... </color></size>\nWe might have some time to catch up before the Dawn Moon Festival begins. Because Malam... isn't currently in Arunafeltz.",
    ["Dialogue1151512"]="Before I followed my mentor to the Nameless Island, Malam and I grew up together—we were close friends, never keeping secrets from each other. That was true then... and it's still true now. If you don't believe me, I can take you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gilded Rose Trading Company</color>. The receptionists there know me well...",
    ["Dialogue1151513"]="Naturally. If everything I've told you is correct, then...\n(Israel lowers his head in a formal bow.)\n... I hope you'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany me somewhere</color>. Just for a bit. Don't worry—I would never harm you.",
    ["Dialogue1151601"]="Whoa, Israel! Long time no see!\n(The receptionist gives him a friendly wave before leaning in with a knowing glance.)\nMalam hasn't returned yet. He's still at... <color=#CA2E0AFF>that place</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1151602"]="Wait, what?! I swore I kept my voice down! Oh no... oh no...",
    ["Dialogue1151603"]="No worries. This Adventurer and I go way back. I was planning to introduce him to Malam myself... Any idea when he's returning?",
    ["Dialogue1151604"]="Hmm... hard to say exactly, but he won't be gone for long. You know, with the Dawn Moon Festival coming up, he'll have to return to Rachel <color=#CA2E0AFF>before it starts</color>. If you're not in a rush, I can get the Adventurer a place to stay in the meantime. How about it? Once Malam is back, I'll have someone inform you...",
    ["Dialogue1151605"]="... Nah, I got their stay covered. Just do your thing and send me a heads-up when Malam's back.\n(Israel gives you a quick pat on the shoulder.)\nAlright then, like we talked about... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1151606"]="Alright then, safe travels! I'll let you know the moment I hear anything!",
    ["Dialogue1151701"]="Oh, you... you—!\n(The unkempt soldier glares at you. But upon noticing your ordinary clothing, he starts yelling at you.)\nYou've got some nerve! You actually dared to hit me?!",
    ["Dialogue1151702"]="You're looking at none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>Musa</color>, Commander of the Temple Guard! I serve the Pope and was sent here to Grey Wolf Village to collect the tithe! And you—you dare stand in my way?! Protecting these ungrateful wretches who refuse to pay their dues?! I'll—I'll—",
    ["Dialogue1151703"]="... Oh yeah? And what? Report this to the Pope and get everyone in Grey Wolf Village executed?\n(Israel lets out a dry chuckle, pulling the child behind him.)",
    ["Dialogue1151704"]="Tell me, commander, do you even understand the tithe system? One in ten, every month. Over the last three months, the entire village has barely managed to mine <color=#CA2E0AFF>seventeen crates</color> of ore. And yet, you—just the other day—robbed them of their family's heirloom, a gold ornament passed down for generations! That's worth at least <color=#CA2E0AFF>a hundred crates</color> of ore!",
    ["Dialogue1151705"]="<size=26>How is this any different from banditry?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1151706"]="Nonsense... All lies! <size=26>What gold? I know nothing about it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1151707"]="(With a cold smirk, Israel yanks Musa closer, his voice dropping to a whisper.)\n... Oh really? So the man I saw near the casino last night, losing every last coin, wasn't you? And that heirloom he used to pay his debts—what a strange coincidence, huh? Exactly like the one you stole from the village chief.",
    ["Dialogue1151708"]="(At Israel's whispered threat, you see Musa gulp nervously.)\nDon't push your luck. Even a cornered rabbit will bite.",
    ["Dialogue1151709"]="D-Damn you! <color=#CA2E0AFF>This isn't over, you hear me</color>?!\n(Musa scrambles away from Israel, practically tripping over himself as he ducks behind his soldiers.)\nWe're outta here! Ow—hey, moron, hold me up!",
    ["Dialogue1151801"]="... What a reckless move…\n(Watching the guards flee, Israel sighs, rubbing shaking his head in regret.)",
    ["Dialogue1151802"]="We should have been more careful. The guards have always had free reign in this village, and the people don't resist—not just because they lack the strength, but because they know the truth: behind these soldiers stands the Temple. Here in Arunafeltz, the Temple is the word of the Goddess. To defy them is to defy her.",
    ["Dialogue1151803"]="Sure, we chased them off for now. But just chasing off a few goons won't fix the real problem. We need to go deeper. Don't you think so, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1151804"]="I insisted on bringing you to Grey Wolf Village because I wanted to be honest with you and ask for your help. The ceremony we witnessed and the cruelty of the Temple Guards are not isolated events but symptoms of a deeply broken system. In places we cannot see, even more unspeakable horrors are unfolding. If we want real change, the only way is to stop the current regime.",
    ["Dialogue1151805"]="Yeah. I've thought this through, and this is the only way. It won't be easy, but if I can save my homeland and make my mentor's wish come true... then I will not hesitate.",
    ["Dialogue1151806"]="... I get it. This is heavy. But we've fought side by side before—I only ask that you don't turn me down outright. Stay in Grey Wolf Village for now; take a look around. By the time the Dawn Moon Festival starts, you'll have seen enough to make your own decision—",
    ["Dialogue1151807"]="... Enough. Cut it out.",
    ["Dialogue1151901"]="(A cold-eyed, silver-haired man interrupts, stepping between you and Israel.)\n... Didn't I say not to provoke the guards? We've spent months lying low, and now you risk exposing everything. If Musa mobilizes a full-scale raid tomorrow, it's over for all of us.",
    ["Dialogue1151902"]="... Sorry, Sartre. I lost my temper today but had to step in when they tried to take Jeremy. I'll deal with the consequences. But for now, I want you to meet this Adventurer—",
    ["Dialogue1151903"]="No thanks. I told you that we don't need outsiders, remember? And your friend here is way too honest to be on our side.\n(Sartre tosses a heavy sack onto the ground, the rope slipping loose to reveal glittering gold.)\nUnless... you think they'd be up for robbing a merchant or two?",
    ["Dialogue1151904"]="... We have no other choice, Adventurer. The Temple has seized every inch of land and imposed heavy tithes on the people. If we don't fight back, how will the weak and elderly survive? And Sartre... he's never hurt anyone. He only robs those who can afford to lose...",
    ["Dialogue1151905"]="... What? We can't take their money?\n(Sartre's voice rises, his glare turning icy as he stomps on the ground.)\nSix centuries ago, their forefathers robbed our people. What do you think? Should we just forget that it ever happened?",
    ["Dialogue1151906"]="I'm not some philosopher like Israel, but I do know one thing—my people are dying. No food, no work, no way to live. The Temple took our land, forced us to settle here, and then took everything from us! Even when we keep our heads down, we're still treated like heathens—",
    ["Dialogue1151907"]="(Blood drips from his fist as he strikes the platform, rage seething in his voice.)\n... Who is this \"Goddess\" anyway? What gives her the right to take everything from us—our land, our lives, our history?!",
    ["Dialogue1151908"]="You know, Adventurer... sometimes I think back on what my mentor used to tell us. The very first lesson we learned was—\n(Israel reaches out, loosening Sartre's grip as the villagers tend to his wounded hand.)\n\"Life or death, good or bad—it doesn't matter. The Goddess loves everyone the same.\"",
    ["Dialogue1151909"]="But now... everything the Temple does goes against its own faith. Even the Goddess herself has become nothing more than a tool to satisfy their greed. This... this is not the future my mentor and I dreamed of. I know I can't change this world alone, so every bit of support matters. Sartre, the villagers, my allies... and you as well.",
    ["Dialogue1151910"]="... Naturally. I'll find you a place to stay here in Grey Wolf Village. Take your time, look around, and make your decision. Whatever you choose, I promise—I'll get you back to Rachel in one piece.",
    ["Dialogue1151911"]="(Israel looks over at Sartre and the villagers, his voice firm.)\nI'm putting my life on the line for this one. Even if the Adventurer doesn't join us, there won't be anyone who knows about what happened today. Should the Adventurer choose to join us, we have found the strongest ally ever.",
    ["Dialogue1151912"]="... Whatever. If you're vouching for this one, I'll let it slide. Take them to the empty <color=#CA2E0AFF>house at the farthest north</color>. But listen up, outsider—\n(The silver-haired young man narrows his eyes, landing a warning on you.)\nThis doesn't mean I trust you.",
    ["Dialogue1151913"]="Heh, alright. Let's see what makes you worth all this fuss from Israel.",
    ["Dialogue1152001"]="Jeremy, you're a big boy now. You shouldn't cry so easily. Mommy's fine. I just need to rest for a bit, and then... and then...",
    ["Dialogue1152002"]="You're... the Adventurer who helped us before? I remember you—you're a friend of Lord Israel.\n(The woman bows deeply, holding her child close.)\nIf not for you, I would have lost Jeremy... Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1152003"]="Don't worry about me. It's barely a scratch...",
    ["Dialogue1152004"]="Mom, your hand! You're still bleeding! I'll... I'll go find some Drosera! The leaves will help, and then it won't hurt anymore...",
    ["Dialogue1152101"]="You're helping us again... I don't know how to repay your kindness. Why don't you come over for dinner? I'll go to work, get my wages, and buy some drinks to treat you!",
    ["Dialogue1152102"]="A small cut like this won't stop me. If I don't work, we won't have anything left to live on...",
    ["Dialogue1152103"]="W-Wait, how could I let you do that?!",
    ["Dialogue1152104"]="Mom! I bet the Adventurer can find so many pretty gems! We could sell them for money, get medicine, yummy food, and even a real glass window, just like the one we saw in the city! Then the wind won't keep us up at night!",
    ["Dialogue1152105"]="He's just a child, Adventurer. You don't have to take his words seriously, I...\n(She falters, clearly uncertain. Though she keeps refusing, her weary expression betrays how much she truly needs help from you.)",
    ["Dialogue1152106"]="I'll accept your help, but I don't know how to thank you properly. So... how about this? Come and have dinner at my place. I work at the quarry southeast of Rachel Plains, <color=#CA2E0AFF>gathering ores</color>—it's tough work, and I bet you'll be starving by the end of it. So... please, let me cook for you.",
    ["Dialogue1152201"]="... Aloy? That woman who's always behind on work?\n(The foreman leans back, chewing on his apple with a bored expression.)\nWhat is it this time? Is her kid sick again? So she sent you to do her shift?",
    ["Dialogue1152202"]="Whatever, I don't care. Pay's based on output anyway. Doesn't matter who's doing the work.\n(He kicks the basket lightly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Grab</color> a <color=#CA2E0AFF>metal detector</color> from there.",
    ["Dialogue1152203"]="Flick the switch and extend the antenna. If there's anything valuable nearby, it'll start beeping. Bring the raw stones back to me—the shinier, the better. I'll pay you <color=#CA2E0AFF>10</color> Zeny per piece. The more you find, the more you earn. Got it?",
    ["Dialogue1152204"]="Go on then. Just make sure you're back before dark.\n(The foreman yawns and waves a lazy hand.)\nGotta get home for dinner on time, after all...",
    ["Dialogue1152301"]="This is junk! I can't even resell this. <color=#CA2E0AFF>5</color> Zeny per piece, take it or leave it!",
    ["Dialogue1152302"]="Buddy, open your eyes. These rocks are worthless! I wouldn't take them for free!\n(He smirks and pushes the basket at you.)\nThink you can do better? Go sell them yourself!",
    ["Dialogue1152303"]="Heh, we got a tough guy here.\n(He leans back smugly.)\nLet's see who's dumb enough to take those off your hands.",
    ["Dialogue1152305"]="Boss! Please take a look at my haul!\n(As you ball your fists, another worker quickly interjects, offering his basket to the foreman.)\nI worked all day in the riverbed to find these gems—good stuff, I swear!",
    ["Dialogue1152306"]="Hmm... let me see... not bad, not bad...",
    ["Dialogue1152307"]="<size=26>I knew you had an eye for quality, boss!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1152308"]="Boss, don't get mad at the rookie—he doesn't know better. Aloy's been breaking her back here for ages. How about... I'll sell my batch at <color=#CA2E0AFF>5</color> Zeny too, and you take his along with them?",
    ["Dialogue1152309"]="Alright, whatever! I'll buy them all!\n(He digs into his coat and flicks a handful of coins onto the ground.)\nNow get lost! And don't come back!",
    ["Dialogue1152310"]="Okay, okay, we're going!\n(He quickly grabs the scattered coins, his grip firm on your wrist, steering you away.)\nDon't make a scene, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1152401"]="Yeah, that sucked, I know. But seriously, don't go picking fights with the foreman. That guy's got more power than he looks.",
    ["Dialogue1152402"]="(With a tired sigh, he shakes his head, smiling faintly.)\n... So you're filling in for Aloy, right? Figures. You wouldn't know the rules of the trade.",
    ["Dialogue1152403"]="The way Arunafeltz runs its gem industry is different. Because ores are crucial for alchemy, their mining, distribution, and trade are all under strict regulation, mostly in the hands of the aristocrats. This quarry is technically noble land, so everything mined here belongs to them. Selling raw materials on the market is illegal. And good luck finding a merchant dumb enough to take them off your hands.",
    ["Dialogue1152404"]="Besides, the foreman controls this whole quarry, which means he's got connections—no doubt about it. He decides what's worth something and what's not, and if we step out of line, he can easily find a reason to make us pay for it. There's no point going against him.",
    ["Dialogue1152405"]="Look, you're an outsider. No need to stir up trouble for yourself.\n(He scoops up the coins and hands them over.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Take your pay</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1152501"]="Hey, Adventurer! Did you get some shiny gems? Did the foreman give you lots of coins? Are we having beef pie for dinner?!",
    ["Dialogue1152601"]="(Aloy takes the pouch, pours the coins into her palm, and counts them carefully.)\n... 4, 5, 6, 7?",
    ["Dialogue1152602"]="Huh...? This is less than what mom usually earns...",
    ["Dialogue1152603"]="Don't apologize, Adventurer. You're not used to this work, right? And that foreman... he definitely underpaid you on purpose. Just getting any money at all is a win. If anything, I should be the one thanking you for helping someone you barely know...",
    ["Dialogue1152604"]="So... what's for dinner, mom?",
    ["Dialogue1152605"]="(Aloy bends down and ruffles his hair lovingly.)\nWe'll have what we always do, alright?",
    ["Dialogue1152701"]="Nope! You messed it up again!<size=26>Didn't I say you need to carry the number over?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1152702"]="Wahhh... Math is too hard! I don't wanna do this anymore...",
    ["Dialogue1152703"]="No way! Math's the foundation for alchemy! If you can't do this, how're you ever gonna learn alchemy?!",
    ["Dialogue1152704"]="But we don't need to learn alchemy! Mom said only the <color=#CA2E0AFF>noble kids</color> in the city have to study it. Laisa and I... we just need to learn how to find ores! As long as we can do that, the nobles will buy them from us!",
    ["Dialogue1152705"]="You... stop staring and do something!\n(Martistine huffs, stomping her foot before giving you a hard shove.)\nDo something! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Just look at their homework</color>! It's a complete mess!",
    ["Dialogue1152801"]="Even in the welfare center, the homework was never this awful! Ms. Petra might've been meek around the director but never slacked off in class! And this village? No school, no teachers—am I seriously expected to start with the alphabet?!",
    ["Dialogue1152802"]="Ugh... this is all your friend's fault! I knew he was up to no good!\n(Martistine slams the workbook into your hands and gestures at the village gate.)\nI quit! You tell him to find another sucker!",
    ["Dialogue1152803"]="Yes! That guy, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color>! Go tell that dude—<size=26>I QUIT!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1152901"]="(After hearing Martistine's complaints, Israel lets out a small, wry smile, his golden eyes tinged with guilt.)\nI see... My apologies, Adventurer. I'm usually the one teaching the kids, but with everything going on with the Temple Guards, I just haven't had the time. That's why I asked for her help...",
    ["Dialogue1152902"]="That's right, Adventurer. There are no schools or teachers in this village. You see, Arunafeltz has always held alchemy in the highest regard. To the Priests and nobles, alchemy is the foundation of the nation, a divine gift from Goddess Freyja. Thus, those who are <color=#CA2E0AFF>not blessed by the gods</color> are <color=#CA2E0AFF>forbidden from practicing</color> it. You may wonder—these villagers believe in the Goddess too, so why aren't they included? That... is one of the many reasons why my teacher and I have sought reform.",
    ["Dialogue1152903"]="(Israel pulls out a small booklet from his pocket, its worn corners showing signs of heavy use.)\nHere, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>See for yourself</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1153001"]="According to this scripture, six centuries ago, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pope Isumia</color> arrived in these desolate lands, bringing with her the sacred <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heron's Feather</color> and a group of Priests to establish a nation. At that time, this place had neither cities nor a formal government, only a sprawling desert inhabited by numerous nomadic tribes. These tribes operated independently, each guarding their own stretch of land. But then Isumia arrived... and changed everything...",
    ["Dialogue1153002"]="Using alchemy, she transformed the barren land. With the divine power of the Heron's Feather, she summoned holy springs and green oases, laying the foundation for what would become Rachel. Seeing this miracle, the nomads hailed her as Goddess Freyja's messenger. The Freyja faith rapidly expanded, welcoming a surge of new followers. While the clergy enjoyed special privileges, the nomadic tribes still had their place in the system.",
    ["Dialogue1153003"]="... Pope Isumia was known for her kindness. She worked tirelessly to bridge the gap between the nomads and the clergy. But it didn't last. After Isumia's death, her policies were slowly abandoned. To gain power, the priests struck deals with the wealthy elite, offering privileges to nobles in return for wealth. In the end, the nomads became the casualties of this system.",
    ["Dialogue1153004"]="That's right, Adventurer. It's not fair—because these nomadic tribes were the first inhabitants of this land. But look at them now—stripped of even the simplest rights. They're barely allowed to eat and dress as they wish, and studying alchemy? That's exclusive to nobles and Priests.",
    ["Dialogue1153005"]="I teach what I can, hoping to give these children something, no matter how small. But in the end, it won't be enough—change must come through the system itself.",
    ["Dialogue1153006"]="(Noticing your hesitation, Israel smiles reassuringly.)\nDon't feel bad, Adventurer. I'm not asking you to decide right away. I'd rather you take the time to see things for yourself before choosing whether or not to stand with me—that's why I brought you to Grey Wolf Village.",
    ["Dialogue1153007"]="(After a brief moment of thought, he gives you a sly grin.)\nThat said... if you're unsure, why not help me with something simple?",
    ["Dialogue1153008"]="Aside from teaching the children, I'm also trying to find more books for them. But in Arunafeltz, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple regulates all publications</color>, meaning common people barely have access to them. I have a friend, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vanessa</color>, who works as a tutor in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Noble Estate west of Rachel</color>. She occasionally smuggles some books my way...",
    ["Dialogue1153009"]="How about you <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect the books</color> for me? Just head to the estate, and no matter what weird stuff Vanessa says or does—don't question it. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Simply follow her instructions</color>. If you succeed, the kids here will get another rare chance to expand their knowledge.",
    ["Dialogue1153101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>What's going on? This was supposed to be today...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1153102"]="Ah, there you are—the new temp worker, right? Took you long enough! Hurry up!\n(Her eyes brighten when she sees you, and before you can even open your mouth, she piles a heavy stack of books into your arms.)\nThese are fresh imports from <color=#CA2E0AFF>overseas</color>—let the young masters and misses pick their favorites!",
    ["Dialogue1153103"]="Enough talking, go!\n(With a firm grip on your shoulders, she turns you around and shoves you forward.)\nListen up! <color=#CA2E0AFF>If they don't take the books, bring them right back</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1153201"]="Ugh... why does Dad keep buying these? I've gone through these entry-level books so many times at school and in the library in Temple. They‘re too simple for me. You can take them back.",
    ["Dialogue1153202"]="(The girl places the brand-new books back into your arms.)\nTell Miss Vanessa too. She knows exactly where I am in my studies. If my dad insists on buying these beginner books, she doesn't need to bring them over anymore—just <color=#CA2E0AFF>do whatever she wants</color> with them.",
    ["Dialogue1153301"]="... Finished your work? Then head back. Your payment will be handled by the steward and processed through the guild. Don't hang around—just leave.\n(She waves dismissively, turning away, seemingly unaware of the books still in your hands.)",
    ["Dialogue1153302"]="Yeah, yeah, I got it! They took everything, didn't they? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Not a single book left</color>? They're thrilled and <color=#CA2E0AFF>want more next time</color>? I'll let the master know—just <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave</color> already!",
    ["Dialogue1153401"]="I appreciate it, Adventurer. This will help the children expand their knowledge even further.",
    ["Dialogue1153402"]="That's right, Adventurer. Even though they're the same age, those noble kids get way better education than Jeremy and the rest of the village. They can grab what we fight so hard to get off a library shelf without a second thought. It must be strange to you too, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue1153403"]="Here in Arunafeltz, that's just how things work.\n(Israel sighs deeply.)\nForget it. It won't change a thing... For now, let's focus on what we can actually do—getting these <color=#CA2E0AFF>books</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>kids</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1153501"]="Whoa, slow down! One at a time! <size=26>I can't read all these books at once, you know!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1153502"]="Woohoo! Fairy tales are the best! In those stories, a single matchstick can grant any wish—I want some of those matchsticks too!",
    ["Dialogue1153503"]="Tell me the story of Pope Isumia! Mom says she was the most amazing pope in history!",
    ["Dialogue1153504"]="Quiet down, everyone! I can't hear what sister Martistine is saying!",
    ["Dialogue1153601"]="I know my limits, so don't worry about me. But this time, you picked a fight with the Temple Guards and even hurt Musa. If you can't scrape together enough money, how are you planning to fix this? Bribing people, pulling favors—it all takes money.",
    ["Dialogue1153602"]="I'll deal with the money! I know people in the city, and at least out of respect for my mentor, they won't leave me hanging. No way am I letting you risk your life over this!",
    ["Dialogue1153603"]="Why are you here, outsider? This has nothing to do with you. Stay out of it—",
    ["Dialogue1153604"]="Actually, your timing is perfect, Adventurer. Could I ask you to go with Sartre for a bit?",
    ["Dialogue1153605"]="Hey, cut this out! Israel, are you sending this outsider as a human punching bag?",
    ["Dialogue1153606"]="Trust me, if the Adventurer gets serious, you won't even last a minute.\n(Israel pats your shoulder as if presenting a premium product to Sartre.)\nHere's the deal—take the Adventurer with you, and I'll take you where you want to go.",
    ["Dialogue1153607"]="... That's your word. Alright—outsider, <color=#CA2E0AFF>you're coming with me</color>!\n(Without fully understanding how, you've apparently just been signed away in a deal between them... like a bargaining chip.)",
    ["Dialogue1153701"]="Let me make one thing clear—I don't care what's the deal between you and Israel. To me, you're still an outsider I can't trust. From now on, keep your mouth shut and follow my lead. And don't make trouble.",
    ["Dialogue1153702"]="... Where? To make some money, obviously. Weren't you paying attention? You guys messed up Musa really badly, and now we need money to clean this up. And considering how broke this village is... it's not gonna be cheap.",
    ["Dialogue1153703"]="With these.\n(Sartre flexes his fist in front of you before nodding toward a nearby alley.)\nSee those guys standing there? That's our target.",
    ["Dialogue1153704"]="That's the entrance to the Underground Arena. In Rachel, there are only two places where you can get rich overnight—the casino, or here. Casinos are a gamble, but here...\n(Sartre cracks his knuckles, looking eager.)\nAs long as I've got fists, it's guaranteed profit. Enough talk, let's go!",
    ["Dialogue1153801"]="Hey, kid! Yeah, I'm talking to you—what are you staring at...? Oh! Well, if it isn't the great Sartre!",
    ["Dialogue1153802"]="(The gatekeeper sidles up, grinning eagerly as he rubs his hands.)\nOh, I caught your last fight! Absolute spectacle! Who's the unlucky guy today? I'm on your side for sure!",
    ["Dialogue1153803"]="... On my side? Heh, you mean your money's on me, huh?\n(With a dry laugh, the silver-haired young man palms the gatekeeper's face and pushes him away.)\nStop wasting my time—let me in.",
    ["Dialogue1153804"]="Of course, sir, right this way—ah, but before that, who are you fighting tonight?",
    ["Dialogue1153805"]="Do I really need to spell it out?\n(Sartre smirks, tapping the heavy pouch at the gatekeeper's waist.)\nWhoever pays the most, that's my guy!",
    ["Dialogue1153901"]="Ah, my dear customer! Betting or exchanging chips? The matches are about to start, so make your move quick!",
    ["Dialogue1153902"]="Neither. I'm here to fight.\n(Sartre knocks on the highest-ranked name on the board.)\nGet me your best fighter.",
    ["Dialogue1153903"]="Really now? Bold move. Taya—that name's been sitting pretty at the top for two months—no one's dared step up. Last time, some hotheaded punk thought he was unstoppable after a few wins, and well... let's just say Taya introduced his face to the wall—hard.",
    ["Dialogue1153904"]="(The bookie licks his lips, chuckling darkly.)\nOh, I was there, all right! By the time they scraped him off the wall, his skull looked like a melon sat by an elephant! Hahaha... that was hilarious...",
    ["Dialogue1153905"]="... Yeah, yeah, whatever. He's the biggest prize here, right?",
    ["Dialogue1153906"]="Tsk tsk, that won't do! Our fights are strictly one-on-one—no double-teaming. But...\n(He grins like a devil, voice dropping into a whisper.)\nWhat do you say about tonight's <color=#CA2E0AFF>special event</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1153907"]="Solo or team-up, your call. Your opponent will be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>special monster</color> picked by the boss. Win, and your prize doubles, but so does the risk. Let's just say the odds aren't in your favor—an 80% fatality rate, to be exact. If you're feeling lucky, just <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign here</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1153908"]="(The bookie smirks, pushing a contract in front of Sartre.)\nLife or death, the arena doesn't care. Make your choice, but hey... You seem a little desperate for money, don't you?",
    ["Dialogue1153909"]="Hah... drop the act, will ya?\n(Sartre smirks, scribbles down his name in one smooth motion, then shoots you a glance.)",
    ["Dialogue1154001"]="<size=26>What an incredible battle, both of you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1154002"]="I must admit, I underestimated you. Defeating those monsters without a scratch... truly impressive. My apologies for my earlier judgment. By the way, my boss was watching from the stands and was quite impressed. If you wouldn't mind, he'd like to have a word with both of you...",
    ["Dialogue1154003"]="Not interested. Just pay up. I have places to be.\n(Sartre crosses his arms, tapping the noticeboard with a finger.)\nWe agreed on double, remember?",
    ["Dialogue1154004"]="Look, our boss doesn't invite just anyone, so I'm being nice here. But if you keep turning us down...\n(The bookie tilts his head, and a group of bouncers close in.)\nLet's not make this messy, yeah?",
    ["Dialogue1154005"]="<size=26>Stop it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1154101"]="(A heavy money pouch hits the counter with a resounding thud. A masked figure steps up, blocking the bookie's path to you.)\nI'm taking them with me.",
    ["Dialogue1154102"]="Well, well... If it isn't Ma—Ahem... My lord, this makes things a little tricky. Our boss specifically asked for them, and now you're stepping in to take them off our hands? That's not exactly playing by the rules.",
    ["Dialogue1154103"]="Cut the crap. I know how this place works.\n(He taps the table, nudging the money pouch forward.)\nThis amount covers ten people. If your boss has a problem with that, he can take it up with me directly.",
    ["Dialogue1154104"]="(The bookie's face twists in displeasure, but he knows better than to push back. After a brief pause, he plasters on his usual smile.)\nOh, come now! If someone like you wants them, our boss would be honored to oblige. Here—this is their signed death waiver. It's all yours.",
    ["Dialogue1154105"]="... Hmph, good call.\n(The young man takes the death waiver, glancing at it briefly before <color=#CA2E0AFF>tearing it to shreds</color> in front of everyone.)\nThey're coming with me. Get your goons out of my way.",
    ["Dialogue1154106"]="Move... move it! You idiots, make way for the Lord!\n(The bookie snarls, and his men reluctantly retreat. The masked man guides you and Sartre past the crowd, exiting the Underground Arena...)",
    ["Dialogue1154201"]="Speaking with the stranger, you learn that this Underground Arena actually belongs to a certain noble (Yus, a part of Rekenber Corp's human experimentation). If you want to stay alive in Arunafeltz, you'd best avoid making enemies of them. Today, luck was on your side—he was here to smooth things over. Next time? No guarantees. When you demand his identity and his reasons for helping, the masked man merely chuckles and lifts his disguise.",
    ["Dialogue1154202"]="Are you both alright? If there's any need, I have a doctor at my residence. I can arrange for treatment—",
    ["Dialogue1154203"]="No, I must decline. Unexpected kindness is often a cause for concern. Moreover...\n(Sartre eyes the stranger warily.)\nIf you really meant to help, why keep your face hidden? What's your deal?",
    ["Dialogue1154204"]="Oh? But as far as I know, this isn't the first time you've benefitted from my help. Otherwise...\n(He chuckles, lifting his mask and meeting your gaze.)",
    ["Dialogue1154205"]="Why do you think Musa never came after you, even after you gave him that beating, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1154301"]="I'd say that makes us even for that dessert in Juno, don't you think?\n(Malam spins his mask in one hand, flashing you a smile.)",
    ["Dialogue1154302"]="Hmm... That's right. What I just spent could've bought me dozens of Cloud Soufflés. So technically, you're the one who owes me a big favor now—but since you're already in the Arunafeltz, I have no doubt you'll find a way to make it up to me.",
    ["Dialogue1154303"]="But tell me, why did you even enter the Underground Arena? As far as I know, that place is a haven for the desperate—no one wagers their life there unless they have no other choice.",
    ["Dialogue1154304"]="(He smirks as his gaze lingers on you and Sartre.)\nSomeone like you... Carl and Philodis wouldn't allow you to take risks unless it's something serious. So, what is it? Grey Wolf Village? Or maybe... you've gotten tangled up with the rebels, Captain Sartre?",
    ["Dialogue1154305"]="(In a blink, Sartre's hand tightens around Malam's throat, his strike missing you by mere inches.)\nKeep talking, lapdog of the nobles. See how I break your neck!",
    ["Dialogue1154306"]="Relax, Adventurer. If he was serious, my head would be rolling by now.\n(Even as his face flushes from lack of air, Malam's voice remains disturbingly calm.)",
    ["Dialogue1154307"]="Easy there, Captain Sartre. Otherwise... next time you pick a fight with the Temple Guards, who's gonna save your ass?",
    ["Dialogue1154308"]="Wait... you're Israel's noble friend?\n(Sartre loosens his grip, then suddenly lets out a strange laugh.)\nHah... Adventurer called you Malam? You've got to be kidding me.",
    ["Dialogue1154309"]="This has to be some kind of joke. Rossin's son... is helping us? Are you crazy, or are we?",
    ["Dialogue1154310"]="... Look, I'm not stupid. I know damn well who was pulling the strings. Of course, your people committed unforgivable crimes—but being used as pawns doesn't mean they get a free pass. However, this... you and I... we have common goals.",
    ["Dialogue1154311"]="(Malam reaches out to Sartre. At this moment, you are still unaware of the conviction he has forged for this very decision.)\nThe real enemy is the man at Torr Volcano. He threatens not just us but the entire Arunafeltz. If that means working together, then so be it.",
    ["Dialogue1154312"]="... Shut up, outsider.\n(Sartre cuts you off sharply. You can tell he's venting his frustration, but you have no idea why.)\nThis is not your business.",
    ["Dialogue1154313"]="(Standing tall, Sartre's voice carries the weight of resentment.)\nI've always been disgusted by the condescending attitude of you people. And why the hell should I trust you? Your people have been stepping on us for six hundred years while preaching about a false god.",
    ["Dialogue1154314"]="That question has the same answer as before. The past can never be erased—the blood spilled, the suffering endured, the sins yet to be repaid. But none of that changes this moment, nor does the battle we both must fight.",
    ["Dialogue1154315"]="(Seeing no response, Malam drops his hand and carries on.)\nYou've led your people from the brink of destruction to survival. That alone tells me you are not short-sighted. You may need time to consider it, but in the end, you will stand by my side, Captain Sartre.",
    ["Dialogue1154316"]="I won't force you to make a decision now... and that goes for you as well, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1154317"]="Yes. I know Israel has told you everything about the rebel. We grew up together as <color=#CA2E0AFF>close friends</color>, and since you once saved him, I owe you the same debt of gratitude. Take your time in Grey Wolf Village. See for yourself what we are fighting for... then make your choice.",
    ["Dialogue1154318"]="Come to the Gilded Rose whenever you've made up your mind. I'll be waiting... and expecting much from both of you.",
    ["Dialogue1154401"]="What took you so long?",
    ["Dialogue1154402"]="So, we ran into your friend, Israel. I never saw that coming... You mentioned your noble connections before, but you never said it was him...\n(Sartre clenches his fist, tension rising between them.)\nYou and him... what's the deal?",
    ["Dialogue1154403"]="... I've told you all there is to know about my past. Malam and I... were raised together. If fate had been kinder—if Uncle Rossin had survived that rebellion, if our mentor had never been banished for speaking out against Yus—then right now, we'd both be serving the Pope as Priests.",
    ["Dialogue1154404"]="Do you... regret it? You were meant to be a Priest, and now you fight alongside rebels.",
    ["Dialogue1154405"]="... That's nonsense, Sartre.",
    ["Dialogue1154406"]="There's much I regret. Not being there for Malam when he needed me most. Not realizing our mentor had lost himself on the Nameless Island. Holding onto blind faith, refusing to wake up until it was almost too late—",
    ["Dialogue1154407"]="(Israel grips Sartre's shoulder with conviction.)\nRegret? The one thing I don't regret is fighting alongside you. I still believe in the Goddess, but her love no longer means what I once thought it did.",
    ["Dialogue1154501"]="You've arrived at the right time, Adventurer. As we agreed, you'll stay in Grey Wolf Village for a few days until Malam returns, at this point, you'll meet the Pope together. This is also a chance for you to observe and connect with the people here... So, tell me, have you made your decision?",
    ["Dialogue1154502"]="Still undecided, are you?\n(Israel smiles gently and waves it off.)\nIt's all right, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1154503"]="Doubt is a part of growth—that's something my mentor always said. Once you find your answer, it means you've moved ahead. I'd rather you think it through carefully. I believe, like Malam does, that you'll make the right call.",
    ["Dialogue1154504"]="No rush, and don't feel pressured. If you need time... focus on your duties first. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dawn Moon Festival</color> is coming, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Malam</color> is already back in Rachel. Weren't you supposed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet the Pope</color> on behalf of Lord Carl and deliver his gift?",
    ["Dialogue1154505"]="Go ahead, Adventurer. But before you do—try to convince Martistine to <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave the robots here</color>. Technology is not exactly welcomed in Arunafeltz, and the Temple is considered absolutely sacred to the followers of Freyja...",
    ["Dialogue1154601"]="Huh? You want me to leave Farbauti and Laufey here?\n(After hearing your request, Martistine looks reluctantly at her robots.)\nWhy can't they come with us?",
    ["Dialogue1154602"]="I know, I know—they'll call Farbauti and Laufey heretical or whatever and get you and Mr. Big Beard into trouble! Well then... you better make sure they're safe! Not a single dent, or... or...\n(You already know how important these robots are to Martistine, before she even finishes talking.)",
    ["Dialogue1154603"]="Fine... you two stay here. Be good.\n(She hugs her robot by pressing her cheek on their belly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>I'll be back very soon</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1154701"]="Well then... are you ready to meet the Pope, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1154702"]="Alright then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me to the Temple now</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1154703"]="Hmm... no matter. There are still a few days before the Dawn Moon Festival. Take your time handling your business, and come find me afterward. I will be waiting at the trading company.",
    ["Dialogue1154704"]="Also, my mentor, Priest Neirun, will be joining the Pope to welcome the distinguished guests from the Republic. Don't worry—they're both very nice. Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass along Lord Carl's message faithfully</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1154801"]="It is an honor to meet you, Adventurer. I am Neirun, one of the Twelve Bishops in Arunafeltz. Today...\n(With a graceful turn, the Bishop unveils the solemn visage of the young Pope atop the sacred throne.)\nBy the word of the Pope, I stand here to greet the envoy from the distant Schwarzwald Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1154802"]="Please rise, both of you. Be at ease... Ahem! Lord Carl and I are bound by deep respect. His letters speak highly of your service to the Republic. Thus, I shall welcome you as a guest of the highest honor. Let Malam guide you through our Temple and into the heart of the Dawn Moon Festival, where you may witness the spirit of our land.",
    ["Dialogue1154803"]="Ah... so you carry the sacred gift Lord Carl prepared for the Goddess' birthday?\n(You may be imagining it, but a sparkle seems to light up in the Pope's heterochromatic eyes.)\nCome, let the gift be <color=#CA2E0AFF>offered</color>. Neirun, if you will—",
    ["Dialogue1154804"]="As you command, Your Holiness.\n(At the Pope's signal, the Priest steps forward, ready to receive the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> in your hands.)",
    ["Dialogue1154901"]="The offering from Lord Carl is now in our hands. When you return to Juno, do bear the Pope's gratitude and words of grace...",
    ["Dialogue1154902"]="Hey, hey! Neirun! What did Carl send?! Lemme see! Is it something I like—?!",
    ["Dialogue1154903"]="Ahem... AHEM! Please bear the Pope's gratitude and thank Lord Carl for his thoughtful concern for both the Pope and the Goddess.\n(With a stern expression, Neirun raises her voice to finish the statement, then mutters quietly.)\nYour Holiness, please mind your manner!",
    ["Dialogue1154904"]="Huh—what?!\nAhem... Adventurer... why do you laugh?",
    ["Dialogue1154905"]="... That must not be done. Lord Carl's offering must first be verified and stored within the royal vaults. Even her Holiness should not open it before the public eyes—it would be improper.\n(She bows slightly.)\nThank you, Adventurer, for your understanding of the young Pope's slight misconduct. Your kindness is appreciated.",
    ["Dialogue1154906"]="Since Neirun said so, then I shall... uh... ah... I-I...\n(As she speaks, the young Pope rubs her eyes, clearly growing drowsy.)",
    ["Dialogue1154907"]="S-Sorry, Neirun... I think I'm...",
    ["Dialogue1154908"]="Worry not, Your Holiness. Rest, for I shall keep watch.\n(The Priest steps forward, cradling the Pope as she surrenders to sleep upon Neirun's shoulder.)",
    ["Dialogue1154909"]="My apologies, both of you. This came unexpectedly—I must excuse myself to escort the Pope back to her bedroom. The rest... Malam, I leave it to your <color=#CA2E0AFF>full discretion</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1154910"]="As you command, mentor.",
    ["Dialogue1155001"]="(Once Neirun's gone, Malam pats your shoulder.)\nSorry about that, Adventurer. The Pope wasn't trying to be rude. She's just been dealing with this condition forever, and we've never found a cure.",
    ["Dialogue1155002"]="From time immemorial, the one crowned as Pope is seen as Goddess Freyja's <color=#CA2E0AFF>earthly vessel</color>. Each communicates with the Goddess in different ways—through prayer, meditation, or simple rites. But the current Pope is different... Perhaps due to her youth, she falls into <color=#CA2E0AFF>sudden slumber</color> whenever receiving the Goddess' Oracle.",
    ["Dialogue1155003"]="Nobody knows what she'll do or say when she has one of her sleep episodes. For her safety, she must be watched at all times to prevent danger or accidents. Occasionally, she even speaks unconscious utterances that appear to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>prophetic</color> in nature.",
    ["Dialogue1155004"]="Huh? That totally sounds like sleepwalking! Wait—so that kid can see the future in her sleep?\n(Martistine tilts her head, looking super curious.)\nCan she do a reading for me too?",
    ["Dialogue1155005"]="The will of the Goddess is unfathomable and must not be forced. But if fate allows... it shall find you unbidden, like a prophecy <color=#CA2E0AFF>woven into your destiny</color>.\n(Strangely, though it seems to answer Martistine, you feel he's speaking to you.)",
    ["Dialogue1155006"]="Alright, now that the meeting's over, <color=#CA2E0AFF>feel free to look around</color>! Just avoid the western room connected to the garden. If you're tired, I've arranged a place for you to rest—just come find me in the archives on the northwest side of the Temple.",
    ["Dialogue1155007"]="Forget me. I wanna look around on my own—this place is seriously fancy! I'll come back once I'm done sightseeing!\n(She waves and darts off running. You and Malam can only shake your heads.)",
    ["Dialogue1155008"]="Alright, I'll leave you to it. Enjoy yourself, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1155101"]="(After parting ways with Malam, you stroll through the Temple. Not far off, a small figure catches your eye.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Within three days... Western Plains... Sleeping Potion...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1155102"]="First... the <color=#CA2E0AFF>catalyst to the gate of dreams</color>...\n(The young Pope does not respond to your calls and instead mutters cryptic words, dashing toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple Hall</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue1155201"]="Present <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gremlin Tear</color> and all you seek—all you long for—shall be revealed to your eyes...",
    ["Dialogue1155202"]="(You try to speak with the Pope, but she remains dazed, her eyes fixed on a <color=#CA2E0AFF>room at the corner</color>, repeating the same words.)\nPresent Gremlin Tear and all you seek—all you long for—shall be revealed to your eyes...",
    ["Dialogue1155301"]="Indeed, this is it. With this, your wish... may be fulfilled...",
    ["Dialogue1155302"]="Yet to walk the realm of dreams, one must sever soul from flesh... and only with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hazy Herb</color> can this be done...",
    ["Dialogue1155303"]="Please... <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1155401"]="This bloom awakens only once at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>new moon</color>... its fragrance is <color=#CA2E0AFF>heady</color>—lulling the flesh to slumber, freeing the soul to soar...\n(The Pope lifts her hand, pointing toward somewhere in the garden.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Please bring it forth</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1155501"]="(As she sees the herb you bear, a serene smile—far too old for her youthful face—graces her lips.)\nWith these offerings... <color=#CA2E0AFF>three days</color> hence, in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>western</color> plains... your wish shall be granted.",
    ["Dialogue1155502"]="Fret not... Remember my words this day, and guard these items well. When the time comes...",
    ["Dialogue1155503"]="What is going on?! I told you to keep a close watch over Her Holiness! I leave for a moment, and you lose track of her?!\nTch... Go check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>garden</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1155504"]="(The Pope's words are interrupted by Neirun's voice. Her eyes glaze over, empty and distant, as she slowly collapses into your arms.)\n... It seems... this is the end for now... I shall await... the day we <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet again</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1155505"]="<size=26>Your Holiness?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1155601"]="(Seeing the pope unconscious in your arms, Neirun cannot hide her shock.)\nWhat on earth happened here, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1155602"]="... You're saying Her Holiness led you to obtain Gremlin Tear and the Hazy Herb growing in this garden? As I understand, these are ingredients for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sleeping potion</color>...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could it be that Her Holiness knows something?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1155603"]="No... What I meant is I apologize for the trouble, Adventurer.\n(Neirun bows slightly and gently takes the unconscious Pope from your arms.)\nI wonder if Malam has already informed you—Her Holiness suffers from a severe case of narcolepsy.",
    ["Dialogue1155604"]="Then surely, you can understand... The Pope's actions are not of her own will but an <color=#CA2E0AFF>oracle</color> delivered through her by Goddess Freyja.\n(She lowers her head, eyes drifting to the two items in your hands.)\nSince it is the Goddess' will—please <color=#CA2E0AFF>accept</color> them.",
    ["Dialogue1155605"]="Don't worry. If you're not sure what to do with them, just <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Malam</color>. I believe the Goddess is on our side.",
    ["Dialogue1155701"]="... So the Pope told you to get these while she was half-asleep?\n(Malam glances at the items and gives a knowing smile.)\nLooks like this is the sign you've been waiting for, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1155702"]="No need to worry. Didn't the Pope say—three days hence, to the west of the plains? Then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep these items safe</color>. When the time is right... their purpose shall become clear.",
    ["Dialogue1155801"]="... You seem unfamiliar, young Adventurer. Outsiders are barred in the Temple—unless...\n(The elder standing before the statue turns around, looking at you.)\nYou are the envoy from the Schwarzwald Republic, yes?",
    ["Dialogue1155802"]="I am no one of note—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Jude</color> is my name. Adventurer, your tale reaches even my ears... Truth be told, I've had many doubts of late, questions I cannot answer alone. Might I ask your thoughts?",
    ["Dialogue1155901"]="... I see... this is your answer. It seems... my resolve pales compared to that of one so young yet so unwavering.",
    ["Dialogue1155902"]="Hoho... Eyes keen as a falcon's. And yet, a mere stripling dares to peer into the soul of one who is halfway into the grave?",
    ["Dialogue1155903"]="To bear a heart of kindness is a noble gift. Yet beware... for unguarded trust often returns as fangs upon your throat.",
    ["Dialogue1155904"]="... You mean, in all your travels, you've received help from many and now wish to return that kindness to others in future journeys?\n(The elder chuckles, stroking his beard.)\nWell said, well said! If it's you, then...",
    ["Dialogue1155905"]="Come with me, Adventurer. There is something I wish to show you.",
    ["Dialogue1156001"]="(The elder stands before a shelf, retrieving an aged yet well-preserved <color=#CA2E0AFF>book</color>, placing it gently in your hands.)\nThe tale of the Arunafeltz may lack the age of kingdoms past, yet for six centuries, it has endured upon this soil. We hold dear our ways, our rites, and our creed... Would you care to <color=#CA2E0AFF>learn more</color>, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1156002"]="Then... you are <color=#CA2E0AFF>free to browse</color> all the books in this room—please, go ahead.",
    ["Dialogue1156101"]="Well, Adventurer? You seem... quite puzzled.",
    ["Dialogue1156102"]="You're confused as to why accounts of the same person and the same event differ so drastically between books, aren't you?\n(The elder smiles gently as if he expected your reaction. He then retrieves a <color=#CA2E0AFF>yellowed notebook</color> from the corner of the shelf and hands it to you.)\nThen... perhaps take a look at this?",
    ["Dialogue1156201"]="(As you close the final page, Jude gently takes the notebook from your hands.)\n... You've finished reading, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1156202"]="No name marks its pages, and the thoughts within lie scattered. I know not whose hand penned these words, and yet...\n(His withered hands drift over the cover, his eyes swirling with turmoil and doubt.)\n... It had shaken my faith and caused the pillars of my belief to tremble.",
    ["Dialogue1156203"]="If one day, you too discover that Odin's Blessing was nothing more than a <color=#CA2E0AFF>lie</color>—he never watched over you... what would you do?\n(The elder raises his head—his clouded, ancient eyes cut through you like a cold wind.)\nAnd the <color=#CA2E0AFF>common folk</color>—those who believe in you, who believe in Odin—what becomes of them?",
    ["Dialogue1156204"]="(Amidst the weighty silence, a voice calls from the threshold of the archives, shattering the stillness.)\n—Master Jude, it is time. You're expected to give the lecture to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pope</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1156205"]="Oh—aren't you the envoy from Schwarzwald Republic? Apologies for interrupting your conversation with Master Jude. However...\n(The Temple servant bows deeply.)\nHer Holiness is already awaiting you, Master Jude.",
    ["Dialogue1156206"]="Hohoho... Though I no longer involve myself in worldly matters, as one of the Twelve Bishops, it is still my duty to guide the young Pope...\n(And so, the sharp glint in his gaze fades, revealing the kind elder you first beheld once more.)",
    ["Dialogue1156207"]="Then... let us leave today's conversation for <color=#CA2E0AFF>another time</color>. It's been a pleasure speaking with you, Adventurer. If the chance arises, feel free to visit me at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priest Estate</color> east of Rachel—I shall await your presence with open doors.",
    ["Dialogue1156301"]="Hey, hey, over there! See it? Looks like there's a secret path at the end of the garden!\n(The girl tugs at your arm, clearly excited.)\nLet's go check it out!",
    ["Dialogue1156302"]="Come on, what's the big deal? Those Priests treat you like royalty! Even if we see something we're not supposed to, they won't mess with you—your big-bearded buddy's got your back!",
    ["Dialogue1156303"]="You all talk like that all the time! Of course I picked it up! Quit stalling—let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak over real quick</color> before someone sees us!",
    ["Dialogue1156401"]="<size=26>Stop it!<size=18>",
    ["Dialogue1156402"]="Officer Musa, this individual is a distinguished guest from Schwarzwald Republic! How could you lay a hand on them?!",
    ["Dialogue1156403"]="Distinguished guest? Hah... Priest Neirun, open your eyes. This \"guest\" broke the Goddess statue first! I'm just doing my job as a Temple Guard—punishing the one who defiled our Goddess!",
    ["Dialogue1156404"]="Broke the statue?\n(Neirun looks up in confusion, then gasps in horror upon seeing the damage.)\nG-Goddess, forgive us...! What... what happened?!",
    ["Dialogue1156405"]="Humph, then perhaps you should ask your so-called guest.\n(Musa shoots you a sharp glare—if not for Malam and Neirun's presence, he might have already thrown a punch.)",
    ["Dialogue1156406"]="What?! You're saying you merely touched it, and the statue just broke on its own?! <size=26>Do I look stupid to you?!</size>\nYou do know that defiling the Goddess gets you <color=#CA2E0AFF>burned alive</color> according to the law of Arunafeltz, right?!",
    ["Dialogue1156407"]="<size=26>No!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1156408"]="This Adventurer is a representative of the Schwarzwald Republic! He came bearing gifts on behalf of Lord Carl—how can we accuse him of a crime?! <size=26>Would that not be <color=#CA2E0AFF>declaring war</color> on the Republic?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1156409"]="Oh? So, Priest Neirun, you're protecting someone who defiled the Goddess? Fine then, I'll take this straight to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Yus</color> and see what he says—",
    ["Dialogue1156410"]="... Officer Musa, matters concerning the Goddess—should they not be judged by the Pope first? Unless, of course...\n(Malam stares at Musa, a hint of challenge in his tone)\nYou believe that Priest Yus outranks the Pope?",
    ["Dialogue1156411"]="<size=26>H-How dare you! This is outrageous!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1156412"]="Please do not misunderstand me, Officer Musa. What I meant was... surely matters concerning the Goddess should be decided by Her will, should they not?",
    ["Dialogue1156413"]="Malam, are you...!",
    ["Dialogue1156414"]="Yes—please allow them to undergo the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess' Trial</color>. As the one who brought them before the Pope, I, too, must bear the blame...\n(Malam steps forward, standing at your side)\nSo, I shall <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany both of them</color> into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1156415"]="<size=26>I oppose it!</size>\nYou know full well what kind of place that is. None who have entered the Ice Cave <color=#CA2E0AFF>have ever returned</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1156416"]="But those souls were sinners, were they not? I believe the Adventurer is innocent. Surely, the Goddess will <color=#CA2E0AFF>grant them protection</color> and not let an innocent soul die in vain... Don't you agree, Officer Musa?",
    ["Dialogue1156417"]="—I'm all for Lord Malam's idea!\n(Musa claps loudly, smug and loud with laughter.)\nI mean, since you think they're innocent—you wouldn't say no now, yes?",
    ["Dialogue1156418"]="I...\n(Neirun scans the room, seeing clearly the intent behind every gaze. Her fists clench—but ultimately, she yields to Malam's pleading eyes)\nI... have no objections either.",
    ["Dialogue1156419"]="Alright, that settles it! <size=26>Someone—<color=#CA2E0AFF>cover their eyes</color> and take them to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1156501"]="Are either of you injured? The guards can be rather rough... If so, I have some medicine with me that you may use...",
    ["Dialogue1156502"]="I didn't get hurt or anything... but those guards were super rough! My wrist's all bruised now...\n(She puffed her cheeks in frustration, still looking shaken.)\nI seriously didn't expect that <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue to just break</color>! What the heck was that?",
    ["Dialogue1156503"]="... You heard someone calling to you? Odin... <color=#CA2E0AFF>She</color> called you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1156504"]="(Hearing your explanation, surprise flashes in Malam's eyes)\n... So you are... the Successor of Odin's bloodline?",
    ["Dialogue1156505"]="No... this actually makes sense now. Perhaps it was your bloodline that allowed the Goddess to bestow her revelation upon you... What did she say, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1156506"]="The voice you heard wasn't a woman's... but that of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young boy</color>?\n(This time, Malam's expression falters)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That... that can't be...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1156507"]="Hey, hey, stop talking in riddles! I can't understand a word! Where even are we?! It's so cold I'm gonna freeze!\n(Martistine stomps her foot and rubs her arms.)\nAnd like, do you hear those creepy sounds over there...?",
    ["Dialogue1156508"]="This is a cave located on the outskirts of Rachel, shrouded eternally in biting cold. It is said that the first Pope, Isumia, once tamed a Ktullanux here. During her reign, this creature served as her most powerful ally, aiding her through countless crises. Followers of Freyja revere Ktullanux as a sacred beast, believing that only those with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>profound bond</color> to the Goddess can command it.",
    ["Dialogue1156509"]="Unfortunately, after Pope Isumia's death, Ktullanux retreated to the depths of the cave, appearing only briefly during succession rites. In the past two centuries, however, it has not been seen at all. Some speculate that the divine power of newer Popes grows increasingly weak, which may be why Ktullanux no longer chooses to appear.",
    ["Dialogue1156510"]="With such a sacred legacy entwined, the Ice Cave is deemed forbidden by the Temple of Freyja, and trespassing is strictly prohibited. Aside from a single entry during the papal succession, access is granted only in cases where Arunafeltz law is unable to render judgment. The cave is a perilous maze, overrun with beasts and twisted paths—few mortals emerge unscathed... If one manages to survive and exit this cave, it proves that...",
    ["Dialogue1156511"]="Ohhh, I get it now! So that's why you told that mustache guy we'd take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess' Trial</color>! If we find the exit, he can't hold the broken statue against us!",
    ["Dialogue1156512"]="You're absolutely right, young lady. However... I must admit, I have my own motives. There's something I need in the Ice Cave, and I couldn't enter it by conventional means.",
    ["Dialogue1156513"]="That... I must ask to keep to myself for now. Let us continue searching for an exit while exploring the area. But rest assured—your safety will always be my top priority.\n(Malam bows slightly; his sincerity makes it hard to say no.)",
    ["Dialogue1156601"]="Blood splatters... sword gashes... and bones long untouched...\n(Malam gently traces the frozen ground, his face shadowed by thought—or mourning.)\nThese signs are clearly aged. Perhaps... remnants of the battle from fifteen years ago.",
    ["Dialogue1156602"]="... Let us <color=#CA2E0AFF>press on</color>, Adventurer. There may yet be more clues hidden in the depths of this cave.",
    ["Dialogue1156701"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Father...</color></size>\n(Malam clenches the wooden trinket, head bowed to hide his face. After a pause, he looks up again.)\nThank you, Adventurer. I could never mistake this—it belonged to my father.",
    ["Dialogue1156702"]="I think what I'm looking for should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>close</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1156801"]="Hey, look—this a letter? There's writing on it!\n(Martistine crouches and tugs hard, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>parchment</color> won't move.)\nArgh... why won't it come off?!",
    ["Dialogue1156901"]="(Malam kneels before the two entwined skeletons, pressing his forehead to the icy floor.)\nFather... Mother... at last, I've <color=#CA2E0AFF>found you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1156902"]="Wait—what?! These are your parents?!\n(The young girl stumbles back in fear, grabbing your sleeve.)\nWhat... what happened to them? Why here?",
    ["Dialogue1156903"]="Fifteen years ago... my father, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rossin</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>died</color> here in this Ice Cave while leading the Temple Guards to suppress a rebellion by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>nomads</color>. My mother, stricken with grief, entered these very depths and vanished. Her sister—Priest Neirun—took me in and raised me as her successor. And the one behind it all—",
    ["Dialogue1156904"]="(With trembling fists and a burning rage you've never seen before, Malam glares into the void.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Yus Amar</color>... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chief among the Twelve Bishops</color>, who now holds absolute power over both the <color=#CA2E0AFF>military and politics</color> of Arunafeltz!",
    ["Dialogue1156905"]="Indeed, we spoke of this before. Sartre's tribe was <color=#CA2E0AFF>manipulated</color> by Yus fifteen years ago—incited into rebellion against Arunafeltz and driven to trespass upon the forbidden grounds. My father, bound by duty, entered the Ice Cave in pursuit. In the end, only one wounded soldier returned to Rachel, claiming <color=#CA2E0AFF>everyone died</color> down there. Back then, Sartre was just a kid like me—barely ten years old...",
    ["Dialogue1156906"]="I won't lie—I do still hold a grudge. But really, the nomads were just used. I know full well that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yus is the true culprit behind it all</color>. If Yus can be brought to justice for his sins, then... I am willing to make peace with the nomads.",
    ["Dialogue1156907"]="(At the mention of his friend, Malam's expression softens at last.)\nYes. This is what Israel and I have been planning in secret. That rebellion from fifteen years back gave Yus total control of the army. I've been running the trading company on my mentor's orders ever since, trying to build up resources...",
    ["Dialogue1156908"]="But right now, we're not strong enough to go up against Yus. He has allied with <color=#CA2E0AFF>foreign powers</color>, depleted the treasury, mass-produced weapons... and handed command of the Temple Guard entirely to his lackey, Musa.",
    ["Dialogue1156909"]="(Malam nodded, smiling with relief.)\nYou are not only strong but wise, Adventurer. Your assistance... truly feels like the goddess' blessing.",
    ["Dialogue1156910"]="It's alright. I understand this isn't the time for such discussions. Now that I've bid my parents farewell...\n(He breathes deeply and stands, the weight of fate that once clung to him finally lifting)\n... I can now move forward, unburdened, to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill what I must</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1156911"]="No... They've found their rest. They need not be disturbed by the chaos of the world again.\n(Malam bends down, hugging the remains one last time.)\nFarewell... Father, Mother.",
    ["Dialogue1157001"]="... Don't you find it strange, Adventurer? Why are there <color=#CA2E0AFF>signs of a camp</color> this deep in the Ice Cave?\n(Malam gazes at the abyss, eyes full of doubt and dread)\nWhat is it? Where does it lead? I've never heard of such a place in the depths of this cave...",
    ["Dialogue1157002"]="You feel it... don't you? The divine power resonance, faint yet clear...?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Odin's might... the Goddess' call...?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1157003"]="Come on, you guys sure like to talk things to death—just <color=#CA2E0AFF>go look</color> if you're that curious!",
    ["Dialogue1157004"]="... Right. If retreat is not an option, then we must move forward, even through danger.\n(Malam laughs heartily, ruffling Martistine's hair, much to her protest.)\nCome on, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head down</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1157101"]="They built all this in a place that's supposed to be totally off-limits...\n(Malam glances up the staircase you came from—now completely hidden.)\nWhoever's behind this has serious influence. But what really matters is...",
    ["Dialogue1157102"]="Yes, why would anyone come all the way down here? It's crawling with dangerous monsters and is considered sacred ground by the Freyja. If caught, the consequences would be dire.",
    ["Dialogue1157103"]="(Hearing your words, Malam grins in agreement.)\nExactly. We must <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep going</color>. Come, both of you!",
    ["Dialogue1157201"]="... Something feels off, Adventurer. Don't you notice? This place feels makeshift compared to the last camp. Like, they weren't living here on purpose—it's like they were just <color=#CA2E0AFF>trying to survive</color> with what little they had.",
    ["Dialogue1157202"]="You're right. And those weird gadgets and machines... It's like some kind of <color=#CA2E0AFF>massive experimental site</color> or something.",
    ["Dialogue1157203"]="Okay, you guys are freaking me out! Are we seriously going forward? Shouldn't we just head back?",
    ["Dialogue1157204"]="No... we must press onward. Regardless of what dangers lie ahead, the paths within this Ice Cave are a labyrinth teeming with monsters. We were blindfolded when we got here, so we've got no clue where the entrance is. We've walked a long way already—heading back could be worse. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Going forward</color> might be our only hope.",
    ["Dialogue1157205"]="(Hearing your thought, Malam nods in agreement.)\nThat's right, Adventurer. All those supplies and machines mean someone's <color=#CA2E0AFF>coming in and out</color> of here. Doesn't matter if they're good or bad—as long as there's someone, there's gotta be a way out.",
    ["Dialogue1157301"]="Are you both alright?\n(Malam checks over you and Martistine while keeping watch behind.)\nIt seems the monster didn't follow us... we should be safe for now.",
    ["Dialogue1157302"]="Wh-What was that thing?! Ugh... that freaks me out...",
    ["Dialogue1157303"]="Sorry, this was on me. I thought we were more than strong enough to take on anything in here. But I've never seen a monster like that... None of the records about this cave mention a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demi-Human Monster</color> so <color=#CA2E0AFF>massive</color>... and <color=#CA2E0AFF>completely white</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1157304"]="(Malam's thinking hard, then suddenly looks excited.)\nWait a sec—don't you think that thing looked kinda like the <color=#CA2E0AFF>special monster</color> in Rachel's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1157305"]="... I've got a few ideas, but nothing solid yet. Not gonna lie. I've been digging into that Underground Arena for a while now. Those masked Demi-Human Monsters are not only incredibly strong—they sometimes exhibit <color=#CA2E0AFF>behavior</color> that seems distinctly <color=#CA2E0AFF>human</color>, such as...",
    ["Dialogue1157306"]="(Malam rubs his chin—you've seen him do that whenever he's thinking hard.)\nI actually saw one of them with a spiked hammer... she avoided vital spots on purpose and pinned her opponent's limbs to the ground. That's not survival instinct—it looked like she <color=#CA2E0AFF>was enjoying the thrill of combat</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1157307"]="Yes. Rather than monsters, I believe they may, in fact, be human—humans with desires and complex emotions.",
    ["Dialogue1157308"]="Raaah—!\n(Malam's words leave you in silence—until a sharp roar brings your focus back to the small creature that just helped you escape danger.)",
    ["Dialogue1157309"]="We got so caught up talking, I almost forgot about it. Thank you for saving us—though I've nothing to offer you at the moment—\n(Halfway through his words, Malam suddenly lets out a small gasp.)\nWait... those spiny, frost-like scales... could it be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ktullanux</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1157310"]="Huh?! You mean this tiny thing is the Ktullanux that helped the first Pope achieve greatness?!\n(Martistine peers down at it—it barely reaches her knees.)\nIt's so... small...",
    ["Dialogue1157311"]="Yeah, it's way smaller than what the books said... looks more like a baby dragon or something. But still, these traits—hey! What—what are you doing?!\n(Before Malam can finish, the small creature tugs at his coat with its teeth, seemingly trying to <color=#CA2E0AFF>lead you all somewhere</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1157401"]="No... It couldn't have vanished into thin air. There must be... a hidden passage we've overlooked...\n(Malam scans the massive stone wall, his gaze sharp as a hawk's)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>There</color>, Adventurer! <color=#CA2E0AFF>On the ice</color>—there's a patch of <color=#CA2E0AFF>black shadow</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1157501"]="Just as I suspected... It seems this is what the Ktullanux hatchling was trying to show us.",
    ["Dialogue1157502"]="(Malam nods.)\nI believe... if it had intended to harm us, it wouldn't have stepped in to save us earlier. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1157601"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>So it's true... There really is a secret passage from the Ice Cave to the Temple...</color></size>\n(Malam mutters, staring at the path you all just crawled out of.)",
    ["Dialogue1157602"]="My apologies for not informing you sooner. Honestly, I only had bits and pieces about the Ice Cave without solid proof... Fortunately, we've now made it out safely. This is the Temple's <color=#CA2E0AFF>basement</color>, and I'm pretty sure it has been abandoned for <color=#CA2E0AFF>decades</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1157603"]="Yeah... I've been wondering too. Why does that passage lead here? And who set up that huge camp and experimental site inside the Ice Cave...\n(Malam crouches, carefully examining the corners of the wall, his expression growing grim)\nAdventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at this</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1157701"]="There's no dust buildup around the corners. The passage fits tightly against the wall, with no signs of wear from <color=#CA2E0AFF>repeated entering and exiting</color>—someone clearly keeps it well-maintained...",
    ["Dialogue1157702"]="Exactly. This place has been unused for years, and the stairway leading here is guarded. If people had been coming and going often, word would've gotten out...\n(Malam gets up, brushing off his clothes)\nThere must be going on in this basement—let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a look around</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1157801"]="(A surge of magic erupts from Malam's staff, and the monsters fall instantly. He lets out a long breath and looks your way, a bit uneasy.)\nAdventurer, did you notice? These roaming monsters...",
    ["Dialogue1157802"]="Yes, I was there that day, watching you and Sartre fight in the Underground Arena. These monsters are just like the ones you fought—same look, same way of attacking. It's like <color=#CA2E0AFF>copy and paste</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1157803"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Temple... Ice Cave... Underground Arena... there must be a connection between them.</color></size>\n(Malam strokes his chin, then lifts his gaze toward a distant archway.)\nOver there... could that be <color=#CA2E0AFF>another room</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1157901"]="Ugh, I'm starving after all this walking. Hey, blondie! Isn't this a Temple? Don't tell me there's nothing to eat here!",
    ["Dialogue1157902"]="(Faced with Martistine's question, Malam offers a wry smile and shakes his head.)\nI'm afraid not. This place once stored food and drink, but nothing has been maintained since it was abandoned over a decade ago. Anything left is probably way past edible.",
    ["Dialogue1157903"]="Whatever! We won't know if it's edible until we look! I'm checking that side—you guys don't just stand there; help me search!\n(And off she goes, running straight for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shelves deeper in the cellar</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue1158001"]="Don't... don't worry about me! I'm fine!\n(Now that you've driven off the monsters, Martistine quickly regains her composure and points to the nearby disordered crates.)\nQuick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at these crates</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1158101"]="These armaments are exactly the same as the ones I saw back in the arsenal at Torr Volcano.",
    ["Dialogue1158102"]="Adventurer, do you recall the time I was absent from Rachel? At that time... I made a detour to Torr Volcano. Yus has an arsenal there. I staged an assault to stir things up, hoping my people could infiltrate or uncover incriminating evidence. The warehouse there was filled with weapons—identical to these.",
    ["Dialogue1158103"]="... Yes. My mentor and I both believe he intends to <color=#CA2E0AFF>start a war</color>. Yus is extremely radical and obsessed with Goddess Freyja in a way that makes no sense. For years, he's resented the <color=#CA2E0AFF>origin of Freyja</color> and refuses to acknowledge it came from a branch of Odin. That's why things have only gotten worse between the Kingdom and Arunafeltz.",
    ["Dialogue1158104"]="(Malam looks genuinely apologetic)\n... I heard things didn't go smoothly at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kingdom's succession ceremony</color>. I'm sorry—Yus may well have had a hand in that.",
    ["Dialogue1158105"]="But I assure you, neither my mentor nor the conservative faction—nor I—have ever been part of his vile schemes. We haven't been able to stop him, but we're not siding with him either. Should we succeed in overthrowing Yus... my mentor and I will personally travel to the Kingdom to offer our apologies.",
    ["Dialogue1158106"]="... You're right, Adventurer. We have more pressing matters for now—this place isn't fully <color=#CA2E0AFF>explored</color> yet.",
    ["Dialogue1158201"]="Whoa... Your friend totally tricked me! Said machines weren't a thing in Arunafeltz and made me hide Farbauti and Laufey!\n(Martistine smacks you twice, clearly displeased.)\nLook at this—aren't these all <color=#CA2E0AFF>machines</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1158202"]="... No, Israel didn't lie to you. Arunafeltz isn't into heavy industry—it places its faith <color=#CA2E0AFF>in alchemy</color> alone. These machines... I've never seen them before, nor know why they're here. The only explanation... Adventurer, do you recall me saying that Yus was colluding with foreign powers? I'm sure you've heard the name—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp</color>, the most renowned tech company in the Republic.",
    ["Dialogue1158203"]="The arsenal at Torr Volcano was built with Rekenber Corp's assistance. I suppose everything here... is the result of their collusion.",
    ["Dialogue1158204"]="... I can't tell what these machines do, but maybe there are records left behind. Let's look around.\n(Malam didn't notice you suddenly going quiet—but deep down, you knew <color=#CA2E0AFF>your stance changed</color> the second you heard that name...)",
    ["Dialogue1158301"]="Adventurer... did you hear that? He...",
    ["Dialogue1158302"]="He... <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>he can talk</color>!</size>\n(Martistine cries out in disbelief before you can even respond.)\nWhat?! Since when do monsters talk?!",
    ["Dialogue1158303"]="You... you must think it's weird too, right? I've never seen a monster that could talk.. unless, unless...\n(The girl clutches your arm tightly. She doesn't dare finish her sentence—but you both already know the answer.)",
    ["Dialogue1158304"]="Don't panic. We must stay calm. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head in a bit deeper</color>... there might be <color=#CA2E0AFF>more leads</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158401"]="(The monster's still moaning on the ground after being defeated. Malam sighs, aiming at its chest.)\n... May the Goddess forgive you. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rest in peace</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158402"]="Ahh! You—!\n(The girl gasps and backs up. You quickly cover her eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue1158403"]="They... could never return to what they once were. To rest in the embrace of the Goddess—perhaps that is for the best.\n(He looks at the lifeless monster with sorrow.)\nLet's go. Over there... I think I see some <color=#CA2E0AFF>bookshelves</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158501"]="Experiment logs... experiment logs... They actually dared to conduct such unethical <color=#CA2E0AFF>human experiments</color> in the Temple...!\n(Malam clenches his fists, gritting his teeth.)\nYus... you're not worthy to serve the Goddess!",
    ["Dialogue1158502"]="... Right, the real question is—why were they researching this? From what we know, those monsters have physical abilities far beyond humans. If they're used in war...\n(You and Malam exchange a worried look.)",
    ["Dialogue1158503"]="I think we'd better hurry back to the temple and tell my mentor and the Pope what we found... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>; I remember a path to the upper level in the central chamber.",
    ["Dialogue1158601"]="(As you reach the end of the staircase, a slender figure blocks your path. She stands against the light, her expression unreadable.)\n... You even kept this from me, Malam. We'd heard rumors of a secret path to the forbidden grounds in the Temple's basement, but this reckless move—you could've died. If you hadn't come back, how could I ever face my sister?",
    ["Dialogue1158602"]="Sorry, mentor... I didn't mean to worry you again. But I wasn't just being reckless...\n(Malam pauses, his gaze falling on you)\nI held a card that could win it all.",
    ["Dialogue1158603"]="Yes, Adventurer. In truth, I'd already heard stories about you from Israel. Your presence gave me the courage to enter the perilous Ice Cave. And look—we made it out and found the key to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring down Yus</color>... You really are the chosen one.",
    ["Dialogue1158604"]="No worries. I'll explain everything. Mentor, Adventurer—I've got a plan.\n(Malam leans forward, a serious look on his face.)\nWe'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>reveal Yus' true face</color> in front of all the nobles and other Priests at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dawn Moon Festival</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1158605"]="<size=26>Malam! Are you crazy?!</size>\nDidn't we agree to play it slowly and cautiously? Yus controls everything right now—if we can't uproot him completely, he'll wipe us out!",
    ["Dialogue1158606"]="... Please, just hear me out. Yus isn't even in Rachel anymore—he went to Torr Volcano himself to deal with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>arsenal</color> assault. That was an unexpected stroke of luck. Our original plan was just to stir things up so our people could sneak in and look for evidence, right?",
    ["Dialogue1158607"]="But... even if Yus isn't in Rachel, Musa is. Don't forget—the Temple Guards are under his command, and we can't take him head-on. And those nobles and Priests? Hah, they'll side with whoever gives them the best odds. They won't risk themselves just because of our words.",
    ["Dialogue1158608"]="Well, that depends on whose word it is, doesn't it?\n(Malam sways his head proudly.)\nMentor, the three people standing before you have just passed the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess' Trial</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1158609"]="(Neirun freezes for a second, then nods in understanding.)\n... You've got a point. No one's made it out of the Ice Cave alive in almost a <color=#CA2E0AFF>hundred years</color>. If you three appear in public, and with the Pope's support, public opinion will turn in our favor... This plan will work.",
    ["Dialogue1158610"]="And that's not all—I have a third card to play—it's time to bring out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>decree</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158611"]="You plan to ally with the rebels now? Why? As far as I know, they were still stubborn. Otherwise, you wouldn't have risked going to the Republic to seek Lord Carl's aid.",
    ["Dialogue1158612"]="Yes. However, not long ago... I saw their <color=#CA2E0AFF>leader</color> in the Underground Arena.\n(Malam lowers his head, chuckling softly.)\nJust like my mother... <color=#CA2E0AFF>fierce in words, gentle in spirit</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158613"]="To him, it's all about <color=#CA2E0AFF>equality</color>. If his people can live like <color=#CA2E0AFF>everyone else</color>, he'll agree to just about anything... That's why we made that decree in the first place, right?",
    ["Dialogue1158614"]="Very well. I trust you. However... I will also take part in this negotiation.\n(Neirun adjusts her glasses and looks at you.)\nSo, Adventurer—are you our enemy... or our ally?",
    ["Dialogue1158615"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp</color>?\n(Malam looks surprised, then suddenly gets it.)\nSo that's it—that's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>real reason</color> Lord Carl sent you to Arunafeltz!",
    ["Dialogue1158616"]="(You hold out your hand. Malam laughs and shakes it.)\nI've no reason to say no. I'll fill you in on everything I know about Rekenber Corp.",
    ["Dialogue1158617"]="Alright then... now that we're on the same page, the next step is getting past all these Temple Guards and reaching Grey Wolf Village.\n(She thinks for a moment, then looks toward the end of the corridor—toward the Pope's bedroom.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Her Holiness for help</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158701"]="Neirun... Malam... and the two from...\n(The Pope lifts her chubby little hand, counting heads one by one.)\n Can I help with something?",
    ["Dialogue1158702"]="Forgive us, Your Holiness, for disturbing your rest. We mean no offense. And yet... we beg your help. Could you help by distracting the attendants and guards outside? Say this: The Goddess has spoken. On the day of the Dawn Moon Festival, calamity shall descend from the east. You must go to the Goddess Shrine and pray through the night—with every Priest and attendant by your side.",
    ["Dialogue1158703"]="Dawn Moon Festival... Calamity... Goddess Shrine... All by my side... Okay! I got it!\n(The Pope repeats the lines while counting them on her fingers, then gives her chubby cheeks a slap and puts on a serious face.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>I shall take my leave.</color>",
    ["Dialogue1158704"]="... Do not be surprised, Adventurer. The Pope is but a child—without guidance, how could she bear the dignity of a sovereign? Over the years, we've always handled meetings like this. Fortunately, she's clever—she remembers my words even if she doesn't fully understand them. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait here</color> for a while until the attendants and guards are gone, and then we will leave the Temple quietly.",
    ["Dialogue1158801"]="(Once the Pope has led the attendants away, the area outside the bedroom falls silent. Neirun stands at the door and gently pushes it open a crack.)\n... Good. They've all left.",
    ["Dialogue1158802"]="Follow me, everyone. We must leave the Temple quietly... and go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grey Wolf Village</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1158901"]="... Lord Malam, what brings such fire to your eyes? Is this about me turning you down last time?",
    ["Dialogue1158902"]="If that's how you want to put it, Captain Sartre... Since you won't work with us, I guess I'll just...\n(Malam notices Sartre's wariness and gives a sly little laugh.)\nOffer you a gift instead. Maybe that'll change your mind.",
    ["Dialogue1158903"]="A gift? Hah... What gift could the temple possibly offer to us <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"savage nomads\"</color>? Is your Goddess really gonna hand us back our land, our culture, our beliefs... and the respect we deserve?",
    ["Dialogue1158904"]="If that's what you truly wish for...\n(Neirun steps forward and hands over a scroll.)\nThen they are all here, Captain Sartre.",
    ["Dialogue1158905"]="N-Neirun?! <size=26>What brings you here?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1158906"]="... It's been a long time, Israel. Malam has told me everything. I‘m truly sorry about Hibram... But now's not the time for reminiscing. Once everything is over, I promise I'll do everything I can to clear your and Hibram's name. For now... let's have Captain Sartre <color=#CA2E0AFF>read this decree</color> himself. See if this gift is to his liking.",
    ["Dialogue1159001"]="... So, Captain Sartre? Is this what you wanted?\n(Neirun opens the decree fully so he can read it.)\nThe Pope's <color=#CA2E0AFF>seal</color> is already there. Once it goes public... it will become official law in Arunafeltz.",
    ["Dialogue1159002"]="(Israel steps forward and gently runs his hand over the seal on the decree.)\n... It's real, Sartre. I've seen the Pope's seal before—there's no doubt. With this... your people won't have to live under anyone's shadow again!",
    ["Dialogue1159003"]="That's right. We plan to have the Pope publicly read this decree <color=#CA2E0AFF>on the day of the Dawn Moon Festival</color>, using the Goddess' birthday as the perfect moment. With the Goddess' Oracle, those nobles won't dare oppose it. But... Musa still controls the Temple Guards. If we push him in front of everyone, he might act out of desperation. So before that happens... we ask you, Captain Sartre, to set aside our differences and help us restrain him.",
    ["Dialogue1159004"]="... So it seems this gift from Priest Neirun comes at a steep price. You said it yourself—Musa controls the Temple Guards. How could a village of the old, the weak, and women stand against trained blades? I won't let my people march to their deaths.",
    ["Dialogue1159005"]="Captain Sartre, let's be honest—at this point, there's no need to beat around the bush. I know you have a handful of dedicated fighters. Not many, but skilled. If you're willing to work with us, I promise... we can capture Musa without bloodshed. And after that...",
    ["Dialogue1159006"]="(Malam tosses the decree into the air—it lands perfectly in Sartre's hands.)\nYour people walk free. We seize the reins of change. This is a victory for us both.",
    ["Dialogue1159007"]="(Sartre stares at the decree. It's everything he's been fighting for... and it's shaking his resolve.)\n... Okay. I'm listening. <color=#CA2E0AFF>What's the plan</color>, Malam?",
    ["Dialogue1159101"]="Everyone, I believe you all know something about Yus. He's held both military and political power in Arunafeltz for decades with ruthless iron fists—there's no way he's clean. Musa, his right-hand man, can't possibly be innocent either. As far as I know, Yus relies on the weapon trade the most, and Musa entirely handles it.",
    ["Dialogue1159102"]="They cover it up as foreign trade, but they're draining the treasury and producing weapons. Yus provides the funding, and Rekenber Corp supplies the tech and transport. Every so often, Musa meets their shipments in Rachel. I've had people investigate their logistics... and the next delivery is <color=#CA2E0AFF>tonight</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1159103"]="(Malam gives a bitter smile and shakes his head.)\nNo, Adventurer... there are too many of them. A direct assault would be suicide. But do you recall... the two ingredients Her Holiness asked you to find the other day?",
    ["Dialogue1159104"]="To be honest... I was quite surprised myself. I've always known Her Holiness possessed the gift of prophecy, but witnessing it firsthand was still overwhelming. Perhaps the Goddess herself is enraged by Yus' actions and has sent a revelation to <color=#CA2E0AFF>punish his sins</color>. Now... please <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand them over</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1159201"]="As long as we seal the two ingredients in a closed container and process them through alchemy, we can produce a powerful <color=#CA2E0AFF>sleeping potion</color>. But since slipping it into their food might be tricky, I'll use heat to vaporize it and smash the container to spread it through the air. I plan to set two traps and <color=#CA2E0AFF>drop them from above</color> when they least expect it—",
    ["Dialogue1159202"]="That's right. Once they breathe it in, they'll be out cold for at least three hours—more than enough time for us to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather evidence</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>capture them alive</color>. Yet for the alchemical formula to function at heat, I'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>two feathers from Captain Hill Wind</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1159203"]="... Alright then. I'll work on the traps while you gather the materials. Be quick, Adventurer—we don't have much time.",
    ["Dialogue1159301"]="Excellent. Only one step remains...\n(Malam gives Martistine a serious pat on the shoulder.)\nLittle one, let me borrow your two robots.",
    ["Dialogue1159302"]="Wait—what?!<size=26>What are you up to now?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159303"]="(The blond young man raises his hand, revealing the cliffs surrounding Grey Wolf Village.)\nBeyond that cliff lies the Rekenber Corp's <color=#CA2E0AFF>airship station</color>. I want your robots to hide up there and drop our traps when they begin unloading cargo...",
    ["Dialogue1159304"]="The cliffs here are too steep for ordinary people to climb, so they didn't bother putting guards up there. That gives us an opportunity—your robots should be able to carry the traps up easily, right?",
    ["Dialogue1159305"]="You guys... Why is everyone so good at making me do stuff?! I never agreed to this—",
    ["Dialogue1159306"]="(Her eyes instantly sparkle, and she stops mid-complaint.)\n... You better not go back on that! Deal's a deal!",
    ["Dialogue1159401"]="... Alright, looks like they're all down. I'll tie them up and take them in—you check the crates, see if there's any <color=#CA2E0AFF>evidence we can use against them</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1159501"]="Once everything is done, Sartre says the rebels will detain everyone here. You’re now free to return to Grey Wolf Village and discuss the next steps.",
    ["Dialogue1159502"]="Ugh, what are these guys made of? So heavy...\n(When you return, Sartre's already got a few Temple Guards tied up and is hauling them onto a cart.)",
    ["Dialogue1159503"]="Nah, we got it. My people can handle the heavy lifting.\nWhat about you—did you find any proof? We gotta hurry before the next flight shows up.",
    ["Dialogue1159504"]="Alright, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back</color>. I'll have the crew <color=#CA2E0AFF>toss these lackeys in the village warehouse</color>. As for Musa...\n(Sartre gives the knocked-out guy a kick and cracks his knuckles.)\n... Mind if I rough him up a bit before you guys need him?",
    ["Dialogue1159601"]="(Neirun breathes out in relief the moment she sees you all return safely.)\n... Thank Goddess, none of you are hurt. My heart is at ease.",
    ["Dialogue1159602"]="With Musa and the Temple Guards under control, and evidence against Yus in hand, the last step is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>expose their crimes</color> during the Dawn Moon Festival and announce the decree... Mentor, is Her Holiness aware of these? She listens to you, yes, but she's still a child under ten... We can't pull this off without her.",
    ["Dialogue1159603"]="Don't worry. I've already explained the meaning of the decree to Her Holiness. She may be young, but she knows justice when she sees it. And with Jude's guidance these past few days, I will stand beside her during the ceremony—",
    ["Dialogue1159604"]="<size=26>Bishop Neirun! Bishop Neirun! Where are you?</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159701"]="Bishop Neirun! Finally... I found you...",
    ["Dialogue1159702"]="... What's the panic? Didn't I tell you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay by Her Holiness' side without leaving</color> until I returned? Why are you here?",
    ["Dialogue1159703"]="Bishop Neirun, you must return to the Temple right away!<size=26>Something's happened to Her Holiness!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159704"]="As you ordered, we remained in the Goddess Shrine by Her Holiness. But just before dawn, she suddenly collapsed in front of the statue and wouldn't wake up! Even her breathing has grown faint... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>come quickly and see for yourself</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1159705"]="<size=26>What?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159801"]="<size=26>I don't believe it!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159802"]="Until now, Her Holiness has often delivered the goddess's will in her sleep many times, and she usually wakes up within minutes! Why is this time different?! I'll interrogate the attendants again—they must tell me everything that happened during her meditation!",
    ["Dialogue1159803"]="Neirun... I've shared every detail of that moment with you. Are you saying you don't believe me now?",
    ["Dialogue1159804"]="Lord Jude, I don't mean to doubt you. But this concerns the Pope's life—are we just supposed to give up?!",
    ["Dialogue1159805"]="... And <color=#CA2E0AFF>what if this is the Goddess' will</color>? Her Holiness, born of divine purpose, came to light our path. Perhaps now... the Goddess simply calls her home. Would you dare oppose the will of the divine?",
    ["Dialogue1159806"]="What?! You mean—<size=26>we're just gonna let her die in her sleep?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1159807"]="... Of course, Adventurer. The doctor was summoned right away but found no signs of illness—he said Her Holiness was merely sleeping. Yet no call stirs her. Her breath grows faint... as if her light is fading from this world. How... how am I supposed to accept this?!",
    ["Dialogue1159808"]="(Hearing your question, the elder sighs deeply at your question.)\n... If you doubt me still... then allow me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>recount it once more</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1159901"]="... Earlier tonight, before resting, my attendant informed me that Her Holiness had received a revelation from the Goddess—that calamity would descend from the east within three days. She wished to meditate through the night, and all Priests and attendants were to accompany her. I dressed quickly and hurried to the Temple. At that time...",
    ["Dialogue1159902"]="(A slight hesitation breaks his voice—he glances toward Neirun, then continues.)\nHer Holiness knelt in prayer before the statue while others quietly attended her. There was <color=#CA2E0AFF>no sign—no warning</color>. But as the first light crept over the horizon... she collapsed.",
    ["Dialogue1159903"]="We hurried to her side—she appeared only to be sleeping. It had happened before, so I thought... she was just fatigued. But this time... she did not wake.",
    ["Dialogue1159904"]="... Then before Her Holiness fell asleep, was there nothing unusual? Or earlier—did she <color=#CA2E0AFF>eat something</color>, or <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet someone</color>?\n(Malam fires off his questions rapidly, glancing around the Pope's bedroom, eyes sharp.)\nMentor, may we investigate Her Holiness' room?",
    ["Dialogue1159905"]="... Yes. The situation is dire—etiquette means little now. Malam, Adventurer—<color=#CA2E0AFF>search as you will</color>. Whatever the consequences, I shall bear them.",
    ["Dialogue1160001"]="... What is it, Adventurer? Why do you look so dazed all of a sudden?\n(Neirun glances at the sleeping Pope, then back at you.)\nIs there... something wrong with Her Holiness' body?",
    ["Dialogue1160002"]="Someone's calling you? Could it be... Goddess Freyja?!",
    ["Dialogue1160003"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A boy's voice...? It was a boy? Wait, no way—</color></size>\n(Neirun suddenly looks at Jude in horror.)\nLord Jude, could it be...?!",
    ["Dialogue1160004"]="This... this is impossible! He was supposed to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>dead—long ago!</color>\n(The silver-haired elder staggers back after getting what Neirun meant.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Dear Goddess... what have we done...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1160005"]="Mentor...? Lord Jude...?\nWhat are you talking about? Who was supposed to be dead? The <color=#CA2E0AFF>voice</color> the Adventurer heard?",
    ["Dialogue1160006"]="This sin... belongs to every Priest of the Temple.\n(Neirun slumps into a chair, defeated.)\nThe Pope... she had a <color=#CA2E0AFF>twin brother</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1160007"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A twin brother... Her brother? That would mean he looks like the Pope...?</color></size>\n(Malam looks up sharply, and at that moment, you both speak in unison—)",
    ["Dialogue1160008"]="<size=26>The Ice Cave!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1160009"]="You... how do you know that Yus threw that child into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1160010"]="<size=26>Because we <color=#CA2E0AFF>saw him with our own eyes</color>!</size>\nDeep within the Ice Cave, we found a boy who <color=#CA2E0AFF>looked almost identical to Her Holiness</color>. He was sealed inside a massive glacier, his <color=#CA2E0AFF>life or death uncertain</color>. The Adventurer tried to break the ice, but then... a giant monster appeared, and we were forced to flee...",
    ["Dialogue1160011"]="(As Malam speaks, Jude suddenly drops to his knees with a heavy thud.)\nOh Goddess... please forgive me...",
    ["Dialogue1160012"]="Adventurer... you're a foreigner, unaware of our sacred rites. We've always regarded the Pope as the Goddess's incarnation—so every chosen one must be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>white-haired woman with heterochromatic eyes</color>. But when the chosen one was revealed to be a twin... it was something never before seen in our history. Yus deeply despised Her Holiness' twin brother and said his very existence defiled the Goddess. So he...",
    ["Dialogue1160013"]="... So he threw a child into the monster-filled Ice Cave?!\n(Malam slams the table in anger.)\n<size=26>And you didn't stop him?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1160014"]="Spare Neirun your anger, Malam. In those days, Yus held absolute power in the Temple. He acted in secret, and when the truth reached us... the child was already lost to the Ice Cave. It was not her sin alone—our silence was shared by all.",
    ["Dialogue1160015"]="Then tell me... did it never cross your mind? That the child may have been the <color=#CA2E0AFF>true Goddess' incarnation</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1160016"]="\"The Ice Cave is the Goddess' trial ground. If he truly is the chosen one, then let him walk out of it alive and prove it.\"\n(Neirun covers her face in pain.)\nThose were Yus' exact words back then. And maybe... maybe <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I believed him too...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1160017"]="... If the boy is truly chosen of the Goddess, then his repeated calls to you must carry meaning.\n(Malam takes a deep breath, trying hard to stay calm.)\nAdventurer, we don't have time to return to the Ice Cave... Do you have a way to speak with him?",
    ["Dialogue1160018"]="You heard his voice... by the statue in the Goddess Shrine? And when you reached out... it shattered?\nAlright... let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the Goddess Shrine</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1160019"]="(Malam bends down and helps Jude to his feet.)\nLord Jude, and mentor... The past cannot be undone. What matters now is overcoming the crisis before us. The Dawn Moon Festival begins in a few hours—let's each do what we can!",
    ["Dialogue1160101"]="Is this... a puzzle? Are we supposed to solve a puzzle now?",
    ["Dialogue1160102"]="To where it belongs... beneath the throne... The <color=#CA2E0AFF>throne</color> lies in the Temple's northern wing, beside the Pope's bedroom. And beneath it...\n(Malam traces something in the air—you realize it's the Temple map.)\nIt's that <color=#CA2E0AFF>room that connects to the Ice Cave passage</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1160201"]="Adventurer—when we came earlier, I got too distracted by the monsters, but now that I'm paying attention... don't these six statues look a bit strange?",
    ["Dialogue1160202"]="Right—they each face different directions, with distinct postures and expressions. Isn't this a reflection of <color=#CA2E0AFF>formless faith and hundred faces</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1160203"]="Yes—let's carefully <color=#CA2E0AFF>examine these statues</color> and see if we can find any clues!",
    ["Dialogue1160301"]="It looks like these scattered parts on the ground might correspond to the six goddess statues in the room...",
    ["Dialogue1160302"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unity in diversity</color>!\n(Malam raises his hand excitedly and high-fives you.)\nAdventurer, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>attach these parts</color> and give it a try!",
    ["Dialogue1160401"]="That sound... It seems to be coming from the floor above. Maybe our actions triggered something—shall we return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shrine</color> and check it out, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1160501"]="(Malam points to the base of the statue. The text you saw earlier has vanished—now a single <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple feather</color> floats in the air.)\n... What's that?",
    ["Dialogue1160601"]="At last, we meet... successor of Odin's bloodline.\n(Within the void, a boy—no more than ten—stands motionless before you. That voice... the one that has echoed in your mind time and again.)",
    ["Dialogue1160602"]="Yes... successor of Odin's bloodline. I am Lumi—known to your world... as the incarnation of the Goddess Freyja. And Pope Runa... she is my twin sister.",
    ["Dialogue1160603"]="You carry countless doubts, I know... Yet the very fact you stand here means you now hold the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heron's Feather</color>, the sacred relic left behind by Pope Isumia.",
    ["Dialogue1160604"]="(He nods, eyes shining with wisdom far beyond his years.)\n... Indeed. That is the Heron's Feather—once held close by Goddess Freyja, imbued with the essence of her divine purity. Long ago, Pope Isumia used its power to turn a lifeless desert into a thriving oasis.",
    ["Dialogue1160605"]="In her final years, Pope Isumia foresaw the burden of divine power. Fearing the chaos it might bring, she sealed the Heron's Feather away. I led you to reclaim it—so that you may <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver it to my sister</color>. Lacking divine strength, she reached me only through <color=#CA2E0AFF>dreams</color>, each message carving away at her soul. But now, with the Heron's Feather to guide her, she shall awaken from her slumber... and the curse of sleep shall plague her no longer.",
    ["Dialogue1160606"]="Indeed, the successor of Odin's bloodline. I reached you through my sister's dreams—leading you to the ingredients for the sleep potion. I trust that you and Malam now hold what you sought?",
    ["Dialogue1160607"]="... You flatter me, successor of Odin's bloodline. Through dreams, I have spoken to Runa—carrying the Goddess' revelations, watching Arunafeltz from afar. Freyja is a goddess of compassion; she would never forsake her people in their pain. I am but her incarnation, and her will is mine to fulfill.",
    ["Dialogue1160608"]="And yet... it is I who owe it to you. You've given so much to lead this land away from ruin. If there is any way I may repay you...\n(The boy's gaze drops, lost in thought.)\nTell me, successor of Odin's bloodline... are you seeking something <color=#CA2E0AFF>tied to the Ymir's Heart</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1160609"]="... So it is true. This sacred relic of Odin... I have heard of it. Whether it aids you or not, I cannot say—but once I sense a similar <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine resonance</color> from Runa's <color=#CA2E0AFF>scepter</color>. Try to look for it when you <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Temple</color>. You may find what you're looking for.",
    ["Dialogue1160610"]="(As he finishes speaking, the boy's figure slowly begins to fade.)\nYou have my deepest thanks, successor of Odin's bloodline. My sister's fate now rests in your hands...",
    ["Dialogue1160701"]="What's going on, Adventurer? The moment you touched the feather, you started acting like someone else, speaking in ways I couldn't understand—<color=#CA2E0AFF>just like when the Pope falls into her slumber</color>...\n(Malam pauses, suddenly realizing something.)\nWait—you too...?",
    ["Dialogue1160702"]="So... we were right. That boy—Lumi—is truly the one chosen by the Goddess.\n(He shakes his head with a bitter smile, sorrowful and resigned.)\nWhat did he say to you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1160703"]="The Heron's Feather? T-That's the sacred relic Arunafeltz has sought for years...\n(Malam looks at the purple feather in your hand, murmuring.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could this truly... awaken Her Holiness?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1160801"]="(Staring at the feather in your hand, Neirun's eyes are filled with disbelief.)\n... The Heron's Feather? Is that the sacred relic once held by Pope Isumia? But... wasn't it lost long ago?",
    ["Dialogue1160802"]="... To think she foresaw that no one would be able to bear its power and sealed it away...?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Pope Isumia... how fitting, her warning became prophecy...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1160803"]="Then... Let's give it a try, Adventurer. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the feather on Her Holiness</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1160901"]="(The feather lands on the Pope's chest, glowing faintly with white light before shooting into her body like an arrow.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Luna... she seems to have heard her brother's voice...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1160902"]="<size=26>Your Holiness?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1160903"]="... Neirun? Hmm... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Why are you crying</color>? Did I do something weird in my dreams again and get you into trouble?\n(She reaches out and clumsily wipes away her tears.)\nSorry... Please don't cry.",
    ["Dialogue1160904"]="It's alright, Your Holiness. From now on... those dreams will no longer haunt you. Your affliction has been lifted. And it's all thanks to this Adventurer.\n(The Priest turns to you and bows deeply.)\nWe're forever grateful, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1160905"]="... You want to examine the Pope's scepter?\n(Neirun pauses—she clearly knows the secret it holds.)\nAdventurer... could it be that you?",
    ["Dialogue1160906"]="(You tell her everything Lumi said. As your story unfolds, Neirun's expression softens.)\n... If even the Goddess seeks to honor your deeds, I shall not stand in the way.",
    ["Dialogue1160907"]="(She steps aside to make way.)\nPlease, Adventurer. See if the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gem on this scepter</color> is what you're looking for.",
    ["Dialogue1161001"]="This is the gem. Fifteen years ago, I saw Yus embed it into the Pope's scepter and cast an alchemical ritual to <color=#CA2E0AFF>convert lifeforce</color>. Hibram defied him and was cast out to the Nameless Island. Jude and I... chose to remain silent for the sake of peace.",
    ["Dialogue1161002"]="Perhaps... this is why the Goddess chose you to take it. For years, Arunafeltz has been shackled by Yus—while the people suffer, the Temple turns a blind eye, celebrating atop the corpses of its own people...!",
    ["Dialogue1161003"]="(Neirun gazes at the gem in your hand. Her eyes hold many emotions—regret to herself, anger toward Yus, worry for the future—but most of all, the resolve to break free.)\nTake it, Adventurer. From this day on... we will rise again.",
    ["Dialogue1161004"]="... Now that Her Holiness is awake, we stick to the plan. In a few hours, the Dawn Moon Festival begins. She will be meeting nobles and Priests from the sacred throne, and I'll have her read the decree in the name of the Goddess. We'll take action on the third <color=#CA2E0AFF>toll of the Temple bell</color>. When the time comes, you and Captain Sartre will <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring Musa into the Temple</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1161005"]="(Neirun lifts her head—the morning sunlight filters through the stained glass, lighting her face.)\nThen let's put on a good show... for Yus.",
    ["Dialogue1161101"]="(The usually bold young man now rubs his hands nervously, pacing in front of the Temple door, listening carefully for sounds from within.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>... Three tolls... three tolls... three tolls...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1161102"]="... Hey! What's so funny?\n(Sartre shoots you a glare.)\nAren't you nervous?",
    ["Dialogue1161103"]="Then why are you laughing at me? Watch out, or I'll punch you—",
    ["Dialogue1161104"]="Tch, don't act all tough. I've faced worse before—",
    ["Dialogue1161105"]="(Sartre's words are cut off by a thunderous bell toll, shattering the brief moment of peace.)\nDONG—",
    ["Dialogue1161106"]="... Let's go, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Looks like it's showtime</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1161201"]="Malam, what is the meaning of this?! Colluding with foreign powers? Arms smuggling? You and the Adventurer were to undergo the Goddess' Trial in the Ice Cave—how is it you now stand in the Temple, casting accusations at Musa?",
    ["Dialogue1161202"]="Mentor, there is much to explain. Yet, as I declared before entering the Ice Cave—I placed my faith in the Adventurer's innocence and the Goddess' divine protection. Now...\n(Malam lifts his head and looks around—many of the Priests and nobles look awestruck or uneasy.)\nUnder the guidance of the Goddess, we have returned. Surely, none here would dare to doubt us.",
    ["Dialogue1161203"]="E-Even if that's true, it only gets you off the hook for blasphemy! But you still insulted and accused Musa, the Temple Guard Commander, of arms smuggling! What about those charges?",
    ["Dialogue1161204"]="Insult? Accuse?\n(Malam lets out a cold chuckle.)\nThen how about you all <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at this evidence</color> first before rushing to judgment?",
    ["Dialogue1161301"]="Outrageous! Illicit arms, theft from the royal treasury, treason against the state! Each a crime worthy of fire execution!\n(Neirun steps forward and slams your photo forcefully at Musa's chest.)\nMusa—what say you now?!",
    ["Dialogue1161302"]="N-No... please, don't kill me... It—it was all Lord Yus' idea! <size=26>I was just following orders!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1161303"]="Musa?! What the heck are you saying?!\n(He steps forward, clearly about to cover Musa's mouth.)\nDon't drag Lord Yus into this!",
    ["Dialogue1161304"]="Oh? Trying to silence him now? Her Holiness is still watching!\n(Malam hauls Musa up and makes him face the Pope.)\nSpeak! Tell them everything—you might just get mercy from Her Holiness!",
    ["Dialogue1161305"]="Alright, I'll talk! I'll spill everything!<size=26>It was Lord Yus—</size>",
    ["Dialogue1161306"]="Tch... so that's what you were planning all along.",
    ["Dialogue1161401"]="Adventurer! He won't get far—we'll split up! I'll chase him toward the market; you check out <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priest Residence</color>!",
    ["Dialogue1161501"]="A guy in blue clothes? Oh yeah, how could I forget?",
    ["Dialogue1161502"]="He jumped off the balcony and ran like crazy—like someone was after him! Kicked over my flowerpot by the door! I tried to stop him to pay for the damage, and he just knocked me over and yelled at me to get lost!",
    ["Dialogue1161503"]="Forget it, Adventurer. That guy ran all the way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>city gate</color> and jumped into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>black car</color>—looked like he came straight from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>. That's where the rich folks live... People like us don't mess with that kind of trouble. Whatever you lost, it's not worth risking your life over, right?",
    ["Dialogue1161601"]="(Seeing you return, shoulders slumped, Sartre slams a fist into the pillar.)\nDamn it! He still got away!",
    ["Dialogue1161602"]="I get it... Once he left Rachel, this was out of our hands. I'm not gonna rush in blindly. Let's head back and <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the Temple's situation</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1161701"]="So? Did you find him?",
    ["Dialogue1161702"]="... Lighthalzen? Makes sense—he's with Rekenber Corp, probably someone pretty high up. No wonder they sent someone to pick him up. Still, Musa's already locked up, and the evidence we've got should keep him behind bars for life. I'll find a way to get more dirt on Yus from him... This time, I'll make sure he never rises again.",
    ["Dialogue1161703"]="Don't worry, Adventurer—she just got a bit shaken up, no injuries. Right now, she's resting with the Pope in Her Holiness' bedroom. We've all been on edge these past few days, afraid to relax. But now... we've taken the first step toward change. There's still a long road ahead, but a short break is well-earned.",
    ["Dialogue1161704"]="Tonight, Rachel's holding a <color=#CA2E0AFF>grand celebration</color>. Bring Martistine—let us <color=#CA2E0AFF>wander the festivities together</color>. Don't forget...\n(Malam smiles, and for a moment, it's like he's the same person you first met.)\nYou guys came to Rachel for a nice, relaxing vacation, remember?",
    ["Dialogue1161801"]="You did not find him either, Adventurer...?\n(As he sees you return alone, Malam's concern visibly deepens.)\nI'll send the Temple Guards out now—house by house if I have to! Even if it means—",
    ["Dialogue1161802"]="Wait—you're saying the guards saw a blonde girl in a car... headed for Lighthalzen?\nSo it's them again—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1161803"]="No, Adventurer—don't be reckless. You can't storm into their base without backup. Lighthalzen might be near Rachel, but it's still under Schwarzwald Republic's control. You should go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color> first. Tell Lord Carl everything—ask for help. With how close you two are... he won't ignore this.",
    ["Dialogue1161804"]="(Another firework blooms in the sky. The Dawn Moon Festival is still in full swing—but you're already facing an unexpected farewell.)\n... Take care, Adventurer. I'll handle things here—explain it all. And the girl's robots... I'll make sure they're sent to Juno. We... will meet again.",
    ["Dialogue1161901"]="The Dawn Moon Festival just ended... You were supposed to enjoy a few more days in Arunafeltz, weren't you? So why...\n(Lord Carl's confusion fades as he notices your grim expression and holds his tongue).\n... Something happened, didn't it? Don't panic. Tell me everything, one step at a time.",
    ["Dialogue1161902"]="What?! That little one... she was kidnapped?!",
    ["Dialogue1161903"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Lighthalzen... Isn't that Rekenber Corp's headquarters?</color></size>\nAdventurer, are you sure they took her there? But... why? Why would Rekenber Corp target a helpless little girl?",
    ["Dialogue1161904"]="<size=26>Human experiments?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1161905"]="(With a thunderous slap on the table, Philodis glares in disbelief and fury.)\nThis is outrageous!<size=26>Lord Carl, how could they treat human life like it's nothing?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1161906"]="... Don't panic yet, Adventurer. The more urgent things get, the more we need to stay calm. I'll order the guards near Lighthalzen to begin a search. Any updates will come straight to me. But...\n(Lord Carl lowers his head, and for a moment, he looks like a caged beast.)",
    ["Dialogue1161907"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color> is where the <color=#CA2E0AFF>headquarters of the Rekenber Corp</color> is located. They won't cooperate with our guards. We... need to be ready to come back with nothing. And the worst-case scenario...\n(He doesn't finish, but you already know what he means.)",
    ["Dialogue1161908"]="Going to Lighthalzen? Are you serious? That's reckless, Adventurer. We're not ready—this isn't the moment to provoke them. If we charge in now, we could ruin everything and hand them the opening they need. We should—",
    ["Dialogue1161909"]="... Philodis, say no more.\n(Lord Carl raises a hand to stop him.)\nJust... look at the Adventurer's face.",
    ["Dialogue1161910"]="(Philodis looks your way, caught off guard. Your eyes meet. The silence is deafening—until he finally lowers his shoulders.)\n... So be it. Right now, the only way to stop you would be to knock you unconscious and lock you away.",
    ["Dialogue1161911"]="Everyone—hold on. It's not time to make the call just yet. I think... this might be our best chance.\nSince you found their experiment site, Adventurer, do you think they've got a replica of Ymir's Heart hidden there?",
    ["Dialogue1161912"]="(You explain everything that happened during the Dawn Moon Festival. Fulkyn's expression turns from shock to growing excitement.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A replica of the Ymir's Heart... hidden in the Pope's scepter? And it's being used... to drive alchemy that converts lifeforce?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1161913"]="<size=26>Adventurer, Quick! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Show it to me</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1162001"]="... So I was right.\n(You place the core into the Mysterious Device. As data flows across the display, Fulkyn's gaze grows ever more resolute.)\nEveryone... I know now. I know what Rekenber Corp's really after.",
    ["Dialogue1162002"]="I've been analyzing the Ymir's Heart beneath Juno these past few days, and... I've found some pretty unusual stuff. Adventurer, you've been closer to the Ymir's Heart than anyone. You know what it is—basically a buildup of elemental energy. With enough of them, they transform into... miraculous phenomena. Isn't that right?",
    ["Dialogue1162003"]="That's right. Unleashing the Water Fragment in a sea bursting with water elements... was like lighting a match in a powder keg. Strouf... lost control. And what happened next can never be undone.",
    ["Dialogue1162004"]="Exactly. Wind and fire feed each other. With the Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart in hand, the dragons brought back a flame that had been dead for a thousand years.",
    ["Dialogue1162005"]="But this core under Juno... it's completely different. No elemental trace at all. Instead...\n(Fulkyn taps on the Mysterious Device)\nIt's showing 99.7% compatibility with machines!",
    ["Dialogue1162006"]="That's the reason, I'm sure of it—why Rekenber Corp wants this Ymir's Heart so badly. And everything you've uncovered, Adventurer... it's all been pointing to the same thing: they're running <color=#CA2E0AFF>experiments</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1162007"]="That's right! They're pushing this Ymir's Heart to its limits—seeing what it can really do. Don't you remember, Adventurer? During the android riot, Rekenber Corp proved they could take control of every android just by swapping a chip. And at Einbroch's Steel Capital Institute... those android powered by the replica of the Ymir's Heart? They could control minds—fight off hundreds by sheer will alone...",
    ["Dialogue1162008"]="(Fulkyn moves two pieces on the strategy board until they touch.)\n... If they fuse these two elements—what kind of disaster are we looking at?",
    ["Dialogue1162009"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>War</color>. And with what the Adventurer said—about them working with Priest Yus from Arunafeltz to mass-produce weapons...\n(Lord Carl pushes a white pawn over, forming a tight triangle.)\nThis would be a war we cannot win.",
    ["Dialogue1162010"]="Let me finish. The Adventurer saw it—they are using Ymir's Heart replicas for human experiments. If it's true... those things aren't human anymore. Not even the Adventurer is confident to take them down solo. If Rekenber Corp starts mass-producing monsters... our soldiers won't stand a chance.",
    ["Dialogue1162011"]="... Then, according to Professor Fulkyn, are we just supposed to sit here and wait to be crushed?",
    ["Dialogue1162012"]="No. That's why I said this could be our one chance to turn the tide. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>... that's Rekenber Corp's headquarters. Every shred of research on the Ymir's Heart—they're hiding it there.",
    ["Dialogue1162013"]="Yes, Adventurer. I want you to wipe that data out. If it comes to the worst...\n(Fulkyn slams his arm through the board, scattering every piece)\nThen burn the whole <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim Institute</color> down. Better ash than war.",
    ["Dialogue1162014"]="... So it's all or nothing. But sending the Adventurer alone? That's suicide. I won't sit safely in this palace while a foreigner bleeds for the Republic on my behalf.",
    ["Dialogue1162015"]="(Lord Carl lifts his head slowly, eyes fixed on his secretary.)\nCall them, Philodis. Get <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rowland</color> on the line. Tell him... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I'm ready to negotiate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1162016"]="<size=26>Lord Carl?!</size>\nYou... you mean, you want to be the bait...?",
    ["Dialogue1162017"]="If Rowland arrives in Juno, he'll need to pull guards from Lighthalzen. Their defenses will be thin... and that's your moment, Adventurer. You'll slip into Rekensheim Institute and find what Fulkyn's after.",
    ["Dialogue1162018"]="But—what if the Adventurer doesn't succeed? If things unfold as Professor Fulkyn said and the lab goes up in flames—Rowland will know it was a diversion! The Lord's Mansion can't defend itself... You're inviting the enemy in—how will you survive it?",
    ["Dialogue1162019"]="If the Adventurer pulls it off quietly, all the better. But if not... don't hold back for my sake. I've been in this chair too long not to be ready. And if the worst happens... I'll do whatever it takes to bring Rowland down with me.",
    ["Dialogue1162020"]="(With a firm tap on his armrest, Lord Carl lets out a smile.)\nEverything else... I'm leaving it to you.",
    ["Dialogue1162021"]="Lord Carl, thinking of <color=#CA2E0AFF>dying with the enemy</color> is still too early. I'll take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>core</color> back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Realm of Time</color>—maybe there's more we can learn. You and Philodis need to figure out how to bring Rowland to Juno without raising suspicion. And you, Adventurer... Get some sleep. You'll need it.",
    ["Dialogue1162022"]="(Fulkyn places a heavy hand on your shoulder, cutting off your words.)\n... Trust me, Adventurer. I won't let you walk into a fight blind. So promise me—you'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay sharp and ready</color> until everything breaks loose.",
    ["Dialogue1162101"]="You're finally here! I've been waiting for days. Before... didn't you give the last dish to that traveler? I heard all about it. That little girl didn't get to try the Cloud Soufflé—she must've been so disappointed. She was so sweet about it, too... it really got to me. So...\n(The shopkeeper bends down and pulls out a box from under the counter.)",
    ["Dialogue1162102"]="Ever since that day, I've been saving one every day, thinking you'd come back eventually—and look, here you are! Come on, take it—wait, huh? That little girl didn't come with you? This stuff doesn't keep well, you know...",
    ["Dialogue1162103"]="... She's not in Juno? Out of town, huh?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh no—that's bad timing! The Grand Peco's breeding season ends in a few days. No more Cloud Soufflés until next year...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue1162104"]="Really...? Alright, I'll save one for a few more days then! Come back together once she's home! I'm telling you—\n<size=26>My Cloud Soufflé, it's hands-down the <color=#CA2E0AFF>best in all of Juno</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1170101"]="(You press the power switch on Farbauti's neck. With a short beep, its eyes go dark.)",
    ["Dialogue1170102"]="(You press the power switch on Laufey's neck. With a short beep, its eyes go dark.)",
    ["Dialogue1170301"]="(The rock is dotted with <color=#CA2E0AFF>splatter</color> marks—some are frozen under layers of ice, while others are exposed and rusted into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep brown</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1170401"]="(The blue-tinted ice is covered in crisscrossing sword marks—clear signs of a brutal battle that once took place here...)",
    ["Dialogue1170501"]="(A massive ice crystal pillar before you—and inside, you can clearly see piles of <color=#CA2E0AFF>human bones</color>. It sends a chill down your spine...)",
    ["Dialogue1170601"]="(You examine the two skeletons closely. They're locked in an embrace, even in death. One of them still clutches an old, weathered <color=#CA2E0AFF>parchment</color> in their hand...)",
    ["Dialogue1170701"]="(Huge, complex <color=#CA2E0AFF>machinal instruments</color> stand like metal giants deep in the cave. You've got no clue what they do—but they sure feel out of place in this frozen world...)",
    ["Dialogue1170801"]="(Crates are stacked neatly in the corner. When you peek inside, you find all kinds of <color=#CA2E0AFF>basic necessities</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>food</color> packed away...)",
    ["Dialogue1170901"]="(Crates are stacked neatly in the corner. When you peek inside, you find all kinds of <color=#CA2E0AFF>basic necessities</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>food</color> packed away...)",
    ["Dialogue1171001"]="(Following Malam's gaze, you scan the stone walls around you. A staircase has been carved into the stone—and there's even a vertical lift that looks like it was used for moving crates...)",
    ["Dialogue1171101"]="(Around the crates, you notice there are signs that someone lived there. It's strange—the supplies are way <color=#CA2E0AFF>fewer</color> than what you saw in the upper camp. And... there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>claw marks</color> everywhere...)",
    ["Dialogue1171201"]="(At the end of the path, you find a hidden cave—and inside, it's packed with <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster bones</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1171301"]="(After walking for quite some time, a giant machine—almost like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>incubation pool</color>—suddenly appears. It's filled with glowing green liquid, and inside floats a gem-like object. You can faintly feel it... <color=#CA2E0AFF>resonating</color> with the power in your blood.)",
    ["Dialogue1171401"]="(With Malam's guidance, you spot a narrow <color=#CA2E0AFF>passage</color> carved into the stone wall—just wide enough for one person. It's sealed with a thin sheet of ice, but one <color=#CA2E0AFF>light punch</color> should be enough to shatter it...)",
    ["Dialogue1171501"]="(The wall looks completely fine—there's no sign of the path you came through. Malam says this place hasn't been used in decades, yet the floor is spotless. Has someone been <color=#CA2E0AFF>cleaning</color> it...?)",
    ["Dialogue1171601"]="(Inside the crate, you find rows of weapons—all jet black, with <color=#CA2E0AFF>no labels or markings</color>. Looking closer, each one seems to glow faintly, like it's covered in <color=#CA2E0AFF>tiny sparks of starlight</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1171701"]="(Inside the crate, you find rows of armor—all jet black, with <color=#CA2E0AFF>no labels or markings</color>. Looking closer, each one seems to glow faintly, like it's covered in <color=#CA2E0AFF>tiny sparks of starlight</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1171801"]="The crates are loaded with ammo, rations, and med kits—this place is a goldmine of military supplies. If <color=#CA2E0AFF>war broke out</color> in Arunafeltz right now, the owner of this stash would be <color=#CA2E0AFF>loaded with resources</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1171901"]="(Inside the sealed incubation pool floats a terrifying <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demi-Human Monster</color>—its features eerily similar to the ones you fought in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color>. Maybe... this is where they were <color=#CA2E0AFF>created</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1172001"]="(The sealed incubation pool appears empty—only glowing <color=#CA2E0AFF>green liquid</color> pulses faintly within. Yet somehow... you feel a subtle <color=#CA2E0AFF>resonance of divine power</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1172101"]="(The rectangular experiment table shines cold under the lights. It's stained with splattered blood and fitted with iron rings—probably for restraining chains...)",
    ["Dialogue1172201"]="(Faint black markings are scribbled across the table. Looking closely, you realize—they match the placement of vital organs if someone were lying on it...)",
    ["Dialogue1172301"]="... Your Holiness? Why are you out here right now...? Do you need something?",
    ["Dialogue1172302"]="The Goddess... has spoken. On the day of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dawn Moon Festival</color>... calamity... shall descend from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1172303"]="Ca-calamity?! From the east?! That's the Ice Cave... no, maybe it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>... or even the Rune-Midgard Kingdom?! What should we do?! I have to tell Neirun right now!",
    ["Dialogue1172304"]="I shall... go at once to the Goddess Shrine and pray through the night. All Priests and attendants are to accompany me. You.. inform Jude now.",
    ["Dialogue1172305"]="Right-right away! Your Holiness!",
    ["Dialogue1172401"]="(At the moment your hand touches the statue, <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious text</color> shimmers into existence upon its flawless pedestal. It reads—)",
    ["Dialogue1172402"]="(<color=#CA2E0AFF>Formless faith and hundred faces. To where it belongs, beneath the throne. Unity in diversity, the true face revealed</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue1172501"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's right hand</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1172601"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's right shirt hem</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1172701"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's left hand</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1172801"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's bottom-left base</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1172901"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's left shirt hem</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1173001"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue's bottom-right base</color>, painted in a grayish-blue and lined with gold, appears—by the shape of its broken surface—to perfectly match a statue within the shrine...)",
    ["Dialogue1173101"]="(The golden scepter shimmers, its surface carved with twisting, deliberate patterns. As your gaze lingers, a subtle order emerges from the chaos—these aren't just decorations. Is this... alchemy hidden in plain sight?)",
    ["Dialogue1173201"]="(Light dances on the massive gem's surface—and as your fingers make contact, a wave of <color=#CA2E0AFF>resonance</color> explodes from your <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood</color> like a hidden memory roaring awake...)",
    ["Dialogue1173301"]="(A prominent trail of footprints runs boldly through the flowerbed, leading directly toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1173401"]="(On the edge of the high terrace wall, traces of dirt and the faint outline of a footprint indicate someone might have <color=#CA2E0AFF>jumped down</color> here...)",
    ["Dialogue1173501"]="(At the foot of the house's corner wall, a shattered flowerbed and toppled objects all point in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>same direction</color>—a sign of a hurried, chaotic escape...)",
    ["Dialogue1173601"]="(The steps leading to the Holy Spring are scattered with messy footprints. You can't tell if any of them belong to Martistine—you'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep looking</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1173701"]="(The crowd bustles joyfully around the market with no sign of disturbance. Yet beyond lies the <color=#CA2E0AFF>city gate of Rachel</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1173801"]="(At the city gates of Rachel, the guards converse idly. You catch just enough—a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blonde girl</color> in a black car, headed toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1173901"]="(The tea's fresh—still steaming. But the dawn is near, and the Pope went to meditate hours ago... so why hasn't it cooled?)",
    ["Dialogue1180101"]="Greetings, Adventurer. I am Sam, elite courier of the Gilded Rose, at your service. I've got two valuable packages from Rachel that require your signature. By the way, have you received Lord Malam's letter?",
    ["Dialogue1180102"]="(The young courier gives you a thumbs-up.)\nGreat! The address checks out—just let me <color=#CA2E0AFF>verify the seal on the letter</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1180103"]="Huh, weird... this is the right address.\n(The young courier frowns, scratching his head.)\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>But without Lord Malam's letter, I can't hand over the goods...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1180201"]="Then please <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the goods</color> to make sure nothing was damaged in transit. If everything looks fine, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign</color> it!",
    ["Dialogue1180301"]="Thank you for your cooperation! That wraps up the delivery process. If there's nothing else, then I'll—",
    ["Dialogue1180302"]="Oh, you mean those symbols on the two robots? I remember—they were already there before packaging...\n(The courier rummages through his bag and pulls out a few photos.)\n... See? These were taken before shipping.",
    ["Dialogue1180303"]="Back then, Lord Malam and I inspected everything carefully. Aside from normal wear and tear, we noticed some deliberate markings on the machines. By policy, we have to record those as existing damage to avoid any disputes later. Even if you're a friend of Lord Malam, I must still follow procedure—please submit a formal report to the Gilded Rose if you have any concerns...",
    ["Dialogue1180304"]="Hmm... You're asking what those markings mean? I—I'm not entirely sure... Oh! Come to think of it, Lord Malam was saying something about teaching math in Grey Wolf Village when he saw these...\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Huh? Lord Malam used to teach math there?!</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1180305"]="<size=26>—Hey! Adventurer!</size>\n(Before you can finish your sentence, Andre waves to you from across the street, with several guards following behind.)",
    ["Dialogue1180306"]="There's something I'd like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>discuss with you</color>. Are you... free right now?\n(He glances at the courier beside you, who quickly takes the hint and excuses himself.)",
    ["Dialogue1180307"]="Looks like you've got company, so I'll get out of your way. If you have any more questions about the package, feel free to visit the Gilded Rose Trading Company in Juno. We offer free consultations! Have a great day!",
    ["Dialogue1180401"]="Was that guy from Gilded Rose, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1180402"]="I see... those robots belonged to that girl... Sorry, I heard what happened. You must be worried.\n(Andre pats your shoulder reassuringly.)\nBut right now, we've got a more important quest—one that's to save her, right?",
    ["Dialogue1180403"]="That's right. I've already received orders from Lord Carl...\n(He leans closer, lowering his voice.)\nOur guest has already boarded the airship and will arrive in Juno soon.",
    ["Dialogue1180404"]="Lord Carl thinks the same. He wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the Lord's Mansion</color> right now and make final preparations. I'll go ahead to the airship station to welcome our guest... the rest's up to you.",
    ["Dialogue1180501"]="Good day, Adventurer. You look a bit tired... sorry, but I'm afraid we can't afford any rest right now.",
    ["Dialogue1180502"]="Just recently, I got word from President Rowland—he's already on the airship to Juno and should arrive soon. The director of the Rekensheim Institute and several senior researchers are traveling with him, so as we expected, Lighthalzen's defenses are now much weaker...",
    ["Dialogue1180503"]="So far, our first phase has gone smoothly. Next, we need to figure out how to get you inside the Rekensheim Institute and find the data about the Ymir's Heart replica.",
    ["Dialogue1180504"]="Of course not, Adventurer. The Rekenber Corp governs Lighthalzen with iron precision—any outsiders entering the city have to go through detailed registration and ID checks... So we'll need another way in. The good news? I've already found someone willing to guide you.",
    ["Dialogue1180505"]="(Philodis shakes his head mysteriously.)\nLet's just say it's a surprise. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Train Station</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch</color> and you'll know when you see him. Take care, Adventurer. We'll be waiting for your report.",
    ["Dialogue1180601"]="It's been a while, Adventurer. You look fine—thank goodness!",
    ["Dialogue1180602"]="It's a long story. Honestly, I didn't expect we'd ever meet again. Back then, you and 140 helped us escape from Irumina's experimental site, but after abandoning the mines our families relied on for generations, we had no idea how to survive. Those were some rough, confusing days...",
    ["Dialogue1180603"]="(Dave lets out a deep sigh—you can still feel the fear lingering in his voice.)\nBut luckily, Odin still watched over us. When we headed north into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hugel</color> region, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Republic Guard</color> took us in, gave us new IDs and citizenship records. That's how we managed to start over...",
    ["Dialogue1180604"]="That's right... It was Philodis who helped us. I know you're close to him. If it weren't for you, he might never have stepped in. Everyone in the village is grateful, so when he asked us to help you infiltrate Rekensheim Institute in Lighthalzen, we all agreed—it's the best way to repay you.",
    ["Dialogue1180605"]="(Dave cuts you off with a confident grin.)\nDon't worry, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>. I'm sure I can get you into the Rekensheim Institute safely.",
    ["Dialogue1180701"]="(Dave looks around cautiously, making sure no one's following, then waves you over.)\n... See this, Adventurer? Give me a hand here.",
    ["Dialogue1180702"]="I know what you're thinking—it looks just like any other maintenance hole in Einbroch, right? But listen, I've actually seen the city's sewer blueprints myself. It's like a maze down there, but if we take the right route, it'll lead us out of the Steel Capital Institute...",
    ["Dialogue1180703"]="(With a soft clang, the maintenance hole opens, revealing a pitch-black tunnel.)\n140 once tried to use the sewers as an escape route, and he did a ton of calculations and research for it... but we never got the chance to put it to use.",
    ["Dialogue1180704"]="But according to his notes, this route should lead to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color> outer slums and even into the Rekensheim Institute itself. I've memorized the paths—the only problem is, the sewers might be crawling with Irumina's guards. Yet to you, Adventurer, such foes are mere trifles, aren't they?",
    ["Dialogue1180801"]="Thanks, Adventurer. I owe you one again.\n(Dave exhales deeply, looks deeply shaken.)",
    ["Dialogue1180802"]="I'd heard that... Irumina liked to use her failed experiments as guards, but I didn't think it was true. Those... those things—they looked almost human, didn't they?",
    ["Dialogue1180803"]="You mean... There are creatures and labs like that under Rachel's temple too?\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>So Rekenber Corp's influence has even reached Arunafeltz...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1180804"]="(Dave nods.)\nGot it. I'll do everything I can to help you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1180901"]="(Standing before the rusted pipes, Dave looks up at the leaking cracks above.)\nSee that bit of light? Follow the pipe—it'll take you straight to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Institute's Storage Room</color>. Sorry... but this is as far as I can go.",
    ["Dialogue1180902"]="I know this quest's dangerous, but I believe in you—you're chosen by Odin. No matter what happens, you'll make it through safely. When it's all over... promise you'll come visit our new home, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1181001"]="<size=26>Adventurer?! What are you doing here?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1181002"]="(As you explain, Seyren's expression eases.)\nI see... So much has happened since the Bloodline Banquet, and you've walked a path worthy of the chronicles themselves. As expected of the legendary Adventurer who bears Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue1181003"]="Me? Well... after the Bloodline Banquet, I got a secret quest. Lord Bohr and Prince Aronst—no, I should call him <color=#CA2E0AFF>His Majesty</color> now—publicly dropped the case against the Walter Family, but secretly, they've been investigating the real cause of King Tristan III's death.",
    ["Dialogue1181004"]="So I went undercover with a few companions, posing as merchants attending an auction. We stayed in a luxury hotel owned by Rekenber Corp in Lighthalzen, but...",
    ["Dialogue1181005"]="(Seyren looks frustrated.)\nThe very night we checked in, someone attacked me.",
    ["Dialogue1181006"]="I don't know. They knocked me out that night. When I woke up, I was already inside this research facility. I've been searching for any trace of my companions—but what's really weird is... why is this whole place empty?",
    ["Dialogue1181007"]="You think it's a trap too? Guess we're on the same page. Still... even if it is, I can't just leave Margaret and the others behind.\n(Seyren lowers his head—you can feel the guilt in his voice.)\nI'm their captain, and I failed to protect them... That's on me.",
    ["Dialogue1181008"]="... Team up? I'd love that.\nHonestly, if I run into the person who ambushed me at the hotel again, I doubt I could handle them alone...",
    ["Dialogue1181009"]="(Seyren laughs and pats your shoulder.)\nIt's been a while since we worked together, Adventurer. Let's hope we can survive this one as well.",
    ["Dialogue1181101"]="A-Adventurer?! What are you doing here?! I... I feel so dizzy...",
    ["Dialogue1181102"]="... Before I passed out? Let me think... That night, we reached Rachel and planned to stay at an inn before heading out the next day. But around midnight, someone slipped a note under the door... It said... right! Names! Trinity, Orfeo, Ivy<size=26>... They were all <color=#CA2E0AFF>kidnapped</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1181103"]="(She tries to get up, but her strength fails and she collapses again—you rush to steady her.)\nDon't stop me! I—I have to go...",
    ["Dialogue1181104"]="(At your words, Goldie looks around in a daze. Her teammates lie sprawled across the room, but their chests rise and fall steadily.)\nEveryone... they are okay? <color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Oh... thank goodness...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1181105"]="(You take out the dagger you found earlier on the road from Rachel to Lighthalzen and return it to Goldie by placing it on her hand.)\nThis is... from when I was attacked—yes! That's it! I went to the location written on the note, but was ambushed there! To leave a clue, I threw my dagger into a nearby bush...",
    ["Dialogue1181106"]="(Goldie stares at the dagger in her hand, trying to recall more, but her face twists in pain.)\n... Then I think they knocked me out. When I woke up... I saw you.\nSorry, Adventurer. My head really hurts... please, <color=#CA2E0AFF>let me rest for a bit</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1181201"]="<size=26>... You bastards! Don't you touch her with those filthy hands!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1181202"]="... Adventurer? What are you... No, wait...\n(Ivy lowers his raised fist, looking around as the rage fades from his eyes.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>This isn't the Underground Arena</color>. Where's Celia?",
    ["Dialogue1181203"]="... I see. You mean... we all went missing in Rachel, and you think Rekenber Corp's behind it, so you snuck into Lighthalzen to find us... This place is the Rekensheim Institute, right?",
    ["Dialogue1181204"]="I do remember... back in the Underground Arena, that bastard said—<color=#CA2E0AFF>\"The lord in Lighthalzen wants them alive.\"</color> Hah... interesting.",
    ["Dialogue1181205"]="That line tells us two things. First, the attack on me, Celia, and Zenlur was premeditated. But ever since we took this quest, everyone's movements have been top secret, so for them to act the moment we reached Rachel... their intel came way too fast. If I'm right... There's a rat among us, isn't there?",
    ["Dialogue1181206"]="Second... why keep us alive? If they wanted to stop the kingdom's investigation, killing us all would've been easier. From what I know, the Rekenber Corp isn't exactly a charity—they must have something to gain from this. But what for? To use me to threaten my father...? No, that doesn't explain why they took Celia and Zenlur...",
    ["Dialogue1181207"]="(The young genius props his chin, lost deep in thought.)\nSorry, Adventurer. I need to think this through a bit more... you should go <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the others</color> first.",
    ["Dialogue1181301"]="No... don't... <size=26>leave me!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1181302"]="You're... Adventurer?\n(Trinity grips your arm tightly. She still hasn't fully escaped the nightmare, tears streaming down her face)\nWhere are we? Where's... Orfeo?",
    ["Dialogue1181303"]="You don't know either? Then... what's going on? I remember, we were in Rachel—we wanted to visit the Holy Spring for inspiration... But we saw a group hiding children in a cellar, trying to smuggle them somewhere. We followed them to help the kids, but it turned out to be a trap!",
    ["Dialogue1181304"]="Orfeo... told me to run back to the inn for help, but he... he didn't make it...\n(Trinity covers her face, voice trembling with grief slipping through her fingers.)\nI'm sorry, Adventurer... please, just let me be alone for a while...",
    ["Dialogue1181401"]="Come on... again! Don't stop! Today I'll definitely get stronger!!!\n(The white-haired boy swings his fists, training even in his sleep.)",
    ["Dialogue1181402"]="Nice... good hit!! Again! <size=26>This time I'll see it clearly!!!</size>\n(Zenlur flips up from the floor, then freezes when he sees you.)\n... Adventurer? You here to box in the Underground Arena too?",
    ["Dialogue1181403"]="Huh? This... this is Rekensheim Institute? Uh... can we still go back? Everyone there is so strong! If I could spar with them, I'd totally become the toughest Shura ever!",
    ["Dialogue1181404"]="Hey—hey?! Don't walk away! Did I say something wrong? Hey, wait...!\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Huh, why get mad all of a sudden...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1181501"]="Hmm... I...",
    ["Dialogue1181502"]="Randel, can you hear me? How are you feeling? Are you hurt anywhere?",
    ["Dialogue1181503"]="That voice... Seyren?\n(The blind youth fumbles forward and grabs his friend's hand.)\nWhere are we? And the others—where are they?",
    ["Dialogue1181504"]="It's probably the Rekensheim Institute. I only saw you and Cecil, and I don't know about the others yet. Still... It's good news that the Adventurer's with us. The more allies in a situation like this, the better. Hey, do you remember what happened before you passed out?",
    ["Dialogue1181505"]="I only remember... someone came through my window in the middle of the night. I heard noises, but that person was strong, even in the dark, he moved super fast. I didn't stand a chance. We struggled for a bit and made a lot of noise, I thought you'd come running, but...",
    ["Dialogue1181506"]="Sorry, Randel. I was attacked as well. Maybe the others had the <color=#CA2E0AFF>same thing</color> happen to them...\n(Seyren looks toward Cecil, who's out cold nearby.)\nAdventurer, could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on Cecil</color> for me? I want to talk a bit more with Randel about the details.",
    ["Dialogue1181601"]="(At your call, Cecil groggily opens her eyes.)\nThis voice... Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1181602"]="Uh... cough! Not really... my head hurts. What happened? I was resting in my hotel room in Lighthalzen. But at midnight... midnight?",
    ["Dialogue1181603"]="(Cecil jerks her head up.)\nOh no! That person attacked me... What about the others? They—",
    ["Dialogue1181604"]="Oh! Looks like our cast is all here.",
    ["Dialogue1181701"]="Good—smart move! I'm pleased you're cooperating. I didn't want to get rough right at the start, because my guard...",
    ["Dialogue1181702"]="(Baroshev turns slightly and points at the girl holding a sword. You recognize her... she's Ygnizem.)\nShe doesn't have much patience, as you can see. If anyone breaks the rules, that sword will go through your throat...",
    ["Dialogue1181703"]="...\n(Ygnizem says nothing, but at Baroshev's cue her long sword starts sliding forward, which is a clear warning.)",
    ["Dialogue1181704"]="Tsk tsk—this isn't your business, Adventurer. I want a good show. If it doesn't please me... then be ready to help bury your friends!",
    ["Dialogue1181801"]="We can't fall for Baroshev's trick. This murder game is clearly meant to make us suspect, hate, or even hurt each other, so he can profit from the chaos. If we stick together and trust each other, then...",
    ["Dialogue1181802"]="... Then what? He's just gonna give up and hand over the hostages?\n(Ivy snorts.)\nI've read up on you, knight. Your name's Seyren, right?",
    ["Dialogue1181803"]="An elite of the Royal Chivalry, the right-hand man of Captain Hallam. The moment your newly crowned little king commands it, you'll die for him without a second thought—but what does that have to do with me?",
    ["Dialogue1181804"]="Look, the only reason I'm here is because you messed up—you got captured and failed the quest. That officer showed up and forced me and Celia into this makeshift, crappy squad...",
    ["Dialogue1181805"]="(The youth's gaze sweeps across everyone there. You'd even call the look venomous.)\n... Now, we're all meat on the chopping block. All of us.",
    ["Dialogue1181806"]="... Adventurer, I know you've fought side by side with them and that you trust each other. But I won't entrust my fate to anyone else. From here on, I'll move alone. Don't try to stop me—even you.",
    ["Dialogue1181901"]="(After Ivy leaves, the main hall falls into silence until Cecil finally speaks.)\nSorry, everyone... I'd like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>act alone</color> for a while too.",
    ["Dialogue1181902"]="That doesn't mean we're enemies, Adventurer. I just... have doubts about all this, and I can't fully trust everyone here. Besides, you know that I always work alone, right?",
    ["Dialogue1181903"]="Don't worry, I won't attack anyone. If I find any clues, I'll tell you right away.\nSo... stay safe, everyone. See you later.",
    ["Dialogue1182001"]="Everyone, I know this sucks, but look on the bright side... according to Baroshev's rules, we've still got twelve hours to figure something out, right?",
    ["Dialogue1182002"]="... You're right. The tougher things get, the more we should focus on what's in front of us. Like...",
    ["Dialogue1182003"]="(Hearing this, Goldie smiles and nods.)\nThen, let's split up. The Adventurer and I will <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>terrain</color> for monsters or traps. The two knights over there can look for a place to rest. As for Zenlur and Trinity—you two can handle food and water...",
    ["Dialogue1182004"]="Once we're done, we'll meet back here to share what we found. Sound good?",
    ["Dialogue1182101"]="<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Experiment logs... weird notes...</size></color>\n(Goldie flips through the books, clearly frustrated.)\nNope... can't make sense of any of this!",
    ["Dialogue1182102"]="That's only natural. If I worked for Rekenber Corp, I wouldn't just leave important stuff lying around for anyone to read either. Right? Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1182103"]="Oh well, let's look somewhere else. Maybe we'll find something more useful out there.",
    ["Dialogue1182201"]="(Surrounded by monsters, you and Goldie retreat into the corridor. She wipes her sweat and looks back at you.)\nWhew... You okay, Adventurer? Hurt anywhere?",
    ["Dialogue1182202"]="Just a few scratches, nothing serious. But... what the heck were those things? They look human, but...\n(Goldie frowns, trying to find the right words to describe these monsters.)",
    ["Dialogue1182203"]="You mean... Rekenber Corp is secretly doing human experiments, turning people into monsters?\n(Goldie grits her teeth, furious.)\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Those bastards...!</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1182204"]="... You're right. We need more evidence if we want to expose their crimes. Let's go, Adventurer. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>check somewhere else</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1182301"]="Adventurer, doesn't this machine look kinda familiar? I swear I've seen it before...",
    ["Dialogue1182302"]="(Goldie's eyes brighten at your answer.)\nThat's it, Adventurer! The hologram wasn't clear before, but this looks almost identical to the machine Baroshev used to imprison the hostages. I'd say... that's no coincidence.",
    ["Dialogue1182303"]="Yeah... or maybe this is the machine they used for human experiments... All right, let's stop here for now. We'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to the main hall</color>, tell Seyren and the others what we found, and decide our next move.",
    ["Dialogue1182401"]="(Everyone's already gathered in the main hall except you and Goldie.)\nYou're back, Adventurer. How did it go?",
    ["Dialogue1182402"]="I see. So there aren't any actual monsters, but creatures wandering around might be <color=#CA2E0AFF>experimental subjects</color>. In that case, Adventurer, Goldie—mark the areas where they show up, and everyone else, stay away from them.",
    ["Dialogue1182403"]="We've got good news too. There are a few rooms in the southwest wing—it looks like the researchers' quarters. Plenty of basic supplies, enough for us to rest up. As for food and water...",
    ["Dialogue1182404"]="Zenlur and I found a cafeteria on the northwest side. Oh, and we checked the main gate too—it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>completely sealed shut</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1182405"]="Hmm... since food and supplies aren't an issue for now, maybe we should all rest up? After everything that's happened, you all look exhausted. Let's talk again once everyone's had some sleep.",
    ["Dialogue1182501"]="Great... can you hear me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1182502"]="No... I'm not Martistine, Adventurer. We've met before at St. Caviderina Welfare Center. Do you remember?",
    ["Dialogue1182503"]="... You can call me Madelina. I know you're worried about Martistine. The good news is that she's safe for now, just locked in the institute's underground prison. So, if you wanna save her...\n(Madelina raises her hand, and a map projection lights up the wall.)",
    ["Dialogue1182504"]="This is the institute's layout. You and your team are on the first floor right now. To get underground, you'll need either the <color=#CA2E0AFF>elevator at the far south</color> or the <color=#CA2E0AFF>emergency passage</color> on the east side. The elevator's under Baroshev's control, and the passage needs a biometric key to open...",
    ["Dialogue1182505"]="Fingerprints, iris scans, or facial bone patterns. From what I know, only people with top-level Rekensheim Institute access can register them. I can try hacking it, but it'll take time. If you can, try to stall Baroshev and keep his attention on you...",
    ["Dialogue1182506"]="Are you doubting who I am, Adventurer?\n(She sighs softly, a sound far too mature for her age.)\n... Fair enough. Martistine and I... never really told you who we are.",
    ["Dialogue1182507"]="You've probably heard that our parents used to work for the Rekenber Corp. More accurately, they were senior researchers at the Rekensheim Institute, running several key projects. Due to confidentiality, all such projects were conducted under <color=#CA2E0AFF>complete isolation</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1182508"]="So from the day we were born, Martistine and I lived with our parents in the institute. We grew up here and knew it inside out. Then an accident happened—our parents were blamed and punished by the institute, and we were forced to become their <color=#CA2E0AFF>experimental subjects</color>...",
    ["Dialogue1182509"]="... Adventurer. You always thought Martistine had a split personality, right? But actually... I'm not another personality—I'm her twin sister. Baroshev used the replica of the Ymir's Heart to fuse our souls into the same body...",
    ["Dialogue1182510"]="(Suddenly Madelina's hologram starts flickering, her voice stutters.)\nInterference... careful... wait for me...",
    ["Dialogue1182601"]="... Everyone's here? But...\n(Trinity looks around, puzzled.)\nZenlur? Where did he go?",
    ["Dialogue1182602"]="That white-haired boy... he...\n(Seyren grits his teeth and falls silent. You have a bad feeling.)",
    ["Dialogue1182603"]="Hahahahaha! What's the matter<size=26>—of course he's dead, Adventurer!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1182604"]="Now that someone's died, it's time for you detectives to act. Tell me—who do you think the killer is?\n(He points at everyone in turn.)\nHim, him... or her?",
    ["Dialogue1182605"]="Each of you gets one vote. The person with the most votes will die. I'll execute according to people's will. Of course, you can also spare your friends and not vote, but that means the killer keeps killing... until everyone here is dead.",
    ["Dialogue1182606"]="... So, <color=#CA2E0AFF>what's everyone's decision</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1182701"]="... Hey, wait! Why is everyone staring at me?\nYou're not thinking... I'm the one who killed that muscle idiot, are you?",
    ["Dialogue1182702"]="But... I remember Zenlur slept in the same room as you yesterday. And you two are both... I mean... Celia...\n(Trinity hesitates as she considers whether to continue speaking.)\nIf we're forced to pick a murderer from among us, aren't you... <color=#A1979FFF><size=18>the one with the biggest motive...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1182703"]="Ha... fine. So you all think I did it, huh?\n(Ivy's face grows cold and mocking at Trinity's doubt.)\nGo ahead then, vote for me if you want—",
    ["Dialogue1182704"]="... Right, everyone, we can't act rashly. Bottom line... is Zenlur really dead? If so, where's the corpse? Who was the first witness?",
    ["Dialogue1182705"]="(Under Goldie's questioning, Seyren slowly raises his hand.)\nI was the one who found him. He was face-down, floating in an incubation pool on the west side of the institute... However, I didn't get a chance to check the face properly...",
    ["Dialogue1182706"]="(He grits his teeth and looks toward Baroshev, who sits by a corner watching calmly.)\nHe wouldn't let me near the body. I could only go by the clothes and that distinctive <color=#CA2E0AFF>white hair</color>—so I guessed it might be that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shura</color> boy...",
    ["Dialogue1182707"]="... Right. In that case, I can even start to wonder whether a killer card really existed among the first eight cards at all. Or did you plant a trap to make us doubt and slaughter one another?",
    ["Dialogue1182708"]="(Baroshev gives a creepy laugh, refusing to answer Goldie.)\nOh my, so it seems you all want to skip today's vote, yes?",
    ["Dialogue1182709"]="What a shame... That means the <color=#CA2E0AFF>killer</color> will have to keep <color=#CA2E0AFF>acting</color>. Same rules: if I don't see another victim within twelve hours, then... you'll see a hostage's corpse right here in this hall.",
    ["Dialogue1182710"]="(The demon bows gracefully, excitement clear in his voice.)\nThe game goes on. Don't let me down, my honored guests.",
    ["Dialogue1182801"]="What do you think, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1182802"]="Really... I don't see any useful clues either. Let's go check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>crime scene</color> Seyren mentioned. I remember it's along the corridor from here all the way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>incubation pool</color> at the far <color=#CA2E0AFF>east</color> end, right?",
    ["Dialogue1182901"]="You okay, Adventurer? That was close...\n(Goldie glances at the stairs, still shaken.)\nYou're not usually that clumsy. How did that happen?",
    ["Dialogue1182902"]="... You think Zenlur might've slipped here like you did and fallen into the pool?\nThat would be an accident, right? But Baroshev clearly said... this was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>murder</color> planned by the killer.",
    ["Dialogue1182903"]="You mean... this was a trap? Someone poured oil here and lured Zenlur over...? But that kind of trick...\n(Goldie hesitates and stares at the pool, then gives a wry shake of her head.)\nNo... you are right.",
    ["Dialogue1182904"]="It only works because the killer targeted Zenlur. That muscle-headed idiot... <color=#CA2E0AFF>wouldn't doubt what his friends told him</color>.\n(Silence stretches between you and Goldie, and both of you know that the killer is now narrowed down to a few people who were <color=#CA2E0AFF>closest</color> to Zenlur...)",
    ["Dialogue1183001"]="(The youth stands at the door, chin in hand, thinking.)\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>It should be right here... but how do we...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1183002"]="... I'm trying to figure out how to open this door. Earlier, I used a special alchemy on Celia that allows me to sense her roughly... she's right behind this door. So... is it possible that Baroshev locked all the hostages behind this door?",
    ["Dialogue1183101"]="Looks like smashing the door down by force won't work.\n(Ivy gives a bitter smile and shakes his head, seeming to drop the idea.)\nAh, well... <color=#A1979FFF><size=18>The only person Celia seems to want to see is Zenlur anyway...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1183102"]="I'm fine. Since you couldn't open the door for me, do me a favor—could you find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aurora Flowers</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vegetable Oil</color> for me? I need to make a few alchemy potions.",
    ["Dialogue1183103"]="(Hearing this, Goldie narrows her eyes, wary.)\nWhat kind of potion needs Vegetable Oil? Why are you making potions right now?",
    ["Dialogue1183104"]="What... you still doubt me? If I wanted to kill that kid, I wouldn't wait until now. Want to guess how many poisons I know that can quietly kill someone with no trace?",
    ["Dialogue1183105"]="(Ivy sneers.)\nBelieve it or not. That bounty hunter with the longbow—her name's Cecil, right? She asked me to make some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Revival Potions</color>. If you want to know why, ask her. I'm going back to the lab. Don't bother me.",
    ["Dialogue1183106"]="... Sorry, should I have been more tactful about my words?\n(After Ivy storms off, Goldie sighs, looking a bit regretful.)\nHe looked... really angry.",
    ["Dialogue1183107"]="We don't have enough clues yet, so we can't jump to conclusions... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I want to talk to the others</color> and hear what they say. How about you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1183108"]="You want to help Ivy finish the Revival Potions? Fine... call it a small bit of recompense for him.\nLet's <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up</color> for now. If either of us finds anything, meet back in the room, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1183201"]="Okay... I'll start tinkering with the potion now. Don't just stand there—<color=#CA2E0AFF>help me mix these materials evenly</color>. It's not hard, right?",
    ["Dialogue1183301"]="Done... here, take it, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1183302"]="(Ivy shrugs.)\nIt was that bounty hunter's request. She told me to give the Revival Potion to you for safekeeping. To be honest, I'm confused by what she's up to. Normally, we only use one at someone's deathbed since it enables a person who's on the verge of death to move and act for a short while...",
    ["Dialogue1183303"]="<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>But this kind of potion does nothing for a healthy person... could it be that she's already...?</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1183401"]="... Sorry, Adventurer. I had to avoid Baroshev's watch to get in touch with you. Our comms can cut out at any time, so I'll be brief. I already told you that after our parents died, Martistine and I were forced to become Baroshev's experimental subjects... later, with Farbauti and Laufey's help, we escaped and met you at the St. Caviderina Welfare Center...",
    ["Dialogue1183402"]="And then... we went with you to Rachel. I'm not sure if it was something you did at the Dawn Moon that put Baroshev on our trail... he realized he could use Martistine to lure you into the Rekensheim Institute, so he had people grab her. He hasn't harmed her yet, but...\n(The girl grits her teeth and stops. But you get the idea.)",
    ["Dialogue1183403"]="Thanks, Adventurer. Like I said, the only ways down to the underground prison holding Martistine will be the <color=#CA2E0AFF>elevator at the far south</color> or the <color=#CA2E0AFF>emergency passage on the east side</color>. I'm working to crack the emergency passage lock but be careful with your companion, they've already...",
    ["Dialogue1183404"]="(While talking, the girl's hologram flickers again.)\nExperi...men...tal... pupp...et...",
    ["Dialogue1183501"]="Adventurer, sorry to bother you.\n(Trinity stands in your doorway, looking worried.)\nCan I have a moment of your time?",
    ["Dialogue1183502"]="I want to know... did you see Goldie? After leaving the main hall, I went back to my room, but she hasn't come back since. I'm kinda worried...",
    ["Dialogue1183503"]="... After leaving the main hall, you and Goldie checked Zenlur's room and the incubation pool, then Goldie said she'd talk to everyone, and you all split up?\n(Trinity looks a bit pale.)\nBut after we came back to the main hall... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I haven't seen her at all</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1183601"]="Oh, hey, Adventurer! Don't think that I'm not aware of your little tricks... Like before, I'll collect the corpses, you lot just go to the main hall and cast your votes for who you think the killer is.",
    ["Dialogue1183602"]="Looks like our brave Adventurer needs a little warning...\n(At Baroshev's words, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ygnizem</color>, who had been standing silently by his side, raises her sword once again.)",
    ["Dialogue1183701"]="Got it, Adventurer? Here, I make the rules. Now take your friends and <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the main hall</color>, or else...\n(As Baroshev speaks to you, Ygnizem presses her blade to your chest—one step closer, and it'll pierce through.)",
    ["Dialogue1183702"]="... Don't blame me if I get rough, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1183801"]="You're finally here. I thought... wait, just you two? Where's Goldie?",
    ["Dialogue1183802"]="... In the library... We saw Goldie fall from the upper floor. She's...\n(Trinity covers her mouth in grief, but your eyes catch the <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing piece</color> of the ornament at her waist. Then, that dreadful voice echoes again...)",
    ["Dialogue1183803"]="Well then, detectives... The killer claimed a second victim. Now it's your turn. Tell me, who do you think the murderer is?\n(Baroshev's gaze sweeps over you all. No one answers, until...)",
    ["Dialogue1183804"]="<size=26>Adventurer?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1183805"]="Oh? How unexpected—I thought you'd be the toughest one to break... So, what's your vote, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1183806"]="Eh—what? Why... are you suspecting me, Adventurer?\n<size=26>We both saw Goldie fall! I couldn't possibly be the killer!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1183807"]="(Listening to you, Seyren frowns thoughtfully.)\nYou mean... Goldie was already dead before you found her? And Trinity staged everything, then dragged you back to the library so you'd serve as her witness?",
    ["Dialogue1183808"]="But... do you have any proof, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1183809"]="Y-You're saying <color=#CA2E0AFF>I lied to you</color>? What do you mean?!",
    ["Dialogue1183810"]="(Trinity's face drains of color as she spots the bell in your palm.)\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Th–that's from my... my costume?! No... how...?!</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue1183901"]="N–no... that's not... I didn't...",
    ["Dialogue1183902"]="Adventurer, you're saying Trinity claimed she never saw Goldie again after leaving the main hall...\n(As Seyren speaks, everyone turns to look at Trinity.)\nYet the bell from her costume was found <color=#CA2E0AFF>beside Goldie's body</color>—am I right?",
    ["Dialogue1183903"]="No... no, I didn't mean to kill her! <size=26>She just wouldn't stop bothering me!!!</size>\n(Trinity's emotions spiral out of control under your questioning.)",
    ["Dialogue1183904"]="... Stop pushing her, Adventurer. We both know the reason—it's because of her fiancé, isn't it?\n(Ivy's face remains cold, but for once, you catch a flicker of empathy.)",
    ["Dialogue1183905"]="Honestly, I can't really blame her. If it were me, I'd do the same to protect Celia. In the end, humans just pick whatever benefits them most, right?",
    ["Dialogue1183906"]="I... I didn't... <size=26>AHHHHHHH—!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1184001"]="HAHAHAHA<size=26>... HAHAHAHA!!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1184002"]="(Baroshev raises his hands, applauding amid his wild laughter.)\nThank you all! What a magnificent show! As I thought... pain truly is the finest nourishment. When humans drown in it, they evolve in the most fascinating ways...",
    ["Dialogue1184003"]="What do I want? Haha... now that's a wonderful question, Adventurer. I'd love to spend a whole day explaining. This—this is a game, an experiment, a milestone on humanity's path to godhood. My masterpiece, years in the making, is about to bloom in full...!",
    ["Dialogue1184004"]="But... what a shame. Our game isn't over yet. Since we're still on stage, we'd better give it our best performance till the end, don't you think?\n(He raises his hand, and unbelievably, the lifeless Ivy and Trinity begin to move like puppets.)",
    ["Dialogue1184005"]="...\n(Ivy doesn't respond. He slowly lifts his weapon, his movements stiff and awkward, like a puppet being controlled...)",
    ["Dialogue1184006"]="...\n(Trinity doesn't respond. She slowly lifts her weapon, her movements stiff and awkward, like a puppet being controlled...)",
    ["Dialogue1184007"]="<size=26>... Get back! Adventurer!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1184101"]="Everyone... what I'm about to say might sound insane, but it's the truth my investigation uncovered...\n(Cecil takes a deep breath.)\nThis killing game... <color=#CA2E0AFF>might've already happened to us many times before</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1184102"]="I know it sounds impossible. It's because we've <color=#CA2E0AFF>lost all the memories in between</color>. From what I can tell, Baroshev had people ambush us at the hotel, knock us out, and secretly move us to his lab. Then he forced us into this killing game. Every time it ends, he wipes our memories... and starts the whole thing over again...",
    ["Dialogue1184103"]="It must be some kind of <color=#CA2E0AFF>human experiment</color>...\n(Cecil pulls her collar down a little. You notice a stitched scar snaking down from her collarbone, a mark from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>surgery</color>.)\nI don't remember ever getting this. Maybe... it's the same for all of you?",
    ["Dialogue1184104"]="What... what's that? I've never had a wound like that... Randel has one too? What about the Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1184105"]="... No, the Adventurer should be fine. He's the only one who entered the lab while still conscious.\n(Cecil turns her gaze toward you.)\nYour memory's intact, so, can you tell me <color=#CA2E0AFF>what day it is today</color>?",
    ["Dialogue1184106"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Five months</color>. It's been <color=#CA2E0AFF>five whole months</color> since we entered Lighthalzen. Cecil might actually be right.",
    ["Dialogue1184107"]="But why? What's Baroshev after? I don't get it—why go through all this trouble just to make us kill each other?",
    ["Dialogue1184108"]="I've thought about that for a long time too... The only thing we can be sure of is that Baroshev's trying to <color=#CA2E0AFF>achieve something</color> through this killing game. So I tried to reason backward—what happens right before he ends the game? That moment... that's when he must've gotten what he wanted.",
    ["Dialogue1184109"]="That's right, Adventurer. They came back to life after dying—stronger than ever. Even if we all fight together, we can't...\n(Suddenly, Cecil lowers her voice sharply.)\nShh—footsteps!",
    ["Dialogue1184110"]="...\n(Boots echo down the silent corridor, the sound growing closer and closer... In the tight space, your companions exchange pale, terrified looks.)",
    ["Dialogue1184111"]="—Adventurer! Can you hear me?!",
    ["Dialogue1184201"]="... Things are bad, so I'll keep it short. Remember the emergency passage at the end of the west corridor? I've hacked the lock and registered your fingerprints. If you can reach it, you'll get into the research lab's underground.",
    ["Dialogue1184202"]="But if we don't disable the lab's surveillance, Baroshev will still be able to track you. The control room and the emergency exit are in opposite directions, which means...\n(Madelina hesitates, but you all understand what she means.)",
    ["Dialogue1184203"]="... No, Adventurer. You shouldn't risk your life.",
    ["Dialogue1184204"]="Did you forget what Cecil just said? Among all of us, you're the only one who hasn't become one of Baroshev's test subjects. You're the only one who can <color=#CA2E0AFF>make it out alive</color>—and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell the world the truth</color>. As for us... Soon we'll end up like Ivy and the others, nothing but mindless killing machines... Let Randel and me go cut the power—Cecil, you go with the Adventurer. You two can still...",
    ["Dialogue1184205"]="Then I'm the one best suited for this task. When it comes to speed and stealth...\n(Cecil picks up her longbow with a proud smile.)\nNo one here can match me, right, Captain Seyren?",
    ["Dialogue1184206"]="... I'll cover you.\n(The blind youth grabs his sword and steps beside Cecil.)\nYou're not built for a head-on fight. If they surround you... you'll lose.",
    ["Dialogue1184207"]="Randel?! You too...?!",
    ["Dialogue1184208"]="... Alright, then it's the two of us.\nAlso... Adventurer, I once asked that young alchemist to make a Revival Potion... Did he ever finish it...?",
    ["Dialogue1184209"]="... Just in case. We never know when death might come for us...\n(Cecil presses a hand to her chest. Beneath the fabric lies that terrible scar, the one that seemed to appear out of nowhere.)\nIf things get bad, maybe this potion can buy me a little more time.",
    ["Dialogue1184210"]="Enough—stop hesitating! You want those monsters to catch up and kill us all?!\n(She pushes you and Seyren toward the other end of the corridor.)\nDon't look back. Go do what you need to do.",
    ["Dialogue1184301"]="Adventurer, do you see that? What... what are those things...",
    ["Dialogue1184302"]="(As you describe what happened at the Rachel Temple, Seyren's expression grows darker.)\nLooks like Cecil was right. Baroshev really is conducting massive human experiments under Rekenber Corp's orders... maybe even Margaret and the others were already...",
    ["Dialogue1184303"]="Adventurer, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>look around</color> a bit more. No matter how this ends... I just want to know where my comrades are.",
    ["Dialogue1184401"]="This is... that dancer's fiancé, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue1184402"]="Sorry... I shouldn't have asked.\n(The knight lowers his head, you can feel he's just as heartbroken as you are.)\nCome on, Adventurer. We still have things to do.",
    ["Dialogue1184501"]="(In the dim cell, little Martistine curls up in a corner. Beside her stands Madelina's holographic projection.)\n... I'm so glad you all made it here safely. But now's not the time to relax...",
    ["Dialogue1184502"]="Baroshev injected her with an experimental reagent—she's in a coma. To wake her, we'll need to inject another <color=#CA2E0AFF>reagent</color> that counteracts it...\n(Madelina gestures for you to pick up the <color=#CA2E0AFF>serum extractor</color> on the table.)",
    ["Dialogue1184503"]="Adventurer, follow the corridor west and you'll reach the lab. There are some... unfinished <color=#CA2E0AFF>experimental subjects</color> there. We can draw the serum from their blood.",
    ["Dialogue1184601"]="Ugh... It hurts...\n(She murmurs weakly, curling tighter into herself. She still hasn't woken up.)",
    ["Dialogue1184602"]="Don't worry, Adventurer. The reagent just needs some time to take effect. I'll look after her. Meanwhile, could you head to the lab at the end of the corridor? Look for an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Acid Solvent</color> strong enough to melt the lock. Without a key, it's the only way to open this cell.",
    ["Dialogue1184701"]="Um... uh...\n(After leaving the cell, Martistine shyly tugs on your sleeve.)\nTh-thank you...",
    ["Dialogue1184702"]="I—I said... thank you! Madelina told me everything! You came all this way, risking your life just to save me...\n(The shy girl fidgets, her gaze darting away, her voice growing smaller and smaller.)\nAnd... I'm sorry. I kept so many things from you...",
    ["Dialogue1184703"]="Then... let's go together! Once we're back in Juno—me, you, Farbauti, Laufey... and you too, Madelina! You're coming with us, okay?\nBaroshev",
    ["Dialogue1184704"]="Of course, I'll come with you. Once we leave this place, we'll never have to be apart again.\n(Madelina tilts her head with a gentle smile, but something about it feels like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>farewell</color>...)\nI've already figured out how we can escape. I just need a bit of help from you, Adventurer... and the knight...",
    ["Dialogue1184705"]="It's fine. What do you need us to do?",
    ["Dialogue1184706"]="I need you to head to the central control room and cut off the core hub's power. Once it's down, the facility will switch to emergency mode, and all exits will <color=#CA2E0AFF>briefly unlock</color> for evacuation. But we can't leave through the main gate since Lighthalzen is still heavily guarded by Rekenber Corp...",
    ["Dialogue1184707"]="So, I plan to leave through the northeastern gate of the facility, which leads to some ruins called the Tomb of the Fallen. I'll wait for you there. But once emergency mode activates, the devices holding the <color=#CA2E0AFF>experimental subjects</color> will lose power too... so be careful, both of you.",
    ["Dialogue1184801"]="Adventurer, before we leave... there's one last thing I need to do. My <color=#CA2E0AFF>comrades</color>... they're still trapped inside those capsule tanks, neither alive nor dead...",
    ["Dialogue1184802"]="(After the power shuts down, red warning lights flood the facility. In the dim glow, you can't see Seyren's face.)\n... I want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give them peace</color>—to let their souls return to Odin's embrace and finally rest...",
    ["Dialogue1184901"]="... Thank you for helping me finish this, Adventurer. Now... it's my turn to <color=#CA2E0AFF>repay you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue1185001"]="(Beside the shattered tank, the girl's hologram smiles warmly at you.)\nHello, Martistine. Hello, Adventurer. I've been waiting... for the chance to speak with you face to face.",
    ["Dialogue1185002"]="Made... lina? What... what's going on? You said you were right here...\n(Martistine looks around in confusion, her voice trembling.)\nWhere are you? Where are you hiding?! Come out—!",
    ["Dialogue1185003"]="I'm sorry, Martistine. I lied to you. Your sister, Madelina... she passed away long ago. I'm just an AI built from all her biological data. You probably remember—though you were twins, her body was always fragile. The doctors said she wouldn't live past ten... and that's why I exist.",
    ["Dialogue1185004"]="Your parents couldn't bear to watch their daughter die, so they secretly used the lab's resources to create a bionic copy of Madelina. But Baroshev found out. They were punished, and both you and Madelina became his experimental subjects. Later, he implanted Madelina's soul into your body. Against all odds, the two of you managed to coexist with two minds in a single body...",
    ["Dialogue1185005"]="... Yes! He said it was the only way to save you! Your body was already ruined. He said if I agreed to share it with you, at least your soul could live on—",
    ["Dialogue1185006"]="That was a lie, Martistine.\n(She cuts off Martistine's cries, her words are sharp and cold.)\nMadelina never survived that experiment, and she died on the operating table.",
    ["Dialogue1185007"]="Baroshev didn't care about her life—he just couldn't stand his experiment failing. So he turned to me... He implanted my terminal inside your body, just to see what would happen... That's the whole truth.",
    ["Dialogue1185008"]="... You mean—you've been pretending to be Madelina all these years? Lying to me, making me think my sister was still alive?\n<size=26>I don't believe you! What's the point of that?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue1185009"]="Because... <color=#CA2E0AFF>protecting you</color> is my highest directive.\n(The girl's hologram kneels, lifting her hand as if to hold Martistine in her arms.)",
    ["Dialogue1185010"]="Madelina's only wish was for you to live a happy life. And since I inherited all her data, I've made that my top priority—no matter the cost.",
    ["Dialogue1185011"]="(You try to speak, but the girl raises a finger to her lips, signaling for silence. The ruined lab is filled only with the sound of Martistine's quiet sobs.)\n... Martistine, once I send you both out of here, you'll have plenty of time to cry and to mourn Madelina. But right now... I need you to stay strong, okay?",
    ["Dialogue1185012"]="This ruin used to be an old research facility destroyed two hundred years ago during the mercenary uprising. Its drainage system is still connected to the new one, leading all the way to Einbroch, near Lighthalzen. All you need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the drain valve</color> and check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>water level monitor</color> to make sure the sewage is cleared, then you can escape through the pipes. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>password</color> to activate the valve has been carved onto Farbauti and Laufey... Can I leave this to you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue1185101"]="Thank you, Adventurer. And finally... please take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>core</color> from the tank. It's my gift to you.",
    ["Dialogue1185201"]="I know you've been searching for a replica of Ymir's Heart, but I'm sorry—the finished models are stored in Rekenber Corp's main vault. Only Baroshev and the director can access it. As a substitute, I managed to decode part of the project's data and stored everything I could reproduce inside this core...",
    ["Dialogue1185202"]="... I trust you'll use it where it truly belongs, right?",
    ["Dialogue1185301"]="(At the Juno airship station, a man in a researcher's coat steps in front of you.)\nHello, Adventurer. A pleasure to finally meet you. I'm Blues Werner—Director of the Rekensheim Institute and Baroshev's immediate superior. Tell me... did you enjoy the little performance we prepared for you?",
    ["Dialogue1185302"]="Hmm... look at that surprised face. Seems he did a decent job. At the very least, he hasn't let down our distinguished Successor of Odin's bloodline, wouldn't you agree?",
    ["Dialogue1185303"]="Hey, easy there, Adventurer.\n(He waves a hand and steps back, grinning from ear to ear.)",
    ["Dialogue1185304"]="You should know, we're here on behalf of Rekenber Corp, meeting with the Lord himself. If I were attacked in public by the Successor of Odin's Bloodline... not only would the Lord be held responsible, but your entire kingdom would be dragged into it. If you really want to start a war...",
    ["Dialogue1185305"]="(He pulls a small <color=#CA2E0AFF>core</color> from his breast pocket, tossing it lightly in the air and catching it again.)\n... Tell me, Adventurer—do you think Rekenber Corp has the power to wipe you all out in one move?",
    ["Dialogue1185306"]="Just saying hello, Adventurer. President Rowland and I have heard plenty about your exploits, and we admire your sharp mind and bravery. So tell me, would you be interested in working with us? Rekenber Corp can reward its allies with fortunes... far beyond your imagination.",
    ["Dialogue1185307"]="No need to answer right away, Adventurer. We have time—think it over. If you change your mind, feel free to contact me anytime.\n(He leans forward, lowering his voice as he slips a business card into your pocket.)\n... I'll be waiting for the day to come, Successor of Odin's Bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue1185401"]="... I'm sorry for worrying you.\n(Martistine lowers her head, gently brushing the robot's flickering light.)\nIt's okay now. I'm not leaving you two again.",
    ["Dialogue1185402"]="... Don't worry about me, Adventurer. I understand everything Madelina said... I won't let her down.\n(She looks up at you, eyes shimmering with tears.)\nAnd—you'll make those people pay, right?",
    ["Dialogue1185403"]="Of course, I trust you... So, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>do what you need to do</color>. Those people... they're probably still in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color>, waiting for your report...\n(She glances at your pocket—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mech Core</color> rests quietly inside.)\nPlease... don't let my sister's sacrifice be in vain.",
    ["Dialogue1185501"]="(In the Lord's quarters, all three turn to you in shock, clearly astonished to see you alive.)\nYou... you're okay, Adventurer? We thought...",
    ["Dialogue1185502"]="... That something happened to you, Adventurer. You wouldn't believe this—just moments ago, we got words that Priest Yus has started a <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebellion</color> at Torr Volcano.",
    ["Dialogue1185503"]="He's declared war on the temple and claimed the current Pope isn't the goddess incarnation, demanding her resignation and a new election...\n(Philodis grips the paper tightly, you can just make out the emblem of the Arunafeltz stamped on it.)\nThis proclamation has already spread across the entire Arunafeltz.",
    ["Dialogue1185504"]="It‘s clear now... He planned this all along. We thought the conservatives gained the upper hand during the Dawn Moon, but looking at it now... it might've all been a trap carefully laid by Yus. To gain the rebels' support, Malam and Neirun passed a decree abolishing slavery, but a lot of nobles weren't happy about it...",
    ["Dialogue1185505"]="And now, Yus is openly questioning the Pope's legitimacy, pushing many neutral nobles to switch sides. Public opinion's turned hard against the conservatives, and with Rekenber Corp supplying them with weapons and resources... they're really hanging by a thread.",
    ["Dialogue1185506"]="... I understand what you mean, Adventurer. But I'm sorry, the cabinet's already been infiltrated by Rekenber Corp. Even if I propose a decree, they would just reject it and claim that it is not our place to meddle in another nation's strife.",
    ["Dialogue1185507"]="(The Lord lowers his head slightly, lost in thought.)\nUnless... we can find solid proof that Rekenber Corp is the one pulling the strings behind this war...",
    ["Dialogue1185508"]="Wait—you're saying... You actually got the replica of Ymir's Heart from Baroshev?!\n(Professor Fulkyn's eyes light up with sudden hope.)\nQuick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>let me see it</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue1185601"]="... Unbelievable. Baroshev, he's a real lunatic... and a real genius...\n(Staring at the massive stream of data pouring from the Mysterious Device, Fulkyn shakes his head grimly.)",
    ["Dialogue1185602"]="... He made a key—a key that can unlock the full potential of the human body. You probably know that the human body has its own <color=#CA2E0AFF>self-protection system</color>. Take my Mysterious Device here, for example...",
    ["Dialogue1185603"]="(Fulkyn taps lightly on the device's panel, pointing to the progress bar at the top.)\nThink of it like a person. In daily operation, I usually only use about 70–80% of its capacity, to preserve its lifespan...",
    ["Dialogue1185604"]="The same goes for the human body. If you keep running it at 100%, or worse, push it past that, it'll burn out, aging and dying fast. That's why the brain keeps your body in check, only lifting the limit when adrenaline kicks in under extreme conditions...",
    ["Dialogue1185605"]="... Looks like you've seen it before, haven't you?",
    ["Dialogue1185606"]="Then my theory was right. Baroshev implanted a replica of Ymir's Heart into the human body, removing the brain's limiter and unlocking explosive strength for a short time... But that kind of power comes at a terrible cost—irreversible damage to the body. If I'm not mistaken, your friends must have already...",
    ["Dialogue1185607"]="(Fulkyn pauses, then gently pats your shoulder.)\n... My condolences, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue1185608"]="The data inside this core is massive, and my Mysterious Device has only just started processing it. For now, I can't say for sure if we'll find the evidence needed to bring Rekenber Corp down...",
    ["Dialogue1185609"]="(The young professor looks up at the leader of the Republic.)\nI need more time, Lord Carl.",
    ["Dialogue1185610"]="You mean... we have to find a way to stall Priest Yus' offensive? But the cabinet will never approve sending troops...",
    ["Dialogue1185611"]="Wait, Lord Carl. Maybe... we don't need the cabinet's approval... Remember? After the <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebellion</color>, the Republic cut ties with them and built its own Guards. However, from what I know, they've still been working with groups all across the continent...",
    ["Dialogue1185612"]="And most importantly... <color=#CA2E0AFF>they absolutely hate Rekenber Corp</color>.\n(Philodis adjusts his glasses, a sly grin spreading across his face.)\nThe enemy of our enemy... is our friend, right?",
    ["Dialogue1185613"]="You mean... the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tyr Mercenary</color>?\n(The Lord looks surprised for a moment, then breaks into a grin.)\nGood idea, Philodis.",
    ["Dialogue1185614"]="I remember they've worked with the Khayr Consortium before. Why not let your teacher out of prison for some fresh air? The Republic's only consortium that can rival Rekenber Corp should be able to offer a reward they'll find... satisfying, don't you think?\n(From just a few words exchanged, you realize—a <color=#CA2E0AFF>prison break</color> plan has already taken shape.)",
    ["Dialogue1185615"]="Don't rush, Adventurer. Right now, what you need most... is <color=#CA2E0AFF>rest</color>.\nYour journey through Lighthalzen must've worn you out. Even as the Successor of Odin's Bloodline, you shouldn't keep pushing yourself. You've done your part—let us handle the rest, alright?",
    ["Dialogue1185616"]="I agree, Adventurer. You should take a break and get some decent sleep. Once Professor Fulkyn finishes analyzing the core, we'll move to the next phase, and we'll definitely need your help. So until that time—<color=#CA2E0AFF>recover</color>, and be ready.",
    ["Dialogue1190101"]="(Farbauti's round belly bears several old scratches. The edges are smooth and overlapping, clearly <color=#CA2E0AFF>not caused by transport damage</color>. Looking closer, you can faintly make out a few <color=#CA2E0AFF>numbers</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1190201"]="(Laufey's arm also bears several old scratches. The edges are smooth and overlapping, <color=#CA2E0AFF>not caused by transport damage</color> either. Looking closer, you can faintly make out a few <color=#CA2E0AFF>numbers</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1190301"]="(The old pipe is covered with rust and water stains. At the far end, you can just make out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>faint glimmer of light</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1190401"]="(You crouch at the blind spot by the door, holding your breath. To your surprise, the hallway outside the storage room is <color=#CA2E0AFF>completely empty</color>...?)",
    ["Dialogue1190501"]="(The once-splendid reception hall is eerily silent. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dust coats the tables and chairs</color>—it seems no one has cleaned the place for quite a while...)",
    ["Dialogue1190601"]="(The massive capsule tank is filled with luminescent liquid that looks disturbingly eerie...)",
    ["Dialogue1190701"]="(There are two beds in the room, one clearly slept in, the other neatly made. Seems like either Zenlur or Ivy didn't come back last night...)",
    ["Dialogue1190801"]="(A thin layer of dust covers the bookshelf. At the edge, you spot a small handprint—too delicate to belong to a grown man, more like a woman's...)",
    ["Dialogue1190901"]="(The frame's glass isn't clean, kind of cloudy, and when you touch it, it feels slick, like... some kind of oil?)",
    ["Dialogue1191001"]="(The water's surface is perfectly still and you can see your reflection crystal clear...)",
    ["Dialogue1191101"]="(Some sort of liquid is spilled on the stairs to the incubation pool—you almost <color=#CA2E0AFF>slip</color>, but Goldie reacts fast enough to grab you...)",
    ["Dialogue1191201"]="(A heavy iron door looms before you. You try to push it, but it won't budge. Beside it, there's a small screen, probably a password <color=#CA2E0AFF>terminal</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue1191301"]="(Various bottles and jars are scattered inside the cupboard. The Vegetable Oil sits near the edge. You pick it up, and it's lighter than expected... Has it almost been <color=#CA2E0AFF>used up</color>?)",
    ["Dialogue1191401"]="(Once you're out of Baroshev's sight, you pick up a tiny <color=#CA2E0AFF>bell</color> lying beside Goldie's body. During the fight, Ygnizem had quietly nudged it toward the library door with her sword...)",
    ["Dialogue1191501"]="(In the dim cell stands a huge capsule tank marked with the number 4. Inside, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Howard</color> is submerged in a glowing, eerie liquid—you can just make out the faint rise and fall of his chest...)",
    ["Dialogue1191502"]="(You and Seyren try to wake Howard, but his eyes stay shut, no response at all...)",
    ["Dialogue1191601"]="(<color=#CA2E0AFF>Trisse's</color> petite figure contrasts sharply with the massive tank. She's curled up slightly, like a child in her mother's embrace...)",
    ["Dialogue1191701"]="(Just like Howard, this capsule tank holds another familiar face—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Kavaski</color>. You and Seyren try to wake him, but he too, remains motionless, eyes closed. Only the faint rise and fall of his chest tells you he's still alive...)",
    ["Dialogue1191801"]="(In the capsule tank marked with the number 1, you see the handsome face of the Bard. The silver ring still gleams on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orfeo's</color> ring finger... but you'll never see his wedding with Trinity...)",
    ["Dialogue1191901"]="(The room is a complete mess as if a fierce battle took place. At first glance, you can't find the black bottle Madelina mentioned...)",
    ["Dialogue1192001"]="(The storage cabinet's glass is shattered, and the potions are spilled everywhere, completely unusable now...)",
    ["Dialogue1192101"]="(You search every corner where a potion could be stored, and finally, in the drawer's corner, you find an unopened bottle of Acid Solvent...)",
    ["Dialogue1192201"]="(The valve is covered in rust—it hasn't been used in ages. You strain with all your strength until it finally turns...)",
    ["Dialogue1192301"]="(A dull click echoes as the switch turns—the monitor's gauge drops into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>green</color> zone...)",
    ["Dialogue1192401"]="(The old screen is cracked all over, and the keyboard is barely visible. Relying on memory, you enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>numbers</color> carved on Farbauti and Laufey in sequence...)",
    ["Dialogue1225601"]="Warning! Eligible information not found. Please enter again. Warning! Eligible information not found. Please enter again. Warning! Eligible...",
    ["Dialogue1225701"]="(The lawn is bestrewn with footprints of various shapes, of humans and monsters. They are overlapping each other, making it difficult to sort out the traces...)",
    ["Dialogue1225801"]="(A lone wrecked wall sits before you, seeming to have collapsed under the impact of some sort of mysterious power. Besides this, there are no other clues...)",
    ["Dialogue1225901"]="The mossy side wall of the well is carved with some unknown runes. When you reach the runes with your hand, an onrushing river of stars dashes across your eyes, as if you have just witnessed the entire course of the world, from creation to destruction...",
    ["Dialogue1225902"]="You are familiar with this power. It constantly resonates with your blood. You recall the prophecy of the Mirror Lake and the Goddess' warning. Could there be another Fragment of Ymir's Heart existing in the world?",
    ["Dialogue1225903"]="Maybe it's the power of Ymir's Heart that drives the monsters here deranged? You can't prove your speculation, but you can take a photo of this dry well and discuss it with Andre...",
    ["Dialogue1226001"]="What happened in the estate after Kiel Khayr went missing?",
    ["Dialogue1226101"]="What is the root cause that turns Kiel Khayr's Estate into its current situation?",
    ["Dialogue1226201"]="What's the evidence that associates Kiel Khayr's disappearance with the androids?",
    ["Dialogue1226301"]="You ready? Let's sort things out from the beginning.",
    ["Dialogue1226401"]="No, it doesn't sound right. Think again.",
    ["Dialogue1226501"]="Yes, this is it!",
    ["Dialogue1408331101"]="Hey! Happy New Year, Adventurer! I have a lot of goodies here, come and have a look!",
    ["Dialogue1408331102"]="You wanna play Guess the Hat? Then let me tell you the rules of the game~\nWatch carefully to see which cool hats I throw <color=#ff5252>flaming bottles</color> at!\nBe careful, they will <color=#ff5252>explode</color>!\nHide near the <color=#528fff>hats without flaming bottles</color> and try to stay alive!",
    ["Dialogue1408331103"]="<color=#ffe788>Please find the hat without the flaming bottle and hide under it!</color>",
    ["Dialogue18005601"]="Happy New Year",
    ["Dialogue2000101"]="(Jacob's face is all red as he clenches his fists.)\n<size=18>Sigh, when will I be brave enough? </size><size=18>Quick, take a step, Jacob! </size><size=18>This is a small step for you, </size><size=18>but a big step for mankind!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2000102"]="<size=24>Ahh! </size><size=24>Y-you gave me a heart attack!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2000103"]="...Um, I was just wondering how I can approach the kids in the choir. I've just moved to Izlude Island with my dad; I haven't got a single friend here, and I don't know how to make any. But I saw those kids in the choir and I really want to join them.",
    ["Dialogue2000104"]="...Ah? No way! I don't know what kind of nursery rhymes people in Izlude Island sing! I don't even dare to move any closer to them, let alone speak to them. Um... Why not... Could you maybe help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out what song they're singing</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2000201"]="(Beasley bobs his head as he sings.)\n<size=18>La lala la ♪</size>",
    ["Dialogue2000202"]="I don't want to talk about nursery rhymes; I want to talk about something more interesting! Have you heard about the latest craze for keeping pets? Rumor has it that even Porings can be kept as pets now. But I don't like Porings. They're too soft; so unmanly!",
    ["Dialogue2000203"]="Hmm, I think a Frog would be a good choice of pet. If you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>get me a Frog</color>, I'll consider talking to you about nursery rhymes!",
    ["Dialogue2000301"]="Wow! You got one! Hehe! Hey little froggy, since you look so delicious... Ah no. Since you look so cute, let's be friends till it's time for Mom to make dinner!",
    ["Dialogue2000302"]="...Weird. Why would an adult want to know about nursery rhymes? But I guess there's no harm in telling you. The first line is: <color=#CA2E0AFF>A giant serpent swallowing the sea ♪</color>. As for the rest of the lyrics? Hehe! They're not sung by me!\n(Beasley makes a funny face at you.)",
    ["Dialogue2000401"]="(Peppy wipes his snot as he sings.)\n<size=18>La lala la ♪</size>",
    ["Dialogue2000402"]="*Sniffs* What ya say? Nursery rhyme? ...Speaking of nursery rhymes, there's a great one about a cave; I can't get it out of my head. I guess it's cos my papa works in a cave! Have ya ever seen the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sparkly gemstones</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Wings Mine</color>? My instructor loves 'em! Go get one for me!",
    ["Dialogue2000501"]="Wow! These sparkly gemstones are so pretty! No wonder Instructor Hamid wants 'em! *Sniffs* You've heard about Instructor Hamid, right? He's a world-famous businessman! And he's sooo nice to all the kids on Izlude Island. He always asks us to trade these sparkly gemstones with him for candy. Ya can get one candy for only five gems. Ain't he great!",
    ["Dialogue2000502"]="Oh, you wanted to know the lyrics to the nursery rhyme! Of course I'll tell ya. The second line is: <color=#CA2E0AFF>A giant serpent swallowing the sea ♪</color> Hmm... What's the next line? Um... The next line is...\n(Peppy stares blankly into space.)",
    ["Dialogue2000601"]="(Lily claps her hands as she sings.)\n<size=18>La lala la ♪</size>",
    ["Dialogue2000602"]="Do you like this nursery rhyme? I do! But I like Grandpa's pumpkins even more. Did you know? My grandpa is the best farmer in Prontera! Every year, he brings so many pumpkins that me and Mommy can't finish them!",
    ["Dialogue2000603"]="Um... But Grandpa got sick; we haven't heard from him for a while. Lately I've been so worried that I can't sleep. If someone can bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pumpkin</color>, maybe I won't miss him so much!",
    ["Dialogue2000701"]="I-isn't this a pumpkin from Grandpa's Green Cotton Farm? You're awesome! I'll use it to make something tasty and take it over to Grandpa! But what should I make? Ah, I'll cook the bat wing and pumpkin stew that mommy taught me! It's really nutritious! I'll give some to you when it's done!",
    ["Dialogue2000702"]="You don't want it? Alright then... As promised, I'll tell you the third line of the nursery rhyme. It's: <color=#CA2E0AFF>A rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead ♪</color>. If you've learned the song, you're welcome to sing it with us!",
    ["Dialogue2000801"]="(Rayns dances around as he sings... but it's so out of tune, you can't tell what he's singing.)\n#$~%&*@~ ♪",
    ["Dialogue2000802"]="Oh! You want to learn this nursery rhyme? Of course I'll teach you! Ah... But I can't remember anything clearly when I'm hungry. If you can get me something yummy... like the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora Prawns</color>, I'll definitely be able to remember the last line!",
    ["Dialogue2000901"]="Ah! That smell! It's... it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora Prawns</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2000902"]="The last line of the nursery rhyme is: <color=#CA2E0AFF>And made a nest upon the sea ♪</color> Wow! I finally get to taste this legendary dish! They say the prawns completely absorb the fragrance of the Mandragora Leaves, so when you take a bite, it's like an explosion of flavor in your mouth.",
    ["Dialogue2000903"]="Ah! Why do I have tears in my eyes? Because...\n<size=24>this dish is AMAZING!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2001001"]="Y-you've learned the nursery rhyme? That's great! Quick, teach it to me!",
    ["Dialogue2001002"]="A giant serpent swallowing the sea ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001003"]="A giant serpent swallowing the sea ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001004"]="A rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001005"]="And made a nest upon the sea ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001006"]="Wow! It's so catchy! I won't have any trouble remembering it! I can finally join the choir now. Ah, but before that, I need to prove to them that I've learned the song. Um, could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>come to the garden with me</color> when I sing it for them? I won't be a nervous if you're there with me!",
    ["Dialogue2001101"]="(Jacob tugs on the hem of his shirt shyly.)\nI-I've finished singing. I've finally learned this nursery rhyme!",
    ["Dialogue2001102"]="<size=24>Ohhh! </size><size=24>You sang really well! </size><size=24>It lit up my soul!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2001103"]="So you were just shy; that's why you didn't sing the last time! *Sniffs*",
    ["Dialogue2001104"]="Let's invite Jacob to join the choir and perform together at the market next week!",
    ["Dialogue2001105"]="Yeah, that would be great!",
    ["Dialogue2001201"]="Ahh! Friendship between children is so innocent and wonderful! I think whoever wrote this song would be very happy to know that it helped build such friendship!",
    ["Dialogue2001202"]="...Oh? Don't you know? The lyrics are from a poem called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Legend of the Kingdom's Founding</color>. It depicts the founding of the Rune Kingdom. Even my mentor is in awe of the metaphors hidden within it! If you're interested, I can sing it for you using modern-day language! Then you'll be able to understand what it's trying to express!",
    ["Dialogue2001203"]="(Morts takes out his lute smugly.)\nAs the Age of Gods came to an end, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jormungand</color> preyed upon the land ♪\nA legendary hero, named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tristan</color>, has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>rainbow-colored eagle</color> crest. He is none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>the founder of the Gaebolg Family</color> ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001204"]="He led six other adventurers to attack the giant serpent and took its head. He was crowned the first king in the afterglow of dusk ♪\nHe established the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom, and declared the capital at the plains where Jormungand fell, naming it Prontera ♪\nThe Gaebolg family ruled over the other six adventurers' families, and they were known to the world as...<color=#CA2E0AFF>the seven royal families</color> ♪",
    ["Dialogue2001205"]="How was it? My singing is most exquisite, don't you agree? Sigh, it's a pity this isn't the complete Legend of the Kingdom's Founding. If we could recover the entire poem and write it into a song, I'm sure it would be even more amazing and the world would sing it for generations to come!",
    ["Dialogue2001206"]="Regrettably, what I sang was only the first half. It's said that there's a second half that tells of an even more secretive history. Could you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Library</color> and try to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second half of Legend of the Kingdom's Founding</color> for me? As a bard, it kills me to not know the full story!",
    ["Dialogue2001301"]="Adventurer, I saw you reading Legend of the Kingdom's Founding! It's strange; that book has been getting a lot of attention lately.",
    ["Dialogue2001302"]="Huh? Who was the last person to borrow it? Haha! I don't even need to check the records to tell you that! It was <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni Briar</color>, the exorcist priestess who serves the Gaebolg Family! I remember it well because she looked unusually worried when she borrowed the book. I've never seen her look so uneasy. It's most worrying!",
    ["Dialogue2001303"]="Where is Parni? High priests and priestesses usually gather at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Church</color>. If you do see her, please send my regards!",
    ["Dialogue2001304"]="<size=18>Come to think of it, before Parni, </size><size=18><color=#CA2E0AFF>Ian Walter's attendant</color> asked about this book too. </size><size=18>But he just flicked through it at the shelf and left empty-handed. </size><size=18>I guess he probably wasn't interested in what was inside.</size>",
    ["Dialogue2001401"]="<size=18>Sigh... </size><size=18>How did something like this happen? </size><size=18>How did an outstanding exorcist priestess like Parni </size><size=18>get banished from the palace?</size>",
    ["Dialogue2001402"]="...Ah! Excuse me, I was talking to myself! But I'm sure you must have been just as shocked by the news? Parni is the best exorcist priestess in Rune Kingdom. Even Archbishop Wolmas is always praising her integrity and intelligence. But a few days ago, <color=#CA2E0AFF>His Majesty the King</color> banished her from the palace! It's baffling!",
    ["Dialogue2001403"]="I've been trying to talk to her these last few days, but no matter how I ask, she refuses to give me a proper answer. She's shut herself away in her room studying a book called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Legend of the Kingdom's Founding</color>. I wonder if that book has anything to do with what happened?",
    ["Dialogue2001404"]="As punishment, the royal family is making her guard the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery behind the cathedral</color>. Poor thing... Such a fall from grace can't be easy. Sadly there's nothing I can do for her.",
    ["Dialogue2001501"]="(Parni's hands are joined. She seems to be praying.)\n<size=18>The true devil often exists in the heart of man. </size><size=18>I pray for Odin's salvation. </size><size=18>May the truth come to light </size><size=18>and may their souls rest in peace.</size>",
    ["Dialogue2001502"]="...Adventurer, since you've come looking for me, I can only assume you wish to find out about the second half of Legend of the Kingdom's Founding? I'm not obliged to tell a stranger, and I don't think you'll be able to comprehend my answer. If you truly wish to discuss it further, then go <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean the three tombstones engraved with golden crosses</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2001601"]="Adventurer, I purposely left this diary on the ground for you to read. Now that you've read both the diary and the words on the tombstones, what are your thoughts on the deaths of the three princes of the Gaebolg Family?",
    ["Dialogue2001602"]="Hmph! I never expected your view to echo that of the royal family. Since we are unable to trust each other, there's nothing left to say. I'll uncover the truth behind the princes' deaths on my own.",
    ["Dialogue2001603"]="Great, it seems you're not fooled by appearances. The truth is, the princes certainly did not die as a result of a failed exorcism. I know this because the evidence is hidden in the second half of Legend of the Kingdom's Founding. Since you've chosen to trust me, I'll tell you both the text and the secrets within. I hope you'll help me investigate the truth behind the princes' deaths.",
    ["Dialogue2001604"]="The second half of Legend of the Kingdom's Founding reads: <color=#CA2E0AFF>A giant serpent swallowing the sea; a giant serpent swallowing the sea; a rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead. Scales started to grow on the haughty eagle, after which it fell from the sky and died.</color> The last two lines of the poem hold a secret that the royal family is unwilling to mention: that the evil serpent Jormungand placed a <color=#CA2E0AFF>curse</color> on the Gaebolg Family before it died, a curse that causes <color=#CA2E0AFF>the eldest son of each generation to die from snake venom</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2001605"]="I was just as shocked as you when I first found out. But the curse can only account for the death of Nate, the eldest prince. It can't explain why Prince Reige and Prince Hans died as well! Since all three princes died on the same day, maybe someone was trying to confuse everyone and make it look like the other two princes died of the curse as well. But in order to prove this theory, I'll need to use some unorthodox methods.",
    ["Dialogue2001606"]="Adventurer, could you bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eyes of Truth</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysts</color>? It is said that they are able to observe and reveal the truth. I believe they will help in our investigation!",
    ["Dialogue2001701"]="Great, this is what I need. Next, I need to use these Eyes of Truth to make a potion that can reveal what's real and what's not. Could you get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yellow Gemstones</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2001801"]="Great! We're all set. The truth lies beneath the <color=#CA2E0AFF>church</color>. Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue2001901"]="This is the place. There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>hidden passageway</color> in the church that leads to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underground tomb of the Gaebolg Family</color>. We shouldn't really be doing this because no one is allowed to disturb the resting bodies of the princes. But to reveal the truth, we have no other choice! Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue2001902"]="Well then, tread as quietly as you can.",
    ["Dialogue2001903"]="Alright, but we mustn't hesitate for too long.",
    ["Dialogue2002001"]="According to the second half of Legend of the Kingdom's Founding, a prince who dies of the serpent's curse will have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>snake scale mark</color> on his body. <color=#CA2E0AFF>check if the three bodies have the mark</color> and let me know what you find.",
    ["Dialogue2002101"]="So unlike Prince Nate, the snake scale marks on Prince Reige and Prince Hans are lighter and blurry? This is indeed suspicious. Try <color=#CA2E0AFF>splashing the Truth Serum I made onto Prince Hans' body</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2002201"]="Oh no, we've alerted the guards! It won't be long before someone comes to check. We can't stay any longer. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave the tomb</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back to the church</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2002301"]="We can finally speak now. I'm sure you noticed the strange reaction after splashing the Truth Serum onto Prince Hans' body? The snake scale mark on his body mysteriously disappeared, which proves my theory: Prince Hans and Prince Reige did not die of the serpent's curse, but rather, <color=#CA2E0AFF>they were poisoned</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>someone made it look like they died of the curse</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2002302"]="This would explain why my exorcism failed. Because even the most powerful exorcist can only exorcise the demon within a person's body. When it comes to the demons within an evil person's heart, no amount of magic can exorcise them!",
    ["Dialogue2002303"]="I've thought about this question. Security in the palace is tight, so only someone close to the princes would have had the opportunity to poison them. Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate someone called Oman</color>? He used to be Prince Hans' attendant, but hastily quit on the day the prince died and returned to his home outside the palace. His behavior is really suspicious. He might be hiding something!",
    ["Dialogue2002401"]="<size=18>Sigh, how long is it going to take to save enough money for Abu's treatment? </size><size=18>By Odin, </size><size=18>as long as my son can get better, </size><size=18>I'm willing to do anything! </size><size=18>Anything at all!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2002402"]="(Helena looks at you warily.)\nW-who told you Oman lives here? Ah! N-no, there no one by that name here! You must have the wrong place. If there's nothing else, p-please excuse me.",
    ["Dialogue2002501"]="Great, your investigation has brought us one step closer to the truth! Things are getting clearer now. Oman's son is very ill, so someone exploited the fact that Oman needs money for treatment to get him to do something. Whatever it was, it probably has something to do with the poisoning. If I'm right, then whoever's behind this is truly despicable!",
    ["Dialogue2002502"]="Adventurer, find a rare leaf called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Leaf of Yggdrasil</color> as soon as possible and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to Oman's wife, Helena</color>. Tell her we're willing to provide all the help her family needs and in return, we hope that Oman can provide us with the information that we need.",
    ["Dialogue2002601"]="Oh my! Merciful Odin, you must have heard my prayers! You have sent your blessings through this generous soul! From now on, our family will be even more pious, and we will pray for this kindhearted adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2002602"]="...Ah? A-aren't you the adventurer who came asking about my husband? He doesn't want me to let anybody know where he is, but you're a savior sent by Odin; we mustn't refuse your request.",
    ["Dialogue2002603"]="To be honest, I don't know what happened in the palace. I only know that ever since my husband returned, he's been hiding in the storeroom and refuses to see anyone. He also looks very on edge. If you wish to speak to him, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait outside the storeroom after sundown</color>; I'll do my best to persuade him to come out and see you!",
    ["Dialogue2002701"]="...What?! Poor Oman. Sigh. Whoever's behind all this is not only very cunning, but also incredibly ruthless. I'm afraid he won't leave any loose ends. I can't imagine what terrible things he might do next.",
    ["Dialogue2002702"]="Adventurer, this is all my savings. Please give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Helena</color> and persuade her to leave this dangerous place!",
    ["Dialogue2002801"]="...Oh, I never would have thought the one to help us during this difficult time would be High Priestess Parni. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>send her my respect and gratitude</color>! Don't worry, I'll get Abu out of Prontera and find a safe place for us to settle down. Now that Oman is gone, I need to become stronger. He's always been our rock, but from now on... I have to be that for Abu!",
    ["Dialogue2002901"]="...I'm relieved to know that they've got away. Sigh, although Oman did have a hand in the princes' deaths, he and his family are also victims in all this.",
    ["Dialogue2002902"]="Ultimately, the most unforgivable person is the culprit who used other people for his dirty deeds! Thankfully we now have undeniable proof. As long as we can present this <color=#CA2E0AFF>poison bottle</color> to His Majesty the King, we'll be able to request the Kingdom Defense Force's help in finding the person responsible. But I've been forbidden from entering the palace; could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take the evidence to His Majesty and explain the situation</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2003001"]="Stop! These are the palace grounds; no unauthorized persons allowed!",
    ["Dialogue2003002"]="...A commoner may not seek an audience with His Majesty! Please leave immediately, otherwise... Wait a minute. Haven't I seen you before? You... Are you the hero who helped the Defense Force and Chivalry eliminate the monsters and was honored in an award ceremony in front of the palace?!",
    ["Dialogue2003003"]="Sorry, I didn't realize it was you! Actually His Majesty had expressed his interest in meeting you many times since hearing about the award ceremony. His Majesty would love to hear you personally recount your adventure. Would you be so kind as to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me into the palace</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2003004"]="Well then, please allow me to lead the way.",
    ["Dialogue2003005"]="I await your order.",
    ["Dialogue2003101"]="Please wait here while I announce your arrival!",
    ["Dialogue2003201"]="Please follow me. The regent is available to see you on behalf of His Majesty!",
    ["Dialogue2003202"]="Since the death of the princes, His Majesty has been in mourning and hasn't been attending court. The regent is currently taking care of all matters in the kingdom on behalf of His Majesty. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>. The regent doesn't like to be kept waiting!",
    ["Dialogue2003301"]="(Ian Walter looks at you with confusion.)\n...Could you kindly explain what exactly this is?",
    ["Dialogue2003302"]="...You are saying that Prince Reige and Prince Hans did not die of the curse but were in fact poisoned by someone? This is a very important discovery. It appears we need to reevaluate our previous conclusion and relaunch the investigation based on this new evidence.",
    ["Dialogue2003303"]="Do not worry. I will lead the Royal Chivalry in finding the one responsible for the princes' deaths. In the meantime, however, I ask that you keep your lips sealed and do not make this known to anyone. I know someone as wise and intelligent as you can appreciate the need to keep all details strictly confidential, and that any leak would cause political turmoil throughout the kingdom?",
    ["Dialogue2003304"]="Ah yes, I suggest you also inform the person who led you to this investigation of what I just said. Unless I'm mistaken, that would be the former exorcist priestess, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni Briar</color>? Tell her that she would do well to mind her own business. Such matters are out of her jurisdiction; I will take care of them.",
    ["Dialogue2003401"]="...So that's what happened at the palace? Ha, I see...\n(A sudden look of realization hits Parni.)",
    ["Dialogue2003402"]="(Parni shakes her head with a bitter smile.)\nAdventurer, please don't investigate any further. The demise of the princes is merely the start of Rune-Midgarts Kingdom's unrest. The real disaster is yet to come. Neither of us can stop what is about to happen; we can only wait and see.",
    ["Dialogue2003501"]="AW 976 – AW 1000 XX/01\nHere lies the eldest son of Tristan III. Odin will take away the curse and leave peace.",
    ["Dialogue2003601"]="AW 979 – AW 1000 XX/01\nHere lies the second son of Tristan III. The kingdom once had high hopes for him, but he now has eternal peace.",
    ["Dialogue2003701"]="AW 980 – AW 1000 XX/01\nHere lies the youngest son of Tristan III. Destiny had bestowed on him a glorious life. It is a great sadness that he was unable able to live it to the fullest.",
    ["Dialogue2003801"]="(There's a dark green snake scale mark on Nate Gaebolg's chest. This must be the curse that Parni mentioned.)",
    ["Dialogue2003901"]="(There's a snake scale mark on Reige Gaebolg's chest. But on closer inspection, not only is its color lighter than Nate's mark, its shape is also a little blurry.)",
    ["Dialogue2004001"]="(There's a snake scale mark on Hans Gaebolg's chest. But on closer inspection, not only is its color lighter than Nate's mark, its shape is also a little blurry.)",
    ["Dialogue2004101"]="(You pour the bubbling Truth Serum onto Prince Hans' body. There is a loud sizzling sound and something shocking happens: The snake scale mark on the prince's chest starts to disappear!)",
    ["Dialogue2004201"]="Oman, someone came asking where you are again today. What should we do?",
    ["Dialogue2004202"]="Remember, no matter who asks, never let anyone know where I am! Otherwise it will be the end for our family. Helena, you must stay alert. Just hang in there for a while longer and our situation will improve!",
    ["Dialogue2004203"]="But Abu... I'm afraid he won't be able to hang on for much longer. When will we be able to get the money?",
    ["Dialogue2004204"]="...I promise you. Just a little while more and we'll be able to...",
    ["Dialogue2004301"]="...A-adventurer, you're too late...",
    ["Dialogue2004302"]="I guess this might be the price I have to pay. A few days ago, someone gave me a bottle of poison and told me to find an opportunity... an opportunity to put it into Prince Reige and Prince Hans' food! He knew that I desperately needed a huge sum of money for Abu's treatment, so he promised he'd give me a lot of Zeny and ensure that my family and I would be able to leave Prontera safely once the task was done.",
    ["Dialogue2004303"]="So I hid in the storeroom and waited... and waited... for a long, long time... but in the end, all that came was an assassin to kill me! ...Haha, this must be Odin's punishment for me. As you sow, so shall you reap. I only hope the princes' murderer... will get what he deserves!",
    ["Dialogue2004304"]="(Oman raises his quivering right hand and points to a tree nearby.)\n...Go there... See...\n(Oman stops moving.)",
    ["Dialogue2005101"]="Phew! You showed up just in the nick of time. I thought those Thief Bugs would eat me for sure.",
    ["Dialogue2005102"]="Sigh, I knew we wouldn't be able to keep this from the instructor.",
    ["Dialogue2005103"]="There's a desperate food shortage among the people in the sewer. They can't wait any longer for the chivalry to distribute resources or cooperate with Eden Group.",
    ["Dialogue2005104"]="I know it is selfish of me to do this, but... there's no other way.",
    ["Dialogue2005201"]="Adventurer, may I ask you for a favor?",
    ["Dialogue2005202"]="Yes, I'm too weak. I intend to admit my mistake to Instructor Bowya and learn battle skills properly.",
    ["Dialogue2005203"]="This has taught me the helplessness of being weak.",
    ["Dialogue2005204"]="Thank you, adventurer! I hope next time we meet, I'll be able to fight alongside you!",
    ["Dialogue2005301"]="Yo, adventurer! What are you doing in the sewer?",
    ["Dialogue2005302"]="Hahaha! Thank you, friends of Eden Group. But it's too late.",
    ["Dialogue2005303"]="Sigh, I don't want to talk about it. You can see the situation for yourself. This place isn't fit for the living anymore. Everyone has either escaped or died. I'm just cleaning up.",
    ["Dialogue2005304"]="The chivalry tried to force us to the surface by controlling our food. Did they even think about how we're supposed to live up there?",
    ["Dialogue2005305"]="Great! The Hobo Brotherhood will be Eden Group's most loyal friend from now on!",
    ["Dialogue2005306"]="Ha, don't underestimate us. We hobos have nothing; if we tried to survive alone, we would have died long ago. The Brotherhood is a place that provides warmth and acceptance for everyone.",
    ["Dialogue2005307"]="Once this issue has been resolved, come find me at the Brotherhood's headquarters on your next visit. I'll be sure to thank you properly. Hahaha.",
    ["Dialogue2005401"]="A bard snuck in while we weren't paying attention. He's bound to get into trouble. We're seriously shorthanded right now; can you help?",
    ["Dialogue2005402"]="Thank you! He headed toward the area where Tarous appear. Go check it out!",
    ["Dialogue2005501"]="Oh my goodness! The monsters are endless! Could this be the end for Caslisse?",
    ["Dialogue2005601"]="Thank you, my savior! I'm Caslisse, a bard! Oh! Are you my guardian sent from the heavens?!",
    ["Dialogue2005602"]="I'm having something of a writer's block. Don't you think the maelstrom of despair, darkness, and chaos in the sewer makes it a great place to find inspiration?!",
    ["Dialogue2005603"]="Just now, a ray of light pierced that maelstrom of darkness! Adventurer, I'm in awe of your heroism in battle! Could you let me see it again?",
    ["Dialogue2005604"]="Hmm... Let me think. Ah, you can engage in a glorious fight to the death against the Tarous! There would certainly be a beautiful poem hidden within the encounter!",
    ["Dialogue2005701"]="Inspiration... Inspiration... Ahhhhhhhhhh! Just a bit more!",
    ["Dialogue2005702"]="My inspiration! It... it... it's gone.",
    ["Dialogue2005703"]="Inspiration... Battle... Wham! Bam! Poof...",
    ["Dialogue2005704"]="(He walks away while deep in thought and making strange noises.)",
    ["Dialogue2005801"]="Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes! My inspiration!",
    ["Dialogue2005802"]="My inspiration came not from your heroism! It came from your protection!",
    ["Dialogue2005803"]="When Ymir turned into the world, it was a form of protection. When the swordsman fought Morroc, it was a form of protection. When the seven royal families defeated the giant serpent, it was a form of protection. And you, you protected me! This is what I'm meant to sing about!",
    ["Dialogue2005804"]="Thank you, adventurer! I'm off to compose the most splendid poem of my career! Your name will go down in history!",
    ["Dialogue2005901"]="Hmm... Should I make some more? No, there isn't enough time today. Arlene will get hungry. I guess I have no choice but to do it myself, but...",
    ["Dialogue2005902"]="Ah, adventurer! You couldn't have shown up at a better time. I have a request for you.",
    ["Dialogue2005903"]="Thank you for your kindness! My backpack was snatched by some Tarous and has something very important inside. I wouldn't stand a chance against them, so I can only count on you!",
    ["Dialogue2006001"]="My backpack is unscathed! You're amazing!",
    ["Dialogue2006002"]="Um, It's likely... because there's food in the backpack and the Tarous smelled it. So...",
    ["Dialogue2006101"]="I'm here in the sewer to deliver some food to Arlene.",
    ["Dialogue2006102"]="Arlene frequently takes part in adventurer requests from the Knight Guild for the survival of our family. I wanted to do something for her so, I thought that I'd bring her a little comfort and surprise. I never expected something like this to happen.",
    ["Dialogue2006103"]="Sigh, I'm so useless...",
    ["Dialogue2006104"]="That's right. I shouldn't add to her troubles. Adventurer, could you take this food to her for me?",
    ["Dialogue2006105"]="Thank you! I don't have to worry about her going hungry now!",
    ["Dialogue2006201"]="The second floor of the sewer is currently under martial law. All unauthorized persons are to leave immediately!",
    ["Dialogue2006202"]="Food? It's... it's from Ivan? He came to the sewer? I appreciate the thought, but it worries that he would come to a dangerous place like this! The fact is I'm his knight! I'm supposed to be the one protecting him!",
    ["Dialogue2006203"]="Ivan is my master and I'm his knight. I've sworn a lifelong vow to protect him, even though I'm just an adventurer now. Sigh, what ever would I do if he got hurt over something like this?",
    ["Dialogue2006204"]="I know very well. Thank you, adventurer. Ivan's food will surely give me lots of strength for my next battle.",
    ["Dialogue2006205"]="How cute! He's arranged the food to make a smiley face! Tee-hee... Erm, ahem! You didn't see anything just now!",
    ["Dialogue2006301"]="Huh? You've been staring at me from over there. Is there something on my face?",
    ["Dialogue2006302"]="Haha! I'm Frank! People call me the Thief Bug Lover! Look at this Thief Bug hat I knitted!",
    ["Dialogue2006303"]="Ah right, I came to the sewer today to catch a Thief Bug for a pet. What do you think of this little dream of mine?",
    ["Dialogue2006304"]="This is a calming potion I made. It will make a Thief Bug calm and docile. Just one little spray should be enough!",
    ["Dialogue2006401"]="I've already failed seventeen times! And my last attempt was the worst yet.",
    ["Dialogue2006402"]="It's time for Plan B!",
    ["Dialogue2006501"]="If I were to hatch Thief Bug babies, they should listen to me, right? Could you help me get some fresh Thief Bug Eggs?",
    ["Dialogue2006601"]="Why was there such an order?! Thief Bugs are so cute! Why do you want to hurt them!",
    ["Dialogue2006602"]="Darn it! I won't give up! I'll be back!",
    ["Dialogue2006701"]="Adventurer, I never thought I'd meet you here off all places.",
    ["Dialogue2006702"]="Hahaha, you're so funny. Don't you know the legend about Prontera's sewer?",
    ["Dialogue2006703"]="Well then, let me tell you about the legend that rose from the founding of this kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue2006801"]="Legend of the Kingdom's Founding tells that before Rune-Midgarts Kingdom was established, the land was occupied by a giant serpent. The first king, Tristan Gaebolg, gathered six heroes to defeat it.",
    ["Dialogue2006802"]="It's said that Prontera was built where the serpent's nest used to be. However, although the serpent is long dead, its underground nest remains.",
    ["Dialogue2006803"]="That's right! The reason why Prontera is the only place in Rune-Midgarts Kingdom with such an elaborate sewer system is because it was already dug!",
    ["Dialogue2006804"]="The nest rumored to have been left behind by the serpent is the source of many mysteries. People ask, why do giant flowers with no life grow in the sewer? Why can unidentifiable growls occasionally be heard coming from the sewer?",
    ["Dialogue2006805"]="Hahaha! I have no answers. And they're nothing more than baseless rumors.",
    ["Dialogue2006806"]="This sewer is indeed a mysterious and interesting place! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue2006901"]="Yo, didn't we meet not long ago?",
    ["Dialogue2006902"]="The chivalry requested us to carry out a secret investigation here.",
    ["Dialogue2006903"]="Hm... Forget it. I don't feel like giving this information to the chivalry anyway. I'd rather tell you since you've helped us so many times.",
    ["Dialogue2006904"]="We found the Golden Thief Bugs' nest.",
    ["Dialogue2006905"]="Shush! Keep it down. Legend has it that the nest is where the seven royal families of old kept their treasure! Are you interested now?",
    ["Dialogue2006906"]="Heh! Exploring ruins is the Eden Group's original line of work. Whether it's the Chamber of Commerce, chivalry, or even adventurers like you, no one does it better than us.",
    ["Dialogue2006907"]="I propose a trade. You verify if the legend is true. If it is, we'll give you 30% of the treasure!",
    ["Dialogue2006908"]="Great! The entrance is in the general northeast direction on this floor. If you manage to find a place that's shining, you're on the right track!",
    ["Dialogue2007001"]="You look like you've been through the wars. Could it be...?",
    ["Dialogue2007002"]="Wow! Really?",
    ["Dialogue2007003"]="This Carapace definitely belongs to a Thief Bug. But this material... Oh my goodness! Quick, tell me how much treasure's in there!",
    ["Dialogue2007004"]="That's right, it's real! The missing treasure that the seven royal families hid away is beneath this very sewer! ...Wait a minute, something doesn't feel right.",
    ["Dialogue2007005"]="Why did they seal up the underground treasury? The Eden Group mustn't be too hasty to move the treasure. There could be a trap.",
    ["Dialogue2007006"]="Adventurer, the Eden Group will be your trusted ally from now on! You've done more for us than many of our members. You can leave the rest of the investigation to us. Don't worry, the Eden Group always returns a favor!",
    ["Dialogue2007101"]="Dammit! Who could have done such a thing?!",
    ["Dialogue2007102"]="I'm Dobbin, the chivalry's head chef. I've just finished cleaning my Serena! Who touched her! When I find out who it was, I'll skin them alive!",
    ["Dialogue2007103"]="Allow me to introduce you. This pot is Serena.",
    ["Dialogue2007104"]="Forget it! She's clean now, and I'm not one to hold a grudge! Forgive and forget, that's what I always say!",
    ["Dialogue2007201"]="You're the adventurer who's been active on the front line, yeah? Thanks to you and the chivalry, everyone was able to evacuate safely. As head chef, I'm thinking of creating a few new dishes as a treat for you guys!",
    ["Dialogue2007202"]="The first dish is called Squeaks! I've already prepared the sauce but I'm still missing some Tarou meat. Adventurer, if you're free, could you get some for me? When the dish is done, I'll save some thigh for you!",
    ["Dialogue2007203"]="Rats squeak? And since Tarou are basically rats, Squeaks is a pretty good name! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue2007301"]="Haha! Not bad at all. When Tarous get aggressive, their meat becomes extra tender!",
    ["Dialogue2007302"]="Don't believe people when they say monster meat is full of harmful substances. Once it's been cooked at a high temperature, any harmful substances are broken down and the texture of the meat improves! The chivalry's old guard are going to love this dish, haha!",
    ["Dialogue2007401"]="The second dish is called Gems and Pearls. I'm still short of some Thief Bug Eggs; looks like I'll have to trouble you again.",
    ["Dialogue2007402"]="The pearls are radishes that have been shaped into spheres; the gems are steamed Thief Bug Eggs. They're similar in color and complement each other nutritionally. When you pick a piece up, you can hardly tell which it is, which gives a sense of mystery to the dish.",
    ["Dialogue2007403"]="What's more, Thief Bug Eggs are packed with protein! They may look pretty disgusting when fresh, but you won't be able to resist them once they've been cooked!",
    ["Dialogue2007501"]="Great! Fresh, warm Thief Bug Eggs! The basis of a true delicacy!",
    ["Dialogue2007502"]="Stand back! I'm about to begin my performance!",
    ["Dialogue2007601"]="Hahaha! Done!",
    ["Dialogue2007602"]="There were people who were initially disgusted by my cooking. They said they'd rather starve to death or end their own lives than eat my food; but in the end, they all had the same reaction as you. Save some and put it on the ground over there, then take the rest to Arlene to distribute!",
    ["Dialogue2007603"]="Why put some on the ground? Because monsters have an exceptional sense of smell. If they smell that one their kind has been cooked, they'll stay away. Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue2007701"]="As soon as that aroma hit my nostrils, I instantly knew it was Dobbin's cooking!",
    ["Dialogue2007801"]="Many in the chivalry have eaten Dobbin's cooking for their entire career. There are lots of rumors about him. They're fascinating.",
    ["Dialogue2007802"]="The most widespread rumor is that he's actually a God of Cooking who's been alive for hundreds of years, because even the most senior captain in the chivalry grew up eating his food.",
    ["Dialogue2007803"]="Every time someone finds a rare recipe, they take it straight to him, because he's the only one who can read it.",
    ["Dialogue2007804"]="I digress... but while I'm on the topic, I have an ancient recipe here. Since I have no use for it, could you take it to Dobbin?",
    ["Dialogue2007901"]="You've worked hard. Come, this is your share.",
    ["Dialogue2007902"]="Thoughts? Haha, nobody would say it tastes bad. In that I have the utmost confidence! People won't say it even in hundreds of ye— in their lifetime!",
    ["Dialogue2007903"]="Huh? This recipe is about... stir frying Goblin meat. Hmm, does this recipe date from the time when goblin was first declared edible?",
    ["Dialogue2008001"]="Wah! Ch-chivalry! Please don't capture me! I'm just lost!",
    ["Dialogue2008002"]="Oh? You're not from the chivalry? What a relief. I thought I was going to get caught by the chivalry before Dinza arrives.",
    ["Dialogue2008003"]="You know her too? My name's Harold; I'm the most hardcore member of Omnipotent. I want to be Dinza's sidekick!",
    ["Dialogue2008004"]="Allow me to give you a brief introduction. Omnipotent is an organization established by merchants who look up to Dinza. The greatest honor among us is to become her sidekick. She has exceptional business sense and amazing combat skills! The organization is called Omnipotent because she's good at absolutely everything and only operates alone!",
    ["Dialogue2008005"]="HUH?! Dinza was caught by the chivalry on the first floor? I thought she'd definitely come here to get information on Golden Thief Bugs, but that seems unlikely now. Well, I'm not going to let this trip be for nothing! Adventurer, I'd like to hire you as my bodyguard!",
    ["Dialogue2008006"]="Great! First let's go to a place where a huge flower grows. There are no nutrients or sunlight in the sewer, so how did such a huge flower grow? Something fishy must be going on!",
    ["Dialogue2008101"]="Who are you people? The second floor of the sewer has been barricaded; how did you get in?!",
    ["Dialogue2008102"]="Oh, you're the adventurer Prince Aronst brought. Please excuse me. The second floor of the sewer has been barricaded and no one is allowed to enter, so...",
    ["Dialogue2008103"]="Understood, we'll escort him back to the surface. There's no need to trouble yourself.",
    ["Dialogue2008201"]="Damn. And after all the trouble I went through for the information.",
    ["Dialogue2008202"]="The chivalry must be hiding something. If you weren't here, I might have been locked up. Let's leave for now and then decide what to do.",
    ["Dialogue2008203"]="Goodbye, Adventurer! Send my regards to Dinza!",
    ["Dialogue2008301"]="Thank you! I'm all perked up after eating Ivan's food! Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue2008302"]="What are you talking about! It's just gratitude toward my master! ...Anyway, forget that. One of our knights, Wyatt, has been bitten by a Familiar and is trapped.",
    ["Dialogue2008303"]="Please take these quick-heal potions so he can get back to us!",
    ["Dialogue2008401"]="So cold... So cold... *Shivers*",
    ["Dialogue2008402"]="That's me. I've been bitten by a Familiar. Please stay back. I think I'm about to turn into a vampire.",
    ["Dialogue2008403"]="It's too late for me. I'm afraid of the cold and sunlight now; quick-heal potions can't help.",
    ["Dialogue2008404"]="I won't die, but if I become a vampire, I'll hurt other people and have to fight my comrades. I don't want that.",
    ["Dialogue2008405"]="A knight's ideals and pride? ...You're right, I can't give up like this!",
    ["Dialogue2008501"]="What else can be done? Let me think... Ah, yes! When I was studying medicines, I saw an ancient recipe that can prevent vampirism.",
    ["Dialogue2008502"]="A knight needs to learn everything that can help in combat!",
    ["Dialogue2008503"]="If I remember correctly, it said: Boil together Familiar Wings, Tarou Fur, and Thief Bug Shell, then drink it.",
    ["Dialogue2008504"]="It sounds a little iffy, but I'm willing to try anything! I'm shivering so badly I can't even hold my sword; I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue2008601"]="How did it go?",
    ["Dialogue2008602"]="Perfect! Next we'll have to use Chef Dobbin's pot to cook it!",
    ["Dialogue2008701"]="I know it's wrong, but please don't let him know you're using it. If he finds out we've used his precious pot, the chivalry will starve.",
    ["Dialogue2008702"]="His pot is near where the chivalry is stationed at the entrance. It should be easy to spot!",
    ["Dialogue2008801"]="You're finally back! The medicine...",
    ["Dialogue2008802"]="Thank you very much! This medicine... The smell and color... Is it safe to drink? It can't be!",
    ["Dialogue2008803"]="No! If the priest can't help me either, I'll be treated like a vampire and killed on the spot! That would no doubt be a huge blow to my ideals and pride as a knight! I won't allow that to happen!",
    ["Dialogue2008901"]="Sigh, is there really no other way? Let me think...",
    ["Dialogue2008902"]="Although... There's no actual evidence that a person will definitely turn into a vampire after getting bitten by a Familiar. But my symptoms of being afraid of light and cold are just like the rumors say.",
    ["Dialogue2008903"]="But... but they're just rumors.",
    ["Dialogue2008904"]="Could I have been mistaken? ...Hmm, what you said does make sense. If this all is just a misunderstanding, then staying here is pointless!",
    ["Dialogue2008905"]="Please, adventurer. I'm unable to fight now; please help me get back to the priest at the entrance! The sewer's crawling with transformed Thief Bugs now; we've got to be careful!",
    ["Dialogue2009001"]="Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue2009002"]="Hmm? Bitten by a Familiar? Bring him here. I'll disinfect the wound and he'll be fine.",
    ["Dialogue2009101"]="What a coincidence, adventurer. Are you here to pay your respects to Don Qix?",
    ["Dialogue2009102"]="Looks like you've never heard of this heroic knight before. Allow me to explain.",
    ["Dialogue2009201"]="Don Qix was injured in battle and took refuge in this windmill.",
    ["Dialogue2009202"]="But one day, he suddenly realized that the windmill is actually a huge monster.",
    ["Dialogue2009203"]="Don Qix fearlessly charged at the monster. Want to guess what happened next?",
    ["Dialogue2009204"]="Hahaha! Isn't this an interesting legend? In any case...",
    ["Dialogue2009205"]="Being me some flowers! How can you possibly pay your respects without flowers?",
    ["Dialogue2009301"]="Flowers fit for a hero.",
    ["Dialogue2009302"]="His fearlessness earned him the favor of Athena. His injuries were healed and he returned to the battleground once more.",
    ["Dialogue2009303"]="He carried this fearlessness with him as he led in countless battles, and till the day he retired, he sustained not a single injury.",
    ["Dialogue2009304"]="Do you know why this windmill is called \"The Knight's Old Enemy\"?",
    ["Dialogue2009305"]="Because Don Qix returned to this windmill after he retired. But the next day, a piece of wood fell from the ceiling and hit him on the head... and killed him.",
    ["Dialogue2009306"]="You want to know how can a windmill be a monster, right?",
    ["Dialogue2009307"]="Hahaha! In reality, of course it's impossible. Everyone thought that Don Qix had gone mad and that the favor of Athena was just a silly rumor. They were only concerned with his bravery and amazing luck.",
    ["Dialogue2009308"]="Though the ending was rather dramatic... Alright! Don Qix's story ends here, but your adventure is far from over. Off you go then!",
    ["Dialogue2009401"]="Hi! What a coincidence!",
    ["Dialogue2009402"]="I was traveling around Prontera when I found this lost girl. I'm at a loss at what to do now.",
    ["Dialogue2009501"]="I said I'm fine.",
    ["Dialogue2009502"]="That's right! I'm Dinza!",
    ["Dialogue2009503"]="After the chivalry brought me back to the surface, I realized that there's a passageway somewhere at West Gate which leads to the second floor of the sewer. So I came here looking for it.",
    ["Dialogue2009504"]="After bumping into this swordswoman, she refused to let me go. She kept saying that it's dangerous out here and that she wants to send me back to Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue2009505"]="You look like you know her! Help me tell her that I, the great Dinza, am very strong! I don't need a bodyguard!",
    ["Dialogue2009601"]="Huh? Is she really okay?",
    ["Dialogue2009602"]="Is that so? Alright, since you say so, I'll believe you!",
    ["Dialogue2009701"]="Heya, how's your training going?",
    ["Dialogue2009702"]="What kind of answer is that? Come, spar with me!",
    ["Dialogue2009801"]="Wow, that's pretty impressive. You've come on leaps and bounds in the short time since I last saw you!",
    ["Dialogue2009802"]="Fighting battles with the chivalry in the sewer? I'm so envious! I'm off to look for training opportunities like that too! Farewell!",
    ["Dialogue2009901"]="Where did that child go? How could I explain myself to his father if anything happened to him?",
    ["Dialogue2009902"]="A-are you an adventurer?! Can you help me save Raven? He ran to the West Gate by himself. It's such a dangerous place. I fear the worst.",
    ["Dialogue2009903"]="I'm sorry, Raven is my son. We had a fight today and he left home in a fit of anger. I followed him all the way here and saw him run out of the West Gate.",
    ["Dialogue2009904"]="Up ahead on this path is where Rockers gather. Sigh, I'll never forgive myself if something happens him.",
    ["Dialogue2010001"]="Erm, the flowers here aren't very suitable. Shall we try somewhere else?",
    ["Dialogue2010002"]="Huh? Who are you?",
    ["Dialogue2010003"]="...No, I cannot return yet.",
    ["Dialogue2010004"]="What do you know?! None of you know! None!",
    ["Dialogue2010005"]="Rocker, attack!",
    ["Dialogue2010101"]="Oh look! Isn't this Dean Mainz's favorite protégé, the pride and glory of Criatura Academy? I heard you've been busy collecting Fragments of Ymir's Heart. Doing so much at such a young age; your future will certainly be bright!",
    ["Dialogue2010102"]="I reckon someone as selfless as you won't mind helping me out with a small favor, right? A few days ago, I gave my student, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wulf</color>, an assignment. But he hasn't handed in yet. I heard he's been brainstorming at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blacksmith's</color>; go ask him how much longer he's going to take to complete the assignment!",
    ["Dialogue2010201"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me see... I have enough coal ore for smelting. I'll still need...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2010202"]="...Hi. Yes, I'm Wulf Lugenburg.",
    ["Dialogue2010203"]="My surname should be unique in the kingdom, I guess. Yes, I'm from <color=#CA2E0AFF>one of the royal families</color>. More specifically, I'm from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lugenburg Family</color> who runs Morroc. Oh? You've met Sheriff Maximilian? He is my grandfather. Please excuse me but I have no interest in idle chat at the moment. The most important thing right now is for me to complete Instructor Hamid's assignment, or else I won't be able to advance to a merchant.",
    ["Dialogue2010204"]="I'm required to <color=#CA2E0AFF>smelt high-quality gold, silver, and iron</color>. However, as a desert dweller, I'm not too sure about where to find the metals needed. I've already got some of the materials from the merchant at the port, but I'm still short of <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 pieces each of gold, silver, and iron ore</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2010301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me see...</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> Yup, I have all the ore I need for smelting now. Next, I have to remove the impurities by using a high heat.</color></size>\nI'll need to turn up the fire on the furnace, but I'm afraid I don't have enough wood. Please get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wood</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Old Clay</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2010401"]="<size=18>Sigh, it's been a while since I've done any work.</size><size=18> My beloved tools are going to rust at this rate!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2010402"]="<size=18>...Strange, </size><size=18>why has everyone been asking me for Wood lately?</size>\nAll the Wood is <color=#CA2E0AFF>just next to me</color>. Take as much as you need!",
    ["Dialogue2010501"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Instructor Hamid said </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>to smelt high-quality metals; </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'll have to control the temperature of the furnace well.</color></size>\nAdventurer, I'll need your help once more. I need you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>add Wood to the furnace</color> the moment I add the ore.",
    ["Dialogue2010601"]="Great! All I have to do now is to hand this high-quality gold, silver, and iron and Instructor Hamid. Then I'll be able to advance to a merchant and be qualified to trade throughout the Midgard. This is very important to me. Although thanking someone is a modest gesture at best, still, thank you.",
    ["Dialogue2010602"]="Why does a royal like me want to become a merchant? Hmm, you're a reliable friend; there's no harm in telling you. Since you've been to Morroc, you should know how scarce resources are and how bleak the economy is. Desert dwellers often completely rely on trade caravans for their daily necessities, but the weather conditions in the desert often hinder them.",
    ["Dialogue2010603"]="Only by building a stable fleet of trade caravans to bring a constant stream of resources to Morroc from around the world can we solve the problem of survival and safeguard the best interests of the desert dwellers. This is my dream, and the reason why I must become a merchant. Grandfather and the rest of the family don't understand, but I'll work hard and show them I'm right!",
    ["Dialogue2010604"]="Hah, you don't understand the Lugenburg Family at all. Of all the seven royal families, mine is the one that's <color=#CA2E0AFF>most focused on physical strength</color>. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Martial arts has been religiously passed down from generation to generation</color>; whether it's my grandfather or elder brother, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Halmod</color>, all they think about is fighting. The hardships of our subjects never cross their minds. Especially Halmod, he's just all brawn and no brains.",
    ["Dialogue2010605"]="(Wulf sighs heavily.)\nIn any case, words can't get through their thick skulls, so I need to prove myself through my actions. <color=#CA2E0AFF>True strength isn't simply being good at fighting, it's being able to protect others</color>. Advancing to a merchant is the first step, but... I have another problem at hand.",
    ["Dialogue2010606"]="I'm a little ashamed to say this, but I have a little sister, Agnes, who came to the island with me. It's just that I've been so busy and neglected her. I have to return to Instructor Hamid now to complete my job advancement, so... could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take care of Agnes</color> for a while? She should be playing in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>garden by the sea</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2010701"]="<size=18>Izlude Island's sea is so beautiful, </size><size=18>and the ships are so majestic. </size><size=18>Why won't Wulf come and take a look?</size>\nHuh? He asked you to look for me? Does he finally have time to play with me?",
    ["Dialogue2010702"]="(The smile on Agnes' face fades.)\nOh, so he's still busy... It's okay! I can play by myself! He works really hard; I need to learn to be more considerate. Ah, I know! I may not be able to disturb him, but I can make a present for him!",
    ["Dialogue2010703"]="(Agnes looks around.)\nI know! I can use flowers to make him a lovely wreath! When he sees it, it will be just like he's seeing me! What do you think? I'll just need a few <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pretty Flowers</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2010801"]="(A huge smile blossoms on Agnes' face.)\nWow! I've never seen such bright, pretty flowers in Morroc! Alright, I'm going start making the wreaths now! I'm going to make two huge wreaths! One for my hardworking big brother and another for... for...",
    ["Dialogue2010802"]="(Agnes starts blushing.)\nI-it's a secret... The wreath is ready! Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to Wulf</color>? Remember to tell him I made it!",
    ["Dialogue2010901"]="...Agnes made this for me? ...Sigh, she's the only one who cares this much about me.\n(Although Wulf tries to remain calm, he can't help but smile a little.)",
    ["Dialogue2010902"]="I really wish I could thank her in person, but I have a lot of work to do. Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass on a message</color>? Tell Agnes that I now have my merchant certificate and am planning to search for business opportunities at the port. When I make my first pot of gold, I'll buy her the most beautiful doll on the island!",
    ["Dialogue2011001"]="(Agnes is not very excited by Wulf's message.)\nOh... He said that? But I don't want any presents. I just...\nI just wish that Wulf and Halmod can stop fighting.",
    ["Dialogue2011002"]="Aren't you curious why I made two wreaths? Well... the other one is for Halmod. I love both my big brothers, but... but why can't they be nice to each other like they are to me?",
    ["Dialogue2011003"]="Grandfather always says that it's our family tradition for the<color=#CA2E0AFF>strongest to be the heir</color>. That's why he really likes Halmod; he's so brave and good at fighting. But big brother Wulf always says that's not true strength. Their different views led to an argument that ended in a huge fight. That's when Wulf brought me here.",
    ["Dialogue2011004"]="I don't really understand the argument, but I hope they can go back to being as friendly as they used to be. And I can tell that Wulf misses home and worries about it, but he tries to hide it and doesn't talk about it. If only there was a way to help my brothers open up about their feelings.",
    ["Dialogue2011005"]="(Agnes looks at the wreath in her hands.)\nI know! I can <color=#CA2E0AFF>give this wreath to Halmod</color>! If he sees it and thinks of Wulf and me, maybe he'll come look for us. But Morroc is so far away, how can I get it to him?",
    ["Dialogue2011101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Damn those monsters! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How they create unrest on my territory again?! If I was ten years younger, I'd slay every last one of them!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2011102"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmph, luckily my grandson, Halmod, inherited my wonderful genes. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Just wait, he'll send word of victory very soon!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2011103"]="Hey, stop cawing like a Pecopeco! I heard you! Halmod is eliminating monsters just <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside Morroc</color>. If you want to join in the fight, just head over and speak to him!",
    ["Dialogue2011201"]="(Halmod is enjoying the battle and doesn't notice you.)\nHaha! I finally get to work out! But these monsters are so weak; this isn't much of a fight. Looks like I'm just too strong!",
    ["Dialogue2011202"]="Huh? What's this? A present from Agnes? Haha! She's such a cutie, don't ya think?\n(Halmod laughs loudly as he puts the wreath in his pocket.)",
    ["Dialogue2011203"]="Come to think of it, I haven't heard about Agnes for a while now. Ah, I know! I'll dedicate this victory against the monsters to my little sister! Warrior, grab your weapon and follow me. Let's go teach those irksome <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anacondaqs</color> a lesson!",
    ["Dialogue2011301"]="(Halmod's eyes light up as he revels in the joy the battle.)\nHaha! These slimy Anacondaqs are no match for me. If I make a necklace out of their Venomous Canines and give it to Agnes, she'll be happy, right?",
    ["Dialogue2011302"]="(Halmod finally notices you.)\nHuh? You're still here? Very good. Someone who can match up to me in a battle must be very strong. If I didn't have another battle to fight, I'd challenged you! But for now, let us set off for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2011401"]="I'm so excited thinking about the next battle! But of course, it will inevitably end in my victory!",
    ["Dialogue2011402"]="Warrior, see these <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golems</color>? They've been giving the residents of Weinst Street and Hope Oasis a lot trouble. Let's dig out their <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hard Stone Hearts</color> as compensation for the people. I dare say I'll be able to dig out a hundred hearts in a single breath!",
    ["Dialogue2011501"]="(Halmod cracks his knuckles as he revels in the joy of battle.)\nThe hearts of these Golems were harder than I thought, but absolute victory is still mine. It may not be perfect, but I have exactly 100 Hard Stone Hearts!",
    ["Dialogue2011502"]="Then let's not delay, and head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>the other side of the desert</color> immediately. Another battle awaits us!",
    ["Dialogue2011601"]="Warrior, the real challenge is here! We'll be facing <color=#CA2E0AFF>desert Wolves</color> next. These monsters are extremely dangerous. They move in packs and never fight alone, but it's easy to bring them down: just <color=#CA2E0AFF>kill the alpha wolf</color>, and the rest of the pack will be nothing to fear!",
    ["Dialogue2011602"]="(Halmod looks at you intensely.)\nWhat? You want to eliminate the alpha wolf on your own? What a bold request! Well then, let me teach you how to lure it out. Take this piece of meat. All you have to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>place it where the wolves appear</color>, and the first wolf that appears to eat it will be the alpha!",
    ["Dialogue2011701"]="(Halmod gives you a thumbs up.)\nI saw that battle. It was amazing! It feels funny fighting alongside someone else. You must the best friend I'm destined to have! I would like to invite you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Morroc</color> with me. I believe that Grandfather would want to meet a true warrior like you!",
    ["Dialogue2011801"]="(Maximilian is so angry that steam is coming out of his ears.)\nWho could have done such a despicable thing? Who... <size=24>who dared kidnap my youngest grandson, Meyer?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2011802"]="Grandfather, what happened?",
    ["Dialogue2011803"]="(Maximilian looks more comforted when he sees Halmod.)\nHalmod, you're finally back! Come, read this letter. Someone actually dared kidnap a member of the Lugenburg Family, and even wrote a letter to provoke us! The kidnapper says... if we want Meyer back in one piece, we'll have to pay <size=24><color=#CA2E0AFF>50 million Zeny</color></size> immediately!",
    ["Dialogue2011804"]="(Maximilian waves the letter around furiously.)\nThis is outright robbery! If the Lugenburg Family had this sort of money, I would have built an arena in the desert long ago!",
    ["Dialogue2011805"]="(Halmod's expression becomes serious as he reads the letter.)\n\"Pay a ransom of 50 million Zeny immediately. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Put it in the dunes outside Hope Oasis</color>...\"\nGrandfather, if we don't pay the ransom soon, who knows what they'll do to Meyer. <size=24>We have to think of something!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2011806"]="There's only one solution now! Halmod, bring Wulf back! That child always had a knack for business. He recently wrote to me and told me he's been making money through trading. He might be able to raise enough money for the ransom.",
    ["Dialogue2011807"]="<size=24>No, </size><size=24>I disagree!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2011808"]="As the eldest grandchild of the Lugenburg Family, how could I task something as important as saving my younger brother to someone else? Furthermore, it's Wulf we're talking about! He's going to say I'm all brawn and no brains again—that I'm just an idiot who can't even raise the ransom!",
    ["Dialogue2011809"]="(Maximilian is lost in thought and ignores Halmod's rant.)\nFine, I guess we have no other choice. That's what we'll do! Adventurer, I'm counting on you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Wulf for help</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2011901"]="(Wulf seems to be in a good mood.)\nIt's been a while, my friend. I have some good news to share. Yesterday, I completed my first business deal and earned my very first pot of gold. I can now fulfill my promise to Agnes.",
    ["Dialogue2011902"]="(Wulf is stunned.)\n...What?! Meyer... My little brother has been kidnapped? What has Halmod been doing? He promised that no harm would come to the Lugenburg Family as long as he's around.",
    ["Dialogue2011903"]="How dare the kidnapper make such an unreasonable demand?! This is really... This is too much! I must return to Morroc at once. Can you get Agnes for me? I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue2012001"]="(Wulf's eyes widen in shock.)\n...Agnes has been kidnapped too?! This... this is all my fault. I've been so busy doing business that I neglected my sister. She hates being alone; she must be so scared right now.",
    ["Dialogue2012002"]="I need to pull myself together. I can apologize as much as I want once I've saved Agnes. We must <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Morroc</color> immediately. Be it paying the ransom or fighting Maya, I'll do whatever it takes to save my siblings.",
    ["Dialogue2012101"]="Let's part ways here. As for Meyer's ransom, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>give this bag of Zeny to Halmod</color>. It's everything I've saved so far. It should be enough to get Meyer back.",
    ["Dialogue2012102"]="I going to Ant Cavern to get Maya's Crown. I know it's dangerous, but my own safety is nothing compared to Agnes' life. Please don't tell anyone. If Grandfather and Halmod found out that Agnes is also in danger, it might be too much for them to bear.",
    ["Dialogue2012201"]="This is unbelievable. Is all this Zeny for me? Thank you so much, friend. As it's to save Meyer, I will shamelessly accept it. But believe me, once I have my brother back, I will return it to you in full!",
    ["Dialogue2012202"]="(Halmod's expression grows stiff.)\nW-what... This money is Wulf's savings? Why didn't he come back himself? Is he trying to mock me in another way? Hmph, I will not accept this money!",
    ["Dialogue2012203"]="<size=24>...You dare call me stupid?</size>\nNobody in Morroc has ever dared to speak to me like that before... but for some reason I get a different feeling from you! Alright, I'll listen to you and accept the money. I'll find a chance to speak to Wulf once Meyer is saved!",
    ["Dialogue2012204"]="Hey, why are you going on and on like Wulf? My ears are hurting from your nagging. Don't try to persuade me. I've only accepted the money because I haven't thought of another way to save Meyer!",
    ["Dialogue2012205"]="In any case, let's go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hope Oasis</color> with the ransom. I want to see if the kidnapper is capable enough to take it!",
    ["Dialogue2012301"]="This should be the place the letter mentioned. Quick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>let's bury the ransom in the dune</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2012401"]="Wait! Let me explain. I don't know anything, I've just been <color=#CA2E0AFF>hired to deliver a letter</color>! I don't know why you suddenly attacked me but I don't want to fight people like you. If you want <color=#CA2E0AFF>this letter</color>, how about I just hand it over?",
    ["Dialogue2012501"]="(Halmod raises his eyebrows as he reads the letter.)\nHmm? This handwriting... This tone...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That little imp...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2012502"]="Thief, tell me, where is the person who hired you? If you dare lie to me, I'll break your legs!",
    ["Dialogue2012503"]="(The thief immediately closes his legs.)\nY-yes sir! ...T-the person who hired me told me to meet him outside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color>! He was afraid his identity might be exposed, so he gave me this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Signal Flare</color>. That's all I know!",
    ["Dialogue2012504"]="(Halmod takes a deep breath.)\n<size=24>...Scram!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2012601"]="Alright, now that we have enough information, it's time for us to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet the \"kidnapper\" who thinks he is so smart</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2012701"]="(Halmod narrows his eyes menacingly.)\nYou little imp, if I hadn't recognized the handwriting in the letter, I would have fallen for your trick! Meyer, you'd better explain yourself right now!",
    ["Dialogue2012702"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Huh? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That stupid thief </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>sold me out.</color></size>\nHaha... Don't get angry, Halmod. I may have faked my own kidnapping, but it wasn't for me. It was for you and Wulf! If both of you weren't so stubborn, Agnes and I wouldn't have had to go to such lengths!",
    ["Dialogue2012703"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oops, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I've given it all away now.</color></size>\nU-um... yes, I was behind Agnes' kidnapping as well. But I was just hoping that my big brothers would finally see each other's strengths and shortcomings. If Wulf realized that Halmod would be a great help in saving Agnes, it would have worked.",
    ["Dialogue2012704"]="(Halmod scowls.)\nYou're pretty smart eh, Meyer?",
    ["Dialogue2012705"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Erm, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>why do I get the feeling he's not done with me yet? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better divert his attention away from me.</color></size>\nOh right, Halmod, there's something I want to tell you. I told Wulf that he'll have to challenge Maya in order to save Agnes. I never thought he'd actually go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> by himself. What should we do now?",
    ["Dialogue2012706"]="...Challenge Maya?! Wulf can't handle monsters of that level! I must <color=#CA2E0AFF>get to Ant Cavern</color>! Meyer, I order you to bring Agnes home immediately! No more fooling around!",
    ["Dialogue2012801"]="Halmod, Wulf, I've finally found you! Bad news! Agnes... Agnes really has gone missing! I went to her hiding place but she wasn't there. A-and there was a huge hole in the ground! I'm afraid... she's been <color=#CA2E0AFF>taken by the ants</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2012802"]="Damnit! I won't let those ants to hurt Agnes! You guys stay here and take care of Wulf. I'll go save our little sister! Don't worry, I'm more than capable of dealing with those monsters!",
    ["Dialogue2012803"]="Wait, Halmod!",
    ["Dialogue2012901"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...Ah, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Halmod has gone off on his own again. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Judging by Wulf's expression, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>he seems to be sulking. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'd better not disturb him.</color></size>\n<size=18>Hey, </size><size=18>adventurer.</size><size=18> Can you help me out?</size>",
    ["Dialogue2012902"]="It's obvious that Wulf is suffering from ant poison. It causes the body to gradually become numb. Can you check the area and see if you can find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lucid Herbs</color>? They should help his condition.",
    ["Dialogue2013001"]="Great! With these herbs, Wulf will be able to move again in no time. Please go <color=#CA2E0AFF>help Halmod</color> now. I'm afraid things might not be as easy as he thinks.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He always tends to underestimate danger.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2013101"]="(Halmod looks at you with respect.)\nFriend, you've helped me once again. This wonderful feeling of fighting together is hard to put into words! Now that we've saved Agnes, let's return to Wulf and Meyer.",
    ["Dialogue2013102"]="When we're safely back in Morroc, I will talk to Wulf, even if I have to use force!",
    ["Dialogue2013201"]="Meyer's applied the medicine; I'm feeling much better. Now let's get out of here.",
    ["Dialogue2013301"]="<size=24>Hahahahaha!</size>\nSo our little imp Meyer was behind all this! You're definitely my grandson! Since you fooled so many people, from this day forth, you will... <size=24>run a hundred laps around Morroc every day!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2013302"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>There it is again. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Grandfather's ultimate skill: </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> unpredictability!</color></size>\nYes, Grandfather! No problem, Grandfather!",
    ["Dialogue2013303"]="Grandfather, what Meyer did may have been bad, but he did it for Wulf and me. None of this would have happened if I'd just listened to my brothers. Please forgive Meyer! Otherwise, I'll run a hundred laps around Morroc with him every day.",
    ["Dialogue2013304"]="...I too am at fault, Grandfather. If I wasn't so stubborn about my own views and didn't ignore my own shortcomings, Meyer and Agnes wouldn't have been so worried. I'm still adamant about pursing my dreams, but now I will learn to work with Halmod... my big brother.",
    ["Dialogue2013305"]="Wulf... Actually, there's been something I've been meaning to tell you. I've decided to leave the future of the Lugenburg Family in your hands! From today on, you're the heir of the Lugenburg Family!",
    ["Dialogue2013306"]="After all that's happened today, I understand that both <color=#CA2E0AFF>physical strength and intelligence</color> are equally important when it comes to protecting our family and territory! You have the brains to make the right decisions for Morroc, so I'll feel assured to leave the fate of Morroc in your hands.",
    ["Dialogue2013307"]="(Wulf is touched.)\nHalmod... Do you really think I'll be able to do it?",
    ["Dialogue2013308"]="(Halmod looks determined.)\nI believe you can! After all—",
    ["Dialogue2013309"]="After all, I have a new battleground now! You haven't heard, right? After you left Morroc, I was chosen as <color=#CA2E0AFF>one of the candidates to inherit the crown</color>; I'll be leaving for Prontera soon to compete. With my strength, is there anyone in the seven royal families who can match me? I think not, haha!",
    ["Dialogue2013310"]="...This country has no hope.",
    ["Dialogue2013311"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...Nope, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>none at all.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2013401"]="(Wulf tries to stand but he seems to have lost all his strength.)\n...Hmph, Halmod, are you here to laugh at me?",
    ["Dialogue2013402"]="You're hurt? Those damned ants... If you want to save Agnes, why didn't you ask me for help? Does it hurt your pride that much to ask for help from someone you look down on, Wulf?",
    ["Dialogue2013403"]="What about you, Halmod? If you want to save Meyer, why didn't you tell me? You've never acknowledged me or my views.",
    ["Dialogue2013404"]="I did not—",
    ["Dialogue2013405"]="...Oh no, oh no! Something bad really happened!",
    ["Dialogue2013501"]="(The footprints are still very clear. They must be quite recent. Quick, follow them!)",
    ["Dialogue2016001"]="Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue2016002"]="Hmph, who told you that. Forget it, I don't want to pursue it. That's right, Kahn is my younger brother. Don't look at me like that. He deserved it.",
    ["Dialogue2016003"]="I told Kahn that if he sets sail in the fog, he's bound to meet the Kraken and the whole ship will perish with him. Sigh, but all he knew was to brag about how strong the Radiance was with her cannons and all.",
    ["Dialogue2016004"]="This stuff was all just talk on the sea of Midgard. But he was young and hotheaded enough to believe in it.",
    ["Dialogue2016005"]="Feel sad? ...Sigh, my brother died. Would you believe me if I told you I don't feel sad? Oh right, he was in the habit of keeping a log. Could you retrieve it so we can find out what happened before the Radiance sank?",
    ["Dialogue2016006"]="It's not with him? Then it must have been taken by Kukres. They like to read human writing.",
    ["Dialogue2016101"]="Yup, this is definitely his log. Look, his name is on the cover. Let me take a look...",
    ["Dialogue2016102"]="\"Attacked by the Shipwreck. Cannons are useless. Attacked by Doppelgangers. All dead.\"",
    ["Dialogue2016103"]="...With just one line, the Radiance was... Hm? There's more on the back.",
    ["Dialogue2016104"]="\"I'm sorry, brother. I lost the bet. Ferrying Ymir's Heart is something that must not be done. No matter how lucrative the reward, it must not be done! I leave Lacus in your care.\"",
    ["Dialogue2016105"]="Lacus is Kahn's fiancée. She isn't in the best of health, but every time Kahn sets sail, she insists on coming here to pray. I was supposed to attend their wedding after Kahn returned, but alas, fate had something else in store.",
    ["Dialogue2016201"]="Adventurer, if you have some time to spare, do visit Lacus too. She'll likely need your help. Now that Kahn isn't here, I'm very worried about her.",
    ["Dialogue2016202"]="Alright, I have nothing else to say. Let me have some peace.",
    ["Dialogue2016301"]="Adventurer! Did you get anything?",
    ["Dialogue2016302"]="Betting all he has on this last voyage and leaving his fiancée in the care of his brother... Such a sad story.",
    ["Dialogue2016303"]="Two lovers separated between life and death in just a split second... Oh my! My inspiration is here! Now I'll definitely be able to create a touching masterpiece!",
    ["Dialogue2016401"]="Great Strouf, please bless my Kahn and allow him to return safely.",
    ["Dialogue2016402"]="Yes, that's me. Hello adventurer, I'm praying for my fiancé. He's Kahn, captain of the Radiance.",
    ["Dialogue2016403"]="I'm aware that the Radiance has run into some trouble, but Kahn is a very experienced captain. I believe he will eventually return.",
    ["Dialogue2016501"]="These clothes, this hat... Kahn... No... *Sobs*",
    ["Dialogue2016502"]="Kahn, what meaning is there for me to live on alone in this world... Argh!",
    ["Dialogue2016601"]="M-my medicine... Where did my medicine go?",
    ["Dialogue2016602"]="P-please... get my medicine... f-from the general merchant.",
    ["Dialogue2016701"]="Would you like to buy something?",
    ["Dialogue2016702"]="Medicine? Huh? Lacus' medicine? Only the pharmacist in Prontera knows how to make it!",
    ["Dialogue2016703"]="Wait! Lacus is suffering from an acute illness; you won't make it in time! Let me think, let me think...",
    ["Dialogue2016704"]="Got it! The main ingredient in the medicine is the hard shards found in Porings' bodies. Quick, get some from the Porings at South Gate. I'll purify them. It should temporarily help! Hurry!",
    ["Dialogue2016801"]="Alright! Give me a moment! (Hammering and heating.) It's done! Hurry, go!",
    ["Dialogue2016901"]="Huff.. Huff... (Can't breathe.)",
    ["Dialogue2016902"]="Th-thank you... (Takes medicine.)",
    ["Dialogue2016903"]="Thank you, I feel... much better now. I've been so focused on praying for Kahn every day that I forgot I've run out of medicine.",
    ["Dialogue2017001"]="Is there really no meaning in praying here?",
    ["Dialogue2017002"]="Kahn isn't coming back, no matter how long I wait here.",
    ["Dialogue2017003"]="I've decided. Since Kahn isn't coming back, I'll go look for him!",
    ["Dialogue2017004"]="Please don't misunderstand. I'm just going to the Treasure Ship to look for Kahn.",
    ["Dialogue2017005"]="I know, but I don't want our last conversation to be the last thing we said to each other.",
    ["Dialogue2017006"]="Adventurer, please... Please take me to Kahn.",
    ["Dialogue2017101"]="Thank you, adventurer. You resolved the greatest regret that Lacus and I had in this lifetime.",
    ["Dialogue2017102"]="Lacus doesn't belong here. The undead aura will affect her weak health. It's time for you to leave.",
    ["Dialogue2017103"]="Please... leave Lacus in the care of someone reliable. The only person I trust in life is Carew.",
    ["Dialogue2017104"]="Goodbye, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2017201"]="Let me check the list of unconfirmed deaths. They might still be bound by the obsessions of the dead. There, got it.",
    ["Dialogue2017202"]="Commander Mort... Hm, it's highly likely that his spirit is still battling Pirate Skeletons! A warrior like him shouldn't be subjected to such circumstances. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue2017301"]="I see... He was fighting for the Radiance even in death. Thank you, adventurer. May he be welcomed by the valkyries.",
    ["Dialogue2017401"]="Alright, next—Gunner Matthew. He should still be waiting for orders on the gun deck. Could it be because he's too dedicated to his duty?",
    ["Dialogue2017501"]="Has he been awaiting an order that will never arrive? His death is so sad.",
    ["Dialogue2017601"]="Bard Ruth... This seems to be a passenger on the Radiance, but why would a passenger have an obsession too?",
    ["Dialogue2017701"]="To bring happiness to the dead? Haha, bards are so weirdly unique even in death.",
    ["Dialogue2017801"]="The last person is... Ah, this is very sad. Priest Parker. It looks like Strouf didn't manage bless the Radiance this time round.",
    ["Dialogue2017901"]="Adventurer, it's been a long time.",
    ["Dialogue2017902"]="Hahaha, bards go where the stories are.",
    ["Dialogue2017903"]="Do you know the origin of the Shipwreck?",
    ["Dialogue2017904"]="Haha, I knew you would say that. See those treasures scattered on the ground? Bring a gold coin over; I'll tell you about the truth that may lie behind it.",
    ["Dialogue2018001"]="See this picture on the coin? Doesn't it look familiar?",
    ["Dialogue2018002"]="The words translate as \"Honor to the Nerius Family.\"",
    ["Dialogue2018003"]="From the look on your face, you didn't expect that, did you? That's right, these gold coins belong to one of the royal families. They're property of the Nerius Family.",
    ["Dialogue2018004"]="I'm afraid that's not possible. Although the Nerius Family isn't known for their martial prowess, pirates stealing such a vast amount of treasure is the stuff of fantasy.",
    ["Dialogue2018005"]="According to ancient texts, the successor candidate for the Nerius Family three hundred years ago was the greatest captain in the sea of Migard.",
    ["Dialogue2018006"]="But she didn't become the king, and no accounts exist of her subsequent whereabouts. Don't you find that strange?",
    ["Dialogue2018007"]="Finding out more would be almost impossible. The whole affair is a closely guarded secret of the Nerius Family. But the name of that ship has been passed down through other means.",
    ["Dialogue2018008"]="It's called the Valkyrie. An excellent name, don't you think?",
    ["Dialogue2018101"]="Hi! I knew you would come!",
    ["Dialogue2018102"]="Because you're my lucky star! You appear out of nowhere every time I'm looking for some kind of spoils! Let me guess your objective this time... Is it the Shipwreck?",
    ["Dialogue2018103"]="I thought the Kraken and the Shipwreck were just legends! When the Chamber of Commerce told me that the Shipwreck appeared, I could hardly believe my ears! This is rare opportunity. Do you have any idea how much treasure is on that pirate ship?!",
    ["Dialogue2018104"]="That's right! But I'm not after those things. Gold coins may be valuable, you can't carry many.",
    ["Dialogue2018105"]="My target is the captain's saber!",
    ["Dialogue2018106"]="A saber that’s been steeped in the aura of darkness for thousands of years would be priceless on the black market! Even Golden Thief Bug shards can't compare!",
    ["Dialogue2018107"]="Heh! Such wit! Your stupidity, ah no... your kindness will make you fodder for those black market merchants. How 'bout this, wanna make a deal?",
    ["Dialogue2018108"]="The cabin in the deepest part of the ship must be the territory of the Shipwreck's captain. Get the saber for me and I'll pay you. Deal?",
    ["Dialogue2018201"]="It looks like you've made a triumphant return. Where's the saber?",
    ["Dialogue2018202"]="Destroyed?! Do you know how much you've cost us?!",
    ["Dialogue2018203"]="...I guess you're right. I may be a merchant who will chase after every penny, but I've never been unethical or immoral.",
    ["Dialogue2018204"]="I would never sell dangerous items just to make money. No, I, the great Dinza, have a great sense of social responsibility.",
    ["Dialogue2018205"]="Leave me for a while... *Cries* It feels like I've take one step further away from financial freedom now. Such mixed feelings.",
    ["Dialogue2018301"]="Huh? So adventurers also come to places like this?",
    ["Dialogue2018302"]="We're a rescue team from Geffen's Adventure Guild. We received an SOS from the Shipwreck. The person we've come to save is a lady called Arlene.",
    ["Dialogue2018303"]="If you find any clues, please let us know. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue2018401"]="St-stay away!",
    ["Dialogue2018402"]="Ahhhhhhhhhh! It's you! Ahhhhh! Quick, save me! There are ghosts everywhere! Ahhhhhhh! It's so scary! Ahhhhhh!",
    ["Dialogue2018501"]="Th-thank you. You really helped me out.",
    ["Dialogue2018601"]="I-I took an adventurer job to exterminate spirits on this ship.",
    ["Dialogue2018602"]="The chivalry said that according to ancient texts, although the leaders of the ship are Drake and the Kraken, there's actually another person hiding behind them.",
    ["Dialogue2018603"]="Adventurers who board the Shipwreck all hear a female voice calling out to them.",
    ["Dialogue2018604"]="It must be a more dangerous, sentient spirit!",
    ["Dialogue2018605"]="I'm not afraid! A knight is fearless!",
    ["Dialogue2018606"]="I'm sorry. I'm terrified... but if the others knew, I'll forever be mocked as a knight who's afraid of ghosts!",
    ["Dialogue2018701"]="That voice! I-is it a spirit!?",
    ["Dialogue2018702"]="Aren't all spirits like that?! They lure you over and then... Ahhhh! I'm too afraid to go on! Adventurer, I'm counting on you! I'm going to hide!",
    ["Dialogue2018901"]="H-human? Argh! It's a human! Ahhhh!",
    ["Dialogue2018902"]="E-excuse me, I haven't seen a living person for a long time. You gave me a shock.",
    ["Dialogue2019001"]="My name is Colorful. I'm sorry, I can't remember anything else.",
    ["Dialogue2019002"]="Huh? You want to exterminate me? But I'm just a normal, wandering spirit. Is there a misunderstanding?",
    ["Dialogue2019003"]="What now? I don't want to disappear. I want to find my memories. I want to know why I became like this!",
    ["Dialogue2019004"]="A substitute? Let me think. I remember that an Axe-wielding Skel Pirate took my gold necklace just before I died. Could you retrieve it for me?",
    ["Dialogue2019005"]="\"I've exterminated the spirit! This necklace is all that's left of her!\" ...Like this?",
    ["Dialogue2019101"]="I-is there any progress?",
    ["Dialogue2019102"]="The spirit has been exterminated? This necklace is all that's left of her? This is great, adventurer! No wonder I stopped hearing that weird sound!",
    ["Dialogue2019103"]="A-adventurer, there's one more thing. Could you...",
    ["Dialogue2019104"]="H-help me keep what happened today a secret? Keep it from everybody... from Ivan...",
    ["Dialogue2019105"]="Thank you! Adventurer, it was great seeing you here! I'll report back now!",
    ["Dialogue2019201"]="I-is it all over?",
    ["Dialogue2019202"]="Phew! Thank you, adventurer. This is the first time in centuries that someone's said they want to exterminate me. It was so frightening!",
    ["Dialogue2019203"]="Adventurer, you're the first living person I've seen in all these years! Could you listen to my wish? There are some things I can't do alone!",
    ["Dialogue2019301"]="I want to recover my memories. Ever since I turned into this, I can't remember most of what happened when I was alive.",
    ["Dialogue2019302"]="And probably because I died here, I can only move around this area. If I were to wander further, I might just disintegrate.",
    ["Dialogue2019303"]="That's right. Adventurer, could you retrieve some of my belongings from when I was alive? They might be able to help me recall some things.",
    ["Dialogue2019304"]="I remember... I have my own cabin on this ship. There's a big table and a comfy chair inside. When I get tired from reading, I'll take a nap on the chair.",
    ["Dialogue2019305"]="There are many books in there. And... and there seems be a photo on the wall? I can only vaguely remember these details.",
    ["Dialogue2019401"]="This photo! Th-this person looks familiar... M-mother?!",
    ["Dialogue2019501"]="This person in the photo should be my mother.",
    ["Dialogue2019502"]="That's right. The first word that came to mind when I saw her was \"mother.\" But apart from that, I can't remember anything else.",
    ["Dialogue2019503"]="Mother... She assigned the royal guards to me... Royal guards... Royal guards?",
    ["Dialogue2019504"]="Ah yes! My royal guards were still fighting nearby to protect me, then...",
    ["Dialogue2019505"]="Adventurer! Could you search the vicinity? Their clothes are different from the Axe-wielding Skel Pirates! If you could find something on them...",
    ["Dialogue2019601"]="Nerius? Nerius... I-I remember my name.",
    ["Dialogue2019602"]="My name is Colorful Nerius!",
    ["Dialogue2019701"]="I remember my name.",
    ["Dialogue2019702"]="Royalty? No, I only remember my name and some fuzzy flashbacks. Oh right, there's a log!",
    ["Dialogue2019703"]="Do you remember the cabin I mentioned? The log I kept must be in there!",
    ["Dialogue2019704"]="I wrote it? Why do I remember that I was the one who wrote it? Wh-who am I?",
    ["Dialogue2019801"]="Day 1: The Valkyrie received an order to escort the Nerius Family's gold coins to Einbroch for a third trade event. Estimated time to destination: 7 days.",
    ["Dialogue2019802"]="Day 4: A message from Prontera Alchemy Center said there will be thick fog over the sea of Midgard in two days and advised the Valkyrie to return. The captain decided to continue onward after evaluating the speed of the voyage.",
    ["Dialogue2019803"]="Day 6: The thickness has grown denser. Everyone on board the Valkyrie is on guard for Kraken's attack.",
    ["Dialogue2019804"]="Day 7: ...",
    ["Dialogue2019805"]="There's no more? What happened? Why can't I recall the most crucial part!",
    ["Dialogue2019806"]="What could have sealed my memory? My gut feeling tells me I've forgotten something extremely important.",
    ["Dialogue2019807"]="...I'm sorry, adventurer. You've gone through so much trouble for me, but I've only managed to remember my name.",
    ["Dialogue2019808"]="You're right, it might be better if certain things are left forgotten. But I will not give up searching for the truth! I-I need to reorganize my thoughts.",
    ["Dialogue2019901"]="Hi! It's been a while! Have you come for the beautiful scenery too?",
    ["Dialogue2019902"]="I think so too, because you're always on the right track.",
    ["Dialogue2019903"]="I'm here to train my combat skills! But my butterfly hair accessory was taken by a Marina. I hate those things!",
    ["Dialogue2019904"]="That hair accessory is very important to me. Please go with me to take it back!",
    ["Dialogue2020001"]="I-it's broken...",
    ["Dialogue2020002"]="It's been with me since the day I became an adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2020003"]="A-and, it's...",
    ["Dialogue2020101"]="...Ah, it's you! Long time no see!\n<size=18>Sigh, </size><size=18>what should I do? </size><size=18>It's such a pain.</size>",
    ["Dialogue2020102"]="Oh, did you overhear? My good friend Veronica is getting married, but things are so busy at the academy that I can't leave. Sigh, I've got her a wedding gift, but how can I <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver it to her</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2020103"]="Really? Then I'll be counting on you to convey my best wishes. Oh right, the wedding will be held at <color=#CA2E0AFF>the church</color>. When you see the bride, Veronica, please send her my congratulations!",
    ["Dialogue2020201"]="(Chino looks at you warily.)\n...Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue2020202"]="...Yes, Veronica's wedding will take place here. The ceremony is about to start. If you are guest, it's about time to enter.",
    ["Dialogue2020301"]="(Chino frowns. He looks like he's thinking hard.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue2020302"]="...I look troubled? ...Actually, I lost my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wedding Invitation</color> but I can't remember where. If I don't find it, I'll miss the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue2020303"]="(Chino seems shocked.)\n...Is that so? Thank you. I think I might have dropped the invitation at one of the places I visited today. I've only been to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin's Statue</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force Training Course</color>. Let's split up and look for it.",
    ["Dialogue2020401"]="Haha! This must be my lucky day! Who would have thought I'd find Commander Bohr's Wedding Invitation while cleaning the sandpit. I do love a good wedding!",
    ["Dialogue2020402"]="...Huh? This is your friend's? And you want me to return it? Is there a name on it?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>\"Chino\"? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh, there really is a name.</color></size>\nAhem. If you want something from a soldier, there's no use asking. You'll have to go through his fists!",
    ["Dialogue2020501"]="This is not my day. Forget it, just take the invitation!",
    ["Dialogue2020601"]="Wow, you found the invitation?\n(Chino brushes the dust off the invitation and carefully puts it in his pocket.)",
    ["Dialogue2020602"]="Thank you. Without your help. I'd be stuck outside. Speaking of which, the wedding will start in less than an hour. Hurry, go wait <color=#CA2E0AFF>inside the church</color>. As for me, I still have some preparations to make. Well then, see you later.",
    ["Dialogue2020701"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Sigh, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>the wedding is starting soon. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Where is Master Bohr?</color></size>\nHello, are you a guest?",
    ["Dialogue2020702"]="Oh, so you're a guest of Veronica's? She will be delighted to see you! Please be seated in the front row!",
    ["Dialogue2020703"]="Where is Veronica? Sigh, she's probably reminiscing about her father in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery behind the church</color>. The poor child lost her father at a very young age. This means that, unlike other girls, she can't hold her father's arm as she walks down the aisle.",
    ["Dialogue2020704"]="I think she must be telling her departed relatives the good news about her wedding now. I hope she doesn't feel lonely.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>You should be by her side at this time. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hurry back, Master Bohr!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2020801"]="...A gift from Alice? I'm so glad she thinks of me even though she's on Izlude Island. And thank you for bringing this precious gift to me!",
    ["Dialogue2020802"]="(Veronica casts her gaze downward.)\nEveryone has been wishing me happiness but... will I really be happy?",
    ["Dialogue2020803"]="Actually Bohr and I only met a few times before our engagement. Although I've loved him since the beginning, I don't know what he thinks of me. There have been countless rumors about this wedding going around the capital. I'm honestly scared that Bohr only chose to be with me because it benefits his family.",
    ["Dialogue2020804"]="Sigh, maybe Bohr really is uninterested in this wedding. That's why he hasn't even shown up yet. After all, a man as wise as him wouldn't be attracted by beauty alone.",
    ["Dialogue2020805"]="(Veronica smiles bitterly.)\n...Beauty might be a kind of weapon, but it doesn't give someone true confidence. Thankfully I have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>lucky crown</color> made from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica Flowers</color>. As long as I have it, I'll have the courage to pursue my happiness.",
    ["Dialogue2020806"]="(Veronica pauses for a moment, then starts smiling at you.)\nThank you for you encouragement. Indeed, I shouldn't be sad on such an important day. Furthermore, I have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>lucky crown</color> made from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica Flowers</color>. As long as I have it, I will have confidence and courage.",
    ["Dialogue2020807"]="These flowers and I are entwined by fate. It's said that when my father proposed to my mother, it was because he used a crown made from Veronica Flowers that my mother fell in love with him. They named me \"Veronica\" because they hoped that I would be as confident as the flower and bloom with pride. That's why I want to carry this blessing as I walk down the red carpet today.",
    ["Dialogue2020808"]="Speaking of which, I got my brother, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aronst</color>, to bring the crown from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>palace</color>, but it's been so long. Why isn't he back yet?",
    ["Dialogue2020901"]="(Aronst looks anxious.)\nWhat should I do, what should I do? How am I supposed to explain this to my sister?! She thinks the crown is the most precious thing in the world. I couldn't stand to see her sad again.",
    ["Dialogue2020902"]="...H-hello! My sister asked you to check on the crown? Erm, it isn't with me now. If you were to ask where it is... Um, it was taken by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crow</color>, hahaha...\n(Aronst laughs awkwardly.)",
    ["Dialogue2020903"]="I chased the Crow all over the palace. I tried shouting at it, throwing stones at it, everything... Nothing worked. I could only watch as it flew higher and higher toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate</color>. Sigh, this is a disaster. How am I going to find that one Crow among all the other Crows in the wild?!",
    ["Dialogue2020904"]="...That crow took something from you before too? You know where it is? What a relief! Please find that Crow! We need to find it before the wedding starts!",
    ["Dialogue2021001"]="Why?! That damn Crow has ruined my sister's beloved crown! I can't let her wear it like this, but how can I fix it?",
    ["Dialogue2021002"]="...What? The headgear merchant outside South Gate can fix it? Great! Hurry, lead me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smile Assistance</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2021101"]="...Oh, by Odin! This crown... I can imagine how beautiful it once was! But how did it end up like this?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is exactly why I hate letting men touch such precious headgear! They ruin everything beautiful.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> So uncouth!</color></size>\nHi! You would like me to fix this crown? It won't be that difficult. As long as you can provide me with enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica Flowers</color>, I can make it good as new!",
    ["Dialogue2021102"]="Can you fix it? It's very important to me!",
    ["Dialogue2021103"]="Of course! There isn't any headgear that cannot be crafted or fixed by Smile Assistance! But the material needed for this crown is very special. In order to restore it to its former glory, I'll need enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica Flowers</color>! But...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But Veronica Flowers aren't that easy to come by!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2021104"]="Veronica Flowers? I think my sister mentioned before that Father found them <color=#CA2E0AFF>in a remote area at the top of a tall cliff</color>. Do I need to climb a cliff? B-but I'm afraid of heights!",
    ["Dialogue2021201"]="(Chino looks anxious and angry.)\nMy Veronica Flowers... What did you do?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Can't I even take care of these flowers properly?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2021202"]="Why am I so upset? Because these Veronica Flowers are my babies. I spent so much effort cultivating them and caring for them, yet you...\n(Chino's expression starts to darken.)",
    ["Dialogue2021203"]="(Chino looks shocked.)\nVeronica needs these flowers? I understand now. In that case, please take them. I only have one request: When the crown has been fixed, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>return any leftover flowers to me</color>. Don't just throw them away.",
    ["Dialogue2021301"]="(Aronst's eyes light up with excitement.)\nSmile Assistance, you're the best! The crown looks exactly like before! Alright, let's hurry and get it to my sister!",
    ["Dialogue2021302"]="Huh? You can't go back with me yet? Alright then. I don't know what could be more important than seeing my sister wear this crown, but remember to hurry up. If you miss the wedding, you're gonna miss seeing how beautiful she looks. You'll surely regret it! I'll get back to the church first. See you later!",
    ["Dialogue2021401"]="(Chino looks glum as he stands still, seemingly lost in thought.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue2021402"]="...These are... Oh, thank you. I'll take care of them.\n(Chino carefully puts the flowers to one side.)",
    ["Dialogue2021403"]="...Oh right! The wedding! The wedding is going to start soon. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back to the church</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2021501"]="(Veronica looks flabbergasted,)\n...What... what happened to Bohr? He was trying to protect me. That's why the assassins got him. It's all my fault!",
    ["Dialogue2021502"]="Veronica, please don't blame yourself. Master Bohr didn't lose consciousness because of the assassins' attack. He's been poisoned.",
    ["Dialogue2021503"]="That's right. According to the test, there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>two types of poison</color> in Master Bohr's body. It was a combination of the poisons that caused him to lose consciousness. This makes the treatment much more complicated.",
    ["Dialogue2021504"]="Adventurer, please bring me an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Magic Core</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vitata</color>, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Magic Core</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color> and an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Magic Core</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mummy</color>. I'll tell you what to do next once we have them.",
    ["Dialogue2021601"]="Very good, you were a lot quicker than I expected. I want to wake Master Bohr up by using these magic cores to cast a spell. Please follow my instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the cores around Bohr's body</color>. I will borrow the powers of these three attributes in Odin's name to expel the poison from Master Bohr's body.",
    ["Dialogue2021701"]="Don't worry, Master Bohr's life is no longer in danger, but he'll need to rest for a while before he wakes up completely.",
    ["Dialogue2021702"]="(Veronica sighs in relief.)\nThank you, Archbishop Wolmas.",
    ["Dialogue2021703"]="This is not over yet, there must be a thorough investigation! We need to know who dared attempt to murder the leading commander of the Kingdom Defense Force!",
    ["Dialogue2021704"]="I've already consulted the Archbishop. The two types of poison that caused Master Bohr to lose consciousness entered his body at different times. Regardless, it was the presence of both poisons that caused him to lose consciousness. Which means... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Bohr only came in contact with the second poison during the wedding</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2021705"]="The only person who came into close contact with Master Bohr during the wedding was—\n(Akand looks toward Veronica.)",
    ["Dialogue2021706"]="(Aronst's face turns red in anger.)\nHey, hey! How dare you suspect my sister?! She's Bohr's wife! Why would she harm him?!",
    ["Dialogue2021707"]="Please let me finish, Lord Aronst. I do not think that Veronica would harm Master Bohr, but she might have been used. If <color=#CA2E0AFF>something on her person</color> was coated with poison—Miss Veronica, where is your <color=#CA2E0AFF>crown</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2021708"]="(Veronica is stunned for a moment, then she reaches to touch the top of her head but finds nothing there.)\n...Wh-where's my crown? Wait, I remember now. During the wedding, Bohr did mention that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the crown smelled strange</color>. After the chaos started, I didn't pay much attention to the crown. Could it really be...?",
    ["Dialogue2021709"]="Then I'm afraid my guess might be correct. The perpetrator coated the crown with poison, then to avoid being found out, stole the crown during the chaos. The question now is, who came in contact with the crown before the wedding? I believe the perpetrator is among them.",
    ["Dialogue2021710"]="The only people here who came into contact with the crown at the venue are Veronica, Lord Aronst, and you. The other people who came into contact with it are Smile Assistance and Chino. I don't believe Veronica, Lord Aronst, Smile Assistance, or you have any reason to harm Master Bohr, but Chino on the other hand...",
    ["Dialogue2021711"]="I investigated the guests straight after Akand's advice. Chino was nowhere to be found when the chaos was over! He must be... Wait a second, why does the name Chino sound familiar? Isn't he the illegitimate—",
    ["Dialogue2021712"]="(Akand coughs deliberately and interrupts Bernard.)\n<size=24>Ahem!</size>\nIn any case, it seems that Chino is the perpetrator. We must arrest him.",
    ["Dialogue2021713"]="Wait a moment, Akand! It doesn't seem very fair to pass judgment on someone based solely on speculation. Could you please investigate further?",
    ["Dialogue2021714"]="Veronica, please leave this to the Kingdom Defense Force! Master Bohr needs you now. Please look after him in the church. We'll take care of everything else. Please don't worry!",
    ["Dialogue2021801"]="(Veronica is still frowning.)\nI still don't think someone should be arrested based on speculation alone. It's just my gut feeling, but I don't think Chino is responsible. Also, did you notice that Commander Bernard and Akand seemed to be hiding something when they were talking about Chino?",
    ["Dialogue2021802"]="You think so too? Looks like things aren't as simple as we thought. Adventurer, I would like to ask for your help to investigate the truth behind Bohr's poisoning. We mustn't let the real perpetrator get away! The Defense Force respects you. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>speak to Commander Bernard and Akand to get more information</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2021901"]="...Huh? Is something the matter? The Defense Force is busy tracking down Chino. Do you have a new lead?",
    ["Dialogue2021902"]="Did I encounter anything strange before the wedding? Hm... I was with Commander Bohr before the wedding. We were...",
    ["Dialogue2022001"]="Bernard, you do still remember what happened on the day the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> was stolen, don't you?",
    ["Dialogue2022002"]="(Bernard looks solemn.)\nHow could I have forgotten! Not only was the holy relic stolen that day, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>three princes of the Gaebolg Family were murdered</color> too. But I don't understand. What's this got to do with our current investigation?",
    ["Dialogue2022003"]="Think, Bernard. Has it never crossed your mind that stealing the Fragment of Ymir's Heart was not the alchemist's sole motive?",
    ["Dialogue2022004"]="You mean... Baroshev had a part in killing the princes too?",
    ["Dialogue2022005"]="...Until we have proof, this is all just speculation. I heard that the alchemist used Thief Bugs from the sewer for his experiments. Start by getting some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Toxin Samples</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mutant Thief Bugs</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2022101"]="Indeed, the markings on this Lunatic are similar to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>snake scale marks</color> on the princes' bodies. It looks like the princes ingested poison made by Baroshev. It's not only deadly, it can also <color=#CA2E0AFF>create the illusion of the serpent's curse</color>.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But the curse has always been a closely guarded secret of the seven royal families; how did Baroshev find out?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2022102"]="Alright, there's nothing more to investigate here. Let's get back to the surface.",
    ["Dialogue2022201"]="After the investigation, we returned to the surface. Surprisingly, Akand suddenly appeared the moment we entered the Training Course. He was all anxious and said he had an emergency to report to Commander Bohr. As for the details of the conversation, you're better off asking <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> himself!",
    ["Dialogue2022301"]="...My conversation with the Commander?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Did he sense something?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2022302"]="This should not be mentioned again, but since you're a close friend of the Defense Force, I'll tell you. I believe you'll understand why I suspected Chino after knowing this.",
    ["Dialogue2022401"]="As you've seen, Chino is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>illegitimate child</color> of the Richard Family. He's the younger brother of Commander Bohr, who has the same father. What shocked me the most was that Commander Bohr wasn't in the least surprised when I told him. In fact, he asked me to keep it a secret.",
    ["Dialogue2022402"]="He must have known Chino's identity long ago, but has never suspected him.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Master Bohr, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>look at what your kindness has gotten you. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I won't let him get away with this.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2022501"]="(Fitz is panting.)\n...Chino...<size=24>We found Chino!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2022502"]="Hmph! When we found Chino, he was sneaking out of a secret passage at <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate Cemetery</color>! I never knew he could be so stubborn! No matter how much we interrogated him, he refused to say a word.",
    ["Dialogue2022601"]="(Chino's tense expression cracks when he sees you.)\n...Why are you here? Do you think it was me too?",
    ["Dialogue2022602"]="(Chino falls silent for a moment, then his expression relaxes.)\n...Under the circumstances, you're probably the only one willing to believe me. As an illegitimate child, I'm used to people's prejudices. Since the Defense Force is adamant that I'm the perpetrator, I refuse to tell them a single thing!",
    ["Dialogue2022603"]="(Chino's gaze shifts a little upon hearing Veronica's name.)\nEven... even Veronica believes me? Thank you for telling me that. You have no idea how important it is to me. Since you two still believe in me, I won't let you down.",
    ["Dialogue2022604"]="Actually, I saw a familiar face at the church. He's found me and bewitched me on many occasions. So when I saw him at the wedding, I immediately raised my guard and kept a close eye on him. During the chaos, I saw him pick Veronica's crown up from the floor. I wanted to see what he was up to, so I followed him out of the church.",
    ["Dialogue2022701"]="...Hey! Stop! This is our territory! If you come any closer, there'll be a price to pay!",
    ["Dialogue2022801"]="When I hit a brick wall, I decided to stop investigating and return to the surface, but the Defense Force soldiers captured me the moment I emerged from the tomb! They've been keeping watch over me ever since. But as I've been here all this time, I'm sure the suspicious man didn't escape from the sewer.",
    ["Dialogue2022802"]="I've been thinking while I've been stuck here. I might know who blocked my progress. In any case, I think <color=#CA2E0AFF>the area where Hobos gather in the sewer</color> is worth investigating. He might be hiding there. But as I can't move around freely right now, could you please investigate for me? You're the only person I can trust right now.",
    ["Dialogue2022901"]="Hey! Stop! Or I'll have to teach you a lesson!",
    ["Dialogue2022902"]="A poisoner? How could Master Bohr's poisoner be in the sewer?",
    ["Dialogue2022903"]="Hmph, you won't find who you're looking for here. Get lost!",
    ["Dialogue2022904"]="Eh... Everyone in Prontera knows what happened to Master Bohr, don't get me wrong! I heard he's been poisoned. I wonder if he's still alive?",
    ["Dialogue2022905"]="Hmph, are you looking down on the sewer dwellers? Get lost!",
    ["Dialogue2022906"]="Eh... So you were trying to trick me! Since I've been exposed, there's no need for any more talk. Die!",
    ["Dialogue2022907"]="Hmph, you don't make sense. Take your nonsense elsewhere!",
    ["Dialogue2023001"]="(Simmons looks at you in shock.)\n...H-how did this crown end up with you?",
    ["Dialogue2023002"]="Huh? Chino? Suspicious man? Hobos?\nForget it, I'm so confused. You're better off explaining it to Commander Bernard at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force Training Course</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2023101"]="You're back. Veronica told me what happened. Thank you for your concern; I'm fine now. About the chaos at the wedding, let's discuss it properly.\nFirstly, I want to apologize to you, Chino. If I'd woken up earlier, you wouldn't have been under suspicion for so long.",
    ["Dialogue2023102"]="(A look of surprise flashes across Chino's face.)\nYou... you don't think it was me either?",
    ["Dialogue2023103"]="I trust you. And I'm sorry that your identity was revealed under such circumstances.\nActually, I've known that Chino is my brother for a long time. But due to many different reasons, I couldn't acknowledge our relationship. However, I've never suspected him. He's not someone who would hurt people for his own gain.",
    ["Dialogue2023104"]="(Chino's expression is complicated.)\n...Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue2023105"]="As for the suspicious man who has been in contact with Chino, he is but a pawn for the real mastermind. Think about it. If all he wanted was to kill me, why did he contact Chino? The answer is simple. It's not just my life that the mastermind wants. He's after the power of the Kingdom Defense Force.",
    ["Dialogue2023106"]="What? Did they think that the Kingdom Defense Force would obey just anyone? If Master Bohr isn't the supreme commander, I will not recognize the force's legitimacy!",
    ["Dialogue2023107"]="(Bohr smiles.)\nThank you, Bernard. This might not have been his first idea, so I was thinking about his motive behind trying to kill me. Then it hit me, the issue I'm investigating must have threatened his interests.",
    ["Dialogue2023108"]="The issue you're investigating... Could it be the poisoning of the three princes?",
    ["Dialogue2023109"]="That's right. I found some clues, so the perpetrator must have felt threatened. The fact that he tried to kill me only further proves my theory, and now I'm sure of his identity. However, I still don't have enough evidence, so please forgive me for not revealing his name.",
    ["Dialogue2023110"]="Now that this is all over and Chino has been proven innocent, there's one more thing to do. I owe something to someone immeasurably important to me. I owe her a grand wedding.",
    ["Dialogue2023111"]="(Veronica looks at Bohr in surprise.)\nBohr...",
    ["Dialogue2023112"]="I've heard about those rumors from Thurman. I'm sorry for leaving you in a state of anxiety. Veronica, please believe me. I, Bohr Richard, did not propose for any reason other than my true love for you. I want to marry you and give you the happiness you deserve. Please, believe me. Now, let us <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the church</color> and continue with the wedding.",
    ["Dialogue2023201"]="Now, I'm not just the head of the Richard Family and the supreme commander of the Kingdom Defense Force. I'm also Veronica's husband and may one day become a father. This means that apart from protecting this kingdom, I will also need to protect my family. This is why I've decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>step down as a successor candidate for the throne</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2023202"]="The interests of the kingdom are far more important to me than competing for the throne. By giving up my right as successor, I believe that the mastermind will let down his guard and it will help in my next investigation. I may have no interest in competing for the throne, but I will not allow some lowly schemer to ascend the throne and lead the kingdom. There are still many things left to be done.",
    ["Dialogue2023203"]="(Veronica holds Bohr's hand tightly.)\nNo matter what happens, I will always be by your side.",
    ["Dialogue2023204"]="(Bohr smiles.)\nThank you, Veronica.\nAdventurer, and thank you for witnessing this magical moment.",
    ["Dialogue2023301"]="(There's no invitation near Odin's Statue. Chino mentioned that he visited the Defense Force Training Course; let's check there.)",
    ["Dialogue2023401"]="(Strange green markings have appeared on Bohr's face. Although he has no visible wounds, his breathing is weak and he has fallen unconscious.)",
    ["Dialogue2023501"]="(A strange marking can be seen under the Lunatic's fur. It looks like some kind of scale?)",
    ["Dialogue2023601"]="(The footprints seem to lead toward the cliff ahead.)",
    ["Dialogue2023701"]="(The footprints seem to lead on ahead.)",
    ["Dialogue2023801"]="Leigh fell in love with a human once too. He was a rather handsome actor. I think his name was Grute.",
    ["Dialogue2023802"]="Huh? You know him too? Is he forgetful like Dilber?",
    ["Dialogue2023803"]="Leigh has been investigating the truth. When I shared what I knew about Dilber, it seemed as though she had something to say. She must know something! Could you help me find out? Please!",
    ["Dialogue2023901"]="Hello, it's rare to see humans make it here. Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue2023902"]="Oh, so Lucie asked you to speak with me. I do know some things, but...",
    ["Dialogue2023903"]="Sigh, those male Obeaunes are here again.",
    ["Dialogue2023904"]="Lucie probably told you what happened to me. Ever since then, I'm constantly being harassed by male Obeaunes. They say things like I would be better off marrying them than getting involved with a land-dweller.",
    ["Dialogue2023905"]="They can't hold a candle to Grute when it comes to looks or reliability! They really do have an inflated opinion of themselves!",
    ["Dialogue2024001"]="Thank you. I think you're a reliable person just like Grute. I'll tell you the results of my investigation.",
    ["Dialogue2024101"]="My emotional journey was just like Lucie's. I thought Grute betrayed me. It made me have nothing but pure hatred for humans.",
    ["Dialogue2024102"]="But I was older than Lucie, and more reflective. So I daringly proposed a request to Master Strouf to find out if Grute really loved me.",
    ["Dialogue2024103"]="At first I thought Master Strouf would fly into a rage and sentence me to death for my stubbornness, but surprisingly he gave me a choice instead.",
    ["Dialogue2024104"]="If I chose to know the truth, I would never be able to set foot on land again. If I wanted to remain free, then I would have to live with not knowing for the rest of my life. This choice will set a precedent for all Obeaunes who fall in love with humans.",
    ["Dialogue2024105"]="Both choices were equally cruel, but regardless of which choice I made, I'll never be able to be with Grute, so I chose to know the truth.",
    ["Dialogue2024106"]="The truth is, this is a curse that Master Strouf has placed upon the Obeaunes. No other species can fall in love with an Obeaune. Otherwise, the curse will activate and they will forget all that has happened.",
    ["Dialogue2024107"]="As a citizen of the sea, what happened next is something that I dare not say...",
    ["Dialogue2024108"]="(In a hushed tone.) I hid my diary on the altar's platform. Please give it to Grute. It contains my thoughts and part of the truth.",
    ["Dialogue2024109"]="I hope that Lucie will be able to get over this. What happened was not any human's fault. The fault lies in our identity as Obeaunes.",
    ["Dialogue2024201"]="You're... Excuse me, I seem to remember you. You're...",
    ["Dialogue2024202"]="For me? Leigh? I have a feeling that... I know this name... Thank you for bringing this for me!",
    ["Dialogue2024301"]="How did it go? Did Leigh say anything?",
    ["Dialogue2024302"]="There it is again! Adventurer, you must know the truth, right?",
    ["Dialogue2024303"]="Hmph! What are you and Leigh hiding?! I'm going to find out for myself! Don't try to stop me! Dilber, I will bring you back!",
    ["Dialogue2024401"]="Goblin Forest is such a contradictory place. Both nature and technology coexist. It's so uniquely beautiful.",
    ["Dialogue2024402"]="Haha, you're right! But this mysterious land constantly attracts people like me with a fascination for the unknown.",
    ["Dialogue2024403"]="Speaking of which, are you interested in Goblin civilization?",
    ["Dialogue2024404"]="Then help me get some Gears from Goblin Steamriders! The secrets of the distant past are imprinted on those Gears.",
    ["Dialogue2024501"]="You got the Gears, yeah? Tell me, do you think Goblins are capable of creating such intricate items?",
    ["Dialogue2024502"]="That's right. Legend has it that Goblins were more intelligent that humans in ancient times. Their technology was highly advanced, and they easily dominated the whole of Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue2024503"]="But the unfortunate thing was that they put their faith in the demon Baphomet.",
    ["Dialogue2024504"]="Odin punished the Goblins and took away their intelligence. They were never the same again, reduced to the monsters that we know today. It was then that humans started to prosper.",
    ["Dialogue2024505"]="And this was how the Goblins you see today came to be. Although they're still able to use the tools created by their ancestors, they will never be able to stop the progress of the human race.",
    ["Dialogue2024506"]="Baphomet is often known as the bane of humanity, but to the Goblins, aren't humans their bane instead? Hahaha, what an interesting cycle.",
    ["Dialogue2024601"]="These Goblins are so unsporting!",
    ["Dialogue2024602"]="It great to have you here! I want to fight a single Goblin to hone my combat skills but that group of Goblins are so unsporting! They always attack together! Can you help me?",
    ["Dialogue2024603"]="According to my observations, a group of five Goblins will walk past here soon.",
    ["Dialogue2024604"]="Could you block off four of them so I can have a fair one-on-one fight with the last Goblin?",
    ["Dialogue2024605"]="Great! Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue2024701"]="....",
    ["Dialogue2024702"]="Didn't we agree to leave one? No, wait... You can take out five Goblins so easily, while I still have to think of ways to fight them one-on-one. I'm still so weak...",
    ["Dialogue2024703"]="I won't give up! You'd better watch out! Who knows, I might become stronger than you one day! That's that! I'm off to train now!",
    ["Dialogue2024801"]="Huh? Are you the adventurer from the Shipwreck that time?",
    ["Dialogue2024802"]="These parts are under the administration of Geffen. We carry out patrols periodically to check if there are any conflicts between adventurers and Goblins... Huh? Did you hear something?",
    ["Dialogue2024901"]="Stay away! I-I'm very strong!",
    ["Dialogue2024902"]="A-adventurer?!",
    ["Dialogue2025001"]="Th-thank you! If it weren't for you, Poya and I might have been eaten by the Goblins.",
    ["Dialogue2025002"]="Ah, wait! My lute! They've taken my lute!",
    ["Dialogue2025003"]="My lute goes everywhere with me! It's literally my soul! It's more important than even my own life! Adventurer, take Poya to safety. I have to get my lute back!",
    ["Dialogue2025101"]="Huh? The voice I heard belonged to a man. Why do you only have a lady with you?",
    ["Dialogue2025201"]="Rest assured, I'll do everything in my power to protect her!",
    ["Dialogue2025401"]="My lute...",
    ["Dialogue2025402"]="Why? Even if you don't understand music, why would you do such a thing? Poya gave it to me as a token of her love. Poya...",
    ["Dialogue2025403"]="(Morts' lute is in pieces all over the ground. The Goblins probably smashed it while waving it around.)",
    ["Dialogue2025404"]="(There's no persuading Morts when he's in this state. I'll just have to protect him first!)",
    ["Dialogue2025501"]="MORTS!",
    ["Dialogue2025502"]="Adventurer, do not interrupt!",
    ["Dialogue2025503"]="Didn't you stop to think about me?! Going to such a dangerous place all alone... What would I do if... if something happened to you?",
    ["Dialogue2025504"]="If you care so much about that lute, I can make you another one. I'm good at making instruments now. I can keep making as many lutes as you need, but if you weren't here anymore...",
    ["Dialogue2025505"]="P-please... Don't be so reckless ever again. *Sobs*",
    ["Dialogue2025601"]="Indeed, this is tough...",
    ["Dialogue2025602"]="Huh? Oh! You're the kid I met back in the sewer! You're right on time. You're about to witness the birth of a new dish!",
    ["Dialogue2025603"]="I haven't decided on a name yet. Let's settle for a boring one first, we'll call it \"Goblin Stir-fry!\"",
    ["Dialogue2025604"]="Huh? Goblins are intelligent beings? What are you talking about? Aren't Goblins a type of monster?",
    ["Dialogue2025605"]="You are now witnessing the birth of a world-renowned dish! Just like before, you'll collect the ingredients and I'll cook! How 'bout it?! I'll need some Goblin meat!",
    ["Dialogue2025606"]="Oh right, remember to pick Axe-wielding Goblins! I've been observing them for a while, and their meat seems to be well marbled. It should have an amazing texture! Don't get it wrong!",
    ["Dialogue2025701"]="Hey! I told you, Goblins are monsters! If you can get me Tarou meat, why can't you get me Goblin meat?",
    ["Dialogue2025801"]="Forget it, you're still too young. How 'bout this. You go bury these traps and I'll deal with the Goblins that get caught. Deal?",
    ["Dialogue2025802"]="See that totem up ahead? They pray there; it's a good place to bury the traps! Off you go!",
    ["Dialogue2025901"]="All set! You're a great help. When the new dish is done, I'll still give you some to try!",
    ["Dialogue2025902"]="What's that look on your face? Are you doubting the taste of Goblin? Trust the ancient recipe and trust this culinary genius! Hahahaha!",
    ["Dialogue2026001"]="Sigh, looks like I'll have to go back to my old line of work.",
    ["Dialogue2026002"]="Ah adventurer, I've been dismissed from my post. I'm back to running errands again.",
    ["Dialogue2026003"]="Instructor Bowya said it's to protect me by keeping me out of upper management's sight for a while. After everything that happened at the Underwater Temple... I completely understand.",
    ["Dialogue2026004"]="Even so, I have to pull myself together. By the way, do you know Finch?",
    ["Dialogue2026005"]="She declined to join the Eden Group before. But for some reason, she recently said she can help the Eden Group on her own accord. Her only request was to have Sherry as her assistant.",
    ["Dialogue2026006"]="That's why I've been tasked to come here and gather materials from the Goblin civilization, but I'm still missing three.",
    ["Dialogue2026007"]="Hehe, thank you! I'm still short of Fuel from Goblin Steamriders, a Bow from the camp, and a photo of the totem. Yup, that would be all!",
    ["Dialogue2026101"]="Perfect! Thanks to you, I can probably get back in time to eat the food Instructor Bowya's ordered!",
    ["Dialogue2026102"]="Yup! In order to celebrate Finch's assistance, Bowya specially invited Chef Dobbin from the chivalry! Word is he'll have a new dish on the menu today!",
    ["Dialogue2026103"]="Yup, that's all. I'm heading back now, bye!",
    ["Dialogue2026201"]="Hey, I saw you talking to Morts just now. Do you guys know each other?",
    ["Dialogue2026202"]="Ahh, that's great... Morts is so handsome, and he sings like an angel. If it weren't for that girl with him... Ahem, pardon me.",
    ["Dialogue2026203"]="The lute Morts is holding looks so old! It's not worthy of a voice such as his! Adventurer, can you help me? I want to make him an Obeaune dragon bone lute!",
    ["Dialogue2026204"]="Pretty please! Just think of it as helping out an innocent fan!",
    ["Dialogue2026205"]="Hehe, humans are becoming more and more passionate nowadays! I'll need some coral and tendons from Marcs! Then I'll be able to make the best dragon bone lute!",
    ["Dialogue2026301"]="Wow! You really are some adventurer! I'll definitely be able to finish the lute before Morts leaves now!",
    ["Dialogue2026401"]="Wait a moment... (Busy.) There, done! This lute is made from the finest materials the sea has to offer. It's sure to elevate Morts' voice to the next level!",
    ["Dialogue2026402"]="C-can you come with me to give it to him? I-I'm a little shy.",
    ["Dialogue2026501"]="This lute...",
    ["Dialogue2026502"]="Hahaha, this fan might be a little shy. I appreciate the thought, but I'm sorry. My lute is more important even than my own life.",
    ["Dialogue2026503"]="It was given to me by this lady beside me, Poya, seven years ago.",
    ["Dialogue2026504"]="Obeaunes may think it coarse in appearance and mediocre in tone, but within this lute is Poya's love and soul.",
    ["Dialogue2026505"]="It has been with me from the very beginning of my musical journey. When Poya isn't by my side, this lute represents her.",
    ["Dialogue2026506"]="I almost went astray once. And the way I see it, only this lute can express the love in my voice.",
    ["Dialogue2026601"]="I never imagined there would be such a story behind Morts' lute.",
    ["Dialogue2026602"]="Sigh, as a musician, I'm still too superficial...",
    ["Dialogue2026603"]="I like Morts even more now! It feels as though he isn't as flamboyant as he looks. It's most attractive, don't you think? Alright! It's time for me to get back to work!",
    ["Dialogue2026701"]="Huh? Are you also here because you received information from the gold mine?",
    ["Dialogue2026702"]="Oh, so you don't know anything. There is a very famous gold mine in Mjolnir Mountains called \"Golden Wings.\"",
    ["Dialogue2026703"]="Don't laugh at the name. Anyway, I have some interest in this mine, and now that it's in the midst of a monster crisis, well...",
    ["Dialogue2026704"]="Come on! I'm a merchant! A merchant! I was planning to make use of this incident to snap up the mine for a rock bottom price!",
    ["Dialogue2026705"]="Hmph! But the boss, Rorke, was a little hard to deal with, so I set up a meeting with his young daughter, Macpennie, at a nearby small mine. Sadly, I couldn't make it.",
    ["Dialogue2026706"]="Sigh, the monster situation is more serious than I thought. What should I do?",
    ["Dialogue2026707"]="Hehe, I knew you would say that! After all, we've worked together so many times! Exit from here, bypass the road on the right a little and you'll reach the place that I was supposed to meet Macpennie! Just tell her you're Dinza's assistant!",
    ["Dialogue2026801"]="Ah! S-stay away!",
    ["Dialogue2026802"]="I'm sorry! I wasn't talking to you... Ah! The spider behind you! AHHHHHHH!",
    ["Dialogue2026901"]="Thank you, I'm Macpennie. Ah, are you the assistant Dinza sent to talk about selling the gold mine?",
    ["Dialogue2027001"]="I'm very sorry, but Golden Wings Mine... isn't for sale right now.",
    ["Dialogue2027002"]="It's not that we don't want to sell it to you... Why don't you speak to my father, Rorke, at the mine? Then you'll understand why. Don't worry, he's open to talking about this now.",
    ["Dialogue2027101"]="For sale? Oh, you're Dinza's assistant?",
    ["Dialogue2027102"]="Look at all the Argiopes around here. Sigh, those disgusting creatures have taken over the mine; we can't operate at all.",
    ["Dialogue2027103"]="She wants to buy the mine? Then she'll have wait till these Argiopes are gone!",
    ["Dialogue2027201"]="Don't even try! They're endless. Sigh, Golden Wings is going to fall even before Morroc arrives.",
    ["Dialogue2027301"]="Sorry it's not good news for now. Just tell Dinza that Golden Wings has been taken over by monsters and there are earthquakes in Mjolnir Mountains. I'll speak to her again about selling the mine once normal operations resume.",
    ["Dialogue2027302"]="Macpennie is still young and has no interest in taking over my business, so I don't need the mine anymore. I just don't want to hand it over in such bad shape.",
    ["Dialogue2027401"]="Huh? So Rorke meant...",
    ["Dialogue2027402"]="...Hmph! This just makes me look like some kind of vulture. Why do I have to look like the bad guy?!",
    ["Dialogue2027403"]="I've decided to put off acquiring Golden Wings for now! Bye!",
    ["Dialogue2027501"]="Hm... Goblins are indeed hard to catch.",
    ["Dialogue2027502"]="Oh! The trap that you set was ingenious! Hahaha, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue2027503"]="It failed, hahaha! Such an old method doesn't work after all! So the Goblins caught me and threw me here to feed Chonchons!",
    ["Dialogue2027504"]="Ha, ropes can't trap me! It's just that the Chonchons are a little aggressive; that's why I'm stuck here.",
    ["Dialogue2027505"]="Hahaha, thank you! Ah right, Chonchon flesh can't be used for cooking, so you don't have to bring it to me!",
    ["Dialogue2027601"]="It's not time to escape yet! I've found something more important!",
    ["Dialogue2027701"]="I discovered that although Mjolnir Mountains are crawling with monsters, it's also a treasure trove of rare and unusual ingredients!",
    ["Dialogue2027702"]="Of course! As a culinary genius, I should never pass up the opportunity to acquire wonderful ingredients!",
    ["Dialogue2027703"]="Deep-fried Hornet wings, stir-fry Stainers, braised Spider Legs... Hmm, I'll try out these three dishes first! Since I can't get any Goblin meat, I'll settle for these for now!",
    ["Dialogue2027801"]="Thank you! From now on, you can try any of my dishes for free! You've been a great help to my research!",
    ["Dialogue2027802"]="Hahaha! Just say it's delicious! Don't be shy now!",
    ["Dialogue2027901"]="Why did Mjolnir Mountains become like this?",
    ["Dialogue2027902"]="Hello, adventurer. A year ago, my lover and I made a pact to meet at the summit of Mjolnir Mountains. I never imagined that Mjolnir Mountains would end up infested with monsters.",
    ["Dialogue2027903"]="Thank you, adventurer! Betta will also be grateful! Well then, let's go!",
    ["Dialogue2028001"]="Huh? Are you here to escort someone to the summit too?",
    ["Dialogue2028002"]="I met a person called Betta in Goblin Forest. He said he's supposed to meet his lover, Tyneil, here.",
    ["Dialogue2028003"]="Hehe, we did a good deed! Ah, it's those annoying Hornets again! I'll protect Betta and Tyneil, you go deal with the Hornets!",
    ["Dialogue2028101"]="Hello, adventurer. Thank you for protecting Tyneil and for helping us reunite. If it weren't for my eyes...",
    ["Dialogue2028102"]="I lost my sight because of an illness; I can no longer see anything now.",
    ["Dialogue2028103"]="Ygnizem just suggested I go to Geffen to search for a doctor at the Place of Sages after Tyneil arrives. I think it's a good idea.",
    ["Dialogue2028201"]="Then I'll lead Betta and Tyneil through Goblin Forest! With my skills, I can go anywhere in Goblin Forest with ease!",
    ["Dialogue2028202"]="Hehe, told you I'll surpass you one day! Till next time!",
    ["Dialogue2028301"]="Sigh, so this is what Mjolnir Mountains are really like.",
    ["Dialogue2028302"]="I heard that Mjolnir Mountains are also known as the mountains of love, so I came here looking for inspiration for love songs. I never expected it to be crawling with monsters.",
    ["Dialogue2028303"]="Adventurer, I heard that there's a heart-shaped rock at the summit. Could you take a photo of it for me? It might offer a different view.",
    ["Dialogue2028304"]="There's no hurry. Inspiration comes and goes like the wind. I can't get stuck in the past.",
    ["Dialogue2028401"]="Isn't this path manmade? This place doesn't live up to its name at all. Such a disappointment.",
    ["Dialogue2028501"]="Sigh, this place isn't going to give me any inspiration.",
    ["Dialogue2028502"]="The poem I came up with in the sewer while you protected me? I did write it down, but my inspiration faded, so I got stuck.",
    ["Dialogue2028503"]="I know! Aren't there big spiders here? It feels kind of similar to your Tarou encounter. Could you show me your martial prowess once more?",
    ["Dialogue2028601"]="This doesn't feel right.",
    ["Dialogue2028602"]="I didn't get inspired at all. Sigh, I've got nothing... Delay? There can be no delay when it comes to poetry!",
    ["Dialogue2028701"]="I'm finally back in my old line of work at the Eden Group. It suddenly feels a little unfamiliar now!",
    ["Dialogue2028702"]="Exploration! Today, I'm not Newbie Instructor Bowya. I'm Vanguard Explorer Bowya. Our target is Ant Hell!",
    ["Dialogue2028703"]="Ant Hell is in the deepest part of Ant Cavern in Sograt Desert.",
    ["Dialogue2028704"]="Legend has it that a mage from Geffen was eaten by the ants in Ant Hell. But his soul would not yield and so became a half-man-half-ant monster who ruled over Ant Hell. Ant Hell is rich in mineral deposits. That's why you also find mineral experts like Giearths there.",
    ["Dialogue2028705"]="Don't go looking for death. This is a place where even we from the Eden Group need to plan before entering. I strongly advise against going alone! Don't underestimate ants!",
    ["Dialogue2028801"]="What did you say? You've traversed Ant Hell? You really are amazing!",
    ["Dialogue2028802"]="I still remember when you were just a rookie back at South Gate. But you've come so far in the blink of an eye. Haha! Your progress is remarkable!",
    ["Dialogue2028901"]="Sigh, what should I do?",
    ["Dialogue2028902"]="Adventurer, I didn't get to thank you that time. Allow me to thank you now for saving us.",
    ["Dialogue2028903"]="Morts has been down in the dumps since he lost his lute. I thought it might help if I made him a new one, but he's still moping about.",
    ["Dialogue2028904"]="Adventurer, could you help me make Morts pull himself together? I always feel that something good will happen when I meet you!",
    ["Dialogue2029001"]="... (Morts stares into the distant desert. He seems to be thinking.)",
    ["Dialogue2029002"]="Excuse me, adventurer. I'm just thinking.",
    ["Dialogue2029003"]="I have a feeling that I'll be able to find something in the desert.",
    ["Dialogue2029004"]="...That's it! Adventurer, could you catch two Condors for me?",
    ["Dialogue2029005"]="Please! I think... I might be able to come to some form of realization!",
    ["Dialogue2029101"]="Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue2029102"]="(Morts holds the Condors and observes them closely.)",
    ["Dialogue2029103"]="(The Condors screech at Morts, furious about being bound by my rope. The screeching is so loud and piercing that it gives me the chills.)",
    ["Dialogue2029104"]="Hmm... This sound originates from power.",
    ["Dialogue2029105"]="(Morts is still deep in thought. I'd best not disturb him for now.)",
    ["Dialogue2029201"]="How is Morts? Can... can he be saved?",
    ["Dialogue2029202"]="Even you can't save him?",
    ["Dialogue2029203"]="I've seen him in this state before. Hmm... The last time was when he decided to start singing!",
    ["Dialogue2029301"]="Oh no! Morts went into the desert alone!",
    ["Dialogue2029302"]="The desert is so dangerous! What if something happens to him?",
    ["Dialogue2029303"]="Adventurer, let's go look for him! A passerby saw him heading toward the oasis!",
    ["Dialogue2029401"]="(Morts is still holding the two Condors. He hesitates for a while, then unties them!)",
    ["Dialogue2029402"]="(The Condors flap their wings and let out a piercing shriek that seems to cut across the sky!)",
    ["Dialogue2029403"]="(Oh no, it looks like they're really angry!)",
    ["Dialogue2029501"]="I understand now. I've finally thought it through! I'm sorry for worrying you and Poya! But I'm completely fine now!",
    ["Dialogue2029502"]="I've been thinking since the lute that Poya gave me was ruined.",
    ["Dialogue2029503"]="For the longest time, I've always thought that it was my voice that complimented the lute and that it was Poya's soul that expressed my love. When Poya's soul was lost, the spirit of my song was lost with it.",
    ["Dialogue2029504"]="That was until I saw the Condors soaring above the desert. They used their voices to express an extraordinary strength, a strength that stems from freedom.",
    ["Dialogue2029505"]="That's right. I will use my own voice to express my love! Just like the feelings I have for Poya!",
    ["Dialogue2029506"]="(Morts takes Poya's hand and they leave together. The way that Poya looks at Morts is filled with tenderness and understanding.)",
    ["Dialogue2029601"]="Sigh, why...?",
    ["Dialogue2029602"]="Oh! Your timing couldn't be better. Do you still remember the wedding dress made from Lunatic fur?",
    ["Dialogue2029603"]="Well, I finished it, and it was very well received in Prontera. But when I brought it to Sograt Desert, the people here were completely uninterested!",
    ["Dialogue2029604"]="I do have a certain amount of pride as a designer, so... could you perhaps ask around and find out what people think of it?",
    ["Dialogue2029701"]="Huh? The Eclipse fur wedding dress? It's so stupid! So puffy and bulky!",
    ["Dialogue2029702"]="Do you know what makes the ideal wedding dress here in the desert? They usually have a simple cut to accentuate the figure of the bride. She is the center of attention after all!",
    ["Dialogue2029801"]="Lunatic Fur wedding dress? Are you kidding me? You're aware that we're in the desert, right? It wouldn't be a good look for the bride to die of heat stroke on her big day.",
    ["Dialogue2029901"]="The weather and to accentuate one's figure... Indeed, the weather in Prontera allows wedding dress designs to be more extravagant. Right, I know what I should do now!",
    ["Dialogue2030001"]="Adventurer, I'm in need of some materials. The most suitable materials in the desert to use for a wedding dress would be young Wolf Pelt and Pecopeco's Egg Shells! I need to test my theory. I'll be counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue2030101"]="Hey, adventurer. Come over here... C'mon, closer! Closer!",
    ["Dialogue2030102"]="(Hamid looks at you with a charming smile.)\nHehe, I have a favor to ask of you. It's a favor that will affect my lifelong happiness! Are you willing to go meet a lady in my place? She is an amazing lady who... is also in love with me!",
    ["Dialogue2030103"]="Hey, what's that look on your face?! You don't believe I'm a ladies' man? You don't think I can compete with Yadrew and the others? Hmph! Looks like only my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pen Pal K</color> has good taste. She's the one who asked me to meet her in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta</color>. Have Yadrew and the others ever received an invitation like that?",
    ["Dialogue2030104"]="To be honest, it's been a while since K and I started corresponding. Ever since I picked up that message in a bottle while I was mining for gold by the sea, I've felt the pull of destiny! That's right, it was that little glass bottle that brought me into K's wondrous world. And it is exactly because I hold this relationship so dear that I'm asking you to meet K in my place!",
    ["Dialogue2030105"]="Erm... You know, women all like to... erm, judge people by their looks. I'm worried that K might be distracted by, um... my slightly beefy appearance and overlook my heart of gold! What's more, doesn't it cost quite a bit to travel to Alberta? If K looks... less than ideal, wouldn't want all my Zeny to have been spent in vain, eh?",
    ["Dialogue2030106"]="...In any case, just go as I tell you to! Remember to pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>roses</color> on your way. Since roses represent love, we've decided to use a bouquet of roses as our code.\nCome to think of it, K seems pretty infatuated with me! Hehehe!",
    ["Dialogue2030201"]="(Kaitlyn checks you out with surprise in her eyes.)\nYou're H...?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I remember H describing himself as an \"almighty, ingenious merchant who is one in a million,\" </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but this person seems...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2030202"]="Yup, you can call me Kaitlyn. I have to say, I was a little shocked when I saw you, but I felt really reassured at the same time! Judging from your style of writing, I did worry that you might be arrogant and chauvinistic, but meeting you has proved me wrong. I can now tell you the truth without worry!",
    ["Dialogue2030203"]="Actually, I asked you to Alberta because I have a favor to ask. Of course, you have the right to decline. After all, it does involve one of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>seven royal families</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2030204"]="Have you heard of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Family</color>? They run Alberta and control the <color=#CA2E0AFF>two largest merchant groups in the city, Serpentrod and Libra</color>. My aim is to teach the Wigner Family a lesson. In my opinion, only a merchant as experienced as you will be able to do it!",
    ["Dialogue2030205"]="(Kaitlyn's expression suddenly turns solemn.)\n...Why do I want to go up against the Wigner Family? Ha, if you were about to lose the fruits of all your hard work because of them, you would do it too!",
    ["Dialogue2030206"]="You've probably heard of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lindra Chamber of Commerce</color>? Though it's doing pretty well now, it was initially just a small merchant group on the brink of collapse. During that time, I pumped in a huge sum of money to save it from bankruptcy. But just as we were about to thrive, we were faced with another crisis due to suppression by the Wigner Family.",
    ["Dialogue2030207"]="Only a weak person would sit back and accept defeat. I, however, will have my revenge!",
    ["Dialogue2030301"]="Are you willing to help me? I understand if you're afraid of the Wigner Family. Even if I have to do it alone, I will achieve my goal!",
    ["Dialogue2030302"]="Great! With your help, going up against the Wigner Family will be a walk in the park! Actually, I already have a plan. I intend to acquire <color=#CA2E0AFF>goods that are rarer</color> than what Libra and Serpentrod are procuring to outcompete them. But the merchant groups of the Wigner Family procure their goods through the ruler of the waves, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson Fleet</color>. It won't be easy to beat them.",
    ["Dialogue2030303"]="Which is why I need your brains! As an experienced and knowledgeable merchant, do you have any good suggestions?",
    ["Dialogue2030304"]="(Kaitlyn thinks for a while and shakes her head.)\n...No, I'm afraid the people of this port city have long ago lost interest in items from the seabed. If we want to capture their attention, we'll have to look further afield. Think again.",
    ["Dialogue2030305"]="How's it going? As an experienced and knowledgeable merchant, do you have any good suggestions?",
    ["Dialogue2030306"]="(Kaitlyn thinks for a while and her face lights up.)\nThe desert... The desert is indeed the best choice! Goods from the mysterious desert will definitely capture the attention of the people who live by the sea. It would be difficult even for the Alson Fleet to bring goods back from the desert. You really are an ingenious merchant!",
    ["Dialogue2030307"]="Great, it's decided then. We'll obtain some rare goods from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Labyrinth</color>. I'll inform Lindra now...\n(Something comes to Kaitlyn's mind and she looks like she's in a dilemma.)\nSigh, the members of Lindra are all girls. I'm a little worried about them going to the desert alone.",
    ["Dialogue2030308"]="...Really? Thank you very much. Kindly head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kafra</color> and wait there. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lindra member</color> I've dispatched will arrive shortly after you. Ah, but that child's swift-footed; she might even arrive before you!",
    ["Dialogue2030401"]="(Betty's jaw drops in surprise.)\n<size=24>Woah! </size><size=24>How could it be you?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2030402"]="Hey, I have the right to be here! Kaitlyn personally appointed me for this mission! More like, what are you doing here? Don't tell me you're the \"ingenious merchant\" Kaitlyn mentioned?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Strange, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>why didn't I notice it when we were up against the Eclipse?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2030403"]="Alright, alright. I trust Kaitlyn's judgment. It's safer than going alone anyway.\n(Betty puffs out her chest with pride.)\nAhem! Speaking of which, I'm fully prepared for this mission! If there's anything that you don't know, just ask!",
    ["Dialogue2030501"]="(Betty holds her head high with confidence.)\nAhem! Now that we're about to set off, is there anything you want to ask me?",
    ["Dialogue2030502"]="Hey! How could you say that? I've painstakingly researched... I mean, you should have a thirst for knowledge! Since you're Kaitlyn's friend, I'll take it upon myself to explain it to you. We're headed for Sphinx Labyrinth. It's near the faraway desert city of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc</color>. The fastest way to get there is to use <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kafra services</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2030503"]="As the leader of our group, I'll head there first! Hurry and catch up! Don't dawdle!",
    ["Dialogue2030601"]="(Betty holds her head high with confidence.)\nAhem! Now that we're about to set off for Sphinx Labyrinth, is there anything you want to ask me?",
    ["Dialogue2030602"]="...Hey! D-didn't I just tell you that you should have a thirst for knowledge? Fine, since you're Kaitlyn's friend, I'll take it upon myself to explain it to you.",
    ["Dialogue2030603"]="Sphinx Labyrinth is located <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest</color> of Morroc. It is a ruin that has been around since <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient Egyptian</color> times. It's said that even the Pharaoh was once lost in it! But for Kaitlyn, we must to enter the labyrinth. As the leader of the group, I-I'll...",
    ["Dialogue2030604"]="(Betty's face flushes.)\n...I, I get it! I'll go on ahead. You follow closely behind, you hear?!",
    ["Dialogue2030701"]="(Betty holds her head high with confidence.)\nAhem! Now that we're about to explore the labyrinth, is there anything you want to ask me?",
    ["Dialogue2030702"]="...I—<size=26>GIVE UP!</size>\nAren't you curious about which monsters we're supposed to hunt? Hmph, luckily I've done my research beforehand!",
    ["Dialogue2030703"]="According to an ancient text, a monster in Sphinx Labyrinth called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zerom</color> carries precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sparkling Light Granules</color>. But the author of the text said that the labyrinth is no place for a delicate young lady...\n(Betty covers her face in annoyance.)",
    ["Dialogue2030704"]="Sigh! And I was thinking about obtaining those goods for Miss Kaitlyn personally! I wonder if there's any kind person who would be willing lend this helpless young lady a hand?\n(Betty peeks at you through the gaps between her fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue2030801"]="Awesome! These Sparkling Light Granules will definitely fetch a good price! But it's still not enough. We need to bring back more goods. According to an ancient text, a monster called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Requiem</color> carries precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Chests</color>. But once again, the text says that the labyrinth is no place for a delicate young lady...",
    ["Dialogue2030901"]="Awesome! These Mysterious Chests will definitely fetch a good price! But it's still not enough.",
    ["Dialogue2030902"]="Hehe! Well then, please go get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ancient Egyptian Swords</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pasana</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2031001"]="Awesome! This is enough! Let's return to Kaitlyn!\nI'm sure she will lavish great praise upon me when she sees what I've done! Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue2031002"]="Ah! The wind is so strong in the desert; I can't hear clearly! Ahem, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry back to Alberta</color>! I bet Kaitlyn can't wait to find out how we've done!",
    ["Dialogue2031101"]="(Kaitlyn studiously goes through the checklist.)\nExcellent, these exotic goods will definitely create hype in Alberta! So as to not let your hard work go to waste, we need to liaise with the Lindra members immediately to put these goods on sale. Betty...",
    ["Dialogue2031102"]="Yes, Kaitlyn! Please allow me to complete this mission! I'm confident I'll do a good job!",
    ["Dialogue2031103"]="Well then, I'll be counting on you. Now for the next step...\n(Kaitlyn turns toward you with a glint of excitement in her eyes.)\nThere's still <color=#CA2E0AFF>an important task</color> waiting for us.",
    ["Dialogue2031201"]="I've just received a piece of good news! The Wigner Family's two merchant groups, Libra and Serpentrod, are planning to <color=#CA2E0AFF>compete for the sole distribution rights of an item from the Merchant's Guild</color>! If I can win the distribution rights for Lindra, I'll be able to take the Wigner Family down a peg. This golden opportunity is too good to miss!",
    ["Dialogue2031202"]="The distribution rights will be awarded based on bidding. If we can think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out Libra's and Serpentrod's bids</color>, we'll be able to...\n(Kaitlyn thinks for a moment.)\n...Got it, maybe that rare treasure can help!",
    ["Dialogue2031203"]="Please speak to Felix the accessory merchant about acquiring the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crown of Eassis</color>. It's crucial to the next part of our plan!",
    ["Dialogue2031301"]="Welco—. Oh, an adventurer. Well then, don't get scared off by the price tags in this store. The items here are mostly high-end products meant for the Wigner Family!",
    ["Dialogue2031302"]="Hmph, just name it! I have everything here. The only thing you need to worry about is affording it!",
    ["Dialogue2031303"]="...Wha-<size=26>what did you say?!</size>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How would a commoner know about such a legendary treasure? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I've only ever mentioned it to Kaitlyn before. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Could this person be an expert?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2031304"]="Ahem, please pardon me. Since you've mentioned the Crown of Eassis, you should know how difficult it is to obtain! A large number of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Magic Stones</color> is needed to craft it, and they can only be found on the god of the underworld, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anubis</color>, in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Labyrinth</color>. Sigh, materials that rare are almost priceless!",
    ["Dialogue2031305"]="(Felix widens his eyes in disbelief.)\n...Are you serious? If you're able to supply enough Red Magic Stones, of course I'll be able to craft a Crown of Eassis! It's the dream of every accessory merchant to bring such a rare treasure back to the world!",
    ["Dialogue2031401"]="(Felix's eyes are filled with excitement.)\n...By Odin, I never imagined I would have the opportunity to craft the Crown of Eassis! But...",
    ["Dialogue2031402"]="Was it the ancient legend that spurred you to acquire this crown? According to ancient Egyptian texts, the Crown of Eassis gives its <color=#CA2E0AFF>wearer the power to bewitch people</color>. And it was said that the ancient Egyptian queen, Eassis, used it to capture the heart of Osiris!\nBut as a strong ruler, would Osiris really have been so easily bewitched? Hm...",
    ["Dialogue2031501"]="(Kaitlyn looks at you in disbelief.)\n...Ah! This... Y-you...",
    ["Dialogue2031502"]="(Kaitlyn is stunned for a moment, then shakes her head vigorously.)\n...Ahem! Excuse me, you look so stunning. Even I couldn't help... But that shows just how amazing the Crown of Eassis is! Using it against <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jurgen</color> is definitely the right choice!",
    ["Dialogue2031503"]="Ha! I bet everyone in Rune Kingdom has heard of Jurgen Wigner. He's the eldest son of Ruvier, the head of the Wigner Family, and the chairman of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Libra Group</color>. Though I think he's far more famous for being a playboy!",
    ["Dialogue2031504"]="It's said that Jurgen never rejects a beauty. If you were to meet him while wearing the Crown of Eassis, he would definitely think you're the most beautiful person in the whole world! Then all you have to do is trick him into telling you <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Libra Group's bid</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2031505"]="(Kaitlyn looks away flustered.)\n...Me? Ahem, for reasons I can't say, I can't meet him. Please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sapphire Blue Tavern</color> and look for Jurgen. He loves lively places like that!",
    ["Dialogue2031601"]="(Jurgen stares at you intently. He lets out a sigh after a long while.)\n...By Odin, never could I have imagined that there would be someone so beautiful in this world!",
    ["Dialogue2031602"]="Please allow me to introduce myself. My name is Jurgen Wigner. May I have the honor of buying you a drink?",
    ["Dialogue2031603"]="...You mean, if I want to buy you a drink I'll first have to answer a question?\n(Jurgen beams at you.)\nI never decline a request from a beauty. Tell me now, what is your question?",
    ["Dialogue2031604"]="(Jurgen is slightly taken aback. He looks down and thinks for a while.)\nAlthough it's a trade secret, I'm willing to bare all in front of you! The Libra Group's bid has always been managed by my assistant, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pollard</color>. He should be near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merchant Guild</color> right now.",
    ["Dialogue2031605"]="...Wait, I haven't bought you a drink yet! Sigh, what an impatient beauty.",
    ["Dialogue2031701"]="(Kaitlyn's eyes light up with excitement.)\nGreat. With this bidding sheet, the Libra Group is already out of the running! Next up, we'll need to deal with...",
    ["Dialogue2031702"]="That's right. Could you speak to the food merchant, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color>, and find out if there's any <color=#CA2E0AFF>rare wine</color> that could knock someone out instantly?",
    ["Dialogue2031703"]="Trust me, it's crucial to our final goal!",
    ["Dialogue2031801"]="(A suggestive smile spreads across Rachel's face after hearing your request.)\nOhoho! You're looking for wine... and wine so strong that it can knock someone out instantly? Pray tell, what mischief are you up to?",
    ["Dialogue2031802"]="Hehe! It's fine if you don't want to say! The wine you're looking for is temporarily out of stock, but I can give you information about the maker! He is none other than the man who everybody calls the Wine Maestro. His real name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juke</color>; he lives in <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Payon</color>. His forte is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wine of No Worries</color>. It's said that just one mouthful will knock someone out for three whole days! Speak to him to find out more.",
    ["Dialogue2031901"]="(Juke squints in a drunken stupor.)\n<size=18>Drinking not to your heart's content </size><size=18>is a life lived with much regret. </size><size=18>Burp! Wine... </size><size=18>Such great wine! </size><size=18>Haha...</size>",
    ["Dialogue2031902"]="...Huh? You... Burp! You want the Wine of No Worries? You'll have to carry me back then. The last few vats have all just gone into my belly! Haha! Burp!",
    ["Dialogue2031903"]="...Huh, I can't just make you another vat. The process is rather complicated. Unless you can get enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Spirit Essence</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wormtails</color>... Otherwise don't come putting a downer on my merrymaking! Burp!",
    ["Dialogue2032001"]="Good, good! Now I'll show you just... just how these ingredients become fine wine in a vat, burp! We just need to wait... to wait... to wait... Wait a minute... Huh?",
    ["Dialogue2032002"]="Erm, this doesn't smell right. Is something missing? Ah! I think I forgot to add <color=#CA2E0AFF>Intact Bear Paws</color>! Burp! Hurry, go get some from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bigfoots</color>. Otherwise, this wine will end up as vinegar instead, burp!",
    ["Dialogue2032101"]="Good, good! Now I'll show you just... just how these ingredients become fine wine in a vat, burp! We just need to wait... to wait... to wait... Wait a minute... Huh?",
    ["Dialogue2032102"]="Haha! You're quite clever, aren't you? You can answer me even before I finish asking, burp! I think I forgot to add in some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pure Sap</color>. Hurry, go get some from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Willows</color>. Otherwise, this wine will end up as vinegar instead, burp!",
    ["Dialogue2032201"]="Good, good! Now I'll show you just... just how these ingredients become fine wine in a vat, burp! We just need to wait... to wait... to wait... wait...",
    ["Dialogue2032202"]="...Huh? What else do you want me to say? All we have to do now is <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait for a while more</color> and the Wine of No Worries will be done. Sigh, young people these days are so impatient, burp!",
    ["Dialogue2032301"]="You said this wine can knock someone out for three days? That's great. It's just what we need to use against Isaac!",
    ["Dialogue2032302"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Isaac</color> is Ruvier's second son and he's also the chairman of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Serpentrod Group</color>. There's not much we can use against him, except for the fact that he's a collector of fine wine. When this Wine of No Worries is given to him, he'll definitely be tempted to drink it. When he does, you'll be able to get Serpentrod Group's <color=#CA2E0AFF>bidding sheet</color> from him!",
    ["Dialogue2032303"]="(Kaitlyn looks away flustered.)\n...I-I seem to know a lot about the members of the Wigner Family? It's just information I've collected... Ahem, please hurry and see Isaac at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Family Mansion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2032401"]="(Isaac looks at you curiously, then starts sniffing.)\n*Sniffs* Th-this smell? What have you brought?",
    ["Dialogue2032402"]="Wow! It smells wonderful!\n(Isaac gulps it down.)\nYawn... So sleepy...",
    ["Dialogue2032501"]="(Kaitlyn's eyes light up with excitement.)\nGreat! Now that we know the bids of both Libra and Serpentrod, Lindra is sure to win the distribution rights! Next, I need to get him to witness it all.",
    ["Dialogue2032502"]="This is my last request: Please see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ruvier</color> at the Wigner Family Mansion and bring him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merchant Guild</color>! If he doesn't witness this glorious moment, everything I've done will have no meaning!",
    ["Dialogue2032601"]="(Ruvier frowns after listening to your request.)\n...What has the bidding got to do with me? Who asked you to come here?",
    ["Dialogue2032602"]="Kaitlyn? Why would she...?\nAlright, looks like I won't be able to understand what's going on unless I see it for myself. Well then, please lead the way.",
    ["Dialogue2032701"]="(Kaitlyn puffs out her chest with pride.)\nThank you. It was all thanks to you that I was able to prove myself to everyone!",
    ["Dialogue2032702"]="(Kaitlyn turns toward Ruvier.)\nFather, all these years, you've been focused on Jurgen and Isaac; you never acknowledged my hard work and success. It is my intention today to prove to you in front of everyone that I'm not inferior to anybody!",
    ["Dialogue2032703"]="......",
    ["Dialogue2032704"]="(Strachey sighs and pulls something out of his pocket.)\nKaitlyn, would you first take a look at these two <color=#CA2E0AFF>bidding sheets</color> I have received? Although I'm in no position to interfere with the internal affairs of the Wigner Family, I don't want you to have any regrets.",
    ["Dialogue2032705"]="...These are?\n(Kaitlyn takes the bidding sheets.)\nThese bidding sheets belong to... Libra and Serpentrod? But why are they blank?",
    ["Dialogue2032706"]="(A look of realization dawns on Kaitlyn's face and she raises head to look at Jurgen and Isaac. She appears to be in shock.)\nNeither of you... intended to compete in the first place?! Why did you do that?! <size=24>Tell me why!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2032707"]="......",
    ["Dialogue2032708"]="......",
    ["Dialogue2032709"]="(Ruvier sighs heavily.)\nWe need to talk, but let's speak after we <color=#CA2E0AFF>return home</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2032801"]="(Kaitlyn frowns.)\nWhy... why did they do that? Is the success of Lindra not because of my ability, but because Jurgen and Isaac have secretly been letting me win?",
    ["Dialogue2032802"]="...Thank you for your consolation. I feel better now. I'm sorry for keeping this from you. I am actually Ruvier's eldest daughter, Kaitlyn Wigner. The real reason I asked for your help is to prove myself by winning the bid, so that my father will finally notice me.",
    ["Dialogue2032803"]="In the eyes of outsiders, I'm royalty and should be held in esteem, but the fact is I've never been valued. Father and Mother entrusted the future of the family to my two younger brothers and have never acknowledged my hard work. All I wanted was to go against destiny for once! But look what happened. I'm nothing but a laughing stock!",
    ["Dialogue2032804"]="(Kaitlyn bites her lip.)\nI just don't understand. Why did Jurgen and Isaac lose on purpose? I really <color=#CA2E0AFF>want to know what they're thinking</color>, but I can't bear to face my family right now.",
    ["Dialogue2032901"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Sigh, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I wonder how Kaitlyn is now. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>She looked so upset. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But if I were to see her now, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>would she feel even worse?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2032902"]="(Jurgen looks at you anxiously.)\nWas it Kaitlyn who asked you to come see me? Is she alright? I never thought my actions would backfire so horribly.",
    ["Dialogue2032903"]="That's right. When you asked me about the bid, I'd already noticed that it was a trap. I willingly walked into it hoping to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill Kaitlyn's wish</color>. I know that the results of this bid are very important to Lindra!",
    ["Dialogue2032904"]="Even if we lost the bid, the Lindra Group could still earn profit from other channels, but if Lindra were to lose, they would face bankruptcy. I couldn't just sit back and watch my big sister's hard work go down the drain. Furthermore, it is only right for a gentleman to protect a lady's dignity in a respectable manner!",
    ["Dialogue2032905"]="(Jurgen hangs his head in dejection.)\nSigh, I never imagined everything I did would make her so upset.",
    ["Dialogue2033001"]="(Isaac looks very down.)\nAhh... How did things come to this? It's really not funny.",
    ["Dialogue2033002"]="Sigh! I gave up the bid because I wanted Kaitlyn to get what she wanted! I never expected it would end up making her unhappy instead. It's so depressing!",
    ["Dialogue2033003"]="Of course. I've drunk countless wines. It takes a lot more than one vat of Wine of No Worries to get me drunk. I only drank it so that Kaitlyn could win the bid. Because to me, there's nothing more important than <color=#CA2E0AFF>seeing my big sister smile again</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2033004"]="In life, all that matters is being happy! If someone you care about is always looking down, what's the point of making so much money? But in the end, she's still unhappy. Looks like I'll be unhappy too, sigh!",
    ["Dialogue2033101"]="(Kaitlyn is still frowning.)\nWhy... why did they do that?",
    ["Dialogue2033102"]="...Jurgen and Isaac noticed my frustration a long time ago? And they did what they did to cheer me up? So it wasn't me that was neglected, but rather I was the one who neglected them!",
    ["Dialogue2033103"]="Thinking back, it was because I was the one who shut them out. That's why there's been a barrier between me and my family! The truths before me are all telling me that running away won't solve any problems. I will return home and <color=#CA2E0AFF>let Father know how I really feel</color>. My closest friend, please come with me to witness this moment!",
    ["Dialogue2033201"]="(Ruvier sighs heavily.)\nSigh, the Wigner Family has always been known for its freedom, and I've always thought that I was open-minded enough. How could I have been so blind?!",
    ["Dialogue2033202"]="If my children didn't tell me about how they felt, I would never have realized how much I've hurt Kaitlyn. It looks like it's time to hand over the reins to the next generation. Only then will the Wigner Family continue to thrive.",
    ["Dialogue2033203"]="Father, I have a great suggestion! Why not let Kaitlyn take over the Libra Group from me?",
    ["Dialogue2033204"]="(Kaitlyn is shocked.)\nNo!",
    ["Dialogue2033205"]="Actually, there's a piece of news that I have yet to announce. I've been chosen as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>successor candidate for the throne</color>! Once I head to the capital to compete, I wouldn't have time to manage the Libra Group anymore. Since Isaac already has the Serpentrod Group to manage, the only suitable person to take my place is Kaitlyn.",
    ["Dialogue2033206"]="She has long proven herself to be a capable merchant! You can definitely entrust your duties to the person who brought Lindra back from the brink of failure!",
    ["Dialogue2033207"]="(Isaac raises his hands in happiness.)\nI wholeheartedly agree!",
    ["Dialogue2033208"]="(Kaitlyn is touched.)\nJurgen, Isaac...",
    ["Dialogue2033209"]="(Ruvier thinks for a while and a look of relief spreads across his face.)\nAlright, in this case... Kaitlyn, the future of Libra Group is in your hands now. Show me what you can do and amaze this old man!",
    ["Dialogue2033301"]="How... how can I ever thank you? You've not only helped me overcome my difficulties, you've also helped me mend my relationship with my family! Before this, I only thought of you as an ordinary pen pal who I could share my troubles with. I even wanted to use you to solve my problems.",
    ["Dialogue2033302"]="(Kaitlyn starts blushing.)\nBut now, my perception of you has completely changed! If you don't mind... can I visit you often on Izlude Island?",
    ["Dialogue2033303"]="(Kaitlyn looks at you incredulously.)\n...What?! Are you telling me you aren't my pen pal H who's been exchanging letters with me all this time? Then who is H?",
    ["Dialogue2033304"]="...Ha, haha! What was that? Hamid is basically the same age as my father, and as for his body shape, well...\n(Kaitlyn's mouth twitches continuously as she speaks.)\nUrgh... Then you better tell Hamid something from me: Sometimes, a little distance makes things look prettier!",
    ["Dialogue20401001"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Large</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Formless</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Neutral</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401002"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Medium</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Plant</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Fire</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401003"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Small</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Fish</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Water</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401004"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Large</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Insect</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Wind</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401005"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Medium</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Brute</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Earth</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401006"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Small</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Demi-Human</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Poison</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401007"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Large</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Angel</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Holy</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401008"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Medium</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Dragon</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Ghost</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue20401009"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Small</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Demon</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Shadow</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2040101"]="(Friedrich frowns, his fingertips tapping on the table. He doesn't seem to notice your arrival.)\nAre you sure it's him? There's no mistaking it? This is a matter of great importance, so we must be certain.",
    ["Dialogue20401010"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! Boss mutation detected! Current Size: <color=#ff5252>Large</color>. Current Race: <color=#ff5252>Undead</color>. Current Attribute: <color=#ff5252>Undead</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2040102"]="...You are?",
    ["Dialogue2040103"]="(The tension between Friedrich's eyebrows finally softens.)\nOh, it's Mainz's student. You're just in time. I need to hear some objective input here. This all seems incredible to me... Winry, can you tell the story again?",
    ["Dialogue2040104"]="Ah, well... Here's the thing. The night before last, I was alone in the library sorting out the list of books. It was almost three o'clock in the morning, and the whole of Geffen Tower was deathly quiet. All of a sudden, I heard a faint voice coming from <color=#CA2E0AFF>the forbidden zone</color>, so I plucked up my courage and walked over. To my surprise, I bumped right into a strange dark figure.",
    ["Dialogue2040105"]="I feared that it might be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>book thief</color>, so I tried my best to stop him from leaving. As I pulled at his arm, a precious document, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color>, fell from his hands! But before I could reach out to pick it up, he snatched it away and escaped my grasp.",
    ["Dialogue2040106"]="It was then that I finally saw his face, but I didn't think it was possible. It was...\n(Winry glances at Friedrich with trembling eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue2040107"]="...It was my son, future heir of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heines Family</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nithil</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2040108"]="Winry, if what you say is true, then I won't go easy on Nithil. But I do have my doubts, and not out of favoritism, but simply because I cannot think of a rational motive for him to do such a thing. Merlin's Manuscript was originally written by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin Heines</color>, an ancestor of our family. Nithil is free to borrow it whenever he wants, so why would he need to steal it?",
    ["Dialogue2040109"]="...Are there any other clues? Is there anything else we can use to verify the identity of the thief?\n(Winry holds her glasses carefully.)\nWell... After that, I did look around the bookshelves, but apart from that brooch...",
    ["Dialogue2040110"]="...Ah, right, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>brooch</color>! I remember it fell from the thief's lapel as I tussled with him! If I recall correctly, it should still be in my drawer.\n(Winry places a glittering brooch on the table.)",
    ["Dialogue2040201"]="(Friedrich goes silent for a moment and then sighs deeply.)\n...Well, now I have nothing more to say.",
    ["Dialogue2040202"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Black-feathered Raven</color> is the Heines Family emblem. This brooch really does belong to my son, Nithil. But I still can't understand. What would he want with Merlin's Manuscript? And at such a critical time...",
    ["Dialogue2040203"]="And here's the trouble—when I arrived home this morning, I found that Nithil was nowhere to be found! If I could ask him to come here and answer for himself, that would be best, otherwise, it will become increasingly difficult for him to extricate himself from this dire situation.",
    ["Dialogue2040204"]="Adventurer, can I ask you to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen</color> to find a young man named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wheeler</color>? He's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nithil's attendant</color>, and should know <color=#CA2E0AFF>where my son is</color>. Please ask him to tell you. I will not allow anything to tarnish the Heines Family's name and my child's reputation.",
    ["Dialogue2040301"]="—Hey! Hold on a minute! What do you think you're doing trying to start a fight with me all of a sudden?!",
    ["Dialogue2040302"]="...You're right, what reason would I have to run? This is the first time we've met! Haha! I'm sorry. I'm a little on edge; I thought you were sent by Lord Friedrich to question me. I didn't know what to think.",
    ["Dialogue2040303"]="(Wheeler opens his mouth in shock and backs off.)\n<size=26>—Ah?! You... you're...</size>",
    ["Dialogue2040304"]="Ah! M-Master Nithil told me <color=#CA2E0AFF>not to tell anyone where he is</color>. Don't put me in this situation. Just pretend you didn't see me, please!",
    ["Dialogue2040305"]="(Wheeler's eyebrows suddenly rise up.)\n—What?! You say it's a matter of Master Nithil's honor? Don't talk nonsense! The young master is the most self-disciplined young man there is! He'd never do anything to harm the reputation of his family! If you don't believe me, go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin Forest</color> and ask him yourself... Ah... Ah!",
    ["Dialogue2040401"]="(Nithil stares at you warily.)\nWho... who are you?",
    ["Dialogue2040402"]="(Nithil begins to look more cautious. He holds the tree trunk with his right hand and tries to get up.)\nHow do you know my name? Are you <color=#CA2E0AFF>one of them</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2040403"]="Answer me! Are you... Hurgh, *cough*... (A stream of blood gushes from Nithil's wound, staining his clothes red.)",
    ["Dialogue2040404"]="(Nithil hesitates for a moment.)\nAlright, if you really want to help me... go and pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dodder</color> and gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Fruits</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mace-wielding Goblins</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2040501"]="(Nithil crushes the Dodder and Red Fruits, and applies it to his wound.)\nIt seems I misunderstood your intentions just now. But we've never met, so how did you recognize me?",
    ["Dialogue2040502"]="So, it was Father and Wheeler... But there's something I still need to do—please, you must help me finish it!\n(Nithil takes out a book with an old cover.)\nPlease take <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color>. You must give it to my grandfather, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2040503"]="I had a good reason for stealing the manuscript from the library. But now is not the time to explain why. If you're willing to believe me, please take the manuscript and set off as soon as possible! Remember, be careful every step of the way. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trust no one, not even familiar faces</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2040504"]="When my wound has healed, I will try to catch up with you.\n(Nithil goes silent for a moment, and cracks a melancholy smile.)\nAlthough I'm not as handy in battle as the rest of my family... I won't let this be the end of me, not just yet.",
    ["Dialogue2040601"]="(Kroneika looks you up and down with unflinching eyes.)\nAhem! Well, you're here. Quickly hand over <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color>. Where did you put it?",
    ["Dialogue2040602"]="How did I know what you're doing here? Uh... Well...\n...Because I am the Great Sage, of course! I know everything! Everything!",
    ["Dialogue2040701"]="(Kroneika holds out a hand and urges you anxiously.)\nCome on, now! Quickly, hand over Merlin's Manuscript! Nithil surely told you to do so. Aren't you going to do as he requested?",
    ["Dialogue2040702"]="...What? Who is Nithil? He's my beloved grandson, of course!\nAre you trying to mock this old man's memory?",
    ["Dialogue2040703"]="...What? You want to know where Bidal went? Erm...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hah, how come he never mentioned that name?</color></size>\n...Ahem. I don't even know who Bidal is. How am I supposed to know where he's gone!",
    ["Dialogue2040704"]="...What? Bidal is a member of the Heines Family? He's been training under the Great Sage, and there's no way the real Kroneika wouldn't know? Well, you got me. There's no need to carry on with this charade now that you know the truth!",
    ["Dialogue2040801"]="(The thief finally shows his true face.)\nHmph! I didn't expect you to see through my disguise! But I'll be taking Merlin's Manuscript from you all the same! And since you're not willing to hand it over, I'll have to take it myself!",
    ["Dialogue2040901"]="(Kroneika knits his eyebrows in a frown.)\nMerlin's Manuscript... Shouldn't this book be in Geffen Tower's Library? For what reason are you giving it to me?",
    ["Dialogue2040902"]="Nithil planned all this? And those assassins who ambushed you along the way were trying to steal Merlin's Manuscript?",
    ["Dialogue2040903"]="(Bidal looks at Kroneika with a worried look.)\nMaster Kroneika, we should go and help Nithil right away. He must have been injured by those assassins while protecting the manuscript, and he may still be in danger as we speak!",
    ["Dialogue2040904"]="Adventurer, hold on a moment. I have another matter I require you to investigate.\n(Kroneika narrows his deep eyes.)\nYou mentioned that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the thief was pretending to be me</color>. Do you remember where exactly you defeated him?",
    ["Dialogue2040905"]="Now, please go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>body of the thief</color> immediately, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report to me as much about his appearance as possible</color>. If we leave it too late, perhaps we won't be able to find any useful clues.",
    ["Dialogue2040906"]="(Bidal nods at you.)\nDon't worry, I'll find him and bring him back safely!",
    ["Dialogue2041001"]="(Kroneika carefully studies the photos of the thief's body.)\nAs I expected. From the looks of these clothes, the thief was part of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mobster gang</color> based just outside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>. But they could never muster the audacity to attack the Heines Family alone. There must be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mastermind</color> orchestrating all this.",
    ["Dialogue2041002"]="(Kroneika opens the crystal bottle containing the strange potion, picks up a pinch of powder and sprinkles it in.)\n...Hmmm, how unusual. From the way it reacts, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy</color> used to create this potion was clearly very precise.",
    ["Dialogue2041003"]="—Master Kroneika! We have returned!",
    ["Dialogue2041101"]="(Nithil goes up to Kroneika, greets him respectfully, and lowers his eyes quickly.)\n...Grandfather. It has been a long time.",
    ["Dialogue2041102"]="(Kroneika nods his head without expression.)\nIt has indeed.",
    ["Dialogue2041103"]="Master Kroneika, when I found Nithil, although he was seriously wounded, he remained fearless despite being besieged by several thieves. On the way back to the Mjolnir Mountains, Nithil told me about a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange incident</color> that occurred in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heines Family mansion</color> a few days ago. That incident marked the beginning of this chaos. I think that you and this adventurer should listen to what happened.",
    ["Dialogue2041104"]="(Nithil takes a slow, deep breath.)\nThis is what happened—",
    ["Dialogue2041105"]="...Thank you for your concern, but I've almost recovered thanks to you and Bidal. It's vital that I recount the events of that day as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue2041201"]="(The attendant gives an embarrassed smile and averts his gaze.)\n...Haha! M-Master Nithil, you're here! I was just... uh... coming to see if you had returned!",
    ["Dialogue2041202"]="(Wheeler looks surprised and angry.)\n—Hey! You... Who are you?! Why do you look exactly the same as me?!",
    ["Dialogue2041203"]="Well, I'm Wheeler, of course—Master Nithil's attendant! And who may you be? You're not from this household, are you?",
    ["Dialogue2041204"]="—Nonsense, I'm Wheeler! I've been serving at Master Nithil's side ever since he was a child!",
    ["Dialogue2041205"]="Haha! Do you even know the Young Master's preferences? Master, I know that your favorite flower is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Winter Cherry</color>, your favorite dish is Stir-fried Tongue, and the person you look up to most is Master Kroneika! I know everything, because I am the real Wheeler!",
    ["Dialogue2041206"]="(The attendant thinks for a moment, and then smiles cunningly.)\nAnd of course, and as the grandson of the Great Sage, hailing from the Heines Family who are famous for their extraordinary magical talent, who else on this continent can compare with your magical ability, Master?",
    ["Dialogue2041207"]="—Haha, you fraud! Now you've really put your foot in your mouth! The Master's hands are far more used to waving paintbrushes than wands. As for casting magic, he can't do it at all.\n(Wheeler suddenly realizes what he just said and covers his mouth with regret.)",
    ["Dialogue2041208"]="...Ah, now that was a mistake.",
    ["Dialogue2041301"]="(The thief finally shows his true face.)\nAlright, since you've seen through my disguise...",
    ["Dialogue2041302"]="(Wheeler quickly grabs the thief's wrist.)\n<size=26>—Don't even think about running!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2041401"]="...Please! Don't hurt me! I'll come clean! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Someone ordered me</color> to sneak into this mansion. I don't want to lose my life for nothing!",
    ["Dialogue2041402"]="It's true! <color=#CA2E0AFF>He</color> gave me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>potion</color> and I drank it down... then I suddenly looked like Wheeler! He said it would make it easier for me to sneak into the Heines Family mansion to steal Nithil's hair.",
    ["Dialogue2041403"]="He said that if he got some of Nithil's hair, he could make a potion that would transform him into Nithil. He said that this was the only way he could enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower Library</color> at will and borrow a manuscript that was only available to the Heines Family. What was it called? Oh yeah, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2041501"]="Needless to say, ever since I discovered that such a transformation potion existed, I couldn't trust anyone anymore. But I knew that as long as whoever was working <color=#CA2E0AFF>behind the scenes</color> coveted the manuscript, sooner or later, he'd try to sneak into Geffen Library through some other form of trickery. Since the library was no longer safe, I had to make a decision for myself—to take Merlin's Manuscript and get it to my grandfather, who has lived in seclusion for many years.",
    ["Dialogue2041502"]="Following the library's lending rules would leave a record of who took the manuscript! Taking it in secret was the only way I could escape pursuit from the person looking for it. I just didn't expect that the thieves would find me.\n(Nithil drops his head in disappointment.)",
    ["Dialogue2041503"]="Stealing it was the right thing to do in that situation. At this point, I see nothing wrong with your actions.",
    ["Dialogue2041504"]="(Nithil looks at Kroneika with a slightly surprised look.)\nGrandfather...",
    ["Dialogue2041505"]="What's more, not everyone would dare to risk his reputation and take on such a dangerous mission alone. The fact that your whereabouts were discovered only shows that our enemy is indeed very cunning, but the wisdom and courage you showed... Not even the mastermind behind all this could have counted on it.",
    ["Dialogue2041506"]="(Nithil exhibits an unnatural look that shows he doesn't seem to be used to accepting the admiration of others.)\nTh... thank you. And so, now...",
    ["Dialogue2041507"]="Adventurer, would you like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>infiltrate that Mobster gang's lair</color> and continue <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigating this situation</color>? If so, please take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Potion</color>. It will help you to obtain some valuable information.\n(Kroneika takes out a small crystal bottle from under his belt.)",
    ["Dialogue2041508"]="This may be our last chance to find out who is behind this. Please be careful as you go. When you're done, meet us in front of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2041601"]="(Piro's eyes look stupefied, his expression stiffens, and he begins spitting out golden bubbles.)\n...Bloop... Pop!",
    ["Dialogue2041602"]="...My name is Piro, leader of the Merciless Mobsters, bloop!\nI've been strictly single and penniless for 35 years, pop! But as long as I can close this <color=#CA2E0AFF>deal</color>, I'll make a huge stash in a flash.",
    ["Dialogue2041603"]="...Half a month ago, a mysterious <color=#CA2E0AFF>stranger</color> came here saying that if we got him <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color>, he'd give us more Zeny than we could ever spend, bloop! At first, he ordered my men to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak into the Heines Family mansion and steal it</color>. After that plan failed, we <color=#CA2E0AFF>followed Nithil Heines</color> and waited for a chance to snatch the book.",
    ["Dialogue2041604"]="...Well, the stranger never talked about himself much, bloop! But one of my more knowledgeable men said that he dressed like an <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2041605"]="...That stranger, he said he'd be staying in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest corner</color> of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Dungeon</color>, pop! Could someone really live in a place like that?\n(Piro's expression looks even more bewildered.)",
    ["Dialogue2041701"]="Hehe! I didn't expect to see you so soon! Your strength has improved yet again, but it won't be enough to catch me.\n(Baroshev slips a hand into his pocket.)\n...We shall see each other later, old friend!",
    ["Dialogue2041801"]="(Kroneika listens as you tell your story.)\n...I see. So this time, your old enemy can give up looking for Merlin's Manuscript, because as long as it is in my hands, no one will take it from me.",
    ["Dialogue2041802"]="Now, let's return to our conversation. It's time to make a decision about what Friedrich mentioned. I hereby announce that the member of the Heines Family going to Prontera to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take the throne</color> is...",
    ["Dialogue2041803"]="(Friedrich frowns and sighs in silence.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue2041804"]="—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Bidal Heines</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2041805"]="(Bidal's pupils dilate with shock.)\nWait a moment, Master Kroneika! You must have made a mistake. I'm not even a direct descendant...",
    ["Dialogue2041806"]="I know, of course, that you are not from the Heines Family lineage, but you possess the most magical ability of your peers, and this is the reason for my decision.\nAs a <color=#CA2E0AFF>magical family</color> well-known across the land for producing several Great Sages, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heines Family's successor</color> must have adequate magical talent. Those like Nithil who <color=#CA2E0AFF>cannot use magic</color> cannot be considered.",
    ["Dialogue2041807"]="(Nithil lowers his head and purses his lips, uttering in a voice that is almost inaudible.)\nI'm sorry...",
    ["Dialogue2041808"]="And so, my decision will not be changed, but that doesn't mean other matters cannot be changed. For example, today I was reminded of the fact that even the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Winter Cherry</color> blooming quietly in the corner must not be deemed inferior.\n(Kroneika looks at Nithil.)",
    ["Dialogue2041809"]="Grandfather...!",
    ["Dialogue2041810"]="There was a time when I used to judge others by their level of magical talent alone, but I inadvertently ignored other important qualities and attributes. Sure enough, there is another form of greatness in the world, which can only be seen from a different point of view.",
    ["Dialogue2041901"]="(When observing the golden brooch shining in the light, a crest resembling a raven's wing can be seen under the translucent ruby.)",
    ["Dialogue2042001"]="(A few drops of blood can be seen on the ground. Judging from the color, they must have been shed not long ago.)",
    ["Dialogue2042101"]="(Sure enough, you find a few more drops of blood leading off somewhere. If you follow these drops, perhaps you can find out whose blood this is.)",
    ["Dialogue2042201"]="(The trail of blood extends all the way to the shade of a tree. Could the injured man be him?)",
    ["Dialogue2050101"]="Stop... Stop it! Queenie! Look, someone's coming!",
    ["Dialogue2050102"]="Hey, Adventurer! How are...\n(The young lady stops mid-sentence. Her eyes dart around as she seems to have thought of a ploy.)\nDo you mind doing a small favor for us...?",
    ["Dialogue2050103"]="(Her eyes widen in surprise.)\nQueenie! You...",
    ["Dialogue2050104"]="You were the ones taking your own sweet time. They're so far ahead of us now! We won't be able to catch up to them with our speed, but if an adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue2050105"]="Hooray! Awesome! I knew it! Kind and brave adventurers are the most reliable!",
    ["Dialogue2050106"]="(She looks to the ground uneasily.)\nR-really...? If this is the case...",
    ["Dialogue2050107"]="Well then, we'll count on this adventurer to help us confirm it! Otherwise, if we really were to meet the princes, Leia would likely be so shy that she'll hide in the ground!",
    ["Dialogue2050108"]="Yup, the two most famous princes among the nobles in this capital—Azer Alm of the Walter Family and Aronst of the Gaebolg Family! Although I only saw a glimpse of their side profile, but I'm confident that you won't be able to find the same handsome side profiles anywhere else in Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue2050109"]="If you're willing, we hope that you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>confirm the identities of the princes on our behalf</color>. It would be even better if you are able to take a few photos of them!",
    ["Dialogue2050110"]="(Queenie pats you on the shoulder. She looks pretty sincere.)\nPlease, Adventurer? The princes' heroic acts have been circulating among the nobles recently... So much so that we all want to see it for ourselves! Especially Leia here! Whenever she hears the princes' names... Ouch! What did you pinch me for?!",
    ["Dialogue2050111"]="(Her face reddens as she stomps her foot on the ground in embarrassment.)\nBig sister Queenie! You... You big bully!",
    ["Dialogue2050112"]="Alright, alright. Stop it. Do you not want to see the princes anymore?",
    ["Dialogue2050113"]="(Rosetta turns around and winks at you slyly.)\nAs you can see, in order to protect our pseudo sisterly love, we'll have to trouble you to make this trip for us! We saw the princes heading towards the direction of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pooler Garden</color> just now. Hmm, but that seems to be a place for love and romance...?",
    ["Dialogue2050114"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Come to think of it, there have been rumors about the two of them hanging out a lot lately. They also forbade guards to follow them while they're out, could they be...</color></size>\nNope! No, no, no! I got to stop thinking about it!\n(Rosetta covers her face shyly all of a sudden, however the excitement that is shining through her eyes cannot be masked.)",
    ["Dialogue2050115"]="Ahem... I-in any case, we'll be counting on you, Adventurer! We'll be waiting for your good news here! Don't let us beautiful ladies wait too long!",
    ["Dialogue2050201"]="Stop chasing them! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2050202"]="Now is not the time for that! Look at Aronst! H-he has been hurt! It's all my fault... It was because Aronst was trying to protect me, that's why...",
    ["Dialogue2050203"]="Me...?\n(Azer looks stunned for a moment, then he looks toward his sleeve that has been slit by a sword.)\nIt's just a cut... It doesn't matter. What's important now is to think of a way to treat Aronst! We... We must...",
    ["Dialogue2050204"]="(Azer closes his eyes and takes a deep breath after hearing what you said. When he opens his eyes again, you see that the whirlwind of emotions that were in his eyes have calmed down.)\nThank you, Adventurer. I need your help now. Aronst has been seriously injured and we cannot move him carelessly. So please hurry back to Prontera Cathedral and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for a priestess who is well-versed in healing</color>. I will stay here to look over Aronst till you come back.",
    ["Dialogue2050301"]="Wha-...! You're saying that there was an assassination attempt on Prince Aronst?! And he's seriously injured?!",
    ["Dialogue2050302"]="Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>lead the way</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2050401"]="(Upon seeing your return, hope lights up Azer's eyes.)\nMargaret! Come over and take a look at Aronst! He's seriously injured!",
    ["Dialogue2050402"]="(Margaret rushes over to Aronst's side. A shocked expression takes over her face.)\nThis... This is...!",
    ["Dialogue2050403"]="Lord Azer! Adventurer! Please step back! I need to start healing Lord Aronst right away!",
    ["Dialogue2050501"]="This... This is impossible! Why didn't my healing spell work?!",
    ["Dialogue2050502"]="The would is still bleeding... No, this doesn't look right. Look at this wound, it is not healing at all. And you can even see that the blood is turning black!",
    ["Dialogue2050503"]="(After hearing what Azer said, Margaret leans over and looks closely at Prince Aronst's wound.)\n...No good. The blood is covering the wound, I can't diagnose the problem accurately.",
    ["Dialogue2050504"]="You're right, Adventurer. That was what I was intending to do. Since the healing spell didn't work, we should take a more direct approach. Please get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean water from the river</color> for cleaning Lord Aronst's wound. Also, there's a kind of herb called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clotting Grass</color> that grows near Mjolnir Mountains. It is a common herb used to treat external wounds. Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some</color> and bring it back as well?",
    ["Dialogue2050601"]="Alright, Adventurer! Now, please help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean Lord Aronst's</color> wounds and <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply the crushed Clotting Grass</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2050701"]="By Odin... What... What kind of evil curse is this?!",
    ["Dialogue2050702"]="I never expected this to be the cause of Lord Aronst's injuries... I'm sorry, Lord Azer, but with my abilities, I'm unable to fully remove this type of curse. We need to find a powerful exorcist to lift the curse from Lord Aronst, or else...",
    ["Dialogue2050703"]="(Azer lowers his head, deep in thought.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>A powerful exorcist... A powerful exorcist... Where to find a powerful exorcist...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2050704"]="We share the same thought, Adventurer. Parni is the most outstanding exorcist priestess in Rune Kingdom. In my opinion, she is the only one who can completely remove this curse!",
    ["Dialogue2050705"]="(Azer narrows his eyes.)\nParni... Parni... I remember this name. She was the exorcist priestess who got expelled due to a failed exorcism, right?",
    ["Dialogue2050706"]="It wasn't like that, Lord Azer! Parni, she... She really is a very outstanding exorcist priestess...\n(Margaret's voice gradually softens. She looks dejected.)",
    ["Dialogue2050707"]="...Is that so.",
    ["Dialogue2050708"]="I won't make light of my best friend's life. But if it's you, the person who once saved this kingdom, then I believe that you are capable of saving this country once more. Aronst is a successor candidate for the kingdom, hence he is closely connected to the fate of the kingdom. Do you understand what I mean, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2050709"]="(Her face lights up in surprise.)\nIn this case... In this case, let's hurry and look for Parni! From what I know, after Parni was relieved of her role as a royal priestess, she headed for Glast Heim to live in seclusion. I'll go with you-... Ah! The exorcism will need a staff, but Parni's staff has been...",
    ["Dialogue2050710"]="I-it's okay! I'll think of a way to steal... No, I mean I'll think of a way to convince the Archbishop to return the staff to Parni! You go <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring Parni back from Glast Heim</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2050801"]="It's been a while, Adventurer. I don't presume you're here to catch up with me?",
    ["Dialogue2050802"]="What did you say?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>After what happened to the three princes who were in the direct line of succession, I never expected that even Lord Aronst...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2050803"]="...You hope that I can return with you to help remove the curse on Lord Aronst?",
    ["Dialogue2050804"]="(Parni frowns. She seems hesitant.)\nTo be honest, Adventurer, I came to this distant ancient city because I wanted to avoid conflict and prevent myself from getting into another situation where I have no choice. But now...",
    ["Dialogue2050805"]="...You are right. Lord Aronst is innocent. He shouldn't have to become a sacrifice for anyone's scheme. Lead the way, Adventurer. I will return with you.",
    ["Dialogue2050901"]="(Parni leans over to observe the wound on Aronst's chest.)\nThere's no doubt... This is...",
    ["Dialogue2050902"]="I think what we need isn't an exorcism, but an opportunity to reveal the truth.",
    ["Dialogue2050903"]="(Azer steps in and interrupts the both of you rather forcefully.)\n...What are the two of you planning to do?",
    ["Dialogue2050904"]="Please do not worry, Lord Azer. We mean no harm towards the royal successor candidate. On the contrary...\n(Parni does not complete her sentence and looks at Azer meaningfully instead.)",
    ["Dialogue2050905"]="(Azer frowns.)\nI don't understand what you mean. I only want to know if Aronst can be saved.",
    ["Dialogue2050906"]="Please calm down, Your Highness. I need some items to create the potion.",
    ["Dialogue2050907"]="(Parni turns around to face you again.)\nDo you still remember those ingredients, Adventurer? The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eye of Truth</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysts</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>a yellow ore with magical powers</color>. These are the items that I need.",
    ["Dialogue2051001"]="That's right, these are the items that I need.\nJust like the last time, let us reveal the truth that has been hidden, Adventurer! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle this potion evenly on Lord Aronst's chest</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2051101"]="As expected... This isn't a curse. That tragedy wasn't the end... It was just the beginning.",
    ["Dialogue2051102"]="What exactly are the two of you talking about?",
    ["Dialogue2051103"]="Wait, Adventurer. Before that, please excuse me—Lord Azer, do you have any clues about the assassination that happened today?",
    ["Dialogue2051104"]="Clues...? Are you referring to the culprits? Are you... suspecting that it's me...?!\n(Azer's eyes widen. Rage like a burning fire can be seen in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue2051105"]="(Parni looks into the prince's eyes calmly and fearlessly.)\nIs it not? How is it that Lord Aronst is so badly injured whereas you are perfectly fine even though both of you were victims of the attempted assassination? If my guess is not wrong, wasn't the trip today planned by you, Lord Azer?",
    ["Dialogue2051106"]="Utterly ridiculous! What reason do I have for taking the life of my best friend! I was indeed the one who asked Aronst to meet me here to practice our swordsmanship, but... Wait, wait a minute...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>It was Father who told me about the blooming flowers in Pooler Garden...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2051107"]="(Azer seems to have thought of something but quickly shakes his head instead.)\n...No. I cannot simply believe your one-sided story, you need to show me evidence.",
    ["Dialogue2051108"]="In truth, this adventurer and me have secretly investigated the deaths of the three Gaebolg princes. Apart from Prince Nate, the snake scale mark on the other two princes disappeared after we used the Truth Serum. Hence, we suspected that the two princes did not die of the curse and were in fact murdered. This adventurer can vouch for me on this matter.",
    ["Dialogue2051109"]="I've heard about what happened to the three princes, but everyone thinks that it was an accident. I've never heard anything about it being a murder.",
    ["Dialogue2051110"]="What...?! You said you gave the bottle which held the poison to Father as evidence, but was warned by Father to keep mum about the secrets of the royal family?! This...",
    ["Dialogue2051111"]="...Now, Lord Aronst, who is also a successor candidate, has his life hanging by a thread for the same reasons. No matter how you think about it, the coincidences of these events seem too intentional.",
    ["Dialogue2051112"]="(Parni lowers her head and looks towards the unconscious Aronst with a hint of melancholy in her eyes.)\nIf this poison in Lord Aronst's body is the same as the poison that caused the death of the princes... We will first have to think of a way to locate the culprit then we might have a chance of getting the antidote from them.",
    ["Dialogue2051113"]="...This adventurer is right. Our priority now is to find a way to save Aronst. I'm willing to pay any price as long as Aronst can be saved.\nI remember that the group of assassins retreated toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>south</color>. Maybe we can start to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate their whereabouts</color> in that direction.",
    ["Dialogue2051114"]="...That's fine. Since you are the neutral party in this, regardless of what the investigation results may be, I'm sure Lord Azer will accept them. While you are at it, I will do my best to take care of Lord Aronst and to alleviate his symptoms. I will be counting on you.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I pray that Odin will lead you on the path of truth this time round...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2051201"]="Did you find any clues, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2051202"]="I see. So, they escaped in the direction of Prontera? I bet they went there thinking that we won't be able to carry out a high profile search in the capital.\nBut too bad, as long as they are in Prontera, they won't be able to hide from the Chivalry.",
    ["Dialogue2051203"]="Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the city gates and interview the guard</color>. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Get</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>list of carriages</color> that have passed in and out of Prontera recently. I believe that the assassin must be among them!",
    ["Dialogue2051301"]="Halt! Why are you loitering around suspiciously?!",
    ["Dialogue2051302"]="Oh, oh! You're... Um, I'm sorry! Please pardon me, the higher-ups have been very strict lately. Everyone's been rather stressed out...",
    ["Dialogue2051303"]="Lord Azer wants you to investigate the carriages that have passed in and out of the city today? Let me see... I should have registered all the carriages that entered the city... The most recent one... Ah yes, here it is. It's a carriage from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Chamber of Commerce</color>. It just passed by not too long ago.",
    ["Dialogue2051304"]="I checked their carriage just now and it was just filled with cargo boxes... If you are still worried, speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>an employee of the Chamber of Commerce</color> to check again. With Lord Azer's order, they will not put you in a spot.",
    ["Dialogue2051401"]="Erm, you want to check the cargo boxes that just arrived...? According to the rules, these are considered trade secrets, right?",
    ["Dialogue2051402"]="...Since this is an order from Lord Azer, I guess there's no choice then. The cargo boxes were recently unloaded so they should still be <color=#CA2E0AFF>at the empty space in front of the warehouse</color>. Once you are done checking, let me know so we can proceed to register the cargo to the warehouse.",
    ["Dialogue2051501"]="Goblins... Goblins were hiding in the cargo boxes?!\nNo wonder we haven't been able to balance the accounts recently... We've been robbed...",
    ["Dialogue2051502"]="Thank you for your help, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2051601"]="Thieving Goblins were hiding in the cargo boxes? And they stole quite a large amount of goods from the Wigner Chamber of Commerce? This...",
    ["Dialogue2051602"]="(The guard scratches his head and looks at you in embarrassment.)\nUm... Adventurer, can you not report this to Lord Azer? This is considered a lapse in our duty. If he were to find out...",
    ["Dialogue2051603"]="Oh! Right! Let me see... The carriage that entered the city before the one from Wigner Chamber of Commerce... was from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>church</color>! <color=#CA2E0AFF>It was a carriage that was carrying a few coffins</color>! S-speaking of which, while I was checking the carriage, there seemed to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange noises</color> coming from within...?\n(The guard shudders and seems to recall certain things that are indescribable.)",
    ["Dialogue2051701"]="By Odin! Finally, someone's here to help!",
    ["Dialogue2051702"]="Adventurer, look at this coffin! I'm trying to appease the spirit within it but its obsession seems to be too strong and my prayers aren't working! From the looks of it, only <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color> that contains Odin's power will be able to calm this vengeful spirit.",
    ["Dialogue2051703"]="Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the Central Fountain</color> on my behalf and ask for Odin's blessing?",
    ["Dialogue2051801"]="Thank you very much, Adventurer. If it weren't for your help, I wouldn't have been able to appease this Wraith.",
    ["Dialogue2051802"]="You would like to know why there is a Wraith in the coffin?",
    ["Dialogue2051803"]="In actual fact, this is what the church does all year round. We accept the remains of the deceased from all over the continent. Among them, there are many whose spirits cannot rest after their death. These spirits will eventually find their final resting place in the blessed land of Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue2051804"]="Oddly enough, we have recently been constantly receiving requests to help the spirits of the dead move on to the afterlife. And most of these requests are from <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside the city</color>... Come to think of it, some of the remains seemed a little unnatural. They seemed to have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>altered</color>...?\n(Zair strokes his beard and seems to be deep in thoughts.)",
    ["Dialogue2051805"]="Oh no! By Odin, please forgive my ignorance! How could... How could something like this happen on these blessed lands!",
    ["Dialogue2051806"]="Adventurer, please forget what I just said! Odin will surely protect his children!",
    ["Dialogue2051901"]="...Ahh?! So, so you mean, th-there really is...\n(Fear can be seen on the guard's face as his teeth start to chatter.)",
    ["Dialogue2051902"]="If you couldn't find what you're looking for in the last two carriages, then this is the only carriage left that entered Prontera today... Erm, Adventurer! I don't mean to be nosy, but there's really no need to check this carriage!",
    ["Dialogue2051903"]="Because <color=#CA2E0AFF>this carriage belongs to the Royal Chivalry</color>! Furthermore, they have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Pass</color>... I'm just a lowly guard, I can't afford to offend them!",
    ["Dialogue20519031"]="...Show it to me.",
    ["Dialogue2051904"]="Yes, sure! Here you go! But once you're done looking at it, please explain to Lord Azer that I didn't fail in my duty!",
    ["Dialogue2052001"]="Did you find any clues, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2052002"]="Oh? So the ones who were hiding in the cargo box were just a group of Goblins who were trying to steal the gold coins.... What a pity. Were there any other clues?",
    ["Dialogue2052003"]="Oh? So the strange sounds that were coming from the coffin in the carriage were from a vengeful spirit that was sealed within... What a pity. Were there any other clues?",
    ["Dialogue2052004"]="You... You said they entered Prontera on a Royal Chivalry's carriage? And they even produced a Royal Pass?!\n(The expression on Azer's face changes and his clenched fists start to shake.)",
    ["Dialogue2052005"]="A Royal Pass... Something only members of the Seven Royal Families possess. The pass allows them unrestricted travel around the kingdom. Among them, the only person who has the power to command the Royal Chivalry is...\n(Parni looks towards Azer who has fallen silent. An air of tension emanates from them.)",
    ["Dialogue2052006"]="(After a long moment of silence, Azer finally unclenches his fists and starts to speak again.)\n...High Priestess Parni, you should have one last way to save Aronst, right?",
    ["Dialogue2052007"]="(Parni frowns. She seems to disagree with what Azer has just said.)\nI do not understand what you mean, Lord Azer.",
    ["Dialogue2052008"]="I once heard that there is a kind of forbidden spell in exorcism that is only passed down to royal priests. A spell that can transfer a curse from one person to another. If you can make use of its theory and transfer the poison from Aronst to me, then Aronst can be saved.",
    ["Dialogue2052009"]="That's too dangerous, Lord Azer!\nI... I know now you had nothing to do with the assassinations. If this whole affair is not what we think it is, you'll...",
    ["Dialogue2052010"]="(Azer smiles. He seems to have made up his mind.)\nBut Aronst will be saved, won't he?",
    ["Dialogue2052011"]="Aronst and I are best friends, but more importantly, I'm his subject. He is indispensable to the kingdom and so to me, protecting him is the same as protecting Rune Kingdom. Be it for duty or my own personal wish, I'm obliged to fulfill it.",
    ["Dialogue2052012"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Besides, who knows? Maybe I'll be able to get the antidote...</color></size>\n(Azer lowers his head as he mumbles to himself. His voice is so soft that it can barely be heard, but the mixed feelings in his voice are unmistakable.)",
    ["Dialogue2052013"]="...Sigh.\nWill you really not regret this, Lord Azer?",
    ["Dialogue2052014"]="Of course. I am ready.",
    ["Dialogue2052015"]="If this is the case, I have no reason to stop you. But in order to use this forbidden spell, I will need the sap of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arcane Fruits</color> to conjure the magic circle. Arcane Fruits usually grow in places where sunlight doesn't reach. It makes use of energy that doesn't belong to our world to grow... I think you should be able to find some in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery to the south</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2052016"]="Thank you, Adventurer. You are indeed the person best suited for this task. I will get ready while I wait for your return.",
    ["Dialogue2052101"]="Thank you, Adventurer. I can now start to conjure the magic circle.\nHowever, I will need to trouble you to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> once more. Find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>skulls and eyeballs of vengeful spirits</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sageworms</color> underground. These items will make up the crux of the magic circle...",
    ["Dialogue2052102"]="...Skulls and eyeballs? Such... grotesque ingredients.",
    ["Dialogue2052103"]="This is a forbidden spell, Lord Azer. It is unlike the kind of palace games that the royals play for fun or to demonstrate their status.... I just need this spell to work. It doesn't have to look pretty.",
    ["Dialogue2052104"]="...You're right, Parni. Maybe we should have learned to walk away from the conventions of the past and look at things from a different perspective. If we had done that, then maybe... <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Maybe the kingdom's fate would have been different...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2052105"]="Alright... There is no time for idle chatter. Lord Aronst can't hold out for much longer. Adventurer, can I trouble you to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim underground</color> once more?",
    ["Dialogue2052201"]="You're right on time, Adventurer. I've just finished conjuring the magic circle.",
    ["Dialogue2052202"]="Now, please place the skulls and eyeballs <color=#CA2E0AFF>around the magic circle in order</color>... Yes, right over there. I've marked it out.",
    ["Dialogue2052301"]="Now... All that is left is my staff.",
    ["Dialogue2052302"]="Convince the Archbishop? Impossible. With Margaret's character, the likelihood of...\nForget it. Given the current situation, as long as we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>get the staff</color>, everything else is not important. Looking at the time, it's likely that Margaret has already successfully carried out her plan...",
    ["Dialogue2052303"]="...Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2052401"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Heh! Just as I expected. Archbishop Wolmas meditates in the confessional at this time every day.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2052402"]="Ahh—W-what! Oh, it's just you! Don't scare me like that! I thought it was Archbishop...\n(Margaret seems to realize something mid-sentence and covers her mouth with her hands. She then starts to cough dramatically.)",
    ["Dialogue2052403"]="Ahem! Ad-Adventurer! Since you came here to look for me, that would mean Parni has already agreed to remove the curse from Lord Aronst, right?",
    ["Dialogue20524031"]="(Tell the truth)",
    ["Dialogue20524032"]="(Hide the truth)",
    ["Dialogue2052404"]="How... How is that possible! Lord Aronst was poisoned?! And Lord Azer intends to... intends to sacrifice his life... I don't believe you! How could Parni allow this to happen!",
    ["Dialogue2052405"]="I knew that Parni would agree to it! This is a great opportunity to regain the trust of the royal family! Heh!\nWell then, there's no time to waste! It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return this staff to its rightful owner</color>! Oh right, please tell Parni that I'm very proud of her! She'll always be my best friend!",
    ["Dialogue2052406"]="She... She has to take the life of the prince whom she serves. Can you imagine how upset she must feel...\n(Margaret covers her face with her hands and sobs quietly.)\n*Sobs* Why must such misfortune always befall Parni?",
    ["Dialogue2052407"]="If this is Parni's choice, the only thing I can do is to give her my full support...\nAdventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>give this staff to my best friend</color>... And tell her that I will always believe in her.",
    ["Dialogue2052501"]="(Parni accepts the staff and touches the decorative gem on its tip gently.)\nI never thought that I would be able to hold this staff again.",
    ["Dialogue2052502"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Such irony. This was taken from me because I failed to save that person's life... And now, it has been returned to me because the life of that person's family member is in danger. By Odin, is this punishment for my incompetence?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2052503"]="...I see. That does sound like something she would say.\n(Parni holds up her staff. The troubled look in her eyes fading away.)\nIf this is the case, then I mustn't let her down.",
    ["Dialogue2052504"]="...Lord Azer, are you ready? You must know that once the magic circle is activated, there will be no more room for regret.",
    ["Dialogue2052505"]="(Nods resolutely.)\nThe word \"regret\" doesn't exist in the Walter Family. I will always be accountable for the choices I make.",
    ["Dialogue2052506"]="Then let us begin. Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay away from the magic circle</color> when I am casting the spell. Do not be consumed by the resentment that emerges from the circle.\nAs for Lord Azer, all you need to do is lie next to Lord Aronst. I will take care of the rest.",
    ["Dialogue2052601"]="(He holds his chest in pain and is unable to even complete a sentence.)\nT-this feeling... The spell succeeded...?",
    ["Dialogue2052602"]="Yes. Lord Aronst's life is no longer in danger and he will wake up after a moment of rest. But you...\n(Parni casts her gaze towards the ground. A profound sense of sadness can be seen in her eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue2052603"]="It's alright... Everything is... Everything is alright as long as Aronst is fine... Now I just have to... get myself home...\n(Azer's voice is weak. He struggles to stand but staggers and sits back down instead.)",
    ["Dialogue2052604"]="R-really? I can't thank you enough... Adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue2052605"]="In this case, I'll stay here and take care of the unconscious Lord Aronst. Adventurer, please... Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>protect Lord Azer</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2052701"]="Hurry... Hurry and tell Father that... *Coughs* I-I'm injured...",
    ["Dialogue2052702"]="Young Master! What happened to you, Young Master! Why are you covered in injuries? Was it... Was it you!?\n(The servant suddenly turns and glares vehemently at you.)",
    ["Dialogue2052703"]="D-don't be rude! This is... This is the adventurer who saved me! *Coughs*",
    ["Dialogue2052704"]="An assassination attempt was made on Aronst and I at the Pooler Garden... Look, look at this...\n(Azer covers his mouth and coughs. He staggers towards the servant and leans on him as he deliberately undoes his shirt.)",
    ["Dialogue2052705"]="...!!\nHow... How... How did this mark... No...<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I don't want to die...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2052706"]="Lord Azer, Lord Azer! Hang in there! I'll inform Lord Ian right away!",
    ["Dialogue2052801"]="(Azer beckons at you. He lowers his voice and speaks into your ear.)\nA-Adventurer... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow him s-secretly</color>... *Coughs* He was assigned to me by Father and I know that he would sometimes report my whereabouts to Father... So... So if he...",
    ["Dialogue2052901"]="Adventurer, how did it go?",
    ["Dialogue2052902"]="(Azer frowns upon hearing what you said and a series a cough escapes from behind the hand covering his mouth.)\n*Coughs violently* Really? H-he met with the people who tried to assassinate me...?",
    ["Dialogue2052903"]="He even mentioned poison and an alchemist...?\n(Azer clutches the front of his shirt tightly as if to hide the evil mark upon his chest.)\nRidiculous... This is utterly ridiculous...",
    ["Dialogue2052904"]="Azer! Are you alright?!",
    ["Dialogue2053001"]="Aronst?! How did you...?!",
    ["Dialogue2053002"]="Lord Aronst regained consciousness not long after both of you left. After he heard about what happened to Lord Azer...",
    ["Dialogue2053003"]="(Parni stops mid-sentence and looks towards Lord Azer's chest meaningfully.)\n...After he heard that Lord Azer has been injured in an assassination, he insisted on coming here to see it for himself.",
    ["Dialogue2053004"]="That goes without saying! Stop talking! Show me your injury! Where is the injury?! Is it on your chest?!",
    ["Dialogue2053005"]="...No, I'm alright... *Coughs* It's just...\n(Azer discreetly adjusts the front of his shirt and lifts up his sleeve that was slit by a sword.)\nIt's just a little cut. Look... It's not serious at all.",
    ["Dialogue2053006"]="(Aronst scratches his head. His expression troubled.)\nHm... Really? But you don't look very well...",
    ["Dialogue2053007"]="I'm just a little tired... After all, I had to protect you too since you still can't fully fend for yourself.\nI don't mean to nag, Aronst. But you really got to improve your swordsmanship... *Coughs* Or else, the next time...",
    ["Dialogue2053008"]="R-right! Treatment! Parni! Hurry and treat Azer's wound!",
    ["Dialogue2053009"]="...I can't do that, Lord Aronst. Now that you've both returned, the task of healing the prince should not be in the hands of an expelled priestess like me.",
    ["Dialogue2053010"]="(Parni lowers her head and bows deeply at the two princes.)\nI believe that the priests of the Walter Family will tend to Lord Azer's injuries with utmost care.",
    ["Dialogue2053011"]="...Thank you for all that you've done today.",
    ["Dialogue2053012"]="Please do not mention it, Your Highness.",
    ["Dialogue2053013"]="What... What about Azer's injuries...?",
    ["Dialogue2053014"]="(After hearing what you said, Azer lifts his head and looks towards the figure that is running towards him. His glare turns sharp.)\nWe can leave the rest to Parish. Also, I will speak to Father about how to deal with those assassins. They will pay for their assassination attempts on the prince.",
    ["Dialogue2053015"]="I'm... I'm afraid we won't be able to see each other for a while, Aronst.",
    ["Dialogue2053101"]="(A few drops of blood can be seen on the ground. Judging by the color, they're fairly fresh.)",
    ["Dialogue2053201"]="(Sure enough, you find a few more drops of blood leading off somewhere. If you follow these drops, perhaps you can find out whose blood this is.)",
    ["Dialogue2053301"]="(The trail of blood stops here. Instead, you find the tracks of a carriage headed in the direction of Prontera.)",
    ["Dialogue2053401"]="(The cargo box is filled with Lucky Four-Leaf Clovers. Nothing else seems strange about it.)",
    ["Dialogue2053501"]="(The cargo box is filled with Empty Bottles. Nothing else seems strange about it.)",
    ["Dialogue2053601"]="(This meticulously and exquisitely crafted pass grants its owner the ability to travel without restriction in and out of all the majors cities in Rune Kingdom. But upon closer inspection, you notice a bloody fingerprint next to the royal seal at the bottom right corner of the pass...)",
    ["Dialogue2053701"]="(A mark appears on Aronst's chest. When you take a closer look, you see that the dark green mark resembles a snake scale...)",
    ["Dialogue2053801"]="(You pour the strange bubbling Truth Serum onto Prince Aronst's body. With a sizzling sound, the snake scale mark on the prince's chest starts to disappear.)",
    ["Dialogue2053901"]="...You—Weren't you supposed to get rid of Prince Aronst? Why was...?!",
    ["Dialogue2053902"]="How is this possible?! We deliberately avoided him when we attacked...",
    ["Dialogue2053903"]="(The servant claws at his cheeks in fear.)\nAhhhh—That's it, we're dead meat! He won't spare any of us!",
    ["Dialogue2053904"]="...He?",
    ["Dialogue2053905"]="(The servant lifts his head suddenly as a thought springs to mind.)\n...Wait a minute. If this poison was created by the alchemist, wouldn't he have the antidote?",
    ["Dialogue2053906"]="Hurry, go find someone for me! If you can find that person in time, we might be saved!",
    ["Dialogue2060101"]="Well, what are we waiting for! We should continue on and try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> the<color=#CA2E0AFF> whereabouts of the Church’s Diplomatic Corps</color>. During your previous mission, even though we lost track of the subject, you were able to get out without exposing your identity. Fortunately, according to previous intelligence,  after leaving Prontera they went straight to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2060102"]="... be careful, Adventurer. I sincerely hope you can bring good news to the kingdom again.",
    ["Dialogue2060201"]="Well, well, well... a most unexpected visitor!",
    ["Dialogue2060202"]="It's been a long time, Adventurer. Let me guess... You're not here just to have a catch up, are you?",
    ["Dialogue2060203"]="I see. You’ve heard the rumor, too?\nAlthough... It's not the Pharaoh’s ghost. It's purely the work of the grave robbers.",
    ["Dialogue2060204"]="In fact, this is not the first time we have had rumors of a giant mummy. Many indigenous people in the desert have seen large mummies, but only during the first quarter of the moon cycle, on monthly intervals. This is due to a plant called <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic thorn</color>. During the rest of the month, they will store magic and then when the first quarter of the moon arrives, there is a concentrated release. If the mummy eats the magic thorn by mistake at this time....",
    ["Dialogue2060205"]="Precisely! The mummies grow much larger because they consume too much magic at once. As long as the magic is consumed, they will return to their original state. As for attacks on humans... I guess, those statements must have come from the grave robbers.... Did they go to hunt <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isis</color> in the Pyramid?",
    ["Dialogue2060206"]="Because the <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood of the Isis</color> has a fatal attraction to the mummy! These two monsters are prey to each other. A mummy will become manic and aggressive once it smells the blood of an Isis.",
    ["Dialogue2060207"]="... it was both accidental and inevitable. History is always made up of countless possibilities, those grave robbers must bear the consequences of their actions, don't you think?\n(Sean shrugs his shoulders, looking rather smug for the grave robber’s misfortune)",
    ["Dialogue2060208"]="Tsssk, you look like you're thinking up some devilish ideas. You don’t need any help, do you?",
    ["Dialogue2060209"]="Ah-hem! It just so happens that today and tomorrow happen to be the first quarter moon.\n(he looks up at the sky, indicating the useful information)\nBut... you wouldn’t use such knowledge to your advantage would you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2060301"]="Long time no see, adventurer... What are you doing here?\n(Neste greets you warmly, but after seeing you, he scratches his head in confusion)",
    ["Dialogue2060302"]="Ah, are you asking the religious people over there? I hear they are going to cross the desert to Morroc’s port. Not long ago, they asked me where they could find a guide who was familiar with the route.",
    ["Dialogue2060303"]="Wha... What....? L...Lead them away?! Investigate the cargo box?!\n(your recollection made Neste gasp in surprise)\n<size=26>This is not——</size>",
    ["Dialogue2060304"]="Uh huh!\n(Neste bears his teeth and draws his claws. He asks you to let him go. Just to be sure, you indicate to him to keep his voice down and then you let go)\nAhhh... Ahhhh... You, Why do you....?",
    ["Dialogue2060305"]="In... In this case... I, I may be able to help you!\nAs long as someone is responsible for distracting the guards, so that you can get close to the material box?",
    ["Dialogue2060306"]="(Neste grabs his head again, showing your familiar simple smile)\nYou've helped us so much in the past... I can’t stand idly by, now that it is you who is in trouble.",
    ["Dialogue2060307"]="No, you're welcome... However, it may not be enough for me alone... We must some of our slum’s most talented individuals. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Quarryman Shah</color>, the most powerful, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gavin the hunter gatherer</color>, the smartest, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Delier</color>, who mingles with <color=#CA2E0AFF>wolves</color> and has super speed abilities... Together, we will pretend to rob food, create a distraction, and lure those guards away!",
    ["Dialogue2060308"]="Alright! I'll go back to Rhinestone street and make some preparations. If you find them, come and meet me as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue2060401"]="Tha.... Thank you so much, Adventurer!\nThese Giearth are tiny, very nimble, and always move in groups. If you hadn't arrived in time, I would have been in real danger!",
    ["Dialogue2060402"]="Eh? How.... How do you know my name?\n(the powerful man scratched the back of his head, looking adorkable)",
    ["Dialogue2060403"]="... you need my help? Well... Typically, I should repay you, seeing as you just saved my life, but....\n(Shah looks at his empty backpack in distress)\nI haven't finished my work for today.....",
    ["Dialogue2060404"]="Ah, it's those creepy little Gierth. If they hadn't robbed me of the ore I worked so hard to collect and fled into the depths of the mine, I wouldn't have to go back and dig again.",
    ["Dialogue2060405"]="Uhhh, really?\nThat would be a huge help! All the <color=#CA2E0AFF>minerals they took from me</color> should be hidden <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep in the mine</color>! If you help me retrieve them, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I can get off work at a reasonable hour</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2060501"]="Now... my quest for today is complete.\n(Shah carefully counts the minerals you brought back and gives you a big smile)\nExcellent! I can go home!",
    ["Dialogue2060502"]="Thank you again for your help, Adventurer! Rest assured, I will fulfill my promise and go to Rhinestone street to meet Nestor!",
    ["Dialogue2060601"]="Water... Give me... Water\n(the person lying on the ground is struggling to speak and seems in a daze. You notice that his lips are dry and cracked, obvious signs of dehydration)",
    ["Dialogue2060602"]="Help... Help me... Adventurer... I've been scouring in the desert all day!\nNot far away... Oasis... Water... I beg you",
    ["Dialogue2060701"]="... Ahhhh. Thank you, thank you... Adventurer. If it hadn't been for you, I could have died.\n(after drinking the water, the young man seems to have finally regained his mind) My name is Gavin. I am a hunter gatherer, here to find some scorched mushroom. How about you?",
    ["Dialogue2060702"]="Looking for.... me? But I... but I don't know you....",
    ["Dialogue2060703"]="I see... I see! Well considering you just saved my life, I am willing to help you!",
    ["Dialogue2060801"]="……\n(from a distance, you scan the desolate Gobi desert, you see a pack of wolves, amongst them a girl with superior speed and agility)",
    ["Dialogue2060802"]="Siii------Saaaa-----\n(she puts her hands on the sides of her mouth and calls out, shouting at the top of her lungs as if she were looking for something)\nWhere are youuu——",
    ["Dialogue2060803"]="... You are?",
    ["Dialogue2060804"]="Why is Nestor looking for me?\n... I'm very sorry, I wont be able to help you at this exact moment. I lost my companion not so long ago. I must find him.",
    ["Dialogue2060805"]="Who...? No... Sisa is a baby desert wolf. I was raised by wolves. These desert wolves are my family.",
    ["Dialogue2060806"]="You will help me find Sisa?\n(Delier looks at you for a moment, her eyes assessing your intentions)\n... OK. I promise you, if you help me find Sisa, I will join your team.",
    ["Dialogue2060807"]="Sisa is a baby desert wolf just six months old. There is a very obvious white tuft of furr on his forehead. He runs around a bit frantically... Mostly because I went out to look for food today and didn't come back in time. Please take these fresh pieces of meat and see if you can find him anywhere nearby. As long as he can smell the meat, the hungry Sisa will certainly turn up sooner or later.",
    ["Dialogue2060901"]="Okay... Okay! You’re not allowed out of my sight! Sisa!",
    ["Dialogue2060902"]="Awww... Aw~\n(the fluffy wolf cub wags its tail happily in Delier’s arms)",
    ["Dialogue2060903"]="Thank you for finding my companion, Adventurer. In return, I will fulfill my promise. I'll see you on Rhinestone street!",
    ["Dialogue2061001"]="Ok... Here we are, all finally together.",
    ["Dialogue2061002"]="You’ve done a great job, Adventurer. Leave the work to us next time! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait a moment</color> before you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to</color> the diplomatic corps<color=#CA2E0AFF>encampment</color> and investigate . Please relax, at that time... No one is going to be there!",
    ["Dialogue2061101"]="I've been looking forward to the opportunity to talk to you, young man.\n(the figure under the coconut tree looks back towards you, and you realize, that this is the young blonde guy who met you at the South Gate)",
    ["Dialogue2061102"]="Yes, it was me who left those notes, with the intention to lead you here. Although, when I first met at the south gate I could roughly guess your identity, but I still want to know, are the rumors true....? Do you really have extraordinary wisdom and courage beyond the reach of others? All throughout this journey... You have given me the most perfect answer.",
    ["Dialogue2061103"]="... who the heck are you?",
    ["Dialogue2061104"]="(the young man waved his hand, motioning you to take it easy)\nI know you must have many questions and doubts, but unfortunately, now is not the time to tell the whole story. Although your plan to distract my companions has worked, they will soon find out. If they see us both.....",
    ["Dialogue2061201"]="It's been such a long time!\nWhy... to come to Morroc for such an important quest? The great heir of Odin’s bloodline!",
    ["Dialogue2061202"]="Eh.....? Am I right?",
    ["Dialogue2061203"]="... Alright, alright! No need to get all physical, I get it! I wouldn’t doubt you, buddy!\n(Halmod pats you on the shoulder with a sincere smile)\nTell me, what can I do for you?",
    ["Dialogue2061204"]="Let me invite those diplomatic corps men to a banquet in the mansion, where we can get them a bit inebriated!?\n(listening carefully, Halmod frowned, thinking about the meaning of your words)",
    ["Dialogue2061205"]="Well... Since it's the request of a close friend... OK! I've decided! You <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me</color> first!",
    ["Dialogue2061301"]="... dear friend, the whistling of the wind and the clear starry sky brings me back to the day we first met——",
    ["Dialogue2061302"]="But these details don’t seem to bother you!\nLook around at these familiar sights, surely it reminds you of the fierce rivalry that we once shared? I saw your raw courage in both victory and defeat, and that is precisely why I regard you as my best friend!",
    ["Dialogue2061303"]="What I mean is, pick up your weapon! You claim to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>brave in battle</color>, now you can re-kindle <color=#CA2E0AFF>my desire to fight</color>.....\n(Halmod vigorously pulls out his sword)\nThen I will grant you your request, my friend!",
    ["Dialogue2061401"]="<size=26>——Have fun!</size>\nIt feels just like old times! Only you are worthy of bringing me such a fun contest!",
    ["Dialogue2061402"]="Sure enough, heroes always look up to one-another... To keep a dear friend like you, in the end is because - <size=26>I am too strong!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2061403"]="<size=24>..... you say I'm still the same as before, only with a bigger head/ego?!</size>\nHahahaha - you haven't changed one bit! Very special and so much sincerity in your evaluations... In the whole of Morroc, only you would dare to talk to me in such a way.",
    ["Dialogue2061404"]="It doesn't matter!\n(Halmod waved his big hand, forthright and stupid)\nIt is important! Win or lose, I will always be there to help my dearest friend!",
    ["Dialogue2061405"]="Don't worry, I'm going to prepare the <color=#CA2E0AFF>banquet</color>! Let the diplomatic corps from the church countries experience the excellent hospitality of the Morroc people!",
    ["Dialogue2061501"]="... you did a good job, young man.",
    ["Dialogue2061502"]="Yes, I can promise you. When we meet again, I will tell you the whereabouts of his majesty... But for the sake of his Majesty's safety, I must confirm some questions with you. First of all... Who entrusted you to come searching for his majesty?",
    ["Dialogue2061503"]="... Bohr sent me.\n(the young man gradually relaxes after hearing such a satisfactory response)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He... He's a good lad....</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2061504"]="Since Bohr sent you here, I have infinitely less doubts about you, we can move on. The next question... Is asked by his majesty. He wants to know... speaking from your heart, what kind of qualities do you think make a perfect king?",
    ["Dialogue2061505"]="(the young blonde man smiles and shakes his head. You can even feel the kindness in his eyes)\nYou're right... But not exactly right. These are all qualities needed by a king, but the most important thing that your majesty needs... Is the quality you have shown throughout your journey to get here, that is, your sincerity.",
    ["Dialogue2061506"]="... people will trust and respect you, if you treat people sincerely. There is no one country in the world. Your majesty sees this in you the most out of the many young people who guard the Rune Kingdom. So... If he can <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand over this country to you</color>, he will be very relieved.",
    ["Dialogue2061507"]="... you all bring hope and a future to this country, and someone should update the out-dated systems. Please remember these words, young man. This is his Majesty's last wish.",
    ["Dialogue2061508"]="In fact... one day I hope to have a good talk with you. Not under such circumstances, but on a sunny afternoon, I will invite you to see the fleur-de-lis sprouting in the garden. In the distance, we will hear the sound of a child’s laughter, as well as the fragrance of black tea and freshly baked cookies.",
    ["Dialogue2061509"]="(he walks up and taps you on the shoulder to signal you to turn around. He puts his hand to your mouth and you smell something strange from his fingertips. You suddenly feel sleepy)\nUnfortunately... It's time, young man. Look in to your past and you will find the answers to all of your questions.",
    ["Dialogue2061601"]="Oh, Ho ~ hello again, my good mate!\nHow's it going? Have you finished your <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret</color> mission?",
    ["Dialogue2061602"]="Mission? Didn't the mission leave set sail from the port this morning? The night before yesterday, I hosted a banquet in their honor at your request. They enjoyed all of the Morroc’s liquour... A lot of them drank a bit too much! It is because of this that they delayed leaving until this morning\n(seeing your paniced expression, Halmod seems to realize something)",
    ["Dialogue2061603"]="Errr... Did you... Fail the mission?",
    ["Dialogue2061604"]="This... These are the ingredients to make anesthetics! You can fall into a coma if you take too much of the youmenglan fragrance at once! You... You’re not being taken advantage of are you?",
    ["Dialogue2061605"]="They set out by boat this morning and may have crossed the border of the Rune Kingdom by now.\n(Halmod shakes his head with regret)\nSorry, dear friend, I'm afraid I can't help you. You will have to get the immigration documents.",
    ["Dialogue2061701"]="Are you okay, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2061702"]="... don't panic. You were there for such a long time, a lot must have happened. Tell me everything, take your time.",
    ["Dialogue2061703"]="(During your recollection, Bohr's face grew colder)\n... you mean that the young man knocked you out using Youmenglan? Two whole days have passed since you woke up? Do you have any other clues?",
    ["Dialogue2061704"]="This, <size=26>Whats this?!</size>\n(you empty the contents of your pockets and Bohr’s face suddenly turns pale with surprise)\nQuickly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>show me </color>this<color=#CA2E0AFF> ring</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2061801"]="……\n(In silence, Bohr looks at the ring in his hand. The light shimmering off the ring’s gem brings back the memory of that night)",
    ["Dialogue2061802"]="... that was not a dream, Adventurer. He is our king, his majesty Tristan III.",
    ["Dialogue2061803"]="The ring in your pocket is a symbol of kingship handed down from generation to generation in the Rune Kingdom. At the coronation ceremony, the previous king will hand over the ring to the next heir to the throne. Now that the ring is in your possession... It must have been him! His majesty! There is no other possibility.",
    ["Dialogue2061804"]="We have been led astray by the clues that were put in front of us, Adventurer. Now think about it... Those cargo boxes must have been used as a cover to mislead us, and the real king may have taken the deformation potion and turned into a member of the diplomatic corps... Gah, I'm so careless!\n(In a moment of frustration Bohr punches the wall with his fist)",
    ["Dialogue2061805"]="Yes... I can't understand his Majesty's reason for doing such a thing. He has clearly discovered your identity and successfully distracted the members of the diplomatic corps. Why wouldn’t he go directly back to Prontera with you? That night... did his majesty say anything else that night?",
    ["Dialogue2061806"]="Give... give this country to us?! So... So, your majesty, is he willing to....\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The future... The future of the Rune Kingdom....</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2061807"]="Whatever the truth of the matter is... Maybe, maybe we must accept this fact....\n(Bohr's voice begins to tremble)\nYour majesty, he... Has decided to hand over the throne to the other heirs.",
    ["Dialogue2061808"]="Adventurer... You and I can't let ourselves be distracted by the magnitude of this moment. I will immediately report this to the princess and start preparing for the throne’s election. After all... The kingdom cannot go on without a king.\nI am slightly worried that the successor election... May not go as smoothly as we expect it to.",
    ["Dialogue2061809"]="(Bohr rests his hands on your shoulder. They are trembling with excessive force. You can feel a heavy burden coming from him)\nThe king... Still needs your help, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2061901"]="(scattered, out of order shoe prints dispersed all over on the ground. It's hard to tell the direction the regiment was heading...)",
    ["Dialogue2062001"]="Have you not heard...? The desert isn’t a very peaceful place these days! Many people say that during the night of the first quarter moon, there are a lot of <color=#CA2E0AFF>giant mummies</color> wandering around the pyramids!",
    ["Dialogue2062101"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Giant mummies</color>? That can’t be... Are you sure you’re not still dreaming and haven't woken up yet?",
    ["Dialogue2062201"]="Yes, it's true! Local people say that the Pharoah is raising the undead to haunt our world and lead his legion to punish us blasphemous human beings! Quite... A lot of <color=#CA2E0AFF>poachers</color> have already been attacked!",
    ["Dialogue2062301"]="All right! What are you talking about! Put your backs in to it! If the boss comes back and you’re not done, you'll be in real trouble!",
    ["Dialogue2062401"]="(a large number of oddly shaped reagent bottles are stacked disorderly in the box. Velvet and satin padding lines the walls of the box to prevent them from braking. There is a familiar pungent smell coming from the box... Could it be the ingredients for making deformation potion?)",
    ["Dialogue2062501"]="(the air dried pickled food gives off an enticing aroma. You can't help but rub your hungry stomach...)",
    ["Dialogue2062601"]="(there is a large copper lock on the box. You can't open it. After observing the box for a week, a piece of paper squashed in the corner of the box catches your eye...)",
    ["Dialogue2062701"]="(a stone falls to the ground. You touch the bruise on the back of your head, checking that is it the masterpiece...)",
    ["Dialogue2062801"]="(some scrolls of books with religious symbols are lying at the bottom of the box. You turn them over and find that you don't recognize the language...)",
    ["Dialogue2062901"]="(after opening the box, you are almost blinded by the dazzling reflection of gold coins...)",
    ["Dialogue2063001"]="(... It's an empty box. If you check it carefully, you might find some scraps of grass left at the bottom...)",
    ["Dialogue2063101"]="(the clutter is piled up in a mess, and there seems to be no system in place to sort them. The handwriting on the note squashed in the corner of the box seems a little familiar...)",
    ["Dialogue2063201"]="... remember, young man. Before leaving the Rune Kingdom, the last city the dipomatic corps must pass through is Morroc, which is the territory of the Lugenburg family. You can ask them for help. Perhaps even ask them to host a banquet for the diplomatic corps in the residence and when they are suitably inebriated, we can take our opportunity... This is our last chance.",
    ["Dialogue2063301"]="... in addition, growing in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color> there is some <color=#CA2E0AFF>youmenglan</color>, I have my own use for it.",
    ["Dialogue2063401"]="..... after that, please go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast of Morroc</color>, there is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pond</color>, wait for me there. If the plan succeeds, I'll wait for an opportunity to meet you while they're drinking at the Lugenburg house.",
    ["Dialogue2070101"]="I've made up my mind. Save your breath, Speeka.",
    ["Dialogue2070102"]="Mother! We're talking about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>candidates of the throne</color>! Aren't Cecilia or I a more ideal choice than Erich not of royal blood?",
    ["Dialogue2070103"]="The letter from Queen Katherine is clear. All family heads shall put forward capable ones from their lineages as candidates of the throne and send them to Prontera to participate in the selection process. Speeka, do you understand now? We're choosing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>capable</color> rather than royal blood.",
    ["Dialogue2070104"]="Y-You mean... <size=26>Erich is better than me?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2070105"]="Calm down, Speeka! That's not what Mother is saying... Gosh... Oh, perfect timing, Adventurer! Come talk some sense into Speeka!",
    ["Dialogue2070106"]="You know, the selection process for the candidates of the throne is about to begin, right? Before the selection officially begins, all Seven Royal Families must send their chosen candidates to Prontera for the selection. Mother chose Erich, but Speeka...",
    ["Dialogue2070107"]="Fighting...? No. There's nothing to discuss and fight on this matter. I am the only one who decides who gets to be the successor of the Nerius Family.",
    ["Dialogue2070108"]="I think you two should stay on Comodo to take over Comodo as its leader. You are raised on this island, and it's the Nerius family's responsibility to offer its people security and prosperity. Erich has traveled the land for years. He has a better grasp of the world than you and is a better fighter. In that sense, he is more suitable to safeguard the kingdom than you.",
    ["Dialogue2070109"]="More suitable to safeguard the kingdom... than me?\n(Speeka suddenly makes a fist. She grinds her teeth and snickers.)\nFine. We shall see who really is more suitable!",
    ["Dialogue2070110"]="What are you doing? Speeka, stop this nonsense! It's not⁠—",
    ["Dialogue2070111"]="I am going to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the Sword of the Valiant from the depths of the dragons' cave</color>, Mother.\nI'm sure you remember that legendary sword symbolizes ultimate power and is guarded by the ancient dragons and monsters. If I managed to retrieve it... then you must admit that I am better than Erich, and that I shall be selected as the candidate of the throne instead.",
    ["Dialogue2070112"]="How arrogant of you, Speeka!",
    ["Dialogue2070113"]="It's only arrogance if I was without strength! I shall prove to you that... I AM a warrior that can protect the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue2070201"]="I'm sorry, Adventurer. I have a personal favor to ask...",
    ["Dialogue2070202"]="Yes... There's something you should know. The Ancient Dragon Speeka spoke of is located deep inside the dragon caves on Comodo. It's not only far away, but is patrolled by powerful monsters. Even though that great dragon was held captive by the Sword of Valiant's power, it can still use Dragon Flame to control surrounding monsters. Many have attempted to retrieve the sword, and none of returned.",
    ["Dialogue2070203"]="Some blinded by arrogance and ego also underestimated the dragon's power because it cannot move... and lost their lives. It is too dangerous for Speeka to go on such a journey alone.",
    ["Dialogue2070204"]="No, not me. I know my sister well. Once she's made up her mind, there's no changing it. If I offer my help, she'd take it as me belittling her like Mother... That's why I can only ask you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take care of her</color>... under the guise of her <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness</color>, not a helper.",
    ["Dialogue2070205"]="(The young maiden wraps her hair around her fingers, feeling embarrassed and helpless.)\nYou ARE a legendary Adventurer. If you offer to stand witness to her retrieving the sword from the caves, I'm sure she'd gladly accept.",
    ["Dialogue2070301"]="Those Megalodons are mine! Adventurer, stand aside!",
    ["Dialogue2070302"]="Cecilia? What's she got you doing here? C-could it be she thinks I'm incapable of taking out of the Sword of Valiant alone—and thinks I need your help?!\n(The young lady's brows furrow angrily, leaving you in no doubt she is on the cusp of an angry outburst. You hurriedly get on with the plan and attempt to console her.)",
    ["Dialogue2070303"]="A... witness? That isn't... so bad! My my, how considerate of Cecilia indeed!\nAbsolutely. I do need a witness to testify to the fact that I alone am truly capable of removing the Sword of Valiant from its place. A successor of Odin's Bloodline as you are, your witness will be more than enough even for someone like my mother... Truthfully, I can think of no better candidate!",
    ["Dialogue2070304"]="(The young lady smiles blissfully as she gives you a forceful pat on the shoulders.)\nThen it's settled! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, oh Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2070401"]="...It looks like we're here already, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2070402"]="You see this great dragon? How long it's been pinned here by the Sword of Valiant, and how long its physique has withered and wilted! I should think it rather easy to remove the sword under these conditions.",
    ["Dialogue2070403"]="You don't have to stress about such things, my dear Adventurer. This poor dragon hasn't had a chance to use its vaunted Dragon Flame in eons, and I trust the nearby Golems have suffered the same fate. Over there would be a great vantage point for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness the heroic moment I take the Sword of Valiant for myself</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2070501"]="Barbara...?\n<color=#A1979FFF>That's weird... I feel like I've heard that name before.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2070502"]="...I'm not sure. But I think it was murmuring a name—Barbara—when I approached. Adventurer, don't you think that's a bit strange? You know, ever since Lady Margaret signed the Peace Treaty of Comodo with the dragons, our dealings with them have been few and far between. I wonder what sort of person it was that could instill itself so thoroughly into the mind of an Ancient Dragon?",
    ["Dialogue2070503"]="...This Barbara and the dragon may go way back... then does it somehow represent the key to plucking out the Sword of Valiant? Adventurer... how about we return to the island and look into a person by the name of Barbara before we do anything rash?",
    ["Dialogue2070504"]="Alright. Let's go now! And stay close!",
    ["Dialogue2070505"]="Huh? Don't you have an unfinished quest in that dragons' cave? Alright... But don't make me wait long. Let's be quick about it!",
    ["Dialogue2070601"]="Alright everybody—stick to your routines! And be careful of your safety! Everyone has one, so don't scramble!",
    ["Dialogue2070602"]="Barbara... Barbara! my goddess in the flesh!",
    ["Dialogue2070603"]="What... What is going on? Has everyone suddenly gone nuts?",
    ["Dialogue2070604"]="You really don't know? Barbara is the most popular dancer these days! She's a graduate of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Euphonic Symphony</color> and a star student of the prior chief! She's been honing her skills for years abroad and just returned! I'm sure Master Callahan will soon feel fit to hand over the reins of the Euphonic Symphony to her!",
    ["Dialogue2070605"]="Yes! Barbara's not only renowned for her bewitching looks and curves... but also for her varied dancing, just like ocean waves. No one can take their eyes off her!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Ah... I get light-headed thinking about it...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2070606"]="Attention, everyone!\nTonight's the night the great Barbara shall be presenting her <color=#CA2E0AFF>premiere</color> on Comodo at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Beach</color>! This is a night that you do not want to miss!",
    ["Dialogue2070607"]="Oh no! Better line up now for the front row!",
    ["Dialogue2070608"]="Hey... W-Wait for me!\nWhat are you doing, you two, just standing there? Hurry up to the front row like us! Or else you could only catch sight of other people's hairstyles!",
    ["Dialogue2070701"]="...Um?\n(Somehow the attention of the blonde dancer falls upon you despite the throng of excited people. There's a flash of surprise in her eyes and she quickens her pace in your direction.)\nAre you... Princess Speeka?",
    ["Dialogue2070702"]="Uh... Do I know you?",
    ["Dialogue2070703"]="Nobility has a way of attracting attention, no matter where they are.\n...Are you coming to watch the performance, milady? It would be a tremendous honor! Was my dancing pleasing to you, your worshipfulness?",
    ["Dialogue2070704"]="(Speeka frowns, seemingly a little uncomfortable with that flattering attitude.)\nI believe that such a most popular performance must have its merits.",
    ["Dialogue2070705"]="That would be most wonderful!\nI heard that the coronation ceremony of the Crown Prince Elect will be very soon. Nerius Family has been invited, right? If only I had a chance to perform at the Royal Banquet, then surely I would contribute to Comodo by...",
    ["Dialogue2070706"]="(Speeka cuts Barbara off at this junction, seemingly mad at this nosy dancer.)\nMiss Barbara... It's not your place to pry, and I'm not here to see your dancing. Let me be blunt. Are you familiar with an Ancient Dragon that dwells deep within a cave on Comodo?",
    ["Dialogue2070707"]="A-a dragon? Your worshipfulness! You jest, surely! Hasn't that dragons' cave been forbidden to people since the war a millennia ago? B-Besides, I am but a dancer. How could I cause serious injury to a dragon despite the defense of monsters?",
    ["Dialogue2070708"]="Miss Barbara, I don't think I ever mentioned it is a severely injured dragon pinned by the Sword of Valiant. You tried so hard to cover that up but flubbed.",
    ["Dialogue2070709"]="A-anyway! I never went into the cave! I-I have no idea what you're talking about! I'm sorry... I'm very tired from today's performance. I really should get some rest. Excuse me.",
    ["Dialogue2070801"]="Did you see that, Adventurer? She's lying! She knows something about that dragon—or at least more than she's willing to admit!",
    ["Dialogue2070802"]="Indeed! She was so effusive at the start, but as soon as she heard any mention of a dragon, it was like flicking a switch. There is something going on there.",
    ["Dialogue2070803"]="...You mean, we should find a way to probe the connection between her and this dragon?",
    ["Dialogue2070804"]="Since Barbara isn't willing, for whatever reason, to come clean with us, maybe our best shot is just to go straight to that dragon... What about us giving the dragon something that proves our acquaintance with Barbara? Maybe we could win its trust that way?",
    ["Dialogue2070805"]="Um... I heard that the monsters are particularly sensitive to the auras of human beings. What if we tried to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>personal belongings</color> of Barbara to test the dragon?",
    ["Dialogue2070806"]="Hey, don't say that! It's not stealing if it's part of working a case! Let's just say we're temporarily borrowing it!",
    ["Dialogue2070807"]="You know the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Galapagos</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Saint Darmain East</color>? This is exactly the kind of thing that they specialize in. Just get them to have a look at a <color=#CA2E0AFF>picture of Barbara</color>, and then buy them a pint of the local's <color=#CA2E0AFF>finest beer</color>. I guarantee they'll agree to whatever you want in front of that sweet golden ale!",
    ["Dialogue2070808"]="Haha, I certainly... Ahem! B-By the way, remember to invent some story so you won't give too much away to Vendra when buying the alcohol! Or she might end up telling the whole thing to mother!\n(Speeka staggers back with a guilty face. While your gaze is averted, she runs off in the direction of the dragons' cave.)\nI-I'll go on ahead! Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>rendezvous at the dragons' cave</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2070901"]="Oh! Look who's here—the most legendary Adventurer on the continent!\nLet me guess from your expression... You're not here just for a fine pint, right?",
    ["Dialogue2070902"]="Huh? You won't buy a drink for me, but for those Galapagos?\n(Vendra gives you a suspicious look-over. Your unexpectedness has drawn her curiosity.)\nWhat game are you playing at, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2070903"]="What's the occasion for the funny business? Perhaps... it was Speeka that sent you here? What's she up to this time?\n(Vendra gives you a resentful stare as if unhappy with your response.)\nNo way. I won't sell you this pint if you are not straight with me!",
    ["Dialogue2070904"]="Huh? Are you really asking me about... what do I think of the relationship between the dragons and us humans? Oh... Well. That's a tough question.\nIn my opinion, personally, and I don't know if it's even politically correct to say so... but I've always felt that both sides, the dragons and we humans, have a right to live.",
    ["Dialogue2070905"]="Oh yes. I did urge Alexia to fight against the dragons. That was just to protect our homeland. Just imagine if we kept falling back...\n(Vendra raises her head to glance over at all the other patrons enjoying their drinks.)\n...Then the ones driven out of Comodo would have been these poor, hapless citizens.",
    ["Dialogue2070906"]="The dragons declared war for the sake of their own species' survival, while we resisted them to protect our homeland. We were both close to the edge of the precipice, and neither had room to move. It's not a question of right or wrong. We are the winning side exactly, but isn't it so ignorant of us... to simply define the dragons' deeds as evil?",
    ["Dialogue2070907"]="Ah, still remember that little event? Indeed. I often snuck into the dragons' cave when I was a little kid and actually came across a dragonling. It was remarkable but brief. I think that's why I, unlike many others, feel we still have room for understanding.",
    ["Dialogue2070908"]="Ideally, I hope we will see a day when dragons and humans can peacefully coexist on Comodo. That'd be wonderful...\n(So saying, Vendra slides a well-prepared pint of beer over your way.)\n...You know, I wonder if the dragons would like what we brew up here.",
    ["Dialogue2071001"]="Beer! Beer-bobo!\n(That bold biped! You really want to pick a fight with me?)",
    ["Dialogue2071002"]="Beeer?! Bobo! Beer-bobo! Beer!\n(Huh? Don't hit me! Not the face! We can talk about it!)",
    ["Dialogue2071003"]="Beer-bobo?\n(Isn't that the female biped who waggled at the beach days ago?)",
    ["Dialogue2071004"]="Beer—Beer-bobo—Beer!\n(Beer! Vendra's special! Give it to me!)",
    ["Dialogue2071005"]="Beer...? Bobo...? Beer-bobo! ♥\n(Huh? A trade for a beer? Alright! I'll handle it!)",
    ["Dialogue2071006"]="Beer! Bobo! Beer! Bobo!\n(See that <color=#CA2E0AFF>volcano</color>? In two hours! We make a delivery there! Deal!)",
    ["Dialogue2071101"]="You took your time getting here!\n(Almost getting bashed, Speeka staggers to dodge the attack from a Golem. Seeing this, you hurry to her.)",
    ["Dialogue2071102"]="No, no! Don't, Adventurer!\nWhere's that dancer's stuff? Take it out and see if the Golems have any reaction!",
    ["Dialogue2071103"]="...Look! Isn't that what your master was seeking?\n(Speeka takes the handkerchief and waves it vigorously. You hesitate inwardly for a moment, mentally preparing yourself for a very ugly confrontation. Instead, a sense of peacefulness descends upon the Golems.)",
    ["Dialogue2071104"]="Shh... You should be more careful, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walk between the monsters.</color> Don't frighten them.",
    ["Dialogue2071201"]="They recognized Barbara's aura!\nIt was only when I first arrived here that I realized the dragon was only manipulating the monsters to drive me out, not deliver a lethal blow. I guess even dragons feel a little bad about killing humans...",
    ["Dialogue2071202"]="And now I realize it was actually waiting for Barbara... The Golems let up on us for fear of hurting Barbara by mistake!\nAdventurer, it's time for us to go up to that <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>show it this handkerchief</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2071301"]="(Speeka bends over and carefully places the handkerchief in front of the dragon.)\nWere you... looking for this?",
    ["Dialogue2071302"]="...\n(The creeping dragon wearily opens its eyes, extends a claw, daintily picks up the handkerchief, and sighs faintly.)",
    ["Dialogue2071303"]="Yikes... Is there a signature on this <color=#CA2E0AFF>handkerchief</color>?! And that signature on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sword</color>... Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a look at this</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2071401"]="Exactly the same! Ha! I knew she was lying, I knew it!",
    ["Dialogue2071402"]="No... Even if the symbol of a rose shows the sword belongs to or is associated somehow with Barbara... then why the dragon doesn't seem hostile to her if she is the one that pin it here? You know, it was Barbara's handkerchief that actually gave us safe passage!",
    ["Dialogue2071403"]="Adventurer, there's something really strange behind all this. And I'm going to figure it out before I take this sword away! We should get back and look for other clues as to what's going on!",
    ["Dialogue2071501"]="Let's sort out the clues we have before us. First of all, we know at least that there's some kind of strange, deep relationship between Barbara and this dragon. At least we have proof that her <color=#CA2E0AFF>handkerchief and sword bear the same signature</color>! But for reasons unknown she appears to conceal this fact.",
    ["Dialogue2071502"]="Besides... remember what those fans were saying? They said something about Barbara being a graduate of the Euphonic Symphony, and that she was a student of the prior chief. She could have forged a career in the troupe. Why leave? And why would she suddenly return to Comodo after all these years?",
    ["Dialogue2071503"]="Ah-ha! Some other members of the Euphonic Symphony may know something we don't! Let's go to their <color=#CA2E0AFF>camp</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out more about Barbara from them</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2071601"]="Hum hum hum ♪\n(A lady sings happily as she dances to and fro while watering flowers, casting faint rainbows off the falling droplets.)\nHello? And who might you be...?",
    ["Dialogue2071602"]="Greetings, my beautiful lady! Could we have the pleasure of talking to you for a moment?",
    ["Dialogue2071603"]="(Speeka's flowery language seems enough to amuse the girl. She covers her mouth for a brief giggle.)\nI'd like to talk to you! What a shame I haven't finished watering the plants yet. Twilight Florals can only be watered with water from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>hot springs</color> in the very heat of the day. We've passed midday, so if I were to talk to you then...",
    ["Dialogue2071604"]="...Oh. Well that case, could you please get some more water from our <color=#CA2E0AFF>camp</color> and come put it on the flowers? I'd be very happy to chat with you afterward.",
    ["Dialogue2071605"]="Deal!",
    ["Dialogue2071701"]="Alright then. Now I've got time to really talk to you. Go on. What did you want to ask about? Don't tell me it's about Barbara...",
    ["Dialogue2071702"]="H-How did you guess?",
    ["Dialogue2071703"]="I'm right? Of course I'm right. Fans, yeah?",
    ["Dialogue2071704"]="(Speeka gives you a sharp kick before you have a chance to finish the sentence. You stop talking as Speeka gives you another piercing look.)\n....Right, right! We're like her biggest fans! Oh... I heard she was a member of the Euphonic Symphony, wasn't she? You must know her really well then, right?",
    ["Dialogue2071705"]="...So many fans recently come to ask about Barbara. You would've heard she learned under Master Doreen... and will probably take over the troupe soon?",
    ["Dialogue2071706"]="(Speeka once again angrily jabs you with her foot while providing a whispered explanation in your ear.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>...Shush! Don't mess it up for me, Adventurer! Doreen is Vendra's mother! And the previous chief of the Euphonic Symphony!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2071707"]="It makes sense you would think that... she's a dancer of the Euphonic Symphony through and through, and Master Doreen has taught her well. But, you know, she actually spent a number of years alone away from Comodo. Because... at that time Barbara was actually considered the <color=#CA2E0AFF>least talented</color> of all of Doreen's students!",
    ["Dialogue2071708"]="What? How's that?",
    ["Dialogue2071709"]="I know, right? No one in the troupe can believe it. Look at how she's dancing today. Well, I can say it's almost like she is completely a different person. She must have really practiced in those intervening years, huh? Some people even started a rumor... She found the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dance of All Dances</color> so she could be what she is today.",
    ["Dialogue2071710"]="\"Dance of All Dances\"?\nYou don't mean the performance by Lady Margaret on the altar when she defeated The Demon King Morroc? But I thought that book should have been lost to time...",
    ["Dialogue2071711"]="Right. No one knows where it got to or if it even still exists. But anyhow, there was a rumor around ten years ago the <color=#CA2E0AFF>book had been squirreled away into some dragons' cave</color> or something... Um, it reminds me that Barbara always screamed for <color=#CA2E0AFF>finding that book in the dragons' cave</color> every time she had a problem in dance classes!",
    ["Dialogue2071712"]="Wow. Look at your expression. It seems like you almost believe it?\n(The young lady gives another giggle. Clearly, your overly serious faces must be somehow very fascinating.)\nHow is that even possible? It's all gossip. Come on.",
    ["Dialogue2071713"]="Alright. That was a great chat, but I really should be getting back to it. Anyway, you two shouldn't waste too much time here. Barbara's big performance is tonight, isn't it? You'd better get there in time to see your goddess, hey?",
    ["Dialogue2071801"]="I had... clearly... almost finished it! Darnit!",
    ["Dialogue2071802"]="Don't talk to me! Adventurer! My tent has been ravaged again by those cursed mobsters from the forest! And this time... this time they've made off with my prized poems!\n(The young bard stomps his feet angrily to the faint rustling of leaves on the ground.)\n<size=23>Unforgivable...</size> <size=26>Absolutely unforgivable!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2071803"]="...Hey, Adventurer, he seems a little peeved. Maybe we'd better not aggravate him?\n(Speeka quietly pulls you back by the corner of your outfit and away from the bard, who seems in the process of a mental breakdown.)",
    ["Dialogue2071804"]="You mean... we do him a favor by finding his lost poems, so he'll tell us about Barbara?\nOh. Makes sense. But where are we going to find his lost poems?",
    ["Dialogue2071805"]="Right! He was just saying \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>mobsters from the forest</color>\" stole his poems! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>earth</color> over there is pretty wet. Anyone would leave lots of <color=#CA2E0AFF>tracks</color> going past. All we need is to take a careful look and I'm sure we're gonna find something! You're brilliant, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2071901"]="You... Are you holding... Could it be?",
    ["Dialogue2071902"]="Thank you so much, you two!\n<color=#A1979FFF>This means I'll be able to finish my song before the ceremony... but I'm not sure whether she'll like it though...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2071903"]="...Can we ask you about something?\n(Warren looks at you with a piercing, guarded expression as he takes his poems from your hand.)\nWhat do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue2071904"]="...Could you tell us a bit about Barbara? I heard she was a dancer in the Euphonic Symphony. You must know her, right?",
    ["Dialogue2071905"]="Barbara...?\n(The young bard seems to heave a sigh of relief, but then his expression quickly narrows again in a kind of pained disgust.)\nDon't tell me... you are her fans?",
    ["Dialogue2071906"]="The greater her popularity, the less impressive her fans. Are her <color=#CA2E0AFF>soulless dances</color> really worth your time and attention?",
    ["Dialogue2071907"]="Of course, it's all spectacle to the average person. You people are blown away by artsy moves. But she seems stiff as a puppet to an artist like me. Our great Doreen once said, \"No two dancers are ever quite alike.\" The same moves, yes, but a different interpretation for each individual. But Barbara? Nope. She just copies and copies and copies.",
    ["Dialogue2071908"]="...If you ask me, Vendra was always the best of Doreen's students. I got to see them side by side, but actually we are talking about the best student next to the worst! Barbara never had a chance to win. In the end, she started <color=#CA2E0AFF>mimicking Vendra's</color> every move, partially out of envy. Now they tell me this lady's the best dancer in the whole world? Ha. The gods sure do have a sense of humor!",
    ["Dialogue2071909"]="Alright, alright... enough. I have nothing to share with people like you who have no appreciation for real art! You gotta go. Don't distract me while I'm trying to compose something important!\n(He waves his hands as if to shoo you away, forcing Speeka back a few steps. She's not happy.)",
    ["Dialogue2071910"]="Alright, alright... Looks like we didn't find out anything useful. We don't want any trouble, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2072001"]="...Oh, are you looking for Master Callahan? I'm afraid he left first thing this morning to check on the strings in Drying Square. He hasn't come back yet...",
    ["Dialogue2072002"]="It's an open area around the south side of the forest. Sheep's guts can't be transformed into strings right away. You need to sun 'em for a bit. It's complicated work, so every now and then Callahan checks on it personally...",
    ["Dialogue2072003"]="But, I think normally he'd be back long before now... <color=#A1979FFF>Oh dear, I hope he hasn't run into any trouble?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2072004"]="You will? Oh, that'd be great!\n(She gives a faint bow in your direction.)\nIf you do find Master Callahan, then can you please tell him to come back as soon as possible? We're actually getting a bit worried.",
    ["Dialogue2072101"]="(Cough) Isn't that Princess Speeka? And the Adventurer... Thank you for being so helpful!\nBut, I must say, I don't think it's merely coincidence that has brought you to me, right?",
    ["Dialogue2072102"]="(Speeka restrains her normally impertinent self and bows at the elderly gentleman.)\nI'm very pleased to see you again after so long, Uncle Callahan. To tell you the truth, we're here specifically to ask you a few things.",
    ["Dialogue2072103"]="Oh, right. You really want to ask something of an old man like me? Must be a matter of ancient history.",
    ["Dialogue2072104"]="You're really sharp, Uncle. I won't beat around the bush. It concerns Barbara, our dance sensation. I heard she used to be a member of the Euphonic Symphony and trained under Doreen. What I want to know is... did she ever gain entry to a dragons' cave and locate Lady Margaret's famous record of the \"Dance of All Dances\"?",
    ["Dialogue2072105"]="Well... you may be young for your years, my princess, but you have authority all your own. Yet I'm tempted to ask you a question in return while we're at it... Are you here in some capacity as an heir of Nerius family to probe to it... Or is it simply a personal matter?",
    ["Dialogue2072106"]="(Speeka hesitates for a moment in the face of Callahan's piercing question. She purses her lips before showing an expression of compromise.)\n...It's personal. None of what we discuss today will reach my mother's ears, I assure you.",
    ["Dialogue2072107"]="Very well. Then I trust we shall have a free and easy conversation.\n(The elderly bard nods with a kindly pat on Speeka's head.)\n...You have guessed correctly. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Barbara really did gain access to a dragons' cave</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>ten years ago</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2072108"]="I remember she hired bounty hunters to guard her into the cave and frozen waterfall within. I don't know why, but in the end she was the only one who made it back to the camp, badly injured. She said everyone was <color=#CA2E0AFF>slaughtered by merciless monsters</color>. She begged me to keep it a secret and I, for Doreen's sake, agreed.",
    ["Dialogue2072109"]="I remember asking Barbara why she wanted to go to the dragons' cave so badly. She never told me why. In fact, my queries might have contributed to her decision to leave Comodo as soon as she recovered. I tried to convince her but in the end found myself sending her to a merchant ship bound for Morroc. I've lost track of Barbara since then, until her recent arrival. And that was when we found out she's become a dance sensation on the continent.",
    ["Dialogue2072110"]="Uh-huh. And what do you think about all this—her sudden return? Are you worried something strange is going on behind it? Uncle Callahan, there are already rumors she's next in line to manage the Euphonic Symphony. Also, when I met her on the beach recently, she even wanted me to take her to Prontera and the Royal Banquet! I think she's got pretty big ambitions!",
    ["Dialogue2072111"]="These facts are known to me. Come to think of it, Barbara has always struck me as a rather ambitious person, even as a child. That's why it was such a shame when even Doreen couldn't make something of her in those early days. So if she really did choose to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go for broke</color> and try to find this lost legendary book, then I guess it wouldn't be entirely surprising.",
    ["Dialogue2072112"]="But whatever you might say about her, the fact remains that Barbara was one of Doreen's most beloved students. I never hope to see her go astray because of one false move. As for that legendary book... Blessed by the predecessors, the Euphonic Symphony persists long, and it has mostly depended on the hard work of its successors. I don't think it matters too much... whether <color=#CA2E0AFF>such a book even really exists</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2072113"]="(Something in Callahan's words seems to heighten Speeka's concerns, but you dare not interrupt. You simply wait for her to respond.)\n...I understand, Uncle Callahan. Thank you for your comprehensive, very honest answer. If anything remains to be done about this matter, I and my Adventurer friend will look into it. Now it's getting late. Please head back to the camp soon as your students must be worried about you.",
    ["Dialogue2072114"]="Thank you, my liege. In that case... farewell. I hope it goes well with you.",
    ["Dialogue2072201"]="Alright then. That took a bit of time, but I wouldn't say we returned empty-handed. The picture I'm building from other troupe members and Uncle Callahan is Barbara really was a member of the Euphonic Symphony and a student of Doreen. Yet also talentless, she envied her outstanding fellow student Vendra and even mimicked Vendra's manners...",
    ["Dialogue2072202"]="Also, she really did hire bounty hunters to help her enter the dragons' cave ten years ago, and was the sole survivor. In the aftermath, she didn't breathe a word of it to anyone, even pleaded with Uncle Callahan to keep it secret, and then hurried away from Comodo... Don't you think that's a bit weird, Adventurer? It seems like she's <color=#CA2E0AFF>really scared of someone knowing what happened at the cave</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2072203"]="Yeah. I think we've found a breakthrough in the case. There's one other thing...\n<color=#A1979FFF>And if I can find that item, everything will be all settled...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2072204"]="Great! It's decided! We'll split up for this one, Adventurer!\nYou <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and confront Barbara</color>. Create a distraction to buy me enough time to confirm the other piece of evidence I need. If she comes clean about the whole thing, that's great. But if she doesn't... Huh! We'll see what I can do about that!",
    ["Dialogue2072301"]="Don't tell me it's you again? I already told you... I <color=#CA2E0AFF>never went into any dragons' cave</color>! I can't understand a word you say! Stop bothering me!\n(Barbara vehemently refuses to admit involvement. You ruffle through your mind for evidence to confront her with.)",
    ["Dialogue2072302"]="He... He told you about that, didn't he? Tsk... I admit I was a little <color=#CA2E0AFF>curious</color>, and I did hire some bounty hunters to help me explore the cave. I just never thought we'd actually be attacked by monsters! And no one else survived... I was just a kid then. I thought the authorities were going to come after me. So the only choice I had was to conceal it and leave Comodo...",
    ["Dialogue2072303"]="Right, right! I'm a dancer, right? Why shouldn't I be interested in the legendary \"Dance of All Dances\"? And if people say the lost book is located in dragons' cave, why shouldn't I look for it? <color=#CA2E0AFF>But I didn't find any trace of any dragons in the cave</color>. OK? Now stop bothering me!",
    ["Dialogue2072304"]="What the... Did you steal my handkerchief? Adventurer! I never thought you'd stoop so low!\nYeah! I know the dragon you're talking about! Because it tried to kill me! And why else would I want to hurt it... if not to save my own skin?",
    ["Dialogue2072305"]="(Barbara grimaces in disgust at your words.)\nI've got no idea what you're talking about. But since you don't have any evidence for what you're saying, I don't see why I should waste any more time talking to you. Just go!",
    ["Dialogue2072306"]="I guess if you've gotten this far, there's no point in me hiding it any longer.\nI used to sneak away to that dragons' cave as a kid. I loved playing there. One day, I found an injured dragonling. I helped it... so we become friends. We played together, grew up together, and even told each other our secrets.",
    ["Dialogue2072307"]="One day I told her it was my dream to perform Margaret's \"Dance of all Dances\"... It said it was going to do all it could to help me achieve my dream... and so we made a pact. But it was a trick. I should never have trusted any dragon!",
    ["Dialogue2072308"]="The dragon had it in for me. It told me that Margaret's book is found by a frozen waterfall and asked me to bring some people along. I did as instructed... Those poor hunters were just trying to protect me as we entered the cave. How was I to know a whole bunch of demons was waiting for us!? And I think I would have died too... if I hadn't driven my sword right into its chest by surprise!",
    ["Dialogue2072309"]="And what happened to the book? Ha... There's no such thing. It's just a hoax. And I never saw it—",
    ["Dialogue2072310"]="<size=26>The lies end here, Barbara!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2072401"]="You're even better at weaving fairy tales than you are at dancing. Have you ever considered a career as a bard?\n(Speeka teasingly shoves an item in front of Barbara's nose.)",
    ["Dialogue2072402"]="You never saw the legendary book, did you? Then explain this—how come I found this in your luggage?",
    ["Dialogue2072501"]="I just couldn't figure it out. Your classmates call you <color=#CA2E0AFF>talentless</color>, that you had to mimic Vendra's every move to graduate. You still have an ex-colleague who described your dancing as \"soulless.\" They say you don't know how to express yourself, that you just \"copy and copy\". But the question is, which book did you copy exactly?",
    ["Dialogue2072502"]="The answer is... Margaret's \"Dance of All Dances\"!\nThe thing is, you managed to learn the moves, but could never figure out how to express the soul within. Yet the Margaret's dance itself is so rarely sublime that your simple mimicries could finagle your way into a most popular dancer on the continent!",
    ["Dialogue2072503"]="Nonsense... nonsense! You don't have a shred of evidence!\nSo what if I carry a book around with me with \"Dance of All Dances\" on the cover? Does that prove it's Margaret's dance?",
    ["Dialogue2072504"]="So you still won't admit it? You know the book is real. But if you need further convincing, well then... Some pages of this book have been stained with water. I found Eden Group to confirm it with me, and they told me... the water on these pages carries unique magical waves, which can be only found in one place across Comodo.",
    ["Dialogue2072505"]="That's right, Adventurer! The ice and snow in the dragons' cave! So the legend was true—Margaret's \"Dance of All Dances\" really was concealed within the frozen waterfall of the cave, and ten years ago... you secretly located and kept that legendary book!",
    ["Dialogue2072506"]="No... That's not true... No way! I, I don't...\n(Barbara steps backward in fright, then suddenly spins around and runs off.)",
    ["Dialogue2072507"]="Stop!",
    ["Dialogue2072601"]="Why? Why? What do you gain from digging up the past? H-has someone hired you to hurt me?",
    ["Dialogue2072602"]="Hurt you? What would I gain from hurting you? I just want to know the truth—I want to know what happened all those years ago!",
    ["Dialogue2072603"]="I-I'll tell you! But you must promise to keep it secret!",
    ["Dialogue2072604"]="Miss Barbara, a deal implies an exchange of value between equal parties. But you have nothing. I have all the evidence which convinces me you hired a bunch of bounty hunters in search of Margaret's legendary \"Dance of All Dances.\" But when it comes to the question of how you alone left the cave alive...",
    ["Dialogue2072605"]="(Speeka drawled on purpose and emphatically adjusted her dress before continuing in the face of the already trembling Barbara.)\n...Our famous dancer Barbara killed every one of those bounty hunters in cold blood to keep her discovery of the book a secret. Are you happy with that as your \"cover story\"?",
    ["Dialogue2072606"]="It wasn't me!<size=23> It wasn't me!</size> They did it to themselves! <size=26>They betrayed me!</size>\n(It is at this point the dancer's determination finally breaks. She screams at you both like a cornered animal.)",
    ["Dialogue2072607"]="They got greedy when realizing I had the book! I paid good money so I could go there safely. We'd agreed I'd only give them the full amount once we got back! But they turned on me after finding that legendary book, saying it's worth much more than me... They desired to steal it anyway!",
    ["Dialogue2072608"]="So you had them all killed? Barbara, how could you...",
    ["Dialogue2072609"]="Do you really think I could have managed that? The dragon did it—and it killed them only because they were planning to hurt me!",
    ["Dialogue2072610"]="But if it saved you... how could you turn around and betray it? Your signature is clearly on the sword pinning the dragon to the cave!",
    ["Dialogue2072611"]="It doesn't matter whether you believe me or not. I'm telling you—I never hurt it.\n(Barbara covers her head in her hands. You can't see her face, but her sobs don't give you much doubt she is feeling very sorry for herself.)",
    ["Dialogue2072612"]="The bounty hunters quickly realized they were no match for the dragon, and wanted to take me down with them... They took me hostage with my own sword... which plunged into the dragon when it tried to save me...",
    ["Dialogue2072613"]="Yes, but I didn't save it. I couldn't. I was terrified. I just got the heck out of there with my precious book while they were busy fighting each other. It was only later I realized the book had been cut in half during the fight. I was too scared to go back... And I've been having nightmares about it ever since... I didn't want to live under this shadow for the rest of my life, so I decided to leave... I think you know the rest.",
    ["Dialogue2072614"]="Ha, well-spoken. Despite several nightmares, you've achieved your ambition with that book at the cost of its freedom. You've made its life a living hell these years... How would you repay it?",
    ["Dialogue2072615"]="...Repay? Why should I?! Why else would it have stuck around all these years if not to get back at me? Princess Speeka, you know it's a dragon! It's a demonic creature and a sworn enemy of all human beings! Don't tell me you're going to take the side of a demon over one of your own kind? You have no right to judge me—even as the heir of Nerius family!",
    ["Dialogue2072616"]="Perhaps not, but I don't think anything you've said gives you the right to escape culpability for your actions.\n(Speeka grips Barbara by her wrist rather forcibly, as she speaks.)\n...Now is the time for you to pay for your sins in full!",
    ["Dialogue2072617"]="W-what are you doing? <size=23>Unhand me!</size> <size=26>Release me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2072701"]="Why are you doing this to me? Am... Am I not a citizen of Comodo? As an heir of Nerius Family, shouldn't you be trying to protect me? How could you send me to my death?",
    ["Dialogue2072702"]="Shut up! Just keep going!",
    ["Dialogue2072703"]="No... I don't want to... I-It must hate me... It's going to kill me on sight because I didn't come back to help it... <size=26>Save me, Adventurer!</size>\n(Barbara pleads with you instead, shaking visibly. She clearly doesn't want to take another step. At just this moment, you hear a deep sound from nearby that puts a stop to your argument.)",
    ["Dialogue2072704"]="B-Barbara... is that you...?",
    ["Dialogue2072801"]="Barbara... you've returned... at last...",
    ["Dialogue2072802"]="Over there. Come closer.\n(Speeka threatens Barbara in a low voice. She gives Barbara a solid push, who stumbles forward rather pathetically toward the dragon.)",
    ["Dialogue2072803"]="...You've grown, Barbara.\n(The dragon sighs deeply and reaches out with its front claws awkwardly. Its voice is rough and dim as if echoing a thousand times across the cavern walls.)\nNow... is the moment that I should...",
    ["Dialogue2072804"]="Phew! No, no... Please don't...!\n(Barbara tenses in horror at the moves of the dragon and tries to escape. Speeka prevents her from leaving.)",
    ["Dialogue2072805"]="Don't move! Look at it!",
    ["Dialogue2072806"]="I should return it to you... Barbara...\n(Finally the sickly dragon opens up its front claws. You see what looks like an ancient book underneath. It seems wrinkled but appears to be well-preserved.)\nYour... dream...",
    ["Dialogue2072807"]="Is this... the <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Dance of All Dances\"</color>?\n<color=#A1979FFF>That's not possible... There's no way!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2072808"]="You lost this book ten years ago, Barbara. To keep this half safe for you, it's been waiting here for you all these years.",
    ["Dialogue2072809"]="Dance... Barbara... Dance like we promised each other once upon a time... <color=#CA2E0AFF>dance the complete \"Dance of All Dances\"</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2072810"]="Do what it says, Barbara.\n(Speeka kneels down to pick up the other half of the book and stuffs it into Barbara's hands.)\nThis is what you're best at... \"Copy.\"",
    ["Dialogue2072811"]="I-I knew it! I'll do that! You... You <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay back</color>! Give me some time!",
    ["Dialogue2072901"]="What is this... <size=26>What is this?!</size>\n(Barbara grips the book for dear life as she gazes with terror upon the dragon's dying body, which grows colder and colder. Her voice crackles from all the emotion.)\nYou waited all these years in this horrible place just so that I could finish my dance?",
    ["Dialogue2072902"]="You all are... insane...! You really are! And so is it!<size=26> It was just a childhood joke!\nPeople make all kinds of promises... Who would take it so seriously?</size>",
    ["Dialogue2072903"]="...Shut up! What right do you have to criticize me? It found the whole book for me, so I gave it the complete dance. If this was our deal, didn't we each fulfill our sides? And what is wrong with you two? Why do you insist on sticking your nose into my business?",
    ["Dialogue2072904"]="(Barbara stares at you and Speeka with a hunted expression as she takes a couple of steps back and jams the book into a pocket.)\nDon't... don't tell me that... you also want this book for yourself?!",
    ["Dialogue2072905"]="Huh! I wish I could show your many fans exactly what their idol is doing right now.\n(Speeka laughs coldly as she gazes contemptuously at Barbara.)",
    ["Dialogue2072906"]="To tell you the truth, the book is a priceless artifact, but not priceless enough to tempt my dignity. Take your precious book and get lost. I don't want to see your face around the territory of Nerius family from this day forth, Barbara.",
    ["Dialogue2072907"]="...You got your wish. Don't worry, you'll never see me again.\n(Barbara turns around to go. Her eyes linger for a moment on her childhood dragon friend's body. She hesitates briefly, but still chooses to put herself first.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>You fool... I hope you make better friends in your next life.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2073001"]="...\n(The interior of the cave once again turns quiet as Barbara's retreating footsteps grow fainter. You and Speeka both seem to carry an unspoken heaviness in your hearts.)",
    ["Dialogue2073002"]="Let it go, Adventurer... This burden will dog her for the rest of her life. She will certainly take this secret to her grave if she still wants to go places.",
    ["Dialogue2073003"]="I made a promise to Uncle Callahan, and a promise is a promise. And anyway, what good is the book to someone like her? She's never going to be a worthy successor to Lady Margaret.",
    ["Dialogue2073004"]="(Speeka approaches the dragon and traces her forefinger across the edges of the blade. Her reflection shines brightly in the metal.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>This book... was a two-edged sword...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2073005"]="...That's alright, Adventurer. And I've made my decision—I'm going to stay in Comodo.\nI think I understand what my mother was trying to tell me. It's not that she thought lightly of my abilities, but that... here I am always looking up at the stars when my mother would much rather have me plant my feet firmly on the ground... and she's right.",
    ["Dialogue2073006"]="To most, Comodo is like a little slice of heaven for the performing arts. We have wonderful musical sessions by night, and endless fun-filled activities by day. But does the sunshine really touch every corner of this beautiful island? Dragons and humans live in their own little worlds, having nothing to do with each other for fear and prejudice... and I include myself in that.",
    ["Dialogue2073007"]="<color=#A1979FFF>That's the story playing out right across this island every minute of every day, whether we're aware of it or not...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2073008"]="(Speeka kneels down to scoop up a handful of snow. She places it next to the dragon like a little burial mound.)\nI tell you, Adventurer, that this is the first life I have ever laid to rest... and I'm sure it will not be the last. But I promise you that I'll do my best from today onward.",
    ["Dialogue2073009"]="Alright then. That's a deal.\n(Speeka smiles. She takes off her hairpin and places it in front of the dragon. The nifty little daisy glitters like a symbolic flower of hope in the snow.)\nI long for the day... I can really transform this place that has nurtured me into a real paradise.",
    ["Dialogue2073101"]="(There's a magnificent, even slightly gaudy wild rose embroidered at the bottom right corner of the handkerchief. You can faintly make out the letters \"B.T.\" beneath...)",
    ["Dialogue2073201"]="(A beautiful but perhaps slightly gaudy image of a wild rose is engraved on the handle of the sword, under which you can faintly make out the letters \"B.T.\"...)",
    ["Dialogue2073301"]="(You can make up scattered footprints of various sizes. Closer examination reveals bits of straw in some of the shoe prints.)",
    ["Dialogue2073401"]="(A very ancient-looking thread-stitching tome that seems a little wrinkled after some <color=#CA2E0AFF>water damage</color> although the cover title \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Dance of All Dances</color>\" is still quite legible. To your surprise, the book actually appears to have been cut in half. <color=#CA2E0AFF>There's no trace of the latter half</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue2080101"]="Looks like the density of transition ions is still not enough. Maybe we can add more mediums, speeding up their movement to offset the instability caused by the low density...",
    ["Dialogue2080102"]="Don't interrupt me, Adventurer! I must think thoroughly about how to optimize the defense mechanism of the Realm of Time! You know, if those things can escape this time, then can escape the next.",
    ["Dialogue2080103"]="A mechanical device fitted with a phase conversion program. After inspection, I found out their central controlling units utilize a retro design that dates back to ancient times, featuring a manufacturing procedure capable of simulating the behaviors of living organisms.",
    ["Dialogue2080104"]="It means... Sigh, forget about it. Fortunately, I have made a backup copy of the details about the appearance information on these things. You see—",
    ["Dialogue2080105"]="Okay, okay. That's what I mean. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a good look</color> at these <color=#CA2E0AFF>photos</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2080201"]="Do you get it? Not long ago, these weird-looking mech creatures escaped from the Realm of Time. To make matters worse, their central controlling units are very unstable. If they are subject to severe impacts or come into contact with flames, they might... explode.",
    ["Dialogue2080202"]="Yes. As you know, the Realm of Time is located inside Juno Library. Outside the library is Juno's Central Plaza, the most crowded area in the city. If these mech creatures go KA BOOM out there... it'll be devastating.",
    ["Dialogue2080203"]="(Fulkyn opens his hand. There are a few pieces of tiny chips.)\nThese are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>receivers</color> I've made, embedded with return protocol. As long as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>install these chips into the interfaces on these mech creatures' chests </color>, they will return to the Realm of Time by themselves.",
    ["Dialogue2080204"]="Three mech creatures have escaped from here. According to the records from the Mysterious Device, they left the library from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast exit</color>. Please find them as soon as possible to prevent this incident from escalating. And I must warn you, that these mech creatures are <color=#CA2E0AFF>highly intelligent</color>. They can use various methods to <color=#CA2E0AFF>evade your pursuit </color>... Please don't let down your guard just because they are robots, or you will pay for it.",
    ["Dialogue2080301"]="<size=26>For heaven's sake! My prosthetic leg!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080302"]="Do I look alright to you?\n(The young man shouts in frustration while grabbing his left leg and pointing it at your nose.)\n<size=26>My freaking leg FELL OFF!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080303"]="Do you even know how to do it? If you get it backward, how am I supposed to walk?\n(As he vents his rage at you, the broken prosthetic leg swings back and forth before your eyes. Quite a scary picture it is.)\nAlright, alright! Just leave me alone. Go after that <color=#CA2E0AFF>robot</color> already!",
    ["Dialogue2080304"]="Aren't you looking for the robot that bumped into me? It dashed out from the library not long ago, the same way you came from...\n(The young man checks you out confusingly.)\nAre you not its master?",
    ["Dialogue2080305"]="That's what I thought! It went <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color>. You'd better hurry up! And I got to say, that thing is fast! If it somehow bumps into elders or kids, I don't think a few apologies will cut it.",
    ["Dialogue2080401"]="Hmmm... What on earth is that thing?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>So fast. If only I could catch it and train it as a mount... Hehe... I would be rich...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2080402"]="...A robot that is fast? W-Why are you asking this?\n(The shrewd merchant checks you out, appearing cautious.)\nTsk, You're not here to undercut my business, are you...",
    ["Dialogue2080403"]="Hey, hey. Let me make it clear! I saw that thing first, and I call dibs on that! Plus, I don't think you can catch up with it. That thing has been running circle after circle around the Central Plaza, and no one was able to... Look! Here it comes again!",
    ["Dialogue2080404"]="(As the merchant speaks, you see a pile of brown stuff dashing your way, along with some unknown weird sound effects.)\nGu—DiDi—ChuPiLiBaBa—o(*￣▽￣*)ブ",
    ["Dialogue2080405"]="You see? This thing is FAST! In a moment, it'll zip past you, and you can't even touch it!",
    ["Dialogue2080406"]="ChuChu—Choo—\n(As if to prove the merchant's words, this mech thing speeds up as it passes through the two of you, and then... it touches the merchant on the head.)",
    ["Dialogue2080407"]="Huh? This little thing is kinda interesting! It's saying hi to———<size=23>MY FOOT!</size> <size=26>WHERE THE HELL IS MY WIG?</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080408"]="Y-Y-You... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go after it now</color>! Get my wig back! And I will let you pick whatever mount you want!\n(After realizing his wig was taken, that stingy merchant suddenly seems a different man and tosses all his mount keys to you.)\n<size=26>GO!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080501"]="Woof! Woof–Woof!\n(The yellow Shiba Inu looks at you, then turns around and stares at the leaving robot, letting out a series of unintelligible barks.)",
    ["Dialogue2080502"]="Woof! Woof–Woof-Woof!\n(Seeing that you have no reaction, the dog becomes more aggressive. It firmly bites on one of your pant legs and keeps pulling. Seems like the dog wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow it</color>... As for the merchant, he might have to wait a bit long for his wig.)",
    ["Dialogue2080601"]="How's that? Beautiful, isn't it? Let me tell you, my Cucchi is not only perfect in its outlook, but it has also undergone professional training from the Royal Pet Association! It can perform a world-class pet show all by itself! Come on, let me show it to you — Cucchi! Stand up! Give me your hand!",
    ["Dialogue2080602"]="...CLICK!\n(As the man speaks, the mech creature at the center of the crowd straightens its leg and places its mechanical claws into the man's palm.)",
    ["Dialogue2080603"]="Oh my! It understands human language!",
    ["Dialogue2080604"]="Aww... So cute! I want one now...",
    ["Dialogue2080605"]="...Not a dog? Adventurer, what are you talking about?\n(The man frowns as he tenderly caresses the round head of the mech creature, letting out a series of admiring sounds.)\nIt's silky smooth... Do you want to pat it?",
    ["Dialogue2080606"]="(Regardless of your refusal, he grabs your hand forcibly and puts it on top of the mech creature's head. In an instant, a chill, metallic feeling travels up from your fingertips.)\n...How's that? Feels good, doesn't it? Isn't that soul-soothing?",
    ["Dialogue2080607"]="...Coo-coo! o(*////▽////*)\n(Your sight seems slightly blurred, as the mech creature's cold surface starts to grow a layer of fur, then...?)",
    ["Dialogue2080608"]="Woof-woof! Purr! Purr!",
    ["Dialogue2080609"]="...Huh???",
    ["Dialogue2080610"]="<size=26>Woof... Woof Woof! Woof! Awooo—</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080701"]="W-What happened? This... This is not my Cucchi!\n(After you successfully retrieved the mech creature, the surrounding crowd seems to snap back to reality. The owner of the Shiba Inu checks out the surrounding in horror, calling his pet.)\nCucchi... Cucchi! Where are you?",
    ["Dialogue2080702"]="...Woof-Awooo—",
    ["Dialogue2080703"]="Good... Good boy! <size=26>I was worried sick about you!</size>\n(The man hugs his dog and starts crying. Seems he has no time to deal with you...)",
    ["Dialogue2080704"]="Please don't mind, Adventurer. He's always like this... For anything that involves Cucchi, he can get as emotional as he can be. Please forgive his faux pas.",
    ["Dialogue2080705"]="Speaking of which... What just happened? Why did we all mistake that mech creature for Cucchi?\n<size=26><color=#A1979FFF>It was like a mass hallucination... This is so strange...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2080706"]="...A similar-looking robot? Hmm... Now that you mention it, I did see a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young man in a Juno University uniform</color> carrying something that looked a lot like this in here a while ago... He was yelling something about <color=#CA2E0AFF>physical training</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2080801"]="Delia! Look at the skeleton of this mech creature! Its grip is absolutely amazing! Can I—",
    ["Dialogue2080802"]="No. Put it down now, Wallace.",
    ["Dialogue2080803"]="Eh-Eh-Eh? But I have never seen such a machine that is so perfect for physical training! Please, let me try it out. Just once!",
    ["Dialogue2080804"]="I said, <size=26>N–O!</size>\nStay away from these random things. They don't even have a safety certificate! What if they explode when you smash on them!",
    ["Dialogue2080805"]="I don't think so... It looks so sturdy! I can get it a good smash if you don't believe me!\n(Wallace lifts up his arm as he speaks, and you hear a loud BANG before you can ever stop him.)",
    ["Dialogue2080806"]="Goo-Goo-Goo... Click-Click-Click?\n(The head of the green mech creature is being knocked sideways, dazedly turning its neck and looking at all of you.)",
    ["Dialogue2080807"]="(Swallowing nervously)\nW-What's it doing?",
    ["Dialogue2080808"]="(Swallowing nervously)\nS-Shut it. Stop talking...",
    ["Dialogue2080809"]="...Whew...\n(After a long few seconds, its green eyes fade slowly, like someone pulled the plug.)",
    ["Dialogue2080810"]="Y-Yes! There is no way it's going to explode! HAHAHAHAHA—",
    ["Dialogue2080811"]="(Unfortunately, before Wallace finishes his sentence, this mech creature starts spinning at high speed, emitting a series of sharp alarms.)\n<size=26>BEEP-BEEP-BEEP-BEEP-BEEP-BEEP-BEEP!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2080812"]="AHHHHHHHHH! Delia! How do you know it is going to explode! What should we do now?! GAAAAAAAAA!",
    ["Dialogue2080813"]="<size=26>You idiot! Quick! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Put it to sleep!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2080901"]="(Watching the mech creature leave safely, without causing any trouble, Delia lets out a sigh of relief. Then she throws a criticizing gaze at you.)\n...What in the world is going on? You are the one who brought it here?",
    ["Dialogue2080902"]="That's no excuse for letting such a dangerous thing run wild across the city! Even though the receiver you installed has automatic navigation, you can't guarantee that it won't cause any trouble on the way back! What if the situation just now happens again? What are those unarmed citizens supposed to do?!",
    ["Dialogue2080903"]="...Hold on! Take this too!\n(With a flick of her wrist, a soft golden hue comes flying your way, which you quickly grab.)",
    ["Dialogue2080904"]="Huh... Huh? Delia! I found it first! I'm calling dibs!",
    ["Dialogue2080905"]="Shut up! Don't always collect random stuff that appears out of nowhere!\n(She gazes at the youngster, then turns around and starts to explain to you.)",
    ["Dialogue2080906"]="Wallace found this in the body of that mech creature, and we have no idea what it is. But such things are scattered throughout various body modules in large quantities, so I speculate they must be something useful. And since you are asked to search for this mech creature, I think all the stuff should be returned to the right owner.",
    ["Dialogue2081001"]="You're back! Even faster than I thought. Now I can tell you the origin of these mech creatures: They are the evidence left behind by some culprit who attempted to alter history.",
    ["Dialogue2081002"]="Not long ago, through spatial fluctuations, the Mysterious Device detected that someone was time-traveling and altering history. I immediately set off to the invaded timeline but failed to spot the perpetrator. At the scene, I only saw these weird-looking mech creatures wandering around. Without a choice, I had to bring them back before deciding my next move.",
    ["Dialogue2081003"]="After that, things like this had been cropping up frequently. Strangely enough, the Mysterious Device always <color=#CA2E0AFF>detected multiple coordinates where spatial fluctuations took place at the same time</color>. All I could do was head to one of them and investigate, but every single time I came back empty-handed. Later, I went through the records on the Mysterious Device and found out that <color=#CA2E0AFF>only one part of history had been altered</color> among these coordinates. The rest... were nothing but smoke and mirrors.",
    ["Dialogue2081004"]="Whoever was behind this wasn't just trying to fool me. They used the loophole in the algorithm. The Mysterious Device can only detect the coordinates where spatial fluctuations occur and use that information to determine whether someone has gone to a timeline where they don't belong. However, it can't tell me which coordinates have been altered immediately. So whoever came up with this trick must be quite familiar with the device... and me.",
    ["Dialogue2081005"]="I am not sure, Adventurer. But we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>start looking for clues from these mech creatures</color>. Maybe we will come across something new.",
    ["Dialogue2081101"]="You... Where did you get this, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2081102"]="Are you saying... Two students from the mechanical engineering department of Juno University discovered the Sands of Time from various major modules of this green mech creature?\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Interesting. Then I take the chance to try out my new algorithm...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue2081103"]="(Fulkyn isn't responding to your question. Instead, he bends down to the Mysterious Device, and his fingers start dancing on the instrument panel until a row of green lights appears on the transmitter.)\n...Come here, <color=#CA2E0AFF>put everything you got from the mech creature in it</color>. I will explain later, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2081201"]="(The Mysterious Device clinks and clangs, as if the metal parts are clashing with each other. Soon after, a cold and hollow mechanical humming sound echoes from the device.)\nCorrelating and analyzing clues... Correlation confirmed... Identical target located... Confirming the next possible coordinates: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Year AW232, Geffen.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2081301"]="As I expected, the Sands of Time carry a large amount of transition ions. Now we can let the Mysterious Device run some tests on them, mapping out all possible combinations of the four-dimensional coordinates so as to pinpoint the sequences with the same order...",
    ["Dialogue2081302"]="Fine. Simply put, the Sands of Time has an ability that passively records the spatial fluctuation coordinates. By analyzing the Sands of Time scattered throughout the mech creatures, we can get numerous spatial coordinates. Then we need to sort them out to find the correlation among these coordinates... Just like a puzzle game, where we look for patterns. Do you get it now, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2081303"]="(Fulkyn stretches out his hand, showing you a few numbers.)\n1, 3, 5, 7... What comes next?",
    ["Dialogue2081304"]="That's how it works. Based on this, I have updated Mysterious Device's algorithm, and it just told me the next set of coordinates: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Year AW232, Geffen.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2081305"]="Yes. So, now...\n(Fulkyn spreads his hand. On his palm, there are some dazzling golden sands that you are quite familiar with.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Hold on tight to the Sands of Time</color>. We should be going now, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2081401"]="Adventurer, although this isn't your first time-travel, I still need to remind you that we are undeniable intruders of the past. Therefore, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demotima</color>, who maintains the law and order of spacetime, must expel us at all costs. From now on, we must stay alert—",
    ["Dialogue2081402"]="Warning! Warning! Danger! Danger...\n(Before Fulkyn finishes the sentence, the Mysterious Device lets out a series of warnings.)",
    ["Dialogue2081403"]="Careful... They are here.",
    ["Dialogue2081501"]="Don't be surprised, Adventurer. Demotima are monsters residing in hyper-dimensional space. Commonly used attacks cannot finish them. Now that they have become vulnerable, we should leave this place at once, <color=#CA2E0AFF>looking for that history-altering culprit</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2081502"]="I am sorry. Based on what we know so far, I can hardly infer his motivation. But this will not change our goal, right? Whatever his reason is, altering history is strictly prohibited. I will go to all lengths to stop him.",
    ["Dialogue2081503"]="Okay... We shouldn't wait any longer, Adventurer. Let's go now. Once these Demotima recover, we'll be facing another tough battle.",
    ["Dialogue2081601"]="Professor Fulkyn, I haven't seen you for a while! Seems you still obsess about poking your nose into people's affairs. What now? How do you think my containment device could be improved? Please enlighten me, professor.",
    ["Dialogue2081602"]="...I should've guessed it was you all along, Barr Venter. These mech creatures are created through biomimetic technology; even their central controlling units are integrated with mana-conducting circuits. These are all fruits of your research during the second technological leap. These special Sands of Time... were a flawed product I inadvertently produced during my own research, and you're the only one who has ever seen it.",
    ["Dialogue2081603"]="Smart as you, how could you have left so many obvious clues for me to trace back here... No, wait. That's not right.\n(In a split second, Fulkyn seems to connect all the threads of the whole incident, getting to see the scheme behind it.)\n...You did it on purpose, Barr Venter.",
    ["Dialogue2081604"]="You are getting old, Professor Fulkyn. Even though time hasn't left much of a trace on your body, your mind surely becomes duller. In the past, I am sure you can see through such a trap at a glance, needing no reminders from others. But now... it's too late.",
    ["Dialogue2081605"]="(At this moment, a sliver of pride emerges on Barr Venter's face, which has always been calm and composed. He tilts his head, looking at the Mysterious Device at Fulkyn's feet.)\nI already got what I want.",
    ["Dialogue2081606"]="No... Adventurer. He is not looking for the device but the algorithm it contains.\n(Fulkyn shakes his head. You can see regret and frustration on his face.)\nNow that he's got the algorithm, it's guaranteed that he can slip under my nose.",
    ["Dialogue2081607"]="Indeed. Those mech creatures are merely the baits I set up. That day in Glast Heim, you ruined my plan, but you had also revealed your trump card—the powerful algorithm of the Mysterious Device. It allows you to trace the invasion time and location of even the slightest spatial fluctuations. So I ordered these mech creatures to move at the same time, traveling back and forth in different spacetime... What a move! Are your feeling overwhelmed, Professor Fulkyn?",
    ["Dialogue2081608"]="Not only that, but I also made some slight adjustments to those mech creatures. The four-dimensional coordinates those transition ions carried were fascinating, weren't they? As a scholar so obsessed with the spacetime theory, you must have used the Mysterious Device without any hesitation to decipher the riddles I embedded in those coordinates. Correct?",
    ["Dialogue2081609"]="...So, you can now use the coordinates to backtrack and figure out the algorithm for that Mysterious Device.\n(Fulkyn sighs deeply, expressing both remorse for his own carelessness and pity for Barr Venter's misguided path.)\nIt's clear why people referred to you as the \"Father of Mechanics.\" To squander such talent is truly a shame.",
    ["Dialogue2081610"]="...Just a meaningless title, nothing special at all. I've never second-guessed my decisions, and you are in no position to criticize me in the eyes of the world.",
    ["Dialogue2081611"]="I am just curious, Barr Venter. Why are you so keen on altering the history from hundreds of years ago? Do you realize that spacetime runs on its own rules and orders? Anyone who dares to tamper with them will—",
    ["Dialogue2081612"]="Don't underestimate me, Professor Fulkyn. I have read all your academic works, including... the experimental records you burned into ashes.",
    ["Dialogue2081613"]="<size=26>You?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue2081614"]="(Seeing the look of disbelief on Fulkyn's face, Barr Venter gently raises his hand.)\nSpacetime Rule Number 1: When two identical objects appear at the same time on the same timeline, the latecomer must continue to wither until it ceases to exist, ensuring the uniqueness of the object in this particular timeline.",
    ["Dialogue2081615"]="Spacetime Rule Number 2: No external intervention can permanently change a factual event in any timeline. The spacetime will always recalibrate itself, restoring all the timelines to their original state.",
    ["Dialogue2081616"]="Spacetime Rule Number 3: The violator of Spacetime Rules will permanently lose their grip on time.\n(Barr Venter gazes at Fulkyn for a while. You can see the unspoken battle between their eyes, which you can't understand, last until this young father of mechanics finishes his sentence.)\nJust like you, Professor Fulkyn.",
    ["Dialogue2081617"]="...Indeed, I breached the Spacetime Rules due to a lack of understanding, and I was punished for it. Now, all I'm doing is seeking redemption. How about you?\n(Fulkyn's usually stoic face now displays anger you rarely see.)\nYou're well aware of the consequences of your actions. Why do you still go down this path?",
    ["Dialogue2081618"]="It's not your concern. As I said, the moment you refused to help me, we were no longer partners.\n(Barr Venter shows an indifferent look, then kicks the device that traps the Demotima. You feel something bad is going to happen.)",
    ["Dialogue2081619"]="This is only a warning: Stay out of my business. Otherwise... The next time we meet, I will send both of you to dimensional rifts. You should be quite familiar with those places, Professor Fulkyn.",
    ["Dialogue2081620"]="You... What the...?",
    ["Dialogue2081621"]="(Along with Barr Venter's mischievous laughter, a bright light erupted from the device at his feet. You shut your eyes. All you can hear is his cold and apathetic voice.)\n...Goodbye, Professor Fulkyn, and the successor of Odin's bloodline. May our paths never cross again.",
    ["Dialogue2081701"]="...Pardon me, Adventurer. This is my personal matter, yet I've repeatedly asked for your assistance... I'm truly sorry.",
    ["Dialogue2081702"]="It's alright. Save your consoling words. I do feel sorry for Barr Venter, and I am also mad at myself for not being able to stop him in time. But being emotional won't get us anywhere... Now that he has decided to breach Spacetime Rules, I must do everything in my power to stop him.",
    ["Dialogue2081703"]="Yes, spacetime will always recalibrate itself, sorting out every event that detours from history and putting them back where they belong. But don't you find it strange? Barr Venter is fully aware of this, yet he keeps altering history once and again. Why is he doing this? The Barr Venter I know would never take risks, which means... something convinced him that he could indeed alter the course of history.",
    ["Dialogue2081704"]="That's what I thought, too, Adventurer. His confidence... Might come from the device that traps the Demotima.",
    ["Dialogue2081705"]="Unfortunately, what we see today is not enough for me to determine the use of the device. As far as we know, Barr Venter used the device to capture a Demotima, and he used the same device to send us from Year AW232's Geffen back to today's Juno... He even warned to throw us into dimensional rifts, if we dare to hinder his plan again.",
    ["Dialogue2081706"]="It's a distorted hyper-dimensional space created by the vibrational frequency discrepancies among various timelines in the universe. Once the vibrational frequency exceeds 30 Aihaar, the space falls into an unstable and random folding state, instantly disintegrating living beings of lower dimensions...",
    ["Dialogue2081707"]="...Anyway, given the intel we have right now, it's quite challenging to figure out what that device is used for. However, I've managed to have the Mysterious Device document all the history nodes and coordinates altered by Barr Venter. We have a small time window to <color=#CA2E0AFF>examine the changes in these historical events</color> before the spacetime restores itself.",
    ["Dialogue2081708"]="(Fulkyn smiles. At this moment, the brilliant and confident time traveler you used to know seems to be back.)\n...Still remember the puzzle game we played before? 1, 3, 5, 7... What comes next?",
    ["Dialogue2081709"]="That's it! Looking for patterns, which the Mysterious Device is good at. As long as Barr Venter keeps altering the course of history, we can find a pattern from the changes... and then figure out what he is trying to achieve.",
    ["Dialogue2081710"]="(With his gaze downcast, Fulkyn clutches the Sands of Time tightly in his hand. You somehow detect a trace of excitement on his face. Probably even Fulkyn himself didn't notice that. Seems... Barr Venter is the only worthy opponent that he has been waiting for a long time.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...Barr Venter, let's have a race. We'll see... which one of us will reach the finish line first.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2081801"]="(This set of gears consists of far more components than typical modules, with a lot of cogs, bearings, springs, and pistons integrated into one unit, as if replicating the skeletal movements of biological creatures. You recall that such biomimetic designs were highly favored during the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second technological leap</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue2081901"]="(Attached to the Mech Core is the Mana Conductor, a device that harnesses mana to propel mechanical functions and is now considered <color=#CA2E0AFF>obsolete</color>. Modern manufacturing has moved on to digital technologies, with chips being the prevalent medium...)",
    ["Dialogue2082001"]="(...There appear to be no leads on this mech creature, which makes no sense. Perhaps you should show Fulkyn the <color=#CA2E0AFF>thing found by Delia</color>?)",
    ["Dialogue2083001"]="(The computation comes to a sudden stop, and the screen turns blue, showing a bunch of incomprehensible equations before Fulkyn.)\nBarr Venter... What exactly is the piece of history you risked breaking the rules of time-space to alter?",
    ["Dialogue2083002"]="(With a light tap on the screen, the progress nearly drops to zero)\nSorting data and calculating the impact of changes. No biggie, the anomalies caused by altering history are in the trillions, <color=#CA2E0AFF>running low on computing power</color> is nothing unusual.",
    ["Dialogue2083003"]="I need two more weeks. That's the best-case scenario, meaning Barr Venter doesn't know about the Mysterious Device and how it works, and assuming our computing power isn't sidetracked by other sudden events during the entire period, then we should get the results we're hoping for.",
    ["Dialogue2083004"]="But...\n(Fulkyn touches a corner of the Mysterious Device with his eyes filled with concerns)\nBarr Venter, once the institute's lead and now the \"Great Sage,\" never leaves anything to chance, whether it's dealing with friends or foes.",
    ["Dialogue2083005"]="(Fulkyn looks at you briefly, moving past the question.)\nPeople who mess with the \"rules\" tend to know them better than the rule-keepers. Since Barr Venter cracked the secrets of time travel, this device, built upon the Spacetime Rule, <color=#CA2E0AFF>holds no secrets for him</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083006"]="Take it easy.\n(As he speaks, a starry blue hologram appears out of thin air.)\nAccording to \"Ripple Theory,\" time-space is an ocean with undercurrent, and disturbing it requires only a slight ripple.",
    ["Dialogue2083007"]="Drop a stone at just the right moment.\n(Fulkyn touches the screen softly, causing the hologram to shatter, then rebuild in the next.)\nThe ripple it creates, in both time and space, will unleash a tsunami of changes.",
    ["Dialogue2083008"]="At that point, nobody will know whether the change came from a mere ripple or which ripple.",
    ["Dialogue2083009"]="Yesterday? Ten years ago? Twenty years ago?\n(Fulkyn brings up a timeline, and you notice three standout red crosses amidst an array of points)\nThese are the earliest ripples. To track them down, I've been practically living on caffeine.",
    ["Dialogue2083010"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Finding those three pebbles from the sea of time, the ones that started the whole tsunami</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083011"]="Besides, in this game, spotting the alterations is merely a defensive play. It's by <color=#CA2E0AFF>understanding the logic and motives behind those changes</color> that we can start to fight back. Rule-breakers believe exploiting loopholes will let them fool everyone, yet their action of \"breaking\" itself is the greatest loophole. Adventurer, as my comrade, I'm officially inviting you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>venture with me to the altered time nodes</color>. After all, my power alone isn’t quite enough to handle the unforeseen threats.",
    ["Dialogue2083012"]="(Fulkyn nods, showing a friendly smile.)\nCould you do me a favor and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Lord's Mansion to retrieve the Sands of Time</color> stored there? I've burned through a ton of it with all the computation lately, and I don't have enough left to start the time travel.",
    ["Dialogue2083013"]="(Fulkyn spreads his hands innocently, tapping the Mysterious Device beside him.)\nI need to fine-tune this thing. Look, it's literally smoking from overload.",
    ["Dialogue2083014"]="(Click... click... click...)",
    ["Dialogue2083101"]="(Taking the Sands of Time, Fulkyn, busy with the Mysterious Device, breaks the silence.)\nHere lies both the key and lock to the gate of time. Never crossed your mind to grab them? You—don't want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>change the past</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2083102"]="No buts. To alter the past is to accept your past being altered.\n(Fulkyn cuts you off with a serious look.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Barr Venter, proud as you are, could you stand your past being rewritten?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2083103"]="Keep today's words in mind.\n(Fulkyn's eyes look far away.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Is it for your own good? For someone else's? Barr Venter, as aloof as you come across, is attached to something and can't let it go?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2083104"]="The Mysterious Device has locked on the coordinates, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Time travel starts in three seconds</color>, and it might make you dizzy; you can hang onto me.",
    ["Dialogue2083201"]="Welcome to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>spring of AW225</color>, Adventurer. We're in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>neutral village up north</color>, where, if we're sticking to the proper timeline, the Rune Kingdom has been established by now, but the Republic and Arunafeltz have yet to enter the annals of history.",
    ["Dialogue2083202"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>One of the Spacetime Rules: if there are repeating units in the same timeline, the newcomers will gradually disappear. Here's where history's been corrected.</color>\n(The Mysterious Device starts buzzing, and it looks like invisible particles in the air are warping.)\nNow, the device is working on restoring what things were like before. Before that, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>explore the corrected history</color> for a bit of comparative analysis.",
    ["Dialogue2083301"]="Gamow! Why so early today, and where's Thanatos? We were just talking about him and Lush... Heh, he's a good one, isn't he?",
    ["Dialogue2083302"]="He's taken his medicine and is resting now. You guys—like him a lot?",
    ["Dialogue2083303"]="Yo, see how Gamow changes his attitude whenever we bring up Thanatos. Don't worry. We treat Lush like our kid. Just keep an eye on that boy; if he's good, then let things happen.",
    ["Dialogue2083304"]="Things...? They... are close?",
    ["Dialogue2083305"]="Come on, you haven't noticed? Well, take my advice, Lush's fine, but Thanatos… he's got some heavy knots in his heart...",
    ["Dialogue2083306"]="Ah... I see, <color=#CA2E0AFF>that makes sense</color>. Looks like he's found himself <color=#CA2E0AFF>a new hope</color>, right?",
    ["Dialogue2083307"]="R-Really...? Gamow, you're so weird today. I gotta go. Go easy on the hunting.",
    ["Dialogue2083401"]="You're back?\n(Fulkyn is turned away from you with his hands dancing over the console.)\nWe still need a bit of time for the restoration; what's up on your end?",
    ["Dialogue2083402"]="(Fingers stop moving, and Fulkyn murmurs to himself, eyes glancing over each line of data on the screen without inputting commands.)\nThanatos, Lush... a Demon Swordsman still wet behind the ears, and a girl from the countryside with no claim to fame. What's the gain in changing history here for him?",
    ["Dialogue2083403"]="Are you saying Thanatos was with this guy, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gamow</color>, and Lush's his kid? Gamow... Gamow... What does he look like?",
    ["Dialogue2083404"]="(After listening to your report, Fulkyn turns the Mysterious Device around, and the screen now shows Gamow's face.)\nIs this him? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Born in AW184, died in... AW225</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083405"]="(Fulkyn folds his hands together, his long fingers covering half of his face, leaving only his overly calm red eyes visible.)\nA hunter, in prime condition, died this year. Unless there is a sudden illness or epidemic, natural death is nearly impossible.",
    ["Dialogue2083406"]="I see...\n(Fulkyn gazes towards the village, a trace of barely noticeable pity in his tone)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>The clues have surfaced.</color> It's not only about Thanatos and Lush; what happens next will change everyone's life here.",
    ["Dialogue2083407"]="The impact of this matter was profound; it could even influence Glast Heim back in AW231, where we first encountered Barr Venter. Adventurer, does that ring a bell?",
    ["Dialogue2083408"]="(Fulkyn nods seriously)\nTime to track down <color=#CA2E0AFF>Thanatos</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083501"]="Thanatos, remember me?\n(A monster crawls out from the cold corpse of Gamow; its skin is covered with crazy, fierce eyes, with three particularly bizarre, bloody ones among them)\nEver since you stabbed and blinded these <color=#CA2E0AFF>three eyes</color>, I never allowed them to heal.",
    ["Dialogue2083502"]="All this pain every day, it's to remind me of the disgrace from years ago and to make you suffer just like I did!\n(Hundreds of eyes stare at Thanatos as the creature bursts into laughter in front of his quivering body.)\nHahaha! Look at you, just like a year ago!",
    ["Dialogue2083503"]="Ah... what got you so mad again? Oh yeah, <color=#CA2E0AFF>your master and senior disciple tried to stop me from eating the villagers, so I killed them both!</color> Hahaha! They had it coming!",
    ["Dialogue2083504"]="Shut up!\n(Thanatos growls, struggling to his feet and nearly falling again.)\nIf only I had been a little earlier, you never would have succeeded...",
    ["Dialogue2083505"]="Ah—Thanatos, the youngest disciple with exceptional sword skills, believing he can take me down solo? Hehe, wrong again! The funniest thing about humans is that you think being strong can change everything, not knowing that some things are decided the moment you're born!",
    ["Dialogue2083506"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>It's who you really are!</color> Thanatos! You haven't forgotten what your master, the old man whose chest I ripped open, said to you as he was dying while holding your arm, have you? \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>You have great talent, but you're too sensitive inside. Don't blame yourself; don't carry it all on your own.</color>\" Touching, isn't it? The great sentiments between humans who aren't even related by blood!",
    ["Dialogue2083507"]="(Word by word, as the monster recounts, Thanatos lifts his head in disbelief, his eyes seeming to well with blood.)\nHow do you know what my master said? Were you... there?",
    ["Dialogue2083508"]="Hey, I feast on agony; I wouldn't miss such a delightful event.\n(The monster's tone turns cold and piercing.)\nThanatos, seeing you happy always makes me want to burn down this entire village!",
    ["Dialogue2083509"]="Why do you get to hang on to a new hope while I have to skulk around, unable to return under Lord Morroc's command?\n(Amidst mad laughter, the monster tosses Gamow's body at Thanatos' feet.)\nI've made up my mind—I'm going to make you <color=#CA2E0AFF>suffer again</color>, even if it costs me my life!",
    ["Dialogue2083510"]="(Gamow's pale face, a mix of agony and regret, his lifeless pupils wide open looking towards Thanatos.)\nHe was the one who took care of you every day, right? I <color=#CA2E0AFF>manipulated him to feed you the sleeping pill</color>, good stuff.",
    ["Dialogue2083511"]="Enough...",
    ["Dialogue2083512"]="What's that? Speak up—how painful is it for you right now? Is it like the time you thought your recklessness had killed everyone in your clan, like you're the curse itself who brought disaster to the village? Because you're the <color=#CA2E0AFF>harbinger of doom</color>, haha!",
    ["Dialogue2083513"]="I said... ENOUGH!",
    ["Dialogue2083601"]="This appears to be the entirety of this piece of history.\n(A few clicks later, the timeline on the screen lights up with new red points.)\nFollow me. Need a minute to settle?",
    ["Dialogue2083602"]="(Fulkyn reaches out to you.)\nOne of us has to keep our cool, okay?",
    ["Dialogue2083603"]="(Fulkyn ponders with his eyes shut.)\nI believe that... whether it's time, destiny, <color=#CA2E0AFF>everyone has their own path to walk</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083604"]="(Fulkyn is still reaching out to you with his hand.)\nThe same goes for Thanatos and Lush, myself, and you. Let's go. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>new spacetime coordinates</color> are locked in.",
    ["Dialogue2083701"]="... This is what you wanted to change? Barr Venter, you, being the \"Destroyer,\" <color=#CA2E0AFF>trying to repair someone else's life</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2083702"]="(Fulkyn shakes his head, smiling wryly.)\nIf he behaved like normal people, he wouldn't be Barr Venter. This is one of many possibilities I discovered.",
    ["Dialogue2083703"]="Perhaps during our years together at the institute, we never really had that understanding we assumed. <color=#CA2E0AFF>He never understood us, and we never really understood him either.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2083704"]="But talking about it now is pointless.\n(Fulkyn pulls down the lever.)\nWhether we understood each other or not, I need to stop Barr Venter from messing with history.",
    ["Dialogue2083705"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Year AW230, a brand-new town</color>. Like always, you go dig around, and I'll safeguard the device.",
    ["Dialogue2083801"]="Next stop, I'm thinking of heading over to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2083902"]="The local posters mention a witch doctor in Glast Heim who knows all about <color=#CA2E0AFF>resurrection</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2083903"]="But we already made a promise to the lord... Thanatos, are you really going to...?",
    ["Dialogue2083904"]="I'll deal with him. You've still got Uncle Gamow's stuff with you, right?",
    ["Dialogue2083905"]="I'm always here, Thanatos, I...",
    ["Dialogue2083906"]="Good, I heard their king is really brutal. You wouldn't need to come with me if the resurrection didn't require bones and blood from relatives.",
    ["Dialogue2083907"]="Lush, once the ritual is completed, you and Uncle Gamow should head back. If it means you can return to your old peaceful life, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I'd give anything</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2083908"]="... Hmm.",
    ["Dialogue2084001"]="Hmm... Was there something stuck here before?",
    ["Dialogue2084002"]="It got torn away, along with your past. So tell me, <color=#CA2E0AFF>what future are you looking for</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2084003"]="I...\n(The girl's confused eyes flicker a spark of hope.)\nI... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I need to find him</color>... Let's look for the future instead of falling into the past...",
    ["Dialogue2084101"]="... Barr Venter, you are no doubt a manipulator.",
    ["Dialogue2084102"]="It's anger!\n(Fulkyn grips his forehead, his voice icy with suppressed fury.)\nTo achieve his goal, he... he actually...",
    ["Dialogue2084103"]="You've heard about Thanatos sealing away Morroc, haven't you? All major events that impact the course of world history boil down to a series of significant or insignificant coincidences, and Thanatos and Lush they're <color=#CA2E0AFF>the most important</color> part!",
    ["Dialogue2084104"]="Of course.\n(Fulkyn snorts.)\nIt's a shame that if it weren't for the unresolved issues between her and Thanatos, perhaps Morroc wouldn't have been sealed away so quickly. This world... Hmph.",
    ["Dialogue2084105"]="(Fulkyn quickly types in a bunch of codes on the Mysterious Device, and then a familiar Dimensional Gap opens up.)\nWe've reached the final time node.",
    ["Dialogue2084106"]="Adventurer, you might think I have no sympathy.\n(Fulkyn pauses briefly.)\nI admit, and if needed, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I will uphold the order of time and space at any cost</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2084107"]="That includes <color=#CA2E0AFF>myself as part of the game</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2084201"]="Yet you're all beat up, with life or death uncertain ahead. Just a glance back, and my heart's still with you...",
    ["Dialogue2084202"]="I've stopped caring; after four years of chasing demons, all ups and downs are just bubbles. Go ahead, dump me in the barren land...",
    ["Dialogue2084203"]="So, your life's just about chasing demons?",
    ["Dialogue2084204"]="For whom do I exist, who exists for me. I've been alone since born, a life filled with regrets, only a wisp of spirit left, burning through my half-empty loneliness.",
    ["Dialogue2084205"]="What... What about me?",
    ["Dialogue2084206"]="Without shared beliefs, we'd always be on different paths. Alas, so many are heartbroken, dear Joanna, thankfully, we resonate together.",
    ["Dialogue2084207"]="Yes, I've heard that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the demon hunters up front are Thanatos and Lush</color>. Their conversations have inspired us, and we hope they'll understand each other's hearts once the war's over.",
    ["Dialogue2084301"]="We don't need to wait for the Mysterious Device to crunch the numbers anymore. Once you understand the underlying logic, you can figure out the alterations in this timeline without needing to verify it on-site.",
    ["Dialogue2084302"]="Hmm, I still have to connect an external power source to the Mysterious Device for the next set of calculations, so...",
    ["Dialogue2084303"]="Blue Venatu's Mech Core.\n(Fulkyn picks up the device, signaling you can set off now.)\nThis is the most important part, I'll be waiting for you in the Realm of Time.",
    ["Dialogue2084401"]="(In the Realm of Time, the Mysterious Device's screen continues to display tons of data, yet this time, some numbers make sense to you.)\nThese coordinates represent the final node we've reached; it's reasonable to think that Barr Venter had Lush confess her feelings to Thanatos before the war, as Lush wished in her flashing memories—",
    ["Dialogue2084402"]="(Fulkyn nods and enters more codes into the Mysterious Device.)\nTherefore, Barr Venter's tempering with history, including what he did when we ran into him in Glast Heim, aims to erase the regrets haunting Lush's soul; this must be his objective or one of his objectives.",
    ["Dialogue2084403"]="No way. <color=#CA2E0AFF>The Barr Venter I know would have never granted someone's wish.</color> Moreover, even if the regret of Lush's soul is resolved and the outcome changes, the rules of the timeline will ensure all alternations meet their fated ends. Time and space are of the ultimate supremacy; he's not dumb enough to challenge that.",
    ["Dialogue2084404"]="(Fulkyn remains silent for a bit, then begins reviewing the data with an expression of disbelief.)\nNo personal life... all his time went into research until...",
    ["Dialogue2084405"]="(It stops at a specific point, and a large blank input box takes up the entire screen.)\nCompute: Barr Venter's objective. Clues: Thanatos, Lush, Fate.",
    ["Dialogue2084406"]="Calculating... ERROR!!",
    ["Dialogue2084407"]="You? Okay then. Adventurer, before you enter anything, I need to tell you something.\n(Fulkyn looks at the Realm of Time, where Androids and humans coexist in Juno.)\nRecords say that Barr Venter kick-started a technological revolution with his mechanical bionic tech, known as the \"Father of Mechanics.\"",
    ["Dialogue2084408"]="But hardly anyone realizes that aside from turning steel into flesh and blood, he achieved even greater things. It was too controversial and revolutionary to validate and I thought it had stopped long ago, perhaps...",
    ["Dialogue2084409"]="Let's put \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>soul</color>\" in as a key clue; maybe we'll luck out and get an answer.",
    ["Dialogue2084501"]="AW706...\n(Shuts down the device that's still operating, Fulkyn murmurs.)\nSo, it's not theory and logic, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>whimsy and madness</color> that one to enter your realm?",
    ["Dialogue2084502"]="Yet now, you've gone past being \"human,\" constantly challenging the order of time and space, even risking yourself? No, I don't get it, and I won't overlook any possibilities. All I can do is...\n(Fulkyn's gaze becomes resolute.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Risking it all to stop you.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2084601"]="I need a sewage sample from Einbroch Field for some comparison research; this is a personal request, and I'll supply the containers; I hope you don't keep me waiting too long.",
    ["Dialogue2084701"]="Are you the one taking the request? Fantastic! Please pass the word to Miss Milian that a retired airship is being taken apart for auction, and we've got a lead on the thing she wants!",
    ["Dialogue2084702"]="I will offer a fair price. Please let Sumi know that to secure it for me.",
    ["Dialogue2084703"]="Oh definitely! Hehe, maybe I could ask Miss Milian out to dinner?",
    ["Dialogue2084801"]="It's a small token of appreciation, but... I hope they know the Environmental Association isn't going to ignore people suffering from pollution.",
    ["Dialogue2084802"]="In this city, what we can offer is still minimal...",
    ["Dialogue2084901"]="The kid Gamow brought back from the mountain seems like a perfect match for his daughter, Lush!",
    ["Dialogue2084902"]="You mean the one teaching my kid swordsmanship? Ah, it's a good pick!",
    ["Dialogue2084903"]="However, the kid's techniques are strangely rare, and they remind me of... reminds me of... hey, Gamow, this way!",
    ["Dialogue2085001"]="Master... Everyone... Sorry... Ah!",
    ["Dialogue2085002"]="... It's a dream? Why did I sleep so long?",
    ["Dialogue2085003"]="Uncle Gamow? Lush? Are you guys here? Anyone?",
    ["Dialogue2085101"]="Is... is it over? Thanatos... Father, something's wrong with him... I hid...",
    ["Dialogue2085102"]="... Kill all monsters in the world.",
    ["Dialogue2085103"]="Thanatos...What happened to you?",
    ["Dialogue2085104"]="Till this body turns to dust. No trust needed, no ties needed; you... are not needed.",
    ["Dialogue2085105"]="All emotions, any emotions, are just hindrances to slaughter.",
    ["Dialogue2085201"]="Does that kid still want to find the monster that's all covered with eyes?",
    ["Dialogue2085202"]="Haven't heard that lately. It's good to have some peace like now.",
    ["Dialogue2085203"]="Yeah, it was scary how beaten up he was when Gamow first brought him back...",
    ["Dialogue2085204"]="He's recovered now, and he's not making a fuss anymore. Hey, I even saw him smiling at Gamow the other day!",
    ["Dialogue2085301"]="Lush? Lush?",
    ["Dialogue2085302"]="Why... Everyone... Left me...",
    ["Dialogue2085303"]="AHHHHHHH!!!!",
    ["Dialogue2085401"]="I need a sewage sample from Einbroch Field for some comparison research; this is a personal request, and I'll supply the containers; I hope you don't keep me waiting too long.",
    ["Dialogue2085501"]="Are you the one taking the request? Fantastic! Please pass the word to Miss Milian that a retired airship is being taken apart for auction, and we've got a lead on the thing she wants!",
    ["Dialogue2085502"]="I will offer a fair price. Please let Sumi know that to secure it for me.",
    ["Dialogue2085503"]="Oh definitely! Hehe, maybe I could ask Miss Milian out to dinner?",
    ["Dialogue2085601"]="It's a small token of appreciation, but... I hope they know the Environmental Association isn't going to ignore people suffering from pollution.",
    ["Dialogue2085602"]="In this city, what we can offer is still minimal...",
    ["Dialogue2086001"]="Four hundred.\n(Goldie puts away the sharpening stone and gently blows on the icy sharp knife.)\nPhew, you're here.",
    ["Dialogue2086002"]="Oh, that?\n(As you follow Goldie's gaze, you see some cute Moles playing nearby.)\nThis knife, after sharpening it four hundred times, I can cut... swish!",
    ["Dialogue2086003"]="(Goldie makes a throat-slitting gesture.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Instantly slice open that Mole's throat</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2086004"]="(Goldie pouts and puts the knife away as you look at her in shock.)\nOkay, fine. Everything here—Metaling, Ungoliant, and Porcellio—has been wiped out. After you leave tomorrow, I'll sharpen it another three hundred times and test it on the Sky Deleter's scales.",
    ["Dialogue2086005"]="You're not leaving?\n(Goldie's eyes sparkle; she pulls you down to sit and starts venting about the entire dispatch team.)\nI'm losing it! This is the most boring trip ever! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Everyone here is nuts!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2086006"]="(Goldie shakes her head and tiredly pulls you down. In a gloomy mood, she starts venting about the entire dispatch team.)\nBy other things to do, do you mean mining with the workers and inhaling toxic fumes? The people here, the poor are sick, the rich are psychopathy, but they're nothing compared to my teammates. <color=#CA2E0AFF>They're all nuts!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2086007"]="The singing and dancing couple only cares about their art; they don't even eat; the white-haired dude is all about flexing muscles; he drank a whole bottle of monster spine extract the other day and had me wait while he got his stomach pumped before a fight; the blonde girl being a simp on the white-haired dude isn't so bad, but with that green-haired guy who spoils her, their trio is bound to become a nightmare!",
    ["Dialogue2086008"]="I don't care! We're six people with different agendas! No teamwork whatsoever. Plus, thanks to the stupid confidentiality agreement, we can only walk, no teleporting. How long is it gonna take to reach Lighthalzen at this pace?!",
    ["Dialogue2086009"]="(Goldie shrugs, looking aloof.)\nYeah, even if we fail the quest, we still get paid in full as per the contract. That's what the big shots told me!",
    ["Dialogue2086010"]="What? Do you want us to leave right away?\n(Goldie points to the empty tent nearby.)\nThen go find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>white-haired dude</color>. He was babbling about body enhancement and ran off somewhere.",
    ["Dialogue2086101"]="Hey Adventurer, it's been a while.\n(Trinity gives a curtsey, her face still a bit red)\nWhat do you need from us?",
    ["Dialogue2086102"]="Zenlur?\n(Trinity looks confused.)\nWho's Zenlur?",
    ["Dialogue2086103"]="The white-haired youngster who chose the path of Asura.\n(Orfeo casually responds to his fiancee's confusion.)\nAdventurer, do you want him back?",
    ["Dialogue2086104"]="(The elegant Minstrel rubs his forehead.)\nSince the journey began, he and the female Shadow Chaser you just spoke with have been fighting non-stop, and my composing isn't going anywhere...",
    ["Dialogue2086105"]="You?\n(Orfeo pauses, then hands you a music sheet.)\nFine... <color=#CA2E0AFF>sing this song</color> with both joyful and sorrowful feelings. I want to experience the emotions of the singer as an audience member.",
    ["Dialogue2086201"]="So that's how it is...\n(Orfeo says to himself, writing notes in his notebook.)\nAdventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenlur and Celia went to train near the river</color>, if you can call that a river...",
    ["Dialogue2086301"]="(In the Porcellio gathering area, Celia tears open their hard shells with her hands, exposing the decayed, twisted guts.)\nWhoa! So these are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>organs</color> that couldn't handle the pollution? Even the Porcellio couldn't resist...",
    ["Dialogue2086302"]="Uh... but I'm a Sorcerer...\n(Caught by you, Celia forms a water sphere in her hand and excitedly tells you her findings.)\nAdventurer! Can you believe it? A few years of air pollution can destroy an immune system that's evolved for centuries!",
    ["Dialogue2086303"]="Why do you look so sick? Is it the exhaust?\n(Celia gets closer.)\nAdventurer, if you don't have another quest, it's better to stay away from Einbroch.",
    ["Dialogue2086304"]="He...\n(The girl kicks the Porcellio corpse aside, looking upset.)\nHe doesn't believe in me and won't let me follow... even though I can help...",
    ["Dialogue2086305"]="So, I'm going to make the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Upgraded Super Healing Pill</color>! Hah... If I get all the materials from Einbroch's mutants, remove the toxins, and follow the original formula, it'll definitely enhance physical strength more than Ivy's method!",
    ["Dialogue2086306"]="Right? The Super Healing Pill is the best! Even if he picks <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivy</color>, I'll make it and hand it to him myself!\n(Blushing, Celia lowers her head as she thinks of something.)",
    ["Dialogue2086307"]="(Celia hangs her head, looking down.)\nDo you also think <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivy's method</color> is better? But... I have my own special formula...",
    ["Dialogue2086308"]="Anyway, Zenlur is with Ivy now, and Ivy seems to want to be friends with him. They should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>back at the camp</color> by now...\n(Celia pats her cheeks and continues looking for materials for the Super Healing Pill.)",
    ["Dialogue2086401"]="Phew!\n(In the steam, the green-haired young gentleman sips slowly and finally looks up lazily.)\nWhat's the matter?",
    ["Dialogue2086402"]="Him... Didn't Celia mention it? Zenlur's body enhancement is a trade secret that can't be disclosed.",
    ["Dialogue2086403"]="(Setting the teacup on a tray held by a Homunculus, Ivy looks at you and arrogantly raises his chin.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Beg me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2086404"]="Get the alchemy equipment ready for me.\n(Ivy ignores you, orders the Alchemist's Homunculus, and adds a sugar cube to his coffee.)\nGuess where the last person who threatened me ended up...",
    ["Dialogue2086405"]="Hmm... You gave in one second faster than I expected.\n(Ivy smirks wickedly.)\nSince you're begging, let me think...",
    ["Dialogue2086406"]="Start by <color=#CA2E0AFF>catching a Metaling</color> for me, and I want it alive.\n(Ivy gives you a heavy cloth bag.)\nThis is what they love to eat.",
    ["Dialogue2086501"]="Great, great. Only young Metaling are stupid enough to stray from the group for food.\n(Ivy pokes the Metaling's cheek and hands it to the Alchemist's Homunculus.)\nTake it down. It'll absorb your body's impurities and produce the crystal I need.",
    ["Dialogue2086502"]="No rush.\n(Ivy takes out a list and feather pen casually checks something off.)\nNext, help me get rid of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>night-digging Mole</color>; their noise is unbearable.",
    ["Dialogue2086601"]="(Ivy takes out the list and feather pen again, and the content of the list is noticeably longer.)\nSorrow and fear should keep them quiet. Let's see... the next in line is—",
    ["Dialogue2086602"]="(Ivy steps aside elegantly, clearing a path.)\nOkay, ever heard of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cyborg Dr. Millian</color>, the one who deals with artificial bodies? Zenlur is at her <color=#CA2E0AFF>clinic</color>. Go on, hope you find him in one piece. I mean, with all his organs and limbs, not <color=#CA2E0AFF>sold off</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2086603"]="(Enjoying your surprised look, Ivy glances evilly toward the clinic.)\nYup, only a fool with a brain full of muscle would believe there's a shortcut to body enhancement.",
    ["Dialogue2086604"]="Ah! Maybe there is.\n(Ivy grins like a mischievous kid with satisfaction.)\nCut off the limbs and swap them with steel or iron, easy.",
    ["Dialogue2086701"]="You...\n(In a hidden corner, the cyborg doctor eyes you suspiciously.)\nIt's you again?",
    ["Dialogue2086702"]="You know you are really getting on my nerves...\n(Milian soon regains her calm)\nSo, what do you want now?",
    ["Dialogue2086703"]="You mean that idiot?\n(Milian looks at Zenlur from afar skeptically.)\nIsn't he here for the body enhancement surgery?",
    ["Dialogue2086704"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2086705"]="Who told you that?\n(Milian stands with arms crossed, warily looking around.)\nThose hypocritical old guys from the Medical Association?",
    ["Dialogue2086706"]="Ha, reaching too far will get your hand chopped off.\n(Milian stands upright, her shadow looming in the sun.)\nThis is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>order from a rich neighborhood in Lighthalzen</color>, people we can't afford to cross.",
    ["Dialogue2086707"]="Just a few unnecessary organs, but they sell for a fortune. Who wouldn't want that? We finally have a suitable donor, so stay out of this. And this kid was referred to us; I didn't kidnap him.",
    ["Dialogue2086708"]="A <color=#CA2E0AFF>green-haired</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>noble</color>, really annoying. You better leave; we'll both be in trouble if this information finds its way on the street.",
    ["Dialogue2086801"]="I have no idea what happened... but...\n(Celia covers her face, crying through her fingers.)\nHe took my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Super Healing Pill</color>, and then he stopped breathing...",
    ["Dialogue2086802"]="(Ivy looks back at you, confused.)\nWhy are you staring at me? I didn't poison him this time.",
    ["Dialogue2086803"]="You... You poisoned him before?!\n(Celia's eyes fill with shock and guilt.)\nFrom the book you gave me...",
    ["Dialogue2086804"]="There were no poison recipes in it.\n(Ivy's expression becomes terrifying.)\nCelia, didn't you borrow it so we could work on new potions together?",
    ["Dialogue2086805"]="I...\n(Celia's face turns red, looking away.)",
    ["Dialogue2086806"]="Say something!\n(Ignoring you, Ivy forces Celia to look him in the eye.)",
    ["Dialogue2086807"]="Enough!\n(A sharp male voice interrupts their argument.)\nI need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lung Herb, Tranquil Mushroom, and Drake Blood</color> to restore his body functions. Who's going to get them?",
    ["Dialogue2086901"]="Fortunately, it's only a state of suspended animation. Celia, what did you give him?",
    ["Dialogue2086902"]="The Super Healing Pill is safe...\n(Celia pouts as you still look skeptical.)\nI removed the toxins, so it wasn't supposed to do this to him...",
    ["Dialogue2086903"]="(As all of you look confused, Celia starts listing rare and bizarre names.)\nOnly the finest materials! Mole eyes for night vision, Sky Deleter's stomach that can digest anything, Teddy Bear's hide for excellent cold resistance, Gig's fang for powerful bite... and so on...",
    ["Dialogue2086904"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2086905"]="Haha! So, Zenlur's body probably went into survival mode. Thankfully, the dose isn't too much, and he should <color=#CA2E0AFF>wake up</color> after taking the medicine... I guess?",
    ["Dialogue2086906"]="Isn't too much?\n(Celia looks up adorably, still counting on her fingers.)\nI also added <color=#CA2E0AFF>Allure Berry, Mystic Grass, and Lip Flower</color>! And there's more...",
    ["Dialogue2086907"]="Cough cough cough—\n(Ivy suddenly starts coughing.)\nThose are from the recipe book, don't tell me you put in...",
    ["Dialogue2086908"]="Yep... that one...\n(Celia fiddles with her fingers, not denying it.)\nThe one you highlighted in the book...",
    ["Dialogue2086909"]="That's because this potion <color=#CA2E0AFF>targets me</color>—hey, don't wake up now!\n(Ivy kicks the half-conscious Zenlur, his voice trembling slightly.)",
    ["Dialogue2086910"]="AHHH!!!\n(The young man grits his teeth in pain, about to get angry, but suddenly changes his attitude when he sees who hit him.)\nIvy... Hehe... I like you a lot...",
    ["Dialogue2086911"]="GET LOST!!! You! Hey Adventurer! Bury this guy!!!\n(Ivy grabs his coat and runs like he's seen something gross, still giving orders while running.)\nGet moving! Damn it! Celia, follow me!",
    ["Dialogue2086912"]="(Zenlur catches Ivy, clinging to him.)\nIvy... Hehe... Your smell... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I like it so much</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2086913"]="(Celia watches the overly \"affectionate\" pair sadly.)\nZenlur... why are you two... acting like this?",
    ["Dialogue2086914"]="What are you thinking, Celia?! Aaaah!!! Get away!!! Are you insane?!",
    ["Dialogue2086915"]="(Zenlur clings to Ivy like bubble gum, about to take the next step.)\nIvy... Ivy... Kiss-Kiss...",
    ["Dialogue2086916"]="<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>ABSOLUTELY NOOOOO!!! GET THE HELL OFF ME!!! NOW!!!</color></size>\n(In the tussle, Ivy's cries grow louder and louder.)",
    ["Dialogue2087001"]="(The elegant Bard quietly steps back, watching the drama with you, then suddenly smiles mysteriously.)\nAdventurer, why do you think Ivy's recipe book, which he lends to Celia, has a love potion targeted at him? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Was he... planning to use it on someone?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2087002"]="Young love is always full of twists and turns, but love is just the heart's flutter!\n(Orfeo intones poetically, watching the trio nearby.)\nPotion-induced love will always be undone by potions. O My!",
    ["Dialogue2087003"]="Hey Adventurer, we probably need to hold off on our trip until the potion's effects wear off.",
    ["Dialogue2087004"]="I don't know them.\n(Orfeo shakes his head.)\nHonestly, Trinity and I are just looking for a thrilling journey to inspire our wedding song.",
    ["Dialogue2087005"]="Trinity and Miss Goldie, it's time to go back.",
    ["Dialogue2087006"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Wait!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2087101"]="(Pushing Zenlur, Ivy sees him pass out from Goldie's strike, then looks around coldly, finally focusing on Goldie.)\nThanks, Goldie.",
    ["Dialogue2087102"]="It's not about you.\n(Goldie turns away, picking up the unconscious Zenlur.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>So, can we go now</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2087103"]="Miss Goldie, What are you doing?",
    ["Dialogue2087104"]="Shut up, you simp. Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>this rescue quest, is it for someone you care about</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2087105"]="Because I'm a thief...\n(The former thief, now a female Shadow Chaser, shakes her head.)\nOnce you learn to read people, it never goes away.",
    ["Dialogue2087106"]="(Goldie balances Zenlur on her back, looking at the varied expressions on her companions.)\nFrom the beginning, I knew this team's chemistry was as bad as a Thief Bug. No one cares about those poor souls in Lighthalzen as long as they get what they want—neither do I.",
    ["Dialogue2087107"]="But from now on, I'm going to make sure we move faster.\n(Goldie thumbs at you, lifting her chin slightly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>My friendship with this guy matters a bit more than the reward for now</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2087108"]="So, if anyone plans on hanging around here for months.\n(Goldie pulls out her weapon, the light of the cold blade reflecting on her face.)\nWhy don't you ask my \"friend\" here?",
    ["Dialogue2087201"]="How long do I have to wait? Do the surgery right now!",
    ["Dialogue2087202"]="It'll be done soon. Hey, you got any more Zeny? Fork it over!",
    ["Dialogue2087203"]="Is it for the surgery fee? Hold on, I'll be right back!",
    ["Dialogue2087204"]="Surgery fee? Where are you going? Faris!",
    ["Dialogue2087301"]="(In the wilds, Orfeo with a lute and tuner, talking to Trinity.)\nLoosen the string a bit, drop E to D... Okay, mute it, then loosen more... What's the deviation now?",
    ["Dialogue2087302"]="It's between -5 and 5.\n(Trinity adjusts the tuner, and you notice some pink gas slowly rising in the middle of their actions...)",
    ["Dialogue2087303"]="Adventurer?\n(Orfeo removes the tuner, strumming a few strings/)\nApologies, we were tuning up for the Steel Capital tour. Care to be our audience?",
    ["Dialogue2087304"]="Only amateur performers use the same songs for every tour.\n(Orfeoand and Trinity exchange a smile.)\nSince we're in Steel Capital, the theme is pretty obvious.",
    ["Dialogue2087305"]="Adventurer, I heard you're also investigating Rekenber. The survey we gathered for our tour might help you.",
    ["Dialogue2087306"]="(Orfeo shakes his tuner.)\nWe haven't gathered them all yet, not until we finish tuning the lute. If you're up for it—",
    ["Dialogue2087307"]="Foreman <color=#CA2E0AFF>Letom</color> from the East Factory, Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Casselir</color>, Journalist <color=#CA2E0AFF>Enchulo</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>W</color> from Kafra. Letom and Casselir should have their surveys done, but Enchulo and W might need more time.",
    ["Dialogue2087401"]="Get up, you slackers! This is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>rush order from Rekenber Corp</color>! Even with them taking 90%, isn't the triple pay enough to make you work? You bunch of lazy bums!",
    ["Dialogue2087402"]="Who are you?\n(Realizing you're intimidated, Letom narrows his eyes, sizing your weapon without a word.)\nAn Adventurer out there? You better stay out of this!",
    ["Dialogue2087403"]="(Letom casually digs into his pocket, bypassing you and cursing the workers.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>I don't have time to fill this</color>! If that dancer wasn't good-looking, I'd have slapped her! Now, get lost, don't waste my time!",
    ["Dialogue2087404"]="(Letom pauses for a second, then unleashes a truckload of curses.)\nHell with you! Trying to mess with me, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2087501"]="(Letom spits out his blood and takes out a crumpled survey from his pocket, filling it out quickly.)\nWhat a crappy day... There, happy now?!",
    ["Dialogue2087502"]="(Letom glares at you with malice as if engraving your face in his memory.)\nDon't force me! No matter what connection or power you have, in Einbroch, anyone who messes with Rekenber, be it their things or secrets, is dead!",
    ["Dialogue2087503"]="You want to stand up for them? It's futile! One group goes down, another replaces them, and if there's no one left, I'll step in!<color=#CA2E0AFF>Cross Rekenber and we'll be stuck with tiny workshop orders, making dolls and teddy bears.</color> Kids here don't celebrate Christmas anymore! When the factory closes tomorrow, and no one can't afford antidotes the day after, everyone will die in the streets!",
    ["Dialogue2087504"]="Go ask them if they want to keep working or be replaced!",
    ["Dialogue2087505"]="Take your <color=#CA2E0AFF>survey</color>—\n(Letom throws the survey at you.)\nAnd your heroism, leave now.",
    ["Dialogue2087601"]="(A blond, blue-eyed merchant stops you, taking a survey out of his pocket.)\nAre you looking for this?",
    ["Dialogue2087602"]="Orfeo told me about you. I'm his string supplier. Here.\n(Casselir moves closer.)\nOh, not leaving immediately? Seems you're curious about something else.",
    ["Dialogue2087603"]="Ah... that's beyond the survey. I must say, Orfeo's questions are very detailed; it'll take a long time to finish them.",
    ["Dialogue2087604"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Obviously not!</color> Hey, what's with that long face? Isn't it normal for merchants to refuse to give things away for free? If the price is right, the return is fair.",
    ["Dialogue2087605"]="I need <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 hearts from Earth Deleters</color>, the untainted ones.",
    ["Dialogue2087606"]="Tsk, tsk, tsk... A top-notch seller never questions the buyer's purpose. Adventurer, I didn't ask why you're looking into Rekenber, right?",
    ["Dialogue2087701"]="Such lively organs, shielded by deformed ones, work hard to keep the host alive. Even though they're dragon hearts, they might be better than human hearts.",
    ["Dialogue2087702"]="(Casselir hums while sealing the dragon hearts.)\nHave you heard of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Senet Celtier Institute</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2087703"]="Even though it's known as a research institute, back during the warring period, it was more of a weapons supplier, sometimes even determining the outcome of battles.",
    ["Dialogue2087704"]="(Casselir smiles wryly.)\nImagine a warhead the size of a dragon's heart releasing radiation enough to kill a small town. The Senet Celtier Institute, the predecessor to Rekenber, no one knows where their groundbreaking tech came from. They seemed to appear out of thin air, pushing history forward with a brutal force.",
    ["Dialogue2087705"]="Not only that, but the institute also chose <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Tyr's Hand\"</color> from many factions offering alliances. After countless collaborations and takeovers, our founding father—then leader of \"Tyr's Hand,\" Lord Tyr—prevailed and founded the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Schwarzwald Republic</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2087706"]="As a core ally of the founding father, the institute grew and rebranded to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber</color>. Their relationship with the Republic became deeply entrenched through generations of leaders. Their business expansion department then took over the airship, railway manufacturing, and basic industry construction, becoming the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Republic's biggest business giant</color>——an unshakable titan.",
    ["Dialogue2087707"]="Sadly, when our Republic is brought up, people probably think of Rekenber's power players rather than the Lord.",
    ["Dialogue2087708"]="Fascinated? The story of Rekenber is common knowledge but does just telling a piece of it to an outsider have this much effect?",
    ["Dialogue2087709"]="Thanks for your patronage!!!",
    ["Dialogue2087801"]="(Orfeo smiles and accepts the survey.)\nDid you find what you were looking for?",
    ["Dialogue2087802"]="None of them complete it?\n(Orfeo looks puzzled as he opens the survey, a vein elegantly pulsing on his forehead.)\nThey really are something, aren't they?",
    ["Dialogue2087803"]="You've been a big help...\n(Orfeo exhales deeply, looking at you with gratitude.)\nNow, it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Enchulo and W</color>. They're trustworthy, so we should get some useful answers.",
    ["Dialogue2087804"]="No ifs.\n(Orfeo tightens his grip on the paper, his threatening words piercing the air.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Even a wooden lute hurts when it hits your head, right?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2087901"]="Hey, it's you!\n(Enchulo locks eyes with you and grabs your shoulder like a hungry tiger.)\nDon't—You—Go—",
    ["Dialogue2087902"]="You—you know someone at the Lord's Mansion, don't you? My people saw you leaving with Philodis! Ahhh—you got to help me!",
    ["Dialogue2087903"]="Tailing isn't stalking! To get to the bottom of this story, the entire newspaper is on board. The whole Lord's Mansion area is under Libet Express' watch! As soon as the target shows up... Hah, we'll get them.",
    ["Dialogue2087904"]="What's the problem? Such a big scoop; if I, Enchulo, can't get to the bottom of it, then it's gonna be a real problem! I was this close; why wouldn't they let me in?!",
    ["Dialogue2087905"]="So, when are you <color=#CA2E0AFF>returning to the Lord's Mansion</color>?\n(Enchulo proudly fixes his collar but nervously watches your every reaction.)\nMaybe... take me with you?",
    ["Dialogue2087906"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Survey? This?</color>\n(Enchulo rummages through his pockets and bag, pulling out a folded paper.)\nThe questions were so detailed that I thought it was a competitor intel spying. So it's just a survey...",
    ["Dialogue2087907"]="(Enchulo looks at you cautiously.)\nIf I fill it out properly, can you take me in...?",
    ["Dialogue2087908"]="Awesome! Please let Lord Carl know that Libet Express wants to publish a special interview about his friendship with President Rowland. Our readers, his citizens, are very curious about his opinion on Rekenber, especially with <color=#CA2E0AFF>President Rowland being out of the public eye for so long</color>. If possible, we'd like to give him some letters we've received from the public.",
    ["Dialogue2087909"]="(Enchulo speaks quietly, passing you a letter.)\nThis is a complaint letter against Rekenber. It's only one of many. It doesn't involve the higher-ups, but we can't overlook what's inside.",
    ["Dialogue2089001"]="(Lord Carl finishes reading the letter with a grave look, and after a long silence, you hear a heavy sigh.)\nThis is likely just a glimpse of Einbroch's dark side. How many more letters like this exist?",
    ["Dialogue2089002"]="Perhaps more than we can imagine. Adventurer, now more than ever, I hope our efforts will disperse the smog hanging over Einbroch, even if it only gives the struggling citizens a bit of brief.",
    ["Dialogue2089003"]="The smog in the sky is easy to clear, but what about the one in our hearts? Tell that reporter I've heard their voices. Please trust that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Republic will do its best to protect its people</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2089004"]="Please trust Philodis and me. Even if we can't bring down Rekenber yet, we'll keep resisting in the shadows, building up for the next fight.",
    ["Dialogue2089005"]="Regarding the interview, I haven't seen <color=#CA2E0AFF>President Rowland for a long time, and I'm not sure if he's even okay</color>. Speaking out now could jeopardize our actions, and the newspaper publishing the interview would be implicated.",
    ["Dialogue2089101"]="... Be implicated?\n(Enchulo's face becomes serious.)\nI understand... Knowing the Lord's attitude is more important than the interview itself.",
    ["Dialogue2089102"]="Ha, don't underestimate my journalistic instincts!\n(Enchulo pats your shoulder with confidence.)\nEven a street quarrel can uncover a great story if you dig into it!",
    ["Dialogue2089103"]="Plus, as a veteran journalist, knowing when to shut up... Ahem, anyway, I'll forget everything I heard today. Let's get back to your initial request! <color=#CA2E0AFF>You want the survey, right? Here!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2089201"]="Adventurer!\n(W rushes over, bows quickly, and starts to leave.)\nSorry! I'm in a big crisis and can't chat with you right now!",
    ["Dialogue2089202"]="Ahhh! A batch of company <color=#CA2E0AFF>cargo was held up at the Border Inspection Station</color>! If we didn't get the paperwork, the loss would be more than W could ever cover...",
    ["Dialogue2089203"]="Android maids! People here buy androids to serve them, right? Our products are fine, but recently, the import-export restrictions on androids tightened, so we didn't have enough paperwork when the shipment arrived...",
    ["Dialogue2089204"]="(W lowers her head, her golden pigtails sagging.)\nThe company wanted to use foreign androids to break through Rekenber and local firms' blockade, but we were just a bit short.",
    ["Dialogue2089205"]="The one from Trinity? Yep, it's done!\n(W gives you the survey, definitely the neatest you've collected by far.)\nSorry, Adventurer, I gotta go!",
    ["Dialogue2089301"]="(The chief inspector points at the mountain of cargo, glaring at you two.)\nIs the paperwork ready?",
    ["Dialogue2089302"]="Apologies. We have the company's documents, but the customs clearance is just a temporary permit. The full paperwork will take another month...",
    ["Dialogue2089303"]="(W winks adorably.)\nBut for companies that meet the customs duty quota and have no violations, shouldn't the Republic have some preferential policies? Like flexible processing or extensions...?",
    ["Dialogue2089304"]="Nope, the benefits only apply to local companies! Even if it goes through, your shipments are marked as foreign, not domestic. <color=#CA2E0AFF>The stamp is the only thing we go after!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2089305"]="Huh? These shipments are totally safe. The paperwork was complete when they left the port. Is it really our fault if policy changes during the long shipping process?",
    ["Dialogue2089306"]="Hmph, slick talker.",
    ["Dialogue2089307"]="(The inspectors exchange a look and approach.)\nYou make a fair point. If you're willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pay a stamping fee...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2089308"]="(The inspector fiddles with the small stamp in his hand.)\nEverything can be fixed before the stamp goes down.",
    ["Dialogue2089309"]="Inspector accounts get randomly checked, so we only take bartering. The rich in the city are crazy about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rainbow Feathers</color> lately. Get us some, and the fee is waived.",
    ["Dialogue2089401"]="W's survey brought up a lot of unknown details—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim's R&D Dept Sector One, Two, and Three</color>... As another major company, Kafra's been collecting info on their competitors as well...",
    ["Dialogue2089402"]="That's right. After the founding, Rekensheim took over the role of Senet Celtier Institute. Today's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Capital Institute came from Rekensheim's R&D Dept Sector Two. Lighthalzen holds the most secretive Sector Three. As for the best but now abandoned Sector One</color>, well...",
    ["Dialogue2089403"]="Orfeo! Trinity!",
    ["Dialogue2089404"]="Looks like the audience can't wait any longer.\n(Orfeo closes the survey, seeming to have memorized everything, and gracefully nods to you.)\nLet the music handle the rest.",
    ["Dialogue2089501"]="Back off! Back off!\n (The Defense Force Soldier comes at you with his weapon, and behind him, the eerie <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dimensional Gap</color> closes and reopens.)\n This isn't a place for adventuring, huh? Who are you?",
    ["Dialogue2089502"]="I see. You're the hero honored by the royal family! But...\n (The Defense Force Soldier hesitates and stands in your way, clearly not willing to let you pass.)\n Apologies, but even you aren't allowed here.",
    ["Dialogue2089503"]="Something like a Dimensional Gap has shown up here, so we've been given the order to guard it to prevent anyone from getting close. We might need your help, Adventurer, but you'll need to get approval from our boss in Prontera...",
    ["Dialogue2089504"]="However, plenty of <color=#CA2E0AFF>scholars and professors</color> have been drawn here. If you're looking for details, they're camping just outside!",
    ["Dialogue2089601"]="(Fulkyn is playing with the Mysterious Device, looking like he's been alone even before you met him.)\n Surprised to run into you here. Are you here to check out the Dimensional Gap too?",
    ["Dialogue2089602"]="Is there anything else in Glast Heim worth my time apart from the Dimensional Gap?\n (Fulkyn shoots an irritated look towards the Defense Force Soldier.)\n Hmph, they'll regret turning me down!",
    ["Dialogue2089603"]="Don't bother.\n (Fulkyn looks away.)\n I don't want to have anything to do with the kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue2089604"]="Moreover——\n (Fulkyn gazes intently at your armor and weapons.)\n They're not the only ones who can help...",
    ["Dialogue2089605"]="I predict that the Dimensional Gap in Glast Heim is just the first, not the last.\n (Fulkyn proudly pats his Mysterious Device.)\n My device has pinpointed <color=#CA2E0AFF>where the next Dimensional Gap will appear</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2089606"]="What's that look? Questioning my findings? Even though it's just getting started, I can handle measuring the spacetime stability around here and finding the biggest fluctuation point. If you are in doubt, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come see me at Geffen tomorrow</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2089607"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2089608"]="Okay then! If you go to Geffen to validate my theory, I'll publish some essays anonymously after the research. Dimensional Gaps have always been a way for monsters to reach Midgard. If studying them helps ordinary people who have been plundered by monsters, it's still in line with my original purpose.",
    ["Dialogue2089701"]="(Fulkyn looks at the wand pointed at his throat, speaking coldly.)\n Threatening my life without any proof, is this how the Mage Guild treats their guests?",
    ["Dialogue2089702"]="You and this device were around before the Dimensional Gap appeared, and it doesn't even surprise you.\n (Sparks flicker from Jesqurienne's wand.)\n According to my crystal ball, you've been using this device to scan and record things.",
    ["Dialogue2089703"]="I need the data to test my theory, but I wouldn't artificially create a Dimensional Gap. Adventurer, since you're here, explain it to her.",
    ["Dialogue2089704"]="So, you're backing him up?\n (Jesqurienne puts away her wand, appearing to assess your credibility.)",
    ["Dialogue2089705"]="I can believe you for now, but Fulkyn has to leave Geffen immediately and let the mages from the Mage Tower take over, including this Dimensional Gap. If it turns out his actions are tied to the Dimensional Gap's creation, Adventurer, your word and reputation will be invalid.",
    ["Dialogue2089706"]="(Jesqurienne steps aside, making way.)\n Sir, you may leave now.",
    ["Dialogue2089707"]="Let's go, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2089708"]="Shouldn't we stick together to meet Master Jesqurienne's expectations? The next Dimensional Gap will appear at... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color>? I'll be there waiting for you <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomorrow</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2089801"]="(A startled Fulkyn sits on the ground; his hands, protecting his head, are bloodied.)\n The last two were only Dimensional Gaps, but now... there are monsters.",
    ["Dialogue2089802"]="(Fulkyn quickly wipes the blood off his hands with a grim expression.)\n It doesn't matter. What's important is why these Scavengers showed up. They're not from Prontera. I wonder... Are they passively drawn by the Dimensional Gap's energy, or is something actively summoning them?",
    ["Dialogue2089803"]="If they're passively drawn, we can estimate the threat level by the monster count and assume the other side isn't hostile for now; maybe it's just a coincidence. But if it's on purpose...",
    ["Dialogue2089804"]="(Gleaming blades spring from the Mysterious Device, gradually moving towards the monster's corpse.)\n Let's check if they have any useful clues...",
    ["Dialogue2089805"]="... Obviously.\n (Fulkyn, facing away, operates the Mysterious Device with his ears blushing.)\n I only got caught because I couldn't remember how to turn on defense mode.",
    ["Dialogue2089806"]="The next Dimensional Gap is at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>. Make sure you're there on time.",
    ["Dialogue2089901"]="(With huge dark circles, Fulkyn nods and pulls up the report from the Mysterious Device.)\n Things don’t look good. These monsters' central nervous systems show they were in intense excitement during their last hour. This isn't something that happens randomly.",
    ["Dialogue2089902"]="Monsters around Prontera are generally weak, and no powerful monsters have been reported moving in. They must be here due to a strong influence from the other side of the Dimensional Gap. Monsters are attracted to power, especially weaker ones. If there's a hostile entity, they'll be the first to follow through.",
    ["Dialogue2089903"]="Plus, this Dimensional Gap has a bigger impact on spacetime stability than the last ones... Ahem, Adventurer, do you hear that?",
    ["Dialogue2090001"]="(Just before the last strike, Fulkyn suddenly grabs your sleeve, and the wounded Hornet runs away.)\n Stop it! You can't kill them all!",
    ["Dialogue2090002"]="(Grabbing you exhausted all his strength, and Fulkyn's face turns pale)\n Hornets... are highly communal monsters... so... cough, cough... there has to be...",
    ["Dialogue2090003"]="During the battle... I... sprinkled some powder. Let's go, follow me...",
    ["Dialogue20901001"]="<color=#ffe788>The Mutant Dragonoid is striking you with its<color=#ff5252> corresponding attribute</color> damage. Quick! Avoid it with an <color=#528fff>attribute counter</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901002"]="<color=#ffe788>The battlefield's <color=#ff5252>temperature</color> is overheated! Dragon Flame Volcano is stirring. We're too late!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901004"]="<color=#ffe788>Gather your party first!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901005"]="<color=#ffe788>Summon<color=#ff5252> a fire dragon and ride it over the valley!</color></color>",
    ["Dialogue20901006"]="<color=#ffe788>The slumbering <color=#ff5252>Guardian of Ice Valley</color> has awoken!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901007"]="<color=#ffe788>The slumbering <color=#ff5252>Guardian of the Glaciers</color> has awoken!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901008"]="<color=#ffe788>Watch out for falling ice to the left! Control your dragon to <color=#528fff>lean right</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue20901009"]="<color=#ffe788>Watch out for falling ice to the right! Control your dragon to <color=#528fff>lean left</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2090101"]="I'm just a bit tired... I'll be fine after a break...",
    ["Dialogue20901010"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#528fff>Disable auto battle</color> before mounting your dragon!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2090102"]="(Fulkyn immediately dozes off on your back, looking like he hasn't slept in a long time.)\n Zzzzz...",
    ["Dialogue2090103"]="(Fulkyn immediately dozes off on the grass, looking like he hasn't slept in a long time.)\n Zzzzz...",
    ["Dialogue2090104"]="(After a while, you spot the Mysterious Device, always with Fulkyn rolling in from the horizon with its top sensor flickering, speaking in a chilly robotic tone.)\n Command timeout... Initiating secondary calculation procedure... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tomorrow's Dimensional Gap Location: Sograt Desert</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2090105"]="Calculation complete. Load and initiate tomorrow's research plan? Estimated remaining time: 0h 57min. Completed: 12h 18min.",
    ["Dialogue2090201"]="Desert Wolf... From the Scavenger below to the Hornet above and now the wolves in the desert, the impact from the other side of the Dimensional Gap is getting stronger. If it keeps going, we can't handle the consequences. Even though I hate dealing with officials, I must report this to the local lord.",
    ["Dialogue2090202"]="Looks like it. The Sograt Desert leads to Morroc and Payon. I'll go to Morroc, and you take care of Payon. Once we've reported to the lord, let's meet at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon West</color>, where the next Dimensional Gap is expected.",
    ["Dialogue2090203"]="(Fulkyn coughs lightly after giving out all instructions.)\n Just so you know, falling asleep yesterday was accidental, okay? But thanks for not letting that Mysterious Device drag me up in the middle of the night for more research.",
    ["Dialogue2090204"]="I just want to solve the mystery quickly.\n (Fulkyn's expression becomes serious.)\n My scholar's intuition tells me we're close to the truth.",
    ["Dialogue2090301"]="My father is supervising new recruits in Archer Village, so it might take a while for him to return.\n (Seeing how weary you look, the young man remarks.)\n What happened?",
    ["Dialogue2090302"]="(Sun Euin looks at the bodyguard, who hands over a kingdom map.)\n Here, here, and here... Can you tell me more about the Dimensional Gap, Adventurer? I'll dispatch more soldiers to reinforce and have my father back as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue2090303"]="Hold on.\n (Sun Euin stares at the markings on the map.)\n Their shapes...",
    ["Dialogue2090304"]="My apologies, I've been tied up with affairs at the manor. This shape looks familiar, but I can't recall from where. Did that scholar mention a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dimensional Gap will show up in Payon West tomorrow</color>? Perhaps we'll uncover something new.",
    ["Dialogue2090401"]="Here you are, Adventurer.\n (Fulkyn points at the pile of monster corpses on the ground.)\n Seems like our hard work wasn't for nothing.",
    ["Dialogue2090402"]="A bunch of monsters drawn by the Dimensional Gap attempted to plunder Hidden Wood Village. Thankfully, the soldiers on duty stopped them. The lord of Payon will be grateful.",
    ["Dialogue2090403"]="Lord Maximilian promised to fight side by side with his people. In the barren lands of Morroc, that's about the best a lord can do. I believe I've figured out the pattern of these Dimensional Gaps.",
    ["Dialogue2090404"]="(Fulkyn points at the sky.)\n It's the star patterns. I've tried different rules to deduce the order of the Dimensional Gap but found nothing. The reason I could predict the next location was because of the powerful calculations of the Mysterious Device, which instantly calculated fluctuations in spacetime stability across areas to determine the coordinates with the highest chance of creating a Dimensional Gap.",
    ["Dialogue2090405"]="Running calculations day and night required constant commands. On the fourth day, I passed out outdoors and woke up at night under a sky full of stars. That's when another idea hit me.",
    ["Dialogue2090406"]="Adventurer, have you, by any chance, connected the six Dimensional Gap locations on a map? They form a pattern...",
    ["Dialogue2090407"]="Are you telling me that Sun Euin has seen this pattern? That's interesting. Based on the predictions, <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomorrow's Dimensional Gap will be in Payon</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2090501"]="Following the seventh Dimensional Gap, my device didn't pick up any more abnormal spacetime fluctuations. This should be the final location. Adventurer, I couldn't have done all this without you.",
    ["Dialogue2090502"]="(Fulkyn bows to you.)\n Now, show us the last piece of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>puzzle</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2090601"]="According to the Euin family's ancient tome, <color=#CA2E0AFF>North Stars</color> is the constellation that governs death. What's going on? Adventurer, I don't know what it means that these Dimensional Gaps are following the stars, but it can't be good. Who is on the other side of these Dimensional Gaps?",
    ["Dialogue2090602"]="Calm down...\n (Fulkyn repeats the unfamiliar name, then meets your gaze.)\n So, is the other side of the Dimensional Gap bound to come and bring us death?",
    ["Dialogue2090603"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Along with death, there's fate</color>.\n (Sky Euin shakes his head.)\n Whoever is beyond the Dimensional Gap must carry a fate tied to the North Stars.",
    ["Dialogue2090604"]="And this fate is connected to death.",
    ["Dialogue2090605"]="I'm afraid that there is more than one entity tied to this fate.\n (Fulkyn looks around and speaks slowly.)\n In fact, my device picked up more than one presence around the Dimensional Gap.",
    ["Dialogue2090606"]="Besides the aura that draws in monsters, there's another, an aura of justice. If the enemy from the other side is destined to come to Midgard, I believe \"he\" will be our savior. And if \"he\" fails—",
    ["Dialogue2090607"]="Then, it might be time for the Adventurer to step up once again.",
    ["Dialogue2090701"]="The grand tour! Up close and personal! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orfeo & Trinity</color>—the only official organizers! Grab your tickets fast!",
    ["Dialogue2090702"]="(A cheerful merchant eagerly hands you a flyer.)\nHey, check this out, guests! Orfeo and Trinity are the biggest names in town—this tour's gonna be legendary!",
    ["Dialogue2090703"]="You seem to be on a trip! Gilded Rose is the official partner of these maestros. Who knows, maybe one day we'll have a shop near you too!",
    ["Dialogue2090704"]="(As people cram together, you barely manage to escape.)\nCareful, careful... watch your steps! Move back; there's plenty of room!",
    ["Dialogue2090801"]="Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2090802"]="(Malam spots the Gilded Rose flyer and chuckles knowingly.)\nOrfeo and Trinity are top-tier partners for Gilded Rose in the art world. Their tour is the biggest event in Rachel right now. Guess today's chat won't have to be all serious.",
    ["Dialogue2090803"]="About this...\n(Malam glances around, lowering the voice)\nNot yet.",
    ["Dialogue2090804"]="Keep your voice down! You want customers to riot on us? They're okay, I swear! It's just that Einbroch had a <color=#CA2E0AFF>toxic spill</color>, and now the whole area is under <color=#CA2E0AFF>travel restrictions</color>. They had to <color=#CA2E0AFF>postpone</color> their schedule.",
    ["Dialogue2090805"]="Orfeo sent me a letter, promising they'd be here before the performance. If you know them, they never return on their word. Einbroch's got railroads everywhere—they'll get here, no doubt.",
    ["Dialogue2090806"]="Oh? You know something else?\n(Malam leans in, eyes gleaming with interest.)\nCome on, spill it. What is it?",
    ["Dialogue2090807"]="Hah... forget it.\n(Malam smirks, shutting down the conversation with an odd proverb.)\n\"Don't thirst for your neighbor's spring... unless your own oasis has dried up.\"",
    ["Dialogue2090808"]="Seems like one of those \"the less you know, the better\" situations.\n(Malam shrugs and drops an odd proverb instead.)\n\"In the face of a sandstorm, one camel is no different from a thousand.\"",
    ["Dialogue2090809"]="(Malam notices your concern and gives your shoulder a light tap.)\nHey, instead of worrying, how about you lend me a hand? Think of it as doing a favor for Orfeo and Trinity.",
    ["Dialogue2090810"]="(Malam dramatically waves toward Rachel.)\nA land this dazzling—don't you think it should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>featured in their grand performance</color>? If you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some useful performance material</color>, their show will be even more breathtaking when you finally see them!",
    ["Dialogue2090811"]="Check out the archives in the Temple! Foreigners can only read our founding history and the Pope's Hymn, but that's plenty of inspiration. Anything beyond that... That's for an Adventurer to figure out.",
    ["Dialogue2090901"]="(Wolmas seems taken aback by your presence.)\nI was told you had set out beyond the kingdom. Have you found what you sought?",
    ["Dialogue2090902"]="(Wolmas' face stiffens, his lips curling slightly as he slowly repeats the name.)\nThat's what they say in Arunafeltz? Saint? Do they really think Isumia was a saint?",
    ["Dialogue2090903"]="Hmm...\n(After a moment of silence, Wolmas smirks, making a wry remark.)\nIf the \"heretic\" I remember is the same person you call a \"saint,\" then yeah, I'd say I know her.",
    ["Dialogue2090904"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Isumia the Heretic</color>—she's in every religious history book. Any priest-in-training will read about her. And she wasn't alone—Akshay, Eryxis, Maruta, Karsis, and so on...",
    ["Dialogue2090905"]="(His tone remains cold, yet his words expose a stark contrast to the reverence these names held in Arunafeltz.)\nThey refused to submit to Odin, instead choosing to worship Freyja, a symbol of impurity and desire. They led lives of decadence, lured their followers into sin, and used the false name of \"holy war\" to rebel against Odin's will!",
    ["Dialogue2090906"]="They chased pleasure, never knowing the cost of sacrifice. Odin's mercy spared them from execution, but they were cast out, never to find refuge here again. And their fate after that? You've been to Arunafeltz—you tell me.",
    ["Dialogue2090907"]="Exiled in <color=#CA2E0AFF>A.W. 400</color>, they wandered into the northwestern lands of nomads. To survive, they <color=#CA2E0AFF>glorified their alchemy as \"Freyja's Gift,\"</color> arrogantly <color=#CA2E0AFF>proclaiming themselves as prophets, even popes</color>. By <color=#CA2E0AFF>A.W. 414, their kingdom was found</color>. This is the true history of Arunafeltz—a kingdom founded on heresy and fraud!",
    ["Dialogue2090908"]="Well, which side of history do you believe?\n(Wolmas exhales, hands behind his back.)\nIf you want answers, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>descendants of the nomads</color>—they know what it means to be exiled.",
    ["Dialogue2091001"]="It's not about the money. What's at stake here is our <color=#CA2E0AFF>reputation</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2091002"]="The kingdom should at least offer an answer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Why did Orfeo and Trinity cancel at the last minute?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2091003"]="The kingdom will cover all your losses. But aside from money, we <color=#CA2E0AFF>have nothing to say</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2091004"]="Ha... money? You might've forgotten just who controls commerce in Arunafeltz. But sure, if you want to make this about money, Gilded Rose is happy to play along.",
    ["Dialogue2091005"]="I doubt this is what your backers expected, Mr. Malam.",
    ["Dialogue2091006"]="The ones who gave me power expect me to bring prosperity to Arunafeltz. Whether it's through diplomacy, dominance, or sheer force... I believe the same applies to you, doesn't it?",
    ["Dialogue2091007"]="... I'll take my leave.",
    ["Dialogue2091101"]="(Syphus looks at you, disbelief in his eyes. Since Juno, he seems more drained than ever.)\nOf all places... we meet here. Lucky? Unlucky? Either way, I assume you caught that conversation.",
    ["Dialogue2091102"]="(Syphus pulls an empty cigarette box from his pocket, then sighs and tucks it away.)\nIt's not just them... it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>everyone </color>.",
    ["Dialogue2091103"]="The entire dispatch team—Orfeo, Trinity, Zenlur, Celia, Ivy, Goldie... all of them are <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>missing</color></size>.",
    ["Dialogue2091104"]="Don't look at me like that. To find them, I pulled strings to get a month's worth of recovery potions—I haven't slept since. I tracked them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color> because it was the <color=#CA2E0AFF>last place they mentioned</color> in the letter.",
    ["Dialogue2091105"]="(Syphus pulls out a wrinkled letter, notes and symbols scribbled all over.)\nWell, so much for keeping things classified.",
    ["Dialogue2091201"]="They should've made it to Lighthalzen by now... and we should've received another letter. But...",
    ["Dialogue2091202"]="(Syphus, weary and bloodshot, stares hard at the inn.)\nThere's a secret in that <color=#CA2E0AFF>inn</color>—something we're missing.",
    ["Dialogue2091203"]="You're saying we should investigate in secret?\n(Syphus shakes his head, disapproving.)\nThat's too risky. The kingdom and Arunafeltz aren't exactly on good terms.",
    ["Dialogue2091204"]="The Republic? Huh, so you've got connections to Lord Carl... Fine. I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>blend in as a tourist and stay</color> at the inn too. Just promise me this—if you find something, let me know first.",
    ["Dialogue2091301"]="(The attendant's eyes dart over your equipment before his tone becomes even more welcoming.)\nHonored guest! Will you be staying alone? How long? Our finest suite is still available, and just for you, it's 20% off!",
    ["Dialogue2091302"]="A <size=26>prestigious customer!!!</size> We also offer the finest crispy pastries, roasted camel hump, and the cactus honey drink—interested?",
    ["Dialogue2091303"]="(The attendant grins from ear to ear, looking ready to kneel down and introduce you to every single service there has to offer.)\nExcellent choice! Any other requests? I'll have your room cleaned and prepped right away—you can settle in as soon as you finish your meal!",
    ["Dialogue2091304"]="(The attendant pauses, then smoothly slips back into his professional demeanor.)\nAh, I'm just in charge of check-ins. If you need to ask about people, you'll want to talk to our boss. Boss—<color=#CA2E0AFF><size=26>Boss!!!</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue2091401"]="(The innkeeper exchanges a glance with the attendant before getting an earful of whispered info.)\nAhhh, so you've got questions? Lucky for you, I've been keeping tabs on every guest coming through here. Go on, ask away—I probably have your answer!",
    ["Dialogue2091402"]="(The innkeeper listens carefully, nodding along.)\nOh... yeah, I know who you're talking about. But before I say more, I gotta ask—what's your business with them? We respect our guests' privacy. So, what's your <color=#CA2E0AFF>relationship</color> to them?",
    ["Dialogue2091403"]="I see... Yeah, they did ask for paper and a pen to send a letter. That means you were the recipient, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2091404"]="What?!!\n(The innkeeper's gaze flicks to your weapon, visibly nervous.)\nAhhh, now that explains it—that Thief girl had a real sour face when she left. Guess she knew trouble was coming!",
    ["Dialogue2091405"]="(With a thoughtful look, the innkeeper starts piecing things together.)\nYeah, they came in as a group—six of them. But I wouldn't call them friends. Once it got late, they all <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2091406"]="That white-haired youngster was dead set on heading to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color> for a fight, and the blonde girl wasn't letting him go off without her.",
    ["Dialogue2091407"]="That fancy green-haired gentleman booked out the finest bathhouse suite. When he came out and saw those two missing, he freaked, chugged some stealth potion, and probably ran after them.",
    ["Dialogue2091408"]="Then there was the lovey-dovey couple. They hired a guide from us and asked specifically to see the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple and Holy Spring</color>, saying they needed \"inspiration\" for their performance.",
    ["Dialogue2091409"]="That's me! But that day, there was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>child abduction</color>. They stepped in, saved the kid, and had me take her somewhere safe. After that... I don't know what went down.",
    ["Dialogue2091410"]="Hehe... Need a guide? Meals, entertainment, and the VIP experience are all yours for a low price of 998 Zeny!",
    ["Dialogue2091411"]="(Seeing the Zeny, the innkeeper perks up, words spilling faster.)\nYou're alright, you are! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Thief girl seemed the most harmless </color>of the six. But... she's the only one checking out. The others never made it back that night.",
    ["Dialogue2091412"]="(Seeing you lost in thought, the sharp-eyed innkeeper nudges the attendant.)\nSanji! Quit spacing out! Get moving and take the guest to that kid already!",
    ["Dialogue2091413"]="Ah! This way, please.",
    ["Dialogue2091501"]="(The innocent little girl beams at you.)\nOh! I remember you, you brought me back.",
    ["Dialogue2091502"]="Hi there, Aisha. Do you recall the people who scared off the bad people?",
    ["Dialogue2091503"]="Of course! They were super good-looking! One had a big instrument, and the other had a whip—they chased the bad guys so far away!",
    ["Dialogue2091504"]="They went to...\n(Aisha holds her head, thinking for a moment.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>An alley with a bunch of people standing guard</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2091505"]="Ehh... sir, are you sure you wanna keep looking into this?",
    ["Dialogue2091506"]="(The attendant sighs, dragging you away so the little girl won't hear.)\nThat alley's just a cover... It leads straight to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color>—exactly where that white-haired brat wanted to go!",
    ["Dialogue2091507"]="I'm telling you, those guys are ruthless. And their boss? Untouchable. Even if someone dies and it gets reported, the only one getting punished is the one who reported it!",
    ["Dialogue2091508"]="(The attendant stamped his foot.)\nMy goodness, are you still planning on going? You certainly don't look short on Zeny, so why risk your life? Besides, the person you're looking for never came back from the arena, and... and who's gonna pay the bill if you can't make it back?!",
    ["Dialogue2091509"]="This isn't about Zeny!",
    ["Dialogue2091510"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2091511"]="O-Okay... I'll wait for you. But listen—you're <color=#CA2E0AFF>on your own</color> from here...",
    ["Dialogue2091601"]="You again!!!",
    ["Dialogue2091602"]="Get lost! No fights today—registration's closed until further notice!\n(Noticing you still standing there, the gatekeeper sighs, irritated.)\nWhat do you want?",
    ["Dialogue2091603"]="(The second the words \"white-haired boy\" leave your mouth, the gatekeeper's face turns grim. He quickly moves behind the bouncers, suddenly wary.)\nWell, well... you just asked the wrong question. Boss says no exceptions, even if you've got ties to the Gilded Rose. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Finish things up!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2091701"]="(Curled up in fear, the gatekeeper's gaze remains fixed on the crystal in your hand.)\nNo! That's mine! Give it back!",
    ["Dialogue2091702"]="(The gatekeeper stiffens, trying to get up for another fight.)\nThe boss gave it to me!",
    ["Dialogue2091703"]="(The guard screams in agony.)\nArghhh! I don't know! We just take care of the mess afterward!",
    ["Dialogue2091704"]="I have no idea! The boss always offers top fighters <color=#CA2E0AFF>a drink</color>. Once they're done, they get taken away, and we just handle the aftermath. If things get messy... we might find something valuable...",
    ["Dialogue2091705"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Outside the city</color>! But I don't know what happens there! Even asking about it can cost me my life! I'd rather not die!",
    ["Dialogue2091706"]="Things got strange lately—some <color=#CA2E0AFF>artists</color> ruined our business. The big shots got beat up, and before skipping town, they told us to keep our heads down. I swear, I don't know where they are now.",
    ["Dialogue2091707"]="I'll keep my mouth shut! I promise no one will hear about this! Just let us go!",
    ["Dialogue2091708"]="If anyone finds out, my crew won't live to see tomorrow either. We're in this together...",
    ["Dialogue2091801"]="(The attendants visibly ease up when they see you're unharmed.)\nAhh, you're alright! Good. The boss asked me to pass something on—he just recalled something important that might help.",
    ["Dialogue2091802"]="(The attendant nods toward a masked figure in the corner—it's Syphus, your contact in disguise.)\nOn the night they disappeared, near dawn, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>masked stranger</color> came to the inn too.",
    ["Dialogue2091803"]="He stayed right next door to the Thief girl. <color=#CA2E0AFF>They checked out one after the other</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2091804"]="Since it was nearly dawn, the boss didn't really think about it. He only remembered after that strange guest checked in just now. Huh... why is he watching us and leaving?",
    ["Dialogue2091805"]="That's... hard to say. If he's not in the city, then he must've headed out. Maybe check with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>guard</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2091901"]="(Syphus keeps just enough distance, acting like a stranger asking for directions.)\nNo worries. No one's tailing us.",
    ["Dialogue2091902"]="(After listening to your intel, Syphus gives a short nod.)\nI'll handle the Underground Arena. The gatekeeper might be useful... If he doesn't, I'll get rid of him.",
    ["Dialogue2091903"]="As for investigating outside the city... Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>not every guard out there is working for the city</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2091904"]="Rekenber guards are stationed here, within Rachel's territory. Tell me—do you really think Malam, for all his influence, could manage something like that?",
    ["Dialogue2091905"]="A fusion of politics, business, and military strength... what follows is a darkness beyond measure.\n(With a respectful step back, Syphus bows to you.)\nGood luck, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2092001"]="Is there a problem?",
    ["Dialogue2092002"]="Masked strangers? Not a chance—Rachel keeps its gates secure. But there was a Thief girl... She was frantic, desperate to get out. Said if we didn't let her pass, she'd draw her dagger.",
    ["Dialogue2092003"]="(With a nod, the guard sighs, his expression softening.)\nShe acted tough, but her face looked like she was about to break down if we stopped her. Probably rushing home for an emergency...",
    ["Dialogue2092004"]="Ah, I remember now! She specifically said she was taking the <color=#CA2E0AFF>eastern route from Rachel to Lighthalzen</color>. Wait—where are you running off to?!",
    ["Dialogue2092101"]="(A squad of armed guards bars your path, the \"Rekenber\" insignia on their uniforms catching the light—a silent but absolute warning.)\nAnother step, and you'll officially be trespassing on Rekenber's property.",
    ["Dialogue2092102"]="(You find yourself completely encircled, no way out.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF><size=26>Are you choosing to stand against Rekenber?</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue2092103"]="(The guards hold up their rifles, chambering rounds one after another.)\n<size=26>Five</size>.",
    ["Dialogue2092104"]="(A crisp click rings out as the bullet slides into the chamber.)\n<size=26>Four</size>.",
    ["Dialogue2092105"]="(\"Click\"—The safety disengages.)\n<size=26>Three</size>.",
    ["Dialogue2092106"]="(Slowly lift their weapons, taking aim.)\n<size=26>Two</size>.",
    ["Dialogue2092107"]="(Weapons lock onto you—aimed directly at your chest.)\n<size=26>One</size>.",
    ["Dialogue2092108"]="A <color=#CA2E0AFF>wise decision</color>. Let's go.",
    ["Dialogue2092201"]="(Syphus stiffens as he looks toward the road you came from.)\nTell me—you found them, didn't you?",
    ["Dialogue2092202"]="What?\n(Syphus' lips tremble from sheer tension as he murmurs your words back to himself.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Goldie's dagger and a distress marker</color>. This is bad. Really bad...",
    ["Dialogue2092203"]="(The tall man paces anxiously.)\nWhen every other possibility is ruled out, what's left—no matter how absurd—must be the truth. And the only organization with the power capable of abducting the kingdom's elite right under our noses... is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2092204"]="I have to inform my superiors, Adventurer. We need to decide on our next move. Ever since Prince Allen took the throne after the king's death, the political situation has been... fragile. And if Rekenber gets involved...",
    ["Dialogue2092205"]="(After a heavy silence, Syphus sighs deeply.)\nAdventurer, this isn't about personal courage. Politics isn't a battlefield, and diplomacy isn't about friendships. You saw it yourself in Juno—Rekenber acts like a company, but they've hollowed out the Republic's government. The Lord is nothing but a puppet.",
    ["Dialogue2092206"]="The Kingdom and Arunafeltz have never been on good terms. If war ever breaks out, the Republic's neutrality will be crucial. That's why, even though we suspect Rekenber is behind the disappearances of both dispatch teams, we have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>consider the consequences</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2092207"]="After all, the first dispatch team was sent to investigate Rekenber's secret research. In a way, we did cross into their territory. Adventurer, I know you want to save your friends... but... the Kingdom has a lot to consider here.",
    ["Dialogue2092208"]="We value your loyalty, Adventurer. The Kingdom won't forget your part in this. I don't know what the higher-ups will do next, but the disappearances are definitely tied to <color=#CA2E0AFF>a leak in our intelligence</color>. If we root out Rekenber's informants, we may turn the tables.",
    ["Dialogue2092209"]="I see... Adventurer. The Kingdom won't forget your part in this. I don't know what the higher-ups will do next, but personally, I would like you to cooperate with us. The disappearances are definitely tied to <color=#CA2E0AFF>a leak in our intelligence</color>. If we root out Rekenber's informants, we may turn the tables.",
    ["Dialogue2092210"]="The road to Lighthalzen is locked down... but you're going to push through, straight into Rekenber's heart, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue2092211"]="(Syphus firmly pats on your shoulder.)\nI could tell right away—you're not like us. Not like the others in the dispatch team either.",
    ["Dialogue2092212"]="More powerful, more untamed... It's not always their own kind that takes down behemoths. A spark, a fire, a bullet—rare as they are, such people have the power to change the course of destiny.",
    ["Dialogue2092213"]="Adventurer, you are one of those people.",
    ["Dialogue2092401"]="(A merchant passes you a heavy book.)\nTake this to Mr. Bouvier. You don't need to chat—just show some respect.",
    ["Dialogue2092501"]="Huh?! Oh! Alright, alright, we'll go meet him now!",
    ["Dialogue2092601"]="I'm dying of boredom! You're an Adventurer, right? How about keeping me entertained with some wild tales?",
    ["Dialogue2092701"]="Interesting... If you're ever free, swing by again. I'll make sure it's worth your while.",
    ["Dialogue2092801"]="So you're the one taking the commission? I've been growing some special fruits just outside the city. Can you check on them and take some photos?",
    ["Dialogue2092901"]="Looking good! Won't be long before they're ripe and ready to harvest!",
    ["Dialogue2093001"]="If we make it there, we can fix history and show everyone the <color=#CA2E0AFF>truth</color>! Do you understand? The truth! That's the ultimate goal of the Eden Group!",
    ["Dialogue2093002"]="(The Eden Group member flails around, rambling nonsense with a familiar manic glint in his eyes.)\nBut first things first—I need a <color=#CA2E0AFF>brilliant partner</color> for this journey. And wouldn't you know it... Ah! I found one!",
    ["Dialogue2093003"]="(You turn away fast—but he's even faster.)\nMy partner—let's hit the road together—!",
    ["Dialogue2093004"]="No!",
    ["Dialogue2093101"]="(After a thorough beatdown, he seems to regain some sanity—but he's still clinging to your leg.)\nC'mon, Adventurer, aren't we fated to be partners?! If I die on this expedition, the archaeology world will lose its rising star! Just think how devastated Captain Alquein would be!",
    ["Dialogue2093102"]="(Curtis clears his throat, his face turning a bit red due to embracement.)\nAhem! First off, nice to meet you! I'm Curtis, first-class archaeologist of the Eden Group stationed in Arunafeltz. Captain Alquein has mentioned you—said you're our unofficial top member!",
    ["Dialogue2093103"]="(Hearing you ask about the captain, Curtis eagerly nods.)\nOh, not just the captain! Everyone in the Eden Group appreciates your kindness and skill! Ahem—right, introductions! Curtis, first-class archaeologist of the Eden Group, stationed in Arunafeltz!",
    ["Dialogue2093104"]="(He rummages in his bag and holds up a photo, his eyes practically shining.)\nYou—you recognize <color=#CA2E0AFF>her</color>, right?",
    ["Dialogue2093201"]="Knew you'd notice! This portrait was her private collection, now stored in the Temple's vault, completely off-limits. It's so ancient that just a little exposure to the light could ruin it, meaning restoration would cost a fortune. But hey, I still managed to get it from my—uh, digging expert friend. Ahem, I mean, my legitimate archaeology colleague!",
    ["Dialogue2093202"]="(Curtis spins in place, dramatically holding up the photo.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Behold—the portrait of Arunafeltz's founder, the very first Pope—St. Isumia</color>",
    ["Dialogue2093203"]="Nice catch! It looks like we make a great team, after all!\n(Curtis gestures at the finely woven areas on the armor's shoulders and elbows.)\nTechnically speaking, this is a special woven chainmail. Based on the timeline...",
    ["Dialogue2093204"]="Probably from five or six hundred years ago? This weaving technique isn't the standard double-helix pattern used today. It actually looks more like an embroidery-based technique. I've seen pieces like this before, but to be sure... we'll need to find the answer in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2093205"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockley</color>, the guy who knows everything about Glast Heim, is waiting for us.\n(Curtis cheerfully pushes you forward.)\nI sent him a heads-up already, so come on, there is no time to waste!",
    ["Dialogue2093301"]="(Rockley peers over his thick glasses, eyes fixed on Curtis.)\nIndeed... this pattern is from Glast Heim. Your assumption is correct.",
    ["Dialogue2093302"]="Roughly eight centuries back, Glast Heim saw both war and prosperity. It became common practice for families to weave armor for their loved ones, discreetly etching their names into it as a form of protection.",
    ["Dialogue2093303"]="After its downfall, it turned into a haven for the impoverished. The custom survived, but its meaning shifted—from a blessing for protection to a way for <color=#CA2E0AFF>women to confess their love</color>. This armor, sized for a man, must be from that period.",
    ["Dialogue2093304"]="(Holding the photo up, Rockley examines the woman's face with deep focus.)\nSomeone of this status... there should be records of her in Glast Heim history.",
    ["Dialogue2093305"]="What?!\n(Rockley's gaze flickers between the photo and you as if weighing the credibility of the claim.)\nArunafeltz does have a tradition of choosing white-haired, heterochromatic women as popes...",
    ["Dialogue2093306"]="This kind of craftsmanship only existed in Glast Heim. So how did it end up in Arunafeltz? And that armor is male in design, which fits the customs of that period.",
    ["Dialogue2093307"]="Ugh, Arunafeltz's history is always wrapped in secrecy, and Glast Heim's records were nearly wiped out after the war. It looks like our usual approach won’t work this time.",
    ["Dialogue2093308"]="(With a loud clap, Rockley gestures toward Macy in the distance.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit summoning! Talking to the dead!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2093309"]="Spirits??\n(Curtis stiffens, eyes darting around nervously.)\nHold on, you know how to deal with spirits?!",
    ["Dialogue2093310"]="(Rockley sighs, rubbing his forehead.)\nIf you're that scared, just stick behind the Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Macy</color> is an expert. She won't summon anything dangerous.",
    ["Dialogue2093311"]="Honestly, I don't feel any malice from this photo. Just grief... and maybe... regret?",
    ["Dialogue2093401"]="(The mysterious medium sways, whispering over the photo like she's in a trance.)\nI see it... I see it...",
    ["Dialogue2093402"]="Such... powerful longing! Hm, yes, yes... Are you thinking of her? From that cold grave, that damp coffin? Don't leave!!!",
    ["Dialogue2093403"]="(Macy suddenly jolts awake, looking dazed.)\nWait... what did I just say?",
    ["Dialogue2093404"]="Hmm... Crafting Seems like the usual approach won't work on spirits this old. I need some special ingredients to brew a ritual-enhancing potion, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dream Potion</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2093405"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Two cups of Spring Water, two Majoruros' Horns, 200ml of Carat' Blood, and two Dream Roses</color>. Just enough for two potions. So, Adventurer... or our friend here from Eden Group—who's taking the second dose?",
    ["Dialogue2093406"]="Oh, well. You need a spirit-sensitive bloodline to actually see the spirit. Even the spirit accepted my connection; you are the ones he wants to talk to. So... you, or him?",
    ["Dialogue2093407"]="(Curtis drops to his knees again and clings to your leg.)\nWaaah, Adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue2093408"]="People only fear ghosts when they've got something to hide.\n(Macy's voice drops, sounding almost otherworldly.)\nSo tell me... have you ever <color=#CA2E0AFF>disturbed</color> their eternal sleep?",
    ["Dialogue2093409"]="No! Never!\n(Curtis practically jumps, eyes blazing.)\nEverything I've done... it was all for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>truth</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2093410"]="I'm fine.\n(Curtis brushes off your question.)\nThey... they'll forgive me. They have to...",
    ["Dialogue2093501"]="(In a corner of the abbey, a male spirit in tattered old robes huddles near the fireplace. Raydric Archers fix their eerie gazes on him.)\nIsumia... Isumia...",
    ["Dialogue2093502"]="(He doesn't answer. Instead, he inches closer to the fireplace, desperate for warmth that will never reach him, whispering a name lost to time.)\nIsumia... Isumia...",
    ["Dialogue2093503"]="Why, why are you talking to nothing? Wait, is there... something there? No way... it's him?!",
    ["Dialogue2093504"]="AHHHH!\n(Curtis jolts back to life, slowly peering from behind you.)\nSo... uh... what's he up to?",
    ["Dialogue2093505"]="(Curtis gulps, glancing around nervously.)\nI think... he's afraid of those <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raydric Archers</color> nearby.",
    ["Dialogue2093506"]="These undead monsters feed on spirits to strengthen themselves. If a spirit carries a powerful blessing, they'll linger for decades, even centuries, waiting for that protection to fade—then they devour what's left.",
    ["Dialogue2093507"]="All you need to know is—spirits don't last this long unless they've been blessed with incredible power. And if he's still clinging to the name \"Isumia\"... that blessing might've come from the first Pope herself. Let's wipe out these monsters first, then talk to him.",
    ["Dialogue2093601"]="Any change?",
    ["Dialogue2093602"]="(Curtis frowns deeply.)\nAsk him... is this where he died?",
    ["Dialogue2093603"]="Spirits who die with regrets keep repeating their final moments over and over, unable to move on. If we don't help them fulfill their <color=#CA2E0AFF>wish</color>, we won't get any answers.",
    ["Dialogue2093604"]="(Curtis grits his teeth, squeezes his eyes shut, and rushes toward the spirit, waving the photo.)\nYou! Y-you—you wanna see this, don't you?!",
    ["Dialogue2093605"]="!!!\n(The male spirit stops whispering on the spot the second he sees the Pope. He stands motionless, his ghostly eyes brimming with unreal but glistening tears.)",
    ["Dialogue2093606"]="(His fingers pass right through the photo, yet they move delicately, tracing the face of the woman seated on the throne—as if longing to touch her.)\nYour face... it's exactly the same...",
    ["Dialogue2093607"]="(His body turns increasingly transparent, seemingly fading.)\nBut... I have already...",
    ["Dialogue2093608"]="Nope! Not happening! You're staying!\n(Curtis snatches the photo back, angrily shaking it at the fading figure.)\nHey! You're not leaving just like that! Talk to us first!",
    ["Dialogue2093609"]="You can't vanish before telling us everything! You knew Isumia, right? Were you two... lovers? At least, at some point?",
    ["Dialogue2093610"]="(The mention of \"lover\" makes the spirit tremble, shaking his head in agony. A dark aura starts creeping over his ghostly form.)\nShe... she never loved me... She put on the armor... the one meant for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eryxis</color>... why...",
    ["Dialogue2093611"]="Crap, I can see him too—he's turning into a wraith!\n(Curtis waves the photo wildly like it's some kind of talisman.)\nStay with us! We won't upset you anymore, just focus on Isumia!",
    ["Dialogue2093612"]="Tell us how to help! If you become a wraith, you'll never get to see Isumia again!",
    ["Dialogue2093613"]="(Light and darkness swirl around the spirit's body, his expression torn between sorrow and tenderness. Struggling, he forces out a few words.)\nI... I miss her...",
    ["Dialogue2093701"]="(Macy crosses her arms, staring at the both of you.)\nYou interrupted the summoning—what exactly did you do?! He'd have fully transformed into something else if I hadn't stepped in!",
    ["Dialogue2093702"]="(After listening, Macy immediately turns on Curtis.)\nYou forced a spirit to recall its own death?! Do you guys even respect the dead?! There are already too many restless spirits in these ruins—if you want to keep working, stop making it harder for us mediums!",
    ["Dialogue2093703"]="Sorry.\n(Curtis lowers his head, silently taking the scolding.)\nTell me... how can we make this right?",
    ["Dialogue2093704"]="(Macy scoffs, her voice dripping with sarcasm.)\nHow about you answer that one?",
    ["Dialogue2093705"]="You talk big about seeking the truth, but do you even understand it? What kind of truth will free him from his past?",
    ["Dialogue2093706"]="This spirit's name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Silvio</color>. You didn't even bother to learn that—how do you expect to uncover the truth?",
    ["Dialogue2093707"]="You don't have to apologize, Adventurer.\n(Curtis stops you.)\nI have to try again—no matter what.",
    ["Dialogue2093708"]="At the very least... we owe it to him to fill in the gaps of these lost centuries—as witnesses to history.",
    ["Dialogue2093709"]="(Curtis exhales, rubbing his tired eyes as he stares at the empty space.)\nAs a first-class archaeologist of the Eden Group stationed in Arunafeltz, I've studied its history. They show that while Eryxis was one of the Twelve Bishops, he was the one the Pope <color=#CA2E0AFF>despised</color> most in her later years.",
    ["Dialogue2093710"]="In his burial site, there are no treasures, no honors. Just chains—the kind meant for sinners.",
    ["Dialogue2093711"]="That's the truth I wanted to share—I don't think the Pope ever cared for Eryxis. The armor she wore... was most likely meant for Silvio instead.",
    ["Dialogue2093712"]="But before she could gift it to him... Silvio died in Glast Heim. And in her later years, the Pope finally uncovered the truth. Left with no way to fix the past, she could only pray endlessly, hoping her lost love would hear her regrets.",
    ["Dialogue2093713"]="As a member of the Eden Group, I want to see history for what it really was. But as the one who caused his spirit to change... I need to find a way to make this right. Love is what trapped this sorrowful soul here. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>end</color> this.",
    ["Dialogue2093714"]="(Macy stares at Curtis, her gaze unreadable.)\nSo you're sharing details that only <color=#CA2E0AFF>grave robbers</color> would know... Are you ready to be exiled from the Eden Group?",
    ["Dialogue2093715"]="When all this comes to an end, I'll tell Rockley everything.",
    ["Dialogue2093716"]="(After a brief moment of thought, Macy steps away.)\nHis <color=#CA2E0AFF>coffin lies ahead</color>. Remember, you only get one shot at this. If he becomes a wraith, centuries of built-up resentment will burn this land to the ground.",
    ["Dialogue2093717"]="When that time comes, none of us will be innocent.",
    ["Dialogue2093801"]="(Deep in the abbey's underground chamber, a broken coffin stands next to an ancient statue of a young girl. It is there that you meet the spirit once more.)\nHow wonderful... Even though you chose to leave me behind for a better life, seeing you standing tall with your scepter... I feel no hatred at all.",
    ["Dialogue2093802"]="You rose to the throne as Pope, and Eryxis stood by your side as your Bishop. But did you ever learn the truth? <color=#CA2E0AFF>He murdered me... and betrayed you!</color> As you laid me to rest, as you whispered your prayers, his gaze was void of love. How horrifying... A Bishop, someone meant to give blessings, yet behind your back, he raised his knife—to murder his dearest friend before his wedding!",
    ["Dialogue2093803"]="You must have figured it out, Isumia. You were always the most brilliant of us. Eryxis never deserved your trust or your heart. Did you know?",
    ["Dialogue2093804"]="Could you... not fall for him...?",
    ["Dialogue2093805"]="Ahem... Mister... Spirit.\n(Curtis looks down, his words shaky.)",
    ["Dialogue2093806"]="I apologize for intruding upon your peace... and for causing harm to your soul. I... I'm Curtis, a human who captured an image of the Pope.",
    ["Dialogue2093807"]="It's fine. I responded to the medium's request—I wanted to meet you. My soul... was meant to disappear the moment Isumia was gone.",
    ["Dialogue2093808"]="(Silvio's spirit turns more transparent, and his words grow fainter.)\nIsumia wouldn't want me to become a wraith. So, I will let go... but I still have a little time. If there's anything you wish to know, ask me now.\n",
    ["Dialogue2093809"]="I don't even know where to start.\n(Curtis exhales, shaking his head.)\nYour connection with the Pope, what Eryxis did, the truth about this land... it's all overwhelming.",
    ["Dialogue2093810"]="(Silvio smiles faintly at Curtis' conflicted expression.)\nBut for now... you can only ask one question.",
    ["Dialogue2093811"]="Okay then.\n(Curtis shakes off his hesitation, takes out the photo, and returns to the start of it all.)\nI want to know... <color=#CA2E0AFF>the story of the armor</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2093812"]="(Silvio nods, his gaze distant as he remembers.)\nEryxis, Isumia, and I were childhood friends. In Glast Heim, women wove armor for the ones they loved—but I was never given one. Everything changed when Isumia discovered a feather in the ruins... one with the power to heal everything. From then on, she was the most beloved Acolyte in the city.",
    ["Dialogue2093813"]="I told myself it was fine. The people needed her. And anyway, we were always close. Soon, Isumia realized something horrifying—the feather wasn't a miracle. It cured one illness, only for another, far worse, to take its place. She was scared... and wanted to tell everyone before her wedding. Eryxis disagreed, but he never tried to stop her.",
    ["Dialogue2093814"]="The night before the wedding, Eryxis appeared. He said Isumia had chosen him, that she had promised to leave Glast Heim with him, and her armor was proof of her love. He told me to stay out of their way.",
    ["Dialogue2093815"]="In my grief, I never saw it coming. And by the time I realized... it was too late. Isumia was weeping over my corpse... and Eryxis said nothing. I lost track of time. But long after, a group came here in secret... and under the Pope's decree, they built her statue beside my grave. Isumia...",
    ["Dialogue2093816"]="(His presence had grown so faint that you could barely see him anymore. The end was near.)\nIsumia... Through all those years without me... did you find more happiness than sorrow?",
    ["Dialogue2093817"]="I see... so that's how it was...\n(Silvio shuts his eyes, looking peaceful.)\nIf I ever meet her again... I won't be at a loss for words...",
    ["Dialogue2093818"]="Never mind... it doesn't matter anymore...\n(Silvio closes his eyes, acceptance settling over him.)\nHundreds of years have gone by... happiness, sadness, does it even matter which outweighed the other?",
    ["Dialogue2093819"]="(His soul dissolves into the void, carrying with it the love that had been lost to time.)",
    ["Dialogue2093901"]="I came the moment I heard from Macy—she said something serious might happen here.\n(Rockley peers toward where you arrived from.)\nSo, did I get here in time... or am I too late?",
    ["Dialogue2093902"]="(After hearing your story, Rockley lets out a long sigh.)\nI never imagined... there was such a tale behind all this...",
    ["Dialogue2093903"]="Curtis, <color=#CA2E0AFF>you are not to reveal this to the world</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2093904"]="Why?\n(Curtis is stunned, and then his anger flares.)\nSir, this is the truth we fought to uncover!",
    ["Dialogue2093905"]="You really have to ask? It's not just about politics, Curtis. And tell me honestly—did you get that photo from a grave robber? Curtis, when you became part of the Eden Group, what was the very first thing I told you?",
    ["Dialogue2093906"]="... Never forge history. Never twist the facts. And never rely on <color=#CA2E0AFF>stolen artifacts</color> to validate the past.",
    ["Dialogue2093907"]="What about you?",
    ["Dialogue2093908"]="Yes, I've worked with grave robbers. But does that mean we should let history rot in the dirt?! This evidence came directly from the first Pope's resting place! Arunafeltz will never allow us to excavate and research the relics. If we don't do something, Freyja will be the only voice in history!",
    ["Dialogue2093909"]="Truth may be hidden, but it's never truly destroyed. The Eden Group will always have a chance to bring it to light. But once faith and principles are broken... they can never return to what they were. Curtis, after all your time in Arunafeltz, can't you see? Their belief in the divine is as strong as that of any ancient empire.",
    ["Dialogue2093910"]="A holy war fueled by the collapse of faith... I will not allow the Eden Group to be its trigger. And Curtis, I can't overlook what you've done—you've fanned the flames of grave robbing.",
    ["Dialogue2093911"]="Besides, history is never just one-sided. You condemn Eryxis, and that's why this truth lingers in your mind. But while his ambitions were selfish, he did lift a barren land into wealth and power.<color=#CA2E0AFF>Good and evil, like light and shadow, are always intertwined.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2093912"]="Funny, isn't it? The Eden Group and the grave robbers—aren't they just like the light and the shadow you spoke of? And yet... now you suddenly have a problem with their evidence?",
    ["Dialogue2093913"]="You...",
    ["Dialogue2093914"]="Whatever.\n(Curtis clenches the photo in his hand.)\nOne day, the world will know the truth that's been hidden for centuries.",
    ["Dialogue2094001"]="(In the photo, a white-haired, heterochromatic woman sits upon the sacred throne, a scepter in her hand. She wears armor... but it doesn't quite fit—it looks like it was made for a man...)",
    ["Dialogue2094101"]="(The veteran journalist gives his cameraman a hearty slap on the back.)\nJust smack your back twice—get it all out! But tell me, how did you puke without getting a single drop on the camera?",
    ["Dialogue2094102"]="Well... I thought about how expensive this camera is! Hehe, figured I'd rather make you mad than pay for a new one~! Oh, wait—Adventurer! It's been ages!",
    ["Dialogue2094103"]="(Enchulo casually lets go of Shana, his eyes gleaming with interest.)\nGiven the time, place, and people involved... Adventurer, you're here for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dawn Moon Festival</color>, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue2094104"]="To be precise, I'm after this year's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mobel Journalism Award</color>. As for the Dawn Moon Festival—\n(Enchulo wags a finger at you.)\nA basic, bandwagon topic like that? No way it will win the top prize.",
    ["Dialogue2094105"]="Winning the Mobel Prize requires three things: fresh ideas, market buzz, and deep reporting. Shana and I trashed so many drafts before we settled on Arunafeltz. It's Midgard's most secretive kingdom and rarely opens its doors to the press. That alone makes it a goldmine of a story!",
    ["Dialogue2094106"]="Thanks to the massive Dawn Moon Festival, they're letting the press in—so naturally, festival stories will dominate the headlines and sell like crazy. But we at Libet Express? We don't just write fluff pieces for cash!",
    ["Dialogue2094107"]="So—\n(Enchulo gives Shana a knowing look.)\nShana, who's your camera focusing on this time?",
    ["Dialogue2094108"]="(Shana excitedly pulls out a magazine, grinning as she points to the cover.)\nDuh! For the best-looking Priest, obviously!",
    ["Dialogue2094109"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2094110"]="(With a flick of her fingers, Shana flips straight to the rankings page.)\nIn the last issue of Juno Glamour, three of the top political heartthrobs were Arunafeltz Priests—ahh! Ouch!",
    ["Dialogue2094111"]="(Enchulo swiftly rolls the magazine into a stick and knocks Shana's head three times.)\nThese mags will put anyone on the list if you pay them enough. If I sent in one of my article fees, I'd be ranked first by tomorrow!",
    ["Dialogue2094112"]="... Pfft.",
    ["Dialogue2094113"]="(Enchulo clears his throat loudly, changing the topic.)\nLook, we're talking about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Iron-Blooded Priest</color>—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Yus Amar</color>. A man pushing seventy, still dominating the field, leading Arunafeltz's military and government. No one else even comes close.",
    ["Dialogue2094114"]="(As if to prove his point, Enchulo pulls a crumpled, yellowed newspaper from his bag and carefully lays it out.)\nThe last time Yus Amar spoke to the press was during the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Night of Lament</color>, fifteen years ago. Shana, only time and human nature can give a story real depth.",
    ["Dialogue2094201"]="What a noble spirit, what an impeccable man!\n(With great care, Enchulo stows the newspaper in the deepest pocket of his bag.)\nSince that day, Yus Amar has turned away all reporters, devoting himself fully to Arunafeltz.",
    ["Dialogue2094202"]="Not only did he uphold his promise, but with unwavering determination, he led a <color=#CA2E0AFF>top-down revolution in Arunafeltz</color>. According to data from the Republic, the conflicts between the Temple and nomads have been dropping for ten years straight, and Freyja's faith is spreading everywhere, even in the backwater villages. Such achievements could very well be called miraculous.",
    ["Dialogue2094203"]="Glad you see it too! That's why I must seize this chance—to sit face-to-face with Bishop Yus Amar at the Dawn Moon Festival and unveil the missing chapters of history. My words will stitch together the past and present, bringing fifteen years of change to light!",
    ["Dialogue2094204"]="You're new here, so I don't blame you for not getting it. But once I sit down with Bishop Yus Amar for my interview at the Dawn Moon Festival, you will feel the weight of his legacy, and the tides of Arunafeltz's history will finally reveal themselves before your eyes!",
    ["Dialogue2094205"]="(Enchulo cackles to himself.)\nFifteen years of political drama plus juicy secrets? I might as well have the Mobel Prize shipped straight to the Libet Express already.",
    ["Dialogue2094206"]="What?!\n (Enchulo's mouth turns into a perfect \"O\" shape, his expression turning ghostly pale to match his teeth.)\nWho said that?",
    ["Dialogue2094207"]="(Tearing up, Enchulo tugs at your clothes.)\nNo way... seriously?",
    ["Dialogue2094208"]="Yeah... if you're the one saying it, then it must be true.\n(Enchulo slumps, looking like he is about to dissolve himself into the ground like a slime.)\nGuess Arunafeltz switched things up at the last minute. Nothing we can do about it.",
    ["Dialogue2094209"]="Tough luck, boss.\n(Shana gives Enchulo a sympathetic pat on his shoulder.)\nHow about you interview the successor of Odin's bloodline—the Adventurer? That should be just as fascinating.",
    ["Dialogue2094210"]="No way!\n(Enchulo quickly bats Shana's hand aside.)\nI'm not ditching my headline that easily! Unless—",
    ["Dialogue2094211"]="Unless—I take a different approach! I'll make the Adventurer my field assistant instead of an interviewee.",
    ["Dialogue2094212"]="(Enchulo's eyes blaze with passion as he sweeps his arm dramatically.)\nThat's it! If I can't get a direct interview, I'll personally <color=#CA2E0AFF>piece together Yus' journey through the last fifteen years of reform in Arunafeltz</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2094213"]="The Iron-Blooded Priest, Yus Amaar, has built his reign upon the divine love of the Goddess, treating all as equals! It is only right that we, the Uncrowned Kings of journalism, document it all! Adventurer, you must join me!",
    ["Dialogue2094214"]="(Enchulo draws a halo over your head.)\nBoom! You're officially a member of the press! But beware—should you <color=#CA2E0AFF>information gathering</color>, you shall bear the crushing debt of one hundred million Zeny!",
    ["Dialogue2094301"]="Adventurer? Ahem, Israel and Sartre aren't around. Try looking somewhere else.",
    ["Dialogue2094302"]="They're off digging for gold. The new <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue tax</color> went up again—\n(The old man coughs hard.)\nAhem, they wish only to present Freyja with the finest of jewels! Ahem!",
    ["Dialogue2094303"]="Aloy's old spot? Nah, it's dry—nothing worth mining anymore.\n(With a trembling hand, the ailing elder gestures towards a new path.)\nFollow the <color=#CA2E0AFF>riverbed</color>, you might find them there.",
    ["Dialogue2094401"]="(Aloy swipes at her forehead, flashing a tired grin.)\nPhew, it's scorching! What're you doing out here, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue2094402"]="(Aloy's face twists with anger as she hears Yus Amar's name.)\nWhy are you asking? You know we can't talk about him! Look, I'm grateful for what you did, but I'm not looking to get executed!",
    ["Dialogue2094403"]="(Aloy looks at you with uncertainty, unease written across her face as she clenches her hands.)\nUh... if you don't need anything, I should probably get back to work.",
    ["Dialogue2094404"]="If you need some quiet time, you can go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dried-up riverbed</color>. It has long been abandoned... so no one will disturb you.",
    ["Dialogue2094501"]="Your face is covered in sand. Apologies, I'm preparing a report for an important meeting—I can only spare a moment for you.",
    ["Dialogue2094502"]="Shh!\n(Malam cuts you off, looking around nervously.)\nIf the guests hear you sympathize with the nomads, this will become a problem.",
    ["Dialogue2094503"]="People here are <color=#CA2E0AFF>hostile</color> toward them. So, are they still whining about getting back to herding? Or maybe they asked you to cut them a tax break? Sorry, no can do—Yus doesn't want the nomads living too comfortably. I run the trade, sure, but I can't even go against his orders. Not for now, anyway.",
    ["Dialogue2094504"]="Wow, you actually remember that fifteen-year-old interview?\n(Malam stops to think, then grins mischievously.)\nDon't tell me—a journalist buddy put you up to this? Hoping to get a juicy headline?",
    ["Dialogue2094505"]="Hahaha! Ignoring the Dawn Moon Festival in favor of covering Yus Amar's reforms? Gotta say, your friend's got a solid news sense—and you're on the right track.",
    ["Dialogue2094506"]="The villagers of Grey Wolf are but a reflection of the foundation of this kingdom. Walk with me, and you'll have the chance to witness the higher-ups within the Temple.",
    ["Dialogue2094507"]="Shall we? Yus is currently absent, which is perfect—I have a few <color=#CA2E0AFF>taxation</color> matters to discuss with his supporters. Relax—nothing's gonna be decided until he's back.",
    ["Dialogue2094508"]="Sir, the changes have been made as per your request.",
    ["Dialogue2094509"]="(Malam glances at the revised report and nods slightly.)\nAdventurer, let's go.",
    ["Dialogue2094601"]="(Malam pulls you behind him.)\nMentor Neirun will arrive shortly. If you have questions, you may ask me instead.",
    ["Dialogue2094602"]="... Hmm, is it still possible to get you out of this place right now?\n(Malam facepalms.)\nQuick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>hide behind the third pillar on the right</color> and keep quiet.",
    ["Dialogue2094701"]="Mentor, as the Dawn Moon Festival draws near, I have reviewed the financial records of our jewelers, preparing for the oncoming flood of trade. Yet, in my search, I stumbled upon troubling discrepancies... and I must bring them before you.",
    ["Dialogue2094702"]="Let's discuss this matter together.",
    ["Dialogue2094703"]="Jewelry has been the unshaken pillar of Arunafeltz's wealth, and since our alliance with the Republic, prosperity has surged. Those among you who have invested in this trade—have you not reaped fortunes beyond measure?",
    ["Dialogue2094704"]="So tell me this—why are your pockets overflowing, yet the treasury is bone-dry? We can't even afford proper fortifications or winter gear for our soldiers? Even when I sought to commission a new statue of the Goddess for His Majesty, I was forced to procure gemstones through the private accounts of the Gilded Rose!",
    ["Dialogue2094705"]="Watch your mouth! That's an insult to Bishop Yus Amar! He's worked non-stop for fifteen years, and every guard in the Temple can back him up on that! Malam, you're the one managing the country's finances—if the military's broke, you're the first person we should be questioning!",
    ["Dialogue2094706"]="Tsk, tsk... But none would dare question the deeds of Bishop Yus Amar. Can we be so certain that some greedy rat hasn't been skimming off the top, using his name as a cover? I am here precisely so that we may decide together how to replenish the treasury and root out such corruption.",
    ["Dialogue2094707"]="Fine, let those outsiders mine more gems. Didn't they want to go back to their sheep and cattle? Easy fix—give them a target. Once they've dug up enough to collapse from exhaustion, then they can leave.",
    ["Dialogue2094708"]="You just don't rewrite decrees on a whim. Have they not already stirred enough dissent? Sigh... Look, people both inside and outside the city are already unhappy with how things are run. An iron grip may silence tongues for a time... but to truly still the storm? That requires patience... and wisdom.",
    ["Dialogue2094709"]="Pathetic! Have you already forgotten how we built this kingdom? We've tried wiping them out many times, but they just keep returning! If they weren't at least somewhat useful for labor, they'd be—",
    ["Dialogue2094710"]="Sylvain, your words tread a dangerous path.",
    ["Dialogue2094711"]="Since no consensus can be reached, and you all remain steadfast in Bishop Yus Amar's innocence, then perhaps the misappropriation of funds lies within our own ranks. Malam, why not start with Sylvain—his fury burns too hot. Prove his hands are clean... if they truly are.",
    ["Dialogue2094712"]="Neirun... who put you in charge of military affairs? When Yus returns, I'm making sure he hears all about your student stepping out of line.",
    ["Dialogue2094713"]="Stepping out of line? Funny, since you're the one pinning the army's money problems on my student. Sylvain, can you really swear, on Bishop Yus Amar's name, that the military isn't burning through funds left and right?",
    ["Dialogue2094714"]="Enough! We leave—now!",
    ["Dialogue2094801"]="(Malam leans against a column, shooting you a laid-back grin.)\nWow! Did you see Sylvain's face? Like a bleeding ruby! If that had escalated further, I might have called you in to knock some sense into them.",
    ["Dialogue2094802"]="No action goes unnoticed. My steps at Torr Volcano have already roused Yus' suspicion, so I'll have to take a different approach to expose him. Adventurer, with all this trade booming, who do you think is raking in the biggest profits—besides the buyers and sellers?",
    ["Dialogue2094803"]="That's right! However, the entire transportation and logistics sector is already controlled by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber</color>. Even if we start a trade war, we've gotta have the muscle to back it up. By the way, how influential is your journalist friend? Would they dare to publish a piece against Rekenber? Money is no issue.",
    ["Dialogue2094804"]="Alright, then. Check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>airships</color> on the outskirts. And watch out—those Rekenber guards pop up everywhere.",
    ["Dialogue2094901"]="Hey, you made it back! Shana, it's time to check the photos—let's see what our rookie reporter at Libet Express managed to snag!",
    ["Dialogue2094902"]="One, two, three, four... huh? Wait, why is Rekenber's insignia here? Did you meet Ms. Irumina?",
    ["Dialogue2094903"]="Pfft—well done, Adventurer! If you ever want a photo collection, I'd be happy to take professional shots free of charge!",
    ["Dialogue2094904"]="I can report to the editor free of charge!\n(Enchulo grabs the camera and waves everyone in.)\nNow, let's take a look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>great accomplishments of the Iron-Blooded Priest</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2095001"]="Select the corresponding photos according to the provided information and analyze the impact of Yus' governance on Arunafeltz over the past fifteen years.",
    ["Dialogue2095002"]="The nomads didn't just decide to settle near Rachel—they were forced into it. Those who resisted? Either wiped out or had their culture reduced to whispers of a forgotten past.",
    ["Dialogue2095003"]="The jewel trade, once the backbone of the Arunafeltz's economy, is now on the verge of collapse due to excessive mining. The kingdom's like a fancy jewelry box—still shiny outside, but nothing is left inside.",
    ["Dialogue2095004"]="Arunafeltz stands divided. Some venerate Yus as their unwavering pillar, while others, their patience worn thin by fifteen years of unrelenting rule, now rise in defiance.",
    ["Dialogue2095005"]="Trade between Arunafeltz and the Republic has flourished, yet Rekenber Corp maintains an iron grip on all logistics. And that's not all—they've got their fingers in every major industry.",
    ["Dialogue2095006"]="The truth is clear—Yus has long abandoned the doctrine he once championed in the interview fifteen years ago. His relentless march toward reform has forged a kingdom riddled with discord, its fractures widening with every passing day.",
    ["Dialogue2095007"]="Something's off... we need to think this through.",
    ["Dialogue2095101"]="Wait, what the hell?\n(Enchulo pulls out an old interview from his bag and slams it onto a new photo from fifteen years later. The contrast is striking—once a kind, smiling Priest, Yus has now become a faceless ruler, hidden behind the power of his regency.)",
    ["Dialogue2095102"]="...\n(A heavy silence settles as Enchulo lifts the photo, gazing at the faces captured within.)\nThis is... complicated.",
    ["Dialogue2095103"]="No, the problem isn't the material. In fact, Adventurer, you nailed it—you captured the rawest nerve of this kingdom. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rising anger from oppression, resources sucked dry, political infighting, and Rekenber sinking its claws deeper</color>... one spark is all it takes to set this fragile stability ablaze and drag everyone into chaos.",
    ["Dialogue2095104"]="The tax records... so even the treasury is compromised... Shana, unless you wanna end up covering wars, you better rethink that vacation.",
    ["Dialogue2095105"]="Understood! So... for the article—\n(Shana hesitates, shrinking back nervously.)\nAre we about to get ourselves deleted...?",
    ["Dialogue2095106"]="Yes.",
    ["Dialogue2095107"]="This isn't about changing the story—it's about uncovering the depths. These issues didn't arise overnight, especially in a giant system like this. I need to go <color=#CA2E0AFF>further back</color> to figure out how it started... and what Yus was really up to.",
    ["Dialogue2095108"]="Fifteen years ago—Night of Lament, the night Yus took control of Arunafeltz's military and government. I want to know more about that Commander Rossin he mentioned, the guy who \"never cared about the nomads.\" Sure, peace needs sacrifices... but what if this wasn't a sacrifice? What if it was <color=#CA2E0AFF>murder</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2095109"]="I see your point.\n(Enchulo taps the pen sticking out of his pocket.)\n The victors always write history... but what does that have to do with me?",
    ["Dialogue2095110"]="Good or bad, I'll write it all down—that's what being a journalist is about. Winning? Well, that's another story...",
    ["Dialogue2095111"]="(Enchulo draws a halo over your head.)\nDidn't I tell you when you joined? We are the Uncrowned Kings!",
    ["Dialogue2095112"]="This crown is often hidden and sometimes tainted, so it exists only in our hearts. We call it—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2095201"]="Hey, hey, what's with that face?\n(She's sweating a little.)\nDon't tell me you're bailing?!",
    ["Dialogue2095202"]="W-What?!\n(The girl blushes, turns away, and squats down, covering her face.)\nDid I just... ramble to a complete stranger?",
    ["Dialogue2095203"]="W-Well, are you free? Or maybe... up for the job?",
    ["Dialogue2095204"]="Really?!\n(Mercy jumps up and grabs your sleeve, eyes full of gratitude.)\nI knew it—luck always balances out! Today must be my lucky day!",
    ["Dialogue2095205"]="(With surprising strength, the bashful girl yanks your sleeve.)\nWait! If I miss the shot today, I might never find someone else! You're an Adventurer, right? I'll beg my professor for extra funds—just please, help me out!",
    ["Dialogue2095206"]="(She pulls you along while tidying up the camp with one hand.)\nWe've gotta catch that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Massive Drosera</color> ASAP—it's for my graduation essay! If we don't get it, I'll have nothing to turn in, and I need to retake the semester...",
    ["Dialogue2095301"]="(You glance where she's looking and see a giant Drosera moving through the desert.)\nOkay, before we go charging in—I should probably tell you what we're up against.",
    ["Dialogue2095302"]="This Drosera has lived in the Rachel Plains since I was a kid. Its size is massive—and its lifespan far exceeds that of any ordinary Drosera.",
    ["Dialogue2095303"]="This place is dry and empty—nothing really survives here except it. It's still going strong after all these years.",
    ["Dialogue2095304"]="I believe if we uncover its <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret to survival</color>, we could apply that knowledge to agriculture—and maybe bring life back to this land.",
    ["Dialogue2095305"]="(Mercy's eyes gleam with hope as she pulls out a potion from her bag.)\nI bought this <color=#CA2E0AFF>extra-strong calming potion</color> from a seasoned hunter. If we soak the Drosera's roots in it, we can extract a good sample.",
    ["Dialogue2095306"]="(She throws a fist in the air, cheering for you.)\nGood luck, Adventurer. I'm counting on you—we'll finish this amazing essay together!",
    ["Dialogue2095401"]="(The huge Drosera falls into a deep sleep. Mercy quietly opens her notebook and starts observing.)\nQuiet... don't wake it up...",
    ["Dialogue2095402"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>leaves</color> are totally <color=#CA2E0AFF>shrunken</color>, probably to reduce water loss from transpiration and photosynthesis. Anything else we can analyze?",
    ["Dialogue2095403"]="This smooth, white <color=#CA2E0AFF>wax coating</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>reflects sunlight</color>, lowering its surface temperature and preventing sunburn. Anything else?",
    ["Dialogue2095404"]="(Mercy nods continuously, quickly jotting down notes.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Extensive root system</color>, increased surface area, maximizes water absorption from the soil.",
    ["Dialogue2095405"]="(She taps the paper with her pen.)\nOkay, so yeah—these are all common traits among desert plants. But why is this one so long-lived? There's still too much I don't know...",
    ["Dialogue2095406"]="(Carefully, Mercy tears off a strand of the Drosera's root.)\nGuess I'll need to get this to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Viola</color> if I want real answers. But, uh...",
    ["Dialogue2095407"]="(Mercy glances away, a little guilty.)\nShe runs the biology lab at school. Let's just say... she's moderately patient.",
    ["Dialogue2095409"]="(Stammering, Mercy shoves the root into your hand.)\nShe might not be patient with me and my essay... but someone like you, with such a righteous look? She'll be fine!",
    ["Dialogue2095410"]="(Picking up the Drosera King soaking in the potion, Mercy bows deeply.)\nAdventurer, I'm begging you! I can't go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>school</color> without my essay done. Hand this root over to Professor Viola for me!",
    ["Dialogue2095411"]="(She bolts with surprising speed, leaving you and the root behind in her echo.)\nShe'll handle it! Just hand it over to Professor Viola!",
    ["Dialogue2095501"]="(The busy lady stops and looks at you with a puzzled expression.)\nYou are...?",
    ["Dialogue2095502"]="Mercy?!\n(Her composed face falters slightly.)\nHeh... where is she now?",
    ["Dialogue2095503"]="Well, isn't that just great—\n(Viola flings her tissue and laughs dryly.)\nThe brilliance of this generation is simply... breathtaking!",
    ["Dialogue2095504"]="They freeload lab resources every other day, don't even know how to maintain the equipment—and now she's treating me like her assistant? A Drosera root report, really? Is that what she asked of you?",
    ["Dialogue2095505"]="Huff, huff...\n(Viola takes a deep breath, and you feel the tension begin to ease.)\nSo that means... as long as there's a report, the girl will hand in her essay?",
    ["Dialogue2095506"]="(Viola grits her teeth and mutters.)\nWe're basically out of paraffin for making slides. The students drained it. I don't have time to restock.",
    ["Dialogue2095507"]="Check around <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Academy</color>—there might be <color=#CA2E0AFF>abandoned Fiery Dimik</color>. Grab their <color=#CA2E0AFF>fuel essence</color> or whatever. Once I have the material, I'll give you the report.",
    ["Dialogue2095601"]="(Viola frowns as she fans the smell from the fuel essence.)\nUgh. No wonder it's been abandoned. Look at all that sediment at the bottom.",
    ["Dialogue2095602"]="(Viola doesn't answer—instead, she hands you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fresh analysis report</color>.)\nHere. I think all her work will amount to nothing once again.",
    ["Dialogue2095603"]="If she's smart, she'll revise her essay topic. As her friend, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Rachel</color> and deliver the message.",
    ["Dialogue2095701"]="(The cheerful girl from before is gone—Mercy now wears only dismay.)\nThis can't be happening...",
    ["Dialogue2095702"]="(She opens the notebook and shoves it into your hands)\nWhat if... what if Drosera <color=#CA2E0AFF>isn't</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2095801"]="(Mercy gazes at you with uncertainty)\nYou... got the analysis report from Professor Viola, right?",
    ["Dialogue2095802"]="This might be... my <color=#CA2E0AFF>last chance</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2095901"]="(Mercy scans the last line and lets out a sigh before reading the report bit by bit)\nAccording to the report, under the microscope, the Droseras root cells have no cell walls—just membranes. So it doesn't photosynthesize.",
    ["Dialogue2095902"]="That means... it's most likely an animal mimicking a plant. My essay... might be dead before it's even born.",
    ["Dialogue2095903"]="(Mercy firmly shakes her head.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>No. I'm not giving up on this</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2095904"]="(She sets the report down with a sigh)\nMy dream has always been to turn my barren homeland into a thriving green oasis.",
    ["Dialogue2095905"]="It was that dream that pushed me to leave my harsh hometown, get into Juno University, and learn under someone as brilliant as Professor Viola.",
    ["Dialogue2095906"]="My Drosera research may have failed... but out there in the Rachel Plains, I'm sure there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>other plants surviving in harsh conditions</color>—perfect samples for my research.",
    ["Dialogue2095907"]="And if no plants exist, I'll shift my research—to soil, climate, maybe even water systems. <color=#CA2E0AFF>I won't stop</color> until my homeland becomes a <color=#CA2E0AFF>paradise</color> full of green where no one goes hungry.",
    ["Dialogue2095908"]="Since I left home, I've seen what paradise can look like. Now, I want to make sure the people who raised me get to see it too—right where we live.",
    ["Dialogue2096001"]="Hey, over here!\n(A girl in a Juno University uniform is waving excitedly at you from across the Rachel Plains.)",
    ["Dialogue2096002"]="(She swipes at her sweaty forehead, grinning.)\nFinally! Someone took my <color=#CA2E0AFF>commission</color>! Are you from Juno? Einbroch? Or, like, way out there somewhere?",
    ["Dialogue2096003"]="Hey, hey, do all of you adventurers take commissions without reading them? Mine pays well, but it's not for just anybody! The last few were sent packing. But... you seem a bit different...",
    ["Dialogue2096004"]="(She shoves a scribbled hand-drawn poster into your hands.)\nTake a good look—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Big Reward! The Drosera King of Rachel Plains</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2096005"]="Everything's on the poster.\n(Mercy throws her arms wide.)\nThe Drosera is like this—huge! Can you take it on?",
    ["Dialogue2096101"]="Oh, it's you again, outsider.\n(The silver-haired young man turns around, his bloodshot eyes filled with sorrow.)",
    ["Dialogue2096102"]="Look, I don't have time for your nonsense. If you're trying to play hero, go talk to your noble friend.",
    ["Dialogue2096103"]="This is a matter of our nomadic people. Not your business.\n(The silver-haired young man rejected you coldly.)\nGet lost. You shouldn't be here!",
    ["Dialogue2096104"]="YOU!\n(Sartre glares at you with fury, and you stare right back.)\nWould you dare defile the peace of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>departed elder</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2096105"]="(Sartre lets out a long sigh. His usually untamed silver hair droops with despair.)\nChief Vadim had been sick for a long time. Last night... he found peace.",
    ["Dialogue2096106"]="It's fine. Death is part of life. He just got there before us. But why can't we even grant him his last wish?",
    ["Dialogue2096107"]="All he wanted was a funeral in our people's way!",
    ["Dialogue2096108"]="(Sartre glares toward the center of the village, where soldiers swarm the execution platform.)\nThe Freyja goons banned our customs! They call it education—but break the rules, and bam, you're labeled a heretic and dragged off to the execution platform for everyone to watch!",
    ["Dialogue2096109"]="My people, descendants of many nomadic tribes, came here with diverse traditions—seeking peace, not rebellion. Doesn't the Temple preach how Freyja loves everyone equally? Yet they can't even tolerate a few law-abiding nomads. Some \"merciful\" Goddess, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2096110"]="I don't care! I've been holding it in for fifteen years—I'm done! The chief never did us wrong. Now that he's gone, we owe it to him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>carry out his final wish</color>. He shouldn't leave this world with regrets.",
    ["Dialogue2096111"]="Honestly, this village needs the funeral. Everyone's been holding their pain in for way too long.",
    ["Dialogue2096112"]="You? Help us?\n(Sartre snorted.)\nWhat, not scared of being hauled off to the execution platform?",
    ["Dialogue2096113"]="Humph.\n(Sartre gives you a sharp, warning glance, though it's not hostile.)\nGo talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zahya</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096114"]="She's Vadim's granddaughter—and our next village chief. If it's <color=#CA2E0AFF>funeral customs</color>, no one knows them better than her.",
    ["Dialogue2096201"]="Thank you all for your concern.\n(The girl wipes her face and gives you a bow.)\nI'll carry on my grandpa's will and do my part for the village.",
    ["Dialogue2096202"]="(Surprised, she covers her face. A shimmer of tears glints in her eyes.)\nAre you sure you want to help us?",
    ["Dialogue2096203"]="I-I...\n(She wipes her nose, holding back tears.)\nThanks. Really. I mean it—thank you.",
    ["Dialogue2096204"]="Our people believe we come from nature, so when we die, we go back to it. But we don't bury our dead, for nomads form no bond with land.",
    ["Dialogue2096205"]="In the most sacred of our rites, a relative carries the deceased into the wilds, their body <color=#CA2E0AFF>covered in seeds and beast blood</color>—to summon birds and beasts to feed upon it.",
    ["Dialogue2096206"]="In this way, the beasts carry the seeds across the land, and new life grows from their flesh. This cycle nourishes future generations of nomads and ensures the tribe survives upon barren soil.",
    ["Dialogue2096207"]="The problem is that the Priests of Freyja think it's barbaric and <color=#CA2E0AFF>heretical</color>—against their faith. Ever since we moved into Grey Wolf Village, no one's been allowed to do funerals the old way.",
    ["Dialogue2096208"]="Before he passed away, Grandpa asked the Temple several times—just to restore our tribal traditions in death. All he got in return was blood on the execution platform and soldiers treating us worse and worse.",
    ["Dialogue2096209"]="(The girl's tear-streaked yet determined smile lingers in everyone's memory.)\nI believe in you all.",
    ["Dialogue2096301"]="(You notice someone you know standing next to Sartre.)\nIsrael? With your status, you shouldn't be getting into trouble like this.",
    ["Dialogue2096302"]="No—please, allow me to help.\n(Israel clenches his fists, his voice full of emotion.)\nChief Vadim was like family to me. Can't I at least do this for him?",
    ["Dialogue2096303"]="Besides... this is the last thing I can do for him.",
    ["Dialogue2096304"]="There's someone being all pushy about joining the funeral plans—not even as a nomad. Oh—don't worry, I'm not talking about you.",
    ["Dialogue2096305"]="Don't say that, Sartre.\n(Israel looks to you, eyes hopeful.)\nAdventurer... do you think I should join?",
    ["Dialogue2096306"]="See? Two to one. You're outvoted, Sartre.\n(Israel chuckles and gives him a pat on his shoulder.)\nNow come on—what's the plan? Those guards are not easy to fool.",
    ["Dialogue2096307"]="Of course we've got a plan. What about you, Adventurer? What have you brought us?",
    ["Dialogue2096308"]="(Israel rests his chin in his hand, eyes flickering with thought.)\nThe funeral rites themselves are simple. What matters most is how we <color=#CA2E0AFF>transport the chief's remains deep into the Rachel Plains</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096309"]="Those Temple Guards patrol the plains all day in shifts. I can probably get their <color=#CA2E0AFF>schedule</color>, but someone's gotta go out there and draw them off.",
    ["Dialogue2096310"]="Alright, let's split up. I'll handle getting the guard schedule. You, Adventurer—go grab the <color=#CA2E0AFF>items we need for the ritual</color>. When I'm back, we'll come up with a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>drive the guards away</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096311"]="Sartre, you know this place best. You'll handle getting the chief's body to the funeral site on the plains, alright?",
    ["Dialogue2096312"]="Alright.\n(Sartre nods, then mutters.)\nHey, Adventurer—find me before you set off. I have something for you.",
    ["Dialogue2096401"]="(Israel examines the materials.)\nTo gather all this so quickly—you honor the name \"Adventurer.\"",
    ["Dialogue2096402"]="(He waves the duty roster in hand.)\nI have the schedule as well. I've been waiting for you to go over it!",
    ["Dialogue2096501"]="Hmm... Looks like late at night, the patrols ease up a lot, with forces concentrating closer to Rachel—that's our chance.",
    ["Dialogue2096502"]="Tch, those watchdogs are everywhere, even at night when people should be asleep.",
    ["Dialogue2096503"]="(Israel shakes his head helplessly.)\nGrey Wolf Village is close to the mining area. Adventurer, we need you to find a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>distract the guards</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>units 3 and 15</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096504"]="Do something to get their attention. Once they're distracted, Sartre and I can sneak Zahya and the chief out to the far end of the plains.",
    ["Dialogue2096505"]="This is for you.",
    ["Dialogue2096506"]="(Sartre presses a still-warm mask into your hand.)\nNo matter what, just don't get caught. That goes for you too, Israel.",
    ["Dialogue2096507"]="I'll be waiting here till we get the signal. Not going anywhere.\n(Sartre avoids your gaze, toe scraping at the dirt.)\nAnyway... thanks, you guys.",
    ["Dialogue2096601"]="(Zahya lets out a smile when she sees you're okay.)\nThanks, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2096602"]="We are now preparing to recite the eulogy for Grandpa. Once the ceremony ends, he will finally return to nature as he wished, no longer a prisoner of Freyja.",
    ["Dialogue2096603"]="But first, one brave soul must <color=#CA2E0AFF>anoint him with seed and beast blood</color>. Tradition demands the rite be fulfilled by one revered or one who has danced with death and returned.",
    ["Dialogue2096604"]="Sartre and Israel have told me of your deeds. I believe that you, who truly harbors a brave soul, are the most fitting choice.",
    ["Dialogue2096605"]="Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>will you do it</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2096606"]="Of course!",
    ["Dialogue2096701"]="(Zahya rises, gazing at the body now covered in seeds and beast blood. Under the night sky, unknown birds circle above, their cries mournful and distant.)\nIt is done.",
    ["Dialogue2096702"]="(Grief fades from her eyes, replaced by a light of resolve.)\nAdventurer, Sartre, and Israel—thank you for all you've done for my grandpa.",
    ["Dialogue2096703"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color>, most of all... Though your creed walks another path, you were willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>embrace two opposing beliefs</color>. Our tribe will remember your grace—and should fate allow, we shall repay it.",
    ["Dialogue2096704"]="No, I simply followed my heart and did what I believed was right. Even now, I don't think I've betrayed the Goddess or strayed from my faith.",
    ["Dialogue2096705"]="(Israel falls silent for a moment, then solemnly recites a tenet of Freyja's doctrine.)\nI have always believed that the Goddess loves everyone equally.",
    ["Dialogue2096706"]="Words once spoken in <color=#CA2E0AFF>blessing... should never have become a chain</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096801"]="(You spot two patrol teams crisscrossing paths nearby. One of the leaders even lifts his weapon in a friendly wave.)",
    ["Dialogue2096901"]="(The elder gazes upon you with a solemn nod.)\nAs the successor of Odin's bloodline, it appears you've reached a new level of understanding on your journey.",
    ["Dialogue2096902"]="Perhaps, then, this explains the strange runes glowing upon that slab...",
    ["Dialogue2096903"]="Yes, the very one you brought back from Glast Heim and entrusted to the church. With the power of the rune, you are granted Odin's Protection to perform a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new class advancement</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2096904"]="Only yesterday did it radiate once again, showing the figure of the Goddess. Adventurer, the moment has come. Should you be ready for this next step, return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> and find the key to your fourth class.",
    ["Dialogue2096905"]="(With a profound look toward Glast Heim, Wolmas speaks.)\nOn the walls of the Glast Heim Chivalry, many have left their stories of valor and sacrifice. Go forth, and may Odin be with you.",
    ["Dialogue2097001"]="(The Goddess, suspended in the air, her eyes one red and one blue, piercing into your soul.)\nYour gaze speaks of your strength as a third-class Adventurer. However, the road to the fourth class is not easy to tread. I cannot simply show you the way.",
    ["Dialogue2097002"]="(Shikoti points to your heart.)\nFirst, you must carry the spark of justice within.",
    ["Dialogue2097003"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Answer my question</color>, so I may know that Odin's glory will never fade within you, whatever path you choose.",
    ["Dialogue2097101"]="Hmm... I see your resolve for justice. Let evil serve as kindling, showing me that this spark can rise into a powerful flame for Odin's glory.",
    ["Dialogue2097102"]="Among the Glast Heim Chivalry, some have fallen and become <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bloody Knights</color>, bowing to Baphomet. They are a blight upon this land.",
    ["Dialogue2097103"]="Defeat them and gather the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Breath of Knights</color>. Throw it into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pit beneath Sage's statue</color>, and should you gather enough, <color=#CA2E0AFF>heroes</color> worthy of the knightly name will appear before you.",
    ["Dialogue2097104"]="These were knights who sacrificed their lives during Baphomet's assault, seeking my blessing to safeguard the people of Glast Heim.",
    ["Dialogue2097105"]="(With a sorrowful sigh, Shikoti tells the story of a bygone age.)\nLong ago, Baphomet harnessed the power of Hermes, leading an army of monsters to invade Glast Heim through the Dimensional Gap.",
    ["Dialogue2097106"]="Among the knights, some chose to surrender, betraying their fellows, while others fought to shield the people, falling back again and again until they took shelter in the great hall where their weapons were kept. The knights' conviction, entwined with the anguished cries of the people, unknowingly stirred me from my deep slumber.",
    ["Dialogue2097107"]="I am not a Valkyrie of war, incapable of battling Baphomet. But the knights remained undaunted; they asked not for survival but for me to use my godly power to grant the people a way to escape, even at the cost of their own lives.",
    ["Dialogue2097108"]="I answered their call, lighting a sacred fire in the hall with the promise that as long as it burned, every soul upon this land could find refuge.",
    ["Dialogue2097109"]="But now, my power has waned, and the sacred fire has faded. Only those fallen knights remain, forever defending the hall as they battle the traitors of their past lives.",
    ["Dialogue2097110"]="Should you gain their <color=#CA2E0AFF>recognition</color>, I will bestow upon you that which you desire.",
    ["Dialogue2097201"]="(The gallant knight rests his hand on his sword, bowing with honor.)\nBy gathering the Bloody Breath, you have done a great service to this land. You've earned our highest respect.",
    ["Dialogue2097202"]="The very Goddess who extended her hand to us a century past—she now asks that you earn our recognition?",
    ["Dialogue2097203"]="It is no easy task... With Glast Heim lying in ruins, there is no place left to conduct the knight's trial... Yet, the Breath of Knights you carry speaks to your strength and courage...",
    ["Dialogue2097204"]="(Lost in thought, the Knight Spirit rests his hand on his chin, then looks up with newfound hope.)\nYou know our tale, then you must also be aware of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>countless shields and weapons</color> gathering dust here?",
    ["Dialogue2097205"]="Each of these pieces is crafted with fine materials, bearing the memories we fought side by side. Yet, as specters, we are doomed to watch them decay, our hands unable to lift them once more.",
    ["Dialogue2097206"]="Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore their shine</color> for us? Even if time will one day claim them all, to see them gleam once more would be enough. Yet be cautious—the Abysmal Knight, more powerful than the Bloody Knight, stands guard there.",
    ["Dialogue2097301"]="We are grateful for your help.\n(The Knight Spirit's eyes carry a deep nostalgia.)\nMy friends of old... they have not gleamed this bright in ages.",
    ["Dialogue2097302"]="You may now <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the goddess</color> and share with her our gratitude, along with our recognition of you.",
    ["Dialogue2097401"]="So, you have their recognition. Successor of Odin's bloodline, please step forward.",
    ["Dialogue2097402"]="(With a gentle touch to the void, Shikoti sends something intangible into your fate, brightening it.)\nI, the goddess who steers the future, grant you this gift, a future touched by divine blessing.",
    ["Dialogue2097403"]="From this moment, you are qualified to undertake the fourth-class advancement. Once you <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach Job Level 60 and your mentor is ready</color>, you may face the challenges that await.",
    ["Dialogue2097404"]="Press onward through what has been, what is, and what is yet to come.",
    ["Dialogue2097501"]="Adventurer, regarding the Rune Slab you retrieved from Glast Heim—",
    ["Dialogue2097502"]="(Wolmas touches his beard, and there is a hint of embarrassment in his eyes.)\nHeh, fear not; the runes have simply grown faint and erratic... We believe it may relate to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shikoti</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2097503"]="Indeed, the Rune Slab concerns the <color=#CA2E0AFF>future of your class advancement</color>, which is most unpredictable. Only the goddess who steers the future may provide insight.",
    ["Dialogue2097601"]="Your concerns are clear to me—set them aside. The rune was created by Odin, a divine artifact that holds the ultimate mysteries of the world, glimpsing futures deeper than my own. Halting your class advancement will lead you, one with Odin's blood, toward a better path.",
    ["Dialogue2097602"]="To force a class advancement now would push your future toward a path of greater peril.",
    ["Dialogue2097603"]="(A moment of surprise shows on Shikoti's face, her eyes showing a thoughtful look.)\nYou... do not fear a fate woven with even darker dangers?",
    ["Dialogue2097604"]="(A flash of surprise crosses Shikoti's eyes, quickly followed by admiration.)\nSo, you seek power to shield those in the present. Very good. I believe I now understand why Odin chose you.",
    ["Dialogue2097605"]="You now hold my recognition, and as the one who steers the future, I must reward such a brave soul. Even if the slab cannot bestow upon you the strength of a fourth-class—",
    ["Dialogue2097606"]="(A faint trace of divine energy swirls at the goddess' fingertip; her expression is kind as she bestows it upon your heart.)\nAccept this—it is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> of future to you. With it, you shall wield <color=#CA2E0AFF>skills equal to a fourth-class</color> Adventurer as you continue your journey.",
    ["Dialogue2097607"]="However, this gift comes with a price. You must keep <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharpening</color> your skills until the time of the Class Advancement Trial, at which point you can turn this gift into genuine power and ascend to a fourth-class Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2097608"]="(The goddess nods approvingly before she vanishes into the air.)\nNow, go with my blessing. The future that belongs to you is not far ahead...",
    ["Dialogue2097701"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, your efforts have awakened the Rune Slab. Now, the time has come to embark on the path of class advancement...",
    ["Dialogue2097702"]="(With her eyes shut, the goddess gazes into your destiny.)\nGo back to where your journey first began; that place that was once your beginning as a Novice is now the starting point for your fourth-class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue2097703"]="Embrace your earliest lessons once more; as a fledgling student, listen to the wisdom of your mentor, letting it be the unceasing beacon on your path.",
    ["Dialogue2097704"]="(The goddess nods slightly, a quiet affirmation.)\nFollow where your heart leads, and go to the place where you are called.",
    ["Dialogue2097705"]="I have granted Wolmas and the others my vision; once you complete the Class Advancement Trial, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Glast Heim Chivalry to join the Class Advancement Ceremony</color>. There, my gift to you shall become your own power, making you a true fourth-class Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2097706"]="And now, I shall fall into rest once more...",
    ["Dialogue2097801"]="Well, look who's back! The great Adventurer!\n(Yadrew lets out a hearty laugh, looking you over from head to toe.)",
    ["Dialogue2097802"]="I hear you're about to become a Dragon Knight—how extraordinary! If the dean finds out, he may very well add you to the academy's book of distinguished alumni!",
    ["Dialogue2097803"]="Yes, yes... I've set up your Class Advancement Trial, but not here in the academy; it's on Comodo. Alone, you must venture to the dragon's lair deep in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo Cave</color> and bring back something for your Ferus.",
    ["Dialogue2097804"]="(Yadrew's face turns serious.)\nOne drop of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Blood</color>, ancient and untainted.",
    ["Dialogue2097805"]="It must be pureblood, unlike Sky Petite, only from a genuine elder dragon. With the Rune Slab guiding your class advancement, the blood will empower your dragon, and the unity of your forces will make you a true Dragon Knight.",
    ["Dialogue2097806"]="The dragon race is one of battle and fury. Do you, Adventurer, understand what lies in wait for you on Comodo?",
    ["Dialogue2097901"]="(The ancient dragon's wings stir the air as it glowers, fangs bared.)\nHuman... you intrude upon us—are you here to wage war once again?",
    ["Dialogue2097902"]="Ferus? Hmm... So, you're a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color> allied with the lesser bloodlines. How does it feel to fight alongside them?",
    ["Dialogue2097903"]="(A fierce dragon roar resounds, and the sounds of weaker creatures panting fill the cave.)\nHuman, a race of lies. I trust none of your words.",
    ["Dialogue2097904"]="(The dragon's tail lashes, bone spikes brushing past your ear as a nearby ice pillar shatters into frosty splinters.)\nAmong dragons, to seek something is to fight for it with flame, to claim it with claws. Come forth, trespassing human—",
    ["Dialogue2097905"]="Show me, then—your <color=#CA2E0AFF>determination</color>. Prove if you are worthy of me offering my blood!",
    ["Dialogue2098001"]="Impossible...\n(The dragon's massive eyes flash with shock, and after a pause, it erupts into laughter.)\nHa-ha-ha! Excellent! Even the lesser bloodline retains such power; the legacy of our kin survives!",
    ["Dialogue2098002"]="(It slashes the flesh along its neck, and a single drop of vibrant dragon blood falls steadily into your hand.)\nThis blood is your <color=#CA2E0AFF>prize</color>, as well as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> from my kin to yours.",
    ["Dialogue2098003"]="It will cleanse impurities from your bloodline, slowly purifying it into true dragon essence. If you wish to become a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Knight</color>, you will need this power.",
    ["Dialogue2098004"]="(The dragon closes its eyes and descends calmly to the ground)\nTake it, human. The gifts of dragons are never reclaimed. But remember, this is our forbidden land. Unless it concerns this Ferus, you may never trespass here again.",
    ["Dialogue2098101"]="Impressive!\n(Yadrew pulls out a peculiar vial, sealing the Dragon Blood inside with great care.)",
    ["Dialogue2098102"]="Criatura Academy will send the Dragon Blood to the church for your ceremony. Now, report to Wolmas the Archbishop at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>. Once your Ferus has leveled up, you'll need to check with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mount Keeper</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>rent your Class Mount again</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2098103"]="Absolutely! As mentors, how could we miss any step of our students' journey? Go on, we'll meet you at Glast Heim Chivalry!",
    ["Dialogue2098201"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now, we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2098301"]="(Alice looks over her shoulder, offering a kind smile.)\nAdventurer, long time no see. Your deeds today, even after becoming an Arch Bishop, are a testament to your unwavering dedication to the light, safeguarding the sacred glow.",
    ["Dialogue2098302"]="Yet, to become a Cardinal, piety is but one part. As you revere the holy light above, do you also cast your gaze upon the countless souls who walk this world with you?",
    ["Dialogue2098303"]="Lately, the number of people seeking confessions at the church has been increasing, and we are short-handed. Should you seek the knowledge of a Cardinal, <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to Prontera Cathedral</color>, listen to the concerns of the citizens and bring your insights back to me.",
    ["Dialogue2098304"]="Go forth, and may you truly listen—not just with your ears but your heart.",
    ["Dialogue2098401"]="I hadn't thought you'd be the one to come! Are our insignificant worries worthy of your time?",
    ["Dialogue2098402"]="It's my child—still unwell despite the medicine given by Acolyte. I've come here on my day off, thinking perhaps a better Bishop could offer us some aid...",
    ["Dialogue2098403"]="Is our time already over? Regardless, I thank you for lending an ear to our concerns.",
    ["Dialogue2098501"]="You must be the legendary Adventurer honored by the kingdom! Wow—amazing!",
    ["Dialogue2098502"]="Heh, actually, I don't have any serious concerns... It's just that...\n(The person shyly fiddles with his fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue2098503"]="My former love has come back to Prontera, and I wish to get back with her, yet... the child with her makes me hesitant...",
    ["Dialogue2098504"]="Sigh, thank you for bearing with my endless chattering.",
    ["Dialogue2098601"]="(Without noticing who you are, the person bows his head in sorrow.)\nMy best friend and I argued... It's my fault. I shouldn't have joked about his departed family...",
    ["Dialogue2098602"]="I wanted to apologize in person, but he returned my gift and rejected my invitation to go out...",
    ["Dialogue2098603"]="I should go now. Adventurer, do you think he'll ever forgive me?",
    ["Dialogue2098701"]="Our Arch Bishop has returned! How was your day?",
    ["Dialogue2098702"]="(Alice quietly listens, nodding now and then to ask for specifics, with her gaze softening as she asks for details.)\nYou speak with gentle compassion and offer thoughtful responses rooted in genuine empathy. This is good.",
    ["Dialogue2098703"]="A Cardinal serves Odin with unwavering faith, attending to the deity and caring for countless souls, bringing Odin's blessings to those in need.",
    ["Dialogue2098704"]="By embodying this love, they attain the title of Cardinal and the right to serve as leaders within the church, becoming Cardinals in every sense.",
    ["Dialogue2098705"]="However, your path is not meant to end in Prontera but to reach across Midgard.\n(Alice's eyes drift to the glowing Teleport Formation behind you, where you can depart from the Criatura Academy.)",
    ["Dialogue2098706"]="The time has come for you to leave. Your Class Advancement Ceremony will be held at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>. Don't keep them waiting.",
    ["Dialogue2098801"]="(Uda gently smooths the creases on the old book, reluctant to part with it)\nAre you sure I can't keep it? I can trade you a sweet potato...",
    ["Dialogue2098802"]="Nope! You already got one!\n(The little girl stands firm, hands on her hips)\nTeacher Israel said every book is precious, and they should go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>people who really need them</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2098803"]="(Uda lowers his head, fidgeting with his fingers)\nBut... I really need it too...",
    ["Dialogue2098804"]="Adventurer!\n(They both rush over as you arrive.)\nTeacher Israel gave out <color=#CA2E0AFF>fairy tale books—there's one extra</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2098805"]="Huh? You like fairy tales too, Adventurer? Well... okay.\n(Uda nibbles his finger, then hands you the book like it's a treasure.)",
    ["Dialogue2098806"]="If there's any word you don't know, you can ask Teacher <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2098901"]="(Seeing the storybook in your hand, Israel chuckles.)\nSo even a famous Adventurer like you enjoys children's tales, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2098902"]="Ah, I remember now. <color=#CA2E0AFF>The Grand Adventure of Niflheim</color>—it's a popular fairy tale among noble kids. It's about a princess bitten by a venomous snake and a prince who journeys through all kinds of danger to retrieve her soul from the underworld.",
    ["Dialogue2098903"]="But... Vanessa's the one who threw it away. Even if I take it, it'll just sit on a shelf. Who else... would care about a children's tale?",
    ["Dialogue2098904"]="(Israel freezes for a second, then bursts out laughing.)\nYou mean <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to Her Holiness</color>? Hahaha...",
    ["Dialogue2098905"]="No, no, it's fine! I didn't mean to laugh at you.\n(Israel wipes away tears of laughter, then nods seriously.)\nYou're right—we could take it to Her Holiness.",
    ["Dialogue2098906"]="Forget the whole \"supreme authority\" thing—she's just a kid. Being locked in the Temple all day learning how to be a proper Pope... it's a bit much, don't you think?",
    ["Dialogue2098907"]="(Israel pats your shoulder)\nYet a gesture such as this is best made through the Republic's ambassador. Otherwise, the Temple would never allow it.",
    ["Dialogue2098908"]="Let's go, our kind-hearted hero! Let's give her this fairy tale book. Let her enjoy a little bit of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>childhood</color> every kid deserves!",
    ["Dialogue2099001"]="(Your sudden arrival interrupts the Pope's lesson with Jude)\nAhem. Looks like class ends here for today.",
    ["Dialogue2099002"]="Beyond written knowledge, the ability to <color=#CA2E0AFF>receive visiting dignitaries</color> is a vital skill. Before the next lesson, I shall inquire about your <color=#CA2E0AFF>insights</color> gained today. I look forward to your progress.",
    ["Dialogue2099003"]="Then I shall take my leave. May this day be kind to you and your people.",
    ["Dialogue2099101"]="(After Jude leaves, the Pope visibly relaxes and lets out a long sigh.)\nPhew...",
    ["Dialogue2099102"]="(The elegantly dressed girl raises her head from the book, speaking softly, formally.)\nA pleasant day to you, Ambassador of the Republic. May our nations remain bound in eternal friendship.",
    ["Dialogue2099103"]="(The Pope's glasses gleam suddenly. She reaches out hesitantly, unsure whether to take it.)\nIs this a gift from Lord Karl? Hmm... it bears signs of age.",
    ["Dialogue2099104"]="(She glances around, but there is no sign of Jude. Then she whispers softly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Go ahead and hand it over</color>, my friend.",
    ["Dialogue2099201"]="(The Pope picks up the book with excitement.)\nThe Grand Adventure of... NI—FL—HEIM? I think Teacher Jude once said—",
    ["Dialogue2099202"]="(Lost in the moment, neither of you notice anything strange.)\nThe <color=#CA2E0AFF>Realm of the Dead</color>? Forsaken by Goddess Freyja...",
    ["Dialogue2099203"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>No living soul may return</color>... What?!\n(A flash of radiant light surrounds the two of you before the sentence finishes.)",
    ["Dialogue2099301"]="(A girl who looks just like the Pope wipes her tears. Standing frozen in front of her is a boy who could be her twin.)\nThe Underworld is cold, yet life is an eternal winter without my brother.",
    ["Dialogue2099302"]="(Startled by your sudden appearance, the girl stares at you nervously.)\nA-Are you a sage from the stories? Or... a hero who protects the weak?",
    ["Dialogue2099303"]="(She bows politely, asking you for help.)\nMy brother once told me that courage and faith can bring miracles... Great hero, will you come with me—Alsa—<color=#CA2E0AFF>to the Underworld and ask the Lord of the Underworld to return my brother Allen's soul</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2099304"]="(Alsa points to two small dark fang marks on the boy's neck.)\nMy hero... My brother Allen was picking herbs when a venomous snake bit him. He's barely hanging on...",
    ["Dialogue2099305"]="A wandering bard spoke of his soul's departure—carried away to a realm known as Niflheim.\n(At her words, the surroundings subtly change, and a road into mystery slowly reveals itself.)",
    ["Dialogue2099306"]="(Still lost in her tale, Alsa doesn't notice your distant stare.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Niflheim, also known as the Underworld</color>, holds a great temple forged from black stone and cold fog. The Lord of the Underworld judges the unjustly fallen, deciding who may return to the mortal world.",
    ["Dialogue2099307"]="(Determination hardens Alsa's young face. You realize—though she looks like the Pope, her spirit is entirely her own.)\nAfter our parents left... my brother became everything to me.",
    ["Dialogue2099308"]="Even if I become one of the dead... even if I must cross the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gjoll</color>, give my flesh to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hell Poodle</color>, and offer my soul to the Lord of the Underworld... I must bring him back.",
    ["Dialogue2099401"]="(At the crossing, the Ferryman blocks your path.)\nYou are not among the dead but one who yet breathes. You're no soul to be ferried. Leave—before I make you part of it.",
    ["Dialogue2099402"]="(Noticing the scraps of flesh on the bone club, Alsa steps forward calmly.)\nYou are the Ferryman appointed to guard the Gjoll. How wearisome it must be to hear the lamentations of souls unceasingly.",
    ["Dialogue2099403"]="(She draws forth her lyre and strums gently; the Ferryman's expression softens in awe.)\nFrom a wandering bard, I once heard a melody beyond all compare. Esteemed Ferryman—if I could soothe these wailing spirits, hush the restless Gjoll... would you <color=#CA2E0AFF>grant us passage</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2099404"]="(After a moment's silence, the Ferryman lets out a booming laugh.)\nVery well. But should you fail, the Gjoll shall claim you—your souls forever chained to its depths.",
    ["Dialogue2099405"]="(Alsa nods, looking at you.)\nMy hero, would you lend me your <color=#CA2E0AFF>beat and rhythm</color>, so that the wails may not break my focus?",
    ["Dialogue2099501"]="(High upon his throne, the Lord of the Underworld smiles, unsettling and majestic.)\nMortals from distant lands... your purpose is known to me.",
    ["Dialogue2099502"]="To cross the Gjoll with courage and wisdom, and behold my true form—such resolve alone merits recognition.",
    ["Dialogue2099503"]="(With but a finger motion, she summons a glow from the shadows.)\nI shall <color=#CA2E0AFF>grant you the soul of Allen</color>, that he may walk beside you into the land of the living once more.",
    ["Dialogue2099504"]="(The girl bows respectfully.)\nThank you for your kindness. My brother and I shall never forget your mercy.",
    ["Dialogue2099505"]="(The Lord of the Underworld chuckles, amused.)\nHahaha... I who dwell in eternal shadow, immortal and unchanged—what use have I for mortal gratitude? Still... only by fulfilling my terms may you claim the soul.",
    ["Dialogue2099506"]="We await your decree.",
    ["Dialogue2099507"]="(The Lord of the Underworld nods approvingly. With a graceful sweep of her sleeve, the entire Underworld splits open—Gjoll included—unveiling a path of darkness.)\nThe road from this land permits no return. Therefore, before you behold the light again—",
    ["Dialogue2099508"]="<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>DO—NOT—LOOK—BACK.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue2099509"]="Should this rule be broken, Allen's soul shall be forfeit—and you shall remain here for all eternity, bound to me as thralls of the dead.",
    ["Dialogue2099510"]="To take from the Underworld is to offer something in return—that, as you mortals say, is but a fair exchange.",
    ["Dialogue2099511"]="As you wish, Your Majesty.",
    ["Dialogue2099601"]="(The blinding light fades, and once more, you stand in the Pope's bedroom. She stirs at your voice, rousing slowly.)\nHmm... Wha-What just happened?",
    ["Dialogue2099602"]="(The Pope blinks, surprised, and starts recounting her dream in a flustered tone.)\nIt was just like the story in the book... But was I the prince? Or Alsa? Or... just me?",
    ["Dialogue2099603"]="In the <color=#CA2E0AFF>end</color> of the story, did they return to the living world?",
    ["Dialogue2099604"]="(The Pope hands you the book and boldly requests—)\nRead it to me—if you will.",
    ["Dialogue2099701"]="(After hearing the ending, she slumps over the desk in relief.)\nPhew... that's such a relief.",
    ["Dialogue2099702"]="(She falls silent for a moment, sorrow creeping into her eyes.)\nIf only our world could be this happy too...",
    ["Dialogue2099703"]="I wish I could <color=#CA2E0AFF>save my brother</color> too... go all out, just like in a fairy tale...",
    ["Dialogue2099801"]="(The middle-aged man coughs weakly and pulls out a worn ring.)\nAdventurer... I've been begging outside the Temple for days. They won't let me in... I'm out of options.",
    ["Dialogue2099802"]="You appear to be a distinguished guest of the Arunafeltz. The guards and attendants all treat you with respect... That's why I had to ask.",
    ["Dialogue2099803"]="Please... deliver this to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priest Neirun</color>. It's just a simple ring... but if she sees it, she'll know who it's from.",
    ["Dialogue2099804"]="(He looks pale, clearly unwell.)\nMy name is Boggs. I'm a traveling merchant who recently returned home. I left Rachel years ago... and lost touch with everyone.",
    ["Dialogue2099805"]="Much has changed. Neirun now serves as the Pope's most trusted Priest, secluded behind layers of walls and guard in the Temple. I cannot meet her without reason. Yet—",
    ["Dialogue2099806"]="(A hollow laugh escapes him.)\nStill... I hope to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put an end</color> to the past I left behind.",
    ["Dialogue2099901"]="(Adorned in finery, the Bishop clutches the simple ring, frozen in silence.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue2099902"]="Give it back.",
    ["Dialogue2099903"]="I don't care who gave it to you. I'll pretend I never saw it.",
    ["Dialogue2099904"]="(Neirun turns away. The warm light casts a shadow at her robe's hem—cold, distant.)\nThe past... and the people I left behind... I chose to <color=#CA2E0AFF>forget</color> them. I won't remember now.",
    ["Dialogue2099905"]="Say no more, Adventurer. In light of Her Holiness' trust and Arunafeltz's future... what weight could this simple ring possibly carry?",
    ["Dialogue2099906"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Return it to its owner</color>. I no longer wish to lay eyes upon him.",
    ["Dialogue2100001"]="Hey, did Neirun just kick you out?",
    ["Dialogue2100002"]="Shhh! Keep it down!\n(Malam glances nervously at Neirun.)\nActually, I didn't just eavesdrop—I peeked, too!",
    ["Dialogue2100003"]="Ahem... anyway, if you wanna change her mind, maybe <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me with you to see the ring's owner</color>? I might not be much help, but... it's worth a try...",
    ["Dialogue2100004"]="(Malam sighs, arms folded, gazing out the window.)\nThey have no connection now... but ten years ago, if Neirun hadn't become a Priest, they would've been married.",
    ["Dialogue2100005"]="You're wondering why love and being a Priest can't coexist, aren't you? It was Isumia—the very first Pope—who made that rule.",
    ["Dialogue2100006"]="A servant of the Goddess has to love all believers equally—they can't give all their love to just one person. That's why Priests today are <color=#CA2E0AFF>forbidden to wed</color>. Even their successors are all adopted from orphans deemed worthy.",
    ["Dialogue2100007"]="They say Pope Isumia herself once turned down her head Bishop using that very rule. But who knows? It's all old history now.",
    ["Dialogue2100008"]="Enough stories. Time to go find Uncle Boggs.\n(A familiar warmth flickers in Malam's eyes.)\nIt's been far too long...",
    ["Dialogue2100101"]="... Malam?\n(Boggs looks at the son of an old friend up and down, surprised and overjoyed.)\nWow... this is wonderful...",
    ["Dialogue2100102"]="It all passed so quickly... The boy's now a man. If Rossin could see you now... He'd be proud.",
    ["Dialogue2100103"]="(Seeing the untouched token in your hand, Boggs looks saddened.)\nSo... she still won't see me, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2100104"]="Cough cough... Well, I guess... that's an answer too.",
    ["Dialogue2100105"]="Uncle Boggs, are you okay?",
    ["Dialogue2100106"]="I'm fine, child. Everyone walks this road someday... I'm just heading to the Goddess a little sooner. She loves us all equally, so I'll watch over you, just like your parents did. Cough, cough...",
    ["Dialogue2100107"]="Don't say that! Uncle Boggs, I remember Sand Pears helping with coughing the most! Adventurer, can you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priest Estate east of Rachel</color> and pick a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sand Pear</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue2100108"]="That Sand Pear tree's been waiting for you too... just like us, all these years....",
    ["Dialogue2100201"]="(The refreshing sweet juice settles his coughing.)\nSo that little sapling from back then... really grew into something that can heal? Time sure is amazing.",
    ["Dialogue2100202"]="We watched you plant it, Neirun and I... Back then, who could've imagined how everything would change?",
    ["Dialogue2100203"]="(Malam forces a bitter smile.)\nIf fate could be seen coming... it wouldn't be fate, would it? Uncle Boggs, we're doing fine... but what about you?",
    ["Dialogue2100204"]="How could you just leave us without a word... and come back like this, sick and alone? Neirun never even mentioned you... but you two were so in love back then!",
    ["Dialogue2100205"]="Sigh... It's all my fault... This failing body, this loneliness... Maybe it's what fate believes I deserve.",
    ["Dialogue2100206"]="The moment I <color=#CA2E0AFF>pointed my finger</color> at Neirun, <color=#CA2E0AFF>accusing her</color> chose power over our vow for lifelong companionship... everything between us ended.",
    ["Dialogue2100207"]="If I could go back... I'd stay with her through the storms even if we couldn't be together.",
    ["Dialogue2100208"]="(Boggs lowers his head, gray strands peeking through.)\nNothing I do now will fix it. She doesn't want to see me... and I deserve that.",
    ["Dialogue2100209"]="So... do you still want to see her?",
    ["Dialogue2100210"]="Child... are you saying...?",
    ["Dialogue2100211"]="I... I want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help you</color>. If one meeting could fix things, I should at least give it a try, Uncle Boggs. Adventurer, I need your help.",
    ["Dialogue2100212"]="I need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cactus Flower</color> from the Rachel Plains and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Camel Milk Wine</color>—only the nomads brew it. You'll have to search Grey Wolf Village for that.",
    ["Dialogue2100213"]="Once you have them, meet me at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery on the outskirts</color>. I'll try to get Mentor Neirun there.",
    ["Dialogue2100301"]="(Zahya chuckles after hearing your request.)\nCamel Milk Wine? Adventurer, you've got the same taste as my grandpa.",
    ["Dialogue2100302"]="By chance... my grandfather left some behind before he died. Wait here—I'll fetch it for you.",
    ["Dialogue2100401"]="Mentor... Uncle Boggs is seriously ill. You still won't go see him?",
    ["Dialogue2100402"]="I've already met him... without telling you. He's aged a lot. He came back... just to say he's sorry.",
    ["Dialogue2100403"]="All these years... have you really let go of what happened back then?",
    ["Dialogue2100404"]="(Neirun remains cold and unmoved.)\nMalam... Have you forgotten the very first lesson I gave you when I took you in?",
    ["Dialogue2100405"]="I didn't forget...\n(Malam lowers his head, pain flickering in his eyes.)\nYou taught me to endure in <color=#CA2E0AFF>silence</color>, no matter how they defamed my parents.",
    ["Dialogue2100406"]="Ah—Adventurer.\n(Malam quickly brings you before Neirun.)\nThe Adventurer came with me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pay respects</color>... and brought something special.",
    ["Dialogue2100501"]="(Seeing your sincerity, Neirun's expression softens slightly.)\nAdventurer... that was very thoughtful of you.",
    ["Dialogue2100502"]="Yeah!\n(Malam nudges you.)\nAhem—how'd you know these were my parents' favorites?",
    ["Dialogue2100503"]="Oh...?\n(Malam clears his throat.)\nGuess he still cares, huh? Right, mentor?",
    ["Dialogue2100504"]="...",
    ["Dialogue2100505"]="(Malam rolls her eyes, but Neirun doesn't notice and keeps going.)\nIf my parents' spirits still linger above, they would not wish to see you like this.",
    ["Dialogue2100506"]="Back then, my mother was the one chosen to become a Priest. But you gave up your own love to take her place—for them.",
    ["Dialogue2100507"]="Uncle Boggs left you... You lost the one you loved. And after the Night of Lament... you lost your family too.",
    ["Dialogue2100508"]="I lost my parents... and the one who loved me like no other—<color=#CA2E0AFF>my aunt</color>—became my \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>mentor</color>.\" I've always held your kindness in my heart... but I never knew how to speak it.",
    ["Dialogue2100509"]="Then don't.\n(Neirun exhales softly, her hand tender on his head.)\nCall me what you will... it won't change how firmly I stand with you.",
    ["Dialogue2100510"]="It's better we stay <color=#CA2E0AFF>allies</color>, not mournful relatives. Blood means nothing to the plan—except giving the enemy a perfect place to strike.",
    ["Dialogue2100511"]="Love. Family. Friendship. They all carry weight... and risk. You're my finest student. Haven't you realized that?",
    ["Dialogue2100512"]="But... what about Uncle Boggs? He doesn't know about the plan. He's been living with regret and sickness for over a decade... Can you really let him die like that?",
    ["Dialogue2100513"]="Mentor, Yus Amar isn't in Rachel right now. I'll be careful about the time and location. Think of it as me repaying your support—just let me do this one thing for you.",
    ["Dialogue2100514"]="... No.",
    ["Dialogue2100515"]="(With grief in her eyes, Neirun shakes her head.)\nI've waited in the dark... all these years. So that one day, I could <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring justice</color> to my sister, her husband... and everyone who died fifteen years ago.",
    ["Dialogue2100516"]="That's exactly why I can't. Everyone knows about me and Boggs. If even a whisper gets out... they'll pounce. Yus, Musa—they're just waiting for a crack.",
    ["Dialogue2100517"]="I won't let them find a crack to strike. You've grown but not strong enough to shield us from the storm. Let us elders continue to bear the burden of <color=#CA2E0AFF>sacrifice</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2100518"]="Some people... were meant to lose. And some regrets... were meant to stay. Don't go against fate. Don't try to undo what's been done.",
    ["Dialogue2100519"]="But—",
    ["Dialogue2100520"]="(No matter how much Malam tried, Neirun wouldn't change her mind.)\nSister, brother-in-law... I've brought your child to see you.",
    ["Dialogue2100521"]="I <color=#CA2E0AFF>don't regret</color> this—never did, and never will.",
    ["Dialogue2100522"]="Once it ends, I'll return—with a new nation in hand—to honor you, who chose the past over the future.",
    ["Dialogue2100523"]="Until we meet again.",
    ["Dialogue2100601"]="(Boggs looks excited as you return.)\nSo? Did she agree to see me?",
    ["Dialogue2100602"]="(Boggs' hopeful expression crumbles, like an old house finally giving in to the wind.)\n",
    ["Dialogue2100603"]="(With sand blowing through Rachel, he rubs his eyes and smiles at you.)\nI see... Thank you, truly.",
    ["Dialogue2100604"]="Neirun worked so hard to become the Bishop... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I shouldn't drag up the past to bother her now</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2100605"]="We split paths and found our own pieces of happiness... that's okay, right? Haha... In my years wandering as a merchant, I've seen much... and I do not regret the journey.",
    ["Dialogue2100606"]="I'll stay here... find a quiet place in Rachel, somewhere with flowers and water—to be buried when the time comes. Heh, guess I'll need to rent a house and hire a few hands... can't just leave my corpse lying around, right?",
    ["Dialogue2100607"]="... Okay.",
    ["Dialogue2100701"]="(Inside Juno Library, Fulkyn closes his history book and greets you.)\nAdventurer, you've arrived.",
    ["Dialogue2100702"]="Strictly speaking, I'm only checking whether history has been altered—whether some temporal manipulator has once again tampered with the past...",
    ["Dialogue2100703"]="... He can't change much. The spacetime rules ensure history always flows toward its <color=#CA2E0AFF>destined end</color>, even if he is Barr Venter.",
    ["Dialogue2100704"]="Trying to erase the regrets in Lush's soul by challenging the spacetime rule again and again... yet in the end, history remains unchanged.",
    ["Dialogue2100705"]="(Fulkyn shows you a highlighted bit in his book.)\nSee? The <color=#CA2E0AFF>history book</color> here already wrote it all down.",
    ["Dialogue2100801"]="Get it now? You can't change the ending, but time sometimes keeps the little things that make it feel right. Like Lush and Thanatos' love.",
    ["Dialogue2100802"]="By leveraging the <color=#CA2E0AFF>convergence principles</color> of time, Barr Venter subtly altered a few key events beneath the \"Lush Death\" conclusion. This led the timeline to accept the legitimacy of her love with Thanatos—and allowed their hearts to truly connect.",
    ["Dialogue2100803"]="(Fulkyn gives a cold smile.)\nBut is that truly all? The Barr Venter I know wouldn't go against the spacetime rule just for someone else's love. There must be <color=#CA2E0AFF>another purpose</color> hidden in what seems like a flawless plan.",
    ["Dialogue2100804"]="(Fulkyn doesn't respond right away. Instead, he begins to recount Barr Venter's glorious past.)\nThe Great Sage Barr Venter, hailed across the Republic as the Father of Mechanics, personally led the second technological leap, ushering the nation's mechanical engineering into a new era.",
    ["Dialogue2100805"]="Upon leaving Juno University, he joined Rekenber Corp's research institute—where his brilliance gave rise to androids that would forever alter daily life.",
    ["Dialogue2100806"]="Yet even the greatest minds face setbacks. Though androids eased burdens, they stole livelihoods—and from this progress, chaos bloomed. The resulting unrest peaked with a rebellion led by the mercenary guilds.",
    ["Dialogue2100807"]="After the violent conflict, Barr Venter was deeply shaken. He halted all his research and disappeared on a journey. For nearly <color=#CA2E0AFF>two years</color>, even I had no idea where he'd gone...",
    ["Dialogue2100808"]="You two really are close, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2100809"]="... Your focus, as ever, clings to the trivial. When Barr Venter returned, the spark in him had changed. Within a single year, he constructed the magical guidance system, birthing the age of biomimetic technology. The others watched in awe and silence, too afraid to ask. Even to me—he said nothing.",
    ["Dialogue2100810"]="So where are we going?",
    ["Dialogue2100811"]="The Mysterious Device calculated our next destination: <color=#CA2E0AFF>A.W.706, Lighthalzen</color>. That was the year Barr Venter joined the Rekensheim Institute—a pivotal moment in his life.",
    ["Dialogue2100812"]="Before we start, remember—just <color=#CA2E0AFF>be a good spectator</color>, alright?",
    ["Dialogue2100901"]="(On the steps, a mechanical maid scans you—she appears to be the only living thing in the manor.)\nWel—come.",
    ["Dialogue2100902"]="(The maid's synthetic eyes shift; her artificial mouth lifts slightly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Today's schedule: A.W.704, Alpha Manor</color>. Guest reception—commencing.",
    ["Dialogue2100903"]="(The maid's eyes blink rapidly as her system processes your command.)\nRepeating—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Today's schedule—A.W.704, Alpha Manor</color>. Guest reception—commencing.",
    ["Dialogue2100904"]="Please remain still. Facial data is being recorded...",
    ["Dialogue2100905"]="Facial input—complete.",
    ["Dialogue2100906"]="(The mechanical maid steps aside, bowing deeply at a perfect angle. She speaks as fluently as a real human.)\nThis way, if you will. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>young master</color> awaits your presence.",
    ["Dialogue2101001"]="(A lavishly dressed blond youth waves a wine bottle at you, clearly drunk.)\nHic! Hey there, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor</color>? Great weather today, right? Love your outfit—where'd you get it?",
    ["Dialogue2101002"]="Oh, how unexpected! A mystic in our midst—how refreshing! I'd assumed the institute was filled with boring folks like my <color=#CA2E0AFF>dear parents</color>. Ha!",
    ["Dialogue2101003"]="(Gulp—the blond youth downs a large swig of wine, boldly wiping his mouth.)\nThe invitation reached me—thanks. But I fear my answer will displease you... ha!",
    ["Dialogue2101004"]="I have made my decision! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mechanical engineering</color> has no place in my future! Never again shall I be shackled by cold, lifeless steel!",
    ["Dialogue2101005"]="(Behind him, the mechanical maid clicks as her neck rotates, then quickly turns away.)\nYoung... master...?",
    ["Dialogue2101006"]="Who's calling me?\n(He digs at his ear, then takes another swig.)\nDad? Mom? Are you mad now, huh?",
    ["Dialogue2101007"]="But it's too late! Haven't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>controlled</color> my life long enough? I never wanted to go to Juno University or inherit your research and carry on your dreams!",
    ["Dialogue2101008"]="I am Barr Venter... and I hate you both... sigh...",
    ["Dialogue2101009"]="(The blond youth slumps down, completely deflated.)\nYou see now, Professor... You'd <color=#CA2E0AFF>invite</color> someone like me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim Institute</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2101010"]="... That's not my name. I'm not <color=#CA2E0AFF>Barr Venter</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2101011"]="(The blond youth shoots you a cold, sharp glare.)\nTamaureen! Dismiss our guest! Cancel all appointments for today.",
    ["Dialogue2101012"]="(The maid lifts her skirt slightly and steps forward.)\nHonored guest... if your business is concluded, allow me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort you</color> from Alpha Manor.",
    ["Dialogue2101013"]="(From behind disheveled hair, the future great sage glares—alcohol amplifying his emotions and sharpening his tone.)\nProfessor... there's nothing left for us to speak of.",
    ["Dialogue2101101"]="(Deep in the courtyard, the mechanical maid halts. Her eyes flicker with a strange glint.)\nS-Sorry about this.",
    ["Dialogue2101102"]="(She gently tugs your sleeve, haltingly beginning Barr Venter's story.)\nMaster... Mistress... renowned scholars...",
    ["Dialogue2101103"]="Strict with the young master... (a twisted, programmed weep) The <color=#CA2E0AFF>air disaster</color>...",
    ["Dialogue2101104"]="Alone, always alone, out of place...",
    ["Dialogue2101105"]="Please... help him...",
    ["Dialogue2101106"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Carry on the dream... acknowledge... his love for machines...</color>",
    ["Dialogue2101107"]="(The mechanical maid raises her hand rigidly. On her cold, synthetic face, a flicker of unscripted urgency.)\nThis heirloom... take it... retrieve their <color=#CA2E0AFF>belongings</color>... I beg you...",
    ["Dialogue2101108"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Airship Office</color>... I am no human... I hold no right... to act in his name...",
    ["Dialogue2101109"]="They... created me...",
    ["Dialogue2101110"]="(The crackling of static intensifies. The mechanical maid seems lost in deep system processes—or something resembling thought.)\n\"I\" wish... for the young master... to be happy...",
    ["Dialogue2101201"]="(With swift, practiced keystrokes, the manager pulls up the records of the air disaster from a year ago.)\nAre you here to retrieve the belongings of the noble couple from Alpha Manor?",
    ["Dialogue2101202"]="(The manager exhales in relief, calls over a colleague, then chats with you.)\nOh man, finally! We didn't know what to do with all this stuff. Their kid didn't even care—said the stuff didn't matter. Crazy, right?",
    ["Dialogue2101203"]="Totally. They were always flying around—almost more than our own staff! The poor kid was stuck in a huge manor with just androids. No wonder he turned out weird. We even tried visiting to discuss the compensation but were turned away every time.",
    ["Dialogue2101204"]="Thankfully, the boy was never without comfort—and possessed a gifted mind. A graduate of Juno... he was destined for success. But this heirloom... does that mean he's finally getting over it? That's awesome!",
    ["Dialogue2101205"]="(The manager sighs and picks up a stamp, beginning the paperwork.)\nJust gotta <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask you a couple of questions</color>, then the stuff's yours to take!",
    ["Dialogue2101301"]="(The manager nods and passes over a packed suitcase.)\nYep, that's it. No clue what it's made of, but it stayed intact—even after a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fatal crash</color> like that...",
    ["Dialogue2101401"]="(The mechanical maid takes the suitcase, holding it motionless for a long moment.)\nMaster... Mistress...",
    ["Dialogue2101402"]="(A buzz of static crackles—somehow, \"she\" seems more human now.)\nI know... you always loved the young master. And... he loved you, too...",
    ["Dialogue2101403"]="The young master... has grown up. Come, I will take you to him...",
    ["Dialogue2101404"]="Please, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me</color> as well.",
    ["Dialogue2101501"]="What's there to see?!\n(Barr Venter slams down the bottle, glaring at you.)\nTamaureen, didn't I tell you to send our guest away?!",
    ["Dialogue2101502"]="(The maid shakes her head and steps in front of you.)\nSir... the professor came with goodwill... who came to retrieve your family's belongings.",
    ["Dialogue2101503"]="This is none of your concern.\n(Barr Venter sneers, eyes flicking to the maid.)\nTamaureen... you of all beings should know. That suitcase... is the thing I despise most.",
    ["Dialogue2101504"]="They carried that suitcase across the skies, chasing fame... Never once thought to come home—to this manor, where only you and I remained!",
    ["Dialogue2101505"]="And in the end, they got what they wanted. The thing they cherished like their own eyes—buried with them in that crash. I should thank them, really. They loved that suitcase more than me—their own flesh and blood!",
    ["Dialogue2101506"]="(The crackling static grows louder as Tamaureen's system overloads from emotional conflict. Her eyes glow an ominous red.)\nN-No, young master... that's not how it is...",
    ["Dialogue2101507"]="What's wrong with you?!\n(With urgency, Barr Venter rises and cuts off the maid's power. The huge manor goes quiet—just you and he left.)",
    ["Dialogue2101508"]="Professor, I need an explanation.",
    ["Dialogue2101509"]="...\n(Barr Venter stares at the suitcase in silence, eyes shadowed.)\nThen... <color=#CA2E0AFF>open it for me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2101510"]="This case... forged to endure flame and flood. Within it lies only what my parents held dearest—their research, their life's obsession.",
    ["Dialogue2101511"]="They poured their hearts into machines... and died by them. I swear, I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>never again touch their field</color>. Never face what consumed them.",
    ["Dialogue2101512"]="(Barr Venter takes another swig, his cheeks flushing red.)\nOnce passion is bound by duty, it becomes a prison. Look at me—hic! Does this look like love for machines? No more words... <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the suitcase</color>. Let's end this.",
    ["Dialogue2101601"]="(Within the suitcase—no gears, no tools. Only a letter, placed with intent, resting above fragile ornaments that seem like gifts.)",
    ["Dialogue2101701"]="What's the point of saying all this now?",
    ["Dialogue2101702"]="(Barr Venter clutches the letter, tears falling despite the cold look in his green eyes, dotting the wrinkled paper.)\nTime? Future?",
    ["Dialogue2101703"]="Your toys have dulled... even <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tamaureen</color> has aged and rusted... And still, you hoped that a child who once loathed you could somehow forgive and begin anew?",
    ["Dialogue2101704"]="It's too cruel... I can't do it. How am I supposed to face anything that reminds me of you?",
    ["Dialogue2101705"]="(Barr Venter shakes his head with a bitter smile.)\nProfessor... at this moment, your expression is exactly like my parents.",
    ["Dialogue2101706"]="Stubborn to the end...\n(Barr Venter gently folds the letter and meets your eyes.)\nMy gratitude, Professor. But... my answer remains no.",
    ["Dialogue2101707"]="(Barr Venter casually opens the maid's access panel.)\nTamaureen's a vintage household android—doesn't break easily. And even if she does, she's a simple fix. Do you think I can't even handle that?",
    ["Dialogue2101708"]="...\n(But no matter what he does, Tamaureen's eyes remain dark.)",
    ["Dialogue2101709"]="Tamaureen?\n(Panic rises—he kicks aside his drink, scrambling to recall all he learned at Juno University. But it's no use.)",
    ["Dialogue2101710"]="(His gaze meets yours—desperate, pleading. Surely, someone from Rekensheim could do something. But as a traveler lacking true technical skill, all you can do... is keep the timeline on track.)\nProfessor, please...",
    ["Dialogue2101711"]="Even... the knowledge to repair Tamaureen?\n(Barr Venter pauses, then lets out a knowing, bitter laugh as he meets your eyes.)\nI see.",
    ["Dialogue2101712"]="Professor... I accept. I will <color=#CA2E0AFF>join Rekensheim</color>. And I thank you—for everything today.",
    ["Dialogue2101713"]="This day... will be <color=#CA2E0AFF>etched</color> into the story of my life.",
    ["Dialogue2101801"]="Thanatos has lost his mind... will you come with me?",
    ["Dialogue2101802"]="But I believe he'll return. Don't you, sir?",
    ["Dialogue2101803"]="... I just hope your wish comes true.",
    ["Dialogue2101804"]="Let me remain at your side... until his return or until you choose to leave this place with me.",
    ["Dialogue2101805"]="Sir, there's no need for that.",
    ["Dialogue2101806"]="It doesn't matter anymore... We've already lost everything.",
    ["Dialogue2101901"]="Huh? Haven't seen you before.\n(The mercenary leader sizes you up and down.)\nThis camp's full. If you want to stay, it won't be easy.",
    ["Dialogue2101902"]="Not a refugee, huh? Then what're you doing here? People here came back to rebuild after the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mercenary uprising</color>. Our republic's in ruins—we're doing what we can. Though I'm a mercenary for hire... for my homeland, I stand as a volunteer.",
    ["Dialogue2101903"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>A.W.716—those android things stole our jobs, so of course we ended up at war!</color> You're acting really weird, you know that? What are you even doing here? Move along, don't mess with our work.",
    ["Dialogue2101904"]="Hmm... you do look like one of us, but man, your equipment is way over the top! Anyway, I run this camp—don't go pulling any stunts around me.",
    ["Dialogue2101905"]="Relative? I know everyone here; I don't think your relative is here! Anyway, I run this camp—don't go pulling any stunts around me.",
    ["Dialogue2101906"]="Trying to hang around and gather intel, huh?\n(The captain tosses you a tool kit.)\nPerfect timing—we've got a few shaky posts that need fixing.",
    ["Dialogue2101907"]="Come on—<color=#CA2E0AFF>volunteer</color>!",
    ["Dialogue2102001"]="(The captain weighs a tool in his hand, nodding in approval.)\nHuh, not bad at all. Once Barr Venter packs up, maybe you can grab his bunk.",
    ["Dialogue2102002"]="Yeah—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Barr Venter</color> came here just like you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>lost and broken</color>. Then, he threw himself into work and earned everyone's trust.",
    ["Dialogue2102003"]="He doesn't talk much, but whenever he does, it's always something crucial for our rebuilding efforts. Barr Venter is the reason why this camp is still standing through storms and rain!",
    ["Dialogue2102004"]="Who can say for sure? A man like Barr Venter—he's not meant for a place so small. Sooner or later, he'll end up in the capital. Lately, he's been climbing the mountains to stare into the distance. We think he's preparing to leave.",
    ["Dialogue2102005"]="How would I know? But every time we talk about <color=#CA2E0AFF>war or androids</color>, he just grabs a bottle and goes up the mountain to drink alone. I'm guessing it has something to do with those androids.",
    ["Dialogue2102006"]="Who came up with those metal hunks anyway? Watching their own kind lose their jobs and suffer in war—how could they not feel <color=#CA2E0AFF>guilty</color>?",
    ["Dialogue2102101"]="(The young messenger wrings his hands, clearly nervous as he joins your conversation.)\nSorry to interrupt, but I heard this Adventurer's been asking about Barr Venter. Do you know him?",
    ["Dialogue2102102"]="I've got a letter for Barr Venter, but for some reason, he refuses to accept it the moment he sees the postmark. He insists I send it back.",
    ["Dialogue2102103"]="(He raises the envelope—clearly stamped with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim Institute</color>.)\nI've got no choice but to keep bouncing between here and the institute. But now you're saying he might leave? How am I supposed to find him then?!",
    ["Dialogue2102104"]="He doesn't... want to work? The institute's pressuring us, saying if Barr Venter doesn't <color=#CA2E0AFF>show up on time</color>, they'll blame the post office for not delivering the letter. The mercenary uprising just ended—I need this job to support my family!",
    ["Dialogue2102105"]="(Maybe relating to the situation, the usually quiet mercenary captain's expression softens.)\nGive me the letter—I'll pass it to Barr Venter.",
    ["Dialogue2102106"]="You?",
    ["Dialogue2102107"]="Yeah, we set up a meeting to check on the camp work—should be right about now.",
    ["Dialogue2102108"]="(He takes the letter from the grateful Messager.)\nTsk, let's see which genius is nagging Barr Venter to get back to work.",
    ["Dialogue2102109"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Sender: Fulkyn?</color>",
    ["Dialogue2102110"]="Gah! Why are you yelling all of a sudden?! Wait, you know someone from the institute?! Hey, Barr Venter!",
    ["Dialogue2102111"]="(He waves toward someone in the distance. Knowing it's not wise to reveal yourself, you decide to leave quickly.)\nHuh? Where're you going? Weren't you the one asking everyone about Barr Venter?!",
    ["Dialogue2102201"]="(The girl's spirit gazes at your face, curious.)\nDo I know you from somewhere?",
    ["Dialogue2102202"]="You... it is you! The brave soul who helped Thanatos and me fight Morroc in Glast Heim! Do you remember? Queen Hermes made a deal with Morroc to destroy the Glast Heim as revenge against King Schmidt. You stepped up and defeated many powerful monsters.",
    ["Dialogue2102203"]="(The ghost maiden is overjoyed to meet someone familiar, circling around you as she recalls your past battles together.)\nBut... it's been <color=#CA2E0AFF>hundreds of years</color>. Why haven't you aged at all? Did I mistake you for someone else?",
    ["Dialogue2102204"]="Is there something you can't talk about? Adventurer, I'm just a spirit now. You can tell me anything.",
    ["Dialogue2102205"]="(The ghost maiden playfully raises a finger to her lips.)\nI will keep it a secret!",
    ["Dialogue2102206"]="Mhm... Barr Venter really is a kind person. Ah, so you couldn't interact with people on this timeline. That's why you kept silent? But then—what made you speak up now?",
    ["Dialogue2102207"]="!!!\n(The ghost maiden's face fills with disbelief.)\nWhy?! I'm already dead, aren't I?!",
    ["Dialogue2102208"]="... I understand. So, if I keep seeing Barr Venter, he won't return to the Rekensheim Institute as history intended. And after that, the entire future will change—countless lives, including yours, will be affected.",
    ["Dialogue2102209"]="I'm sorry...\n(The ghost maiden lowers her head in sorrow.)\nI just saw someone who was hurting like I was and couldn't help but want to comfort him.",
    ["Dialogue2102210"]="Perhaps this is what it means to be a ghost—to disappear, to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sever all bonds</color>, and purge the echoes of what should never have lingered.",
    ["Dialogue2102211"]="Don't worry, I understand. From now on, I won't <color=#CA2E0AFF>appear in front of Barr Venter</color> again. Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait here</color> for a moment—Barr Venter will return soon.",
    ["Dialogue2102212"]="As for me... It's time for me to show both you and him my resolve.\n(The girl's spirit fades from into the air, leaving no trace behind.)",
    ["Dialogue2102301"]="(Above the ruins, the Great Sage stands poised—blonde hair, green eyes—and the memory strikes you in that moment. This is how you first met, back in A.W.704 at Alpha Manor.)\nI was sixteen... when you trailed behind Tamaureen, entering Alpha Manor as if led by fate.",
    ["Dialogue2102302"]="Perhaps it is only fitting... to call you \"Professor?\" You, who traversed time again and again to forge the man I've become—a fool who defied the supreme rules of spacetime and your most flawless creation.",
    ["Dialogue2102303"]="(Barr Venter smiles with both grace and cruelty.)\nIsn't that so? Every artist lives for the praise of others. Then come—let us <color=#CA2E0AFF>reflect</color> upon how you carved \"Barr Venter\" into being... across the spacetime.",
    ["Dialogue2102304"]="When I was sixteen, you visited Alpha Manor and helped young Barr Venter resolve his issues with his parents, which directly led to his joining Rekensheim.",
    ["Dialogue2102305"]="By the second year, he had achieved what seemed a humble milestone—ushering androids into the fabric of labor. The world crowned him \"Father of Mechanics,\" raising him high on a pedestal woven from applause and prestige.",
    ["Dialogue2102306"]="Yet his fellow humans, stripped of livelihood, saw only betrayal. Fueled by resentment toward the tireless, soulless machines, they rose in revolt—obliterating Rekensheim R&D Dept Sector One. And the war that followed crushed his spirit. He wandered the world, seeking truth—though perhaps, in his heart, he knew the world had no answers to give.",
    ["Dialogue2102307"]="Thankfully, he met Lush—a gentle, kind soul. He chose to stay by her side, never returning to the research institute even after it was rebuilt.",
    ["Dialogue2102308"]="But then... you appeared again.",
    ["Dialogue2102309"]="When I was twenty-six, you stood once again in my path—at Juperos Plains and persuaded Lush to stop responding to my calls—taking away my only comfort and planting the idea of creating a mechanical version of her to stay by my side.",
    ["Dialogue2102310"]="Yes, you did preserve the timeline. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Because everything you just did in the past—was always meant to be done by you.</color>",
    ["Dialogue2102311"]="Let me guess—who's the one pulling the strings behind the brave Adventurer, sending them into other people's lives over and over again? When he made plans for you, did he promise it would all go smoothly, that you'd never make mistakes, never suffer punishment like I did for breaking spacetime rules?",
    ["Dialogue2102312"]="Heh... Professor Fulkyn is still the same as ever—always speaking half of the truth. In that case, let me tell you one more thing.",
    ["Dialogue2102313"]="The letter urging me back to the research institute—wasn't it signed by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Fulkyn</color>? He and I have deep ties. He's the one who <color=#CA2E0AFF>invited</color> me to join Rekensheim. After my parents died, he kept in contact with me. He was the <color=#CA2E0AFF>director of Rekensheim Institute</color> and a key member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2102314"]="That's why both Tamaureen and I mistook you for Professor Fulkyn. After I joined Rekensheim, I tried to thank you in person—but realized this \"Professor Fulkyn\" was someone else entirely.",
    ["Dialogue2102315"]="I carried that doubt with me for a long time—until I saw someone by Professor Fulkyn's side, traveling through time with him, who had the exact same face as the person I remembered.",
    ["Dialogue2102316"]="And then it struck me—<color=#CA2E0AFF>the one I met at sixteen... was none other than you, returned from the future through the tides of time</color>.",
    ["Dialogue2102317"]="By the look on your face... you knew nothing.\n(Barr Venter leans in, his smile cold and unreadable)\nAnyway, enough catching up. Isn't it about time for you to go back to Professor Fulkyn?",
    ["Dialogue2102318"]="And yet, can you still call him your ally without a shadow of a doubt? Ah... how I await this moment—two artists who've carved my entire life... what fate will you now carve for yourselves?",
    ["Dialogue2102319"]="(He waves as he leaves)\nDon't let me down, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue2102401"]="(Fulkyn looks at you anxiously as you return)\nThere was a glitch when the Mysterious Device activated. The coordinates shifted—are you hurt?",
    ["Dialogue2102402"]="(After hearing your story, Fulkyn falls into deep silence)\nAn ouroboros—devouring its tail, endlessly repeating. Perhaps we are already trapped in the vortex of time. Without a <color=#CA2E0AFF>starting point</color>, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>loop</color> will never end.",
    ["Dialogue2102403"]="...\n(Your words vanish into silence. The scholar, stooped in thought, continues his careful tuning of the Mysterious Device—perhaps pondering enigmas far beyond your reach.)",
    ["Dialogue2102404"]="Barr Venter—I believe he's the one who caused the coordinate shift. Given his interference, I'll need to carefully consider our next steps. Until then, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>do not disturb</color> me.",
    ["Dialogue2102405"]="(He lifts his gaze, eyes gleaming with unspoken weight)\nAnd you—perhaps now is the time... to decide if your <color=#CA2E0AFF>trust</color> still lies with me.",
    ["Dialogue2102501"]="The successor of Odin's Bloodline, you've arrived. I foresaw a threat from the Dimensional Gap, a vast and evil force that had crossed over from another world.",
    ["Dialogue2102502"]="(The goddess nods.)\nThat's right. Ever since they arrived, this evil force has been after a silver-haired girl and her friends. Their actions will bring massive destruction to Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue2102503"]="Fear not. The travelers from another world will be an exceptional help to you. Adventurer, you must set off now to find them.",
    ["Dialogue2102504"]="You will find them in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>. Be careful not to judge by what you see—while these travelers don't have great power, they possess unmatched courage and resilience. Most importantly, they have the ability to <color=#CA2E0AFF>change everything</color>, which is vital for our victory.",
    ["Dialogue2102601"]="Umm... You've been staring at me for a while. Do we know each other?\nAnyway, glad you're here. Have you seen a breathtaking pretty silver-haired girl around here?\nWe got split up... Oh, and... what is this place?",
    ["Dialogue2102602"]="What? You're telling me this is Prontera in Midgard?\nI have no idea what you're talking about...\nAll I recall is going out with Mili and Rem, and then we ran into a Dimensional Gap...",
    ["Dialogue2102603"]="Another world, huh? You've got to be kidding me... But, looking at the buildings and clothes, it's definitely different from Lugunica... Wait a minute...\n(Subaru Natsuki gets suspicious.)\nWho are you? How do you know I'm from another world?",
    ["Dialogue2102604"]="What?! Are the evil forces from my world here too? And they've been chasing after Emilia and Rem?\nI can't make sense of all this, but things are looking really bad... Have you seen them? As I told you earlier, one is a breathtakingly pretty silver-haired girl, and the other is a short blue-haired girl in a maid outfit.",
    ["Dialogue2102605"]="Ugh... I must find them quickly!",
    ["Dialogue2102606"]="That'd be great, but... are you sure?",
    ["Dialogue2102607"]="So, you're doing it for the world, and I'm doing it for Mili and Rem, but we're facing the same enemy. In that case, I'm counting on you!\n(Subaru Natsuki slowly clenches his fist.)\nEmilia, Rem, hang in there. I must save you!",
    ["Dialogue2102701"]="Adventurer?\n(Rem bows gracefully in her maid outfit.)\nHi there. Is there something I can help you with?",
    ["Dialogue2102702"]="Is that so...\nWell, if you don't mind, I'd like to talk to you about...",
    ["Dialogue2102703"]="I heard there are lots of playscripts and poems in this world.\nI'd love to read some if I get the chance...",
    ["Dialogue2102704"]="So, Adventurer, do you happen to know where I could find those books?\nIf I ever come across a good story, I want to share it with Subaru.",
    ["Dialogue2102705"]="(Rem's eyes sparkle slightly.)\nIs there such a person who travels all over the world and sings about the deeds of heroes?\nThere are bards too!",
    ["Dialogue2102706"]="If so, would you please buy me a copy?\nOf course, I will cover the cost!",
    ["Dialogue2102801"]="Adventurer?\n(W bows slightly.)\nAre you here to schedule something with Kafra Corporation?",
    ["Dialogue2102802"]="Oh, you're searching for Morts. Great! I know exactly where he is!",
    ["Dialogue2102803"]="(W looks a bit embarrassed.)\nActually, I just came back from Isabella's tavern, and Morts is over there.\nHe... seems a bit drunk, and Isabella is struggling to deal with him. You should go check on him now!",
    ["Dialogue2102804"]="By the way!",
    ["Dialogue2102805"]="Please don't tell Dyplon that I snuck off to the tavern during working hours. Otherwise, I'll get yelled at again! Please keep it a secret, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue2102901"]="Burp!\n(Morts let out a hiccup, clearly drunk.)\nI live for the drink! Tomorrow can wait!",
    ["Dialogue2102902"]="Adventurer? Oh, it's you! Come, have a drink with me!",
    ["Dialogue2102903"]="Poetry collection? It's not for sale! My masterpieces aren't something money can buy!",
    ["Dialogue2102904"]="Ahem... Well, how about this? If you get me a glass of Rose Red Wine, I'll think about giving you a copy of my latest piece. I might even include you in my poetry, granting you immortality in song.",
    ["Dialogue2102905"]="Go on, go on!\n(Morts urges, lying back down slowly.)\nI trust you!",
    ["Dialogue2103001"]="This Morts is out of hand, Adventurer. Leave him be!",
    ["Dialogue2103002"]="(Isabella looks shocked, then checks your forehead.)\nNo fever... This drunkard has been running up a tab for ages, and you're still trying to get him more wine? Why?",
    ["Dialogue2103003"]="I see... But listen, Adventurer, even if it sounds harsh, I won't hand you that wine. He was already misbehaving, hitting on the Obeaune earlier while drunk. One more drink, and who knows what he'll do!",
    ["Dialogue2103004"]="If that's the case...\nHere's the deal: the kitchen's out of Lunatic Meat. Could you bring me ten pieces, Adventurer? Then I'll give you a glass of Rose Red Wine. Deal?",
    ["Dialogue2103101"]="Impressive as always, Adventurer, you're fast!\nBy the way... didn't Morts mention putting you in his poetry? Immortality in song—doesn't that sound appealing?",
    ["Dialogue2103102"]="I knew it. Here, take it, and let the Bard know this is his final drink today.",
    ["Dialogue2103201"]="(Morts sniffs the wine deeply.)\nAh! No doubt, this is the best wine in the tavern!\nAdventurer, you're truly my best friend! I'll write you a poem!",
    ["Dialogue2103202"]="Here, just take it! We're best friends, aren't we? No need to ask for such a small thing. Now let me enjoy my drink!",
    ["Dialogue2103301"]="So, this is the poetry collection you mentioned?\n(Rem's eyes are shining with stars, looking thrilled.)",
    ["Dialogue2103302"]="Ah, no spoilers, please! I want to keep the surprise for later.\nAnyway, thank you so much for bringing this to me, Adventurer.\nPlease accept this as a thank you for taking up your time. It's alright. Just take it.",
    ["Dialogue2103401"]="Adventurer, ever since I came to this world, I've realized something...",
    ["Dialogue2103402"]="\nThe mana flow here is a little different compared to my world.\nThere are lesser spirits in this world, too, and I'm trying to talk to them, but it just hasn't gone well...",
    ["Dialogue2103403"]="They're spirits that haven't grown up yet.\nMy mind's still a bit fuzzy, so I can't ask them much about this world...",
    ["Dialogue2103404"]="\nStill, it's a great opportunity, and I'm really curious about this world, whether it's the spirits or the magic here.\nAdventurer, do you know where I can learn more about the magic here?",
    ["Dialogue2103405"]="(Emilia had a look of frustration on her face.)\nYou mean Geffen, the city of magic?\nWhat should I do... If I want to borrow Geffen's books, someone needs to get an ID for me. We didn't have that on our surprise visit.",
    ["Dialogue2103406"]="Can I ask you for help?\nThank you so much.\nOf course, if you can borrow it for me, I'll reward you properly!",
    ["Dialogue2103501"]="What brings you here today?\nYou're always so busy—I doubt you're here to read!",
    ["Dialogue2103502"]="Now that you mention it, I do recall that traveler from another world.\nA few days back, a lady with stunning silver hair was here looking to borrow magic books...",
    ["Dialogue2103503"]="Unfortunately, without a proper ID, she was only allowed to borrow regular books...\n(Winry shrugged with a hint of resignation.)",
    ["Dialogue2103504"]="Sorry, Adventurer, rules are rules, and everyone has to follow them!",
    ["Dialogue2103505"]="However... if Archmage Jesqurienne can vouch for this traveler from another world and prove she isn't up to any mischief with magic, then we might be able to work something out.",
    ["Dialogue2103601"]="(Jesqurienne sizes you up and down.)\nLong time no see... So, our hero won't show up without a reason. What do you need help with?",
    ["Dialogue2103602"]="I see...\n(Jesqurienne frowns slightly.)\nAdventurer, this does go against the Mage Guild's Magic Library Regulations... unless...",
    ["Dialogue2103603"]="Unless you can show that this otherworldly guest intends to use this magic book purely for learning, not harm.",
    ["Dialogue2103604"]="I see. If she's the prophesied one, I believe she can be trusted.\n(Jesqurienne pens a letter.)\nTake this to Winry, and she'll give her the right books.",
    ["Dialogue2103701"]="You're impressive, Adventurer, getting Jesqurienne on board...",
    ["Dialogue2103702"]="Let me see...\nAh, this one! Beginner's Magic Guide—it's mostly beginner spells but has plenty of foundational info that should suit your friend.\nRemember, it needs to be back in seven days!",
    ["Dialogue2103801"]="Beginner's Magic Guide...\n So with this, I'll be able to learn a lot about the world, right?",
    ["Dialogue2103802"]="So, the librarian was a lady.\nSpeaking of which, she was really tough on me when I tried borrowing books before... But I guess she's actually really kind...",
    ["Dialogue2103803"]="Adventurer, thank you so much for working hard for me.\nThis is just a little something to show my gratitude... I hope you'll accept it.",
    ["Dialogue2103804"]="Well, you've helped me a lot.\nIf you need anything in the future, let me help you.",
    ["Dialogue2103901"]="Meow?\n Adventurer? Wow, for someone so busy, you actually made time to visit me, meow?",
    ["Dialogue2103902"]="(Xavier nods proudly.)\nGood, I didn't expect my best student would drop by to see his mentor.\nMeow... showing up empty-handed? Isn't that a bit rude?",
    ["Dialogue2103903"]="How about this!\n(Xavier's whiskers perk up, and his cat's face shows a mischievous grin.)\nLately, there's been this guy dressed in strange exotic clothes, staring at me while I fish. He doesn't seem dangerous, but his constant staring is really messing with my fishing vibe! It's gotten so bad I can't even enjoy my dried fish in peace anymore!",
    ["Dialogue2103904"]="I can't let this go on, and it's ruining my life! Adventurer, could you find out who this guy is? Oh, and let him know that if he wants fishing lessons, he should just ask me directly!",
    ["Dialogue2104001"]="Alright, I think I'm set.",
    ["Dialogue2104002"]="All I need to do is ask the cat to give it to me, and I'm good.",
    ["Dialogue2104003"]="AHHHHHH!\nAdventurer?! You gave me a heart attack. What do you want?",
    ["Dialogue2104004"]="So, I've been spotted all along...\n(Subaru Natsuki rubs the back of his head, embarrassed.)\nActually, there is nothing particularly important. The other day, I was just strolling around the south gate when I saw that cat catching a fish.",
    ["Dialogue2104005"]="(Subaru Natsuki's eyes gleam with excitement.)\nThat's right! It looks exactly like the fish from my hometown, and it's delicious!\nYou know, the kind with red scales.\nSince I saw it, I haven't been able to get it out of my head. I just want to get some of that fish so Mili and the others can feast on it. I want to host a seafood party as well, so Rem and I are setting things up right now.",
    ["Dialogue2104006"]="By the way, adventurer, I have something to trouble you.\nI want to buy that fish from Xavier, but I'm short on ingredients and still trying to figure out the party menu.\nSo, if it's alright with you... could you buy it for me? I promise to treat you to some amazing sashimi after!",
    ["Dialogue2104101"]="(Xavier's tail swishes a few times on the ground.)\nSo, did you find the rude person spying on me?",
    ["Dialogue2104102"]="Oh, that's how it is. In that case, I can go along with it. Have him come by tomorrow to learn my fishing tricks.\nLooks like even travelers from another world can't resist my fishing skills!",
    ["Dialogue2104103"]="Just buying a fish, huh?\n(Xavier's tail drops in disappointment.)\nSorry, Adventurer, I'd be happy to sell you one, but Isabella, from the Rose Red Tavern, just placed an order for all of them.",
    ["Dialogue2104104"]="So, if your otherworldly friend wants to try some tasty Sea Bream, it looks like you'll have to do it yourself.",
    ["Dialogue2104201"]="That's the one!",
    ["Dialogue2104202"]="Adventurer, thank you so much! That takes care of the seafood.",
    ["Dialogue2104203"]="(Subaru Natsuki looks a bit embarrassed.)\nActually, Adventurer, I've got one more favor to ask...\nYou know, being new around here, there's a lot of things I'm not familiar with...\nCan you do me another favor if you can...?",
    ["Dialogue2104204"]="Really? You're a lifesaver! Don't worry, I'll make it worth your while.\nI'm just missing the last ramen dish and a few magic props for the party.\nIf you bring me what I need, I'll reward you.\nThanks a lot!",
    ["Dialogue2200001"]="Adventurer! I'm gathering material for my next sci-fi novel, but my camera is not working! Could you please take a photo inside the lab for me? I'd really appreciate it!",
    ["Dialogue2200002"]="Thank you so much! If the book gets published, I'll send you a whole set!",
    ["Dialogue2200003"]="This place is like the peak of academic research—I really want to know more about it! Adventurer, could you interview the lab staff for me? I'm too shy to ask myself...",
    ["Dialogue2200004"]="What do I think of my research? Uh... sigh... regret. Just pure regret. I never should've joined this lab back in school...",
    ["Dialogue2200005"]="\"(You tell Ram what Jane thinks about the research.)\nOh, noooo! My essay is doomed! It's all over, waaah—\"",
    ["Dialogue2200006"]="You're the one my sister sent? Thank you... Could you please find some healing potions for me? I can't move right now...",
    ["Dialogue2200007"]="Sorry... I thought I could handle an adventure on my own... but I was wrong. Let's head back to my sister.",
    ["Dialogue2510902"]="The <color=#ffe788><color=#ff5252>Red Demon Tower</color>'s impenetrable barrier has been dispelled!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2510903"]="The <color=#ffe788><color=#ffe788>Yellow Demon Tower</color>'s impenetrable barrier has been dispelled!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2510904"]="The <color=#ffe788><color=#528fff>Blue Demon Tower</color>'s impenetrable barrier has been dispelled!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2510905"]="Be careful, disaster strikes when there are no targets in range where the sickle falls!",
    ["Dialogue2510906"]="The destroyed demon crystals will be cleansed into Emperium. Avoid Baphomet's lava hell!",
    ["Dialogue2510907"]="Baphomet's afterimage charges up faster when it is near a Demon Tower. You can only deal damage to it if you have the same enchantment as the afterimage.",
    ["Dialogue2610902"]="<color=#ffe788>Pull these negative-emotion monsters to the rooms on the left and right and kill them!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2610903"]="<color=#ffe788>Rooms on both sides are permanently open!</color>",
    ["Dialogue2610904"]="<color=#ffe788>Please head to nearby areas searching for totem monsters!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27000101"]="<color=#ffe788>Defeat </color><color=#ff5252>Goblin</color><color=#ffe788> with </color><color=#ff5252>Multi Firing</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000102"]="<color=#ffe788>Place</color> <color=#ff5252>Claymore Trap</color><color=#ffe788> in the path of <color=#ff5252>Marduk</color>.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27000103"]="<color=#ff5252>Watch out!</color><color=#ff5252> Baphomet is here!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27000104"]="<color=#ffe788>The trial will start soon!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27000105"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. You've defeated a powerful demon.",
    ["Dialogue27000106"]="Baphomet is defeated. Complete your trial!",
    ["Dialogue27000107"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Provoke</color><color=#ffe788> to get Threat from monsters</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000108"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Zeny Storm</color><color=#ffe788> to defeat</color><color=#ff5252> Skeleton Worker</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000109"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Cart Blitz</color><color=#ffe788> to crush</color><color=#ff5252> Giearth</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000110"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color> <color=#ff5252>Charge Attack</color> <color=#ffe788>when mounted to defeat </color><color=#ff5252>Zombie</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000111"]="<color=#ffe788>Use </color><color=#ff5252>Bowling Bash</color><color=#ffe788> to gather monsters around you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000112"]="<color=#ff5252>Hide</color><color=#ffe788> to clear Threat from monsters</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000113"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Venom Dust</color><color=#ffe788> to attack </color><color=#ff5252>Merman</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000114"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Mirror Image</color><color=#ffe788> to defeat</color><color=#ff5252> Wooden Dummy</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000115"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color><color=#ff5252> Signum Crucis</color><color=#ffe788> to attack</color><color=#ff5252> Bathory</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000116"]="<color=#ffe788>The priest can also deal damage to Undead/Demons with healing skills; </color><color=#ffe788>use</color><color=#ff5252> Sanctuary</color><color=#ffe788> to attack </color><color=#ff5252>Mummy</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000121"]="<color=#ffe788>Use counter element to deal greater damage to monsters</color>.",
    ["Dialogue27000122"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color> <color=#ff5252>Meteor Storm</color> <color=#ffe788>to defeat Hodes</color>",
    ["Dialogue27000123"]="<color=#ffe788>Use</color> <color=#ff5252>Earth Spike</color> <color=#ffe788>to defeat Hornets</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101001"]="<color=#ffe788>The path to the left armory platform is unlocked.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101002"]="<color=#ffe788>The path to the right armory platform is unlocked.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101003"]="<color=#ffe788>The boss has moved to Area 2. Chase it now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101004"]="<color=#ffe788>The boss has moved to Area 3. Chase it now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101013"]="<color=#ffe788>The door of the left Energy Extractor is unlocked.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101014"]="<color=#ffe788>The door of the right Energy Extractor is unlocked.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101015"]="The door of the top Energy Extractor is unlocked.",
    ["Dialogue27101016"]="<color=#ffe788>The Energy Extractor on the left has been destroyed. No more monsters spawning on the left.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101017"]="<color=#ffe788>The Energy Extractor on the right has been destroyed. No more monsters spawning on the right.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101018"]="<color=#ffe788>The Energy Extractor on the top has been destroyed. No more monsters spawning on the top.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101019"]="<color=#ffe788>All 3 Energy Extractors have been destroyed. The boss has appeared in the central area.</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101023"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper Type II has initiated the destruction sequence. All units will be destroyed after <color=#528fff>3 minutes</color>! Destroy the Energy Extractors now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101024"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper Type II will destroy all units after <color=#528fff>2 minutes</color>! Destroy the Energy Extractors now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101025"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper Type II will destroy all units after <color=#528fff>1 minute</color>! Destroy the Energy Extractors now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101026"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper Type II will destroy all units after <color=#528fff>10 seconds</color>! Destroy the Energy Extractors now!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101027"]="<color=#ffe788>Ah... stowaway from another dimension, are you Verus people's last hope?</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101028"]="<color=#ffe788>Is this all you've got? Do you want to take me on with that? Hahaha! Humans are all equally foolish!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101029"]="<color=#ffe788>Amusing. Entertain me with more of your struggles! Who knows, maybe you're worth keeping around...</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101030"]="<color=#ffe788>I am the master of Ymir's Heart, the deity of machines! Surrender now, or face annihilation...</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101031"]="<color=#ffe788>Do you see? Only I can wield the full power of Ymir's Heart. The fall of Verus marks the rise of a god!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101032"]="<color=#ffe788>Not nearly enough... All of you, Ymir, Midgard... hand over your power!</color>",
    ["Dialogue27101033"]="<color=#ffe788>You've gained 1 stack of energy.</color>",
    ["Dialogue30000001"]="<color=#ffe788>The boss has entered the Berserk state!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30000002"]="<color=#ffe788>The boss has lost its patience. Entering the Berserk state in 10 seconds!</color>",
    ["Dialogue300001101"]="<color=#ffe788>The dean found a strange spore in the sewer </color><color=#ffe788>for you to train against</color>.",
    ["Dialogue300001201"]="<color=#ffe788>Oh no!</color> <color=#ffe788>The spore has mutated and is dividing into more spores</color>! <color=#ffe788>Quickly, use your </color><color=#ff5252>skills</color><color=#ffe788> to destroy them.</color>",
    ["Dialogue300001301"]="<color=#ffe788>The Goblin clan is united and </color><color=#ffe788>gangs up on enemies</color>. <color=#ffe788>Use </color><color=#ff5252>area of effect skills</color><color=#ffe788> to destroy them all at once</color>.",
    ["Dialogue300001401"]="<color=#ffe788>Now for your final trial! </color><color=#ffe788>Destroy the Goblin Leader!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3000101"]="Welcome back, adventurer. It's been a while since we last met, and you've become an outstanding swordsman. I think it's time for you to take the next step forward.",
    ["Dialogue3000102"]="As swordsmen, we should take our place at the vanguard and protect our teammates with our lives. All swordsmen who share this fearless spirit seek out Captain Hallam of the Rune Kingdom Royal Chivalry to become an honorable knight so that they can continue to do their duty.",
    ["Dialogue3000103"]="Haha! I knew you were born to be a knight as soon as I saw that look of anticipation in your eyes! Go to Captain Hallam and complete his trial. May you prevail in all your battles!",
    ["Dialogue3000201"]="This magic is so powerful and full of potential... Welcome back. You are now a capable mage. I'm sure you must be curious about how you can improve.",
    ["Dialogue3000202"]="A mage stands behind their teammates and wreaks havoc on their enemies with the power of the elements. Iskren, master of Geffen's Mage Guild, will teach you how to wield this powerful magic to become a wizard.",
    ["Dialogue3000203"]="Take care not to be consumed by the power of the elements and don't lose yourself in the storm of magic. I hope you will be able to pass her trials and make a triumphant return.",
    ["Dialogue3000204"]="Sages empower teammates with the elemental power, finding a balance between offense and defense in obscure magical texts. If you are interested in becoming a Sage, Great Sage Kroneika in the Mjolnir Mountains will guide you.",
    ["Dialogue3000205"]="Magic takes us out of the ordinary, and the study of magic makes everything return to being ordinary. I hope you can maintain your clarity until the very end.",
    ["Dialogue3000301"]="Welcome back, adventurer! Odin has witnessed your growth and I can sense his approval. It is time for you to choose to continue practicing Odin's faith.",
    ["Dialogue3000302"]="An outstanding acolyte loathes all that is evil and views all undead creatures as their lifelong enemies. Acolytes have a merciful heart and bless their teammates with Odin's power. If you have no doubts about this mission and wish to travel further along this path, go to Bishop Wolmas at the Prontera Church to become a priest.",
    ["Dialogue3000303"]="Your soul and your eyes are so pure that they seem to radiate a holy light. I know you will pass Bishop Wolmas' trial. In of name Odin the Allfather, I pray for your triumphant return.",
    ["Dialogue3000304"]="An outstanding Monk evolves soul, body, and spirit for a higher calling. If you are ready to carry the guilt of the world and embark on a new path, then undertake the trials with Master Peerless Jin in Payon South!",
    ["Dialogue3000401"]="Heh, you look like you're in good shape, adventurer. I can tell from how you're holding your bow that you're already able to wield it as naturally as your own limbs. It's time to teach you something new.",
    ["Dialogue3000402"]="An archer lives and dies by their bow. They are as sharp as an arrow in flight, and just as deadly. Their only mission is to dispatch their enemies with ruthless efficiency. If you have become accustomed to acting as I have described, you are ready to continue learning the secrets of the bow. It is time for you to become a hunter. Master Sky Euin of the Payon Archer Village is waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue3000403"]="Your eyes that are as sharp as arrows have given you away. Haha! I already know your answer. Advance toward the target in your heart. I pray for your triumphant return.",
    ["Dialogue3000501"]="Oh? Your footwork is looking good. It's been a while since I last met a thief with as much potential as you. However, you must know that the path ahead of you is paved with thorns.",
    ["Dialogue3000502"]="Hiding in the shadows, you will always be watching your enemies' backs as you prepare to deal a fatal blow. This is the bloody and dangerous life of a thief. Hassan, master of Morroc's Assassins Guild, will always welcome any thief adventurer who wants to learn these skills.",
    ["Dialogue3000503"]="You will need to confront your fear of death and the condemnation of the \"just,\" as well as torture your enemies with poison. Fighting fairly is just a joke to you. Everything you do is for the sake of victory and your own justice.",
    ["Dialogue3000504"]="Do you feel lost? It doesn't matter. Heed these words: Everything you do is for your own justice. If you choose to be an assassin, the assassin life will choose you as well. I believe you'll shake off your doubts and return here.",
    ["Dialogue3000505"]="The Rogues... hah! Perhaps they're the most freedom-loving bunch of people. Acting provocatively, making poison, and backstabbing... They could play the good and evil guys to rob you blind. Unlike Assassins who serve the darkness or High Priests who embrace the light, Rogues play on the gray side of morality.",
    ["Dialogue3000506"]="Just so they're special, they don't have an official group.\n(Moxie covers her mouth as she laughs at you, seeing your confusion)\nWell... Perhaps an old friend of mine in Weinst street is willing to help you out.",
    ["Dialogue3000507"]="No more questions.\n(Moxie puts a period on your question with an indifferent look on her face, handing you a crumpled piece of letter.)\nHere.",
    ["Dialogue3000508"]="(It seems like she didn't hear you as she kept sniffing the rose. Maybe she just didn't care about your question.)\nKeep your eyes open and make sure you deliver this letter to the most Rogue-looking person in Desert Green Tavern. Take it easy, and you can always bet on my expertise as a class master. However, if you aren't able to identify which one it is, you should give up being a Rogue.",
    ["Dialogue3000601"]="Haha! What do you think about the adventures of a merchant? Don't you think it's interesting? Do you want to know of more interesting routes that you can explore?",
    ["Dialogue3000602"]="Stop and think. Where does our power come from? Exactly! From shiny Zeny! What's the most reliable way to make money? To make your own wares and sell them! Blacksmith is the class to choose for all adventurers who desire this! The most famous blacksmith instructor is naturally Sindre of Alberta!",
    ["Dialogue3000603"]="If you become a blacksmith, your furnace will be your partner. The more you sweat, the more muscular your body will become! The shining light that appears when you finish making something will fill you with an immense feeling of achievement! You'll definitely fall in love with this lifestyle!",
    ["Dialogue3000604"]="You can choose to become an Alchemist if you don't want to research rough ores or deal with sparks sputtering everywhere! Trust me. Countless people will pay a lot of Zeny for your potion. Nicolas, the Alchemist Guild's leader, is very concerned with the development and growth of recruits, and you can pay him a visit in Al De Baran!",
    ["Dialogue3000605"]="I'm proud of you, my student!\n(Hamid gives you a praising thumbs up.)\nEven though these Alchemists bury their heads in their own world, I guarantee you will learn a thing or two from Nicolas!",
    ["Dialogue3000606"]="I don't allow my student to dislike Zeny!\n(Hamid smacks your shoulder with his hand.)\nListen up! Alchemy is such an unbelievable wonder that turns scraps into riches. Besides making potions, there are... Hehehe, I'm not supposed to say this.",
    ["Dialogue3000607"]="Why are you still here? As an Alchemist, you should chase knowledge like how you pursue wealth! You're not gonna catch the airship to Al De Baran if you horse around!",
    ["Dialogue3000701"]="Hah! Welcome to the Royal Chivalry! Since you've sought me out, I presume you're here to learn about being a knight?",
    ["Dialogue3000702"]="We are responsible for training the Royal Chivalry, which is loyal to the royalty of Rune Kingdom, and providing a pathway for adventurers to become knights. Although we are loyal to different masters, we are bound by the same knightly code!",
    ["Dialogue3000703"]="Now, let me find out if you have the potential to become a knight! Don't get nervous though; I just need to ask you a few questions!",
    ["Dialogue3000801"]="Adventurer, welcome to the Mage Guild! Geffen is home to all the elite wizards of this land. You've come to the right place if you seek more knowledge of this class.",
    ["Dialogue3000802"]="Although every person has a different understanding of how elemental magic is used, to become a wizard, you must at the very least share our ideals. There is no right or wrong answer, but I cannot take you as a student if we have contradictory ideals.",
    ["Dialogue3000803"]="Now, think carefully before you answer the following questions.",
    ["Dialogue3000901"]="By Odin... Your clear gaze has shown me your devotion to the Allfather. I believe you'll make a good priest.",
    ["Dialogue3000902"]="However, that is just the minimum requirement for priesthood. What I need to know is how you will practice your faith.",
    ["Dialogue3000903"]="Hahaha, consult your heart and be faithful to your soul when you answer.",
    ["Dialogue3001001"]="Haha, very good! The fact that you managed to find me in the remote mountains tells me you are full of curiosity about hunters.",
    ["Dialogue3001002"]="Hunters are solitary but not lonely. No one will cheer for them, but their longbows, sharp arrows, and loyal falcons will always keep them company. The unique charm of this lifestyle is precisely what attracts people to this class.",
    ["Dialogue3001003"]="It's time to find out whether you're ready for this type of adventuring life. Are you ready for my quiz?",
    ["Dialogue3001101"]="...I won't yabber on any longer. Your answer will determine whether you're suitable to be an assassin.",
    ["Dialogue3001201"]="Aha! You want to be a blacksmith with such scrawny arms and legs? Look at my muscles! Look at my skin! They've been honed by countless hours of toil before the fire and steam of my furnace!",
    ["Dialogue3001202"]="Listen up! The most important thing for becoming a blacksmith is passion! A passion that burns hotter than the fire of your furnace! Only then will your forging table respond to your calls! Come, let's shout out the blacksmith's slogan!",
    ["Dialogue3001401"]="Very good! Your answer tells me you have great potential to become an outstanding knight! Shielding your teammates with your body and staying calm, fair, and humble when faced with great temptation are all basic principles of a knight!",
    ["Dialogue3001402"]="Haha, have you already forgotten? What is the dearest companion of a knight?",
    ["Dialogue3001403"]="Your Pecopeco mount! Every moment of a knight's life of adventure and battle is spent with their faithful Pecopeco. You are partners, comrades, and dare I say it, the most important things in each other's lives!",
    ["Dialogue3001404"]="Ahem... E-either way, a knight must have a relationship built on love and trust with their mount, or you will have no hope of exploiting their maximum potential in battle! This is why you'll need to prove that you can get along closely with your mount in the upcoming trial. That's the only way you'll show me that you're eligible to be a knight candidate!",
    ["Dialogue3001405"]="Relax, Pecopeco have a kind and gentle nature. Feed them their favorite food and they'll listen to you obediently. Bring me one of the feathers from it buttocks, but don't try to take it directly or else...",
    ["Dialogue3001406"]="An expert in the chivalry knows much more about this than I do. Ask him for details.",
    ["Dialogue3001501"]="Hmm, it looks like you hold elemental magic in the same high esteem as us. Welcome to our large family of wizards! You possess the basic qualities to become one of us.",
    ["Dialogue3001502"]="However, this is just the beginning, for our wizard training and selection are very strict. All wizards, no matter how talented they are, will need a mana crystal to absorb the magic power that they lose control of while learning how to wield the elements.",
    ["Dialogue3001503"]="Mjolnir Mine is rich in mana crystals. Many years ago, before that incident took place, mana crystals were extremely common magic tools, but now... I believe you'll need to put in some effort. It shouldn't be a problem for an aspiring wizard though.",
    ["Dialogue3001504"]="Remember, it is prohibited to directly mine for mana crystals in the mine. I will disqualify you immediately if I catch you doing that.",
    ["Dialogue3001601"]="Hahaha! I see you've decided to practice your faith with the holy light. The Prontera Church welcomes adventurers like you. You must now prove your faith.",
    ["Dialogue3001602"]="Go to the Sunken Ship and purge it of the undead creatures that do not belong in this world. The omniscient and almighty Odin is watching your actions from his throne in Asgard. Remember, undead creatures do not deserve sympathy.",
    ["Dialogue3001701"]="Excellent answer. You won't complain even if no one looks up to you. Your arrows, traps, and falcon will be your greatest companions. Since the solitary and anonymous nature of a hunter hasn't diminished your motivation to become one, I have one last question for you: Are you willing to dedicate yourself to the mission of a hunter?",
    ["Dialogue3001702"]="This arduous mission is also shared by all archers, Archer Village, and even Payon: to protect this world from the undead of Munak Cave.",
    ["Dialogue3001703"]="Haha, we will not force any adventurers to join us. You are not from Payon; thus, there is no reason for you to be burdened by the weight of this mission. Go to the general's tomb in the south and pay your respects. That great man is Payon's... No, he is a hero to the whole world and a role model to all archers.",
    ["Dialogue3001801"]="...Good answer. A thief who cannot stay true to their own sense of justice cannot become a true assassin.",
    ["Dialogue3001802"]="Your next task is to bring me a lute. The bard Caslisse who is currently in Morroc has one. You can just steal his.",
    ["Dialogue3001803"]="Assassins never ask about the reason when they receive jobs. This is the rule. Now go.",
    ["Dialogue3001901"]="Bahaha! I knew it! I knew that you are a friend of all blacksmiths! Compared to those fellows who hide in a gloomy lab all day... Ahem, I got carried away...",
    ["Dialogue3001902"]="Let me ask you, what is the first thing that comes to mind when you think of a blacksmith?",
    ["Dialogue3001903"]="Bahaha! Muscles that are used to swing our hammers, of course! Do you know what gives the Blacksmith Guild its biggest headache? Finding a way to help scrawny merchants like you push your carts with ease!",
    ["Dialogue3001904"]="Spar with the skeletons at the Shipwreck for now and return to me once you become confident in your muscles! Listen up, your muscles won't lie; they'll reflect the results of your training very clearly!",
    ["Dialogue3002001"]="So you want to learn more about Pecopeco? You've come to the right person!",
    ["Dialogue3002002"]="What is the favorite food of Pecopeco? What else could it be other than fragrant pumpkin? The Pecopeco we train here often sneak out to Green Cotton Farm outside the South Gate to eat the pumpkins there, and our knights are always having to go bring them back.",
    ["Dialogue3002003"]="If an adventurer puts in the effort to bake a fragrant pumpkin pie, hehehe, I bet the Pecopeco will follow you forever. How about it, do you want me to teach you how to make the Pecopeco's favorite pumpkin pie?",
    ["Dialogue3002004"]="Since it's called pumpkin pie, we can't possibly make it without pumpkins. But then, we also add Muka flesh into the pumpkins for the Pecopeco. The aroma created by the combination of cactus and pumpkin is simply irresistible to humans too.",
    ["Dialogue3002005"]="Pumpkin and Muka flesh, got it? Now go.",
    ["Dialogue30021001"]="Mutant Dragonoid keeps absorbing strength from the slumber, while occupying the four areas and cutting off their strength sources to make them weak.",
    ["Dialogue3002101"]="Hmm, you've got enough ingredients to try several times even if you fail. Let's make a perfect pumpkin pie!",
    ["Dialogue3002102"]="Listen carefully! Step 1: Add the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pumpkin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3002103"]="Step 2: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bake it at low heat</color> until it starts smelling nice.",
    ["Dialogue3002104"]="Step 3: Add the diced <color=#CA2E0AFF>raw</color> Muka flesh.",
    ["Dialogue3002105"]="This is how you make the Pecopeco's favorite pumpkin pie! So, did you get all that? Do you need me to repeat it?",
    ["Dialogue3002106"]="Good, you can start now!",
    ["Dialogue3002201"]="(Hmm, I think the first step was...)",
    ["Dialogue3002202"]="(It's looking good! After that... What heat do I use?)",
    ["Dialogue3002203"]="(Yes! Last of all, I need to add...)",
    ["Dialogue3002204"]="(It's done!)",
    ["Dialogue3002205"]="Whoa, I'm impressed. You actually managed to make it before the ingredients ran out. Judging from the greedy look on the Pecopeco's face, my experience as a Pecopeco expert tells me that your pie is a nine out of ten.",
    ["Dialogue3002206"]="All you need to do now is to place it near a wild Pecopeco habitat. Remember to place it in a remote corner; I'm not sure you'll be able to handle all the Pecopeco that come to fight over it.",
    ["Dialogue3002207"]="(Huh? Something doesn't seem right... Let's try again.)",
    ["Dialogue3002301"]="Hmm... Yes, this is a feather from the buttocks of a Pecopeco. I believe you've mastered how to get along with Pecopeco now. You're now eligible to be a knight candidate.",
    ["Dialogue3002302"]="You can choose to join us, or you can choose another path after learning more about another class.",
    ["Dialogue3002303"]="You'll need to decide when you reach Job Lv.50. The Royal Chivalry will always welcome you.",
    ["Dialogue3002401"]="Another human here for mana crystals!",
    ["Dialogue3002402"]="Hahaha, seeing a mage adventurer at Mjolnir Dead Pit is a dead giveaway. I'm telling you though, mana crystals aren't that easy to get. The Great Sage said he'd kill us all if we excavate them without permission!",
    ["Dialogue3002403"]="Mumu Be doesn't know either! All Mumu Be knows is that Skeleton Workers have mana crystal fragments on them! Mumu Be loves those crystals, but Mumu Be can't beat them.",
    ["Dialogue3002404"]="If you want to thank Mumu Be, you should bring back some extra crystal fragments for me! Mumu Be loves those pretty, sparkly things!",
    ["Dialogue3002501"]="Thank you! You're Mumu Be's friend! Mumu Be only needs one!",
    ["Dialogue3002502"]="Yay! Now Mumu Be has a crystal fragment too!",
    ["Dialogue3002601"]="Yes... This should be enough. Now I need to test your understanding of the elements.",
    ["Dialogue3002602"]="You'll need to infuse the power of the four elements into these crystal fragments in the right order. The power of the elements will keep this crystal together and make it a source of power for you. Remember this order: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fire → Earth → Wind → Water</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3002603"]="It's very simple. Add the fire element first. The only thing you need to bear in mind is that the preceding element will counter the element that follows it. For example, fire counters earth, which is why earth is infused after fire.",
    ["Dialogue3002604"]="Do you understand? Do you need me to tell you again?",
    ["Dialogue3002605"]="Good, give it a try then! Don't worry about failing; I'll protect you.",
    ["Dialogue3002701"]="(Hmm... I remember the first element is...)",
    ["Dialogue3002801"]="(Okay, I think that was right. Now I need to infuse the element that fire counters...)",
    ["Dialogue3002901"]="(Perfect! Next up is the element that earth counters...)",
    ["Dialogue3003001"]="(Great! Now for the last element!)",
    ["Dialogue30031001"]="<color=#ffe788>Ken-Oh Raoh is about to destroy everything! Pick up the <color=#528fff>Tome of Fist</color> to unleash corresponding skills!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30031002"]="<color=#ffe788>There will be <color=#528fff>Tome of Fist</color> shows up around the map to counter Raoh's abilities! Pick it up to inherit the <color=#528fff>Legacy of Hokuto Shinken</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30031003"]="<color=#ffe788>The ultimate battle is about to begin. Proceed and challenge Ken-Oh Raoh!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30031004"]="<color=#ffe788>Adventurers who inherit the <color=#528fff>Legacy of Hokuto Shinken</color> can reset lethal points by touching them!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30031005"]="<color=#ffe788>Hurry and group up with the immobilized Adventurers!</color>",
    ["Dialogue30031006"]="<color=#ffe788>Double Shichosei is imminent, gather up!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3003101"]="Hehe, you've lived up to my expectations. This is a mana crystal; it's used by wizards to control their magical power. It helps stabilize your magic and keep it under control.",
    ["Dialogue3003102"]="Back in the days when the wizard training system had not yet been fully developed, many wizards ended up getting hurt when they lost control of their magical power. That's why my Wizard Guild rules state that I won't teach a wizard until they make their own mana crystal.",
    ["Dialogue3003103"]="Congratulations, you're now eligible to be a wizard candidate. I've never seen a crystal combine so successfully! You're a rarity among the many candidates I've seen in recent years.",
    ["Dialogue3003104"]="Keep this with you. Even if you choose another class in the future, we have no reason to confiscate this crystal. After all, you made it with your own hands.",
    ["Dialogue3003105"]="You'll need to decide when you reach Job Lv.50. The doors of the Wizard Guild will always be open to you.",
    ["Dialogue3003301"]="I hate those Whispers!",
    ["Dialogue3003302"]="I'm the resident priest of the Radiance! Without my prayers, Odin will not bless us and help us repel our enemies in this critical moment!",
    ["Dialogue3003303"]="But those Whispers stole my prayer book! You're the adventurer the captain hired, right? Please get my book back for me!",
    ["Dialogue3003304"]="(There's no doubt the priest before you has been dead for many years. He died before he could complete his duty as the ship's resident priest, and has been tormented by anxiety for the centuries since his death.)",
    ["Dialogue3003305"]="(Must I use Odin's holy light to destroy a soul who was so devout in life merely because he has become an undead creature? No, the holy light shouldn't be put to such use! I have to help him complete his unfinished business!)",
    ["Dialogue3003306"]="What are you waiting for?! There's no time to lose!",
    ["Dialogue3003401"]="Damn, they damaged the prayer book... but there's no time to be picky. Go to the bar next door and get me some wine to use as an offering.",
    ["Dialogue3003501"]="Urgh... This wine is awful, but beggars can't be choosers.",
    ["Dialogue3003502"]="Mighty Odin, your faithful servant offers you fine wine and sincerely asks for your blessing. The Radiance is under attack by undead creatures. Please grant us the power of your holy light!",
    ["Dialogue3003503"]="(A priest who has long been a ghost praying devoutly for the power of the holy light... The scene is both sad and beautiful.)",
    ["Dialogue3003504"]="(The holy light summoned by his faith enshrouds the priests fading body. His expression is calm and tranquil as he remains unaware of the destiny that awaits him.)",
    ["Dialogue3003505"]="(It looks like the holy light brings them salvation instead of destruction. It's the same for this priest as it was for Anna and Lukas before.)",
    ["Dialogue3003601"]="The look on your face... It appears that you have a new understanding of the holy light.",
    ["Dialogue3003602"]="So you will practice your faith by using the holy light for salvation and not destruction? And you will show undead creatures the same compassion you would show any other?",
    ["Dialogue3003603"]="Hahaha, there's no need to apologize; your answer pleases me. I'm amazed you managed to comprehend that the true purpose of the holy light is salvation.",
    ["Dialogue3003604"]="As priests, we cast blessings on our teammates and try to guide our enemies to salvation. This holy light, that treats everything impartially without discrimination, is the true form of Odin's gospel. You have proven your faith to me by not being misled by my words.",
    ["Dialogue3003605"]="I'm very happy to welcome you as a priest... is what I would like to be able to say. Tell me, has everything you've learned changed your mind about how to practice Odin's faith? Is the holy light really what you seek?",
    ["Dialogue3003606"]="I'm not in a rush to hear your answer; you're already eligible to be a priest candidate. If you want to join us, you can come back to me when you reach Job Lv.50. When that happens, I'll guide you along the path illuminated by the holy light under the vigilant watch of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3003701"]="Hi, I'm the tomb keeper here. Have you come to pay your respects to General Qi Euin?",
    ["Dialogue3003702"]="Your reaction tells me you're not too familiar with the events of Payon's past. Did Instructor Sky Euin tell you to come?",
    ["Dialogue3003703"]="In that case, let me tell you about the exploits of General Qi Euin! Don't give me that look; I know all his stories by heart!",
    ["Dialogue3003704"]="But before that, please offer some incense to the general to pay your respects.",
    ["Dialogue3003801"]="General Qi Euin is a great hero who has been the pride of Payon for generations.",
    ["Dialogue3003802"]="A long time ago, the people of Payon lived in isolation as farmers in the eastern forests, where they slowly developed into large tribe. The largest family in the tribe was the Euin Family, to which Qi Euin belonged.",
    ["Dialogue3003803"]="Every member of the Euin Family was a highly skilled archer, and the general shared his family's secret archery techniques with the people of Payon. His original intention was to give everyone the ability to protect themselves in the harsh natural environment, but then that fateful day came...",
    ["Dialogue3003804"]="The people of Payon have a tradition of burying the dead, as we believe that their souls exist in another world after death. That's why they transformed Munak Cave to look like a town of the living and placed the bodies of the dead inside. However, in the words of your kingdom in the midland... the dark energy of the dead built up inside, and instead of allowing them to rest them in peace, it turned them into undead creatures.",
    ["Dialogue3003805"]="On that day, undead creatures swarmed out of Munak Cave and massacred those who lived outside Payon. General Qi Euin formed the Spirit Quellers with a group of volunteer adventurers to repel the undead army all the way back to Munak Cave.",
    ["Dialogue3003806"]="But how was it that they were able to repel an undead army that had been growing in strength for over a thousand years? To seal the cave, the Spirit Quellers called upon the power of the gods, and gave the lives of all its members as the offering.",
    ["Dialogue3003807"]="The general's younger brother fulfilled the general's dying wish. He built Archer Village outside the entrance of Munak Cave, ensuring that the archery skills of the Spirit Quellers were passed down through the generations, right up to this very day. Instructor Sky Euin must have told you about the mission of all hunters?",
    ["Dialogue3003808"]="It's been centuries since the Spirit Quellers sacrificed themselves, and the undead power leaking out of Munak Cave has grown stronger over time. Instructor Sky Euin is extremely worried about the calamity that will descend upon Rune Kingdom if this energy breaks the seal now that the Spirit Quellers are no more.",
    ["Dialogue3003809"]="He hopes that the hunter adventurers of today will carry on the Spirit Quellers' duty to protect this world.",
    ["Dialogue3003810"]="Haha, Instructor Sky Euin will be overjoyed to see such a passionate and responsible adventurer. W-watch out, adventurer! Behind you!",
    ["Dialogue3003811"]="Roar!",
    ["Dialogue3003812"]="A-an undead creature! How did it...?",
    ["Dialogue3003901"]="Could this be the imminent calamity Instructor Sky Euin spoke of? I have to warn him!",
    ["Dialogue3004001"]="The tomb keeper told me what happened. Thank you for saving her and protecting the general's tomb.",
    ["Dialogue3004002"]="Since you now have some understanding of the mission of all hunters, please tell me your answer. Just so you know, I just want to know what you truly think; this won't affect your eligibility as a hunter candidate.",
    ["Dialogue3004003"]="As it should be... Hahaha, I would expect nothing less from an adventurer who graduated from Criatura Academy! Melbrun has taught a group of excellent students! My worries for this world have been somewhat allayed now that I know there's a group of responsible adventurers like you around.",
    ["Dialogue3004004"]="Brave hunter candidate, I welcome you. You can change your mind at any time now, but you must make your final decision when you reach Job Lv.50.",
    ["Dialogue30041001"]="Devimon has arrived on the battlefield. Heroes, hurry and take him down!",
    ["Dialogue30041002"]="The Power of Evolution has appeared! Get it now!",
    ["Dialogue3004101"]="Sigh... Where's my precious lute gone?",
    ["Dialogue3004102"]="I'm Caslisse... Sigh, please don't speak to me. Someone's stolen my lute. Sigh... What will I do without my precious lute?",
    ["Dialogue3004103"]="The thief escaped in the direction of the Pyramid. Can you get my lute back for me? I'll reward you handsomely! Please, it's extremely important to me!",
    ["Dialogue3004104"]="One more thing. Please don't hurt the thief. I could tell from her eyes that she's a kind person. She must have done it because she had no other choice. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue3004201"]="I should be able to pass the Assassins Guild's test now! But then again, it feels wrong stealing something so important to someone. He seemed quite sad... No, no, I can't hesitate now that I've finally made up my mind! Misha, it's time to go!",
    ["Dialogue3004202"]="Whoa! Wh-who are you? Do you also need this lute to pass the Assassins Guild's test? I won't let you take it. I-I have to pass the test!",
    ["Dialogue3004301"]="Ah! My lute! Yes, this is the one! I can't thank you enough. You are its savior; I must compose a great poem for you!",
    ["Dialogue3004302"]="No, you deserve this praise. Now let me think of a title for the poem...",
    ["Dialogue3004303"]="(I'd better leave quietly while he's lost in his own world.)",
    ["Dialogue3004401"]="...Why did you come back? I won't be able to pass the test now that I've lost the lute. That bard's the only person with a lute in all Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue3004402"]="I know, it's not like I stole it because I wanted to. I had no other choice if I wanted to pass the test.",
    ["Dialogue3004403"]="You want to help me? But I got in your way just now. Also, what other way is there?",
    ["Dialogue3004404"]="Make a lute? Oh! You're right! I won't need to hurt anyone if I make one! But there's only one person in Morroc who knows how to make a lute.",
    ["Dialogue3004405"]="B-but I just caused so much trouble for him; surely he won't want to see me?",
    ["Dialogue3004406"]="You're right. I did the wrong thing and I shouldn't try to run away from it. I can't pretend it didn't happen. Let's go to the bard!",
    ["Dialogue3004501"]="We meet again, adventurer! Oh? Isn't this the...",
    ["Dialogue3004502"]="I'm sorry! Actually... (She explains the whole story.)",
    ["Dialogue3004503"]="Hahaha! I see. If you would like me to make you a lute, you have only to ask. I would be only too happy to spread such wonderful music throughout the land!",
    ["Dialogue3004504"]="I can see the guilt in your eyes! It's decided! I will use my exquisite memory to make you a fine lute! Get me a string from a Metaller! I want quality, not quantity! Do you understand?",
    ["Dialogue3004505"]="Y-yes!",
    ["Dialogue3004601"]="Okay, now leave the next part to me!",
    ["Dialogue3004602"]="(*Clang* *Bang* *Swoosh*)",
    ["Dialogue3004603"]="All done! Here you go!",
    ["Dialogue3004604"]="Can I really have it?",
    ["Dialogue3004605"]="Of course! Take it. I don't know why Hassan picked on me, but I just can't leave a cute girl in distress!",
    ["Dialogue3004606"]="Hahaha, that's a story for another day. I'll tell it to you in great detail if we meet again!",
    ["Dialogue3004701"]="Did the two of you compete the mission together?",
    ["Dialogue3004702"]="Erm... Yes! Caslisse made me a lute thanks to this adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3004703"]="I did say that you could just steal his lute. Caslisse is no match for you; why make it more difficult for yourself? What would you have done if he didn't know how to make a lute?",
    ["Dialogue3004704"]="Was it because stealing something important to someone would contravene your sense of justice? ...Hmph, you did well. You both pass the test.",
    ["Dialogue3004705"]="Huh?",
    ["Dialogue3004706"]="An assassin walks in the darkness, and many assassins have lost themselves to the darkness as desire and evil corroded their hearts. The most important thing to an assassin is a strong heart and firm belief in their one's own sense of justice.",
    ["Dialogue3004707"]="You did not let me mislead you into doing evil. Instead, you stayed true to your own beliefs and even managed to guide others with your firm sense of justice. This is a precious quality in an assassin.",
    ["Dialogue3004708"]="Whereas you... What's your name?",
    ["Dialogue3004709"]="I-I'm Misha!",
    ["Dialogue3004710"]="I wanted to tell you that you weren't cut out to be an assassin due to your weak and wavering will, but this adventurer changed you in such a short time and made you confront your weakness. I believe it won't be long until you are strong enough.",
    ["Dialogue3004711"]="Th-thank you!",
    ["Dialogue3004712"]="You're both eligible to be assassin candidates now. Come back to see me once you reach Job Lv.50. I'm certain your firm sense of justice will aid you in the future, even if you choose another class.",
    ["Dialogue3004801"]="Hi, Sindre suggested you come here to for muscle training, right?",
    ["Dialogue3004802"]="Let me introduce myself. I'm Howard, a whitesmith who happens to be passing through these parts. I guessed what you're up to as soon I saw a novice merchant doing muscle training. Ah, it was like looking back at myself in my younger days!",
    ["Dialogue3004803"]="Did you know there's a more effective way to train on this ship than fighting Skel Pirates? Do you want to know what it is?",
    ["Dialogue3004804"]="Hehe, I'll teach you if you get me some Marina tentacles.",
    ["Dialogue3004901"]="Oh! That's an impressive haul. Okay, you need one last thing. Go to the ship's bar and get me some wine!",
    ["Dialogue3004902"]="Hahaha! What do you mean? I'm offering my secret recipe because I can't bear to see a young blacksmith training the hard way! Off you go now!",
    ["Dialogue3005001"]="Glug, glug, glug... Blergh! Even good wine tastes nasty if it's been kept around for too long!",
    ["Dialogue3005002"]="Here, let me make you a cup of Howard's special energy drink!",
    ["Dialogue3005003"]="......",
    ["Dialogue3005004"]="......",
    ["Dialogue3005005"]="It's done!",
    ["Dialogue3005006"]="Don't worry, it won't kill you! You should have some faith in my skills! Drink it and you'll feel your body get warmer! Bottoms up!",
    ["Dialogue3005007"]="Do you feel your body burning up like some sort of power wants to burst out of you?",
    ["Dialogue3005008"]="Hehe, go back to Sindre now! I'm sure he'll be amazed by your astonishing progress! See ya!",
    ["Dialogue3005101"]="Hmm! You must have trained incredibly hard based on your muscle growth!",
    ["Dialogue3005102"]="Yes! Based on my understanding of muscles, you must have defeated some 50 Skel Pirates to obtain this physique!",
    ["Dialogue3005103"]="That's right, 50. You aren't looking well; did something happen?",
    ["Dialogue3005104"]="For every ounce of effort you put into training, your muscles will reward you accordingly. Nothing more, nothing less. Yes, muscles are truly our greatest allies!",
    ["Dialogue3005105"]="Oh right, I bet that useless instructor Hamid didn't teach you the rules of business survival, did he?",
    ["Dialogue3005106"]="Haha, seeing as you train your muscles so hard, I'll share this knowledge with you. Remember to take notes!",
    ["Dialogue3005107"]="First, always maintain a close relationship with your customers. The easiest way to do this is to make use of your relationships with peers and classmates!",
    ["Dialogue3005108"]="(I guessed what you're up to as soon I saw a novice merchant doing muscle training. Ah, it was like looking back at myself in my younger days!)",
    ["Dialogue3005109"]="Second, a merchant makes money from gaps in information. The key is to use unimportant information about yourself to get people to trust you. But remember, don't be too quick to trust other people.",
    ["Dialogue3005110"]="(I'm offering my secret recipe because I can't bear to see a young blacksmith training the hard way!)",
    ["Dialogue3005111"]="Finally, being good at stirring up people's emotions and getting them to trust you is the ultimate victory!",
    ["Dialogue3005112"]="(Don't worry, it won't kill you! You should have some faith in my skills! Drink it and you'll feel your body get warmer! Bottoms up!)",
    ["Dialogue3005201"]="The Royal Chivalry welcomes you. Adventurer, it looks like you've decided that the path of a knight is one and the same as your path as an adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3005202"]="Very good. Let us tarry no longer and begin the job advancement quest!",
    ["Dialogue3005203"]="Haha, there's no need to panic; you've already proven your eligibility as a knight candidate. You'll soon be temporarily granted the status of full knighthood and do battle against monsters. We need to test whether you have learned how to fight like a knight. May luck be with you! Come to me in the Training Course once you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue3005301"]="Yes! The majestic way you wielded your spear astride your Pecopeco! You were born to be a knight!",
    ["Dialogue3005302"]="Let's not delay. Gather the materials you need to make your own suit of knight's armor!",
    ["Dialogue3005303"]="We usually make our armor out of the Oridecon found on Giearths. You can buy the cloth for your cape directly from me, haha.",
    ["Dialogue3005304"]="Ahem, the Chivalry won't overcharge you. Don't dawdle any longer now. Off you go!",
    ["Dialogue3005401"]="Hmm... That's everything you need! Now, there's only one thing left to do!",
    ["Dialogue3005402"]="You'll need to return to where you first started your adventures. That's right, I'm referring to Criatura Academy.",
    ["Dialogue3005403"]="The completion of your job advancement symbolizes that you have graduated and become a full-fledged adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3005404"]="Dean Mainz and Instructor Yadrew are waiting for you at the Temple of Dawn.",
    ["Dialogue3005501"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become a swordsman.",
    ["Dialogue3005502"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3005503"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3005504"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3005601"]="Hmm, it looks like everything's ready. Now stand in front of the sacred statue of the goddess so that I can preside over your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3005701"]="Oh? Why do you look so hesitant? Have you already decided to learn even more profound magic?",
    ["Dialogue3005702"]="Excellent! I would expect no less from you. Let's not waste any more time. Hurry up and start the job advancement quest!",
    ["Dialogue3005703"]="Don't be nervous. You're now qualified to be a wizard candidate, but I need to keep observing you for a little longer. If you have the strength of an official wizard, you shouldn't have any problem fighting the monsters. Personally, I think you'll be fine! Go to the middle of the room when you are ready and we'll start immediately.",
    ["Dialogue3005801"]="I'm truly amazed by your control over the elements. It's been a long time since I've seen such a talented wizard candidate. Yes, this is indeed high praise from the Mage Guild leader, but you deserve it!",
    ["Dialogue3005802"]="Now you need to gather the materials to craft your own wizard's robe!",
    ["Dialogue3005803"]="Do you know of the Mysts that roam around Mjolnir Dead Pit? The silk thread of wizard robes is made from their hearts. As for the cloth, you can buy it from the Mage Guild.",
    ["Dialogue3005804"]="Hmm... Since you're so talented, I will personally make the cloth you need! But I won't be giving you any discounts, okay? Now get going!",
    ["Dialogue3005901"]="Okay, you've got all the materials. Now leave the rest to the Mage Guild! Go back to Criatura Academy for now!",
    ["Dialogue3005902"]="That's right. Once you complete the job advancement and become a wizard, you'll have graduated from Criatura Academy and become an official member of the Wizard Guild.",
    ["Dialogue3005903"]="Dean Mainz and Charles are waiting for you at the Temple of Dawn.",
    ["Dialogue3006001"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become a mage.",
    ["Dialogue3006002"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006003"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3006004"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006101"]="Hohoho, adventurer, does this mean you've decided to practice Odin's faith with the holy light?",
    ["Dialogue3006102"]="Good. I'm very relieved that a successor of Odin's bloodline like you has chosen the path of the holy light. Let's start the job advancement quest now!",
    ["Dialogue3006103"]="Hohoho, by Odin! You've already received his approval and are an eligible priest candidate, but Odin will continue to observe how you use the holy light. He has bestowed upon you the power of an official priest and the ability to do battle against monsters. You'll be fine under his watchful gaze, so give it your all! Start preparing in the church once you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue3006201"]="By Odin... It's as if you're one with the holy light. I feel like I can even see Odin's hand guiding you.",
    ["Dialogue3006202"]="What you need to do next is to gather the materials to make a priest's robe. This is Odin's final test for you on your path to priesthood.",
    ["Dialogue3006203"]="Adventurer, do you know what monster the inner fabric of a priest's robe comes from?",
    ["Dialogue3006204"]="Whispers. Hohoho, I bet you didn't expect that. Once the holy light brings salvation to the Whispers, their cloth gains a strong affinity with Odin's power. To get the fabric for the outer layer, you simply have to make a sufficient donation.",
    ["Dialogue3006205"]="Hohoho, it truly is Odin's blessing. You should go now, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3006301"]="Hmm... Very good. Now that you have these materials, Odin should be able to grant you a holy priest's robe. It's time for you to return to the radiance of Brunhild. Dean Mainz and Alice are waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue3006302"]="Yes, the Temple of Dawn. That was where you started your career as an acolyte; it's only fitting that it should be where it ends.",
    ["Dialogue3006401"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become an acolyte.",
    ["Dialogue3006402"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006403"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3006404"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006501"]="Hmm... Hahaha, very good! I believe you meant it when you said you were willing to shoulder the responsibility of saving the world. That alone makes you worthy of being called a hunter.",
    ["Dialogue3006502"]="We will now start the job advancement quest!",
    ["Dialogue3006503"]="You look so nervous. The job advancement quest isn't as difficult as the responsibilities of a hunter. Candidate hunters like you must be taught how official hunters do battle before you advance. Don't worry though; I won't make things difficult for you. We'll start once you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue3006601"]="Whoa... Hahaha, did you see that? Your falcon is cut from the same cloth as you! Spectacular. You're a natural hunter!",
    ["Dialogue3006602"]="Okay, the only thing you lack now is a hunter's attire. You will need to collect these materials yourself. After all, true hunters rely on themselves, haha.",
    ["Dialogue3006603"]="Have you seen what all the coolest hunters wear? The best fur is from Martins. Hahaha, you look shocked. Unbelievable, right?",
    ["Dialogue3006604"]="The Hunter Guild will provide you with the other cloth you need... but at a cost.",
    ["Dialogue3006605"]="Haha, the cloth is a specialty of the Payon region, so you won't find it in anywhere in your kingdom in the midland. You should go now. I'll wait here for you.",
    ["Dialogue3006701"]="Hmm... Yes, this is more than enough! The tailors of Payon will do the rest. Dean Mainz and Melbrun are waiting for you at Criatura Academy.",
    ["Dialogue3006702"]="Of course. We hunters won't just take any kid from the academy. Go and prove that you're eligible to be one of us.",
    ["Dialogue3006703"]="Yes!",
    ["Dialogue3006801"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become an archer.",
    ["Dialogue3006802"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006803"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3006804"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3006901"]="Since you've returned, I assume you've decided to become an assassin?",
    ["Dialogue3006902"]="You've chosen to become an assassin and the assassin's will has chosen you. Now you must take the trial.",
    ["Dialogue3006903"]="An assassin's fighting style isn't flashy or glamorous. It would be a good idea to try out what it's like to fight like an official assassin. If it's not to your liking, you're free to leave; we would never force anyone to tread this path. If you understand everything, start preparing inside the guild.",
    ["Dialogue3007001"]="Hmph, not bad.",
    ["Dialogue3007002"]="You now need to make your assassin's armor, but you have to collect the materials yourself. Remember, the Assassins Guild never does anything for free. As a favor for our beginners, we're willing to collect the cloth for you, but you'll have to pay for it.",
    ["Dialogue3007003"]="Everything we do has a reason. The bone decorations on the outfit come from Pirate Skeletons. Don't alter them too much; an assassin needs such materials with aura of darkness. That's all. You can go now.",
    ["Dialogue3007101"]="This is everything; you can leave the rest to us. Go to Criatura Academy and prepare for the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007102"]="Dean Mainz and Moxie will preside over your graduation ceremony. You'll be an assassin once it's over.",
    ["Dialogue3007201"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become a thief.",
    ["Dialogue3007202"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007203"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3007204"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007301"]="Bahaha! Welcome to the Blacksmith Guild! Have you decided to become a blacksmith and embrace the lifelong pursuit of muscular strength?",
    ["Dialogue3007302"]="Hahaha! Are you ready for the blacksmith trial? If so, go to the Wigner Mansion and begin! Use your muscles to show me you're ready to become an official blacksmith!",
    ["Dialogue3007401"]="Hahaha! Not bad! I can see how much effort you've put into your training from how easily you pushed those carts!",
    ["Dialogue3007402"]="Now take off those thick, heavy clothes; blacksmiths don't need to wear that much! The Blacksmith Guild will make a set of new clothes for you!",
    ["Dialogue3007403"]="What's that? We're merchants; of course we'll charge you! But we won't waste time haggling like the other guilds. It's a fixed price of 100,000 Zeny for one set. Assuming you pass, I'm sure a decent merchant would have no trouble making 100,000 Zeny?",
    ["Dialogue3007404"]="After you pay for your clothes, leave everything else to Dean Mainz and Hamid. Return to the Temple of Dawn and they'll preside over your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007501"]="Great, I've received your 100,000 Zeny! Now go back to the Temple of Dawn!",
    ["Dialogue3007502"]="You'll be a member of the Blacksmith Guild once the ceremony ends.",
    ["Dialogue3007601"]="Hohoho, it's been a while since we last met, adventurer; you've come far. I still vividly remember the moment you completed the job advancement to become a merchant.",
    ["Dialogue3007602"]="We can no longer teach you anything here at Criatura Academy. Congratulations on proving your potential and inner strength. However, there's one more thing you need to do before your graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007603"]="Give me your job manual. You no longer have any need for it.",
    ["Dialogue3007604"]="Hohoho, there's no need to panic. I'll give you the job manual for the second job advancement, which is also your graduation certificate, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3007701"]="Welcome, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3007702"]="With your extraordinary wisdom and courage, you thwarted the counterattack that Baphomet had been planning for a long time and banished his incarnation into the dimensional gap. You saved Prontera... No, you saved the whole of Rune Kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue3007703"]="As the Great Sage of Rune Kingdom, I thank you from the bottom of my heart on behalf of all its people.",
    ["Dialogue3007704"]="Yes, you truly have the heart of a hero, just as I would expect of a successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue3007705"]="I have invited you here today for your award ceremony, to be witnessed by Captain Hallam, Archbishop Wolmas, and Commander Richard, linchpins of Rune Kingdom. I will preside over the ceremony and channel Odin's almighty power into you.",
    ["Dialogue3007706"]="That's right, this is the Transcendent Second Class ceremony. A normal adventurer would have to complete an extremely rigorous trial and prove themselves in order to gain this honor. However, you have made an incomparable contribution to the kingdom, and the many difficulties you have overcome to date all prove that you deserve the title granted by the Transcendent Second Class.",
    ["Dialogue3007707"]="I'm sure you're familiar with the job advancement ceremony. Once you're ready, give me your job manual and stand before Odin's Statue. The ceremony will then begin.",
    ["Dialogue3007801"]="The monsters on the other side of the dimensional gap stir in anticipation as the Night of Calamity draws near. The ominous aura is stronger than ever before. Adventurer, Rune Kingdom faces an unprecedented disaster.",
    ["Dialogue3007802"]="When the land of the humans and land of the undead intersect, the evil aura from Niflheim, the kingdom of the dead, will weaken the seal of the dimensional gap. When the seal is at its weakest, the monsters on the other side will swarm out. This is known as the Night of Calamity. The most fearsome among them is Baphomet, who was personally sealed by Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3007803"]="Rune Kingdom has survived countless Nights of Calamity over the centuries. We have fought all manner of foe, from powerful Munak kings to the weakest of Whispers. Some say that the distance between Niflheim and Midgard determines the strength of our enemies, but the reality is we know absolutely nothing about this.",
    ["Dialogue3007804"]="No one knows what we'll be up against. The only thing we can do is to suppress the forces of evil that stir throughout the land, remain vigilant, and prepare to fight the coming monsters.",
    ["Dialogue3007805"]="Hahaha, now that we have the successor of Odin's bloodline on our side, we have a much greater chance of overcoming the Night of Calamity. I want you to help the regional leaders deal with the monsters and use the power of Odin's bloodline to reinforce the dimensional gap seals that are on the verge of collapse. Only you can help us.",
    ["Dialogue3007806"]="Excellent, then I can put my fears to rest. The first seal you need to reinforce is located in Mjolnir Mine, right beneath our feet.",
    ["Dialogue3007807"]="Haha, this is the true secret mission of Golden Wings Mine. There's a dimensional gap under Mjolnir Mine, and our Heines family has created four seals in the depths of the mine where the richest mana crystal lodes are located.",
    ["Dialogue3007808"]="However, the seals have weakened over time as more and more mana crystals have been mined. Even the most stable seal of Mjolnir Mine needs to be repaired... Hmm?",
    ["Dialogue3007901"]="A-are you an adventurer?! This mine is very dangerous! Leave quickly before the undead creatures appear!",
    ["Dialogue3008001"]="Mumu Be thanks you for your help!",
    ["Dialogue3008002"]="There are some super scary cracks in the mine! Recently, powerful monsters have been coming out of one of the cracks every time there's been an earthquake! The Giearth aren't good at fighting; the others have all left, but this is where Mumu Be grew up; Mumu Be wants to protect this place!",
    ["Dialogue3008003"]="A-adventurers are such nice people! When Mumu Be was still a little Giearth, a kind adventurer collected mana crystal fragments for Mumu Be to cheer Mumu Be up.",
    ["Dialogue3008004"]="Now an adventurer is taking a risk to help Mumu Be save the mine! Mu-Mumu Be is so touched!",
    ["Dialogue3008005"]="Crystals! Yes, that's what Mumu Be has been protecting all along! Mumu Be will guide you!",
    ["Dialogue30081001"]="It's gift time—come get yours!",
    ["Dialogue30081002"]="Everyone! Let's come out and have some fun!",
    ["Dialogue30081003"]="Nice fighting, everyone! Let's go another round!",
    ["Dialogue30081004"]="Keep it going! Let's turn up the heat!",
    ["Dialogue30081005"]="That was fun today—I'm outta here!",
    ["Dialogue30081006"]="Welcome, everyone! The show's about to start!",
    ["Dialogue30081007"]="Enjoy the fun—no crying allowed, okay?",
    ["Dialogue30081008"]="The current boss is over. Deviling has appeared at the Central Fountain—start patrolling now!",
    ["Dialogue3008101"]="Mumu Be doesn't know much about the origin of these crystals! They always appear whenever the monsters become active in the mine. If they didn't, Mumu Be could search the whole mine and not find any.",
    ["Dialogue3008102"]="Yeah! Giearths have a strong sensitivity for minerals, but we can't find them either! It's so strange!",
    ["Dialogue3008103"]="Those monsters from before must have come out of this crack! Let's seal it!",
    ["Dialogue3008201"]="The seals have been repaired for now, but the crystals at one of the seals have been destroyed. I can sense a demonic power flowing out of Mjolnir Mine.",
    ["Dialogue3008202"]="We can take a breather, but we mustn't let our guard down. I'll contact the Heines family right away and start repairing the seal inside the mine.",
    ["Dialogue3008203"]="I want you to inform the Lugenburg family as soon as possible. Sphinx Cavern has always been home to demonic forces, so we must be vigilant. Take this letter to Chief Maximilian; he'll understand what's happening. Remember, you must make haste. We don't have much time until the Night of Calamity.",
    ["Dialogue3008204"]="Return to Prontera as soon as you finish up in Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue3008205"]="The Heine family will take the helm in Geffen, whereas Morroc can depend on the Assassins Guild and the Lugenburg family for protection. Although the Hunter Guild of Payon won't be able to repel the monsters of Munak Cave by itself, it should be able to hold out until our reinforcements arrive. As for Prontera... If Baphomet attacks Prontera in person, no one would be able to defeat him other than you, the successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue3008206"]="That being said... Adventurer, you are the hero chosen by Odin. You can decide your own course of action. If you have another fight, Prontera will do all it can to hold out until you arrive.",
    ["Dialogue3008207"]="We trust your judgment.",
    ["Dialogue3008301"]="Oh! It's been a long time. Hmm? A letter from Sage Kroneika? Let me see...",
    ["Dialogue3008302"]="......",
    ["Dialogue3008303"]="Hahaha, there's no need to worry. I've already dispatched an adventurer to Sphinx Cavern. There shouldn't be any problems with her there.",
    ["Dialogue3008304"]="Yes, one person. She's more than capable of putting up a good fight against Halmod!",
    ["Dialogue3008401"]="W-why are so many humans here to make trouble for us today?",
    ["Dialogue3008402"]="Revive the great pharaoh, King Seti! The Lord said that as long as King Seti joins forces with him, he would be able to return to this world and show you fools who support Osiris that King Seti is the greatest pharaoh of Egypt!",
    ["Dialogue3008403"]="I-I won't say anything! The last fool who revealed the Lord's identity ended up being dragged into that dark place.",
    ["Dialogue3008404"]="His agonizing screams were... Argh! No, I won't talk, not even on pain of death!",
    ["Dialogue3008501"]="Huh? Are there other adventurers? It's very dangerous here now.",
    ["Dialogue3008502"]="Hmm... That means our goals are aligned. I'm Misha; I've been tasked by the lord of the Lugenburg family to investigate the strange occurrences here. I'm sure those dumb Pasana at the door have told you about their plan to revive the pharaoh and about some so-called \"lord.\"",
    ["Dialogue3008503"]="It's so frustrating. He was killed by strange magic before he could say a word. I'd be lying if I said it didn't make me wonder about the connection between the terrifying person in the shadows and the Night of Calamity. What a waste of the special interrogation poison I gave him.",
    ["Dialogue3008504"]="Yes, it's best you don't know what it does. What? You think it's too cruel? To protect Morroc, I won't show any mercy to my enemies.",
    ["Dialogue3008505"]="Let's get back to the matter at hand. I happened to find some pieces of papyrus on those Marduk just now; there's some sort of plan written on it in Egyptian hieroglyphs. Can you collect all the pieces for me? Maybe we'll make a discovery!",
    ["Dialogue3008601"]="Wow! You managed to get them all! Let me see...",
    ["Dialogue3008602"]="Everyone born and raised in Morroc can more or less understand some of it... Aha! This is it! The pact with the demon king will soon be signed. When the supreme power converges on the throne, the door to another world will open and the great Pharaoh Seti will return to Midgard. Egypt, your king has returned!",
    ["Dialogue3008603"]="Dimensional gap? What's that?",
    ["Dialogue3008604"]="So the demonic power in Sphinx Cavern is connected to this. If their plan succeeds, the demon king will revive here and destroy the entire land!",
    ["Dialogue3008605"]="The only place in Sphinx Cavern that could be considered a throne is the pharaoh's sarcophagus. Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue3008701"]="You... How dare you...?",
    ["Dialogue3008702"]="It's all over! I'll be sending you back to the arms of the goddess of death now; give up on your dream of reviving and conquering the world!",
    ["Dialogue3008703"]="Revival? Hahaha, that doesn't matter at all. Judging from the look on your face, I assume you don't actually know anything?",
    ["Dialogue3008704"]="Everything I have done is to shroud this land in demonic power, so that terror may rule this place once more! My dream is to stand together with the majestic Lord Baphomet!",
    ["Dialogue3008705"]="Baphomet! So that's the lord you spoke of...",
    ["Dialogue3008706"]="Hmph... Lord Baphomet has already left for the final land of despair. Now that the demonic power of Sphinx Cavern has been released, no one can stop us! Hahahahaha! Ahem... Y-you have no hope!",
    ["Dialogue3008707"]="From the gates of hell, I will feast on the terror and despair you experience during the Night of Calamity. After that, Lord Baphomet will lead us back.",
    ["Dialogue3008801"]="He's dead... It looks like Baphomet's demonic power can only revive him for a short time. I feel sorry for those who follow him.",
    ["Dialogue3008802"]="Yes. We need to return to Morroc and report our findings to Lord Maximilian and Master Hassan. There's no way to stop the demonic power at Sphinx Cavern, so I'm afraid the Night of Calamity will descend upon us earlier than we expected. The Lugenburg family and the Assassins Guild must stand ready. What will you do?",
    ["Dialogue3008803"]="A place filled with demonic power in Rune Kingdom... Aha! It must be Munak Cave! The Spirit Quellers made a great sacrifice to seal the undead creatures down there. If the seal is broken...",
    ["Dialogue3008804"]="Hmm... Honestly speaking, I don't feel very sure about this.",
    ["Dialogue3008805"]="Hurry! In a crisis such as this, each of us has our own mission!",
    ["Dialogue3008806"]="(Return to Prontera as soon as you finish up in Morroc.)",
    ["Dialogue3008807"]="(As for Prontera... If Baphomet attacks Prontera in person, no one would be able to defeat him other than you, the successor of Odin's bloodline.)",
    ["Dialogue3008808"]="(If you have another fight, Prontera will do all it can to hold out until you arrive.)",
    ["Dialogue3008809"]="(We trust your judgment.)",
    ["Dialogue3008810"]="Of course! Even though this is our first time fighting together, I'm not sure why, but I feel like you're a super hero!",
    ["Dialogue3008811"]="Hehe, although I don't know what battles lie ahead of us, surely we'll meet again? I'll be waiting for you at the bar in Morroc, okay?",
    ["Dialogue3008901"]="Hmm... So you're the adventurer with Odin's bloodline that Great Sage Kroneika mentioned in his letter?",
    ["Dialogue3008902"]="We've received a letter from Great Sage Kroneika warning us of the recent strange events in Munak Cave. For this reason, we've summoned all the adventurers from the Spirit Quellers and requested help from the kingdom army. However, those numbers are just a drop in the ocean compared to what we need. If monsters swarm out of the cave, I'm afraid we'll be powerless to stop them.",
    ["Dialogue3008903"]="The vanguard has already entered Munak Cave to investigate the strength of the seals. We'll be able to make a decision once we have the results. One more thing... in his letter, he mentioned that you'll definitely come to help us.",
    ["Dialogue3008904"]="No, the undead creatures in Munak Cave are unusual; a rookie like you won't be of much help. We do, however, need you to do something only you can help us with.",
    ["Dialogue3008905"]="When Munak Cave was sealed, the Spirit Quellers made a great sacrifice, and so too did the archbishop of the kingdom. With Odin's power, he created three seals in Payon, and they have effectively suppressed the power of the undead creatures of the cave. That's the story of the Spirit Quellers' sacrifice to seal the monsters.",
    ["Dialogue3008906"]="The general recorded the locations of the seals in poetry and paintings, and wrote in his will that these works were to be buried with him.",
    ["Dialogue3008907"]="However, no one could have foreseen that the relationship between Payon and the church of Odin would sour in just a few short years. Payon destroyed all records pertaining to the seals, and swore to sever all ties with the church. Now the only records that survive are in the general's tomb.",
    ["Dialogue3008908"]="Recently, undead creatures have attacked the general's tomb many times. We've been doing our best to repel them, but more than half of the documents have been burned, leaving only some cryptic poems. Their objective was to prevent us from strengthening the seals! You're the only one who can help us in this desperate time.",
    ["Dialogue3008909"]="I knew you'd accept this mission. These are the only remaining document, poetic verses describing the three locations are all that survived.",
    ["Dialogue3008910"]="The first is, \"Southern meadow knows no hate; a grave as home to winter shrubs.\"",
    ["Dialogue3008911"]="The second is, \"West spring meets a sandy land; rippling willow, pavilion front.\"",
    ["Dialogue3008912"]="The third is, \"Journey to the clear eastern skies; harvest falls with western rains.\"",
    ["Dialogue3008913"]="Hahaha! The general loved to write poetry. I bet he never expected that this would be the only record left in this world! Still, I believe if there's anyone who can find the correct locations, it's you!",
    ["Dialogue3009001"]="......",
    ["Dialogue3009002"]="So this is the current generation's successor of Odin's bloodline... How disappointing... How foolish...",
    ["Dialogue30091001"]="Devimon has arrived on the battlefield. Heroes, hurry and take him down!",
    ["Dialogue30091002"]="The Power of Evolution has appeared! Get it now!",
    ["Dialogue3009101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue3009102"]="Keep struggling. This despair is simply delicious. Do you think you'll be able to stop me like this?",
    ["Dialogue3009103"]="So weak and arrogant. Prepare to surrender to the power of Lord Baphomet.",
    ["Dialogue3009201"]="Now that despair has descended, wallow in regret, successor of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue3009202"]="Hmph... Midgard shall welcome the return of the great Lord Baphomet.",
    ["Dialogue3009301"]="Welcome back, adventurer. The vanguard that investigated the cave has returned. The seals inside are very stable, so it looks like we have nothing to fear now. This is all thanks to your contribution in strengthening the seals!",
    ["Dialogue3009302"]="You saw a phantom Baphomet Jr. when you were strengthening the seals, but it didn't attack you? And it said some peculiar things? How strange. Haven't they been doing everything possible to prevent us from strengthening the seals so that they can release the demonic power from Munak Cave?",
    ["Dialogue3009303"]="Yet they stood aside and didn't do anything to stop you. Could it be possible that Munak Cave isn't their target?",
    ["Dialogue3009304"]="W-where's the adventurer who inherited Odin's bloodline?",
    ["Dialogue3009401"]="P-please hurry back to Prontera! An army of monsters has launched an attack! Great Sage Kroneika has taken command of the defense of the capital, but the monster horde just keeps on growing!",
    ["Dialogue3009402"]="Damn, so Munak Cave was just a distraction! The kingdom's army and the successor of Odin's bloodline were in the wrong place. So that was Baphomet's plan!",
    ["Dialogue3009403"]="We'll leave as soon as you're ready! Prontera needs you!",
    ["Dialogue3009501"]="Are you ready? Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue3010101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Tsk, we can't wait any longer.</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>What's up with Hollgrehenn?</color></size>\nOh, it's you... I'm in a little trouble; can you do me a favor?",
    ["Dialogue3010102"]="Not long ago, the Defense Force placed an order with the blacksmith, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color>. He always makes his deliveries on time, but for some reason he's late this time. If he doesn't get here soon, our new recruits won't have any <color=#CA2E0AFF>supplies</color> to use. Please chase him up for me!",
    ["Dialogue3010201"]="(Hollgrehenn tugs his hair anxiously.)\n<size=18>Argh!</size><size=18>The Defense Force keep sending people to chase up the order... </size><size=18>but what can I do?</size> <size=18>I'm at the end of my tether here!</size>\n…Hey, don't tell me that's why you're here.",
    ["Dialogue3010202"]="<size=24>…I knew it!</size>\nSigh, I guess I'll have to tell you the truth. I can't do anything without my \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Drubby</color>\"! You could hound me day and night, but without it, I can't forge a single thing!",
    ["Dialogue3010203"]="It's the hammer I've been using for over 10 years! Look, all my hammers are unique. For example, \"Drubby II\" is used to forge large items, \"Drubby III\" is used to forge small items, and \"Drubby IV\" is used for finishing work. Sigh, basically I need all of them!",
    ["Dialogue3010204"]="You want to know where my \"Drubby\" is? It's a terrifying story. Are you sure you want to hear it? Last night, me and my pal Xavier were out drinking at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fishing hole outside the South Gate</color>. Just as we were starting to get merry, a blue, furry ball suddenly jumped out from under a tree near us. I thought the drink was making me see things, but it got closer and closer...",
    ["Dialogue3010205"]="That's when I realized what it was. A <color=#CA2E0AFF>blue Lunatic</color>, half the height of a human, was standing right in front of me! We were terrified; we ran away screaming. That's when I lost \"Drubby\", and I don't know where.\n<size=24>Oh, my dear </size><size=24>Drubby,</size><size=24> I'm sorry I let you down!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3010206"]="W-what? You're willing to find Drubby for me? That's great! I'll be waiting here for your good news!",
    ["Dialogue3010301"]="(Hollgrehenn is so touched that tears fill his eyes as he hugs Drubby tightly.)\n... D...<size=24>Drubby!</size>\nYou've finally returned to me! I'll never let you go again!",
    ["Dialogue3010302"]="That's right, the order for the military supplies... Leave it to me. It'll be a piece of cake now that Drubby has returned to me! But if you want the order ready as soon as possible, I'll need some premium feathers. I asked someone from the Chamber of Commerce about a batch a week ago. Can you go and ask the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chamber of Commerce Worker</color> when they'll be delivered?",
    ["Dialogue3010401"]="...Hollgrehenn's feathers? Ah, I remember now! I'm so sorry though; we've currently stopped selling feathers due to a defect. The Wigner Chamber of Commerce has a policy of never selling defective goods. It's vital to maintaining our reputation.",
    ["Dialogue3010402"]="Yes. Our dedicated staff inspect the quality of all our goods before we start selling them. In the last inspection, we discovered that the white, flawless feathers had been contaminated with <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange blue feathers</color>. That seriously affected the quality and appearance, so we wrote them off as defective.",
    ["Dialogue3010403"]="Feathers are a very commonly used material, so this situation is terrible for us. We're at risk of failing to meet the huge daily demand. It's causing a major headache for us.",
    ["Dialogue3010404"]="Our problem would be solved if someone was willing to help us by going <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside the South Gate</color> to bring us back an adequate supply of <color=#CA2E0AFF>spotless white feathers</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatics</color>! Oh, are you planning on helping us? That's great! If you can bring back enough, the Wigner Chamber of Commerce will be in your debt!",
    ["Dialogue3010501"]="Thank you! You've really helped us out of a bind! Don't worry, I'll deliver Hollgrehenn's batch to him as soon as possible.\nHowever…\n(The Chamber of Commerce Worker looks worried.)",
    ["Dialogue3010502"]="...Actually, before you arrived, we dispatched a merchant to purchase the supplies we need, but she hasn't come back. It's been quite a long time now; I'm getting a little worried. I remember she left from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate</color>. Could she have run into danger along the way?",
    ["Dialogue3010601"]="(Betty pats some dust off her skirt)\nPhew! That was a close one! Thank you, brave adventurer! I'm Betty Lindra, a merchant of the Wigner Chamber of Commerce! This is the first time I've been dispatched to complete a task alone. Alas, I don't think I'm off to a good start!",
    ["Dialogue3010602"]="(Betty covers her face with her hands.)\n<size=24>That's right,</size><size=24> it's all its fault!</size>\nI finally got the chance to purchase goods by myself, but then I was attacked by a nasty Eclipse on my way back.",
    ["Dialogue3010603"]="I lost all the cargo I worked so hard to transport! I wonder if anybody would be kind enough to help a poor girl and retrieve her <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lost Cargo</color>?\n(Betty peeks at you through the gaps between her fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue3010701"]="<size=18>Let me verify the contents.</size><size=18> Giant Tiger Prawns, Sweet Sauce, Leather, Durian Grass... D-Durian Grass...?</size>\nOh no! Where's the precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Durian Grass</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3010702"]="(Betty covers her face with her hands.)\nI'm done for! Durian Grass is an expensive commodity imported from overseas! If I lose it, the Wigner Chamber of Commerce will have to bear the loss. The scariest thing of all is that half of the losses will be deducted from my salary! <size=24>I can't let that happen!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3010703"]="That damn Eclipse... It must have taken my goods! I wonder if anybody would be kind enough to help a poor girl and retrieve her <color=#CA2E0AFF>backpack full of Durian Grass</color>?\n(Betty peeks at you through the gaps between her fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue3010801"]="(Betty looks heartbroken.)\n...Sigh...<size=24>Eh——?!</size>\nDon't tell me that Eclipse ate all the Durian Grass in the backpack? There's no way it could eat that much, is there?!",
    ["Dialogue3010802"]="Ah! Who's talking about the Eclipse?",
    ["Dialogue3010901"]="(Bertha approaches you mysteriously.)\nI thought I heard someone talking about the Eclipse just now. Have you seen it around here?",
    ["Dialogue3010902"]="Hehe! I'm Bertha, a monster researcher. I'm also a die-hard monster fan! I thought I already knew everything there was to know about the monsters of South Gate, but the sighting of the Eclipse has opened a door to a new world for me! It's so exciting!",
    ["Dialogue3010903"]="Ah! Don't you think that the blue feathers make it look noble? And it's so much bigger and stronger than a normal Lunatic. Isn't it just majestic? Indeed this rare mutant is an amazing evolution of the Lunatic species!",
    ["Dialogue3010904"]="(Betty interrupts her angrily.)\nI don't know what's so great about it. That Eclipse is nothing but trouble! It ate my precious Durian Grass!",
    ["Dialogue3010905"]="(Bertha cries out in surprise and shakes with excitement.)\nWow! Are you telling me that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eclipses are interested in Durian Grass</color>? That's a major discovery! I'm one step closer to understanding them!",
    ["Dialogue3010906"]="If I dare to make a bold hypothesis... I would even say that maybe Durian Grass is what causes Lunatics to mutate! If that's true, I'll have discovered one possible way that monsters can evolve. Tell me, is there something special about Durian Grass?",
    ["Dialogue3010907"]="Hmph! Of course there is: Durian Grass is <size=24>extremely</size><size=26> smelly!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3010908"]="(Bertha's expression changes.)\n...Extremely smelly? Hold on, does that mean the stinky plant my father hates at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Farm</color> is Durian Grass?! If it's so attractive to Lunatics, could that mean Green Cotton Farm is in... Oh no!",
    ["Dialogue3010909"]="Hey! Where are you going? How can you run off like that in the middle of a conversation?! How rude!",
    ["Dialogue3011001"]="Hang on, if I heard correctly, that monster researcher just mentioned that there's Durian Grass on Green Cotton Farm, right?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Maybe you'll be able to recover your losses there. This is a great business opportunity, Betty. Someone as smart as you can't afford to pass it up!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3011002"]="Ahem, I'm worried that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Farm</color> might be in trouble. Why don't we hurry over there and keep an eye on the situation! Hey! Why are you looking at me like that?",
    ["Dialogue3011101"]="(Klaus yells furiously.)\nArgh! My precious wheat... My precious pumpkins! Those Lunatics... They've ruined all my crops!",
    ["Dialogue3011102"]="As I expected, these Lunatics were attracted by the Durian Grass on the farm and have gathered here.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Fortunately, father is...</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>His shouting</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> at least it means he should be fine.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3011103"]="This smelly weed is called Durian Grass? Whatever, its name isn't important. I don't know where the seeds came from, but they've been growing like crazy for the last few days; I haven't had time to get rid of them. Those Lunatics have been trespassing here. There were only a few at first, but then there were more and more of them!",
    ["Dialogue3011104"]="By Odin, those Fabre were already more than enough for me. Now it's Lunatics as well. It looks like it might be time for me to retire.",
    ["Dialogue3011105"]="(Bertha cries out in surprise and shakes with excitement)\nWow! So Eclipses have such an amazing reproductive capability! That's a major discovery! I'm yet another step closer to understanding them!",
    ["Dialogue3011106"]="Shut up, Bertha. No one wants to understand these terrible monsters! I just want them gone from the farm! Someone... anyone, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>get rid of the little blue Eclipses</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3011201"]="(Klaus looks at his crops in distress.)\nSigh, thank you for saving Green Cotton Farm from disaster. But I'm still very worried; the Lunatics ate almost all the smelly weeds, but given how fast they grow, it won't be long before the place is overrun again. When that happens, Lunatics will be back, and lots of them!",
    ["Dialogue3011202"]="Father, calm down. Do you see that <color=#CA2E0AFF>young merchant</color> over there? She's been staring at your fields with glee all this time. My intuition as a monster researcher tells me she has a solution to your Durian Grass troubles. Adventurer, isn't she with you? Why don't you ask her about it?",
    ["Dialogue3011301"]="<size=18>Let me calculate it again...</size><size=18> The price of one piece of Durian Grass is 800 Zeny. If I buy it from Green Cotton Farm for 200 Zeny, I'll make 600 Zeny profit!</size><size=18> If I can buy 100, I'll make 60,000 Zeny!</size><size=18> The key thing is they won't think the price is too low; they'll even be grateful!</size><size=18> Betty, someone as smart as you can't afford to miss this opportunity!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3011302"]="Ahem! I have a business proposal for your farm! I believe you'd very much like to get rid of all this Durian Grass, but rather than letting it go to waste, it would be better if the Wigner Chamber of Commerce buys it from you! I promise I'll offer a good price!",
    ["Dialogue3011303"]="But… the Durian Grass is growing... in the soil. How could a young lady possibly dirty her hands with such labor? I wonder if anybody would be kind enough to help a poor girl and <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect the Durian Grass</color>?\n(Betty looks at you with a sad look on her face.)",
    ["Dialogue3011401"]="Great! Then I can return to the Chamber of Commerce with peace of mind! I may not have journeyed with you for long, but I'm glad I met such a hardworking friend! I need to get back to Prontera as soon as possible now. I hope we meet again someday. Goodbye!",
    ["Dialogue3011501"]="(Bertha looks like she has thought of something funny and snickers.)\nHehehe!",
    ["Dialogue3011502"]="(Bertha quickly puts her hands behind her back.)\nOh, it's you! I thought that merchant had come back.",
    ["Dialogue3011503"]="(Bertha looks around and brings her finger to her lips.)\nShush. Don't tell anyone, but I kept some Durian Grass for myself. As long as I have it, my lovely Eclipses will never go extinct. I couldn't stand for that to happen!",
    ["Dialogue3011601"]="You're just in time, Adventurer. I happen to have something to discuss with you.",
    ["Dialogue3011602"]="I wonder if you have heard the rumors about the hidden gods in the Glast Heim recently?",
    ["Dialogue3011603"]="yes. In recent days, there have been many disappearances all over Glast Heim. The victims, mostly other Adventurers, went to the Glast Heim Churchyard to investigate. People are saying whilst they were investigation they all found a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange Horong</color>, and anyone who came into contact with the Horong would immediately vanish....",
    ["Dialogue3011604"]="But what's more strange is that the missing people, without exception, re-appeared in front of the Glast Heim <color=#CA2E0AFF>goddess statue</color> a few days after they disappeared. Not only were they unharmed, they regained consciousness quite quickly. The only problem is that they <color=#CA2E0AFF>couldn’t remember what happened during the disappearance</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3011605"]="(Rockley nods cautiously)\nYes, Adventurer. I also think this strange phenomenon may be caused by some channel connecting Dimensional Gap, which is somewhat similar to what happened to you, when you travelled back through time and space. Can you help us?",
    ["Dialogue3011606"]="If you wish to investigate, I would go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Churchyard</color>. There have been no casualties up until this point, however I always worry that that the worst could still happen....\n(Rockley bites his teeth and looks uneasy)",
    ["Dialogue3011701"]="(the ray of light flickers on and off, you hear an ethereal voice)\nTrial one, those who are disrespectful are invisible.....",
    ["Dialogue3011801"]="(the ray of light flickers on and off, you hear an ethereal voice)\nTrial two, those who are not brave are invisible.....",
    ["Dialogue3011901"]="(the ray of light flickers on and off, you hear an ethereal voice)\nTrial three, those with no love in their heart are invisible.....",
    ["Dialogue3012001"]="Heir of Odin's blood, I have been waiting for a long time.",
    ["Dialogue3012002"]="My name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sikoti</color>. Under Odin, I am one of the female martial gods. Since the god’s twilight battle, most of my hands and feet have turned to dust, only by virtue of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>power of Lu en</color> I maintain my divine consciousness . Now, each day, Odin's bloodline awakens. It's time to hand over the fate of the world to you.....",
    ["Dialogue3012003"]="Now now, there is no need to be confused, <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick up</color> the slate <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of me</color>. No matter how dangerous the road is in the future, we must remember our purpose....\nOdin... <size=18>Will always be proud of you....</size>\n(the figure of the goddess slowly fades into nothingness...)",
    ["Dialogue3012101"]="Are you okay, Adventurer?!",
    ["Dialogue3012102"]="Can I not be concerned? <size=26>It's been seven days</size> since you went to the Glast Heim Churchyard!",
    ["Dialogue3012103"]="What the hell happened? You... Do you remember any of it?",
    ["Dialogue3012104"]="The soul of a goddess?! She gave you a stone slab?\n(Rockley suddenly raises his pitch in his voice. I don't know whether he is surprised or excited)\nCan you show me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3012105"]="<color=#A1979FFF>... um, um! No mistake! This must be!</color>\nAdventurer! If I'm not wrong... What's engraved on this stone slab is Rune text!",
    ["Dialogue3012106"]="This is the oldest character on the mainland. Its usage and meaning have long been lost. In legend, the lord god Odin hung himself upside down on the top of Yggdrasil for nine days and nine nights before he obtained the Rune text. The three goddesses of fate use this text to write the ultimate mystery of the world....",
    ["Dialogue3012107"]="(Rockley rubs his chin thoughtfully)\n... I remember that the youngest of the three goddesses, the goddess of fate, is responsible for “weaving the future\"... Her name is \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Scotty</color>\".",
    ["Dialogue3012108"]="You're right! It must be her! So, do you think she did all of that in order to find the true heir of Odin's bloodline?\n<color=#A1979FFF>No wonder, from the moment you went in to the cemetery no one else has mysteriously disappeared.....</color>",
    ["Dialogue3012109"]="... do you want to know the meaning of the text on the slate? Sorry... Adventurer. Since ancient times, Rune script has been regarded as having divine power and wisdom. Not only is this outside the scope of historical archaeology, but unfortunately the help that the Eden Group can give you is very limited.",
    ["Dialogue3012110"]="But as far as I know, quite a few theological books are written in Rune... So maybe the church would be able to give you more clues than we can! It's not too late. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>slate</color> to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archbishop Wolmas</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue3012201"]="Adventurer, where did you get this?!",
    ["Dialogue3012202"]="(throughout your recollection, Archbishop Wolmas acts more and more surprised)\nI never... expected... In my lifetime, to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Script</color> again.......",
    ["Dialogue3012203"]="Yes, this is the Rune script that represents the origins of the world. Since Odin removed these <color=#CA2E0AFF>24</color> letters from the Yggdrasil, they have since held great power... I am sincerely happy for you, Adventurer, this shows that you have been recognized by Odin. From today forward, the strength in your blood with awaked, and you will rise to new heights.",
    ["Dialogue3012204"]="... that is to say, with the strength of Rune, you are granted Odin's protection, and a new <color=#CA2E0AFF>job advancement</color>.\n(Archbishop Wolmas stroked his beard in relief)",
    ["Dialogue3012205"]="Don't worry, Adventurer. Before hosting the job Advancement ceremony for you, I will have to make some preparations. And you, too, must take advantage of this period to exercise your body and dedication. After all, this is a Rune used to record the fate of all things. It is strength, trust and hope.....",
    ["Dialogue3012206"]="(the old man with white beard solemnly taps on your shoulder)\nThe goddess chose you, and therefore you should also bear the corresponding responsibility - from today on, you will shoulder the \"future\" of the entire kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue3012207"]="Well..... Please come back to me when you reach level <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>. When that time comes, I will host a new job advancement ceremony for you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3012901"]="(Peerless Jin appears completely unsurprised by your arrival. You note a bottle of bright red liquid in his hand.)\nA bottle of liquor called Purification Elixir symbolizes the turning over of a new leaf. Are you <color=#CA2E0AFF>resolved to become a Monk</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3012902"]="Very good!\n(Peerless Jin puts the bottle in the palm of your hand. You're surprised at how warm it feels.)",
    ["Dialogue3012903"]="The effects of the Purification Elixir on the body are much strengthened by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>well-fought battle</color>. Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue3013001"]="You truly have changed, Adventurer. It is time to weave clothing more suitable for your new class. I've already prepared all the necessary materials. I'll leave the acquisition of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chanting Beads</color> to you.",
    ["Dialogue3013002"]="You will find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Guardian Statue</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep within the forest of East Payon</color>, the fabled sacred guardian of all travelers and children. Pray to the statue with a true heart, and you'll be judged worthy of receiving a special Chanting Bead. Worry not for the strength of your conviction. Consider it no more than a special blessing the \"Odin of Payon\" gives all travelers such as yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3013101"]="Hmm... Very good. We can confer the monk's robe upon you with such materials in hand. It's time for you to return to the radiance of the goddess. Your masters are waiting.",
    ["Dialogue3013201"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become an Acolyte.",
    ["Dialogue3013202"]="Criatura Academy has no more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your potential beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task yet before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3013203"]="Give me your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>. You no longer need it. I'll present a Class Manual for your Second Class Advancement, which doubles as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3013301"]="Heh. Ready for your graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3013401"]="(Peerless Jin is already at his feet as if awaiting your arrival.)\nIt is good to see you again after all this time, stranger.",
    ["Dialogue3013402"]="Perfection in the Way of the Monk implies a communion with the heavens and a oneness with the universe. To cut a long story short, I've been waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue3013403"]="The miraculous that can be put into words is but a poor reflection of the Eternal Way that cannot be put into words, Adventurer. The first step of the Way of the Monk is to understand your own \"Way\" or, for Odin's believers, your \"faith.\" Are you ready to testify as to your \"Way\"?",
    ["Dialogue3013501"]="Since this is your decision, we shall begin the preparation of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purification Elixir</color> at once.",
    ["Dialogue3013502"]="Truly. The Purification Elixir will do wonders for your body—evolving it for the most vigorous of martial exercises, imbuing bone and sinew with new power. The drink will initiate your journey and requires three main ingredients: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Beast Blood</color>, Evil Spirits, and Lotus Seeds. You may purchase Beast Blood from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Albel in Seocho Market</color>. Or, if you have it with you already, simply give it to me now.",
    ["Dialogue3013601"]="Evil spirits, by Payon legend, are the spirits of humans deceived into pernicious corruption. You may locate them from the Bongun. These evil powers command the Munak under cover of night, and will open the graves of those long laid to rest. Wave the Soul Enchanter to restrain these entities for own use.",
    ["Dialogue3013602"]="However, Bongun magic only restrains the souls of those who practice evil. As long as you can maintain control of your mind, you have little to fear from their beguiling habits.\n(Peerless Jin hands you a flag with a skeletal adornment.)",
    ["Dialogue3013603"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Wave the Soul Enchanter</color> once you're ready for this task. Its magic will transport you to a place of Evil Spirits, or perhaps a grave site, or even a place of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bonguns</color> themselves. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wave it again</color> once you're finished <color=#CA2E0AFF>collecting the Evil Spirits</color> to return to the Incense Pavilion.",
    ["Dialogue3013701"]="Incorporeal Evil Spirits cannot be used, Adventurer. Furthermore, we will need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lotus Seed obtained from the Bright Lotus Pond</color> to bind the Evil Spirits to our purposes. Then we'll need to pray for the souls at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moonlit Temple</color> for purification before our preparations can be complete.",
    ["Dialogue3013801"]="I can guess from the look on your face your journey was quite unexpected?",
    ["Dialogue3013802"]="(Peerless Jin looks at the dark-colored Lotus Seed in your hand and smiles slightly.)\nAdventurer, do you believe that learning the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Way of the Monk</color> is a noble or foolish endeavor?",
    ["Dialogue3013803"]="But cannot an evil person also learn the Way?",
    ["Dialogue3013804"]="Thus I tell you the Way has no intrinsic nobility nor fault. That lies with the practitioner. Just as with the Evil Spirits you collected—the Spirit itself has no affiliation except its owner makes it so. As the wheel of fate turns, the souls of practitioners who have done evil shall be imprisoned by the Bongun, the same Bongun you fought. And you also shall face the same <color=#CA2E0AFF>choices between good and evil</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3013805"]="(Peerless Jin nods in approval at your answer.)\nPayon legend also tells that a Lotus Seed bound to an Evil Spirit can be lifted up to the gods to separate the <color=#CA2E0AFF>spirit from its evil</color>. Relieved of evil, the spirit can enter the Hall of Judex while the evil remains on the lotus.",
    ["Dialogue3013806"]="The Purification Elixir used by a Monk has no need of the pearly white Lotus Seed, but the Seed that can withstand the darkness of sin. For a Monk must have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>heart the size of a mountain and the reflexes of a bolt of lightning</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3013807"]="Once you drink this elixir you'll be condemned to carry the guilt that is not yours <color=#CA2E0AFF>through life</color>. With that said, do you still wish to become a Monk?",
    ["Dialogue3013808"]="I do not require an answer yet. And I will prepare your Purification Elixir regardless of what you decide to do ultimately. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>give me the Lotus Seed</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3013901"]="(Archbishop Wolmas strokes his beard and takes a long, happy look at you.)\nHow you've grown in just this last week since I saw you! I believe you are ready for Class Advancement Guidance.",
    ["Dialogue3013902"]="As I said, the Rune is a gift of the goddess and a witness to your strength. But do I suppose rightly you're still a little unsure of how to use this power?",
    ["Dialogue3013903"]="Right. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit your Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and battle skills. And... may have some exciting surprises in store too. Heh...",
    ["Dialogue3013904"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await your good news... and hopefully \"rebirth\" in front of Odin's Statue!",
    ["Dialogue3014001"]="...Really? The goddess gave you that Rune?\n(Alice smiles gently, as usual)\nWell... I always knew you could do it.",
    ["Dialogue3014002"]="(Alice listens to your recollection, nodding.)\nYou are an excellent student and, of course, I would be delighted to see continued progress. But you cannot simply become a Shura without obtaining a great understanding.",
    ["Dialogue3014003"]="I received a letter not long ago from Master Peerless Jin inviting us to Payon for your Class Advancement trial. I will leave immediately. Please find me and Master Jin in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> once you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue3014101"]="You've already become a champion of world-renown since we bid farewell at your Monk trials. I have no doubt you have been as much changed from within as without.",
    ["Dialogue3014102"]="How much guilt must one carry on the road from Monk to Champion? No doubt many Champions are wearied by ordinary emotion so taken are they with the martial way. Yet I judge them not, for if they did not suspend their passions, the guilt of so many past lives would overwhelm them.",
    ["Dialogue3014103"]="This is why some Champions have turned their back on the Way of the Monk and \"compassion upon the multitude\" to embrace the Way of the Shura for more power. Become a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fierce and aggressive</color> Shura, and of that, you can be certain. Alice, would you allow the Adventurer to become a Shura?",
    ["Dialogue3014104"]="No! I won't allow any student of mine to become a heartless beast <color=#CA2E0AFF>bereft of human emotion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3014105"]="And what do you say for yourself, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3014106"]="So you would <color=#CA2E0AFF>fall into the evils of the Shura Way</color> just for more power? I'm sure you know your spirit may also be captured by the Bonguns once your Shura evil outweighs your karmic good?",
    ["Dialogue3014107"]="In the ancient books of Payon, Shura is born from sins and has the power of a god and desires of a human being. Their devotees have eyes, ears, and hearts, yet no feeling nor compassion; having ears, they hear not the cries of the needful. Having eyes, they understand not the Way. They are cold-hearted, arrogant, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>never end well</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3014108"]="Oh?\n(Peerless Jin looks at you keenly, inviting you to continue.)",
    ["Dialogue3014109"]="I don't want to abandon my oath!",
    ["Dialogue3014110"]="You mean, you wish to become a kind-hearted Shura? As I understand it, you are still quested to locate a Fragment of Ymir's Heart, each of which offers unbounded, almost limitless energy. If you should fall into the evils of the Shura Way, wouldn't such power be a disaster for us all?",
    ["Dialogue3014111"]="You...\n(Peerless Jin hesitates for a moment, exchanging glances with Master Alice.)\nYou have nothing to prove, Adventurer. In fact, I fear you are overeager to rush into that you know not.",
    ["Dialogue3014112"]="Remember the Chanting Bead you received from the Earth Guardian Statue before becoming a Monk? Take it with you and <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray once again at the Statue</color>. Perhaps a prayer of peace might still your heart.",
    ["Dialogue3014201"]="You don't mean... it gave you this...?",
    ["Dialogue3014202"]="(Peerless Jin looks at you in surprise as if finally seeing you for the first time.)\nWhat have you been entrusted with...",
    ["Dialogue3014203"]="Master Jin?",
    ["Dialogue3014204"]="(Cough) Did you really receive this from the Earth Guardian Statue? It's impossible! Never has it been recorded that any Shura has practiced the <color=#CA2E0AFF>karmic virtues of goodness</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3014205"]="I cannot tell yet, but I assure you that if you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather for me 10 samples of blood</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak, Bongun, and Sohee</color> and return alive then I shall! Adventurer, I have a sad chapter of Payon's history to reveal to you and one, I'm afraid, is little known and much less discussed.",
    ["Dialogue3014301"]="Let me think about where best to begin... alright. I shall start my account from the Earth Guardian Statue deep within the forest...",
    ["Dialogue3014302"]="The so-called Earth Guardian is not, in fact, a god, but was originally a <color=#CA2E0AFF>man from a far eastern kingdom in ancient times</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3014303"]="I assure you that I was as surprised as you when I first heard this.\n(Peerless Jin sighs and then continues over your surprised expression.)\nIt was only because this man was kind to children and a traveler that the people of Payon afterward fashioned him into the patron saint you see today.",
    ["Dialogue3014304"]="Payon was subject to a terrifying <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Invasion</color> one thousand years ago. So great was the horde that the sun could not be seen for its light, and the stench of death and poison filled the air.",
    ["Dialogue3014305"]="It was a young man from an ancient eastern kingdom who saved us all. He seemed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>attract</color> the monsters as a moth to a flame. In fact, the monsters could not attack anyone else in Payon with this man present, but fought him as closely as his own shadow.",
    ["Dialogue3014306"]="The people of Payon proposed an alliance with the mysterious traveler and they counterattacked. They had no need to fear that the young would perish for his powers in battle were indeed akin to those of a god.",
    ["Dialogue3014307"]="The people only learned of this youth's name after the battle, the pronunciation of which is similar to <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Earth Guardian.\"</color> Thus the people of Payon welcomed the so-called \"Earth Guardian\" with open arms, and elevated him into a kind of divinity. Yet he rejected all this.",
    ["Dialogue3014308"]="The Earth Guardian said that he was not worthy of \"godhood\", nor was there any need to proclaim it. For in the eyes of the people from whence he came, any person to accumulate enough good karma would naturally transcend into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"blessed state\".</color> It was this blessed state that could save us all.",
    ["Dialogue3014309"]="The Earth Guardian agreed to live amongst the people of Payon, who discovered even after decades he had <color=#CA2E0AFF>not aged a day</color>, nor did wrinkles appear on his face.",
    ["Dialogue3014310"]="Eventually, an even greater Monster Invasion arrived. As before, Earth Guardian fought with the people of Payon, but unlike before he received little thanks. Some even believed he was in some way associated with the monsters, or at least partly responsible for drawing them hither.",
    ["Dialogue3014311"]="(Peerless Jin looks at you anxiously.)\nAdventurer, perhaps you'd best take a step back and wait by the well. It is best not to invest oneself overmuch in these matters...",
    ["Dialogue3014401"]="To continue my story, for whatever reason—popular distrust or the brutality of the invasion—the Earth Guardian and his Payon co-defenders could <color=#CA2E0AFF>no longer see eye-to-eye</color>. They banished the Earth Guardian outside the city walls and awaited the next day's battle.",
    ["Dialogue3014402"]="The armies of the city marched out the next morning to find a pile of monster corpses as high as a mountain, but no trace of Earth Guardian's body. Had he been ripped to shreds? But these words were found written on the battlefield in monster blood:<color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Before Hades is empty, I shall not end my journey.\"</color>In the culture of the Earth Guardian's homeland, the evil and sinful went to a place called \"Hades\" to be punished. So saying, the Earth Guardian vanished.",
    ["Dialogue3014403"]="Based on the objects you were given by his statue, I think not. Only a \"Holy One\" could give Holy Beads or have heard your prayers... or given anything to you.",
    ["Dialogue3014404"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>I gave you the Chanting Bead myself!</color> I placed it there when your eyes were closed in prayer. Are you impressed? The statue was erected by the people of Payon in guilt over their mistreatment of the Earth Guardian, which is also why almost all reference to his real identity has been scrubbed from our books. Yet they dared not build the statue within the city walls, but only in the forest outside.",
    ["Dialogue3014405"]="Be of good cheer, I mean nothing harm to you. I've just been struggling with how Earth Guardian could have chosen the Way of the Shura as a means to express his beliefs. I felt I had to orchestrate this meeting when I saw you had chosen the same path.",
    ["Dialogue3014406"]="It was only when I saw the Holy Bead I realized I'd been fixated on a question I need not answer. Surely, to judge a person on their chosen class is far too narrow-minded?",
    ["Dialogue3014407"]="Very well. If the Earth Guardian accepts you, then I'm afraid that I must also accept your choice as well! Master Alice, you should also return.",
    ["Dialogue3014408"]="I-I'm sorry, I was rather spellbound by that account. Adventurer, and my dear pupil, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Wolmas the Archbishop</color> to perform your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>. Come with me!",
    ["Dialogue3014501"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3014601"]="Heh, you look like you're in good shape, adventurer. I can tell from how you're holding your bow that you're already able to wield it as naturally as your own limbs. It's time to teach you something new.",
    ["Dialogue3014602"]="An archer lives and dies by their bow. They are as sharp as an arrow in flight, and just as deadly. Their only mission is to dispatch their enemies with ruthless efficiency. If you have become accustomed to acting as I have described, you are ready to continue learning the secrets of the bow. It is time for you to become a hunter. Master Sky Euin of the Payon Archer Village is waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue3014603"]="Arrows turn into lyres and whips, and bows hide poems and dances. If you still have compassion in the rain of arrows, and would like to comfort both deities and humans, you can learn to be a poet or dancer. Mr. Gallacher of Babchka Forest is waiting for you.",
    ["Dialogue3014604"]="Your eyes that are as sharp as arrows have given you away. Haha! I already know your answer. Advance toward the target in your heart. I pray for your triumphant return.",
    ["Dialogue3014701"]="(A graceful middle-aged man stands atop a natural terrace, unaware of your approach.)\nThe sound of the water flow is just right, and the bubbles burst at the perfect interval... The temperature of the hot springs today is very pleasant, very suitable for...",
    ["Dialogue3014702"]="Adventurer?! Ahem... it's improper on Comodo to visit a gentleman able to bathe... What are you here for?",
    ["Dialogue3014703"]="I see.\n(Callahan picks up his clothes without questioning your intrusion further.)",
    ["Dialogue3014704"]="The Euphonic Symphony is willing to offer instruction and guidance to talented Bard and Dancer prospects. You just demonstrated to me you are refined, but are you as graceful and elegant within? According to the rules, we will test you through a <color=#CA2E0AFF>quiz</color>. Do you accept?",
    ["Dialogue3014801"]="Not bad, you're now eligible for the next round. Next, as an interim instructor, I shall teach you the first lesson: auditory perception.",
    ["Dialogue3014802"]="Whether in battle or performance, auditory perception is essential, and the sound of nature is the simplest form. If you care enough, it's not that hard to perceive the sea breeze of Kokomo Beach, the rustlings of Papuchicha Forest, and the cackling bonfire on Comodo.",
    ["Dialogue3014803"]="(Callahan nudges his glasses, smiles, and nods.)\nWell then, we will begin the test on that note. Please collect for me <color=#CA2E0AFF>the sound of sea breeze assembling and dispersing, the sound of a forest growing, and the sound of flame passing through the ground surface</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3014804"]="Note that I said \"collect\"! Every sound has a corresponding vessel. Our first bards and dancers parlayed their auditory perception of the sounds into such representations for inspired performances. The most remarkable bards and dancers were said to be able to pacify even <color=#CA2E0AFF>the most relentless monsters and bestow upon them the deepest slumber</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3014805"]="Three sounds, three vessels. Are you ready to answer, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3014901"]="Waaah, bad Adventurer! I've been looking for the conch for a long time...!",
    ["Dialogue3014902"]="I don't want it!\n(She tries to wipe her tears away only to cry even harder.)\nYou grown-ups always cheat children like this! That's the conch I want to give to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bard</color> over there!",
    ["Dialogue3014903"]="He trained for a long time to get on the stage. I... I wanted to go cheer him, but my mother wouldn't let me, so I could only wait here...",
    ["Dialogue3014904"]="Really? If you would take me, I can probably give you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second best-looking conch</color>! You wouldn't lie to a kid, would you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3014905"]="Yay!\n(She shouts out in glee, wraps her arms around your leg, and looks at you with innocent eyes.)\nWould you let me ride piggyback?",
    ["Dialogue3015001"]="He's so cool! Wait, what are you still doing here?",
    ["Dialogue3015002"]="Oh yeah!\n(She hands you a spotless conch and you can feel it's still a bit warm.)",
    ["Dialogue3015003"]="Now we're even! Oh, do you plan to give it to someone you like?",
    ["Dialogue3015004"]="The sound of a forest growing? Hmm, maybe <color=#CA2E0AFF>Toland in Papuchicha Forest</color> would know! Wouldn't you go there to figure out what it is, anyway?",
    ["Dialogue3015101"]="The sound of a forest growing... Perhaps this is what you're looking for, Adventurer.\n(Toland grabs a small pouch from the warehouse behind him and hands it to you.)",
    ["Dialogue3015102"]="Only one kind of tree could grow to be a whole forest on its own. It roots deeply and wide, forming a network as branches and leaves expand until it becomes one huge, dense foliage.",
    ["Dialogue3015103"]="You know I'm telling the truth if you've ever seen a thousand-year-old banyan tree.",
    ["Dialogue3015104"]="Yes, it is the seed of a banyan tree. Millennial banyan trees will muscle every other tree out, so only the Papuchicha Forest is vast enough for it to grow. Take the seed to your master. Maybe when you become an outstanding performer, the tree would also be in its finest form.",
    ["Dialogue3015105"]="Ahem... Mind if I trouble you with a request, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3015106"]="Can you deliver an outfit to someone in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo lighthouse</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue3015107"]="Alas... I can't go into it too much.\n(Toland starts to cough.)\nAll you have to do is give it to her.",
    ["Dialogue3015201"]="Did an old man hand this to you? I...\n(Her hands tremble as she rubs the edge of the costume, her voice a little choked up.)",
    ["Dialogue3015202"]="Sorry, but I can't go back... I...",
    ["Dialogue3015203"]="No... Maybe tomorrow is a new day... I can go back then...",
    ["Dialogue3015204"]="(She never turns around to see you.)\nAnyway, thank you. How can I repay you?",
    ["Dialogue3015205"]="The sound of fire passing through the ground? No amount of flame could heat the expansive ocean, much less land.",
    ["Dialogue3015206"]="The faster it flows, the quicker it cools, until it becomes a dark, hollow <color=#CA2E0AFF>rock</color>, and no one could ever tell it was once hot.",
    ["Dialogue3015207"]="(She puts the costume aside and ignores you.)",
    ["Dialogue3015301"]="Now, you're even more qualified. We'll resume the lesson when your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level reaches 50</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3015302"]="Heh! Why don't you take a guess as to what lesson is next?",
    ["Dialogue3015401"]="There you are.\n(Callahan acknowledges you with a nod.)\nI set up a spacious field of <color=#CA2E0AFF>battle</color> for you. Watch for the very first whoosh of the wind. That's the warning from nature to you.",
    ["Dialogue3015402"]="When you're confirmed to pass the test, you'll receive the appropriate class costume from the Euphonic Symphony. Go forth, future performer.",
    ["Dialogue3015501"]="Heh, it's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember when you first became an Archer!",
    ["Dialogue3015502"]="We here at the Criatura Academy have nothing left to teach you. Congratulations on reaching your potential. However, there's one more thing you need to do before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3015503"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>, you no longer need it. I'll give you a new Class Manual for your second class, which doubles as your <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3015601"]="Ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3015701"]="(Archbishop Wolmas strokes his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily.)\nI haven't seen you for a few days and apparently you have changed quite a bit! It seems you are ready for class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3015702"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, thus proving you have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused over how to use the power.",
    ["Dialogue3015703"]="It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit your Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and combat skills... plus perhaps a few exciting surprises too.",
    ["Dialogue3015704"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await the good news, and hopefully I could witness your \"rebirth\" before the Odin's Statue soon!",
    ["Dialogue3015705"]="Ooh! Mr. Callahan has expressed his appreciation for you to me. If you're ready, come with me to Papuchicha Forest for your new lesson!",
    ["Dialogue3015801"]="(The elegant middle-aged man takes his time examining your clothing before nodding slightly.)\nPerception of the sounds of nature is not nearly enough to become an outstanding Wanderer or Minstrel. This time, I'd like you to show me your <color=#CA2E0AFF>empathy for human emotions</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3015802"]="Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>throw these pearls into the Kokomo Sea</color> and then bring back what surfaces. If everything proceeds as usual, it will be an old musical composition. That is your test, as well as the wager between Miss Vendra and me. You will determine who wins.",
    ["Dialogue3015803"]="(Callahan smirks as if he's expecting something out of you.)\nWin or lose is not important, your answer is.",
    ["Dialogue3015804"]="We're betting on the manuscript that you retrieved... the <color=#CA2E0AFF>emotional tone of Frederick and Osanna's final work</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3015805"]="What who?",
    ["Dialogue3015806"]="(Callahan is too immersed in his own thoughts to notice your question.)\nMinstrel Frederick's tunes are somber and sorrowful, whereas Wanderer Osanna danced to very energetic rhythms. It is said they often criticized each other publicly before the marriage.",
    ["Dialogue3015807"]="Even though it was an arranged marriage that forced them to go through thick and thin for ages, they have never performed in public together, and their separation was a common occurrence.",
    ["Dialogue3015808"]="But Frederick's pupil claimed the two had a fantastic relationship, and before he passed from illness, Frederick even wrote a score with Osanna. However, she buried it at sea alongside Frederick's body and vanished without a trace afterward.",
    ["Dialogue3015809"]="Ahem! Miss Vendra and I both believe the pupil's story, but differ in our opinions of the style and emotional tone underlying the composition. We couldn't quite hold a civil discussion, thus we decided to invite a trustworthy third party to <color=#CA2E0AFF>preside over the wager</color>. It will not invalidate the friendship between us, no matter who wins.",
    ["Dialogue3015901"]="Callahan:\n(He flips through the manuscript at an amazing speed and frowns even more with each page turned.)\nHow come...?",
    ["Dialogue3015902"]="(Callahan seems incredulous.)\nThis isn't on their level at all, Vendra!",
    ["Dialogue3015903"]="(Vendra takes the composition, browses, and chuckles.)\nThis is indeed on their level, Callahan, just not what we're expecting.",
    ["Dialogue3015904"]="You two mind speaking in a way I could understand?",
    ["Dialogue3015905"]="At first, we thought if the couple were to collaborate, one of the two would take the lead. Callahan thinks after a hard life, Frederick finally met the love of his life only to then be terminally afflicted, so the circumstance would prompt a tear-jerker out of him, especially when Osanna was likely to grant him that final wish.",
    ["Dialogue3015906"]="I see the complete opposite. Osanna was spoiled since her childhood. She never cared for Frederick's aspiration to create the \"magnum opus of sorrow\" and even publicly mocked his quest as the \"magnum opus of cheesiness.\"",
    ["Dialogue3015907"]="Aside from conflicting personalities, even if Osanna was willing to change, it definitely wouldn't be because of her husband's impending demise, which she'd see as a shallow gesture. Rather, she would cheer him up with a lively score.",
    ["Dialogue3015908"]="Now, this is a sad song with forced joy for a vibrant dance underlined by sorrow. A work like this has no meaningful expression and is more akin to a product of beginners who try to cram every emotion only to end up with nothing substantial. Callahan, our <color=#CA2E0AFF>bet is inconclusive</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3015909"]="Alas, if the style could be consistent, coupled with the pair's talent and accomplishments, it would have been a legendary masterpiece...",
    ["Dialogue3015910"]="Very good of you to discern that.\n(Callahan nods, then sighs.)",
    ["Dialogue3015911"]="Since the couple passed away, countless scholars have studied and analyzed their work with no shortage of praise, but very few noted that behind the creations hid the facts that Osanna became infertile from excessive fasting, and Frederick's abuse of tobacco and alcohol turned his health into a mess. Is it worth dedicating your life and emotions to intangible arts? And will one truly get what one wants afterward?",
    ["Dialogue3015912"]="I cannot begin to theorize it, let alone anticipate, except to offer you blessings as your master. Whether you will become a Minstrel mingling among the prestigious or a Wanderer among the masses, there's always room for withdrawal and resurgence.",
    ["Dialogue3015913"]="Bodies have emotions but are not bound by them. My pupil, you don't have to fight over your profession. Just living your life with a clear conscience will suffice. Now, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Archbishop Wolmas</color> for the Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3016001"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. We may formally begin the Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time you prove your resolve to Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3016101"]="Ooh! Mr. Callahan has expressed his appreciation for you to me. If you're ready, come with me to Papuchicha Forest for your new lesson!",
    ["Dialogue3016201"]="Heh, it seems our little Adventurer is a seasoned Super Novice already. Very well, Criatura Academy needs more motivated youngsters.",
    ["Dialogue3016202"]="Becoming an Expanded Super Novice means learning more class skills and more combos. Wouldn't varying your combat approach to baffle the enemy before dealing them a surprise blow be a very cool way to fight?",
    ["Dialogue3016203"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Tanders in Mjolnir Mountains</color> has been in charge of all Job Advancement tests for Novices. He inherited the title of Windmill Knight and wandered the land until returning to Mjolnir Mountains at sixty years of age, so he's turned into an acerbic old man.",
    ["Dialogue3016204"]="Heh! Deep in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest of Mjolnir Mountains</color> hid something very interesting. It will be a challenge for you, little Adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue3016301"]="(Atop the peak, a hale old man looks at you, frowns and barks loudly.)\nExaminee, why do you just arrive now?",
    ["Dialogue3016302"]="Don't you know because you are two minutes late, the prison wagons of spirits are rolling over the valley. The poor gnomes are taken by the Queen of the Underworld's minions solely for their familiarity with jewel making. The weeping of the dead and the wailing of the living still haunt my pure, compassionate heart to this date!",
    ["Dialogue3016303"]="Sir, that is the caravan delivering ore from the Mjolnir Dead Pit.",
    ["Dialogue3016304"]="Shut up, Sansha, I am the wise master here. You are just an unwaveringly loyal servant. This was established thirty-three years ago when we both became Novices. Are you questioning my judgment now?",
    ["Dialogue3016305"]="(The middle-aged squire sighs and drags his enunciation.)\nAllllll right, Maaaaster, then how should we greet this rising star here for the trial?",
    ["Dialogue3016306"]="Sansha, my obtuse servant! How could a star be made without baptism by fire, blood, death, and loathing? Remember your objective, examinee: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Proceed to the deceptive, bewildering forest in the mist and retrieve The Scroll of Destined Fate</color>. This is the sole criterion for passing the test!",
    ["Dialogue3016307"]="Your eyes are full of haughtiness! Do not underestimate this test, examinee! In it, you will encounter a cunning sage, a flirtatious witch, and a rancid new king! They are all part of the trial. You must succeed in order to exit the forest!",
    ["Dialogue3016308"]="The naivete in your eyes is identical to mine when I was young! Remember, <color=#CA2E0AFF>do not debate with the sage, do not fall for the witch, and do not beg for the king's mercy</color>. You must follow your heart whenever you are in the mist!",
    ["Dialogue3016309"]="Examinee, do you still remember answering Dean Mainz's question in the Temple of Dawn? Now stand up straight and <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer me</color> this again!",
    ["Dialogue3016401"]="Very good!\n(Tanders points to the entrance of Labyrinth Forest in the distance.)\nNow, let the <color=#CA2E0AFF>test begin</color>! Keep up with us, Sansha!",
    ["Dialogue3016402"]="It is not necessary for an examiner to accompany the examinee, sir.",
    ["Dialogue3016403"]="I am more aware than you, Sansha. That is why they will always manage to spot the portent of disasters and become the warriors who fight such alone. In fact, I am hearing the countless bees buzzing at the foot of the mountains, attempting to intrude into the juicy flower chambers with their filthy mouthparts and siphoning the vitality of the entire range.",
    ["Dialogue3016404"]="Sir, it is common for Hornets to be devoured by the carnivorous Flora when gathering honey. And according to the rules, we must stay here until the test is over.",
    ["Dialogue3016405"]="Ah, the laziness of the mediocre... Sansha, the one before you, has sworn a vow. From that moment henceforth, the illusions of the Labyrinth Forest can no longer deceive the eyes. Completion of the test is merely a matter of time, just like me.",
    ["Dialogue3016406"]="(Tanders stands up straight and pats you on the shoulder firmly.)\nIsn't that right, examinee!",
    ["Dialogue3016407"]="Is that so? Then welcome to your destiny! I shall welcome mine, as well! I have a feeling that this disaster <color=#CA2E0AFF>is different from all before</color>, but to Tanders the Windmill Knight, it's nothing worth mentioning! Fetch my steed, Sansha!",
    ["Dialogue3016501"]="Hmm, you are not carrying any compass or magic guiding device on you, are you?",
    ["Dialogue3016502"]="How foolish! Tanders will not search your body, so why wouldn't you bring instruments for the test? Let me guess, you have no water, rations, salves, or any such provisions, either?",
    ["Dialogue3016503"]="How foolish! Going into the Labyrinth Forest totally unprepared... Is this how your Novices rush through tests? Or do you not even know what's involved?",
    ["Dialogue3016504"]="That's right. But until then, you must choose a portal next to me for passage. Listen up, only one out of these four portals is the right one, and you only get one chance. Hence, this is a multiple-choice challenge.",
    ["Dialogue3016505"]="But you are very lucky, examinee. As a sage, I loathe all uncertainties. As a proctor, I have the authority to revise the test question to a certain degree. Each of the four portals corresponds to a difficult question about Super Novice class skills. For each question you answer correctly, I will eliminate one incorrect choice for you.",
    ["Dialogue3016506"]="\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Never regret the choice made this moment</color>.\" Do you remember the oath you took when becoming a Novice, examinee? Now, use all means at your disposal to choose the correct answers.",
    ["Dialogue3016507"]="Oh? You already know the answer? Or are you just guessing randomly?",
    ["Dialogue3016508"]="What are you doing? Hey, I'm a proctor. Don't come any closer!",
    ["Dialogue3016601"]="(A sad yet glamorous witch sidles up. She glides her vermilions nails over your facial features before letting go in lament.)\nYou are not my Anthony, nor do you belong here...",
    ["Dialogue3016602"]="Scroll in the deep forest? Indeed, I promised an old man to point the way for the approved. But you're not <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anthony</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3016603"]="Anthony is a very fine man. He's never lied to me... Therefore, he will certainly come back. I just have to wait for him here...",
    ["Dialogue3016604"]="I don't know... When I began the wait, my hair was still above the ears, and it has reached my lower back now. But I'm willing to wait. Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>waiting is not tedious</color>. If you know the person will surely come, perhaps he will emerge the very next second...",
    ["Dialogue3016605"]="Surely... not. I can't leave here.\n(Hope gleams in the witch's eyes for a fleeting second.)\nHowever, are you truly willing to take me to find Anthony?",
    ["Dialogue3016606"]="Then I choose to believe you.\n(The witch takes a ring off and stares at the deep depression on her ring finger.)\nAnthony said that no one could bear to, or would dare to, lie to the witch.",
    ["Dialogue3016607"]="This is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anthony's ring</color>. It will take you to the next challenge as well as to its master. Whether you find Anthony, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>make sure to come back</color>, Adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue3016701"]="Ahem... Who are you? Ahem, ahem!\n(A frail young man gazes at you after a round of severe coughs.)\nAre you here to take me away?",
    ["Dialogue3016702"]="Anthony... The name sounds very familiar... I don't remember, though. You're the first person I see since I've been awake... Ahem, ahem!",
    ["Dialogue3016703"]="That is...\n(A stunned Anthony raises a hand to show an <color=#CA2E0AFF>identical ring</color> on his ring finger.)\nWhy do I have one too...? My head... Ugh, ugh...!",
    ["Dialogue3016704"]="I am... My name is... No, how can I even forget her...",
    ["Dialogue3016705"]="I don't want to forget... Must remember, I must remember...\n(Anthony brutally pounds on himself. His bloodshot eyes glare grudgingly at the sky obscured in fog.)\nCurses... Why did this happen to me?!",
    ["Dialogue3016706"]="I really can't recall anything...\n(Anthony clutches your hands as if holding on to a life-saving plank.)\nWhoever you are... I beg you... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take me... to...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3016801"]="You've changed on the outside, Anthony, but you're still the same inside...",
    ["Dialogue3016802"]="(Anthony's red eyes open wide, looking incredulously at Zealotus.)\nReally? Anthony is my name...?",
    ["Dialogue3016803"]="Yes. Before the Void tainted the Labyrinth Forest, you're the warden here. One day, I wanted to set the flowers ablaze because I failed to get the first Breeze Orchid in the spring. It was you who stopped me.",
    ["Dialogue3016804"]="You're an exceedingly dutiful warden, Anthony. And that is why you became so tainted with the Void because you would not abandon this forest, even to the bitter end.",
    ["Dialogue3016805"]="I'm... dead?",
    ["Dialogue3016806"]="Yes...\n(The witch nestled in Anthony's arms smiles in relief.)\nAnd it's time we part...",
    ["Dialogue3016807"]="Did you forget, Anthony? Your body was devoured clean by the monsters in the Void long before help arrived... As for me, I could only keep your spiritual remnants around with the last thread of my sanity... This Adventurer's mentor promised me if I would watch over this place forever, in a hundred years your spirit will <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow your last will and reunite with me...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3016808"]="So you are the last person I wanted to see? I'm sorry, I only remember I had to see someone but couldn't recall who. I can't believe you waited so long by yourself...",
    ["Dialogue3016809"]="I got used to it, Anthony.\n(The witch kisses his eyes.)\nI'm ecstatic if waiting for you can take up my lengthy yet dull life.",
    ["Dialogue3016810"]="But... we just met! Why do I have to leave? I don't want to go anywhere!",
    ["Dialogue3016811"]="No, you must go. Worry not, the place you're going to isn't like the Labyrinth Forest that's always shrouded in haze. Don't you miss the sun's warmth, Anthony? Before the Void, we used to lay among the Breeze Orchid and you would tell corny stories...",
    ["Dialogue3016812"]="I don't miss it! I'm not the warden of Labyrinth Forest anymore! If this forest is destined to be shrouded in fog, so be it! I just want to stay here...",
    ["Dialogue3016813"]="But I miss it...\n(Zealotus gently comforts an Anthony teetering on madness.)\nPromise me you'll enjoy the sunshine for me, Anthony...",
    ["Dialogue3016814"]="(The witch gradually fades and a new portal appears behind her.)\nAll of you shall begin a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new destiny</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3016815"]="Don't go! Stay!\n(Anthony grasps at the fading figure in vain, only to realize he is fading too.)\nHow... Why...?",
    ["Dialogue3016901"]="(Tanders waves a hand and stands in your path.)\nHalt! You've proven your resolve to me, Examinee. Now I shall give you a new task!",
    ["Dialogue3016902"]="That cunning monster had a glimpse of its own fate and <color=#CA2E0AFF>fled toward the desert</color>! I, Tanders the Windmill Knight, shall foil the dastardly effort!",
    ["Dialogue3016903"]="You got what my master is trying to say!",
    ["Dialogue3016904"]="Be quiet! For a true genius, even when incidental mishaps were made, they could be more than compensated with subsequent planning! I need your assistance, examinee!",
    ["Dialogue3016905"]="When the leader flees, the underlings become restless... Such is a matter too trivial for my blade but you to handle.",
    ["Dialogue3016906"]="Brandish your weapon and pacify its minions. Forge your glory with blood!",
    ["Dialogue3016907"]="March into the desert with this lazy servant of mine and shatter all conspiracies, of course! The evil portent is clear, Sansha. Perhaps the <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple haze</color> from centuries past is returning.",
    ["Dialogue3016908"]="Are you sure not to report this to Dean Mainz, Master? A returning Void is not something we can deal with! Not to mention the monster broke containment and took...",
    ["Dialogue3016909"]="We will discuss it later.\n(Tanders cuts Sansha off to spare you an irritated glance.)\nWhy are you not moving, examinee?",
    ["Dialogue3017001"]="This object shall help our desert journey. Keep it in your hands, Sansha!",
    ["Dialogue3017002"]="Am I allowed to decline?",
    ["Dialogue3017003"]="No, you lazy servant! Examinee, I acknowledge that you have what it takes to be an Expanded Super Novice. However, you're still one step away!",
    ["Dialogue3017004"]="Real battle experience it is! When your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job level reaches 50</color>, you may <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Prontera Cathedral</color> and experience the power of Expanded Super Novice in a real battle! Onward. When you're mighty enough, I will return from the desert for you!",
    ["Dialogue3019601"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Fire attribute enhancement. Using Water/Poison attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019602"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Water attribute enhancement. Using Wind attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019603"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Wind attribute enhancement. Using Earth/Poison attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019604"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Earth attribute enhancement. Using Fire/Poison attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019605"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Holy attribute enhancement. Using Shadow/Undead attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019606"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Shadow attribute enhancement. Using Holy attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019607"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Ghost attribute enhancement. Using Ghost/Undead attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3019608"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has gained Undead attribute enhancement. Using Fire/Holy attribute attacks will be more effective!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3020101"]="(Tanders clutches his head in agony.)\nArgh! It hurts! <size=24>It hurts!</size>\nThose damned monsters stung me where I don't have any hair. If I'd known, I would have bought a wig from Vera!",
    ["Dialogue3020102"]="(Tanders freezes momentarily and immediately tries to act nonchalant.)\nAhem, that's right, I am Windmill Knight Tanders! I believe we've met a couple of times at Prontera West Gate. Did you decide to leave your hometown to travel the world as a chivalrous knight just like me?",
    ["Dialogue3020103"]="Aha! I knew it! You're also a warrior with a sacred mission! Come, join me in stamping out the atrocities in the world to end all suffering! I assume you've come to Mjolnir Mountains to challenge the Mistress and get her stinger to make the legendary sword, am I right?",
    ["Dialogue3020104"]="Aha! I knew it! There isn't any warrior in this world who doesn't want a powerful weapon! I must remind you, however, that the path ahead of you is treacherous; only a determined person like me has what it takes to get stung by a swarm of Hornets until his head swells up like a balloon. Erm... I mean, to stay calm while fighting the Mistress!",
    ["Dialogue3020105"]="Ah, that sure was an epic battle! My head... Erm, I mean... my body sustained serious injury! But I must regain my strength as soon as possible to press on and save the world. Why don't you ask the owner of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color> if there's any potion that can <color=#CA2E0AFF>treat my injuries</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3020201"]="Adventurer, have you come to obtain some medicine for that knight?",
    ["Dialogue3020202"]="(Bidal makes a helpless expression.)\nI've been observing him for some time now. His head was obviously stung by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hornets</color> in the mountains, but I haven't been able to help him because he's been pretending that nothing happened.",
    ["Dialogue3020203"]="In fact, potions aren't necessary to treat the hornet venom. You just need to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cold Vanilla that grows in these parts and apply it to the wound</color> to accelerate the healing. However...\n(Bidal frowns slightly.)",
    ["Dialogue3020204"]="Sigh, it's just that the Hornets of Mjolnir Mountains have always been docile and have never attacked humans unless they were threatened! Looking at the condition of that knight, I can't imagine how many Hornets he must have provoked to end up in such a miserable state.",
    ["Dialogue3020301"]="(Tanders secretly takes out a few stalks of Cold Vanilla when you aren't paying attention. When you look at him again, you realize that the top of his head looks a little green.)\nAhem, I feel a lot better now; it doesn't hurt anymore! Damn, were it not for my <color=#CA2E0AFF>faithful companions</color> waiting for news down the mountain, I'd go back for a 300-round battle against the Mistress!",
    ["Dialogue3020302"]="Now, I sincerely invite you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany me down the mountain to find my companions</color>. I'm not inviting you because I'm afraid of danger, but because a great knight could never leave a friend alone in such a dangerous place where monsters lurk around every corner! Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue3020401"]="Adventurer, thank you very much for bringing Tanders back. If you hadn't, given his propensity for trouble, I doubt he would have made it back down alive!",
    ["Dialogue3020402"]="(Morts holds his forehead in despair.)\n...I was roped into traveling with him! All I did was tell him a few stories about heroic adventurers. The next thing I knew, he was making a big fuss about imitating those heroes and insisting on following me on my travels.",
    ["Dialogue3020403"]="Sigh, to make free-spirited bard such as I travel with an old man is like caging a bird or locking the sun in a box! If I could choose, I'd prefer the company of a few beautiful ladies!",
    ["Dialogue3020404"]="You can't say that. You'll be grateful for this experience one day! You have the opportunity to witness my great achievements with your own eyes on this journey; you'll be able to record them as ballads that will survive through the ages! Take my battle with the Mistress for example, I've even come up with a title for you. You can call it The Battle of Mjolnir. What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue3020405"]="Okay, I'll definitely describe how you insisted on climbing the mountain to challenge the Mistress with no regard for the obstacles ahead of you, and how you returned with a swollen head!",
    ["Dialogue3020406"]="Oh? You want to know about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>legend of the Mistress</color>?\n(Morts makes his signature smile.)\nIn that case, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>sit in front of me</color>. Let me tell you the story as only a bard can!",
    ["Dialogue3020501"]="I read this ballad in my teacher's notes. It tells the story of the birth of the Mistress, but some of it's missing. Actually, I came to Mjolnir Mountains to search for the answer. This need for scrutiny and exploration is precisely what makes ballads so fascinating, wouldn't you agree?",
    ["Dialogue3020502"]="You're asking me if the Mistress really exists? Haha! To a bard, there is no such thing as a legend that does not exist! However, all I know is written in that ballad. If you want to learn more, I suggest you ask the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster researcher</color> who came here with us. She's been completely engrossed in her work since she saw the monsters in the mountains. Perhaps she's made a discovery!",
    ["Dialogue3020601"]="(Bertha is deep in thought about something.)\n<size=18>Hmm, this truly is a major discovery.</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020602"]="<size=18>The Hornets of Mjolnir Mountains have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>especially active</color> lately. This means that another phenomenon worth studying is about to occur.</size> <size=18>What could it be? I need to know!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020603"]="<size=18>If I were to hazard a guess, I would say a mutant has arisen in the colony</size><size=18> or a marvelous evolution has taken place. Ahhh! Both scenarios are equally fascinating! I can't wait to find out the answer.</size><size=18> Let's just catch a Hornet to study!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020604"]="<size=18>Hehe! Fortunately, I prepared some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Honey</color> in advance. I had a feeling this would happen.</size> <size=18>I just need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put it in a place where Hornets often appear</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>lure</color> a Hornet!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020605"]="(Bertha seems to think of something and frowns.)\n<size=18>Hmm, but this type of monster is very sensitive. If I can't <color=#CA2E0AFF>pacify</color> it after luring it over, it's very likely that it'll attack. </size><size=18>It isn't appropriate for a scholar to do something so dangerous.</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020606"]="...Ah! Since you're already here, why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>trap the Hornet</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3020701"]="(Bertha cries out in surprise and shakes with excitement.)\nWow! You actually did it! Look at that pair of dexterous wings and that sharp stinger. It's like a work of art—a masterpiece of nature!",
    ["Dialogue3020702"]="To further study these Hornets, I must first <color=#CA2E0AFF>figure out what caused the changes to the colony</color>. The best way to do that is have a conversation with it!",
    ["Dialogue3020703"]="(Bertha covers her mouth and laughs mysteriously.)\nHehe! Of course I need to use their unique method of communication. Just wait and see!",
    ["Dialogue3020801"]="(Bertha clenches her fists as her face flushes red with anger.)\nWh-who would do such a thing?!",
    ["Dialogue3020802"]="The Hornet just told me that a human stole something very important to their species! The recent commotion among the Hornets on the mountain has been in an effort to recover their lost treasure. Grr, which fool could have caused such a mess? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tail this Hornet</color>. I want to see who it is for myself!",
    ["Dialogue3020901"]="...Ahem, I was just about to challenge those Ambernites to a duel when you suddenly appeared.\nArgh! Where did this Hornet come from?!",
    ["Dialogue3020902"]="(The Hornet makes a low buzzing sound.)\nBzzz!",
    ["Dialogue3020903"]="(Bertha squints at Tanders and makes a complicated expression.)\nJudging from the reaction of this Hornet, it seems to be really unhappy with you. Hold on, what's that <color=#CA2E0AFF>pupa</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3020904"]="Aha! So you've finally noticed it?\n(Tanders puffs out his chest with pride.)\nThis is my glorious trophy! Take a look!",
    ["Dialogue3020905"]="While I was searching for the Mistress, I discovered a swarm of Hornets guarding a Large Pupa. I thought it must be something evil, so I decided to steal... er, I mean, use my skills to take it away!",
    ["Dialogue3020906"]="Ah, it was an epic battle! I ventured deep into the colony and fought a hundred foes to get this pupa! Although they chased me with furious determination, and I somehow ended up being surrounded by Ambernites, punishing evil is always fraught with danger. I've already prepared myself for the worst. <size=24>Argh! Stay away from me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020907"]="(The Hornet makes a sharp buzzing sound and flies around Tanders' head.)\n...Bzzz!",
    ["Dialogue3020908"]="…Punishing evil?\n(Bertha sneers before lowering her head as her body trembles with rage.)\nHaha... So you're the one who threw the colony into turmoil! Tanders! I… <size=24>I've had enough of your ignorance!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020909"]="<size=24>Every single time… </size><size=24>I'm always the one who protects monsters that are good for us! </size><size=24>But every single time… </size><size=24>there's always some ignorant fool who creates a crisis for the species </size><size=24>and thinks that they're some kind of amazing hero! </size><size=24>You have no idea how important that pupa is to the colony. </size><size=24>And it almost became food for the Ambernites because of you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3020910"]="Argh! I've had enough of it! <size=24>Feel the</size> wrath of a monster researcher!\n(Bertha punches Tanders on the top of the head.)",
    ["Dialogue3020911"]="(Tanders looks shocked and aggrieved as he groans and presses his hand against the swollen lump on his head.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3020912"]="(Bertha dusts off her hands and turns sharply to face you.)\nAlright, now that we've sorted out this problem, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>take this precious pupa to a safe place</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue3021001"]="This pupa looks extremely fragile. You must be extremely careful when handling it!",
    ["Dialogue3021101"]="(Bertha examines the pupa carefully.)\n...What's this damage? Oh no! The pupa is very weak! If we can't keep it warm, it'll die before it can complete its incubation. Look around for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Firewood</color> to start a fire. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue3021201"]="(Bertha carefully examines the pupa once again and breathes a sigh of relief.)\nIt's all good. It should be able to complete its incubation smoothly now.",
    ["Dialogue3021202"]="(The Hornet makes an intermittent buzzing sound.)\n...Bzz! Bzz! Bzz!",
    ["Dialogue3021203"]="Is it a warning? What's happening? ...Oh!",
    ["Dialogue3021301"]="(Bertha cries out in surprise. She's so excited that she can barely breathe)\n...It-it's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mistress</color>! But it's very weak. Quickly, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stainers</color> nearby and fetch some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Insect Honey</color> to feed it!",
    ["Dialogue3021401"]="Human, I've seen everything you've done. Bzzz... Thank you for helping me be born into this world. Your kindness has saved the swarm from catastrophe... Bzzz...",
    ["Dialogue3021402"]="Every Mistress is born with the same mission: to protect the peace of the swarm when a <color=#CA2E0AFF>great catastrophe</color> strikes. Bzzz... Although I can't say exactly what catastrophe is coming, I can vaguely sense that it has something to do with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3021403"]="(The Mistress looks in the direction of Labyrinth Forest.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>The ancient seal</color> has been lifted, and there is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange force</color> there that I dare not approach. Part of it comes from <color=#CA2E0AFF>above ground</color>; the other part—the strangest part—comes from <color=#CA2E0AFF>under</color> the forest. Bzzz...",
    ["Dialogue3021404"]="I will be the one to lead the swarm in the future. I will do everything I can to protect them!",
    ["Dialogue3030101"]="(Eassis looks worried.)\nSigh, how I hope that this is the end of the changes in the pyramid, but alas, I'm afraid the real disaster has just begun...",
    ["Dialogue3030102"]="Yes... Although I don't want to say anything disrespectful, the greatest threat in the pyramid is now Lord Osiris! His body has reformed, but his soul is still in a state of chaos. If we can't find a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>appease Lord Osiris' soul</color>, the power of the pharaoh will surely bring unimaginable disaster to the pyramid and the outside world if it spirals out of control!",
    ["Dialogue3030103"]="I vaguely remember someone. If there's anyone who can save Lord Osiris, it's him. However...\n(Eassis holds her head in distress.)\nHowever, whenever I try to remember, my memories of the time when I was alive become fuzzier and fuzzier. Maybe this is the price of returning to the world of the living after death.",
    ["Dialogue3030104"]="I think I will only be able to remember the key to saving Lord Osiris if I can regain my memories. It just so happens that there are some <color=#CA2E0AFF>murals</color> in the pyramid that depict the history of the Egyptian Empire. Perhaps they'll have the answers we seek.",
    ["Dialogue3030201"]="Hmph! Let me see, who has overestimated their abilities and dares covet the treasures of the Egyptian Empire? I've guarded this mural for nearly a thousand years and have punished more desecrators than there are stones in this pyramid. Neither of you will be able to escape!",
    ["Dialogue3030202"]="Silence! I refuse to hear the explanations of desecrators! Die!",
    ["Dialogue3030301"]="(Kessoso looks around in horror. After he sees that there's nowhere to hide, his eyes twitch and he starts to smile flatteringly)\nEr... Hehe, you'll have to forgive my poor eyesight; I didn't see that two warriors have come! Um... What have you come here for? It won't be an issue as long as it's within my abilities! No issue at all!",
    ["Dialogue3030302"]="...Oh! You should have told me earlier. So, you just want to learn about the history depicted in this mural! As the guardian spirit, I can <color=#CA2E0AFF>send you into the mural</color>. It won't be an issue as long as you both agree! No issue at all!",
    ["Dialogue3030401"]="(Kessoso rubs his hands together gleefully.)\nAre you both ready?",
    ["Dialogue3030402"]="Excellent! I will now cast the spell!",
    ["Dialogue3030403"]="Fine, whatever you say!",
    ["Dialogue3030501"]="(Eassis looks all around like she's trying hard to remember something.)\nI feel like I've been here before. Huh? There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young man</color> lying on the ground over there. He looks very weak. Let's check on him!",
    ["Dialogue3030601"]="...Thank you for saving my life. I thought I was destined to die in this desert and be buried in its sands.",
    ["Dialogue3030602"]="...You might not believe me, but I'm actually the chief of an Egyptian tribe in the desert. Originally, my tribe and I lived farther south, but a natural disaster destroyed our home. Since then, I've had no choice but to lead my people on a journey to migrate elsewhere. However, our journey was long and we never managed to find a suitable place to settle.",
    ["Dialogue3030603"]="Most of the strong and young members of our tribe were killed by the natural disasters, and many of the others died during the migration. Only the young, elderly, infirm, and womenfolk survived, and it seemed like they wouldn't last much longer either, so I left alone to find food and water for them. However, there's nothing but wind and sand in this desert. If you hadn't show up when you did, I'm afraid I would have died of thirst.",
    ["Dialogue3030604"]="(The man sighs deeply.)\nI don't fear death, but I'm afraid my people will have no hope of survival if I die. If the almighty Ra really does exist, why has he closed his eyes to my people's suffering?",
    ["Dialogue3030605"]="Don't lose hope! You've already found the very thing you seek. There's an <color=#CA2E0AFF>oasis</color> just up ahead!\n(Eassis turns to you.)\nAdventurer, he's still too weak; I must request you to go to the oasis and bring back some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Tomatoes</color>. They're just what he needs!",
    ["Dialogue3030701"]="(The man examines the Desert Tomato.)\nI never knew food like this could be found in the desert. Thank you so much for your help. This precious food will surely restore my people's strength! Maybe I should bring them here to settle at this oasis. Hmm, what should I call it?",
    ["Dialogue3030702"]="\"Hope\"...? It's good name.\n(The stranger's eyes shine bright. He hesitates for a moment before turning to Eassis.)\nWhat... what's your name?",
    ["Dialogue3030703"]="(Eassis lowers her head and smiles shyly.)\nEassis. My name is Eassis.",
    ["Dialogue3030704"]="(The man stares deeply at Eassis.)\n…Eassis. I'll remember that. We'll surely meet again. Please remember the name of the person you saved. My name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Osiris</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3030801"]="Oops! Did I interrupt at the most exciting part? Unfortunately my power is only strong enough to show you this much of the past. If you ask me, no matter how good the past seems, the present is always better. The dead are not as good as the living!",
    ["Dialogue3030901"]="(Eassis' eyes are filled with nostalgia as she quietly watches the mural.)\nI remember now. That was the first time I met Lord Osiris. It's a shame it's impossible to return to that time.",
    ["Dialogue3030902"]="I remember that the Egyptians took root in this land because Lord Osiris led his tribe on a journey of migration. After that, he used the resources of Hope Oasis to make the tribe strong, building the capital city of Egypt at the center of the oasis and leaving countless great achievements that none have surpassed ever since.",
    ["Dialogue3030903"]="But my memories of what happened after are still very vague. Why don't we <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at the next mural</color>? Maybe it'll tell us even more about the past.",
    ["Dialogue3031001"]="(Issoso keeps coughing and looks very weak.)\nCough...! Please be gentle with this mural. It has been battered by wind, frost, and rain for thousands of years, and is as fragile as the old bones in my body.",
    ["Dialogue3031002"]="(Issoso looks troubled.)\n...I'm happy to send you into the mural, but... Cough...! As you can see, my strength has weakened with the passage of time and won't last long enough for me to finish casting the spell.",
    ["Dialogue3031003"]="If you can get me enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Hearts</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Matyrs</color> around here, maybe I'll be able to restore some of my strength.",
    ["Dialogue3031101"]="(Issoso gulps down the Monster Hearts like he hasn't eaten anything for a long time.)\n...Ah! I haven't felt like this for a long time! Finally, fresh strength is entering my body. Let me send you on a journey through time before my strength dissipates!",
    ["Dialogue3031201"]="The long river of history flows endlessly. Are you ready to board this boat?",
    ["Dialogue3031202"]="In that case, let me guide you in the right direction.",
    ["Dialogue3031203"]="I can wait, but not for long.",
    ["Dialogue3031301"]="(Eassis looks around her and seems a little surprised.)\nThis is... this is outside the capital! But why do I sense a peculiar aura of monsters ahead of us? Let's take a look!",
    ["Dialogue3031401"]="(Anubis looks at you majestically.)\nHumans... Did you kill this Phreeoni? Have you lost the reverence that all living beings must have? How dare you kill a monster of the underworld without authorization?",
    ["Dialogue3031402"]="Like me, the Phreeoni originate from another world. They are messengers I sent here to harvest lives. The souls they devour are sent directly to the underworld through their mouths. Your actions are an affront to the underworld. Do you not fear punishment?",
    ["Dialogue3031403"]="(Osiris' eyes shine brightly, without a hint of fear.)\nThis Phreeoni hurt my people; it deserved its punishment. No matter who they are or where they are from, anyone who dares invade my territory is my enemy!",
    ["Dialogue3031404"]="(Eassis looks at Osiris with reverence.)\nLord Osiris...",
    ["Dialogue3031405"]="(Anubis raises his chin and looks arrogantly at Osiris.)\n...Human, do you know the price of saying those words? It is enough for me to take your life. However, what interests me more is the kingly aura that radiates from you right now.",
    ["Dialogue3031406"]="It makes me want to see what miracles you can create if you are allowed to live on. I, Anubis, god of the underworld, hereby make a prediction:\nYour tribe will grow into a mighty empire and you will eventually become the pharaoh of Egypt.",
    ["Dialogue3031501"]="Ahem... Sorry, I had to bring you back to reality. My power has been exhausted. But please enjoy the mural while I take a break.",
    ["Dialogue3031601"]="(Eassis stares quietly at the mural, her eyes clearer than before.)\nI remember now. Lord Osiris did indeed have a fierce battle with a Phreeoni. This battle won him the respect of all the desert tribes, and no one dared doubt the strength of the young chief from then on.",
    ["Dialogue3031602"]="But these scenes from my memory are still fragmented; I can't put them together properly. I need more information about the past. Hurry, let's take a look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next mural</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3031701"]="(Rossoso covers his ears and looks very irritable.)\nGet out of here, you raucous demons! Oh, if it isn't a human. Whoever you are, help me teach those annoying <color=#CA2E0AFF>Side Winders</color> a lesson! Otherwise I won't be able to get a moment's peace. Argh! They're so noisy!",
    ["Dialogue3031801"]="(Rossoso frowns and looks around.)\nFinally, some peace and quiet. Tell me, why have you come here?",
    ["Dialogue3031802"]="...Hey! I'm a guardian spirit, not a tour guide! I guess I can help you, but you'll have to come back regularly to get rid of those annoying monsters for me in the future!",
    ["Dialogue3031901"]="So, are you ready to enter the mural yet?",
    ["Dialogue3031902"]="Oh, let's go then!",
    ["Dialogue3031903"]="Argh! You're so annoying!",
    ["Dialogue3032001"]="(Eassis looks around her and her eyes instantly well up.)\nOh, this is... this is the capital of Egypt where I lived with Lord Osiris! Yes, I remember the smell of the earth and the appearance of the palm trees. I lived in this city until I died. Every plant and tree here is worth remembering!",
    ["Dialogue3032002"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>palace</color>... The home I shared with Lord Osiris should be located at <color=#CA2E0AFF>the center of the city</color>. It must look exactly the same as in the past. I must go and see it!",
    ["Dialogue3032101"]="(Rossoso shakes his leg impatiently.)\nThat's it. I can only take you back that far. If you don't need me for anything else, go away and stop disturbing me!",
    ["Dialogue3032201"]="(Eassis lowers her eyes with a very complicated expression on her face.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3032202"]="Sorry, I'm just a little afraid to carry on watching. The past isn't only filled with happy events. I have a vague feeling that the following part of history will be full of sadness. I don't believe I will be able stay a calm onlooker when I face these painful memories. Maybe seeking answers from history is not wise.",
    ["Dialogue3032203"]="...You're right, every part of this history was something I experienced when I was still alive, so I shouldn't try to run from it. In that case, please come and stand <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of the last mural</color> with me. No matter what is recorded within it, I will be brave as I bear witness to everything!",
    ["Dialogue3032301"]="...Hey, it costs one bag of gold coins to take one look at the mural and twice that for two looks! Do you know how many times you looked at it just then? Hurry up and search the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jars</color> around here for all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>money</color> you owe me!",
    ["Dialogue3032401"]="(Lassoso's eyes light up when he sees the money.)\n...Hehe, that's more like it!",
    ["Dialogue3032402"]="Hmm? You want to know what a guardian spirit needs money for? It's for counting, of course! How can humans, who are so superficial that they only know how to spend money, possibly understand the joys of counting money?!",
    ["Dialogue3032403"]="By the way, why have you come here? I'll tell you now that this mural is an important piece of property of the Egyptian empire and no one is allowed to do anything to it!",
    ["Dialogue3032404"]="What? There's such a valuable relic right in front of you, yet all you want to do is find out the historical events recorded in it? Fine, I can send you in, but you only get one free trip. I'm charging you if you want a second one!",
    ["Dialogue3032501"]="I advise you to enter the mural as soon as possible. I've already started to calculate how much I should charge you for the time you're wasting. You'd better get ready before I work out exactly how much!",
    ["Dialogue3032502"]="You're not that dumb after all. I'm going to start casting the spell now.",
    ["Dialogue3032503"]="Okay, one gold per one minute. No discounts.",
    ["Dialogue3032601"]="(Eassis stares straight ahead.)\nThe man in front of us... It's Lord Osiris! Something seems to be wrong with him. What happened?",
    ["Dialogue3032701"]="(Osiris' head is lowered, and he keeps repeating the same thing hoarsely.)\nRevenge... I must get revenge...",
    ["Dialogue3032702"]="(Osiris clenches his fists and looks at you with bloodshot eyes.)\n...My empire was attacked by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>demon king Morroc</color>. My people were ravaged by the flames of war. My wife, Eassis... She died to protect me! Whereas I, Osiris, couldn't do anything other than watch as all this took place.",
    ["Dialogue3032703"]="(Eassis stands rooted to the spot as tears roll down her cheeks.)\n...Lord Osiris...",
    ["Dialogue3032704"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soul Obelisk</color> before us contains the power of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anubis, the god of the underworld</color>. I must <color=#CA2E0AFF>challenge Anubis' Phantom</color> and obtain this power. Only then will I be able to protect my territory and avenge my lost wife. I will make Morroc pay for all the blood shed by the people of the desert!",
    ["Dialogue3032801"]="Morroc, today is the day you die. I will cut off your head and offer it as a sacrifice to my empire!\n(After speaking, Osiris rushes out of the pyramid without any hesitation.)",
    ["Dialogue3032802"]="...No! Lord Osiris, don't go! Actually...",
    ["Dialogue3032803"]="That's enough. The next part isn't something that people of the present can get involved in.",
    ["Dialogue3032901"]="(Lassoso yawns lazily.)\n...Ahh! Why did you come back so soon? I thought you wanted to immerse yourself in the tragic and majestic history of Egypt and experience everything.",
    ["Dialogue3032902"]="I brought them back.",
    ["Dialogue3032903"]="(Lassoso jumps up in shock.)\n<size=24>…Ah!</size> <size=24>You're!</size><size=24>A-a-a…</size>",
    ["Dialogue3032904"]="Human, please come to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>center of the pyramid</color>. I have something important to say to you.",
    ["Dialogue3033001"]="Very good. We will talk here.\n(Anubis turns to face Eassis majestically.)",
    ["Dialogue3033002"]="Wife of the pharaoh, I noticed that you just tried to prevent the battle between Osiris and Morroc. The reason I destroyed the illusion and stopped you is because no one can change the course of history.",
    ["Dialogue3033003"]="Although you know that Osiris would die in battle and that his sacrifice could not prevent the demise of the ancient Egyptian empire, he was destined to experience those events, just as he was also destined to become the new king of the underworld after his death.",
    ["Dialogue3033004"]="Wife of the pharaoh, I must offer you a reminder. Have you lost yourself in your obsession with the past? Have you forgotten your original intention?",
    ["Dialogue3033005"]="(Eassis freezes momentarily before lowering her eyes ashamedly.)\n...I entered the murals to help me remember the past so that I could find a way to appease the soul of Lord Osiris.",
    ["Dialogue3033006"]="Very good. Well, the answer you sought is now in front of you. I can <color=#CA2E0AFF>appease the soul of Osiris</color>. However, first I will need you to collect the items required to cast the spell.",
    ["Dialogue3033007"]="I need you to get me enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>weapons</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archer Skeletons</color>. These weapons house the heroic spirits of former soldiers. Only they can awaken Osiris' consciousness.",
    ["Dialogue3033101"]="Osiris, destiny arranged for your path to intersect many times with mine. I predicted your coronation as a king, and you sought to obtain strength from me to take revenge. Now I will rescue your soul from the chaos and give you all my remaining power as the god of the underworld.",
    ["Dialogue3033102"]="Lord Anubis, why...?",
    ["Dialogue3033103"]="Our meeting was predestined. You are fated to become <color=#CA2E0AFF>the next god of the underworld</color>! When the monsters sealed under Morroc reawaken, it is time for you to take your rightful place.",
    ["Dialogue3033104"]="(Anubis looks down at Osiris solemnly.)\nOsiris... You were never an ordinary person. Despite your ill-fated destiny, the past will make you a great king. Now, answer me: Are you ready to undertake heavier responsibilities and continue forward even if it means losing more in the future?",
    ["Dialogue3033105"]="(Osiris pauses for a moment and then looks directly at Anubis with more determination than before.)\nWithout question.",
    ["Dialogue3033201"]="(The young man collapses to the ground and his lips are chapped from thirst. He looks like he's at death's door.)\nWater...",
    ["Dialogue3033202"]="Oh no! He's dying of thirst! We must help him! Adventurer, I vaguely remember that there's an oasis not far from here. Please bring some <color=#CA2E0AFF>water</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3033301"]="(The man opens his eyes slowly, and his expression changes when he sees Eassis and her clear concern for him.)",
    ["Dialogue3040101"]="(Phillas buries his face in his hands, his body trembling the whole time.)\n<size=18>Oh, Rosie... Rosie! What must I do to make you forgive me? Who will help me? Who?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3040102"]="(Phillas raises his head slowly, and you see a strange murkiness in his eyes.)\nHaha, someone's finally responded to my request. I made a big mistake and Rosie refuses to forgive me. Surely you'll help me beg her for forgiveness, right?",
    ["Dialogue3040103"]="Thank Odin! I had a feeling you would help me! Shush—listen, Rosie is pressuring me again. Go to the desert and search for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Vein Vanilla</color>. You'll be able to see Rosie if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>set it on fire in the ruins</color>!\n<size=18>Sigh, this is all my fault... This is all my fault...</size>",
    ["Dialogue3040201"]="(Rosie wipes the sweat from her head with the back of her hand.)\nGeez, it took me three whole days to excavate these ruins! How precious must the things here be for them to be hidden so well?",
    ["Dialogue3040202"]="<size=24>Uwah! You frightened me!</size>\nHold on... Were there any other people here before? Who are you? Don't tell me... Y-you're an ancient spirit of these ruins!",
    ["Dialogue3040203"]="...Huh? So, a person called Phillas asked you to come here to ask for my forgiveness? What's up with that? Did he do something bad to me?\n(Rosie frowns for a moment as she wonders about it, but waves her hands impatiently soon after.)\nUh, whatever, now's not the time to dwell on this. I finally found this <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient clay tablet</color>. I have to figure out what's recorded on it as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue3040301"]="(Rosie gently wipes the dust off the clay tablet.)\nHmm... These are hieroglyphs of the ancient Egyptian empire. This means the translation should be...\n<size=24>Aha!</size> <size=24>I knew I'd unearthed treasure!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3040302"]="Yeah, and you're a really lucky person! Not everyone has the good fortune to see a rare cultural relic like this with their own eyes. Since fate has brought us together today, I'll read out the translation to you—\n(Rosie clears her throat and points confidently at the slanted characters on the clay tablet.)",
    ["Dialogue3040303"]="\"Here lies a seal placed personally by the pharaoh himself. Unless one sacrifices a Muka's remains to it, the spell cannot be broken to release the monster sealed within.\"\n(Rosie frowns slightly.)",
    ["Dialogue3040304"]="Hmm, the second half of the text is rather worn. Based on the words, \"monster,\" \"kind,\" \"careful,\" and \"submit\" that I can make out, I think it should be saying that the \"monster\" is \"kind\" and it will \"submit\" to humans as long as you are \"careful\" when dealing with it!",
    ["Dialogue3040305"]="Yes, that must be it! The thing sealed in these ruins isn't evil; perhaps it's an important monster that can offer us clues to ancient secrets.\n(Rosie's face flushes red with excitement.)\nIn short, we must find a way to break the pharaoh's seal! I'm going to leave it to you to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Muka remains</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3040401"]="Hmm...\n(Rosie is dumbfounded for a few seconds, but laughs out loud soon after.)\nHaha! Could this Antsy be the monster that the pharaoh personally sealed away? I have no idea why he would do that, but a problem this small can't stop me!",
    ["Dialogue3040501"]="(The Antsy is curled up in a corner and hangs its head weakly.)\nJiji... Jiji...",
    ["Dialogue3040502"]="Aww, if you take a closer look, this Antsy is such a cute little guy! Antsy, although I don't understand what you're saying, I guess you must be starving after being sealed away for so long?",
    ["Dialogue3040503"]="(The Antsy blinks with teary eyes and rubs its head back and forth along Rosie's ankle.)\nJi... Jijiji...",
    ["Dialogue3040504"]="Aww, I must be right! I wonder what ants like to eat? According to the notes of one archaeologist, some insect monsters eat the corpses of other insects.",
    ["Dialogue3040505"]="(The Antsy is so excited that it walks around in circles, scratching Rosie's leg the whole time.)\nJi... Jiji... Ji...!",
    ["Dialogue3040506"]="Haha, so I guessed right again?! Adventurer, I'm going to have to trouble you to get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragrant Grasshopper Legs</color> while I stay here to keep the Antsy company. I can't bear to leave the little fella alone!",
    ["Dialogue3040601"]="Great! The Antsy seems to love these Grasshopper legs! By the way, it's growing incredibly fast. Every time I look at it, it seems bigger than last time. Hmm, I think we need even more food for it. Which type of monster corpse should we search for next?",
    ["Dialogue3040602"]="...Hey, where are you going?\n(Rosie shouts and chases the Antsy before she can greet you.)",
    ["Dialogue3040701"]="(Rosie clasps her hands together in front of her chest and looks surprised and frightened.)\n<size=18>...Wh-why is this happening? Why is it getting more aggressive</size> <size=18>as it grows?</size>",
    ["Dialogue3040702"]="<size=18>...What went wrong? </size><size=18>Why have I been getting the feeling that... </size><size=18>that it's getting more and more terrifying? </size><size=18>Calm down, Rosie</size>. <size=18>Remember what it said on the clay tablet. </size><size=18>It said the monster is kind, </size><size=18>so it can't possibly...</size>\n(Rosie gasps.)",
    ["Dialogue3040703"]="<size=18>Hold on... </size> <size=18>What if that wasn't what the worn-out characters meant? </size><size=18>What if it was a warning for future visitors not to break the seal? </size><size=18>For example... </size><size=18>What if it meant: This \"monster\" is not \"kind,\" </size><size=18>so be \"careful\" </size><size=18>and don't be fooled as it will temporarily \"submit\" to you?</size>\n(Rosie's pupils dilate with panic.)",
    ["Dialogue3040704"]="...Oh no! This was a mistake from the very beginning! Quickly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take Phillas to the ruins</color>! There's no time to waste!",
    ["Dialogue3040801"]="(Phillas' arms are folded like he is holding a baby. His eyes are bloodshot, but the corners of his mouth are raised strangely.)\n<size=18>Haha, how could this be a monster? It's obviously a harmless baby. </size><size=18>That's right, it's a little baby that belongs to me alone.</size>",
    ["Dialogue3040802"]="...Rosie?\n(Phillas raises his head blankly.)\nWho is Rosie? The ancient ruins you just mentioned... Where is that?",
    ["Dialogue3040803"]="Haha, stop talking nonsense. Come over and take a look at my dear little baby. Did you know that it was born in some <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient Egyptian ruins</color> and that I raised it myself?\n(Phillas' smile freezes suddenly.)",
    ["Dialogue3040804"]="Hold on, the ruins you just mentioned... Could they be the ruins of the ancient Egyptian pharaoh? No, you must never go there. The most terrifying thing in the world is sealed within. Everything will be destroyed!",
    ["Dialogue3040805"]="(Phillas scratches his cheeks in pain.)\n...Ah! Yes, it's... <size=24>it's coming!</size>\nI must get to the ruins before it's too late. It cannot be allowed to be here. I won't let it be born into this world!",
    ["Dialogue3040901"]="(Bowya grabs your shoulder firmly with a worried look on her face.)\n...Phew! You're finally awake.",
    ["Dialogue3040902"]="I'm Bowya, an instructor with the Eden Group. I don't know how long you would have been trapped in that <color=#CA2E0AFF>hallucination</color> if I hadn't shown up when I did! Phillas asked you to set fire to the Spirit Vein Vanilla, right? Geez, when will that guy return to normal?",
    ["Dialogue3040903"]="It was an ingredient used to create dream potions in ancient Egypt. Its fragrance has a hallucinogenic effect. If a person receives a suggestion and then smells the smoke it gives off when burned, they'll hallucinate about things they yearn for but do not belong to this world. Sigh, since Phillas put you up to this, I assume you met a girl called Rosie in the hallucination? It you're willing to trust me, tell me everything you saw in the hallucination!",
    ["Dialogue3040904"]="(Bowya sighs deeply.)\n...Just as I expected. What you saw was both true and false! Let me know if you want to know more about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phillas' story</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3041001"]="I need to tell this story from the very beginning. A long time ago, Phillas and Rosie were partners in the Eden Group. They worked hard to break the pharaoh's seal in the ancient Egyptian ruins, and managed to release the Antsy you saw in the hallucination.",
    ["Dialogue3041002"]="They both loved that Antsy very much at first, but their opinions diverged over time as they raised it. Rosie discovered the brutal nature of the monster hidden behind its harmless appearance and soon grew suspicious, becoming wary of the creature. Phillas was the exact opposite. His feelings for the monster grew warmer over time; he even treated it like a harmless child and refused to admit that it was a monster.",
    ["Dialogue3041003"]="The most frightening thing was that the monster seemed to have the ability to read people's minds. It noticed the changes in the attitudes of the two people raising it, and it deliberately distanced itself from Rosie while getting closer to Phillas. On one hand, it would act cute in front of Phillas, but on the other hand, it would secretly do things to hurt Rosie. This continued until the day it suddenly disappeared.",
    ["Dialogue3041004"]="(Bowya stops suddenly and her expression changes drastically.)\n...Hey, where did Phillas go? Did he run back into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> again? Geez, we have to bring him back!",
    ["Dialogue3041101"]="It seems that Phillas has fallen into one of his hallucinations again. Acting rashly might be counterproductive. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>observe</color> what he wants to do first.",
    ["Dialogue3041201"]="(Phillas stares vacantly at the edge of the cliff.)\n<size=18>...Rosie... I'm here, Rosie...</size>",
    ["Dialogue3041202"]="...Oh, it's you! Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>burn another piece of Spirit Vein Vanilla</color>. I can feel that Rosie is in this cave!",
    ["Dialogue3041203"]="(Phillas looks sad.)\nOh... Please, I'm begging you! This is extremely important to me. I can no longer choose to run away from this!",
    ["Dialogue3041301"]="(Phillas wraps his arms around his body and shivers like a helpless child.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3041302"]="...I think you probably saw the ending of the previous story in this hallucination. Yes, the ant monster eventually escaped to the edge of the cliff, where it cruelly devoured the pursuing Rosie and merged its body with hers.",
    ["Dialogue3041303"]="When Phillas broke free of the ant's bewitchment, the \"Rosie\" before him was a creature with an ant's abdomen and six legs. Her one familiar soul was nowhere to be found within the insect's body. And lingering in his ears was the monster's smug, sinister laughter.",
    ["Dialogue3041304"]="That drove Phillas mad. He couldn't forgive the monster's actions, nor could he forgive himself for being bewitched by the monster and causing the death of his companion. Since that day, Phillas spends every day wandering the Ant Cavern and begging people to burn Spirit Vein Vanilla, reliving that painful experience over and over again.",
    ["Dialogue3041305"]="(Bowya shakes her head in frustration.)\nSigh, maybe this is how Phillas thinks he can atone for his sins! Rosie never said she wouldn't forgive him. He was the one who wouldn't forgive himself all along. All we can do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>get Phillas safely back to the surface</color>. This cavern is very dangerous. We can't leave him here alone.",
    ["Dialogue3041401"]="Okay! It looks safe enough here! Thanks for helping us. I'll take care of Phillas from here on.",
    ["Dialogue3041402"]="(Bowya seems to suddenly remember something and taps your shoulder firmly.)\nOh right, if you see that half-ant, half-woman monster in the Ant Cavern one day, please remember what happened to Phillas. That creature is not at all kind. You must not show it any mercy!",
    ["Dialogue3041403"]="(Phillas buries his face in his hands, his body trembling the whole time.)\n<size=18>Oh, Rosie... Rosie, what must I do to make you forgive me? Who will help me? Who?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3050101"]="(Leona sighs in distress.)\n...Adventurer, can you help me, please?",
    ["Dialogue3050102"]="Lord Nield has been depressed ever since the death of Princess Lucia. He wanders around the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coral Garden</color> every day and is reluctant to leave—even his face has become haggard. I've heard that human beings have the most delicate and rich emotions and are good at solving problems of the heart. Can you think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help Lord Nield overcome his grief</color> and cheer up?",
    ["Dialogue3050201"]="(Nield looks sadly at the garden in front of him.)\nLucia... My daughter...",
    ["Dialogue3050202"]="Lucia loved this garden when she was still alive. She went to great lengths to develop these flowers called Kiss of the Sea, but they have now lost their vitality. Sigh, perhaps even flowers and plants have a soul and miss their master too? Now that Lucia is gone, maybe this garden will also gradually fall into decline, just like the gods.",
    ["Dialogue3050203"]="Could it be that you are trying to make these Kisses of the Sea bloom again? I remember these flowers are very delicate and Lucia nurtured them with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bradium</color> obtained from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3050301"]="(Nield looks at the Bradium in your hand in surprise.)\nThis Bradium... Did you find it?",
    ["Dialogue3050302"]="...I see, in that case, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle the Bradium throughout the garden</color>! If a miracle really does happen—if Lucia's spirit in the afterlife is willing to console her father... Then please <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick some blooming Kisses of the Sea</color> for me as a memento.",
    ["Dialogue3050401"]="(Nield hugs the Kisses of the Sea emotionally, and his eyes finally regain their luster.)\nThank you for letting me see these beautiful flowers again! I'll think of my daughter whenever I look at them.",
    ["Dialogue3050402"]="However, I wasn't the only one to suffer misfortune from the underwater chaos. Many of the sea's inhabitants are frightened and in greater need of help and reassurance than me. Sadly, given the powers currently at my disposal, I'm afraid...\n(Nield frowns almost imperceptibly.)",
    ["Dialogue3050403"]="...No, it's nothing. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>convey my regards to the people</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>help them out where you can</color>! I noticed that you are not only brave, but also possess the noblest moral character. I'm most assured leaving this matter in your hands.",
    ["Dialogue3050501"]="(Simon hums a song leisurely.)\n...Sideways, sideways, let's see who swims the fastest under the sea ♪",
    ["Dialogue3050502"]="(Simon looks at you blankly.)\nA crisis? What crisis? Bloop! Are you talking about the chaos at the Underwater Temple? I have used my brilliant mind to figure out the reason! That alchemist must be behind it.",
    ["Dialogue3050503"]="If he hadn't made the fake sparkling wine, the inhabitants of the sea wouldn't have gone crazy after they got sore tummies from drinking it! You must be careful in the future. Fake wine is dangerous! Fake wine is dangerous, bloop!",
    ["Dialogue3050504"]="At least everything is over now, bloop! However, we still need to pay more attention to the current crisis.\n(You hear a rumbling noise that continues for a while.)\nLook, my stomach has declared a crisis of its own, bloop! Please hunt the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen</color> and get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>fresh meat</color> so that I can have a good meal, bloop!",
    ["Dialogue3050601"]="Ka! Kaka! Sure enough, good food never lets anyone down, bloop! Speaking of which, did Princess Lucia find her father? She had such a worried expression on her face that time, and it really made me wonder if something serious had happened to Lord Nield.",
    ["Dialogue3050602"]="Bloop! What a relief! Anyway, it's time to start preparing for my next meal.\n(Simon hums as he walks off.)\nEight legs, two pincers... Big fish, little fish, out of my way ♪",
    ["Dialogue3050701"]="(Brady is really excited to see you.)\nBloop! It's you! I've never forgotten your kindness. You saved poor Marko's father from sadness and despair! Come here, son, what do I usually teach you? At times like these, you should—",
    ["Dialogue3050702"]="(Little Baxter flaps his fins to swim in front of you and spits out a heart-shaped bubble.)\nBloop! Me and Dad love you!",
    ["Dialogue3050703"]="Oh, Master Strouf is simply too considerate, bloop! Indeed, although it seems like calm has returned to the undersea world, not everyone has been able to resume their previous lives so easily. For example, when Little Baxter and I were planning to move back to our home a while ago, we found that a group of nasty Marine Spheres had occupied it, bloop!",
    ["Dialogue3050704"]="Those mean rascals... I couldn't force them to leave even when I used the moves of the legendary martial arts master Jackie Fish! It seems I must wait for a hero who surpasses all the legends to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get rid of those nasty Marine Spheres</color>, bloop!\n(Brady's eyes sparkle with excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue3050801"]="Bloop! You were so cool just now! You did a zip and a zap and boom! Those Marine Spheres went flying! Please express my heartfelt gratitude to Lord Nield.\n(Brady's expression instantly dims as he suddenly remembers something.)",
    ["Dialogue3050802"]="...Lord Nield must be in a terrible mood? I've heard about what happened to Princess Lucia. It really saddens me. As a father, I understand Lord Nield's feelings very well. If I lost Little Baxter, I... Bloop! I can't bear to think about it! I really hope Lord Nield can cheer up soon, bloop!",
    ["Dialogue3050901"]="(Leona prays devoutly.)\nMay the waves soothe the wounds of our hearts and bring peace to the Underwater Temple.",
    ["Dialogue3050902"]="Thank you for thinking of me, but as a high priestess of the Underwater Temple, I don't have time to be sad. Although you took the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, its impact has not been fully negated. Until order has been restored to the underwater world, I must guide the inhabitants of the sea with my wisdom and lead them forward.",
    ["Dialogue3050903"]="Some inhabitants of the sea who mutated due to the power of the fragment have recovered their minds, but some fish... some fish will never be the same. For example, no matter how hard I or the other priests try, we'll never be able to suppress the Swordfish's aggression. If we continue to do nothing, a new crisis will befall the underwater world.",
    ["Dialogue3050904"]="(Leona bites her lip hard and pauses for a long time before speaking again.)\n...Adventurer, if you want to help us, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>eliminate the Swordfish</color> for me.",
    ["Dialogue3051001"]="...It seems that the matter has been settled. Speaking of which, how is Lord Nield now? Did he calm down after you spoke to him?",
    ["Dialogue3051002"]="You say Lord Nield looks a little weak? Instead of taking action himself, he entrusted you to help the inhabitants of the sea?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...Could it be? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Is he...?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3051003"]="...Adventurer, can you help me with one final request? If you manage to obtain a dish called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Snake</color>, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take it to Lord Nield</color>. It was his favorite dish as well as Princess Lucia's signature dish.",
    ["Dialogue3051101"]="(A mixture of joy and sorrow can be seen in Nield's eyes.)\nLucia used to always make Fresh Snake for me.",
    ["Dialogue3051102"]="Ah, I will remember your words. I feel so relieved now that I see everyone settling down again. Adventurer, see this <color=#CA2E0AFF>trident</color> in my hands. This holy relic was bestowed unto me by Odin. It symbolizes the strongest power and supreme authority under the sea. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take it to High Priestess Leona</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3051103"]="(Nield looks at you with a calm and firm gaze.)\nShe'll understand my intentions.",
    ["Dialogue3051201"]="(Leona steps back with a look of disbelief on her face.)\n...Lord Nield! How could you?",
    ["Dialogue3051202"]="(Leona closes her eyes in anguish.)\nPlease place the trident <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of the monument</color>. It will reveal the final answer.",
    ["Dialogue3051301"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, since you have appeared once more and brought this trident here, I presume the \"last days\" are upon us.",
    ["Dialogue3051302"]="There are things that I can't tell you in person, which is why this illusion exists. In the war between the gods and demons thousands of years ago, Ymir's Heart and Yggdrasil, which housed it, were destroyed by the demon Baphomet. This resulted in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the fall of Asgard</color>, the realm of the gods, and the exhaustion of the gods' source of power ushered in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ragnarok</color>—the twilight of the gods.",
    ["Dialogue3051303"]="The gods have grown weaker and weaker ever since, and even I cannot escape this fate. My divine power is exhausted, and I will soon fall into a long, deep slumber. Before that happens, I have something to say to the two humans I trust the most—",
    ["Dialogue3051304"]="(Nield's phantom turns to Leona.)\nHigh Priestess Leona, although a disaster has just subsided, this may just be the beginning of difficult and dangerous times. Please take care of all the creatures of the sea for me.",
    ["Dialogue3051305"]="(Leona nods sadly.)\nI will not fail you.",
    ["Dialogue3051306"]="(Nield's phantom turns to you.)\nSuccessor of Odin's bloodline, I must thank you for everything you've done for those under the sea. Although it is time to bid you farewell, my heart is full of hope, for I firmly believe that you will eventually <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather all the fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>. Perhaps I will reawaken at that time and we may yet meet again.",
    ["Dialogue3051307"]="From now on, the future is in your hands.\n(Nield's phantom gradually dissipates.)",
    ["Dialogue3051401"]="(Leona still looks a little vacant.)\nI never expected things to happen so quickly.",
    ["Dialogue3051402"]="Don't worry. Although Princess Lucia has passed away and Lord Nield has fallen into a deep slumber...\n(Leona raises her head with a determined expression on her face.)\nFor as long as the Underwater Temple needs me, I will protect this place with the Obeaune, regardless of how difficult it may be or how long it might take.",
    ["Dialogue3051501"]="Adventurer, it's up to you now, bloop! Please eliminate these <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mad Marine Spheres</color> with a bang!",
    ["Dialogue3060001"]="The Demon in the Temple with <color=#7FFFAA>Wind Attribute Shield</color> appears. Summon Inosuke Hashibira to break the shield",
    ["Dialogue3060002"]="The Demon in the Temple with <color=#4169E1>Water Attribute Shield</color> appears. Summon Zenitsu Agatsuma to break the shield",
    ["Dialogue3060003"]="The Demon in the Temple with <color=#FA8072>Fire Attribute Shield</color> appears. Summon Tanjiro Kamado to break the shield",
    ["Dialogue3060004"]="The Demon in the Temple with <color=#D2691E>Earth Attribute Shield</color> appears. Summon Hinokami Tanjiro Kamado to break the shield",
    ["Dialogue3060101"]="(John looks crestfallen.)\n<size=18>This is terrible.</size> <size=18>What will I do?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3060102"]="Why am I so unlucky? First getting shipwrecked, then losing young Gail Wigner! You finally managed to find Gail, but he found true love and decided to elope with her? Argh! How can I possibly tell the Wigner Family? Adventurer, you must help me find a solution!",
    ["Dialogue3060103"]="Ah, it might be a good idea to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Macheda Alson</color> for help! I remember that he's old friends with Ruvier, the head of the Wigner Family. Maybe he can think of a suitable solution. Since you've already helped me, can you see things through to the end and take a message to Mr. Alson for me? I think you should be able to find him near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>harbor in Alberta</color>. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue3060201"]="(Alson sighs emotionally after hearing about Gail.)\nSigh, as expected from a member of the Wigner Family. The blood of \"freedom\" flows through their veins! Gail isn't the first and certainly won't be the last member of the Wigner Family to do something like this. Their family history is full of partings caused by their pursuit of freedom.",
    ["Dialogue3060202"]="Hmph, that family! Have you heard of the legend of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wind Chaser</color> in Alberta? The title belongs to a young woman who loved the sea more than anything else in this world, and even gave up her status as a noble for it. Decades ago, she cast off the shackles of being the family heiress and sailed out to sea one night on her beloved ship. She never returned home after that. Her name was <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colorful Wigner</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3060203"]="Colorful is the older sister of Ruvier, the current head of the Wigner Family. As you can imagine, Gail's actions are nothing compared to hers, which is why it wasn't hard for Ruvier to accept that Gail left without saying goodbye.",
    ["Dialogue3060204"]="Adventurer, a flower called Colorful grows everywhere in Alberta's harbor. They've always been precious to Ruvier. You can pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colorful flowers</color> and take them with you when you see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ruvier</color>. I'm sure they will help him understand Gail's decision.",
    ["Dialogue3060301"]="(Ruvier stares silently at the Colorful flowers, seemingly lost in his memories.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3060302"]="(Ruvier shakes his head sadly.)\nSo Gail too... Since he made this decision himself, I will choose to respect it. Please tell my old friend <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson</color> that I will not blame any member of the fleet for this. He can tell those sailors who have gone elsewhere to come back.",
    ["Dialogue3060401"]="Adventurer, you're back. Does that look on your face mean this matter has been successfully resolved?\n(Alson sighs suddenly.)",
    ["Dialogue3060402"]="Sigh, let me tell you what happened. Do you remember the fog incident at sea not long ago? After you eliminated the Corsair, the fog dissipated and the Alson Fleet resumed its normal operations. Strangely, just one day ago, one of the ships disappeared! The most peculiar thing is that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Albert</color>, one of the sailors on the ship, has appeared completely unscathed in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>harbor</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3060403"]="Trying to establish what happened has proved difficult. It seems that Albert is so terrified that he can barely talk. We need to calm him down before we can figure out the truth... but how?",
    ["Dialogue3060404"]="Ah, I have heard of a dish called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fly Leg Folk Remedy</color>. It purportedly has the effect of stabilizing emotions and has helped many sailors overcome the shock of storms at sea! Why not take some to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Albert</color>? It should help him come back to his senses!",
    ["Dialogue3060501"]="Nom nom nom...\n(Albert gobbles down the Fly Leg Folk Remedy.)\nBurp! Ah, I feel much better now.",
    ["Dialogue3060502"]="(Albert's face becomes pale.)\nWhat I experienced at sea? ...It-it was a nightmare! Just last night...\n(His expression indicates that he is trying to remember what happened.)",
    ["Dialogue3060503"]="Last night, as we were making our way back to port, a huge ship appeared and headed straight for us. I saw it clearly in the moonlight—it was the rumored <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shipwreck</color>! We quickly changed course, but couldn't get away. When I recovered from the panic, I found myself on <color=#CA2E0AFF>another ship</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3060504"]="...I couldn't figure out what had happened! B-but what happened next was even more terrifying. I saw a face. It was the face of a dead man! I saw <color=#CA2E0AFF>First Mate Hobbe</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3060505"]="...Argh! I still can't fully believe it! Did I die? Why else would I see someone who's supposed to be dead? Is all this real, or is it an illusion after my death? Even the food I just ate... It should have tasted disgusting! But why did I find it so tasty? Or could it be that I'm still unconscious? Wait, can a dead person even be unconscious?",
    ["Dialogue3060506"]="You'll find out the truth for me? Th-thank you so much! Please, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>figure out what happened last night</color>, otherwise I'll go out of my mind!",
    ["Dialogue3060601"]="(Hobbe looks at you with surprise.)\nAdventurer, why are you here too?",
    ["Dialogue3060602"]="(Hobbe looks to his side.)\nI don't know what's happened recently. Living people have been appearing one after another. If I look closely, I see that they're all familiar faces! Look, <color=#CA2E0AFF>this sailor next to me</color> was an old friend of mine when I was in the Alson Fleet.",
    ["Dialogue3060701"]="(Rudolph frowns heavily.)\nWhat? Did you suddenly appear on this ship too?",
    ["Dialogue3060702"]="So... does this mean our ship sank? Fortunately, everyone was able to escape in time, but I was separated from my crewmates when I arrived on this ship. I'm the first mate, so I can't leave without confirming their whereabouts!",
    ["Dialogue3060703"]="Sigh... Everything was calm and peaceful last night, but all of a sudden, our <color=#CA2E0AFF>navigator, Colin</color>, issued a warning just before that terrifying giant ship appeared. I hastily instructed our <color=#CA2E0AFF>helmsman, Zavier</color>, to change direction, but he panicked and steered our ship <color=#CA2E0AFF>into a reef</color>. You know the rest.",
    ["Dialogue3060704"]="What happened after is a blur. All I know is that we were attacked by monsters after we arrived on this ship. By the time I managed to hide in this cabin, I realized that the others were no longer behind me. Damn, if I wasn't so exhausted, I would <color=#CA2E0AFF>search the ship for them</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3060801"]="(Colin breathes a sigh of relief.)\nPhew! You arrived just in time! I'm so exhausted. I can barely stand, let alone fight off monsters!",
    ["Dialogue3060802"]="Hmm... Before everything happened, I was on lookout duty in the crow's nest. Suddenly, I noticed a shipwreck, so I notified First Mate Rudolph as soon as I could. After a moment, I felt a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strong impact</color> and fell out of the crow's nest. I... I have no idea about what happened after that.",
    ["Dialogue3060803"]="Although I have the strangest feeling that the shipwreck didn't mean us any harm; it just encountered us by chance. But why did it appear? Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue3060804"]="Haha, I just knew that First Mate Rudolph wouldn't leave us behind! Thanks for telling me. I'll go meet up with him right now!",
    ["Dialogue3060901"]="Those monsters just wouldn't give up! I'd teach them a lesson if I wasn't so weak since falling into that <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange gap</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3060902"]="That's right. Before I fell into the sea, I noticed that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>air above the water was distorted</color> and a strange gap had opened up! I appeared on this ship after being sucked into it. Although I don't understand why it happened, I'm still alive because of it.",
    ["Dialogue3060903"]="Did you say First Mate Rudolph was looking for the lost sailors? I'd better not keep him waiting then!",
    ["Dialogue3061001"]="(Tim trembles with his hands pressed against his head.)\nPlease... H-hurry up and kill all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wandering Whispers</color> around here! I can't stand things like ghosts. Just the sound of them is enough to make me faint!",
    ["Dialogue3061101"]="By Odin, thank you for saving me! Why was I unlucky enough to be sent to such a terrifying place by that <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange gap</color>?\n(Tim shudders.)",
    ["Dialogue3061102"]="The reason I appeared on this ship is because I passed through a strange gap just above the water as I was falling into the sea! Oddly enough, I think I saw <color=#CA2E0AFF>the exact same gap</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>captain's cabin</color> when I was hiding from the monsters chasing after me. Say, do you think there's a connection between them?",
    ["Dialogue3061103"]="So, the first mate and the others are waiting for me in the prayer room? Thank goodness! I'm off to find them now!",
    ["Dialogue3061201"]="(Colorful looks surprised.)\n...That's strange, why are there living people on my ship?",
    ["Dialogue3061202"]="(Colorful puffs out her chest with pride.)\nThis shipwreck was originally a merchant ship called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unicorn</color> that belonged to the Wigner Family, and I, Colorful Wigner, am the captain of the Unicorn.",
    ["Dialogue3061203"]="...What? You've heard of me?",
    ["Dialogue3061204"]="(Colorful's expression changes from surprise to sadness, and she lowers her head silently.)\n<size=18>I didn't realize so much time had passed since then.</size>\nAdventurer, you've probably only heard part of my story. Would you be willing to find out what happened after that?",
    ["Dialogue3061205"]="It wasn't long after I left Alberta that I encountered the legendary monster, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kraken</color>. I died fighting it, but my soul fused with my beloved Unicorn. This death did not scare me. I could still sail the seas and realize my dream of exploring the world! However, those happy days didn't last long, as an uninvited guest took over my ship.",
    ["Dialogue3061206"]="Yes, the arrival of the Corsair made me and the Unicorn lose our freedom! Strangely, I suddenly regained control of the Unicorn a few days ago. I'm sure you can imagine how happy I was. I resumed my dream journey, but I almost collided with a merchant ship right after I set sail!",
    ["Dialogue3061207"]="Fortunately, I'm a highly trained captain! Just at the last moment, I turned hard and missed them, but they seemed to have hit a reef and sank anyway. The silver lining is that the sailors didn't fall into the sea! That's because I used the space-time power of the Unicorn to send them to a safe place connected to the temporal turbulence.",
    ["Dialogue3061208"]="So the sailors are safe? That's great news, except the Unicorn is in a little trouble. Do you see those <color=#CA2E0AFF>Disobedient Skel Pirates</color>? They keep making me misjudge the course, and I can't get rid of them because I don't have a body anymore. Can you help me out?",
    ["Dialogue3061301"]="Thanks a lot for helping me. The Unicorn feels much better now! I will now sail it to waters where no one ventures so that I don't intersect with the world of the living anymore.",
    ["Dialogue3061302"]="Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>apologize to the Alson Fleet</color> for me, and...\n(Colorful hesitates for a moment and makes a somewhat lonely expression.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Never mind. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>After everything that's happened, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>it would be best to just let my family carry on believing that I managed to obtain my freedom.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3061401"]="(Alson holds your hand with gratitude.)\nAdventurer, thank you for helping us yet again. Thanks to your efforts, these unfortunate sailors were able to return to Alberta safely. No matter what difficulties you encounter at sea in the future, remember that the Alson Fleet will always be your ally!",
    ["Dialogue3061402"]="(Alson's eyes widen in shock.)\n...You mean the shipwreck used to be the Unicorn?! And you met Colorful on board? By Odin, if Ruvier knew about this, I wonder if he'd be happy or sad?",
    ["Dialogue3061403"]="(Alson smiles sadly.)\nYou're right. Let everyone think that Wind Chaser is still sailing the high seas! Sure enough, the sea is the best place for her. I've always thought that the obsession with freedom and ideals is exactly what makes the Wigner Family so fascinating, don't you agree?",
    ["Dialogue3061404"]="(Alson nods sorrowfully.)\n...In that case, let me be the one to tell Ruvier. At least Colorful managed to realize the dream she had when she was still alive, right? Even death couldn't stop her yearning for freedom. Perhaps this is the ending she sought.",
    ["Dialogue3070101"]="(Fulkyn's head is lowered as he is deep in thought.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...The question now is how we can get them back. If I am unable to make contact with the people of this world, the number of feasible methods remaining will be equal to 3,924 minus 3,923...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3070102"]="...Oh it's you. We meet again.",
    ["Dialogue3070103"]="(Fulkyn takes out a pocket watch and looks at it.)\nOh? So, I'm currently in this dimension. In that case, please ignore what I just said. Memory loss is inevitable when one has been traveling between dimensions for a long time.",
    ["Dialogue3070104"]="But let's not talk about this for now. The most important thing at the moment is to resolve the current space-time crisis as soon as possible. As long as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color> are scattered everywhere, the impact they have will affect the order of parallel universes, and may even cause the destruction of other alternate timelines that are derived from the current true timeline.",
    ["Dialogue3070105"]="As I was saying, someone must help me retrieve the Sands of Time! They are magic particles that I use for time travel, and they can be extremely dangerous depending on how they are used and what they are used for. When I first landed at these coordinates, I <color=#CA2E0AFF>spilled some Sands of Time in the lands nearby</color>. I won't be able to stop worrying until you retrieve all the Sands of Time for me.",
    ["Dialogue3070106"]="...Oh? Would you like to spend several thousands of hours listening to my explanation? I certainly don't mind if you're willing, but if you don't want to hear it, please activate the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> beside me as soon as possible. It will guide you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>whereabouts of the Sands of Time</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3070201"]="(The young stranger is sweating profusely.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Geez... How could I lose something so important? She'll be here soon. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Wh-what should I say?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3070202"]="Oh! Jing—\n(The young man rubs the back of his head awkwardly when he sees your face.)\nAhem, er, I'm sorry. I thought you were <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jingyin</color>! It's a good thing it wasn't her, or else...",
    ["Dialogue3070203"]="...Sigh, I lost the <color=#CA2E0AFF>precious gift</color> I got for her! But I clearly remember that I was holding it when I came out today. How could it... Ah! Could I have dropped it on the way here? Can you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for it nearby</color>? It's a small gift, but it means a lot!",
    ["Dialogue3070301"]="(The young man happily takes the gift and looks at you with gratitude.)\nI'm so relieved! Thank you so much! Fortunately you found it for me, otherwise...",
    ["Dialogue3070302"]="...Liu, have you been waiting long?",
    ["Dialogue3070401"]="(The young man scratches the back of his head in bewilderment.)\nThey say \"give and you shall receive in turn\"... But this is not a \"thank you\"... It's just to show you how I feel...\nUm... Do you understand the meaning of the poem she recited at the end?",
    ["Dialogue3070402"]="(The young man looks at you in surprise.)\nSo... Does this mean that Jingyin won't accept my feelings for her? But she didn't look unhappy just then. Something doesn't feel right.",
    ["Dialogue3070403"]="(The young man's eyes sparkle with excitement.)\nSo you're saying that Jingyin...! She understands my feelings and is willing to be with me forever?! Ah! I, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Liu Wuye</color>, am so happy! This is the happiest moment of my life! Thank you for making my life-long wish come true!",
    ["Dialogue3070404"]="I'm sorry, I was so anxious that I forgot to introduce myself. My name is Liu Wuye. Well, I hope we meet again someday!\n(Liu Wuye smiles heartily before running off shouting Jingyin's name.)",
    ["Dialogue3070501"]="Excellent, thank you for bringing back the Sands of Time. Now...",
    ["Dialogue3070502"]="Time waits for no one. Please keep it short.",
    ["Dialogue3070503"]="Oh? Didn't I already introduce myself to you? ...Oh, right, I introduced myself to you in \"the future,\" and \"your future\" is \"my past.\" Simply put, I am a traveler, but unlike other travelers, I travel through time and space. The past and the future, and events that take place in the flow of time, are simply part of the scenery of my journey.",
    ["Dialogue3070504"]="(Fulkyn doesn't look surprised at all.)\nYes, the events that happened earlier weren't an illusion you created, but another effect of the Sands of Time. It subverts the restrictions of the fourth dimension and <color=#CA2E0AFF>moves people within a certain range to different time nodes at the same coordinates</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3070505"]="Simply put, the Sands of Time took you <color=#CA2E0AFF>through time and space</color> to meet Liu Wuye at a certain time in the past, which made it possible for you to witness the moment he and his lover, Jingyin, shared their feelings for one another. However, since you did not belong to that time, Demotima appeared to correct the error by removing you. Do you understand now?",
    ["Dialogue3070506"]="Don't try to use the Sands of Time to change anything that has happened in the past. It is taboo to engage in time travel for such a purpose. Trying to change the past is tantamount to simultaneously making two or more assumptions that cannot co-exist at the same time. This is a common feature of all paradox problems and this logical contradiction will be corrected by time.",
    ["Dialogue3070507"]="In other words, <color=#CA2E0AFF>no one can change the past</color>! This is the first and most important rule of the Code of Time Travel. If you intend to violate it, then both time and I will punish you.",
    ["Dialogue3070508"]="...Everyone is just a speck of dust in the torrent of time. Regardless of what happens, everything is destined. Since that's the case, isn't it better to focus on finding ways to solve your current problems? There are still many scattered <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color> waiting for you out there.",
    ["Dialogue3070601"]="(Liu Wuye's face is distorted with pain.)\nArgh... Why... why did things turn out this way?!",
    ["Dialogue3070602"]="(Liu Wuye clutches his hair in despair.)\n...Could it be because of that <color=#CA2E0AFF>man</color>? Is he responsible for <color=#CA2E0AFF>making you this terrifying</color>, Jingyin?",
    ["Dialogue3070603"]="...Yes, it must be him! I saw him <color=#CA2E0AFF>manipulate the Munak</color> with my own eyes. But I failed to protect you! Don't be afraid, Jingyin. I will find him... and I will kill him! I must return you to normal!",
    ["Dialogue3070604"]="(Liu Wuye looks up at you.)\n...You're willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>rescue Jingyin</color> with me? Good, let's go then. There's no time to lose!",
    ["Dialogue3070701"]="Excellent, thank you for bringing back the Sands of Time. Now...",
    ["Dialogue3070702"]="...Sigh, when will people finally understand how precious time is? Time waits for no one. Please keep it short.",
    ["Dialogue3070703"]="...Oh? So, the Sands of Time took you back in time again and showed you and Liu Wuye what happened when <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jingyin was transmogrified into the Moonlight Flower</color> this time? Hmm, that is truly a tragic story. Well, let's continue to search for the Sands of Time now.",
    ["Dialogue3070704"]="(Fulkyn's face instantly darkens.)\nI don't like repeating myself—<color=#CA2E0AFF>no one can change the past</color>! What I know for a fact is that the failure to resolve our current troubles will only make the future worse. So, let's focus on <color=#CA2E0AFF>finding the Sands of Time</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3070801"]="(Liu Wuye looks at you in surprise. His face is very haggard.)\nIt's you. I didn't expect us to meet again. Thank you for agreeing to find for Jingyin for me before. As for what happened to her in the end... The people of the Euin Family have told me everything.",
    ["Dialogue3070802"]="...Please don't blame yourself. You and the Euin Family just did what you needed to do. Compared to living like that... perhaps death was actually a form of relief to Jingyin. I came here to bury her <color=#CA2E0AFF>hairband</color> in this <color=#CA2E0AFF>maple forest</color>. This used to be her favorite place. It should be her soul's final resting place.",
    ["Dialogue3070803"]="You mean <color=#CA2E0AFF>glowing sand</color>? I think I did see it somewhere around here. It was over there.\n(Liu Wuye points at a spot <color=#CA2E0AFF>under a tree</color> beside him.)",
    ["Dialogue3070901"]="(Liu Wuye looks blankly at everything around him.)\n...Wh-what just happened? Did you feel the air around us twisting into a ball? What the...?",
    ["Dialogue3070902"]="(Liu Wuye frowns warily.)\n...Watch out! It's...?!",
    ["Dialogue3071001"]="(Eddga bows politely to you.)\nMy friends, I apologize if I frightened you. It's just that very few humans stay here, and I just wanted to speak with someone again. It's been so long.",
    ["Dialogue3071002"]="...People call me <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eddga</color>. I may look monstrous, but inside am <color=#CA2E0AFF>human being</color> just like any other? People fear what they see on the outside, but don't understand that not all monsters are evil, just as not all humans are good.",
    ["Dialogue3071003"]="Many years ago, I too lived a peaceful life with the woman I loved. However, a terrible <color=#CA2E0AFF>disaster</color> struck, causing me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>lose the love of my life</color>. Since then, I have committed many <color=#CA2E0AFF>wrongs</color> in an effort to regain everything I lost. But in the end, the only thing I have to show for it is this grotesque appearance. I guess this is the punishment I deserve.",
    ["Dialogue3071004"]="You want to know why I'm wandering around in this Maple Forest?\n(Eddga looks around affectionately.)\nBecause I can still feel her here. This is the only place where I can feel <color=#CA2E0AFF>my beloved</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3071005"]="(Liu Wuye sighs imperceptibly.)\nI understand what it feels like to lose someone you love.",
    ["Dialogue3071006"]="(Eddga only now looks directly at Liu Wuye.)\n<size=24>...Y-you're...</size>",
    ["Dialogue3071101"]="Adventurer, what was that just now? I've never seen that monster in Payon before. What's going on?!",
    ["Dialogue3071102"]="...So, you mean this glowing sand is used for time travel, and a person called Fulkyn is able to control it? Can he travel freely between the past and the future?!",
    ["Dialogue3071103"]="(Liu Wuye's eyes light up with excitement.)\nPlease... please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me to meet Fulkyn</color>! He might be the only person in this world who can help me!",
    ["Dialogue3071201"]="Very good! You've gathered all the missing Sands of Time. I can finally leave for the next part of my journey.",
    ["Dialogue3071202"]="Wait!",
    ["Dialogue3071203"]="...I must ensure that the word \"wait\" becomes forbidden in time travel. How can I teach people that time waits for no one? Fine, what is it now? Who are you?",
    ["Dialogue3071204"]="My name is Liu Wuye. Please take me with you when you travel through time! I must return to a time before everything happened. I must regain everything I lost!",
    ["Dialogue3071205"]="(Fulkyn falls silent for a moment before staring at Liu Wuye with a cold gaze.)\n...I sympathize with your situation, but I only have one answer to what you just said: Trying to change history is the greatest taboo in time travel. <color=#CA2E0AFF>No one can change the past</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3071206"]="There are rules for everything, and this breaks the rules of time. If anyone insists on breaking this rule... I will let them know just how cruel the sanctions of time can be.",
    ["Dialogue3071207"]="But...!",
    ["Dialogue3071208"]="Enough. It is almost time for me to go.\nThe future is too distant and the past has passed. The wisest decision you can make is to always cherish the present.",
    ["Dialogue3071301"]="(Liu Wuye stands in silence, his eyes obscured by the shadow of his cloak.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3071302"]="...Start a new life? But what's the point of having a future if life in the present has lost its meaning?",
    ["Dialogue3071303"]="(Liu Wuye falls silent for a moment, his eyes still fixed in the direction of Fulkyn.)\n...Indeed, it's pointless just thinking about it. I already know what I intend to do next.",
    ["Dialogue3071401"]="(The device makes beeping sounds and the probe turns to point to the southeast of Payon.)",
    ["Dialogue3071402"]="Is it near a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pond</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast of Payon</color>? Adventurer, you should know what to do next.",
    ["Dialogue3071501"]="(The device makes beeping sounds and the probe turns to point to the west of Payon.)",
    ["Dialogue3071502"]="Is it in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hidden Wood Village</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon West</color>? Adventurer, you should know what to do next.",
    ["Dialogue3071601"]="(The device makes beeping sounds and the probe turns to point to the east of Payon.)",
    ["Dialogue3071602"]="Is it in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maple Forest</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east of Payon</color>? Adventurer, you should know what to do next.",
    ["Dialogue30800101"]="You've collected 1 chest. Defeat 3 more waves of monsters for the next chest.",
    ["Dialogue30800201"]="You've collected 2 chests. Defeat 3 more waves of monsters for the final chest.",
    ["Dialogue30800401"]="Challenge failed! Please quit the instance and try again!",
    ["Dialogue3080101"]="Adventurer, thank you for your generous help! Thanks to you, I've recovered my mind and body. I can finally continue to help General Qi Euin eradicate the monsters of Munak Cave as a soldier of the Spirit Quellers. But before I can go, there's something that makes me really uneasy.",
    ["Dialogue3080102"]="Sigh... Although my soul has been freed, many deceased <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Queller soldiers</color> have yet to be liberated! Their souls are <color=#CA2E0AFF>crazed and restless</color> because they've lost most of their memories. They can only wander in this cave in the form of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Horongs</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3080103"]="Unless someone can help them <color=#CA2E0AFF>make their last wishes come true</color>, my brothers who went through life and death with me will never be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>recover their sanity and reform their bodies</color>. This isn't an easy task; I can't think of anyone else who would be willing to help!",
    ["Dialogue3080104"]="(Qinghe looks at you excitedly.)\n...D-do you really mean it? I knew it! I just knew you were exceptionally brave and wise! If those soldiers can recover their minds, they will definitely return to the command of General Qi Euin. After all, some things, such as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mission of the Spirit Quellers</color>, can never be forgotten, no matter how many years pass by!",
    ["Dialogue30801101"]="Monster Wave 1 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801201"]="Monster Wave 2 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801301"]="Monster Wave 3 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801401"]="Monster Wave 4 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801501"]="Monster Wave 5 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801601"]="Monster Wave 6 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801701"]="Monster Wave 7 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801801"]="Monster Wave 8 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30801901"]="Monster Wave 9 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue30802001"]="Monster Wave 10 Appeared",
    ["Dialogue3080201"]="(The Horong bounces about irritably.)\n...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Hajen</color>... Hajen! Where is she? Bring Hajen to me now!",
    ["Dialogue3080202"]="...Hajen... She must still be waiting for me under <color=#CA2E0AFF>the tree</color>. That's the promise we made to each other. She would never forget!",
    ["Dialogue3080203"]="...That's the tree, bigger than all the others! All the lovers of Payon promise their love for each other under that tree. Hajen and I carved our <color=#CA2E0AFF>oath</color> on it. Hurry! Find Hajen and bring her here! I want to see her!",
    ["Dialogue3080301"]="Your expression tells me you're puzzled by something again! Like I said before, you're welcome to consult me about anything!",
    ["Dialogue3080302"]="...Ah, I see! You must be talking about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wishing Tree</color> at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>center of Payon</color>! I've heard that it has the same status as Frigga, the goddess of love, to the people of Payon. Many lovers believe that if they make their vows in front of the tree, it will bless their love so that it will be as strong and long-lasting as the tree itself! Because of this, many young people think they'll have the chance to meet the love of their life under the Wishing Tree.",
    ["Dialogue3080303"]="(W suddenly seems to notice something, and blushes as she covers her mouth.)\nOh! Could you be...? Ahem, don't worry! My lips are sealed. I won't tell anyone!",
    ["Dialogue3080401"]="(The young girl looks at you shyly before speaking in a quiet voice.)\n...Um, who are you?",
    ["Dialogue3080402"]="...N-no, my name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Haju</color>. I came to the Wishing Tree to remember my ancestors. By the way, where did you hear of Hajen? She passed away many years ago.",
    ["Dialogue3080403"]="(The young girl looks shocked.)\n...Oh, I think I know who you're talking about! Adventurer, are you willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>listen to an old story about the Wishing Tree</color>? It might hold the answers you're looking for.",
    ["Dialogue3080501"]="(Haju raises her head and looks at the ancient tree in wonder.)\nAdventurer, what do you think is the saddest thing in the world? Many people think it is lovers who are separated by death, but I think it is trying to keep a promise that can never be kept.",
    ["Dialogue3080502"]="Once upon a time, a young couple promised to love each other for the rest of their lives under the Wishing Tree. They decided to get married when the tree blossomed the next year, but no one could have foreseen that a Munak uprising would break out in Payon.",
    ["Dialogue3080503"]="To protect his hometown, the man joined the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Quellers</color> and fought the monsters, whereas the woman had to flee to safety outside the city with the other residents. \"Don't worry about me,\" the man said as he attempted to comfort her. \"We will see each other again under this Wishing Tree!\"",
    ["Dialogue3080504"]="However, before even the lingering warmth of his hand could dissipate from hers, a shocking piece of news hit her like a bolt from the blue: Every one of the Spirit Quellers had died in a battle to encircle and eradicate the Munaks, and even their bodies had sunk into the ground with Payon. Ever since then, the woman waited under the Wishing Tree every day for her beloved to return, even though she knew better than anyone that their promise would never come true.",
    ["Dialogue3080505"]="Yes, the man in the story is called <color=#CA2E0AFF>An Munho</color>. He is the Spirit Queller martyr you encountered in Munak Cave! And that woman who kept her promise until the day she died was <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hajen</color>, one of my distant relatives. To think that the soldier still hasn't forgotten his promise even after a thousand years... It must be some form of comfort to Hajen.",
    ["Dialogue3080506"]="...The martyr's last wish is to see Hajen? But everything has changed; there's no way it can come true... unless... I know! The people of Payon always say that even the plants and trees have a souls. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Break a branch off the Wishing Tree</color>. I believe he will be able to feel the oath he made.",
    ["Dialogue3080601"]="He gave Hajen this <color=#CA2E0AFF>hair accessory</color> as a gift. It was her most cherished possession. She wore it until she passed away. Please take these two items with you and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give them to him</color>. I believe he will be comforted to some extent if he can feel Hajen from them.",
    ["Dialogue3080701"]="...Ah, I finally remember many things from my past, but I didn't expect time to pass by so quickly. A thousand years in the blink of an eye... I presume my beloved Hajen is no longer alive, and I am now the only one to still have this obsession.",
    ["Dialogue3080702"]="(An Munho is surprised at first, but then smiles with both gratitude and sadness.)\n...I see. So, Hajen kept that promise until the day she died. Hmm, maybe it's my turn to wait for her under the Wishing Tree now. Maybe we'll be able to reunite under the tree as spirits one day. I wonder if that counts as fulfilling my promise to her?",
    ["Dialogue3080703"]="But before that, I have another promise to fulfill: the one I made to the people of Payon as a soldier of the Spirit Quellers! There are many people in love with each other in this world, and it is the mission of the Spirit Quellers to <color=#CA2E0AFF>spare as many lovers as possible from the pain of separation</color>. I will fight to the very end for this cause, and then I will go and meet Hajen with a smile of relief on my face.",
    ["Dialogue3080801"]="(The Horong writhes in pain.)\n...Ah!... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mother</color>, I have failed you! I am a terrible son! You will probably never forgive me. Have I broken your heart?",
    ["Dialogue3080802"]="...As the eldest son, it's my responsibility to take care of you, but I couldn't even give you a grandson and the happiness of family life. Can you ever forgive me?",
    ["Dialogue3080803"]="...You're willing to help me apologize to my mother? That's great! My home is on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west side of Payon</color>... Oh, I remember it was <color=#CA2E0AFF>next to a waterfall</color>, and I could hear the sound of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>waterwheel</color> when I opened the window. I remember smelling familiar food with smoke every evening. Mother, I miss you so much!",
    ["Dialogue3080901"]="Adventurer, we meet again. You look like you're in a hurry. Are you looking for something?",
    ["Dialogue3080902"]="(Won Chunghan opens her eyes slowly.)\n...So, you're looking for a house next to a waterfall and a waterwheel? There is indeed such a house in the Former Site of Hidden Wood Village. Why are you asking about it?",
    ["Dialogue3080903"]="...I see. It seems like the gods really do guide us without us knowing. Adventurer, I hope you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>listen to an old story</color>. Maybe it will be I requesting help instead of you afterwards.",
    ["Dialogue3081001"]="(Won Chunghan raises her head slowly)\nAdventurer, what do you think <color=#CA2E0AFF>filial piety</color> is? The concept today means providing support, but my ancestor, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Won Yeong</color>, believed that only those who <color=#CA2E0AFF>carry on the legacy of their parents</color> are truly pious.",
    ["Dialogue3081002"]="Won Yeong's husband died very early on, and she raised her children by all by herself. When the Munak plague broke out in Payon, she was the first to step forward and make a decision that the villagers did not expect—she sent <color=#CA2E0AFF>Won Bin</color>, her only son, into battle and told him to join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Quellers</color> to fight the monsters.",
    ["Dialogue3081003"]="\"Don't you remember how your husband died?\" the villagers asked, concerned that the widow had lost her mind. However, Won Yeong always gave them the same answer: \"I have never forgotten, but my husband died to protect this village, so my son should carry on his legacy.\"",
    ["Dialogue3081004"]="After that, they received news that the Spirit Quellers had all died in the final battle against the Munaks. They lamented the widow's fate and asked Won Yeong sympathetically if she had any regrets. \"I do have one regret, but it isn't that I sent my son to join the Spirit Quellers,\" Won Yeong replied. \"Instead, it is that I wasn't able to tell him how proud I am of his bravery and selflessness before he died.\"",
    ["Dialogue3081005"]="You guessed correctly. Won Yeong's eldest son is the Spirit Queller martyr you met in Munak Cave, and the house he mentioned to you is the ancestral house of the Won Family where I used to live. Adventurer, I believe you did not come here by chance. You are the only one who can liberate that child's soul now, and only you can help Won Yeong, make up for her only regret.",
    ["Dialogue3081006"]="(Won Chunghan exhales slowly.)\nCan you collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>delicious Bear Paws</color> for me? It seems that the cooking skills passed down from my ancestors have finally come in useful.",
    ["Dialogue3081101"]="Very good, these are exactly what I need. Now, can I ask you to get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Wild Mushrooms</color>? These ingredients are indispensable if I want to recreate that same taste.",
    ["Dialogue3081201"]="Hmm... Fortunately, it seems my skills haven't deteriorated. Could I trouble you to take this dish to <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Spirit Queller soldier</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3081202"]="This is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bear Paw Stew with Wild Mushrooms</color> recipe that has been passed down through my family. According to legend, it was because Won Yeong made this dish that her children became so strong. I think that he will remember the aroma. If he can feel his mother from it, I think it will help him overcome his obsession and free his soul.",
    ["Dialogue3081301"]="(Won Bin's eyes instantly fill will tears when he looks at the dish in his hand.)\nAh, this aroma... I remember everything now. This is my mother's specialty, Bear Paw Stew with Wild Mushrooms! But a thousand years have passed. My mother... She would be... Where did you get it?",
    ["Dialogue3081302"]="...I... So Mother wasn't disappointed in me? She was proud of me for joining the Spirit Quellers and fighting for my home!\n(Won Bin wipes the tears from his eyes, his gaze becoming firmer.)",
    ["Dialogue3081303"]="In that case, my next course of action is clear. I will fulfill the mission of the Spirit Quellers and eradicate the monsters in this cave <color=#CA2E0AFF>so that fewer mothers will have to be separated from their children</color>! I will go to meet my mother again once I complete my mission. I believe she will be even more proud of me by then!",
    ["Dialogue3081401"]="(The Horong sways and flickers anxiously.)\n...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Ayu</color>... Where are you, Ayu? Is he well? Can someone help me find Ayu?!",
    ["Dialogue3081402"]="...Hurry up and find him. My son, Ayu, must be at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lady Euin's house</color>! Since my wife died, it's just been me and my son. I promised him I would pick him up after the battle... but I wasn't able to! I wasn't able to!",
    ["Dialogue3081403"]="...It's her! She's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wife of General Qi Euin</color>! I left Ayu in the care of Lady Euin, but it has been too long since I saw him. Ayu... Is Ayu doing well? Can anyone tell me what's happened to him?",
    ["Dialogue3081501"]="...It's you. Whatever you want to talk about, can we talk about it later? There are some things I need to deal with at the Lord's Residence.",
    ["Dialogue3081502"]="(Sun Euin frowns slightly.)\n...Are you telling me that you've come to fulfill the last wish of a Spirit Queller martyr? This isn't something to joke about, so please be clear.",
    ["Dialogue3081503"]="...I see. If what you said is true, the martyr doesn't need to worry about the safety of his child. In the past, the Euin Family took in many orphans who lost their parents in battle, and all those children survived and went on to lead good lives.",
    ["Dialogue3081504"]="Lady Euin treated them like her own children, taught them skills to make a living, and helped them settle down. Some of them worked in agriculture, while some became merchants, and others joined Archer Village. Many of the Payon residents of today are their descendants.",
    ["Dialogue3081505"]="I understand your concern, and I have come up with a solution. Not far from the Lord's Residence is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>orphanage</color> originally established by the Euin Family to house those children. Go there and you'll see children playing. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take a photo of them</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3081601"]="Have you taken the photo? Now, I have another important thing to give you.\n(Sun Euin places a scroll painting into your hand.)",
    ["Dialogue3081602"]="This <color=#CA2E0AFF>Picture of a Hundred Children</color> was painted by General Qi Euin's wife. The children in the painting are all orphans she took in. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>give these two items to the Spirit Quellers martyr</color>. I think they'll put his mind at ease.",
    ["Dialogue3081701"]="(Muhyeon picks up the Picture of a Hundred Children and studies it carefully.)\n...Ah, I remember now. I remember everything! If I'm not mistaken, doesn't this face in the painting belong to my son, Ayu?",
    ["Dialogue3081702"]="...S-so this Picture of a Hundred Children was painted by Lady Euin herself?! Even an uneducated person like me can sense her deep love from the delicate brushstrokes! The Euin Family did not let me down! They took good care of Ayu!",
    ["Dialogue3081703"]="(Muhyeon picks up the Photo of the Orphanage, and his eyes widen in surprise.)\nThe orphanage in this picture was established by the Euin Family? I see... So they helped raise all the orphans who lost their parents in battle, and the Euin Family is still providing protection for all children who need it!",
    ["Dialogue3081704"]="Sigh, I was so worried over nothing. Since the Euin Family has been protecting Payon in their own way, I too must protect this land in my own way! Just you wait and see, I will <color=#CA2E0AFF>ensure that those children will never have to live through such turmoil again</color>. This is the mission of the Spirit Quellers and something I will always strive for!",
    ["Dialogue3081801"]="(Qinghe listens as you recount the events of the Spirit Queller soldiers and sighs emotionally.)\nAlas, the battle against the Munaks forever separated many Spirit Queller soldiers from their loved ones. But when I think of how our sacrifice has made it possible for so many people to attain happiness, though it pains me, I will still stay strong and fight until the very end.",
    ["Dialogue3081802"]="Adventurer, thank you again for helping the Spirit Quellers. You helped those soldiers fulfill their last wishes and made it possible for their bodies to reform and for their souls to be liberated! I thought that everything in this world would be different after a thousand years, but at least I can see that your eyes shine with the same light as ours!",
    ["Dialogue3081901"]="(Sure enough, there are some faint marks on the trunk that read \"Munho and Hajen... always of one heart...\" Although most of the writing is long gone, it is still possible to feel the passion and hope of those two young lovers a thousand years ago.)",
    ["Dialogue3090101"]="I have some shocking gossip that I bet you're dying to hear! You look like the trustworthy sort, so I'll make an exception and tell you.",
    ["Dialogue3090102"]="My fellow disciple, Busang, has always been calm and arrogant, as well as a stickler for rules. He's the most disciplined disciple among us, but guess what?! I've seen him sneak out of here several days in a row now, and even at midnight a few times. I wonder what he's up to.",
    ["Dialogue3090103"]="Sigh, why are you acting just like Munmi? I'm looking out for my fellow disciples, but he says I waste my time gossiping all day, and wants me to focus on my classes. Please help me. I won't fall asleep tonight unless I find out what Busang is up to.",
    ["Dialogue3090104"]="It isn't hard at all. Go steal some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wood Crystal Powder</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wormtails</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby field</color>. It's an important part of my plan. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue3090201"]="Everything's ready. Now we just need to wait for the right time!",
    ["Dialogue3090202"]="(Comet Euin turns around.)\nFortunately, I have a secret recipe that's sure to succeed.",
    ["Dialogue3090203"]="(Comet Euin puts his hands behind his back.)\nHehe, it's nothing, don't mind me. Busang's favorite dish is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fruity Squid</color>. I don't know how good a cook you are, but I still want to ask you to make it for me.\nYou're sure to be a better cook than me. Even I wouldn't dare eat something I've cooked.",
    ["Dialogue3090301"]="Perfect timing. Look, this is the Euin Tracer Pill I just made. Let me add it to this bowl of Fruity Squid. Done! Haha, now I'll be able to find out where he's sneaking off to for most of the night.",
    ["Dialogue3090302"]="Hehe, I have a cunning plan, but I'll need you to take this bowl of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fruity Squid with the Euin Tracer Pill in it</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Busang</color>. Make sure he eats it while it is still hot. Tell him... tell him I made it specially for him, and make sure he tries it.",
    ["Dialogue3090401"]="What's this?",
    ["Dialogue3090402"]="Comet?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why's he acting so nice all of a sudden?</color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF> Could he be in trouble again?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3090403"]="Thank you for taking the time to bring it to me.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I couldn't possibly decline his kind offering in front of an outsider, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but since when did he learn how to cook?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3090404"]="(Busang eats the food quickly.)\nThank Comet for me. <color=#CA2E0AFF>There's something important I need to do</color>, so I'll bid you farewell now.",
    ["Dialogue3090501"]="So? How was it? Did he eat the Fruity Squid?",
    ["Dialogue3090502"]="Excellent! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Euin Tracer Pill</color> I added is a special something I invented. It makes the person who eats it give off a <color=#CA2E0AFF>unique scent that no one can smell</color>. However, my pet, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bobo</color>, is <color=#CA2E0AFF>extremely sensitive</color> to this smell. Now we can find out where he's been going.",
    ["Dialogue3090503"]="I'll hand Bobo over to you now. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Busang</color> for me.",
    ["Dialogue3090601"]="You're finally back. Did you manage to find out what Busang is doing?",
    ["Dialogue3090602"]="What?! Are you sure it's the abandoned house south of the city?! How's that possible?!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>No one's lived there for years. Who could he be meeting there? There must be a conspiracy afoot!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3090603"]="No! Could some supernatural being have set a trap for him? I have to stop him from falling into it! Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon East Forest</color> and collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Mystical Star Leaves</color>. I need to come up with a perfect plan.",
    ["Dialogue3090701"]="These Mystical Star Leaves ensure that my plan will be half successful. Let me think... Busang loves eating fish. My plan will definitely go smoothly if we have a Fish Fillet! I'll leave the important task of cooking it to you.",
    ["Dialogue3090702"]="(Comet Euin turns around with his back to you.)\n<size=18>Hmm... Let me find the recipe</size><size=18>. That's right... This should be okay...</size>",
    ["Dialogue3090703"]="You'll find out later. Start preparing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Fillet</color> now. Don't dawdle.",
    ["Dialogue3090801"]="I have the perfect plan to uncover the truth! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue3090802"]="Look, this is the Dizzying Powder I just made. Once Busang eats the food with Dizzying Powder in it, he'll fall unconscious and won't be able to attend the meeting. We're roughly the same height and build. With my intelligence plus a disguise, I'm confident I'll be able to pull this off!",
    ["Dialogue3090803"]="Of course! Don't underestimate me. Now take this special <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Fillet</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Busang</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3090901"]="Hmm... Did Comet also make this himself?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>What's he done wrong this time?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3090902"]="In that case... thanks.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh well, I'm surprised he remembers what food I like. He's gotten into trouble so many times. There's bound to be a way to help him.</color></size>\n(Busang starts eating the Fish Fillet.)",
    ["Dialogue3090903"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I never realized he was such a good cook, but... why do I suddenly feel so dizzy and sleepy? Oh no!</color></size>\n(Busang faints and falls to the ground.)",
    ["Dialogue3091001"]="We'll let him sleep for now while we execute the plan. I'll have sorted everything out by the time he wakes up. Here, take this.",
    ["Dialogue3091002"]="This is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Black Dog Blood</color>. I have a feeling that we'll need it. Just bring it with you.",
    ["Dialogue3091003"]="You might not believe me, but my instincts are always right. I'm going to change into his clothes now. Wait for me <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside the abandoned house</color>. Hurry!",
    ["Dialogue3091101"]="I've been waiting for some time. This is the plan: I'll pretend to be Busang and go meet that woman. You'll hide here and wait for my instructions. I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>give you a signal</color>. When you see it, pour the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Black Dog Blood</color> over her. I can't wait to see what kind of monster she is. How dare she target Busang?!",
    ["Dialogue3091201"]="Ahhh! She's a Sohee! Speak, fiend! Where did you come from?! Why did you approach Busang? How dare you bewitch him?!",
    ["Dialogue3091202"]="You're wrong. Calm down. I mean him no harm, and I haven't bewitched him. I... I just fell in love with him.",
    ["Dialogue3091203"]="You love Busang? Hmph... I don't believe it. Sohees are vile creatures, filled with a lifetime of resentment. They will affect the lifespan and sanity of any living person they have prolonged contact with. If you do love him, why continue these rendezvous? The only reason Busang would agree to meet a Sohee behind our backs is if you've bewitched him.",
    ["Dialogue3091204"]="You misunderstand me. Busang and I truly are in love with each other. I know I shouldn't see him anymore, but I just can't let go.\n(Eunsook looks like she is about to cry.)",
    ["Dialogue3091205"]="No way! I won't let a Sohee like you keep pestering Busang. If you really care about him, you should leave this place immediately.",
    ["Dialogue3091206"]="Eunsook! You're getting bold, aren't you! How dare you keep meeting these lowly mortals behind your mistress's back?!",
    ["Dialogue3091301"]="You should leave now! Eunju must have told my mistress.",
    ["Dialogue3091302"]="The mistress was originally a <color=#CA2E0AFF>10,000 year-old Vixen</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forest of the General in east Payon</color>. There are many abandoned graves there that no one visits. The mistress digs up the bones and ashes of these dead people to control their souls. She forces Sohees like us to bewitch the living and steal their vitality. You should leave now. The mistress is too strong, and Eunju will certainly bring her here for revenge.",
    ["Dialogue3091401"]="Comet, I trusted you. How could you do this?",
    ["Dialogue3091402"]="I-I was just worried you were being deceived. Master always says I'm too naive, but you've always been prudent and obedient to Master's instructions. Why... why did you believe this Sohee? She's a Sohee...",
    ["Dialogue3091403"]="(Busang falls silent for a moment.)\nEunsook... She's never harmed me. I must save her.",
    ["Dialogue3091404"]="(Comet Euin presses his hand helplessly against his face.)\nYou... you... Sigh, forget it. I don't know what to do about you. You can go save her, but you have to take me with you. That Vixen sounds really powerful. I won't let you face danger alone.",
    ["Dialogue3091501"]="Adventurer, Busang, thank you for saving Eunsook. She is just a poor soul. She has no way to repay you.",
    ["Dialogue3091502"]="Eunsook, everything's fine now. From now on, no one can force you to do anything.",
    ["Dialogue3091503"]="Busang, I have wronged you. I was lucky enough to meet you in this life; I do not dare to ask for any more. I only hope that I will be able to meet you again in the next life. Please forget about me in this life.",
    ["Dialogue3091504"]="Eunsook...",
    ["Dialogue3091505"]="Adventurers, can you go to my grave and <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebury </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>my urn</color>? Don't let anyone else use me to hurt anyone ever again.",
    ["Dialogue3091506"]="(Busang clenches his fists in sadness.)\nEunsook... I'll respect your wishes.",
    ["Dialogue3091601"]="(Eunsook stares lovingly at Busang as she gradually fades away.)\nIt's finally over. Thank you for everything.",
    ["Dialogue3091602"]="Eunsook...\n(Busang looks at Eunsook sadly.)",
    ["Dialogue3091701"]="If only things could be as beautiful as when we first met... You should go.",
    ["Dialogue3091702"]="Busang, I...",
    ["Dialogue3091703"]="Give me some time.\n(Busang stares sadly at the tombstone.)",
    ["Dialogue3100101"]="(Omari is rubbing his stubble, still clearly distressed.)\nTsk! This won't do at all! If the underground air weren't so damned acidic, it wouldn't have corroded this badly.",
    ["Dialogue3100102"]="—Huh?! How did I get in here? Do you think a magic barrier is enough to keep me away from such a marvelous ancient civilization? You believe a few monsters can stifle my desire to explore cultural relics? Let's just say, there are no ancient ruins in the world that we, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group</color>, cannot infiltrate! As long as I have my trusty shovel in my hand, I can dig my way through the entire continent!",
    ["Dialogue3100103"]="Hmm, but what was the use of even coming here? I finally found this stone tablet, thousands of years old, but the characters on it have been made illegible due to years of acidic erosion!",
    ["Dialogue3100104"]="They say that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gangrene Grass</color> can reverse any kind of tarnishing, as well as restore handwriting, but it only grows in haunted places where monsters gather.\n(Omari mutters between curses.)",
    ["Dialogue3100201"]="(Omari puffs out two rings of smoke excitedly.)\nOh! That's just the grass I needed! I wouldn't have guessed that someone so skinny could be so capable!",
    ["Dialogue3100202"]="Now then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>quickly apply the Gangrene Grass juice to the ancient stone tablet</color>. I'd like to see if this actually works.",
    ["Dialogue3100301"]="(Omari moves closer to the stone and squints.)\nWell, let me see...\nThe ancient elven city... here... training here...",
    ["Dialogue3100302"]="Gosh, how did those ancients manage to carve so many small characters on this <color=#CA2E0AFF>stone tablet</color>? I'll need you to read it for me; I need to record it word for word in my logbook!",
    ["Dialogue3100401"]="(Timothy wipes the sweat from his forehead and salutes you respectfully.)\nMaster, you're here! I searched the area according to your instructions and found a <color=#CA2E0AFF>suspicious object</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3100402"]="Didn't you say that the magical magnetic field in this area seems to be very unusual, as though it seems to contain some kind of dangerous force? When I found that object, it was emitting a strong and intricate aura. Maybe it's the source of all the strange happenings here. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color> and take a look!",
    ["Dialogue3100501"]="(Timothy looks shocked and confused.)\nThese... I've seen these Deviruchi in my Monster Encyclopedia! They're from the world of the dead—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Niflheim</color>! But what are these undead monsters doing here in Midgard?",
    ["Dialogue3100502"]="Do you mean that this fragment contains the same <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark power</color> as the world of the dead, and these two forces have collided to tear a rift between the worlds, bringing these demons into our world? But if that's true, isn't Geffenia...",
    ["Dialogue3100503"]="—Master! Something just happened!",
    ["Dialogue3100601"]="(Byron rushes toward you.)\nMaster, <color=#CA2E0AFF>something's wrong</color> with several of those apprentice mages. Please follow me and see for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue3100701"]="(Sybil's head is hung low, and she doesn't seem to notice your arrival.)\nDark power... will finally rise... The King of the Dead...",
    ["Dialogue3100702"]="<size=26>—Yaaargh!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3100801"]="(Sybil's eyes become clear again.)\nYou... What the...?",
    ["Dialogue3100802"]="...What happened just now? Sorry, I can't remember. To be honest, I don't even know why I'm standing under this tree. I could've sworn I was with my friends just now.\n(Sybil looks confused.)",
    ["Dialogue3100803"]="Master, this kind of thing has been happening quite often among the apprentice mages recently. They're not only becoming increasingly dependent on the magical magnetic field in this area, but they're also becoming more obsessed with it. Their temperaments even change sometimes, and they lose their memory.",
    ["Dialogue3100804"]="I'm afraid... %^@#$*&...\n(Byron's words start slurring.)",
    ["Dialogue3100901"]="(Omari's voice sounds from afar.)\n...Hey! You #$%*&?",
    ["Dialogue3100902"]="Hey, don't scare me. Could it be because of the ruins... @#$*& possession?!",
    ["Dialogue3100903"]="...Heck, I'm an archaeologist, not an exorcist! If this carries on, all I can do is crack open your head with my pipe and take a look inside!\n(Omari raises his pipe.)",
    ["Dialogue3100904"]="So, you've finally snapped out of it! So, what happened exactly? Why did you suddenly stop talking and slip into a trance like that?",
    ["Dialogue3100905"]="...Master, training, Fragment of Ymir's Heart? Hold on, this all sounds like—\nYou passed through the memory of the world-famous mage, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin Heines</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3100906"]="Oh, yes! It must be true! According to the research records, Merlin Heines led his apprentices to train in the Geffenia Ruins because of the strong magical magnetic field there! They also discovered a Fragment of Ymir's Heart buried here. The ancient books didn't describe all the details, but what you saw and heard fills the gaps in the story!",
    ["Dialogue3100907"]="Ah, how lucky you are to tune into the memories of the ancient master! If I had the chance, I'd also like to witness those great historical moments with my own eyes.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But since that's probably not going to happen any time soon, I'll have to make full use of this marvelous adventurer before me!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3100908"]="Ahem, what I mean is, there are many more ancient relics waiting for us to explore and study. There's no time to lose. Quick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3101001"]="(Omari digs a broken staff out of the soil, alternately looking at it through a magnifying glass and shining his flashlight on it.)\nThere's no doubt about it, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>staff</color> is also a relic from a thousand years ago! But it's completely covered in dirt. Ahem, come and <color=#CA2E0AFF>help me wipe it clean</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3101101"]="(The corners of Wyatt's mouth rise slightly when he sees you coming.)\n...Oh, hey! It's a good thing you came along. Can you do me a favor?",
    ["Dialogue3101102"]="Hmm? Have we met before? No, I must be mistaken; I'd never forget a gorgeous face like yours so easily! Haha!\n(Wyatt's smiling eyes suddenly twitch.)",
    ["Dialogue3101103"]="...Sorry, it seems this isn't really the right time to be joking around. Could you gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cliff Grass</color> for me as quickly as you can? I'm afraid I won't last much longer with this wound.",
    ["Dialogue3101201"]="Thank you, that should be enough. Could you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply</color> the herbs here?\n(Wyatt smiles apologetically while looking at the wound on his waist.)\nThe magic that caused this <color=#CA2E0AFF>wound</color> was so powerful that I can't even move my body.",
    ["Dialogue3101301"]="(Wyatt clenches his teeth and stands up slowly.)\nThank you. I feel much better now. Without your help, maybe this so-called <color=#CA2E0AFF>War of the Mages</color> would have been the end of me.",
    ["Dialogue3101302"]="Didn't you see the calamity that happened just now? The apprentice mages training in the Geffenia Ruins lost their minds one after another and began fighting for this holy place. The weak of will easily succumb to the dark side of their own hearts under the influence of dark elemental power. Everything happened so quickly, just as Master Merlin predicted.",
    ["Dialogue3101303"]="Hey, I'm a high wizard, and a member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pentagram</color>! Even in the toughest battle, it'll take more than that to put me in the ground. But if <color=#CA2E0AFF>someone I trust</color> casts a spell on me from behind...",
    ["Dialogue3101304"]="(Wyatt's eyes suddenly become serious.)\n...That's a whole 'nother kettle of fish.",
    ["Dialogue3101305"]="Well, now that I'm back on my feet, I have to head back to Master Merlin as soon as possible and tell him what just happened. As for you... Since you also seem to be able to resist dark elemental power, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look around here</color> and see if there are any other injured people who need help!",
    ["Dialogue3101401"]="(Omari watches your every move with expectant eyes.)\nHaha! It looks like it's true! All you need to do is touch an ancient relic and you can enter the memory of its owner! Come on, what did you see this time?",
    ["Dialogue3101402"]="(Omari excitedly scribbles down notes while puffing out rings of smoke.)\nVery good, very good... This is a huge leap forward in the study of history! Let's go. There are loads more <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient relics</color> waiting for us to excavate and study! We can't delay for even a second. Come on!",
    ["Dialogue3101501"]="(Omari finds a tattered diary in the corner, but as soon as he reaches out, he screams.)\n...Hot damn!",
    ["Dialogue3101502"]="My friend, this diary has a powerful magic barrier around it. Someone must want to keep it intact, and they've protected it with magic! Hmm, an important story must lie within it. Gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Monster Nails</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Marionettes</color>. They're the only thing that can break the magic barrier!",
    ["Dialogue3101601"]="Okay, take these Sharp Monster Nails and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place them on the diary</color>. My archaeologist's intuition tells me that its content will play a crucial role in the continuing study of history.",
    ["Dialogue3101701"]="(Dracula raises his haughty head.)\nHehe, welcome, human who bathes in blood! Congratulations, you have rid yourself of the morality and beliefs of your base race and submitted to the dark desire in your heart!",
    ["Dialogue310170101"]="Stop being reckless! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue3101702"]="I am <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dracula</color>, leader of the Blood Clan and hand of Demon King Morroc. It is I who called you here to give you the opportunity to serve the glorious legion of the dead.",
    ["Dialogue310170201"]="Stop healing! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue3101703"]="(Dracula opens his arms.)\nCome, hand the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> over to me. I will take you across the gate of life and death in the name of Lord Morroc, and show you the endless magical power and mysteries beyond the reach of humans!",
    ["Dialogue310170301"]="Stop gathering! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue310170401"]="Stop fighting alone! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue310170501"]="Stop being static! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue310170601"]="Stop breathing! Otherwise, you shall feel his wrath!",
    ["Dialogue3101801"]="Hey, you've finally regained consciousness. Look what I found!\n(Omari points to the name on the cover of the diary, his face glowing with excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue3101802"]="\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Truman Capet</color>\"... I recall this name appearing in Pentagram: A History! There's no mistaking it, this diary belongs to Truman, a disciple of Archmage Merlin Heine and a member of Pentagram. There must be some truly extraordinary deeds recorded in it. Quick, tell me, what did you see this time?",
    ["Dialogue3101803"]="(Omari is struck dumb, his eyes blinking.)\n...That means Truman was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>traitor</color> to Pentagram. He massacred his companions in the War of the Mages a thousand years ago... and delivered the Fragment of Ymir's Heart to the Blood Clan?",
    ["Dialogue3101804"]="According to historical records, the Fragment of Ymir's Heart was eventually retrieved by Merlin from the Geffenia Ruins. Could it be that he appeared just in time to stop Dracula's plan? So what happened to Truman?",
    ["Dialogue3101805"]="You're right, the answer should be in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blood Abbey</color>. Let's follow Truman's past footsteps and witness where the path he once walked led!\n(Omari steps forward resolutely.)",
    ["Dialogue3101901"]="(Truman clasps his head in his hands, but his pupils are no longer wrapped in chaos.)\nMy... master... Sorry... sorry...",
    ["Dialogue3101902"]="You... How do you know my name? I've been wandering in the darkness for thousands of years. Even I... I've forgotten who I am...",
    ["Dialogue3101903"]="(A slight sign of relief appears on Truman's face.)\nSo, someone finally found my diary. It's a pity that although it has been completely preserved, I have fallen under the control of others. Just a monster possessing a living body.",
    ["Dialogue3101904"]="Yes, Dracula turned me into this. What you see standing before you now is no longer Truman, the disciple of Merlin, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priest of Darkness</color>! My soul, it was plunged into darkness long ago for those unforgivable sins. Even if I regain my sanity for a short time, such as now, I will soon become a slave to the dark elemental power once more.",
    ["Dialogue3101905"]="(Truman reveals a bitter smile.)\nThank you for your kindness, but I'm doomed to this dark bondage, for my life's final wish shall never come true.",
    ["Dialogue3101906"]="But I'm still glad to know that the tale of a thousand years past is now finally known. Perhaps helping the world see the truth is a kind of atonement, late though it may be.",
    ["Dialogue3102001"]="(The remains of a mage. After looking at it carefully, you see a fatal wound on his chest very similar to that of the wounded mage just now.)",
    ["Dialogue3102101"]="(The remains of another mage. After looking at it carefully, you see a fatal wound on his neck very similar to that of the wounded mage just now.)",
    ["Dialogue3102201"]="(A strange dimensional gap, constantly emitting the aura of the world of the dead from its center.)",
    ["Dialogue310220101"]="Shelter has entered a Holy-dominant state.",
    ["Dialogue310220201"]="Shelter has entered a Shadow-dominant state.",
    ["Dialogue31101001"]="<color=#ffe788>Race started!</color> Temporary",
    ["Dialogue31101002"]="<color=#ffe788>Race failed!</color> Temporary",
    ["Dialogue31101003"]="<color=#ffe788>Race succeeded!</color> Temporary",
    ["Dialogue31101005"]="<color=#ffe788>Summon <color=#ff5252>Fire Dragon</color> and ride them across the valley!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31101006"]="<color=#ffe788>The slumbering <color=#ff5252>Guardian of Ice Valley</color> has awoken!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31101007"]="<color=#ffe788>The slumbering <color=#ff5252>Guardian of the Glaciers</color> has awoken!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31101008"]="<color=#ffe788>Ice block is about to fall on the left side! Tilt the Draco to the <color=#528fff>right</color>!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31101009"]="<color=#ffe788>Ice block is about to fall on the right side! Tilt the Draco to the <color=#528fff>left</color>!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3110101"]="(Katrina looks at you seriously.)\nAdventurer, I would like to ask you to find someone in Geffen for me. He may be the only one who can help my master solve her troubles.",
    ["Dialogue31101010"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#528fff>Disable auto battle</color> before mounting the Draco.</color>",
    ["Dialogue3110102"]="Shh! Keep your voice down! It's because I can't directly propose this to my master that I've asked you to do it.",
    ["Dialogue3110103"]="As a matter of fact, since you took the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the Artifact, my master locks herself in Geffen Tower all day long looking for new energy sources that can be used as a substitute. She believes that repairing the Artifact is the responsibility of the Mage Guild, and she refuses to let outsiders interfere in any way.",
    ["Dialogue3110104"]="But I've heard that there's a man in Geffen who knows how to solve this problem. His name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>De'qeen</color>, and he's a member of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alchemist Guild</color>! The Alchemist Guild has continuously been studying the structure of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir's Heart</color>, so perhaps he can offer us some valuable advice.",
    ["Dialogue3110105"]="...Of course you won't find the Alchemist Guild in Geffen, as they're an organization from the neighboring city, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aldebaran</color>. In order to promote academic exchange, the major guilds send emissaries to each other's cities every year, and De'qeen was the emissary sent by the Alchemist Guild to Geffen.",
    ["Dialogue3110106"]="Essentially, as an emissary of his guild, it is De'qeen's duty to help us resolve this matter! Since my master is unwilling to converse with others, I must ask you to find his residence in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest of Geffen</color>. Please ask him to fulfill his duty as an alchemist!",
    ["Dialogue3110201"]="De'qeen wasn't home and just left this letter?\n(Katrina quickly reads the letter.)\nBut what does it mean?! He's an alchemist! What does he have to do with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Research Institute</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3110202"]="Of course, I know that from the letter, De'qeen must have gone after the escaped test subject! But if the subject can really make others harm themselves using the power of his mind, doesn't that mean De'qeen is in danger?",
    ["Dialogue3110203"]="No! De'qeen isn't the only one in danger. If the test subject escapes to Geffen, everyone here will also be in harm's way! This can't be allowed to happen. We have to find out where the test subject is... but how?\n(Katrina stamps her foot impatiently.)",
    ["Dialogue3110204"]="You're right, this letter has provided us with enough clues. So, according to the letter, our <color=#CA2E0AFF>first step</color> should be—",
    ["Dialogue3110205"]="...Hey, this doesn't seem right? This is important; please try to be more precise!",
    ["Dialogue3110206"]="Right. We should first find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>person possessed by the subject</color>, and then use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>special flash grenade</color> to make the subject show its true form! Since the letter says that the host will invariably be exhibiting <color=#CA2E0AFF>abnormal behavior</color>, we should <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask the residents of Geffen for information</color> to help us find the target more quickly.",
    ["Dialogue3110207"]="As for sealing away the test subject... I think the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic ward</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>under Geffen Tower</color> should work, but the question is, how do we get the subject there? We're going to need to improvise.",
    ["Dialogue3110208"]="(Katrina raises her head determinedly.)\nAdventurer, are you confident that you can carry out this task alone? This is extremely important, but it'll also be very dangerous.",
    ["Dialogue3110209"]="Very good. Well, I'll let you take care of this first. When I'm done reporting the situation to Jesqurienne, I'll hurry along to support you!",
    ["Dialogue3110301"]="(Daphne puts her hands on her hips discontentedly.)\nAh... This is giving me a real headache! If that guy shows up again, I'll have to send him away.",
    ["Dialogue3110302"]="You don't know the half of it. I met a real weirdo recently! He comes here to buy <color=#CA2E0AFF>green hair dye</color> from me almost every day, and he keeps asking if it's toxic and how long it will last.",
    ["Dialogue3110303"]="The weirdest thing is, the amount he buys each time is more than a normal person can even use. Because of him, my shop is completely out of green hair dye!",
    ["Dialogue3110304"]="I don't know that weirdos name, I just know that he lives nearby.\n(Daphne rolls her eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue3110305"]="How about this? If you can get me enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wild Mistletoe</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin Forest</color>, I'll tell you where he lives!",
    ["Dialogue3110401"]="(Daphne claps her hands happily.)\nHee-hee! Great! With this Wild Mistletoe, I can make some new green hair dye to refill my shelves in no time!",
    ["Dialogue3110402"]="Oh yeah, do you still want to know where that weirdo lives? He lives in a small wooden cabin <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of Geffen</color>. But be careful. It's possible that his brain was zapped by some really evil magic!",
    ["Dialogue3110501"]="Ah, where has that boy gone? If he doesn't come back... *cough, cough, cough*...\n(Eddie coughs weakly.)",
    ["Dialogue3110502"]="...Thank you for your concern, young adventurer, but if you really want to help me, can you go to the food vendor <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nicola</color> and buy some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Traveler's Rations</color> for me? As you can see, my legs are not up to the task.",
    ["Dialogue3110601"]="Thank you for your help, young adventurer! May I ask, when you went to find Nicola, did you see my son <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amber</color> there?",
    ["Dialogue3110602"]="Well, my boy said he was going shopping, but he hasn't come back yet. I don't know why, but he's been <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneaking out of the house</color> a lot these days. Sometimes when I clean his room, I find empty cans of green hair dye.",
    ["Dialogue3110603"]="A few days ago, I heard him say something like <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>... <color=#CA2E0AFF>8 PM</color>... <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest corner</color>... This kind of nonsense. Do you think he might have been possessed by a demon? He's never acted this way before!",
    ["Dialogue3110701"]="Damn... What do you think you're doing, interrupting my date with Agatha?! If you hadn't shown up and scared her away, we... we would have...\n(The man stomps his feet indignantly.)",
    ["Dialogue3110702"]="(Amber's face flashes red and white.)\n...Hmph, what of it? I just like tough, strong girls. No one has the right to interfere with my business!",
    ["Dialogue3110703"]="It's just a shame that Orc girls don't date outside their race, so I'm forced to paint my skin green and pretend to be one of them. Ahem, anyway, this has nothing to do with you! What are you doing wandering around outside town in the middle of the night?",
    ["Dialogue3110704"]="Ah-hah! Well, I'm certainly not the one you're looking for, but I did meet an <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> not far from here, and he was <color=#CA2E0AFF>acting quite strangely</color>. It looked as though he was badly injured from the way he was walking, but no matter how much I questioned him, he didn't seem to be able to hear me.",
    ["Dialogue31108001"]="<color=#ffe788>Destroy the Spell-breaker Orb of the corresponding color to dispel the object's Invulnerable status!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108002"]="<color=#ffe788>Discovered the trapped <color=#839d34>Purified Seed</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108003"]="<color=#ffe788>The <color=#839d34>Purified Seed</color> is cleansing the entire forest! Deliver it safely to the <color=#528fff>Spring of Origins</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108004"]="<color=#ffe788>The <color=#839d34>Purified Seed</color> has grown into a <color=#839d34>Purified Sprout</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108005"]="<color=#ffe788>The <color=#839d34>Purified Sprout</color> has grown into a <color=#839d34>Purified Seedling</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108006"]="<color=#ffe788>The <color=#839d34> Purified Seed</color> has entered its next growth phase! Protect it by eliminating the nearby <color=#ff5252>monsters!</color></color>",
    ["Dialogue31108007"]="<color=#ffe788>The <color=#839d34>Purified Seedling</color> has reached the Spring of Origins! Purification begins!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108008"]="<color=#ffe788>Watch out! A <color=#ff5252>Giant Chonchon</color> is attacking the seedling and preventing its growth!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108009"]="<color=#ffe788>Wait for the seedling to grow and survive!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3110801"]="Wow, you don't see this kind of flash grenade around too often these days. Were you sent by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Research Institute</color> to track me down?",
    ["Dialogue31108010"]="<color=#ffe788>Select a halo of purification to predict the future of the Purified Seedling!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108011"]="<color=#ffe788>Careful! <color=#ff5252>Beelzebub</color> is about to unleash a powerful attack! Use the Spell-breaker Orbs to dispel Beelzebub's Invulnerability and cancel its attack!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108014"]="<color=#ffe788>Hah! Prepare to feel the wrath of Beelzebub! Arise, my army of the undead!</color>",
    ["Dialogue31108015"]="<color=#ffe788>I shall show you the true meaning of power!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3110802"]="(The Doppelganger's face suddenly sinks.)\n...The last person to call me that was a man named <color=#CA2E0AFF>De'qeen</color>, but as you can see, he's now lying dead at my feet. Who is the prey and who is the hunter? Maybe he hadn't thought about that until the moment he died.",
    ["Dialogue3110803"]="But whoever you are... Now that you've run into me, you shall meet the same end. Now that De'qeen is no longer of use, you shall be my <color=#CA2E0AFF>next host</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3110901"]="(The Doppelganger flies around behind you, and you hear an ethereal sound running through your skull and into your brain.)\nHuman beings really are pathetic creatures. It was not until I departed from my former body that I finally noticed your frailty.",
    ["Dialogue3110902"]="You can't let go of your mundane and meaningless feelings, but you can abandon more important things.\nYou think you're always right, but you don't have the courage to look within your souls.",
    ["Dialogue3110903"]="I can help free you from the shackles of your heart... or perhaps I should say, I can free your truest, most atavistic nature.\nNow, please answer my question: Have you ever been afraid of death? Have you ever been afraid of those stronger than you?",
    ["Dialogue3110904"]="So, are you willing to entrust the burden of consciousness to me?\nWill you let me take away those stifling fears and help you let go of your mediocre and empty existence?",
    ["Dialogue3110905"]="(The Doppelganger's eyes blink happily.)\nVery good. To seal our alliance, let's do something you would not have been able to do so easily before, such as... <color=#CA2E0AFF>challenge the champion of Orc Village</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3110906"]="Oh, it seems that your willpower is stronger than that of an ordinary person. It's a pity that such a calm mind is often the most boring kind. Well, there's no fun in manipulating a puppet that won't listen. I'd better go and find another host.",
    ["Dialogue3111001"]="(The Doppelganger shows a playful look.)\nAh, the Orcs are an ancient and proud race. This big guy doesn't seem to appreciate your arrival.",
    ["Dialogue3111002"]="It seems that a single battle would be enough to end you. Well, if we are to have a truly thrilling battle on our hands, you must first find a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>offend the honor of the Orc Hero</color>, and thus arouse his desire to fight!",
    ["Dialogue3111101"]="(The Doppelganger looks up in surprise.)\nWell, that's a surprise... I didn't expect you to survive against such a formidable foe.",
    ["Dialogue3111102"]="But this is just the beginning.\n(The Doppelganger thinks for a moment.)\nSince one-on-one battles seem to be a little too easy for you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color> may be the best place to go!",
    ["Dialogue3111201"]="People often say that, although the Kobolds are small and weak, when they unite in groups, their strength is superior to that of any large monster. This is why few people dare to enter Kordt Forest. But I don't want you to just step into the domain of the Kobolds.\n(The Doppelganger cracks a sly smile.)",
    ["Dialogue3111202"]="I've heard that for some reason, the Kobolds hate the Doram and all other <color=#CA2E0AFF>feline creatures</color>, and they can't stand when people compare the two races. But this surely wouldn't stop someone who doesn't want to live. So, march your brave and unstoppable soul over there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>shout out with everything you've got in front of the Kobolds</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3111301"]="(The Kobold guard stares at you with vigilant eyes.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3111302"]="(The Kobold guard's eyes beam with murderous intent.)\nAwooh!",
    ["Dialogue3111401"]="(The Doppelganger looks helpless.)\nAh, how could this be? How could I succeed in controlling a human's mind, but unable to take its life?",
    ["Dialogue3111402"]="(The Doppelganger's face suddenly twists into a ferocious mass.)\n...You want to know why I hate human beings? Because the pain you have inflicted on me far exceeds anything I could ever do to you. Because I am a demon of your creation!",
    ["Dialogue3111403"]="The purpose of my existence is to lead human beings to death, and now that you and I are united, you must do as I say.\nNow, I order you to answer my question: What can I do to kill you?",
    ["Dialogue3111404"]="Oh, so you mean the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underground caves of Geffen</color> are so dangerous that none who enter can make it out alive? Very well. Let's head there at once. I hope the caverns will be your final resting place!",
    ["Dialogue3111501"]="(The Doppelganger look at its body in horror.)\nWait... What is this feeling? Why is the strength in my body slowly dissipating?!",
    ["Dialogue3111502"]="What? It's not humans who can't leave this cave after entering, but demons like me?\n(The Doppelganger's face gradually calms down, even showing a trace of amusement.)",
    ["Dialogue3111503"]="Adventurer, I never would have guessed that you'd pretend to be under my control and obey my demands in order to lead me to this magic ward. It seems that there are souls on this continent that cannot be corrupted by evil.",
    ["Dialogue3111504"]="Well, in return for the unexpected pleasure you have given me, let me leave you with these words:\nThe truth is, the real \"demon\" has not yet revealed itself, but sooner or later, it will, and it shall take away all that you cherish.",
    ["Dialogue3111505"]="Hehe, it's not becoming of a demon to explain such things with this degree of benevolence. Well, let's get this over with! You will never be able to truly kill me, for as long as there is a dark side to the human heart, I will be reborn.",
    ["Dialogue3111601"]="Adventurer, I heard from Katrina about what happened earlier. Did you find the escaped test subject?",
    ["Dialogue3111602"]="—What?! The emissary of the Alchemist Guild... De'qeen was killed by the test subject? How is it that not even a member of the guild was able to control this situation? That so-called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Research Institute</color>... What kind of monster have they created?!",
    ["Dialogue3111603"]="The way I see it, compared to De'qeen's death, just knowing the organization that sent the letter to him probably controls the entire Alchemist Guild is even more chilling. If only one escaped test subject is enough to pose a threat to the continent, then the kind of power those researchers are trying to unlock must be more terrifying than we can imagine.",
    ["Dialogue3111604"]="Master, this matter...\n(Katrina clenches her fists, then hesitates and slowly relaxes her hands.)",
    ["Dialogue3111605"]="Well, it's up to you to investigate this matter, Katrina. Let's see how things will develop in the future.",
    ["Dialogue3111606"]="(Katrina's eyes sparkle with gratitude.)\n...Alright!",
    ["Dialogue3111701"]="(There seems to be no response. The wooden door remains motionless. You try to pull the handle and find that the door is not locked.)",
    ["Dialogue3111801"]="(The light in the room is dim. There's no one in sight, and not a sound can be heard. Could the hut's owner have left in a hurry?)",
    ["Dialogue3111901"]="(The alchemist breathes his last breath. The cuts all over his body tell you that he was embroiled in a fierce battle before he died.)",
    ["Dialogue3120101"]="Adventurer! You're just in time! Quickly, explain to this dolt that I'm not a mobster! I've tried to explain it to him a dozen times already, but he just won't believe me! It's driving me nuts!",
    ["Dialogue3120102"]="This suspicious-looking female thief has been seen sneaking around outside Geffen City for several days now, and she looks like she's up to no good. Since I'm responsible for keeping the peace along the Geffen City perimeter, I can't let her get away without a thorough interrogation.",
    ["Dialogue3120103"]="You sneaky, stone-faced simpleton! I'm a member of the Assassins Guild! It's my job to be slinking around here, okay?!",
    ["Dialogue3120104"]="So, a member of the Assassins Guild has come to our Mage Guild headquarters in secret instead of just walking through the door. And you say you're not one of those mobsters here to make trouble?",
    ["Dialogue3120105"]="(Trisse's face reddens with anger. She clenches her fists and her knuckles turn pale.)\nYou... you stinking mage! I'm here to catch the leader of the same mobster gang you're talking about! She defected from the Assassins Guild. If you don't believe me, come to the mobster camp with me!",
    ["Dialogue3120201"]="No, this is impossible! This is right where they were—I've been watching them for days. How could they have just disappeared all of a sudden? They must be hiding somewhere. Yeah, they must be planning an ambush! Be careful!",
    ["Dialogue3120202"]="How are we supposed to trust a cunning thief like you? Are you trying to trick us again?",
    ["Dialogue3120203"]="I'm not lying! Don't you dare talk trash about me, you stinking mage!",
    ["Dialogue3120204"]="Wow! Where did this little treat come from? Hmm... You must have a lot of guts to walk straight into our hands like this. Haha, well, we shouldn't look a gift horse in the mouth, eh?",
    ["Dialogue3120301"]="Everybody, just calm down! There's no need to fight. We can talk this out. Why don't we all just try to get along? If there's anything you need, we'll do all we can to help you.",
    ["Dialogue3120302"]="Hmph! Now that you know what we're all about, don't think about pulling any funny stuff. Tell me where your leader is!",
    ["Dialogue3120303"]="Ah... Well... (The mobster leader looks around awkwardly, as if hesitating.)",
    ["Dialogue3120304"]="Tell me. If you don't... (Bairde raises his staff with a blank expression.)",
    ["Dialogue3120305"]="Hey now, let's not get carried away! Look, our boss has had a new target in her sights recently—a caravan transporting precious medicinal herbs. It's supposed to be passing through Sograt Desert at the moment, so the boss took a few men to go and ambush it early in the morning.",
    ["Dialogue3120306"]="Sograt Desert? That heartless traitor! She'd even steal from her own hometown?! This time, I'll catch that treacherous devil!",
    ["Dialogue3120307"]="The Sograt caravan? If it's just valuable herbs she's after, the Geffen caravan would be a more convenient choice, but she's targeting Sograt Desert. Is there some special reason for this? Well... The Assassins Guild can't let her go ahead with this, regardless.",
    ["Dialogue3120308"]="Excellent! Thank you, adventurer. Let's go to Sograt right now. You have a good heart, not like that stony-faced mage! Huh? What are you looking at? Want me to put you in your place?",
    ["Dialogue3120401"]="Oh-ho! Would you like to buy some herbs for a rainy day? Our herbs are the best in all Sograt, and their quality is absolutely guaranteed!\n(Elkson speaks with a slippery smile, his enthusiasm coming across as a little overwhelming.)",
    ["Dialogue3120402"]="We're not here to buy herbs.",
    ["Dialogue3120403"]="Hmm? You're not here to buy herbs? I'm not running a charity here!\n(The corners of Elkson's mouth immediately drop, and a mean and indifferent look sweeps across his face.)",
    ["Dialogue3120404"]="Elkson, we're here to guarantee the safety of your caravan. It's been targeted by a group of mobsters, and they may attack at any moment!",
    ["Dialogue3120405"]="Huh—? What?! I knew it! There are always penniless wretches eyeing up my goods. Do they think these precious herbs just fell from the sky? Fortunately, I had the foresight to hire a team of adventurers to wipe out the monsters around here. You lot, hurry up and bring those adventurers back here. I won't let anyone take what's mine. Whatever happens, I must put up a fight!",
    ["Dialogue3120406"]="Forget it, adventurer, pay him no mind. Let's go and bring back that adventurer team. This is our best chance to catch the mobsters.",
    ["Dialogue3120407"]="No, no, no, you can't leave me here alone! Those mobsters are inhuman thieves! If they see me here defenseless, they'll surely come and steal all I have and leave me for dead! This shabby-looking woman here looks quite tough... I mean this warrior—you must stay here and protect me!",
    ["Dialogue3120408"]="(Trisse looks at Elkson with enormous contempt.)\nAlright, alright... Adventurer, be careful out there alone! Go ahead and come back quickly. I'll wait for you here.",
    ["Dialogue3120501"]="We meet again, adventurer! Are you also here to gain some experience? We came here to wipe out the monsters here for our employer, but we didn't expect there to be so many ferocious ones in the desert!",
    ["Dialogue3120502"]="What?! We can't let our employer fall victim to mobsters. We'll go back to the camp immediately, but I must ask if I can trouble you to fetch Kavaski back. He's eliminating the Frilldoras not far from here all by himself. He hates it when we interfere, so he went off to fight alone. I'll go back to protect Elkson with Abessie.",
    ["Dialogue3120601"]="You've impressed me somewhat. The last time I saw you was in Archer Village. Are you here looking for a new opponent?",
    ["Dialogue3120602"]="They would only put off my aim. And Abessie is always muttering on about something or other... I can't take it.",
    ["Dialogue3120603"]="(Kavaski rolls his eyes with disgust.)\nWe are a team of adventurers, not a pack of guard dogs for some caravan. Since when are we responsible for their safety?",
    ["Dialogue3120701"]="You're back at last! I need your help! Those mobsters just sent me a threatening letter. My heavens, how can those low lives be so shameless?",
    ["Dialogue3120702"]="Look, the leader of this mobster gang claims to be a \"G.W.\" in her letter. She says that they already know exactly what our cargo is, and they plan to plunder everything we've got. They're nothing but... but scumbags!",
    ["Dialogue3120703"]="I have two warehouses in the north and the south at both ends of Sograt Desert. All of my assets are in those warehouses. Without them, I'm ruined! Ruined, I tell you!",
    ["Dialogue3120704"]="Money, money, money—that's all you know, isn't it? Just tell us where they are so we can catch the mobsters.",
    ["Dialogue3120705"]="Elkson, there's no need to panic. With our adventurer team on the job, your property will be perfectly safe!",
    ["Dialogue3120706"]="There are only a few people on your adventurer team, and our north and south warehouses are so far apart. Who knows which one the thieves will attack first?! It's over, it's all over, I tell you! My money! Ah—no, my herbs...!",
    ["Dialogue3120707"]="In that case, it would be best for Ygnizem to take our adventure team to the warehouse in the north, and Trisse and the adventurer can check the warehouse in the south. That way, we'll have all bases covered.",
    ["Dialogue3120801"]="Huh? There are so many herbs here. It's so... strange.",
    ["Dialogue3120802"]="The desert is a barren land. The residents here are often forced to endure great hardships, simply because they can't get the medicine they need. So, medicine has always been a precious commodity here in the desert. But look at the caravan's warehouse—there are enough medicinal supplies to keep the entire region in good health!",
    ["Dialogue3120803"]="It's very strange. I must stay and investigate the truth behind all this. Why don't you go to the warehouse in the north and check the situation there with the adventure team?",
    ["Dialogue3120901"]="Adventurer, you're not hurt, are you? Hmm, these two foolish underlings want to steal those herbs from Ygnizem... How naive.",
    ["Dialogue3120902"]="Adventurer, you're just in time. Ygnizem and I were preparing to head south to find you. This warehouse, and the entire caravan, are really quite suspicious.",
    ["Dialogue3120903"]="Look, there's a price list for medicinal materials on that wooden box. If you take a look at it, you'll understand what I'm talking about.",
    ["Dialogue3121001"]="Ordinary people can't afford those kinds of prices. In this barren, impoverished desert wasteland, the prices of vital life-saving medicine shouldn't be so high. Don't you think this caravan's mercenary tactics are a little too much?",
    ["Dialogue3121002"]="What?! So, we must assume that this caravan is in fact an unscrupulous, profiteering organization established to extract as much money as possible from the locals, regardless of their circumstances. It's despicable! Herbs are the scarcest materials in the desert, but they're hoarding them and selling them at sky-high prices! I'll never forgive them.",
    ["Dialogue3121003"]="Don't you think it's at all strange, Ygnizem? The thieves said they'd attack the warehouse and steal all the medicinal materials, but they only sent two men—and the leader didn't even show up.",
    ["Dialogue3121004"]="Oh, no! This must've been a diversion! Let's head back to where the caravan is stationed!",
    ["Dialogue3121101"]="I'm ruined... It's all over...",
    ["Dialogue3121102"]="You! What's the use in you coming back now?! You couldn't even see through such an obvious diversion! How dare you call yourselves an adventure team?! As soon as you left, the mobsters rushed in and took all of my gold and herbs. My goods... All the gold coins I managed to save up...",
    ["Dialogue3121103"]="Quickly come and help, everyone! The caravan members are all injured. I need to heal them as soon as possible, otherwise their lives may be in danger!",
    ["Dialogue3121104"]="Saving them is what's important right now. Kavaski and I will go right away and find the herbs you need and bring them back here.",
    ["Dialogue3121105"]="No problem. We'll stay here and look after them, but we still need to ask these merchants where the mobsters went as soon as possible. The longer we wait, the more difficult it will be to track them down.",
    ["Dialogue3121201"]="Huh...? Southeast? Well done, indeed! You really have a talent for sniffing out clues! Now we have a clear direction to follow! A blue-haired woman... Ferocious looking... Could he be talking about...? It's not too late. Let's get going!",
    ["Dialogue3121301"]="I've been waiting for you for such a long time, and sure enough, you didn't let me down.",
    ["Dialogue3121302"]="Hmph! I heard a while ago that you were helping out that caravan. I knew you'd catch up sooner or later to take back the herbs, so of course, I prepared a little surprise for you. You're lucky the explosives didn't get you, but... Don't act too rashly; you wouldn't want anything to happen to your friends now, would you?",
    ["Dialogue3121401"]="Don't underestimate the Assassins Guild, Goldie!\n(Trisse gets up quietly in the middle of the conversation without you realizing.)",
    ["Dialogue3121402"]="Goldie! Even though you were in the Assassins Guild for such a long time, you seem to have forgotten that you're not the only one who knows how to set up a surprise attack! Adventurer, let's teach her a lesson!",
    ["Dialogue3121403"]="How is that possible? You didn't fall into my trap?! But... no one could've escaped that easily! Who in the world are you?",
    ["Dialogue3121404"]="Hehe! Guild Master Hassan reminded me before I left that setting traps is your specialty, so I came here with that in mind.",
    ["Dialogue3121405"]="You're from the Assassins Guild?!",
    ["Dialogue3121406"]="Enough nonsense! Adventurer, quickly! Don't let this scumbag get away again!",
    ["Dialogue3121501"]="Huh? What are you doing here? You... you guys? What are you trying to do to her?",
    ["Dialogue3121502"]="You know her? She's the head of these mobsters and the defector the Assassins Guild has been pursuing. Why would you have anything to do with her?!",
    ["Dialogue3121503"]="I don't believe it! She's not like that! Not at all! We grew up on the roughest street in Morroc. If it wasn't for Goldie, we slum kids would never have survived. Back then, she'd fight off anyone who gave us trouble, and did whatever she had to do to make sure we didn't go hungry.",
    ["Dialogue3121504"]="It was Goldie's heroic inspiration that gave me the courage to embark on the path to becoming an adventurer. She gave me the confidence to aspire to become the first swordswoman on the continent. I can't believe that Goldie would ever do anything so despicable!",
    ["Dialogue3121505"]="Even if that's true, it doesn't change the fact that Goldie is a mobster leader who loots and plunders wherever she goes. Crime is crime... She has violated the principles of the Assassins Guild and must be punished.",
    ["Dialogue3121506"]="(Trisse lowers her head and ponders for a moment)\nAdventurer, can I ask you something? Please take Goldie back to the Assassins Guild with Ygnizem. I have to ask Elkson about something.",
    ["Dialogue3121601"]="Where are you going? How about you come over to my house for a while?",
    ["Dialogue3121602"]="What?! You're escorting Goldie to the Assassins Guild to receive punishment?! Corel! Hailu! Come quickly! Somebody's taking Goldie away!",
    ["Dialogue3121701"]="No, you can't just take Goldie away! She's the savior of our entire street! We won't let anyone do anything bad to her!",
    ["Dialogue3121702"]="If it wasn't for Goldie, our whole family would've been done for, sleeping in the desert, in the blistering heat... without a hope in the world. Goldie used her savings to find us a place to live.",
    ["Dialogue3121703"]="Goldie sold all her belongings so that the whole street would have food and seeds... All so that we could at least make a living in the desert and not starve to death on the streets.",
    ["Dialogue3121704"]="That's enough...",
    ["Dialogue3121705"]="Goldie has always been like this. She has always cared about everyone in her own way. Even if she is misunderstood, she never tries to explain herself. We must let Guild Master Hassan know of Goldie's true intentions. She must have stolen those medicinal materials for the sake of the people, not for herself.",
    ["Dialogue3121801"]="Goldie! It's Goldie. Where is she going with her new friends?",
    ["Dialogue3121802"]="No, this can't be! Why are you taking Goldie to be punished? Goldie is a good person! You must be bad people! Waaah!",
    ["Dialogue3121803"]="Waaah! Why? Why are they picking on Goldie?! Mom... Some people... Some people are bullying Goldie! Waaah!",
    ["Dialogue3121804"]="Don't cry, we're not bad people... We...",
    ["Dialogue3121901"]="Why are you picking on Goldie like this? She's such a nice person!",
    ["Dialogue3121902"]="These two children... Their mother was seriously ill, and it was Goldie who collected the precious herbs they couldn't afford and sent them to their home. She saved their mother. Goldie is the savior of our entire street. You can't do this to her!",
    ["Dialogue3121903"]="We're all trying to tell you how good Goldie is. She's really not the mobster leader you think she is. Why must you be so stubborn?",
    ["Dialogue3121904"]="This adventurer has promised he'll tell Master Hassan the truth. You don't have to worry. I believe he'll keep his promise.",
    ["Dialogue3122001"]="Goldie, with your intelligence and prowess, you should be a first-class assassin of the Assassins Guild, but you have violated the guild's creed, and your actions have corrupted your virtuous reputation. You have disappointed us all.",
    ["Dialogue3122002"]="Hah! What has a virtuous reputation ever done to help your guild and this city? Do you wish to see a day when your guild members can earn a living without resorting to the vilest cruelty? Do you want to see the good people of Morroc living the lives they deserve? I don't believe you do.",
    ["Dialogue3122003"]="To pursue the way of the assassin is not to pursue a good life.",
    ["Dialogue3122004"]="I'm not talking about pursuing a good life, just striving for the ability to protect those you hold dear. You haven't experienced real hunger or pain, you haven't seen civilians struggling to afford herbs just to survive. Your so-called virtue and reputation are nothing before the realities of life.",
    ["Dialogue3122005"]="Only by forsaking all else can I protect the people and things that really matter to me.\n(Goldie clenches her fists without a trace of hesitation in her eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue3122006"]="No traitor has ever left the Assassins Guild alive.",
    ["Dialogue3122101"]="Wait a minute, Master Hassan!",
    ["Dialogue3122102"]="Trisse? What are you doing back here?",
    ["Dialogue3122103"]="Master, before you deal with Goldie, please listen to the information I've gathered first. The truth is, the merchant group Goldie plundered has held a monopoly on the medicinal materials in the desert for a long time now. They hoarded a huge quantity of herbs and sold them at extortionate prices, and so these scarce medicinal materials were hard to obtain. Many people died as a result.",
    ["Dialogue3122104"]="I believe that although Goldie's methods were questionable, her intentions here good. She wanted to prevent the caravan from making money from the desperation of Morroc's most vulnerable citizens.",
    ["Dialogue3122105"]="You're right! Goldie really is a good person! We just passed by the slums of Morroc, and almost all of the people there tried to stop us from taking Goldie away. She's helped so many people, and even Corel's mother was cured thanks to the herbs she donated. Master Hassan, can you reconsider punishing Goldie for her actions?",
    ["Dialogue3122106"]="(The weight of these words shows on Hassan's face and he stares at Goldie with a grave expression for a moment.)\nGoldie, your betrayal is unforgivable, but since so many people have spoken on your behalf, it is apparent that what you have done for the poor of Morroc was in accordance with the principles of justice. I'll make an exception this time and let you go.",
    ["Dialogue3122107"]="You are no longer a member of the Assassins Guild. From now on, if you do anything that goes against the morals and principles of justice by which we live, no member of the Assassins Guild will show you mercy.",
    ["Dialogue3122201"]="(Injured Merchant 1 curls into a ball, shivering.)\nDon't kill me... Don't kill me...",
    ["Dialogue3122202"]="...D-do you want to know how many people there are in that gang? I didn't see clearly... But I remember one of them, a fierce looking blue-haired woman... Ahh!\n(Injured Merchant 1 covers his head in fear.)",
    ["Dialogue3122301"]="(Injured Merchant 2 covers the wound on his arm in fright.)\nAck! Why won't the blood stop? Am... am I going to die?!",
    ["Dialogue3122302"]="I beg of you... you must find those Mobsters! I remember them retreating to the southeast. Please make sure those treacherous thugs pay with their lives!",
    ["Dialogue3122401"]="(Some grass is scattered on the ground. Upon closer inspection, you can smell a faint aroma of herbs.)",
    ["Dialogue3122501"]="(Some grass is scattered on the ground. Upon closer inspection, you can smell a faint aroma of herbs.)",
    ["Dialogue3122601"]="(Some grass is scattered on the ground. Upon closer inspection, you can smell a faint aroma of herbs.)",
    ["Dialogue3122701"]="(There is a layer of dust on the crate that has been nailed shut. You step closer to take a whiff and catch the smell of moldy herbs.)",
    ["Dialogue3122801"]="(The barrel is very heavy. You open the lid and see that it's filled to the brim with herbs turned medicinal from being pressed in the barrel.)",
    ["Dialogue3130101"]="S-save me! It's terrifying!",
    ["Dialogue3130102"]="A monster! A terrifying monster! I've never seen anything so terrifying before! It must be a monster! It's so scary!",
    ["Dialogue3130103"]="The monster was exceptionally huge! It has the face of a lion, but snakes were growing out of its head. Its body and limbs were like that of a goat. I've never seen such a terrifying monster before. It looks like a demon that came straight from hell.",
    ["Dialogue3130104"]="Fortunately, I was fast enough to outrun it. You better not head northwest. I think that monster has already made it to the <color=#ffe788>northwest district</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3130201"]="Blanche! Your arm is bleeding! Hurry, Jean! Go get some bandages to stop your mother's bleeding! Blanche, hang in there! Stay awake!",
    ["Dialogue3130202"]="Clotting Grass? That's right, a herb like that can definitely stop Blanche's bleeding quickly. Please go gather some <color=#ffe788>Clotting Grass</color>! And be quick! Blanche is in a terrible state!",
    ["Dialogue3130301"]="What a relief. I've got a handle on Blanche's injuries now. The Clotting Grass really lived up to its name. Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3130302"]="I saw a monster chasing down a citizen when I was in the city. In order to help that citizen escape the control of the monster, I had no other choice but to lead it to my home. But by doing so I caused my wife and child to be injured instead. Sigh, I should have thought of a better plan.",
    ["Dialogue3130303"]="Although it is common for vicious monsters to roam Glast Heim, I've never seen a monster of that size and ferocity. If we were to let it be, the citizens here will suffer.",
    ["Dialogue3130304"]="Sigh... How can a group of ordinary people like us who can't even feed our children and are powerless to protect out families <color=#ffe788>fight against</color> such a <color=#ffe788>vicious monster</color>...? But perhaps a powerful adventurer such as you might have a way?",
    ["Dialogue3130401"]="You look like you've been through a fierce battle. Tell me what happened!",
    ["Dialogue3130402"]="This... What should we do? We're in trouble if even you can't subdue this monster. If only a powerful monster researcher can provide us with detailed information. It's beyond difficult for us to defeat this monster since we don't know anything about it right now. There are only refugees and people like me in Glast Heim. There aren't any monster researchers here.",
    ["Dialogue3130403"]="You mean you've thought of a suitable monster researcher? That's great! Why don't you <color=#ffe788>take a photo of the monster</color> and take it to ask the monster researcher for detailed information!",
    ["Dialogue3130501"]="(Norten's eyes widen as he studies the photo carefully.)\nThis... Something like that actually happened? I've never heard of that before. This is strange... This is so strange...",
    ["Dialogue3130502"]="Hmm... You'll understand what I'm saying if you take a look at the book called \"The Monsters of Midgard\" on the shelf over there.",
    ["Dialogue3130601"]="Do you get what I mean now? I never expected this fierce beast that should have died hundreds of years ago to come back to life and wreak havoc on the world. How did this happen? I'm really puzzled by this. It seems that I need to investigate the root cause of the matter. I think I'll need to trouble you after all because I need some <color=#ffe788>Chimera's saliva</color> for testing.",
    ["Dialogue3130701"]="So the corpses of the monsters that the Chimera had gnawed on really were covered in Chimera's saliva. I believe we'll definitely make a discovery.\n(Norten raises the reagent in his hand and seems to be preparing to perform a test.)",
    ["Dialogue3130702"]="(Norten shakes the test tube in his hand and makes a serious expression after carefully observing the liquid in the test tube.)\nThis saliva is filled with an evil aura of darkness, and it seems that it is under some kind of ancient curse. We won't be able to kill the Chimera for good unless we can find the source of the curse and purify it.",
    ["Dialogue3130703"]="That's right, but what I find most peculiar is the way in which the evil curse is triggered. There's always a specific action that triggers such a curse. Adventurer, do you know who was the first person to witness this giant Chimera?",
    ["Dialogue3130704"]="Maybe the unintentional actions of this Hylas triggered the curse afflicting this Chimera, causing it to suddenly come back to life. It seems that you'll have to ask <color=#ffe788>Hylas</color> about this.",
    ["Dialogue3130801"]="Oh my, when I see you, I can't help but remember that creepy monster. I hope I'll never get involved with something that terrifying again.",
    ["Dialogue3130802"]="Something different from usual? I... I think... I don't think there was anything... Oh! If anything, I took <color=#ffe788>some water trickling down from the Goddess Statue</color> and drank it because I was just too thirsty.",
    ["Dialogue3130803"]="In fact, <color=#ffe788>a warning against drinking the water of this city</color> has been circulating among the old inhabitants of Glast Heim for generations, but I was simply too thirsty. I thought it wouldn't be a big deal either.",
    ["Dialogue3130901"]="Adventurer, what is it? Why do you look so upset? Could it be... Has that terrifying monster returned?!!",
    ["Dialogue3130902"]="What!? That terrifying monster was resurrected because I drank some water from this city? This... This... This is all my fault. I should have heeded the warning of my predecessors. It's all my fault... Sigh... Is there a way to lift the curse?",
    ["Dialogue3130903"]="Is my blood all you need to end that monster? Come on, <color=#ffe788>collect</color> my <color=#ffe788>blood</color> then. I don't want to bear the sin of resurrecting this monster and getting the innocents of the city killed. This blood is the price I must pay for my indiscretion.",
    ["Dialogue3131001"]="I must personally confirm that this terrifying monster is dead. I really didn't expect that I would cause so much trouble by ignoring the warning of my predecessors. Thank you so much this time. Your composure and resourcefulness is the reason this problem was resolved without a hitch.",
    ["Dialogue3131002"]="I just never expected such a terrible curse would be left on the Goddess Statue that guards this land. Looks like we really shouldn't ignore the warnings of our predecessors, or there's no telling what disasters might be caused.",
    ["Dialogue3131101"]="(There are footprints of a four-legged creature on the ground. Upon closer observation, the prints of its front feet look like they were made with beast claws, but the prints of its rear feet look like that of sheep's hooves...)",
    ["Dialogue3131201"]="(The footprints continue forward into the distance. For some reason, these seem larger than the previous ones...)",
    ["Dialogue3131301"]="(Fresh dirt is scattered around the footprints. It looks like these were just formed...)",
    ["Dialogue3131401"]="(The Goddess Statue emits a strange aura, and there are some unusual nicks on its base. However, it is difficult to see them in any detail as they are obscured by a thick layer of dust...)",
    ["Dialogue3131501"]="(As the layers of dust gradually fall off, a paragraph of text appears—)",
    ["Dialogue3131502"]="I have left a curse here:\nThe people of Glast Heim and their descendants must never touch the city's water source, or else a beast most brutal will be resurrected and destroy everything. The only way to stop this is to have the blood of the one who triggered the curse flow under my feet...",
    ["Dialogue3131601"]="Uh...... Did it die?",
    ["Dialogue3140101"]="This situation is indeed unusual. It seems likely that the Shadow Hunters are active again.",
    ["Dialogue3140102"]="Oh, it's you, Adventurer. You arrived at just the right time. Maybe you'll be able to help us with your ingenuity. Recently, two Eden Group members who went out for archaeological activities have disappeared one after the other. It's been three days now. We haven't been able to get in touch with them even though we've tried many methods.",
    ["Dialogue3140103"]="We unanimously agree that the Shadow Hunters may be active again.",
    ["Dialogue3140104"]="The Shadow Hunters are an assassin organization that exclusively tracks and hunts Eden Group members. Countless Eden Group members have died by their hands in the past few decades. I've been tracking this mysterious organization since I joined the Paladins. However, I'll need to check the scene before I can confirm whether the Shadow Hunters really are responsible for this incident.",
    ["Dialogue3140105"]="The last Eden Group member to disappear was Sarence, who was originally responsible for the archaeological excavations in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest area of Glast Heim</color>. I think you can investigate the site. Maybe you'll find something there.",
    ["Dialogue3140201"]="This shovel should belong to Sarence, the missing Eden Group member. The dirt on this shovel is dry, and it looks like the shovel has been left here for several days. Hmm... It looks like...",
    ["Dialogue3140202"]="I'm not sure yet, Adventurer. Can you get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloudy Alcohol Reagents</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carats</color>? This is vital for my next investigation.",
    ["Dialogue3140301"]="You're quite fast! Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>splash the Cloudy Alcohol Reagents around this pointy shovel</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3140401"]="Fortunately, it seems that we aren't too late.",
    ["Dialogue3140402"]="I inspected the traces at the scene carefully while you were away. Although the current evidence and signs indicate that the Shadow Hunters are responsible for the disappearance of the missing Eden Group members, I didn't find any blood or signs of fighting around here. This means that the Shadow Hunters have only abducted the Eden Group members, and we still have a chance to rescue them.",
    ["Dialogue3140403"]="No traces of human footprints were found by the several reagent tests we performed earlier. As far as I know, only the Shadow Hunters know such superb track concealment techniques. Well, we face a big problem now...",
    ["Dialogue3140404"]="We need to find where the Eden Group members are trapped without having any clues as to their whereabouts. I mean, we can't even find a single footprint. It'll be really difficult to track down the Shadow Hunters.",
    ["Dialogue3140405"]="Wear a disguise? Do you mean... Do you want to disguise yourself as an Eden Group member and lure out the Shadow Hunters? Hmm... I admit that this is a good idea, but it's too dangerous for you because you've never dealt with the Shadow Hunters before. It'll be more appropriate for me to do it.",
    ["Dialogue3140406"]="Hold your horses, I have something more important that I need your help with. Time is of the essence, so we must <color=#CA2E0AFF>act separately. I'll return to ask Rockley for an old worn-out Eden Group uniform and put it on. Meanwhile, you'll find a way to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Monster Saliva and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soft Water Weeds. You better get going.",
    ["Dialogue3140501"]="I've been waiting for you for a long time now! As planned, the Shadow Hunters have fallen for our trap. Master Seyren has been abducted and taken to the place where all the Eden Group members are imprisoned. My master secretly released me to guide you there.",
    ["Dialogue3140502"]="I'm not any old pet! I'm my master's important comrade-in-arms, so you better not look down on me! Follow me!",
    ["Dialogue3140601"]="Huh? Their injuries look quite serious, so we must find a way to treat them first. Look at him. He looks like he can't make any sounds, maybe his vocal cords have been damaged.",
    ["Dialogue3140601702"]="I don't know what happened either. After that terrible man captured me, he used all sorts of cruel methods to interrogate me about the whereabouts of a document. That man is really terrifying. I fainted when he tortured me, and I still have no idea what document he was referring to. Ouch... my back... I'm sorry, can you take a look at my back for me? I feel an inexplicable pain there.",
    ["Dialogue3140602"]="Let me think... Aha! I know, maybe the grass called Clatterweed that loves dark places can be used to treat his vocal cords. The environment here is dark and humid, so we might be able to find some here.",
    ["Dialogue3140701"]="Ahem... T-thank you. I can finally speak again. It's already been several days since I lost my voice.",
    ["Dialogue3140801"]="Ah... OUCH! It hurts really badly! Can anybody help me... Ouch...",
    ["Dialogue3140802"]="His arm seems to have been severely burned. We urgently need a cold compress for a wound this big. Fetch some water from the Lionheart Pool. His arm will be done for if we don't treat it now.",
    ["Dialogue3140901"]="Oww... T-thank you. This water you brought me has finally given me some brief respite from the pain of my suffering...",
    ["Dialogue3140902"]="My back?",
    ["Dialogue3140903"]="\"Arsonists should also experience the agony of burns\"? I have absolutely no idea what this terrible kidnapper was talking about. He kept asking me about some document, but I had never heard of the document he asked me about, so he tried everything he could to interrogate me, and tortured me until I ended up like this.",
    ["Dialogue3140904"]="What? He tortured you? I hope my master will be okay!",
    ["Dialogue3141001"]="I can't find Master Seyren anywhere around here. How strange! I remember that he was obviously locked up here when I left...",
    ["Dialogue3141002"]="Your master? Are you looking for someone?",
    ["Dialogue3141003"]="Oh, you're referring to the last person who was captured. I think he said he knew where the document was, so the people who abducted us forced him to go and search for it. He's your friend?",
    ["Dialogue3141004"]="My master must have said that on purpose to get rid of the Shadow Hunters and give us the chance to rescue everyone!",
    ["Dialogue3141005"]="Calm down first. We can't act rashly, or else we will fail to save my master and might end up delivering ourselves into the hands of the Shadow Hunters instead. Hmm... Let me see... Apply the Fresh Monster Saliva from before all over your body.",
    ["Dialogue3141101"]="Yes, this saliva really can disguise the human scent on your body. But that won't be enough. Take the Soft Water Weeds you collected earlier and fasten them to the soles of your shoes.",
    ["Dialogue3141201"]="Now take a few steps. Very good, these water weeds have eliminated the sound of your footsteps.",
    ["Dialogue3141202"]="You probably don't know this. The Shadow Hunters are all blind, but that's exactly why their sense of smell and hearing is very sensitive. You'll need to completely conceal the human scent on you and the sound of your footsteps to avoid their detection and not be discovered.",
    ["Dialogue3141203"]="Actually, I sensed a familiar aura when I was examining things just now. Maybe it was a clue left by my master...",
    ["Dialogue3141301"]="Aha! Given my master's wisdom, I just knew he would give us some clues! Yes! We'll definitely be able to find them now that we have this Directional Leaf.",
    ["Dialogue3141302"]="The Directional Leaf is a leaf that falls from a special tree in my hometown. As it is colorless and odorless, but fluorescent at the same time, there's a legend in the forest that one will be able to find the way home by following the Directional Leaf. Very few people know of this legend. I believe my master must have left us this clue. You'll definitely find my master if you follow these leaves!",
    ["Dialogue3141401"]="You don't have to do this. I believe he is hired by someone who is compelling him to act in this way.",
    ["Dialogue3141402"]="Hmph... Enough of your nonsense. You are of no value to me since you don't know the whereabouts of the document. I was careless to fall into your hands. Just do it.",
    ["Dialogue3141403"]="I have no intention to kill you. Look, this is the remains of the chip I just removed from your neck. I have already destroyed it.",
    ["Dialogue3141404"]="You aren't from the Eden Group?",
    ["Dialogue3141405"]="I'm sorry for deceiving you, but I had no other way to save everyone.",
    ["Dialogue3141501"]="Yes, I am not a member of the Eden Group.\n(Seyren takes off the Eden Group Uniform as he speaks, causing his suit of armor to make clanging sounds.)",
    ["Dialogue3141502"]="You're a knight?",
    ["Dialogue3141503"]="(Seyren pauses for a moment before smiling gently.)\nAs expected of a Shadow Hunter. You are able to guess my identity just by hearing the sound of my armor. Yes, I am a crusader, and my objective is to protect the members of the Eden Group and Shadow Hunters like you.",
    ["Dialogue3141504"]="Protect us? The Shadow Hunters? Hmph... What a joke? Aren't you here to hunt down the Shadow Hunters?",
    ["Dialogue3141505"]="This is not my first time seeing the chip in my hands. I have tracked and encountered many Shadow Hunters, and the chip at their necks would suddenly explode and kill them whenever I was about to capture them.",
    ["Dialogue3141506"]="I'm afraid this chip is meant to monitor the whereabouts of these Shadow Hunters, as well as to kill them remotely in crucial moments to prevent them from falling into enemy hands and leaking secrets. Are you going to remain so blindly loyal to an employer who doesn't take your life seriously?",
    ["Dialogue3141507"]="Hmph!\n(Randle snorts coldly, his eyes revealing disdain and indifference.)",
    ["Dialogue3141508"]="Your employer made your group of Shadow Hunters search for the document, but at the same time, they gouged out your eyes to prevent you from peeping at the secrets of the document. Is it really worth it to work yourself to the bone for an employer who distrusts you to such an extent and only treats you like a tool?",
    ["Dialogue3141509"]="So what? All humans exploit one another! Is there a better choice for an orphan like me?",
    ["Dialogue3141510"]="(Seyren shakes his head disappointedly.)\nEverybody has options as long as they are still alive. You can always choose how you want to live your life. I'm offering you the opportunity to live another life.",
    ["Dialogue3141511"]="Although I must take you back to the capital for trial because you tortured the Eden Group members, since you did not kill any of them, I will do my best to ensure you get conscripted to atone for your crimes.",
    ["Dialogue3141512"]="Hah! You sure are interesting. If you don't kill me now, aren't you worried that I'll return to the Shadow Hunters and return to my old ways after I finish my sentence? When that happens... I'll get my revenge against all of you!",
    ["Dialogue3141513"]="Haha, well... Let's just wait and see.\n(Seyren smiles brightly.)",
    ["Dialogue3141601"]="(The soil on the Pointy Shovel has already dried up. Other than that, there are no other suspicious objects or signs nearby...)",
    ["Dialogue3141701"]="(After lifting Laforet's coat, you see a line of words that have been carved onto his back with a sharp blade—\n\"Thieves should also experience the pain of loss\".)",
    ["Dialogue3141801"]="(Leaves are scattered all over the ground like fireflies gathered together, radiating a pleasing and soothing glow...)",
    ["Dialogue3150101"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>That's impossible. Other than the members of the Institute, no one else can do that... unless... unless...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3150102"]="(Fulkyn lowers his head and mutters to himself. He doesn't seem to have noticed your arrival at all.)\nNo, that's not necessarily the case. A person who studied Vanidu's second law of space-time at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Institute</color> should be able to quietly collect the power left in rifts between dimensions by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demotima</color> without alerting me, to replace...",
    ["Dialogue3150103"]="...Be quiet! I'm sorting out my thoughts! If you interrupt me now, I'll have to recalculate everything again from the 5,412th inference!\n(He slaps your hand with a resounding slap. You look at the swollen back of your hand and decide to play a prank on Fulkyn.)",
    ["Dialogue3150104"]="I already told you to be—<size=24>What?!!!</size>\n(Fulkyn screams and subconsciously covers his pockets with both hands, making him look rather ludicrous.)",
    ["Dialogue3150105"]="My Sands... Hold on, did you just play a prank on me?\n(The young man who has been immersed in his own world finally turns his head and glares at you.)\nAdventurer! How can you be in the mood to play a prank at such a critical moment!",
    ["Dialogue3150106"]="I'm telling you now that things are looking bad! According to my deductions based on the second law of space-time and discarding the threshold that doesn't meet the quadrant rule, the only result left is a non-prime number! Do you know what that means? It means that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>quantum force in a high-dimensional space is having a backflow phenomenon</color>. If we don't intervene as soon as possible...",
    ["Dialogue3150107"]="What I mean is... Sigh, forget it, you should just <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look at this first</color>. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> next to me will tell you the answer.",
    ["Dialogue3150201"]="Do you understand now, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3150202"]="That's right! Since this instrument is a positioning system manufactured in strict compliance with traceability rules, each coordinate has a unique value in its database. Once it starts sounding the alarm that a critical point is approached, it means there is a high probability that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>time flow has been displaced at multiple points</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3150203"]="It means that the history of Glast Heim in the year AW231 has been invaded! According to my experience, this is by no means normal time travel, and the intruder does not have any pure intentions.",
    ["Dialogue3150204"]="For example, the intruder may have the intention to tamper with history as we know it to cause a parallel shift. If we don't do anything about this, our existence may also be affected. In the worst case scenario, time-space will mistake us for something that needs to be automatically corrected and will delete us along with the displaced data.",
    ["Dialogue3150205"]="It'll be worse than disappearing, Adventurer. If space-time identifies us as something unnecessary, we will be removed like a lesion just like this! *Crack*\n(Fulkyn raises his hand and places it against his neck horizontally, then slices viciously from the left to the right!)",
    ["Dialogue3150206"]="Our only option now is to go back to the year AW231 and find the intruder who is trying to tamper with history. If necessary, I may need to use... Oh... Oh no! I'm out of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tear Spirits</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3150207"]="Tear Spirits are energy crystals formed from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>last teardrop left behind by a pure soul before dying</color>. Because it contains the thoughts of the deceased, just like the Sands of Time, it is a precious item that can be used to intervene with time-space. I need it to activate many of my instruments... but unfortunately, I've used all the Tear Spirits I collected.",
    ["Dialogue3150208"]="...Are you referring to the mysterious fountain water in the Quiet Garden? Indeed, that's where the goddess once...\nOkay! Can you please go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spring of Quiet</color> and look for some? Don't tarry, Adventurer, as we don't have much time.",
    ["Dialogue3150301"]="Very good, it seems that the Goddess of Luck is on our side this time.\n(Fulkyn takes the flickering orb of light from your hand and puts it into the magical instrument he carries with him.)",
    ["Dialogue3150302"]="It's one of my newest inventions. When it is used with the Sands of Time, it can <color=#CA2E0AFF>control the flow of time in space nodes</color>. I like to use this against those... scoundrels who don't play fair. Hmph!\n(Fulkyn squints and snorts twice, making his bitter hatred obvious to all.)",
    ["Dialogue3150303"]="Adventurer, I must travel to the year AW231 now to find the intruder. I'm not sure of my chances either since I've never set foot in that time-space before...",
    ["Dialogue3150304"]="(Fulkyn nods.)\nI was right about you, Adventurer. Since you've been to that time-space before, I'm certain you'll be able to help me find the intruder sooner. Okay, pick up the Sands of Time. We'll leave now.",
    ["Dialogue3150401"]="Welcome to the year AW231, Adventurer.\n(Fulkyn bends down and salutes you in a rather pretentious manner.)",
    ["Dialogue3150402"]="It doesn't look like a place that is full of happiness, right?\n(Fulkyn shrugs. You follow his gaze and look at your surroundings. You see devastation all around you and find it unbearable.)",
    ["Dialogue3150403"]="Unfortunately, we don't have time to let you experience the profound weight of history right now. If we don't find the intruder as soon as possible, even this terrible history will disappear completely. Do you remember the hint given by the Mysterious Device? The pointer pointed at the east, indicating that the source of the time-space displacement is in that direction.",
    ["Dialogue3150404"]="Yes, that was the residence of King Schmidt... Although that unprecedented battle should have ended by this current point in time, we should still be careful, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3150501"]="We have to catch up, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3150502"]="That's a Demotima, a guardian responsible for defending the order of time and space. Generally speaking, they won't attack humans without provocation unless...",
    ["Dialogue3150503"]="(Fulkyn nods solemnly.)\nDemotima only enter this aggressive state of alert when the order of time and space has been provoked. They will continue to search for people who don't belong to the current time-space until all time travelers are eliminated. In other words...",
    ["Dialogue3150504"]="Yes, we just need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow it</color> to find the intruder who is attempting to alter history!",
    ["Dialogue3150601"]="Shush... Listen, Adventurer.\n(Fulkyn puts his index finger against his mouth and motions for you to be silent.)",
    ["Dialogue3150602"]="(Fulkyn nods and draws your attention to the nearby river with his eyes, lowering his voice.)\nThe sound is coming from over there... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Let's go take a look</color>. Remember to tread lightly, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3150701"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>How could it be... Is it because I didn't promise to help him that's why he...?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3150702"]="...I'm not sure yet, but the blond sage is called Barr Venter, and he is an old acquaintance of mine... It's possible that the reason he has come here is related to me. I must figure out the causality of this situation.",
    ["Dialogue3150703"]="Don't worry. No matter what happens, my most important mission is to maintain the stability and order of time and space. I won't confuse it with my personal affairs. It's just that it isn't convenient for me to make an appearance in this situation... Can you mediate the matter between these two people? I reassure you that I'll be following you the whole time and will use my device to stop time at critical moments.",
    ["Dialogue3150704"]="...Oh no!\nLook over there, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3150801"]="Do you see it? The Clock Tower Manager is the evidence.\n(Barr Venter raises his head, and his arrogant posture makes him look like a god looking down on the common people.)",
    ["Dialogue3150802"]="...How boring.",
    ["Dialogue3150803"]="(Squints)\nSuch a mechanical product requires science and technology that greatly exceeds your understanding. Isn't this enough to prove what I'm saying?",
    ["Dialogue3150804"]="...So what?",
    ["Dialogue3150805"]="<size=24>So you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>give up on searching for Morroc</color>!!!</size>\nIf you don't, you... no, it won't be just you—you and your companions are heading toward certain death!",
    ["Dialogue3150806"]="(Thanatos sneers.)\nHah... Are you a \"prophet\" from the future? You look more like a follower of the Demon King who has come with a hideous monster to ask me to stop searching for Morroc. Could it be that you're in cahoots with Morroc?",
    ["Dialogue3150807"]="You stubborn fool!\nWhy are you reluctant to choose another path now that you know how this path ends? This might be your only chance to change your destiny!",
    ["Dialogue3150808"]="Do all \"prophets\" have so much spare time on their hands? They even have the time to interfere in other people's lives?\nWhat's more, what does my destiny have to do with you? This is my own choice, and I will bear the consequences myself.",
    ["Dialogue3150809"]="But there are some things that you can't do alone!\nI'll ask you one last time. Are you willing to give up on hunting Morroc?!",
    ["Dialogue3150810"]="Never! I must kill Morroc!",
    ["Dialogue3150811"]="...Very well. I gave you a chance, Thanatos.\n(Barr Venter's expression becomes calm after his rage subsides, and he even smiles wryly.)\nIt's now time for you to pay the price.",
    ["Dialogue3150812"]="What can you do to me? You can't beat me with your swordsmanship. Or will you—",
    ["Dialogue3150813"]="No, none of that. I just want to ask you if you would say those exact same words as before if the price you need to pay is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>life of the most important person to you</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3150814"]="(Frowns)\nWhat do you mean... Hold... Hold on, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lucci</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3150815"]="(Barr Venter laughs and seems to take pity on him like a god.)\nYou want to know the answer? Then go and see for yourself. I hope you won't regret it, Thanatos.",
    ["Dialogue3150901"]="Tsk...! That darned \"prophet\"!\n(Thanatos seems to be infuriated. He punches the wall hard, causing a layer of gray dust to fall off the mottled wall.)",
    ["Dialogue3150902"]="He must have taken Lucci. How dare he lay a hand on Lucci...",
    ["Dialogue3150903"]="What's that...?\n(Thanatos looks in the direction you are pointing, and his eyes light up instantly when he sees <color=#CA2E0AFF>the thing on the tree</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue3151001"]="...There can be no mistake. This is Lucci's manteau. There are also some claw marks. These marks are way too deep in the soil. It's almost like something heavy was being carried...",
    ["Dialogue3151002"]="(Thanatos nods.)\nThese <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange marks</color> outside the door weren't here when I left... There is no doubt that this is related to Lucci's disappearance.",
    ["Dialogue3151003"]="...You're saying that these marks are so obvious that it seems like a trap instead?\n(Thanatos lowers his eyes and seems to be thinking, but raises his head again soon.)\nNo... I must go.",
    ["Dialogue3151004"]="Although what you said is reasonable, this concerns Lucci's safety... This is my only clue, so I can't give up on it.\n(The young man squeezes the sword in his hand with a determined look on his face.)\nIf this really is a trap, then I will smash through it and rescue Lucci.",
    ["Dialogue3151101"]="*Coughs* Thanatos... I...\n(Lucci covers her nose and mouth, but the sound of sporadic coughing escapes from between her fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue3151102"]="...Are you hurt? Where does it hurt?",
    ["Dialogue3151103"]="I... I'm fine... I'm just... *Coughs*",
    ["Dialogue3151104"]="I remember there's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fuchsia-colored herb</color> around here that can be used to treat wounds. Wait for me while I go—Lucci?\n(Thanatos stops while getting up. When you follow his surprised gaze, you see that Lucci has reached out to quietly tug at Thanatos' clothes.)",
    ["Dialogue3151105"]="(Thanatos looks at how weak Lucci is and nods after staying silent for a long time.)\n...I understand. Please pick some herbs that can be used to treat wounds. I'll guard her here.",
    ["Dialogue3151201"]="Okay, Lucci. Can you tell me where you've been hurt?\n(Thanatos puts one arm around Lucci's shoulders to help her up.)",
    ["Dialogue3151202"]="Thanatos, I...\n(Lucci raises her head and glances at Thanatos like she wants to say something, but swallows her words.)",
    ["Dialogue3151203"]="...What's wrong?",
    ["Dialogue3151204"]="...*Sobs*\n(Lucci doesn't reply him. She lowers her head and whimpers quietly.)\nI want to... go home...",
    ["Dialogue3151205"]="...What did you say?",
    ["Dialogue3151206"]="...I said I want to go home.\n(Lucci suddenly raises her head. Glistening tears escape from her beautiful eyes and roll down her cheeks like pearls.)\nPlease! Thanatos, take me home!",
    ["Dialogue3151207"]="Forget about Morroc! Let's return to our hometown! Don't you miss the days of the past? We didn't need to run around everywhere and wear ourselves out back then, and we didn't need to fight or get hurt either!",
    ["Dialogue3151208"]="Just like before, we can go to the yard and plant—\n(The young lady's voice stops abruptly because she sees Thanatos' cold and indifferent expression. He is looking into Lucci's eyes like she has absolutely nothing to do with him.)",
    ["Dialogue3151209"]="You... Don't you want to return home, Thanatos?\n(Lucci stares at the person in front of her. Thanatos' silence makes the light in her eyes dim like a setting sun sinking into the horizon.)",
    ["Dialogue3151210"]="...This doesn't sound like something you would say, Lucci.",
    ["Dialogue3151211"]="I just... I just feel tired...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Why... Why won't you say yes? Thanatos... You know I'm—</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3151301"]="As rumored, Thanatos is a selfish and cold-blooded swordsman...\n(Barr Venter appears from the darkness. He picks up the dagger dropped by the mechanical magic doll and plays with it.)\nSure enough... I must kill you to put an end to everything.",
    ["Dialogue3151302"]="...It's you. Where is Lucci? What did you do to her?",
    ["Dialogue3151303"]="(Barr Venter bursts into laughter after hearing his words.)\nWhat? Do you actually care about the life and death of your companions? You weren't moved at all when \"Lucci\" cried and begged you to take her home. I thought that the great swordsman only cared about Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue3151304"]="...There's no way Lucci would say those things to me. Someone like you cannot understand what we pursue.",
    ["Dialogue3151305"]="Is that so? But you actually... you've never turned around to take a good look at Lucci, right?\n(The blond sage walks closer to the wounded swordsman. He smiles as he walks forward at a casual pace, but every word that comes out of his mouth is like the whispers of the devil.)",
    ["Dialogue3151306"]="How can you be so certain that... that isn't what the real Lucci thinks?",
    ["Dialogue3151307"]="Shut up! You liar! I will not be fooled by you!",
    ["Dialogue3151308"]="That person who fights by your side, she has been following you this whole time without any complaints no matter what difficulties she has encountered. She has even regarded your pursuit as her own dream... But you know the truth, don't you? You know that she hides her injuries from you whenever she gets hurt and dresses her wounds in secret. Is it because you're afraid that you deliberately pretend not to notice? Are you worried that if you show her any concern, she will say—",
    ["Dialogue3151309"]="<size=24>I told you to shut up!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3151310"]="...Just admit it, Thanatos. You don't know Lucci as well as you think.\n(Barr Venter stops and looks down contemptuously at Thanatos who is half-kneeling on the ground.)\nI'll consider sparing you if you give up on hunting Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue3151311"]="...What if I say no?",
    ["Dialogue3151312"]="Oh...? Do you think you're in the position to say that?\n(Barr Venter raises the dagger again. This time, he points the blade at Thanatos' chest.)\nThis... is why I hate boorish fools who don't use their brains.",
    ["Dialogue3151313"]="(Thanatos frowns and looks down at his chest. The wound he suffered when the dagger sliced through his clothes starts to ache faintly.)\nCould it be that you... Argh!",
    ["Dialogue3151314"]="(The swordsman with one knee on the ground tries to get up several times but fails every time.)\nYou... You laced your dagger with poison? How despicable!",
    ["Dialogue3151315"]="I'm not you. In my plans... people never get a second chance.\n(Barr Venter raises the dagger in his hand up high and looks at Thanatos condescendingly. The wry smile fades from his face, leaving nothing but coldness and arrogance.)\nNow, please... die for me.",
    ["Dialogue3151401"]="As you can see, Adventurer, I have stopped the flow of time in this space because Thanatos cannot die yet.",
    ["Dialogue3151402"]="(Fulkyn shakes his head to tell you to stop asking questions.)\nThis device can only be used for a limited time. We must find a way to correct the flow of history before the energy of the Tear Spirits is exhausted.",
    ["Dialogue3151403"]="First of all, we must find a way to restore Thanatos' ability to move...\n(Fulkyn leans down and observes Thanatos' wound carefully.)\n...I see.",
    ["Dialogue3151404"]="Adventurer, l want you to look for a monster called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sageworm</color> and collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gold Dew</color> you'll find on them. This is a powerful antidote that should relieve Thanatos' symptoms.",
    ["Dialogue3151501"]="You returned at just the right time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3151502"]="As you can see, I swapped their positions and put the dagger in Thanatos' hands. Now, you just need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply the Gold Dew on Thanatos' wound</color> to relieve the paralysis of his body. After that, we just need to restart the flow of time...",
    ["Dialogue3151503"]="...We have no other choice, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3151601"]="Okay, Adventurer, it's time to put an end to this farce.",
    ["Dialogue3151701"]="Don't kill him, Thanatos!",
    ["Dialogue3151702"]="(Thanatos is very surprised when he sees Lucci running over from a distance.)\n...Lucci?! You're alright?!",
    ["Dialogue3151703"]="I'm fine! Thanatos!\nThis person... This person didn't hurt me. He just knocked me out and locked me in a room... He didn't mean to harm me, so please don't kill him, okay?",
    ["Dialogue3151704"]="(Frowns)\nBut...",
    ["Dialogue3151705"]="I'm begging you, Thanatos! Although I don't know why he did this, maybe he... What if he has his difficulties?\n(Lucci bows her head and glances at Barr Venter with a strange emotion in her eyes.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I can't help thinking that...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3151706"]="(Thanatos looks at Lucci's pleading expression and hesitates. After a moment, he draws his sword.)\nWell... I'll let him go as long as he promises not to get in our way.",
    ["Dialogue3151707"]="(A silver light flashes as the sword stops next to Barr Venter's neck. Thanatos looks down at him coldly and arrogantly just like how he looked him earlier.)\nWhat's your answer, \"prophet\"?",
    ["Dialogue3151708"]="...Fine.\n(Barr Venter glances at Lucci and then nods. Maybe you saw wrong, but you get the feeling that his lips had curled into a smile...)",
    ["Dialogue3151709"]="...Remember what you said today. Don't show up in front of us again, or else I won't give you any chance to defend yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3151801"]="It really is you, Fulkyn. I knew that no one could do something like this other than you.",
    ["Dialogue3151802"]="...When you decided to interfere with history, you should have expected that I will definitely stop you. In fact, you could even say that I saved you because anyone who tries to violate the rules of time-space will be punished. If we didn't arrive in time and stop the crazed Demotima, do you think you could plot against Thanatos so leisurely? Those monsters would have torn you to pieces ages ago, Barr Venter!",
    ["Dialogue3151803"]="...I should be grateful to you for dealing with the Demotima for me, but that doesn't change the fact that we have are on opposite sides. Fulkyn, we were no longer companions from the moment you refused to help me.",
    ["Dialogue3151804"]="Barr Venter!\n(Fulkyn's voice becomes louder. He steps forward and grabs Barr Venter by the collar.)",
    ["Dialogue3151805"]="You've already violated the rules of the Institute by activating the Clock Tower without authorization! You even used the Demotima to travel through time in an attempt to change history! Do you know the consequences of your actions? Everyone's data will be changed! Everyone! Even you!",
    ["Dialogue3151806"]="...Fulkyn, don't forget that I was once a member of the Institute. I know just as much as you about the \"rules\". So what? You take the \"rules\" as your creed, whereas I have something more important to me. In any case... Doesn't your research also subvert traditional understandings?",
    ["Dialogue3151807"]="(Barr Venter pries Fulkyn's hand loose. He smoothens his collar indifferently and even dusts off some non-existent dust.)\nYou see, if rules are never broken, humans will never make progress.",
    ["Dialogue3151808"]="You... Why are you...\n(Fulkyn takes two steps back and shakes his head.)\nNo, you won't tell me why you're doing this. Moreover, the reason isn't important anyway.",
    ["Dialogue3151809"]="—No matter what reason you have, history should never be changed. If you refuse to see the error of your ways... then I won't show you any mercy the next time we meet.",
    ["Dialogue3151810"]="...Right back at you.\n(Barr Venter bends over and bows to Fulkyn.)\nGoodbye, Professor Fulkyn. I hope we... never meet again.",
    ["Dialogue3151811"]="...It's time to go back, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Give me the Sands of Time</color>.\n(Fulkyn takes one last look at Barr Venter. His eyes make a complicated expression that reveals regret, sorrow, grievance... and a warning that cannot be ignored.)\nBarr Venter... I hope you behave yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3151901"]="...Okay, we've returned safely. Thank you for your assistance, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3151902"]="Do you want to ask about my relationship with Barr Venter? I'm sorry... It's a long and complicated story, so forgive me for not being able to tell you it now. You'll know the whole truth one day.",
    ["Dialogue3151903"]="People who try to change the past definitely have some sort of obsession in their heart. On the other hand, what obsession is powerful enough to compel a person to even overthrow the proof of their existence? You must know that although time has infinite possibilities, for us, our own existence is the truth. No one can predict the consequences of wanton tampering with established reality. In other words, doing so may even threaten one's own existence.",
    ["Dialogue3151904"]="...Yet Barr Venter already knew and understood this \"rule\" before he made his mind to change the past... He won't give up so easily.",
    ["Dialogue3151905"]="Exactly... Why? I want to know the answer too.\n(Fulkyn sighs, and you can see how exhausted he is from his expression.)",
    ["Dialogue3151906"]="But even if I know the reason... Will I be able to persuade him to give up... \n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>After all, \"humans\" are very limited in what they can do...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3151907"]="No... It isn't necessary to console me, Adventurer. Ever since... Ever since... I've decided long ago that I'll never waver no matter what happens. The rules of time must not be violated. If anyone tries to tamper with history... I'll give them the punishment they deserve.",
    ["Dialogue3151908"]="...Maybe you're right. If one day...\n(Fulkyn glances at you and laughs suddenly.)\nAdventurer, I won't show any mercy even if it's you.",
    ["Dialogue3151909"]="Hahaha, that would be best. After all...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I don't want to... become enemies with the successor of Odin's bloodline.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3152001"]="(The instrument flashes with a dazzling red light as the alert alarm sounds endlessly. Upon closer inspection, you see that the pointer at the top of the instrument is trembling and pointing to the east. The numbers \"231\" are faintly visible on the display screen at the bottom...)",
    ["Dialogue3152101"]="...I already told you. You must give up on hunting the Demon King Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue3152102"]="Is that why you lured me over here?",
    ["Dialogue3152103"]="You'll only lose something more important to you if you continue your foolish hunt.",
    ["Dialogue3152104"]="Isn't it even more foolish to trust the words of a madman who claims to be a \"prophet\"?",
    ["Dialogue3152201"]="(A tattered piece of black cloth hangs on the branch. Upon closer inspection, you see several sets of monster claw marks on the gray bricks under the tree...)",
    ["Dialogue3152301"]="(A series of monster claw marks are deeply imprinted on the gray bricks. You even find a few strands of blue hair on the ground along the direction of the claw marks...)",
    ["Dialogue3152401"]="(The monster's claw marks extend all the way to the steps and disappear in front of the wooden door.)",
    ["Dialogue3152501"]="(The gate guard salutes you with respect — along with a cautious face)\nAllow me to have a quick word, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3152502"]="Indeed it is. A message from Commander Bohr just got around. He said that... the case you investigated earlier has made significant progress, and hopes you can visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force training grounds</color> upon receiving this message. Commander Bohr will be waiting for you there.",
    ["Dialogue3152601"]="... You're here, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3152602"]="I believe you already know why I contacted you. In fact, we've just received new information regarding His Majesty's whereabouts... As for further details, you can hear it from the Defense Force themselves. Peddy, you're up.\n(Bohr gestured to the soldier beside him, who then knowingly took a step forward)",
    ["Dialogue3152603"]="Yes Commander Bohr!",
    ["Dialogue3152701"]="The information I have begins with a group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>the outsider</color> who left via the Prontera South Gate not long ago. After receiving orders from Commander Bohr, the Defense Force set up a barrier at the Prontera South Gate, and carefully checked all the people and their goods passing through with success, until said group appeared...",
    ["Dialogue3152702"]="(Upon seeing your look of concentration, the soldier continued talking)\nAnyway, just as I was routinely stopping them and informing them that their cargo needed to be checked, they...",
    ["Dialogue3152703"]="...... Ah, you have other important business to attend to?\nIf so, then you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>quickly go and come back</color>! I'll be <color=#CA2E0AFF>right here waiting</color>for you!",
    ["Dialogue3152801"]="... You have no right to stop us, soldier.",
    ["Dialogue3152802"]="Sorry, gentlemen. Although it was sudden, we still must follow Commander Bohr's orders to check all goods and people passing through Prontera before letting them through. So please, cooperate with us and wait here while we check.",
    ["Dialogue3152803"]="Like I said before, <size=26>you have no right to stop us, soldier!</size>\nWe are from the Church-state, and we're here to exchange tokens between the two countries and bring them back. If you delay us, you will cause a feud between the Church-state and the kingdom... You don't want that, do you?!",
    ["Dialogue3152804"]="... Sorry Sir, I'm just following my orders.\n(After speaking, Peddy waved his hand to the soldiers behind him, motioning them to come to inspect)\nYou two, do your thing. As for the rest of you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me now</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3152805"]="Yes Sir!",
    ["Dialogue3152806"]="...\n(After realizing that Peddy has no time for fun and games, the Church-state corps leader seemed to frown, and then quietly glanced at his companions behind him)",
    ["Dialogue3152901"]="You bold... bold man! You're just a mere guard at the city gate! How dare you go through the token that represents the friendship between our two countries without permission!",
    ["Dialogue3152902"]="... I have said this time and time again, it doesn't matter who you are, no one is exempt from these orders of an urgent matter.\n(After squabbling about with the Church-state's leader, Peddy's suspicions have already peaked. He did not want to waste any more time, and headed straight for the largest <color=#CA2E0AFF>square cargo box</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3152903"]="<size=26>W-wait!</size>\nL-look at this, our diplomatic contract with the Rune Kingdom — it has been known ever since that a fast lane must be established for our cargos to enter and exit, and that any trade goods and tokens may be exempted from verification!",
    ["Dialogue3152904"]="(He takes out a roll of parchment from his pocket and slams it down in front of Peddy)\nThis thing, there's no way you don't recognize it! Open your eyes and <color=#CA2E0AFF>confirm</color> it for me right now!",
    ["Dialogue3153001"]="W-well? How about it! This is a special pass for the kingdom granted by the Seven Royal Families themselves! If you insist on bothering us again, that would be a serious crime, breaking the diplomatic relations between our countries! Do you get it now?! Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry and let us go</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3153002"]="<color=#A1979FFF>This is... Lord Walter's seal...?</color>\n(Peddy examined the parchment again and again in disbelief, and eventually waved his hand at the Defense Force soldiers)\n... (Sigh) Let them go.",
    ["Dialogue3153003"]="(Hmph!) That's more like it! Bother us again and you'll be in for a treat!",
    ["Dialogue3153004"]="(Peddy frowned as he watched the sly group leaving)\n... I'm going to report this to Commander Bohr. As for everyone else, continue to guard the border — every single person and every item must be inspected, no questions asked! Do I have your understanding?",
    ["Dialogue3153005"]="Yes, Captain!",
    ["Dialogue3153101"]="... This is what just happened at the south gate. However, this alone is not enough to prove our suspicions...\n(Peddy turned his head, glanced at Bohr, and upon receiving a nod from him, he turned to look at another soldier waiting by the side)\nAngelo, the rest is on you.",
    ["Dialogue3153102"]="Yes, Captain!\nThe information I scouted was about two suspicious people at the south gate this morning. At the time, I was patrolling the main road outside the south gate...",
    ["Dialogue3153103"]="In the woods near the entrance of the city, I heard some strange noises — so I moved closer to inspect, and it was not what I expected...",
    ["Dialogue3153104"]="Huh... You seem tired... right, Adventurer?\nNot a problem, we can take a break! When you are <color=#CA2E0AFF>ready</color>, come back later and <color=#CA2E0AFF>let me know</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3153201"]="... These are all the clues I found this morning.",
    ["Dialogue3153202"]="That's right, Adventurer. It was only after hearing this information that I was able to determine that the Church-state corps was the one behind the disappearance of His Majesty. Remember our previous inference? His Majesty was unconscious, and was hidden in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>huge cargo box</color>, and the corps happened to be carrying a large number of trade goods that could be exempted from inspection...",
    ["Dialogue3153203"]="With all due respect, Lord Bohr, and Adventurer — now that His Majesty is in captivity, I think we should send more men to intercept that corps and force them to hand over His Majesty. As long as they are surrounded by our forces, I'm sure they won't dare play any more tricks!",
    ["Dialogue3153204"]="... you're too impulsive, Peddy. It is precisely the reason that His Majesty's safety is at stake that we need to be more cautious, in case we alert someone. Bandits will always be bandits, so there is no guarantee that they will not do anything to harm His Majesty. The only way to rescue His Majesty now is to send our elite members to operate in secret.",
    ["Dialogue3153205"]="Of course, but we will still need your help, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3153206"]="(Showing an approving glance)\nWell then, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a short break</color>. After you finish your preparations, we shall continue to discuss the details of the rescue operation.",
    ["Dialogue3153301"]="... Looks like you're ready, Adventurer.\nIn that case, here's my plan in full detail — I want you to pretend that you're someone from the Church-state, blend in with their members, and try to bring His Majesty back safely without alerting the enemy.",
    ["Dialogue3153302"]="Yes, in order to execute this plan, we will still need to make some other preparations, especially...\n(Bohr looked at you for a moment, while in deep thought)\nWe must get you a set of the Church-state's clothing...",
    ["Dialogue3153303"]="I once heard about a merchant in Prontera named Vera, she seemed to be really obsessed about... what's it called again? R-roleplaying...?\n(Bohr appears to have little clue as to what he was talking about, showing a rare look of confusion)",
    ["Dialogue3153304"]="... Anyway, her sewing skill is one of a kind. I think we can ask her for help. Please go to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>the temporary camp of the Church-state corps</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside the South Gate</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>of their costume</color> for Vera. She can make a costume of that style for you.",
    ["Dialogue3153401"]="Ohhhhh....! You want me to make these clothes, Adventurer?\n(Vera immediately got excited as soon as she saw the picture, so excited that she couldn't help grabbing your shoulder)",
    ["Dialogue3153402"]="Ahh... sorry sorry! It's just... been such a long time since I saw such artistic clothing!\n(She releases her tight grip on your shoulder — turning to the photo and murmurs)\n<color=#A1979FFF>My creative soul... has never been so excited!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3153403"]=".... Of course! There's no costume that I, Vera the Master Tailor, can't make! \nHowever, an exotic costume such as this will always require some <color=#CA2E0AFF>special materials</color> to fully reflect its glamor...",
    ["Dialogue3153404"]="We'll definitely need the gloomy <color=#CA2E0AFF>Light Blue Down Fur</color>! All you need to do is defeat one <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sturdy Eclipse</color> and you can get it. It's a piece of cake for you, Adventurer. Oh, and for the icing on the cake, also get me some pretty <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica Flowers </color>and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Superior Leather</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3153501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Ummm... I'm running out of... creative inspiration...</color>\nOne moment please, Adventurer! I'll start making the clothes you want right now!",
    ["Dialogue3153502"]="(Vera took out her sewing toolkit. An exotic costume was made from her skillful sewing)\n... Ta-da! Here it is, Adventurer! Is it good enough for you?",
    ["Dialogue3153503"]="(Feeling your sincerity, Vera rubbed her head with a shy look)\nWell... It will be great if it helps you! Anyway, here you go, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>costume</color>is <color=#CA2E0AFF>yours</color>! If you have any other similar requests in the future... feel free to come to me.",
    ["Dialogue3153601"]="Wow... it really does live up to your reputation, it looks almost as if it were real.",
    ["Dialogue3153602"]="Without further ado... Adventurer, please take action as soon as possible. According to our intelligence, the corps won't be around the South Gate for too long. They should be heading to the Sograt Desert soon. As for the cargo box that contains His Majesty... I think they'll have someone keep a close eye on it to avoid any accidents. But we still have a chance...",
    ["Dialogue3153603"]="Do you remember the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious person</color> Angelo mentioned? You can tell he is respected by all the corps members. If you can disguise yourself as the trusted follower of \"That Lord\"...",
    ["Dialogue3153604"]="I believe in your courage and wisdom. But remember, be careful. If you feel like there's <color=#CA2E0AFF>any danger</color>, do not hesitate to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fall back</color>. Being reckless won't help our plans, and will only put His Majesty in danger.",
    ["Dialogue3153605"]="Let's go then, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3153701"]="…… Halt! Who's there!",
    ["Dialogue3153702"]="Change shifts...?\n(The young man in exotic clothes looks at you with a puzzled expression)\nWho are you? I've never seen you before.",
    ["Dialogue3153703"]="That Lord...?\n(He thought for a while and suddenly realized)\nS-Sorry! I didn't realize it was...",
    ["Dialogue3153704"]="(The youth covered his mouth frantically at your warning)\nS-sorry... I didn't mean to... If that's from \"The Lord,\" I'll... just go and rest now. Please go ahead.",
    ["Dialogue3153801"]="……?!\n(A young blond was drawn by the sound. You clearly saw the surprise in his eyes when you made eye contact with him)\nYou are...?",
    ["Dialogue3153802"]="Are you new here? But...\n(He begins to scan you, which should make you extremely defensive. However, you have a gut feeling that he means no harm)\nYour look familiar... Can you tell me your name, young lad?",
    ["Dialogue3153803"]="<color=#A1979FFF>...Ahh... now I remember... It's you...\n(Despite your best efforts to hide it, he still showed a dazed expression)\nDon't be nervous, I'm not your enemy. I'm just...",
    ["Dialogue3153804"]="<size=26>... over there! Hurry and check it out!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3153805"]="... Get out of here quickly. Leave this to me.\n(The young man steps across the room — standing between you and the corps. Looking at his back, you felt a sense of déjà vu)",
    ["Dialogue3153806"]="Whatever your purpose is here, I do hope this is <color=#CA2E0AFF>the last time</color> we meet, young lad.",
    ["Dialogue3153901"]="How did it go — did you find out where His Majesty is?",
    ["Dialogue3153902"]="(Upon hearing your explanation, Bohr could not hide his disappointment)\nIs that so... what a pity. With just a little more... we could've successfully saved His Majesty...",
    ["Dialogue3153903"]="No, it's not your fault, Adventurer. I believe you did everything you could've done. Besides, I highly insist that you do not act rashly. All actions must always put the safety of His Majesty first. So... if anything... it should be my fault, so you don't need to blame yourself for that.",
    ["Dialogue3153904"]="(Bohr pats you gently on the shoulder)\nIt's okay. At least we still have a chance before they leave the kingdom. It's just... we can't <color=#CA2E0AFF>waste any more time</color>, Adventurer. If they can successfully reach the Port of Morroc and set sail... then His Majesty would...",
    ["Dialogue3153905"]="...The Defense Force can only give you limited support, as the road's distance is very far this time. However, I do believe that your wisdom and courage will pull you through any difficulties. As for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange young blond</color>... right now, we can't tell if he's a friend or foe. All I can say is — you must stay vigilant, and never trust others...",
    ["Dialogue3153906"]="So then...if you are ready to go — please take off as soon as possible, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3154001"]="(The corners of these supply boxes are riveted together ever so tightly. You reach out to try and open the lid — only to find that it's almost impossible to open it...)",
    ["Dialogue3154101"]="Be wary! If there is any mistake... you'll be on the chopping block!",
    ["Dialogue3154102"]="Y-yes, I understand...",
    ["Dialogue3154103"]="... Remember, \"That Lord\" has already well-arranged your route. After a while, bring this with you when you go through the <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate</color>, and cross the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>. There will be a boat at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Port of Morroc</color> waiting for you. Throughout the whole trip... you must take good care of him! After all... he is the King...",
    ["Dialogue3154104"]="Please feel free to tell \"That Lord,\" that we will take turns to guard him and never let him out of our sight!",
    ["Dialogue3154105"]="(Their voices gradually fade away, to the extent that you can barely hear them)",
    ["Dialogue3154201"]="(The huge supply box is filled with piles of exotic clothing — it appears that they are the daily clothes carried by the corps members...)",
    ["Dialogue3154301"]="(You immediately smelled the wine aroma upon opening the box, and the precious wines were neatly arranged in the box — one would not expect that the corps would still be in the mood for wine...)",
    ["Dialogue3154401"]="(...The bright, shining, sharp gleam makes you close your eyes in discomfort. When you open your eyes again, you see a dazzling assortment of weapons lying quietly in the box, emitting an icy cold gleam.)",
    ["Dialogue3154501"]="(The cargo box is filled with fresh Durian Grass. You vaguely remember that this smelly plant is the favorite of some kind of monster...)",
    ["Dialogue3160101"]="Adventurer! You're here at last. I've been waiting for you here for a long time!\n(after seeing your figure, the anxious guard finally has some hope in his eyes)",
    ["Dialogue3160102"]="No... It isn’t me.... the palace, something happened in the palace!",
    ["Dialogue3160103"]="Your majesty... No, your highness....\n(he hesitated for a long while, he couldn't even say a complete sentence. Obviously, he was extremely flustered.)\nI, where should I start to say... Yes, yes!",
    ["Dialogue3160104"]="Commander Bohr explained to me before he left! If you come, I will escort you directly to the palace’s back gardens. He... He will wait for you there!",
    ["Dialogue3160105"]="Alright..... Alright! Come with me please, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3160106"]="Well... You should come back quickly. It's really urgent!",
    ["Dialogue3160201"]="Ah... Well, I know it's not all your responsibility. After all, on this special day, your Majesty must also hope to be alone with the princes for a while. It's no use investigating matters of the past. Our top priority is to hurry up.....\n(whilst you have been talking, Bohr seems to have noticed you)",
    ["Dialogue3160202"]="... it seems that our rescuers have arrived. Please allow me to introduce you all. This is the Adventurer I mentioned to you, Princess. His wisdom and courage have helped us through many difficult times. What we are experiencing now is no exception.",
    ["Dialogue3160203"]="(Bohr turns to you and respectfully introduces the noble woman standing beside him)\nAdventurer... This is his Majesty's wife, Princess Catherine.",
    ["Dialogue3160204"]="... please stand up, Adventurer. Now is not the time for formalities. Since Bohr recommended you so strongly, I trust that your skills are outstanding... I hope you can help us solve this matter as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue3160205"]="... suddenly, I can only go straight, Adventurer.\nIn fact, just this morning, his majesty, he... Suddenly disappeared.",
    ["Dialogue3160206"]="At present, we are also in the process of sorting out clues. Let the chief bodyguard of the Royal Palace personally explain the situation to you. He was the primary witness.",
    ["Dialogue3160207"]="Yes, Lord Bohr!\n... this is what happened. His majesty has long intended to come to mourn from Price Nate on what would have been Prince Nate’s birthday. Today is Prince Nates Birthday, so early in the morning, we escorted his majesty to the royal tomb and waited at the door.",
    ["Dialogue3160208"]="His majesty entered the tomb as he normally would have done, so that the three princes were alone... Soon after he entered, we heard a loud noise coming from the tomb! We rushed in to check the situation. Unexpectedly, we found that his majesty had fallen nearby the prince's coffin. I quickly ordered the guards to carry the king out of the tomb and back to the palace. I went to the church to find Archbishop Wolmas and asked him to diagnose his majesty...",
    ["Dialogue3160209"]="Then... The strangest thing happened!\nWhen I returned to the palace with Archbishop Wolmas, I found that his majesty, who had fainted, had transformed into Prince Nate’s remains......",
    ["Dialogue3160210"]="I am not lying to you, really! I have a loyal servant to his majesty for many years! Lord Bohr, you know! I would give my life for the crown!",
    ["Dialogue3160211"]="(Bohr patted the bodyguard on the shoulder and motioned him to take it easy)\nCalm down. I believe in your loyalty to your majesty. There is no question about that.",
    ["Dialogue3160212"]="Adventurer, we don't have any more useful clues now. It's too early to conclude what truly happened. For the time being, why don't you help Archbishop Wolmas to confirm the identity of the body? If this is really Prince Nate’s body... this will be our starting point.",
    ["Dialogue3160301"]="(the old man is standing over the body with a serious look on his face. When he sees you coming, he nods slightly to greet you)\nHere you are, Adventurer. Instructed by Bohr, I have carefully investigated the condition of the body. Whether it's physical features or the iconic snake scale pattern... It is clear to us that this is Prince Nate.",
    ["Dialogue3160302"]="... however, the situation is too complex and I must investigate further before I can reach a definitive conclusion, I hope to further confirm my suspicions. If you are willing to help... Please go to the sewer of Prontera and collect some rotten blood of Familiar, and the foul mucus of the female thief bug. These will allow me to reach a conclusion.",
    ["Dialogue3160401"]="... yes, that's what I need. Now, please try to drop the rotten blood and foul mucus on the body, and observe what happens to the body.",
    ["Dialogue3160501"]="No mistake... This is the magic artifact I personally inserted into the bodies of the three princes.",
    ["Dialogue3160502"]="In fact, when the three princes died, the king and the princess, not ready to say goodbye to their children, begged me to try to preserve the bodies of the three princes. Entrusted by him, I put the magic artifact storing Odin's divine strength into the remains of the three princes. It served two purposes. On one hand, it can prevent the body from decaying. On the other hand, it can also prevent the souls of princes from being eroded by the power of shadow attributes....",
    ["Dialogue3160503"]="Just now, when you dripped the rotten blood and foul mucus on to the prince’s body, the strength of the magic artifact created a golden barrier. So I'm sure... This body is Prince Nate of the Gaebolg family. There's nothing wrong with it.",
    ["Dialogue3160601"]="How's it going, Adventurer? Has the Archbishop reached a conclusion?",
    ["Dialogue3160602"]="This... Is this really Nate's body? What about his majesty?",
    ["Dialogue3160603"]="No... it's impossible! No one has touched Prince Nates's body since the burial. All the bodyguards present can prove this to each other! Even when we escorted the king out of the tomb, the bodies of the three princes were well preserved in the coffin! Otherwise... Otherwise, it would be impossibly for no one to notice that there is nothing in the coffin.",
    ["Dialogue3160604"]="Well..... Was there anyone stationed guarding the tomb after you left?",
    ["Dialogue3160605"]="No... all the guards should have followed the team escorting the king back to the palace....",
    ["Dialogue3160606"]="(Bohr frowns after hearing the captain's answer)\nIf so, is the tomb now completely unguarded?",
    ["Dialogue3160607"]="... Bohr, if you have made a decision, you must act on it as soon as possible. No matter who is responsible for today's incident, our most urgent task now is to find his majesty. After all... His Majesty's safety is directly related to the fate of the whole Rune Kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue3160608"]="Yes, your highness.\nThe Adventurer and I will set out immediately and go to the royal tomb for an on-site investigation. The princess will stay in the palace and preside over the overall situation for the time being. Please do not fear... No matter what happens, I will give my life to ensure his Majesty’s safe return.",
    ["Dialogue3160701"]="……\n(Bohr frowns and looks at the coffin in front of him. The place where Prince Nate's body should be enshrined is now empty)\nIt seems that this matter is more complicated than I thought, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3160702"]="No... I don't think he lied. He has no motive to lie, nor can he get any benefit from it. There must have been great confusion when the guards witnessed his majesty faint to the ground... Maybe something unexpected happened during this time.",
    ["Dialogue3160703"]="Adventurer, lets split up and search the tomb separately. I believe there is always something to be found. There must be some useful clues left around here somewhere",
    ["Dialogue3160801"]="Anything, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3160802"]="Sure enough... As far as I know, the tomb is specially cleaned by an assigned person every morning. It would be impossible for there to be such obvious tracks. Therefore, the footprints must have been left after the king came to mourn the prince. And then there are my findings....",
    ["Dialogue3160803"]="Look here - the fresh flowers in Prince Nate's sarcophagus should have been replaced this morning. But now, they have obvious signs of withering\n(Bohr picks up the delicate bouquet and holds it in front of you)\nNot only that, it seems to have splashed a strange black liquid.....",
    ["Dialogue3160804"]="Yes, these liquids give off a pungent smell. Although this is just a guess... Could these unusual liquids have come from some complex alchemy potion?",
    ["Dialogue3160805"]="... Specialized in technology, Adventurer. We cannot rely on our guesses to find his majesty. Only a professional alchemist, such as Lawrence can identify the true origins of these liquids for us. Please collect some liquid samples from the flowers and go to the Prontera library for help!",
    ["Dialogue3160901"]="Adventurer, where did you find this?",
    ["Dialogue3160902"]="... Oh. Well, seeing as you cannot tell me, I will not ask any more.\n(Lawrence notices you have turned quite pale. He strokes his beard and changes his focus to the sample solution in your hand)\nBut if you want information about this bottle of potion......",
    ["Dialogue3160903"]="Unfortunately, I will not be able to give you an immediate answer. If my guess is correct, it is an extremely rare alchemy potion. I only got a glimpse from a rare book by chance. If I want to further determine its true features, I must request something from you. You must help me catch a Lunatic alive. I need further experiments to prove my theory.",
    ["Dialogue3161001"]="Good, adventurer. Now... Put my hair in.....",
    ["Dialogue3161002"]="(seeing your disdainful expression, Lawrence stamps his foot and glares right at you)\nThis is part of the experiment! Don't you dare look at me as if I am some sort of pervert!",
    ["Dialogue3161003"]="... well, feed the medicine to the Lunatic! You'll get the answer you want soon!",
    ["Dialogue3161101"]="This, this is really a deformation potion!",
    ["Dialogue3161102"]="Joo... Jomi?!! JOJO jomi!!!\n(the Lunatic turns towards Lawrence and swings his arm and jumps hard. You have to give him a carrot to win him over)",
    ["Dialogue3161103"]="As the name suggests, this is a medicine that can alter appearances. As long as the hair of the target object is added during boiling, the person who drinks the medicine will transform into the appearance of the target object. Even the most skilled doctors can't identify a user from a non-user with 100% accuracy! In order to prevent this potion from being abused, it was added to the list of prohibited potions many years ago.",
    ["Dialogue3161104"]="In addition, this is also one of the most difficult alchemy potions to prepare. Those who can make deformation potions... Must have superb alchemy technology!\n..... don't know this information, can it help you?",
    ["Dialogue3161105"]="You're welcome, Adventurer. But honestly, I have received many favors from you, you do not have to be so polite! Although You were a little vague in your explanation, I feel..... You shoulder a very important quest, correct? Go! I sincerely hope... You can return in triumph!",
    ["Dialogue3161106"]="It doesn't matter. The deformation potion is time-effective. It won't take long, and it will turn back to the original Lunatic. Don’t be afraid to finish what you set out to do!",
    ["Dialogue3161201"]="Look at your expression, Lawrence shouldn't have let us down?",
    ["Dialogue3161202"]="... a potion that can completely transform a person’s appearance into another? Sure enough... Now all the clues can be connected.",
    ["Dialogue3161203"]="Just in time.... When you were gone, I too made some new discoveries. Look at the grass beside the sarcophagus, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3161301"]="Did you find out, Adventurer? It looks like some people... And some large goods were hidden in the grass here.",
    ["Dialogue3161302"]="Now, I think it's time find out whether our assumptions are the truth. Have you explored all of the key points of this case? Prisoner... By what means did his majesty vanish from this tomb guarded by many guards?",
    ["Dialogue3161303"]="Well... It seems that our guesses are both different. Let's have another look, shall we",
    ["Dialogue3161304"]="Our theory’s are identical, Adventurer. I too believe that the prisoner used this rare potion to lay a blindfold, so that he could clip past the guards and take his majesty from under their noses. Their plan was to make his majesty drink the medicine and change into.....",
    ["Dialogue3161305"]="Yes, they only had to make his unconscious majesty and prince Nate exchange appearance and positions, then make a loud and strange noise, which lead the guards into the room to check what was happening. Then, the guards were so distracted by the \"King's Majesty\" lying on the ground, no one noticed that the his majesty the King had been placed in the original position of Prince Nate in the coffin. So, who was behind all of this.... ?",
    ["Dialogue3161306"]="You 're right! They must have known his Majesty's schedule in advance, snuck into the tomb in advance, stunned his majesty, and then used deformation potion to deceive the guards. After they hurriedly took away the decoy king, the heavily guarded tomb was completely deserted. This sawdust left in the grass must be  a clue as to what vehicle they used to carry away his majesty.",
    ["Dialogue3161307"]="Now that the target has been locked... Next you must attack with all your strength.\nCome with me, Adventurer, we're going back into the ground.",
    ["Dialogue3161401"]="Adventurer, according to our conclusion, this is obviously a carefully planned kidnapping. Although we don't know the purpose of the perpetrator, it is our job to recover his majesty in one piece.",
    ["Dialogue3161402"]="I have ordered the Royal defense force to carry out a street-by-street search throughout the city. All personnel, vehicles, horses and materials entering and leaving Prontera must be searched to ensure that there are no missing fish! I'll let you know as soon as there is any new news. When the time comes... I will continue needing your help.",
    ["Dialogue3161501"]="(when approaching the surface of the corpse, the blood of corrupted blood evaporates...)",
    ["Dialogue3161601"]="(the foul mucus also cannot touch the body. When it drips, you can even see a golden barrier above the surface of the body...)",
    ["Dialogue3161701"]="(muddy footprints are scattered in front of the flower bed. Careful observation shows that there are broken flower branches and leaves nearby...)",
    ["Dialogue3161801"]="(in front of the flower bed on the other side, there are more muddy footprints and broken branches and leaves...)",
    ["Dialogue3161901"]="(the two sets of shoe prints meet on the steps and move forward side by side, one left and one right. From the frequency of the footprints, it seems that their owners worked together to lift something...)",
    ["Dialogue3162001"]="(two sets of footprints extend all the way to the exit and disappear outside the gate of the tomb...)",
    ["Dialogue3162101"]="(a huge square imprint can be seen on the brick surface next to the sarcophagus. After careful observation, it seems that scattered around are wood chips and <color=#CA2E0AFF>footprints</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3170101"]="(the guard at the gate respectfully salutes you, but looks at you cautiously)\nPlease take a step and speak, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3170102"]="Yes, the news came from commander Bohr. It is said that... Significant progress has been made on the important cases you were investigating earlier. Bohr hopes that you can go to the defense force training ground as soon as possible. He will be waiting for you there.",
    ["Dialogue3170201"]=".....You're back, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3170202"]="I think you could have guessed the reason why I contacted you. In fact, the defense forces have got some new information about his Majesty's whereabouts... I will let them reveal the information to you themselves. Paddy, you first.\n(Bohr gestured to the soldier beside him, who steps forward)",
    ["Dialogue3170203"]="Yes! Lord Commander!",
    ["Dialogue3170301"]="The information I have comes from a group of foreigners who left through the Prontera South Gate not long ago. After receiving commander Bohr's order, our defense forces set up checkpoints at the south gate and carefully checked all passing personnel and goods until this team appeared.....",
    ["Dialogue3170302"]="(seeing your concentration, the soldier continues on)\nHowever, just when I routinely stopped them and told them that they needed to check their carry on goods, they.....",
    ["Dialogue3170303"]="... well, do you have any other urgent matters?\nThen I have no other choice, quickly get back here! I am waiting for you!",
    ["Dialogue3170401"]="... you have no right to stop us, soldier.",
    ["Dialogue3170402"]="Sorry, guys. Although the accident happened suddenly, commander Bohr had just issued an order that all personnel and goods entering and leaving Prontera must be inspected before they can pass. We would appreciate your cooperation.",
    ["Dialogue3170403"]="As I said, you have no right to stop us, soldier!\nWe are a diplomatic corps from Arunabez. We are responsible for exchanging the tokens of our two countries. We are expected to bring them back untouched and in one piece. If we are delayed, there will be a rift between our leaders and the Kingdom... Can you afford to be the cause of such a rift!",
    ["Dialogue3170404"]="... sorry, emissary, I just follow orders.\n(after saying this, Paddy waved a hand to the soldiers behind him and motioned them to come forward for inspection)\nYou two, check here. The rest of you, come with me!",
    ["Dialogue3170405"]="Yes, Captain!",
    ["Dialogue3170406"]="……\n(after realizing that he could not stop Paddy, the leading member of the mission frowned and winked at his companions behind him)",
    ["Dialogue3170501"]="Bold... Very bold! Just a gate guard! He believes he is allowed to search the tokens representing the diplomatic relations between the two countries without authorization!",
    ["Dialogue3170502"]="... I have reiterated time and time again that I am only doing my orders, no one can be exempted.\n(after being repeatedly stopped by the other party from taking a look inside the cargo box, Paddy has grown very suspicious. He doesn't want to become too entangled with the travelers, and goes straight to the largest square container)",
    ["Dialogue3170503"]="Stop it!\nIn our diplomatic contract with the Rune Kingdom, it has long been stated that we need to open a fast passage for our envoys to enter and leave through these gates! Any trade goods and tokens can be exempted from verification! You... Look here!",
    ["Dialogue3170504"]="(he takes a roll of parchment out from under his arm and slams it onto Paddy’s chest)\nThis! There is no way you can't recognize this as an official document! Use your eyes, tough guy!",
    ["Dialogue3170601"]="How, how! This is a special pass for the Kingdom granted by the seven Royal Families themselves! If you insist on blocking us again, it will be a felony of undermining diplomatic relations between our two countries! Do you not understand? Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue3170602"]="... this seal is Lord Walter's...?\n(Paddy takes the parchment and scans it through again and again. After a long while, he finally waves to the soldiers behind him.)\n... let them go.",
    ["Dialogue3170603"]="Hah! You know, delaying our trip doesn’t make you look bad!",
    ["Dialogue3170604"]="(Paddy frowns as he watches group disappear into the distance,)\n... I'll report it to Lord Bohr. Keep a strict check on every cargo box! Do you understand?",
    ["Dialogue3170605"]="Yes! Commander!",
    ["Dialogue3170701"]="... the above is what just happened at the south gate. However, these alone are not enough to prove our suspicions.....\n(Paddy turns his head and looks at Bohr. After receiving the latter's nod, he looks at another soldier waiting)\nAngelo, you’re up. ",
    ["Dialogue3170702"]="Yes! Captain!\nThe information I have is regarding two suspicious individuals at the South Gate this morning. At that time, I was patrolling the main road outside the South Gate.....",
    ["Dialogue3170703"]="Near the woods near the city gate, I heard some strange sounds, so I approached to check. I didn't expect it to be......",
    ["Dialogue3170704"]="Well... You look tired, Adventurer?\nWe can have a rest if you wish! We can continue when you're ready!",
    ["Dialogue3170801"]="... these are all the clues I found this morning.",
    ["Dialogue3170802"]="Yes, Adventurer. It was only after hearing this your information that I was able to determine those men disguised at the diplomatic corps were the ones who kidnapped his majesty. Remember our deductions? The king was taken away, unconscious in a large container. The diplomatic corps that left through the South gate happened to carry a large number of trade goods that were exempted from inspection.",
    ["Dialogue3170803"]="With all due respect, Lord Bohr, there are some other Adventurers. Now his majesty is being held captive. I think we should directly send more people to intercept the diplomatic corps and force them to hand over his majesty. As long as they are surrounded by our defense forces, they dare not play any tricks again!",
    ["Dialogue3170804"]="... Far too impulsive, Paddy. His Majesty's safety is paramount and therefore we need to be more cautious in our approach. If we back them in to a corner, there is no telling what they will do, it is difficult to ensure that the bandits will not hurt his majesty. Now, I think the safest way is to summon elite members to rescue your majesty secretly.",
    ["Dialogue3170805"]="Of course, but it depends on your strength, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3170806"]="(looks approvingly)\nWell, please take a break. After you finish your preparation, we will continue to discuss the details of the rescue operation.",
    ["Dialogue3170901"]="... looks like you're ready, Adventurer.\nRight, it’s time to reveal my plan - I want you to pretend to be a member of the church, sneak into the corps and try to bring his majesty back safely without disturbing the enemy.",
    ["Dialogue3170902"]="Yes, we will have to make some preparations, if we are going to implement this plan, starting with.....\n(Bohr looks at you for a moment, thoughtfully)\nI have to find you a set of religious clothes......",
    ["Dialogue3170903"]="I’ve heard of an appearance merchant in Prontera named Vera. She is known to have a passion for ... Cosplay?\n(Bohr seems to digest the meaning of this strange word slowly, showing a rare look of doubt)",
    ["Dialogue3170904"]="... anyway, she has excellent sewing skills. I think we can ask her for help. Please go to the south gate to find the temporary camp of the diplomatic corps. Wait for an opportunity to take photos of their outfits and then ask Vera to replicate them as close as possible.",
    ["Dialogue3171001"]="Hmm?! You want me to tailor these kinds of clothes, adventurer?!\n(Vera, who has just seen the picture, suddenly get extremely excited and grabs your shoulder)",
    ["Dialogue3171002"]="Oh, sorry, I haven't ben asked to make such eccentric clothing for a very long time!\n(she releases her grip on you and mumbles into the picture)\nMy creative soul... Is burning with desire!",
    ["Dialogue3171003"]="... of course! Any type of clothing is possible with Vera’s skillset!\nHowever, to create clothing with so much exotic charm, we will need to find some particular materials.....",
    ["Dialogue3171004"]="Of course, we will need light blue down fur full of melancholy color! It's enough to beat a mighty Eclipse, which should be a piece of cake for Adventurers! Not only that! Not only that! For the icing on the cake, I will also need some beautiful Veronica Flowers and high-quality leather.",
    ["Dialogue3171101"]="Ahh... My creative soul... Is about to burn out!\nJust a moment, Adventurer! I'll start crafting your outfit!",
    ["Dialogue3171102"]="(Vera takes out her crafting tools. You look on in amazement as her needle and thread weave up and down. Before you know it a vivid exotic outfit appears)\n... done! Adventurer! Come and have a look. What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue3171103"]="(seeing your sincerity, Vera touches her head with embarrassment)\nHey... I am very happy to help you! The outfit is yours! If you ever want anything else in the future... Please be sure to come back to me (๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧",
    ["Dialogue3171201"]="Hmm... it really is a work of art. It will be difficult to tell the difference between this outfit and the real deal.",
    ["Dialogue3171202"]="You’ve still got time, Adventurer. Time is of the essence. Our sources are telling us, the regiment will not stay in the south gate for long. It will leave for the Sograt Desert soon. As for the container where they are hiding his majesty... I am sure they will have someone guarding it at all times to make sure there nothing slips through the cracks. But we will have an opportunity....",
    ["Dialogue3171203"]="Do you remember the mysterious character Angelo spoke of? It is said that everyone in the diplomatic corps respect him. You must pretend to be one of the “Lord’s” trusted followers....",
    ["Dialogue3171204"]="There is no doubting your courage and wisdom, but please remember not to scare the snake. If you ever feel any danger, don't hesitate to retreat immediately. Acting rashly will not only expose us, but also put his majesty at risk.",
    ["Dialogue3171205"]="Well.... What are we waiting for, Adventurer! ",
    ["Dialogue3171301"]="... stop! Who's there!",
    ["Dialogue3171302"]="Change posts?\n(the young man in the outfit looks at you with a puzzled expression)\nWho are you? I've never seen you before.",
    ["Dialogue3171303"]="Lord....?\n(he thinks for a moment and suddenly realizes)\nSo..... Sorry! I was Yi——",
    ["Dialogue3171304"]="(under your warning, the young man covers his mouth in panic)\nSo.... sorry... I made a mistake. Since it's the order of the \"Lord\", I'll... Go and rest now. Please help yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3171401"]="……?!\n(attracted by the sound is a young blonde-haired man. When your eyes meet, you can see the surprise in his eyes)\nWho are you.....?",
    ["Dialogue3171402"]="Are you new here? But.....\n(he begins to observe you closely, which would normally make you tense up. But somehow, you instinctively feel that he means you no harm)\nYou look familiar. Can you tell me your name, young man?",
    ["Dialogue3171403"]="... ah... I see... It's you\n(although you tried to hide it, he still showed a sudden expression)\nTake it easy. I'm not your enemy. I just.....",
    ["Dialogue3171404"]="——There! Look, quickly!",
    ["Dialogue3171405"]="... you get out of here. Leave it to me.\n(the young man takes a step forward and stands between you and the members of the corps. Watching him do this, something feels familiar and you suddenly feel a sense of déjà vu)",
    ["Dialogue3171406"]="Whatever your purpose is here... I hope that this is the last time we meet, young man.",
    ["Dialogue3171501"]="Well, have you found where they are holding his majesty?",
    ["Dialogue3171502"]="(hearing your explanation, Bohr can't hold back his disappointment)\nReally... What a pity. We were close... Maybe we can still rescue his majesty.",
    ["Dialogue3171503"]="No, it's not your fault, Adventurer. I believe you handled the situation well. Moreover, I was the one who urged you not to act rashly. All actions must be based on ensuring his Majesty's safety. So... If there was a mistake, it would naturally be my responsibility. You shouldn’t blame yourself for it.",
    ["Dialogue3171504"]="(Bohr gently taps you on the shoulder)\nIt doesn't matter. At least, we still have a chance before they leave the kingdom. It's just... We have to hurry, Adventurer. If we allow them to reach the port of Morroc and get to sea... His Majesty.....",
    ["Dialogue3171505"]="..... this time, due to the long journey, the defense force will only be able to give you limited amounts of support. I still believe that your wisdom and courage will be your greatest guide to overcome any difficulties. As for that mysterious blonde man... At this moment it is hard to judge whether he is an enemy or a friend. I can only urge you to tread carefully and not to trust him too much......",
    ["Dialogue3171506"]="So - if you are ready, please set out as soon as possible, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3180101"]="... since we can't find the reason, we can't sit back and relax. Starting from today, add two more patrols. Be on high alert! Don't let anyone suspicious through!",
    ["Dialogue3180102"]="But Captain, we don't have any more men.....",
    ["Dialogue3180103"]="Are you... The Adventurer from the Rune Kingdom?\n(the guard army officer looks at you for a while and all of a sudden makes an expression)",
    ["Dialogue3180104"]="Yes... You know, strange things have been happening over and over again in the city recently. The guard army are low on manpower. And now we have another terrible <color=#CA2E0AFF>headache</color>... We'd appreciate it if you could help.\n(Gerner puts his hand on his chest and solemnly salutes to his badge)",
    ["Dialogue3180105"]="We were just discussing it... About a month ago, a psychopath began tormenting the urban area in the southeast of the city. The guard army rushed to the scene and found that he had attacked several innocent people. Not only that, but the subject went through some strange physical changes. His physical strength and agility were levels far beyond us ordinary people. It took several guards to subdue and arrest him....",
    ["Dialogue3180106"]="The most... The most terrifying thing was that he couldn’t feel any pain. To try and stop him from continuing on his rampage, we decided to fire warning shots. One of the bullets hit him and it looked like it broke his leg, it didn’t stop him from rushing us. His ferocious expression was like... Like a soul reviver in a mythical story....\n(Pierson turned pale, the memory obviously still haunting him)",
    ["Dialogue3180107"]="Don't say such unfounded things! We cannot let the seriousness of the situation get to us!\n(Gerner interrupts the team member sharply)\nBesides, I have already said... someone must be the root of all this chaos.",
    ["Dialogue3180108"]="Of course, I have my reasons. These cases couldn’t be caused by a common disease, but must by someone deliberately! You may ask how I have come to this realization... Take a look at this poster, Adventurer! I'm sure you will reach the same conclusion as me.",
    ["Dialogue3180201"]="Could someone have made a mistake? In the light of the guard’s report, the timing of these posters is quite... convenient. Every time a new madman appears, many others spring up in every corner of the city. This makes me believe that someone is doing this on purpose, playing every trick in the book to mislead us. Even this strange madness is likely to have been engineered by him!",
    ["Dialogue3180202"]="The most puzzling thing is the strange unknown symbol in the signature of each poster\n(Gerner frowns and points to the strange symbol in the corner of the poster, you don’t recognize it at all)",
    ["Dialogue3180203"]="Unfortunately, we don't know what these symbols mean. They come in all sorts of different shapes, and it bears no resemblance to any distinguishable words... This could be another one of the tricks the perpetrator is playing on us. He considers himself a god among men, and simultaneously incites panic amongst the people.....",
    ["Dialogue3180204"]="... challenge him? That is to say... Do criminals openly provoke people and flex their muscles by creating mysterious unknown symbols?\n(Gerner touches his cheek, seriously considering your suggestion)\nIt's unpleasant... But it's also a possibility.",
    ["Dialogue3180205"]="However, no matter what the real motive of the criminal is, for us, the most important objective is to catch him and prevent him from continuing to cause such chaos.",
    ["Dialogue3180206"]="You mean, you want to start from the top? I suppose this is is a good starting point..! I see. Then, you must go to the riverside alley in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast of the city</color> to find a doctor named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elle</color>. He witnessed the onset of the first patient when it happened a month ago. Listen to his recount of the events.",
    ["Dialogue3180301"]="(as you enter the clinic, there is a doctor taking care of a patient. He looks up at you and the strange mask he is wearing on his face takes you by surprise)\nWhat's the matter, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3180302"]="... yes, I'm Elle. If you are here for consultation, I'm sorry. As you can see, I'm busy at the moment. You might have to wait a while.",
    ["Dialogue3180303"]="Investigate the psychotic incident? I see. Did you come here at the request of officer Gerner? Then I will do my best to help you, but.....",
    ["Dialogue3180304"]="Roar——\n(In the middle of his sentence, the patient lying down in front of the doctor suddenly opens his eyes and with sheer ferocity bursts into a wild animal-like roar. You quickly jump into to held the doctor restrain the patient down into the chair)",
    ["Dialogue3180305"]="……！ Steady! Steady, Adventurer!\n(the doctor yells and quickly takes a syringe filled with a red potions and injects it into the patient's body. A moment later, the crazed patient calms down again)",
    ["Dialogue3180306"]="It's a tranquilizer. I don’t usually administer it for patients, due to the side effects. However, this time, the patient was frantic and out of control. In order to avoid hurting them, I had to administer the potion. As you have just seen... Once the effects of the potion runs out, they will return to that deranged state.\nHowever, too many people have been getting ill these days. My <color=#CA2E0AFF>potion</color> has....",
    ["Dialogue3180307"]="... really? That would be great. If you can help me take care of these patients, I can tell you the whole story in detail. Fortunately, the tranquilizer is not very complicated to prepare. You will need to help me find <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 Dead Soul Grass</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Brilight wings</color>. These ingredients would be enough to help me treat these patients.",
    ["Dialogue3180401"]="(carefully examining the medicinal materials you retrieved, Elle give your a smile of satisfaction)\nGood. Now, lets sit down and talk about what happened.",
    ["Dialogue3180402"]="Yes, I reported it to the guard, because the first patient happened to be an old client of mine. This all started over a month ago. He suddenly stopped coming in for consultations. I was worried about his health, so I went and visited him at his home. When I got there... He unexpectedly lurched at me grabbed my neck!",
    ["Dialogue3180403"]="Fortunately, a patrol guard passed by. They managed to subdue the patient and by doing so saved my life. After that, I was commissioned by the guard army to investigate this strange disease. With more and more infected patients popping up every day, I have noticed a strange pattern....",
    ["Dialogue3180404"]="Most of these cases had pre-existing diseases before they went psychotic. Strangely, after they went psychotic, these pre-existing diseases all disappeared. For example this patient, his leg was completely disabled but now it has miraculously recovered, even stronger than normal!",
    ["Dialogue3180405"]="... abiding by the principle of <color=#CA2E0AFF>exchange things of equal value</color>, providing mortals a better life?\n(he murmurs your words thoughtfully)",
    ["Dialogue3180406"]="Does this mean... At the expense of all reason and common sense, you exchange your sanity for a stronger body?\nTsssk... That's terrible.",
    ["Dialogue3180407"]="In fact, over the past few days, several of my patients, many of whom are terminally ill, have stopped contacting me. The could also have been bewitched by the strange poster you had.....",
    ["Dialogue3180408"]="... here. All of my patients details are recorded in this medical record book.\nTheir homes are <color=#CA2E0AFF>scattered all around the city</color>. I'm afraid you can't handle all of that by yourself. I think you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>report the matter to governor Gerner</color> first, and then work with them to formulate a plan of action.",
    ["Dialogue3180501"]="... what happened, Adventurer? Why do you look flustered?",
    ["Dialogue3180502"]="Is this... The doctor's diagnostics record? Have you found anything unusual?",
    ["Dialogue3180503"]="Exchange things of equal value means.... to exchange reason for a sound body? Is this the message those posters are spewing?\n... damn it! This is fundamentally wrong, especially for our guard army!",
    ["Dialogue3180504"]="Pierson! Scott! Take this diagnostic record with you immediately and check every patient, one by one! No patient is allowed to go unchecked!\nAs for the Adventurer... Please go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>north of the city</color> with me to find this deaf patient named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palin</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3180601"]="Shhh-Shh, Adventurer. Look over there....\n(officer Gerner raises his finger to his lips, and then points with his eyes to the people in the darkness of the alley)\nThat's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palin</color>, the waitress at the bar nearby.",
    ["Dialogue3180602"]="She is in a very similar state to those who are suffering from the psychotic illness. Although she seems calm, did you notice the skin on her neck? It has begun to turn gray, and there are many abnormal muscle textures... According to our previous experience, if we approach too quickly, she will attack us !",
    ["Dialogue3180603"]="Don't disturb her too abruptly. I think we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak up</color> on her from behind and <color=#CA2E0AFF>knock her out</color>, but be careful not to hurt her... When you're ready, give me a signal and I'll follow your lead.",
    ["Dialogue3180701"]="I knew... Once a new patient appeared, these strange posters would start appearing too.",
    ["Dialogue3180702"]="... yes, <color=#CA2E0AFF>look carefully</color>, the symbol in the lower right corner has changed again.",
    ["Dialogue3180801"]="Again, I do not recognize any of the so-called words and symbols... Goodness, it's really puzzling. When did the criminal put up the poster?",
    ["Dialogue3180802"]="Yes, I noticed it, too. When we arrived the posters must have just been posted on the wall, but I didn’t notice anyone suspicious... Did the criminals already figure out that there would be new patients here?",
    ["Dialogue3180803"]="... forget it, this is not the time to discuss it. Now that new patients have been found here, it means that the whole block should be covered with these strange posters. We may need to split up, Adventurer. I'll take Palin to the doctor for treatment. As for the posters... Please have a look around and <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> them one by one.",
    ["Dialogue3180901"]="Well... They all have similar attributes, but they can't completely replace..... Maybe I am over thinking it..... This symbol originally represents the metal lanthanum.",
    ["Dialogue3180902"]="... in addition to the purification symbol here... What should be left is... Helium?",
    ["Dialogue3180903"]="Helium... Lanthanum... He... La... <color=#CA2E0AFF>HeLa</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3180904"]="My only explanation.... could be the goddess of disease and disaster, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Haila</color>..... wow?!\n(the annoying young man jumps back in surprise, and the poster in his hand is hissed and torn in half)\nWho are you?",
    ["Dialogue3180905"]="Who, who is sneaky! You're sneaky! I'm just studying the symbols on the poster!",
    ["Dialogue3180906"]="Of course! This measly puzzle couldn’t defeat me!",
    ["Dialogue3180907"]="According to my previous guesses, plus the new <color=#CA2E0AFF>inverse transformation symbol</color>, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reverse</color> the meaning of this paragraph... Wait, wait?\n(he seems to have snapped out of it and glares at you fiercely)\nWhy should I tell you?!",
    ["Dialogue3180908"]="Damn, wow... It's a routine....! Yes.... I finally figured it out! I can't possibly tell you.... a complete stranger!\nOtherwise, I wouldn’t receive any praise from Guild Leader Nicholas... Hmph!",
    ["Dialogue3180909"]="... Anyway! I have to look for other clues now! You must stop following me... And you are not allowed to set me up again! Goodbye!",
    ["Dialogue3181001"]="... you're back, Adventurer. Officer Gerner told me what happened. Thank you so much for saving my patient. In addition... I also administered sedatives to these patients, and we will not have any problems for the time being.",
    ["Dialogue3181002"]="Shortly before you came back, officer Gerner received an emergency message. I vaguely heard the person on the other end of the transceiver mention <color=#CA2E0AFF>Epsilon's house</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest of the city</color>",
    ["Dialogue3181003"]="(he pauses for a second and looks worried)\nI don't know if this news is also related to the psychotic incidents, but... The Epsilons were also consulted. They... They all have varying degrees of heart disease, which runs in the family.",
    ["Dialogue3181004"]="Before he left, Officer Gerner told me to tell you the news if you came back. I hope you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>help them</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3181101"]="You got here just in time, Adventurer!\nNot long ago, there was an attack on some civilians by several psychotics. Even though we were able to subdue it, a considerable number of people here are in a state of panic.",
    ["Dialogue3181102"]="In order to calm our nerves, can you help us make some <color=#CA2E0AFF>mixed congee</color> and hand it out to these people?",
    ["Dialogue3181201"]="Thank you very much for your help, Adventurer. I'm also sorry for the delay. I know you're looking for Officer Gerner. He's just up ahead in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>square</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3181301"]="Hoo... Sure enough, I was right to ask you for help, Adventurer.\n(Officer Gerner breathed a sigh of relief and put away his weapon. He squatted down and carefully observed the three patients who were knocked unconscious on the ground)\nIs this... The Epsilons who live nearby?",
    ["Dialogue3181302"]="You don't know, Adventurer. During a psychotic episode, there are strange changes in the skin and muscle texture of patients, and their faces usually turn rabid. It is difficult to specifically confirm the identity of the patients before they have settled down like this.",
    ["Dialogue3181303"]="... he told you that in the emergency transmission I received, someone mentioned <color=#CA2E0AFF>Epsilon's</color> house in the southwest of the city?\nThat is impossible!",
    ["Dialogue3181304"]="The soldiers of the guard army were on patrol and happened to witness the psychotic man attacking innocent people... They didn't have time to confirm the patient's identity at that time! How did Elle know?\nUnless... Unless.....",
    ["Dialogue3181305"]="——He's a prisoner!\n(you and officer Gerner came to the conclusion at the same time and see the surprise in each other's eyes)",
    ["Dialogue3181306"]="..... I see. I trust your judgment, Adventurer. This is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>transceiver</color> distributed by our guard. Keep it hidden. If you are ever in danger... Please signal to me immediately!",
    ["Dialogue3181401"]="... how's it going? Are the Epsilons all right?",
    ["Dialogue3181402"]="Really..... Then why do you have that expression on your face, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3181403"]="oh Do you want to ask me about this incident?\nWell... To be fair, as a Doctor, I quite appreciate the ability of this \"divine envoy\". Although I don't know what method he used, but he can cure what we thought were incurable diseases. This could be seen as an act of God!",
    ["Dialogue3181404"]="(the doctor shrugs as if he didn't care what you said)\nThere is no such thing as a free lunch in this world. In the final analysis, you will always have to make a choice.\n... but is that all you want to ask, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3181405"]="(hearing what you have said, he smiles with interest)\n... go on, Adventurer. What you have deduced from this is very interesting to me.",
    ["Dialogue3181406"]="... hahaha... Hahaha! What a surprise! Adventurer! You thought very hard about this!\n(suddenly, he let out a wild laugh, and he looks at you completely crazed)\nYou’re correct! The symbols on the posters represent <color=#CA2E0AFF>Haila, the goddess of disaster</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3181407"]="... on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>contrary</color> to the divinity, in the myth, the God in charge of <color=#CA2E0AFF>administering and creative medicine</color> and the most trusted waiter of Diva Frigga... Is the female warrior god named Elle.\n(the person standing in front of you smiles with a wildness. He slowly and carefully takes off his mask. Shockingly revealing a familiar face)\nCongratulations, Adventurer... You found <color=#CA2E0AFF>me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3181501"]="... you never let me down, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3181502"]="Oh, what's the matter? Are you not excited to see an old friend?",
    ["Dialogue3181503"]="... a conspiracy? No, no, I am benefiting all of mankind! Do you see the strength of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart? Even if it's just a <color=#CA2E0AFF>replica</color>... It can cure many stubborn and incurable diseases that are impossible for modern medicine to cure today! Look at Como! His left leg, which was chronically disabled is now stronger than any ordinary person’s leg! And Palin, she was deaf at birth. I let her hear the voice of the world again!",
    ["Dialogue3181504"]="As for the Epsilon family... Do you know how serious their disease is? Without me... Everyone in their family would never have lived to be over 40!",
    ["Dialogue3181505"]="Ha... As I said, Adventurer, they were presented with a choice. I never forced them to accept my offer, but you don’t understand their desire for strength. The principle thought of alchemy is exchanging things of equal value... I just receive my due reward.",
    ["Dialogue3181506"]="Let me guess, is that officer Gerner on the other side of the transceiver? Did you let him hear our conversation in order to have me arrested?\n(Baroshev smiles again, and you begin to smell something fishy)\n... unfortunately, will things really go as smoothly as you expected?",
    ["Dialogue3181601"]="Don't move!\nI never expected it to be you, the cause of all these cases, Dr. Elle... Or, maybe I should call you Baroshevf?",
    ["Dialogue3181602"]="A name is only a name. Please feel free to call me however you would like Mr Gerner. But if you want to arrest me... I'm afraid they will have to answer no.",
    ["Dialogue3181603"]="What did you say?",
    ["Dialogue3181604"]="Put the gun down!!!",
    ["Dialogue3181701"]="Stop it!\nSir! You have no right to arrest him!",
    ["Dialogue3181702"]="Are you from... The Alchemist Guild?\n(Gerner frowns at the uninvited guests, his eyes fixed on the silver badge on the intruder’s chest)",
    ["Dialogue3181703"]="Now that you know who I am, I don't have to bother. According to the cooperation treaty signed between the Alchemist Guild and Aldebaran, all criminal cases related to the members of the guild should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>transferred to the alchemist guild</color> for independent trial and punishment. This is the transfer application written by President Nicholas himself and the prisoner’s identity certificate. Please have a look.",
    ["Dialogue3181704"]="... if there is no objection, we will take the prisoner to be held at trial at the alchemist guild.",
    ["Dialogue3181705"]="I can’t believe it! After so many days of hard investigation, we finally caught him and now.....!",
    ["Dialogue3181706"]="... stop it, Pierson. The seal on the transfer application is no fake. This case... Is no longer under our jurisdiction.",
    ["Dialogue3181707"]="It's very sensible of you to do so.\n(Ramda nodded slightly with a look of arrogance. He pointed to the two guild memebers standing beside Baroshev and ordered)\n... you, go and cuff him! Take him!",
    ["Dialogue3181708"]="Oh, well... It seems like we might not see each other for a while, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3181709"]="Tut Tut, then you think too highly of me, Adventurer. In this case, I'm just a gambler, but it happened that the goddess of luck chose to stand on my side\n(he pierces his lips and smiles arrogantly)",
    ["Dialogue3181710"]="Although just like a coin has two sides, one's luck is always 50/50. But if you’re careful and use the right method, the coin thrown upward... Will certainly appear the side I planned for.",
    ["Dialogue3181711"]="(Baroshev pretentiously raises his eyebrows and whistles)\nThank you for your advice, Adventurer. I'll keep it in mind. But now... I have to go back to the guild and accept a just trial~",
    ["Dialogue3181712"]="Finally, as a souvenir of this meeting, let me leave you with a small gift.\n(he throws something in his hand at you, and the silver light crosses a circular arc in the air, and then falls firmly in the palm of your hand. It's a delicate coin)\nSee you later... Adventurer",
    ["Dialogue3190101"]="Please stay a while, brave Adventurer. Could you please kindly offer me help?",
    ["Dialogue3190102"]="It's about my student Trinity... I saw her rushing over to Zenhai Marsh this morning. She hasn't come back yet. This is the first she's ever left to do something like this without telling me... She is always quiet, but she never had me worried before. It was quite abnormal.",
    ["Dialogue3190103"]="You guessed it. I'd like your <color=#CA2E0AFF>help finding her</color>, Adventurer. You should know that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color> is very close to the dragons' cave, and so monsters do show up from time to time... It's certainly not a safe place for a young lady.",
    ["Dialogue3190104"]="Why do I... I... Uh...\n(The blond bard sighs all of a sudden. He dips his head as if in defeat.)",
    ["Dialogue3190105"]="I suppose I should be straight with you... Actually she didn't just leave for no reason. We had had a bad argument. I'm afraid I might have gone a bit overboard in some of the things I said... and I must be the last person she'd want to see right now. But if you could persuade her for me... I'd be very grateful.",
    ["Dialogue3190106"]="Wonderful! Thank you so much, Adventurer. Oh, besides... please let me know if Trinity does anything <color=#CA2E0AFF>really unusual</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3190107"]="Lately I've been getting the feeling Trinity's up to something she doesn't want me to know about... I noticed her putting some stuff away as soon as I came to her. Adventurer, I'm not asking you to pry into her secrets. I simply consider Trinity my greatest student, and don't want to see her get mixed up in anything... As her teacher, I have my reasons, please understand.",
    ["Dialogue3190201"]="...\n(You see a lady in a beautiful green outfit crouching behind a nearby tree. She seems to be gazing intently at some sort of meal on the ground.)",
    ["Dialogue3190202"]="...Shh. You'll frighten it away.",
    ["Dialogue3190203"]="(She ignores you while crouching in the shadows like a leopard about to pounce on its prey. Next, this leopard strikes so suddenly like lightning.)\n<size=26>Got you!</size> ",
    ["Dialogue3190301"]="In pieces... This one is useless.\n(The young lady looks down as she kicks away the crushed shells of a Tri Joint with some disgust.)",
    ["Dialogue3190302"]="None of your business, Adventurer.\n(She ignores you and focuses on twirling her dagger in the air, before deftly picking the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bones of the Tri Joint</color>.)\nI know. Master Orfeo sent you... but I'm not going back.",
    ["Dialogue3190303"]="I suggest you don't waste any more of your time here. I have something to do and I will not return before it is accomplished.",
    ["Dialogue3190401"]="Don't you know, Adventurer, what a boor you are for hanging around a girl who doesn't want to see your face? It's intensely irritating.",
    ["Dialogue3190402"]="(She rather coldly interrupts you.)\nI already told you. Have you not been listening? I'm not going back. I'd rather not waste my time trying to explain it. Once I collect enough of this moss, I'm going to collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>legs of the Nereid</color>. I don't have a lot of time, so leave me alone.",
    ["Dialogue3190501"]="Is this for me?",
    ["Dialogue3190502"]="(That may have done the trick. Trinity doesn't seem quite so hostile to your presence now.)\nIn that case... help me place this <color=#CA2E0AFF>insect legs and moss mixed dish</color> on some nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>open flat ground</color>. It's Alligators' favorite. I'm sure it'll attract one.",
    ["Dialogue3190601"]="...\n(The young lady remains sullenly quiet, only the quick motions of her dagger as she picks the bones of the insect filling the silence.)",
    ["Dialogue3190602"]="You Adventurers... Do you always have to get up in everybody's business?\n(She sighs almost as if resigned to your presence.)\nAlright then... because you helped me.",
    ["Dialogue3190603"]="I'm carrying a <color=#CA2E0AFF>red book</color> with me in my saddle. You can have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> of it... I don't have time to explain it to you.",
    ["Dialogue3190701"]="...This is why I'm collecting the bones of these monsters, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3190702"]="That's right. I want to see Tao Gunka, and I want it to fulfill my wish.",
    ["Dialogue3190703"]="...None of your business, Adventurer. Even if it was Master Orfeo that sent you here anyway... I don't think you have any right to snoop on my things.\n(Trinity turned her face away. Her tone is curt, but you can still detect a hint of shyness.)",
    ["Dialogue3190704"]="Do I hate him? Is that... Is that what my teacher told you?\n(Trinity's voice shakes. She turns to look at you, her bright emerald eyes gleaming brightly in the faint mist.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Hate him? How could I possibly hate him...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3190705"]="...Go, Adventurer.\nGo and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell Master Orfeo</color>: I am putting a stop to the whole matter. And from now on... I forbid him from feeling troubled at my fate.",
    ["Dialogue3190801"]="You've returned, Adventurer!\n(It seems that Orfeo has been anxiously awaiting your return for some time. He casts an eager glance over your shoulder. The disappointment in his face when he realizes you've returned alone is palpable.)\nTrinity... didn't want to come back?",
    ["Dialogue3190802"]="To summon... Tao Gunka? And did she have you read a book called \"Where to Find Magical Demons\"?",
    ["Dialogue3190803"]="No... I didn't, but I just... heard about it from a nearby merchant I know.\n(The blond bard rubs his lips anxiously. He seems quite unsettled.)\nDid... Did she tell you why she wanted to summon the demon?",
    ["Dialogue3190804"]="<color=#A1979FFF>\"Troubled\"? I-Is that how she sees it? Our interactions are troublesome?</color>\n(The light fades from Orfeo's eyes. He unconsciously clenches his hands, giving a sad note from the Lute within.)\n...I understand.",
    ["Dialogue3190805"]="If that is what Trinity wishes to do, then, as her teacher, I should at least try to support her cause... Could I trouble you to return then and help her, Adventurer? Regardless of what happens, she'll always be the most important student I've ever had. And could you... do your best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>protect her on my account</color>? I don't want her to come to any harm.",
    ["Dialogue3190901"]="Why are you back, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3190902"]="To help me? He wanted you... to help me complete what I wish to do sooner?\n(Trinity speaks slowly, deliberately enunciating every word. You glance at her face, her eyes red with emotion.)\nAlright then. Then help me, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3190903"]="I need these Nether Flowers to open the Circle of Spiritual Summons. But the petals were dead by the time I got here. And something tells me... <color=#CA2E0AFF>it's not an accident</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3191001"]="...So what's the deal with these Nereids? Could they be the ones destroying the Nether Flowers?",
    ["Dialogue3191002"]="(The young lady frowns at your answer.)\nBut the ground around us shows signs of human interference... don't you think it's a bit early to conclude that?",
    ["Dialogue3191003"]="Right... That's just what I thought. Besides Nereids' tracks around here, it's almost like something or someone has gone through the flowers. And I can't rule out human interference.",
    ["Dialogue3191004"]="Well, since we can't use the Nether Flowers, we may as well have a look at how the Dark Mushrooms are growing before we do anything else.",
    ["Dialogue3191101"]="It looks like we're just a bit too late once again, Adventurer.\n(Trinity looks at the destroyed flowers with a grim expression.)\n...Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a look</color> at if there are still <color=#CA2E0AFF>available Dark Mushrooms</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3191201"]="...Do you think it was some sort of monster that did this?",
    ["Dialogue3191202"]="(Trinity shakes her head in disagreement.)\nNo. The first time could have been a coincidence... but twice in a row? I'm pretty sure someone or something doesn't want this ceremony to take place.",
    ["Dialogue3191203"]="Right. Coincidences like this don't just happen: when I'm about to deploy the Circle, the monsters just happen to destroy all the materials I need?",
    ["Dialogue3191204"]="I suggest we have a look around the southwest corner of Papuchicha Forest. There's the last material I need there called Undying Grass. But I'm starting to worry... I might not even be able to get my hands on it.",
    ["Dialogue3191301"]="Oh? You're asking about Undying Grass?\n(He scratches his head in confusion.)\nThe village chief ordered us to cut it...",
    ["Dialogue3191302"]="As for the reason... I dunno. But it's something we do every now and then... You'd better ask Chief Norris. You'll find him in the house over to the northwest.",
    ["Dialogue3191401"]="(A kindly elder gentleman rubs his whiskers with a smile upon seeing the two of you.)\n(Cough) Is... that you, Trinity? What brings you here? Orfeo gave you another errand?",
    ["Dialogue3191402"]="Not this time, Chief. Nothing to do with him... I just have something to ask.\nI happened to notice your villagers are clearing away all the Undying Grass from those fields to the south... Did you ask them to do that?",
    ["Dialogue3191403"]="The Undying Grass? Oh yes, I did. Undying Grass tends to crowd everything out. Leave it and hardly anything else will grow nearby. Not to mention the soil is therefore getting poor. So we need to get rid of it every now and then for the sake of our regular crops... Is that strange to you?",
    ["Dialogue3191404"]="Then... did you also give the order to dispose of the Nether Flowers in the marsh, and the Dark Mushrooms on Kokomo Beach?",
    ["Dialogue3191405"]="...I'm not really sure what you're getting at, Trinity. Nether Flowers and Dark Mushrooms are both important cash crops. Why on earth would I want to destroy them?",
    ["Dialogue3191406"]="Nether Flowers... Dark Mushrooms.... and also Undying Grass?\n(Norris chews over the names of these plants in his mind. The truth dawns.)\nI see, Trinity... Don't tell me you've read \"Where to Find Magical Demons?\"",
    ["Dialogue3191407"]="You know about that, Chief? Well, then why would you...",
    ["Dialogue3191408"]="Well... I came across the book at a black market run by some pirates almost a year ago. I was perfectly aware that it contained techniques for summoning powerful evil demons. But the author's anonymous, and no one knows if this book is trustworthy or not. The other thing is... I don't want to put a stumbling block in the way of your future with Orfeo. That's up to you two to decide, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue3191409"]="(Trinity's eyes redden with emotion during his explanation.)\nChief, I...",
    ["Dialogue3191410"]="I take it our Adventurer has no idea what happened between you two?\nThen again it's not exactly a secret nowadays... Trinity and Orfeo are great heroes to all of us, heroes who five years ago drove the evil Tao Gunka out and protected this village from calamity.",
    ["Dialogue3191411"]="...The problem is that Tao Gunka is a demon who is said to drink from the Fountain of All Knowledge. So naturally he has the great power to <color=#CA2E0AFF>change the future</color> and the malevolence to use it. He cursed Trinity and Orfeo in revenge...",
    ["Dialogue3191412"]="(Trinity looks down. The unkempt state of her dress seems in this moment to reflect the complexity of her feelings.)\n...Yes, Adventurer. After that campaign, my teacher and I... we... were compelled to be together forever in a romantic sense. And we both would lose our lives if either one of us left the other.",
    ["Dialogue3191413"]="... Difficult though it is, I cannot say that this curse was entirely outside the will of Odin.\n(Norris shakes his head. His eyes remain sharp even if dimmed by age.)\nTrinity... Have you asked yourself recently whether it really is that important to remove the curse?",
    ["Dialogue3191414"]="I'm afraid I don't quite get your meaning, Chief.",
    ["Dialogue3191415"]="I remember how the pair of you have cleaved to one another these years, traveling about to search for Tao Gunka... and actually I had an inkling you would end up together even without that curse. I honestly think, Trinity... you have to see the forest through the trees.",
    ["Dialogue3191416"]="Of course, if you've determined in your heart that you want to summon Tao Gunka, I'm not going to stop you. The Undying Grass we cleared away hasn't been burned. And I'm sure the village warehouse has more than enough Dark Mushrooms and Nether Flowers for your purposes since we do keep them. And if you do want them... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Toland, the warehouse manager</color> is the man to find.",
    ["Dialogue3191501"]="Oh... An instruction from the Chief?\n(The dutiful warehouse manager rubs his head nervously as he explains where to find the goods.)",
    ["Dialogue3191502"]="You can find the Nether Flowers and Dark Mushrooms on the outermost racks in the warehouse. As for the Undying Grass we cut... if I recall, we deposited the whole bunch in an open area up ahead. Take as much as you want.",
    ["Dialogue3191503"]="Thank you, Toland. So, Adventurer, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>prepare what we need</color> and then <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the summoning site</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3191601"]="...Here it is, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3191602"]="I've finished the dark pentagram according to the book. Can I get you now to place the <color=#CA2E0AFF>remaining materials in their proper locations around the Summoning Circle</color>? I'll take care of the monster bones in the Eye of the Circle. And those plants... I'll leave you to them.",
    ["Dialogue3191701"]="Get your stinky paws off my face, you disgusting human! Don't you know that you are speaking to the mighty demon of old, Tao Gunka!? Bow before me in worship... Ouch?!\n(The demon at your foot takes one look at Trinity and then suddenly stops talking. It seems utterly shocked.)\n You... You again?!",
    ["Dialogue3191702"]="I... I didn't do anything to you! What's wrong with you, always trying to summon me?\n(The round-faced demon seems to feel hard-done-by, crying out in pain.)\nWh-What the heck are you trying to do?",
    ["Dialogue3191703"]="I would you like to... I want you to...<color=#A1979FFF> remove the curse...</color>\n(Something has gone wrong for Trinity. Her voice falters, becoming quieter and quieter until she stops speaking.)",
    ["Dialogue3191704"]="Nothing... If that's what my teacher wants, I'll do whatever it takes to help him achieve it. But...",
    ["Dialogue3191705"]="Well... I want him to be free again. He's a traveled and well-read minstrel of thousand famous songs... A true hero, and an eagle who should soar rather than be chained to my side... What an insult to him!\n<color=#A1979FFF>And... what an insult to my feelings for him...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3191706"]="Hang on, hang on! Are you talking about... that \"curse\" five years ago?\nY-You summoned me to remove that curse?",
    ["Dialogue3191707"]="Yes...",
    ["Dialogue3191708"]="You... idiots! What is wrong with you people? There was no curse! I didn't do anything! I made it up to get back at you! You hear me? <size=26>It's a total lie!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3191709"]="Curses are difficult to execute at the best of times, let alone a curse to span two persons' entire lives... Why would I waste my valuable energy on frustrating a pair of stupid humans? But you made me look bad by punching my handsome face! So I went one better: I made up this curse to scare you through.",
    ["Dialogue3191710"]="That was... a trick? There was no curse?",
    ["Dialogue3191711"]="Exactly! I was <color=#CA2E0AFF>just messing with you</color>!\nAnd another thing... didn't your supposed \"teacher\" <color=#CA2E0AFF>know this all along</color>? He summoned me a year ago in the same way. Don't you ever talk to each other?<size=26>Hey, hey!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3191712"]="(Tao Gunka cries out in horror. Her eyes going red, the lady in green turns around and hurries to the exit.)\nWh-Where are you going?<size=26> Don't go! No, stay!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3191713"]="...Why does she run, Adventurer? I haven't even heard her wish yet.\n(The demon wrestles to break free of the Circle. You release your foot. It tries to vault out, but seems restrained as if by an invisible force. It's stuck.)\n<size=26>How do I get out of this stupid thing if I don't fulfill her wish?</size>",
    ["Dialogue3191714"]="(Tao Gunka gulps, casts an eye toward your warm-hearted smile, and then opens his mouth in trepidation.)\nWould you... care to take over her wish then, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3191715"]="Hey, hey! Don't abandon me!\n(You <color=#CA2E0AFF>run hurriedly after</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trinity's</color> departing figure to the shouts and howls of Tao Gunka behind you.)",
    ["Dialogue3191801"]="...You knew it all along?\n(Trinity and Orfeo are already well-engaged in conversation by the time you catch up to her. The blond bard is having trouble meeting Trinity's eye level. He looks defeated and spent.)",
    ["Dialogue3191802"]="Master... why didn't you tell me that the curse was a lie? You could have been free. You could have gone to see the world, writing about new mountains and oceans in your songs. Rather than just being... stuck with me, imprisoned on this lonely island...",
    ["Dialogue3191803"]="Imprisoned? Trinity, you have no idea. This island may mean a prison to you... but a family to me.",
    ["Dialogue3191804"]="(Orfeo looks really tired. Darkness gathers in his gray-purple eyes. He seems on the point of despair.)\nI'm not all you think I am. I have my want and need too... that is, to keep you with me—<color=#CA2E0AFF>I've always admired and loved you</color>, Trinity.",
    ["Dialogue3191805"]="I summoned Tao Gunka after coming across that book in the pirate's market. I already had some idea then there is no curse, and the curse had nothing to do with why I want to be with you. After fighting shoulder-to-shoulder for so many years, I've already...",
    ["Dialogue3191806"]="I resolved that day, Trinity, to tell you the truth plainly... But when it came to that moment, you excitedly announced that you had embarked on your own quest to meet Tao Gunka... I couldn't look directly into your joyful eyes, which made me feel myself less of a man. I concealed everything, finagling you to my side... As things went on, I just couldn't figure out how to tell you...",
    ["Dialogue3191807"]="That was me... I had a moment of sheer panic when I realized you'd found the book too and were going to summon Tao Gunka following its instructions. I was terrified that you would leave me once you found out the curse wasn't real... so I had the Nether Flowers and Dark Mushrooms destroyed.",
    ["Dialogue3191808"]="(Orfeo is having trouble looking at Trinity. His sense of embarrassment is clearly out of something more than his hidden love.)\nI'm just so sad that you had to see this side of me, Trinity, of your supposedly \"great teacher.\" I'm merely a coward.",
    ["Dialogue3191809"]="No, no, that's not true... I don't think... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I mean, I wasn't necessarily trying to lift the curse</color>. <color=#A1979FFF>Actually I also, uh...</color>\n(Blushing bashfully, Trinity speaks softly as she continues to nervously fidget with the outlines of her dress.)",
    ["Dialogue3191810"]="You didn't want to lift the curse? Then... are you saying that...?\n(The bard has finally found himself without words. You can't help but give him a hand.)",
    ["Dialogue3191811"]="Right, right... But then... what should I do?\n(With a rare confusion, Orfeo plays a few strings of Lute, producing a kind of meaningful dark melody.)",
    ["Dialogue3191812"]="Ahem-ahem! Behave! Behave yourself, Adventurer!\n(The legendary bard shoots you a look that could kill as he goes red in the face. You quickly hide your face in your hands, watching the proceedings through your fingers.)",
    ["Dialogue3191813"]="Master, I would like to... ask you...",
    ["Dialogue3191814"]="...Ahem, hold on. The Adventurer is right... It's not the time for \"ladies first.\"\n(You can faintly make out the blond bard drops to one knee, his face brushing, as he delicately and nervously clasps the hands of the young lady before him. He gives the back of her hand a light kiss.)\nThis should have been said a long time ago, but it's still not too late...",
    ["Dialogue3191815"]="Trinity, will you... marry me?",
    ["Dialogue3191901"]="(The size and shape of the shoe prints in the mud seem to have been left by a somewhat petite lady.)",
    ["Dialogue3192001"]="(You also see a scattering of what look like monster claw markings and drops of blood nearby, as well as a rather nice emerald-colored veil trampled into the mud...)",
    ["Dialogue3192101"]="(The earth here is particularly soft after having been moved recently, and you can find nearby traces of broken twigs and purple flower petals. Examination reveals occasional claw prints from monsters and the impact of what must have been a round and slightly sharp object...)",
    ["Dialogue3192201"]="(The earth here is particularly soft after having been moved recently. Examination reveals occasional claw prints from monsters and the impact of what must have been a <color=#CA2E0AFF>round and slightly sharpened bow end</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3200101"]="<color=#A1979FFF>I just don't know what to do... Am I going to my death?</color>",
    ["Dialogue3200102"]="Not well... Not well at all! I'm going to my death... (Sobbing)",
    ["Dialogue3200103"]="Isn't it obvious? I've been sent to Saint Darmain East to investigate <color=#CA2E0AFF>you-know-who</color>! What are they doing sending a rookie like me? Oh—wait!\nYou're that—<size=26>legendary Adventurer who hangs around the leader, aren't you?</size> ",
    ["Dialogue3200104"]="Y-You would be willing to help me?\n(A wave of relief mixed with surprise washes over the young pirate's face. He vigorously clasps you by the hands and gives an encouraging shake. His voice is crackling with gratitude.)",
    ["Dialogue3200105"]="Well... she's actually a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bounty hunter</color> who's been hunting down our brethren! She and her <color=#CA2E0AFF>red longbow</color> just showed up in the waters of Comodo about a month ago. She doesn't care for love or money, just killing pirates. And she's very good at it. Lost quite a few squads recently, just in the last few days...",
    ["Dialogue3200106"]="And we just got word our main hideout in Saint Darmain Southeast is under attack! Spencer was worried we, I mean the Gangash Pirates, were her next target. That's why he had everyone move to a <color=#CA2E0AFF>makeshift base on the beach west</color> to keep Captain Drake safe. I was sent with a few brothers to get a handle on her movements over in Saint Darmain East... B-But we...",
    ["Dialogue3200107"]="Of course! She's not a lady, she's a demon! A pirate-killing monster!\nSo Adventurer, would you be willing to help us? All we need you to do is just take a look around Saint Darmain East and let us know if she's around... if you see anything at all. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Drake</color> is waiting for an answer!",
    ["Dialogue3200201"]="...It must be her. I've waited years for this day... and now it's here.",
    ["Dialogue3200202"]="...Ha. How could I not?\n(Spencer laughs bitterly as he takes the arrow from your hands and throws it to the ground angrily in a demonstration of contempt.)\nTwo-timing traitor! So she found the courage to return, did she?",
    ["Dialogue3200203"]="Adventurer, this one-eye symbol on the arrow belongs to none other than the lady <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cecil Devine</color>, Captain Drake's adopted daughter, and former fellow Gangash Pirates. We took her in as a babe, clothed her, gave her food, taught her how to fight, made her into a woman who can take care of herself... and how does she repay us? Words cannot express it!",
    ["Dialogue3200204"]="Forget it... Spencer. What's the use of going on and on about it?",
    ["Dialogue3200205"]="But Cap! We wouldn't have endured the loss of so many brothers if she hadn't sold us out to the bounty hunters.! We should thank our lucky stars she's back because this is just our chance—",
    ["Dialogue3200206"]="<size=26>Bad news, Captain!</size> ",
    ["Dialogue3200301"]="Captain! The brethren... sent to trade with the villagers of Saint Darmain West... were attacked!",
    ["Dialogue3200302"]="<size=26>Attacked?!</size>\nDo you think it's...?",
    ["Dialogue3200303"]="Yes, Cecil! I got to see her face clearly! She had a red longbow. She took some of the brothers hostages and told us... she told us...\n(The young underling's face turns a pallid white as he whispers his next words to the Corsair.)\nShe said she'll only spare their lives in exchange for yours, my Captain...",
    ["Dialogue3200304"]="Where does she get the right!?\nAdventurer! It's high time I made a formal request for your help—<color=#CA2E0AFF>help us capture this traitor</color> so I can slit her neck myself!",
    ["Dialogue3200305"]="Need I remind you the Gangash Piratess are currently allies of your leader? We should expect some assistance, just as your leader does from us. I don't think they would appreciate it if we Gangash Piratess were suddenly to lose our leader. Think of all the infighting and renegotiated treaties... Adventurer, we're all in the same boat!",
    ["Dialogue3200306"]="(The veteran Corsair seems to wrinkle his brow in disapproval of his underling's methods.)\nSpencer, what happened was between me and Cecil. You'd best stay out of it.",
    ["Dialogue3200307"]="We'd love to, but she won't let us, will she?\nYou see how many brothers she's laid to rest already? And a fair few of 'em never got involved in <color=#CA2E0AFF>that event years ago</color>... That sounds fair to you? Listen, Cap: this has got to end now!",
    ["Dialogue3200308"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Sheesh...</color>\n(Drake shakes his head in stern refusal. He sighs the way a person does when ready to accept a terrible compromise.)",
    ["Dialogue3200401"]="S-Save me!",
    ["Dialogue3200402"]="It's the traitor... Cecil!\nThat pirate-killing bounty hunter... She took our wares first, and then our brothers too...",
    ["Dialogue3200403"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>North</color>... They were headed <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3200501"]="...This is the first time we've ever met, isn't it, Adventurer? Unless I'm mistaken. So what interest do you have in my business? And why would you get in my way?",
    ["Dialogue3200502"]="They called me a pirate-killing monster, eh? And asked you to come and find me, eh? \n(Cecil stares at you with a terrible, cold intensity behind those amber eyes.) \nHa. Let it never be said that the pirates lack a sense of humor...",
    ["Dialogue3200503"]="Let me guess... Captain Drake told you he lovingly took me in, raised me, and that I became a terrible traitor for selling out the Gangash Pirates. Ring a bell?",
    ["Dialogue3200504"]="Ha... so I guess they left out the bit about how I became an orphan? \nI only became an orphan because they plundered my parents' village, and then burned everyone alive!",
    ["Dialogue3200505"]="I was the only survivor of that terrible fire... But even this wasn't enough for him. You think Drake took me in out of kindness? Because he felt bad? Far from it. He only took me in out of his sick sense of humor... He just loved the idea of raising a child on bread obtained from her parents' death... and the psychological torture of having to live next to the one who killed them!",
    ["Dialogue3200506"]="...I'll never forgive, nor forget! You know what he did after I crawled my way out of the ruins of my village? He found it so hilarious. He had me chained to the bottom of the ship, took my weapons, and force-fed me by dislocating my jaw...",
    ["Dialogue3200507"]="...I lived. Yes, how I wanted to die in those days, but I lived. Dying would have been easier. The only thing that kept me going was the desire for revenge.",
    ["Dialogue3200508"]="Misunderstanding? Hah. Well, there's no time like the present for clearing it up. Why don't you take me to Drake yourself? \nThen I'll be able to talk to him <color=#CA2E0AFF>face-to-face</color>. It'll give you the perfect chance to see who's lying... and who deserves to die.",
    ["Dialogue3200601"]="Looks like I win, Adventurer. Still want to hear Drake's another word? He's obviously fled in terror, happy enough to leave his so-called brothers to the dogs...",
    ["Dialogue3200602"]="(Cecil gives a half-conscious pirate on the ground a sharp kick.) \n<color=#A1979FFF>What a shame... Where did you run off to? Don't forget. I know all your tricks. You were a good teacher.</color>",
    ["Dialogue3200603"]="(She doesn't answer, but crouches down to stare intently at a smattering of footprints nearby. A confident smile begins to form.) \n...Looks like I found you, Drake.",
    ["Dialogue3200604"]="Yes... They're different from the others. His left boot presses harder than his right... because I managed to stick a poison arrow in his right foot three years ago. Made him a cripple.",
    ["Dialogue3200605"]="It's time I did the same to his whole body. As for you, I really hope you don't interfere. You seem like a well-meaning person. You don't need to stick your neck out for those good-for-nothing pirates.",
    ["Dialogue3200606"]="(She stares intently at you with a hint of warning in her eyes.) \n...But if you'd rather play Drake's useful idiot, I'm warning you: you'll share their fate, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3200701"]="<color=#A1979FFF>No way... Captain... Don't go...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3200702"]="Mint... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Peppermint</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3200801"]="Th-Thank you, Adventurer. I feel a lot better now.",
    ["Dialogue3200802"]="It was... Captain Drake... \n(Spencer isn't his confident self as usual, struggling to get the words out. You think you can guess what happened.)",
    ["Dialogue3200803"]="Yeah. Cut us loose... but that's not the whole story. I remember he used to keep... what was it? Oh... his <color=#CA2E0AFF>diary</color>. Over there. Read it and you'll understand.",
    ["Dialogue3200901"]="By now you should be getting a better idea of what happened. Here's the truth... Captain really didn't want to hurt anyone in Cecil's village. It was more about self-defense than anything else. No one expected things to go south so quickly... and all of us warned him against taking that kid in. There were other ways of saving her. Sounded pretty dangerous to me. But he...",
    ["Dialogue3200902"]="He thought he'd crossed a line, and was determined to make it up to someone, darn it all. You know, he never told Cecil the truth. He was smart enough to know what could happen... but...",
    ["Dialogue3200903"]="Adventurer, I'm not saying Cecil's completely out of left field, but I don't think it's fair. We really did try to take care of her. And Cap never forgave himself. So she wants revenge, OK. But doesn't she have the right to know <color=#CA2E0AFF>the whole story</color> first?",
    ["Dialogue3200904"]="I'm guessing... he's probably on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Queen's Revenge</color>. That's where our story got started.",
    ["Dialogue3201001"]="...You again. Don't tell me you've got a death wish. So get away from him right now or I'll... \n(She aims the blood-red longbow square in your direction. Her steely amber eyes signal this is not an empty threat.) \nYour brains will be all over that filthy balustrade before you know it.",
    ["Dialogue3201002"]="Why the heck not? My father, mother, friends, and my homeland... were all ruined in his fire... I'm alive today for one reason only: revenge!",
    ["Dialogue3201003"]="What is this...?",
    ["Dialogue3201004"]="... \n(Under your sincere gaze, Cecil opened the diary. To the rustling of old pages flipping, her expressions start to change.) \nDrake...",
    ["Dialogue3201005"]="Remember why you are here, Cecil. \nNo matter what this says, I'll never ask for your forgiveness. I was ready to embrace this ending the day I adopted you.",
    ["Dialogue3201006"]="Do not meddle, Adventurer. This is between her and me. \n(The Corsair squints. You've seen the same warning in Cecil's amber eyes before.)",
    ["Dialogue3201007"]="I won't forget my purpose, but Drake... I'm not you, nor will become like you. \n(The girl squints and you're puzzled, since the mannerism reminds you of Drake.)",
    ["Dialogue3201008"]="I changed my mind. You're not fit for a merciful death yet, Drake. \nMy loved ones wailed in the fire for a whole day and night, for which you shall pay back in hundred folds. I want you to remember the nightmare they went through every day of your miserable life from this point on.",
    ["Dialogue3201009"]="You shall regret, remorse, repent, with all this pain etched in your soul until the day you die... \n(She raises her head proudly, eyes glistening in confidence.)",
    ["Dialogue3201010"]="Until that day, apologize to my loved one in the abyss, Drake.",
    ["Dialogue3201101"]="(A pirate falls, breathless. Examination reveals a deep arrow hole over his heart, but the arrow is missing...)",
    ["Dialogue3201201"]="(This pirate is also shot, the wound between the eyes seems to be a testament to the killer's superior archery skills...)",
    ["Dialogue3201301"]="(There's a broken shaft on sand. Examination reveals a special mark resembling an eye near the fletching of the arrow.)",
    ["Dialogue3201401"]="(Pirates sprawled on the ground, unconscious. Looking around, you don't see Drake Gangash...)",
    ["Dialogue3210101"]="Don't get excited yet. I understand how you feel. This is certainly a discovery that can rewrite history, but it must be backed by undisputable proof. From what clues we have so far, it's just theory...",
    ["Dialogue3210102"]="We'll need more people if we want to look further into it... Huh? \n(Walsh turns to you.) \nHere, Adventurer, over here!",
    ["Dialogue3210103"]="What else but the help of a legendary Adventurer, of course! \nYou heard what Instructor Salisbury just said, right? If you could help us prove the new discovery, you'll forever leave your mark on history!",
    ["Dialogue3210104"]="Have you heard about how the Ice Cave of Comodo was formed? Before, scholars always believed the ice in the cave came from a cold wave thousands of years ago, since the north side has an inward funnel gap that compressed and filtered cold ocean air into the cave... But, the Eden Group's findings over the last few days could overturn that!",
    ["Dialogue3210105"]="You're interested too? We do have a lot in common!",
    ["Dialogue3210106"]="(Salisbury notices that you're reluctant and implores you to help with sincerity. You just can't decline someone who lent you a hand during the hard time.) \nTo be honest, Adventurer, as an archaeologist, I cannot overlook the new leads Walsh has brought or the possibilities they entailed. It would be wonderful if you would help.",
    ["Dialogue3210107"]="Well then, I shall explain more to you in detail later in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>caves of Comodo</color>! Please get ready and meet me there!",
    ["Dialogue3210201"]="These are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>rock samples</color> we dug up from the depth of the chasm, Adventurer. Come <color=#CA2E0AFF>see</color> how they're different from normal rocks.",
    ["Dialogue3210301"]="Have you noticed the difference between the samples and normal rocks?",
    ["Dialogue3210302"]="That's right, these are all characteristics of <color=#CA2E0AFF>magma rocks</color>! \nOdd, isn't it, for volcanic magma rocks to be in the chasm of an ice cave... Or perhaps this cave was originally full of lava?",
    ["Dialogue3210303"]="I know what you mean. Comodo is a volcanic island, so it's not out of the ordinary for it to have lava caves... But it will reduce the conclusion of the ocean air bringing cold wave that froze the cave to rubbish!",
    ["Dialogue3210304"]="Let's not even debate whether such intense cold wave ever happened and assume it did... Then, how it didn't affect the volcanos on Comodo but the cave that was sealed?",
    ["Dialogue3210305"]="I got other evidence, Adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, I'll take you there right now!",
    ["Dialogue3210401"]="Come check out these Ice Vein samples scrapped off from the rock surface. See anything unusual?",
    ["Dialogue3210501"]="Notice anything, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3210502"]="(Walsh rubs his chin proudly in approval of your answer.) \nKeen observation, Adventurer! As the reward, Mr. Walsh will give you another clue...",
    ["Dialogue3210503"]="Remember the Ice Vein we found from the Megalodon? We compared the two samples and found the magical pulses on both to be almost identical... Furthermore, we found the same energy on even older biological fossils!",
    ["Dialogue3210504"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer! You'll be astounded by what you see!",
    ["Dialogue3210601"]="Come <color=#CA2E0AFF>see the bone</color>. According to records, this is the Ancient Dragon that signed the Peace Treaty of Comodo with Lady Margaret. Over the last few days, we dusted off the calcium deposits on the bones and found certain <color=#CA2E0AFF>peculiar traits</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3210701"]="Notice the streaky scars on the bones? Examination indicated the scars formed very long ago and matched the time of the dragon's death, about <color=#CA2E0AFF>a thousand years</color> back... Also, the residual magic energy in it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>almost identical</color> to that found in previous Ice Vein samples.",
    ["Dialogue3210702"]="That means these ancient creatures very likely met a major disaster in the cave! Regardless of whether that was a cold wave, it certainly has to do with the magic energy on the dragon's remnant!",
    ["Dialogue3210703"]="Too bad no one in the Eden Group is proficient with magic, and that has bottlenecked the research.",
    ["Dialogue3210704"]="What? You know the leader of the Mage Guild? \nThis is great, Adventurer! Can you invite her here and examine the magic on the bones?",
    ["Dialogue3210705"]="You said she's busy? I can see that. She's the leader of a guild, after all. In that case, would you mind taking the bone fragment to Geffen for me?",
    ["Dialogue3210706"]="But such precious relic shouldn't be disassembled or moved casually. We must first collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>sour berries</color> favored by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Megalith</color>, as well as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>venomous spit</color> of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gargoyle</color> to make the fumigant for preserving relics.",
    ["Dialogue3210801"]="All right, I made a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fumigant</color> out of the raw materials to provide a protective film to buffer against damage in removal and transition.",
    ["Dialogue3210802"]="Now, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply the fumigant evenly on the bone's surface</color>, then gently <color=#CA2E0AFF>remove the fragment</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3210901"]="Wow, you're doing much better than a beginner would! If you ever quit adventuring, maybe you can join me in the Eden Group? Don't worry, you'll be treated nicely!",
    ["Dialogue3210902"]="Come on... We're too tight to be haggling over pay now, aren't we?",
    ["Dialogue3210903"]="Hey, be gentle with that bone! It's super expensive! And another thing... \n(Walsh shouts behind you. The echo bounces throughout the vast, empty cave.)",
    ["Dialogue3210904"]="The instructor and I will wait for you at the Eden Group's base! Please come back from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen</color> soon... soon... soon...",
    ["Dialogue3211001"]="Please halt, Adventurer! I feel strong magic energy coming off you... Are you carrying a rare artifact? May I see it?",
    ["Dialogue3211002"]="It's a bone of a creature? \n(Jesqurienne carefully rubs the surface and the glow responds to her touch, trailing after her fingers.) \nThis is marvelous... Never thought I'd see long-lost magic like this.",
    ["Dialogue3211003"]="The energy on this bone is very special, and figures in the streaky pattern... Yes, this is the legendary magic known as Aurora.",
    ["Dialogue3211004"]="I'm ashamed to admit I thought I'd never come in contact with lost magic. Unfortunately, I cannot disclose the specific reason... But luck would have it, on the shelf behind you is the book, <color=#CA2E0AFF>The Rise & Fall of Ancient Magic</color>, with included terminologies for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aurora magic</color>. Why don't you get it and we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> together?",
    ["Dialogue3211101"]="So that means Nithil not just created Aurora magic, but only he has mastered it... \n(Jesqurienne stares at the fragment in your hand with infinite longing.) \nSorry for being blunt, but would you sell this to the Mage Guild?",
    ["Dialogue3211102"]="The Ancient Dragon's bone? Oh my... I'm so sorry and I take back what I said. Relics like this belong with the Eden Group. \nHowever, why would traces of Nithil's magic be on the Ancient Dragon?",
    ["Dialogue3211103"]="(Jesqurienne ponders for a while and shakes her head.) \nNo. While Nithil and Margaret are close friends, he never set foot on Comodo in his life... That's all I know.",
    ["Dialogue3211104"]="The collection in the Mage Guild isn't comprehensive, so if you want to learn about the life of Nithil, it's better to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit the Great Sage Kroneika</color>. As a descendant of the Heine family, he'd know much more than I do.",
    ["Dialogue3211201"]="Ah, it's been a long time, successor of the Odin's Bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue3211202"]="You want to know about Mr. Nithil? I recall on the bookshelf in the sage's cabin is a diary he kept during his time there. If you're interested, I don't see any problem in <color=#CA2E0AFF>letting you read it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3211301"]="Just like what we discussed. First, calm everyone down. Second... \n(Alexia notices you in midst of talking to the guards, pauses briefly and gives you a big smile.) \nOh, it's you, Adventurer. How can I help you?",
    ["Dialogue3211302"]="Margaret's correspondences? I know they are important documents sealed in the antechambers flanking her tomb... What do you want with them?",
    ["Dialogue3211303"]="For the Eden Group? No way, My Lady! Absolutely not!",
    ["Dialogue3211304"]="Quiet. I know what I'm doing. \n(Alexia glared at the guard before she smiles at you again.)",
    ["Dialogue3211305"]="Worry not, since I already promised to have the Eden Group open to all ruins on Comodo for excavation, I will not go back on my words. However, the chambers are dark, cluttered, and inconvenient. Why don't I get someone to retrieve any information you need and put it in the main hall for you?",
    ["Dialogue3211306"]="Okay, I'll make the arrangement. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>notify the Eden Group</color> as soon as possible, then we'll go to the east side of Saint Darmain and visit Margaret's tomb.",
    ["Dialogue3211401"]="You're back, Adventurer! How did it go?",
    ["Dialogue3211402"]="The leader consented to us examining Margaret's grave goods? \n(Salisbury strokes his mustache, somewhat surprised.)",
    ["Dialogue3211403"]="Although she did promise excavation to Eden Group before passing away, but it is sacred ground for the Nerius family with connections to the Heine family. It would have been understandable for her to turn it down. \n<color=#A1979FFF>How unexpected... It seems the leader has made up her mind this time...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3211404"]="Of course. No matter what lies ahead, Eden Group's goal always has been to reveal the historical truth. \nWalsh, please inspect the... \n(No sooner Salisbury looks his way, he's cut off by an excited Walsh.)",
    ["Dialogue3211405"]="All instruments are ready! I can't wait to see what's really buried in the tomb! \n<size=26>I'll be going now, instructor!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3211501"]="Hurry, Adventurer! Nerius servants have retrieved Margaret's correspondences from the antechambers. Let us begin!",
    ["Dialogue3211502"]="Wait, Walsh, have you forgotten what I said? To preserve the relics, we must...",
    ["Dialogue3211503"]="I know, I know! We must apply gladiolus fluid to the hands to prevent the oil and sweat on our skin from damaging precious documents... I already smeared it on myself! \n(Walsh proudly holds up both hands, which are indeed covered in a layer of shiny liquid.) \nI can start once it's dry!",
    ["Dialogue3211504"]="Oh, uh... \n(Walsh stares blankly at you.) \nI forgot to bring some for you...",
    ["Dialogue3211505"]="How about you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gladiolus fluid</color> yourself...? It's on the entrance lot, very close by!",
    ["Dialogue3211506"]="Sorry, Adventurer, you must do that in order to preserve these documents. \nWalsh and I will start looking over the documents. Come back when you're done <color=#CA2E0AFF>applying</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>gladiolus fluid</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3211601"]="That is the scent of the gladiolus fluid. Now you don't have to worry about ruining the documents with the oil and sweat on your hands.",
    ["Dialogue3211602"]="Walsh and I found the <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> you mentioned among the documents. From the signature, it was from Mr. Nithil. Come <color=#CA2E0AFF>see it with us</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3211701"]="Instructor, Adventurer, look! This is Margaret's response to Mr. Nithil! \n<color=#A1979FFF>Odd, if it was written, why wasn't it sent?</color>",
    ["Dialogue3211702"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Read it</color> and then you'll find out.",
    ["Dialogue3211801"]="It seems to be the whole truth. \n(Salisbury lets out a long sigh. For the moment, he seems to gaze into the ancient past.)",
    ["Dialogue3211802"]="A thousand years ago, despite signing the Peace Treaty of Comodo, Margaret was still concerned that the powerful dragons will reemerge. To protect her land, she commissioned Great Sage Nithil to cast Aurora magic and seal the searing cave with Dragon Flame in ice...",
    ["Dialogue3211803"]="Do you still remember the bone of the Ancient Dragon's death pose? \n(He extends his arms and makes an embracing motion.) \nI believe the Aurora magic froze the dragon to death and it was trying to protect the eggs underneath.",
    ["Dialogue3211804"]="So, this is the truth we've been after... \n(The absentminded Walsh turns serious for a moment and it throws you off.) \nYeah, that is quite a revelation.",
    ["Dialogue3211805"]="The gravity of history could never be described in one sheet. The fact you realized that is progress. \nSo, we can count on you to compile and announce the findings, right, Walsh?",
    ["Dialogue3211806"]="Should we announce it, instructor? \n<color=#A1979FFF>I'd call this a secret of the Seven Royal Families.</color>",
    ["Dialogue3211807"]="I think if the leader was willing to let us see the letters, she's probably figured it all out already. She sought to change the current system on Comodo, and maybe revealing what really happened a millennium back is her first move.",
    ["Dialogue3211808"]="Not to mention keeping quiet out of fear for punishment is not Eden Group's way. The purpose of archaeology is to help people uncover buried mysteries and redefine history, as well as aid us in realizing where we came from and where we should be going. It has nothing to do with whether history itself has been true or not.",
    ["Dialogue3211809"]="(The wise scholar formally hands the letter to Walsh.) \nRemember, we're all truth seekers. We kowtow to nothing else.",
    ["Dialogue3211901"]="(The dark gray surfaces are uneven and <color=#CA2E0AFF>full of pores</color>. Looking closely, you can see <color=#CA2E0AFF>stripes</color> of different colors running through the entire rock mass.)",
    ["Dialogue3212001"]="(The translucent crystals shine <color=#CA2E0AFF>brightly</color> as if covered with stars. Upon touch, you can also feel the <color=#CA2E0AFF>might of magic</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue3212101"]="(The huge bone looms majestically in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>kneeling position</color> as if holding something important before its demise. The bone is marred with <color=#CA2E0AFF>streaky scars</color> among glows like stars in the milky way.)",
    ["Dialogue3212201"]="This is probably not a good idea, My Lady...",
    ["Dialogue3212202"]="It's fine. The world ought to know the truth, anyway.",
    ["Dialogue3212203"]="But your mother said the past cannot be changed, and protecting family honor is the most important duty!",
    ["Dialogue3212204"]="Putting the past in the correct perspective is the first step into the future. And the future of Nerius shall be decided by me.",
    ["Dialogue3220101"]="(Master Sage Kroneika gives your approach the slightest of nods from the front of the Sage Hut.)\nIt has been a long time, Adventurer. And, according to the Class Advancement customs of the Criatura Academy, I have the honor of serving as your Sage Class Master.",
    ["Dialogue3220102"]="(The white-haired, white-whiskered old man taps on the ground lightly with his cane to summon your attention.)\nI need you to answer a few questions to demonstrate that you are indeed worthy of the title of Sage before your formal examination.",
    ["Dialogue3220201"]="Well done. Now, any student of Kroneika must possess three qualities in abundance: <color=#CA2E0AFF>talent, hard work, and kindness</color>. And your words have already told me much of your resolve. Now it is time for action to complete your examination.",
    ["Dialogue3220202"]="Unlike Magicians who accumulate endless knowledge of endless magic, the Sage is more focused on the holistic integration of magical knowledge into a unique system for themselves.",
    ["Dialogue3220203"]="How difficult it is for you to form such an integrated system depends largely upon your magical knowledge as a Magician—as well as talent, of course. But, generally, greater knowledge leads to a more holistic system.",
    ["Dialogue3220204"]="Yet even the mightiest talent is nothing if not joined with hard work and knowledge. What I need from you now, Adventurer, is to integrate all the magic you have learned into your own unique system and present it to me in <color=#CA2E0AFF>essay</color> form.",
    ["Dialogue3220205"]="Indeed. I shall raise questions in relation to your composition and you shall, by answering, demonstrate whether you deserve to pass.",
    ["Dialogue3220206"]="(Kroneika brushes his whiskers and gives you a long, hard look.)\nI am happy to read whatever you are happy to write. And I have two friends and scholars—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Norten and Lawrence</color>—who are even now studying in the Prontera Library. You may ask for their assistance.",
    ["Dialogue3220301"]="(A young scholar chants strangely under his breath with his back to the bookshelf.) Place the Magnolia into an oven set at a constantly rising temperature. The Magnolia will fry itself, but be advised: you will only be able to identify which side of the Magnolia you have fried after opening the oven.",
    ["Dialogue3220302"]="We conjecture that, prior to identifying the result by opening the oven, the Magnolia actually exists in a superimposed state where both sides are cooked in a non-real sense. Don't tell me that's... that's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Norten's Magnolia</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3220303"]="Oh dear! I fear you've overheard a major theoretical discovery of mine!",
    ["Dialogue3220304"]="Phew!\n(Norten breathes a sigh of relief before glaring at you, curiously.)\nWhat did you choose for a thesis subject?",
    ["Dialogue3220305"]="No, no, no! Your results don't mean anything, not to mention you lack any theoretical basis whatsoever. What were you doing? Reading all that literature while daydreaming? What about all those magic you \"studied\"? <size=26>Rewrite</size>!",
    ["Dialogue3220306"]="(Cough) Although that's not to say you'd have to start over from scratch necessarily... the delivery I ordered from the Rose Red Tavern should be at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>door to the Library</color> by now. Could you fetch it for me? We could talk over a meal.",
    ["Dialogue3220401"]="Ah! My favorite! An all-egg banquet! How come you're not eating?",
    ["Dialogue3220402"]="(Norten glares curiously in your direction before shoving a generous helping of books piled on a nearby shelf into your arms.)\nLiterature references! I think they'll be very helpful for your essay!",
    ["Dialogue3220403"]="Huh?! A summary? Adventurer, do you think that Kroneika is going to grill you based on a \"summary\"? Do you think your enemies are going to attack you based on a \"summary\"? Are your teammates going to ask for your help based on a \"summary\"? <size=26>The summary is everything and everything is the summary</size>!",
    ["Dialogue3220404"]="Hey! You'd better start <color=#CA2E0AFF>reading</color>! Come to think of it, why don't we pull an all-nighter with these books? I'll get the food.",
    ["Dialogue3220501"]="(A rather relaxed elderly scholar gazes with some interest at the mountain of books in front of you while leaning on a library handrail.) May I introduce myself? I'm a scholar of alchemy, Lawrence. I believe you're the Adventurer Kroneika mentioned?",
    ["Dialogue3220502"]="A bit tricky, you see... I couldn't help but overhear you and Norten just now. I'd also quite like to see that Obeaune performance at Rose Red Tavern.",
    ["Dialogue3220503"]="So what was the issue?",
    ["Dialogue3220504"]="(Lawrence picks up your half-completed essay.)\nAh. As far as I can tell, your essay suffers from two relatively minor issues.",
    ["Dialogue3220505"]="The first is that it lacks depth. The second is it lacks creativity.",
    ["Dialogue3220506"]="And so there are two solutions, as I see it.",
    ["Dialogue3220507"]="First, choose a different topic. Secondly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>rewrite</color> the essay.",
    ["Dialogue3220508"]="(Cough) But that's not to say you have to start from the ground up...\n(Lawrence extricates one book from the huge pile on the ground and hands it to you.)\nThis is what you want to be focusing on. We can have a bit of a chat and writing session after you <color=#CA2E0AFF>return it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3220601"]="They are two fine scholars with tremendous expertise in their chosen fields, but I'm afraid general magical studies and alchemy couldn't be further apart. But I'm sure that whatever <color=#CA2E0AFF>unique habits of thought</color> you've learned in their company will come in handy during essay preparation.",
    ["Dialogue3220602"]="Don't mention it.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Once these three get themselves sorted out, I'd also quite like some eggs and to watch that Obeaune performance!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3230101"]="Are you ready for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Disputation Ceremony</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3230102"]="Why do we focus so much on magical enhancement initially?",
    ["Dialogue3230103"]="(Kroneika nods imperceptibly before continuing.)\nYou discussed theories around the elemental countering system in your essay, a very rich field of study. Whose insights did you draw upon primarily?",
    ["Dialogue3230104"]="(Kroneika nods imperceptibly before continuing.)\nYou discussed the importance of melee combat at length in your Sage essay despite practicing as a ranged Magician. Why is this?",
    ["Dialogue3230105"]="(Kroneika nods imperceptibly before continuing.)\nI'm glad to see that, although your ideas are a little \"under-developed,\" you are capable of independent thinking in Norten and Lawrence's absence.",
    ["Dialogue3230106"]="(Kroneika abruptly cuts you off.)\nThis is your process of study, and I'm only interested in your results. I am happy enough as Master Sage to permit your return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> for participation in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Battle Trial</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3230107"]="(His expression suddenly softens to that of an amiable uncle rather than Master Sage.)\nPlease don't disappoint me!",
    ["Dialogue3230201"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Magician.",
    ["Dialogue3230202"]="Criatura Academy has no more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your potential beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task yet before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3230203"]="Give me your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>. You no longer need it. I'll present a Class Manual for your Second Class Advancement, which doubles as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3230301"]="Heh. Ready for your graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3240101"]="Greetings, Adventurer. It has been days since we last met. I hear you went to the Comodo... Did everything go well?",
    ["Dialogue3240102"]="You say you retrieved a king's crown from a band of pirates? That can only mean one thing—those pirates must have encountered King Tristan III on that remote island in the sea of Arunafeltz!",
    ["Dialogue3240103"]="You have a point. Though our chances are slim, we must try to find him, all the same. Even if... Even if all we find are his remains, we have a duty to bring them home and lay him to rest.",
    ["Dialogue3240104"]="No, Adventurer... This is a task for our kingdom's Defense Force. I shall dispatch our quickest soldiers to scour that island for any signs of our king shortly. As for you... I require your strength for another, more important matter.",
    ["Dialogue3240105"]="(Bohr holds up an envelope.)\nFirst, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a look</color> at this, Adventurer. It's an <color=#CA2E0AFF>anonymous letter</color> that I received just this morning. Its contents are... quite interesting, to say the least.",
    ["Dialogue3240201"]="Tell me, successor of Odin's bloodline...\n(Bohr deliberately repeats the title with a half-smiling expression.)\nWould you care to tell me more about this letter?",
    ["Dialogue3240202"]="It seems you two share more than a few small secrets. Despite being the highest-ranking commander of the Defense Force, I was surprised to learn that both successors to the throne had been victims of an assassination attempt. A grievous dereliction of duty, indeed... Perhaps I should go speak with that enthusiastic citizen, after all? Would you mind taking me to her, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3240301"]="Hey! How could you sell me out like that, Adventurer?! I only wrote that letter because I was worried about the two princes...\n(Realizing that there is no escape, Margaret immediately begins shouting and gesturing towards Bohr with a pained expression on her face.)\nY-You even brought him along... I'm done for...",
    ["Dialogue3240302"]="Greetings... \"Lady M, the Enthusiastic Citizen,\" I presume?\nOr should I say... Margaret, the Exorcist Priestess? Tell me, does hearing this name remind you of your orders? Of your sworn duties?",
    ["Dialogue3240303"]="(Bohr appears calm, but his tone has grown much colder. This is the first time you have seen him vent his anger so openly.)\nYou and this Adventurer have some nerve, hiding the details of the princes' assassination attempt from me. Have you forgotten that one of them is to be named king soon? If something had happened to them, the consequences would have been far greater than anything you could bear!",
    ["Dialogue3240304"]="I-I, uh...\n(Scared out of her wits, Margaret quickly darts behind you.)\nH-Help me, Adventurer! He's scaring me!",
    ["Dialogue3240305"]="(You tell Bohr the full story behind the two princes' assassination attempt. As you recount the tale, Bohr's expression grows grimmer.)\nSo this is why <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prince Azer</color> asked you to keep it a secret from me? Because he believed he knew who had plotted the assassination, and wanted to <color=#CA2E0AFF>resolve things in private</color>? Heh... And you were foolish enough to believe him, all because of that?",
    ["Dialogue3240306"]="Hey, what's that supposed to mean? Are you saying you suspect Prince Azer of planning the assassination?\n(Margaret pokes her head out from behind you just to rebuke Bohr.)\n<size=26>That's totally impossible!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3240307"]="Not only was he a victim in all of this... he even saved Prince Aronst by <color=#CA2E0AFF>transferring the poison into his own body</color>! How could you guys even begin to suspect someone like him? That's completely out of line!",
    ["Dialogue3240308"]="\"You guys\"?\n(Bohr's eyes widen slightly as he notices something in Margaret's statement.)\nAside from myself... <color=#CA2E0AFF>who else are you talking about</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3240309"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni</color>, of course! She's suspected the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walter family</color> for ages now! W-Wait a second! <size=24>I misspoke</size>! <size=26>You didn't hear anything</size>!\n(Clearly panicking, Margaret immediately covers her mouth with her hands. The way she looks is even a bit comical.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>God... Parni made me swear not to tell anyone...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3240310"]="Given the importance of the information you have provided me, I am willing to overlook your concealment of the assassination attempt on the princes... But make no mistake, I will report all of this to the Archbishop. As his disciple, your punishment is to be decided by him, not me. As for you, Adventurer... Surely, you must know where <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni Briar</color> currently resides, yes?",
    ["Dialogue3240311"]="I intend to personally pay a visit to this former Exorcist Priestess. The information she possesses exceeds my imagination... I believe that compared to Margaret, you understand this matter more clearly. With the royal election being so close at hand, I must eliminate any and all threats to the throne, so that our new king's appointment proceeds without incident.",
    ["Dialogue3240401"]="(Even after seeing you and Bohr approaching, Parni continues bandaging her patient's wounds with nimble, precise hands.)\nLong time no see, Adventurer... You as well, Lord Bohr. My apologies, but I'm a bit too busy to prepare a proper welcome. Please sit wherever you'd like.",
    ["Dialogue3240402"]="(Parni cuts you off before you have a chance to say anything.)\nI can guess why you two are here. However, you'll have to wait until these two patients wake up... Otherwise, the answers you seek may be lost forever.",
    ["Dialogue3240403"]="These two have suffered serious injuries, and no ordinary medicine will awaken them from their stupor... However, if you bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Quelling Seal</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Majoruros</color>, as well as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune of Coagulation</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carat</color>, I should be able to call upon the Holy Light to heal them. But you must do so quickly, as I fear they won't last much longer now...",
    ["Dialogue3240501"]="We have the materials you requested, Miss Parni... Now, will you please hear my request?",
    ["Dialogue3240502"]="If I'm not mistaken, Lord Bohr... You must be worried about the Walter family as well, yes?",
    ["Dialogue3240503"]="It appears we are of the same mind, Miss Parni. No wonder Margaret mentioned that you have suspected the Walter family for some time now... Tell me, when did you begin investigating the matter? Was it after the incident with the three princes of the Gaebolg family?",
    ["Dialogue3240504"]="Indeed. And I was not the only one to do so...\n(She turns to look at you.)\nI believe you still remember that servant, Adventurer? The one who calls himself Oman?",
    ["Dialogue3240505"]="That's right... He was once Prince Hans' personal attendant, but he resigned shortly after the prince's death... Naturally, this drew my attention, but during our investigation, we saw his murder happen right before our eyes. Worrying for his family's safety, I entrusted you with the delivery of some of <color=#CA2E0AFF>belongings</color> to his wife, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Helena</color>. We urged her to take her child and flee Prontera as soon as possible...",
    ["Dialogue3240506"]="But in the end... The worst still came to pass, Adventurer.\n(Turning slightly, Parni gestures towards the two patients lying unconscious behind her.)\nDo you recognize them now?",
    ["Dialogue3240601"]="As a precaution, I left one of my homing pigeon whistles in her possession, and sure enough... not long afterward, I received Helena's distress call. I raced over to them as fast as I could, but in the end... I was only able to rescue them in this state.",
    ["Dialogue3240602"]="So Oman was killed, and his family was also targeted? This is...\n(With just the small amount of information provided, the young commander quickly begins to piece things together.)\nWere they being <color=#CA2E0AFF>silenced</color>? If so, then the three princes... Does this mean their death wasn't accidental?",
    ["Dialogue3240603"]="How... <size=26>How could you be so impudent?!</size>\nWhy didn't you report this to the Defense Force sooner, Parni?",
    ["Dialogue3240604"]="You never would have believed me, given that I had no evidence at the time. Also...\n(Parni briefly pauses as she gives you an inscrutable look.)\nAdventurer? Would you mind bringing me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>fountain water from the Quiet Garden</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3240605"]="Helena and Abu still require further treatment... I fear that their conditions are worsening. We can continue our discussion once I finish tending to their wounds.",
    ["Dialogue3240701"]="Thank you for bringing us more fountain water, Adventurer... But it appears we no longer need it.\n(Parni takes the fountain water and sets it down, then looks towards Bohr.)\nMy reason for sending you away was not to fetch water... but to test you, Lord Bohr.",
    ["Dialogue3240702"]="So, you were testing me all along, were you?",
    ["Dialogue3240703"]="Yes, Lord Bohr, and this is precisely the reason why I never revealed the details of my investigation on the Walter family to the Defense Force. The truth is, up until just now... I had no way of knowing whether you were friend or foe, so I sent the Adventurer away in order to see how you would react...",
    ["Dialogue3240704"]="And if I had acted against you and Oman's family, it would have proven that I was in league with the Walter family... Is that correct?\n(Bohr's face reveals a mixture of surprise and consternation.)\nTo stake your own life on a gamble like that... How incredibly foolhardy of you, Miss Parni.",
    ["Dialogue3240705"]="Testing you was only one of my intentions, Lord Bohr. The other... was to demonstrate my resolve. I wanted to prove to you that I am willing to sacrifice myself in order to bring this criminal to justice.",
    ["Dialogue3240706"]="Ever since the three princes of the Gaebolg family met their demise, I have seen so many innocent people lose their lives... Oh Odin, please have mercy on these innocent lives...",
    ["Dialogue3240707"]="Believe me when I say I understand how you feel, Miss Parni... which is precisely why we should be working together! With your help, we can find the true culprit behind these heinous crimes. I beg of you, Miss Parni... Share your knowledge with me, so that we can finally put an end to all of this suffering.",
    ["Dialogue3240708"]="I acknowledge your wisdom as well as your devotion to the royal family, Lord Bohr. I have no doubt that you will lead us to the truth behind this violent plot and deliver our kingdom from peril... However, because of my carelessness, the crucial evidence needed to implicate the Walter family has already fallen into the enemy's hands.",
    ["Dialogue3240709"]="(As you recount your conversation with Ian at the palace, Bohr's expression grows more and more serious.)\nIan Walter... So he walked away with the murder weapon and even warned you to stay out of it?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I see... Damn the Regent and his wicked treachery...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3240710"]="As it stands, I have no evidence to prove any of my suspicions, and there is no telling if or when Helena and Abu will awaken from their comas... Our only option is to hunt down the <color=#CA2E0AFF>assassin</color> who came after them.",
    ["Dialogue3240711"]="After rescuing Helena and her child, I entrusted the tracking of their assassin to a childhood friend. We've known each other for many years, and he is one of my most trusted confidantes. Just before you arrived, I received a letter from him saying that he had found and captured the assassin, who is a member of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>. However, I cannot leave Helena and Abu in their current state...",
    ["Dialogue3240712"]="Why not send the Adventurer in your stead? That would give me more time to listen to every detail of your investigation, which may produce new leads in our search for the truth. What say you, Miss Parni?",
    ["Dialogue3240713"]="I agree... In that case, we leave things in your capable hands, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3240801"]="It's been ages, Adventurer!\n(Seyren smiles as he claps you on the shoulders, and he looks as light-hearted as ever.)\nTell me, what brings you to these parts?",
    ["Dialogue3240802"]="Huh? You mean I never told you? Well, it's true: Margaret, Parni, and I have been the closest of friends ever since we were little! Parni asked me to track down an assassin, which is why I came here all the way from Prontera... I hear this guy was sent by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walter</color> family to silence that poor woman and her child?",
    ["Dialogue3240803"]="I see... Well, Parni's right about not having enough evidence.\nAh... If only we could get more information out of this guy! He's proving to be a real tough nut to crack... Randel has tried everything to get a confession out of him, but he just won't talk.",
    ["Dialogue3240804"]="(You look past Seyren and see a young man squatting next to the assassin. He raises his head slightly, but says very little; it seems he does not wish to be disturbed.)\nHello.",
    ["Dialogue3240805"]="Surprised, Adventurer? Well, you should be! Randel's a part of the Royal Chivalry now, and one of my most stalwart companions! If it wasn't for him, we never would have captured this slippery snake of an assassin!",
    ["Dialogue3240806"]="You talk too much. Focus on the task at hand.\nWhere is the formula for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Potion</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3240807"]="Oh right, I almost forgot!\n(Seyren pulls out a crumpled piece of paper and reads it aloud with some difficulty.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let's see here... Margaret's formula for a Truth Potion...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3240808"]="First, we'll need freshly-clipped <color=#CA2E0AFF>Confusion Grass</color> buds, which must be carefully folded and stored in a dark place. Next, we'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shimmering Algae Bulbs</color>, which must be sealed in a bottle and frozen using an ice spell. Lastly, we'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bone Dust</color>, which must be scraped from an Abysmal Knight's ribcage... Th-This is way too complicated, don't you think?!",
    ["Dialogue3240809"]="Er... We knights aren't exactly experts on potion-making, you know? I had to ask Margaret to put together a Truth Potion formula for us, but I have no idea how well it'll work...",
    ["Dialogue3240901"]="Perfect, we have all the materials we need now! So, uh... How exactly do we make it?\n(Seyren pulls out the crumpled formula and reads from it again.)",
    ["Dialogue3240902"]="\"Dissolve the Shimmering Algae Bulbs in runic water, then add the Bone Dust and stir well. Crush the Confusion Grass and divide its juice into three parts, then gradually add each part to the concoction. Remember to cast an awakening spell after every addition, or else the subject will quickly lose consciousness after taking the potion...\" It just doesn't get any easier, does it?!",
    ["Dialogue3240903"]="Forget it... Let's just mix them all together and try our luck!\n(Tossing the formula aside, the young knight takes the materials from you and jams them into an empty bottle before shaking it vigorously.)\nAnd... Done! Here, Adventurer! You can do the honors and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give him the Truth Potion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3241001"]="Eww! What... What did you fools give to me?!\n(The assassin stares at you with intense hatred, but his expression quickly begins to slacken under the effects of the Truth Potion.)\nUrgh... I...",
    ["Dialogue3241002"]="Whoa... Looks like it's working, after all! Time to test out our home-brewed Truth Potion!\nHey! Tell me your name!",
    ["Dialogue3241003"]="(The assassin stares blankly in front of him, like a soulless puppet.)\nI... I am Talbot... Talbot <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corman</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3241004"]="<size=26>Corman?!</size>\nWhat is your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lorenzo Corman</color>?!",
    ["Dialogue3241005"]="Lord Lorenzo... adopted me... raised me... I... I must repay Lord Lorenzo... for his kindness...",
    ["Dialogue3241006"]="So he's the one who ordered you to murder Helena and her child?",
    ["Dialogue3241007"]="Lord Lorenzo said... they were in our way... They had to be eliminated... at all costs!\n(For some reason, his voice grows fainter as his head slowly begins to droop.)",
    ["Dialogue3241008"]="Hey! Snap out of it! Who else is in cahoots with Lorenzo? Hey!!!\n(Seyren tries to awaken the assassin several times, but he has become completely unresponsive.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>He's out cold... Dammit! Is it because of the Truth Potion?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3241009"]="If I recall, he's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>servant of the Walter family</color>...\nIt looks like Parni's hunch may have some merit after all, Adventurer. I'm taking this man back to Prontera right away for further questioning. As for Parni... Would you mind telling her everything that happened here?",
    ["Dialogue3241101"]="Welcome back, Adventurer. What did you learn?",
    ["Dialogue3241102"]="Lorenzo Corman...?\nThe servant who has been with the Walter family for the last twenty years? He's one of Ian Walter's most trusted confidantes...",
    ["Dialogue3241103"]="Indeed, but still... The word of an assassin does little to implicate the Walter family. If they are truly ready to rebel, the situation could turn on its head practically overnight... As it stands, we still require Helena's testimony, as well as sufficient proof of the Walter family's betrayal.",
    ["Dialogue3241104"]="I understand... I will notify you as soon as she comes to, Lord Bohr.",
    ["Dialogue3241105"]="With the royal election fast approaching, we must do everything in our power to uncover the Walter family's plot and ensure that our new king is appointed without incident. Your role in our mission is indispensable... Do you still remember the words of our king? He wished for you to help us find the most suitable successor to the throne—one who can bring new life to our kingdom once more.",
    ["Dialogue3241106"]="Once you return to Prontera, please pay a visit to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lyanna, the Court Clerk</color>... She will provide you with further guidance on your quest.",
    ["Dialogue32412"]="(The two of them are lying on the bed with their eyes shut, barely breathing. That's the wife of Oman, Helena, along with their son, Abu. You notice that Helena crosses her arms before her chest and holds on to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>old money pouch</color> tightly...)",
    ["Dialogue3250101"]="Good morning, brave Adventurer. The seven-day election for our new king has come to an end, and the Court Clerks worked diligently through the night to tally the votes. The princess will announce the results of the election at the Bloodline Banquet, which will be held later today, and the coronation ceremony will officially begin. Please accept this banquet invitation from Lord Bohr and do not be late.",
    ["Dialogue3250102"]="Lord Bohr departed for his provisional office in the palace early this morning. He had many preparations to make for today's banquet and could not personally hand you an invitation. Please go speak to him at the Banquet Hall, if you so choose.",
    ["Dialogue3250103"]="Let's not be so hasty, Adventurer. The banquet has yet to begin, so why not take some time for yourself? In fact...\n(The soldier turns his head and clears his throat a few times, signaling you over to him.)\nCome closer, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3250104"]="We received a report from our scouts this morning. It seems the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knights</color> gathered outside of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color> have begun to move. Strangely enough, they don't show any indication of wanting to enter Prontera... Instead, they appear to be wandering about with no clear goal. Lord Bohr wishes for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>spy on them</color> before the banquet begins.",
    ["Dialogue3250201"]="Well? Did you find him?",
    ["Dialogue3250202"]="I've checked every tree and bush in this godforsaken forest, but still no sign of him. Honestly... How could Lord Azer disappear at a time like this?",
    ["Dialogue3250203"]="To tell the truth... I saw Lord Azer ride out of the city with Prince Aronst this morning. I don't think anyone has seen Lord Azer since then.",
    ["Dialogue3250204"]="Wh-What?! Why are you only telling us this now?! If anything happens—",
    ["Dialogue3250205"]="That's enough! Have you forgotten that we're on the main road to Prontera? Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>find someplace quiet</color> before having this discussion!",
    ["Dialogue3250301"]="We should be fine here, right? Now out with it: did you tell \"him\" about Prince Azer, as well?",
    ["Dialogue3250302"]="Of course I did! But he told me not to panic, and that it was part of the plan, so I didn't pursue the subject...",
    ["Dialogue3250303"]="But now... Prince Aronst is still at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color>, and Prince Azer is nowhere to be found... Could this really still be part of the plan? Shouldn't we go back and ask for confirmation?",
    ["Dialogue3250304"]="Let's just drop it for now. Since our lord was clear on not asking further questions, we have no business making any assumptions about his plans. We should just focus on the task at hand...",
    ["Dialogue3250401"]="Adventurer? What are you doing, sneaking around like that? I almost mistook you for the assassin who poisoned Prince Aronst...",
    ["Dialogue3250402"]="(Your question is aimed mostly toward Aronst, but Moffit clearly fails to notice and begins to panic and complain.)\nYou mean you didn't know? Prince Aronst snuck out on his own last night! The Bloodline Banquet is about to begin, and the Luminary Dream in his body is about to take effect... Of all the times to go running off—",
    ["Dialogue3250403"]="Enough, Moffit. I just wanted to be alone for a moment... I fear that after today, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I won't have a chance to do so ever again</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3250404"]="Y-You must be joking, my prince? Your words have been awfully strange today... But there's no time to worry about that now! Come, my prince; there is still enough time for you to rest before the banquet.",
    ["Dialogue3250405"]="No, Moffit... I wish to stay here a while longer. You, on the other hand, can return to the palace and prepare my clothes for the feast. After all... no one else knows me better than you.",
    ["Dialogue3250406"]="I-I could never leave you out here all alone, my prince! It's far too dangerous!",
    ["Dialogue3250407"]="(Aronst silently turns his gaze to you for a moment before smiling and nodding in agreement.)\nThat works, too. I was just about to pay my respect to the deceased, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>orchids</color> outside of the cemetery appear to be in full bloom... Would you mind <color=#CA2E0AFF>picking a bunch</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue3250408"]="Er, I suppose it's fine, as long as the Adventurer is with you... I will do as you ask, my prince, and return to the palace to prepare your clothes... But please do not tarry any longer than necessary. It will not do to be late on a day such as this!",
    ["Dialogue3250501"]="Cough, cough... Y-You're back, Adventurer...\n(Even speaking a few words seems to be abnormally difficult for Prince Aronst. Despite his best efforts, he cannot hold back a painful coughing fit.)",
    ["Dialogue3250502"]="I-I'm fine... Perhaps it's because of the poison, I've been showing symptoms of a cold lately... Still, it's of no concern.",
    ["Dialogue3250503"]="Not yet, but for them to go through all the trouble of poisoning me with something like this... It can only mean that they intend to put their plans into motion during the Bloodline Banquet today. If Bohr has already put his security measures in place like I know he has... then the culprits will have no way to escape once they're discovered.",
    ["Dialogue3250504"]="You wish to know about my secret meeting with Azer from last night, yes?\n(Aronst lowers his head slightly. He appears to be smiling, but another coughing fit racks his body the moment he tries to speak.)\nCough, cough, cough... Does this mean you suspect Azer of being the culprit, as well?",
    ["Dialogue3250505"]="If you and Bohr have already gathered so much evidence... then why ask for my opinion? It appears that no matter what I say or think, you two have already decided to apprehend him at the end of the banquet, yes?",
    ["Dialogue3250506"]="Know what, Adventurer? Azer's whereabouts?\nWhy don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>place those orchids before this grave</color> first? I have a story I wish to share with you...",
    ["Dialogue3250601"]="Namely, the story of this tombstone's owner... Have you heard of him?",
    ["Dialogue3250602"]="He was a very lucky man, a talented person who came from a prominent and respectable family... But in the end, he lost everything and led an unfortunate existence until his very last breath. Now, even his name and face have been lost to the passage of time... All that remains is this nameless tombstone, a testament to his heroic, yet tragic life... Do you wish to know why he suffered such a cruel fate?",
    ["Dialogue3250603"]="Because people like you forced him to compete with his own brother for supremacy. They were both born of the same flesh and blood, and each was talented in his own right... So why were they turned against one another for the sake of others? This man cared little if he won or lost... But the prospects of victory all but consumed the heart of his elder brother!",
    ["Dialogue3250604"]="And so... his brother betrayed him. He was banished from their homeland and left with nothing to his name... And after using him as a stepping stone, the elder brother eventually ascended to the position of head of his family...\n(You feel a chill down your spine as Aronst finishes the tale. Is it truly just a story, or could there be more to it?)",
    ["Dialogue3250605"]="I was merely answering your question, nothing more... But yes, Adventurer, it's true that I saw Azer last night. We spoke for hours and said farewell to one another just before sunrise. I don't know where he is now, nor would I tell you if I knew. I have no intention of letting my brother share the same fate as the man interred here.",
    ["Dialogue3250606"]="(You try to console Aronst, but he refuses to speak. Turning his back to you, he kneels before the unmarked grave and offers a silent prayer.)\nSorry... But I'm a little tired now. Please... Just let me rest for a moment before we <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the palace</color>. The most important moment of my life is fast approaching... I hope you enjoy the show, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3250701"]="Welcome, Adventurer. The Bloodline Banquet is about to begin, and Lord Bohr is expecting you in the Banquet Hall. Would you be so kind as to find your seat?",
    ["Dialogue3250801"]="You're late, Adventurer. Did you run into trouble on the way here?",
    ["Dialogue3250802"]="You say Aronst and Azer met in secret last night... And while Aronst has safely returned to the palace, Azer is still nowhere to be found?\n(Bohr's eyes narrow slightly, a tell-tale sign that he is deep in thought again.)\nThat would explain why Ian was constantly staring at the entrance of the Banquet Hall earlier...",
    ["Dialogue3250803"]="Yes, that is another of my concerns. For seven days now, the assassins have been biding their time... I fear that they will finally spring their trap during the Bloodline Banquet. With so many dignitaries to protect, our forces will be stretched thin should a battle occur. Thankfully, I just received word from Parni a few hours ago.",
    ["Dialogue3250804"]="Yes, Adventurer... Helena and Abu have awakened, and their testimony is the key to our victory over our enemies. The three of them are on their way to Prontera as we speak, and I have already arranged for an armed escort to receive them; they should be here any minute now. Also, a few days ago... I recruited a powerful ally to our cause, one who can contend with the Walter family's forces.",
    ["Dialogue3250805"]="(Bohr chuckles, apparently amused by your nervous look.)\nWhile our enemy may be confident in their schemes, we are not without our own preparation, either. You can relax, Adventurer; after all, what are a handful of scheming mortals compared to the battles you've survived? Not even Dragons could best you, my friend.",
    ["Dialogue3250806"]="Now then, I believe Archbishop Wolmas would like a word with you. From what I understand, he requires your assistance with the coronation ceremony. Do not keep him waiting long.",
    ["Dialogue3250901"]="I've been expecting you, Adventurer. A minute longer and it would have been too late.",
    ["Dialogue3250902"]="Time is scarce, so just do as I say for now. I need you to descend into the sewers and <color=#CA2E0AFF>slay 10 Familiars</color>, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>drink water from the Central Fountain</color>, and finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather an Ash Branch and an Elm Branch</color>. Return to the Banquet Hall once your tasks are complete, and I will explain everything afterward.",
    ["Dialogue3251001"]="Just a moment, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3251002"]="A banquet servant arrived with new orders not long ago. The Banquet Hall will be sealed once the Bloodline Banquet begins, and none will be allowed to enter or leave until it has concluded. As such, please remember to <color=#CA2E0AFF>make all necessary preparations before entering the Banquet Hall</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3251003"]="Then please enter, Adventurer. I pray that everything proceeds as planned.",
    ["Dialogue3251004"]="Understood. Just speak to me when you are ready, and I will escort you into the Banquet Hall, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3251101"]="Truth be told, Adventurer... The princess and I decided long before the Bloodline Banquet to have you preside over the coronation ceremony. Your contributions to our kingdom are many and great, and you were the last person to see our beloved King Tristan III and hear his final words... As such, we would be honored if you bestowed this ring, which you retrieved for us, on the hand of our newly-appointed king.",
    ["Dialogue3251102"]="As for the three tasks I set before you... They were part of an ancient ritual, one that has been passed down in the Rune Kingdom since time immemorial. You are familiar with the legend of Odin and his three magnificent feats, yes? The first was leading his divine brethren to victory over the giants. The second was sacrificing his eye to drink from the Well of Mimir and discover the secrets of the Rune script. The third was shaping the first two humans out of ash and elm and breathing life into their bodies...",
    ["Dialogue3251103"]="Indeed, Adventurer. The three tasks I gave you correspond to Odin's three greatest accomplishments. Anyone who presides over a new king's coronation must complete these tasks in order to inherit Odin's will. Only then can they serve as his witness and bestow supreme authority upon our new ruler.",
    ["Dialogue3251104"]="Once the princess announces the official results of the election, it will be your turn to appear on stage. You must hand this ring and this sword, symbols of his royal sovereignty, to our new king. Do not be nervous; I will not be far from you.",
    ["Dialogue3251105"]="The princess has taken the stage. Let us bear witness to this <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine moment</color> together, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3251201"]="On this blessed day, the Rune Kingdom shall appoint its fifty-seventh king to the throne. It is my honor and privilege to witness this sacred moment alongside all of you, our esteemed guests. Before all who have gathered here today, and before the gods themselves, I hereby announce the man who shall be named king—",
    ["Dialogue3251202"]="Aronst Gaebolg!",
    ["Dialogue3251203"]="Prince Aronst!",
    ["Dialogue3251204"]="I knew it would be him all along!",
    ["Dialogue3251205"]="Now, let us welcome the successor of Odin's bloodline to the stage to bestow divine authority upon our new sovereign!",
    ["Dialogue3251301"]="Go now, Adventurer... It is a great honor for any king to have their <color=#CA2E0AFF>coronation presided over</color> by one of Odin's bloodline. I believe this day will prove unforgettable for Prince Aronst.",
    ["Dialogue3251401"]="You fools... Do you have any ideas about what you've done? Did anyone even consider the consequences of putting the fate of the entire kingdom in my hands? Why me, of all people, and not Bidal, or Erich, or Halmod, or even Jurgen?",
    ["Dialogue32514010"]="No... I believe the time for questions is long past... Now is the time for all of you to receive your punishment.",
    ["Dialogue3251402"]="Aronst...? What... What is the meaning of this?",
    ["Dialogue3251403"]="Still fumbling in the dark? Allow me to shed light on things... Do you still remember all that happened in our kingdom prior to this meaningless election? The death of the three Gaebolg Family princes, the attempt on Lord Bohr's life at his wedding, the mysterious disappearance of King Tristan III... None of you have uncovered the truth behind these unfortunate occurrences yet, have you?",
    ["Dialogue3251404"]="Prince Aronst... Are you implying that you know who the culprit is?",
    ["Dialogue3251405"]="Of course... Which makes me all the more excited to see your expressions when I reveal the truth!\n(Aronst closes his eyes, with a look of pure pleasure on his face.)\nAnd that truth... is that I am the one behind all of it! Me!",
    ["Dialogue3251406"]="You, Aronst?! But how could this be?!",
    ["Dialogue3251407"]="Feeling remorseful, Jurgen? You also voted for me, didn't you? Such a shame... But it's too late now.\n(The young king raises his hand in triumph, and the entire room turns its gaze upon the ring on his finger.)\nBehold! From this day forth, I hold the highest authority in the entire kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue3251408"]="<size=26>Hold your tongue, Aronst!!!</size>\nThis is a royal banquet, not some third-rate theater's stage! Now apologize to everyone here!",
    ["Dialogue3251409"]="\"Stage,\" you say...? Ha! I quite like that word, Halmod!\n(Aronst begins to applaud fervently, his wild laughter echoing in the otherwise silent banquet hall.)\nYes, yes... This is a stage, and you are all actors in my latest masterpiece!",
    ["Dialogue3251501"]="<size=26>Have you lost your mind, Aronst?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue32515010"]="No villain would wear his treachery on his face for the world to see... Has anyone stopped to notice that the guards are only listening to him now? This is undeniable proof that he has been plotting this all along... Even the Imperial Guards are at his beck and call!",
    ["Dialogue32515011"]="Everyone, please remain calm! Doesn't something about Prince Aronst seem strange to you? His speech and behavior are completely different than usual... as though he is being controlled with magic! We should examine the prince to make sure nothing is amiss!",
    ["Dialogue32515012"]="So even you are convinced of this traitor's innocence, Lord Bidal? Could it be... You're all in league with each other, aren't you?! Death would be too merciful of a punishment for you!",
    ["Dialogue3251502"]="Heheheh... My dear Halmod, is this not the performance you've been expecting? My apologies if it hasn't been to your liking, but don't worry... The real show is about to begin.",
    ["Dialogue3251503"]="(The banquet hall sits in utter silence as Aronst continues to rant and rave. After surveying the faces of his captive audience, he points toward Ian Walter.)\nTell me, my lord, what do you have to say about my performance thus far?",
    ["Dialogue3251504"]="Lord Aronst... Forgive my ignorance, for I know not what you mean.\n(Ian bows his head respectfully before Aronst and the rest of the room. You see his hand make what appears to be a secret gesture from within his sleeve.)",
    ["Dialogue3251505"]="<size=26>W... Well, then?!</size>\nWhat are you waiting for, guards?! Why haven't you apprehended this shameless criminal yet?!",
    ["Dialogue3251506"]="Everyone calm down! We must observe due process before labeling anyone a criminal, especially for a matter as significant as this! Now tell us, Aronst... If you truly are responsible for these acts, what was your reason for doing so?",
    ["Dialogue3251507"]="Indeed! Prince Aronst was already a perfectly viable successor to the throne, to begin with! Why risk it all just to usurp it?",
    ["Dialogue3251508"]="What mockery is this? A branch family prince such as Aronst could never ascend to the throne unless the three princes of the main family were eliminated! I'm certain he had something to do with the incident at Lord Bohr's wedding, too! As for King Tristan III's disappearance... If he truly is the culprit, disposing of the king would only be a natural part of his treason!",
    ["Dialogue3251509"]="You... You speak without proof! We have all seen Prince Aronst's kindness and generosity for ourselves! Why on earth would he do something so brazenly wicked?!",
    ["Dialogue3251601"]="As for you, the successor of Odin's bloodline... What role did you play in his murderous schemes?!",
    ["Dialogue3251602"]="... Enough, all of you. Before you pass judgment on Prince Aronst, I ask that all of you answer one last question.\n(The Defense Force commander raises his hand, and everyone in the room falls silent once again.)",
    ["Dialogue3251603"]="If we ultimately decide that Aronst is not fit to be king... Then who shall take the throne in his place?",
    ["Dialogue3251604"]="If the successor who was elected is not worthy of being named king, then it stands to reason that the title should go to the runner-up! Tell us, Archbishop Wolmas... Who was it that placed second in the election?",
    ["Dialogue3251605"]="If the Court Clerks are not mistaken... That would be Prince Azer, of the Walter Family.",
    ["Dialogue3251606"]="(Bohr chuckles quietly upon hearing this.)\nI see... So this was your desired outcome all along? Very well, then... It appears the time has come for me to play my hand.",
    ["Dialogue3251701"]="Before deciding on the rightful successor to the throne, allow me to share my findings with you all. There is no denying that the three princes were slain most unjustly, and that the true culprit has yet to be captured... As commander of the Defense Force, I must claim partial responsibility for this. With the blessings of Odin, however, I have finally discovered a crucial witness on the matter.",
    ["Dialogue3251702"]="I will not recount the details regarding the deaths of the three princes, as you are all fully aware of them... We have all been led to believe that their deaths were the result of a curse, one that has been passed down the Gaebolg Family for generations, but the truth is... Aside from Prince Nate, the markings we found on the other two princes were falsely planted on their bodies. Their cause of death... Was poisoning.",
    ["Dialogue3251703"]="P-Poison...?!",
    ["Dialogue3251704"]="Indeed, and on the day that the princes met their doom, a loyal servant by the name of Oman suddenly resigned from his duties, and disappeared without a trace. Suspecting foul play, the Exorcist Priestess Parni began to investigate the matter...\n(Bohr steps aside, and Parni walks out before everyone.)",
    ["Dialogue3251705"]="It is just as Lord Bohr says... In the course of tracking down the servant Oman, the Adventurer and I watched as he was murdered before our very eyes. In his final moments, Oman realized that he was nothing more than a pawn, but he died before he could reveal the identity of the mastermind behind these evil schemes.",
    ["Dialogue3251706"]="From that moment on, I took it upon myself to ensure the safety of his wife, Helena, and their child, Abu. My plan was to help them leave Prontera and start new lives... But even a widow and a fatherless child were not safe from the culprit's murderous intent. Soon after, I realized that their attack was an act of desperation, possibly because these two victims had the evidence needed to implicate the culprit.",
    ["Dialogue3251707"]="And so, I enlisted the help of a good friend, who was quickly able to track down the family's attacker...\n(Parni motions to Seyren, who then leads the shackled killer out before everyone.)\nI leave the rest to you, Seyren.",
    ["Dialogue3251801"]="My lords, my comrade and I apprehended this assassin in Glast Heim. He was given a Truth Potion just before the start of the banquet, so feel free to ask him any questions you see fit to ask.",
    ["Dialogue32518010"]="Lord Lorenzo commanded me... To dispose of Oman... As well as his wife, Helena... And to destroy that secret letter... The one bearing their family crest...",
    ["Dialogue32518011"]="\"Secret letter\"...? What did it say? Where is this letter now?",
    ["Dialogue32518012"]="Allow me to answer that, Lord Bidal.\nThe man this assassin just mentioned is a familiar name to everyone here. He speaks of Lorenzo Corman, a loyal servant to the Walter Family and Lord Ian's right-hand man.",
    ["Dialogue32518013"]="The letter in question, which they sought to destroy, was a correspondence between Oman and the Walter Family... A promise of riches in exchange for the murder of the three princes of the Gaebolg Family!",
    ["Dialogue32518014"]="Y-You have no proof! And even if it was Lorenzo's ambition to murder the princes, what right do you have to implicate his master, Lord Ian?!",
    ["Dialogue32518015"]="I would not make such claims without proof, my lord. Helena, <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring it out for all to see</color>.\n(Parni turns to Helena and holds her hand, comforting her.)\nDon't worry, we won't let any harm befall you or your child.",
    ["Dialogue32518016"]="V... Very well... This was given to me by my husband, Oman. I have held it close to me ever since...",
    ["Dialogue3251802"]="... Leave this to me. I am fairly knowledgeable in the art of potion-making... If everyone trusts in my judgment, I can verify whether the assassin is telling the truth.",
    ["Dialogue3251803"]="Of course, Lord Bidal! After all, you studied under Kroneika the Great Sage!",
    ["Dialogue3251804"]="I agree, as well. None here would claim to know more about magic than you, my lord!",
    ["Dialogue3251805"]="It doesn't matter who does it! Let's just get this over with already! Do as you must, Lord Bidal!",
    ["Dialogue3251806"]="(Bidal nods politely to the crowd before turning towards the assassin.)\nYoung man... Can you tell me your name?",
    ["Dialogue3251807"]="Talbot... Corman...",
    ["Dialogue3251808"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Corman?! He shares the same name as Lord Ian and his family...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3251809"]="... Were you hired by someone to murder a man named Oman, as well as his wife and child? If so, can you tell us who it was?",
    ["Dialogue3251901"]="Despite what you have said, letters can be easily forged...",
    ["Dialogue32519010"]="In conclusion, Lord Ian... I have more than enough reason to suspect that it was Prince Azer who poisoned Prince Aronst. Furthermore... In exchange for the antidote, he was forced to make those unbelievable claims and serve as your scapegoat!",
    ["Dialogue32519011"]="I-I see now!\nOdin preserves us... No wonder the prince acted so out of character today!",
    ["Dialogue32519012"]="I have spoken my part, Lord Ian... Now, what rebuttal do you have to offer? Because without one... I will have no choice, but to arrest you and the entire Walter Family, as well as the members of the Royal Chivalry whom you convinced to defect to your side.",
    ["Dialogue32519013"]="(Under Bohr's piercing gaze, the hero who had maintained his composure throughout the entire banquet finally reveals his first smile.)\nMy... Young people can be quite terrifying... A shame that naivety goes hand-in-hand with youth.",
    ["Dialogue32519014"]="Allow me to teach you a valuable life lesson, Bohr. When one plays at the gambling table, the rules of the game are of the utmost importance. A normal person follows the rules, while a clever person uses them to their advantage... But a person with absolute power can shatter the very rules that govern the game!\n(He raises his hand in the air, as though giving some sort of signal.)",
    ["Dialogue32519015"]="<size=26>Silence! Silence, all of you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue32519016"]="(Aronst roars over the crowd, stunning them back into silence. Amused by their cooperation, he begins clapping and laughing maniacally.)\nThank you, Lord Bohr and Lord Ian, for your wonderful contribution to our show tonight. To show my appreciation, I shall come up with a fitting name for this act, one that perfectly captures the darkness and desperation you have shown us today! But before I do...",
    ["Dialogue32519017"]="(Aronst's sinister gaze passes over Bohr and Ian, and the sound of swords being drawn rings out in the room.)\nThere is still the matter of your punishment for interrupting the show! Let this be a reminder to you both that I am the playwright here, not you!",
    ["Dialogue3251902"]="Very well... But I believe I speak for everyone here when I say that Lorenzo should be made to confront Helena before we continue. However...\n(Bohr chuckles quietly as all eyes turn to Ian Walter.)\nIt appears your loyal servant is not with you today, Lord Ian.",
    ["Dialogue3251903"]="... Lorenzo is well into his golden years, and left Prontera over a month ago to spend the rest of his days in the comfort of his hometown... Or do you believe that a retired servant of the Walter Family must still answer to the Defense Force, Lord Bohr?",
    ["Dialogue3251904"]="Not at all, Lord Ian... Unless, of course, that servant is a prime suspect in the murder of three princes; the Defense Force has no choice but to intervene in such instances. If, for whatever reason, you cannot call him back to the capital to testify, we would be more than happy to find him and escort him back... With your help, of course.",
    ["Dialogue3251905"]="Is something the matter, Lord Ian? You've gone completely silent... Tell me, is it because you fear that we will find Lorenzo alive and well? Or perhaps that we will find proof of your murderous plot?",
    ["Dialogue3251906"]="H-How dare you speak to Lord Ian like that, Bohr?!",
    ["Dialogue3251907"]="My apologies if you find this unpleasant... But I still have more to recount, and it goes beyond the murder of the three princes. Does everyone remember the speech from exactly seven days ago? At the time, Prince Aronst was attacked by a man in black on the way to the cathedral... At roughly the same time, my subordinates witnessed Prince Azer putting on similar garments.",
    ["Dialogue3251908"]="If that is still not enough for you all... Prince Aronst rarely takes the main road to the cathedral, and prefers taking side roads and alleys to avoid causing a commotion. There are only two people who are aware of his preferred route: his servant, Moffit... And Prince Azer. Not only was Prince Aronst injured in this attack, he was also forced to imbibe an unknown poison!",
    ["Dialogue3251909"]="(Bohr holds up a document in his hands for all to see. You recognize it as the lab report given by Mainz on the day that Prince Aronst was attacked.)\nThe poison is known as Luminary Dream, and has long since been included on the list of banned potions. Those who ingest it will begin to experience its harmful effects in seven days, and the antidote for this poison changes depending on which ingredients were used to make it. As a result, we have yet to find a cure for Prince Aronst.",
    ["Dialogue3252001"]="You... How dare you...",
    ["Dialogue3252002"]="Well? Do you understand who is truly in control now? After all, I didn't put all of this effort into devising such an elaborate scheme... Just so you could give the credit to this Walter Family dog!",
    ["Dialogue3252003"]="Enough, Aronst! Spare us your trivial lies!\nA powerless branch family prince such as yourself could never convince Ian's most loyal servant to obey you, much less convince these knights to abandon their duties!",
    ["Dialogue3252004"]="Everyone here can see through your childish act. Now that the truth is known to all, our priority is finding the antidote before it's too late. You have no reason to keep playing these games, Aronst...",
    ["Dialogue3252005"]="\"Aronst\", you say? Ha! Why don't you take a closer look, Lord Bohr... <color=#CA2E0AFF>And see who I truly am</color>?\n(As he speaks, he begins to wipe the makeup from his face.)",
    ["Dialogue3252101"]="I must admit, I had no idea it would take you all so long to realize my true identity... Do Aronst and I really look so alike?\nI suppose it makes sense... We are blood brothers, after all.",
    ["Dialogue32521010"]="For your information, my reach extends far beyond lowly guards and the Royal Chivalry... In fact, my men have already planted explosives in every corner of the palace! All I have to do is give the signal... And boom! We all go up in a brilliant ball of flames!",
    ["Dialogue32521011"]="So now, my dear guests, I offer you two options. You can either kneel before Odin's Statue and the portraits of our past kings, and swear your loyalty to me... Or you can die. The choice is yours.",
    ["Dialogue32521012"]="So this is what you've wanted all along, Azer, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue3252102"]="Odin preserve us! What on earth is happening...?",
    ["Dialogue3252103"]="Prince Azer?! Wh-What do you think you're doing?!",
    ["Dialogue3252104"]="You... You want to know... What I'm doing?! Haha... Hahahaha! After all of this, you dare ask such a stupid question?!\nI already told you, fools! I wish to become the most powerful man in this kingdom! With Odin and you all as my witnesses, I shall take this sword and ring in hand, and ascend to my rightful place on that throne!",
    ["Dialogue3252105"]="So this is why you pretended to be Aronst all this time... To be crowned king in his place? This is...\n(Jurgen falls silent, but he shares the same expression as everyone else in attendance. It is clear that they all believe the young prince has gone mad.)",
    ["Dialogue3252106"]="Make no mistake, Jurgen... Not once have I ever claimed to be Aronst. If you wish to fault anyone, fault yourself and the others for not realizing it sooner. Still, if it wasn't for your ignorance, I never would have been able to put on such a spectacular performance. As a reward for everyone, I think I shall change the ending of my little drama... Tell me, which do you all prefer? Comedies... Or tragedies?",
    ["Dialogue3252107"]="Comedies, tragedies... What difference does it make?",
    ["Dialogue3252108"]="It makes a world of difference! It will determine if you will live in disgrace... Or die with dignity! Now, which will it be?\n(Azer holds his blade aloft, trembling slightly as he points it towards Bohr's chest.)",
    ["Dialogue3252109"]="I haven't forgotten, Lord Bohr... You think I have no way of turning the Royal Chivalry against you? Why don't you try giving your Defense Force soldiers an order? I wonder what will happen if you do...",
    ["Dialogue3252201"]="To live in disgrace, or die with dignity... How very humorous of you, Azer.\nI am starting to believe that you are capable of doing all of this, if only because of that blackened heart of yours. You would turn against your comrades, your kin... Even yourself. For someone who lives their life on a knife's edge, nothing is out of the question.",
    ["Dialogue3252202"]="Finally, someone with an ounce of reason! Then are you prepared to swear your loyalty to me, Bohr?",
    ["Dialogue3252203"]="I wasn't finished speaking, Azer. All of the crimes I mentioned—Murdering the three princes, attacking and poisoning Prince Aronst, inciting rebellion within the Royal Chivalry, and usurping the throne... I have no doubt that you are capable of carrying them out. However... Your father is just as capable, as well.",
    ["Dialogue3252204"]="(Bohr turns to look at Ian, who has been maintaining his silence the entire time. His face looks calm, but you notice that his hands are clenched tightly into fists behind his back.)\nIan Walter... Compared to your son, you would have even fewer qualms about committing these crimes. In fact... I believe you are the real mastermind behind them. Azer is merely carrying out your orders.",
    ["Dialogue3252205"]="Now then, Can you prove to us that Ian Walter had nothing to do with these atrocious acts?",
    ["Dialogue3252206"]="Ah... You have a point, Bohr. Let me get this straight...\n(Azer lowers his head slightly, as though lost in thought. Upon seeing this, Bohr finally appears to relax somewhat.)",
    ["Dialogue3252207"]="Just kidding!",
    ["Dialogue3252208"]="What...?",
    ["Dialogue3252209"]="(Azer throws his head back and cackles tauntingly at Bohr.)\nYou think I don't know what's going through your head, Bohr?!",
    ["Dialogue3252210"]="You wish to stall for time, yes? So that your subordinates can dispose of all of my explosives, and round up my men? An amusing ploy... But utterly meaningless, all the same.",
    ["Dialogue3252211"]="My patience has run out, Bohr. What my father said earlier was completely right: only someone with absolute power can break the rules of the game, and that someone... Is me!",
    ["Dialogue3252212"]="The time has come to draw the curtains on my masterpiece. I would like to call this final act \"Blood and Resolve.\" Naturally, it's about my resolve... And your blood.",
    ["Dialogue3252301"]="May Odin bless these poor, unfortunate souls...",
    ["Dialogue3252302"]="(The venerable archbishop just shakes his head mournfully.)\nThe prince's soul... Has already departed for another realm. Merciful Odin, please guide him to his rightful resting place...",
    ["Dialogue3252303"]="You are far too kind, Archbishop! A bloodthirsty murderer like him doesn't deserve Odin's grace!",
    ["Dialogue3252304"]="She's right! The ceremonial banquet has been all but ruined... When will we be allowed to leave?!\nMay he fall into the darkest depths of the Realm of the Dead, and atone for his sins in the waters of the Gjoll!",
    ["Dialogue3252305"]="Ah... I respect your intentions, Adventurer, but unfortunately... This is no longer our decision to make.",
    ["Dialogue3252306"]="Given his egregious behavior today, Prince Azer has all but lost the right to be buried in the royal cemetery... Even as Archbishop, I can offer him nothing more than my sincerest prayers now... I only hope that his soul finds peace in the next life...",
    ["Dialogue3252307"]="Forgive me, Adventurer... If you still have the strength to do so, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>help Lord Bohr finish the ceremony</color>. I... I require solitude right now...",
    ["Dialogue3252401"]="What happened? It was not yet time... So why did you act?!",
    ["Dialogue3252402"]="B-But Lord Bohr, we received a message from a noble saying that there was an emergency in the banquet hall! He claimed that you sent him out to call for help!",
    ["Dialogue3252403"]="What nonsense is this? You knew that the banquet hall was completely sealed before the ceremony began! There's no way for anyone to enter or exit the room, so how could I have sent for your help?!",
    ["Dialogue3252404"]="You're saying that those servants were responsible? But weren't they working for Azer? Why would they do something that would guarantee their master's death?!",
    ["Dialogue3252405"]="He wanted to die? But why?",
    ["Dialogue3252406"]="(As you recount the story to Bohr, you suddenly realize that Azer had already foreseen his own death at the time.)\nAzer... He told you about the Walter Family's history?",
    ["Dialogue3252407"]="Indeed... Judging from your account, he was already disguised as Aronst when he told you that story at the West Gate Cemetery... Which was taken from the very real history between his father, Ian Walter, and his father's younger brother, Ivan Walter. It happened many years ago... Ian ultimately became the head of the Walter Family, while his own brother was stripped of his identity, and cast out of the kingdom...",
    ["Dialogue3252408"]="This matter is no secret within noble circles. Ivan has been dead for many years now, but he was never laid to rest in his family's cemetery, and the Walter Family has gone to great lengths to conceal his existence. With each new generation, this part of their history gradually fades into the passage of time...",
    ["Dialogue3252409"]="You think he did all of this just to avoid repeating history... So that he and Aronst didn't suffer the same fate as their father and uncle, yes?",
    ["Dialogue3252410"]="Perhaps... But there's no point in guessing anymore.\n(Bohr shakes his head sullenly. You begin to wonder if he feels remorse for what he did today... But perhaps this was the best possible outcome for the Rune Kingdom's sake.)",
    ["Dialogue3252411"]="Now isn't the time to discuss these things... We should <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for those Banquet Servants</color>. They may be able to provide us with more insight.",
    ["Dialogue3252501"]="Azer really did think of everything... He never would have left us such an obvious clue. It appears those servants fled from the palace during the chaos earlier.",
    ["Dialogue3252502"]="Shall we seal the banquet hall once again, Lord Bohr? We may still find clues hidden within...",
    ["Dialogue3252503"]="(Bohr shakes his head at the Defense Force Soldier's suggestion.)\nI'm afraid we have a more pressing matter at hand, which is finding the real Prince Aronst. If the Adventurer is right, Azer began masquerading as his brother early this morning... This means Aronst has been missing for a full day now.",
    ["Dialogue3252504"]="The princess already announced the results of the election today. Prince Aronst is our rightful king now, and we must do everything in our power to find him and ensure his safety. As for everyone here...",
    ["Dialogue3252505"]="(Bohr quietly surveys the banquet hall. Everyone in attendance, including himself, is responsible for the well-being and success of the entire kingdom, and yet...)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Heh... Despite our status and our education, it appears a foolhardy prince was still able to get the better of us all...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3252506"]="It's nothing. Men, open the doors of the banquet hall, and escort everyone back to their quarters.",
    ["Dialogue3252507"]="Yes, even the Walters.\n(Bohr looks towards Ian, who has been surrounded by a group of officials. He smiles back at Bohr with his usual elegant composure.)",
    ["Dialogue3252508"]="Azer paid for his crimes and conspiracies with his life today, and his hostility towards Ian has proven his father's innocence... Now that Azer has been brought to justice, I can no longer hold the Walter family accountable for his sins.",
    ["Dialogue3252509"]="Only begrudgingly so, Adventurer... But with matters as complicated as they are now, I fear we cannot afford to act rashly. The foundation of our kingdom has just been rocked to its core, and Aronst is nowhere to be found... If we handle the Walter Family without his permission, it will only tarnish his reputation as our newly-appointed king.",
    ["Dialogue3252510"]="But don't worry, Adventurer. One way or another... They will be made to pay.",
    ["Dialogue3260101"]="This... This goes too far! You would send your own brother to his death?!",
    ["Dialogue32601010"]="Damn it all... If the victor can only be determined in battle, then draw your blade, brother!",
    ["Dialogue32601011"]="Very well... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Draw your blade</color> as well, brother! I swear I will lose at all costs!",
    ["Dialogue3260102"]="Just remember that Lord Naght Sieger will kill us both if we fail to obey him!",
    ["Dialogue3260103"]="Wh-What?! You mean you've never heard of Lord Naght Sieger?! He is Queen Hel's most powerful subordinate! Not only does have the power to dispense punishments... He has the power to calm Queen Hel's heart, as well! Cross him, and he'll bring the full weight of Niflheim down on your head!",
    ["Dialogue3260104"]="He... He asked us to take part in the Grand Celebration!!! Waaaaaaaah!!!\n(You cover your ears to block out their desperate wailing.)\nWhat should we do, brother?! I don't want to die!!!",
    ["Dialogue3260105"]="I-I don't want to die either, brother! But what hope do we have? Our opponent is the Lord of the Dead... Everyone knows that he and the Mutegirl have never lost at a Grand Celebration, not even once! Who knows how many undead souls have been pierced by that monstrous lance...",
    ["Dialogue3260106"]="\"Just a celebration\"...? <size=26>\"JUST\"</size>?!\nWhat do you think they do around here for entertainment, you idiot?! We're not talking about snacks and party favors... We're talking about a death match!",
    ["Dialogue3260107"]="Queen Hel personally selects the combatants for her \"Grand Celebrations,\" and pits them all against each other in the arena. The only way to survive is to kill another opponent and advance to the next round! But if you die in the arena... Then your soul will truly vanish into oblivion!!!",
    ["Dialogue3260108"]="Which is why my older brother should be the one to participate! His sword skills are far greater than mine!",
    ["Dialogue3260109"]="What are you blabbering about, fool?! My swordsmanship could never hold a candle to yours!",
    ["Dialogue3260201"]="(The two Undead Soldiers, still reeling from their defeat at your hands, suddenly embrace each other and burst into tears once again.)\nThe two of us didn't stand a chance against this greenhorn, and he's never even been to a Grand Celebration! We're as good as dead, brother!",
    ["Dialogue32602010"]="If you want to survive, stay away from the Lord of the Dead during the battle! We'll free you once the fighting is over!",
    ["Dialogue32602011"]="(With a resounding clang, the enormous iron gate slams shut behind you, trapping you inside the arena.)\n<size=26>We're counting on you, greenhorn!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3260202"]="Er... Wh-Why don't you go finish the mission instead, brother? At least one of us will survive if you do!",
    ["Dialogue3260203"]="What? No! Why does it have to be me, brother?",
    ["Dialogue3260204"]="Well, uh... B-Because I'm the smarter one! Who better to look after our family's business but me?",
    ["Dialogue3260205"]="You... Are you calling me stupid?! Damn you... I don't want to be brothers with you anymore!\n(The brothers have gone from hugging each other to strangling each other. You have no choice but to intervene once again.)",
    ["Dialogue3260206"]="Butt out, greenhorn! This is a battle between us, and I intend to... W-Wait a minute, brother!\nLord Naght Sieger's order was to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle this potion on the Lord of the Dead's body</color>... But he didn't say we had to do it ourselves!",
    ["Dialogue3260207"]="Y... You don't mean...\n(The brothers stop their quarreling, and immediately turn their attention to you.)",
    ["Dialogue3260208"]="<size=26>You do it, greenhorn!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3260209"]="(One brother shoves a potion into your hands while the other shoves you through the arena's gates. Apparently, their bitter struggle for life and death is just a distant memory now.)\nI can't think of a better person to handle such a dangerous task! Now get out there and <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle this potion on the Lord of the Dead's body</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3260301"]="(The skeletal knight glares down at you from atop his steed, and points his sharpened lance at your forehead. He does not appear to be the kind to take \"no\" for an answer.)\nBefore the battle begins, young warrior... I ask that you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer some questions of mine</color>. They are simple in nature, but require your honest responses... What say you?",
    ["Dialogue3260401"]="Thank you for your sincerity, young warrior. I have now taken the full measure of your character... When the battle begins, just stand behind me.",
    ["Dialogue3260402"]="(Without answering you, the knight tugs on his horse's reigns slightly, and faces the other combatants.)\nYou will survive this, young warrior. On my honor as a knight... I shall guarantee it.",
    ["Dialogue3260403"]="Hey! You there, Adventurer! Don't just stand there, <color=#CA2E0AFF>get over here</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3260501"]="So you passed the Lord of the Dead's trial too, eh? Great! You're with us now, so stick close by and try not to get killed!",
    ["Dialogue3260502"]="I'm talking about those questions he just asked you! They say he does that before every battle, to decide whether you're a friend or a foe... And it looks like you made the cut! Good thing too, or else you'd be... Oh, it looks like <color=#CA2E0AFF>the battle has already begun</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3260503"]="Oh, you don't have to worry too much about that anymore. Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>come here</color>, and you'll see exactly what I mean!",
    ["Dialogue3260601"]="Very well... You all know what to do now. Draw your weapons and kill me.",
    ["Dialogue32606010"]="Let's just get it over with! I don't want my soul to be sent to oblivion!",
    ["Dialogue32606011"]="M-Me, either...",
    ["Dialogue32606012"]="It's an easy enough job, everyone! Just grab your weapons and surround him, then slowly, gently...\n(At the young man's encouragement, everyone carefully approaches the kneeling knight. You suddenly realize that <color=#CA2E0AFF>this is the perfect opportunity to sprinkle the potion on the Lord of the Dead</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3260602"]="You are... An unfamiliar face here. I see... This must be your very first Grand Celebration, yes? It is little wonder you are unaware of the rules.",
    ["Dialogue3260603"]="In this battle, hiding behind my shield is not enough to guarantee your survival; you must defeat at least one opponent in order to leave this place with your soul intact. I could never ask you all to fight amongst yourselves, which is why...",
    ["Dialogue3260604"]="(He kneels down once more, and holds up his empty hands.)\nI ask that you all take up arms, and strike me down at the same time. This is the only way I can guarantee your survival.",
    ["Dialogue3260605"]="Thank you for your kind concern, young warrior... It was you who helped me best those wraiths in battle, was it not? You have no reason to worry about me, for I have defeated enough opponents to qualify for the next battle. Even if I should fall today... Hel will not let me stray far from the arena.",
    ["Dialogue3260606"]="Even so, I can't just kill someone like this...",
    ["Dialogue3260607"]="That's right! No matter what you say, you saved us all! How could we repay you like this?!",
    ["Dialogue3260608"]="(As everyone begins to hesitate, the young man who called you over at the start of battle stands up and starts to shout.)\nWhat's the matter with all of you? We're all undead! We don't even feel pain! And besides, he assured us that he'll survive regardless of what we do... If we don't hurry up and kill him, the Soul Bell will ring, and all of us will disappear!",
    ["Dialogue3260609"]="Is... Is this really okay...?",
    ["Dialogue3260701"]="By Odin's beard... You actually survived!\nWhere's the potion? Did you manage to sprinkle it on the Lord of the Dead?!",
    ["Dialogue3260702"]="You did it... You really did it! Now we don't have to die, brother!",
    ["Dialogue3260703"]="And it's all thanks to your brilliant idea! I've never been prouder to call you my brother in all of my life!\n(The brothers sob hysterically as they embrace each other once again, forcing you to pull them apart yet again to answer your questions.)",
    ["Dialogue3260704"]="Oh, just Lord Naght Sieger's extra-special... Wait a second... Oh no!!!\n(The older brother begins screaming in terror.)",
    ["Dialogue3260705"]="<size=26>We're done for! That was Lord Naght Sieger's extra-special tracking potion!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3260706"]="You mean that impossibly-expensive tracking potion... Made from only the rarest ingredients in all the realms... That only works for an hour after it's been taken? THAT tracking potion?!",
    ["Dialogue3260707"]="<size=26>It's over for us, brother! Lord Naght Sieger will never forgive us for this!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3260708"]="Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!!!",
    ["Dialogue3260709"]="Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!!!\n(The brothers begin howling and sobbing uncontrollably once again. It seems you will have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait until they finish crying</color> before getting any more answers...)",
    ["Dialogue3270101"]="B... Brother... Hic! What should... Hic! What should we do... Hic!",
    ["Dialogue3270102"]="H-Hey! Don't talk to my brother like that! There's nothing wrong with a little crying when you're about to die! Waaaaaah!!!",
    ["Dialogue3270103"]="Why don't you what? What could you possibly do... W-Wait! This greenhorn was able to survive Hel's Grand Celebration, right brother? Maybe he can even track down the Lord of the Dead for us!",
    ["Dialogue3270104"]="You're absolutely right!\n(In an instant, the two Undead Soldiers cease their blubbering and grab you by the sleeves, their eyes burning with newfound hope.)\nIt's up to you now, greenhorn! Take this! It's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Potion of Revelation</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3270105"]="Listen carefully! Lord Naght Sieger tasked us with not only sprinkling that tracking potion on the Lord of the Dead during the Grand Celebration, but also <color=#CA2E0AFF>following him</color> to a remote location and <color=#CA2E0AFF>convincing him to drink this Potion of Revelation</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3270106"]="Lord Naght Sieger noted a change in the Lord of the Dead's combat style, and has reason to believe that he has been cheating in the arena. This Potion of Revelation is capable of nullifying most magical effects in this world... So once the Lord of the Dead imbibes it, make sure to report any changes to us!",
    ["Dialogue3270107"]="Also, the tracking potion you used on him contains a rare fruit juice, one which will attract luminescent insects to him. Just follow their trail, and you should find the Lord of the Dead in no time! Now get to it!",
    ["Dialogue3270201"]="(Before the Undead Soldiers finish their explanation, you already spy a set of glowing footprints on the ground nearby. They appear to be made by a pair of skeletal feet, and are already surrounded by a number of oddly-glowing insects...)",
    ["Dialogue3270301"]="(As you follow the trail, the footprints grow <color=#CA2E0AFF>heavier</color> and less balanced. You can almost perceive a great deal of <color=#CA2E0AFF>pain</color> from the person who left them behind. You also notice a few wet areas on the ground; whether they were made with sweat or tears remains unclear to you...)",
    ["Dialogue3270401"]="(The glowing footprints begin to drag heavily through the dirt, and disappear into the toxic, frigid waters of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hvergelmir</color>. You spot a small pool of viscous <color=#CA2E0AFF>vomit</color> near the last set of footprints on the riverbank...)",
    ["Dialogue3270501"]="We were too late... What do we do now?! He's gone to... Mmph?! Mmph mmph mmph!!!",
    ["Dialogue3270502"]="Gone, er... Gone across the river!\n(He covers his brother's mouth with one hand and chokes his brother with the other. Apparently, he was about to say something important.)",
    ["Dialogue3270503"]="Wh-What my brother meant to say, is that because you failed to find the Lord of the Dead before he crossed the Gjoll, the tracking potion's effects have expired!",
    ["Dialogue3270504"]="Yes, it is! This means your only choice now... is to go to his home and wait for him to return! Regardless of where he is right now, he's bound to go home at some point, right?",
    ["Dialogue3270505"]="Mmph! Mmph-mmph-mmph!",
    ["Dialogue3270506"]="... Quiet, fool! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>calamity</color> is a secret! What do you think you're doing, telling people about it like it's nothing?!",
    ["Dialogue3270507"]="A... Anyway! The Lord of the Dead lives in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the northernmost house of Niflheim</color>! Go find a place to hide and wait for him to return home and relax... then seize the opportunity to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give him the Potion of Revelation</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3270601"]="Huff, huff—\n(You wait quietly for a while, but there seems to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>no change in the Lord of the Dead</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue3270602"]="Cough... Ahem... Psst...",
    ["Dialogue3270701"]="(Nimble footprints are scattered all over the ground, clearly left by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>young girl</color> who left in a hurry just now. In the dim fluorescent glow, <color=#CA2E0AFF>luminescent insects</color> gather from all directions to lap up the potion spilled on the soil...)",
    ["Dialogue3280101"]="... Sir, I failed to stop his plot many years ago, and now I can only repay you by saving your life in this way... I only hope that what I have done can alleviate your pain...",
    ["Dialogue3280102"]="You... Just now, were you...",
    ["Dialogue3280103"]="... No, I'm not. But now, after everything you've seen...\n(The girl raises her hand slightly, and a sharp dagger appears in her palm.)\nSorry, but I'll have to ask you to go to sleep for a while.",
    ["Dialogue3280201"]="... Urgh... This wound... I was too careless...",
    ["Dialogue3280202"]="Don't worry yourself, stranger. Instead, perhaps you can tell me something... Why are you following me?",
    ["Dialogue3280203"]="You... used a tracking potion on me and followed me from the Undead Arena all the way to here?",
    ["Dialogue3280204"]="(As she forces a wry smile, a sigh flows from her pale lips.)\nIn that case... you must have guessed by now that I'm an impostor, and the one sleeping at home right now is the real Lord of the Dead.",
    ["Dialogue3280205"]="... You want to know why I would do such a thing?\n(In a trance, she looks at the gravestone in front of her again.)\nIt's a long story, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3280206"]="If you're willing to spend some time talking with me about the past... First, <color=#CA2E0AFF>cast your eyes upon the epitaph on this gravestone</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3280301"]="The exploits of this knight cannot be found in the history books. His life was buried under the ruins of Glast Heim. No one remembers him... and no one knows of his deeds. Even this tomb was built for him after I fell into the Realm of the Dead...",
    ["Dialogue32803010"]="(The girl suddenly covers her mouth and coughs. Her chest heaves violently, as though she is finding it difficult to breathe.)\nI... I want to ask something of you... W... What happened today... Cough, cough, cough!",
    ["Dialogue32803011"]="(She purses her lips, holding back her discomfort, and points at the swaying <color=#CA2E0AFF>herb</color> nearby.)\nT... That...",
    ["Dialogue3280302"]="... Yes, I engraved it myself. Do you want to know how I know this secret?",
    ["Dialogue3280303"]="Because... I also experienced the war that destroyed Glast Heim and even witnessed the whole plot through which the Holy Fire Knight was framed. The culprit was a malicious squire who would stop at nothing to lure the Holy Fire Knight into his trap, even if it meant using an innocent civilian as bait...",
    ["Dialogue3280304"]="... Yes. I am the one he used. He caught me and told the Holy Fire Knight that there was still someone who had yet to evacuate from the battlefield. At that time, the city had already been besieged by monsters, and even though he was an unparalleled fighter, he could not make it through the horde unscathed. As I lay locked in the cellar of that abandoned house, how I wished that he would never show up again!",
    ["Dialogue3280305"]="... But he came, nonetheless. As always, he carried out his brand of justice as resolutely as ever. He took me out of the cellar. I struggled with all my might, wishing he would just leave me there, but I couldn't utter a sound back then due to the throat condition I was born with. I could only watch as that squire scattered flames around the oil-soaked haystacks outside the house and lured countless monsters into attacking us!",
    ["Dialogue3280306"]="(The girl closes her eyes, and her voice trembles. At this moment, it is as if you can see her younger self shivering in the arms of the knight all those years ago.)\n... I should have died there. The Holy Fire Knight stopped a burning beam from crushing me, blocking it with his body. Because of me, he ended up trapped there, unable to move. I couldn't save him. All I could do was return to the street to find help...",
    ["Dialogue3280307"]="No... I couldn't find anyone willing to help, Adventurer. At that time, Glast Heim was a scene of pure chaos. There were people trying to flee left, right, and center and they couldn't understand why this mute girl insisted on going back to the middle of the battlefield, so no one was willing to answer my pleas when I asked them to come to the burning abandoned house with me... I watched him die, but I couldn't do a thing to help him.",
    ["Dialogue3280308"]="... Afterward, when Glast Heim collapsed, I was forced to leave my hometown and finally died of illness. But I never expect to meet my former benefactor again after descending into the Realm of the Dead. He hadn't changed at all... Although he was imprisoned, he never for one second betrayed his devotion to justice...",
    ["Dialogue3280309"]="That's right, Adventurer... That ghastly Lord of the Dead is, in fact, the Holy Fire Knight. Every time he joined a Grand Celebration, he would protect the good souls threatened by Hel's oppression with his shield, and after defeating all of the Wraiths, he would sacrifice himself to let them get through the game unharmed. All I could do was try my best to imitate him... Cough...",
    ["Dialogue3280401"]="... Adventurer, I know you are a kind person. At the party just now, you didn't hide behind my shield or choose to kill me. If you are willing to keep everything you've seen today a secret... I would be very grateful to you.",
    ["Dialogue3280402"]="... Do you want to know about the \"calamity\"? Hmm... Actually, it's not really that much of a secret. Every soul that enters Niflheim must be cleansed in the poisonous glacier of Hvergelmir. This process is essentially equivalent to breaking down and reassembling one's soul, so it is called the \"calamity\" by the undead.",
    ["Dialogue3280403"]="Hel initially decided to let the Holy Fire Knight take part in the Grand Celebration because she wanted to see what kind of choice this great hero would make when faced with having to take so many lives. What the Holy Fire Knight did surprise her so much that she left his soul untouched and allowed him to compete again and again, on the condition that after each competition, the Holy Fire Knight must return to the Gjoll and experience the torture of the calamity again and again...",
    ["Dialogue3280404"]="(Seeing your doubt, the girl's eyes drop slightly, and several sighs escape her mouth.)\nRight... Ordinary Undead does not feel any pain. But Hel even restored the Holy Fire Knight's ability to feel pain in order to see him yield...",
    ["Dialogue3280405"]="... Every time he dies in the competition, the Holy Fire Knight suffers heart-piercing pain. After the competition, he returns to the Gjoll and experiences the torment of his soul being torn asunder over and again! However, he has always borne this fact in silence and never mentions it to the kind-hearted undead on the competition field...",
    ["Dialogue3280406"]="I just... couldn't stand by and watch the man who saved me suffer. So, I also signed up for the Grand Celebration to hone my combat skills in the arena, hoping to be strong enough to do something for him one day. When the time was ripe, I offered up my body to the necromancer of Niflheim in exchange for a few formulae...",
    ["Dialogue3280407"]="That's right... It's a dream elixir that can awaken the Holy Fire Knight from his dream. Before that, I also secretly fed him a dream-generating potion to make him take part in the Grand Celebration in his dream and believe it to be true. I drank the deformation potion and pretended to be him...",
    ["Dialogue3280408"]="... So, that's what happened. You really pulled the wool out under everyone's eyes, didn't you?",
    ["Dialogue3280501"]="... Do you really think you all can escape from me?\n(Someone grabs the girl's arm with such force that she begins coughing.)",
    ["Dialogue32805010"]="Hah... Naght Sieger. I am not afraid of death. I will not yield to you.\n(She raises her pale face, pride beaming from her red eyes.)\nBut, how about we make a bet?",
    ["Dialogue32805011"]="If you win, I will, according to your request, accuse the Holy Fire Knight of being an impostor. But if I win... please remove him from the list of Grand Celebration participants and let him live in the Realm of the Dead in peace.",
    ["Dialogue32805012"]="... Well, what are we betting on?",
    ["Dialogue32805013"]="(The girl smiles and approaches Naght Sieger's ear. You can't hear what she whispers to him, but you can see from Naght Sieger's expression that it is something pleasing to him.)\n... Do you have the courage, Judge of the Underworld?",
    ["Dialogue32805014"]="What is there to be afraid of? Presumably, the Queen will also gladly agree to this wager. I will go to the temple and report this. Hurry back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Arena </color>and wait for me. Of course, don't say I didn't warn you, and don't think about sneaking away. Otherwise... prepare for the fright of your lives.",
    ["Dialogue3280502"]="Cough, cough... Cough, cough, cough... Na...Na...ght! Naght Sieger!",
    ["Dialogue3280503"]="(He looks at you with malicious eyes.)\nWatch your manners, filth. I could have given you the benefit of the doubt because the potion you left behind helped me to find this sinner disguised as the Lord of the Dead for me. But if you are equally riddled with sin... forgive me for what I must do to you.",
    ["Dialogue3280504"]="Cough... You... You don't have to get so riled up! It was all me... I'll take all the blame. Let the Adventurer go!",
    ["Dialogue3280505"]="... Oh? Well... check the goods, then!\n(Naght Sieger sneers and tears the girl's clothes apart. The broken cloth falls to her shoulder, revealing the scarred skin beneath her collarbone.)",
    ["Dialogue3280506"]="Sure enough... These scars made by sharp weapons are evidence enough. Unexpectedly, like that fool, someone would rather bear the pain of penetrating their heart to save a bunch of irrelevant strangers... Hah, despicable hypocrites.",
    ["Dialogue3280507"]="My actions may be hypocritical... but the Holy Fire Knight always endeavored to save everyone! You have no right to insult him like that!",
    ["Dialogue3280508"]="In the Underworld... I am the all-powerful executioner of the realm... No one is better qualified than me to punish criminals violating the rules of this land? Remember that no one can bear the deserved retribution of the Lord of the Dead! As for you... maybe I can still give you a chance?",
    ["Dialogue3280509"]="(Naght Sieger's voice carries a vapid sense of joy while his incessant giggles betray the preaching of a bitter, unsatisfied soul.)\nIf you are willing to let him take the blame for the matter at hand... I may spare your life, little girl.",
    ["Dialogue3280601"]="... Damn it! Damn you all to hell! How dare you violate the rules of the Grand Celebration!",
    ["Dialogue32806010"]="If you wish to save the citizenry, <size=26>then just die! Why should I exchange your life for that of my people?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue32806011"]="... But he did die following his own path, Naght Sieger.\n(Faced with Naght Sieger's anger, the girl becomes increasingly calm.)",
    ["Dialogue32806012"]="The Holy Fire Knight was willing to sacrifice himself to protect the weak, and he finally realized his ultimate belief at the cost of his life. But you feel that his selfless devotion was not merely self-satisfying hypocrisy, so you must avenge yourself at the expense of others. I have no right to judge who is right and who is wrong—that is Odin's duty. However, I have shown you a fact related to this bet...",
    ["Dialogue32806013"]="(She raises her hand and points to those on the battlefield who do not wish to harm the Holy Fire Knight.)\nYou see, the self-satisfaction and hypocrisy you were talking about can still win so many followers on his behalf.",
    ["Dialogue32806014"]="You... You... Well, you will all be buried with the great Holy Fire Knight!\n(A flame rises from the sword's blade upon his command, and an overwhelming sense of oppression follows.)",
    ["Dialogue32806015"]="... There's no need for that. We are all familiar with the rules of the Grand Celebration. It will not be long before those who fail to pass the competition's trials disappear amidst the sound of the Soul Bell... I just hope that you and Hel can abide by your agreement and will not torture innocent knights again. Of course, even if you break your pact...",
    ["Dialogue32806016"]="... The Holy Fire Knight would never betray his vision of justice. As long as he doesn't give in, we... will never lose.",
    ["Dialogue32806017"]="Dong—Dong—Dong—\n(The soul bell in the distant temple rings along with the girl's voice, signifying that the Grand Celebration is over.)",
    ["Dialogue32806018"]="Wait a minute! This... this girl!\n(The knight who has been silent so far finally accepts his judgment. He bends down and kneels before the petite girl and stares her in the eye.)\n... May I know your name?",
    ["Dialogue32806019"]="I am just an ordinary person who has been granted your favor. Most people would never receive the chance to repay such a debt... You don't have to remember my name, but if what I do can become the foundation of your faith...",
    ["Dialogue3280602"]="Naght Sieger! Have you forgotten our bet?!\nWe already said that if no one is willing to take the life of the Holy Fire Knight in this round, you should remove him from the Grand Celebration list and never disturb him again!",
    ["Dialogue32806020"]="(The girl's body gradually turns into flame amidst the sound of the Soul Bell, but her face is brimming with a vivid smile.)\n... Well, I should be very happy. Goodbye, my hero.",
    ["Dialogue3280603"]="... Or do you want to renege again and kill those who fought by your side?",
    ["Dialogue3280604"]="You... How did you know... Could it be that...\nNo! Impossible! You should have died in that house with him!",
    ["Dialogue3280605"]="... I wish I could have died in that fire. If I had, I wouldn't have had to watch my savior being engulfed by those flames, nor would I have had to run around that devastated city searching for help, but I fell into utter despair because nobody would help me... Not to mention, after returning to my benefactor's burial mound, I need to put up with your hateful face that gazes upon me like a clown and tramples on the bones of the Holy Fire Knight!",
    ["Dialogue3280606"]="(With a crash, a golden badge is thrown at the feet of Naght Sieger, clanging several times with a clear sound.)\nDo you remember this badge, Naght Sieger?",
    ["Dialogue3280607"]="This is proof that you belong to the Glast Heim Chivalry. You have sworn upon it—Do not bully the weak, do not fear the strong, unfaltering loyalty, undying love! But in the end, you ground your own glory beneath your feet! Aren't you ashamed?!",
    ["Dialogue3280608"]="What do you know...?! You don't understand?!\nIf it were not for him, would my wife and daughter have been tortured to death by those animals?!",
    ["Dialogue3280609"]="(He points his sword at the Lord of the Dead, his empty eyes full of hate.)\nHoly Fire Knight... What a Holy Fire Knight! How noble and kind-hearted you are! Even unwilling to harm prisoners of war and risk being punished for saving them... But those beasts instantly sparked a rebellion in the city and abused our people!",
    ["Dialogue3290101"]="(Rogge rips open the envelope. A few seconds later, he crumples it up and then tosses it to the bouncer behind him.)\nGo, put it into the trash can. You, get over here.",
    ["Dialogue3290102"]="Why do you come to me when you're one of the Moxie's?",
    ["Dialogue3290103"]="(Rogge hands over the letter to the bouncer.)\nLamy, read this out for him.",
    ["Dialogue3290104"]="Got it! \"My admiration for the almighty Rogge renders me sleepless at night, and the tears I've shed over the fact that I'm not yet his follower will turn an arid basin into a pond with running streams. Even the infamous Lugenburg Family owes you respect since you took over the Weinst Street. O MY ROGGE! Moxie pales in comparison to you. Please guide me, lead me, and push me to become an outstanding Rogue!\"",
    ["Dialogue3290105"]="To join us, you'll need to bite your fingertip and sign a pact with your blood. Well, since you picked me over Moxie...\n(A gloomy laugh breaks out from Rogge)\nHaha, the rules still must be followed! Lamy, if one does not use their own blood, what should one do?",
    ["Dialogue3290106"]="Let the enemy shed blood for them!",
    ["Dialogue3290107"]="Good. How about this—you now answer a few of my questions, and we'll talk about your <color=#CA2E0AFF>token of allegiance</color> later.",
    ["Dialogue3290201"]="Hahaha! Very good! The joy of seeing new blood in here never gets old! We, the Rogues, do not act like those pompous punks out there. You call me the boss, and I will treat you as my <color=#CA2E0AFF>own blood</color>, whether it's the best or the worst of our time.",
    ["Dialogue3290202"]="Now you only need to get the token of allegiance done! Let me think...",
    ["Dialogue3290203"]="Lamy! Did <color=#CA2E0AFF>McGille</color> punch you in the gut yesterday?",
    ["Dialogue3290204"]="Yes, boss! He did!",
    ["Dialogue3290205"]="Lamy! If this Adventurer makes him pay for that, will you stick up for him in the future?",
    ["Dialogue3290206"]="Of course! I treat my pals like my family!",
    ["Dialogue3290207"]="Well say. No matter how they phrase us out there, they are no comparison to us in how we treat each other! Adventurer, now is your turn to make that bonehead pay for what he did. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Leave the rest to me</color>, and I assure you if Lamy ever eats his word, I will be the first one to end his life.",
    ["Dialogue3290301"]="Drink up! Huh...?\nA drunk <color=#CA2E0AFF>black market merchant</color> walks up to you with a snifter in his hand.)\nWho are you?",
    ["Dialogue3290302"]="OUCH!\n(McGille gets knocked down to the floor, curled up like a boiled shrimp.)\nYou dare to punch me???",
    ["Dialogue3290303"]="Here! Over here! Someone's trying to jump me!",
    ["Dialogue3290304"]="Protect the boss!",
    ["Dialogue3290401"]="Rogge! What's your deal here?",
    ["Dialogue32904010"]="Don't speak nonsense, McGille! Adventurer, chuck this thing down his throat!",
    ["Dialogue32904011"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Potion</color>?! H-How did you get it? It belongs to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>military</color>!",
    ["Dialogue32904012"]="McGille, it's a fair game for everyone. You used to be in charge of the most prominent black market in Morroc. Now I see you're getting rusty and can't even tell what I'm doing here.",
    ["Dialogue32904013"]="Can't you tell something is off? Why didn't the <color=#CA2E0AFF>boss</color> of this tavern or the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's soldiers</color> show up after all the mess we made? It's been a while already.",
    ["Dialogue32904014"]="You... You're saying?!",
    ["Dialogue32904015"]="Adventurer, do what you're gonna do.",
    ["Dialogue3290402"]="Deal? McGille, I've warned you before. Don't mess with the wrong people, and don't get your filthy hands on something that does not belong to you...",
    ["Dialogue3290403"]="You and I got no history whatsoever. You can keep your sorry ass in Morroc while I do my own business in the Sograt Desert... But you just wished to reach into Sograt Desert, into <size=26>my Weinst Street!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3290404"]="(Rogge pulls out a dagger and sweeps it across McGille's face.)\nMcGille, you should've seen this coming at you before letting your filthy goods flow around in the market, in my family...",
    ["Dialogue3290405"]="Now I own you, McGille. Don't make me remind you what you should do...",
    ["Dialogue3290406"]="The rule says... In exchange for my life... I must give up my most precious thing...",
    ["Dialogue3290407"]="Ha... HAHAHAHA!\n(McGille rolls on the floor, laughing with tears)\nI thought you, Rogge the Great, was something, but not anymore!",
    ["Dialogue3290408"]="What? Do you think I'm stupid or something? Resources in the desert are scarce, and they have always been. It's doing business that makes you rich, not the pocket change you get from the protection fee. You're just gunning for my caravans as well as their trade routes and want them to become yours!",
    ["Dialogue3290409"]="Rogge, do you know who this is behind me? It's in your best interest to let go of me even though I can't utter the name of <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"That Lord.\"</color>",
    ["Dialogue3290501"]="(Rogge smiles at you brightly without giving a damn about the bloody-faced McGille lying on the floor.)\nWelcome to the family!",
    ["Dialogue3290502"]="His end is yet to come. In fact, it was right after Lamy got his beating that I decided to make a deal with<color=#CA2E0AFF> a great one who resides on Izlude Island</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3290503"]="Now that the deal is closed, why don't you run an errand for me to Izlude Island and notify their agent on the dock that their master's business has been taken care of?",
    ["Dialogue3290504"]="Don't worry. He'll come after you once you get there. I've made an agreement with their master, so they won't be harsh.",
    ["Dialogue3290601"]="My friend, you are... Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3290602"]="Shh! Shh! Now that the mess has been cleared up, my master can start heading home.",
    ["Dialogue3290603"]="Stop it here, Adventurer! The message has been received, and you should be heading back!",
    ["Dialogue3290701"]="You're back! Did the Lugenburg Family do anything to you?",
    ["Dialogue3290702"]="Are you asking why I made a deal with the second prince of the Lugenburg Family or how I got in touch with them?",
    ["Dialogue3290703"]="Hah! Being stupid is sinful for a Rouge, but taking on your stupidity is a rare virtue. The best possible outcome among the trades of Rogues is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get what you need and part ways</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3290704"]="\"That Lord\" wants to build his own caravan, but somehow, the black market merchants who work for McGille have been interfering with his plan. That's why he hired me to take care of McGille so that he could make his first move. Actually, I'll also have one less enemy who always stirs up my rules. Isn't it perfect?",
    ["Dialogue3290705"]="Tsk... There are always some idiots who are willing to get their hands dirty just to get rid of the biggest rat within the family with the minimum of fuss. I bet the Assassin Guild is getting busy again.",
    ["Dialogue3290706"]="A family known for its iron-fisted approach can actually raise a shrewd kid like this... interesting...",
    ["Dialogue3290707"]="(Rogge takes a look around him.)\nDesert Green Tavern sure has a good boss, right? It won't take long for word of McGille's death to spread. You and I will have to stay lowkey on Weinst Street for a while.",
    ["Dialogue3290708"]="Hah!\n(Rogge shakes the snifter in his hand until the foam dissipates, leaving only the clear amber liquor at the bottom.)\nAs for this question... Wait until you reach <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Lv.50</color> and officially become a Rogue. By then, you may find out about it.",
    ["Dialogue3290709"]="(Rogge gulps down all the remaining liquor and holds the snifter in the air, toasting to you)\nOff you go. I will prepare a Rouge Set for you while you hone your class skills. For Rouges, no enemies are everlasting, but only interests; to me, however, my family are permanent as well.",
    ["Dialogue3300101"]="(At Alchemist Guild's front entrance, Nicolas is surrounded by students and does not realize you're here.)\nSlow down, kids. All of your questions will be answered here.",
    ["Dialogue3300102"]="Master, I followed your instruction and added Frosty Grass to the Heat-resistance Potion. Why does the crucible still blow up?",
    ["Dialogue3300103"]="Master, there is a formula of Mad-bull Potion in the script of Master Howard... But the name of those materials...",
    ["Dialogue3300104"]="Scorched Mushrooms grow on igneous rocks which form from the cooling and solidified lava, so they contain plenty of fire elements. You can suppress their volatility by adding Frosty Grass, which contains water elements. These two kinds, however, will eventually counteract each other and create inevitable damage to the crucible, which causes it to explode.",
    ["Dialogue3300105"]="If you wish, you may go to the volcanic crater and gather some of the Scorched Mushrooms. While doing so, scoop a handful of the igneous rocks and bring them back for the craftsman to craft you a new crucible. Since Scorched Mushrooms grow on igneous rocks, using a crucible made from these rocks can absorb and enhance the fire elements even more. By then, Frosty Grass is no longer needed.",
    ["Dialogue3300106"]="As for you, Master Howard is a Kobold Alchemist, whose kind uses a different language than us. The bull in his script represents strength, so if you interpret it in our human language, it's just a Strength Potion that enhances your strength. Simple as that.",
    ["Dialogue3300107"]="Adventurer? It's been a while! I've heard from Hamid you want to become an Alchemist. I'm glad you've chosen a path that is full of wisdom.",
    ["Dialogue3300108"]="Before I lead you on the path of this class, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer three questions</color> to prove the determination and goodness you possess. Be advised that studying Alchemy involves lots of forbidden knowledge and tests of human nature. Many misguided Alchemists in Midgard have gone down a different path, and I don't want you to be the next one.",
    ["Dialogue3300109"]="(Nicolas hands you a sealed clear test tube.)\nDrink this Truth Potion in front of me, and you may start to answer the questions.",
    ["Dialogue3300110"]="(Your heart fills with an inexplicable sense of trust as his voice becomes deep and mellow.)\nKid, tell me your answers...",
    ["Dialogue3300201"]="You've made the right choice. Kid, one must know becoming an Alchemist is nothing compared to the vast knowledge we need to learn throughout the life of an Alchemist. The moment you successfully create your own Alchemy Potion, you're then qualified to be called an Alchemist.",
    ["Dialogue3300202"]="As the name implies, it possesses the ability to turn anything into gold, as how Alchemy first started. It can create golds to pay for Guild's daily expenditures and everyday materials. I will get you those secondary materials, but you're going to get the three primary materials by yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3300203"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Mineral Soil x5, Strong Alcohol x10, Hardened Soul x1</color>. For the first two materials, you can find them at Mjolnir Dead Pit 1F. As for how to obtain the Hardened Soul... I'll fill you in after you get the Mineral Soil and Strong Alcohol.",
    ["Dialogue3300301"]="Now only the last material needs to be collected. In the field of Alchemy, we abide by the supreme law of Equivalence Exchange. In other words, there is a consequence for every change and every move. Even the Alchemy Potion is a low-tier potion, but we still follow the formula and pay the corresponding price.",
    ["Dialogue3300302"]="Yes... With enough souls, they can substitute for any required materials or any price needed to be paid. Sigh... I have nothing against using monsters' souls as the Alchemy materials... But seeing those Alchemists go straight to the monsters just because the formula told them so and not even glance at a single page of the Alchemy Tome makes me sad. Some of them even reach their hand beyond the monsters to their same kind...",
    ["Dialogue3300303"]="Ahem! Don't be scared, kid. Where were we? ... Oh! Hardening the soul! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Myst's Soul</color> is the perfect medium for making an Alchemy Potion.",
    ["Dialogue3300304"]="You'll need enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soul Fixer</color> to deal with the dissipating soul. A few days ago, Ivy requested a truckload of Soul Fixer to collect monster souls from several locations. I will ask him to go to the Mjolnir Dead Pit first to make sure you have enough Soul Fixer, since there are few left in the Guild to spare you.",
    ["Dialogue3300305"]="This kid is spoiled by the Alchemists in the Guild. He's talented but acts like a child. Sigh, what if he gets hurt...\n(Nicholas frowns and thinks for a while as if he cannot do anything about his son.)",
    ["Dialogue3300306"]="Never mind, just tell him to go back home earlier...",
    ["Dialogue3300401"]="Huh? Did my father tell you to collect the materials here too? I don't get why he cared about these trivial matters... Those hair-pulling businesses in the Guild are eating him up already.",
    ["Dialogue3300402"]="Oh, this one. This is the Hardened Soul you are looking for. A shiny little thing like the gem, isn't it beautiful?\n(Ivy laughs uncannily.)\nThese are my materials, so get your own if you need them.",
    ["Dialogue3300403"]="Friendly reminder, Myst is the poison attribute monster. And here, I only have this Soul Fixer left.\n(Ivy tosses you a test tube, and he spreads his hands as if he's got nothing else for you.)",
    ["Dialogue3300404"]="After you defeat all these monsters, <color=#CA2E0AFF>drop the Soul Fixer on their souls before they dissipate</color>. Then you will have the thing you want. Ahh! I have to get started with my experiment now!",
    ["Dialogue3300501"]="Now you can go to the Alchemy Platform. Keep this in mind. Add the Strong Alcohol first and wait until it boils, then immediately add in the Mineral Soil and half the amount of those secondary materials, and stir them up in a clockwise direction. When you see the mixture turn into a brownish-yellow color with precipitate forming, it's time to pour in the rest of the Strong Alcohol.",
    ["Dialogue3300502"]="Wait until the Strong Alcohol boils, then add the rest of the secondary materials. When you see the precipitate dissolving, add the Hardened Soul quickly and stir them in a counterclockwise direction in the crucible. As soon as the mixture turns golden, you can put it into a test tube after filtering out the impurities.",
    ["Dialogue3300601"]="Excellent! You have proven yourself qualified to become an Alchemist, and the Guild will prepare you an official Alchemist gown. Once you <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach Job Lv.50</color>, you may <color=#CA2E0AFF>begin the Class Advancement Trial</color> to become a real Alchemist!",
    ["Dialogue3310101"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Thief.",
    ["Dialogue3310102"]="We here at the Criatura Academy have nothing left to teach you. Congratulations on reaching your potential. However, there's one more thing you need to do before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3310103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>, you no longer need it. I'll give you a new Class Manual for your second class, which doubles as your <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3310201"]="Heh. Ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3320101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily.)\nI haven't seen you for a few days and apparently you have changed quite a bit! It seems you are ready for class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3320102"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, thus proving you have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused about how to use the power.",
    ["Dialogue3320103"]="Right. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit your Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and combat skills... plus perhaps a few exciting surprises too. Heheh...",
    ["Dialogue3320104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await the good news, and hopefully, I can witness your \"rebirth\" before Odin's Statue soon!",
    ["Dialogue3320201"]="I see you're merging with the darkness right now. Very good. I'm proud of you.",
    ["Dialogue3320202"]="Shadow Chaser is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>incarnation of darkness, the lord of shadow</color>. They can initiate attacks while shrouded by the shadow, crisscrossing unhindered in the presence of shadow. When enemies are strangled by the darkness, Shadow Chasers begin their hunt.",
    ["Dialogue3320203"]="It is possible to attain such strength through practice year after year. But we, as future Shadow Chaser, the advancement of Thief, must look the other way. We need to find a <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerful monster lying in darkness and acquire its power</color> for our own good.",
    ["Dialogue3320204"]="Come see me at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Green Tavern</color> in Morroc.\n(As the red rose touches Moxie's lips, her smirk becomes even more mysterious and dangerous.)\nI will show you step by step how to seize the power of \"that one,\" and we might have to return to our old business.",
    ["Dialogue3320301"]="Caslisse, where is my stuff?",
    ["Dialogue3320302"]="Uhh...\n(Caslisse puts down the instrument and takes out a crumpled piece of paper from his pocket.)\nMs. Moxie, are you sure this <color=#CA2E0AFF>cringy poem</color> is what you came for?",
    ["Dialogue3320303"]="(Moxie glances at the paper and nods her head in satisfaction after receiving it.)\nThat's right, the more cringy it is, the better. Worry not. This is <color=#CA2E0AFF>an Ode from a servant to their master</color>, and I assure you it's not written in your name, Adventurer. But I think Caslisse over there would love to lend you a hand if you ever needed one.",
    ["Dialogue3320304"]="I refuse! There's no way I'd write such a thing against my will if it weren't to teach McGille a lesson.",
    ["Dialogue3320305"]="Shh! Being mysterious is part of being a Shadow Chaser. Meet me at the entrance of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pyramid 1F</color>, and you might find the answer.",
    ["Dialogue3320401"]="We are here. The monster in this pyramid has the offering for \"that one.\" Listen up, the monster we're summoning is called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Betrayer of Light</color>, which was a tyrannical and greedy pharaoh who loved <color=#CA2E0AFF>flattery from his servants and the servitude of beautiful women. Of course, he sought blood for pleasure by launching war after war</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3320402"]="We now have the offering for \"servant's flattery,\" and we must collect the remaining ones for the ritual, which symbolizes \"beautiful women's servitude\" and \"bloody wars.\" You can get the first one from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isis</color> and the second from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archer Skeleton</color>. Adventurer, if you managed to keep yourself alive after getting those, pay me a visit at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anubis Statue</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3320501"]="Excellent! With the completed offerings and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anubis' Blessing</color>, we are getting close.",
    ["Dialogue3320502"]="Indeed, the God of the Underworld appeared in the pharaoh's dream when he was at death's door, and he was unwilling to part with all his honor and glory. Not only he refused to leave with Anubis, but he also commanded his servants to build him the pyramid that would entitle him to eternity and immortality.",
    ["Dialogue3320503"]="The furious Anubis, God of the Underworld, commenced a pursuit of the pharaoh with his Undead Legion, leaving the desperate pharaoh with no choice but to turn himself into one of the Morroc's monsters and give up his sanity forever.",
    ["Dialogue3320504"]="Having surrendered his sanity, this Betrayer of Light only retained <color=#CA2E0AFF>greed and fear</color> from his former life.",
    ["Dialogue3320505"]="The greed he seeks for the world will make him answer our summon without a second thought, but his fear of death allows him to descend only through his projection. With the power of the mighty God of the Underworld, we can forbid the return of his projection to the main body. Soon as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat</color> him, I can deprive the projection of Shadow Power, send it to the church, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cleanse</color> it to make it yours.",
    ["Dialogue3320506"]="Adventurer, don't even think about it! If one's power is entirely from a monster, it makes him no different from a monster. Now, place the offerings beneath the statue, and wait for the descent of the Betrayer of Light.",
    ["Dialogue3320601"]="The power of Berserk Shadow... Adventurer, now <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring it to Wolmas the Archbishop</color> for cleansing. It will assist you in becoming a true Shadow Chaser.",
    ["Dialogue3320701"]="Once again, I witness an Adventurer who seeks the Shadow Power. People in the church see Shadow Chaser as an evil class that turns their back on the light. I reason this in the same way that Odin allows it to exist, even the power of shadow can do its part to strive for justice.",
    ["Dialogue3320702"]="There was a heated confrontation between both sides on this topic. Finally, the church enacted a new rule: The host of the Shadow Chaser Class Advancement Ceremony must take responsibility for guiding people toward kindness and righteousness.",
    ["Dialogue3320703"]="Your good deeds on Midgard have proved you are a good person. If you've made up your mind, <color=#CA2E0AFF>proceed to Odin's Statue and vow beneath it</color> that you will retain and guard the justice within your heart and shall never let them tainted by the evils. By then, I will cleanse this power and host the Class Advancement Ceremony for you.",
    ["Dialogue3320801"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. We may formally begin the Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time you prove your resolve to Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3330101"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Merchant.",
    ["Dialogue3330102"]="Criatura Academy has no more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your potential beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task yet before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3330103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>, you no longer need it. I'll give you a new Class Manual for your second class, which doubles as your <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3330201"]="Heh. Ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3340101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily.)\nI haven't seen you for a few days and apparently you have changed quite a bit! It seems you are ready for class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3340102"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, thus proving you have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused about how to use the power.",
    ["Dialogue3340103"]="Right. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit your Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and combat skills... plus perhaps a few exciting surprises too. Heheh...",
    ["Dialogue3340104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await the good news, and hopefully, I can witness your \"rebirth\" before Odin's Statue soon!",
    ["Dialogue3340201"]="Haha! How does it feel to become a Creator? I heard you've done Midgard a lot of good ever since you became a Creator. Good job!",
    ["Dialogue3340202"]="I guess you're here to ask me about how to become a Genetic! Listen up! Genetic is a powerful class that involves the transmutation of lives. In other words, they crack the code of lives like deciphering the code of safe boxes, and they pursue the evolution of lives just like how people keep track of the market. Let's say, a Creator can only create Homunculi under the existing human knowledge, but a Genetic...",
    ["Dialogue3340203"]="(The smart Merchant lowers his voice.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>A Genetic can create lives beyond lives... species beyond species...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3340204"]="Of course! These are all the nonsense out there. I'm nobody but only a Merchant, why would I know anything about genetics, coding, yadda yadda? So, I suggest you look another way and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go see Nicolas</color>. Seems like he likes you a lot!",
    ["Dialogue3340301"]="Good to see you again, Creator from afar. Your eyes are still filled with wisdom, which tells me that you're upholding the promise you made when you first became an Alchemist.",
    ["Dialogue3340302"]="Genetic... The last time I saw someone so young wanting to become a Genetic was years ago. Okay, I'll let you know the requirements to become a Genetic.",
    ["Dialogue3340303"]="Hah... there's nothing wrong with what he said. Just as I've told you before, the path to becoming an Alchemist is full of taboos and temptations. Kid, the first step of becoming a Genetic is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>complete the Life Transmutation using yourself as the sample</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3340304"]="You heard me right, kid. Do you realize what you are made of? Hair, blood, flesh, bones, nerves, organs, and a completed brain. Basically, it takes all these to complete this Life Transmutation. Besides, you need to draw an Alchemy Circle using your own blood and pay a price for it.",
    ["Dialogue3340305"]="(Nicholas nods in delight.)\nYou don't want to deprive someone else of their life, do you?",
    ["Dialogue3340306"]="It is the ability to observe the finest details of lives and understand how things work in the universe that makes a Genetic live up to their name, rather than seeing everything from a macro-perspective. Kid, there are many humanoid monsters with similar genetic structures to humans. You can find better replacements from them, saving you a lot of time in the process of collecting materials.",
    ["Dialogue3340307"]="But the downside of using these replacements is their <color=#CA2E0AFF>unknown impact</color> on the product of Life Transmutation. As a scholar, I'm not superstitious at all, but I wish you the best of luck anyway.",
    ["Dialogue3340401"]="You're back. Now, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>draw an Alchemy Circle using blood and place the materials in it</color> to complete the Life Transmutation.",
    ["Dialogue3340501"]="Well done, Adventurer. You should now <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> and complete your Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3340502"]="This is your work. I'll fix it in shape with our potion so that it can be used for crafting your Class Set. Believe me. You will not be disappointed...",
    ["Dialogue3340503"]="(Nicolas interrupts your questions.)\nAdventurer, do you forget about the law of Alchemy?",
    ["Dialogue3340504"]="Yes, with enough souls, every price can be paid. Adventurer, if you must go into the final step, then tell me... <color=#CA2E0AFF>What kind of souls should be paid for the Life Transmutation based on a real human sample?</color>",
    ["Dialogue3340505"]="Shh...\n(Nicolas stops you from answering the question.)\nWe have come to the end of the course. Remember this by heart: Stand firm and never ever sell your soul.",
    ["Dialogue3340601"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. We may formally begin the Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time you prove your resolve to Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3340701"]="(A wadding-like mass wraps around your finger gently. It's hollow in the center.)",
    ["Dialogue3350101"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Thief.",
    ["Dialogue3350102"]="Criatura Academy has no more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your potential beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task yet before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3350103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>, you no longer need it. I'll give you a new Class Manual for your second class, which doubles as your <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3350201"]="Heh. Ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3360101"]="Heh, it's been a while. I see you are now a certifiable Adventurer! I still remember vividly when you became a Super Novice.",
    ["Dialogue3360102"]="Criatura Academy has nothing more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your talent and resolve beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task before graduating.",
    ["Dialogue3360103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>. You don't need it anymore. I'll give you a new Class Manual, which doubles as the diploma, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3360201"]="So, are you ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3360301"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and measures you up and down with a smile.)\nHow have you grown over the last few days! It seems you are ready for some guidance on Job Advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3360302"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, and this proves you do have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused as to how to use your powers, right?",
    ["Dialogue3360303"]="That's the right attitude. Now, it's time for you to take the pursuit of knowledge to <color=#CA2E0AFF>your Class Master</color>. They will familiarize you with the new class and combat skills. And maybe... a surprise or two as well, heh!",
    ["Dialogue3360304"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I await good news from you. I hope the next time we meet... it's to witness your rebirth under Odin's statue.",
    ["Dialogue3360401"]="Are you that Super Novice from before? What are you doing here?",
    ["Dialogue3360402"]="Oh? So you're an Ultra Super Novice already?\n(As Tanders examines the changes in you, his expression turns from content to somber.)\nTime is cruel, Sansha...",
    ["Dialogue3360403"]="Yes, Master, that is why you cannot leap into battle without a complete recovery like you could fifty years ago.",
    ["Dialogue3360404"]="No, this is not a battle. It's my purpose...\n(Tanders pats you on the shoulder.)\nWhen I first saw you, Adventurer, I knew god has made the decision.",
    ["Dialogue3360405"]="It's a punishment for me losing the scroll. As the guardian, I must accept it. As the <color=#CA2E0AFF>successor of the Windmill Knight</color>, I shall tolerate no blemish on my honor!",
    ["Dialogue3360406"]="(Tanders' sword unsheathes in a flash and rests on your shoulder.)\nWill you <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany me</color>, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3360407"]="Very well!\n(You see a fleeting gleam in Tanders eyes.)\nBelieve me, when you leave this desert, you will know how to become a <color=#CA2E0AFF>true Super Novice</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3360501"]="(The sandy wind flutters Tanders' beard, making the knight appear older than at first glance.)\nAdventurer, I apologize for withholding information previously, but since you are here, you must know the truth.",
    ["Dialogue3360502"]="I withheld certain truths about Labyrinth Forest from Mainz. That escaped monster not only broke containment but stole <color=#CA2E0AFF>a scroll</color> as well.",
    ["Dialogue3360503"]="Correct. That's a divine scroll exclusive to the Super Novice class. According to the record, it contained a trace of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>God's Will</color>. To become a true Super Novice, you must gain the scroll or its guardian's approval.",
    ["Dialogue3360504"]="(Tanders shakes his head.)\nEver since you became the Ultra Super Novice, I could no longer sense its whereabouts. Perhaps it has found a new keeper.",
    ["Dialogue3360505"]="You ask too many questions, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3360506"]="But I suppose it's all right. Since the scroll chose you, you are entitled to more. I think the scroll no longer approved me not because I lost it, but because I chose to lie about it.",
    ["Dialogue3360507"]="I hid the fact from Mainz, went to the desert alone to fight the monster, and was soundly defeated. Following the Void, that monster gained greater cunning and realized it couldn't attain a higher form like that of a Demon or Blood Clan due to race constraint, so it settled on a sacrifice...",
    ["Dialogue3360508"]="Sigh... In the bowels of Sphinx Cavern sits a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sacrificial altar</color> built by the ancient Egyptian despot Osorsennes IV in his quest for eternal life. Legend has it that on the altar, a dying Osorsennes sought to trade the lives of all his people to Morroc for immortality, but Morroc deemed the sacrifices too few for his liking and turned Osorsennes into an immortal monster.",
    ["Dialogue3360509"]="Now, the pharaoh called \"Betrayer of Light\" is imprisoned outside the Dimensional Gap with Morroc, but the altar survived. And that monster <color=#CA2E0AFF>transformed to look like the pharaoh</color> to rule other monsters in the cave. I was thrashed because I was outnumbered...",
    ["Dialogue3360510"]="(Tanders chuckles and level a sword across his chest.)\nWhen I succeeded the title of the Windmill Knight, my father ingrained in me that it was the result of efforts through generations.",
    ["Dialogue3360511"]="Every failure made public is a blemish on the name of Windmill Knight. No one remembers the countless successes, but is only too glad to scrutinize when a Windmill Knight fails. The purpose of successors is simply to<color=#CA2E0AFF>keep the honor of Windmill Knights spotless</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3360512"]="But Master, only gods are without blemish. What we experience is genuinely what mortals would encounter.",
    ["Dialogue3360513"]="I understand what you mean, Sansha, but that's my goal and life's pursuit. Do not worry, I will not let the aspiration bring harm to others.",
    ["Dialogue3360514"]="While waiting for the Adventurer, I've already sent Mainz a letter that explained everything. Even if we perish, Mainz is certain to send assistance, likely posthaste through Kafra's portal. Since the scroll chose you, Adventurer, I shall protect your life to the best of my abilities.",
    ["Dialogue3360515"]="You know everything now. Do you still want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>proceed with the trial</color>, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3360516"]="Consider it carefully. You are still young and still have time. You too, Sansha.",
    ["Dialogue3360517"]="\"I will always follow you\" is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>vow</color> I made when we both became Novices, Master.",
    ["Dialogue3360518"]="Hence, I do not understand what you mean.\n(Sansha takes a step and blocks Tanders' path.)\nI am Sansha, Squire of the Windmill Knight, as I was, as I am in the present.",
    ["Dialogue3360601"]="I know thou, Heir of Odin's Blood...",
    ["Dialogue3360602"]="Thou wish me to resurrect the guardian of humans? Negligence of duty may be overlooked, but what merits his resurrection?",
    ["Dialogue3360603"]="Oh? Thou begging me? Thou deeds are sufficient for me to make an exception, but my powers have waned in the prolonged slumber. If I consent to thou...",
    ["Dialogue3360604"]="Did thou not here to seek power? Thou are willing to trade victory for the lives of two failed fools?",
    ["Dialogue3360605"]="I shall remember thy words today. Heir of the Supreme Deity, may I know why the object is alluded to as Destined Fate?",
    ["Dialogue3360606"]="It is not a scroll, but an oath instead. To gain my approval, one must assert an unbreakable vow, with life as the beginning, death as the end, and this destined fate shall never be abandoned in between.",
    ["Dialogue3360607"]="Thou must vow <color=#CA2E0AFF>to protect Midgard from the beginning to the end, never stray into the path of evil, and never serve Baphomet</color>. If you break the oath, the gods shall punish you. Do you swear?",
    ["Dialogue3360608"]="Promise made, and it shall be kept. Go forth, and I anticipate meeting you again in Valhalla.",
    ["Dialogue3360701"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal Job Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3370101"]="Hey! <size=26>The Adventurer over there! Can you hear me?</size>",
    ["Dialogue3370102"]="Hi there, Adventurer. You seem to be wandering around for a while. Are you in trouble or something? I'm a local hunter living nearby, and quite familiar with the surroundings. Maybe I can help you.",
    ["Dialogue3370103"]="Hmm... I don't see any little girl around... But not long ago, I did hear some heavy footsteps over the woods. At first, I thought it was a bear, so I took my shotgun and went out there to check it out. But there was nothing... Except for some weird footprints, left along the roadside. They were big, definitely not from humans or beasts... Could they be from the robot you are talking about?",
    ["Dialogue3370104"]="The woods are not far from here. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tread along this road down to the north</color>, and you will get there. Good luck, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3370201"]="(There are some unusual traces on the moist soil, looking like footprints but much larger than those of a human. You recall the hunter's words. Maybe these footprints are from Martistine's robot?)",
    ["Dialogue3370301"]="(These giant footprints appear to come from a nearby fence, and those right next to the tent's entrance are even deeper. Whatever this thing is, looks like it stayed there for a while. Considering the ashes of the bonfire are still warm, you are almost certain that someone has taken a break here...)",
    ["Dialogue3370401"]="Hey! Martistine! You are back! Ms. Petra is really mad this time!",
    ["Dialogue3370402"]="Oh! Crap!",
    ["Dialogue3370501"]="(The moment he sees you, Logan covers his ear unconsciously.)\nYou... Stay away! My ears still hurt like hell!",
    ["Dialogue3370502"]="I will... I will tell you everything! I am on the lookout for Martistine!",
    ["Dialogue3370503"]="Yes! She has two giant robots, you know? Hopping onto their shoulders, you can easily climb over this wall... She always gets off the welfare center in this way!",
    ["Dialogue3370504"]="How... How am I supposed to know? I am only a lookout! If I do what I was told, she's gonna bring me something cool when she's back here...\n(Logan looks aggrieved. He doesn't seem to realize the thing they are doing mirrors the \"remunerative relationship,\" which usually exists among adults. If his behavior were not corrected in time, he could turn into an adult just like the director.)",
    ["Dialogue3370505"]="...Yes, I learned that from Martistine. If you blend Algae and Goat's Glands together and heat the mixture, it will produce a smell that lures monsters here... Sometimes, I even think she knows more things than Ms. Petra...",
    ["Dialogue3370506"]="And... Don't keep asking me where she is! I have no idea, I swear! Martistine never tells me where she's going or what she's doing! She assures me that as long as I keep it a secret, she's going to get me tons of good things from the sky... Right. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>look in that direction</color>?\n(Logan raises his hand and points at The City of Sky. This direction is...?)",
    ["Dialogue3370601"]="(Up the hillside towards Juno, a rounded robot is sitting at the roadside. You can vaguely hear a little girl's faint cries coming from nearby.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Boo... I'm so hungry... Mom...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3370602"]="Who are you? How did you recognize me? I-I am already hiding...",
    ["Dialogue3370603"]="Hm... This is the robot Mom left me. The rounded shortie is Farbauti, and the tall and skinny one is Laufey... Mom told me that they would protect me...",
    ["Dialogue3370604"]="I'm not telling you! Did the director send you here to catch me? I am not going back... <size=18>I AM NOT</size>! <size=26>Not to that damned place!</size>\n(Even though you don't see the girl, you can tell by her sobbing tones that she is resisting hard. Maybe now it's best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>console her in another way</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue3370605"]="Hungry... Boo... I am so hungry... I want Mom's specialty dish... In my hometown, the grown-ups would make an oven-baked dish using <color=#CA2E0AFF>Algae</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goat's Glands</color> to celebrate a kid's birthday. It's said that having the dish on the birthday helps the kids grow up strong and healthy...",
    ["Dialogue3370606"]="Yes... Today is my birthday... But Mom will never <color=#CA2E0AFF>make the dish</color> for me again! She doesn't want me anymore! Boo...\n(Martistine starts sobbing again and won't talk to you. It seems that you have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get her the birthday dish</color> to open the lock in her heart.)",
    ["Dialogue3370701"]="...What are you going to do, Adventurer? I gotta warn you, that mixing Algae and Goat's Glands together produces a strange smell, which is irresistible to some monsters. They will follow the smell and swarm over here!",
    ["Dialogue3370702"]="You already knew that? Then why are you...\n(Auntie Cook suddenly turns mute, frowning and glazing at you. She then waves her hand and stops talking.)\n...Looks like I'm being nosy.",
    ["Dialogue3370703"]="Now that you know what these things are capable of, I only have one suggestion for you: Stay away from the kids when you are using them. Don't get them hurt.",
    ["Dialogue3370704"]="Alright, alright. Now, out of my way. I'm going to make a fire. If you have nothing to do, why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>lend me a hand</color>? Just get this over with so I don't have to deal with these awful smells.",
    ["Dialogue3370801"]="OK. Here you go. Don't spill it. I have wrapped this thing with dampened plant ashes. It can seal the smell for now. When you are ready to use it, just unwrap the cloth.\n(Auntie Cook hands you a package-like item.)\n...Don't use it for bad things, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3370802"]="...You want to know the adoption procedure here? Aha... Ever since I started working here, I don't recall anyone being adopted.\n(She snorts sarcastically, pointing at the sky.)\nThose upper-class elites are living in Juno. Why would they want to adopt a kid down here?",
    ["Dialogue3370803"]="Even if there were someone who wants... That greedy old bastard would never let go of such an opportunity of getting rich. He would use the kid as leverage to milk the last drop from them. However... If the kids <color=#CA2E0AFF>run away by themselves</color>, it'll be another story.",
    ["Dialogue3370804"]="(Auntie Cook pauses for a second. You can tell she's insinuating something.)\nThe director just wants this welfare center to be his golden goose forever. As for a few kids coming or leaving here...<color=#CA2E0AFF>He doesn't give a damn about it</color>. So, do you get what I'm saying, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3370901"]="(Upon the desolate hillside, the lone robot is still there. When you approach it, the little girl's voice comes again.)\nYou... The thing you're holding, is it the birthday dish for me?",
    ["Dialogue3370902"]="...Yes. It's been a long time since I had this the last time...",
    ["Dialogue3370903"]="...N-No. How do I know you're not lying to me? Open this up first and hand it to Farbauti... Let me take a look inside.\n(Martistine's wariness has far surpassed other girls at her age. Is it because of the environment, or she never intends to trust you in the first place?)",
    ["Dialogue3370904"]="What are you saying? I don't understand. Come on now... Hand it to Farbauti! Isn't this for my birthday? Or you're just bluffing?",
    ["Dialogue3370905"]="Is this a trap? You... You all are the same! Just trying to get me back there!\n(Martistine's high-pitched voice fills with anger and scorn, making you feel somewhat remorseful. She doesn't trust you, which means <color=#CA2E0AFF>you can hardly solve this in a peaceful way</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue3371001"]="<size=26>I... I didn't ask you to save me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3371002"]="<size=26>Die! To hell with you hypocritical humans! Kill this Adventurer now, Farbauti!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3371101"]="What... What are you doing! Martistine! Follow my order!",
    ["Dialogue3371102"]="Don't be unreasonable, sister. This Adventurer is different than those despicable people in the center. I can feel it. Please believe me.",
    ["Dialogue3371103"]="Greetings, Adventurer. I apologize for my sister's capriciousness.\n(The unruly little girl seems to be a completely different person all of a sudden. She greets you elegantly and has nothing similar to the Martistine who wanted to end your life just now.)\n...Thank you for saving her, even in this situation.",
    ["Dialogue3371104"]="I am Martistine! Dammit! Don't try to stop me! Farbauti— <size=26>Do it now!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3371105"]="<size=26>No, Farbauti.</size>",
    ["Dialogue3371106"]="...Error, command error. Inexecutable. Error, command error. Inexecutable...\n(The rounded robot comes to a halt due to the conflicting commands Martistine gives. As you watch the little girl <color=#CA2E0AFF>talking to herself</color>, some peculiar thoughts emerge in your mind.)",
    ["Dialogue3371107"]="Yes... So what? You also think I'm a psycho, right? I knew it. You... and everyone else... are all the same!\n(Seeing the little girl getting irritated, you are now certain about your assumption. And you suddenly realize this might be the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underlying cause</color> of why Martistine was getting isolated. In this case, all her impulsive and rebellious behaviors make sense now.)",
    ["Dialogue3371108"]="Wha-What's so funny? You all treat me like a fool! Ouch!\n(With her buried secret revealed, Martistine starts running in a fluster. But somehow, she falls heavily to the ground when she turns around.)\nScrew it... Screw it all! Farbauti! Take me away—",
    ["Dialogue3371201"]="...What on earth are you trying to do? I don't get it... Wasn't the director sending you to get me back? Judging from your accent, you are not even from the Republic...\n(At this moment, this girl, who has been quite worked up, seems to give up the idea of running away. She lowers her head, looking apathetic and desperate.)\nYou... Are you trying to sell me to another country?",
    ["Dialogue3371202"]="Hmm... Adventurer is right. You are still a kid, sister.",
    ["Dialogue3371203"]="Calm down, sister. We all know you are constantly starving in the welfare center, and nobody cares about you. You got into fights with other kids; even though you got hurt the worst, they would say you deserved it... So you did bad things on purpose, just to get their attention, but everyone just kept their distance, and no one was willing to talk to you...",
    ["Dialogue3371204"]="(You're now aware that two souls are residing in Martistine's body, yet for some reason, you feel this side of her possesses maturity and wisdom far beyond her age.)\n...Face the reality, sister. Look, the Adventurer just gave you everything you wanted, right?",
    ["Dialogue3371205"]="Everything... for me?\n(She looks at you in a daze and then looks at the wound on her ankle, which has been neatly bandaged.)\nBesides my mom... nobody has ever bound my wounds.",
    ["Dialogue3371206"]="You... The grown-ups are always saying pretty words! You are either trying to sell me... or Farbauti and Laufey! I heard it from the director, with my own ears! There's some kind of logo on Farbauti and Laufey... and thus they can be sold at a good price! More money than he could ever make in his entire life!",
    ["Dialogue3371207"]="(Hearing the name, the girl's eyes light up immediately.)\nYes... Yes! Mom and Dad used to say this name a lot. <color=#A1979FFF>Perhaps, perhaps...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3371208"]="Pinky swear...? You want to help me look for my mom and dad?\n(Martistine stares at you in confusion, as if she doesn't understand your words.)\nBut... Didn't the director ask you to bring me back to the welfare center?",
    ["Dialogue3371209"]="Huh... Eh? What? What are you doing? Put me down! Hey—\n(As Martistine's foot got injured, you quickly scoop her up. This teenage girl is thin and fragile, like a puff of cloud in your arms...)",
    ["Dialogue3371301"]="Why are you taking me to Juno? Let me tell you, kids like me were dumped at the welfare center. We don't get to live here!",
    ["Dialogue3371302"]="You applied for a temporary residence permit in Juno and rented this house? Hah...\n(Martistine chuckles. Along the way back to Juno, she has given up the idea of running away but still remains wary of you.)\nBut what does that have to do with me?",
    ["Dialogue3371303"]="You... You are kidding! I don't need it! Families, friends, partners... I need none of that! Farbauti and Laufey are just enough!\n(She turns around in a fit of pique, hugging Farbauti's big, metal belly.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Eventually... Eventually, you will leave this place... This is not your hometown...</color>",
    ["Dialogue3371304"]="Then... Then I don't need it! If I'm still all alone in the end, it's better not to encounter anyone in the first place!\n(The girl buries her head into the robot's arms, from where her voice sounds muffled and hollow. You couldn't imagine how many lonely nights she had been through that she developed such a drastic yet indifferent mindset.)",
    ["Dialogue3371305"]="And... I am not lonely at all... Farbauti and Laufey are my family... They will never leave me...",
    ["Dialogue3371306"]="...Then what does it take to be a real family?\n(Martistine turns around and stares at you with hostility. Her eyes are reddened, looking like a fierce little beast.)",
    ["Dialogue3371307"]="Mom and Dad said we were family, but they dumped me and left me all alone! The director and the teacher said we were family, but they didn't care about me at all! And you! What kind of home are you going to get me?",
    ["Dialogue3371308"]="Huh, huh...? A place where I can return anytime... That's home? No matter how heartbroken I feel out there, you will make my favorite dishes, waiting for me at home?",
    ["Dialogue3371309"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Boo... I don't believe it... You and everyone else are all sweet talkers... liars...</color>\n(This little girl remains skeptical of your words. She keeps mumbling about you being a liar, avoiding contact with you. You know she won't open her heart to you easily. But it's fine because...)",
    ["Dialogue3380101"]="Also, the military's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color> is based on the island, offering <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gunslinger</color> training to novices. His stern military methods often spark debates in the academy, so if you opt for his guidance, be sure to maintain a strong posture and a loud voice.",
    ["Dialogue3380201"]="A coward has no way to become a Gunslinger. You! Stand firm and hold your head high!",
    ["Dialogue3380202"]="Bah, typical recruit! Now listen, as a Gunslinger, you need to train your eyes eagle-sharp. Only by this can you toast your enemies before they aim. Got it?",
    ["Dialogue3380203"]="Louder!",
    ["Dialogue3380204"]="(Instructor Miller casually cleaned his ears)\nThat's the spirit. Gunslinger training is military-organized, which means you either quit or graduate. Even if exhaustion has you crying out for help, there's no way to turn to your dean or instructor. It's a tough experience akin to Niflheim's torments, so brace yourself for shedding a layer of skin!",
    ["Dialogue3380205"]="That said, you'll acquire knowledge that college professors couldn't possibly cram into your head for their lifetime. You'll learn to identify various gun parts, assemble them into lethal weapons, send each bullet precisely into the enemy's heart, and overcome the tears and trembles that come with killing. It will transform you in every shape and form.",
    ["Dialogue3380206"]="To put it simply, before facing the enemy, it is crucial to <color=#CA2E0AFF>confront and conquer your personal demons of fear, sloth, and inadequacy</color>. Understand?",
    ["Dialogue3380207"]="Excellent! Now, to start the Job Advancement Ceremony, you can go talk to your dean. Once your <color=#CA2E0AFF>job level reaches 49</color>, you may approach me to request enrollment in the Job Advancement training program for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rebellion</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3390101"]="Every Gunslinger who has undergone military training exudes a distinct aura, setting them apart from academy graduates. The scent of gunpowder, the hardened hands, and the piercing gaze all indicate that the former student has transformed beyond their novice self.",
    ["Dialogue3390102"]="I am delighted, young Adventurer. You can shine brightly beyond the confines of the academy. To tell you the truth, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color> holds you in high regard and has approved your enrollment in the professional training for Rebellion.",
    ["Dialogue3390103"]="At the moment we're speaking right now, he is on the way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>, where you will learn how to become a Rebellion.",
    ["Dialogue3400101"]="Ah, you've arrived right on time. Your presence indicates that you have made a resolute choice to accept the professional training for Rebellion.",
    ["Dialogue3400102"]="Military Gunslinger training is results-driven. Put simply, your ability to shoot with precision, speed, and capacity to complete assigned tasks from the instructor will determine your success.",
    ["Dialogue3400103"]="Obedience is the first duty of a soldier. However, the next phase for a Gunslinger is known as \"Rebellion.\" This name originates from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Night of Gunfire</color> 700 years ago. Ever since, aspiring Rebellions have <color=#CA2E0AFF>sought this abbey to follow in their ancestors' footsteps</color>, and your mission is no exception.",
    ["Dialogue3400104"]="Assuming you're well-versed in history, you should recognize the name of King Schmidt I. He was the inaugural and only ruler of Glast Heim, who reigned over the wealthiest lands, espoused the most beautiful queen, commanded the most formidable troops, and above all, harbored the most ruthless ambition.",
    ["Dialogue3400105"]="(Instructor Miller's gaze fixes upon the fragmented dome of the abbey.) \n700 years ago, fifteen courageous warriors assembled at this very place, vowing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>slay the savage King Schmidt</color> and bring an end to the dynasty's tyranny.",
    ["Dialogue3400106"]="Among them, some witnessed their siblings being captured, compelled to construct a palace, and perishing by the date of completion. Some lost their wives to monstrous officials. And some whose parents were forced to surrender their lands, leaving families to struggle in shabby dwellings. Moreover, some affluent and skilled Gunslingers joined the ranks, choosing to defy King Schmidt's commands.",
    ["Dialogue3400107"]="In the nighttime abbey, they pledged vows that echo to this day:",
    ["Dialogue3400201"]="Having pledged their vow, they stealthily navigated into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Sewer</color> system. Tracing the water pipes' path and ascending the largest, they could access the palace's underbelly. Masquerading as sewage workers—regarded as barely more significant than palace slaves—they split into three squads to infiltrate the palace inconspicuously.",
    ["Dialogue3400202"]="To purge impurities, one must risk corruption. Gunslinger soon to bear the label of a \"Rebellion\", are you ready for what lies ahead?",
    ["Dialogue3400301"]="(Instructor Miller shoots you a look, steps forward, and flicks some dust off your shoulder.) \nMost new recruits would ask for a delay or beat a quick retreat hearing the sewer stuff. But you, you're a different breed. Good job.",
    ["Dialogue3400302"]="The operational map, procured through bribes by the Gunslingers' leader, didn't feature this door. Perhaps the provider hid its existence intentionally, or perhaps they were simply unaware of this doorway.",
    ["Dialogue3400303"]="(Glancing sideways, you spot the entrance to Glast Heim Prison.)\nKing Schmidt, convinced that criminals didn't merit sunlight or the right to dwell among his subjects, demanded the construction of an underground prison. In a twist of irony, the craftspeople became its first prisoners, and the location's knowledge was buried with them. The rebels' operation, though unintended, broke this long-standing taboo.",
    ["Dialogue3400304"]="Every job changer entering Glast Heim Prison has a tradition: <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather a bunch of Soulsoothing Grass to honor the restless souls</color>. I'll wait for you further ahead.",
    ["Dialogue3400401"]="All burned?",
    ["Dialogue3400402"]="And so, then the story goes on. A covert warrior, armed with a dagger and smoke bombs for clandestine assassinations, slipped into the prison. His mission was to procure valuable intelligence for his comrades.",
    ["Dialogue3400403"]="Originally, the plan was to quietly apprehend a prison guard and coerce him into revealing the prison's layout. Yet, as the brave warrior infiltrated the prison, he discovered an eerie absence of guards. Or more accurately, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the guards weren't human at all</color>, but dwellers of the dark sewers, wandering about even to this day.",
    ["Dialogue3400404"]="Indeed, they resemble elderly, diminutive humans, but being magical creatures, they favor places like schools and mage towers. Yet, why would King Schmidt, who proclaimed himself of noble blood, hire such mystical beings as prison guards? And what could possibly compel the cleanliness-loving, light-seeking Sageworms to dwell in the sewers?",
    ["Dialogue3400405"]="Upon rejoining his comrades, the warrior shared his puzzling observations but found no answers. Luckily, the prison's darkness rendered the Sageworms sluggish, like sightless, elderly scholars. After subduing a few, the rebels managed to gather some crudely scrawled map pieces, akin to children's sketches.",
    ["Dialogue3400406"]="At this juncture, abortion was no longer an option. Clutching the incomplete map, the warriors resolved to improvise. As they braced for battle, the prison gates surprisingly swung open.",
    ["Dialogue3400407"]="Beyond the door, two lines of silent Sageworms faced the warriors. Following a tense standoff, a white-haired <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sageworm</color> emerged from the crowd, whose cloudy eyes were shimmering red, but surprisingly spoke with the tone of a human woman.",
    ["Dialogue3400408"]="This being, or \"she,\" extended an invitation to the warriors, beckoning them deeper into the prison, towards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Churchyard</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3400501"]="Arriving here demonstrates your worthiness to be a Rebellion. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>after reaching job level 50</color>, you can return to the academy for the subsequent combat trial.",
    ["Dialogue3400502"]="Here, the warriors found strength a hundredfold that of the \"Rebellion\" and marched towards their destined end. But for you, the conclusion is yet distant. When you're ready to become a Predator, Adventurer, return here and seek me out.",
    ["Dialogue3400503"]="I'll guide you back 700 years and unveil the hidden mysteries of the Predators to you.",
    ["Dialogue3410101"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Gunslinger.",
    ["Dialogue3410102"]="Criatura Academy has nothing more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your talent and resolve beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task before graduating.",
    ["Dialogue3410103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>. You don't need it anymore. I'll give you a new Class Manual, which doubles as the diploma, at the graduation ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3410201"]="So, are you ready for the graduation ceremony?",
    ["Dialogue3420101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and measures you up and down with a smile.)\nHow have you grown over the last few days! It seems you are ready for some guidance on Job Advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3420102"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, and this proves you do have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused as to how to use your powers, right?",
    ["Dialogue3420103"]="That's the right attitude. Now, it's time for you to take the pursuit of knowledge to <color=#CA2E0AFF>your Class Master</color>. They will familiarize you with the new class and combat skills. And maybe... a surprise or two as well, heh!",
    ["Dialogue3420104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I await good news from you. I hope the next time we meet... it's to witness your rebirth under Odin's statue.",
    ["Dialogue3420201"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dimensional Gap</color> ahead leads to the Glast Heim Churchyard of 700 years ago, as well as the ultimate conclusion of the \"Night of Gunfire.\" To ascend as a Predator, you must find \"her\" and accept \"her\" plea.",
    ["Dialogue3420202"]="(Instructor Miller shook his head.)\n\"Her\" identity is a secret closely guarded by the military. A word of caution - even if you have clues, keep them to yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3420203"]="Also, if you'd rather avoid a spot on the wanted list, refrain from disclosing all about this future, 700 years ahead, to \"her.\" Your task is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill her request, gain power, and return safely</color>. Clear?",
    ["Dialogue3420301"]="(The purple-haired girl in a black dress regards you icily. For reasons unknown, she conjures an image in your mind of the goddess enshrined in the Heart Pedestal.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue3420302"]="(Before your words flow, the girl's icy fingers have brushed your forehead.)\nA mere mortal, not even a Predator. Do you aspire to mimic your fallen comrades and assassinate the king? King Schmidt has already instigated a <color=#CA2E0AFF>great purge</color> in the city. As we speak, your comrades' bodies are hanging from the city walls.",
    ["Dialogue3420303"]="... Leave. I will no longer bestow my power upon you.",
    ["Dialogue3420304"]="If you don't leave now, you may cross paths with King Schmidt and his forces, eh? Tsk, perhaps I should turn you in, then I won't need to fabricate a tale to justify the origin of your comrades' power.",
    ["Dialogue3420305"]="Well... How would a captive not know her jailer? The entire palace, the whole dynasty, is his jail. It's only due to my appealing appearance and usable power that I stand here, lending an ear to your righteous pledge.",
    ["Dialogue3420306"]="Or, have you cast aside humanity's feeble concept of justice, simply coming here in the pursuit of power?",
    ["Dialogue3420307"]="Ha...haha... \n(The girl's laughter resonates with a pompous tone.)\nYou humans, why? Why do you always echo the same sentiments?",
    ["Dialogue3420308"]="Do you truly comprehend from whom you seek strength? Allow me to reveal a secret concealed even from your predecessors. The reason I exist here is solely due to the subjects delivered by that very king! Tomorrow, the day after, or perchance at the precipice of demise, you too shall become one of them.",
    ["Dialogue3420309"]="Your unwavering commitment to justice is admirable, but are you willing to let it be tainted? Retreat now, for I have drained enough lifeforce today and hold no interest in you.",
    ["Dialogue3420310"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>To purge impurities, one must risk corruption</color>...\n(The girl mutters your words and draws closer.)\nVery well, then. Let us strike a vile bargain.",
    ["Dialogue3420311"]="(The girl smiles, pointing to her own chest.) \nEnd my life. If you encounter <color=#CA2E0AFF>someone bearing a resemblance to me</color>, eliminate her without hesitation.",
    ["Dialogue3420312"]="(Enormous black wings unfurl, enshrouding you all within their grasp. Enveloped in a mesmerizing trance, you feel something merging within your body.)\nAs a greeting gift, the demon has bestowed upon you half of its malevolence. Before you strike me down, I shall remain here, siphoning the lifeforce of the innocent. Now, will you dethrone the king from his lofty seat first, or shall I drain his subjects to the last drop?",
    ["Dialogue3420313"]="Ha...haha... People slay the king, the king defies the gods, and the gods massacre the people. Oh, human, I eagerly anticipate our next encounter...",
    ["Dialogue3420401"]="It appears that you have fulfilled your mission.\n(Instructor Miller pats you on the shoulder.)\nErase from your mind all that has transpired<color=#CA2E0AFF> and proceed to your intended destination</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3420501"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal Job Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3440103"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Akahyo</color> is the current instructor for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ninja Class</color>. He's part of \"Hidden Spirits,\" a group that isn't allied with anyone. He took this position all because of a deal he made with the previous dean. Hah! I have to remind you that Ninja's training is even more controversial than Gunslinger's. Some believe it's nothing but physical and mental torture that wrecks your body and mind and does absolutely nothing to your strength. Adventurer, I respect your decision, but I still don't want my students to suffer that much. Hah!",
    ["Dialogue3440201"]="Too weak.",
    ["Dialogue3440202"]="Weak bodies and weak looks. Even as a Ninja, you won't survive to see the dawn the next morning.",
    ["Dialogue3440203"]="Getting mad for no good reason is a sign of weakness. Be thankful you're not the prey.",
    ["Dialogue3440204"]="Consider this: the advancement of Ninjas is not a test but a trial of your life. You don't make it out alive if you fail. If you're up for that... Do everything to keep yourself alive until you reach <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level 49</color>. Come see me when you get there.",
    ["Dialogue3450101"]="(Dean Mainz kindly pats your head.)\n Becoming a Ninja is not an easy task, Adventurer. If you stick to this path, you'll be up against more challenges than other classes.",
    ["Dialogue3450102"]="(Mainz nods and starts telling you about the origins of Ninjas.)\n In the Rune Kingdom, out of all classes, Ninjas are the only ones not from around here; they originated from way off in some distant land. They stick to strict rules and disciplines that most people can't even understand, constantly training their bodies and minds to peak their skill levels. In order to achieve this, there's a brutally tough selection process among Ninjas. And here is the most infamous one — \"Only the strongest among us deserve to survive.\"",
    ["Dialogue3450103"]="The art of Ninja is split into three: Wind, Water, and Fire. There's a death match every five years, and the outcome of the loser is at the mercy of the winner. Your master, Akahyo, was the winner of the last death match. His Fire Ninjutsu is top-notch. He knocked out the Wind and Water Clans in one go and seized the Ninjutsu Scroll from each of them. That's why you're able to practice Fuuton and Suiton during the first class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3450104"]="I bet he's aiming to pick and train the best one for the next death match, keeping the advantage of his clan. Adventurer, you're a student at Criatura Academy, no less talented than anyone else. Winning should be a breeze for you, but here, just stay low ley and focus on your class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3450105"]="Shh... I think you get what I mean. Go on, Master <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akahyo</color> is expecting you at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon Munak Cave 1F</color>. By the way, inside the Munak Cave, there's this underground river called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forgotten Lake</color>. Ninja believe it's a sacred river that connects life and death. They sink the bodies of those who lose into it as offerings, and that's where your Class Advancement Trial takes place. Sigh... Adventurer, it's not too late to back out now.",
    ["Dialogue3460101"]="(Inside the Munak Cave, two Ninjas stand beside Akahyo. A male Ninja is holding his sword silently while a female Ninja checks you out curiously.)\n The last one.",
    ["Dialogue3460102"]="By the rules, there's only <color=#CA2E0AFF>one winner</color> in this trial. It's time for you to find out who you're up against. Souzo, better conceal your murderous aura.",
    ["Dialogue3460103"]="Humph!\n (A Ninja named Souzo sheathes his sword, and that's when you notice his thumb has been pressed against the mouth of the sheath the whole time.)\n Akahyo, one day, I will have this sword up against your throat. The shame of our clan shall be washed away with your blood!",
    ["Dialogue3460104"]="(The next second, when the Ninja Sword hits the ground, Souzo is sent flying. Those lingering marks of fingers are gripping his throat.)\n Keep your heart still and your soul moving. Cut through all things when the wind ceases — this is Iaijutsu. Looks like you're no better than your teacher was a decade ago.",
    ["Dialogue3460105"]="You are in no position to talk about the skill!\n (Souzo, with a grim look, coughs heavily and then spits out a bloody tooth.)\n I'm not turning into him.",
    ["Dialogue3460106"]="(Akahyo looks at the other side indifferently.)\n What about you?",
    ["Dialogue3460107"]="(Ohka keeps backing off after a brief moment, then helps Souzo up.)\n I... the Water Clan has no intention to challenge your authority. Akahyo, I just wanted to help him up.",
    ["Dialogue3460108"]="(As if to prove her points, Ohka reaches out her hand to you.)\n You... Are you Akahyo's student? I'm Ohka, a Ninja of the Water Clan. I'll be joining this Class Advancement Trial with you.",
    ["Dialogue3460109"]="(Ohka holds your hand and gives it a couple of excited shakes.) So, I heard you've mastered Fuuton and Suiton? This is amazing!",
    ["Dialogue3460110"]="(Ohka pulls her hand back slowly.)\n Anyway, I'm looking forward!",
    ["Dialogue3460111"]="(Akahyo glances at you all, then leaps up to the cliff.)\n <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defeat these Skeletons</color> and be the first winner to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach the Forgotten Lake Waterfall</color>. Also, you must toss the relics from these Skeletons into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forgotten Lake Waterfall</color>. If any of you end up as corpses... The Forgotten Lake is still the final resting place.",
    ["Dialogue3460112"]="Since ancient times, the resting place of every Ninja, the abyss beneath your feet, and the distant waterfall have all been the Forgotten Lake. Any more questions?",
    ["Dialogue3460113"]="Excuse me... Akahyo?",
    ["Dialogue3460114"]="...",
    ["Dialogue3460115"]="(Ohka's eyes sparkle when she hears a reply.)\n The teacher mentioned there's this formal oath ceremony before the trial to become Kagerou and Oboro?",
    ["Dialogue3460116"]="...",
    ["Dialogue3460117"]="... Uh, for Akahyo, an oath isn't exactly necessary.\n (After a moment of silence, Ohka scratches her head.)\n ...Sorry, Akahyo!",
    ["Dialogue3460118"]="I don't believe in them.\n (Akahyo gives no clear response.)\n And it's not fair if an oath is kept by just one side.",
    ["Dialogue3460119"]="We are different from you, Akahyo.\n (Souzo wipes the blood from his mouth and stands up, leaning on Ohka.)\n Our teacher told me that you've broken your oath, and that's why you despise making oaths.",
    ["Dialogue3460120"]="(A shuriken whizzes by Souzo's ear and hits the wall.)\n Next time, it will be pinned in the dojo of the Wind Clan.",
    ["Dialogue3460121"]="(Akahyo's figure slowly blends into the darkness, leaving only his whisper in the air.)\n You, my student, it's up to you to follow or not. The winner gets the privilege of not being bound by oath.",
    ["Dialogue3460201"]="You wanna win, right? In this case, wanna team up?",
    ["Dialogue3460202"]="Of course! But... Not right now.",
    ["Dialogue3460203"]="Souzo and I aren't aiming for the Forgotten Lake over the bridge but for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Universe Stone Formation</color>. The monsters on that path are tough, even for us. So, we need a temporary partner.",
    ["Dialogue3460204"]="Ohka, you're telling this guy too much.",
    ["Dialogue3460205"]="We're just a bunch of rookie Ninjas. Anyway, as temporary partners, we'll help him get to the Forgotten Lake and win the trial. Meanwhile, he needs to give it his all and blaze a trail with us too. Should we bite the dust on the way to the Forgotten Lake, he can step over our dead bodies and keep going. If he gets seriously injured or dies near the Universe Stone Formation, we can just leave him in the Munak Cave.",
    ["Dialogue3460206"]="Once we hit our goal, we'll go our separate ways. How does that sound? Are you in?",
    ["Dialogue3460207"]="It's a secret! Take it easy; our action has nothing to do with your victory, and there's nothing we're hiding from you.\n (Ohka takes a quick look around and gives you a mysterious smile.)\n In fact, Akahyo is <color=#CA2E0AFF>monitoring</color> everything we do.",
    ["Dialogue3460208"]="(Ohka pulls out her weapon regretfully.)\n As Ninja, we should steer clear of any pointless fights and win every battle we're in. Adventurer, do you see the howling Forgotten Lake below you? With your triple mastery of Wind, Water, and Fire, you can't defeat me or Souzo, who only specialized in one mastery. No matter the outcome, no one gets to complete their quest.",
    ["Dialogue3460209"]="Pleasure working with you!\n (Ohka quickly runs behind Souzo, tugging at his shirt.)\n Stop looking so mean! This is our new partner!",
    ["Dialogue3460301"]="It's definitely the monster from the Class Advancement Trial. Seriously... for real... it's gonna take some effort...",
    ["Dialogue3460302"]="... N-Nothing... Just don't forget what you promised... Hey, stop playing tough; you look pale as a ghost...",
    ["Dialogue3460303"]="I was born with it.",
    ["Dialogue3460304"]="... Pfft.\n (Ohka gets up and brushes the dirt off her clothes.)\n Can't give up now, Adventurer. Watch my back!",
    ["Dialogue3460401"]="We're here.",
    ["Dialogue3460402"]="A deeper, more dangerous place. I bet only those who reach the third class can go in and out freely.\n (Ohka pulls out a scroll and hands it to you.)\n Here you go. Toss it into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forgotten Lake</color>, so that completes the trial!",
    ["Dialogue3460403"]="Hey, don't give me that look. We're not enemies now, but one day, we'll eventually fight each other over different standpoints. Adventurer, you should know better if you are really Akahyo's student.",
    ["Dialogue3460404"]="Are you saying you were a student at Criatura Academy? You... You've decided to become a Ninja?\n (Ohka widens her eyes, mumbling to herself.)\n This guy could be even crazier than us... What else do you know about Ninjas?",
    ["Dialogue3460405"]="...\n (Ohka facepalms and points at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>scroll</color> in your hand.)\n Hope it fills the knowledge gap of your skills. Souzo, let's go.",
    ["Dialogue3460501"]="You won.\n (Akahyo's tone doesn't sound approving, but this is the first time he looks you in the eyes.)\n The Job Advancement begins when the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level reaches 50</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3460502"]="Or you are seeking certain answers.",
    ["Dialogue3460503"]="(Akahyo turns around, looking at the scroll you tossed down that's yet to sink.)\n No one made it out alive during that trial. Consider yourself lucky that the relics weren't laced with poison. Obviously, I'm not talking about the relic owner but your temporary partner who escorted you to the Universe Stone Formation. When Ohka hands you the scroll, you reach out to it with a dumb look on your face.",
    ["Dialogue3460504"]="\"The corpses of the fallen ones calm Forgotten Lake's cravings, and their wails ease its anger. After it devours all that's left of them, it gives them another chance, a chance to wash away their shame, but in a way that's not exactly what you called \"living.\" <color=#CA2E0AFF>Because the Forgotten Lake is the everlasting sacred river that runs between life and death. </color>\"",
    ["Dialogue3460505"]="Legend has it that in the era before the Ninjas split their ways, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>First Ninja</color>, hunted by enemies, took a sip of the water from the Forgotten Lake when he almost gave in. Soon after, he was <color=#CA2E0AFF>reborn</color>. Ever since, he treated the Forgotten Lake as both parent and deity, expecting his descendants to do the same.",
    ["Dialogue3460506"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>I'm not a good son nor a devout follower.</color>.\n (Akahyo heads deeper into the Munak Cave.)",
    ["Dialogue3460507"]="Same as your temporary partner. Huh, so the Wind and Water Clans are now relying on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>souls of the defeated ones</color> to win?",
    ["Dialogue3470101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and measures you up and down with a smile.)\n How have you grown over the last few days! It seems you are ready for some guidance on Job Advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3470102"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, and this proves you do have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused as to how to use your powers, right?",
    ["Dialogue3470103"]="That's more like it. Now, it's time for you to take the pursuit of knowledge to <color=#CA2E0AFF>your Class Master</color>. They will familiarize you with the new class and combat skills. And maybe a surprise or two as well, heh!",
    ["Dialogue3470104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I await good news from you. I hope the next time we meet... it's to witness your rebirth under Odin's statue.",
    ["Dialogue3470201"]="(Akahyo, leaning against the wall like usual, seems a bit more worn out.)\n For some reason, you can proceed directly from Universe Stone Formation to Land of Trials.",
    ["Dialogue3470202"]="... I just want to fight those who aim for the shortcut. Listen up, I won't be with you in this trial. Once you're in Pale Spirit Town, do whatever it takes to stay alive, even if it means crawling out in pieces without arms and legs.",
    ["Dialogue3470203"]="Plus, since you escorted Ohka and Souzo during the second-class advancement, they have a much better idea about the terrain layout than you... In the third-class trial, the winner and loser can't be alive at the same time. You should know the rules by now.",
    ["Dialogue3470204"]="This is the quest assigned to this little guy by those old bags of bones who are trying to cut the corner.\n (Akahyo falls silent for a second.)\n Twelve years ago, right here during the third-class advancement, I ended my deepest bond and sank my <color=#CA2E0AFF>best friend</color> to the bottom of the Forgotten Lake...",
    ["Dialogue3470205"]="From Ninja to Yata, we share our <color=#CA2E0AFF>weaknesses</color> and swear never to harm each other. Even with weapons drawn, we must fight each other fair and square. But I... betrayed that oath. Water Clan... If his spirit has been summoned by his clan members, he would probably come after me...",
    ["Dialogue3470206"]="You are a lucky one. Your bond shouldn't be a reason preventing you from drawing the sword. As for Souzo and Ohka... Ha, someone's going to repeat the history no matter who lives or dies.",
    ["Dialogue3470207"]="(A flash of confusing emotion crosses Akahyo's eyes.)\n You're not at liberty to choose how to win just yet. However, you can choose to give up.",
    ["Dialogue3470301"]="I knew you'd show up here. This is Akahyo's student. What do you think? Pretty different from Akahyo, huh?",
    ["Dialogue3470302"]="Indeed.\n (A warm male voice echoes from the Horong.)\n There is no raging hostility, not even fully drawing the weapon; having a student like this somehow changes Akahyo over time.",
    ["Dialogue3470303"]="Indeed, but only one of us gets to live today. Why are you still hesitating to tell us? You know, I'm closely related to you.",
    ["Dialogue3470304"]="No.\n (The Horong's voice is gentle but firm.)\n Once an oath is made, there's no turning back.",
    ["Dialogue3470305"]="But he broke the oath, killed you with the weak points you told him, and dumped you into the Forgotten Lake, turning you into Susa. Why don't you tell us about his weak point so we can avenge you?",
    ["Dialogue3470306"]="(A soft sigh lingers in the empty Pale Spirit Town.)\n <color=#CA2E0AFF>I didn't die full of hatred and resentment.</color>",
    ["Dialogue3470401"]="Nagi... I didn't expect to see you again this way. Why did you...?",
    ["Dialogue3470402"]="Do I have to speak it out?\n (The voice in Horong goes silent, then chuckles.)\n Well, if I must, maybe your look was more upset than me at that moment.",
    ["Dialogue3470403"]="The ruthless killer suddenly becomes a kid crying over a stolen lollypop. I was out cold before I could even get mad. Hah, maybe your weapon is too sharp.",
    ["Dialogue3470404"]="You know, if you were still all poker-faced back then, I might've just revealed all your weak points now. Akahyo, I've heard a lot about you from them. But there's one thing that I need to get a straight answer from you.",
    ["Dialogue3470405"]="I'm listening.",
    ["Dialogue3470406"]="Have you realized what's <color=#CA2E0AFF>causing all this sorrow</color> and started doing something about it?",
    ["Dialogue3470407"]="Of course!\n (Akahyo is about to speak, then notice the three of you in the trial.)\n It's hard... I need much more time...",
    ["Dialogue3470408"]="It's okay. If there's anyone who can put an end to this, I bet it's you. Since the trial can be stopped, you three...",
    ["Dialogue3470409"]="I'll change everything... I will... do everything I could... to <color=#CA2E0AFF>turn things around</color>... So can you!",
    ["Dialogue3470410"]="(Akahyo lowers his head.)\n But now...",
    ["Dialogue3470411"]="Eventually... the day will come. Akahyo, you don't want us to determine the winner through a life-and-death battle, correct? You hate bloodshed, so you didn't take out anyone from the Wind or Water Clans after winning. And by taking the tomes, you want to maintain your winning streak and prevent people from dying, even though we're all about \"killing each other.\"",
    ["Dialogue3470412"]="Are you looking for peace?\n (Souzo looks at Akahyo in disbelief.)\n Are you going to <color=#CA2E0AFF>break our rules</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3470413"]="Blood debts, the shame of defeats, our master's death... Akahyo, do you even have a slight idea of what you're doing? And you, out of all people...",
    ["Dialogue3470414"]="He's right, Akahyo. The hatred between the three clans is going to snowball over time. What you're trying to stop is a part of <color=#CA2E0AFF>inevitable history</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3470415"]="(Ohka shuts her eyes; after a brief moment, she opens her eyes and smiles at Souzo with all her emotions concealed.)\n It's down to one of us surviving.",
    ["Dialogue3470416"]="There's no way I'll fight you.",
    ["Dialogue3470417"]="Heh, so Adventurer, don't feel guilty.\n (Ohka pulls out her weapon.)\n Now, you are up against <color=#CA2E0AFF>two enemies</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3470501"]="Nagi follows Ohka as she's leaving. Now, you will become one of the Susa Tsukuyomi. As for the others... I'll let their clans know the trial results. Forgotten Lake... is about to get more souls.",
    ["Dialogue3470502"]="...",
    ["Dialogue3470503"]="This is a Ninja thing, Adventurer. Aren't you a student at Criatura Academy?\n (Akahyo changes his tone all of a sudden.)",
    ["Dialogue3470504"]="You...\n (Akahyo is stunned for a moment before he finally says something vague.)",
    ["Dialogue3470505"]="\"The corpses of the fallen ones calm Forgotten Lake's cravings, and their wails ease its anger. After it devours all that's left of them, it gives them another chance, a chance to wash away their shame, but in a way that's not exactly what you called \"living.\" Because the Forgotten Lake is the everlasting sacred river that runs between life and death. \"",
    ["Dialogue3470506"]="Here's something crazy: the Forgotten Lake can flow <color=#CA2E0AFF>backward</color>; even life and death are <color=#CA2E0AFF>reversable</color> under its command.",
    ["Dialogue3470507"]="You're not ready to handle the truth.\n (Akahyo gives your shoulder an awkward pat...)\n ... If you really want to do something, then aim <color=#CA2E0AFF>beyond the third class</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3470508"]="By then, I won't be your mentor but your opponent.",
    ["Dialogue3470601"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal Job Advancement Ceremony.\n It's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3480101"]="Heh, it's been a while. I see you are now a certifiable Adventurer! I still remember vividly when you became a Ninja.",
    ["Dialogue3490104"]="On top of that, there's a class called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Taekwon</color> where folks grind hard to toughen up themselves. When they get good, they don't need any real weapons or spells. Their superior kicking skills and bodies that are tough as steel are their best tricks for winning. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mr. Phoenix</color> is a big deal in Taekwon, and he's here on the island looking for students. I bet he can teach you a lot!",
    ["Dialogue3490201"]="Huh? You must be the novice around here. If you have any questions about Taekwon, feel free to ask me! It's really important to have someone to light the way in the world of martial arts!",
    ["Dialogue3490202"]="No training comes without \"hardship,\" Taekwon's the same deal! But hey, how can you tell if you haven't given it a shot? Kid, if you're ready to become one of us, I'd gladly be your master!",
    ["Dialogue3490203"]="Hang in there and keep training hard! We'll meet again when your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level reaches 49</color>. But until then, you've got to tread that path by yourself!",
    ["Dialogue3500101"]="Whoa, look at those muscles; you've changed quite a lot! If I, an old geezer, had those kinds of muscles, the title of \"The Most Popular Academy Instructor\" might not necessarily go to Yadrew this year! Adventurer, you're now ready to seek out Mr. Phoenix for your second-class advancement; he's hanging out in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3500102"]="(The Dean winks and gives you a big thumbs up)\nGo on; the serious grinding starts now. Wish you all the best!",
    ["Dialogue3510101"]="I'm expecting you! Seeing the determination in your eyes at the beginning told me we'd cross paths again!\n(Phoenix reaches out his fist)\nIt's a Taekwon gesture! Come on now! Show me your strength with your fist!",
    ["Dialogue3510102"]="Hmm! With power like that, you're up for my Star Gladiator Class Advancement Trial! But before that, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer my questions</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3510103"]="Being a Star Gladiator means you've moved beyond the initial stage and are now a true martial artist.\n(Phoenix points at your heart)\nIn all your training, did you ever forget about this? Did you reflect on what made you step on this path?",
    ["Dialogue3510104"]="To get stronger? To defeat all your enemies, to use power to conquer all? Or... for justice? Now, question your heart, establish your original intent, and never turn away from it!",
    ["Dialogue3510201"]="Keep your vow in mind, Adventurer. On the journey of martial arts, it's the ones who remain loyal to their first intent who advance the farthest. To become a Star Gladiator, you first need to understand \"The Way of Slow.\"",
    ["Dialogue3510202"]="(Phoenix kneels down, strapping bags of rocks to your arms and legs)\nHow do you feel now?",
    ["Dialogue3510203"]="It's supposed to feel heavy. From the way you threw that punch, you've got more training to do. Quick, careless moves will expose your weak spots. It's a fatal flaw when neither your strength nor speed are up to the Star Gladiator standards.",
    ["Dialogue3510204"]="To deal with impatience, you've gotta start by slowing down and taking it from the top. Practice with extra weight until you're getting used to them, then slowly return to where you were without rushing.",
    ["Dialogue3510205"]="(Phoenix weights the rocks in his hand)\nThis... should be enough to deal with the sluggish <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golem</color> in the desert. Smash them and bring me the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stone Heart</color> as proof.",
    ["Dialogue3510301"]="Impressive progress!\n(Phoenix unties the rocks from you)\nDo you feel much lighter now?",
    ["Dialogue3510302"]="Remember this feeling. Next, we're diving into \"The Way of Speed.\" Have you ever caught an Anacondaq hunting in a flash? Dealing a fatal blow at a speed that's hard to catch with the naked eye. I want you to learn the strength of speed by going after Anacondaq. Get its Venomous Fang for me, and you'll pass the trial!",
    ["Dialogue3510401"]="Consider the loot a badge of honor. Congrats! I've got another student ready to become a Star Gladiator! Adventurer, when your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level hits 50</color>, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Trial</color> at Prontera Cathedral will be available for you!",
    ["Dialogue3510402"]="Apply what you've learned over time to your Class Advancement Trial. \"The Way of Slow/Speed\" is merely the starting point, and only with countless practice can you advance on the path of the Star Gladiator. Hope you keep at it. Go forth, my proud student!",
    ["Dialogue3520101"]="Heh, it's been a while. I see you are now a certifiable Adventurer! I still remember vividly when you became a Taekwon.",
    ["Dialogue3530101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and sizes you up and down with a smile.)\nHow have you grown over the last few days! It seems you are ready for some guidance on the Class Advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3530102"]="As I said before, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, and this proves you do have the power to shape the future. However, you are probably still somewhat confused as to how to use your powers, right?",
    ["Dialogue3530103"]="That's the right attitude. Now, it's time for you to take the pursuit of knowledge to <color=#CA2E0AFF>your Class Master</color>. They will familiarize you with the new class and combat skills. And maybe a surprise or two as well, heh!",
    ["Dialogue3530104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I await good news from you. I hope the next time we meet, it's to witness your rebirth under Odin's statue.",
    ["Dialogue3530201"]="From Novice to Taekwon, from Taekwon to Star Gladiator, then Star Monarch. Now, you are going to become the formidable Stellar Fist. Adventurer, I'm glad to have been your mentor and witnessed your entire journey of getting stronger. However, you need to risk your life in the trial of the Stellar Fist. Do you still want to proceed?",
    ["Dialogue3530202"]="Good! That's the spirit! Looks like you haven't forgotten your vow from the day you stepped into the world of Taekwon! The first step to becoming a Stellar Fist isn't about how to hit hard but about how to master your defense. This is the focus of today's first trial—\"The Way of Defense.\"",
    ["Dialogue3530203"]="The learning path of martial arts is unending; we can't ever claim to be the strongest. So, how do you survive or even overcome someone far stronger than you?",
    ["Dialogue3530204"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Flail-wielding Goblin</color> in this forest will teach you, just like how they kept the Orc tribes at bay. Master \"The Way of Defense\" as you fight them, and don't ever underestimate a goblin for their size!",
    ["Dialogue3530301"]="(Phoenix takes a glance at you)\nDid you learn anything from the Goblins' defense? Their modified weapons and formations did cause enough trouble for the Orcs. However, defense alone can't turn the battle around. Orcs value blood ties and unity. Should they team up with other tribes outside these woods, the end of the Goblins here is inevitable.",
    ["Dialogue3530302"]="Sure, but nearly impossible. Hundreds of years of conflict have implanted a deep fear of Orcs in the Goblins, nearly exhausting their will to attack. It's in the nature of all creatures to avoid death and strive to survive; we humans are no exception. However, as my student and a future Stellar Fist, I hope you can overcome it.",
    ["Dialogue3530303"]="Now, we're off to the place to learn \"The Way of Attack\" at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Arena</color>. Orcs are born warriors and among the strongest species in Geffen. These battles for survival are second to none in getting you up to speed in your learning process.",
    ["Dialogue3530304"]="Every life meets death, and to me, I'd much rather die in battle than wither away on a sickbed. To evolve and emerge as a true Stellar Fist, you must conquer your fear. Adventurer, come see me at the arena.",
    ["Dialogue3530401"]="You made it.\n(Phoenix nods, letting out a sigh of relief only after seeing the Orc Hero is finally down, then turns to put an arm around your shoulders)\nThis... is what it takes to be a recognized Stellar Fist!",
    ["Dialogue3530402"]="So many times... His weapon nearly crushed your skull, and I was... okay, a little nervous. The important thing is that you've now got that seasoned look in your eyes, the kind that's seen life and death. I'm now ready to lead you on the journey to becoming a Stellar Fist!",
    ["Dialogue3530403"]="Every old warrior in the Orc tribes, unable to join the fray, dreams of a heroic demise in combat. You've granted him that honor; don't overthink it.",
    ["Dialogue3530404"]="Well done, my student. You're now ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to Prontera</color> for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color> that Wolmas the Archbishop has set up for you. Legend has it that there are even stronger classes beyond Stellar Fist. I'm excited to see how far you'll go, maybe even outshining us all!",
    ["Dialogue3530501"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal Job Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3540101"]="Successor of Odin's bloodline, your efforts have awakened the Rune Slab. Now, the time has come to embark on the path of class advancement...",
    ["Dialogue3540102"]="(With her eyes shut, the goddess gazes into your destiny.)\nGo back to where your journey first began; that place that was once your beginning as a Novice is now the starting point for your fourth-class advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3540103"]="Embrace your earliest lessons once more; as a fledgling student, listen to the wisdom of your mentor, letting it be the unceasing beacon on your path.",
    ["Dialogue3540104"]="(The goddess nods slightly, a quiet affirmation.)\nFollow where your heart leads, and go to the place where you are called.",
    ["Dialogue3540105"]="I have granted Wolmas and the others my vision; once you complete the Class Advancement Trial, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Glast Heim Chivalry to join the Class Advancement Ceremony</color>. There, my gift to you shall become your own power, making you a true fourth-class Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3540106"]="And now, I shall fall into rest once more...",
    ["Dialogue3540201"]="So, you've come.\n(Charles pulls forth a <color=#CA2E0AFF>scroll</color> from the folds of his robe.)\nOnce mastered, this will make you an Arch Mage.",
    ["Dialogue3540202"]="It's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>forbidden spell</color>. What else could it be?",
    ["Dialogue3540203"]="Hah, never underestimate the academy's wisdom.\n(Charles lifts his head with pride)\nFear not; it won't kill you. At worst... you'll end up half-dead.",
    ["Dialogue3540204"]="Ready yourself.\n(Charles seizes your wrist, pressing it to the aged scroll. A mysterious light flickers, and a Dimensional Gap begins to open in front of you.)",
    ["Dialogue3540205"]="(Charles raises his staff, pointing expressionlessly at the Dimensional Gap.)\nTo learn forbidden spells is to invite danger. Are you not <color=#CA2E0AFF>going in</color>? Or must I push you?",
    ["Dialogue3540206"]="Five, four, three, two...",
    ["Dialogue3540301"]="Calm yourself—don't resist them!\n(A soft light radiates from Charles' staff, filling you with a gentle force that gradually strengthens your spirit.)",
    ["Dialogue3540302"]="Created by the founding magic instructor of Criatura Academy, this incantation was designed to forcibly broaden mental power. Its perilous nature led the academy to declare it forbidden.",
    ["Dialogue3540303"]="Only by mastering this can you learn further forbidden spells without being lured by the taboo knowledge within and becoming a wandering spirit of the tome.",
    ["Dialogue3540304"]="They were Criatura students like yourself—Warlocks consumed by forbidden knowledge. Do you see? The study of magic is treacherous; here at Criatura Academy, even as a Warlock, a single slip can make you a creature beyond recognition.",
    ["Dialogue3540305"]="After becoming an Arch Mage, you'll continually face trials like this to gain more knowledge. Tell me, do you have the courage to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go further and pursue the supreme mysteries of magic</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3540306"]="...Very well.\n(Charles' face reflects both pride and concern.)\nYou may now go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3540401"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now, we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3550201"]="Adventurer? Why are you here?\n(Hamid, clad in gold and silver, stares at you in confusion.)\nAh... it seems I am indeed working outside my business as a profitless mentor.",
    ["Dialogue3550202"]="Ah! I see! So you want to be a Meister? Admirable! A new class brings new profit opportunities—I see you love Zeny as much as I do!",
    ["Dialogue3550203"]="In the spirit of our mutual love of Zeny, I'll grant you a rare piece of advice. Previously, the token of a Mechanic was the core of Magic Gear, so this time...",
    ["Dialogue3550204"]="Precisely! But don't expect my help this time—do you have any idea of the cost of maintaining the trial mechanisms? After blowing through the academy's funding, I had to chip in myself! So, for the stronger Magic Gear, head to Al De Baran's Clock Tower. They say time flows oddly there... And, well, my age is catching up, ahem...",
    ["Dialogue3550205"]="(Hamid marks a spot on your map.)\nGo here... descend to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clock Tower B2</color>, and you'll find an abandoned platform. Defeat the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alarm</color>, gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Mechanical Cores</color>, and then I'll take care of your class advancement!",
    ["Dialogue3550206"]="Huh?\n(Surprised, Hamid covers his mouth with his ring-covered fingers.)\nAdventurer, did you forget we're Merchants?",
    ["Dialogue3550207"]="(Hamid flashes his hand in front of you.)\nFair deal—fifty-fifty split! My advice fee is covered, so your class advancement fee will be paid in Mechanical Cores!",
    ["Dialogue3550301"]="Ah yes! Those things! They're what gave me these dreadful white hairs back when I was still a Merchant! Ahem... Adventurer, you're... feeling okay, yes?",
    ["Dialogue3550302"]="A worthy successor of Odin's bloodline indeed! How about a business partnership, hmm? I've got a line of customers eager to explore the mysteries of the Clock Tower.",
    ["Dialogue3550303"]="(With a nervous look, Hamid examines you up and down, his hand on his chin.)\nLet's see... no lines, no gray hairs... looking sharp! But, just in case, you might want to visit the church for a cleansing ritual—I'll cover the costs!",
    ["Dialogue3550304"]="Ah, getting carried away... Anyway, it's time for your Meister class advancement ceremony! Wolmas the Archbishop is waiting for you at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3550305"]="(Hamid wipes his eyes, clapping you heartily on the shoulder.)\nWith your new class as Meister, you'll be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>rent stronger Magic Gear from the Mecha Rental Store</color>. Why am I feeling this pride all of a sudden? Has my heart not yet been filled with enough Zeny?",
    ["Dialogue3560201"]="(Moxie plays with a rose, flashing you a bewitching smile.)\nAh, my beloved student, your thirst for the art of darkness is as fierce as ever.",
    ["Dialogue3560202"]="Shh...\n(The rose rests against your lips as Moxie whispers.)\nLet me guess—you wish to become a Shadow Cross, correct?",
    ["Dialogue3560203"]="How could I refuse a request from a student I care for so deeply?\n(With a graceful spin, Moxie lifts her skirts.)\nThe name of Shadow Cross has no charm at all—I'd rather call it... Shadow Waltz.",
    ["Dialogue3560204"]="A dancer in the shadow's deadly waltz—there's no better name. If you desire an invitation to this \"ball,\" you have to pay your life upfront!",
    ["Dialogue3560205"]="In the depths of Labyrinth Forest, so the legend goes, lies the den of Baphomet Jr.—vile creatures tied to Baphomet. With their power and secret hideout, few Adventurers are bold enough to launch a raid against them.",
    ["Dialogue3560206"]="Adventurer, I want you to enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> alone, eradicating them without a sound, including the mightiest of all—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baphomet Jr. King</color>. Your entry ticket to becoming a Shadow Cross is its <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Heart</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3560207"]="(Moxie tilts your chin up, her smile unreadable.)\nAhhh, do come back unharmed. If my favorite student went missing, I'd have to hunt down your enemies myself.",
    ["Dialogue3560301"]="Such vile creatures have no place in this world; let their deaths pave the way for my most cherished student.",
    ["Dialogue3560302"]="(Moxie holds the blackened heart with her pale fingers, a pleased smile on her lips.)\nNow, you may become a powerful Shadow Cross. Every shadowed place beyond the sun's reach will be yours to command.",
    ["Dialogue3560303"]="The Class Advancement Ceremony will be conducted by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>. All your mentors will be there. My dear Adventurer, don't keep us waiting too long.",
    ["Dialogue3570201"]="(Melbrun, overflowing with excitement, circles you.)\nSo, Adventurer, you're seeking the path of Wind Hawk? Hahaha! Such rapid growth—worthy of my best student!",
    ["Dialogue3570202"]="However, for this Class Advancement Trial, your prey won't be beasts...\n(Melbrun's eyes grow wide.)\nThey'll be spirits!!!",
    ["Dialogue3570203"]="Ta-da! Criatura Academy's Summer Courage Trial location is set! Before it begins, though, we need a top student to clear the hazardous <color=#CA2E0AFF>spirits</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ghastly Graveyard</color>, leaving only the friendly little ones. Adventurer, we're counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue3570204"]="(Melbrun presents you with a small, square packet.)\nThis is a Spirit-Summoning Incense—light it, and you'll draw forth spirits that usually only appear on Halloween!",
    ["Dialogue3570205"]="Don't worry! Your arrows can already tear through the chest of any physical being, but as a Wind Hawk, your arrows will be able to claim even the <color=#CA2E0AFF>unseen</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3570206"]="Do you wish to test your worth as a Wind Hawk? Ready your bow, steady your aim, and focus—every unseen creature has a weak point, and you're the one to find it.",
    ["Dialogue3570207"]="Go now, for your falcon, and your bow will reveal the truth.",
    ["Dialogue3570301"]="You're back! So, how was it?",
    ["Dialogue3570302"]="(Melbrun listens intently, then extends his hand.)\nIt seems you truly have the skill of a Wind Hawk. However, let me examine your bow to verify the honesty of its wielder.",
    ["Dialogue3570303"]="(Melbrun inspects your weapon, a pleased look crossing his face.)\nEven the sincerest vow can be false, but your arrows never lie. You may now proceed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>, where Wolmas the Archbishop will conduct your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3570304"]="Your Warg will also grow stronger; head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mount Keeper</color> to obtain your <color=#CA2E0AFF>New Class Mount</color>. Similarly, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Falcon Keeper</color> awaits with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>New Falcon Companion</color> for you. Congratulations, Criatura's Wind Hawk.",
    ["Dialogue3580201"]="Well, look who's back! The great Adventurer!\n(Yadrew lets out a hearty laugh, looking you over from head to toe.)",
    ["Dialogue3580202"]="I hear you're about to become an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Imperial Guard</color>—extraordinary! If the dean finds out, he may very well add you to the academy's book of distinguished alumni!",
    ["Dialogue3580203"]="Right... so you need to go for the Class Advancement Trial, but it's not happening at the academy, and I'm not the one overseeing it. The Imperial Guards are selected by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knight selection system</color> of the royal family. From this moment, your weapon defends the kingdom's peace and prosperity.",
    ["Dialogue3580204"]="No need to worry. When the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Slab</color> was awakened, the Royal Chivalry was expecting new members. Just go see Captain Hallam now. He'll make sure you become a real Imperial Guard.",
    ["Dialogue3580301"]="(Hallam squints at you, sizing you up, then smiles with satisfaction.)\n...You're looking stronger than before, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3580302"]="(He gives a nod of approval.)\nThat's not bad. Even here in Prontera, I hear your name from those Bards. They write songs about your adventures and sing them far and wide. You've become a well-known Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3580303"]="However, if you think the knights will welcome you in after that, you've got it all wrong. To join the Royal Chivalry and become one of the elite members of the Imperial Guard, there's one last trial.",
    ["Dialogue3580304"]="So tell me—\n(Hallam draws his sword, raises it high, then gently places it on your shoulder.)",
    ["Dialogue3580305"]="Do you swear, from now on, to live by the knight's creed: to never harm the weak, fear no one, betray no friend, and stay true to your heart?",
    ["Dialogue3580306"]="(He waves his hand, cutting you off.)\nYou don't need to say anything, Adventurer. A knight's oath can only be proven with the sword in your hand. If you're ready, head to the palace's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grand Banquet Hall</color> and take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>trial of Royal Chivalry</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3580401"]="... As expected of you, Adventurer. You've got the presence of a seasoned knight. No doubt—you've passed!",
    ["Dialogue3580402"]="(Hallam pats your shoulder with a smile.)\nGo on, <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to the Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and get ready for your Class Advancement Ceremony. From today on... we're brothers fighting side by side.",
    ["Dialogue3590101"]="Ah, it's you. No wonder I feel the elements stirring so intensely. They're all gathering here... Soon, you'll have new power.",
    ["Dialogue3590102"]="(Usually strict mentor is smiling with pride now.)\nCongratulations, Adventurer. You've just obtained access to the Elemental Hall.",
    ["Dialogue3590103"]="(He laughs and waves his hand.)\nGo ahead. Lord <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika</color> should've already heard about the Rune Slab being awakened. He'll probably be waiting for you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color>. Pass his test, and you'll become a true Elemental Master.",
    ["Dialogue3590201"]="Ah, it's you again, Adventurer. I still remember our first meeting clearly, and now, just a few years later, that greenhorn Magician can already keep up with me. I'm amazed by how quickly you've grown.",
    ["Dialogue3590202"]="(Kroneika laughs, stroking his gray beard.)\nThere's a lot for you to learn, but I've got nothing more to teach. To progress further... we'll need the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient manuscripts of Great Sage Merlin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3590203"]="That's right... it's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin's Manuscript</color>. You once assisted the Heines Family in recovering this rare artifact from thieves. Upon learning of your Rune Slab awakening, I retrieved it for study, hoping to aid your class advancement. Fortunately, just yesterday, I discovered a method that may unlock further elemental secrets for you.",
    ["Dialogue3590204"]="According to the manuscript, Merlin attempted to merge four basic elements—Wind, Water, Fire, and Earth—to create a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new elemental spirit</color>. But as he grew older and weaker, he sealed it away deep in the Labyrinth Forest, leaving behind a method for future generations to unlock it...",
    ["Dialogue3590205"]="(Kroneika nods his head.)\nThat's right, Adventurer. Use the manuscript's instructions to <color=#CA2E0AFF>unseal the spirit</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take it as your own</color>. Merlin didn't want his creation to stay trapped in that cold, foggy forest forever.",
    ["Dialogue3590206"]="The elemental spirit created by Merlin called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Serpens</color>, is sealed under the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest cliff of the Labyrinth Forest</color>. The spirit carries <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poison Attributes</color> and looks like a three-headed snake, each head with its own meaning—<color=#CA2E0AFF>white for creation</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple for protection</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>black for destruction</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3590207"]="To lift the seal, head to the Labyrinth Forest and grab the three <color=#CA2E0AFF>Divine Charms</color> Merlin hid in the hands of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Creator</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Protector</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Destroyer</color>... Then, take the charms to Serpens and burn them at the corresponding snake head to awaken it. However, to make it obey, you'll have to demonstrate your power.",
    ["Dialogue3590208"]="... I'm sorry, but I don't really know what it means. Merlin only left these lines in the manuscript—",
    ["Dialogue3590209"]="\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>The creator builds. The protector protects. The destroyer never bows.</color>\" You will have to figure out the rest yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3590210"]="... Great. I see that determination in your eyes. Don't hesitate—give it a try! I'll be here waiting for your success. Come back if you need help with anything.",
    ["Dialogue3590301"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great One</color> may be gone, but their brilliance lives on, guiding the ones who come after...♪",
    ["Dialogue3590302"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Servant</color> rests, but should the master call, they will respond...♪",
    ["Dialogue3590303"]="Here's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Token</color>, for whoever comes next. Good luck...♪",
    ["Dialogue3590304"]="Adventurer, my duty has been fulfilled. From now on, it's all up to you.\n(As the melody goes on, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>weird little piece of paper</color> drops out of Morts' pocket...?)",
    ["Dialogue3590401"]="And with this, you are truly worthy of being called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elemental Master</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3590402"]="It's time to set off, Adventurer. Return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>attend</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3590501"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now, we can hold a formal Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3590601"]="(Look at this ancient tree—it's been through ages, and yet, every year, fresh leaves grow back. Feels like the Great Sage Merlin's hints are tied to this somehow.)",
    ["Dialogue3590602"]="(You reach out to the tree, and the moment you touch it, there's a flash of light, and suddenly, you've got this <color=#CA2E0AFF>weird charm</color> in your hand...)",
    ["Dialogue3590701"]="(Megalith opens its mouth, and a faint <color=#CA2E0AFF>ray of light</color> drifts out slowly...)",
    ["Dialogue3600201"]="Oh, my dear student! Have you heard?\n(Moxie pulls you into an embrace and whispers in your ear.)\nIt's been a bit uneasy lately. Criatura Academy's packed with terrifying...",
    ["Dialogue3600202"]="Take a guess.\n(You feel Moxie's warm breath on your ear; it's a little ticklish, and there's an oddly teasing tone to it.)\nIf you guess correctly, I'll give you a reward!",
    ["Dialogue3600203"]="Tch... You're no fun. I mean, it's all because you awakened the Rune Slab, and now Criatura Academy is buzzing with all these clueless newbies. And you, the protagonist, are really late to the party!",
    ["Dialogue3600204"]="Hmm... clueless and brave. So you probably don't know that to become an Abyss Chaser, you have to gaze into the abyss and seek out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Death Experience</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3600205"]="(Moxie says nothing, giving you a mysterious smile.)\nLet's go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Umbala</color>. I'll see if your courage can bear the consequences.",
    ["Dialogue3600301"]="Adventurer, once you cross here, you enter the territory of Hel, Queen of the Underworld. The key to your class advancement is to sign a contract with her while you're still alive. But the price is your soul, forever marked by the Realm of the Dead.",
    ["Dialogue3600302"]="Once you die, Hel will claim you as her servant forever, never resting in peace... Even so, do you still want to become an Abyss Chaser?",
    ["Dialogue3600303"]="... Sigh, you really stuck with it, huh? From a Rogue to this... Alright, go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zorser</color>, the Necromancer. Get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Contract</color>, throw it into the Wraith Forge, and... uh... yeah, that should probably be enough?",
    ["Dialogue3600304"]="(Before you know it, Moxie's already kicked you into a tree hole, her playful voice fading in the distance...)\nDon't forget the <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>offering</color>!</size> That's all I can do for you; the rest is up to YOU. You... you...",
    ["Dialogue3600401"]="Mmm... such a fresh soul, overflowing with the scent of the living... and the taste of powerful ambition!",
    ["Dialogue3600402"]="Empty-handed and calling me by name? Tsk, tsk... Moxie sure doesn't teach her students any respect...\n(Zorser rubs his skull like he has a headache—though you're pretty sure he can't actually feel anything.)",
    ["Dialogue3600403"]="Ahem! Rules are rules—no offering, no contract! But... since Moxie and I go way back...",
    ["Dialogue3600404"]="(The Necromancer rubs his chin, eyeing you up. Somehow, even with his hollow eye sockets... he looks a little too sneaky for a skeleton.)\nHey, don't you have a camera? Get me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Photo of Loli Ruri</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3600405"]="Hehehe... I'm a genius! That hot-tempered witch never lets anyone near! Get too close, and she'll knock you senseless. But with a photo? Now I can just hang it up and stare all day! Hehehe...",
    ["Dialogue3600501"]="(Zorser grabs the photo in a flash, eagerly inspecting it.)\nOoooh... The angle, the details... <size=26>PERFECT VIEW!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3600502"]="Honestly, kid, you should advance to photography. It's got a way BRIGHTER future than Abyss Chaser.",
    ["Dialogue3600503"]="What a shame, truly a shame... You can't talk sense into a stubborn ghost. Tsk, tsk... Well then, here's your Undead Contract! You already know what it means by <color=#CA2E0AFF>signing</color> this, right? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Read carefully</color>—until your name is on it, you can still walk away.",
    ["Dialogue3600601"]="One last step—just <color=#CA2E0AFF>throw the Undead Contract into the Wraith Forge</color>...\n(Zorser chuckles, the eerie clatter of his bones ringing out.)\nOnce you do, your contract with Hel, the Queen of the Underworld, is official!",
    ["Dialogue3600602"]="The next time we cross paths, I'm sure you'll be Hel's loyal little servant. Seeing you bow and scrape will be most entertaining! Hehehehe...",
    ["Dialogue3600701"]="(Moxie eyes you up and down, then smirks once she confirms you're in one piece.)\nAs expected... My lovely student, how could a mere Queen of the Underworld steal you away? Far more breathtaking adventures await you.",
    ["Dialogue3600702"]="Walking the thin line between life and death, gambling with the eyes lurking in the abyss. As an Abyss Chaser, you will be the nightmare hidden in the shadows...",
    ["Dialogue3600703"]="The Class Advancement Ceremony will be conducted by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>. All your mentors will be there. My dear Adventurer, don't keep us waiting too long.",
    ["Dialogue3610201"]="Sigh... Another talented student lost to the Euphonic Symphony.\n(Melbrun covers his face in exaggerated sorrow.)\nOh my Odin, why didn't you guide them to become a dashing Wind Hawk?!",
    ["Dialogue3610202"]="<size=26>You don't get it at all!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3610203"]="Fourth Class... It's the Fourth Class! This is the kind of achievement that goes down in the history of Criatura Academy! You even got a revelation from Goddess Shikoti and awakened the lost Rune Slab! Sniff... If I had only known... <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>my dream of becoming the \"Outstanding Mentor\" would've been within reach...!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3610204"]="You—You—How dare you attack your mentor with the very weapon I taught you to use?! Unbelievable! Disgraceful!\n(Melbrun, seething, raises his bow and thwacks you on the butt.)\nGet out of my sight! Go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color> and find the losers in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Euphonic Symphony</color>! I don't want to see your face!",
    ["Dialogue3610302"]="Of course, Uncle Callahan! Awakening the Rune Slab is no small feat! Adventurer, as soon as we got the news, we hurried back to set up your Class Advancement Trial...",
    ["Dialogue3610303"]="(Vendra unfurls the scroll and hands it over.)\nHere, Adventurer—take a look.",
    ["Dialogue3610304"]="I had Alexia help retrieve this <color=#CA2E0AFF>autobiography</color> from Lady Margaret's resting place. She was known for creating numerous works <color=#CA2E0AFF>based on herself</color>. Some called her self-absorbed, while others even blamed her pride for the destruction of Dragon Flame...",
    ["Dialogue3610305"]="Uncle Callahan and I, however, think differently. To us, this is what made Lady Margaret special. She was fearless, self-assured, and resilient. Above all, she never doubted her own strength or worth. That self-awareness is what let her stay true to her path, no matter what the world thought of her.",
    ["Dialogue3610306"]="If not for that... how could she have ever reclaimed this paradise back from the dragons for the Nerius Family?\n(Vendra lifts a hand and points forward. You follow her direction and see the entire Comodo unfold before you.)",
    ["Dialogue3610307"]="Most say bards tell the stories of heroes, and dancers bring the lives of great figures to the stage—as if we're just here to document history. But here's the truth—every piece of art is, at its core, a projection of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>self</color>. If you <color=#CA2E0AFF>don't know who you are</color>, how can you ever truly understand the world?",
    ["Dialogue3610308"]="As Lady Margaret once wrote—A bard must first tell their own tale, and a dancer must first find joy in themselves. So before we begin your fourth class advancement, I want you to become the protagonist in your own story.",
    ["Dialogue3610309"]="What Uncle Callahan means is, if we asked you to turn <color=#CA2E0AFF>your own journey</color> into a work of art, what would it look like?",
    ["Dialogue3610310"]="(Vendra sees your troubled expression and offers a comforting smile.)\nDon't worry, Adventurer. This isn't something you have to answer right away. Think it over carefully. If you're lost, maybe revisiting familiar places will help you see things differently.",
    ["Dialogue3610401"]="(The coffin remains untouched, just as you recall. You remember why you first came here—to aid the Eden Group in investigating the truth behind the <color=#CA2E0AFF>destruction of Dragon Flame</color>. Many blamed Lady Margaret, claiming that sealing Morroc made her conceited and reckless. But... was that truly the case?)",
    ["Dialogue3610402"]="(You remember reading her letter to the Great Sage Nithil. She was fully conscious of the criticism her choices would draw, but she never faltered. Her purpose was clear—to shield the people of Comodo and release them from the relentless terror of dragon attacks. Regardless of others' words, <color=#CA2E0AFF>her spirit remained unchanged</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3610501"]="(Though now decayed, the structure hints at its former magnificence. You remember the polarizing figure of King Schmidt—a tyrant, without question, who sacrificed warriors on the altar of his own ambition...)",
    ["Dialogue3610502"]="(Still, his legacy includes great achievements. Before he met Hermes, his empire was at its height. Were it not for that single, fatal mistake, Glast Heim could still exist, potentially defining the continent as we know it. But King Schmidt was, after all, only a mortal, ultimately undone by his own inner demon....)",
    ["Dialogue3610601"]="(Standing before the Walter Family's grave, you remember the untold royal secrets that were never meant to be known. Humanity is <color=#CA2E0AFF>fickle</color>—driven by greed, fear, and hatred. Even the smallest ember can grow into an unstoppable inferno of ambition. But... what about you?)",
    ["Dialogue3610602"]="(Objectivity is easy with others' stories. But faced with your own story, could you stand as firm as Lady Margaret? Or would you, like King Schmidt and the Walter Family, be led astray and plunge into darkness?)",
    ["Dialogue3610603"]="(Callahan said that every work of art is ultimately a reflection of its creator. He wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>see yourself clearly</color>... but standing here, you only feel more uncertain. Perhaps... you need to go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>where it all began</color> to find your answer...?)",
    ["Dialogue3610701"]="(A voice you recognize pulls you from your deep thoughts. Looking around, you suddenly realize that you've wandered back to the place where it all started.)\nI'm Kiki! It's been forever! I heard you awakened the Rune Slab—so you're finally becoming a Fourth Class Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3610702"]="Wow, what a change! The first time we met, you were just a Novice who knew nothing... and now you're a legendary Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3610703"]="I think we took a photo back then, right? Haha, do you remember what you looked like? So clueless, so innocent... but with a fearless heart and infinite potential! No wonder Dean Mainz always says that Novices are like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blank page</color>—you never know how their story will unfold...",
    ["Dialogue3610704"]="Eh? Eh?! What's happening? Hey, wait! <size=26>Where are you going?!</size><size=28> I'm not done talking—!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3610801"]="(Even the ever-kind Callahan now looks stern.)\nAdventurer, I believe you're not the type to take shortcuts. If you've chosen this blank page as your answer, then surely, you have a reason. Would you share it with us?",
    ["Dialogue3610802"]="... What do you mean by that, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3610803"]="You're telling me... you're just an <color=#CA2E0AFF>ordinary person</color>?\n(Vendra blinks in confusion as if trying to process your words.)",
    ["Dialogue3610804"]="Lady Margaret possessed an unshakable resolve, impervious to both opinion and convention. This strength, however, was uniquely hers. You've witnessed how readily others succumb to their desires.",
    ["Dialogue3610805"]="So this blank page is your way of reminding yourself—no matter what, you must always <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay true to your heart</color>, the very heart when you first started your adventure.\n(Vendra rubs her head, looking puzzled before turning to Callahan.)\nWait... wait a minute. Uncle Callahan, I think I actually agree with the Adventurer now...",
    ["Dialogue3610806"]="... You might be right, Vendra. Perhaps we are the foolish ones...",
    ["Dialogue3610807"]="We gave you this question so that, through writing your own tale, you could better understand yourself. And realizing your weaknesses and ordinariness—doesn't that count as true self-awareness?",
    ["Dialogue3610808"]="(Callahan nods, stroking his beard.)\nIndeed, I find this answer very fitting. As you move forward—through triumphs and hardships—whenever you stand at a turning point, I hope you will always recall this moment and stay true <color=#CA2E0AFF>to your heart when you first started your adventure</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3610809"]="Well then, it's time for you to move forward. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Return to the Glast Heim Chivalry</color>. Wolmas the Archbishop is more than ready to conduct your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>. Hohoho!",
    ["Dialogue3620201"]="Man... It's getting harder to make a living now...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I seriously need to come up with a new business plan...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3620202"]="Get lost! You're making me mad just by standing there—YOU! Yeah! It's you! When did you secretly awaken the Rune Slab?! And why didn't you give me a heads-up?!",
    ["Dialogue3620203"]="This is a once-in-a-lifetime business opportunity! Do you know what people are willing to pay the most for?!\n(Hamid slaps the table so hard his belly jiggles.)\n<size=26>It's fame! The power of exposure!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3620204"]="Fourth Class, my friend! Do you know how insanely rare that is?! Rune-Midgard has had barely any in centuries! Every magazine and newspaper will be after you! Get famous, score some sponsorships and bam—you'll be set for life!",
    ["Dialogue3620205"]="I knew it... I just knew it! You're hopeless! Someone like you, with zero sense about Zeny, should stick with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nicolas</color> and his beakers!\n(Hamid shoots you a sharp look.)\nGo on, shoo! Merchants are no friends of Alchemists! Don't waste my time!",
    ["Dialogue3620301"]="Ah, Adventurer! It's been a while. Word is, you've awakened the Rune Slab. I take it you're here for some class advancement advice?",
    ["Dialogue3620302"]="You never fail to impress. It feels like just yesterday you became an Alchemist, and now you stand at the threshold of becoming a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Biolo</color>. But before you go down this path, you'll need an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Evolution Potion</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3620303"]="First, you need to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Twilight Creeper</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Entwined Root</color>, use an alchemy circle to amplify their lifeforce, and top it off with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dew of Spirit Tree</color>... Making the Evolution Potion is simple, but there are two crucial rules to follow.",
    ["Dialogue3620304"]="(Nicolas raises his hand and holds up one finger.)\nRule number one: The <color=#CA2E0AFF>person who consumes</color> the Evolution Potion must not be the one who crafts it.",
    ["Dialogue3620305"]="It's all about oversight, Adventurer. Alchemy treads the line between forbidden knowledge and temptation. Many times, falling into corruption happens in a split second... Evolution Potions, which drastically improve your body's capabilities, are no different. The guild is here to guide you, but it's also our duty to make sure you use that power responsibly.",
    ["Dialogue3620306"]="(Nicolas raises another finger.)\nRule number two: You must gather the materials for the Evolution Potion to prove you can handle its power.",
    ["Dialogue3620307"]="Twilight Creeper and Entwined Root are dropped by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dryad</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooden Golem</color>, while the Dew of Spirit Tree is hidden in the depths of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Luluka Forest</color>, where monsters dwell... Successfully collecting these materials will be your trial before the Class Advancement Ceremony. But I have no doubt this will be a piece of cake for you, right?",
    ["Dialogue3620401"]="Perfect, now the materials are all here. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait a moment</color>, Adventurer. I'll get the Evolution Potion ready for you.",
    ["Dialogue3620501"]="This potion will create astounding changes in your body. Drinking it will cause your genes to mutate and reorganize, unlocking strength that goes beyond human limits... But remember, any power that defies the rules of nature always comes with a cost.",
    ["Dialogue3620502"]="Alchemy is often seen as the key to the realm of god, a means to exchange anything for an equivalent price. But what kind of door does this key actually unlock? And beyond that door... is the truth we've been chasing all along really there?",
    ["Dialogue3620503"]="(Nicolas holds out a test tube to you.)\nThis is your final chance, Adventurer. Will you... unlock this door?",
    ["Dialogue3620504"]="(Nicolas nods in satisfaction as you drink the potion without a moment's doubt.)\n... Excellent. You'll never discover what lies ahead if you never step beyond the door. I'm proud of you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3620505"]="(Seeing you refuse, Nicolas chuckles as he withdraws the test tube.)\nThat's fine. Caution is a trait few possess in alchemy, and it's something to be respected. I'll hold onto the potion for now—whenever you're ready, you can return for it.",
    ["Dialogue3620506"]="(Nicolas lets out a hearty laugh.)\nAdventurer, I never said you had to drink the Evolution Potion to become a Biolo!",
    ["Dialogue3620507"]="What I said was that successfully collecting these materials will be your trial before the Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3620508"]="(Nicolas pats your shoulder with a warm smile.)\nAlright, it's time. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> and attend your Class Advancement Ceremony. Don't keep Wolmas the Archbishop waiting too long!",
    ["Dialogue3630201"]="... Took you long enough, Adventurer.\n(Alice closes her book and flashes you that ever-familiar gentle smile.)",
    ["Dialogue3630202"]="When you became a Shura, I was afraid you'd lose yourself to obsession and drift down the wrong path. But now, I see that I was worried for nothing. Your strength has surpassed all my expectations—you really are my best student.",
    ["Dialogue3630203"]="(Alice gives a knowing nod.)\nOf course. I knew you'd want to push forward after awakening the Rune Slab. So, I reached out to Master <color=#CA2E0AFF>Peerless Jin</color> to ask him to guide you through your next class advancement...",
    ["Dialogue3630204"]="By now, he should be waiting for you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Incense Pavilion</color>, expecting your arrival.",
    ["Dialogue3630301"]="(Peerless Jin stands before the Incense Pavilion, arms crossed, looking like he's been expecting you.)\nWe meet again, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3630302"]="Alice's message filled me in on everything about your awakening of the Rune Slab. Even after becoming a Shura, you haven't lost your heart... That's reassuring.",
    ["Dialogue3630303"]="Naturally, I'm here to guide you and help you sharpen your skills. But how strong you become... that depends on you.",
    ["Dialogue3630304"]="Not bad, not bad! That's the spirit!\n(Peerless Jin laughs heartily, pulling out a tome and passing it to you.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Take a look</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3630401"]="This tome holds the secrets of the Monks. From what I understand, the poem's word \"Nether\" refers to the Munak Cave beneath Payon. As for \"Buddha's Heart\"...",
    ["Dialogue3630402"]="Exactly, Adventurer. You've been through the Munak Cave before, so you should recall the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Broken Butsudan</color> deep inside. All you need to do is find it and <color=#CA2E0AFF>kneel before it in devotion</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3630403"]="Haven't I said it already? How strong you become depends on you.\n(Peerless Jin smirks, tapping his chin thoughtfully.)\nIf your faith is strong enough, <color=#CA2E0AFF>they</color>... will guide you.",
    ["Dialogue3630501"]="You're back, Adventurer. Judging by your expression... I take it you've found your answer?",
    ["Dialogue3630502"]="(Bathed in the glow of the flame, Peerless Jin's face softens into a proud smile.)\nNot bad... I had a feeling <color=#CA2E0AFF>they</color> would accept you.",
    ["Dialogue3630503"]="They were once like you—Shuras who walked this path yet still carried compassion in their hearts. The flame you hold... it is their <color=#CA2E0AFF>souls</color>, locked inside the statues by their own will upon death.",
    ["Dialogue3630504"]="They walked this path before you, knowing all its hardships. So they offered their souls as fuel, burning away the thorns in the road for those who follow. This is both sacrifice... and legacy.",
    ["Dialogue3630505"]="(Peerless Jin presses your hands together, allowing the flame to fade into your skin. A burning sensation courses through your body, settling deep in your chest.)\nAdventurer, don't forget—this flame is the unfinished journey of those before you. Their power is yours now, but so is their duty.",
    ["Dialogue3630506"]="... Very good. The trial is over. Now, it's time for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3630601"]="For those who inherit our will, place the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Netherfire</color> before us, and your desire shall be fulfilled...",
    ["Dialogue3630602"]="Pass through the burial grounds of the perished heroes, step into the forgotten realm, and collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wandering souls</color> still lingering there...",
    ["Dialogue3630701"]="(The flame stands out in the dark cave, its light unwavering. As you walk closer, there is no burning sensation. When you finally reach out, it shatters into glimmering stardust... and <color=#CA2E0AFF>merges into your body</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3640201"]="Hohoho... Look at you, young Novice! You've gotten stronger again. Such breathtaking progress—it truly astonishes me.",
    ["Dialogue3640202"]="Ah... I can see it—you've no intention of stopping here. You seek to dive deeper into the path of the Novice. Alright, go see your mentor, Tanders! Maybe the Windmill Knight is already waiting in the Mjolnir Mountains with a trial just for you!",
    ["Dialogue3640301"]="Adventurer, you're finally here!",
    ["Dialogue3640302"]="The master... <size=26>has gone missing!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3640303"]="(He rubs his hands nervously and speaks fast.)\nSomeone came by a while ago and challenged the master to a duel in the Sphinx Cavern. You know how it is—no knight would turn down an honorable fight, especially not the brave Windmill Knight!",
    ["Dialogue3640304"]="So the master went... but he never came back! I've been waiting forever!\n(Sansha talks really fast, he almost seems... pleading.)\nAdventurer, please! Come help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>find my master</color>! I'm so worried!",
    ["Dialogue3640305"]="Eh? You mean why I didn't go with him to the Sphinx Cavern...?",
    ["Dialogue3640306"]="(Sansha looks away, a thin sheen of sweat broke out on his forehead.)\nUh... well... Knight duels are supposed to be fair, right? Master said that it would break the code of chivalry if I were to tag along...",
    ["Dialogue3640307"]="<size=26>... Yeah, that's it!</size> So he told me to stay and watch the bags! It's part of my duty, you know?",
    ["Dialogue3640308"]="(Sansha seems anxious—his hands are trembling a bit. But when your eyes meet, he suddenly freezes... maybe he's just nervous?)\nAdventurer, no time to waste—let's get to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color> and find my master! Hope he's not in trouble...",
    ["Dialogue3640401"]="(Pointing to the staggered footprints, Sansha speaks without hesitation.)\nLook—those <color=#CA2E0AFF>uneven</color> footprints gotta be Master's. He has a slight limp from an old injury from his younger days. But...",
    ["Dialogue3640402"]="(He looks up at the dark cave.)\nWe have no choice... We'll have to <size=26>head deeper</size> inside.",
    ["Dialogue3640501"]="(After Calest walks away, Tanders suddenly looks up—right at where you and Sansha are hiding.)\nSo, you all heard about it?",
    ["Dialogue3640502"]="Don't look so shocked, young one.",
    ["Dialogue3640503"]="Yeah, what happened?",
    ["Dialogue3640504"]="Calest is a serpent girl I saved when I was younger. After escaping the hunters, she's been traveling the continent, saying she's looking for a way to make everyone happy... Haha, what a dramatic reunion. Looks like she's learned a lot in all that time.",
    ["Dialogue3640505"]="(Tanders looks a bit helpless. He glances toward where Calest went and lets out a soft sigh.)\nThe world's a complicated place. Even a blank sheet can get stained by whatever brush touches it. The same goes for a young heart—toss it in messy dye, and it's going to change.",
    ["Dialogue3640506"]="(At that, Tanders suddenly looks at you.)\nAdventurer, what do you think makes a life a <size=26>\"good one\"</size>?",
    ["Dialogue3640507"]="(The old knight nods approvingly.)\nGood answer. But Calest... she's dead set on the idea that happiness lies in wealth, delicious meals, cozy homes, and fancy clothes. That's her version of a \"good life.\"",
    ["Dialogue3640508"]="So... what about us? Fighting monsters every day, eating under the stars, sleeping on rocks—are we just...",
    ["Dialogue3640509"]="Exactly. That's why she asked me—why I like living this kind of \"miserable\" life.",
    ["Dialogue3640510"]="<size=26>Pfft!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3640511"]="Anyway, once Calest made up her mind, she went all out and saved up tons of Zeny. That sweet, silly girl invited me, hoping I'd just enjoy all the nice things she prepared for my retirement. I really do appreciate it. But...",
    ["Dialogue3640512"]="But too bad—this old bald guy's still the most stubborn knight around! I'm a Windmill Knight, born for glory! You think I'd let age take me down? As long as I can swing this sword, I'll never give up on what I believe in!",
    ["Dialogue3640513"]="(Hearing that, Sansha proudly raised his head.)\nI made the same vow as my master the day I became a Novice。",
    ["Dialogue3640514"]="Nice! That's the spirit—I knew I saw it in you!\n(Tanders claps your shoulder hard and laughs, but a gloomy female voice soon ruins the mood...)",
    ["Dialogue3640515"]="(At some point, Calest returns. She stands not far off, frowning deeply and clearly upset...)\nWhy... <size=26>Why don't any of you get me?! Nobody understands me!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3640601"]="Did I... really do something wrong? Why?",
    ["Dialogue3640602"]="It's not about right or wrong, Calest. Who you want to be—that's up to your heart. Some want a stable life, while others chase thrills and adventure. Warriors fight with resolve; Novices walk the path of their heart... and that's the path I chose.",
    ["Dialogue3640603"]="I get it; you've seen a lot in your travels and picked up new ideas. But Calest, the path you take must be the calling of your own heart.",
    ["Dialogue3640604"]="Yeah... it's got all the answers.",
    ["Dialogue3640605"]="(After listening, she lowers her head in thought, then places a hand on her chest and nods.)\nI get it now! I'll... ask it properly!",
    ["Dialogue3640606"]="Whew... finally...\n(Sansha lets out a long sigh of relief.)\n<size=26>It's finally over!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3640607"]="(Tanders' eyes sparkle with emotion—happy, pride... maybe even a little proud of you?)\n<size=26>Well done! I knew you had it in you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3640608"]="I was actually gonna set up another trial for you... but what do you know? Calest just happened to throw me a challenge. Since she's confused about her heart, why not let you—our soon-to-be Hyper Novice—show her the ropes? Two birds, one stone!",
    ["Dialogue3640609"]="Don't be silly! Playing tricks on you together?\n(Sansha shakes his head, sounding totally serious.)\nThis is your class advancement trial!",
    ["Dialogue3640610"]="Well done! Well done!\n(Tanders laughs and slaps your back so hard you nearly stumble forward.)\nWhat are you standing around for? Go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> and get that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color> going!",
    ["Dialogue3640701"]="(Two sets of trails lead to the cave—one human, with the left foot lighter than the right. The other definitely isn't human—it looks like something dragged a tail.)",
    ["Dialogue3640801"]="... Tanders, why not drop this knight stuff and try living a cozy, comfy life? I set it all up—it took me forever! Or maybe just try a bite? I found this myself—",
    ["Dialogue3640802"]="Calest, you still don't get it.",
    ["Dialogue3640803"]="(Clang... something shatters on the floor. Then comes a sigh, the sound of scales scraping the ground... slowly fading away. She's probably gone.)",
    ["Dialogue3650201"]="Welcome, my dear Adventurer! Oh, should I say, my awesome ninja? I just wanted you to keep yourself in one piece on this path of ninjutsu, but wow—you really made it your own. Impressive!",
    ["Dialogue3650202"]="However, if you want to get even stronger, you still have more tests ahead!",
    ["Dialogue3650203"]="(The director strokes his beard, eyes full of excitement—though it feels like it's not just about the fourth class...)\nAkahyo left a message for you. He's probably waiting at Forgotten Lake Waterfall. Looks like a new trial's ready!",
    ["Dialogue3650204"]="Well, if you're curious, better go check it out! Hope you come back with good news, haha!",
    ["Dialogue3650301"]="Took you long enough. Have I taught you nothing?",
    ["Dialogue3650302"]="You're hesitating, or is that fear?\n(He scoffs—he's way more serious than usual today.)\nYou think you can fight me with that confused look?",
    ["Dialogue3650303"]="Want to know why Fire, Wind, and Water clans are stuck in endless deathmatches?\n(Akahyo looks into the rippling waters of Forgotten Lake Waterfall, smirking bitterly.)\nLong ago, the first heirs of the ninja arts made a vow before the Forgotten Lake...",
    ["Dialogue3650304"]="<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>On the Asura's trinity road, the blades remain, until the end.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3650305"]="So you remember... Good. Indeed, Forgotten Lake can <color=#CA2E0AFF>reverse life and death</color>. It's said the first ninja, chased and on the brink of death, drank from it—and rose anew. Since that moment, all who walk the ninja's path have worshiped it as <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine water</color>. But divine gifts are never free. The price is blood—your enemy's... or your own.",
    ["Dialogue3650306"]="Yet this is no history lesson for today. Now—\n(He lifts his chin, motioning toward the raging Forgotten Lake below.)\n<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>Jump</color></size>.",
    ["Dialogue3650307"]="Scared? Seriously?\n(Seeing your hesitation, he lightly kicks your leg—just enough to send you <color=#CA2E0AFF>tumbling into the water</color>...)",
    ["Dialogue3650401"]="... Not bad. Quicker than I expected.",
    ["Dialogue3650402"]="It looks like you figured it out—yes, the Munak Cave waterways are connected. Follow the current from Forgotten Lake, and you'll end up at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stream of the Fallen Deity</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3650403"]="(He points to the Pale Spirit Town in the distance, voice flat and unreadable.)\nThose who fail their class advancement are tossed into Forgotten Lake. The current brings them here. Some with strong willpower survive by absorbing the cave's energy—turning into Horong, like Nagi. But most...",
    ["Dialogue3650404"]="(Akahyo's lips tremble. He takes a deep breath.)\nThey get <color=#CA2E0AFF>overwhelmed by the wild magic</color>... and become Munak, the Undead. That's what reversing life and death really means.",
    ["Dialogue3650405"]="That's right, you've taken the poisoned fragment of Ymir's Heart, but the curse Forgotten Lake carved into their bodies still lingers. The Undead keep getting washed down from upstream, and the Munak roams endlessly, spreading that damn curse to the living. It's like fate—ninjas trapped in a cycle of death over and over again...",
    ["Dialogue3650406"]="(His sorrow and rage are muffled behind the cold mask—his breathing grows heavy.)\nAnd those old geezers... they think this is what makes ninjas strong. Forgotten Lake devours the souls of the losers, and the winners use their fallen comrades as stepping stones to sharpen their skills...",
    ["Dialogue3650407"]="Yeah, and? We worship strength here. Only the strong get a say. I am powerless before those elders as well. What can your convictions ever hope to change?",
    ["Dialogue3650408"]="As a comrade of Souzo and Ohka, as an Adventurer who still believes in justice, and as my student, you are determined to end this wicked cycle...?",
    ["Dialogue3650409"]="(Akahyo mutters your words, then suddenly chuckles. He raises his hand, summoning two ninja puppets from the sky.)\n—Bold words. I never said you were my student.",
    ["Dialogue3650410"]="Still mourning your friends? If you want to go further on the ninja path...\n(While you hesitate, your blindfolded master sends the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ninja puppets</color> charging at you—faces you once fought side by side.)\n<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>You'll have to cut me down to move forward!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3650501"]="... I lost. You did well. Go on, finish this.\n(Your weapon is at his neck, but he doesn't move. He waits for you to end this.)",
    ["Dialogue3650502"]="I've come to realize that... someone will carry on down this path—a path that ends this cursed evil. You'll go farther than I ever could—clean, honest, and free of all this mess.",
    ["Dialogue3650503"]="(Akahyo grabs your weapon and moves it toward his neck.)\nI'm no longer alone on this path. I've got no regrets.",
    ["Dialogue3650504"]="(The weapon hits the ground. Even your usually emotionless mentor looks confused.)\nWhat are you doing? I don't need your pity. And you—must not cling to such sentiments—it'll only slow you down. Being alone and heartless—that's a ninja's fate.",
    ["Dialogue3650505"]="(As you point to the ninja puppets, Akahyo's voice finally wavers.)\nWhat nonsense are you spouting? I forced you into a duel. I turned their corpses into puppets—they can't even rest in peace. And you call that salvation?",
    ["Dialogue3650506"]="(Maybe it's your words—something inside him shatters. The stern mentor lowers his head and covers his face.)\nYou're right. This way, at least, they won't become those cursed monsters. It was what Nagi wished for...",
    ["Dialogue3650507"]="(He pauses, then looks at you again.)\nBut what does that prove? Or... do you plan to turn me into one of them too?",
    ["Dialogue3650508"]="... You're not going to kill me or raise a blade against your comrade again. And on top of that, you're going to keep climbing to the top of the ninja path—just to face those elders and rip off their rotten masks? To prove that being strong doesn't mean stepping on the corpses of your comrades?",
    ["Dialogue3650509"]="<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>This is... the only way to shatter the curse of Forgotten Lake?</size></color>\n(Your blindfolded mentor stays kneeling, trying to make sense of your words, as you reach out a hand...)",
    ["Dialogue3650510"]="... Heh... ha... HAHAHAHA!",
    ["Dialogue3650511"]="(Akahyo grabs your hand, laughing wildly as he stands.)\nI really underestimated you. I thought a cozy place like Criatura Academy couldn't raise anything sharp. Ninjas are thorny weeds watered in blood. So when Mainz first recommended you to me...",
    ["Dialogue3650512"]="... No. I just spent a long time figuring out how to let you survive this trial and still save face for the academy.",
    ["Dialogue3650513"]="Turns out... I was narrow-minded. The ninja path has stayed hidden too long, stuck in its little world. We ignored how things were changing outside... and almost missed someone like you—a blazing new star.",
    ["Dialogue3650514"]="Let's see what kind of splash a stubborn rock like you makes in still water.\n(He laughs, this time with real admiration.)\nGo on. Don't stop now. Even if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>become a Shinkiro</color>... that's still not the end.",
    ["Dialogue3650614"]="Let's see what kind of splash a stubborn rock like you makes in still water.\n(He laughs, this time with genuine admiration.)\nGo on. Don't stop now. Even if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>become a Shiranui</color>... that's still not the end.",
    ["Dialogue3660201"]="Hohoho! Look at you, Adventurer! You've bulked up since taking the path of martial arts! All those battles did your body good! Seeing you now makes me want to spar a little, too.",
    ["Dialogue3660202"]="Still, the journey of martial arts is endless. To ascend further, seek out your mentor—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Phoenix</color>. It is said he has prepared a class advancement trial for you for some time. Go on, don't keep him waiting!",
    ["Dialogue3660301"]="Whew... just made it in time...",
    ["Dialogue3660302"]="(Phoenix bumps fists with you, totally out of breath.)\n\nSorry, I'm late, kid. Thank you for waiting.",
    ["Dialogue3660303"]="Heh—it's a secret.\n\n(He grins mischievously and smacks your back.)",
    ["Dialogue3660304"]="Alright, time's ticking—let's go! Your fourth class trial is waiting!",
    ["Dialogue3660305"]="Oh, right—almost forgot! Today's trial theme is... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Way of Strength</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Way of Flow</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3660401"]="See those Medusas? First trial—<color=#CA2E0AFF>beat them down</color>. Show me how much you've grown!",
    ["Dialogue3660402"]="(Phoenix bursts out laughing.)\n\nWant to know the trial theme? Too bad! Before you pass the trial, I'm not telling you anything! You'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>figure it out yourself</color>! Let's get moving!",
    ["Dialogue3660501"]="Looks like you figured it out, huh?",
    ["Dialogue3660502"]="Well done! With every punch and kick, your body unleashes more force, adding weight and momentum to each blow. This is the <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>Way of Strength</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3660503"]="Channel your core strength and smash your enemies with full force! The Way of Strength grants you the initiative in many battles—where fate is decided in a heartbeat.",
    ["Dialogue3660504"]="(He proudly pats your shoulder—you can tell he's really happy for you.)\n\nThat's my student! But don't get too full of yourself—there's a tougher trial up next. Come on, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3660601"]="Check it out—my new buddy! Go on, say hi!\n\n(He points at the mutated Stalactic Golem by the totem. You're starting to wonder if you're dreaming.)",
    ["Dialogue3660602"]="(The mutated Stalactic Golem sways like it's waving back at you...)\nRooar!",
    ["Dialogue3660603"]="Hahaha! You two hit it off right away! But it looks like my dear student is confused. Wanna ask why a Stalactic Golem from Comodo Cave is here?",
    ["Dialogue3660604"]="Ahem... That's actually why I was late today—I followed this big guy all the way from Comodo!",
    ["Dialogue3660605"]="This Stalactic Golem traveled across oceans and mountains just to find strong opponents and toughen up its rocky armor. And look at it—it really worked!",
    ["Dialogue3660606"]="<size=26>Ah—such is the romance of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>martial arts</color>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3660607"]="(The Golem wobbles proudly in sync with Phoenix's praise. You have no idea how they're communicating, but the mutual admiration is real...)\n\nRooaaar—",
    ["Dialogue3660608"]="Mastering sheer strength is essential for any martial artist—no exceptions. But now, you and this Stalactic Golem are evenly matched. So, how will you overcome it?",
    ["Dialogue3660609"]="(Phoenix offers a fist bump with a grin.)\n\nGo on—hope you <color=#CA2E0AFF>find your own answer</color> in this fight!",
    ["Dialogue3660701"]="(After the fight, both Phoenix and the Stalactic Golem look at you expectantly.)\n\nSo? Any new insight?",
    ["Dialogue3660702"]="That's right! Throwing a hard punch is easy—but sometimes, brute force holds you back. That's when you switch up your thinking.",
    ["Dialogue3660703"]="To wield the power of flow is to unveil the foe's flaws, dissolve their strikes, and transform their force into their downfall. This is the true essence of martial arts: the perfect blend of hard and soft, using gentleness to overcome rigidity. You've truly grasped it all.",
    ["Dialogue3660704"]="I'm so proud of how far you've come! You've totally got what it takes to be the Sky Emperor now. If there's ever a chance, I'd love to <color=#CA2E0AFF>spar</color> with you...\n\n(He says it casually, but the look in his eyes? He's dead serious. Wait, what...?)",
    ["Dialogue3660705"]="<size=26>Hahahahaha!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3660706"]="(Seeing you flustered, Phoenix bursts out laughing and slings an arm around your shoulder.)\n\nAlright then! It's a promise—we'll have a proper spar someday! But for now... I'll let you off the hook. After all, Wolmas the Archbishop is already waiting to host your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color> at Glast Heim Chivalry!",
    ["Dialogue3670201"]="Hohoho! Look at you, my dear Adventurer! You've gotten stronger again! Come here, let me get a good look at you!\n(The dean's as friendly as ever, waving you over with a relaxed smile.)",
    ["Dialogue3670202"]="(The kindly smile vanishes. His voice weighs heavy.)\nThe fourth class... So you've chosen this path?",
    ["Dialogue3670203"]="Going from Predator to Night Watch isn't just a name change... My child, are you ready for the price it demands?",
    ["Dialogue3670204"]="(The dean sighs and shakes his head.)\nSigh... Find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color>. He used to be a Night Watch—he knows what it means. If you're serious about it, he'll guide you.",
    ["Dialogue3670301"]="Not fast enough.",
    ["Dialogue3670302"]="You're strong. But to walk further down the path of firearms, you've got to pass a new trial.\n(He looks at you, you know he's waiting for your answer.)",
    ["Dialogue3670303"]="(Seeing your resolve, Instructor Miller finally relaxes.)\nNot bad... that's the kind of look I want to see. If there were even a bit of doubt in you, you'd never make it through this trial.",
    ["Dialogue3670304"]="Lately... I've been receiving reports about Glast Heim. Monsters down there are going wild, attacking travelers. We've had dozens of cases—missing people, injured ones. I sent rescue squads, but only a few survivors made it back.",
    ["Dialogue3670305"]="And then... all who survived—without exception—spoke of a voice, <color=#CA2E0AFF>whispering madness from the dark</color> when the monster appeared... And they all saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>girl in a black dress</color> wandering near the Glast Heim Churchyard.",
    ["Dialogue3670306"]="(Instructor Miller totally notices your shocked face, but weirdly, he doesn't ask. Maybe he's just in a hurry.)\nAbout your trial this time... It's to figure out what's going on and fix it. Any questions? No? Then gear up—we're <color=#CA2E0AFF>heading out</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3670401"]="It seems... we are too late.",
    ["Dialogue3670402"]="(With a solemn breath, Instructor Miller leans down to close the terrified eyes of the deceased, then takes the stained name tag from your hand.)\nLeave it to me. We couldn't save him—but we can still send him home...",
    ["Dialogue3670403"]="Wait, you saw her in your third-class advancement trial? So, you think she's also tied to this incident?",
    ["Dialogue3670404"]="(Miller smirks and doesn't confirm or deny your theory about the strange girl. After a brief silence, he meets your eyes.)\nAlright, if that's what you think—go ahead. As your trial overseer, I'll stay here and wait. But heads-up—whatever happens next, I'm not stepping in.",
    ["Dialogue3670405"]="However, the objective of your trial remains unchanged. Whether you save her or take her down, that's up to you. I only care about the result, got it?",
    ["Dialogue3670406"]="Good. Off you go—don't keep me waiting too long.",
    ["Dialogue3670501"]="(She shakes her head, scolding you for being late, then lazily points at the clueless Zombie Prisoners nearby.)\nHa! But it's fine. I guess I should be a bit more generous as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>winner</color> of our little bet!",
    ["Dialogue3670502"]="Look at these pretty little things—King Schmidt used to offer them up as tribute.\n(A small Zombie Prisoner stumbles past; she picks it up like it's a doll, cradling its deformed, rotting face.)",
    ["Dialogue3670503"]="As for me... I've already feasted on their souls!",
    ["Dialogue3670504"]="How long's it been since King Schmidt sent his last tribute? Twenty years? Fifty?",
    ["Dialogue3670505"]="(She tosses aside the Zombie Prisoner and cackles wildly. Your stare only excites her more.)\nHahaha! I've devoured every last one of his people! Think he ever felt guilty? Nah—he never did...",
    ["Dialogue3670506"]="He got what he deserved! Everyone in this kingdom deserves to die—every last one of them! Humans, oh humans... so pathetic and arrogant. Gone at last!\n(Her face twists, her voice distorts—she rants about her glory in a frenzy. It's almost pitiful.)",
    ["Dialogue3670507"]="You... what did you say?\n(She freezes. Her eyes flicker with something unreadable—grief, rage, despair... or something else?)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The people rose for freedom. They stood against the tyrant and built a new world. Though Glast Heim crumbles, it chains no one now...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3670508"]="No! Impossible! This cannot be! <size=26>That tyrant couldn't have died so easily!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3670509"]="(The silence between you stretches on. You can even hear the dew drip from the goddess statue—like a countdown to sunrise. And then she...)\nYou really made up all that for a dumb little bet? Haha... Hahaha! That's hilarious!",
    ["Dialogue3670510"]="(She suddenly erupts in a near-maniacal scream.)\nFeeble, trembling humans! Forever weaving lies to fool the divine!",
    ["Dialogue3670511"]="<size=26>Liars!!! You all <color=#CA2E0AFF>deserve to die</color>!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3670601"]="(She slumps to the ground, dazed and lost. You know it's finally over.)\nWhy... why...?",
    ["Dialogue3670602"]="(She suddenly shudders at your words. Her vacant eyes fix on yours—but they see something far beyond you.)\nName...? No... no! Kill him—kill King Schmidt!",
    ["Dialogue3670603"]="Damn you, King Schmidt, die... die...\n(She keeps muttering, lost in her own world. You suddenly recall the unfinished promise—and you realize...)",
    ["Dialogue3670604"]="The goddess... huh? Yeah, that's right! He betrayed her—framed her! <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>He deserves to die!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3670701"]="(Leaning against the wall, he watches you with a knowing smile.)\nLooks like you kept your promise, huh?",
    ["Dialogue3670702"]="As the successor of Odin's bloodline, you always attract attention. Those who care enough... they pay attention. You don't have to say anything—<color=#CA2E0AFF>we</color> just know.\n(He's vague, but you catch the message.)",
    ["Dialogue3670703"]="Stop tugging on my tail with all those questions. You're still green—I'm not telling you anything at this point. If you really want answers, keep climbing—until you can stand above the rest. I'll be waiting there.",
    ["Dialogue3670704"]="(Instructor Miller folds his arms with a relaxed look—but there's a glint of pride in his eyes.)\nYou know me. I never go in unprepared. Everything you went through—I planned it just for you. Calling in those resources... that's the perk of having power.",
    ["Dialogue3670705"]="Alright, it's time to head to the Glast Heim Chivalry for your Class Advancement Ceremony. This is your first step to the top.",
    ["Dialogue3670801"]="(The corpse is draped in a popular coat favored by many adventurers—he must've been a traveler. His belongings are scattered, with a name tag: Raphael Jones. You and Instructor Miller both know that name—missing person posters for him are all over the city...)",
    ["Dialogue3680101"]="Look at those muscles; you've changed quite a lot! If I, an old geezer, had those kinds of muscles, the title of \"The Most Popular Academy Instructor\" might not necessarily go to Yadrew this year! No need to rush! Let me guess, you're itching to get stronger, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue3680102"]="The way of Taekwon is to defeat your enemies with a tough body and quick movement. You've met Phoenix already, right? He'll teach you how to wield your greatest weapon—your own fists and feet.",
    ["Dialogue3680103"]="A body tempered through hardship gives rise to an unbreakable will. It's that courage that drives every ordinary soul forward. Adventurer, may your journey ever upward bring you the truth you seek.",
    ["Dialogue3680104"]="Or perhaps you'd rather become a Soul Linker? \"They\" will reveal themselves to you, guiding you along the border between life and death. If that's your path, then the Moonstrider in Payon will show you the way.",
    ["Dialogue3680105"]="Beyond life lies the fear called death. Grasp it, master it—then cross that terrifying chasm.",
    ["Dialogue3690101"]="Come with me.",
    ["Dialogue3690102"]="Yes, it's our first meeting. I'm Moonstrider, mentor to the Soul Linker—likely your mentor-to-be as well.",
    ["Dialogue3690103"]="You seem surprised. True, we haven't met before. Don't bother trying to remember when or where... Hm? You're wondering how I know you?",
    ["Dialogue3690104"]="You remember Phoenix, your first-class mentor, don't you? He's been talking constantly about some genius rookie at the academy and plotting every day how to drag you in as his apprentice. After hearing it so often, of course, I'd recognize you... Haha.\n(Thinking of Phoenix's prized prodigy standing right in front of him, Moonstrider lets out a mischievous chuckle.)",
    ["Dialogue3690105"]="Ahem, since you're standing here, that means you've made up your mind to become a Soul Linker. Close your eyes, open your heart, and let your whole body listen to the voice flowing within. Now, question your own resolve.\n(Moonstrider straightens up, his face calm and cool. He taps your forehead lightly, and you close your eyes without thinking.)",
    ["Dialogue3690201"]="Impressive, that went smoother than I expected. You're definitely born for this.",
    ["Dialogue3690202"]="That was your body resonating with the world around you. It's the main reason why Soul Linker can wield spiritual art. You can think of it as \"the world questioning you.\" The rest will unfold as your journey continues.",
    ["Dialogue3690203"]="Alright, time for your first Soul Linker trial. My informant from the west of Payon says monsters there have been acting up lately, attacking travelers and locals for no reason.",
    ["Dialogue3690204"]="Yes, this has caused serious trouble for the local residents. So, go take care of them now.",
    ["Dialogue3690301"]="Those frenzied snakes are almost at the village, and it's worse than expected. No time to waste, let's get started!",
    ["Dialogue3690302"]="I can't help you once the trial starts. Remember to harness the power of resonance you just established with the world. Warm up, and strike when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue3690401"]="How do you feel?",
    ["Dialogue3690402"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>... You managed this much without my guidance? Very impressive, Successor of Odin's Bloodline...</color></size>\nYou're right on the mark. A Soul Linker's power comes from resonating with the world's elemental forces. Through that resonance, you can hear the whispers of all things. Beyond your body, it's your breath that ties you to the world.",
    ["Dialogue3690403"]="When your breath flows in harmony with the pulse of the world, self and nature dissolve into one—and that's when power starts channeling through you. That feeling means you've started drawing on the world's spiritual power. That's the first step to becoming a true Soul Linker.",
    ["Dialogue3690404"]="... Phew, talking this much is tiring. Anyway, keep going with the trial and get better at controlling that power. There's still that rampaging Bigfoot up north waiting for you.\n(Moonstrider sighs in relief and waves you off casually.)",
    ["Dialogue3690501"]="Oh, here you come.",
    ["Dialogue3690502"]="You felt it too? Yeah, I followed that strange aura here, but it vanished around this spot... Huh? You sensed it as well?",
    ["Dialogue3690503"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hmm... You got this far just from the lingering aura? That's beyond my imagination...</color></size>\nAnyway, you're right. This weird energy might be what's driving the forest animals crazy. We can't just let it go.",
    ["Dialogue3690504"]="As for you... you did great. Hardly any novice Soul Linker can sync with their inner spiritual power that perfectly, let alone use it so smoothly in a fight. I'm impressed.",
    ["Dialogue3690505"]="I'll keep tracking this case. Once your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Level reaches 50</color>, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement</color> quest at Prontera Cathedral will unlock for you. After this trial, take a break and get ready for your next battle.",
    ["Dialogue3700101"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Soul Linker.",
    ["Dialogue3700102"]="We here at the Criatura Academy have nothing left to teach you. Congratulations on reaching your potential. However, there's one more thing you need to do before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3700103"]="Turn in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Manual</color>, you no longer need it. I'll give you a new Class Manual for your second class, which doubles as your <color=#CA2E0AFF>graduation certificate</color>, at the ceremony.\n",
    ["Dialogue3710201"]="See that? Today's trial is inside the forest. Go in when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue3710202"]="You're asking why I gave you Soul Linker robes but don't dress like one myself?",
    ["Dialogue3710203"]="(Moonstrider folds his arms and tilts his head up. Even with the blindfold, you can feel his gaze pressing down on you.)\n... So, have you memorized the chants of spiritual art? Recite them twice—today's trial won't be as easy as you think.",
    ["Dialogue3710204"]="Alright then, let's go.",
    ["Dialogue3710301"]="How convenient—saves me the trouble of luring that evil spirit out myself. That's your test for this trial.",
    ["Dialogue3710302"]="That's not the point.\n(Moonstrider clicks his tongue, though from his smirk, he's clearly pleased with his own moves.)",
    ["Dialogue3710303"]="I can feel your spiritual power flowing. See over there? Those souls—they're being chased by a wraith.",
    ["Dialogue3710304"]="That's right—it was a good soul calling out. Huh, you're learning faster than I expected. I should be guiding you through the \"vision\" phase now, but I guess I'll just tell you everything.",
    ["Dialogue3710305"]="When a Soul Linker can freely control their spiritual power, they'll be able to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>another world</color>—the realm of the dead. The living can't sense it, but departed souls linger there for a while, waiting for nature to guide them to eternal rest.",
    ["Dialogue3710306"]="But some souls stay behind because of their obsessions from life. Aside from a few that were evil to begin with, most are \"good souls.\" Still, when those good souls get trapped by their regrets and can't move on...",
    ["Dialogue3710307"]="(Moonstrider pauses. When you look at him curiously, he lets out a faint sigh.)\nWhen that happens... a \"good soul\" turns into an \"evil spirit.\"",
    ["Dialogue3710308"]="Yeah, just like the name says—an evil spirit gets stronger by devouring good ones and wreaks havoc in the world of the living. The one in front of you... it's probably the <color=#CA2E0AFF>root cause</color> of the chaos in Payon.",
    ["Dialogue3710309"]="Hey...",
    ["Dialogue3710310"]="You two over there...",
    ["Dialogue3710311"]="Stop chatting and help! <color=#CA2E0AFF><size=26>Help! Somebody help me!!!</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue3710312"]="Alright, enough panic. Sending good souls to rest and cutting down evil ones—that's the duty of a Soul Linker! Use your talisman and take it down. This fight counts toward your trial score, so take it seriously.",
    ["Dialogue3710401"]="Thank you, kind hero.",
    ["Dialogue3710402"]="... Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue3710403"]="Thank you. But next time, maybe prioritize saving people over chatting...",
    ["Dialogue3710404"]="Let's hope there isn't a next time. Now then, are you ready to go, kind souls? You heard what we said, we're Soul Linkers.",
    ["Dialogue3710405"]="Hmm... Yeah, we're ready...",
    ["Dialogue3710406"]="Ah, it's dangerous to stay in this world... Forget it. That giant cloudy-fluffy-spicy-salad I've been craving... I'll just save it for my next life. I'll go take a nap now.\n",
    ["Dialogue3710407"]="Hopeless idiot...",
    ["Dialogue3710408"]="Then, see you in the next life. I'll treat you to that... cloud-whatever salad next time, alright?\n(Moonstrider holds a talisman between his fingers and waves gently; the chattering souls fade away like the wind.)",
    ["Dialogue3710409"]="I'm not sure.",
    ["Dialogue3710410"]="You're saying that the evil spirit has some kind of dark power, not something from the soul itself? Yeah... that does seem to be the case. We can assume there's someone behind the scenes pulling the strings—maybe even the one who created and raised that spirit.",
    ["Dialogue3710411"]="Dragging good souls back from the Realm of the Dead... and turning them into killers...\n(Moonstrider frowns, lost in thought for a while, then finally looks up at you.)",
    ["Dialogue3710412"]="We'll need proof to confirm that... Anyway, you did great in this trial. You can go join the academy's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color> now. But don't slack off—being a Soul Linker only gets tougher from here.",
    ["Dialogue3710413"]="Go on, my best student.",
    ["Dialogue3710501"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now, we can hold a formal Class Advancement Ceremony.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3720201"]="Hohoho! Well, look who it is—our little Adventurer! You've grown into a real Soul Reaper! And already it's time for your Fourth Advancement trial. That sneaky Moonstrider has already arranged your trial. Go on, kid.",
    ["Dialogue3720301"]="?!\n(Moonstrider suddenly appears right in front of you, looking shocked. Or... was he there the whole time, and your eyes were somehow blinded? When did that happen?!)",
    ["Dialogue3720302"]="(Seeing you ready your weapon, Moonstrider lets out a cold snort.)\nWhat's this? You're planning to turn on your mentor before even becoming a real Soul Ascetic?",
    ["Dialogue3720303"]="You mean... We've walked right into someone else's formation without noticing? Well... actually...\n(Moonstrider's usually calm face shows a rare hint of embarrassment as he looks away.)",
    ["Dialogue3720304"]="... This formation was actually mine.",
    ["Dialogue3720305"]="Once you become a Soul Ascetic, you'll be walking between life and death a lot more. Things will get dangerous, so you'll need sharp senses to tell who's alive, who's dead, and who's your enemy.",
    ["Dialogue3720306"]="So I made a formation that conceals the presence of living, to train your senses. If you can find the right path in this maze of fake energy without hurting any living thing, you'll pass the trial.",
    ["Dialogue3720307"]="But it looks like... someone deliberately tampered with my formation and turned it into a death trap. Heh... guess the hunter's become the hunted. There's no helping it—let's pause the trial, I'll get you out of here first.",
    ["Dialogue3720308"]="... Oh? You want to turn the tables and lure them out, huh?\n(Moonstrider lowers his head, thinking for a moment.)\nWell, not a bad idea. With me around, nothing major will go wrong. Alright then—let's move.",
    ["Dialogue3720401"]="... You're... Frostveil?!",
    ["Dialogue3720402"]="Moon-Moonstrider? Did... Did I hurt you?",
    ["Dialogue3720403"]="Yes, it's me. Calm down, Frostveil. We're fine.",
    ["Dialogue3720404"]="Moonstrider... My sister... she died... and came back...",
    ["Dialogue3720405"]="... Frostveil, Leafshade's already at rest. She's free from pain now.",
    ["Dialogue3720406"]="She's Frostveil's sister, also my childhood friend. When she was sixteen, she died in an accident... but not long after, she returned, twisted into something monstrous. Around that time, the elders also discovered that a fragment of the Soul Linker's secret art had been stolen. Maybe that's how she came back.",
    ["Dialogue3720407"]="(Moonstrider gives a wry smile and nods.)\n... Yeah, you guessed right—it was me. Leafshade and I grew up together, and her life ended so suddenly when we were sixteen. How could I accept that? So I stole the village's secret art and tried to bring back the soul that should've moved on...",
    ["Dialogue3720408"]="Maybe those old geezers in the village never imagined it—the ancient secret art, incomplete and useless for centuries, ended up being finished by some reckless kid. After that... yeah, just like you guessed, I desecrated Leafshade's life and brought back a monster that knew only killing. Her soul was in torment... in the end, she even begged me to end her suffering...!",
    ["Dialogue3720409"]="... Yeah. I granted Leafshade her final wish, but after that, I couldn't face the village anymore. I left Frostveil, who was still young, with the elders and wandered the world until I met Dean Mainz. I thought I'd never see anyone from my past again... but Frostveil—why is he here now?",
    ["Dialogue3720410"]="Secret art... I... fell... ground... ah—hurt—\n(As Frostveil whimpers, something slips from his body and falls to the ground by his feet...)",
    ["Dialogue3720501"]="Let me see.\n(He takes the ancient tome from your hands, his brow suddenly furrowing.)",
    ["Dialogue3720502"]="Yeah... It's the missing fragment of the secret art. But back then, after finishing the ritual, I handed it back to the elders, and I even saw them seal it away. No... this isn't the same one I knew. Some parts... they're different...\n(Moonstrider flips through the pages quickly, his face deepening with concern.)",
    ["Dialogue3720503"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>No casting medium...? That means the spell could trigger at any moment... just like a bomb. Did someone else tamper with the secret art after me? But who...?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3720504"]="Moonstrider... Ahh...\n(The monster lets out a rasping wail, breaking Moonstrider's thoughts.)\nI... want... to die... like a person...",
    ["Dialogue3720505"]="So this is... the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cost</color> of defying the natural order?",
    ["Dialogue3720506"]="... You need to remember this too. As a Soul Linker, we walk by the power of nature's order. The most important thing is to respect the cycle of all life and death. \"Resurrection,\" at its core, is just forcing a soul to stay inside a rotting shell... It is a lesson carved into me... by the life of my beloved.",
    ["Dialogue3720507"]="(Moonstrider's voice trembles as he slowly lifts his weapon and looks at Frostveil.)\nFrostveil, all of this happened because of me. You did nothing wrong. I'm sorry... that you have to walk the same path as Leafshade...",
    ["Dialogue3720508"]="You mean... you'll do it?\n(Moonstrider looks surprised, but clearly feels your sincerity. He lowers his weapon and gently pats your shoulder.)\nPlease... make it quick... let Frostveil drift into sleep free of pain.",
    ["Dialogue3720601"]="Frostveil...",
    ["Dialogue3720602"]="(The wraith fades under your purification. Frostveil's weakened soul regains a brief moment of clarity. In his final moments, he looks at Moonstrider...)\nMoonstrider... I've always wanted to see you again.",
    ["Dialogue3720603"]="Back then... I had no right to blame you. I once thought about stealing the secret art too. You just acted before I did... None of us knew the price of reversing life and death would be so cruel. If I ever resented you for killing my sister, then now... all I feel is gratitude—that you freed me, so I can finally see her again...",
    ["Dialogue3720604"]="... I'm sorry. I couldn't save either of your... or Leafshade...",
    ["Dialogue3720605"]="You don't need to apologize, Moonstrider. What matters now is your task—it's far more important than anything. The secret art fragment I carry isn't the same one you gave the elders back then...",
    ["Dialogue3720606"]="...Yes, I noticed. Did you rewrite the secret art, Frostveil? But why conceal the casting medium? That means it <color=#CA2E0AFF>could go off at any time</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3720607"]="(Under your gaze, Frostveil slowly shakes his head.)\nIt wasn't me. The real one... was <color=#CA2E0AFF>stolen</color>. I left our village to reclaim it from the one who took it.",
    ["Dialogue3720608"]="What...?!",
    ["Dialogue3720609"]="I followed him north. Along the way, I saw innocent people—just like my sister—dragged back from \"that world,\" turned into raging monsters. I tried to catch him, but he tricked me, pretended to lose, handed me a false fragment, and lured me right into a den of monsters...",
    ["Dialogue3720610"]="In my panic, the secret art activated. I got tangled up with that wraith... it took over my body. All this time, I've watched it slaughter the innocent and couldn't stop it... But thank goodness—I met you...!",
    ["Dialogue3720611"]="Moonstrider, back then... I had no right to blame you. None of us knew the price of reversing life and death would be so cruel. If I ever resented you for killing my sister, then now... all I feel is gratitude—that you freed me, so I can finally see her again...",
    ["Dialogue3720612"]="(Frostveil's voice fades, his soul beginning to fade into the thin air...)\nMoonstrider... please... You have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the secret art</color>...! Don't let anyone else end up like me and my sister...!",
    ["Dialogue3720613"]="... I promise. Frostveil, rest in peace now, with Leafshade.",
    ["Dialogue3720614"]="(As Frostveil's spirit fades, Moonstrider lets out a long sigh into the lonely wind.)\nSometimes I wish... there really was a next life.",
    ["Dialogue3720615"]="Of course I do. But... <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>who knows? Maybe it's better if we never meet again...</color></size>\n(Moonstrider gives a small, bitter smile, then pats your shoulder.)\n... Anyway, enough of that. You did great on today's trial.",
    ["Dialogue3720616"]="You did way better than I expected. By now, you should understand that being a Soul Linker isn't just about a strong body or mind. It's about respecting life itself. Only when you truly revere all living things can you draw on their strength. Don't make the same mistakes I did... ones you can never undo.",
    ["Dialogue3720617"]="... I'll never forget the mistake I made ten years ago. Even now, though I teach at the academy, I'm still walking my road of atonement. So... if you don't want a sinner as your mentor, I'll understand. I'll just write down your training plan, and you can—",
    ["Dialogue3720618"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hah... You...</color></size>\n(Moonstrider pauses, then lets out a soft sigh.)\n... Alright. Thank you. I truly believe you'll go farther than I ever did on the path of spiritual art.",
    ["Dialogue3720619"]="Alright then—go join the academy's Class Advancement Ceremony with pride. Next time we meet, you'll be a full-fledged Soul Ascetic!",
    ["Dialogue3800101"]="Huh? Adventurer? What brings you here all of a sudden?",
    ["Dialogue3800102"]="Hey, I'm looking through some old photo albums and just realized it's almost the anniversary of when I met Margaret and Seyren. I think I'll make some albums as gifts for them while they're away.",
    ["Dialogue3800103"]="More than a long time—we've known each other since we were born, grew up together, and everything!",
    ["Dialogue3800104"]="... Adventurer? Are you feeling okay?",
    ["Dialogue3800105"]="You don't look so good... did something happen? Or am I just talking too much again? Come on, tell me—I can help share a little of that worry!",
    ["Dialogue3800106"]="(Parni smiles, clasping her hands together, ready to listen.)\nWe're friends, so don't hold back—just tell me...",
    ["Dialogue3800107"]="Are you saying...",
    ["Dialogue3800108"]="Margaret and Seyren... <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>got into an accident!?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3800109"]="Don't jest about such things...",
    ["Dialogue3800201"]="This is...\n(Parni holds the keepsakes her friends left behind, silent for a long while.)",
    ["Dialogue3800202"]="I...",
    ["Dialogue3800203"]="(The shock still lingers in Parni's mind. She chokes back a sob, then looks up at you.)\nSorry... I lost my composure. Let me just gather these scattered photos first, okay?",
    ["Dialogue3800204"]="You'll help with the photos? Then I'll leave it to you... I'll try to snap out of it soon.",
    ["Dialogue3800205"]="(Parni's eyes are red. She bites her lip, forcing herself to calm down before turning aside.)\nOkay... I understand.",
    ["Dialogue3800301"]="(In the photo's center is a giant chocolate parfait. You recall it as a famous dessert everyone was crazy about in Prontera a few years ago.\nParni was in front, holding the camera at an angle, while Margaret peeked from behind the parfait, both giggling and flashing peace signs.)",
    ["Dialogue3800401"]="(A blurry photo—it barely shows young Seyren and Parni wrestling with a small Poring, while half of Margaret's body is visible as she seemed to drop the camera in a hurry to help her clumsy friends.)",
    ["Dialogue3800501"]="(In this photo, teenage Margaret and Seyren stood beneath a Wishing Tree, both blushing and shouting something—everyone knew how they felt, yet they hadn't confessed. You can't figure out what they were saying back then.)",
    ["Dialogue3800601"]="Whoa, Margaret! You finally said it! I was dying waiting for you two to just admit it!",
    ["Dialogue3800602"]="Who are you? How do you even know us?\n(They look at you with youthful, curious faces—so much younger than the friends you remember. Better think of a quick excuse.)",
    ["Dialogue3800603"]="Oh? So you're just a passing Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3800604"]="That's weird... how would a random Adventurer know our names?",
    ["Dialogue3800605"]="Seriously! We haven't caused any trouble lately—who's out to get us this time?\n(This young, lively Parni is so different from the composed Exorcist Priestess she'll grow into—you can't help but smile at her.)",
    ["Dialogue3800606"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Hmm, an Adventurer...</color>\nThat's right! An Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3800607"]="Judging by your look, you're one of those super-experienced Adventurers, right? The kind who can finish any quest with just a snap of your fingers! Am I right, am I right?!",
    ["Dialogue3800608"]="Yay! I knew there was always a way out—",
    ["Dialogue3800609"]="Then help Margaret solve her biggest problem right now! <size=18>This is my once-in-a-lifetime request!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3800610"]="Par-Parni... Wait...!",
    ["Dialogue3800611"]="Don't worry! This Adventurer and I hit it off right away—everything's gonna be okay! Trust me!\n(Even as she says that, Parni keeps glancing your way, clearly hinting for you to step aside and talk privately.)",
    ["Dialogue3800701"]="Of course it's about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> having feelings for Margaret too! Oh, maybe you didn't know—Seyren's the one Margaret likes! These two idiots, honestly! Without me serving justice, they'd never confess—",
    ["Dialogue3800702"]="I don't want them turning into old Granpa and Granny still hung up on each other! Their happiness shall be ours to defend!\n(Parni grabs your hands tightly, eyes blazing with determination.)",
    ["Dialogue3800703"]="Alright, hero! No more hesitating, we must act now! A bouquet is the spear of love—absolutely essential! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pick some flowers</color> now, and I'll dash into town to buy ribbons! Let's split up!",
    ["Dialogue3800801"]="Then... I'll accept these flowers. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue3800802"]="Sorry for dragging you into this... Yeah, I do like Seyren. But I'm not sure this is the right thing to do. What if he doesn't feel the same? Wouldn't confessing just make things awkward?",
    ["Dialogue3800803"]="And we're both busy preparing for our exams... I'd hate to mess up his focus. Maybe I'm overthinking it, huh? How foolish of me, haha!",
    ["Dialogue3800804"]="Huh—Adventurer, you sound like you've known me for a long time? I...\n(Margaret pauses, suddenly recognizing the familiar footsteps behind her.)",
    ["Dialogue3800805"]="Parni? Why aren't you coming?",
    ["Dialogue3800901"]="I... I heard everything. I'm sorry, Margaret. I got too excited and didn't think about how you'd feel...",
    ["Dialogue3800902"]="Pfft—",
    ["Dialogue3800903"]="Hey, what are you laughing at...",
    ["Dialogue3800904"]="You look cute when you're feeling down. Honestly, I agree with you—it's hard to express feelings when you're worried about the outcome. If I keep holding back and never speak of it, it'll only get harder, and I might lose the courage to speak up.",
    ["Dialogue3800905"]="Then...",
    ["Dialogue3800906"]="That's right! I'll talk to Seyren properly! If he gets mad, I'll just apologize later!",
    ["Dialogue3800907"]="(Hearing that, Parni nearly jumps up, shouting.)\nOh, come on! The chance of Seyren having no feeling for you is slimmer than I'm the <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>King Poring!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3800908"]="(While Margaret looks away, flustered, Parni tugs your sleeve and whispers quietly.)\nAdventurer, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3800909"]="(Lower her voice)\nShe's acting all cheerful, but I bet she's super nervous inside. Could you go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> and tell him to meet her at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wishing Tree</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3800910"]="I swear, really—there's no way Seyren doesn't like her! You won't be wasting your time!",
    ["Dialogue3800911"]="Hmm... he's probably training at the Poring Ruins now.",
    ["Dialogue3800912"]="Adventurer, just look for a guy with <color=#CA2E0AFF>gray hair and gray eyes</color>, holding a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Knightly Sword</color> and looking a bit clueless—that's Seyren for sure!",
    ["Dialogue3800913"]="Come on, what if I mess up and say something dumb? Please, please! Let's meet at the Wishing Tree later—I'll bring Margaret there!",
    ["Dialogue3801001"]="You are...?\n(Noticing your approach with an odd expression, Seyren's hand tightens on his sword.)",
    ["Dialogue3801002"]="Wh-what...? Go—to the Wishing Tree? Uh, okay! Okay, I got it!\n(He stammers nervously, hands fidgeting and cheeks burning red. You can't help but think of how he'll become one day.)",
    ["Dialogue3801003"]="But... I haven't finished my quest yet! I need to complete the assignment for my knight exam first! I'll finish it quickly so I won't keep Margaret waiting!",
    ["Dialogue3801004"]="The deadline's not until next month, but I want to finish early and ask for more training to become stronger...",
    ["Dialogue3801005"]="Sorry, what did you say?",
    ["Dialogue3801006"]="Wh-Why am I so obsessed with the knight exam? I... I really do want to be a knight—it's my biggest dream. And also...",
    ["Dialogue3801007"]="(Under your intense stare, Seyren clasps his hands, turning away. After a long pause, he mutters softly.)\nMargaret is amazing. I just want to...",
    ["Dialogue3801008"]="I still need to help clear out <color=#CA2E0AFF>three types of monsters</color>... Wait, what—you're helping me? No, no, it's my quest, I've gotta do it myself!",
    ["Dialogue3801009"]="Huh? Picking flowers? Wait—what kind of flowers?! <size=18>Adventurer! Hey, don't just walk away!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3801101"]="Adventurer! You're back already...?\n(Seyren practically jumps up, hiding a broken flower behind his back as he offers you a fresh bouquet.)",
    ["Dialogue3801102"]="N-no, nothing! Are these flowers okay? They're all the ones Margaret likes—I think she'll love them.",
    ["Dialogue3801103"]="Still... I really think I should do my own quests... Sorry, I'll stop talking. Please don't give me that look...",
    ["Dialogue3801201"]="Look who finally decided to show up? It's our busy guy!",
    ["Dialogue3801202"]="Parni...",
    ["Dialogue3801203"]="Parni...",
    ["Dialogue3801204"]="(Both of them look shyly at Parni for help, but she shrugs and pretends not to notice.)\nHey, stop staring at me! I'm leaving!",
    ["Dialogue3801205"]="(Whisper)\nAdventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me!</color>",
    ["Dialogue3801301"]="So? How'd it go? Everything okay?",
    ["Dialogue3801302"]="Heh-heh! Told you so! Now we just wait from a distance for their good news!",
    ["Dialogue3801303"]="...\n(Seyren hides the bouquet behind him, staring at the ground but sneaking glances at Margaret.)",
    ["Dialogue3801304"]="...\n(Margaret hugs the bouquet, staring off to the side. The words on her lips never make it out.)",
    ["Dialogue3801305"]="These two idiots...",
    ["Dialogue3801306"]="<size=18>YOU—TWO—! Just say it already!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3801307"]="(Apparently encouraged, they both speak at once.)\nSeyren! I—",
    ["Dialogue3801308"]="Margaret! I—",
    ["Dialogue3801309"]="Whoa! I've got to take a ton of photos of this moment!",
    ["Dialogue3801310"]="<size=26>I'll become the strongest knight! You should keep working hard too!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3801311"]="<size=26>I'll become the best priestess! You'll be a good knight too!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3801312"]="...\n(Parni's face freezes. You've never seen her look this speechless—now or ever.)",
    ["Dialogue3801313"]="Unreal! Absolutely fools! Both of them!!! I'm taking a photo—I'll mock you two for <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>the rest of your lives</color>!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3801314"]="(Flustered, Parni accidentally flings her camera, but you manage to catch it before it hits the ground.)\nAdventurer! Hit the shutter!",
    ["Dialogue3801401"]="Adventurer, are you okay? You suddenly fainted... You really weren't feeling well, huh?\n(Parni looks at you with worried eyes, red-rimmed and still damp with tears.)",
    ["Dialogue3801402"]="You've entered a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dimensional Gap</color> anchored to this photo by strong emotion?\n(Parni looks at the photo you handed her, wishing she could meet her friends again in the past, but fate denies her that mercy.)",
    ["Dialogue3801403"]="... Adventurer, I want to place Margaret's hairband and Seyren's pocket watch under the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wishing Tree</color>. Could you... come with me?",
    ["Dialogue3801404"]="Thanks. I don't need any more rest. There's something more important to do. Let's go.",
    ["Dialogue3801501"]="This was the gift I gave them after we passed our first exam. I saved up for a long time to buy them. Moments like that always made me believe we'd be together—forever.",
    ["Dialogue3801502"]="Yeah... if those two saw me like this, they'd definitely say, \"Parni, don't be sad—live happily, no matter what.\" Ha... kind of a cruel thing to say, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue3801503"]="(Parni clasps her trembling hands, eyes shut as she whispers a prayer.)\nO Odin, who reigns in merciful heaven—gaze upon these kindred spirits. Bless their pure hearts, guide them skyward, not into shadow, and clothe them in thy radiant shroud, granting them eternal rest in thy light.",
    ["Dialogue3801504"]="I don't want to say goodbye. I believe we'll meet again when I reach my destination.",
    ["Dialogue3880101"]="Sorry to bother you during your break, Adventurer. I know that you have been helping us to deal with the mutinous androids around the clock recently and haven't gotten a good rest. But unfortunately, we just received an urgent request from St. Caviderina Welfare Center...",
    ["Dialogue3880102"]="Yes. It's a social welfare institute located at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>eastside of Kiel Khayr's Academy</color>, dedicated to housing orphans, and jointly sponsored by the Republic and the Khayr Consortium. Of course, there are on-duty staff in the center, but if they encounter unsolvable problems, they may also report to the Republic Guard, and we will send our people to deal with them. So...",
    ["Dialogue3880103"]="A kid went <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing</color>. But I haven't gotten a chance to get into the details. You know, our guards have been stretched thin recently, struggling to main law and order in the city. We can't even spare any manpower to respond to such requests. Adventurer, if you are willing to help, can you run this errand for me?",
    ["Dialogue3880104"]="Thank you, Adventurer. And don't forget to take this. It's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Welfare Support Funds</color> from the government, issued to the welfare center quarterly. Please give this to the institute director on my behalf. Uh, as for the books and fruits here...",
    ["Dialogue3880105"]="(Andrew lowers his head, pointing to the package beside him.)\nWell, my little gifts for the children. Please bring these to the kids in the welfare center and send my regards to them.",
    ["Dialogue3880106"]="Oh, by the way, I have good news for you. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>temporary residence permit</color> you applied for has been approved! Once you're done with this request, just go take a look at your new place and <color=#CA2E0AFF>get settled down</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue3880201"]="(Following Andre's instruction, you arrive at the institute located on the east side of Kiel Khayr's Academy. In front of the building stands a man, who seems to be expecting you for quite a while.)\nGreetings, esteemed visitor. Do you... happen to bring the welfare support funds for this quarter?",
    ["Dialogue3880202"]="Oh, pardon me! Allow me to introduce myself. I'm the Director of St. Caviderina Welfare Center, responsible for all related affairs to the center's operations. The guards have informed me that an Adventurer will come here today to deliver the <color=#CA2E0AFF>welfare support funds</color>... I guess it must be you, right?",
    ["Dialogue3880203"]="So... Did you... bring the money?\n(The director's greedy expression makes you a little displeased, but thinking of Andre's commission, you still hand over the <color=#CA2E0AFF>envelope</color> to him.)",
    ["Dialogue3880301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>...48, 49, 50... Tsk! It's too little...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3880302"]="Oh! You want to ask about that troublemaker <color=#CA2E0AFF>Martistine</color>? I already told the guards about her. That kid runs away all the time, but usually, she just disappears for a while. When dinner is served, she comes back by herself. No need to be this serious!",
    ["Dialogue3880303"]="It... Has it been a day? Weird, this is longer than usual...\n(Apparently, the director isn't sure about his answer. Seeing your face turning increasingly serious, perhaps, he lets out a few coughs to cover up his uncertainty.)",
    ["Dialogue3880304"]="Ahem, dear Adventurer... Don't get me wrong. I'm just too busy with my routine work, having no time to attend to the children personally. Their daily routines are taken care of by Auntie Cook and the teaching staff. I feel sorry that something like this has happened... B-But, if it worries you a lot, how about you go ask around? I... I have nothing to do with this, umm, incident...",
    ["Dialogue3880305"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let's be real. None of those higher-ups cares about the lives of these kids... They're born and dumped immediately into this rathole filled with radiation. Just making it through another day is already a blessing...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3880401"]="<size=26>...Where's their conscience gone?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3880402"]="What's the matter? Look at these poor little kids! They can only eat spoiled rubbish! And even the rubbish has a quota! And you bunch, how dare you hide in your fancy room, enjoying your meaty feast?",
    ["Dialogue3880403"]="Not what? I've seen people like you. Claiming to deliver the welfare support funds, you must have split the money with that greedy old bastard right under the table! And don't even get me started on the supplies and food the government provided... I can bet: Everything ends up in your pockets!",
    ["Dialogue3880404"]="(You tell Auntie Cook everything about Andre's commission. While you're speaking, she seems to calm down a bit, but still harboring doubts.)\n...You said you're not with those people? Why should I believe you?",
    ["Dialogue3880405"]="...Fine, since you're saying that, then help me out with the ingredients. As you can see, there are over a dozen kids in the welfare center, and I prepare every single meal all by myself. Plus, that cheapskate is cutting my food budget...",
    ["Dialogue3880406"]="(Auntie Cook gives you a gesture, and following the direction of her finger, you find some rotting vegetables and ground meat on the cutting board, emitting a foul odor.)\nThese things... Can't even feed the kids. Luckily, the fields around here, despite being barren, can produce something to eat. Now turn around. Do you see the forest over there?",
    ["Dialogue3880407"]="Go there and get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>tree roots</color>. Also, look for those round-shaped robots nearby. They are abandoned by the Khayr Consortium. If you happen to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crude Engine Oil</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fireflowing Core</color> on them, bring them back as well.",
    ["Dialogue3880408"]="...Eat, or die. These kids have no choice, and neither do I. Enough talk. Going or not, it's your call, Adventurer.\n(With that, she says no more and simply focuses on tossing the ingredients from her cutting board into a water bucket, carefully cleaning the rotten parts...)",
    ["Dialogue3880409"]="(The young Auntie Cook is beyond mad. You even think she is going to crack open your head with her spatula.)\n<size=26>How come you still have the appetite?</size>",
    ["Dialogue3880501"]="...Good. We have our meal for tonight.",
    ["Dialogue3880502"]="...It's edible.\n(Auntie Cook appears to have predicted your uncertainty and her straightforward response makes you feel as if you're the one out of place.)\nBelieve it or not, this is how these kinds and I have managed to survive all these years.",
    ["Dialogue3880503"]="Alright, don't bother yourself with the ingredients. I guess you are here for Martistine?",
    ["Dialogue3880504"]="Sorry, I don't know... And I don't really care.\n(To your surprise, even Auntie Cook, who cares so much about making good meals for the children, shows a hint of disdain when you mention Martistine.)",
    ["Dialogue3880505"]="That troublemaker is not welcome here. This is not the first time she has run away, and I bet it won't be the last time, either. Oh, if you are commissioned to look for her, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask those kids playing in front of the sandpit</color>. Because the last time I saw Martistine, she was arguing with those kids. Petra even gave them a good scolding for it...",
    ["Dialogue3880506"]="She is the only teacher here and probably the closest person to the kids. You can go talk with her sometime. Maybe you'll find some useful information.",
    ["Dialogue3880601"]="Ms. Petra said that a pizza should be round-shaped, and there should be lots of meat on top... Huh? What? Why is it getting dark all of a sudden?\n(The little girl playing in the sandpit blinks. As she looks up, she soon starts frowning the moment her eyes meet yours.)\nYou, don't stand there... You are blocking all the sunlight!",
    ["Dialogue3880602"]="...Play? But I'm not playing...\n(She stares at the sand in her hand confusingly, then suddenly widens her eyes.)\nI get it! Are you hungry too?",
    ["Dialogue3880603"]="Let's make a pizza together! I'll give you a slice when it's done!",
    ["Dialogue3880701"]="It's finally done... I'm starving. Can we start eating it now?",
    ["Dialogue3880702"]="Of course, let me split the pizza for everyone: This is for Max; this is for Ms. Petra; and I'm saving this for Auntie Cook...\n(The girl discreetly pushes a slice of sand-made pie to you.)\nAnd here's yours! I promised to give you a slice!",
    ["Dialogue3880703"]="You are welcome! Then, let's dig in—",
    ["Dialogue3880704"]="I am going to eat my pizza now—\n(Max grabbed the \"pizza\" slice and eagerly sent it into his mouth. You thought they were just playing house, but then you see Max takes a good bite of the \"pizza.\")\n...Hmm! Pizza... So the pizza tastes like this?",
    ["Dialogue3880705"]="Huh? What...? Why not?",
    ["Dialogue3880706"]="Pizza... (sobbing). My pizza is broken... I-I want my pizza...\n(The girl sobs softly and blames you for destroying the \"food\" she made.)\nI am hungry... I <color=#CA2E0AFF>want something to eat</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3880801"]="Ms. Petra said that there are many delicious things up in the sky... So it's true...\n(The little boy finished the fruits you gave him, sucking his fingers with a longing look on his face.)",
    ["Dialogue3880802"]="I am not hungry anymore! Thank you so much for giving me something so delicious! Loti likes you! Loti wants to be your friend!",
    ["Dialogue3880803"]="Hmm... You want to know why we argued with Martistine, right? Because she <color=#CA2E0AFF>broke Max's and my castle</color>! We worked so hard and spent a lot of time on it... With that castle, I can become a princess, wearing nice dresses, eating a lot of candies, and having someone tuck me in with a bedtime story... But my castle collapsed! Ruined by Martistine's robot...",
    ["Dialogue3880804"]="Don't be sad, Loti... We can just make another castle. Ms. Petra has promised, that the new castle only belongs to us... As for Martistine, that bad girl, she only deserves to sleep outside the castle, and she will never become a princess!",
    ["Dialogue3880805"]="O-Of course! She's always getting scolded! And not only Ms. Petra dislikes her! The director doesn't like her, either. So I don't like her... And no one likes her!",
    ["Dialogue3880806"]="Yes! And you! You can't make friends with Martistine, either! If... <color=#CA2E0AFF>If you become her friend, then we won't play with you anymore</color>!\n(The little girl puts her hands behind her back, acting like an adult. She doesn't even realize how terrible are the things coming out of her mouth.)",
    ["Dialogue3880807"]="Why am I supposed to know the whereabouts of that nuisance! Maybe she is somewhere, fighting with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Logan</color> again... Hmph! I hope she never comes back!",
    ["Dialogue3880901"]="<size=26>Hey! Who are you?</size>",
    ["Dialogue3880902"]="Bully? Hah! Those fools deserve it! They should have known that mixing these things together would attract monsters! Idiots! They don't deserve to sit on the rocking chair!",
    ["Dialogue3880903"]="Of course!\n(Logan raises his head proudly, like a victorious little rooster.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Martistine</color> once said about this recipe, and I memorized it!",
    ["Dialogue3880904"]="<size=18>Ug-oh... Crap...</size>\nNo... no! I read it from a book! This has nothing to do with Martistine! The director said she's a liar and never speaks the truth, so we shouldn't trust her at all!",
    ["Dialogue3880905"]="<size=26>Ugh, you're getting on my nerves! Stop asking!</size>\n(He interrupts you quickly and pulls out a weird <color=#CA2E0AFF>paste-like substance</color> from his pocket, which looks quite similar to the one he used to attract the monster before.)\nGet lost! Or I'll smash you with this!",
    ["Dialogue3881001"]="<size=26>...Ouch! Ouch! Let go of me!</size>\n(Taking advantage of your physical strength, you easily nab Logan by the ear, ready to teach him a thing or two.)",
    ["Dialogue3881002"]="Forgive me... Please forgive me! I will never use this thing again! I promise to throw everything away—\n(Logan hurriedly turns his pocket inside out, and lots of strange stuff falls out, including the paste-like substance that attracts monsters.)",
    ["Dialogue3881003"]="Fine! I will! (Sobbing) Can you let go of me now...",
    ["Dialogue3881004"]="(Your \"physical persuasion\" seems to work. Logan, who has always been tough, suddenly bursts into crying.)\nI... I didn't mean to! But if I don't pick on others, someone will start to pick on me!",
    ["Dialogue3881005"]="Director... The director said it... Hic! He said in such a lowlife-crowded place, only the law of the jungle prevails! If one doesn't fight for their needs, they will always be at the bottom of the food chain! Wah...",
    ["Dialogue3881006"]="...It's not that I'll be bullied if I don't bully others. Instead, <color=#CA2E0AFF>I'll be bullied because I've bullied others</color>...?\n(Logan repeats your words in a daze. For someone his age, understanding this sort of thing might be too much.)\nUmm... It's so confusing... I don't get it...",
    ["Dialogue3881007"]="(You put the <color=#CA2E0AFF>enlightenment books</color> Andre prepared <color=#CA2E0AFF>into Logan's hands</color>, yet he's still looking displeased.)\n...What's good about reading? Ms. Petra has read all the books in the world... And she's still stuck with us in this welfare center. So is Martistine! She has lots of weird knowledge... But no one wants to be her friend!",
    ["Dialogue3881008"]="I... I don't know... Frankly speaking, no one here cares whether she's alive or dead! You know, she's got two powerful robots as her bodyguards. No one can actually bully her...",
    ["Dialogue3881009"]="And... If you want information about Martistine, you'd better ask Ms. Petra! I heard that she scolded Martistine really bad this morning. And then she's gone... Hmm. She's probably hiding somewhere, crying like a baby, I guess. What a troublesome nuisance...",
    ["Dialogue3881010"]="(You couldn't help but notice that when Logan's speaking, his eyes seem shifty, nervously looking at the center's wall behind.)\n<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>There's nothing to worry about... She'll be back in no time...</size></color>",
    ["Dialogue3881101"]="...Okay. That's it for today. Wash your hands and get ready to eat... Huh? You are...?",
    ["Dialogue3881102"]="I see. So you're the Adventurer commissioned to search for Martistine, right? I'm sorry... Even though I'm the reason she ran away, I really don't know where she is.",
    ["Dialogue3881103"]="Martistine is a very... special kid. When she first came here, everyone thought she was from a prestigious family, not only because of her fine dresses but also because she was accompanied by <color=#CA2E0AFF>two robots engraved with the logo of Rekenber Corp</color>. At that time, she claimed that her parents were senior managers of Rekenber Corp, so our director went to all lengths to search for her parents, hoping for generous compensation in return...",
    ["Dialogue3881104"]="Not long after, however, the director's pipedream was busted: No one had ever come here to claim this kid. As time went on, he no longer believed the words from Martistine and even labeled her as a \"bad investment.\" In this welfare center, you know, everyone needs to live at the mercy of the director. If he doesn't like her, then we have to isolate her, lest we get ourselves into trouble. As for Martistine, she has pride and arrogance in herself...",
    ["Dialogue3881105"]="(The young teacher sighs deeply. You can tell that she feels guilty about this.)\nThis morning, the kids were playing near the sandpit and didn't want Martistine to join them. Then she ordered her robots to crush the castle, where the other kids had invested so much effort and time! I was so mad at that time, so I scolded her...",
    ["Dialogue3881106"]="...Yes, that was the last time I saw Martistine. She didn't show up for lunch today either. I was a bit concerned, so I asked the director to call the guards to see if they could find her...",
    ["Dialogue3881107"]="I didn't take it seriously at first, because the director didn't care about her at all. He thought Martistine was a \"Shepherd's Girl,\" who ran away only to grab the attention of others. She had been sneaking out of the welfare center before, but usually <color=#CA2E0AFF>took a stroll outside the fence</color>. If no one paid attention to her, she would return by dinner. But this time...",
    ["Dialogue3881108"]="Adventurer... C-Can you help me out? I swear I don't know she would have such a big reaction. I did throw a few angry words at her but...\n(She nervously fidgets with her dress, looking afraid that you might turn down her request.)",
    ["Dialogue3881109"]="A-Awesome... Thank you, Adventurer!\nI... I'll talk to Auntie Cook and have her save a meal for Martistine. Hopefully you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring her back as soon as possible</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3890101"]="Excuse me, Chief Lyra.\n(Andrew pulls you to a poised blonde lady.)\nAdventurer, this is Michelle Lyra, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Head of the Republic Guard Intelligence Bureau</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3890102"]="Umm, about the investigation I promised you earlier, the one over Ymir's power in the well of Kiel Khayr's Estate and the mysterious runes found on the wellhead... Well, for some reason, Ms. Lyra will now take it over. (Turning head) Ms. Lyra, Adventurer is someone we can trust, so...",
    ["Dialogue3890103"]="As a soldier, you talk too much, Chief.\n(Lyra glances sharply at you, then continues her line of questioning.)\nBesides, Andre, I haven't even started to look into the guards' overreach in their law-enforcement practice yet. And now here you are, asking me to take care of an outsider?",
    ["Dialogue3890104"]="Chief Lyra, we're stationed here on Minister Philodis' orders, so please be careful what's coming out of your mouth next. Besides, Adventurer is a guest, personally invited by Minister Philodis. As representatives of Juno, I don't think we should make things difficult for a guest.",
    ["Dialogue3890105"]="Hmph, Philodis... Let me tell you, Andre. Even if they are with Philodis, why am I, Head of the Intelligence Bureau, the last to find out? Furthermore, if you're so convinced that the well inside Kiel Khayr's Estate is the source of this demonic calamity, you should let the Intelligence Bureau file the case first and then start the investigation over it. That's called the line of authority.",
    ["Dialogue3890106"]="Don't forget: The division of duties between the Armed Force and the Intelligence Bureau was decided by Lord Carl. Andre, you are not even a cabinet member. How dare you question Lord Carl's decision?",
    ["Dialogue3890107"]="(Andre's expression freezes as he tightly grips the hilt of his sword.)\nMichelle, you are in no position to judge my loyalty to the Republic. What are you trying to say?",
    ["Dialogue3890108"]="Hmph, I'm trying to say...\n(Lyra snorts coldly, looking Andre in his eyes without hesitation.)\nYou, your troops, and this suspicious Adventurer, when will you <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave Kiel Khayr's Estate</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3890109"]="You!!!",
    ["Dialogue3890110"]="Chief Andre, please calm down. I am not even done yet.\n(Lyra smiles at you, starting to fiddle with her jewelry watch casually.)\nTo prevent those with malicious intentions from sneaking in, the Intelligence Bureau has decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>completely lock down the scene, putting it off-limits to all personnel.</color>",
    ["Dialogue3890111"]="You are an Adventurer, right? Sorry, it's all about national security. We can't simply take your word for it. My advice: Leave here. Now. Until the investigation is finished.",
    ["Dialogue3890112"]="(Andre takes a step forward, blocking Lyra's line of sight.)\nSo this is your attitude, Chief Lyra?",
    ["Dialogue3890113"]="That's right. If you have any objections, you may appeal to His Excellency at Lord's Mansion.\n(Lyra suddenly bursts into strange laughter.)\nThe only concern is if you can meet Lord Carl in person.",
    ["Dialogue3890114"]="...I'll definitely follow through. As per the regulations, the Armed Force is responsible for safeguarding every inch of the Republic's territory. You can't just investigate and stay here indefinitely. Lyra, you must give me a time.",
    ["Dialogue3890115"]="As for the duration of the lockdown... Let's make it indefinite before we get the evacuation notice.\n(Lyra shrugs, as if nothing happened.)\nEnough talk. I should head back and make arrangements for my people to take over the work. Chief Andre, goodbye.",
    ["Dialogue3890201"]="These folks from Intelligence Bureau... Hmph, a pain in the ass, as always.\n(Andre pouts as Lyra turns away, but suddenly, he puts his arm around your shoulders.)\nWhat's wrong, my friend? You seem upset.",
    ["Dialogue3890202"]="You mean the investigation? Don't worry about it. Locking down the scene is a standard trick they play when they can't find clues. Besides, can you believe that she rushed over just to make us leave this place? That's a dead giveaway that she holds even less information than us.",
    ["Dialogue3890203"]="When dealing with these politicians, it's not wise to go head-on, Adventurer. Sometimes you have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>beat around the bush</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3890204"]="Ahem... You also need to show some decisiveness to the wavering people. Listen, I've carefully examined the photos of the wellhead. If my guess is right, the first stop for your investigation will be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno Scholar Association</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3890205"]="Yes, you didn't hear me wrong. When it comes to the depth and breadth of academic research, no one even remotely comes close to the Scholar Association in the entire Republic. The thing you will be investigating has been thoroughly researched by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Alena from Juno Scholar Association</color>. The findings were already published in a paper.",
    ["Dialogue3890206"]="(Andre looks at you with pride.)\nAren't you surprised? Let me tell you one more secret: I have read that particular essay in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Association Journal</color>, and it was fascinating!",
    ["Dialogue3890207"]="Of course! Juno is a city that admires knowledge. When I was an ordinary soldier, the Association Journal was a must-read for me! Hehe, you think I'm just a savage man who only knows how to beat up those androids?",
    ["Dialogue3890208"]="Conclusion... The conclusion is...\n(Andre frowns with a miserable expression.)\nAs I recall, it should be...",
    ["Dialogue3890209"]="Anyway! Professor Alena will be giving a lecture every day at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Plaza</color>. When she's finished, you can ask her about the photos. As for Ymir's Power in the well... Since the mysterious runes showed up together with it, I suspect the two might have something to do with each other.",
    ["Dialogue3890301"]="A student? Well, I don't see any confusion in your eyes as in those of many others, yet I don't see the naivety they still possess, either. So, as a scholar, I don't recall the association has taken in such a young scholar like you. You seem quite unfamiliar with the Sage Plaza, let alone you don't even know me...",
    ["Dialogue3890302"]="So, Adventurer from afar, what do you want from me?",
    ["Dialogue3890303"]="Indeed. I have done some research about the content of the photos. In fact, these ancient mysterious runes have been one of the major research topics of the Scholar Association. Each of us is trying, more or less, to decipher these runes within the scope of our respective fields.",
    ["Dialogue3890304"]="My research direction is the evolutional history of ancient grammar, which requires a lot of comparisons between contemporary and ancient references to analyze the evolution of grammar. Adventurer, if you somehow know a bit of these runes, maybe we can work together.",
    ["Dialogue3890305"]="Ancient book restoration, I mean. Coincidentally, I and my students are trying to restore an ancient book written exactly in such runes. If you are willing to help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>piece together the torn pages</color>, I may offer you some answers from my research field.",
    ["Dialogue3890401"]="(Taking over the sorted ancient book, Alena opens a page and signals you to sit down next to her.)\nFrankly speaking, based on the comparison with existing references, the academic community has determined that these runes are from an untraceable ancient script. Therefore, most of the research can only be conducted through trial and error, in an attempt to verify the possibility of its decipherment.",
    ["Dialogue3890402"]="Yes. This kind of script has a different origin than any other existing languages on the continent. Comparing the similarity of its grammar and morphology to other languages, it should be something from <color=#CA2E0AFF>another civilization</color> that has no connection to those on the continent. We have reason to believe that it has a longer history than Juno, even hundreds of years longer.",
    ["Dialogue3890403"]="But since this kind of script has an extensive, lengthy history, why is there no evidence of it blending into or influencing the language system on the continent? That's an interesting question worth exploring. So, based on what we have now, I can say this script is isolated, and so is its civilization. But if that's the case, what's the purpose of this civilization showing up in Juno?",
    ["Dialogue3890404"]="Feeling distressed in uncertainty? Relax. In the academic world, the unknown is much more alluring than the known. The questions that remain unanswered in this generation might find their way to the answers in the next one. Now, let us eliminate a few incorrect answers for our descendants. Ok, what else do you want to ask?",
    ["Dialogue3890405"]="That's beyond my scope of knowledge.\n(Alena smiles and shakes her head.)\nHowever, the collision of different fields might often spark up imaginations and ideas.",
    ["Dialogue3890406"]="About the meaning of the runes, it falls into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Valcone</color>'s expertise. You may consult him to further your investigation.\n(Alena points her finger.)\nLook, that's the gentleman sketching the patterns of the pillars in the plaza.",
    ["Dialogue3890407"]="(Alena shows a look of disagreement.)\nSorry, but I have to ruin the little fantasy of yours. Things with such mythical background, like Ymir's power, are impossible to exist in a Republic built upon technologies. Adventurer, if you wish to conduct your research in Juno, then better not plant the seeds in this barren soil.",
    ["Dialogue3890501"]="Where... Where did you take this? Let me have a good look at it!",
    ["Dialogue3890502"]="I see... I see! If you want to know the meaning of these runes, you've come to the right person! Honestly, I haven't deciphered much, but with this piece of paper and the runes in Juno, I, Valcone, should be able to figure it out.",
    ["Dialogue3890503"]="Yeah, in many places. You see, the photo here has the runes symbolizing <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Pathway\" and \"Seal,\"</color> and the adjacent ones between them also appeared in Juno. In other words, by comparing them side by side, we will know exactly what the runes mean in this photo!",
    ["Dialogue3890504"]="So... If you don't mind, can I use this photo as a reference picture in my essay? I can compensate you with Zeny, an honorary title, or a recommendation letter. Just name it!",
    ["Dialogue3890505"]="You just want to take a look? All right, but... You'd better consider it carefully. Even if you have no interest in academic research, getting compensated for yourself is totally reasonable. After all, this is Juno, and everyone is willing to pay for knowledge.",
    ["Dialogue3890506"]="Fine, then I'll respect your decision. Just so you know that we scholars hold our own pride in a certain way. Since you provided me with knowledge, I have to resolve your confusion. Now, come with me. Let's witness the <color=#CA2E0AFF>new discovery</color> of ancient semiology!",
    ["Dialogue3890601"]="(Valcone sits on the ground, staring at the photos as if he is trying to burn a hole with his stare.)\nIt's weird... Could this one be polysemous?",
    ["Dialogue3890602"]="Look. This string of symbols can be seen repeatedly in these four photos. Apparently, it is a crucial word. I've been thinking over and over, but still can't understand its meaning. I'm sorry, but it seems we're missing an important piece here. Without it, we can't come to a rigorous academic conclusion.",
    ["Dialogue3890603"]="Without a doubt, they represent <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Boundary,\" \"Delineation,\" and \"Hover.\"</color> My speculation is that these mysterious runes surrounding Juno formed a magic circle and delineated the boundary of the hovering land. Historically, after all, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno was originally a city on the ground, but suddenly, it became \"The City of Sky\" one day</color>. There must be an extraordinary force behind this.",
    ["Dialogue3890604"]="An invasion from a foreign civilization. That's what I'm talking about. Don't forget, Juno is still \"The City of Sky\" so far. If it weren't because of its incredibly advanced technology that keeps the city afloat, then it must be...",
    ["Dialogue3890605"]="This civilization still exists—in an extremely secretive manner.",
    ["Dialogue3890606"]="Hey, overthinking by yourself can easily lead you down a rabbit hole! If you're stuck, how about sorting out the information you have right now and looking in another direction? Sometimes, I even seek help from my seniors in this research field. Nothing to be embarrassed!",
    ["Dialogue3890607"]="(In a scribble sound, Valcone jots down a name and address in his notebook.)\nThe only thing we can confirm now is that Juno was indeed \"lifted up\" to the sky by some mysterious force. Unfortunately, this subject lies beyond the scope of ancient semiology. If you want to learn more about this, I suggest you turn to the elemental scholar, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Laurent</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3890608"]="Just a friendly reminder, Professor Laurent has quite a volatile temper. He's probably gone to confront Eden Group again! Alas, as far as I know, Professor Laurent's research has reached its crucial stage. If someone thinks locking down the scene can interrupt a scholar's research, they'll be too naive. And wrong, completely wrong!",
    ["Dialogue3890609"]="Ymir? Isn't Ymir a mythical figure? Wait...\n(Valcone's eyes widen.)\nGod's divine power? Descendants? Interesting... Even though I'm not holding a high hope, I will try to interpret it in the direction you suggest.",
    ["Dialogue3890701"]="Hey! A straight hit in my face? Where's your decency?\n(Laurent boldly rolls up his sleeves, revealing his strong muscles.)\nWait there! Let me take off this scholar robe, then we will go Round Two!",
    ["Dialogue3890702"]="(The leading Eden Group member winks a signal to the back, and you see someone leaving discreetly.)\nProfessor Laurent, we have no intention to clash with you, but please respect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>exclusive exploration right</color> that the Eden Group holds in El Mes Gorge.",
    ["Dialogue3890703"]="Bah! Don't palm me off with this nonsense! You rascals cordoned off the gorge completely, just to research the ruins all by yourselves and figure out why Juno is floating, right? Let me tell you, the government gave you an exclusive exploration right, not to shut us scholars out!",
    ["Dialogue3890704"]="...Professor Laurent, you're free to say whatever you want. However, you can't go over there today.",
    ["Dialogue3890705"]="And how dare you ask me to watch my mouth? My mouth is only loyal to the truths found in academic research! All right, if you want to hide the secrets of Juperos Ruins, then I'll be obliged to expose them to the world! I don't think anyone of you knows, that the kinetic energy gathered on the surface of Juno is in complete consistency with the radiation energy flowing under the ground, and the intensity of the radiation peaks near these underground ruins!",
    ["Dialogue3890706"]="In other words, the extraordinary force that keeps Juno afloat could possibly <color=#CA2E0AFF>come from Juperos Ruins</color>! For us, old bones obsessed with our research, whoever enters the ruins first will take the lead in their research and seize the achievements alone!",
    ["Dialogue3890801"]="Adventurer, seems we always bump into each other in difficult scenarios.\n(Philodis stands between the two sides, slightly raising his hands in a \"stop\" gesture.)\nProfessor Laurent, and the members of the Eden Group, may I say something?",
    ["Dialogue3890802"]="Professor, their exclusive exploration right was personally granted by the Lord, which means they have all the legal rights to regulate this area. You shouldn't make things too difficult for them.",
    ["Dialogue3890803"]="Hmph! I understand how much the Lord values the Eden Group. But what about Juno Scholar Association? If the Eden Group could file a report to the government and ask our respected Sir Philodis to intervene in this affair, couldn't the Scholar Association do the same thing?!",
    ["Dialogue3890804"]="Huh?\n(Philodis glances at Laurent coldly, sending a chill down your spine.)\nProfessor, are you saying the Lord and I should respond to anyone's request?",
    ["Dialogue3890805"]="...\n(Laurent is disgruntled, mumbling to himself while staring at the floor and finally falls silent.)",
    ["Dialogue3890806"]="Thank you. I appreciate your silence.\n(Philodis turns to you, giving you a courteous smile.)\nAdventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Lord likes to invite you for a meet</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3890807"]="Indeed. About the discovery in that ancient well, His Excellency has something to speak to you in private. Folks, please calm yourselves down here while I am off taking the Adventurer to the Lord's Mansion. I believe that by the time I return, all of you will have reached a friendly consensus. Now Adventurer, this way, please.",
    ["Dialogue3890901"]="(Inside the Lord's office, a sturdy Lord Carl stands with his hands behind his back. Before him lies a large sandbox.)\nWelcome! All the way from the Rune Kingdom to the Republic. Quite a journey, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue3890902"]="Your Excellency, please, shall we skip the civilities and proceed to the main subject?",
    ["Dialogue3890903"]="Why so serious, Philodis? You always keep that straight face, you know? No wonder the ladies in the Lord's Mansion are too scared to talk to you.\n(Lord Carl draws a symbol on the sandbox, which is precisely one of the runes that appeared in Kiel Khayr's Estate on the wellhead.)\nHmm... I heard you were investigating this?",
    ["Dialogue3890904"]="Your honesty touched me.\n(Lord Carl sweeps away the writing on the sandbox.)\nAdventurer, seems our different origins and allegiances would not prevent us from becoming trusted allies.",
    ["Dialogue3890905"]="Aha, so cautious in this office. Not a bad choice, actually.\n(Lord Carl sweeps away the writing on the sandbox.)\nAdventurer, please do believe that we have the same goals. Well, to an extent.",
    ["Dialogue3890906"]="For instance, I'll admit that I know fearsomely little about occultism. But since you have somehow arrived at a <color=#CA2E0AFF>solid conclusion</color>, plus you're also an important partner invited to assist in this <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret operation</color>, there's something you should know.",
    ["Dialogue3890907"]="Shh... How about playing a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sandbox Game</color> with me?",
    ["Dialogue3891001"]="This, my dear fellow, is the truth of the Ymir's power you have sensed.",
    ["Dialogue3891002"]="At this moment, a heart—the heart of an ancient god—is pulsating beneath the foundations of Juno. It was once held by a now-destroyed higher civilization, the Welsh Civilization, but now it's providing inexhaustible energy to the technological development of the Republic, just like it used to do for the Welsh. I can tell you, from the mysterious runes in Khayr Estate to the Republic's first technological leap, they are all legacies of civilizations.",
    ["Dialogue3891003"]="So we, the new civilization that rose from the remains of the fallen one, must shoulder the duty of guarding this heart. Adventurer, I believe you can foresee this: if an intact sacred relic, capable of providing perpetual energy, were to emerge, numerous conflicts would arise in Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue3891004"]="We are the keepers of this secret. Throughout the continent, aside from <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Lords of the Republic, the descendants of the Welsh who live in seclusion, and the Eden Group that has been studying the ruins for hundreds of years</color>, no one else knows the existence of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["Dialogue3891005"]="To keep this secret, the Lords sealed off all archives related to Ymir's Heart, leaving behind only one document as the Republic's top secret. And the descendants of the Welsh burned all the ancestral legacies about Ymir's Heart, trying to wipe out every trace of relevant information. They also destroyed the entrance, preventing anyone from accessing it.",
    ["Dialogue3891006"]="As for the Eden Group, all their doings in Juperos Ruins are monitored by the government. I know what you might say, Adventurer, but humans are unpredictable. Compared to cutting off access to Ymir's Heart through administrative edicts, it's better to entrust the exploration right to a renowned non-profit organization. In this way—endorsed and funded by the government, I mean, it becomes the bearer of responsibility. And to be honest, the Eden Group might be the only non-profit organization that can operate in a high-radiation environment.",
    ["Dialogue3891007"]="That well... it does look like a <color=#CA2E0AFF>neglected entrance</color>, but we still don't know who found it and who told Kiel Khayr that Ymir's power is beneath the well. Alas, if all of this nuisance was only driven by the wild speculation within the Khayr Consortium, we might still be able to find some traces. However, if such information was deliberately leaked by someone who hides in the shadow, using the consortium as a marionette... Then the enemy we're facing might be far beyond our recognition...",
    ["Dialogue3891008"]="The re-emergence of Ymir's Heart is not a good sign at all, especially for the states on the continent that desperately need to stand united at this moment. I need to discuss this matter with other secret keepers. But before that, I hope you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>forget everything</color> that happened here and today when you walk out of the Lord's Mansion.",
    ["Dialogue3891009"]="Oh, you don't have to worry about the Intelligence Bureau. They surely have the right to intervene, but neither the department nor Michelle has access to this republic-wrecking top secret. By the way, Andre told me that they had forcibly locked down the scene and thrown both of you out of the place?",
    ["Dialogue3891010"]="Hmm. Not necessarily a bad thing. Now you have learned the truth, why not play along, <color=#CA2E0AFF>leaving this lockdown what it is</color>? It keeps the citizens away from danger and meanwhile saves Andre from being short-staffed. Moreover, given that the entrance has been revealed but we are not swept away by the radiation storm, I assume that whoever left the entrance open was not of malevolent intentions.",
    ["Dialogue3891011"]="I believe those Welsh runes on the wellhead are for purposes of protection, not destruction. This feels familiar... Just like the decision the Welsh people made in the face of calamity: burying their civilization under the ground and sending their new city into the sky.",
    ["Dialogue3900101"]="Adventurer! Please don't go!\nCan I take the liberty to ask you... have you seen Commander Bohr today?",
    ["Dialogue3900102"]="Ah... Actually, I've seen you going to and from the capital with Lord Bohr recently, so I assume you might know where Lord Bohr is going...\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>After all, this matter...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3900103"]="Don't you know? How terrible...",
    ["Dialogue3900104"]="(The young Defense Force Soldier looks worried.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The Bloodline Banquet is about to begin, but now this has happened... What should we do?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3900105"]="Really?! That would be a big help!\nAfter all, you are an Adventurer recognized by Commander Bohr. If you are willing to help us... I believe this problem will soon be solved!",
    ["Dialogue3900106"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer! Let me take you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>scene of the crime</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3900201"]="Are you all right, old man?!",
    ["Dialogue3900202"]="<size=26>It's... It's all your fault!</size> ",
    ["Dialogue3900203"]="In the morning, I asked you to look at <color=#CA2E0AFF>the things on the ground</color>, but you couldn't tell what it was! I want to clean up the mud around here so you can make sure... I just picked up some water and found myself surrounded by monsters!",
    ["Dialogue3900204"]="However, I told you to stay away from this place. A matter this significant must be reported to the officer first...",
    ["Dialogue3900205"]="What's there? Dead people... Look! The rain yesterday washed away all the heaps of soil! They're full of dead people!",
    ["Dialogue3900206"]="Drat! What awful luck! What's this fuss? So early in the morning?!\nI don't care. I want to go home! Go check it yourself!",
    ["Dialogue3900207"]="Don't! I want you to tell the Adventurer about the situation here!\n(The little soldier shouts as he grabs the old man's arm. Unexpectedly, the stout old man twists his arm away and breaks free.)\nHey! Don't go, old man! Damn... He's gone.",
    ["Dialogue3900208"]="... Basically, like the old man just said, after the rainstorm last night, <color=#CA2E0AFF>seven bodies suddenly emerged from this field</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3900209"]="Because this is a sensitive time, the time of the Bloodline Banquet, I wanted to report this matter to Commander Bohr, as he could decide how to deal with it, but now...\n(He rubs his head and looks at you, obviously waiting for your instructions.)",
    ["Dialogue3900210"]="Okay, I'll listen to you, then! There's also some water the old man gathered. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>clean up the soil on the bodies</color> first, and see if we can find some useful clues!",
    ["Dialogue3900301"]="Adventurers! I've seen this kind of tag before! The royal palace gives these <color=#CA2E0AFF>special tags</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>servants</color> responsible for preparing the Bloodline Banquet! It's exactly the same as the one in your hand!",
    ["Dialogue3900302"]="Perhaps... We should collect all of these tags and show them to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palace Head Steward</color>. These days, the Palace Head Steward has been busy preparing for the banquet. He probably knows the situation of these waiters better than anyone else!",
    ["Dialogue3900401"]="(After seeing the tag in your hand, the dignified steward finally shows a relieved expression.)\nThank you very much. These are the tags we lost. Without these, those might have had to sleep in the streets tonight.",
    ["Dialogue3900402"]="Sleep in the streets tonight...?\n(The young soldier looks at you, and you both see some confusion in each other's eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue3900403"]="Yes, these tags are specially made by royal craftsmen and are only distributed to servants responsible for preparing the Bloodline Banquet. They are used as passes to access the palace and banquet hall. Just now, several servants told me that their tags were missing, and I was wondering where they had gone.",
    ["Dialogue3900404"]="Just now?!",
    ["Dialogue3900405"]="... Yes, just now. Today, we came to the market to purchase goods for the Bloodline Banquet, but the tags were found to be lost soon after we left the palace. The young ones were so worried...",
    ["Dialogue3900406"]="D-D-Don't scare me, boss! They're not dead—",
    ["Dialogue3900407"]="Ow, ow, ow, ow—\n(The soldier utters a painful wail. You take the opportunity to speak on his behalf.)",
    ["Dialogue3900408"]="Well... according to today's work plan, we still need to prepare all kinds of things for the Bloodline Banquet. They should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>on the shopping street near the Central Fountain</color>.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Speaking of which, we have to quickly deliver these tags to them... Hey, who's free to lend a hand now?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3900409"]="... Sorry, Adventurer. I can't go with you.\n(To your surprise, the little soldier suddenly interrupts you, winks at you quietly, lowers his voice, and whispers to you.)",
    ["Dialogue3900410"]="This matter is a little peculiar. You can use returning the tags as an excuse to <color=#CA2E0AFF>secretly investigate the servants</color>... But make sure you <color=#CA2E0AFF>don't really give the tags back to them</color>! This is important evidence! And I want to take this opportunity to confirm the whereabouts of Lord Bohr... Later, we will meet near the tavern, okay?",
    ["Dialogue3900411"]="So... Your Excellency, my rest time is almost over. I have to rush back to the South Gate to stand guard immediately, but the Adventurer can deliver these tags to the servants on your behalf. Please rest assured!",
    ["Dialogue3900412"]="Hmm... Okay, thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3900501"]="I gave you the list of materials to be purchased two days ago. Why are you only telling me now that they're out of stock?",
    ["Dialogue3900502"]="It's not our fault... Didn't you just say that you wanted to add another batch of materials this morning? There's also some strange stuff on the list... Look at what's written here?",
    ["Dialogue3900503"]="(The youngster lifts the paper in his hand, full of resentment.)\nWhy do we need the front teeth of a Lunatic to hold a party?",
    ["Dialogue3900504"]="This... This is beyond my control! Anyway, the lord steward has ordered that all the materials must be prepared by today, otherwise... you can all kiss your jobs goodbye!",
    ["Dialogue3900505"]="What?! Without this job, I... I...",
    ["Dialogue3900506"]="Listen, you'd better go back to the high street and try your luck. These materials can be obtained from the monsters outside the South Gate. Maybe Adventurers who often travel between the Mjolnir Mountains and Prontera might have some... Hey, look! Isn't that one over there?",
    ["Dialogue3900507"]="(As the blonde servant speaks, she turns to look at you with a sparkle in her eyes.)\nA-Adventurer, would you happen to have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stiff Front Tooth</color> or two dropped by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatics</color>...? Or <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Beaks</color> dropped by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Condors</color>? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colored Silk</color>from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fabres</color> is good, too! Can you sell some to us?",
    ["Dialogue3900508"]="Are you willing to help gather these materials for us? That's great!\nPlease rest assured that we'll make it worth your while, and all of the materials will be based on the market price—",
    ["Dialogue3900509"]="Eighty percent of the market price! Eighty percent!\n(The blonde servant quickly interrupts your conversation and glances up at you.)\nThis transaction has not gone through the formal entrustment process. This may be somewhat risky... Do you understand?",
    ["Dialogue3900601"]="... Didn't you say that the royal palace was magnificent and is the most symbolic building of Prontera? Why have you changed your mind after only a few days?",
    ["Dialogue3900602"]="Erm... When did I say that? Oh, you must have remembered wrong! I meant that, as the most pious follower of Odin, I insist that there must be a solemn statue of Odin on the banquet's invitation letter!",
    ["Dialogue3900603"]="Heavens! Yesterday, I asked you to come with me and pray in the church, but you didn't want to. Now you're suddenly a devout Odin worshipper?!\nA woman's heart truly is a fickle thing...",
    ["Dialogue3900604"]="Y-You really love the sound of your own voice, don't you... It's not like that at all! Let's take a picture of all the scenic spots and then vote. How about that?\nI just saw... Right! Adventurer! Yeah, you!",
    ["Dialogue3900605"]="That's right! I see you have a camera... You must be good at taking pictures, right? Can you help us take pictures of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palace, Odin's Statue, and the Central Fountain</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3900606"]="Please, please! Maybe your photos will be printed on the official Bloodline Banquet invitation letter! It's quite the honor, right?\n(The girl grabs your camera, determined to achieve her goal.)",
    ["Dialogue3900701"]="What's wrong, Adventurer? Are there any clues worth noting?",
    ["Dialogue3900702"]="... It's strange. There are only two days until the banquet begins. How can we change the list of materials now? Besides... why do you need Lunatics' teeth?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Aren't they used... for making weapons?</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3900703"]="The words of those servants are really contradictory... Although most people in the Rune Kingdom believe in Odin... why would the average person change so much in just a few days?",
    ["Dialogue3900704"]="This matter is definitely not as simple as it seems! However, you have already met with those servants. If you stay here again, you may be exposed... Why don't we switch quests?",
    ["Dialogue3900705"]="I previously confirmed that Lord Bohr is talking with Commander Dardano in front of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Chivalry</color> residence. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report this matter to Lord Bohr</color> for me, and I will stay here to continue monitoring those odd servants.",
    ["Dialogue3900801"]="Dardano, you must give me a reason. Why are so many people unable to join the Guardian Troops?",
    ["Dialogue3900802"]="... Lord Bohr, it is very clear from the dispatch list that these knights were only transferred to a new station because of the change of jurisdiction. It was not that the Royal Chivalry interfered intentionally. Why are you putting up such an overbearing front?",
    ["Dialogue3900803"]="Dardano! Don't be ridiculous!\nI said that the transfer order for the Guardian Troops was signed by the princess personally and should have the highest administrative effect. Even if those knights have been transferred from the capital, why can't they be recalled?!",
    ["Dialogue3900804"]="In addition, there are many knights who are sick or absent for personal reasons on this schedule. Could you explain in detail what ailments they have and what personal reasons they have that are important enough for them to ignore the orders of the princess?!\n(Enraged, Bohr slams the things in his hand into Dardano.)",
    ["Dialogue3900805"]="... I have answered you again and again, Lord Bohr.\n(Dardano, after being hit by a thick stack of paper, shows little emotion. He simply squats down to sort out the scattered papers and calmly hands them back to Bohr.)",
    ["Dialogue3900806"]="There is nothing else I can say. I'm sorry I can't give you more of an explanation.",
    ["Dialogue3900807"]="Good... Very good!\nIn that case, I must take this further! Please call Captain Hallam here! Let him explain it to me in person!",
    ["Dialogue3900808"]="I'm sorry, Lord Bohr. Captain Hallam left the capital a month ago. As for his whereabouts, please don't ask. This is the secret for the knights alone.",
    ["Dialogue3900809"]="If you want to transfer the Captain of the Royal Chivalry's position, you must obtain the king's permission. However, His Majesty Tristan III has been missing for some days now, and you have not reported this matter to the princess. Therefore, this transfer order is invalid!",
    ["Dialogue3900810"]="... Lord Boer, please listen to me and stop this pointless badgering. As Commander of the Defense Force, you must have many important things to deal with. There is no need to waste your precious time on me. You see that Adventurer over there? An old acquaintance of yours, perhaps? He has been standing there for some time.\n(Prompted by Dardano, Bohr finally notices you.)",
    ["Dialogue3900811"]="... What are you doing here? Could it be...\n(Bohr seems to realize something before finishing his sentence. He gives you a look and then turns to confront Dardano.)",
    ["Dialogue3900812"]="Well, let's put this to one side for now. But Dardano—note well that I will not stop investigating this matter until I find the person responsible. I hope you can give me a satisfactory answer the next time we speak... otherwise, I shall see you in military court!",
    ["Dialogue3900901"]="... Fine, let's leave it at that. Sorry, Adventurer, I assume you've come to me about the Bloodline Banquet... It's not convenient for me to talk with you just now.",
    ["Dialogue3900902"]="Are you talking about Dardano? He is the Commander of the Royal Chivalry, making him second-in-command after Hallam. If what he said is true, Hallam was transferred from the capital more than one month ago...\n(Bohr shakes his head and looks somber.)",
    ["Dialogue3900903"]="... I'm afraid that the power of the knights has declined. It's not surprising that I received this deployment list from the Guardian Troops.",
    ["Dialogue3900904"]="During the Bloodline Banquet, Prontera will host many important people, and there will also be many illegal forces seeking opportunities during this period. To this end, Princess Kaitlyn signed a transfer order under my command to transfer elite personnel from the Defense Force and the Guardian Troop to form the Guardian Troop, which will be responsible for matters of security during the banquet.",
    ["Dialogue3900905"]="I discussed this with the Princess at length. All the people on this list were carefully selected and confirmed to be loyal to the royal family. Today, however, I received <color=#CA2E0AFF>order feedback</color> from Dardano... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take a look</color>, Adventurer. They really wrote their rebellious intent on this piece of paper.",
    ["Dialogue3901001"]="Now, do you understand my worries? Originally, the transfer order signed by the Princess should have the highest authority, but now, so many knights are absent for various ridiculous reasons. There must be some reason for this. Maybe it's also related to Aronst's poisoning...",
    ["Dialogue3901002"]="... You and the soldiers stationed at the South Gate found a bunch of dead bodies in the outskirts? They were also carrying special nametags made by royal craftsmen?!\nAdventurer, is this what you were eager to tell me just now?",
    ["Dialogue3901003"]="It is reasonable to say that these nametags are enough to prove the identities of the bodies. However, when you followed this clue and went to the Palace Head Steward, he told you that these nametags were reported lost while the servants who supposedly died were still working hard in the palace?",
    ["Dialogue3901004"]="You and the little soldier have done very well, Adventurer. The strange deaths and resurrections of these servants are by no means accidental. In addition, this unusual schedule in my hand...\n(Bohr stares at the paper in his hand. For a moment, he laughs slightly with scorn.)\nHah... So, that's it. I see now.",
    ["Dialogue3901005"]="Adventurers, if my guess is correct, these two matters may be the work of the same party. Their purpose... is to shuffle the key personnel responsible for the Bloodline Banquet.",
    ["Dialogue3901006"]="Yes. Perhaps those servants were not \"resurrected\" but are, in fact, impersonating the servants, taking advantage of their status and access to do something at the Bloodline Banquet. As for this schedule, many of the absent knights have worked with you in the past... I believe you may know more about their positions.",
    ["Dialogue3901007"]="..I promised Aronst that I would not fight the Walter family until the Bloodline Banquet was over—but standing by and doing nothing does not mean I have resigned myself to fate. What we should do now is gather information, make adequate preparations, and then... fight back the moment the enemy attacks.",
    ["Dialogue3901008"]="Come with me, Adventurer. In fact, I noticed changes in the knights some time ago, and I have also sent people to investigate their whereabouts in secret. Recently, they have been meeting regularly in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>woods outside the West Gate</color>. We can <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow them in secret</color> to see if we can find out some useful information.",
    ["Dialogue3901101"]="... With all due respect, Your Excellency, Lord Bohr, isn't eavesdropping on someone's conversation considered ungentlemanly behavior?\n(He looks at you warily and almost seems as though he is about to draw his sword. Taken aback, you unconsciously put your hand on your weapon.)",
    ["Dialogue3901102"]="Don't misunderstand me. I wasn't eavesdropping on your conversation. I just happened to have something to discuss with you. Would you like to join the Guardian Troop?",
    ["Dialogue3901103"]="(Seeing your surprised look, Bohr gives you a reassuring glance. He gently taps your hand and signals for you to release your weapon.)\nYou must have heard about this matter. In order to ensure the success of the Bloodline Banquet, the princess personally signed a transfer order to transfer personnel from the Defense Force and the knights to watch over the banquet.",
    ["Dialogue3901104"]="Yes... we all know this. But as far as I know... the knights here should not be on the list of personnel, no?",
    ["Dialogue3901105"]="Such is the case. However, due to the absence of most of the knights listed on the deployment order, the number of Guardian Troop is insufficient. After discussing this with Commander Dardano, he suggested that I come here directly to ask your opinion. If anyone of you wishes to join voluntarily, he will not stop you. In addition, although it is only short-term, the payment will be more than twice as high as that of the knights... So, what do you think?",
    ["Dialogue3901106"]="... No, I must decline, Your Excellency, Lord Bohr.\n(He sighs slightly and finally takes his hand off the sword's hilt.)",
    ["Dialogue3901107"]="Recently, the affairs of the knights are also complicated. We can't leave our posts without a good cause... I can only thank you for your kindness in thinking of me, Bohr.",
    ["Dialogue3901108"]="Really...? What a pity. In that case, I won't bother you anymore. Now, This Adventurer and I will continue seeking the opinions of the other knights. If you change your mind, please come to me at any time.",
    ["Dialogue3901109"]="... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Let's go</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3901201"]="Did you hear what those knights said, Adventurer? The people they planted in the palace... must be the \"resurrected\" servants you saw today.",
    ["Dialogue3901202"]="In this way, the rebellion of the Royal Chivalry is almost a certainty. The reason why they have not made their move is that the result of the royal election is not yet clear... Once the banquet is officially held, and if the person who ascends to the throne is not the one they hope for... I'm afraid that the whole of Prontera will become a bloody battlefield.",
    ["Dialogue3901203"]="No... Adventurer, now is not the best time to act. It is not difficult to guess who the mastermind behind all this is. The difficult thing is... finding conclusive evidence of his rebellion. Helena and Abu have not yet awakened, and the Royal Chivalry is ostensibly under the command of Dardano...",
    ["Dialogue3901204"]="If we act at this time, he can provide a scapegoat and rid himself of all suspicion... or take advantage of the fact that most of the capital's forces are concentrated under his command and launch a mutiny in advance... Either outcome would not be in our favor.",
    ["Dialogue3901205"]="... Although this was not my intention, perhaps Aronst made a mistake and gave us the most suitable solution. There are still two days to go before the Bloodline Banquet. I will try my best to reach an alliance with the other royal families and seek their help, but beyond that, I have one more thing to take care of.",
    ["Dialogue3901206"]="You are indeed sharp, Adventurer. Now, I am concerned that the enemy will threaten us with the antidote for Luminary Dream if backed into a corner. At Aronst's insistence, I had to withdraw the hidden one I placed on Azer, but in fact, I also hope that he really had nothing to do with the plot... It's a shame that Aronst's good faith will be betrayed.",
    ["Dialogue3901207"]="You just told me that those servants died within the past three days. As early as two weeks ago, I placed surveillance operatives around all the members of the Walter family. It would have been almost impossible to get rid of these servants and replace them with their people without my operatives noticing, but before today, I received no reports on this matter at all...",
    ["Dialogue3901208"]="... It's not that I seek to doubt Azer, but I have no other choice. If it were you, could you still fully trust him under such circumstances?",
    ["Dialogue3901209"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Really...? If I could go back ten years, I may have made the same decision as you. Unfortunately...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3901210"]="... A very sensible answer, Adventurer. No wonder even His Majesty Tristan III has high hopes for you.",
    ["Dialogue3901211"]="However, I have promised Aronst that I will not do anything to Azer until the Bloodline Banquet is over. Publicly, I am an official; privately, I am an elder. Regardless of my position, I am not permitted to break my promise. Besides... I really need more time to seek out more bargaining chips for us to use against the Walter family. Therefore, I wish to ask you one thing...",
    ["Dialogue3901212"]="I hope you can do your best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ensure Aronst's safety</color> over the next two days. As long as we survive the last two days... it will be our turn to sound the counterattack, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3901301"]="Judging from the degree of decay, these people all died <color=#CA2E0AFF>within the past three days</color>. They all had a fatal wound through the chest, and the murder weapon seems to be some kind of double-edged weapon. In addition, in the pockets of the deceased, you find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>nametags made of special materials</color>...",
    ["Dialogue3901401"]="... You just came back from Glast Heim, so you don't know the situation in Prontera. As early as a month ago, Captain Hallam was transferred. Now all the affairs of the knights are in charge of Commander Dardano.",
    ["Dialogue3901402"]="R-Really?! But how could Captain Hallam agree to such a thing?!",
    ["Dialogue3901403"]="Why would he disagree? Do you know who ordered the transfer? Commander Dardano has the support of <color=#CA2E0AFF>the lord</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3901404"]="Quiet! How can you dare say such a thing! Are you trying to get yourself killed?!",
    ["Dialogue3901501"]="Tut... Disgusting. This bloody smell can't be washed away... It's all over my new clothes.",
    ["Dialogue3901502"]="You can bear it. Those rebels this morning were not easy to take care of—it was never going to be a clean affair. When this matter is over, you can pick whatever clothes you like.",
    ["Dialogue3901503"]="Besides, this is the last bunch... Now that all the \"rats\" have been disposed of and those nobles have reached an agreement with the lord... our moment of glory is almost here...",
    ["Dialogue3901601"]="Have you sorted out everything in the palace?",
    ["Dialogue3901602"]="Don't worry, Captain. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Our men have all been planted</color>. On the day of the banquet, they will pay close attention to the situation at the scene and send a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blue signal</color> immediately if the plan fails. If we see the signal, we just need to rally...",
    ["Dialogue3901603"]="<size=26>... Wait! Who's there?!</size> ",
    ["Dialogue3910101"]="(Archbishop Wolmas stroked his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily)\nI haven't seen you for a few days. It seems that you have changed quite a bit. It seems that you are ready to accept the job advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3910102"]="As I said earlier, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, which proves that you have the strength to mold the future. However, you are most probably still a bit confused how exactly to use this power",
    ["Dialogue3910103"]="That's right. Therefore, now that you have had these experiences, it's time for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>class master</color>. They will teach you how to adapt to your new career and battle skills. Maybe... There will be some exciting surprises waiting for you, Heh, heh~",
    ["Dialogue3910104"]="Off you go, Adventurer, I'll be waiting to hear your good news. I hope to see you next time... We can witness your rebirth in front of the statue of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3910201"]="... oh? Amazing... You got the Rune Script?",
    ["Dialogue3910202"]="So, when you came to me today, you must want to know how to become a qualified <color=#CA2E0AFF>Guillotine Cross cutter</color>?\n(Moxie smiles brightly and waves to you)\nCome with me, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3910203"]="A curriculum with such significance and importance naturally needs the most appropriate venue. Let's go to the Mjolnir Dead Pit. I... Will teach you well, hehe~",
    ["Dialogue3910301"]="Lets get down to business. An assassin’s two most important skills are concealing his breath and the rational use of concealed weapons. So today, your challenge is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>without disturbing</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gierths</color>, you must find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>items in the treasure chests</color> that I have scattered throughout the mine... Remember, even if you are discovered by one Giearth, you will fail ~!",
    ["Dialogue3910302"]="I'll wait for you at the elevator leading to mine shaft 2F. Be quick. After all, I can be quite impatient.",
    ["Dialogue3910401"]="... the recipe I just told you, can you remember it all?",
    ["Dialogue3910402"]="Ugh... What a blockhead. You have been holding these bottles and cans for such a long time now and you haven’t been bothered to investigate them?\n(Moxie reaches out her finger and pokes your forehead)\nIt is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>potion potency enhancement</color> recipe!",
    ["Dialogue3910403"]="Hah... So now you want it? Too late!\n(Moxie quickly hides the things in her hand behind her back and laughs maliciously)",
    ["Dialogue3910404"]="Since you haven’t found my good intentions, this recipe can't just be handed over to you. Although... The tolerant and kind Lord Moxie has decided to give you a second chance. If you can pass my test with a perfect score... It's not that I can't forgive~",
    ["Dialogue3910405"]="Hehehe ~ On the 2F of Mjolnir Dead Pit there is a ~ ~ ~ <color=#CA2E0AFF>Giant Giearth</color>? If you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>stealthily hide yourself</color> and silently <color=#CA2E0AFF>deal a fatal blow</color>... Then I will have to reluctantly admit that you are qualified to become a Guillotine Cross~",
    ["Dialogue3910501"]="Hehe ~ what an excellent student... Now, I have no reason to make things difficult for you~",
    ["Dialogue3910502"]="(Moxie smiles as if she was a cat who just caught a fish, holding up the thin piece of paper and shaking it in front of you)\nOh, Ho ~ do you still want this ~?",
    ["Dialogue3910503"]="Ahem Ahem ~ for your sake... This recipe is <color=#CA2E0AFF>officially handed over to you</color>.\nCongratulations, now you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Prontera</color> and attend your Job Advancement ceremony~",
    ["Dialogue3910601"]="Well... I strongly believe it. This comes not only from your determination, but also from those who help you progress. I hope that in your future adventures, you continue to follow your heart and and give those who entrust the future to you your trust and support.",
    ["Dialogue3910602"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time... To prove your dedication to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3920201"]="You have come, Adventurer. I heard that you obtained the Rune of Rune from the goddess?",
    ["Dialogue3920202"]="Well... You deserve it.\n(Charles nodded with satisfaction, then quickly changed into his Master tone)",
    ["Dialogue3920203"]="However, we must not get complacent. You probably still don't know how to use the strength of Rune to become an official <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warlock</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3920204"]="Of course, it would be my pleasure to guide you, but it will be a tough challenge. You must understand, it's no use only using my guidance. Following the works of the predecessors of the Pentagram... They should be the goal of your studies.\nLet's get to Geffen right away!",
    ["Dialogue3920301"]="Before your challenge begins, I must give you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>container of this element</color>. As you have learned, the fundamental condition for using magic is to learn to control elements, and the more powerful the warlock is, the more proficient he is in controlling elements. Just like Warlock Merlin, you should never be limited to controlling one element, but instead <color=#CA2E0AFF>integrate</color> all elements to produce <color=#CA2E0AFF>new changes</color>.....",
    ["Dialogue3920302"]="You may find it difficult to understand, but that's why we're here. All knowledge can be consolidated through training, and magic is no exception. So what you need to do now is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect elements from the monsters</color>, until you <color=#CA2E0AFF>fill</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>container</color>. After that... your understanding of elements will increase significantly.",
    ["Dialogue3920303"]="Well, I'll wait for you on <color=#CA2E0AFF>the platform just north of Geffen Dungeon 2F</color>. Keep it up, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3920401"]="Although it took a long time... I believe it was worth the wait. Remember what I said? Being able to skillfully integrate all elements and make new changes is a essential for becoming a Warlock. So now... You have to try to integrate these elements and produce even more strength....",
    ["Dialogue3920402"]="Don't worry. Understand that the predecessors of Pentagram are ready to help you overcome this together. Calm down, <color=#CA2E0AFF>put down the element container</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>feel the flow</color> of elements within it.....",
    ["Dialogue3920501"]="(Charles looks at the container in your hand and smiles with great satisfaction)\n... yes, very good. Now, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>heart of the element</color> is yours.",
    ["Dialogue3920502"]="This is proof of your Job Advancement and the key to helping you master magic. Only those who have the hearts of elements will be recognized formally as Warlocks. Congratulations, Adventurer. Now you can go back to Prontera and attend your job advancement ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3920701"]="(you begin to manipulate the elements in the container, powerful magical waves collide with each other, the container bursts full of colors. The colorful waves finally merge into one and bloom like a rainbow...)",
    ["Dialogue3930101"]="(Archbishop Wolmas stroked his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily)\nI haven't seen you for a few days. It seems that you have changed quite a bit. It seems that you are ready to accept the job advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3930102"]="As I said earlier, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, which proves that you have the strength to mold the future. However, you are most probably still a bit confused how exactly to use this power",
    ["Dialogue3930103"]="That's right. Now that you have had these experiences, it's time for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>class master</color>. They will teach you how to adapt your battle skills to your new career. Maybe... There will be some exciting surprises waiting for you, Heheh~",
    ["Dialogue3930104"]="Off you go, Adventurer, I'll be waiting to hear your good news. I hope to see you next time... We can witness your rebirth in front of the statue of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3930201"]="Oi, Oi! Don't you see I'm busy making money! Stop bothering me all the time!\n(Hamid is extremely focused on calculating his revenue. He doesn't seem to have time to talk to you at all)",
    ["Dialogue3930202"]="Oh, I said, don't... Wait, wait! <size=26>You said you got the Rune script?!</size>\n(Hamid retreats several steps in fear, and his gold chains clangs against him)\nCan this be true!? Is this legend true?!",
    ["Dialogue3930203"]="No, I mean... Cough! Since you obtained the Rune script, you must have come to ask me to guide you to get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanic’s job advancement token</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3930204"]="(he groaned and stroaked his moustache)\nHuh? Why don't you know this? Forget it, forget it. Come with me. We have to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim St. Abbey</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3930205"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hoo... I hope the old man wasn’t lying to me... Should \"that thing\" be stored in the Abbey? Or this old chap is going to lose his hair [○･｀Д´･ ○]</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3930301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Let me feeeeel it... Eh? Yes, yes!</color></size>\n(Hamid pouts his buttocks and feels around the pillar, and suddenly jumps up in surprise)\nHere we go, here we go! This is it!",
    ["Dialogue3930302"]="Hmm, of course, it's to help you prepare for the job Advancement ceremony! If you want to be a real mechanic, the power of rune is not enough!",
    ["Dialogue3930303"]="You know, mechanics are elite <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic gear</color> operators. Whatever kind of battle they find themselves in, as long as they are carrying magic gear, they are invincible!",
    ["Dialogue3930304"]="However, due to its strength and power, magic gear is a strictly controlled item in the kingdom. In order to lease the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanic tokens</color> you must apply to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>superintendent</color>. As for this token.....",
    ["Dialogue3930305"]="Ah... Ah! Young people these days, really are so impatient!\n(Hamid pretends to be his mentor)\n... Not listen up kid, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanical core</color> is the only token that can prove the true strength of a mechanic!",
    ["Dialogue3930306"]="According to the records of professional trade unions, we can search the bodies of the ancient <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanical monsters</color> to find for their powerful magic cores. The more powerful the monster, the more powerful the magic contained in its core! Just make sure that you are well catered for and you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>do it yourself</color>! Anyway, this is the fastest and most effective way for you! Alright!",
    ["Dialogue3930307"]="All right, all right, stand in the middle of the hall... Okay! That's it! A little <size=26>further away</size> from me!\n... Now, let me show you the treasures that I have been holding on to for a long time!",
    ["Dialogue3930401"]="Um... A powerful surging magic pulse... Make no mistake! That's it!\n(Hamid looks carefully at the magical core in your hand and has a pleasant expression on his face)",
    ["Dialogue3930402"]="No, no, after all, I'm only a know-it-all uncle! Don't take such trifles to heart!\n(he waved his hand, his moustache floating proudly on his face)\nNow, you can go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> and attend your <color=#CA2E0AFF>job advancement ceremony</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3930501"]="Well... I strongly believe it. This comes not only from your determination, but also from those who help you progress. I hope that in your future adventures, you continue to follow your heart and and give those who entrust the future to you your trust and support.",
    ["Dialogue3930502"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time... To prove your dedication to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3930601"]="(the red magic core flashes flickering light, just like a living and beating heart...)",
    ["Dialogue3940201"]="... really? You got the rune from the goddess?\n(Alice shows her usual gentle smile)\nWell... I knew you could do it.",
    ["Dialogue3940202"]="(throughout your recollection Alice follows along, nodding)\nYou are an excellent student. Of course, I would like to witness your continuing growth. However, if you wish to be an <color=#CA2E0AFF>archbishop</color>, I think the thing that you lack now... Is not strength.",
    ["Dialogue3940203"]="Come with me, Adventurer. Let's go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>.\nSome things are a lot harder to express in words. I hope you can experience it yourself.",
    ["Dialogue3940301"]="... I'm very sorry, adventurer... I may have some bad news.",
    ["Dialogue3940302"]="While waiting for you, I helped the residents in the ancient city repel two waves of monsters. But during the battle, an <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient book</color> I was carrying was taken from me by those<color=#CA2E0AFF>Carat</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Majoruros</color> in the city... I think it contains magic, which is what attracted the greedy monsters. I wonder... Would you like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help me find</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient book</color>?",
    ["Dialogue3940401"]="(Alice takes the remnant page in your hand and gently puts it withing two pages of an in-tact ancient book)\n... thank you very much, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3940402"]="Yes, it can bring hope to this barren land.\nCome on, let's go to the palace square... Someone is waiting for us.",
    ["Dialogue3940501"]="(Alice, surrounded by children, turns around and soon all of their eyes are fixed on you)\nCalm down, children. Calm down. Is the Adventurer going to tell you a story?",
    ["Dialogue3940502"]=".... The Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3940503"]="Remember I told you a story about the fragments of Ymir’s Heart?\nThe protagonist of that story... Is the Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3940504"]="Wow - I want to listen!\n(the little girl quickly jumps up into your arms)\nHave you finished collecting those fragments, Adventurer?!",
    ["Dialogue3940505"]="Although it's not all set yet, the Adventurer will try his best to finish it, right?\n(Alice winks at you and hands over the book that has since been repaired)\nNow, tell your story to the children?",
    ["Dialogue3940506"]="This is a legend compiled by the church about <color=#CA2E0AFF>a brave man collecting fragments of Ymir’s heart</color>. Although the story has not been completed yet, I have told these children some parts written in the book. Now, they want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hear the follow-up</color> to the story - will you, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3940601"]="……\n(Alice looks at you with a smile as you tell the children a story. After a while, your story finally comes to an end)",
    ["Dialogue3940602"]="Eh... Later, later!\nDid the Demon Swordsman defeat the Demon King Morroc?!",
    ["Dialogue3940603"]="No, no, it doesn't matter!\nI want to know, does the thief girl end up with her true love?!",
    ["Dialogue3940604"]="Well, that's all for today's story. If I tell you it all at once, what will I tell you next time?",
    ["Dialogue3940605"]="... no harm, Adventurer. This is what I want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>grant you</color>.\nAlthough it has not been completed yet, I believe that one day, you will give it a <color=#CA2E0AFF>satisfactory ending</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3940606"]="(Alice holds the children with a smile as she looks at you)\nJust like the story in the book, you have done very well along the way, but the object of the holy light should be not only regard the dead, but most importantly the living.",
    ["Dialogue3940607"]="... and <color=#CA2E0AFF>your existence</color> is a new hope and future for all.",
    ["Dialogue3940608"]="Huh... What are you talking about? Will the Adventurer come and tell us a story next time?\n(the little girl tugs on the hem of your clothes, full of expectation)",
    ["Dialogue3940609"]="The Adventurer has more important things to be doing. After that, of course, he will come back and tell you a story.\n(Alice gently touches the little girl's head and looks at you)",
    ["Dialogue3940610"]="But now he must <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color>, where he will become his new self.",
    ["Dialogue3950101"]="(Archbishop Wolmas stroked his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily)\nI haven't seen you for a few days. It seems that you have changed quite a bit. It seems that you are ready to accept the job advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3950102"]="As I said earlier, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, which proves that you have the strength to mold the future. However, you are most probably still a bit confused how exactly to use this power",
    ["Dialogue3950103"]="That's right. Therefore, now that you have had these experiences, it's time for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>class master</color>. They will teach you how to adapt to your new career and battle skills. Maybe... There will be some exciting surprises waiting for you, Heh, heh~",
    ["Dialogue3950104"]="Off you go, Adventurer, I'll be waiting to hear your good news. I hope to see you next time... We can witness your rebirth in front of the statue of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3950201"]="Hello, Adventurer! It has been many moons since I last saw your sword, yet it is still sharp... No, should I say, is it more dazzling?",
    ["Dialogue3950202"]="... what’s this?!\n(Yadrew looks at the slate slab in your hand in surprise. When he realises, he smiles again.)\nThat's amazing! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3950203"]="I had a hunch that you would amount to great heights... But this surprise came too early! I'm so proud of you!\n... now, can guess why you came to me? You’re seeking advice with your job advancement, right?",
    ["Dialogue3950204"]="No problem, I will try my best to help you become an excellent <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color>! Come on, let's go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> in the south of the Sograt Desert. Deep underground is where we will find the the secret of your job advancement!",
    ["Dialogue3950301"]="It's hot here, isn't it, Adventurer?\n<color=#A1979FFF>That being said, it is because of the heat, we have the spark to keep on going</color>",
    ["Dialogue3950302"]="(Yadrew smiles, but doesn't directly answer your question)\nSo... From now on, this challenge belongs to you alone. You must rely on your own skills to go to the Ant Cavern’s innermost <color=#CA2E0AFF>Abyssal hole</color>. You must show no mercy and <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat anything</color> that gets in your way.",
    ["Dialogue3950303"]="I will accompany you as a witness and be the judge of whether you have successfully completed the challenge. When you are ready, please start!",
    ["Dialogue3950401"]="(Yadrew walks towards you clapping his hands in applause, the appreciation in his eyes is self-evident)\nYour performance is impeccable, Adventurer. Now, feel free to choose your favorite <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon egg</color>~",
    ["Dialogue3950402"]="You’re right. This is the key to becoming a Rune Knight - you must have your own dragon!",
    ["Dialogue3950403"]="Yes, as recent as one thousand years ago, when the Nerius Family obtained autonomy of comodo island by defeating the dragon people who inhabited it, dragons were rarely seen in the kingdom. It is well known that the only Dragons alive today live in the Dragon Nest of Comodo island, and the dragon eggs stored here by the class guild are traded by the merchants who venture deep into the Dragon Nest.",
    ["Dialogue3950404"]="The dragon egg you choose will become your closest partner in your future Adventures. You will fight side by side and grow together. Don't worry, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>think it over</color> before you <color=#CA2E0AFF>make</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>decision</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3950501"]="(the white dragon egg you are holding is warm and heavy. You can feel a heartbeat through the eggshell...)",
    ["Dialogue3950601"]="Well... I can sense strong magic from this budding partnership... You two will make a strong and reliable duo!\nCongratulations, Adventurer! Now, you can go back to Prontera and attend your Job Advancement ceremony!",
    ["Dialogue3950701"]="Well... I strongly believe it. This comes not only from your determination, but also from those who help you progress. I hope that in your future adventures, you continue to follow your heart and and give those who entrust the future to you your trust and support.",
    ["Dialogue3950702"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time... To prove your dedication to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3960101"]="(Archbishop Wolmas stroked his beard and takes a long look at you, smiling happily)\nI haven't seen you for a few days. It seems that you have changed quite a bit. It seems that you are ready to accept the job advancement.",
    ["Dialogue3960102"]="As I said earlier, the Rune is a gift from the goddess, which proves that you have the strength to mold the future. However, you are most probably still a bit confused how exactly to use this power",
    ["Dialogue3960103"]="That's right. Now that you have had these experiences, it's time for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>class master</color>. They will teach you how to adapt your battle skills to your new career. Maybe... There will be some exciting surprises waiting for you, Heheh~",
    ["Dialogue3960104"]="Off you go, Adventurer, I'll be waiting to hear your good news. I hope to see you next time... We can witness your rebirth in front of the statue of Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3960201"]="Hello, Adventurer. It’s been a while!\nWell... It's gratifying to see that you have grown up!",
    ["Dialogue3960202"]="You, you got the <size=26>rune script?!</size>\n(Melbrun's eyes widened with a surprised expression)\n<color=#A1979FFF>I know that I haven't seen you for a while, but I would never have thought, you could have become so strong....</color>",
    ["Dialogue3960203"]="... cough, hmm. In that case, are you paying me a visit to participate in the traditional sacrificial ritual of Payon?",
    ["Dialogue3960204"]="Yes, the archer guild shall only grant a Ranger token to those who prove their bravery through the sacrificial ritual. If you don’t obtain this, you wont be able to perform the job Advancement ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3960205"]="All right, come with me, Adventurer!\nPayon’s most sacred sacrificial ritual... Naturally, it should be held in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak Cave</color> where many heroes have laid to rest!",
    ["Dialogue3960301"]="……\n(Melbrun looks around and fidgets with the bow and arrow in his hand)",
    ["Dialogue3960302"]="How, how is this possible! I’ve experienced so much....\n<color=#A1979FFF>Day after day, I was thrown into the Munak Cave for monster training</color>\n(his voice is trembling. It can’t be a good memory)",
    ["Dialogue3960303"]="Well, then... I'll introduce you to the process of sacrificial ritual.",
    ["Dialogue3960304"]="This ceremony is not only a tribute to the dead, but also a test for you. You must go through the Munak Cave alone. Your objecting is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect Munak eyes</color>, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bongun fingers</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sohee hair</color>. Then to comfort the spirits of the dead you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>place</color> these as tributes on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>idol altar</color> in the deepest part of the zombie cave. Only then, the sacrificial ceremony is completed.",
    ["Dialogue3960305"]="(Melbrun waves at you)\nDon't worry, adventurer. If you are really a qualified person... At the end of the ceremony <color=#CA2E0AFF>for me</color>, someone will naturally grant you this token.\nNow, you just need to focus on completing the sacrificial ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3960306"]="Well, I'll first <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait for you at the idols and prayer altar</color>. If you are ready, get started as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue3960401"]="I had a hunch that one day I would meet you again for such an occasion, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3960402"]="There is no doubt that I am your last opponent in this trial!\nNo matter how sincere the oath may seem to be, it may still be hypocritical. Although, the arrow in your hand will never deceive people. Come on! If you're really determined to be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ranger</color>... Try your best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue3960501"]="No more words, Adventurer.\nYour arrow has proved your devotion. Now, put the tributes you collected on the altar!",
    ["Dialogue3960601"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. The sacrifice ritual has been completed.\n(Melbrun smiles and claps for you)\nThis wolf whistle is a token for Rangers.",
    ["Dialogue3960602"]="Hahaha, how extraordinary! The whistle that you are holding! This is the token that our Spirit Quellers received when they reached an agreement with the Devil Wolf living in the west of Payon. As long as you have it, those fiendish Devil Wolves will listen to your orders. In this way, no matter what trouble you get into... You have a card up your sleeve.",
    ["Dialogue3960603"]="(Qi Euin pats you on the shoulder, he looks firm and solemn)\nI entrust this token to you, that is, on behalf of all of the of all the Spirit Quellers laid to rest here I entrust it to you with their long cherished wish. I hope that in the future... No matter what the circumstances, you can recall your determination at this time.",
    ["Dialogue3960604"]="So... My todays quest is now completed. I have to go back... <color=#A1979FFF>And dance once again with those Munak, hahaha.....</color>\n(as his hearty laughter gradually dissipated into the air, the figure rising from the clouds gradually disappeared)",
    ["Dialogue3960605"]="... We should be <color=#CA2E0AFF>setting off</color> too, Adventurer?\nNow, you can take the wolf whistle... Go and make your <color=#CA2E0AFF>job advancement ceremony</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3960701"]="Well... I strongly believe it. This comes not only from your determination, but also from those who helped you on this journey. I hope that in your future adventures, you continue to follow your heart and and give those who entrust the future to you your trust and support.",
    ["Dialogue3960702"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time... To prove your dedication to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3970001"]="Welcome back, Adventurer. It's been a while since we last spoke, in which time you've become an outstanding Swordsman. It's time for the next step.",
    ["Dialogue3970002"]="If you wish to become a well-rounded <color=#CA2E0AFF>Knight</color>, you need only to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hallam</color> of the Royal Chivalry, and complete whatever trials he decrees. On the other hand, if you would rather be an indomitable <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crusader</color>, then I'm sure the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crusader Captain</color> stationed in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> will be more than happy to guide your path.",
    ["Dialogue3970003"]="Yet both will involve a commitment to stand at the vanguard of your squad and protect your teammates to the death! So, brave Adventurer, I wish you all the luck in the world on your great adventure! Fair travels!",
    ["Dialogue3970101"]="Greetings, Adventurer! It has come to my ears that you are desirous of a new class as a glorious Crusader?",
    ["Dialogue3970102"]="Bravery such as yours is to be admired, Adventurer! Know this, to become a Crusader you must possess the heart of a lion, a spirit of utter devotion, and the ability to shield your teammates from death at the vanguard of your force!",
    ["Dialogue3970103"]="I'm afraid it will take much more than a few words to prove that you are willing to live out the Crusader pledge. In what follows I will ask you a few questions which, I hope, will give me a truer picture of your stance.",
    ["Dialogue3970201"]="I see... You've given me much insight into the true state of your heart. Yet words mean little in the face of danger. I'd rather see the strength of your resolve in action with my own eyes!",
    ["Dialogue3970202"]="Come with me, Adventurer, to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color> where I have prepared a special test for you: to demonstrate whether you truly fit to wear the title of Crusader.",
    ["Dialogue3970301"]="A Crusader must be rich in the qualities of grit and perseverance! This winding mountain road provides every prospective Crusader with a true test of willpower! See these chests, Adventurer? Your task is to haul the <color=#CA2E0AFF>supplies</color> within <color=#CA2E0AFF>all the way</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color> at the top of the mountain!",
    ["Dialogue3970302"]="What, you think yourself unequal to the task?",
    ["Dialogue3970303"]="Do not be hasty to answer. I applaud you for the temerity to give yourself an honest judgement of your abilities, which does not come easily to everyone. I'm happy to provide you with a choice then.",
    ["Dialogue3970304"]="I'll allow you to decide on a fixed number of supplies to move. But I must remind you: the supplies moved and time taken will have a bearing on your evaluation. Furthermore, I must warn you dangerous monsters dwell along these mountain roads. You cannot afford to lower your guard on this journey.",
    ["Dialogue3970305"]="Then I shall await your arrival from the mountain peak! Fare thee well, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3970401"]="(You gaze over the precipice of the mountain. You cannot see the bottom, but can hear the echoes of the falling supplies. Could you retrieve them? Out of the question. You're just going to have to tell the captain what happened.)",
    ["Dialogue3970501"]="Hmm. I'm sorry to see a recruit filled with so much promise has failed to complete their task! Could you reveal to me what happened, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3970502"]="I am a little surprised your isolated path fell to a Creamy ambush... but I suppose a person of your talent made short work of the attack, correct?",
    ["Dialogue3970503"]="The supplies were encumbering your movements? But did I not forewarn you of monsters on your journey? And laid no burden on you to transport the whole amount, correct?",
    ["Dialogue3970504"]="You wanted to obtain a perfect mark?\nThen what if I were to tell you that the chests contained nothing but worthless stones, stones much beloved by the Creamy as food?",
    ["Dialogue3970505"]="Behold, this is a trial, Adventurer. I trust you can see now the true object of the test: not resolve, but self-knowledge. We Crusaders must meet the enemy head on as shields and guardians of our companions... who implicitly placed their lives in our hands.",
    ["Dialogue3970506"]="Suppose that the chests contained not rocks but emergency provisions for the front? Or that you had much more powerful monsters then Creamy to contend with? Or suppose I asked you not to transport supplies but fight a dangerous enemy? Could your companions or those that need you rely on your decision-making?",
    ["Dialogue3970507"]="Courage is to be praised in all forms, Adventurer, particularly in a trial. But courage without ability is nothing more than foolhardy recklessness. I believe you'll make the right choice in the face of danger, but only after you have gained a full understanding of your \"limits.\"",
    ["Dialogue3970508"]="I'd rather you take some time to reflect on my words, Adventurer. I invite you to come and see me again in Prontera once you have reached <color=#CA2E0AFF>class level 50</color>. If you still wish the Crusader life then, I would be very happy to hold a proper Class Advancement Ceremony for you.",
    ["Dialogue3970601"]="We meet again, brave Adventurer! From the looks of you, I take it you've decided to become a member of the heroic Crusader class?",
    ["Dialogue3970602"]="Then as your formal instructor, I must apply the most rigorous standards of the Crusaders upon you from now on. First of all I would have you familiarize yourself well with all of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crusader class skills</color> and use in battle. I've already furnished the field with suitable enemies. Let's brook no delay. Begin!",
    ["Dialogue3970701"]="Well fought, Adventurer! I'm happy that you have removed all doubt in my mind that you're a true born Crusader!",
    ["Dialogue3970702"]="Your quest is not yet over. Your next task is to defeat a group of vicious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skeleton Workers</color> at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mine</color> to obtain their <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demoncores</color>. Then purchase 10 items of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clothing Fabric</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pieter</color> and, lastly, return the fabric to me.",
    ["Dialogue3970703"]="This is a centuries-old traditional Crusader test. The forging of a Crusader's armor requires personal sacrifice. Well, enough dawdling. Be off with you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3970801"]="Excellent. These materials will allow me to furnish you with an excellent suit of armor!",
    ["Dialogue3970802"]="All in good time, Adventurer! You still have one final quest to complete while I craft your armor.",
    ["Dialogue3970803"]="Today's Crusaders benefit from all the privileges of an education at the Criatura Academy, a sure sign of practical skill and theoretical study. This moment behooves us to carry out a grand ceremony at your old institution!",
    ["Dialogue3970804"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Return to the Academy</color>, the starting point of your journey, and have a look around. I believe you may find your master and Dean Mainz waiting for you there!",
    ["Dialogue3970901"]="Heh. It's been a while since we last met, Adventurer. You've come so far! I still vividly remember your Class Advancement to become a Swordsman.",
    ["Dialogue3970902"]="Criatura Academy has no more to teach you. Congratulations on proving your potential beyond all doubt! However, you have one more task yet before graduation.",
    ["Dialogue3970903"]="Give me your Class Manual. You no longer need it.",
    ["Dialogue3970904"]="Heh. There's no need to panic. I'll present a Class Manual for your Second Class Advancement, which doubles as a graduation certificate, at the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3971001"]="It seems all is ready. Now stand in front of the sacred statue of the goddess so that I can preside over the ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3971101"]="(Archbishop Wolmas strokes his beard and takes a long, happy look at you.)\nHow you've grown in just this last week since I saw you! I believe you are ready for Class Advancement Guidance.",
    ["Dialogue3971102"]="As I said, the Rune is a gift of the goddess and a witness to your strength. But do I suppose rightly you're still a little unsure of how to use this power?",
    ["Dialogue3971103"]="Right. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and battle skills. And... may have some <color=#CA2E0AFF>exciting surprises</color> in store too. Heh...",
    ["Dialogue3971104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await your good news... and hopefully \"rebirth\" in front of Odin's Statue!",
    ["Dialogue3971201"]="Hello, Adventurer! It has been many moons since I last saw your sword. Yet it is still sharp... or should I say, dazzling?",
    ["Dialogue3971202"]="...What's this?!\n(Yadrew looks at the slate slab in your hand in surprise. He soon smiles again.)\nAmazing, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue3971203"]="I knew you'd rise to great heights, but this... has come almost too early. I'm so proud of you!\nNow I know why you've come. You seek my counsel regarding your Class Advancement, right?",
    ["Dialogue3971204"]="I'd be honored to help, but I'm afraid you could gain a much more suitable instructor than I. You'll find him in Glast Heim and, I believe, you have crossed paths before...",
    ["Dialogue3971205"]="Seyren indeed, wise Adventurer. And I trust <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> will be excited at the chance to impart his knowledge of Class Advancement to a brave Adventurer such as yourself. But I must ask you to do something before you formally set out for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>: <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain in Prontera</color>. Believe me, you will need it.",
    ["Dialogue3971301"]="It has been far too long since our last meeting, friend. You have changed, I believe. Wait—is that Holy Water in your hands?\n(Seyren's surprise quickly turns into a smile.)\nIt seems you have decided on a Class Advancement into the Royal Guard?",
    ["Dialogue3971302"]="It'd be a privilege and an honor to defend this great kingdom by your side, but I'm afraid the Royal Guard Class Advancement trial is a most complex and difficult one. It is not to be undertaken lightly—even by one of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue3971303"]="Then come with me, Adventurer. It's time we set forth for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and if all goes well... there you will find your own personal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Relic</color> amidst a place of eternal rest for countless heroes.",
    ["Dialogue3971401"]="Adventurer, if you hereby swear to uphold the tenets of the Royal Guard, then that means you also swear to give your life to the defense and benefit of the Kingdom. This is why we hold our Class Advancement trial in the company of the fallen heroes around us now—where the calamity from the Fragment of Ymir's Heart laid countless heroes to rest.",
    ["Dialogue3971402"]="History left us a record of their bravery even if Morroc ultimately destroyed Glast Heim. But many of the unfortunate warriors who fell here were also condemned to chains, cursed by monsters, unable to gain their rest.",
    ["Dialogue3971403"]="Remember these fallen heroes as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>purify their spirits with Holy Water</color>. By so doing you give credence to your eternal commitment to the Royal Guard and so gain Odin's approval.",
    ["Dialogue3971404"]="Adventurer! It is time to follow in the footsteps of heroes who have gone before!",
    ["Dialogue3971501"]="Now is the time to use the Holy Water in your hands to <color=#CA2E0AFF>purify</color> this poor hero's <color=#CA2E0AFF>spirit</color> of a monstrous affliction. This is your final test. Maintain your devotion to Odin! Hesitate not, but save him from his terrible fate!",
    ["Dialogue3971601"]="Thank you... stranger...",
    ["Dialogue3971602"]="(The warrior's vengeful spirit is consumed by countless glittering ashes under the effects of the Holy Water, which is absorbed into the bottle in your hand.)",
    ["Dialogue3971701"]="I have not seen a purification rite conducted so well or so honorably in years. Congratulations, Adventurer. You have passed our test!",
    ["Dialogue3971702"]="The Nameless Knight has also recognized the value of your convictions and consented to pass some of his courage onto you. Purified spirits are not only Relics of your Class Advancement trials, but are also key to the further purification of your armor into a vessel capable of shouldering Odin's power. Remember today, Adventurer, and your oath forever!",
    ["Dialogue3971703"]="Now you must head back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> and to the Class Advancement Ceremony that he has prepared for you. Fare thee well, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3971801"]="Well... I strongly believe it. It's a mark not only of your determination, but the trust of all who've helped you on this journey. I pray you continue to follow your heart and offer wise counsel to all on your future adventures!",
    ["Dialogue3971802"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3980101"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop strokes his beard and takes a long, happy look at you.)\nHow you've grown in just this last week since I saw you! I believe you are ready for Class Advancement Guidance.",
    ["Dialogue3980102"]="As I said, the Rune is a gift of the goddess and a witness to your strength. But do I suppose rightly you're still a little unsure of how to use this power?",
    ["Dialogue3980103"]="Right. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit your Class Master</color> who'll fill you in on everything you need to know about your new class and battle skills. And... may have some exciting surprises in store too. Heh...",
    ["Dialogue3980104"]="Off you go, Adventurer. I'll await your good news... and hopefully \"rebirth\" in front of Odin's Statue!",
    ["Dialogue3980201"]="From the look of you... very good.\n(Charles projects a friendly voice from somewhere under his hood.)\nI'll wait for you by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3980301"]="(You find Kroneika standing in front of the Magic Circle, seemingly quite well-prepared for your special ceremony.)\nI'm happy to say that you're only one step away from becoming an Elemental Envoy.",
    ["Dialogue3980302"]="Elemental Envoys were gifted with special power in days of old—to commune with and sign Contracts with Elemental Spirits. Legends tell even of powerful Elemental Envoys unifying all nine elements within themselves on our mortal plane.",
    ["Dialogue3980303"]="The Elemental Envoys and their special gifts became few and far between after the days of Ragnarok, and the Elemental Spirits also faded into obscurity. It took many years to uncover their secrets and the Spirits' Magic Circles from deep within the archives.",
    ["Dialogue3980304"]="If you're resolved to do this, simply stand in the middle of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Circle</color> and drip your blood in. Those whom the Spirits approve shall receive a Contract from their world afterward.",
    ["Dialogue3980401"]="It's a... Contract from an Elemental Spirit! Adventurer, the codex ties this \"Song of Water\" with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>certain place on this continent</color>. Your task now is to set out and find this place at once!",
    ["Dialogue3980402"]="In truth, none of us know exactly what we'll find. But I assure you this location will hold the key to your becoming a genuine Elemental Envoy!",
    ["Dialogue3980403"]="I'll go with you.",
    ["Dialogue3980501"]="You've got your hands on the complete Contract? Quick, <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the Contract in the Magic Circle</color>! Now! It's eating away at my powers!",
    ["Dialogue3980601"]="(Kroneika looks at you with delight.)\nI've no doubt of your worthiness as an Elemental Envoy, and I'm equally sure that Wolmas the Archbishop will be quite happy to hold your Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["Dialogue3980602"]="Thank you for your guidance.\n(Charles motions you to return after you give Kroneika a bow.)\nAdventurer, we should be getting back.",
    ["Dialogue3980701"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. Now we can hold a formal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>.\nIt's time to prove your worthiness before Odin.",
    ["Dialogue3990101"]="Greetings, Adventurer. I have been waiting here for a long time. The seven-day royal election is about to begin. If you have made a decision, please inform me as soon as possible so that we can carry out the follow-up calculations.",
    ["Dialogue3990102"]="Why, your vote, of course!\nHaven't you decided which successor to vote for?",
    ["Dialogue3990103"]="H-How absurd...\nThough clearly shouldering the most critical responsibility of an <color=#CA2E0AFF>elector</color>, you are still so unfamiliar with the rules and procedures of the royal election! It appears I must teach you myself!",
    ["Dialogue3990104"]="Listen, Adventurer—from today on, the candidates from the Seven Royal Families will engage in a fierce scramble for the throne. After <color=#CA2E0AFF>seven days</color>, the person with the most votes will be officially crowned at the Bloodline Banquet and become the next King of the Rune Kingdom, Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue3990105"]="During this period, all <color=#CA2E0AFF>publics</color> of the kingdom have the right to cast a vote, and the members of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>noble committee</color> will also choose the most suitable monarch according to their own inclinations. These ballots account for eighty percent of the total votes. As for the remaining twenty percent... that depends on your decision, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3990106"]="Yes, you will serve as an elector in this election. Successive electors hold the most critical vote. In the final results, this vote will account for <color=#CA2E0AFF>twenty percent</color>. In other words, your decision will largely affect the result of the royal election!",
    ["Dialogue3990107"]="But you currently have no idea of what it means to be an elector!\nThis is no good. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer a few questions</color> to make sure that you have committed all of the processes and rules to memory.",
    ["Dialogue3990201"]="At last, you're finally starting to look like an elector. However, you still have to...",
    ["Dialogue3990202"]="... You haven't received the elector notification?! How is this possible?! Ahem... A rigorous court clerk such as myself does not make such a mistake!\n(Lyanna suddenly approaches you and bares her little tiger teeth.)\nYou must have forgotten! R-i-g-h-t?!",
    ["Dialogue3990203"]="Humph! That's right.\n(She shakes her head proudly and takes out her notebook.)\nSo, please tell me which candidate you would like to vote for?",
    ["Dialogue3990204"]="Hey... Don't you know how to choose?\nBut I heard that the last king, His Majesty Tristan III, entrusted you with the crown ring... Didn't His Majesty leave you any instructions?",
    ["Dialogue3990205"]="Well... it seems that our elector may need a little time to think.\n(She closes her notebook again with a snap and smiles at you.)\nHowever, such an important matter should not be decided in a hurry, right?",
    ["Dialogue3990206"]="Do you want to talk to the seven candidates again? Of course, Adventurer.\nIt happens that today is the first day of the royal elections. According to tradition, all candidates will attend the noble assembly being held today at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Cathedral</color>, and will take turns to make political speeches to solicit votes.",
    ["Dialogue3990207"]="You can listen to their speeches and take this opportunity to talk with them. In addition, as the identity of the elector will not be disclosed to the public, there is no need to worry about candidates feigning courtesy for your benefit. Please don't worry, I will be waiting here until you make a decision.",
    ["Dialogue3990301"]="... Compared to Lord Kroneika's profound knowledge, I still have a lot to learn. I can't accept your praise. Instead... Huh?\n(Seeing you arrive, Bidal smiles and shakes his glass.)\nIt has been a while, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3990302"]="You came just in time, successor of Odin's bloodline. We are talking with Lord Bidal about his reform plan. He suggests that the assembly adopt a draft on <color=#CA2E0AFF>the construction of a public magic school</color>. Once implemented, the popularity of magic among the civilian class will greatly increase... As the noblest magic family in the kingdom, it is truly amazing that such an idea can be put forward.",
    ["Dialogue3990303"]="(Hearing the noble's compliment, Bidal shakes his head repeatedly.)\nNo, no... Actually, this was Lord Kroneika's idea. I'm just taking up the wisdom of others... I can't accept any praise... If you think this bill is feasible, please support me in the voting stage.",
    ["Dialogue3990304"]="... Since the founding of the Rune Kingdom, although there is no law expressly stipulating that civilians cannot learn magic, the concentration of resources amid the nobility results in civilians having little to no access to magic education... Before we get into that, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Nithil's</color> matter...\n(Bidal pauses and exchanges a tacit look with you.)",
    ["Dialogue3990305"]="Recently, Lord Kroneika has been wondering whether one's degree of talent is really a rigid requirement. If we give more people access to magic, will we discover countless diamonds in the rough? And this is also an opportunity to increase the strength of the ailing kingdom...",
    ["Dialogue3990306"]="Oh!<size=24>Look! </size><size=26>If it isn't my good friend!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3990401"]="(With a strong and loud voice, he gives you a bear hug.)\nI haven't seen you in so long, but you are still as energetic as ever. I'd expect nothing less from my best buddy!",
    ["Dialogue3990402"]="You're so rude, Halmod!\n(Jurgen pulls you out of Halmod's powerful embrace and gently smooths the wrinkles on your clothes for you.)\nWhen dealing with such beauty, one must be as gentle as one would caring for a flower.",
    ["Dialogue3990403"]="Jurgen, what are you talking about? One of us might become the next king! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>heart of a fierce warrior</color> is essential for any leader!\nOver the years, it is through this belief that the Lugenburg family has cultivated so many brave heroes! If we want to make the kingdom stronger, we must also strengthen our military might!",
    ["Dialogue3990404"]="No, no, no! You're wrong, Halmod! Violence is the mark of barbarism! That which can truly make the people wholeheartedly surrender their will<size=26>—is </size><size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>aesthetics</color></size><size=26>!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3990405"]="Truly beauty can overcome all obstacles! Therefore, since its establishment, Wigner's Libra Group has been committed to supporting poor artists, who can bring new ideas and change to society...",
    ["Dialogue3990406"]="Cough, cough!",
    ["Dialogue3990501"]="(A loud cough draws your attention. You look around and see Azer passing you with his head down and walking toward Wolmas the Archbishop standing nearby. There is another young noble beside him, and you can just about make out their conversation.)\nSorry, Archbishop... Cough, cough...<color=#CA2E0AFF> I'm late</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3990502"]="... Azer?\nYou look ill... What is the matter?",
    ["Dialogue3990503"]="There's no problem, just... cough, cough... I just caught a cold last night. Please don't worry. I will do the best I can in today's meeting... Cough, cough...",
    ["Dialogue3990504"]="Really...? Then, allow me to introduce Erich to all the distinguished guests present. He traveled a long way from Comodo to be here, so it was inevitable that he would experience some fatigue.\n(The Archbishop leans to one side to introduce the young man beside him to Azer.)\nYou are about the same age and should hopefully get along. Would you like to show Erich around for me?",
    ["Dialogue3990505"]="Of course, I can do that—",
    ["Dialogue3990506"]="... No, Archbishop, I must refuse. I just hope you can allow me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>decline the chance to make a speech today</color>. The Nerius family has no illusions about the throne. My aunt also hopes that I can return to Comodo as soon as possible to help her deal with some family affairs...",
    ["Dialogue3990507"]="Erich, as I told you before, it is not up to you and me to decide. The royal election has begun, like an arrow loosed from the string, its trajectory cannot be changed. It is better to face up to your responsibilities than evade them... Speaking of which, I also said the same to Aronst…\n(Upon saying this, the Archbishop looks up and scans the room.)",
    ["Dialogue3990508"]="... What's this? The speech session is about to start, and Prince Aronst hasn't arrived yet?",
    ["Dialogue3990509"]="Help... <size=26>Help me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3990601"]="Thank you, thank you... Adventurer!\n(An unfortunate-looking fellow surrounded by flies grabs your wrist, and an indescribable smell strikes you instantly, causing your eyes to momentarily go blind.)",
    ["Dialogue3990602"]="... This is Moffit, Adventurer. He is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prince Aronst's retinue</color>.\n(The Archbishop moves a little farther away, frowning and covering his nose.)\nMoffit, what have you done to yourself? What is going on?",
    ["Dialogue3990603"]="I... I accidentally fell into the sewer on my way here, and the flies got me... But there's no time for that now, Archbishop! Prince Aronst... He's been attacked!",
    ["Dialogue3990604"]="<size=24>Prince Aronst has been attacked?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3990605"]="<size=26>By Odin! How could this have happened?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3990606"]="(Moffit's words are like stones stirring up ripples in a pond. The nobles in the hall immediately begin whispering, and the Archbishop raises his hands to signal everyone to stop making noise.)\n... Everyone, please be quiet. Let's all listen to Moffit.",
    ["Dialogue3990607"]="I-It's like this, Archbishop. Earlier, Prince Aronst and I set out from our residence to attend today's candidate speech at the cathedral, but as we were passing through an alley in the east of the city, we were attacked! Although I tried my best to protect him, I still failed to stop the culprit from escaping after hurting the prince...",
    ["Dialogue3990608"]="Local Defense Force soldiers have cordoned off the crime scene and brought a doctor to treat the prince, so I finally had a chance to come here and report the news to you... I'm afraid Prince Aronst can't participate in today's meeting.",
    ["Dialogue3990609"]="... How badly was he hurt? By Odin, how could such a thing happen in this land protected by the gods...!",
    ["Dialogue3990610"]="Now, it appears that although the prince is in a coma, his condition is stable... I need to head back to the scene of the crime to help the Defense Force search for the attacker...",
    ["Dialogue3990611"]="... Alright. Given all that has happened, today's speech will be suspended temporarily. I will stay here to deal with matters. As for Prince Aronst, I believe that Bohr should also be at the scene soon. I hope you can help them<color=#CA2E0AFF> find the person who did this</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3990701"]="Sorry, I'm late. I heard Aronst was injured in an attack, so I had to get Dr. Dante to come with me to treat Aronst.\n(Bohr points at the middle-aged man treating Aronst, then looks at you.)\nHow's the situation here, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue3990702"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Moffit</color>... That's Aronst's personal guard, right?\nI heard he was also attacked. I happen to have a few questions for him, so let's go <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk to him</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3990801"]="Moffit! I've already heard about what happened, but there are still some details that I can't quite figure out. I hope you can answer my questions truthfully.",
    ["Dialogue3990802"]="Y-Yes, Lord Bohr.",
    ["Dialogue3990803"]="First, I would like to know why you passed through the alley. Starting from Gaebolg's manor, the fastest way to the cathedral should be down the central avenue. Why did you take a detour?",
    ["Dialogue3990804"]="My lord, um, the Prince prefers taking this route to the cathedral. It's a little bit out of the way, but the alley is very quiet and doesn't see a lot of pedestrians, so there's no risk of the Prince being recognized...",
    ["Dialogue3990805"]="Aronst... prefers?\n... Tell me what happened again, Moffit.",
    ["Dialogue3990806"]="Yes, my lord. The Prince and I entered the alley from the south as usual, and there were no other pedestrians at the time. When we reached this area, we heard hurried footsteps behind us. Out of the corner of my eye, I saw a figure in black rushing up to us and smacking the Prince on the head with a stick!",
    ["Dialogue3990807"]="I was scared and tried to call for help, but the figure in black tied my hands and stuffed my mouth. Then he took out a strange bottle of medicine and poured it down the Prince's throat as he lay unconsciously on the ground. I think I remember the bottle... Look, that's it! It's still by the Prince's foot.",
    ["Dialogue3990808"]="You said the attacker tied your hands and stuffed your mouth? How did you get out of the restraint and ask the soldiers for help, then?",
    ["Dialogue3990809"]="I-I also found it quite unbelievable. After the figure ran away, I tried really hard and the rope loosened! Maybe... the attacker was in a hurry, and the knot wasn't very good?",
    ["Dialogue3990810"]="This makes no sense. If the attacker already knocked down Aronst, why didn't he do the same to you? Why didn't they kill you to leave no clues behind? Aren't they afraid of you remembering their features and identifying them later?",
    ["Dialogue3990811"]="The figure was dressed completely in black and exposed nothing. If I had to say...\n(Moffit scratches his head, trying to remember the details.)\nThe attacker... was coughing or clearing his throat from time to time...",
    ["Dialogue3990812"]="(Bohr suddenly looks energized.)\nWhere is Padgar? Get Padgar here now!",
    ["Dialogue3990813"]="Yes, my lord!",
    ["Dialogue3990814"]="I think I might know who's behind all this, but we have to wait for my soldiers to bring back evidence to prove my speculation. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>see how Aronst</color> is doing. I think <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dr. Dante</color> is done.",
    ["Dialogue3990901"]="Why do you look so nervous? He's fine! He was just knocked out.",
    ["Dialogue3990902"]="He'll wake up in a while if you just leave him alone. If you can't wait, then find me a few things and I'll make him wake up immediately. What will it be?",
    ["Dialogue3990903"]="Time is of the essence, Adventurer. We need Aronst's testimony to start looking for suspects.",
    ["Dialogue3990904"]="You're right. Time is of the essence, and we need Aronst's testimony to start looking for suspects.",
    ["Dialogue3990905"]="In that case, get me <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatic Blood</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Condor Leg Bone</color>. I can concoct a Sober Potion that'll wake him up immediately.",
    ["Dialogue3991001"]="He should wake up soon.",
    ["Dialogue3991002"]="Thank you so much, Dr. Dante.",
    ["Dialogue3991003"]="Don't thank me just yet. I didn't say he'll be fine when he wakes up. The hit on his head was not lethal, but I'm not sure about <color=#CA2E0AFF>what the attacker poured down his throat</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3991004"]="I don't know what it does, but... I don't think they would have given him some kind of supplement, right? You should prepare for the worst, just in case.",
    ["Dialogue3991005"]="But if you don't even know what it is, then what can ordinary doctors do? Should we ask the alchemists for help instead?",
    ["Dialogue3991006"]="Yes, with his standing and knowledge, he should be able to help us. Here, take this bottle with you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go see Lawrence at the library</color> and ask him to help us identify the liquid in the bottle. Also, don't tell anyone what about happened to Aronst, so that we don't alert the wrong people.",
    ["Dialogue3991101"]="Well met, Adventurer. It's been a while, hasn't it? Let me guess, you have something strange that needs to be identified?",
    ["Dialogue3991102"]="Based on experience, this should be something rare again.\n(Lawrence takes the bottle, opens it and smells the content.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This smell...?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue3991103"]="Looks like you'll have to collect some ingredients for me to identify what's in the bottle. I need 3 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sea Breeze Vines</color>, some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phosphorus Soil</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocker Wing</color>. Please bring them back to me as soon as possible, because I have a very bad feeling about the concoction.",
    ["Dialogue3991201"]="(Lawrence immediately starts working once he has the ingredients. You wait for a long time, but he only shakes his head at the end.)\nAdventurer... You're going to have to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color>.",
    ["Dialogue3991202"]="What's left in the bottle is extremely complex. I compared it with all my samples, but I couldn't get a definitive answer. I'm going to take a bold guess and say that the concoction is forbidden, and that the answer can only be found at the library of the Academy.",
    ["Dialogue3991203"]="(Lawrence hands you the bottle and a sheaf of papers.)\nI've summarized the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lab Report</color> in this document. Give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> and you should get an answer. I'm sorry, but this is the most I could do.",
    ["Dialogue3991301"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>The edge of the Sea Breeze Vine appears to be corrupted after dipping... Unable to dissolve Phosphorus Soil... And burning occurred with Rocker Wing?!</color></size>\n(The Dean slams the report shut, looking pale.)\nYou... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue3991401"]="Adventurer, you must tell me how you got your hands on the forbidden concoction. This is extremely dangerous!",
    ["Dialogue3991402"]="You... can't tell me? If it's a secret you must keep, could it be about...\n(The Dean contemplates your silence, and it should not be hard for someone full of wisdom to speculate that it has to do with the election of the heir.)",
    ["Dialogue3991403"]="Never mind, Adventurer. I believe that you wouldn't do anything that violates the law, so there is no need for you to make excuses.\n(He is not angry, and taps you on the shoulder to comfort you.)",
    ["Dialogue3991404"]="If you must keep it a secret, I will not ask further questions, and you can take the data with you. I must remind you, however, that whoever got the concoction must wield immense power. Be careful.",
    ["Dialogue3991501"]="A-adventurer? You're here, too?\nAhem... What's the big deal?",
    ["Dialogue3991502"]="Big deal? You think protecting a Prince that may become the next King from assassins is overkill?\nYou really should think about your identity, Aronst! Now that you're a candidate for the throne, your life belongs to the people. If you do not take care of yourself, you're putting the entire kingdom in danger!",
    ["Dialogue3991503"]="This is not the right time for it, please forgive my outburst.\nDid you find out what was in the bottle?",
    ["Dialogue3991504"]="Lumina...? Oh no...\n(Bohr's voice shakes and his clenched fist turns pale.)\nDo they want Aronst to die... during the heir's feast?",
    ["Dialogue3991505"]="I changed my mind, Adventurer. We cannot wait any longer, and we have to arrest those who crafted the poison, or those who purchased the poison to kill Aronst. We will leave no stone unturned.",
    ["Dialogue3991506"]="(Bohr raises his hand and every Defense Force Soldier stands ready.)\nDefense Force! Proceed to the Walter Manor and arrest Prince Azer!",
    ["Dialogue3991507"]="<size=26>Yes, my lord!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue3991508"]="Bohr?! What is the meaning of this?\n(Aronst struggles to stand up, and then stumbles toward the soldier in the front, yelling with a hoarse voice.)\nStop! Stop now! I command you!",
    ["Dialogue3991509"]="Are you stopping me as an heir, or the future ruler of the Rune Kingdom? But... either way, you cannot stop me from throwing a usurper into the dungeons of Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue3991510"]="A usurper? What are you talking about? Azer would never do such a thing! Do you have any evidence?",
    ["Dialogue3991511"]="If you need evidence, I shall show you. But I hope that once we have this conversation, you will open your eyes and take a good look at the people around you without being affected by your emotions.",
    ["Dialogue3991512"]="<size=26>Padgar!</size>\nTell the Prince about every single lead that you pursued!",
    ["Dialogue3991513"]="Yes, my lord!",
    ["Dialogue3991601"]="Prince Aronst, I have been secretly following Prince Azer under the command of Lord Bohr.",
    ["Dialogue3991602"]="Secretly? Bohr, you put Azer under surveillance? How could you? He's a Prince!",
    ["Dialogue3991603"]="... Not just Azer, I put my people near every single member of the Walter family. I must extinguish every spark before they become a fire and endanger the kingdom. You still believe that Azer is your friend and brother, right? Now open your eyes and see for yourself.\nPadgar, what did Azer do today?",
    ["Dialogue3991604"]="Prince Azer left very early this morning, and I followed him into a dark alley in this area. It was a dead-end, and I didn't want to expose myself, so I waited at the alley entrance. After a while, only a figure completely dressed in black came out. Plenty of black market merchants make their deals here, so I paid the figure no mind, but...",
    ["Dialogue3991605"]="But Azer never came out of the alley, right?",
    ["Dialogue3991606"]="(The young knight nods, looking embarrassed.)\nI waited for a long time before realizing something was wrong, but there was no one in the alley. Then I remembered something about the figure in black that reminded me of Prince Azer...",
    ["Dialogue3991607"]="The coughing. For the last couple of days, Prince Azer has not been feeling well. He tried his hardest not to cough, but I am certain. The figure in the manteau was coughing when he walked past me, and it sounded exactly like Prince Azer.",
    ["Dialogue3991608"]="That'll be it for now.\nReturn to your position, Padgar.",
    ["Dialogue3991701"]="Coughing. That was the key element that helped me put everything together. Padgar heard the figure in black coughing, and Moffit said the attacker was coughing. Most importantly... Adventurer, do you remember telling me that after Aronst and Azer were attacked, Azer saved Aronst by transferring the poison to himself?",
    ["Dialogue3991702"]="Yes, I gave it some thought, including the timing at which it happened, and I realized that Azer has been looking sick since the incident. He has been having uncontrollable coughing fits...",
    ["Dialogue3991703"]="I heard you went to the cathedral today, too. Did you see Azer? Was he... showing the symptom I just described?\n(Even though the question was directed at you, Bohr's eyes never left Prince Aronst, whose face pales with each question.)",
    ["Dialogue3991704"]="But that can't be used as evidence against him! As you said, he's been sick since saving me.",
    ["Dialogue3991705"]="Do I have to spell it out for you, Aronst? I think you already know the truth. Who else knows that you take this eastern passage to the cathedral? After the assassination attempt, it did look like Azer saved you with his life. But if it was the same poison, why was he fine but you were unconscious?",
    ["Dialogue3991706"]="If you still don't believe me, ask the Adventurer what time Azer arrived at the cathedral today. Was he late? And was it right around the time when you were attacked?",
    ["Dialogue3991707"]="No, this... can't be. Azer? No...",
    ["Dialogue3991708"]="I know he is important to you, and you have a hard time accepting the truth. But I must arrest him immediately to protect you. We need to interrogate him to get more information on the antidote...",
    ["Dialogue3991709"]="No, I do not approve. You cannot arrest Azer. I'm also requesting that you stop spying on him immediately.\nThis is an order. If you still recognize my identity, then you must listen to me.",
    ["Dialogue3991710"]="Aronst!\nWhat do I have to tell you to wake you up? You are a prince, but you're also a possible candidate for the next king! I'm very disappointed at your recklessness.",
    ["Dialogue3991711"]="(You notice Aronst calming down unexpectedly, while Bohr gets angrier every second.)\nIt is precisely because I am a candidate for the heir that I cannot doubt my best friend and my brother right now.",
    ["Dialogue3991712"]="To tell you the truth, I was still feeling lost before I left today. I was not sure how I could convince the people to vote for me. I'm not very smart or wise, and I'm not talented in swordsmanship or magic. My personality is often mocked, and I know that behind my back, they say I don't look or act like a royal. So... why me?",
    ["Dialogue3991713"]="So, do you finally know the answer to your own question?",
    ["Dialogue3991714"]="Yes, I do.\n(Aronst stands up and stops the soldiers from advancing, even though the tip of their silver spears are just inches from his eyes.)\nMy sincerity, Bohr. I am sincere.",
    ["Dialogue3991715"]="I'm weak, and there are plenty of things that I can't do. And because of that, I have received a lot of help, and I believe that's what being a king is all about. Even a powerful king can't run a kingdom on his own. If I need their help and trust, then I must be open to them. Sincerity for sincerity. That is my answer.",
    ["Dialogue3991716"]="A very moving speech, Aronst. If you were in the cathedral, I think many would have thrown in with you. Unfortunately, I cannot risk your life with just... trust. What if Azer betrays you? You know that sincerity is precious, so you should also know that whoever shows sincerity first has the highest chance of being backstabbed.",
    ["Dialogue3991717"]="I am not completely clueless, Bohr. Since the poison takes seven days to kill me, that means there are still things I can do during the next seven days. If I use myself as bait, the assassins will act again. Spying on everyone in the Walter family is like trying to look for a needle in a haystack, but if you protect me with everything you've got, then you're lying in wait. As a commander, you should know better which scenario has a better chance of catching all of them at once.",
    ["Dialogue3991718"]="Aronst, you...\n(Bohr's face reflects everything that's going on in his mind, and you're not sure if he's surprised at Aronst's maturity, or shaken by Aronst's determination. You do, however, know that as the elector, it's time to make your choice.)",
    ["Dialogue3991719"]="Adventurer?! You...",
    ["Dialogue3991720"]="Are you going to tell me, \"over your dead body,\" if I want to arrest Azer?\n(Bohr waves in resignation and appears to want to compromise.)\nAlright, we can discuss this.",
    ["Dialogue3991721"]="I will stop spying on Azer as you requested, but from this moment on, you must be under the protection of the Defense Force at all times. We only have seven days to catch the culprit, and our deadline is before the end of the Bloodline Banquet. If we can't find the antidote, we will arrest Azer no matter what. This is the best I can do.",
    ["Dialogue3991722"]="I'm very moved by what you said. Maybe that's what the King wanted to see from you. I hope Azer doesn't... take your sincerity for granted.\nI envy your passion, but I'm also worried.",
    ["Dialogue3991801"]="Good to see you again, elector. Did you find the answer you were looking for?",
    ["Dialogue3991802"]="So... Who will it be? Is it <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bidal</color>, who came from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heine family</color>, and trained under Lord Kroneika for many years to become a talented mage? I heard the new bills he proposed during the noble assembly earned a lot of supporters!",
    ["Dialogue3991803"]="No? Could it be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Halmod</color>, the master swordsman with unparalleled courage? He came from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lugenburg family</color>, which controls the highest military power and will undoubtedly make the kingdom stronger? But if he becomes the king, will we be required to stay fit?",
    ["Dialogue3991804"]="Not him either? Ah, you must have fallen for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Jurgen's</color> charm!\nI knew it! No one in the kingdom... no, the entire land, can keep their cool in front of him. You are no exception!",
    ["Dialogue3991805"]="Um, could... could it be <color=#CA2E0AFF>Erich</color> from the Nerius family? Um, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nerius</color> king? That is unprecedented! After all, they care more about the profits of Comodo than the throne itself. But if it's your decision, I will respect your choice.",
    ["Dialogue3991806"]="Still? Elector, you are a unique one. Are you throwing in with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Azer</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walter</color> family? He is a quiet one, and so are his supporters. You really do have an eye for talent. It's too bad that he was on such great terms with Prince Aronst until the election...",
    ["Dialogue3991807"]="Hmm? The only one left is Prince <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aronst</color> of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gaebolg</color> family. He is the least popular... No, he is the only one who hasn't campaigned for himself. But he might be the most orthodox heir because of his bloodline...",
    ["Dialogue3991808"]="I see. I believe you have thought about this at great length before coming to your decision, and I will report it to the lords of the committee.\nThank you for your contribution to the election. Please look forward to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bloodline Banquet</color> in seven days. We have not had one of these in decades, and it will definitely be unforgettable.",
    ["Dialogue3991901"]="(A young man lies on the ground with his eyes closed and the back of his head swollen. A <color=#CA2E0AFF>black puddle</color> forms on the ground under his mouth.)",
    ["Dialogue3992001"]="(A mostly empty <color=#CA2E0AFF>glass bottle</color> is on the ground not far from him. A little bit of <color=#CA2E0AFF>black liquid</color> is inside the bottle.)",
    ["Dialogue4000101"]="Sigh... If this goes on, it will be the end of the Gray Family's farm. This is an unprecedented crisis.",
    ["Dialogue4000102"]="Oh no! They've finally come! Our farm is under attack by Fabres! Help us! If you don't, this'll be the end of Green Cotton Farm!",
    ["Dialogue4000201"]="This is giving me such a headache! These Lunatic are ruining everything!",
    ["Dialogue4000202"]="It's all because of these Lunatics! They've blocked the trade route outside the South Gate, affecting our store's supply chain! Drive them away for us!",
    ["Dialogue4000301"]="Stay calm... I was once a great knight. I mustn't let this get to me.",
    ["Dialogue4000302"]="Those Rockers have been making a racket every night. I haven't been able to sleep a wink. They have violins, but just use them to make noise. Please do something about them, I'm begging you.",
    ["Dialogue4000401"]="All squads, attention! We need to drive away the Condors and show them who are the masters of Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue4000402"]="Are you the adventurer who's come to help drive away the Condors? Excellent! Teach them a lesson they won't forget!",
    ["Dialogue4000501"]="Hello, adventurer! Since you're here, I take it you've seen the Kingdom Defense Force's request?",
    ["Dialogue4000502"]="In short, the Thief Bugs at the cemetery are running amok. We hope you adventurers can deal with them.",
    ["Dialogue4000503"]="Do you remember what I told you? NEVER DOUBT YOUR COMMANDING OFFICER! Now go!",
    ["Dialogue4000601"]="......",
    ["Dialogue4000602"]="Naturally! It doesn't matter how hard your fists are, they won't do much to Chonchons. Are you the adventurer who's come to accept the request? I don't care if you use a weapon or magic, just hurry up and get rid of those buzzing pests!",
    ["Dialogue4000701"]="The Chivalry must always be ready to fight the monsters of the sewers.",
    ["Dialogue4000702"]="There's nothing to fear about the other monsters. However, we have to take those Familiars seriously, or else they'll escape to the surface. Please help us suppress their attacks!",
    ["Dialogue4000801"]="Hmm? Look how skinny you are. Won't you get gobbled up by a Thief Bug?",
    ["Dialogue4000802"]="I'm just thinking about your safety. Recently, the Female Thief Bugs and Male Thief Bugs have been fighting a heated battle in the sewers. According to their habits, when one side wins, they'll turn around and attack the humans.",
    ["Dialogue4000803"]="You need to keep their numbers balanced so they fight each other for longer. This time, deal with the Female Thief Bugs first!",
    ["Dialogue4000901"]="Hmm? Look how skinny you are. Won't you get gobbled up by a Thief Bug?",
    ["Dialogue4000902"]="I'm just thinking about your safety. Recently, the Female Thief Bugs and Male Thief Bugs have been fighting a heated battle in the sewers. According to their habits, when one side wins, they'll turn around and attack the humans.",
    ["Dialogue4000903"]="You need to keep their numbers balanced so that they fight each other longer. Hmm... The Male Thief Bugs have been a bit rampant lately. Keep them in check!",
    ["Dialogue4001001"]="The monsters on the second floor of the sewers are getting unruly. We need an adventurer to help us!",
    ["Dialogue4001002"]="Very good! The Drainliars on the second floor pose a major threat. They'll breach our defensive line if we let our guard down. Show them that we're not to be messed with!",
    ["Dialogue4001101"]="Hello, I made this request as an ordinary person, not as a member of the Chivalry. I hope you'll keep it a secret from Captain Rodney.",
    ["Dialogue4001102"]="Ahem, don't pay too much attention to the details. I want you to exterminate the Plankton in the sewers!",
    ["Dialogue4001201"]="Boohoo... What will I do when those Hornets return?",
    ["Dialogue4001202"]="Wow! You've come at just the right time, adventurer! Those Hornets have gone on a rampage in the Mjolnir Mountains. Even the Petites have had to hide from them. There's nothing we can do! Please punish them for us! I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue4001301"]="Hmph! Are you the only one? This Dustiness crisis isn't something that can be handled by just one person! Don't come back crying when things go south!",
    ["Dialogue4001302"]="I'll trust you this time, but only because you look so confident. Those monsters may look like Chonchons, but don't underestimate them. If you do, you'll be in for a world of hurt!",
    ["Dialogue4001401"]="Argh... My head hurts...",
    ["Dialogue4001402"]="I originally planned to come to this chaotic place to search for the inspiration lost in the depths of my soul. I never expected that these noisy things would have occupied this place. Help me shut them up!",
    ["Dialogue4001501"]="I can't stand those raucous Yoyos!",
    ["Dialogue4001502"]="The monkeys that live in Labyrinth Forest often make trouble in the Mjolnir Mountains and West Gate. This time, they've even decided to come after the millet I planted!",
    ["Dialogue4001503"]="Unforgivable! I can't abandon my duty as a guard, so I'll leave it to you to teach those Yoyos a lesson!",
    ["Dialogue4001601"]="Since you've accepted my request, you probably won't be trying to talk me out of it by saying something stupid like Stainers are good insects?",
    ["Dialogue4001602"]="Hmph, someone has finally come. Customers have recently been complaining that there are Stainers among the gold ore. If we don't get rid of them, it won't be long before no one will buy our ore.",
    ["Dialogue4001701"]="I really should talk to my father about moving away from here as soon as possible. Sigh, forget it. What am I thinking?",
    ["Dialogue4001702"]="Adventurer, a-are you afraid of spiders?",
    ["Dialogue4001703"]="Great! I knew I was right to ask an adventurer for help! I'm especially afraid of Argoses, but it's absolutely impossible to persuade my father to move away. Please help me! Reduce the number of Argoses, even if it's just a little bit!",
    ["Dialogue4001801"]="No, if things are left like this...",
    ["Dialogue4001802"]="Everyone in Labyrinth Forest is in danger! I need your help!",
    ["Dialogue4001803"]="According to recent observations, the forest's beetle population is out of control. It will be a disaster if they're allowed to eat too many plants! Their numbers have to be brought down!",
    ["Dialogue4001901"]="Huff...puff! Creating the sharpest weapon is my goal in life!",
    ["Dialogue4001902"]="I heard that there's a creature called a Mantis, and that their weapons can rival a blade of steel. If the rumors are true, it would be a perfect material for my craft! Adventurer, help me verify if it's true!",
    ["Dialogue4002001"]="In short, we received many reports from the church about frequent Savage-related injuries in Labyrinth Forest. You look tough, but I suggest you don't push yourself too hard. Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue4002002"]="Good, I wish you the best of luck.",
    ["Dialogue4002101"]="Damn! If I ever catch one of those Martins...",
    ["Dialogue4002102"]="Our mine has been plagued by unexplained accidents that have stopped humans wanting to work for us!",
    ["Dialogue4002103"]="Thanks to those Giearth experts, we realized that it was all because Martins were digging holes in the ore vein! You have to get rid of them! If not, the mine won't be able to operate!",
    ["Dialogue4002201"]="The light of Odin is spread across the land, and our church's vision is to bring salvation to all. For those who pass away with hatred in their hearts, we must guide them in the right direction.",
    ["Dialogue4002202"]="By Odin, those miners who died with resentment in Mjolnir Mine have not been able to transcend to the afterlife due to the darkness of the underground. We must help them.",
    ["Dialogue4002301"]="Sigh... How worrying.",
    ["Dialogue4002302"]="I heard that Roda Frogs have recently absorbed dark energy from the Shipwreck and become really tough. Although I'm retired, I still worry about the members of the fleet operating in those waters",
    ["Dialogue4002303"]="Haha! The former novice has truly come a long way! Good, I'll leave everything to you!",
    ["Dialogue4002401"]="Hehehe, this is a once-in-a-lifetime discovery.",
    ["Dialogue4002402"]="Of course! Once I complete my investigation into this creature, I will forever be a leading name in the field of monster research!",
    ["Dialogue4002403"]="A monster that looks like a cross between a Marina and Plankton has recently been discovered on the Shipwreck. Help me test its fighting ability. I'll thank you at the end of my academic paper, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4002501"]="Are you the adventurer who's determined to go up against the Mukas? Very good!",
    ["Dialogue4002502"]="Remember, although Mukas have sharp spines, there's no need to fear their cold radiance if your body is tough enough! Show them how powerful humans are!",
    ["Dialogue4002601"]="The Shipwreck... Truly a place of misfortune.",
    ["Dialogue4002602"]="There are some rumors about this ship that could be true or false. You'll find out when you get the chance. But, by Odin... We discovered it, so we have the responsibility to bestow Odin's radiant blessing upon its crew and send them to the afterlife in peace.",
    ["Dialogue4002701"]="By Odin! These vile pirates got exactly what they deserved in ending up like this!",
    ["Dialogue4002702"]="But Odin is kind. We must strive to save even the most evil of beings. Let us send them to the afterlife! Maybe they'll correct their evil ways in the next life.",
    ["Dialogue4002801"]="Ant Cavern has become a really dangerous place recently. We are here to stand guard under the order of Commander Bernard. Who are you?",
    ["Dialogue4002802"]="I see. Then let me explain the situation first. The ants, led by Maya, live deep in Ant Cavern. It used to be that they were rarely seen, other than when they would occasionally search the surface for food.",
    ["Dialogue4002803"]="However, many recent eyewitness reports claim that Andres of the ant vanguard force have appeared in the desert and even stolen food from the Chamber of Commerce. It seems the ants have turned their attention to the surface for some reason.",
    ["Dialogue4002804"]="Eliminate some of the Andres, and show them that humans are not to be trifled with!",
    ["Dialogue4002901"]="Hmm... It looks like the process isn't very reliable when it comes to taming wild Pecopecos.",
    ["Dialogue4002902"]="Oh, welcome. I've hired so many adventurers to teach those unruly Pecopecos a lesson, but every one has been beaten black and blue. Do you want to give it a go?",
    ["Dialogue4002903"]="Yes, domesticated Pecopecos are adorable, but wild ones are extremely violent! Don't underestimate them!",
    ["Dialogue4003001"]="The desert... So this is what it's really like?",
    ["Dialogue4003002"]="I originally thought the desert was a quiet and ethereal place, but it's actually noisy and wild. Those Metallers are ruining the atmosphere! Adventurer, please silence them for me! This is not the desert I imagined!",
    ["Dialogue4003101"]="The situation is getting worse and worse.",
    ["Dialogue4003102"]="The Andres took no notice of our warning. Instead, their attacks against humans intensified. These Andres are nothing like they used to be. They're far more powerful.",
    ["Dialogue4003103"]="Don't act rashly now. They can't expand without the Pieres, which means that losing Pieres will have a huge impact on them. Bypass their soldiers and target the weaker Pieres to deal them a fatal blow!",
    ["Dialogue4003201"]="These stones that are in my way...",
    ["Dialogue4003202"]="It's those Golems. Although they are cowards and not at all aggressive, they've blocked the route used by the merchants.",
    ["Dialogue4003203"]="Use the method of your choice to persuade them to move on.",
    ["Dialogue4003301"]="We're about to face the main force of the ants. The situation is urgent, so I'll keep things short.",
    ["Dialogue4003302"]="The Deniroes are the ants' main fighting force. They're on a completely different level! We must disrupt their formation quickly before they can gather together.",
    ["Dialogue4003401"]="Vitatas... Truly a rare sight.",
    ["Dialogue4003402"]="They are Maya's loyal guards. Only once we defeat them will the Kingdom Defense Force have the chance to attack the leader. Adventurer! Help us bring this to and end!",
    ["Dialogue4003501"]="Sigh... Although I'm a pet merchant, I sometimes feel that the world is really unfair.",
    ["Dialogue4003502"]="Have you heard of Desert Wolves before? Their cubs are either caught for their fur or domesticated to become pets. Their hatred for humans is beyond measure. I can't blame them though. If I was one of them, I'd feel just the same.",
    ["Dialogue4003503"]="Those poor animals attack any human they see in the desert. I know this request may be a bit strange coming from me, but please... please set them free.",
    ["Dialogue4003601"]="What a pain in the neck. We can't get near the pharaoh's sarcophagus until we deal with those guards.",
    ["Dialogue4003602"]="Whoa! You're here! Adventurer, are you interested in the past of the Egyptian empire?",
    ["Dialogue4003603"]="Hehe, as an archaeologist, this epic history is simply a feast for the mind!",
    ["Dialogue4003604"]="It's just that those accursed Soldier Skeletons are standing so close to the pharaoh's sarcophagus! Get rid of them for me so I have a chance to get close to it!",
    ["Dialogue4003701"]="Adventurer, have you ever encountered a black animal in the pyramid?",
    ["Dialogue4003702"]="Yes, to be precise, it's a fox with nine tails. They are auspicious creatures in Payon culture, but the ones in the pyramid seem to radiate evil and misfortune.",
    ["Dialogue4003703"]="They must be causing my bad luck! Adventurer, eliminate them for me!",
    ["Dialogue4003801"]="The Lugenburg Family has always been interested in legends of the strong and powerful. So, please help me verify this legend!",
    ["Dialogue4003802"]="Some of the Soldier Skeletons in the pyramid have retained the archery skills they possessed in life. It's said that their archery skills can rival those of our best hunters! Help me test if it's true!",
    ["Dialogue4003901"]="......",
    ["Dialogue4003902"]="Yes, I'm sorry... When I think of those horrible Argiopes, I can't help... It's all my father's fault! Why do we have to live in such a scary place full of bugs?!",
    ["Dialogue4003903"]="They've even come to the mine! Adventurer, please help me!",
    ["Dialogue4004001"]="The discipline of magic has a long and profound history. There are still many ways to use magic that we have yet to discover.",
    ["Dialogue4004002"]="For example, those ancient Egyptian warlocks in the Sphinx employ a form of magic that originates from the system used in the Egyptian empire thousands of years ago. It is very valuable for research.",
    ["Dialogue4004003"]="Fight them and record data on their magic.",
    ["Dialogue40041001"]="Folks, hurry and find me some fresh blood!",
    ["Dialogue40041002"]="Don't move more than 5 meters within 5 seconds to prevent being detected by a swarm of mosquitoes!",
    ["Dialogue40041003"]="An Adventurer has reached the destination in Round 1. Rainbow stars have been refreshed! Keep it up!",
    ["Dialogue40041004"]="An Adventurer has reached the destination in Round 2. Rainbow stars have been refreshed! Keep it up!",
    ["Dialogue40041005"]="Watch out! The edge of the platform is about to collapse!",
    ["Dialogue40041006"]="Watch out! The edge of the platform is collapsing again!",
    ["Dialogue40041007"]="Watch out! The platform is becoming increasingly dangerous!",
    ["Dialogue4004101"]="The church has always found it difficult to treat adventurers who have been attacked by Side Winders. They are ancient creatures, and we need to collect more information to develop a treatment plan.",
    ["Dialogue4004102"]="Please be careful. We don't have a real cure yet.",
    ["Dialogue4004201"]="Alberta has experienced a spate of Marina poisonings recently. Sigh, as lord of the city, I'm most concerned.",
    ["Dialogue4004202"]="Adventurer, please help Alberta resolve this situation. The Wigner Family will reward you handsomely!",
    ["Dialogue4004301"]="As the secrets of ancient Egypt are gradually uncovered, a series of shocking events has come to light.",
    ["Dialogue4004302"]="The ancient Egyptian pharaoh Osiris had so many living people buried with him! Sigh... By Odin, the cruelty!",
    ["Dialogue4004303"]="I heard that even the masons who built his tomb were mercilessly sealed underground. Let us spread the benevolence of Odin and help them transcend to the afterlife.",
    ["Dialogue4004401"]="You're here at last! Any later and those fish would have poked my boat full of holes!",
    ["Dialogue4004402"]="I'm talking about those hyperactive Phen! Ordinary wood doesn't stand a chance against their spear-like bills! Hurry up and deal with them, or I'll never be able to set sail!",
    ["Dialogue4004501"]="As the secrets of ancient Egypt are gradually uncovered, a series of shocking events has come to light.",
    ["Dialogue4004502"]="The ancient Egyptian pharaoh Osiris had so many living people buried with him! Sigh... By Odin, the cruelty!",
    ["Dialogue4004503"]="I heard that even the carpenters who built his tomb were mercilessly sealed underground. Let us spread the benevolence of Odin and help them transcend to the afterlife.",
    ["Dialogue4004601"]="Did the cruelty of the ancient Egyptians know no bounds?!",
    ["Dialogue4004602"]="They even committed the brutal act of making dogs into mummies! Do you know that these dogs retain the friendly personalities they had in life, but they can't protect themselves from being corrupted by dark energy?",
    ["Dialogue4004603"]="It's... it's just so sad. We must set them free!",
    ["Dialogue4004701"]="Do you know who we archaeologists hate the most?",
    ["Dialogue4004702"]="That's right! Tomb robbers! Out of pure greed, they wantonly destroy history, causing countless truths to be lost forever!",
    ["Dialogue4004703"]="What's worse is that the tomb robbers who die from the curse of the pyramid become obstacles that stop others from getting closer to the truth! Please send them to hell! Don't show them any mercy!",
    ["Dialogue4004801"]="Are you surprised that I would make request?",
    ["Dialogue4004802"]="Even the Great Sage's quest for knowledge never ends. This is especially true when it comes to ancient dragons, as we humans know far too little about them. For example...",
    ["Dialogue4004803"]="Are Petites dragons or not?",
    ["Dialogue4004804"]="Haha, this is something that can only be verified by getting adventurers like you to fight them.",
    ["Dialogue4004901"]="Have you ever heard the legend of Medusa?",
    ["Dialogue4004902"]="Yes, it is a monster from the legend of another world, but it has not yet appeared in Midgard. However, there's a monster in the pyramid that seems quite similar to it.",
    ["Dialogue4004903"]="Yes, I want you to collect enough information to prove that it doesn't have the power to turn people to stone. We don't have any potions capable curing petrification.",
    ["Dialogue4005001"]="......",
    ["Dialogue4005002"]="I-I... Of course I'm scared! This is Baphomet we're talking about! What will we do if Baphomet is resurrected?",
    ["Dialogue4005003"]="Y-you're right! It's only Baphomet Jr. that's been seen so far. I'm begging you, adventurer, please help me find out what's going on!",
    ["Dialogue4005101"]="Tsk... What a pain. Did you know that even mummies can wake up in a bad mood?",
    ["Dialogue4005102"]="You heard right. Don't look at me like that. Just calm them down so they don't interfere with my research.",
    ["Dialogue4005103"]="Yes, I don't care if you destroy them or persuade them in some other way. Just deal with them.",
    ["Dialogue4005201"]="Adventurer, are you interested in undersea adventures? Fighting with Obeaunes, for example?",
    ["Dialogue4005202"]="Hahaha! Don't look so surprised. Obeaunes may look weak, but most adventurers are helpless against them!",
    ["Dialogue4005203"]="They've been looking down on us humans lately. So, what do you say? How about you show them what we're made of?",
    ["Dialogue4005301"]="Hey! Adventurer, can you help me with something? I'll reward you handsomely!",
    ["Dialogue4005302"]="Hmm... It's no fun when you're so serious. Fine... The fleet we work with told me that their usual fishing waters have been occupied by Marcs.",
    ["Dialogue4005303"]="Although they're usually quite gentle, they will ferociously attack anyone who encroaches on their territory. You'll have to defeat them thoroughly and decisively.",
    ["Dialogue4005401"]="Have you heard of an amazing fish called a Deviace? I bought one when I was a child and kept it in a small tank. It's gaping mouth was so cute.",
    ["Dialogue4005402"]="It eventually grew too big, so I had to release it into the sea. I've been wanting another for years, but I haven't been able to buy one. Their deep sea habitat makes them hard to come by.",
    ["Dialogue4005403"]="Please! I'll pay you top Zeny if you can catch one!",
    ["Dialogue4005501"]="Ahem, are you the warrior who's come to carry out the secret mission?",
    ["Dialogue4005502"]="Hmm... Yes, I-I am Mystery Man #1! I want you to go into the forest to teach those fearsome wolves a lesson and bring back some wolf pelts. But you can't tell anyone about it!",
    ["Dialogue4005601"]="Meow! Can you really do it all by yourself? Those Snakes that live under the tree are always bullying me. Surely you can't bear to see a cute cat like me being picked on, right?",
    ["Dialogue4005602"]="It's just that it's beneath me to use my mighty Meow Punch on such low-level monsters! It-it's definitely not because I'm afraid!",
    ["Dialogue4005701"]="Just to double-check, are you sure you're not scared of those densely-packed, squeaking, slithering, disgusting multi-legged creatures?",
    ["Dialogue4005702"]="Great! The Arclouzes in the pyramid have seriously affected the Eden Group's excavation. Please eliminate those annoying pests as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue4005801"]="I heard that Skeletons have recently been wandering around the entrance to Munak Cave and trying to breach the barrier. It seems you need to put a stop to their antics.",
    ["Dialogue4005901"]="Ah! I'm so annoyed! How is it that those lumbering Elder Willows are always able to squash the exact vegetables I want to pick with such accuracy?",
    ["Dialogue4005902"]="I can't stand them! Since they refuse to watch where they're going, please teach them a lesson for me!",
    ["Dialogue4006001"]="According to the records, Munaks move by jumping around. Is it possible that they only walk normally when fighting? Oh, this is fascinating!",
    ["Dialogue4006002"]="So, I'll need you to prove this for me! Fight the Munaks and tell me what you observe, hehe!",
    ["Dialogue4006101"]="According to the records, Dokebies always have a smile on their faces. Is it possible that they won't grimace even when attacked? Oh, this is fascinating!",
    ["Dialogue4006102"]="So, I'll need you to prove this for me! Fight the Dokebies and tell me what you observe, hehe!",
    ["Dialogue4006201"]="Recently, I heard a rumor that a monster called the Greatest General has the blueprint of the divine weapon once used by the great general!",
    ["Dialogue4006202"]="Every blacksmith dreams of seeing this treasure. Would you be able to get it?",
    ["Dialogue4006301"]="Not all monsters are evil, like those Horongs in Munak Cave. Rumor has it that they are actually the wandering souls of departed heroes.",
    ["Dialogue4006302"]="Since it's impossible to resurrect them, let's save their souls another way!",
    ["Dialogue4006401"]="I've always been curious... do you think those monsters that swing hammers every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["Dialogue4006402"]="—Oh?! I can tell that you want to find out through combat, right? I must say, I admire your straightforward and manly approach. Go get 'em!",
    ["Dialogue4006501"]="Sigh, Nightmares have been tormenting my family to the point of exhaustion. Please help us! I'm begging you!",
    ["Dialogue4006502"]="According to the fortune teller, these Nightmares were created by a Giant Whisper in a cave in Payon. You have to weaken it to get rid of the Nightmares!",
    ["Dialogue4006601"]="I've always been curious... do you think those monsters that swing hammers every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["Dialogue4006602"]="—Oh?! I can tell that you want to find out through combat, right? I must say, I admire your straightforward and manly approach. Go get 'em!",
    ["Dialogue4006701"]="I've always been curious... do you think those monsters that swing hammers every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["Dialogue4006702"]="—Oh?! I can tell that you want to find out through combat, right? I must say, I admire your straightforward and manly approach. Go get 'em!",
    ["Dialogue4006801"]="Hmm... Do you think the Jakks' pumpkins are their actual heads or just something they wear?",
    ["Dialogue4006802"]="If it is something they wear, then it will be a very interesting material. Why don't you see if you can bring back some Pumpkin Heads?",
    ["Dialogue4006901"]="Hey, can you help me test how strong this armor is?",
    ["Dialogue4006902"]="Let me think... Hmm, the armor you're wearing seems to be a good reference. I know! Why don't you go to Geffen Dungeon 1F and see how long you can survive being attacked by Ghouls?",
    ["Dialogue4007001"]="(Bertha covers her face in excitement.)\nAh! Don't you think that a Goblin would make the perfect pet?",
    ["Dialogue4007002"]="Think about it. The nimble body, those pointy ears, and the round head... Ahhh! They're just as cute as Dorams!",
    ["Dialogue4007003"]="Hehe, a research subject that can also be a pet... I'm getting excited just thinking about it! There's only one thing for it: I'll need you to catch me a Goblin!",
    ["Dialogue4007101"]="This is great! Someone is finally willing to come! Since you have the guts to participate in a weapon strength test that requires you to kill orcs, it must mean you're very confident in your weapons and abilities?",
    ["Dialogue4007102"]="Yes! Take that confidence with you to the Orc Dungeon!",
    ["Dialogue4007201"]="Hehe, I've thought of a brilliant idea for this year's costume party!",
    ["Dialogue4007202"]="I bet I'll be the center of attention if I dress up as a Marionette! But art that's all about looks has no soul. Can you help me find out how Marionettes move and fight?",
    ["Dialogue400891101"]="Huff— Wheeze—\n(The flames slowly pulsate.)",
    ["Dialogue40181001"]="Both faction bosses are activated, spawning in the central area of the map in 20 seconds.",
    ["Dialogue40181006"]="<color=#d25f62>Red Faction</color>'s entire lane of towers has been destroyed. Their <color=#ffcd55>Base</color>'s Final DMG Reduction is reduced by 50%.",
    ["Dialogue40181007"]="All towers of the <color=#d25f62>Red Faction</color> have been destroyed. Their <color=#ffcd55>Base</color> will now take full damage.",
    ["Dialogue40181008"]="<color=#8a98f8>Blue Faction</color>'s entire lane of towers has been destroyed. Their <color=#ffcd55>Base</color>'s Final DMG Reduction is reduced by 50%.",
    ["Dialogue40181009"]="All towers of the <color=#8a98f8>Blue Faction</color> have been destroyed. Their <color=#ffcd55>Base</color> will now take full damage.",
    ["Dialogue4050101"]="Whoa! There are much fewer Fabres here! This is great! Maybe we really will be able to eliminate all of them one day!",
    ["Dialogue4050102"]="In the past, Green Cotton Farm used to collect Fabre Silk Thread. I don't know when they turned from friend to foe. Now they cause problems so often that we have no choice but to rely on adventurers for help.",
    ["Dialogue4050103"]="Hahaha! I'm sorry, people do like to ramble on when they get old. Thank you, adventurer. I think I'll ask you for help again next time!",
    ["Dialogue4050201"]="Haha! Thanks to your hard work, our goods have finally arrived! Nice job! If they get up to mischief again, I'll go straight to you!",
    ["Dialogue4050301"]="Oh! Peace at last! I'm sure I'll have a good night's sleep tonight. I just hope those Rockers stay quiet for a very long time.",
    ["Dialogue4050401"]="Excellent work! But those Condors won't give up so easily. I'll remember your efforts!",
    ["Dialogue4050501"]="Nicely done! The kingdom will only become more peaceful with the assistance of adventurers like you!",
    ["Dialogue4050601"]="Phew, that's much better. I'll get you to help me again if the Chonchons come back! The Lugenburg Family needs an expert Chonchon killer like you! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue4050701"]="The Chivalry is grateful for your assistance! Those pests should be under control for now.",
    ["Dialogue4050801"]="Great! The Male Thief Bugs should have the upper hand in their battle now. We'll let them be proud of that for a while, hehehe!",
    ["Dialogue4050901"]="Hehehe! I bet those Female Thief Bugs are feeling pleased with themselves right now. We'll let them be proud of that for a while.",
    ["Dialogue4051001"]="The Chivalry is grateful for your assistance! Those vile Drainliars probably won't give in so easily though!",
    ["Dialogue4051101"]="Yes! There's a lot less Plankton now. Good job!",
    ["Dialogue4051102"]="Harm? Isn't looking terrifying the greatest harm?!",
    ["Dialogue4051103"]="...I'm sorry... To be honest, I'm terrified of Plankton. If Captain Rodney ever finds out...",
    ["Dialogue4051201"]="Haha! I'm so happy to see those Hornets take such a hit! It's a shame Great Sage Kroneika said that Hornets are an indispensable part of the Mjolnir region's ecosystem. This is as far as we can go.",
    ["Dialogue4051202"]="I don't know when they'll come back again, but it shouldn't be a problem as long as there are adventurers around!",
    ["Dialogue4051301"]="Hahaha! I had no idea adventurers were this amazing!",
    ["Dialogue4051302"]="Great! I thought all adventurers were unreliable. I never knew there'd be someone like you among them! I'll be depending on you in the future!",
    ["Dialogue4051401"]="Oh... This refreshing tranquility... This is the Labyrinth Forest I was looking for!",
    ["Dialogue4051402"]="(Best not disturb him for now. He looks really enthralled.)",
    ["Dialogue4051501"]="...Those Yoyos... I'll never forgive them!",
    ["Dialogue4051502"]="They actually came to take revenge on me! I won't let them get away with it! I'll get adventurers to punish them every day!",
    ["Dialogue4051503"]="(Best leave for now. He looks really angry.)",
    ["Dialogue4051601"]="Hmph, it seems that it's more reliable to get adventurers to do this sort of thing. Those guys from the kingdom's army refused to help because of what Kroneika said. Well, since they're supposed to be \"good insects,\" I'll just ask you for help again in the future.",
    ["Dialogue4051701"]="I feel a lot better now that I don't have to see those hairy legs anymore, hehe! You're so reliable!",
    ["Dialogue4051801"]="Although your efforts might not seem very effective in the short term, Labyrinth Forest will remember your contribution! Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue4051901"]="It was a tough battle? Hahaha, this is great. Who could have imagined that such an amazing material would exist in the natural world? Now, which adventurers should I ask to help me test it?",
    ["Dialogue4052001"]="Excellent work. We'll stay here until the situation improves, and ask you for assistance again if we need it.",
    ["Dialogue4052101"]="You've eliminated almost all of them? ...No... those Martins are very cunning; they won't give up this easily. We can't let our guard down!",
    ["Dialogue4052201"]="By Odin! Thank you for your assistance. Too many people have fallen while searching for new resources in the mine over the past 1,000 years. We have a long way to go...",
    ["Dialogue4052301"]="I recently received a letter from a former colleague, and heard that you helped out a lot on the Shipwreck! It seems I was right to ask you for help, hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue4052401"]="Hmm... In regard to their fighting ability, they've inherited the toxicity of Marina and the non-aggressiveness of Plankton? Isn't that a rather wasteful evolution? I wonder why it happened. Should I investigate further...",
    ["Dialogue4052402"]="(She seems lost in her thoughts. It's probably best to not disturb her.)",
    ["Dialogue4052501"]="No good... Although you're strong enough, you're not tough enough. I hope you will train hard and become truly powerful!",
    ["Dialogue4052601"]="This ship used to be full of warriors who were loyal to the Rune Kingdom, but look at it now. Sigh... Even Odin is a little unfair sometimes.",
    ["Dialogue4052701"]="May Odin protect them and ensure they walk the right path in their next life.",
    ["Dialogue4052801"]="Thank you very much. However, we don't know how the ants will react to what we've done. We must stay vigilant and be prepared for anything!",
    ["Dialogue4052901"]="How was it? Was I right?",
    ["Dialogue4052902"]="Hahaha, at least you came back in one piece. That's more than I can say about the others!",
    ["Dialogue4053001"]="......",
    ["Dialogue4053002"]="It's quiet now, but why do I feel so irritated? Is it because I don't belong here? Could it be that I am the wrong note in the chord?",
    ["Dialogue4053003"]="(He seems to be troubled over something strange. Best leave him alone for now.)",
    ["Dialogue4053101"]="Very good! This means their expansion will be somewhat hindered. We also need to find a way to make them less effective in battle. Please check out the other requests!",
    ["Dialogue4053201"]="Thank you very much. I instructed the merchants to proceed along the route when you drove the Golems away.",
    ["Dialogue4053202"]="At the Libra Group, we never fail to deliver. This is our way of doing things. Please come again.",
    ["Dialogue4053301"]="Excellent! The ant armies are confused and won't be able to mount any effective attacks for some time. Thank you for buying us the time we need!",
    ["Dialogue4053401"]="The loss of the Vitatas has dealt them a huge blow!",
    ["Dialogue4053402"]="No, we'll never be able to say we've won unless we defeat Maya. But this is as far as we can go for now. What will they do next?",
    ["Dialogue4053501"]="May they rest in peace... Sigh.",
    ["Dialogue4053601"]="Sigh... Is there any other way?",
    ["Dialogue4053602"]="These soldiers will never die as long as the pharaoh's power exists. It will simply put the bones back together. I think we need to try another way!",
    ["Dialogue4053701"]="Adventurer... I have some bad news for you.",
    ["Dialogue4053702"]="When a Matyr is killed, all its misfortune is transferred to the one who killed it.",
    ["Dialogue4053703"]="Hahaha! Just kidding! Adventurer, the look on your face was priceless. Even if gods and ghosts really do exist, Odin will surely protect us. There's nothing to worry about!",
    ["Dialogue4053801"]="Well, it looks like the rumors are true. Very good, hahaha! The new archer mercenaries have some suitable training targets now!",
    ["Dialogue4053901"]="I-I'm definitely going to think of a good way to discuss leaving Mjolnir Mountains with my father.",
    ["Dialogue4053902"]="Living like this every day isn't good for my heart.",
    ["Dialogue4054001"]="What an incredible description. It seems that this data is nowhere near enough. To learn more about their magic, we'll need data from more adventurers from a variety of perspectives.",
    ["Dialogue4054101"]="This is valuable information. It will definitely come in useful. Thank you so much for your contribution, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4054201"]="Haha, adventurer, the sailors of the Alson Fleet have been praising you non-stop lately. Someone even came up with a nickname for you: Marina Slayer!",
    ["Dialogue4054202"]="Marinas may look cute, but they cause heavy losses to Alberta every year. This request will be available for a long time, so come back and help us again if you're interested!",
    ["Dialogue4054301"]="May they enjoy a peaceful afterlife, free of tyranny.",
    ["Dialogue4054401"]="Hahah! That was fun! The Phens usually love to show off, but look at them now. You'll be my first person I call if they dare cause trouble again!",
    ["Dialogue4054501"]="May they enjoy a peaceful afterlife, free of tyranny.",
    ["Dialogue4054601"]="Humans are such cruel creatures. The more I interact with pets, the stronger this feeling gets. I hope everyone can treat animals well.",
    ["Dialogue4054701"]="Hmph, they've finally gone to where they should have gone in the first place.",
    ["Dialogue4054702"]="Sympathy? No, this is what they deserve. I'll never feel any sympathy for them.",
    ["Dialogue4054801"]="Hmm... The way they fight is somewhat similar to the young dragons in the history books. This confirms my suspicions.",
    ["Dialogue4054802"]="But I'll need more information to get closer to uncovering the truth. Thank you, adventurer, for verifying this crucial matter for me.",
    ["Dialogue4054901"]="So it's just a legend. Isis does not possess such an ability. Still, we'll keep collecting information from more sources. After all, we can't rule out the possibility that you're just very lucky.",
    ["Dialogue4055001"]="Baphomet Jr.'s? Great. They're strong for their size, but at least the situation is still under control.",
    ["Dialogue4055002"]="I'll continue to track down information about them! I'm terrified, but monster researchers conduct research for the purpose of saving others! I hope you'll assist with my studies again next time. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue4055101"]="Hmm? ...Oh, thanks, but please don't interrupt my research. I'll ask you for help again next time.",
    ["Dialogue4055201"]="The Obeaunes seem to be behaving themselves recently. Ahem, but I have some bad news.",
    ["Dialogue4055202"]="It seems that more Obeaunes are looking to challenge you. You're something of a celebrity to them now, hahaha! Sorry about that! It looks like you might have a lot on your plate.",
    ["Dialogue4055301"]="Sigh... The situation hasn't improved at all. Those Marcs are far more determined to defend their territory than I expected.",
    ["Dialogue4055302"]="I expect this to be a very long battle. We'll definitely have the chance to work together again in the future.",
    ["Dialogue4055401"]="The Deviaces were ferocious and would rather die than surrender. You couldn't even catch one? Is this the end of my wish?",
    ["Dialogue4055402"]="...No, I won't give up. I must find another Deviace like the cute and gentle one I had before!",
    ["Dialogue4055501"]="How did it go? Where are the wolf pelts?",
    ["Dialogue4055502"]="...What? The wolves ran too fast for you to get their pelts? But...\nArgh! How will I prove my courage to the kids if I don't have a wolf pelt?!",
    ["Dialogue4055601"]="Meow! I bet those stinky snakes know what I'm capable of now, right? To express my gratitude, I will let you squeeze my paw. You must feel very honored, human? Meow!",
    ["Dialogue4055701"]="Whoa! Finished already? Please lend us a hand again if the Eden Group encounters any more trouble in the future!",
    ["Dialogue4055801"]="Thank you! I hope our comrades guarding the entrance to Munak Cave will be able to live a peaceful life as a result of your kind deeds.",
    ["Dialogue4055901"]="Great! And if the Elder Willows don't remember, then I'll invent a dish that uses bark as an ingredient! Hmph!",
    ["Dialogue4056001"]="...What? Munaks also jump when they fight? I think I need to make a note: Death makes people forget the proper way to use their legs.",
    ["Dialogue4056101"]="...What? The Dokebies don't stop smiling? I think I need to make a note: This monster is very good at managing its emotions.",
    ["Dialogue4056201"]="What?! You didn't find the blueprint? Could the rumors be false? No, you must have just been unlucky!",
    ["Dialogue4056301"]="Thank you for everything you've done. May the souls of the departed heroes rest in peace!",
    ["Dialogue4056401"]="Oh? So the Flail-wielding Goblins aren't that strong? Although that doesn't surprise me. After all, they aren't swinging my Drubby every day, hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue4056501"]="(Hugo breathes a long sigh of relief after hearing your words.)\nPhew... I can't thank you enough. I hope my family can sleep peacefully from now on!",
    ["Dialogue4056601"]="Oh? So the Mace-wielding Goblins aren't that strong? Although that doesn't surprise me. After all, they aren't swinging my Drubby every day, hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue4056701"]="Oh? So the Mace-wielding Kobolds aren't that strong? Although that doesn't surprise me. After all, they aren't swinging my Drubby every day, hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue4056801"]="So, how did it go?",
    ["Dialogue4056802"]="<size=24>—What?!</size> Jakks die after they lose their Pumpkin Head?! So that means... By Odin! What a cruel thing we've done!",
    ["Dialogue4056901"]="...Wow! You managed to come back without any injuries?! I wasn't expecting that. Could it be that the Zombies haven't grown any stronger even after all this time? Sigh...\n(Kennan shakes his head regretfully.)",
    ["Dialogue4057001"]="So? So the Goblins didn't want to be captured?",
    ["Dialogue4057002"]="Oh yeah! That spirit of resistance is really exciting.\n(Bertha's eyes light up with excitement.)\nI'll never give up!",
    ["Dialogue4057101"]="...Wow! Your weapon is still in perfect condition even after such a fierce battle?! The rumors might be true after all—a weapon's strength is affected by its user's ability!",
    ["Dialogue4057201"]="...Aha, I see! So Marionettes always float in midair? Fortunately, that isn't a problem to someone as skilled in magic as me!",
    ["Dialogue4100101"]="Sigh, there are too many new students at the moment. We've run out of the juice we need to teach cooking. It's just one thing after another!",
    ["Dialogue4100102"]="Really? Can I? Thank you! You're such a reliable adventurer! The juice of the Mandragoras that grow just outside Prontera is the best juice for cooking!",
    ["Dialogue4100201"]="What is the difference between the biological structures of Willows and ordinary trees? I'm really curious.",
    ["Dialogue4100202"]="Enthusiastic adventurer! I need specimens! Haha, don't be scared. I just need some of their branches!",
    ["Dialogue4100301"]="Hmm... We have far too little material to fix all these brushes... Oh! Adventurer, we're a little busy today...",
    ["Dialogue4100302"]="Oh, it's you! We're in urgent need of some Savage Bebe Bristles! It's the best material for crafting and fixing brushes!",
    ["Dialogue4100401"]="This feels kinda cruel...",
    ["Dialogue4100402"]="Ohh! That's it! If you adventurers are the ones to do it instead...",
    ["Dialogue4100403"]="Cough, cough, I need the Grass sprouting atop the Wormtails in the Labyrinth Forest!",
    ["Dialogue4100404"]="Don't you worry! The Grass will grow again very quickly even if it's been pulled in half. Once I finish cooking with this batch of Grass, I'll leave some aside for you.",
    ["Dialogue4100501"]="Hello, adventurer. You'll find I do things differently from Bishop Wolmas. I hope you understand.",
    ["Dialogue4100502"]="According to our research, the Venom from Spores contains a highly effective detoxifying element. If you could carefully bring some back for us, the church will reward you handsomely.",
    ["Dialogue4100503"]="Be careful you don't become a victim yourself and become a burden to the church.",
    ["Dialogue4100601"]="If Eclipse Fur is no good, maybe we can make do with the Baby Desert Wolf Fur...",
    ["Dialogue4100602"]="Please gather some Ecli—I mean, Baby Desert Wolf Fur for me!",
    ["Dialogue4100603"]="No, please pay my wishes no mind. I wouldn't risk another's life for the sake of my own desires. Just some Baby Desert Wolf Fur would do. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue4100701"]="The Honey from a Creamy... Oh, I do miss the taste of eating it raw...",
    ["Dialogue4100702"]="Ohh! Wonderful timing! You will now go in search of this continent's greatest dessert! Honey from a Creamy!",
    ["Dialogue4100703"]="That Honey you just collected from a Creamy... The smell is intoxicating! Never have I known such culinary perfection as a gourmet! Come, savor this with me!",
    ["Dialogue4100801"]="Oh no... If what's written in the book is true...",
    ["Dialogue4100802"]="Quick! You must help me! If we continue to ignore them, the world is doomed!",
    ["Dialogue4100803"]="The Pine Nuts the Cocos are always holding! If they store too many of them in their nests, it'll crack the earth, causing the continent to split and drift apart! Humanity will be destroyed...! We have to stop them!",
    ["Dialogue4100901"]="The mysterious magic contained within those Leaves is very intriguing... Meow.",
    ["Dialogue4100902"]="Meow, meow?! Don't you remember what I wrote on the Mission Board, meow? I will take no questions, meow! Just bring me the Leaves atop the Smokies' heads, meow!",
    ["Dialogue4101001"]="This... This is completely unreasonable.",
    ["Dialogue4101002"]="This is a biological miracle! The Sasquatch migrated such a long distance from its original home in the northern side of the continent to the Labyrinth Forest!",
    ["Dialogue4101003"]="Please bring me their Fur! I must see the evidence with my own eyes!",
    ["Dialogue41011001"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#528fff>Galin Horne Horn</color> has sounded! Let the real battle begin!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41011002"]="The pillar is currently in use by others and cannot be operated.",
    ["Dialogue41011003"]="The small pillar has been opened! Your faction earns 100 points!",
    ["Dialogue41011004"]="The central pillar has been opened! Your faction earns 200 points!",
    ["Dialogue41011005"]="<color=#f76b7a>The small pillar has been opened! The red faction earns 100 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41011006"]="<color=#7cb7ff>The small pillar has been opened! The blue faction earns 100 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41011007"]="<color=#f76b7a>The central pillar has been opened! The red faction earns 200 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41011008"]="<color=#7cb7ff>The central pillar has been opened! The blue faction earns 200 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue4101101"]="Do you know which race is the most proficient in mining?",
    ["Dialogue41011011"]="The <color=#ffe788>small pillar</color> will be activated in <color=#ffe788>10 seconds</color>! The faction that opens it earns <color=#ffe788>100</color> points!",
    ["Dialogue41011012"]="The <color=#ffe788>central pillar</color>will be activated in <color=#ffe788>10 seconds</color>! The faction that opens it earns <color=#ffe788>200</color> points!",
    ["Dialogue41011013"]="All unopened small pillars will return to an inactive state in 5 seconds!",
    ["Dialogue41011014"]="The unopened central pillar will return to an inactive state in 5 seconds!",
    ["Dialogue41011015"]="<color=#ffe788>It's the final moment—<color=#528fff>double the speed</color> of earning points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41011016"]="Both safe zones are gone! Time for the final showdown!!",
    ["Dialogue4101102"]="Correct! They say the Giearths each hold a book of Mining Secrets that's passed down from generation to generation, safely kept out of the hands of humans.",
    ["Dialogue4101103"]="Heheheh... Hey, adventurer, what if you went and...",
    ["Dialogue4101201"]="A dish made out of Hydra Tentacles is the ultimate offering during the Strouf Festival. I don't know which buffoon came up with that idea but everyone bought it. I seriously doubt the Stroufs care for such a disgusting meal.",
    ["Dialogue4101202"]="Ah, forget it. The bigwigs are the bosses here and what they say goes. Go gather up some Hydra Tentacles for me. I'll deal with the rest.",
    ["Dialogue4101301"]="Blasted Doppelgangers! They tarnish the honor of the Nerius family! Please, defeat the skeletons bearing stone axes and bring me proof of the deed.",
    ["Dialogue4101401"]="Blasted Doppelgangers! They tarnish the honor of the Nerius family! Please, defeat the skeletons bearing knives and bring me proof of the deed.",
    ["Dialogue4101501"]="Hmm? Oh, it's you. The church thinks highly of you. I hope you will continue to meet my expectations.",
    ["Dialogue4101502"]="We successfully extracted a type of poison from our Spore Venom research last time. We believe the same poison can be found in large quantities in the Snake Gall of an Anacondaq, so I would like you to bring us Snake Gall this time.",
    ["Dialogue4101503"]="By the way, forget what I said last time. The church will spare every effort to save your life if you were poisoned.",
    ["Dialogue4101601"]="By the gods, what an astounding creature... Its body must contain so many secrets!",
    ["Dialogue4101602"]="Myst! Its body composition is unlike anything I know! The Dark Crystal within its body must be its core. Please bring it to me.",
    ["Dialogue4101603"]="Hmm... Should I consult Miss Chiskleen, or Master Norten next?",
    ["Dialogue4101701"]="What... What should I do...?",
    ["Dialogue4101702"]="Adventurer, if you were given the choice of death or realizing your dreams, each with a 50% chance of coming true, which would you choose?",
    ["Dialogue4101703"]="You're right. This dream is worth staking my life! Please, adventurer, bring me Scorpion Venom!",
    ["Dialogue4101801"]="Adventurer, do you think Magnolias are artificially created?",
    ["Dialogue4101802"]="What kind of person would fry an egg then transform both the egg and the pan into a single magical creature? What could a masterful chef like that possibly be thinking?",
    ["Dialogue4101803"]="I must know! Please bring me the Eggs from Magnolias.",
    ["Dialogue4101901"]="......",
    ["Dialogue4101902"]="(She nods and shows me a picture book with writing on it.)",
    ["Dialogue4101903"]="(I wish to know the secrets hiding underneath the cloth of a Whisper. Please bring me the Whisper's Cloth.)",
    ["Dialogue4101904"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue4102001"]="The Mummy-making process is the stuff of legend, but no one has cracked the secret to crafting the bandages yet. This won't prove a problem for me though!",
    ["Dialogue4102002"]="I ran out of bandages from my last research. Adventurer, please bring more pieces of Mummy Cloth to me!",
    ["Dialogue4102101"]="After the veritable baptism of Scorpion Venom I received, I find myself reborn! Now there's nothing I fear!",
    ["Dialogue4102102"]="Albertan fishermen never haul up giant Vadon from the deep sea. Do you think their meat is as tasty as their shallow-water counterparts? I'd love to find out!",
    ["Dialogue4102103"]="Please bring me some Deep Sea Crab Meat! I'll reward you handsomely!",
    ["Dialogue4102201"]="Do you know what's the toughest natural-occurring material according to legend?",
    ["Dialogue4102202"]="It's the Cornutus Shell! It's said the Shell can withstand the penetrative force of a sledgehammer! I happen to have some samples here that require testing. Please use them to try and break through the Shell of a Cornutus!",
    ["Dialogue4102203"]="There's no better way to test out the capabilities of my newly-forged sledgehammers!",
    ["Dialogue4102301"]="The evolution of a Sky Petite is the puzzle of the century...",
    ["Dialogue4102302"]="Hmm? The Great Sage Kroneika is also researching about the Petite dragons? Sad to say, my aspirations aren't so grand. I only wish to find out why the Petite dragons evolved into sky and ground variants despite being in the same location and having the same ancestors.",
    ["Dialogue4102303"]="As luck would have it, I've run out of the Dragon Wings used for my research. Can you help me gather a few more? I feel like I'm close to a breakthrough...",
    ["Dialogue4102401"]="Even though they're obstructing my research, some of these monsters are deserving of my respect.",
    ["Dialogue4102402"]="It's said the Anubis were once the Pharaoh's loyal guards. They were still in their prime when they gave up a life of wealth and luxury willingly to be buried alongside their Pharaoh.",
    ["Dialogue4102403"]="Please bring me the Anubis Helms that they wear. Don't forget to treat them with the utmost respect.",
    ["Dialogue4102501"]="Have you ever had the urge to eat strange-looking creatures?",
    ["Dialogue4102502"]="Hah! The innocence of youth! The reason these creatures look so hideous is to keep themselves from being eaten! Just like that Swordfish...",
    ["Dialogue4102503"]="No, I demand the strangest of the strange. I want the Swordfish Fin! My intuition as a seasoned gourmet demands it! Go forth!",
    ["Dialogue4102601"]="Tell me. Which do you think is sturdier? My sledgehammer or Minorous's?",
    ["Dialogue4102602"]="Hahaha! I think so too. Find a way to bring me some Hammer Shards. I'd like to see the craftsmanship of Ancient Egypt for myself.",
    ["Dialogue4102701"]="Just the other day, the men at the port told me they use cuttlefish Ink to write. I don't believe it! There's no way natural-occurring Ink would be superior to man-made ones! Help me gather some!",
    ["Dialogue4102702"]="Oh, right. While I still don't believe them, I feel I should warn you anyway. They say Cuttlefish Ink stains take more than three months to wash off, so do mind yourself in battle.",
    ["Dialogue4102801"]="(Juke drunkenly shakes his head.)\nHic! Must brew... The finest wine... Need...",
    ["Dialogue4102802"]="Earth Spirit Essence from.... Wormtail... I need them... Hic!",
    ["Dialogue4102901"]="(Juke struggles to keep his heavy eyelids half-open.)\nOh... You're here! It's not... strong enough...",
    ["Dialogue4102902"]="I need... an Intact Bear Paw... from Bigfoot! Need it! Hic!",
    ["Dialogue4103001"]="Heh! I hear the Anubis in the Sphinx Cavern are draped in Gold Jewelry. If you bring me some, I'll be rich—Ahem! I mean, I'll be able to conduct some research.",
    ["Dialogue4103101"]="Have you seen the Bongun in Munak Cave? It's said the Rune of Resurrection on their foreheads can bring back the dead. I think if I...\n(Cho Bin clenches his fists.)\nNevermind that. I don't care if it's just a rumor, I have to try!",
    ["Dialogue4103201"]="Sigh. Hey, adventurer, mind helping me with this fashion dilemma?",
    ["Dialogue4103202"]="I'm about to create a retro-styled skirt, but I can't make heads or tails of the material or pattern of the traditional female Payon outfit.",
    ["Dialogue4103203"]="It'd be a great help if you could bring back some thousand-year-old Robe Cloth from a Sohee!",
    ["Dialogue4103301"]="You must be the grownup who can defeat Eggyras. Then again, are you really a grownup if you can't defeat Eggyras?",
    ["Dialogue4103302"]="Anyway, I'd like some Egg Shells from the Eggyras. Please pass them to Miss Villard in Seocho Market. She promised she'd make me a cool-looking Egg Shell Hat!",
    ["Dialogue4103401"]="Did you know there are many ancient monster legends in Payon? The most famous among them is the legend of Nine Tail and it... Uhm...\n(W's face turns red.)",
    ["Dialogue4103402"]="The legend says the Nine Tail can transform into a very beautiful woman. Each of its Tails possesses the magic to beguile the hearts of men! So I was wondering... if you could bring back some Tails of a Nine Tail for me...",
    ["Dialogue4103403"]="I—I'm just curious about the legend! That's all!",
    ["Dialogue4103501"]="Tch, Payon is experiencing a retro revival recently, but not everything from the past is worth learning from.",
    ["Dialogue4103502"]="Take for example the Skeleton Generals in Munak Cave...\n(Leming lowers his voice.)\n<size=18>I hear they frequently lop off their own necks accidentally with the scimitar they wield.</size> <size=18>What a terrible design flaw, don't you think?</size>",
    ["Dialogue4103503"]="If you could bring me some samples of Long Scimitars from the Skeleton Generals, I'd love to use them as examples of what not to do when forging weapons.",
    ["Dialogue4103601"]="According to the Chamber of Commerce's internal investigations, merchants have been frequently losing their coin while delivering goods recently and each incident has occurred while passing through Goblin Forest. It doesn't take a genius to figure out who's responsible.",
    ["Dialogue4103602"]="No one in Rune Kingdom, be it man or monster, has the right to meddle in the business of Wigner Chamber of Commerce. Please teach those Goblins a lesson and retrieve the stolen Gold Coins.",
    ["Dialogue4103701"]="Did you know? Some monsters are capable of inadvertently sparking a new fashion trend. Just look at the Orc Warriors in Orc Village!",
    ["Dialogue4103702"]="Fashion magazines predict metallic gray will be trendy color of the year next year. If I can craft new headgear by emulating a Orc Warrior Helm, I'd be at the forefront of fashion!",
    ["Dialogue4103703"]="Ho hum. No one in Geffen dares to question my taste! Now then, go bring me back some Helm samples please.",
    ["Dialogue4103801"]="Human adventurer, bring me some Soft Bristles from the Kobolds in Kordt Forest. Quickly, meow. They may not look like much, but they're top-notch enchantment material, meow!",
    ["Dialogue4103802"]="<size=24>Meeeow?!</size> <size=24>Don't be ridiculous, meow!!</size>\nI, Meylande, am a brilliant and noble Doram, who would never step one paw near the stinky domain of a Kobold, meow!!\"",
    ["Dialogue4103901"]="It seems we only bought ourselves a few days of calm. Merchants are once again reporting lost coin while delivering goods through the Goblin Forest. This is causing the Chamber of Commerce a lot of grief.",
    ["Dialogue4103902"]="There's no two ways about it. Everyone knows Goblins love all things shiny, especially Gold Coins and Diamonds. They just can't resist!",
    ["Dialogue4103903"]="Could I trouble you to do a search of those Goblins? I have no doubt you'll find a good chunk of lost coin that belongs to the Chamber of Commerce!",
    ["Dialogue4104001"]="Hmm...? Could it be? You're the one who's willing to help me obtain Sticky Mucus from Orc Zombies?",
    ["Dialogue4104002"]="O-of course I'm not going to use something that disgusting in my cooking! It's just that Jeanne told me the mucus is the primary ingredient for crafting wolf deterrent sprays...",
    ["Dialogue4104101"]="Monsters like the dragons that have existed since ancient times tend to hold many mysteries that are difficult to solve. For example, many experienced scholars believe to this day that dragons are inextricably linked to ancient magics.",
    ["Dialogue4104102"]="Much more research has to be conducted to prove whether this is true. Adventurer, could you kindly bring this old man some Sky Petite Dragon Scales to use as research material?",
    ["Dialogue41341002"]="Someone else is activating the mechanical device—you cannot operate it right now!",
    ["Dialogue41341005"]="<color=#f76b7a>The small device has been activated! The red faction earns 100 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41341006"]="<color=#7cb7ff>The small device has been activated! The blue faction earns 100 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41341007"]="<color=#f76b7a>The large device has been activated! The red faction earns 200 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41341008"]="<color=#7cb7ff>The large device has been activated! The blue faction earns 200 points!</color>",
    ["Dialogue41341011"]="The <color=#ffe788>small mechanical device</color> will be activated in <color=#ffe788>10 seconds</color>! The faction that opens it earns <color=#ffe788>100</color> points!",
    ["Dialogue41341012"]="The <color=#ffe788>large mechanical device</color> will be activated in <color=#ffe788>10 seconds</color>! The faction that opens it earns <color=#ffe788>200</color> points!",
    ["Dialogue4200101"]="My foolish disciple thinks he's his own master now with just a fishing rod in hand. Hmph, he's gone fishing but I suppose some experience will do him good. Staying sheltered would just breed more idiocy.",
    ["Dialogue4200102"]="Could you bring him something to eat? When I was younger, I enjoyed chewing on some Hode jerky when I was tired from training.",
    ["Dialogue4200103"]="Yes, he must be exhausted and at a loss on Izlude Island right now. If he's handed his master's secret treasure right now, it'll serve as encouragement and boost his morale.",
    ["Dialogue4200201"]="Sigh... I send letters to my daughter every week, but she never writes back. I wonder if she'll ever forgive me...",
    ["Dialogue4200202"]="She's the only successor to this farm. We got into a huge argument when she decided to go to Prontera to become a monster researcher. She packed up and left for Criatura Academy after that. I couldn't stop her.",
    ["Dialogue4200203"]="I beg you. I heard she's become an exceptional monster researcher in Prontera. All I want to do now is respect her wishes and hope for her forgiveness... Please. Give her this letter.",
    ["Dialogue4200301"]="Sigh... What do I have to do to earn senior Dobbin's approval?",
    ["Dialogue4200302"]="Do you have someone you admire, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue4200303"]="To fight shoulder-to-shoulder with your idol and strive toward that alluring horizon... That's my dream, but senior Dobbin always refuses me and is very harsh about it. He won't let anyone tell me why either.",
    ["Dialogue4200304"]="Please! Help me find out why Dobbin keeps rejecting me!",
    ["Dialogue4200401"]="Sigh... How could someone be so foolish?",
    ["Dialogue4200402"]="Adventurer, I'm sure you've seen the message on the Mission Board. You don't mind destroying a young woman's dream—no, fantasy, right?",
    ["Dialogue4200403"]="Right then. Do you know about the fountain in the center of the garden on Izlude Island? I don't know when it became known as the Spring of Fate, but anyone who makes a wish about love there tend to have the wish come true.",
    ["Dialogue4200404"]="My best friend, Maina, is obsessed with this urban legend. She's there every single day, fantasizing about that person.",
    ["Dialogue4200405"]="I have proof that person won't ever be coming home, but I don't want to be the one who destroys her fantasy. Please deliver this package to her. She'll understand once she sees what's inside.",
    ["Dialogue4200501"]="Adventurer! This is an emergency!",
    ["Dialogue4200502"]="Based on what I read in the books recently, the world is about to be destroyed!",
    ["Dialogue4200503"]="I urgently need the second volume of this book from the library! Please hurry to Izlude Island and ask the librarian for it, then bring it to me! Here's the list!",
    ["Dialogue4200601"]="Here's the report. Please hand it over to the monster researcher, Bertha Gray. It contains vital treatment plans for monster poison. Make sure it's delivered to the right person.",
    ["Dialogue4200701"]="We've been having a lot of trouble communicating with our colleagues working in the pyramid. To make things worse, the monsters have blocked off our supply line too.",
    ["Dialogue4200702"]="Please help us transport these basic supplies to our colleague in the pyramid, adventurer. His name is Clauro. As for what he looks like... Uh, just look for a human. You should have no trouble identifying him.",
    ["Dialogue4200801"]="Heh heh, you're one lucky adventurer! Did you hear? After the Rose Red Tavern and Desert Green Tavern shared their recipes with each other, they came up with even more delicious specialty drinks!",
    ["Dialogue4200802"]="The recipe this time is... Hm... Yes, this is the one! Please give this Heflee. I'm confident it'll be an explosive desert hit!",
    ["Dialogue4200901"]="Ah, adventurer. Kafra Corp. is ever at your service! You must be... here to accept a mission, correct?",
    ["Dialogue4200902"]="You see, Kafra Corp. has been having difficulty reaching our Morroc branch due to increased monster activity. Please help us deliver this documentation to Ms. Taylin, the person in charge of the Morroc branch.",
    ["Dialogue4201001"]="Alberta... Will this lovely port city be my final destination?",
    ["Dialogue4201002"]="Do you know what it feels like to be drawn to a flower, adventurer? Her long flowy black hair, her warm friendly smile... And the pure innocence in her eyes!",
    ["Dialogue4201003"]="No! I won't fear her rejection! I won't give up! I'm in the middle of writing fine poetry for her... But before that, I'd like you to help me deliver this love letter to her.",
    ["Dialogue4201101"]="Ahh! Where has that lazy rascal gone off to now? Blasted idiot!",
    ["Dialogue4201102"]="That's it! I'm in no position to support a layabout! You there, adventurer! Go summon Pascal back here.",
    ["Dialogue4201103"]="If he's not working, you should be able to find him at the bar street. Tell him... Tell him the boss is very angry, so he should hurry and sneak his way back.",
    ["Dialogue4201104"]="That Pascal... Ah, forget it. It's a long time ago anyway. Just go tell him to make his way back.",
    ["Dialogue4201201"]="You must be familiar with Captain Carew if you're an adventurer, right?",
    ["Dialogue4201202"]="Great. I hope you can deliver this letter to Marko.",
    ["Dialogue4201203"]="And... Mm, if possible, please let me know Marko's answer too.",
    ["Dialogue4201301"]="Oh... You're here. This is the letter.",
    ["Dialogue4201302"]="(Vienna hands you an envelope. It says: Please do not open the seal if you are not Miss Clarice, or you will be responsible for the consequences!)",
    ["Dialogue4201401"]="Hello, this is Kafra Logistics. How may we be of service?",
    ["Dialogue4201402"]="Ah, ok, thank you! (Clarice takes the letter but doesn't look at it, and places it to the side)",
    ["Dialogue4201403"]="Threatening letters are sent to me all the time and the contents... Well, I don't read letters that have not been hand-delivered.",
    ["Dialogue4201404"]="The person who sent the request is probably not going to pay you in person. Why not go to the Mission Board and have another look?",
    ["Dialogue4201501"]="It got delivered? Take it. Sigh... I really hope that person finds someone else to torment. Then again, there's no one else as kind as me who'd take it.",
    ["Dialogue4201502"]="(Vienna sighs, and hands you another envelope. It says: If you are not the sender, please don't open the seal, or you will be responsible for the consequences!)",
    ["Dialogue4201601"]="Ah, adventurers. Are you here about the Mission?",
    ["Dialogue4201602"]="Perfect timing. I have a new batch of mechanical weapons here. Could you help me deliver them to the Kafra Warehouse?",
    ["Dialogue4201603"]="When inspiration comes, my hands simply cannot rest!",
    ["Dialogue4201701"]="Hello, this is Kafra Logistics. How may we be of service?",
    ["Dialogue4201702"]="Ah, these... Are these goods from Rupert again? He's been having a high output recently. Looks like the storage fees will have to be increased at times like these...",
    ["Dialogue4201703"]="Ah, okay, we'll do the warehouse transaction procedures right away!",
    ["Dialogue4201801"]="Oh, are you the adventurers who accepted the request? Hurry over here, these are all hot out the pot!",
    ["Dialogue4201802"]="There's this dish, this, and this one...",
    ["Dialogue4201803"]="There are just so many guards, and I'm in charge of their meals. I've been busy recently and can't spare the time, so I put up a request.",
    ["Dialogue4201804"]="After all, we can live here safe and sound thanks to their hard work.",
    ["Dialogue4201805"]="Okay, that's about it! Hurry along and hurry back! Don't let it get cold!",
    ["Dialogue4201901"]="Hold it, adventurer. What are you doing here?",
    ["Dialogue4201902"]="Ah! You're here on behalf of that person? No wonder I could smell deliciousness from afar!",
    ["Dialogue4201903"]="Thank you, adventurer, but we can't walk away from our posts to eat while standing guard, so please leave it here.",
    ["Dialogue4201904"]="Sigh... If this goes on, we're all going to get fat.",
    ["Dialogue4202001"]="…Oh? The successor of Odin’s bloodline… What a coincidence, we meet again.",
    ["Dialogue4202002"]="Shhh… The past need not be mentioned again. Today, I am just an ordinary person who wants to celebrate the festival with you.",
    ["Dialogue4202003"]="Hmm? I think I saw the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sky Companion Badge</color> in your hand... Is that a New Year's gift for me?",
    ["Dialogue4202004"]="…Thank you, Adventurer. Happy New Year.",
    ["Dialogue4202201"]="I hate people who eat their words! Adventurer! Please let Ronald know I'm not gonna talk to him anymore!",
    ["Dialogue4202301"]="I lost track of how many times this had happened. I will personally inform Klein that Ancille would be the most upset one before he pays off the debt.",
    ["Dialogue4202401"]="Newborns always cheer people up. Yvette and I would like to send our blessing to the family. I wonder if she has finished making the accessory?",
    ["Dialogue4202501"]="Are you talking about the accessory for the baby? It will be ready to go after a little bit of touch-up. Tell Benson not to worry about it and to take good care of himself.",
    ["Dialogue4202601"]="Great! I hope they will like our gift! Haha!",
    ["Dialogue4202701"]="I've put all the questions on the Mission Board. You will be well compensated once you return with the answer.",
    ["Dialogue4202801"]="I was right not to hold my breath on Humphrey's business strategies... Hey, give him my shopping list, and no peeking!",
    ["Dialogue4202901"]="I see... that's why. You're an Adventurer with a bleeding heart!",
    ["Dialogue4203001"]="Wait a moment! Adventurer! Could… Can you do me a favor? This letter… please help me give this letter to… to the pretty blonde ponytailed woman in the tavern…",
    ["Dialogue4203002"]="Yes, the table next to the fireplace. The girl was having a good chat with Ida and her people... I fell in love at first sight when I saw her comely eyes...",
    ["Dialogue4203003"]="I know it's gonna be hard! She's probably from a prestigious family by looking at how she dressed, graceful and elegant. And here I am, a nobody but a sailor... Even so, I want to send her my love! Please help me, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4203101"]="Huh? Is this a love letter for me? Finally... The heir of Odin's Bloodline has fallen for my beauty.",
    ["Dialogue4203102"]="Adventurer, there's no need to hide. The pursuit of aesthetics is part of human nature, no matter how noble one may be. There's no way you can resist. I'm flattered... but I have to reject you since Jurgen's beauty is not for one person only but everyone. My apologies for turning you down.",
    ["Dialogue4203103"]="I know that you’re just speaking your mind. It's okay baby, you don’t need to feel bad about this. I can invite you to join the \"Jurgen Fan Club\" and give you some privileges. You can always come to me when you want to see me, and I will definitely make time to see you.",
    ["Dialogue4203104"]="Rest assured. Jurgen will never let down anyone who loves her. That includes you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4250101"]="A package from master...? Aahh! Hode! This must be master giving me guidance. Look at this fine packaging! The bait must be top-notch!",
    ["Dialogue4250102"]="Thank you, adventurer! If you have the time, please pass on my thanks to master! I'll definitely catch the biggest fish ever with this bait!",
    ["Dialogue4250201"]="Hello there. Yes, I'm Bertha Gray. You are...?",
    ["Dialogue4250202"]="A letter...? Ah, I see. This again.",
    ["Dialogue4250203"]="I can't go back yet, not until I make a breakthrough in my current research. It's pointless to return otherwise.",
    ["Dialogue4250204"]="My purpose here is to figure out what happened between the time when Fabres were considered allies to Green Cotton Farm to their current status as enemies.",
    ["Dialogue4250205"]="I doubt anything will change even if father learns of this. To him, the only correct solution is to eradicate the pests. Thank you for bringing this news to me, but I'm not about to change my mind.",
    ["Dialogue4250301"]="A delivery from Perini?",
    ["Dialogue4250302"]="Adventurers like you are a dime a dozen, and I have to repeat the same explanation to every one of you. At this rate, I'll have all the lines memorized.",
    ["Dialogue4250303"]="Do you know what kind of job Perini and I have? We're gourmets.",
    ["Dialogue4250304"]="A gourmet isn't what many of you think it is. Our job isn't lying about all day tasting delicious food. To be a true pioneer and discover delicacies never seen before, we have to go through countless disgusting, and even poisonous foods.",
    ["Dialogue4250305"]="I don't want Perini to follow me just to chase after my ideals. This is a dangerous job.",
    ["Dialogue4250306"]="Knowing Perini, she'll only become more determined when she learns of my reasons. I won't ask you to keep it secret, only that you understand where I'm coming from.",
    ["Dialogue4250401"]="Hello, adventurer! Are you here to wish for love too?",
    ["Dialogue4250402"]="I come here every day to pray for his safe return... That's right, he made me a promise before he went out to sea. We'll get married in this garden once he returns!",
    ["Dialogue4250403"]="I know he'll keep his promise, so I'm going to wait for him here too. It has nothing to do with the spring water, really. It's just... This is where we made our promise.",
    ["Dialogue4250404"]="Hm? What's this package...? Give it to Sherry? Well, all right. I'll take care of it! Sherry is always scolding me for being a dreamer, but I know she means well. She's my best friend!",
    ["Dialogue4250501"]="Huh? This handwriting... It's Kryon, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue4250502"]="He always gets so engrossed in the stories in these novels, he can't tell truth from fiction. Like how he believed Cocos are the true reason the continents split apart. It's why I haven't let him check out the last Ice Age book.",
    ["Dialogue4250503"]="Aah! This book is even worse! The hero gets deceived in the end and helps the gods destroy the world. No, no, no, who knows what Kryon would think if he reads this?",
    ["Dialogue4250601"]="Thank you for the letter! Archbishop Bescas is quite meticulous, isn't he...",
    ["Dialogue4250701"]="Hm? Were you looking for me?",
    ["Dialogue4250702"]="Yes, that's me. You mean these supplies are from Nicole? Thank you. I'm in the middle of something however, so I must go now.",
    ["Dialogue4250703"]="(Mr. Clauro... He really is quite a character.)",
    ["Dialogue4250801"]="This is big sister's recipe? Hm... I see, I see... If we handle the texture this way... I see now! That's brilliant!",
    ["Dialogue4250802"]="Ahaha! Sorry, sorry. I got carried away while reading. Thank you for your help. Please do come back anytime!",
    ["Dialogue4250901"]="Kafra Corp. strives for perfection in service for you in this desert landscape... Hm? Documents for me? Thank you, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4251001"]="Hi! I'm Shuling from Kafra's Alberta branch! Please enjoy your stay in our lovely port city!",
    ["Dialogue4251002"]="Hm? This letter... Ah, it's from Mr. Cassias, correct? What to do.",
    ["Dialogue4251003"]="Yes, I prefer the kind of love that is bravely shown before me. For him to do it this way is a little... Hahaha, forgive me. There are some words I shouldn't use as a Kafra employee.",
    ["Dialogue4251004"]="I will take this letter off your hands. Thank you, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4251101"]="Hic! Another round for me! Before the boss finds out I'm gone...",
    ["Dialogue4251102"]="Whoaa! L-look at the time! I gotta get back! Thank you, adventurer! I would've been in big trouble if he found me missing!",
    ["Dialogue4251201"]="A letter from Alson...? I'm not interested. Do whatever you want with it.",
    ["Dialogue4251202"]="He's already written me three months' worth of letters, and they're all the same. I'm not going back to Alson's sea crew. Those cutthroats.",
    ["Dialogue4251203"]="That's none of your business. Leave me alone.",
    ["Dialogue4260101"]="Poor La Grada... I heard that she's not having the best time in her new heels. Please send her my regards.",
    ["Dialogue4260201"]="Tell him to get lost.",
    ["Dialogue4260301"]="Still trying to make up your mind? What a nice day, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4260401"]="I'm running low on materials because Vivica's things are still not here. I want to tell her to hurry up... please help!",
    ["Dialogue4260501"]="Things are difficult to come by, because they're checking everything these days. But don't worry, you can trust me!",
    ["Dialogue4260601"]="... Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue4260701"]="It's nothing important. I just want you to say hi to Curara, and ask her if she would like to have dinner with me.",
    ["Dialogue4260801"]="I'm fine. Please tell Tomasa that he can trust me. I'll pass on the gathering, though.",
    ["Dialogue4260901"]="She's a nice gal, isn't she? Thank you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4261001"]="Adventurer! It's really lonely to train in the morning. Is there no one else in Umbala that wants to train with me in the morning other than Danielova?",
    ["Dialogue4261101"]="I want to sleep in! Can we jog at night?",
    ["Dialogue4261201"]="No!\n(Koobacka suddenly looks at you hopefully.)\nWill you run with me and embrace the first morning light?",
    ["Dialogue4261301"]="I hope Antares recovers soon. Thank you for visiting Antares.",
    ["Dialogue4261401"]="As always, Darien is very considerate. Please thank her for me.",
    ["Dialogue4261501"]="Everyone in Umbala is hoping for a speedy recovery for him.",
    ["Dialogue4261601"]="Adventurer, we found demons in the Labyrinth Forest. Please help us defeat them!",
    ["Dialogue4261602"]="Zenitsu Agatsuma and Inosuke Hashibira are there, too. We will help you when it's necessary!",
    ["Dialogue4261701"]="If life ends inevitably in death, then what's the point of living?",
    ["Dialogue4261702"]="I, have been waiting for an answer. I won't stop asking until I get one...",
    ["Dialogue4261703"]="Adventurer, do you have an answer?",
    ["Dialogue4261704"]="Thank you for answering. Then, I wish you a wonderful day.",
    ["Dialogue4261801"]="Hmm... Hmm... Could you ask Vanessa about her schedule for tomorrow afternoon? I hope she can save it for me, if that's okay with her.",
    ["Dialogue4261901"]="Are you asking if I am free tomorrow afternoon? Sorry, I'm not.",
    ["Dialogue4261902"]="Kasen?\n(Vanessa turns away her blushed face.)\nOkay then... That's a yes for him.",
    ["Dialogue4262001"]="Vanessa said yes? That's great! Hahaha! Thank you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4262101"]="Here is the note from the last class. Please give it to Kasen. Hmm... Just tell him it's the note Professor Owen handed down to everyone. I was just keeping it for him.",
    ["Dialogue4262201"]="(Kasen reads confusingly the note you gave him, while suddenly, a pink bookmark falls out.)\nThis is...",
    ["Dialogue4262202"]="(Kasen hides the notebook behind his back in a panic.)\nN-Nothing! Thank you for getting it for me! And... Please say thank you for me to Vanessa.",
    ["Dialogue4262301"]="...What's the look on your face? W-We are just classmates!",
    ["Dialogue4262401"]="My commission is simple. Just dig out and bring back the thing I lost at the Border Inspection Station.",
    ["Dialogue4262402"]="Relax, it's not contraband. But if someone opens it before me... Then I don't guarantee.",
    ["Dialogue4262403"]="Haha, don't worry. You will be well compensated for your honesty when it's done.",
    ["Dialogue4262501"]="Good. I always like honest people. Maybe, we can go for long-term cooperation...",
    ["Dialogue4262601"]="Hi, I'm Adler, a traveling photographer. Of course, I used to be an Adventurer, until those goddamn Goblin archers shot an arrow in my butt...",
    ["Dialogue4262602"]="Ahem... Anyway, I would ask you to go to El Mes Gorge to collect some photo materials. Considering my current health situation, I don't think I can make such a long trip.",
    ["Dialogue4262701"]="Nice photo, buddy! I hope we can work together again!",
    ["Dialogue4262801"]="It's this one... Can you help me?",
    ["Dialogue4262901"]="Thank you! Even if we were to part ways in the future, this would leave me a memory to treasure...",
    ["Dialogue4300101"]="Oh, kindhearted adventurer! Could you help this old man visit an old friend's grave? At my age, even the regular paths I used to walk every day feel like a mountain road.",
    ["Dialogue4300102"]="His grave lies behind the Prontera Cathedral. I planted some of his favorite indigo mushrooms in front of it. They should be growing nicely now.",
    ["Dialogue4300103"]="Once you find it, please tell him his old friend isn't feeling well today and won't be coming, then bring those mushrooms back to me.",
    ["Dialogue4300201"]="There are a lot of similarities between a flower and a woman, don't you think?",
    ["Dialogue4300202"]="Their beauty and fragility bringing forth the desire to protect... Just like my fans. I'd like to show them my gratitude for their support with some lovely Morning Glories. Please pick some for me from the highlands near the West Gate.",
    ["Dialogue4300301"]="You made it. The goods are very fragile this time around, so be careful with the delivery.",
    ["Dialogue4300302"]="Do you see the purple flowers in the ground over there? You must carefully uproot them and bring them to Norten in the Prontera Library.",
    ["Dialogue4300303"]="With how anxious they look, whatever this is must be very important. Please be careful!",
    ["Dialogue4300401"]="Ugh... Where did I go wrong...? Why can't I catch great fish like master does?",
    ["Dialogue4300402"]="That's it! It must be the bait that's the problem!",
    ["Dialogue4300403"]="Master's fishing bait uses the red mushrooms that grow next to his tent. I don't know what they are, but it must contain some great secret!",
    ["Dialogue4300404"]="Master's tent is just outside the South Gate, adventurer. I just need one mushroom for my research. Please help me out!",
    ["Dialogue4300501"]="I wonder how Cocoa is doing... Is it eating right...?",
    ["Dialogue4300502"]="Oh, hello there. Cocoa is the Pecopeco I personally raised since it was a chick. It's supposed to be delivered to an adventurer knight soon, but it suddenly went missing.",
    ["Dialogue4300503"]="It loves Pumpkins. Maybe it ran off to the farm outside the South Gate! Please bring it back here!",
    ["Dialogue4300601"]="It's been a long time, adventurer. I'm so happy to see you've become so dependable!",
    ["Dialogue4300602"]="It's an embarrassing tale. We had a backpack packed with food that was snatched by Crows and carried back to their nest, but no one in Eden Group is capable of climbing that cliff to get it back...",
    ["Dialogue4300603"]="Ha, ha! You really are dependable. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue4300701"]="This is going to be a problem. If the carrier pigeons can't find us, we won't be able to communicate with headquarters in Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue4300702"]="We temporarily relocated to better guard Ant Cavern, but it seems headquarters didn't relay the new instructions to the carrier pigeons. It's likely the pigeons are waiting where we were originally supposed to station.",
    ["Dialogue4300703"]="Please help us retrieve the orders from headquarters from the carrier pigeons.",
    ["Dialogue4300801"]="I wonder how he's doing...",
    ["Dialogue4300802"]="A son? No, no, no, I'm talking about my pride and joy. When I was still working in Sograt Desert, I used the best wood I could find to craft an indestructible Road Sign.",
    ["Dialogue4300803"]="Now that I'm retired, I find myself worrying how the Road Sign is holding up. But these tired old bones aren't made for the harsh environment of the desert anymore.",
    ["Dialogue4300804"]="Could you help check up on it, adventurer? It's mounted near the desert oasis.",
    ["Dialogue4300901"]="An adventurer? Wonderful! What perfect timing! We're short-staffed at the moment. I'd be grateful if you could do us a small favor.",
    ["Dialogue4300902"]="There's a Cactus behind the bar. I'd like you to cut off a small part of it and bring it back. It's a magic Cactus that we planted specifically for the purpose of making our cactus specialty drink.",
    ["Dialogue4301001"]="Did you know there's a little black bird that likes to steal?",
    ["Dialogue4301002"]="Yes! Those wretched birds! They've started to turn up around Alberta with their eyes set on the precious jewels carried on merchants and noblewomen.",
    ["Dialogue4301003"]="These Crows aren't native to Alberta. They're causing undue misery to everyone in the city. Rumor has it there's a Crow Nest hidden in some corner of the city. Please help us retrieve our lost belongings!",
    ["Dialogue4301101"]="Hmm... Not bad. You look like the reliable sort! The adventurer who helped me last kept pocketing some of my Bamboo. You wouldn't do that to me, would you?",
    ["Dialogue4301102"]="Of course! I planted some Bamboo in the forest to the south of Payon, near Alberta's main gate. Monsters have been running rampant there lately and trampling the Bamboo. If you can find any Bamboo worth saving, please help me bring some back!",
    ["Dialogue4301201"]="Wouldn't it be great if an outfit could look gorgeous and smell fragrant at the same time?",
    ["Dialogue4301202"]="We have everything except the fragrance, and the aroma produced by the Daisies in the cave at the bottom of the ocean is the best in the world. Do you have the courage to investigate the ocean depths, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue4301203"]="Wonderful! The Daisy has a very peculiar shape, akin to two tentacles, but its scent is no joke! You'll know when you find it!",
    ["Dialogue4350101"]="Ha, ha! That's the mushroom I wanted. Thank you, kind adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4350102"]="I don't know how long I have left in this world. Perhaps all I can do now is ask adventurers to visit the grave. Ha ha ha... Time truly waits for no man.",
    ["Dialogue4350201"]="Thank you, adventurer. These flowers are a perfect match for their beauty. Now then...",
    ["Dialogue4350202"]="This flower in full bloom is well suited for your refined figure.",
    ["Dialogue4350203"]="Hehe, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue4350204"]="This budding flower is well suited for your lovely and youthful temperament.",
    ["Dialogue4350205"]="Thank you! I knew there was a reason I took a liking to you!",
    ["Dialogue4350206"]="This flower bud is well suited for your frosty elegance. I'm sure it'll be equally magnificent once it blooms.",
    ["Dialogue4350207"]="... Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue4350208"]="This little flower that has yet to bloom is of course well suited for a cute little girl like you!",
    ["Dialogue4350209"]="Thank you, big brother Morts!",
    ["Dialogue4350301"]="Ohh! Is this the specimen?",
    ["Dialogue4350302"]="Cough! Cough, cough! I'm alright. Here, give that to me.",
    ["Dialogue4350401"]="Hmm... Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue4350402"]="This is... It's just a normal mushroom. Is this really the secret technique? Could I be mistaken...? I'm missing something here...",
    ["Dialogue4350403"]="(He's fallen into deep thought. Let's leave him alone.)",
    ["Dialogue4350501"]="Ah! Cocoa! I'm so glad you're all right!",
    ["Dialogue4350502"]="Coo! Coco!! Cocoa!!!!",
    ["Dialogue4350503"]="It's... It's saying it doesn't want to leave me. Of course I know that. I don't want to be apart from it too.",
    ["Dialogue4350504"]="But this is what I do as a Pecopeco Keeper. I raise Pecopecos and give them to adventurers.",
    ["Dialogue4350505"]="This isn't my first Cocoa. I give all the Pecopecos I raise the same name, to give myself the illusion that I'm taking care of the same one. It... doesn't feel good when they have to leave, after all.",
    ["Dialogue4350506"]="Thank you, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue4350601"]="Hm? It was tossed to the bottom of the cliff...? It doesn't look like anything's missing. I guess the Crows weren't interested, which is good! These are snacks for the children who'll be visiting the amusement park, not those thieving Crows!",
    ["Dialogue4350701"]="Thank you very much. I believe we'll have need of more help from adventurers until we can assign new carrier pigeons. We would appreciate it if you could keep an eye on requests from us on the Mission Board.",
    ["Dialogue4350801"]="Everything is well? Ohohoho! Wonderful. It was well worth all the effort I put into this masterpiece. What a relief!",
    ["Dialogue4350901"]="Thank you for the help! But we're very busy, so I'll be skipping the rest of the pleasantries.",
    ["Dialogue4351001"]="Wonderful! The goods may have been stolen, but nothing was damaged. Unfortunately, incidents like this are bound to happen again with the Crows still running free. Sigh, how troublesome...",
    ["Dialogue4351101"]="Only one left?! Darn it! Those blasted monsters! We'll have to toughen up our watch...",
    ["Dialogue4351201"]="That's it! That's the one! The Daisy Cloth... A long lost art that's about to be reborn by my hand! I'd happily fail a thousand times to bring my master's last wish to life!",
    ["Dialogue4351301"]="Sigh... What should I do... The factory will go out of business soon like this...",
    ["Dialogue4351302"]="Aha! Adventurer! You're here to help, this is really...",
    ["Dialogue4351303"]="This is awesome! Wonderful! The factory will be saved! Haha!",
    ["Dialogue4351304"]="Let's get going soon! Head to the factory, and you will know what you should do!",
    ["Dialogue4351401"]="Ah! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue4351402"]="Christmas is around the corner, and everyone is busy preparing. Darn Garm, how dare he send his baby to make trouble at this particular time!",
    ["Dialogue4351403"]="Garm Baby has bewitched a large group of residents, and has wreaked havoc in the Toy Factory.",
    ["Dialogue4351404"]="(The Christmas Envoy looks anxious) The managers are no match for the Garm Baby at all. If it goes on like this, I'm afraid no one can get the toys from the Toy Factory on time this Christmas.",
    ["Dialogue4351405"]="There's no time to waste. Go to the Toy Factory now, and someone will meet you there.",
    ["Dialogue4351501"]="Thank heavens! You’re finally here!",
    ["Dialogue4351502"]="There's still time, Adventurer. Our mission is to bring new toys to people for Christmas. Anyway, please stop Garm Baby!",
    ["Dialogue4351503"]="You'll be generously rewarded when it’s done!",
    ["Dialogue4351601"]="Hey Adventurer, how's everything going? Where is the Garm Baby?",
    ["Dialogue4351602"]="Brilliant! It's not too late for production then. I’ll see to it now. Please accept these as a token of our appreciation!",
    ["Dialogue4508001"]="The Tyr Altar has been occupied by the <color=#FF0000>attackers</color>. Attackers within range of the Tyr Altar will receive stat buffs.",
    ["Dialogue4508002"]="The Tyr Altar has been occupied by the <color=#0000FF>defenders</color>. Defenders within range of the Tyr Altar will receive stat buffs.",
    ["Dialogue4550001"]="%s defeated the %s-point crystal",
    ["Dialogue4550002"]="%s defeated the %s-point crystal",
    ["Dialogue4550003"]="%s defeated the %s-point crystal",
    ["Dialogue4550004"]="%s defeated the %s-point crystal",
    ["Dialogue500500101"]="Long time, no see, Adventurer! Hmm... It looks like your studies have finally commenced! I knew you had it in you! But this is just the beginning—there are some things you can study for a lifetime and barely scratch the surface, so don't you slack off like that Jarod...",
    ["Dialogue500500102"]="Ahem... What? I didn't say anything! Anyway.. Congratulations on enrolling! You're now officially a student of Criatura Academy. According to the school rules, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply for a Master according to your own personal needs</color>. They're all from Criatura Academy, too, and I know you'll get along with them just fine.",
    ["Dialogue500500103"]="Of course! Maybe one day, you'll also become a revered Master!",
    ["Dialogue500500104"]="Looking forward to it, huh? Well, you can go ahead and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Dean Mainz</color> to start your first lesson!",
    ["Dialogue500500201"]="Hoho! Kiki told me you would like to choose a Master! Well played, well played! Of course, your academic achievements will depend entirely on how much you put into your studies, but if you have a Master to guide you, you can achieve double the results with half the effort! Therefore, you should take your Master's <color=#CA2E0AFF>training</color> seriously, whatever it may be.",
    ["Dialogue500500202"]="That's the spirit! Go, find the right Master for you. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Study with an open mind and study well</color>. Maybe one day, your name will become forever engraved upon the history of this continent...",
    ["Dialogue500510101"]="That little Adventurer I once knew has found his own way. I'm proud of you, child.",
    ["Dialogue500510102"]="Hohoho, we are indeed recruiting a new batch of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Masters</color> into the academy. We've had such a large intake of new students recently... Seeing all of these fresh young faces makes me feel like a boy again!",
    ["Dialogue500510103"]="Hmm... You're certainly strong enough to be a Master, but do you have what it takes to stand strong when your students come face to face with life's many crises, and to let them go when they graduate, many never to return again? For every student who leaves Criatura Academy, whether the journey ahead is one of mediocrity or glory—the impact of their Master's teachings resonates throughout every aspect of their life. When faced with a critical decision, a Master's words, whether intentional or not, can set their students upon the path to a bright and smooth future.",
    ["Dialogue500510104"]="Therefore, the fate shared by a Master and student does not end when the student graduates. Those seeds of wisdom planted in their hearts... The flowers that blossom and the fruits they bear determine where your fate ultimately lies.",
    ["Dialogue500510105"]="(Dean Mainz seems to have been reminded of a certain memory, and his gaze passes through you and falls somewhere in the distance.)\nA position of such profound significance cannot be bestowed carelessly. Adventurer, are you willing to accept Criatura Academy's challenge? Will you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take the Masters' Examination</color>?",
    ["Dialogue500510201"]="A Master should not only possess great power, but must also maintain an objective position. In a distant pyramid dwells a band of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soldier Skeletons</color> who stubbornly guard the Empire's lost glory. The loyalty they demonstrated while alive was commendable, but many Adventurers have died at their unyielding hands. Take up your weapon and defeat them. Gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 Undying Medals</color> for me as proof that you've put an end to their hopeless existence!",
    ["Dialogue500510301"]="Adventurer, you have passed the first stage of the examination. Congratulations. Are you ready for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>second test</color>?",
    ["Dialogue500510302"]="(Dean Mainz pats you on the shoulder with a meaningful smile.)\nDon't worry. While remaining objective, a Master should also learn to listen to their own inner voice, as well as their students. That is why the second trial is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>quiz</color>.",
    ["Dialogue500510401"]="It's time for the second test. Would you like to hear my advice before you begin?",
    ["Dialogue500510402"]="When in doubt, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow your instincts</color>.",
    ["Dialogue500510501"]="Congratulations on passing the second test. Now, it's time for you to take an oath, then you will officially become Criatura Academy's newest Master!",
    ["Dialogue500510601"]="Before any Adventurer becomes a Master, they must swear an oath to the Goddess. Repeat after me.",
    ["Dialogue500510602"]="In the name of the Goddess, from today on, I will serve as a Master of Criatura Academy.",
    ["Dialogue500510603"]="I will do my utmost to build a bridge between ignorance and wisdom, until my dying breath.",
    ["Dialogue500510604"]="I hope you will remember this moment many years from now. Young Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>you have passed the Masters' Examination</color> and are now an official Master of Criatura Academy. Go and meet your students—<color=#CA2E0AFF>your journey as an educator</color> has just begun!",
    ["Dialogue55011001"]="No one can catch <color=#FF6100>me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue55011002"]="The <color=#33A1C9>Little Fairy</color> appears in the illusion in the blink of an eye!",
    ["Dialogue55011003"]="<color=#ffe788>Faeries</color> show up with blessings!",
    ["Dialogue55011004"]="<color=#ffe788>Faeries</color> appear! Accept their blessings!",
    ["Dialogue55011005"]="<color=#ffe788>Faeries</color> are here to assist Adventurers!",
    ["Dialogue55011006"]="<color=#ffe788>Faeries</color> appear in the city! Accept their assistance!",
    ["Dialogue55011007"]="<color=#ffe788>The brave Adventurers have won!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55011008"]="<color=#ffe788>The monsters return to the darkness after losing their leader!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55011009"]="The <color=#33A1C9>Little Fairy</color> has appeared! The Adventurer who kills the <color=#33A1C9>Little Fairy</color> will get its treasure!",
    ["Dialogue55011010"]="<color=#ffe788>Adventurers have successfully fended off the <color=#ff6347>First Wave of Monsters</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55011011"]="<color=#ffe788>Successfully defeated the <color=#ff4500>Second Wave of Monsters</color>! Prontera catches a moment of peace...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55011012"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#ff5252>The Third Wave of Monsters</color> is gone. Keep it up!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55012001"]="<color=#ff6347>Karmic Flames</color> has appeared with the first group of evil spirits behind him. Please be careful!",
    ["Dialogue55012002"]="<color=#ff6347>In tonight’s story... there are no survivors...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55012003"]="<color=#ff6347>You will no longer be bedridden with diseases once you fall into an eternal slumber...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013001"]="<color=#ff4500>Hehe... Nurarihyon is after your head... I mean, your hair...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013002"]="<color=#ff4500>So red blood flows through the veins of these monsters...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013003"]="<color=#ff4500>Send despair to those who have hope...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013004"]="<color=#ff4500>I will be... waiting for you in hell...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013005"]="<color=#ff4500>It’s your misfortune to encounter me at this time...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013006"]="<color=#ff4500>Watch over... this world for me...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013007"]="<color=#ff4500>Meat! I want fresh meat!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55013008"]="<color=#ff4500>I will sacrifice myself if my death can save my parched homeland...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55014001"]="<color=#ff5252>Dawn... will never break...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55014002"]="<color=#ff5252>Have you ever heard someone crying in the grave?</color>",
    ["Dialogue55014003"]="<color=#ff5252>There can only be so much killing to cease further killing...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55014004"]="<color=#ff5252>The ship has collapsed... It is time for me to go too...</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230001"]="<color=#ffe788>Failed to release due to insufficient energy. Please proceed to the Energy Pillar or the Energy Robot to gain more energy.</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230002"]="<color=#ffe788>Mech Armor has been destroyed. Keep pushing!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230003"]="<color=#ffe788>The Essence Energy will explode after <color=#528fff>30 seconds</color>! Hurry to the turret and blast the boss to destroy the shield!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230004"]="<color=#ffe788>The Essence Energy will explode after <color=#528fff>20 seconds</color>! Hurry to the turret and blast the boss to destroy the shield!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230005"]="<color=#ffe788>The Essence Energy will explode after <color=#528fff>10 seconds</color>! Hurry to the turret and blast the boss to destroy the shield!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55230006"]="<color=#ffe788>Meet your end, Human!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55231001"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper Type I has received the Mech Armor, reducing its damage taken significantly. Now, transform into a Destruction Robot to perform Shatter.</color>",
    ["Dialogue55231002"]="<color=#ffe788>Human, you'll never defeat me! Your damage just makes me more powerful!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55231003"]="<color=#ffe788>Human, you'll never defeat me! As long as the core exists, I'm immortal!</color>",
    ["Dialogue55231004"]="<color=#ffe788>Vesper has removed all transformation effects from the field!</color>",
    ["Dialogue552451001"]="Run while you can... Little ones...",
    ["Dialogue552451002"]="Smash the ice crystal and save your party member!",
    ["Dialogue571001"]="You wanna play Collect Carrots? Then let me tell you the rules of the game!\nWatch carefully to see the moving path of the wolves.\nBe careful, as they will <color=#ff5252>attack you</color>!\nAvoid wolf attacks and try to stay alive!",
    ["Dialogue571002"]="<color=#ffe788>Please keep avoiding wolf attacks until you reach the goal!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue600001201"]="<color=#ffe788>The monsters have been exterminated. Delve deeper into the sewers.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001301"]="<color=#ffe788>Poisonous gas is filling the room. Exterminate the monsters quickly.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001401"]="<color=#ffe788>The monsters have been exterminated. Delve deeper into the sewers.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001501"]="<color=#ffe788>Look out!</color> <color=#ff5252>Get out of the way!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001601"]="<color=#ffe788>Watch the damage you're doing!</color> <color=#ff5252>Red shells</color> <color=#ffe788>reflect physical damage, while</color> <color=#528fff>blue shells</color> <color=#ffe788>reflect magical damage.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001701"]="<color=#ffe788>The Golden Bug is summoning a</color> <color=#ff5252>Golden Thief Bug</color> <color=#ffe788>to heal itself. Exterminate it quickly!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001801"]="<color=#ff5252>Becoming Super Enraged!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600001901"]="<color=#ffe788>Move out of the</color> <color=#ff5252>red circle</color> <color=#ffe788>area!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002001"]="<color=#ffe788>Watch out for Drake's Waterball. <color=#ff5252>Break the Waterball</color> to free your trapped friends.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002101"]="<color=#ffe788>Drake is repairing his own pegleg. <color=#ff5252>Break his Water Shield</color> to interrupt his repairs.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002201"]="Show me your battle style in the trial! Defeat 4 waves of enemies in 3 minutes!",
    ["Dialogue600002301"]="First, a warm up with some common enemies! (Wave 1/4)",
    ["Dialogue600002401"]="How will you fare against a large mob of enemies? (Wave 2/4)",
    ["Dialogue600002501"]="Oh, dear! Don't underestimate these oversized monsters now! (Wave 3/4)",
    ["Dialogue600002601"]="Now for the final challenge! Defeat him and claim your victory! (Wave 4/4)",
    ["Dialogue600002701"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for<color=#ff5252>坎</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1097] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002702"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for <color=#ff5252>乾</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1092] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002703"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for <color=#ff5252>兌</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1093] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002704"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for <color=#ff5252>坤</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1099] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002705"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for <color=#ff5252>艮</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1095] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002801"]="<color=#ffe788>The word for <color=#ff5252>離</color> and the [s s=40.0 url=Icons/Item/1094] trigram appear faintly on the statue.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600002901"]="<color=#ffe788>The exterminated monster matches the trigram on the statue. You receive Luna's Blessing.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003001"]="<color=#ff5252>The exterminated monster does not match the trigram on the statue. You are cursed by the Biteback Spell.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003101"]="<color=#ffe788>The seal for this area is broken. The barrier to the next area is lifted.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003201"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian's armor has been broken. Use <color=#ff0000>Firecrackers</color> to deal a large amount of damage</color>.",
    ["Dialogue600003301"]="<color=#ffe788>Nian has escaped. Go to the <color=#ff0000>other areas</color> of Payon Village to stop Nian from causing destruction</color>.",
    ["Dialogue600003401"]="<color=#ffe788>Warning! A <color=#ff0000>Baby Nian</color> has appeared in this region!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003501"]="<color=#ffe788>Arriving at the Sealed Island...</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003601"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>The Dark Illusion</color> is about to appear! Get out of the labyrinth quickly!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003701"]="<color=#ffe788>Concentrate your attacks<color= on the #ff0000>Illusion Gate</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003801"]="<color=#ffe788>Arena challenge start!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600003901"]="<color=#ffe788>Get ready for the next opponent!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004001"]="<color=#ffe788>Throughout the inner and outer city—<color=#ff5252>northwest, northeast, southwest, southeast</color>—new <color=#ff5252>MVPs</color> and <color=#ff5252>Mini Bosses</color> have appeared!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004101"]="<color=#ffe788>The city's Central Fountain has been taken over by many <color=#ff5252>Mini Bosses</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004201"]="<color=#ffe788>The city's Central Fountain has been taken over by many <color=#ff5252>Mini Bosses</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004301"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Tough</color> characteristic has appeared! It has high defensive attributes.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004302"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Angry</color> characteristic has appeared! The lower its HP, the harder it hits.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004303"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Violent</color> characteristic has appeared! It has great reflect and absorb abilities.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004304"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Cunning</color> characteristic has appeared! It has incredible stealth abilities.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004305"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Swift</color> characteristic has appeared! It possesses the power of teleportation.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004306"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Protective</color> characteristic has appeared! It can summon Scarecrow, the God of Protection.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004307"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Freeze</color> characteristic has appeared! Its slow and freeze abilities are very powerful.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004308"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Thrower</color> characteristic has appeared! It can throw random traps.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004309"]="A monster with the <color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Reviver</color> characteristic has appeared! It has a resurrection halo over its head.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004501"]="<color=#ffe788>A new <color=#ff5252>MVP</color> has appeared in the <color=#ff5252>northwest region</color> of the outer city!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004601"]="<color=#ffe788>A new <color=#ff5252>MVP</color> has appeared in the <color=#ff5252>northeast region</color> of the outer city!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004701"]="<color=#ffe788>A new <color=#ff5252>MVP</color> has appeared in the <color=#ff5252>southwest region</color> of the outer city!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004801"]="<color=#ffe788>A new <color=#ff5252>MVP</color> has appeared in the <color=#ff5252>southeast region</color> of the outer city!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600004901"]="<color=#ffe788>Get ready for the final battle!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600005001"]="<color=#ffe788>Mimic casts dark energy and will enter the prison labyrinth.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600005101"]="<color=#ffe788>The flame barrier has been cleared.</color>",
    ["Dialogue600005201"]="<color=#ffe788>Moonlight Flower is using</color> <color=#ff5252>Land Protector</color>! <color=#ffe788>End the Earth Element Bonus early by entering together</color>!",
    ["Dialogue600005401"]="The Storm Dragon Veldora circles above the battlefield. Go to <color=#ff0000>another area</color> of South Prontera Gate to find him and complete the challenge.",
    ["Dialogue600005501"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>Elite</color> Monster appears! Processing an unknown powerful strength!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600005601"]="<color=#ffe788>Moonlight Flower is using</color> <color=#ff5252>Land Protector</color>! <color=#ffe788>End the Earth Element Bonus early by entering together</color>!",
    ["Dialogue600006001"]="<color=#ff5252>Queen Cloud<color=#ffe788> is casting the skill:</color> <color=#ff5252>Bewildering Cloud</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006002"]="<color=#ff5252>Queen Cloud<color=#ffe788> is casting the skill:</color> <color=#ff5252>Cloud Acceleration</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006003"]="<color=#ff5252>Queen Cloud<color=#ffe788> is casting the skill:</color> <color=#ff5252>Water Prison</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006006"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>The production line on the left</color> is processing a large number of<color=#ff0000> mechanical monsters</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006008"]="<color=#ffe788>A giant Goren <color=#528fff>Bru</color> that has not yet been controlled has been found! Please attack the Goren to activate the generator and charge <color=#528fff>Bru</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006009"]="<color=#ffe788>Attention! The Gorens on each side are immune to <color=#528fff>physical</color> and <color=#ff5252>magical</color> damage respectively!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006011"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#ff0000>The production line on the right</color> is mass producing <color=#ff0000>Mech Monsters</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006013"]="Process... Process...",
    ["Dialogue600006014"]="Minions! Turn them all into spare parts!",
    ["Dialogue600006015"]="Let me make you as tough as steel!",
    ["Dialogue600006016"]="As expected, flesh and bone cannot even stand one blow!",
    ["Dialogue600006017"]="I'll toss you all onto the production line!",
    ["Dialogue600006019"]="This is the power of machines!",
    ["Dialogue600006021"]="Argh... Leader...",
    ["Dialogue600006022"]="<color=#ffe788>The production line has begun processing!</color>.",
    ["Dialogue600006023"]="<color=#ffe788>The horrible <color=#ff5252>Gatekeeper Goren</color> has appeared! Please proceed with caution!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006024"]="<color=#ffe788>Attacking Gorens will activate the generator to recharge <color=#528fff>Bru</color>!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006025"]="<color=#ffe788><color=#528fff>Bru</color> has won!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006026"]="<color=#ffe788>I'm so sorry! <color=#528fff>Bru</color> lost the battle!!!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006027"]="Magical damage can’t hurt me!",
    ["Dialogue600006028"]="Physical damage does not have any effect on me!",
    ["Dialogue600006029"]="AREA CLEAR！",
    ["Dialogue600006030"]="Guard… Guard… Treasure… Chest…",
    ["Dialogue600006031"]="Search… for… Invaders…",
    ["Dialogue600006032"]="It is the material for making magical items!",
    ["Dialogue600006033"]="Chief… Please help me!",
    ["Dialogue600006034"]="There's no way you're getting out of here alive!",
    ["Dialogue600006035"]="Human! Come here!",
    ["Dialogue600006036"]="Come on! He’s coming over!",
    ["Dialogue600006037"]="Charging for Master Ryder!",
    ["Dialogue600006038"]="Bones are just poor substitutes.",
    ["Dialogue600006039"]="Grow! Grow into a big tree!",
    ["Dialogue600006040"]="Please, take me to the Spring of Origins.",
    ["Dialogue600006041"]="Darn! Beelzebub's miasma is corroding the entire forest!",
    ["Dialogue600006042"]="Protect me! I'll cleanse this poisoned forest!",
    ["Dialogue600006043"]="Darned Chonchons! Stop them!",
    ["Dialogue600006301"]="Last 30 seconds!",
    ["Dialogue600006990"]="<color=#ffe788>Jokers meet, game over. I win the bet!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600006991"]="<color=#ffe788>Not enough players in the game, all out!</color>",
    ["Dialogue600007001"]="The elevator is activating, arriving at the next floor in 10 seconds.",
    ["Dialogue600007101"]="The boss on this floor has appeared.",
    ["Dialogue600007201"]="The next wave of monsters appears in 5 seconds.",
    ["Dialogue6000101"]="(The corners of the mysterious swordsman's lips turn upward in a smile as a slight glimmer twinkles in his eyes.)\nAdventurer, it must be rare fate that brought us here, watching the sea together...",
    ["Dialogue6000102"]="Look at this sea in all its endlessness. Every time I stand here for a while, I remember those things, those people...",
    ["Dialogue6000103"]="The girl I liked, and... my soon-to-be-fulfilled dreams... Those childish but blood-boiling moments...",
    ["Dialogue6000104"]="(The mysterious swordsman looks at the surface of the sea with a twinkle in his eyes, seemingly lost in his memories.)\nOnce upon a time, my dream was to become a hero and create a happy land for the people I love, for people who have dreams, and for all the people whose hearts are full of warmth and love.",
    ["Dialogue6000105"]="...Do you think this dream can come true?\n(The mysterious swordsman turns to look at you with a smile full of meaning on his face.)\nPerhaps our meeting is meant to tell me the answer to this question.",
    ["Dialogue6000201"]="Adventurer, will you work to protect the people of this paradise?",
    ["Dialogue6000202"]="Wonderful! Actually, no matter how far you go, some things will always be important. The most precious part of the journey to attain our dreams is <color=#CA2E0AFF>remembering what started it all</color>. Do you still remember the first monster you fought when you first began your adventure on this continent?",
    ["Dialogue6000203"]="Then, please go and kill 678 Porings. See how strong you've become! Please remember to hurry back though. I have to go home once it gets dark.\n(The mysterious swordsman gives a sad smile and winks at you.)",
    ["Dialogue6000301"]="(The mysterious swordsman's face is a bit flushed, as if he'd just been drinking.)\nOh, you came back so quickly! Seems like it was an easy victory for you. But from the look on your face, it seems you have some unsolved doubts, yes?",
    ["Dialogue6000302"]="...Actually it's nothing more than a number. But this number is a kind of memorial to me.\n(The mysterious swordsman suddenly takes on a solemn look.)\nIf you want to become a hero, you're destined to endure some hardships. But back then, I wasn't able to overcome them. I endured for 678 days, no more, no less.",
    ["Dialogue6000303"]="I made this trip to Payon because I have <color=#CA2E0AFF>some wishes I'd like to fulfill</color>. I had such a good time chatting with you today that I almost forgot about them.",
    ["Dialogue600031101"]="It is the duty of a soldier to guard the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue6000401"]="Oh? You want to help me fulfill my wishes?\nI found the right person, indeed! Now then, could you please bring me <color=#CA2E0AFF>99 pieces of Iron</color>? Remember to be quick about it. I can't stay here for too long. A new adventure is waiting for me.",
    ["Dialogue6000402"]="Adventurer, if you really want to become a hero capable of protecting this joyous land, ninety-nine pieces of iron shouldn't be too difficult for you, right?",
    ["Dialogue6000403"]="Hahaha! You can smell the alcohol on my breath? It's rare that I come back here, so I went for a few drinks at Juke's, but it would take more than a few flagons of his peach blossom wine to get me drunk! Ninety-nine pieces of iron... Now that's something indispensable on the road to becoming a hero. Think you're up to it?",
    ["Dialogue6000501"]="Hahaha, I knew you could do it. If you have the time, please bring me <color=#CA2E0AFF>1 Clover</color>! It's very important to me. But please be swift; it's almost time for me to leave.",
    ["Dialogue6000601"]="(The mysterious swordsman lowers his head and stares at the Clover.)\nThank you. It's beautiful.",
    ["Dialogue6000602"]="You want to know their meaning, do you? ...On the road to becoming a hero, it is very important to have a hero's willpower. Iron symbolizes that heroic willpower. As for the Clover, sometimes having an iron-like will needs a bit of luck, too.\n(The mysterious swordsman's eyes darken slightly.)",
    ["Dialogue6000701"]="(The mysterious swordsman lets out a barely-audible sigh.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue6000702"]="...Oh no! You saw right through me! ...Yes, the truth is, there's one more thing I need to get. A very rare item...",
    ["Dialogue6000703"]="(The mysterious swordsman lifts his head, eyes twinkling in surprise.)\nR-really?! Thank you so much! Before it gets dark, please bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Witherless Rose</color>. I'll be waiting here for you. Please return quickly. Once night falls, I'll have to set off on my journey.",
    ["Dialogue6000801"]="(The mysterious swordsman looks at the rose in his hand with a soft glint in his eyes.)\nSo there really are things in this world that are eternal. The Witherless Rose... It'll never die.",
    ["Dialogue6000802"]="(The mysterious swordsman smiles, seemingly lost in sweet memories.)\nThis flower is for the person I love—the girl who never left my side, even throughout countless hardships.",
    ["Dialogue6000803"]="(The mysterious swordsman is silent.)\nNo matter where I am... I'll always look out for her.",
    ["Dialogue6000901"]="Thank you, adventurer. It's been so, so long since I had such a cordial conversation partner.",
    ["Dialogue6000902"]="Oh... All my friends call me Radish. You can call me <color=#CA2E0AFF>Radish Warrior</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6000903"]="Oh? You're asking about my dream? Well, why don't you answer me this instead? In all your time spent on this continent, running, fighting, chasing... Did you enjoy every moment?\n(Radish Warrior looks at you sincerely.)",
    ["Dialogue6000904"]="(Radish Warrior smiles, pleased.)\nThen my dream... I guess it has come true. Adventurer, I will come here every year on <color=#CA2E0AFF>June 6 and December 27</color>. If you can complete my quest on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>same day</color>, I bet she will be very happy...",
    ["Dialogue6001001"]="We were really destined to meet, adventurer! To be able to share the same scenery once, then reunite again, is a rare opportunity indeed.",
    ["Dialogue600100101"]="<color=#ffe788>So everyone fully experiences the thrill of competition, I made some changes to the field! Please keep an eye out for them!\nHahaha. Without further ado, let's see who will come out on top! —Host: Barrowson</color>",
    ["Dialogue600100201"]="<color=#ffe788>The field has changed. Keep an eye out.</color>",
    ["Dialogue6001101"]="(Radish Warrior looks surprised, then laughs in delight.)\nYou... You remembered what I said before? That is truly—Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue6001102"]="Ha, ha! A true friend is worth more than gold. I think she'd be very happy if she knew I made such a good friend on this continent. Oh, can you do me one last favor? Could you place this Witherless Rose in front of the sacrificial stone under the maple tree behind me?",
    ["Dialogue6001201"]="Yes. This feels right. Thank you again for your help, kind adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue6001202"]="(Radish Warrior falls silent, quietly looking at you with a mysterious gaze.)\n... Do you remember when I told you I experienced a harrowing moment? Life ebbs and flows. There are good times and bad times, but no matter how far I fell, I never gave up hope. However, my iron will wasn't enough to carry me. In the end, I lacked just that little bit of luck... As for the Witherless Rose...",
    ["Dialogue6001203"]="(Radish Warrior looks toward the rose placed before the sacrificial stone.)\nNo matter where I am... I'll always look out for her.",
    ["Dialogue6001204"]="Oh my, did that \"sayonara\" mean goodbye...?\n(Radish Warrior smiles and waves.)\nThen, goodbye, my friend! May we meet again another time! Whenever that may be.",
    ["Dialogue6001301"]="(You take a closer look. There are faded letters carved on the sacrificial stone. It reads: \"True love will never be forgotten, Radish Warrior.\" Could this stone be...?)",
    ["Dialogue6001401"]="Adventurer, you're right on time! Come check out my magic fish bait, meow!",
    ["Dialogue6001402"]="That's right, meow! I went to Geffen to visit a friend I haven't seen in a while. Mewlande taught me the new enchantment magic he learned recently. Once I came back, I realized how fantastic enchantment is, so I made this fine magic fish bait overnight, meow!\n(Xavier proudly puffs up his whiskers.)",
    ["Dialogue6001403"]="Ha, ha, ha! I knew you'd like my magic fish bait! Who wouldn't fall in love with such exquisite high quality fishing gear, meow?",
    ["Dialogue6001404"]="But I can't just tell you how to use this magic fish bait for free, meow! You have to give me a—What's the word you humans use?—fee! That's right, you have to pay me a fee of <color=#CA2E0AFF>some fish</color>, meow!",
    ["Dialogue6001501"]="Meowow! There's a lotta fish! You must really want this magic fish bait! In that case, let me teach you how to use it, meow!",
    ["Dialogue6001502"]="First, you attach the magic fish bait to your fishing line and throw your line into the water. Once you hook a fish, you have to shout \"mewzinya, mewzimya\" before reeling it in. That way you can make a fish print out of it! If you don't like the fish you caught, you can release it, meow.",
    ["Dialogue6001503"]="Now go <color=#CA2E0AFF>try it out</color>! Don't forget the magic in the fish bait has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>time limit</color>, so don't get too greedy, meow!",
    ["Dialogue6001601"]="Come meow, let me see the fish print you made... Meowow! My magic fish bait worked like a charm. What a beautiful fish print!",
    ["Dialogue6001602"]="If you ever make a fish print I'm interested it, I'll be happy to trade you for my treasures, meow!",
    ["Dialogue6001603"]="Why am I collecting fish prints, meow? Meowhahaha! What could be more attractive to a master fisherman like me than an endless collection of artistic prints of different fish?",
    ["Dialogue6001701"]="What a touching oath. I think that even Odin would be touched by your sincere affection.",
    ["Dialogue6001702"]="However, establishing the contract is only the first step to getting married. According to the traditions of Rune Kingdom, you must prepare wedding outfits and find a suitable witness to preside over the vow ceremony and the wedding. Naturally, you must prepare all of this yourself because only a ceremony filled with love will be blessed by the gods.",
    ["Dialogue6001703"]="For your witness, you just need someone who is willing to act as a witness to your relationship. I think your top priority is to craft wedding outfits that suit you the best. I have just the person for you—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>old tailor, Mewt</color>, who lives in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Prontera</color>. He was once the most prestigious outfit designer in Prontera, but unfortunately, ever since... Sigh, either way, he's stopped taking orders for years now.",
    ["Dialogue6001704"]="Hmm... So, you need someone to make your outfit? I have just the person for you—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>old tailor, Mewt</color>, who lives in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Prontera</color>. He was once the most prestigious outfit designer in Prontera, but unfortunately, ever since... Sigh, either way, he's stopped taking orders for years now.",
    ["Dialogue6001705"]="But if it's you, perhaps you'll be able to help Mewt regain his passion... In short, I want you to visit him and try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>persuade him to make custom wedding outfits for you</color>. Trust me, he won't let you down.",
    ["Dialogue6001801"]="Why are they not back yet?",
    ["Dialogue6001802"]="This is strange... He should have returned ages ago...\n(The gray-haired old man is hunched over as he looks into the distance from the door)\nW-who are you...?",
    ["Dialogue6001803"]="... Sigh. I've told Wolmas many times that I'll never touch needles and thread again. Why won't he listen?\nI'm sorry, you two. I retired a long time ago because I'm getting old, have poor eyesight, and no longer have the stamina I used to have when I was young. You should look for another tailor as soon as possible while you still have plenty of time to avoid delaying your wedding.",
    ["Dialogue6001804"]="I'm busy right now and don't have time to entertain you. Just go... Go away. Don't just stand here.\n(The old man waves his hand and motions for you to leave. At the same time, he raises his head and looks to the end of the path with anxiety and concern in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue6001805"]="... Actually, it isn't a big deal. It's just that my grandson hasn't returned yet. He's usually home on time before dinner. I wonder what's holding him up today...?",
    ["Dialogue6001806"]="You... You're willing to help me?\nT-thank you so much! My grandson is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jimmy</color>. He usually plays with his friends <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the field outside Prontera West Gate</color>. If you see him, can you tell him to come home as soon as he can? I'm really anxious.",
    ["Dialogue6001901"]="Connie... Connie...! Don't cry! Jimmy will be fine... M-maybe he already went home...",
    ["Dialogue6001902"]="*Cries* I blame all of you...! Why did all of you bully Jimmy... *Cries*",
    ["Dialogue6001903"]="Huh? You're asking me about Jimmy's whereabouts... Um...\n(Broca scratches the back of his head and looks to one side guiltily.)",
    ["Dialogue6001904"]="Jimmy... Jimmy has gone missing! It's all Broca's fault! He called Jimmy a liar and Jimmy got mad!",
    ["Dialogue6001905"]="This is what happened... We were playing hide and seek here like usual today, but Broca started quarreling with Jimmy while we were playing. Jimmy said his grandpa is the best tailor in all of Prontera, and Broca thought that Jimmy was lying. They had a big fight, then Jimmy ran off angrily and never came back. W-we're getting worried because it's getting darker and darker...",
    ["Dialogue6001906"]="B-but I've never seen Grandpa Mewt make clothes! They don't even have any thread or needles at home! H-how would I know whether he was telling the truth...",
    ["Dialogue6001907"]="Oh...? Even Archbishop Wolmas said that...? I-in that case, I guess it's true...",
    ["Dialogue6001908"]="Look! It's all your fault! We can't find Jimmy now! What should we do? *Cries*",
    ["Dialogue6001909"]="...I remember that the... <color=#CA2E0AFF>c-cemetery</color> is further along that way in the direction of all the trees...",
    ["Dialogue6001910"]="...Um, if you find Jimmy, can you help me tell him that I'm sorry? I didn't mean that... If he's willing to forgive me, I'll still be waiting for him here tomorrow to play hide and seek together!",
    ["Dialogue6002001"]="*Cries* Grandpa...",
    ["Dialogue600200101"]="Squad, concentrate your attack on the <color=#ff5252>Small Scythes</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6002002"]="Whoa...! W-who's there?!\n(The little boy clenches his fists. He is very scared, but he straightens his back staunchly.)",
    ["Dialogue600200201"]="When the Baphomet Jrs. are <color=#ff5252>very close to each other</color>, they will have high damage reduction. Eliminate them separately.",
    ["Dialogue6002003"]="Grandpa asked you to come looking for me...? *Sob* D-don't scare me like that then...",
    ["Dialogue600200301"]="Destroy the 4 <color=#ff5252>Demon Towers</color> and the rest of the monsters before Boss Energy reaches <color=#ff5252>100%</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6002004"]="I-I thought of a way to make grandpa happy! I know that grandpa used to be the most famous outfit designer of Prontera. I saw a dress grandpa made for grandma. That was the most gorgeous and beautiful dress I have ever seen! But... grandpa has not touched any needles or thread since grandma passed away...",
    ["Dialogue600200401"]="Dodge the incoming area attacks according to the <color=#ff5252>rune order on the side of the battlefield</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6002005"]="W-well... Can you take a picture of me in front of grandma's tombstone? The thing is, after grandma died, grandpa has rarely visited her here in the cemetery because he gets really sad and takes a long time to recover every single time. But I remember that grandma always said she loved the clothes grandpa made. She said that she felt like grandpa was by her side whenever she wore the clothes he made.",
    ["Dialogue6002101"]="Thank you! I... I just hope this picture will make grandpa happier...",
    ["Dialogue6002102"]="...Uh-huh! I'm sure it will! Let's return home then!",
    ["Dialogue6002201"]="Jimmy...! What took you so long? What happened?!",
    ["Dialogue6002202"]="... Jimmy has something for me? What is it?",
    ["Dialogue6002203"]="Grandpa... Look at this.",
    ["Dialogue6002301"]="... Did you go to the cemetery, Jimmy?",
    ["Dialogue6002302"]="I'm sorry, grandpa, I didn't mean to make you worry...",
    ["Dialogue6002303"]="You want me... to cheer up?",
    ["Dialogue6002304"]="Grandpa... In the past, whenever I was unhappy, grandma would cook a delicious meal and tell me that as long as I ate the food she cooked and wore the clothes you made, it'll be as if we're always with each other. Although grandma is gone now, if she knows that you've always been so unhappy and even stopped making clothes...",
    ["Dialogue6002305"]="(Jimmy sniffs hard and tries his best to not cry.)\nThen grandma will feel really sad! Because... Because grandma... she loved the clothes you made the most, grandpa!",
    ["Dialogue6002306"]="(The gray-haired old man squeezes the picture in his hands tightly as the rim of his eyes become red.)\nJimmy... Y-you...",
    ["Dialogue6002307"]="(After taking a deep breath, he hugs Jimmy and holds him tightly in his arms.)\nDon't cry! Or... or else your grandma will say you aren't acting like a man again!",
    ["Dialogue6002308"]="*Cries* I... I... *Cries*\n(The little boy buries his head in his grandfather's arms and makes indistinguishable sounds as he tries to speak.)",
    ["Dialogue6002309"]="Phew... I-I also want to thank you both. Like Jimmy said, maybe... maybe Ellie wouldn't want to see me the way I am right now because she has always supported my work as a tailor... I'll always remember the way she looked when she wore the dresses I made...",
    ["Dialogue6002310"]="... If you don't mind, I hope I can make your wedding outfits for you. Although I'm already an old man... I promise I can make you the most gorgeous outfits in all of Prontera if I have the right materials.",
    ["Dialogue6002311"]="Haha, then I'll show you that I've still got the touch. Come back to see me after you've collected all the materials!",
    ["Dialogue6002401"]="How is it? Are you satisfied with it?",
    ["Dialogue6002402"]="(He laughs and waves his hand.)\nYou earned this with your sincerity, so you don't need to thank me. I hope that in the days to come, you will continue to support and love each other, as well as remember your true feelings.",
    ["Dialogue6002403"]="You must live together happily for a lifetime, just like Jimmy's grandparents!",
    ["Dialogue6002501"]="Huh? You want to end your marriage with your partner, Adventurer? I still remember the beautiful vow you once made... \"Not the rising sun, nor the dark of night shall separate us... From today on, we will share our triumphs and strife alike...\" That sweet scene still lingers in my mind. Are you sure you want to give up on this once-in-a-lifetime relationship?",
    ["Dialogue6002502"]="Eh? You want to end your marriage vow, Adventurer? According to my wedding ceremony registration form, it seems that you and your partner are still waiting to hold your wedding. If you choose to end your vow right now, the wedding will automatically be canceled, and <color=#ffe788>the wedding fees you've already paid will not be refunded</color>! Do you really want to give up this chance for eternal happiness?",
    ["Dialogue6002503"]="Perhaps every relationship inevitably comes to an end... Sometimes knowing when to separate is an achievement in itself. Saying goodbye... may be the last beautiful thing you can do for each other. Now then, please choose the way in which you wish to end your marriage vow.",
    ["Dialogue6002504"]="As this is an uncontested divorce, please party up <color=#ffe788>fe788>with your partner</color> and come to me, <color=#ffe788>fe788>together</color>, to end your vow...",
    ["Dialogue6002505"]="If both of you are absolutely sure that you want to end your relationship, and are determined to start over, please sign the agreement in front of you and agree to divorce.",
    ["Dialogue6002506"]="It seems that you haven't reached an agreement yet. If you haven't settled things completely, it would be wise for you to talk it through before making a decision.",
    ["Dialogue6002507"]="Sometimes, when fate brings us together, and life pulls us apart, you can find solace in the beauty of the memories you share, and let go of those moments of resentment. Remember the good times, and from then on, the world will open its arms to you. You will be free to find beauty in new memories...",
    ["Dialogue6002508"]="You made an eternal vow, but for one of you, the bond has run its course... Although everyone has the right to pursue happiness, those who break their promises must pay <color=#ffe788>the corresponding price</color>—a reminder of the weight of their actions. Of course, this price depends on your <color=#ffe788>Adventurer Level, Couple Level, and your partner's last login time</color>. Are you sure you want to proceed?",
    ["Dialogue6002509"]="For everything lost, something is gained. Let today's farewell herald serendipitous encounters in the future. Congratulations on your newfound freedom... To the pursuit of happiness!",
    ["Dialogue6002510"]="If you're not ready to pay the price for breaking your promise, please think again and come back to me when you have enough money.",
    ["Dialogue6002601"]="(Footprints continue all the way from the grass to the woods. The steps aren't very large, but they are quite dense. It looks like someone widly ran through here.)",
    ["Dialogue6002701"]="(The footprints in the forest don't look so clear anymore. Fortunately, these crushed leaves indicate the direction.)",
    ["Dialogue6002801"]="(The muddy footprints lead to the south and disappear at the entrance of the cemetery... Why did he come here?)",
    ["Dialogue6002901"]="Let me guess—judging from your delighted expression, I believe you managed to get wedding outfits that you fancy. Am I right?",
    ["Dialogue6002902"]="(Wolmas sighs lightly, and you can see regret and reluctance in his expression.)\nSigh... While it's true that the most painful thing to two people who have pledged to spend their lives together is the death of either of them... one shouldn't stagnate because of this.",
    ["Dialogue6002903"]="(Wolmas takes both of your hands separately and places them on top of each other.)\n... Even if we can't change the final outcome, we must be grateful for all our encounters. I hope you will both take each other's company to heart, become a team, and embark on a journey that belongs exclusively to you.",
    ["Dialogue6002904"]="Now... Although I can't wait to see how you look in those outfits, there's one last thing you have to do. You need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> a <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness</color> who is willing to bear witness to your sincere relationship and <color=#CA2E0AFF>invite that person to preside over the vow ceremony and the wedding</color>, as well as give a speech for you.",
    ["Dialogue6002905"]="This is the only thing I can't help you with, because this witness is an important person who has bore witness to your relationship, and only you two, who have experienced this adventure together and progressed together to reach this point, can decide who is suitable. That being said... I believe that no matter who you choose, the person you invite will definitely accept your invitation joyfully.",
    ["Dialogue6003001"]="Oh? What's this...?\n(The dean strokes his beard and smiles knowingly, as if he has already guessed something.)",
    ["Dialogue6003002"]="Ohohoho! Your witness, huh... To a mentor, nothing is more satisfying than bearing witness to their own student walking into the wedding hall, holding hands with the love of their life!",
    ["Dialogue6003003"]="Of course I'm willing. What reason do I have to refuse?",
    ["Dialogue6003004"]="Ohohoho! A wedding speech? I'm honored that you have tasked me with it. I must prepare my speech properly... Come on, tell me your story. What was the most touching moment in your adventures? It would be even better if you could show me the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pictures of your happy memories together</color>...",
    ["Dialogue6003101"]="I see, so the most touching moment was your first encounter? I understand. As people say, no one knows when love first springs to life, but we fall so deeply once we fall in love. That is why the fate between people is so wonderful. When you first met, would you have guessed that the person in front of you would become your most important partner in your adventures?",
    ["Dialogue6003102"]="Excellent! I think I know what I'll say at your wedding now. Don't worry, I'm sure the vow ceremony and the wedding will be a memorable experience that you'll never forget. Ohohoho!",
    ["Dialogue6003201"]="Hmm... It seems only fitting to have the mentor who watched your growth to witness the happiest moment in your life.",
    ["Dialogue6003202"]="(The Archbishop strokes his beard and looks at you with satisfaction.)\nCongratulations on completing all the preparations. It's now time to perform the vow ceremony you've been waiting so long for. With the blessing of the gods, I hope you will grow old together and be happy forever.",
    ["Dialogue6003301"]="...Is that so? You're about to hold the vow ceremony... I give my sincere blessings to both of you.",
    ["Dialogue6003302"]="...I'm so happy that you invited me, but if I have to leave this place...\n(The Great Sage looks at the flower garden around him and makes a hesitant expression.)",
    ["Dialogue6003303"]="No, I'm very willing, but as you know, this flower garden is filled with herbs that I put a lot of effort into growing, and they are important materials that I need to discover the truth of magic. If I am to be your witness, I will have to leave this place for many days. If the nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hornets</color> do anything to my plants during this time...",
    ["Dialogue6003304"]="It'll be great if you're willing to help.\nPerhaps this is a good opportunity for you to verify your mutual trust...",
    ["Dialogue6003401"]="(Kroneika strokes his beard and looks at you with satisfaction.)\nI'm amazed at your strength. Not only that, I also saw your tacit understanding and trust. I am honored to witness your vow ceremony and wedding with my own eyes.\nWithout further ado, let's go now.",
    ["Dialogue6003501"]="What's wrong, soldier? Is there anything you want to report to me?",
    ["Dialogue6003502"]="...You are inviting me to be the witness at your wedding? You're really... really brave! Hahahaha! Congratulations! I'll gladly preside over the vow ceremony and the wedding for you!",
    ["Dialogue6003503"]="However, after you get married, you mustn't forget that you're both members of the Kingdom Defense Force! You must always remember your mission to defend the kingdom! Do you understand?!",
    ["Dialogue6003504"]="Very good! Now, I order you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>eliminate the monsters in the sewers</color> immediately!",
    ["Dialogue6003505"]="Do you remember the first rule you learned when you joined the Kingdom Defense Force? You must never question your commanding officer!\nNow go!",
    ["Dialogue6003601"]="As expected of one of my soldiers! I'm proud of you!\nNow hold your head high and complete the vow ceremony that belongs only to you! I will witness everything until the last moment for you!",
    ["Dialogue6003701"]="...You want me to preside over your vow ceremony and wedding?\n(A look of surprise flashes momentarily across Hallam's face.)",
    ["Dialogue6003702"]="No, of course I can, and I would love to. It's just that... Ahem, I can't go in these dirty clothes. Alas, I blame those <color=#CA2E0AFF>Thief Bugs</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drainliars</color> in the sewers who are always ready to stir up trouble at the drop of a hat. That elimination operation has left me in quite the sorry state...",
    ["Dialogue6003703"]="Really? You're willing to help? I feel so embarrassed that I need to trouble you to do this kind of thing at this time... In that case, I'll take the opportunity to change into a clean formal outfit then. Let's meet here again afterwards.",
    ["Dialogue6003801"]="Oh? What perfect timing!\nIt's time to go to your vow ceremony now. Let's go!",
    ["Dialogue6003901"]="...You want me to be your witness for your vow ceremony and wedding?\n(Jesqurienne looks at your interlocked hands and falls deep in thought for some reason.)",
    ["Dialogue6003902"]="Oh, please don't get me wrong, it isn't that I'm not willing. On the contrary, I'm really honored that you invited me. It's just... I have something I want to ask you about.",
    ["Dialogue6003903"]="To be honest, recently, a... friend has often been asking me some questions about love. She seems to have fallen in love with someone, but is suffering because she isn't able to express her feelings to him... I can see that you trust each other greatly. I also want my friend to have a love as perfect as yours. Do you have any advice for her?",
    ["Dialogue6003904"]="(Jesqurienne's eyes light up suddenly.)\nA gift? Yes, it might be possible to make the other person aware of her feelings with the right gift... If you had to choose a gift, what <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> do you think is most suitable for expressing one's love?",
    ["Dialogue6004001"]="I see, even I can feel the love inside the gift...\nI'll convey your opinions to C... Ahem, my friend. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue6004002"]="Of course, I'll definitely be there at your vow ceremony and wedding on time. It's my great fortune to be able to witness your happiest moment.",
    ["Dialogue6004101"]="Hey! It's been a long time, my friend! How are you?",
    ["Dialogue6004102"]="(Jimmy Lin's handsome eyes gleam as they widen in surprise.)\nYou're getting married? Well... this sure is something worth celebrating! I need to prepare a great gift for you!",
    ["Dialogue6004103"]="You want me to be your witness for the wedding? Of course I'm willing to! I mean, I'm absolutely delighted to! You're the first good friend I made in this world, and we've been through so many exciting and thrilling adventures together! I'm so lucky that I get to witness the wedding between you and the love of your life!",
    ["Dialogue6004104"]="(Jimmy Lin starts laughing and gives you a high five.)\nOf course, this adventure is far from over. More happy memories await us in the future!\nLet's go, my friend! It's time to witness the happiest moment in your life!",
    ["Dialogue6004201"]="You can't walk here. You'll become bait for Titans...",
    ["Dialogue6004301"]="My mom is missing... I can't find my home. Waaah...",
    ["Dialogue6004401"]="My child!\n(She hugs the little girl tight.)\nOh, thank goodness...",
    ["Dialogue6004402"]="Mom, the Adventurer brought me back, and a guy in weird clothes saved me!",
    ["Dialogue6004403"]="Thank you, thank you... Child, let's leave this place together!",
    ["Dialogue6004501"]="I'm lucky to have survived...",
    ["Dialogue6004601"]="One day... It would be great to go exploring in the outside world...",
    ["Dialogue6004602"]="The water in fire! The world of ice! Seas of sand! The world outside must be many times wider than the walls!",
    ["Dialogue6004701"]="I can't believe I didn't notice until the gas was nearly used up...",
    ["Dialogue6004801"]="(The tall man who looks like an ape is looking quietly at the walls of Prontera, with nothingness and indifference in his eyes)\nStones... There aren't enough...",
    ["Dialogue6004802"]="Can you help me find some stones?",
    ["Dialogue6004803"]="How can I get in without stones?...\n(The men take no notice of you. It seems as if they won't retreat to the wall for shelter without \"stones\".)\nThe ones needed are pointy, round , flat, square. There are many indeed...)",
    ["Dialogue6004901"]="Ah... enough holding it in.",
    ["Dialogue6004902"]="Back? Of course. We will meet again seen...",
    ["Dialogue6005001"]="This is a big problem... Everyone, start cleaning immediately.",
    ["Dialogue6005002"]="This is one of the conditions of you coming here. You should abide by it.",
    ["Dialogue6005101"]="A big cleanup of the Palace?! But I already cleaned their rooms in the Palace two says ago. It's still clean!",
    ["Dialogue6005102"]="Cough... Did you clean before you discussed the Load-out with them, or after?",
    ["Dialogue6005103"]="(Calvin lowers his voice and moves close in front of you.)\nThe cleanliness of the Parallel World guests is getting worse... Okay, we'll organize another big cleaning, with magic!",
    ["Dialogue6005201"]="I'll go see the rooms you cleaned. I'll leave this place to you.",
    ["Dialogue6005301"]="You mean the strange gust from the Parallel World? There's no way to make this stuff at the moment, but me and my old Magic Furnace buddy have been working on a short time replacement, so I'm sure we'll have good news soon!",
    ["Dialogue6005401"]="I'm now... doing what I can...",
    ["Dialogue6005501"]="The bustling streets, the busy stores, the marvelous fountain...",
    ["Dialogue6005502"]="I... Adventurer, in your kingdom, is there someone that dresses like me?",
    ["Dialogue6005503"]="I used to dream about someone whose face was always blurry, but I was not scared. We talked about anything and everything like we were best friends. On the day before our coming-of-age ceremony, we arrived at a river, and I never saw him again after he got on a boat.",
    ["Dialogue6005504"]="I know it sounds crazy, but I want to find him. I know I can! So I joined a caravan to travel the world and look for him. Will you help me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue6005505"]="But I can't write in your language... Adventurer, can you help register my search notice on the Mission Board? In return for your kindness, I can teach you a simple game from my homeland. According to our calendar, today is the best day for Egg Balancing!",
    ["Dialogue6005506"]="By the way, the name of the commissioner is Lingjun Chu in your language. Thank you for your help.",
    ["Dialogue6005601"]="Thank you again for your generosity!\n(Lingjun Chu smiles and makes a strange gesture at you.)",
    ["Dialogue6005602"]="This is a popular game in our hometown. It's said that if you place an egg vertically during the day, when the positive energy is at its peak, you will receive a mystery gift. If you are one of the fortunate few, the gift you receive will be even more magical! Adventurer, are you ready to give it a go?",
    ["Dialogue6010101"]="How can someone like me make such a stupid <color=#CA2E0AFF>mistake</color>?\n(If I confess to the queen now, they will surely throw me out...)",
    ["Dialogue6010102"]="Who goes there?",
    ["Dialogue6010103"]="(Morts calms down when he sees it's you.)\nOh, it's you... Wait, did you hear everything?",
    ["Dialogue6010104"]="Then you must help me! If her majesty finds out that I lost her <color=#CA2E0AFF>invitations</color>, she will no longer think that I'm mature and dependable! And not just her! Isabella from the Rose Red Tavern, and the Obeaune, too!",
    ["Dialogue6010105"]="Morts, why are you called Morts?\n(Morts plays a short and sad melody, and you see the light of hope in his glittering eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue6010106"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>invitation to ROX's 1st Anniversary Music Festival</color>, where musicians gather and play amazing music on the promised day. Drinks, songs, and cheers... even I, the greatest bard in modern history, decided to join. I had too many drinks, and when I woke up, the tickets in my pocket were gone. Only this was left...",
    ["Dialogue6010107"]="(Morts tosses a ball of white fur at you.)\nIt must be the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatic at the Prontera South Gate</color>! Only they have such soft and thick white fur! Ah-choo! Please help me get the invitations back from them! Ah-choo!",
    ["Dialogue6010108"]="No, they're too cute! I can't do it! And... ah-choo!",
    ["Dialogue6010109"]="What?! Come back soon! Ah-choo!",
    ["Dialogue6010201"]="Good, you would have had to go inside if you were late just a little...",
    ["Dialogue6010202"]="(Morts plays a happy melody on his lute.)\nTake the friendship of the bard, Adventurer. Ah-choo! By the way...",
    ["Dialogue6010203"]="(Morts pulls out a list, and you see the Lunatic's fur on his hand.)\nI... I need to send these invitations... Ah-choo!",
    ["Dialogue6010301"]="(The Parrot Mailbox accepts the invitation and stops to look at one of the shining names.)\nThat's them! I can't believe there's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>band</color> that looks good and sings better than the parrot family! Unless it's in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hokkien</color>! Hey, are they really coming?",
    ["Dialogue6010401"]="(Isabella takes the invitation and focuses on one of the shining names.)\nAn interesting invitation. Hmm, <color=#CA2E0AFF>a rock band formed by five friends</color>? Maybe I can invite them to perform at the Rose Red Tavern after the festival.",
    ["Dialogue6010501"]="(Hallam takes the invitation and focuses on one of the shining names.)\nEntertainment of a parallel world? But the knights do need music to loosen them up. If they can <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a good time</color> with this <color=#CA2E0AFF>male singer from Taipei</color>, maybe it will help them with their stress.",
    ["Dialogue6010601"]="(Wolmas the Archbishop takes the invitation and focuses on one of the shining names.)\nSo is this the <color=#CA2E0AFF>female singer and songwriter</color> that the young people are talking about? Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue6010701"]="This is not for sale! I had no idea you had something so precious!\n(Vienna carefully puts the invitation in her backpack, and her gaze passes over one of the shining names nonchalantly.)",
    ["Dialogue6010702"]="Name your price, Adventurer. The customers from Lindra are also looking for a musical journey. I heard this <color=#CA2E0AFF>female singer can even perform musicals</color>. She must have a wonderful voice.",
    ["Dialogue6010703"]="Um, right. But Morts is standing by the fountain and looking at us. Does he want to say something?",
    ["Dialogue6010801"]="(He takes the invitation and signs his name coolly.)\nAhem! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Here's your</color> autographed copy of the ROX 1st Anniversary Music Festival invitation.",
    ["Dialogue6010802"]="That's right! Those who are willing to lend a helping hand will be remembered in my song because I am a kind bard. Now that my mission is over, Adventurer, I will see you <color=#CA2E0AFF>during the stream at 20:00 on October 15</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6020101"]="What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue6020102"]="I swear by next week's vacation that this piece of music is the best I've heard recently! So, don't worry, everyone will love it!",
    ["Dialogue6020103"]="But...",
    ["Dialogue6020104"]="Shhh! Hmm hmm, hmm hmm hmm...\n(As Rowan hums, everyone falls silent in the bustling Rose Red Tavern. For a moment, you see a look of hesitation on the Obeaune's face.)",
    ["Dialogue6020105"]="What do you think? Does it sound good?",
    ["Dialogue6020106"]="(Rowan's eyes light up, and he gives you a look of acknowledgement.)\nIt should sound good. The TOYS is a famous <color=#CA2E0AFF>singer-songwriter</color> in the parallel world, and you just heard his unfinished creation! Look, even though he's created such a beautiful piece of music, my friend is still searching for more inspiration to make it even better!",
    ["Dialogue6020107"]="You're right. Everyone likes different styles of music. It's truly difficult to create music that everyone likes. Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue6020108"]="Mixing a variety of genres and integrating them into songs has always been something The TOYS is good at... Actually, The TOYS has always wanted to travel all over the world to find musical inspiration, but I've always used his safety as a reason to stop him.\n<color=#A1979FFF>The monsters out there are too dangerous, and I've been busy working in the Library, so it's been difficult to accompany him.</color>",
    ["Dialogue6020109"]="As far as I know, beyond Prontera is the desert city where the Demon King Morroc is sealed, the magician's paradise of Geffen, Izlude Island where pirate treasure is hidden, and the pure land of Payon surrounded by mountains...",
    ["Dialogue6020110"]="(After listening to his friend's words, Rowan's face shows a look of longing. He then takes a deep breath and looks at you slowly.)\nAdventurer, can you do me a favor?",
    ["Dialogue6020111"]="I heard you've traveled every inch of the kingdom, and bards sing your tales in their poems. Even the strongest monster is unable to resist your attacks. It would be great if you'd be willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for inspiration</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>with</color> The TOYS and protect him along the way.",
    ["Dialogue6020112"]="Thank you so much! Rowan said that every adventurer puts a <color=#CA2E0AFF>river lantern</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Verdant Lotus Pond</color> at the South Gate when they leave to pray for safety. After I finish packing my luggage, let's meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>at the entrance of Rose Red Tavern</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6020201"]="I'm done! Adventurer, what <color=#CA2E0AFF>river lantern</color> should we choose at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>? I want one that looks like a Poring or a Lunatic!",
    ["Dialogue6020301"]="Stop running! I caught another one putting a river lantern in. Meow! Look at this pond. If I didn't dredge out all the river lanterns, they would have blocked the river a long time ago!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Anyone who get in the way of my fishing will dream of Ghostrings!</color>",
    ["Dialogue6020302"]="Tut, tut, tut... Putting river lanterns in the water to pray for safety is no longer popular. This is what everyone is doing now! Meow!",
    ["Dialogue6020303"]="Ta da! This is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drift Bottle</color>! Any adventurer who <color=#CA2E0AFF>goes fishing before January 1, 2022</color> will have the chance to fish out Drift Bottles that have been thrown by other adventurers. Drift Bottles that are thrown into creeks flow into rivers, lakes, and even the sea with the current. They may be picked up by strangers or they may continue to drift. Isn't this more meaningful than a river lamp that will eventually go out?",
    ["Dialogue6020304"]="He's right. Adventurer, can you show me how to throw a Drift Bottle? Although there's something similar in my world, it's my first time doing this in a parallel world!",
    ["Dialogue6020305"]="You've got quite the discerning eye, young man! Almost all the adventurers in Prontera have taken fishing lessons from me, but I don't recall seeing you before?",
    ["Dialogue6020306"]="Looking for inspiration? I don't know what type of music I like, and I don't understand music theory. Meow! But I've always lived in Prontera, so I couldn't possibly dislike it if you wrote a song about Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue6020307"]="Prontera?",
    ["Dialogue6020308"]="Yes, Prontera is the capital of the kingdom. It's repelled countless monster invasions. Its walls are considered one of our strongest <color=#CA2E0AFF>lines of defense</color>. Ahem... I've said too much. If you want to know more about Prontera, I can share my <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret base</color> with you. Come back to me after throwing a Drift Bottle!",
    ["Dialogue6020401"]="We're here! This is my secret base, which is also the only remaining ruins of ancient Prontera! Adventurer, do you know how the Evil Serpent Jormungand was killed?",
    ["Dialogue6020402"]="That's right! Seven adventuring heroes lead by Tristan Gaebolg killed the serpent and founded the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom. The place where the serpent died was where Prontera was later built.",
    ["Dialogue6020403"]="This was once part of Prontera's <color=#CA2E0AFF>outer wall</color>. It wasn't called Prontera back then. It was just a stone wall used to defend against monsters. Poring's blessed by the Goddess and panicked people lived inside the city, and there was a large army of monsters outside the.",
    ["Dialogue6020404"]="(Xavier strokes a non-existent beard.)\nThe city wall was breached before the decisive battle. As a result, the dwellings everyone had painstakingly built were destroyed. This was when seven adventurers stepped up to fight for the people. They slayed Jormungand as recorded in the records and ended the war. Later, more and more adventurers poured into Prontera. The walls were reinforced many times, leaving these ruins here.",
    ["Dialogue6020405"]="I see. So the lovely murals on the walls are actually from such a long time ago. I...\n(The TOYS stares silently at the murals of Porings, appearing to grasp something abstract and fleeting.)",
    ["Dialogue6020406"]="I have an idea! Adventurer, inspiration comes and goes, so I must go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> to continue creating. I hope I'll be able to perform my new piece for you the next time we meet!",
    ["Dialogue6020501"]="Adventurer, this is the melody I created based on my inspiration from before. If I had to depict my impression of Prontera in musical form, then this is surely it! Thank you for your assistance! Hmm... How should I perform this? Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>dance</color>?",
    ["Dialogue6020502"]="It doesn't matter. Close your eyes and surrender yourself to the music; you'll naturally move to the beat. Don't worry, leave the music to me!",
    ["Dialogue6020503"]="Excellent! I believe our performance will win everyone's applause. Are you ready? Three, two, one! <color=#CA2E0AFF>IT'S SHOW TIME!</color>",
    ["Dialogue6020601"]="Amazing! I announce that our performance is a resounding success!",
    ["Dialogue6020602"]="Are you amazed at the speed of my creativity? It's thanks to the inspiration I got from this ancient yet flourishing city, as well as the fishing master. Adventurer, although I don't know what style of music most people like, I think that if a piece of music reminds people of their hometown, then most people won't dislike it at the very least.",
    ["Dialogue6020603"]="Are... Are you willing to accompany me as I create my next piece?",
    ["Dialogue6020604"]="That's great! Rowan said you've traveled every inch of the kingdom. If you can help me learn more about the residents of each major city and their <color=#CA2E0AFF>customs and culture</color> before I start creating, then I'll be able to integrate the styles of all the major cities and create an excellent piece. Haha, I can't wait to pack my bags. I'll see you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>entrance of Rose Red Tavern</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6020701"]="Thank you for waiting! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude Island</color> isn't far from Prontera, so I believe we'll be there soon!",
    ["Dialogue6020801"]="You are...?\n(Old Clay looks up and down before his gaze rests on your right hand.)\nSo you're the adventurer who helped me repair the Mission Board. I remember you had amazing craftsmanship. So, have you decided to become my assistant?",
    ["Dialogue6020802"]="Hahaha! Of course you can! But I haven't finished my woodwork yet. Look at this freshly delivered wood. If I don't <color=#CA2E0AFF>wax and polish</color> it immediately, it'll soon be <color=#CA2E0AFF>corroded</color> by the moisture in the air. Izlude Island is an island after all, so the consequences will be dire if it rains after that!",
    ["Dialogue6020803"]="So, young adventurer, do you want to learn another type of craft?",
    ["Dialogue6020901"]="Yes, now I don't have to worry about it getting corroded! Come, I'll show you my lifetime's greatest work, which is also the <color=#CA2E0AFF>most dazzling pearl</color> of Izlude Island!",
    ["Dialogue6021001"]="Criatura Academy is the pride of every person of Izlude Island. I am the <color=#CA2E0AFF>designer of Criatura Academy</color>; it's like a child to me. But no matter how strong and majestic a building is, if the materials aren't replaced in time, it will eventually be corroded beyond recognition. That's why I was so anxious about that batch of wood.",
    ["Dialogue6021002"]="Have you also noticed it, adventurer? Criatura Academy's materials have been replaced many times since it was built. Perhaps the parts will be replaced again and again when maintenance is performed on it after I leave this world.",
    ["Dialogue6021003"]="A craftsman's work allows him to live forever. However, when successors entirely replace the work to the extent that not one inch of the original work remains, then who is the one living on?",
    ["Dialogue6021004"]="Perhaps you're right. My teacher used to tell me that craftsmen infuse their work with blood, sweat, and tears before offering them to the world. However, this gift must not be opened by the craftsman themselves because it belongs to the entire world. Regardless of how it transforms, Criatura Academy will always be the most beautiful building on Izlude Island. Countless students have chosen their job classes at Criatura. I'm just satisfied as long as my name is associated with this place.",
    ["Dialogue6021005"]="I'm just <color=#CA2E0AFF>satisfied</color> as long as my name is associated with this place. Adventurer, what is this young lad's profession?",
    ["Dialogue6021006"]="He works with music? How wonderful! Young man, if you lack inspiration, you could remain on Izlude Island and work as my assistant for a while.",
    ["Dialogue6021007"]="Thank you for your kindness. After listening to your story, I've also been inspired by this magnificent building. Adventurer, I'll see you at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6021101"]="There's no time to lose! Let's start right away!",
    ["Dialogue6021201"]="Even though the musical style I've used this time is completely different from before, the result is surprisingly good! Oh right, before packing, we'll have to wash off the wax on our hands.",
    ["Dialogue6021301"]="Oh! We'll need to take a really long ship ride to reach the next stop:<color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6021401"]="(A young man wearing a sailor's uniform is stabbing bread with a fork and slowly dipping it into soup. When you recognize him, he looks up at you, the corners of his mouth covered in breadcrumbs.)\nWhoa! Who... Who sent you? Oh no, I just remembered! I haven't lowered the fleet's anchors yet. I better go!",
    ["Dialogue6021402"]="Ahem! Oh, it's you, adventurer, haha, haha... Why are you looking for me? I'll tell you now, you can't go out fishing; it's closed season!",
    ["Dialogue6021403"]="No way! Adventurer, there's a saying in Alberta:<color=#CA2E0AFF>\"If you don't eat well, you won't work well.\"</color> Since I haven't even finished eating my bread appetizer, let alone the entire meal, how do you expect me to have the strength to take you out?",
    ["Dialogue6021404"]="3 hours.",
    ["Dialogue6021405"]="Oh? That's a strange look on your face, adventurer. Would you like to sit and join me?",
    ["Dialogue6021406"]="My sailor's intuition tells me you're not very happy right now. All right, to cheer up my dear friend, I've decided to share the most authentic dish among us Albertan sailors:<color=#CA2E0AFF>baked seabird eggs</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6021407"]="Bake the eggs completely before peeling the shells open, revealing smooth egg whites and soft yolks. Then, cut them into pieces and dip them in the sauce before eating. It's absolutely... irresistible! That dish is the only way I could even consider cutting my eating time from 3 hours to 3 minutes.",
    ["Dialogue6021408"]="Sadly this restaurant doesn't serve baked seabird eggs, but if you're willing to go to the nest at the port... There's three of us, so <color=#CA2E0AFF>three eggs</color> should be enough!",
    ["Dialogue6021501"]="Baked seabird eggs! One serving each, finish up, and we'll be ready to depart!",
    ["Dialogue6021502"]="Oh, oh! I know where to bring you! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6021601"]="(With his back towards you, Pascal gazes at the anchored ships.)\nAlberta is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>incredibly bustling but also incredibly tranquil</color> city.",
    ["Dialogue6021602"]="At any time of the day, there are be ships of various sizes docked at the port. All manner of people disembark and impatiently blend in with the crowds at the markets, shopping streets, and taverns. Vendor cries, sailor yells, seabird noises, and the sounds of breaking waves are ceaseless and unending.",
    ["Dialogue6021603"]="You can only experience Alberta in its quietest state before dawn and during the evening. People admiring the sunrise and sunset rarely talk, and under the dim light, seabirds fold their wings and allow you to stroke them. On rainy days, it seems as though the entire world has fallen silent.",
    ["Dialogue6021604"]="(Pascal smiles in a sly but delighted manner.)\nOnly experienced sailors know that those are the best times to get bird eggs.",
    ["Dialogue6021605"]="What? I can't hear you... Why don't you enjoy the beautiful scenery for now. Who knows? You might find some inspiration after a while.",
    ["Dialogue6021606"]="I can't believe that such beautiful scenery can also be found in a parallel world.\n(The TOYS closes his eyes and you see a gentle sea breeze lift up the hair on his forehead.)",
    ["Dialogue6021607"]="Extreme levels of tranquility and bustle and the citizens' tacit understanding of each other—this is indeed a miraculous city! Mister sailor, can I <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> aboard your ship?",
    ["Dialogue6021608"]="You found your inspiration so quickly? Well then... it just so happens that there's a ship headed for Prontera. I swear upon the Alson Fleet's good name that its deck is definitely not leaky!",
    ["Dialogue6021701"]="Adventurer, come and listen to my latest piece! I hope you don't get seasick. After all, this melody is inspired by the ocean.",
    ["Dialogue6021801"]="Your dancing was simply exquisite! Perhaps when this journey is over, you can come to the tavern regularly and perform with me? But before that, we must pack for the next journey. Meet you at the usual place!",
    ["Dialogue6021901"]="I'm here! A large part of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc region</color> has been covered by the desert. I hope we don't get lost.",
    ["Dialogue6022001"]="Long time no see, adventurer! Is this your friend? If so, you should try the Desert Tomato juice. It's the tavern's new offering and I highly recommend it!",
    ["Dialogue6022002"]="Sorry, I cannot leave the tavern for the time being. Furthermore...",
    ["Dialogue6022003"]="It's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pattie</color>, my new friend. Ever since she arrived at the tavern, she's been trapped by Morroc's sandstorms; she hasn't been able to go outside for ages. Do you want to make a deal with me, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue6022004"]="A seasoned traveler like you must have collected quite a few exotic trinkets during your journeys? It would be great if you could <color=#CA2E0AFF>put a smile on my new friend's face</color> by gifting her some. If you do so, I can tell you everything I know about Morroc.",
    ["Dialogue6022101"]="That's right, this is the most mysterious place in all of Morroc: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color>! To this day, even scientists and scholars have no idea why this cavern is still intact after thousands of years. Maybe it's been blessed by Drops? Or maybe the magic circle inside is still working? Then, there are those people who say that Anubis, God of the Underworld, slumbers here, and anybody who trespasses will perish in his dreams.",
    ["Dialogue6022102"]="However, desert travelers can find water, food, and shelter in the surrounding area. Legends say that the Desert Tomatoes found here were once tokens of love between Pharaoh Osiris and his queen, Eassis. On the one hand, it represents the danger of death. On the other hand, it represents the arrival of love. Isn't it romantic? Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue6022103"]="Hey! Handsome young man, what else do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue6022104"]="I seem to have come across the name \"Morroc\" in Rowan's Library before. Why would a city be named after the Demon King?",
    ["Dialogue6022105"]="You are right. The name Morroc does indeed belong to the Demon King. Legend has it that Lady Margaret of the Nerius family employed a trick to split open Morroc's abdomen. The Demon King fled in panic but was <color=#CA2E0AFF>sealed</color> at this very location by a powerful swordsman. The lucky people that survived then established a new city here, Morroc, both as a witness and a warning.",
    ["Dialogue6022106"]="Oh, I see! The unique desert landscape, a legend surrounding death and love... Adventurer, I suddenly feel a spark of inspiration and must compose something immediately!",
    ["Dialogue6022201"]="You're here. The musical style I used this time is completely different from the one in Alberta. I'm still thinking about how I can integrate the styles together! Anyway, are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue6022301"]="It's hard to believe, but we've already completed most of the journey. The time has just flown by. I'll cherish every last minute that remains. I'll come and find you after I've washed all the sand off my body.",
    ["Dialogue6022401"]="Ahem... I was almost late. If only there was a type of magic that made it possible to travel through time. If so, would we be able to see ourselves returning to Prontera?",
    ["Dialogue6022501"]="Underground... Underground monsters... I must... <color=#CA2E0AFF>photograph</color>... Master...",
    ["Dialogue6022601"]="For the past few days, I've been trying to find a way to strengthen the barrier. Thank you, adventurer. In a moment, I'll ask the magician to strengthen the barrier. By the way, why are you visiting Geffen?",
    ["Dialogue6022602"]="I can't believe there are people who would visit this city apart from magicians. Since you bear no ill will against Geffen, I'll be happy to welcome you to our city. Although, Geffen is surrounded on three sides by the territories of different races, so we are constantly being harassed by monsters all year round. The only place left that's both safe and can spark inspiration is the interior of Geffen Tower.",
    ["Dialogue6022603"]="I understand. In that case, we'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit Geffen Tower</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6022604"]="Just a minute! You're from a parallel world. Is there so-called \"magic\" in your world?",
    ["Dialogue6022605"]="Regretfully, I...\n(The TOYS gazes at Jesqurienne's gleaming palms, which are twinkling with starlight)\nWh-What is that?!",
    ["Dialogue6022606"]="This is a beam of light shaped by magic. It will follow you to every nook and cranny in Geffen Tower. If you <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill certain conditions</color>, it will appear and speak to you.",
    ["Dialogue6022701"]="Oh? Looks like you've already discovered the conditions for triggering the magic.",
    ["Dialogue6022702"]="This is my first time seeing real magic. How interesting! Adventurer, I'd like to try teleporting back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>. See you later!",
    ["Dialogue6022801"]="Until now, I can still remember the way that beam of light came into being in Master Jesqurienne's hands. Would you like to listen to this magical melody?",
    ["Dialogue6022901"]="I wish I could stay in Geffen for a couple more days to experience more of the wonders of magic. All right, adventurer, let's continue with our journey!",
    ["Dialogue6023001"]="Adventurer, have you heard of the legendary Valkyries? Word has it that the Gods used to live in Glast Heim. Perhaps we can witness real miracles in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6023101"]="O almighty but silent Goddess, your pious people humbly beg for your mercy...",
    ["Dialogue6023102"]="Shush... Don't interrupt my <color=#CA2E0AFF>prayer</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6023103"]="Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang!",
    ["Dialogue6023104"]="...\n(A sudden clanging sounds interrupts your conversation. You notice a look of resignation in Helmor's eyes.)\nO almighty but silent Goddess, your pious...",
    ["Dialogue6023105"]="Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang! Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang!",
    ["Dialogue6023106"]="Ugh...",
    ["Dialogue6023107"]="Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang! Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang! Clang clang! Clang clang clang! Clang clang clang clang! Clang!",
    ["Dialogue6023108"]="(The elderly woman heaves a long sigh and gradually stops praying.)\nAdventurer, that piercing clanging has severely affected my prayer. Can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>convey this concern</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue6023201"]="Huh? My clanging is too loud?",
    ["Dialogue6023202"]="Oh... I sincerely apologize. But please pass on some advice to the old lady: if she wants her husband to stay healthy, she should go to the cathedral and look for an acolyte there. Prayers are useless by themselves.",
    ["Dialogue6023203"]="The Goddess who used to protect Glast Heim has since left us. The people she left behind have no choice but to fend for themselves.\n(As Brock raises his hammer, you notice his extremely muscular physique.)",
    ["Dialogue6023204"]="What happened?",
    ["Dialogue6023205"]="You aren't from around here, I assume. These are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruins of Glast Heim</color>. The old people say this used to be a prosperous place! As for why it's fallen into this state...\n(Brock Sledgehammer points his hammer at the distance, towards the praying Helmor, seemingly indicating that you should ask her instead.)",
    ["Dialogue6023301"]="Thank you ever so much. You are truly kind. As I'm not long for this world, my only wish is for the Goddess to watch over us and make my husband well again.",
    ["Dialogue6023302"]="Ma'am, can you tell us why the Goddess left?",
    ["Dialogue6023303"]="(Upon hearing the word \"left\", Helmor suddenly waves her hands agitatedly, as if she wants to chase you away.)\nNonsense! The Goddess hasn't left us; she's merely temporarily asleep. Why would you vilify the Goddess so?",
    ["Dialogue6023304"]="You're not here for blasphemous reasons?\n(Helmor eyes your clothing with suspicion.)\nHah, if you're so musically inclined, can you hear the wails of the undead reverberating all around us?",
    ["Dialogue6023305"]="I...\n(The TOYS gently hums a melody, one that sounds like a lullaby to you.)",
    ["Dialogue6023306"]="(The soothing music causes the old woman to gradually lower her guard.)\nFine! What's the point of making things difficult for you? It won't help Joelso.",
    ["Dialogue6023307"]="No! To leave Glast Heim is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>betray</color> the Goddess. We'll be punished! Besides, where would I go? At this point, my only hope is for the Goddess to hear my prayers and bless us with her divine grace in the near future, so that Joelso can be cured.",
    ["Dialogue6023308"]="You don't know this, but I've been proficient at prayer since a young age. I was the city's most devout follower, so much so that even the old abbot praised how quickly and accurately I could recite my prayers. He said that I was bound to receive the Goddess' blessing. But even after begging her for over half a year, Joelso remains bedridden. Tell me, do you think that the Goddess will actually respond to her followers' prayers?",
    ["Dialogue6023309"]="(Helmor's cloudy eyes bulge furiously for an instant before shriveling up again. The light in her eyes has also gone out.)\nFine... I can't provide the inspiration you seek, and neither can this city. But when we were younger, Joelso and I wanted to settle down in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color>. I've heard that there are no terrifying monsters there and that it is truly a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pure land</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6023310"]="The Goddess will awaken again. When that happens, the entire city of Glast Heim will once again be full of life and Joelso will get well again!\n(As Helmor clasps your hands, you feel a faint, almost non-existent sensation of warmth in the palms of her hands.)\nThank you!",
    ["Dialogue6023311"]="(Helmor clasps her hands together and once again assumes the prayer posture she has taken thousands of times before.)\nMay the Goddess watch over you.",
    ["Dialogue6023401"]="My inspiration this time around wasn't from that old lady. No... Maybe her experiences evoked some emotions in me, and those emotions ultimately inspired me. Would you listen for a while, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue6023501"]="The next stop on our journey is also the last. Is the city known as Payon truly a pure land? I'd like to see it for myself, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue6023601"]="We're finally heading to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color>, but how will we get there? In any case, we won't be using the waterways...",
    ["Dialogue6023701"]="Live for today; worry not about tomorrow! Hic, what a familiar adventurer! Hmm, the fellow behind you has the potential to become a great martial artist. He would make an excellent disciple!",
    ["Dialogue6023702"]="Sigh, I've been inundated with chores lately; I'm just not in the right frame of mind to bring you sightseeing. Whatever will be, will be; you can't force it! While fate does not smile upon us, perhaps your destiny lies with someone else!",
    ["Dialogue6023703"]="Oh my! Since you're sincerely asking me for your destiny, I shall be compassionate and show you a path. Once you leave here, turn right and you'll find a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new visitor to Payon</color> at the Pine Pavilion. If you cheer that person up, perhaps fate will lead you back to me!",
    ["Dialogue6023704"]="Adventurer, do you still remember what we experienced in Morroc? Let's choose some exotic gifts!",
    ["Dialogue6023705"]="Wonderful! Not only do you have the potential to become a great martial artist, you also possess innate intelligence, a quality that is hard to come by. Would you like to become my final disciple? Hey, don't leave yet; stay for a drink!",
    ["Dialogue6023801"]="Not bad, not bad at all. You have completed my test, and our fated encounter, as expected, did happen on the following day. Fine then, what is it you wish to know?",
    ["Dialogue6023802"]="As you rightly said, Payon does indeed have the title of \"A Pure Land\". It is cut off from the rest of the world and does not get involved in any of the squabbles that occur in the rest of the continent. For thousands of years, Payon has remained an isolated city. However, do you know how it was established?",
    ["Dialogue6023803"]="Young people are so impatient! Firstly, let me be clear that what I say next is sourced from writings carved into the walls of an unnamed cave that I happened to chance upon. Those writings were carved deep into the rock and were absolutely heart-wrenching, but nowhere in the writings could a person's name be found. Regardless of their authenticity, I could not bear to keep this to myself, which is why I am telling you about this now. Consider this a sign of the fated ties linking you to Payon.",
    ["Dialogue6023804"]="(After standing around for a while in deep thought, Peerless Jin slowly begins his account.)\nThe writings carved into the rock state that thousands of years ago, Payon was but an isolated land surrounded by lofty mountains. Due to its inaccessibility, Payon did not suffer monster invasions and became one of the few truly pure lands on the continent.",
    ["Dialogue6023805"]="(As he speaks in an unhurried manner, you can't help but follow his lead, calm yourself down, and immerse yourself in his story.)\nThereafter, a group of our ancestors found this idyllic place after suffering the horrors of war, and decided to settle down here.",
    ["Dialogue6023806"]="(Peerless Jin seems to have entered some sort of unfathomable state and does not reply to your query.)\nYes or no; does the answer truly matter? In any case, the leader of this group of ancestors somehow found the way to enter Payon and led the entire party in making a <color=#CA2E0AFF>vow</color>, that none of them will ever leave this place again. Therefore, plumes of chimney smoke began to rise in this deserted and barren land, and the naive but kind people made this place their home, until...",
    ["Dialogue6023807"]="Until...\n(Peerless Jin suddenly stretches his neck and gradually walks towards Seocho Market.)",
    ["Dialogue6023808"]="Until... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seocho Market's liquor store</color> is open!",
    ["Dialogue6023901"]="(Peerless Jin breaks the seal of a wine jug and fills the many bowls in front of him to the brim.)\nDrink!",
    ["Dialogue6023902"]="Until Payon's population grew rapidly, and its leader had to send young people to gather supplies nearby. A hunter, weary of easy prey, discovered a cave shimmering with strange light. He went inside the cave without informing anyone.",
    ["Dialogue6023903"]="His speed hastened as the light brightened to the point where it hurt his eyes. Suddenly, the hunter realized he had left Payon. This was an <color=#CA2E0AFF>exit</color> unbeknownst even to the leader!",
    ["Dialogue6023904"]="Enthralled by his discovery, the hunter told his trusted partner, who then told the young captain of the hunting party, until all the young people knew the secret and kept it from the elders. They began to contact the outside world, filled with violent monsters and suffering people.",
    ["Dialogue6023905"]="Compared with the outside world, the people of Payon wore clean clothes that had never been stained by blood and had bright eyes that had never been tarnished by tears. The moment they loosed their arrows, few monsters could survive.",
    ["Dialogue6023906"]="The fame of these legendary archers quickly spread across the continent. Girls adored them, bards sang of them, and adventurers revered them. In the secluded Payon, however, such fame and glory were unthinkable.",
    ["Dialogue6023907"]="Finally, their late return drew the leader's suspicion. Enraged by the truth, the leader immediately ordered the expulsion of the young man who led them and ignored all pleas for mercy. Can you tell who that was, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue6023908"]="Exactly. Without showing any remorse, all he asked was to retrieve his belongings from Payon. The leader had him escorted to the cave and <color=#CA2E0AFF>sealed the entrance</color>. Along the way, the young man rebuked the leader for ignoring the plight of the outside world.",
    ["Dialogue6023909"]="He fell silent midway and as he neared the exit, and pleaded with tears not to be expelled, only to be told that their ancestors had sworn an oath and that the tribe would be punished by the gods for any violation, except the first violator. The leader simply wished to get him to safety.",
    ["Dialogue6023910"]="Sensing the leader's determination, the hunter stopped crying and pledged to the leader that he would become the strongest warrior in the world to protect the tribe from punishment and he would never tell anyone about Payon.",
    ["Dialogue6023911"]="Three years, or maybe thirty, had passed. After undergoing many ordeals, the hunter eventually grew stronger. When he was able to smash the sealed cave in the hopes of saving the tribe, all he saw were <color=#CA2E0AFF>skeletons</color> and the most hideous monsters.",
    ["Dialogue6023912"]="Utterly disheartened, he threw aside his bow and charged at the rampaging monsters. Nobody knows what happened in the end.",
    ["Dialogue6023913"]="I just want you to know that there is no such thing as a truly pure land in the world, only a reflection of desires. The elders, longing for peace, saw Payon as a paradise; yet, to the fame-seeking youth, it was merely a place to dwell.",
    ["Dialogue6023914"]="Too much obsession resulted in the devil within. No need to feel sorry, adventurer. Everyone's fate has been predestined. All we have to do is let go of our fixation and accept our fate.",
    ["Dialogue6023915"]="Understood. Adventurer, I'll go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> and start writing! This is both the start and the end of the journey!",
    ["Dialogue6024001"]="Adventurer, thanks for keeping me company. This song was inspired by my time in Payon as well as <color=#CA2E0AFF>our friendship</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6024101"]="What a fantastic performance! I wish time could stop now, adventurer. On this journey, I've accumulated more than just ideas. I'm going to devote all of my energy to creating. Only the best works can memorialize this epic musical journey!",
    ["Dialogue6030101"]="(The unfamiliar young man is looking around warily and mumbling in the corner.)\nEven if the dean's not bald, Hamid's stomach size is still beyond the norm. Getting me to come back to the academy as a professor at this time but not discussing the rank... There must be something behind it I'm not aware of! Travers, you have to think this over carefully...",
    ["Dialogue6030102"]="Think carefully, and... Hm? Judging from your clothing you're a student of Criatura Academy, right?",
    ["Dialogue6030103"]="Waaaah—\n(He covers his buttocks and quickly pulls you into the shadows of the stairwell.)\nAhem! You... Do you know who I am?",
    ["Dialogue6030104"]="(Under your non-anticipating gaze, he introduces himself to you with great delight.)\nStudent, I am going to be the professor of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>new course</color> at Criatura Academy. You shall address me as Professor Travers.",
    ["Dialogue6030105"]="That's right, the academy is exploring the possibilities of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Multi-class Conversion</color>, and I am the widely-acknowledged all-rounder in this. I certainly am the right person for this professor position! Would you like to be my first student?",
    ["Dialogue6030106"]="Good! That's the spirit! Now go to the library Archives drawer and get my file. I need it to report for duty. No peeking!",
    ["Dialogue6030107"]="Because... Ahem. Anyway, I can't meet with them right now! I'll wait for you right here. You have to come back!",
    ["Dialogue6030201"]="Hoho, student records are one of the most valuable assets of Criatura Academy. They can't be accessed easily!",
    ["Dialogue6030202"]="(After listening to your description of what happened, Dean Mainz pulls out a file from the Archive drawer and hands it to you, with an expression stuck between tears and laughter.)\nThis is the file that Travers doesn't want you to see. Hm... I have my suspicions about why the academy wants him to be a professor. Looks like the young man is also aware of what he had done <color=#CA2E0AFF>back then</color>...",
    ["Dialogue6030301"]="Now, do you understand why the academy wants his as a Class Conversion professor? However, he suspects that we're hiding something from him. A person pursuing Class Conversion must be extremely knowledgeable about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>relations between the various Class systems</color>, and this is not something that hard work alone can achieve. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Exceptional talent</color> is also required.",
    ["Dialogue6030302"]="I see this same talent in you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue6030303"]="(Mainz hands the file to you. You notice that the usually amiable dean has a mischievous look on his face.)\nSince he's calling himself Professor Travers, he will be sure to come back and pick up this file to report for duty. Let's hide and give him a scare!",
    ["Dialogue6030401"]="(Cornered by the two of you, Travers gradually runs out of options and a fierce, determined look flashes in his eyes.)\nI was wrong, Dean Mainz!",
    ["Dialogue6030402"]="……",
    ["Dialogue6030403"]="You... You don't really want me to be at Criatura Academy, do you?",
    ["Dialogue6030404"]="Hoho, yes indeed. In fact, other than myself, six other professors objected to letting you return to the academy to teach.",
    ["Dialogue6030405"]="That's...\n(Travers looks askance at you.)\nBut I've already found my first student, Dean Mainz! It's this Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue6030406"]="Right! From what I remember of academy rules, courses offered are based on student demand. So long as the Adventurer wants to learn, there is no refusing it. I caused a lot of controversy in the past because I did not do my duty properly, and I made many mistakes too. Only the professors were unreservedly...",
    ["Dialogue6030407"]="The opinions of the six professors are not exactly prejudiced... There is bound to be situations where factors are not taken into account or even the delaying of the main Class due to the differences between the weapons, fighting styles, and team positioning of the different Classes, and so on. If it were me, I would not be willing to let my students lose their way in trying to <color=#CA2E0AFF>break Class barriers</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6030408"]="But please believe me when I say I really want to stay in the Criatura Academy. So even if I have my suspicions about some plot... I... I still came.",
    ["Dialogue6030409"]="Hoho, perhaps I should let the other professors hear this. We have discussed this, and in the cases of students with the talent, isn't it a waste to only limit their talents to one Class? In the end, we decided to make a change in the original academy rules and allow a small number of outstanding students to <color=#CA2E0AFF>study other courses simultaneously</color> and improve mastery at the same time.",
    ["Dialogue6030410"]="Adventurer, your excellence is irrefutable. However, are you truly willing to embark on this path that is full of the unknown?",
    ["Dialogue6030411"]="(Beside him, Travers lets out a sigh before the sentence is finished.)\nThat's close... Adventurer, you can now officially address me as Professor Travers.",
    ["Dialogue6030412"]="Mm-hm, the six professors actually have one more request.",
    ["Dialogue6030413"]="Huh?",
    ["Dialogue6030414"]="The six Masters believe that, outside of your ability, your on-campus performance leaves much to be desired in the realm of actual teaching. Even with my guarantee, they want you to demonstrate your teaching ability by getting the Adventurer to master at least one Class as soon as possible. Hmm... How about a week for the deadline?",
    ["Dialogue6030415"]="A-A week?\n(Travers looks helplessly at the clock on the wall of the library.)\nDean Mainz, isn't that too soon? What do you think, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue6030416"]="Uh... Okay!\n(He pulls out a thick hard leather book and flips carefully to the title page.)\nThis is the lesson plan I wrote before coming to the academy. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Great Hall of Job Advancement now and start on our lessons!</color>",
    ["Dialogue6030501"]="Adventurer! This will be where our classes are held from now on. I'll be handing out the lesson materials now. No skipping classes!",
    ["Dialogue603441101"]="Sorry, the Lord's Mansion is currently under martial law. Please hand over your weapons before entering.",
    ["Dialogue604001101"]="A night of good sleep is the best, and waking up is the worst.",
    ["Dialogue6040101"]="(Gingerbread Man with a distinctive outlook is waving arms and jumping and hopping at you.)\n Adventurer! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue6040102"]="I'm the most attractive local in the Lutie! The Icing Gingerbread! And I am the holiday ambassador for this Snow Festival here! Everyone around here wishes to share the joy of this festive occasion with the outside world to every Adventurer out there! That's why I'm here!",
    ["Dialogue6040103"]="Hey, hey! Do you want to join the Snow Festival? We have interesting Ice Fishing and Wishing events, and you may also compete in the Fishing Showdown to win even better rewards!",
    ["Dialogue6040104"]="Come on! Lutie is dedicated to offering every Adventurer the most enjoyable holiday experience! So, whether you are new or old around here, no worries at all! Are you ready? Let's go to Lutie with me now!",
    ["Dialogue604031101"]="Can I see Vanessa tomorrow as well?",
    ["Dialogue604041101"]="The person you want to meet is right next to you.",
    ["Dialogue604091101"]="If you are bored, I've got something for you to do.",
    ["Dialogue604101101"]="A photographer is the sculptor of light!",
    ["Dialogue604441101"]="Sacrifice is inevitable, but it can be meaningful.",
    ["Dialogue604451101"]="Offer assistance and goodwill to those who really need it.",
    ["Dialogue604461101"]="Airship maintenance is quite the science...",
    ["Dialogue6060101"]="God's Descendant, though your bloodline hails from Odin, the King of the Gods, you are not allowed to casually eavesdrop on the whispers of a god.",
    ["Dialogue6060102"]="I am known as the ever-burning solar flame and the eternal sun. Mundilfari, the colossal ruler of time and the cycles of day and night, fathers me; Mani, the god presiding over the stars and the moon, is my brother. My radiance graces every inch and bestows life upon all living things.",
    ["Dialogue6060103"]="Is that so? The present generation of God's Descendants truly possesses a remarkable knowledge of the divine lineage. Not only can you carve the countenance of the King of the Gods, but you also remember my appellation.",
    ["Dialogue6060104"]="God's Descendant, even though your eavesdropping was uncovered, you have still meddled with the course of destiny...",
    ["Dialogue6060105"]="You shall know in due time. When the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fire Boulders of Muspelheim descend upon the continent</color> and plunge all beings into madness, God's Descendants shall rise, just as prophesied by the Norns.",
    ["Dialogue6060106"]="Muspelheim, the origin of flames, heat, and radiance. The fusion of its heat and the cold of Niflheim gave rise to the first spark of life. Odin, our King of the Gods, once captured the fire of Muspelheim and fashioned the sun and the moon from two largest fireballs.",
    ["Dialogue6060107"]="The eternal silence bestowed by the frigid mist of Niflheim shrouds all creatures, while the Fire Boulders of Muspelheim propel everything into a state of chaotic frenzy. In this manner, they serve as the fuel that ignites the creation of the sun and the moon.",
    ["Dialogue6060108"]="First, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the scorching weather will transform all familiar landscapes</color>. Second, creatures infused with fiery lifeforce<color=#CA2E0AFF> will succumb to a frenzied state</color>, driven by their instinct to kill. And lastly, the order among humanity will be plunged into chaos...",
    ["Dialogue6060109"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Retrieve the Fire Boulders and deliver them to me</color>; this is your mission. God's descendant, the capital where you currently reside will serve as the launching point for the sun chariot in the mortal realm. Perhaps the initial shard of ember that descended upon this world lies in close proximity.",
    ["Dialogue6060110"]="(The goddess incarnate remains silent, and after a while, you heard a sigh.)\n... I also seek Odin's revelation, but he no longer answers.",
    ["Dialogue6060201"]="That's weird...",
    ["Dialogue6060202"]="Blazing fires. Flying ashes. And everything burns. That's what the place should resemble. \n(The goddess gazes at the ravaged farm.)\nYet, it falls short.",
    ["Dialogue6060203"]="Did you hear what you just said? I don't know where you're from, but how dare you think it's not sufficient?! Adventurer, is she your friend?",
    ["Dialogue6060204"]="Shush.",
    ["Dialogue6060205"]="Adventurer, don't try to stop me, I'm gonna...!",
    ["Dialogue6060206"]="(The goddess shoots a cold glance at Klaus. In an instant, scattered sparks rise from the scorched earth and congregate at her fingertips.)\nBestowing miracles is the sacred duty of gods.",
    ["Dialogue6060207"]="(The land regains its lush greenery; wheat sprouts, grows tall, and then yields golden, full ears. Everything appears usual as if nothing had occurred.)\nIt is the responsibility of God's Descendants to manifest the grace of God.",
    ["Dialogue6060208"]="You... you're a magician? Wow... thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue6060209"]="It seems you have fulfilled your duty, God's Descendant. Before I go, I'll leave behind an illusion to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect the Fire Boulders</color>. Do not forget your <color=#CA2E0AFF>mission</color>.",
    ["Dialogue6060210"]="Even if the King of the Gods doesn't answer anymore, I still want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out why all of this is happening</color>. The Fire Boulders have fallen, and the sun chariot ceases to move. Don't the gods of Asgard understand the consequences of this?",
    ["Dialogue6060301"]="Sol...\n(Under the Heart Pedestal, the illusory figure of the Valkyrie makes a rare gentle expression.)\nThe brilliance of the Sun Goddess is still fascinating to all the gods. If they are still feasting in Valhalla, I will drink the mead heartily with you.",
    ["Dialogue6060302"]="How can the mead of the Aesir compare with the blood mead of Muspelheim, the Flameland? Brunhild, when we find the Fire Boulder, not even the presence of our father or the King of Gods can stop us from drinking from dusk to dawn.",
    ["Dialogue6060303"]="However, since the God of Kings personally conferred upon you the duties of a Valkyrie, why don't you join me in eradicating the monsters sowing chaos in the mortal realm? You must know I've burned enough monsters along the way to fill up your temple!",
    ["Dialogue6060304"]="(The Valkyrie's eyes become dimmer.)\nMy divine power is running out. According to the King of Gods' revelation, I must use it to sense the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and guide the heir of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue6060305"]="After Ragnarok, we will no longer reign over mankind, and all living beings will be in control of their own fates. All we gods can do is watch over the chosen heirs of Odin's bloodline and protect them from a second Ragnarok.",
    ["Dialogue6060306"]="My dear friend, although I don't know why you endured the pain of having your <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine consciousness split</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>reversed time and space</color> to come here, I'm overjoyed to see you again and don't want to hide anything from you.",
    ["Dialogue6060307"]="(Sol stares at Brunhild in disbelief, like a dying flame after burning its brightest.)\nW...What? Are you saying that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ragnarok... is already...</color>",
    ["Dialogue6060308"]="...",
    ["Dialogue6060309"]="No! I don't believe that! Brunhild, Ragnarok will never come as long as Skoll fails to overtake my sun chariot! Have you forgotten? This was prophesized by Nolan—and those seers! Those gods, who control their own destiny, would they sentence themselves to death?",
    ["Dialogue6060310"]="Also, the day and night cycles of my father, Mundilfari, are still alternating. When the night falls, my brother Mani's moon chariot is going to hang high in the sky as the noblest light in the darkness!",
    ["Dialogue6060311"]="Brunhild, I—\n(As Sol reaches out, sunlight penetrates the painted windows of the Temple of Dawn, reflecting on her sacred and determined face.)\nUnless this place is plunged into eternal darkness, I will not believe that Ragnarok has come.",
    ["Dialogue6060312"]="My dear friend...\n￼I have no intention of arguing with you. Let's take a look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>￼Underwater Temple</color>￼. Mani, the God of the Moon, has already been sleeping there for a hundred years...(Brunhild sighs heavily as her figure enters the Heart Pedestal.)￼\n\n",
    ["Dialogue6060401"]="This place... I really can sense the aura of my younger brother...",
    ["Dialogue6060402"]="(Sol stares at the ancient blue magic circle for a long time. Light seems to flow in her eyes.)\nYou are the God of the Moon. This is not what you should be.",
    ["Dialogue6060403"]="(The magic circle seems dormant, completely unresponsive, and the Goddess beside it starts to breathe faster.)\nAs the prince of the Flameland, you should never let yourself fall into such a lightless place.",
    ["Dialogue6060404"]="But we are gods!\n(Fires flash in Sol's eyes.)\nMy younger brother and I are the masters of the moon and the sun. Yet now, with my brother still in deep slumber, the moon continues to hang high in the night sky, and the scorching sun still shines brightly during the daytime. If this is the case, then what is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>meaning of our existence</color>?",
    ["Dialogue6060405"]="Ha... Ha...\n(Desolate laughter echoes in the empty Underwater Temple, as water curtains start to ripple and then fall silent once again.)\nMani...",
    ["Dialogue6060406"]="You had tens of thousands of followers, but in the end, not even a single person offered you any wine in sacrifice.",
    ["Dialogue6060407"]="You?\n(Sol takes a glance at you.)\nWhat are you going to offer? Present offerings to honor him, be buried together with him, or burn yourself as immolation?",
    ["Dialogue6060408"]="... Forget it. I shouldn't take out my rage on you. God's Descendant, if you really mean what you said, then pick a <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Luna\"</color> for me.",
    ["Dialogue6060501"]="(Flames burst out at Sol's fingertip, instantly reducing the Luna Flower into ashes. However, the ashes of the flower, like stardust, glow faintly on the pitch-dark seabed. For a moment, both of you are caught by silence.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue6060502"]="I...\n(Sol's voice becomes softer.)\nI still have <color=#CA2E0AFF>three matters</color> to be resolved.",
    ["Dialogue6060503"]="The first is to reclaim all the Fire Boulders. The second, to find out why Ragnarok befell us. The third...",
    ["Dialogue6060504"]="As Brunhild once said, I split my divine consciousness and reversed time and space to come here. If what you see is just a strand of my divine consciousness, then why did the real I send the consciousness here?",
    ["Dialogue6060505"]="I have a feeling: once these three matters are clarified, your world <color=#CA2E0AFF>will be delivered from crises</color>...",
    ["Dialogue6080101"]="As Sol told me, you have been assisting her in gathering Fire Boulders over recent months. Her appreciation for you resonates deeply with me.",
    ["Dialogue6080102"]="And how do you perceive her?",
    ["Dialogue6080103"]="Well... based solely on this audacity, I can see why Sol recognized you.",
    ["Dialogue6080104"]="Sol, Sun Goddess, is seldom acknowledged. Be it in Asgard or Muspelheim, the Flameland. And even fewer gods ever gain her recognition.",
    ["Dialogue6080105"]="The gods of Asgard distance themselves from Sol, not only because she's the Titan Princess but also due to the contempt they harbor for the Titans, once conquered by Odin, their King. As for the Titans of the Flameland... they begrudge the royal family for their disgraceful defeat, yet their bloodline forces them into submission. Alas. The emotional intricacies of the gods often surpass those of humans.",
    ["Dialogue6080106"]="I am a creation of the King of Gods, not a deity by birth. Odin has gifted all Valkyries with wisdom, compassion, and justice, and among them, I stand as the finest. As such, I can serenely witness the descending of Ragnarok and shepherd the successors of Odin's bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue6080107"]="Indeed. Adventurer, you ought to understand that as a goddess, Sol has already fallen in Ragnarok. What remains of Sol now is merely a fragment of her divine consciousness projected into the future, or perhaps, a lingering fixation...",
    ["Dialogue6080108"]="But when a fixation finds its fulfillment, it also finds the time to fade. It was initially anticipated that a year would suffice to reclaim all the Fire Boulders, with some time to spare before that decisive moment... \n(A flicker of bewilderment crosses Brunhild's face.)\nYet now, \"she\" has become so <color=#CA2E0AFF>feeble</color> that her presence eludes my senses.",
    ["Dialogue6080109"]="...My friend has finally attained tranquility. I ought to bestow heartfelt blessings. Yet, for reasons unknown, I find my heart incapable of conjuring even a sliver of such sentiment.",
    ["Dialogue6080110"]="Departing the Heart Pedestal would deplete my divine power... a power solely devoted to the protection of this continent. \n(Following a brief silence, Brunhilde's form gradually fades, transforming into an impassive stone statue.)\nThis is the decree of the King of Gods, and also... my chosen path.",
    ["Dialogue6080111"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Bid her farewell</color> on my behalf. Sol, should the day arrive when the King of Gods returns, perhaps we'll reunite at the grand feast in Valhalla.",
    ["Dialogue6080201"]="Is that you? \n(Amidst the raging fire, you find Sol lying in the flames, her countenance a torturous mix of pain and a strange fanatic fervor.)\nQuick, alert Brunhild, I'm <color=#CA2E0AFF>losing control</color>!",
    ["Dialogue6080202"]="These Fire Boulders are rousing my memories... I remember! I recall everything! \n(Sol taps her forehead, emitting an \"hehe\" sound.)\nSol, what's the purpose of dispatching the Fire Boulders to the future? What's the aim of binding yourself to them?",
    ["Dialogue6080203"]="Escape is futile! Ragnarok is destined to descend! Jormungandr, Hati, Skoll, they shall feast upon the gods, desecrate the royal court, and nothing could elude their havoc!",
    ["Dialogue6080204"]="I, I am... \n(\"Sol\" abruptly shifts her tone.)\nGod's Descendant, <color=#CA2E0AFF>make haste and depart</color>...",
    ["Dialogue6080301"]="(A pristine white feather softly alights on your shoulder, and a voice—seemingly impossible—whispers.)\nThat's enough.",
    ["Dialogue6080302"]="(Sol, amidst the flames, shudders unnaturally, and following a moment, a weak voice emerges.) \nYou're aware of everything? Don't fault me... I merely wish to prevent the prophecy from coming true...",
    ["Dialogue6080303"]="(The raging inferno blazes on, and amid the flame-sea, two figures, one red and one white, lock gaze with each other across the distance.) \nEvery god yearns to avert the fulfillment of Ragnarok.",
    ["Dialogue6080304"]="The pledge Frigga forced all beings to made, the God of War's forsaken right arm, and Sun Goddess Sol... All these deities aimed to deter the world from succumbing to an eternal night due to Skoll's raid. For this, Sol hid the Fire Boulders in the future.",
    ["Dialogue6080305"]="The Sun Goddess understood if the Fire Boulders lost control, their enormous, chaotic energy could plunge all creatures into an unbridled frenzy. Thus, she detached a fragment of her divine consciousness, instilled with an obsession to \"reclaim all fire boulders,\" and dispatched it alongside the fire boulders into the future timeline.",
    ["Dialogue6080306"]="To expedite the retrieval process, she even tethered her divine sense to the largest Fire Boulder, luring creatures impacted to approach out of their own accord. \n(Brunhild turns to Sol, her voice becoming icy and penetrating.)\nHence incurred your current <color=#CA2E0AFF>corroded</color> state.",
    ["Dialogue6080307"]="...You're indeed Odin's most reliable instrument, irritatingly astute as he is. \n(\"Sol's\" attractive visage gradually morphs into a ferocious one.)\nBut all your efforts are fruitless! Ragnarok is destined to descend! This world needs neither the dead nor the living. Only chaos reigns!",
    ["Dialogue6080308"]="No! It isn't so... Brunhild... ahem... I've found a way... you will understand... Hurry, I can't hold on any longer!",
    ["Dialogue6080309"]="Indeed...",
    ["Dialogue6080310"]="(Under your disbelieving stare, Brunhild raises the holy spear and swiftly <color=#CA2E0AFF>impales</color> Sol's body. Blood erupts from her while the surrounding flames gradually subside.)\n…",
    ["Dialogue6080311"]="Cough, cough... Well executed, my confidant. Back on the battlefield, you ended the lives of my kin without flinching yet mournfully laid them to rest. Even as all gods show their vile sides at Ragnarok, not a hint of cowardice marks your face.",
    ["Dialogue6080312"]="(As though summoning all her strength to relay a crucial message, Sol utters your name.)\nGod's Descendant, cough cough... Once I'm gone, the frenzied beasts will cease to seek me. They'll be scorched by the Fire Boulders until their very last vestiges of life are consumed... until this twisted bond of symbiosis is broken. Confronting these dying and deeply frenzied creatures, you must not let down your guard...",
    ["Dialogue6080313"]="At the expense of my own existence, I've retrieved the largest Fire Boulder, and I am truly content... My dear friend, cough cough... \n(Sol gazes at Brunhild with a sorrowful look.)\nIn truth, upon regaining my memory, I knew that this day was inevitable...",
    ["Dialogue6080314"]="Much like the Ragnarok that sealed our fates, gods are also captives of destiny... <color=#CA2E0AFF>But after today, who else would understand you as I could...</color>\n(Sol's hand slackens and falls, her body vanishing like smoke, leaving behind solely a fragment of red firestone.)",
    ["Dialogue6080315"]="(Brunhild doesn't even glance at the firestone; she simply folds her wings and speaks slowly in an empty direction.)\nThe moment I awoke from the Heart Pedestal, I held no expectation of being understood by anyone, nor did I ponder about friendship.",
    ["Dialogue6080316"]="Rest in peace, my friend. Before the frenzy completely dissipates, I'll descend upon the capital in your guise and carry on your incomplete mission. When the strength of God's Descendant suffices to safeguard this continent, I, too, shall enter my sleep. Perhaps we don't need to wait for the King of Gods' awakening, we... are destined to reunite eventually.",
    ["Dialogue6090101"]="(The goddess closes her eyes in solemn silence, her gentle hum echoing through the air, unaware of your arrival.)\nFrom the heavens descends a sacred mountain—and with it, the savior from another world walks among us...",
    ["Dialogue6090102"]="You have come, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue6090103"]="The space-time turbulence roars, binding worlds that were never meant to meet, bringing forth a hero from beyond the veil...",
    ["Dialogue6090104"]="Yes, one such visitor has arrived in Prontera—a young man known as the \"Savior,\" Wataru Ikusabe.",
    ["Dialogue6090105"]="At the same time, a mysterious mountain appears outside Prontera, its body split into seven layers and ringed by a rainbow. The world whispers its name—Mt. Soukai.",
    ["Dialogue6090106"]="Go now, Adventurer. Witness the journey of this young man on my behalf.",
    ["Dialogue6090201"]="You are... Right! Hello, I'm Wataru Ikusabe, everyone just calls me Wataru!",
    ["Dialogue6090202"]="Oh! I see! You're the Adventurer from Prontera! What a coincidence! The \"Savior\" you're looking for is me!",
    ["Dialogue6090203"]="(Wataru shakes his head, puzzled.)\nI'm not really sure... My friends and I split ways to take care of various things, but suddenly, I found myself here in Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue6090204"]="But the darkness that ruled Mt. Soukai has followed it into this world. They steal people's kindness—and those stripped of kindness fall into despair, becoming vessels of evil.",
    ["Dialogue6090205"]="Please, help me gather clues about kindness. Together, we'll drive the darkness off this land!",
    ["Dialogue610011101"]="Let my voice heal your wounds!",
    ["Dialogue610011201"]="Are you here to listen to my singing too?",
    ["Dialogue610011301"]="Thank you for the gift! May you be blessed with wonderful music!",
    ["Dialogue610011401"]="Thank you for your kindness!",
    ["Dialogue610011501"]="Oh? Um, this isn't what I need.",
    ["Dialogue610012101"]="If you get hurt at the carnival, let me use my song to heal your wounds.",
    ["Dialogue610021101"]="Welcome, adventurer! We'll always provide you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue610021301"]="Huh?! Are you really giving this to me? Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610021401"]="I really like it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610021501"]="Thank you, but W has no use for it right now.",
    ["Dialogue610022101"]="Welcome, Adventurer! During the holiday season, Kafra Company is still dedicated to providing you a quality service!",
    ["Dialogue610031101"]="If you need to cross the sea, you come to me!",
    ["Dialogue610031201"]="Navigating the open sea is not as easy as you think!",
    ["Dialogue610041101"]="Hi! I'm Smile Assistance. How can I help you?",
    ["Dialogue610041301"]="I love it! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610041401"]="Thank you very much.",
    ["Dialogue610041501"]="Is something the matter?\n(Smile Assistance blinks, having never received a gift before.)",
    ["Dialogue610051101"]="You wanna inlay cards? Put some sockets in your equipment? Leave it to me!",
    ["Dialogue610051201"]="Is the hammer heavy, you ask? Ha, ha, ha! What an interesting question!",
    ["Dialogue610051301"]="Thank you, youngster. This looks great!",
    ["Dialogue610051401"]="Not bad at all. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610051501"]="It's all young people's stuff. Keep it for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue610052101"]="I'm a true professional, all year round, and Halloween is no exception. Come on over!",
    ["Dialogue610061101"]="Keh! What are you lookin' at? Never seen such a handsome messenger, have you!? Keh!",
    ["Dialogue610062101"]="Little old Halloween won't affect the efficiency of the Parrot Family!",
    ["Dialogue610071101"]="Nothing can escape my keen eyes!",
    ["Dialogue610081101"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["Dialogue610081301"]="Puff! Puff!\n(The flames look like they're dancing with joy.)",
    ["Dialogue610081401"]="Puff, puff...\n(The flames crackle.)",
    ["Dialogue610081501"]="Huff— Wheeze—\n(The flames slowly pulsate.)",
    ["Dialogue610082101"]="Puff... Puff...!",
    ["Dialogue610083101"]="Puff... Puff... (Hello friend, what quality equipment do you want to strengthen?)",
    ["Dialogue610083102"]="Puff... Puff... (Weapon, or armor?)",
    ["Dialogue610083103"]="Puff... Puff... (Let me guess... What kind of weapon do you usually use...)",
    ["Dialogue610083104"]="Puff... Puff... . (Armor, Muffler, Shoes... They're all essential)",
    ["Dialogue610091101"]="Ha ha! Swing a sledgehammer a hundred times a day, and you'll have perfect biceps just like me!",
    ["Dialogue610091301"]="What? For me? It's exactly what I needed!\n(Hollgrehenn looks very emotional.)",
    ["Dialogue610091401"]="Oh, thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610091501"]="If there's nothing else, I have to get working.",
    ["Dialogue610092101"]="If you swing your sledgehammer 100 times a day, you'll end up with a firmer figure than even old Jakk!",
    ["Dialogue610101101"]="You can find anything you need here at the Exchange Center.",
    ["Dialogue610101301"]="Thank you so very much!",
    ["Dialogue610101401"]="Alright, thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610101501"]="Sorry, I can't take it.",
    ["Dialogue610102101"]="Trading at the Purchase Shop will proceed as normal, even during Halloween. Come and buy whatever you want!",
    ["Dialogue610111101"]="The Chamber of Commerce is at your service.",
    ["Dialogue610111301"]="Thank you so much for this. I'll make good use of it.",
    ["Dialogue610111401"]="Thank you very much.",
    ["Dialogue610111501"]="This... I don't think I'll be needing it.",
    ["Dialogue610112101"]="Hi, Adventurer! Even during Halloween, the Chamber of Commerce will still provide you with the very best service!",
    ["Dialogue610121101"]="We recently got some new stock. Anything catch your eye?",
    ["Dialogue610131101"]="Ugh, that guy's hairstyle was soooo ugly... Eh? I wasn't talking about you!",
    ["Dialogue610131301"]="Oh? You seem to know what's trendy. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610131401"]="Being fashionable takes practice, but your taste is passable. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610131501"]="Huh? Do you think this is worthy of my beauty?",
    ["Dialogue610132101"]="What color eyes should you choose for Halloween? It always pays to take advice from a fashion expert!",
    ["Dialogue610141101"]="(Mission Boards can't talk. That's impossible.)",
    ["Dialogue610151101"]="Midgard is home to so many fascinating stories! I can tell you all about them if you're interested.",
    ["Dialogue610161101"]="... Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue610171101"]="If you need to cross the skies, just let me know!",
    ["Dialogue610181101"]="(A device used for KVM event registration.)",
    ["Dialogue610191101"]="Hello, adventurer. I am the Guild Housekeeper. I can help you with all manner of guild affairs.",
    ["Dialogue610201101"]="(Rocks can't talk. That's impossible.)",
    ["Dialogue610211101"]="(Monkeys can't talk. That's impossible.)",
    ["Dialogue610221101"]="Do you want to create a guild and become the most famous guild leader in the land? I can help make your wish come true!",
    ["Dialogue610231101"]="(Vending Machines can't talk. That's impossible.)",
    ["Dialogue610241101"]="If you'd like to take part in the OX Quiz, let me know and I'll sign you up.",
    ["Dialogue610241301"]="This really suits my style. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610241401"]="Well, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610241501"]="Superficial objects don't interest me.",
    ["Dialogue610301101"]="Welcome, adventurer! Kafra Corporation always provide you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue610311101"]="Come to me if you need any enchantments, meow!",
    ["Dialogue610311301"]="Y-you're really giving this to me? Thank you, meow!",
    ["Dialogue610311401"]="Thanks, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610311501"]="This... this doesn't seem like something I can use, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610321101"]="Welcome, adventurer! Kafra Corporation is your ever-reliable adventuring companion.",
    ["Dialogue610331101"]="There are so many Guild Orders every day...",
    ["Dialogue610341101"]="Hi, adventurer! Kafra Corporation is here to provide you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue610351101"]="Come to us at Kafra Corporation if there's anything you need!",
    ["Dialogue610361101"]="Welcome, adventurer! Kafra Corporation is your ever-reliable adventuring companion.",
    ["Dialogue610371101"]="I built this Amusement Park myself so that I may bring happiness to everyone!",
    ["Dialogue610371301"]="Oh, that looks very interesting. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610371401"]="Let me see. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610371501"]="This old man has no need for these things.",
    ["Dialogue610391101"]="The Guild Store is here to serve your every need.",
    ["Dialogue610391301"]="You're very generous. I'll gladly take it.",
    ["Dialogue610391401"]="Thank you for the gift.",
    ["Dialogue610391501"]="Oh? It doesn't seem worth much.",
    ["Dialogue610401101"]="Give it a twist and a turn! You never know what surprises are in store at the Vending Machine!",
    ["Dialogue610431101"]="Get your supplies here and battle to your heart's content.",
    ["Dialogue610441301"]="Thank you for thinking of Cynthia. I'm really touched.",
    ["Dialogue610441401"]="Thank you for the gift.",
    ["Dialogue610441501"]="Uh... This might not suit Cynthia.",
    ["Dialogue610461101"]="Welcome, adventurer! We'll always provide you with the very best!",
    ["Dialogue610471101"]="What would you like to add to your pet? We have everything you need here!",
    ["Dialogue610471301"]="Oh? This looks very interesting. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610471401"]="I'll gladly take it. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610471501"]="What is this? I don't want it!",
    ["Dialogue610481101"]="Welcome! We sell weapons catered to new students of Criatura Academy. Have a look!",
    ["Dialogue610491101"]="Welcome! We sell armor catered to new students of Criatura Academy. Have a look!",
    ["Dialogue610501101"]="Welcome! We sell accessories catered to new students of Criatura Academy. Have a look!",
    ["Dialogue610511101"]="Our weapons are just what a passionate new adventurer needs to make their mark in the world. We get good reviews all year round. You won't be disappointed!",
    ["Dialogue610511301"]="Ah! The wonderful temperament of life seems to be flowing within it! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610511401"]="Haha! Well then, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610511501"]="Hmm... I can't feel the temperament of life.",
    ["Dialogue610521101"]="Our armor is just what a passionate new adventurer needs to make their mark in the world. We get good reviews all year round. You won't be disappointed!",
    ["Dialogue610521301"]="This looks like a surprise for me! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610521401"]="Well then, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610521501"]="Huh? I don't think I have a use for this.",
    ["Dialogue610531101"]="Our accessories are just what a passionate new adventurer needs to make their mark in the world. We get good reviews all year round. You won't be disappointed!",
    ["Dialogue610531301"]="This will surely bring me new inspiration! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610531401"]="You're thoughtful too. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610531501"]="It didn't spark any inspiration for me.",
    ["Dialogue610541101"]="Do you want a carefree adventure in the desert? It's a guaranteed experience if you take our weapons with you!",
    ["Dialogue610541301"]="Thanks, I'll make good use of it.",
    ["Dialogue610541401"]="Oh? For me? Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610541501"]="If there's nothing else, then please stop blocking my view!",
    ["Dialogue610551101"]="Do you want a carefree adventure in the desert? It's a guaranteed experience if you take our armor with you!",
    ["Dialogue610551301"]="This looks pretty useful. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610551401"]="Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610551501"]="I have no use for this, I think you should take it back.",
    ["Dialogue610561101"]="Do you want a carefree adventure in the desert? It's a guaranteed experience if you take our accessories with you!",
    ["Dialogue610561301"]="You must have gone through a lot of trouble to get a gift like this. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610561401"]="I'll gladly take it. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610561501"]="Hmm... I think you should give it to someone more suitable so that it doesn't go to waste.",
    ["Dialogue610571101"]="With our weapons, your safety is guaranteed against monsters prowling the forests and when traversing perilous caves!",
    ["Dialogue610571301"]="Oh, thanks a lot.",
    ["Dialogue610571401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue610571501"]="(Leming continues to smelt iron without looking up.)",
    ["Dialogue610581101"]="With our armor, your safety is guaranteed against monsters prowling the forests and when traversing perilous caves!",
    ["Dialogue610581301"]="Thank you so much.",
    ["Dialogue610581401"]="You're giving it to me? Well, thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610581501"]="Um... Does this have a quality guarantee?",
    ["Dialogue610591101"]="With our accessories, your safety is guaranteed against monsters prowling the forests and when traversing perilous caves!",
    ["Dialogue610591301"]="This customer's got good taste. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610591401"]="Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610591501"]="Eh... Maybe it's better to give it to someone else.",
    ["Dialogue610601101"]="The pinnacle fusion of forging techniques and magic! Weapons made in Geffen have the best quality you'll find in the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue610601301"]="Oh, your taste isn't too bad. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610601401"]="I guess this gift will do, thanks.",
    ["Dialogue610601501"]="I will not accept such a gift.",
    ["Dialogue610611101"]="The pinnacle fusion of forging techniques and magic! Armor made in Geffen has the best quality you'll find in the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue610611301"]="It looks great! I'll gladly take it.",
    ["Dialogue610611401"]="Looks like it costs a lot. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610611501"]="Don't give me something I don't need.",
    ["Dialogue610621101"]="The pinnacle fusion of forging techniques and magic! Accessories made in Geffen have the best quality you'll find in the kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue610621301"]="Oh, thank you. I really like it.",
    ["Dialogue610621401"]="Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610621501"]="Oh... That doesn't seem to suit me.",
    ["Dialogue610631101"]="The omniscient and almighty Odin shall draw out the hidden potential in your equipment and steer you onto the right path on your adventure.",
    ["Dialogue610631301"]="That's exactly what I wanted! Thanks a lot!",
    ["Dialogue610631401"]="Oh, I'll take it. Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue610631501"]="This is....",
    ["Dialogue610641101"]="The omniscient and almighty Odin shall draw out the hidden potential in your equipment and steer you onto the right path on your adventure.",
    ["Dialogue610641301"]="Woaah! This is such a creative gift! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610641401"]="Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610641501"]="Ahem, I think we'd better change the subject. (Hobson smiles at you.)",
    ["Dialogue610651101"]="Welcome to the Mysterious Endless Shop, adventurer. You can buy Blessings here with the Tower Stones you get from climbing the tower.\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>(Blessings only work while inside the Endless Tower. It resets every week with Tower Climb.)</color>",
    ["Dialogue610661101"]="The Pharaoh's power shall grant your weapon mysterious strength. Praise the great Pharaoh Osiris!",
    ["Dialogue610671101"]="The Pharaoh's power shall grant your armor mysterious strength. Praise the great Pharaoh Osiris!",
    ["Dialogue610671301"]="This really suits my taste!",
    ["Dialogue610671401"]="I'll gladly take it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610671501"]="Hmm, it's not very pretty. You should keep it.",
    ["Dialogue610681101"]="The Pharaoh's power shall grant your accessories mysterious strength. Praise the great Pharaoh Osiris!",
    ["Dialogue610681301"]="Oh my, this really suits this lady's elegance!",
    ["Dialogue610681401"]="Thank you, meow!",
    ["Dialogue610681501"]="This lady has much better taste than that, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610691101"]="Let the Rainbow City of Payon's power infuse your weapon with renewed color!",
    ["Dialogue610691301"]="I'll take good care of it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610691401"]="Thanks a lot.",
    ["Dialogue610691501"]="Although I appreciate it, I don't think I'll be needing it.",
    ["Dialogue610701101"]="Let the Rainbow City of Payon's power infuse your armor with renewed color!",
    ["Dialogue610701301"]="Wow, I think I can smell my favorite scent!",
    ["Dialogue610701401"]="Not bad. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610701501"]="How about just helping me figure out how to get into Munak Cave?",
    ["Dialogue610711101"]="Let the Rainbow City of Payon's power infuse your accessories with renewed color!",
    ["Dialogue610711301"]="As expected, natural is best, meow! Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610711401"]="Thank you, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610711501"]="Oh... Thanks, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610721101"]="The source of our enchantments is the purest magic of the Heines Family. We can grant your weapon greater strength without praying to any god.",
    ["Dialogue610721301"]="Oh! Now this is a gem. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610721401"]="I'll make good use of it. Thank you．",
    ["Dialogue610721501"]="Hmm... This should be given to someone more suitable.",
    ["Dialogue610731101"]="The source of our enchantments is the purest magic of the Heines Family. We can grant your armor greater strength without praying to any god.",
    ["Dialogue610731301"]="I can't thank you enough! You shall be blessed with magic's divine protection!",
    ["Dialogue610731401"]="Thank you very much.",
    ["Dialogue610731501"]="You should give it to someone who needs it more.",
    ["Dialogue610741101"]="The source of our enchantments is the purest magic of the Heines Family. We can grant your accessories greater strength without praying to any god.",
    ["Dialogue610741301"]="Not bad! It's worthy of my noble status. Thank you, meow.",
    ["Dialogue610741401"]="I gladly accept your generosity, meow. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610741501"]="One must always be graceful. Thank you, meow!",
    ["Dialogue610751101"]="What would you like to add to your pet? We have everything you need here!",
    ["Dialogue610751301"]="This?! I can really take it? Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610751401"]="Well, thanks.",
    ["Dialogue610751501"]="Thank you for your kindness, but you should keep it.",
    ["Dialogue610761101"]="The Otherworld Gate is open... Are you ready to accept your trial, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue610771101"]="Looking for a fair fight? Or eager to showcase your skills? Welcome to my arena, where every clash upholds absolute fairness. Rise to claim the winner's crown!",
    ["Dialogue610771102"]="Excellent! You have the courage to compete, and have proved that you are an excellent monster hunter. Please wait for the notification of the competition's commencement.",
    ["Dialogue610771103"]="You don't have an invitation? Well... I have a few unsent invitation letters here, just in case anyone else is interested in taking part in the competition. Do you understand?",
    ["Dialogue610771104"]="Hahaha! Alright, since you seem to be doing so well, I'll accept for now. But I have a limited number of tickets on hand. Of course I'll have to give them to whoever offers the highest price. If someone offers more than you, don't blame me.",
    ["Dialogue610771105"]="You've signed up for the Ultimate Hunter Showdown. Don't forget to enter the arena before the competition begins.",
    ["Dialogue610771106"]="Don't worry, it's all sorted. I've already signed you up. The competition is about to begin. Get in there!",
    ["Dialogue610771107"]="Well... I'd like to help you, but someone has already offered me a higher price, so... I'm sorry. But I can only give you half of the money back. The other half is for all my hard work. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue610771108"]="Don't worry, I won't forget. It's still being processed, so I can't do much. You can come back and confirm it once the registration deadline is over.",
    ["Dialogue610781101"]="The only thing worth praying for here is that your opponent isn't too strong!",
    ["Dialogue610801101"]="Within every weapon lies unlimited potential! Prontera's upgrade techniques will greatly enhance your weapon's performance!",
    ["Dialogue610801301"]="Yeah, it looks great. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610801401"]="Thanks! I'll make good use of it.",
    ["Dialogue610801501"]="Don't waste a good thing.",
    ["Dialogue610811101"]="Within every piece of armor lies unlimited potential! Prontera's upgrade techniques will greatly enhance your armor's performance!",
    ["Dialogue610811301"]="This must be from my family. Don't worry, I won't tell anyone. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610811401"]="Is this for me? I'll keep it safe. Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue610811501"]="People like me don't accept any average gift.",
    ["Dialogue610821101"]="Within every accessory lies unlimited potential! Prontera's upgrade techniques will greatly enhance your accessory's performance!",
    ["Dialogue610821301"]="Wow, thank you so much for such a fantastic gift!",
    ["Dialogue610821401"]="Huh? This is for me? Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610821501"]="It doesn't really suit me.",
    ["Dialogue610831101"]="In our hands, your weapon will be able to unleash even greater potential. Adventurers from Criatura Academy get an additional discount!",
    ["Dialogue610831301"]="I can't thank you enough for such a precious gift!",
    ["Dialogue610831401"]="Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue610831501"]="This doesn't seem to fit me, but thanks anyway.",
    ["Dialogue610841101"]="In our hands, your armor will be able to unleash even greater potential. Adventurers from Criatura Academy get an additional discount!",
    ["Dialogue610841301"]="Now this is worth this young master's beauty.",
    ["Dialogue610841401"]="Mmm, it's acceptable, I guess.",
    ["Dialogue610841501"]="This doesn't match me at all. Please keep it.",
    ["Dialogue610851101"]="In our hands, your accessories will be able to unleash even greater potential. Adventurers from Criatura Academy get an additional discount!",
    ["Dialogue610851301"]="Wow, how did you know I liked this? Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610851401"]="Huh? This is for me? Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610851501"]="Oh, no. I can't take it. I don't have enough room for anymore useless stuff.",
    ["Dialogue610861101"]="A light tap here and a hard hammer there. The most practical weapon often comes from the most simple craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue610861301"]="Eh? This looks like good material. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610861401"]="I could use this. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610861501"]="What can I do with this?",
    ["Dialogue610871101"]="A light tap here and a hard hammer there. The most practical armor often comes from the most simple craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue610871301"]="Wow. It looks great. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610871401"]="Thanks so much!",
    ["Dialogue610871501"]="Um... I don't have a use for this.",
    ["Dialogue610881101"]="A light tap here and a hard hammer there. The most practical accessory often comes from the most simple craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue610881301"]="You've got good taste. Thanks a lot.",
    ["Dialogue610881401"]="Thanks! I'll make good use of it.",
    ["Dialogue610881501"]="No thanks. I have no use for it.",
    ["Dialogue610901101"]="Come take a look! I've got things you newbies are sure to love!",
    ["Dialogue610901301"]="It looks quite expensive. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610901401"]="Hmm... Let me check its market value. It should be good. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610901501"]="Hmm, it doesn't have market value potential. You should keep it.",
    ["Dialogue610902101"]="Don't you want to check out our new Halloween goods?",
    ["Dialogue610911101"]="You best stop by and ready your supplies with us if you're venturing into the desert.",
    ["Dialogue610921101"]="Welcome! We have specialty Payon items for sale here. Guaranteed different from what you find in the midland!",
    ["Dialogue610931101"]="Even common goods are made special once pure Geffen magic is added to them!",
    ["Dialogue610941101"]="These are all goods that just arrived from across the ocean. Wanna take a look?",
    ["Dialogue610951101"]="Heh, heh. Delicious snacks, school lunches... We have everything you could ever want, and it all tastes amazing!",
    ["Dialogue610951301"]="Wow! Thank you very much. We'll give you a discount next time you come eat!",
    ["Dialogue610951401"]="Not bad! Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue610951501"]="Oh, I don't need this. Big Sis doesn't keep useless things.",
    ["Dialogue610961101"]="Yes, I used to be the palace's head chef... Now, taste the pure royal flavors of my cuisine!",
    ["Dialogue610961301"]="I see you appreciate the finest ingredients too! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610961401"]="Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610961501"]="I don't think I can make anything good out of that.",
    ["Dialogue610962101"]="Royal cuisine should always be done justice. It's the same during Halloween.",
    ["Dialogue610971101"]="Our cooking is like this vast desert. It may look rough around the edges, but there's a refined delicacy underneath. A unique experience, to be sure!",
    ["Dialogue610971301"]="It looks like we'll have another new recipe. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610971401"]="You didn't have to do that. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610971501"]="I have no use for it. How about you keep it for yourself?",
    ["Dialogue610981101"]="Delicious and healthy—that's the principle behind Payon's cuisine.",
    ["Dialogue610981301"]="This seems worthy of a closer look. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue610981401"]="I'll make good use of it. Thank you．",
    ["Dialogue610981501"]="This doesn't have enough research value. You can have it back.",
    ["Dialogue610991101"]="Hehe, do you believe that we have added a mysterious delicious magic to our cooking?",
    ["Dialogue610991301"]="You really get me! Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue610991401"]="Thank you, but I don't accept advances.",
    ["Dialogue610991501"]="Uh... No thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611001101"]="Our cuisine is rich with the smell of the sea breeze!",
    ["Dialogue611001301"]="You've got good taste. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611001401"]="Oh? Looks good. Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611001501"]="Huh? I'm not interested.",
    ["Dialogue611011101"]="Do you want to be the king of all fishermen? Then you definitely need our fishing gear!",
    ["Dialogue611011301"]="Thank you. May Strouf bless you.",
    ["Dialogue611011401"]="Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611011501"]="I don't think I have a use for it.",
    ["Dialogue611021101"]="Clang, clang! The sound of mining tools crashing into ore makes such splendid music!",
    ["Dialogue611031101"]="You get what you pay for in Alberta. There's always a good reason an item has a high price tag!",
    ["Dialogue611031301"]="From my first glance, I knew this adventurer had a shrewd business acumen. We can definitely benefit from our friendship.",
    ["Dialogue611031401"]="Mm, it's worth watching its market value. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611031501"]="I don't invest in people or things that don't have long-term value.",
    ["Dialogue611041101"]="If you have any of those mysteriously elusive Crystals, just head on over to me!",
    ["Dialogue611041301"]="So you do you get me! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611041401"]="It's not as good as my Crystals, but it's worth collecting. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611041501"]="Even if you don't have Crystals, you can't just give me whatever.",
    ["Dialogue611051101"]="Welcome! Our headgear is sure to bring you happiness!",
    ["Dialogue611061101"]="Glasses require the most meticulous craftsmanship.",
    ["Dialogue611061301"]="From what I understand, this takes quite a bit of effort to obtain. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611061401"]="Oh? Looks nice. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611061501"]="From the overall look, function and smell of it, I don't think it's for me.",
    ["Dialogue611071101"]="If you want to hide your face, just buy a mask! But don't use it to commit crime!",
    ["Dialogue611071301"]="Ooh. It's giving me inspiration for my next season's mask.",
    ["Dialogue611071401"]="Thank you. This looks interesting.",
    ["Dialogue611071501"]="(Villard puts on his mask and shakes his head.)",
    ["Dialogue611081101"]="We've got headgear for academy students! Of course, even those who aren't students of Criatura Academy are welcome to try them on!",
    ["Dialogue611081301"]="It's SOOO cuuute! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611081401"]="Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611081501"]="Uh... I don't think this gift is for me.",
    ["Dialogue611091101"]="Once you put on our headgear, you'll feel like a magical beautification spell has been cast on you, and that's no lie!",
    ["Dialogue611091301"]="Not bad. I approve of your taste.",
    ["Dialogue611091401"]="Your taste could be better, but I accept your generosity.",
    ["Dialogue611091501"]="Don't take out such a tasteless thing!",
    ["Dialogue611101101"]="Even beautiful Obeaune princesses are dying to get their hands on our headgear!",
    ["Dialogue611101301"]="Haha. Doesn't this look like good material for a fish-head hat?",
    ["Dialogue611101401"]="Oh? Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611101501"]="I'm not interested in anything that doesn't have character.",
    ["Dialogue611111101"]="Look no further than us for some fun and delightful lower headgear!",
    ["Dialogue611121101"]="Come relive that timeless joy of childhood!",
    ["Dialogue611131101"]="Do you want to become as majestic as a valkyrie? Your wish can come true with enough Valkyrie Coins!",
    ["Dialogue611131301"]="This looks really cool. It's really for me? Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue611131401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue611131501"]="This is too childish. Don't you look down on me just because I'm a girl.",
    ["Dialogue611141101"]="Step right up! Don't walk away or you'll regret it! With the Paup Shop, you never have to worry about not spending your MVP Coins again!",
    ["Dialogue611151101"]="Step right up! Don't walk away or you'll regret it! With the Florence Shop, you never have to worry about not spending your Mini Coins again!",
    ["Dialogue611161101"]="Hi! If you know any heroes who have been to the Endless Tower before, remember to tell them to spend their Gold Coins here and get some one-of-a-kind equipment!",
    ["Dialogue611161301"]="I'll take it. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611161401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue611161501"]="No thanks. Keep it.",
    ["Dialogue611181101"]="Danger lurks in every corner of the desert. Why not stop by and raise your weapon attributes before you start your journey?",
    ["Dialogue611181301"]="Hmm... Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611181401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue611181501"]="...No thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611191101"]="Danger lurks in every corner of the desert. Why not stop by and raise your armor attributes before you start your journey?",
    ["Dialogue611191301"]="How did you know what I like? Could it be that you're my soulmate?",
    ["Dialogue611191401"]="Considering your sincerity, I'll take it.",
    ["Dialogue611191501"]="People like me don't accept any average gift.",
    ["Dialogue611201101"]="Danger lurks in every corner of the desert. Why not stop by and raise your accessory attributes before you start your journey?",
    ["Dialogue611201301"]="Thanks! I really like it!",
    ["Dialogue611201401"]="Seems like I could use this. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611201501"]="It's better not to waste such a good thing on me.",
    ["Dialogue611211101"]="All the best raw materials from across the continent can be found in Alberta. Naturally, you can find the best Weapon Craftsmen like us here too! Why not take a look?",
    ["Dialogue611211301"]="It looks great. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611211401"]="Oh, not bad. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611211501"]="Hmm... You should keep it.",
    ["Dialogue611221101"]="All the best raw materials from across the continent can be found in Alberta. Naturally, you can find the best Armor Craftsmen like us here too! Why not take a look?",
    ["Dialogue611221301"]="What a thoughtful gift. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611221401"]="Oh? Is this for me? Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611221501"]="Hmm... I don't think I have a use for this.",
    ["Dialogue611231101"]="All the best raw materials from across the continent can be found in Alberta. Naturally, you can find the best Accessory Craftsmen like us here too! Why not take a look?",
    ["Dialogue611231301"]="It looks like there's a story behind it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611231401"]="Oh? Is it for me? Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611231501"]="Umm... Was this meant to be a pleasant surprise or an unpleasant one?",
    ["Dialogue611241101"]="The most exquisite craftsmanship, and the most fabulous materials! We're devoted to providing the highest quality service when it comes to decorating your weapon!",
    ["Dialogue611241301"]="Ooh, this seems like it's worth taking a look at.",
    ["Dialogue611241401"]="Nice, I'll make good use of it.",
    ["Dialogue611241501"]="You can keep this. I don't need it.",
    ["Dialogue611251101"]="The most exquisite craftsmanship, and the most fabulous materials! We're devoted to providing the highest quality service when it comes to decorating your armor!",
    ["Dialogue611251301"]="Ooh, that looks very interesting. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611251401"]="Well, thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611251501"]="This didn't seem like something I could use.",
    ["Dialogue611261101"]="The most exquisite craftsmanship, and the most fabulous materials! We're devoted to providing the highest quality service when it comes to decorating your accessories!",
    ["Dialogue611261301"]="Oh? This has given me new inspiration. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611261401"]="Hmm... Let me take a look. It must have some redeeming quality.",
    ["Dialogue611261501"]="This seems like something I already have.",
    ["Dialogue611271101"]="Sacred shrubs sprout among the trees, and from tranquil waters, lotus flowers emerge. Let this wind awaken the strength slumbering within your weapon!",
    ["Dialogue611281101"]="Sacred shrubs sprout among the trees, and from tranquil waters, lotus flowers emerge. Let this wind awaken the strength slumbering within your armor!",
    ["Dialogue611291101"]="Sacred shrubs sprout among the trees, and from tranquil waters, lotus flowers emerge. Let this wind awaken the strength slumbering within your accessory!",
    ["Dialogue611291301"]="Ah! It looks great. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611291401"]="Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611291501"]="Hmm? This isn't for me, right?",
    ["Dialogue611301101"]="There is no \"best\" in Geffen—only \"better.\" We can unleash greater potential in that weapon in your hand with the use of magic!",
    ["Dialogue611301301"]="Hmm, not bad. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611301401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue611301501"]="You should take it back.",
    ["Dialogue611311101"]="There is no \"best\" in Geffen—only \"better.\" We can unleash greater potential in that armor you're wearing with the use of magic!",
    ["Dialogue611311301"]="I actually needed this. I thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611311401"]="I'll take it this time. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611311501"]="You don't have to spend so much time on me.",
    ["Dialogue611321101"]="There is no \"best\" in Geffen—only \"better.\" We can unleash greater potential in that accessory you're wearing with the use of magic!",
    ["Dialogue611321301"]="Ohh, aren't you a smart cookie. You know what this lady likes!",
    ["Dialogue611321401"]="Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611321501"]="What's this? It doesn't look like anything I could use.",
    ["Dialogue611331101"]="The pursuit of excellence is every crafter's motivation! Even precious hard-earned weapons can radiate with a new brilliance in our hands. Come see for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611331301"]="Thanks a lot! I'll try to not let Matilda take it away.",
    ["Dialogue611331401"]="Oh? Looks really interesting. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611331501"]="(He laughs awkwardly and waves his hands.)",
    ["Dialogue611341101"]="The pursuit of excellence is every crafter's motivation! Even precious hard-earned weapons can radiate with a new brilliance in our hands. Come see for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611351101"]="The pursuit of excellence is every crafter's motivation! Even precious hard-earned accessories can radiate with a new brilliance in our hands. Come see for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611351301"]="Wow, this must have cost a lot of Zeny. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue611351401"]="Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue611351501"]="No thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611361101"]="The pursuit of excellence is every crafter's motivation! Even precious hard-earned accessories can radiate with a new brilliance in our hands. Come see for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611371101"]="Do you want to be the most unique and eye-catching individual in the Amusement Park? Libby's headgear will make you the center of attention!",
    ["Dialogue611381101"]="Give your personality an upgrade and become the center of attention—You'll treasure the headgear from Rosha's shop forever.",
    ["Dialogue611381301"]="Great choice. I'll take it. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611381401"]="Oh? Seems pretty nice. Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611381501"]="How could I like something with so little personality?",
    ["Dialogue611382101"]="If you want to make a splash at the Halloween party, don't miss out on Rosha's boutique headgear!",
    ["Dialogue611411101"]="Please don't use those common, boring, infuriating layman's terms when speaking to me... They make my head buzz, thank you very much.",
    ["Dialogue611421101"]="At Rekenber Institute, we never ask questions about each other's lives.",
    ["Dialogue611441101"]="You want to know everything that's happened in the kingdom? Well, I have all of it written in my journal!",
    ["Dialogue611451101"]="Even a newly-created guild deserves to be well maintained. Why not take a look at the guild materials over here?",
    ["Dialogue611451301"]="...Mm... really... Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue611451401"]="...Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611451501"]="This... I... (Lethi looks at you with an awkward expression.)",
    ["Dialogue611461101"]="You never know what value a collection might bring. Building an excellent guild is impossible without these materials from my collection.",
    ["Dialogue611461301"]="Woohoo. Another one for my collection. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611461401"]="Well, thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611461501"]="There's plenty of stuff like that in my collection. You should keep it for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611471101"]="One should strive to maintain one's manners when trading in the desert. Fortune favors the elegant.",
    ["Dialogue611471301"]="I would like to express my sincere gratitude. (Takes hat off to you.)",
    ["Dialogue611471401"]="Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue611471501"]="Pardon my bluntness. This does not suit me.",
    ["Dialogue611481101"]="Based on past experience, a devastating disaster is likely to befall this continent within the next hundred years. The guild must be prepared.",
    ["Dialogue611481301"]="This is worth looking into. I'm feeling lucky. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611481401"]="This is worth keeping.",
    ["Dialogue611481501"]="Is there any use for such things?",
    ["Dialogue611491101"]="Sincerity is the number one essential in both life and business. My guild materials are priced fairly, and everyone receives the same treatment!",
    ["Dialogue611491301"]="Haha, this is exactly what I was looking for. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611491401"]="Not bad! Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611491501"]="I'm sure someone else in Payon needs it. Not me.",
    ["Dialogue611501101"]="If magic can create miracles, then infusing your guild materials with magic will surely create surprising miracles for your entire guild!",
    ["Dialogue611501301"]="Ooh, this looks very interesting. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611501401"]="Haha, not bad! Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611501501"]="This seems better suited for someone else.",
    ["Dialogue611511101"]="The equipment materials we sell are premium quality goods worthy of the Kingdom Defense Force!",
    ["Dialogue611511301"]="Wow, haha. It looks great. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611511401"]="Well, thank you very much.",
    ["Dialogue611511501"]="Um... I don't think I have a use for this.",
    ["Dialogue611521101"]="Quality goods are just like peaceful days... Both are eternally scarce in the desert.",
    ["Dialogue611521301"]="It's been a while since I've received such a thoughtful gift. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611521401"]="Well, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611521501"]="You should keep it for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611531101"]="Why not pick up some materials to upgrade your equipment's performance? It never hurts to be prepared, especially when you have the respite to actually think about it.",
    ["Dialogue611531301"]="Mmm, natural is best, meow! You have good taste!",
    ["Dialogue611531401"]="Oh? Is this for me? I'll keep it safe. Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue611531501"]="Hmm... These youthful things don't interest me.",
    ["Dialogue611541101"]="Add a little magic to these equipment materials and they'll always far exceed any expectations you may have!",
    ["Dialogue611541301"]="Ooh! Where did you find such a cute gift? Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611541401"]="I will happily take it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611541501"]="Huh? I don't like this sort of thing.",
    ["Dialogue611551101"]="Every day, I record three kinds of fish and their prints to make a list. If you complete one of the three kinds of fish prints, or if the fish print is big enough, it will...",
    ["Dialogue611561101"]="I've finished dealing with all guild affairs today—Is what I wish I can tell you personally every day.",
    ["Dialogue611571101"]="Ahem! No matter the ask, you won't go wrong leaving it to Bennit!",
    ["Dialogue611581101"]="I LOVE seeing smiles on everyone's faces! I'll work super hard to make it happen!",
    ["Dialogue611581102"]="Adventurer, Kafra Corporation provides you with the best delivery service available!",
    ["Dialogue611591101"]="The boundless might of the ocean will send new power flowing through your weapon!",
    ["Dialogue611601101"]="The boundless might of the ocean will send new power flowing through your armor!",
    ["Dialogue611611101"]="The boundless might of the ocean will send new power flowing through your accessory!",
    ["Dialogue611621101"]="The hymn of Strouf shall infuse your weapon with new power!",
    ["Dialogue611631101"]="The hymn of Strouf shall infuse your armor with new power!",
    ["Dialogue611641101"]="The hymn of Strouf shall infuse your accessory with new power!",
    ["Dialogue611651101"]="Don't miss this chance to upgrade your equipment's performance! You won't find quality materials like these anywhere else.",
    ["Dialogue611651301"]="Wow! This has a youthful vibe to it. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue611651401"]="Big Sis will take it. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue611651501"]="How about you keep this cute thing for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue611661101"]="If you want to stay on the cutting-edge of the latest trends, you should always start from the head down.",
    ["Dialogue611661301"]="Mm. It goes well with my new haircut.",
    ["Dialogue611661401"]="Looks like you have some good taste.",
    ["Dialogue611661501"]="I can't wear something so old-fashioned.",
    ["Dialogue611671101"]="As the night of Halloween descends, faint whispers echo through the royal city...\nI can take you to the Twilight Banquet Illusion.\nBe careful not to get lost in there!\n<color=#FF0000>Event Time: 19:00–20:00</color>",
    ["Dialogue611681101"]="Hi there! Adventurer!\nI see that you're loaded from the illusion and decryption events.\nIf you don't want to miss out on my exclusive gifts, hurry up and exchange them before they expire!",
    ["Dialogue611691101"]="The illusion has yet to dissipate. Do you want to return to reality?",
    ["Dialogue611701101"]="This land seems to have many things worth exploring. It looks like you are curious about me as well. Maybe our story begins in this Rose Red Tavern!",
    ["Dialogue611711101"]="Dreams remain dreams unless you take action to achieve them.",
    ["Dialogue611721101"]="Dreams remain dreams unless you take action to achieve them.",
    ["Dialogue611721301"]="Wow, this is what I've been looking for. Thank you so much.",
    ["Dialogue611721401"]="Looks pretty good. Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue611721501"]="Eh... This may not really suit me.",
    ["Dialogue611731101"]="An elite combat unit will always make ample logistical preparations.",
    ["Dialogue611741101"]="The service and accomplishments of the Kingdom Defense Force cannot be tarnished by anyone!",
    ["Dialogue611751101"]="Do you also have a dream wedding in mind? Let me make your dream come true!",
    ["Dialogue611761101"]="It's easy to fake things when you're pretending, but it's hard to hide true feelings.",
    ["Dialogue611801101"]="I hear that when the gold and silver rabbits meet, they create a beautiful scene of flames and sparks.",
    ["Dialogue611831101"]="There are so many cute animal rocking chairs here, so let's have a riddle about animals.\nGuess which animal is the answer and sit in that chair to win!\nIf you don't get the chair, come to me and I'll give you a new riddle.",
    ["Dialogue611871101"]="Search for the secret to getting stronger within the lost civilization. Start with Weapon Ascension!",
    ["Dialogue611881101"]="Search for the secret to getting stronger within the lost civilization. Start with Armor Ascension!",
    ["Dialogue611891101"]="Search for the secret to getting stronger within the lost civilization. Start with Accessory Ascension!",
    ["Dialogue611901101"]="The mysterious power left in this land by the Goddess infuses your weapon with a mighty strength!",
    ["Dialogue611911101"]="The mysterious power left in this land by the Goddess infuses your armor with a mighty strength!",
    ["Dialogue611921101"]="The mysterious power left in this land by the Goddess infuses your accessory with a mighty strength!",
    ["Dialogue611931101"]="Glast Heim's weapon crafting is an accumulation of hundreds of years of craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue611941101"]="Glast Heim's armor crafting is an accumulation of hundreds of years of craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue611951101"]="Glast Heim's accessory crafting is an accumulation of hundreds of years of craftsmanship!",
    ["Dialogue611961101"]="Why not enjoy a delicious dish while admiring such grand cultural relics?",
    ["Dialogue611971101"]="Who says Glast Heim doesn't have superior equipment materials? The materials I've got for sale are all the best of the best!",
    ["Dialogue611981101"]="If you want to protect your guild, fine materials are a must!",
    ["Dialogue611991101"]="To become unbeatable, you cannot overlook the importance of Weapon Ascension.",
    ["Dialogue612001101"]="To become unbeatable, you cannot overlook the importance of Armor Ascension.",
    ["Dialogue612011101"]="To become unbeatable, you cannot overlook the importance of Accessory Ascension.",
    ["Dialogue612021101"]="In Aldebaran, let the true essence of time infuse your weapons with boundless magic.",
    ["Dialogue612031101"]="In Aldebaran, let the true essence of time infuse your armor with boundless magic.",
    ["Dialogue612041101"]="In Aldebaran, let the true essence of time infuse your accessories with boundless magic.",
    ["Dialogue612051101"]="As the sands of time refine, you will understand that the exquisite weapons produced in Aldebaran are incomparable to those made elsewhere.",
    ["Dialogue612061101"]="As the sands of time refine, you will understand that the exquisite armor produced in Aldebaran is incomparable to those made elsewhere.",
    ["Dialogue612071101"]="As the sands of time refine, you will understand that the exquisite accessories produced in Aldebaran are incomparable to those made elsewhere.",
    ["Dialogue612081101"]="The materials we produce here will definitely help you build the strongest guild.",
    ["Dialogue612091101"]="Aldebaran's specialties are not to be outdone by Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue612101101"]="Getting outstanding crafting materials is the first step to creating the best equipment!",
    ["Dialogue612111101"]="You can always find surprises and dreams with me!",
    ["Dialogue612121101"]="Welcome",
    ["Dialogue612121102"]="See you next time",
    ["Dialogue612131101"]="On my trip, I collected every wonderful surprise in this little backpack of mine!",
    ["Dialogue612181101"]="Do you like sweet or salty rice dumplings? As for me... I want both of course!",
    ["Dialogue612191101"]="Do you see anything you like, distinguished visitor? Oh, and I should mention that the prices on everything I have here are always clearly marked!",
    ["Dialogue612201101"]="Arise young warrior, recognized by the demon army and voyager of this wonderland! Muster your courage and wisdom and explore! Battle on, Adventurer! Although I come from a different world, your strength transcends the boundaries of your realm!",
    ["Dialogue612201102"]="I'm not even remotely interested in destroying the world. After all, I'm not an evil Slime!",
    ["Dialogue612211101"]="If you want to exchange items, look for me in the Wonderland~",
    ["Dialogue612211102"]="Lord Rimuru's wish is Shuna's command!",
    ["Dialogue612241101"]="The fireworks that never go out and the sun that never sets are guarded with constantly improving weapons.",
    ["Dialogue612251101"]="The fireworks that never go out and the sun that never sets are guarded with constantly improving armors.",
    ["Dialogue612261101"]="The fireworks that never go out and the sun that never sets are guarded with constantly improving accessories.",
    ["Dialogue612271101"]="Few nights on Comodo are completely dark. Even when you close your eyes, magic will quietly light up your weapons.",
    ["Dialogue612281101"]="Few nights on Comodo are completely dark. Even when you close your eyes, magic will quietly light up your armors.",
    ["Dialogue612291101"]="Few nights on Comodo are completely dark. Even when you close your eyes, magic will quietly light up your accessories.",
    ["Dialogue612301101"]="Peace can be intoxicating, and it's easy for us to forget the old days. I hope that you'll never have to take up your weapons.",
    ["Dialogue612311101"]="Peace can be intoxicating, and it's easy for us to forget the old days. I hope that you'll never have to take up your armors.",
    ["Dialogue612321101"]="Peace can be intoxicating, and it's easy for us to forget the old days. I hope that your accessories are just for decoration.",
    ["Dialogue612331101"]="Making the best use of everything and everyone is the only way to build the strongest Guild.",
    ["Dialogue612341101"]="Everyone says Remy's dishes will make you more attractive. Do you want a bite?",
    ["Dialogue612351101"]="We have never received any negative review about our equipment materials. See you next time!",
    ["Dialogue612361101"]="I adapted to the new world in nine hours, because nine is my lucky number!",
    ["Dialogue612361301"]="Wow! I... I've always wanted one of these!",
    ["Dialogue612361401"]="Oh my gosh! Thank you! What a great gift!",
    ["Dialogue612361501"]="Huh? This is... I'll take good care of it.",
    ["Dialogue612411101"]="Woof!",
    ["Dialogue612421101"]="Meow!",
    ["Dialogue612431101"]="I absolutely love the scenery of Morroc. Maybe I'll be able to stay here!",
    ["Dialogue612431301"]="This is... amazing! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue612431401"]="Thank you so much. You're the best!",
    ["Dialogue612431501"]="Huh? You're giving it to me? You don't need me to pass it on to someone else?",
    ["Dialogue612441101"]="Hey! Have you got any new adventure stories for me?",
    ["Dialogue612441301"]="Ooooh! This is... Very nice! I've had a flash of inspiration!",
    ["Dialogue612441401"]="Of course I like the gift! Here, let me see it.",
    ["Dialogue612441501"]="Wow, thank you. I'll put it right over there.",
    ["Dialogue612471101"]="What does White Valentine's Day taste like? Strawberry, chocolate, candy, or honey? It tastes like love!",
    ["Dialogue612481101"]="Some people say that the three best things in life are reunion after a long separation, recovery and false alarm...",
    ["Dialogue612491101"]="Remember to ascend your weapons before breaking the thorn.",
    ["Dialogue612501101"]="Remember to ascend your armor before facing a powerful enemy.",
    ["Dialogue612511101"]="Remember to ascend your accessories before tackling obstacles.",
    ["Dialogue612521101"]="Each enchanted weapon bears the blessing of Yggdrasil.",
    ["Dialogue612531101"]="Each enchanted piece of armor bears the blessing of Yggdrasil.",
    ["Dialogue612541101"]="Each enchanted accessory bears the blessing of Yggdrasil.",
    ["Dialogue612551101"]="Do you want to see how the Utan tribe makes weapons? You've come to the right person!",
    ["Dialogue612561101"]="Do you want to see how the Utan tribe makes armor? You've come to the right person!",
    ["Dialogue612571101"]="Do you want to see how the Utan tribe makes accessories? You've come to the right person!",
    ["Dialogue612581101"]="There is no material that can't be bought. Only prices that can't be afforded.",
    ["Dialogue612591101"]="That's the magic a cook works—turning ordinary ingredients into extraordinary food!",
    ["Dialogue612601101"]="I don't sell mere materials. I sell powerful but unformed weapons.",
    ["Dialogue612611101"]="If fate abandons you to the night, remember to look up and gaze upon the moon.",
    ["Dialogue612621101"]="Wrap rice dumplings with silk threads, and twist vanilla to wear. Don't cry if you miss out, there'll be other chances.",
    ["Dialogue612631101"]="Fashion goes in a cycle, you know!",
    ["Dialogue612641101"]="Acts only in the interests of justice. Having someone like this become an Ultraman is not a bad thing.",
    ["Dialogue612651101"]="Evacuate from this area at once and seek protection from the police officer.",
    ["Dialogue612661101"]="I will not hesitate if someone asks me for help, because I don't want to feel sorry for the rest of my life.",
    ["Dialogue612671101"]="Gender is never the yoke of love and beauty.",
    ["Dialogue612691101"]="Are you trying to tell me you're the great hero—Ultraman?",
    ["Dialogue612701101"]="Greetings, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue612841101"]="A handsome penguin requires a good-looking ice-fishing rod.",
    ["Dialogue612851101"]="The Snow Festival welcomes every Adventurer who loves ice fishing! Make a wish, and you might catch yourself a big fish to exchange for mysterious rewards!",
    ["Dialogue612861101"]="Stranger from afar, how about making a trade with me? I'm sure you will be well compensated.",
    ["Dialogue612871101"]="Wah... No one likes a gingerbread who wears a poopy hat... I've prepared gifts for exchange...",
    ["Dialogue612881101"]="Y-You're not around here! C-Can you exchange gifts with me?",
    ["Dialogue612891101"]="Work hard to play harder; follow the rules to be unbound from the rules.",
    ["Dialogue612901101"]="I want to say this to you! 말하고 싶어！",
    ["Dialogue613071101"]="Lutie, Snow Festival, Ice Fishing, and Wishing! This is the best winter plan ever!",
    ["Dialogue613081101"]="You can find everything about weapon ascension in Juno.",
    ["Dialogue613091101"]="You can find everything about armor ascension in Juno.",
    ["Dialogue613101101"]="You can find everything about accessory ascension in Juno.",
    ["Dialogue613111101"]="By the title of a mere mortal, I grant weapons the wonder of magic.",
    ["Dialogue613121101"]="By the title of a mere mortal, I grant armor the wonder of magic.",
    ["Dialogue613131101"]="By the title of a mere mortal, I grant accessories the wonder of magic.",
    ["Dialogue613141101"]="We pursue ethereal knowledge, as well as make sharp weapons.",
    ["Dialogue613151101"]="We pursue ethereal knowledge, as well as make solid armor.",
    ["Dialogue613161101"]="We pursue ethereal knowledge, as well as make magnificent accessories.",
    ["Dialogue613171101"]="Money never betrays you. So do materials.",
    ["Dialogue613181101"]="Hmph! I will not sell my ingredients to someone who wastes food!",
    ["Dialogue613191101"]="The equipment materials are all listed! Choose whatever you like!",
    ["Dialogue613201101"]="Gazing at the sun is an act of great bravery, but there's no need to become consumed by fanaticism.",
    ["Dialogue613201102"]="The trial serves to rekindle the glory of our heroic souls!",
    ["Dialogue613211101"]="Yoooooo! Don't be silent, and don't be shy! Let it out loud if you rhyme! Yoooooo!",
    ["Dialogue613231101"]="Wool balls, scratching post, and teaser... Whatever makes a pet happy, you can hand them to me. Meow!",
    ["Dialogue613261101"]="By the command of the goddess, I will enable the transfer and inheritance of Shadow Equipment's power for the bearers.",
    ["Dialogue613271101"]="In the City of Steel, the art of weapon ascension really teaches you about perfection and imperfection.",
    ["Dialogue613281101"]="In the City of Steel, the art of armor ascension really teaches you about perfection and imperfection.",
    ["Dialogue613291101"]="In the City of Steel, the art of accessory ascension really teaches you about perfection and imperfection.",
    ["Dialogue613301101"]="Weapon enchantment and ascension are part of the same art; you go with magic, and I go with steel.",
    ["Dialogue613311101"]="Armor enchantment and ascension are part of the same art; you go with magic, and I go with steel.",
    ["Dialogue613321101"]="Accessory enchantment and ascension are part of the same art; you go with magic, and I go with steel.",
    ["Dialogue613331101"]="Weapon crafters love their weapons just as much as those who own them.",
    ["Dialogue613341101"]="Armor crafters love their armor just as much as those who own them.",
    ["Dialogue613351101"]="Accessory crafters love their accessories just as much as those who own them.",
    ["Dialogue613361101"]="Supplies are super important for keeping the guild together. Need to replenish?",
    ["Dialogue613371101"]="Fruits are children of the soil, unlike humans.",
    ["Dialogue613381101"]="Crafting equipment needs tons of materials, but taking them off needs tons of courage.",
    ["Dialogue613391101"]="Adventurer, do what you can and deliver the gifts to the next stop!",
    ["Dialogue613401101"]="With your help, every gift will end up exactly where it's meant to be!",
    ["Dialogue613411101"]="...Big thanks for helping out! You managed to find all the Lost Fireworks for us!",
    ["Dialogue613421101"]="Brrr... The place up ahead is where they extract Energy Crystals. It's freezing outside...",
    ["Dialogue613481101"]="I'm Wataru the Savior! As a hero, I can't just ignore people in trouble!",
    ["Dialogue613491101"]="If you ever need my help, just raise your sword to the sky and call my name—I'll always be with you!",
    ["Dialogue613501101"]="Weapon enchantment, a trick to make your gems shine even brighter.",
    ["Dialogue613511101"]="Accessory enchantment, a trick to make your gems shine even brighter.",
    ["Dialogue613521101"]="Armor enchantment, a trick to make your gems shine even brighter.",
    ["Dialogue614051101"]="Every weapon ascension is a blessing from Goddess Freyja.",
    ["Dialogue614061101"]="Every armor ascension is a blessing from Goddess Freyja.",
    ["Dialogue614071101"]="Every accessory ascension is a blessing from Goddess Freyja.",
    ["Dialogue614081101"]="Forging weapons with alchemy gemstones is like establishing our Rachel in a desolate desert.",
    ["Dialogue614091101"]="Forging armor with alchemy gemstones is like establishing our Rachel in a desolate desert.",
    ["Dialogue614101101"]="Forging accessories with alchemy gemstones is like establishing our Rachel in a desolate desert.",
    ["Dialogue614111101"]="How about purchasing some guild materials before returning to the guild?",
    ["Dialogue614121101"]="Enjoy the delicious Rachel cuisine to your heart's content!",
    ["Dialogue614131101"]="What's your equipment made of? Give Rachel materials a try!",
    ["Dialogue619261101"]="You can ask me just anything about the Farmland.",
    ["Dialogue619271101"]="If you want to decorate your home, then come see me with your blueprints.",
    ["Dialogue619281101"]="Esteemed Adventurer, welcome home.",
    ["Dialogue619301101"]="There are five types of Ore Veins depending on their richness in minerals. The bigger the size, the more the yields.",
    ["Dialogue619311101"]="My fishing skill is a lot better than Xavier's!",
    ["Dialogue619321101"]="I am Ronald, the butler of your home. Welcome home, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue619321102"]="Don't miss out on this once-in-a-lifetime deal to get yourself a luxurious estate!",
    ["Dialogue619331101"]="I want to become strong.",
    ["Dialogue619341101"]="A bunch of trash! Gets nothing done without me!",
    ["Dialogue619351101"]="I'm Hellish Blizzard. You should have heard about me.",
    ["Dialogue619361101"]="I'm the leader of the Dark Matter Thieves, the lord of the universe, Boros!",
    ["Dialogue619371101"]="My hobbit is... I mean, I'm a professional hero, Saitama.",
    ["Dialogue619381101"]="The only place that light cannot touch, except the bottom of the abyss, is under the human heart.",
    ["Dialogue619391101"]="Just between you and me, I'm actually from the moon!",
    ["Dialogue619531101"]="Garm's ambition is always insatiable, and its aggression is unending...",
    ["Dialogue619671101"]="Lalalalalalalalala....Larva! Helping me to win the Sausage Battle earns you the Winning Camp Rewards!",
    ["Dialogue619681101"]="Lalalalalalalalala....Larva! Helping me to win the Sausage Battle earns you the Winning Camp Rewards!",
    ["Dialogue619731101"]="If giving my life means bringing light to the world...",
    ["Dialogue619741101"]="Even if the odds are 99% against me, I'll fight for that 1% chance to win. That's the fate of the Successor of Fist of the North Star.",
    ["Dialogue619751101"]="I have no regrets about the life that I've lived!",
    ["Dialogue6197711"]="My name is Subaru Natsuki. Not only am I clueless, but I'm also broke beyond compare!",
    ["Dialogue6197712"]="Whoa! I've been eyeing this for a long time! Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue6197811"]="My name is Emilia. Just Emilia. Nice to meet you.",
    ["Dialogue6197812"]="That must be what you picked for me. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue6197911"]="I'm Rem, a maid at the Roswaal Mansion. I'll take care of all the chores.",
    ["Dialogue6197912"]="Is this for me? Thank you, Adventurer. I'm really happy.",
    ["Dialogue619811101"]="You—got—a—problem?",
    ["Dialogue619821101"]="The stars never lie.",
    ["Dialogue619841101"]="Amusement parks are made of dreams. So—do you prefer sweet dreams or nightmares?",
    ["Dialogue619861101"]="I'm so hungry after all that fighting... Taichi! Get me some taiyaki!\n<color=#e14558>Earn Digital Core (up to 20) and Heart of Innocence (up to 100) by consuming Odin's Blessings while AFK.\nThe limit resets daily at 05:00.</color>",
    ["Dialogue619871101"]="We made it this far, thanks to all of you! This bond we share is what gives me courage!",
    ["Dialogue619891101"]="For victory, for glory! Heroes, let's move out!",
    ["Dialogue619901101"]="Fusing science into weapons—that's the essence of enchantment.",
    ["Dialogue619911101"]="Fusing science into armor—that's the essence of enchantment.",
    ["Dialogue619921101"]="Fusing science into accessories—that's the essence of enchantment.",
    ["Dialogue619931101"]="You can buy anything in this world, unless you don't have enough money.",
    ["Dialogue619941101"]="These ingredients are all carefully chosen, you can trust me.",
    ["Dialogue620011101"]="Only by honing the virtue in your heart can you achieve greatness!",
    ["Dialogue620021101"]="...Magic cannot be described by mere words.",
    ["Dialogue620031101"]="Nothing lasts forever, be it happiness or sadness.",
    ["Dialogue620041101"]="Principles are beyond me. All I know is we all have to fight for what we want. Of course, whether or not you're capable of getting it is another matter altogether.",
    ["Dialogue620051101"]="\"Payon's Number One Archer\"—You got it, that's me... some day at least!",
    ["Dialogue620061101"]="Shh! ...Did you hear that? That's the sound of gold dropping more than ten meters away!",
    ["Dialogue620071101"]="Do come to me if you have any questions!",
    ["Dialogue620081101"]="Real adventurers should know how to enjoy life more than fighting.",
    ["Dialogue620091101"]="I see infinite possibilities in your eyes! Ha ha ha!",
    ["Dialogue620101101"]="Protecting the peace of this kingdom is more important than anything else.",
    ["Dialogue620111101"]="The Rose Red Tavern is your ultimate choice when you need to loosen up! ♥",
    ["Dialogue620121101"]="Odin's servants fear no danger.",
    ["Dialogue620121201"]="Odin will hear your prayers, young one.",
    ["Dialogue620131101"]="Silence! Or... I'll turn you into an ugly Poring!",
    ["Dialogue620141101"]="You want a Pecopeco? Then you'll need to prepare enough food. They eat more than you'd think!",
    ["Dialogue620151101"]="You can always get the help you seek at the Prontera Cathedral. Odin will provide sanctuary to all.",
    ["Dialogue620161101"]="Let me know if you find new work to do!",
    ["Dialogue620171101"]="The Kingdom Defense Force is the impregnable armor of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue620181101"]="The soldiers of the Defense Force First Squad are the cream of the crop! The softies in Second Squad can hardly compare!",
    ["Dialogue620191101"]="If one wants to become a monk, they must first have an understanding.",
    ["Dialogue620201101"]="The academic field has countless branches, but alchemy is the most profound among them. Oh, is there something about alchemy you'd like to explore with me?",
    ["Dialogue620211101"]="What is magic? That is an eternal question for discussion for all mages.",
    ["Dialogue620221101"]="The soldiers of the Defense Force Second Squad possess brilliant minds! Those First Squad brutes who solve all their problems with violence can hardly compare!",
    ["Dialogue620231101"]="♪ Who saw more than me? Who understands my sorrows?\nThe moon, beautiful wine, and a lute. I'll hold her memories close at heart. ♪",
    ["Dialogue620241101"]="Bless my family, Odin, and every soldier in the Kingdom Defense Force...",
    ["Dialogue620251101"]="The first recorded sage in history appeared in Juno. He was the forerunner of all sages.",
    ["Dialogue620261101"]="Hold your head up high, soldier!",
    ["Dialogue620271101"]="...I never talk nonsense.",
    ["Dialogue620281101"]="Please don't talk to me while I'm on duty!",
    ["Dialogue620291101"]="A knight must have courage and decorum at all times.",
    ["Dialogue620301101"]="Did I do something wrong again?! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!",
    ["Dialogue620311101"]="A rogue who can't draw graffiti isn't much of a rogue!",
    ["Dialogue620321101"]="The Royal Chivalry is my home and the knights my family.",
    ["Dialogue620331101"]="Guess which is faster: your head, or my arrows?",
    ["Dialogue620341101"]="Did you know Old Charlie is the best craftsman in Prontera?",
    ["Dialogue620351101"]="Odin will provide sanctuary to all... even this fragile heart of mine...",
    ["Dialogue620361101"]="Falcons are our partners. You must treat them with kindness.",
    ["Dialogue620371101"]="The academic field has countless branches, but monster research is the most fascinating among them. Oh, is there something about monsters you'd like to explore with me?",
    ["Dialogue620381101"]="Believe in Strouf? No! Odin is the only one who protects this world.",
    ["Dialogue620391101"]="Welcome to Alberta, the Wigner Family's territory!",
    ["Dialogue620401101"]="Every man and woman of the sea knows the name Alson.",
    ["Dialogue620411101"]="... (Stares at you.)",
    ["Dialogue620421101"]="What is magic? That is an eternal question for discussion for all mages.",
    ["Dialogue620431101"]="The Lugenburg Family welcomes all adventurers who possess true strength!",
    ["Dialogue620441101"]="Mom always says to marry an honest man and not a rich man. But it seems like dad has both qualities!",
    ["Dialogue620451101"]="The road to repairing the Golden Wings Mine is a long one.",
    ["Dialogue620461101"]="The people of Eden Group can get a little too enthusiastic sometimes.",
    ["Dialogue620471101"]="The selection of wine is quite varied for a tavern in the desert.",
    ["Dialogue620481101"]="I don't have time to talk! I have to prepare for this year's weather forecast competition!",
    ["Dialogue620491101"]="You have to work hard to get the approval you want from others. An illustrious family background isn't enough to carry you.",
    ["Dialogue620541101"]="It's not how much strength you have that matters—it's how you use it that counts.",
    ["Dialogue620551101"]="Hm? What does it feel like to be sealed away for a thousand years? Well... Do you wanna try it for yourself?",
    ["Dialogue620561101"]="I can see the ocean below me and a great big sky above me. Apart from not being able to smell the ocean tides, it's no different from my life from before.",
    ["Dialogue620571101"]="Death isn't scary. What's scary is we can't choose how we go...",
    ["Dialogue620581101"]="I only wield this sword in my hand for the sake of my loved ones.",
    ["Dialogue620591101"]="If you can solve a problem with your fists, there's no need for further communication!",
    ["Dialogue620601101"]="No one wants to become my target, not even you.",
    ["Dialogue620611101"]="I will become the sharpest blade in the land.",
    ["Dialogue620621101"]="One day, you and I will also become part of the ancient ruins. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue620631101"]="Oh, hi! What an honor for you to run into me!",
    ["Dialogue620641101"]="(Gurgle, gurgle.)",
    ["Dialogue620651101"]="Can you go blind if you stare at the desert too long?",
    ["Dialogue620661101"]="My mama always says talking to people taller than you all the time will wear down the bones in your neck!",
    ["Dialogue620671101"]="They say being in the sun can help you grow taller... Good thing I don't work under the sun!",
    ["Dialogue620681101"]="Hm~ Hmm hmm hmm~ ♪",
    ["Dialogue620691101"]="Want to see some magic? Ahem! Abracadabra, alakazam! And now—your wallet has vanished!",
    ["Dialogue620701101"]="Out of the way! Out of the way! I hate standing under someone else's shadow!",
    ["Dialogue620721101"]="If you happen to see Trisse, can you tell her to give me back my wallet?",
    ["Dialogue620731101"]="I'm not interested in goods that circulate the market through proper channels.",
    ["Dialogue620741101"]="Protecting the pyramids is an honored mission bestowed upon me by my ancestors!",
    ["Dialogue620751101"]="Even if a thousand years have passed and the person I know is no more, I'll still see love through my eyes.",
    ["Dialogue620761101"]="I've been thinking a lot lately. What's the worst thing that can happen to a sailor: fear of water or seasickness?",
    ["Dialogue620771101"]="My dad hopes that I'll become \"thick as thieves\" with the other kids on the island, but... I think it's wrong to steal!",
    ["Dialogue620781101"]="You wanna know who's the king of all the kids in this area? That's right! It's me! Heh heh.",
    ["Dialogue620791101"]="...Huh? You want to play with us?",
    ["Dialogue620801101"]="Do you think Lily can visit grandpa in Prontera during the holidays this summer?",
    ["Dialogue620811101"]="Fancy a game of rock, paper, scissors? The loser has to frog jump in place 100 times. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue620821101"]="♪ Who saw more than me? Who understands my sorrows? The moon, beautiful wine, and a lute. I'll hold her memories close at heart. ♪",
    ["Dialogue620831101"]="Knowledge will bring you wealth and wisdom, which will guide you to love.",
    ["Dialogue620841101"]="A person who is pure of heart will surely find their way through the darkness and into the light.",
    ["Dialogue620851101"]="The true devil is in the hearts of men.",
    ["Dialogue620861101"]="It's a great honor for a soldier to be chosen to guard the palace!",
    ["Dialogue620871101"]="There are no shortcuts to success... Your fate is determined by the heavens, but your own efforts are the deciding factor.",
    ["Dialogue620881101"]="Is there something you'd like to talk about? I mean, do you have any business matters to discuss?",
    ["Dialogue620891101"]="Do I like the desert or the ocean better? Hmm... I like wherever my big brothers are at!",
    ["Dialogue620901101"]="Hmph! My fists are justice!",
    ["Dialogue620911101"]="A real man's place is on the battlefield.",
    ["Dialogue620921101"]="This is our territory. We make the rules!",
    ["Dialogue620931101"]="Coo, Coco, Cocoa!",
    ["Dialogue620941101"]="Mumu Be is a proud Giearth!",
    ["Dialogue620951101"]="Mumu Be is a proud Giearth!",
    ["Dialogue620961101"]="(It radiates a gentle light.)",
    ["Dialogue620971101"]="(He seems oblivious to his current situation.)",
    ["Dialogue620981101"]="Please slow down. This is General Qi Euin's resting place.",
    ["Dialogue620991101"]="Without my lute... My life, my very purpose for existing is...",
    ["Dialogue621001101"]="Just you wait and see! I'll become an assassin one day!",
    ["Dialogue621011101"]="The key to becoming a blacksmith is powerful muscles and an unbending will!",
    ["Dialogue621021101"]="The art of blacksmithing is also full of ancient wisdom!",
    ["Dialogue621031101"]="It's not how much strength you have that matters—it's how you use it that counts.",
    ["Dialogue621041101"]="Protecting the peace of this kingdom is more important than anything else.",
    ["Dialogue621051101"]="You can always get the help you seek at the Prontera Cathedral. Odin will provide sanctuary to all.",
    ["Dialogue621061101"]="Compared to the interests of the Kingdom, family affairs are merely trifling matters.",
    ["Dialogue621071101"]="(It radiates an unknown scent.)",
    ["Dialogue621081101"]="(It radiates a gentle light.)",
    ["Dialogue621091101"]="(The gentle light has disappeared and it no longer responds.)",
    ["Dialogue621111101"]="I—I don't know anything! Don't ask me!",
    ["Dialogue621121101"]="Hmph. The Sphinx Cavern really does contain many secrets.",
    ["Dialogue621131101"]="It is I who is the greatest king of the Egyptian kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue621141101"]="(This is the place... I think.)",
    ["Dialogue621161101"]="(Quietly staring at you without saying a word.)",
    ["Dialogue621171101"]="Prontera is facing a massive crisis!",
    ["Dialogue621201101"]="The purpose of my journey is to become the strongest pet tamer in Midgard!",
    ["Dialogue621221101"]="To seek the truth in the past...",
    ["Dialogue621241101"]="Ashes to ashes, dust to dust... My eternal resting place is in the ocean.",
    ["Dialogue621251101"]="I love mommy and daddy so so much! And everybody in Weinst Street too!",
    ["Dialogue621261101"]="(Concentrating on work.)",
    ["Dialogue621271101"]="All Allie and I have left are each other...",
    ["Dialogue621281101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621291101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621301101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621301301"]="You are such a kind person. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue621301401"]="Thanks, I'll take it.",
    ["Dialogue621301501"]="Is this a gift for mounts?",
    ["Dialogue621311101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621321101"]="This is the Lord's Residence. You do not have permission to enter!",
    ["Dialogue621331101"]="Payon's mountain paths may be rocky and uneven, but I can traverse them as swift as a deer. Wanna see?",
    ["Dialogue621341101"]="You came to find me... Yikes! Please don't say it's because the Senior Disciple sent you!",
    ["Dialogue621351101"]="...If you wish to chat, I am unfortunately unable to accommodate you.",
    ["Dialogue621361101"]="Oh-hoho! Fishing from dawn till dusk, then it's home for dinner!",
    ["Dialogue621371101"]="Only when a tree has endured the wind and rain can its roots become strong, and the sword will only reveal its edge once polished.",
    ["Dialogue621381101"]="Those in training should treat nature with empathy and act according nature's laws.",
    ["Dialogue621391101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621401101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue621431101"]="Sigh, people always say the name Abessie sounds like a girl's name. Why couldn't I have been named something like Ike or Alfred?",
    ["Dialogue621441101"]="Heh, heh. The calendar says today, tomorrow, and the day after are the perfect time to rake in some cash!",
    ["Dialogue621451101"]="When do you think mother will take me somewhere other than Payon to play?",
    ["Dialogue621461101"]="Even your greatest skill will become rusty with time. You have to keep practicing.",
    ["Dialogue621471101"]="Incalculable delicacies hold no value and sobriety is worthless; drunken stupor should prevail... Burp!",
    ["Dialogue621481101"]="True beauty can only be admired, not owned—But that's never stopped people from pursuing it, has it?",
    ["Dialogue621491101"]="Life never turns out the way you want it to, so don't take it too seriously! Haha.",
    ["Dialogue621501101"]="(A sign meant for indicating directions, but the closer you look, the blurrier the words on the sign become. Are you just seeing things?)",
    ["Dialogue621501201"]="(A line of text appears on the sign: Follow this correct path and you'll be able to admire the Blue Sealstone left behind by the witch.)",
    ["Dialogue621511101"]="(A sign meant for indicating directions, but the closer you look, the blurrier the words on the sign become. Are you just seeing things?)",
    ["Dialogue621511201"]="(Follow this correct path and cross a river and you'll be able to admire the Green Sealstone left behind by the witch.)",
    ["Dialogue621521101"]="(A sign meant for indicating directions, but the closer you look, the blurrier the words on the sign become. Are you just seeing things?)",
    ["Dialogue621521201"]="(Follow this correct path and you'll be able to admire the Purple Sealstone left behind by the witch.)",
    ["Dialogue621531101"]="Time can create everything, but it can also destroy it all.",
    ["Dialogue621551101"]="Not all things will become forgotten with the passing of time.",
    ["Dialogue621561101"]="I'm afraid a monster that can escape the bite of my arrow has yet to be born.",
    ["Dialogue621571101"]="\"Let martial arts draw out the energy within. Let your art and energy become one.\" Such is the peak state for a martial artist.",
    ["Dialogue621581101"]="The myriad beauty seen in this world are little more than a glass facade hovering above a pool of darkness, just waiting to shatter with a single blow.",
    ["Dialogue621591101"]="A family's reputation is important, but it is useless if it cannot be used to protect the family.",
    ["Dialogue621601101"]="Hmm, let me see... The cover and pages aren't damaged. This book must have had a gentle owner!",
    ["Dialogue621611101"]="Master Nithil looks particularly down in the dumps, you say? Haha! That's just because you don't know how to make him laugh!",
    ["Dialogue621621101"]="Some answers take a lifetime to find.",
    ["Dialogue621631101"]="Life is no different from magic: it never ceases to amaze and surprise.",
    ["Dialogue621641101"]="No need to beat around the bush. Spit it out!",
    ["Dialogue621651101"]="Advanced magic is simple compared to understanding people's emotions...",
    ["Dialogue621661101"]="Great God, your people pray with all their hearts…",
    ["Dialogue621671101"]="People who know how to taste wine are the ones who really know how to enjoy life~",
    ["Dialogue621681101"]="Clothes are made stitch by stitch, and in that sense, life passes day by day.",
    ["Dialogue621691101"]="Is there anything more precious than spending long hours with your family?",
    ["Dialogue621701101"]="Rights and obligations should be balanced, how can the nobility just indulge in pleasure every day?",
    ["Dialogue621721101"]="They say there was a civilization that flourished here, but I don't feel it…",
    ["Dialogue621731101"]="As long as you have faith, the great Gods will protect this land!",
    ["Dialogue621741101"]="If you want to verify historical truths, you need to speak with evidence!",
    ["Dialogue621751101"]="Of course, we should make bold assumptions and carefully verify them when doing research.",
    ["Dialogue621761101"]="Even if time goes on, we must not let the truth be buried in the dust of history!",
    ["Dialogue621771101"]="Smart people use their brains to solve problems, while idiots can only rely on brawn.",
    ["Dialogue621781101"]="Everything has a cause. Let me see the cycle of fate turn within the hearts of the common people...",
    ["Dialogue621791101"]="Oh yeah! To a merchant like myself, profit's the only thing worth mentioning...",
    ["Dialogue621801101"]="Stop! Show me your pass!",
    ["Dialogue621811101"]="The clock tower is a place of strategic importane. No passage!",
    ["Dialogue621821101"]="The true essence of searching for magic and adventure is nothing without fighting side by side with friends!",
    ["Dialogue621881101"]="Every person has something they would be willing to give everything for. I'm no exception.",
    ["Dialogue621891101"]="If... if I had enough Ymir crystals, I could...",
    ["Dialogue622191101"]="Follow the rules and we will never fall.",
    ["Dialogue622221101"]="The sea is a testament to my undying allegiance to the captain!",
    ["Dialogue622251101"]="The ocean gives us hope, but has also buried many of our friends.",
    ["Dialogue622261101"]="The Eden Group watches history unfold, and will also eventually be part of history.",
    ["Dialogue622271101"]="My grave will be adorned with the bones of my prey.",
    ["Dialogue622281101"]="Music is the oldest language. Everything I wish to say is written in this song.",
    ["Dialogue622291101"]="Nobody is to become his burden, including me.",
    ["Dialogue622301101"]="Welcome, traveler. Your visit is an honor to the whole village.",
    ["Dialogue622311101"]="No matter how big a country is, it needs responsible warehouse management. No matter how small a family is, it needs a responsible father.",
    ["Dialogue622321101"]="Lofty dreams...? No, I just want to be able to live out my days without worry.",
    ["Dialogue622331101"]="At sea, the stars show us the way.",
    ["Dialogue622351101"]="History is always written by the victors; I prefer to trust my own eyes.",
    ["Dialogue622361101"]="Alchemy works according to the law of equivalent exchange... That's right, your life for mine.",
    ["Dialogue622371101"]="... If I am to stay in this lighthouse forever...",
    ["Dialogue622381101"]="So-called heroes are people who die tragically to give people new hope.",
    ["Dialogue622391101"]="Comodo is a city that never sleeps. So... Very few people have noticed that the sunrise here is even more beautiful than the sunset.",
    ["Dialogue622401101"]="I haven't given up on dancing. I just... chose something even more important.",
    ["Dialogue622411101"]="Don't ask me why I came to Comodo. Everyone who knows this secret has become fuel for this furnace.",
    ["Dialogue622431101"]="​The loser knows only pain, while the winner knows only glory. May the heavens rejoice as you accept your crown!",
    ["Dialogue622441101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue622451101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>High Wizard</color>",
    ["Dialogue622461101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Assassin Cross</color>",
    ["Dialogue622471101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sniper</color>",
    ["Dialogue622481101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sniper</color>",
    ["Dialogue622491101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>High Priest</color>",
    ["Dialogue622501101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>High Priest</color>",
    ["Dialogue622511101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>LikMyMANA</color>, the first Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sniper</color>",
    ["Dialogue622521101"]="It's Travers. Professor Travers, who has mastered the secrets of Multi-class Conversion. <(￣︶￣)>",
    ["Dialogue622541101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Majapahit</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Bishop</color>",
    ["Dialogue622551101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sukhothai</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shura</color>",
    ["Dialogue622561101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ayothaya</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue622571101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ayothaya</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Guard</color>",
    ["Dialogue622581101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ayothaya</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warlock</color>",
    ["Dialogue622591101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Chaser</color>",
    ["Dialogue622601101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue622611101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-SHARK</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 4\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ayothaya</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sorcerer</color>",
    ["Dialogue622621101"]="It's up to each Defense Force Soldier to create a more prosperous Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue622661101"]="Hah! Do you like the deliciously smelling Lutie as well?",
    ["Dialogue622671101"]="Kids in the Toy Factory are the happiest kids in the world!",
    ["Dialogue622681101"]="Want a hot Cocoa? Don't rush back to work!",
    ["Dialogue622691101"]="Get back to work as soon as you're done! Hurry up!",
    ["Dialogue622701101"]="You've got to believe that Santa Claus truly exists! Ho-Ho-Ho, he's already here!",
    ["Dialogue622711101"]="Hehehe! You never know... where the Clown is hiding...",
    ["Dialogue622721101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ranger</color>",
    ["Dialogue622731101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shura</color>",
    ["Dialogue622741101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Bishop</color>",
    ["Dialogue622751101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Guard</color>",
    ["Dialogue622761101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Bishop</color>",
    ["Dialogue622771101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warlock</color>",
    ["Dialogue622781101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Bishop</color>",
    ["Dialogue622791101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nameless Nobody</color>, the second Champion Team in the War of the Chosen\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Opera Phantom</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unknown</color>",
    ["Dialogue622811101"]="Be the most loyal blade! Hmm, except for holidays.",
    ["Dialogue622821101"]="Never waste your time on pointless things.",
    ["Dialogue622831101"]="There's nothing I'm scared of! Hmm... Except for the steaming rage of Delia.",
    ["Dialogue622851101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wanderer</color>",
    ["Dialogue622861101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sorcerer</color>",
    ["Dialogue622871101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Super Novice</color>",
    ["Dialogue622881101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tsukuyomi</color>",
    ["Dialogue622891101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue622901101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warlock</color>",
    ["Dialogue622911101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Bishop</color>",
    ["Dialogue622921101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>「G-String」</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 7\nSub Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Genetic</color>",
    ["Dialogue623031101"]="For me, searching for the truth is the only thing that matters.",
    ["Dialogue623041101"]="Welcome to Einbroch's largest prosthetics factory! Need any assistance?",
    ["Dialogue623051101"]="From here, the rail can get you to any place you desire.",
    ["Dialogue623221101"]="What the customer wants, we deliver!",
    ["Dialogue623231101"]="Move it. I don't care about money.",
    ["Dialogue623241101"]="Sweet and cheap—desert fruits for sale! Come check it out!",
    ["Dialogue623271101"]="Cough... Wonder if I'll live to see that day...",
    ["Dialogue623281101"]="Mom, Dad... why aren't you back yet?",
    ["Dialogue623451101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Wanderer</color>",
    ["Dialogue623461101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E1AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623471101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623481101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E4AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623491101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\n Server: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\n Class: <color=#CA2E3AFF>Tsukuyomi</color>",
    ["Dialogue623501101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623511101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E1AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623521101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-String</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 8\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Susa</color>",
    ["Dialogue623531101"]="Hmm, let me see... Ahh, what a deliciously fresh soul...",
    ["Dialogue623621101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E5AFF>Trouvere</color>",
    ["Dialogue623631101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E4AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623641101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E5AFF>Arch Mage</color>",
    ["Dialogue623651101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E4AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623661101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E3AFF>Abyss Chaser</color>",
    ["Dialogue623671101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623681101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nemesis</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E3AFF>Elemental Master</color>",
    ["Dialogue623691101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>G-PANDA!</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 9\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Elemental Master</color>",
    ["Dialogue623781101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623791101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shiranui</color>",
    ["Dialogue623801101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623811101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Abyss Chaser</color>",
    ["Dialogue623821101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623831101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arch Mage</color>",
    ["Dialogue623841101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623851101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>UNKNOWN</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 10\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boulders and Horns</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elemental Master</color>",
    ["Dialogue623861101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>斯芬克斯</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623871101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>斯芬克斯</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E1AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue623881101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>壁畫迴廊</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E2AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623891101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>斯芬克斯</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E3AFF>Hyper Novice</color>",
    ["Dialogue623901101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>蘇克拉特</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E4AFF>Hyper Novice</color>",
    ["Dialogue623911101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>蘇克拉特</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E5AFF>Dragon Knight</color>",
    ["Dialogue623921101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>壁畫迴廊</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E6AFF>Inquisitor</color>",
    ["Dialogue623931101"]="A member of <color=#CA2E0AFF>共享隊友</color>, the Grand Champion of War of the Chosen Season 6\nServer: <color=#CA2E0AFF>壁畫迴廊</color>\nClass: <color=#CA2E7AFF>Cardinal</color>",
    ["Dialogue630011101"]="Who says girls can't become famous adventurers?",
    ["Dialogue630021101"]="An Angeling without a Halo just isn't beautiful anymore, por...",
    ["Dialogue630031101"]="Before Lady Valkyrie left, she put me into a deep sleep in the ruins. Oh, when will she come to take me home, por?",
    ["Dialogue630041101"]="One day, I'll become the best swordswoman in all the land!",
    ["Dialogue630051101"]="You can get really generous rewards for completing requests! If I didn't have to guard the Mission Board, I'd become an adventurer too. Sigh...",
    ["Dialogue630061101"]="I'm a soldier now, too! My mom is gonna be so happy when she finds out!",
    ["Dialogue630071101"]="...Stay away from me. Stop sticking your nose where it doesn't belong!",
    ["Dialogue630081101"]="...Go away.",
    ["Dialogue630091101"]="Have you gone on the Carousel in the Amusement Park yet? It's so much fun!",
    ["Dialogue630101101"]="The darkest, the purest—this is the power I seek.",
    ["Dialogue630111101"]="We move forward in the direction Master Strouf guides us.",
    ["Dialogue630121101"]="The successor of Odin's bloodline... We don't have much time left.",
    ["Dialogue630131101"]="Captain Fitz is kinda terrifying but... Hey, you! D-don't go telling him I said that!",
    ["Dialogue630141101"]="A real man's place is on the battlefield.",
    ["Dialogue630151101"]="Have you met Edward? Haha, he's my little brother!",
    ["Dialogue630161101"]="Drest says he's had enough of Jack's tastes. I feel the same way.",
    ["Dialogue630171101"]="Ahh, how much longer is it going to take me to become a knight like Captain Hallam!",
    ["Dialogue630181101"]="I'm a soldier now, too! My mom is gonna be so happy when she finds out!",
    ["Dialogue630191101"]="You can't go wrong working for Boss Rorke!",
    ["Dialogue630211101"]="The day the ship sank was an utter nightmare...",
    ["Dialogue630221101"]="I wonder if ma back home would cry if she knew what I've become?",
    ["Dialogue630241101"]="You're as good as garbage in the Heines Family if you possess zero magical talent. Even so, I'll persevere.",
    ["Dialogue630251101"]="I hope Master Kroneika will stop having a biased view of Nithil.",
    ["Dialogue630261101"]="(Nithil's face is deathly pale. He's fallen into a deep state of unconsciousness.)",
    ["Dialogue630271101"]="The glory of the Heines Family trumps all else. Those who can't bring glory to our family are not worthy of inheriting the family name.",
    ["Dialogue630281101"]="What's one more pain in this life of hardship~♪\n...Do you like it? I learned this song from a bard in the east.",
    ["Dialogue630291101"]="It... hurts...",
    ["Dialogue630301101"]="Keh, keh, keh, keh! What would you like to turn into? A patch of algae, or a tentacle?",
    ["Dialogue630311101"]="Ask yourself what you already have before you think about what you want.",
    ["Dialogue630321101"]="(You listen carefully and seem to hear the sound of running water.)",
    ["Dialogue630331101"]="(You should know better: Look, don't eat.)",
    ["Dialogue630341101"]="(You wouldn't want to pass out drunk in this place.)",
    ["Dialogue630351101"]="(You listen carefully and seem to hear a storm rumbling.)",
    ["Dialogue630361101"]="(You listen carefully and seem to hear a humming from the earth.)",
    ["Dialogue630371101"]="(You listen carefully and seem to hear the crackle of flame.)",
    ["Dialogue630381101"]="I am eternal.",
    ["Dialogue630391101"]="Bargaining with a merchant only ends with you feeling like you've \"won\"!",
    ["Dialogue630401101"]="You shouldn't think too highly of your health, nor should you underestimate the temperament of illness.",
    ["Dialogue630411101"]="(Gurgle, gurgle.)",
    ["Dialogue630421101"]="Which is more complicated: a woman's heart, or the riddles contained in poetry?",
    ["Dialogue630431101"]="Only a life full of challenges can ignite my passion!",
    ["Dialogue630441101"]="You shouldn't judge others by their family name... Look into my eyes. You'll find I'm different from other Wigners.",
    ["Dialogue630451101"]="Obeaune look to ocean waves while humans look to the stars, but emotions reflect the same in their eyes.",
    ["Dialogue630491101"]="You must have so many things you can't do yourself. It's alright. Come talk to me about it?",
    ["Dialogue630501101"]="The ocean is our greatest protector.",
    ["Dialogue630511101"]="(Tail wagging incessantly.)",
    ["Dialogue630521101"]="Leona said human males aren't as handsome as male Obeaune. Is that true?",
    ["Dialogue630531101"]="Bloop, bloop! Seagrass stewed pearls!",
    ["Dialogue630541101"]="Dad said mommy went far far away to explore another ocean... Since then, he always worries I'll leave him too, but why would I do that?",
    ["Dialogue630551101"]="Have you heard of braised crab, drunken crab, and spicy crab? I really want to know... what kind of Vadon are they?",
    ["Dialogue630561101"]="People tend to fear the unknown, yet still yearn for its fantasy. Just like how a Obeaune longs for the land and sky while clinging to the reefs.",
    ["Dialogue630581101"]="Is there a more peaceful way to live than gazing upon the mountains and rivers, enriching one's mind, and cultivating one's soul? ^-^",
    ["Dialogue630591101"]="Sigh, those days of tranquility feel like they happened only yesterday...",
    ["Dialogue630601101"]="*Cries*",
    ["Dialogue630611101"]="... (Staring at you unhappily.)",
    ["Dialogue630621101"]="...H-have you seen my dad?",
    ["Dialogue630631101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue630641101"]="I don't want to forget my pain, because that pain... allows me to remember who I am.",
    ["Dialogue630651101"]="Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue630661101"]="(Bouncing restlessly.)",
    ["Dialogue630671101"]="Sometimes, faith does not originate from one's duty, but from one's love for the land and all that exists upon it.",
    ["Dialogue630681101"]="I wonder... What has become of the world outside this cave...?",
    ["Dialogue630691101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue630701101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue630741101"]="Don't talk to me while I'm on duty!",
    ["Dialogue630751101"]="A knight of the Royal Chivalry must have courage and decorum at all times.",
    ["Dialogue630761101"]="The Darkness will never fade away.",
    ["Dialogue630781101"]="Have you seen... anything shiny nearby, gob?",
    ["Dialogue630801101"]="The Darkness will never fade away.",
    ["Dialogue630821101"]="Live life with your head raised high or die with it lowered.",
    ["Dialogue630841101"]="The word \"Jofar\" in the orc language means resolute. May the boy grow up to be like his father.",
    ["Dialogue630851101"]="I have seen too many people... who because they can't let go of anything aren't able to achieve anything.",
    ["Dialogue630901101"]="The glory of the past has perished, but the glory of our ancestors will always remain in our hearts.",
    ["Dialogue631081101"]="The recent weather changes on Izlude Island have been very unusual.",
    ["Dialogue631111101"]="I didn't plan to seal myself in alongside the Deviling when I was sealing it away. Something must be wrong with the spell!",
    ["Dialogue631121101"]="Next to my darling daughter, this mine is the only other thing most precious to me.",
    ["Dialogue631141101"]="I wish dad will let me see the world. Staying in Mjolnir Mountains all the time is super boring.",
    ["Dialogue631421101"]="Focus on survival before thinking about honor!",
    ["Dialogue631431101"]="Follow Chieftain Woofka's plan!",
    ["Dialogue631441101"]="The Kobolds were once very united. When will our present strife end?...",
    ["Dialogue631451101"]="Bones and territory are the most important things.",
    ["Dialogue631461101"]="Endless internal unrest will only make the clan lose confidence in the future.",
    ["Dialogue631481101"]="I... I will become the second Kobold God!",
    ["Dialogue631491101"]="We will eventually move on from the past. Fortunately, we can look forward to the future.",
    ["Dialogue631501101"]="(The roots of the vines make a crunchy, eerie sound.)",
    ["Dialogue631511101"]="Death is but the opening of another door to the truth.",
    ["Dialogue631521101"]="Time may not be able to heal all wounds, but it can give people the courage to let go and forgive!",
    ["Dialogue631621101"]="May all sins be forgiven one day.",
    ["Dialogue631641101"]="The dead can no longer be persecuted. Let the past rest in silence, forever...",
    ["Dialogue631651101"]="(The Bloody Knight silently stares at you. Silence wins over sound.)",
    ["Dialogue631661101"]="Who else can stand against me!? My dynasty is truly without equal!",
    ["Dialogue631671101"]="Quickly! Move it!",
    ["Dialogue631711101"]="*huff* I can't... go on...",
    ["Dialogue631721101"]="If I don't finish my work, I'll be whipped again tomorrow...",
    ["Dialogue631731101"]="When will these dark days come to an end...?",
    ["Dialogue631741101"]="(The old piano is covered in dust. Perhaps it was valuable in the past, but now, there is nobody to even repair the missing keys...)",
    ["Dialogue631751101"]="Help... H-Help me...",
    ["Dialogue631771101"]="(The dining table is a mess with only a flickering candle on it...)",
    ["Dialogue631791101"]="(The statue of the knight standing in front of you is quite lifelike. There seems to be a gaze that can discern truth beneath the armor.)",
    ["Dialogue631811101"]="I will forever follow the faith in my heart and protect the prosperity of this dynasty!",
    ["Dialogue631881101"]="By the glory of the knights, I will protect the people.",
    ["Dialogue631891101"]="My prey never escapes my grasp!",
    ["Dialogue631901101"]="Kindness and sincerity—these are the most precious treasures.",
    ["Dialogue632091101"]="(The old, broken boiler is covered in rust and crackles as steam flows out. It seems like it could fall apart any second.)",
    ["Dialogue632191101"]="All travelers are making their journey home.",
    ["Dialogue632201101"]="At risk? That's right. Only un-adventurous businesses lose money.",
    ["Dialogue632361101"]="Of course, the work of the guard is tiring... But it's not painful.",
    ["Dialogue632381101"]="Al De Baran’s business is my business.",
    ["Dialogue632421101"]="No one is able to completely block out dark thoughts.",
    ["Dialogue632571101"]="I..... where am I? Where's my brother.....?",
    ["Dialogue632591101"]="I just want to be Aaron's hero.",
    ["Dialogue632631101"]="Never allow yourself to go hungry. Hunger always goes hand in hand with sadness.",
    ["Dialogue632641101"]="The fish drift with the waves... What do people drift with?",
    ["Dialogue632651101"]="Believe me, life needs a little surprise every now and then~",
    ["Dialogue632721101"]="Depend on your battle companions? Joking, I only trust in my own weapons.",
    ["Dialogue633061101"]="One piece of ore makes 80 Zeny. If I could collect 20 pieces a day, I'd be able to afford a house in Prontera in 110 years.",
    ["Dialogue633071101"]="I've seen many beautiful places. But none can compare to my homeland.",
    ["Dialogue633171101"]="Lady Alexia, I got urgent news!",
    ["Dialogue633181101"]="My sword is wielded for those who cannot fight.",
    ["Dialogue633521101"]="My Lady! Princess Cecilia is in trouble!",
    ["Dialogue633711101"]="The Utan tribe... Shall never go against the will of the Yggdrasil.",
    ["Dialogue633741101"]="There are all kinds of ways to make money, but the quickest way... Will always be taking it from other people's wallets!",
    ["Dialogue633751101"]="S-So hungry... *Sniffle*",
    ["Dialogue633761101"]="The way to take control of destiny... depends on nothing but yourself.",
    ["Dialogue633771101"]="The Mother Tree shines like the stars above! So long as you follow its guiding light, you shall never lose your way!",
    ["Dialogue633791101"]="Have you ever seen a flower bloom from ashes? That's exactly what hope looks like.",
    ["Dialogue633831101"]="(A breeze sets the leaves on its head rustling...)",
    ["Dialogue633861101"]="(The young Wootan chief doesn't seem fully awake. Its eyes are dull and lifeless, like dusty jewels...)",
    ["Dialogue633881101"]="I sacrifice this life in the name of Hel, Queen of the Underworld!",
    ["Dialogue633901101"]="The queen's bounty is as good as mine now!",
    ["Dialogue634041101"]="Mark my words... I shall take back all that belongs to me someday.",
    ["Dialogue634061101"]="May the beacon, which shall guide all into the new world... Be ignited with my own life.",
    ["Dialogue634141101"]="You want to live? Well, that's easy! You just have to die first!",
    ["Dialogue634171101"]="This isn't the time or the place to be loafing around, Adventurer! Chirp!",
    ["Dialogue634181101"]="Does faith serve to protect our souls... Or enslave them?",
    ["Dialogue634501101"]="Your dream and your responsibility always lie in different paths. That's why you need to make a decision.",
    ["Dialogue634541101"]="I've made up my mind to protect this city, for those I lost.",
    ["Dialogue634551101"]="Angelica... How can this be...?",
    ["Dialogue634561101"]="Sigh... No matter how handy a machine is, it's no comparison to a warm human heart.",
    ["Dialogue634601101"]="It's my duty to protect the city.",
    ["Dialogue634681101"]="No time to waste!",
    ["Dialogue634761101"]="What's going on?",
    ["Dialogue634771101"]="As a Republic investigator, I must get to the bottom of this!",
    ["Dialogue634791101"]="Welcome to Kiel Khayr's Estate, my honored guest. I wish you a wonderful night.",
    ["Dialogue634861101"]="...A problem? If money can fix it, it's not a problem.",
    ["Dialogue634931101"]="Like a coin with its two sides, luck too swings both ways.",
    ["Dialogue635031101"]="Advancement comes with a cost, and I've long prepared for it.",
    ["Dialogue635051101"]="(The enormous transmitter unit is covered with a variety of sophisticated instruments, overwhelming everyone...)",
    ["Dialogue635061101"]="(The enormous transmitter unit is covered with a variety of sophisticated instruments, overwhelming everyone...)",
    ["Dialogue635071101"]="My job is to be the bridge that connects the past and the future.",
    ["Dialogue635081101"]="To me, all the people fall into two categories — those willing to die for me and those destined to die by my hand.",
    ["Dialogue635181101"]="The food ingredients here are the freshest!",
    ["Dialogue635211101"]="One day, I'll become the most renowned Adventurer on this land!",
    ["Dialogue635271101"]="Weird... Where did all those monsters come from?",
    ["Dialogue635281101"]="Weird... Where did all those monsters come from?",
    ["Dialogue635361101"]="(You've got a mini comm device hidden in your ear; just tap it to chat with Philodis...)",
    ["Dialogue635401101"]="This world should have an ending as beautiful as a fairy tale.",
    ["Dialogue635411101"]="Dad promised to take me to the ocean and the desert once I'm better! Just wondering when I'll be better...",
    ["Dialogue635471101"]="For Nina... I'd do anything.",
    ["Dialogue635481101"]="... If anyone had a choice, who'd want to stay in this dump?",
    ["Dialogue635491101"]="Help... I can't breathe—",
    ["Dialogue635501101"]="Cough, cough...",
    ["Dialogue635511101"]="This... this is the medicine rich people use...",
    ["Dialogue635581101"]="Hello, cute little guest. Please open your mouth. It's time for today's check-up.",
    ["Dialogue635591101"]="If you can't seize the present, you shouldn't talk about the future.",
    ["Dialogue635661101"]="Everything in this world has a price, including your life.",
    ["Dialogue635671101"]="People always say you'll be left behind if you don't move with the times. But my old bones just can't keep up...",
    ["Dialogue635681101"]="(The inactive admin robots are lying on the ground, only their power light blinking slowly...)",
    ["Dialogue635881101"]="Step right up—don't miss out! Best Cloud Soufflé in all of Juno—",
    ["Dialogue635941101"]="(With a courteous nod and a cheerful glint in his eyes, the blond young man greets you.)",
    ["Dialogue636021101"]="Even surviving... is a luxury.",
    ["Dialogue636031101"]="Mom always says that living each day to the fullest is what matters most!",
    ["Dialogue636051101"]="Business is simply about mutual needs.",
    ["Dialogue636141101"]="Though I was born in darkness... one day, they will bring me the dawn.",
    ["Dialogue636161101"]="Even the frailest of wings... dreams of holding up the sky for millions who believe.",
    ["Dialogue636181101"]="We can't alter the past—but the future is still full of choices.",
    ["Dialogue636191101"]="In the end... we all return to the Goddess.",
    ["Dialogue636231101"]="Would you like to join Lulu for a game?",
    ["Dialogue636251101"]="Dad keeps pushing alchemy on me, but I want to be a hero—just like Rossin!",
    ["Dialogue636261101"]="Time is fair to all, and so is knowledge.",
    ["Dialogue636281101"]="Sniff... those scary men... they are here again...",
    ["Dialogue636291101"]="Do you know about Pope Isumia? It's said her Heron's Feather can make any dream come true...",
    ["Dialogue636331101"]="Green is my favorite color... But it's a rare sight in the desert...",
    ["Dialogue636671101"]="(The silent gaze rests upon you—eyes full of sorrow, as though grieving for all creation...)",
    ["Dialogue636741101"]="If you have no solid proof, I will hold you accountable for slander!",
    ["Dialogue636761101"]="Hah, just one side of the story? How could it be trusted?",
    ["Dialogue636781101"]="O Goddess, please... forgive us...!",
    ["Dialogue636941101"]="Gilded Rose always delivers!",
    ["Dialogue640011101"]="My dad hopes that I'll become \"thick as thieves\" with the other kids on the island, but... I think it's wrong to steal...",
    ["Dialogue640021101"]="...This house is my everything.",
    ["Dialogue640031101"]="There's always something exciting happening in Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue640041101"]="...If you wish to consult me, please make an appointment with my attendant. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue640051101"]="How may I serve your majesty?",
    ["Dialogue640061101"]="...Go away.",
    ["Dialogue640071101"]="What do I think about my two elder brothers? Hmm... They're my family! ^-^",
    ["Dialogue640081101"]="Hehe... Are you my next quarry?",
    ["Dialogue640091101"]="Doing business with the Wigner Group practically guarantees profits!",
    ["Dialogue640101101"]="... (Looking at you without saying a word.)",
    ["Dialogue640111101"]="There's always something exciting happening in Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue640121101"]="...If you wish to consult me, please make an appointment with my attendant. Thank you.",
    ["Dialogue640131101"]="How may I serve your majesty?",
    ["Dialogue640141101"]="I would serve the Richard Family for the rest of my life.",
    ["Dialogue640151101"]="Wow, I really envy you... I've always wanted to live a life of freedom, traveling around the world!",
    ["Dialogue640161101"]="... (Eyes narrow suspiciously.)",
    ["Dialogue640171101"]="Compared to the interests of the Kingdom, family affairs are merely trifling matters.",
    ["Dialogue640181101"]="Compared to the interests of the Kingdom, family affairs are merely trifling matters.",
    ["Dialogue640191101"]="(Leisurely chewing on grass...)",
    ["Dialogue640201101"]="It's our duty to guard Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue640211101"]="Buzz! Buzz!",
    ["Dialogue640221101"]="(Crackling and popping while it burns.)",
    ["Dialogue640231101"]="(Buzzing weakly.)",
    ["Dialogue640241101"]="My destiny was decided from the day I was born...",
    ["Dialogue640251101"]="(You have a strong hunch that nothing good will come from actually knowing what he's mumbling about...)",
    ["Dialogue640261101"]="...For the tribe's future.",
    ["Dialogue640271101"]="(You have a strong hunch that nothing good will come from actually knowing what he's mumbling about...)",
    ["Dialogue640281101"]="(You have a strong hunch that nothing good will come from actually knowing what he's mumbling about...)",
    ["Dialogue640291101"]="(You have a strong hunch that nothing good will come from actually knowing what he's mumbling about...)",
    ["Dialogue640301101"]="Pitiful humans... Taste the might of the underworld!",
    ["Dialogue640311101"]="The fate of the people of the desert are my own!",
    ["Dialogue640321101"]="*Whistle!*",
    ["Dialogue640331101"]="I never grow tired of excavating the ruins. I find something better than before every time!",
    ["Dialogue640341101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue640351101"]="I wield this sword only for Master Kahn.",
    ["Dialogue640361101"]="Even the goddess of destiny would be willing to marry me once I earn a few more millions. Probably. Heh, heh!",
    ["Dialogue640371101"]="Captain Kahn once said his passion for sailing would be a fraction of what it is without my cooking!",
    ["Dialogue640381101"]="... (Frowning)",
    ["Dialogue640391101"]="Everything I do... I do for Morroc!",
    ["Dialogue640401101"]="Everything I do... I do for Morroc!",
    ["Dialogue640411101"]="*Wails* Big brother is all I have left...",
    ["Dialogue640421101"]="Success comes with backbreaking work and determination!",
    ["Dialogue640431101"]="Archeology is always full of surprises!",
    ["Dialogue640441101"]="Shh... Before you wake the dead around here.",
    ["Dialogue640451101"]="None can solve my riddles!",
    ["Dialogue640461101"]="Popo... Pori, pori!",
    ["Dialogue640471101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue640481101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue640491101"]="Welcome to the Mage Guild.",
    ["Dialogue640521101"]="Ahh...! Why is the weather out at sea as fickle as a maiden's heart?",
    ["Dialogue640531101"]="Have you ever stood at the bow of a ship at sunset, lit a cigarette, and watched the sun go down?",
    ["Dialogue640541101"]="First officer Rudolph always praises me for my good eyesight, but lately I feel like the things near me are becoming blurry...",
    ["Dialogue640551101"]="A life without purpose is like sailing without a compass.",
    ["Dialogue640561101"]="I think becoming a sailor is every man's dream.",
    ["Dialogue640571101"]="My desire for freedom will be the wind in my sails. One day, it'll take me to the other side of the horizon!",
    ["Dialogue640581101"]="Why do humans think the ocean cold and merciless? Can't they see the gentle love in each ocean wave?",
    ["Dialogue640591101"]="Why do humans think the ocean cold and merciless? Can't they see the gentle love in each ocean wave?",
    ["Dialogue640611101"]="I may look like Baroshev, but my strength is nothing like his. That's why I'm nothing more than his substitute...",
    ["Dialogue640631101"]="The six instructors of Criatura Academy were once famous adventurers. All their adventures are recorded in the Criatura Academy Chronicles.",
    ["Dialogue640651101"]="Chivalry means fame and glory are little more than fleeting ideas best left to drunken tales in a tavern.",
    ["Dialogue640661101"]="Everyone has a duty to make money, but it must be done with honesty.",
    ["Dialogue640671101"]="Oh! Master Jurgen's good looks are far too dashing and radiant! I can't stare at him for more than three seconds!",
    ["Dialogue640681101"]="...Ngh, please don't speak to me... I can't seem to focus or think when I'm near Master Jurgen...",
    ["Dialogue640691101"]="Oh, to hear Master Jurgen speak is like listening to a most lovely smooth melody!",
    ["Dialogue640701101"]="Everything I do is for Master Jurgen!",
    ["Dialogue640721101"]="I'm fortunate to always be able to meet such kind and lovely people in this vast world!",
    ["Dialogue640731101"]="To always see the good in the world is, in itself, a talent.",
    ["Dialogue640761101"]="Life is bound inextricably by cause and effect. All things are but a fleeting dream, like the shadow of a bubble. It can be as fickle as fading mist and change as suddenly as a bolt of lightning.",
    ["Dialogue640781101"]="(The Horong bounces about irritably.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue640791101"]="Mgh, please stop staring at me... Is there something on my face?",
    ["Dialogue640801101"]="Mgh, please stop staring at me... Is there something on my face?",
    ["Dialogue640811101"]="Time waits for no man. A thousand years is but a twinkling of an eye...",
    ["Dialogue640821101"]="(The Horong writhes in pain.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue640831101"]="I wonder... What has become of the world outside this cave...?",
    ["Dialogue640841101"]="(The Horong sways impatiently.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue640851101"]="If I could just see Payon one last time... Haha, what a foolish pipe dream!",
    ["Dialogue640911101"]="I would never do anything that goes against my master's teaching.",
    ["Dialogue640931101"]="It's tragic that we met at such an inopportune time...",
    ["Dialogue640951101"]="I'm but a victim of fate's meddling too...",
    ["Dialogue640991101"]="I wanna grow up quickly so I can take care of mom!",
    ["Dialogue641021101"]="I wanna grow up quickly so I can take care of mom!",
    ["Dialogue641031101"]="Sigh... When will this famine end...?",
    ["Dialogue641041101"]="There's no way flowers from a greenhouse can be as dazzling as a poisonous rose in muddy ground.",
    ["Dialogue641091101"]="Hey! Less talk, more action!",
    ["Dialogue641101101"]="...No one knows Master Nithil better than I do!",
    ["Dialogue641121101"]="...Well, bloop, what else do you want to hear?",
    ["Dialogue641161101"]="My master once said that honesty is the rarest wisdom.",
    ["Dialogue641171101"]="The mediocre feel threatened by one another, while the talented cherish each other!",
    ["Dialogue641181101"]="...Hmm, have you seen my staff?",
    ["Dialogue641191101"]="Time may not be able to heal all wounds, but it can give people the courage to let go and forgive!",
    ["Dialogue641211101"]="Forgetting the past is an act of betrayal.",
    ["Dialogue641281101"]="Enduring eternal loneliness is a fair price for attaining eternal life.",
    ["Dialogue641291101"]="Varied styles and gorgeous colors, mix them together and bam! That's fashion!",
    ["Dialogue641301101"]="If only there was magic that could fix my old bones...",
    ["Dialogue641311101"]="Ugh, strong and fierce women... are so sexy!",
    ["Dialogue641331101"]="...Living but dead inside. You ever felt that way before?",
    ["Dialogue641351101"]="Bones and territory are the most important things!",
    ["Dialogue641371101"]="Advanced magic is simple compared to understanding people's emotions...",
    ["Dialogue641381101"]="We mustn't miss our opportunity when a fat sheep falls into our lap!",
    ["Dialogue641391101"]="My herbs are only for the most distinguished of guests. You should see a philanthropist if you're penniless!",
    ["Dialogue641461101"]="Kindness is the most important quality.",
    ["Dialogue641471101"]="I always remember the kindness I received from others.",
    ["Dialogue641481101"]="Even the desert can't stop us from loving life.",
    ["Dialogue641491101"]="When I grow up, I want to be a heroine like Goldie!",
    ["Dialogue641561101"]="*Cries* Nobody is allowed to bully Goldie!",
    ["Dialogue641571101"]="Although life is not good in the desert, it's a place where warm and true feelings exist.",
    ["Dialogue641581101"]="There's no such thing as an absolutely good or absolutely bad person in this world.",
    ["Dialogue641601101"]="My understanding of dimensional gaps is that they are like... finding chocolate hazelnuts in a strawberry-filled pastry!",
    ["Dialogue641611101"]="Sniff... Sniff... Arlene won't play with me.",
    ["Dialogue641621101"]="If you see any strange monster footprints, please contact me immediately.",
    ["Dialogue641631101"]="Meeeow, meeeow.",
    ["Dialogue641641101"]="I don't care whatever reasoning you have. Show me the proof if you want to persuade me.",
    ["Dialogue641651101"]="Our merchant group's products are top of the line!",
    ["Dialogue641661101"]="I can't accept anyone doubting the quality of our goods.",
    ["Dialogue641671101"]="Ordinary goods cannot compare to those from Cat Hand Services.",
    ["Dialogue641681101"]="For the Chamber of Commerce and peace in the city, the plan to destroy the Goblins is imperative!",
    ["Dialogue641691101"]="Every living thing has its reason for existence. No one can decide the future of a species.",
    ["Dialogue641701101"]="When I say I'll travel around the world, I'm not saying it just for the fun of it.",
    ["Dialogue641791101"]="Things people mention all the time like faith and reputation mean nothing in the face of life and death.",
    ["Dialogue641811101"]="Hmph... Only those who pray with piety shall receive divine protection...",
    ["Dialogue641821101"]="Hmm. I'm just trying to survive...",
    ["Dialogue641841101"]="Please... I've been starving for three days...",
    ["Dialogue641871101"]="So that my friends can live on together, I will become stronger...",
    ["Dialogue641951101"]="My grandpa is the greatest outfit designer in all of Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue641961101"]="0",
    ["Dialogue641971101"]="0",
    ["Dialogue641981101"]="What? You're asking me who's cuter between Connie and Talia? I-I...",
    ["Dialogue642021101"]="Adventurer, I heard that you will be attending Princess Veronica's wedding ceremony, can you tell me about it? It must be a wedding ceremony that all women covet, right?",
    ["Dialogue642031101"]="Eh... Being a noble's daughter must be so boring! Hair must be neat, dress must not be messy... How can you train like that?",
    ["Dialogue642041101"]="Hello, Adventurer. Sorry if my sister has troubled you. As an apology, I'd like to make some tea for you. How's some Earl Grey sound?",
    ["Dialogue642101101"]="I've followed Prince Eigen for many years... Of course this is Master Ian's order.",
    ["Dialogue642111101"]="(The surface of the coffin looks ancient and gives off a very strange, horrible stench.)",
    ["Dialogue642121101"]="(Around the array, a bright light appears... It appears to be waiting...)",
    ["Dialogue642161101"]="*sigh* I should have taught him better...",
    ["Dialogue642201101"]="I... I don't wanna be left behind... Dad... Where are you...?",
    ["Dialogue642221101"]="If you want to verify historical truths, you need to speak with evidence!",
    ["Dialogue642231101"]="Murder is the worst way to deal with any problem.",
    ["Dialogue642241101"]="Murder is the worst way to deal with any problem.",
    ["Dialogue642251101"]="One day, I'll become the most amazing scholar in the Eden Group!",
    ["Dialogue642261101"]="The joy of archaeology lies in uncovering hidden truths!",
    ["Dialogue642271101"]="Being kind to your enemy is being cruel to yourself.",
    ["Dialogue642291101"]="If rules are never broken, humanity will never make progress.",
    ["Dialogue642331101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue642341101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue642351101"]="......",
    ["Dialogue642371101"]="Never underestimate the utility of wisdom!",
    ["Dialogue642381101"]="The most precious gemstones must be appraised by only the most astute experts.",
    ["Dialogue642511101"]="(...The prince's eyes are closed. He seems to be being tortured by an unknown curse...)",
    ["Dialogue642551101"]="Every encounter is a gift of fate.",
    ["Dialogue642561101"]="A warm heart is worth cherishing a lot more than a fabricated appearance.",
    ["Dialogue642611101"]="In his position, seek his governance, do his duty.",
    ["Dialogue642651101"]="I'm always waiting for a chance.",
    ["Dialogue642661101"]="When is justice right or wrong? It's just a different perspective.",
    ["Dialogue642671101"]="(the tamed mummy has a nice face and the eyes under the bandage seem to sparkle with a pink heart...)",
    ["Dialogue642681101"]="Hmm... how much food can I get from today's mining haul?",
    ["Dialogue642691101"]="In this barren desert, even stomach half full is a luxury.",
    ["Dialogue642701101"]="The wolves gave me everything. They will always be my family.",
    ["Dialogue642721101"]="I hope everything I do from now on can become the cornerstone of the city’s progress.",
    ["Dialogue642731101"]="Some people like to keep secrets, while others like to search for the truth.",
    ["Dialogue642741101"]="Don't listen to Waldon's nonsense! Everything I said is a true recount.",
    ["Dialogue642751101"]="He is the hero of the bedtime story, responsible for guarding the dreams of all children.",
    ["Dialogue642761101"]="The stage is like a microcosm of life. What role do you play in it?",
    ["Dialogue642771101"]="Oh, Ho ~ let me reveal to you the beauty of my muscular form~",
    ["Dialogue642781101"]="The woman in my heart, she is like a beautiful rose in full bloom~",
    ["Dialogue642791101"]="Even if I could go back in time, I have no regrets or hesitations.",
    ["Dialogue642801101"]="(she looks at you silently with no waves in her eyes...)",
    ["Dialogue642811101"]="Alchemy is not magic. Our power comes from the awe and respect for all things in the world.",
    ["Dialogue642821101"]="Truth and illusion depend on each other, and I am the only truth.",
    ["Dialogue642831101"]="I hope our story... Will never end.",
    ["Dialogue642841101"]="It's not sad that I was taken down a bad path..... I never had a clear path to follow.",
    ["Dialogue642851101"]="Your Majesty's wish is my wish.",
    ["Dialogue642861101"]="No one can question my loyalty to his majesty.",
    ["Dialogue642881101"]="I would like to offer everything for the kingdom.",
    ["Dialogue642891101"]="For a patrolman, no news is the best news.",
    ["Dialogue642901101"]="Al De Baran still has many shortcomings... But I am willing to adapt with it.",
    ["Dialogue642911101"]="The law alone is far from enough to maintain a fairn and just society",
    ["Dialogue642981101"]="(The statue of the god standing before you looks stern and solemn. Its lowered eyes seem to shine with a ghostly light...)",
    ["Dialogue643111101"]="(the members of the mission fell asleep and seemed unaware of your arrival...)",
    ["Dialogue643261101"]="Some people like to keep secrets, while others like to search for the truth.",
    ["Dialogue643331101"]="I need help over here! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue643361101"]="Odin, why do these terrible things happen to me.....?",
    ["Dialogue643371101"]="Odin, thank you for your kindness",
    ["Dialogue643491101"]="Everyone is equal in the face of death and disease.",
    ["Dialogue643501101"]="There are no unsolvable puzzles in the world, only fools who cannot find the answers~",
    ["Dialogue643731101"]="Human desire is the most delicious food in all the world.",
    ["Dialogue643961101"]="H-Help... Please h-help... me...",
    ["Dialogue644041101"]="An adventure starts with dreams and friends.",
    ["Dialogue644051101"]="Your humble servant at your service!",
    ["Dialogue644071101"]="If this world does not have justice, I will become justice.",
    ["Dialogue644101101"]="Good wine, good food, and good music make the perfect day.",
    ["Dialogue644131101"]="A pirate should spend his life at sea. No island can keep a pirate tethered to dry land.",
    ["Dialogue644171101"]="Our line of business comes with risks. Shush, be careful.",
    ["Dialogue644181101"]="As a fully qualified pirate, let me tell you: What's yours is mine, and what's mine is still mine!",
    ["Dialogue644201101"]="There are strangers in the forest. I hope they leave soon.",
    ["Dialogue644241101"]="Doyle, someday you will never be able to leave me...",
    ["Dialogue644371101"]="That boy will get his comeuppance one day...",
    ["Dialogue644391101"]="Oh! I thought it was Doyley! Hello!",
    ["Dialogue644411101"]="No man can compare to good booze and the sea. Get that straight.",
    ["Dialogue644421101"]="Doyle is the blessed child of the God of Music! Doyle is the spirit of the flowers!",
    ["Dialogue644431101"]="Party drinks are to be enjoyed with the ones you love.",
    ["Dialogue644441101"]="I wanna take a bath in all the beer in Comodo, hehehehe!",
    ["Dialogue644451101"]="You should know the person standing before you is the future Pirate King: Mottle!",
    ["Dialogue644461101"]="Beep boop!",
    ["Dialogue644491101"]="No hesitation. To start on something is always meaningful. Just do it.",
    ["Dialogue644501101"]="Once you've seen Barbara perform, you'll understand. She's the epitome of perfection.",
    ["Dialogue644511101"]="I will become the brightest star in the universe.",
    ["Dialogue644521101"]="You can always see fireworks in Comodo during festivals!",
    ["Dialogue644531101"]="One thing shared by all stories is that they eventually come to an end.",
    ["Dialogue644541101"]="Why do people not tell the truth when they're sober, but chose to speak the truth when they're drunk?",
    ["Dialogue644551101"]="... Bar... bara... My... My friend...",
    ["Dialogue644911101"]="I can't die in a place like this. I still don't know anything about this world's true situation...",
    ["Dialogue644921101"]="Where's mom... I want mom...",
    ["Dialogue644931101"]="Has anyone seen my child?!",
    ["Dialogue644941101"]="The outside world is definitely many many times bigger than what's within these walls!",
    ["Dialogue644951101"]="No matter who, I will stop them from killing Eren. Other than that, I don't need any reason.",
    ["Dialogue644971101"]="(The tall ape-like man looks quietly at the walls of Prontera, with nothingness and indifference in his eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue644991101"]="This is what I have always believed, and I believe the most effective way to discipline someone is through pain.",
    ["Dialogue645021101"]="Curse you... You won't get a single word out of me!",
    ["Dialogue645031101"]="Prince Aronst always said that he wanted nothing more than to become a normal person...",
    ["Dialogue645041101"]="Pain is the privilege of the living! Have you ever seen a dead person cry out in pain?",
    ["Dialogue645051101"]="I swore to Odin I would pledge my eternal allegiance to my king.",
    ["Dialogue645061101"]="You will need to hand over your weapons before entering the palace. Those are the rules, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue645071101"]="Sorry, the banquet is still being prepared. Thank you for your patience!",
    ["Dialogue645081101"]="Sorry, the banquet is still being prepared. Thank you for your patience!",
    ["Dialogue645091101"]="... I have already chosen my path.",
    ["Dialogue645111101"]="One day, I will be Master Jesqurienne's favorite student!",
    ["Dialogue645151101"]="Murder is the worst way to deal with any problem.",
    ["Dialogue645681101"]="Welcome to Prontera! Please present your Adventurer's Handbook!",
    ["Dialogue645691101"]="A man without morals is not fit to be the king's successor!",
    ["Dialogue645701101"]="It's better to deal the cards rather than have them be dealt to you.",
    ["Dialogue645711101"]="Death is inevitable, so which should I choose? To die in depression... Or to go out with a bang?",
    ["Dialogue645911101"]="A tombstone with no name engraved upon it, seems to record an unknown event.",
    ["Dialogue645941101"]="Niflheim is our home! Let's all take good care of it!",
    ["Dialogue645951101"]="So long as there is light in my heart, I shall never fear the darkness.",
    ["Dialogue645961101"]="Even the weak should have a chance to live...",
    ["Dialogue645971101"]="Even the smallest embers of kindness... Can grow into a blazing, life-sustaining fire.",
    ["Dialogue645981101"]="Should I fall into the abyss, then let this world fall with me...",
    ["Dialogue645991101"]="From this moment on... I, Aronst, would no longer be me.",
    ["Dialogue646001101"]="Niflheim is our home! Let's all take good care of it!",
    ["Dialogue6463401"]="For Rogues, their turf is their home.",
    ["Dialogue6463701"]="The sea breeze in the port will eventually turn into a sandstorm.",
    ["Dialogue646401101"]="如果我可以，登上那舞台……",
    ["Dialogue646411101"]="追逐我们的梦想，但不必强求实现……",
    ["Dialogue646821101"]="My way of martial art needs no explanation.",
    ["Dialogue646841101"]="(The Mysterious Device's antenna spins round and round as if waiting for your input...)",
    ["Dialogue647051101"]="It... is... nice... to... meet... you...",
    ["Dialogue647061101"]="Get lost. I have no interest in human bodies.",
    ["Dialogue647211101"]="To present everyone with the best show, Nenna's dream it is!",
    ["Dialogue647541101"]="Every single word of my script, Enchulo Kasen's script, is worth a FORTUNE!",
    ["Dialogue647551101"]="Inferior desires are only held by inferior beings.",
    ["Dialogue647561101"]="The job of a scholar is to visualize abstract things, not the other way around.",
    ["Dialogue647571101"]="Stop hiding yourself in the Ivory Tower! How about going on fieldwork with me?",
    ["Dialogue647581101"]="To learn knowledge is to reason with others; to practice martial art is to make those unreasonable—reason with you.",
    ["Dialogue647591101"]="Speak up, Adventurer. I need to go home and prepare dinner for my kids.",
    ["Dialogue647601101"]="Dad, Mom...? Hmm... What's that? I only know my teachers and the dean...",
    ["Dialogue647611101"]="Some said up in the sky, there are infinite food and robots that will never break... Is that true?",
    ["Dialogue647621101"]="Stop crying. If you want something back, go get it yourself!",
    ["Dialogue647631101"]="The boundless sky is beautiful, but the land is where life nurtures.",
    ["Dialogue647731101"]="There is a labyrinth inside every heart.",
    ["Dialogue647751101"]="Time wears down the soul, but love mends it.",
    ["Dialogue647761101"]="I know someone is waiting, but I have forgotten who.",
    ["Dialogue647811101"]="Only the ideal is immortal following twilight.",
    ["Dialogue647861101"]="Live your life today before thinking about tomorrow.",
    ["Dialogue647901101"]="An excellent hunter will not let anything slip away. Shh, listen, something is coming.",
    ["Dialogue647911101"]="The giant robot sits alone at the roadside, its empty eyes shimmering with a faint blue glow...",
    ["Dialogue647921101"]="I don't trust anyone... Except for me, right?",
    ["Dialogue647961101"]="The giant robot sits alone at the roadside, its empty eyes shimmering with a faint blue glow...",
    ["Dialogue648001101"]=" As all stars move in harmony, all beings are set for their destinies. ",
    ["Dialogue648011101"]="Never point your gun at your comrades. This is an order!",
    ["Dialogue648131101"]="I will always yearn for a final bullet that grants me eternal rest.",
    ["Dialogue648181101"]="Life is like flowing water, and emotions are like falling petals.",
    ["Dialogue648191101"]="Shame washed away by glory, I shall never make the same mistake twice.",
    ["Dialogue648281101"]="Suck up the sorrow, chew on the grief, humans, give me more!",
    ["Dialogue648441101"]="Both letting go and bearing the burden hurt just as much.",
    ["Dialogue648451101"]="If I hadn't survived, would everyone else have lived?",
    ["Dialogue648601101"]="Why even think about tomorrow when you can't even get through today?",
    ["Dialogue648621101"]="A wise seller never asks for the buyer's purpose.",
    ["Dialogue648631101"]="Would you turn down Zeny? I sure wouldn't.",
    ["Dialogue648681101"]="Understanding the true essence of martial arts in the midst of extreme hardship is a step towards rising from the flames anew.",
    ["Dialogue648921101"]="If you liked our service, don't forget to leave a good review!",
    ["Dialogue649021101"]="May the Goddess Freyja bless my business with prosperity and success!",
    ["Dialogue649031101"]="Do you have anything to say to Aisha?",
    ["Dialogue649091101"]="The sands of time bury all... but I exist to excavate the truths hidden beneath them.",
    ["Dialogue649111101"]="Isumia... Isumia...",
    ["Dialogue649241101"]="Be practical, be truthful—that's how it should be.",
    ["Dialogue6492711"]="We nomads don't settle down. We belong to nature.",
    ["Dialogue649301101"]="Who dares to trespass into the lair of dragons?!",
    ["Dialogue649351101"]="The pain of losing my loved ones—I don't want to endure it a second time...",
    ["Dialogue649361101"]="Would you hear the symphony of the Underworld? Beneath the Gjoll, the wailing of lost souls never ceases.",
    ["Dialogue649371101"]="Even death itself bows before me.",
    ["Dialogue649391101"]="Even riches beyond measure... can't buy back the time that's gone.",
    ["Dialogue649401101"]="Even riches beyond measure... can't buy back the time that's gone.",
    ["Dialogue649411101"]="(Bzzzt—) Welcome to Alpha Manor.",
    ["Dialogue649421101"]="Barr Venter",
    ["Dialogue649431101"]="Juno Airship Office at your service.",
    ["Dialogue649481101"]="No cash, no mercenaries.",
    ["Dialogue649541101"]="Hmm... let me see if there's any mail for you...",
    ["Dialogue649791101"]="There are more challenges ahead, but I won't stop moving forward.",
    ["Dialogue649821101"]="We need more herbs.",
    ["Dialogue649821201"]="My loyalty belongs only to Captain Drake.",
    ["Dialogue649821301"]="We're in charge of guarding the camp.",
    ["Dialogue649821401"]="With Goldie gone, I'm the boss around here.",
    ["Dialogue649852101"]="When will I finally become a reliable grown-up...?",
    ["Dialogue649862101"]="What... will the future even look like?",
    ["Dialogue649872101"]="I'll definitely become the best knight ever.",
    ["Dialogue650021101"]="(A Crow's feather? Maybe there are more clues lying around...)",
    ["Dialogue650031101"]="(Another Crow's feather! There's no mistake! The Crow must have flown off in this direction.)",
    ["Dialogue650031102"]="(There's a Crow Feather... Does it belong to the crow that was here just now? If I trace these marks... God knows I may even find the Halo!)",
    ["Dialogue650041101"]="(There's a cliff up ahead. A Crow can fly, so that means...)",
    ["Dialogue650041102"]="(There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cliff</color> not far away from here that seems like a perfect fit for a bird's habitat. I heard crows love bringing <color=#CA2E0AFF>sparkling</color> stuff back to their nest, maybe...?)",
    ["Dialogue650771101"]="(This set of footprints look like they came from a large monster. Could they have been left by an Eclipse?)",
    ["Dialogue650781101"]="(The Backpack is empty. Not a single blade of Durian Grass is left.)",
    ["Dialogue653381101"]="I beg you, kind Adventurer... Please help me...",
    ["Dialogue653571101"]="All things must wither and perish in time... You and I are no different.",
    ["Dialogue660111101"]="Click, clack… Click, Clack… Santa Claus, on a beautiful day like this, just left me here! I’m gonna sell all of his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elk Slingshots</color>! Click, clack…",
    ["Dialogue660131101"]="Ahem! I declare you a backup member of the Eden Guerilla Forces! As for whether you can be successfully promoted... That depends on how much Candy you can snatch back! Get ready to go, rookie!",
    ["Dialogue660141101"]="Hey! Check out my perfected slingshot skills!",
    ["Dialogue660161101"]="As, as long as it's Captain Altyna's order, I'm willing to follow it...",
    ["Dialogue670001101"]="♪ Who saw more than me? Who understands my sorrows? The moon, beautiful wine, and a lute. I'll hold her memories close at heart. ♪",
    ["Dialogue670011101"]="Master always said fishing would one day be as easy as catching fish with your bare hands once fisherman and fishing rod become one.",
    ["Dialogue670021101"]="They say if you make a wish at this fountain, you'll be able to meet The One. Is that true...?",
    ["Dialogue670031101"]="This farm can provide Prontera with a steady supply of food!",
    ["Dialogue670041101"]="This is where I earn my glory, and where the last curtain for the battle shall fall!",
    ["Dialogue670051101"]="Studying monster ecology is my life's pursuit!",
    ["Dialogue670061101"]="It's dangerous up ahead. Don't go any farther if you're not strong enough.",
    ["Dialogue670071101"]="The fundamentals of martial arts is to be one with your mind and body. That is how you strengthen both body and soul.",
    ["Dialogue670081101"]="We must stay alert and always guard against these enemies from below ground.",
    ["Dialogue670091101"]="The more dangerous an area, the better the business opportunities!",
    ["Dialogue670101101"]="So many secrets lie buried beneath my homeland!",
    ["Dialogue670111101"]="The ocean is my home!",
    ["Dialogue670121101"]="Boundless treasure lie within the ocean.",
    ["Dialogue670131101"]="The more dangerous places tend to hide the most hidden truths...",
    ["Dialogue670141101"]="The church isn't just the center for theology, it's also the center for medicine.",
    ["Dialogue670151101"]="Fashion is important! It's my duty to help women look even more beautiful!",
    ["Dialogue670151201"]="I'm sorry, you're too late. The flowers are all sold out today. Please come again tomorrow!",
    ["Dialogue670161101"]="Do you know how many delicacies there are in this world? No? Haha, I don't either!",
    ["Dialogue670161201"]="You want to know what happened after that story so many years ago? I'm sorry, youngin', but some tales aren't so easy to look back on. Sigh, if only that intel was accurate...",
    ["Dialogue670171101"]="(Reading intently.)",
    ["Dialogue670181101"]="For the glory of the Nerius Family!",
    ["Dialogue670191101"]="Ah! I want to try every delicacy from across the continent so much I dream about it...",
    ["Dialogue670201101"]="... (Stares at you.)",
    ["Dialogue670211101"]="Adventuring is a dangerous job that brings one far too close to death... I just got extremely lucky.",
    ["Dialogue670221101"]="Agh! Maina is making me so anxious!",
    ["Dialogue670231101"]="Every day, I record three kinds of fish and make a list. If you complete one of the three kinds of fish prints, or if the fish print is big enough, it will...",
    ["Dialogue670241101"]="No one will notice if I slack off for a bit, right...?",
    ["Dialogue670251101"]="What should my next song be... Ah! I got it! Inspiration has struck!",
    ["Dialogue670261101"]="This sewer is very dangerous! It's the best place to do business!",
    ["Dialogue670271101"]="Ordinary people have no idea how dangerous it is down here!",
    ["Dialogue670281101"]="Darn it, is this really all the strength I have...?",
    ["Dialogue670291101"]="Please, god, you can't let such a brilliant bard die here!",
    ["Dialogue670301101"]="Hahaha! It seems the gods have not forsaken me!",
    ["Dialogue670311101"]="The people of Eden Group can get a little too enthusiastic sometimes.",
    ["Dialogue670321101"]="I'm Ivan Lugenburg's knight, Arlene!",
    ["Dialogue670331101"]="Those... Those blasted fiends from the chivalry!",
    ["Dialogue670341101"]="A mysterious air of despair and hope surges through this land...",
    ["Dialogue670351101"]="I don't want to turn into a vampire!",
    ["Dialogue670361101"]="The wounded shall come inside. This way, please.",
    ["Dialogue670371101"]="The Golden Thief Bug's treasure belongs to Eden Group!",
    ["Dialogue670381101"]="I'm a merchant who's been practicing the Style of All-Mastery for a long time!",
    ["Dialogue670391101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue670401101"]="Food is the only thing in this world that will never let you down!",
    ["Dialogue670411101"]="I don't want to turn into a vampire!",
    ["Dialogue670611101"]="Yes? Would you like another glass? Or should I come take care of you for a little while?",
    ["Dialogue670651101"]="No one gets to eat until our training ends at nightfall!",
    ["Dialogue671011101"]="Yes? Would you like another glass? Or should I come take care of you for a little while?",
    ["Dialogue671011201"]="You think every Rose Red Tavern customer is only here to see me? Hahaha, that's flattering, thank you. My wine is one of a kind too though!",
    ["Dialogue671391101"]="This is a great place to train and grow stronger!",
    ["Dialogue671401101"]="Even a place that looks safe has danger lurking around every corner...",
    ["Dialogue671411101"]="I'm a scout for Eden Group starting today!",
    ["Dialogue671421101"]="Something's not right about this place...",
    ["Dialogue671431101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671441101"]="Riddles are the most fascinating thing in this world.",
    ["Dialogue671451101"]="I didn't expect to run into her here...",
    ["Dialogue671461101"]="Hm... What a lovely sound.",
    ["Dialogue671471101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671481101"]="My Raven... Oh, what should I do...?",
    ["Dialogue671491101"]="(Examining the flower on the ground intently.)",
    ["Dialogue671501101"]="(Examining the flower on the ground intently.)",
    ["Dialogue671511101"]="Ahhhh! Help!",
    ["Dialogue671521101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671531101"]="I have to find a way out of here now!",
    ["Dialogue671631101"]="These jerks are making a mess of our work...",
    ["Dialogue671641101"]="Ahhhh! Help!",
    ["Dialogue671651101"]="You have awful timing, adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue671661101"]="This mysterious place just smells like the perfect place to do business in, don't it?",
    ["Dialogue671671101"]="This mysterious place just smells like the perfect place to do business in, don't it?",
    ["Dialogue671681101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671691101"]="I break into cold sweat every time I come to the Labyrinth Forest...",
    ["Dialogue671701101"]="I break into cold sweat every time I come to the Labyrinth Forest...",
    ["Dialogue671711101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671721101"]="I never want to come to the Labyrinth Forest ever again!",
    ["Dialogue671731101"]="So sleepy... Maybe I'll go back to sleep for another few hundred years...",
    ["Dialogue671751101"]="The truth is always only ever known by a few...",
    ["Dialogue671761101"]="The freshmen from this batch are the worst I've ever seen!",
    ["Dialogue671771101"]="(Already passed out.)",
    ["Dialogue671781101"]="The enemy is attacking! The enemy is attacking!",
    ["Dialogue671791101"]="Sigh, I'm bored...",
    ["Dialogue671801101"]="(The lute is playing strange music.)",
    ["Dialogue671811101"]="(Praying intently.)",
    ["Dialogue671821101"]="The situation here is really bad...",
    ["Dialogue671831101"]="The best poems always come about unexpectedly!",
    ["Dialogue671841101"]="May Strouf bless and protect my Kahn...",
    ["Dialogue671851101"]="Thank you. We finally get to meet...",
    ["Dialogue671861101"]="I'm a follower.",
    ["Dialogue671871101"]="Another year, another day for new students to join the academy!",
    ["Dialogue671881101"]="(It's still possible to tell what it should look like, but it's completely broken.)",
    ["Dialogue671891101"]="Captain Hallam entrusted me with the mission of guarding the Mission Board, and guard it I will!",
    ["Dialogue671901101"]="I've labored as a carpenter my entire life!",
    ["Dialogue671911101"]="The battle here has ended. Things should be a lot safer now.",
    ["Dialogue671921101"]="Please show your support for Kafra!",
    ["Dialogue671931101"]="Vote for Cool Event Corp.!",
    ["Dialogue671941101"]="Cat Hand Services is the best!",
    ["Dialogue671951101"]="(Emits a weak glow.)",
    ["Dialogue671961101"]="The Mjolnir Mountains are the best place to gather materials!",
    ["Dialogue671971101"]="History is merely tales written by the victors.",
    ["Dialogue671981101"]="The treasure of the Thief King—I mean, Pirate King, is mine!",
    ["Dialogue671991101"]="The chivalry just brings nothing but trouble...",
    ["Dialogue672001101"]="(*Trembling*) Why did I come here...",
    ["Dialogue672011101"]="(*Trembling*) Why did I come here...",
    ["Dialogue672021101"]="My memories... They're calling to me...",
    ["Dialogue672031101"]="What a lovely view! I can almost forget what kind of place I'm in right now.",
    ["Dialogue672041101"]="What a lovely view! I can almost forget what kind of place I'm in right now.",
    ["Dialogue672051101"]="The sea floor is a true treasure trove! I can just taste the profits!",
    ["Dialogue672061101"]="The world is made up of newly-forgotten things.",
    ["Dialogue672071101"]="Humans are all baddies! Liars!",
    ["Dialogue672081101"]="Oh, I'm lost. How troublesome.",
    ["Dialogue672091101"]="Leave this to me!",
    ["Dialogue672101101"]="This isn't the bottom of the ocean... This isn't the bottom of the ocean...",
    ["Dialogue672111101"]="You wanna know about cooking with crab? I'm the best person to ask!",
    ["Dialogue672121101"]="You mustn't lower your guard here!",
    ["Dialogue672131101"]="Elliott reporting! The mission was a success!",
    ["Dialogue672141101"]="To have seen such wondrous beauty as a bard, I can leave this world without any regrets.",
    ["Dialogue672151101"]="(Morts is singing. It sounds wonderful as always.)",
    ["Dialogue672161101"]="There's a new clarity to Morts's songs. Don't you think so, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue672171101"]="Hmph! For a singing human, you're... not bad.",
    ["Dialogue672181101"]="Our destiny is preordained. There's nothing we can do...",
    ["Dialogue672191101"]="(Mesmerized by Morts' singing.)",
    ["Dialogue672211101"]="I'm an Obeaune priest. Are you here to seek Strouf's blessing?",
    ["Dialogue672221101"]="The light breeze carries with it the scent of a primitive time... There's a sense of tranquility here.",
    ["Dialogue672231101"]="Gotta keep training! I gotta get stronger!",
    ["Dialogue672241101"]="....",
    ["Dialogue672251101"]="There are more reckless people than I thought...",
    ["Dialogue672261101"]="Stay away! All of you!",
    ["Dialogue672271101"]="(Panting heavily. Still recovering from that desperate run.)",
    ["Dialogue672281101"]="(At a loss.)",
    ["Dialogue672291101"]="Help us, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue672301101"]="But Morts...",
    ["Dialogue672311101"]="Mmm, after reading this cookbook, I think I can already smell the fine delicacies wafting from the forest.",
    ["Dialogue672321101"]="I'll work hard to complete my duties no matter what's assigned to me!",
    ["Dialogue672331101"]="I'm sorry...",
    ["Dialogue672341101"]="(Poya's body is shaking as she holds back tears of rage in her eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue672351101"]="Morts, this is amazing!",
    ["Dialogue672361101"]="Ahh... To be standing so close to my idol...",
    ["Dialogue672371101"]="Is this really a gold mine...?",
    ["Dialogue672381101"]="Dinza isn't here yet?",
    ["Dialogue672391101"]="Is this it for the Golden Wings...?",
    ["Dialogue672401101"]="Hahaha! My bad, my bad!",
    ["Dialogue672411101"]="This isn't the Mjolnir Mountains I remember...",
    ["Dialogue672421101"]="I feel bad for the people here, but it really is a great place to train!",
    ["Dialogue672431101"]="I'm sorry but... I can't see you.",
    ["Dialogue672441101"]="How am I supposed to get any inspiration from a mountain of love?",
    ["Dialogue672451101"]="I feel bad for the people here, but it really is a great place to train!",
    ["Dialogue672461101"]="I'm sorry but... I can't see you.",
    ["Dialogue672471101"]="Take a good look at how amazing Eden Group is at their job!",
    ["Dialogue672481101"]="I'm worried about Morts...",
    ["Dialogue672491101"]="I'm worried about Morts...",
    ["Dialogue672501101"]="(He looks deep in thought. It doesn't feel right to bother him.)",
    ["Dialogue672511101"]="I understand completely...",
    ["Dialogue672521101"]="Welcome to the desert! It's not a place for rookies to wander into!",
    ["Dialogue672531101"]="The passion of the desert will affect you too!",
    ["Dialogue672541101"]="The genuine world's first wedding dress...",
    ["Dialogue672551101"]="The god of cooking? Hmph! I'm the saint of cooking and I don't approve!",
    ["Dialogue672981101"]="An exciting journey of adventure begins!",
    ["Dialogue680011101"]="(The blazing bonfire is getting you some delicious food.)",
    ["Dialogue691001101"]="Welcome to the chest floor, dear adventurer! Two types of rooms will appear on this floor: the monster room and the chest room. You may only choose to enter one of the rooms. Once you've decided, defeat the guard guarding the entrance to that room and the door will open. I bid you good luck, adventurer! (Rocks really can talk!)",
    ["Dialogue699010101"]="\"Tick tock... Tick tock...\"The invention of the telegraph made it possible for humans to use electricity for communication.",
    ["Dialogue699010102"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>10</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010103"]="If you don't understand, please refer to the <color=#839d34>Morse Code</color> chart!",
    ["Dialogue699010104"]="Yes! Get to work, telegrapher!!!\nEach Banquet Messenger may play a code consisting of multiple letters. I separated the codes with acoustic isolation.",
    ["Dialogue699010199"]="I will give you a bit more hints! \n·The answer is a blessing phrase in <color=#528fff>Danish</color>.\n",
    ["Dialogue699010201"]="Don't think of yourself as a hunter who has already aimed at the target. The answer can be <color=#528fff>slightly off</color>, just like your arrow!",
    ["Dialogue699010202"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>10</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010203"]="The letters you can see have been shifted backward by <color=#528fff>5</color> positions.",
    ["Dialogue699010204"]="Oh! You shouldn't have any trouble with something this simple.",
    ["Dialogue699010301"]="Don't think of yourself as a hunter who has already aimed at the target. The answer can be <color=#528fff>slightly off</color>, just like your arrow!",
    ["Dialogue699010302"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>9</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010303"]="The letters you can see have been shifted backward by <color=#528fff>6</color> positions.",
    ["Dialogue699010304"]="Oh! You shouldn't have any trouble with something this simple.",
    ["Dialogue699010401"]="Today, I'll become the nightmare that haunted your schooldays. Prepare to face the trial of <color=#839d34>mathematics</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue699010402"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>7</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010403"]="Arrange the 26 letters in order. A corresponds to 1, B corresponds to 2, and so forth.\nIn this way, each letter <color=#528fff>corresponds to a number</color>.",
    ["Dialogue699010404"]="Okay, I'll give you a few more hints. It isn't hard to see that the solution to the equation must be a <color=#528fff>positive integer</color>.\nCandidates, please pick up your pen and paper now.",
    ["Dialogue699010501"]="Play a game of chess with me, Adventurer!\nWe'll naturally play the game in the form of decryption. The <color=#839d34>chessboard</color> exists in our hearts.",
    ["Dialogue699010502"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>11</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010503"]="<color=#839d34>Polybius</color> is the chessboard cipher! 26 letters are also arranged in order in a 5x5 table, and the plaintext corresponding to each letter is the coordinates of the letter on the chessboard.",
    ["Dialogue699010504"]="Ciphers are amazing, right?",
    ["Dialogue699010601"]="Substitution techniques are often used in magic tricks. It's the same for today's ciphertext.",
    ["Dialogue699010602"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>6</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010603"]="The answer is written in <color=#528fff>binary codes</color> with <color=#528fff>special uppercase and lowercase fonts</color> representing 1 and 0!",
    ["Dialogue699010604"]="The <color=#839d34>Bacon's Cipher</color> truly is a little difficult... Oh! Did I give things away?!",
    ["Dialogue699010701"]="Hehe! Let's play <color=#839d34>Pigpen Cipher</color> today!",
    ["Dialogue699010702"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>9</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010703"]="In the pigpen cipher, 26 English letters are represented by <color=#528fff>26 different graphical images</color>. Amazing, right?\nOf course, I don't mind if you need to look for some relevant information.",
    ["Dialogue699010704"]="Everything follows a certain <color=#ff5252>pattern</color>. The same applies to the graphical images in the plaintext. Now, set your wits to work!",
    ["Dialogue699010801"]="Hi, it's you again! Let's play the <color=#839d34>Atbash Cipher</color>!",
    ["Dialogue699010802"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>9</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010803"]="Learn more about the <color=#839d34>Atbash Cipher</color>. It's very interesting!",
    ["Dialogue699010804"]="Of course, once you crack the cipher, you'll soon realize the answer is <color=#528fff>around you</color>.",
    ["Dialogue699010901"]="A <color=#839d34>fence</color> may stop my footsteps, but it can't stop my thoughts!",
    ["Dialogue699010902"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>12</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699010903"]="Imagine a fence and how each plank is staggered.",
    ["Dialogue699010904"]="Don't tell me you have been stumped by the <color=#839d34>Rail-Fence Cipher</color>!",
    ["Dialogue699011001"]="Don't think of yourself as a hunter who has already aimed at the target. The answer can be <color=#528fff>slightly off</color>, just like your arrow!",
    ["Dialogue699011002"]="The deciphered code is the ciphertext! It has <color=#ff5252>9</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011003"]="The letters you can see have been shifted backward by <color=#528fff>5</color> positions.",
    ["Dialogue699011004"]="Oh! You shouldn't have any trouble with something this simple.",
    ["Dialogue699011101"]="\"Tick tock... Tick tock...\"The invention of the telegraph made it possible for humans to use electricity for communication.",
    ["Dialogue699011102"]="The cipher you need to crack is a code made up of <color=#ff5252>8</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011103"]="If you don't understand, please refer to the <color=#1EAEA4>Morse Code</color> chart!",
    ["Dialogue699011104"]="Oh! You shouldn't have any trouble with something this simple.",
    ["Dialogue699011201"]="Good evening, Adventurer! Let's play <color=#839d34>ADFGX Cipher</color> today.",
    ["Dialogue699011202"]="The cipher you need to crack is a code made up of <color=#ff5252>6</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011203"]="The ADFGX cipher is similar to a chessboard cipher. The 26 letters are also arranged in order in a 5x5 table, with A as the origin point and ADFGX as the coordinate units!\nToday's English letters are placed in each grid in the following order: btalpdhozkqfvsngjcuxmrewy.",
    ["Dialogue699011204"]="In addition, the letters i and j will be placed in the same grid!",
    ["Dialogue699011301"]="Have you looked at the <color=#1EAEA4>calendar</color> yet? It's already <color=#528fff>November</color>! Prontera sure is cold!",
    ["Dialogue699011302"]="The cracked cipher is the ciphertext! It consists of <color=#ff5252>11</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011303"]="Use <color=#528fff>M, T1, W, T2, F, S1, and S2</color> to represent Monday to Sunday respectively, then lock the date according to the number behind them representing the week of the month and convert the date to letters.",
    ["Dialogue699011304"]="Stop rambling on! Grab the November calendar with you and go to the Shadow Messenger! Remember to wear extra layers of clothing before going. They aren't afraid of the cold!",
    ["Dialogue699011401"]="A <color=#1EAEA4>fence</color> may stop my footsteps, but it can't stop my thinking!",
    ["Dialogue699011402"]="The cracked cipher is the ciphertext! It consists of <color=#ff5252>12</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011403"]="Remember not to follow your usual habits. Read the puzzles from left to right.",
    ["Dialogue699011404"]="Don't tell me you really have been stumped by the <color=#1EAEA4>fence cipher</color>?",
    ["Dialogue699011501"]="Don't think of yourself as a hunter who has already aimed at the target. The answer can be <color=#528fff>slightly off</color>, just like your arrow!",
    ["Dialogue699011502"]="The cracked cipher is the ciphertext! It consists of <color=#ff5252>8</color> English letters!",
    ["Dialogue699011503"]="The letters you can see have been shifted backward by <color=#528fff>5</color> positions.",
    ["Dialogue699011504"]="Oh! You shouldn't have any trouble with something this simple.",
    ["Dialogue699971101"]="Thank you for choosing Kafra's VIP card service! I will respond to the bell and be at your service anytime, anywhere!",
    ["Dialogue699981101"]="Thank you for choosing Kafra's VIP card service! Your day will be wonderful with me by your side.",
    ["Dialogue7000001"]="Hello, are you interested in learning about what we do at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Exchange Center</color>? I notice you've garnered quite a bit of credibility in the Rune Kingdom. Working with the Exchange Center will surely bring more joy and profit to your adventures!",
    ["Dialogue7000002"]="(Jakdal pushes his glasses up confidently.)\nA well-traveled adventurer like you must amass a lot of goods you want to sell off, and have an urgent need for hard-to-get items. The Central Exchange Center will be able to help you resolve these problems and give you additional benefits in daily events!",
    ["Dialogue7000003"]="More importantly, the Central Exchange Center was established thanks to direct investment from the royal family. We welcome all citizens of the kingdom to join us. Plus, we have the best ability to safeguard your transactions! If you want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign a cooperation contract</color>, please read the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Exchange Center Rules and Regulations</color> carefully.",
    ["Dialogue7000101"]="Welcome, adventurer! What pet items are you looking for today?",
    ["Dialogue7000102"]="Oh my. You seem lost. Is this your first time dealing with pet-related matters?",
    ["Dialogue7000103"]="Hehe, then you've stopped by at the perfect time! Are you interested in a lesson on how to catch pets hosted by our senior pet tamer Taksch? The fee is waived if you buy a Pet Slingshot from us!",
    ["Dialogue7000104"]="Great! The Pet Slingshot can accurately control a pet's HP. I'll even throw in a Basic Projectile and a Rainbow Carrot for free. Remember to buy these too.",
    ["Dialogue7000201"]="Alright, now that you're equipped with the basic tools for catching pets, go meet Taksch at the South Gate! You'll know it's him once you see a man with a powerful-looking pet!",
    ["Dialogue7000301"]="Are you the newbie trying to learn about pets that Lyra was talking about?",
    ["Dialogue7000302"]="Hehe, trust me! Catching pets isn't difficult at all. See that Lunatic over there? That's the basic target all pet tamers practice on!",
    ["Dialogue7000303"]="Go on. I'll teach you how to use pet catching skills to capture your very own pet!",
    ["Dialogue7000401"]="Haha! That was easy, wasn't it?",
    ["Dialogue7000402"]="Wrong! Remember, if you want a high quality pet, you have to earn their approval through bitter combat!",
    ["Dialogue7000403"]="Ahem! That is to say, the lower your pet's HP when you catch them, the better your chances of getting a high-quality pet. Understand?",
    ["Dialogue7000501"]="Meow! You really are an energetic adventurer! You must have come looking for me—\n(Xavier looks at you with anticipation.)",
    ["Dialogue7000502"]="Meow! Hahaha! Then you came to the right person! I'm known as the Kingfisher on this continent. Many fishing enthusiasts are my followers and worshipers! I remember back when I caught that legendary fish in the pond at South Gate... I have been world-famous since then.\n(Xavier looks to be recalling fond memories.)",
    ["Dialogue7000503"]="And that's why I chose to hide at South Gate. After all, starting and ending my career at the same spot makes for quite the romantic and philosophical adventure, don't you think?",
    ["Dialogue7000504"]="I can't help but like bright youngsters such as yourself, meow! Now, as a token of our newfound friendship, please accept this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Larvae</color>. ...What? How can it help with your fishing, you ask? Of course you'll have to try it out for yourself to find out, meow!",
    ["Dialogue7000505"]="(Xavier carries his fishing rod triumphantly.)\nNow then—lift up your <color=#CA2E0AFF>fishing rod</color> and cast a line toward the start of your fishing career!",
    ["Dialogue7000601"]="Great job! I noticed your performance just now. You've got quite the talent, meow! It's only a matter of time before you become a great fisherman. But of course, you're quite a long way from attaining anything close to my level, meow!",
    ["Dialogue7000602"]="Oh right, I'll let you in on a secret. If you want to make fishing even more fun, you can try different kinds of <color=#CA2E0AFF>bait</color>. I'm sure <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hayden</color>'s shop in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta</color> will meet your needs. With a little help from different bait, you'll be able to catch all sorts of rare fish, and maybe even some treasures that have never been caught before, meow!",
    ["Dialogue7000701"]="You want to learn more about gardening? And Xavier sent you here? Hah! You've come at a perfect time, adventurer! Green Cotton Farm's wheat harvest is doing extraordinarily well this year, so we need to offload some of the wheat!",
    ["Dialogue7000702"]="Do you see the wheat in the fields over there? Go pick some and bring them back here. Get a little taste of gardening while you're at it. Can you do that, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue7000801"]="Ohh! You've picked some fine wheat. Consider this a gift to you, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7000802"]="Haha! Don't worry about it. What's a little wheat if my gift inspires you to enjoy a life of gardening?",
    ["Dialogue7000803"]="What's that? You want to know if there are any other adventuring lifestyles besides gardening and fishing? Hmm... I got it! How about mining?",
    ["Dialogue7000804"]="That's right! Tirelessly searching for the shiniest ore while sweating through backbreaking work can be quite the experience.",
    ["Dialogue7000805"]="When it comes to mining, no one knows better than Rorke over in the Mjolnir Mountains! That man is a true mining master! Go on, adventurer! Go discover your favorite adventuring lifestyle!",
    ["Dialogue7000901"]="What a coincidence! I was just looking at your equipment. So, what'll it be? Do you want to upgrade it today, or refine it? My Drubby, my companion, and my muscles are all itching to have a go at it.",
    ["Dialogue7000902"]="(Hollgrehenn's arms drop somewhat disappointedly.)\nOh, so you're here to ask how to get those ores and metals often needed for adventuring, are you? Indeed, without them, us blacksmiths wouldn't be able to work.",
    ["Dialogue7000903"]="Well, taking your biceps into consideration, I recommend going to the mine in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color> and personally <color=#CA2E0AFF>mining some ore</color>.\nHey, wait a minute. You don't have any mining tools yet? Pay a visit to General Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vienna</color> first and buy a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Normal Pickaxe</color>. Then you can get to work!",
    ["Dialogue7001001"]="Oh! You're finished? Let me have a look... Haha, a fine color and the smell of sweat!",
    ["Dialogue7001002"]="...Hm? Why didn't I warn you about the monsters in the mine? Well, of course, because the same is true of both mining and smelting: the more dangerous it is, the better it'll feel to move your muscles. Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue70010101"]="Hello there! Prontera continues to be full of strange and fascinating stories today, doesn't it? Speaking of which, would you like to hear an old story about the Gaebolg family's ancestor, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tristan Gaebolg</color>? This story comes from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>manuscript my mentor left behind</color>. You probably won't find the likes of it in the Prontera library!",
    ["Dialogue70010102"]="Oh~ Young gifted Tristan, favored by Odin, and beloved by young women all~♪\nFor even the goddess of dawn could not resist her desire for his affection. Eos took the form of a beautiful young woman, and moves to express her love~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010103"]="Alas, cruel fate! The perfect young man is cursed with a single imperfection—<color=#CA2E0AFF>arrogance</color>~♪\nTristan rejected the goddess and mocked her publicly, decrying her fanciful desires as a vain attempt to curry his good graces~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010104"]="The shock of the crowd could scarce compare to the goddess's humiliation. Her shame turned to tears, becoming a <color=#CA2E0AFF>clear spring</color> as they fell and pooled on the ground~♪\nShock turns to horror as all present realize the otherworldly nature of the woman before them~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010105"]="I take it you've figured out the reason I'm here in Prontera by now. That's right, I intend to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>clear spring made from the goddess's tears</color>! According to my mentor's manuscript, the spring has now become Prontera's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color>. I do wonder what the tears of a goddess taste like. Could I trouble you to collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spring Water</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue70010201"]="(Morts slowly savors the Spring Water when a look of realization flashes across his face. He quickly downs the rest.)\nYes, good! Very good! If you want to know what happens next, then stick around for the tale.",
    ["Dialogue70010202"]="Humiliation caused Eos to close off her heart. She refused to show herself again. Alas, this spelled misfortune for man—without the only god who could pull open the curtain to dawn~♪\nThe world was plunged into darkness—an eerie, silent, and cold eternal night. Monsters attacked in the cover of dark, bodies lie scattered in the open, despair and weeping filled the air~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010203"]="So many lost their loved ones, so many resented Tristan for his arrogance. If he had not insulted the goddess, they would not be suffering this terrible disaster~♪\nIt was then she stood up, the dancer known as Nerius. With her eyes blazing, she spoke: ♪",
    ["Dialogue70010204"]="She said: Give me your face for I would use it to smile kindly, give me your strength for I would use it to ensure no more loved ones are lost to monsters~♪\nWhat have you done with your gifts but use them as fodder for your arrogance? If this is what it means to be the chosen child of god, I would rather remain mortal~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010205"]="Her words cut through the young man like ice. In that instant, he realized he had failed to live up to the honor of his gifts. He did not deserve the reverence bestowed upon him by the people~♪\nHe decided to make amends. He gathered 10 Jellopies and crafted a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jellopy Mirror</color> that reflected only beauty~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010206"]="Hmm...\n(Morts suddenly stops speaking, falling into deep thought.)",
    ["Dialogue70010207"]="What's the hurry? I need a hand before I continue the story! Could you bring me <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 pure Jellopies</color>? Maybe I can recreate what Tristan did so many years ago.",
    ["Dialogue70010301"]="(Morts examines the Jellopies carefully before grunting in approval and putting them away in his pocket.)\nThank you kindly! Now then, let's continue the story!",
    ["Dialogue70010302"]="Tristan finds the resplendent Dawn Temple where the goddess Eos resides and places the Jellopy Mirror in front of a window~♪\nHe shouts from beyond the window: The most beautiful goddess in the world has graced the realm of the gods! When Eos peers outside out of curiosity, she sees instead her own reflection in the mirror~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010303"]="What a delightful surprise! Eos's heart was fit to burst with joy. It was then Tristan emerged to apologize for his past arrogance~♪\nThus, light returned to the land, banishing the darkness to where it belongs. When Tristan once again regained the people's reverence, he had become quite the modest youth~♪",
    ["Dialogue70010304"]="A wonderful tale, is it not? ^-^ My mentor's manuscript is full of thought-provoking tales like this, and my dream is to compile them all into songs that will last for generations! To do that, I intend to retrace my mentor's footsteps and revisit all the places he explored while writing his manuscript. Truly an exciting experience for any bard!",
    ["Dialogue70010305"]="Perhaps we'll meet again soon.\n♪~Just as birds fly free and with purpose, a bard too shall travel~♪\n(Morts takes out his lute and begins to play while singing.)",
    ["Dialogue7001101"]="(The wounded man has already passed out. It looks bad! Hurry!)",
    ["Dialogue7001201"]="Thank goodness you arrived when you did! We managed to pull him back from the brink. Leave the rest to us. You can keep the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mount</color>. I believe it'll be able to do more good staying with you.",
    ["Dialogue7001301"]="Heya, newcomer! Would you like to have this year's Criatura <color=#CA2E0AFF>New Student Headgear</color>?",
    ["Dialogue7001302"]="Haha, it's your lucky day! Normally, we would arrange for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>headgear crafting</color> trial to teach you how to craft one for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue700130211111"]="Haha, we're not about to give it to you for free! As a new student recruiter, it's my duty to teach you how to craft equipment!",
    ["Dialogue7001303"]="Lucky for you, it's still early, so the proctors aren't ready yet. You can have this <color=#CA2E0AFF>headgear</color> for free for now!",
    ["Dialogue700130311111"]="First, you'll need the materials to craft the headgear! Hmm... go bring back some Lucky Clovers!",
    ["Dialogue7001304"]="By the way, what <color=#CA2E0AFF>headgear</color> you get depends on your luck. Isn't that fun? Haha!",
    ["Dialogue700130411111"]="You'll find them on the monsters outside the South Gate. Look for Smile Assistance once you have what you need and she'll explain how to craft the headgear!",
    ["Dialogue7001401"]="A-ha! Is it finally my time to shine? I'm Smile Assistance. Please feel free to ask me anything about headgear!",
    ["Dialogue7001402"]="Oh, yes! You're a new student here to craft headgear for the first time, yes? Once you have all the materials, I'll give you a blueprint and step-by-step tutorial on how to make your own headgear!",
    ["Dialogue7001501"]="Ohh, what adorable headgear! I see Smile Assistance has taught you well how to craft one of your own.",
    ["Dialogue7001601"]="Ohh, what adorable headgear! I see Smile Assistance has taught you well how to craft one of your own. Do you feel the urge to take a selfie?",
    ["Dialogue7001602"]="Oh, you don't have to be embarrassed! With such wonderful designers in the academy, it's normal to want to snap a selfie! Go ahead, take one!",
    ["Dialogue7001701"]="Haha! You look so cute with that headgear in this photo! Alright, seeing as you and your new headgear are both cute as buttons, I declare you've passed the class with full marks!",
    ["Dialogue7001801"]="Please go see what happened, adventurer! Things will be very difficult for the citizens without the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7001901"]="(Pieces of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> are scattered across the ground. You can still vaguely make out its beautiful design while it was whole.)",
    ["Dialogue7002001"]="Until the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> is repaired, all <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board Quests</color> are on hold.",
    ["Dialogue7002002"]="It's just as you see it. This is just vile! The citizens have enough problems to deal with and someone comes along to make it worse!",
    ["Dialogue7002003"]="Thank you! If we can find the carpenter Old Clay, he'll be able to come fix the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>! He lives in the house next to the blacksmith!",
    ["Dialogue70020101"]="♪~The moon may hoard the stars in the night sky, but nothing compares to the light in her eyes~♪\n♪~So gracefully she dances across the forest floor, mist-like satin swirling behind delicate limbs~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020102"]="Hey there, we meet again! Who was that song about? It's the legendary beauty who once lived in Labyrinth Forest—the witch <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vivienne</color>, who else? The reason I came to Mjolnir Mountains is to learn more about the story about her and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nithil Heines</color>, the ancestor of the Heines family. I can tell you all about it if you're interested.",
    ["Dialogue70020103"]="Young Nithil was apprentice to the great wizard, Merlin. He had a brilliant mind and great talent, but also a heart as pure as a child's~♪\nThe beautiful Vivienne is a witch with a mastery over spatial magic. She had grace and charm and had the ability to bewitch the hearts of men~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020104"]="They could not be more different and never crossed paths until the day Nithil stumbled into Labyrinth Forest, becoming trapped in the illusion created by spatial magic~♪\nSave him! Save him! The young sorcerer has fallen into a trap~♪\nNo, no, be calm. The timing must be right. That is what the witch told herself~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020105"]="Just as Nithil was about to be swallowed up by vines, Vivienne slowly emerged. Her long hair flowed behind her as she strolled closer. The trees and plants parting to give way~♪\nDear naive Nithil was easily taken in by her beauty. He drank the <color=#CA2E0AFF>potion</color> she offered, not knowing it had the ability to <color=#CA2E0AFF>make him forget his past</color>~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020106"]="According to my mentor's manuscript, the potion is made by boiling down <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora Seeds</color>. Do the seeds really hold such magical properties? Bring some to me so I can study them, please!",
    ["Dialogue70020201"]="(Morts picks up a seed and sniffs it. He grimaces and pinches his nose shut before shoving the seeds deep into his pocket.)\nUgh... Alright, alright. Let's continue with the story.",
    ["Dialogue70020202"]="Without his memories from before entering the forest, Nithil thought the witch to be his spouse. He felt fortunate to have such a beautiful woman by his side and wanted to stay with her forever~♪\nBut the wise Merlin realized something was wrong. He tracked down his apprentice to the forest's entrance and figured out her ploy~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020203"]="Dearest Vivienne, Merlin called from the edge of the forest, dare you take a gamble with me? Let us wager whether Nithil will still love you when <color=#CA2E0AFF>his memory returns</color>~♪\nShould you win, I shall allow him to stay by your side. However, this will never happen as he did not fall in love willingly~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020204"]="Just as Merlin had predicted, the witch was too confident to back down. She agreed to let Merlin <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispel the effects of the potion</color> from her beloved to prove the strength of their love~♪\nBut the moment Merlin's <color=#CA2E0AFF>spell</color> took effect, Nithil chose to break up with her no matter how hard the pregnant Vivienne begged~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020205"]="Why did Nithil's attitude take such a turn? The answer lies in the spell Merlin casted on him. It's known as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spell of Metis</color>. If I remember correctly, there are records of the spell in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Library</color>. Be a dear and go take a look, would you?",
    ["Dialogue70020301"]="Excellent! You've learned the truth! That's right, Merlin's spell was never meant to remove the effects of the potion, but to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reverse its effects completely</color>! It caused Nithil to remember everything before entering the forest while forgetting the time he spent together with Vivienne within it. If you want to know what happens next, then stick around for the tale.",
    ["Dialogue70020302"]="Love became resentment, and resentment grew into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>curse</color>. Vivienne trembled as she looked at the man who betrayed her trust and spoke: ♪\nIf you insist on leaving, then never look back, or else you will suffer the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pain of separation</color> and it will tear your heart to shreds. Just like how I feel now~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020303"]="The witch's words ring clear in Nithil's mind as they embark on the long journey home. He carefully kept himself a step behind his master at all times, too afraid to overtake him~♪\nThat is until they came upon the hanging bridge at the entrance. The young sorcerer let down his guard and cheered excitedly as he ran ahead~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020304"]="Hooray! We didn't fall for her trap! Nithil shouted, but received no answer from his master in turn. Instead, there was a terrible scream~♪\nNo! Master is in danger! Panicked, the youth turned around. The moment he laid eyes on the other side of the bridge, Merlin had become a <color=#CA2E0AFF>great tree</color> that stretched into the heavens~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020305"]="...Speaking of which, that tree should still be at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>top of the mountain</color>, right? Hm... I need to know. Could you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a photo of the great tree</color> and bring it back to me?",
    ["Dialogue70020401"]="(Morts stares at the photo for a long time before sighing in disappointment.)\nSigh... I was hoping the tree would look a lot like Merlin. Guess I had my expectations too high for that one... Anyway, let's continue the story.",
    ["Dialogue70020402"]="This was the witch's revenge. The scream was a hallucination created by Vivienne. She wanted the man who broke her heart to fall into the same pit of despair~♪\nPoor, poor Nithil blamed his own <color=#CA2E0AFF>lust</color> for ending his master's life. He decided to cut off all attachments of love, and lived as a hermit in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color> at the top of the mountain~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020403"]="Whose fault was it? And who was left to hold on to this obsession? The souls of the lovers of yore have returned to the land. Only the great tree Merlin had become remains the same over the past one thousand years~♪\nThere is a legend that has stuck around. I'll leave it to you to decide whether you believe it. They say in his final years, Nithil can be seen gazing toward the Labyrinth Forest with an indescribable yearning on his face~♪",
    ["Dialogue70020404"]="So how do you feel? The story leaves you with some complicated feelings, doesn't it? I think this is why my mentor chose to leave the manuscript behind, so that everyone can come away with their own feelings on the matter. Speaking of which, the only son of the current head of the Heines family seems to go by Nithil too... I wonder if the young man inherited the magical talents of his predecessor?",
    ["Dialogue7002101"]="Can you help me move all this wood to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>, young one? I have to fix the Mission Board as soon as possible!",
    ["Dialogue7002102"]="Haha, here to help repair the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>, are you? The wood is over here. I just need a zealous youngster to help me move it! I'll wait for you by the Mission Board in the meantime!",
    ["Dialogue7002201"]="Excellent work, adventurer! I saw you helping out with Mission Board repairs. You're starting to feel more and more like a proper adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7002202"]="Adventuring is not just about becoming stronger, you know. You come across a lot of interesting things too!",
    ["Dialogue7002203"]="Turn that frown upside down! Come on, I'll show you the prime fishing spot I just found. You can catch some real big ones there!",
    ["Dialogue7002204"]="It's right near the dock on this island. Let's go, let's go!",
    ["Dialogue7002301"]="Hehe! Fishing is fun, am I right?",
    ["Dialogue7002302"]="An experienced adventurer just told me there are all sorts of interesting things we can get into like <color=#CA2E0AFF>fishing</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>mining</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gardening</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7002303"]="And we can use all the stuff we get from those activities to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cook</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7002304"]="I get that you're serious about being an adventurer, but if you don't try to enjoy the adventuring lifestyle, you'll lose the motivation to grow stronger!",
    ["Dialogue7002305"]="Alright, off I go! See you around!",
    ["Dialogue7002401"]="Another fresh-faced adventurer! Welcome! We sell armor that's perfect for newcomers. Take your pick!",
    ["Dialogue7002501"]="Oh! It looks like you've gotten some adventuring experience under your belt. Let's give you a little test!",
    ["Dialogue7002502"]="A test about your opinions on <color=#CA2E0AFF>guilds</color> as an adventurer! Remember, I'm the <color=#CA2E0AFF>guild guide</color>, so your choices will help me decide what to teach you!",
    ["Dialogue7002503"]="What kind of adventurer do you aspire to be in Midgard? A lone wolf? Do you want to be part of a family? Or would you like to be a leader of a party?",
    ["Dialogue7002504"]="Oh, that's unexpected. Do you really want to go it alone? There are a lot of benefits to joining a guild, you know.",
    ["Dialogue7002505"]="That's unfortunate but alright. If you're not interested in interacting with others, I won't take up more of your time. Happy adventuring!",
    ["Dialogue7002506"]="In that case, a guild would be perfect for you! You can help your friends and adventure together in a guild. There are no problems too great to solve when you work as a team!",
    ["Dialogue7002507"]="There are <color=#CA2E0AFF>guild quests</color> to help with your training, along with various <color=#CA2E0AFF>stores</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>red envelopes</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>prayers</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>skill buffs</color>, and more! If you like to make things a little easier for yourself, you can't go wrong joining a guild.",
    ["Dialogue7002508"]="I'll let you experience the nitty-gritty for yourself! Join a guild and have fun!",
    ["Dialogue7002509"]="I knew it! No one can possibly ignore the allure of a guild. Let's start over!",
    ["Dialogue7002510"]="Wow! You're ambitious! The role of guild leader would be perfect for you!",
    ["Dialogue7002511"]="I can help you with <color=#CA2E0AFF>guild creation</color> where you'll be starting from scratch. There's also <color=#CA2E0AFF>building your guild territory</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>researching guild buildings</color>, but it'd take forever to explain them all.",
    ["Dialogue7002512"]="Just know that being guild leader is not an easy job and not for everyone. If you're ready for that responsibility, come find me again and get ready to create your own guild!",
    ["Dialogue7002601"]="Oh! Over here, adventurer! Quickly!",
    ["Dialogue7002602"]="Yes, yes, yes, my goodness, you're finally here! Help me finish a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chamber of Commerce quest</color>. Quickly!",
    ["Dialogue7002603"]="There are three large Chambers of Commerce on this continent. They tend to issue requests for adventurer aid.",
    ["Dialogue7002604"]="Earning the favor of adventurers in a particular territory basically means staking a claim to business in that area. The three big Chambers of Commerce are currently competing over Prontera.",
    ["Dialogue7002605"]="As the first adventurer to come forward, you get first pick on whose Chamber of Commerce quest gets chosen first in Prontera! Don't get too stressed out. It really doesn't make a difference!",
    ["Dialogue7002701"]="Hello, I'm the Kafra Corporation representative. We are constantly striving to satisfy our customers' needs while upholding our three main principles: honesty, credibility, and integrity. We spare no expense on maintaining proper service training and administrative work.",
    ["Dialogue7002801"]="Hello, I'm the Cool Event Corporation representative. We work closely with Kafra Corporation, but our culture is geared toward followers of other religions. If you have any religious concerns, then please choose us.",
    ["Dialogue7002901"]="Yo! I'm the Cat Hand Services representative! Don't worry if you haven't heard of us. We're the pioneers of business in this other world. Sounds amazing, right? Why not give us your vote?",
    ["Dialogue7003001"]="Thank you! You've completed the first <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chamber of Commerce quest</color>. Congratulations!",
    ["Dialogue7003002"]="Hm? Where did they go? Well, the winner's already been decided here, so they're probably rushing to the next location. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue70030101"]="Oh? You want to know about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>origin of Izlude Island</color>? It just so happens I just finished composing a relevant story from my mentor's manuscript into song. Would you like to be its first audience?",
    ["Dialogue70030102"]="Oh, dear listener, come with me to a time before Ragnarok, when humans and powerful giants shared the land~♪\nThe giants were few in number, but they were tough as nails and tall as trees. One in particular goes by the name <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude</color>, a simple-minded, greedy, boorish giant~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030103"]="With fists the size of mountains, Izlude wandered the outskirts of villages, threatening to beat the villagers into a bloody pulp if they didn't hand over their food~♪\nAnger and resentment festered, but no one dared say a word. Day after day, they traded their hard labor for safety and grew used to the oppression. Everyone except <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ewan Richard</color>, that is~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030104"]="When their freshly harvested wheat was once again pillaged, Ewan clenched his fists and came up with a plan to enact revenge against Izlude~♪\nEwan was a quiet young man, but Odin knows he had a courageous heart, an unyielding will, and great wisdom~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030105"]="Speaking of which, it's hard to imagine a giant preferring to eat healthy food like <color=#CA2E0AFF>Island Wheat</color>, isn't it? Does it contain some strength-enhancing properties? Bring some to me so I can find out for myself!",
    ["Dialogue70030201"]="(Morts hesitates before putting the wheat in his pocket.)\n...Nevermind, it's probably a better idea to cook it before eating, like a civilized person. Let's get back to the story!",
    ["Dialogue70030202"]="Ewan waited until early spring of the second year to farm in earnest. He tilled more fields than ever before and his harvests were many times more generous than previous years~♪\nBut no one did expect him to offer his full crop to the giant. He even made quite an enticing vow to Izlude~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030203"]="O great Izlude, spare your feet the walk to the village, spare your fists the threat of a swing~♪\nI, your willing servant, shall do your bidding. You need only ask from the comforts of your mountain cave, and I shall bring all the delicacies to you~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030204"]="He must be mad! His family and friends shunned him, but the young man had earned Izlude's trust. He could come and go from the giant's den as he pleased~♪\nAfter all, who could say no to free food and drink? To be rewarded without putting in the work? The giant grew complacent and lazy as he waited for Ewan to feed him day after day~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030205"]="As for what happens next... Why don't we continue after you bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat n' Pumpkin</color>? I definitely put in the work for this and am not asking for food for free. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue70030301"]="(Morts looks grateful but doesn't eat the food. He places it aside.)\nThank you! I'll eat this after I finish the story!",
    ["Dialogue70030302"]="As the days go by, Izlude grew fatter and fatter. He was so flabby he could only lie prone within his cave~♪\n\"My good friend, Ewan,\" the giant mumbled. \"Place the food directly in my mouth from now on. I can no longer move, or raise a fist\"~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030303"]="Ewan agreed, obedient as ever. However, when he returned to the village, this was what he said instead~♪\n\"Bring your knives and hatchets and come with me to Izlude's home! The time has come to walk the road to revenge I paved\"~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030304"]="Izlude was deep in slumber, unaware of Death at his doorstep. Ewan was the first to charge forward, cutting out a piece of the giant's flesh with his knife~♪\nThus encouraged, the villagers followed suit. By the time Izlude woke from the pain, he was too out of shape to resist~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030305"]="Oh, right, I once read the Dark Ingredients Encyclopedia describe the taste of giant meat to be similar to that of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vocal</color> thigh. Not sure how true that is... Could you bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocker thighs</color> so I can try it for myself?",
    ["Dialogue70030401"]="(Morts gingerly picks up a Grasshopper leg and tosses it into his mouth. He immediately turns around and nearly pukes his guts out.)\n...Urgh... Ugh! Now I know why it's called the Dark Ingredients Encyclopedia! By Odin... Let's just get to the end of the story.",
    ["Dialogue70030402"]="O, powerful Izlude, once awe-inspiring in his dominion. He never expected he would die because of <color=#CA2E0AFF>laziness</color>~♪\nWith the passing of time, the giant's bones became the <color=#CA2E0AFF>island</color> of the same name today. But would the people now living on the island be willing to sing this ballad to future generations~♪",
    ["Dialogue70030403"]="That's right, the protagonist of this tale is none other than the ancestor of one of the seven royal families—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Richard family</color>! He became known as a great hero thanks to his giant-slaying deeds. And it seems that same courage and righteousness continue to flow in the veins of his descendants.",
    ["Dialogue7003101"]="(The tablet emits a strange glow, as if luring people to touch it.)",
    ["Dialogue7003102"]="A mysterious teleportation magic bursts forth from the tablet. You can now use the power of the tablet to <color=#CA2E0AFF>teleport</color> to a certain unknown dimension!",
    ["Dialogue7003201"]="Are you here to look into the Endless Tower trial too, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue7003202"]="There's an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Endless Stone Stele</color> on Byalan Island that is used to enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Endless Tower</color>. But it would only allow entry to those whose strength it deems worthy.",
    ["Dialogue7003203"]="It's a tower located in another world. No one knows how high up it goes or the purpose of its existence.",
    ["Dialogue7003204"]="The tower seems to possess a will of its own. It attracts the strong to climb it and is populated with monsters from our world. It's said in the circle of those who climb the tower, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>number of floors climbed</color> is considered a badge of honor.",
    ["Dialogue7003205"]="Why would monsters from our world appear in a tower from a different world? Where do the people who fail the challenge go? The tower is mired in rumor and mystery.",
    ["Dialogue7003206"]="Remember, the Endless Tower is endless. Make all your preparations before challenging it!",
    ["Dialogue7003301"]="Ah... This is a problem...",
    ["Dialogue7003302"]="Oh! Adventurer, what a coincidence! My Magic Furnace is broken, you see. I'm here to look for materials to repair it.",
    ["Dialogue7003303"]="I really, really need it! The Hornet's stinger is both tough and lightweight, the ultimate repair material. But Hornets tend to move in groups, and I haven't been able to find a way to get one.",
    ["Dialogue7003401"]="...Ugh, these stingers...",
    ["Dialogue7003402"]="Ahahaha, it's nothing. Just some cold sweat thanks to my imagination. These stingers look real sharp and stabby. I'm really glad you're here. Thanks! Come find me when you're in Prontera. I'll teach you how to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft equipment</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7003501"]="Oho! Welcome! Thanks for your help with the Magic Furnace last time! Hollgrehenn's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Equipment Crafting</color> is officially open for business!",
    ["Dialogue7003502"]="Without further ado, let me show you how to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft equipment</color>! Do you see the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Equipment Crafting Merchant</color> over there? I've given him all authorization to <color=#CA2E0AFF>craft equipment</color>! Go try him out!",
    ["Dialogue7003601"]="Hello, adventurer! Look over here. As long as you have the material, I'll be able to craft you the best weapon in all of Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue7003602"]="As a note, the equipment you can craft is different in each city, so be sure to visit them to find the best equipment that suit your needs!",
    ["Dialogue7003701"]="Now you've witnessed the true power of the Magic Furnace! Haha! Come back anytime you find some new materials!",
    ["Dialogue7003801"]="Thanks for fixing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>! You look a lot more serene. Did you find the path to becoming stronger?",
    ["Dialogue7003802"]="When you're stuck on where to go next, it's time to hit up your good pal the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color>! You can help the citizens and become stronger all in one go!",
    ["Dialogue7003901"]="Meowha! Are you here because you've heard of the Cat Hand clan's awesome magic?",
    ["Dialogue7003902"]="Hmmeow? No? Eh, don't worry about it meow! The Cat Hand clan's contemporary disciple, Lil' Kitty, has returned from his training! Our enchantment business is now open meow!",
    ["Dialogue7003903"]="Enchanting can unleash your equipment's hidden potential meow! Do you wanna know how much potential your equipment still holds? Then give us a try meow!",
    ["Dialogue7004001"]="What do you think? Did you discover how powerful your equipment actually is meow?",
    ["Dialogue7004002"]="We rely on the mystic powers of the Cat God meow! Do come back again meow!",
    ["Dialogue70040101"]="... Sigh, it's always the good ones who die young. Did you know a <color=#CA2E0AFF>nobleman of the seven royal families</color> is buried in this here cemetery? If not for that business from so long ago, he'd be resting with the rest of his family in the cemetery behind the church instead. Say, would you like to hear his story?",
    ["Dialogue70040102"]="There once was a pair of twins. They were born to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walter family</color>, and while they may look identical, their personalities and talents were completely different from one another~♪\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Ian</color> is the older twin. He was sharp and had a silver tongue. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivan</color> was the younger twin. He was quiet and reticent. Ian was terrible with a sword, but Ivan's swordsmanship rivals that of the god of war Ares~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040103"]="They were inseparable, and even those closest to them had a hard time telling them apart by looks alone. They were the best of friends and were the envy of many~♪\nIan would speak for Ivan often, while Ivan would accept swordsmanship training in Ian's stead. The Walter family had been graced with two prodigies, people would exclaim~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040104"]="Until one day, the king heard the tale of the \"talented twin knights\" and decided to hold a tournament on the day the twins became adults~♪\nOh no, this is bad, Ian cried while covering his face. Everyone will know my shortcomings. I'll embarrass our family~♪\nPlease don't fret, Ivan comforted gently. I'll do my best to protect your dignity~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040105"]="Speaking of which, can you help me take a <color=#CA2E0AFF>photo</color> of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>square in front of the palace</color>? They say the tournaments back then were always held there. Maybe I can relive the scenes of the past with my imagination!",
    ["Dialogue70040201"]="(Morts accepts the photo and gasps.)\nWow! This is gorgeous! Alright then, let's continue the tale of the tournament of yore!",
    ["Dialogue70040202"]="As promised, Ivan once again donned Ian's armor and won battle after battle in the tournament, striking fear into the hearts of his opponents~♪\nBut as one round after another ended, it was the brothers who made it into the final match. Their father soon appeared with an ultimatum: ♪",
    ["Dialogue70040203"]="Knighthood is the core of the Walter family, and swordsmanship is our soul~♪\nThe one who wins the tournament shall become the true heir of our family~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040204"]="But I should be the rightful heir! Ian cried out in his heart, for he believed himself the wisest among his family and he was older than Ivan~♪\nWhat kind of rule is this?! It's ridiculous! Do I have to give it all up just because my little brother is more talented at wielding a sword?! ♪",
    ["Dialogue70040205"]="But oh dear sweet Ivan—he was still trying to think of ways to lose to Ian, blissfully unaware of the evil thoughts brewing in his older brother's crazed mind~♪\nThe flames of <color=#CA2E0AFF>jealousy</color> had destroyed all sense of reason and was flowing through Ian's veins like poison from the devil's candy~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040206"]="(Morts' tummy suddenly starts grumbling.)\n...Ugh, I guess I'm hungry. Uh, in order to maintain the quality of my storytelling, could you bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steamed Egg n' Fish</color> to warm my belly?",
    ["Dialogue70040301"]="(Morts gulps down two mouthfuls of the stew and smiles in content.)\nYes! Much better! Let's continue!",
    ["Dialogue70040302"]="On the day of the final match, the masses were eagerly anticipating a brilliant contest of might. Ivan had other plans though. He would pretend to be struck by his brother's blade during an attack and fall over~♪\nBut when the horn sounded to begin the match, Ivan discovered he had lost his strength. He didn't even have the strength to raise his hand, or stand, or pull out his sword~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040303"]="What is he waiting for? Why isn't he attacking? The crowd began to murmur amongst themselves. Even his family began to have suspicions~♪\nIt was then Ian stepped forward. He fell to one knee before his father and regretfully began to reveal the \"secret\" that had been hidden all these years~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040304"]="Dearest father, this is as far as our lies go. I'll tell you the whole truth now~♪\nThe truth is out of the two of us, only I'm capable of wielding a sword. Ivan was the one who begged me to dress up as him to participate in this tournament and lie to all of you~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040305"]="That was when dear sweet Ivan discovered the truth of Ian's deception~♪\nThis was how his brother had intended to frame him and forever mar Ivan's good name is shame and shadow~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040306"]="Ahh, how terrible it must feel to be betrayed by one closest to you! Could you please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pooler Garden</color> and pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Flowers</color> for me? We'll have use for it later.",
    ["Dialogue70040401"]="(Morts looks sad.)\nThese Fresh Flowers should be good enough. Let's continue the story.",
    ["Dialogue70040402"]="Ivan didn't bother trying to explain himself. He was always bad with words and there was never any proof of everything he had done for his brother. And besides, Ian's actions already made his heart ache~♪\nTears of shame streaked down his cheeks as Ivan chose to silently remain kneeling on the ground. He could see Ian sneering from here as he listened to the crowd spurn him in a daze~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040403"]="Many years later, a wanderer named Ivan joined many others on the continent. No one knew his family name, and he always hid his face beneath a mask~♪\nIt was only when he lay on his death bed that Ivan met his only confidant—a bard who memorialized Ivan's final moments on paper~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040404"]="Please bury me in the West Gate Cemetery after I die~♪\nI have no desire to reunite with the people I once considered my family, even on the other side~♪",
    ["Dialogue70040405"]="That's right. The bard Ivan met was none other than my mentor! It's thanks to their chance encounter that the truth to the Walter family history could see the light of day again. Remember the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Flowers</color> I asked you to pick for me earlier? Please place them on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivan's gravestone</color>. Perhaps it'll bring him some measure of solace.",
    ["Dialogue70040501"]="My mentor added his final thoughts at the end of the manuscript. He hoped to let the masses know of Ivan's story, to make people aware of the truth. And this is why I'm making a collection of my mentor's manuscripts. I won't let the world forget any of the ballads that can serve as a cautionary tale.",
    ["Dialogue7004101"]="Adventurer! Do you want to take part in some refinement or transferring?",
    ["Dialogue7004102"]="Haha, to tell you the truth, I added the ability to refine to my furnace recently but I was too worried about opening the doors to the business without testing it first. Are you up for a gamble, adventurer? You could be Hollgrehenn's research assistant from now on!",
    ["Dialogue7004103"]="If not, you can consider this a refinement testing request from me! Come on! Please!",
    ["Dialogue7004201"]="Hahaha! I've got an impressive furnace here, don't I? You can feel the urge to give it a try, can't you?",
    ["Dialogue7004202"]="Heheh, this magic furnace can automatically refine or transfer even without me by its side. Just let it work its magic!",
    ["Dialogue7004301"]="Welcome! Another brave adventurer about to befriend a falcon, I see!",
    ["Dialogue7004302"]="A falcon is your companion in combat. As a certified hunter, you have to learn how to fight alongside it. If you're ready, come rent a falcon from me.",
    ["Dialogue7004401"]="Welcome! Another brave adventurer who completed the second Job Advancement, I see!",
    ["Dialogue7004402"]="A mount is your companion in combat. As a certified adventurer, you have to learn how to fight alongside it. If you're ready, come get a class mount from me.",
    ["Dialogue7004501"]="Another young merchant with zeal, I see! Well met! The pushcart is an essential companion for a traveling merchant. Come rent one from me!",
    ["Dialogue7004601"]="Hi there! What a lively, young adventurer you are! If it's potions, materials, and other consumables you need, please come to us at Lindra Sundries Store located in each city!",
    ["Dialogue7004701"]="My goodness, I was worried the military courier won't bring you back here in time.",
    ["Dialogue7004702"]="It's terrible! The monsters are everywhere and thanks to the power of the Haze, they get right back up again after they're defeated! The Defense Force Soldiers and Knights' Order alike are fighting an arduous uphill battle.",
    ["Dialogue7004703"]="The Great Sage Kroneika has ordered the evacuation of most of the citizens in advance. They're seeking refuge at the palace. Once the Defense Force Soldiers finishes escorting the last of the citizens, we'll be drawing all forces to defend the palace—Ah! Look out!",
    ["Dialogue7004801"]="Haha! You saved my life again, adventurer! I owe you another one.",
    ["Dialogue7004802"]="Simmons sent me a distress call a few minutes ago, but I have to escort the citizens back to the palace. I can't leave them behind, so please, could you go help in my stead?",
    ["Dialogue7004803"]="Good! They should be near the Tower Telescope! But be very careful. Whatever it is, it's strong enough to force Simmons to make a distress call.",
    ["Dialogue7004901"]="Hahaha! I was expecting Fitz, but it seems I got a much better backup!",
    ["Dialogue7004902"]="They answered the call of Valhalla while defending the people... Don't look so sad. It's our job as Defense Force Soldiers to sacrifice ourselves to protect the citizens! Speaking of which, where's Fitz?",
    ["Dialogue7004903"]="Haha! He's working hard too, huh? Then I can't fall behind. The citizens behind me should be the last of the people of Prontera who needs to be evacuated. The Great Sage Kroneika should be waiting for you in front of the palace gates. Hurry!",
    ["Dialogue7005001"]="Adventurer, thanks to you, we were able to safely evacuate all the citizens.",
    ["Dialogue7005002"]="Don't apologize. I know you feel like it's your fault you were tricked by Baphomet and lured to Payon, but any good hero would have given their all for Payon in the same situation.",
    ["Dialogue7005003"]="I told you before. We trust in what you choose to do.",
    ["Dialogue7005004"]="Anyway, now's not the time for that. The people are safely evacuated and anyone still alive are trickling back to defend the palace. The monsters are going to launch a full assault on us soon.",
    ["Dialogue7005005"]="Sir! Monsters are crossing the Central Fountain Square and preparing a frontal assault on the palace!",
    ["Dialogue7005006"]="Listen up! Prontera is facing an unprecedented crisis! Behind us are the citizens and our king! The very people the Knights' Order are sworn to protect!",
    ["Dialogue7005007"]="A true knight never surrenders! By the grace of Odin, we'll burn the flames of our soul to the last and show these monsters a human's true strength!",
    ["Dialogue7005008"]="Adventurer, the final battle looms. Please lend us the might of Odin's bloodline!",
    ["Dialogue70050101"]="Heya, have you met the sheriff of this city before? He's a real hot-tempered old man. He's just as bad as his warmongering son actually. Speaking of which, the Lugenburgs are known as the family with \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>lava flowing in their veins</color>.\" The reason for that dates back to a tale from a long time ago. Do you want to hear about it?",
    ["Dialogue70050102"]="Look on! The sun is blazing on bent backs as whips whistle and crack through the air. It is the slaver's mining crew~♪\nPoor emaciated <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alex Lugenburg</color>. He was sold into slavery as a child and knew only starvation and humiliation. He had no future and no home to return to~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050103"]="Yet the most frightening thing to the young man wasn't his master's abuse, but the beatings from the other slaves~♪\nA tragic state of affairs, this! Robbed of their morality as slaves, they'd rather bully the weak than band together under the banner of rebellion~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050104"]="Life was bleak and gloomy until the day their master spoke: Rare Red Crystals had been discovered in the cave, and those who can collect one hundred crystals would earn their freedom~♪\nHowever, the miserly slaver smiled and shook his head, I will not give you any mining tools. You have to use your bare hands~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050105"]="Hmm... I wonder what kind of crystal that is, to pique the slaver's interest so. Could you mine some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Crystals</color> for me? Help me expand my horizons!",
    ["Dialogue70050201"]="(Morts admires the Red Crystal under the light.)\nOh my, the light reflecting from it sure is dazzling! Now then, I suppose I'll just accept this as my storytelling fee. Thank you kindly ^-^~",
    ["Dialogue70050202"]="Pain was nothing compared to his yearning for freedom, Alex dug up one hundred Red Crystals until his hands bled crimson~♪\nBut he was ambushed by the other slaves on his return journey. They took the fruits of his labors and claimed them for their own, yet this still wasn't the end of the violence~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050203"]="If we let Alex go, he'll expose us! The slaves decided to throw the youth into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Lava</color> to silence him for an eternity~♪\nBut I've never done anything to anyone! Please let me live! The youth begged and cried, yet none would listen to the cries of the weak~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050204"]="Makes you angry, doesn't it? But such is human nature. Men were always wont to succumb to their best interests or power. Still, I'm very curious what the lava pool that consumed a member of the seven royal families looks like... Could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of the Golden Lava</color> and show me?",
    ["Dialogue70050301"]="(Morts looks horrified.)\nThis... I shudder to imagine what it feels like to be thrown in there! As for what happened to Alex next, let me tell you all about it.",
    ["Dialogue70050302"]="It was miserable! The molten lava melted away Alex's skin and flesh, the punishing heat ate away his bones~♪\nBut just as he was about to be burned into nothing, a vaguely derisive voice rang through his mind. It spoke with a sigh, or was it trying to entice? ♪",
    ["Dialogue70050303"]="Foolish child, I am <color=#CA2E0AFF>Loki, the god of fire</color>. Your predicament has wrought a great sorrow within me， and thus I shall bestow upon you new life~♪\nSwallow the lava before you and it will return your body to what it once was. The more you swallow, the greater your strength shall become. Such is my mercy~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050304"]="The fear of death and the desire for power prompted Alex to open his mouth. He drank his fill of lava until his stomach could fit no more~♪\nAnd just as Loki had promised, the youth became a giant. But his heart shall never know peace again, for an insatiable violence took its place~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050305"]="(Morts suddenly starts coughing.)\n...Cough, cough! Sorry, the desert climate is doing a number on me. My mouth is so dry it feels awful! I remember the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Muka</color> outside the city produces sweet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cactus Dew</color>. If you could bring some for me to drink...?",
    ["Dialogue70050401"]="Yes... That's much better. I can continue.",
    ["Dialogue70050402"]="The cunning Loki did not reveal one of his conditions: as the youth gains more power, he loses some measure of rationality and control~♪\nAlex burned the mine that brought him so much suffering into the ground. Yet even that wasn't enough to quench the raging flames of anger in his soul~♪",
    ["Dialogue70050403"]="A raging giant has wandered the desert since then. He could uproot trees from the ground and make mountains tremble. There were none who dared disobey his will~♪\nYet only the giant himself knew that he was never truly free. He may no longer be a slave, but he was now chained to the demon known as <color=#CA2E0AFF>fury</color>.",
    ["Dialogue70050404"]="And that was the story of Alex Lugenburg. It's hard to say whether that was a good or bad end for him, but what I do know for sure is that fire still flows in the veins of Alex's descendants. To this day, that fire still burns within the Lugenburg family.",
    ["Dialogue7005101"]="Ohoho... Prontera's deadliest Night of Calamity since our nation was founded and we made it through safely because we worked together.",
    ["Dialogue7005102"]="Yes, we won.",
    ["Dialogue7005103"]="Prontera may be marred with scars and desolation and we will surely mourn the dead, but the future is bright. Peace will reign over Prontera once more and it's all thanks to you, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7005104"]="You don't understand. Without your help, demonic power would have burst forth from Mjolnir Mountains and Sphinx Cavern. Once that happens, Prontera would not have been able to fight back the monsters, and Midgard will once again be ruled by Baphomet.",
    ["Dialogue7005105"]="You nipped the bad omens at the bud and ended the final battle. You led us into victory against Baphomet with Odin's might. This is all your doing, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7005106"]="Great Sage, I'd like to award this adventurer with the \"special promotion.\" What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue7005107"]="Special promotion... Hm... I approve. I'm sure the captain of the Richard army, Dean Mainz, and Archbishop Wolmas would feel the same way.",
    ["Dialogue7005108"]="Hahaha! Come find us in Prontera Cathedral once your class reaches level 50, adventurer. We will give you a reward that best suits your honor.",
    ["Dialogue7005401"]="Thank you for your help. I'll be able to repair the Mission Board quickly with all this wood. Oh yes, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Upgrading Metal</color> is your reward. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color> in Prontera to upgrade your equipment.",
    ["Dialogue7005501"]="You've run out of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Upgrading Metals</color>? Well, I need to craft some armor. If you could help me collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocker</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shells</color>, I'll pay you in Upgrading Metals.",
    ["Dialogue7005601"]="Oh, these are very nice shells. I'll be able to make some quality armor with these. Here's the payment we agreed on. Now you can continue to upgrade your equipment!",
    ["Dialogue7005701"]="Equipment of different upgrade levels require different upgrading items. I can teach you how to get advanced upgrading items, but first you need to learn how to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fish</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7005801"]="You can get smelting materials by fishing. I've prepared some materials for you in advance so you can try smelting a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phracon I</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7005901"]="Not bad! A final reminder: equipment on different slots also use different upgrading items. Now go on with your adventure!",
    ["Dialogue7006001"]="Young one, you seem tired. Would you like to take a break and allow Odin's benevolence to cleanse your mind and body?",
    ["Dialogue7006002"]="You can receive Odin's Blessing by praying before the statue. Go on, adventurer. Go receive Odin's protection!",
    ["Dialogue70060101"]="Look! Alberta truly is a beautiful and prosperous city! That it's still booming to this day is thanks to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner family's</color> proper management. It seems they've learned the lessons from their ancestors well and will never let <color=#CA2E0AFF>greed</color> consume their hearts again.",
    ["Dialogue70060102"]="Oh my, it seems you haven't heard of this story! Then allow me to sing it for you so that you may relive that piece of history.\n(Morts eagerly begins to play his lute.)",
    ["Dialogue70060103"]="This story begins in Alberta back when there were no mansions and ships, only a few families who fish for a living~♪\nLive may be simple but there's no limit to ambition! That is what a fisherman would tell himself. His name was <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ricky Wigner</color>~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060104"]="While other struggle to provide for themselves, Ricky had other plans. He ignored the villagers advise and spent all his savings to buy himself a fishing net and a harpoon~♪\nIt's a long term investment, the young man would say. I refuse to be poor forever! I'll bring fortune to my doorstep~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060105"]="His wish quickly came true, He caught an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune</color> on one of his fishing trips and he was pleasantly surprised as he admired the monster of legend~♪\nFate has finally seen fit to grant me a miracle! Ricky exclaimed. I knew you wouldn't let a smart man like me wallow in mediocrity~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060106"]="Sigh... It's a shame. I've read about many beautiful women, but I've never seen a monster as beautiful as an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune</color>! I'd settle for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>photo</color>! If only someone could take a picture and show it to me.",
    ["Dialogue70060201"]="(Morts sizes up the photo of the Obeaune with great interest.)\nHmm, I see. No wonder Ricky Wigner fell for her at first sight! Listen on if you want to know what happened next!",
    ["Dialogue70060202"]="Please don't hurt me! The Obeaune pleaded pitifully. She presented him with a crystal-clear <color=#CA2E0AFF>pearl</color>, hoping to buy her freedom with it~♪\nBut Ricky was greedy. He wished to keep the beautiful Obeaune for himself, so he came up with a plan to keep both the treasure and the Obeaune~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060203"]="A single pearl isn't enough, he said regretfully while shaking his head. If you wish to return to the sea, you must come home with me and fulfill <color=#CA2E0AFF>three demands</color>~♪\nThe Obeaune had no choice but to agree. She made only one request in return, that no one should be nearby when she makes a pearl~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060204"]="I want <color=#CA2E0AFF>ten pearls</color>! That was Ricky's first demand. He sold the treasure to a merchant and used the gold coins he earned to establish a merchant fleet and a port~♪\nI want <color=#CA2E0AFF>a hundred more pearls</color>! That was Ricky's second demand. He needed more wealth so he could build mansions~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060205"]="Speaking of which, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>port</color> is built using Ricky's funds! Though the nearby sailors have been telling me that ocean-bound ships were being attacked by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vadons</color> recently. Why don't we lend Alberta a hand and teach those monsters a lesson?",
    ["Dialogue70060301"]="Well done, very well done! I'm sure Ricky would be grateful for your kindness. Of course, he was lost in his dreams of riches in his youth. Let's take a look at what happened next.",
    ["Dialogue70060302"]="Not long after, the Age of Gods arrived and Midgard was plunged into chaos. The legendary hero, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tristan Gaebolg</color> called for those willing to fight the monsters~♪\nWhile most people fled, Ricky sensed a business opportunity. He remembered he could make one more demand of the Obeaune and went to find her~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060303"]="Give me <color=#CA2E0AFF>a thousand pearls</color>! I have different plans for them this time. I'll use all my wealth to support and follow Tristan's expedition across the continent~♪\nJust as the young man predicted, Tristan became king. And thanks to Ricky's great contribution in the founding of the nation, he returned home as one of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>seven royal families</color>~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060304"]="Look at me! I'm a noble now! Ricky was eager to share the good news with the Obeaune and was blind to how frail she had become. She had spent too long away from the ocean~♪\nYou have everything you wanted, please let me go home... As the Obeaune weakly tried to remind Ricky of his promise, she discovered he wanted to go back on his word~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060305"]="Disheartened and heartbroken, the Obeaune shed a single <color=#CA2E0AFF>tear</color>. It was only when the tear crystallized into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood red pearl</color> that Ricky realized something was wrong~♪\nCould it be the source of the treasures this whole time was...?! Ricky was consumed with regret but there was little he could do to stop the Obeaune's life from fading as she shed the last of her tears~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060306"]="Sigh. Now that I know the source of <color=#CA2E0AFF>pearls</color>, it makes me appreciate how precious these treasures are! Could you harvest some from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune</color>? I'll stow them away properly, I promise.",
    ["Dialogue70060401"]="(Morts smiled gratefully.)\nThank you! I'll keep these pearls at my side always. They'll be there to remind me to never make a beautiful woman cry. Now, the story is almost at its end, so listen well.",
    ["Dialogue70060402"]="With the passing of the Obeaune, the pearls too became foam and Ricky was left with nothing but self-loathing and regret~♪\nSince then, he would always warn other merchants to be wary of the demon named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Greed</color>. It will corrupt a man's heart and force him to lose sight of himself and make mistakes~♪",
    ["Dialogue70060403"]="This story may be tragic but it also became a precious lesson for others, so I guess it had a good ending. By the way, there's a common folklore around here that says romance between man and Obeaune never ends well. Sigh, I do hope this tragedy doesn't repeat itself!",
    ["Dialogue7006101"]="Remember this, adventurer. You're destined for extraordinary things! No matter how difficult your journey ahead, Odin will always watch over you.",
    ["Dialogue7006201"]="Adventurer, your success is guaranteed now. As long as you have Odin's Blessing, you can do battle without fear!",
    ["Dialogue7006301"]="Oh? Are you the adventurer who's here to help us? Then let's not waste anymore time. Let's move.",
    ["Dialogue7006302"]="...Huh? Did no one tell you what's going on?\n(Emanuel unhappily turns toward his assistant.)\nJesse... Jesse! Didn't I tell you to... Tch, I bet you forgot, <size=26>didn't you?!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7006303"]="(Jesse tenses. His muscles stiff and his expression tight as he stares ahead, willing himself to become one with his surroundings.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue7006304"]="...Alright, fine! I guess I'll be doing the explaining! Not long ago, a terrifying <color=#CA2E0AFF>disease</color> started spreading rapidly across the Schwarzwald Republic. And thanks to the friendly relationship between our two nations, the disease has entered Rune-Midgarts too.",
    ["Dialogue7006305"]="At first, we thought the disease only infected monsters, but we soon realized it could make the leap onto humans... Long story short, it's dangerous. We can't waste anymore time. Let's move!",
    ["Dialogue7006306"]="...Huh? Did no one tell you what to do?\n(Emanuel angrily turns toward his assistant.)\nJesse... Jesse! I swear... <size=26>HEY!</size> <size=26>I know you're listening!!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7006307"]="(Jesse tenses. His muscles stiff and his expression tight as he stares ahead, willing himself to become one with his surroundings.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue7006308"]="...Alright, fine! I'll do the explaining! The fact is the researchers from the Rekenber Institute developed a vaccine in the early days of the outbreak, but they didn't have enough virus specimens to mass produce the vaccine. So, we're hoping you can retrieve virus specimens from infected monsters...",
    ["Dialogue7006309"]="(Emanuel holds out a booklet irritably.)\nYeah, yeah, I know, I know! No one told you which monster carries the virus either, did they?! Essentially, the answer can be found in this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Virus Specimen Handbook</color>. Please take a look through it yourself!",
    ["Dialogue7006401"]="So? Do you get it now? This Virus Specimen Handbook has the latest research on the virus. If there's nothing else you need, please get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cell Solution</color> for me as soon as possible!\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Remember!</color> You <color=#CA2E0AFF>can you retrieve Cell Solution</color> by <color=#CA2E0AFF>killing the monsters using Odin's Blessing</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7006501"]="(Emanuel is carefully examining the virus specimen.)\nYes... Good, very good. This is the Cell Solution we need! Should the virus decide to mutate in the future, I'll update the Virus Specimen Handbook immediately. The virus specimens required to create the vaccine could be different by then so come to me to verify the details any time.",
    ["Dialogue7006502"]="For now... Tsk! Please give the virus specimens to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesse</color> at once. If he's still pretending to be deaf, I'll test the new medicine on him instead!",
    ["Dialogue7006601"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh no, oh no, oh no, oh no... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Mr. Emanuel instructed me to explain the situation to adventurers</color></size> <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but I, I COMPLETELY FORGOT!!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue7006602"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Did I just...</color></size> <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Am I in the clear now?</color></size> <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh, thank the heavens...</color></size> <size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Now the earth just needs to swallow me up!!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue7006603"]="<size=24>Aaahhh!! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!</size> <size=24>I'm sorry!!</size>\nWait... What's that you're holding in your hand?! It's not another weird testing agent, is it?!\n(Jesse hugs himself tightly in terror.)",
    ["Dialogue7006604"]="Oh, phew... It's just the virus specimen for the vaccine. I thought Mr. Emanuel got angry and is going to use me as a test subject again. Haha... W-wait a minute, you're not going to collect virus specimens looking like that, are you? I mean, aren't you taking any kind of protective measures when you come in close contact with the monsters?",
    ["Dialogue7006605"]="(Jesse steps back in shock.)\nWhat? Nothing? Not... Not even a face mask?",
    ["Dialogue7006606"]="(Jesse takes another step back.)\nUh... What about gloves? You wear them when you pick up the virus specimens, right?",
    ["Dialogue7006607"]="(Jesse takes a bigger step back in horror.)\nYou... I... You..!! Go get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>protective equipment</color> created by the Rekenber Institute and put it on, quickly! Use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>virus specimens</color> to exchange for it at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Epidemic Prevention Center</color> over there... Hurry! Hurry and get away from me!",
    ["Dialogue7006701"]="How is it? Rekenber Institute products are classy, aren't they? If you want more of the most technologically-advanced products this continent has to offer, then please keep collecting more virus specimens!",
    ["Dialogue7006702"]="...Hm? What's the point of wearing protective equipment when you've already touched the source of the infection?\n(Jesse smiles brightly.)\nWhat a silly question. So you won't infect others, of course!",
    ["Dialogue7006801"]="Congratulations! You've successfully signed a contract with the Central Exchange Center! A most prudent decision. After all, the Exchange Center is the fairest, and highest authority in Rune Kingdom's commodity market.",
    ["Dialogue7006802"]="(Jakdal bows respectfully.)\nWell then, we hope you enjoy trading with us, and wish you a safe and pleasant adventuring journey!",
    ["Dialogue7006901"]="Hello there, adventurer! Come help me out. I need some valuable data and you'll be able to provide by playing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lucky Kingdom Guessing Game</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7006902"]="My name is Lyanna and I'm the kingdom's court clerk. I keep a record of all things big and small in the kingdom, including everyone's data. The only data point I'm missing is luck. I couldn't find a way to incorporate it into my books.\n(Lyanna lowers her head, crestfallen.)",
    ["Dialogue7006903"]="Don't underestimate the importance of luck. It's a key element to success too! Just think, you need luck to traverse the continent on adventures, to run a business, and even to manage a kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue7006904"]="As a certified court clerk, I will not allow such vital data to go unrecorded!\n(Lyanna looks up again. Her hands clenched tightly.)",
    ["Dialogue7006905"]="(Lyanna proudly straightens her back and runs a finger under her nose.)\nHeh heh. Thankfully I've come up with a plan. I invented the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lucky Kingdom Guessing Game</color>! With this event, I'll be able to determine everyone's luck and provide some entertainment along the way!",
    ["Dialogue7006906"]="Details on how to play and the rules are written in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kingdom Record Book</color>. Open it up and take a look!",
    ["Dialogue7007001"]="Now that you know the rules, you'll be able to provide me the most accurate data by <color=#CA2E0AFF>playing the Lucky Guessing Game regularly</color>! Of course, I'm not asking you to do this for free. If you manage to guess the correct number, I'll give you a really big prize!",
    ["Dialogue7007002"]="(Lyanna walks up to you and whispers.)\nHeh heh. Just between you and me, they say kindness brings luck. If you help out as many people across the continent as you can and reap all the good deeds, you might just raise your chances of winning the prize!",
    ["Dialogue70070101"]="Hey~ Have you heard of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Beautiful Bells band</color>? They have an extended history and has been credited with the birth of countless famous dancers and bards across the continent... And I happen to be a member of this band. One day, I'll be as famous as my seniors before me!",
    ["Dialogue70070102"]="I can tell you about the band's history if you're not aware of it. As it happens, I just finished turning the story of the founder of the band, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Margaret Nerius</color>, into song. Won't you be my first listener?",
    ["Dialogue70070103"]="Our story takes place in a time when the Egyptian empire had fallen, humanity had lost their faith, and the desert became a haven for monsters~♪\nThe ruthless <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demon King Morroc</color> possessed unparalleled strength. He hosted a celebration every year just to find amusement in toying with young human girls~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070104"]="I shall choose the most beautiful among you all! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>priestess</color> declared her horrifying pledge. She assured the young girls that their beauty will be preserved when they become <color=#CA2E0AFF>dancers</color> for the celebration~♪\nBut little did anyone know that the young girls were performing a sacrificial dance. And at the end of thunderous cheers and applause, they would be sacrificed into Morroc's belly~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070105"]="Meanwhile an orphan wandered the Sograt Desert. She couldn't remember her own name, let alone the faces of her parents~♪\nShe met a refined woman dressed in colorful raiments and a veil, who gently took the young girl's hand and said: ♪",
    ["Dialogue70070106"]="I am the priestess of the Demon God, and I would adopt you. So long as you willingly dance for the Demon King on your eighteenth birthday, immeasurable happiness will be yours~♪\nThe young girl blinked and nodded in response, not knowing that she had sealed her fate in that moment~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070107"]="(Morts' stomach rumbles.)\nOh... Traveling such a long way by foot is taxing on the body. I'm famished. Bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed Salad</color> to fill my belly, would you?",
    ["Dialogue70070201"]="(Morts nods as he eats, seemingly enjoying himself.)\nThank you, thank you. Eating Water Weed in the middle of the desert is quite the experience! Alright. I'm stuffed. Let's continue the story.",
    ["Dialogue70070202"]="The priestess named the young girl <color=#CA2E0AFF>Margaret</color>, meaning noble princess. She was raised among the other orphan girls and spent her days learning proper etiquette and dance steps~♪\nOn her eighteenth birthday, Margaret had grown into a fine and lovely young woman, with a perfect figure and equal dancing form. She was truly irresistible~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070203"]="Yet on the night before the celebration, Margaret dreamed of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>goddess Valkyrie</color>~♪\nShe was told the cruel truth of her fate and given a divine decree~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070204"]="Tomorrow's celebration shall determine your fate and those of your fellow dancers. If you do nothing, you shall be served to the Demon King Morroc on a platter~♪\nFor this I bring to you a sign from Odin. May it free you from your troubles. If you wish to escape your fate, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>before the waters of Hope Oasis</color>~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070205"]="By the way, could you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of the Hope Oasis</color> and bring it back to me? I can't help it. The thought of the legendary dancer Margaret having been there before piques my curiosity.",
    ["Dialogue70070301"]="(Morts examines the photo carefully.)\nHmm... A view like this must look quite unusual to someone raised in Comodo! If you want to know what Margaret discovered in the Fountain Water, listen on.",
    ["Dialogue70070302"]="On the day of the celebration, Margaret wore her finest clothes and danced her more graceful dance as she awaited her pivotal moment~♪\nAs expected, the Demon King Morroc appeared once the dance was complete. He relished in the women's screams but there was one among them who remained calm~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070303"]="Why are you not afraid? Morroc asked, curious~♪\nI have no reason to escape when I'm about to be eaten anyway, Margaret replied calmly~♪\nTo be sacrificed to the demon god is an honor, and so I would like to present to you <color=#CA2E0AFF>three suggestions</color> for your consideration~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070304"]="My first suggestion is that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>eat me first</color>. The finest meal should always be savored first, and I am the most outstanding dancer here, be it in dance or in appearance~♪\nMy second suggestion is that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>swallow me and everyone else whole</color>. You'll be able to preserve our form this way and we would be able to dance for you in the underworld~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070305"]="My third suggestion is that you eat this <color=#CA2E0AFF>small, round fruit</color> before eating us. It's tart and sweet and would <color=#CA2E0AFF>whet your appetite</color>~♪\nMorroc was pleased and decided to accept her suggestions, proclaiming her to be loyal~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070306"]="According to my mentor's manuscript, the fruit is called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sweet and Sour Berry</color>! They say it's great for making all sorts of delicious appetizers. Bring back some for a taste, would you?",
    ["Dialogue70070401"]="(Morts chews on the Berry and nods toward you gratefully.)\nThank you for complying with all my wishes. Let us return to the story.",
    ["Dialogue70070402"]="The fruit did indeed whet Morroc's appetite. One by one, he swallowed the dancers whole but still he wasn't satisfied~♪\nHe had no choice but eat his own priest, followed by the rest of the spectators. The demon king's <color=#CA2E0AFF>gluttony</color> fattened up his belly until he could do nothing but sit weakly on the ground~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070403"]="It was then a dagger burst through his belly, splitting Morroc's abdomen in half. He howled in pain and looked down to see Margaret leap out~♪\nThe dancer's steps were light, her form ever graceful, but the steely determination in her eyes shocked even the demon king~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070404"]="O pitiful monster, the young girl lamented as she looked up at Morroc. You are fated for defeat this day because of your foolishness~♪\nThe goddess Valkyrie came to me in my dream and showed me the key to your defeat within the Fountain Water. What I saw within is what controls destiny~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070405"]="What did you see? The people were eager to ask of Margaret later. Her answer was always the same. She saw <color=#CA2E0AFF>her own reflection</color>~♪\nThis was the sign from god that man's fate can only be changed by oneself. Only man can determine for themselves whether they rise from the ashes or fall to ruin~♪",
    ["Dialogue70070406"]="And that's all seven tales about the seven royal families written by my mentor in his manuscript. Of course this is only a small portion of everything my mentor has seen and heard in his lifetime. There are so many more stories and legends waiting for me to interpret and add to. Thank you for being such a faithful audience. Let's meet again in the next leg of our journey! ^-^",
    ["Dialogue7007101"]="Wow!! I knew you were special when I first laid eyes on you! You win the grand prize!",
    ["Dialogue7007102"]="As of just now, everyone in the kingdom has heard of your win! They now know you're the Child of Fortune! I'm going to note down your extraordinary luck in my data records right now!",
    ["Dialogue7007103"]="This is just a legend but they say when someone gets so lucky that Lady Luck's radiance shines down upon them, they'll be lucky for a period of time. They'll succeed in everything they do, and that's why they're known as the Child of Fortune.",
    ["Dialogue7007104"]="Heh heh. It's been my greatest wish to find the Child of Fortune ever since I started keeping a record of everyone's luck! But many people aren't so sure the legend of the Child of Fortune is true. They want to see it to believe it. I remember <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color> is one such person! Why don't you go show him the power of a Child of Fortune?",
    ["Dialogue7007201"]="Oh me, oh my, let me take a good look at you. You're so radiant it looks like you've been cloaked by light from good old Lady Luck. I can't help but want to make an exception and play a song for you—But that's after I'm certain you're the legendary Child of Fortune.",
    ["Dialogue7007202"]="Why am I so interested in the Child of Fortune, you ask? Because a talented bard like me must gather up all the fantastic stories of this majestic continent and turn them into beautiful songs!",
    ["Dialogue7007203"]="If the Child of Fortune really exists, then such a captivating story will be my ultimate creative source material. A song built around it will last for generations and be passed on among the masses! So, come, let me verify the truth of this rumor. If you can correctly answer my song riddle, I'll know you're the real Child of Fortune!",
    ["Dialogue7007301"]="Are you ready? Let's begin!",
    ["Dialogue7007302"]="♪~The sobering cuisine hides in the forest, meat and vegetables are mixed in with kitchen utensils.\nGuests are eager to taste the flavor, but that one ingredient is hard to fine~♪",
    ["Dialogue7007303"]="What am I?",
    ["Dialogue7007304"]="Wrong, wrong, wrong! Sigh, I knew the Child of Fortune was nothing more than a rumor. I'm off to look for other fantastic stories.",
    ["Dialogue7007305"]="(Morts' eyes widen in disbelief as he stares at you.)\n<size=24>I can't believe it. You... You got it right!</size>\n<size=18>This is a secret only a super knowledgeable person like me knows!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7007401"]="It seems the rumors are true. The Child of Fortune really does exist!",
    ["Dialogue7007402"]="(Morts lowers his head and looks depressed.)\n<size=18>Sigh, why should a brilliant gentleman as charming, suave, and brimming with limitless talent like me be forsaken by Lady Luck's light? With it, I'd be able to solve those riddles I have yet to complete. And that lovely lass I've been pursuing for so long would have just come running into my arms... (／_＼)</size>",
    ["Dialogue7007403"]="Sighs, thanks for trying to comfort me. When you're a deep thinker like me, you tend to end up with a bundle of things to worry about...\n(Morts suddenly looks up as if he remembering something.)\nThat's right! I just remembered. A while ago, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color> was asking everyone he met whether they know where the Child of Fortune is. Why don't you check in on him and see if he needs anything?",
    ["Dialogue7007501"]="(Hollgrehenn looks anxious.)\nYou're the Child of Fortune! I've been looking for you for so long!",
    ["Dialogue7007502"]="No, no, I just need to borrow your good luck so I can find my precious refinement stone!",
    ["Dialogue7007503"]="I managed to find a Refinement Stone after a lot of effort a while ago. I was thinking about what luxury equipment to refine with my Drubby on my way back when I discovered the stone had gone missing from my pocket. I immediately retraced my steps to try and find it but no luck so far... What rotten luck!",
    ["Dialogue7007504"]="Clues? Let's see... Oh! I was bumped into by a group of kids on the way back. Nearly knocked me right over. Luckily, my reflexes were quick enough that I used Drubby to keep myself upright and... <size=24>Oh, Drubby!</size> <size=24>You're truly the best friend a man could have!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7007505"]="I heard them mutter something like \"gotta hide it\" and \"treasure.\" Maybe the kids got into some kinda of treasure hunting game. They must have <color=#CA2E0AFF>hidden my Refinement Stone somewhere in the city</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7007506"]="(Hollgrehenn lowers his head and looks a little depressed.) Sigh. With my rotten luck, I couldn't find any clues as to where they could have hidden it. If I go looking now, I'd probably never get my Refinement Stone back, so please lend me your good luck! Help me find it! Bring my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Refinement Stone</color> back!",
    ["Dialogue7007601"]="(Hollgrehenn accepts the Refinement Stone with joyful tears in his eyes.)\nThank you so, so much! This is... This is... <size=24>By Odin!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7007602"]="This... This isn't my Refinement Stone at all. This is a Refinement Guarantee Stone! It's the rarest of rare among Refinement Stones!",
    ["Dialogue7007603"]="No, no, no! You're the Child of Fortune. There's no way you made a mistake! Things aren't as simple as it looks... I know! It's because of your immense luck that a common Refinement Stone was somehow transformed into a rare treasure!",
    ["Dialogue7007604"]="(Hollgrehenn doesn't seem to hear your explanation as he laments.)\nAhh~! That must be it! You're definitely the Child of Fortune!",
    ["Dialogue7007605"]="Here, you can have the Refinement Guarantee Stone. I hope Drubby and I will be able to rely on your good luck the next time we run into trouble!",
    ["Dialogue7007701"]="The Kafra Corporation is here to provide you with an exclusive warehouse service, 100% safe so you can rest at ease! If you want to expand your warehouse's capacity, you can purchase a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warehouse Expansion Voucher</color> from Crystal Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sinclair</color> in Alberta.",
    ["Dialogue7007801"]="Adventurer, come here quickly. Shh, whisper. Look over there at that guy who's surrounded by Obeaunes.",
    ["Dialogue7007802"]="I don't know where he came from either. He just suddenly appeared at the tavern a few days ago. Turns out he's also a musician. He casually sang a few songs and won over a bunch of my fans. All the Obeaunes gather around him. I don't get his strange appeal.",
    ["Dialogue7007803"]="Jealous? Hahaha, as if. I am the most talented bard in Midgard and adored by countless women. Me being jealous of some stranger? No way, I'm... I'm just concerned that he'll deceive nice and innocent girls. Help me find out who that guy really is. I want to have a fair musical duel with him so that everyone can see who's the real star of this continent.",
    ["Dialogue7007901"]="Hey there. It looks like you're curious about me?",
    ["Dialogue7007902"]="Haha, it's still very obvious, huh? I've noticed that too. I don't think I belong in this world. I'm an artist. The other day, I finished my Halloween show and skateboarded past an entrance to a very flashy bar. I recall the name being something like Rose Red. After pushing the door open, I passed through a wondrous halo of light, and then I arrived here...",
    ["Dialogue7007903"]="A dimensional gap? I heard a lot about this land in the past two days and learned that when a dimensional gap is opened, something like what happened to me could occur. It looks like I need to investigate further to find a way back... But anyway, you came to see me. Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue7007904"]="So someone wants to play music with me. Of course they're welcome to anytime. After all, music has no boundaries. I'm also looking forward to hearing the music of this continent.",
    ["Dialogue7008001"]="So? Did you find out who he is?",
    ["Dialogue7008002"]="What?! He's actually an artist from a different world? No wonder he dresses so strangely. Everyone must've just been attracted to his uniqueness. Once I show him up with true musical talent during our duel, everyone will know who's the real musician. Yeah, I'm certain of it.",
    ["Dialogue7008003"]="N-nervous? As if. I'm the top bard in the continent. How can I lose to a measly outsider? Let's head over there quickly!",
    ["Dialogue7008101"]="Hey, how's it going? You're the musician who wants to have a musical exchange with me, right?",
    ["Dialogue7008102"]="Hello, I am Morts, Bard of Midgard, and I would like to have a fair musical duel with you.",
    ["Dialogue7008103"]="Hahaha, no problem. Inspiration sprouts from the exchange of musical notes. Let us give the audience a wonderful performance.",
    ["Dialogue7008201"]="You really are a great musician. I heard a very moving story through your music.",
    ["Dialogue70082010"]="That's right. It has been my travel companion for many years. It allows me to freely traverse this land. I seem to have lost it when I was being transported. These past two days, the patrons at the tavern have been telling me about a person named Vienna Lindra who is selling a strange item that sounds like my skateboard.",
    ["Dialogue70082011"]="What does your skateboard look like exactly? Maybe we can look around and bring it back to you?",
    ["Dialogue70082012"]="It's a flat and long black board with four silver wheels underneath. I think you'll be able to recognize it once you see it.",
    ["Dialogue7008202"]="I didn't think you would be able to harmonize with my lute. Your singing voice actually matches very well with it.",
    ["Dialogue7008203"]="So your instrument is called a lute? It has a unique sound I've never heard of before. It makes one want to sing.",
    ["Dialogue7008204"]="(A faint blush appears on Morts' face.) Oh, it's not that great. Your singing voice, on the other hand, is quite enchanting. Look around you. People are captivated by our performance.",
    ["Dialogue7008205"]="This is all the beauty of music, Mr. Morts. I also hear the sincerity and passion in your music. If you don't mind, would you like to be my first friend in this land? And also this here adventurer, of course. Thanks to you, we could have this splendid performance today.",
    ["Dialogue7008206"]="I'm very honored, but after speaking this long, we still don't know your name.",
    ["Dialogue7008207"]="Right, I forgot to introduce myself. My name is Jimmy Lin, but you guys can call me Jim.",
    ["Dialogue7008208"]="Okay, Jim. What do you plan on doing next?",
    ["Dialogue7008209"]="I don't think I'll be able to return soon, so I've decided to embark on a new adventure on this continent and figure out how to get back along the way. But before that, I have to find my skateboard.",
    ["Dialogue7008301"]="Oh, Adventurer, what are you looking for? I have everything you need here. I also have some strange items I received recently.",
    ["Dialogue7008302"]="Here, look. I happened to get this device when the dimensional gap appeared. I think it must be a valuable item from some strange world. If I can find the right buyer, I'll be able to sell it for a good price. After all, there are many adventurers who like researching about the other worlds.",
    ["Dialogue7008303"]="Huh? You know what this thing is?",
    ["Dialogue7008304"]="I see. Since this is your friend's lost possession, why don't you take this strange thing back to him? The Lindra Family is not in the dirty business of appropriating other people's belongings. Oh yes, I also have a peculiar item that I obtained together with the skateboard. It looks like it came from another world as well. Why don't you also take this back to your friend? Maybe he lost this too.",
    ["Dialogue7008401"]="Wow! Thank you so much. This really is my skateboard. Great, now I'm even more excited about the new adventure.",
    ["Dialogue7008402"]="Oh? Is there something else?",
    ["Dialogue7008501"]="What?!! I thought I'd never get this model back. I can't believe you have it.",
    ["Dialogue7008502"]="It's a race car model. Car racing is a kind of... speed competition in my world. In any case, this model represents something important to me, and I'm very thankful that you've brought it back to me. I actually carried many of these things in my backpack while I was being transported. If you collect other such race car models during your travels, please be sure to bring them back to me.",
    ["Dialogue7008503"]="This is great. I'm incredibly excited for this new journey now. Perhaps I can also spread my music and culture to this new land. Adventurer, I hope that in our future adventures, we can find new dreams and create unique memories together!",
    ["Dialogue7008601"]="Hello, esteemed Adventurer. Congratulations on achieving great feats and fame in this land through your skill and talent. We have all heard about your deeds. I believe you've come to me this time after receiving a secret letter from the Kingdom Guards.",
    ["Dialogue7008602"]="We actually sent you a secret letter because after multiple scouting missions not long ago, our secret agents discovered a dimensional gap of unknown origin in a corner of the kingdom. Niflheim's many spirits and monsters are up to something bad...",
    ["Dialogue7008603"]="At the moment, it seems that we must eliminate all the monsters that have escaped from the rift in order to prevent them from continuing to tear the narrow gap. Once these monsters tear it completely open and invade Midgard, the Rune Kingdom will become the first battlefield.",
    ["Dialogue7008604"]="To prevent the worst case scenario, we must be prepared to take the fight to them immediately. The king entrusted us Kingdom Guards to gather the strongest adventurers in the whole continent to form an adventurer squad that can eliminate the monsters that have escaped from the gap. Adventurer, are you willing to join this monster-slaying squad?",
    ["Dialogue7008605"]="I knew you wouldn't stand idly by during the kingdom's crisis! Please start by helping us gather some war preparation resources. Here is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kingdom's War Preparation Resource Manual</color>. It lists the current resources we are most in need of. When facing a great battle, complete preparedness is paramount.",
    ["Dialogue7008701"]="Adventurer, I believe you're up to date on which war preparation resource we have a shortage of. Please help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharpening Stones</color>, which is the most needed material at the moment.",
    ["Dialogue7008801"]="I've taken careful inventory of our resources. We are indeed most in need of this war preparation resource. In order to be fully prepared for combat, we may need additional resources in the future. I will keep the latest needed resource updated in the War Preparation Resource Manual. You may come to me to view the manual at any time. Now please deliver the precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharpening Stones</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Freida</color>, Captain of the Second Regiment's Assault Squad.",
    ["Dialogue7008901"]="It's you. You're the adventurer who recovered the Fragment of Ymir's Heart by themselves, right? I've heard all about your deeds. Not bad at all. You did not dishonor the Kingdom Defense Force. Although you were only a reservist at the time, you showed extraordinary ability.\n(Freida smiles satisfyingly and pats you on the shoulder.)",
    ["Dialogue7008902"]="Oh? So it was the staff officer who sent you to me. In that case, you must have brought materials we need for war preparation. He's been putting a lot of effort into this lately.",
    ["Dialogue7008903"]="These war preparation resources are crucial for maintaining peace in the kingdom. Of course, the kingdom greatly appreciates your hard work in bringing these materials to us and we will reward you generously in return.",
    ["Dialogue7009001"]="What you see here are tokens of the kingdom's appreciation for adventurers who took the trouble to collect resources for us. If you come with <color=#CA2E0AFF>new war preparation resources</color>, you will be given great <color=#CA2E0AFF>rewards from the Kingdom.</color>",
    ["Dialogue7009002"]="What? You're already itching to go to war, young man? How spirited, hahaha. But don't be too eager. We're still waiting for the continent's most elite warriors to assemble. We need to be fully prepared before setting out.",
    ["Dialogue7009101"]="Adventurer, it seems that you've had many extraordinary experiences in your adventures during this time. I can see the brilliance of Odin's bloodline in your demeanor. Maybe it's time to tell you about the oracle left by the Goddess of Fate.",
    ["Dialogue7009102"]="Before Ragnarok, the three Norns in charge of fate foresaw the impending disaster. To leave seeds of hope in the world after Ragnarok, they warned the gods, and so the gods placed fragments of their consciousness into vessels called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Equipment</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7009103"]="The fragments of their consciousness lie dormant within the Shadow Equipment, which means that when a Shadow Equipment is awakened, it can call upon the power of the gods to temporarily summon divine weapons. If you have already made up your mind to fight for the future of the continent of Midgard, I will tell you how to obtain Shadow Equipment. Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue7009104"]="In order to guide adventurers and organizations possessing the power to change the world after Ragnarok and lead the world into the light, the Goddess of the Present, Verthandi, preserved her consciousness in this way on the continent of Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue7009105"]="So, when you pray to the Goddess Statue in your guild, Verthandi's preserved consciousness will guide you to obtain your fated Shadow Equipment. Successor of Odin's bloodline, enter your <color=#CA2E0AFF>guild territory</color>, find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Statue</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray</color> beneath it. The Goddess of Fate will give you the correct guidance.",
    ["Dialogue7009106"]="Well then, come back to me when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue7009201"]="What took you so long!",
    ["Dialogue7009202"]="This isn't good at all! You've almost missed your own wedding!",
    ["Dialogue7009203"]="The guests have already arrived. The only one missing is you, the main character of today! I'm telling you, it's the wedding season right now. Do you know how difficult it is to book a venue for a wedding?! Don't you want to have a grand and gorgeous wedding with the love of your life after you establish a contract with them?",
    ["Dialogue7009204"]="What...?! You haven't established a contract?! You haven't held the vow ceremony?! How can you get married then?!",
    ["Dialogue7009205"]="There's no time to waste. Follow me! I'm taking you to Archbishop Wolmas!",
    ["Dialogue7009301"]="(The Archbishop looks at you with a resigned expression.)\n...Doris, I've told you many times that the vow ceremony is very sacred and you shouldn't just go through the motions.",
    ["Dialogue7009302"]="First of all, both parties who have a solid relationship with one another need to be present to establish the contract. After establishing the contract, they must have a custom outfit made and find a suitable witness to bear witness to their feelings for one another. The official vow ceremony and wedding can only be held after all these preparations are completed. It's obvious that this adventurer hasn't met any of the conditions I mentioned.",
    ["Dialogue7009303"]="What? But my customer should have already...\n(Doris glances at you and becomes shocked.)\nNo... This isn't right! You aren't my customer?!",
    ["Dialogue7009304"]="(Doris freezes for two seconds then she holds her head in despair.)\nDid I actually... mistake you for someone else...?! Oh no... What should I do now...? The wedding... Has the wedding already started...?\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I'm done for... Nolan is going to scold me again... *Cries*</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue7009401"]="It's been a while since I last contacted you, Archbishop Wolmas. Adventurer... Did my wife cause you any trouble? I'm really sorry about this and apologize to you on her behalf.",
    ["Dialogue7009402"]="I'm fine, Nolan. This adventurer, on the other hand, was forcibly brought here by Doris. Hopefully nothing important was delayed.",
    ["Dialogue7009403"]="...Did Doris mistake you for the customer who is holding the wedding today?",
    ["Dialogue7009404"]="I'm sorry, I... Sigh, I messed everything up again. I'm just too stupid.\n(Doris lowers her head and looks really downcast as she draws circle after circle with the tip of her toes.)",
    ["Dialogue7009405"]="Oh...? Is that what happened?",
    ["Dialogue7009406"]="This adventurer is right. Doris, although you're reckless... you have sincere feelings that others can't match. Your enthusiasm also influences those who are about to get married, which makes them cherish their relationship even more.",
    ["Dialogue7009407"]="I... Actually, I'm not a lot of help... It's Nolan who plans... Huh? Huh? Oh right! The wedding! What happened to the customer's wedding?!",
    ["Dialogue7009408"]="(Nolan shakes his head helplessly and then reaches out to pat Doris' head.)\n...Relax, I've made arrangements for everything. The wedding is proceeding as scheduled, and the Flower Parade they reserved will be held after the wedding.",
    ["Dialogue7009409"]="Really? Nolan, you're the best!\n(Doris wraps her arms around Nolan's neck and kisses him fiercely.)",
    ["Dialogue7009410"]="(Nolan glances at you with an expression that looks like he is secretly pleased with himself).\n...The Prontera Wedding Planners also offer a blind dating service. If you want to try it out, I can give you a 20% discount on the registration fee.",
    ["Dialogue7009411"]="That being said, <color=#CA2E0AFF>custom weddings</color> are our main business. Don't let Doris' ditzy appearance fool you. She's actually quite talented at designing and planning weddings. From booking a venue to arranging the Flower Parade, we provide a one-stop service that guarantees you'll have a memorable wedding you'll never forget. How about it? Would you like to give it a try?",
    ["Dialogue7009412"]="Haha, then come to us after you <color=#CA2E0AFF>complete the vow ceremony</color> so we can customize your wedding! We look forward to seeing you!",
    ["Dialogue7009413"]="Ah, what a pity. It doesn't matter though. We're ready to serve you whenever you change your mind.",
    ["Dialogue7009501"]="Hello! Greetings, brave adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7009502"]="Nice to meet you! I'm Moon and I'm in charge of the Lantern Festival this year. These two cute little fellows, Gold and Silver are my partners and assistants! Come on, say hi to the adventurer!\n(The furry bunnies bounce in a circle around Moon.)",
    ["Dialogue7009503"]="Hehe! Do you see the gorgeous neon lights behind me? This is the Lantern Festival—a grand celebration we specially prepared for all adventurers!",
    ["Dialogue7009504"]="That's right! The Lantern Festival is a celebration held on the night with the first full moon of the year. It celebrates the start of a new year and new beginnings. People eat dumplings on this day in the hope that their families will stay together in the new year and to wish for happiness for the whole family. Of course Moon wants to spend such an important day with everyone!",
    ["Dialogue7009505"]="So, at my strong request, during the whole duration of the Lantern Festival, a lively Lantern Festival celebration will be held at the South Gate Amusement Park! Other than having fun on the rides with your friends, you can also play the fun games I have specially prepared! You'll get all sort of generous prizes if you win the games!",
    ["Dialogue7009506"]="Naturally! But don't underestimate Moon! It won't be easy to win these games! Are you ready for the challenge, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue7009507"]="Oh my, you look so charming when you're so energetic and motivated...\nOkay! I won't lose to you either! I'll help everyone create the most perfect memories of this Lantern Festival!",
    ["Dialogue7009508"]="You're not going to participate? What a pity... But it doesn't matter. You can come back to me at any time before the festival ends! I'll always be waiting for you!",
    ["Dialogue7009601"]="How can you have a Lantern Festival without lantern riddles!\nAhem... To tell you the truth, I have quite the reputation as a riddle solver in my hometown. So, do you want to have a competition with Moon?",
    ["Dialogue7009602"]="Heh, how boastful of you! No one has ever beaten me when it comes to solving lantern riddles and answering quizzes! I'll wager Gold and Silver's food for today. I'm going to beat you!",
    ["Dialogue7009701"]="Y-you're too good at this!\nSure enough... In the world of riddle solving, no one is the best—it's just a matter of whether you encounter someone who is better than you... I need to work harder to keep improving!",
    ["Dialogue7009702"]="Don't get too proud because of this! The Lantern Festival has just begun, and more trials await you in the amusement park!",
    ["Dialogue7009703"]="I won't be your opponent in the upcoming challenges. Instead, you'll compete against other adventures who have guessed the riddles correctly like you. Are you confident in your ability to defeat everyone else and become the ultimate winner?",
    ["Dialogue7009704"]="This is the momentum I wanted to see! Come with me, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7009801"]="Do you see these rocking chairs, Adventurer? The next game is a challenge that tests you physically and mentally! I will give you a riddle when the game starts, and the answer is hidden among in these rocking chairs. You'll need to compete with all the adventurers here to sit on the correct rocking chair. Please note that I'll fail you if you fail to get on the right chair, which means you'll need to take the challenge again!",
    ["Dialogue7009802"]="Are you ready? Here comes the riddle!",
    ["Dialogue7009901"]="You're amazing! You're good at solving riddles, and you even have top-notch reaction and speed! You looked as majestic as a swooping eagle when you ran for the rocking chairs... You must have experienced a lot during your adventures, right?",
    ["Dialogue7009902"]="Moon is really looking forward to seeing you become the ultimate winner now! However, your challenge is far from over! Follow me to the next game!",
    ["Dialogue7010001"]="Do you see the carousels on both sides? This is your next challenge! Speaking of it, it seems that the dream I had last night will be perfect for today's riddle. Whether you can win or not depends on whether you can solve my dream! Remember, you must ride on the correct carousel to pass the challenge!",
    ["Dialogue7010002"]="Are you ready? Here comes the riddle!",
    ["Dialogue7010101"]="What amazing wisdom, Adventurer! If you complete the final challenge, you'll get the Lantern Festival gift that Moon specially prepared!",
    ["Dialogue7010102"]="Oh my, that won't do. Isn't the most interesting part of riddles the process of solving them? How can I possibly reveal the answer in advance!",
    ["Dialogue7010103"]="This one is very simple. Adventurer, take the Mini Train with your most important friend!",
    ["Dialogue7010104"]="This is the simplest, but also the most important trial. The Lantern Festival is a festival that has been given many beautiful meanings, and it is a lively and warm custom. Whether it's enjoying the lanterns and lion dance, eating dumplings, or solving lantern riddles, the most beautiful blessing of this festival is the blessing to reunite with our family and friends and spend this festive day together! So, I want to give this blessing to the bravest adventurers!",
    ["Dialogue7010105"]="Although one lantern cannot illuminate the entire sky, as long as everyone pools together their efforts, I believe that even the darkest night will be greeted by the most beautiful dawn!",
    ["Dialogue7010106"]="Do you already have an answer? Uh-huh! That person must be someone important who has accompanied you on your adventures! Moon wants to hear your story... It's a pity that we don't have that much time. Let's chat about your wonderful adventures together after the Lantern Festival is over, okay?",
    ["Dialogue7010107"]="Now, invite the person in your heart and create the most memorable holiday memories together!",
    ["Dialogue7010201"]="Ooh! It seems that the final winner of the game has been born!\n(Moon lifts the corner of her skirt and swirls in a circle, looking even more excited than you.)",
    ["Dialogue7010202"]="You possess fearless courage and extraordinary wisdom, but more importantly, I have been deeply moved by the bond between you and your partner. You'll surely become the strongest adventurer on this land one day...\nAww, Moon really wants a friend like you...",
    ["Dialogue7010203"]="Huh? Really...?\n(Moon's eyes widen in surprise)\nAww... Moon is so touched! Adventurer, Moon loves you the most!",
    ["Dialogue7010204"]="I've decided! In addition to the prize of the game, I'll also give you Gold and Silver's food! These dumplings are delicious! Help yourself! Take them all!",
    ["Dialogue7010205"]="Also, the Lantern Festival will continue for a long time. Since we're already good friends, you have to come and play with me every day!\n(Moon shakes her head cutely and waves at you as she hops about.)\nYou have to come! I'll be waiting for you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7010301"]="\"In my dream last night, I was a novice who had just embarked on an adventure.\"",
    ["Dialogue7010302"]="\"Near the Prontera South Gate, a group of monsters chased after me because they claimed I had stolen something important to them.\"",
    ["Dialogue7010303"]="\"Their leader wore a crown and a manteau, just like the statue on the carousel over there—\"",
    ["Dialogue7010304"]="Okay, now make a guess. Which is the correct carousel?",
    ["Dialogue7010401"]="\"In my dream last night, everything was dark at first.\"",
    ["Dialogue7010402"]="\"Gradually, light appeared in the darkness, and a wonderful creature swam towards me.\"",
    ["Dialogue7010403"]="\"It looked like a beautiful blue parasol as it wobbled gracefully in the water, just like the statue on the carousel over there—\"",
    ["Dialogue7010404"]="Okay, now make a guess. Which is the correct carousel?",
    ["Dialogue7010501"]="Look who it is, an old adventurer? It's been a while, and you look stronger! Come on, roll up your sleeves and let me see.",
    ["Dialogue7010502"]="\"<size=26>Oooh, incredible improvements!</size>\n</size> It looks like you've gotten stronger on your journey here. I almost didn't notice you carrying that old, useless <color=#CA2E0AFF>Equipment</color>. Let it continue to collect dust in your backpack, it can't be worth much.\"",
    ["Dialogue7010503"]="What? You wouldn't consider recycling and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smelting</color> for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Equipment Materials</color> to make you stronger?",
    ["Dialogue7010504"]="(Hollgrehenn confidently brings his arms to his chest an nods in the direction of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color>.) Haha, of course I'll give it to my most loyal friend. Let's give it a try!",
    ["Dialogue7010601"]="Adventurer, wait! You're that adventurer who brought back the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue7010602"]="Great, I've finally found you! I'm Lysons of the Mage's Guild. We heard that you successfully retrieved the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, so we were thinking... Perhaps you could help us unravel a secret we've been guarding for a long, long time?",
    ["Dialogue7010603"]="I'm sure you've heard of the prophecies left behind by the three Norns. Each Norn left hope for the world after Ragnarok with her own remnant consciousness. Yet the fragment of remnant consciousness from Urd, the Norn who represents the \"past\", has been hidden away...",
    ["Dialogue7010604"]="Yes. This is the secret that the Mage's Guild has been guarding. The Norn Urd's remnant consciousness was gathered by the great Archmage Merlin and infused into several crystal balls. Within each crystal ball is sealed an <color=#CA2E0AFF>illusory battlefield of the past</color> that the Norn left for future generations—classic battles that exist only in epics.",
    ["Dialogue7010605"]="According to records, after Archmage Merlin founded the Pentagram, he used these crystal balls to <color=#CA2E0AFF>increase</color> the Pentagram's members' <color=#CA2E0AFF>combat capabilities</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>teamwork</color>. However, nobody after Archmage Merlin has known how to open these illusions. We can only rely on Archmage Merlin's manuscripts to find clues. But...",
    ["Dialogue7010606"]="All the materials mentioned in Merlin's manuscripts are difficult to obtain, and there are even some records we haven't been able to decipher. So when we heard that the heir of Odin's bloodline had appeared and brought back the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, we felt that we had a new hope. Maybe you can help us.",
    ["Dialogue7010607"]="I believe you can do it. Come with me!",
    ["Dialogue7010701"]="Adventurer, we've researched the crystal ball before you for a long time. According to records in the first chapter of Merlin's Manuscript, the illusory battlefield of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baphomet's legendary invasion of Prontera</color> is sealed within. So long as we can find the right way to open it, we can enter the illusion.",
    ["Dialogue7010702"]="According to Merlin's Manuscript, the illusion sealed within each crystal ball represents a type of conviction. The first chapter is called \"The Chapter of Courage.\" I think the battle at Prontera represents courage, so only a brave warrior with firm conviction can unlock the illusion within this crystal ball.",
    ["Dialogue7010703"]="We concocted this potion that represents courage—the \"Song of the Martyr\"—according to the records in Merlin's Manuscript, but we're just missing one important ingredient. Perhaps only you can help us. The ingredient is Warrior's Blood. I think that since you've faced so many challenges alone and are of Odin's bloodline, perhaps you're the warrior we've been searching for all along.",
    ["Dialogue7010801"]="I think we've actually finished making the \"Song of the Martyr\"! Adventurer, try sprinkling this potion on the crystal ball!",
    ["Dialogue7010901"]="You mean we just let it go?!",
    ["Dialogue7010902"]="But, but we can't even get close to the Heart Pedestal, let alone Ymir's Heart!\nUnless... unless it's the successor of Odin's bloodline...",
    ["Dialogue7010903"]="A-Adventurer?!",
    ["Dialogue7010904"]="Just in time, child! This is a dangerous and daunting quest, one only you can accomplish! \n(The ghostly old man stomps his feet, and you can hear a hint of anxiety in his ethereal voice.)",
    ["Dialogue7010905"]="Listen carefully, child! What I am about to tell is a hidden history unknown to the world! About a thousand years ago, the Archmage Merlin established an organization that brought together many high wizards called Pentagram, of which we were members. But no one knew that the purpose of its founding was to guard the dimensional gap under Geffen.",
    ["Dialogue7010906"]="Yes! It's a dimensional rift that leads straight to Niflheim! During that time, many monsters emerged from it attempting to invade Midgard. To stop them, Pentagram created Geffen Tower and the Magic Barrier to seal the Dimensional Gap underground along with these monsters. The ones who carried on our bloodlines, our descendants... They established the Mage Guild and have continued to maintain Geffen's peace to this day.",
    ["Dialogue7010907"]="...We were supposed to closely guard the Dimensional Gap under Geffen Tower with our companions. But recently, Lowell and I often sensed an evil aura seething out from underground. My guess is that the long passage of time has gradually loosened the seal placed by Archmage Merlin...",
    ["Dialogue7010908"]="That's the reason why we left Geffen, Adventurer. Although the seal still exists, there is already a strong aura of darkness leaking out. It will gradually spread its influence on the world, especially the Fragments of Ymir's Heart, the source of this world. It is extremely susceptible to the infestation of darkness.\n(Lowell lowers his head, seemingly to evade your eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue7010909"]="(As you look on puzzled, Eleanor jumps in.)\nSo... that's why we want to find the successor of Odin's bloodline to assist us in <color=#CA2E0AFF>purifying the tainted Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>! Otherwise, the fragments that have been placed on the Heart Pedestal will slowly fuse together with the elements of darkness...",
    ["Dialogue7010910"]="(Seeing you agree, Eleanor instantly shows a delighted expression.) \nIt's simple! Just like the Goddess taught you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>transmit the divine power of Odin within you to the Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>! This will strip away the dark aura from the fragments, giving you a chance to <color=#CA2E0AFF>destroy the evil power!</color>",
    ["Dialogue7010911"]="There's no time to lose. Let's head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>. Don't worry, Adventurer, I'll assist you from the sidelines! As for Lowell... Just wait here for our good news!",
    ["Dialogue7011001"]="Thank you so much for your willingness to help us, Adventurer.\n(Eleanor, who's waiting by the Heart Pedestal, bows to you respectfully.)\nAlso, please take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purgatory Mark</color>. It's important.",
    ["Dialogue7011002"]="The Purgatory Mark is a magic item that can collect dark energy. When you <color=#CA2E0AFF>transmit the power of Odin in your body to the Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>, the stripped dark energy crystallizes into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purgatory Mark Fragment</color>. Once the dark elemental energy accumulates to certain amount, a complete <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purgatory Mark</color> can be formed, which can then be used as a medium, allowing you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat the evil monsters that grow from the Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color> and complete its purification.",
    ["Dialogue7011003"]="However, the darkness-infested Fragments of Ymir's Heart emit stronger magic than usual, <color=#CA2E0AFF>imbuing the monsters with new powers</color>. Therefore, you must be even more careful.",
    ["Dialogue7011004"]="In addition, if you can obtain all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystals</color> they carry after defeating them, you can bring them to me. These crystals contain immense energy and can be refined into various items that will certainly benefit your adventures.",
    ["Dialogue7011005"]="Then... I'll leave the rest to you. May you return triumphantly, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7011101"]="Darn it... If only collecting samples was faster...\n(Sarence lowers his head and flips through the notes in his hand, muttering something you can't make out. As you are about to greet him, he suddenly raises his head.)\n<size=24>Ahh! Where is my hard-working and brave adventurer?</size>",
    ["Dialogue7011102"]="<size=24>...Adventurer?!</size>\n (Seeing you appear, Sarence's eyes widen with glee. He shakes your shoulder frantically, trying to share his joy with you.)\nYou finally showed up!!!",
    ["Dialogue7011103"]="Ah, sorry, sorry. I was just too happy and couldn't control my emotions for a second. After all, you're the brave hero who once traveled back in time and space to retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the Demon King Morroc! With your help, we'll be able to do our research twice as fast with half the effort!",
    ["Dialogue7011104"]="Huh? Woah! Don't throw up on me! Hey!!! This area is very arid, don't you know! You can't wash yourself here!\n(Sarence looks at the greenish goo on his clothes, his facial expression shifting multiple times.) \nFor-Forget it. After all, this is for something greater. For scientific research, sacrifices must be made!",
    ["Dialogue7011105"]="Ahem! Adventurer, since you have come here, it means that you have received my letter, right? I'll be straight with you. This Eden Group discovery can be said to be a breakthrough not seen in the archaeological world for many years! Look here—\n(Sarence holds up his notes to you, showing unknown words written on them.)",
    ["Dialogue7011106"]="Half a month ago, we found this poem in one of the cells of the Glast Heim Prison. It was engraved on the bricks in the corner of the wall, written in a contemporary script. According to some surviving information from the Eden Group, we learned that the owner of the cell was a bard who had angered King Schmidt by going around extolling the deeds of the Goddess. During his time in prison, the hopeless bard could only record his sufferings in writing...",
    ["Dialogue7011107"]="That's right! All the evidence points to the great battle—the very one you experienced when you fought the Demon King Morroc! Unfortunately, a considerable amount of written materials were destroyed in the war, leading to our inability to fully decipher the poem. Therefore, our research progress has been at a standstill...",
    ["Dialogue7011108"]="If you want to know the truth about that period of history, the first thing you have to do is decipher the ancient text of that period! If we have enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>text samples</color> for comparative analysis, we can find and map the relationships between ancient and modern scripts according to linguistic patterns, gradually determining the meaning corresponding to each symbol. The biggest problem we face now is the lack of text samples...",
    ["Dialogue7011109"]="This is the reason why the Eden Group seeks help! Adventurer, have you ever noticed that certain <color=#CA2E0AFF>long-living demons</color> carry devices with <color=#CA2E0AFF>unknown figures imprinted on them</color>? After observation, we believe that those figures and ancient scripts possess similar patterns and are most likely ancient artifacts that have been passed down from that period to the present, making them very suitable as samples for studying ancient scripts!",
    ["Dialogue7011110"]="As for which specific samples are needed, I have recorded them all in my <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archaeological Notes</color> here. Adventurer, you have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read them carefully</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7011201"]="Oh? Did you memorize the sample texts we need so quickly? Not bad for an Adventurer! Now please collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shrine Fragments</color> for me first!",
    ["Dialogue7011301"]="Thank you for your contributions to the Eden Group Institute, Adventurer! However, these samples alone are not enough to uncover true history. The work of deciphering the text is currently under the sole responsibility of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Laforet</color>. You can pass these samples to him to help him advance <color=#CA2E0AFF>research progress</color> together. Also, if there are any changes in the sample requirements, I will update them in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archaeological Notes</color>, so please remember to check them!",
    ["Dialogue7011401"]="I've been waiting for you for a long time, Adventurer. Quickly show me the samples you've brought!",
    ["Dialogue7011402"]="(Laforet takes the Shrine Fragment, puts it in his palm, looks at it carefully, and smiles with satisfaction.)\nGreat, this is the sample I need!",
    ["Dialogue7011403"]="Oh? Are you interested in the writing as well, Adventurer?\n(Laforet turns around excitedly, allowing you to observe the fragment in his hand, which has some strange patterns printed on it.)\nYou see the figures here? They are the same strokes repeated many times...",
    ["Dialogue7011404"]="That's right! Usually, most of the writing that appears on shrines is related to time. From this, it can be assumed that these words represent numbers and related calendars...\n(While Laforet talks endlessly, you can see in his eyes the ceaseless desire to learn, but then suddenly he hangs his head somewhat in frustration.)\nUnfortunately... with only these, it's not yet possible to determine the exact numbers that correspond to the figures...",
    ["Dialogue7011405"]="Adventurer, we are all very grateful for all the effort you put in searching for historical truth. Therefore, Sarence and I have discussed it, and agreed to giving you complete access to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group Supply Depot</color> while you look for texts for us, so please feel free to take whatever you need.",
    ["Dialogue7011501"]="How was it? Picked out the supplies you want?",
    ["Dialogue7011502"]="...Huh? You're saying you want to know how many samples it would take to decipher the full poem?\n(Laforet lowers his head, counting his fingers.)\nWell... It's hard to say... It might take a rather large number.",
    ["Dialogue7011503"]="0",
    ["Dialogue7011504"]="But I believe that if we persist in our research, one day these lost histories will be revealed and shown to the people once again!\n(Laforet grips the Shrine Fragment in his hand firmly, expressing his resolve.)\nThe Eden Group exists for this very reason!",
    ["Dialogue7011601"]="Adventurer, come here quickly. Shh, whisper. Look over there at that guy who's surrounded by Obeaunes.",
    ["Dialogue7011602"]="I don't know where he came from either. He just suddenly appeared at the tavern a few days ago. Turns out he's also a musician. He casually sang a few songs and won over a bunch of my fans. All the Obeaunes gather around him. I don't get his strange appeal.",
    ["Dialogue7011603"]="Jealous? Hahaha, as if. I am the most talented bard in Midgard and adored by countless women. Me being jealous of some stranger? No way, I'm... I'm just concerned that he'll deceive nice and innocent girls. Help me find out who that guy really is. I want to have a fair musical duel with him so that everyone can see who's the real star of this continent.",
    ["Dialogue7011701"]="Hey there. It looks like you're curious about me?",
    ["Dialogue7011702"]="Haha, it's still very obvious, huh? I've noticed that too. I don't think I belong in this world. I'm an artist. The other day, I finished my Halloween show and skateboarded past an entrance to a very flashy bar. I recall the name being something like Rose Red. After pushing the door open, I passed through a wondrous halo of light, and then I arrived here...",
    ["Dialogue7011703"]="A dimensional gap? I heard a lot about this land in the past two days and learned that when a dimensional gap is opened, something like what happened to me could occur. It looks like I need to investigate further to find a way back... But anyway, you came to see me. Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue7011704"]="So someone wants to play music with me. Of course they're welcome to anytime. After all, music has no boundaries. I'm also looking forward to hearing the music of this continent.",
    ["Dialogue7011801"]="So? Did you find out who he is?",
    ["Dialogue7011802"]="What?! He's actually an artist from a different world? No wonder he dresses so strangely. Everyone must've just been attracted to his uniqueness. Once I show him up with true musical talent during our duel, everyone will know who's the real musician. Yeah, I'm certain of it.",
    ["Dialogue7011803"]="N-nervous? As if. I'm the top bard in the continent. How can I lose to a measly outsider? Let's head over there quickly!",
    ["Dialogue7011901"]="Hey, how's it going? You're the musician who wants to have a musical exchange with me, right?",
    ["Dialogue7011902"]="Hello, I am Morts, Bard of Midgard, and I would like to have a fair musical duel with you.",
    ["Dialogue7011903"]="Hahaha, no problem. Inspiration sprouts from the exchange of musical notes. Let us give the audience a wonderful performance.",
    ["Dialogue7012001"]="You really are a great musician. I heard a very moving story through your music.",
    ["Dialogue7012002"]="I didn't think you would be able to harmonize with my lute. Your singing voice actually matches very well with it.",
    ["Dialogue7012003"]="So your instrument is called a lute? It has a unique sound I've never heard of before. It makes one want to sing.",
    ["Dialogue7012004"]="(A faint blush appears on Morts' face.) Oh, it's not that great. Your singing voice, on the other hand, is quite enchanting. Look around you. People are captivated by our performance.",
    ["Dialogue7012005"]="This is all the beauty of music, Mr. Morts. I also hear the sincerity and passion in your music. If you don't mind, would you like to be my first friend in this land? And also this here adventurer, of course. Thanks to you, we could have this splendid performance today.",
    ["Dialogue7012006"]="I'm very honored, but after speaking this long, we still don't know your name.",
    ["Dialogue7012007"]="Right, I forgot to introduce myself. My full name is Schumann Maxwell Herbert. Please just call me Schumann.",
    ["Dialogue7012008"]="Schumann, what are you going to do next?",
    ["Dialogue7012009"]="I don't think I'll be able to return soon, so I've decided to embark on a new adventure on this continent and figure out how to get back along the way. But before that, I have to find my skateboard.",
    ["Dialogue7012010"]="That's right. It has been my travel companion for many years. It allows me to freely traverse this land. I seem to have lost it when I was being transported. These past two days, the patrons at the tavern have been telling me about a person named Vienna Lindra who is selling a strange item that sounds like my skateboard.",
    ["Dialogue7012011"]="What does your skateboard look like exactly? Maybe we can look around and bring it back to you?",
    ["Dialogue7012012"]="It's a flat and long black board with four silver wheels underneath. I think you'll be able to recognize it once you see it.",
    ["Dialogue7012101"]="Oh, Adventurer, what are you looking for? I have everything you need here. I also have some strange items I received recently.",
    ["Dialogue7012102"]="Here, look. I happened to get this device when the dimensional gap appeared. I think it must be a valuable item from some strange world. If I can find the right buyer, I'll be able to sell it for a good price. After all, there are many adventurers who like researching about the other worlds.",
    ["Dialogue7012103"]="Huh? You know what this thing is?",
    ["Dialogue7012104"]="I see. Since this is your friend's lost possession, why don't you take this strange thing back to him? The Lindra Family is not in the dirty business of appropriating other people's belongings. Oh yes, I also have a peculiar item that I obtained together with the skateboard. It looks like it came from another world as well. Why don't you also take this back to your friend? Maybe he lost this too.",
    ["Dialogue7012201"]="Wow! Thank you so much. This really is my skateboard. Great, now I'm even more excited about the new adventure.",
    ["Dialogue7012202"]="Oh? Is there something else?",
    ["Dialogue7012301"]="What?!! I thought I'd never get this model back. I can't believe you have it.",
    ["Dialogue7012302"]="It's a race car model. Car racing is a kind of... speed competition in my world. In any case, this model represents something important to me, and I'm very thankful that you've brought it back to me. I actually carried many of these things in my backpack while I was being transported. If you collect other such race car models during your travels, please be sure to bring them back to me.",
    ["Dialogue7012303"]="This is great. I'm incredibly excited for this new journey now. Perhaps I can also spread my music and culture to this new land. Adventurer, I hope that in our future adventures, we can find new dreams and create unique memories together!",
    ["Dialogue7012401"]="Hey! Dear Adventurer, want to add something different to your adventurous life? Wanna have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>faithful travel companion</color> that's cuddly to you but ferocious to your enemies? Come to Lyra's Pet Shop for all your needs!",
    ["Dialogue7012402"]="Huh? Is this your first time coming into contact with a pet?",
    ["Dialogue7012403"]="No problem! As the manager of Lyra's Pet Shop, it's my duty to explain everything about pets to new and valuable customers, free of charge. Hmm... Let me think of where to start... Ah! How about you start by <color=#CA2E0AFF>ordering a slingshot</color> from me? A proper slingshot can precisely control the HP of pets to gently tame them!",
    ["Dialogue7012404"]="As the manager of Lyra's Pet Shop, it's my duty to explain everything about pets to new and valuable customers, free of charge. Hmm... Let me think of where to start... Ah! How about you start by <color=#CA2E0AFF>ordering a Pet Slingshot</color> from me? When using a Pet Slingshot to tame a pet, it <color=#CA2E0AFF>deals True Damage equal to 30% HP of the target pet</color> every time. Use the proper slingshot to precisely control the HP of pets and gently tame them!",
    ["Dialogue7012501"]="(Lyra sees that you haven't left and rushes to greet you.)\nDear customer, is there anything else you need?",
    ["Dialogue7012502"]="Oops! That was an oversight on my part. It looks like I'll have to add instructions next time.. The slingshot and the bullets work together. By <color=#CA2E0AFF>loading the bullet into the slingshot</color>, you can utilize the power of both. Dear customer of unlimited potential, come back to me when you're done loading it to start the next step of the tutorial!",
    ["Dialogue7012601"]="You finished so quickly! Ooh, look at that exquisite pattern and that excellent workmanship! A product worthy of Lyra's reputation!",
    ["Dialogue7012602"]="I'm so sorry! Got caught up in the artistry of slingshots for a moment... Now that you've loaded it, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go see my friend Taksch at Prontera South Gate</color>. Though this guy often owes me money, I have to admit he's a pet catching master and can surely show you the tricks to capturing them!",
    ["Dialogue7012603"]="I'm so sorry! Got caught up in the artistry of slingshots for a moment... Now that you've equipped it, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go see my friend Taksch at Prontera South Gate</color>. Though this guy often owes me money, I have to admit he's a master pet tamer and can surely show you the tricks to taming them!",
    ["Dialogue7012701"]="Hmm? I haven't seen you before.",
    ["Dialogue7012702"]="(Taksch quickly interrupts you)\nI see! So you‘re Lyra's customer! Did my outstanding pet capturing skills attract you here as well?",
    ["Dialogue7012703"]="Not talking? Well, I like modest and reserved newbies because they can often seize opportunities and obtain their desired pet the fastest. See that Lunatic? Take your slingshot and <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat it</color>. Then...",
    ["Dialogue7012704"]="Huh? Wait!",
    ["Dialogue7012801"]="Ugh...",
    ["Dialogue7012802"]="(Taksch looks at you with a sorry face and sighs.)\nAdventurer, I admit you have extraordinary talent, but... do you remember what I said at the end?",
    ["Dialogue7012803"]="(Taksch pats you on the shoulder, giving you cheerful smile)\nOkay okay, listen carefully this time. Defeating a monster doesn't mean a successful capture. To make a monster become a pet that fights for you, we also need the power of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pet Encyclopedia</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7012804"]="That's right. Follow my tips...",
    ["Dialogue7012901"]="Not bad, not bad. Now... next is the last part of the lesson. The taming process is inevitably accompanied by fighting, but something every newcomer must learn is how to appease their future battle companion.",
    ["Dialogue7012902"]="When it comes to catching pets, <color=#CA2E0AFF>winning them over</color> is of vital importance. Guess which kind of items can attract monsters?",
    ["Dialogue7012903"]="Hmm, <color=#CA2E0AFF>each type of pet has its own favorite item</color>. Between the following two items, which one would you use to tame the corresponding pet?",
    ["Dialogue7013001"]="Well, <color=#CA2E0AFF>each pet has its own preference</color>, and your choice of item is only preferred by some. In addition, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the lower the HP of the monster, the higher the probability of catching it</color>. Depleting their HP is also a challenge for trainers.",
    ["Dialogue7013002"]="I guess not, Adventurer. You've learned the principles, but real-world practice will teach you more. Why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>try to catch a pet of your choice</color> now! You're sure to learn more about the ways of pets as you fight alongside them!\nHmm... Since I taught Lyra's customer, shouldn't that square my account...?",
    ["Dialogue7013003"]="For pet taming, it's very important to <color=#CA2E0AFF>know the monster's preference</color>. In addition, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the lower the monster's HP, the higher the success rate</color>. Once you've dealt 90% HP of True Damage to the monster <color=#CA2E0AFF>after using the slingshot the third time</color>, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>stop attacking</color> the monster and try to tame it.",
    ["Dialogue7013004"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>After using the taming skill</color>, let your fate take control of the result and <color=#CA2E0AFF>determine whether it's a success or not</color>. Just wait for it. It's said that for whoever <color=#CA2E0AFF>tames a pet the first time</color>, Lady Luck will endow them with a magic that <color=#CA2E0AFF>guarantees their success</color>, but meantime <color=#CA2E0AFF>it eliminates the chance of taming a pet of superior quality</color>. Besides luck, you also need to keep sharpening your skill in pet taming in the future.",
    ["Dialogue7013005"]="After successfully taming a pet, you can then decide whether to adopt it as your pet. Only will it be added to your pet list <color=#CA2E0AFF>once you confirm the adoption</color>. Remember to <color=#CA2E0AFF>spend more time with it</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7013101"]="Hang on to this. This is a gift for you. Remember! The lower the Pet's HP, the easier it is for you to catch it, and your chances of getting a high Grade Pet will also be higher.",
    ["Dialogue7013201"]="Huh? That's odd... How come only you can see us?!",
    ["Dialogue7013202"]="That can't be... I thought no one would notice if I kept my aura hidden.",
    ["Dialogue7013203"]="No, that's not it. You look like an ordinary human from the outside, and you hid your aura well.",
    ["Dialogue7013204"]="So, that means...?",
    ["Dialogue7013205"]="Yes, that's the answer. Perhaps this world has corresponding records—no, not just for anyone—for a certain individual named Rimuru Tempest.",
    ["Dialogue7013206"]="Huh?! Me?! In another world?!",
    ["Dialogue7013207"]="After all, Lord Rimuru, it is understandable that your great name would transcend other worlds.",
    ["Dialogue7013208"]="But Lord Rimuru, we have other matters to attend to here. In your efforts to avoid detection, it seems you haven't obtained the information we require.",
    ["Dialogue7013209"]="Although, spending time alone with Lord Rimuru is a rare treat indeed, so I certainly won't object to us extending our time together.",
    ["Dialogue7013210"]="Ah, yes! We came here to track down the Orc Disaster, but it looks like Shuna's the only one who followed me here...",
    ["Dialogue7013211"]="Oh, my apologies! I forgot I was talking to you. But anyway, I'm afraid we're chasing a truly terrible monster, you see. If we let it go, the kingdom could very well face destruction!",
    ["Dialogue7013212"]="All I had to do was land the finishing blow on the thing, but it ignored all of our interference and ran straight into the teleportation spell. We came here after it, but it somehow managed to elude us.",
    ["Dialogue7013213"]="Searched high and low, we did, but not even Lord Rimuru could find a trace of Orc Disaster. Who knows what kind of catastrophe will unfold if we let it wreak havoc on this world?!",
    ["Dialogue7013214"]="(Whispering) I also don't know why Raphael's abilities aren't that useful in this place...",
    ["Dialogue7013215"]="Yes, that's it. We need to gather intelligence anew after journeying to this strange world—we'll just have to accept our temporary powerlessness.",
    ["Dialogue7013216"]="*whispering* Ah, well, I suppose if that's how it is...",
    ["Dialogue7013217"]="Oh my, oh my! I didn't expect the people of this world to be so kindhearted!",
    ["Dialogue7013218"]="We actually came here with quite a large crew, but we got separated when crossing over. Therefore, we'll have to locate them all first before we can take further action.",
    ["Dialogue7013219"]="I think they might try to contact us, too. If you see any names like Benimaru or Shion on the Mission Board, or anywhere similar, please be sure to let me know!",
    ["Dialogue7013220"]="Let's go, Shuna. We've finally made some progress, so let's start taking action.",
    ["Dialogue7013221"]="As you wish, Lord Rimuru!",
    ["Dialogue7013301"]="Oh, it's you! Have you come across any information pertaining to the Orc Disaster's whereabouts?!",
    ["Dialogue7013302"]="Ah! Yes, indeed! This has the Orc Disaster written all over it!",
    ["Dialogue7013303"]="It seems that, even if they're from different worlds, swine will always prefer to roll around in the mud with their own kind...",
    ["Dialogue7013304"]="That's it, indeed.",
    ["Dialogue7013305"]="*whispering* Come on, you're making me look bad...",
    ["Dialogue7013306"]="By the way, we also picked up some amazing information on our travels. *leaning in* (Would you like to hear it?)",
    ["Dialogue7013307"]="Before even managing to find Benimaru and the others, we found a \"portal\" of sorts.",
    ["Dialogue7013308"]="As it only remains open for very short stretches of time, I assume that it was generated by the magical fluctuations caused by our rather sizable expedition to this world.",
    ["Dialogue7013309"]="But really it's something that must be seen with one's own eyes... Come on! I'll show you!",
    ["Dialogue7013310"]="Behold! the \"Wonderland\"!",
    ["Dialogue7013311"]="As the magic elements we brought here with us were clearly too powerful, it seems that a residual impression of them has been imprinted here!",
    ["Dialogue7013312"]="It's like an almost perfect replication. I've never seen such a thing in my life!",
    ["Dialogue7013313"]="It seems that this wonderland has specific rules, which are quite different from those of the real world.",
    ["Dialogue7013314"]="Indeed. For the convenience of this explanation, let's say that these \"rules\" are essentially based on the principle of \"moving by rolling dice\".",
    ["Dialogue7013315"]="And what's more, it seems even outsiders who enter this place can directly interact with the things here. In other words, everything here appears to be removable!",
    ["Dialogue7013316"]="But back to business—there's something I must talk to you about.",
    ["Dialogue7013317"]="In addition to finding this wonderland, we of course found Benimaru and the others.",
    ["Dialogue7013318"]="However, they are all dealing with the monsters at the locations they each happened to find themselves, and they haven't had a chance to meet up with us.",
    ["Dialogue7013319"]="But as I mentioned, when they arrived here, they made intelligent use of the Mission Board.",
    ["Dialogue7013320"]="I went to have a look for myself—they've already posted many interesting missions!",
    ["Dialogue7013321"]="Now that we've ascertained his location, all that remains is to crush him!",
    ["Dialogue7013322"]="Thank you for your help... Now, let's get down to brass tacks!",
    ["Dialogue7013501"]="Adventurer, wait! You're that adventurer who brought back the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue7013502"]="Great, I've finally found you! I'm Lysons of the Mage's Guild. We heard that you successfully retrieved the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, so we were thinking... Perhaps you could help us unravel a secret we've been guarding for a long, long time?",
    ["Dialogue7013503"]="I'm sure you've heard of the prophecies left behind by the three Norns. Each Norn left hope for the world after Ragnarok with her own remnant consciousness. Yet the fragment of remnant consciousness from Urd, the Norn who represents the \"past\", has been hidden away.",
    ["Dialogue7013504"]="Yes. This is the secret that the Mage's Guild has been guarding. The Norn Urd's remnant consciousness was gathered by the great Archmage Merlin and infused into several tomes. Within each crystal ball is sealed an illusory battlefield of the past that the Norn left for future generations—classic battles that exist only in epics.",
    ["Dialogue7013505"]="According to records, after Archmage Merlin founded Pentagram, he used these tomes to increase Pentagram's members' combat capabilities and teamwork. However, nobody after Archmage Merlin has known how to open these illusions. We can only rely on Archmage Merlin's manuscripts to find clues. But...",
    ["Dialogue7013506"]="All the materials mentioned in Merlin's manuscripts are difficult to obtain, and there are even some records we haven't been able to decipher. So when we heard that the heir of Odin's bloodline had appeared and brought back the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, we felt that we had a new hope. Maybe you can help us.",
    ["Dialogue7013507"]="I believe you can do it. Come with me!",
    ["Dialogue7013601"]="Aside from the fated hero, the prophecy also mentions that \"a controller of events will create a key for the hero.\" I wonder who it could be?",
    ["Dialogue7013602"]="Let me see... \"Manager of ancient codices\"... \"Ancient wisdom within reach\"... Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue7013603"]="Indeed, Winry is likely the person who best fits this description. Perhaps it's her?",
    ["Dialogue7013701"]="\"Create a key\" and \"controller of events\"? It sounds a bit cryptic. It's hard to make heads or tails of it.",
    ["Dialogue7013702"]="Specifically, it states that \"the hero will bring an offering with which the controller of events will create a key.\"",
    ["Dialogue7013703"]="Perhaps it's requesting the adventurer to bring something, and then having Winry do something with it? Look, Winry, here's what you need to do in detail...",
    ["Dialogue7013704"]="Hmm, I see... First I do this, then this... I understand.",
    ["Dialogue7013705"]="I've got the gist of it. So long as the adventurer brings me a suitable object, I can create the key. Well then, let's do an experiment.",
    ["Dialogue7013801"]="We've done it! Now, all we need to do is pass through here to arrive in the illusion the prophecy spoke of. I don't know if I have what it takes, though...",
    ["Dialogue7013802"]="Hmm... Let me give it a try. Could you put it back on that bookshelf?",
    ["Dialogue7013901"]="Ah! So this is the gate the prophecy spoke of...",
    ["Dialogue7013902"]="The \"key\" and \"gate\" are all present, so naturally the \"path\" will open. Hero, we've further recreated the prophecy. Now we can go into the illusion.",
    ["Dialogue7013903"]="... Wait a moment, hero.",
    ["Dialogue7014001"]="We've found the prophesized hero, and the path to the events has been opened, but there's still part of the prophecy remaining. We'd best not be too hasty.",
    ["Dialogue7014002"]="\"The illusion depicted in the event is an ancient battlefield that not even the mightiest of warriors can brave alone...\"",
    ["Dialogue7014003"]="\"The prophesized hero will come to the coordinates. The locator will show the way\"...",
    ["Dialogue7014004"]="Yes, it seems the locator plays an important role in the next step. But what clues do we have about it?",
    ["Dialogue7014005"]="Ah, wait a moment. Did the crystal ball over there just...?",
    ["Dialogue7014101"]="How unexpected! We'd always believed this crystal ball to be nothing more than a decoration.",
    ["Dialogue7014102"]="If I must give an explanation, perhaps only the prophesized hero can interact with the relic?",
    ["Dialogue7014103"]="Maybe? But the crystal ball has been active ever since it was activated just a moment ago, so perhaps we woke it up?",
    ["Dialogue7014201"]="But the prophecy doesn't seem to have ended yet. Have a look, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7014202"]="Half of a prophecy seems to remain inside the crystal ball. It looks like our work isn't over just yet.",
    ["Dialogue7014203"]="\"Heroes who gather here, be warned that the illusion is not harmless; it can bring true pain and even death unto heroes.\"",
    ["Dialogue7014204"]="\"The illusion is not completely isolated from reality, thus heroes must be cautious in their influence on the illusion. The illusion will last for seven days, during which objects must not be taken from within it more than once.\"",
    ["Dialogue7014205"]="If there was no risk, then it wouldn't have been preserved in such a way. The gods naturally have their own considerations, I guess...",
    ["Dialogue7014301"]="I don't know if any parts of the prophecy were left out.",
    ["Dialogue7014302"]="Ah, there's only two more lines left in the prophecy, so you should be able to get an answer... Hmm, \"the controller will hold the proof; <color=#CA2E0AFF>Illusion Certificate</color>￼ will aid the hero.\"",
    ["Dialogue7014303"]="Speaking of which, when the Illusion Key was made just now, a lot of magic flowed onto the page over here.",
    ["Dialogue7014304"]="It looks like it's some sort of certificate. There's one more sentence, too: \"Those who wield proof may compete for their reward; only the most qualified will receive it.\"",
    ["Dialogue7014305"]="Generally speaking, no. But that's where the prophecy ends. As for how to train heroes in the illusion, I guess you'll have to experience it for yourself to find out.",
    ["Dialogue7014306"]="There's no time to lose.",
    ["Dialogue7014501"]="The successor of Odin's bloodline... The envoy who carries out his order... Here you come...",
    ["Dialogue7014502"]="Midgard is shrouded in darkness once again. Their evil greed eventually makes the fate of both worlds intersect as they covet the strength that lies within the Fragment of Ymir's Heart...",
    ["Dialogue7014503"]="You know, Satan Morroc has never stopped trying to break through the seal in the bottomless Dimensional Gap. Even though his body is imprisoned, his power has far reached into the continent of Midgard, becoming a persisting violet haze that lurks around and gets more powerful day after day.",
    ["Dialogue7014504"]="Haze has engulfed Midgard, and devastating disasters shall fall upon Midgard. There is no way I can predict which side will win this time...",
    ["Dialogue7014505"]="The light and darkness, good and evil, co-exist with each other... Listen to my guidance and look for the hero of light, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ultraman</color>. Don't be scared. No darkness will remain hidden under Odin's watch...",
    ["Dialogue7014601"]="(A man wearing a weird outfit is checking out the surroundings, and he looks you in the eye suddenly.)\nYou! You were looking at me just now!",
    ["Dialogue7014602"]="Hey! Don't underestimate my attention to detail. What's your deal here? This place is dangerous, and I suggest you find somewhere to hide.",
    ["Dialogue7014603"]="I'm not trying to scare you, \"that group\" might have landed their eyes on this world. I am not going to let this happen!",
    ["Dialogue7014604"]="God?! Huh??? Do you mean those things that fly in the air??? So, you're the servant of God?",
    ["Dialogue7014605"]="No, No, No! I'm too young for this...",
    ["Dialogue7014606"]="Ahem... I mean... We should help each other out, right? You know the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Star of Darkness</color> is hard to deal with. We might see the god for real if we don't take it seriously!",
    ["Dialogue7014607"]="Aha! I like you! Then let's get started! It's our battle from now on!",
    ["Dialogue7014701"]="Adventurer, my crew has detected unusual energy frustration everywhere on Midgard, and we can not factor out the possibility that the monsters are causing this.",
    ["Dialogue7014702"]="In our opinion, this investigation should be tasked to the local who is more familiar with this land. If you are willing...",
    ["Dialogue7014703"]="Are you willing to help...? Nice! Adventurer, we will narrow down the places that need to be investigated and send the <color=#CA2E0AFF>on-site photos</color> to you.",
    ["Dialogue7014704"]="You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach the destination</color> by following the clues from the photos. Please be very careful once you get there! Because... We are not sure what we are facing.",
    ["Dialogue7014705"]="(Kotaro Higashi pats your shoulder.)\nPromise me that you are coming back in one piece!",
    ["Dialogue7014801"]="You are back! Let me see... hmm... limbs are intact, and blood still flows in your vein. I knew that I could count on you!",
    ["Dialogue7014802"]="So... it's reward time! Adventurer! Thank you for the service of guarding peace and justice. Now please accept this reward!",
    ["Dialogue7014901"]="(The bulky man sizes you up and down, smiling at last.)\nAdventurer, the great successor of Odin's bloodline. How have you been lately?",
    ["Dialogue7014902"]="Ah, seems you've had your hands full.",
    ["Dialogue7014903"]="Adventurer, hear me out. I want to invite you to join the new arena competitive event—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Party Tussle</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7014904"]="Even the strongest stand vulnerable alone, Adventurer. A formidable lion can be cornered by hyenas without its pride. Therefore, to prepare everyone to <color=#CA2E0AFF>tackle future threats and challenges</color>, I've set up the Party Tussle.",
    ["Dialogue7014905"]="Your task, Adventurer, is to recruit your party members, <color=#CA2E0AFF>creating an unbeatable party</color>. In the arena, mutual trust and collaboration are the keys to survival. Only in unity will you prevail.",
    ["Dialogue7014906"]="Our goal is to select a true warrior <color=#CA2E0AFF>who can lead us into the future</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7014907"]="That's the spirit I'm talking about!",
    ["Dialogue7014908"]="Step into the fray, Adventurer! Only true heroes can bathe in the glory of triumph. I can't wait to see you unleash your might in the arena!",
    ["Dialogue7015001"]="Yo, Adventurer! Come over here real quick.",
    ["Dialogue7015002"]="Here's the thing. Tony Chir, the Head of the Free Arena, has rolled out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new competitive event</color>. He asked me, the wandering bard, to spread the word.",
    ["Dialogue7015003"]="Ahem! That's not the point. I've been thinking you might just be the right person for this task.",
    ["Dialogue7015004"]="Nah. You are the famed hero of Midgard. If you make a splash in the arena, I will ensure your tales spread far and wide. How does that sound?",
    ["Dialogue7015005"]="Find Tony Chir, and he will clue you in what to do next.",
    ["Dialogue7015301"]="(The man busy promoting his business reaches out to stop you.)\nHi there! Check it out and see if you find yourself your dream house! You know we are offering a <color=#CA2E0AFF>crazy discount</color> right now. You don't want to miss it!",
    ["Dialogue7015302"]="That's okay. You can take a look now and set it as your goal.\n(The man sizes you up and down, thinking about something.)\nHold on, are you the legendary Adventurer, the hero everyone's talking about?",
    ["Dialogue7015303"]="Great! Since you are the hero of the kingdom, I can figure out something for you. To honor your contributions to the kingdom, I've decided to offer you a property for <color=#CA2E0AFF>free</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7015304"]="However...",
    ["Dialogue7015305"]="On one condition, I need you to do me a small favor. As long as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>get this done for me</color>, you will become a proud owner of a brand-new home.",
    ["Dialogue7015306"]="Just so you know, all our properties are upscale and fancy estates that come with top-notch butlers from every industry. We're cool with all the other butlers; it's just this particular one, Peierls, the butler responsible for the pond. We still need to iron out some details in the contract.",
    ["Dialogue7015307"]="I've heard that the fishing expert, Xavier, is right down at Prontera's Southgate. If we could get a letter of endorsement from him, I bet this whole thing would be a walk in the park. However, I don't really know him that well, so you are the only person I can turn to, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7015308"]="Adventurer, I'm counting on you.",
    ["Dialogue7015401"]="(There's Xavier slumped by the water, moaning softly. He came back to life once he saw you.)\nHa... Haha! Ad-Adventurer! Here you come!",
    ["Dialogue7015402"]="Adventurer, it has been days since I caught anything. No fish, no dried fish, no nothing... I'm dying here. If I don't make it this time... I want you to take good care of this fishing rod...",
    ["Dialogue7015501"]="Hmm... It's raw. This is gonna upset my stomach.",
    ["Dialogue7015502"]="(Xavier gobbled down the Carp in no time.)\nWhew, I'm good now. Thanks to you, Adventurer. By the way, make it dried fish next time; no more sashimi, okay?",
    ["Dialogue7015503"]="(Xavier bounced up.)\nSpill it. Why are you here?",
    ["Dialogue7015504"]="I see... Leave this to me. Me and Peierls go way back. Consider it done, Adventure.",
    ["Dialogue7015601"]="I expect nothing less from the successor of Odin's bloodline, the legendary Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7015602"]="Great! With this letter, I'm sure Peierls will take the job at the estate now!",
    ["Dialogue7015603"]="Here, Adventurer, accept your reward. I've prepared you with a luxurious estate. Now, take a tour of your new home.",
    ["Dialogue7015701"]="Greetings, Adventurer. I've walked you through the <color=#CA2E0AFF>basics of the mine operation</color> before, and now I will get into more advanced features and functions for you.",
    ["Dialogue7015702"]="Yes, even though I can handle the daily management of your mine, you are the person in charge if you want to keep constructing the mine and receive rich mineral resources. I need you to step up the game and know the ins and outs of the mine.",
    ["Dialogue7015801"]="Congratulations, Adventurer. You have now mastered the basics of the mine operations.",
    ["Dialogue7015802"]="You're welcome, Adventurer. I'm just doing my job as your estate butler.",
    ["Dialogue7015803"]="Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait patiently until the mining is completed</color>, then I will fill you in on the next step.",
    ["Dialogue7015901"]="Adventurer, the skill set you've got under your belt is good enough for us to build a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mine of a higher level</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7015902"]="Building a higher-level mine allows us to get even more rare mineral resources, laying a solid foundation for our home construction in the future.",
    ["Dialogue7015903"]="When the mine upgrade is completed, you can start constructing <color=#CA2E0AFF>a home of a higher level</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7016001"]="Here you are, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7016002"]="Adventurer, can you tell me how much you know about fish?",
    ["Dialogue7016003"]="Delicious...\n(Peierls gets all serious.)\nLooks like I need to prep you from the beginning. I don't want to see you turn the pond into a hot mess!",
    ["Dialogue7016101"]="(Peierls nods with satisfaction.)\nFinally, you're looking a bit like an estate owner.\nBut remember, you're still a rookie in fish farming.",
    ["Dialogue7016102"]="Hmm... Even though you're just starting out, I think you are ready to step up to a <color=#CA2E0AFF> higher-level pond</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7016103"]="It's time to upgrade your pond to Lv.2. I will help you out.",
    ["Dialogue7016201"]="Adventurer, keep this in mind: a fish pond isn't like a mine where you can just sit back and chill. These fingerlings are delicate and need constant care.",
    ["Dialogue7016202"]="I get it; you've got a lot on your plate. You are an Adventurer, after all.",
    ["Dialogue7016203"]="Let me think.\n(Peierls' eyes sparkle.)\nI've got it! When you're out, <color=#CA2E0AFF>assign one of your pets</color> to take care of your pond, and I will teach them how to do so. Sounds good?",
    ["Dialogue7016204"]="You better send a smart one.",
    ["Dialogue7016301"]="Aha, here you are, Adventurer. I believe you have talked to Peierls and Lehner. How did that go?",
    ["Dialogue7016302"]="Haha, don't you start chilling yet. The most <color=#CA2E0AFF>demanding and difficult task</color> in home construction is the farmland. Get yourself ready for it.",
    ["Dialogue7016303"]="(Skylie pats her chest with full confidence.)\nBut hey, don't sweat it too much. I've got your back, the professional farmland expert Skylie!",
    ["Dialogue7016401"]="Nice work! Adventurer, you're natural.",
    ["Dialogue7016402"]="Keep the ego in check. These are just the basics. But for now, they're good enough for you.",
    ["Dialogue7016403"]="Right, there are plenty of empty lots over there. Don't waste them.",
    ["Dialogue7016501"]="Adventurer, here's good news: I've done an analysis for the ore vein layout, and there could be an <color=#CA2E0AFF>extremely precious ore vein</color> hidden in your mine!",
    ["Dialogue7016502"]="Easy there, don't start celebrating yet. Your mining setup is not ready for in-depth exploration, so we are going to upgrade the mine first.",
    ["Dialogue7016503"]="Besides, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>assign a pet</color> to the mine. It can help you to avoid some potential risks and handle the mining business when it is free.",
    ["Dialogue7016601"]="Adventurer, this is the estate I've prepared for you. It's all yours from here on out.",
    ["Dialogue7016602"]="(Ronald smiles with a hint of regret.)\nHowever, it doesn't come with the full-service home management since it's free. No worries, though. We will still get you the essential butlers in your home to keep your place in check.",
    ["Dialogue7016603"]="Yes, we have assigned them in every corresponding area to help you settle in and learn everything about your new home.",
    ["Dialogue7016604"]="Your home is more than just a place to live. If you want to, you can roll up your sleeves and get to work. Of course, everything you earn is yours to keep.",
    ["Dialogue7016605"]="Now, follow me. Let me give you a tour of different facilities and their corresponding butlers in your home.",
    ["Dialogue7016701"]="Adventurer, this is our mine butler, Lehner. He's a senior mineral resource manager who excels in analyzing, researching, and exploiting ore veins.",
    ["Dialogue7016702"]="Hello, Adventurer. I'll be the one to walk you through the functions and operations of the mine in your home.",
    ["Dialogue7016703"]="First off, we need to explore the mine and pinpoint the exact location of an ore vein. When we know where it is, we can get to mining. I'll spot you an easy ore vein to start with; it's not much, but it's great for starters.",
    ["Dialogue7016704"]="By the way, this is for you—the Stamina Potion specially crafted by the kingdom. It's a big help for those of us who do a lot of physical work. Busy as you'll be, but make sure to take breaks, okay?",
    ["Dialogue7016801"]="Adventurer, this is our fishing expert and your pond butler at your home, Peierls. Should you have any questions about the pond, he's the guy you want to talk to.",
    ["Dialogue7016802"]="You must be the legendary Adventurer. Heard a lot about you.",
    ["Dialogue7016803"]="Let's get down to business. I'll show you how the pond works around here. First things first, it's all about fingerlings in the pond. We will provide you with various types of fingerlings for you to choose from. You can get used to how to release fingerlings, and I will explain more details to you.",
    ["Dialogue7016901"]="Adventurer, this is our farmland butler, Skylie. You can ask her any questions about the farmland.",
    ["Dialogue7016902"]="Greetings, Adventurer! I'm your farmland butler, Skylie.",
    ["Dialogue7016903"]="I assume you've met Peierls already, and you should have a basic idea of how to manage your home. So, you'll probably understand what I'm about to say very quickly.",
    ["Dialogue7016904"]="Just like the pond, the farmland also provides you with many different seeds to choose from. Before we start, I need you to familiarize yourself with the soil and seeds.",
    ["Dialogue7016905"]="Heads up, don't plant the seeds and just leave them there. Fertility in the soil is limited, and it's directly related to your yield. I will keep an eye on the fertility but do come back often to fertilize them.",
    ["Dialogue7017001"]="Very good, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7017002"]="Spotting the ore vein is only the beginning. Next, I need you to give the minecart a try and start gathering from the ore vein.",
    ["Dialogue7017003"]="Keep in mind that even though the minecart does the mining by itself, it has a limited capacity that only holds up to 50 units. Be sure to drop in and empty it from time to time. Plus, upgrading the mine also increases your minecart's capacity.",
    ["Dialogue7017101"]="Wait, hold on! Where are you going, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue7017102"]="(Peierls takes a deep breath.)\nRaising fingerlings is nothing like mining ore veins, where you simply hit the buttons on the machines and wait for them. If you are slacking, they'll take forever to grow.",
    ["Dialogue7017103"]="Yes, fish growth requires all sorts of nourishment, but the food in the pond is limited. You need to feed them regularly to speed things up. I have a bag of Growth Bait here. Give it a try.",
    ["Dialogue7017201"]="Adventurer, those three you've been introduced to are the butlers responsible for different tasks in your home. They are all the big shots in their own industry! It's all about offering our clients the best experience possible!",
    ["Dialogue7017202"]="One more thing: even though they will assist you in handling various tasks in your home, you are the chief in charge here, so make sure you are on top of everything.",
    ["Dialogue7017203"]="As of now, your home development is reaching the bottleneck. I think you can try to bump up the level of your home.",
    ["Dialogue7017301"]="From beyond the Dimensional Gap, here they come... The continent of Midgard is set for another showdown between good and evil... Adventurer, the Dimensional Gap will open again in a month. While it's closed, you need to fight side by side with the heroes to kick some serious evil butt.",
    ["Dialogue7017302"]="Villains named Mosquito Girl and Ashura Kabuto will be entering our world one after the other. The good news is we've got some major force with overwhelming power to stand against evil, especially a hero named Saitama. This dude's strength is unreal; he could turn the tide of the entire fight with one punch!",
    ["Dialogue7017303"]="You all will meet each other at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>. Adventurer, crank up your sensing power, and go look for the strongest aura in the crowd. Maybe the most ordinary passerby is the hero we're looking for. Also, the flow of time in our world doesn't affect their world, so if the hero's pulling his hair (if there's any) over it, just let him know.",
    ["Dialogue7017401"]="Rushing for that sweet supermarket discount, I kinda ignored the misty stuff floating around and... walked right into it...",
    ["Dialogue7017402"]="You know me? Yep, that's right. Did you say something about the Dimensional Gap?",
    ["Dialogue7017403"]="So, I'm counting on you for sending me home! And you say there are villains?",
    ["Dialogue7017404"]="Got here by accident like me? And who are you?",
    ["Dialogue7017405"]="I see, a hero in this world! Alrighty then, I'll send them flying before I go back!",
    ["Dialogue7017501"]="(The butler of the estate stops you excitedly)\nThere you are, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7017502"]="Of course, as the top butler of an estate, I'm all about being efficient with time, so I won't bother you with any trivial matters.",
    ["Dialogue7017503"]="Do you remember the estate we gave you? It's actually unfinished. But don't worry. Our company is dedicated to our client and their properties, so we will continue with the renovation, construction, and routine maintenance.",
    ["Dialogue7017504"]="Absolutely. Our company is known for excellent customer service and after-sale support.\n(Ronald points to someone far off.)\nLook, That's Rony, the man in charge of building our estates.",
    ["Dialogue7017601"]="Ronald, here you are.\n(Rony sizes you up and down.)\nI guess this must be my boss, the owner of this estate, and the renowned Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue7017602"]="Adventurer, Rony is a top-notch architect and a talented crafter. If he had chosen weapon crafting instead of furniture, I bet he would be up there with Brock Sledgehammer.",
    ["Dialogue7017603"]="To each their own, Ronald. I don't think I'm in the same league as Brock Sledgehammer. However, to me, crafting furniture is a better measure of craftsmanship than making weapons.",
    ["Dialogue7017604"]="Adventurer, your home is almost done. You can take a look at the indoors and see if you like it or not.",
    ["Dialogue7017605"]="(Rony looks at you regretfully.)\nUnfortunately, we're really behind schedule, so it isn't quite up to par yet. Please be patient for the upcoming renovations.\nTo make up for it, here's a Simple Single Bed I made. Please accept it.",
    ["Dialogue7017701"]="Adventurer, how's everything? Are you happy with the space in the house?",
    ["Dialogue7017702"]="Does it feel too empty? I'm just about to talk about it. As you know, I'm a craftsman, so I can make just any furniture or ornaments you want.",
    ["Dialogue7017703"]="Of course. But you need to provide me with the required materials.",
    ["Dialogue7017704"]="Yes, but no worries. You can find everything within your home. Now, please bring me some normal ores, and I will start crafting your very first piece of furniture.",
    ["Dialogue7020101"]="Hi adventurers, nice to meet you. I am Mirabelle, the emissary of the White Valentine's Day event. Love you!\n(The pretty strange girl waves to you and then makes a hand heart.)",
    ["Dialogue7020102"]="Wow, it's nice to meet a stranger with love on such a special day! I feel that my work is getting more meaningful!",
    ["Dialogue7020103"]="I will cherish this little heart! And I hope that you can find the one who will make a hand heart together with you!\n<color=#A1979FFF>Ahem, actually I have found one!</color>",
    ["Dialogue7020104"]="You know, the White Valentine's Day is a the continuation of Valentine's Day. Princess Kaitlyn hopes that even in such a time when monsters are rampant, love will be spread to every corner of the kingdom, so you can still participate in the event even if you haven’t found your true love! Adventurers, we have prepared a lot of gifts for this event, do you want to join us?",
    ["Dialogue7020105"]="Our event is a simple one, but only available for <color=#CA2E0AFF>teams formed by Friends</color>! Adventurers can team up with your friends and go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amusement Park at Prontera South Gate</color>. Attention! He or she must be in your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Friends List</color>! Whether you’re just friends, more than friends, or lovers, just keep it a secret!",
    ["Dialogue7020106"]="Then, you may pick a good time to ride the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carousel, Rotating Bench, or Mini Train in the Amusement Park</color> with a pre-prepared gift. You should ride together for at least <color=#CA2E0AFF>five seconds</color>! You can enjoy the scenery or look into each other's eyes! If you meet the above conditions, you will <color=#CA2E0AFF>receive a gift</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7020201"]="You seem to have completed your quest!\n(Mirabelle magically takes out the gift from behind and hands it to you.)\nPlease accept the gift that Belle has prepared for you!",
    ["Dialogue7020202"]="During the event, Belle will be waiting for adventurers here <color=#CA2E0AFF>every day</color>! Just enjoy the moonlight in Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue7020701"]="Adventurer! Look at you! Are you also here to sign up for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Street Party</color>?",
    ["Dialogue7020702"]="Huh, you don't know?\n (Heflee winks at you with a small secret smile.)",
    ["Dialogue7020703"]="The Desert Green Tavern got hired by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lugenburg</color> Family to throw a massive party right in the scorching Morroc Desert!",
    ["Dialogue7020704"]="Speaking of the perfect game for a scorching desert... That's right—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Gun Battle</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7020705"]="Lately, Prince Halmod's been hearing some wild stories from bards, and now he's all fired up about <color=#CA2E0AFF>boosting tourism</color> and lifting Morroc out of poverty. He even gave the tavern some funding and told me to set up a <color=#CA2E0AFF>water gun</color> tournament—with big rewards to lure Adventurers from all over...",
    ["Dialogue7020706"]="Prince Halmod's going all out this time! Rumor is, he spent his entire stash to set up a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Midgard Tour</color>—<color=#CA2E0AFF>seven</color> amazing cities, all packed with culture and flavor! By <color=#CA2E0AFF>earning fuel</color> in the Water Gun Battle, everyone has a chance to visit their dream destination!",
    ["Dialogue7020707"]="No problem! I'll get your signup sheet ready. You just need to head to the venue of the Water Gun Battle—uh, wait...?!\n(Heflee suddenly freezes.)",
    ["Dialogue7020708"]="<color=#A1979FFF><size=18>Oh no...! I totally forgot to look for a venue...!</size></color>\nAhem! Hey, Adventurer? Since you're joining anyway, could you help me find a good spot for the Water Gun Battle?",
    ["Dialogue7020709"]="(Heflee blows you a kiss with a charming smile.)\nThe desert's super dry, and hauling water would be a pain. So if the place has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>water source</color> nearby, that'd be perfect! And maybe... I'll go easy on you during the match!",
    ["Dialogue7020801"]="What a gorgeous spot! I think it's near the Hope Oasis, right? Can't wait for it!",
    ["Dialogue7020802"]="You mean, why did Prince Halmod suddenly want to host an event like this?\n(Heflee furrows her brows as if trying hard to recall something.)\nHe showed up at the tavern a few days ago with a weird bard—looked kinda like a Marse, honestly...",
    ["Dialogue7020803"]="The bard said that people in his hometown are big fans of this team-based multiplayer competitive game that features <color=#CA2E0AFF>water guns</color>—they even have full-on leagues for it! They mix paint into the water, leaving colorful <color=#CA2E0AFF>graffiti</color> all over during the game. Contestants can then dive into those color zones to zoom around walls and floors...<size=22>Huh?</size><size=26>Huh???</size>",
    ["Dialogue7020804"]="(At this point, Heflee stares at you through gritted teeth.)\nAdventurer, do I look stupid?",
    ["Dialogue7020805"]="Come on—who actually looks like a Marse?! And that stuff about diving into colored graffiti to zoom around walls or floors... <size=22>How is this possible? </size><size=26>That guy was definitely trolling me!</size>",
    ["Dialogue7020806"]="Adventurer, if you run into him during the Water Gun Battle, please give him a good beating for me!",
    ["Dialogue7030101"]="Adventurer! Look at you. You are also here for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Songkran Festival</color> in the desert?",
    ["Dialogue7030102"]="Huh, I never thought there was something you didn't know!\n(Heflee winks at you with a small secret smile.)",
    ["Dialogue7030103"]="Let's see… Uh-huh! It is said to be a grand festival introduced to Midgard from the Parallel World. On this day, people will throw water at each other to bless and worship their elders, and it is said that you can also see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Gun Battle</color> and elephant parades in the streets! And elephants are all painted with color!",
    ["Dialogue7030104"]="And… Oh no! The venue for the water gun battle has not been confirmed. Adventurer, can you help us find a suitable venue? It's too dry in the desert, so it would be nice if the celebration could be held in an <color=#CA2E0AFF>oasis</color>! In return, I might show you some mercy during the battle!",
    ["Dialogue7030201"]="What a beautiful place. I remember it was close to the Hope Oasis. Hee-hee! Do you know how I got this information from the Parallel World and became the first person to celebrate the Songkran Festival in the desert?",
    ["Dialogue7030202"]="(Heflee's expression suddenly freezes as if she's trying to remember something.)\nIt was… Who was it? It seems that a machine told me. A machine? How can that be? Then its owner…",
    ["Dialogue7030203"]="I don't remember… He seems to be a man who travels around and maybe doesn't like to travel… He came to the pub that day, soaked to the skin, but refused my towel and said it was a blessing from Bangkok…",
    ["Dialogue7030204"]="(Heflee stares at you through gritted teeth)\nAdventurer, do I look stupid?",
    ["Dialogue7030205"]="Because the man looked at me as if to say that Miss Heflee had written the word \"idiot\" on her face! Adventurer, if you meet a guy with a strange machine that talks incomprehensibly when you <color=#CA2E0AFF>travel in Bangkok</color>, please do beat him up for me!",
    ["Dialogue7030206"]="That man looked at me as if saying that Miss Heflee had written the word \"idiot\" on her face! Adventurer, if you meet a guy who carries a strange machine and talks nonsense during your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Island Tour</color>, please do beat him up for me!",
    ["Dialogue7040101"]="Adventurer, are you interested in experiencing the latest enchantment techniques in Al De Baran? Kunna, Meowdelle and I have recently developed a magical <color=#CA2E0AFF>enchantment conversion crystal</color> and are looking for volunteers!",
    ["Dialogue7040102"]="Ahem! Well, according to their respective functions, these stones can be divided into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dark Enchantment Conversion Crystals for weapons, Astral Enchantment Conversion Crystals for armor, and Stellar Enchantment Conversion Crystals for accessories</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7040103"]="After using an Enchantment Conversion Crystal, <color=#CA2E0AFF> Enchantment Stat will change location to </color>. Currently, because it’s our patent, it can only be used in Al De Baran~",
    ["Dialogue7040104"]="Absolutely not! The materials used to craft Enchantment Conversion Crystals are very precious. As a professional enchanter, it would be a disgrace to waste them!",
    ["Dialogue7040105"]="Ohhhh... Okay! If you're willing to be our first test subject and keep it a secret, I suppose we could share some of the crafting requirements...",
    ["Dialogue7040106"]="(Zachary carefully took out 6 pieces of radiant colored stones from a cloth bag) You’ll need to reach <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lv. 10 Life Skills</color> to craft them, but the time and materials you spend can further advance your Enchantment techniques.",
    ["Dialogue7040107"]="Be sure to make good use of them!",
    ["Dialogue7040201"]="Adventurer, my head still hurts...",
    ["Dialogue7040202"]="I failed to refine a customer’s weapon... My big strong arms protected my body, but not my head...",
    ["Dialogue7040203"]="But, how could the greatest blacksmith admit defeat! After tireless research with my old friend from the Magic Furnace, I finally created an item that can protect equipment while refining!",
    ["Dialogue7040204"]="Clang! Clang! Here, I’ve forged a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Weapon Protection Crystal</color> for refining weapons, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Armor Protection Crystal</color> for refining Armor, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Accessory Protection Crystal</color> for refining accessories. If your equipment happens to have a mishap while refining, you can use them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>prevent damage</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7040205"]="Protection crystal’s with a higher level, can protect more advanced refinements. If your <color=#CA2E0AFF>mining</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>smelting</color> skills reach the required level, you can collect raw materials and make them yourself!",
    ["Dialogue7040206"]="How about it? Want to take a gamble on your equipment and give it a try? If you wish to do so, I can even tell you the secret behind how to use the crystals!",
    ["Dialogue7040207"]="You have quite the eye! I'm actually exploring how to use them to craft armor, protect customers’ equipment AND protect the blacksmith, to provide a more friendly trading atmosphere...",
    ["Dialogue7040208"]="Ahahahahahaha~ Nice doing business with you!",
    ["Dialogue7050101"]="The bustling streets, the busy stores, the marvelous fountain... The royal city of Prontera is just like imagined! Hey Adventurer, is this your first time in Prontera too?",
    ["Dialogue7050102"]="Great! Do you know where I can find food and medicine? I hurt my leg on the way and had to rely on the kindness of a caravan to bring me to Prontera. They say the people of this city are kind-hearted, just like them.",
    ["Dialogue7050103"]="Huh... I heard that there’s something called the Mission Board. As long as you write down the commissioner’s name and mission details, all sorts of adventurers will be eager to reach out. Adventurer, can you help register my supplies request on the Mission Board? In return for your kindness, I can teach you some simple ways to communicate from my homeland. Maybe you can use them when you’re out adventuring!",
    ["Dialogue7050104"]="But I can't write in your language... Adventurer, can you help register my supplies request on the Mission Board? In return for your kindness, I can teach you some simple ways to communicate from my homeland. Maybe you can use them when you’re out adventuring!",
    ["Dialogue7050105"]="By the way, the name of the commissioner is \"Kusari\" in your language. Thank you dearly for your help~",
    ["Dialogue7050201"]="Thank you again for your generosity!\n(Kusari smiles and makes a strange gesture to you)",
    ["Dialogue7050202"]="This is a popular blessing in our hometown. It’s said that people with noble intentions <color=#CA2E0AFF>who offer up first prayers everyday at sunrise will receive a mystery gift</color>. If you are one of the pious and fortunate <color=#CA2E0AFF>few</color>, the gift you receive will be <color=#CA2E0AFF>even more magical</color>! Adventurers, are you ready to give it a go?",
    ["Dialogue7050203"]="This is a communication to god, making <color=#CA2E0AFF>blessing</color> gestures to others. Legend has it that one can receive <color=#CA2E0AFF>wonderful gifts</color> by making such a gesture in the blessed City of Eternal Night. Hmm... This city, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>, is also one of the many blessed cities! Come on, Adventurer, give it a try!",
    ["Dialogue7060101"]="Adventurer, are you going back?",
    ["Dialogue7060102"]="Tsk tsk...\n(Heflee raises three fingers and shakes them in front of you)\nJust wait another month. That's when it gets really hot out here.",
    ["Dialogue7060103"]="Oh, and it sounds like the Desert Green Tavern is looking for <color=#CA2E0AFF>an oasis to escape from the heat</color> in the desert. Put some parasols and iced drinks under the coconut trees, and we have ourselves a paradise!",
    ["Dialogue7060104"]="Building sand castles, playing volleyball on the beach, splashing each other with water guns... We can have a great summer even in the desert!",
    ["Dialogue7060105"]="(Heflee suddenly comes up to you)\nAdventurer, can you help us find a suitable place? In return, all of your drinks during the festival are <color=#CA2E0AFF>half off</color>. How does that sound?",
    ["Dialogue7060201"]="What an amazing place! I'll get the decorations ready right away. Make sure you come back when we're done!",
    ["Dialogue7070101"]="(Before the teleportation formation, a petite girl is pacing uneasily)\nDear warrior, please do me a favor!",
    ["Dialogue7070102"]="(\"Snap\", Andre slaps you on the shoulder)\nPlease! I need to </color>collect the escaped magic energy<color=#CA2E0AFF> immediately. Otherwise, the whole Geffen will be affected!",
    ["Dialogue7070103"]="I'm Andre, a reserve Magician of Geffen Tower. Recently, my roommate Diorus has been avoiding everyone and he seemed to be working on something strange. So I sneaked into his dormitory while he was out...",
    ["Dialogue7070104"]="I could never have imagined what he had studied was actually the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic of converting genders</color>! It's just that the magic was unstable. Part of the residual magic energy entered my body, and another part of it has escaped to the underground area of the Geffen Tower... If the monsters there are also affected, there will be dire consequences...",
    ["Dialogue7070105"]="What should I do? My fiancée is still waiting for me to marry her, but now... Boo-hoo!",
    ["Dialogue7070106"]="(The petite girl stops crying all at once and peeps at you through her fingers)\nAhem—So you found out after all...",
    ["Dialogue7070107"]="(Andre's voice suddenly becomes sweet and greasy. With her pink hair, there is a strange girly vibe)\nPlease... I really need your help!",
    ["Dialogue7070108"]="If it fails... the esteemed Master Jesqurienne may also... well... be the same as me... And protective clothing has been broken by the monsters underground...\n(Andre's voice trailed off, as if ashamed)",
    ["Dialogue7070109"]="For real? You are a great person, warrior! It's actually quite simple. Just bring the collection device to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Dungeon 1F</color> and collect the energy! Also, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore the protective clothing that was damaged by the monsters</color>. It was broken by Jakk on my way to collect just now.",
    ["Dialogue7070110"]="(Andre looks around and quietly adds)\nBut if you want to change your gender, it's not entirely impossible!",
    ["Dialogue7070111"]="Hehe, I get it! Well, I'm going to need you to look for something in Geffen that can be used for the restoration. Diorus seems to have bought the crafting materials from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Priscilla</color>. It will definitely work if we use the most robust <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon Scale</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7070201"]="Ahem...\n(The girl coughs in a gruff voice)\nI... I can feel... something is different about me now...",
    ["Dialogue7070202"]="I want to wear a pink dress, and a fluffy cake dress with a little tiara!",
    ["Dialogue7070203"]="(Andre suddenly covers her mouth and looks at you in horror)\nYou're right, I... I can't allow myself to be affected by this evil spell! I'll start sewing right away!",
    ["Dialogue7070301"]="This is it! I have no idea what Diorus wants to do with his research. You know what? I'm gonna report to the master right now. Let's hope Diorus never finds out...",
    ["Dialogue7070302"]="Hey, what's wrong? You look weird!",
    ["Dialogue7070303"]="S-Stay away!",
    ["Dialogue7070304"]="Whoaaa! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Are you affected too</color>? Don't worry, I'll definitely apply for a meeting with Diorus for you, just... right here in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>! Hey, you're getting too close!",
    ["Dialogue7070401"]="Hello, beautiful guest, my name is Diolos.\n(The elegant lady wearing a wizard hat smiles at Andre)",
    ["Dialogue7070402"]="(Andre avoids eye contact and secretly blushes)\nH-Hello, Diorus...",
    ["Dialogue7070403"]="I... Diorus, aren't you...",
    ["Dialogue7070404"]="(Diolos tucks a strand of hair behind her ear, seemingly untroubled by your question)\nLet me introduce myself. I'm a Magician from Geffen, and my research direction is gender conversion. As ordered by the master, I will further my studies in Prontera and provide <color=#CA2E0AFF>gender conversion services</color>. As for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>item</color> used for the conversion, I have asked <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sinclair, the crystal merchant of Alberta</color>, to sell it.",
    ["Dialogue7070405"]="Exactly! As you can see, my research was successful. Speaking of which, I have to thank Andre for collecting the escaped magical energy. But...",
    ["Dialogue7070406"]="(Diorus looks wistfully at Andre, while the latter is trying to bury her head into her collar)\nPoor little fella, looks like you still haven't recovered from the conversion. Although the energy in your body will gradually disappear, I can also help you remove it manually. It happens that the new drug has not been tested yet...",
    ["Dialogue7070407"]="No... No thanks!",
    ["Dialogue7080101"]="My friend from afar, it has been a long time since we heard about you from the Bards in Geffen. But across the vast continent of Midgard, your deeds, the legends of Odin's descendant, are going from mouth to mouth. And now, the dust-covered Merlin's Manuscript has led to a new Trial Illusion. Are you willing to follow the guidance of your destiny and return to the long-forgotten <color=#CA2E0AFF>Thanatos Tower</color>?",
    ["Dialogue7080102"]="Self-Locking Tower, Nightmare Tower, Eclipse Tower... Whatever the name was, people—even historians of later generations—were frightened by the evil locked in the tower and daunted by the infamous reputation of its master. As a result, they would only refer in vague terms to this high tower amid the yellow sands. Only a legendary mage—wise and courageous—dared to reveal the actual name of this tower in his manuscript: Thanatos.",
    ["Dialogue7080103"]="Hatred, despair, sorrow, agony... He extracted all his negative emotions with his own hands and sealed them in Thanatos Tower. Some say these emotions were thrown away because their master pursued the purest form of ultimate power, and they have gained self-consciousness over time. Yet some would say the master of these emotions is still hiding in the tower, vainly attempting to revive his only companion through an evil ritual. Whatever the fact might be or however it revealed itself to the world, one thing remains undebatable: one hundred years ago, a calamity struck the mortal realm, causing the seal within the tower to crumble; Thanatos, on the other hand, was nowhere to be found...",
    ["Dialogue7080104"]="The tower shall crumble, and the land shall sink. As Demon Swordsman's name fades away, the radiance of truth and wisdom shall never decay. As Merlin's Manuscript states, \"In the raging sands and gusting winds, here came the Godsend. Along with Merlin, into the tower they walked. Three days later, upon the tower and the sands, tranquility descended.\"",
    ["Dialogue7080105"]="As the manuscript prophesies, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Godsend</color> is the key to reinforcing the seal. Should the seal ever weaken, the evil in the tower would resurge, and Godsend would return to the mortal realm, eradicating the malevolence. However, as for the summoning ritual, its materials, and objects, not a single word can be found in the manuscript...",
    ["Dialogue7080106"]="Adventurer, you have a unique connection to the Trial Illusion. You also defeated Morroc's projection in \"The Chapter of Courage.\" So I sincerely hope you can return to the time and space where this tale took place to unfold the truth hidden inside Thanatos Tower. Perhaps, when the calamity strikes again, tragedy needs not repeat itself.",
    ["Dialogue7080107"]="Humans' hymn is a song of bravery. Adventurer, if you have mastered the philosophy behind it, then you are eligible to <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain the corresponding Illusion Key</color> from Winry and set off to your destiny.",
    ["Dialogue7080201"]="Greetings, the hero from afar! My material body has sealed me in this script to offer some meager guidance for your trial.",
    ["Dialogue7080202"]="He's in the illusion, expecting your arrival.",
    ["Dialogue7080203"]="All coincidences have their innate inevitability. As I suppose, your destiny and that of my material body might have intertwined with each other since long before. The sealing totems Thanatos left in the tower are already damaged beyond repair, but fortunately, my material body has discovered the legendary Urd's Solution in ancient literature and managed to repair it. Only with this solution can you purify the energy of endless negative emotions within the tower.",
    ["Dialogue7080204"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Eliminate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> that emerged from the negative emotions. Then use the purified energy to <color=#CA2E0AFF>generate new sealing totems</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7080205"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Agony, hatred, sorrow, despair</color>... All of these are born from the darkest sentiment hidden within Thanatos, get materialized into monsters, and even enable an <color=#CA2E0AFF>evil Thanatos to emerge from himself</color>...",
    ["Dialogue7080206"]="Now, on <color=#CA2E0AFF>the bookshelf behind me</color>, the manuscript left by my material body has started the next chapter. When you <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> it, you will find the entrance to the illusion...",
    ["Dialogue7090101"]="Adventurer! (A muscular man swings his hammer before you.) Look! My mighty new technique!",
    ["Dialogue7090102"]="Secret Technique—Star Card Upgrade! Adventurer, if you happen to have many low-level cards that you don't know what to do with, my technique is a perfect solution to this!",
    ["Dialogue7090103"]="Consuming cards with the same names will upgrade the card's star level. Each star will get you an extra stat. If your upgrade is successful, your card will become much different!",
    ["Dialogue7090104"]="Adventurer, don't compare me with those dabblers like Hollgrehenn! (Brock growls, showing you his bulky muscles.) This powerful physique is the best testament to my skill!",
    ["Dialogue7100101"]="Adventurer, it's really you! The Great Sage was just saying there was some familiar smell inside this Dimensional Gap, thinking we might get back to the world before the reincarnation took place... Well! Even though I'm not sure whether the things on my computer still exist, it's great to see you again!",
    ["Dialogue7100102"]="Right! Is the Wonderland we left last time still here? I remember there were many adventure items in there... On the other hand, if the magical fluctuation triggered by successful travels is what opens Wonderland, then we might be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter it again</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7100103"]="Answering. Wonderland is reopened now. As Rimuru Tempest's competence improves, various data in Wonderland have been enhanced accordingly, deriving a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new set of \"Tribal\" rules</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7100104"]="Individuals who enter Wonderland <color=#CA2E0AFF>must join one of the following tribes: Kijin, Dragonewt, and Orcs</color>. Moreover, they have to roll the dice to advance and trigger various encounters that happen along the way to win corresponding tokens and other rewards.",
    ["Dialogue7100105"]="Huh...? Only one tribe to join? I hate to get split up with my Jura fellows... Besides, I don't even know how to reach a good ending. Raphael's ability is not working right now...",
    ["Dialogue7100106"]="Ahhh! This is not the Rimuru I know! Pull yourself together! Okay! Anyway, just treat this as a recap session for the demonic knowledge! Hmm... Where should I start?",
    ["Dialogue7100107"]="Notifying. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Your choice will determine the type of tokens you obtain during the adventure, and different tokens can be exchanged for different items</color>. I recommend you take advice from the natives.",
    ["Dialogue7100108"]="Native?\n(Rimuru suddenly looks toward you with high hopes.)\nThen, can you pick a tribe for me and help me get more information? Thanks!",
    ["Dialogue7100109"]="Adventurer, it's really you! I'm Rimuru! Do you remember me? It has been ages, and I'm so happy to see you again!",
    ["Dialogue7100110"]="Right! Is the Wonderland we left last time still here? I remember there were many adventure items in there... Maybe we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Wonderland again</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7100111"]="Notifying. Wonderland is reopened now. As it lasts in Midgard for quite a while, various data in Wonderland have been enhanced accordingly, deriving a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new set of \"tribal\" rules</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7100112"]="Huh... I can only pick one tribe?",
    ["Dialogue7100113"]="Hmm... This is hard. Where should I start?",
    ["Dialogue7120101"]="(Standing before the church, Wolmas the Archbishop slowly turns the pages of the sacred tome. Among the aged pages, a distant call echoes, harmonizing with your soul.)\nAdventurer, it seems you have heard them.",
    ["Dialogue7120102"]="As the successor of Odin's bloodline is recognized by Valkyrian, the Head Priest who propagates Odin's doctrine shall guide the chosen one to uncover the legacy of the gods.\n(Wolmas the Archbishop closes the sacred tome.)\nThis is the oracle bequeathed by the first archbishop. Now, the destined moment has come.",
    ["Dialogue7120103"]="According to the doctrine of Odin, the almighty Odin hung himself upside-down on Yggdrasil for nine days and nights to acquire omniscient wisdom. Upon stepping onto the ground, he became both the lord of wisdom and the prisoner of fate. He saw the glory and destruction of the gods, foresaw the inevitable Ragnarok, and fell into eternal agony.",
    ["Dialogue7120104"]="He sent out Valkyrie to lead the fallen heroes to become Einherjar, chained the giant wolf Fenrir, and banished Jormungandr and Hel. He created the god of nature who would slay the god of darkness, but none of his plans altered the prophesied outcome. Knowing the inescapable fate, Odin resolved to leave a final <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> for his successor bearing his bloodline.",
    ["Dialogue7120105"]="This is the power of the gods, reuniting with Yggdrasil alongside the fallen gods in Ragnarok, only to be scattered across the world with Yggdrasil's downfall. Though now scarce, it still holds the power to overturn the order in the mortal realm.",
    ["Dialogue7120106"]="\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Divinity</color>.\" This is the name of the power, existing as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tokens of the gods</color>. Only the archbishops among the followers of Odin know how to find them. In fact, we have long awaited your arrival.",
    ["Dialogue7120107"]="Adventurer, are you ready to accept it?",
    ["Dialogue7120108"]="(With a serious and sacred demeanor, Wolmas pats your shoulder reassuringly.)\nNow, come forth.",
    ["Dialogue7120201"]="May you use this power wisely, Adventurer. To become the master of \"Divinity\" is to interwind your destiny to that of the world. Your good deeds will make the world better, but your sins will ultimately lead to your downfall. Remember my words; perhaps, in the shadow, the \"Divinity\" still watches over you on behalf of its former master.",
    ["Dialogue7130101"]="(Beneath the Heart Pedestal, the goddess, looking both sympathetic and determined.)\nSurvivors of the apocalypse, endless plundering will only lead to more tragedy...",
    ["Dialogue7130102"]="I see a devastated wasteland beyond time and space, where violence reigns, and the weak are at the mercy of the strong. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raoh</color>, the Ken-Oh, controls a massive <color=#CA2E0AFF>legion of monsters</color> with his fists, planning to invade Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue7130103"]="Yet, brave souls still rise in the name of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Successor of Fist of the North Star</color> to defend their lands. Their unwavering hearts truly move me.",
    ["Dialogue7130104"]="Adventurer, you must go back to Prontera, inform the Kingdom Defense Force, and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kenshiro</color> and his allies. Kenshiro's fate is intertwined with Raoh's; he's the key to our victory and to sending the outsiders <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to the Otherworld</color>. After stopping Raoh, the Dimensional Gap will open again.",
    ["Dialogue7130201"]="Adventurer, glad you're here.\n(Bernard, looking grim, gives you a letter.)\nThis was nailed to the gate of the training ground early this morning. Read it.",
    ["Dialogue7130301"]="I thought it was a hoax until I saw that arrow...",
    ["Dialogue7130302"]="(Bernard tightly clenches his fists, grinding his teeth.)\nThat arrow carrying the challenge letter came from the knights' arsenal, meaning that they'd already fought and defeated our border guards and even infiltrated Prontera!",
    ["Dialogue7130303"]="The battle report is probably on its way. No matter what tactics they used, their power is no joke. Adventurer, I need to go to the palace right now to report to the queen and plan our next moves with the ministers. This concerns our entire kingdom, and we must be prepared to fight to the death.",
    ["Dialogue7130304"]="Otherworld? If they're truly from beyond Midgard, our Intelligence Bureau will have a hard time. Is that \"justice force\" you mentioned trustworthy? Will <color=#CA2E0AFF>working with them</color> improve our chances of winning?",
    ["Dialogue7130305"]="I trust you.\n(Bernard solemnly pats your shoulder.)\nI'll take care of things in the kingdom. Since you've got the goddess's guidance and have solved otherworld problems before, you're the best one to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Kenshiro</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7130401"]="(In the crowd, your eyes meet Kenshiro's.)\nMy homeland doesn't have splendid scenes like this. Is it your call that brought me here, Adventurer from Otherworld?",
    ["Dialogue7130402"]="(Kenshiro's face turns serious when he hears the name Raoh.)\nRaoh... I can't believe he's here too. The upcoming battle will be intense. You guys should hide; innocent people shouldn't have to die for no reason.",
    ["Dialogue7130403"]="You're saying... fight with us? However, the fights between the Successors of Fist of the North Star are always one-on-one, no matter the place. Thank you for the goddess's guidance.",
    ["Dialogue7130404"]="(Kenshiro listens closely, and when you mention \"protect Midgard,\" his eyes seem to see right through you.)\nYes, against invaders, everyone has the right to fight. If it's to minimize casualties and fend off Raoh's legion together... Adventurer, my friends, and I will assist you with training and support.",
    ["Dialogue7130405"]="Time is of the essence, and we must begin our training right away. Let's hope our victory sets your world back on track...",
    ["Dialogue7140101"]="Yes, staying alive is the only way I can protect you.\n(Kenshiro stares at his fists)\nBut Raoh...",
    ["Dialogue7140102"]="Hold on, Kenshiro.\n(A beautiful long-haired lady turns and smiles at you.)\nAre you also out enjoying the peace?",
    ["Dialogue7140103"]="Is it the guidance of your goddess?\n(Kenshiro stands in silence for a moment with his face partly in shadow.)\nNot every past is worth recalling, but if it's the guidance of the goddess...",
    ["Dialogue7140104"]="I am the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Successor of Hokuto Shinken</color>, an ancient martial art dating back 1,800 years. The former successor, Ryuken, adopted four boys as foster sons while searching for the next successor. Besides me and Raoh, there are Toki and Jagi. We lived, trained, and fought together for the title of successor until our master chose me as his successor. Raoh, who was not chosen, has left us ever since.",
    ["Dialogue7140105"]="Raoh's ambitions never died. After he left, he used Fist of the North Star to beat countless martial artists and form a powerful Ken-Oh legion, earning the title—\"The Conqueror of Century's End.\"",
    ["Dialogue7140106"]="Even if we push back the vanguard, for now, he won't halt his invasion whatsoever. The real challenge will be Raoh's legion. As far as I know, Raoh will <color=#CA2E0AFF>personally come to the battlefield</color> to check if his opponent is worthy or not, delivering a devastating blow to whoever stands in his path.",
    ["Dialogue7140107"]="He—\n(Kenshiro, sensing something, stands before Yuria.)\nAdventurer, get ready for battle!",
    ["Dialogue7140201"]="(A tall figure suddenly appears, cutting off the conversation.)\nIn any world, Kenshiro, you always go against my way.",
    ["Dialogue7140202"]="The peace in this world is fragile. The end of the century is all about war and chaos. Do you really want to risk your life to \"save\" it? Your heart is filled with unrealistic dreams and weak emotions. That's why you lost to Shin and why you can't defeat me!",
    ["Dialogue7140203"]="Domination, power, and conquest are the fastest means to create a new order! After defeating you, both worlds and everything in them, including Yuria, will be mine.",
    ["Dialogue7140204"]="There's no way I'm letting that happen.",
    ["Dialogue7140205"]="Roar—Roar—Roar—",
    ["Dialogue7140206"]="Hahaha, looks like I'm not the only one who finds this funny! Kenshiro, and all you rebels, your naivety is making me sick. I'm not here for negotiations!",
    ["Dialogue7140207"]="Your battle with the vanguard was notable, but if you truly want to fight me, try surviving a <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster legion</color> a hundred times bigger than the vanguards!",
    ["Dialogue7140208"]="By the way, Adventurer, have you ever noticed a star near the Big Dipper at night, one that flickers?",
    ["Dialogue7140301"]="Are you alright? If Toki were around, he could heal you right away. Do you want Yuria to patch you up?",
    ["Dialogue7140302"]="Did you see it? The Big Dipper rules over death, and the star next to it, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shichosei</color>, is said to bring death within a year to those who see it. If you did see it, don't hide it from me; I don't want any of my comrades facing death alone.",
    ["Dialogue7140303"]="Then don't ever look at it. The sorrow of death will stay with your loved ones forever, and the scars it leaves can't be healed, not even by time. Live on for their sake.",
    ["Dialogue7140304"]="You...\n(Kenshiro's eyes fill with deep sadness, and he places his giant hand on your shoulder.)\nHow merciless heaven is... Why must they take away the lives of innocents?",
    ["Dialogue7140305"]="The prophecy of Shichosei is certain, but if you see it, you still have a year to turn things around. There has to be a way to survive this!",
    ["Dialogue7140306"]="(Kenshiro looks at the empty sky.)\nOnly one Successor of Fist of the North Star is allowed to exist in this world. If the star eventually appears, I'll face it calmly during my final battle with Raoh upon the fall of the monster legion.",
    ["Dialogue7140307"]="See you when the battle's over.",
    ["Dialogue7150101"]="(In the quiet cemetery, you hear Yuria whispers softly.)\nDeath can't erase your existence; the living will remember the sacrifices of those who are gone.",
    ["Dialogue7150102"]="Oh, it's you, Adventurer.\n(Yuria moves aside, revealing names on the tombstones.)\nWar has filled this cemetery with new names. I'm here to offer my prayers.",
    ["Dialogue7150103"]="Kenshiro is completely focused on his upcoming fight with Raoh.\n(Yuria starts coughing.)\nCough, cough... If you can't find him, he's probably still training somewhere.",
    ["Dialogue7150104"]="I'm fine.\n(Yuria covers her face with her sleeve.)\nMy life won't end here, at least not before the final fight.",
    ["Dialogue7150105"]="(Yuria gently shakes her head.)\nOnce the wheel of fate starts turning, it won't stop for anyone. All I can do is ensure these two chosen men stay focused on their battle.",
    ["Dialogue7150106"]="As the Jibosei, I'll sincerely pray for whoever rests in the cemetery. Adventurer, could you <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray for the fallen soldiers</color> the way in your world before you head to the next battlefield?",
    ["Dialogue7150201"]="Are you looking for me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue7150202"]="I'll stop Raoh, no matter the world.\n(Kenshiro tightens the strap on his wrist.)\nEven though... we trained under the same master, he was like an older brother to me.",
    ["Dialogue7150203"]="This is the fate of those who practice Fist of the North Star. From the first time we punched and sparred, fate was sealed. Now, Raoh and I both accept it.",
    ["Dialogue7150204"]="(You are about to speak, but Kenshiro beats you to it, which is unusual.)\nIt's beautiful here—I mean, your world.",
    ["Dialogue7150205"]="Life here isn't half bad. I hope after we win, your world gets back on track, and my homeland returns to how it was. You were at the cemetery, right? What those people risking their lives to protect, it's our turn now.",
    ["Dialogue7160101"]="Your heroic efforts have created a new future for Midgard. Adventurer, I can see the Dimensional Gap reopening and the day Kenshiro and his friends go back to their world.",
    ["Dialogue7160102"]="(Brunhild gently shakes her head.)\nRaoh and Kenshiro are still entangled in their roles as \"Conqueror\" and \"Savior.\" Their world isn't really saved yet.",
    ["Dialogue7160103"]="(Brunhild avoids the question and starts talking about \"love.\")\nBefore you ask me, I'd like to know what you think about \"love.\"",
    ["Dialogue7160104"]="As a goddess, love isn't necessary for me, but I've been wondering—what's stronger in an apocalyptic world filled with chaos and numbness: <color=#CA2E0AFF>bearing love or rejecting it</color>?",
    ["Dialogue7160105"]="I see... Love is complicated, can't be forced, and can't be held onto. When it's gone, those who held it bear endless sadness but grow stronger by carrying on their journey in the world. Adventurer, your answer has enlightened me.",
    ["Dialogue7160106"]="I see... Love is complicated, can't be forced, and can't be held onto. In this case, why not reject it and drop all the burdens, even if it means reaching the top alone. Adventurer, your answer has enlightened me.",
    ["Dialogue7160107"]="Okay, since we're about to say goodbye, as the host of this world, let's listen to what our guests wish for.",
    ["Dialogue7160201"]="Adventurer, you're back from Izlude Island?",
    ["Dialogue7160202"]="(Kenshiro looks around; the signs of war are fading.)\nIt's over now, and all that's left can only be done when I return to my world.",
    ["Dialogue7160203"]="(After thinking for a moment, Kenshiro's eyes soften.)\nYuria and Lin once grew a pot of fresh flowers that bloomed in the post-nuclear soil, but it was later destroyed by the legion of Ken-Oh.",
    ["Dialogue7160204"]="I figure if she could <color=#CA2E0AFF>receive some flesh flowers from you</color>, it might help ease that regret.",
    ["Dialogue7160205"]="Even though we've had different paths, you're just as right for this. Yuria isn't a girl who is driven only by love. I trust she'll understand the meaning no matter who gives her the flowers.",
    ["Dialogue7160301"]="(Receiving the flesh flowers, Yuria holds them delicately and looks at you.)\nAre these... flowers? Is it really for me?",
    ["Dialogue7160302"]="Take them as a gift.",
    ["Dialogue7160303"]="(Yuria gently touches the petals, then declines your suggestion regretfully yet firmly.)\nIt can't make it in a world where water is scarce. I'd rather it stay here and live freely instead of withering away far from their homeland. Adventurer, did Kenshiro ask you to bring me these flowers?",
    ["Dialogue7160304"]="Kenshiro... We may be separated again once we return, but my heart will always long to reunite with you.",
    ["Dialogue7160305"]="Yes, love brings endless sadness when it's gone, but no one can reject the warmth it brings. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kenshiro feels it, and so does Raoh.</color>",
    ["Dialogue7160306"]="Like your goddess said, love is complicated. Adventurer, since you have no impact on their fate, why not watch from the side, finding answers and witnessing the destinies of the Savior and the Conqueror of the century's end unfold? Time will answer once love and hate settle. It'll be a fascinating tale.",
    ["Dialogue7180101"]="Adventurer! Ahem! I've made a big upgrade to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trial Illusion entrance</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7180102"]="Tired of running all the way from Prontera to Geffen Library? Sick of squeezing in with your party members and getting death stares from cranky students? Wouldn't it be awesome to just teleport straight into the epic battle?",
    ["Dialogue7180103"]="Those annoying trips? A thing of the past! Using Master Merlin's manuscript and a lot of my hard work, I've anchored the portal—just touch it, and you're instantly inside!",
    ["Dialogue7180104"]="(With a proud smirk beneath the wizard hat, the scholar's eyes sparkle with wisdom.)\nCome on now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow my guidance</color>!",
    ["Dialogue7190101"]="Oh! Are you the Adventurer who's come to guard me?",
    ["Dialogue7190102"]="I'll leave it to you! I trust the Payon people's choice!",
    ["Dialogue7190103"]="P-Please make sure to <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep me safe</color>! The monsters are coming...",
    ["Dialogue7200101"]="Thanks for the effort! But the monsters won't give up—they know my power is priceless!",
    ["Dialogue7200102"]="Don't forget to come back <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomorrow</color>! Bruises or no bruises, I just like being with human Adventurers!",
    ["Dialogue7210101"]="The bustling streets, the busy stores, the marvelous fountain... The royal city of Prontera is just like imagined! Hey Adventurer, is this your first time in Prontera too?",
    ["Dialogue7210102"]="Great! Do you know where I can find food and medicine? I hurt my leg on the way and had to rely on the kindness of a caravan to bring me to Prontera. They say the people of this city are kind-hearted, just like them.",
    ["Dialogue7210103"]="Huh... I heard that there's something called the Mission Board. As long as you write down the commissioner's name and mission details, all sorts of people will be eager to reach out. But I can't write in your language... Can you help register my supplies request on the Mission Board? In return for your kindness, how about I teach you a bit of <color=#CA2E0AFF>astrology</color>?",
    ["Dialogue7210104"]="(The girl, full of excitement, pulls out a star-covered compass.)\n Don't let my age fool you! Back home, I'm a famous astrologer! These star trails may seem chaotic, but they contain the rhythm of the universe! Trust me—astrology skills will make your adventures way smoother!",
    ["Dialogue7210105"]="Ah, my bad! Can't believe I forgot something that important!\n (She slaps her forehead and chuckles awkwardly.)\n My name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Uma</color>! Hope we get along well, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue7210201"]="Thanks again for your help, Adventurer! Now, as we agreed...\n (Uma pulls a small booklet from her backpack and hands it to you.)\n Here! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Astrology Manual</color>—just like we agreed!",
    ["Dialogue7210202"]="It's the beginner's guide to astrology! Back in my hometown, people revere the stars as deities! We believe that with <color=#CA2E0AFF>sincere prayers</color> and careful observation, the stars will bring guidance and protection. By studying the manual, you can earn <color=#CA2E0AFF>Astrology Points</color> and receive the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gifts</color> of Stars!",
    ["Dialogue7210203"]="Hmm... No worries! Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the manual's instructions</color> step-by-step! But be careful! The <color=#CA2E0AFF>power of stars can also affect monsters</color>, making them stronger! Stay alert during astrology—monsters might ambush you!",
    ["Dialogue7210204"]="Don't sweat it—I'll be in Prontera for a while. If you have any questions about astrology—feel free to see me!\n (Uma flashes you a bright smile.)\n Good luck, Adventurer! May the morning star shine on your path!",
    ["Dialogue7220101"]="Step forward, the successor of Odin's bloodline.\n(The goddess bows her head, her eyes probing, seeking answers.)\nThe moment you step into the Temple of Dawn, I sensed a strange aura from you...",
    ["Dialogue7220102"]="I see... A resonance from your ancestral blood. Then perhaps... this is why Muninn has come to us.\n(With a light tap of her staff, the goddess reveals a <color=#CA2E0AFF>raven</color>, silent and still, resting by her feet.)",
    ["Dialogue7220103"]="Caw—",
    ["Dialogue7220104"]="Muninn, Odin's messenger and unseen watcher, who speaks to all beings. Before Ragnarok, it soared by day to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hear prayers</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness evil</color>, returning at night to whisper all to Odin himself... So then, Muninn's arrival is no coincidence—it heralds the <color=#CA2E0AFF>divine will of Odin</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7220105"]="After Ragnarok, I never saw Muninn again... yet not long ago, it returned with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Contract</color> penned in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elvish</color>...\n(With a graceful gesture, the goddess unveils a <color=#CA2E0AFF>scroll</color> bathed in prismatic light, floating in her open palm.)\nSuccessor of Odin's bloodline... this is your <color=#CA2E0AFF>new power</color>.",
    ["Dialogue7220106"]="Caw—Caw—",
    ["Dialogue7220107"]="You must know of the tales of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alfheim</color>. The elven kingdom, once a beacon of light and Odin's most loyal, now lies fractured. Ragnarok shattered the Rainbow Bridge, severing their divine blessing and casting them into disarray and shadow.",
    ["Dialogue7220108"]="Now that Muninn could reach them again, it must be thanks to your collection of Fragment of Ymir's Heart, reawakening the power of Odin... Congratulations, successor of Odin's bloodline—you now hold the power to use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Contract</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>bond</color> with the elves in Alfheim.",
    ["Dialogue7220109"]="(The <color=#CA2E0AFF>scroll</color>, aglow with rainbow light, floats forth and stops right in front of you. Its parchment is etched with vivid patterns and unknown script.)\nJust remember, to bond with an elf is no mere promise—it is a vow sealed in divinity. They shall become your eternal Companions in light and in darkness, rising to your aid in times of dire need. Should destiny grant you more Companion contracts, guard them well and wield them wisely—to fulfill the divine mission Odin has laid upon your path...",
    ["Dialogue7220110"]="Go forth... and may I one day behold the moment when Ymir's Heart returns to where it belongs...",
    ["Dialogue8010101"]="Adventurer... Would you listen to my request? I know you have no obligation to help a deceased man you've never met but... I don't have anyone else to turn to for help...",
    ["Dialogue8010102"]="I was once a <color=#CA2E0AFF>captain</color> of a ship. The coat of paint on this merchant ship was once new, you know. Packed with goods and travelers... Until the day we ran afoul of the evil Corsair during a shipwreck. He robbed my crew and the innocent passengers of their memories, leaving them only the obsessions they had when they were still alive.",
    ["Dialogue8010103"]="If we don't <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill the spirits' last wishes and free them from their obsession</color>, they will be cursed to roam the land of the living forever, unable to move into the afterlife. I only ask that you help me free these dead souls from their obsessions and usher them into the kingdom of the dead. Will you do it?",
    ["Dialogue8010201"]="(Spencer swings his sword valiantly.)\nDarn these blasted Dead Planktons! How dare they cause trouble on Captain Kahn's ship! I'm going to get rid of all of...! That's weird. I can't seem to hit these monsters with my sword...",
    ["Dialogue8010301"]="Ahh... Those awful planktons finally got what they deserved. What a relief... Thank you for your help! I feel so much better now...\n(Spencer slowly disappears.)",
    ["Dialogue8010401"]="(Forde is talking to himself nervously.)\n<size=18>600, 800, 1.2... </size><size=24>1.2 million?!</size>\nOh, no, no, no, how much zeny did I lose?!",
    ["Dialogue8010402"]="It can't be! ...Can it? I was carrying a load of precious goods on this voyage but my blasted memory... I can't remember where I put them all! I'm not leaving this ship until I <color=#CA2E0AFF>find those goods</color>. Think you can help me, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8010501"]="(Forde finishes counting the goods and lets out a sigh of relief.)\nPhew... That's all of them. Huh? Why are they all covered in Water Weed anyway? And so filthy... Ah, doesn't matter. As long as they're found...\n(Forde slowly disappears.)",
    ["Dialogue8010601"]="(Sousa is deep in thought.)\n<size=18>Agghh! </size><size=18>I can't take this! </size><size=18>What in the world are the ingredients for the Healthy Meal the captain was talking about?! </size><size=18>Is it Sardine? </size><size=18>No, maybe it's Giant Shrimp?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8010602"]="Right on time! Bring me a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Healthy Meal</color> quickly! As a master chef of exotic delicacies, I refuse to be defeated by a commoner's dish!",
    ["Dialogue8010701"]="So this is a Healthy Meal?\n(Sousa eats a big spoonful and frowns.)\n...Hold on, isn't this just fried wheat and egg? It's that simple?!",
    ["Dialogue8010801"]="You've helped free everyone from their obsessions... Thank you. Now their lost souls can finally rest...",
    ["Dialogue8010802"]="(Kahn looks surprised then bursts out laughing.)\n...Haha, you've already freed me from my obsession actually... All this time I've blamed myself for failing as a captain. It was because of my mistakes that people lost their lives...",
    ["Dialogue8010803"]="But thanks to you, they're no longer bound to the land of the living... You fulfilled my last wish by helping their spirits move on...",
    ["Dialogue8020101"]="(Hobbe appears lost in thought. He sighs deeply.)\nSigh... I thought I already remembered everything about my past, but I just realized I don't actually remember <color=#CA2E0AFF>what happened during the shipwreck</color> clearly... That memory is very important to me. Can you help me get it back?",
    ["Dialogue8020102"]="I remember writing down all my experiences during the voyage in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>nautical log</color>. If I can just get my hands on those <color=#CA2E0AFF>log pages</color> that are lost somewhere in the sunken ship, I should be able to piece together everything that happened...",
    ["Dialogue8020201"]="So that's what happened the day the ship sank... Thank you for helping me remember the final piece of my life.",
    ["Dialogue8020202"]="What am I going to do now? It's just like it says in the log, I'll never be able to leave this place... But I'm not upset. I have my old mate to keep my company, after all...\n(Hobbe's expression softens as he looks toward the sunken ship.)",
    ["Dialogue8020203"]="I put my heart and soul into this merchant ship. Getting to spend an eternity by its side isn't all that bad, I think...",
    ["Dialogue8030101"]="(Annie frowns.)\nThat's strange... Why doesn't it taste right?",
    ["Dialogue8030102"]="...I-I'm figuring out <color=#CA2E0AFF>mom's recipe</color>! Did you know, my momma is a great cook! The smell of her cooking always draws in kids and the poor from the whole street. And no matter who it is that comes to the door, momma will always give them a bowl of something hot!",
    ["Dialogue8030103"]="Her best dish is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat n' Pumpkin</color>! Everyone who's tried it says each spoonful gives them a feeling of happiness! I really want to learn how to make it but no matter how hard I try, it just doesn't taste like how momma makes it.",
    ["Dialogue8030104"]="(Annie looks like she's about to burst into tears. She wipes at her eyes and continues to think.)\nHmm... Is it because I used poultry instead of the Large Meat Piece in the recipe? But Large Meat Pieces are so expensive, I can't afford them...",
    ["Dialogue8030201"]="(Annie's eyes grow wide in excitement.)\nOh wow! These are... Large Meat Pieces! Thank you! Do you wanna help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>make Meat n' Pumpkin</color>? I'm sure we can make a dish that tastes just like momma's if you help gather all the ingredients in the recipe!",
    ["Dialogue8030301"]="(Annie gets a taste of your cooking and cheers happily.)\nOh wow! It's so good! It's not quite like momma's but it's super good! I have another really small favor to ask though if that's okay?",
    ["Dialogue8030302"]="My papa works on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Weinst Street</color>. It's very hard work, so I've been trying hard to make this dish to let papa know he doesn't have to worry while at work! Can you bring this <color=#CA2E0AFF>box</color> of Meat n' Pumpkin to my papa?",
    ["Dialogue8030401"]="(Neste opens the bento box and reels in shock.)\nThis... This is...?!",
    ["Dialogue8030402"]="(Neste chokes back his emotions. It takes him a while to speak again.)\n...Annie was the one who asked you to bring this Meat n' Pumpkin to me? That child... She's grown so much since her mother passed away, unlike me. I can't seem to stop grieving.",
    ["Dialogue8030403"]="Annie didn't tell you, did she? Her mother, Arlene, died a month ago from a monster attack... We've been grieving her loss ever since. Arlene was so kind and so strong. She was always trying to use her delicious cooking to bring strength to those in dire straits...",
    ["Dialogue8030404"]="And now, I feel the same strength from this very dish. I gotta get it together! Homph, nom, sob, homph, nom, sob...!!!\n(Neste starts taking big bites out of the dish, finishing the bento in an instant. He looks up with glistening eyes.)\nAlright, it's time to work hard again!",
    ["Dialogue8040101"]="...It's you. Do you mind giving me a hand? Ever since the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange force field</color> appeared, <color=#CA2E0AFF>children have been going missing</color> in Morroc. I sent an assassin named Zhaka to investigate. Could you tell them that Hassan needs a report on his findings as soon as possible?",
    ["Dialogue8040201"]="(Zhaka looks at you warily.)\n...What do you want?",
    ["Dialogue8040202"]="(Zhaka visibly relaxes and starts talking.)\nI want to report back to the guild as soon as I can, but I've run into a snag during my investigation. A few days ago, I finally found one of the missing children's family, but...",
    ["Dialogue8040203"]="But every time he sees me, he runs away! I even went to the effort to find out his favorite food was this weird thing called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fruity Squid</color>! But it doesn't matter when I can't even get near that brat, let alone talk to him... <size=24>Do I look scary? </size>\n(Zhaka frowns deeply, making his already unfriendly features look even scarier.)",
    ["Dialogue8040204"]="Anyway, I can't talk to him. Can you help?",
    ["Dialogue8040301"]="Wow! It's the popular Fruity Squid!\n(Arno suddenly looks startled and looks around nervously before breathing a sigh of relief.)",
    ["Dialogue8040302"]="Phew... I don't see that scary guy following me anymore. Did you know this scary-looking man has been trying to come near me recently? He looks like a super bad guy, so I'm not gonna fall for it! Thank you for bringing me these tasty snacks though! I'm sure <color=#CA2E0AFF>Allie</color> would be happy too if she sees this...\n(Arno looks down sadly.)",
    ["Dialogue8040303"]="Allie is my baby sister. She got caught by baddies because I was too careless... But I already found those baddies' camp, so all I need is an adult and I'll be able to save her!",
    ["Dialogue8040304"]="You will? But you have to prove that you're strong enough first. Hmm... How about this? If you can bring enough Snake Scales from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anacondaqs</color> outside the city, I'll believe you can help me! Big brother Halmod always says beating up monsters is easy as pie for a warrior!",
    ["Dialogue8040401"]="(Arno looks at you with admiration in his eyes when he sees the Snake Scales.)\nWooww! You really did it! There's no mistake, you must be an awesome warrior like big brother Halmod! And if that's the case, you'll be able to beat up the baddies who kidnapped Allie! Come on! Let's go! I'll take you to their <color=#CA2E0AFF>camp</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8040501"]="(Arno wipes at the tears on his face and looks at you gratefully.)\nThank you for saving my sister! I'm gonna be a big strong adventurer like you too when I grow up, then I'll be able to keep Allie safe!",
    ["Dialogue8040601"]="(Zhaka quietly listens to your report. His expression growing darker by the second.)\n...So all these kidnappings were done by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demon King's followers</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8040602"]="A thousand years ago, a group of people appeared in the desert. Their hearts corrupted by darkness. They betrayed their people in exchange for the power of evil, and chose to serve the ruler of the land at the time, the demon god Morroc...",
    ["Dialogue8040603"]="But they disappeared after the swordsman sealed Morroc away. I can't believe they're making a move again after all this time... I have a bad feeling about this. This might be the end of our peaceful days in the desert.",
    ["Dialogue8050101"]="Hiya, adventurer! How's it going? You don't look like a resident of the desert. Were you drawn here by the magnificent <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient ruins</color> too?",
    ["Dialogue8050102"]="(Bowya laughs brightly.)\nI'm Instructor Bowya from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group</color>. Don't tell me you haven't heard of the Eden Group. If there's a ruin, we're not far away! My team and I are here in Morroc to dig and study the ancient ruins. It may not look like much, but it's very important work.",
    ["Dialogue8050103"]="Speaking of, I wonder how my team is doing. We split up a while ago so I'm hoping their dig has been going well. I remember Omari went to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>canyon southeast</color> of Morroc, Brennan went to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color>, and Casey is researching the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pyramid</color>...",
    ["Dialogue8050104"]="Well, since you're already here, why don't you help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>check in on my coworkers</color>! ^-^\n(Bowya gives your shoulder a hardy smack.)",
    ["Dialogue8050201"]="(Omari's face is red with rage.)\n...Those darn thieves! The Eden Group is not to be trifled with, you know!",
    ["Dialogue8050202"]="Hmph, I was on the way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>canyon</color> to conduct a dig in the ruins when these good-for-nothing <color=#CA2E0AFF>thieves</color> got in my way and wouldn't let me pass! As a member of the Eden Group, I won't let anyone get in the way of my research! Tell me what's the best weapon I can use to defeat them. Is this pointy shovel good enough?!\n(Omari makes a vicious attacking motion.)",
    ["Dialogue8050301"]="...What's that? You already dealt with the thieves? Hmph, they should be thankful they didn't have to fight me.\n(Omari dusts off his hands coolly.)\nNow there's nothing keeping me from my work. I have a feeling this is going to be the biggest archaeological find yet!",
    ["Dialogue8050401"]="(Brennan lowers his head and sighs deeply.)\nSigh... Me and my bad luck. What do I do now?",
    ["Dialogue8050402"]="Sigh, I was gong to do a dig in the ruins inside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color> when this weirdo calling himself the \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Keeper</color>\" got in my way! He said I have to solve his riddle before he'll let me in!",
    ["Dialogue8050403"]="(Brennan shakes his head dejectedly.)\nI've never heard of any Sphinx Keepers in all my years of historical research! I bet he's just some crazy riddle fanatic! Help me get rid of him!",
    ["Dialogue8050501"]="Ohohoho! I am the Sphinx Keeper! If you wish to enter, you must first <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer my riddle correctly</color>! If you have not the confidence in your intellect, you may choose to leave. Ignorant fools who try to force their way into the cavern will suffer the <size=24>CURSE</size> of Lord Sphinx!!\n(Giza spreads out his arms exaggeratedly.)",
    ["Dialogue8050502"]="I am taller when sitting and wear a jacket in all four seasons.\nI am now wrapped in a shroud and bare my teeth wailing.\nWhat monster am I?",
    ["Dialogue8050503"]="(Giza laughs in delight.)\nOhohoho! Unfortunate, very unfortunate. It seems no one can yet solve my esoteric riddle. Please leave this place!",
    ["Dialogue8050504"]="(Giza's eyes widen in shock.)\nYou... How did you figure it out? I thought so long and hard to come up with this ultimate riddle. Darn, blast it! I'll have to let you through this time!",
    ["Dialogue8050601"]="Excellent! You really are as smart as you look! Now I can finally enter the Sphinx Cavern and study these amazing ancient ruins. Ah, I can already feel my heart brimming with joy. Thank you!\n(Brennan's eyes glisten with gratitude.)",
    ["Dialogue8050701"]="(Casey is trembling while clutching her head.)\n...Aahhhh! I didn't see anything! I didn't see anything! I didn't see anything!",
    ["Dialogue8050702"]="...You... <size=24>YOU'RE ALIVE!! (ಥДಥ)~</size>\n(Casey starts to bawl loudly.)",
    ["Dialogue8050703"]="Please help me! I ran into those scary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soldier Skeletons</color> the second I walked into the pyramid! No one told me this archaeological site would be so terrifying! Hurry! Hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>get rid of them</color> or I won't even have the strength to lift my pointy shovel!",
    ["Dialogue8050801"]="(Casey is still trembling as she looks around nervously, before letting out a sigh of relief.)\nPhew... Those scary monsters are finally gone. I should get to work and study these ruins. I don't want to hold my colleagues back.",
    ["Dialogue8050901"]="(Bowya listens to your report on her fellow Eden Group members and laughs happily, clapping your shoulder hard.)\nHaha! I was right to ask you to check in on them! That does mean I'll have to thank you for your help on behalf of the Eden Group. You can come straight to me from now on if you have any questions about ancient ruins.",
    ["Dialogue8050902"]="Where will our team go next? Once we finish studying the ruins in this area, we'll move on to the next miraculous discovery. After all, there is still so much for the Eden Group to discover, and we'll never stop moving toward realizing those goals!\n(Bowya's eyes are shining with staunch determination.)",
    ["Dialogue8060101"]="(Trisse places her hands on her hips impatiently.)\nHey! When are you gonna stop following me?! And stop saying pori pori! I don't understand what you want!",
    ["Dialogue8060102"]="(Drops bounces up and down excitedly.)\nPopo!! <size=24>Pori pori!! (>///<)~!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8060103"]="You! Come help me now! This... This <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drops</color> has been bugging me for some time and I can't get rid of it! It's been shadowing me since I finished my last mission in the desert and won't leave me alone. Unless this means... my charm has transcended race and even monsters are becoming attracted to me?",
    ["Dialogue8060104"]="Po~ri... Po~ri pori... (╥△╥)……",
    ["Dialogue8060105"]="(Trisse's face turns red.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Dang it. That's too cute... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>No, get it together, Trisse! You're a stone cold assassin. Suppress it. Suppress it... </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Trisse! </color></size>\nHey, you! Don't think you can do whatever you want just because you're cute! Assassins don't keep pets! I... <size=24>I won't adopt you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8060106"]="(Trisse turns to you.)\nHey, adventurer, I remember hearing about a <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster researcher</color> who recently arrived in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc</color>. Maybe she'll know how to get rid of the Drops. Mind bringing her here?",
    ["Dialogue8060201"]="Oh dear me! We meet again! What can I do for you today? Did you encounter a mutant golem, or perhaps a burnt Magnolia?",
    ["Dialogue8060202"]="...You mean you found a Drops that won't leave a human girl alone? That is highly unusual for small monsters. I wonder why... Oh dear me, this is quite fascinating! You must bring me to see it. I can't wait to figure this out, hehe!\n(Bertha shivers in excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue8060301"]="Popo... Popo! Po-<size=24>po~ri! (>△<)~!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8060302"]="Hold on. I think the Drops is trying to tell us something! I believe what it's saying will be key to its strange behavior. I must translate it at once. Let me write this down—",
    ["Dialogue8060303"]="(Bertha takes out her research notebook excitedly and begins to furiously write in it.)\n...Mmhmm, it's saying it and its companions ran into some big trouble and it would like Trisse to help...",
    ["Dialogue8060304"]="Huh?! That's why you've been bugging me all this time? If you need my help, you gotta pay a commission. That's the rule of the Assassins Guild, and we don't make exceptions for monsters either!",
    ["Dialogue8060305"]="Po! Po~po, po~ri~ (✪. ✪)~\n(Drops's expression shifts and directs a pair of starry eyes at Trisse.)",
    ["Dialogue8060306"]="...Oh dear me, a monster that knows how to compliment a human? This little fella says the reason it followed Trisse is because of how cool she is! It's been deeply drawn in by her ever since the day it saw her spectacular fight against the Desert Wolves in the desert. It has never met a more beautiful or courageous human, and believes she must be the kind of hero who is righteous and helps the weak!",
    ["Dialogue8060307"]="(Trisse looks stunned as she eavesdrops on Bertha's muttering, then looks away with a red face.)\n...Hmph. W-well, there's no question about that!",
    ["Dialogue8060308"]="Po... Popo~pori, poriri... (╥﹏╥)……",
    ["Dialogue8060309"]="...Really? That happened? Drops says an evil and greedy monster named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phreeoni</color> appeared in Sograt Desert recently. It's been using its powerful magic to run rampant and terrorize the smaller and weaker monsters... A hero who's willing to help them get rid of Phreeoni will have Drops singing them praise forever, until the hero's name is known throughout the desert!",
    ["Dialogue8060310"]="...Ahem... That hero being me, right?\n(Trisse crosses her arms confidently, unable to stop the smirk on her face.)\nI guess the Drops leaves me no choice... For the good and peace of the desert, I'll go <color=#CA2E0AFF>teach that blasted Phreeoni a lesson</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8060401"]="Oh no, no, no, why did I say yes to that? A big monster like Phreeoni won't be easy to take down. I gotta come up with a good plan...\n...Ahem! Would you go to Eremes and ask to borrow some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poison</color>, please? I'll have use for it later.",
    ["Dialogue8060501"]="...Did you just say Trisse wants to borrow some Poison?\n(Eremes frowns suspiciously.)\nYou should know how powerful this stuff is... Don't go fooling around with it now.",
    ["Dialogue8060601"]="Very good! That's exactly what I need! Now go get me some delicious-smelling, hot <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nutritious Frog Meat</color>. I gotta prepare a special \"delicacy\" for Phreeoni. Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue8060701"]="Lovely! We're ready to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color> and show that arrogant Phreeoni the mighty power of a heroine! (๑•̀ㅂ•́)و✧~! Huh? What are you still standing around for? I never said I'm gonna go alone. Of course you're coming with me. Get moving!",
    ["Dialogue8060801"]="(Trisse carefully coats the frog meat with poison.)\nHehe, it's going to get it now! Hurry and place this <color=#CA2E0AFF>poisonous meal</color> where <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phreeoni tends to visit</color>. We're about to get a good show!",
    ["Dialogue8060802"]="Hmph! I bet no monster will dare pick on the weak and defenseless in this desert anymore! Let's go give the good news to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drops</color>! It should be able to go back to its people now.",
    ["Dialogue8060901"]="Ahem! The evil Phreeoni has been defeated by yours truly!",
    ["Dialogue8060902"]="(Drops spins around Trisse happily.)\nPo~!! Pori, po~pori! (≧ω≦*)~~",
    ["Dialogue8060903"]="Hehe, the Drops says it's very grateful for your help. And... Oh dear me, it says it has prepared a very precious <color=#CA2E0AFF>gift</color> for you too!",
    ["Dialogue8060904"]="Oh my, it didn't have to. How nice...!\n(Trisse is so happy she covers her face with both hands.)\nA hero doesn't require a reward... Of course, if you're gonna give me one anyway, it'd be rude not to accept...",
    ["Dialogue8060905"]="Po~popopo, <size=24>pori! ヽ(✿ﾟ▽ﾟ)ノ~♪</size>\n(The Drops dances in place until a round fruit suddenly poofs into existence.)",
    ["Dialogue8060906"]="Ah! This... Could this be...\n(Trisse's eyes widen.)\nHey, hey! Isn't this just an apple?! I'd rather take the commission... Hey, don't you run away! <size=24>HEY!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8070101"]="(Dobbin rests his cheek against his hand with a solemn expression.)\n<size=18>Hmm... </size><size=18>There must be a reason why this <color=#CA2E0AFF>legendary recipe</color> came into my possession...</size>",
    ["Dialogue8070102"]="Who are you... <size=24>Oh? </size><size=24>Are you the emissary sent by the culinary gods to help me?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8070103"]="Then listen well to what I'm about to say next, because it's about to change our destinies. I was out gathering ingredients one day when I fell off a cliff and right into this dark cave. When I woke up, there was a tablet carved with undecipherable ancient text right in front of me. And right on top of the tablet's pedestal is this legendary recipe—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Unforgettable Octopus Sashimi</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8070104"]="Anyway, I knew I found my calling at that moment. I have to revitalize the dish in this recipe! That's also why I'm here by the ocean, to get my hands on the super premium ingredient for the Unforgettable Octopus Sashimi—the Gem of the Deep Ocean, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kraken's Meat</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8070105"]="(Dobbin knits his brows together as he thinks.)\nAs for how to do that... Hmm, I remember cuttlefish like to eat <color=#CA2E0AFF>Giant Tiger Prawns</color>, so I should get my hands on some of that first...",
    ["Dialogue8070106"]="(Dobbin looks at you incredulously.)\nHuh? What are you talking about? The precious hands of a master chef aren't meant for hard labor like this! We have to work together to bring the legend back to life. That is to say, it's all in your hands now!",
    ["Dialogue8070201"]="Good! I've turned these Giant Tiger Prawns into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragrant Bait</color> with my cooking skills! Now go place it in <color=#CA2E0AFF>areas of the underwater cave where Krakens often appear</color>. Then wait for the tasty targets to take a bite!",
    ["Dialogue8070202"]="(Dobbin looks at you incredulously.)\nHuh? What are you talking about? The precious hands of a master chef aren't meant for hard labor like this! We have to work together to bring the legend back to life. That is to say, it's all in your hands now!",
    ["Dialogue8070301"]="(Dobbin's face turns red in excitement.)\nOohhh! So this is the Gem of the Deep Ocean, Kraken's Meat! Good! We're one step away from bringing the legend back to life. My hands are blessed by the food gods, you know. I'll use them to recreate a miracle in the world of cooking!",
    ["Dialogue8070401"]="(Dobbin serves you the Unforgettable Octopus Sashimi, his eyes shining with excitement.)\nLook at how fresh the meat is, how tender the skin... It's bound to be an explosive experience for our taste buds! Let us bear witness to its flavor!\nHomph, nom, homph, nom...",
    ["Dialogue8070402"]="......",
    ["Dialogue8070403"]="......",
    ["Dialogue8070404"]="(Dobbin wipes at the hot tears in his eyes.)\nI... I finally understand why it's called the Unforgettable Octopus Sashimi.\n<size=24>That is way too much mustard!!! இдஇ~！</size>",
    ["Dialogue8080101"]="(Perini waves at you.)\nHey, hey, adventurer! Can you help me out? I'm trying to make a dish but one of the ingredients is really hard to get...",
    ["Dialogue8080102"]="...Huh? Cliffs and caverns and legendary recipes? Get with the times! It's AW1000 and that's way too old-fashioned! I'm just trying to make the legendary dish, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heartbreak Shrimp</color>, to show senior <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dobbin</color> how good I am.",
    ["Dialogue8080103"]="Siiiigh, it's true... I secretly followed senior Dobbin all the way to this island! He's so tall, handsome, and talented! And most importantly, unlike how cold he is to me all the time, he's obsessed with cooking! <size=24>Kyaaaa!! (*/▽＼*)~~</size>",
    ["Dialogue8080104"]="Oh, that's right. I forgot to tell you what I needed help with! The key ingredient to Heartbreak Shrimp is <color=#CA2E0AFF>King Dramoh's Meat</color>, but you need to first get King Dramoh's favorite food, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed</color>, if you want to get near it.",
    ["Dialogue8080201"]="Wow! You got the Water Weed already? But we're not done yet!\n(With shocking speed, Perini turns the water Weed into bait.)\nThis is for the tall, handsome, and ever-talented senior Dobbin! Now go place the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragrant Bait</color> where <color=#CA2E0AFF>King Dramohs frequent</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8080301"]="Wow! The King Dramoh's Meat looks so tender! These delicious ingredients must be just as eager to leap into senior Dobbin's mouth... Siiiiigh~! Just thinking about the tall, handsome, talented senior Dobbin eating the food I make is enough to make all this effort worth my while! <size=24>Kyaaaa!! (*/▽＼*)~~</size>",
    ["Dialogue8080401"]="Hurry! Bring this Heartbreak Shrimp <color=#CA2E0AFF>to senior Dobbin so he can eat it</color> while it's still hot! This is my best dish yet. He's sure to love it!",
    ["Dialogue8080402"]="(Perini's gaze suddenly wavers and she covers her reddened face with both hands.)\nHaaaaaahh! What if senior Dobbin cries from how moved he feels? Would he grow so overwhelmed and say, \"The person who marries a perfect woman like Perini will be a happy individual indeed\"? <size=24>Kyaaaa!! (*/▽＼*)~~</size>",
    ["Dialogue8080501"]="You mean... This is Perini's cooking?\n(Dobbin frowns suspiciously and cautiously takes a bite of the Heartbreak Shrimp.)",
    ["Dialogue8080502"]="Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue8080503"]="Ah...",
    ["Dialogue8080504"]="......",
    ["Dialogue8080505"]="Seriously, Perini... Could you please tell her...",
    ["Dialogue8080506"]="<size=24>To never cook onions with shrimp ever again?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8090101"]="(Morts looks pleased with himself.)\nHeheh! My dear adventurer, have you noticed anything different about me lately?",
    ["Dialogue8090102"]="Hey, don't you start! I've been taking good care of my body, you know! Take a closer look. Don't you see the vibrant color in my eyes? The healthy red tinge on my skin? And all this is thanks to her... My dream <color=#CA2E0AFF>girl</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8090103"]="Haha! I knew you'd be able to tell! That's right, my eyes are full of color and my skin is a much healthier sheen of red! And all this is thanks to her... My dream <color=#CA2E0AFF>girl</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8090104"]="(Morts dreamily plays his lute.)\nAhh~ She has the purest of souls~ Not even Freyja, the goddess of love, can compare~♪\nAhh~ She dances to the music of my lute, infusing my notes with her very soul~♪",
    ["Dialogue8090105"]="Ahh~ I've sung praises to many a flower but her beauty turns my tongue to iron~♪\nAhh~ From the moment we met, I knew... She was the one destined for me~♪",
    ["Dialogue8090106"]="Sigh, but it's too early to celebrate... There's something missing on this enchanting young lady, and it's that those cherry red lips are unable to make a sound! As a bard who sings of love and beauty, how can I bear to allow such a beautiful jade be marred with imperfection? Adventurer, will you help <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore</color> my love's voice?",
    ["Dialogue8090107"]="Actually, I did meet a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young acolyte</color> on my way here. I'm sure he'll be able to help solve this problem. Surely he's the emissary sent by Odin to realize my dreams!",
    ["Dialogue8090108"]="(Morts continues to dreamily play his lute.)\nAhh~ I was once a lost boat drifting out at sea~♪\nBut I've finally found my eternal dock with you~♪",
    ["Dialogue8090201"]="(Abessie seems lost in thought.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Sigh... I can't believe it. </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I forgot to ask that swordswoman's name!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8090202"]="...Oh, my apologies! You wish to restore someone's voice, yes? It's quite simple, really. All you need to do is get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Refreshing Crab Paste</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vadons</color> nearby and leave the rest to me!",
    ["Dialogue8090301"]="One moment please. I'll turn the crab paste into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Voice Potion</color> right now... Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to a person who has lost their voice</color> and you'll see instant results!",
    ["Dialogue8090401"]="Haha! That's wonderful! With her voice restored, my love will become perfection! No other girl in the world can compare! Quickly! Bring the Voice Potion to her in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color> where she lives.\n<size=18>Ahh~ ahh~ </size><size=18>I can't wait to hear her angelic voice!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8090402"]="What's so strange about that? The goddesses in songs live in the heavens after all!\nAhh~ She belongs to the ocean, seen only by the chosen few~♪",
    ["Dialogue8090501"]="(The girl cautiously drinks the potion then clutches her throat in a panic.)\n...Mn... Erk... Egh... Hnn...",
    ["Dialogue8090601"]="(Poya looks at her fish tail in a panic.)\n...I-I'm sorry! I... I...!",
    ["Dialogue8090602"]="...You know the truth now. That's right, I'm not human. I'm an Obeaune from under the sea. I didn't transform myself to look human to do anything bad! I just didn't want to show my fish tail to that handsome young man. This... ugly fish tail that's different from all the other girls who live on land...",
    ["Dialogue8090603"]="You... You've met the handsome bard? I didn't want him to hate me, so I exchanged my voice for a pair of human legs... But it turns out the potion you gave me contains licorice root that Obeaunes can't eat. It's that very herb that forced me to reveal my true form...",
    ["Dialogue8090604"]="Oh... You mean the bard is the one who wanted to help restore my voice? And he said I'm... I'm...\n(Poya hides her blushing face behind her hands.)\nOh, hearing you say that is so embarrassing! That means my feelings aren't just wishful thinking and I can give that to him, right...?",
    ["Dialogue8090605"]="(Poya shyly hands over a letter.)\nThis is it. I... It took a lot of courage to write my feelings into this <color=#CA2E0AFF>love letter</color>! Could you help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>give this to the bard</color> and tell him...",
    ["Dialogue8090606"]="Ask him if... If...\n(Poya covers her face with her hands again.)\n...Would he still love me if I'm an Obeaune?",
    ["Dialogue8090701"]="(Morts accepts Poya's love letter with shaky hands. He looks ecstatic.)\nBy Odin, you mean this love letter is from that girl?! But why did she write her charming words on a piece of fish scale? And why is it written in some illegible... Huh?! What is this?",
    ["Dialogue8090702"]="(Morts instantly turns pale.)\n...W-w-w-wh... <size=24>WHAT?!</size>\nYou're telling me that perfect beauty is a... is an... an... <size=24>Obeaune?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8090703"]="(Morts rolls up his sleeves to show you his arms covered in goosebumps.)\nSee for yourself. I've been terrified of fish my whole life!! Ahh!! Why! Why does she have to be an Obeaune?! I would have taken an Isis!!",
    ["Dialogue8090704"]="...Er, hmm?",
    ["Dialogue8090705"]="...Huh? Did I sing that before? Haha... To be honest, I think I shouldn't be too hasty with my decisions...\nI believe it's time I go on a new journey!",
    ["Dialogue8100101"]="Hello there. My name is Dinza. I'm a merchant from the Merchant Guild...\n(Dinza looks around her secretively and excitedly moves closer to your ear.)\nI'll let you in on a secret. I'm about to make all the money!!",
    ["Dialogue8100102"]="(Dinza proudly shows off a crystal clear pearl from her pocket.)\nHeh heh! See this <color=#CA2E0AFF>pearl</color>? It's no common pearl. It's the rarest <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune's Tear</color> from the deep ocean! I bought this special from a sailor in Alberta for a very high price, but it's not the pearl itself that's valuable. It's the trade secret I got from the sailor!",
    ["Dialogue8100103"]="Heh heh, it's common knowledge that a single pearl can you get me a handful of coin but I'll have an endless stream of income with this business! That's right! The sailor told me <color=#CA2E0AFF>how to get more Obeaune's Tears</color>! And now I'm here in the Underwater Temple to get myself more pearls. Soon I'll become the greatest merchant in the Merchant Guild! Hehe! What do you think? Will you help a future businesswoman reach her goal?",
    ["Dialogue8100104"]="How about this. You go over to a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color> and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coarse Shell Powder</color>, then I'll use it to...\n(Dinza quickly covers her mouth.)\nOh man, I nearly gave it away. What comes next is a trade secret! I'm not about to tell you!",
    ["Dialogue8100201"]="Wow! You got your hands on so much Coarse Shell Powder so quickly! I see having powerful adventurers like you as a money-making business partner is not a bad idea... Hm, hm...",
    ["Dialogue8100202"]="But we're not done yet! I need you to gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smelly Shrooms</color> that grow at the bottom of the ocean, then I'll use it to...\n(Dinza quickly covers her mouth.)\nOh man, I nearly gave it away. What comes next is a trade secret! I'm not about to tell you!",
    ["Dialogue8100301"]="Wonderful! I knew you could do it! Next I'll just have to...\n(Dinza turns away and starts to fiddle about secretively.)\nTada~! Presenting the special Obeaune <color=#CA2E0AFF>Liquid Tear Gas</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8100302"]="Heh heh. According to the sailor, all we need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>pour the Liquid Tear Gas on an Obeaune</color> and we'll be able to collect Obeaune's Tears! But since we're here anyway, I'd like to try something out too...",
    ["Dialogue8100303"]="(Dinza shows you a sly smile.)\nHeh, heh, heh... I'm assuming the tears from an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaune High Priestess</color> would be worth more than a regular Obeaune, so why don't you pour the Tear Gas on a Obeaune High Priestess for me?",
    ["Dialogue8100401"]="(Leona looks devastated.)\nUgh... What... What is this smelly liquid?!",
    ["Dialogue8100402"]="(Leona shakes her head in exasperation.)\nWhat nonsense. This isn't how you harvest Obeaune's Tears! If the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tears don't come from the heart</color>, it won't crystallize into a pearl. If not for that, the humans would have captured and turned us into slaves long ago! Ugh...",
    ["Dialogue8100501"]="(Dinza looks at you expectantly.)\nWell? Did you get the Obeaune's Tears?",
    ["Dialogue8100502"]="<size=24>HUH?! </size><size=24>What did you say?! </size>\nYou're saying the Liquid Tear Gas can't harvest Obeaune's Tears at all?! But that sailor said...",
    ["Dialogue8100503"]="(Dinza suddenly clutches her cheeks in horror.)\n...Oh! Oh no!! What if... <size=24>It can't be!! </size>\nYou! Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>show this pearl to the Obeaune High Priestess</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8100601"]="(Leona stares at the pearl and is silent for a long moment.)\n...Uhm, why are you showing a fish eye to me?",
    ["Dialogue8100602"]="Sigh, this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gleaming Fish Eye</color> is easy enough to get from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phens</color> nearby. I have no use for it. You can keep it for yourself.",
    ["Dialogue8100701"]="(Dinza's eyes widen in delight.)\nWow! How did you get so many pearls?!",
    ["Dialogue8100702"]="<size=24>WHAT?! </size><size=24>You mean I... </size><size=24>A well-versed merchant like me </size><size=24>was conned by a mere sailor?! </size>\nBlast it, this is my greatest failure since I started doing business! When I find that guy, I'll...",
    ["Dialogue8100703"]="<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Hang on a minute, if these fish eyes can trick someone like me, then how would the commoners know they're not actually Obeaune's Tears? Maybe I can...</color></size>\nHeh, heh, heh...",
    ["Dialogue8100704"]="(Dinza's eyes are sparkling with Zeny.)\nAhem! No worries, no worries! I swear I'll uphold my honesty and integrity as a merchant and \"manage\" these fish eyes properly! Hehe!",
    ["Dialogue8100705"]="Heh heh! Like I said, there's no way a well-versed merchant like me can be conned by a mere sailor! I'll just be...\nMaking biiiig piles of money with these precious Obeaune's Tears!\n(Dinza's eyes are sparkling with Zeny.)",
    ["Dialogue8110101"]="(Abessie looks at you shyly.)\nAdventurer, can I... That is... Could you... Uhm...",
    ["Dialogue8110102"]="<size=18>No, no... Even if the swordswoman did save me in that cave, it was still our first time meeting each other. This wouldn't be appropriate.</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110103"]="<size=18>Besides, there's no way she'd remember an unremarkable guy like me. Someone so brave and beautiful and heroic would never... </size><size=18>Ahhhh!! Abessie, what are you thinking?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110104"]="<size=18>...No, no, no. It's exactly because she's so brave and beautiful and heroic that I shouldn't let this opportunity slip me by. What if I never get to...</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110105"]="...Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait! Please help me find a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purple-Haired Swordswoman</color> in this cave and tell her... Tell her I... I... I...",
    ["Dialogue8110106"]="(Abessie sucks in a deep breath and says with all his might.)\n<size=24>...Tell her! </size><size=24>I would like to <color=#CA2E0AFF>be her partner</color>!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110201"]="Oh, it's you! I was wondering what other adventurer had such skill. Haha!",
    ["Dialogue8110202"]="...Oh? I didn't know the young man I saved was called Abessie. He's right. I did save him from a monster attack once, but that sort of thing is normal for a brave adventurer. You'd do the same, wouldn't you? Tell him he doesn't have to go through the effort to thank me.",
    ["Dialogue8110203"]="What? Abessie wants to be my partner?! It's difficult enough trying to achieve my dream of becoming the best swordswoman in Midgard. I can't go babysitting a wannabe who can't even protect himsel—Ahem! What I meant to say is, adventuring is full of danger and hardship. If he wants to join me, he'll have to at least be as strong as you!",
    ["Dialogue8110204"]="(Ygnizem shakes her head.)\nWords won't be enough in this instance. There has to be proof! Tell you what, I heard the Phens around here are quite the problem. If Abessie can get enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Bones</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phens</color>, I'll acknowledge his strength!",
    ["Dialogue8110301"]="(Abessie is so emotional, he looks like he's about to cry.)\n...Y-you mean Ygnizem is willing to give me a chance?? This... This is... It's... \n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Ahhh!! I'm so happy I could burst...! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>N-no, Abessie, you gotta calm down first!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8110302"]="(Abessie takes a deep breath and clenches his fists with determination.)\nAlright. Fish Bones from Phens, right? I got it! I'll go get them right now! I'll put my life on the line if it means getting closer to Miss Ygnizem!",
    ["Dialogue8110303"]="(Abessie blinks his clear shining eyes.)\nThat's right. I'm just an acolyte. I know a lot about healing, but I've never done anything like killing monsters! But I'll do it for Miss Ygnizem... As long as it's for Miss Ygnizem, I-I'll give my life for glory!",
    ["Dialogue8110401"]="(Abessie looks at you with admiration in his eyes.)\nAmazing! You're just as awesome as Miss Ygnizem! But sadly I didn't contribute at all...",
    ["Dialogue8110402"]="<size=18>...Oh no, oh no! D-does this mean I failed Miss Ygnizem's test? I mean, she never said I had to complete it alone, b-but she also never said I can get help from someone else!!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110403"]="<size=18>I'm doomed! I'm doomed! If Miss Ygnizem finds out I didn't get these Fish Bones myself, will she think less of me? Will she hate me?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110404"]="<size=18>Sigh, an ordinary guy like me should just be thankful I ran into a perfect woman like that at all... </size><size=18>I should be happy! But I keep thinking about getting closer to her... </size><size=18>Aahhhh!!! Abessie, what are you thinking?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110405"]="...Oh, yes, yes! I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring these Fish Bones to Miss Ygnizem</color> right away!",
    ["Dialogue8110501"]="(Ygnizem frowns in dismay as she looks at the Fish Bones.)\nI didn't expect Abessie to actually succeed... Looks like I'll have to think of another way to get him to give up...",
    ["Dialogue8110502"]="Ahem! Anyway, I'm just about to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>exterminate some monsters</color>. That place is far more dangerous than this cave. I could get hurt if I'm not careful or even... die! So how about it? Are you brave enough to come with me? I won't judge you if you don't, the life of an adventurer is not just for anybody...",
    ["Dialogue8110503"]="...Get... hurt?\n(Abessie's eyes widen in shock.)",
    ["Dialogue8110504"]="Heh, that's right. Scary, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue8110505"]="(Abessie's gaze suddenly becomes very determined.)\nNo. With me there, I won't let you get hurt at all! Please let me come with you! I... I'll definitely be useful!",
    ["Dialogue8110601"]="Alright, this is it. The monsters in this Underwater Temple mutated thanks to a powerful burst of terrible energy, and it's my job to get rid of the crazed monsters in this area! If you're strong enough, you should have no trouble teaching the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mutant Fish</color> nearby a lesson. Let's split up and...",
    ["Dialogue8110602"]="M-miss Ygnizem, wait...",
    ["Dialogue8110603"]="If you can do this, I'll acknowledge you're strong enough!\n(With that, Ygnizem runs off.)",
    ["Dialogue8110701"]="(Abessie sighs dejectedly.)\nSigh, I could have helped Miss Ygnizem if we went together... I guess there's nothing I can do but face this head on! I have no experience fighting monsters but if it's for Miss Ygnizem... As long as it's for Miss Ygnizem, I-I'll give my life for glory!",
    ["Dialogue8110801"]="(Abessie looks toward Ygnizem in a panic.)\nM-miss Ygnizem...?!",
    ["Dialogue8110802"]="(Abessie hurriedly crouches down next to her.)\nMiss Ygnizem, what happened to you? Your face is so pale... Wait a minute! What's this?!",
    ["Dialogue8110803"]="(Ygnizem grits her teeth. She looks like she's in a lot of pain.)\n...",
    ["Dialogue8110804"]="(Abessie is examining Ygnizem's injury attentively.)\nOh no... Miss Ygnizem has been bitten by a venomous Deviace! Only the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pinnatifida</color> that lives on the sea floor can counter the venom. Can you get me the herbs as fast as you can?",
    ["Dialogue8110805"]="Please don't worry. I may be no good in battle but I can definitely keep myself and my companions safe from injury! I have to stay here and stop Miss Ygnizem's bleeding... Please hold on. I'll help you get better!",
    ["Dialogue8110901"]="(Abessie carefully places the Pinnatifida over Ygnizem's wound and breathes a sigh of relief.)\nPhew... She's out of danger now. All she needs is some rest and Miss Ygnizem will be up and moving in no time. If I had stayed with Miss Ygnizem from the start, none of this would have happened...",
    ["Dialogue8110902"]="(Abessie looks startled by a realization and blushes all the way down to his neck.)\n<size=24>...A-aahhhhh! </size><size=24>W-what am I saying?! I'm sorry, I'm sorry! I wasn't doubting your strength at all, Miss Ygnizem! </size>\nI- I...",
    ["Dialogue8110903"]="No, you were right. I misjudged you and suffered for it. All this time I thought strength was all that mattered and forgot about all the people who have been silently protecting and supporting me all along... I'm the one who should apologize. Please forgive my arrogance!",
    ["Dialogue8110904"]="As of right now, I would accept... No, I gladly invite you to be my companion, to form an adventurer's squad with me and explore the realm of Midgard! You're an indispensable part of my journey and I hope to become the same in your eyes!",
    ["Dialogue8110905"]="Miss Ygnizem...\n(Abessie's voice is quiet. His face still red as he tries to muster up the courage to speak.)\n...Miss Ygnizem... The truth is... <size=24>The truth is I...!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8110906"]="Haha! I know, I know! I feel the same way about you too! From now on, we'll be the best of friends! You'll forever be my trusted confidant and companion!",
    ["Dialogue8110907"]="...What?! <size=24>Whaaat?! இдஇ——?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8120101"]="(Ygnizem stares at Kavaski intently.)\nI'm sure a powerful archer like you must want to leave this village behind to see the world and make a name for yourself!",
    ["Dialogue8120102"]="I heard about Kavaski in the course of my adventures. He's an exceptional prodigy in Archer Village and I'd love to invite him to join our adventurer's squad to become the strongest adventurers there ever was in Midgard!",
    ["Dialogue8120103"]="Hmph, a prodigy? I bet you didn't hear that from my master. Everyone knows I'm the most talented among my peers. I could kill two birds with one arrow at the age of ten. I excel in every class. And yet Master Sky Euin refuses to acknowledge me. He never praised me once growing up. What makes you think I'm a prodigy?",
    ["Dialogue8120104"]="I...",
    ["Dialogue8120105"]="Hmph! If you really want me to join your little squad, then prove to me you're strong enough. I'm the only archer in the village who can exterminate the Willows in the forest the fastest. If you really want to be the strongest swordswoman in the land, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>collecting</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>100 Willow Barks</color> in a day shouldn't be a problem, right?",
    ["Dialogue8120106"]="What?! 100...?! That's absurd...\n(Abessie looks on in disbelief.)",
    ["Dialogue8120107"]="(Ygnizem looks determined.)\nAlright! I'll do it! And when I do, you'll have to join us!",
    ["Dialogue8120201"]="Phew, I finally got them all. Great! Thanks for helping out, you two. It'll be a pain to collect all of these by myself. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Kavaski</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8120202"]="Miss Ygnizem... You don't have to thank us. We're a team. I-I know my strength is limited, but... but I feel honored just being able to help you!!",
    ["Dialogue8120301"]="Hmph. I guess you pass my test. I could do this easily since I was ten, but master would only say I lack patience and perseverance. What good is patience when I already have the strength that I do?",
    ["Dialogue8120302"]="Kavaski, I think your master is right. I was like you once. I thought strength was everything and that I had no need for patience or to play the long game. But there are some things you can only get by persevering.",
    ["Dialogue8120303"]="(Kavaski looks back with disdain on his face.)\nOh? Is that so? If patience is so precious to you, why don't you go to the south, west, and east sides of Payon and gather 10 Purple Herbs, 10 Grim Grass, and 10 Chrysanthemums. I'd love to see how patient you actually are.",
    ["Dialogue8120304"]="You... You... You're just being difficult now! Miss Ygnizem... Th-this is too much...!",
    ["Dialogue8120305"]="(Ygnizem looks determined.)\nAlright! I accept your challenge! Once I bring you those herbs, you can't give me any more excuses!",
    ["Dialogue8120306"]="Heheh, just you wait!",
    ["Dialogue8120401"]="Mr. Kavaski is being really unreasonable. I think we should split up to gather everything. Miss Ygnizem and I can gather the Purple Herbs to the south and the Grim Grass to the west. Could you help us gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Chrysanthemums</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon East</color>, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8120402"]="Thank you, everyone. I have faith we'll be able to change Kavaski's mind yet!",
    ["Dialogue8120501"]="Oh? Grim Grass and Chrysanthemums? Where's the remaining 10 Purple Herbs? Speaking of, where's the swordswoman? Didn't she come back with you? I guess all her talk of patience really is just hot air.",
    ["Dialogue8120502"]="That's not true! Miss Ygnizem would never just give up!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>But... she really has been gone a long time... Ah! </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Do you think she could be in danger?!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8120503"]="Hmph, I'm not about to wait. I'm sure she got tired of it and gave up. She's just another person who's all talk without the skills to back it up. I know all about people like her.",
    ["Dialogue8120504"]="I won't let you talk about Miss Ygnizem that way! You don't know her at all! She'd never break a promise! She must be in danger. <color=#CA2E0AFF>We should go look for her.</color>\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Oh, I hope Miss Ygnizem is all right...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8120601"]="Huh? Why are you here? I'm sorry I'm late! I finished gathering the Purple Herbs but I ran into some trouble on the way back.",
    ["Dialogue8120602"]="What?! WHAAAT?! Trouble?! Miss Ygnizem, are you alright?!!\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>This is all my fault... I should have stayed by your side... I-if you got hurt, I... I...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8120603"]="I'm alright. I found an old man collapsed on the side of the road on my way back. He was in a bad state so I couldn't waste any time.",
    ["Dialogue8120604"]="Stop blathering. Where are my Purple Herbs?",
    ["Dialogue8120605"]="The herbs...? Oh, I apologize. I used them to help the old man recover, so I won't be able to complete your quest right now. However, if you don't mind giving me more time, I'll go gather more for you right now!",
    ["Dialogue8120606"]="What?! Did you forget the reason you spent all that time gathering the herbs to begin with? Don't you want me to join your team?",
    ["Dialogue8120607"]="Of course I want you to join us! But <color=#CA2E0AFF>sometimes there are things more precious than our own goals </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>that should be protected.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8120608"]="(Kavaski looks very confused.)\nSomething more precious? What can be more important than proving ourselves?!",
    ["Dialogue8120609"]="Integrity, kindness, the life of a companion. I only just learned this on my recent adventure myself. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Not sacrificing another person for my own benefit </color><color=#CA2E0AFF>should be the true mark of a great adventurer.</color>\n(Ygnizem's smile is confident and resolute.)",
    ["Dialogue8120610"]="(Kavaski lowers his head pensively.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Is this why my master would never acknowledge my talents? </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>All I ever thought about was growing stronger, </color></size><size=18><color=#A1979FFF>but I never really considered why I should be... Or what I should be protecting.</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8130101"]="(Sun Euin frowns deeply.)\nIt's been many years since so many monster corpses were found in Payon. We must investigate.",
    ["Dialogue8130102"]="All of Payon West is fearful and on alert lately thanks to the frequent appearance of piles of monster corpses. The rumors are getting wildly out of control.",
    ["Dialogue8130103"]="I understand I'm asking a lot but for the sake of the citizens, could you help us investigate in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon West</color>, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8130201"]="Where in the world did you come from? You're getting in the way of my trial!",
    ["Dialogue8130202"]="(Zenlur looks indignant.)\nI don't need your 'help'! There's not a single monster in this world that can harm a hair on my head. Now get out of my way. I have to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon South</color> to exterminate some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wormtails</color>. I don't have time for this.",
    ["Dialogue8130301"]="The weak should get out of the area right now! I won't rescue you if you get hurt.",
    ["Dialogue8130401"]="Looks like you're good enough to be a match for me. But let's make one thing clear, I chose Peerless Jin as my mentor first. You can't have him!",
    ["Dialogue8130402"]="You don't know who Master Peerless Jin is?! I wandered far and wide before I discovered this master who has hidden himself away from the world. He doesn't care for worldly matters, but time and again, he has refused my requests to be his disciple.",
    ["Dialogue8130403"]="(Zenlur looks proud and determined.)\nShows what you know! Of course such a transcendent master won't just take anyone for a disciple! It's customary to go through some trials first. As long as I persevere and complete the trials he gave me, I'll prove to him my strength and determination. He's sure to accept me then.",
    ["Dialogue8130404"]="Since you're not interested in learning from the master, why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell Peerless Jin that I've completed my trials</color>? See whether I've finally met his standards. You can see for yourself how great he is too.",
    ["Dialogue8130501"]="(Peerless Jin clasps his hands behind his back.)\nHm, have you come to learn from me as well, young one? Come closer and let me take a good look at you. It has been many years since I saw so much youthful energy.",
    ["Dialogue8130502"]="Hahaha! I see. He has exterminated the monsters and completed his trials! Very good! I knew he could do it. A talented martial artist with so much potential is hard to come by these days. With proper training and guidance, I can pass on my mantle and have him accomplish great things with my techniques.",
    ["Dialogue8130503"]="I've waited many long years for a youngster like that to come and return my martial arts to glory. Of course I intend to take him under my wing and teach him well.\nHowever, he seems to be the type of youth who could be difficult, so I have to be mindful of my approach...",
    ["Dialogue8130504"]="(Peerless Jin smiles slyly.)\nHeh heh, you must understand. He would only come to treasure the opportunity if he believes I'm distant and uninterested. The harder he has to work for me to accept him, the more he would pour his heart into my art.",
    ["Dialogue8140101"]="(The goddess looks surprised.)\nYou... No wonder...",
    ["Dialogue8140102"]="(The goddess stares at you in disgust.)\nYou have a very familiar scent... One I loathe very much. Feh...",
    ["Dialogue8140103"]="You are just like me. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ominous blood</color> flows in your veins...",
    ["Dialogue8140104"]="Hah! The blood of the gods? What of it? You must have never seen true despair and darkness, adventurer. Felt the kind of fear that bubbles from the depths of your soul, eager to consume your very being...",
    ["Dialogue8140201"]="(The goddess smiles mysteriously.)\nI shall indulge your curiosity and give you a special demonstration. Are you ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>face true darkness head-on</color>? To see the dark side of this seemingly beautiful world and how deeply it drags men into the pit of despair?",
    ["Dialogue8140202"]="You have courage, I give you that. Very well... Let us begin.",
    ["Dialogue8140203"]="Hehe... It's all right if you can't take it. You can always turn back.",
    ["Dialogue8140301"]="(Sarah Arlene looks pale.)\n...W-where am I? W-who are you...? Did you save me?",
    ["Dialogue8140302"]="I remember... helping mom look for food in the forest. And then... I don't remember... I live in the village up ahead! My dad's the head of the village. Oh, my name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sarah Arlene</color> by the way. Thank you for your help!",
    ["Dialogue8140303"]="(Sarah Arlene looks like she's about to cry.)\nThe village is starving. So many people have died, and mom keeps giving me all the food we have. But I can tell her health is growing worse by the day, so I thought I'd come to the forest to get her some food, but...",
    ["Dialogue8140304"]="Oh no, I didn't realize it's so late! I have to go back before my parents worry. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue8140401"]="Show me. My, I see a tinge of despair in your eyes...",
    ["Dialogue8140402"]="What you saw was a mere prelude to true despair. Return to me again if you wish to know more...",
    ["Dialogue8140501"]="Oh? You're prepared to witness the depths of this darkness?",
    ["Dialogue8140502"]="Such courage! Very well...",
    ["Dialogue8140503"]="You'd do well to reconsider. It's not too late to turn back if it proves to be too much for you.",
    ["Dialogue8140601"]="The adventurer...? What are you doing in our village? You shouldn't get involved! You have to leave quickly!",
    ["Dialogue8140602"]="The goddess was the one who saw fit to bless us with two emissaries. They were so close to saving us... It was almost over... It's your fault for showing up and ruining everything!\n(Devlin looks at you ruefully.)",
    ["Dialogue8140603"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>The goddess's emissaries</color> have figured out the cause of the famine. It's caused by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ominous bloodline</color> that flows in my wife and daughter's veins. That bloodline is the reason calamity has befallen Payon!",
    ["Dialogue8140604"]="I have to end this bloodline... I must... There's only one left... Once I do that, life will go back to normal...\n(Devlin's smile is twisted and warped.)",
    ["Dialogue8140605"]="Sarah, my dearest daughter... What are you doing all the way over there? Come to papa...\n(Devlin's smile grows more sinister.)",
    ["Dialogue8140701"]="Did the story go the way you expected it to, adventurer? How naive...\n(The goddess smiles darkly.)",
    ["Dialogue8140702"]="There's no need to hurry. I will show you the rest. Come find me again when you're ready.",
    ["Dialogue8140801"]="Are you ready to witness what comes next?",
    ["Dialogue8140802"]="Hehe. Then let us continue...",
    ["Dialogue8140803"]="Hehe... It's still not too late to change your mind...",
    ["Dialogue8140901"]="No, no, no, don't come any closer...! *Sobs* Please! Please let me go...! *Sobs*",
    ["Dialogue8140902"]="There's nothing to be scared of. Come closer.",
    ["Dialogue8141001"]="The calamity is over. Odin has not deserted us...",
    ["Dialogue8141002"]="I am an emissary of Odin, here to save Sarah's poor soul. She is still in shock but I shall be here to soothe her. The wound on her hand requires treatment, however. Would you gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cerulean Grass</color> outside the village?",
    ["Dialogue8141101"]="Adventurer, your task here is done. You may go.",
    ["Dialogue8141102"]="Sarah has experienced severe mental trauma, and scars of the soul tend to be the hardest to heal. For her sake, she has been <color=#CA2E0AFF>taken to the realm of the gods</color> for further treatment. There's no need to worry, adventurer. I shall care for her and raise her as my own daughter.",
    ["Dialogue8141103"]="Sometimes it's the flowers that grow in harsh barren soil that have the most vibrant bloom. Don't you think so, successor of Odin's Bloodline?",
    ["Dialogue8141201"]="Flowers that grow in harsh barren soil have the most vibrant bloom. Hehe... What do you think?",
    ["Dialogue8141202"]="Not all goddesses who look, feel, and speak the same as all the rest should be considered \"gods.\"",
    ["Dialogue8141301"]="(A little girl is collapsed on the ground. Her breathing weak.)\nWater... water...",
    ["Dialogue8150101"]="Looks like it's going to take some effort to get into the underground cave... But I'm not about to give up on the chance to visit an ancient city that's been slumbering away for a thousand years.",
    ["Dialogue8150102"]="There's a famous ruin known throughout the field of archaeology in an underground cave in Archer Village. I wanted to study it for myself, but Archer Village has some very strict rules and we've been trying to figure out how to get in...",
    ["Dialogue8150103"]="I did hear that all matters in Archer Village get resolved by the Archer Guild leader, Sky Euin. How about you help <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring our case to Sky Euin</color>, adventurer? Ask him to make an exception for us to enter the cave to investigate?",
    ["Dialogue8150201"]="You look troubled, adventurer. What is the matter?",
    ["Dialogue8150202"]="What?! Absolutely not! Munak Cave is exceedingly dangerous. We have only managed to keep the peace in Archer Village all these years thanks to our strict regulations. Only a strong, capable, and trustworthy adventurer like you would be allowed entry. Commoners are forbidden.",
    ["Dialogue8150301"]="What did Sky Euin say? I swear my team and I will follow all the rules.",
    ["Dialogue8150302"]="(Bowya sighs in disappointment.)\nSigh, very well. I was aware of how strict Archer Village is before this. It seems we're not destined to see the ancient city within the cave for ourselves. But since you did get approval. Could you help us look for some research material inside the cave?",
    ["Dialogue8150303"]="I've heard of so many unique locales within that ancient city. Let's see... There's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forgotten Lake Waterfall, Yin-Yang Taiji, Soul Devourer</color>, and oh, and can't forget the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Butsudan</color>! Oh, I wish I could see it with my own two eyes. Please, adventurer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bring</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>photos</color> back to us.",
    ["Dialogue8150401"]="(Bowya's eyes are sparkling.)\nAmazing! So these... These are the legendary ruins! It's more fascinating than the books describe... Even the dilapidated and crumbling walls carry a mysterious eastern flair. It's truly captivating to look at...",
    ["Dialogue8150402"]="Hmm... At this rate, these photos won't be anywhere near good enough for proper research. Adventurer, could you bring back some relics from the cave? I'm thinking 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Remains</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skeletons</color> and 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Runes of Resurrection</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bonguns</color> should suffice.",
    ["Dialogue8150501"]="(Bowya looks very excited.)\nThese truly are legendary relics! I can feel the extraordinary energy radiating from them... Oh, if only I could enter the cave myself...\nWhat if I dug a tunnel under the guards at the entrance... That way I could go in and explore and hopefully discover more hidden secrets!",
    ["Dialogue8160101"]="Coward! Show yourself! Hic! I'll show you what's what!",
    ["Dialogue8160102"]="Hic! I've been in a good mood lately so I used some premium ingredients to make three jars of osmanthus flower brew! I h-hid them in the wine celler but when I... Hic! When I came to get them this morning, they were all gone! Adventurer, help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate and find the brazen thieves</color> who <color=#CA2E0AFF>stole my wine</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8160201"]="Hic! You disappeared for half a day just to bring back this... This monkey? Hic! A monkey bold enough to sneak into MY wine cellar and STEAL from me? Let me get a better look... Heh heh, maybe I can ferment its noggin into some wine... Hic!",
    ["Dialogue8160202"]="*Squeaks*",
    ["Dialogue8160203"]="Hic! This... This monkey has a name? Abu...? Hahahaha! You were framed...? How absurd... Hic! Tell me... Who's the culprit then?",
    ["Dialogue8160204"]="*Squeaks!*",
    ["Dialogue8160205"]="Oho? Interesting... You were threatened with violence? Hic! The monkey has a boss! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bring me to him then</color>, or else... Or else I'll ferment you into wine and drink you myself! Hic!",
    ["Dialogue8160301"]="You stupid monkey! It's just two jars of wine! What took you so long? Or were you that eager for a taste of my fists?",
    ["Dialogue8160302"]="(Juke grins drunkenly.)\nHic! So you're the one... You're the one who's been stealing my wine! Hahaha! Hic! Is a couple decades all it took for you to... To sink to asking monkeys to steal wine for you? What happened? Can't afford it no more? Hic! Ahahaha!",
    ["Dialogue8160303"]="(Peerless Jin looks solemn with his hands clasped behind his back.)\nHmph! I can get any wine I desire. I sent the monkey on an errand to keep it out of trouble, not to steal from you. Hmph! Seems it has bad taste in wine too.",
    ["Dialogue8160304"]="Oho~ The stubborn old fool thinks my wine isn't good enough, does he? Hic! You still holding a grudge from that time I gave you three jars of osmanthus flower brew and... And got you sick in front of that girl you liked? Hic! How was I supposed to know that'd happen! Everyone else drank it fine!",
    ["Dialogue8160305"]="You.. Shut your mouth, you drunken fool! I'm not that petty! I've merely been busy with my martial arts techniques and lost interest in wine...\n(Peerless Jin is blushing to the tips of his ears. He presses his lips together tightly.)",
    ["Dialogue8160306"]="...Stubborn as ever, I see! Hic! Then you don't gotta d-drink my wine today neither! Gimme back my... Hic! Gimme back my wine!",
    ["Dialogue8160401"]="(There are footprints on the ground. They don't have the typical size and shape of human shoe prints though...)",
    ["Dialogue8160501"]="(Another set of footprints. Perhaps you'll find the wine thief if you follow it?)",
    ["Dialogue8170101"]="Actually, I... Erm... Well, why don't you go and see Katrina? She knows more about places outside of Geffen than I do.",
    ["Dialogue8170102"]="No, no, no. After my divination two days ago, I discovered that Katrina's elemental energy field is completely opposite to mine, so there's no way she can help me collect samples. Beudie, among all the members of the Mage Guild, you are the only one with an energy field that perfectly matches mine, so I've already made up my mind. I must complete this task with your help.",
    ["Dialogue8170103"]="(Beudie seems surprised to see you. His eyes twinkle as he pulls you aside and whispers in a low voice.)\nAdventurer, you must help me. This Celia really is so difficult. They say she has thrown herself into studying all these strange, unorthodox practices since she was a child that are totally different from what the other students at the magic academy usually learn.",
    ["Dialogue8170104"]="What are you talking about? Beudie, can we go now?\n(Celia approaches you and interrupts Beudie without a care in the world.)",
    ["Dialogue8170105"]="Er... Adventurer... You're just in time! Yes, Celia, look... This is the successor of Odin's bloodline! He'll help you to carry out your sample collection plan perfectly. I have several important things to handle for the Mage Guild. You should go and collect your samples quickly. I'll take my leave now!",
    ["Dialogue8170106"]="Beudie! Don't go!\n(Celia turns to look at you in dismay, but suddenly her eyes light up.)",
    ["Dialogue8170107"]="Odin's successor! I can see the radiance of Odin's bloodline within you! What Beudie said is true: you really can help me to finish my important work!",
    ["Dialogue8170108"]="Oh, I forgot to introduce myself. My name is Celia. I've been an exchange student at the Juno-Schuberz Academy for two semesters now. I came back this time to study the basic composition of Porings—you know, Porings are the most amazing monsters on the entire continent, but no one has studied their composition carefully up to now. It's really a pity...",
    ["Dialogue8170109"]="Well, since I've been away from the kingdom for such a long time, I'm a bit rusty at reading the local maps. A reliable guide is exactly what I need! After all, Porings can't be found in Geffen.",
    ["Dialogue8170110"]="(Celia blushes with shyness, and seems to be slightly embarrassed.)\nAnd anyway... Beudie put me in your hands, adventurer. You have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me to collect the Poring samples I need</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8170201"]="Quickly, adventurer! Look at this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pink Potion</color> I prepared for those lovely Porings! I call it Poring Passion! Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>throw it on the ground</color> and it will lure in all the Porings, then you can catch them all in one go!\n(Celia's eyes sparkle with excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue8170202"]="Hee-hee! Off you go! I'm expecting some good news from you!",
    ["Dialogue8170301"]="You're the successor of Odin's bloodline; of course I knew you could do it! But the truth is, I still have a small wish you can make come true... I know you'll help this poor little girl from out of town!",
    ["Dialogue8170302"]="I hear that the lovely little Porings are not the only monsters around here. The legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Angeling</color> has also been sighted around here. If I manage to collect some Angeling samples, I may just become the first person on the whole continent to uncover the composition of an Angeling! What an honor that would be!",
    ["Dialogue8170303"]="It's not a matter of greed—this is all in the spirit of persevering in one's research and tackling new challenges head-on! I know a mighty adventurer like you must be able to understand what I mean, right? Right?\n(Celia's big, shining eyes flicker as she stares at you expectantly.)",
    ["Dialogue8170304"]="So, let's go then!",
    ["Dialogue8170401"]="This must be the place... I've prepared a <color=#CA2E0AFF>special potion</color> just for this occasion. Here it is... See how it glitters and shines? It contains all the sparkling materials Angelings love most. If you're lucky, you should be able to attract the attention of an Angeling! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sprinkle it over the ground</color> for me.",
    ["Dialogue8170501"]="You really got a lot this time. Thank you so much! But...",
    ["Dialogue8170502"]="...In fact, of all the Porings in the land, there is only one specimen I'm still missing. If I go back without taking this chance to study the Poporings of Payon, I know I'll regret it for the rest of my life. You don't want to see me live a life wallowing in depression just because of such an easily-avoidable regret, do you?",
    ["Dialogue8170503"]="I know you don't have the heart to let such a thing happen, do you? You're going to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me to Payon to find the Poporing</color>, right?\n(Celia's long eyelashes flutter, and her eyes sparkle like glistening crystals.)",
    ["Dialogue8170601"]="You again? I really don't need any help. I just have a lot of time on my hands, so I've been using the nearby Poporings to practice my skills. If you hadn't interfered, I would've been done here ages ago.",
    ["Dialogue8170602"]="What a... dashing hero! Thank you very much! I'm Celia... I just need a Poporing specimen. I'm sorry to disturb your training.\n(A suspicious blush creeps across Celia's cheeks.)",
    ["Dialogue8170603"]="You're collecting Poporing specimens? What for?",
    ["Dialogue8170604"]="(Celia hangs her head low. Only the hand holding the corner of her coat seems to expose her nervousness.)\nErm... I'm writing a research paper entitled \"99 Delicious Juices: A Compositional Analysis of Porings\", so I'm collecting different samples from the Poring family.",
    ["Dialogue8170605"]="Making juice... from Porings? What's the point of that? You're one strange little girl...",
    ["Dialogue8170606"]="Well... Actually, I... I also think it's a bit strange...\n(Celia smiles shyly and smooths the messy hair around her ears.)",
    ["Dialogue8170607"]="Erm... Adventurer, can you introduce this... this dashing hero to me? You seem to be very familiar with each other... Hey! Don't go...!",
    ["Dialogue8180101"]="Eiffel... This is all my fault. I shouldn't have left you alone in the village... *sob, sob, sob*",
    ["Dialogue8180102"]="Eiffel is my friend, <color=#CA2E0AFF>an orange cat</color> I met a few days ago on the path outside Kordt Forest. I brought him home, but this morning, I went out to go play with Arlene, and when I got home, he had disappeared. I couldn't find him anywhere. It's all my fault! Waaah!",
    ["Dialogue8180103"]="When I got home, I realized that all the windows were open. Eiffel must've been hungry and ran out to find something to eat. I came all the way from the village to talk to Po and found out that a passing merchant said that he had seen a cat in Goblin Forest, so I came to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Eiffel</color> right away. But... but I've been searching and searching, and I still haven't found him! *sob, sob, sob*",
    ["Dialogue8180201"]="Thank you so much. If you hadn't arrived when you did, I wouldn't have been able to find this lovely big kitty! How could anyone not smile when looking at such a cute fat face?",
    ["Dialogue8180202"]="So, your name is Eiffel! I know just what to do with you, big kitty!",
    ["Dialogue8180203"]="Ha-ha! Adventurer, you're obviously not a resident of the City of Magic! If you were used to the strange magical experiments of the city's scholars, you certainly wouldn't be so surprised by a giant cat like this. I'm a member of the Mysterious Monster Research Institute. I heard that a giant orange cat had been seen wandering around here, so I came to take it in.",
    ["Dialogue8180204"]="However, this orange cat seems to be very irritable for some reason. As soon as he saw me, he chased me off! It seems that the only way we can capture it is to shrink it down a mite. Adventurer, I remember there being some Rahem Grass not far from here. If you could get me some, I think I may have a way. So, please go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some Rahem Grass</color> for me!",
    ["Dialogue8180301"]="Alright, here's the Shrinking Potion. This should make everything much easier, adventurer. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed this potion I've prepared to Eiffel</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8180401"]="Meow!",
    ["Dialogue8180402"]="This cat...? Do my ears deceive me? He seems to be talking? Did he say... \"idiot\"?",
    ["Dialogue8180403"]="Oh, no! I hope it's not what I think it is... Adventurer, go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>scrape some sap from the Sacred Tree</color>.\nIf what I think has really happened, there'll be trouble...",
    ["Dialogue8180501"]="This is exactly what I need. All I have to do is add it to this test tube and mix it... Quickly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed this medicine to Eiffel</color>, and I think we'll be in the clear.",
    ["Dialogue8180601"]="You idiots! I basically spelled it out for you, and it still took you this long to figure out I'm not a damn cat!",
    ["Dialogue8180602"]="Who's Eiffel?! My name's not Eiffel! If it wasn't for that guy's magic, I wouldn't have been dragged home by that stupid kid. Fortunately, I was smart enough to escape from the window while he was out.",
    ["Dialogue8180603"]="It seems the Magic Usage Supervision Committee have their work cut out for them here. You know, it's strictly forbidden to cast transformation spells on humans. This Hurst you mentioned must have a real problem with you to risk being caught doing such a thing. What did you do to him?",
    ["Dialogue8180604"]="I didn't do anything to him! I just planted some Durian Grass in my garden and he complained that his pet cat was allergic to it, even though he feeds his fat cat this strange squid all day long. Of all things?! How can a cat eat squid?!",
    ["Dialogue8180605"]="He said he wanted to show me exactly what Durian Grass does to cats, and then he dared to actually use this kind of forbidden magic on me! I'll show him what happens when you abuse magic like this!",
    ["Dialogue8190101"]="Adventurer, I need you to do me a favor. I've been waiting years for this chance. It's not every day one gets to impress Lord Howard. This will be my best opportunity to prove myself! I can't miss it!",
    ["Dialogue8190102"]="(Hollgrehenn smiles mysteriously.)\nAdventurer, put out your hands, quickly. Behold my latest masterpiece: the Midnight Sun, forged by yours truly!",
    ["Dialogue8190201"]="What do you think of it? Isn't it truly the perfect weapon, a treasure beyond your imagination? I spent a great deal of time and effort to craft this masterpiece. The craftsmanship behind this Midnight Sun is extremely exquisite. Even my idol, Howard, may not have been able to accomplish such a feat!",
    ["Dialogue8190202"]="Yes, you're right. This was made according to the shape of your weapon. In order to test the durability and sharpness of this weapon, I need the assistance of a powerful adventurer to test its actual effect. I've investigated this matter carefully, and have finally come to the conclusion that you are the ideal candidate.",
    ["Dialogue8190203"]="Indeed, and so I've been building this Midnight Sun using your usual weapon for several days. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>use this glorious Midnight Sun, that I so expertly crafted</color>, to <color=#CA2E0AFF>kill 20 Flail-wielding Goblins and 20 Mace-wielding Goblins</color>, and then take it to Howard to show him the ultimate power of the Midnight Sun!",
    ["Dialogue8190301"]="The weapon you hold exhibits a high level of forging skill. It is clear that the crafter is a highly-accomplished weapon smith. However...",
    ["Dialogue8190302"]="Just look here, and here... There are several obvious dents, which must have been caused by the impact of fighting monsters. I believe this kind of damage can only be repaired by a mage named Riedling. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell the forger of this weapon</color> that if they want to ensure the lethality and durability of this weapon, they must <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Riedling for help</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8190303"]="Huh? Adventurer, what are you doing here? Eh? That weapon in your hand...\n(Howard's eyes fall on the Midnight Sun and instantly light up.)",
    ["Dialogue8190304"]="I see... Please show me the weapon. I'm interested to see what kind of magical weapons the next generation of crafters are capable of forging!",
    ["Dialogue8190401"]="What?! Is that really what Master Howard said? How... how can this be? He wants me to go to Riedling?!",
    ["Dialogue8190402"]="Riedling is a member of the Magic Transformation and Application Association. He has been an enemy of the Merchant Guild for as long as I can remember.",
    ["Dialogue8190403"]="A first-class blacksmith like me, of course, pays close attention to the manufacturing and upgrading of his weapons through his own forging and tempering techniques. This is a blacksmith's pride!",
    ["Dialogue8190404"]="But the Magic Transformation and Application Association are solely concerned with using magic to enhance weapons. I can't allow myself to condone such opportunistic behavior! It's an insult to my profession!",
    ["Dialogue8190405"]="Allowing a mage to enhance the weapons I create is as good as admitting that blacksmithing alone is incapable of leading to the finest weapons, and can only rely on external assistance to produce the best results. I don't understand why Howard, a veritable Whitesmith, asked me to go to Riedling for help. There must be another way. Please, give me the Midnight Sun first.",
    ["Dialogue8190501"]="Alright, there's sure to be no problem now. I have reinforced this weapon with a unique forging technique; its attack power and durability have now been enhanced to new heights. Adventurer, please use it to kill <color=#CA2E0AFF>20 Orc Babies and Orc Warriors</color>, then we'll see what Howard thinks of the weapon I made.",
    ["Dialogue8190502"]="I believe that through my professional tempering and repairing techniques, and by adding the necessary upgrading materials during the casting process, this kind of thing will not happen again. I will never lose to that damned Magic Transformation and Application Association!",
    ["Dialogue8190601"]="(Howard looks at the weapon you handed him and shakes his head disappointedly.)\nAdventurer, come. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Try fighting me with this weapon</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8190602"]="Come on.",
    ["Dialogue8190701"]="Even if we were to go on fighting, the outcome would be the same.",
    ["Dialogue8190702"]="Adventurer, look at the weapon in your hand.",
    ["Dialogue8190703"]="This weapon has lost almost all of its destructive power and is already damaged. Adventurer, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take me to meet the maker of this weapon</color>. I think that perhaps I'm the only one who can impart some wisdom upon this aspiring crafter who seems so adamant to ignore good advice.",
    ["Dialogue8190801"]="How...? How could the Midnight Sun have been damaged to such an extent? I used the most advanced forging technology. It's impossible! Only a weapon of unparalleled power could have wrecked it like this.",
    ["Dialogue8190802"]="No, I used a common hand axe to fight against your weapon. It's just that the hand axe was enchanted with a magical blessing, granting it additional attributes.",
    ["Dialogue8190803"]="But as a craftsman, how can I rely on magic to enhance my weapons? Perfecting my forging skills is what I live for!",
    ["Dialogue8190804"]="What do you believe to be the most important thing for a blacksmith?",
    ["Dialogue8190805"]="Forging the most powerful weapons, of course.",
    ["Dialogue8190806"]="But your behavior tells me that you think your self-esteem is more important. I've met many blacksmiths who complacently rest on their laurels due to their so-called pride. They believe that traditional forging is a matter of dignity for blacksmiths. However, they don't understand that all techniques and technologies have their limitations. It is also very important to think about ways to break through these limitations and embrace professional opinions from other fields.",
    ["Dialogue8190807"]="I...",
    ["Dialogue8190808"]="If you can't let go of your arrogance, you will never be a truly great blacksmith. I came to Geffen to learn from the Magic Transformation and Application Association how to best integrate magic into the forging of my weapons. This is because I know that if I want to make the most powerful weapons in the world, I must travel to every corner of this continent to learn all I can.",
    ["Dialogue8190809"]="You must accept that there are great people working in various fields who can contribute greatly to our work and help us to forge weapons of unprecedented power.",
    ["Dialogue8190810"]="Adventurer, how did it go? After my repairs and enhancements, the attack power and endurance must have been much better than before. I'm sure I couldn't have disappointed Howard this time!",
    ["Dialogue8200101"]="This is the third time we've been robbed by those damned Goblins this month! This is getting out of control, meow!",
    ["Dialogue8200102"]="Why don't they just go and make their own money instead of stealing from other people?! Those sickening crooks! Meow!",
    ["Dialogue8200103"]="Those greedy Goblins probably guessed we'd be transporting goods through the forest they live in, and now they always come and plunder our pockets! All those gold coins and precious gems... Why should they be allowed to have them without even doing a single hard day's work in their lives?",
    ["Dialogue8200104"]="What are Wigner's Anti-Goblin Association grunts actually good for, meow?!",
    ["Dialogue8200105"]="It's not just our band of merchants who hates those Goblins, but the Wigner Chamber of Commerce has also been robbed many times by the fiends. That's why they've united with people from all walks of life to form an Anti-Goblin Association dedicated to driving off the Goblins. I hear they're still developing special items to deal with them.",
    ["Dialogue8200106"]="Haven't they been developing a kind of magical potion that can completely eliminate the Goblins? How come there's been no news of it so far? Meow!",
    ["Dialogue8200107"]="Adventurer, why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Lezard of the Anti-Goblin Association</color> and find out how the development of this magic potion is going?",
    ["Dialogue8200108"]="You look like a righteous adventurer indeed, meow! I'm sure you won't stand by and watch us being bullied by those Goblins over and again! Go and help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out how the potion's coming along</color>! Thanks, meow!",
    ["Dialogue8200201"]="(Lezard looks down and seems to be murmuring to himself.)\nNow, if we want to make any significant breakthroughs, it seems that will be the only way... But we don't have extra hands to help us catch some Goblins...",
    ["Dialogue8200202"]="Hmm? You seem to know a lot about what we're doing here. Indeed, our development of the potion has hit a bottleneck. If we wish to move forward, we'll need at least three kinds of Goblin blood samples. Since you also seem to be concerned with our research, why don't you help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>get these three kinds of Goblin blood</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8200203"]="I believe you have what it takes to get the job done.",
    ["Dialogue8200301"]="Ah-hah! Adventurer, you must be here to observe the Goblins, too. It appears more and more adventurers have unexpectedly become fascinated by mysterious creatures such as these. As a member of the Mysterious Monster Research Institute, I'm glad to have you join me!",
    ["Dialogue8200302"]="I'm Kersace, a member of the Mysterious Monster Research Institute. I'm here to record the living conditions of the Goblins. Although they are stubborn creatures, they are vital to maintaining the ecological balance of this forest.",
    ["Dialogue8200303"]="One of their main food sources is a poisonous red fruit that emits a noxious gas. This plant can survive the harshest conditions and reproduces with a rampant ferocity, yet it is only eaten by Goblins. Without them here to consume it, this forest would become a poisonous marsh, and might even threaten the safety of Geffen, the City of Magic.",
    ["Dialogue8200304"]="(Kersace shakes his head helplessly.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Come with me</color>, adventurer. Maybe you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>see the extent of this cruelty with your own eyes</color>...",
    ["Dialogue8200401"]="These Goblins were all killed by humans who hate their race. Although the Goblins have caused much trouble for human society, each creature holds a meaningful place in nature. Even evil monsters are an important part of this continent's ecosystem. In their eyes, maybe we are also seen as ferocious invaders, and even as monsters.",
    ["Dialogue8200402"]="In any case, culling any species in large numbers is sure to destroy this ecological balance, and may bring about new and unexpected disasters.",
    ["Dialogue8200501"]="How is it going with that Goblin blood? Our next research breakthrough will almost certainly depend on those samples.",
    ["Dialogue8200502"]="Very good. With these blood samples, our plan to eliminate the Goblins will soon enter its final stages. Thank you, adventurer. You will be listed among the contributors to this historical triumph!",
    ["Dialogue8200503"]="You mean, you met someone from the Mysterious Monster Research Institute? Those guys... Even if they refuse to contribute to our elimination of the Goblins, obstructing our research is going too far. I don't know what they could be thinking, but never mind. If you don't want to help, I'll find someone else.",
    ["Dialogue8210101"]="You see, it's very simple, really. Just press here, right here, see? And then...",
    ["Dialogue8210102"]="(The fierce Kobold bares its teeth.)\nShut it! Say another word, and... I'll end you!",
    ["Dialogue8210103"]="Please, Guard, it's really a very simple request. Just do me a small favor: take a single picture for me and I'll leave immediately. Please...",
    ["Dialogue8210104"]="Arooo! I'm gonna maul you to pieces!",
    ["Dialogue8210201"]="In any case, thank you very much. Those guards just wouldn't listen... Why were they so grumpy? I just wanted to take a picture.",
    ["Dialogue8210202"]="Ah, young adventurer! Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture</color> for me? I need a picture of <color=#CA2E0AFF>me with this strange-looking orange tree</color>. Please use this camera to take a pictures for me. Just press the pink button on top!",
    ["Dialogue8210301"]="Wow, I didn't expect that your photography skills to be so good! The light, the composition... Every element reveals an extraordinary aesthetic eye, young adventurer! You almost slipped it by me!",
    ["Dialogue8210302"]="Young adventurer, I've been thinking. After acting so rashly in the forest, maybe I was too reckless not to anticipate things like this happening. It's extremely dangerous! So, I have a somewhat selfish invitation to extend to you. I would like for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany me to the Goblin Camp</color>. Seeing you fight those Kobold guards just now has filled me with a newfound inspiration.",
    ["Dialogue8210303"]="Please, young adventurer, I still have some photos that I must take. They are the goal of this trip.",
    ["Dialogue8210401"]="Young adventurer, this seems to be the Goblin Camp. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>kill 10 Goblins</color> for me. I want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture with their corpses</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8210402"]="Please, I have my reasons. This photo is very important to me. Please believe me!",
    ["Dialogue8210501"]="Wow! Young adventurer, your photography skills really are exceptional! I look so heroic in this photo! Anyone who sees it will think I'm a mighty warrior!",
    ["Dialogue8210502"]="Hmm... But it's still not quite enough. If we want to convey even more vigor, we'll need an even more powerful photo! If you were to take a picture of me <color=#CA2E0AFF>with the Orc Lord</color>... Oh, the pride I would feel!\n(Reyard looks at you with expectant eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue8210503"]="Young adventurer, I promise that this will be the last photo I ask you to help me with. Please take me to the Orc Lord!",
    ["Dialogue8210601"]="Noble Lord, could I please trouble you to take a picture with me? We won't disturb you for long. You see, all you need to do is stand beside me and look at the Magic Camera in his hand. It'll just take a few seconds.",
    ["Dialogue8210602"]="A picture? I can't believe a puny human would actually dare to make such a bold request of me! We Orcs will never stand side by side with human beings, let alone pose in front of such strange devices like fools!",
    ["Dialogue8210603"]="My Lord, please don't leave! Please, listen to my story before you make your decision. The reason I'm here in this forest is because of my daughter, Lassia, my poor bed-bound child who can do nothing but lie in a hospital bed afflicted by a grave illness.",
    ["Dialogue8210604"]="What does that have to do with me? If your child is sick, take her to a doctor!",
    ["Dialogue8210605"]="My Lord, my poor daughter is in a comatose state. This camera of mine was augmented by a kind-hearted mage of Geffen so that the photos it takes can be directly transmitted to my daughter's mind.",
    ["Dialogue8210606"]="As a child, Lassia believed that I would become a great adventurer and travel around the continent with her. However, I didn't have the strength to achieve this dream. But now I have this camera! Yes! And I can send all of these images of my grand adventures to her, so that she can see the sights of the world—the sights of adventure! This may be... the only way for us to realize our dream.",
    ["Dialogue8210607"]="Please, My Lord. This is a very important picture for me and my daughter, Lassia.",
    ["Dialogue8210608"]="Well, human, although I still don't understand how such a contraption can help you realize your dreams, get over here. I will give you what you want.",
    ["Dialogue8210701"]="Thank you so much, My Lord. This photo means the world to me!",
    ["Dialogue8210702"]="Leave now. Don't disturb our village again.",
    ["Dialogue8210703"]="Let's leave now, adventurer. Now I have only one last wish. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>come with me to Geffen's Magic Fountain</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8210704"]="No, you'll understand when we get there.",
    ["Dialogue8210801"]="Adventurer, please return the Magic Camera to me now. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Strike a cool pose</color> in front of this fountain. Remember, it must be your coolest pose.",
    ["Dialogue8210802"]="Of course this extra cool photo is for you. Hurry and pose. Don't dawdle...",
    ["Dialogue8210901"]="Haha, it really is a perfect photo. We're done here.",
    ["Dialogue8210902"]="When I get home, I'll be sure to tell my daughter about this dashing adventurer, who's both passionate and kindhearted. I've never met a more heroic friend during my adventures.",
    ["Dialogue8220101"]="(The old woman is pleading reverently to the statue in front of her.)\nPlease listen to my request!",
    ["Dialogue8220102"]="It must be my fault that the goddess suddenly stopped responding to my requests.",
    ["Dialogue8220103"]="One month ago, I came to the Goddess Statue to pray for the safety of my family. Perhaps my sincerity touched the goddess, because she responded to me. It must have been the miracle that I prayed day and night for. The goddess told me that she will always protect my family as long as I worship her regularly. But for some reason, she is no longer responding to me today.",
    ["Dialogue8220104"]="It must be my poverty and disrespect that made the goddess unwilling to take pity on me anymore, but the tribute she has requested lately has far exceeded what I can afford.",
    ["Dialogue8220201"]="Ahem... Umm... As I just said, even a goddess is very busy and doesn't have the time to listen to all her followers... Umm...",
    ["Dialogue8220202"]="Hmph! Anyway, offer me <color=#CA2E0AFF>three Pure-water Sturgeons</color> first before telling me your prayer.",
    ["Dialogue8220301"]="Umm... Since you have offered me your tribute, you can now make your request.",
    ["Dialogue8220302"]="Supreme goddess, it is I, your pious subject, Helmor. For some reason, my husband, Joelson, has become delirious recently, and had even been acting mad all day like a crazy person. I, your pious subject, pray that you can restore his sanity.",
    ["Dialogue8220303"]="Well... that's not too difficult, but as I just said, um... I'm busy dealing with the endless stream of worshipers who come to pray to me. I have so many prayers to deal with that they are lined up until next year... However, if you make a sincere prayer with a jug of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Star Orchid Wine</color>, hehe... I guess I can consider giving priority to your prayers in advance.",
    ["Dialogue8220304"]="S-Star Orchid Wine? My goddess, I am just a commoner with limited money. I can't afford to buy such expensive wine...",
    ["Dialogue8220305"]="Then I can't help you. Do as you please.",
    ["Dialogue8220401"]="Adventurer, this bracelet is an heirloom that is passed down my family. I think it should be worth some money. My legs don't work as well as they used to now. Can you take this to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akarret the wine merchant in the city</color> and exchange it for a jug of Star Orchid Wine?",
    ["Dialogue8220402"]="No, the goddess and her supreme powers are undeniably real. The goddess helped me solve my problems every time I had trouble in the past. When my chicken went missing, it had returned back to its coop by the next day. When my house was haunted, everything returned to normal immediately after I prayed to the goddess. Please, Adventurer, help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>exchange it for a jug of Star Orchid Wine</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8220501"]="This bracelet looks like a precious relic that has seen many years, and it looks rather valuable. Why did you hand this to me?",
    ["Dialogue8220502"]="Oh, so you want to exchange this bracelet for Star Orchid Wine? You've come to the right person. No problem, take this Star Orchid Wine with you.",
    ["Dialogue8220601"]="Umm... Since you've brought me this fine wine, I believe in your sincerity and will handle your prayer first. Helmor, return home and wait patiently. Your husband will soon regain his sanity.",
    ["Dialogue8220602"]="Thank you! Thank you, my goddess! I can't thank you enough! Oh, and you too—thank you, young adventurer.\n(Helmor chokes with emotion as she bows to the Goddess Statue and you while holding your hand with slightly trembling hands.)",
    ["Dialogue8220701"]="(Several monster claw marks are everywhere to be found around the Goddess Statue. Some marks seem new, while some marks seem to have been around for a while...)",
    ["Dialogue8220801"]="(Upon closer observation, the area is full of new and old monster claw marks. However, they all seem to disappear at the bush in the front...)",
    ["Dialogue8220901"]="Heh! Come here! I saw everything that just happened. After my careful observation, I am sure that the voice of that so-called goddess came from the bush over there.",
    ["Dialogue8220902"]="Wait up! Don't act rashly and alert the enemy in case it backfires. I have a good idea. Look around the neighborhood and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find some Stinking Monster Waste</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8221001"]="Urgh... This stench is so foul... Okay, I'm sure that my plan will work with this...\n(Vienna Lindra pinches her nose and turns the waste you gave her into a Stink Bomb.)",
    ["Dialogue8221002"]="Alright, it's done! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Throw this Stink Bomb into the bush</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8221101"]="*Wails* Don't hit me! I was just blinded by greed! Please let me go!",
    ["Dialogue8221102"]="I... I hid in this bush by accident when I was being chased by an extremely powerful monster hunter the day before yesterday. I was seriously injured at the time and couldn't help but groan out in pain. I didn't expect that old woman think mistake that as the goddess' response.",
    ["Dialogue8221103"]="I... I didn't have any options. I was seriously injured and realized that I could get food and wine easily by pretending to be the goddess. So, I...",
    ["Dialogue8221104"]="(Majoruros' voice fades gradually as its eyes look around cowardly.)\nI just sowed some chaos at her home and waited for her to freak out and come to ask me to solve her troubles. Even the delirious state of her husband was caused by my sorcery... b-but I'll make you a promise!",
    ["Dialogue8221105"]="If you're willing to let me live, I'll cure his illness immediately and give them water and food every day as compensation. I'll never deceive them again!",
    ["Dialogue8230101"]="I went to great lengths to save up this box of oddyfruits. Do you know how precious they are? I'll make a lot of money if I sell them to a royal chef! A lot of money! Do you understand!?",
    ["Dialogue8230102"]="So, does that mean you don't have any clues? I don't care about its value. I need clues.",
    ["Dialogue8230103"]="Adventurer, you came at the right time. This lady is just too difficult to communicate with. Why don't you help me ask her what clues she has found?",
    ["Dialogue8230104"]="Are you referring to why I'm here? Master Jesqurienne asked me <color=#CA2E0AFF>to join Ygnizem's team</color> and go on an adventure with them. So, I did it since Jesqurienne asked me.",
    ["Dialogue8230105"]="Because Ygnizem's team has become more and more famous in the kingdom recently, they've received more requests accordingly. Miss Ygnizem believes they'll be able to help more people if they split up the requests they've received and complete them separately.",
    ["Dialogue8230106"]="Hey, hey! Where did you come from? How can you interrupt our conversation so casually! My goods were stolen!! Do you know how angry I am that they were stolen?!",
    ["Dialogue8230107"]="Since you butted into our conversation, you should help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the thief</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8230201"]="(Messy shoe prints are scattered everywhere around the cargo boxes. Upon closer observation, you see that an orange-red liquid is mixed with one set of shoe prints...)",
    ["Dialogue8230301"]="It seems that Dinza left most of these shoe prints herself when she moved the cargo, but the shoe prints that are mixed with the orange-red liquid seems to be a different size compared to the other shoe prints. If I remember correctly, oddyfruit juice is... orange-red!",
    ["Dialogue8230302"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>shoe prints with orange-red juice</color> should belong to the thief who stole the goods. Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow their trail</color> and take a look.",
    ["Dialogue8230401"]="(The shoe prints that are mixed with the orange-red liquid continue in the direction ahead of you. Judging from the size of the sole, the shoe prints should belong to a male adult...)",
    ["Dialogue8230501"]="(The shoe prints are deep in the mud, and the person who left these shoe prints stumbled from time to time like they found it very difficult to walk...)",
    ["Dialogue8230601"]="(The shoe prints extend all the way to a dilapidated camp in front of you before disappearing.)",
    ["Dialogue8230701"]="This should be a gathering place for the local beggars. Although the clues all point here, I can't shake the feeling that something is wrong. We'll do this. You will <color=#CA2E0AFF>return and tell Dinza about the situation first</color>. I need to stay here and confirm some things.",
    ["Dialogue8230801"]="Tell me now! Who did it? Who stole my oddyfruits?!",
    ["Dialogue8230802"]="What?! It really was those shameless beggars! I have long heard of how chaotic things are here because no one is managing things. I wouldn't come back if it weren't for the scarce goods that can only be found here! See what happened? My goods were stolen right after I arrived. Hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>arrest that wicked group of beggars</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8230901"]="(Bairde stares at the beggars on the ground sternly.)\nYou do look quite weak and don't seem to be deceiving me.",
    ["Dialogue8230902"]="We really... It's been so long since we've seen food like this...",
    ["Dialogue8230903"]="Adventurer, can you make some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Soup with Frog Legs I</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue8231001"]="(Bairde bends down and hands the food to the beggars sitting weakly on the ground.)\nEat this food first.",
    ["Dialogue8231002"]="Adventurer, did you notice anything unusual...?",
    ["Dialogue8231003"]="Yes, the goods that Dinza lost were food. The beggars wouldn't be so hungry if they really did steal her goods. Also, those footprints that appeared only go from the storage area to here, but there are none going to the cargo area.",
    ["Dialogue8231004"]="So you noticed it too. Those footprints that appeared only go from the storage area to here, but there are none going to the cargo area. From the looks of it, we can't say for certain that it was the beggars stealing goods. I also found some suspicious marks nearby. They might be an important clue. How about you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go check it out</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8231101"]="(A line of small footprints is mixed in with the adults' footprints. Judging by the size, they seem to be a child's...)",
    ["Dialogue8231201"]="Come look at these footprints. They're a lot smaller than your average adult. I think they belong to a child. Looks like something fishy is going on.",
    ["Dialogue8231202"]="Let's follow the footprints to see where they lead and investigate. I'm sure we'll find something. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Quickly, follow me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8231301"]="These monsters are so scary... Th-Thank you...",
    ["Dialogue8231302"]="So you were the ones who stole the oddyfruits Dinza lost.",
    ["Dialogue8231303"]="Look at that pair of <color=#CA2E0AFF>boots</color>.\n(Bairde calmly points at the wall. There is a pair of worn-out, adult-sized boots in the corner.)",
    ["Dialogue8231304"]="(Fred nervously clenches the corner of his own worn-out coat. He raises his head as if he's made up his mind.)\n...You're right. We did it. But we were just trying to survive. If we orphans don't think of ways to get by, we'd have already starved to death on the streets.",
    ["Dialogue8231305"]="We don't have any abilities to make a living off of, so all we can do is steal. But the folks here are already wary of us, so we could only target adventurers from other places. We also stole some grown up's shoes to pin the blame on beggars. We thought if we did that, we wouldn't get caught...",
    ["Dialogue8231306"]="(Fred's face reddens slightly.)\n...We're just so hungry. We already ate all those fruits... I'm sorry... And you guys saved us, too...",
    ["Dialogue8231307"]="Here, I'll give you this <color=#CA2E0AFF>pretty rock</color> we worked really hard to find. You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to the owner of the goods</color> as an apology from us!",
    ["Dialogue8231401"]="Do you know how much Zeny those boxes of oddyfruits cost? And you're just giving us a lousy rock!? How can this offset the cost of my oddyfruits!? ...Wait... Hold up... This rock is...?\n(Dinza suddenly stops complaining. Her eyes go wide as she starts examining the stone in her hand.)",
    ["Dialogue8231402"]="This rock is... Hahahaha! This is a Magicloud Jade! This Magicloud Jade hasn't been seen on the market in ages! This is amazing. It's priceless! Bairde, you really are something. Can't you tell? With this, I've earned so much more this trip! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue8231403"]="You really are... You get your hands on something valuable and you make a complete 180...",
    ["Dialogue8231404"]="That's not important. Seems like if I'm with great allies like you, I might be able to earn some unexpected extra income. Although adventuring and whatnot seems dangerous, no risk no reward, right? ...Hm... I've decided! Mister Bairde, how about you go back and ask your adventuring parties if they need a clever and sensible businesswoman like myself?",
    ["Dialogue8240101"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Hmph, it's definitely fake... What cure-all...?</color>\n(In the corner by the wall, a young man is muttering to himself while holding something in his hands. He looks quite odd.)",
    ["Dialogue8240102"]="Eeeeeh!?\n(The young man jumps, frightened. A paper bag flies from his hands into the air, stirring up a bunch of powder.)",
    ["Dialogue8240103"]="Th-This isn't mine...! Don't misunderstand! It belongs to a witch doctor in the city! He sold this powder to the people in Glast Heim. He said eating it would cure illnesses and heal wounds!",
    ["Dialogue8240104"]="Me? I'm Hylas. I live here, in that house over there...\n(The young man points to a dilapidated old house nearby.)",
    ["Dialogue8240105"]="So what happened is... Not long ago, a weird witch doctor came to Glast Heim. Everyone calls him <color=#CA2E0AFF>Patrick IV</color>. He calls himself the Spirit Emissary. He says he can use flames to summon spirits and dispel ill fortune. And that's not all. He also sold the ashes burned in a ritual to the people in the city, saying that it can cure all diseases and prolong one's life... Isn't it obvious he's just trying to swindle people!?",
    ["Dialogue8240106"]="Even more importantly—how can Odin's children take part in heresy!?\n(Hylas stomps and kicks up dust.)",
    ["Dialogue8240107"]="*Sighs* At the end of the day, it's all because life in Glast Heim is so hard... If it weren't for everyone going hungry, they wouldn't think Odin abandoned this barren land... Eh?\n(Hylas pauses and suddenly begins to look you up and down.)",
    ["Dialogue8240108"]="Speaking of which...<size=18>A-Aren't you that adventure who's the successor to Odin's bloodline!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8240109"]="(The eyes of this young man dressed in ragged clothes suddenly light up with hope.)\nA-Are you willing to help me expose that witch doctor for the fraud he is?",
    ["Dialogue8240110"]="Thank you so much! I knew Odin wouldn't abandon us! There's no time to waste. We have to act now!\nFrom what I know, Patrick IV should be at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bonfire on the east side of Glast Heim</color> carrying out a ritual... Trust me! This is a good chance to gather information!",
    ["Dialogue8240111"]="R-Really...? No, You're right to be cautious. You are of Odin's bloodline, after all!\nNow then, from what I know, Patrick IV should be at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bonfire on the east side of Glast Heim</color> carrying out a ritual... Trust me! This is a good chance to gather information! We don't have much time. Let's set out as soon as possible, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8240201"]="%$#*&@$%...\n(Hylas looks at the amulet and mumbles to himself before angrily throwing it on the ground and stomping on it.)\nWhat are these stupid pictures!? I can't understand them at all!",
    ["Dialogue8240202"]="Looks like we need your help, Adventurer! Someone who's good with magic should be able to figure out what this amulet is, right?",
    ["Dialogue8240203"]="Oh? There's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>spellcaster from Geffen, the City of Magic,</color> in that group of adventurers? Perfect! Then <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask him</color> to help us <color=#CA2E0AFF>appraise this</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8240301"]="(Bairde pushes his glasses up his nose and makes a thoughtful expression.)\nOh? Where did you get such a fascinating thing, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8240302"]="That Patrick IV, who's always carrying out rituals in the city? Hm... There's no doubt about it. You've been tricked.",
    ["Dialogue8240303"]="This is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>teleportation charm</color>. It's not used for summoning at all. If I had to wager a guess, Patrick IV pulled a few strings while casting and teleported some foreigners who don't speak the same language to this place, then pretended to translate their foreign language which the citizens don't understand, so as to confuse the public with strange powers.",
    ["Dialogue8240304"]="Of course, we can't have him deceiving the people like this. Let me think... Ah, here it is.\n(Bairde raises his eyebrows as he pulls a thin scrap of paper from his belongings.)\nWhile he's <color=#CA2E0AFF>carrying out the ritual</color>... <color=#CA2E0AFF>secretly throw this into the fire</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8240305"]="You'll know once you use it. Trust me... It will make him show his true colors.",
    ["Dialogue8240401"]="According to my investigation, Patrick IV may hold himself in high regard and won't readily hold a ritual for his followers... but, he has a fatal weakness!",
    ["Dialogue8240402"]="Yes! So long as we tempt him with a lot of money, he'll be sure to take the bait! However, the people here are poor and helpless, and he knows we can't possibly come up with a lot of money. Now, we only have...",
    ["Dialogue8240403"]="Then I'll head to the ceremonial bonfire and wait for you! Also, Patrick IV lives in the northeast of Glast Heim. If you see a house surrounded by followers... that's the one.",
    ["Dialogue8240501"]="Ahem...! What business do you have with me? Please, keep it brief! The Spirit Emissary is quite busy. I have only three minutes to hear your request.\n(The follower-surrounded witch doctor juts out his chin as he looks at you with a high and mighty look on his face.)",
    ["Dialogue8240502"]="You want to ask me to carry out a blessing ceremony that can relieve ill fortunes? I can, but...\n(He furrows his brow and scrutinizes your clothing.)\nPoor adventurer. You think you can afford the offerings for the divine spirit?",
    ["Dialogue8240503"]="I knew...<size=18>What!? F-F-Fi... </size><size=24>Fifty million Zeny</size>!?\n(Patrick IV's eyes open wide. He turns his back quickly, and he can't stop his shoulders from trembling.)\n<color=#A1979FFF>Yes, yes yes! I've found a fool! Hahahaha</color>!!!",
    ["Dialogue8240504"]="(Patrick IV turns back around and quickly switches to an honest expression.)\nAhem! What I mean is, the divine spirit will not forsake any follower!",
    ["Dialogue8240505"]="Since you are so devout, I can't refuse you. However, before the ceremony begins, I'll need to ask the will of the divine spirits and make some preparations. Leave for now, then come back later and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find me by the bonfire</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8240601"]="Deviant son...! You've brought shame on our family!",
    ["Dialogue8240602"]="(Patrick IV watches the figure emerging from the flames with his eyes wide open in horror.)\nYou... You...",
    ["Dialogue8240603"]="What do you mean, \"you, you\"!? You don't even recognize your own <size=24>father</size>!?\n(The floating spirit stomps his foot, causing the flames to sway.)",
    ["Dialogue8240604"]="Did you think that nobody will care about what you're doing after I kicked the bucket? I've been watching you from above, and I can clearly see what you're doing!\nTo think you dare to sully the Patrick family name with your swindling! Are you really not afraid of your ancestors waking from their graves!?",
    ["Dialogue8240605"]="Swindling!?",
    ["Dialogue8240606"]="<size=18>Swindling!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8240607"]="<size=18>Swindling!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8240608"]="zUsing an amulet to teleport people from elsewhere? Cheating others into giving you offerings? Can't you just be an honest person!?\n(The old spirit waves a hand and points to the surrounding followers, including yourself.)",
    ["Dialogue8240609"]="Didn't I teach you <size=24>not to swindle ignorant children!?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8240610"]="I didn't... I didn't!\n(Patrick IV holds his head and shakes it vehemently, hiding like an ostrich.)\nThis isn't real! It's all fake! I must be dreaming!",
    ["Dialogue8240611"]="Dreaming? I'll wake you up!\n(The strong man raises a foot and kicks Patrick IV's bottom.)",
    ["Dialogue8240612"]="Waaaaaaah! Mom, save me—!<size=24>Dad's back!</size>\n(The young witch doctor rolls around on the ground. He seems to be just waking up from a dream. He runs into the distance, wailing.)",
    ["Dialogue8240613"]="Stop! Don't you dare run—just you wait for your punishment!",
    ["Dialogue8240701"]="Hahahahahaha—!\n(Hylas folds his arms over his waist and lets out a hearty laugh.)\nI don't know what exactly happened just now, but that was great!",
    ["Dialogue8240702"]="Yeah, I think so too! It must have been the work of that talisman he gave us!\nAdventurer, let's go <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Spellcaster Bairde</color>! I'd like to thank him face-to-face.",
    ["Dialogue8240801"]="Judging by the looks on your face, it would seem you've already exposed this fraudster, yes?\n(Bairde has the look of a man with a trick up his sleeve. The glasses on the bridge of his nose gleam.)",
    ["Dialogue8240802"]="Yes! It's all thanks to your talisman!\n...Speaking of which, what exactly is that thing?",
    ["Dialogue8240803"]="Actually... It's just a normal summoning talisman. I simply pulled a few strings to make it so that the caster is guaranteed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>summon a spirit from his own family</color>.\n(Bairde shrugs his shoulders. An imperceptible smile creeps to the corner of his mouth, making him look like a Deviruchi baring its fangs.)",
    ["Dialogue8240804"]="I didn't imagine the effect would be so... explosive.\n<color=#A1979FFF>Looks like next time, I can use it to teach a lesson to... Ahem</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8240805"]="(Hylas scratches his head, seemingly not understanding what you're talking about.)\nRight... Speaking of, I haven't thanked you two. Thanks for helping me expose that fraudster's evildoings. Now, nobody will believe him anymore! As for payment, I have...",
    ["Dialogue8240806"]="...No, there's no need for compensation. It was just a talisman. That's nothing compared to the safety of Glast Heim's citizens.\n<color=#A1979FFF>Besides, you helped me test my latest talisman's effect. I'd say that's enough compensation. Yeah</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8240807"]="Eh...? You don't even want payment? Hahaha, I guess there still are good people in this world!\nThanks so much, you two!",
    ["Dialogue8240808"]="Of course! With this as a warning, I'm sure nobody will believe in these heretics going forward. After all—\n<size=24>We should all be devout children of Odin, right? Hahahaha!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8250101"]="Just what's going on lately? We keep hearing the sound of a kid crying coming from that ruin lately. It's so loud, it's driving us all crazy! If this keeps up, it's going to be hard to get a good night's sleep.",
    ["Dialogue8250102"]="Yeah, I don't know why, but recently, the sound of <color=#CA2E0AFF>a child crying</color> can often be heard coming from that abandoned <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruin</color>. But we're just normal people without power to do anything. We don't dare step foot into that desolate place. Adventurer, could we ask you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look into what's going on</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8250201"]="Adventurer, you're back so quickly! Did you find anything?",
    ["Dialogue8250202"]="Goodness! You mean the crying sound in those ruins is the ghost of a child? That's terrifying! Good thing we didn't rush in there. Looks like we'll need to ask that famous medium for help.",
    ["Dialogue8250203"]="Yeah, there's a famous medium in our city named Macy. I hear her powers are quite outstanding—no matter what supernatural problems you have, so long as Macy's there, there's nothing to worry about. Adventurer, could you help us get Master Macy to bust this ghost? Thanks.",
    ["Dialogue8250301"]="You seem to have an aura of death on you, Adventurer. Have you come to me because of an encounter with the paranormal?",
    ["Dialogue8250302"]="Oh? You mean to tell me there's a child's ghost haunting that ruin near the city? Hm... Typically, spirits remain in the world of the living because an obsession that was not resolved prior to their death is keeping them from crossing over. As long as we can <color=#CA2E0AFF>find whatever that girl is obsessing over and fulfill her final wish</color>, her spirit will naturally disappear.",
    ["Dialogue8250303"]="Hm... Now that I think of it, there's no way for you to communicate. How about this? Take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit-quelling Orchid</color> and give it a try. The scent of the Spirit-quelling Orchid can calm restless spirits down. Try using it to sooth that little girl's ghost and seeing if you can talk with her.",
    ["Dialogue8250401"]="...Who are you...? I'm still waiting for daddy. But you're not my daddy... No...",
    ["Dialogue8250402"]="Mommy died when I was born, so daddy always took care of me, but... but one day, he left and never came back. All I could do was just wait at home for him... But there was nothing to eat at home...",
    ["Dialogue8250403"]="(The little girl turns and points <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep within the ruins</color>.)\nThis is my home...",
    ["Dialogue8250501"]="(An old, dust-covered bell has fallen into the rubble. Upon closer examination, you see a line of text carved into the bell—\n\"To my darling Rey. Love, your father\")",
    ["Dialogue8250601"]="You're back! So, did you take care of the ghost in the ruins? I'm sure Master Macy helped you come up with the perfect solution!",
    ["Dialogue8250602"]="When you put it like that, I feel pretty bad for both the little girl's ghost and her father. But at least now there's a perfect ending, and we can keep living in peace. Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue8260101"]="Oh no, I'm done for... How could I lose it...?",
    ["Dialogue8260102"]="I lost a very valuable <color=#CA2E0AFF>jewelry box</color>. It's worth a fortune...",
    ["Dialogue8260103"]="Eh... I lost it when I went to the underground churchyard. Who would've thought...",
    ["Dialogue8260104"]="You probably don't know much about Glast Heim's underground churchyard. This is the resting place of the precious burial jewelry of the most prosperous period of the former Schmidt Empire. Since the city is deserted and neglected, there's no need to hand any treasure unearthed from the tombs here over to the kingdom. Because of this, many jewelry merchants come here every year to try their luck...",
    ["Dialogue8260105"]="I was planning to dig in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest corner</color> of the churchyard this time. But who would've thought we'd be attacked by monsters while digging! My friends were all killed in the attack. Only I managed to escape.",
    ["Dialogue8260106"]="But I lost an incredibly valuable jewelry box. My friends gave their lives for that thing...! But now, I don't even have the courage to go back and face their corpses... Adventurer, you look quite extraordinary. Could you go to the underground churchyard and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find that jewelry box I lost</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue8260201"]="(There's nothing in the merchant's pockets. Upon closer inspection, you see cuts from a dagger on his coat...)",
    ["Dialogue8260301"]="(There's nothing in the merchant's pockets. You carefully examine his remains and don't see any scratches from a monster on him...)",
    ["Dialogue8260401"]="(There's nothing in the merchant's pockets, but there is a broken arrow lodged in his chest...)",
    ["Dialogue8260501"]="Ow... Save me... It hurts... Am I about to die...?",
    ["Dialogue8260601"]="Thank you so much. If it weren't for you, even if I didn't die at those robbers' hands, I wouldn't have been able to escape these monsters.",
    ["Dialogue8260602"]="We're just a group of jewelry merchants. A bunch of robbers ambushed us while we were digging in the churchyard. <color=#CA2E0AFF>My friends were all brutally murdered</color>. Only I... I took advantage of the confusion and hid. That's how I managed to survive.",
    ["Dialogue8260603"]="What!? That's all lies. This jewelry box I'm holding is valuable indeed, but I risked my life to hold it and keep it from being taken by those thieves scouring the place! That guy must be lying to you! Take me to see this Byreon so I can confront him face to face!",
    ["Dialogue8260701"]="How did it go? Did you find anything in the churchyard? Did you find my jewelry box?",
    ["Dialogue8260702"]="Huh...? No... Who did you hear that from? We were just attacked by monsters. What do you mean, thieves? That didn't happen...",
    ["Dialogue8260703"]="You're lying! You're no jewelry merchant! It was you! You're the one who killed my friends! You horrific thief! Adventurer, this is the guy who robbed us and murdered my friends!",
    ["Dialogue8260704"]="You—!? Hmph... Seems a fish slipped through the net...",
    ["Dialogue8260801"]="(The formerly friendly-looking Byreon has suddenly changed into someone else entirely. There's a fierce gleam in his eyes, and his expression has become cunning and cruel.)\nSince you guys figured it out, yeah, we robbed you lot of unlucky merchants. What are you looking at me like that for? We risked our lives too, you know!",
    ["Dialogue8260802"]="I was hoping to use this naive adventurer to retrieve the last jewelry box, but... Forget it. Take it as blood money. May we never meet again.",
    ["Dialogue8260901"]="Thanks to you, I didn't let my late friends down in the end. I protected the jewelry box, and I avenged them. Thank you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8270101"]="Honestly, no..... Honestly no..... We have to go by ourselves?",
    ["Dialogue8270102"]="But Captain, we don't have permission to enter the bell tower?",
    ["Dialogue8270103"]="If I say so... Just sneak in! Whether he has authority or not!",
    ["Dialogue8270104"]="Who?!\n(the frightened gunner pulls out the gun without hesitation. The dark muzzle shakes in front of you, and you quickly raise your hands)",
    ["Dialogue8270105"]="..... Adventurer? What are you doing here?\n(after he recognizes that it is you, Officer Gerner puts away his gun)",
    ["Dialogue8270106"]="..... yes. Now that you've heard about it, I’m not going to keep covering it up. In fact, a few days ago, we sent a team member in to the clock tower to investigate, but it is strange that he has not returned yet. The tracking device he carried stopped working yesterday in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of the clock tower 2F</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8270107"]="This situation is too strange to gloss over. We are going to have to make the difficult decision and sneak into the clock tower....",
    ["Dialogue8270108"]="You mean... Would you like to enter the bell tower for us to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing player</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8270109"]="... thank you very much, Adventurer.\nOur team member is Joyce. If you find him, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring him back safely</color> as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue8270201"]="(after careful observation, bloody footprints are distributed messily on the ground nearby, and bullet holes sprayed all over the guardrail and wall. It seems as though there had been a fierce battle.....)",
    ["Dialogue8270301"]="(a transceiver fell to the ground, and the signal light above the display screen flickered faintly...)",
    ["Dialogue8270401"]="Don't move, Adventurer. Otherwise, I might be forced to shoot.\n(the young man in the guard uniform raises his gun and confronts you)",
    ["Dialogue8270402"]=".....Who are you?",
    ["Dialogue8270403"]="You said..... Did officer Gerner ask you to come for me?\n(the young man looks at you up and down, and then puts away his gun)\nSorry, how rude of me... I'm Joyce.",
    ["Dialogue8270404"]="No... Adventurer, before I return, there is one more important thing that I must finish.\nEarlier, when I was investigating <color=#CA2E0AFF>this floor</color>, I was attacked by Monsters. Not only was I injured, but I lost my transceiver and an investigation record. I have remained here to try and retrieve them....",
    ["Dialogue8270405"]="But luckily you're here now. I hope you can help me first <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> those <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigation records</color>, otherwise... I will go home empty handed.",
    ["Dialogue8270501"]="(Joyce’s face flashes with joy, as he confirms the document you brought back)\n... thanks, Adventurer, that's exactly what I'm looking for.",
    ["Dialogue8270502"]="You...... Peeked at my investigation records?",
    ["Dialogue8270503"]="... Oh, would you please not poke your nose into my business. Now that we have the important documents in hand, we should go back and give them to officer Gerner as soon as possible, shouldn't we?\n(after that, Joyce turns with the document and runs quickly to the exit of the bell tower without looking back)",
    ["Dialogue8270601"]="(a man in a Republic guard uniform fell to the ground with no signs of life. Careful observation shows that he seems to be holding something in his pocket...)",
    ["Dialogue8270701"]="(officer Gerner holds the certificate you brought back, and his voice trembles)\nJoyce... Has Joyce?",
    ["Dialogue8270702"]="... two guards? It's impossible!\nFrom the very beginning, we only sent Joyce to sneak into the bell tower to have a look around! You were obviously cheated by that man! Now we are going to have to steal back Joyce's investigation report! I'm afraid to say that...... it’s normally only the lackeys of Rekenber Company who get up to this despicable business.",
    ["Dialogue8270703"]="In fact, we have always doubted the original intention of Rekenber Company’s investment in the construction of the clock tower. Every time we sent an application to investigate the clock tower to Rekenber Company, it was rejected due to infringing on their private property. That's why we finally made the terrible decision to let Joyce sneak in alone after pretending to try to find some clues, but I never expected it to end up in such a mess.....",
    ["Dialogue8270704"]="... captain! If they were not guilty of being thieves, why would they murder witnesses?! That clock tower... There must be evidence of their evil deeds hidden in there somewhere! We can't let them get away with this!",
    ["Dialogue8270705"]="Calm down, Pierson... I know you and Joyce are close friends. He is not only your best friend, but also one of my most capable subordinates. But it is precisely because of this that if we act rashly... His sacrifice will seem worth it.",
    ["Dialogue8270706"]="(Gerner patted Pierson on the shoulder, looking sad but firm)\nBelieve me... As long as the time is ripe, I will make them pay the price they deserve.",
    ["Dialogue8270707"]="... no, Adventurer. I'm very grateful for you. At least you retrieved Joyce's relics for us, which makes me more convinced... Rekenber Company's plot is not simple. For Al De Baran, and for countless soldiers who died like Joyce... I swear that one day, I will expose all their plots.",
    ["Dialogue8280101"]="Alas\n<color=#A1979FFF>Even the greatest artists can't avoid creative block</color>",
    ["Dialogue8280102"]="Oh? Are you an Adventurer? Are you interested in listening to my poetry?",
    ["Dialogue8280103"]="(Morts shakes the lute and starts singing)\nThe Devil King's claws appear from the depths, tearing the earth and cutting the sky♪",
    ["Dialogue8280104"]="The goddess’s pure white feathers are covered by darkness, the blade snaps and falls into oblivion♪",
    ["Dialogue8280105"]="Bones of the dead float lifelessly down the river, a once rich earth’s surface is scorched♪",
    ["Dialogue8280106"]="Until a hero appears, he awakens the hope of the sleeping.....\n(Morts chanting stops here)",
    ["Dialogue8280107"]="Unfortunately, Adventurer. My creativity becomes stuck here, there is no historical record of what kind of person the hero is!\nAs a great bard, I cannot bear when my poetry sounds like a common fireside folktail, which uses shoddy rhetoric to describe the good deeds of the protagonist. I need some more detailed materials to add inspiration to my creation!",
    ["Dialogue8280108"]="Living in a small village west of Morroc, there are two brothers named Welden and Walden. Their ancestors were survivors of the war. To help me finish my poetry, can you go there and find out their story for me? Please go to them and ask them about their ancestors heroic deeds throughout the war.",
    ["Dialogue8280201"]="... Wah! Help the Bard finish his epic tale?\nWell! Then you have come to the right place! Our ancestors personally experienced the war! This history has also been regarded as a treasure by our family and has been passed down from generation to generation.",
    ["Dialogue8280202"]="Well.... you say that you would like to know what the hero looks like? As far as I know, he was a beautiful specimin of a man, which words cannot do justice in describing him... Oh! Yes! If you go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of the monster chicken</color>, I'll give you a detailed description when you bring the photos back!",
    ["Dialogue8280301"]="Like this delicate <color=#CA2E0AFF>pink</color> feather, the hero’s hair was as subtly and beautifully colored like a lady’s blush.",
    ["Dialogue8280302"]="No! That's not right! Grandfather clearly said that the hero's hair was as dark as the night sky. It should be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious dark blue</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8280303"]="(Welden reaches forward and angrily yanks his brother's beard)\nGrandpa also said that he saw a pink Poring! It is nonsense! He was so blind he could hardly see a person from two meters away! You might as well believe that it is going to snow in the desert tomorrow!",
    ["Dialogue8280304"]="All right, Adventurer, whats next! What else do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue8280305"]="Hmm... the hero's weapon? Of course it's gorgeous and exquisite... No, no! The elegance of heroic weapons cannot be described by such flimsy words! Adventurer, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring me back the Pharaoh's staff</color>! With this, I will be a fountain of creativity!",
    ["Dialogue8280401"]="Magnificent and dazzling brilliance... As far as I know, the weapon used by the hero is slightly shorter than this <color=#CA2E0AFF>staff</color>. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>stars and moon decoration</color> on the head of the staff would glow and guide the hero through the darkest of times!",
    ["Dialogue8280402"]="Incorrect! Grandfather clearly said that the hero’s weapon was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pitch Black Greatsword</color> that was so dark, it could blend into the night!",
    ["Dialogue8280403"]="(Welden reaches forward again and angrily yanks his brother's beard)\nThat's because grandpa was a butcher his entire life! He always carries slaughter on him himself. He is obviously fantasizing that our hero uses the same weapon!",
    ["Dialogue8280404"]="All right, Adventurer, whats next! What else do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue8280501"]="... Oh, oh! Finally, my favourite moment!\nIt's time to open up my long cherished <color=#CA2E0AFF>heroic biography</color>, Adventurer! Come on, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take it out</color>, let's read together!",
    ["Dialogue8280502"]="Incorrect! Grandfather clearly said that the hero’s weapon was a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pitch Black Greatsword</color> that was so dark, it could blend into the night!",
    ["Dialogue8280503"]="(Welden reaches forward again and angrily yanks his brother's beard)\nThat's because grandpa was a butcher his entire life! He always carries slaughter on him himself. He is obviously fantasizing that our hero uses the same weapon!",
    ["Dialogue8280504"]="All right, Adventurer, whats next! What else do you want to know?",
    ["Dialogue8280601"]="\"... the hero is not afraid of the monster before him. The brilliance of the magic wand shines with the stars and the moon. In the dazzling light, the back looks just like a singing and dancing goddess- <color=#CA2E0AFF>representing love and peace! Destroy you!</color>\"",
    ["Dialogue8280602"]="<size=24>——No!</size><size=26>That's not right at all!</size>\nThis is not a Heroic Biography! That’s the story of the <Desert Woman Warrior: Star Moon Rabbit>!",
    ["Dialogue8280603"]="Grandfather once said, that the hero who defeated Morroc was very arrogant and he didn’t talk much. He would not say anything even in the most fiercest battles! But his golden pupils would burn with fighting spirit, nothing could escape from him!",
    ["Dialogue8280604"]="(Welden reaches forward again and angrily yanks his brother's beard)\nYou're talking crap... Absolute crap! Nonsense!",
    ["Dialogue8280605"]="Adventurer, I tell you that everything is true and historically accurate! You must <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell the Bard the truth</color> and let him create the greatest and magnificent poem!",
    ["Dialogue8280701"]="Oh, it seems that you have collected a lot of useful information, Adventurer. Don't worry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell me slowly</color>. I'll incorporate it into my poetry.\n... cough, hum ~! Well, let's start with the hero’s appearance——\n(Morts raises his lute and begins to sing)",
    ["Dialogue8280702"]="The hero appeared and he awakened the sleeping hope♪",
    ["Dialogue8280703"]="For example... Well, what does the hero look like?",
    ["Dialogue8280704"]="Hair as beautiful as a girl's Blush, evoking a touch of unknown emotion ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280705"]="Like the deep night sky, his beautiful hair is shining with the dawn of light ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280706"]="He's holding... Well, what weapon does the hero use?",
    ["Dialogue8280707"]="Wielding the star moon staff in his hand, he captures the deer in the demon king's heart ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280708"]="The light returns to the earth with a deep black greatsword",
    ["Dialogue8280709"]="The demon king is forced into a corner and surrounded - well... What is the hero like <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the final battle</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8280710"]="Heroes sing the songs of their lands, filled with love and peace ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280711"]="Even in silence triumph is a happy sound, and the hero's sword walks with glory♪",
    ["Dialogue8280712"]="People watched him leave, and the great legend opened a new chapter♪",
    ["Dialogue8280713"]="... done!\nEh, eh, but there seems to be something wrong... Forget it... Just don't delay the draft!\nThank you very much for your help, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8280801"]="\"... the hero is not afraid of the monster before him. The brilliance of the magic wand shines with the stars and the moon. In the dazzling light, the back looks just like a singing and dancing goddess- <color=#CA2E0AFF>representing love and peace! Destroy you!</color>\"",
    ["Dialogue8280802"]="<size=24>——No!</size><size=26>That's not right at all!</size>\nThis is not a Heroic Biography! That’s the story of the <Desert Woman Warrior: Star Moon Rabbit>!",
    ["Dialogue8280803"]="Grandfather once said, that the hero who defeated Morroc was very arrogant and he didn’t talk much. He would not say anything even in the most fiercest battles! But his golden pupils would burn with fighting spirit, nothing could escape from him!",
    ["Dialogue8280804"]="(Welden reaches forward again and angrily yanks his brother's beard)\nYou're talking crap... Absolute crap! Nonsense!",
    ["Dialogue8280805"]="Adventurer, I tell you that everything is true and historically accurate! You must <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell the Bard the truth</color> and let him create the greatest and magnificent poem!",
    ["Dialogue8280901"]="Oh, it seems that you have collected a lot of useful information, Adventurer. Don't worry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell me slowly</color>. I'll incorporate it into my poetry.\n... cough, hum ~! Well, let's start with the hero’s appearance——\n(Morts raises his lute and begins to sing)",
    ["Dialogue8280902"]="The hero appeared and he awakened the sleeping hope♪",
    ["Dialogue8280903"]="For example... Well, what does the hero look like?",
    ["Dialogue8280904"]="Hair as beautiful as a girl's Blush, evoking a touch of unknown emotion ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280905"]="Like the deep night sky, his beautiful hair is shining with the dawn of light ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280906"]="He's holding... Well, what weapon does the hero use?",
    ["Dialogue8280907"]="Wielding the star moon staff in his hand, he captures the deer in the demon king's heart ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280908"]="The light returns to the earth with a deep black greatsword",
    ["Dialogue8280909"]="The demon king is forced into a corner and surrounded - well... What is the hero like <color=#CA2E0AFF>in the final battle</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8280910"]="Heroes sing the songs of their lands, filled with love and peace ♪",
    ["Dialogue8280911"]="Even in silence triumph is a happy sound, and the hero's sword walks with glory♪",
    ["Dialogue8280912"]="The people’s gaze watched him leave, as the legend started a new chapter.....♪",
    ["Dialogue8280913"]="... done!\nEh, eh, but there seems to be something wrong... Forget it... Just don't delay the draft!\nThank you very much for your help, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8281001"]="(a thick book. But its cover is too nice to be a historical biography...)",
    ["Dialogue8290101"]="Ahhhh<size=24> - I don't understand! </size><size=26>What exactly does Xiuling like about him?!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8290102"]="You're just in time, Adventurer! Come and help me decide!\n... you know what? Recently, Xiuling found a new boyfriend... No, this is not the point, the point is - that man, if you can call him a man at all, <软蛋！>doesn't deserve Xiuling at all!",
    ["Dialogue8290103"]="As a close friend, I must find a way to let Xiuling see the man's true colors... Adventurer! You must help me!",
    ["Dialogue8290104"]="You’re a big guy... No, no, you really are strong! Especially suitable for playing a predatory villain capable of stealing! If you steal something from them while they are out together walking, that soft guy will be scared to death! In this way... Hey, can Xiuling realize how unreliable he is~\n(Taylin cackles to herself like a little devil)",
    ["Dialogue8290105"]="But... your temperament doesn’t quite fit with someone who is trying to play a villain... We may have to fix it up a bit.\n(Taylin walks in a circle around you and and slaps you in the back of the head)\nCome with me, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8290201"]="Adventurer, let me introduce you - this is Tania, the most famous costume designer in all of Al De Baran! She is willing to lend us a costume of \"terminator tide\", which is said to be an evil pirate in a famous play! It's perfect for you, isn't it? It's just that you may have to do a couple of favors for it...heheh~",
    ["Dialogue8290202"]="(Tania pushes the glasses up the bridge of her nose, and a shrewd edge twinkles in her eyes)\nThe costume you wanted to borrow suffered a little accident in the last performance, and its wings were damaged. If you can help me collect some Bat wing of brilight, I can repair it completely and lend it to you.",
    ["Dialogue8290301"]="Oh? Worthy of being an adventurer, he moves very quickly. In this way, I can repair the wings of this costume. Please wait a moment.",
    ["Dialogue8290302"]="Hmmm ~ this is the perfect first step! So, Adventurer, just wait here until the costume is repaired. I'll go to the martial arts guide to arrange the next training for you!",
    ["Dialogue8290401"]="Now, you need to receive combat training from the theater troupe! Although you are quite experienced in actual combat, we need to be able to scare the layman's fancy fists and embroidered legs more than actual combat skills!",
    ["Dialogue8290402"]="Oh ho ~ don't worry, darling ~ I'll be gentle teaching you ~\n(the buff martial arts instructor clapped his hands, and several members of the troupe instantly surrounded him)",
    ["Dialogue8290403"]="Here ~ have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bout</color> with my own disciples ~ you will better understand the true meaning of a stage performance ~",
    ["Dialogue8290501"]="Ahhhh ~ too perfect, darling ~ your style is more beautiful than the strongest member in my whole troupe!",
    ["Dialogue8290502"]="That's right, that's right. In this way, your moves can be fluid and fierce without damaging the fragile little fellow.\n<color=#A1979FFF>If by any chance he is injured, Xiuling will not be very happy... Hmmm.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8290503"]="Well then, it's time for us to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Klaus</color> for the final lesson! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow me</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8290601"]="Finally, I must introduce you to our exclusive writer of the troupe, the magnificent Klaus! I hope you can learn some skills from him... how to be a manipulative and fierce communicator!\n<color=#A1979FFF>If we can frighten that fragile fellow before the battle even began, that would be half the effort for twice the result! Haha~</color>",
    ["Dialogue8290602"]="Well......I must confess! <size=26>You do have a taste!!! </size>All these books are my masterpieces, each is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>peerless work</color>! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go ahead! Read as you please</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8290701"]="Ahhh......Let me see......\n(Taylin walked around you and talking to herself)\n……Great! Now you are a rascal through and through!",
    ["Dialogue8290702"]="Adventurer, time<color=#CA2E0AFF>to arm yourself</color>!<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow my lead</color>, the show is on!",
    ["Dialogue8290801"]="As far as I know, Xiu Ling and her little boyfriend take a walk here everyday. We just take cover here, <color=#CA2E0AFF>when time is up</color>......you just make the move! Remember, <color=#CA2E0AFF>move on my mark<color=#CA2E0AFF>!",
    ["Dialogue8290901"]="Who......are......you?\n(Although your weird outfit startled him, the man still shield Xiu Ling behind himself)",
    ["Dialogue8290902"]="Huh? What do you want?!\nXiu……Xiu Ling, fear not! I will protect you!",
    ["Dialogue8290903"]="Ro......<size=26>Robbery?!</size>\nSomebody! Help! Robber!\n(The man is frightened to the core but still shield Xiu Ling)",
    ["Dialogue8290904"]="<size=18><color=#CA2E0AFF>Beat him</color>! Adventurer!</size>\n(Taylin hide in the shadow of the store signboard, made a gesture to her neck)",
    ["Dialogue8291001"]="Stop<size=26>……Stop!</size>\n(Xiu Ling move on to protect Pergamon lay unconscious)\nYou can have all the money! <size=26>Stop!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8291002"]="……&*%￥……\n(Taylin raised a fist to you. You have no choice but take up the weapon)",
    ["Dialogue8291003"]="What……do you want?\n(Xiu Ling looked at you and to herself, then her eyes widen)\nAre you……?!",
    ["Dialogue8291004"]="……&*%￥……\n(Taylin send several signals, but you are clueless. Guess you are on your own now.)",
    ["Dialogue8291005"]="???!!!\n(Xiu Ling is obviously terrified and Taylin covered her face in great pain. Seems everything gone wrong. And Pergamon slowly regain consciousness.)",
    ["Dialogue8291006"]="You shall……not……hurt Xiu Ling……\n(He get on his feet with great effort and hold Xiu Ling fragile frame into his arms)\nI have……you now……",
    ["Dialogue8291007"]="Well, with what?",
    ["Dialogue8291101"]="Look at yourself! You are weak and no nothing about fight! How will you protect her if there is danger?\n(After mocked Pergamon, Taylin turns to her best friend, intend to give Xiu Ling a good lesson)\nXiu Ling, now you should understand me<size=26>—Xiu Ling??</size>",
    ["Dialogue8291102"]="<size=26>My love, how should I live on without you?</size>\n(Liu Xiu is in tears and clearly moved by Pergamon’s action)\nI didn’t expect……you could do this for me……",
    ["Dialogue8291103"]="Xiu……Xiu Ling……It is my fault to put you in danger……I’m so powerless……But I will be stronger! And one day, I will be a worthy man to you!",
    ["Dialogue8291104"]="My Love!\n(Xiu Ling staring at Pergamon with deep love)",
    ["Dialogue8291105"]="My Love!\n( Pergamon staring at Xiu Ling with deep love)",
    ["Dialogue8291106"]="(Hand to the chest)\nYou……You……",
    ["Dialogue8291107"]="I won’t give up! <size=24>To marry Xiu Ling,</size><size=26> you have a long way to go!!</size>\n(Taylin’s hollowing echo with the dusk of Al De Baran)",
    ["Dialogue8300101"]="1……2……3……4……I lost count……\n(Macpennie wobbling her head, make the count with fingers)",
    ["Dialogue8300102"]="Ah, here is the Adventurer!\nMacpennie is counting how many times grandpa warrior challenged the Sky Petite! But There were so many times, Macpennie can’t keep it up with fingers! What should I do?",
    ["Dialogue8300103"]="Grandpa warrior……It is the grandpa warrior?\n(Macpennie tilted her head, failed to grasped the idea.)",
    ["Dialogue8300104"]="My father called him “the old man Tolkien”, but Macpennie think grandpa warrior better!",
    ["Dialogue8300105"]="Because the grandpa warrior is super brave! He challenges the Sky Petite every day!\n(Macpennie raised her chubby finger and pointed at <color=#CA2E0AFF>the south side of Mjolnir Mountains</color>)\nAlthough he always ended up black and blue, and everyone laughed at him……",
    ["Dialogue8300106"]="But he never gives up! Macpennie believe……well?\n<color=#A1979FFF>If the Adventurer help him……then the grandpa warrior will realize his dream!</color>\nI’m so smart!\n(The little girl talking to herself and jumping around with joy.)",
    ["Dialogue8300107"]="Oh, Great Adventurer, can you <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the grandpa warrior</color>? Macpennie heard he’s not well today and very worried! What if……well! If you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>hunt few the Sky Petites</color>, the grandpa warrior must be more than happier! Maybe even made full health!",
    ["Dialogue8300201"]="AAAAAAAA—My waist!",
    ["Dialogue8300202"]="Don’t mind me! It’s an old problem, I will come around! But you…… I never saw an Adventurer strong like you!\n(The old man grabs on your arm and rather excited.)\nCan you help me hunt some the Sky Petites?",
    ["Dialogue8300203"]="Leave it, such minor wounds will heal soon enough!",
    ["Dialogue8300204"]="Mac……Macpennie? She sends you for me……? Alas……only that girl cares a old man like me……\n(The old man struck the ground with wooden crane twice, and sat on the rock by the roadside.)",
    ["Dialogue8300205"]="Fine, I’m a man of my word. I will stay here and <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait for you</color>. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clotting Grass </color>around here will help me address the wounds. But……you must promise me! You will help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>hunt the Sky Petites</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8300301"]="Enough……The pain is gone!\nNow, Adventurer, will you help me hunt the Sky Petites?",
    ["Dialogue8300302"]="I……I have my own reason!\n<color=#A1979FFF>If I can find that today……</color>\n(He grabs on your arm, you can hardly refuse him.)",
    ["Dialogue8300303"]="(Tolkien seems to argue but only twitch the beard under your gaze.)\nFine! Fine! I will stand aside and watch you fight! You happy now!",
    ["Dialogue8300401"]="S……Stop! I see it!\nRight there! That <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruby</color>! Help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>get the ruby</color>! Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8300501"]="<color=#A1979FFF>Finally……I have you now……Lizz</color>\n(Tolkien rubs the ruby in hand and rather excited, you can see his eyes turn red.)",
    ["Dialogue8300502"]="Come with me, Adventurer, I need you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>see some one</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8300601"]="Lizz......Lizz\n(You see an old lady in tidy dressing standing in front of a house. Tolkien couldn’t help himself, but raise the crane and shout.)",
    ["Dialogue8300602"]="This is my wife! Hurry, Adventurer, give<color=#CA2E0AFF> her the ruby</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8300701"]="……\n(Surprisingly, the old lady with the ruby in possession still show no emotion.)",
    ["Dialogue8300702"]="Lizz……Look at me……Now, we can finally put the Dragon's Eye Stone on our wedding ring……\n(Tolkien hold Lizz’s hand, let her hold the stone tight.)",
    ["Dialogue8300703"]="Lizz and I......used to live in a village by the Mjolnir Mountain. We were not rich but live a content live......3 years ago, Lizz had a brain cancer and doctor said she had no more than 6 months. I couldn’t just give up, so I sold everything and brought her to the Republic where science is much developed. I thought we can find the cure, but......",
    ["Dialogue8300704"]="The doctor said the only solution is to install a machine brain, and Lizz will lost all memory and emotions as a human...... But we decided to give it a try. And she turned into what it is now.....",
    ["Dialogue8300705"]="......This is the promise I made for Lizz. On our wedding day, I told her that petty ring will have the most expensive diamond ever installed......\n(The old man rubs the wedding ring on his wife’s ring finger, drown in the mix of nostalgia and regret.)\nWhat if Lizz remembers all the memory if I keep my promise……",
    ["Dialogue8300706"]="Whatever that lay ahead of me……I kept my part of the promise. Thank you, Adventurer.\n(Tolkien seems finished the story. He remains silence and lower his head, hug the old lady. All he missed is a tiny spark in Lizz’s eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue8310101"]="Alright, children, stay calm. I had Ivy to investigate the Clock Tower and I believe the truth will be available soon. Before that happens, you just wait here.",
    ["Dialogue8310102"]="Really? If it is Mr. Ivy......then there is nothing to worry about.",
    ["Dialogue8310103"]="I trust the power of Ivy, but……I fear……\n(Nicolas lower his head and start think. Then, he finds you among the crowd.)",
    ["Dialogue8310104"]="……Adventurer? If you can help us……then it would be the best.\nActually, we are experiencing an anomaly for a few days now.",
    ["Dialogue8310105"]="As an annual tradition, Juno University will send a batch of top students to the Guild for internship. One of their training courses is to enter the bell tower and collect a key material for alchemy known as Lunar Dew. However, many students lost contact after entering the Clock Tower. This is rather strange......",
    ["Dialogue8310106"]="I’ve send Ivy to look into it But......as you may aware, even Ivy was the ace among his folks, he remain a student. It is better to have the Adventurer with combat experience to help him.",
    ["Dialogue8310107"]="Thanks. I think Ivy and other students are in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northern side of underground first floor of the Clock Tower</color>, because Luna Dew can only be found in that zone. Adventurer, hope you can bring good news.",
    ["Dialogue8310201"]="<color=#A1979FFF>……Alas</color>\n(A young man hiding in the shadow casted by the rock nearby and amused by observing the commotion in the cave. Judging by the facial features resemble to Nicolas, you have a few ideas.)\n",
    ["Dialogue8310202"]="Hush—\n(The young man lowered his voice and you can faintly tell how excited now)\nWe will talk later. I’m having fun.",
    ["Dialogue8310301"]="Well......This is interesting. Don’t you think?",
    ["Dialogue8310302"]="(The young man waves his hand before you explain yourself.)\nI know, my father sends you……to assist me, right?\n<color=#A1979FFF>Ahhhh……He worried too much……</color>",
    ["Dialogue8310303"]="So....... Adventure, you’ve watched the show, do you have the answer now?\n(Judging by his facial expression, you can’t sure if he is test your strength.)",
    ["Dialogue8310304"]="... Correct. Just like you said, the vanishing of those students is the handy work of that Zealotus. These monsters feed on young males, using illusion to control the prey. Once reach the witch territory, victims will be encaged for later consumption until their life force gets completely drained...",
    ["Dialogue8310305"]="(Ivy crunch down and pick up a blooming Luna Dew)\nAnd this flower field……must be the trap to lure students in. As for those enter the Clock Tower earlier……They must be inside the witch’s cave and reduced to <color=#CA2E0AFF>dry bones</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8310306"]="Indeed......If we want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>save him</color>, now is the time, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8310401"]="Mr......Mr. Ivy?!\n(The student stand between you and the witch.)\nDon’t hurt her! We……we love each other!",
    ["Dialogue8310402"]="……Love? Haha.\n(Ivy snorted and the sarcasm is plain to see. His index finger landed heavily on the student’s chest.)\nAriel, what kind of love is this? That is the witch’s spell!",
    ["Dialogue8310403"]="No……You are wrong! I’m awake! <size=26>I love her!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8310404"]="So... Does she love you?\n(Ivy turns to look at the silent Zealotus.)\nWhy don't you ask your loved one, will she love her food?",
    ["Dialogue8310405"]="……\n(She fall silent in face of Ivy’s question.)",
    ["Dialogue8310406"]="My dear?",
    ["Dialogue8310407"]="Or you can let her make a vow in the name of love, <size=26>claim herself never cast illusion spell on those miss vanished students?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8310408"]="……\n(The witch remains silent. And you can see despair in the Ariel’s eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue8310409"]="You……Are you lying all along?\n(He moves backward and seems all too sad.)\nAll that between us……are not real?",
    ["Dialogue8310410"]="No......I’m not......I......!\n<color=#A1979FFF>I……I love you……</color>",
    ["Dialogue8310411"]="……Wake up, Ariel. Stop being a puppet.",
    ["Dialogue8310412"]="(Ivy whispers to the Ariel and you believe Ivy is the being that more close to a monster that bewitch common folks.)\nIs it worthy to waste your grand future for this sort of love? My father told me that he has high hope of you and want you work in the guild after graduation.",
    ["Dialogue8310413"]="……Well, I will go back.\n(Ariel turn to look at the witch with complicated expression on his face.)\nMr. Ivy, can you……not……just",
    ["Dialogue8310414"]="Fine, I know. Just go back, everyone is waiting. I <color=#CA2E0AFF>won’t kill her</color>.\n<color=#A1979FFF>……Of course, not before you leave.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8310501"]="Well, Adventure……We are done here.\n(Ivy licks the lips, and stretch out as if warming up himself.)",
    ["Dialogue8310502"]="……Remains? Haha.\n(Ivy laughs out loud on hearing your words.)\nAdventurer, you are so dumb cute.",
    ["Dialogue8310503"]="Enter the cave and you will understand. If my guess is right……there is only a bunch of half-wits <color=#CA2E0AFF>sleeping for few days</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8310601"]="Those half-wits…… must be having a good time with that witch?\n(Ivy looks at you with head tilts sideway, and his innocent smile makes you chill to the bones.)",
    ["Dialogue8310602"]="What do you mean? They are still alive or there is no illusion spell for Ariel?\n(Ivy stares at you with smile on his face.)\nI know it all. Since I’m the best.",
    ["Dialogue8310603"]="To solve the problem... the easiest way is always the best. Ariel will never go back unless he believes this love is unreal. Besides, if I can't let you know the Zealotus was behind all this, how can I get your wholehearted support?",
    ["Dialogue8310604"]="So, it is become all too easy. Just blame the witch.\n(He looks up to meet your gaze and show you another innocent smile. But you find a child creep up along your spine.) \nBesides, those monsters are total evil. Am I right, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8310701"]="（The soil between the stone plates is clearly been tempered, and some broken roots are barely visible......)",
    ["Dialogue8310801"]="(A trail of monster’s small foot prints dotted with soil extend ahead. By taking a close look, several dry stern and flower buds are visible......)",
    ["Dialogue8310901"]="(Students sleeping on the ground with their eyes closed and no visible wounds.)",
    ["Dialogue8320101"]="You were born in fire and shall return to fire... Scram, scram!",
    ["Dialogue8320102"]="(Grantham's eyes snap open as if waking from a nightmare, his beard drenching in cold sweat.) \nIt's you, Adventurer...",
    ["Dialogue8320103"]="A <color=#CA2E0AFF>very powerful force</color> is hovering above <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color>, calling for its master. It's very lethal, yet very tantalizing... Shhh, did you hear that?",
    ["Dialogue8320104"]="No, I cannot say... The Hermit must restrain his voyeurism. If you are curious, Adventurer, go to the marsh and find the source. Perhaps, it's waiting for you...",
    ["Dialogue8320201"]="Phew, those Alligators wanting to tear us apart were terrifying.",
    ["Dialogue8320202"]="(The stranger pats his chest and shudders.) \nI'm okay, but the Alligators hurt my friend and there's no healer nearby. What to do...?",
    ["Dialogue8320203"]="I'm counting on you, then, helpful Adventurer! Please come back as soon as possible. The Obeaune is very important to me...",
    ["Dialogue8320204"]="Thank you, master...",
    ["Dialogue8320205"]="Don't mention it! We've traveled this far together. I'm not going to abandon you!",
    ["Dialogue8320206"]="(The Obeaune weakly puts a hand on your wrist as if wanting to say something.) \nCan't... can't delay... master's precious...",
    ["Dialogue8320207"]="(The stranger averts your inquisitive gaze and remains concerned about his companion on the ground.) \nPardon me but I can't tell you too much. We are delivering a precious item of great significance that must reach the capital of Comodo <color=#CA2E0AFF>as soon as possible</color>. The consequences will be dire if someone seizes it. We only chose the shortcut through Zenhai Marsh to expedite the task...",
    ["Dialogue8320208"]="Cough... You're right, master... Please leave your servant behind... The lowly Obeaune is used to pain... The precious is of utmost urgency!",
    ["Dialogue8320209"]="It's not a treasure, it's a jinx!",
    ["Dialogue8320210"]="The treasure is not a jinx! Cough, cough, cough! You, esteemed Adventurer, lowly servants don't need rare herbs. Can you help a lowly Obeaune?",
    ["Dialogue8320211"]="Please... protect master... protect the precious...",
    ["Dialogue8320212"]="You're not coming with us?",
    ["Dialogue8320213"]="(The Obeaune shakes head feebly and musters a labored smile.) \n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Along the west coastline</color>... cough... is the safest... The lowly Obeaune awaits your return... Be sure to take the west side!",
    ["Dialogue8320301"]="What a tough fight, but how come the spiders are with the pathetic crabs?",
    ["Dialogue8320302"]="Are you suspecting the Obeaune? He almost gave up his life for us. Without him, we probably would have encountered two, three, or even more giant Argos! You have no idea what troubles we ran into because of this precious!",
    ["Dialogue8320303"]="(The man calms down following your explanation.) \nThank you for the thought, but I'd rather trust my companion. Companions should trust each other, right? I guess we're also companions now, Adventurer. See, we're almost at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>journey's end</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8320304"]="I only heard about the Comodo volcano in bedtime stories told to me when I was little. Supposedly, the lava never cooled and would destroy this jinx of a treasure... Precious? Wait, why would I call it precious?",
    ["Dialogue8320401"]="Thieves! How dare you try to steal Lord Obeaune's precious!",
    ["Dialogue8320402"]="It's you! Wonderful, are you here for us?",
    ["Dialogue8320403"]="You? No, Obeaune is here for my own precious, and I'm its sole owner! You two thieves... <color=#CA2E0AFF>How come the spider didn't devour you?!</color>",
    ["Dialogue8320404"]="You drew the spider here?",
    ["Dialogue8320405"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>What if it was?!</color> How could esteemed Obeaunes serve a mere human? Give it back to me, you two, or else!",
    ["Dialogue8320406"]="The plan is to rob you clean and toss you into the volcano, naturally, then take precious back! Now cough it up, I'm running out of patience!",
    ["Dialogue8320501"]="Alas...",
    ["Dialogue8320502"]="He's the first friend I made after leaving home. I always thought we'd go back and get drunk in the tavern together... Tell everyone about this trip, find a bard who then writes a song about it...",
    ["Dialogue8320503"]="I was too gullible...",
    ["Dialogue8320504"]="(The man pauses, then wipes his face indiscriminately.) \nWe don't have much time left. We <color=#CA2E0AFF>must destroy it now</color>. Come with me, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8320601"]="Treasure... You're mine... Don't leave...",
    ["Dialogue8320602"]="No, no! With the treasure, Comodo... No, the entire Midgard will be under my command! Wealth, power, prestige... I shall establish a new kingdom and be the sole ruler!",
    ["Dialogue8320603"]="Wh-Why aren't you speaking?! Are you here to take my treasure away, too? Leave, all of you! Or <size=26>I'll kill you!</size>",
    ["Dialogue8320701"]="Treasure... No... Where's the ring?",
    ["Dialogue8320702"]="But why I do feel so tired and aching all over...?",
    ["Dialogue8320703"]="I see. The ring granted the owner great powers, but also exerted control over him in the meantime. To destroy it, I went through all the trouble in the world and almost didn't make it... Thank you for finishing the last step for me!",
    ["Dialogue8320704"]="How should I repay you...? How about a chronicle of our adventures? I'm the star, of course, but the parts about you will be the most important! Maybe when you get back to Comodo someday, you'll hear your own story! So, what should I name the book?",
    ["Dialogue8320705"]="I got it, I'll title it <color=#CA2E0AFF>The Ring of Comodo</color>! Can't leave the island out when it's where the story ends! I'll start writing it now. Everyone, not just the people in my hometown, will know about it!",
    ["Dialogue8330101"]="Old Toland... This is not good...",
    ["Dialogue8330102"]="Greetings, Adventurer. I'm Norris, the village chief. \nI'm sighing because of the Old Toland... It's really unfortunate.",
    ["Dialogue8330103"]="His daughter Lindsey has been hanging around the lighthouse by Kokomo Beach for three years now... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Three years!</color> She wanders up in the lighthouse all day, all night, not eating or sleeping. Not only is she ruining herself, but she's also got Toland stressed to no end. \nEveryone in the village can't bear to watch it, yet no one knows the truth behind it...",
    ["Dialogue8330104"]="Old Tolan rarely speaks to us now. We hardly even see him at all.",
    ["Dialogue8330105"]="It's not his fault. We tried to help, only to scare Lindsey into hiding in the lighthouse for <color=#CA2E0AFF>three days and nights</color>. We couldn't recognize her when she came down. \nSo the only option left is to seek outside help. Please, a competent Adventurer like you can surely find a way to make them talk!",
    ["Dialogue8330201"]="You are not from around here... What business do you have of me?",
    ["Dialogue8330202"]="Alas, my poor, poor Lindsey... Did the villagers tell you about her?",
    ["Dialogue8330203"]="It all started three years ago... Those goddamn <color=#CA2E0AFF>pirates</color>... That bastard Kirk! He mesmerized her with his glib tongue and convinced her to wait for him there.",
    ["Dialogue8330204"]="You know how untrustworthy, promiscuous those scallywags are! But she just refused to listen, not doing anything but running to the lighthouse, letting herself go. She keeps waiting in vain for that vile pirate...",
    ["Dialogue8330205"]="That bastard Kirk swore a <color=#CA2E0AFF>vow</color> to Lindsey that was more like a riddle, a bunch of nonsense... But she believed in it wholeheartedly.",
    ["Dialogue8330206"]="If you could find out what he promised, maybe all this would come to an end. Unfortunately, only Lindsey knows the <color=#CA2E0AFF>whole vow</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8330301"]="If the villagers sent you, please go back. I'll be here <color=#CA2E0AFF>waiting for eternity</color>, if necessary...",
    ["Dialogue8330302"]="Oh? You believed in the power of love and <color=#CA2E0AFF>vows</color> too? Thank Heavens, someone finally understands me!",
    ["Dialogue8330303"]="Before Kirk left, he promised me, \"When the starbells bloom, when the fledgling ragglers sing, when the glacier melts into flows, I shall return to you.\"",
    ["Dialogue8330304"]="My lover is late surely because he's accomplishing something big, but I can wait. My love will certainly outlast the glaciers, even time itself! He would not abandon me unless he met the worst fate at the sea... No, he loved me and would not let that happen. Oh, Kirk...",
    ["Dialogue8330305"]="You don't know how wonderful he is. When I talk about him, I can never find words good enough to describe him. \nI wish I could <color=#CA2E0AFF>hear the birds sing, see the flowers bloom</color> right now... I'll be here for you...",
    ["Dialogue8330401"]="Starbells, fledgling ragglers, and melting glaciers... Does this mean that he...",
    ["Dialogue8330402"]="Look, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pirate flag</color>! He has returned! He didn't lie... My Kirk! \nHe's a man of his word. When the starbells bloom, the fledgling ragglers sing, and the glacier melts,<color=#CA2E0AFF> he'll come to marry me! I was right, he didn't lie!",
    ["Dialogue8330403"]="(Flustered from overjoyed) Adventurer... My benefactor! Would you do me a big favor and tell him Lindsey from three years ago is waiting for him up in the lighthouse, that <color=#CA2E0AFF>I've been waiting for him this whole time</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8330404"]="I must make myself presentable. I can't let Kirk see me like this. Please, you must tell him Lindsey is waiting for him.",
    ["Dialogue8330405"]="You're finally back, Kirk... My Kirk... I have so many things to tell you...",
    ["Dialogue8330501"]="Huh? Who are you and what do you want with me?",
    ["Dialogue8330502"]="You still remember? Last time I came here I was just a deckhand, but now I'm the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corsair</color>! Made that about a year ago! So what do you want? I got no time for catching up!",
    ["Dialogue8330503"]="Lindsey? Yeah, I remember, no one on the island was prettier than her. I and the boys had a <color=#CA2E0AFF>wager</color> on who could get the prettiest girl here. I wouldn't have won if she wasn't so innocent!",
    ["Dialogue8330504"]="We probably would've been married if I <color=#CA2E0AFF>wasn't in this line of work</color>. Though if I wasn't a pirate, I probably couldn't snooker her!",
    ["Dialogue8330505"]="What did you say?",
    ["Dialogue8330506"]="Haha... Hahahaha! \nNo way, nobody can wait three years these days! What a fool, and for a pirate yet. No one could tell who on this ship three years ago would live to today. If I died, she'd be a widow! <color=#CA2E0AFF>What a joke</color>! It's just a rumor, so don't nauseate me or Lindsey with it, or else.",
    ["Dialogue8330507"]="I don't know who you are or where you came from, but Lindsey <color=#CA2E0AFF>must be long married by now</color> and I got a wife of my own, so let the past be the past. <color=#CA2E0AFF>It's foolish to seek storybook romance in the real world.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8330508"]="Go, scram. Tell the story somewhere else. I'm a pirate and <color=#CA2E0AFF>never meant</color> to be with her!",
    ["Dialogue8330601"]="Where's Kirk? He didn't come with you?",
    ["Dialogue8330602"]="My Kirk must be on that ship, right? Did he tell you he didn't come with you because he wanted to surprise me? It's okay to tell me and I'll pretend I don't know! We'll surprise him back!",
    ["Dialogue8330603"]="Please, tell me if he's coming or not. I <color=#CA2E0AFF>just want</color> to know that...",
    ["Dialogue8330604"]="...I see. He's not coming? He didn't want to come to see me?",
    ["Dialogue8330605"]="Three years ago, he said when that happens, he'll come back... No, that's probably not Kirk but someone else you talked to...",
    ["Dialogue8330606"]="It was really a lie...? Pirates would break promises? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Is it my fault</color>...",
    ["Dialogue8330607"]="...Thank you. No, please leave. Why is it my fault, Kirk? No, it's Kirk's fault, he's bad...",
    ["Dialogue8340101"]="Oh? You're interested in the treasure from the high sea too? These are all rare valuables, but they can also cost you everything you got...",
    ["Dialogue8340102"]="(After what you said, Jack nudges the crown back almost unnoticeably.) \nI'd advise not to ask a pirate how he got his treasure, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8340103"]="Fine, for the Zeny, my pal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jimmy</color> got this crown. He's been making a killing behind our backs lately. Hey, do you want it or not?",
    ["Dialogue8340104"]="(Jack shows disdain, his finger almost nailing you in the forehead.) \nScrew you, I never give anything out for free, not even if you... got a lot of Zeny! Unless...",
    ["Dialogue8340105"]="We barter in goods! I heard the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shellfish</color> carried the shiniest <color=#CA2E0AFF>sea pearl</color>, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aster</color> can produce exquisite <color=#CA2E0AFF>coral crystals</color>, which would greatly help my business. If you could get me some, I could consider lending the crown!",
    ["Dialogue8340201"]="Where did you get this?",
    ["Dialogue8340202"]="So it's that money-grabbing trader... I hope he remembers my cut.",
    ["Dialogue8340203"]="(Jimmy glances at the crown in your hand and starts getting nervous.) \nThis? Well, it's from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>very close acquaintance</color>. You know, we'd help someone in trouble sometimes and they gave us something good in return.",
    ["Dialogue8340204"]="Look, a flying Poring!",
    ["Dialogue8340301"]="Stop beating me! Boohoo...",
    ["Dialogue8340302"]="I really don't know much! That fellow just wanted us to take him out of there and mentioned nothing else! I've never even seen him eat! He has a creepy look that screamed \"Leave me alone!\"... I would've tossed him overboard if it wasn't for the crown!",
    ["Dialogue8340303"]="Why are you doing this? I recall he <color=#CA2E0AFF>wore a cape as red as blood and a scary mask... He didn't even have shoes on</color>! That's all I know!",
    ["Dialogue8340304"]="Stop hitting me! Okay, he wanted to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hermit's Village</color> and told us not to tell anyone about it or we'll die a horrible death... Boohoo...",
    ["Dialogue8340305"]="(The bruised Jimmy cries and then sniffles.) \nIt's all Jack's fault... You can't trust merchants at all!",
    ["Dialogue8340401"]="It's impolite to not even apologize.",
    ["Dialogue8340402"]="(He points toward where you stood and grumbles.) \nOver there, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>guy in a red cape and mask</color> was watching you in that corner. He has weird gestures, too. I asked him what he was doing, but he ran off and left his belongings behind!",
    ["Dialogue8340403"]="What a big <color=#CA2E0AFF>puppet</color>... Is he a puppet master? Hey, what's this?",
    ["Dialogue8340501"]="(The footprints on the soil are in different shapes, sizes, and directions. Looking closely, some are bare feet without shoes.)",
    ["Dialogue8340601"]="(The muddy barefoot prints go forward, leading up to the wooden passage and back.)",
    ["Dialogue8340701"]="(The trail of muddy footprints ends at a cabin. Other than the tracks going in-and-out at the door, there are no other indications.)",
    ["Dialogue8340801"]="(The corpse falls to the ground, but it's not the wizard you just fought. Upon examination, you sense intense Undead Aura from the dead body, with foreign words imprinted on the chest.)",
    ["Dialogue8350101"]="Hey, what brought you to me, my friend? Or... did you hear my complaint just now?",
    ["Dialogue8350102"]="It's a gaffe for me as the lead bard here... to expose my impotence in public.",
    ["Dialogue8350103"]="Ahem, yes. Although I, Callahan, dare not proclaim to be respected by all bards, I at very least can lead a troupe, so I didn't expect anyone to get out of hand.",
    ["Dialogue8350104"]="There's a young fellow named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doyle</color> who's a lecherous narcissist. Good bards should praise everything, but he indulges only in so-called romance, love, and the ladies around him! I'd never call others out for being undisciplined, but he shouldn't have treated a performance that everyone took seriously like it was nothing.",
    ["Dialogue8350105"]="He really needs a lesson, but I have to stay behind to clean up his mess. I implore you to show him what-for, my friend, not just for me and the troupe, but for the local community.",
    ["Dialogue8350106"]="His tent is on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east side</color>. You should be able to track him from there. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>girls</color> he charmed should be staking it out already by now... Anyway, believe me when I say it's for everybody's good to adjust his attitude.",
    ["Dialogue8350201"]="What do you want with him? Also, please don't interfere with<color=#CA2E0AFF>Doyle Fan Club</color> business, as you just ruined the formation I took so long to choreograph.",
    ["Dialogue8350202"]="Doyle? Yes, he promised to take me aboard the majestic <color=#CA2E0AFF>pirate ship</color> sailing to the treasure island!",
    ["Dialogue8350203"]="He did not! He promised me he would scale the highest step of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pyramid</color> with me, just like the ancient Pharaoh and his queen!",
    ["Dialogue8350204"]="He said...",
    ["Dialogue8350205"]="Doyle told me...",
    ["Dialogue8350206"]="(The scene is getting chaotic with everyone trying to talk over each other, convinced they're his absolute favorite...)",
    ["Dialogue8350207"]="Quiet, all of you! Our rule is to speak one at a time. Do you know why Doyle neglects you? It's because you all lacked basic manners!",
    ["Dialogue8350208"]="Look at you, you got taste... But we'll never share our secrets with Doyle with you for naught. You'll have to trade us with something relevant to him! Let me give you a freebie: I composed songs with Doyle and he still sings what I wrote in public!",
    ["Dialogue8350209"]="Everyone here came together through sharing Doyle moments. You're no exception.",
    ["Dialogue8350210"]="Well, how about you show us the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pirate ship</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pyramid</color>? Bring the pictures from these two places back and we'll tell you.",
    ["Dialogue8350301"]="Oh my, that's where he and Great Sage Kroneika defeated the corsair...",
    ["Dialogue8350302"]="Do you know Doyle steal the secret from this Pyramid and saved the entire Sograt Desert...?!",
    ["Dialogue8350303"]="He is so mighty and brave! He's the greatest warrior and lover on this land!",
    ["Dialogue8350304"]="He's not just talented, he went on adventures too... No one is more dashing than him!",
    ["Dialogue8350305"]="You never heard of his many exploits? How can anyone be so ignorant? Okay, listen up, one of Doyle's greatest feats is none other than <color=#CA2E0AFF>quelling the monster crisis in Prontera</color> single-handedly!",
    ["Dialogue8350306"]="Also, he unearthed many secrets in Glast Heim, the haunted city where no ordinary man would dare tread! Furthermore...",
    ["Dialogue8350307"]="Furthermore, he solved the ancient puzzle <color=#CA2E0AFF>himself</color>! What a living legend!",
    ["Dialogue8350308"]="Bite your tongue! Doyle is far more valiant than a chump like you could hope to be! How dare you take credit for his deeds! You must think we're stupid enough to fall for your lines!",
    ["Dialogue8350309"]="I was wondering what you're doing here... So you want to smear Doyle's reputation!",
    ["Dialogue8350310"]="Leave now, you're not welcome here anymore!",
    ["Dialogue8350401"]="Who said it was him? We almost beat up the wrong guy!",
    ["Dialogue8350402"]="...Sorry, we're too livid and focused on getting <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doyle</color>, so when we saw you show up at the time he's supposed to meet the villagers, we thought you were him...",
    ["Dialogue8350403"]="You don't know half of it! That bastard could sweet-talk and sweet-write love letters that wrapped all the women in a village around his finger!",
    ["Dialogue8350404"]="The bastard doesn't discriminate... Whether it's a blossoming young dame or a married lady, he'd make a move and \"dedicate my eternal love\" to everyone... How disgusting!",
    ["Dialogue8350405"]="He probably caught wind of it and ran! You getting waylaid could be in his <color=#CA2E0AFF>plan</color> too. Doyle is such a vile, despicable scoundrel!",
    ["Dialogue8350406"]="Olivia? She lives in the Main City of Comodo. You'll see her easy enough. Pity her for attracting that fellow's attention...",
    ["Dialogue8350501"]="Hello. I don't know you, but what can I help you with?",
    ["Dialogue8350502"]="You're <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doyle's friend</color>? Hello. Did he send you with a message? Did the rendezvous spot change?",
    ["Dialogue8350503"]="Oh, so he's hanging out with something else. It's all right, I got my own things to do.",
    ["Dialogue8350504"]="What's wrong? It's not like those prepubescent girls can wrest him away from me.\n",
    ["Dialogue8350505"]="He told me I got something that no other girl got, and that's sophistication. Doyle is the only man to see that in me, so he wouldn't give me up. I let him play, as long as he comes back when he gets sick of those ones!",
    ["Dialogue8350506"]="How do you know about that? Did Doyle send you to test me? Well, he told me the color of the blue iris complements my hair perfectly. I thought he'd give me one, but I guess he wanted me to wear it next time.",
    ["Dialogue8350507"]="Young people are into everything, aren't they? Heheh. Can I trouble you, Doyle's friend, to pick a few <color=#CA2E0AFF>blue irises</color> for me? I'm rather busy at the moment to do it myself...",
    ["Dialogue8350601"]="Wow, they are pretty flowers! Let me see, should I make a loop, a laurel, or just pin them here... (Olivia gestures with the flowers on her head)",
    ["Dialogue8350602"]="Don't they look pretty... What did you say?",
    ["Dialogue8350603"]="Thank you, friend of Doyle. Drop by and don't be a stranger. It gets <color=#CA2E0AFF>very lonely by myself</color> here.",
    ["Dialogue8350701"]="...What? I'm busy. Go away while you can.",
    ["Dialogue8350702"]="You're looking for that fellow? Let me make it clear, whether you're here for a favor or a grudge, it's got nothing to do with me. I'm here for his booze.",
    ["Dialogue8350703"]="Otherwise, who would come here for some stupid sunset? I'm tired of seeing that on the ship... <color=#CA2E0AFF>How passe</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8350704"]="Well, he said he's getting some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tri Joints</color> for the next round with drinks, but who knows where he went. That's how he is, bragging and then vanishing like the wind. He'd leave the booze here, but not this time, so I'm left waiting.",
    ["Dialogue8350705"]="As delicate as he is, you could tell he's <color=#CA2E0AFF>sheltered and pampered</color>. You wouldn't expect him to catch anything in the wild. He's probably surrounded by the bugs, screaming for his mommy right now... <color=#CA2E0AFF>I get a kick out of that notion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8350801"]="Thank you, unnamed warrior! I swear I shall compose a poem to glorify your deed throughout Comodo!",
    ["Dialogue8350802"]="Warrior? What are you doing...",
    ["Dialogue8350803"]="How dare that <color=#CA2E0AFF>wizard</color> send others to curb my freedom! You're just his minion! Scram!",
    ["Dialogue8350804"]="(Doyle offers no resistance and falls into the water.) Why you...! How dare you do this to me! My girls won't stand for this!",
    ["Dialogue8350805"]="...What are you doing? Stay away!",
    ["Dialogue8350806"]="Okay, I will! Please spare me! Yes, whether it be <color=#CA2E0AFF>taking the public performance seriously</color> or <color=#CA2E0AFF>coming clean with my appropriations</color>, I'll do all of that! Just don't bring that worm over!",
    ["Dialogue8350807"]="(Doyle conspicuously hesitates, but once your hand moves closer, he drops to his knees and almost plants his face into the dirt) I got it! I will do that! Thank you for saving and sparing me! I'm forever in your debt!",
    ["Dialogue8350808"]="Okay, okay...",
    ["Dialogue8360101"]="Don't let me catch you, foul culprit!",
    ["Dialogue8360102"]="Alas. Many tavern patrons were <color=#CA2E0AFF>waylaid</color> on their way home recently. What's worse, we not only haven't caught the perpetrator but also didn't even get a good look. This keeps up, and no one will visit anymore.",
    ["Dialogue8360103"]="Thank you! The victims Eugene, Gordon, and Mottle are around. When the perp is caught, I'll treat you to the most genuine Comodo beer!",
    ["Dialogue8360201"]="Damn, first day on Comodo and this... Curse my luck!",
    ["Dialogue8360202"]="(Eugene grabs you by the hand and his eyes start to water.) \nI came to Comodo to work. I just got paid yesterday. Miss Vendra even offered me a free round of <color=#CA2E0AFF>beer</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>after closing</color>. She is so pretty. I was to write her a poem, but as soon as I <color=#CA2E0AFF>spoke the first line</color>, that damn fellow hit me! The beer was gone, and I hurt all over...",
    ["Dialogue8360301"]="Another foreigner! Cheers! If it wasn't for my injured legs, I'd take you drinking and grilling on the beach!",
    ["Dialogue8360302"]="At <color=#CA2E0AFF>night</color> when you couldn't see anything and nobody else was on the beach, of course! Oh, he also took my <color=#CA2E0AFF>beer</color>. I fought back and <color=#CA2E0AFF>screamed</color>, but he gagged me with sand! Pah!",
    ["Dialogue8360401"]="Who's dumb enough to sneak attack me! Show yourself, I'll beat the crap out of you!",
    ["Dialogue8360402"]="At <color=#CA2E0AFF>night</color> when you couldn't see anything and nobody else was on the beach, of course! Oh, he also took my <color=#CA2E0AFF>beer</color>. I fought back and <color=#CA2E0AFF>screamed</color>, but he gagged me with sand! Pah!",
    ["Dialogue8360501"]="Any leads?",
    ["Dialogue8360502"]="A clue? Well, I'll wait for the good news!",
    ["Dialogue8360601"]="(It's fixated on the beer in your hand and still trying to take it from you.) \n\"Beer... Beer-bobo!!\"",
    ["Dialogue8360602"]="(It rubs its head and follows you like a scolded dog.) \nBeer-bobo...",
    ["Dialogue8360603"]="(While struggling, you notice the beer mug in its hand has the<color=#CA2E0AFF> Vendra's Tavern logo</color> on it.) \n\"Beer... Beer-bobo!!\"",
    ["Dialogue8360701"]="You're back! Where's the assailant?",
    ["Dialogue8360702"]="A Galapago? \n(Vendra locks eyes with the Galapago and giggles.) \nI didn't expect these little fellas to be into beer!",
    ["Dialogue8360703"]="Beer-bobo!",
    ["Dialogue8360704"]="Okay, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>no robbery</color> next time! Come see me if you want some. The tavern will be more lively with you around too!",
    ["Dialogue8360705"]="Beer-bo!",
    ["Dialogue8400101"]="Just the person I'm looking for.\nThe patrols just notified me that they saw <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aronst</color> at the gate.",
    ["Dialogue8400102"]="Not so fast. I already asked the patrols to escort him back to the palace. He looked really weak, and his mind was a mess, so Dr. Dante took a look at him and suggested that we replenish his stamina with something not too strong.",
    ["Dialogue8400103"]="Here's the recipe for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vegetable Stew</color> that I got from Dr. Dante. It requires calming herbs that are not found in the city. So...",
    ["Dialogue8400104"]="Yes, Adventurer, Aronst is special. Given that another uprising happened at the most recent Bloodline Banquet, I can't trust anyone else but you to attend personally.",
    ["Dialogue8400105"]="Here is the recipe from Dr. Dante with details for making the Vegetable Stew. The main ingredients are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mint</color> growing outside Prontera South Gate and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goldflower Stamen</color> of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora<color=#CA2E0AFF>. In addition, we need the </color>Premium Grease</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Savage Babe</color> to offset the bitterness of the two herbs.",
    ["Dialogue8400106"]="I'll stay with Aronst for the time being to calm him down. Once the stew is finished, please come back. I'll be waiting in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>palace</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8400201"]="I feel much better now... Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8400202"]="Can you tell me where you have been the past several days, Aronst? You've been missing ever since the Bloodline Banquet. Princess and I sent people to scour every corner of the kingdom. She even thought... you're no longer alive.",
    ["Dialogue8400203"]="I'm sorry, Bohr. I didn't mean for you to raise concern. I've been recuperating on a farm in the Schwarzwald Republic. As for how I got there... I don't remember. My memory stopped on the morning of the Bloodline Banquet when I was talking to Azer in the Pooler Garden, and he offered me a mysterious potion...",
    ["Dialogue8400204"]="I found myself in the Republic when my eyes opened again. For days after I came to, I was in a daze and couldn't remember who I was. But the friendly people on the farm encouraged me to stay until I regained my memory, so I did. Then, my recall slowly returned, and every night, I'd have the same weird dream...",
    ["Dialogue8400205"]="Meeting Azer in the Pooler Garden. He seemed to be telling me something important, but no matter how hard I tried, I couldn't make out what it was. I could sense, however, that I was very familiar with the garden in the dream. It was perhaps somewhere I lived before. If I could return to it, maybe I could recall the missing memory. That was why I decided to leave the farm.",
    ["Dialogue8400206"]="I see. I can almost piece the puzzle together now. I believe what Azer offered you was something to cloud your mind, intending for you to temporarily forget who you are. Then he sent you to the Republic for the people on the farm to care for you, so you would miss the feast altogether.",
    ["Dialogue8400207"]="That's what I think as well... But what I don't understand is why would Azer do that?\n(Aronst tugs at Bohr and pleads.)\nBohr, where is Azer? I want to see him.",
    ["Dialogue8400208"]="You're still too weak to do much right now.\n(Bohr holds Aronst's hands gently and consoles him while quietly exchanging a glance with you.)",
    ["Dialogue8400209"]="Do you mind getting some holy water from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color> for Aronst, Adventurer? We can talk more when he is calmer.",
    ["Dialogue8400301"]="Can you tell me where Azer is, Bohr? I have many questions for him... Please don't look at me like that. I've asked many people, but no one wanted to tell me... I want to know why!",
    ["Dialogue8400302"]="Gone?\n(Aronst looks at you, stunned, obviously not fully grasping what you meant.)\nYou mean Azer is... dead?",
    ["Dialogue8400303"]="Calm down, Aronst, and listen to me...",
    ["Dialogue8400304"]="No, impossible! I refuse to believe it!",
    ["Dialogue8400305"]="(He strains to get up and stumbles toward the Walter residence.)\nYou are lying to me... I'll go see him myself... I know he's waiting for me to come back...",
    ["Dialogue8400306"]="Stop, Aronst! You can't go to Walters on a whim. They're now on the end of their rope and could bite you at any time! At least wait until you officially... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Knock him out</color>, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8400401"]="Thank you, Adventurer, and I apologize for making you do it. When Aronst is getting better, I'll try to help him process all this.",
    ["Dialogue8400402"]="Yes, and very quickly, too, for the Gaebolg blood runs in his veins, so he shall be indomitable, resilient, and dutiful... just like Tristan III. All we have to do is just bear witness. Aronst will never let us down.",
    ["Dialogue8410101"]="There you are, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8410102"]="What could happen to me? I'm standing before you in one piece and perhaps will even succeed to the throne soon...\n(His chuckles are full of scoff.)\nBut Azer... he's dead without so much as a burial.",
    ["Dialogue8410103"]="Don't worry, Adventurer, I'm not one to give up on myself. What Azer sacrificed his life for, I will cherish. But can you tell me what exactly happened?",
    ["Dialogue8410104"]="(Aronst casually waves it off.)\nNever mind. If you don't tell me, I'll go ask Bohr. By chance, he just sent a soldier to me saying he wants to chat about what happened lately... Do you mind coming with me, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8410201"]="I've been waiting a long time, Aronst. How are you holding up?",
    ["Dialogue8410202"]="I can handle a chat. What would you like to talk to me about? Is it about Azer?",
    ["Dialogue8410203"]="Yes. I just got more news about Azer... Actually, make that something Azer left behind.\n(Bohr waves a bard over.)\nExplain it, Kain.",
    ["Dialogue8410204"]="Yes, Lord Bohr.\n(He bows slightly and takes out a hefty letter.)\nPleased to meet you, Lord Aronst and Adventurer. I am Kain.",
    ["Dialogue8410205"]="Please permit me to recount everything for you. Not long ago, Lord Azer tasked me with the duty of delivering this letter to his father, assuming Prince Aronst is safe and sound following the Bloodline Banquet.",
    ["Dialogue8410206"]="However, in the following days with Lord Azer, everything he did moved me deeply... Therefore, I made the call to hand Lord Bohr the letter. I don't think Lord Ian would understand it, but maybe you can.",
    ["Dialogue8410207"]="What did the letter say?",
    ["Dialogue8410208"]="Everything you wanted to know, Aronst, but I won't force you to read it. You can leave it with me for the time being until you're ready to accept the truth.",
    ["Dialogue8410209"]="No, please give it to me, Bohr. I want to know what this is all about.",
    ["Dialogue8410301"]="(Puke) Cough, cough...",
    ["Dialogue8410302"]="Are you all right, Aronst?",
    ["Dialogue8410303"]="I'm fine, just a little dizzy... (Puke)",
    ["Dialogue8410304"]="Water! Somebody get some water now!",
    ["Dialogue8410401"]="Azer, you...\n(Aronst holds his head in agony, the fingers on his other hand that is holding the letter are turning pale as the sheet rustles.)",
    ["Dialogue8410402"]="Not like this, Aronst. You're not completely recovered yet... Perhaps we should call it a day.",
    ["Dialogue8410403"]="No... Give me something to keep me up. I can... I must finish reading.",
    ["Dialogue8410501"]="Is this all that's in there?",
    ["Dialogue8410502"]="Yes, Lord Aronst. Once Lord Azer was kind enough to help my troupe, so when he in turn was in need of aid, we did not hesitate to extend a helping hand. And in accordance with his plans, we dressed up as servants in the Banquet Hall and did as he bid us during the Bloodline Banquet... Perhaps because of everything I saw, I cannot accept that he should meet such an end.",
    ["Dialogue8410503"]="So... what do you expect me to do now that you have given me this letter? Punish the Walter family? Or restore Azer's good name?",
    ["Dialogue8410504"]="Is that what you wish to do, Aronst?",
    ["Dialogue8410505"]="There is no rush to respond, and there is one more thing I want to tell you before you make the decision as the new king.\n(Bohr raises his hand to silence Aronst. Bohr's eyes are full of sadness, and you start to guess what is happening.)\nNot long ago... we found the remains of King Tristan III.",
    ["Dialogue8410506"]="Yes... When you gave me the news about the crown, I sent soldiers to search for him in the waters near Arunafeltz. At an abbey on a nameless isle, they found him deceased... He was still wearing the same robe as the day he disappeared, and had been stripped of anything of any value.",
    ["Dialogue8410507"]="But he died clutching one item, something he wished to protect. It was a letter, written in blood... It was his last wish, written in his last moments.",
    ["Dialogue8410508"]="His... his last wish?\n(Aronst covers his eyes, but you glimpse the young man's tears between his fingers.)\nI am sorry... Adventurer, read the letter. I...",
    ["Dialogue8410601"]="Aronst, by now you know the truth behind the rebellion. There can be no defense of the Walter family's betrayal, and the members of the Royal Chivalry who took part must too be punished. But our late king was right, Lord, in that a ruler must consider the bigger picture. To imprison the entire Walter family, one of the Seven Royal Families, would do great harm to the country.",
    ["Dialogue8410602"]="Having won the election, you are the rightful heir to the throne. It is your right to decide their fate. But whatever you decide, I hope you will remember...",
    ["Dialogue8410603"]="I, and the Defense Force, will never waver in our support of you.\n(Bohr opens his palm. He is holding the ring which symbolizes the authority of the king—the ring you recently placed on Azer's finger and then removed.)",
    ["Dialogue8410604"]="(Aronst hesitates for some time before he decides to place that ring, the ring Azer wore for such a brief period, on his own finger.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Is this... Is this what they killed Azer for? Ha... I cannot let them escape...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8410605"]="But... I cannot do that. I cannot fail His Majesty and Azer... nor the people who place their trust in me. So... I must...\n(He sobs, tears falling from his cheeks, but he raises his hand high so that all may see the ring.)",
    ["Dialogue8410606"]="I, Aronst Gaebolg, the fifty-seventh king of the Rune Kingdom, reprieve Ian Walter as well as his co-conspirators of their punishments and permit them to swear loyalty to the crown.",
    ["Dialogue8410607"]="(As Aronst speaks through his sobs, Bohr lowers his head to kiss the young king's hand.)\nI will follow your orders, Your Majesty.",
    ["Dialogue8410608"]="So it is like this... I am starting to see why Lord Azer chose you. Lord Aronst, allow me to tell you something. Just as you have not failed the trust Lord Azer placed in you, nor did Lord Azer... nor did he ever turn his back on his king.",
    ["Dialogue8410609"]="That dawn, as you and Lord Azer spoke at Pooler Garden, I was nearby watching over you. He said something which you may not recall, but that was a promise he made to you. He said—",
    ["Dialogue8410610"]="Aronst, for me, there can be no other king. Whether you wear the crown or not... I will remain loyal to you forever.",
    ["Dialogue8420101"]="(On the airship's platform, the well-dressed man is muttering to himself.)\nIf I knew this was such a pain in the butt, I should have taken sick leave when I first got assigned to this task. The worst case scenario is to put up with the yelling from my boss, but now if I fail the task, I might have to take a permanent leave... with my boss as well...",
    ["Dialogue8420102"]="My main task is hard enough for me already, and now I have to be a tour guide, work overtime to take care of the travel permit, and babysit the targets for whatever they might need along the way, while they are good for nothing but a pile of dead meat I drag behind...",
    ["Dialogue8420103"]="I shouldn't have signed up for the military academy in the first place. What's good for a royal guard? I can't even out-fight them. A tour guide sounds much better; everyone goes on a happy trip to the Republic and gets deported back to the kingdom with a smile on their face...",
    ["Dialogue8420104"]="Yes... No-no-no, I'm not! Huh? You...",
    ["Dialogue8420105"]="Do you know me?",
    ["Dialogue8420106"]="(As if suddenly woken from a dream, the man puts on a serious face.)\nHere is not a good place to talk, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8420201"]="(He brings you to a corner where no one is around.)\nHello, Adventurer. I have nothing against you, but in fact, this is not the first time we have met.",
    ["Dialogue8420202"]="At the kingdom's award ceremony, you were bestowed with honor for suppressing the monsters' riot in the capital. I was there with my boss, and you left a deep impression on everyone.",
    ["Dialogue8420203"]="Adventurer, I am <color=#CA2E0AFF>Syphus, aide-de-camp of the Rune Kingdom's Foreign Minister</color>. I reveal my identity to you because I need your help. As both of us are citizens of Rune Kingdom, you are the perfect fellow I can turn to. This is a serious deal, and please forgive me for not revealing everything to you at this moment. But I truly hope that you will lend me your hands without holding back.",
    ["Dialogue8420204"]="Thank you. In fact, I was assigned to escort <color=#CA2E0AFF>a man and a woman</color> to enter the Republic through the Border Inspection Station, but I lost contact with them due to my dereliction of duty.",
    ["Dialogue8420205"]="Embarrassed of me. The two of them adapted to the new environment way better than me, and their curiosity was off the chart. When I was still getting used to the trip, they had already blended into the crowd and gone missing.",
    ["Dialogue8420206"]="The political environment here in Juno is totally different than that in Prontera. Have you seen the guards patrolling on the street? They are there to suppress the androids in the riot. This country is on the verge of flipping over. As for our \"passionate\" friends out there on the street, it's only a matter of time before they attract enough attention and expose themselves. By then, my identity is nothing compared to the devastating outcome caused by the failed mission, and it will become a serious diplomatic issue.",
    ["Dialogue8420207"]="(His face turns even more serious as he speaks)\nAdventurer, we must bring the two of them back here as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue8420208"]="Ha! Speaking of names, I would rather tell you about their unique temperament. <color=#CA2E0AFF>One of them is a lady, who runs her mouth with a loud and rough voice with little to no manners. She wears purple hair, and it seems like she is always looking for a fight</color>. When we were on the way here, I heard someone talking about a hostile new face in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>marketplace</color>. Maybe you can start from there.",
    ["Dialogue8420209"]="By the way, the two of them have \"bonded\" pretty well along the way. If you manage to locate the lady, I think <color=#CA2E0AFF>she can point you in the right direction to the other one</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8420210"]="(The man gives you a discreet military salute.)\nThank you for your service! You can rest assured that your good deed will be remembered by everyone!",
    ["Dialogue8420211"]="(His determined face becomes helpless all of a sudden.)\nMy boss told me to report to him immediately once I arrived in Juno...",
    ["Dialogue8420212"]="Well then, I will now take care of the Kingdom's business. Please keep your head down, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8420301"]="(Among the crowd, a purple-haired girl puts her feet on the cart's wheel spoke, slamming a navy blue crystal on the desk before the stall owner.)\nAm I a joke to you?! You have the guts to ask for <color=#CA2E0AFF>2,000 Zeny</color>? For a Mana Crystal with such inferior purity! Are you selling crystals or junk here?",
    ["Dialogue8420302"]="What's wrong? Does it not worth the price for something that can replenish your mana in a blink of an eye? You weigh Zeny over your life? If I'm selling high-purity crystals, you won't be able to afford it!",
    ["Dialogue8420303"]="Duh! Don't act like you have those of high-purity. They are only for sale on the official channels. That piece of junk you've got here looks like it was taken from the mother crystal.",
    ["Dialogue8420304"]="(The girl pulls out a dagger and quickly stabs it into the wooden price tag.)\nLet me tell ya, I am in the mood to change the price tag here, <size=26>how about 200 Zeny</size>?",
    ["Dialogue8420305"]="200? Get lost! Don't waste my time if you are broke! 2,000 Zeny it is! That's the price for everyone! You want a discount? Come walk over my dead body!",
    ["Dialogue8420306"]="Huh...<color=#CA2E0AFF>Are you trying me</color>?\n(The blade is out of the sheath, and the shiny metal reflects on the girl's murderous face.)",
    ["Dialogue8420307"]="Whoa-whoa-whoa! You got yourself a backup here?\n(The stall owner stands upright and stares at you two while cracking his knuckles.)\nI want to find out <size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>whether I end up giving out the discount today, or you end up giving up your life!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8420401"]="Haha! Who would have thought the famous Adventurer was good at bargaining. Sigh, if it's not that everyone recognizes you, I really want you to join my team. Now let's talk business. How do you want me to repay you?",
    ["Dialogue8420402"]="Zeny, for sure! That punk named Syphus told me there are a lot of money-making opportunities in Juno. Even an idiot can make a crazy amount of money here. Huh, such a sweet talker. I don't want to take orders from him anymore!",
    ["Dialogue8420403"]="But... I'm a bit strapped lately, and my team wasn't getting any business. Buying and flipping things here kinda helped out the situation.",
    ["Dialogue8420404"]="Take a look at this Mana Crystal. If I bring it back to the kingdom and sell it to the mages, or just simply \"make\" it a royal sapphire that is popular among the nobles... Tsk, who would say no to the profit there?",
    ["Dialogue8420405"]="What? That punk sent you to get me?\n(Goldie frowns and mutters a few words.)\nTsk, that sucks. Never mind, since you helped me out just now, I won't cause you more trouble.",
    ["Dialogue8420406"]="Adventurer, we'd better split up here. Thanks for helping me out.",
    ["Dialogue8420407"]="That guy? He is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>muscular white-haired kid. Good at fighting but doesn't talk much</color>. We had about 30 good fights along the road, but the words I got out of him couldn't even make up a complete sentence!",
    ["Dialogue8420408"]="Hmm... it looks like he <color=#CA2E0AFF>went to the school with a bunch of students in nice clothes</color>. Weird, he never looks like an A+ student to me...",
    ["Dialogue8420501"]="(The white-haired kid with red pupils knocks the monster into the air with a punch, flexing his fingers at you.)\nEleven.",
    ["Dialogue8420502"]="This is the eleventh time that someone has interrupted my trial. Are you a challenger? Or... a trouble marker?",
    ["Dialogue8420503"]="It was me, indeed.\n(Zenlur nods his head and glances at you while cracking his knuckles.)\n...Never mind. I will take on every one of you at the same time.",
    ["Dialogue8420504"]="Hold on! Adventurer, don't get it wrong! Zenlur is our newly recruited <color=#CA2E0AFF>volunteer</color>. Those monsters were just the disposable objects for testing the Muscle-Building Potion.",
    ["Dialogue8420505"]="Ah... Zenlur? Thank you so much for your cooperation. I believe our mentor will be very happy to see this data!",
    ["Dialogue8420506"]="Humph... Adventurer, have you not noticed that your location has changed?",
    ["Dialogue8420507"]="(The student up front gives out a crazy look.)\nYes! This is the cradle of technology, the swaddle of magic, the home of knowledge, and the hall of truth—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno University</color>! Adventurer, you are lucky enough. Now it's just the time of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>425th Juno Campus Festival</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8420508"]="Now, please allow me—Adel Albert, a freshman of alchemy at the Hubawooz Magic School, Juno University to introduce our alchemical masterpiece to you, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Muscle-Building Potion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8420509"]="This potion, infused with the sweetness of strawberry and the texture of clouds, provides the user with the strength of a tiger and the speed of a leopard. It turns your muscle into a rock with explosive energy! Look—",
    ["Dialogue8420510"]="(Adel ignores Zenlur's dissatisfied expression in his eyes, and starts to obsessively flex Zenlur's muscle by stretching his limbs, making poses one after another.)\nTake a look. Such a beautiful experimental object with marvelous bone structure... Oh! Pardon me. It's just like the youth from heaven, one that's on par with David! Who made all this happen?",
    ["Dialogue8420511"]="You guess it right! It's our MUSCLE-BUILDING POTION!\n(Adel holds up a shiny bottle of yellow liquid with both hands, walking toward you.)\nIt... It's calling the name of its next master! The next lucky master!!!",
    ["Dialogue8420512"]="(Adel stops before you.)\nYou, are you willing to drink it?<size=26>Are you willing to devote yourself to the miracle?</size>",
    ["Dialogue8420513"]="Good! I knew it when I first saw you! Adventurer, after you finish this bottle of Muscle-Building Potion, you can try out the Maglev Skateboard at the booth of the Noriega School of Science. It can greatly increase your movement speed! Since all of us are the dream chasers in the path of science, I am fully confident in their scientific research!",
    ["Dialogue8420514"]="(Adel's face turns pale all of a sudden. He steps back as if suffering unbelievable shocks.)\nY-You, don't want it? No... How is it possible for anyone to turn down this bottle of Muscle-Building Potion? I knew it! You are a speed chaser, aren't you? You are fond of something fast, something that can improve your movement speed, like the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maglev Skateboard from the Noriega School of Science</color>! Tell me I am right!",
    ["Dialogue8420515"]="Improve the speed? Interesting.",
    ["Dialogue8420601"]="(Before the booth, three Juno students are silently exchanging eye contact with Zenlur.)\nDo... you... want... to... try... it... out...?",
    ["Dialogue8420602"]="Is it really fast? How fast?",
    ["Dialogue8420603"]="(Three students point at the sky with an unthinkably low speed.)\nFaster... than... Gryphon...",
    ["Dialogue8420604"]="...Should... we... let... them... try... it... together...?",
    ["Dialogue8420605"]="Let... me... think... hmmm...\n(After taking a good while, he decided to ask the fellow next to him.)\nWhat... do... you... think...?",
    ["Dialogue8420606"]="I... think... hmm... yes... they... can... race... the... skateboard...",
    ["Dialogue8420607"]="(The physics student takes the skateboard off the booth.)\nWatch... my... move... you... need to... be quick... when getting... on the... skateboard...",
    ["Dialogue8420608"]="(Zenlur has had enough of this and pushes the student away, doing a run-up on the spot.)\nHeavens, no! Hey, let's race! And the destination will be... the stall over there!",
    ["Dialogue8420609"]="It's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Engineering</color> weirdo...",
    ["Dialogue8420701"]="I... lost?",
    ["Dialogue8420702"]="Humph... So the opponent this time is technology... Interesting... Hey! How many of these you've got? Tell me all you know!",
    ["Dialogue8420703"]="Over there...",
    ["Dialogue8420704"]="The <color=#CA2E0AFF>engineering</color> weirdo...",
    ["Dialogue8420705"]="That's the power of technology, too? Fine, come on!",
    ["Dialogue8420801"]="Ho-ho-ho... Adventurers from afar, you do have a beautiful set of figures... We are engineering students of the Noriega School of Science. Do you want to take a closer look at these human-friendly kids?",
    ["Dialogue8420802"]="Oh? Great reaction... I believe there's no better one than the two of you to be this kid's teacher...",
    ["Dialogue8420803"]="Yes...\n(The student-like youngster fondly holds up the hand of this mech creature, then twists its wrist 360 degrees with a smile on his face.)",
    ["Dialogue8420804"]="For a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mechanical</color> child that can simulate human actions, how can it be mass-produced if there is not a human teacher?",
    ["Dialogue8420805"]="It seems the two of you are eager to join our <color=#CA2E0AFF>test project</color>. Don't be shy. Just relax and stretch out your body. Take it easy, please. Who's first?",
    ["Dialogue8420806"]="(Zenlur steps back.)\nNot me. I am stiff.",
    ["Dialogue8420807"]="Okay, okay! You are here to get me back, right?\n(Zenlur fiddles with the mech creature in standby mode with genuine interest.) \n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Let me check this machine inside out, then I'll go back with you.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8420808"]="Ho-ho! Looks like both of you have reached an agreement. Adventurer, this way.",
    ["Dialogue8420901"]="That person... wasn't lying.",
    ["Dialogue8420902"]="The one who got us together. He was right. If we make good use of the things there, we can become stronger and realize our vision of martial arts.",
    ["Dialogue8420903"]="Drinking the potions, using those skateboards, buying mech creatures, we need one... No, make it two! Right, how much Zeny do you have now?",
    ["Dialogue8420904"]="(Gazing at the wallet you are holding firmly, Zenlur snorts at you and walks away.)\nIf one cannot become stronger, having all that Zeny is meaningless.",
    ["Dialogue8420905"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>That works for me. Needs not explanation, needs not argument.</color>Now, let's get going. Aren't we heading back?",
    ["Dialogue8421001"]="(Once the aide-de-camp sees you, he walks up to you immediately.)\nYou are back!",
    ["Dialogue8421002"]="Don't worry. They have been transferred to a safe place. There shouldn't be anything like this happening again before the official rally.",
    ["Dialogue8421003"]="That's right, Adventurer. The sole reason I'm here is to form a team of 6. Other than Goldie and Zenlur, <color=#CA2E0AFF>there are four more members unaccounted for.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8421004"]="(After a moment of silence, Syphus shakes his head at you, firmly.)\nSorry, this order is initiated by the royal family and is strictly confidential. I'm not at liberty to discuss this with anyone else, even with a decorated hero like you.",
    ["Dialogue8421005"]="I am afraid not. Ever since they are back to the team, their whereabouts have become the classified information of the kingdom. However, judging by the complexity of Juno's political environment and the urgency of the rally, I'm in desperate need of an <color=#CA2E0AFF>unofficial assistant</color> to deal with all sorts of issues during the rallying.",
    ["Dialogue8421006"]="(Syphus scratches his hair and laughs bitterly.)\nAdventurer, are you willing to help me again? From the military standpoint, they are... being overly undisciplined.",
    ["Dialogue8430101"]="Brave Adventurer, I might have to trouble you again for rallying the team.",
    ["Dialogue8430102"]="This time, we are rallying two people out of the rest four. Due to personal arrangements, they arrived in Juno before us. And we have promised, that we would inform them to return to the team before the task starts. Now it's just the time.",
    ["Dialogue8430103"]="Well, <color=#CA2E0AFF>the male has blond hair, and the female has light-pink hair</color>. You see, not only do they <color=#CA2E0AFF>look attractive, but they are also adept at singing and dancing, and they always perform together</color>. Sigh, they are no troublemakers, but they are too famous, which is not good for completing the tasks.",
    ["Dialogue8430104"]="But, if we are lucky enough, we might run into them in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>busy Commercial District</color>. If that's the case, I will be counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue8430201"]="(The song has ended. Orfeo walks toward you with Trinity.)\nGreetings! What a surprise that we now meet again in Juno! We haven't seen each other ever since the farewell on Comodo. How's it going, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8430202"]="(The bard and the dancer turn their head away embarrassingly, with their hands still holding tight.)\nAhem... After the whole Tao Gunka thing, we both knew the feelings of each other, so...",
    ["Dialogue8430203"]="Trinity, I will be right here protecting you, till the end of the world.",
    ["Dialogue8430204"]="(The love confession from the beloved one is blazing and candid. Trinity looks down at the ground, too shy to make eye contact with Orfeo.)\nMaster...",
    ["Dialogue8430205"]="I apologize. Seemed I could hardly control myself with Trinity around. Anyway, why are you looking for us, Adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue8430206"]="This... It's not that we don't want to keep the promise, but for this trip to Juno, we do have another <color=#CA2E0AFF>equally important matter</color> other than completing the task.",
    ["Dialogue8430207"]="It's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>upcoming Tour Concert</color>. At the moment, the tickets have been sold out for the next session, and we are preparing all sorts of required items for the concert. I'm afraid, that we won't be able to return to the team before the curtain call. Adventurer, performing high-quality shows for the continent has always been our goal, and I hope you and Mr. Syphus can understand this.",
    ["Dialogue8430208"]="(After thinking for a while, Trinity suddenly starts talking.)\nMaster, how about we let Adventurer prepare the items with us? You haven't been sleeping well because of this concert.",
    ["Dialogue8430209"]="But the Adventurer has helped us a lot already...\n(Orfeo looks at you and speaks softly.)\nOn top of that, this is a show for the two of us, and I don't want another person...",
    ["Dialogue8430210"]="Master, I know how you feel. How about...\n(Trinity puts her face next to Orfeo's ear and starts whispering.)",
    ["Dialogue8430211"]="Ahem... Sorry to keep you waiting, and I apologize for excluding you. Now, I officially ask you to help us collect three important items for the show: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno Student Uniform, Old Noble's Outfit of the Republic, and Mechanical Bionic Creatures in various models.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8430212"]="Okay, let me first tell you how to collect them. You can ask the students of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno University's Drama Club</color> to lend you two sets of stage costumes. If you see some youngsters on campus rehearsing with strange outfits, they must be the ones you want to talk to. As for the mecha-bionic creatures, we might have to take some risks...",
    ["Dialogue8430213"]="According to the script, those outdated mecha-bionic creatures are perfect stage props for the show. But something like this... only the <color=#CA2E0AFF>old Lonnis in Exchange Center</color> can get you one of these. Honestly, he is not one of us, so I suggest you take the stuff and leave at once.",
    ["Dialogue8430214"]="(Orfeo laughs softly and plucks the strings on his lute; a lilting little tune flows from his fingertips.)\nBe my guest. No matter how it ends up, we will save a seat for you.",
    ["Dialogue8430301"]="Listen up! The characters we are playing at this time are all outstanding people, great people in the Republic, especially you—\n(The girl at the front points at a teenager with blond hair and blue eyes, and with a glimpse, she catches your presence.)\nYou are?",
    ["Dialogue8430302"]="Y-You mean THE Orfeo and Trinity?! The legendary bard and dancer? Where? Where are they?",
    ["Dialogue8430303"]="What? Are they dating right now? I knew it!!! I knew they would be together the very first time I watched their show! Aha! There goes the next theme for our show!",
    ["Dialogue8430304"]="Calm down, president...",
    ["Dialogue8430305"]="Oh, excuse me... Right, why are you here?",
    ["Dialogue8430306"]="...President, the Adventurer is here to borrow the stage costumes, a set of the student uniform, and a set of old noble's outfits of the Republic.",
    ["Dialogue8430307"]="Oh, I remember it now! But—How do you prove that you are not lying? All of our costumes are expensive; we don't lend them out casually!",
    ["Dialogue8430308"]="(She wags her finger proudly.)\nHehe, how about you <color=#CA2E0AFF>answer a few questions</color>? If you are indeed a friend of the legendary couple, you can get them right undoubtedly!",
    ["Dialogue8430401"]="(The girl pulls out a pen and paper, and takes down your answers while talking to herself.)\nI see... Hmm... Uh-huh... The deduction is slightly off, but the conclusion is basically right...",
    ["Dialogue8430402"]="President...",
    ["Dialogue8430403"]="Finally got the things I need! MAHAHAHA! Huh? Sorry, sorry, two sets of costumes you said? Leave your address, and our logistics robot will deliver them to you!",
    ["Dialogue8430501"]="(The shrewd merchant glances at you with a subtle sweep.)\nAnother bad kid, and a marked-price hater. Aha... You are not from Juno, are you?",
    ["Dialogue8430502"]="Tsk... So the buyers are some sort of artists, huh? I knew there ain't gonna be a big fat check coming in today. I surely have the old stuff, but... I don't take Zeny.",
    ["Dialogue8430503"]="Ever heard of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brown Venatu</color>? I have a customer who is so interested in their parts that he even wants to buy a complete set to put in the living room. Of course, transporting the entire set will definitely put you on the radar of authorities, so...",
    ["Dialogue8430504"]="Bring me a few parts. I need to run a background check on this customer to see whether it's worth the risk. Hehe...",
    ["Dialogue8430505"]="Not a lot. Ten will be good for a starter. Then we'll go bartering: You bring them to me, and I'll give what you want to you.",
    ["Dialogue8430601"]="(An elegant salute from the blond-haired bard)\nAdventurer, we have received all the props. Now, our show is about to begin; I hope you can join us as an honored guest.",
    ["Dialogue8430602"]="Again, thanks for your help.",
    ["Dialogue8430603"]="(Orfeo turns his body sideways, showing you an increasing number of the audience crowded on the street.)\nFor all living ones, there will be a pathfinder in each era.",
    ["Dialogue8430604"]="In the era of human and machinery's coexistence, their pathfinder is named the \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Sage</color>.\" His deeds have been chanted and passed down to this day.",
    ["Dialogue8430605"]="And here I am, a chanter as well.",
    ["Dialogue8430701"]="(Orfeo puts down the lute silently and watches the last audience leaving.)\n...It's over.",
    ["Dialogue8430702"]="(Trinity walks over, picks up the lonely lute, holds it in her chest, and stays with Orfeo without saying a word.)\nMaster...",
    ["Dialogue8430703"]="Don't worry about me, Trinity.\n(Orfeo touches the girl's silky hair.)\nI'm fine. It's just whenever a show is over, that I wish the time could be paused at that exact moment.",
    ["Dialogue8430704"]="Master, we still...",
    ["Dialogue8430705"]="I remember.\n(Orfeo then turns to you, who has been waiting on the side.)\nSo, even though we couldn't care less about the royal family and politics, we should be heading back with you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8430706"]="Sign... Adventurer, maybe it's hard for someone like you, who leaves your footprints at every corner of the continent, to understand our difficulty— It's nice to live in seclusion, but that's no good for gathering materials to pursue your path of art.",
    ["Dialogue8430707"]="Think about it. Even if you are on Kokomo Beach, after you watch the tides go up and down, and witness the sun rise and set, for thousands of times, you will soon realize, that it won't be able to wake up your numbed sensation. Without material and creation, a bard is nothing but a slave of the void.",
    ["Dialogue8430708"]="Trinity, if <color=#CA2E0AFF>this Juno trip could really provide some best material for the wedding ceremony</color>, as Mr. Syphus has said, then we don't have a reason to turn it down.",
    ["Dialogue8430709"]="Master, I don't really care...",
    ["Dialogue8430710"]="(Orfeo shakes his head gently.)\nBut I want to provide you with the best. Trinity, you are worth it.",
    ["Dialogue8430711"]="Master...",
    ["Dialogue8430712"]="(Orfeo is tranced at first and becomes shy suddenly.)\nAdventurer, seems I forgot to tell you.",
    ["Dialogue8430713"]="(He holds up the hand of his fiancée and kisses her ring finger.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Me and Trinity are about to get married.</color>",
    ["Dialogue8440101"]="(Under the astonished eyes of the crowd, the stubbly-bearded aide-de-camp is pulling his hair, again and again.)\nO MY ODIN, why me? Why am I the one rallying these troublemakers...",
    ["Dialogue8440102"]="Here you are, sigh...\n(Syphus pats you on the shoulder.)\nAdventurer, if those two can be remotely as punctual as you, we could've set off two days ago.",
    ["Dialogue8440103"]="I can't believe it! They are exchange students in the KINGDOM, who have been told the FINAL rally time. But now, no one has shown up yet! I... I don't know why someone like <color=#CA2E0AFF>Celia</color>, an infamous unruly girl in Geffen, could be chosen to carry out the secret mission!",
    ["Dialogue8440104"]="I trust you with your integrity.\n(Syphus rubs the dark circles around his eyes and lets out a deep breath.)\nAs a servant of the kingdom, I shouldn't question the Lord's judgment. But as a person in their right mind, I choose to retain my opinion.",
    ["Dialogue8440105"]="Adventurer, I want you to go to Juno University and bring back the last two members, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Celia and Pierre</color>. Our expected departure date has been postponed again and again, and the higher office is urging me and my boss to complete the task. So, if they show any signs of backtracking or refuse to come with you, don't be pushy. Just deliver this message to them, on behalf of my superior.",
    ["Dialogue8440106"]="\"Backing out of a promise comes with a consequence.\" Since they have accepted the benefits of the kingdom, they must be held accountable when breaking the promise.",
    ["Dialogue8440201"]="(Inside the library, Celia is sitting still in the middle of passed-out students, a hardcover book with a hot stamping cover laying on her knees.)\nWeird... It looks like a normal book to me. No problem with its paper and content, and there are no traces of <color=#CA2E0AFF>dizzying magic</color>...",
    ["Dialogue8440202"]="Could it be that the sample pool is too small?\n(Ivy kicks a passed-out student in the face with the tip of his boot, but the student seems dead as a doornail.)\nHey, wake up... Tsk, what a weakling.",
    ["Dialogue8440203"]="Celia, I will be back in no time. As for you guys...\n(Ivy pulls out a potion and starts to fiddle with it in front of the trembling students.)\nIf you try to run, then this precious antidote will— KA-BOOM! Not even a drop left.",
    ["Dialogue8440204"]="Antidote? Ivy, aren't these people volunteers?\n(Celia looks at Ivy confusingly, making a big Cross in the air with her both arms.)\nEven though it's hard to find volunteers, you can't force people into it. Never!",
    ["Dialogue8440205"]="(Skeptically, Celia bends down and touches a student's burning forehead; her limpid eyes are filled with worries.)\nAre you okay? It's alright if you want to quit. Volunteers are absolutely free to go!",
    ["Dialogue8440206"]="Then... Then I'll quit...",
    ["Dialogue8440207"]="Huh?",
    ["Dialogue8440208"]="Back off! I am a volunteer! Let me do it!",
    ["Dialogue8440209"]="(Celia's eyes light up immediately, and she drags the student to the book in a rush.)\nThat's great! As long as we have enough samples, I can log down a more comprehensive reading reaction to examine the cause. Get on it now!",
    ["Dialogue8440210"]="Adventurer? Why are you here? Wait... If you are here, does it mean Zen—",
    ["Dialogue8440211"]="Humph! They're only here to stop us, I'm afraid.\n(Ivy squeezes in between you and Celia and stops the conversation.)\nAdventurer, your voice is loud. Is it because you want to volunteer yourself?",
    ["Dialogue8440212"]="Huh? You wanna help? Speaking of which, Adventurer helped me a lot while collecting the samples of Poring back in Geffen.",
    ["Dialogue8440213"]="Oh? So the two of you know each other back in Geffen?\n(Ivy gives you a \"twisted\" smile that has nothing to do with a smile.)\nIn this case, I believe the Adventurer must be willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help us again</color>, right?",
    ["Dialogue8440214"]="This book, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno University: Some School History...</color>\n(He turns to the title page and hands over the book to you. With only a glance of it, the texts start to pierce into your mind like a sharp blade.)\nThis book might get you dizzy if you read it too long, but I think our Adventurer will be just fine!",
    ["Dialogue8440301"]="Are you awake? There you go, the Successor of Odin's Bloodline!\n(Celia wags two fingers in front of your eyes, while Ivy, with a regretful look on the side, seems to be hiding something.)\nWhat's the number here?",
    ["Dialogue8440302"]="Alright, alright! Since you are awake, I need you to tell me everything you saw!\n(Celia readies her pen and paper quickly.)\nOkay, start talking! I'm ready!",
    ["Dialogue8440303"]="Are you telling me you weren't seeing anything? How's that possible? You pulled out your weapon in front of us just now! How could the renowned Successor of Odin's Bloodline be a sleepwalker?",
    ["Dialogue8440304"]="Also, you are here to take me and Pierre back to the team, right? Humph! If you don't tell me whatever happened there, or if I failed to solve the mystery of this book, then—<size=26><color=#CA2E0AFF>I WILL NEVER GO BACK!!!</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue8440401"]="Marionette, Nightmare, Disguise... All of them are monsters of Ghost attribute...\n(Celia quickly lists out various details of these three monsters on the paper.)\nI recall there was a powerful magic spell, which is primarily in Ghost attribute...",
    ["Dialogue8440402"]="Yes! It's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic of Confusion</color>! Adventurer, which page were you reading when you passed out?",
    ["Dialogue8440403"]="Celia is saying that the page that makes you pass out has been cast with a powerful Magic of Confusion. If we can locate the page, then we are not far away from solving the mystery.",
    ["Dialogue8440404"]="Interesting, even Juno University has its shady parts...",
    ["Dialogue8440405"]="(Ivy looks at the silent library, then chuckles suddenly.)\nCelia, when we solve this, you'll be holding something on those old bones in the school office.",
    ["Dialogue8440406"]="By then, not only will they revoke all your disciplinary punishments, but you can also ask for more academy resources easily.",
    ["Dialogue8440407"]="Huh? Why would I want them revoked? I did do those things. Moreover, the professor thinks of me whenever something is going on!",
    ["Dialogue8440408"]="But those records will blemish your transcript. Celia, do you want to become the exchange student with the most disciplinary records in the kingdom's history?",
    ["Dialogue8440409"]="You...\n(Celia frowns and stares Ivy in the eye.)\nYou want to erase whatever you have done and then hide yourself in the shadows? What a wacko.",
    ["Dialogue8440410"]="I...\n(Ivy apparently becomes nervous and realizes you are there, watching them talking all along.)\nAdventurer, you haven't said which page it is!",
    ["Dialogue8440411"]="Page 374? Let me see...\n(Celia ends the topic unconcernedly, walks past Ivy, and beckons you to hand her the book.)",
    ["Dialogue8440412"]="Hold on!\n(Ivy stops Celia, who is about the turn the page. He blushes faintly when touching her hand.)\nN-No! You can't open it like this! The Wakeup Potion... Yes! Adventurer, I need you to help me <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some materials to make the Wakeup Potion</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8440413"]="Give it back! Ivy!",
    ["Dialogue8440414"]="(Ivy seizes the school history book and tries to reason with the furious Celia.)\nListen to me, Celia! The Magic of Confusion is a powerful spell; it attacks your mentality. If you don't use the Wakeup Potion before opening the book, the only thing waiting for you is madness!",
    ["Dialogue8440415"]="We need <color=#CA2E0AFF>Menblatt's Sleepless Flower, Rafflesia's Dream-Shatter Grass, and Marin's Fixation Crystal</color>. I'm counting on you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8440416"]="As for you guys...\n(Ivy seems to find himself a more interesting thing to toy with, and carelessly tosses the precious antidote to the students.)\nIn ten seconds, I want every one of you out of my face.",
    ["Dialogue8440417"]="Huh?",
    ["Dialogue8440501"]="This is...?\n(A thin piece of paper is being checked repeatedly by Celia, but nothing seems out of place.)\nOnly one sentence?",
    ["Dialogue8440502"]="I don't get it...\n(Celia keeps mumbling with terms you don't understand and scratching her blonde hair.)",
    ["Dialogue8440503"]="This is just a simple statement of fact in the library... Even if I burn all the books in the library into ashes... It's still a true statement...",
    ["Dialogue8440504"]="Could there be any book that I haven't read here? No, it's impossible. Except for this one, which popped up out of nowhere, I've read the rest of them. All of them!",
    ["Dialogue8440505"]="No! There must be something that I am unaware of... <color=#CA2E0AFF>A reason worthy enough to make someone use the Magic of Confusion to hide it in the school history</color>... What could it be?",
    ["Dialogue8440506"]="(After zoning out momentarily, Celia gives you a guilty look.)\n...Adventurer, can I break the promise?",
    ["Dialogue8440507"]="Sigh... But it's boring with Pierre. He washes his hands ten times a day, reads books in alphabetical order, and even eats the main dish and side dish separately!... I really don't want to work with him...",
    ["Dialogue8440508"]="(As soon as Celia hears the name <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenlur</color>, she grabs you by the arm, and her eyes start blinking.)\nR-Really?",
    ["Dialogue8440509"]="Ah... Sorry! I couldn't help myself...\n(Celia tugs at the hem of her skirt with a blushed face.)\nThen, let's get going. Shall we?",
    ["Dialogue8440510"]="Ahem-Ahem! Adventurer, I need to speak with you in <color=#CA2E0AFF>private</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8440601"]="I need the truth. Adventurer, what exactly are you guys doing?",
    ["Dialogue8440602"]="It's fine if you want to keep it to yourself. But how can you not count me in on an exciting trip like this?\n(Ivy's playful look turns into a cold stare.)\nAnyway, I want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go on the trip with you guys in place of Pierre</color>. This is not a request. It's an order.",
    ["Dialogue8440603"]="No?\n(Ivy gives you an innocent look; his green eyes look like hazy emeralds.)\nBut, I heard that Pierre is sick all of a sudden. At the moment, he can't even get up from bed.",
    ["Dialogue8440604"]="Yeah, that's right. It happens tomorrow, no, I mean today. I just received the message, poor Pierre.",
    ["Dialogue8440605"]="I don't like to be rejected... except by Celia.\n(Step by step, you are forced into a corner by Ivy. He then puts his face next to you and speaks in devil's tongue.)\nKindhearted Adventurer, I don't think you want to see Pierre <size=26>getting sicker</size>, do you?",
    ["Dialogue8440701"]="If you want to take me back to the team, then tell me the monsters you saw in the illusion <color=#CA2E0AFF>in sequence</color>. I heard there were a lot of people who encountered <color=#CA2E0AFF>scary dolls, spectral horses, and masked ghosts</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8440702"]="How about we choose <color=#CA2E0AFF>Marionette</color> first?",
    ["Dialogue8440703"]="The doll is so cute! Hehe, maybe I can send the photo to my toy designer friend. He will have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"sweet dream\"</color> after receiving it!",
    ["Dialogue8440704"]="I don't believe the nightmare can actually devastate your sleep. I was the one who had the soundest sleep at the Halloween <color=#CA2E0AFF>Masquerade</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8440705"]="Hmm... Seems we are one step closer to the truth...",
    ["Dialogue8440706"]="I have no clues... Let's try again.",
    ["Dialogue8450101"]="(The bulky aide-de-camp waves at you; it looks like he's in better shape now.)\nAdventurer, we meet again!",
    ["Dialogue8450102"]="Yes, but this might be the last time we meet in Juno. The Dispatch Team has set off on a quest, and my boss orders me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the kingdom and report back</color> immediately. Adventurer, things wouldn't go so smoothly if it weren't for your help!",
    ["Dialogue8450103"]="This...\n(Syphus frowns for a while, as if considering whether to tell the truth.)\nAdventurer, you always surprise me with your determination.",
    ["Dialogue8450104"]="I've never doubted your attitude... But I don't know if this is a good place to continue our talk.",
    ["Dialogue8450105"]="Yes, since the quest has been completed, I think you have <color=#CA2E0AFF>part of the right</color> to know the truth, especially since you've helped the royal family on multiple occasions. And with the information I have, it won't be a long conversation even if I reveal everything to you. Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>please follow me</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8450201"]="Here should be fine.\n(Syphus takes out a secret letter from his chest pocket.)\nThis is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rally Order issued by the royal family to the team</color>. It also points out their quest objective.",
    ["Dialogue8450202"]="According to the schedule, the team, along with backup members, should have secretly arrived at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8450203"]="Shhh—\n(Syphus gives you a shush gesture, directing your eyes towards the Lord's Mansion, which is heavily surrounded by Rekenber Guards.)\nThis name is not what you want to mention in Juno.",
    ["Dialogue8450204"]="Those guys prefer to call their headquarters—<color=#CA2E0AFF>The City-State of Prosperity</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8450205"]="SHHHHH—Sigh… Adventurer, read the secret order first.",
    ["Dialogue8450301"]="Judging by the look on your face, you are quite familiar with the people on the list, aren't you?",
    ["Dialogue8450302"]="I bet you are, Adventurer. These missing contacts are all very important talents to the royal family. Even if they are trapped abroad, we must rescue them.",
    ["Dialogue8450303"]="This... To be honest, my boss only told me to rally the team for the rescue mission. About the reason why they went missing, I <color=#CA2E0AFF>have no knowledge</color>, either.",
    ["Dialogue8450304"]="(Syphus pats you on the shoulder.)\nDon't worry. My boss chose the team members personally, and this mission is just another chance for them to showcase their skills. If everything goes as planned, they will be back with the missing contacts, safe and sound.",
    ["Dialogue8450305"]="Okay, so much for the talk. It's time for me to head back. Adventurer, after everything we've been through, do you want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a photo with me before the airship</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8450401"]="Hmm... That's a good one! Now, I'm going to take a nap on the airship. When I reach the kingdom, I'll be the handsome me again!",
    ["Dialogue8450402"]="Sure thing! But everything about the Dispatch Team has been marked as top secret. Even the members were told to investigate the case in the dark. For the sake of the mission, Adventurer, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep your lips sealed</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8450403"]="Then, my salute to you again. Let's meet in the Rune Kingdom!",
    ["Dialogue8460101"]="Time's ticking!!! Where on earth are you, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shana</color>?! The chief editor has told me, if you don't show up now, you are getting no Zeny next month!",
    ["Dialogue8460102"]="And you are? Well, never mind. Even if Shana's not here, I'm gonna follow through with this event anyway. <color=#CA2E0AFF>This is Rekenber's new product release conference! The headline of tomorrow's Libet Express!</color> If I screw it up, I can go find an airship and dive down without a parachute!",
    ["Dialogue8460103"]="You have no idea? You... Aren't you a reporter?",
    ["Dialogue8460104"]="Hmm...\n(Enchulo pondered for a moment, and suddenly, his eyes lit up. He grabs your arm and tries to squeeze into the crowd.)\nFollow me! Since Shana is not here, you'll do the shooting job!",
    ["Dialogue8460105"]="Relax! Don't panic! Just point your camera at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Irumina</color> when you get there. Don't take anything else. They are worthless anyway!",
    ["Dialogue8460106"]="Y—You... You don't even know Irumina? Pardon me, the god of journalism... Why am I picking this uncivilized barbarian to be my photographer...",
    ["Dialogue8460107"]="Er... I mean, your muscles are impressive! Carrying a tripod should be no problem for you! Now, listen up! Irumina is by far <color=#CA2E0AFF>the most popular mechanic, period! She's also the spokesperson for Rekenber's full range of products</color>! The women in our office, and our female readers, are all crazy for her!",
    ["Dialogue8460108"]="So, amateur, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>take enough photos from multiple angles for me to choose</color>.\n(Enchulo straightens his back, pounding his chest with pride.)\nOnly the best photos are worthy of being featured in my article, Enchulo Kasen's article! Now follow me!",
    ["Dialogue8460201"]="(A female mechanic with alluring androgynous charm helps you to your feet.)\nBeing overly passionate can get you hurt, young reporter.",
    ["Dialogue8460202"]="(With a graceful smile, Irumina brings you to the podium. The enthusiastic cheering sound immediately engulfs you two.)\nHowever, I like passionate people. If those researchers in Rekenber could be more passionate about their work, they would develop more satisfying products.",
    ["Dialogue8460203"]="Well, my passionate friend from the mass media industry, do I have the honor to invite you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>experience the interactive system newly developed by Rekenber</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8460204"]="Me!!! Ms. Irumina!!! Pick me!!!",
    ["Dialogue8460205"]="Pick me!!! Ms. Irumina!!! I WILL DO IT!!!",
    ["Dialogue8460206"]="(As the sound waves become increasingly intense toward the podium, there seems to be a slight annoyance in Irumina's smiley purple eyes. It could be just an illusion though.)\nMy friend, are you turning down my invitation?",
    ["Dialogue8460207"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>YES!!!</color>Your support for Libet Express is much appreciated!!!\n(Enchulo winks at you crazily from the audience.)\nAren't you the one who insisted on meeting Irumina? What now? Feeling light-headed?",
    ["Dialogue8460208"]="...Ha, you have a very concerned \"mentor.\" Don't worry, the new model is a smart kid. All you need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>approach it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8460301"]="(The tall and menacing mech creature lowers its head, docilely rubbing against its master.)\nGood... Good... Now let's say hi to our friends from various media. Soon after, you will be serving the archaeological team sponsored by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Khayr Consortium</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8460302"]="What? May I ask if there will be an in-depth collaboration between Khayr Consortium and your company in the near future?",
    ["Dialogue8460303"]="What makes the two commercial giants in the Republic join hands with each other? Any insider news?",
    ["Dialogue8460304"]="I heard that President Khayr is still unconscious. Is there any hidden agenda behind the collaboration?",
    ["Dialogue8460305"]="(Irumina gives out a flawless smile. In an instant, the entire venue falls silent, captivated by her charm.)\nEveryone, I understand your feeling, but please hear me out.",
    ["Dialogue8460306"]="(Irumina slightly adjusts her voice and tone. You are also holding your doubts, waiting for her response.)\nIndeed, President Khayr's illness has made a huge impact on the consortium's operation. As a partner, we sincerely wish him to get well as soon as possible.",
    ["Dialogue8460307"]="But to the best of my knowledge, President Khayr had already entrusted the board to take all business affairs before he went into a coma. In other words, the collaboration this time has received unanimous approval from the board of the consortium. Please, if I may say so, let the speculation stops here.",
    ["Dialogue8460308"]="Thanks to the trust and faith of President Khayr and the board, we were able to jointly accomplish something of great significance to Rekenber before the grievous news hit us—",
    ["Dialogue8460309"]="Ladies and gentlemen, allow me to proudly make the announcement: With the consent of President Kiel Khayr and his board of directors, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp has completed the acquisition of the Khayr Consortium</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8460310"]="OK. That's all for the conference. We can take some souvenir photos shortly after. Please take your time. Aha, young reporter, are you leaving now?",
    ["Dialogue8460311"]="Of course not!\n(Enchulo, under the podium, instantly raises his camera and points the lens to you.)\nMs. Irumina, <color=#CA2E0AFF>please look this way</color>!",
    ["Dialogue8460401"]="Shana!\n(Enchulo frowns in anger, shaking his female partner's shoulders vigorously.)\nLet me get this straight, the reason you skipped your work was to get an autograph from Irumina???",
    ["Dialogue8460402"]="Yep! Look at this!\n(The petite female reporter holds up the autographed photo and spins around.)\nTell you what! If you can't score a proper picture for your article, this photo should do the trick!",
    ["Dialogue8460403"]="Hmph! Even without a picture, my article—Enchulo's article—is still worth a fortune! I suggest you start making up excuses for your no-show. I don't have any Zeny to spare before I get my paycheck.",
    ["Dialogue8460404"]="Eh... Is it too late for me to start the photo shoot now?\n(Shana stares at the floor with guilty.)\nSorry... I didn't mean to...",
    ["Dialogue8460405"]="Stop playing innocent. Fortunately, I got myself a backup photographer. Adventurer, where are your <color=#CA2E0AFF>photos</color>?",
    ["Dialogue8460501"]="Gosh, can't even find one good photo out of all these. Should I be surprised, or comforted for having anticipated such an outcome? Sigh, lucky for me to have a plan B.",
    ["Dialogue8460502"]="I made up my mind when I was in the crowd: I'll personally take a photo of you and Irumina and put it in my article. Consider yourself lucky, amateur. This will be Tomorrow's Headline.",
    ["Dialogue8460503"]="(Enchulo isn't answering your question. Instead, he wants you and Shana to take a look at the photos in his camera.)\nShana, do you see it?",
    ["Dialogue8460504"]="Ms. Irumina in this photo... Seems to be more handsome?\n",
    ["Dialogue8460505"]="Oh, please! It's more <color=#CA2E0AFF>realistic...</color>\n(Enchulo helplessly rolls his eyes.)\nShana, I can't believe how slow you are on the uptake.",
    ["Dialogue8460506"]="Hmm... Hmm... Let me see it again... Ah! I get it now!",
    ["Dialogue8460507"]="You... You are the lucky one around whose shoulders Irumina put her arm! AHHHHHHHH! I AM BUYING YOUR JACKET! Take my wallet and all my Zeny! Please! Sell it to me!",
    ["Dialogue8460601"]="Listen, each photo has to be reviewed carefully. I'm looking for a front-facing photo that is clear and has a proper angle.",
    ["Dialogue8460602"]="Hmm... The <color=#CA2E0AFF>first one</color> looks pretty good. It got a <color=#CA2E0AFF>close-up</color> shot of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Irumina</color> and that giant <color=#CA2E0AFF>robot</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8460603"]="Nah, let's check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second one</color>. It's important to capture the reaction of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>audience below the podium</color> as well.",
    ["Dialogue8460604"]="This angle is horrible... And why in the world am I in this photo? Give the <color=#CA2E0AFF>third one</color> to me. Yes, the one with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Irumina</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>securities</color>, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>giant robot</color>.",
    ["Dialogue8460605"]="You've done well. Leave the rest to me.",
    ["Dialogue8460606"]="My thought has been disrupted by your <color=#CA2E0AFF>unorderly sequence</color> of picking photos. Let's do it again.",
    ["Dialogue8460607"]="Good. I'm glad that you have a basic sense of aesthetics as a photographer.",
    ["Dialogue8460608"]="This is trash. What makes you think it fits my article?",
    ["Dialogue8470101"]="Adventurer, tell me honestly—where was Goldie taken?",
    ["Dialogue8470102"]="Not long ago, an officer came here. He took Goldie away and even left a hefty payment. No doubt someone's buying her life. Considering your ties with the kingdom, Adventurer, you must know something... or maybe, you're involved too?",
    ["Dialogue8470103"]="(Watching you say nothing, Hassan sighs deeply.)\n... Fine. If you won't talk, I can guess the rest. It was her choice—I've no right to interfere. But could you do me... no, could you do Goldie a favor?",
    ["Dialogue8470104"]="Exactly. You know that camp outside the Orc Village was built by Goldie herself. Since she left, other factions have been eyeing it greedily. I want you to check things out, they might need your help.",
    ["Dialogue8470105"]="(Hassan gives a bitter smile and shakes his head.)\n... I tried, of course. But Goldie's team is just as stubborn as she is. They yelled that they'd never work with assassins and kicked my people out. I had no other choice but to ask you.",
    ["Dialogue8470106"]="I know you're close with Goldie. She trusts you. If you truly see her as a friend, you won't turn me down, right?",
    ["Dialogue8470201"]="Everyone, stand straight! Look at you all—what a bunch of rogues!",
    ["Dialogue8470202"]="Huh... but, Ebel, we are rogues, aren't we?",
    ["Dialogue8470203"]="Shut up!\nYou're driving me crazy! If Goldie finds out about today, you'll be tossed into the orc arena as punching bags!",
    ["Dialogue8470204"]="Adventurer! Perfect timing! Let me tell you, these rookies are pathetic—they got scared off by a bunch of Orc Babies during patrol! Before Goldie gets back, I need to whip them into shape with some hardcore training, or else...",
    ["Dialogue8470205"]="Hey, little Ebel—\n(A voice calls out, interrupting Ebel. An old man waves from a nearby tent.)\nCan you come take a look over here?",
    ["Dialogue8470206"]="Ah! Uncle Heisen, hang on, I'll be right there!\nUgh... what do I do now...",
    ["Dialogue8470207"]="W-would you help me train them?!",
    ["Dialogue8470208"]="That's the spirit!\n(Ebel slaps you hard on the back twice, which kinda hurts.)\nNo wonder Goldie's friends with you!",
    ["Dialogue8470209"]="Alright, they're all yours! Don't go easy on them—show them what a legendary Adventurer is made of!",
    ["Dialogue8470301"]="(As soon as Ebel leaves, the rookies slack off completely and start chatting.)\nWhew, finally done... Let's just call it a day, huh? We've been patrolling all night, I'm dead tired...",
    ["Dialogue8470302"]="Let's grab something to eat, I'm starving!",
    ["Dialogue8470303"]="Sure, mushrooms or berries? Supplies are low in the camp lately. Maybe we could catch a few fish by the river for dinner...",
    ["Dialogue8470304"]="(As you shout, the rookies look at each other. You can tell they don't take you seriously.)\nYou're not seriously gonna spar with us, are you?",
    ["Dialogue8470305"]="Interesting... Hey! Nobody move!\n(A young man steps forward, clearly the leader of the rookies.)\nMake your move!",
    ["Dialogue8470401"]="Wait, wait—okay, we give up! You win! Who are you, anyway? Ebel said you're a famous Adventurer and close with Goldie, but...\n(After a moment of thinking, he suddenly looks up, shocked.)\nYou—you're that Odin bloodline...?!",
    ["Dialogue8470402"]="S-sorry!\n(He bows so fast and pushes his teammates' heads down too.)\nWe didn't know who we were messing with!",
    ["Dialogue8470403"]="Yes, sir!!! Thanks for the lesson!!!",
    ["Dialogue8470404"]="Well, well! Looks like the training paid off!\n(Ebel hurries back to you, having finished helping the old man.)\nKnew I could count on you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue8470405"]="Sorry to ask again, but I've got another request. This morning, Jud led a group escorting a doctor to the Goblin Forest for herbs, but I just got word they were attacked by monsters and trapped near the Flail-wielding Goblin tribe. The monsters aren't particularly strong, but their numbers are overwhelming. Jud's team might not be able to hold out alone...",
    ["Dialogue8470406"]="(Ebel nods.)\nSorry, Adventurer. The camp's short-staffed, and Goldie's away. I really can't leave right now... could you go for me?",
    ["Dialogue8470501"]="Thanks for the help, Adventurer. Without you, we'd probably be stuck here out of supplies... Did Ebel send you?",
    ["Dialogue8470502"]="Yeah, we came to collect herbs, but those annoying goblins trapped us here. Normally I'd have brought more people, but lately...\n(He sighs softly, lowering his head.)\nThe herbs are still out of reach, and some of my men are hurt. I've failed as a captain.",
    ["Dialogue8470503"]="Captain Jud, don't say that. If I hadn't been greedy for those rare herbs, you wouldn't have risked coming into the Flail-wielding Goblin territory.",
    ["Dialogue8470504"]="At the roots of that big tree nearby. You'll have to cross the Flail-wielding Goblin territory to get there.",
    ["Dialogue8470601"]="Let me thank you again, Adventurer. With these herbs, the camp can hold out a little longer.",
    ["Dialogue8470602"]="But, Captain, Haglis' gang keeps causing trouble lately. Our guys get hurt all the time, and we're running out of medicine and even bandages! Now that Goldie's gone, we—",
    ["Dialogue8470603"]="(Jud raises his hand, stopping him.)\nEnough with the gloom! Have you forgotten Goldie's words before she left? Until she's back... no matter what happens, we protect the camp!",
    ["Dialogue8470604"]="They're another gang we've been fighting over territory with. Haglis is their leader. Honestly, I was wondering earlier that Flail-wielding Goblins aren't normally aggressive. If we'd been careful, we could've passed through their territory safely. So I checked the ones you defeated... and found this.",
    ["Dialogue8470605"]="(Jud pulls a small pouch of white powder from his pocket.)\nFound this on them. The doctor ran a quick test, and it turns out it's mixed with stuff that makes monsters go berserk.",
    ["Dialogue8470606"]="Goldie looked into this before, and she found out Haglis used it to control monster tribes around Geffen, making them attack trade caravans. Then, he'd swoop in pretending to save them, charging a rescue fee. Goldie had a plan to raid his drug lab, but before we could move... that officer showed up... and took her away.",
    ["Dialogue8470607"]="Before leaving, Goldie told me not to act rashly and to keep the camp safe. She said we'd deal with Haglis when she got back... only, she never said when that would be.",
    ["Dialogue8470608"]="You... you're really gonna help us?\n(Jud looks shocked.)\nBut... why?",
    ["Dialogue8470609"]="... Got it. Come with me, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue8470701"]="(The footprints are clear—too clear that it's almost like someone wanted you to find them...)",
    ["Dialogue8470801"]="(The footprints are just as clear as before, clearly staged. White powder scatters around them, leading onward as if luring you to keep following...)",
    ["Dialogue8470901"]="Alright, now... shall we talk about these drugs, Haglis?",
    ["Dialogue8470902"]="Bah! Now that bitchy Goldie's gone—you punks think you can start eyeing my turf? My men'll have you—uh! Cough, cough...",
    ["Dialogue8470903"]="(Haglis' rant is cut short as Jud punches him in the stomach.)\nShow some respect to our leader, Haglis. Want me to teach you some manners?",
    ["Dialogue8470904"]="You... you won't last long! More folks will hear of Goldie's death and your turf will get split up. Better join me now—if I'm feeling generous, I might toss you a meal!",
    ["Dialogue8470905"]="... Thanks, but you don't need to get your hands dirty, Adventurer. Would you mind running back to the camp for me? Ask Ebel to go to the Goblin Forest to fetch the doctor and the wounded, then send people here to clean this up?",
    ["Dialogue8470906"]="(Jud flexes his wrist, staring down at Haglis on the ground.)\nAs for me... I'll stick around and have a little chat with this guy. Let's see where he hid the rest of those drugs.",
    ["Dialogue8471001"]="(Ebel waves at you while juggling a bunch of wrenches.)\nHey, Adventurer! You're back? Where's Jud and the others?",
    ["Dialogue8471002"]="What—really? You captured Haglis? That's a surprise!\n(Ebel's eyes widen in shock.)\nGot it, don't worry. I'll finish up here and head out to bring them back myself!",
    ["Dialogue8471003"]="Oh, this is nothing! When Goldie was around, she handled everything herself. Before she left, she made me promise a hundred times to take care of everyone... I bet she never imagined I'd end up fixing water pumps, huh?",
    ["Dialogue8471004"]="Most of us here were picked up by Goldie. She protected us, cared for us, gave us a home... protecting it just feels natural, doesn't it?",
    ["Dialogue8471005"]="(With a loud clack, Ebel shuts her toolbox, wipes her sweat, and smiles at you.)\nAlright then, I'll go pick up Jud and the others! Thanks for all your help today, Adventurer! When Goldie's back, we're throwing her a big welcome party—you're coming too, okay?",
    ["Dialogue8480101"]="(Benjamin peeks out from behind a crate, waving you over.)\nPsst, Adventurer—over here! You're heading to see Captain Drake, right? Is it... about Cecil?",
    ["Dialogue8480102"]="(The old pirate's expression turns sorrowful as you remain silent.)\nSo it's true then... Cecil, she's really...?",
    ["Dialogue8480103"]="The rumor's been going around for a while. People say that the bounty hunter who hunts pirates hasn't shown up in ages, and some even think she's dead... Even in the Gangash Pirates, gossip spread fast. Spencer and I tried to shut it down, but word still reached Captain Drake...",
    ["Dialogue8480104"]="(Benjamin sighs heavily.)\nI know... The captain never says it, but he's been worrying about Cecil all this time. It's taken a toll on his health. I can hear him coughing his lungs out late at night...",
    ["Dialogue8480105"]="I still remember... I saw him dig Cecil out from the ruins with his own hands. He tried everything to keep her alive... I—I just can't stand to see this...",
    ["Dialogue8480106"]="Adventurer, please... don't tell the captain about Cecil yet. At least not until he's feeling better...",
    ["Dialogue8480107"]="—You two! What are you talking about? Cecil's dead?",
    ["Dialogue8480201"]="Benjamin—say that again.\n(The old captain grips the pistol at his waist, his hand trembling.)\nCecil... is she dead?",
    ["Dialogue8480202"]="C-Captain, please, calm down! Just... hear me out...\n(Benjamin shoots you a desperate look—you can tell he wants you to help calm Drake down.)",
    ["Dialogue8480203"]="... You're brave, Adventurer. Thank you for being honest. She...",
    ["Dialogue8480204"]="... Don't bother lying, Adventurer. I already had a feeling... I was ready for it. She...",
    ["Dialogue8480205"]="(After a long silence, you can tell Drake wants to say a lot—but in the end, he just clenches his fists and asks a simple question.)\nCecil... did she have any last wishes?",
    ["Dialogue8480206"]="... To have her longbow buried in her hometown? I see... cough, cough\n(A storm of coughs forces Drake to bend over.)",
    ["Dialogue8480207"]="Captain! Sit down—please! I'll go grab your medicine right now!",
    ["Dialogue8480208"]="No... get a ship ready. Send a few men to escort the Adventurer to Cecil's hometown. You know where it is, Benjamin.",
    ["Dialogue8480209"]="(Drake lifts his head, staring at the sea chart on the wall.)\n... I've been there many times over the years. But it'll never look the way it did when I first saw it...",
    ["Dialogue8480301"]="Hey, Mr. Mead! Where are you going this early?",
    ["Dialogue8480302"]="Just grabbing some stuff to patch the wall at home. It's got a hole big enough to walk through now.",
    ["Dialogue8480303"]="The wall's broken already? Didn't they just finish building those houses a few years back?",
    ["Dialogue8480304"]="Yeah, those who build with greed instead of care—never once have they brought peace of mind!",
    ["Dialogue8480401"]="Drake, I want candy!",
    ["Dialogue8480402"]="You already had some today. No more, or Mom will scold me again.",
    ["Dialogue8480403"]="I don't care! I want it! If you don't buy me candy, I'll cry!",
    ["Dialogue8480404"]="Hahaha, look at this kid!",
    ["Dialogue8480501"]="So this is your determination, Cecil?\n(Drake sneers, crushing the old wooden bow beneath his boot.)\nYou call this piece of junk your proof?",
    ["Dialogue8480502"]="If not today, then tomorrow! If not tomorrow, then the next!\n(Tears well up in Cecil's eyes, but she refuses to bow her head.)\nOne day, I'll make you pay for everything you've done!",
    ["Dialogue8480503"]="Hah... not bad. Let's see if you can back up that talk.\n(With a clang, a beautiful longbow lands before Cecil—you realize it's the same bow she later entrusted to you...)",
    ["Dialogue8480504"]="Go on—draw it. Aim right at my heart. But this isn't your little wooden toy. Think those scrawny arms can handle it, kid?",
    ["Dialogue8480505"]="You bastard! I'll kill you—!\n(Through Drake's mocking laughter, Cecil grabs the bow, straining with all her strength, but the string won't budge. You realize... she's not yet the fearsome bounty hunter she'll one day become.)",
    ["Dialogue8480506"]="Why... why can't I draw it?! I've trained so hard for this!",
    ["Dialogue8480507"]="Darn it!!!",
    ["Dialogue8480601"]="Sigh... Drake, it's been years. Why not tell her the truth? Cecil's not a kid anymore—maybe she'd understand!",
    ["Dialogue8480602"]="That longbow... from picking the wood to stringing it... You poured your heart into it. Don't think I don't know—it was supposed to be Cecil's coming-of-age gift! I've never seen a father and daughter as stubborn as you two!",
    ["Dialogue8480603"]="(Watching Cecil's back as she walks away, Drake just chuckles bitterly and shakes his head.)\nEnough, Benjamin. How's that thing I asked you to look into?",
    ["Dialogue8480604"]="Don't worry. Spencer's handled everything. Anyone trying to traffic kids on Gangash Pirates' turf will find themselves ending up in a shark's stomach!",
    ["Dialogue8480605"]="Good. Let's head back to the ship... and send someone to keep an eye on Cecil. Don't let her do anything reckless.",
    ["Dialogue8480606"]="Aye, captain.",
    ["Dialogue8480701"]="(Seeing the little girl stop crying, Cecil breathes a sigh of relief.)\nThank goodness... finally stopped crying. Where are your parents? I'll help you find them.",
    ["Dialogue8480702"]="... My parents? I don't know... They took me to the market, but there were so many people... when I turned around, they were gone...",
    ["Dialogue8480703"]="You—you got lost? That's not good...",
    ["Dialogue8480704"]="It's okay, don't worry! I met some nice uncles, and they said they'd help me find Mom and Dad! See—they even gave me candy!\n(The girl digs in her pocket and pulls out a handful of colorful sweets.)\nLook! So many candies! I'll share one with you, okay?",
    ["Dialogue8480705"]="(Cecil's expression grows serious. She takes one candy and sniffs it—and her expression changes.)\nLily, where are those people now?",
    ["Dialogue8480706"]="Over there in the market! I will show you!",
    ["Dialogue8480801"]="Ship...? Crap!",
    ["Dialogue8480802"]="(She grabs the girl and hides her behind a stack of crates by the docks.)\nLily, stay here and don't come out, no matter what! I'll come back for you, I promise!",
    ["Dialogue8480901"]="... Say it! Where are the other kids?!\n(Cecil stomps down on the bandit leader's wrist.)",
    ["Dialogue8480902"]="Ow ow ow—stop, stop! They're over there—those crates! We just gave them sleeping pills, that's all! We didn't touch them at all, I swear!",
    ["Dialogue8480903"]="Crates...?\n(Following the bandit's finger, Cecil looks toward a stack of boxes, where a small head peeks out, waving at her.)",
    ["Dialogue8480904"]="Big sis! Can I come out now?",
    ["Dialogue8480905"]="Lily... Lily?!\n(From the crowd, joyful cries ring out as a woman sweeps the girl into her arms.)",
    ["Dialogue8480906"]="Huh... Mom? Dad?!",
    ["Dialogue8480907"]="Lily! Where have you been? We thought... we thought you...",
    ["Dialogue8480908"]="(The man wipes his eyes and smiles gratefully at Cecil.)\nThank you, miss. Those traffickers have been around in the city for a long time, and lots of kids have been taken. We had no choice but to post a bounty... You're amazing! You must be a famous bounty hunter, right?",
    ["Dialogue8480909"]="Don't—don't turn me in for the bounty! I can pay more! Double—no, triple!",
    ["Dialogue8480910"]="No, I'm not a—wait, bounty hunter?\n(Cecil looks down at her longbow, lost in thought. You realize this might be the moment she decides to become a bounty hunter.)\nIsn't this... the perfect chance?",
    ["Dialogue8480911"]="... Hey, get up! Congrats—you're my first bounty!\n(Grinning, Cecil hums a tune as she hauls the bandit up.)\nFrom today on, I—Cecil Devine—am officially a bounty hunter!",
    ["Dialogue8480912"]="Huh—wait, you're not even a bounty hunter?! Then why'd you get involved?! Don't push me—I'm not going to jail!!",
    ["Dialogue8480913"]="Enough talking—move it! The Bounty Hunter Guild's this way, right?\n(Cecil gives the bandit a hard shove and walks off amid the crowd's cheers. She overlooks Drake and a few pirates watching from the crowd—guarding and keeping an eye on her...)",
    ["Dialogue8481001"]="(Suddenly, the market, the pirates, Cecil, the children—all fade away. Only the sound of calm waves and a gentle breeze remains. When you open your eyes again, you're standing in a place both unfamiliar and warm. Maybe this is where Cecil longed to return?)",
    ["Dialogue8481101"]="So you've already found a resting place for Cecil, right?",
    ["Dialogue8481102"]="Then... may I bury her keepsake myself, Adventurer? I know Cecil didn't want to come back to me, but... cough cough, I didn't raise her just out of guilt. Long ago... I've long seen her as my own kin.",
    ["Dialogue8481103"]="... Thank you, Adventurer.\n(He steps forward and takes Cecil's keepsake from your hands.)",
    ["Dialogue8481104"]="... I see. Maybe, in your eyes, I'm still not worthy to be her father, right?\n(He steps back, giving you space.)\nThen at least... allow me to watch as you lay her to rest.",
    ["Dialogue8481105"]="(Time slips away with the rhythm of the shovel striking soil. Before you lies a humble mound—the sum of Cecil's fleeting life.)\n... Funny, years ago, it was right here that I dug little Cecil out of the rubble. When our eyes met, I thought I saw hope... but to her, I must've looked like a monster...",
    ["Dialogue8481106"]="How cruelly ironic... Perhaps if she and I had both perished in that fire, maybe it would've been for the best...\n(Drake lowers his head. You can't see his face or hear his words clearly—only feel that it's time to quietly walk away. This is their final farewell...)",
    ["Dialogue8481201"]="The migrants rebuild a bustling market over the ruins, enjoying their lively nights. Those facing the sea feel the cool breeze on their backs—was this the same breeze that once brushed across Cecil's childhood?",
    ["Dialogue9000501"]="Meow! You came! You've been adventuring to so many interesting places recently. Oh, how I envy you, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9000502"]="I can't bear to leave this place. They have the most delicious dried fish I've ever eaten here, but if you like, you can always bring me back some souvenirs!",
    ["Dialogue9000503"]="Great! I can't wait to see what you'll bring me!",
    ["Dialogue9000601"]="Puff... Puff... Puff—\n(The flames flicker heartily, as if greeting a long lost friend.)",
    ["Dialogue9000602"]="Puff... Puff...\n(The flames crackle as though they're trying to tell you something.)",
    ["Dialogue9000603"]="Puff! Puff!\n(The flames dance happily, as though thanking you.)",
    ["Dialogue9000701"]="It's you! Long time no see! I bet you've expanded your travel map quite a bit, haven't you! Oh, how I envy you!",
    ["Dialogue9000702"]="I haven't saved up enough to go traveling just yet, but when I'm ready, I'll set off with my map of the continent and go to all the places I haven't already stuck a flag on... But I'll still be stoked if you find the time to bring me some souvenirs whenever you can!",
    ["Dialogue9000703"]="Thank you so much! I'm looking forward to seeing what surprises you'll bring me!",
    ["Dialogue9000801"]="A-hah! Adventurer, you're here! It looks like you've been on the road a long time... I bet you have a whole load of fantastic tales to share with me! I'd love to go traveling, too... I bet I'd have a fantastic adventure of my own!",
    ["Dialogue9000802"]="But alas, some things are best left in one's imagination... Although, if you could bring me some souvenirs from your journey, and share your stories with me, I'd accept them all gladly!",
    ["Dialogue9000803"]="Well then, I'll be here waiting for you!",
    ["Dialogue9000901"]="Just look at you, so energetic and raring to go... You young people are so full of life, adventuring all over the place the way you do!",
    ["Dialogue9000902"]="I've grown accustomed to the temperature and weather in the desert over the years... and I'm really too lazy to go out gallivanting again. If you come across anything interesting, be sure to share it with me!",
    ["Dialogue9000903"]="Then I'll just stay right where I am and look forward to those gifts you're gonna bring me!",
    ["Dialogue9001001"]="Hey, it's good to see you again! You didn't disappoint me... You're virtually glowing with the spirit of adventure! You must have enjoyed many beautiful encounters on this continent since we last met. I must admit, I'm rather jealous!",
    ["Dialogue9001002"]="Although I too crave the unlimited pursuit of all things beautiful, I won't leave here until I remove Hassan's mask with my own hands. But I suppose you can bring me some small trinkets you may pick up along your travels around the world, from time to time. Remember—I like gifts that come with a story best!",
    ["Dialogue9001003"]="In that case, I wish you the most beautiful adventures in the world!",
    ["Dialogue9001101"]="Meow! You came back! It seems you've been to a lot of places, and you even have a new outfit! Oh, I really envy you, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9001102"]="I can't just leave here whenever I please. After all, as a noble Doram Enchanter, there are still many people who need my help! However, that doesn't mean you shouldn't bring me back some souvenirs as often as you can!",
    ["Dialogue9001103"]="Meowww! I know you won't let me down, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9001201"]="Haha! Young adventurer, it's you! You seem to love the adventurer's life... and what a life it is! It really does bring back memories...",
    ["Dialogue9001202"]="Hahaha! I'm tired of the vagabond's life. No, I'm satisfied just watching the young adventurers pass by and helping them advance in any way I can. If you happen to think of me as you journey the world, you can bring me back some valuable souvenirs, and help me relive those treasured years!",
    ["Dialogue9001203"]="Well, thank you, young adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue9001301"]="Hello, there! Long time no see! Wow... It looks like you've grown a lot. You must have experienced many things throughout your adventure so far... Ah, I really miss those days, traveling alone across the continent...",
    ["Dialogue9001302"]="Hahaha! Well, at least I have my memories... But now I suppose I have even more important responsibilities to fulfill. Having said that, if it's not too much bother... please bring me some of the treasures you find on your travels! The odd souvenir here and there is just what I need to keep those memories alive!",
    ["Dialogue9001303"]="Thank you, adventurer, truly.",
    ["Dialogue9001401"]="Meow! I see you've collected an assortment of new materials! It's no surprise that an experienced adventurer like you would be able to pick up more useful research materials than me!",
    ["Dialogue9001402"]="I haven't learned all humanity has to share on founding an academy, so I can't leave just yet, but if you're willing to share any interesting materials you've collected from the wide world, I'd be very grateful!",
    ["Dialogue9001403"]="Thank you so much, meow! That'll certainly be a great aid to my research!",
    ["Dialogue9001501"]="Oh, it's you! I haven't seen you in a while, but I'm sure you must have seen the most magnificent scenery the world has to offer on your travels. The unique experiences of your youth will have a great impact on your future. Cherish this time!",
    ["Dialogue9001502"]="Hahaha! Look... Nothing beats the sunset from this port, don't you agree? I can't bear to leave it behind... However, I'd be very glad to receive any gifts you might spy on your travels to the furthest reaches of this continent. After all, everything in this world bears its own unique memories...",
    ["Dialogue9001503"]="Hahaha! I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of surprises you'll bring me.",
    ["Dialogue9001601"]="It's been a while! You've been to many new places recently, and must have tasted countless delicious wines... Why didn't you bring some back for me? Ah, the freedom of an adventurer... How I envy you!",
    ["Dialogue9001602"]="Me...? I can't leave here just yet. Well, not until he comes back, at least...\n(There seems to be a trace of fleeting loneliness in Nastia's eyes.)\nBut if you want to, you can bring me some of the items you're bound to collect from all over the world as a gift!",
    ["Dialogue9001603"]="Meowww! I know you won't let me down, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9001701"]="Meow, you're back! I can only imagine the fascinating places you've visited since I last saw you... If they have any particularly delicious dried fish there, I wanna go, too!",
    ["Dialogue9001702"]="No, no, no... There are no two ways about it, meow. The sea here is so beautiful, and the delicious dried fish... Yum! Why would anyone choose to leave this place!? Ah! I just thought of something! Why don't you gather some interesting things to bring back for me from your travels?",
    ["Dialogue9001703"]="Wow! Thank you so much, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9001801"]="We meet again! It looks like you've grown a lot since I was you last. Although I didn't see your latest adventure with my own eyes, I know it must've been wonderful... If only I could travel around like you, I'm sure I'd learn many new things, too!",
    ["Dialogue9001802"]="No, I have unfinished business here... I will never leave Payon until she says yes! But... if you could bring back some special items for me from your adventures, I believe they may also help me in my quest!",
    ["Dialogue9001803"]="Well, if that's the case, I really can't thank you enough! You're a true friend!",
    ["Dialogue9001901"]="Ah! It's good to see you again! Do you have any new stories for me? And have you met any new ghosts? If you run into any, make sure you tell me! I wish I could see them, too...",
    ["Dialogue9001902"]="Hmm... When will we discover some interesting new ghosts on this continent? Ah! How about this... In the future, if you come back often and bring me some of the things you find during your adventures, maybe I can glean some clues from them!",
    ["Dialogue9001903"]="Thank you! You're the best!",
    ["Dialogue9002001"]="Meow! I haven't seen you in so long! It looks like you're still alive and kicking... Meow! You must have been to a lot of interesting places... Mewleta wants to meet some nice new people, too!",
    ["Dialogue9002002"]="Haha! But I can't turn my back on the cool shade of Payon—and the people here are so friendly! How about you gather some neat curios for me from around the continent first?",
    ["Dialogue9002003"]="Wow! Thank you so much, meow!",
    ["Dialogue9002101"]="Oh, it's you again! It looks like you've changed a lot... You've clearly gained a lot of experience on your adventures—much more than those narrow-minded mages...",
    ["Dialogue9002102"]="They always insist that enchantment isn't magic... but anyone with a shred of common sense can see that enchantment and magic go hand in hand! How can they even understand when they spend their lives holed up in this city? Huh? I know... Why don't you collect some materials for me during your travels! Maybe then I'll have enough evidence to put them in their place!",
    ["Dialogue9002103"]="I'll leave it to you, then. I just know that your gifts will be invaluable to me!",
    ["Dialogue9002201"]="Hi! It's good to see you again! Wow, you've grown! I bet you've seen it all by now, but remember to always stay safe when out there adventuring!",
    ["Dialogue9002202"]="But I'm really curious to know more about your journey across this land... If I could, I'd like to witness the great prosperity of this continent with you. Could you bring me some gifts from your journey?",
    ["Dialogue9002203"]="Thank you, adventurer... Truly, thank you!",
    ["Dialogue9002301"]="Meow! I never expected you'd grow so much, so quickly! I suppose the Doram aren't the only great adventurers out there, and you're proof of that, my friend! If possible, I'd really like to witness your great adventure with my own eyes...",
    ["Dialogue9002302"]="That's not going to happen anytime soon... I still have a whole load of magic research to carry out in Geffen, and the noble Doram never give up on anything halfway! But, being as smart as I am, I've come up with a perfect solution for you, meow! You can gather together some of the items you pick up along your journey and give them to me, so that I can enjoy the thrill of adventure, too!",
    ["Dialogue9002303"]="I know, I know, you think I'm a genius, meow. I'm used to it—everyone's been telling me so since I was a kid.",
    ["Dialogue9002401"]="Beth has been ignoring me for three days…",
    ["Dialogue9002402"]="Yes, but I don't want to get her a reconciliation gift at all. Adventurer, can you help me with the gift?",
    ["Dialogue9002403"]="Hee-hee, anything that is funny!",
    ["Dialogue9002501"]="Adventurer, I ask for your help.",
    ["Dialogue9002502"]="If you come across something interesting in your travels, can you bring it to me? My family would love to hear about your adventures!",
    ["Dialogue9002503"]="Thanks so much and have a great trip!",
    ["Dialogue9002601"]="Alas… My paws are a little too worn to dig for shiny things, meow.",
    ["Dialogue9002602"]="I can’t buy dried fish if I can't dig for the shiny stuff meow. Adventurer, will you help me?",
    ["Dialogue9002603"]="Thank you, meow! I'm sure you'll bring something I like!",
    ["Dialogue9010101"]="My welcome guest, you're here at last. I have some good news to share with you!",
    ["Dialogue9010102"]="Right! Esteemed adventurer, according to the Kafra Corporation's records, you have used our delivery service more than 100 times and have therefore entered our loyal customer list! I am honored to provide further excellent services to distinguished customers such as yourself!",
    ["Dialogue9010103"]="What a blessing! If you're willing to help me with a few small things, our special customized service may become available to you one day! Does that sound pleasing to you?",
    ["Dialogue9010104"]="In order to provide comprehensive and high-quality service, I need to clear the warehouses of all our customers. Currently, I need some Lotus Grass to purify the warehouse's amazing artifacts! So, could you please gather me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lotus Grass</color>? You can find this special grass beyond <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9010201"]="Wow! You really didn't let me down! Thank you so much for bringing back the Lotus Grass so soon! This is the last of the materials I needed!",
    ["Dialogue9010202"]="In fact, in order to thank our customers for their long-term support and to show our sincerity and warmth, the Kafra Corporation has decided to make a set of down pillows for our loyal customers like you, embroidered with their names! However, I still need some more Down Fur to make more pillows! Could you please go and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Down Fur</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baby Desert Wolves</color>?",
    ["Dialogue9010203"]="You're awesome! Thank you! I'll be waiting! And remember, safety first!",
    ["Dialogue9010301"]="You truly are an adventurer of both strength and courage. As expected, the Kafra Corporation's most loyal adventurers are the most discerning. It's a great honor to serve you. However, if you want to enjoy our customized service, I still have a few questions to test you on your knowledge of the Kafra Corporation. Are you ready?",
    ["Dialogue9010302"]="If you don't pass, you won't be able to make it onto our VIP list! Be careful when choosing your answers!",
    ["Dialogue9010303"]="Alright! I will start asking the questions now. Good luck.",
    ["Dialogue9010401"]="Dear customer, please listen to the following questions! Every answer is very important!",
    ["Dialogue9010501"]="Ah! I knew you could do it! You are indeed a loyal customer of the Kafra Corporation! You have now entered the first batch of candidates for our customized service. However, before the service is officially launched, I will conduct a follow-up review on behalf of the Kafra Corporation, so please come and chat with me more in the future!",
    ["Dialogue9020101"]="You're just in time! What kind of birthday present do you think someone as fabulous as Defolty would like? I finally have the chance to thank her for her help, but I want to get this right!",
    ["Dialogue9020102"]="Eh, eh, eh? You were really thinking of perfume, too? I also wanted to give Defolty some perfume, but I'm not sure what kind is in fashion right now? Choosing a fine fragrance can be so tricky. Do you have any suggestions?",
    ["Dialogue9020103"]="Thank you so much! Maybe <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vienna Lindra</color> might know what the most popular perfume is nowadays.",
    ["Dialogue9020201"]="Huh? You want to buy my most popular perfume? I wish I could help, but I just sold the very last bottle of that particular fragrance.",
    ["Dialogue9020202"]="So, W is looking for a birthday present for Defolty... Let me think. I have a special perfume formula here that I bought from a mysterious merchant. If I had the materials, I could make her a very unique fragrance. However...",
    ["Dialogue9020203"]="To make this perfume, I'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Tough Vines</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Hinalles</color>, found on Vocals. But the thing is, I don't have time to collect the materials right now. Adventurer, do you think you could get them for me?",
    ["Dialogue9020301"]="Well done! You are really amazing! Alright, let me mix this special perfume for you.",
    ["Dialogue9020401"]="Alright, adventurer. I'll give you this special perfume. Remember, the name of this perfume is Miraculous Encounter. I'm really looking forward to W receiving it, so it's on the house this time. Let's say it's a little piece of my heart. By the way, tell her to wish Defolty a happy birthday from me!",
    ["Dialogue9020501"]="You're finally back! How did it go? Have you got anything for me?",
    ["Dialogue9020601"]="Wow, this sure looks like a fine perfume! It must have been very expensive!",
    ["Dialogue9020602"]="Vienna is a genius! Miraculous Encounter? What a great name! I feel that meeting both Defolty and you, adventurer, was a miracle! I'm very grateful! Thanks to your hard work gathering materials, I have such a wonderful perfume to give as a gift to Defolty!",
    ["Dialogue9020603"]="No, I must show my thanks to you. In fact, according to what I've seen during our acquaintance, I can confirm that you are a special customer of great strength, wisdom, sincerity, and bravery, who fully meets the requirements for Kafra's customized service! Therefore, I have decided that from today on, you will be able to enjoy the privileges of our customized service!",
    ["Dialogue9030101"]="Oh? Well if you're not here for sightseeing, why have you come to see me?",
    ["Dialogue9030102"]="(Flessi's eyes widen as he looks closely at the music box in front of him.)\nWow! This... this is...! Adventurer, where did you get this music box?!",
    ["Dialogue9030103"]="It's actually mine, and it's very important to me, adventurer. Can you give it back to me?",
    ["Dialogue9030201"]="Adventurer, I really don't know how to thank you. You don't know what this music box means to me.\n(Flessi's eyes are red and his hands are shaking slightly.)",
    ["Dialogue9030202"]="You've guessed correctly. This music box... It was given to me by a very important friend. He has been away for many years, and this music box is the only memento I have of him. The melody in the music box, it's the last creation of his he left me.\n(Flessi reaches out and twists the dial, but the music box only creaks and squeaks.)",
    ["Dialogue9030203"]="It seems that there's something wrong with the parts. I suppose I didn't expect finding it so easily, but it's a shame I couldn't keep the song. Maybe this is fate.\n(Flessi lowers his head sadly and sighs.)",
    ["Dialogue9030204"]="You mean, the bard, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color>, might be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fix</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>music box</color>?\n(There seems to be a glimmer of hope in Flessi's eyes.)\nYou're right. He's a proficient musician and should know a way. If he can repair it for me, I'd forever be in his debt!",
    ["Dialogue9030301"]="Huh? What seems to be the trouble, adventurer? Do you need my help?",
    ["Dialogue9030302"]="Oh? This music box seems very interesting. Is it broken? Hmm... Let me take a look...",
    ["Dialogue9030303"]="Based on my years of experience with musical instruments, this music box must have something wrong with its spring. However, I've never repaired such a delicate device before. An adventurer like you should be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the library</color> and find the book, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Deep Within the Music Box</color>, for me, right? I believe it would be no problem if I had a professional book like that to refer to.",
    ["Dialogue9030401"]="Now, let me see what the problem is...\n(Morts flicks through the book as he opens the music box and fiddles with the parts that have already been disassembled.)",
    ["Dialogue9030402"]="Don't worry. I'm an artist who respects music. I'll be careful with this delicate music box.\n(Morts continues fiddling with the parts with his head down and a look of concentration on his face.)",
    ["Dialogue9030403"]="Don't worry. It is only with patience that we'll discover the problem. Based on my years of experience and my keen intuition as a musician, I deduce that the deformation of the spring has caused some kind of internal jamming. Hmm... Adventurer, how's your relationship with Hollgrehenn?",
    ["Dialogue9030404"]="To repair this music box, I'll need a special metal: Maple Iron. Only this special metal is suitable for this music box's spring, but I have nothing in common with Hollgrehenn. He and his Drubby are not from the same world as me and my beloved lute. Could I trouble you to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color> and get me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maple Iron</color>?",
    ["Dialogue9030501"]="Is there anything I can do for you, adventurer?",
    ["Dialogue9030502"]="You need Maple Iron to fix a music box, you say? Oh, that's no problem. I have plenty of Maple Iron here. Help yourself!",
    ["Dialogue9030601"]="That was quick, adventurer. I've studied the whole structure of this music box carefully. I'll be able to repair it once I have that Maple Iron, just you watch!",
    ["Dialogue9030602"]="Alright, alright... This should be fine now. Let's take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>music box</color> back to its <color=#CA2E0AFF>owner</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9030603"]="Of course, this music box has given me inspiration for my next song! I can't miss this opportunity to dig into the story behind it.",
    ["Dialogue9030701"]="Adventurer, how goes it? Did you manage to fix it?\n(There's a hint of tension in Flessi's expression.)",
    ["Dialogue9030702"]="Don't worry. With a musical genius like me on the case, your music box is now in perfect condition. Look...\n(Morts hands the music box to Flessi.)",
    ["Dialogue9030703"]="(With slightly shaking hands, Flessi takes the music box. He gently twists the dial, and a soft and beautiful melody slowly flows from it.)",
    ["Dialogue9030704"]="This... this melody seems so familiar. It's almost as if I've heard it somewhere before.",
    ["Dialogue9030705"]="That's right. If you've ever been to the amusement park on a Sunday morning, you're sure to have heard it. This is the only gift given to me by the other founder of amusement park. Little Rick and I are both orphans. When we were children, we always dreamt of creating a paradise for children. Unfortunately...",
    ["Dialogue9030706"]="(Flessi's eyes are slightly red. He gazes at the carousel in the distance, and looks as though he misses the past.)\nThis song was actually Little Rick's gift to all the people who come to the amusement park. As long as the children could find some happiness here, it was enough for us. Adventurer, thank you for returning this important memory to me. The amusement park will always be open to you.",
    ["Dialogue9040101"]="Adventurer, it's good to see you.\n(There seems to be a sadness in Flessi's drooping eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue9040102"]="You see... In fact, there is something I haven't been able to finish for a long time. Many years have passed and I haven't achieved it, but since recovering the music box, your appearance in my life has given me a glimmer of hope. Maybe you can help me realize this wish.",
    ["Dialogue9040103"]="Do you remember Little Rick? The truth is, many years ago, we encountered some frenzied monsters in the forest. Little Rick blocked a deadly attack for me in that battle and was grievously injured. Before he died, he gave me the music box and the score of its melody, and told me to bury him deep in the forest. Over the years, I used to go there to visit him. However, weeds have grown over his tombstone recently, and I'm too old to clear them by myself. So, before I continue with this story, could you please <color=#CA2E0AFF>clear the weeds from his tombstone</color> for me?",
    ["Dialogue9040201"]="(Flessi silently looks at the tombstone engraved with a single musical note, and slowly reaches out his hand as if he wants to touch the cold stone.)",
    ["Dialogue9040202"]="You must be wondering why there's no name on his tombstone. It's because Little Rick said that he only wanted to leave his music in this world, and not his name. Before he left me, he gave me his music, hoping that his tombstone would leave behind a melody that brings people happiness, not sadness.",
    ["Dialogue9040203"]="I always wanted to write this piece of music on his tombstone by myself, but I couldn't find the right pigment. Ordinary inks and pigments can't withstand the weathering of the wind and rain, so I couldn't achieve it. It was only recently, when I heard that Squid Ink used by the royal family, a bodily fluid from Cornutuses, could last for a hundred years, that I was given hope. Adventurer, would you please bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus ink</color>?",
    ["Dialogue9040301"]="Great, now I can finally realize the wish I've held for all these years.\n(Flessi's eyes turn red as he looks at the ink in his hand, and his voice cannot hide his excitement.)",
    ["Dialogue9040302"]="Adventurer, thank you for getting this precious ink for me. I have one last thing to ask of you. Little Rick loved Cotton Candy more than anything. Every time I come here, I ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grace</color> to make some. Please see her and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cotton Candy</color> for me. I'll write the music on the tombstone.",
    ["Dialogue9040401"]="Oh? You're here to get some Cotton Candy for Flessi? He usually comes himself. I've always wondered if he has a secret grandson or something that he hasn't told anyone about.",
    ["Dialogue9040402"]="I didn't think it was a bad guess. If you don't want to tell, I won't ask! Take your Cotton Candy!",
    ["Dialogue9040501"]="(Flessi looks at the tombstone attentively, as if relishing the vivid images of his memory once more.)",
    ["Dialogue9040502"]="Adventurer, thank you for everything you've done for me and Little Rick. Please put this Cotton Candy in front of Little Rick's tombstone. Let him know that I have a new friend, as sincere and kind as he was.",
    ["Dialogue9050101"]="You always like to buy different baits, and you always buy a lot. You must be a pro fishing enthusiast!",
    ["Dialogue9050102"]="Excellent! I haven't met an adventurer who likes fishing so much in a long time. Most people only come to visit me once in a while. Only you exude a pure passion for fishing! I know it!",
    ["Dialogue9050103"]="Of course! But I do business by the sea all year round, so haven't had the chance to go fishing by the river for a long time. I've heard people say that there's a precious species of fish in Prontera River: the <color=#CA2E0AFF>White Cloud Fish</color>. I've never seen it before, but I'd love to if I ever get the chance.",
    ["Dialogue9050201"]="Heavens! You really brought me a White Cloud Fish! I've never seen such a beautiful fish! Look at those amazing fat fins! Thank you so much! I'll take good care of it, but my fish tank is a little sparse. It could do with some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shells</color> for decoration.",
    ["Dialogue9050301"]="Thank you so much. Now I can create a lovely new home for this White Cloud Fish. Ah! I've been chatting with you for so long, and I still have a batch of <color=#CA2E0AFF>bait</color> to be delivered to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson Fleet</color> today. They must be wondering where their bait is. What should I do?!",
    ["Dialogue9050302"]="Thank you so much. They shouldn't be too far away! I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue9050401"]="Thanks to you, this White Cloud Fish is settling in nicely. Thank you so much for all your help today! It's rare to meet a new friend who is so sincere and loves fishing. Feel free to come talk with me some more in the future. I'll definitely recommend the most suitable fishing gear and bait for you!",
    ["Dialogue9060101"]="Wait... I actually have something very important I need your help with!",
    ["Dialogue9060102"]="Here's the thing... I-I finally made a date with Elysia to watch the stars with me tomorrow night.",
    ["Dialogue9060103"]="(A blush creeps across Hayden's cheeks. He lowers his head slightly, looking quite shy.) But the things is, I don't know anything about astrology, so I wanted to ask if you have any ideas.",
    ["Dialogue9060104"]="That's a good idea. There must be some books related to astrology in the library. If I can catch up on the subject a bit, maybe I can actually impress her!",
    ["Dialogue9060201"]="Oh? You're looking for reference books on horoscopes and astrology? Hmm... Let me think... \"Guide to the Stars\" on the shelf over there should be the most suitable for beginners. You can go get it yourself.",
    ["Dialogue9060301"]="(Hayden takes the book and immediately looks through it, mumbling the words as he reads.) Astrological rituals often require the use of energy crystals, among which, the power of Purple Spirit Crystals is the most concentrated... Hmm, I wonder if this is true. Can you help me get some more Purple Spirit Crystals? I hear they can be found in abundance in the depths of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Cave</color>. Please, I need your help!",
    ["Dialogue9060401"]="Thank you so much. I'm sure Elysia will be very happy to see that I have these stones ready. She likes these mysterious things best. Adventurer, do you think I have anything else to prepare for this date?",
    ["Dialogue9060402"]="Something romantic? That's a good point! I agree I'm missing something...\nAh! I've got it! Red wine! How can you have a romantic date without red wine? Adventurer, please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isabella Trista</color>, the owner of Rose Red Tavern, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring me back a bottle of red wine</color>!",
    ["Dialogue9060501"]="Oh? Adventurer, is there something I can help you with?",
    ["Dialogue9060502"]="Oh-ho-ho! Hayden's finally going to make his move? Of course I'll help him. This is the most popular red wine in my tavern. Please take it to him. I'm looking forward to seeing what happens between him and Elysia!",
    ["Dialogue9060601"]="Hayden gladly takes the red wine, saying that everything is ready. Today, he plans to cram up on his knowledge of astrology and thanks you for your help and support. To show his gratitude, he will fully cater to all your fishing needs in the future. Whether his date is successful or not, you will be his special friend for life and are welcome to come see him any time.",
    ["Dialogue9060602"]="Wow! This bottle of red wine looks great! Nothing can go wrong now. All I need to do is study up on some astrology tonight.",
    ["Dialogue9060603"]="Thank you very much. Without you, I really don't know who I could've turned to. No matter whether my date with Elysia goes well or not, you and I are best friends from now on. If there's anything I can help you with fishing-wise, just let me know! We're gonna be friends forever, and I'll make sure to save my most special goods for you!",
    ["Dialogue9070101"]="Adventurer, don't go just get! Seeing how you often come to see an accomplished stylist like me to change your hairstyle, it's not difficult to see that you seem to have your finger on the pulse of the latest fashion trends, so today I'm going to offer you an olive branch. I'm sure it will lead you to the highest heights of the continent's fashion circle. I want you to be my model in the hairstyle contest!",
    ["Dialogue9070102"]="That's right! The kingdom of Rune-Midgarts is about to hold its annual hair fashion contest. Although with my extraordinary skills and taste, we'll make it to the top three, no problem! But if we want to earn the top spot, the choice of model will be of the utmost importance!",
    ["Dialogue9070103"]="Heh-heh, my request is that you pass a few of little tests first! To start with, to be a good model, you have to have your own understanding and way of expressing fashion, so my first test is to ask you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go out</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take your own photos in three settings</color> that you think are the best match for your clothes and hairstyle. I'll judge whether your understanding of fashion and aesthetics meets my standards through your photos.",
    ["Dialogue9070201"]="Your fashion taste seems to fit mine quite well. It seems that the first test was just a trifling exercise for you. So, let me give you your second test. As a model in the competition, of course, an essential part is your ability to face the public's response and your ability to be adaptable when put on the spot. Therefore, for your second test, I'd like to invite you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> to take part in an <color=#CA2E0AFF>arm-wrestling match</color>. I want to see if you can remain calm under pressure from the crowd.",
    ["Dialogue9070202"]="You go ahead. I'll send someone to watch you in secret!",
    ["Dialogue9070301"]="According to my reliable sources, you did great in the arm-wrestling match and have the potential to be a hair model without compare! Now, how about I officially make you my hair model?",
    ["Dialogue9070302"]="Excellent! Now I'm 90% sure, but... if you can help me get my hands on something, I'll be 100% sure!\n(Chester steals a glance in your direction and then looks up again with a proud look.)",
    ["Dialogue9070303"]="You really are the perfect model for me, but if we want make a big splash in the competition, I'll need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Butterfly Wing Powder</color> as our secret weapon. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate</color> and get some from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockers</color> there! I'll be waiting here for some good news! Hurry along, now!",
    ["Dialogue9070401"]="Thank you! With this powder as our secret weapon, we're sure to win the championship, but we still have some time before it begins. Let's take this time to cultivate our understanding of one another. If you have time, come and talk with me some more. I have a lot of information to share with you. You won't want to miss out on it!",
    ["Dialogue9080101"]="I haven't seen you in so long! After we won the championship with such ease, it's obvious that you've been coming to see me less and less. You're lucky I still see you as a close friend. Hmph...",
    ["Dialogue9080102"]="Alright. I was just joking. Of course I know you're very busy trying to become the strongest adventurer on the continent, but I really need to discuss something with you. It's something I've been thinking about for a long time, and there's no one else I can talk to about it.",
    ["Dialogue9080103"]="Do you remember Vera, the hairdresser who matched my skills quite evenly in the competition? The one with the hot temper and the unusual obsession with color.",
    ["Dialogue9080104"]="Yes, that one. She's about as good as me, and it was lucky that we managed to keep in step with each other during the championship. The thing is though, actually... she and I once, well, we have a history.",
    ["Dialogue9080105"]="...In fact, we never actually broke up. It's just that after some trivial quarrels we've been at something of a stalemate up till now. After the competition, I feel that as a well-mannered man, I should take the initiative to make the first move. So, could you please take this new bottle of Hair Dye to her for me to see if she wants to make up?",
    ["Dialogue9080201"]="Huh? Adventurer, you look... a little familiar. Have we met somewhere before?",
    ["Dialogue9080202"]="Hairstyle contest...? Ah! I remember now, you're that model! Well, it's not a good idea for you to come see me like this. Tell me, what are you doing here?\n(Vera's face immediately looks impatient.)",
    ["Dialogue9080301"]="Oh... Chester asked you to bring me this?\n(Vera's mouth rises slightly at the corners and then quickly returns to normal.)\nHmph... He still has a trace of conscience left, but I won't forget how he criticized my hair coloring for being \"rustic.\" He even said it would best suit a farmer. That's just going too far! If he really wants to apologize, he should come see me himself to show his sincerity.",
    ["Dialogue9080302"]="If he hasn't forgotten our arrangement, he should know what to do.",
    ["Dialogue9080401"]="What? She... she said what?\n(A little nervousness appears on Chester's face, but it soon returns to a look of pride.)",
    ["Dialogue9080402"]="She didn't forget. I knew that even though she has a sharp tongue, she has a soft heart, and that there must still be a little of me in that heart! Hahaha! Very good. Can I trouble you with one more thing? You see, we had an agreement: If Vera won the hairstyle contest, I'd make her a unique Cloud Blossom flower crown. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloud Blossoms</color> grow near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crow's nest</color> by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9080501"]="Great, that's it! With these Cloud Blossoms, I can bring a flower crown to Vera like I agreed. To thank you for all you've done for me, I've decided to give you a date outfit I've treasured for many years. It's guaranteed to give you luck! You don't have to thank me too much. After all, this is an outfit that only those who really understand fashion can make work!",
    ["Dialogue9090101"]="If there's nothing pressing you need from me, don't disturb me while I count these crystals! Or... do you have anything good for me?",
    ["Dialogue9090201"]="Hey! Wow! Isn't this the Crystal Heart?!\n(Sinclair's face cannot hide his obvious ecstasy, but he recovers his composure immediately.)\nAhem... I've met several people who claim to have possessed the Crystal Heart recently, but they've all been fake. If you can prove that this Crystal Heart is real, come see me again and we'll talk turkey!",
    ["Dialogue9090202"]="You can go and borrow a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Authenticator</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Russell</color>. Such a valuable item must be verified with the most sophisticated instruments. Ahem... As for that arrogant fellow Russell... Don't be fooled by appearances. He's actually a very cunning businessman, and he has a lot of strange items in his possession!",
    ["Dialogue9090301"]="I expected no less from Sinclair. He'd never miss an opportunity to take advantage of me. Are you here to borrow the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Authenticator</color>, too?",
    ["Dialogue9090302"]="Congratulations on becoming the fifth adventurer to borrow my authenticator this month. It seems everyone's doing all they can to get in with Sinclair these days.\n<color=#A1979FFF>If I went around telling the world what I was into, I wonder if people would go around collecting priceless goods for me, too. Sinclair's more cunning than he makes himself out to be. He's always one step ahead of me.</color>",
    ["Dialogue9090303"]="Here you are. I really hope there won't be a sixth person asking for it. Good luck.",
    ["Dialogue9090401"]="You're back so soon! Russell must be jealous of me now! Hahaha!",
    ["Dialogue9090402"]="(Sinclair holds the authenticator and carefully scans the Crystal Heart, then begins observing it.)\nHmm... The color is bright, the refractive index is accurate, and there are no defects visible through the authenticator's magnification scope. There is a real hope that this is the Crystal Heart.\n(He weighs the Crystal Heart in his hand and holds it up to the sun, looking at it again and again, showing a satisfied smile.)",
    ["Dialogue9090403"]="Hehe... Although your Crystal Heart has passed the authenticator's precise inspection, there is an even more important test to confirm whether this is indeed the real thing. According to legend, if Morning Dew of Yggdrasil is dropped onto the crystal, the real Crystal Heart will emit a special light. Quickly go and fetch me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morning Dew of Yggdrasil</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hydras</color> and we'll see.",
    ["Dialogue9090501"]="So, let's witness it together—whether the Crystal Heart we have here today is the real deal!",
    ["Dialogue9090502"]="(Sinclair carefully drops the Morning Dew of Yggdrasil on the Crystal Heart. A bright yellow light rises slowly from the inside of the crystal and radiates outward, reflecting Sinclair's burning eyes and surprised expression.)",
    ["Dialogue9090503"]="Yes! This really is the Crystal Heart! Adventurer! You really weren't lying to me! You're no ordinary adventurer. How much do you want for this Crystal Heart?",
    ["Dialogue9090504"]="Huh?! You really just want to give this precious Crystal Heart to me?",
    ["Dialogue9090505"]="I wasn't wrong to put my faith in you! In that case, I won't say no! From now on, you will be an honorary member of the Sinclair Crystal Association. You're welcome to come to me to exchange Crystals any time you want!",
    ["Dialogue9100101"]="You haven't come to visit my shop in quite a long time. But it's a good thing you came here today. I have a whole load of goodies to show you!",
    ["Dialogue9100102"]="What do you think this could be?! (Sinclair mysteriously pulls you to the corner and takes a crumpled parchment with a map of Midgard printed on it out of his pocket. There are two lines of text in the corner.)",
    ["Dialogue9100103"]="I knew I could trust you—great minds think alike! I came upon this in an old book. Based on my years of experience, it must be an invaluable treasure map. It might even lead to a huge stash of crystals! Unfortunately, I've never been good at deciphering these kinds of things. Why don't you take a look at it for me? \"It's as light as a fairy, with a dancing spirit resting on its shoulder...\" \"Its steps are as heavy as steel, and its palms are as pure as snow...\" It sounds like a riddle about monsters, perhaps. How are we supposed to guess such an abstract thing?",
    ["Dialogue9100104"]="Oh yeah, how could I have forgotten about those two <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster researchers</color>? Well, please see if they can help, and you may be able to <color=#CA2E0AFF>figure out the answer</color>. But remember, you need to ask them separately! Don't let them find out about the treasure map!",
    ["Dialogue9100201"]="Oh? What is such a cute adventurer doing looking so perplexed? Do you have any monster-related questions you need answering?",
    ["Dialogue9100202"]="\"It's as light as a fairy, with a dancing spirit resting on its shoulder...\" What could this sentence possibly mean?! (Bertha's eyes throw a surprised look at you from behind her thick lenses, expressing her confusion.)",
    ["Dialogue9100203"]="Well, the light creature with a dancing spirit on its shoulders must be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vocal</color> with a violin on its shoulder, of course. Do you get it now?",
    ["Dialogue9100301"]="Norten gives an explanation and answers immediately after listening to your riddle, but he asks where you found it, because it seems as though this riddle was published in a children's magic textbook studied by junior students of Criatura Academy. You muddle through his inquiries carefully, and happily prepare to return to Sinclair with the answer.",
    ["Dialogue9100302"]="Adventurer, what can I do for you?",
    ["Dialogue9100303"]="\"Its steps are as heavy as steel, and its palms are as pure as snow...\" Isn't this a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sasquatch</color>? Why are you asking me this riddle all of a sudden? It's from a textbook published a few years ago. All the freshmen in Criatura Academy are made to study it.",
    ["Dialogue9100304"]="What you said is also true. After all, adventurers like you now travel around relying on actual combat to accumulate experience. The knowledge found in textbooks is really quite useless to you.",
    ["Dialogue9100401"]="You're back at last. What was the conclusion? Were those two monster researchers worth their salt in the end?",
    ["Dialogue9100402"]="I see! So, those monsters are essentially in line with the characteristics described in the riddle. A place with both Sasquatches and Vocals... It could only be Labyrinth Forest! Yes, it must be, adventurer! I know that someone with your character would never take the treasure for themselves. It would be best if you went to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> and brought the treasure back!",
    ["Dialogue9100403"]="If someone as elegant and noble as I were to venture into a place like Labyrinth Forest, it would certainly draw attention. It really wouldn't be wise to reveal the existence of the treasure so soon. Adventurer, please go and bring back the treasure. I'll be waiting here for the good news!",
    ["Dialogue9100501"]="(Sinclair opens the treasure chest with glee, but the joy on his face suddenly freezes.)\nWhat the...?! Adventurer, you... really didn't open this chest?\n(Sinclair looks at you suspiciously.)",
    ["Dialogue9100502"]="(Sinclair smacks his head in frustration and takes a piece of paper from the box.) \"Dear Student, congratulations on completing your first semester's basic magic homework assignment.\" Is this some kind of prank?!",
    ["Dialogue9100503"]="What a waste of time and energy. Well, adventurer, although I didn't get the treasure, I feel like our friendship has reached a new level after all that running around. From now on, I'd like to count you among my best friends; I'll even open a new special store exclusively for you! No one else deserves such special treatment! Come and have a look!",
    ["Dialogue9110101"]="Adventurer, you seem to have a lot of experience. You must have faced hundreds of battles and traveled to many places, right?",
    ["Dialogue9110102"]="Hmm... In fact, I have something of a presumptuous request. I need an important material to complete an ornament I'm crafting. However, my strength is somewhat limited, and I haven't been able to obtain this material. A knowledgeable adventurer like you may just have what I need. I'd be willing to buy it from you at a very high price!",
    ["Dialogue9110103"]="I need an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Oliver Wolf Eyeball</color>. If you have one, please give it to me. I really need it. It's because... (Ingael blushes, then looks at you seriously, his eyes seeming to flicker with hesitation.)",
    ["Dialogue9110104"]="I want it because... The person I like... (Ingael clenches his fists and turns his head away sheepishly.)",
    ["Dialogue9110201"]="It's... it's the Oliver Wolf Eyeball I needed! Thank you, adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue9110202"]="(Ingael begins to blush.) Umm... Have you met the beautiful, gentle enchanter Eufemiah in Geffen? You see, the relationship between her and me all began with the Oliver Wolf hood on my head.",
    ["Dialogue9110203"]="No! This is a wolf! Well... In fact, she thought it was a husky as well. She absolutely loved it when she first saw it, but still she's convinced it's nothing more than husky fur. I know how good I am at making headgear. I just want her to know what I can really do.",
    ["Dialogue9110204"]="I hope to make some Oliver Wolf Headgear that can really make her feel my heroic spirit, then give it to her... and then tell her how I feel! So, adventurer... You have to help me! Since we were lucky enough to meet like this, you can help me collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolf Pelts</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coarse Fur</color> from Desert Wolves. I'm counting on you!",
    ["Dialogue9110301"]="Hmm... Now we have all the necessary materials, I can start making it. Thank you very much, adventurer. Ah! Well, now that you've already helped me so much, you wouldn't mind doing me one last little favor, would you?",
    ["Dialogue9110302"]="You're so kind, handsome, and talented. I knew you wouldn't turn me down. I want to put some special incense on this headgear to fully reflect my unique feelings for her. So, please go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color> outside the city and fetch some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papyrus</color>!",
    ["Dialogue9110401"]="Now everything is finally ready. Adventurer, take a look. Does this Oliver Wolf Headgear fill you with a sense of heroism? Doesn't it demonstrate the skill and passion of an excellent headgear maker and convey the depth of his taste, his eye for beauty, and his understanding of the noble wolf? I really am quite a genius! Hahaha...",
    ["Dialogue9110402"]="I know, I know, you want to praise my brilliant work. It's okay to be lost for words in the face of such genius. But instead of flattering me, why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take this headdress to Eufemiah</color> for me and try to find out what she thinks of it? Ahem... Just tell her it was made exclusively for her by the talented headgear maker Ingael, Midgard's one and only.",
    ["Dialogue9110501"]="Huh? Adventurer, you don't seem to be here for an enchantment? What is this headgear all about?",
    ["Dialogue9110502"]="Wow, I never thought Ingael could make another husky hood as lovely as the last one! Please thank him for me and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give him</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloak</color> as a gift to pay him back! Now, I have a lot of customers waiting for enchantments! Please excuse me!",
    ["Dialogue9110601"]="This... this... this Cloak! It must be a token of her love! (Ingael dances excitedly with the Cloak.)",
    ["Dialogue9110602"]="Adventurer, there's no need to go into detail. I understand. Thank you so much for all you've done for me today. Without you, I wouldn't have been able to finish that headgear, and I wouldn't have been able to find out how she feels.",
    ["Dialogue9110603"]="(Immersed in his own world, Ingael seems unable to hear you.)\nMaybe I should be more proactive about this. You shouldn't make a girl wait too long! Oh! By the way, adventurer, thank you! You'll always be a friend of mine. Make sure you come and chat with me often!",
    ["Dialogue9120101"]="How dare you say that?! I wouldn't be in this embarrassing situation if you had just told me what Eufemiah said. You're partly responsible for this!",
    ["Dialogue9120102"]="I didn't let you speak? I... Then you shouldn't have let me think Eufemiah liked me! I went ahead and brought her roses, but she turned me away! And to top it all off, a row of annoying mages were passing by at that exact moment! Ahh! I'll never live this down, and it's all your fault!",
    ["Dialogue9120103"]="Basically, you're responsible for this awful way I feel right now! Now what should I do? I need to think this through again, but no matter what, you can't just stand by and watch while I'm falling apart! Hmm... Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juke</color> and get me <color=#CA2E0AFF>two flagons of wine</color> first! Let's take our time about this!",
    ["Dialogue9120201"]="*hiccup* Adventurer, what can I do you for?",
    ["Dialogue9120202"]="And I thought it was a big deal. He's just lovesick, burp! Well, lovesickness wine is all I've got here. See that bottle of Wine of No Worries over there? It was made for just this kind of occasion. You can take some back to your friend, burp!",
    ["Dialogue9120301"]="This looks like some pretty good wine. Let me try it!\n(Ingael takes the flagon and pours the wine into his mouth.)\nMmm... That really hit the spot. Alright, since you got me this wine, I'll forgive you just this once.",
    ["Dialogue9120302"]="I've come to the decision that a talented headgear maker like me shouldn't give up on true love because of a minor setback like this! If Eufemiah can't see how much I like her yet, I'm just gonna have to keep trying! She's currently studying various kinds of armor materials to work out the effects of her enchants, but there's still one she has yet to find. If you can find it for me, it'll make up for everything you've put me through!",
    ["Dialogue9120303"]="I need you to go and bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Whisper's Cloth</color>. I hear she's been looking for this kind of fabric for a long time, so if I can give her some as a gift, she'll no doubt be able to feel how serious I am about her! Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Treasure Ship</color> and find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Whispers</color> there. This is all going to work out!",
    ["Dialogue9120401"]="Yes, that's the stuff! It contains the unique essence of the Whispers. This is going to make Eufemiah's day!",
    ["Dialogue9120402"]="In consideration of your painstaking efforts, I'll write off our misunderstanding this time! I need to move forward without a trace of fear in my heart. I'll give this gift to Eufemiah in person, and with my charm, we'll build a friendship and see where it goes! I know things are going to be okay now!",
    ["Dialogue9120403"]="Wait, don't hurry off just yet! I still have a gift to give you. Although my last attempt failed, I still need to thank you for supporting me so much through all this. That's why I've decided to give you my new Oliver Wolf series, carefully designed by me! Please take it! This is pure Oliver Wolf series, absolutely second to none and with absolutely no husky!",
    ["Dialogue9130101"]="Hi, long time no see! You must have made a lot of new friends. I also went to many new cities and experienced a lot of new things. I recently made friends with a musician. She's a singer named Arielle, and her singing voice is heavenly. It has given me a lot of inspiration. Do you happen to know her?",
    ["Dialogue9130102"]="Oh, great. I just prepared a gift for Arielle. Could you please deliver this to her for me? I heard that she had some problems with her voice recently. This is a special throat remedy for singers. I brewed it based on my memory of its taste. It will definitely help Arielle's voice, which is the most important thing to a singer.",
    ["Dialogue9130201"]="Cough, cough... Sorry, my throat has been a little sensitive lately. What... what is this? It smells very sweet.",
    ["Dialogue9130202"]="So it's Jim's. I can't thank him enough. Cough... Sweet Pear Juice? It's the first time I've heard of such a drink, but I'm sure a singer like him knows best about these kinds of drinks and their effects. I'm sure it'll be useful. Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue9130203"]="Actually, I also happen to have something I want to ask Jim for help with. My good friend Speeka is preparing a banquet for the Nerius Family. She invited me to perform at the event a month ago, but I didn't expect that I would not be able to attend due to my recent voice problem, and the performance is next week.",
    ["Dialogue9130204"]="So... I thought of Jim and wondered if he would be willing to do me the favor of performing a show at the Nerius Family's banquet?",
    ["Dialogue9130301"]="Well? How did Arielle like my gift?",
    ["Dialogue9130302"]="So Arielle's voice has been exhausted to this extent recently? Then she must take her time to recuperate. I do not want this continent to lose such a beautiful, heavenly voice.",
    ["Dialogue9130303"]="No problem. Of course I can perform in her place. But I heard that the Nerius Family is a prestigious noble family. I wonder if I need to specially prepare anything for my performance. My casual attire is probably too sloppy-looking, huh?...",
    ["Dialogue9130401"]="Is... is Jim willing to help me? If it's too much to ask...",
    ["Dialogue9130402"]="Really? I knew I chose the right person. Someone as kind as Jim would definitely help. This will give me peace of mind. Thank you guys so much.",
    ["Dialogue9130403"]="Don't worry. It's true that he needs to prepare fancier clothing for the performance at the Nerius Family's banquet, but since he is willing to help me, I will definitely help him prepare everything he needs. Unfortunately, my tailor-made outfit at Victor Sorrows' only fits women. Adventurer, maybe you can help Jim then. Go to Victor Sorrows to get a magnificent tailor-made performance outfit.",
    ["Dialogue9130404"]="Hmm, let's see. We'll need at least <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Gold</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Silver</color> as a deposit to order the Magnificent Performance Outfit. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Give these materials to Victor Sorrows</color> and tell him that you want a tailor-made performance outfit for the Nerius Family's banquet. He will understand.",
    ["Dialogue9130501"]="Oh? Since you're a customer paying such a large deposit, you must want an expensive and magnificent outfit. What kind of clothing do you need specifically?",
    ["Dialogue9130502"]="So it's a performance attire for the Nerius Family's banquet? It's known to be a grand and lavish event with song and dance. That's why Arielle had her outfit tailor-made here. I wonder who's the artist that needs this men's outfit? You don't look like that person...?",
    ["Dialogue9130503"]="Hey, don't look at me like that. I didn't mean anything by it. Making an outfit like that could take a month. It won't be ready by the time the banquet starts if I have to make a new one from scratch. But... if you are willing to help me out a little, I do have a suitable ready-made outfit in my possession.",
    ["Dialogue9130504"]="Hey, don't look at me like that. So it's for Jimmy Lin, the one who's taken the whole continent by storm. No wonder... Making an outfit like that could take a month. It won't be ready by the time the banquet starts if I have to make a new one from scratch. But... if you are willing to help me out a little, I do have a suitable ready-made outfit in my possession.",
    ["Dialogue9130505"]="I recently received a new batch of orders from the Chamber of Commerce for a series of winter uniforms, which require <color=#CA2E0AFF>sturdy Thin Pelts</color>. If you go get some from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smokies in the Labyrinth Forest</color> and bring them back to me, I will sell you the ready-made Magnificent Performance Outfit. It is an exclusive item I made with meticulous care.",
    ["Dialogue9130601"]="Great work. It's exactly the high-quality fur I needed. Since you helped me collect these furs, I'll sell you my exclusive tailor-made magnificent performance outfit! But remember to remind Jimmy Lin to make good use of it because I spent a whole month putting my heart and sweat into making it. The inlaid gems are the finest in the entire continent of Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue9130701"]="Wow, this outfit really exudes an air of nobility. Attending the Nerius Family's banquet truly requires dressing up. Thank you so much, Adventurer. I will definitely prepare well for this performance.",
    ["Dialogue9130702"]="By the way, to thank you for rushing about for me, I have some gifts for you that I collected during my adventures. I hope you like them.",
    ["Dialogue9140101"]="Hmm... This world should also have fresh Fish Tail, and the juice from these plants should be available at the Sundries Store.",
    ["Dialogue9140102"]="But what would be a good substitute for this? I wonder if the Muka juice here is the same as cactus juice...",
    ["Dialogue9140103"]="Hmm... Hm? Ah! It's you, Adventurer. You scared me haha. Sorry, I was just working on my recipe.",
    ["Dialogue9140104"]="Hahaha. To be more specific, I am working on a seasoning sauce recipe that I created myself. I used to always add it when cooking. It would make even the most ordinary dishes become tasty.",
    ["Dialogue9140105"]="Actually, it's like this. I met a new friend at the Desert Green Tavern in Morroc. Maybe you know her too, Stefanie, the chef. She told me that food ingredients are scarce in Morroc. To let the inhabitants of the desert get a taste of delicious cuisine, she has been researching ways to make even the humblest of desert ingredients appetizing. Therefore, I was reminded of this special sauce of mine.",
    ["Dialogue9140106"]="Don't underestimate my universal sauce. If I succeed in recreating it, it will definitely help Stefanie out. It's just that...",
    ["Dialogue9140107"]="It's just that I still don't know the ingredients of this world that well yet, and I'm not sure I can succeed. There are some things I simply don't know where to get... It's a real headache...",
    ["Dialogue9140108"]="(Jimmy Lin's eyes light up.) That's right. You're here, Adventurer. Please help me collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tails</color>. I'm sure with your help, we can succeed!",
    ["Dialogue9140201"]="Haha, I knew you could do it. With ingredients this fresh, we'll definitely get great results. I'll take care of the final ingredients and prepare for the mixing. Oh yes, there is one more question I wanted to ask you. Are there any non-harmful plants in the desert that can be used to add more flavor? I still need a spice to lock in the aroma of the sauce.",
    ["Dialogue9140202"]="You mean the Rosemary Orchid on the desert borders? Why didn't I think of that? The mild aroma of Rosemary Orchid is most suitable for ingredients from the desert. Could you please go out again and bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rosemary Orchids</color>? I really appreciate it.",
    ["Dialogue9140301"]="Yes... This subtle aroma is a perfect addition to my sauce. I'm sure the result will be fantastic this time.\n(Jimmy Lin carefully crushes the Rosemary Orchid petals and sprinkles them onto the prepared sauce.)",
    ["Dialogue9140302"]="(Jimmy Lin dips his fork into the sauce and tastes it.)\nFantastic! This is the taste I remember. Adventurer, I've finally done it! This is great!",
    ["Dialogue9140303"]="Thank you for your help. I couldn't have completed the sauce without you. Now could you please take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>sauce</color> and its <color=#CA2E0AFF>recipe</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stefanie</color> for me? We share the same ideals. Hopefully this can help her with her culinary research.",
    ["Dialogue9140401"]="Hello, Adventurer. What can I help you with? Everything I sell here are ingredients from the desert. Although they don't look as exuberant as ingredients from other regions, they have a unique flavor to them.",
    ["Dialogue9140402"]="Oh, what's the matter?",
    ["Dialogue9140501"]="This is...? What a unique sauce. It has a mouth-watering aroma. Did you make this?",
    ["Dialogue9140502"]="I see. This is the Special Sauce that Jim has meticulously created. Thank you both for the kind help. I will definitely make good use of the sauce and cherish its precious recipe. One day I will give all people of the desert the chance to taste simple and delicious cuisine. Oh, I just made a brand new dish that seems like it will work really well with this sauce.",
    ["Dialogue9140503"]="(Stefanie carefully adds the adequate amount of sauce to the dish in her hand.)\nMmm... This aroma. It's been brought to life. I'm sure it's going to taste delicious. Adventurer, could you please take this dish back to Jim? I want the first person to taste this be Jim since this is both of our masterpiece.",
    ["Dialogue9140601"]="This is... a dish with the Special Sauce added? Only a culinary master like Stefanie can combine ingredients and the sauce so expertly. Wonderful. I hope the people of Morroc will also be able to taste good cuisine soon. Adventurer, thank you for your constant company and assistance. Actually, I have prepared a gift for you as well. I hope you like it.",
    ["Dialogue9150101"]="Adventurer, please accept my sincerest gratitude. I've gotten all my precious race car models back thanks to your help.",
    ["Dialogue9150102"]="In my world, racing symbolizes perseverance until the very end, an ideal I strive for. These models have been with me for many years, just like my skateboard, so they mean a lot to me. It's just that...\n(Jimmy Lin's gaze falls on the skateboard in his hand, revealing a sense of gloom.)",
    ["Dialogue9150103"]="When I arrived on this continent, I was lonely and lost, but because of you and the company of many other friends, I discovered endless new possibilities from what I thought would be an agonizing fate. I wish to enrich this land with the spirit and culture of my world. However, this skateboard, which has been with me since I realized my aspirations, is showing some signs of problems. I am worried that it may not be able to accompany me in the future.",
    ["Dialogue9150104"]="But I don't even know what's wrong with it, and there's nobody on this continent who knows how to fix a skateboard. I think I may have to give up on it...",
    ["Dialogue9150105"]="A whitesmith? You mean he'll have a way to fix my skateboard?\n(Jimmy Lin's dull gloomy eyes seem to light up again.)",
    ["Dialogue9150106"]="So, I'm counting on you to get it fixed. It really is important to me.",
    ["Dialogue9150201"]="(Howard looks curiously at the skateboard in your hand.)\nWhat is it, Adventurer? Did you come see me about this strange device of yours? Looks quite interesting...",
    ["Dialogue9150202"]="I see. So this curious device is called a skateboard. It's my first time seeing it, but I think devices of this world adhere to the same principles. With a little research, I should be able to find a solution. Why don't you let me take a look at it and go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to get me a book called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mechanic's Log</color>? I think it will be of help.",
    ["Dialogue9150301"]="Oh, you're looking for the Mechanic's Log? That book hasn't been borrowed for a long time. It's on the top of the shelf over there. You can grab it yourself.",
    ["Dialogue9150401"]="(Howard looks like he's very familiar with the handbook as he flips through it nodding frequently.)\nI see. Adventurer, after my initial analysis and consulting the principles in the handbook, I believe I've found the issue. It should have something to do with lubrication of the bearings.",
    ["Dialogue9150402"]="Based on my assessment, if I can create a suitable lubricant, I'll be able to get this skateboard rolling like new again. But for the lubricant mix, I'll need 10 Goldflowers. Its sap is a core component of lubricant. Why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick 10 Goldflowers</color> for me while I prepare the rest of the materials.",
    ["Dialogue9150501"]="You've arrived just in time. I've finished preparing the other materials. Now we just need to add in the Goldflowers to complete it.\n(Howard adds the Goldflowers to the bottle of reagent and shakes it a few times.)",
    ["Dialogue9150502"]="There's no problem now. Let's see if this bottle of lubricant can save this jammed skateboard.\n(Howard carefully pours the lubricant onto the skateboard's four bearings.)",
    ["Dialogue9150503"]="(Howard places the skateboard on the ground and rolls it back and forth with a satisfied smile.)\nAll fixed. The board's good as new. Hurry and take it back to your friend. Tell him he doesn't have to worry about losing his aspirations here and that this land is one brimming with wonders. One must never give up lightly.",
    ["Dialogue9150601"]="My skateboard! It's back to normal. The whitesmith is truly great. Thank you guys so much. It has accompanied me for so many years, always reminding me of my aspirations, to never give up on my beliefs and to have the courage to take risks.",
    ["Dialogue9150602"]="By the way, I actually have a gift for you as well to thank you for all you have done for me. It's also something that I've cherished for many years. I hope you gain strength and inspiration from it, and may it bring you new and exciting experiences.",
    ["Dialogue9160101"]="Dear customer, may I take a moment of your time? Based on your transaction history, the Purchase Shop has determined that you have potential to become an Purchase Shop VIP Customer. However, wealth is only one of our criteria. If you wish to become a VIP Customer candidate, we require you to participate in several tests prepared by the Purchase Shop. Would you be interested in this opportunity?",
    ["Dialogue9160102"]="All right, dear customer. In order to ensure the interests of the Purchase Shop, we need you to prove other aspects of your ability. The Purchase Shop's deliveries are frequently intercepted by monster attacks, so in your first test, we wish for you to go slay <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Savages</color> and bring back <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Jellopies</color>. Prove your courage and strength to the Purchase Shop. I'll be waiting here for your return. May your expedition be a successful one!",
    ["Dialogue9160201"]="Dear customer, you really are a cut above the rest. Congratulations on having completed your first test with the Purchase Shop. The next test assesses your trustworthiness. The Purchase Shop has a long-standing relationship with the general merchant Vienna Lindra. Your tasks are to deliver these precious items to her and bring back our cooperation agreement safely. I am sure you will be able to accomplish this test without a hitch. I'll waiting here for your successful return.",
    ["Dialogue9160301"]="Oh, today is delivery day for the Purchase Shop. Thank you very much for your assistance. I almost forgot.",
    ["Dialogue9160302"]="Sigh, as you can see I've been swamped with work lately. I've signed the agreement. You can take it back now. Thanks for your hard work.",
    ["Dialogue9160401"]="Thank you so much, dear customer. You have completed all the tests to become a VIP customer. We will complete the following procedures for you as soon as possible so that you may enjoy our special services. If you have any questions during this period, you may come speak with me anytime.",
    ["Dialogue9170101"]="(Jakdal is quietly muttering something seemingly unaware of your arrival.)\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>Silk, gold, mink fur... What else? After I get out off work, I'm gonna get that Victor to hurry it up...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue9170102"]="Ooh, you're here. My apologies, I was thinking about today's dinner and didn't notice you.",
    ["Dialogue9170103"]="Uh, that... No, I was saying mink... mink meat with steamed egg requires removal of the fur first... What is it? You wanted to see me about something?",
    ["Dialogue9170104"]="Well... if there's nothing else, I have to get back to work. Let's talk afterwards.\n<size=18><color=#A1979FFF>I can't reveal it until it's completely ready... I wonder if that Victor guy will give it away...</color></size>",
    ["Dialogue9170105"]="(Jakdal turns away to continue with his work, pretending not to have heard you.)",
    ["Dialogue9170201"]="Oh, another new customer that wants a custom outfit today? What kind of clothing do you need, Adventurer? Whether it's formal attire for a banquet or a superstar costume for the stage, I can tailor it all to meet your needs.",
    ["Dialogue9170202"]="Jakdal? You mean the Purchase Shop customer? He did order a custom high-end outfit. It was the most expensive order I've received in recent years.",
    ["Dialogue9170203"]="Yes, i heard that it's for a very important VIP. Due the sophisticated design and expensive materials of this custom outfit of his, a lot of effort and resources has been spent on making it. We're still working on it right now. You'll have to wait 72 hours before you can pick it up.",
    ["Dialogue9170204"]="Mmm, dear customer, don't look so surprised. Our mission is to put the customer first, so meeting the customer's needs is our highest priority. In order to display the distinguished status of this outfit's owner, we are using 999 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gold</color> for the seams. We're also making a custom coat with top-quality <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kobold Fur</color> and creating the waist accessory with pure <color=#CA2E0AFF>Silver</color>. Just acquiring these materials requires great effort.",
    ["Dialogue9170205"]="Before the custom order was placed, Jakdal said he would help us with procuring the materials, but it looks like the Purchase Shop has been extremely busy lately, so he hasn't come by in a long time. It looks like the completion of the outfit is still a long way off.",
    ["Dialogue9170301"]="Oh? Is this the material you collected on behalf of Jakdal? I can't believe that he has such a thoughtful friend. This will speed up the creation process a lot.",
    ["Dialogue9170302"]="This lavish custom outfit is finally complete. Adventurer, how about you deliver it to Jakdal?",
    ["Dialogue9170401"]="Huh? You're holding...?!",
    ["Dialogue9170402"]="Eh!?... Where did you get that information? I wanted to give you a surprise! It must've been that unreliable Victor...",
    ["Dialogue9170403"]="Okay, okay, forget it. The result is the same anyways. I actually made this custom order on behalf of the Purchase Shop to give to you, our distinguished first VIP. This exclusive attire was designed to display your grace and poise, to emphasize your esteemed status. I hope you like it.",
    ["Dialogue9180101"]="Adventurer, you've come to me because of this brilliant Meteor Shard in your hand, haven't you?\n(Hollgrehenn has an excited look on his face as he stares at the Meteor Shard you're holding.)",
    ["Dialogue9180102"]="Hmmm, no, that's not quite it. It's actually not important to me, but to an old buddy of mine!\n(Hollgrehenn points at the Magic Furnace not too far away.)",
    ["Dialogue9180103"]="You must not know it. My old buddy had a very mysterious master back in the day. They say he was a powerful mage, and he's the one who forged the Magic Furnace. For some reason, though, he disappeared after that. Nobody knows just where he went...",
    ["Dialogue9180104"]="I'll let you in on a secret, something I only learned about when my old buddy asked me for help years after we first knew each other. Apparently, before its master departed, he left behind a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Riddle Box</color>. Its master said that when the Magic Furnace solves the riddle, it'll be able to see him once more.",
    ["Dialogue9180105"]="That's right—that legendary Riddle Box can only be opened by a Starlight Key. Because of this, my old buddy's been collecting the materials to forge a Starlight Key, and the most important material is 100 Meteor Shards. Actually, my old buddy has already gathered 99 shards, and fortunately, you've brought the last one today. I'm sure my old buddy will be really happy. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>give the shard to it</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9180201"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180202"]="My old buddy's thanking you! It hasn't been this happy in ages!",
    ["Dialogue9180203"]="Puff puff—puff... Puff puff—puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180204"]=" I see... I understand. We'll do everything we can to help you. Adventurer, my old buddy told me that in addition to the 100 Meteor Shards, there's a few more materials needed to make the Starlight Key. Surely you'd be willing to help my old buddy out a bit more, right?",
    ["Dialogue9180205"]="Hm... My old buddy said that first, we need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rotten Solid Trunks</color>. Hm... Let me think... You should be able to get some from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Willows growing in</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color>. We're counting on you, Adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue9180301"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180302"]="Hahaha, seems like you're starting to understand my old friend's language! But I'm guessing you couldn't make out any of the other materials it mentioned. Actually, we still need a few things to make the Starlight Key. Looks like I'll have to ask you to help gather them again.",
    ["Dialogue9180303"]="Hm... Let me think... We need <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 pieces of Iron Ore</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 pieces of Muspellium</color>.Yep, once we have those two things, I assure you, we can easily make a Starlight Key.",
    ["Dialogue9180401"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180402"]="Excellent! My old friend says that's all the materials we need. Now we can forge the Starlight Key. Seems like my old friend needs a moment to work. Once the key is made, we can open the Riddle Box. Oh, I'm getting excited just thinking about it!",
    ["Dialogue9180403"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180404"]="The key is finished! Come here, Adventurer. Come <color=#CA2E0AFF>take</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>key</color> from Drubby!",
    ["Dialogue9180501"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180502"]="I know, don't worry, old friend. We'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>open</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Riddle Box</color>. Adventurer, come <color=#CA2E0AFF>use</color> that <color=#CA2E0AFF>key</color> you've got to open it.\n(Hollgrehenn pulls out a glowing, silver box from who-knows-where. There is a shiny, colorful keyhole on the front of the box.)",
    ["Dialogue9180601"]="It's open! The Riddle Box is finally open. Come on, old friend, look and see what riddle your master left you! \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Revelation of Starlight</color>\"? Is this the title of the riddle?",
    ["Dialogue9180602"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9180701"]="This riddle... It seems so profound. Why can't I make heads or tails of it? Old friend, can you understand what your master is saying?",
    ["Dialogue9180702"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9190101"]="Puff puff—puff—\n(The Magic Furnace's flames jump in a particularly excited way.)",
    ["Dialogue9190102"]="Let me have a chat with my old friend, Adventurer. I think it must've encountered something really happy to make it jump for joy like this!",
    ["Dialogue9190103"]="Yes! That's great! Adventurer, my old friend told me about some things hinted at in Revelation of Starlight. It's already got everything it needs. Thanks to your help, it'll meet its master soon. That's why it's so happy!",
    ["Dialogue9190104"]="That's a good question. Because according to the hints in the Revelation of Starlight, apart from collecting these materials to guide the departed back, it doesn't mention how exactly to guide them. However, I've heard the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Material Merchant Sampson</color> is quite curious about these strange, paranormal-type things. Perhaps he'll know about the Revelation of Starlight. How about you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>pay him a visit</color>?",
    ["Dialogue9190201"]="Oh-ho! You've got quite the mysterious aura on you, Adventurer. How exciting! So, what is it? Do you have anything special to give me?",
    ["Dialogue9190202"]="Oh? The Revelation of Starlight? That does ring a bell! Wait just a moment, I'm sure I can find it!\n(Sampson hurriedly rummages around in his backpack as he mutters something to himself.)",
    ["Dialogue9190203"]="I found it! I knew I'd seen this name somewhere. It took me a while to find, but according to this ancient letter, the Revelation of Starlight is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>formula for a type of ancient medicine</color>. Legend has it that it can guide specific spirits back home and <color=#CA2E0AFF>make them reappear</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9190204"]="Oh... No, there's no record of that in this letter. But I know where we can find it. From what I know, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>'s <color=#CA2E0AFF>library</color> should have a book called <color=#CA2E0AFF>A Compendium of Ancient Medicinal Formulas</color>. But I can't say for sure if Norten will be willing to lend it out to you.",
    ["Dialogue9190301"]="The library is a place of learning. People with other intentions are not welcome. What do you want?",
    ["Dialogue9190302"]="A Compendium of Ancient Medicinal Formulas? What do you need that for? We won't give those evil-minded merchants material to curry favor with. Those ancient, traditional prescriptions have no practical use now. They only have academic value now.",
    ["Dialogue9190303"]="Oh? I see... Seeing as this was the last wish left by our one of our forebearers a hundred years ago, I'll help you this once. The book is on the third shelf behind me. Go and get it yourself. But remember! Never use it for personal gain. If you do, I won't let you off easily!",
    ["Dialogue9190401"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["Dialogue9190402"]="Adventurer, how did it go? Did you get any information? What did you give my old friend...?\n(Hollgrehenn questions you earnestly and anxiously.)",
    ["Dialogue9190403"]="I see. Old friend, did you hear that? I think now you'll be able to make the Revenant Water from this recipe!",
    ["Dialogue9190404"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9190501"]="Great! My old friend is finally going to see his master. I'm so curious about what kind of person this legendary mage is!",
    ["Dialogue9190502"]="Puff puff... Puff puff...",
    ["Dialogue9190503"]="Don't worry, old friend, we're here to help you find your master. Adventurer, go pour this bottle of Revenant Water on the ground in front of my old friend.",
    ["Dialogue9190601"]="Long time, no see my child. You've finally arrived!",
    ["Dialogue9190602"]="Puff puff puff—puff—\n(The Magic Furnace's flames jump with joy. It's like a child seeing its mother for the first time in a long time.)",
    ["Dialogue9190603"]="(Swick's soul gently touches the outer wall of the Magic Furnace with a gentle look in his eyes.)\nYou were still young when I left you. To keep you shining on this continent and protect you from being used by evil forces, I left the Revelation of Starlight and used my last bit of power to leave a final piece of my soul in the world of the living, waiting for the day when you might unlock it.",
    ["Dialogue9190604"]="Sure enough you didn't disappoint me. You were able to open the Riddle Box and create the Revenant Water. You've become an intelligent, mature Magic Furnace. I'm sure you already have your own friends and thoughts. Now, I can rest easy.\n(As Swick speaks, he turns and smiles at you and Hollgrehenn with a gratified look on his face.)",
    ["Dialogue9190605"]="Puff puff—puff—\n(The Magic Furnace's flames jump. It seems to be acting like a spoiled child.)",
    ["Dialogue9190606"]="Now, let me <color=#CA2E0AFF>give you this all-new power</color> that I prepared. I'm sure you're able to distinguish right from wrong and use these powers for good. Don't worry, my child. My spirit will always be with you. You will never be lonely.\n(Swick's soul slowly transforms into a dark blue light that goes into the Magic Furnace. The Magic Furnace's flames seem to jump with more liveliness.)",
    ["Dialogue9190607"]="Puff puff—puff—\n(The Magic Furnace's flames jump. It seems to make a whimpering sound.)",
    ["Dialogue9200101"]="Hi, long time no see! You must have made a lot of new friends. I also went to many new cities and experienced a lot of new things. I recently made friends with a musician. She's a singer named Arielle, and her singing voice is heavenly. It has given me a lot of inspiration. Do you happen to know her?",
    ["Dialogue9200102"]="Oh, great. I just prepared a gift for Arielle. Could you please deliver this to her for me? I heard that she had some problems with her voice recently. This is a special throat remedy for singers. I brewed it based on my memory of its taste. It will definitely help Arielle's voice, which is the most important thing to a singer.",
    ["Dialogue9200201"]="Cough, cough... Sorry, my throat has been a little sensitive lately. What... what is this? It smells very sweet.",
    ["Dialogue9200202"]="Ah, it was Schumann, thank him so much. Oh, sugar pear juice? I've never heard of such a drink, but a singer like him can't be wrong and I'm sure this will be useful. Thank you, adventurer.",
    ["Dialogue9200203"]="My friend Speeka is preparing for the Nerius Family's banquet and she invited me to perform for them a month ago, but I'm afraid I will disappoint her as I am having voice problems. The performance is set to be next week and I don't think I can attend in my current state.",
    ["Dialogue9200204"]="So... I thought of Schumann and wondered if he would be willing to do me this favor and perform at the Nerius Family's banquet?",
    ["Dialogue9200301"]="Well? How did Arielle like my gift?",
    ["Dialogue9200302"]="So Arielle's voice has been exhausted to this extent recently? Then she must take her time to recuperate. I do not want this continent to lose such a beautiful, heavenly voice.",
    ["Dialogue9200303"]="No problem. Of course I can perform in her place. But I heard that the Nerius Family is a prestigious noble family. I wonder if I need to specially prepare anything for my performance. My casual attire is probably too sloppy-looking, huh?...",
    ["Dialogue9200401"]="Would… would Schumann help me? If he really cannot…",
    ["Dialogue9200402"]="Really? I knew someone as kind as Schumann would be willing to help me. This will give me peace of mind. Thank you all so much.",
    ["Dialogue9200403"]="Don't worry, you do have to prepare a gorgeous performance costume to perform for the Nerius family, but since he is willing to help me, I will definitely help him prepare everything he needs. Unfortunately, my custom-made costume from Victor Sorrows is a women's costume. Adventurer, maybe you can help Schumann. Go to Victor Sorrows to customize a magnificent performance costume.",
    ["Dialogue9200404"]="Hmm, let's see. We'll need at least <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Gold</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Silver</color> as a deposit to order the Magnificent Performance Outfit. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Give these materials to Victor Sorrows</color> and tell him that you want a tailor-made performance outfit for the Nerius Family's banquet. He will understand.",
    ["Dialogue9200501"]="Oh? Since you're a customer paying such a large deposit, you must want an expensive and magnificent outfit. What kind of clothing do you need specifically?",
    ["Dialogue9200502"]="So it's a performance attire for the Nerius Family's banquet? It's known to be a grand and lavish event with song and dance. That's why Arielle had her outfit tailor-made here. I wonder who's the artist that needs this men's outfit? You don't look like that person...?",
    ["Dialogue9200503"]="Hey, don't look at me like that. I didn't mean anything by it. Making an outfit like that could take a month. It won't be ready by the time the banquet starts if I have to make a new one from scratch. But... if you are willing to help me out a little, I do have a suitable ready-made outfit in my possession.",
    ["Dialogue9200504"]="Hey, don't look at me like that. Oh, it's for the very famous Schumann. I see... Customizing a costume like that usually takes about a month, and I don't think you have that much time. But... if you can do me a little favor, I do have a costume ready for him.",
    ["Dialogue9200505"]="I recently received a new batch of orders from the Chamber of Commerce for a series of winter uniforms, which require <color=#CA2E0AFF>sturdy Thin Pelts</color>. If you go get some from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smokies in the Labyrinth Forest</color> and bring them back to me, I will sell you the ready-made Magnificent Performance Outfit. It is an exclusive item I made with meticulous care.",
    ["Dialogue9200601"]="Great job! I really need the best furs. Since you helped me collect these furs, I will sell you my gorgeous custom-made performance ccostume! Make good use of it - I spent a whole month on it and used the best gems found anywhere on the entire continent of Midgard.",
    ["Dialogue9200701"]="Wow, this outfit really exudes an air of nobility. Attending the Nerius Family's banquet truly requires dressing up. Thank you so much, Adventurer. I will definitely prepare well for this performance.",
    ["Dialogue9200702"]="By the way, to thank you for rushing about for me, I have some gifts for you that I collected during my adventures. I hope you like them.",
    ["Dialogue9210101"]="Hmm... This world should also have fresh Fish Tail, and the juice from these plants should be available at the Sundries Store.",
    ["Dialogue9210102"]="But what would be a good substitute for this? I wonder if the Muka juice here is the same as cactus juice...",
    ["Dialogue9210103"]="Hmm... Hm? Ah! It's you, Adventurer. You scared me haha. Sorry, I was just working on my recipe.",
    ["Dialogue9210104"]="Hahaha. To be more specific, I am working on a seasoning sauce recipe that I created myself. I used to always add it when cooking. It would make even the most ordinary dishes become tasty.",
    ["Dialogue9210105"]="Actually, it's like this. I met a new friend at the Desert Green Tavern in Morroc. Maybe you know her too, Stefanie, the chef. She told me that food ingredients are scarce in Morroc. To let the inhabitants of the desert get a taste of delicious cuisine, she has been researching ways to make even the humblest of desert ingredients appetizing. Therefore, I was reminded of this special sauce of mine.",
    ["Dialogue9210106"]="Don't underestimate my universal sauce. If I succeed in recreating it, it will definitely help Stefanie out. It's just that...",
    ["Dialogue9210107"]="It's just that I still don't know the ingredients of this world that well yet, and I'm not sure I can succeed. There are some things I simply don't know where to get... It's a real headache...",
    ["Dialogue9210108"]="(Schumann's eyes light up) Right, you are still here. Adventurer, please help me collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tail</color>. With your help, I'm sure we can succeed!",
    ["Dialogue9210201"]="Haha, I knew you could do it. With ingredients this fresh, we'll definitely get great results. I'll take care of the final ingredients and prepare for the mixing. Oh yes, there is one more question I wanted to ask you. Are there any non-harmful plants in the desert that can be used to add more flavor? I still need a spice to lock in the aroma of the sauce.",
    ["Dialogue9210202"]="You mean the Rosemary Orchid on the desert borders? Why didn't I think of that? The mild aroma of Rosemary Orchid is most suitable for ingredients from the desert. Could you please go out again and bring me some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rosemary Orchids</color>? I really appreciate it.",
    ["Dialogue9210301"]="Ha, this subtle aroma is perfect for my sauce. I think it will be a big hit this time. \n (Schumann carefully rubbed the petals of Rosemary Orchid into the prepared sauce)",
    ["Dialogue9210302"]="(Schumann dips his fork into the sauce and has a taste) \n Wonderful! This is exactly the taste I remember. Adventurer, I finally made it! How great!",
    ["Dialogue9210303"]="Thank you for your help. I couldn't have completed the sauce without you. Now could you please take this <color=#CA2E0AFF>sauce</color> and its <color=#CA2E0AFF>recipe</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stefanie</color> for me? We share the same ideals. Hopefully this can help her with her culinary research.",
    ["Dialogue9210401"]="Hello, Adventurer. What can I help you with? Everything I sell here are ingredients from the desert. Although they don't look as exuberant as ingredients from other regions, they have a unique flavor to them.",
    ["Dialogue9210402"]="Oh, what's the matter?",
    ["Dialogue9210501"]="This is...? What a unique sauce. It has a mouth-watering aroma. Did you make this?",
    ["Dialogue9210502"]="Oh I see, it's a secret sauce developed by Schumann. Thank you for being so kind. I will definitely make the most of it. I will treasure this precious recipe, and one day, I will make simple and delicious dishes available to the people in the desert. By the way, I just made a brand new dish, and it seems to be a good match for this sauce~",
    ["Dialogue9210503"]="(Stefanie carefully adds a small amount of sauce into the dish she has on hand) \nHmm, this sauce seems to have brought soul to the dish. I believe it must be very delicious. Adventurer, why don't you take this dish back to Schumann. I want him to be the first one to taste this dish. It's our joint masterpiece.",
    ["Dialogue9210601"]="This is... a dish with the Special Sauce added? Only a culinary master like Stefanie can combine ingredients and the sauce so expertly. Wonderful. I hope the people of Morroc will also be able to taste good cuisine soon. Adventurer, thank you for your constant company and assistance. Actually, I have prepared a gift for you as well. I hope you like it.",
    ["Dialogue9220101"]="Adventurer, please accept my sincerest gratitude. I've gotten all my precious race car models back thanks to your help.",
    ["Dialogue9220102"]="To me, car racing is about never giving up or losing hope even at the last moment. It is also an important dream of mine. They have been with me for many years and are important to me, just like my skateboards, but...\n (Schumann looks at his skateboard, and there seems to be a hint of gloom in his eyes)",
    ["Dialogue9220103"]="When I arrived on this continent, I was lonely and lost, but because of you and the company of many other friends, I discovered endless new possibilities from what I thought would be an agonizing fate. I wish to enrich this land with the spirit and culture of my world. However, this skateboard, which has been with me since I realized my aspirations, is showing some signs of problems. I am worried that it may not be able to accompany me in the future.",
    ["Dialogue9220104"]="But I don't even know what's wrong with it, and there's nobody on this continent who knows how to fix a skateboard. I think I may have to give up on it...",
    ["Dialogue9220105"]="Whitesmith? You mean he can fix my skateboard? \n (Schumann's eyes seem to light up again)",
    ["Dialogue9220106"]="So, I'm counting on you to get it fixed. It really is important to me.",
    ["Dialogue9220201"]="(Howard looks curiously at the skateboard in your hand.)\nWhat is it, Adventurer? Did you come see me about this strange device of yours? Looks quite interesting...",
    ["Dialogue9220202"]="I see. So this curious device is called a skateboard. It's my first time seeing it, but I think devices of this world adhere to the same principles. With a little research, I should be able to find a solution. Why don't you let me take a look at it and go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to get me a book called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mechanic's Log</color>? I think it will be of help.",
    ["Dialogue9220301"]="Oh, you're looking for the Mechanic's Log? That book hasn't been borrowed for a long time. It's on the top of the shelf over there. You can grab it yourself.",
    ["Dialogue9220401"]="(Howard looks like he's very familiar with the handbook as he flips through it nodding frequently.)\nI see. Adventurer, after my initial analysis and consulting the principles in the handbook, I believe I've found the issue. It should have something to do with lubrication of the bearings.",
    ["Dialogue9220402"]="Based on my assessment, if I can create a suitable lubricant, I'll be able to get this skateboard rolling like new again. But for the lubricant mix, I'll need 10 Goldflowers. Its sap is a core component of lubricant. Why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick 10 Goldflowers</color> for me while I prepare the rest of the materials.",
    ["Dialogue9220501"]="You've arrived just in time. I've finished preparing the other materials. Now we just need to add in the Goldflowers to complete it.\n(Howard adds the Goldflowers to the bottle of reagent and shakes it a few times.)",
    ["Dialogue9220502"]="There's no problem now. Let's see if this bottle of lubricant can save this jammed skateboard.\n(Howard carefully pours the lubricant onto the skateboard's four bearings.)",
    ["Dialogue9220503"]="(Howard places the skateboard on the ground and rolls it back and forth with a satisfied smile.)\nAll fixed. The board's good as new. Hurry and take it back to your friend. Tell him he doesn't have to worry about losing his aspirations here and that this land is one brimming with wonders. One must never give up lightly.",
    ["Dialogue9220601"]="My skateboard! It's back to normal. The mastersmith is truly great. Thank you guys so much. It has accompanied me for so many years, always reminding me of my aspirations, to never give up on my beliefs and to have the courage to take risks.",
    ["Dialogue9220602"]="By the way, I actually have a gift for you as well to thank you for all you have done for me. It's also something that I've cherished for many years. I hope you gain strength and inspiration from it, and may it bring you new and exciting experiences.",
    ["Dialogue9230101"]="Yawn...",
    ["Dialogue9230102"]="Hmm, a bit. There hasn't been much excitement lately.",
    ["Dialogue9230103"]="Usually I'd play <color=#CA2E0AFF>horror games</color>, but I can't do that in this world.",
    ["Dialogue9230104"]="Even a haunted house would suffice. But aren't most of the haunted houses here quite dangerous?",
    ["Dialogue9230105"]="How I wish I could walk around inside a <color=#CA2E0AFF>spooky</color> place!",
    ["Dialogue9230201"]="All these places are spooky. Let me see.",
    ["Dialogue9230202"]="Munak Cave, the Pyramid, the Geffen... Do you want me to pick one? Hm...",
    ["Dialogue9230203"]="Let me think a bit...",
    ["Dialogue9230204"]="I want to go all of them! But let's check out <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak Cave</color> first. I've always wanted to see what's inside!",
    ["Dialogue9230205"]="Yes, let's go!",
    ["Dialogue9230301"]="Compared with those fake haunted houses, this place is definitely spooky...",
    ["Dialogue9230302"]="No way! This is what I love! Let's keep exploring!",
    ["Dialogue9230303"]="Oh, right! We should take a picture to <color=#CA2E0AFF>commemorate</color> our experience in a real haunted house!",
    ["Dialogue9230401"]="Ahh! That was so scary! Phew...",
    ["Dialogue9230402"]="I was so focused on snapping pictures that I didn't notice the Buddha statue. It frightened the life out of me when I turned around!",
    ["Dialogue9230403"]="Don't laugh at me! Pfft...",
    ["Dialogue9230404"]="Hahahaha!",
    ["Dialogue9230405"]="This place sure is exciting! Thank you!",
    ["Dialogue9230406"]="You've been a wonderful friend, looking after me, giving me gifts, and taking me on adventures.",
    ["Dialogue9230407"]="I feel bad that I'm the one that gets all the presents! Actually, I <color=#CA2E0AFF>have some things</color> for you as well. It's just there wasn't a good time to give them to you.",
    ["Dialogue9230408"]="It's a bit weird giving a gift in Munak Cave. But at least the timing is right. Enjoy!",
    ["Dialogue9240101"]="Woo... Aroo!\n(It trembles with fear.)",
    ["Dialogue9240102"]="Gru...\n(Defensively, it leans back and arches its back.)",
    ["Dialogue9240103"]="Woof! Aroo!\n(Frightened, it runs off.)",
    ["Dialogue9240201"]="Aroo...\n(It looks at you, less afraid.)",
    ["Dialogue9240202"]="(It walks towards you, wagging its tail.)",
    ["Dialogue9240203"]="(You notice a number <color=#CA2E0AFF>9</color> on the collar. Looks like it has an owner.)",
    ["Dialogue9240301"]="Woof! Woof!\n(All of a sudden, it leaps and tugs on your clothes.)",
    ["Dialogue9240302"]="Woof!\n(It runs back and forth, as if beckoning you to follow it.)",
    ["Dialogue9240303"]="Woof!\n(It hops and dashes towards Ant Cavern.)",
    ["Dialogue9240401"]="Woof! Woof!\n(It faces the cavern's interior. Something appears to be inside.)",
    ["Dialogue9240402"]="Woof! Woof!\n(It glances at you and then runs straight inside.)",
    ["Dialogue9240501"]="Aroo! Woof! Woof!\n(Happy, it rushes and rubs against the cat.)",
    ["Dialogue9240502"]="Meow...\n(As the cat crouches, you notice it is also wearing a collar with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>9</color>.)",
    ["Dialogue9240503"]="Woo...\n(It stares at you with its big, watery eyes.)",
    ["Dialogue9240504"]="(It follows the dog and looks at you, too.)",
    ["Dialogue9240601"]="I was so worried. I thought I'd lost you...\n(The girl hugs the cat and dog, her eyes welling up.)",
    ["Dialogue9240602"]="Thank you so much! We got separated on our way here and I couldn't go look for them. That's why I asked someone to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put up a poster</color> for me.",
    ["Dialogue9240603"]="I was worried no one would help me. Thank you so much!",
    ["Dialogue9240604"]="We came from <color=#CA2E0AFF>another world</color>. But for some reason, I arrived in Payon and they ended up somewhere else. We're so lucky to have you!",
    ["Dialogue9240605"]="But we can't keep living like this. Actually, you're the first person I've told in this world.",
    ["Dialogue9240606"]="We don't seem to be able to find our way back, so the most crucial thing is to settle down.",
    ["Dialogue9240607"]="Really? You're so kind! I don't know anyone around here. I might have to bother you a lot in the future!",
    ["Dialogue9250101"]="Have you noticed something off about Pattie?",
    ["Dialogue9250102"]="It's not good. But we don't know how to send her back. Plus, I don't want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>part with her</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9250103"]="All we can do is to try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>cheer her up</color>. But how?",
    ["Dialogue9250104"]="Simply show her how much we care about her. But remember to keep it a <color=#CA2E0AFF>surprise</color>! You go get the materials, and I'll make the gift.",
    ["Dialogue9250201"]="You guys...",
    ["Dialogue9250202"]="We noticed you've been a bit down lately, so we wanted to cheer you up a little.",
    ["Dialogue9250203"]="Although we can't send you back, we hope you can...",
    ["Dialogue9250204"]="Oh, this is awkward...",
    ["Dialogue9250205"]="(She takes out a few things from behind her back.) I thought I'd <color=#CA2E0AFF>surprise</color> you first... Thank you for keeping me company.",
    ["Dialogue9250206"]="Those are...",
    ["Dialogue9250207"]="As I don't know what you like, I just picked things I love. Hope you enjoy them! Haha!",
    ["Dialogue9250208"]="So this is what's been troubling you lately. Oh, wait a minute... I've never met a girl as nice as you... (sniff)",
    ["Dialogue9250209"]="Here, Heflee. I got this hat for you. Let me put it on for you.",
    ["Dialogue9250210"]="And this is for you. Thank you for telling me that I can stay here.",
    ["Dialogue9260101"]="Sigh, it can't keep going on like this.",
    ["Dialogue9260102"]="Have you noticed how empty the tavern is? We're getting fewer and fewer customers.",
    ["Dialogue9260103"]="I wouldn't be so frustrated if I knew!",
    ["Dialogue9260104"]="Since you asked, would you mind looking into it? Even though I don't have any customers, I can't just leave during business hours.",
    ["Dialogue9260201"]="Huh? What can I do for you?",
    ["Dialogue9260202"]="Heflee said...",
    ["Dialogue9260203"]="I see. I can't say I know the whole story, but I do know something.",
    ["Dialogue9260204"]="Just follow me and you'll know.",
    ["Dialogue9260301"]="I see. It makes sense now.",
    ["Dialogue9260302"]="Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue9260303"]="Oh, sorry! You mean what should we do? Let me think...",
    ["Dialogue9260304"]="We can't just do nothing, but we can't send her away either. What can do about this nice girl?",
    ["Dialogue9260305"]="Ah! I know! Why not ask her to come to Desert Green Tavern?",
    ["Dialogue9260306"]="If you say she's the cause, then the problem will be solved if she moves!",
    ["Dialogue9260307"]="Why would someone so beautiful stand outside in such bad weather? If you offer her the chance to stay in the tavern, she'll gladly accept!",
    ["Dialogue9260308"]="But to keep the story consistent, I can't go. Please speak with her for me, adventurer. This is a win-win situation for both her and me, no, a win-win-win situation for all three of us!",
    ["Dialogue9260401"]="Hi! Is something the matter?",
    ["Dialogue9260402"]="I was still undecided on what to do. But it seems I can't hide it any longer.",
    ["Dialogue9260403"]="Yeah. I wonder if you could help me. I'm from another world.",
    ["Dialogue9260404"]="I'd love to go back. But first, I need to find a place to stay. You look like a good person, and that's why I decided to tell you. Please help me.",
    ["Dialogue9260405"]="Great! I'll go right away! You're are a good person!",
    ["Dialogue9270101"]="Tsk, what to do, what to do...?",
    ["Dialogue9270102"]="You brought The TOYS here not too long ago, didn't you? Not only does he perform at the tavern, but he also takes the time to come here and read. He finished reading all the books on history and monsters these past few days!",
    ["Dialogue9270103"]="Not only that, he wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go on an adventure himself</color>! It sure is worrying.",
    ["Dialogue9270104"]="The problem is he's not a trained adventurer, so we need to keep his <color=#CA2E0AFF>safety</color> in mind. Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue9270105"]="If you're willing, then I can think of no better solution. After all, your dependability will put me at ease the most! Haha!",
    ["Dialogue9270201"]="Hey, friend! Are you going on another adventure soon? Are you thinking about bringing me along?",
    ["Dialogue9270202"]="Haha, I see. Then that's great! I've been thinking about this for a long time!",
    ["Dialogue9270203"]="Look, while I was reading, I drew up this <color=#CA2E0AFF>route</color>. I think for my first adventure, it'd be best to go visit each of these places.",
    ["Dialogue9270204"]="How about it? What do you think of this route? Before we set off on an adventure, we need total preparation for everything to go smoothly!",
    ["Dialogue9270205"]="Well then, no time to waste! Let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>set off</color>! I'll go get my things. Give me just a moment!",
    ["Dialogue9270301"]="Phew! I never thought I'd be able to travel around the world of Ragnarok! I'm so happy I could burst!",
    ["Dialogue9270302"]="Of course! This is one of my <color=#CA2E0AFF>favorite games</color>! Oh, it's almost time for us to head back, isn't it?",
    ["Dialogue9270303"]="Before we head back, how about we get a souvenir for Rowan? It's a shame he was too busy to come with us.",
    ["Dialogue9270401"]="Heh, thanks, friend. Wait right here for a moment!",
    ["Dialogue9270402"]="Actually, asking you to take him out was part of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>plan</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9270403"]="That's right! Come look at what we prepared for you!",
    ["Dialogue9270404"]="You're the one who brought him here, after all, and you're more or less the first person he met in this world.",
    ["Dialogue9270405"]="Besides, you've been taking care of him all this time, so it makes sense to thank you...",
    ["Dialogue9270406"]="That's right! Here, take it!",
    ["Dialogue9280101"]="What should we do?",
    ["Dialogue9280102"]="Long story short, it's because I lost contact with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pen pal</color>.",
    ["Dialogue9280103"]="Usually he replies really quickly, but it's been a while now. I'm worried about him, but I don't have any other way to contact him.",
    ["Dialogue9280104"]="I need to stay at the Library, and I don't have time to go look into this. So, could I ask you to keep an eye out for any news about my pen pal?",
    ["Dialogue9280105"]="I know his stage name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>The TOYS</color>. He's a person who's <color=#CA2E0AFF>devoted to music</color>, but I don't have any information on him... I'm sorry.",
    ["Dialogue9280201"]="Keh keh! Is there anything I can do for you?",
    ["Dialogue9280202"]="Rowan did send and receive several letters, keh keh. <color=#CA2E0AFF>The TOYS</color>... I do recall that name. Hmm...",
    ["Dialogue9280203"]="Keh... No, but as Prontera's most professional courier, I should at least have an understanding of mailing addresses, but I don't know this person's address. How strange, keh keh.",
    ["Dialogue9280301"]="... I... This is...",
    ["Dialogue9280302"]="Ah, wait! A-Aren't you a Ragnarok legend?!",
    ["Dialogue9280303"]="You are, aren't you? You are! Th-Then this place is the world of Ragnarok, isn't it?! (He looks at himself, then looks around for a bit.) Oh my gosh! I'm in the world of Ragnarok!",
    ["Dialogue9280304"]="Ahem. Sorry. Is there anyone here named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rowan</color>?",
    ["Dialogue9280305"]="Then I've got the right place! I'm his <color=#CA2E0AFF>friend</color>. Could you take me to him?",
    ["Dialogue9280401"]="And... this is...?",
    ["Dialogue9280402"]="So this is what you look like, Rowan! I'm <color=#CA2E0AFF>The TOYS</color>! Do you remember me?",
    ["Dialogue9280403"]="... Huh?",
    ["Dialogue9280404"]="Hmm, so you're my missing friend, and you came here from another world...",
    ["Dialogue9280405"]="Yeah! Didn't I always say I wanted to come here?",
    ["Dialogue9280406"]="You really had me worried there!",
    ["Dialogue9280407"]="But I'm glad to see you're alright, hahaha! As for how you came here, let's not talk about it for now. Since you're a guest here, we should get you a place to stay.",
    ["Dialogue9280408"]="Let's chat a bit first!",
    ["Dialogue9280409"]="You're the one who brought him here, right? Thank you! I was right to come to you!",
    ["Dialogue9280410"]="No way! If you hadn't found me, I bet I'd still be wandering around in the wilderness! You really are a great adventurer!",
    ["Dialogue9280411"]="Alright, The TOYS. If you want to stay here... Let me think... Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Rose Tavern</color>. Tell them Rowan sent you. Maybe they'll let you perform there.",
    ["Dialogue9280412"]="Sounds good to me. To Red Rose Tavern!",
    ["Dialogue9290101"]="冒险者，今天真是哈维尔的好日子！你知道为什么吗？\n（哈维尔的眼睛亮闪闪地盯着你，毛绒绒的尾巴在身后欢快地左右甩动）",
    ["Dialogue9290102"]="\"（不等你继续追问，哈维尔已经迫不及待地揭晓谜底）\n因为本喵的愿望已经实现了喵！很快就能领到吃不完的小鱼干，本喵再也不用每天早起钓鱼，然后被蚊子咬的满头包了！\"",
    ["Dialogue9290103"]="你看那边！许愿树回应了本喵的愿望！\n（哈维尔指向<color=#CA2E0AFF>许愿树下的美丽身影</color>）\n这样优雅的身姿，天使一般的面容，她……她的名字一定是阿芙洛狄忒！",
    ["Dialogue9290104"]="\"可是……本喵不知道怎么和天使开口……直接伸手说“给我小鱼干”会不会被天使讨厌呢……\n（哈维尔耷拉着脑袋，低头摆弄起自己的猫爪）\"",
    ["Dialogue9290105"]="冒险者……要不……你替本喵领回小鱼干？本喵知道继承奥丁血脉的冒险者一定可以的!",
    ["Dialogue9290201"]="你好，异世界的陌生人~\n（许愿树下的天使提起裙摆优雅施礼）",
    ["Dialogue9290202"]="（天使小姐的侧脸染上一丝微粉）\n谢谢你的赞美，陌生人。不过我的家可不在天堂，而是在一个名为<color=#CA2E0AFF>韩国</color>的地方。",
    ["Dialogue9290203"]="异世界？那这里是？",
    ["Dialogue9290204"]="（天使小姐不可置信地指向远处的哈维尔）\n那么……刚才一直注视着我们的猫人，也不是特型演员吗？",
    ["Dialogue9290205"]="总觉得他很想和我说话，但又很害羞的样子……虽然互不认识，有些话还是直接说比较好哦~都憋在心里的话，会让毛色变暗的~",
    ["Dialogue9290301"]="你回来啦！啊啊啊喵！你把天使带回来了喵！怎么办怎么办，本喵今天没有好好梳毛就出门了！",
    ["Dialogue9290302"]="你好，我是林允儿~",
    ["Dialogue9290303"]="原来是允芙洛狄忒！啊可是……如果是<color=#CA2E0AFF>允芙洛狄忒</color>，就不能给本喵带来吃不完的小鱼干了……",
    ["Dialogue9290304"]="呜呜呜……小鱼干没了……哈维尔又要变成自给自足的哈维尔了……<color=#CA2E0AFF>哈维尔肚子好饿</color>……",
    ["Dialogue9290305"]="许愿树都是假的！假的！骗人！呜呜……呜呜呜……\n（哈维尔的哭声越来越大，很快在地上打起了滚）",
    ["Dialogue9290306"]="呜呜呜……",
    ["Dialogue9290307"]="你居然要打一只可爱的猫猫！呜呜……呜呜呜……还是一只饿着肚子的小猫……\n（哈维尔委屈地瞪了你一眼，似乎得不到鱼就不会起来）",
    ["Dialogue9290308"]="真的？\n（哈维尔猛地从地上坐了起来）",
    ["Dialogue9290309"]="反正……本喵就在这里等你了！",
    ["Dialogue9290401"]="生的……好饿……\n（哈维尔啃了一口你们给他的鱼，默默吐出两个字）",
    ["Dialogue9290402"]="哈维尔先生，在公共场合打滚哭泣可不是成年猫该做的，也不符合绅士的礼仪哦。",
    ["Dialogue9290403"]="天使小姐……\n（哈维尔的脸色突然变得通红，语气也渐渐弱了下来）",
    ["Dialogue9290404"]="好吧……本喵也不是没有错……天使小姐，你还没有尝试过这个世界的美食吧！要不要和我们<color=#CA2E0AFF>一起去玫瑰红酒馆</color>？那里的酒馆主人可好了，你和她一定能成为好朋友！",
    ["Dialogue9290405"]="当然好呀，我也想多认识一些异世界的朋友呢！",
    ["Dialogue9290501"]="冒险者，在你旁边的这位是？",
    ["Dialogue9290502"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>初次见面，我是林允儿。</color>这里就是玫瑰红酒馆吗，闻到了非常棒的蛋糕香气呢~",
    ["Dialogue9290503"]="哈哈~客人的夸赞总能让人心情愉悦，这是我们新推出的戚风蛋糕，需要长时间低温烘烤。若时间太短会不熟，温度太高的话会烤焦。目前的配方还在改良中，客人也有兴趣？",
    ["Dialogue9290504"]="嗯！在我们的世界里，也有类似名字的蛋糕，而且我也很喜欢烘焙！",
    ["Dialogue9290505"]="太好了！哈维尔，麻烦你去厨房把新做好的蛋糕端出来，不准偷吃哦~",
    ["Dialogue9290506"]="喵！怎么又是我？！",
    ["Dialogue9300101"]="奈斯……你在哪里……",
    ["Dialogue9300102"]="冒险者，你有没有见到一条土黄色的柴犬？它叫<color=#CA2E0AFF>奈斯</color>，是塔克士的宠物，塔克士外出修行时，把奈斯交给我照顾，可就在昨天，奈斯突然跑了出去，现在还没有回来……",
    ["Dialogue9300103"]="好吧……如果你见到它，请一定要告诉我！奈斯肚子是奶白色的，眉毛上方有两个白点，是很亲近人的狗狗……",
    ["Dialogue9300104"]="它最喜欢的是鸡腿，但蔬菜和蛋也会乖乖的吃进去，从不咬人……",
    ["Dialogue9300105"]="诶……你愿意帮我吗？普隆德拉这么大，会很辛苦哦！",
    ["Dialogue9300201"]="你看，脚印是在这里结束的，也就是说……",
    ["Dialogue9300202"]="希望，它没有走太远……",
    ["Dialogue9300301"]="咦，你们怎么都来了？\n（塔克士亲昵地揉搓着奈斯肥嘟嘟的脸颊肉）\n奈斯~是不是你把他们带过来的呀~",
    ["Dialogue9300302"]="这……真对不起，奈斯他可能是闻到我的味道，就跑出来了……奈斯坏狗狗，怎么可以让别人为你担心呢！",
    ["Dialogue9300303"]="好啦好啦~\n（林允儿摸了摸耷拉着狗头的奈斯）\n远隔千里也时常想念，这就是宠物和主人之间的羁绊吧~",
    ["Dialogue9300304"]="嘿嘿……谢谢你们能原谅它！\n（塔克士举起奈斯的狗爪）\n奈斯，向允儿姐姐<color=#CA2E0AFF>道歉</color>！",
    ["Dialogue9300401"]="冒险者，刚才真是辛苦你了，陪我满城找一只小狗，一定跑累了吧。",
    ["Dialogue9300402"]="哈哈，不用担心我~\n（林允儿爽朗一笑）\n只是想起了我们家<color=#CA2E0AFF>莱奥</color>，不知道它现在在干什么呢？",
    ["Dialogue9300403"]="是呀，莱奥是一只纯白色的小可爱，无论什么时候，看到我都会摇着尾巴飞奔过来，是个可爱又聪明的孩子。",
    ["Dialogue9300404"]="我还以为它和我一起来到了米德加兹，看来，它还在家中等我回去呢……",
    ["Dialogue9300405"]="唉，很久没有和莱奥出去散步了，为它预定的狗粮也没有下单，还有狗窝、磨牙棒、飞盘玩具……",
    ["Dialogue9300406"]="就算不能见到，如果能寄一些莱奥喜欢的东西也好……冒险者，这个世界有类似的<color=#CA2E0AFF>宠物用品</color>吗？还有，我的世界和米德加兹，真的没有互通的可能性吗？",
    ["Dialogue9300407"]="宠物用品的订制可以交给我！毕竟我也是宠物训练师嘛，给你们友情价哦~但是如何寄送……冒险者，你有办法吗？",
    ["Dialogue9300501"]="（沃尔玛斯沉思片刻后，对你们摇了摇头）\n冒险者，除了时空裂隙，教会没有任何方法能让两个世界互通，也无法预测下次时空裂隙出现的时间。",
    ["Dialogue9300502"]="世界与世界间的隔绝，是奥丁神对我们的保护。就算你们向他祈求，我想奥丁神也不会答应的。",
    ["Dialogue9300503"]="别急，听说这位少女起初的降落地点，是米德加兹的许愿树？",
    ["Dialogue9300504"]="嗯……那么，不如换一个祈愿对象。我一直认为，<color=#CA2E0AFF>许愿树</color>的存在自有它的道理，至于为何总是不灵，大概是人们的愿望中，总是掺杂着太多复杂的情绪与欲望，而非它真的无能为力。",
    ["Dialogue9300505"]="冒险者，如果你们的愿望仅仅是为异世界的小生命送去一份关怀，我想许愿树一定会回应你们的。",
    ["Dialogue9300506"]="不过在此之前，何不试试<color=#CA2E0AFF>向奥丁祈祷</color>呢？要知道，仁慈的奥丁神一直注视着我们。",
    ["Dialogue9300601"]="我们成功了吗？你看，我们的东西真的消失了！",
    ["Dialogue9300602"]="嗯，一定成功了！冒险者，我刚才真的很认真地想着莱奥在许愿哦，希望它能收到这些东西，就算主人不能立刻回到它身边，我们之间的羁绊也会超越两个世界的距离的！",
    ["Dialogue9300603"]="也许吧……但是不知道为什么，许完愿后突然轻松了很多，就好像刚才莱奥回到了我身边，我还摸了摸它呢！那种感觉……我想许愿树一定有听到我的愿望！",
    ["Dialogue9300604"]="谢谢你，冒险者。无论如何，我都很感谢你为我所做的一切。虽然时空旅行有些孤独，不过能与善良的人相遇，这也是<color=#CA2E0AFF>命运的温柔之处</color>吧~",
    ["Dialogue9310101"]="看来，那位借走《舞台之梦》的陌生人和我有共同的爱好呢，是我来晚了一步。罗温，谢谢你告诉我这些。",
    ["Dialogue9310102"]="（金发青年点点头，轻推鼻梁上的眼镜）\n这个人借走的不只《舞台之梦》，还有其他关于表演的教科书与学术著作，图书馆的规定是……",
    ["Dialogue9310103"]="嘘……抱歉请等一下，我看到了一位朋友~\n（允儿朝你眨了眨眼睛）\n冒险者~你也是来借书的吗，想看什么？",
    ["Dialogue9310104"]="二楼第三个书架，第五排第六本。",
    ["Dialogue9310105"]="都……没有听说过呢。冒险者，你听说过一本叫<color=#CA2E0AFF>《舞台之梦》</color>的书吗，它是宫廷乐师富尔维奥的自传，里面记载了他从吟游诗人到宫廷乐师的一生。听说普隆德拉图书馆有原版书可供借阅，我就过来了！",
    ["Dialogue9310106"]="不过……看来有人比我更需要这本书呢~对了罗温，你刚才想说什么？",
    ["Dialogue9310107"]="咳咳，那么话题继续。图书馆的规定是珍贵的原版书籍只能在馆内阅读，不能外借。除此之外，还需要登记详细的个人信息。",
    ["Dialogue9310108"]="（罗温向你们展示了一张照片）\n图书馆允许小范围的传阅，他叫<color=#CA2E0AFF>海伊</color>，你们可以在馆内自行寻找。",
    ["Dialogue9310109"]="谢谢！冒险者，我们走吧~",
    ["Dialogue9310201"]="（沉浸在书海的年轻人狠狠薅了一把头发）\n“体验派”是什么意思？“表现派又是什么？”为什么会有这么多学派？",
    ["Dialogue9310202"]="（小山般的书堆中探出一张疲惫的青年面孔）\n是……谁……",
    ["Dialogue9310203"]="你……你还好吗？如果身体已经到了极限，硬撑下去只会更加难受哦。",
    ["Dialogue9310204"]="没关系……你……你是天使吗？妈妈，我好像到了不得了的地方啊。",
    ["Dialogue9310205"]="《舞台之梦》？\n（青年疲惫的眼睛瞬间亮了起来）\n你们喜欢表演吗？我也是！",
    ["Dialogue9310206"]="（海伊从书堆中精准抽出一本厚厚的硬皮封面书，刚准备递给你们时，又突然缩回了手）\n不行，喜欢表演不能只是简单的口头说说而已！",
    ["Dialogue9310207"]="如果你们也是表演爱好者，那一定也能<color=#CA2E0AFF>回答这些问题</color>吧！",
    ["Dialogue9310301"]="（海伊把书依依不舍地递给你们）\n这本书可是很珍贵的，要小心翻页哦……",
    ["Dialogue9310302"]="嗯！你也要注意休息，就算是为了比赛，也要注意劳逸结合呀~",
    ["Dialogue9310303"]="你……你也是来参加比赛的吗？",
    ["Dialogue9310304"]="是王国举办的演员选拔大赛！前十名可以直接进入奈里乌斯家族的剧团进行为期一年的学习，冠军更是能直接加入奈里乌斯剧团，我真是做梦也想获得这样的机会！",
    ["Dialogue9310305"]="可是……我的家乡梦罗克并不是培养演员的地方，支持我来普隆德拉参赛的，也只有老师。",
    ["Dialogue9310306"]="我的父母，他们更希望我可以成为一名战士或者商人，能够保护自己，或者改善家庭的经济状况。",
    ["Dialogue9310307"]="（他偷偷藏起了袖口的线头）\n其实，我也不知道自己能不能获得名次……甚至，我还没有一件像样的<color=#CA2E0AFF>演出服</color>。",
    ["Dialogue9310308"]="不过，老师告诉我演出服只能锦上添花，被磨炼过的演技才能雪中送炭，所以才提前来到了图书馆……",
    ["Dialogue9310309"]="所以，你很想要一件演出服吗？",
    ["Dialogue9310310"]="我……\n（海伊看着地板，眼神躲闪着回答了你们的问题）\n我的确……很想要……",
    ["Dialogue9310311"]="（林允儿拍了拍年轻人的肩膀）\n那么，一定要记住今天的答案，然后带着想要赢的心情上台。",
    ["Dialogue9310312"]="想穿漂亮的衣服、想赢得比赛获得机会，都不是羞耻的事情。只有对自己许下了实现梦想的诺言，却因为一些小事而中途放弃才是羞耻的。",
    ["Dialogue9310313"]="我们的梦想，或许有相似之处呢~所以，让我来帮助你吧~",
    ["Dialogue9310314"]="（海伊看了一眼小山般的书堆）\n我……好吧，那、那就麻烦你们了！我对款式没什么要求，合身就可以了！",
    ["Dialogue9310401"]="来定制服装的吗？我看看材料……在衣服上镶嵌宝石，是要参加什么特殊场合？",
    ["Dialogue9310402"]="这样啊……比赛的事情我也有所耳闻，不过你们来得有点晚了哦，按照正常的工期，是没有办法赶制出来的。",
    ["Dialogue9310403"]="（柏莉想了想，从身后的小房间里拿出一件款式有些过时的成衣）\n这件可以吗？虽然款式旧了些，尺码也未必合身，但我可以很快调整，你们的材料就算是手工费了~",
    ["Dialogue9310404"]="这可是我成为高级制衣师时，制作的第一件礼服哦！别看它没有任何的宝石镶嵌，布料和细节都是我亲手把控的！你们所说的年轻人，应该是第一次登台吧，不如把为衣服镶嵌宝石的机会，留给未来的他？",
    ["Dialogue9310405"]="留给……未来的自己吗？那么，就按您说的做吧~",
    ["Dialogue9310501"]="呵呵，身为老师，怎么能让学生一个人面对呢~看，我为你带来了什么？",
    ["Dialogue9310502"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>演……演出服！</color>",
    ["Dialogue9310503"]="老师……这……",
    ["Dialogue9310504"]="这……\n（莫尔斯大笑起来）\n哈哈！初赛穿一件，复赛穿一件？海伊，你可不能初赛就被淘汰了啊！\n",
    ["Dialogue9310505"]="我看看你借的书……什么？怎么还有<color=#CA2E0AFF>一本闲书</color>？喂，现在就把它还掉！",
    ["Dialogue9310506"]="什……什么？我没有借这样的书啊？",
    ["Dialogue9320101"]="冒险者最近在干什么呢？过得开心吗~",
    ["Dialogue9320102"]="哈哈，作为朋友，我希望冒险者一直开开心心的~所以，要一起煮东西吃吗？是在韩国非常受欢迎的<color=#CA2E0AFF>泡菜锅</color>！据说和好朋友一起吃，就会美味加倍！",
    ["Dialogue9320103"]="等到食材全部下锅，第一块煮好的肉一定是分给冒险者的，毕竟我们已经是好朋友啦~",
    ["Dialogue9320104"]="那就开始准备吧！首先我们需要<color=#CA2E0AFF>足够大的锅，和足够多的食材</color>……",
    ["Dialogue9320201"]="哦？\n（忽克连盯着你的手臂肌肉）\n冒险者，你是要用锅来练肌肉吗？",
    ["Dialogue9320202"]="哼哼，不过就算再怎么努力，你也是无法战胜我这一身从小练出的肌肉的！不信，我们比一比？",
    ["Dialogue9320203"]="哦？泡菜锅？是什么异世界特殊的美食吗？能增肌吗？",
    ["Dialogue9320204"]="你默认了？好吧，我会按照你的要求去做，不过报酬就是……我也要尝一口！",
    ["Dialogue9320205"]="你的表情是怎么回事？是不相信我的手艺吗？还是不相信我的肌肉？",
    ["Dialogue9320301"]="嗯……蔬菜和锅都已经备齐了，制作泡菜就交给我吧~接下来要准备肉了，这可得多备些~",
    ["Dialogue9320302"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>猪肉、牛肉、海鲜……</color>冒险者，拜托你啦！",
    ["Dialogue9320401"]="辛、辛苦了！带着一大堆肉回来，一定很重吧~",
    ["Dialogue9320402"]="烹饪环节就放心交给我吧，冒险者只要和我一起定好邀请的朋友名单，然后寄送邀请函就可以了！",
    ["Dialogue9320403"]="希澈哥是一定要叫上的，如果没有他，聚会时会少了很多乐趣呢！",
    ["Dialogue9320501"]="准备完成！接下来就等待朋友们上门吧~",
    ["Dialogue9320502"]="我也要去处理食材了，还要准备酒和饭后甜点！允儿来到异世界后的第一次烹饪大秀，敬请期待吧~",
    ["Dialogue9330101"]="（容貌俊美的青年仍保持着推门的姿势，他愣愣地转过头，和W四目相对）\n这里是哪？",
    ["Dialogue9330102"]="抱歉！\n（W涨红了脸，手忙脚乱地操纵着面前的虚拟光幕）\n这里是卢恩王国的普隆德拉……您……您的名字是？",
    ["Dialogue9330103"]="啊……请不要过于紧张！我们卡普拉公司一定会对客人负责到底的！只要您告诉我您的姓名和目的地，我们会立刻启动传送功能！如果您还有别的不满，也可以告诉W！只要……只要不投诉W……",
    ["Dialogue9330104"]="卡……普拉？这是什么咒语的名字吗？哦！我是<color=#CA2E0AFF>金希澈，目的地嘛……地球？韩国？呃……如果可以的话，请把我送回来的地方就好，明明刚才只是普通地推开家门，难道我家的门还有传送功能？嚯，不愧是<color=#CA2E0AFF>宇宙大明星的家门！",
    ["Dialogue9330105"]="您……您是异世界的客人？",
    ["Dialogue9330106"]="当然啦，我是很讲道理的地球人，所以不会投诉你的~\n（金希澈好奇地打量着四周的建筑）\n哇~是完全不同的建筑风格呢~",
    ["Dialogue9330107"]="谢谢您……但是事故就是事故……客人请稍等片刻，W会向总部申请开启传送回溯的权限，我们会通过传送记录追溯您的上一次空间传送的坐标，绝对不会有问题！",
    ["Dialogue9330108"]="（一通操作后，你看到W面前的光幕上出现了克拉丽丝的身影）\n克拉丽丝前辈！那个……我想申请<color=#CA2E0AFF>传送回溯的权限……W会努力弥补的……会写检讨书的……呜……八千字可以……呜……也会去找陪同人的……谢谢前辈！",
    ["Dialogue9330109"]="（等对方切断通讯后，W向你投来求助的目光）\n冒险者，你可不可以陪这位客人一起进行传送回溯啊……",
    ["Dialogue9330110"]="这位客人所在世界的坐标，在总部的定位系统上相当模糊……甚至他本人在米德加兹大陆的坐标，同样无法精准定位……",
    ["Dialogue9330111"]="也就是说，如果回溯失败，系统只能将他传送回米德加兹大陆，却不能保证传送回普隆德拉……",
    ["Dialogue9330112"]="（W满怀期待地看着你）\n所以才需要一个善良又强大的原住民，充当<color=#CA2E0AFF>引路人的角色……",
    ["Dialogue9330113"]="（W委委屈屈地对起了手指）\n异世界的传送回溯，是受到管制的……这位客人被系统评估为无能力作恶的普通人，所以才批准使用回溯功能……",
    ["Dialogue9330114"]="那就是最好的结果了，绝对没有问题！冒险者的坐标在我们的定位系统上相当清晰，一定能将您成功传送回普隆德拉！",
    ["Dialogue9330115"]="那……那W就当冒险者同意了哦~这位客人，冒险者是非常善良又热心的传奇人物，您可以相信他！也请相信卡普拉公司对每位客人的心意！",
    ["Dialogue9330116"]="我明白了！\n（他友好地和你握了握手）\n请多指教哦，异世界的旅伴~",
    ["Dialogue9330201"]="失、失败了吗？知道了……我会再联络一次……",
    ["Dialogue9330202"]="（W点开了与克拉丽丝的通讯）\n克拉丽丝前辈……那个……可不可以<color=#CA2E0AFF>再回溯一次……呜……真的吗？谢谢前辈！",
    ["Dialogue9330203"]="克拉丽丝前辈说我已经没有申请回溯的次数了……不过她可以帮我最后再申请一次！",
    ["Dialogue9330204"]="这也是最后的豁免了……对不起，W只能做到这里……",
    ["Dialogue9330205"]="唉……既然这样，那也没有办法啦。",
    ["Dialogue9330206"]="您……您不怪W吗？",
    ["Dialogue9330207"]="有一点哦~但是看到你们这样努力又真诚地弥补，再生气的话，好像有点过于残酷了呢~",
    ["Dialogue9330208"]="而且……\n（金希澈环顾四周）\n这么美丽的风景，如果能待上一阵好好欣赏，也不错啊~",
    ["Dialogue9330301"]="唉……",
    ["Dialogue9330302"]="唉……\n（W揉乱了一头金发）\n冒险者，卡普拉的系统不会出错第二次，除非……",
    ["Dialogue9330303"]="在卢恩王国，我们的异世界传送业务受教会管制，或许你们可以去找<color=#CA2E0AFF>沃尔玛斯大主教。",
    ["Dialogue9330304"]="如果教会也无能为力……这位客人，卡普拉公司将会为您制定相应的赔偿方案，我们会尽最大努力保证您在异世界的健康与舒适。",
    ["Dialogue9330305"]="明白了！冒险者，我们走吧~",
    ["Dialogue9330401"]="愿奥丁保佑你们……冒险者？",
    ["Dialogue9330402"]="（沃尔玛斯大主教露出了长者般和蔼的微笑）\n那么，这位就是异世界的客人吧。",
    ["Dialogue9330403"]="您好，我是金希澈。主教大人，我还有回去的可能吗？",
    ["Dialogue9330404"]="当然。但卡普拉的传送功能缺少你所在世界的坐标，只能等待那道影响传送的时空裂隙再次出现在米德加兹大陆。",
    ["Dialogue9330405"]="你们来得正好，孩子们，还有更紧迫的事情亟待解决，也只有你们能解决。",
    ["Dialogue9330406"]="我需要你们前往两次传送回溯失败后的落脚点，<color=#CA2E0AFF>关闭强行传送回溯时，残留的<color=#CA2E0AFF>时空裂隙。",
    ["Dialogue9330407"]="在此之前，你们还需要<color=#CA2E0AFF>去奥丁神像下祈祷，让奥丁赋予你们看见与关闭它的力量。",
    ["Dialogue9330501"]="（W拉着你们仔仔细细的检查了一遍）\n吓死W了！听说你们一起去关闭了时空裂隙，W很担心你们！",
    ["Dialogue9330502"]="当然啦！苦瓜脸才不是W的风格呢~而且，我是来和这位客人商讨卡普拉的补偿方案的！锵锵！",
    ["Dialogue9330503"]="（W将一份文件袋递给金希澈）\n内容是保密的，先生，如果你愿意接受这份补偿，可以在明天，把签好字的文件袋还给W哦~",
    ["Dialogue9330504"]="是~秘~密~哦~",
    ["Dialogue9340101"]="哦！是那时候陪我传送的冒险者！难道……你也喜欢喝酒吗？",
    ["Dialogue9340102"]="我也喜欢，最喜欢了！那你知道<color=#CA2E0AFF>瑞草坊市的艾乐贝尔</color>在哪里吗？听说五年一度的百酿会就在这里举行，艾乐贝尔是主办人。这样热闹的盛会，我当然要拜托W传送过来了！",
    ["Dialogue9340103"]="诶？我还以为你也是来参加<color=#CA2E0AFF>瑞草坊市的百酿会</color>的呢，听说是五年一度的活动，所以立刻拜托W把我传送过来了。她还说我可以找<color=#CA2E0AFF>艾乐贝尔</color>了解详细情况，她是百酿会的主办人。",
    ["Dialogue9340104"]="既然碰上了，一起去怎么样？虽然到了斐扬，但这里的路我一点也不认识……",
    ["Dialogue9340201"]="欢迎你们~在百酿会举行期间，全场美酒都可以免费试喝哦~",
    ["Dialogue9340202"]="（金希澈的眼睛亮了起来）\n哇好厉害~~~请问我真的可以喝到一百种酒吗？如果没有一百种，我真的会闹哦~",
    ["Dialogue9340203"]="哈哈~看来这位客人也是好酒之人，当然可以啦！如果你想多喝一些，还可以加入我们斗酒活动的众评团，不过一旦加入，可是要不醉不归的~",
    ["Dialogue9340204"]="请务必让我加入！！！我的名字是金希澈！唯一不能放弃的快乐是喝酒！",
    ["Dialogue9340205"]="你、你不问问斗酒活动的规则吗？",
    ["Dialogue9340206"]="完！全！不！用！和酒有关的活动一定是世界上最快乐的活动！",
    ["Dialogue9340207"]="真是心急的客人啊……所谓斗酒活动呢，就是大陆各地的酒商齐聚一堂，拿出自己近五年获得或自酿的最好美酒与所有人分享。然后由众评团通过观色、闻香、品味三个环节选出最好的五味美酒。",
    ["Dialogue9340208"]="等酸、甜、苦、辣、涩五味美酒都被选出后，众评团会再次选出其中至纯至味的一种酒，即是本届的百酿酒王了！先生还有什么不懂的吗？",
    ["Dialogue9340209"]="没有没有！现在还不能开始吗，如果是我的话，边喝酒边准备活动也不在话下！",
    ["Dialogue9340210"]="（艾乐贝尔额头上滚落了一颗豆大的汗珠）\n哈哈……现在还不可以呢~百酿会除了一百种酒，也需要一百位大陆各地的酒商。少一位，都不叫百酿会……",
    ["Dialogue9340211"]="难道说？啊……有什么我能帮上忙的请尽管提出！",
    ["Dialogue9340212"]="谢谢您的慷慨……其实，有一名叫<color=#CA2E0AFF>李酌</color>的酒商一直没有来到会场，昨日他告诉我自己已经来到了<color=#CA2E0AFF>斐扬南部</color>，可是今天却……",
    ["Dialogue9340213"]="虽说我们已经派人将斐扬周围危险的魔物尽数驱赶，但万一有所遗漏，那就……唉，大家为了准备百酿会已经超负荷工作三天了，实在无法调派人手前去寻找。",
    ["Dialogue9340214"]="我明白了！这件事就交给我吧，只要告诉我他的相貌就好！",
    ["Dialogue9340215"]="你……你可以吗？外面的魔物虽不致命，也很难保证不受伤的。",
    ["Dialogue9340216"]="我……",
    ["Dialogue9340217"]="冒险者，你……\n（金希澈惊讶地看着你，突然抹了一把并不存在的眼泪）\n好朋友！",
    ["Dialogue9340301"]="（以奇怪姿势躺在地上的青年看见你们后，用力地眨了两下眼睛）\n救我……麻了……",
    ["Dialogue9340302"]="是魔菇的麻麻粉……我需要<color=#CA2E0AFF>长老树精携带的向日葵</color>……救救我……",
    ["Dialogue9340401"]="（闻到向日葵的香气后，李酌缓慢地坐了起来）\n腿还是好麻……这些讨厌的魔菇，希望他们永远喝不到我的千岁酿！",
    ["Dialogue9340402"]="没错！\n（李酌激动地锤了一下大腿）\n疼疼疼……它的配方可是我李酌寻访了无数酿酒大师才完整复原的！",
    ["Dialogue9340403"]="酿酒的材料，有些并不在人族手里，还要与粗野的兽人、洁癖的人鱼甚至喝血的吸血鬼打交道！奥丁在上，这酒酿成时还引来了哥布灵的强夺，幸好我事先在地下埋了两坛，这才不至于空手而来。",
    ["Dialogue9340404"]="你们……应该不是来抢酒的吧？",
    ["Dialogue9340405"]="怎么会呢？真正的爱酒之人，是不会用抢的方式夺走别人的藏酒的！和好朋友一起喝，并把他喝趴下，才是我金希澈的风格哈哈哈！",
    ["Dialogue9340406"]="说得对！冲你这句话，我们今天就要把酒言欢，才不算辱没了这坛千岁酿！",
    ["Dialogue9340407"]="好！所以你要不要先开一坛，不是有两坛吗？开一坛吧~~~",
    ["Dialogue9340408"]="（李酌被金希澈的动作吓得往后一缩，连忙看向相对冷静的你）\n这可不行。不过，可否麻烦你们<color=#CA2E0AFF>将这两坛酒先送到斐扬的艾乐贝尔处</color>？我现在的状态，可能还需要一些时间才能恢复。",
    ["Dialogue9340409"]="如果因为一个人，一坛酒无法让百酿会准时开始，就太遗憾了。",
    ["Dialogue9340410"]="哈哈~这五年来我走南闯北，身体可比以前强壮多了！更何况同为爱酒之人，就应该知道找到一个志趣相投的酒友有多难。",
    ["Dialogue9340411"]="两坛千岁酿，一坛斗百酒，一坛与朋饮。你们出发吧，我一定会来！",
    ["Dialogue9340501"]="（你们站在空桌前，金希澈却迟迟没有坐下）\n冒险者，他来了吗？",
    ["Dialogue9340502"]="啊~我已经闻到酒香味了~\n(金希澈看向对面的空座位)\n不行，我等不了了！！！！",
    ["Dialogue9340503"]="这里这里~快快快，冒险者，你先迎接他，我去选酒，今天就要喝个痛快，谁都不要管我！！！",
    ["Dialogue9350101"]="嘘……现在等待彩排的时间，要保持安静哦。",
    ["Dialogue9350102"]="嗯哼~其实我已经答应了在克里图拉学院迎新典礼上表演，这里将会成为<color=#CA2E0AFF>宇宙大明星</color>闪闪发光的首秀舞台~",
    ["Dialogue9350103"]="秘密~身为宇宙大明星，怎么会只给一个人表演呢~况且我的表演，嗯……如果观众只有一个，表演效果也会受到影响的！",
    ["Dialogue9350104"]="等等！\n（金希澈连忙喊住了你）\n咳咳……身为宇宙大明星的朋友，你……",
    ["Dialogue9350105"]="我是说……如果特别想看的话，也不是不可以……",
    ["Dialogue9350106"]="不过我的演出，是真的很需要观众，而且观众越多演出效果越好哦！真的真的~我在玫瑰红酒馆的<color=#CA2E0AFF>花瓣</color>们也这么说~",
    ["Dialogue9350107"]="嗯，我在<color=#CA2E0AFF>玫瑰红酒馆</color>遇见了许多同样热爱音乐的人，或许你可以去那里找到观众~",
    ["Dialogue9350108"]="啊哈~花瓣是我的粉丝名哦，我们互相陪伴，互相支持，对我来说，<color=#CA2E0AFF>花瓣是非常重要的人</color>呢！相信在<color=#CA2E0AFF>玫瑰红酒馆</color>，一定能找到观众的！",
    ["Dialogue9350109"]="去吧去吧~我也要去准备了，一会儿普隆德拉南门游乐园见！",
    ["Dialogue9350201"]="冒险者，你在这里干什么呢~",
    ["Dialogue9350202"]="你是说，有金希澈的表演可以看？嗯……这的确是玫瑰红酒馆多数人无法拒绝的活动呢。",
    ["Dialogue9350203"]="谢谢你的消息，可惜我还要处理酒馆里的一堆事务，如果姑娘们都去看演出了，我就得自己干活了。不如……",
    ["Dialogue9350204"]="冒险者，想体验酒馆侍应生的生活吗？一边流汗，一边擦桌扫地的激情，可不是谁都能享受到的~",
    ["Dialogue9350205"]="怎么会呢？这样吧，只要你帮我<color=#CA2E0AFF>打扫酒馆</color>，我就为你推荐一位既有影响力，又能让演出变得更精彩的<color=#CA2E0AFF>观众</color>怎么样？",
    ["Dialogue9350301"]="不愧是冒险者，什么都难不倒你呢~现在，你可以去找<color=#CA2E0AFF>允儿</color>了，她和金希澈都是异界的客人，有他们两个在，表演一定会大受欢迎的！",
    ["Dialogue9350302"]="允儿的性格也很好，只要你礼貌地邀请她，应该不会被拒绝的！",
    ["Dialogue9350401"]="你是说，想邀请我去看希澈哥的表演，而他的表演效果一定需要足够的观众才能保证效果？",
    ["Dialogue9350402"]="可以是可以，不过……很奇怪，希澈哥向来是一个人也可以完成整场表演的人，为什么一定要这么多的观众呢？",
    ["Dialogue9350403"]="……啊！\n（似乎想到了什么，允儿的表情突然变得很复杂）",
    ["Dialogue9350404"]="没事。冒险者，不如我们再找一位会唱歌的观众？如果是正常的表演，一定需要伴唱吧~你觉得<color=#CA2E0AFF>摩尔托斯</color>怎么样？",
    ["Dialogue9350405"]="毕竟是出人意料的金希澈啊，唉，谁让我们是他的好朋友呢，只能包容这个要做宇宙大明星的哥哥了~走吧，去找摩尔托斯，观众们一定很想念他的歌声与鲁特琴~",
    ["Dialogue9350501"]="哦？有露天演出需要我的加入？\n（摩尔托斯清了清嗓子）\n咳哼……",
    ["Dialogue9350502"]="最近我在教导唱诗班的孩子们，嗓子已经……咳咳咳！没有办法为大家献唱了。",
    ["Dialogue9350503"]="咦？可是你昨天明明还和酒馆的人鱼小姐一起唱歌，连伊莎贝拉姐姐都拉不走呢~该不会是因为这件事，所以声音才哑了吧？",
    ["Dialogue9350504"]="允儿小姐，你！\n（摩尔托斯还想争辩，却在事实前败下阵来）\n好吧……但我的嗓子是真的哑了……",
    ["Dialogue9350505"]="如果不能马上恢复，恐怕也不能教唱诗班的孩子们了，生气的玛嘉雷特神官很可怕，因为生气所以不给我润喉糖的玛嘉雷特神官就更可怕了！",
    ["Dialogue9350506"]="是超级神奇的<color=#CA2E0AFF>清新润喉糖</color>——玛嘉雷特神官为了唱诗班的孩子们，请宫廷药剂师一起调配的！虽然价格很便宜，但轻易不对外出售，所以冒险者……如果是你，说不定能买到哦~",
    ["Dialogue9350507"]="有了它，我就可以参加你们的表演了！嘿嘿，如果可以的话，记得多买几颗~",
    ["Dialogue9350601"]="不错不错，人都到齐啦~虽然场地简陋了一些，但热闹的氛围才是最关键的！冒险者，谢谢你为我做的这些，所以就由你当我的<color=#CA2E0AFF>助演嘉宾</color>吧！",
    ["Dialogue9350602"]="那么，演出就开始了~冒险者，请你把自己想成一颗番茄，把我想成你的番茄同伴，嘘，要进入角色了……",
    ["Dialogue9350603"]="……",
    ["Dialogue9350604"]="……",
    ["Dialogue9350605"]="（沉默良久后，金希澈缓缓开口）\n我们不是番茄吗，我们会讲话吗？",
    ["Dialogue9350606"]="果然冷笑话是最棒的对吧！那么接下来，请你把自己想成……",
    ["Dialogue9350607"]="对呀~我可是准备了<color=#CA2E0AFF>几十个不同类型的冷笑话</color>呢！讲冷笑话，难道不是气氛越热烈，效果就越好吗？",
    ["Dialogue9350608"]="导师们都很喜欢呢！哈米德先生还问我能不能把这些笑话整理成册卖给学生们，涉及到版权问题，所以我拒绝了。",
    ["Dialogue9350609"]="希澈哥……真的知道自己在干什么吗……哈……哈哈……我就知道会是这样……",
    ["Dialogue9350610"]="既然如此，还是由我摩尔托斯为大家高歌一曲……",
    ["Dialogue9350611"]="喂，先听我说完啊！",
    ["Dialogue9360101"]="你有没有听说普隆德拉最近流行的“<color=#CA2E0AFF>交换礼物</color>”活动？允儿、W还有伊莎贝拉，她们玩得可开心了~",
    ["Dialogue9360102"]="（希澈悄悄把礼物藏到了身后）\n咳咳，才没有呢！礼物是拿来交换的，因为大家都不知道对方准备了什么礼物，所以才好玩呀~",
    ["Dialogue9360103"]="要是我直接给你，那就是单方面的赠送，这样就不好玩了~冒险者，你有准备和我交换的礼物吗？",
    ["Dialogue9360104"]="游戏机！我超级喜欢游戏机！！！自从来到这个世界，我没有一天不在想念家里的游戏机和里面的游戏……唉，冒险者，为什么你们的世界里没有游戏机呢？",
    ["Dialogue9360105"]="游戏机就是……就是……\n（金希澈在空中比划了一个四四方方的东西）\n糟糕！能说的太多，反而不知道从何说起了……",
    ["Dialogue9360106"]="喂，不要用怀疑的眼神看我啊！如果你能看到<color=#CA2E0AFF>我的记忆</color>，就会知道<color=#CA2E0AFF>游戏机</color>是多么有趣的东西了！几乎每个男孩子，都不会拒绝拥有一台游戏机！",
    ["Dialogue9360107"]="你是说，可以通过魔法变出一台游戏机？",
    ["Dialogue9360108"]="那我在这里等你~这个世界的魔法我还不太了解，如果需要配合，随时回普隆德拉找我哦！",
    ["Dialogue9360201"]="吉芬塔永远为渴求知识的正义魔法师敞开大门，冒险者，欢迎你的到来。",
    ["Dialogue9360202"]="变出异界之物的魔法？冒险者，你的所求总是那么特别，不过有一种魔法，或许能满足你的愿望。",
    ["Dialogue9360203"]="具象魔法，能将记忆中的存在具象为片刻的真实。你所说的“游戏机”，似乎并非战车一类的复杂的巨大物件，而记忆的主人又对它印象深刻，理论上并无实施难度。",
    ["Dialogue9360204"]="你将那位异界客人带来吉芬，再<color=#CA2E0AFF>去吉芬塔地下1F开采一些具象魔晶</color>交给我即可。不过，你要小心具象魔晶周围盘踞的<color=#CA2E0AFF>魔物</color>，它们被公会封印多年，憎恨一切来自地上的生灵。",
    ["Dialogue9360301"]="我感受到吉芬塔下魔物们躁动的气息，一定是你打败了具象魔晶的看守者吧。",
    ["Dialogue9360302"]="看来，加固封印和具象魔法的仪式，要同时进行了。冒险者，你现在可以<color=#CA2E0AFF>返回普隆德拉</color>，将那位记忆的主人带回吉芬。我需要先加固封印，再准备仪式。不出意外的话，你们可以在<color=#CA2E0AFF>吉芬塔地下1F传送阵</color>附近见到我。",
    ["Dialogue9360401"]="你回来了！看你的表情，是不是我的游戏机有着落了？",
    ["Dialogue9360402"]="赞美魔法！那还等什么？我们快走！",
    ["Dialogue9360501"]="在仪式开始之前，我必须告诉你一些注意事项。作为记忆的主人，你需要在整个仪式内努力回想所求之物的每个细节，一刻也不能停下。",
    ["Dialogue9360502"]="长期处于精神高度集中的状态下，你会很快感到疲劳与不适，但这种状态保持越久，所求之物就会越真实。",
    ["Dialogue9360503"]="……二周目？",
    ["Dialogue9360504"]="好，冒险者，<color=#CA2E0AFF>摆放具象魔晶</color>的任务就交给你了，这位客人，请你站到法阵中央，我们的仪式要开始了。",
    ["Dialogue9360601"]="哇！！！我的宝贝，你回来了！\n（金希澈激动地在造型奇特的物件上摁了几下）\n开机成功！我的游戏也在，太好了！",
    ["Dialogue9360602"]="冒险者，等回到普隆德拉，我们就可以一起打游戏了！要是允儿看见，一定会超级羡慕的哈哈哈！",
    ["Dialogue9360603"]="嗯？哦……想起来了！给你，要好好珍惜哦~",
    ["DialogueBubble10001"]="Grow and keep growing! I'm so fond of all these greens and little flowers!",
    ["DialogueBubble10002"]="I'm a hardworking little gardener. Let me water each of you!",
    ["DialogueBubble10011"]="Dart at your own pace, tiny fish.",
    ["DialogueBubble10012"]="It's time to eat! Grow bigger!",
    ["DialogueBubble10021"]="Clink–Clink! Mine the gems to trade for Diamonds!",
    ["DialogueBubble110000"]="You are a force to be reckoned with, human... You have passed my test!",
    ["DialogueBubble11001"]="Master, it gets pretty lonely here on my own. Don't forget to swing by now and then.",
    ["DialogueBubble11002"]="Wonder when I'll get to have my own piece of farmland?",
    ["DialogueBubble11003"]="Being a pet that my master trusts a lot, I need to live up to that responsibility!",
    ["DialogueBubble11004"]="The fruits from the field smelled amazing the last time. I'm drooling just thinking about it (slurp).",
    ["DialogueBubble11101"]="Tiling the soil... watering... fertilizing... Then, just wait for the awesome time to harvest!",
    ["DialogueBubble11102"]="Huff, huff... the toughest part of farming is getting water from the pond...",
    ["DialogueBubble11201"]="Here comes the exciting fall and winter harvest season!",
    ["DialogueBubble11202"]="This moment, right here, is what all that hard work is for, isn't it?",
    ["DialogueBubble12001"]="If there are fish in the pond, I enjoy watching them just swim around without a care.",
    ["DialogueBubble12002"]="Maybe I could learn some fish facts from Peierls when I have some spare time?",
    ["DialogueBubble12003"]="I've got to stay focused; I don't wanna make a mistake and end up getting yelled at!",
    ["DialogueBubble12004"]="They say a fish's memory only lasts for seven seconds.",
    ["DialogueBubble12101"]="(Sniff, sniff) Huh? Why would such adorable fish eat something like this?",
    ["DialogueBubble12102"]="If fish grow faster by eating this... maybe I could...",
    ["DialogueBubble12201"]="The harvest's looking good. Wonder if I'll get a grilled fish as a reward this time?",
    ["DialogueBubble12202"]="I've been around these fish for a while now, and I'm attached to them...",
    ["DialogueBubble12203"]="Figuring out these ore veins is so complicated. How did my master ever learn to do it?",
    ["DialogueBubble12204"]="Could I find some ore that's been missed if I roam around here a bit longer?",
    ["DialogueBubble13001"]="Hold up, hold up! That's the smell of an advanced ore vein!",
    ["DialogueBubble13002"]="What should I eat during my next break?",
    ["DialogueBubble13003"]="Hold up, hold up! That's the smell of an advanced ore vein!",
    ["DialogueBubble13004"]="What should I eat during my next break?",
    ["DialogueBubble13101"]="Ores! Gems! Shiny things are my absolute favorite!",
    ["DialogueBubble13102"]="Why are these things so popular when you can't eat or drink them?",
    ["DialogueBubble21000101"]="Miss Obeaune, play another song on the piano for us!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000201"]="You guys took so long!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000301"]="Careful! These Porings seem to be going crazy!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000401"]="Aha! It's time for the instructor to show you how it's done!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000402"]="Novice, pick up your knife now!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000501"]="These Porings are so relentless...",
    ["DialogueBubble21000502"]="Don't back down! Hit them hard!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000601"]="Hang on, here comes a big guy! It's never-ending...",
    ["DialogueBubble21000602"]="Novice, you've got to evade the King Poring's skill!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000603"]="This guy is way stronger than a normal Poring!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000701"]="Novice, you have done your best.",
    ["DialogueBubble21000702"]="Let me teach you how to retreat!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000801"]="Use this skill to recover your stamina!",
    ["DialogueBubble21000901"]="I'll leave everything to you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21001001"]="You finally caught up!",
    ["DialogueBubble21001101"]="Haha! So long, kids!",
    ["DialogueBubble21001301"]="Good, let's go!",
    ["DialogueBubble21001401"]="That's right! That's the way it's done!",
    ["DialogueBubble21001501"]="It's all up to you now, adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble21010201"]="Are you alright?",
    ["DialogueBubble21010301"]="You're finally here, Reserve!",
    ["DialogueBubble21010501"]="Thank you. I feel much better now!",
    ["DialogueBubble21010901"]="Who?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21011001"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21011201"]="This... How is this possible!?",
    ["DialogueBubble21011301"]="You're buying me a drink? Ohoho, how generous!",
    ["DialogueBubble21011401"]="Another glass? You got it! I can drink everything you throw at me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21011501"]="Mm... This wine is tasty... Hic!",
    ["DialogueBubble21011601"]="Why do I feel... Kinda dizzy...",
    ["DialogueBubble21011901"]="Jack's on sewer entrance guard duty today, isn't he?",
    ["DialogueBubble21011902"]="That guy likes to come up with some strange passwords. What's today's again...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21011903"]="I think it was... Egg Fried Fabre?",
    ["DialogueBubble21011904"]="Ugh... Sounds awful.",
    ["DialogueBubble21012101"]="Thank goodness! You found all the lost knights!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020201"]="Thank you. I'll find shelter once I get my strength back.",
    ["DialogueBubble21020301"]="Help me, adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020401"]="Thank you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020501"]="Thank you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020601"]="Thank you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020701"]="This is... My staff!",
    ["DialogueBubble21020901"]="Great job. I'll go get ready in the prayer room first!",
    ["DialogueBubble21021001"]="Please... help me...",
    ["DialogueBubble21021101"]="Adventurer, I knew you would come.",
    ["DialogueBubble21021201"]="Careful... Here they come!",
    ["DialogueBubble21022301"]="This is the port city, Alberta!",
    ["DialogueBubble21022401"]="I don't want to be a burden so I'll wait for you here. Please be careful!",
    ["DialogueBubble21022501"]="The Captain's Cabin is just past this door!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040101"]="Help! Somebody help me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040201"]="We're saved. Thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040301"]="Oh, my beloved Byrd! I'm so glad you're safe!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040401"]="Alright, the medicine is ready.",
    ["DialogueBubble21040402"]="Bring it to me now!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040501"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble21040601"]="(Dying emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble21040701"]="It's done. Ladle the medicine out while it's still hot!",
    ["DialogueBubble21040801"]="(Throwing up emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble21040901"]="I'm saved. Thank you! Bloop!",
    ["DialogueBubble21041001"]="...Dad!",
    ["DialogueBubble21050301"]="Oh! That's right! That's it!",
    ["DialogueBubble21050401"]="My old friend, it's time for us to fight side by side again.",
    ["DialogueBubble21060101"]="Hey! I... I'm not afraid of death...",
    ["DialogueBubble21060102"]="Even if I lose my life here, I will be reborn in Niflheim!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060103"]="And this time... Not even Merlin Heines can save Geffen!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060104"]="Hehe... We have the power of Ymir's Heart...",
    ["DialogueBubble21060105"]="The Darkness shall return to the continent of Midgard!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060201"]="Even in the face of death, you're still so determined?",
    ["DialogueBubble21060202"]="What did you say?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060301"]="Phew... What a pain...",
    ["DialogueBubble21060401"]="Goblin-blin-blin!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060402"]="Goblin-blin-blin!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060403"]="...Human-man-man!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060501"]="...Goblin! Reborn... Reborn!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060502"]="...Goblin! Rise up! Rise up!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060601"]="...Goblin! Reborn... Reborn!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060602"]="...Goblin! Rise up! Rise up!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060701"]="Little friend, look where you're going!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060801"]="L-l-little what?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21060901"]="Hmph! Wait until you take a dose of this!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061001"]="You disgusting human! You... What did you make me drink?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061101"]="How dare you talk back to me?! Hmph! It seems the dosage wasn't quite enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061201"]="This... this disgusting taste! You've killed me... Killed me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061301"]="Ah! That wasn't enough to stop you?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061401"]="....N-n-no way! I'll tell you... I'll tell you everything!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061501"]="I know who sent you...",
    ["DialogueBubble21061502"]="Attacking his own people? Is that really his way of doing things?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061503"]="It seems there's no need to prolong this with pointless words.",
    ["DialogueBubble21061601"]="(Growling.)",
    ["DialogueBubble21061701"]="Then it's all up to you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061801"]="This is... Joao's helmet!",
    ["DialogueBubble21061901"]="Murloma! You're okay!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062001"]="Master, Joao's child—I mean the offering has been taken to the underground cave.",
    ["DialogueBubble21062002"]="Now for the ritual process...",
    ["DialogueBubble21062101"]="Very good. To accomplish great things, some sacrifices have to be made!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062102"]="Shh, wait. There seems to be a guest outside.",
    ["DialogueBubble21062201"]="Urgh...",
    ["DialogueBubble21062301"]="Haha, it's too late. It's too late...",
    ["DialogueBubble21062401"]="...Are you really going to sacrifice this child?",
    ["DialogueBubble21062402"]="Then...\nI'll leave the rest to you.",
    ["DialogueBubble21062501"]="—Urgh! Argh!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062601"]="Of course, the sacrifices must be pure infants with the powerful blood of the Orcs.",
    ["DialogueBubble21062602"]="Please, don't feel as though you can't bear to do it. This is a glorious sacrifice!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062603"]="I, Gerrush, will prove to you—the Orcs' god will answer my request!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062701"]="Hmph... Why not kill me? The Orcs...",
    ["DialogueBubble21062702"]="Will remember my name forever!",
    ["DialogueBubble21062801"]="Wh-who are you!?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063001"]="...What are you trying to do?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063101"]="...Already dead?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063102"]="Check another time—don't waste a single drop!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063201"]="Yes, boss, we've already extracted all the blood we can!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063202"]="Right!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063301"]="Right!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063401"]="Did you locate the guards?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063501"]="Now, bring them out!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063601"]="Excellent. I'll gladly take this blood.",
    ["DialogueBubble21063602"]="No, this is far from enough. After all, you've already killed so many of your people. You don't care how many are killed, do you?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063603"]="For the sake of our great cause, bring me more fresh blood! I will wait for you at the appointed place... Hehehe...",
    ["DialogueBubble21063701"]="Then now we can...",
    ["DialogueBubble21063801"]="Wow, could it be you think you can stop The Darkness' plans? Don't you understand? You're nothing more than pitiful pawns!",
    ["DialogueBubble21063802"]="And pawns should know their place—",
    ["DialogueBubble21063803"]="How about I have my underlings play with you?",
    ["DialogueBubble21063901"]="Darn it, I can't move...",
    ["DialogueBubble21070101"]="Hm, I don't know how it's going...",
    ["DialogueBubble21070201"]="...What do we do now?",
    ["DialogueBubble21070301"]="Ah, this house...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21070401"]="Yes, that's the flower...",
    ["DialogueBubble21070501"]="Ah, this fragrance is so familiar...",
    ["DialogueBubble21070601"]="Thank you, this is exactly what I need to do...",
    ["DialogueBubble21070701"]="Well then, I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21070801"]="Th-this is...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21070901"]="This wooden box...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071001"]="La... Lady Hermes...",
    ["DialogueBubble21071101"]="Be careful... The aura of the monsters have gotten stronger!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071201"]="How did it go? Are they all here?",
    ["DialogueBubble21071301"]="Great. I'll hear this guy's excuse!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071401"]="Good. This is enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071501"]="Oh Odin... What wrongdoings have we committed...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071601"]="Hm, next should be...",
    ["DialogueBubble21071701"]="Ah, this is unbelievable!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071801"]="Yes, yes, that's it!",
    ["DialogueBubble21071901"]="Excellent, another riddle is solved!",
    ["DialogueBubble21072001"]="Haha, good thing you were helping!",
    ["DialogueBubble21072101"]="Haha, awesome!",
    ["DialogueBubble21072201"]="I knew you could do it!",
    ["DialogueBubble21072301"]="Now the biggest problem is here...",
    ["DialogueBubble21072401"]="Eh? It's a complete mess.",
    ["DialogueBubble21072501"]="Wh-what's the meaning of this...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21072601"]="...Unbelievable. Completely unbelievable!",
    ["DialogueBubble21072701"]="...Hey, you. Come here.",
    ["DialogueBubble21072801"]="You dare to loiter around here!?",
    ["DialogueBubble21072901"]="Hmph, don't even think about lazing around. I've got my eye on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073001"]="Ugh, can't you be a bit quicker?",
    ["DialogueBubble21073101"]="Hehe, Very good, very good!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073201"]="Hehe, don't let its deliciousness tempt you to into eating it all by yourself!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073301"]="Ah, food... Food!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073401"]="Blegh... My stomach hurts...",
    ["DialogueBubble21073501"]="H-Help me... I'm innocent!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073601"]="...My food has been snatched away again...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21073701"]="What a scumbag! He deserved to die!",
    ["DialogueBubble21073801"]="Thank you very much...",
    ["DialogueBubble21073901"]="Thank you. I'll feel a lot better with these herbs...",
    ["DialogueBubble21074001"]="So what's the situation?",
    ["DialogueBubble21074101"]="What's going on...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21074201"]="Save me... Save me...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21074301"]="Save me... Save me...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21074401"]="Save me... Save me...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21074501"]="Q-quick, take me away from here... I don't want to stay here for even a second longer!",
    ["DialogueBubble21074601"]="Ah, kill me...",
    ["DialogueBubble21074701"]="It's my fault, all my fault...I-I'm so sorry!",
    ["DialogueBubble21074801"]="Hey, you're back. How did the archaeological research go?",
    ["DialogueBubble21074901"]="Watch out... Don't let your guard down.",
    ["DialogueBubble21075001"]="Thanks, I feel a lot better!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075101"]="Thank you. I feel like I've got strength again!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075201"]="Thank you. I feel like I've got strength again!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075301"]="Thank you. I feel like I've got strength again!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075401"]="Thanks. I'm getting out of here!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075501"]="Thank you very much.",
    ["DialogueBubble21075601"]="Well fought, Adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble21075701"]="Hm, did you get that fragment?",
    ["DialogueBubble21075801"]="Well this is bad...",
    ["DialogueBubble21075901"]="Roar—",
    ["DialogueBubble21076001"]="*Coughing* ...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076101"]="*Sobs* ...I beg you, let me go...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076201"]="I don't want to die...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076301"]="...Why? Why me?",
    ["DialogueBubble21076401"]="Please, let me go. I want to go home...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076501"]="Ah, merciful priest, I beg you...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076602"]="...This is?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21076701"]="Ah, this feeling...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076702"]="Thank you, kind adventurer...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076801"]="You have showcased all eight characteristics of a knight and have passed my trial.",
    ["DialogueBubble21076802"]="Please come stand before me now...",
    ["DialogueBubble21076901"]="*Sniffs* Is it really here? This smell...",
    ["DialogueBubble21077001"]="...Food, give it to me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21077101"]="Beat it! I saw it first!",
    ["DialogueBubble21077201"]="Who let you rest!?",
    ["DialogueBubble21077301"]="S-Sorry...",
    ["DialogueBubble21077401"]="But we're just too tired...",
    ["DialogueBubble21077501"]="—Shut it! Lazy oaf!",
    ["DialogueBubble21077601"]="Heh, now it's nice and quiet.",
    ["DialogueBubble21077701"]="Aooohhhhh—",
    ["DialogueBubble21077801"]="...Q-quickly, deal with them!",
    ["DialogueBubble21077901"]="...Y-you're back again!?",
    ["DialogueBubble21078001"]="N-no, I don't want to see this...",
    ["DialogueBubble21078002"]="It's not my fault... I order you to st-stop!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080101"]="......What kind of rules is this?",
    ["DialogueBubble21080201"]="What rules? This is down right bully!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080301"]="Aye, let us pass!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080401"]="Ah! Move aside, I’m the one in charge here.",
    ["DialogueBubble21080501"]="My, my luggage!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080601"]="Someone......get him!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080701"]="By Odin, finally!!",
    ["DialogueBubble21080801"]="You morons! What should we do now?",
    ["DialogueBubble21080901"]="Calm down! Let me think——",
    ["DialogueBubble21081001"]="Don’t......don’t move.....",
    ["DialogueBubble21081101"]="Ahhhhh--!",
    ["DialogueBubble21081201"]="I told you to stay put, can you just don’t move?",
    ["DialogueBubble21081301"]="As expected, the body can behave.",
    ["DialogueBubble21081401"]="(Sigh)",
    ["DialogueBubble21081501"]="You're finally back.",
    ["DialogueBubble21081601"]="Hey, where is my lost cargo?",
    ["DialogueBubble21081701"]="What? What do you want to do?",
    ["DialogueBubble21081801"]="Pass confirmed —— Welcome to Al De Baran!",
    ["DialogueBubble21081901"]="Burnt......Burn",
    ["DialogueBubble21082001"]="......All is lost.....",
    ["DialogueBubble21082101"]="Wh-what's the meaning of this...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21082201"]="Hey! I’m ordering you to report your mech classification.....",
    ["DialogueBubble21082301"]="Stop!",
    ["DialogueBubble21082401"]="Click——click——",
    ["DialogueBubble21082501"]="Ah... Thank you so much for your help...",
    ["DialogueBubble21082601"]="——?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21082701"]="This is indeed rather unusual...",
    ["DialogueBubble21082801"]="Great.",
    ["DialogueBubble21082901"]="Halt! No traffic allowed through here!",
    ["DialogueBubble21083001"]="Alarm——Invader——Alarm——",
    ["DialogueBubble21083101"]="Please, don’t hurt me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21083201"]="No......Not enough...",
    ["DialogueBubble21083301"]="Souls......More souls!",
    ["DialogueBubble21083401"]="......Thanks.",
    ["DialogueBubble21083501"]="......Yes, that’s it.",
    ["DialogueBubble21083601"]="Top wheat flour, freshly baked bread——Now or never!",
    ["DialogueBubble21083701"]="Ha——(Brother’s name)! I knew I can find you on the market!",
    ["DialogueBubble21083801"]="Wow~Aren’t you the Shorty?",
    ["DialogueBubble21083901"]="Out here alone in the night, you should have a few Zeny on you, right?",
    ["DialogueBubble21084001"]="Hehe...",
    ["DialogueBubble21084101"]="Good, you are here.",
    ["DialogueBubble21084201"]="(Brother’s name), sorry......",
    ["DialogueBubble21084301"]="——Guards! Escort him away!",
    ["DialogueBubble21084401"]="Aye!",
    ["DialogueBubble21084501"]="Hmm... Hmm...",
    ["DialogueBubble21084601"]="Well~This tender shell, it seems rather tasty~",
    ["DialogueBubble21084701"]="Look at this perfect arc! This is a piece of art~",
    ["DialogueBubble21084801"]="Ah~I can see the Goddess of Miracle waving to me.",
    ["DialogueBubble21090101"]="...This is ridiculous!",
    ["DialogueBubble21090201"]="I know, but...",
    ["DialogueBubble21090301"]="You mean...",
    ["DialogueBubble21090401"]="...Large-scale burn!",
    ["DialogueBubble21090501"]="(Grateful Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble21090601"]="Why am I... so unlucky?",
    ["DialogueBubble21090701"]="Oh... so it did save my life!",
    ["DialogueBubble21090801"]="Ah, I see.",
    ["DialogueBubble21090901"]="Is this...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21091001"]="This is the only room left unexplored...",
    ["DialogueBubble21091101"]="Watch out, don't alert them!",
    ["DialogueBubble21091201"]="Yes, yes, these are it!",
    ["DialogueBubble21091301"]="Time to reveal the truth!",
    ["DialogueBubble21091401"]="Thanks. Please wait.",
    ["DialogueBubble21091501"]="...What are these?",
    ["DialogueBubble21091601"]="...I've decided.",
    ["DialogueBubble21091701"]="But if the leader starts pointing fingers...",
    ["DialogueBubble21091801"]="Thanks, I feel a lot better!",
    ["DialogueBubble21091901"]="Wonderful, I can fight again!",
    ["DialogueBubble21092001"]="The fire... It disappeared?",
    ["DialogueBubble21092101"]="Thanks. Perfect timing on your part!",
    ["DialogueBubble21092201"]="Thank you very much...",
    ["DialogueBubble21092301"]="Thank Odin, I thought I was dead meat!",
    ["DialogueBubble21092401"]="(Shocked Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble21092501"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble21092601"]="(Thumbs Up Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble21092701"]="(Blow Kisses Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble21092801"]="Thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble21092901"]="Nice work, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble21093101"]="...Looks like my guest has arrived.",
    ["DialogueBubble21093102"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21093201"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21093301"]="This team right here, keep your eyes on the Lord.",
    ["DialogueBubble21093401"]="The rest... follow me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21093501"]="Yes sir!",
    ["DialogueBubble21093801"]="Damnit... Hold your ground!",
    ["DialogueBubble21093901"]="Speed up!",
    ["DialogueBubble21094001"]="We can't let it go off here!",
    ["DialogueBubble21094101"]="Okay, watch this!",
    ["DialogueBubble21094301"]="J-Just put it back to sleep mode, right?",
    ["DialogueBubble21094401"]="...Something does go wrong.",
    ["DialogueBubble21094501"]="...Boo Coo...",
    ["DialogueBubble21094502"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21094701"]="Why are there monsters here?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21094801"]="...Hiss...",
    ["DialogueBubble21095001"]="Watch out! Here they come!",
    ["DialogueBubble21095101"]="How long until it's fixed?",
    ["DialogueBubble21095201"]="Almost! Hang in there!",
    ["DialogueBubble21095401"]="Why are there monsters here?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21095501"]="...Hiss...",
    ["DialogueBubble21095601"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21095602"]="Watch out! Here they come!",
    ["DialogueBubble21095701"]="How long until it's fixed?",
    ["DialogueBubble21095801"]="Almost! Hang in there!",
    ["DialogueBubble21095901"]="22",
    ["DialogueBubble21100101"]="We must retrieve the sacred relic quickly...",
    ["DialogueBubble21100201"]="But the Wizard...",
    ["DialogueBubble21100301"]="You saw it yourself. There's something wrong with Tatanka...",
    ["DialogueBubble21100401"]="Never mind. I've made up my mind...",
    ["DialogueBubble21100501"]="No... My kids!",
    ["DialogueBubble21100601"]="This, this is...!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble21100701"]="Hey! Where's my stuff?",
    ["DialogueBubble21100801"]="Thanks! You are our savior too!",
    ["DialogueBubble21100901"]="Even here has reached the threshold...",
    ["DialogueBubble21101001"]="Great.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101101"]="Right. This is it.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101201"]="Need some Refreshing Dew.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101301"]="Good. Now, I need to have a serious conversation with you...",
    ["DialogueBubble21101401"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21101501"]="Still missing something...",
    ["DialogueBubble21101601"]="Now, let me prove it.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101701"]="This is exactly what I want.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101801"]="Nice, you're quick.",
    ["DialogueBubble21101901"]="Leave it to me.",
    ["DialogueBubble21102001"]="Loud and clear? You bunch of garbage!",
    ["DialogueBubble21102101"]="Y-Yes, sir!",
    ["DialogueBubble21102201"]="Don't you dare to slack off!",
    ["DialogueBubble21102301"]="Hm. Much better.",
    ["DialogueBubble21102401"]="... Hey, what is this?",
    ["DialogueBubble21102501"]="Alright, let's get started.",
    ["DialogueBubble21102601"]="No, please don't... I'm not dead yet...",
    ["DialogueBubble21102701"]="Eat... Hisss—",
    ["DialogueBubble21102801"]="Eat 'em all—Hisss!",
    ["DialogueBubble21102901"]="Give it to me! Do you want to get your ass kicked again?",
    ["DialogueBubble21103001"]="Waah, I found it first... I'm starving...",
    ["DialogueBubble21103101"]="Shut up! Everyone is starving here! Let go of it!",
    ["DialogueBubble21103201"]="(Bare teeth angrily—)",
    ["DialogueBubble21103301"]="I-I will share your pain...",
    ["DialogueBubble21103401"]="W-Why am I... so unlucky?",
    ["DialogueBubble21103501"]="Hisss—taint of the rotten meat",
    ["DialogueBubble21103601"]="Retreat now! Inform everybody...",
    ["DialogueBubble21103701"]="The angry Beetle King breaks through the quarantine zone!",
    ["DialogueBubble21103801"]="Stay away... Stay away from me!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble21103901"]="Haha, what? Was that not enough shiny magic for you?",
    ["DialogueBubble21104001"]="Ke-ke, ke-ke!",
    ["DialogueBubble21104101"]="Hey, don't tickle me... Hahaha, you brunch of naughty little things.",
    ["DialogueBubble21104201"]="Choo-choo, choo-choo!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110102"]="These folks are just brazen!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110201"]="Hmm...",
    ["DialogueBubble21110202"]="More Steel Capital Institute cargo...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21110302"]="Quit talking! Start working!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110501"]="Quit messing around; let's go back!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110602"]="Bad guy! Don't touch me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110702"]="Don't say another word!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110703"]="I won't go anywhere without seeing Nina!",
    ["DialogueBubble21110901"]="Dad!",
    ["DialogueBubble21111101"]="Love Emoticon 7",
    ["DialogueBubble21111201"]="How did it go?",
    ["DialogueBubble21111202"]="... How much can we get this time?",
    ["DialogueBubble21111301"]="Tsk... The higher-ups are getting stingier than ever.",
    ["DialogueBubble21111401"]="... Fine, it's a deal.",
    ["DialogueBubble21111501"]="Nina, the flowers on your head are so pretty!",
    ["DialogueBubble21111601"]="Idiot! White flowers are for when someone dies in the family!",
    ["DialogueBubble21111701"]="You, you're making it up...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21111801"]="Thanks for your patronage!",
    ["DialogueBubble21111901"]="... Great, that's the one.",
    ["DialogueBubble21112001"]="Alright, now to assemble...",
    ["DialogueBubble21112102"]="S-Stay away...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21112201"]="Phew... I feel much better.",
    ["DialogueBubble21112301"]="Thank you, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble21112401"]="... How do you have this on you?",
    ["DialogueBubble21112501"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21112601"]="Are you ready?",
    ["DialogueBubble21112602"]="Let's go!",
    ["DialogueBubble21112701"]="Yes!",
    ["DialogueBubble21120101"]="Today's the day...",
    ["DialogueBubble21120102"]="Hopefully, nothing goes wrong...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21120201"]="Stay in line, folks! No pushing!",
    ["DialogueBubble21120202"]="No cutting in line! No rushing!",
    ["DialogueBubble21120401"]="Enjoy your meal!",
    ["DialogueBubble21120501"]="... It's the same familiar taste.",
    ["DialogueBubble21120601"]="Thanks for the meal.",
    ["DialogueBubble21120602"]="... Guess I'll be on my way now.",
    ["DialogueBubble21120701"]="Th-Thank you... I'm feeling a lot better.",
    ["DialogueBubble21120801"]="Ugh... look at this thing...",
    ["DialogueBubble21120901"]="... It's not worth much.",
    ["DialogueBubble21121001"]="Eh... good enough, I guess.",
    ["DialogueBubble21121101"]="Huh...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21121202"]="Seriously...? How could you not know this?",
    ["DialogueBubble21121301"]="Ugh... books are no fun.",
    ["DialogueBubble21121401"]="... Another book about alchemy?",
    ["DialogueBubble21121501"]="... I've already read all of these.",
    ["DialogueBubble21121601"]="Nice! Something new to read!",
    ["DialogueBubble21121701"]="Hmm... what does this word mean?",
    ["DialogueBubble21121801"]="Um... could you read it out loud for me?",
    ["DialogueBubble21122001"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21122101"]="If the Goddess is watching...",
    ["DialogueBubble21122102"]="Please forgive my sins...",
    ["DialogueBubble21122201"]="...!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble21122301"]="... Exactly what I suspected.",
    ["DialogueBubble21122401"]="Now that I think about it, how did the Pope find out...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21122501"]="Everything is ready!",
    ["DialogueBubble21122601"]="Uh... brother...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21122701"]="What...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble21122801"]="Impossible...!",
    ["DialogueBubble21122901"]="Nonsense! You're slandering me!",
    ["DialogueBubble21123001"]="This presence...?",
    ["DialogueBubble21130101"]="Confirmed! Thank you for your cooperation!",
    ["DialogueBubble21130201"]="Tch... lost them again.",
    ["DialogueBubble21130202"]="Hmmm... that looks familiar.",
    ["DialogueBubble21130301"]="Hmm... I...",
    ["DialogueBubble21130401"]="Cough... Let her go!",
    ["DialogueBubble21130501"]="No... Master...",
    ["DialogueBubble21130601"]="I... I can still fight... Come on!",
    ["DialogueBubble21130701"]="Eh...",
    ["DialogueBubble21130801"]="... Cough! Cough cough...",
    ["DialogueBubble21130901"]="Looks like basic survival's covered, at least...",
    ["DialogueBubble21131001"]="There's gotta be a way...",
    ["DialogueBubble21131101"]="Nice... just the right amount.",
    ["DialogueBubble21131301"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble21131401"]="You've done well, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble21131501"]="Urgh... My head hurts...",
    ["DialogueBubble21131601"]="Martistine... We finally get to meet...",
    ["DialogueBubble21131701"]="Alright then... this is as far as we go.",
    ["DialogueBubble21131702"]="Safe travels!",
    ["DialogueBubble21998201"]="The Mini Train is about to depart! Please get on if you wish to board!",
    ["DialogueBubble22000101"]="Ahh! That is troubling...",
    ["DialogueBubble22000201"]="Woah! What a touching scene!",
    ["DialogueBubble22000301"]="Sigh, I feel so sorry for Parni.",
    ["DialogueBubble22000401"]="You have arrived. I have been waiting for you.",
    ["DialogueBubble22000501"]="Odin, please have mercy on my child...",
    ["DialogueBubble22000601"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22000701"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble22000801"]="Sigh...",
    ["DialogueBubble22000901"]="Adventurer, come over.",
    ["DialogueBubble22001001"]="This is...",
    ["DialogueBubble22001101"]="Urgh... Adventurer...",
    ["DialogueBubble22010101"]="Hey, you! Come here quick!",
    ["DialogueBubble22010201"]="Where am I supposed to find high-quality gold...?",
    ["DialogueBubble22010301"]="Thank you. I'll still need some silver ore and gold ore.",
    ["DialogueBubble22010401"]="Great, I'm just short of some gold ore now.",
    ["DialogueBubble22010501"]="I think this is enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble22010601"]="Thanks!",
    ["DialogueBubble22010701"]="Please help me add some firewood first.",
    ["DialogueBubble22010801"]="The fire's dying again. Please add more!",
    ["DialogueBubble22010901"]="Very good. Stoke the flames more, please.",
    ["DialogueBubble22011001"]="Excellent! The smelting is successful!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011101"]="I'm so lonely...",
    ["DialogueBubble22011201"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22011301"]="Is that...?",
    ["DialogueBubble22011401"]="It's all up to you now!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011501"]="With Halmod around, those monsters are going to pay!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011601"]="You came. Looks like I put my faith in the right person!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011701"]="You're really slow, my friend!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011801"]="Darn it! Stupid kidnapper!",
    ["DialogueBubble22011901"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22012001"]="...Agnes!",
    ["DialogueBubble22012002"]="What a relief! You're all back safely!",
    ["DialogueBubble22020101"]="Sigh, what do we do now?",
    ["DialogueBubble22020201"]="It's all up to you now!",
    ["DialogueBubble22020301"]="Weird... Where did the invitation go?",
    ["DialogueBubble22020401"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22020501"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22020601"]="...Oh no, oh no, she's going to be so upset!",
    ["DialogueBubble22020701"]="(Depressed emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22020801"]="That's enough. Now you just have to be patient for a moment.",
    ["DialogueBubble22020901"]="Alright. Please hold onto this flower crown!",
    ["DialogueBubble22021001"]="Wow! That's amazing! It looks just like new!",
    ["DialogueBubble22021101"]="(Shocked emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22030101"]="Ahhh!! It's all in the name of love!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030201"]="You're... H?",
    ["DialogueBubble22030301"]="(Shocked emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22030401"]="Too slow! Too slow!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030501"]="Ohh! I bet I can sell this for a good price!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030601"]="Ohh! I bet I can sell this for a good price!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030701"]="Ohh! I bet I can sell this for a good price!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030801"]="You... You collected them all?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22030901"]="By Odin, you look so pretty now!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031001"]="A gentle lady is worth her weight in gold, a beautiful lady is as brilliant as diamond, and a smart woman is as precious as art. As for all of you... You're greater than all of those treasures combined.",
    ["DialogueBubble22031101"]="Ahh!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031201"]="Master Jurgen!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031301"]="I'm suffocating!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031401"]="Wonderful! That's exactly what I wanted!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031501"]="Ohh! You're not bad at all!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031601"]="Ohh! You're not bad at all!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031701"]="Ohh! You're not bad at all!",
    ["DialogueBubble22031801"]="Ohh! The smell of this wine is making me drunk...",
    ["DialogueBubble22031901"]="This wine has a real kick to it. Just one glass can knock you out the whole day, so you have to drink in moderation! Hic!",
    ["DialogueBubble22032001"]="Wonderful! That's exactly what I wanted!",
    ["DialogueBubble22032101"]="Why... why did they do that?",
    ["DialogueBubble22040101"]="...Are you sure it's him?",
    ["DialogueBubble22040201"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble22040301"]="What am I going to do? What am I supposed to do now?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22040302"]="If Master Friedrich asks, what should I say?",
    ["DialogueBubble22040303"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22040401"]="...Who's there?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22040501"]="Thank you, that's exactly what I need.",
    ["DialogueBubble22040601"]="...You have my deepest gratitude.",
    ["DialogueBubble22040701"]="Well, it's all up to you now.",
    ["DialogueBubble22040801"]="Stop right there. Hand over Merlin's Manuscript!",
    ["DialogueBubble22040901"]="Put down Merlin's Manuscript or prepare to face death!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041001"]="Surrender the book quietly!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041101"]="Ahem, you're just in time!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041201"]="This book, it's...!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041301"]="(Shocked emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22041401"]="Wh...who are you?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041501"]="...Hey! You're not allowed in here! Get out!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041601"]="...Why haven't those brothers returned yet?",
    ["DialogueBubble22041701"]="Just go and steal a book! What's there to worry about?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22041702"]="It's the employer this time, he can afford a surprisingly high commission.",
    ["DialogueBubble22041801"]="You can't judge a book by its cover. It could be that the money was obtained through questionable means.",
    ["DialogueBubble22041802"]="Are you thirsty? Let's talk later. I'll go get some water for us to drink.",
    ["DialogueBubble22041901"]="*cough, cough* So... thirsty...",
    ["DialogueBubble22042001"]="(Stunned emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22042101"]="Adventurer, it's like we were destined to meet!",
    ["DialogueBubble22042102"]="If only you didn't thwart my plans every time...",
    ["DialogueBubble22042103"]="I almost feel like... I want to make friends with you! Hehe!",
    ["DialogueBubble22042201"]="You're back, adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble22042301"]="(Smirk emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22042302"]="So, let me take these test subjects.",
    ["DialogueBubble22042303"]="—I have a reunion gift for you!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050101"]="...I think I got my point across.",
    ["DialogueBubble22050201"]="No, I can never accept it!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050301"]="Hmph, fine, I shall try it out on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050401"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22050501"]="Fortunately, I didn't miss Barbara's show!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050601"]="I heard it's impossible to get tickets for her show in other towns...",
    ["DialogueBubble22050701"]="We love you, Barbara!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050801"]="We love you, Barbara!",
    ["DialogueBubble22050901"]="We love you, Barbara!",
    ["DialogueBubble22051001"]="Have you seen her dance, Odin?",
    ["DialogueBubble22051101"]="Of course! She's at least on par with Freyja...",
    ["DialogueBubble22051601"]="—♪—♪",
    ["DialogueBubble22051701"]="Darn it... Those incorrigible mobsters!",
    ["DialogueBubble22051901"]="Weird, how come not back yet...",
    ["DialogueBubble22052001"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22052101"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22052201"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22052301"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22052401"]="(Roaring)",
    ["DialogueBubble22060101"]="Adventurer, please come over for a conversation.",
    ["DialogueBubble22060201"]="Cough cough...",
    ["DialogueBubble22060301"]="Adventurer, welcome here.",
    ["DialogueBubble22060401"]="I've been expecting you.",
    ["DialogueBubble22060501"]="Very well, you did a good job.",
    ["DialogueBubble22060601"]="Now, please allow me to explain.",
    ["DialogueBubble22070101"]="...Tsk, did it run away?",
    ["DialogueBubble22070102"]="We got to catch it back...",
    ["DialogueBubble22070201"]="Darn it...",
    ["DialogueBubble22070202"]="What exactly was that?",
    ["DialogueBubble22070401"]="Woof... Woof Woof! Woof!",
    ["DialogueBubble22070501"]="Look at this elegant figure...",
    ["DialogueBubble22070502"]="And beautiful hair...",
    ["DialogueBubble22070503"]="The best breed indeed!",
    ["DialogueBubble22070902"]="Could it be...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22071002"]="Hey, that's enough...",
    ["DialogueBubble22071201"]="Clatter-Clatter...",
    ["DialogueBubble22071301"]="Tap-Tap-Tap...",
    ["DialogueBubble22071401"]="Start analyzing...",
    ["DialogueBubble22071501"]="(Click... click... click...)",
    ["DialogueBubble22071601"]="Does that kid still want to find the monster that's all covered with eyes?",
    ["DialogueBubble22071701"]="Haven't heard that lately. It's good to have some peace like now.",
    ["DialogueBubble22071801"]="Yeah, it was scary how beaten up he was when Gamow first brought him back...",
    ["DialogueBubble22071901"]="He's recovered now, and he's not making a fuss anymore. Hey, I even saw him smiling at Gamow the other day!",
    ["DialogueBubble22072001"]="The kid Gamow brought back from the mountain seems like a perfect match for his daughter, Lush!",
    ["DialogueBubble22072101"]="You mean the one teaching my kid swordsmanship? Ah, it's a good pick!",
    ["DialogueBubble22072201"]="However, the kid's techniques are strangely rare, and they remind me of... reminds me of... hey, Gamow, this way!",
    ["DialogueBubble22072301"]="Master... Everyone... Sorry... Ah!",
    ["DialogueBubble22072401"]="... It's a dream? Why did I sleep so long?",
    ["DialogueBubble22072501"]="Uncle Gamow? Lush? Are you guys here? Anyone?",
    ["DialogueBubble22072601"]="Uncle... Gamow?",
    ["DialogueBubble22072701"]="Thanatos... Run...",
    ["DialogueBubble22072801"]="Run? You... want me to run?",
    ["DialogueBubble22072901"]="Monster... Inside my body... Kid... S-Sorry...",
    ["DialogueBubble22073001"]="Is... is it over? Thanatos... Father, something's wrong with him... I hid...",
    ["DialogueBubble22073101"]="... Kill all monsters in the world.",
    ["DialogueBubble22073201"]="Thanatos...What happened to you?",
    ["DialogueBubble22073301"]="Till this body turns to dust. No trust needed, no ties needed; you... are not needed.",
    ["DialogueBubble22073401"]="All emotions, any emotions, are just hindrances to slaughter.",
    ["DialogueBubble22073501"]="Heard about it? The lord summoned demon hunters to take care of the recent monster surge!",
    ["DialogueBubble22073601"]="A man and a woman, right? I know where they are, come with me!",
    ["DialogueBubble22073701"]="They're really good... Especially that guy named Thanatos...",
    ["DialogueBubble22073801"]="Can you smell that... Ugh... Let's get out of here...",
    ["DialogueBubble22073901"]="Lush? Lush?",
    ["DialogueBubble22074001"]="Why... Everyone... Left me...",
    ["DialogueBubble22074101"]="AHHHHHHH!!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22074201"]="... How did it go?",
    ["DialogueBubble22074301"]="Pretty good, we plan to start the simulation test next week.",
    ["DialogueBubble22074401"]="The sewage output today went over the limit again.",
    ["DialogueBubble22074501"]="The microfilters are wearing out quicker and quicker...",
    ["DialogueBubble22074601"]="Please present your pass and follow the security procedures!",
    ["DialogueBubble22074701"]="Please present your pass and follow the security procedures!",
    ["DialogueBubble22074801"]="Requesting a transfer to the mines? Are you out of your mind?",
    ["DialogueBubble22074901"]="No worries, the people from Einbech will work for us...",
    ["DialogueBubble22075001"]="I heard the Environmental Association filed another complaint with the city hall.",
    ["DialogueBubble22075101"]="Yeah, right on time, like afternoon tea.",
    ["DialogueBubble22075201"]="Rekenber's new mask, cool right?",
    ["DialogueBubble22075301"]="Brilliant invention!",
    ["DialogueBubble22075401"]="Cough cough...",
    ["DialogueBubble22075501"]="Save... us...",
    ["DialogueBubble22075601"]="Trinity, about the melody I composed for you...",
    ["DialogueBubble22075701"]="Very, very nice, I... Huh, Adventurer?",
    ["DialogueBubble22075801"]="Master, your coffee...",
    ["DialogueBubble22075802"]="Master, your sugar...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076001"]="Spare us, please...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076101"]="This is not okay...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076201"]="We haven't had a rest for five days...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076301"]="We've got to figure something out...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076401"]="This is...?",
    ["DialogueBubble22076501"]="Ugh... I can't keep up...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076601"]="There are fewer and fewer easy marks...",
    ["DialogueBubble22076701"]="Someone from Kafra? Come get your stuff!",
    ["DialogueBubble22076801"]="Hmph, stamp it.",
    ["DialogueBubble22076901"]="Told to rest in dirt and gloom, giants above us loom.",
    ["DialogueBubble22076902"]="War and blood pave the way; weak ones watch, and alliances stay.",
    ["DialogueBubble22076903"]="Roots twist tight, bone they chew, split in three. What's the clue?",
    ["DialogueBubble22076904"]="One is lost, chaos remains, unseen leaders, where power reigns?",
    ["DialogueBubble22076905"]="Throne of the land, overturned by hand, machines roar, cries unmanned.",
    ["DialogueBubble22077001"]="What's going on? How did you know a Dimensional Gap would appear in Geffen?",
    ["DialogueBubble22077101"]="Go away, you annoying monsters!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077201"]="Ha——ha...",
    ["DialogueBubble22077301"]="Orfeo and Trinity! The grand tour! Up close and personal!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077401"]="What?! The show's canceled?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077402"]="Refund! Refund!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077403"]="Sorry... I'm really sorry...",
    ["DialogueBubble22077501"]="Sorry... we just found out, too...",
    ["DialogueBubble22077502"]="Do you have any idea how far we came for this?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077503"]="If you can't pull it off, then don't even try!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077601"]="Adventurer?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077701"]="Great. Three maniacs. Just what I needed.",
    ["DialogueBubble22077702"]="Just how much are we losing with the place shutting down?!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077801"]="The holy spring tastes just as sweet today!",
    ["DialogueBubble22077901"]="Praise the Goddess!",
    ["DialogueBubble22078001"]="We've got all kinds of potions—pick your favorite!",
    ["DialogueBubble22078101"]="I want the strawberry-flavored healing potion!",
    ["DialogueBubble22078201"]="I'll have the cactus-flavored one!",
    ["DialogueBubble22078301"]="O gracious Goddess, may my child offer these flowers to you...",
    ["DialogueBubble22078401"]="What a breathtaking courtyard...",
    ["DialogueBubble22078501"]="Hush! This estate is owned by the priests!",
    ["DialogueBubble22078601"]="Is it true this place is devoted to Freyja?",
    ["DialogueBubble22078701"]="Hope they'll like our products...",
    ["DialogueBubble22078801"]="Cough... Wonder if I'll live to see that day...",
    ["DialogueBubble22078901"]="Mom, Dad... why aren't you back yet?",
    ["DialogueBubble22079001"]="We found something big!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22079101"]="Hmm... Let me see...",
    ["DialogueBubble22079201"]="!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22079301"]="Stir, stir, stir... Alright, Adventurer, come forward.",
    ["DialogueBubble22079401"]="Isumia, did you send them to me?",
    ["DialogueBubble22079501"]="Urgh... Arunafeltz's airship... I think I'm gonna throw up—",
    ["DialogueBubble22079601"]="AHHHHHHH—NOT ON ME!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22079701"]="So if there's no raw stone here either... what's the plan for tomorrow?",
    ["DialogueBubble22079801"]="Go to the execution platform.",
    ["DialogueBubble22079901"]="Double-check this and this again.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080001"]="No mistakes are allowed when it comes to numbers.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080101"]="Double-check this and this again.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080202"]="No mistakes are allowed when it comes to numbers.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080301"]="We have to catch it this time!",
    ["DialogueBubble22080501"]="... If this truly is his final wish...",
    ["DialogueBubble22080502"]="I'll do my best to make it happen.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080601"]="... Right on time, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080602"]="Let's get started.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080701"]="Huh? Looks like there's an extra book?",
    ["DialogueBubble22080702"]="W-What do we do now?",
    ["DialogueBubble22080801"]="This is incorrect, Your Holiness.",
    ["DialogueBubble22080901"]="Sorry, Teacher Jude.",
    ["DialogueBubble22081001"]="I'll start over... right now.",
    ["DialogueBubble22081201"]="When will the Bishop arrive?",
    ["DialogueBubble22081302"]="I heard the church is swamped with work; they might not make it after all.",
    ["DialogueBubble22081403"]="Look! Is that the legendary Adventurer?",
    ["DialogueBubble22081601"]="Please wait a second, the Adventurer right there.",
    ["DialogueBubble22081602"]="Could you do me a favor?",
    ["DialogueBubble22081701"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22081801"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble22081901"]="This is... my sister's favorite flower.",
    ["DialogueBubble22082001"]="And... Rossin's favorite wine.",
    ["DialogueBubble22082101"]="The course of history has already changed...",
    ["DialogueBubble22082201"]="Hic! Tamaureen? Do you need something else?",
    ["DialogueBubble22082202"]="The thing in your hand...",
    ["DialogueBubble22082301"]="Take them away! I don't want to see them!",
    ["DialogueBubble22082401"]="Thank you for your kindness, but my decision has been made...",
    ["DialogueBubble22082501"]="My friends, we've finally returned!",
    ["DialogueBubble22082502"]="Time to rebuild and do something big, people!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22082503"]="OHHHHH!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble22082601"]="Lush?",
    ["DialogueBubble22082602"]="Where are you? I've come back!",
    ["DialogueBubble22082603"]="... Got it.",
    ["DialogueBubble23050101"]="Sigh. We can't keep going on like this...",
    ["DialogueBubble23050201"]="Lucia...",
    ["DialogueBubble23050301"]="These flowers are exactly the same as before!",
    ["DialogueBubble23050401"]="Lucia made this dish...",
    ["DialogueBubble23050501"]="Please deliver this to Leona. She'll know what to do.",
    ["DialogueBubble23050601"]="(Shocked emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23060101"]="What now, what now, what now?",
    ["DialogueBubble23060201"]="This is... a Colorful Flower?",
    ["DialogueBubble23060301"]="What is this subtle scent...?",
    ["DialogueBubble23060401"]="I'm in agony!",
    ["DialogueBubble23070101"]="This is bad...",
    ["DialogueBubble23070201"]="Oh no... Where did I put that thing?",
    ["DialogueBubble23070301"]="(Uncertain emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23070401"]="That's it! That's what I need. But I need a lot more than that...",
    ["DialogueBubble23070501"]="Jingyin... I swear I'll save you...",
    ["DialogueBubble23070601"]="(Howling)",
    ["DialogueBubble23070701"]="No! Jingyin!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23070801"]="That's it! That's what I need. But that's still not enough...",
    ["DialogueBubble23070901"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23071001"]="Adventurer, what was that just now?",
    ["DialogueBubble23071101"]="Now we can get ready to cross dimensions.",
    ["DialogueBubble23071201"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble23080101"]="Adventurer, wait!",
    ["DialogueBubble23080201"]="Hello, what can I do for you this time?",
    ["DialogueBubble23080301"]="Oh, please accept this hair accessory as well.",
    ["DialogueBubble23080401"]="The scent on this branch...",
    ["DialogueBubble23080501"]="This hair accessory! I...",
    ["DialogueBubble23080601"]="It's been a while, adventurer...",
    ["DialogueBubble23080701"]="That's enough...",
    ["DialogueBubble23080801"]="Please wait a moment.",
    ["DialogueBubble23080901"]="It's done!",
    ["DialogueBubble23081001"]="Some food from home will help him get better.",
    ["DialogueBubble23081101"]="(Drooling emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23081201"]="What are you doing here?",
    ["DialogueBubble23081301"]="I'm counting on you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23081401"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23081501"]="This photo...!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090101"]="Wow! Perfect timing!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090201"]="That's enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090301"]="That's it. That's it! Mm... it smells lovely!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090401"]="I'll leave everything to you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090501"]="(Uncertain emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23090601"]="That's enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090701"]="That's it. That's it! Mm... it smells lovely!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090801"]="I'll leave everything to you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23090901"]="(Uncertain emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23091001"]="Ahem! That is... Even a short time apart feels like an eternity.",
    ["DialogueBubble23091002"]="Now! Do it now!",
    ["DialogueBubble23091101"]="No! You're not Busang! He'd never say something like that! Who are you?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23091201"]="What did you do?",
    ["DialogueBubble23091301"]="...Let's give her a proper burial.",
    ["DialogueBubble23091401"]="Weird, what on earth was that thing?",
    ["DialogueBubble23091501"]="Boo... Boohoo...",
    ["DialogueBubble23091601"]="Could it be...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23091701"]="...Are you sure you want to make a dish out of this?",
    ["DialogueBubble23091801"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23091901"]="You... Stay away!",
    ["DialogueBubble23092001"]="Farbauti! Laufey! Get it off here!",
    ["DialogueBubble23100101"]="Tsk! What an annoyance.",
    ["DialogueBubble23100201"]="Dark... power... will finally rise.",
    ["DialogueBubble23100301"]="—Aaahh!",
    ["DialogueBubble23100401"]="Aha, I smell an ancient relic!",
    ["DialogueBubble23100501"]="Ugh, I can't move it at all.",
    ["DialogueBubble23100601"]="Thank you. Now... it feels better.",
    ["DialogueBubble23100701"]="Dark... power... will finally rise.",
    ["DialogueBubble23100702"]="The King of the Dead... Once again...",
    ["DialogueBubble23100703"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble23100704"]="Ahhhh!",
    ["DialogueBubble23100801"]="Aha, I smell an ancient relic!",
    ["DialogueBubble23100901"]="...Please... please help me! I'm really badly hurt.",
    ["DialogueBubble23101001"]="...What have you done?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23101101"]="Traitor... You have betrayed Pentagram!",
    ["DialogueBubble23101201"]="No, you're not like that.",
    ["DialogueBubble23101202"]="...Please, stop it!",
    ["DialogueBubble23101301"]="Hehehe, welcome, blood-soaked human!",
    ["DialogueBubble23110101"]="Adventurer, come...",
    ["DialogueBubble23110201"]="How did it go? Did you find De'qeen?",
    ["DialogueBubble23110301"]="Ah, this is unbelievable!",
    ["DialogueBubble23110401"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23110501"]="Hmm... Where has that child wandered off to?",
    ["DialogueBubble23110601"]="Ah, @#$*%~...",
    ["DialogueBubble23110701"]="Ah... My dear Agatha, from the first time I laid eyes on you, your sexy muscles brought me to my knees.",
    ["DialogueBubble23110702"]="Your tough green skin appears in my dreams every night.",
    ["DialogueBubble23110703"]="Maybe we can give this a try and see where it takes us.",
    ["DialogueBubble23110801"]="(Shy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23110802"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23110901"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111001"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111101"]="Ahh! What have you done?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23111201"]="Damn it! This is all your fault.",
    ["DialogueBubble23111301"]="Woah, someone actually still has it.",
    ["DialogueBubble23111401"]="(Yawning emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111501"]="(Angry emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111601"]="(Howl—)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111701"]="Hmm, that's surprising.",
    ["DialogueBubble23111801"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23111901"]="Adventurer, what's the situation?",
    ["DialogueBubble23120101"]="You... you'd better let me go at once! Otherwise...",
    ["DialogueBubble23120102"]="Otherwise, you're as good as dead, you stinking mage!",
    ["DialogueBubble23120201"]="...Otherwise?",
    ["DialogueBubble23120301"]="...Huh? Where did everybody go?",
    ["DialogueBubble23120401"]="These guys... They're just as tough as before.",
    ["DialogueBubble23120501"]="Ygnizem, I will try my best to protect you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23120601"]="...Huh? It's you?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23120701"]="Hmph! Even the monsters in the desert aren't worth a damn.",
    ["DialogueBubble23120801"]="...It's you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23120901"]="Ah... What am I supposed to do now?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23121001"]="These goods... Don't you think there's something strange about them?",
    ["DialogueBubble23121101"]="What a coincidence. I was just on my way to come find you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23121201"]="...Adventurer, watch out!",
    ["DialogueBubble23121301"]="Ouch! Enough, stop it already!",
    ["DialogueBubble23121401"]="Young adventurer, you need to see the situation clearly.",
    ["DialogueBubble23121601"]="G-Goldie?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23121701"]="That's... Goldie? Goldie's back!",
    ["DialogueBubble23121801"]="I'll never...let you take this child...",
    ["DialogueBubble23121901"]="Wah! It's Goldie!",
    ["DialogueBubble23122001"]="Sniff... Sniff... You bullies...",
    ["DialogueBubble23122101"]="(Angry emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23130101"]="Blanche, Jean... Are both of you alright?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23130102"]="Away......You foul monsters!",
    ["DialogueBubble23130103"]="(Howl—)",
    ["DialogueBubble23130201"]="This is... I'm forever in your debt!",
    ["DialogueBubble23130501"]="How did it go? Did you deal with them?",
    ["DialogueBubble23130701"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23130702"]="Very good, very good!",
    ["DialogueBubble23130801"]="Eh? You again...",
    ["DialogueBubble23140101"]="You mean, they mysteriously disappeared?",
    ["DialogueBubble23140201"]="It's been three whole days, and I haven't heard a word.",
    ["DialogueBubble23140301"]="Hm, this situation...",
    ["DialogueBubble23140401"]="Eh? These wounds...",
    ["DialogueBubble23140501"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23140601"]="...It hurts...!",
    ["DialogueBubble23140701"]="Ah, thank you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23140801"]="Great. But it's not over yet.",
    ["DialogueBubble23140901"]="Yes, just like that!",
    ["DialogueBubble23141001"]="This is... a Directional Leaf?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23141101"]="H-help...",
    ["DialogueBubble23141201"]="......!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23141301"]="They're the kidnapped Eden Group members!",
    ["DialogueBubble23141401"]="I remember the switch to open the iron gate is by the Lionheart Pool...",
    ["DialogueBubble23141501"]="...Where?",
    ["DialogueBubble23141601"]="There's no scrolls here. I lied to you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23141701"]="Stop, there's still time...",
    ["DialogueBubble23141801"]="...Darned scammer.",
    ["DialogueBubble23150101"]="I have to figure this out...",
    ["DialogueBubble23150201"]="Well done, this is exactly what I need.",
    ["DialogueBubble23150301"]="Has it begun...?",
    ["DialogueBubble23150401"]="Wait, there's noise coming from somewhere near here...",
    ["DialogueBubble23150501"]="How... how could it be him?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23150601"]="So, do you still think I'm a lunatic?",
    ["DialogueBubble23150701"]="Ugh, I was too late...",
    ["DialogueBubble23150801"]="...This cloth strip!",
    ["DialogueBubble23150901"]="Thana... tos...",
    ["DialogueBubble23151001"]="...Hey, hold on!",
    ["DialogueBubble23151101"]="...I have underestimated you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23151201"]="Great, now all that's left is the final step.",
    ["DialogueBubble23151301"]="That's enough.",
    ["DialogueBubble23151401"]="Please wait a second...",
    ["DialogueBubble23160101"]="How......is this possible?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23160201"]="This is......",
    ["DialogueBubble23160202"]="——Please, please trust me!",
    ["DialogueBubble23160203"]="In the name of Odin, I shall not lie!",
    ["DialogueBubble23160204"]="……",
    ["DialogueBubble23160301"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23160401"]="——Tweet~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble23160501"]="Tweet——Tweet!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23160801"]="Adventurer, come!",
    ["DialogueBubble23160901"]="Here’s what I found out from my investigation.",
    ["DialogueBubble23161001"]="Commander, if we put the pieces together...",
    ["DialogueBubble23161101"]="Yes, the answer is clear now.",
    ["DialogueBubble23161201"]="... Can't make any mistakes...",
    ["DialogueBubble23161301"]="... The king...",
    ["DialogueBubble23161401"]="—Hush, quiet!",
    ["DialogueBubble23161501"]="Wow—Look at the elegant color!",
    ["DialogueBubble23161601"]="These flowers are as beautiful as the legend says...",
    ["DialogueBubble23161701"]="Fantastic! Piglet skin is perfect for crafting a tunic!",
    ["DialogueBubble23161801"]="Adventurer, what’s going on?",
    ["DialogueBubble23170101"]="Adventurer, come!",
    ["DialogueBubble23170201"]="......This is what I have investigated.",
    ["DialogueBubble23170202"]="Commander, if we put the pieces together!",
    ["DialogueBubble23170203"]="Yes, the answer is clear now.",
    ["DialogueBubble23170301"]="......Make no mistake......",
    ["DialogueBubble23170302"]="......and the King......",
    ["DialogueBubble23170303"]="——Hush, quiet!",
    ["DialogueBubble23170401"]="Wow——Look at the elegant color!",
    ["DialogueBubble23170501"]="These flowers are as beautiful as the legend says......",
    ["DialogueBubble23170601"]="Fantastic! Piglet skin is perfect for tunic~",
    ["DialogueBubble23170701"]="Adventurer, what’s going on?",
    ["DialogueBubble23180101"]="......We have sent people to search the city......",
    ["DialogueBubble23180102"]="But these people’s identity and locations are to hard to track......",
    ["DialogueBubble23180103"]="(Sigh emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23180201"]="Oh, is that what happened......",
    ["DialogueBubble23180202"]="Thanks, that’s very important.",
    ["DialogueBubble23180401"]="squawk,squawk——!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180501"]="So, this is the thing everyone talking about?",
    ["DialogueBubble23180502"]="Relief effort......Will that really cure people?",
    ["DialogueBubble23180503"]="Ah, I really hope the envoy of god can come for me.",
    ["DialogueBubble23180504"]="Me too......",
    ["DialogueBubble23180505"]="But who is he?",
    ["DialogueBubble23180601"]="The will of god and strength of giant......",
    ["DialogueBubble23180602"]="Yes, it must be that Sacred Relic!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180701"]="...It's you.",
    ["DialogueBubble23180801"]="——Stay away!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180802"]="Patients of mad disease dead ahead, very dangerous!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180803"]="Eh? It's a complete mess.",
    ["DialogueBubble23180804"]="Somebody......Can anyone help me?",
    ["DialogueBubble23180805"]="Ah, thank you!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180806"]="I could really have some of this hot porridge.",
    ["DialogueBubble23180901"]="I’m ordering you——Get Back!",
    ["DialogueBubble23180902"]="squawk,squawk——!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23190101"]="Don't tell me that child went to...",
    ["DialogueBubble23190102"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23190301"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23191001"]="Tao Gunka...",
    ["DialogueBubble23191002"]="Tao Gunka...",
    ["DialogueBubble23191003"]="Tao Gunka, heed my summon!",
    ["DialogueBubble23191004"]="Darn it... this familiar feeling!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23200101"]="Wh-What are we going to do?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23200201"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23200401"]="Help me... Help...",
    ["DialogueBubble23200501"]="Just tell me Drake's whereabouts...",
    ["DialogueBubble23200502"]="N-Never... You mad demoness!",
    ["DialogueBubble23200801"]="...Hmm, um.",
    ["DialogueBubble23201001"]="How, after all these years of bounty hunting...",
    ["DialogueBubble23201002"]="Did it turn you soft?",
    ["DialogueBubble23201003"]="Hmph, worry not, I'll shut your ugly trap up permanently right now.",
    ["DialogueBubble23210101"]="...Look at this! It definitely means trouble!",
    ["DialogueBubble23210102"]="Hmm...",
    ["DialogueBubble23210601"]="What's this...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23220101"]="Weird... Who could it be...",
    ["DialogueBubble23220201"]="Looks like it still needs...",
    ["DialogueBubble23220301"]="Thanks.",
    ["DialogueBubble23220401"]="... Thanks.",
    ["DialogueBubble23220501"]="Yes, this is it.",
    ["DialogueBubble23220601"]="This, how should I handle it?",
    ["DialogueBubble23220701"]="Hmm, let me recall...",
    ["DialogueBubble23220801"]="Ugh... Ahem!",
    ["DialogueBubble23220901"]="Any progress?",
    ["DialogueBubble23221001"]="How did he manage to fight back in his current state?",
    ["DialogueBubble23221101"]="ALL OF YOU... GO TO HELL!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble23230101"]="Odin, you are finally here!",
    ["DialogueBubble23230201"]="I would expect nothing less from the candidate recommended by Lord Kroneika!",
    ["DialogueBubble23230301"]="Lord Bidal's perspective really enlighten me!",
    ["DialogueBubble23230401"]="I don't deserve all that credits...",
    ["DialogueBubble23230501"]="Wonderful! This is exactly what I wanted!",
    ["DialogueBubble23230601"]="Indeed. These are the ones.",
    ["DialogueBubble23230701"]="Okay, allow me to take a look...",
    ["DialogueBubble23230801"]="Oh? This is...",
    ["DialogueBubble23230901"]="...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23231001"]="Ugh... W-What happened to me...?",
    ["DialogueBubble23231101"]="Here you are!",
    ["DialogueBubble23240101"]="La-LaLa 🎵",
    ["DialogueBubble23240201"]="(Surprised Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble23240301"]="(Crying Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble23240401"]="W-we meet again, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble23240501"]="You people can't get anything done right.",
    ["DialogueBubble23240601"]="But those merchants said yes...",
    ["DialogueBubble23240701"]="Yes, yeah. These are good quality.",
    ["DialogueBubble23240801"]="Thanks a lot! This really helps!",
    ["DialogueBubble23240901"]="I vote for the palace!",
    ["DialogueBubble23241001"]="No, no. No one but Odin is the supremacy of this kingdom...",
    ["DialogueBubble23241101"]="Now I reconfirm with you once more...",
    ["DialogueBubble23241201"]="Okay, let's talk.",
    ["DialogueBubble23241301"]="Like this, clues are connected.",
    ["DialogueBubble23241501"]="What! You like—",
    ["DialogueBubble23241601"]="Shh! Quiet! Don't say it out loud!",
    ["DialogueBubble23241701"]="—Seyren?!",
    ["DialogueBubble23241801"]="Margaret... doesn't like me...",
    ["DialogueBubble23241901"]="Like me... doesn't like me... like me...",
    ["DialogueBubble23242001"]="Doesn't...?! No—No! Another one!",
    ["DialogueBubble23242101"]="Um...",
    ["DialogueBubble23242201"]="Margaret... I...",
    ["DialogueBubble23242301"]="W-wait! I've got something to say too!",
    ["DialogueBubble23242402"]="...",
    ["DialogueBubble23250101"]="Adventurer, about the promise I made for investigating the mysterious runes...",
    ["DialogueBubble23250201"]="From the development aspect, their vocabulary and grammar present a complementary relationship...",
    ["DialogueBubble23250301"]="When I finish copying this, I can...",
    ["DialogueBubble23250401"]="Professor Laurent, you can't go in there!",
    ["DialogueBubble23250501"]="(Shake fist) For what reason? This is an abuse of power!",
    ["DialogueBubble23250601"]="Q-Quick! Stop him!",
    ["DialogueBubble23260101"]="Good day, Adventurer! Could you do me a favor?",
    ["DialogueBubble23260201"]="Here you go. Hold on tight.",
    ["DialogueBubble23260301"]="Hope the kids like it.",
    ["DialogueBubble23260401"]="Hmm... Should be there in any minute.",
    ["DialogueBubble23260402"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble23260403"]="Lord... That dearest Lord! IS HERE!",
    ["DialogueBubble23260501"]="Tsk, that's it...? Won't be enough for those kids.",
    ["DialogueBubble23260601"]="...Alright, that should do it.",
    ["DialogueBubble23260701"]="Hmm... These look pretty tasty though...",
    ["DialogueBubble23260801"]="Loti, do you like steak for dinner?",
    ["DialogueBubble23260901"]="Nope! We had steak last night already!",
    ["DialogueBubble23260902"]="Today should be a pizza day!",
    ["DialogueBubble23261001"]="What is this...?",
    ["DialogueBubble23261101"]="I've never had this before...",
    ["DialogueBubble23261201"]="*Cries* Stay away from me...",
    ["DialogueBubble23261301"]="I—I don't want to sit on the rocking chair anymore!",
    ["DialogueBubble23261302"]="Logan! Tell them to get off here!",
    ["DialogueBubble23261401"]="Porings are the most commonly seen monsters on this continent.",
    ["DialogueBubble23261402"]="They have rounded bodies without limbs, like a soft jelly to the feel...",
    ["DialogueBubble23261501"]="Wow... I wanna have a bite...",
    ["DialogueBubble2510001"]="Look, on the city walls! That's...",
    ["DialogueBubble2510002"]="Fall back! Fall back!",
    ["DialogueBubble2510003"]="You humans overestimate your strength.",
    ["DialogueBubble2510007"]="I'll take care of the city gate. You enter the city!",
    ["DialogueBubble2510008"]="Safe journeys to you, adventurers!",
    ["DialogueBubble2510009"]="Our work here is done. I'll leave the rest to you, people of the future!",
    ["DialogueBubble26000101"]="Don't let your guard down. We're at the critical stage of the outbreak!",
    ["DialogueBubble26000201"]="Good. Let me take a look...",
    ["DialogueBubble26000301"]="Living between heaven and earth, time seemingly flashes by in the blink of an eye, then suddenly, nothing.",
    ["DialogueBubble26000401"]="Lovely! You really did manage to get 99 Iron!",
    ["DialogueBubble26000501"]="Beautiful! A perfect Lucky Clover!",
    ["DialogueBubble26000601"]="This is the Witherless Rose?",
    ["DialogueBubble26000701"]="Hello! We meet again!",
    ["DialogueBubble26000801"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble26000901"]="Hello. Are you interested in learning about what we do at the Exchange Center?",
    ["DialogueBubble26001001"]="Hmm... Hmm... Magic sure is convenient, meow!",
    ["DialogueBubble26001201"]="Let's try out the Magic Bait meow!",
    ["DialogueBubble26001301"]="Hey, adventurer! Could you give me a hand?",
    ["DialogueBubble26001401"]="Wow! Congratulations!",
    ["DialogueBubble26001501"]="Oh my, you look positively radiant today!",
    ["DialogueBubble26001701"]="Ahhh! How could I be so unlucky?!",
    ["DialogueBubble26001801"]="It looks like a big battle is unavoidable.",
    ["DialogueBubble26001901"]="Good, I was right about you!",
    ["DialogueBubble26002001"]="It seems as though a sign from the goddess has arrived...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002101"]="We won't make it in time!",
    ["DialogueBubble26002201"]="What should we do...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002202"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble26002301"]="I-it's all your fault... *Cries* ...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002401"]="This is...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002501"]="Hm, everything is ready now.",
    ["DialogueBubble26002601"]="Adventurer, wait...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002701"]="This is the place...",
    ["DialogueBubble26002801"]="No, no way! How can I?!",
    ["DialogueBubble26002901"]="You have to do it!",
    ["DialogueBubble26003001"]="Here, Adventurer... Here...",
    ["DialogueBubble26003101"]="It's not enough. We still need more samples.",
    ["DialogueBubble26003201"]="This is what I want, Adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble26003301"]="Let's stop by the Pet Store! There's a grand opening!",
    ["DialogueBubble26003401"]="Looks like.. I have to buy items at Lyra's place again...",
    ["DialogueBubble26010101"]="(Crying Emoticons bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble26010201"]="Phew, lucky I wasn't eaten...",
    ["DialogueBubble26010301"]="Gah?",
    ["DialogueBubble26010401"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble26010501"]="This is...?",
    ["DialogueBubble26010601"]="(Grateful Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble26010701"]="(Like Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble26010801"]="You are back!",
    ["DialogueBubble26010901"]="This is not for me.",
    ["DialogueBubble26020101"]="(Sigh emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble26020201"]="This bread smells so good!",
    ["DialogueBubble26020301"]="The seal has weakened again?",
    ["DialogueBubble26020401"]="The warrior named by the prophecy...",
    ["DialogueBubble26020501"]="This is...!",
    ["DialogueBubble26020601"]="The locator has awakened. The heroes shall gather here.",
    ["DialogueBubble26030101"]="...Something must be wrong!",
    ["DialogueBubble26040101"]="Has anyone seen my child?!",
    ["DialogueBubble26060101"]="Darn it! Turn me back now!",
    ["DialogueBubble26080101"]="Ahem...",
    ["DialogueBubble26090101"]="There you are, Adventurer.",
    ["DialogueBubble26090201"]="Assemble Hyper Players and search for gold equipment, costumes, and Refinement Vouchers in the Hyper Return!",
    ["DialogueBubble26110101"]="Yuria, no matter what happens, I will protect you.",
    ["DialogueBubble26110201"]="Then stay alive, Kenshiro. That's my only wish.",
    ["DialogueBubble265001"]="Kiki remembers you!",
    ["DialogueBubble265002"]="I've been waiting so long for you, little Adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble26999801"]="Are you free tonight? Want to come over to my place for a drink?",
    ["DialogueBubble26999901"]="I know we only just met each other but it feels like I've known you forever.",
    ["DialogueBubble27010101"]="Come forward, the one inherited the Odin's Bloodline",
    ["DialogueBubble27020101"]="That it! Take it down!",
    ["DialogueBubble27030101"]="......Look! Sister Alice is here!",
    ["DialogueBubble27030201"]="Yes, it’s Alice!",
    ["DialogueBubble27030301"]="Sister Alice, what’s the story you have today?",
    ["DialogueBubble27030401"]="I will be a warrior when I grow up!",
    ["DialogueBubble27030501"]="Hmm...I really want to see the world outside......",
    ["DialogueBubble27040101"]="We meet again, adventurer~",
    ["DialogueBubble27040201"]="I just knew it......You are bound to return here.",
    ["DialogueBubble27040301"]="......And I will witness the last moment just for you.",
    ["DialogueBubble27050101"]="ZZZZZ……",
    ["DialogueBubble27050201"]="ZZZZZZ……",
    ["DialogueBubble27050301"]="ZZZZZZZ……",
    ["DialogueBubble27050401"]="Yes, it is the saliva of the Sky Petite~",
    ["DialogueBubble27050501"]="Claw washer for Bigfoot~Confirm~",
    ["DialogueBubble27050601"]="And the last......Muka juice......there you go!",
    ["DialogueBubble27060101"]="Swordman Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27060201"]="Acolyte Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27060301"]="Magician Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27060401"]="Thief Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27060501"]="Archer Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27060601"]="Merchant Trial",
    ["DialogueBubble27070101"]="Are my weapons and armor fixed, Sansha?",
    ["DialogueBubble27070102"]="They're fixed, Master, but your injuries...",
    ["DialogueBubble27070103"]="Since they're repaired, let us proceed.",
    ["DialogueBubble27080101"]="... Great, that's the one.",
    ["DialogueBubble27080201"]="Now, just one more thing...",
    ["DialogueBubble27080301"]="Hmm... what a pristine lifeforce...",
    ["DialogueBubble27090101"]="You're... too late.",
    ["DialogueBubble28070101"]="Yes, this has to be the hand of destiny...",
    ["DialogueBubble28070201"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28070301"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28070401"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28070501"]="Ohh! It's finished!",
    ["DialogueBubble28080101"]="Sigh. How do I make senior Dobbin notice my hard work?",
    ["DialogueBubble28080201"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28080301"]="I'll be waiting!",
    ["DialogueBubble28080401"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28080501"]="Ta-dah! It's finished!",
    ["DialogueBubble28080601"]="This is...?",
    ["DialogueBubble28080701"]="(Sweating emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28080801"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28080901"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28081001"]="By Odin, this smell... Are the two ingredients canceling each other out?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28081101"]="(Crying emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28090101"]="Heh. It's been a while, adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble28090201"]="That's it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28090301"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28090401"]="......?",
    ["DialogueBubble28090501"]="(Happy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28100101"]="Hi, adventurer. Mind helping me out?",
    ["DialogueBubble28100201"]="That's more than enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble28100301"]="That's more than enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble28100401"]="(Throwing up emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28100501"]="(Speechless emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28100601"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28110101"]="Adventurer, I...",
    ["DialogueBubble28110201"]="Hmph, I'm going to teach you a lesson!",
    ["DialogueBubble28110301"]="This is enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble28120101"]="So why should I join you again?",
    ["DialogueBubble28120102"]="You're so annoying! I told you I don't need it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28120201"]="I have to defeat stronger monsters!",
    ["DialogueBubble28120301"]="And make lots of friends!",
    ["DialogueBubble28120501"]="How is it? Do you feel better?",
    ["DialogueBubble28120601"]="Cough... Thank you, young one.",
    ["DialogueBubble28130101"]="That is strange indeed...",
    ["DialogueBubble28130201"]="Hmph, today will become the anniversary of your death!",
    ["DialogueBubble28130301"]="Strange... Why isn't that kid here yet?",
    ["DialogueBubble28140101"]="Hmph. How nostalgic...",
    ["DialogueBubble28140201"]="Hmm...",
    ["DialogueBubble28140301"]="...Is it really dead?",
    ["DialogueBubble28140302"]="Find her! Leave none alive!",
    ["DialogueBubble28140303"]="You are...?! Hmph! She finally showed up. Get her!",
    ["DialogueBubble28140401"]="Hmm... But I heard there's also a child...",
    ["DialogueBubble28140501"]="Mnn... What's wrong with mom and dad?",
    ["DialogueBubble28140502"]="AAHHH!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble28140601"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble28140701"]="You... You dare interfere with the master's plan?",
    ["DialogueBubble28140702"]="...Tch. How annoying. Retreat!",
    ["DialogueBubble28140801"]="Wait. That aura... Could he be Odin's...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28140901"]="Very well. I'll take good care of it.",
    ["DialogueBubble28150101"]="Sigh. I can't just go back empty-handed.",
    ["DialogueBubble28150201"]="So, how'd the discussion go?",
    ["DialogueBubble28160101"]="Who—Hic! Who did this?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28160201"]="*Squeaks!!*",
    ["DialogueBubble28160301"]="...A monkey?",
    ["DialogueBubble28160401"]="Hey, monkey. Where's the wine I wanted?",
    ["DialogueBubble28170101"]="...You really can't do it?",
    ["DialogueBubble28170201"]="Um... Actually, I...",
    ["DialogueBubble28170301"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28170401"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28180101"]="*Sobbing* Eiffel, where did you go?...",
    ["DialogueBubble28180201"]="That's right, this is the grass!",
    ["DialogueBubble28180301"]="Thank you. Now, let's take a look...",
    ["DialogueBubble28180401"]="Meow, meow...",
    ["DialogueBubble28180402"]="S-stupid, meow!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble28180501"]="Meow, meow...",
    ["DialogueBubble28190101"]="Hey... hey! You're finally here! I've been waiting for you.",
    ["DialogueBubble28190201"]="Hey, how'd it go? You can't praise Howard enough, right?",
    ["DialogueBubble28190301"]="Give up now. You can't beat me.",
    ["DialogueBubble28190401"]="...H-Howard?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28200101"]="How can this be...? How can this be, meeoow?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28200201"]="Yes... I have to figure out a way...",
    ["DialogueBubble28200301"]="Hey, over here! I'm here!",
    ["DialogueBubble28200401"]="So, did you get it?",
    ["DialogueBubble28200501"]="Damn humans, how dare they kill our kind...",
    ["DialogueBubble28200601"]="They cannot be forgiven, gob!!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210101"]="Haha, watch, just click here...",
    ["DialogueBubble28210201"]="Shut up... Shut up, intruder!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210301"]="Hmm... Why aren't they listening to me?",
    ["DialogueBubble28210401"]="I'm counting on you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210501"]="Oh, thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210601"]="So, I'm counting on you to take the photo!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210701"]="Oh, thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210801"]="Oh, thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble28210901"]="Oh, thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220101"]="Ah... Please, hear my request!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220201"]="Hm... That's just about it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220301"]="It's all up to you now!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220401"]="Wow! What a fine bracelet...!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220501"]="Hm... That's just about it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220601"]="...Chuu!",
    ["DialogueBubble28220701"]="Hmph, watch this!",
    ["DialogueBubble28230101"]="That's... a box full of oddyfruits!",
    ["DialogueBubble28230201"]="I'm asking about clues...",
    ["DialogueBubble28230301"]="So, did you find out anything?",
    ["DialogueBubble28230401"]="...What you mean is, this has been happening for a long time?",
    ["DialogueBubble28230501"]="We haven't eaten a full meal in months...",
    ["DialogueBubble28230601"]="Please, help yourselves to some food and water!",
    ["DialogueBubble28230701"]="S-stay back!",
    ["DialogueBubble28230801"]="Aaaahhh—!",
    ["DialogueBubble28230901"]="*Cries*",
    ["DialogueBubble28231001"]="...H-help!",
    ["DialogueBubble28231101"]="...Hey, what's this for?",
    ["DialogueBubble28240101"]="Oh. Seems pretty suspicious...",
    ["DialogueBubble28240201"]="Eh? What's this...?",
    ["DialogueBubble28240301"]="Ah, I'd expect nothing less from an apostle!",
    ["DialogueBubble28240401"]="We'd do anything to get divine help!",
    ["DialogueBubble28240501"]="Bwahahaha!",
    ["DialogueBubble28240601"]="I'm so mad. I'm so, so mad!!",
    ["DialogueBubble28240701"]="Haha, what's going on?",
    ["DialogueBubble28250101"]="Sigh, what should we do now...?",
    ["DialogueBubble28250201"]="*Crying*",
    ["DialogueBubble28250301"]="Eh? You're back already? How?",
    ["DialogueBubble28250401"]="You... You are?",
    ["DialogueBubble28250501"]="So how's the situation?",
    ["DialogueBubble28260101"]="Sigh, it's over... It's all over!",
    ["DialogueBubble28260201"]="H-Help me...",
    ["DialogueBubble28260301"]="Urgh...",
    ["DialogueBubble28260401"]="...I'm forever grateful to you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28260501"]="How did it go? Did you find it?",
    ["DialogueBubble28260601"]="Hmph, he asked for it.",
    ["DialogueBubble28270101"]="Sir, this is strange......",
    ["DialogueBubble28270201"]="......But how do we get in?",
    ["DialogueBubble28270301"]="Thanks, this is what I need.",
    ["DialogueBubble28270401"]="......But where did you get this?",
    ["DialogueBubble28270501"]="(Sigh emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28280101"]="Ah...This just won’t do!",
    ["DialogueBubble28280201"]="——Ah, ah, this is it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28280301"]="——Ah, ah, this is it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28280401"]="——Ah, ah, this is it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28280501"]="You're finally back!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290101"]="Ah, this is unbelievable!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290201"]="Here you are!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290301"]="Here you are!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290401"]="Here you are!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290501"]="Hey, hey! This way, adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290601"]="Hey, hey! This way, adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble28290701"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28290801"]="(Shy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28300101"]="Will grandpa warrior be lucky today?",
    ["DialogueBubble28300201"]="(Howling)",
    ["DialogueBubble28300301"]="Ah... Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch!",
    ["DialogueBubble28300401"]="Haha, you are so considerate!",
    ["DialogueBubble28300501"]="Yes, yes, that's it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28300601"]="……",
    ["DialogueBubble28310101"]="Guild Leader, this is nor normal......",
    ["DialogueBubble28310201"]="Please, you must do something!",
    ["DialogueBubble28310301"]="(Intimate chatting......)",
    ["DialogueBubble28310401"]="...Oh? This is interesting.",
    ["DialogueBubble28310501"]="How's it going? Am I right?",
    ["DialogueBubble28310601"]="(Blow Kisses emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28310701"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble28320101"]="Heheh, interesting...",
    ["DialogueBubble28320201"]="Out of the way, damn you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28320301"]="Gaaah!",
    ["DialogueBubble28320401"]="No, why would I do that...",
    ["DialogueBubble28320501"]="It's my treasure... Why would I toss it?",
    ["DialogueBubble28320601"]="Yeah, I certainly could keep it...",
    ["DialogueBubble28330101"]="Alas, what should I do?",
    ["DialogueBubble28330201"]="Chirp ♪",
    ["DialogueBubble28330301"]="Chirp, chirp ♪",
    ["DialogueBubble28330401"]="...What are these?",
    ["DialogueBubble28330501"]="Hey, scored big this time!",
    ["DialogueBubble28330601"]="I knew I couldn't go wrong with you!",
    ["DialogueBubble28330701"]="Where's that Kirk of mine?",
    ["DialogueBubble28340101"]="Don't miss out!",
    ["DialogueBubble28340201"]="Ouch... What rotten luck.",
    ["DialogueBubble28350101"]="That guy is a veritable scoundrel...",
    ["DialogueBubble28350201"]="Your face is a divine creation, your eyes are as deep as the ocean, Doyle!",
    ["DialogueBubble28350301"]="(Blow Kisses Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28350401"]="I'll always be yours, Doyle!",
    ["DialogueBubble28350501"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28350601"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28350701"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28350801"]="...Scram and don't stink up my manteau!",
    ["DialogueBubble28360101"]="What's going on?",
    ["DialogueBubble28360201"]="Hmm? What's that behind you?",
    ["DialogueBubble28370101"]="... Y-You, why don't you go?",
    ["DialogueBubble28370201"]="I see.",
    ["DialogueBubble28380101"]="What should I do... What the heck should I do?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28380201"]="... N-No way?!",
    ["DialogueBubble28380301"]="... zZZ...",
    ["DialogueBubble28380401"]="Ahem... P-Please pardon my rudeness...",
    ["DialogueBubble28380501"]="Drink this... and you will wake up...",
    ["DialogueBubble28380601"]="... Hmm... I...",
    ["DialogueBubble28390101"]="Please forgive me...",
    ["DialogueBubble28390201"]="... Thank you.",
    ["DialogueBubble28400101"]="... What is this...",
    ["DialogueBubble28400201"]="Thank you, Adventurer...",
    ["DialogueBubble28400301"]="Thanks, I feel a lot better.",
    ["DialogueBubble28410101"]="(Silent, speak nothing...)",
    ["DialogueBubble28420101"]="Darn it. They disappear again...",
    ["DialogueBubble28430101"]="Adventurer, please wait...",
    ["DialogueBubble28440101"]="How come they are still not there yet...",
    ["DialogueBubble28440201"]="Please let us go...",
    ["DialogueBubble28450101"]="It's finally over...",
    ["DialogueBubble28460101"]="Shana? Shana!",
    ["DialogueBubble28460201"]="Ladies and gentlemen! Welcome to Rekenber's new product release conference!",
    ["DialogueBubble28460202"]="For the next thirty minutes, I need to borrow your attention and give it to our most shiny product—",
    ["DialogueBubble28460203"]="Digger No.2!",
    ["DialogueBubble28460301"]="Shana! Where have you been?",
    ["DialogueBubble28460401"]="Aww! Irumina is so handsome...",
    ["DialogueBubble28470101"]="... Adventurer, I hope you'll tell me the truth.",
    ["DialogueBubble28470201"]="(Heart Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28470301"]="Hahaha! You actually fell for it!",
    ["DialogueBubble28470401"]="—Get them!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480101"]="Hey, hey! Adventurer! Over here!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480201"]="Boohoo...",
    ["DialogueBubble28480301"]="(Sigh Emoticon)",
    ["DialogueBubble28480401"]="D-Don't cry! Here, take this!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480501"]="Useless fool... You couldn't even handle a kid!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480601"]="Boss, she kept crying about wanting to see the seagulls—I couldn't stop her!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480701"]="Whatever! One less doesn't matter!",
    ["DialogueBubble28480801"]="Take the rest and get moving! The ship's about to leave!",
    ["DialogueBubble29010101"]="I have some good news to tell you!",
    ["DialogueBubble29010201"]="Back already? I wouldn't expect anything less from you!",
    ["DialogueBubble29020101"]="What a pain...",
    ["DialogueBubble29030101"]="To create a paradise for the children... That's all we wanted.",
    ["DialogueBubble29030201"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble29040101"]="To create a paradise for the children... That's all we wanted.",
    ["DialogueBubble29040201"]="(Grateful emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble29050101"]="You're back again! It seems you're really serious about fishing!",
    ["DialogueBubble29050201"]="Not bad, not bad at all! This should be enough!",
    ["DialogueBubble29050301"]="What took you so long?",
    ["DialogueBubble29060101"]="You're just in time! I need your help!",
    ["DialogueBubble29060201"]="Thank you so much! This is really going to help!",
    ["DialogueBubble29070101"]="If I want to win the championship, I'm going to need a model!",
    ["DialogueBubble29070201"]="Well done. I see you have great potential!",
    ["DialogueBubble29070301"]="Looks good! This is exactly what I need!",
    ["DialogueBubble29080101"]="You're here! I was hoping you'd come help me with something.",
    ["DialogueBubble29080201"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble29090101"]="I don't care what kind of currency you're carrying. If it's not high-quality crystals, I'm not interested!",
    ["DialogueBubble29090201"]="What a surprise. Sinclair's sent someone to borrow my stuff again.",
    ["DialogueBubble29090301"]="Things seem to be going well.",
    ["DialogueBubble29100101"]="Hey! It's you! Come here, quick!",
    ["DialogueBubble29100201"]="From the looks of things, the Monster Encyclopedia will be ready for publication soon.",
    ["DialogueBubble29110101"]="This time, I must prove myself to her!",
    ["DialogueBubble29110201"]="Hey! Wait!",
    ["DialogueBubble29110301"]="You're back at last!",
    ["DialogueBubble29120101"]="This is embarrassing. This is so embarrassing! Sad emoticon bubble",
    ["DialogueBubble29120201"]="Wow! It smells delicious!",
    ["DialogueBubble29130101"]="Hey! Long time, no see!",
    ["DialogueBubble29130201"]="You're here at last! I'm short of helping hands!",
    ["DialogueBubble29140101"]="Well... I'll need some materials to extract the flavor...",
    ["DialogueBubble29150101"]="Now we're all set!",
    ["DialogueBubble29160101"]="It is my pleasure to serve you.",
    ["DialogueBubble29160201"]="You're back already? You have lived up to expectations!",
    ["DialogueBubble29170101"]="It seems that there are still a few things missing...",
    ["DialogueBubble29180101"]="This is great!",
    ["DialogueBubble29180102"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["DialogueBubble29190101"]="You're back so quick. I'd expect nothing less of you!",
    ["DialogueBubble29200101"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["DialogueBubble29210101"]="Looks like we still need a Sasquatch Bone.",
    ["DialogueBubble29220101"]="... Yawn.",
    ["DialogueBubble29220201"]="Ooh, this is...!",
    ["DialogueBubble29220301"]="There's more than one floor! Come!",
    ["DialogueBubble29230101"]="Aroo... Aroo!",
    ["DialogueBubble29230201"]="Aroo...",
    ["DialogueBubble29230301"]="Aroo!",
    ["DialogueBubble29230401"]="Meow!",
    ["DialogueBubble29240101"]="Puff...",
    ["DialogueBubble29250101"]="... What's the matter?",
    ["DialogueBubble29250201"]="... Woah!",
    ["DialogueBubble29260101"]="... Hmm, if that's the case...",
    ["DialogueBubble29270101"]="Hmph...",
    ["DialogueBubble31000101"]="Take a look at what I've prepared for you, my dear!",
    ["DialogueBubble31000102"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31000103"]="Go away, pervert.",
    ["DialogueBubble31000201"]="So? Have you fallen for my supernatural charm?",
    ["DialogueBubble31000202"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31000301"]="Then it's agreed. You'll help Ygnizem and I'll take the other student.",
    ["DialogueBubble31000401"]="Fine, fine. Ugh... How annoying.",
    ["DialogueBubble31000402"]="What was your name again? Ygnazem?",
    ["DialogueBubble31000403"]="Come along, Ygnazem!",
    ["DialogueBubble31000501"]="...It's Ygnizem.",
    ["DialogueBubble31000502"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31000503"]="It's Ygnizem!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble31000601"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31000602"]="Who did this?!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010101"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31010201"]="Hand over the Alchemy Device!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010301"]="Those assassins have gone too far!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010302"]="Nothing... Another day and I would have lost a huge sum of Zeny!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010401"]="The money isn't the problem though. It's... wrath that I don't wanna deal with.",
    ["DialogueBubble31010402"]="Have you retrieved the device yet?",
    ["DialogueBubble31010403"]="Shh! Quiet!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010501"]="Help me!",
    ["DialogueBubble31010601"]="Careful! Stay right where you are!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020101"]="...This is a complete and utter mess!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020102"]="And what should we do about the wounded?",
    ["DialogueBubble31020103"]="Rorke has already gone to the Great Sage for help!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020201"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31020301"]="You are...?",
    ["DialogueBubble31020401"]="Sailor, I won't allow you to desert your post!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020402"]="How many times do I need to tell you!? I'm not your sailor!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020403"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31020404"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31020501"]="My... ring...",
    ["DialogueBubble31020601"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31020602"]="I can't believe you actually barged your way onto my boat!",
    ["DialogueBubble31020603"]="Time to die!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030101"]="May the love between Trisse and I be as indestructible as the strongest ore!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030102"]="Indestructible! Waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030103"]="Indestructible! Waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030104"]="That's right! Indestructible, waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030105"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31030201"]="May my life with Trisse be as hot as molten lava!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030202"]="Molten lava! Waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030203"]="Molten lava! Waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030204"]="Uh-huh! Molten lava, waka!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030205"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31030301"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31030602"]="I can't believe you actually barged your way onto my boat!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030603"]="Time to die!",
    ["DialogueBubble31030701"]="This...",
    ["DialogueBubble31030901"]="Sailor, I won't allow you to desert your post!",
    ["DialogueBubble31031101"]="Please... help me...",
    ["DialogueBubble31031201"]="I... remember...",
    ["DialogueBubble31031301"]="You... How did you get in here!?",
    ["DialogueBubble31031401"]="Hand over the Fragment of Ymir's Heart!",
    ["DialogueBubble31031501"]="Your days of using it to make undead monsters are over!",
    ["DialogueBubble31031601"]="You'll never enslave anyone ever again!",
    ["DialogueBubble31031701"]="Time to die!",
    ["DialogueBubble31040101"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31040201"]="Dang... This sure is tricky... What does this all mean?",
    ["DialogueBubble31040301"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31040401"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble31040501"]="Is this how it's done?",
    ["DialogueBubble31040502"]="That's the ticket. My potion will place Strouf into a deep slumber. Now, pull out that scale...",
    ["DialogueBubble31040503"]="Father won't be harmed, will he?",
    ["DialogueBubble31040504"]="Don't worry, he'll be fine.",
    ["DialogueBubble31040601"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble31040701"]="(Surprised emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble32000101"]="A giant serpent swallowing...~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000201"]="A giant serpent swallowing...~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000301"]="...swallowed it instead... ♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000401"]="...made a nest across the sea...~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000501"]="A giant serpent swallowing the sea~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000601"]="A giant serpent swallowing the sea~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000701"]="A rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000801"]="And made a nest across the sea~♪",
    ["DialogueBubble32000901"]="(Thumbs up emoticon pops up at the same time)",
    ["DialogueBubble32001001"]="Hey! Have you heard?",
    ["DialogueBubble32001101"]="It seems the old succession system will be starting back up...",
    ["DialogueBubble32001201"]="Of course! Now all seven families can compete for the throne!",
    ["DialogueBubble32001301"]="I can't wait to see what'll happen! Hehehe!",
    ["DialogueBubble32001401"]="The other six of the seven royal families are following this matter with great interest!",
    ["DialogueBubble32001501"]="His Majesty must be very worried right now, no?",
    ["DialogueBubble32001601"]="I wonder... Which of the seven royal families will be next to call this palace their home?",
    ["DialogueBubble32001701"]="The three immediate heirs of the Gaebolg Family died under suspicious circumstances.",
    ["DialogueBubble32010101"]="(Shocked emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble32010201"]="Meyer... Just what do you think you're doing!?",
    ["DialogueBubble32010301"]="This...",
    ["DialogueBubble32010401"]="Darn...",
    ["DialogueBubble32010501"]="Hee-hee... Another spare tire for the collection!",
    ["DialogueBubble32010601"]="Agnes!",
    ["DialogueBubble32010701"]="Whoa... I don't want to be eaten!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020101"]="Haha! Look what I found!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020201"]="Is this... an invitation card? Could it be that the wedding is today...?",
    ["DialogueBubble32020301"]="That's right. I'll be able to get a glimpse of Veronica's beautiful face!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020401"]="Ah... It's a real shame that Princess Veronica's marrying Bohr of the Richard Family!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020501"]="Right you are... The greatest beauty in the land is going to end up with that emotionless fink!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020601"]="And the marriage is nothing more than a deal between the royal family and the Kingdom Defense Force...",
    ["DialogueBubble32020701"]="Can you believe it? The wedding is about to start and the new couple still hasn't shown up!",
    ["DialogueBubble32020801"]="The perfect start to an imperfect marriage...",
    ["DialogueBubble32020901"]="Shh! Keep your voice down—the Richard Family butler is just over there!",
    ["DialogueBubble32021001"]="Ridiculous! Now, get out of here!",
    ["DialogueBubble32021101"]="Hmph! So, you refuse the Master's request? You might regret it...",
    ["DialogueBubble32021201"]="Are you threatening me!?",
    ["DialogueBubble32021301"]="Aren't you jealous? Though you're of the same blood, Bohr gets to marry the woman you love...",
    ["DialogueBubble32021401"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble32021501"]="...Trust me. As long as you do as the Master says, you will get your way... even if you are just the illegitimate son of the Richard Family!",
    ["DialogueBubble32021601"]="Not only will you become the new Commander of the Kingdom Defense Force, you will also get your hands on your beloved Veronica!",
    ["DialogueBubble32021701"]="I...",
    ["DialogueBubble32021801"]="Who's there!?",
    ["DialogueBubble32030101"]="I shall now announce the results of the bidding——",
    ["DialogueBubble32030102"]="The Lindra Trading Company acquired a monopoly on this product!",
    ["DialogueBubble32030201"]="Ah!",
    ["DialogueBubble32030301"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble32030401"]="......",
    ["DialogueBubble32030501"]="Father... I was wrong. I shouldn't have competed with my brothers in such a way...",
    ["DialogueBubble32030502"]="But I also want the Wigner family to respect me!",
    ["DialogueBubble32030503"]="I hope you can finally acknowledge my talents and let me contribute to the family business!",
    ["DialogueBubble32030601"]="Nonsense! Only my heirs can——",
    ["DialogueBubble32030701"]="Father... Please allow her.",
    ["DialogueBubble32030801"]="Father... Please allow her.",
    ["DialogueBubble32030901"]="You...",
    ["DialogueBubble32050101"]="That's right. I guessed it was them...",
    ["DialogueBubble32050201"]="Then go back and have a look!",
    ["DialogueBubble32050301"]="I... It's best if you go!",
    ["DialogueBubble32050401"]="You know who we are, don't you?",
    ["DialogueBubble32050501"]="Assassinate the prince—do you have a death wish?",
    ["DialogueBubble32050601"]="—Get outta the way, or don't blame us for getting rude!",
    ["DialogueBubble32050701"]="You're finally back!",
    ["DialogueBubble32050801"]="What... what's going on?",
    ["DialogueBubble32050901"]="...Wait, this is?!",
    ["DialogueBubble32051001"]="This mark...",
    ["DialogueBubble32051101"]="Adventurer? How could you...",
    ["DialogueBubble32051201"]="...As expected.",
    ["DialogueBubble32051301"]="How did it go? Did you discover anything?",
    ["DialogueBubble32051401"]="...I see. So it was them!",
    ["DialogueBubble32051501"]="...How did it go?",
    ["DialogueBubble32051601"]="Look at those suffering souls...",
    ["DialogueBubble32051701"]="The roar from the netherworld will soon drown them...",
    ["DialogueBubble32051801"]="*Cries* ...",
    ["DialogueBubble32051901"]="In the name of Odin, grant them a peaceful, eternal slumber—",
    ["DialogueBubble32052001"]="Odin, this is no easy matter...",
    ["DialogueBubble32052101"]="You're finally here.",
    ["DialogueBubble32052201"]="...How did it go?",
    ["DialogueBubble32052301"]="How did your investigation go?",
    ["DialogueBubble32052401"]="Yes, that's the fruit.",
    ["DialogueBubble32052501"]="Great. This is enough.",
    ["DialogueBubble32052601"]="Nice, just like that.",
    ["DialogueBubble32052701"]="Ah, perfect timing!",
    ["DialogueBubble32052801"]="Great. Everything is ready now.",
    ["DialogueBubble32052901"]="Is this... enough?",
    ["DialogueBubble32053001"]="L-Lord Azer, you're...?!",
    ["DialogueBubble32053101"]="*Coughs* ...Ahem.",
    ["DialogueBubble32053201"]="Adventurer, come...",
    ["DialogueBubble32053301"]="Pfft, darn it...",
    ["DialogueBubble32053401"]="...At any rate, I've already got what I came for. Fall back!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060101"]="Adventurer, are you ready?",
    ["DialogueBubble32060201"]="(Love emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble32060301"]="Ha——ha......",
    ["DialogueBubble32060401"]="--Gahh, Geez --!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060502"]="......Hurry, back to camp!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060503"]="Hurry up, aren’t you worry about ambush?",
    ["DialogueBubble32060602"]="You touching Nana Ba’s stone, die!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060701"]="You touching Nana Ba’s stone, die!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060801"]="Phew! Thank you so much!",
    ["DialogueBubble32060901"]="H-Help me...",
    ["DialogueBubble32061001"]="Gurgle--gurgle......",
    ["DialogueBubble32061101"]="What should I do, where is it?",
    ["DialogueBubble32061201"]="*Crying*",
    ["DialogueBubble32061301"]="Siza, glad you are alright!",
    ["DialogueBubble32061401"]="......Finally see you in person.",
    ["DialogueBubble32061501"]="--Haha, is the adventurer!",
    ["DialogueBubble32061601"]="Good job, my friend!",
    ["DialogueBubble32061701"]="......Thanks.",
    ["DialogueBubble32061801"]="Adventurer, I’ve been waiting.",
    ["DialogueBubble33050101"]="The successor of Odin's bloodline... We meet again...",
    ["DialogueBubble33050102"]="Come closer... I have something to tell you",
    ["DialogueBubble33070101"]="Liu, why did you ask me here?",
    ["DialogueBubble33070201"]="Last time you mentioned how beautiful you thought the maple leaves in the forest were, so I made a bookmark just for you...",
    ["DialogueBubble33070202"]="If you like it, please use it...",
    ["DialogueBubble33070301"]="(Shy emoticon bubble)",
    ["DialogueBubble33070302"]="They say \"give and you shall receive in turn\"... But this is not a \"thank you\"... It's just to show you how I feel...",
    ["DialogueBubble33070401"]="Hmph... You followed me all the way here.",
    ["DialogueBubble33070501"]="Give Jingyin back to me!",
    ["DialogueBubble33070601"]="Hee-hee! Even if I give her back to you, do you think... she'll still remember you?",
    ["DialogueBubble33070701"]="Jingyin!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble33070801"]="Hmph! Take a look! She will become my greatest masterpiece!",
    ["DialogueBubble33090101"]="Eunsook... Why... are you avoiding me?",
    ["DialogueBubble33090102"]="What happened?",
    ["DialogueBubble33090103"]="Okay, but I'll be back this evening.",
    ["DialogueBubble33090201"]="(Eunsook's back is to Busang)\nNo... You... Leave this place now. It's dangerous here, Busang. Didn't I tell you that we shouldn't meet again...",
    ["DialogueBubble33090202"]="I'm sorry, I... I have my own problems to deal with. You... You'd better get out of here.",
    ["DialogueBubble4000401"]="Hehe... I smell fresh human flesh! Hmph! Stupid humans, you've come seeking death again!",
    ["DialogueBubble4000501"]="Help... Help me! My friends all collapsed when they entered. This place is cursed, I tell you!",
    ["DialogueBubble4001001"]="Friend, can you come and talk with me for a while?",
    ["DialogueBubble4001101"]="Are men really so clueless? Don't they know women despise frivolous men?",
    ["DialogueBubble4001201"]="Are you teasing me?",
    ["DialogueBubble4001301"]="It's just like Julie to do such a rotten thing in broad daylight!",
    ["DialogueBubble4001401"]="Let's find somewhere to talk.",
    ["DialogueBubble5399701"]="Don't hit me! There aren't any treasure chests here!",
    ["DialogueBubble5399801"]="It's all a lie!",
    ["DialogueBubble54026101"]="For the glory of the Knights' Order!",
    ["DialogueBubble54028101"]="Defend Prontera!",
    ["DialogueBubble5540401"]="I... couldn’t escape in the end...",
    ["DialogueBubble5540402"]="Hmph! There’s no way you’re getting away with my treasure!",
    ["DialogueBubble55405"]="Damn... You caught up to me...",
    ["DialogueBubble55406"]="Evil spirit, I banish thee!",
    ["DialogueBubble55407"]="In with good fortune, out with evil...",
    ["DialogueBubble55408"]="Scatter beans to banish the evil spirits!",
    ["DialogueBubble55421"]="With the power of these beans, I banish all evil!",
    ["DialogueBubble600012101"]="Another young adventurer...",
    ["DialogueBubble600032101"]="Welcome. Welcome to Izlude Island.",
    ["DialogueBubble600042101"]="Unauthorized personnel are to stay clear of the sewers!",
    ["DialogueBubble600042201"]="Wigner Manor is ahead! Please mind your words and actions!",
    ["DialogueBubble600052101"]="Just look at his armor... How handsome!",
    ["DialogueBubble600062101"]="I wish I could become an adventurer one day!",
    ["DialogueBubble600072101"]="The boat's here!",
    ["DialogueBubble600082101"]="He must've gone to Criatura Academy. They've been recruiting new students recently!",
    ["DialogueBubble600092101"]="The boat's here! The boat's here!",
    ["DialogueBubble600112101"]="Now that's a beautiful boat!",
    ["DialogueBubble600152101"]="*Cough* When I was young, boy did I love a good adventure...",
    ["DialogueBubble600162101"]="Many young people come here from across the sea every year.",
    ["DialogueBubble600192101"]="Welcome to Izlude Island. Will you be attending Criatura Academy?",
    ["DialogueBubble600202101"]="Young adventurer, Izlude Island is a marvelous place.",
    ["DialogueBubble600212101"]="From the look in your eyes, I can tell that you must be a very powerful person!",
    ["DialogueBubble600222101"]="Welcome, guest from afar.",
    ["DialogueBubble600232101"]="A true knight should be chivalrous! Don't be like those other embarrassments to the Knights' Order!",
    ["DialogueBubble600242101"]="Right! Never forget the knight's ultimate mission!",
    ["DialogueBubble600242201"]="This is a Pecopeco... We're gonna get on just fine, right? Bloop!",
    ["DialogueBubble600252101"]="I want a companion like yours, too... That settles it—I want to be a knight!",
    ["DialogueBubble600262101"]="Odin is all-seeing and all-knowing. He is connected to everything, even when he is sleeping...",
    ["DialogueBubble600262201"]="May the dead bathe in Odin's blessings and relish the fruits of their heroic fate...",
    ["DialogueBubble600262301"]="Everyone buried here has been chosen by Odin. They are destined to become Epic Spirits.",
    ["DialogueBubble600312101"]="You can use the Scarecrow in the Training Course to test your fighting skills!",
    ["DialogueBubble600322101"]="Welcome to Prontera! Please feel free to take a look around—I hope you enjoy it here.",
    ["DialogueBubble600332101"]="Libra and Serpentrod's discounts really are nothing to sneeze at today.",
    ["DialogueBubble600342101"]="It's thanks to the fierce competition between them that we can get such cheap dishes.",
    ["DialogueBubble600352101"]="The Serpentrod Group has some super special promotions for you! We've got Morroc handicrafts—come and experience a taste of the exotic!",
    ["DialogueBubble600362101"]="Special products, courtesy of the Libra Group! Payon Green Plants! Take one home today!",
    ["DialogueBubble600372101"]="The Serpentrod Group brings you the freshest organic vegetables from the Northern Republic! All super-cheap and of the highest quality!",
    ["DialogueBubble600382101"]="Today's fruit is now on sale—everything must go! You can always count on the Libra Group!",
    ["DialogueBubble600392101"]="Hey, these are all the treasures from the ocean depths! Wanna try your luck?",
    ["DialogueBubble600402101"]="Fancy a glass of orange juice from the Rose Red Tavern?",
    ["DialogueBubble600492101"]="They say that couples who sit on the carousel together will be together forever.",
    ["DialogueBubble600492201"]="The Rose Red Tavern's Catwomen really live up to their reputation.",
    ["DialogueBubble600502101"]="Seriously? Then I'll sit down...",
    ["DialogueBubble600502201"]="Every time I hear music playing in the tavern, I feel like I could fly!",
    ["DialogueBubble600512101"]="I wanna spin and spin, 'round and 'round! The spinning teacups are the heart and soul of the amusement park!",
    ["DialogueBubble600512201"]="I hear a lot of adventurers come to the board just to see Isabella.",
    ["DialogueBubble600522101"]="Does such a soul even exist?",
    ["DialogueBubble600522201"]="Right! Are you going to pick a song from the jukebox?",
    ["DialogueBubble600532101"]="Haha! Kids are so energetic... These old bones can't keep up with them!",
    ["DialogueBubble600542101"]="Welcome to the Poring Amusement Park! Please buy your tickets here!",
    ["DialogueBubble600552101"]="All travelers wishing to take the train, please wait for a moment!",
    ["DialogueBubble600562101"]="Love Emoticon",
    ["DialogueBubble600572101"]="Nod Emoticon",
    ["DialogueBubble600582101"]="Blow a Kiss Emoticon",
    ["DialogueBubble600592101"]="Note Emoticon",
    ["DialogueBubble600642101"]="Get to work! Don't let the adventurers see you lazing about!",
    ["DialogueBubble600642201"]="I, I'm not drunk...! Hic! See, I... I'm rowing! Rowing!",
    ["DialogueBubble600652101"]="This is the best place to enjoy the sunset in all of Alberta!",
    ["DialogueBubble600652201"]="I... I'm not lazing about!",
    ["DialogueBubble600662101"]="All students who wish to go to Criatura Academy—this way, please!",
    ["DialogueBubble600672101"]="Mom, I'm going to become an adventurer, too! I'm gonna be a hero!",
    ["DialogueBubble600672201"]="Dad, why is that girl dressed like a cat?",
    ["DialogueBubble600692101"]="If you choose to wield a sword, it is your responsibility to uphold justice. To be a real Swordsman, one must protect the world with both sword and shield!",
    ["DialogueBubble600702101"]="Magic is a serious and dangerous subject. The more marvelous it looks, the more unseen sacrifice has gone into it. If you choose this path, don't take it lightly.",
    ["DialogueBubble600712101"]="Acolytes are Odin's emissaries. We believe in Odin, serve him, and walk with him. We are Odin's messengers in Midgard.",
    ["DialogueBubble600722101"]="Remember, to become a Thief is to choose a path shunned by the world. Hone your inner beliefs and sneak from the shadows and into your future!",
    ["DialogueBubble600732101"]="It's time to let the world know the power of money! Merchants should not only be strong and powerful, but should also be able to see into the hearts of others—this is the true charm of a Merchant!",
    ["DialogueBubble600742101"]="The sound of arrows piercing the sky lives deep in your bones, deep in your soul, bringing with it the salvation of the Goddess of the Dead... If you decide to choose the path of freedom, are you willing to embark upon the path of ruthlessness?",
    ["DialogueBubble600882101"]="I'm so busy! If I finish my work before it gets dark, I can finally go home!",
    ["DialogueBubble600892101"]="A lot of goods have been pouring into Alberta recently...",
    ["DialogueBubble600902101"]="Thanks to the Libra and Serpentrod Groups, our fleet's performance has tripled.",
    ["DialogueBubble600912101"]="If only I had a few more helpers...",
    ["DialogueBubble600922101"]="The Sapphire Blue Tavern is holding a homecoming celebration for the sailors!",
    ["DialogueBubble600922201"]="Today is registration day at the academy! It's half price on orange juice!",
    ["DialogueBubble600932101"]="Wanna experience the unique style of Alberta's bars?",
    ["DialogueBubble600932201"]="The area up ahead has been privately reserved. No one is allowed to enter without an invitation!",
    ["DialogueBubble600942101"]="As long as you have a sailor's certificate, you'll be eligible for exclusive drinks at the Sapphire Blue Tavern!",
    ["DialogueBubble600942201"]="How can I help you? Our special orange juice is highly recommended!",
    ["DialogueBubble600952101"]="Although Prince Jurgen and Prince Isaac are opposed, they are still both members of the Wigner Family.",
    ["DialogueBubble600962101"]="How long has it been since they attended a Wigner Family banquet...?",
    ["DialogueBubble600972101"]="Even if the two princes haven't been back in so long, the master has still asked for dinner to be prepared for the entire family every day.",
    ["DialogueBubble600982101"]="Welcome to Alberta. We're sure you'll love the customs here on our island!",
    ["DialogueBubble600992101"]="Hmm... You're still young. You'll understand when you grow up. Now, let's have a quick meal!",
    ["DialogueBubble601002101"]="Let us celebrate the fact that we're about to become adventurers! Cheers!",
    ["DialogueBubble601012101"]="Unfortunately, we're not old enough to drink just yet. Cheers!",
    ["DialogueBubble601022101"]="Orange juice isn't a bad choice, either! Cheers!",
    ["DialogueBubble601032101"]="*Munch, munch* Mmm... So tasty!",
    ["DialogueBubble6015021"]="Capricorn's meteor shower... Is he thinking of me?",
    ["DialogueBubble60250"]="Care for a pint of Comodo's finest?",
    ["DialogueBubble60251"]="A joint recommendation from Vendra and the Galapagos!",
    ["DialogueBubble60252"]="Here's my next song for y'all: A Song of Wine and Fire ♪",
    ["DialogueBubble60253"]="Wow!",
    ["DialogueBubble60254"]="Great song!",
    ["DialogueBubble60255"]="I love it!",
    ["DialogueBubble60256"]="Anything fun?",
    ["DialogueBubble60257"]="Over here. I'll show you!",
    ["DialogueBubble60259"]="Welcome to my home!",
    ["DialogueBubble60260"]="Hey, there you are again!",
    ["DialogueBubble60262"]="Long time no see!",
    ["DialogueBubble60263"]="This is my debut concert. Please...",
    ["DialogueBubble6026421"]="Welcome!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026422"]="Welcome!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026423"]="Liquor is for mushrooms too?",
    ["DialogueBubble6026424"]="\"Hundred Ways to Prepare Mushrooms\" claims it's tastier this way!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026425"]="Huff, puff...",
    ["DialogueBubble6026621"]="Welcome!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026622"]="Welcome!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026623"]="The coconut tree is so tall!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026624"]="Train under the waterfall and be the mightiest mushroom!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026625"]="Good luck!",
    ["DialogueBubble6026626"]="Good luck!",
    ["DialogueBubble60267"]="Amazing voice!",
    ["DialogueBubble60268"]="Applause!",
    ["DialogueBubble60269"]="Should get my daughter to learn singing as well...",
    ["DialogueBubble60270"]="Back to my archaeological studies after this song...",
    ["DialogueBubble60271"]="Let's go surfing today!",
    ["DialogueBubble60273"]="I'd like some barbecued fish. Yummy!",
    ["DialogueBubble60274"]="Don't eat the fish with roe!",
    ["DialogueBubble60277"]="Pretty normal. Look at this report...",
    ["DialogueBubble60278"]="Today's tide comes at the wrong time...",
    ["DialogueBubble60279"]="Keep quiet!",
    ["DialogueBubble60280"]="Keep quiet!",
    ["DialogueBubble60281"]="Today's motion is...",
    ["DialogueBubble60282"]="What are we gonna eat?",
    ["DialogueBubble60283"]="What do we play?",
    ["DialogueBubble60284"]="Hey, you two!",
    ["DialogueBubble60285"]="Safe travels!",
    ["DialogueBubble60286"]="Give Captain Drake's name if something happens!",
    ["DialogueBubble60287"]="Cheers!",
    ["DialogueBubble60288"]="Cheers!",
    ["DialogueBubble60289"]="Together!",
    ["DialogueBubble60290"]="Together!",
    ["DialogueBubble60291"]="The age of this drink...",
    ["DialogueBubble60292"]="Vendra is skilled in making drinks!",
    ["DialogueBubble60294"]="Today's gonna be another jolly day!",
    ["DialogueBubble60297"]="Today, we have the Umbala Fruit Wine recommended by our lord!",
    ["DialogueBubble60298"]="Today, we have the Umbala Fruit Wine recommended by our lord!",
    ["DialogueBubble60299"]="I need a translator...",
    ["DialogueBubble60300"]="Tour guiding, translating, or shopping... I'm the guy!",
    ["DialogueBubble60301"]="Where should I learn Utan's language?",
    ["DialogueBubble60302"]="Sir! I can't take off the mask!",
    ["DialogueBubble60303"]="... We can only pay the Lord a visit...",
    ["DialogueBubble60304"]="!&&%$##*... Yggdrasil!",
    ["DialogueBubble60305"]="!&&%$##*... Wizard...",
    ["DialogueBubble60306"]="!&&%$##*... Become the warrior!",
    ["DialogueBubble60307"]="Let's take a beautiful picture here!",
    ["DialogueBubble60308"]="1, 2, 3... Cheese!",
    ["DialogueBubble60309"]="Comping up—Song of Luluka!",
    ["DialogueBubble60310"]="Lu-lu",
    ["DialogueBubble60311"]="Lu-lu",
    ["DialogueBubble60314"]="Mi-mi",
    ["DialogueBubble60315"]="Miao",
    ["DialogueBubble60317"]="%%!*... Let's dance!",
    ["DialogueBubble60318"]="Dance it up!",
    ["DialogueBubble60321"]="%%!* For Utan!",
    ["DialogueBubble60322"]="%%!* We're not afraid!",
    ["DialogueBubble60323"]="If I jump... Then I can see the one I miss...?",
    ["DialogueBubble60324"]="*...# Protect!",
    ["DialogueBubble60325"]="*...# Protect!",
    ["DialogueBubble60326"]="*%&&...# Danger!",
    ["DialogueBubble60327"]="*%&&...# Leave!",
    ["DialogueBubble60328"]="What a unique piece of art.",
    ["DialogueBubble60329"]="Shh... Someone's coming!",
    ["DialogueBubble60330"]="Too expensive!",
    ["DialogueBubble60331"]="There are so many plants that I've never seen before.",
    ["DialogueBubble60332"]="Taste good?",
    ["DialogueBubble6034321"]="Military area, no trespassing!",
    ["DialogueBubble6034721"]="No entry without an order!",
    ["DialogueBubble6039221"]="Who allows you lot to be here!",
    ["DialogueBubble6039321"]="We demand to see Lord Carl!",
    ["DialogueBubble6039421"]="(Gun Pointed) Leave! Now!!!",
    ["DialogueBubble6040021"]="Who am I? Where did I come from? Where am I going?",
    ["DialogueBubble6040121"]="Mom, I want to go to Juno College!",
    ["DialogueBubble6040221"]="Finish your homework first...",
    ["DialogueBubble6040321"]="Vanessa, can we study together?",
    ["DialogueBubble6040421"]="Hmm...",
    ["DialogueBubble6040721"]="I heard that above the clouds, there's a floating island...",
    ["DialogueBubble6040821"]="I-I'm kinda dizzy...",
    ["DialogueBubble6041121"]="Juno is ahead. Please obey the border entry regulations!",
    ["DialogueBubble6041321"]="Hey buddy, this Butterfly Bow in pink fits you perfectly!",
    ["DialogueBubble6041421"]="Error! Error! Gender Setting Error!",
    ["DialogueBubble6042121"]="The thing in the folder... Is it only between us?",
    ["DialogueBubble6042221"]="As long as you keep your promise... I assure you.",
    ["DialogueBubble6042321"]="This is our headquarters?",
    ["DialogueBubble6042421"]="Wow!",
    ["DialogueBubble6042521"]="Seems familiar...",
    ["DialogueBubble6042621"]="There is something big... underground...",
    ["DialogueBubble6042721"]="Someone said the previous owner of this place had something to do with us...",
    ["DialogueBubble6042821"]="Let's pack it up and work on it in the afternoon!",
    ["DialogueBubble6042921"]="Yes Sir!",
    ["DialogueBubble610012101"]="Let my voice heal your wounds!",
    ["DialogueBubble610022101"]="The Kafra Corporation is here to serve your every need.",
    ["DialogueBubble610032101"]="The ship has reached the shore. You can disembark now!",
    ["DialogueBubble610042101"]="No matter what kind of headgear you like, I have the blueprints right here!",
    ["DialogueBubble610052101"]="As long as you have the materials, I can make any equipment you want!",
    ["DialogueBubble610053101"]="It seems as though there are more people carrying Familiar Cards during Halloween!",
    ["DialogueBubble610062101"]="In terms of letter delivery, parrots are much more professional than owls! Keh—!",
    ["DialogueBubble610063101"]="Why did that guy place so many Whispers here!? Could it be that you're jealous of my good looks? Do you really want to scare such a handsome messenger to death?!",
    ["DialogueBubble610072101"]="Oh! All these appraisals... I'm running out of eye drops...",
    ["DialogueBubble610082101"]="*Blop, blop, blop*",
    ["DialogueBubble610083101"]="Puff... Puff...",
    ["DialogueBubble610092101"]="My weapons are all of excellent quality!",
    ["DialogueBubble610093101"]="After a day's hammering, I can't wait to go to Red Rose to see if there are any special Halloween tunes there!",
    ["DialogueBubble610103101"]="During the Halloween period, please don't wear strange clothes when entering the Purchase Shop, otherwise, you may scare our customers!",
    ["DialogueBubble610113101"]="They say that the Kingdom ordered 857 pumpkin lanterns from the Chamber of Commerce in order to decorate Prontera this year!",
    ["DialogueBubble610122101"]="We recently got some new stock. Anything catch your eye?",
    ["DialogueBubble610132101"]="How boring would it be to have the same hairstyle every day?",
    ["DialogueBubble610133101"]="If you want to compete with Jakk, don't forget your red contact lenses!",
    ["DialogueBubble610152101"]="Legend has it that a certain shipwreck lies in the ocean depths...",
    ["DialogueBubble610152102"]="Over many years, it was dragged to the bottom of the sea by the Kraken...",
    ["DialogueBubble610152103"]="After that, only those who have been shipwrecked have seen it...",
    ["DialogueBubble610152201"]="Do you see that tower on the cliff?",
    ["DialogueBubble610152202"]="There's an interesting story about it...",
    ["DialogueBubble610152203"]="A beautiful princess with long hair once lived in the tower...",
    ["DialogueBubble610152204"]="This all happened a long, long time ago...",
