    ["Guild_kvmnote"]="Guild KVM Rules\n\nSeason Rules:\n1. Each season lasts for 7 days. The total points for the season will be tallied with reward distribution every 7 days.\n2. Season Points Tally: Sunday at 23:00.\n3. Season Points Reset: Monday at 05:00.\n4. Season Reward Distribution: Personal ranking rewards are sent by mail. Guild ranking rewards are sent to the Warehouse and distributed by the Guild Leader.\n\nGameplay Rules:\n1. Participation Level: Lv.40.\n2. Guild KVM Days: Tuesday, Thursday, and Sunday.\n3. Guild KVM Time: Usually from 20:30 to 22:00. Please refer to the notice for changes.\n4. Number of Guild KVM matches that follow the standard rules for calculating points: 3 matches.\n5. To participate in matchmaking, all members of the party must be from the same guild. Matchmaking cannot be carried out when a non-guild member is in the party.\n\nPoints Rules:\n1. In Guild KVM, different match results earn you various points.\n① For the first three matches, points will be calculated using the standard rules: For a 2:0 result, the winner gets 5 points, and the defeated one gets 1 point. For a 2:1 result, the winner gets 4 points, and the defeated one gets 2 points.\n② After 3 matches, points calculation will not follow the standard rules: Only 1 point will be added to the winner / deducted from the defeated one.\n\n2. MVP Points:\nBoth parties' performances will be tallied after each game of a match. Then MVP and SVP will be selected based on a comprehensive calculation of damage dealt, healing done, damage taken, kills, and resurrections.\nThe MVP will be the Adventurer who achieves the highest points in the winning party, and the SVP will be the Adventurer who achieves the highest points in the losing party.\n3. Final Points Rules:\nAdventurer's Final Points = Standard Points + MVP & SVP Points.\n\nForce Quit Punishment:\nA force quit before the KVM Results Phase will result in the following punishments:\n1. In addition to the standard penalty for losing, an additional 5 points will be deducted.\n2. After a force quit, you won't be able to rejoin the KVM matchmaking for the next 2 minutes.\n\nLeaving a Guild:\n1. Adventurers' individual points are bound to the guild. If an Adventurer leaves the guild, their individual points will be reset to zero. At the same time, the guild's total points are reduced by the departing member's points.\n2. The player will not be able to obtain the Individual Ranking Reward for that season if they leave their guild.\n3. The points that a new guild member obtained from their previous guild will not be transferred to the new one.\n",
    ["Guild_kvmnote_crossServer"]="\n\nCross-Server Guild KVM Rules\n\nSeason Rules:\n1. Each season lasts for 7 days. The total points for the season will be tallied with reward distribution every 7 days.\n2. Season Points Tally: Sunday at 23:00 (UTC+7).\n3. Season Points Reset: Monday at 05:00 (UTC+7).\n4. Season Reward Distribution: Personal ranking rewards are sent by mail. Guild ranking rewards are sent to the Warehouse and distributed by the Guild Leader.\n\nGameplay Rules:\n1. Participation Level: Lv.40.\n2. Cross-Server Guild KVM Days: Tuesday, Thursday, and Sunday.\n3. Cross-Server Guild KVM Time: Usually from 20:30 to 22:00 (UTC+7). Please refer to the notice for changes.\n4. Number of Cross-Server Guild KVM matches that follow the standard rules for calculating points: 3 matches.\n5. To participate in matchmaking, all members of the party must be from the same guild. Matchmaking cannot be carried out when a non-guild member is in the party.\n6. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unlike normal KVM, during the Cross-Server KVM, guilds from sub-servers within the same main server will be matched. Guild rankings will be based on guilds from all sub-servers in the main server. </color>\n\nPoints Rules:\n1. In Guild KVM, different match results earn you various points.\n① For the first three matches, points will be calculated using the standard rules: For a 2:0 result, the winner gets 5 points, and the defeated one gets 1 point. For a 2:1 result, the winner gets 4 points, and the defeated one gets 2 points.\n② After 3 matches, points calculation will not follow the standard rules: Only 1 point will be added to the winner / deducted from the defeated one.\n\n2. MVP Points:\nBoth parties' performances will be tallied after each game of a match. Then MVP and SVP will be selected based on a comprehensive calculation of damage dealt, healing done, damage taken, kills, and resurrections.\nThe MVP will be the Adventurer who achieves the highest points in the winning party, and the SVP will be the Adventurer who achieves the highest points in the losing party.\n3. Final Points Rules:\nAdventurer's Final Points = Standard Points + MVP & SVP Points.\n\nForce Quit Punishment:\nA force quit before the KVM Results Phase will result in the following punishments:\n1. In addition to the standard penalty for losing, an additional 5 points will be deducted.\n2. After a force quit, you won't be able to rejoin the KVM matchmaking for the next 2 minutes.\n\nLeaving a Guild:\n1. Adventurers' individual points are bound to the guild. If an Adventurer leaves the guild, their individual points will be reset to zero. At the same time, the guild's total points are reduced by the departing member's points.\n2. The player will not be able to obtain the Individual Ranking Reward for that season if they leave their guild.\n3. The points that a new guild member obtained from their previous guild will not be transferred to the new one.\n\n",
