    ["ItemDes_10405069"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Twilight. Use a Tome of Twilight to select one card from the following: Eclipse Series Card, Dragon Fly Series Card, Mastering Series Card, or Ghostring Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405070"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Glory. Use a Tome of Glory to select one card from the following: King Dramoh Series Card, Toad Series Card, Deviling Series Card, or Angeling Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405071"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Fate. Use a Tome of Fate to select one card from the following: Mistress Series Card, Phreeoni Series Card, Kraken Series Card, or Eddga Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405072"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Eternity. Use a Tome of Eternity to select one card from the following: Maya Series Card, Orc Hero Series Card, Pharaoh Series Card, or Orc Lord Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405073"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Origin. Use a Tome of Origin to select one card from the following: Golden Thief Bug Series Card, Drake Series Card, or Osiris Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405074"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Absolution. Use a Tome of Absolution to select one card from the following: Strouf Series Card, Moonlight Flower Series Card, or Dracula Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405075"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Sages. Use a Tome of Sages to select one card from the following: Doppelganger Series Card, Amon Ra Series Card, Dark Priest Series Card, Vagabond Wolf Series Card, or Dark Lord Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405076"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of the Ancient. Use a Tome of the Ancient to select one from the following cards: Time Holder Series Card, Morroc Series Card, Owl Duke Series Card, Chimera Series Card, or Mysteltainn Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405077"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Shade. Use a Tome of Shade to select one card from the following: Tao Gunka Series Card, Lost Dragon Series Card, Ogretooth Series Card, Necromancer Series Card, or Mutant Dragonoid Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405077_1"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Shade. Use a Tome of Shade to select one card from the following: Tao Gunka Series Card, Lost Dragon Series Card, Ogretooth Series Card, or Necromancer Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405078"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Undead. Use a Tome of Undead to select one card from the following: Lord of the Dead Series Card, Fallen Bishop Card, Naght Sieger Card, Coelacanth Series Card, or Beelzebub Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405079"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Ingenuity. Use a Tome of Ingenuity to select one card from the following: Gioia Series Card, Arc Angeling Series Card, Skeggiold Series Card, or Observation Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405080"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Ego. Use a Tome of Ego to select one card from the following: RSX-0806 Series Card, Nidhoggr's Shadow Series Card, Queen Scaraba Series Card, or Faceworm Queen Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405081"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem an Oracle Book. Use Oracle Book to choose one of the following cards: Gloom Under Night Series Card, Retribution Series Card, Ktullanux Series Card, or Shelter Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10405082"]="A valuable fragment. Collect 360 of them to redeem a Tome of Genes. Use a Tome of Genes to select one card from the following: Shadow Chaser Gertie Series Card, Genetic Flamel Series Card, Sorcerer Celia Series Card, or Ranger Cecil Series Card.",
    ["ItemDes_10406001"]="Cooking ingredient. A common type of fish that is easy to catch.",
    ["ItemDes_10406002"]="Cooking ingredient. An aggressive fish that has thin, small teeth.",
    ["ItemDes_10406003"]="Cooking ingredient. Fresh, delicious meat that is very suitable for cooking.",
    ["ItemDes_10406004"]="Cooking ingredient. An especially large prawn found commonly in freshwater environments.",
    ["ItemDes_10406005"]="Cooking ingredient. A snail that can be found in most places, lying lazily beneath the water's surface.",
    ["ItemDes_10406006"]="Cooking ingredient. A plant that grows underwater. It feels very wet.",
    ["ItemDes_10406007"]="Cooking ingredient. A small animal with agitated cheeks. It makes a croaking sound.",
    ["ItemDes_10406008"]="Cooking ingredient. A slippery Watersnake. If you don't firmly grasp it, it'll easily slip away from your hands.",
    ["ItemDes_10406009"]="A social fish of the sea that often swims in a group to scare off large predators. Can be used for cooking.",
    ["ItemDes_10406010"]="Cooking ingredient. Used in the cooking of high-grade fishes. Because of its high price, ordinary people can't often eat it.",
    ["ItemDes_10406011"]="Cooking ingredient. Why does it seem that animals with tentacles are unexpectedly delicious when cooked?",
    ["ItemDes_10406012"]="Cooking ingredient. They become round when in danger. Chefs have to be careful of their poisonous spines.",
    ["ItemDes_10406013"]="Cooking ingredient. It looks like a long, slender belt and swims quite elegantly in the water.",
    ["ItemDes_10406014"]="Cooking ingredient. Kelp that sways with the waves. It has high nutrition value.",
    ["ItemDes_10406015"]="Cooking ingredient. Algae that lives on the seabed. It has a salty, fishy taste.",
    ["ItemDes_10406017"]="An island-style shell. If you hold it up to your ear, you can hear the ocean.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Enriched Elunium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406018"]="This kind of scallop looks like a butterfly when it's opened, hence its name.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406019"]="A sharp shell that is often used by seabed dwellers to make decorations.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Carnium III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406020"]="A clam shell filled with mysterious power. Many mages favor them.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Bascyx III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406021"]="Its tail is like a slender whip with strong texture.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce STR Stone II and VIT Stone II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406022"]="Lives in hot areas all year round. Its heat-resistant body makes it hard to cook.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Bascyx II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406023"]="With a luminous ball on top of his head, it looks like a floating lamp in the water from a distance.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Enriched Oridecon.",
    ["ItemDes_10406024"]="Cooking ingredient. This large, colorful fish seems to be a favorite of Prontera's wealthy.",
    ["ItemDes_10406025"]="It's said that it was once a normal, unspectacular stone, but after a water aura coagulated around it, it turned into an extraordinary pearl. \nUsed as a smelting material to produce HD Bradium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406026"]="This glittering, translucent fish is actually a carnivorous creature, loving only rancid, rotten meat.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce HD Elunium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406027"]="Its scales are serrated and sharp.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce AGI Stone II and LUK Stone II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406028"]="People in deserts regard this fish as a gift from the God of Fire.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406029"]="A ferocious, carnivorous fish with sharp teeth that glow with a cold light. It feeds on insects and small fish.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce HD Oridecon.",
    ["ItemDes_10406030"]="Cooking ingredient. Emits a faint glow in the water at night.",
    ["ItemDes_10406031"]="Cooking ingredient. A giant prawn that likes crawling along the water bed.",
    ["ItemDes_10406032"]="A Vadon with an incredibly hard shell. It's very hard to handle without special processing.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Carnium II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406033"]="Bright bits of coral that makes one think of rainbows in the sky.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce INT Stone II and DEX Stone II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406034"]="A precious pearl that emits a fluorescent light in dark environments.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Enriched Bradium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406035"]="Who would have guessed from its ingredients and plain appearance that this is actually a beloved delicacy in Midgard?",
    ["ItemDes_10406036"]="Cooking ingredient. An edible plant that grows in lakes.",
    ["ItemDes_10406037"]="A common shell that can be found anywhere.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406038"]="A uniquely-colored stone.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Carnium I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406039"]="A small, smooth stone that's cool to the touch.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Bascyx I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406040"]="Cooking ingredient. A carnivorous fish whose meat is tender, with few bones and a rich taste.",
    ["ItemDes_10406041"]="Cooking ingredient. A delicious Vadon found commonly in freshwater environments.",
    ["ItemDes_10406042"]="A spiral-shaped shell.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce STR Stone I and VIT Stone I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406043"]="Groups of them often appear in mountain streams.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce AGI Stone I and LUK Stone I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406044"]="A valuable and extremely rare freshwater fish.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce INT Stone I and DEX Stone I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406045"]="Cooking ingredient. A common freshwater fish that has a lively personality and is good at jumping.",
    ["ItemDes_10406046"]="Cooking ingredient. A flexible fish with a pointed mouth and a slender body.",
    ["ItemDes_10406047"]="A small, cute, and dreamlike creature that feeds on rotten plants. It naturally gravitates toward the source of special odors.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Oridecon I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406048"]="Lurking in the bottom of rivers, they purify their digestive system by huffing and puffing hard sand and stones.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Elunium I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406049"]="Having a fiery-red color akin to maple leaves, it likes being near plants of colors similar to its own. Perhaps it's seeking a sense of security.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Bradium I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406050"]="Cooking ingredient. A fish that is used for food, medicinal, and ornamental purposes.",
    ["ItemDes_10406051"]="Cooking ingredient. Has a dusky-gray clam shell and is nothing special, but the meat inside is delicate and delicious.",
    ["ItemDes_10406052"]="Cooking ingredient. A fish that has adapted for two homes, the trout has a freshwater form and marine form.",
    ["ItemDes_10406053"]="Cooking ingredient. It has a long, thin body and a cylindrical shape with sticky skin.",
    ["ItemDes_10406054"]="It gets its name from the gradual yellowing of its scales.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Oridecon II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406055"]="Practically covered in a suit of armor, ordinary knives can't get at it.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Elunium II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406056"]="Its shell is covered in strange markings, giving it quite a mysterious look.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Blessed Bradium II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406057"]="Cooking ingredient. A green-backed fish found in frozen waters. It's very healthy.",
    ["ItemDes_10406058"]="Cooking ingredient. A fish that has terrifying teeth. Some hobbyists catch it to use for aesthetic purposes.",
    ["ItemDes_10406059"]="Cooking ingredient. A yellow mantis shrimp. As a food material, it is rare and difficult to handle.",
    ["ItemDes_10406060"]="Cooking ingredient. It can be found in all kinds of shallow and muddy waters, and its meat is very delicious.",
    ["ItemDes_10406061"]="It is named for its knife-like appearance and it violently attacks small living creatures.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon IV.",
    ["ItemDes_10406062"]="A ferocious fish with sharp teeth powerful enough to crush fishing hooks, though its body is weaker than one would expect.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Carnium IV.",
    ["ItemDes_10406063"]="An ancient fish with spines as sharp as crystal.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Bascyx IV.",
    ["ItemDes_10406064"]="Cooking ingredient. Delicious shellfish.",
    ["ItemDes_10406065"]="Cooking ingredient. A shrimp that lies in bodies of water close to shore.",
    ["ItemDes_10406066"]="Cooking ingredient. A frog that prefers to live in deep bodies of water.",
    ["ItemDes_10406067"]="A tortoise with unusually sharp teeth that can devour metal.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize STR Stone Ⅲ and VIT Stone Ⅲ.",
    ["ItemDes_10406068"]="A small squid with poor eyesight. Can only see brightly colored things.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize AGI Stone III and LUK Stone III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406069"]="Very sensitive to magic. Earned its name from its tendency to approach anything with magic power.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize INT Stone III and DEX Stone III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406101"]="A small, yellow piece of Great Earth imbued with the Earth attribute. Merchants can use it in production.",
    ["ItemDes_10406102"]="A small, red piece of Flame Heart imbued with the Fire attribute. Merchants can use it in production.",
    ["ItemDes_10406103"]="A small, green piece of Rough Wind imbued with the Wind attribute. Merchants can use it in production.",
    ["ItemDes_10406104"]="A small, blue piece of Mystic Frozen imbued with the Water attribute. Merchants can use it in production.",
    ["ItemDes_10406105"]="An ore with magical powers. When using magic, it can negate the magic's counteractive power for the caster.",
    ["ItemDes_10406106"]="An ore with magical powers. When using magic, it can negate the magic's counteractive power for the caster.",
    ["ItemDes_10406107"]="A Lv.1 Gold Ore that contains gold. Further processing is required to reveal its true value.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Gold I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406108"]="A Lv.1 Iron Ore that contains iron. Further processing is required to reveal its true value.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Iron I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406109"]="A Lv.1 Coal Ore that contains coal. Further processing is required to reveal its true value.\nIt is a great smelting medium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406110"]="A Lv.1 Silver Ore that contains silver. Further processing is required to reveal its true value.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Silver I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406111"]="A Lv.1 Impure Jewelstone that contains dark unknown substances.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce AGI Stone I, VIT Stone I, and DEX Stone I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406112"]="A Lv.1 Rough Bradium that seems to contain certain magical powers.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Bradium.",
    ["ItemDes_10406113"]="A Lv.2 Muspellium that is very strong and highly resistant to flames, but extremely difficult to process.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Morroc Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406114"]="A Lv.2 Upgrading Metal that feels cold to the touch.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon II, Carnium II, and Bascyx II.",
    ["ItemDes_10406115"]="A Lv.1 Pure Jewelstone that is as untainted as glass.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce STR Stone I, INT Stone I, and LUK Stone I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406116"]="A Lv.3 Muspellium that is very strong and highly resistant to flames, but extremely difficult to process.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Izlude or Alberta Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406117"]="A Lv.1 Muspellium that is very strong and highly resistant to flames, but extremely difficult to process.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Prontera Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406118"]="A Lv.1 Upgrading Metal that feels cold to the touch.\nUsed as an upgrading material to upgrade weapons from levels 1 through 20, armor from levels 1 through 10, and accessories from levels 1 through 5.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon I, Carnium I, and Bascyx I.",
    ["ItemDes_10406119"]="A Lv.3 Upgrading Metal that feels cold to the touch.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Phracon III, Carnium III, and Bascyx III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406120"]="A Lv.2 Gold Ore that contains gold. Further processing is required to reveal its true value.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Gold II.",
