    ["ItemDes_10406201"]="Cooking ingredient. An edible pumpkin with a robust flavor.",
    ["ItemDes_10406202"]="Cooking ingredient. A common type of grain, often consumed as a staple food.",
    ["ItemDes_10406203"]="Cooking ingredient. A type of plant that springs up after the rain.",
    ["ItemDes_10406206"]="A reed-like aquatic plant.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Munak Cave 1F.",
    ["ItemDes_10406207"]="A mysterious plant that sings songs of sorrow on full moon nights.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Munak Cave 1F.",
    ["ItemDes_10406208"]="A massive and powerful looking plant.",
    ["ItemDes_10406209"]="A sweet little flower that sways even in the absence of wind.",
    ["ItemDes_10406210"]="A tough vine often used to reinforce things.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Prontera Enchantment Stone.",
    ["ItemDes_10406212"]="Withered thorns that grow on arid lands.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Morroc Enchantment Stone.",
    ["ItemDes_10406213"]="Cooking ingredient. Sweet and juicy tomato, likely to have grown in a pleasant environment.",
    ["ItemDes_10406214"]="Cooking ingredient. A spiny, succulent plant with high water content.",
    ["ItemDes_10406216"]="A plant that's slightly bent over and looks like a tiny lantern.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Munak Cave 1F.",
    ["ItemDes_10406217"]="A specialty of the desert that symbolizes wealth and power.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Morroc Enchantment Stone.",
    ["ItemDes_10406218"]="A mushroom that thrives in hot climates and is warm to the touch.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Morroc Enchantment Stone.",
    ["ItemDes_10406219"]="A curled up leaf that looks as if it's very shy. Commonly used for smelting and crafting.",
    ["ItemDes_10406220"]="A flower that radiates a spiritual aura. It's a material of high quality.",
    ["ItemDes_10406221"]="Cooking ingredient. A flower commonly seen in Payon, it has a refreshing scent.",
    ["ItemDes_10406222"]="Cooking ingredient. A type of leaf with the scent of tea. People in Payon love to use it to flavor water.",
    ["ItemDes_10406223"]="Leaves enfolded around a flower bud.",
    ["ItemDes_10406224"]="Cooking ingredient. A plant with unique scent, can help to keep one alert.",
    ["ItemDes_10406225"]="It generates a strange magical power in the moonlight.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Geffen Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406226"]="A little white flower that grants one inner peace just by looking at it.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Payon Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406228"]="A deep blue mushroom that glows in the dark. Commonly used for smelting and crafting.",
    ["ItemDes_10406229"]="It appears gloomy, often found in dark and damp caves. \nUsed as a smelting material to produce Payon Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406231"]="A tiny mushroom with a crystal-like cap.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Prontera Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406232"]="Looks ordinary on the surface, but it contains a mysterious power.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Prontera Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406233"]="Flower seedling in a darker shade. It has no fragrance but smells like the soil after rain passes. \nUsed as a smelting material to produce Payon Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406234"]="A pure and clean looking flower, it makes people think of priests who pray silently in chapels.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Geffen Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406235"]="A beautiful cyan rose that looks like a small crystal from afar.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Geffen Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406236"]="A purple herb with unique scent and energizing properties.\nUsed as a crafting material to produce Purple Medicine Kits and PVP Purple Medicine Kits.",
    ["ItemDes_10406237"]="Cooking ingredient. A small fruit that tastes both sweet and sour.",
    ["ItemDes_10406238"]="Cooking ingredient. A bright red fruit with a pungent smell that makes people teary-eyed.",
    ["ItemDes_10406239"]="Cooking ingredient. A floating aquatic plant that is ideal for cooking.",
    ["ItemDes_10406240"]="Cooking ingredient. A type of flower that only blooms in the depths of a forest. Because it only blooms in certain seasons of the year, it is hard to chance upon this flower.",
    ["ItemDes_10406241"]="Cooking ingredient. A type of plant that grows in deserts and is resilient to drought and sandstorm.",
    ["ItemDes_10406242"]="Cooking ingredient. Biting its scarlet leaves gives one a fiery sensation.",
    ["ItemDes_10406243"]="A seemingly inconspicuous plant. When it lacks nutrients, its roots will self-decompose so as to survive. It gives off a pungent smell that is pretty unbearable.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Labyrinth Forest.",
    ["ItemDes_10406244"]="A type of mushroom that is hard to the touch and can grow inside rock cracks.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Labyrinth Forest.",
    ["ItemDes_10406245"]="A type of grass that grows on the side of the road. It is often used as a reference point for finding the way due to its vibrant colors.\nFishing bait. Used for fishing in Labyrinth Forest.",
    ["ItemDes_10406246"]="Grows in humid environment. When the tides are approaching, it will face towards the sea.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Izude or Alberta Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406247"]="A type of plant that grows on saline soils, its color is blue like the sea.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Izude or Alberta Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406248"]="Its leaves give off a faint glow at night.\nUsed as a smelting material to produce Izude or Alberta Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406249"]="It grows in dark, humid caves. It is rumored to bind the soul of the deceased to it.",
    ["ItemDes_10406250"]="It has fine hair on its leaves and gives off a faint glow in dark places.",
    ["ItemDes_10406251"]="Regardless of its surrounding temperature, the dew on its leaves will turn into frost, enveloping them completely.",
    ["ItemDes_10406252"]="Cooking ingredient. It gives off a special, sweet scent. It can be commonly found in caves.",
    ["ItemDes_10406253"]="Cooking ingredient. A sour, citrus fruit that can quench one's thirst.",
    ["ItemDes_10406254"]="Cooking ingredient. A type of herb with an overpowering smell that will give you an intense, but enjoyable, head rush.",
    ["ItemDes_10406255"]="Cooking ingredient. A dark olive with a salty bitter taste.",
    ["ItemDes_10406256"]="Cooking ingredient. A red rose that can be used for both flavoring and decoration.",
    ["ItemDes_10406257"]="Cooking ingredient. Filled with the taste of nostalgia. Has a faint aroma.",
    ["ItemDes_10406258"]="A rust-colored mushroom that earned its name from its appearance.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Blessed Oridecon ⅡI.",
    ["ItemDes_10406259"]="A vine with a warm fragrance. Has small flowers growing on it.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Blessed Elunium III.",
    ["ItemDes_10406260"]="An unremarkable small flower. Can be found growing on every street corner.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Blessed Bradium ⅡI.",
    ["ItemDes_10406261"]="Wandering ghosts will sometimes attach themselves to surrounding plants.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Glast Heim Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406262"]="A flower that feels sacred but can grow in harsh conditions.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Glast Heim Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406263"]="The petals feel hard and cold, like icy metal.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Glast Heim Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406264"]="Cooking ingredient. A very sweet berry with very little moisture.",
    ["ItemDes_10406265"]="Cooking ingredient. Refreshingly sweet snow-white fruit.",
    ["ItemDes_10406266"]="Cooking ingredient. Spicy-tasting herb.",
    ["ItemDes_10406267"]="A low-profile but luxurious dark-colored flower.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Aldebaran Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406268"]="A mushroom with special magical properties that grows in a place eroded by time.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Aldebaran Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406269"]="A canopy-like vine that glows faintly in the dark.\nSmelting material. Used to synthesize Aldebaran Enchantment Stones.",
    ["ItemDes_10406301"]="The favorite food of Lunatic.",
    ["ItemDes_10406401"]="Equipment upgrading material. Grade I iron. Despite being a strong metal, it remains lightweight and is easy to temper compared to other metals.",
    ["ItemDes_10406402"]="Equipment upgrading material. Grade I gold. A hard and stable metal that shines as bright as the sun.",
    ["ItemDes_10406403"]="One of the hardest metals found in the Ash Vacuum, it is difficult to temper because of its high density.\nUsed as a material to refine accessories from levels 1 through 4.",
