    ["JobBranch_radarImageLabel6"]="Support",
    ["JobBranch_tips1"]="You can view skill details on the skill panel on the right, and customize your setup before trying out a class.",
    ["JobIntroduce"]="Class Description",
    ["JobItemTips1"]="Unable to equip because you do not have this item!",
    ["JobLevelTips"]="<color=#97BCF8FF>Job Level: </color>\n\n1. Job EXP can be obtained by <color=#CCFF66>killing monsters, completing Mission Board Quests, COC Missions, instances, OX Quiz</color> and other events.\n2. Upgrade Job levels to obtain <color=#CCFF66>skill points</color>, which can then be used to increase skill levels.\n3. When the Job level is <color=#CCFF66>maxed out</color>, you won't earn Job EXP anymore, but you can advance to a higher-tier class. Upon completing the class advancement, your Job level will reset to <color=#CCFF66>zero</color>.\n4. The requirements for each class advancement:\nFirst Class: Novice Job <color=#CCFF66>Lv.10</color>\nSecond Class: First Class Job <color=#CCFF66>Lv.50</color>\nTranscendent Second Class: Second Class Job <color=#CCFF66>Lv.50</color>\nThird Class: Transcendent Second Class Job <color=#CCFF66>Lv.70</color>\nFourth Class: Third Class Job <color=#CCFF66>Lv.60</color>\n5. Classes without access to the fourth class will have their Job level calculated as <color=#CCFF66>Fourth Class Job Level</color> after obtaining the <color=#CCFF66>Divine Skill</color>. So when they advance to the fourth class later, there will be no loss of Job EXP.",
    ["JobLvID"]="Job Lv.%s",
