    ["LeaseShopUnlocktips"]="Item unlocked successfully.",
    ["LeaseShop_001"]="Requires Tier 3 Kafra Employee Favor.",
    ["LeaseShop_UIInfo_001"]="Requires <color=#d14d75>%s</color>.",
    ["LeaseShop_UIInfo_002"]="<color=#d14d75>Lv.[%s]</color> required to rent.",
    ["LeaseShop_UIInfo_003"]="You have already received %s...",
    ["LeaseShop_UIInfo_004"]="Failed to rent %s!",
    ["LeaseShop_UIInfo_005"]="Successfully obtained %s!",
    ["LeaveConfirmation"]="Would you like to exit the Wardrobe?",
    ["LeaveFromTeam"]="You have already left the party.",
    ["LeaveTips1"]="This quest requires you to leave the current area to continue. Are you sure you want to leave?",
    ["LetterText1040011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> A thousand years ago, I sealed a Deviling in this forest, but soon realized I had trapped myself, too. The four sealstones are the crystallized essence of my power, and by activating them with the help of your friends, you reawakened my full strength. You also released the Deviling, but fortunately, that's all been taken care of now. I am free once more, thanks to you, but it's not really fitting for a witch to convey such gratitude face-to-face now, is it? So, I've gone on my way, but have included some small gifts in this letter to you. Please accept them! \n<color=#FFFFFF00>123456789123451234</color> Evelyn",
    ["LetterText1170011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> In the ancient era of the gods, the Frost Giant Ymir was slain by the god Odin, and his body formed the world we live on. Spawned from a void (the time rift, Ginnungagap), the world became separated into three levels. <color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> The gods, ruled by Odin, live in the highest level, known as Asgard, where Odin resides in the golden palace of Valhalla. Mortals, led by human beings, live in the middle level of Midgard, which is surrounded by a vast ocean and connects to the kingdom of the gods through the rainbow bridge, Bifrost.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> The third and lowest level, called Niflheim, lies deep beneath Midgard, and is the land of the dead and eternal night. <color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> There also exist many gaps in time and space between these three worlds. They do not possess the energy to create vast continents as Ginnungagap once did, but they have spawned countless dangerous realms, filled with powerful",
    ["LetterText1170012"]="monsters. The elemental laws in these realms are also very different from those of Midgard. After Ymir's death, the only part of his body that was not transformed into part of the new world was his heart. Ymir's Heart held the power of the nine elements: Water, Earth, Fire, Wind, Poison, Holy, Shadow, Ghost, and Undead, and these nine elements possessed the power to create and destroy the world. The power it emitted could even split space. Odin realized that Ymir's Heart contained boundless energy, and he buried it under the budding world tree, Yggdrasil, which supported Asgard",
    ["LetterText1170013"]="and Valhalla. Ymir's Heart eventually became the world tree's source of power, and over time, Ymir's Heart became entangled in the roots of Yggdrasil. <color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> Baphomet, the first demon born from the hidden realms, was drawn to the power of Ymir's Heart, and tore his way through time and space to reach it. A long war between the gods and demons ensued, bringing great calamity to the world. Although Odin finally succeeded in repelling Baphomet's forces back to their world, the remaining demons swarmed into Midgard and ravaged the continent, committing all manner of atrocities. It was in response to this that the very first adventurers emerged in Midgard, and these heroes have written countless legendary chapters in human history ever since. Many gifted young people have awakened their inner strength by battling the demons, and their varied talents have opened up new paths to becoming stronger.",
    ["LetterText1170014"]="This drive and relentless innovation formed the roots of what we now call the Job System. \n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> Before being sealed in the dimensional gap, Baphomet used the last of his strength to shatter Ymir's Heart held in the roots of the world tree, simultaneously destroying the source of Yggdrasil's power. The Age of Gods came to an end as Yggdrasil withered. Now, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragments of Ymir's Heart lie scattered across Midgard</color>.",
    ["LetterText1200102"]="\nA.W. 1000 XX/1 \n\n...<color=#CA2E0AFF>The exorcism</color> failed, and the prince departed to the afterlife.\nI lost His Majesty's trust, and he ordered me to be banished.\nBut the prince's death wasn't my fault! Something is not right here...",
    ["LetterText1200103"]="\n\nA.W. 1000 XX/2\n\n...I have found the poem of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Legend of the Kingdom's Founding</color>,\nbut the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second half of the poem has been torn to shreds</color>.\nThis proves my theory that the prince's death must be a conspiracy! I must uncover the truth...",
    ["LetterText1200104"]="\nA.W. 1000 XX/3\n\n...It turns out that the administrator of the Prontera Library was a historian,\nI believe that he must have read the poem. Maybe he knows the <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret</color> behind the Legend of the Kingdom's Founding?",
    ["LetterText1200202"]="\n\n\n\nA giant serpent swallowing the sea...\n\nA giant serpent swallowing the sea...\n\nA rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead...\n\nAnd made a nest upon the sea...",
    ["LetterText1200302"]="Dear Lugenburg Family:\nBy the time you receive this letter, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Agnes</color> will already be in my hands.\nIf you wish to see her again, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> as soon as possible and retrieve <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maya's Crown</color>. Once you have it, <color=#CA2E0AFF>place it beneath the sand dunes of Hope Oasis</color>.\nI believe that with your capabilities, in particular those of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Halmod</color>, this should be an easy task to accomplish.\nI, along with Agnes, will be waiting for your response!",
    ["LetterText1200402"]="<size=14>Dear Lugenburg Family,\nparticularly Lord Halmod, who I assume is reading this letter:\nThe reason I am sending this letter is because I know you can't afford a sum as vast as 50 million Zeny.\nBut don't worry, I've come up with a solution for you—\nThey say that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wulf</color> of the Lugenburg Family is a talented businessman. You, Lord Halmod, should seek help from Wulf, the only member of your family who possesses significant financial resources.\nAs long as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Halmod is willing to bow his head and admit his mistakes</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cancel the monthly tournament as an apology</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>while admitting that force cannot solve everything</color>... Wulf will surely agree to put the past behind him and lend you enough Zeny!</size>",
    ["LetterText1200502"]="A.W. 1000 XX/5 18:30 \nWeather: Foggy\n...Ten hours after leaving Alberta, a strange <color=#CA2E0AFF>mist</color> suddenly appeared on the open sea. I suggested to the captain to change course, but he insisted on <color=#CA2E0AFF>passing through the mist</color> to deliver our goods to the port on the other side of the sea as soon as possible. We had no choice but to trust the captain's judgment and hope that all would be well...",
    ["LetterText1200602"]="A.W. 1000 XX/5 19:45 \nWeather: Foggy\n...After entering the fog, we soon realized that we were completely lost. The sea seemed calm and windless, but the stench of damp, rotten flesh intermittently drifted across our nostrils. In order to keep spirits high, I encouraged the sailors to take heart, follow my commands, lower the sails, and adjust the rudder. But as I stood on the observation deck to give my orders, I noticed the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shadow of a huge ship</color> approaching us at full speed...\n\"Pirates! Pirates incoming!\" I blew the warning horn and yelled, but suddenly realized that the deck was empty and all of the sailors were gone... As I searched for them, I noticed <color=#CA2E0AFF>a strange crack</color> in the cabin and saw something that I will never forget—A giant <color=#CA2E0AFF>tentacle</color> protruding from the hole, dragging the captain into a dark void! Have all of the sailors met the same fate? There is no time to waste—I must find a way to save them...",
    ["LetterText1200603"]="\n\"Pirates! Pirates incoming!\" I blew the warning horn and yelled, but suddenly realized that the deck was empty and all of the sailors were gone... As I searched for them, I noticed <color=#CA2E0AFF>a strange crack</color> in the cabin and saw something that I will never forget—a giant <color=#CA2E0AFF>tentacle</color> protruding from the hole, dragging the captain into a dark void! Have all of the sailors met the same fate? There is no time to waste—I must find a way to save them...",
    ["LetterText1200702"]="A.W. 1000 XX/5 23:55 \nWeather: Unknown\n...After investigating it more closely, the strange crack seems to be a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>, but no matter how many times I travel through it, I can't seem to find the dimension my companions were taken to. I sat on the deck, tired and frustrated, and finally realized that this merchant ship had become a dimensional vessel. Time no longer exists here. All that remains is eternity...\nThere is no way for me to escape from this stretch of sea. I cannot return to my friends and family... I don't even know if I'm still alive...\nIf life does have an end, where does my end lie?\nIf only I had done more to convince the captain not to sail into that mist, perhaps things would have been different...",
    ["LetterText1200802"]="(Spell of Metis: A spell that <color=#CA2E0AFF>reverses an elixir's effect</color>. Due to the similarity in their incantations, it is often confused with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spell of Menos</color>, which <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispels elixir effects</color>.)",
    ["LetterText1200902"]="\nA.W. 1000 X/16\n\n...Today, I once again managed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escape them</color>. Ever since I touched <color=#CA2E0AFF>that thing</color>, I have known that its significance is far beyond an ordinary person's comprehension! Knowing this, why do I not give up on this lowly and ridiculous <color=#CA2E0AFF>mission</color>? Why do I refuse to resort to hiding in the darkness of the underground? All I do, is for my <color=#CA2E0AFF>great research</color>...",
    ["LetterText1200903"]="\nA.W. 1000 X/28\n\n...They are really becoming increasingly irascible, but fortunately, I unexpectedly heard some interesting information! What have they been saying? That I'm probably in collusion with that madman <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch</color>. Can it be that there are still other like-minded people here on the continent?",
    ["LetterText1200904"]="\nA.W. 1000 X/9\n\n...I knew that Geffen's magic barrier was no simple creation, but I didn't expect that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merlin Heines</color> could have made it into an instrument to use for his own devices! He must know how to <color=#CA2E0AFF>control and power that force</color>. I must get that <color=#CA2E0AFF>manuscript</color>, no matter the cost!",
    ["LetterText1201001"]="Urgent Letter",
    ["LetterText1201002"]="Recently, a highly-dangerous <color=#CA2E0AFF>test subject</color> has escaped. Specific details are as follows:\nSubject Name: K-406\nDescription: K-406 has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>human form</color> that is usually invisible and can only be made visible with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>special flash bomb (included with letter)</color>. According to observations, K-406 will randomly <color=#CA2E0AFF>possess a nearby human</color>. Those possessed usually <color=#CA2E0AFF>behave abnormally</color>. Most attempt self-harm until they end their lives. There is reason to believe that K-406 has the ability to <color=#CA2E0AFF>control human minds</color> and that he enjoys the process of invading the host's mind and inducing suicide. People with strong willpower may be able to resist the test subject's invasion, but this theory has not yet been confirmed due to very few surviving cases.",
    ["LetterText1201003"]="Detainment Measures: The only known method of detaining K-406 is to seal it inside a <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerful magic ward</color>, such as Doctor ██'s lab tank, which has a successful record of containment. \nThere is sufficient evidence to indicate that K-406 is no longer within the country. All relevant personnel who have received this letter are requested to immediately <color=#CA2E0AFF>track down his whereabouts</color> and attempt to apprehend him.\n\n\n\n████Institute",
    ["LetterText1201201"]="Price List\nSea Buckthorn 100,000 Zeny\nDivine Red Deer Grass 500,000 Zeny\nLicorice 1,000,000 Zeny\nScarlet Flower 5,000,000 Zeny",
    ["LetterText1201301"]="The whirling <color=#CA2E0AFF>starlight</color> dances in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>spiral</color>.\nThe <color=#CA2E0AFF>tears of tyrants</color> fall in the wind,\nand the <color=#CA2E0AFF>foliage that guides you home</color> sways in the sunset.\nWhen all are reunited, the departed soul shall soon return.",
    ["LetterText1201401"]="The Revelation of Starlight is a potion formula left behind by an ancient god, said to possess the ability to guide a departed soul back to the world of the living.\nOnly a powerful mage can use it. The ingredients differ depending on who left the riddle. Only by <color=#CA2E0AFF>infusing of a sense of longing</color> and, <color=#CA2E0AFF>using a Sasquatch Bone as a vessel</color>, putting <color=#CA2E0AFF>all ingredients</color> indicated inside and <color=#CA2E0AFF>extracting them at a high temperature</color> can one obtain <color=#CA2E0AFF>Revenant Water</color>, which can summon back a soul.",
    ["LetterText1201501"]="A.W.228\nThe Sage Academy's work will be forced to cease tomorrow. King Schmidt's policy of valuing military over culture is finally going to be used to deal with the officials of the entire Sage Academy. When that time comes, more people will become victims, and I'm no exception...",
    ["LetterText1201502"]="A.W.228\nI never would have imagined that King Schmidt would send everyone in the Sage Academy to oversee work in the sewers, performing hard labor and never seeing the light of day. In the eyes of King Schmidt, are civil servants like us really worthless?",
    ["LetterText1201503"]="A.W.228\nTomorrow, I must leave to work in the sewers. Although I can imagine this job will be difficult, at least I can earn a living. Maybe this can improve Rey's life. Regardless, I hope this job won't be too busy so that I can spend more time with Rey...",
    ["LetterText1201601"]="        The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chimera</color>, wild and vicious by nature, has the head of a lion and body of a goat. Behind its head is a hideous multi-headed snake monster. Once the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pet of King Schmidt</color>, it became unsatisfied with being controlled and fled to town when it found its chance to escape. There it went on a rampage, devouring humans and livestock, spewing fire and destroying people's homes. The untamable beast brought violence and devastation wherever he went. Ultimately, it was King Schmidt's Chivalry Commander <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heinrich</color> who finally killed it by throwing a spear coated with graphite into its fire-breathing mouth.",
    ["LetterText1201701"]="I didn't expect the tower to harbor so many monsters. I don't know if it’s because of them, but I kept feeling like the concept of time was chaotic and different somehow from the outside world. Sometimes, it felt like a few seconds passed, while other times it felt like years. I even saw images of my past memories.",
    ["LetterText1201801"]="At one point, I saw a suspicious man suddenly appear with a little girl. I wanted to follow them, but after turning the corner they were engulfed in a beam of light. As I went up to take a closer look, I heard the man's voice not far behind me. I went over to see that he was seriously injured, but to my surprise the little girl accompanying him didn’t seem human...",
    ["LetterText1201901"]="The underlying pipes do more than simply drain rainwater. I witnessed monsters gushing out of them and even spied people in lab coats going in and out on one occasion, who I suspect are connected to other facilities.",
    ["LetterText1202001"]="It looks like we found its whereabouts. Our transceivers were lost while in pursuit the past few days. Do you remember the secret exit that was tunneled in the northeast section of Building 1? If you make a run for it, you should be able to get out. The document must be brought out safely – there’s no turning back.",
    ["LetterText1202101"]="The identification certificate of a member of the Republican Guard. It has the guard’s serial number and name written on it.",
    ["LetterText1202202"]="A note by an unknown author. It indicates that the next camp location of the Church mission is in the northeast of the Sograt Desert.",
    ["LetterText1202302"]="A note by an unknown author. It indicates that the next camp location of the Church mission is in the southwest of the Sograt Desert. The note is very long-winded, seeming to have been hastily written down.",
    ["LetterText1202402"]="A note by an unknown author. The person who wrote the note indicates that he knows the purpose of your travels, but what you are looking for is not here. He says he can provide further clues and wants to meet you under the golden coconut tree on the western side of the desert.",
    ["LetterText1510011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> Legend has it, that deep beneath Prontera, in a vault beside the second floor of the sewers, lies the countless treasures of the Kingdom of Louen. However, this vault is home to a Mutant Thief Bug fused with the essence of gold, a terrible monster known as the Golden Thief Bug. If you wish to defeat this fearsome monster, you will need <color=#CA2E0AFF>the power of Odin's divine blessings</color>.",
    ["LetterText1510012"]="Defeating the Golden Thief Bug requires being blessed with the power of Odin. Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test Test",
    ["LetterText1510021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> One of the known Fragments of Ymir's Heart is believed to be in the hands of the Gaebolg Family in Rune-Midgarts.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> Legend has it that Tristan Gaebolg I was able to defeat the evil serpent Jormungand and rule this land with the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. We have reason to believe that the fragment contains power comparable to that of a god...\"",
    ["LetterText1560011"]="History of Midgard Before A.W.0\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> ...According to reliable records, Geffen was established on the site of an ancient ruin known as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffenia</color>, which emitted a magical magnetic field. Its great power attracted many mages to make pilgrimages here for training. During this period, the great archmage Merlin Heine sensed an unusual force hidden underground. After much investigation, he finally found the source of Geffenia's powerful magnetic field—a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> containing <color=#CA2E0AFF>dark elemental power</color>.\n",
    ["LetterText1560012"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> In order to reduce the negative effects of the fragment, Merlin prepared to make this discovery public, but it was too late. The fragment's dark element had already evoked the mages' inner greed, causing more and more of them to fight for the exclusive possession of this holy land of cultivation. The constant fighting between the mages caused fluctuations of magic elements and triggered the connection between the dark elemental power contained in the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and the dark power from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Niflheim</color>, the world of the dead. The bond tore open <color=#CA2E0AFF>rifts between dimensions</color> and allowed countless undead to come pouring in from below the earth.",
    ["LetterText1560013"]="To stop the spread of this scourge, Merlin Heines' disciples gathered together to form a legion of high wizards, which later became known as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pentagram</color>. They fought a sustained war against the invading undead. Finally, after the sacrifices of countless heroes, they sealed the forces of The Darkness underground in the ruins of Geffenia.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color> After the great war, the Pentagram constructed the Geffen Tower atop the ruins to suppress the magical wards that seal the undead. To ensure that the power of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart would not get out of control again or fall in the hands of someone wanting to exploit it, Merlin Heines created the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Artifact</color>...",
    ["LetterText1640011"]="There may be overgrown thorns and overcast skies,\nbut my heart remains and the light within will never fade.\nI fight for the honor and faith of a knight.\nEven if the road ahead is abyssal and filled with darkness...\nI swear by the spirit of a knight,\nto keep the light and strength in my heart ablaze.\nFor the return of honor and faith,\nI will be indomitable.\n(You look down at the book, which records the beliefs and principles of the Chivalry since its founding.)",
    ["LetterText202202"]="...Tonight is the first quarter moon. \nIt won't be long until we pack up and depart for the next camp in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of the desert</color>...",
    ["LetterText202302"]="...Reader of this letter, go quickly to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest of Sograt Desert</color> to find the Church mission's <color=#CA2E0AFF>temporary camp</color>.\n(The note is messily scribbled and smudged. It was clearly written in a panic.)",
    ["LetterText202402"]="....The <color=#CA2E0AFF>crown</color> is not here. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Whoever seeks the crown</color>, go to the golden coconut tree on the western side of the desert, and I will be waiting for you.",
    ["LetterText202502"]="A.W.1000 February 4\n... Today I caught another person who came to pick moondew. Humans are so strange – willing to abandon everything for such ethereal feelings... But why do I feel a little envious? If I were to stop using spells and treat others with kindness... would someone be willing to give me their affection?\n\nA.W.1000 May 18\nI haven't eaten in many days. Although my body is a little weak, I am in good spirits. Today, I saved a nearby human who was attacked by a monster. He seemed afraid of my appearance and trembled as he thanked me... Am I really that hideous? I remember my peers used to praise me for my good looks... Perhaps tomorrow I’ll start trying to dress up like a human? Maybe then the next time we meet... he won’t be so scared.",
    ["LetterText202503"]="A.W.1000 September 6\nI... I finally saw him again. He brought flowers and a strange little box with a silver metal ring inside, and put the ring on my hand... What does it mean? I don’t quite understand, but he beamed with such a sweet smile... If one day I can leave this dim underground world and live with him in the bright sunshine, how lovely would that be...",
    ["LetterText202504"]="A.W.1000 September 6\nI... I finally saw him again. He brought flowers and a strange little box with a silver metal ring inside, and put the ring on my hand... What does it mean? I don’t quite understand, but he beamed with such a sweet smile... If one day I can leave this dim underground world and live with him in the bright sunshine, how lovely would that be...",
    ["LetterText202602"]="Private Kingdom Pass\nThis pass is granted to the Kingdom's ally, the Church of Arunabez. Whoever holds it may enter and leave any town in the Kingdom freely without inspection. May the friendship between the two great kingdoms endure for time eternal.\n                                                                                                                                   --Signature of the Seven Royal Families\n                                                              (The corner of the pass displays a golden fire lacquer seal, which appears to be the Walter family crest)",
    ["LetterText202702"]="The items are ready. Pick them up three days from now at the usual place in the city’s southwest quarter.\n                                                     ——Dr.",
    ["LetterText202802"]="Spellbound\nTechnique: Transformation - Forbidden\nAcquisition Difficulty: S\nDanger Level: S++\nSpellbound originates from a very ancient alchemy. Legend has it that the technique was born out of a primitive sacrificial ritual that served to remove the soul of the sacrifice from its body as an offering to the gods. The process of the ritual is very complex, requiring three alchemy arrays to be carved into the back of the neck of the sacrifice, and the preparation of sacred vessels to be left for the gods. In the process of performing the ritual, the priest places a pure black stone into the mouth of the sacrifice to be used as a vessel for storing the soul, which is then removed after the ritual is over. They believe that if the stone’s color changes, it means the soul has been sealed inside, and if it does not change, the ritual is considered a failure and the sacrifice must be rechosen. However, according to scholars, this change is simply a pigment reaction when the alchemical stone comes into contact with a powerful divine force, and the so-called sacred vessel may very well be the legendary Fragment of Ymir's Heart.\nBecause the spell inflicts great pain on the person it is cast on, in order to prevent the separated soul from being aggrieved, the sacrifice is completed after the ritual. The Water of Corruption is placed in the corpse’s mouth in order to dissolve the remains of its soul, visibly vaporizing it...\n\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Warning: The actual use of this technique is strictly prohibited. This entry is for record keeping only.</color>",
    ["LetterText202803"]="However, according to scholars, this change is simply a pigment reaction when the alchemical stone comes into contact with a powerful divine force, and the so-called sacred vessel may very well be the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>.\nBecause the spell inflicts great pain on the person it is cast on, in order to prevent the separated soul from being aggrieved, the sacrifice is completed after the ritual. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water of Corruption</color> is placed in the corpse’s mouth in order to dissolve the remains of its soul, visibly <color=#CA2E0AFF>vaporizing</color> it...\n\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Warning: The actual use of this technique is strictly prohibited. This entry is for record keeping only.</color>",
    ["LetterText202902"]="A.W.1000 May 30\nHe's gone. How can I come to terms with this? Perhaps there’s one way I can bring him back in another sense...",
    ["LetterText203002"]="A.W. 1000 May 21\nIt seems that the Father of Mechanics’ theory is more complicated than I imagined. Today is my 69th failure. I still need to perform more research...",
    ["LetterText203102"]="“A Study of the Unity of the Soul and the Mechanical Body”\n... If we are to pursue the perfect life form, I assert that it must be of a sound mind, and possess a body that never ages and can repair and iterate itself, both of which are indispensable traits. But the mystery of the human soul is truly beyond my reach. I have tried several times to combine a mindless body with a conscious object, however the only condition that can keep the two together is if it is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>beloved object</color> of the deceased, or an object that <color=#CA2E0AFF>brings together their thoughts with their loved ones</color>...",
    ["LetterText203202"]="A.W.1000 June 3\nI was so happy when my brother finally “resurrected”. At first everything was perfectly normal, but why is his soul becoming more and more unstable and manic? Even stranger, he often disappears for no apparent reason, and when he returns his soul is calm again...",
    ["LetterText203302"]="(The instability of merged souls is generally due to the torture and grievance caused by the distortion of their soul before death. Unless we can rewrite history and spare the soul of the deceased, the only way to maintain a stable state is to allow the soul to continuously devour other fresh souls.)",
    ["LetterText203303"]="To change this, the only way to heal the suffering of the deceased is through the principle of time travel. Otherwise....\n(At the end of the page, the words <color=#CA2E0AFF>time travel</color> are angrily crossed out. The pen’s strokes have ripped through the page, as if in an eruption of fury. Based on the penmanship, it wasn’t done by Lancaster. Could it have been the reader?)",
    ["LetterText203402"]="Dear Brother,\nCongratulations on your acceptance into the Alchemists’ Guild. Since the death of our parents, the two of us have had to depend on each other to survive. You sacrificed many opportunities to study in order to take care of me, for which I have always felt guilty... But this time, you finally accomplished your dream. For this, I am truly overjoyed for you. Although you will be even busier in the future, and may not have any time for me, please don't worry. I am old enough to take care of myself now.\nP.S. I still have the owl doll you gave to keep me company! I’ll never be alone! :-)\n                                                                                                                        Aaron",
    ["LetterText203502"]="Dear Aaron,\nI have brought back your new prescription. This time the doctor changed the order, so please remember to <color=#CA2E0AFF>first take the red pill, then the blue one, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>finally</color> the clear one</color>.\nAlso, it’s been more than three months since I took up my position at the Steel Capital Institute. Have you been taking care of yourself? I think the irises at home must be flowering by now. If they are already in bloom, can you take a picture for me? I will be on duty at the Alchemists’ Guild headquarters until tomorrow. I hope you can come by the lab to pay a visit.\n                                                                                                                                                  Brother Liu",
    ["LetterText203702"]="There is heat relief medicine and mannitol in the medicine chest which you may take as needed. If you need an on-site diagnosis, please go to the Golem Habitat in the northwest of the desert to find a doctor.\n\"A great healer is either in search of medicine or on their way to find it.\" —— Famous quote",
    ["LetterText203802"]="By the will of the gods, drawing from the power of giants, and on the principle of equality, may we give relief to mortals.\n\n\n                                                                                                      ——God's Messenger\n\n(Upon looking carefully, the following symbol is visible in the lower right corner of the poster: Ψ)\n",
    ["LetterText203902"]="By the will of the gods, drawing from the power of giants, and on the principle of equality, may we give relief to mortals.\n\n\n                                                                                                      ——God's Messenger\n\n(Upon looking carefully, the following symbol is visible in the lower right corner of the poster: ۞)\n",
    ["LetterText204002"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204102"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204202"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204203"]="Where to Find Magical Demons—by Newman Scott\n Like many demonic creatures, Tao Gunka is incredibly cunning, adept in covering its tracks. To date, there's no surefire way of capturing Tao Gunka, with the Circle of Spiritual Summons being the sole feasible option. Making certain offerings in the circle can forcibly summon Tao Gunka. According to the pact, the summoned demon must fulfill a wish for the summoners in order to leave the Circle.\n Appendix: How to Use a Circle of Spiritual Summons\n① Paint an inverted pentagram with the blood of a virgin\n② Place the bones of Tri Joint, Alligator, and Anolian in the center \n③ Get one each of Nether Flowers, Dark Mushrooms, and Undying Grass to place at the five corners\n④ Offer sincere prayers and shout out the demon's name",
    ["LetterText204204"]="Where to Find Magical Demons—by Newman Scott\n Like many demonic creatures, Tao Gunka is incredibly cunning, adept in covering its tracks. To date, there's no surefire way of capturing Tao Gunka, with the Circle of Spiritual Summons being the sole feasible option. Making certain offerings in the circle can forcibly summon Tao Gunka. According to the pact, the summoned demon must fulfill a wish for the summoners in order to leave the Circle.\n Appendix: How to Use a Circle of Spiritual Summons\n ① Paint an <color=#CA2E0AFF>inverted pentagram</color> with the blood of a virgin\n ② Place the bones of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tri Joint</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alligator</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anolian</color> in the center\n ③ Get one each of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nether Flower</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dark Mushroom</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undying Grass</color>",
    ["LetterText204205"]="to place at the five corners\n ④ Offer sincere prayers and <color=#CA2E0AFF>shout out the demon's name</color>",
    ["LetterText204301"]="August 17, A.W. 990\n The ship is running out of food. Without provisions, we won't return to Comodo alive... I must find a way. According to the chart, we might approach an island on the border where there should be some settlements. If worse comes to worst, we'll have to...\n \n August 22, A.W. 990\n ...I finally gave the order to plunder the ordinary village, but never expected such tenacity from the locals, who opted for mutual destruction in the face of our threat... All granaries have been burned. The wind carried the fire and set the whole village ablaze. I failed to save those people... Forgive me, Odin...",
    ["LetterText204302"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204303"]="August 23, A.W. 990\n Spencer found a kid in the ruins. She suffered no lethal injuries, just a little weak. However, I also found no desire to live in this child. She refused to talk to us or accept food. Perhaps to her, we're demons from the abyss that deprived her of all her loved ones... No, this can't be. I must find a way for her to live. I must save her.\n \n August 29, A.W. 990\n If my kindness couldn't invoke her hope for life, I'd rather she continued hating me. Let it be. I'll raise this child and make her into a true warrior. I believe one day she'll take my life and avenge her loved ones...\n",
    ["LetterText204304"]="August 4, A.W. 990\n ...Forgive me, gods. This is perhaps a sin I cannot ever erase, but please spare the child, so maybe I can give her back everything one day...",
    ["LetterText204305"]="August 17, A.W. 990\n The ship is running out of food. Without provisions, we won't return to Comodo alive... I must find a way. According to the chart, we might approach an island on the border where there should be some settlements. If worse comes to worst, we'll have to...",
    ["LetterText204306"]="August 22, A.W. 990\n ...I finally gave the order to plunder the ordinary village, but never expected such tenacity from the locals, who opted for mutual destruction in the face of our threat... All granaries have been burned. The wind carried the fire and set the whole village ablaze. I failed to save those people... Forgive me, Odin...",
    ["LetterText204307"]="August 23, A.W. 990\n Spencer found a kid in the ruins. She suffered no lethal injuries, just a little weak. However, I also found no desire to live in this child. She refused to talk to us or accept food. Perhaps to her, we're demons from the abyss that deprived her of all her loved ones... No, this can't be. I must find a way for her to live. I must save her.",
    ["LetterText204308"]="August 29, A.W. 990\n If my kindness couldn't invoke her hope for life, I'd rather she continued hating me. Let it be. I'll raise this child and make her into a true warrior. I believe one day she'll take my life and avenge her loved ones...",
    ["LetterText204309"]="August 4, A.W. 990\n ...Forgive me, gods. This is perhaps a sin I cannot ever erase, but please spare the child, so maybe I can give her back everything one day...",
    ["LetterText204401"]="Dear Margaret,\n I hope this finds you in good spirits. It has been several months since we parted in the cave. Is everything all right on Comodo?\n Lately, I've been thinking if what we did was right. You asked me to cast Aurora magic in the dragons' cave and seal the lava cave in ice. Although the act was to protect mankind and prevent the dragons from resurging, but the destruction of Dragon Flame also meant they could no longer propagate and would only face extinction... Do we really have the right to decide the fate of an entire race? Can there truly be no peaceful co-existence between humans and dragons?\n I am certainly not questioning you with these words, Margaret. We fought alongside before and I trust you like I trust myself. If you believe this is the correct path and are willing to devote yourself to the cause, I shall help to the best of my abilities without pausing. What I am concerned with are the changes in you... Is everything you do now out of your genuine intent? Or... would you change your mind because of the voices of the others?\n Your Pal, Nithil",
    ["LetterText204402"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204501"]="To My Pal Nithil,\n It is nice to hear from you.\n I am grateful for you keeping the issue of Aurora magic confidential. I fully understand your concern for my fate should it come to light, but from the years of fighting with me, you must also know I don't much care how others view me. Since I killed Morroc, I have known well that one's destiny can only be changed by oneself. I never felt the dragons' presence should be denied, but if the choice was to trade that for the survival of my kind, I would never regret my actions, despite my sorrows for dooming them.\n Perhaps one day the truth will be revealed, but that is insignificant to me. They may call me cold-blooded and bull-headed, but that's the real me who managed to create the equality that would otherwise never be seen on Comodo.\n Maybe this letter will not be sent, Nithil, for I sense I should not have to explain this to anyone as I write this. I can live with what I've done, and you surely will take that secret to the grave with you. Hence, let the past be buried deep underground with me.\n From Margaret",
    ["LetterText204502"]="                                                                     Invitation\nDear friends,\n      We will be holding the ROX <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Anniversary Music Festival</color> on October 15, 2021, from 20:00 to 22:30. We look forward to seeing you there!\n      Let's meet up once more!\n                                                                                                                                ROX\n                                                                                                                                Not far away in the future",
    ["LetterText204602"]="\"The Rise and Fall of the Ancient Secret Arts\"\nSecret Art - Aurora\nThe secret art created by the Heine Family ancestor, Nithil Heines. It is the earliest known multi-element magic, and one of the most powerful area attack magics. The caster needs to call upon the power of both wind and water elements, and the process of converting and fusing them absorbs a lot of heat, causing a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dramatic temperature drop in the environment</color>. The external manifestation is a huge frost storm that is so powerful that it can turn hot lava into permafrost. The name 'Aurora,' was derived from the traces of injuries that remain from being hurt by the spell. The frostbite marks look like flowing water, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut deep to the bone</color>. The mark cannot be removed and look like the Aurora Borealis in the night sky...",
    ["LetterText204702"]="B.W.11 March 6\nOne year has passed in the blink of an eye since I started training with Master Merlin. Master has taught me what he learned in his life, and I have benefited greatly. \nToday, my Master and I talked about the use of multiple element magic. As we all know, due to the different adaptability levels of individuals to elements, the magic that exists today is divided into singular elements. However, according to my Master's theory, if trained for a long time and supplemented with a strong environmental element, it is theoretically possible to cast a multi-element spell where multiple elements are merged. In order to confirm this theory, we decided to set out to find a place on this continent that is thick with elements to conduct experiments...",
    ["LetterText204802"]="B.W.6 December 31\nTime flies. This year is almost over. It has been three years since my Master was buried in the misty forest. I spend my days reminiscing and blaming myself. My Master would not have been transformed into a tree because of the witch's curse if it had not been for my carelessness. Since then, I have moved here to study day and night, but I have not been able to find a way to bring my Master back. Am I heading down the wrong track in my research?\nIn addition, in recent days, a beautiful woman often appears in my dreams. She has a child with her, and she's calling my name. She seems to have some connection tome... What in the world is going on?",
    ["LetterText204902"]="A.W.3 July 12\nAfter returning from Comodo, I was afraid of my own actions. I couldn't eat or sleep well. But this matter must not be known to the world. I have made up my mind to keep this secret until I die. It's just... I wonder if this will affect Margaret? I sent a letter a few days ago, but she has not replied yet, and I can't help but worry... But on second thought, this unwavering confidence is proof that she has not lost heart.",
    ["LetterText205001"]="Encyclopedia of Ancient Monsters",
    ["LetterText205002"]="\"...Dragons held their bloodline in noble regard. They preferred isolation, away from monsters and not much to do with mankind. They are <color=#CA2E0AFF>immense in size</color>, just the claw alone is as big as a matured man. The palm of their talon is <color=#CA2E0AFF>triangle</color> in shape, with <color=#CA2E0AFF>three thick, long fore-toes</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>one short hind-toe</color>. Except the palm, dragon bodies are covered in <color=#CA2E0AFF>hard scales</color> impenetrable to normal weapons. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>barbs</color> on them could even prevent weapons from withdrawing...\"",
    ["LetterText205101"]="Encyclopedia of Ancient Monsters",
    ["LetterText205102"]="\"Those who anger a dragon shall endure the pain of Dragon Flame. Dragon Flame is the fire of the abyss, <color=#CA2E0AFF>dreary and dark</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>staying lit</color>. Any injured by Dragon Flame may only be healed with <color=#CA2E0AFF>thousand-year-old glacier snow</color>.\"",
    ["LetterText205201"]="Peace Treaty of Comodo",
    ["LetterText205202"]="\"From this date forth, the dragons shall not leave the cave in western Comodo, or be considered act of aggression against mankind.\"\n \"While dragons adhere to the pact, Nerius family must ensure dragons' survival by providing sufficient food and resources, as well as defense of their cave.\"\n \"May this pact last forever in great Odin's witness.\"\n (The parchment is signed by Margaret Nerius and a huge dragon claw print.)",
    ["LetterText205302"]="To Mother Dearest,\n Please forgive my actions, but it is not my intention to betray the Nerius name. Just the opposite, I did all for the honor of the family.\n As I compose this letter, I can still recall when you told me and my sister about the family tenet: \"Everyone should be able to find peace and happiness on Comodo. Those who stir conflicts and disputes shall face a horrible fate.\" You interpreted that as humility, harmony, patience, and sacrifice—all traits passed down through generations of Nerius family.\n But what happened on the island in the past few years has made me dubious of its veracity, for those conflicts had always been stirred by the dragons that coveted Comodo! If peace has to be obtained through war, are we, as heirs of Nerius family, not responsible? Do not forget, Comodo was reborn in the blood of Lady Margaret, who wrote the tenet.\n Mother, it is time to open your eyes and see me, my sister, Kurulus, Vendra, and the soldiers still fighting invaders... Please witness our resolve and determination.\n \n (Cecilia did not sign, but the bottom of the letter was stained with crimson fingerprints, like bloody flowers of her resolution.)",
    ["LetterText205402"]="DNT",
    ["LetterText205502"]="DNT",
    ["LetterText205602"]="BeelzebubA.W. 1000 8.7\nIs it one, two, or three years? I've lost track of time. Day in and day out, all I have around my ears are the whispers of Master Beelzebub. The pope banished us to the isolated island. Thankfully, Master Hibam is with us. He's the High Priest that we all trust the most. Those people would never have guessed what they expected to rot like worms could achieve such a grand plan!\n\nA.W. 1000 9.12\nJust one last stone artifact to go, but there is nothing here! Damn the island! Damn the bodies! Let me out!\n\nA.W. 1001.1.2\nThe pirates are here. Those outlaws should be able to bring what I want, but what can I offer in exchange?\n\nA.W. 1001.1.3\nMaster Beelzebub, it won't be long before you rise again...",
    ["LetterText205603"]="A.W. 10XX 8.7\nIs it one, two, or three months? I've lost track of time. Day in and day out, all I have around my ears are the whispers of the ancient gods. The pope banished us to the isolated island. Thankfully, Master Hibam is with us. He's the High Priest that we all trust the most. Those people would never have guessed what they expected to rot like worms could achieve such a grand plan!\n\nA.W. 10XX 9.22\nFor the lack of the last two artifacts, our plan was forced to stop. When I was out looking for materials, I accidentally heard the sound of chains colliding from the abbey in the center of the island. There was someone inside! The prisoner with a crown on his head was surrounded by a sophisticated magic boundary. Yeah, I recognize this tormenting spell. Its power decreases as the prisoner's life drains. The poor guy will see hope and then despair again before his last breath. But what does any of that have to do with me? I'm after the artifact, nothing but the artifact!\n",
    ["LetterText205604"]="A.W. 10XX.10.2\nThe pirates came, but they refused to take me away. That man named Jimmy laughed at my face and said they could collect my body for free when the time came. Bloody outlaws! What can I offer them in exchange for my freedom? Great ancient gods, have mercy on your servant...\n\nA.W. 10XX.10.3\nPraise the ancient gods! By your will, I have broken the fragile boundary in the abbey, and the nameless king was too weak to fight back. He couldn't do anything when I took off his crown. Those foolish pirates surely went after the treasure that did not belong to them. All-knowing and all-powerful ancient gods, when you return, your humble servant will kneel at your feet and kiss the corner of your robe with reverence...",
    ["LetterText205605"]="A.W. 10XX.10.2\nThe pirates came, but they refused to take me away. That man named Jimmy laughed at my face and said they could collect my body for free when the time came. Bloody outlaws! What can I offer them in exchange for my freedom? Great ancient gods, have mercy on your servant...",
    ["LetterText205606"]="A.W. 10XX.10.3\nPraise the ancient gods! By your will, I have broken the fragile boundary in the abbey, and the nameless king was too weak to fight back. He couldn't do anything when I took off his crown. Those foolish pirates surely went after the treasure that did not belong to them. All-knowing and all-powerful ancient gods, when you return, your humble servant will kneel at your feet and kiss the corner of your robe with reverence...",
    ["LetterText205702"]="Date: xx xx\n- Attend the handshake event on the north side of the forest (Excellent job today, Doyle, you are so adorable!)\n- Meet Tracy on the suspension bridge in front of the waterfall on the east side of the forest (I have a terrible feeling. I will bail if necessary.)\n- Pick a blue iris for Olivia (I wish it can wash away the cheesiness of that pink hair of hers...)\n- Invite Leslie to enjoy the sunset (Even the sunset can't compete with her rosy cheeks, hoo hoo!)",
    ["LetterText205802"]="Criatura Academy Graduate Archives\n—Masters' Evaluation\nName: Travers W. Feld\nAcademic Number: AW0358641\nClass: Acolyte\nDate: AW10XX/X/XX\nMainz: Hoho! I'm sure you professors will have a lot to say about this student. Write your best wishes for him in brief!\nAlice: Travers is very responsible. He always uses the hymn book to prop up his desk in class quizzes, but he still writes good reviews.\nMoxie: Heh. I don't get how an Acolyte can learn the skills of a thief but this doesn't mean he can steal my roses to feed them to feral Lunatic!\nCharles: Hey, you forgot the most important point. Why does an Acolyte student need evaluations from six Masters?\nHamid: It's because he's worth six times as much, of course! That said, turns out that new rose Travers recommended to me is Moxie's! Hahahahaha!\nMelbrun: I recall him sneaking into my classroom once. He seemed bent on improving the accuracy of hitting people with hymn books... Are all you Acolyte students like this?!\nYadrew: He's always used his talents in dangerous, creative ways. I would have asked him to leave the classroom immediately if he didn't have decent sword skills. ",
    ["LetterText205901"]="\"Ode of the Elemental Envoy\"\nA Song of Water\nI buried my dreams of adventure at the bottom of the sea on the seventh day,\nlike faded Obeaune laid resting by coral reefs.\nRotten treasure within a cave upstarted at me:\n\"You are neither silver nor gold, so get thee hence!\"\nNeither are the faded doors of broken-down palaces, nor empty courts that glitter no more.\nEven the Gods have become transient rocks; dreamwalkers that whisper dreams.",
    ["LetterText206001"]="A Song of Fire\nOn the fifth day I became like a thief of fire,\na spirit of sacred, regal intent to keep watch within a high tower.\nA shocked face fell silent by the edge of my staff:\n\"Below... below is a jungle of the dead!\"\nDon't panic!\nThe holy fire ravages most where sins are carried out.",
    ["LetterText206101"]="A Song of Earth\nOn the third day I was crowned on the red dirt,\nand wore scarlet blood for my cloak and bones for vestments.\nI finally ventured into the arena of the catacombs below,\ncasting aside all medals, belts of honor, and crowns.\nThey are devils and so am I.\nFor I would enjoy fighting with the defeated more.",
    ["LetterText206201"]="A Song of Wind\nOn the first day I was a scarecrow enjoying the stars on a windy night,\na friend to birds passing a lover's nightscape.\nI saw the farmer of the field pacing,\nscattering himself into deep trenches,\npraying to windmills:\nFray me! Free me!",
    ["LetterText206402"]="Young Adventurer:\nI trust you are going well.\nI've organized the time for this letter to be sent to you. I had a careful reading of the essay I received. Please return to the Mjolnir Mountains and find me by the Sage Hut to carry out your Disputation Ceremony once you reach <color=#CA2E0AFF>class level 50</color>.\nKroneika",
    ["LetterText206501"]="Dear Bohr,\nPlease be sure to protect Prince Aronst and Prince Azer Alm during the king's election. As I learned that a failed <color=#CA2E0AFF>assignation</color> was attempted on them not while ago, and it was the <color=#CA2E0AFF>brave successor of Odin's bloodline</color> that prevented this tragedy from happening. What makes me worry even more is that the culprit is still on flee, and it's getting close to the election, which I suspect they will make their moves again. For you being the commander of the Defense Force, <color=#CA2E0AFF>please fulfill the task that falls into your scope of responsibility</color>.\n                                                                                                                                    A concerned Prontera citizen, Miss M",
    ["LetterText206601"]="A poison that was used to be one of the torturing items. It has a considerably complicated formula in which the potion-maker can substitute the <color=#CA2E0AFF>key ingredient</color> to achieve different effects for torturing the prisoner. Without an antidote, one will suffer various levels of pain based on its effect throughout the course of seven days, and then they will <color=#CA2E0AFF>breathe their last at the end of the seventh day</color>. Based on the potion-maker's habit, various changes occur in the potion formula, rendering it <color=#CA2E0AFF>impossible to reverse-engineer a universal antidote</color> in this case. Due to the potion's brutal nature, the government has passed a law on A.W.762 to include it on the list of <color=#CA2E0AFF>banned potions</color>, with a total of one hundred and seventy-two items on the list. But it's said that it is still circulating on the black market today. If you encounter any organization selling this potion, please report it to Defense Force immediately!",
    ["LetterText206602"]="(Placeholder: After reading the book in the library's forbidden book area, you realize that the poison in this bottle is called X. It circulates on the black market at a steep price. People won't notice after taking the potion, but they are as dead as a doornail after seven days without an antidote. Due to X's flexibility in choosing the key ingredient to use when crafting this potion, only the potion-maker who knows about the exact formula of X can make the antidote.)",
    ["LetterText206701"]="Deployment List of the Guardian Troops\nRodney Workum | Sick leave\nZudd González | Change of duty area: Geffen\nIverson Rodrigues | Change of duty area: Glast Heim\nPlester Brown | On vacation\nHarold Montague | Sick leave\n...",
    ["LetterText206802"]="Honorable Oman, Your Excellency,\n       Everything is ready to go. They are located at the corner of the Palace Garden walls to the west. By taking them, you agree to the deal, <color=#CA2E0AFF>put them into the dishes prepared for the princes</color>, and the deal is done. We will <color=#CA2E0AFF>well compensate</color> you for your assistance afterward.\n        Our lord has attached a keepsake for his identity to show our respect in this letter. Please ensure you take good care of it and don't let others see it.\n\n (There is no signature, but you can clearly see the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Walter family emblem</color> on this expensive parchment...)",
    ["LetterText206902"]="Dear teacher,\n        In the blink of an eye, it has been a month since I left Nameless Island. I wonder how you and all my friends are doing on the island. I hope everything is good.\n        This time, I arrived at the rainforest in Umbala to investigate the artifact Hel mentioned before. She didn't say much about it when I was in Niflheim, which makes me feel even more suspicious about the whole thing, and that's why I left the island to search for the clue to this artifact.\n        According to Hel, this artifact is guarded by Yggdrasil's power. Here I am, the place said to be created by Yggdrasil's power in the legend, Umbala rainforest, to investigate the Utan tribe who have stayed here since the beginning of time. Through my research, I suspect the artifact that Hel was talking about might be the Earth Fragment of Ymir's Heart that the Utans use to keep this rainforest in peace. This artifact has acted as the heart of the Umbala rainforest since ancient times, maintaining the balance of various elements in the rainforest. Once it's lost, a devastating disaster is deemed to fall upon Umbala! And Hel didn't mention any of the consequences to us... Teacher, she must be hiding something from us, and we must not lower our guard!\n        I recall the original purpose for you to summon the ancient god was to release all beings from the agony in this current rotten world. But now, for the sake of commencing this summoning ritual, we are risking the life of everyone in the Umbala rainforest. Even your soul needs to be put on the table for the ritual! Teacher... Is this worth it?\n        Teacher, we should take a step back and review this so-called ancient god or search for another way to realize our wish without sacrificing anybody. I beg you... put a hold on the ritual for now, even if it makes all our effort go waste, but I truly believe that everyone will stay by your side, and we can work on it from scratch.\n                                                                                                                     Your student, Israel\n\n(At the bottom of the letter, there is annotation in totally different handwriting with great force, almost like the words are carved into the paper with a bloody red color.)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Read. The decision is final, and nothing shall change my mind. I'm returning this letter with my reply to show you my resolve.</color>",
    ["LetterText207002"]="Israel,\n       I've read your advice in the letter, but I am sorry to say that we don't have the leisure for trial and error based on the current circumstance. I'm afraid I won't live long enough to see the birth of the new world if we do not seize this opportunity to bring the ancient god into the human world. Since ancient, none of the greatness bothered with the details. In order to achieve our goal, sacrifices are needed, and for this, we have already lost many brothers and sisters who share the same vision as us along the path. Don't you remember what did Lareia say before she died? Isreal, do not be fooled by the momentary softness. As you look towards the future, you should envision a new world order where all sacrifices are redeemed.\n       Ever since Lady Hel opened up her heart and shared her past with us, I firmly believe that she will be the most loyal ally by our side. She longs for redemption, and the only way to achieve that is to assist the ancient god's advent to the world, so she deliberately withholds the truth of the Utan sacred relic from us. We shouldn't be pointing our fingers at her. In fact, the earlier we complete the ritual, the better the chance of minimizing the unnecessary sacrifices of Utan.\n       Not a while ago, I signed a soul contract with Lady Hel. Because of this, after the ritual is completed... you must take on my unfinished work and lead everyone to the new world order under the ancient god's guidance. Isreal, remember your duty by heart and don't let anything shake it. Now, return to me at once; there is not much time left for us to be with each other, and I want to teach you everything I learned throughout my life. Please try to understand the good deed your teacher is doing for the world and for you.\n                                                                                                                                   Your teacher, Hibram\n",
    ["LetterText207101"]="Father,\n       This might be the last time I address you as my father.\n       By the time you see the letter, I am already done with my duty—In the way of disobeying your order, of course. I'm unsure whether my performance in the Bloodline Banquet is good enough to fill up your sinful heart.\n       I know you don't ever shame yourself for your desire. You admit your treasonous intention to me back on the day when you try to poison Aronst. From the three princes of the Gaebolg family, followed by Bohr and Aronst, you turn yourself into a demon and drag the whole family to the bottomless abyss just for an ice-cold throne. If I expose your conspiracy to the world, my mother, brother, teacher, and even my best friend will all go down with you.\n       Of course, you will not let me slip away; in fact, I am the most crucial part of your master plan. You want to send me to the throne and become your puppet for ruling this kingdom. You pretended to be an excellent father just to make me follow your orders and promise that you would spare Aronst once the Walter family seized the supreme authority.\n       I chose to comply with you, not because I believe in you; only by doing this can I be close to you—to shatter your plan a bit by a bit. As expected, on the first day of the election, you already wanted me to take the opportunity and make Aronst drink the Memory Erasing Potion prepared by you. You claimed that this would only make him forget about the assassination and pose no side effect to him... But how could I trust you that you don't use this as an opportunity to dose him another poison?",
    ["LetterText207201"]="       By seeing this, I deliberately escalated this incident and let Moffit witness the entire course of how Aronst was dosed with the potion. I even left the bottle on the scene just for their reference. If the potion really was a toxic substance as I thought it would be, then the bottle I left there could definitely assist them in finding the cure...\n       Just where my intuition points me, you never wanted to spare Aronst's life. All the things you ever told me were nothing but a pure lie. As soon as Aronst took the poison—the poison named Luminary Dream, you started to reveal the cunning face before me and use Aronst's life to threaten me that I must follow your order to make Aronst the scapegoat of the Walter family if I want to have the antidote. Otherwise, on the day of the Bloodline Banquet... I will see Aronst turning into a corpse.\n       I am fully aware of why you insist on taking Aronst's life; you worry about his popularity among the citizens, and it could become an obstacle along your path to supremacy. As for the treason... this is a dead end for the Gaebolg family that will shatter their long-holding reputation overnight. To this end, you ordered me to lure Aronst to Pooler Garden the night before the Bloodline Banquet and dose him with the deadly potion. By doing this, Aronst will follow everything I say, and I can make him admit to all the crimes during the Bloodline Banquet. He then will be disqualified even if he wins the election, and the throne will fall to the next runner-up, which is me. To calm me down, you fabricate another lie and assure me that I can pardon Aronst's sin in the name of the new king once everything is settled...\n       At this moment, I realize that maybe I do belong to the Walter family, inheriting the cold-blooded strain from my ancestor. Somehow I can fake my compliance to your request while secretly planning how to destroy everything on the other hand. I even take a wild guess on the reason you wanted me to be the one who ends Aronst's life because you want me to turn into the same kind of person as you, whose hands are stained by their closest one's blood. You trust no one but your own kind.\n       The night before the Bloodline Banquet, I overheard the secret conversation between you and Dardano. It turns out that Royal Chivalry has switched their side long ago, and all the servants in the palace are actually the people from the Walter family. You received the insider news in advance and learned that Aronst was way ahead in the election and would undoubtedly be the new king. You then ordered Dardanom; whether Aronst becomes the scapegoat or not, you want him dead just for precaution.\n       I hate myself for being so naive that expecting a cold-blooded prisoner to retain his kindness and conscience. No... There is no time to waste, and I must carry out my plan immediately. This is the only way to protect Aronst and the Walter family...",
    ["LetterText207301"]="       I don't have much time left, and I have to set up everything before this thing becomes irreversible. I stole a list from your office, which on the list are the rats you planned in the palace. I follow what you taught me, make them spit out the information I need, and kill them all. After that, I replace them with my people. Would you be proud of me if you knew what I had done?\n        Of course, this is far from enough. Didn't you want someone who could be the scapegoat for the Walter family? I think this role fits me the best. I dosed Aronst with the illusion potion and ordered him to go to the Schwarzwald Republic in Mjolnir Mountains, and there will be someone waiting for him. I need to hide him from you—so that I can pretend to be Aronst and admit all the crimes in the Bloodline Banquet. Those supporters of Aronst must start to defend him hysterically, and they will exhaust every piece of evidence just to put the Walter family behind the bar... I need a moment like this, a moment when they have used up all their cards and chips. By then, I will reveal my true identity and admit all the crimes in the name of Azer Alm, making me nothing but a traitor... Everything will soon be settled following my death.\n        I don't think I will ever forgive you. I have spoken to you with my heartfelt feeling that I am not into this throne, and I don't want to hurt someone I care just for the power the throne brings me. But you scorn my true feeling. The moment you started to use me as a tool to realize your ambition, we were no longer father and son. May the icy cold path to the throne lead you to a lonely death.\n                                                                                                                                                          Azer Alm",
    ["LetterText207401"]="To whom it may concern,\n       Greetings, stranger. Regardless of who you are, since you found my letter, I shamelessly ask you for a favor. If you will, please deliver this letter to Bohr, a Defense Force officer in Prontera, the capital of Rune-Midgarts Kingdom. He will compensate you for your kindness. If he doesn't... then just let it slip and treat this as the last will of a dying person.\n       As I look back on my life with long days but short years, I was fortunate enough to be a king. My capabilities prevented me from making the kingdom prosper in my life, which caused many people to become greedy around me. Even though I don't blame them, a crown seized by a coup isn't very convincing to others, and it's an unforgivable act if it puts the kingdom in a vulnerable position. Midgard is now undergoing a major change that has never been seen before for the past thousand years. The undercurrent makes it hard to determine who wins and who loses. Please think twice before you act, and don't do something that you will regret later.\n       All things aside, even though I can't be there to witness who takes over the crown, I truly wish you would put the fate of this kingdom before anything. King must not rule a kingdom to his liking; in times of crisis, he must unite everyone in his kingdom to survive. To forgive is not necessarily a sign of weakness, but it teaches us how to weigh various things and value them appropriately as part of self-improvement.\n       As a final note, I'd like to thank all of you for reading this far. It is my sincere wish that you all be blessed by Odin and live a wonderful life.\n                                                                                                  Tristan III, The Fifty-sixth King of the Rune-Midgarts Kingdom",
    ["LetterText207502"]="Xerand Kunha (A.W.205–A.W.231)\nHere, a great knight rests in peace.\nSword, \"Holy Fire\"\nShield, \"Summum Bonum\"\nUse the sword to sunder the sin of all beings.\nUse the shield to bear the pain of all beings.\nHe witnesses the glory and the doom of Glast Heim.\nHe carves his name on the this Tome of Fame.\nHe has high morals.\nNever ever pointed his sword at ordinary people, regardless.\nHe owns a soul made of steel.\nHe will never abandon his oath, even in the face of unfairness.\nBut fate makes him suffer.\nHis life ended with delusion and deception perpetrated by his dearest friend.\nThe flame may burn everything into the ground.\nBut it won't exhaust his heart of purity.\nDeath is only the beginning.\nThe true adventure belongs to this knight of greatness\nHas yet to begin...",
    ["LetterText207601"]="Dear Successor of Odin's bloodline,\nDo please forgive me for my impoliteness in sending you this very abrupt invitation. Yet recently, Juno has found itself in the grip of chaos, with <color=#CA2E0AFF>many androids going out of control</color>, vandalizing the city to the ground, and attacking human citizens. Our guards have been suppressing the riot with full force, but the situation has hardly improved. On reflection, I think only with the help of the wise and courageous Successor of Odin's Bloodline can the crisis be resolved. If you are willing to help, please return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color> with Minister Philodis together. I sincerely look forward to your arrival.\nCarl, Lord of the Schwarzwald Republic",
    ["LetterText207701"]="Appendix: Mech Agreement\n*The revised fourth draft version, voted and approved by the council, effective in A.W. 674.\n\n1. Any robot manufactured for the purpose of simulating and acting like human beings (hereinafter referred to as \"Android\") must be installed all terms of this agreement into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chip</color>, and any unit that violates this legislation must be destroyed immediately once verified.\n\n2. An Android must fully comply with the order issued by the master.\n\n3. It is strictly <color=#CA2E0AFF>prohibited</color> for an Android to perform any <color=#CA2E0AFF>harmful act to any human</color> unless the Android has double-confirmed that the order is issued by the master as the highest priority.\n\n",
    ["LetterText207801"]="Dear Lord Carl,\nYour Excellency, please pardon me for bothering you. A few days ago, I happened to receive a document that is logged with the detail of the latest android's <color=#CA2E0AFF>chip</color> developed by the Khayr Consortium. After reading it carefully, I suspect there is a chance for this chip model to <color=#CA2E0AFF>breach the restriction stated in the Mech Agreement</color>, and cause the androids to malfunction, even to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go out of control and attack humans</color>. To prevent this from escalating, I have hidden the said document inside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Academy</color>, along with the emergency response plan. Feel free to retrieve them, Lord Carl.\nP.S.: To prevent this letter from falling into the wrong hands, there is a large number of <color=#CA2E0AFF>airborne surveillance devices</color> patrolling above the campus. No personnel but Lord Carl can enter the academy at this moment. Please note.\nBy Anonymous",
    ["LetterText207802"]="4. When a life-threatening situation occurs on the master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>protecting the master</color> will become the Android's highest priority, and both of the aforementioned protocols will be reduced to the lowest priority.\n\n5. Any Android, when being designed, must be integrated with a self-destruction mechanism in response to a situation of emergency.\n\n6. <color=#CA2E0AFF>It is prohibited to design an Android with high-level physical resemblances to human beings</color>. Under special circumstances, the Android must at least include certain <color=#CA2E0AFF>exterior mechanical appearance</color> for distinguishing purposes.\n...",
    ["LetterText207901"]="\"Non-Official\" Dispatch Team Rally Order:\nWe hereby invite the strongest in the kingdom, to assemble a \"Non-Official\" Dispatch Team going to Lighthalzen for a search and rescue mission. All expenses and remuneration will be compensated by the kingdom, through the official channel.\n\nAttachment:\nMissing Contacts List:\nEremes Guile\nSeyren Windsor\nCecil Devine\nKatrina Keyron\nHoward Alt-Eison\nMargaret Sorin\n\nForeign Minster of the Kingdom: Lonagatt Dejan\nA.W.10XX.XX.X",
    ["LetterText208001"]="Dear Successor of Odin's bloodline,\nMy Right Honorable friend, I've heard much about your reputation. You have single-handedly saved the Rune Kingdom from crises many times. And now, the fate of our kingdom is at stake again. After prolonged and prudent consideration, we are now at our last resort to send out this letter to you. If you are willing to lend us your help, please go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>airship platform</color> on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude Island</color> tonight. I will be waiting there for your arrival.\nSincerely, <color=#CA2E0AFF>F</color>",
    ["LetterText208101"]="※\n※\n※\n※\n※\nIn the year of AW575, when Juno University was first established, there was a secret underground lab in the school library. But it had only existed for 3 days before it was demolished. The construction materials were recycled and then used to build a warehouse in Khayr Estate.\n※\n※\n※\n※\n※",
    ["LetterText208201"]="\"Non-Official\" Dispatch Team Rally Order:\nWe hereby invite the strongest in the kingdom, to assemble a \"Non-Official\" Dispatch Team going to Lighthalzen for a search and rescue mission. All expenses and remuneration will be compensated by the kingdom, through the official channel.\n\nAttachment:\nMissing Contacts List:\nEremes Guile\nSeyren Windsor\nCecil Devine\nKatrina Keyron\nHoward Alt-Eison\nMargaret Sorin\n\nForeign Minster of the Kingdom: Lonagatt Dejan\nA.W.10XX.XX.X",
    ["LetterText208301"]="Project X Experiment Record, May 27\n32nd Compatibility Test. After factoring in all known data gathered so far, it should be ready for deployment in a short while.\nThis is a new attempt in which I've integrated a backdoor program in the chip that allows it to bypass the Mech Agreement detection protocol and <color=#CA2E0AFF>free it from the control of humans</color>. To achieve this, I've conducted countless experiments, and in each failed attempt, the chip in the test subject was <color=#CA2E0AFF>reduced to ashes due to the punishing mechanism triggering</color>. But everything will be worth it at the end of the day.\nKayak said that those people plan to secretly install my chips in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gen-Series</color> civilian androids developed by the Khayr Consortium. In this way, they'll only need to find the best time to activate the backdoor program in the chip to awaken the androids in unison and throw Kiel Khayr into a blind alley... Hmph, they're making painstaking efforts just to take over the consortium.\n...Never mind, this is not a bad thing for me. I can take this opportunity to gather more data in the future. I believe that one day, these androids will make history and lead humanity to a better future. Compared to humans who only live for their own desires, machines with their absolute rationality are the most perfect beings in the world...",
    ["LetterText208401"]="Gen-Series Civilian Android Factory Settings Record\nOperation Mode: General\nChip Status: Inactive\nAdministrator Identification: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr</color>\nPermission Settings: Locked. Only the administrator can modify.\nRemote Data Connection: Enabled. Only the administrator can connect.\nMech Core Status: Normal\n...\nApproval Status: Approved for deployment.\nApprover:<color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr</color>\n(An elaborate seal is stamped at the bottom of the document. The unmistakable logo of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Khayr Consortium</color> is clear for all to see.)",
    ["LetterText208501"]="\nArchive No.: RB-00001\nSecurity Classification: Top Secret\nSecurity Measures: RB-00001 should be secretly stored 1,000 meters below the ground of Juno in a completely sealed space to retain its original state. Anyone who learns about its existence through illegal means, studies its composition, or utilizes its power will be prosecuted for treason.\nDescription: RB-00001 is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>intact Ymir's Heart</color> from a future timeline, i.e., the heart of Ymir, the \"Ancestral Frost Giant.\"\n\nTo prevent the dispersion of its divine power, RB-00001 should be secretly stored together with the control unit RB-00001-1. RB-00001 should be put under S-Class monitoring status at all times in order for it to provide perpetual levitation power for Juno.\n\nRB-00001 was once associated with RB-00002 as a core technological creation of RB-00002.\n\n\n\nArchive No.: RB-00002\nSecurity Classification: Top Secret\nSecurity Measures: RB-00002 should be secretly archived in the Schwarzwald Republic Archives to retain its unknown status. Anyone who learns about its existence through illegal means, studies its composition, or utilizes its power will be prosecuted for treason.\n\nDescription: RB-00002 (destroyed) is from a higher civilization a millennium later. Its descendant, RB-00002-1, is referred to as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Welsh Civilization</color>.\n\nIn AW490, RB-00002, along with RB-00001, first appeared above Juperos Plains (now Juperos Ruins) and crashed after 5 hours.\n\nAccording to RB-00002-1, the crash of RB-00002 was caused by a failed dimensional transfer experiment.\n\nAppendix: Excerpted from RB-00002-1 & RB-00002-2's last words\nRB-00002-1: Control unit... Is it fixed?\nRB-00002-2: It's fixed... (sobbing) Professor... Try not to speak... You've lost a lot of blood...\nRB-00002-1: Stop crying, kid... (coughing) Let's carry out the plan.\nRB-00002-2: But... (sobbing) Myers, Fennie, and Watley all fell off... I just want to go home...\nRB-00002-1: Don't worry... Welsh will not fall easily... (coughing) Listen, kid... Wait until I send the civilization down there to the sky... I'm taking you home...\nRB-00002-2: (Sobbing) Professor... You are engulfed by the radiation storm... Does it hurt?\nRB-00002-1: It will only last a split second... Kid, go take a nap... when you are done...",
    ["LetterText208502"]="Archive No.: RB-00002\nSecurity Classification: Top Secret\nSecurity Measures: RB-00002 should be secretly archived in the Schwarzwald Republic Archives to retain its unknown status. Anyone who learns about its existence through illegal means, studies its composition, or utilizes its power will be prosecuted for treason.\n\nDescription: RB-00002 (destroyed) is from a higher civilization a millennium later. Its descendant, RB-00002-1, is referred to as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Welsh Civilization</color>.\n\nIn AW490, RB-00002, along with RB-00001, first appeared above Juperos Plains (now Juperos Ruins) and crashed after 5 hours.\n\nAccording to RB-00002-1, the crash of RB-00002 was caused by a failed dimensional transfer experiment.\n\nAppendix: Excerpted from RB-00002-1 & RB-00002-2's last words\nRB-00002-1: Control unit... Is it fixed?\nRB-00002-2: It's fixed... (sobbing) Professor... Try not to speak... You've lost a lot of blood...\nRB-00002-1: Stop crying, kid... (coughing) Let's carry out the plan.\nRB-00002-2: But... (sobbing) Myers, Fennie, and Watley all fell off... I just want to go home...\nRB-00002-1: Don't worry... Welsh will not fall easily... (coughing) Listen, kid... Wait until I send the civilization down there to the sky... I'm taking you home...\nRB-00002-2: (Sobbing) Professor... You are engulfed by the radiation storm... Does it hurt?\nRB-00002-1: It will only last a split second... Kid, go take a nap... when you are done...",
    ["LetterText208601"]="Day 1:\n Seeing my fellow brothers' bruised faces as they touched the ground haunted my dreams for a week. Good thing it's me doing the trial. **** told me that the number of participants is half what it was last time. At this rate, all three Ninja paths will fade away eventually. But besides the Water Clan, no one is making any objections, nor do they care about us. Maybe it's because the Water Clan has the least number of ****? Aggressive as fire, swift as wind. We only have a slight advantage on <color=#CA2E0AFF>poisoning and spirit summoning</color>. However, since the trial takes place in the Forgotten Lake, we might turn things around with some terrain tricks. I'm planning to sneak into the riverbed alone and hang tight until they and those Skeletons wear each other out, and then I'll show them what a true Ninja looks like.\n\n Day 2:\n They say anyone who desecrates the Forgotten Lake is a goner, but all I found in the river were bones, and I even had dreams about my younger self. My opponents are smart. They didn't **** right off the bat but grouped up to sort out their duties, aiming to race to the Forgotten Lake after eliminating every Skeleton together. My senior was also super smart. He found me and brought the Ninjas from Wind and Water Clans with a plan to team up to take on the toughest Fire Clan after clearing everything. I asked him why he was sharing intel with me when there could only be one winner. He said his goal isn't to win the trial but to keep his peers alive while winning the trial. The clan wants to protect **** young Ninjas no matter what it takes, even if it ****.\n\n Day 3:\n I should've seen this coming! If they can team up with us against the Fire Clan, why couldn't they join forces with them to knock us out first? Damn! they couldn't really be thinking ****?\n\n Day 4:\n In my dream, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forgotten Lake was calling me</color>, but then I woke up to betrayal and death hitting so suddenly. I have to find a way out before my supplies run out. The trial for the second class allows both winners and losers to live, but they won't let me off the hook, and I won't spare them either.",
    ["LetterText208701"]="Military Consumables Breakdown (Q3)",
    ["LetterText208702"]="August 6:\n90 tons of refined rare ore | Transported to Einbroch\n420 tons of α-3 alloy | Stored\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Note: Batch No. S-1028L, Class-1 Restricted Material</color>\n...",
    ["LetterText208703"]="August 19:\n420 tons of α-3 alloy | Transported to Einbroch\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Note: Batch No. S-1028L, Class-1 Restricted Material</color>\n...",
    ["LetterText208704"]="August 21:\n600 tons of smelting liquid | Transported to Einbroch\n350 tons of α-3 alloy | Invested (Einbroch Branch)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Note: Batch No. S-1028L, Class-1 Restricted Material</color>\n...",
    ["LetterText208705"]="September 17\n20,000 sets of bipolar circuit boards | Stored\n90 tons of refined rare ore | Invested (Einbroch Branch)\n...\n\nSchwarzwald Republic Military Office\nA.W.1002.10",
    ["LetterText208706"]="July 12\n600 tons of smelting liquid | Stored \n100,000 polymer units | Transported to Juno\n200 tons of transformation crystals | Invested (Juno Branch)\n...",
    ["LetterText208801"]="Purchase Order (Q3)",
    ["LetterText208802"]="August 6\n90 tons of refined rare ore (Batch No. C-1158L)\n...",
    ["LetterText208803"]="August 20\n90 tons of dissolution oil (Batch No. C-5347L)\n70 tons of α-3 alloy (Batch No. S-1028L)\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Note: For RT project use only</color>\n...",
    ["LetterText208804"]="September 17\n120 tons of water-based putty (Batch No. C-6679L)\n90 tons of refined rare ore (Batch No. C-9327L)\n...\n\nSteel Capital Institute - Procurement Department\nA.W.1002.10",
    ["LetterText208805"]="July 8\n270 tons of thickener (Batch No. C-7795L)\n30 tons of laser coating (Batch No. C-2168L)\n10,000 micro control units (Batch No. C-421L)\n...",
    ["LetterText208901"]="Dear the successor of Odin's bloodline,\nTime has flown, and you've been in Juno for several days now. I am embarrassed for not fulfilling my duties as your host. As an apology, I sincerely invite you to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch</color> to experience the grandeur of the Republic. If you are interested, kindly make your way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color> at your earliest convenience for a detailed discussion. I will be expecting your arrival.\nSincerely, Carl",
    ["LetterText209001"]="RT-X Project Processing Log",
    ["LetterText209002"]="October 22\nOverall progress: 77%\nCore material status: Polishing completed\n...",
    ["LetterText209003"]="October 29\nOverall progress: 89%\nCore material status: Chamber loading completed\n...",
    ["LetterText209004"]="November 2\nOverall progress: 100%\nCore material status: Rifling completed\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Delivered to the Eastern Factory as scheduled by the contract</color>\n...",
    ["LetterText209005"]="October 19\nOverall progress: 68%\nCore material status: Receipt confirmed\nTracking number: TL33019-SG\n...",
    ["LetterText209101"]="Mining Area Section Door Construction Plan (Third Edition Revised)\nDesign Purpose\nTo stop airflow between the mine and Nogg Cave, preventing an <color=#CA2E0AFF>explosion</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>methane</color> leakage meeting <color=#CA2E0AFF>high temperatures</color> in the cave.\n\nMain Design Features\n1. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seal all other entrances and exits</color> except for the mechanical gate.\n2. The switch status <color=#CA2E0AFF>can be controlled remotely</color> and requires <color=#CA2E0AFF>multi-factor authentication</color>. It's advised to use the latest <color=#CA2E0AFF>Type III Admin Robot</color>.\n3. Install an <color=#CA2E0AFF>alarm system</color> to constantly monitor the methane concentration in the air.\n4. Deploy <color=#CA2E0AFF>Noxious</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Venomous</color> to absorb the methane in the air.\n5. In conjunction with the mechanical gate, construct <color=#CA2E0AFF>gas pipelines</color> to use methane as fuel for other heavy equipment.\n...",
    ["LetterText209201"]="Einbech Village Population Data Sheet",
    ["LetterText209202"]="Dave Samo\nAge: 42\nGender: Male\nNotable Features: N/A\n...",
    ["LetterText209203"]="Nina Samo\nAge: 7\nGender: Female\nNotable Features: Stage IV Pneumoconiosis, no prosthetic implants\n...",
    ["LetterText209204"]="Harlin Malia\nAge: 26\nGender: Female\nNotable Features: Blindness in left eye, C-28 prosthetic implant installed\n...",
    ["LetterText209205"]="Anton Platt\nGender: Male\nAge: 68\nNotable Features: Amputated right leg, no prosthetic implants\n...",
    ["LetterText209301"]="\"Rekenber Times Weekly\" #32\nThe bidding process for the mining area's industrial transformation project is nearing its conclusion, and the municipal government plans to unveil the successful bidder soon. According to our intel, this project is set to be the most significant construction in Einbroch over the last decade, with the government allocating a budget of over 120 million for it. In a special interview, the mayor showed high hopes for the future of the project and hinted at the desire for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp to handle the project</color>...",
    ["LetterText209302"]="\"Rekenber Times Weekly\" #44\nA year into the mining area's industrial transformation project, our team revisited some of the miners originally from Einbech Village. An elder miner, known as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shyte</color>, told our team that Rekenber Corp had relocated all the miners who lived in Einbech Village, providing them with new jobs and homes as soon as the project kicked off. Plus the additional financial compensation from the government, he expressed that he could now <color=#CA2E0AFF>enjoy his elder years in peace</color>, no longer needing to work...",
    ["LetterText209303"]="\"Rekenber Times Weekly\" #69\nToday marked the completion of the highly anticipated mining area's industrial transformation project. President Rowland appeared in the ribbon-cutting ceremony and stated that the revamped mining area would spearhead Einbroch's industrial journey. As Einbroch's <color=#CA2E0AFF>top-selling weekly</color>, we are honored to have President Rowland join us in an exclusive interview. During the interview...",
    ["LetterText209401"]="Winning Bid Announcement\nProject Name: Einbroch Mining Area Transformation\nProject ID: CBP-8623\nWinner: Rekenber Corp\nWinning Bid: 860 Million Zeny\nList of Bidding Committee Members:\n...",
    ["LetterText209402"]="Appendix: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unemployment Compensation</color> for Einbech Village Miners\n1. Compensation calculation formula: Miner's years of service x 60,000 Zeny\n2. For miners with children under 12 or elderly above 60 in the family, an extra 12,000 Zeny is added per headcount.\n3. Miners disabled due to work-related injuries are eligible for a one-time subsidy of 30,000 Zeny\n...\nThe above compensations are <color=#CA2E0AFF>funded by the government and distributed by Rekenber Corp</color>, with payments to be made within 3 months before the project starts.\nEinbroch Municipal Government\nJuly 23, AW995",
    ["LetterText209501"]="June 15, AW1002\nExperiment ID: RT-2259-6\nMachine: RT-057X\nTest Subject: Harlin Malia\nProcedure: Utilized laser therapy to revive cellular activity in the subject's left eye.\nObjective: <color=#CA2E0AFF>To attempt the restoration of vision in the subject's left eye.</color>\nResult: Successful\n...",
    ["LetterText209502"]="August 7, AW1002\nExperiment ID: RT-2376-1\nMachine: RT-098X\nTest Subject: Worster Edmond\nProcedure: Utilized the surgical module on the machine to remove part of the subject's lung tissue.\nObjective: <color=#CA2E0AFF>To treat the subject's pulmonary infection.</color>\nResult: Successful\n...",
    ["LetterText209503"]="September 28, AW1002\nExperiment ID: RT-2684-3\nMachine: RT-140X\nTest Subject: Dave Samo\nProcedure: Utilized a mental filter to hypnotize and address the subject's traumatic recollections.\nObjective: <color=#CA2E0AFF>To reduce the subject's mental stress index to normal levels for self-healing.</color>\nResult: Unsuccessful\n...",
    ["LetterText209601"]="\"Cultural Administration Archive (Newspapers and Magazines)\"\nID: 89757\nPublication Name: Rekenber Times Weekly\nPublication Number: PRX/9930502-M\nIssued Date: May 18, AW993\nValidity Period: 30 Years\nNote: Non-profit publication; for <color=#CA2E0AFF>internal distribution</color> only; <color=#CA2E0AFF>sales prohibited</color>.\n...",
    ["LetterText209701"]="100,000 Zeny is stashed as promised in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the depths of Nogg Cave</color>. Whoever finds this note, retrieve it quickly.\n\n(This short message is signed with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp</color> logo. You don't quite get it, but you know going to the cave now is suicide, so you should look elsewhere for <color=#CA2E0AFF>clues</color> first...)",
    ["LetterText209801"]="Dear Adventurer,\nPlease treat this letter as a face-to-face farewell. Sorry to say goodbye like this, but by the time you read this, 140 will likely be no more. Don't be sad for me. Right from the start, when you and Dave returned to \"Paradise,\" I knew everything from his memories and foresaw my fate. I've never regretted my choice, and I believe you haven't either. It’s a shame... after today, we won't be able to chat about the future together.\nAdventurer, I'm so happy to have you as my friend. Even though we haven't known each other long, you're the only one who considered me an equal. As a token of my appreciation, I've left you a gift. You should have found it with this letter—it's my heart, 140's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mech Core</color>. While I couldn't keep my word to help you uncover evidence against Rekenber Corp, this Mech Core should help you in some way. I hope you make good use of it.",
    ["LetterText210001"]="To the next conquered soul:\n\nSurrender! I am the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vanguard</color> of Ken-Oh Raoh, \"The Conqueror of Century's End.\" I am here to establish a new reign under his command! Resistance and struggle are futile. It is the nature of the weak to fear the strong, and it is the fate of the weak to be conquered by the strong. Even in a different world, our iron hooves will remain undefeated! Future opponent, if you have survived the arrow bearing this message, then choose between surrender or annihilation and walk the path of life or death!\n\nKen-Oh Raoh's First Vanguard",
    ["LetterText210101"]="Dear the Successor of Odin's Bloodline,\nGreetings. Sorry to bother you during your rest, but an <color=#CA2E0AFF>important guest</color> is visiting the Lord's Mansion today. The meeting concerns the <color=#CA2E0AFF>task</color> you accepted earlier, so I hope you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>stop by in two hours</color>. I'll be waiting.\nCarl",
    ["LetterText210102"]="Tour: His & Her Poetry\n—Orfeo & Trinity\nDate: XX.XX.X\nTime:XX:XX-?\nTicket Price (Zeny): 888/1,288/1,688/2,588\nOrganizer: Gilded Rose",
    ["LetterText210103"]="Pope's Hymn: Prologue\nSt Isumia, the first to bear the crown of faith...\nHeeding Freyja's divine whisper, she set forth from her homeland...\nFrom Midgard to Rachel, she walked the path of destiny, and in her hands, alchemy bloomed...\nShe cast out despair and darkness, bringing forth gold and wisdom...\nPraise the Pope, praise St. Isumia!\n(Countless lines of embellished praise follow—skipping for your sanity.)",
    ["LetterText210104"]="Dear Mr. Syphus, Due to the travel restrictions in Einbroch, Trinity and I, along with the others, had no choice but to reroute through Rachel. We're staying at an inn in Rachel and wanted to update you on the situation. We plan to head to Lighthalzen after some rest. Once we get there safely, we'll send another message.\nBest regards, Orfeo",
    ["LetterText210105"]="Yus Amar—The \"Iron-Blooded\" Priest With A Warm Heart\"\n\nFifteen days ago, on the fateful \"Night of Lament,\" tragedy struck—the western nomads slaughtered Commander Rossin and his elite warriors in a merciless attack. Anger swept through the nation, demanding swift vengeance, even the complete removal of the nomads from the land. But amidst the cries for blood, one man stood firm—\"Iron-Blooded Priest\" Yus Amar. Instead of fueling the flames of war, <color=#CA2E0AFF>he chose peace, insisting that the cycle of violence must end and that no more \"Rossins\" should fall</color>.\"\n",
    ["LetterText210107"]="Q: Yus, word has it that after the \"Night of Lament,\\' you pushed hard for reconciliation with the nomads—even surviving an assassination attempt from those who disagreed with you. What's your take on all this?\nA: Peace always comes at a cost—that's something Rossin and I both understood. But as a follower of Freyja, I believe it's time for a change. The nomads don't need suppression; they need reassurance. That's why our future policies will focus more on diplomacy rather than suppression—something my predecessor never tried. I just hope people will support this path.",
    ["LetterText210108"]="Q: The person responsible for Commander Rossin's murder was executed yesterday, and there's now an official plan to develop the nomadic settlements. Was this your idea?\nA: We're also working on providing jobs for the nomads and helping them integrate into Arunafeltz's way of life. Once they come to share our devotion to Freyja, they'll understand why the people mourned so deeply. After all, the Goddess loves everyone equally, and she grieves for every life lost.",
    ["LetterText210109"]="Q: How long do you think change will take?\nA: As soon as we let go of old grudges, change will come. Arguing over who was right or wrong won't bring back the dead. So let's stop the mourning with yesterday and end the hatred with our generation. I swear, as the \"Iron-Blooded Priest,\" <color=#CA2E0AFF>I won't walk the same path as Commander Rossin</color>.",
    ["LetterText210110"]="Big Reward! The Drosera King of Rachel Plains!\nDifficulty: Super Hard!\nPayout: Super Generous!\nTarget: (A wonky doodle of a Drosera)\nMission: Seeking a powerful Adventurer to accompany the client in capturing the Drosera King in the Rachel Plains. Generous reward guaranteed upon success. No amateurs!\nClient: The adorable Mercy!\nContact Info: Juno University—xxxxxxx",
    ["LetterText210111"]="Drosera King Observation Log\n\n1/xx/xx Clear\nToday marks the first day of observing the Drosera. In addition to the regular doses of calming potion and nutrient solution, I placed it under the sun—it needs warmth to stay healthy!\n\n2/xx/xx Clear\nThe leaves are looking a bit wilted... Did I not use enough nutrient solution? But I followed the directions precisely! Maybe this oversized variant just needs a bit more?\n",
    ["LetterText210112"]="3/xx/xx Cloudy\nThe Drosera's withering condition remains unchanged. Its leaves are starting to curl and turn yellow—definitely getting worse. Something's seriously wrong. I mean, it's getting everything it needs: sun, water, nutrients... So why is it dying?\n\n4/xx/xx Overcast\nI cut back on the calming potion today to test it out. It woke up and bit me!",
    ["LetterText210113"]="Patrol Manual\n0:00-6:00\nUnit 1 Rachel Gate\nUnit 2 Rachel Plains\nUnit 3/15 Grey Wolf Village, Mining Area\n\n6:00-12:00\nUnit 4/5/6 Rachel Gate\nUnit 7/8 Eastern Plains, Western Plains\nUnit 9/10 Southern Plains, Northern Plains\nUnit 11/12 Grey Wolf Village, Mining Area\nUnit 13 Ice Cave\n",
    ["LetterText210114"]="12:00-18:00\nUnit 14/15/1 Rachel Gate\nUnit 2/3 Eastern Plains, Western Plains\nUnit 4/5 Southern Plains, Northern Plains\nUnit 6/7 Grey Wolf Village, Mining Area\nUnit 8 Ice Cave\n\n18:00-24:00\nUnit 9/10 Rachel Gate\nUnit 11/12 Rachel Plains\nUnit 13/14 Grey Wolf Village, Mining Area",
    ["LetterText210115"]="7/xx/xx Overcast\nI haven't been in the mood to write lately. Partly because I've been verifying the data, but mostly because I still can't accept the possibility that the Drosera... may not be a plant at all.\nIt has actual breathing and digestive organs! It ate a chunk of my burger patty that fell on the ground... and later, it pooped. How could this be happening?! What am I supposed to do about my essay? Can I still unravel the secret of its longevity and apply it to desertification control?",
    ["LetterText210116"]="8/xx/xx Rain\nIt's still lively, even in the rain. The way its stem moves—like it's breathing—plants aren't supposed to do that, right? It's obsessed with my burger patty, by the way.\nMaybe I've been wrong all along. What if it's actually an animal?\nI'm hoping Professor Viola's analysis proves me wrong. Fingers crossed.",
    ["LetterText210117"]="A long, long time later, a faint light finally appeared on the dark, lamp-less path.\n\nThe prince stopped walking and saw the Lord of the Underworld appear again, leading the princess' soul—and smiling faintly at him from afar.\n\n\"Dear prince,\" she said, her eyes glinting with malice, \"I came all this way just to return your beloved's soul.\"\n\nThe Lord of the Underworld gave the unconscious princess a gentle push. The noble girl stumbled forward, arms open, as if asking the prince for a warm hug.\n\nHer eyes sparkled like jewels, her lips soft and rosy like petals. It felt like she had a thousand things to say to the prince—all filled with longing.\n\n\n",
    ["LetterText210118"]="The Lord of the Underworld watched with satisfaction. \"Look, this is your true love. You walked through the darkness and didn't even check if you'd left the most precious thing behind?\"\n\n\"I saw it myself—a demon took the princess without a sound. That's why I waited for you at the exit.\"\n\"Prince,\" she urged again, \"take a good look at what you're carrying. Is that really the princess? If it's not... she might never wake up again.\"\n\n\"Hurry up,\" the Lord of the Underworld thought to herself.\n\n",
    ["LetterText210119"]="One glance—that's all it takes. You'd be trapped here forever, bound as my servants.\n\nBut the handsome prince didn't do what she hoped.\n\nAs the \"princess\" watched in disappointment, the prince passed the demon by—carrying the one he truly loved.\n\nAt the gate to the living world, bathed in light, the prince looked down at the wicked Lord of the Underworld—and declared his love for the princess.\n\n\"O Lord of the Underworld, you can stop lying to me.\"\n\n\"How could I ever forget the face of the one I'm meant to spend my life with?\"",
    ["LetterText210120"]="A.W.XX, Thanatos sealed away the Demon King Morroc. Yet his beloved partner and wife, Lush, lay grievously wounded. No healing could save her—she drew her final breath, cradled in his arms. Stricken with sorrow, the hero who once sealed evil became a maddened Demon Swordsman...",
    ["LetterText210121"]="To our dearest child,\nForgive us, my child—for fate has chosen this cruel way to make us miss your birthday once more. We left some gifts at the bottom of this suitcase—hope you'll like them. We always thought there was more time—to make up for the distance between us. But we forgot that fate has its own plans.\nDeath may take our lives, but it can never take away a parent's love for their child. Barr Venter, our brave child—strength shines in you, but we fear that our absence may leave you in silence, your heart closed to the world. We're sorry—for placing the burden of our work on you and taking away your childhood. Could time be undone, our only wish would be for your laughter to echo in open fields—not lost beneath piles of cold, lifeless data.\nBut time doesn't rewind. Even if we've emptied the document box you loathed, the moments we missed... are still gone. Remember Tamaureen, the mechanical maid we built together? She'll take care of you now. Trust her—let her take you out, meet people, maybe even... find someone special?\nAnd in the end, do not lay blame upon the airship office—this was merely fate's cruel hand. If someone must be taken, let it be us, the ones who changed our flight. Our lives will live on in you, Barr Venter. And your future will shine far brighter than ours. Even from the heavens—we shall love you, endlessly, eternally.\nWith undying love, Your Father and Mother",
    ["LetterText210122"]="\"Happiness lies straight ahead.\"\n\n\"But if we turn back, it's nothing but a bottomless pit.\"\n\nNo matter how the Lord of the Underworld screamed, threatened, or begged, he never once looked back.\n\nAnd at the story's end... the king gave them a wedding fit for legends. In that castle, the prince and princess lived out their days in joy—forever and always.\n\n—The End\nWritten by Hans Christian\n",
    ["LetterText210201"]="Math Exercise",
    ["LetterText210202"]="7-6=2 (×)\n3+14=18 (×)\n8+12+5=28 (×)\n88+11=90 (×)\n...",
    ["LetterText210301"]="Sacred Codex, Chapter I, Verse III",
    ["LetterText210302"]="...\nFrom the southeast, the envoy of the divine shall descend,\nbearing divine blessings to bathe the world in light.\nAll who follow shall be counted among the chosen,\nand all they desire—be it thought, dream, or plea—shall be made real.\nBut the <color=#CA2E0AFF>savage</color> and the stray shall be cast as <color=#CA2E0AFF>heretics</color>,\nand stripped of all that they see, all they hear, all they know... and all they ever held dear.\n...",
    ["LetterText210401"]="Sacred Codex, Chapter I, Verse V",
    ["LetterText210402"]="\nThe Lord bestowed upon her the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heron's Feather</color>,\nto call forth rain upon barren lands.\nHe granted her <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ktullanux</color>,\nto crush the wicked demons to naught but ash.\nHe gave unto her the <color=#CA2E0AFF>scepter</color>, the throne, and the sanctum,\nto lead the faithful toward triumph—\n...",
    ["LetterText210501"]="Chronicles of Arunafeltz",
    ["LetterText210502"]="... A.W.400 marked the beginning of a new century—and the arrival of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>chosen one</color> who would change everything. Her name was <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isumia</color>. A simple nun born in Glast Heim, she could no longer stay silent while Odin turned a blind eye to the pain of his followers. Moved by her sincere prayers, the great <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Freyja</color> descended a miracle. Guided by divine revelation, Isumia left the forsaken lands of Odin and, with her earliest followers, established a new kingdom blessed by the Goddess...",
    ["LetterText210601"]="Targeted Study on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Religious Revolution</color> of the Rune-Midgard Kingdom",
    ["LetterText210602"]="... The religious revolution that swept through the Rune-Midgard Kingdom has been shrouded in controversy for generations. Many records were <color=#CA2E0AFF>stolen</color> or lost to <color=#CA2E0AFF>destruction</color>, leaving behind only fragmented memories among the people—memories of a nun named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isumia</color>. She came from Glast Heim and remained obscure in Prontera, even overshadowed by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eryxis</color>, who hadn't yet been baptized. And yet, it was this overlooked nun who ultimately ignited a sweeping revolution that <color=#CA2E0AFF>fractured the faith</color>.",
    ["LetterText210701"]="...\nI'm begging you—stop praying to me... This is not a miracle. Every wish <color=#CA2E0AFF>comes with a price</color>!",
    ["LetterText210702"]="...\nIt's finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>my turn</color>. I'm dying...",
    ["LetterText210703"]="...\n(This page is blank, except for a rough sketch of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>feather</color> and a huge <color=#CA2E0AFF>X</color>.)",
    ["LetterText210704"]="...\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Silvio</color>, I miss you so much...",
    ["LetterText210705"]="...\nDear god, please forgive me...",
    ["LetterText210801"]="<size=26>Malam...\nI love you.</size>\n\n(This parchment bears only those few words. The handwriting is messy and fragmented, maybe written with the last of her strength.)",
    ["LetterText210901"]="Experiment ID: 4439-D\nTest Subject: No. 681\nResult: Failure. The body has been transferred to the Ice Cave as per protocol.",
    ["LetterText211001"]="Experiment ID: 577-C\nTest Subject: No. 118\nResult: Failure. Survived but suffered irreversible mutation and complete mental breakdown. The body has been transferred to the Ice Cave as per protocol.",
    ["LetterText211101"]="Experiment ID: 103-A\nTest Subject: <color=#CA2E0AFF>No. 7</color>\nResult: Successful. The subject adapted well to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fission reagent</color>, demonstrating physical capabilities <color=#CA2E0AFF>five to six</color> times beyond average human and a strong affinity with <color=#CA2E0AFF>fire attribute</color>. The subject has passed all Trails in the Underground Arena and will be transferred to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim Institute</color>in seven days.",
    ["LetterText211201"]="In the sacred presence of the Goddess,\nand by the authority of the twenty-fourth Pope of Arunafeltz,\nI hereby declare:\nHenceforth, all who <color=#CA2E0AFF>hold faith in the Goddess</color> shall be counted among her chosen.\nThey shall be granted <color=#CA2E0AFF>everlasting freedom</color>, and the sacred right to defend it.\nThey shall <color=#CA2E0AFF>stand as equals</color>, no longer bound by titles, ranks, or noble blood.\nThey shall hold dominion over their <color=#CA2E0AFF>wealth and lives</color>, and gain the means for <color=#CA2E0AFF>learning and sustenance</color>.\nThey shall receive the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess' love—equal and unjudged</color>—as all others do.\n...",
    ["LetterText211301"]="Shipping List (To Rachel)\n8/17\nR-series Automatic Rifle x300\nTwin-Edged Combat Knives x720\nShield Gauntlets x420\n...\n9/26\nCollapsible Compound Bows x150\nReinforced Exosuit Armor x210\nAssorted-Caliber Rounds x450\n...\n10/7\nInfantry-Class Long Spear x530\nAmplification Staff x330\n...\n\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>*Note: Total payment of 5,600,000 Zeny has been received in full.</color>",
    ["LetterText211401"]="9/3 Sunny\nI didn't finish my homework again. Teacher Jude's gonna scold me. But it's not like I want to sleep all day! I just... can't help it...",
    ["LetterText211402"]="9/11\nNeirun said I mumbled weird stuff again in my sleep today... but this time felt different. I still don't remember what I did, but... I think I heard <color=#CA2E0AFF>my brother's voice</color>...",
    ["LetterText211403"]="9/19\n... So sleepy... I can't stay awake... just for today...",
    ["LetterText211404"]="(The diary's entries are simple—just like a ten-year-old girl's thoughts. But... who is this <color=#CA2E0AFF>brother</color>?)",
    ["LetterText212501"]="The living pain, forgotten—\nThe undead revelry, gathered—\nThe underworld wine, toasted—\nThe abyssal power, awakened...\n\nSoul of the Offering:\n(An empty space, waiting for the name to be signed...)",
    ["LetterText212601"]="Mysterious Tome",
    ["LetterText212602"]="Through the underworld, wisdom sought;\nFierce winds rage through boundless skies.\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Sacred fire</color> burns the dark to ash,\nVirtue and honor forever remain.",
    ["LetterText212701"]="Dear Adventurer,\nIn accordance with our agreement, I have secured Farbauti and Laufey and entrusted them to an elite courier from the Gilded Rose. They are expected to reach Juno in the coming days. Upon their arrival, please hand this sealed letter to the courier as proof of delivery.\nSincerely, Malam\n(A vivid <color=#CA2E0AFF>wax rose</color> blooms at the end of the letter, which should be the seal of the Gilded Rose Trading Company.)",
    ["LetterText212801"]="Rekensheim Institute—Temporary Visitor Log",
    ["LetterText212802"]="A.W.1003 April 29\nVistor: Eva Taylor\nPurpose: Business Consultation\nReceived By: Isabella Martinez\nTemporary Access: Information Department Meeting Room / Primary Laboratory\n...",
    ["LetterText212803"]="A.W.1003 May 8\nVistor: Liam Smith\nPurpose: Business Consultation\nReceived By: Sherlon\nTemporary Access: Central Conference Room / Logistics Office\n...",
    ["LetterText212804"]="A.W.1003 June 17\nVistor: █████████\nPurpose: Business Consultation\nReceived By: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baroshev</color>\nTemporary Access: Maximum Clearance\n...\n\n(On the final page, the visitor's name has been completely <color=#CA2E0AFF>erased</color>. You see a familiar name appear next to \"Received By.\" And the date... It's from just over half a month ago, the very day you and Martistine departed for Rachel...)",
    ["LetterText212901"]="(A finely crafted little card, its gold thread outlining a figure wearing a deerstalker hat and holding a pipe. Beneath it are the words: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Detective</color>.)",
    ["LetterText213001"]="Chronicles of the Schwarzwald Republic",
    ["LetterText213002"]="... A.W.715, the Schwarzwald Republic was shaken by the most catastrophic uprising in its history—triggered by the androids engineered by the Rekenber Corp. Since the second technological leap, under the leadership of \"Father of Machines\" Barr Venter, the Republic rapidly industrialized its android industry. These mech creatures, vastly cheaper than human labor, became essential to both civil and military production. Their efficiency propelled the nation's productivity to new heights—yet, in doing so, they displaced countless workers. Within mere years, the resulting social conflict reached a breaking point.",
    ["LetterText213003"]="In the end, the Tyr Mercenary, which had cooperated with the Republic for nearly two centuries, was the first to strike. In an act of mutual destruction, they destroyed the Rekensheim Institute and demanded that the Republic dismantle all military androids and restore the mercenary order. A year later, the rebellion was suppressed—but perhaps to remember the catastrophe it brought, the Rekenber Corp kept the ruins intact, sealing them off and building a new research facility atop the wreckage...",
    ["LetterText213101"]="Project Y.H. Experiment Logs",
    ["LetterText213102"]="A.W.10XX\nThird Adaptation Experiment. Subject 77 perished upon administration of the Fission Reagent. Subjects 56 and 27 exhibit full compatibility, transferred to Observation Sector.",
    ["LetterText213103"]="A.W.10XX\nAll subjects deceased. The Third Adaptation Experiment is a failure. Preparations for the Fourth Adaptation Experiment initiated.",
    ["LetterText213104"]="A.W.10XX\nAn S-Rank compatible subject identified. Emergency procedures engaged...",
    ["LetterText213201"]="... She fainted again. The doctor says she might not live to celebrate her tenth birthday. Odin... why must You do this to my child...? No. I've made up my mind. I'll keep her—I'll save her my own way.",
    ["LetterText213202"]="Mysterious Notes",
    ["LetterText7006011"]="The deposit is enclosed with the letter. Please retrieve the <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 Alchemy Devices located at the South and West Gates of Prontera</color>. I'll be awaiting your return at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>, where I'll reward you with the rest of your fee.",
    ["LetterTitle104001"]="Dear Adventurer,",
