    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_001"]="Collect Floating Lamp",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_002"]="Wealthy",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_003"]="Knowledgeable",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_004"]="Odin Hobbyist",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_005"]="Pet Lover",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_006"]="Skilled Craftsmen",
    ["LoiKratongTaskDes_007"]="Floating Lamp Wish",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_001"]="Collect Floating Lamps to exchange for Beautiful Floating Lamps",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_002"]="Total Diamonds Topped Up During Event",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_003"]="Total number of OX questions answered correctly",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_004"]="Total Odin Consumption",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_005"]="Total Pet Captures",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_006"]="Total Crafted Floating Lamps",
    ["LoiKratongTaskName_007"]="Total Beautiful Floating Lamps Used",
    ["LoiKratongTips_001"]="Event Rules: \n·The event is divided into the Event Phase and Reward Claiming Phase.\n\n·During the Event Phase, the progress of the Charming Lantern quest will be tallied normally, and rewards can still be collected. There will be additional rewards for Carnival Activity. Use Odin's Blessing to kill monsters above Lv.25 to get extra materials to craft Small Floating Lamps.\n\n·During the Reward Claiming Phase, players can still use/exchange Beautiful Floating Lamps, craft Small Floating Lamps, claim completed task rewards, and purchase Floating Lamp Gift Packs. The quests in the Charming Lantern will no longer be counted in the progress.\n\n·Beautiful Floating Lamps can only be used by the river next to the Wishing Tree at Prontera South Gate. There is a chance to get the Floating Lantern Festival limited \"Fairy Rabbit\" Pet or \"Moony Osmanthus\" Mount. On your 50th and 150th use, you are guaranteed to get either the \"Fairy Rabbit\" or \"Moony Osmanthus\" Mount. On your 250th use, you are guaranteed to get the \"Moony Osmanthus\" Mount. After which, every 250 times you use the Beautiful Floating Lamps, you will receive an additional \"Moony Osmanthus\" Mount. (Fairy Rabbit and Moony Osmanthus obtained from the Beautiful Floating Lamps are both unbound.)",
    ["LoiKratongTips_002"]="Spend <color=#CA2E0AFF>%s</color> Diamonds to purchase the gift pack?",
    ["LoiKratongTips_003"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>%s</color> Total Premium Floating Lamps Used\nLamp rewards guarantee cycles: 50/150/250 (every 250 uses)",
    ["LoiKratongTips_004"]="Total of <color=#CA2E0AFF>%s</color> made!",
    ["LoiKratongTips_005"]="Event Time: %s (Rewards Claim Ends: %s)",
    ["LoiKratongTips_006"]="Buy Limit Today: <size=22>%s</size>",
    ["LoiKratongTips_007"]="Mission Stopped",
    ["LongTime"]="Longer Time",
    ["Loop_Title_1497"]="Emilia's Fan — Emilia's Fan",
    ["Loop_Title_1498"]="Subaru Natsuki's Fan — Subaru Natsuki's Fan",
    ["Loop_Title_1499"]="Rem's Fan — Rem's Fan",
    ["LotteryEventTips1"]="Adventurer %s's character's Base Level has reached Lv.%s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips10"]="Adventurer %s used the Card Vending Machine and drew %s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips11"]="Adventurer %s used the Skill Book Vending Machine and drew %s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips2"]="Adventurer %s successfully advanced to the %s class!",
    ["LotteryEventTips3"]="Adventurer %s's equipment refining level has reached Lv.%s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips4"]="Adventurer %s killed %s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips5"]="Adventurer %s caught %s from fishing with rare bait!",
    ["LotteryEventTips6"]="Adventurer %s completed today's %s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips7"]="Adventurer %s completed %s COC Missions!",
    ["LotteryEventTips8"]="Adventurer %s used the Equipment Vending Machine and drew a %s!",
    ["LotteryEventTips9"]="Adventurer %s used the Headgear Vending Machine and drew a %s!",
    ["LotterySumTips1"]="Total Number of People Whose Character Base Level Reached Lv.%s This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips10"]="Total Number of Rare Cards Drawn from the Card Vending Machine This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips11"]="Total Number of Rare Skill Books Drawn from the Skill Book Vending Machine This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips2"]="Total Number of Adventurers Who Undertook First Job Advancement This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips3"]="Total Number of Adventurers Whose Equipment Refining Level Reached Lv.This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips4"]="Total Number of Times Killed by %s This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips5"]="Total Number Of Adventurers Who Caught Rare Costumes This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips6"]="Total Number Of Adventurers Who Completed the %s Event This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips7"]="Total Number Of Adventurers Who Completed %s COC Missions This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips8"]="Total Amount of Rare Equipment Drawn from the Equipment Vending Machine This Week: %s",
    ["LotterySumTips9"]="Total Amount of Rare Headgear Drawn from the Headgear Vending Machine This Week: %s",
    ["LotteryTicketsTips001"]="Haven't played the Lucky Lottery yet? What are you waiting for!? Participate now for a chance to win huge prizes!",
    ["LotteryTicketsTips002"]="There's still %s minutes left until the Lucky Lottery begins! Are you ready, Adventurer?",
    ["LotteryTicketsTips003"]="The Lucky Lottery is now underway! Open the event screen to check it out!",
    ["LotteryTicketsTips004"]="Lucky Adventurer %s was the first to guess all of the lucky numbers in the current Lucky Lottery event! Next time, it could be you!",
    ["LotteryTips1"]="You cannot place any bets!",
    ["LotteryTips10"]="Unlocked!",
    ["LotteryTips11"]="You currently have a number bar that has been unlocked but not wagered. Are you sure you want to close it?",
    ["LotteryTips12"]="You can only Hobnob with the Lucky once each day!",
    ["LotteryTips13"]="Unable to view target information!",
    ["LotteryTips14"]="Please enter your bet number!",
    ["LotteryTips15"]="Please unlock the previous number selection area first!",
    ["LotteryTips2"]="This is the Kafra VIP channel!",
    ["LotteryTips3"]="Insufficient currency!",
    ["LotteryTips4"]="You cannot unlock this!",
    ["LotteryTips5"]="Phase %s",
    ["LotteryTips6"]="This phase's Kingdom Quiz rewards are on the way! Please wait a while longer!",
    ["LotteryTips7"]="Lucky Number No.%s for this phase's Kingdom Quiz is %s! Did you guess correctly?",
    ["LotteryTips8"]="Nobody won the prize!",
    ["LotteryTips9"]="Are you sure you want to spend %s %s to unlock the number bar and take part in the quiz?",
    ["LuckyRefineTips1"]="If equipment refinement fails, you will get Luck.",
    ["LuckyRefineTips2"]="Failing to refine a weapon will produce Weapon Refinement Luck. Failing to refine armor will produce Armor Refinement Luck. Failing to refine an accessory will produce Accessory Refinement Luck.",
    ["LuckyRefineTips3"]="After accumulating a certain amount of Luck, you can use Lucky Refinement. Lucky Refinement will increase the success rate of refining to 100%.",
    ["LuckyRefineTips4"]="Different qualities and types of equipment will give different amount of Luck when refinement fails and so the amount of Luck needed for Lucky Refinement will be different as well.",
    ["LuckyRefineTitle"]="Lucky Refinement",
    ["MVPActivityTips_1"]="Dormant",
    ["MVPActivityTips_10"]="At 06:00 (UTC+7) each day, a random selection of bosses will be scheduled to spawn and enter a countdown timer.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_11"]="Defeating bosses will remain dormant for the day. Defeating a boss that wasn't selected to spawn for the day will cause it to immediately enter dormancy.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_12"]="A daily curfew is in effect from 00:00 to 06:00 (UTC+7). During this time, defeating any boss will send it directly into dormancy.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_13"]="%s's reward is as follows:",
    ["MVPActivityTips_2"]="In Combat",
    ["MVPActivityTips_3"]="1. Each boss now drops significantly more rare rewards and will also drop MVP/MINI Reward Boxes.\n2. There's a curfew from 02:00 to 06:00 (UTC+7), please check the details page for the rules.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_4"]="MVP/MINI Rewards",
    ["MVPActivityTips_5"]="The settlement will take place when the MVP dies, and only the top 15 parties in terms of damage dealt will participate in the distribution of MVP/MINI rewards. If all members within a top-15 party have 0 remaining rare reward chances that party will not be allowed to participate in the distribution, and the next party in rank order will be considered.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_6"]="Getting MVP/MINI rewards costs rare reward chances. Party members with 0 remaining rare reward chances or who have already received a rare reward during this kill will not participate in the distribution.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_7"]="The settlement will take place when the MVP dies, and only the top 15 parties in terms of damage dealt will participate in the distribution of MVP/MINI rewards. If all members within a top-15 party have 0 remaining rare reward chances, that party will not be allowed to participate in the distribution, and the next party in rank order will be considered. Rewards from the event-exclusive MVP do not consume the chance.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_8"]="Party members with 0 remaining rare reward chances or who have already received a rare reward during this kill or whose damage contribution is less than 0.1% will not participate in the distribution, and their contributed damage will not be factored into the weightage allocation.",
    ["MVPActivityTips_9"]="Curfew",
    ["MVPDes_21030"]="The leader and mother of all Hornets. One Mistress is enough for a colony to develop. The Mistress represents both power and beauty in the Hornet tribe. Its stinger has evolved to become a stinging ring that dances lethally in the Abyssal Arcade.",
    ["MVPDes_21031"]="The original meaning of \"Phreeoni\" is \"devouring the sky\". Its tongue and huge mouth full of sharp teeth makes it look as though it wants to swallow everything in the world. Legend has it that it was a hero who was cursed by the Poison Dragon. He now roams the Abyssal Arcade endlessly. If you do not want to become its food, you better be careful.",
    ["MVPDes_21032"]="The overlord of the seas crowned with the name of \"Kraken.\" Rumor has it that not one of those who saw its third eye has managed to escape the maelstrom. The great waves in Abyssal Arcade will rise because of it.",
    ["MVPDes_21033"]="The Eddga warrior who sees gentility and fighting as faith was seen in Abyssal Arcade. The Pipe in its hand is not just for smoking and posing. If you have the misfortune of becoming his opponent, do be careful.",
    ["MVPDes_21034"]="The ruler of the Ant Cavern. There are rumors about it once being a possessed Mage who could no longer recover her original form after regaining control over her body and ended up becoming a real Maya. Her bewitching yet beautiful figure charms every living being in Abyssal Arcade.",
    ["MVPDes_21035"]="The strongest Orc Warrior in Abyssal Arcade. His hair is an extraordinarily vibrant red in a visual rock style. He welcomes the strong to challenge him and never stoops to despicable means. A fair fight is what brings Orcs honor.",
    ["MVPDes_21036"]="An unrivaled king of strength. Even in Abyssal Arcade, the heads hanging from his waist foretell the future of those who dare to challenge the chief...",
    ["MVPDes_21037"]="An ancient ruler of the deserts. He searches Abyssal Arcade for his forgotten past. Even if he no longer possesses the glamor from his past, a Pharaoh's dignity is not something that can be challenged.",
    ["MVPDes_30001"]="This kind and carefree monster is valkyrie's pet. It was left behind in Midgard and enjoys helping adventurers grow, provided they pass its test of strength.",
    ["MVPDes_30003"]="The embodiment of humanity's evilness, this immortal creature loves to play pranks. Its life motto is \"Become badder each day.\"",
    ["MVPDes_30007"]="The queen bee. She holds command over the entire bee tribe and is crucial to their unity and prosperity. She is adept at confusing her opponents, and one should not underestimate her strength.",
    ["MVPDes_30008"]="Once a hero, until one day he was cursed by the Poison Dragon. An insatiable hunger consumed him and he became a powerful monster with a huge, horrendous maw.",
    ["MVPDes_30009"]="The mother of all ants and the rightful queen of Ant Hell. Do not be taken captive by her beauty, or you will become food for her children.",
    ["MVPDes_30010"]="A strong yet gentlemanly beastman that is always seen wearing a top hat and smoking a pipe. It also seems to be familiar with the human language.",
    ["MVPDes_30012"]="This orc abides by the warrior's code and has been granted the title of \"Hero.\" He is a symbol of his entire tribe's honor and strength, for he is the strongest among his kind.",
    ["MVPDes_30014"]="Once the restless Undead Doppelgangers have you in their grasp, you must be careful not to let them discover your weakness, lest the cold, dark grip of their Undead Aura consume you...",
    ["MVPDes_30015"]="The chief of the orc tribe. Though old, he still possesses great strength. The heads hanging from his waist foretell the future of those who dare to challenge the chief...",
    ["MVPDes_30017"]="An ancient ruler of the deserts. When he was young, he lost his way in the labyrinth of the Sphinx and lost his name and identity, along with his sense of time...",
    ["MVPDes_30019"]="The powerful demon king who was once sealed has never given up coveting this continent. Brave adventurers should be guard at all times and prevent the demon king from coming back…",
    ["MVPDes_30020"]="Doomed to an eternity of tragic hubris, greed and blind ambition drive him to wave his scepter with conceit, even after death. Watch out for his deathly shadow, or abandon all hope of survival.",
    ["MVPDes_30021"]="A fallen genius lurks beneath Geffen... From time to time, one can even hear the rumbling of his deep, low breath, accompanied by the frenzied turning of pages...",
    ["MVPDes_30022"]="One of the original twelve <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bishops</color> of Arunafeltz, who is highly respected and has many followers. During his youth, he traveled around every country. He thought that god had abandoned this land after witnessing countless sufferings among the living beings. Therefore, he wishes to establish an entirely <color=#CA2E0AFF>new religion</color>. He signed a pact with Hel to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sell his soul</color> in order to fulfill his wish. But is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient god</color> he believes capable of restoring order in this world?",
    ["MVPDes_30023"]="The Kraken, as it is called, is a monster that once wreaked havoc on the seas. According to legend, anyone who saw its third eye would not survive the encounter.",
    ["MVPDes_30024"]="A demon with a twisted personality who takes pleasure in bewitching and teasing human beings. It enjoys watching humans fall prey to their desires, believing that this is the ultimate joy of life.",
    ["MVPDes_30025"]="Although this creature who once ruled Comodo a millennium ago has gradually declined after losing the power of dragon flames, it still should not be underestimated.",
    ["MVPDes_30026"]="A knight with high morals. Never betrays the oath he swore even though he had already fallen into the Realm of the Dead. However, Hel, who is fond of observing the sin of humans, is displeased with his acts, and she then exhausts all her might to torture and humiliate this knight. Eventually, all the suffering became a clear mirror that reflects the kindest heart that lies within this knight...\n\"Sword, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Fire</color>. Shield, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Summum Bonum</color>. Use the sword to sunder the sin of all beings and use the shield to bear the pain of all beings.\" —The epitaph on a nameless tome in the Glast Heim Cemetery.",
    ["MVPDes_30031"]="The concentrated energy from instable activities of dimensional gap. Each eye on it stands for a parallel world. It is the guardian of the order of time and space and will not spare anyone who disrupts the order of time and space.",
    ["MVPDes_30032"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Poring family's</color> newest member, who was not included in the family until recently. From a Monsterology perspective, it should have the <color=#CA2E0AFF>same origin as Angeling</color>. However, what confuses every researcher the most is that the two monsters share <color=#CA2E0AFF>almost the same habits and characteristics</color> and live in totally different habitats. There is an ongoing debate in the academic world, and no one can present a plausible answer.\n\"If I can solve this problem, then I must be the winner of the next <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mobel Prize</color> in Monsterology...\" Midnight, inside the lab, a fifty-year-old monster researcher pushes his glasses back to his nose and starts implementing crazy algorithms on the scratch paper.",
    ["MVPDes_30033"]="A rare creature made of <color=#CA2E0AFF>unknown energy</color> that looks like a toy consists of <color=#CA2E0AFF>three cube-shaped blocks</color>. In fact, its body is full of <color=#CA2E0AFF>electric current</color>, making it a hazardous monster. The majority of its life is spent in standby mode, living off <color=#CA2E0AFF>electrons</color> from the surrounding environment. Wakes up only when it's fully charged.\n\"The tiny cubes that float aside the Gioia act like a battery's <color=#CA2E0AFF>positive and negative anodes</color>, responsible for transmitting energy. So, the best way to defeat a Gioia is to break its arms...\" Before entering the ruins, the leader of the expedition draws out a detailed body diagram on a portable blackboard for the teammates on their first mission.",
    ["MVPDes_30034"]="The RSX series, Rekenber Corp's first <color=#CA2E0AFF>semi-automatic mining machine</color>, was a significant milestone in the industrialization reform of the Einbroch mining area. It shone for decades before it gracefully retired to make way for new, fully automated mining robots, and now it's a prized exhibit at a museum. But the most important <color=#CA2E0AFF>RSX-0806 Prototype</color> mysteriously went missing just before it was scheduled to be recycled. Not long after, an engineer responsible for managing the mining area reported seeing the lost RSX-0806 <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep in the mines</color> in a surveillance video, surprisingly, its <color=#CA2E0AFF>operator</color> was...?!\n\"Teacher, does <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pitman</color> actually know how to use these mining machines?\" a boy eagerly questioned in the Einbroch City Library exhibit hall, his eyes wide with wonder.",
    ["MVPDes_30035"]="Over the years, the front desk at the Einbroch Monster Management Bureau has continually received reports of dragons spotted in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nogg Cave</color>. A lot of people think there's a secret <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon nest</color> there, which might be the source of all the dragons that soar above Einbroch Field. However, some <color=#CA2E0AFF>fanatic religious scholars</color> argue that the deep cave leads to the legendary Yggdrasil and that the dragon in question is none other than Nidhoggr, the malevolent dragon perched atop the poisonous glaciers of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hvergelmir</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>feasting on the roots of Yggdrasil</color>.\n\"... And when it severs the root of Yggdrasil, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ragnarok</color> will dawn upon us again! We're doomed... all doomed! Hahahahaha...\" The sound of a forehead repeatedly banging against metal is heard as a madman, admitted nearly three years ago, starts another day of his relentless shrieking and howling...",
    ["MVPDes_30036"]="According to the Mystic Phenomena Research Association, dozens of stories about the Gloom Under Night exist. Some believe it's a demon that clawed its way back from Niflheim's abyss. Others say it's the tormented souls of fallen warriors, twisted into a faceless monster after dying in the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color> fifteen years ago. And then there are those who whisper that the Ice Cave has long been a <color=#44afee>human experiment site</color>, and the Gloom Under Night, it's just one of the <color=#44afee>monsters created by the experiment</color>...",
    ["MVPDes_30037"]="Human <color=#44afee>desires</color> are boundless. And so, the heavens sent forth their <color=#44afee>messenger</color>, to bring <color=#44afee>retribution</color> upon the foolish and the wicked.",
    ["MVPDes_30039"]="<color=#44afee>Goldie Wie</color> was born in the barren desert region of <color=#44afee>Morroc</color>. Once a rising star of the Assassins Guild, she broke their code by <color=#44afee>attacking a merchant caravan</color> and was ultimately exiled. But she wasn't driven by greed; she just couldn't stand by while the poor in the slums suffered from <color=#44afee>hunger and disease</color>. To help them, she became an outlaw, a thief for justice...\n\"If justice fails to protect the weak, then let it be cast aside.\"—Goldie Wie",
    ["MVPDes_30040"]="<color=#44afee>Ivy Flamel</color> is the only son of Nicolas Flamel, the current head of the Alchemist Guild. A <color=#44afee>prodigy</color> studying at Juno University, his intelligence far surpasses ordinary people, giving him limitless potential in alchemy, but also isolating him as someone most would call a <color=#44afee>madman</color>. He seems to have an unusual, unspoken <color=#44afee>obsession</color> with Celia...\n\"Life is infinite, but never repeating.\"—Ivy Flamel",
    ["MVPDes_30090"]="The king had originally planned to save his family and his kingdom... yet after being affected by the 'Starved' skill, he was just too hungry. He swallowed up everything in front of him, including his own ability to govern.",
    ["MVPDes_30091"]="Storm Dragon: A fallen star challenges you. If you are determined to protect this land, you will need courage and strength to face the storm. But as a dragon, Veldora doesn't want to be defeated by you, so be careful.",
    ["MVPDes_30099"]="Nian is a legendary evil beast that raids villages at the end of each year, indiscriminately slaughtering the innocent. It periodically switches its armor attributes, and Fireworks can deal extra damage to it. Remember, when things start to get too dangerous for Nian, it will try to escape!",
    ["MVPDes_30181"]="Using his fairy tale power, Warg's leader enjoys destroying the world of fairy tales. He is unable to endure the transmog power of <color=#5A7D29>Cookie</color>, <color=#ff3300>Christmas Cookie</color>, <color=#FFFF00>Myst Case</color>, and <color=#0033ff>Cruiser</color> and is eventually defeated. Their kinds were then cast out into a far-off snowfield. Having kept a low profile for many years, they plan to launch an all-out attack during Christmas once again.",
    ["MVPDes_30203"]="The strongest creation in the \"House of Evolution.\" Known for its advanced evolutionary state and formidable physical strength, severely lacks a sense of morality. In battle, he triggers \"Carnage Mode,\" forsaking his sanity for a week to vent his primal battle urges. This makes him a highly dangerous experimental entity.",
    ["MVPDes_30204"]="Coming straight out of the \"House of Evolution,\" this freak of nature controls swarms of bloodthirsty mosquitoes to inject energy into her blood, turning herself into a monster. She usually has a sleek, striped appearance in black and white and can control loads of mosquitoes for hunting. But when things get dicey, she goes all out, swelling up with blood to enter a much more powerful second phase.",
    ["MVPDes_30209"]="The Successor of the Nanto Kokaku Ken and the Yosei of the Nanto Rokusei Ken, symbolizing betrayal and beauty. He thinks he's the most handsome and powerful man in the world, yet his true danger lies in his devious and treacherous personality.",
    ["MVPDes_30212"]="The Sin Archbishops of the Witch Cult, representing sloth. He turned extremely paranoid due to the Witch Factor he carries.\nWith powerful and strange abilities, he's the main antagonist hunting down Emilia and her group.",
    ["MVPDes_30213"]="An enormous whale-like Mabeast summoned from another world by the Witch Cult, with a horn on its head and eerie glowing red eyes.\nIt's got a giant pink halo above its head, and its body is covered in white fur and has countless blowholes.\nIt's said to have been created by a powerful figure for special purposes.",
    ["MVPDes_30216"]="Piedmon is a strange-looking and elusive Wizard Digimon shrouded in mystery. Unlike Demon and Undead Digimon, Wizard Digimon are essentially beings from another dimension, their true identities remaining hidden. Neither its motives nor its reason for existing are clear, and nobody has a way to figure it out yet. But one thing's for sure—it's insanely powerful. If you run into Piedmon, well, good luck. All that's left is to curse your fate.",
    ["MVPDes_30217"]="Clad in jet-black clothes, this Fallen Angel Digimon was once a shining Angemon, but got corrupted in some twisted part of the Digital World. That ominous mark on his chest proves it. Devimon's sneaky, brutal—and highly intelligent.",
    ["MVPDes_30218"]="The Dark Demon King of the Demon Realm, Doakudar, commands power on par with the Mashin. With his unholy might, he conquered Mt. Soukai, draining its rainbow colors and sealing away Seiryuhi. Under his oppressive shadow, the people of Mt. Soukai suffer in despair. To Doakudar, the worthless are undeserving of life—not even his own followers or family are spared...",
    ["MVPDes_31001"]="The champion of the Roda Frogs that has slow movements and loves to sing. It claims that its voice is better than the Obeaunes, but the other creatures in the sea beg to differ...",
    ["MVPDes_31002"]="The king of the Poring family. Donning a regal mantle and crown, the way it leads the Little Porings to battle is a truly majestic sight to behold.",
    ["MVPDes_31004"]="A elite among the Chonchons and a talented combatant. Its nimble physique allows it to assassinate swiftly and silently.",
    ["MVPDes_31005"]="A wicked, lone wolf that was exiled from the pack for killing its own kind. Wandering in the deserts alone for a long period leads it to become more cunning and vicious.",
    ["MVPDes_31006"]="A Lunatic covered in blue fur. Although it looks as innocent and harmless as the others, it is advisable to avoid provoking it...",
    ["MVPDes_31008"]="The hatred of restless spirits taken form, roaming eternally in a shipwreck and refuse to leave. Just by being close to it, one will be engulfed by strong, negative emotions, so do not approach it without extreme caution.",
    ["MVPDes_31009"]="This giant monster hidden at the bottom of the sea is said to have escaped from a cook's wok when it was little. It later mutated to have razor-sharp pincers and impenetrable armor, but its red marks from being scorched are still visible.",
    ["MVPDes_31010"]="The monster has a lion’s head and a goat’s body and can spit fire. It is vicious and bloodthirsty by nature. Everywhere it goes, it turns into a barren landscape, and the only way to kill it is to use the Spear of Graphite to penetrate its throat.",
    ["MVPDes_31011"]="The ominous sword that legend says will lead the world to its doom is nothing more than a mistletoe growing on the edge of the gods' kingdom. It has a shield that is immune to <color=#ff3300>Physical</color> and <color=#0033ff>Magic</color> damage, and breaking it will awaken the strong shadow power lying dormant inside it. It extinguished the life of the God of Light, Baldur, and ignited Ragnarok…",
    ["MVPDes_31012"]="Legend has it that this was the sword of Tyr, the God of War. The blade shines brightly like fire and never rusts. Once unsheathed, blood will inevitably be spilled. It is a magic sword that can bring supreme glory to its wielder, but can also lead them to their destruction.",
    ["MVPDes_31014"]="An apostate who has fallen into depravity after being tempted by demons. No longer faithful to its original beliefs, it has also lost the rationality all human beings have.",
    ["MVPDes_31015"]="Coelacanth is a very <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient</color> monster. It's said that it was born in the poisonous glacier of Hvergelmir and existed even before the time of gods. They wander in Gjoll and <color=#CA2E0AFF>live off the undead</color>, and their sharp jaw teeth can pierce through the <color=#CA2E0AFF>hollow spirits</color> to make them feel the long-forgotten pain once again. This is one of the most horrifying punishments among Niflheim. Hel will dump the sinful undead into Hvergelmir for them to rot in the corrosion from the poison while suffering the unbearable flesh-tearing pain from the Coelacanth...",
    ["MVPDes_31016"]="One of Hel's most important servants, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Executioner of the Underworld</color>, has absolute control over the living and dead. In spite of being Undead, he gives up the appearance of his former life and refuses to discuss it with others. It's said that a servant found a bloodstained <color=#CA2E0AFF>Squire's Medallion</color> in his room while cleaning...\n\"Huh? Naght Sieger? I like how he takes revenge on someone, even on the slightest things... Killing one's own kind is the most beautiful thing humans can do. Ha-ha-ha...\" Lately, whenever someone mentions this newly appointed Executioner of the Underworld to Hel, she shows a delightful smile.",
    ["MVPDes_31017"]="Ever since the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Khayr Estate</color> was invaded, reports have been flying to the guards saying that an <color=#CA2E0AFF>unknown monster</color> with <color=#CA2E0AFF>white wings</color> appears next to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>abandoned dry well</color> in the estate. Strange enough, every single one who has had <color=#CA2E0AFF>eye contact</color> with it loses their memories of the day soon after, and all they recall is a pair of crystal-clear eyes that look down from the sky high above, as if it <color=#CA2E0AFF>stares at the fate among every mortal</color> incessantly.\n\"He equally gives everyone his love and equally grants everyone their death.\" A pale hand gently touches the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious runes</color> carved on the dry well, as the lament fades away in the cold air at night.",
    ["MVPDes_31018"]="Monsters that only exist in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juperos Ruins</color>. They share a face similar to Gioia but lack the cube-shaped arms to transmit energy. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>colloidal substances</color> that structure their bodies have a unique composition, allowing them to reproduce by <color=#CA2E0AFF>self-splitting</color> or become stronger by <color=#CA2E0AFF>devouring their own kind</color>. Those tiny little wings and tails they have are absolutely adorable, and it's said that ornaments made after the appearance of Skeggiold are trendy among young girls.\n\"The latest Skeggiold cushion! Pendant! Earrings! Don't miss out by walking out!\" In the busy market in Juno City, a grocery merchant is selling his latest products tirelessly.",
    ["MVPDes_31019"]="There have been recent sightings of a Queen Scaraba <color=#CA2E0AFF>wandering alone</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch Field</color>, which is pretty rare for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>gregarious</color> Golden Scaraba. Monster researchers believe she could be a former leader who was <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeated</color> in a duel. Golden Scaraba operates under a strict hierarchy, with the queen at the top, and everyone has clear roles and responsibilities. However, if multiple leaders emerge, their pheromones can get mixed up, leading males and workers to abandon their duties, potentially destroying the colony. When this happens, the queens <color=#CA2E0AFF>capable of reproduction</color> will <color=#CA2E0AFF>duel</color> for dominance, with the winner becoming the new leader and the loser <color=#CA2E0AFF>forced to leave the group</color> and live in solitude...",
    ["MVPDes_31020"]="The monsters found deep in Nogg Cave are said to emerge from <color=#CA2E0AFF>magma that's loaded with magic</color>. Their bodies, crystallized from <color=#CA2E0AFF>concentrated magic</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>take in magic</color> through glands on their skin, so their size depends heavily on the concentration of magic in the environment, potentially expanding to many times their original size. When their bodies store nearly too much magic, they <color=#CA2E0AFF>reproduce</color> by <color=#CA2E0AFF>splitting</color>. \n\"I spent three months in Nogg Cave to get this larva! I nearly ended up a snack for that Faceworm Queen! Now, just to soak it in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>high-concentrated magic solution</color>, and then I can cash in big time...\" In a shadowy, damp basement, a poacher was humming away, pouring a colorful liquid into a container holding the larva with his partner.",
    ["MVPDes_31021"]="Ktullanux holds an extremely <color=#44afee>high</color> status in the hearts of the people of Arunafeltz. The teachings of the Freyja say that this <color=#44afee>sacred beast</color> once fought alongside the very first pope to shape the kingdom. After the pope's death, it withdrew to the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color>, watching over generations of successors. Yet, in recent years, something strange has happened. It seems to have faded from public view, and <color=#44afee>no longer answers those who call upon it</color>. Why has it gone silent? What secret lies beneath its eternal slumber?",
    ["MVPDes_31022"]="<color=#44afee>Death</color> is not the end. <color=#44afee>Sleep</color>, my sheep. <color=#44afee>Rest</color>, my sheep. Beyond the veil lies the <color=#44afee>eternal bliss</color> that awaits all.",
    ["MVPDes_31023"]="<color=#44afee>Celia Aide</color> is a sweet and cheerful girl from <color=#44afee>Geffen</color> in the Rune-Midgard Kingdom. She's currently studying abroad at the <color=#44afee>Hubawooz Magic School</color> in Juno. Overflowing with <color=#44afee>curiosity</color>, she loves questioning even the most obvious things and exploring the truth behind them. Unfortunately, that same curiosity often gets her into <color=#44afee>unpredictable</color> danger...\n\"The unknown is the most exciting thing in the world.\"—Celia Aide",
    ["MVPDes_31024"]="<color=#44afee>Kavaski Icarus</color> is one of the top young archers from Payon Archer Village. He's determined to prove his strength, though sometimes, he is too <color=#44afee>narrow-minded</color> to see the bigger picture. To sharpen his skills, he set out on a journey, hoping to one day <color=#44afee>earn the recognition of his master, Sky Euin</color>. But after crossing into the Schwarzwald Republic with his companions, all contact with him was suddenly lost...\n\"I will find what I was truly meant to protect.\"—Kavaski Icarus",
    ["MVPDes_36000"]="The leader of the alien terrorist organization Dark Planet and the culprit of the missing human incident. His proposal to the S.S.S.P. has driven the world into absolute fear and madness, in which he requests half the land of the entire world, or he will wipe out half the population instead.",
    ["MVPDes_36001"]="Alien Adacic is an interplanetary mixed-breed species. Besides being highly intelligent, they also possess a considerable mighty combat power. Hence, the galactic committee never allow them to migrate to other planets. The Alien Adacic discovered during this incident could be one of the not many illegal immigrants.",
    ["MVPFirstHit"]="First Hit Bonus",
    ["MVPKillActivityRule_1"]="Event Rules:\n1. While within the event's Kill Points calculation period, Adventurers can earn points through the following methods each time they engage in an MVP battle:\n1) First Hit Points: In a battle where an MVP/Mini dies, the Adventurer who first deals damage to the MVP/Mini will earn the First Hit Points.\n<color=#ff5252>(If the MVP/Mini escapes mid-battle, the Adventurer who delivers the first hit will be determined again in the next battle until the battle ends.)</color>\n2) Last Hit Points: The Adventurer who delivers the fatal blow to the MVP/Mini will earn the Last Hit Points.\n3) Participation Points: Once the MVP/Mini dies, the Adventurers who were in battle with the MVP/Mini will earn the Participation Points.\n4) Damage Ranking Points: Adventurers will earn points according to the damage ranking of their Party in the current battle.\n\n2. The Kill Points from the current battle = First Hit Points + Last Hit Points + Participation Points + Damage Ranking Points.\n\n3. The sum of an Adventurer's <color=#ff5252>10 highest</color> Kill Points from 5:00 on the day until 5:00 the next day will be the Kill Points for that period. The points will be calculated again for the next day from 5:00 the next day.\n\n4. At the end of the Kill Points calculation period, Adventurers will be ranked and given rewards according to the sum of their Kill Points. Rewards will be sent by mail. (Adventurers who earn the same score will be ranked by who earned the points first, with the earliest score ranking higher.)\n\n5. Only MVP/Minis that spawn in the wild count toward points, and they share the same scoring system. The rules for scoring are as follows:\nSource of Points Points Earned\nFirst Hit 15\nLast Hit 30\nParticipation 5\nNo. 1 in Damage Ranking 50\nNo. 2 in Damage Ranking 46\nNo. 3 in Damage Ranking 43\nNo. 4 in Damage Ranking 40\nNo. 5 in Damage Ranking 36\nNo. 6 in Damage Ranking 33\nNo. 7 in Damage Ranking 30\nNo. 8 in Damage Ranking 26\nNo. 9 in Damage Ranking 23\nNo. 10 in Damage Ranking 20",
    ["MVPKillActivity_1"]="Participate in an MVP kill to earn Kill Points!",
    ["MVPKillActivity_2"]="Event Time: %s",
    ["MVPKillActivity_3"]="Kill Points Calculation Time: %s",
