    ["MieGui_Desc_share"]="Get rewards from your first share each day.",
    ["MieGui_desc"]="Rid the kingdom of monsters, in the name of Midgarts!",
    ["MieGui_help"]="Operation Monster Hunter Rules:\n\n1. During the event, killing <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demon</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demi-Human</color> Monsters can add to Monster Hunting Progress.\n\n2. Points gained depend on the size of the Monsters: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Small Monsters</color> provide 1 point, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Medium Monsters</color> 2 points, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Large Monsters</color> 3 points.\n\n3. Quest Points can be obtained without unlocking Odin's Blessing.\n\n4. Overall Server Progress signals the overall Monster Hunting Progress of all players in the server.\n\n5. Reaching certain points in Overall Server Progress unlocks rewards for all, and reaching the end unlocks hidden events!",
    ["MieGui_server"]="Overall Server Progress",
    ["MieGui_serverDesc"]="Reaching 100% in Overall Server Progress unlocks mysterious events!",
    ["MieGui_subtitle1"]="Until every monster is slain",
    ["MieGui_subtitle2"]="There can be no rest",
    ["MieGui_task"]="Monster Kills (Individual)",
    ["MineStartTips_12816601"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816602"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816603"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.2 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816604"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.2 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816605"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.3 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816608"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.3 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816609"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.4 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816610"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.4 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816611"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.5 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816612"]="The current mining vein can produce Lv.1-Lv.5 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816613"]="The current ore vein can produce Lv.1–Lv.6 Ore. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineStartTips_12816614"]="The current ore vein can produce Lv.1–Lv.7 ores. Please refer to the Mining Encyclopedia for details.",
    ["MineUse_001"]="Smelting Material",
    ["MineUse_002"]="Shadow Equipment Material",
    ["MiniFirstHit"]="First Hit Bonus",
    ["MiniGame_1"]="<color=#71d6c5>%s</color> won the arm wrestling minigame!",
    ["MiniGame_drink_btnName"]="DrinkUp",
    ["MiniLastHit"]="Last Hit Bonus",
    ["MiniLiveDrop"]="Participation Bonus",
    ["MiniRankDrop"]="Damage Ranking Bonus",
    ["MiniRareDrop"]="Rare Bonus",
    ["MiniRules_1"]="Rare Bonus",
    ["MiniRules_10"]="Settles upon the death of the MINI. Adventurers who dealt the last hit to the MINI will receive the reward. MINI of a higher version level yields more MINI Coins; event-exclusive MINI will drop unique event items.",
    ["MiniRules_11"]="You can obtain the Last Hit Reward %s times per day. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not count toward this limit, but there's still a daily cap on them.",
    ["MiniRules_12"]="%s's Last Hit Bonus is as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_13"]="Individual Participation Bonus",
    ["MiniRules_14"]="Settles upon the death of the MINI. Adventurers who were in combat with the MINI and within the MINI's scene before its death can receive rewards. MINI of a higher version level yields more MINI Coins; event-exclusive MINI will drop unique event items.",
    ["MiniRules_15"]="You can obtain the Participation Reward %s times per day. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not count toward this limit, but there's still a daily cap on them.",
    ["MiniRules_16"]="%s's Individual Participation Bonus is as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_17"]="First Hit Bonus",
    ["MiniRules_18"]="Settles upon the death of the MINI. Adventurers who dealt the first hit to the MINI will receive the reward. MINI of a higher version level yields more MINI Coins; event-exclusive MINI will drop unique event items.",
    ["MiniRules_19"]="You can obtain the First Hit Reward %s times per day. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not count toward this limit, but there's still a daily cap on them.",
    ["MiniRules_2"]="This bonus is determined when the Mini dies. Parties are ranked according to the damage they dealt to the Mini itself. The more damage the party dealt, the higher the chance of getting this bonus. The drop rate is shared between all party members who contributed in combat.",
    ["MiniRules_20"]="%s's Discovery Bonus is as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_21"]="Minis that spawn during the in-game morning and daytime drop normal Mini cards. Minis that spawn during the in-game night drop Night Mini cards. Minis that spawn during the Void phenomenon (in-game time does not matter) drop Void Mini cards",
    ["MiniRules_22"]="Bonus Rewards",
    ["MiniRules_23"]="1. Bonus player trigger conditions: Can be triggered when below World level 30.",
    ["MiniRules_24"]="2. Party with a bonus player. Every time the bonus player uses 1 Instance reward chance, the non-bonus player will get a reward.",
    ["MiniRules_25"]="3. Party with a bonus player. Every time the bonus player uses 1 MVP/mini chance, the non-bonus player will get a reward.",
    ["MiniRules_26"]="4. Party with a bonus player. Every time the bonus player uses 500 Odin points, the non-bonus players close to the bonus player will get a reward.",
    ["MiniRules_27"]="5. Exclusive Odin EXP Multiplier\n10x for Lv.1-49 Adventurers\n9x for Lv.50-69 Adventurers\n8x for Lv.70-89 Adventurers\n7x for Lv.90-99 Adventurers\n6x for Lv.100-160 Adventurers",
    ["MiniRules_3"]="Adventurers can get rare rewards %s times per day. In order to participate in the distribution of rare rewards, a Party with members who are still eligible to claim rare rewards must be ranked top-15 in the damage rankings. If all members of a Party ranked top-15 have no reward chances left, the rewards will be given to the Party ranked No. 16, and so on. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not count toward this limit.",
    ["MiniRules_31"]="The settlement will take place when the MINI dies, and only the top 10 parties in terms of damage dealt will participate in the distribution of rare rewards. If all members within a top-10 party have 0 remaining rare reward chances, that party will not be allowed to participate in the distribution, and the next party in rank order will be considered. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not consume the chance.",
    ["MiniRules_32"]="Party Distribution Weightage = Party's Damage Ranking Weightage + Party's Damage Proportion Weightage",
    ["MiniRules_33"]="The party's damage ranking weightage distribution rules are as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_34"]="The party's damage proportion weightage distribution rules are as follows:\nThe damage proportion weightage for each party = (%s - total ranking weightage) x the party's damage proportion.",
    ["MiniRules_35"]="Party members with remaining rare reward chances not equal to 0 have an equal probability of getting drops.",
    ["MiniRules_36"]="Party members with 0 remaining rare reward chances or who have already received a rare reward during this kill will not participate in the distribution, and their contributed damage will not be factored into the weightage allocation process.",
    ["MiniRules_4"]="%s's Rare Bonus is as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_5"]="Ranking Bonus",
    ["MiniRules_6"]="Settles upon the death of the MINI. There will be a ranking for all participating Parties based on total damage dealt. Parties ranked the 1st and the 2nd will receive 3 and 2 MINI Coins, respectively. Parties ranked from the 3rd to the 10th will receive 1 MINI Coin. Event-exclusive MINI will drop unique event items.",
    ["MiniRules_7"]="You can obtain the Ranking Reward %s times per day. Rewards from the event-exclusive MINI do not count toward this limit, but there's still a daily cap on them.",
    ["MiniRules_8"]="%s's Ranking Bonus is as follows:",
    ["MiniRules_9"]="Last Hit Bonus",
    ["MinigameDialogueBoy_01"]="Wow! Mom, look! He's so awesome!",
    ["MinigameDialogueBoy_02"]="They modeled that spinach-eating sailor after you, didn't they!",
    ["MinigameDialogueBoy_03"]="Aw man! It was over way too soon.",
    ["MinigameDialogueBoy_04"]="He must eat a lot of spinach!",
    ["MinigameDialogueGirl_01"]="Wow! I've never met someone this strong before!",
    ["MinigameDialogueGirl_02"]="I made the right bet! I'm gonna get me some new flavor of candy today!",
    ["MinigameDialogueGirl_03"]="I stuffed the lollipop in there!",
    ["MinigameDialogueGirl_04"]="Put some oomph into it, red! You're about to lose!",
    ["MinigameDialogueMan_01"]="Hang in there, buddy! We can win this!",
    ["MinigameDialogueMan_02"]="That is too cool! I'm gonna be your number one fan!",
    ["MinigameDialogueMan_03"]="That's it! Get him!",
    ["MinigameDialogueMan_04"]="Man, it's decided then...",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldMan_01"]="Amazing! The ultimate union of grace and power!",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldMan_02"]="Not bad, youngster. I wonder if you're taken...",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldMan_03"]="Can't beat the younger generation, huh.",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldMan_04"]="Ah, my age is showing. I'd be an equal match back in my day.",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldWoMan_01"]="I gotta get my grandson into this.",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldWoMan_02"]="You can do it, youngin'!",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldWoMan_03"]="Oh to be young again...",
    ["MinigameDialogueOldWoMan_04"]="My grandson's too small for this...",
    ["MinigameDialogueTie_01"]="It's always gotta be red versus blue!",
    ["MinigameDialogueTie_02"]="It's a rare tie!",
    ["MinigameDialogueTie_03"]="There's only room for one champion here!",
    ["MinigameDialogueTie_04"]="I want a rematch! We don't know who's stronger yet!",
    ["MinigameDialogueTie_05"]="They're evenly matched!",
    ["MinigameDialogueWoMan_01"]="And the winner is blue!",
    ["MinigameDialogueWoMan_02"]="That's the Chosen One! I choose him!",
    ["MinigameDialogueWoMan_03"]="I think the other side is losing on purpose...",
    ["MinigameDialogueWoMan_04"]="I think there's still a chance to turn it around!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_01"]="Welcome to the tavern! Would you like to try a unique minigame? We have lots of prizes!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_02"]="You look... strong! You'd be perfect for arm wrestling!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_03"]="Go pet the cat at the counter if you're not interested. Spots are limited though.",
    ["MinigameDialogue_04"]="Yaaaaawn... Sorry, sorry. I got tired of waiting. (%ds)",
    ["MinigameDialogue_05"]="Hey, hey! Someone's not happy!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_06"]="Come join an exciting duel!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_07"]="You need both a big belly and speed to win!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_08"]="Who's last year's drinking champion? Ugh... Don't remind me!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_09"]="Urf! Hah! Gotta limber up for that extra burst of power!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_10"]="(Whispers) I heard someone once tried to cheat the competition and suffered the consequences... Heh.",
    ["MinigameDialogue_11"]="Looks like it's a tie! One more match to decide the victor then!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_12"]="This is too boring. Please leave.",
    ["MinigameDialogue_13"]="What's the secret to winning? It's... Look! Someone dropped some Zeny!",
    ["MinigameDialogue_14"]="The strong may not always look strong, but the weak... Well, they tend to look that way.",
    ["MinigameDialogue_15"]="Relax, relax! It's just arm wrestling. No one's ever broken their arm doing it... Right?",
    ["MinigameDialogue_16"]="Hmm~ Hmm, hmm~♪\nSomeone's biceps are twitchy~♪",
    ["MinigameTips_01"]="Your team members are playing a minigame! You cannot enter the instance right now!",
    ["MinigameTips_02"]="Your team members are playing a minigame! You cannot climb the tower right now!",
    ["MinigameTips_03"]="You can't do this while matchmaking!",
    ["MinigameTips_04"]="%s wants to %s with you.",
    ["MinigameTips_05"]="You've been asked to leave your seat.",
    ["MinigameTips_06"]="The player has left.",
    ["MinigameTips_07"]="The player has refused.",
    ["MinigameTips_08"]="You can't invite any more players at the moment. Try again later!",
    ["MinigameTips_09"]="%s has invited you to play again.",
    ["MinigameTips_10"]="So you lost, huh? Just try again!",
    ["MinigameTips_11"]="Too bad... You almost had it!",
    ["MinigameTips_12"]="Well, I still reckon you'll win...",
    ["MinigameTips_13"]="Fate can be so cruel sometimes...",
    ["MinigameTips_14"]="Never give up! Never surrender!",
    ["MinigameTips_15"]="Strange... You look so strong...",
    ["MinigameTips_16"]="I just know you'll win next time!",
    ["MinigameTips_17"]="Ahh! Keep training and try again!",
    ["MinigameTips_18"]="(Whispering) Hey... You lost on purpose, didn't you?",
    ["MinigameTips_19"]="You've used up all of your reward claiming chances for today! Come again tomorrow!\n(Reward chances reset at 5:00 every day.)",
    ["MinigameTips_20"]="The other player has reconnected.",
    ["MinigameTips_21"]="Yikes! Your opponent has left the arena!",
    ["MinigameTips_22"]="Your opponent must be afraid of your unspeakable power! Just look at how fast they ran away!",
    ["MinigameTips_23"]="Your opponent seems to have something urgent to attend to. It looks like you'll have to wait until next time to beat them!",
    ["MinigameTips_24"]="Your opponent hasn't left yet. Seize this opportunity to put them to shame!",
    ["MinigameTips_25"]="Obviously you let them win just now... So, let's see your true strength this time!",
    ["MinigameTips_26"]="They got lucky... but this time it's for real!",
    ["MinigameTips_27"]="Wow! You're so awesome—you scared your opponent away!",
    ["MinigameTips_28"]="The goddess of victory is on your side... Your opponent didn't dare to stick around!",
    ["MinigameTips_29"]="Haha! Your opponent left in a huff!",
    ["MinigameTips_30"]="Since you're in such prime condition, go ahead and seize victory while you can!",
    ["MinigameTips_31"]="Your opponent doesn't seem to be giving in... So give them a good reason to! One more match!",
    ["MinigameTips_32"]="It seems your opponent hasn't had enough! It's time for another match!",
    ["Minute"]="minute(s)",
    ["MissingSpecifiedPendant"]="You can only use this skill if you rent a Hovercannon.",
    ["ModeText1"]="Solo",
    ["ModeText2"]="Duo",
    ["ModeText3"]="Form Party",
    ["ModeText4"]="Team",
    ["ModeText5"]="Solo, Party",
    ["MonCollectAtInstance"]="Found in the [%s] instance. Cannot auto-path.",
    ["Monster52530"]="\n\nYuda has arrived on the battlefield. Heroes, hurry and take him down!\n\n",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10000"]="ASPD +30%, Haste +10%, MSPD +50%.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10001"]="There's a chance to reflect 0.1% of Holy DMG when attacked, up to a maximum of 10% of the player's Max HP.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10002"]="Once in a while, hide for 8 seconds.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10003"]="Once in a while, gain a reflective shield (1% reflect rate) for 3 seconds, up to 20% of the player's Max HP.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10004"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to gain a damage immunity shield (blocks 150 hits) for 10 seconds. If the shield is not broken by the time it disappears, it restores 10% of Max HP.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10005"]="There's a chance to generate mist when injured, reducing the P.DMG and M.DMG taken by all monsters within the mist by 100%.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10100"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflect all hit targets with Virus (reduces healing received by 100% and deals True DMG periodically, unstackable).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10101"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to restrict the vision of all hit targets for 3 seconds.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10102"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to drain 30% of Max SP from all hit targets.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10103"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Burn on all hit targets (deals True DMG periodically, stackable).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10104"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Chill on all hit targets (reduces MSPD and ASPD; freezes the target upon reaching 5 stacks).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10105"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Corrosion on all hit targets (reduces Final DMG; prevents the target from dealing normal attacks and skills upon reaching 5 stacks).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10200"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to inflict an electrifying effect on 5 random threat targets nearby (interrupts and immobilizes the target).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10201"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to generate 1 vortex at the location of 1 random threat target nearby (pulls the target).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10202"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to teleport 2 random threat targets nearby to its position and apply a Death Link on them (deals True DMG periodically until the skill expires or the link is broken).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10203"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to make all threat targets move in the opposite direction.",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10204"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to make 2 random threat targets nearby enter the Irresistible state (moving towards the monster uncontrollably).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10205"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to inflict a Thunder Wrath mark on 1 random threat target nearby, striking them with lightning (deals massive shareable True DMG to the target within a small area).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10300"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to generate 1 persistent poison circle at the location of 3 random threat targets nearby (reduces the players' MSPD, P.DEF, and M.DEF and deals True DMG periodically).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10301"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to trap 2 random threat targets nearby into an aqua sphere (players inside the aqua sphere take massive True DMG when the sphere disappears but can be saved by other players touching the sphere).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10302"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to send 4 random threat targets nearby to four locations and link them in pairs with positive and negative charges (linked players must collide with the one in the same pair to remove the link; otherwise, they will take massive True DMG at the end).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10303"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to create 2 Scythe of Hell in front and behind it (activates after a delay, dealing a small amount of True DMG if players are within range or a moderate amount of True DMG to a large area if there are no players within range).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10304"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon a spirit bomb and a protective shield around (The spirit bomb activates after a delay, dealing a massive amount of True DMG to a large area).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10305"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to infect 1 random threat target nearby with the viral spores (greatly reduces healing effects and deals True DMG periodically while spreading the virus to nearby players).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10400"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 3 Golden Thief Bugs around you (deals True DMG to nearby players continuously).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10401"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 1 damage reduction tablet that exists for 10 seconds around it (players cannot deal damage to any monster within a 5-meter radius of the tablet).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10402"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 1 Evil Heart that exists for 10 seconds around it (if not destroyed in time, it deals a massive amount of True DMG to a large area).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10403"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 2 fire tablets that exist for 15 seconds around it (periodically releases fireballs that deal True DMG and reduce P.DEF and M.DEF of the hit target).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10404"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 1 healing pillar that exists for 10 seconds around it (periodically heals the monster; players can try to block its link but will take True DMG while doing so).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10405"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 1 blinding tablet around it (periodically restricts the player's vision in a large area and reduces their Hit Rate by a moderate amount).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10500"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to select 2 random threat targets nearby, summoning 10 lightning strikes (deals a moderate amount of True DMG in a small area each time).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10501"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to summon 2 cyclones nearby to chase after players (deals True DMG to surrounding areas periodically and inflicts Slow).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10502"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to select 3 random threat targets nearby, generating a radiant cross at their locations after a delay (deals a moderate amount of True DMG).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10503"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to select 1 random threat target nearby, generating a clock at the target's location (deals a large-area immobilize effect at the end).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10504"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to select 2 random threat targets nearby, dropping meteors at their locations after a delay (deals True DMG in a large area and knocks them back).",
    ["MonsterAffixDes_10505"]="Once in a while, there's a chance to select 2 random threat targets nearby, generating 1 mine at their locations after a delay (triggers after a delay and deals a moderate amount of True DMG).",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10000"]="Judgment - Fervor",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10001"]="Judgment - Spikes",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10002"]="Judgment - Invisibility",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10003"]="Judgment - Reflective Shield",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10004"]="Judgment - Healing Shield",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10005"]="Judgment - Protective Mist",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10100"]="Curse Breaker - Virus",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10101"]="Curse Breaker - Restricted Vision",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10102"]="Curse Breaker - Arcane Leech",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10103"]="Curse Breaker - Burn",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10104"]="Curse Breaker - Chill",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10105"]="Curse Breaker - Corrosion",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10200"]="Prophet - Electrify",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10201"]="Prophet - Vortex",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10202"]="Prophet - Death Link",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10203"]="Prophet - Disrupt",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10204"]="Prophet - Irresistible",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10205"]="Prophet - Thunder Wrath",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10300"]="Revelation - Venom Pit",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10301"]="Revelation - Aqua Sphere",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10302"]="Revelation - Polar Charge",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10303"]="Revelation - Scythe of Hell",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10304"]="Revelation - Spirit Bomb",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10305"]="Revelation - Viral Spores",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10400"]="Annihilation - Blazing Golden Thief Bug",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10401"]="Annihilation - Mitigation Tablet",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10402"]="Annihilation - Evil Heart",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10403"]="Annihilation - Fire Tablet",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10404"]="Annihilation - Life Link",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10405"]="Annihilation - Blinding Tablet",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10500"]="Ark - Thunderstorm",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10501"]="Ark - Cyclone",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10502"]="Ark - Radiant Cross",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10503"]="Ark - Time Shackles",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10504"]="Ark - Meteor",
    ["MonsterAffixName_10505"]="Ark - Timed Mine",
    ["MonsterAffixPreview"]="The affix is about to take effect.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10000"]="Increases ASPD, Haste, and MSPD.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10001"]="There's a chance to reflect damage when attacked.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10002"]="Activates Hiding once in a while.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10003"]="Gains Reflective Shield once in a while.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10004"]="Gains Count Shield once in a while, provides healing if not broken.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10005"]="There's a chance to generate mist upon injury, reducing damage taken by monsters within the mist.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10100"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflect all hit targets with Virus, dealing damage and reducing their healing received by 100%.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10101"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to restrict the vision of hit targets.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10102"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to drain SP from hit targets.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10103"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Burn on hit targets, stackable.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10104"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Chill on hit targets, freezing them when fully stacked.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10105"]="Normal attacks and skills have a chance to inflict Corrosion on hit targets, disabling normal attacks and skills when fully stacked.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10200"]="Inflicts an electrifying effect on 5 random threat targets, interrupting and immobilizing them.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10201"]="Generates a vortex at the location of 1 random threat target, continuously slowing and pulling the target.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10202"]="Teleports 2 random threat targets, linking them together.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10203"]="Makes all threat targets move in the opposite direction.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10204"]="Makes 2 random threat targets move toward monsters uncontrollably.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10205"]="Applies a mark on 1 random threat target, dealing a massive amount of shareable damage.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10300"]="Generates a venom pit at the location of 3 random threat targets, dealing damage while reducing their MSPD and DEF.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10301"]="Traps 2 random threat targets into an Aqua Sphere, dealing a massive amount of damage if it's not broken.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10302"]="Teleports 4 random threat targets, linking them together in pairs with positive and negative charges.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10303"]="Generates Scythe of Hell to attack Adventurers within range. If no Adventurers are nearby, then it deals damage over a large area.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10304"]="Summons a Spirit Bomb and a protective shield. The Spirit Bomb deals damage after a delay.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10305"]="Applies Viral Spores on 1 random threat target, with spores continuously spreading.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10400"]="Summons 3 Golden Thief Bugs that continuously burn nearby players.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10401"]="Summon 1 Mitigation Tablet that grants damage reduction to monsters within range.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10402"]="Summons 1 Evil Heart that deals a massive amount of damage if not destroyed in time.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10403"]="Summons 2 Fire Tablets that keep launching fireballs.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10404"]="Summons 1 Healing Pillar that keeps healing monsters.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10405"]="Summons 1 Blinding Tablet that reduces the vision and Hit Rate of players within range.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10500"]="Selects 2 random threat targets, striking them with lightning.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10501"]="Summons 2 cyclones to chase after players, dealing damage and slowing them down.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10502"]="Generates a delayed Radiant Cross that deals damage at the location of 3 random threat targets.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10503"]="Generates a clock at the location of 1 random threat target, causing immobilization in a large area when it ends.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10504"]="Generates a delayed Meteor that deals damage with a knockback effect at the location of 2 random threat targets.",
    ["MonsterAffixShortDes_10505"]="Generates a delayed mine that deals damage at the location of 3 random threat targets.",
    ["MonsterCollection10001"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Poring, a monster found all throughout Midgard, is more akin to being a mascot of Midgard than a monster. Even the bravest adventurer is no match against a Poring's cuteness. Apparently, people who adore Porings have come together and organized themselves into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poring Supporters' Group</color>. \"Adventurers who kill Porings without a care are heartless creatures!\" said a member of the supporters' group, wearing a Poring-shaped hat and wiping away tears.",
    ["MonsterCollection10002"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Fabres, often found near crops, has only one means of self-defense—<color=#CA2E0AFF>spinning silk</color>. Yet, who could have thought that the silk produced by Fabres is the raw material for Prontera's luxury silk?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"They are aggressive when they are hungry but they continue to spin silk docilely one fed. What a simple nature!\" remarked Monster Researcher Bertha as she stood in the field and wrote in her notebook.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"That's enough! Get these insects off my farm right away!\" cried Bertha's father angrily from the side.",
    ["MonsterCollection10003"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> When <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fabres</color> reach a certain stage of growth, they turn into Pupae, seen everywhere out in the fields. Rumor has it that in the quiet of the night, the pupae split open to reveal the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Creamy incubated</color> inside, but as nobody has ever seen the complete process of a Creamy emerging from a pupa, how much truth there is in the rumor remains to be verified.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monster Researcher Bertha would like to remind everyone that the Fabre contributes greatly for mankind, so please do not break open pupae just for fun!",
    ["MonsterCollection10004"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The bunny monster which dwells near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> has an inexhaustible store of energy hidden within its tiny body. Despite a Lunatic's cute appearance, due to the fact that its <color=#CA2E0AFF>fur</color> is an <color=#CA2E0AFF>excellent material</color>, there are already calls to set up a \"Lunatic Conservation Society.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The following is an extract from the important news section of the Kingdom Times: Novices should take care in distinguishing the color of the Lunatic's fur. Should an Eclipse be discovered, please hide immediately and inform the Kingdom Defense Force!",
    ["MonsterCollection10005"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> In the kingdom's <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color>, brown spherical objects, sticky and extremely disgusting, can be seen all over the place. Nobody who can avoid it will ever dream of touching it. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Breaking</color> them while they are still eggs can effectively <color=#CA2E0AFF>prevent the hatching of Thief Bugs</color>.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Perhaps only the god of cooking, Dobbin, can turn such things into a dish...\" said Grace, giving up after looking at the Thief Bug Eggs on her chopping board.",
    ["MonsterCollection10006"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A flying monster with big watery eyes. According to research statistics, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sunflower Nectar</color> outside the West Gate is their favorite food. Chonchons bloated from feasting on nectar hovering low in the air are often seen there.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"... So why are they called Chonchons?!\" yelled Ygnizem as she ran away, unable to strike at the Chonchons due to their cuteness.",
    ["MonsterCollection10007"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>sentient</color> plant monster freed from the restriction of its roots. Though it looks rather scary, its nature is actually very playful <color=#CA2E0AFF>like a little child</color>. As Willows of very small sizes exist, the monster research academia has reasons to believe that there are great variations in size between different Willows.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"The Willows we have found at present are all in their infancy. An adult Willow Sage must be...\" Monster Researcher Bertha's eyes brightened.",
    ["MonsterCollection10008"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An amazing saltwater frog most often found dwelling in the shallowest parts of seas. Apparently, they feed on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chonchons</color>, but no crossing of paths has been discovered between the two in their natural habitat, so it remains unproven. There are even rumors of Roda Frogs being capable of reading, comprehending, taking a liking to human books.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Those are all tall tales. They're just normal sea monsters,\" yawned Hayden who runs a business by the sea all year round, waving his hand dismissively.",
    ["MonsterCollection10009"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Once an insignificant bug, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>mutated</color> once corrupted by the dark energy in the sewers. Adventurers should be advised not to show it any mercy.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The following is an extract from the news section of the Kingdom Times: Thief Bug lovers have taken to the streets today to protest the kingdom's order that encourages the extermination of Thief Bugs. The Kingdom Defense Force is now in communication with the Thief Bug lovers. Negotiation is still ongoing.",
    ["MonsterCollection10010"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A rocker-shaped monster with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>violin in hand</color> that possesses extraordinary musical talent. Apparently, music is their means of communication. However, the origin of those violins in their hands remains unknown.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Who could have known that such a romantic race exists in the monster world,\" sang Morts, plucking at the strings of his lute.",
    ["MonsterCollection10011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A cute chick monster that <color=#CA2E0AFF>never</color> seems to <color=#CA2E0AFF>grow up</color> from the moment of its birth. The debate about their appearance in their true complete form has yet to cease amongst the academics. It is in tight competition with the Drops for the first place on Morroc's ranking for the most popular monster. However, do not underestimate their attack. These little fellas have caused the injuries and deaths of several adventurers.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The following is an extract from a warning board in the Morroc wilderness: Please exercise caution when dealing with harmless-looking monsters!",
    ["MonsterCollection10012"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Fire Poring with a cute appearance similar to normal Porings. However, due to its own magic attribute, Drops can purify <color=#CA2E0AFF>more advanced materials</color> than normal Porings. Perhaps it is because they understand this point too, Drops are not as docile and friendly as normal Porings in interacting with humans.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> It is in a tight competition with the Picky for the first place on Morroc's ranking for the most popular monster. However, on the kingdom's ranking for the most popular monster, it is still a long way behind the Poring.",
    ["MonsterCollection10013"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Pecopeco Egg Shells can be grounded into a shiny powder. It is an excellent <color=#CA2E0AFF>raw material for decorations</color> and is popular in the kingdom. However, it is advised not to steal Pecopeco Eggs for fun, or else you will invite the furious attacks of angered Pecopecos.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A gentle reminder from Baldwin of the Royal Chivalry: Please gather Egg Shell materials only after the Pecopeco chicks have hatched!",
    ["MonsterCollection10014"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Condors living in the desert are extremely proud and cannot stand being deprived of their freedom. However, they do not appear as handsome closeup as they do up in the sky. In fact, they look somewhat silly. Perhaps even if they were astoundingly handsome, they would still lose out as they are associated with the word <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"con.\"</color> <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A friendly reminder from Monster Researcher Bertha: Be extra careful of their cries if you wish to keep your eardrums intact.",
    ["MonsterCollection10015"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A monster which passes off as cute and innocent with its appearance, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>viciousness</color> can occasionally be observed from its <color=#CA2E0AFF>gaze</color>. It often dashes around on its short legs in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wilderness beyond the West Gate</color>, often accidentally bumping into adventurers before being pet by them for a good while. Perhaps their original intention may have been to attack.",
    ["MonsterCollection10016"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> To quicken the growth of their pups, Desert Wolves always leave them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fend for themselves</color>. Therefore, groups of Baby Desert Wolves can always be seen living together.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"High-grade <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baby Desert Wolf Fur</color> is <color=#CA2E0AFF>more valuable</color> than adult Desert Wolf Fur.\" It is rare to see a glimmer of greed in the eyes of the usually gentlemanly Jude.",
    ["MonsterCollection10017"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A bird monster which <color=#CA2E0AFF>can only walk upright</color> despite having wings. Its sharp and powerfully-built beak can scare away egg thieves from afar. After all, once an angry Pecopeco has its eyes on you, it won't be possible to get away without losing some blood.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Thank goodness I run fast. Otherwise it wouldn't have just been that egg thief who got a good pecking,\" sighed Pet Merchant Lyra, still in lingering shock.",
    ["MonsterCollection10018"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A desert monster with amazing facial expressions. Despite having an appearance similar to a cactus, it is actually a dancer with a musical soul at heart, and can start <color=#CA2E0AFF>swaying to a rhythm</color> at any time.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Nobody thinks about quenching thirst with it, unless you are willing to have a row of Muka beard on your chin,\" said gourmet chef Stefanie as she blew away the sand in her fingernails, looking at the Muka some distance away with a grin.",
    ["MonsterCollection10019"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Some Rockers have gone astray in the pursuit of their musical dreams and have become obsessed with <color=#CA2E0AFF>heavy metal</color>. The language their violins play has become completely independent from that of their original race. Therefore, they have a new name.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The kingdom's ecology conservation society has already dispatched specialists to keep an eye on the state of development of the Metallers and to follow up on their evolution at all times.",
    ["MonsterCollection10020"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> New adventurers easily overlook how poisonous they are, but to experienced adventurers, their <color=#CA2E0AFF>Venom</color> is a rather remarkable <color=#CA2E0AFF>profit-making material</color>. As a result, organizations such as the Anacondaq Conservation Society have come into being. After all, when the buying stops, the killing can too!",
    ["MonsterCollection10021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A formidable existence in the desert. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>stinger</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>two pincers</color> radiate an aura of danger and even the mesmerizing purple tail cannot conceal the intimidation of its <color=#CA2E0AFF>poison</color>. Rumor has it that thousands of adventurers have been stung by them.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Keep that scary thing away from me. Haven't you heard Monster Conservation Society's news? It's extremely likely to evolve into a giant scorpion,\" said Rylai, tightening her protective clothing and taking another two steps back.",
    ["MonsterCollection10022"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A monster with very obvious <color=#CA2E0AFF>man-made traces</color>. Nobody knows how they appeared. Traces of having been <color=#CA2E0AFF>built out of bricks</color> cover their entire body and a<color=#CA2E0AFF>magical</color> light shines from their eyes. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"They may hold the secrets of a vanished magic civilization and are worthy to be considered very good research material,\" said Armor Merchant Dael, stealthily taking a photo of Golems feeding and seeming to already have a plan to catch one for research.",
    ["MonsterCollection10023"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Few are the adventurers who have seen Hodes in their entirety in the desert. Apparently, strange <color=#CA2E0AFF>large eyes</color> hide beneath those budging and <color=#CA2E0AFF>wriggling sand dunes</color>, but nobody has been able to provide photos as evidence yet. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The following comes from a Monster Conservation Society's notice: Please do not dig pits all over the place to take a photo of a Hode. This speeds up the degradation of the natural ecological environment.",
    ["MonsterCollection10024"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Due to the cruel experiences they went through when they were young, they have grown into <color=#CA2E0AFF>fearsome Desert Wolves skilled in fighting</color>. After experiencing countless battles, their fur have turned into hardened armor and are no longer worth as much as the soft fur they had when they were young. However, apparently, there are still people secretly buying adult Desert Wolf Fur for use as armor material on the Black Market.",
    ["MonsterCollection10025"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A dangerous-looking animal with ugly features. However, they actually <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed on pests all year round</color> and make great contributions to the conservation of the environment. Hopefully biologists can help them restore the reputation they deserve someday.",
    ["MonsterCollection10027"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Death after a <color=#CA2E0AFF>stinging attack</color> is a thing of the past. The stinger is its present combat weapon. Its appearance is similar to a cross between a bee and a spirit. Despite having a <color=#CA2E0AFF>cute human face</color>, it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>aggressive and does not like losing</color>, never admitting defeat upon encountering a strong rival. Ygnizem is one of their victims.",
    ["MonsterCollection10028"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A slow, crawling animal on the surface. The mysterious patterns on the Ambernite shell that faintly give off a <color=#CA2E0AFF>magical aura</color> will escape notice without close observation. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> According to information from the Geffen Guild, Ambernites are a type of stealthy magical creature and highly dangerous. Please be careful!",
    ["MonsterCollection10029"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A mouse with a giant onion growing on its body. You may think of them in this way, but do not ever voice it out. They are creatures <color=#CA2E0AFF>born naturally</color> in the forests and apparently have a certain degree of <color=#CA2E0AFF>divinity</color>. Best not to trifle with them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10030"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Chonchon that is <color=#CA2E0AFF>fast-moving and with sharp mouthparts</color>. Be careful not to be stung by it, or you may lose a lot of blood. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Not one part of its entire body has any edible value. I'm not interested,\" said Albel, shaking her head in disdain after a careful scrutiny of the Dustiness in the cage.",
    ["MonsterCollection10031"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An aggressive fellow. The Horn on its head is the key to it being crowned the <color=#CA2E0AFF>King of Insects</color>. Apparently, some people have them engage in fights for fun after taming them, but evidence has yet been found.",
    ["MonsterCollection10033"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An Anacondaq residing <color=#CA2E0AFF>inside a pyramid</color>. Although it looks no different from the Anacondaqs outside, since it can survive safe and sound in the poison-filled air within the pyramids for years on end, it must have its own <color=#CA2E0AFF>extraordinary venom</color>. Adventurers, please treasure your lives and stay away from Side Winders.",
    ["MonsterCollection10034"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The branch of Petite dragons dwelling on land. Currently, monster researchers are still studying why such a huge difference exists within one race. However, the Ground Petites are no lower in status although they are <color=#CA2E0AFF>unable to fly</color>. Despite being the dragons of legend, somehow they are not as intimidating.",
    ["MonsterCollection10035"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The branch of Petite dragons capable of flight. Currently, monster researchers are still studying why such a huge difference exists within one race. The Sky Petites put on a prouder air to the outside world, but their <color=#CA2E0AFF>status within the race is in doubt</color>. Rumor has it that the Sky Petites have sent a letter of challenge to the Ground Petites. It seems they have long held the belief that it is high time the superiority between the Ground Petites and the Sky Petites is determined.",
    ["MonsterCollection10036"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monster researchers have discovered after many studies that complete <color=#CA2E0AFF>fire elements</color> exist within the bodies of Earth Spirit Elders, seemingly overcoming their bodily restrictions. This is a groundbreaking discovery for all of monster research. It is not known when the first findings about them will be published.",
    ["MonsterCollection10037"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A strange creature shrouded in mystery, sharing the title of Midgard's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster of Mystery</color> together with the Magnolia. No one knows where it got those straight brows from, nor what it will hatch into. Apparently, some are conspiring to turn it around counterclockwise. Who knows what may happen if that is done?",
    ["MonsterCollection10038"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A large bear with brown fur. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Docile in nature</color> and does not initiate attacks against humans. Similar in appearance to the Sasquatch. Biologists usually believe them to be from the same race. Apparently, only creatures that have gained their approval can have a chance to share their favorite honey.",
    ["MonsterCollection10039"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>No discovery</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>baby monsters</color> with matching biological characteristics to this monster has been found. Legend has it that Savage Bebes are the young of Savages, but the vast differences between their habitats and physical appearances are unexplainable, and so it remains a mystery for the biologists. \"It is far too hasty to conclude the two are from the same race solely on the basis of the additional 'Bebe' in the name.\" Monster Researcher Bertha firmly refuses to acknowledge any relationship between Savages and Savage Bebes.",
    ["MonsterCollection10040"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Magnolia, with its <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious origins</color>, has always been the favorite topic of discussion among monster lovers. The most commonly accepted explanation about its origins at present is that someone broke edible Pecopeco Eggs and the restless souls inside the eggs transformed into Magnolias which fry themselves continually.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Anyway, even if it fried itself to a perfect over medium, I don't think anyone would want to try this delicacy,\" said the gourmet Nicola who was passing by as she raised her eyebrows.",
    ["MonsterCollection10041"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Demi-humans from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>primitive civilization</color>. Researchers are currently studying their potential associations with the Giearth, Goblin, and other civilizations. Don't ever underestimate their intelligence just because of their silly smiles. If you are not careful, you may find yourself surrounded by these Deviruchis.",
    ["MonsterCollection10042"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Flames wandering where the dead are found. Anyone who touches it will be unwittingly burnt. Whether it is a type of monster or a natural phenomenon is still a mystery. However, in Payon's local culture, <color=#CA2E0AFF>evil ghosts</color> are believed to be behind it.",
    ["MonsterCollection10043"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A stone tablet inscribed with \"Great General of the Realm.\" According to research verification, it originally was really a stone tablet, and is suspected to have transmogrified after absorbing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doppelganger aura</color> seeping out from the Payon Dungeon, strangely retaining the proud figure of the general.",
    ["MonsterCollection10044"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A weak creature <color=#CA2E0AFF>living in the darkness</color>. Unless they band together in groups, they pose no threat. They always watch their invading enemies silently from the dark. If while on an adventure in the sewers you suddenly feel a strange gaze following you, don't be alarmed, for it may well be observing you from the darkness.",
    ["MonsterCollection10045"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Appears harmless, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spore Hat</color> on its head is the actual <color=#CA2E0AFF>source of danger</color>. Apparently, its real body is hidden behind its astonishingly large mouth. Many can't help reaching out to touch it after being bewitched by the cute expression of its lower body, and so they end up offering a delicious hand for the Spore's dinner.",
    ["MonsterCollection10046"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A very <color=#CA2E0AFF>docile</color> monster that <color=#CA2E0AFF>likes playing with humans</color>. Sometimes, many adventurers are scared away by their enthusiasm. However, it is a curious sight to behold when they dance around humans in groups.",
    ["MonsterCollection10047"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Permanently dwells in the damp and dark <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color>. Its two red eyes gives people involuntarily goosebumps.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"The scariest things in the sewers are obviously those scurrying rats, not Thief Bugs and bats,\" muttered Hervor, as he watched the Kingdom Defense Force walking away in the distance.",
    ["MonsterCollection10048"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>mutated Thief Bug</color> monster corrupted by the dark energy in the sewers. Its attack and agility are far greater than a normal Thief Bug. It is the enemy of Male Thief Bugs—another type of Mutant Thief Bug—and they dwell in different areas of the sewers. A friendly reminder from the Kingdom Defense Force: Mutant Thief Bugs have been running rampant recently. Adventurers, please be careful if you run into Mutant Thief Bugs.",
    ["MonsterCollection10049"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>mutated Thief Bug</color> monster corrupted by the dark energy in the sewers. Its attack and agility are far greater than a normal Thief Bug. It is an enemy of Female Thief Bugs—another type of Mutant Thief Bug—and they dwell in different areas of the sewers. A friendly reminder from the Kingdom Defense Force: Mutant Thief Bugs have been running rampant recently. Adventurers, please be careful if you run into Mutant Thief Bugs.",
    ["MonsterCollection10050"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pack</color> monsters. They appear to be like a normal wolf pack. Their pelts are akin to the hardest armors. No one knows where they have migrated from, and it seems some of their distant relatives live in the desert far away too.",
    ["MonsterCollection10051"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A colorful <color=#CA2E0AFF>carnivorous plant</color> that wanders aimlessly in the forest all day. Be very careful when approaching it. Even its skin is a constant reminder to not get too close. It's <color=#CA2E0AFF>poisonous</color>!",
    ["MonsterCollection10052"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Although the Poison Poporing also has a sizable fanbase, some adventurers are still concerned about its poison and do not dare to touch it casually.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> According to Finch's latest research, Poporing's Poison attribute manifests as <color=#CA2E0AFF>resistance to poison</color> instead of being poisonous. Adventurers may rest assured.",
    ["MonsterCollection10053"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An Anacondaq living in Payon's forests. It looks no different from the snakes outside. Its colors look terrifying but it is actually <color=#CA2E0AFF>non-venomous</color>. Nonetheless, a bite from its sharp fangs will still leave you in pain for days. Don't provoke carelessly~",
    ["MonsterCollection10054"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Fabre's imago form. It only inhabits the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> and survives by <color=#CA2E0AFF>sucking nectar</color>. A Creamy's wings are very beautiful, completely incomparable to its appearance when it was a Fabre. The nectar gathered by Creamies is an excellent health supplement, provided you can survive their attacks to enjoy it.",
    ["MonsterCollection10055"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A brightly colored insect. It has many natural enemies but has survived thanks to its <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerful reproductive capabilities</color>. Each Stainer has a fixed number of 8 spots on its body. Is this a characteristic of the race? A special reminder: Stainer Shells are edible!",
    ["MonsterCollection10056"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>It belongs to the same race as Chonchons</color> but has even more exotic colors, as though informing all creatures on sight that it is very dangerous and strangers ought not approach. Such a warning also indirectly protects itself. However, apparently, there is still a group of Chonchon-hunting hobbyists who occasionally provoke them despite the danger. Of course, the price is rather painful. After all, it doesn't feel good being besieged by a swarm of Steel Chonchons.",
    ["MonsterCollection10057"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A cute monster with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>big tail</color>. The bushy tail is not only their <color=#CA2E0AFF>key to climbing trees easily</color>, but also the cutest part of their entire body. Cocos' survival depends on gathering Acorns. Don't ever take their Acorns!",
    ["MonsterCollection10058"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Despite having the appearance of a cute animal, it is actually a monster, so don't be fooled. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>leaves on their heads</color> are not there because of the wind, but are actually their markings. Rumor has it that this isn't how they really look, but the result of a transformation!",
    ["MonsterCollection10059"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A weak and cowardly monster willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sacrifice its own spines</color> in self-defense. Promise me that you won't ever think of attacking them. Their spines are lost for good upon use, and a Caramel with no spines left isn't a Caramel anymore.",
    ["MonsterCollection10060"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Often, some adventurer is deceived by the innocence in its eyes, but in actual fact, it is a very ferocious monster. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp claws</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tail</color> are both very powerful weapons. Being one of the few monsters that can be <color=#CA2E0AFF>tamed</color> by humans, it is also the monster biologically closest to humans.",
    ["MonsterCollection10061"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A skeleton dressed as a sailor. They must have been <color=#CA2E0AFF>brave and good at fighting</color> when they were alive. However, their taste in fashion doesn't seem to be any good. With a pirate's bandana and eye patch matched with the standard boots of the kingdom, they are often criticized by the self-proclaimed fashionista, Vera, as the monsters most incapable of outfit matching in Midgard.",
    ["MonsterCollection10062"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> In the crowded Megalo monster clan, they seem insignificant, with little pure blood inherited, but their <color=#CA2E0AFF>furious</color> nature is totally an undeniable truth. Born with <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerful jaws</color>, they could bite through bones. Surprisingly, however, they seem <color=#CA2E0AFF>to be attracted only to moving objects</color>, and become much less aggressive against stationary things.\n \"Megalodons have nothing but bones in their bodies, and no food is needed. Given this, it is assumed that they don't hunt for food, but follow their instincts.\" The famous Monster Researcher adjusted the glasses, and left a signature on the essay just finished.",
    ["MonsterCollection10063"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A mushroom monster that appears in dark sewers. Its body swaying to and fro and its wicked expression are exactly identical to a Spore's. However, their <color=#CA2E0AFF>nature</color> is more <color=#CA2E0AFF>aggressive</color>, and both their spikes and fangs are covered in <color=#CA2E0AFF>fatal venom</color>. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Some say that they are the mutants of Spores corrupted by dark energy while others say they are another branch of Spores. This question has been the topic of endless debate between various Spore experts in the monster research academia.",
    ["MonsterCollection10064"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A ghostly creature drifting aboard the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Treasure Ship</color>. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>vacant eyes</color> look as though they can readily suck you into its heart. However, most of the time, it simply wanders around aimlessly, only occasionally pranking accidental adventurers by appearing in front of them, causing shrieks and screams.",
    ["MonsterCollection10065"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Carapace animal living on the seabed, it occasionally forages for food in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shallow sea</color>. Its four limbs are very sharp, so be careful not to get pricked. Bacteria from the seabed is not to be trifled with. Apparently, it is a close relative to lobsters, but nobody can provide biological proof of this.",
    ["MonsterCollection10066"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A bright-colored mollusk living on the seabed and full of <color=#CA2E0AFF>toxins</color> from head to foot to protect itself. Its trailing <color=#CA2E0AFF>tentacles</color> are the main weapons it uses in attacks. They can be cut off first in battles. It is very friendly toward other sea creatures, often taking an active part in helping ward off invaders, and is the main battle force of the sea.",
    ["MonsterCollection10067"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Inhabiting the shoal near Kokomo Beach, they are shy and timid. They rarely attack humans, and only threats bring out their intimidating strength. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colorful</color> sand and stones are their favorite, which are always swallowed at first sight, wrapped by their body fluids, and turned into pretty <color=#CA2E0AFF>pearls</color> later. Stones of various colors make pearls of different shades, which fetch a stunning price in the black market.",
    ["MonsterCollection10068"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An <color=#CA2E0AFF>aggressive</color> sea warrior. Despite being a target of human fishing, it still tries to protect other sea creatures. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>crab claws</color> show no mercy to enemies invading the seabed. Be careful not to get caught in its claws!",
    ["MonsterCollection10069"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>cute, naive, and peaceful</color> sea creature and every Hydra's crush. It often reveals expressions so cute that they make people scream involuntarily and is one of the best at acting cute amongst the seabed dwellers. It likes to play with humans very much and is a mollusk more popular than Planktons.",
    ["MonsterCollection10071"]="A gloomy underwater creature, which is said to look like a middle-aged Shellfish. The pattern on its shell is <color=#CA2E0AFF>unique</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>artistic</color>, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tender flesh</color> beneath the hard shell is <color=#CA2E0AFF>a great ingredient</color> for cooking. Experienced cooks will put the caught Cormutus in clear water for a few days to let it vomit up all the filth in its body and then cook it.",
    ["MonsterCollection10072"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A fighter of the sea, battling continually with a spirit that never admits defeat. Apparently, its <color=#CA2E0AFF>long, hard jaw</color> can pierce the deck of ships. Therefore, many sailors want to use it to craft weapons. However, defeating it requires a lot of effort too.",
    ["MonsterCollection10073"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Usually curled into a ball in a corner and completely still, it is easily overlooked if little attention is paid. The pattern on its shell is dizzying and hard to stare at for long. Marine Sphere Shells are speculated to have some sort of magic effect, rendering predators <color=#CA2E0AFF>stunned</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>unable to concentrate</color>. Therefore, adventurers wishing to hunt Marine Spheres should take extra notice.",
    ["MonsterCollection10074"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The most common fish in the sea, <color=#CA2E0AFF>mutated</color> as a result of being affected by Ymir's Heart. Despite having large eyes, close observation will reveal that they seem to have <color=#CA2E0AFF>poor eyesight</color>. The following is a friendly reminder from the Midgard Culinary Association: For the sake of your health, please do not consume mutated fish.",
    ["MonsterCollection10075"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An intelligent creature living on the seabed and possessing a <color=#CA2E0AFF>self-consciousness</color> which normal sea creatures do not. They are united and friendly, and—according to human beauty standards—look like very beautiful <color=#CA2E0AFF>young girls with fish tails</color>. In legends, daughters of Strouf were all born in the form of Obeaunes. How wonderful would it be to see those beautiful princesses.",
    ["MonsterCollection10076"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Many adventurers find themselves going soft-hearted and unable to attack when confronted with the watery <color=#CA2E0AFF>big eyes</color> of Marses. However, perhaps within that very second of your hesitation, a Marse may already have quickly launched an attack on you. <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Recently, there has been one question that has puzzled Monster Researcher Bertha for a long time. \"Why is it that the one producing ink is not the Marse, but the Cornutus? What a mystery...\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10077"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters <color=#CA2E0AFF>with the body of a human and the head of a fish</color>, capable of living on the earth and underwater, with two respiratory systems. Usually hidden in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep sea</color>, they are sometimes found on the land for some reason. According to many Adventurers who have faced a Merman, they are <color=#CA2E0AFF>cunning</color> monsters with knowledge of human languages. An arrogant oversight, and you are in for their traps.\n \"O eyes of the abyss, gaze into them and you are deprived of rationality. O whispers of the ancient gods, open your ears and you will sacrifice your soul...\" At a night without moonlight, on a shoal touched by waves, Mermen gather in a circle, enchanting the creepy songs...",
    ["MonsterCollection10078"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A fish with a very strange ecology. Apparently, there are <color=#CA2E0AFF>no different genders</color> for their race. Their bodies are very beautifully <color=#CA2E0AFF>streamlined</color>, but their faces are somewhat indescribable. Their spines are good materials for crafting strings for music instruments. An appeal from the Monster Conservation Society: Please protect rare sea monsters. Strings can be made using artificial materials as replacements but if Marcs become extinct, there is no replacement for them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10079"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Deviace may appear to move slowly, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second mouth</color> on its head is very flexible and can quickly track down targets. This monster very much lives up to its nickname of \"Kissing Fish.\" If its mouth is fixed on you, be prepared to have an unusual intimate encounter.",
    ["MonsterCollection10080"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Ordinary inhabitants with <color=#CA2E0AFF>golden</color> bodies. However, don't underestimate them. Despite having lackluster capabilities, they are ever <color=#CA2E0AFF>united and vigilant</color>. You can't tell if they have got a huge reinforcement behind them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10081"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Builders with <color=#CA2E0AFF>yellowish green</color> bodies. They are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>builders</color> of the Ant Cavern and unimaginable strength is hidden within their tiny bodies. When enemies invade, they are temporarily transferred away to act as defenders, awaiting reinforcements from the Deniros.",
    ["MonsterCollection10082"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Defenders with <color=#CA2E0AFF>red</color> bodies. They are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>regular forces</color> of the Ant Army and are very terrifying when they come at you in a swarm. Each of them is always in the company of their companions. To protect the safety of the Ant Cavern, they never retreat.",
    ["MonsterCollection10083"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Maya guards <color=#CA2E0AFF>with black</color> bodies. Their special duty is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>protect Maya</color> and, despite being few in number, each of them can fight ten others. When you see them, it means Maya is somewhere close by. Be fully prepared before provoking them!",
    ["MonsterCollection10084"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>mutated form of Familiars</color> living in the Ant Cavern for extended periods of time. To better hide itself, its body has evolved to become entirely red. Apparently, its wings are also a type of precious medicine. However, if you want to get its wings, you'll have to be prepared to lose some blood. An appeal from the Monster Conservation Society to all adventurers: Everyone has a responsibility to protect the endangered Drainliars. Start with your own actions!",
    ["MonsterCollection10085"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>Demi-Human</color> monster that sighs \"waka waka\" at times. It is a fervent mining enthusiast, spending long periods of time in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mine</color>, so don't interrupt its mining work without cause. Even though its spade looks the worse for wear, it still looks rather handy in mining. Perhaps it is made from some special material.",
    ["MonsterCollection10086"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Appears to look like a strange beetle. However, different from everyone's expectations, an Arclouze only <color=#CA2E0AFF>curls up</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>when attacking</color> and does not, as everyone suspects, curl up for defense.",
    ["MonsterCollection10087"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skel Pirates</color> have simple equipment but they move with greater agility than Pirate Skeletons. From the wear and tear of their equipment, it seems that they have been dead for many years and once <color=#CA2E0AFF>their bones are scattered, it would be impossible to put them back together</color>. However, adventurers should still be careful, for a hit from the weapon in its hand is rather painful.",
    ["MonsterCollection10088"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A corpse wandering in the world <color=#CA2E0AFF>without consciousness</color>. The soul within it can no longer transcend to the afterlife. Therefore, the most common method is to destroy it completely. However, there is also evidence to show that the key to <color=#CA2E0AFF>driving Zombies'</color> movement is <color=#CA2E0AFF>some chemical</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10089"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An undead creature with an <color=#CA2E0AFF>exotic aura</color> that is very <color=#CA2E0AFF>uniquely</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>dressed</color>, attracting the interest of many Doppelganger lovers. Instead of the usual disgust Doppelgangers cause, they seem to be somewhat... <color=#CA2E0AFF>cute</color>? And it is apparently amongst the top three in the popularity ranking of the Payon Doppelganger Club?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color>\"I won't leave till I see the legendary Munak!\" said Eudora who was waiting outside the Munak Cave with her eyes fixed resolutely on the Euin Family elder.",
    ["MonsterCollection10090"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An undead creature with an <color=#CA2E0AFF>exotic aura</color> and, from its style of dress, seems to be from the same era as the Munaks nearby. Instead of the usual disgust Doppelgangers cause, they seem to emanate...<color=#CA2E0AFF>heroism</color>? The recent expansion of the Payon Doppelganger Club with its gradually increasing proportion of female adventurers voted for it to make it one of the top three in the popularity ranking.",
    ["MonsterCollection10091"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An undead creature with an exotic aura and very uniquely dressed. If it wasn't for the fact that her drifting figure <color=#CA2E0AFF>hovering in mid air</color> gives away that she is a Doppelganger, many adventurers would believe that they are going to have a romantic encounter. Ranks <color=#CA2E0AFF>first in the Payon Doppelganger Club popularity ranking all year round</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10092"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An animal symbolizing good luck in Payon's culture. It has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>proud nature</color>. In Payon's legends, Nine Tails <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring good luck</color> and help people. However, everyone is often puzzled as to why although it's called \"Nine Tail,\" it actually has ten tails.",
    ["MonsterCollection10093"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A very <color=#CA2E0AFF>cowardly</color> creature. Very few humans have seen them active. They are allies with the Giearths. The Safety Helmets on their heads are supposedly gifts from Giearths. Apparently, their activity can cause geological disasters, although unintentional. Currently, biologists in the kingdom are thinking about how to correctly guide them in reasonable activity that doesn't trigger geological disasters.",
    ["MonsterCollection10094"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Miners who met with a mining accident and still wander around the place where they died. They very much <color=#CA2E0AFF>hate Martins</color> and believe them to be the culprit behind his death. Yet, the pickaxes in their hands look brand new. What could have been used in preserving them?",
    ["MonsterCollection10095"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A mysterious monster living in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jade and Silver Mine</color> all year round. Despite appearing to have a physical body, it dissipates immediately upon death. This is completely incongruous with known monster research and biology and it is suspected to have come from another world. Nobody knows what they eat or how they take in energy. It seems as though they have been there since the day the Mjolnir Mine was discovered.",
    ["MonsterCollection10096"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> In her right hand a <color=#CA2E0AFF>crucifix</color> twined with roses and thorns, in her left a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dark Bible</color> that curses all things in the world, she wanders back and forth through Glast Heim St. Abbey. Legend has it that she was a heroine adulated by thousands, however, she became haunted by insurmountable resentment after her death, eventually causing her to turn her back on her faith and degenerate into an immortal <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doppelganger High Priestess</color>.\n\"That Evil Druid's hair style is much cooler than any ordinary demon's... Just look at that super-slick retro goddess style. That's why they call her the beauty who chases your soul through the night.\" Chester shrunk into a corner and watched through a high-powered binoculars.",
    ["MonsterCollection10097"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Very skilled in the techniques of <color=#CA2E0AFF>wielding twin blades</color> and seems to be still fighting to complete the last order received before he turned into a Skel. His skeleton is complete and not damaged in any way. He stays in the Munak Cave all year round looking for something. Perhaps it has to do with his last mission?",
    ["MonsterCollection10098"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An archer without any combat skills but has <color=#CA2E0AFF>proficient shooting skills</color>. However, apart from aiming and shooting, it has no other skills. The style of its weapon is very unique, different from any in the kingdom and amongst the pirates. The bow and arrows turn into ash upon its death and their creator has not been identified for now.",
    ["MonsterCollection10099"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Its appearance resembles wolves, but it is really a fox. Its long tail seems to have <color=#CA2E0AFF>artificial blades</color> equipped and if it brushes against you because you let down your guard, it probably means being in bed for the next few days.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A howl from biologists: Just who named them Matyrs?!",
    ["MonsterCollection10100"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> All of them were <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient Egyptian noblemen</color> before their deaths who had the privilege of being mummified. Perhaps even they had not expected that their wish for revival would really be fulfilled, though it was reanimation in the form of monsters which everyone shrinks from. Perhaps it is because their brains have rotted in the ages passed, Mummies <color=#CA2E0AFF>do not have self-consciousness</color> and are monsters that attack on instinct.",
    ["MonsterCollection10101"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>pet carcass</color> reborn after absorbing power from inside the pyramid. It has limited intelligence, looks like a fiendish guard dog and is unable to suppress its desire to bark madly. No wonder the tomb keeper Kessoso is always annoyed by them to the point of having a constant headache.",
    ["MonsterCollection10102"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> From their attire, they look to be <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient adventurers</color> who crawled out from the cemetery. As to who erected them tombstones in this underground place with no light, it is impossible to find out. Apparently, there are many ways of dealing with them, such as <color=#CA2E0AFF>holy water, light magic</color> and... peas?",
    ["MonsterCollection10103"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Serpent spirits with extraordinarily bewitching upper bodies. Legend has it that they are all <color=#CA2E0AFF>Osiris' female sevants</color>. However, don't ever stare at them. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>snake tails</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp claws</color> are no joke. Legend has it that some Isis actually keep their memories from before their death. Maybe some lucky people may be able to hear ancient gossip from them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10104"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An ox monster wielding a heavy Warhammer in its hands. Apparently, it was Osiris' guard before its death. Despite having <color=#CA2E0AFF>immense strength</color>, it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>slow in movement</color>, and neither its sight nor its hearing are sensitive enough. The Warhammer in its hands has seen as many ages pass as the pyramid has, but remains bright and shiny like new.",
    ["MonsterCollection10105"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Originally a normal spider, it mutated after being affected by an unknown energy and became gigantic. Perhaps the Mjolnir Mountains have a magnetic field which attracts curious creatures, and the mutated creatures are only getting larger. Don't panic if you encounter an Argos on the road. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>eyesight is poor</color>. Moving slowly can fool them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10106"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Why it carries a <color=#CA2E0AFF>retro messenger bag</color> all year round is unknown. Is this a new fashion amongst Mantises? Though the way they move with quick tiny steps seems somewhat timid and cowardly, they show no mercy to their enemies, so don't be fooled by them. A cut made by such <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp blades</color> is not something to joke about.",
    ["MonsterCollection10107"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> It is difficult to determine whether it is an animal or a plant based on biology. Those <color=#CA2E0AFF>straight white teeth</color> simply make people involuntarily believe a legend in which according to an anonymous record, a young girl in the prime of her youth died due to weight loss, possibly attributed to a plant which happened to be nearby at the time of her death. It isn't willing to miss out on the delicacies of the world just like that, so it opens and closes its mouth continually, wishing to make up for all the food missed during the diet.",
    ["MonsterCollection10108"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange insect with a hundred feet</color> and strange protruding spikes on its head. Getting too close may trigger trypophobia in some adventurers. It has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>gentle nature</color> and does not attack adventurers without cause under normal conditions.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An appeal from the Monster Conservation Society: Adventurers, please do not take an Argiope's shoes for fun. Losing its shoes may cause it to become uneasy and aggressive and launch retaliatory attacks against humans.",
    ["MonsterCollection10109"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The fifth in the goblin family. Possesses <color=#CA2E0AFF>immense strength</color> but only knows how to use a simple Spinecrusher. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is a born <color=#CA2E0AFF>pessimist</color>. It speaks with a stammer too.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Goblin Private Archive: Likes glittering things. Often subjected to his older brother's bullying pranks.",
    ["MonsterCollection10110"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The fourth in the goblin family. Brawny and accustomed to using its blacksmith hammer in battles. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>unperturbed</color> regardless of whatever happens. It has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>face of indifference</color> and always looks as though it is half asleep. It carries out some crafting work with its hammer in its tribe, but it is only limited to basic crafting. It doesn't have the high intellect of the Goblin Steamriders.",
    ["MonsterCollection10111"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The third in the goblin family. It can move with <color=#CA2E0AFF>incredible agility</color>. Fights with a Chain which requires advanced skills. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is born <color=#CA2E0AFF>simple and optimistic</color>, and brings joy to everyone.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Private Goblin Archive: In the annual Goblin Fighting Competition, they have held the champion position as the best fighters of the goblin family for many years with the highly difficult Flail technique.",
    ["MonsterCollection10112"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The second in the Goblin family. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Slow in movement</color>. Uses a Skullsplitter taller than itself in battles. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>cute, silly, and muddle-headed</color>. It speaks little too, as though always unaware of the situation.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Private Goblin Archive: Apparently, due to adequate exercise, their figure is acknowledged as the golden proportion in the tribe.",
    ["MonsterCollection10113"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The eldest in the Goblin family. Has superb <color=#CA2E0AFF>dagger</color>-wielding skills. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>lively and restless</color>. It loves to play pranks, but due to its <color=#CA2E0AFF>exceptional capabilities</color>, it is still respected by everyone as the eldest.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Private Goblin Archive: They hate string music but enjoy drum music. May have been influenced by ancient customs.",
    ["MonsterCollection10114"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>highly intelligent member</color> of the Goblin family. It became an assassin due to its <color=#CA2E0AFF>mastery in the crafting of bows and arrows</color>. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp-tongued, perceptive</color>, and always keeps an eye on its enemy's weaknesses.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Private Goblin Archive: A true battle maniac, but does not strike arbitrarily. Perhaps only prey that piques its interest are worthy of its archery skills.",
    ["MonsterCollection10115"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>highly intelligent</color> Goblin. The jet machine on its back is the culmination of its knowledge. Its nature is just like its mask, for it is <color=#CA2E0AFF>cheerful and thinks out of the box</color>. It is always mumbling words like \"science,\" but outsiders can't understand it.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A record from the Private Goblin Archive: It is the heir to the ancient Goblin civilization and may be the key figure to the continuation of Goblin culture.",
    ["MonsterCollection10116"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stonemasons</color> who took part in the building of the Sphinx Cavern and were forcibly buried together upon completion of the construction. While the power of the Sphinx has allowed them to gain <color=#CA2E0AFF>eternal life</color>, they can never be freed from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pressure of toil</color>. According to hearsay in Morroc, mysterious individuals from the church are summoning adventurers to help them transcend humanely.",
    ["MonsterCollection10117"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carpenters</color> who took part in building the Sphinx Cavern and were forcibly buried together upon completion of the construction. While the power of the Sphinx has allowed them to gain <color=#CA2E0AFF>eternal life</color>, they can never be freed from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>pressure of toil</color>. According to hearsay in Morroc, mysterious individuals from the church are summoning adventurers to help them transcend humanely.",
    ["MonsterCollection10118"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Originally an ancient Egyptian warlock, but turned <color=#CA2E0AFF>undead</color> after absorbing the power of the Sphinx. Nobody knows what form they actually take under those robes. Looking at them from the side reveals that they <color=#CA2E0AFF>don't even have legs</color>. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>magical powers</color> also differ from the known system. The Mage Guild seems to be investigating the matter in secret.",
    ["MonsterCollection10119"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Nobody knows their exact identity, and whether a rotting visage lies underneath their mask is a matter of everyone's imagination. Currently, the most common guess at their identity is that they were <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomb robbers</color> who coveted Osiris' treasure. Yet, despite being tomb robbers themselves, they have now become obstacles for their peers. Adventurers, do be careful.",
    ["MonsterCollection10120"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> If an orc fights to its last moments without giving up and chooses with the strength of its will to fight on after death, it will turn into a Zombie. They <color=#CA2E0AFF>know no pain and never give up</color>, forever carrying on the glory of the race. However, nobody knows where this strange magic comes from. Perhaps it is from traditional orc shaman magic.",
    ["MonsterCollection10121"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The Orcs are the best example of a race in which <color=#CA2E0AFF>all members are soldiers</color>. They usually reside peacefully outside Geffen, but once another race invades, every resident of the lowest class turns into a soldier and obeys the High Orc's commands to defend the honor of the race. Listen to their war cries carefully. They seem to be saying, \"Let's fight, mortals!\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10122"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The shaman magic handed down amongst Orcs can turn the strongest Orcs into evil creatures. This type of Orc Skeleton not only possess the battle prowess of Orcs, but also the mysterious power of <color=#CA2E0AFF>immortality</color>. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>heads</color> can <color=#CA2E0AFF>rotate 360 degrees</color>, preventing sneak attacks. The shields and battle axes in their hands are the symbols of power of the best warriors in the Orc race.",
    ["MonsterCollection10123"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A female orc, but its combat abilities are in no way inferior to the male orcs'. If you touch its child, you may be pursued to the end of the world by the rampaging female orc. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>persistence and stubbornness</color> exceed those of male Orc Warriors. Apparently, the last adventurer who challenged a female orc ran off to hide on Comodo. The orcs are indeed a scary race...",
    ["MonsterCollection10124"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> It is said that they are a branch of orcs cursed as punishment. They have mutated and lost their original orc forms. However, their combat abilities seem entirely unaffected. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>gigantic mutated palms</color> deal more damage instead and the dark and cursed shaman powers seem to have infused them with an unfaltering battle spirit.",
    ["MonsterCollection10125"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The formidable ones of the Chonchons. Apart from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>color mutation</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>difference in combat abilities</color> caused by their living environment, no significant difference has yet been found between them and normal Chonchons. They live in groups for long periods of time in the Labyrinth Forest. Be extra careful not to become entangled with them, or else you may be attacked in swarms.",
    ["MonsterCollection10126"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An Orc that uses a bow and arrows as its weapons. Due to their <color=#CA2E0AFF>accurate control of strength</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>excellent eyesight</color>, powerful shots can still be fired despite their very crude equipment.",
    ["MonsterCollection10127"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An Orc Warrior who has already proved itself, thereby obtaining superior equipment. It is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>main force</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>battles</color> and has an intelligence exceeding normal orcs, knowing how to lead soldiers instead of using merely brute force. Of course, that's judging by orc standards.",
    ["MonsterCollection10128"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chain</color>-wielding Kobold warrior with the inborn <color=#CA2E0AFF>pure and virtuous gaze</color> of the Kobold race. However, don't underestimate it. If you are hit by a sweep of the Kobold's Chain, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wound</color> will take <color=#CA2E0AFF>very long to heal</color>, probably caused by the Chain's special material. Even Doctor Wallace who specializes in unusual illnesses opines that at least two months of treatment will be needed.",
    ["MonsterCollection10129"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hammer</color>-wielding Kobold warrior with the inborn <color=#CA2E0AFF>pure and virtuous gaze</color> of the Kobold race. However, don't underestimate it. It is said that they have the greatest strength in the entire Kobold race. A smash from them may cause an immediate loss of mobility.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Between the Hammer-wielding Kobolds and the Orcs, I wonder whose strength is greater?\" Bertha pushed up her glasses and swiftly began calculating in her notes.",
    ["MonsterCollection10130"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Kobold good at using <color=#CA2E0AFF>crossbows</color> and with the proven ability to craft crossbows independently. Being the intelligent ones in the Kobold race, they have the most complete set of <color=#CA2E0AFF>weapon crafting abilities</color>. Apparently, a majority of the weapons used by other Kobolds are made by them too.",
    ["MonsterCollection10131"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Kobold good at using <color=#CA2E0AFF>axes</color>. They keep a superficial peace with the Hammer-wielding Kobolds and are not happy with them taking the title of the strongest. They are always on the lookout for opportunities to prove their standing in the race.",
    ["MonsterCollection10132"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An elegant gentleman in <color=#CA2E0AFF>black formal wear</color> with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>peculiar smile</color> on his face all year round. His head is not really a pumpkin. Adventurers bold enough to touch it, please remember to share how it felt like with the Monster Society. Halloween's trendiest Pumpkin decorations are supposedly created with his head as inspiration.",
    ["MonsterCollection10133"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A monster wandering around blindly underground in Geffen. Origin unknown. Nobody knows who is manipulating their controllers, and these cute dolls don't seem to have self-consciousness either. The most common theory is that the Marionette is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>taboo product</color> from the secret experiments of Alchemists, and many innocent lives seem to have been sacrificed.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> After hearing of this rumor, the Alchemist Guild specially issued a clarification notice. However, it feels even more suspicious. All sorts of rumors damaging to the Alchemist Guild are still circulating in Midgard.",
    ["MonsterCollection10134"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A troublemaker amongst Demons. It holds a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mini trident</color> in its hand, has a sly look on its face, and teasing its prey is its favorite activity. It dreams of becoming a great Demon, but this dream is crushed again and again by heartless adventurers. \"Look at those <color=#CA2E0AFF>little wings</color> on its back. They're just so cute! Who would believe it to be a Demon?\" Alexia picked up the struggling Deviruchi with her formidable powers, no less expected of the famous mischief maker of Geffen.",
    ["MonsterCollection10135"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Demons born from people's nightmares. Their pairs of eyes forever gazing into the void can <color=#CA2E0AFF>look into people's hearts</color>, see their inner fears, and bring them forth in the form of dreams. Legend has it that they are the Mounts of Spirit Knights and can come and go freely across the boundaries of the living and the dead. However, stay away from them if you still want a good night's sleep.",
    ["MonsterCollection10136"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Compared to a common Tarou, Cramps have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sturdier body</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tougher fur</color>, making them better able to survive in the perilous Clock Tower. When threatened, Cramps will concentrate magic onto the fur on their back, forming <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp spines</color> which they use to attack or defend. This is particularly useful when their opponent lets down their guard, allowing Cramps to gain the upper hand with a surprise attack.\n\"Don't underestimate Cramps just because they're small and cute! That's just asking to be turned into a Muka!\" The Monster Master raps his hand against the blackboard, emphasizing a crucial lesson for his students at the end of term.",
    ["MonsterCollection10137"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The Punk that inhabits one of the floors of the Clock Tower has a <color=#CA2E0AFF>round body</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>shimmering eyes</color>, but don't be fooled by its cute exterior. Born of <color=#CA2E0AFF>dust</color>, these monsters are very <color=#CA2E0AFF>cunning</color> and flutter their long ears to appeal to passing humans. Once their \"prey\" lets down their guard, the monster will reveal its savage nature...\n\"I don't want to think about that day again. It was a nightmare. It was as tame as a Pufferfish, then it opened its bloody maw and nearly tore my neck open with its sharp teeth!\" A fearful patient has a hand over his chest as he lies on the hospital bed in the Aldebaran Municipal Hospital.",
    ["MonsterCollection10138"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> When one thinks of witches, one typically associates them with black cats, magic cauldrons, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>flying brooms</color>. However, the Bathories of the Clock Tower are clearly different from the witches of rumor. They don't have black cats or cauldrons, and merely fly around on their brooms all year long in search of <color=#CA2E0AFF>fresh blood</color> to nourish themselves. Also, unreliable sources indicate that Bathories are afraid of the dust-born Punks. I wonder why?\n\"Ah... Achoo!\" A Bathory lets out a loud sneeze while riding her broom and wipes at her nose in disgust. That looks a lot like an allergy.",
    ["MonsterCollection10139"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters with clock-like appearances tend to be obsessed with time, and Alarms are one of the more <color=#CA2E0AFF>meticulous</color> ones. The guards stationed outside the Clock Tower will always hear <color=#CA2E0AFF>alarms</color> ringing from within the building at the same time every day. The Alarms wake up on time, hunt on time, eat on time, and even sleep on time. That's right, they're as rigid as the most well-trained soldier and keep time down to the second.\n\"That's... That's horrible... It reminds me of my time in boot camp... Sob...\" The newly-arrived recruit for Clock Tower guard duty covers his face. He looks like he's about to cry.",
    ["MonsterCollection10141"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Clocks are a <color=#CA2E0AFF>slow-</color><color=#CA2E0AFF>moving</color> monster. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>cumbersome</color> frame makes it difficult to actively hunt prey, so it tends to wait for a chance to strike. Unfortunately, long waits can sometimes put Clocks into a dormant state, giving them the appearance of a regular grandfather clock. Once upon a time in Aldebaran, a man mistakenly brought a dormant Clock into his shop, thinking it was an antique he could sell. It took an army of guards to put down the threat.",
    ["MonsterCollection10142"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> These guardians have been devoutly guarding the iconic building of Aldebaran for a very long time. No one knows where they come from, only that they've existed since the Clock Tower was built. Some fanatical Monster Researchers snuck into the heavily-guarded Clock Tower in an attempt to solve this mystery, but all they found were strange letters etched onto the monster's bodies...\n\"<color=#CA2E0AFF>R</color>.<color=#CA2E0AFF>B</color>.517D... I don't know what this means but it's written in the language of humans, which means... these Clock Tower Guardians were created by humans!\" says a certain Mech Monster Fanatic.",
    ["MonsterCollection10143"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The <color=#CA2E0AFF>infant</color> form of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ants</color>. Completely impossible to see any resemblance to their grown up forms. Very nutritious apparently, with six times as much protein as in beef. Mouthfeel... Ahem. As for its mouthfeel, fellow adventurers with discerning tastebuds, please try for yourselves.",
    ["MonsterCollection10144"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Penomena tentacles are <color=#CA2E0AFF>soft and chewy</color>, and have a texture akin to cartilage when heated, but they contain mucus that has a powerful <color=#CA2E0AFF>hallucinogenic</color> effect. Before cooking a Penomena, you must remove the gland from the tip of its tentacles and soak the tentacles in light salt water for some time. Then, place the tentacles in oil to fry at medium heat. Simmer with butter, onions, and white pepper and spread a layer of cheese croutons on top. Place it in an oven to cook for ten minutes and you have yourself a perfect bowl of Penomena Soup with Croutons au Gratin!\"\n—An excerpt from Cook's Strange Foods, by a chef dedicated to the creation of strange and novel dishes.",
    ["MonsterCollection10145"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> If you underestimate it just because it looks similar to normal Skels, then you'll be dead meat. Observe closely and you will discover that both their skeletons or their weapons glow with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>battle-hardened</color> dark light. Perhaps before they turned into Soldier Skeletons, they had already slaughtered the soldiers of many cities. Now, with dark energy in their possession, they have even less to fear.",
    ["MonsterCollection10147"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Despite being very similar to Planktons, its <color=#CA2E0AFF>vivid purple</color> subtly reveals hints of danger. It has always been an unchanging truth that the more beautiful something is, the greater the lurking danger. They inhabit places thick with Doppelganger aura for long periods of time and have lost their docility.",
    ["MonsterCollection10148"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Skel Pirate equipped with a double-edged dagger. It seems to have had extraordinary skills before its death. They appear to have died many years ago, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>double-edged</color> daggers they wield are still razor-sharp. A friendly reminder from the Mariner Association: If you unfortunately encounter a Dagger-wielding Skel Pirate on a Shipwreck, please be thoroughly prepared for battle. The opponent is a veteran with <color=#CA2E0AFF>plenty of battle experience</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10149"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Those Vocals that pursued music with <color=#CA2E0AFF>more power</color> eventually became Vocals. How do the violins in their hands play rock music? Humans can't understand it, but those Vocals have figured it out, displaying their power just by relying on sound waves. However, recently they've heard of an outstanding human bard who can play rock music with his lute. How about discussing music with him?",
    ["MonsterCollection10150"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A large bear with pure white fur. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Docile in nature</color> and does not initiate attacks against humans. Legend has it that they used to inhabit the Arctic in the northwest. Why did they migrate here? The priceless pure white furs of the Sasquatches has attracted many ambitious and greedy rogues, but they usually meet ends that are...",
    ["MonsterCollection10151"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Apart from their <color=#CA2E0AFF>mini stature</color>, there is almost no difference in appearance between them and the legendary Baphomet when their holding scythes. Many adventurers have suffered from their <color=#CA2E0AFF>powerful attacks</color>. Their appearance had once caused a huge panic—was that infamous demon god Baphomet about to be revived?",
    ["MonsterCollection10152"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Dwells together with the Picky in Morroc all year round. Rumor has it that they are the <color=#CA2E0AFF>infant forms of the Picky</color> and will shed the Egg Shell on their heads once they reach maturity. The way they move forward and hop is just like the Picky. However, strangely, it seems nobody has ever seen a Picky's Egg.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A notice from the Monster Academic Research Society: A bounty for Picky's Eggs are available all year round. We will give the discoverer an academic discovery reward of 100,000 Zeny.",
    ["MonsterCollection10154"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A messenger transformed from the soul power left behind in this world by the god of the underworld, Anubis. He has always existed as a guardian in Sphinx Cavern. Legend has it that he <color=#CA2E0AFF>guards the entrance to the underworld</color> and is responsible for maintaining the balance between the powers of this world and the underworld. However, there are always some adventurers who chance upon Anubis roaring with laughter during their adventures. What could have tickled them so?",
    ["MonsterCollection10155"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Legend has it that a Whisper's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloth</color> is actually the <color=#CA2E0AFF>physical materialization of spirit power</color> and is extremely rare. Therefore, the body size of a Giant Whisper is evidence of its great strength.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monster Researcher Bertha pushed up her glasses and remarked, \"If I sew 10 normal-sized Whisper's Cloths together, will I get a Giant Whisper? This is certainly an idea worth testing out!\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10157"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The strongest warrior amongst Skeletons. Its status is evident from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>superior equipment</color> it wields. Evil skeleton creatures do not have crafting abilities. So where did their equipment come from? Currently, no remains of any civilization have been found to bear resemblance to their equipment. The Monster Academic Research Society is in the midst of a new round of research and exploration. Should any relevant lead be found, please contact them immediately.",
    ["MonsterCollection10158"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>baby orc</color>. Its adorable features betray no hint of its future appearance. Of course, if you are accidentally bitten by it, you'll learn that the first signs of its combat ability are already showing. Remember to visit Doctor Wallace for some medication.",
    ["MonsterCollection10159"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Goblin which battles by controlling some strange flying machine. It is a type of <color=#CA2E0AFF>highly intelligent</color> Goblin and has learned to control this flying machine known as a helicopter in an extremely short time. Legend has it that it was designed and crafted by the Goblin Leader. Whether the Goblin Leader possesses an intelligence surpassing humans remains to be proven. However, at least there is evidence that Rotar Zairo already has the ability to learn high-tech skills.",
    ["MonsterCollection10163"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A Wizard obsessed with studying magic before his death. He was unfortunately <color=#CA2E0AFF>struck by lightning</color> and became a Necromancer with the help of his last obsession for magic. Being a master of <color=#CA2E0AFF>wind magic</color>, he infused the power of the wind into his staff, so he can raise a storm by simply holding it up. A notice from the Monster Academic Research Society: Adventurers are advised to remove all valuables before engaging in battle with Wind Ghosts to avoid them being blown away.",
    ["MonsterCollection10164"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> An Undead monster which perished due to starvation. The longing for food when it was alive manifested into an insatiable gaping mouth under its Manteau. However, what it wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>devour</color> at present is no longer food, but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>souls of the living</color>. Don't approach it unless you wish to become a fulfilling meal for it.",
    ["MonsterCollection10166"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A clown troupe performing at a noble banquet in Glast Heim were transformed into monsters cursed with <color=#CA2E0AFF>eternal smiles</color> after being overcome with dark energy. Roaming the ruins of the ancient city day and night, perhaps their collective memory as a family of <color=#CA2E0AFF>clowns</color> runs too deeply, because although they have lost their souls and consciousness, they still practice <color=#CA2E0AFF>juggling</color> every day. It seems that they one day hope to stand before an audience, awaiting a wave of cheers.\n\"If you look at them from afar, they look just like Amusement Park balloons. Who can tell that they're vicious monsters?\" exclaimed Morts, who had personally been chased by the clowns.",
    ["MonsterCollection10167"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Once a great power of the world, Glast Heim was not lenient when dealing with prisoners of war and criminals. Captured envoys were sentenced to death, and had their bodies <color=#CA2E0AFF>pierced with steel nails</color>. The torture they suffered in prison transformed into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bloody tears</color> you see flowing from their eyes. If they set their sights on you, rest assured that it is not in jest, for the accumulated resentment of a hundred years shall soon fall heavily upon your head.",
    ["MonsterCollection10168"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> As the only soldiers of the Chivalry whose bodies have disappeared completely, they lurk at the entrance of the Chivalry's base all day long, <color=#CA2E0AFF>running tirelessly in place</color>, as if staying forever trapped in a long-forgotten moment. Their <color=#CA2E0AFF>reddish armor</color> and helmets hint at the heroic swordsmen they were many years ago, but now they are merely undead soldiers who wave about their weapons blindly.",
    ["MonsterCollection10170"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> As the empire's former iron bastion, although this group of expert archers' <color=#CA2E0AFF>physical bodies</color> have already <color=#CA2E0AFF>withered away</color>, their souls still remain in the endless dark of the abyss, seeking a way to continue battle. They have never laid down their <color=#CA2E0AFF>bows and arrows</color>, and they search everywhere for their next target. Legend has it that they never miss their target, and none who enter the range of their arrows have any hope of escape.\n\"Even if the Raydric Archers come to fight us, when it comes to archery, the Euin Family will not lose,\" says Sun Euin proudly.",
    ["MonsterCollection10171"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Majoruros brandishes the large hammer in its hand, roaring with rage at every invader who dares disrupt his peace and quiet. Although it has <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp horns</color> akin to those of a bull, it is more accustomed to wielding the extremely heavy <color=#CA2E0AFF>hammer</color> it carries in battle. After all, in legend, it is said to be the king of a nation of minotaurs, so it has some consciousness from its half-human blood—at the very least, it must learn to use tools.\n\"Look at that steer! It seems I've already found inspiration for a new recipe—braised Majoruros! Sounds like it'll be just as delicious as braised Lunatic head!\" The cooking merchant Novia excitedly pointed at the Majoruros in the photo as her eyes lit up with anticipation.",
    ["MonsterCollection10172"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> In the long-abandoned Glast Heim Prison roams what is said to be the strongest Zombies of all time. After all, in life, these Zombies were warriors who weathered great bloodshed. Despite being unfortunately captured, their martial prowess is nothing to snuff at, and though their legs are shackled, a murderous air can still be felt seeping from behind their iron masks.\n\"Zombies and whatnot are so cool! Especially those Zombies wearing the iron masks. Just thinking about it gets me excited!\" The headgear merchant Rosha waved her hands about enthusiastically.",
    ["MonsterCollection10173"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> It is similar in appearance to a common Stainer except for its soft <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple</color> forewings. The Monster Researchers believe this change happened so that it can adapt to the dim environment of the Clock Tower. Its appearance is not the only thing that changed, however, as it has different habits and stronger <color=#CA2E0AFF>attacks</color> compared to the red Stainers. Be careful.\n\"To better adapt to life in the perilous Clock Tower, these Brilight are even showing signs of shifting towards <color=#CA2E0AFF>carnivorous</color> tendencies. They're remarkable survivors!\" Monster Researcher Bertha is rapidly jotting down notes of her observations.",
    ["MonsterCollection10175"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> If I have to name a monster that is the <color=#CA2E0AFF>epitome of a gambler</color>, it would be the Joker. Even in death, it remains bound to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Joker card</color>. Once it spots you, there's no escaping without playing a game or two with it. Of course, you always have the choice of winning a gamble or winning in battle.\n\"An obsession born from a gamble can only end in a gamble.\" A flash of steel arcs across the air. The armored adventurer lightly brushes shredded cards from his shoulder before he turns to walk away.",
    ["MonsterCollection10179"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> As the oldest group of insect monsters, they have their own pride. No matter how you put it, they are elders filled with wisdom who serve as positive role models for young children. Their stooped backs give off a scholarly style even in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color>—after all, there is no other group of monsters in the entire continent who both <color=#CA2E0AFF>carry books</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>wear Scholar Hats</color>, is there?\n\"Perhaps their wisdom has already reached a point where they can communicate with humans. If we could hold the first-ever Monster-Human Academic Exchange Conference, they would certainly be the first guests to be invited.\" Monster Researcher Bertha carefully observed the Sageworm photo for a moment before lowering her head and swiftly writing in her notes.",
    ["MonsterCollection10180"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Just who was it who sealed Dark Frame in the world within the mirror? Even it doesn't remember; all it remembers is that it spent great effort trying to break free of the mirror world, but sadly, it was fettered by a new dark force halfway through the implementation of its plan. And from that moment onward, it became a strange monster that <color=#CA2E0AFF>bears the burden of the world within the mirror</color>. It is still searching for a way out, and it's said that recently, it's trying to use a scapegoat method to draw a targeted adventurer into the mirror and replace itself.\n\"Hm... Does this so-called mirror world actually exist? Just what kind of energy does it contain? Seems worthy of investigating...\" The armor merchant Dael is seeking inspiration from monsters to design new armor.",
    ["MonsterCollection10182"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Perhaps it is because they have been entangled in the swamps for too long that the vengeful spirits of the nobility floating around Glast Heim finally coalesced into this elegant and noble appearance. Never without their gentlemanly <color=#CA2E0AFF>white gloves</color>, they invite passersby to dance with them. Of course, even if one is attending a dance in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color>, they must still don their distinct <color=#CA2E0AFF>bow ties</color>—how else would they display their status as Sting nobility?\n\"Ugh, what's with that sticky hand? I can't handle this sort of thing. It's just like the Ghouls under Geffen! That Payon Munak boy is still the cutest!\" Eudora took several steps backward as she looked at the Sting off in the distance.",
    ["MonsterCollection10184"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Who could have imagined that in the glorious past, this now limping group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>steel-clad Skels</color> were the beautiful lady knights of the Khalitzburg Chivalry, which were quite popular in Glast Heim. However, at this moment, they are shrouded in endless darkness and an aura of rage, leaving behind naught but soulless, empty shells brandishing their <color=#CA2E0AFF>blades</color>, turning them into monsters emitting evil auras in the ruins.\n\"I'm so curious what the ladies of the Khalitzburg looked like...\" Eudora, who is only interested in Doppelgangers, couldn't help but let out a sigh as she read \"A Comprehensive Guide to Doppelgangers.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10185"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Although the Zealotus roaming the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Churchyard</color> is famed for her glamor, just one look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bloodstained whip</color> in her hands tells you that this rose's thorns are razor sharp. If one wants to approach her, they may have to offer her their heart. Don't be fooled by her <color=#CA2E0AFF>enchanting</color> walk, charming like a top model in Midgard though, for she will be merciless when she brandishes her whip.\nReminder from the Glast Heim Ruins Conservation Association: A dangerous enchantress has appeared in the Glast Heim Churchyard. Beware of this beauty's traps, and be careful, adventurers!",
    ["MonsterCollection10187"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A civilization's prosperity is always accompanied by countless bones and sacrifices—though of course, if one is lucky, they'll become a prisoner of war thrown into a dark jail. However, Glast Heim's prisoners never imagined that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shackles</color> on their wrists and ankles would give them an opportunity for immortality. After endless slavery and torture, these prisoners of war clad in <color=#CA2E0AFF>striped prison uniforms</color> were corrupted by a dark aura, becoming Skeleton Prisoners that would roam the Glast Heim Prison until the end of days, waiting for the next adventurer to pass by.",
    ["MonsterCollection10190"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> With one hand <color=#CA2E0AFF>wielding a hook</color> and the other wielding a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp magic saw</color>, Rybio has appeared near the Glast Heim Churchyard for many years. It seems to have never removed the <color=#CA2E0AFF>unique hood</color> covering its head, leading to curious adventurers often trying to steal it. However, not one of them has ever succeeded, and numerous people have been even been reduced to ghosts beneath Rybio's saw blade.\n\"I'm less interested in Rybio's weapons than its hood. If anyone can grab me that hood, I'll give them a limited-edition entrance ticket to visit my most prized collection.\" Material Merchant Sampson carefully evaluated everything on Rybio's person before making this judgment.",
    ["MonsterCollection10192"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Phendarks with <color=#CA2E0AFF>absolute power</color> are the last barrier to the Clock Tower. Over the years, a number of adventurers have attempted to explore deep into the Clock Tower to find out what’s going on, but almost no one has been able to break their iron-clad defenses. Only curious Monster Researchers can take a keen interest in their true appearance under the mask. “Look! There’s a strange <color=#CA2E0AFF>mark</color> on the brow of that mask! I speculate that this is probably some kind of power-suppressing spell! In other words, if the mask can be removed, these Phendarks will become even more powerful!” A Monster Researcher holding binoculars hides in the distance, his tone revealing an uncontainable excitement.",
    ["MonsterCollection10193"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Battle is their entire reason for being. In the pursuit of the highest realm of combat, in life, they scoured the land in search of worthy adversaries to duel. After they lost to the commander of the White Knights, they remained in Glast Heim, where they devoted themselves to their training and prepared to face their former opponent once more. Little did they know that when Glast Heim underwent its massive change, they would be reduced to Wanderers, <color=#CA2E0AFF>destined to wield their swords forever</color>.\n\"Just look at this <color=#CA2E0AFF>exotic attire</color>! If he hadn't been changed into an evil monster, surely he would be as handsome as Master Halmod himself!\" Enchantment Merchant Stella shook her head with regret as she gazed at the Wanderer's figure in the distance.",
    ["MonsterCollection10194"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Once the world-renowned White Knights of Glast Heim, they have now become the sinister witnesses to the haunted city of Glast Heim, gazing into the abyss of death and emerging from people's nightmares. These warriors, driven mad by bloodlust, still carry the banner of the Kingdom of Glast Heim, and all that remains on their once-handsome faces are their ferocious, <color=#CA2E0AFF>bloody maws</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>six</color> terrifying <color=#CA2E0AFF>eyes</color>. Though they were once clad with suits of armor, these knights are now demonic spirits covered in ghoulish scales.\n\"The Abysmal Knight and his warhorse can be said to have a profound friendship. I too will never give up on my Cocoa!\" After hearing the legend of the Abysmal Knight, Young pet his own Pecopeco mount with a sparkle of determination in his eyes.",
    ["MonsterCollection10195"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> If it is not for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bloody stench of their breath</color> that can be smelled coming from their faces when near them, they would look like large statues with teeth and claws. They move slowly and almost motionlessly. However, their <color=#CA2E0AFF>spiked shields</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>sharp swords</color> will mercilessly pierce the chest of any enemy who approaches.\n\"I don't want to fight like those monsters. They're just Orc Warriors wearing top-notch armor.\" Weapon Merchant Anderson held his own new weapon tightly, afraid of scraping the newly-made hilt.",
    ["MonsterCollection10196"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Lurking in the coral reef in the shallow sea, they <color=#CA2E0AFF>hide themselves</color> among the bright colors of coral, waiting for a chance to seize a passing fish. Their bodies are decorated with pupil-shaped patterns, which shine ominously at night. For some reason, they <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the orders of Mermen</color> under certain circumstances.",
    ["MonsterCollection10197"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> When the worn claws have too many ages to swim in the underwater torrents, even a Vadon would long for some peaceful years in the old age. Look at all the peace here, Comodo is obviously a perfect place. The moist and salty sea breeze flutters the grey tentacles, and the warm currents bring <color=#CA2E0AFF>algae</color> to the rotten teeth. As for predators...?\n <color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"Pew! Pew pew, pew pew! (Hmph, you crippled bird is never going to catch this crab moving sideways!)\" Crab waves the <color=#CA2E0AFF>claws</color> in complacence and looks at the Ragglers jumping on the distant beach, spitting lots of bubbles.",
    ["MonsterCollection10198"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> These monsters should be living in the seas, but gradually moved to the dry <color=#CA2E0AFF>deserts</color>. In adaptation to lives on the land, they hide the big tails used to push water by squeezing them into <color=#CA2E0AFF>seashells</color>. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>shells</color> they carry now serve as important tools by cutting the tough skins of desert plants, providing the key method of water supply.\n \"Look! The Sea Otters have started their shell maintenance! Polish them on the rocks, rinse them in plant juice, and rub them with fish oil to prevent oxidation...\" Naughty children hide behind the bushes, quickly writing on something with \"Monster Observation Diary\" on the cover. Oh, it seems that the due date of winter vacation assignment is not far away.",
    ["MonsterCollection10199"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Unable to fly due to <color=#CA2E0AFF>short wings</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>born crippled</color> because of a certain genetic disease, they seem to devote their lives to returning to the sky, even imitating humans. Even equipped with special <color=#CA2E0AFF>goggles</color> made for human pilots, they can only stand on the tip of toe, and jump to draw near the sky in their dreams.\n \"Their crippled bodies do not stop their hearts from soaring.\" A famous adventurer commented when arriving here.",
    ["MonsterCollection10200"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters with their own <color=#CA2E0AFF>society</color>, where clear hierarchy and divided tasks are established. They are capable of quick learning and utilizing tools, and love to settle beside water, where their resilient body brings an advantage in speedy food acquirement. Due to the similar living habits, however, they are often engaged in territory clashes with Alligators, monsters also inhabiting Zenhai Marsh, and really have a beef with them.",
    ["MonsterCollection10201"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Branches on the back are there to<color=#CA2E0AFF>absorb sunshine</color>, enabling them to spend a whole day in the sun without moving. Surprisingly, a Stem Worm also feeds on organisms, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>hunts for insects</color> to keep itself in function, when not getting enough sunshine for a while. As a result, the debate about their identity as animals or plants never stops.",
    ["MonsterCollection10202"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Different from Roda Frogs, who love to bathe in the sea, Thara Frogs prefer exposing themselves to the air, and control the skin moisture by producing <color=#CA2E0AFF>mucus</color>. The bright color signals the <color=#CA2E0AFF>lethal poison</color> they have, not from poison glands, but from the food they intake. Thara Frogs are said to have special digestive systems, which separate and discharge the poisonous substances, while absorbing only the safe components.",
    ["MonsterCollection10203"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Unusual penguins living in the sand, with habits more similar to Martins instead of birds. With <color=#CA2E0AFF>stout</color> bodies, they are unexpectedly <color=#CA2E0AFF>agile</color> and hard to catch. Also, they are natural alcohol lovers, making trouble for local residents to get a drink or two. Words have that they would hide beside local bars, follow the customers and <color=#CA2E0AFF>steal their clothes</color>, so that the beers are handed out...\n \"Eh... Eh?! That's all! I promise, that's all! You've got all my beers! At least leave my trousers!\" Screams of a young man echo on the beach at night, and are washed away by the waves...",
    ["MonsterCollection10204"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Pest is the name, and the pupil-shaped organ is actually their <color=#CA2E0AFF>mouthparts</color>, while their eyes have long been out of function due to all the time spent underground. To compensate for the lost sight, many of their nerves are transferred to the skin, thus the extreme sensitivity to <color=#CA2E0AFF>vibration</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>temperature fluctuation</color>. Legends have that, the flexible skin of Pests once served as the main material of<color=#CA2E0AFF>strings</color> for bards.\n \"...And then? Later, people found that sheep intestines boast more suitable length, and the string-making skills using Pest skin are gradually lost. If you have something with Pest skin strings, you're gonna be rich.\" The bard with a grey beard cleared his pipe, exhaling gently an elegant smoke ring.",
    ["MonsterCollection10205"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Bug-like monsters with <color=#CA2E0AFF>hard shells on their back</color>, multiple feet and no wings. With their <color=#CA2E0AFF>palates</color> sticking out like horns, they hunt and intimidate enemies. The lifetime of an individual is short, but the species has been around for a long time, being the proud <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness</color> of centuries of changes here on Comodo.",
    ["MonsterCollection10206"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>gang</color> wandering beside the residence of Euphonic Symphony, whose main task is robbing, targeting no one but dancers and bards inside the residence. They always <color=#CA2E0AFF>shoot and run</color>, and never stay for long - typical bastards. Members abide by a strict dressing code, where everyone <color=#CA2E0AFF>dyes their hair red, steps on clogs, and wears golden chains with shorts</color>. More importantly, clothes can never be worn before torn, so their wild nature is displayed.",
    ["MonsterCollection10207"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> With slim bodies, smooth skins, short limbs and strong muscles, they move extremely fast. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poison Glands</color> hide inside the mouth, with which they inject poison into preys with teeth and numb them. Nereid makes <color=#CA2E0AFF>great medicine</color>, so the island residents have been trying to cultivate them for more financial benefits.",
    ["MonsterCollection10208"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters living in groups in the northeastern part of Zenhai Marsh, gathering near <color=#CA2E0AFF>ponds and streams</color>, and skillfully hiding in streams during hunting. Despite the ferocious appearance, they actually rarely start a fight. When revealing their <color=#CA2E0AFF>claws</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>teeth</color>, they are basically bluffing, except for encounters with Alligators also residing at Zenhai Marsh. The two clans are always fighting over <color=#CA2E0AFF>territory issues</color> and on really bad terms.",
    ["MonsterCollection10209"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Ancient, mysterious monsters spending most of their lives in <color=#CA2E0AFF>slumber</color>. They live on the ample magic in the cave of Comodo, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>rarely require any food</color>. Just like <color=#CA2E0AFF>annual rings</color>, the totems on their bodies grow with age. Older the Megalith, more complex the pattern. Thanks to the trait, they are historians' favorite monsters, and are said to have finally confirmed the era where the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dragon War</color> on Comodo was waged.",
    ["MonsterCollection10210"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bad memory</color>, always <color=#CA2E0AFF>covering their heads</color> in attempts to recall important things. Failure to remember would render them crazy, and give them serious headaches. Please note, that the Seals in the above condition are extremely <color=#CA2E0AFF>aggressive</color>. Please keep away, Adventurers, or you will have to see who has the <color=#CA2E0AFF>harder</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>head</color> between you and the Seal.\n \"Really? The Seals are pounding their heads again? Hurry... take the coconuts for smashing, now!\" Islanders harvesting coconuts are totally exhilarated. Great, seems that someone else is doing the work, again.",
    ["MonsterCollection10211"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Considered as the most <color=#CA2E0AFF>concrete</color> barrier found in monsters, they rarely take physical damage. On contrary, the extraordinary defense is accompanied by terrible movement and agility, which put them at disadvantage against fast enemies. Once in a while, they shed skins and suffer from decreased defense, so a hidden corner is always chosen for the period.",
    ["MonsterCollection10212"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monsters enjoying advantages due to high <color=#CA2E0AFF>speed</color> and great <color=#CA2E0AFF>balance</color>, as well as perfect <color=#CA2E0AFF>dynamic vision</color>, capable of precisely targeting the prey during speedy flight. They use unique bow and arrows as weapons, and the arrow heads are especially different. Forged from unknown materials, the arrow heads emit <color=#CA2E0AFF>red</color> radiance when infused with magic, as if surrounded by fire.\n \"So the Gargoyles keep wandering around the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon eggs</color>? Hmm... Could it be that dragon eggs are the key to the arrow head mystery?\" The Craftsman always staying with the stove is finally traveling outside the Hermit's Village, determined to compete with the Gargoyles in terms of forging skills.",
    ["MonsterCollection10214"]="Beautiful things are always poisonous, which Medusa is perfectly described by this phrase. Monsters like these are good at deceiving their prey with their <color=#44afee>beautiful appearance</color>. Almost no one can keep a straight head under the influence of Medusa's smile. When they fall into it, the warm, gentle touch they enjoy will transform into <color=#44afee>venomous fangs</color> that pierce the veins under their neck. Run? No, you can't run from it. She's got <color=#44afee>a pair of eyes</color> that can reflect your fear and make you into a <color=#44afee>stone sculpture</color> forever.",
    ["MonsterCollection10215"]="In this lawless land of Niflheim, the Queen of the Underworld allows everything that can unleash your inner self. Hence, the Bloody Murderers were born and fed with <color=#44afee>blood</color>. Their favorite game is to attack the lone traveler in the dark with their <color=#44afee>masks</color> covering their faces.\n\"Who... who's there? Get lost! Stop following me!\" There is no response to his hysterical questions in this dimly lit darkness. It's at this moment that the <color=#44afee>blade</color> hidden in the shadow touches his neck...",
    ["MonsterCollection10217"]="<color=#44afee>Insect</color> monsters that live in Kalala Swamp. They are <color=#44afee>mellow</color> creatures that <color=#44afee>hate confrontation</color>, and they survive by taking in the magic power within the <color=#44afee>gravel and soil</color>. In return, they nurture this land with their droppings, which makes them an indispensable part of the ecosystem of Kalala Swamp.",
    ["MonsterCollection10219"]="This Nameless Island is a secret <color=#44afee>execution site</color> located in the Arunafeltz territorial waters. Besides housing outcasts, this is also the place where executed prisoners are buried. Those decapitated by the executioner become monsters filled with hatred, living on the <color=#44afee>souls of living</color> to fuel their unquenchable <color=#44afee>fire of hatred</color>.\n\"The flame surrounding those skulls can extend the dying's lifespan to a certain extent. We named them <color=#44afee>Eternal Flame</color> and included them in our potion-making research topic...\" The researcher with glasses turns on the switch, and the glass container fills with a massive amount of liquid, submerging the screaming flame skull...",
    ["MonsterCollection10220"]="Being a Wootan, but on the wrong side of the tribe. They are the \"weaklings\" who failed to pass the trial upon reaching adulthood and were filtered out by their kind. Their pasts brought them together as Wootan Shooters. Despite lacking innate strength and muscular physiques, their <color=#44afee>intelligence</color>, <color=#44afee>dexterity</color>, and <color=#44afee>endurance</color> allowed them to survive and find their place in Kalala Swamp.\n\"... Interesting. Is there oppression and resistance in the monster society as well? Maybe one day... They will rule the forest among all Wootan Fighters and ascend to the throne.\" The scholar watching a Wootan Shooter craft his weapon laughs slightly, reflecting his deep emotions.",
    ["MonsterCollection10221"]="Hell Poodle is the most loyal servant of Hel, Queen of the Underworld. But this loyalty isn't from the true intent of the heart but a piece of paper, a <color=#44afee>soul contract</color> that cannot be revoked until the end of time. All living creatures who entered a pact with Hel will surrender their souls forever when they die, becoming the <color=#44afee>Realm of the Dead's gatekeeper</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10223"]="When the <color=#44afee>dead</color> return from the Underworld, they refuse to rest beneath the soil, even though their bodies are rotten. However, some hidden worshipers believe that this is a <color=#44afee>miracle</color> that brought back the dead from a netherworld.",
    ["MonsterCollection10224"]="True leader of Kalala Swamp, who manages and leads other groups that reside in the forest. He worships <color=#44afee>strength</color> and does not allow weaklings or those with inborn disabilities to remain in his tribe, even for his own kind. Upon reaching adulthood, every Wootan Fighter must pass a harsh <color=#44afee>trial</color>, and those who fail will be expelled from the tribe.",
    ["MonsterCollection10225"]="These monsters are <color=#44afee>lively</color> and <color=#44afee>noisy</color>, but their intelligence is on par with humans. They had a good relationship with Utans long before the Umbala rainforest became a tourist attraction, and they are now even the setter of this wildly popular Choco pet trend among the aristocrats. According to an unreliable source, some Choco pet enthusiasts are preparing the first <color=#44afee>Pet Contest</color>, during which the evaluator will select the breed most widely accepted by the majority based on fur color, size, and exercise performance. This is a systematic buying guide for anyone looking to get a Choco as a pet.",
    ["MonsterCollection10226"]="A creepy and evil monster. A baby-shaped <color=#44afee>fruit</color> will grow on its branch after absorbing a <color=#44afee>huge amount of soul</color>, during which it will keep devouring souls to fuel its energy. Upon ripening, it falls to the soil, becoming a new <color=#44afee>seed</color> for other yet to emerge Gibbets.",
    ["MonsterCollection10227"]="Share a similar appearance as Ragged Zombie, but the academic field has yet to determine whether it belongs to the same class of monsters as Ragged Zombie because these Zombie Slaughters <color=#44afee>attack their own kind</color> without hesitation. Compared to the slow-moving Ragged Zombies, their movement and intelligence are superior, and they can even use <color=#44afee>cold weapons</color>. Don't try them if you don't feel confident enough.",
    ["MonsterCollection10228"]="Many people have wondered why there are so many pumpkins in the Realm of the Dead. You will find the answer to this once Dullahan attacks you. As ferocious monsters, they are always searching for their lost heads and eager to <color=#44afee>decapitate anyone who looks like them</color>. If they ever set their eyes on you, the only way to escape is to place the <color=#44afee>pumpkin</color> on their neck to fool them into thinking they have found the head. Thus, every household in Niflheim began to grow pumpkins on their own...\n\"Brainless (think of a monster).\" —Selected from the Niflheim Riddles Collection. Please check the appendix for answers.",
    ["MonsterCollection10229"]="According to Utan legend, Spirit Tree was grown from the sprout of the Yggdrasil. As the descendent of Spirit Tree, Miwa is considered a spirit that carries <color=#44afee>Yggdrasil's power</color>. They can <color=#44afee>manipulate grass and trees</color> to ripen fruits that contain special powers, making them the <color=#44afee>leader</color> among all creatures in Luluka Forest.",
    ["MonsterCollection10230"]="Her cute appearance is totally out of place in the Realm of the Dead. With a <color=#44afee>cost</color>, Loli Ruri has squared a deal with the Queen of the Underworld for Niflheim's residency, inspiring the ideas of many artists because of her action, and many works were born because of this.\n\"A charming girl who is afraid of eternal night has fallen into the Underworld for her loved one. Ahh, what a romantic background setting...\" A new writer gathers ideas for her work while reading the legend of Loli Ruri, exclaiming her heartfelt feelings.",
    ["MonsterCollection10231"]="A monster in the legend that can predict the future, wearing clothes made of a shroud. It spreads the signal of death during darkness, and people consider it an <color=#44afee>ill-omen</color>. In fact, Banshee doesn't actively attack humans but only cries over the death taint.",
    ["MonsterCollection10232"]="There is no doubt that Dragon Tail is a <color=#44afee>tender</color> monster, but you should never underestimate its destructive power. The <color=#44afee>stinger</color> is Dragon Tail's most effective and aggressive weapon after it emerges from a pupa in adulthood. Their <color=#44afee>wings</color> that shine under sunlight are poachers' favorite since a complete set of <color=#44afee>Transparent Wings</color> is only enough to make a veil shorter than a finger, but its prices are the same as gold.",
    ["MonsterCollection10233"]="Although it looks remarkably like a human, it is a monster incarnated from a tree. Share the same habit as vegetation, as it will search for a place filled with sunlight and bury itself in the soil for energy recovery.",
    ["MonsterCollection10234"]="Stone Shooters are crafted in a similar way to Wooden Golems, where the body is composed of <color=#44afee>delicate machinery</color>, but the appearance is disguised as Plant Monsters. Since Stone Shooter has a shorter lifespan than Wooden Golem, it has a <color=#44afee>limited amount of energy reserved</color>, reducing its durability after each attack. They reach the end of their lives when they exhaust all energy stored within.\nAfter witnessing Stone Shooter's death, a bard begins mumbling a poem, \"Your life must be burnt... For the fireworks to go off!\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10235"]="Compared to ordinary Frilldora, it has <color=#44afee>tougher skin and claws</color> to ensure it can dig up the worm eggs deep down in the soil. Dislikes sunlight and fond of gloomy and damp areas. When it senses danger, it opens up the umbrella-shaped membrane around its neck and it goes into an <color=#44afee>estivation</color> state when the weather gets hot enough and sleeps in a discreet shadowy place until the next season arrives.",
    ["MonsterCollection10236"]="Even though they are classified as a monster, they are more like delicate pieces of machinery. Every day, they repeat the same routine, and no one knows who programmed them that way. Someone has tried to dissect a dead Wooden Golem just to find out there is a strange <color=#44afee>gear core</color> inside the body. The toothed crown consists of <color=#44afee>twenty-four</color> teeth that are evenly distributed around the bearing, which takes twenty-four hours for it to go through a cycle. At midnight on the hour, the core <color=#44afee>resets to its original position</color> and starts <color=#44afee>cycling for another round</color>...\nAfter witnessing how Wooden Golem functions for their day, this random traveling Bard begins mumbling a poem, \"They never die yet only have one day of their lives.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10237"]="A monster without a <color=#44afee>physical form</color>, <color=#44afee>almost undetectable with bear eyes</color>, let alone catching it. It's extremely sensitive to changes in the environment. If the air pressure is too high or too low, it <color=#44afee>dissipates</color>. For monster researchers, how to obtain a Breeze that can be used in long-term research has become the most debatable topic in the academic world.\n\"Have you heard? A lot of Breezes appeared inside Kiel Khayr's Estate recently, which is incredible! If I can get my hands on one of those...\" Inside the monster department's classroom of Juno University, two students are excitedly discussing the trending news.",
    ["MonsterCollection10238"]="A monster that exists in the folktales and legends. Rather than a living creature, it is more like an <color=#44afee>aggregation of consciousness</color>. It can enhance its power by absorbing humans' <color=#44afee>negative emotions</color>. Confoundingly, however, this malevolent monster has a really cute and endearing appearance. When its <color=#44afee>glistening eyes</color> meet yours, almost nobody can withstand its attack of <color=#44afee>adorability</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10239"]="Poring of <color=#44afee>frost attribute</color>, with its girlish <color=#44afee>Morandi Purple</color>, has won many fans. It has been the <color=#44afee>runner-up</color> in the \"Poring Supporters' Group\" for years in terms of popularity, only one place behind the original mascot Poring. However, due to its <color=#44afee>bad temper</color>, it can hardly be a house pet.\n\"Darn it... So close... I will do better on the poll next time! One day, I will lift <color=#44afee>Marin</color> to the throne of Porings...\" After yet another popularity contest, a little boy holds tightly to his Marin doll with a frustrated face.",
    ["MonsterCollection10240"]="A lovely monster resembling a beautiful <color=#44afee>butterfly</color> that feeds on dew and Nectar. On each <color=#44afee>full-moon night</color>, they gather together and gracefully dance around blossoms. The <color=#44afee>phosphorus powder</color> on their wings contains a touch of magic power, which can expedite the blossoming of plants. Hence, they are the favorite kind of monsters of flower growers.\n\"Shh... Look, these Menblatt start dancing already. We must not disturb them. By sunrise, these roses will bloom.\" Under the silver moonlight, an experienced flower grower gently taps his grandson's head, silently appreciating this once-a-month celebration.",
    ["MonsterCollection10241"]="Looking like a walking sunflower at first glance, it's easily mistaken for a plant monster. But in fact, it's a type of insect in <color=#44afee>parasitic form</color>. Using its <color=#44afee>gigantic disc floret</color>, it lures in the prey and devours them with the mouth hidden within its stamens. As this habit can be used to <color=#44afee>get rid of flies and mosquitoes at home</color>, many people have a household Geographer as their pet. Just beware: don't get eaten by it!\n\"Ouch! Ouch! Ouch! AHHHH! Let go of me! Delia... Help me! Delia! It's biting my head again!\" Wallace, whose head has taken numerous <color=#44afee>Geographer</color> bites, is desperately seeking help from his friend.",
    ["MonsterCollection10242"]="<color=#44afee>Guardians of the Ruins</color> in the depth of Juperos Ruins. The various colors on their bodies are painted to distinguish their <color=#44afee>range of operation</color>. For example, the <color=#44afee>brown</color> one only shows up around the <color=#44afee>experimental base ruins</color> located at the center of the ruins. Moreover, the behavior of Venatu demonstrates a set pattern. Once they discover someone is approaching the ruins, they will show extreme <color=#44afee>hostility</color> against the target. Eden Group speculates that the ancient civilization might have used Venatu as a protective barrier for the ruins. If one could break through their guards, they might be able to reveal the truth of this part of history.",
    ["MonsterCollection10243"]="A monster that hides behind <color=#44afee>leaves</color> to cover up its ugly appearance, only revealing its eyes and feet. It's said that nobody, up to this day, has seen what it truly looks like. Due to its <color=#44afee>timid</color> and <color=#44afee>shy</color> nature, this kind of monster closes its eyes and retracts its feet whenever it's scared, becoming a curled-up <color=#44afee>grass ball</color> in solitude. And because of its <color=#44afee>featherlight weight</color>, it often gets blown away by the wind while staying in this form, making it difficult to find the way home.",
    ["MonsterCollection10244"]="Initially, it was just ordinary <color=#44afee>sand</color>. But somehow, it took shape after absorbing the <color=#44afee>unknown energy</color> from Juperos Ruins and would return to its original state once leaving the birthplace. It neither <color=#44afee>feeds</color> nor <color=#44afee>thinks</color>. The only thing it does is constantly moving toward the place where the energy is more concentrated. Therefore, many Eden Group members are using this nature of Sleeper to pinpoint prime exploration zones inside the ruins.\n\"Boss, the Sleeper deployed at G3 has started moving toward Spot S, which is highly similar to our previous estimation...\" In the camp located at El Mes Gorge. Isaack points at the blinking red dot on the instrument, reporting to Alquein his investigation results.",
    ["MonsterCollection10245"]="To cope with the limited food supply in the desert, these monsters <color=#44afee>migrated</color> here from the faraway Morroc, eventually making <color=#44afee>Juno</color> their home. In response to environmental changes, evolution graces them with even more <color=#44afee>vivid tail feathers</color>, allowing them to fan these feathers for courtship or to deter enemies. They are rarely treated as mounts in the technologically advanced Republic. Instead, their <color=#44afee>delicious eggs</color> are widely known as a local delicacy.\n\"Today' Chef Special: Creamy Scrambled Eggs. Note: Prepared using wild-caught Grand Peco eggs. A seasonal specialty that's only available for a limited time.\" As comes the annual mating season of Grand Peco, restaurants in Juno have all released their new seasonal menus.",
    ["MonsterCollection10246"]="Developed by <color=#44afee>Khayr Consortium</color>, this retro robot is inspired by the mech wreckage unearthed from Juperos Ruins in many aspects, making it extremely popular among history enthusiasts. The <color=#44afee>color paint</color> on their shoulders is for <color=#44afee>identifying their models</color>. For instance, the <color=#44afee>green color</color> means the model has an advantage in <color=#44afee>speed</color>. These robots were first made for <color=#44afee>security tasks</color> in Kiel Khayr's Academy but soon got abandoned due to their complex maintenance process. Nowadays, most Dimiks have become collectibles, with only a few of the <color=#44afee>malfunctioning ones</color> remaining in the woods next to the academy, forsaken and forgotten.",
    ["MonsterCollection10247"]="Inhabitants of the <color=#44afee>El Mes Gorge</color>, these gregarious monsters have developed slender and nimble <color=#44afee>hooves</color> for hopping between the cliffs, allowing them to move with ease on the sheer rock surface. These monsters, <color=#44afee>docile by nature</color>, munch on the <color=#44afee>shrubs</color> commonly seen in the gorge, and will never initiate attacks on humans. The fur on their backs is soft, which is ideal for making winter coats.",
    ["MonsterCollection10248"]="<color=#44afee>Guardians of the Ruins</color> in the depth of Juperos Ruins. The various colors on their bodies are painted to distinguish their <color=#44afee>range of operation</color>. For example, the <color=#44afee>blue</color> one only shows up at the <color=#44afee>cable car ruins</color> located south. Moreover, the behavior of Venatu demonstrates a set pattern. Once they discover someone is approaching the ruins, they will show extreme <color=#44afee>hostility</color> against the target. Eden Group speculates that the ancient civilization might have used Venatu as a protective barrier for the ruins. If one could break through their guards, they might be able to reveal the truth of this part of history.",
    ["MonsterCollection10249"]="<color=#44afee>Guardians of the Ruins</color> in the depth of Juperos Ruins. The various colors on their bodies are painted to distinguish their <color=#44afee>range of operation</color>. For example, the <color=#44afee>orange</color> one only shows up at the <color=#44afee>massive structure ruins</color> located northeast. Moreover, the behavior of Venatu demonstrates a set pattern. Once they discover someone is approaching the ruins, they will show extreme <color=#44afee>hostility</color> against the target. Eden Group speculates that the ancient civilization might have used Venatu as a protective barrier for the ruins. If one could break through their guards, they might be able to reveal the truth of this part of history.",
    ["MonsterCollection10250"]="Developed by <color=#44afee>Khayr Consortium</color>, this retro robot is inspired by the mech wreckage unearthed from Juperos Ruins in many aspects, making it extremely popular among history enthusiasts. The <color=#44afee>color paint</color> on their shoulders is for <color=#44afee>identifying their models</color>. For instance, the <color=#44afee>orange color</color> means the model has an advantage in <color=#44afee>strength</color>. These robots were first made for <color=#44afee>security tasks</color> in Kiel Khayr's Academy but soon got abandoned due to their complex maintenance process. Nowadays, most Dimiks have become collectibles, with only a few of the <color=#44afee>malfunctioning ones</color> remaining in the woods next to the academy, forsaken and forgotten.",
    ["MonsterCollection10251"]="A demi-human monster with <color=#44afee>broad wings</color> that loves to nest atop high trees or cliffs and use their distinct <color=#44afee>shrieks</color> to attract prey. Numerous folktales depict the Harpy as an evil spirit that snatches infants, saying that it wanders in the dead of night, tracks down the babies by their cries, and sneaks them off to its nest to consume.\n\"Stop crying! Didn't I tell you that kids crying at night are going to be eaten by the Harpies? No more tears, and now go to your bed...\" Late at night in St. Caviderina Welfare Center, a distraught young lady is trying to get a bunch of kids to sleep. However, a pair of <color=#44afee>scarlet eyes</color> are hiding on the treetop, not far from the window, overseeing everything through the gaps in the foliage...",
    ["MonsterCollection10252"]="Developed by <color=#44afee>Khayr Consortium</color>, this retro robot is inspired by the mech wreckage unearthed from Juperos Ruins in many aspects, making it extremely popular among history enthusiasts. The <color=#44afee>color paint</color> on their shoulders is for <color=#44afee>identifying their models</color>. For instance, the <color=#44afee>red color</color> means the model has an advantage in <color=#44afee>shooting range</color>. These robots were first made for <color=#44afee>security tasks</color> in Kiel Khayr's Academy but soon got abandoned due to their complex maintenance process. Nowadays, most Dimiks have become collectibles, with only a few of the <color=#44afee>malfunctioning ones</color> remaining in the woods next to the academy, forsaken and forgotten.",
    ["MonsterCollection10253"]="<color=#44afee>Guardians of the Ruins</color> in the depth of Juperos Ruins. The various colors on their bodies are painted to distinguish their <color=#44afee>range of operation</color>. For example, the <color=#44afee>green</color> one only shows up at the <color=#44afee>altar ruins</color> located west. Moreover, the behavior of Venatu demonstrates a set pattern. Once they discover someone is approaching the ruins, they will show extreme <color=#44afee>hostility</color> against the target. Eden Group speculates that the ancient civilization might have used Venatu as a protective barrier for the ruins. If one could break through their guards, they might be able to reveal the truth of this part of history.",
    ["MonsterCollection10254"]="Developed by <color=#44afee>Khayr Consortium</color>, this retro robot is inspired by the mech wreckage unearthed from Juperos Ruins in many aspects, making it extremely popular among history enthusiasts. The <color=#44afee>color paint</color> on their shoulders is for <color=#44afee>identifying their models</color>. For instance, the <color=#44afee>blue color</color> means the model has an advantage in <color=#44afee>supporting capabilities</color>. These robots were first made for <color=#44afee>security tasks</color> in Kiel Khayr's Academy but soon got abandoned due to their complex maintenance process. Nowadays, most Dimiks have become collectibles, with only a few of the <color=#44afee>malfunctioning ones</color> remaining in the woods next to the academy, forsaken and forgotten.",
    ["MonsterCollection10255"]="An <color=#44afee>ancient android</color> that has yet to be fully analyzed. However, it gradually gains recognition from the public following the excavation of Juperos Ruins. This android, equipped with <color=#44afee>mechanical exosuit</color> to cope with the high-intensity industrial work, looks much <color=#44afee>taller</color> and mightier compared to those widely used androids in Juno.\n\"Who would have thought that such breathtaking mechanical technology existed even hundreds of years ago... But what made such civilization perish?\" Facing the exquisite mech body in the glass showcase, a museum employee expresses his admiration and bewilderment.",
    ["MonsterCollection10256"]="A mech monster with a strange appearance, possessing <color=#44afee>three</color> identical <color=#44afee>faces</color>. According to the research, its system incorporates a language module, which allows it to communicate with humans in <color=#44afee>simple words</color>. However, sometimes it tends to utter sentences of unknown meanings. Some theologians speculate that Apocalypse might have been appointed as <color=#44afee>deity's incarnation</color> in a certain part of history, using its <color=#44afee>foretelling statements</color> to steer people into actions that favored the <color=#44afee>ruling class's objectives</color>. Sadly, with the rapid growth of productivity and technology, these primitive perceptions gradually disappeared from society, rendering this monster devoid of its purpose of existence.",
    ["MonsterCollection10257"]="From the Poring family, a new member exclusive to the <color=#44afee>Einbroch</color> region has developed a distinctive <color=#44afee>circulatory system</color>. This system allows it to breathe in air and <color=#44afee>filter</color> out <color=#44afee>toxins</color>, which are then expelled through <color=#44afee>tubular organs</color> on its back. In the field of bioengineering, they believe that unlocking the mysteries of Metaling could offer a beacon of hope for Einbroch's residents suffering from lung disease.\n \"Metaling, a <color=#44afee>new species</color> found in the Einbroch area within the <color=#44afee>last century</color>, if they truly evolved from Poring, it means that polluted air can be purified within a living organism. With this concept, we might develop artificial organs suited for human use...\" In an effort to secure funding, a young researcher passionately pitches his project to <color=#44afee>Rekenber Corp</color> at an important scientific conference.",
    ["MonsterCollection10258"]="This insect monster is covered in <color=#44afee>tough carapace</color> all over the body, featuring three pairs of <color=#44afee>compound eyes</color> and four pairs of <color=#44afee>limbs</color>, with an extra pair of <color=#44afee>jaws</color> on its mouthparts that evolved from limbs, crucial for feeding, fighting, and mating. It feeds on <color=#44afee>metals and minerals</color> and occasionally snacks on <color=#44afee>berries</color> to hydrate. Even though it's quite <color=#44afee>shy</color> and doesn't attack humans, it often <color=#44afee>causes accidents</color> by munching on industrial goods and the metals in buildings. In the year when Einbroch began its major industrial construction, Porcellio was classified as a major <color=#44afee>pest</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10259"]="Moles living in the Einbroch region have exceptionally <color=#44afee>hard claws</color>, allowing them to dig through dirt mixed with minerals to build nests <color=#44afee>deep underground</color>. A long time ago, when humans still used primitive tools for mining, the Moles had a <color=#44afee>mutually beneficial</color> relationship with them. They assisted humans in mining with their claws, and in exchange, humans provided them with food, shelter, and harsh, cheap <color=#44afee>tobacco</color>. Sadly, this partnership ended with the arrival of Rekenber Corp, as both humans and Moles lost their place to mechanized, automated production in mines. Now, the Moles have returned to the expansive <color=#44afee>Einbech Field</color> to dig, burrow, and nest, although they still occasionally visit the familiar <color=#44afee>Einbroch Mining Village</color> to meet their <color=#44afee>old friends</color> and smoke in a few puffs.",
    ["MonsterCollection10260"]="This creature, a mix between a spider and a centipede, has two sets of <color=#44afee>enormous jaws</color> that can easily grind hard metals to bits. It feeds on <color=#44afee>metal</color> and is commonly found in areas rich in minerals, also attracted to piles of metal items. Rekenber Weekly reported that steel mills in the <color=#44afee>Einbroch Field</color> often suffer invasions by numerous Ungoliant. To tackle this, the steel mill placed a garbage disposal site at their backdoor, effectively destroying worthless scrap at no cost and calming the hungry monsters.\n\"Before long... they'll have devoured all the machines. Hmph, looking for data on the <color=#44afee>project</color>? You might have to dig through the monster's waste!\" On a moonless night, a figure stands aloft, watching a bunch of Ungoliant frantically eating <color=#44afee>androids</color> behind the fences.",
    ["MonsterCollection10261"]="Genetically, the Earth Deleter and the Ground Petite are closely related, but their habitats are far apart and very different. Experts believe that with their <color=#44afee>stubby, web-less legs and lack of sufficient muscle strength</color>, the Earth Deleter couldn't have crossed the sea from the Mjolnir Mountains to <color=#44afee>Einbroch Field</color>. The debate on how this species managed to settle here was intense among the monster research academia until...?\n\"... Could it be that they didn't arrive by themselves? The tectonic plates of this continent have been moving slowly since its formation. Maybe, many years ago, there was a significant fracture or shift that brought some Sky Petite along with the migrating land, which then evolved into the Earth Deleter we recognize today to <color=#44afee>adapt to the environment</color>...\" A geologist, who accidentally ended up at the wrong conference, listened in silence for a while and then offered his insight. At that moment, all the monster researchers realized just how different their fields were...",
    ["MonsterCollection10262"]="Genetically, the Sky Deleter and the Sky Deleter are <color=#44afee>closely related</color>, but their habitats are far apart and very different. Experts believe that with their <color=#44afee>wings having too low a bone density and insufficient muscle strength</color>, the Sky Petite couldn't have crossed the sea from the Mjolnir Mountains to <color=#44afee>Einbroch Field</color>. The debate on how this species managed to settle here was intense among the monster research academia until...?\n\"... Could it be that they didn't arrive by themselves? The tectonic plates of this continent have been moving slowly since its formation. Maybe, many years ago, there was a significant fracture or shift that brought some Sky Petite along with the migrating land, which then evolved into the Sky Deleter we recognize today to <color=#44afee>adapt to the environment</color>...\" A geologist, who accidentally ended up at the wrong conference, listened in silence for a while and then offered his insight. At that moment, all the monster researchers realized just how different their fields were...",
    ["MonsterCollection10263"]="The gas form of Venomous. It can alternate between its two forms when <color=#44afee>certain temperature and pressure conditions are met</color>. Its body consists mostly of toxic <color=#44afee>industrial gas</color>, and it feeds on a <color=#44afee>variety of poisonous elements</color>. Because of their trait, Rekenber Corp has kept them near the methane pool in the <color=#44afee>Einbroch mining area</color> to keep the mining staff safe.",
    ["MonsterCollection10264"]="The liquid form of Noxious. It can <color=#44afee>alternate between its two forms</color> when <color=#44afee>certain temperature and pressure conditions</color> are met. Its body consists mostly of toxic <color=#44afee>industrial sewer</color>, and it feeds on a <color=#44afee>variety of poisonous elements</color>. Because of their trait, Rekenber Corp has kept them near the methane pool in the <color=#44afee>Einbroch mining area</color> to keep the mining staff safe.",
    ["MonsterCollection10265"]="Characterized by their terribly bad temper, these little demons are composed of a blackish, unidentifiable substance, likely some sort of unclassified <color=#44afee>psychic energy</color>, so no physical attack can actually harm them. Even when squashed, they quickly <color=#44afee>bounce back to shape</color>. Moreover, they are keen on <color=#44afee>imitating human behavior</color>, stealing miners' hats and pickaxes, joyriding in minecarts, and turning tidy piles of ore into chaos before laughing and running away.\n\"... Where do you think you're going?\" yelled a miner as he slammed his shovel down, smashing the <color=#44afee>mischievous</color> Pitman into a pancake. But as he turned around, cursing, the crushed demon let out a tiny \\'whoosh\\' and started to slowly puff up like a <color=#44afee>balloon</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10266"]="Typically, obsidian is created when <color=#44afee>hot magma</color> <color=#44afee>cools suddenly</color>, but in Einbroch, thanks to the <color=#44afee>magic-rich</color> magma in the Nogg Cave, the obsidian has turned into living, magical creatures. These creatures usually <color=#44afee>cluster in groups</color>, <color=#44afee>bathing in the magma</color> to soak up magical energy. It's rumored, though not proven, that the strongest among them can evolve into a humanoid Lava Golem.",
    ["MonsterCollection10267"]="Monsters that emerge from <color=#44afee>rare gems</color> evolve into various <color=#44afee>subtypes</color> based on the mineral type, with the population in the Einbroch region primarily consisting of those from <color=#44afee>citrine</color>. They live by absorbing and transforming the energy contained within the minerals, often placing their favorite stones <color=#44afee>on their heads</color> for easy \"snacking.\" Once the energy in a stone is depleted, they switch it out for a new one.\n\"Research indicates that minerals drained by Minerals often turn <color=#44afee>dull</color> and greatly diminish in value. Experts are currently investigating the causes of this phenomenon and expect significant breakthrough soon...\" —Excerpt from \"World Mineralogy,\" Issue 175, published on July 16, AW988",
    ["MonsterCollection10268"]="<color=#44afee>Parasitizing</color> an old, abandoned <color=#44afee>iron furnace</color>, this monster adopts a <color=#44afee>deceptive</color> appearance to survive. It is both <color=#44afee>timid and careful</color>, always remaining inside its furnace hideout and never showing itself. When danger approaches, it releases a burst of <color=#44afee>steam</color> through the chimney, using it as a smokescreen to escape. The real identity of what's known as the \"Waste Stove\" is a <color=#44afee>mystery</color> that has bothered the monster research academia for years, though it might just be a mischievous <color=#44afee>Pitman</color> playing tricks inside.\n\"Ting, ting, ting... Hehehe...\" In the dead of night, a weird laugh fills the air of the mining area, mingling with the light clinking of metal hitting the ground...",
    ["MonsterCollection10269"]="\"The toy that knows you best\"—that advertising slogan used to be a beloved classic among the people of Einbroch, and the main character, Teddy Bear, was the <color=#44afee>dream toy</color> of all children in the region. The toy company took a bold step by incorporating advanced <color=#44afee>biomimetic technology</color> into Teddy Bear's design, which made it wildly popular from the get-go. No child could say no to a cute doll that could talk, laugh, and even play games with them. Unfortunately, it wasn't long before parents started noticing <color=#44afee>unexpected behaviors</color> in their Teddy Bears, and around the same time, there were widespread reports that biomimetic technology might enable machines to develop <color=#44afee>self-awareness</color>. While the accuracy of these reports was debatable, the negative publicity caused Teddy Bear's sales to plummet. After struggling for a while, the company had to destroy all unsold stock and resort to selling shares to recover... Today, you might still see some old but intact Teddy Bears at some of Einbroch's garbage disposal sites. If one wobbles over and greets you, don't be afraid—<color=#44afee>it's just a Teddy Bear</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10270"]="Crafted from <color=#44afee>Fire elements</color>, this monster's body is a roaring flame through which you can vaguely see a pulsing <color=#44afee>crystal core</color>. If it ever loses this core, it vanishes instantly, which is why it constantly searches for the right <color=#44afee>\"shell\"</color>—typically <color=#44afee>metals</color> or <color=#44afee>mineral shards</color>—to wrap around its body. However, due to the <color=#44afee>extreme temperature</color> of the flame, these shells tend to melt quickly.\n\"Look! That Blazzer looks like it's wearing a <color=#44afee>mask</color>! It's so cool!\" On an open day at Einbroch Monster Park, students invited to the event lean excitedly against the <color=#44afee>heatproof</color> glass, chattering like a flock of sparrows.",
    ["MonsterCollection10271"]="This <color=#44afee>cute</color> and <color=#44afee>docile</color> monster is perfect for a <color=#44afee>pet</color>. It shares some traits with cats, like rolling over and <color=#44afee>purring</color> when it's happy, which is a perfect time for a belly rub. The <color=#44afee>flame-like fur</color> on its neck serves as an indicator of its health. A healthy Explosion keeps a body temperature around <color=#44afee>40 degrees Celsius</color>, and the fur on its neck should feel slightly hot. If the temperature is too high or too low, immediately seek advice from your vet.\n\"If it's your first time owning a pet, I'd recommend starting with an Explosion. They're adorable, easygoing, have minimal environmental needs, and rarely get sick. Their main drawback is <color=#44afee>poor eyesight</color>, which might require some extra effort in teaching them how to get around...\" In the pet shop, a new salesperson is eagerly trying to close their first deal.",
    ["MonsterCollection10272"]="Despite its name, the Gig neither lives in the desert nor possesses any venomous glands. It got its name because its <color=#44afee>brown carapace</color> helps it hide in the sand, leading people to mistakenly believe it migrated from desert areas. The <color=#44afee>red crystals</color> on its back are not venom sacs but are crystals formed from <color=#44afee>fire elements</color>.\n\"... The Gig will hide in <color=#44afee>gaps within rocks</color>, waiting to catch its prey off-guard with a fatal blow. Even though it isn't poisonous, watch out for its <color=#44afee>large pincers</color>. Remember this part; it's going to be on your final exam. Everyone, please read it aloud together... \"As the sun warms the classroom, the voices of students reciting their lessons echo through the school, as young Adventurers study hard in their classes before their true journeys begin.",
    ["MonsterCollection10273"]="This strange monster exists as an entity between spirit and physical form, and <color=#44afee>loves to prank</color>, often using <color=#44afee>fire magic</color> to burn off people's clothes or hair. It's said that they <color=#44afee>vanish</color> if anyone sees their true form, which is why each Diabolic meticulously outfits itself, covering everything but its <color=#44afee>wings, limbs, and tail</color>. Some even go as far as to draw faces on their clothes to act as their own. If you ever find some <color=#44afee>old clothes</color> missing from your wardrobe, it's likely a sign that these Diabolic paid you a visit.",
    ["MonsterCollection10274"]="With a physique similar to Bigfoot's, this creature has developed special organs to survive the intense heat of the <color=#44afee>Nogg Cave</color>. It's believed that its sweat glands produce an oil that <color=#44afee>shields it against fire</color>, preventing lava burns. The creature has a <color=#44afee>huge appetite</color>, eating almost anything; oddly enough, it doesn't eat honey—a favorite of all types of bears.\n\"... It could be due to the harsh environment of the Nogg Cave that no bees can survive there. Over extended periods of evolution, the Grizzly's genes might have simply forgotten about honey...\" The old monster researcher taps his pen against the book, leaving tiny ink marks on the paper as he ponders over this unsolved puzzle and murmurs to himself.",
    ["MonsterCollection10275"]="A monster that is frequently seen in the depths of the <color=#44afee>Nogg Cave</color>, made entirely of <color=#44afee>boiling magma</color> but with obvious <color=#44afee>humanoid traits</color>, such as a head and four limbs. It usually <color=#44afee>soaks itself in magma</color> to absorb magic, which is essential for its survival; hence, it can't stray too far from magma, or it will begin to dry up. Some believe that the Lava Golem might have evolved from the strongest among the Obsidian, though this has yet to be confirmed.",
    ["MonsterCollection10276"]="According to legend, this creature emerged from the <color=#44afee>soul of a warhorse</color>, reborn through the <color=#44afee>trial of hellfire</color>. It can <color=#44afee>withstand intense heat</color> and can <color=#44afee>create dreamscapes</color> where it <color=#44afee>feeds</color> on the <color=#44afee>magic</color> of its prey during their nightmares, thereby nourishing itself. Those haunted by Nightmare Terror are said to often meet <color=#44afee>their demise in their dreams</color>.",
    ["MonsterCollection10279"]="Among all known magical creatures, Anopheles is the <color=#44afee>smallest</color>, and in the brutal world of nature, that makes it easy prey. But these tiny beings have developed a remarkable survival instinct—the moment they hatch, they begin their search for their fated partners. Once a <color=#44afee>trio</color> is formed, they remain <color=#44afee>inseparable for life</color>. No matter the task—eating, sleeping, even laying eggs—they maintain a <color=#44afee>triangle formation</color>, always watching each other's backs. If one is attacked, the other two will instantly react.\n\"With their <color=#44afee>hermaphroditic</color> nature, gender plays no role in their choices—only <color=#44afee>strength</color> decides who stays and who perishes. The weak are eliminated early, and <color=#44afee>less than a third</color> ever live to see adulthood...\" In the dim glow of the lab, the professor tapped on the petri dish. Inside, tiny larvae writhed within their translucent eggs, wriggling desperately. Any moment now, they would emerge into a world where only the strong survive.",
    ["MonsterCollection10280"]="Long ago, in an effort to curb the Anopheles outbreak on the Rachel Plains, the Midgard Kingdom introduced several <color=#44afee>foreign species</color>. But survival on these plains is a cruel game—only one species endured: the Drosera. It adapted by growing a large amount of delicate, stamen-like <color=#44afee>tendrils</color> beneath its leaves to <color=#44afee>capture moisture from the air</color>, clinging to every last drop of <color=#44afee>water</color> in the arid land. For years, Arunafeltz has studied its <color=#44afee>drought resilience</color>, hoping to use its secrets to cultivate crops and solve the kingdom's food shortages. But as research deepens, more and more scholars are starting to notice something strange—its biological structure seems far closer to <color=#44afee>magical beasts</color> than plants...",
    ["MonsterCollection10281"]="A monster with an unyielding desire for the <color=#44afee>sky</color>, <color=#44afee>its mastery of gliding is almost unmatched</color>. As long as the wind carries it, it can remain suspended in the air for hours, wings still and silent. But nature is cruel. Burdened by <color=#44afee>bones too heavy</color> for easy takeoff, it can only ascend by leaping from the edge of a cliff. If the <color=#44afee>wind fails to catch it</color>... then all that awaits is a tragic fall to ruin.\n\"To soar is to live. To fall is to die.\" These words were penned by a bard, struck by inspiration upon witnessing Hill Wind's breathtaking flight.",
    ["MonsterCollection10282"]="One of the most common magical creatures on the rocky deserts of the <color=#44afee>Rachel Plains</color>, and one of the few species that has fully adapted to such a barren environment. It is <color=#44afee>solitary</color> by nature, wandering alone without need for a pack. Even when faced with enemies far larger than itself, it chooses to stand its ground and <color=#44afee>fight alone</color>. Its fur <color=#44afee>shifts with the seasons</color>—dark brown and bristly in the summer, long and pale as frost in the winter—allowing it to blend perfectly into the landscape for <color=#44afee>stealth</color> and survival. But beware. It has powerful <color=#44afee>glands</color> near its <color=#44afee>tailbone</color>. Get too close from behind, and you might find yourself choking on a lethal <color=#44afee>gas</color> attack.",
    ["MonsterCollection10283"]="Settled on the outskirts of Rachel, the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color> stands as a sanctuary of elemental magic, a place where only beings as ethereal as Aqua Elemental can thrive. Their <color=#44afee>bodies are made entirely of elemental energy</color>, granting them unmatched <color=#44afee>elemental affinity</color>. But this is also their biggest weakness—if the elemental concentration in the surroundings drops, they <color=#44afee>vanish</color> instantly. So if you cross paths with an Aqua Elemental in the Ice Cave—don't fight, just <color=#44afee>run</color>. The moment you step outside, you'll be safe.",
    ["MonsterCollection10284"]="A subspecies of Aqua Elemental, Phylla lacks the ability to fully control elemental energy, limiting it to manipulating <color=#44afee>liquid water</color> for both offense and defense. That's why it has developed an unusual habit—it always carries its own water source. Each Phylla owns a special <color=#44afee>water container</color>, ensuring it never runs out of water. But here's where things get interesting—studies have confirmed that these containers are made of pure elemental energy. And yet... Phylla <color=#44afee>lacks the ability to transform elements into one another</color>, so how do they even create these containers...?\n\"\\... Taking all this into account, I propose a theory: while Aqua Elemental and Phylla do not reproduce in the traditional sense, there may exist a <color=#44afee>parent-child</color> relationship between them. Perhaps stronger Aqua Elemental craft these water containers for Phylla, just as humans <color=#44afee>protect and provide for their children</color>...\" As the annual research conference reached its peak, scholars gave it their all, hoping to impress the panel. For them, this was the final shot at winning the Mobel Prize in Monsterology.",
    ["MonsterCollection10285"]="The <color=#44afee>baby</color> form of a Snowier is among the rarest monsters, undergoing a unique <color=#44afee>metamorphosis</color> as they grow. At birth, they are almost hairless, but soft gray-white fur begins to sprout once they reach their first full moon. Then, every six months, they <color=#44afee>shed and regrow their coat</color>, with each new layer growing thicker and stronger. Then, at the <color=#44afee>age of ten</color>, a transformation takes place—they <color=#44afee>sprout their front limbs</color>, much like a tadpole emerging from the water. This marks the beginning of their journey into adulthood.",
    ["MonsterCollection10286"]="Known as the most dangerous monster in the Ice Cave. This monster usually disguises itself as an ordinary icicle, <color=#44afee>blending</color> seamlessly with the frozen walls. Until it attacks, there's no way to tell it apart from the real thing. But once prey steps too close, it drops like a guillotine, <color=#44afee>splitting</color> into razor-sharp <color=#44afee>ice blades</color> that can <color=#44afee>cut through bone</color> in a split second, killing the prey.\n \"...In fact, this thing behaves less like a monster and more like a <color=#44afee>trap</color>. Some radical theories propose that an ancient civilization exists at the deepest part of the Ice Cave—one we have yet to uncover. If these icicles are <color=#44afee>defense mechanisms</color> set up by the civilization, then it would explain why, despite all our technological advancements, their <color=#44afee>true composition remains a mystery</color>...\" A professor in Juno University lectured passionately in class, but unfortunately, the students—focused on passing their exams—had zero interest in anything that wasn't on the syllabus.",
    ["MonsterCollection10287"]="The <color=#44afee>adult</color> form of a Snowier is among the rarest monsters, undergoing a unique <color=#44afee>metamorphosis</color> as they grow. Upon reaching adulthood, it grows <color=#44afee>massive in size</color>, develops <color=#44afee>thick fur</color>, and sports <color=#44afee>razor-sharp fangs</color>, making it far more dangerous than its baby form. Fortunately, Snowiers are solitary monsters. Aside from young ones staying with their mothers, most adults prefer a life of <color=#44afee>isolation</color>. Each one claims a <color=#44afee>territory</color> of its own, avoiding both conflict and communication with others of its kind. If you're planning to hunt a Snowier, your best bet is to work as a team—taking one down alone is no easy feat.",
    ["MonsterCollection10288"]="A colossal monster dwells in the depths of the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color>, its body held together by the <color=#44afee>high concentration of water</color> that saturates the air. Its movement speed is inversely affected by temperature—the <color=#44afee>hotter the environment</color>, the <color=#44afee>slower</color> and stiffer it becomes. Because of this, <color=#44afee>fire</color> is the most effective way to defeat it. Some speculate that the Ice Titan evolved from the strongest Gazeti, but no one has been able to prove it.",
    ["MonsterCollection10289"]="Very few monsters can endure the brutal cold of the <color=#44afee>Frozen Cave</color>, but the Ice Wolf thrives where others falter. Its <color=#44afee>thick coat</color> keeps the deadly chill at bay, while its <color=#44afee>sharp claws</color> and <color=#44afee>fangs</color> guarantee it never goes hungry in this harsh wasteland. Some say its back is laced with hidden <color=#44afee>ice spikes</color>. With lightning-fast <color=#44afee>reflexes</color>, the Ice Wolf drives its prey into a corner before landing the killing blow.",
    ["MonsterCollection10290"]="In the <color=#44afee>dead of night</color>, this <color=#44afee>small monster</color> likes to wander within the <color=#44afee>Holy Ground</color>. Using its <color=#44afee>massive eye</color>, it casts <color=#44afee>illusions</color>, trapping its prey in hallucinations before launching an attack. However, it has a <color=#44afee>frail body</color> and stands no chance in close combat—once its illusion is broken, all it can do is flap its wings and flee.\n\"Listen carefully—never, under any circumstances, remove this talisman. It carries the pope's prayer, a gift from the goddess herself, and will shield you from the Beholder's deception.\" On their first day as attendants, the young novices listened intently, unaware that the tiny pendant hanging around their necks would one day be the only thing standing between them and certain doom.",
    ["MonsterCollection10291"]="A slender and <color=#44afee>flexible</color> monster. It <color=#44afee>sleeps by day and hunts by night</color>, lurking in caves, <color=#44afee>underground</color>, and even city sewers. It <color=#44afee>fears the light</color>; its eyes have completely degenerated, leaving it blind. However, its sense of smell and hearing are highly sensitive. The wing-like structures on its back are actually exposed <color=#44afee>bone spikes</color>, completely useless for flight—but when it comes to hunting and self-defense, they prove to be quite the weapon.",
    ["MonsterCollection10292"]="With an almost <color=#44afee>eternity</color> lifespan, this monster pays the price by spending most of its existence in <color=#44afee>sleep</color>. Its movement speed is inversely affected by temperature—the <color=#44afee>hotter the environment</color>, the <color=#44afee>slower</color> and stiffer it becomes. Because of this, <color=#44afee>fire</color> is the most effective way to defeat it. Some unverified theories suggest that, after countless years of refinement, an Gazeti may eventually evolve into a humanoid Ice Titan.",
    ["MonsterCollection10293"]="\"Experiment ID: 5836-D. Just another <color=#44afee>failure</color> among the countless others. The second I laid eyes on this experimental entity, I knew he was a waste of resources—scrawny, feeble, completely useless. What's the point anyway? He wouldn't even last through the first trial. But that also made him cheap—no special requirements, no extra costs. Just another nameless <color=#44afee>hobo</color> plucked off the streets.\"\n\"... What the hell are the guards doing?! He got out?! The test zone is now a complete mess, and the armory is missing weapons—a <color=#44afee>dagger</color> and a <color=#44afee>butcher knife</color>. He's likely made his way to the <color=#44afee>upper level</color>. Fortunately, this <color=#44afee>temple</color> is under our complete control. Just need to get rid of him before Lord Xiron loses his patience.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10294"]="A <color=#44afee>machinal</color> monster built to resemble the Beholder, nearly identical at first glance. But the Seeker <color=#44afee>cannot cast illusions</color>. Its eye has been replaced with a <color=#44afee>miniature camera</color>, feeding real-time video back to the terminal. With unmatched <color=#44afee>mobility</color> and <color=#44afee>stealth</color>, it's clear—this thing was built for <color=#44afee>monitoring</color> or <color=#44afee>spying</color>. But why would such a monster exist in the technologically primitive Arunafeltz?\n\"... Found it. The experimental entity took the stairs in Section C. Relax—the temple guards are all ours. He won't survive the night. No signs of trouble elsewhere. I'll keep watching. Okay... Got it. I'll call in if anything happens. Over.\" Bathed in the glow of countless flickering <color=#44afee>screens</color>, a middle-aged man watched the <color=#44afee>surveillance feed</color>—then ended the call.",
    ["MonsterCollection10295"]="\"Experiment ID: 923-C. Watching a <color=#44afee>former coworker</color> become an experimental entity—it's a surreal experience. I told her, didn't I? Don't get involved. Don't sympathize with the experimental entities. Or she'd <color=#44afee>become one of them</color>. But she was young, idealistic, still clinging to childish dreams of heroism. Meanwhile, people like me? Rational, composed, and self-sufficient. We don't play the hero. So, when she finally crossed the line, I smiled and injected the <color=#44afee>fission reagent</color> into her body.\"\n\"I won't lie—her last look almost got to me. We both knew she wasn't going to make it. To ease my guilt, I <color=#44afee>welded a mask to her face</color>, watching as fresh blood seeped through the tiny holes, covering her unseeing eyes. Good. Now, I wouldn't have to look at her hatred anymore. But her screams—too loud. The other subjects were getting <color=#44afee>irritated</color>. I had no choice but to <color=#44afee>rip out her tongue</color>. A shame indeed. I was hoping to hear her sing me a lullaby one last time...\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10296"]="Resembling Gremlin in behavior, this monster has <color=#44afee>no eyes</color>, navigating purely through <color=#44afee>exceptional hearing</color> ability. Its greatest weakness lies in its exposed <color=#44afee>spinal column</color>, stretching from the base of its skull to its tailbone. This area is so packed with nerves that any damage is almost impossible to recover from. To compensate, it developed a natural armor-like skin. Recently, <color=#44afee>Novice armor</color> made from Hodremlin <color=#44afee>skin</color> has become popular in Rachel. Of course, you'd have to ignore the <color=#44afee>foul stench</color> that comes with it—but it's a tempting bargain for the price.",
    ["MonsterCollection10297"]="\"Experiment ID: 1149-C. The final trial of adaptability. The <color=#44afee>fission reagent</color> is still far from stable. We have no idea how much human cells can withstand—most <color=#44afee>experimental entities</color> don't make it past this stage. They either die or go insane. Yet, <color=#44afee>Subject 17</color> proved different. He survived the agony; his body refused to break, and his mind stayed intact. I administered the last dose and waited in silence. The answer would come in time.\"\n\"... What a waste of time. He went <color=#44afee>mad</color> anyway. Seventy-two hours. That was all he needed to pass the threshold. We were ready—his <color=#44afee>mask</color>, attire, and weapons had been prepared, and Henrik was expecting him. But the moment his fingers wrapped around the <color=#44afee>scythe</color> and <color=#44afee>dagger</color>, his sanity collapsed. Fortunately, the company's <color=#44afee>security measures</color> are flawless. The <color=#44afee>guards</color> put him down before he could act. It feels wasteful to dispose of him so soon—perhaps a <color=#44afee>control device</color> would make him useful again? Of course, this means we must recalculate everything about the fission reagent's safety limits. Let's hope the next subject will give me something worth keeping.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10298"]="\"Experiment ID: 204-B. It's been a long time since I've seen such a flawless experimental entity. Every metric is exceptional, but her <color=#44afee>muscular power</color> is particularly breathtaking—those <color=#44afee>scarlet fibers</color> are the ultimate sign of evolution. So, she's <color=#44afee>Subject 17's sister</color>? Logistics is a joke—how do they fail to document something this crucial? <color=#44afee>Twin</color> DNA is highly identical, making them incredibly rare and genetically valuable.\"\n\"Whatever. No use crying over it now. S-003 was an extreme case, and even if I had handled it, success was far from guaranteed. Besides... Baroshev was a lunatic, and I lack the insanity to take risks like he did. Fortunately, she's doing great. She's being sent to the <color=#44afee>arena</color>, where Henrik will shape her into a warrior. She chose a <color=#44afee>massive mace</color>—just picture metal crushing bone, <color=#44afee>rivets</color> piercing through flesh. That's true <color=#44afee>brute-force beauty</color>. I've secured the best seat in the house, right at the top. From there, I'll watch every second of your performance. Don't disappoint me, sweetheart.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection10299"]="<color=#44afee>Cecil Devine</color>—born upon a lonely isle adrift on the endless sea. The Gangash Pirates came in fire and blood, claiming all she held dear. Only she remained, taken in by their ruthless captain, <color=#44afee>Drake</color>. Growing up among her enemies, Cecil developed a <color=#44afee>desperate thirst for strength</color>. To her, Drake's care and training were nothing but <color=#44afee>humiliation</color>. She dreamed of one day nailing him to the mast of the Queen's Revenge, to honor her family who perished in that fire. Unfortunately, that wish would never come true.\n\"When you strike down your enemy, strike to end all roots of evil.\"—Cecil Devine",
    ["MonsterCollection10300"]="<color=#44afee>Margaret Sorin</color>—<color=#44afee>Royal Exorcist Priestess</color> of the Gaebolg Family. Beneath her gentle, absent-minded grace lies a heart <color=#44afee>acutely perceptive</color> to every whisper of sorrow. None perceives anguish as swiftly as she does, and none brings solace with such quiet strength. Wolmas the Archbishop believes she was born for the priesthood and has even hinted at passing his mantle to her. Now, under the Gaebolg Family's command, she has traveled to the Schwarzwald Republic to <color=#44afee>secretly investigate the mysterious death of the late King Tristan III</color>...\n\"All unfolds by the will of Odin. Be thankful for every meeting, for every soul upon your path.\"—Margaret Sorin",
    ["MonsterCollection10301"]="<color=#44afee>Howard Alt-Eisen</color>—the legendary <color=#44afee>Whitesmith</color> whose hammer rings across the battlefields of Adventurers. His forge is not confined to an anvil, but found amid the clash of steel and blood. To him, a Whitesmith must not hide behind the lines; only by <color=#44afee>standing beside warriors</color>, feeling the rhythm of their strikes, can he temper weapons to their fullest potential. That's why, even during <color=#44afee>dangerous quests</color>, he fights alongside his comrades as their most reliable support.\n\"Those who fear to fail will never dare to create.\"—Howard Alt-Eisen",
    ["MonsterCollection10302"]="<color=#44afee>Eremes Guile</color>—the unseen blade of the Assassin Guild. <color=#44afee>Quiet and withdrawn</color>, and he's known for his <color=#44afee>invisible presence</color>, but that's exactly what makes him such a talented assassin. His mastery of <color=#44afee>Hiding</color> allows him to slip past enemy detection and take on dangerous quests like espionage and assassination. He seems to take a strange pleasure in <color=#44afee>living on the edge</color>, obsessively pursuing the thrill of difficult assignments.\n\"Endure. Wait. Hide within the dark. Then... strike once, and end it.\"—Eremes Guile",
    ["MonsterCollection10303"]="<color=#44afee>Fiona Ludea</color>, a <color=#44afee>senior instructor</color> of the Rune-Midgard Royal Chivalry, is gifted and hardworking in swordsmanship. She's also known for being a bit blunt and lacking social grace, and her harsh training often leads to complaints, but her devotion to her students runs deeper than she lets on. Recently, she left Prontera on a <color=#44afee>special quest</color> to the Schwarzwald Republic, and hasn't been heard from since...\n\"There are no easy paths in the way of the sword. Every sleepless night, every drop of sweat—these are the wages of life itself.\"—Fiona Ludea",
    ["MonsterCollection10304"]="<color=#44afee>Roselia Heines</color> comes from a prestigious family of mages that values <color=#44afee>bloodline</color> above all else. Despite her extraordinary talent, she's treated unfairly for being a <color=#44afee>collateral relative</color>. She holds deep resentment toward the current heir, Nithil Heines, accusing him publicly of wasting the family's resources while achieving nothing. Determined to overturn the corrupt inheritance system, Roselia <color=#44afee>aims to become the next Great Sage</color>. She even volunteered for a dangerous investigation quest, hoping to prove herself...\n\"What you desire will never be granted—unless you seize it by your own will.\"—Roselia Heines",
    ["MonsterCollection10305"]="<color=#44afee>Cecile Anciro</color> is an orphan raised by the <color=#44afee>Euphonic Symphony</color>. Over twenty years ago, on a full-moon night, the waves carried a small boat to the shores of <color=#44afee>Comodo</color>, with a sleeping <color=#44afee>baby girl</color> inside—that baby was Cecile. Since then, the peaceful island became her home. She grew up surrounded by love and felt <color=#44afee>deep gratitude</color> toward Euphonic Symphony. So when officers arrived to select a skilled dancer for a secret quest, she didn't hesitate to volunteer....\n\"Give your best, every single day.\"—Cecile Anciro",
    ["MonsterCollection10306"]="<color=#44afee>Abrucci Umbar</color> is a young warrior brimming with <color=#44afee>passion</color> for the martial arts. He loves studying the <color=#44afee>techniques of different schools</color> and has developed his own <color=#44afee>unique fighting style</color> through relentless practice. Cheerful, energetic, and full of justice, he seems to make friends with everyone—and before anyone notices, he's already become the party's <color=#44afee>natural leader</color>.\n\"There's no best—only better.\"—Abrucci Umbar",
    ["MonsterCollection10307"]="<color=#44afee>Craig Briman</color> is a novice Alchemist who only recently passed his class advancement trial to become a new <color=#44afee>Creator</color>. He's gentle and a bit <color=#44afee>timid</color>, often unable to refuse even when something isn't his responsibility. Because of that, he tends to take on more than he should—and that's exactly how he ended up on this <color=#44afee>dangerous journey</color>...\n\"Maybe... being ordinary isn't such a bad thing after all.\"—Craig Briman",
    ["MonsterCollection10308"]="<color=#44afee>Sua Clausel</color> is a well-known bounty hunter—though not for his strength, but for his <color=#44afee>ruthless</color> way of doing things. <color=#44afee>Cold</color> and utterly <color=#44afee>lacking in empathy</color>, he sees human life as nothing more than a bargaining chip. For him, everything has a price, and he'll take any job as long as the <color=#44afee>pay is right</color>.\n\"In my world, money can buy anything.\"—Sua Clausel",
    ["MonsterCollection30001"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A manifestation of Odin with its original meaning being <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Angel's Ring\"</color>. Its Angel Hairband is also a fashion symbol popular in the Rune Kingdom. It is very cute, has a lively nature and, being as playful as children, its favorite is to dart amongst clouds playing hide and seek with everyone.",
    ["MonsterCollection30002"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The final stage of evolution for Mutant Thief Bugs and the absolute strongest Thief Bugs in history. Its majestic <color=#CA2E0AFF>gold shell</color> emanates traces of a kingly aura. However, in the eyes of a many adventurers, its pure gold shell has no deterring effect and is instead an encouragement for everyone to kill it and exchange that pure gold shell for tons of wealth.",
    ["MonsterCollection30003"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A manifestation of Baphomet with its original meaning being <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Demon's Ring\"</color>. The Evil Wings on its body is also an accessory popular with the fans in the Poring Supporters' Group. Legend has it that it was sealed up in the Labyrinth Forest by Witch Evelyn. However, the recent energy fluctuations seem to hint at its stirring desire to revive.",
    ["MonsterCollection30004"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A pirate who <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruled the seas</color> before his death. After being attacked by the Kraken, he retained control over his ship and even wanted to talk the Kraken into joining his conquest of the seas. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>weapon</color> he wields can <color=#CA2E0AFF>sell for a high price</color> on the Black Market. However, adventurers may have to put their lives on the line if they want to snatch the weapon from Drake's hands. After all, when Drake and the Kraken join forces, they are invincible. No fleet has escaped unscathed from them thus far.",
    ["MonsterCollection30005"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The ruler of the seas. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trident</color> in his hand can cast lightning and storms. Though Strouf Statues are everywhere, the real Strouf still naturally inspires a feeling of oppression. Apparently, the Strouf existing in the world at present is not the real one, but just a projection of his power. However, its power is still not to be underestimated. It is the projection of a god after all.",
    ["MonsterCollection30007"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The leader and mother of all Hornets. One Mistress is enough for a colony to develop. The Mistress represents both <color=#CA2E0AFF>power and beauty</color> in the Hornet tribe. Its stinger has evolved to become a <color=#CA2E0AFF>stinging ring</color>, so the Mistress poses a huge threat that can attack from all directions. Once you provoke the Mistress, be prepared for attacks from the whole colony. Adventurers, don't let your guard down! Tanders has already provided a disastrous demonstration.",
    ["MonsterCollection30008"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The original meaning of \"Phreeoni\" is <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"devouring the sky,\"</color> a very figurative description of its most obvious characteristic. Its tongue and huge mouth full of sharp teeth makes it look as though it wants to swallow everything in the world. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>four eyes</color> on top of its head allow it to observe enemies easily. However, as it eats everything and never brushes its teeth, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>smell</color> which permeates the air around it is usually <color=#CA2E0AFF>painfully foul</color>.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Monster Researcher Bertha had once remarked during a sneaky attempt at taking photos of the Phreeoni, \"Regardless of how great its research value is, before I get my hands on a hazmat suit to cut off the smell, I'm staying away from it. Oh, I can't take it anymore! I have to get back and shower and spray more Sunflower perfume.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection30009"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The ruler of the Ant Cavern. After thousands of years, due to some mysterious reason, it gained <color=#CA2E0AFF>certain features of a human appearance</color>. Its <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious and bewitching</color> looks are obviously not the results of natural evolution. There are also many rumors about it once being a possessed Mage who could no longer recover her original form after regaining control over her body and ended up becoming a real Maya.",
    ["MonsterCollection30010"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Eddga warriors who see <color=#CA2E0AFF>gentility</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>fighting</color> as their faith are currently in Midgard gaining experience through challenges and seem to be staying at Payon for now. The Pipe in its hand is not just for smoking and posing. If you have the misfortune of becoming its opponent, do be careful. Apparently, those who were smashed by the Pipe either died then and there or were left with serious trauma. Adventurers are advised not to challenge it carelessly, or it will use the thorny wristband on its arm to teach you how to behave.",
    ["MonsterCollection30011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A petite Kitty Girl with the appearance of a cute young lady. If her weapon isn't so conspicuous, her combat potential may pass completely unnoticed. A long stick is attached to a huge bell, forming the same effect as a Chain. Is this a funeral bell?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> If her <color=#CA2E0AFF>tail</color> is pulled, she will become very <color=#CA2E0AFF>aggressive</color>. If you do not wish to die, don't provoke her!",
    ["MonsterCollection30012"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The <color=#CA2E0AFF>strongest</color> Orc Warrior. His hair is an extraordinarily vibrant red like Rockers and the equipment on his entire body all show off his past glory and honor. However, he is <color=#CA2E0AFF>considerate</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>at heart</color>, which is the opposite of his appearance, staying his hand when faced with weak opponents. He welcomes the strong to challenge him and never stoops to despicable means. A fair fight is what brings Orcs honor.",
    ["MonsterCollection30013"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The <color=#CA2E0AFF>first ruler</color> of ancient Egypt. After his death, he was buried in the pyramid. Perhaps because his desire to protect his land and people was too strong, he obtained help from mysterious powers and turned into the incredibly strong <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mummy</color>. All sorts of secrets and legends surround him. However, the most famous of which is surely the romantic story of him and his wife Eassis swearing their lives to each other. The bard Morts has written many songs about them that are sung around the world.",
    ["MonsterCollection30014"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Once the restless Undead Doppelgangers have you in their grasp, you must be careful not to let them discover your weakness, lest the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cold, dark</color> grip of their Undead Aura consume you...",
    ["MonsterCollection30015"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The chief of the Orc tribe. Though old, he still possesses <color=#CA2E0AFF>great</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>strength</color>. The heads hanging from his waist foretell the future of those who dare challenge the chief...",
    ["MonsterCollection30016"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Not even his <color=#CA2E0AFF>flamboyant, handsome shirt</color> can hide the loneliness in Dracula's heart. Joyous banquets for the dead are always held in his castle, with gurgling pools of flowing blood and dancing spirits of the departed. Everything seems to be as perfect as he could ever hope for, but perhaps only feasting on new <color=#CA2E0AFF>souls</color> and fresh <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood</color> can truly fill the void in his heart. If you happen to pass by his castle, do not be fooled by the dancing and music, unless you wish to console him by offering up your own neck.",
    ["MonsterCollection30017"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ancient rulers</color> of the deserts. When they were young, they lost their way in the labyrinth of the Sphinx and lost their names and identities, along with their sense of time... Apparently, the leader of the Eden Group, Bowya, once tried to find out their real identities and make records for this period of ancient Egyptian kingdom history. However, as there were too many and all could not be verified in turn, Bowya had to give up.",
    ["MonsterCollection30019"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The <color=#CA2E0AFF>great power</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Demon King</color>, who has razed cities to the ground, needs no introduction. Although Morroc is <color=#CA2E0AFF>sealed away</color> once more with the combined strength of many adventurers, it continues to keep a watchful gaze over Midgard through the dimensional gap. The scars of battle from sealing Morroc away are ones that will not fade with time, and so the people keep vigilant day and night to prevent the Demon King from rising again.",
    ["MonsterCollection30020"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Doomed to an eternity of tragic hubris, greed and blind ambition drive him to wave his <color=#CA2E0AFF>scepter</color> with conceit, even after death. Watch out for his deathly shadow, or abandon all hope of survival.",
    ["MonsterCollection30021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A fallen genius lurks <color=#CA2E0AFF>beneath Geffen</color>... From time to time, one can even hear the rumbling of his deep, low breath, accompanied by the frenzied turning of pages...",
    ["MonsterCollection30022"]="One of the original <color=#44afee>twelve Bishops</color> of Arunafeltz, who is highly respected and has many followers. During his youth, he traveled around every country. He thought that god had abandoned this land after witnessing countless sufferings among the living beings. Therefore, he wishes to establish an entirely <color=#44afee>new religion</color>. He signed a pact with Hel to <color=#44afee>sell his soul</color> in order to fulfill his wish. But is the <color=#44afee>ancient god</color> he believes capable of restoring order in this world?",
    ["MonsterCollection30023"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The overlord of the seas crowned with the name of \"Kraken.\" Rumor has it that not one of those who saw its <color=#CA2E0AFF>third eye</color> has managed to escape the maelstrom. Legend has it that Drake suffered great losses after being attacked by it. However, it is said that Drake once tried to talk it into joining forces to conquer the seas.",
    ["MonsterCollection30024"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Demons with a peculiar nature, deriving joy from <color=#CA2E0AFF>tempting and tricking humans</color>, enjoying seeing humans <color=#CA2E0AFF>falling for desires</color>, and considering it as the utmost joy in life. To do this, they are willing to spend a long time lurking around humans, seducing them into <color=#CA2E0AFF>corruption</color>, and realizing their wishes. However, even Tao Gunka could fail, and that is when Tao Gunka suffers from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebound curse</color> itself.\n \"Ugh... Darn humans! Next time... Next time, I'll show you my power!\" The Demon trapped in a summoning magic circle screams furiously, even looking somehow devastated.",
    ["MonsterCollection30025"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The rulers of Comodo thousands of years ago. Though on the decline after losing the power of Dragon Flame, they are no easy enemies. The dragons remaining in the dragons' cave today are somehow different from their ancestors thousands of years ago, with changes in figures, scale colors and wing shapes, probably from adaptation to the environment in the cave. Born with <color=#CA2E0AFF>high-level wisdom</color>, they are capable of communicating with humans, which is rare for monsters.",
    ["MonsterCollection30026"]="A knight with high morals. Never betrays the oath he swore even though he had already fallen into the Realm of the Dead. However, Hel, who is fond of observing the sin of humans, is displeased with his acts, and she then exhausts all her might to torture and humiliate this knight. Eventually, all the suffering became a clear mirror that reflects the kindest heart that lies within this knight...\n\"Sword, <color=#44afee>Holy Fire</color>. Shield, <color=#44afee>Summum Bonum</color>. Use the sword to sunder the sin of all beings and use the shield to bear the pain of all beings.\" —The epitaph on a nameless tome in the Glast Heim Cemetery.",
    ["MonsterCollection30027"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The ruler of the once prosperous <color=#CA2E0AFF>Schmidt dynasty</color>. His greedy ambition has made him fall into the endless darkness. He has lost his mind and incarnated as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>demon</color>. Only blood and killing can decorate the white bones on its shoulders, ready to submit to the darkness…",
    ["MonsterCollection30028"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>Jayw</color>”… In recent days, a number of unexplained disappearances have occurred, including victims from different ages and walks of life. The only common denominator is that each victim lost contact after a late-night trip. One of the victims was able to be traced back to a dark alley near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clock Tower</color>. Due to the serious implications of the case, the Guard has launched an urgent investigation and advises all residents not to go out at night for now.\n“According to eyewitness testimony, on the night of the murder, he heard the raspy hiss of a wild animal coming from a dark alley. Curious, the witness followed the curious sound and discovered a <color=#CA2E0AFF>giant owl</color> wearing a bowler hat and a <color=#CA2E0AFF>man dressed in white</color> at the end of the alley. The owl was pecking savagely at a human’s organs with its sharp beak, while the man in white drew bizarre formations... As the testimony was far too absurd and no remains matching the testimony have been found, the Guard deemed that it couldn’t rule out that the witness hallucinating due to excessive shock. At present, the case is still under close investigation. The agency will continue to follow up on this matter and is committed to bringing first-hand news to the general public...\"\n——Al De Baran Times, A.W.1000, July 10, Issue 1154.",
    ["MonsterCollection30029"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The current leader of dragons, having considered nothing but war as the solution between the clans, with a bottomless hatred for humans. Thanks to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>, the Dragon Flame is rekindled, and the war against humans is resumed. The goal is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>seize control of Comodo</color> from the Nerius family, and rebuild the past glory of the dragons.",
    ["MonsterCollection30030"]="A cunning <color=#44afee>demon</color> from Otherworld excels at deluding people. He was seriously injured in Ragnarok and fell to the Realm of the Dead after going into a coma. Upon awakening, he starts <color=#44afee>searching for a way to recast his body</color>. Under Hel's influence, he <color=#44afee>disguises himself as a god</color> and responds to a follower's summon...\n\"I hear thee. Human... Say thy request, and say thy name. I shall bring thee a <color=#44afee>miracle</color>...\" Somewhere on the island in Arunafeltz, a devoted follower in a prone posture is listening to the oracle from the <color=#44afee>orb</color>...",
    ["MonsterCollection30031"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A guardian of order in time and space. It's essentially a <color=#CA2E0AFF>collection of energy</color> generated by unstable activity in the dimensional gap, so it has no true form. It can present itself in various forms, with the most common being a spheroid with <color=#CA2E0AFF>countless eyes</color>. Its pupils are <color=#CA2E0AFF>gears</color> and it's said each eye represents a parallel world. Monsters like this will not attack humans, but it will punish those who try to disrupt order in time and space.\n\\No one should ever interfere with the laws of time and space or you'll become fodder for the Time Holder!\" a silver-haired time traveler warns angrily.\"",
    ["MonsterCollection30032"]="<color=#44afee>Poring family's</color> newest member, who was not included in the family until recently. From a Monsterology perspective, it should have the <color=#44afee>same origin as Angeling</color>. However, what confuses every researcher the most is that the two monsters share <color=#44afee>almost the same habits and characteristics</color> and live in totally different habitats. There is an ongoing debate in the academic world, and no one can present a plausible answer.\n\"If I can solve this problem, then I must be the winner of the next <color=#44afee>Mobel Prize</color> in Monsterology...\" Midnight, inside the lab, a fifty-year-old monster researcher pushes his glasses back to his nose and starts implementing crazy algorithms on the scratch paper.",
    ["MonsterCollection30033"]="A rare creature made of <color=#44afee>unknown energy</color> that looks like a toy consists of <color=#44afee>three cube-shaped blocks</color>. In fact, its body is full of <color=#44afee>electric current</color>, making it a hazardous monster. The majority of its life is spent in standby mode, living off <color=#44afee>electrons</color> from the surrounding environment. Wakes up only when it's fully charged.\n\"The tiny cubes that float aside the Gioia act like a battery's <color=#44afee>positive and negative anodes</color>, responsible for transmitting energy. So, the best way to defeat a Gioia is to break its arms...\" Before entering the ruins, the leader of the expedition draws out a detailed body diagram on a portable blackboard for the teammates on their first mission.",
    ["MonsterCollection30034"]="The RSX series, Rekenber Corp's first <color=#44afee>semi-automatic mining machine</color>, was a significant milestone in the industrialization reform of the Einbroch mining area. It shone for decades before it gracefully retired to make way for new, fully automated mining robots, and now it's a prized exhibit at a museum. But the most important <color=#44afee>RSX-0806 Prototype</color> mysteriously went missing just before it was scheduled to be recycled. Not long after, an engineer responsible for managing the mining area reported seeing the lost RSX-0806 <color=#44afee>deep in the mines</color> in a surveillance video, surprisingly, its <color=#44afee>operator</color> was...?!\n\"Teacher, does <color=#44afee>Pitman</color> actually know how to use these mining machines?\" a boy eagerly questioned in the Einbroch City Library exhibit hall, his eyes wide with wonder.",
    ["MonsterCollection30035"]="Over the years, the front desk at the Einbroch Monster Management Bureau has continually received reports of dragons spotted in the <color=#44afee>Nogg Cave</color>. A lot of people think there's a secret <color=#44afee>dragon nest</color> there, which might be the source of all the dragons that soar above Einbroch Field. However, some <color=#44afee>fanatic religious scholars</color> argue that the deep cave leads to the legendary Yggdrasil and that the dragon in question is none other than Nidhoggr, the malevolent dragon perched atop the poisonous glaciers of <color=#44afee>Hvergelmir</color>, <color=#44afee>feasting on the roots of Yggdrasil</color>.\n\"... And when it severs the root of Yggdrasil, <color=#44afee>Ragnarok</color> will dawn upon us again! We're doomed... all doomed! Hahahahaha...\" The sound of a forehead repeatedly banging against metal is heard as a madman, admitted nearly three years ago, starts another day of his relentless shrieking and howling...",
    ["MonsterCollection30036"]="According to the Mystic Phenomena Research Association, dozens of stories about the Gloom Under Night exist. Some believe it's a demon that clawed its way back from Niflheim's abyss. Others say it's the tormented souls of fallen warriors, twisted into a faceless monster after dying in the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color> fifteen years ago. And then there are those who whisper that the Ice Cave has long been a <color=#44afee>human experiment site</color>, and the Gloom Under Night, it's just one of the <color=#44afee>monsters created by the experiment</color>...",
    ["MonsterCollection30037"]="Human <color=#44afee>desires</color> are boundless. And so, the heavens sent forth their <color=#44afee>messenger</color>, to bring <color=#44afee>retribution</color> upon the foolish and the wicked.",
    ["MonsterCollection30039"]="<color=#44afee>Goldie Wie</color> was born in the barren desert region of <color=#44afee>Morroc</color>. Once a rising star of the Assassins Guild, she broke their code by <color=#44afee>attacking a merchant caravan</color> and was ultimately <color=#44afee>exiled</color>. But she wasn't driven by greed; she just couldn't stand by while the poor in the slums suffered from <color=#44afee>hunger and disease</color>. To help them, she became an outlaw, a thief for justice...\n\"If justice fails to protect the weak, then let it be cast aside.\"—Goldie Wie",
    ["MonsterCollection30040"]="<color=#44afee>Ivy Flamel</color> is the only son of Nicolas Flamel, the current head of the Alchemist Guild. A <color=#44afee>prodigy</color> studying at Juno University, his intelligence far surpasses ordinary people, giving him limitless potential in alchemy, but also isolating him as someone most would call a <color=#44afee>madman</color>. He seems to have an unusual, unspoken <color=#44afee>obsession</color> with Celia...\n\"Life is infinite, but never repeating.\"—Ivy Flamel",
    ["MonsterCollection31001"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Appears to be merely a huge Roda Frog <color=#CA2E0AFF>with a crown</color>. However, at its command, all Roda Frogs will forsake their lives to execute its command. Its glory as king is beyond doubt. Wearing a crown means carrying its weight. It holds its head up proudly, never letting the crown fall.",
    ["MonsterCollection31002"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A manifestation of the god of light, Baldr, with its original meaning being <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Leader's Ring\"</color>. With a crown on its head and a staff in its hand, it is obvious to everyone that it is the leader of the Porings. The Mastering bears the heavy responsibility of protecting the Poring race. It shows no mercy to people who harm Porings maliciously, so be prepared for the wrath of the Mastering!",
    ["MonsterCollection31004"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The Dragon Flies which dwell in the Sograt Desert have <color=#CA2E0AFF>pearlescent compound eyes</color> more attractive than common Chonchons and particularly eye-catching in the barren desert. However, according to Monster Researcher Bertha's years of observation, Dragon Flies go crazy during certain special weather conditions. Its attack power then is no less than the Kraken in the sea. Adventurers should watch out for sudden sandstorms in the desert, for those may have been caused by crazed Dragon Flies.",
    ["MonsterCollection31005"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A <color=#CA2E0AFF>wolf chief that lost</color> in its bid to become the Wolf King. It wanders the desert while harboring hatred towards its own kind, <color=#CA2E0AFF>attacking any living creature it sees</color> out of an insatiable craving for their flesh.",
    ["MonsterCollection31006"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> Has an exceptional sense of smell which can locate others of their kind, even just the smell of their furs. Seems to favor <color=#CA2E0AFF>Durian Grass</color>. In appearance, it only differs from the Lunatic in terms of fur color. However, the Eclipse is not as gentle as the Lunatic. Despite their fur being excellent clothing material, adventurers are advised not to provoke Eclipses for their fur.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The following is an extract from the important news section of the Kingdom Times: Novices should take care in distinguishing the color of the Lunatic's fur. Should an Eclipse be discovered, please hide immediately and inform the Kingdom Defense Force!",
    ["MonsterCollection31008"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A manifestation of the god of darkness Hodur's accessory with its original meaning being <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Ghost's Ring\"</color>. The Ghostring aglow with an eerie blue light hides under an empty ghost shell. Nobody has seen its real body. Rumor has it that it is a shy blue Poring and because it is not good at communicating with other Porings, hides itself under a bed sheet and appears to all as a ghost.",
    ["MonsterCollection31009"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> A gigantic monster hidden in the depths of the sea. Apparently, it escaped from a chef's pot when it was young and mutated to have sharp <color=#CA2E0AFF>pincers</color> and an impenetrable <color=#CA2E0AFF>armor</color>. However, close observation will reveal that its body is covered with <color=#CA2E0AFF>irregular stripes</color> caused by being steamed at high temperatures. Who could have thought that such exceptionally strong monsters had almost become dinner for the nobles?",
    ["MonsterCollection31010"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> \"...The arrogant and tyrannical King Schmidt attempted to defile the Goddess in a show of power. This sparked an uproar in the city, spurring resentment and indignation. To intimidate his citizens, King Schmidt captured the legendary Chimera, a monster with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>head of a lion and body of a goat</color>. Those who dare speak up against him are fed to the beast alive. It wasn't long before no one dared speak of the matter in the open again.\n\"However, the Chimera is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bloodthirsty and vicious</color> beast. It couldn't be tamed, no matter how long it was kept. All it took was one momentary slip-up by the servant charged with watching the beast for the Chimera to escape. Freed of its prison, the Chimera ran rampant across Glast Heim, hurting people and damaging property alike. Unable to bear it any longer, the Goddess readied a seal and bestowed upon man a graphite spear which King Schmidt's Chivalry Commander Heinrich used to pierce the beast's throat, slaying it. However, the people are no longer allowed to touch the water in the city as it will break the seal and bring the beast back to life.\"\n—The Mysterious Collapse of Glast Heim, Eden Group Third Edition.",
    ["MonsterCollection31011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color> The ominous sword of legend that is said to have led the gods to their doom. It was transformed from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mistletoe</color> growing at the edge of the realm of gods. When the god of light Baldr dreamt that his life was about to be extinguished, Queen Frigga asked all living creatures to swear an oath to her that they would never harm Baldr. All of them, that is, except the mistletoe that was overlooked because it was too small and weak. In the end, it was that very mistletoe that transformed into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysteltainn</color> and killed Baldr, bringing forth Ragnarok.",
    ["MonsterCollection31012"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color>It's said to be a sword of Tyr, the God of War, with a blade as brilliant as flames and that never rusts. Inevitably drawing blood whenever it is unsheathed, it is a sword that brings its wielder supreme glory. However, it is also a <color=#CA2E0AFF>demonic sword</color> that can lead to its wielder's destruction. Every swing puts its wielder to the test. Failure to remain true to one's beliefs means that the wielder will become food that nourishes this demonic sword.",
    ["MonsterCollection31014"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>jayw</color>An apostate who was enticed by demons, <color=#CA2E0AFF>fell into depravity</color>, becoming disloyal to his former belief and losing the rationality that made him a human. Regarding the voice from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>abyss</color> as an oracle, he would do anything so that this \"god\" can come to this world.",
    ["MonsterCollection31015"]="Coelacanth is a very <color=#44afee>ancient</color> monster. It's said that it was born in the poisonous glacier of Hvergelmir and existed even before the time of gods. They wander in Gjoll and <color=#44afee>live off the undead</color>, and their sharp jaw teeth can pierce through the <color=#44afee>hollow spirits</color> to make them feel the long-forgotten pain once again. This is one of the most horrifying punishments among Niflheim. Hel will dump the sinful undead into Hvergelmir for them to rot in the corrosion from the poison while suffering the unbearable flesh-tearing pain from the Coelacanth...",
    ["MonsterCollection31016"]="One of Hel's most important servants, <color=#44afee>Executioner of the Underworld</color>, has absolute control over the living and dead. In spite of being Undead, he gives up the appearance of his former life and refuses to discuss it with others. It's said that a servant found a bloodstained <color=#44afee>Squire's Medallion</color> in his room while cleaning...\n\"Huh? Naght Sieger? I like how he takes revenge on someone, even on the slightest things... Killing one's own kind is the most beautiful thing humans can do. Ha-ha-ha...\" Lately, whenever someone mentions this newly appointed Executioner of the Underworld to Hel, she shows a delightful smile.",
    ["MonsterCollection31017"]="Ever since the <color=#44afee>Khayr Estate</color> was invaded, reports have been flying to the guards saying that an <color=#44afee>unknown monster</color> with <color=#44afee>white wings</color> appears next to the <color=#44afee>abandoned dry well</color> in the estate. Strange enough, every single one who has had <color=#44afee>eye contact</color> with it loses their memories of the day soon after, and all they recall is a pair of crystal-clear eyes that look down from the sky high above, as if it <color=#44afee>stares at the fate among every mortal</color> incessantly.\n\"He equally gives everyone his love and equally grants everyone their death.\" A pale hand gently touches the <color=#44afee>mysterious runes</color> carved on the dry well, as the lament fades away in the cold air at night.",
    ["MonsterCollection31018"]="Monsters that only exist in the <color=#44afee>Juperos Ruins</color>. They share a face similar to Gioia but lack the cube-shaped arms to transmit energy. The <color=#44afee>colloidal substances</color> that structure their bodies have a unique composition, allowing them to reproduce by <color=#44afee>self-splitting</color> or become stronger by <color=#44afee>devouring their own kind</color>. Those tiny little wings and tails they have are absolutely adorable, and it's said that ornaments made after the appearance of Skeggiold are trendy among young girls.\n\"The latest Skeggiold cushion! Pendant! Earrings! Don't miss out by walking out!\" In the busy market in Juno City, a grocery merchant is selling his latest products tirelessly.",
    ["MonsterCollection31019"]="There have been recent sightings of a Queen Scaraba <color=#44afee>wandering alone</color> on the <color=#44afee>Einbroch Field</color>, which is pretty rare for the <color=#44afee>gregarious</color> Golden Scaraba. Monster researchers believe she could be a former leader who was <color=#44afee>defeated</color> in a duel. Golden Scaraba operates under a strict hierarchy, with the queen at the top, and everyone has clear roles and responsibilities. However, if multiple leaders emerge, their pheromones can get mixed up, leading males and workers to abandon their duties, potentially destroying the colony. When this happens, the queens <color=#44afee>capable of reproduction</color> will <color=#44afee>duel</color> for dominance, with the winner becoming the new leader and the loser <color=#44afee>forced to leave the group</color> and live in solitude...",
    ["MonsterCollection31020"]="The monsters found deep in Nogg Cave are said to emerge from <color=#44afee>magma that's loaded with magic</color>. Their bodies, crystallized from <color=#44afee>concentrated magic</color>, <color=#44afee>take in magic</color> through glands on their skin, so their size depends heavily on the concentration of magic in the environment, potentially expanding to many times their original size. When their bodies store nearly too much magic, they <color=#44afee>reproduce</color> by <color=#44afee>splitting</color>. \n\"I spent three months in Nogg Cave to get this larva! I nearly ended up a snack for that Faceworm Queen! Now, just to soak it in a <color=#44afee>high-concentrated magic solution</color> and then I can cash in big time...\" In a shadowy, damp basement, a poacher was humming away, pouring a colorful liquid into a container holding the larva with his partner.",
    ["MonsterCollection31021"]="Ktullanux holds an extremely <color=#44afee>high</color> status in the hearts of the people of Arunafeltz. The teachings of the Freyja say that this <color=#44afee>sacred beast</color> once fought alongside the very first pope to shape the kingdom. After the pope's death, it withdrew to the <color=#44afee>Ice Cave</color>, watching over generations of successors. Yet, in recent years, something strange has happened. It seems to have faded from public view, and <color=#44afee>no longer answers those who call upon it</color>. Why has it gone silent? What secret lies beneath its eternal slumber?",
    ["MonsterCollection31022"]="<color=#44afee>Death</color> is not the end. <color=#44afee>Sleep</color>, my sheep. <color=#44afee>Rest</color>, my sheep. Beyond the veil lies the <color=#44afee>eternal bliss</color> that awaits all.",
    ["MonsterCollection31023"]="<color=#44afee>Celia Aide</color> is a sweet and cheerful girl from <color=#44afee>Geffen</color> in the Rune-Midgard Kingdom. She's currently studying abroad at the <color=#44afee>Hubawooz Magic School</color> in Juno. Overflowing with <color=#44afee>curiosity</color>, she loves questioning even the most obvious things and exploring the truth behind them. Unfortunately, that same curiosity often gets her into <color=#44afee>unpredictable</color> danger...\n\"The unknown is the most exciting thing in the world.\"—Celia Aide",
    ["MonsterCollection31024"]="<color=#44afee>Kavaski Icarus</color> is one of the top young archers from Payon Archer Village. He's determined to prove his strength, though sometimes, he is too <color=#44afee>narrow-minded</color> to see the bigger picture. To sharpen his skills, he set out on a journey, hoping to one day <color=#44afee>earn the recognition of his master, Sky Euin</color>. But after crossing into the Schwarzwald Republic with his companions, all contact with him was suddenly lost...\n\"I will find what I was truly meant to protect.\"—Kavaski Icarus",
    ["MonsterDropTips"]="Current Level's EXP Gains: %s%%. Material Drop Gains: %s%%.",
