    ["NpcName69999"]="Test NPC",
    ["NpcStoryContent200011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Bleh...\" Klaus heaves a sigh. The recent month has been the darkest month he has faced ever since he took over Green Cotton Farm from his father.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Green Cotton Farm mainly rear Fabres. Fabres are docile, and the silk they make is an important material for Prontera silk. Because of that, Green Cotton Farm has been a key place of production for Rune Kingdom.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>However, despite constant pestering from merchants requesting for goods, Klaus could not do anything, because the Fabres are on strike! Yes, it is true, Fabres—which are as meek as lambs— actually went on strike!<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>This reminds him of Bertha, the little girl who always tells him that \"Fabres are our friends, not our slaves.\" It is said that she became a monster researcher after graduating from Criatura Academy, and her research on Fabres is well-known throughout the kingdom. \"How I wish you were here. I bet you'd know what to do in this situation...\" Klaus smiles helplessly. A flashback of Bertha saying her last words before she left the farm she grew up at comes to his mind. \"I'll never return to this Fabre slave den!\"<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>At the same time, Bertha is at Prontera South Gate, which is not too far from the farm. Based on her understanding of Fabres, she knows that the only possible reason is that they are hungry; however she does not think that Klaus would make such an elementary mistake. She is deeply concerned about the situation at Green Cotton Farm, but remembering what she said before she left, she is unwilling to help.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>And it is up to me to bring them together.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I used Bertha's method and lured the gigantic Fabre to the farm. Yes, it is the culprit for the shortage of food at the farm. After solving this issue, Green Cotton Farm should be back to normal. Will the two of them patch up? I think not, as ideological differences do not go away easily. Perhaps, things are fine this way. Because despite them using different methods, they both love Green Cotton Farm.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"What is Music?\" Morts once believed that music is the vessel of love. Those who heard his singing recount that it was as if his affection transformed into musical notes floating in the air. His songs and looks mesmerized many young women, and his fame gradually grew until eventually became the most popular idol around. Ever since then, he changed his singing style to cater to his fans' liking, and thus did the soul of his music begin to fade as the days went by; one day, all that will remain is an empty husk of what he once was. \n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>When I first met Morts at Prontera South Gate, I saw a typical idol, exhausted by his popularity. Although he yearns for his lover, for the sake of his career, he does not hesitate to keep his relationship hidden.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>And what about his lover, Poya? I can see the anxiety in her eyes. I wonder if I will ever meet them again.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200022"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Helping Poya to pass a gift to Morts became a turning point for them. Who would have known?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Poya is one who works behind the scenes. She had been with Morts even before he became famous, and when Morts was in the limelight, she would willingly step, not wanting to obstruct his road to stardom. But as time passed, her love for Morts turned into hatred, and her jealousy of the girls around him was like a seed of darkness, taking root in her heart, sprouting and growing at a rapid speed. She tries to convince herself by saying, \"Morts is not serious about them. The reason he says that he's not in a relationship is to protect his career in showbiz!\" However, deep down in her heart, a voice was screaming, \"Am I nothing to you, Morts? I'm the only one who truly loves you!\" In the eyes of many, a 7-year-long relationship is a stable one, but Poya found no security in it at all. I believe... Morts has not even noticed this—or perhaps he's selectively ignored it?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>What would you do if you wanted a person solely to yourself? Poya chose the most extreme method—to die together. Her jealousy of the girls around Morts reached a point where it consumed her and broke her heart. To Poya, her only escape is dying together with Morts, for by doing so, they will be together eternally—in another world.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>To my surprise, Morts decided to leave showbiz temporarily.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It seems that Morts is not as frivolous as I thought; rather, he is a simple-minded musician. It was not the temptation of beauty or fame that caused him to lose his way, but his desire for recognition. \"The people love my songs, so I'll write something they like\" This is what he is thinking in his mind as he presses on. Unfortunately, in the process, he neglected those beside him, especially Poya.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"I wish to take back the soul of my music.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"I wish to take back Poya's love.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"I wish to take back what I lost.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Morts' determined look was the reason I felt it right to help him.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200023"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It did not take long before I met him again. The two of them headed to the Underwater Temple, probably to look for the Obeaunes, a race with a flair for music. Legend says that they hate humans, but it seems that Morts' songs managed to win their respect. In the presence of Strouf, Morts sang the proposal song he composed for Poya. However, after gaining the boon of Strouf, Morts abandoned his plan to propose.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>He did this because he thought the timing was not right. First, he plans to regain the lost soul in his singing, which was full of the spirit of love. After that, he will introduce Poya to all his fans and propose to her in front of them. He confided only to me, yet in the corner of my eye, I caught a glimpse of Poya smiling. I could not help but wonder if Poya managed to sense what Morts was conveying through his song.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Oh yes, there was another small episode. I have been curious about Morts' old, worn lute; it turns out it was a gift from Poya, something she made personally. In a sense, this lute played a critical role in preventing Morts from drowning in vanity.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200024"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Talking about music to Goblins is like casting pearls before swine, and it gets you into danger on top of that.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Morts and Poya found themselves in danger in the Goblin Forest. To protect Poya, the powerless Morts had to use his lute as a lure to buy time for me to come to their rescue. Sadly, the lute was destroyed in the process. If you say Morts sings for love, then this lute that Poya gave him would be the carrier of that love. The depressed look on Morts' face after he lost the lute worries me, but I decided to give them some time to settle down. Somehow, I still believe in Morts. If he truly loves music from his heart, he can recover from this loss.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>After all, he is a natural-born genius whose songs can touch the hearts of all those who hear.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200025"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The barrenness of the desert gives one a feeling of emptiness, but for someone who seeks to meditate, it is the ideal location.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Morts is deep in thought, thinking about things that even Poya cannot understand. It is a crucial step for someone to become great, and many had tried but gave up midway; however, I feel that he can succeed, so I caught the condors that he requested.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>What kind of creature is the condor? When they are still fledglings, they must fight hard to survive, but when they soar in the sky, they are free, with no one obstructing their flight. Their high, shrill screams pierce the air, striking fear into my heart, yet Morts is unmoved. Is he reaching enlightenment? I will find out soon enough.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Morts had been pondering the purpose of his lute to him. In the past, the lute was Poya's soul. Without its sound, his singing would have no soul—that was until he saw the condor, not bound by anything. He felt the power in the condor's cry, and in that instant, he realized something.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"I'll sing my love for Poya with my voice! My voice has power in it!\" Morts shouts delightedly like a little kid, while Poya watches him with a gentle look of indulgence.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200031"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The first impression Soros gave me was unique—he likes to address himself and others using archaic words.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>He is a master tailor who specializes in designing and making wedding dresses. His dream is to come up with the best wedding dress design in the world. One day, I found some exquisite Eclipse Fur and gave it to him. He was so grateful to me that he intends to sew my name on the wedding dress. Heh, I guess I have no reason to stop him. I wonder if I would get the chance to see the end product? The best wedding dress in the world... it would be amazing.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Oh yes, there was another thing I learned—Do not use Eclipse Fur to draw out an Eclipse. Although Soros is silent on this subject, he probably has some painful memories regarding it.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200032"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>A long, long time has passed, so long that I almost forgot about Soros, until I met him in the desert.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It seems that he had been traveling around the world with the wedding dress he made, hoping to gain the recognition of all. The people in Prontera revered his so-called best wedding dress in the world, but in a place like Sograt Desert, no one showed any interest.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The brides in Sograt Desert prefer wedding dresses that have a simple cut and are cooling, short and revealing to accentuate their curves. To them, Soros' Eclipse Fur wedding dress is not as good as the ones that he made creatively using improvised materials. Despite making a name for himself, it makes Soros wonder, \"What is the best wedding dress in the world?\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Do all masters seek to be the best in the world? Are all artisans like this?",
    ["NpcStoryContent200041"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>There is a standby actor named Grute in Prontera. When I first met him, I thought that he had all the qualities of a lead actor: he has the looks, is fluent in speech and most importantly, he can act. The one thing stopping him from becoming a lead actor is his poor memory. It's so bad that I would go as far as saying that it is atrocious.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It is a pity, but all I can say is, he's just a normal guy. I wish him all the best for his acting career.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200042"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The title I gave to this note is no longer valid, because when I met him previously, I did not know that he was related to Strouf—that is, until I met another person suffering from a similar ailment.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>This person is called Dilber; not only does he look just as good as Grute, his memory is so bad that it reminded me of him. Dilber claims that an Obeaune, whom he does not recognize, is hunting him. While fighting that Obeaune, who is named Lucie, she showed no intention of causing harm. The thing that caught my interest is, she called Dilber a \"heartless man.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>However, Dilber had the same reaction as Grute. His memory is so bad that it cannot possibly be an act. What exactly happened? I cannot help but wonder.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200043"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Just as I thought, I met Lucie in the Underwater Temple. Although she has sharp teeth, she is not a terrible person... or fish. According to her, Dilber proposed to her with a ring but was caught while she was preparing to elope. As a result, he was punished by Strouf and had disappeared ever since then, therefore Lucie calls him a \"heartless man.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>To my surprise, from her mouth came a familiar name: Grute!\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Grute's Obeaune lover, Leigh, chose to question Strouf on what caused Grute to be in the state he is in now, in exchange for her residing in the Underwater Temple eternally. Leigh told me that Obeaunes can never have true love with a person from another race, or that person will be cursed by Strouf and forget everything. The following passage is an excerpt from Leigh's diary. It led me to think that I was right not telling Lucie the truth:\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I do not know why Lord Strouf put such a curse on Obeaunes as he is not hostile to humans. Although humans are not welcomed here, we would not cause them any harm. Is Lord Strouf trying to stop the mixing between humans and Obeaunes? I do not think so, because he told me this: \"No one's at fault. All we can blame that is we are children of the sea.\" Could it be that this curse did not originate from Lord Strouf? Is that why even though Obeaunes are more powerful than humans, we can never go on land?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>If the curse was not Lord Strouf's doing, then whose is it? Is the culprit behind the curse afraid that the people of the sea will dominate the land? So many \"whys,\" and the future is bleak. If Lucie learns about this, she will probably cause mayhem.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200051"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The knight and the princess, a favorite trope of scriptwriters. But what about the knight and the prince? Hey, don't let your imagination run amok. This is a story about a prince from a minor branch of the seven royal families and his female knight.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Ivan Lugenburg: Those who are familiar with the seven royal families will know that strength is everything to the Lugenburg Family. Someone frail like Ivan has no place in such a family, thus he has always been a prince in name only.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Arlene: Her family has served as knights under the command of the princes of Lugenburg for generations. Since birth, she had to put on armor and take up arms to protect the princes. She hated her identity, so she broke her family's rule and became an adventurer. As punishment for what she did, she was assigned to serve Ivan.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Little did they know, this would be the turning point in their lives. Ivan loves to make pastries, write poems, and draw. He always prepares food for Arlene whenever she heads out, and this was how I first met them. Despite being a prince, Ivan receives no support, so Arlene has to take up adventurer assignments to earn some money for both families. Although they are master and servant, Ivan treats Arlene as his own and his equal. Everyone around Arlene says that she is of lower status, that's why Ivan hit her in a soft spot.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>When I brought food prepared by Ivan to Arlene, who was on the frontlines, the expression she showed was that of a cute young girl and not a knight. I would say that it is definitely more fitting for her age!",
    ["NpcStoryContent200052"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Ivan is powerless. As much as he would like to share Arlene's burden, it is an impossible feat for him due to the cold, harsh reality of his frailty. He can memorize the entire layout of the Labyrinth Forest, but he needs a bodyguard following him closely.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Yet at the same time, Ivan is powerful. There was a time when they lost their way, and Arlene was worried that they could never return home. However, all it took was one glance at Ivan, and just like that, Arlene was back to her usual reliable self.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It is obvious to even a bystander like me that they are dependent on each other. Their relationship surpasses one of a master and servant, it is something like... a family? A couple? Neither describes it accurately.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>All I can say is that they cannot live without each other.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200053"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>When Ivan is not around, Arlene becomes her girlish self once more.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I know that she has fear of ghosts, so I do not understand why she wanted to go on a mission to exterminate them. Be it to earn money for the family, or a knight's honor, all these are useless before instinctual fear. The shipwreck is full of Arlene's worst fears: Whispers, White Skeletons, and the ghost princess in the rumors. During this short mission, I witnessed new faces of Arlene: She is afraid of ghost, delicate, and also willful. Just as I thought, Arlene is just like any other girl. I wonder how she managed to act all reliable and tough? Of course, I will keep this a secret to Ivan for her sake.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>She seems to wish to continue to keep her trustworthy image of a knight before Ivan. Though in my opinion, Ivan probably does not care about all this and would rather Arlene be more genuine before him.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200061"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The Mira family was once a powerful one, but it declined over time on their own accord. They regarded Evelyn the witch as the chief goddes and worshipped her, and because of that, every descendent of that family carries some form of special ability.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Despite living in an age when Odin is considered the chief god, they had no intention of going with the flow. They decided to withdraw from the secular world and protect the witch and the truth regarding her for generations. Thus, only rumors are left in the records regarding this family.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>One day, I heard rumors that Raven, a young boy who can summon monsters and talk to them, was spotted outside Prontera West Gate, so I headed there to talk to him. To my surprise, I found out that his father is named Punk Mira. Because of the rumors surrounding the Mira family, I was curious about Punk. Why did he return to the secular world? Why did he abandon his wife and return to Labyrinth Forest to fulfill his duty?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>And just what is Mira family's duty?",
    ["NpcStoryContent200062"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>In a calm and quiet tone, Punk Mira recounted the truth behind the War of Witches. He said that the witches have disappeared from this world, and only those belonging to Odin's bloodline can see them. Finding what he said confusing and absurd, I shifted my gaze between him and the witch levitating beside him.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>It seems that Punk truly could not see the witch who he reveres, despite her being right next to him. This is something that every generation of children in the Mira family goes through. To will themselves to fulfill their duty, their ancestor laid a curse on themselves and they were doomed to forever rely on Labyrinth Forest's magical power to survive. As time passes, the Mira family's honor and duty became a heavy burden. The curse which brought them honor became a curse that brings them pain.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Should I tell him that his wife and child is waiting for him?",
    ["NpcStoryContent200071"]="Story Content",
    ["NpcStoryContent200072"]="Story Content",
    ["NpcStoryContent200073"]="Story Content",
    ["NpcStoryContent200081"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Oh Lord Strouf, I'm Colorful Nerius, the strongest in the sea of Midgard and the captain of the Valkyrie, flagship of the Unicorn Fleet. I'm under orders to transport important goods for the Nerius Family to Einbroch.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Colorful Nerius was the heir apparent to the Nerius Family and also one of the few promising contenders to the throne. Although she felt that a simple transport task like this was not befitting of her Valkyrie, she had no choice but to obey as it was an order from above. The task had only one condition: To deliver the shipment to Einbroch within eight days. Usually, it takes seven days to travel to Einbroch by sea, but six days will suffice if she goes at full speed.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The ship was transporting only the Nerius Family's gold coins... and possibly other things that she did not know of because the goods were loaded on board by the royal guards, and even the great Captain Colorful was not allowed to know its contents. She was thinking, \"What does it matter? It's just a transport mission. Scrambling the Unicorn Fleet for it is a waste of resources.\" At that time, she did not sense anything strange. In hindsight, this might be one of the reasons why she was not suited for the throne.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The first three days were quiet and uneventful. The Unicorn Fleet was en route to its destination. It happened on the fourth night. A messenger pigeon from the Prontera Alchemy Center arrived on the deck.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"In two days, there will be thick fog over the sea of Midgard. It's too risky to continue the journey. Turn back immediately.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Turning back would mean that the Unicorn Fleet had failed its mission, and the Nerius Family's reputation would be tarnished; continuing the journey would mean that the Unicorn Fleet may encounter the king of the fog—the great Marse Kraken and its pirate ships. Colorful did not even think for a split second before deciding the fleet's fate.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"A Kraken? Hah, that's great! It's time to prove who is the true ruler of the sea!\" Colorful was bored by the dull mission. It was inevitable that she would jump at the opportunity to challenge such a powerful adversary.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"But captain, our mission is to...\" Her first mate reminded her fearfully.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Don't worry! At full speed, we will arrive within two days. Even if we don't meet the Kraken, I'm fine either way.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The first mate could only stare helplessly at the captain, who was overwhelmed with excitement, and did not dare say anything further.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The Unicorn Fleet continued its journey, with the Valkyrie leading the way, guiding the fleet in the supposedly correct direction in the fog. All seemed to be going smoothly... until the sixth night.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Damn it, I didn't expect this to happen...\" There was no sign of land. The Valkyrie was lost at sea. When Colorful was thinking of the next step, the thundering roar of the cannon interrupted her mid-thought.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Enemies incoming! It's the Kraken!\"<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Heh, how kind of you to show up. I'd all but given up!\" Colorful thought delightfully as she jumped off the sofa and headed to the bridge to issue battle orders. In the next instant, she sensed an aura of death spreading in the air. This aura was not magical, but rather formless and filling the air.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>What happened next was a nightmare of a battle—after being touched by the aura, the soldiers of the Unicorn Fleet all fell to the deck, writhing in pain as they were slain by the Skeletons that boarded the ship. The next time they rose, they had joined the ranks of the enemy. Within moments, the tide turned, and Colorful's army collapsed in the blink of an eye.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Damn it!\" Despite being affected by the same aura, Colorful endured the pain coursing through her body and readied her sword along with the royal guards. However, a giant blade fell from the sky and knocked the wind out of them.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"Ugh, we couldn't even put up a fight...\" Colorful cursed in her mind. Just before losing consciousness, she heard the owner of the blade, Drake, say in a low, piercing voice, \"This ship is big enough for Lord Kraken. He will surely find this place comfortable. Boys, this ship belongs to us now!\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>On the next day, the Unicorn Fleet emerged from the thick fog. After some quick calibrations, they managed to find the correct direction and reached their destination. However, their flagship was not among them. There's no doubt that its captain's stubbornness led to its downfall.",
    ["NpcStoryContent200091"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Betta and Tyneil were just your average couple.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>One year after they parted ways, they arranged to meet at the peak of Mjolnir Mountains, so Ygnizem and I escorted them there separately. This is just another day in the field, as helping others is a piece of cake for us.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Betta lost his sight in an accident. That is why Ygnizem escorted them to Geffen to seek treatment from the Sage Guild. Again, this is nothing too special. I can summarize their story as, \"Oh poor Betta. How unfortunate!\" Period.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>So why did I choose to write their story, then?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I have a feeling about the words \"Blind\" and \"Sage.\" they seem to ring a bell... Did I hear these words in some other mission?",
    ["NpcStoryContent210011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>\"A giant serpent swallowing the sea; a giant serpent swallowing the sea; a rainbow-colored eagle swallowed it instead; and made a nest upon the sea.\"\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>This is a well-known nursery rhyme that sings of the brave ancestors of the seven royal families slaying Jormungandr and establishing the kingdom of Rune-Midgarts.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The seven royal families are:\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Gaebolg: The leader of the serpent-slaying heroes, Tristan Gaebolg, came from this family.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Nerius: A matriarchal family.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Heines: Magical power flows in their veins. The current Great Sage of Geffen is from this family.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Wigner: This family seeks freedom and avoids conflict.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Lugenburg: A family of strong fighters.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Richard: Holds the reins of the army.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Walter: The embodiment of the spirit of chivalry.<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>For generations, the king of Rune-Midgarts was selected from one of these seven families. Of these families, the Gaebolg Family suffers the most as the eldest son of each generation is doomed to die a tragic death. Despite the family claiming that their crown prince died of disease, from fighting monsters, performing some heroic feat, or other unfortunate incidents, all these coincidences point to one truth.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>—\"The Gaebolg Family is cursed\" That's the rumor on the streets.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Does such a curse truly exist? With one less successor candidate in each generation, what will the seven families plan to do? After all, it is a war of succession. No matter how united their ancestors were, it is inevitable that the relationship between their descendants would deteriorate, especially during such a time.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Tristan Gaebolg III and his three sons have not appeared before the people for a long time. The other six royal families are all eager for an opportunity to act. What happened to the king and the princes? After sharing this story, Rhodes apologized, saying that what happens after is a closely guarded secret of the royal families, and it is not for him to know.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I guess it is true that since ancient times, there will always be shadows looming over the throne.",
    ["NpcStoryContent210021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I have been curious about the reason why there is such a massive underground sewer in Prontera. How did the ancient people manage to construct it? There is factual proof that confirms the validity of my question. This unusual sewer does have some history behind it.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Remember what was written in Legend of the Kingdom's Founding? The seven royal families slew Jormungandr, established the kingdom of Rune-Midgarts, then built Prontera on top of the serpent's nest. You heard me right—the nest of Jormungandr was reconstructed as the sewers.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Although the serpent is dead, its dark energies still fill the air. That is why one can often find mutated monsters, oversized yet lifeless flowers, and water channels with no entrance in the sewers. Would it be possible that the sewers serve as a barrier between Prontera and the darkness left behind by the serpent?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>On a side note, there is a rumor that every underground labyrinth contains treasure. This could be true after all.",
    ["NpcStoryContent210031"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Did you know about the existence of the witch? It's not a simple rumor. How did the Labyrinth Forest come to be? Did sealing the Deviling here distort space? I learned a secret hidden by Odin from the hermit, Punk...\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>There are two reasons why gods are gods: 1) They are worshipped and revered by people. They are the law itself. 2) They are almighty. They are power itself. To Odin, the existences that threaten him are those that have the power of a god, but do not adhere to the concept of order—Evelyn the witch was one of them. Odin thinks that Evelyn is challenging the order of the world, but the truth is, Evelyn does not care about all this—all she cares about is living and protecting the land she loves, freely.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>However, with great power comes great responsibility. Baphomet's demonic ring transformed into Deviling, causing mayhem and harming the people. Odin chose to ignore this to force the witch to act. His believers would probably think that this was another test from their god. However, the witch had to fight for the land that she loves.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>All went according to Odin's plan. Although the battle between the witch and the Deviling was not as devastating as the final battle against Morroc, it still changed the landscape of the Labyrinth Forest forever. The witch cast a forbidden spell to seal the Deviling in the forest—at the cost of her life. Her body vanished, and her soul transformed into the Stone of the Witch. Its endless magical power engulfed the entire forest, distorting the space and time there. This is the reason why one will lose their sense of direction and spatial awareness when they enter the Labyrinth Forest.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>No one is aware of the existence of the witch anymore, so Odin and his believers naturally claimed the credit for sealing away the Deviling, leaving the ordinary people ignorant of the witch's deeds as they continue on with their daily lives.\n",
    ["NpcStoryContent210041"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>What is the difference between a king and a god? A king can be the highest and most powerful being in a realm, but only after he has gained the reverence of the people can he be called a god.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Strouf was simply called the King of the Sea before he became the God of the Sea. He was the only king in the sea of Midgard and was known to be ruthless and tyrannical. Anyone who dared to blaspheme against him would be swept away by the sea's waters. Those who sailed or those who lived by the sea would tremble in fear whenever someone mentioned him. To them, he was the highest and most powerful being. They feared his power and prayed to him for peace.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Did they worship him? No they merely did it out of fear. The turning point was the battle against Baphomet.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Strouf was fiercely protective of his realm and would not allow anyone to invade his sea. Thus, he worked with Odin and forced Baphomet to fight on the land. The people who once feared him started to worship him after witnessing his valiant endeavors. The storms and lightning caused by Strouf were no longer a sign of disaster, but a symbol of peace and protection. And this was how Strouf became a bastion of might for the people.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>After the battle, to thank Strouf for his contributions, Odin granted divinity to him. After gaining both this status and his own worshippers, Strouf learned to keep his temper and treated every being in the sea as his own, protecting, loving, and fighting for them.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>And this was how the King of the Sea became the God of the Sea and a protector.",
    ["NpcStoryContent210051"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Would you believe me if I told you that Goblin civilization once dominated Midgard?\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>You must be thinking: \"Are you kidding me?\" Yes, that was how I felt as well until I saw those unbelievably intricate devices that Goblin Steamriders carry on their backs—then I realized the horrifying truth hidden behind them.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Legends say that the Goblin civilization thrived in ancient times. Their intelligence surpassed that of humans, and they were a technologically advanced society. It was an easy feat for them to conquer Midgard. The devices carried by Goblin Steamriders were probably only one of their inventions. Unfortunately, they chose the wrong side.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>They worshipped Baphomet.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>After the Final War, Odin naturally would not allow any race that worships a foreign god to rule the land. Thus, he unleashed his wrath on the goblins, stripping them of their intelligence and erasing their history. All this happened long before humans established the kingdom of Rune-Midgarts, so naturally, records of the Goblin civilization are not found in human history and only exist as legends and myths.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Today, the Goblins are common monsters found everywhere. Some Goblins who are exceptionally smart managed to learn how to speak simple human language and operate those jet devices left behind from ancient times, but in the end, they are just monsters. Baphomet is often known as the bane of humanity, but to the Goblins, humans are their bane.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>Now, the scary question: If humans chose the wrong chief god, would humans be in the place of the goblins today? Are we simply powerless pawns in Odin's game of chess?",
    ["NpcStoryContent220011"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>A windmill that is known as \"Knight's Bane\"? A strange tale, but interesting nonetheless!\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>This was the story of a knight named Don Qix. He sustained injuries from battle, so he retreated to a windmill, where he would wait for his wounds to heal. One day when he was having a stroll outside the windmill, it transformed into a gigantic monster. Being the brave knight he was, he charged at it fearlessly. His heroic act earned the favor of the god of war. After returning to the battlefield, he spearheaded many attacks but did not suffer any injuries until he retired.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>If you ask for my opinion about this story, I would say that it is all bullshit. I am pretty sure the truth is like this:\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>After Don Qix retired, he returned to the windmill to live out the rest of his days. However, the next day, a rotten log fell from the top of the windmill, hit his head and he never woke up again... What a sad ending. If the favor of the god of war truly existed, then Don Qix would have died on the battlefield instead...",
    ["NpcStoryContent220021"]="<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The Shipwreck is the remains of a pirate ship—many believe in this saying as it is home to fearsome monsters and bountiful treasures. Few have managed to escape from its attack, but those that do return with shocking items: gold coins from the pirate ship.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>The words engraved on the back of the coins translate to \"Honor to the Nerius Family\" The possibility of a pirate ship holding such a massive amount of wealth of the Nerius Family, one of the seven royal families, is beyond my imagination. Despite not being a family that is known for its martial prowess, the Nerius Family is a force not to be reckoned with, definitely out of the league for simple pirates.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>I specially made my way to Criatura Academy to check out the family scrolls of the seven royal families. Three hundred and twenty-five years ago, Colorful Nerius, the successor candidate for the Nerius Family, was the captain of the flagship of the most powerful fleet in the sea of Midgard. What was strange is that she did not become king and records about her fleet could not be found. It is as if they disappeared into thin air.\n<color=#FFFFFF00>1234</color>What exactly happened to her flagship, the Valkyrie?",
