    ["PetText_007"]="Success Rate: <color=#62b562>%0.1f%%</color>",
    ["PetText_008"]="Stats Required for Star Upgrade: %s/%s",
    ["PetText_009"]="Must reach %s Favor.",
    ["PetText_010"]="(Stats: %s)",
    ["PetText_011"]="%sStats:",
    ["PetText_012"]="Total Stats",
    ["PetText_013"]="You've pet this pet the maximum number of times today!",
    ["PetText_014"]="You've interacted with this pet the maximum number of times today!",
    ["PetText_015"]="You've reached the maximum number of total interactions today!",
    ["PetText_016"]="This pet is resting. They'll be able to fight once they've recovered their Stamina!",
    ["PetText_017"]="Grade: %s",
    ["PetText_018"]="The pet appearance system has not been unlocked. Coming soon!",
    ["PetText_019"]="This pet is in the deployment list. Cannot release.",
    ["PetText_020"]="This pet cannot evolve yet. Stay tuned!",
    ["PetText_021"]="This pet is already deployed. Cannot evolve.",
    ["PetText_022"]="Insufficient Favor. Cannot evolve.",
    ["PetText_023"]="Insufficient Pet Rank. Cannot evolve.",
    ["PetText_024"]="You can feed this pet <color=#ffad38>%s</color>/%s more time(s) today.",
    ["PetText_025"]="You've fed this pet the maximum number of times today!",
    ["PetText_026"]="You've reached the maximum number of total feedings today!",
    ["PetText_027"]="Pet already deployed. Cannot remove from lineup.",
    ["PetText_028"]="This pet hasn't reached the Rank needed to unlock this skill...",
    ["PetText_029"]="Pet Stats has reached the maximum.",
    ["PetText_030"]="Insufficient Favor. Cannot advance.",
    ["PetText_031"]="Evolve the pet %s to obtain.",
    ["PetText_032"]="Caught in the wild.",
    ["PetText_033"]="Use the item %s to obtain.",
    ["PetText_034"]="At least ONE pet must be kept after release.",
    ["PetText_035"]="Are you sure you want to release this adorable pet?",
    ["PetText_036"]="This pet's Favor is already at maximum. There's no need to keep interacting with them!",
    ["PetText_037"]="<color=#e7bb22>Pet Taming Tips</color>\n1. Taming a pet consumes the pet's Favorite Items.\n2. Equipping a Pet Slingshot allows you to inflict True damage equal to 30% HP of the monster on each normal attack.\n3. Only specified monsters can be tamed as pets.\n4. To tame a monster as a pet, your level must be higher than the monster's.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Stamina Tips</color>\n1. When a pet's Stamina is 0, you will not be able to deploy it.\n2. You can replenish a pet's Stamina by feeding it.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Favor Tips</color>\n1. Pet Favor = Pet Level.\n2. As a pet's Favor level increases, so will all of its attributes.\n3. Pet Favor can be increased by interacting with the pet and giving gifts.\n4. You can keep interacting with the pet by holding the Pat button on the interaction interface or the item icon.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Advancement Tips</color>\n1. Advancing a pet will increase its stats, which will increase its attributes.\n2. The stats must reach a certain value before a pet's Rank can be increased.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Evolution Tips</color>\n1. To be evolved, a pet must reach a certain Rank and Favor level with the required evolution materials. The success rate of pet evolution is guaranteed 100%.\n2. A pet's evolution materials include both items and costumes.\n3. A successfully evolved pet will become a stronger variant with increased rarity.\n4. The pet's quality might change when evolving (the change, if occurring, will be shown on the page).\n<color=#7ACEFF>5. A successfully evolved pet will not inherit its pre-evolution Favor level, stats, skills, and skill levels. Adventurers will need to re-train it.</color>\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Refining Tips</color>\n1. Adventurers can redistribute a pet's stats by refining it.\n2. Refining a pet will not change the total stats of the pet.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Deployment Tips</color>\n1. Pets must be on the Deployment List before being deployed onto the battlefield. You can only deploy 1 pet at a time.\n2. Pets will consume Stamina continuously while they're on the field. When Stamina reaches 0, they will be automatically called back.\n3. One point of Stamina will be deducted every 60 seconds. Stamina can be purchased in the shop.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Release Tips</color>\n1. After a pet is released, a proportion of consumed training materials will be returned to your Backpack.\n2. If there is only one pet remaining in the Pet Backpack, you won't be able to release it.\n3. The quantity of returned materials may vary according to the quality of the pet released.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Transfer Tips</color>\n1. Transferring pets requires the pets to have the same name but be of different quality.\n2. After transferring, the selected pets will switch their quality with each other (the inheritance ratio will be based on the current pet refining progress).",
    ["PetText_038"]="<color=#e7bb22>Pet Evolution</color>\n1. Evolution requirements include Rank, Favor level, and evolution materials. It is also dependent on success rate.\n2. A pet's evolution materials include both items and costumes. Successful evolution will consume all materials. Failed evolution will only consume the pet items; the costume will be returned.\n3. A successfully-evolved pet will become a stronger variant with increased rarity, and their Favor level will return to Lv.1.",
    ["PetText_039"]="Please enter a new pet nickname.",
    ["PetText_040"]="This pet's Rank is already at maximum. Cannot continue advancing.",
    ["PetText_041"]="This pet's Stamina is already full. There's no need to keep feeding them!",
    ["PetText_042"]="<color=#e7bb22>Catching Pets</color>\n1. Each type of pet has their own preferred item. Specific items are used to catch pets.\n2. Pet Slingshot Projectiles will decrease the pet's HP by a certain percentage. The lower a pet's HP, the greater your chances of successfully catching them.\n3. Green quality pets have a base capture rate of 5%, which can be increased up to 15%.",
    ["PetText_043"]="<color=#e7bb22>Catching Pets</color>\n1. Each type of pet has their own preferred item. Specific items are used to catch pets.\n2. Pet Slingshot Projectiles will decrease the pet's HP by a certain percentage. The lower a pet's HP, the greater your chances of successfully catching them.\n3. Blue quality pets have a base capture rate of 2.5%, which can be increased up to 7.5%.",
    ["PetText_044"]="Since you do not have a pet yet, you cannot open the pet feature.",
    ["PetText_045"]="Skin Details: %s",
    ["PetText_046"]="Spend the following times to unlock this pet’s skin?",
    ["PetText_047"]="Replaced!",
    ["PetText_048"]="Skin unlocked~",
    ["PetText_049"]="Normal",
    ["PetText_050"]="Good",
    ["PetText_051"]="Excellent",
    ["PetText_052"]="Outstanding",
    ["PetText_053"]="Epic",
    ["PetText_054"]="Legendary",
    ["PetText_055"]="Encyclopedia Level",
    ["PetText_056"]="Pet Encyclopedia",
    ["PetText_057"]="Taming EXP",
    ["PetText_058"]="+%s Stat",
    ["PetText_059"]="Pet transfer only works on <color=#F2AD18>pets with the same name</color>.\nOnly <color=#F2AD18>Stat Medals</color> are swapped after the transfer.",
    ["PetText_060"]="Level %s",
    ["PetText_061"]="Transfer",
    ["PetText_062"]="<size=18>Level</size> <size=26>%s</size>",
    ["PetText_063"]="Current Total Pet Stat: %s/%s",
    ["PetText_064"]="Quick Feed",
    ["PetText_065"]="The pet is currently in battle preparation. Unable to select.",
    ["PetText_066"]="<color=#e7bb22>Pet Taming Tips</color>\n1. Taming a pet consumes the pet's Favorite Items.\n2. Equipping a Pet Slingshot allows you to inflict 30%% fixed damage to the monster on each normal attack.\n3. Only the specified monster can be tamed as a pet.\n4. Taming pets can increase the the Taming Level.",
    ["PetText_067"]="Pet Quality\n1. Pet Quality includes three levels: B, A, and S\n2. A pet's quality is reflected in its stats. The higher the quality, the higher the stats bonus.\n White Rarity: B+0, A+12, S+24\n Purple Rarity: B+0, A+16, S+32\n Orange Rarity: B+0, A+24, S+48",
    ["PetText_068"]="Heartwarming Patting\n<color=#ff7e80>+%s</color>",
    ["PetText_069"]="Current Total Pet Stat %s+%s",
    ["PetText_070"]="This pet is on the deployment list. Cannot be selected.",
    ["PetText_071"]="The current pet has full stamina already! There's no need to keep feeding them!",
    ["PetText_072"]="Free patting attempts have reached today's maximum limit!",
    ["PetText_073"]="Insufficient Heartwarming Patting attempts. Unable to proceed.",
    ["PetText_074"]="Please select the pet you want to release.",
    ["PetText_075"]="Are you sure to release the selected pet?",
    ["PetTips_1"]="Pet stats transferred successfully. Sub pet successfully fused with main pet.",
    ["PetTips_10"]="This pet turns away shyly and does not allow you to check on it.",
    ["PetTips_11"]="Max Pet Taming Level",
    ["PetTips_12"]="Pet level reached master's level cap. Use again after increasing master's level.",
    ["PetTips_13"]="You only own one pet currently. Unable to release it or return it to the cage.",
    ["PetTips_14"]="Pet Stats Transfer Confirmation\nAfter transferring, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sub pet</color> will <color=#CA2E0AFF>disappear</color>.",
    ["PetTips_15"]="Learn Skill Confirmation\nLearning a skill may <color=#CA2E0AFF>overwrite</color> currently learned skills.",
    ["PetTips_16"]="Insufficient Stamina! Unable to catch pet!",
    ["PetTips_17"]="Pet backpack is full! Unable to catch pet!",
    ["PetTips_18"]="Pet cannot return to the cage when in a fatigued state.",
    ["PetTips_19"]="Unable to feed Favor food as pet is already at max Favor.",
    ["PetTips_2"]="<color=#e7bb22>Pet System Tips:</color>\n\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Tags:</color>\n1. There are melee/ranged and physical/magical pets.\n2. Melee pets, as the name says, excel in melee combat; caster pets need to learn spells.\n3. Pets have the same element they had when they were monsters.\n4. If the sum of the five stats of a pet is more than 225, it will be a Superior pet and can be returned to the cage.\n5. A pet can have the following natures:\nAggressive (actively attacks monsters)\nCalm (fights alongside its master)\nProtective (attacks monsters that attack its master)\n6. A pet can have the following affixes: \nTough - Max HP increases by 10%\nViolent - ATK increases by 10%\nSwift - DEF increases by 10%\nHoly - M.ATK increases by 10%\nShadow - M.DEF increases by 10%\nMerchant - Can run a shop \n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Intimacy:</color>\n1. A pet can only be deployed when it has 100 intimacy.\n2. There are five levels of Intimacy. Different Intimacy levels affect the pet's mood.\n3. Intimacy can be increased by feeding the pet or fighting alongside it.\n4. When a pet or its master dies, Intimacy will decrease.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Satiety:</color>\n1. There are five levels of Satiety.\n2. Satiety can be increased by feeding the pet.\n3. When a pet is hungry, its Intimacy will continuously decrease.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet EXP:</color>\n1. A pet gains EXP when fighting alongside its master and is affected by Odin's Blessing.\n2. You can grant a pet EXP by giving them Pet EXP Potions.\n3. A pet's level cannot be higher than its master's level\n<color=#e7bb22>Stats Transfer:</color>\n1. You can increase a pet's stats by transferring stats from another pet will the same name.\n2. After transferring, the sub pet will disappear.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Skill Learning:</color>\n1. A pet can learn from a Pet Book of the <color=#66ccff>corresponding element</color>.\n2. A pet can learn from a <color=#66ccff>General</color> Pet Book\n3. When learning, there is a chance that the skill will be learned in a <color=#66ccff>new skill slot</color>, or an existing skill will be <color=#66ccff>overwritten</color>.\n4. Pet books cannot be studied repeatedly.\n<color=#e7bb22>Pet Trading:</color>\n1. You can return a pet to the cage by tapping the relevant button in the pet interface.\nThe pet's <color=#66ccff>attributes</color> and <color=#66ccff>skills</color> will be unchanged.\n2. You can buy a cage using Diamonds.\n3. A pet returned to the cage will be auctioned at the Diamond Auction House.\n4. After getting a cage, tap on it to release the pet from it.\n5. If you only have one pet left, you cannot release it or return it to the cage.",
    ["PetTips_20"]="Only pets that have a sum of stats of more than 225 can be returned to the cage.",
