    ["PumpkinMechaUnlock"]="Use the item Pumpkin Genesis to unlock.",
    ["PunchHoleStateTips_1"]="<color=#ffffff>Normal Card Slot</color>",
    ["PunchHoleStateTips_2"]="<color=#ffd700>Elite Card Slot</color>",
    ["PunchHoleStateTips_3"]="<color=#ffa500>Embedded</color>",
    ["PunchHoleStateTips_4"]="<color=#f5f5f51>Socketed</color>",
    ["PunchHoleStateTips_5"]="<color=#a9a9a9>Unsocketed</color>",
    ["PunchHoleTips_1"]="Insufficient materials.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_10"]="Card slots that have been unlocked cannot be transferred through Equipment Stat Transfer, but opened slots of the original equipment can be retained by ascending. When socketed equipment is dismantled, the materials used for socketing will not be returned.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_2"]="Insufficient crystals.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_3"]="Successfully socketed.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_4"]="This equipment does not have any more sockets.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_5"]="This card slot is an elite card slot. Only elite cards can be inserted into it. Are you sure you want to put some sockets on it?",
    ["PunchHoleTips_6"]="When an equipment in a player’s backpack has a card slot that has not yet been unlocked, the player can socket the card slot of that equipment.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_7"]="There are two types of card slots for equipment: normal card slots and elite card slots. Most equipment has only normal card slots, and some equipment has both normal and elite card slots.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_8"]="The 2 card slots have different socketing costs. Elite Card Slots have a much higher cost than Normal Card Slots.",
    ["PunchHoleTips_9"]="Any card can be inserted into a socketed Normal Card Slot, but only cards that have Elite Card Desc can be inserted into Elite Cards Slots.",
    ["PurchaseTips"]="There is a problem with your account, and the payment feature has been temporarily restricted. Please recharge via the official website!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_1"]="%s/%s",
    ["PurgatoryTips_10"]="Use Soul Contract to perform a quick buyback?",
    ["PurgatoryTips_11"]="Current Soul Lost",
    ["PurgatoryTips_12"]="Not enough Soul Contracts!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_13"]="Soul Buyback successful!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_14"]="Quick Buyback successful!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_15"]="Buyback time: %s",
    ["PurgatoryTips_16"]="You are not buying back any equipment.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_17"]="<color=#edd2ff>%s</color> required to enter.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_18"]="Soul required: <color=#edd2ff>%s</color>",
    ["PurgatoryTips_19"]="Nightmare Mode Rules\n 1. Entering Nightmare difficulty costs Nightmare Marks.\n Nightmare Marks can be synthesized using fragments obtained from Normal and Hard instances every day.\n 2. Adventurers above Base Lv.50 who help other Adventurers 5 levels below them clear instances of any difficulty will also receive an Assist Chest.\n Opening an Assist Chest grants Nightmare Mark fragments.\n 3. Clearing Nightmare difficulty grants Ymir Crystals that can be used to unlock various features at Nightmare Merchants around the Heart Pedestal.\n 4. Adventurers that die in Nightmare Mode will not be revived using the skills of other Adventurers. They can be 100% revived by way of a teammate providing the Nightmare Leaf of Yggdrasil or by using a Resurrection Scroll.\n Normal revival will result in a chance of random equipment slots and their corresponding equipment stats being stripped. The lost equipment slots can be bought back using the Soul Buyback feature.\n 5. Leveling up the Soul Shop increases the chance of being exempt from resurrection penalties and decreases the buyback time for equipment slots.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_2"]="Resurrection limit reached.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_20"]="<color=#e7bb22>%s</color> does not have enough Nightmare Marks.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_21"]="You cannot use this skill in Nightmare Mode.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_22"]="<size=15>Weekly Reward chances: %s/%s</size>",
    ["PurgatoryTips_23"]="<color=#ff3300>%s</color> has been stripped of their <color=#ff3300>%s</color> slot!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_24"]="<color=#e7bb22>%s</color>'s level is not high enough.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_25"]="Requires <color=#FFFFFF>Lv.%s</color> to enter.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_26"]="Unlock Nightmare Shop II for more items.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_27"]="Unlock Nightmare Shop III for more items.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_28"]="Unlock Nightmare Shop IV for more items and the refresh items feature.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_29"]="Level Up Shop",
    ["PurgatoryTips_3"]="Time to resurrection: %ss",
    ["PurgatoryTips_30"]="Not enough Ymir Crystal.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_31"]="Unable to use items!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_32"]="Your <color=#ff3300>%s</color> slot has been bought back!",
    ["PurgatoryTips_33"]="You have been stripped of <color=#ff3300>%s</color> equipment slots. Equipment in the stripped equipment slots will have no effect! Stripped equipment slots can be bought back from Nightmare Merchants.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_34"]="Not enough <color=#d14d75>Nightmare Leaf of Yggdrasil</color>.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_4"]="Not enough Resurrection Scrolls.",
    ["PurgatoryTips_5"]="Strip immunity chance: <color=#D63BC4FF>%s%%</color>",
