    ["SeasonInstanceTips003"]="No rewards will be granted unless submitting the Blazing Rune.",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips004"]="Activation Time Ended",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips005"]="1. After the instance performance is settled, tap the Frenzy Firestone that appears in the scene, submitting Blazing Runes to activate the Boss.",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips006"]="2. Adventurers who fail to submit their Blazing Rune will not receive corresponding rewards.",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips007"]="3. Deal as much damage as possible to the Boss within 3 minutes to increase your party rating.",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips008"]="4. The rating will be calculated based on your Party's overall damage and deaths.",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips009"]="Rating",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips010"]="Party Damage (Higher Than)",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips011"]="Deaths (Lower Than)",
    ["SeasonInstanceTips012"]="Fire Boulder Fragment",
    ["SeasonInstance_Des"]="Imprisoned offerings, seeking to awaken the Demon Lord within the forbidden realm...\nThe chance of making it out alone is slim; have faith in your allies and overcome the darkness together!",
    ["SeasonInstance_Help"]="Oblivion Realm Explanation:\n1. Oblivion Realm is accessible during the entire season, with various difficulties for Adventurers to participate in a party.\n2. There's a weekly limit on how many times clearance rewards can be claimed. The limit will be reset on every Monday.\n3. For this season, the occurrence rate of Prophet and Judgement monster affixes has been boosted.",
    ["SeasonLabelHelp"]="New season, new generation. Certain affixes will have a bigger chance of appearing during the season.\nThe featured affixes for this season are <color=#5096B7>Ark</color> and <color=#3B6389>Revelation</color>, which appear 3 times as much as the rest of the affixes.\nAdventurers can activate sets by switching the Divinities, allowing them to more effectively counter monster affix effects.",
