    ["SeasonTaskTips_01"]="Current Week: %s/%s",
    ["SeasonTaskTips_02"]="Instance Points: <color=#de8b40>%s</color>/%s",
    ["SeasonTaskTips_03"]="Arena Points: <color=#de8b40>%s</color>/%s",
    ["SeasonTaskTips_04"]="1. There are weekly, monthly, and seasonal quests in the Instance Odyssey.\n2. Completing quests will earn you Instance Points.\n3. There's a cap on Instance Points for weekly quests, and you can earn rewards once you hit the objective in each phase.\n4. Challenge quests are tricky, but completing them gets you tons of rewards.\n5. Weekly quests refresh at 05:00 every Monday, monthly tasks reset on the 1st of each month at 05:00, and seasonal quests stay as they are.\n6. Once you reach the required Instance Tier, you can claim double rewards (Arena and Instance).",
    ["SeasonTaskTips_05"]="1. There are weekly, monthly, and seasonal quests in the Apex Arena.\n2. Completing quests will earn you Arena Points.\n3. There's a cap on Arena Points for weekly quests, and you can earn rewards once you hit the objective in each phase.\n4. Challenge quests are tricky, but completing them gets you tons of rewards.\n5. Weekly quests refresh at 05:00 every Monday, monthly tasks reset on the 1st of each month at 05:00, and seasonal quests stay as they are.\n6. Once you reach the required Arena Tier, you can claim double rewards (Arena and Instance).",
    ["SeasonTaskTips_06"]="Arena Points obtained from leaderboard mail: %s",
    ["SeasonTask_Cycle_text"]="Complete %s time(s).",
    ["SeasonTask_Help"]="Season Quest Explanation:\n1. A new set of weekly season quests will become available every Monday.\n2. Added repeatable quests to the season quests, which you can complete multiple times to obtain rewards.\n3. A repeatable quest marked as \"Ended\" means this quest cannot be completed anymore.\n4. To obtain the weekly reward, Adventurers only need to complete a specified number of quests for the current week. Completing the repeatable quest once counts as completion of the quest.\n5. Complete the season quests to obtain season points, increase your season level, and win season-exclusive rewards.",
    ["SeasonTask_Level_exp"]="Season Points: %s/<color=#8484b7>%s</color>",
    ["SeasonTask_Lock_text"]="LOCK",
    ["SeasonTask_Reward_lock"]="Claimable after finishing the specified number of season quests in the current week",
    ["SeasonTask_Week1_text"]="ST WEEK",
    ["SeasonTask_Week2_text"]="ND WEEK",
    ["SeasonTask_Week3_text"]="RD WEEK",
    ["SeasonTask_Week4_text"]="TH WEEK",
    ["SeasonTask_WeekReward"]="Complete this week's quest to claim <color=#fbe26d>%s/%s</color>",
    ["SeasonTask_Week_lock"]="<color=#5e606d><size=24>%s</size></color><color=#5e606d><size=16>%s</size></color>",
    ["SeasonTask_Week_open"]="<color=#434561><size=24>%s</size></color><color=#434561><size=16>%s</size></color>",
    ["SeasonTask_Week_progress"]="<color=%s>%s / %s</color>",
    ["SeasonTeamBattle_Daily"]="Participate in %s matches in any mode of any gameplay today",
    ["SeasonTeamBattle_DailyTask"]="Complete 1 Infinite Showdown match of any mode every day",
    ["SeasonTeamBattle_Help"]="Infinite Showdown Explanation:\n1. Reach the specific tier in Infinite Showdown within the season to receive rewards.\n2. Season points are awarded by participating in Infinite Showdown ranked matches of any mode during the season, with more points for wins and a weekly reset of the point acquisition limit every Monday.\n3. Complete a match in any mode of Infinite Showdown (normal or ranked) every day to earn quest rewards, with new missions available daily.",
    ["SeasonTeamBattle_Level"]="Reach tier %s in Infinite Showdown during the season",
    ["SeasonTest_001"]="The current quest has yet to reach the unlocking time",
    ["SeasonTitle_Name"]="S9",
    ["SeasonTitle_Time"]="Season Time: %s (Exchange Duration: %s)",
    ["SeasonTowerInfiniteEndTips"]="Realm closing in 1 minute",
    ["SeasonTowerListNumberTips1"]="This week's remaining leaderboard attempts",
    ["SeasonTowerListNumberTips2"]="This week's remaining leaderboard attempts\nCurrently in a fixed party. No leaderboard attempts will be consumed.",
    ["SeasonTowerTips_1"]="Challenge Time\n1. Every day from 01:00 to 05:00 is the break period; Oblivion Realm is inaccessible during this time.\nUnlock Description\n1. Reach 3 stars to unlock the next difficulty.\n2. When partying up, the leader's difficulty unlocking progress is shared across the party.\n3. If a party earns a 3-star rating in a cross-difficulty challenge, all members will unlock all difficulties that were locked previously.\nReward Description\n1. Rewards can be claimed once per week at most.\n2. Upon Oblivion Realm settlement, you may either claim the reward or skip it. Skipping a reward doesn't consume your chance of claiming rewards.\n3. The reward tier is determined by the total stars earned from each floor of the challenge.\n4. The rating is determined by the party's clear time and death count.\n5. All premium rewards are dropped by chance, with higher difficulties offering better odds.\n6. No regular rewards for Infinite Mode.\nFloor Rating Standards Description\n- 1 Star: Clear the stage in no more than 300 seconds.\n- 2 Stars: Clear the stage in no more than 180 seconds.\n- 3 Stars: Clear the stage in no more than 180 seconds and also fulfill:\nDifficulty 1-3: No more than 10 deaths.\nDifficulty 4-7: No more than 6 deaths.\nDifficulty 8-10: No more than 3 deaths.\nLeaderboard Record Attempt Description This Week's Leaderboard Record Attempts: <color=#528fff>%s</color>/%s\n1. Each week, Adventurers have five attempts to record their Oblivion Realm's clearing scores (Infinite Mode) on the leaderboard. Recording scores from other modes won't use up these attempts.\n2. If all party members have remaining leaderboard record attempts, an attempt is used automatically upon entering Oblivion Realm, and the score is recorded after defeating any boss of any floor.\n3. If any party member runs out of leaderboard record attempts, the score won't be recorded, and no rewards are given. In this case, it won't consume the other party members' leader record attempts.\n4. If a party member quits Oblivion Realm midway and the remaining party members defeat any boss of any floor, the quitter's score won't be recorded, and their leaderboard record attempt won't be refunded.\n5. If a record attempt is used in a party, the party is fixed and stays that way as long as no members change. Any member leaving, joining, or the party disbanding will render the fixed status invalid.\n6. Entering Oblivion Realm with a fixed party does not consume leaderboard record attempts.\n7. Solo Adventurers cannot trigger the fixed party effect.\nReset Description\n1. The leaderboard resets every Monday during the Oblivion Realm period, retaining the unlocked difficulty progress.\n2. Upon reset, all leaderboard ranking records and record attempts are reset, and rewards are distributed based on the rankings.\n3. Upon reset, all boss affixes across difficulties will be randomized.\nInfinite Mode\n1. Reach 3 stars in Difficulty 10 to unlock Infinite Mode.\n2. No retries in Infinite Mode. Once you fail, you will enter the result screen.\n3. Each Adventurer gets two revives per floor in Infinite Mode. Once used up, you can't revive anymore. This applies to both natural and skill-based revives.\n4. Infinite Mode has a 15-minute time limit. Once reached, the challenge is terminated, and results are calculated.\n5. If the entire party is wiped in Infinite Mode, the challenge is considered a failure regardless of any remaining revives.",
    ["SeasonTowerTips_2"]="◆ Settlement Time: Every Monday at 05:00\n◆ Leaderboard Rewards: If the Adventurers' results are the same, the rewards of the highest ranking are granted regardless of the Adventurers' rankings.\n◆ Leaderboard rewards will be sent via mail.",
    ["SeasonTowerTips_3"]="This Week's Affixes",
    ["Season_ActityType_1001"]="Day",
