    ["SlimeUI_Adventure1"]="Start Big Adventure",
    ["SlimeUI_Adventure2"]="Complete Story Now",
    ["SlimeUI_Adventure3"]="Big Adventure completed in total: %s",
    ["SlimeUI_AdventureDes"]="<color=#4099ff>Rimuru's Big Adventure Rules:</color>\n\nRoll the Dice to move Rimuru forward.\nThe Dice can be obtained through <color=#4099ff>Town Request</color>, purchases at <color=#4099ff>Dice Shop</color> or other events. Using a <color=#4099ff>Remote Control Dice</color> allows you to roll any number you want.\n\nEvents will be triggered when Rimuru arrives at specific tiles:\n<color=#4099ff>Chest:</color> Receive a random number of exchange store tokens.\n<color=#4099ff>Minigame:</color>Receive a corresponding number of exchange store tokens based on the minigame rating.\n<color=#4099ff>Encounter:</color>Receive a different number of exchange store tokens and Adventure EXP based on the level of the encounter. There is a small chance of getting the Faded Jigsaw Puzzle and Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle in advanced encounters.\n<color=#4099ff>Teleport:</color> Send Rimuru to the nearby teleport destination—Swoosh!\n<color=#4099ff>Advance:</color> Move forward automatically based on the number shown on the dice.\n<color=#4099ff>Hot Spring:</color> Map events will be refreshed when Rimuru returns and rests at the hot spring after a round.\n<color=#4099ff>Some other strange locations:</color> Strange things will happen when they are stepped on. Try it out!\n\nAuto mode is always an option for Adventurers to guide Rimuru, which is further divided into <color=#4099ff>Auto</color> and <color=#4099ff>Semi-auto</color>.\nIn <color=#4099ff>Auto mode</color>, all events, including Minigames, are automatically completed, granting the minimum rewards for a 1-Star rating, while in <color=#4099ff>Semi-auto mode</color>, Minigames triggered require manual operations, and Adventurers shall be fully rewarded for their performance!\n\nRemember, only <color=#4099ff>Normal Dice</color> can be used in auto mode. And Dice will be consumed in all modes. Do keep an eye on the remaining dice you have!",
    ["SlimeUI_BP1"]="Upgrade to Claim",
    ["SlimeUI_BP2"]="Activate Pass",
    ["SlimeUI_BP3"]="Spend %s Diamonds to activate Holy Knight Pass?",
    ["SlimeUI_BP4"]="%s Activated",
    ["SlimeUI_BP5"]="Activated",
    ["SlimeUI_BP6"]="Adventure Lv.%s",
    ["SlimeUI_BP7"]="EXP %s/%s",
    ["SlimeUI_BP8"]="Claimed",
    ["SlimeUI_BP9"]="Claimable",
    ["SlimeUI_BPDes"]="About <color=#7c73d5>Attack on Holy Knight</color>\n\n1. The Holy Knight Pass contains two types of rewards: free rewards can be claimed directly after leveling up, and paid rewards can only be claimed after activating and upgrading the Pass.\n\n2. Upon reaching Adventure Level 70, rewards cycles will get unlocked. Adventurers can then repeatedly claim rewards by increasing their EXP.\n\n3. When purchasing Adventure Levels, only the unlocked part can be purchased each time. The rest can be unlocked and purchased once the Adventurer reaches the corresponding Adventure Levels.\n\n4. To increase Adventure Level, Adventure EXP can be obtained by killing MVP & MINI, participating in Rimuru's Big Adventure, etc.\n\n5. When Odin's Blessing is activated, killing a monster within 6 levels above or below your Base Level grants you a chance to obtain Adventure EXP. Up to 650 Adventure EXP can be obtained in this mode every day, and the limit will be reset daily at 5:00 local time.",
    ["SlimeUI_CampRec1"]="Recommended by the Great Sage: Tokens can be traded at a good price in Exchange Center.",
    ["SlimeUI_CampRec2"]="Recommended by Great Sage: A conclusion made after some tedious calculation.",
    ["SlimeUI_CampSel1"]="Selected Dragonewt to strengthen the bond.",
    ["SlimeUI_CampSel2"]="Selected Kijin to strengthen the bond.",
    ["SlimeUI_CampSel3"]="Selected Orc to strengthen the bond.",
    ["SlimeUI_Cooking1"]="Current Progress: %s",
    ["SlimeUI_CookingDes"]="About <color=#a274bf>Shion's Delicacies</color>\n\nWhen Odin's Blessing is activated, killing a monster that is within 6 levels below your Base Level grants you a chance to obtain the ingredients required by Shion's Delicacies.\n\nDaily Acquisition Limit:\nColorful Mushroom — 70\nThorny Vegetable — 35\nWriggling Meat Chunk — 14\nBitter Honey — 7\nThe limit will be reset daily at 5:00 local time.\n\nFind enough ingredients and submit them to Shion to cook the delicacies. Rewards can be claimed from Shion after finishing each of her delicacies.",
    ["SlimeUI_Daliy1"]="Daily requests refresh at 5:00 every day",
    ["SlimeUI_Puzzle1"]="Spend %s %s to unlock",
    ["SlimeUI_Puzzle2"]="Unlocking Progress: %s",
    ["SlimeUI_PuzzleDes"]="About <color=#5E87EF>Wonderland Jigsaw Puzzle</color>\n\n1. The following items can be obtained from Rimuru's Big Adventure, Shion's Delicacies, and Town Request: Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle and Faded Jigsaw Puzzle.\n\n2. The puzzle needs to be unlocked in a specific order. Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle will be <color=#5E87EF>consumed first</color> by default. When there is not enough Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle, Faded Jigsaw Puzzle will be used automatically. (Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle x1 = Faded Jigsaw Puzzle x99)\n\n3. The mount: Veldora, the Storm Dragon\ncan be obtained when the last piece of the puzzle is completed. (Its unlocking progress will be displayed on the interface in real time.)\n\n4. When the gameplay is completed, the remaining pieces of Artistic Jigsaw Puzzle and Faded Jigsaw Puzzle can be used in <color=#5E87EF>Tempest Market</color> to exchange for other rewards.",
    ["SlineUI_Main1"]="Event Time: %s",
    ["SlineUI_Main2"]="Exchange Deadline: %s",
    ["SlingShotNoPellet"]="No pet slingshot ammo available currently. Please replenish at the Pet Merchant.",
    ["SlotName_1"]="Main-hand",
    ["SlotName_10"]="Mouth",
    ["SlotName_11"]="Back",
    ["SlotName_12"]="Tail",
    ["SlotName_13"]="Outfit",
    ["SlotName_14"]="Talisman",
    ["SlotName_15"]="Secret Shop",
    ["SlotName_16"]="Magic Shop",
    ["SlotName_2"]="Off-hand",
    ["SlotName_3"]="Two-handed",
