    ["SongkranFestivalTask_013"]="Win Water Gun Battle %s/%s times",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_001"]="%s Odin's Blessings can be claimed daily during the event!",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_002"]="Your party needs three members.",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_003"]="Not a Water Gun Battle team.",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_004"]="Event Time: %s",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_005"]="Exchange Period: %s",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_006"]="Not listed",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_007"]="No Adventurers listed",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_008"]="Landmark Tour\n 1. Complete quests to obtain Fuel, advance your Travel Progress, and get rewards from various attractions.\n 2. Rewards for each attraction can only be obtained once and cannot be claimed again.\n 3. Quests are divided into daily quests and cumulative quests. Daily quests are refreshed at 05:00 AM every day, while cumulative quests will accumulate your current progress for each completed quest until the next stage. Unclaimed rewards cannot be recovered after quests are refreshed, so Adventurers should remember to claim their rewards in time.\n 4. Rewards not claimed after the event will be sent to the mailbox and are valid for 30 days.",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_009"]="Water Gun Battle\n 1. During the event, players can form a party or use matchmaking to join a party. The Water Gun Battle is a 3v3 PVP mode, with each match lasting for 3 minutes.\n 2. In this mode, each Adventurer is equipped with a Water Cannon, and Normal Attack is replaced by Water Shell. The water cannon can shoot a water shell in a specific direction, inflicting Soak on the first enemy unit hit. If the opponent is already in the water ball, they will not be affected.\n 3. After an Adventurer is fully soaked, they will be trapped in a water bubble and unable to attack or move, with the Soak inflicted on them cleared. Other party members can rescue the Adventurer by moving to their side and tapping the Rescue button. The rescue process takes time, and the rescuer cannot use skills while performing it. Any movement by the rescuer will cancel the rescue. After being rescued, the Adventurer will regain the ability to attack and move.\n 4. Adventurers can eliminate opponents by popping their water bubbles. Adventurers trapped inside a water ball for too long without being rescued will also be eliminated.\n 5. The sand wall can partially block attacks and adventurer movement. After receiving a certain number of attacks, the sand wall will disappear.\n 6. Adventurers can obtain items during pre-game preparation or via in-game supply points. Each item allows an Adventurer to wield a powerful skill!\n Lifebuoy: Can escape from a water bubble or resist three attacks within a certain time. Can not be used repeatedly during a short period of time.\n Super Water Balloon: Selects an area that will inflict Soak on all enemies within a large range after a brief delay.\n Pressure Boost Valve: Reduces water shell's cooldown for a period of time.\n Water Balloon: Selects an area to inflict Soak on all enemies in a small range after a period of time.\n Energy Drink: Increases MSPD for a period of time and continuously reduces Soak.\n 7. Winning the Water Gun Battle grants you powerful item rewards. Your first win of the day grants extra Clear Water and two random bonus drops: Seafood Onigiri x12 (50% chance) or Tropical Salad x6 (50% chance).",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_010"]="Party Star\n1. Adventurers will be ranked according to how much Clear Water they obtain during the event period. Rankings will be finalized after the event ends. Rewards will be sent via mail and are valid for 30 days.\n2. Clear Water can be obtained via event quests and Street Party Blessing Packs redeemed from the Graffiti Store.\n3. Clear Water obtained after the event ends will no longer apply to rankings. Please remember to claim your rewards and use Street Party Blessing Packs in time!",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_011"]="Odin's Blessing\n 1. You can collect 1 Odin's Blessing reward per day here during the event period, which will be refreshed at 05:00 AM each day.\n 2. Claiming attempts and the total number of Odin's Blessings are non-cumulative. Please remember to claim them every day!\n 3. During the event period, spend Odin's Blessings and kill monsters to redeem items and earn a chance to get rare Mystic Water, which can be used in the Graffiti Store to redeem special rewards.",
    ["SongkranFestivalText_012"]="Graffiti Store\n 1. Use event exchange items here for costumes, mounts, and items.\n 2. Every redeemable item has a limit; once you reach it, you can no longer exchange for that item.\n 3. Check the reminder box to receive a notification when you can redeem an item.\n 4. Any unused exchange items will be reclaimed after the event ends.",
