    ["TargetName_ultraman"]="Monster Invasion",
    ["TargetNoRequestSkillTip01"]="The player has not learned <color=#44afee>Ensemble Invitation</color>.",
    ["TargetNoRequestSkillTip02"]="A <color=#44afee>party</color> member who has learned <color=#44afee>Ensemble Invitation</color> must be selected.",
    ["TargetOutOfRange"]="Target is too far away.",
    ["TaskAbandon1"]="Abandoning this quest (<color=#f6723e><%s></color>) will reset all progress. \nAbandon quest?",
    ["TaskAbandon2"]="Abandoned quest (<color=#f6723e><%s></color>).",
    ["TaskAccept"]="Talk to <color=#f6723e>%s</color>.",
    ["TaskAccept1_1"]="Go to <color=#f6723e>%s</color> and talk to <color=#f6723e>%s</color>.",
    ["TaskAccept2"]="Accept quest (<color=#f6723e>%s</color>).",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition1"]="Job advancement after completing quest (<color=#891106><%s></color>).",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition2"]="Quest continues after reaching Base Lv.<color=#f6723e>%d</color>. You can use <color=#f6723e>Odin's Blessing</color> to level up while AFK.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition2_Lv15"]="Quest continues after reaching Base Lv.<color=#f6723e>15</color>. You can level up by completing <color=#f6723e>Tutorial Quests</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition2_Lv24"]="Quest continues after reaching Base Lv.<color=#f6723e>24</color>. You can level up by completing <color=#f6724e>Mission Board Quests</color> in the <color=#f6724e>Carnival event</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition3"]="Quest continues after <color=#f6723e>job advancement</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition4"]="Quest continues after obtaining <color=#f6723e>%s</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition5"]="Quest continues after equipping <color=#f6723e>%s</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition6"]="Job Advancement Quest unlocks after reaching Job Lv.<color=#891106>%d</color>.",
    ["TaskAcceptCondition7"]="Please stay tuned for future versions.",
    ["TaskDescription1"]="Test Quest Description",
    ["TaskDescription10000"]="1st Job Advancement",
    ["TaskDescription100001101"]="As a novice arriving at the Central Fountain of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>, you can't help but feel a little lost in this vast world. At this moment, an enthusiastic voice suddenly calls out...",
    ["TaskDescription100001102"]="It turns out, it's Kiki, the novice recruiter of the Criatura Academy, calling to you. Her enthusiasm is something else...\nAfter registering you, Kiki asks you to place your hand on a copy of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy Adventurer Log</color> next to her. \"Remember to do it lightly, or else something horrible will happen!\"",
    ["TaskDescription100001103"]="You successfully obtain the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Academy Handbook</color>, and Kiki's facilitation duties are finally over. But she looks like she still has something to say. Why not ask what's on her mind?",
    ["TaskDescription100001104"]="Kiki tells you that she loves Prontera's beautiful <color=#CA2E0AFF>fountain</color>. Let's use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>camera</color> to capture this moment for her!",
    ["TaskDescription100001105"]="The good news is that Kiki loves the photos you took of her! The bad news is that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jarod</color>, the new student instructor sent by the academy, has sneaked off to avoid work... Looks like Kiki needs me to bring him back. I've heard that Jarod frequents the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>, so let's seek him out there first!",
    ["TaskDescription100001106"]="You find Jarod, who confidently wants to show off his social skills to you. Since he's so adamant about it, go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>watch</color> him do his thing...",
    ["TaskDescription100001107"]="Sure enough, Jarod is rejected by Isabella, the tavern owner's wife. The humiliated and upset Jarod makes a deal with you that he'll meet any of your demands if you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>make a new friend</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100001108"]="You successfully make a new friend, and Jarod has finally agreed to go back with you to see Kiki. But it's already getting late. Kiki could be getting anxious.",
    ["TaskDescription100001109"]="Kiki tells you that you need to head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> next, but the girl she mentioned named Ygnizem... Where could she be?",
    ["TaskDescription100001110"]="You finally find the missing academy student, Ygnizem, only to see her being chased by a group of Porings... In the process of helping Ygnizem, you learn that King Poring is very angry about something. I wonder what happened... Why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Ygnizem about it</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100001111"]="You learn from Ygnizem that she lost <color=#CA2E0AFF>Angeling's Halo</color> due to her impulsive behavior. Seeing how anxious she is, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay with her and search for the halo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100001112"]="You clearly remember that the halo was taken by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>crow</color>, so you follow its trail all the way to a <color=#CA2E0AFF>cliff</color> where it's probably hiding. But how do you get up there?",
    ["TaskDescription100001113"]="You manage to find the halo on the cliff, but since Ygnizem is too embarrassed to face the Angeling, you decide to return it to the original owner for her. You hear that the Angeling is near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poring Ruins</color> at the South Gate, so it seems a trip is in order!",
    ["TaskDescription100001114"]="The halo has finally been returned to its rightful owner, and the Angeling is very happy! Hearing that you need to get back to the Amusement Park as soon as possible, the Angeling decides to lend you its mount. So <color=#CA2E0AFF>get on this Big Poring</color> and return to Kiki!",
    ["TaskDescription100001115"]="You are met with great news at the Amusement Park: You passed the Criatura Academy Novice Trial! It turns out that Kiki's assessment of you actually began the moment you met her! Now as an official student, you can receive your very own <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy Hat</color> from Smile Assistance. So what are you waiting for? Go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smile Assistance</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100001116"]="You didn't expect her run out of materials for making the academy hat... What bad luck! You spend a long time gathering all the missing materials. Now go give them to Smile Assistance!",
    ["TaskDescription100001117"]="You finally got your own academy hat! Now follow Kiki's directions and take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate Express</color> to the port!",
    ["TaskDescription100001118"]="The huge ship moored at the harbor must be bound for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Izlude Island!</color> Wait a second. That looks like Ygnizem's back amongst the crowd... Why don't you go say hi to her before you board the ship?",
    ["TaskDescription100001119"]="After a long voyage, you finally arrive at Izlude Island, a satellite city located southeast of Prontera. Before you report to the academy, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go say goodbye to Captain Carew</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100001120"]="Ygnizem has left with Jarod. For the rest of the trip, Kiki will be your dedicated recruiter, and will give you a comprehensive tour around the island. How exciting!",
    ["TaskDescription100001121"]="When you arrive at Criatura Academy, you should, of course, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Hall of Job Advancement</color> first and meet the famous <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color>, who is one of the world's few Great Sages. He may be able to teach you something unique!",
    ["TaskDescription100001122"]="Dean Mainz channels the power of Criatura Academy adventurers through the ages into you. For a brief time, you will <color=#CA2E0AFF>experience the profound power of each job class</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100001123"]="Dean Mainz seems think very highly of you! After completing the job advancement ceremony, pick up your <color=#CA2E0AFF>1st Class Certificate</color> from him.",
    ["TaskDescription100001124"]="Dean Mainz asks you to take a close look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color> behind him. What importance does it hold?",
    ["TaskDescription100001125"]="So it turns out that the Heart Pedestal is a divine artifact, and one of the most important reasons for its existence is to hold the legendary <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragments of Ymir's Heart</color>. Follow Dean Mainz instructions, and go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to learn more about the story of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir's Heart</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100001126"]="While you are busy researching, Kiki appears out of nowhere and tells you that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>academy assembly</color> is about to begin. There's no time to lose. Quickly follow her to the academy assembly!",
    ["TaskDescription100001127"]="You follow Kiki's directions and check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> on Izlude Island. There you discover something awful...",
    ["TaskDescription100001128"]="Turns out the Mission Board is badly damaged! The Mission Board Guard is so anxious about this that he asks you to look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Old Clay</color>, the carpenter of Izlude Island. But Old Clay is... well, old. Will he be able to repair the Mission Board?",
    ["TaskDescription100001129"]="Although the Mission Board has been repaired, the Mission Board Guard's mood hasn't seemed to get any better... Seeing his sad face, you have a feeling it isn't that simple...",
    ["TaskDescription100001130"]="At the end of the trial, you have chosen your own path to becoming stronger! Go and tell Dean Mainz about your decision.",
    ["TaskDescription100001131"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001132"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E1AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001133"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E2AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001134"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E3AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001135"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E4AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001136"]="Dean Mainz suggests that you take more in-depth lessons from the <color=#CA2E5AFF>Instructors</color>, each of whom are experts in their respective fields. You're sure to gain new insights from your discussions!",
    ["TaskDescription100001137"]="After you complete your first job course, Kiki asks you to go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> to meet Dean Mainz. You wonder what he'll say when he sees how much you've grown.",
    ["TaskDescription100001138"]="Experience the secrets of each class in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trial</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100002101"]="While completing many quests, you've gained experience and grown a lot! Remember when Kiki told you that the Kingdom Defense Force posts the <color=#CA2E0AFF>King's Decrees</color> on the Mission Board? Why don't you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mission Board</color> and check it out now?",
    ["TaskDescription100002102"]="Joining the Kingdom Defense Force is a dream come true for many adventurers. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>lower section of the airship</color> and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color>, the Court Clerk of the Defense Force, to figure out how to join!",
    ["TaskDescription100002103"]="You follow Akand's instructions and meet your squad captain, Fitz, on the airship. He looks like a man you don't want to mess with... You wonder what you're going to experience on this airship next.",
    ["TaskDescription100002104"]="To your surprise, Captain Fitz makes you perform a parachute jump to test your courage! Even more alarming is that your parachute malfunctioned, allowing a strong wind to blow you off course. You end up landing in front of a young lady, frightening her. Let's calm her down.",
    ["TaskDescription100002105"]="Turns out this young woman is a service employee of the Kafra Corporation. She informs you that a few other parachuters landed far away in the direction of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color>... Oh no! You almost forgot about Captain Fitz's orders! He mentioned meeting up at the Central Fountain in Prontera! Why don't you head over there now and look around?",
    ["TaskDescription100002106"]="Seeing your late arrival, Akand tells you that Captain Fitz had already left with the rest of the reservists... He hands the last set of the military supplies to you... Follow his instructions and take these Basic Upgrading Stones to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blacksmith Hollgrehenn</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100002107"]="You anxiously head to Prontera West Gate to meet up with the First Squad of the Defense Force... You're sure Captain Fitz's quite upset right now.",
    ["TaskDescription100002108"]="Upon just finishing the trial, you suddenly hear a cry for help. Rushing forward to check it out, you find a Defense Force reservist being attacked by a mutated monster... This is very unusual. Ask the reservist about what happened.",
    ["TaskDescription100002109"]="Reservist Yohan states that he saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> on the tower stairs that may have something to do with the monster's mutation. You decide to bring it back to show <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Fitz</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100002110"]="Captain Fitz is worried about the other reservists, so he decides for you and him to split up and make sure everyone is safe. Hurry and check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery nearby</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100002111"]="Reservist Marc says that he saw a <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color>... Could it be the same device?... Let's go check it out!",
    ["TaskDescription100002112"]="Captain Fitz doesn't seem to know the origins of the device either... Let's just follow his instructions and bring the device to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Court Clerk Akand</color> to see if he can discover anything new.",
    ["TaskDescription100002113"]="Akand suggests getting help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lawrence, a scholar at the Library</color>, to investigate the device. With his help, you discover the great secret hidden in the Alchemy Device...",
    ["TaskDescription100002114"]="To your surprise, the alchemy stone is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>copy of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>! This must be reported to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> immediately! You wonder how he'll react to this.",
    ["TaskDescription100002115"]="Akand asks you to head for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for the Captain Simmons of the Second Squad</color>. See if similar incidents has occurred where he is.",
    ["TaskDescription100002116"]="The trial for the Second Squad of the Defense Force is at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Farm</color>. Go there and make sure that everyone's safe!",
    ["TaskDescription100002117"]="Sure enough, the Second Squad of the Defense Force encountered unusual events too! After saving Zach from assassins, he entrusts you with taking the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange device</color> he found to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Simmons</color>. Don't forget to show <color=#CA2E0AFF>the letter</color> either. Things are getting really weird. It's hard to believe it's all a coincidence...",
    ["TaskDescription100002118"]="It's an emergency! Quickly report to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> what you saw at Green Cotton Farm!",
    ["TaskDescription100002119"]="In order to find where the remaining Alchemy Devices are hidden, you'll have to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> mentioned in the letter to get information. The person who hired the assassins is bound to turn up there, so go and check it out!",
    ["TaskDescription100002120"]="You eavesdrop on a conversation between two suspicious men and determine that one of them is the assassin-for-hire you're looking for. But he's very wary... Do you have any tricks to get him to talk?",
    ["TaskDescription100002121"]="After some effort, you finally obtain the tavern owner Isabella's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Truth Liquor</color>. Try giving it to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>suspicious man</color>! Hope he provides useful information!",
    ["TaskDescription100002122"]="Hurry and tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> the information you heard in the tavern. Wonder what he'll plan to do next?",
    ["TaskDescription100002123"]="While searching for the Alchemy Device at the cathedral's cemetery, you meet a little boy who seems to have hidden it. He won't tell you where it is, and instead, offers to trade <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica's Picture</color> for it, so it looks like you'll have to do what he says first!",
    ["TaskDescription100002124"]="You finally get your hands on the fourth Alchemy Device and wonder if <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akand</color> has managed to find the last one. Let's return and ask him!",
    ["TaskDescription100002125"]="You didn't expect Akande's search to be obstructed by the Royal Chivalry! Seeking support, you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>square in front of the palace</color> to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bernard</color>, Commander of the Kingdom Defense Force, who is shocked to hear the news. He tells you with a grave look that the Fragment of Ymir's Heart in the palace had been stolen a few days ago...",
    ["TaskDescription100002126"]="Commander Bernard suspects that the Royal Chivalry has something to do with the theft of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Infiltrate the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Chivalry</color> and seek out more information!",
    ["TaskDescription100002127"]="Looks like the last Alchemy Device is really in the sewers! Captain Bernard is becoming increasingly suspicious of the Royal Chivalry's motives. Follow his instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the sewers</color> to figure out what's going on.",
    ["TaskDescription100002128"]="After answering the password correctly, you finally entered the first floor of the sewer. You wonder what happened to that <color=#CA2E0AFF>expedition squad</color> of the Royal Chivalry. Hurry up and find them!",
    ["TaskDescription100002129"]="Through a conversation with the expedition squad's captain, Rodney, you learn that they're in a bad situation... It turns out they also encountered trouble in the sewers, and you decide to help them find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>two missing squad members</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100002130"]="The first person you find is Zudd, a member of the expedition squad. He mentions that he was rescued by Iverson, another lost squad member, but he's too afraid to search for him with you... Since it's an emergency, you decide to go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Iverson</color> on your own.",
    ["TaskDescription100002131"]="You manage to free Iverson from the web, but just as you breathe a sigh of relief, Iverson states that he has something important to report to Rodney right away... Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort Iverson back to the squad</color>, and listen to what he has to say.",
    ["TaskDescription100002132"]="You unexpectedly learn from Iverson the whereabouts of the alchemist and the stolen Fragment of Ymir's Heart. It seems that the incident was indeed the alchemist's plot... Quickly inform <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chivalry Captain Hallam</color> about the expedition squad's discovery.",
    ["TaskDescription100002133"]="After some communication, the misunderstanding between the Kingdom Defense Force and the Royal Chivalry is finally resolved. You all decide to work together to search for the alchemist, but it is difficult to find the target quickly due to the complicated sewer system... Luckily, Captain Hallam remembers that his old friend <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charlie</color> was involved in the design of the capital's sewers. Find him and ask to borrow the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sewer Blueprint</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100002134"]="While looking at old Charlie's Sewer Blueprint, you discover a hidden pipe on the second floor of the sewers that leads to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate Cemetery</color>! It'll be real bad if the alchemist escapes from there. No time to lose. Let's go check it out!",
    ["TaskDescription100002135"]="You enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewer's second floor</color> through the hidden passageway <color=#CA2E0AFF>beneath the tombs</color>. How are the members of the expedition squad doing now?",
    ["TaskDescription100002136"]="You help the expedition squad clear out the Male Thief Bugs that were blocking the way. It seems the only way to catch the cunning alchemist is to work together!",
    ["TaskDescription100002137"]="You offer to assist the expedition squad in their search for the alchemist. Leave no stone unturned. This villain must not be allowed to escape!",
    ["TaskDescription100002138"]="You see a golden monster deep in the sewers... It looks like it won't be taken down easily. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Library</color> and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Scholar Norten</color> for a way to subdue it!",
    ["TaskDescription100002139"]="After consulting with the monster researchers and reading related literature, you learn that the most effective way to overcome the golden monster is to receive Odin's Blessing and gain his power. To do this, you must go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>statue of Odin in front of the Palace Square</color> and ask for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archbishop Wolmas'</color> assistance.",
    ["TaskDescription100002140"]="It looks like you need to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color> to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color> before the blessing ceremony. You're only one step away from defeating the monster, so don't relax yet! Let's go!",
    ["TaskDescription100002141"]="While blessing you, Archbishop Wolmas seems to have discovered something and looks happily surprised... Now that you've received Odin's blessing, hurry back to the second floor of the sewer and join Rodney!",
    ["TaskDescription100002142"]="Now you're fully prepared. Go take care of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Thief Hatchling</color>! This is a fight you can't and won't lose!",
    ["TaskDescription100002143"]="So the Golden Thief Hatchling <color=#CA2E0AFF>broke through the wall</color> and escaped? Let's go after it and deliver the final blow!",
    ["TaskDescription100002144"]="In the Sewer Vault, you finally see the villain that caused the monster rampages: Baroshev. Although the treacherous and crafty criminal slipped away, you are able to recover the stolen Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Report the whole ordeal to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hallam and Commander Bernard</color>. After a busy day, it's time to bring them some good news!",
    ["TaskDescription100002145"]="In recognition of your service, Captain Hallam and Commander Bernard are organizing an <color=#CA2E0AFF>award ceremony</color> for you! Let <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rodney</color> know when you're ready. Don't make them wait too long!",
    ["TaskDescription100002146"]="You complete the award ceremony in the midst of cheers and applause, and your relationship with the Kingdom Defense Force and the Royal Chivalry has been strengthened... But there's still an important issue to resolve. Go and discuss it with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hallam</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100002147"]="You make a request to take the Fragment of Ymir's Heart back to Criatura Academy for safekeeping, which Captain Hallam quickly agrees to. What will <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> have to say when you tell him about everything?",
    ["TaskDescription100002148"]="Follow Dean Mainz's instructions, and place the Fragment of Ymir's Heart on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100002149"]="The Heart Pedestal is glowing!",
    ["TaskDescription100002150"]="The Fragment of Ymir's Heart has been successfully placed and activated! Just as you wonder what to do next, you suddenly hear a mysterious and ethereal female voice nearby...",
    ["TaskDescription100003101"]="You follow the goddess's directions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the coast</color> to investigate. Hurry and see if anything unusual is happening in the waters around Izlude Island.",
    ["TaskDescription100003102"]="According to Captain Carew, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious fog</color> has appeared around the island waters, causing several ships to go missing. Captain Carew has never seen such <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange weather</color>... Quickly find the island's meteorologist, Kleine, and figure out what's going on. Hopefully he'll know the source of the fog!",
    ["TaskDescription100003103"]="After some research, Kleine discovers that the mysterious fog at sea is an omen of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Haze</color>! He requests that you immediately seek help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> of the Criatura Academy. Seeing Kleine's frightened look causes you to worry as well.",
    ["TaskDescription100003104"]="Dean Mainz tells you that the foggy weather will bring unforeseeable catastrophe to the land of the living. He asks you to quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather the Academy instructors outside</color> and tell them to get ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defend Izlude Island</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003105"]="While you were talking to Dean Mainz, an army of the undead began its invasion of Izlude Island, seizing the opportunity created by the mysterious fog. You fight alongside the instructors and find the Corsair that started the invasion at the port. No one could have guessed that he was in possession of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart!</color> It looks like things are not as simple as they seem. Go and hear what Dean Mainz has to say about this.",
    ["TaskDescription100003106"]="Everybody agrees that as long as the Fragment of Ymir's Heart is in the Corsair's possession, the undead will attack Izlude Island again sooner or later. For this reason, Dean Mainz asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Mjolnir Mountains</color> to get help from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Sage Kroneika</color> who lives there in seclusion, as he has ample experience in fighting the undead.",
    ["TaskDescription100003107"]="Upon arriving at the foot of the Mjolnir Mountains, you learn that the Golden Wings Mine has collapsed. In order to save the injured miners, the owner of the mine, Rorke, has gone to ask for help from the Great Sage, Kroneika. You also learn that the Great Sage lives at the top of the Mjolnir Mountains. There's no time to lose. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Head to the top of the mountain and find the Great Sage</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003108"]="On your way up the mountain, you meet Rorke, the owner of the Golden Wings Mine, who seems to be very afraid of bugs and wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort him to the top of the mountain</color>. Since you are heading there anyway, go up with him!",
    ["TaskDescription100003109"]="You finally reach the top of the mountain, but Bidal tells you that the Great Sage has left his hut. He heard that the Great Sage has gone deep into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> to investigate strange fluctuations of magic energy and has not returned. You offer to go into the forest to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the Great Sage</color>, which Bidal greatly appreciates.",
    ["TaskDescription100003110"]="You didn't expect to run into your old friend Ygnizem in the Labyrinth Forest! She's trying to light a Red Sealstone, which requires <color=#CA2E0AFF>fresh Witch Flowers</color>. Hurry up and pick some for her!",
    ["TaskDescription100003111"]="You follow Ygnizem's instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the Witch Flowers in front of the Red Sealstone</color>. You have a vague feeling that something about her has changed...",
    ["TaskDescription100003112"]="Ygnizem tells you that you can check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign</color> in front of the nearby teleportation point when you can't find your way. You wonder why she knows the secrets of this forest...",
    ["TaskDescription100003113"]="You go in the direction indicated by the sign and encounter Ygnizem once again. This time she asks you to help her take down the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Chonchon</color> most hated by witches. You can't put your finger on it, but Ygnizem seems to be getting weirder and weirder...",
    ["TaskDescription100003114"]="You help Ygnizem light the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blue Sealstone</color>, but she doesn't even thank you for your efforts... The most important thing right now is to find the Great Sage as soon as possible, so check the nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign</color> and find the way forward!",
    ["TaskDescription100003115"]="You go in the direction indicated by the sign but somehow come across Ygnizem again... She's frustrated that she can't light the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Sealstone</color>, so help her get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Life Seeds</color> from nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cocos</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003116"]="You help Ygnizem light the Green Sealstone, but she still doesn't seem to want to talk to you... She just tells you that you can find the Great Sage at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>end of the road ahead of you</color> and then runs off on her own.",
    ["TaskDescription100003117"]="You follow Ygnizem's directions and really find the Great Sage Kroneika, but he is trapped in vines! What he tells you next comes as a great surprise. The Great Sage says that a swordswoman trapped him there, and that Ygnizem, whom you came across in the Labyrinth Forest, is likely possessed by the spirit of the witch Evelyn!\nHer lighting of sealstones all over the forest is very suspicious, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>it's imperative that she is stopped</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription100003118"]="After you speak with Evelyn, the two of you finally resolve your misunderstandings. Seeing that she was only trying to free her soul, there's no need to continue fighting with her. Now let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Kroneika back to the Sage Hut on the Mjolnir Mountains</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100003119"]="After you say your goodbyes to Evelyn and Ygnizem, you follow Kroneika back to the Sage Hut. Now it's time to tell Kroneika about what happened on Izlude Island!",
    ["TaskDescription100003120"]="Bidal mentions the mine owner Rorke's request for help, saying that there are still injured miners down the mountain waiting for Kroneika's aid. Kroneika asks you to take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Panaceas</color> he's made down the mountain and distribute them to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>injured miners</color> at the Golden Wings Mine.",
    ["TaskDescription100003121"]="At the bottom of the hill, you meet Rorke's daughter, Macpennie, who says that there have been many <color=#CA2E0AFF>Manic Stainers</color> crawling out of the ground since the mine's collapse. Now Rorke is very worried about this, and you feel compelled to help. Go to the mine and eliminate the Manic Stainers!",
    ["TaskDescription100003122"]="Rorke is very moved when he learns of your good deed. He tells you that he will pull himself together and rebuild the Golden Wings Mine. Hurry back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Hut</color> and convey Rorke's gratitude to the Great Sage. Also check if he's ready to depart!",
    ["TaskDescription100003123"]="You and Kroneika return to Izlude Island. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>port</color> and meet up with the expedition squad!",
    ["TaskDescription100003124"]="Unexpectedly, your ship is wrecked amid a fog not long after you set sail. Now you can't remember exactly what happened. Go to Dean Mainz to figure out what's going on!",
    ["TaskDescription100003125"]="After learning that Alice and Melbrun were separated from the main force, you split up and launch a search operation. You rescue a terrified Melbrun, who was surrounded by a group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Roda Frogs</color>. You discover that he isn't afraid of the undead, but he's terrified of cold-blooded brutes...",
    ["TaskDescription100003126"]="Melbrun says he had heard a <color=#CA2E0AFF>scream from Alice</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next cabin</color>. Was there an accident? Let's go and find out!",
    ["TaskDescription100003127"]="During your investigation, you are transported to an unknown ship through a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>... What is this place, and where is Alice?",
    ["TaskDescription100003128"]="You finally find Alice, who says she's been haunted by the ghost in front of her since her arrival. She lost her <color=#CA2E0AFF>staff</color> in the process. Find and return it to Alice, then hear what she plans to do next!",
    ["TaskDescription100003129"]="Based on Alice's observation, she believes the ghost is under the influence of an evil force, which has muddled its memories. She says she can use the ship's prayer room to restore the ghost's consciousness, but she needs time to prepare. Think of a way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>distract the ghost</color> and buy Alice more time!",
    ["TaskDescription100003130"]="You manage to buy time for Alice and lead the ghost to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>prayer room</color>. Hopefully, Alice's' prayers will redeem the soul of the deceased...",
    ["TaskDescription100003131"]="With Alice's help, the ghost of First Mate Hobbe finally regains consciousness! He now remembers his past and offers to take you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearest safe place</color>. He also mentions that he would like you to say goodbye to Alson on his behalf if you get the chance. Leave the ship and fulfill his wish!",
    ["TaskDescription100003132"]="With Hobbe's help, you're finally back under the sunshine, but this doesn't seem to be the port of Izlude Island...",
    ["TaskDescription100003133"]="After asking an old gentleman for directions, you're surprised to find out that he's Alson, the person First Mate Hobbe wants you to find! He is very saddened to hear about what happened to Hobbe, but upon learning of your punitive expedition against the monsters of the sea, he decides to help you <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Shipwreck</color>. After all that has happened, you wonder how your comrades on the Shipwreck are doing now...",
    ["TaskDescription100003134"]="When you returned to the Shipwreck, you are attacked by Whispers. To your surprise, one of them still retains its humanity and is desperate for help to restore its memories. According to the Whisper, it can regain its memories by obtaining a Rose Ring currently in the possession of a Zombie at the end of the deck. Why not help it before rushing to meet up with the expedition squad?",
    ["TaskDescription100003135"]="After receiving the Rose Ring, the Whisper finally regains its memory. Turns out she was a mage named Anna! From listening to Anna's story, you learn how she and her lover Lukas were persecuted by a Corsair at their wedding, and how a Fragment of Ymir's Heart was taken from them. Anna hopes you can help her find Lukas. But before you can do that, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up with your comrades on the ship</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003136"]="Dean Mainz indicates that he is aware of what you experienced, and it just so happens that the expedition squad has advanced to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>upper deck</color>. He asks you to go ahead and fulfill your promise to Anna, the Whisper!",
    ["TaskDescription100003137"]="You help Anna find her deceased lover Lukas. To your surprise, Lukas says he can help you locate where the Corsair is on the ship after hearing about your expedition plan! It is also Anna's and Lukas' dying wish for the Corsair to be taken down. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>spell casting location</color> and accept their help!",
    ["TaskDescription100003138"]="Anna and Lukas mark a route for you with the power of the Rose Ring. Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the markers to find the Corsair</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003139"]="You follow the markers to the Corsair's hideout and find the rest of the expedition squad already there. Now, let's all work together to take down the wicked <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corsair</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100003140"]="The expedition team defeats the Corsair and recovers the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Dean Mainz declares the expedition a resounding success. Hurry and share the good news with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Carew</color>, who's waiting for you on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>lower deck</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100003141"]="Upon your return to Izlude Island, Dean Mainz asks you to place the Fragment of Ymir's Heart that you brought back from the Shipwreck on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>. What will the goddess Brunhild say to you this time?",
    ["TaskDescription100004101"]="You follow the goddess' instructions and head to the desert city of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc</color> to investigate. It's said that this city has always been dangerous and rife with crime. You wonder if anything unusual has happened here lately.",
    ["TaskDescription100004102"]="You learn from the Kafra service employee that the number of travelers to Morroc has dropped significantly lately. When you ask the local sheriff, Maximilian, for the reason, he shows neither knowledge nor concern.\nInstead, he tells you about a well-known <color=#CA2E0AFF>information peddler</color> who lives <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside of Morroc</color>. It's said that he knows everything about city. Why don't you go ask him?",
    ["TaskDescription100004103"]="The information peddler's reaction to seeing you seems a bit odd. He says that fairness is important when doing business. If you want to get information from him, you have to give him something he wants, which right now is some<color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Cactus</color>. Go get what he wants so that you can learn what's been happening in Morroc!",
    ["TaskDescription100004104"]="Seeing that you brought the fresh cactus, the information peddler finally reveals some information.\nIt turns out that Morroc has been suffering from water, food, and material shortages due to the sharp decline of trade caravans traveling to and from the city! When you're about to ask for more information, the peddler tells you to go out again and get a<color=#CA2E0AFF>Huge Pecopeco Egg</color> for him...",
    ["TaskDescription100004105"]="After you bring him the Huge Pecopeco Egg, the information peddler tells you that the reason for the decline in caravans is the strange climate.\nThe temperature around Morroc has risen sharply recently, making it unbearable even for the native desert dwellers. Just as you are about to ask the reason for the rise in temperature, the information peddler stops talking once again. He wants you to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chewy Grasshopper Legs</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Metallers</color>, otherwise, he won't continue answering questions...",
    ["TaskDescription100004106"]="Seeing as you brought him the Chewy Grasshopper Legs, the information peddler tells you that the rising temperatures is related to a strange force field that appeared in the desert. But if you want to learn more about it, you'll have to first get rid of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anacondaqs</color> that prowl around and threaten the safety of the residents.",
    ["TaskDescription100004107"]="After seeing you complete his requests one after another, the information peddler finally reveals his true identity—Rocky, the Legendary Thief! It turns out he's an old friend of Maximilian's!\nRocky is pleasantly surprised by your arrival and believes that you are the one who can figure out this anomaly and fix Morroc's problem. He wants you to join forces with the Assassins Guild to investigate the force field and says that its appearance may have something to do with the Fragment of Ymir's Heart... Quickly follow his instructions and bring the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Signal Flare</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hope Oasis</color> in the Sograt Desert to meet with someone from the Assassins Guild.",
    ["TaskDescription100004108"]="After using the Signal Flare given to you by Rocky, an assassin by the name of Eremes appears before you. Follow him to check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange force field</color>! Though his cold way of speaking will take some time to get used to...",
    ["TaskDescription100004109"]="Eremes tells you that the force field contains strong <color=#CA2E0AFF>water elemental power</color> and recommends that you ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sean</color>, the archaeologist who first discovered the force field, for advice on how to dispel it.",
    ["TaskDescription100004110"]="You find the archaeologist, Sean, but he's already delirious from heatstroke. The doctor by his side, Wallace, says that his supply of heatstroke medicine has long been depleted. Now he can only to try curing Sean using a traditional remedy.\nIn order to make the remedy, Wallace needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Scorpion Stingers</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hard Stone Hearts</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Scorched Sand Poison Herbs</color>… Can these really be used to cure him?",
    ["TaskDescription100004111"]="Seeing that you have brought the ingredients, Wallace excitedly urges you to toss them into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cauldron</color> by the side to brew the remedy.",
    ["TaskDescription100004112"]="You follow Wallace's instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir the potion clockwise</color> for five minutes. Then you <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir it counterclockwise</color> for another five minutes. Afterward, you pinch your nose hard, hoping Sean will be able to tolerate the smell...",
    ["TaskDescription100004113"]="The heatstroke medicine is ready at last! The last step is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed it to the archaeologist, Sean</color>... Hopefully, it works better than it smells...",
    ["TaskDescription100004114"]="After regaining consciousness, Sean tells you that the force field is a rare phenomenon produced by a great divine power. Through his research, he developed a method to dispel it. You have to figure out its elemental property, find its corresponding <color=#CA2E0AFF>counter attribute stone</color> and place the stone on top of the force field.\nHurry and use this method with Eremes to <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispel the Water Force Field</color> once and for all!",
    ["TaskDescription100004115"]="After a lot of hard work, you and Eremes finally dispel the Water Force Field! He tells you that there is still a force field in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast corner of the desert</color>, which his companion, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trisse</color>, is in charge of guarding...\nEremes looks a little worried, and you're not sure why. Why not go there and check it out?",
    ["TaskDescription100004116"]="On your way to the next force field, you meet a terrified archaeologist who tells you about a sinkhole that has appeared in the southeast corner of the desert. He saw with his own eyes a <color=#CA2E0AFF>girl dressed as a thief</color> fall into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>terrifying Ant Cavern</color>... That couldn't be Trisse, could it?",
    ["TaskDescription100004117"]="You meet a bawling Giearth at the entrance to the cavern. After helping him retrieve his lost food, Giearth depressingly complains that Boss Nana Ba is infatuated with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bossy and headstrong woman</color> who demands that he hold a decent wedding for her. Giearth has been breaking his back just to fulfill her wishes...\nYou have a vague feeling that this bossy, headstrong woman might be Trisse...",
    ["TaskDescription100004118"]="As you make your way deeper into the cavern, you quickly run into another bawling Giearth. After helping him recover his lost wine, Giearth depressingly complains that Boss Nana Ba is infatuated with a <color=#CA2E0AFF>woman who fell from the sky</color> and that she demands that he hold a decent wedding for her. This Giearth has also been breaking his back just to fulfill her wishes...\nA bossy, headstrong woman that fell from the sky? The more you hear, the more you think they're talking about Trisse....",
    ["TaskDescription100004119"]="Shortly after moving forward, you encounter a bawling Giearth again. This one tells you that he has lost Boss Nana Ba's bride, so you follow some footprints to look for her. After some searching, you really do find Trisse hiding!\nWhile speaking with her, you learn that she is in charge of guarding the Wind Force Field and that the one <color=#CA2E0AFF>Great Earth</color> in the cavern that can dispel the Wind Force Field is in the hands of Boss Nana Ba.\nAs fate would have it, the only option you two have is to go back and have a fake wedding. Then you'll have the opportunity to get close and steal the Great Earth... For this plan, Trisse asks you to pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vertigo Mushrooms</color> first. What on earth is she planning to do this time?",
    ["TaskDescription100004120"]="After returning to the wedding venue with Trisse, Nana Ba invites you to be their <color=#CA2E0AFF>witness</color>. You need to find an opportunity to add <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vertigo Mushrooms to the food and wine</color> during the ceremony. Be careful, it's now or never!",
    ["TaskDescription100004121"]="Things go awry as you try to steal the Great Earth! Fortunately, Nana Ba and his minions are no match for you and cannot stop you. Now that the Great Earth is in your hands, hurry up and go with Trisse to <color=#CA2E0AFF>dispel the Wind Force Field</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100004122"]="You and Trisse use the Great Earth to dispel the Wind Force Field but are still unable to find the Fragment of Ymir's Heart nearby... Why don't you return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Assassins Guild</color> with Trisse? Maybe they've made some new developments in their investigation?",
    ["TaskDescription100004123"]="You help Kai of the Assassin's Guild dispel the third force field—the Earth Force Field—located outside of Morroc. Kai tells you that Rocky has made some inquiries at the tavern about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>... Now that you finally have a lead on the fragment, hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tavern</color> to meet with Rocky!",
    ["TaskDescription100004124"]="Rocky asks you to find a way to get more information about force fields and the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from McGille, a black market merchant. However, all McGille has on his mind is the barkeeper, Heflee... You have no choice but to help him first by finding out Heflee's drinking preferences. Who knew that this beautiful woman would say she wants to taste wine brewed with the dead bodies of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chonchons, Rockers, and Anacondaqs</color>?!\nSince love makes men irrational, McGille offers to trade any commodity or information for these materials. This is your chance! Help him make his wish come true!",
    ["TaskDescription100004125"]="Give the black market merchant the dead Chonchons, Rockers, and Anacondaqs. I wonder what kind of information... or love could be exchanged for these gag-inducing ingredients?",
    ["TaskDescription100004126"]="According to McGille, the last force field and Fragment of Ymir's Heart are <color=#CA2E0AFF>inside the Pyramid</color>! Quickly inform Rocky about this great discovery. On your way out, wish McGille good luck. He looks quite pleased with himself...",
    ["TaskDescription100004127"]="As soon as you enter the Pyramid, you meet a crazy old tomb keeper who mistakes you for a wandering dead. He tells you that the \"fiery red force field\" is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest corner of the Pyramid</color>...\nIt's reported that the force field's appearance has brought terrible effects to the surrounding area. Go check out what's going on inside the Pyramid!",
    ["TaskDescription100004128"]="You meet a mysterious woman named Eassis on the southwest platform of the Pyramid, who tells you that the elemental power of the Fire Force Field has been absorbed by the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, and simply dispelling the remaining force field can no longer solve the problem...\nEassis says she knows where the fragment is. She's willing to remove it and give it to you herself, but only if you first help her retrieve the <color=#CA2E0AFF>scattered body parts of Osiris</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100004129"]="You have recovered all the scattered body parts of Osiris. Deliver them to Eassis, who is waiting <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of the central coffin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100004130"]="From the look on Eassis's face when she recovered Osiris' corpse, it is clear that she had a special relationship with Osiris... The king is dead, but his dignity remains. Why don't you wait in reverence in front of the central coffin?",
    ["TaskDescription100004131"]="You had no idea that Eassis was the queen of Ancient Egypt, the wife of a pharaoh! Thanks to her help, you were able to resolve the misunderstanding with Osiris and get your hands on the Fragment of Ymir's Heart.\nSo far all the force fields in the Morroc region have been dispelled and their effects have ceased. It's time to end this adventure, so go say goodbye to Rocky!",
    ["TaskDescription100004132"]="The goddess Brunhild is awaiting your return in the Temple of Dawn. Hurry and place the third fragment on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005101"]="According to the goddess' instructions, the fourth Fragment of Ymir's Heart is at the bottom of the sea. How will you get there? Go and ask the veteran seafarer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Carew</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005102"]="According to Captain Carew's description, there is a secret passage that leads to the ocean floor on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Byalan Island</color>, which is situated in the middle of the deep sea! This is an incredible discovery. Get to the island and find the passage to the ocean floor!",
    ["TaskDescription100005103"]="Not long after landing on Byalan Island, you encounter a worried-looking sailor who claims that the merchant ship he works on was shipwrecked while passing through the area. One of the people on board, a young man named Gail Wigner, is now missing at sea.\nSince the Wigner Family is one of the famous seven royal families, the rest of the ship's survivors are afraid to return to Alberta until Gail is found. However, the sailor says that everyone who has went to search for him in the cave ahead of you hasn't returned. Go help him find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing crewmates and travelers</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005104"]="You find the wounded merchant Keanste in an underwater cave and listen to his story about how he heroically saved a fellow traveler—a doctor named Byrd—and how he sustained injuries performing his noble deed...\nOut of concern for the doctor—or for his own wounds—Keanste wants you to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Byrd</color> as soon as possible and bring the doctor to him.",
    ["TaskDescription100005105"]="You soon find Byrd and save him from a monster. To your surprise, Byrd's version of events completely differs from Keanste's tale of heroism. He says Keanste was actually a cowardly and selfish fellow who ran away by himself as soon as they were attacked by the monster!\nLuckily for him, Byrd is a kind doctor. He decides to put aside his grievances to treat Keanste's wounds. Hurry and escort him back. Let's see if Keanste will feel a sense of shame after this...",
    ["TaskDescription100005106"]="Byrd does not appreciate Keanste's false concern one bit. He only asks you to throw the ingredients you just collected into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cauldron</color> for brewing. Go ahead and do as he says!",
    ["TaskDescription100005107"]="After some conversation, you finally get to the bottom of what happened. It turns out that the reason they went into the cave to explore was because of a poem describing of treasure on the island!\nBesides Keanste and Byrd, another traveling pair has gone <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep inside the cave</color> and has yet to return... Find them and make sure they're safe!",
    ["TaskDescription100005108"]="Following the suspicious footprints, you find the bard, Theodore, quietly singing a ballad about the mysterious treasure of Strouf. He is trying to solve its riddle...\nAs you listen to him talk to himself, ideas pop into your head. If you can help Theodore <color=#CA2E0AFF>solve the riddle</color>, maybe he'll follow you back!",
    ["TaskDescription100005109"]="After you show Theodore the picture of the skeleton with gold teeth, his gears start turning and he figures out the song's riddle! But that doesn't completely relieve Theodore's worries, as he believes he has missed the opportunity to solve the next riddle.\nTheodore has figured out that the underwater treasure has something to do with Obeaunes. He once saw an Obeaune with his own eyes, but he couldn't catch up with her because he ran out of stamina... Instead, Yorkshire continued the chase. Maybe he's discovered the secret of the Obeaunes.\nFollow Theodore to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for Yorkshire</color>! He won't stop until he's solved all the puzzles!",
    ["TaskDescription100005110"]="After speaking with Yorkshire, you learn that he saw Gail Wigner while pursuing the Obeaune! However, Gail acted very strangely. When Yorkshire went to greet him, Gail completely avoided him...\nWhat's going on with Gail? Hurry and find out!",
    ["TaskDescription100005111"]="While secretly observing Gail, you discover that he's trying to reveal his feelings to a young Obeaune. You inform Theodore and Yorkshire about this, but it makes them even more worried.\nTheodore suspects that Gail is trying to obtain the legendary secret treasure from the Obeaune, and Yorkshire thinks that Gail has been seduced by her... Whatever the reason, you must find a way to bring Gail back!",
    ["TaskDescription100005112"]="After talking to Gail, you learn that he has fallen in love with an Obeaune who saved his life during the shipwreck. Although she's been unwilling to respond to his feelings, Gail won't leave until he gets an answer from her.\nYou've decided to help the smitten Gail win over the Obeaune. Do as Gale requested and place the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bouquet</color> he handmade at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>edge of the water</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100005113"]="Gail is very dismayed to learn that the Obeaune remains unmoved... But on second thought, he believes it might be because the Obeaune doesn't understand human courtship and couldn't understand his feelings!\nHow about helping him collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pretty Pearls</color> from the nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Marinas</color> to give as a gift?",
    ["TaskDescription100005114"]="Gail fashions the Pearls into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pearl Necklace</color>. Hurry and place it <color=#CA2E0AFF>near the water</color>. Hopefully the Obeaune will like it!",
    ["TaskDescription100005115"]="After learning that the Obeaune is still unaffected, Gail falls into despair... Eventually he decides to write a love letter to express his feelings, but regular paper disintegrates when it meets water...\nHow about helping him get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hard Leather</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color> in place of paper?",
    ["TaskDescription100005116"]="Gail wrote a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Love Letter</color> on the Hard Leather. Go place it <color=#CA2E0AFF>near the water</color>. Hopefully the Obeaune will be moved!",
    ["TaskDescription100005117"]="This time, the Obeaune finally reveals her feelings to you! It turns out that this Obeaune princess named Lucia had already developed a crush on Gail, but her lack of human legs had made her so self-conscious that it was difficult for her to face her feelings.\nNow that Gail's letter has given Lucia some courage, she has decided to share her feelings with Gail herself! Why don't you join her at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>place of confession</color> and witness the sweet moment?",
    ["TaskDescription100005118"]="With your help, the two lovers finally share their feelings and decide to be together! To return to land and live with Gail, Lucia wishes to acquire human legs.\nIt's said that a <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> who possesses great magic lives in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color>. Why don't you go there and ask for his advice?",
    ["TaskDescription100005119"]="The alchemist says that the only way to make an Obeaune grow human legs is to swallow the largest scale on Strouf's chest and apply a magical ointment to their fish tail. Go back and share this information with Lucia!",
    ["TaskDescription100005120"]="Lucia is so ecstatic to learn that she can transform her tail into legs that she decides to take the scale from her father's chest herself and asks you to help her gather the materials she needs to make the ointment.\nGather the ingredients and give them to Lucia! Hopefully, this magical ointment will help grant her wish!",
    ["TaskDescription100005121"]="Touched by Lucia's actions, Gail decides to give up his royal status for love and accompany Lucia to the desert, a place she has always wanted to see.\nNow that nothing is impeding the lovebirds' pursuit of happiness, why don't you help Gail inform the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sailor</color> of his decision?",
    ["TaskDescription100005122"]="After learning what happened, the sailor is shocked. Seeing his distress, you can't help but worry about the price behind this choice...",
    ["TaskDescription100005123"]="There's strong tremors coming from underground, following which a group of Obeaunes suddenly appear in front of you! It turns out that they are Obeaune priestesses from the bottom of the sea. High priestess Leona anxiously asks you about Lucia's whereabouts and tells you that something terrible has just taken place in the Underwater Temple...",
    ["TaskDescription100005124"]="Leona explains that Nield, God of the Sea, has completely lost his mind and that the cause of his madness is the loss of the scale that Lucia took!\n",
    ["TaskDescription100005125"]="Leona tells you that Nield, God of the Sea, once absorbed the power of a Fragment of Ymir's Heart after being enticed by an alchemist. Although he seemed much stronger for a time, he would frequently lose control...\nThe scale on Nield's chest contains his divine power. Once the scale was removed, he is no longer able to resist the influence of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart...\nNow the only way to save the sea is to ask the princess to return the scale. There's no time to lose. Head to the desert and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Lucia</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005126"]="You find Gail at Hope Oasis. He tells you that Lucia has fallen seriously ill due to not being accustomed to the climate. Go and check on her!",
    ["TaskDescription100005127"]="You unexpectedly see your old acquaintance Doctor Wallace by Lucia's side! The doctor states that the princess is suffering from dehydration. In order to make a remedy that can save her, he needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Everlasting Skulls, Rotten Hearts, and Smooth Snake Scales</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100005128"]="Follow Wallace's instructions and toss all of the ingredients into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cauldron</color> to brew the remedy.",
    ["TaskDescription100005129"]="That's right. Just <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir it clockwise</color> for five minutes, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>stir it counterclockwise</color> for another five minutes. It's a familiar recipe with a familiar smell!",
    ["TaskDescription100005130"]="Wallace is still really confident about his remedy! Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed the Lucia the potion</color>. Hopefully it won't be as bad as last time...",
    ["TaskDescription100005131"]="When Lucia regains consciousness, you tell her what has happened at the bottom of sea. She is shocked and saddened by what she hears and decides to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the seabed</color> immediately to the fix her mistake!",
    ["TaskDescription100005132"]="At the entrance to the Underwater Temple, you find Brady under attack by mutant fish surrounding him. After getting him out of danger, Brady tells you that many underwater creatures have gone mad due to strange power fluctuations emanating from the temple... \nThe few people who retain their sanity have fled. While fleeing from the temple, Brady was separated from his son Baxter... Seeing his anxious face, you decide to help him find <color=#CA2E0AFF>little Baxter</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005133"]="You find little Baxter weeping and learn that he was rescued by Leona and is out of danger now. Quickly take Baxter to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Divine Altar</color> and reunite the father and son!",
    ["TaskDescription100005134"]="Brady is very grateful for your help and asks you to give his thanks to Leona. The underwater situation is worse than expected. How does High Priestess Leona plan to solve this disaster?",
    ["TaskDescription100005135"]="Leona says that the only way to end the chaos at the bottom of the sea is to defeat Nield, move in close while he's in his most weakened state, and then return the scale to his chest. \nYou only have one shot at this. You must be determined and work as one! When you're ready, head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100005136"]="Along the way, you encounter another crazed underwater creature. Things are getting worse. Go deeper into the temple and investigate!",
    ["TaskDescription100005137"]="You save Simon from a group of Obeaunes. According to him, the Underwater Temple has turned into a living hell, and there are no sane people left except for the alchemist. Simon says the alchemist is the only one kind enough to stay with Nield, and he insists on brewing a potion for him...\nHearing this, Lucia realizes that everyone has been deceived by that villainous trickster. Hurry and find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>crazed Nield</color> before things get even worse!\n",
    ["TaskDescription100005138"]="It turns out that the culprit behind the chaos is yet again the alchemist Baroshev! Although you eventually restore Nield's sanity according to plan, you did not know the cost was Lucia's life...\nLegend says that love between Obeaunes and humans is doomed to fail. Even so, there are those who pursue love despite the odds... There's a kind of beauty in love's fragility. Perhaps this is the \"fate\" the goddess speaks of?",
    ["TaskDescription100005139"]="You finally got the fourth Fragment of Ymir's Heart, but in the process of getting it, you witnessed the sacrifice of a companion for the first time...\nA price too heavy was paid. Hurry now and place the fragment where it belongs—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100006101"]="You follow the instructions of the goddess, and arrive at the mountain town of Payon.\nAs soon as you arrive, you see W looking around in high spirits. Why don't you go ask her about the local area?",
    ["TaskDescription100006102"]="According to W, the administrator of this town is Lord Ocean Euin. It is said that the Euin Family has ruled this land since the founding of Payon. He knows everything about the town.... I'm sure Lord Ocean Euin will be able to provide some useful clues. Go visit him at the Lord's Residence!",
    ["TaskDescription100006103"]="You meet a girl named Moon Euin at the entrance of the Lord's Residence.\nAfter hearing why you came to Payon in search for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, she asks you to come with her... Where exactly is she taking you?",
    ["TaskDescription100006104"]="It turns out that Moon Euin wanted to take you to her uncle and master of the Archer Guild, Sky Euin.\nBut as soon as you explain to him your purpose of coming to Payon, Sky Euin strongly urges you to give up the idea of obtaining the Fragment of Ymir's Heart... He says you'll understand why after you see the Munak Cave deep in the village. Follow Moon Euin and find out what's going on!",
    ["TaskDescription100006105"]="After you return from Munak Cave, Sky Euin tells you about the history of the cave.\nIt turns out there was once a famine in Payon that caused countless townsfolk to starve to death. Although they were buried at the former site of the town, their souls did not rest in peace. The dead were transformed into monsters called Munaks. They crawled out of the ground and attacked the townsfolk who were still alive. Because of this, an ancestor of the Euin Family, Qi Euin, had to establish the Spirit Quellers. They joined forces with the Indrah Sect to seal the Munaks in an underground cave.\nSky Euin says that the Fragment of Ymir's Heart you are looking for was used to subdue the Munaks and has long been sealed deep in the cave. He also states that now it is dangerous to even go near the entrance of the cave, let alone go deep inside...\nBut Moon Euin seems to have a different view. Let's hear what she has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription100006106"]="Moon Euin says that Master Taixuan of the Indrah Sect should know the exact location of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. It's difficult to meet with the master directly, but her younger brother Comet Euin is the last disciple of Master Taixuan and may have a way to help you.\nHowever, when you meet Comet Euin, you find that he's having a hard time gathering the herbs his master told him to collect. One such herb is the Ice Soul Grass, which he still hasn't managed to get. Go and help him find the rare herbs he needs!",
    ["TaskDescription100006107"]="After you help Comet Euin find the Ice Soul Grass, you thought you could finally go with him to see Master Taixuan. However, Comet suddenly remembers that he was still missing an ingredient called Meat Pie Mushroom. Hurry and help him gather the missing ingredient!",
    ["TaskDescription100006108"]="After you help Comet Euin find the Ice Soul Grass, you thought you could finally go with him to see Master Taixuan. However, Comet suddenly remembers that he was still missing an ingredient called Sprout of Yggdrasil. Hurry and help him gather the missing ingredient!",
    ["TaskDescription100006109"]="Comet finally says that all the ingredients have been gathered and he can now take you to see Master Taixuan! The master is living in isolation at the Indrah Sect's Ancient Ancestral Hall. Follow Comet to the hall!",
    ["TaskDescription100006110"]="You meet Comet Euin's senior fellow disciple of the Indrah Sect, Munmi, outside the Ancient Ancestral Hall.\nThrough your conversation with Munmi, you learn that Master Taixuan had gone into Munak Cave with Lord Ocean Euin to strengthen the seal, but for some unknown reason after their return, Master Taixuan was inflicted with a strong poison that he still can't dispel... The ingredients you collected are exactly what Master Taixuan needs to make an antidote for the poison. Follow Munmi to the Ancient Ancestral Hall and meet Master Taixuan!",
    ["TaskDescription100006111"]="You come across an unexpected scene at the Ancient Ancestral Hall—signs everywhere indicate that a battle took place. It looks like Master Taixuan and the few Indrah Sect disciples guarding him have long since disappeared!\nHurry back to Archer Village and tell Sky Euin about the situation!",
    ["TaskDescription100006112"]="After speaking with Sky Euin, you learn that Lord Ocean Euin went missing even before Master Taixuan! It was reported that Sun Euin was the first to discover Ocean Euin's disappearance. Why don't you go find him to learn more?",
    ["TaskDescription100006113"]="According to Sun Euin's description, it is apparent that the Lord was forcibly abducted... After the incident, the Euin Family did not make the news of the Lord's disappearance public in order to avoid panic. They made Sun Euin act as the Lord of Payon while Sky Euin secretly investigated.\nWhy don't you seek out Sky Euin and find out how his investigation is going?",
    ["TaskDescription100006114"]="While talking with Sky Euin, you learn that the Hidden Wood Village west of Payon was invaded by Munaks not too long ago! Perhaps you can learn why they had appeared from the surviving villagers. Go to Hidden Wood Village to continue your investigation!",
    ["TaskDescription100006115"]="You first find the chief of Hidden Wood Village, Won Chunghan, who is deep in grief and asks you to speak with the other villagers to learn about the current situation... Seeing her in such pain, you can't help but wonder what kind of tragedy occurred on night of the Munak invasion...",
    ["TaskDescription100006116"]="You learn from three villagers about the night of the Munak invasion and how it involves an old well in the village.\nAccording to Won Chunghan, the old well is located in the northern part of Hidden Wood Village's former site. Go to there and see if there's anything strange about the well!",
    ["TaskDescription100006117"]="As you enter the Former Site of Hidden Wood Village, Wandering Munaks block your path. Hurry and take them down!",
    ["TaskDescription100006118"]="The well's water is giving off a faint sweet smell... Alarmed, Moon Euin tells you that the smell must be abnormal. Draw some well water up for investigation!",
    ["TaskDescription100006119"]="Moon Euin captures a Big-Footed Cub and asks you to feed it the well water and observe what happens next...",
    ["TaskDescription100006120"]="As expected, the Big-Footed Cub mutated after drinking the water! It looks like the water in Hidden Wood Village has been contaminated for a long time and the Munaks were originally villagers who mutated after drinking the well water as well..\nJust as you were wondering who could have done such a vile thing, you hear a noise nearby...",
    ["TaskDescription100006121"]="A man named Liu Wuye overheard your conversation with Moon Euin. Only after you explained your purpose for coming did Liu Wuye feel comfortable enough to tell you what happened to him.\nIt turns out that he and his lover, Jingyin, also drank water from the old well and underwent a mutation. However, the effects on them were quite unique. Jingyin gained great strength while Liu Wuye retained his human mind. The man who tampered with the well's water called Jingyin \"the perfect results of his research\" and threatened to bring her to the Butsudan in front of Munak Cave to complete the last step of his grand plan...\nWhatever the Munak-creating culprit wants to do next, you must enter Munak Cave to stop him!",
    ["TaskDescription100006122"]="You inform Sky Euin of what you learned at Hidden Wood Village and decide to head into Munak Cave to hunt down the criminal before something even worse happens!",
    ["TaskDescription100006123"]="It's much better after you clear away the monsters blocking path. Now hurry and explore the area ahead!",
    ["TaskDescription100006124"]="You find Master Taixuan unconscious in front of a broken Butsudan! Why is he here?",
    ["TaskDescription100006125"]="You encounter a Horong in front of the Butsudan. It seems that it was drawn to you by the power of the rune fragment in your hand. The Horong says that if you assemble the rune tablet, it can return to its original form. Help the Horong find the rune fragments scattered around the cave!",
    ["TaskDescription100006126"]="You find the second rune fragment in the Universe Stone Formation, but you don't seem to have enough to put the rune tablet together. You should continue your search elsewhere.",
    ["TaskDescription100006127"]="You finally put the rune tablet together! Hurry and take it back to the Horong.",
    ["TaskDescription100006128"]="You use the power of the rune to help the Horong return to its living form. It turns out he is the legendary general, ancestor of the Euin family, Qi Euin!\nAfter hearing your reason for entering the cave, Qi Euin informs you that the Butsudan you're looking for is not the one in front of you, but another one deep inside the cave.\nSealed inside the Butsudan is the Poison Fragment of Ymir's Heart. The person who caused the Munak invasion must be planning to use the Fragment of Ymir's Heart to commit more evil acts... Qi Euin asks you to take the rune into the cave and assemble the wandering ghosts of the Spirit Quellers. After a thousand years, Payon requires their aid once again.",
    ["TaskDescription100006129"]="You find the ghost of a Spirit Queller in a corner of Munak Cave. He was a former soldier of the Spirit Queller army! Quickly take him to Qi Euin!",
    ["TaskDescription100006130"]="After you reunite the Spirit Quellers, Qi Euin entrusts you to use the dimensional gap to take Master Taixuan back to the surface and retrieve the weapon he used before he passed away... It seems that even in his undead form, Qi Euin still wants to do his best to protect Payon.",
    ["TaskDescription100006131"]="You follow Qi Euin's orders and traverse through the dimensional gap to reach the mountains behind Payon. Now who can help you figure out where the Sun-Piercing Bow is?",
    ["TaskDescription100006132"]="You try to convince Sun Euin to let you into the Tomb of the General, but he unexpectedly tells you that he doesn't have the authority to permit you.\nIt turns out that the keepers of the Tomb of the General are two Euin elders, and only by passing their trials will you be allowed to enter... You heard that one of the elders, Xiao Euin, is currently fishing by the Exquisite Pond. Why don't you go there and prove your capability to him first?",
    ["TaskDescription100006133"]="Elder Xiao Euin is being tormented by Elder Willows. It seems that the elder will not pay attention to you unless get rid of these monsters first.",
    ["TaskDescription100006134"]="Elder Xiao Euin states that his biggest hobby is fishing. It seems that the elder won't let you pass the trial unless you help him catch a Crucian Carp first...",
    ["TaskDescription100006135"]="You fulfill both of Xiao Euin's requests, and now he's finally willing to take you into the Tomb of the General! But you vaguely remember there being more than one tomb keeping elder....",
    ["TaskDescription100006136"]="Elder Cliff Euin says that you can't prove your worthiness without beating him in a duel. In order to get into the Tomb of the General, do as Xiao Euin says—defeat the Euin elder!",
    ["TaskDescription100006137"]="You passed the trials of the two elders and are allowed to enter the Tomb of the General. Go and retrieve General Qi Euin's divine weapon, the Sun-Piercing Bow!",
    ["TaskDescription100006138"]="In the Tomb of the General, you are ambushed by monsters once again! After coming to your rescue, Sky Euin informs you that Master Taixuan has awakened and is waiting for your return at Archer Village... Does Master Taixuan have something important to tell you after all that has happened?",
    ["TaskDescription100006139"]="The reawakened Master Taixuan recounts what happened to him.\nIt turns out that he and Lord Ocean Euin had taken the Fragment of Ymir's Heart out of Munak Cave before being abducted. The fragment has fallen into the wrong hands, and now the villain will complete the last step of his evil plan at the Butsudan in Munak Cave.\nThe only way to protect Payon is to retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart!",
    ["TaskDescription100006140"]="You manage to meet up with Qi Euin and the others in Munak Cave. Now that the battle preparations have been made, it's time to head deep into the cave!",
    ["TaskDescription100006141"]="You reach a fork deep in the cave. How about splitting up to search more efficiently?",
    ["TaskDescription100006142"]="You find a strange alchemy workshop in the cave.\nLooking at the weird magic circles and bubbling cauldrons, you begin feeling like you've seen it all before...",
    ["TaskDescription100006143"]="You run into Moon Euin while she was investigating and help her get rid of poisonous Moonlight Flowers. Now you wonder how the others doing. Go further ahead and find out.",
    ["TaskDescription100006144"]="You come across an anxious Comet Euin. It turns out that his fellow disciples were poisoned during a battle with the monsters. Comet urgently needs some Sparkling Zargons to make antidotes. Hurry and get them from Horongs!",
    ["TaskDescription100006145"]="You meet Sun Euin on the platform below the Butsudan and learn that Qi Euin and Master Taixuan have been forced back to the stone platform in front of you by the monsters... Hurry over and make sure they're both safe.",
    ["TaskDescription100006146"]="During your pursuit, the identity of the culprit is finally revealed—Baroshev, your old foe that's been committing heinous crimes everywhere!\nAlthough you still couldn't catch the cunning criminal, you finally find the missing Lord Ocean Euin and recover the Fragment of Ymir's Heart... Now go and hear what General Qi Euin has to say to you.",
    ["TaskDescription100006147"]="Qi Euin thanks you for all you've done for Payon and asks you to return to the surface as soon as possible with the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. He's prepared to fight the cave monsters to the end. As long as new heroes continue to be born, Payon will be able to overcome any and all difficulties.",
    ["TaskDescription100006148"]="You bid farewell to the Euin Family and to the idyllic mountain town of Payon. Quickly take the fifth Fragment of Ymir's Heart back to the Temple of Dawn for safekeeping!",
    ["TaskDescription100007101"]="You follow the Goddess' instructions and arrive at Geffen, the City of Magic. Before you start looking for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, you should talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kafra Service Employee W</color> to learn more about the situation in the city!",
    ["TaskDescription100007102"]="According to W, other races have been ravaging the areas around Geffen much more frequently than before. She even heard a mage mention that the magic barrier protecting Geffen is in danger. This indeed seems to be a very unusual situation!\nCould these attacks have something to do with the Fragment of Ymir's Heart? And what about the rumor W mentioned? You should go and talk to Guild Leader <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower</color> for more details!",
    ["TaskDescription100007103"]="Upon entering Geffen Tower, the leader of the Mage Guild, Jesqurienne, is nowhere to be found, but you meet her senior disciple, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Katrina</color>.\nAccording to Katrina, an important object known as the Artifact—originally sealed in Geffen Tower—has disappeared. This Artifact powers the magic barrier around Geffen, and if it is not returned, the consequences could be catastrophic!\nYou want to help Katrina look for it, but before you can even open your mouth, she asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow her and investigate</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100007104"]="Katrina takes you to a table at the Place of Sages and explains to you that this is where the Artifact is kept. When you feel the powerful aura of dark elemental energy surrounding the table, Katrina insists that the Artifact is the source of this aura.\nHowever, something tells you that the truth is not so simple. All you can do now is <color=#CA2E0AFF>catch up with Katrina first</color> and ask questions later!",
    ["TaskDescription100007105"]="After following the trail of dark elemental energy to its end, you and Katrina find the Blood Clan monster Luszman. However, the demon mockingly claims that you have fallen into his trap, as while you were following the dark aura, his minion seized the chance to steal the Artifact!\nKatrina is furious about being tricked, and you are very concerned about the fact that the Fragment of Ymir's Heart Luszman just mentioned has fallen into the hands of the Blood Clan. After realizing why you came to the tower, Katrina tells you that the Blood Clan monster's lair lies beneath Geffen Tower, but if you want to enter the underground caves, you'll need the power of the Artifact.\nIn any case, it seems you must first find a way to retrieve the Artifact. Go and ask Jesqurienne, who is currently defending against attacks on the outskirts of Goblin Forest, if she has any ideas!",
    ["TaskDescription100007106"]="You find Jesqurienne outside Goblin Forest, but she is extremely busy dealing with monster raiders.\nIt seems you'll have to help Jesqurienne <color=#CA2E0AFF>repel the Goblin attackers</color> before you get a chance to tell her that the Artifact has been stolen!",
    ["TaskDescription100007107"]="After helping Jesqurienne resolve her immediate obligations, you finally have a chance to tell her what happened in Geffen Tower. Faced with a major crisis and a guilt-ridden Katrina, Jesqurienne says that the most important thing right now is to find the Artifact as soon as possible, and so she begins channeling the special connection between herself and the Artifact to determine its whereabouts. While she tries to find it, it will be up to you to protect Geffen.\nJesqurienne asks you to talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bairde</color>, who is responsible for maintaining the magic barrier. He will know what to do next.",
    ["TaskDescription100007108"]="Bairde explained the Goblin situation to you and asked for help investigating their camp.\nYou saw that the Goblins were holding a secret ritual. What were they doing? Better hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report this to Bairde</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007109"]="Bairde suspects that the Goblins are carrying out some kind of sacrificial ritual. In order find out what exactly they are up to, Katrina suggested you capture and interrogate a Goblin!\nThat would undoubtedly be the most effective method right now. Gather some of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crunchy Nuts</color> that Goblins love and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place them near the Goblin camp</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007110"]="You've successfully lured Shorty the Goblin out of the forest with the Crunchy Nuts. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>subdue him</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007111"]="You've successfully subdued Shorty. Take him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Katrina</color> and see how she intends to deal with him.",
    ["TaskDescription100007112"]="In order to find out what the sacrificial ritual is about, Katrina ordered you to force the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pungent Potion</color> she made <color=#CA2E0AFF>down Shorty's throat</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007113"]="The Pungent Potion is incredible! Shorty spilled the truth almost immediately.\nThe Goblins are erecting multiple totems around the forest in an attempt to revive their dead leader through evil sacrificial rituals that tap into the dark elemental power deep underground.\nAt this point, Bairde commented that it is impossible for the Goblins to understand elemental power, so someone else must have told them about it. Just then, Jesqurienne ended her meditation. She has located the Artifact. It's at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin stronghold</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007114"]="At the Goblin stronghold, you see the revived Goblin leader and Luszwen, the Blood Clan monster who stole the Artifact.\nYou killed the revived Goblin leader, but Luszwen managed to get away. It looks like the trouble is far from over. Report the situation to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007115"]="You told Jesqurienne what happened at the Goblin stronghold. She thinks the Blood Clan monster won't return the Artifact without a fight. It seems she still has something important to tell you. Return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Place of Sages</color> in Geffen and speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color> again!",
    ["TaskDescription100007116"]="After returning to the Place of Sages, Jesqurienne told you the story of the Artifact. Originally, the source of the Artifact's energy was dark elemental power, but Archbishop Merlin Heines altered it into a device that can change its power source.\nAfter you mentioned your reason or coming to Geffen, Jesqurienne said that she has already heard about you from Katrina, and it is now time to let you know about that part of history. She has instructed Katrina to take you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>forbidden book</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007117"]="With the book, you finally understood the origin of the Artifact. Its core is the Fragment of Ymir's Heart that contains the dark elemental power you have been looking for!\nAfter returning to the Place of Sages, Jesqurienne told you that she has located the Artifact, and it is currently in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>. If you want to help search for clues, meet up with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bairde</color>, who's conducting an investigation there.",
    ["TaskDescription100007118"]="Bairde told you that Orcs detest those who use elemental power to inflict damage. Therefore, members of the Mage Guild are discouraged from <color=#CA2E0AFF>entering the village to investigate</color>. You'll have to take on this task instead!",
    ["TaskDescription100007119"]="After entering Orc Village, you saw that Joao the orc hero was surrounded by his fellow Orcs. He was still furious after being saved, as he cannot understand why his brother, Chief Jolak, would command his men to kill him.\nJoao said that if Jolak is out to kill him, he would definitely go after his family in the village. He asked you to take his <color=#CA2E0AFF>helmet</color> to his wife, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Murloma</color>, and tell her to flee the village with their son.",
    ["TaskDescription100007120"]="You found Joao's wife, Murloma, in the village, but she told you something shocking! Their child, Jofar, has just been taken by Shaman Gerrush's men!\nSince Murloma is unwilling to leave without her child, go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>shaman's hut</color> to investigate and see if you can find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jofar's whereabouts</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007121"]="You overheard Gerrush's conversation with his disciples at the shaman's hut and told Murloma what they said. She suddenly broke down, worried that her son will be used as a sacrifice!\nThe situation is desperate; inform Orc Hero <color=#CA2E0AFF>Joao</color> immediately and listen to what he has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription100007122"]="You told Joao what happened to Jofar, and he furiously asserted that the Orc chief must also be involved in the plot! Joao has decided to overthrow the chief to save his family. But first, he will have to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>battle arena</color> and defeat all the Orc warriors in order to gain the support of the clan!",
    ["TaskDescription100007123"]="Joao officially challenged his elder brother and current chief, Jolak, at the battle arena. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Help Joao win this battle</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007124"]="You helped Joan win the battle. However, he still looks troubled.\nAfter speaking to him, you realize he is worried that a fight might break out between those who support different leaders. He hopes you can help <color=#CA2E0AFF>subdue those who oppose him</color>, but asks that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>spare their lives</color> in the process. Otherwise, this fight for leadership will spell the end for the Orcs.",
    ["TaskDescription100007125"]="After much hard work, you've finally subdued all those who oppose Joao. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chief's hut</color> and regroup with <color=#CA2E0AFF>him</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007126"]="You received another piece of news when you arrived at the chief's hut. Jolak and Gerrush entered the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underground cave</color> a while ago!",
    ["TaskDescription100007127"]="You and Joao went to the underground cave and took care of the Orc Zombies wandering around the entrance.\nSaving Jofar is going to be a race against time. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Press on</color> and see if you can find any clues!",
    ["TaskDescription100007128"]="You found a semi-conscious Orc, Nagosh, on the ground. Follow Joao's instructions and gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cliff Grass</color> from nearby!",
    ["TaskDescription100007129"]="You gave the Cliff Grass to Joao, but now he also wants you to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Foul Slime</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Skeletons</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007130"]="After much hard work, you managed to save Nagosh's life, and he told you everything he knows. The reason for the chief's erratic behavior is that he has been bewitched by Gerrush.\nHurry, find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chief Jolak</color>, and stop him from making another mistake!",
    ["TaskDescription100007131"]="You and Joao arrived at the altar and killed the Orc guards that tried to stop you. Jofar's cries could be heard. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hurry over</color> and find out what's happening!",
    ["TaskDescription100007132"]="You finally found Jofar in the middle of the altar, but according to Gerrush, Jofar has already become a successful subject in an experiment on the fusion of Orc physiology and dark elemental power. You have a hunch that this has something to do with Luszwen, the Blood Clan monster who stole the Artifact. Hurry, <color=#CA2E0AFF>save Jofar</color> before things get even worse!",
    ["TaskDescription100007133"]="Tragedy ultimately couldn't be avoided.\nJust as Joao was about to pick up his child, Luszwen appeared and took Jofar away. Chief Jolak saw what happened and finally realized his mistake. He invited you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>chief's hut</color> for a chat.",
    ["TaskDescription100007134"]="Jolak said that he will do everything in his power to bring Joao's child back, even if it costs him his life. The Orcs now have a stronger leader in Joao.\nAt that moment, Bairde appeared in Orc Village and told Jolak that the Mage Guild has decided to help the Orcs. He asked you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Geffen Tower</color> with him to talk with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007135"]="While you were away, Jesqurienne found a new lead on the Artifact. The aura of the Artifact has recently moved to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color>.\nIf you are willing to continue to help with the investigation, then go meet up with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Katrina</color>, who has already left for Kordt Forest!",
    ["TaskDescription100007136"]="You and Bairde did not find Katrina at the entrance to Kordt Forest. Could she have entered the forest herself and started investigating?\nIn any case, <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the area</color> to see if she has left any clues!",
    ["TaskDescription100007137"]="Following the suspicious tracks, you finally found an unconscious Katrina at the Spinecrusher Clan camp.\nAccording to Woofka, chieftain of the Spinecrusher Clan, one of them attacked Katrina with a blow dart that causes paralysis. Suddenly, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spinecrusher Clan guard</color> came rushing over. Listen to what he has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription100007138"]="You helped the Spinecrusher Clan investigate the attack on their guards and found out that the culprits are none other than the strongest of the Kobold clans, the Skullsplitter Clan!\nWoofka said that he isn't strong enough to go up against the Skullsplitter Clan alone, and asked for your help to seek the aid of Wooflard, chieftain of the Gutripper Clan. To show your sincerity, take along some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat n' Pumpkin</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooflard</color>'s favorite food.",
    ["TaskDescription100007139"]="Woofka's request put Wooflard in a difficult situation. He said that although he was willing to help, his guards have been mysteriously going missing recently.\nInvestigate the area around the Gutripper Clan's camp to see if you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the missing guards</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007140"]="You saved a Gutripper guard from a Skullsplitter guard. According to him, some of his comrades are also patrolling the area.\nCheck the area to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ensure that the guards are safe</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007141"]="You found several Gutripper guard bodies surrounded by Skullsplitter guards!\nYou don't understand why the Skullsplitter Clan would kill their own kind. In any case, report back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooflard</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007142"]="You told Wooflard what happened to the Gutripper guards. He was grief-stricken and blamed his weakness for fueling the arrogance of the Skullsplitter Clan.\nHe asked for your help to seek the aid of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wooflorn</color>, chieftain of the Arrowtongue Clan. He hopes that Wooflorn's wisdom can help the Kobold race out of this predicament.",
    ["TaskDescription100007143"]="After listening to your account, Wooflorn said that things are not as simple as they seem. If the Skullsplitter Clan is willing to incur outrage for their aggression, there must be deeper secret.\nTo be safe, Wooflorn taught you how to make a dish called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crispy Carp</color> and instructed you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>place it where the Skullsplitter guards patrol</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007144"]="With the help of the Crispy Carp, you managed to avoid a head on confrontation with the Skullsplitter guards. You are nearing Skullsplitter camp, so move cautiously!",
    ["TaskDescription100007145"]="After much hard work, you finally uncovered the conspiracy between Luszwen and Woofsten, chieftain of the Skullsplitter Clan. Woofsten was trading his clansmen's blood for the divine weapon, which was once wielded by the Kobold God.\nUnder the threat of violence, Woofsten finally revealed the location where he will be meeting Luszwen. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow Woofsten</color> and capture that scoundrel!",
    ["TaskDescription100007146"]="He is indeed in front of the Kobold God totem pole. Now that you've found Luszwen again, don't let him get away!",
    ["TaskDescription100007147"]="Luszwen once hinted about searching for the truth of the Kobold race's divine weapon at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kobold God totem pole</color>. What would the Kobold God think of this old weapon?",
    ["TaskDescription100007148"]="Although the scheming Luszwen managed to escape, at least the unrest among the Kobolds has been quelled.\nReport the events of Kordt Forest to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007149"]="Jesqurienne said that the aura of the Artifact is now <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep beneath Geffen Tower</color>. Maybe this time, you will be able to find out the true intentions of the forces of darkness.",
    ["TaskDescription100007150"]="Jesqurienne suddenly came to a stop after arriving under Geffen Tower. She said she was trying to pinpoint the exact location of the Artifact, but the many other dark elemental power sources in the area prevented her from making an accurate judgment.\nIt seems that the fastest way to locate the Artifact will be to <color=#CA2E0AFF>split up and investigate</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007151"]="Just as you were contemplating where to start the investigation, you heard a mysterious voice that guided you toward a dimensional gap.\nAfter killing all the monsters that emerged from it, the mysterious voice spoke once more. She asked you to search for her body <color=#CA2E0AFF>at a tombstone</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007152"]="You met the owner of the mysterious voice. She is a wizard by the name of Alexia. She told you about her past with Pentagram and advised you to go <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color> and search for another <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007153"]="You found the second dimensional gap and saw that Bairde was trapped by dark elemental vines. Just as the both of you were at your wits' end over how to destroy the vines, another mysterious voice spoke. It told you that splashing <color=#CA2E0AFF>Poisonous Blood</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ghouls</color> will solve the problem.",
    ["TaskDescription100007154"]="Following the mysterious voice's advice, you managed to cut the vines around Bairde. Hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tombstone</color> and see if you're able to find the owner of the voice!",
    ["TaskDescription100007155"]="The soul of another wizard appeared from the tombstone. He was surprised that you have an aura similar to that of his master and advised you to head <color=#CA2E0AFF>east</color> and search for the next <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007156"]="Following Huey's advice, you found the third dimensional gap and also found Katrina sitting on the ground.\nAfter conversing with her, you found out that she was poisoned while fighting monsters and no matter what magic medicine she used, her wound wouldn't heal. At that moment, another mysterious voice spoke. He hinted for you to go get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Essence</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jakks</color>, as it is the only thing that can cure Katrina.",
    ["TaskDescription100007157"]="Following this mysterious voice's advice, you managed to heal Katrina's wound. Chances are the owner of this voice is also at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tombstone</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100007158"]="A member of Pentagram named Wyatt told you that the Blood Clan is merely trying to distract the Mage Guild by stealing the Artifact. Their real motive is to open dimensional gaps beneath Geffen Tower to summon hordes of undead monsters from Niflheim!\nSuch an intricate plan must have been devised by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dracula</color>. Wyatt reminded you to hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>teleporter in the east</color> to find the Artifact.",
    ["TaskDescription100007159"]="You finally defeated Dracula with the help of the three wise souls of Pentagram. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dark Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Geffen</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100007160"]="You bid farewell to Jesqurienne and Geffen, the mysterious City of Magic. Quickly take the sixth Fragment of Ymir's Heart back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> for safekeeping!",
    ["TaskDescription100008101"]="You follow the goddess' guidance and arrive at Glast Heim. Here, you talk with the Kafra employee W again. Thanks to her introduction, you learn that there was once a glorious Schmidt Empire in Glast Heim. Though it was a prosperous civilization, for reasons unknown, this flourishing empire collapsed in just a few short decades. If you want to learn the truth of Glast Heim's decline, you'll need to seek out members of the Eden Group and ask about the conclusions of their research. This is the way to the Eden Group's base. Why don't you go ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group Instructor Rockley</color> for more information?",
    ["TaskDescription100008102"]="You learn from the Eden Group instructor that the Eden Group's members are stationed here long-term to prove that Glast Heim once had a Fragment of Ymir's Heart, and that Glast Heim's prior prosperity has a definite connection to the Fragment's powers. If you wish to learn the truth about Glast Heim's history, go find the Eden Group members carrying out the excavation and see if you can help them with anything. If you can help them overcome their difficulties, then it's only a matter of time before the Fragment of Ymir's Heart is found. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palace's Back Garden</color> and find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group members</color> there first.",
    ["TaskDescription100008103"]="You find Eden Group member Larens at the ruins of the back garden. He's at his wit's end as to what to do about a ghost girl who lost their memory. The ghost girl tells you that she once lived in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the grandest building in Glast Heim</color>. Her words seem to make you think of a certain place. Go to that spot you're thinking of and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture</color> to show the ghost girl!",
    ["TaskDescription100008104"]="After looking at the photo of the palace, the ghost girl finally remembers that she was a servant in the palace named Lorraine. She recalls that King Schmidt ordered her to concoct a medicated wine. To help Lorraine recover more of her memories and remember past events, help her obtain some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amaranth Herbs</color>, some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lapis Flowers</color>, and some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glowing Fountain Water</color> to make the medicated wine.",
    ["TaskDescription100008105"]="You gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amaranth Herbs</color> near the palace, pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lapis Flowers</color> in the southwest corner, and find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glowing Fountain Water</color> from the Quiet Garden. Go bring the materials to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lorraine</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100008106"]="With your help, Lorraine mixes the medicated wine that King Schmidt had once ordered her to make, but she still can't remember the wine's effect or any more detailed memories. Larens tells you that there's a very knowledgeable wine merchant in Glast Heim named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Akarret</color>. Perhaps he knows something about this wine. Go find Akarret to learn just what it is.",
    ["TaskDescription100008107"]="The wine merchant Akarret tells you that the wine Lorraine mixed is a very rare type of poisoned alcohol that can completely remove divine powers from one's body. Go relay this <color=#CA2E0AFF>information</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lorraine</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008108"]="After learning that the alcohol she made can remove divine powers, Lorraine faintly remembers some pieces of her past. She was executed for protecting a woman who wore a snow-white robe and had divine wings. You seem to have thought of something in connection to this. Go to the place you recalled and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take pictures of related things</color> to help Lorraine remember more.",
    ["TaskDescription100008109"]="After seeing the photo of the Goddess Statue, Lorraine finally remembered various things from before her death. Larens is surprised that the Goddess Hermes once came here searching for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart and has decided to stay here and continue investigating other leads. Lorraine asks you to help her with her final wish. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort Lorraine</color> to the Quiet Garden and pick some roses!",
    ["TaskDescription100008110"]="You escort Lorraine to the Quiet Garden and successfully pick some roses. She tells you that she wants to give these roses to the innocent citizens who died to King Schmidt's tyranny. You decide to escort her to make her final wish come true. Follow Lorraine to the citizens' residences in <color=#CA2E0AFF>the northeastern part of the city</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008111"]="You follow Lorraine to the old residence of the person who was one of Glast Heim's most talented artists, Resley, where you hear the story about how King Schmidt's cruelty killed Resley. After defeating a monster who was attracted to the area, Lorraine tells you that she's remembered another person. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort Lorraine to have a look</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008112"]="You follow Lorraine and find what was once the old residence of the beautiful dancer Meryl. Lorraine tells you that her wish has been fulfilled. Lastly, she wants to see the Goddess Statue in person. Take Lorraine <color=#CA2E0AFF>to the statue</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008113"]="After saying goodbye to Lorraine, you feel uncertain about what she mentioned regarding King Schmidt turning against the faith of Odin and building an abbey to worship the goddess. Because of this, you decide to go to Glast Heim St. Abbey to investigate. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to Glast Heim St. Abbey</color> and find some clues.",
    ["TaskDescription100008114"]="You encounter the second Eden Group member, Cassius, at Glast Heim St. Abbey. Cassius is currently troubled over restoring an Evil Druid's mental capabilities. To ask the Evil Druid about the true history, Cassius has asked you to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the score to \"Requiem\" in the abbey</color>. Go look for it.",
    ["TaskDescription100008115"]="You find the first Requiem Page Fragment on a bookcase in the abbey. You defeat the monster guarding the page and obtain another Requiem Page Fragment. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>search somewhere else for more clues</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008116"]="You find the third Requiem Page Fragment among some books scattered on a desk. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>search some other places in the abbey</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008117"]="It wasn't an easy task, but you finally find the last page of \"Requiem\". Take all of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Requiem\" Pages</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cassius</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100008118"]="Cassius is very happy that you've managed to recover \"Requiem\" in its entirety. However, he tells you that he just examined that piano and discovered that it's missing a white key. The only way to play \"Requiem\" in its entirety is by using a monster's bone to replace the lost key. Go to a place with Raydric Archers and get a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Bone</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008119"]="You use the Monster Bone to replace the lost piano key and play \"Requiem\", restoring the grieving Evil Druid's mind. Cassius excitedly questions the Evil Druid about the truth of past events and the origins of the abbey, but the Evil Druid hesitates. You're surprised at Cassius' excitement. He tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the secret underground chamber in the abbey</color> to have a look around and <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring back</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>terrible item</color> you discover there. You now know why he's so excited.",
    ["TaskDescription100008120"]="You find Tangled Hairs and Crimson Pool Water in the secret underground chamber. Cassius tells you that these hairs were tested and found to belong to at least a few dozen different women. As for the pool water, it contains human blood. Because of this, the abbey must have some hidden secret, but the Evil Druid is unwilling to tell the truth. Cassius asks you to go to a place with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raydrics</color> and get <color=#CA2E0AFF>Slimy Monster Eyeballs</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Monster Blood</color>. He seems to have an idea.",
    ["TaskDescription100008121"]="Cassius uses the items you brought back to craft a Revelation Potion, which is said to be specially made by Eden Group for research of ancient truths. He decides to bring the Revelation Potion along with the Evil Druid to the secret underground chamber, then use the Revelation Potion's powers to force the Evil Druid into revealing the truth. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Cassius into the abbey's secret underground chamber</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008122"]="You follow Cassius to a coffin in the secret underground chamber. He tells you that as long as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Revelation Potion before the submerged coffin</color>, a vengeful spirit of the dead will appear immediately. Go give it a try.",
    ["TaskDescription100008123"]="You say goodbye to Cassius and, shocked at the cruel truth behind the abbey, you prepare to go to the Glast Heim Chivalry to investigate a clue connected to the truth. Cassius tells you that perhaps another member of Eden Group, Zachary, will need your help. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the Glast Heim Chivalry</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zachary</color> and hear what's troubling him.",
    ["TaskDescription100008124"]="Zachary informs you that he's currently troubled over a riddle that will unlock the Archmage Statue. According to Zachary's hypothesis, the riddle is likely connected to the eight knights represented by the eight Knight Statues in the hall. Because of this, so long as you can solve the riddle of the eight statues, you'll be able to solve the final riddle. However, most of the text on the bases of the statues has been eroded over the years and is illegible. To restore the text on the bases of the statues, he asks you to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gangrene Grass</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008125"]="You successfully pick the Gangrene Grass and bring it back to Zachary. Zachary asks you to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>rub the Gangrene Grass on the bases of the Knight Statues</color> to restore the engraved text.",
    ["TaskDescription100008126"]="After rubbing the Gangrene Grass on the statues, you follow the engravings' instructions to retrieve the Bloody Knight's Skulls to prove yourself a hero and pass the first Knight's Code trial. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue on to the next Knight Statue</color> and solve the riddle of the next Knight's Code trial.",
    ["TaskDescription100008127"]="At the second statue, you learn about the trial of the code of glory. You place the Knightly Sword you got from the Bloody Knight in front of the statue and complete the second statue's trial. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the third statue</color> to check the next riddle.",
    ["TaskDescription100008128"]="At the third statue, you accept the trial of mercy. Having a heart filled with compassion for the world is an important part of the Knight's Code. You offer food to suffering souls and passed the statue's trial. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the next statue</color> to accept the next trial.",
    ["TaskDescription100008129"]="At the fourth statue, you answer a series of questions regarding the fourth Knight's Code, candor, and easily pass the Knight Statue's trial. Zachary excitedly tells you that you've completed half of the trials, and that you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the next statue</color> and work hard to solve the riddle.",
    ["TaskDescription100008130"]="Even knights born of the highest nobility should have a humble heart. The fifth statue's trial is a reminder to remember humility. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the sixth statue</color> and complete the next trial.",
    ["TaskDescription100008131"]="Standing before the sixth statue, you face the trial of \"sacrifice\" in which you must use fresh blood to awaken the unconscious Bloody Knight. You successfully use your own blood to do it, passing this statue's trial. Now it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the next statue</color> to complete its trial.",
    ["TaskDescription100008132"]="You recite \"Faith of Light\" without a hitch, solving the seventh statue's riddle for the code of will. However, Zachary tells you that this is where things will start to get difficult. It turns out that the eight statue was destroyed long ago, and even its base fell into a deep pit. There is no way to read the engraving and understand the trial's true meaning. Zachary suggests that you lie to the Archmage Statue and say that you've completed all eight of the code trials, but you firmly refuse. Unexpectedly, at the moment you refuse, the Archmage Statue suddenly shakes and indicates that you have completed the trial. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>hear Zachary tell you</color> what exactly happened.",
    ["TaskDescription100008133"]="After completing the Archmage Statue's trial for the Knight's Code and seeing fragments of Great Sage Barr Venter and Chivalry Commander Heinrich's history, you come to understand that the truth of Glast Heim's decline may have something to do with what happened in the sewers. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the entrance to the Glast Heim Sewer</color> to investigate.",
    ["TaskDescription100008134"]="You find a strange gem at the entrance to the Glast Heim Sewer. Following an odd dizzy spell, you see a person calling himself King Schmidt. He naturally thinks you to be his royal guard and commands you to escort him into the Glast Heim Sewer to search for the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. It's at this time that you realize that you may have traveled back in time. It seems all you can do to investigate the truth of Glast Heim civilization's disappearance is first <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort King Schmidt into the sewers</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008135"]="You and King Schmidt enter the sewers, where you encounter a Supervisor Sageworm watching over laboring slaves. He doesn't seem to recognize King Schmidt. Instead, he demands you two clean the torture devices. King Schmidt arrogantly states that he is a noble king, who will not heed the orders of those below him on such a degrading task. It looks like you have to be the one to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Writhing Rotten Meat</color> from the Supervisor Sageworm, then dig up some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Slimy Moss</color> by the corner of the wall.",
    ["TaskDescription100008136"]="You manage to get the Rotten Meat and dig up some Slimy Moss and give them to the supervisor. You ask the supervisor what the materials are for. The supervisor just laughs and says you'll know when it's done, then tells you to go fetch water from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lionheart Pool</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008137"]="You bring the water you drew from the Lionheart Pool to the supervisor. It turns out he's using these disgusting materials to make food for the prison laborers. He tells you to go <color=#CA2E0AFF>distribute it among the prisoners</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008138"]="You learn from the prison laborers that although their food is unbelievably disgusting, it will still be fought over every day. Some prisoners have already given up on eating in hopes of an earlier death. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>report back to the Supervisor Sageworm</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008139"]="King Schmidt orders you to kill Supervisor Sageworm. Feeling puzzled, you ask King Schmidt if this is for the miserable slaves, but the king denies it. He arrogantly states that he's doing it not for the slaves, only because the supervisor's discourtesy disgraced his majesty. And now, he orders you to continue <color=#CA2E0AFF>escorting him deeper into the sewers</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008140"]="You and King Schmidt encounter laborers Darens and Tyler deep in the sewers. You learn from them that they were once commoners of Glast Heim. Because their families lived in poverty, they accepted their current job and started working as slaves in the sewers. The heavy labor leaves them out of breath, and the supervisor's physical abuse has left them injured and exhausted. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bluegrass</color> to help them heal their wounds.",
    ["TaskDescription100008141"]="You deliver healing herbs to the two pitiful people. They're very grateful, but Darens tells you that because they've been significantly injured, they can't go maintain the boiler they were supposed to be maintaining. You decide to help Darens maintain the boiler. Since Darens has agreed, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go check on the boiler</color> now.",
    ["TaskDescription100008142"]="You follow the steps and methods as Darens taught you to maintain the boiler, but it can't run properly. Thus, Darens asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find another boiler</color>, think of a way to remove the spare pipe valve, and then use it to replace the one in the boiler that needs maintenance. Go find another boiler!",
    ["TaskDescription100008143"]="After you finally find the spare valve to replace the broken one in the boiler, you return to the civilian laborers, only to discover that King Schmidt, who has grown impatient, has killed them. The cruel King Schmidt also orders you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue escorting him</color> deeper underground to search for clues about the Fragment of Ymir's Heart.",
    ["TaskDescription100008144"]="When you and King Schmidt enter the Glast Heim Prison, you're immediately surrounded by hordes of prisoners. You wonder how these underground prisoners who seemed to have no memory of King Schmidt suddenly recovered their knowledge and hatred of him. What's going on here? Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask King Schmidt</color> about it.",
    ["TaskDescription100008145"]="After you repel the attacking prisoners, you suddenly discover that King Schmidt has disappeared. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> Glast Heim Prison and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the missing King Schmidt</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008146"]="You discover a mysterious wooden door in the prison, with a voice calling for help behind it. It might be King Schmidt, even though you haven't asked who the person behind the door is. Hearing the miserable screams coming from inside, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get the wooden door's key</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zombie Prisoner</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008147"]="The person you save from behind the wooden door isn't King Schmidt, but a prisoner who has been locked up for a long time. You must find King Schmidt as quickly as possible. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> the other areas to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the missing King Schmidt</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008148"]="You hear a mysterious voice calling for help in front of a torture device, but the torture device's bolts have long since rusted over, preventing you from opening it. Because of this, the mysterious voice tells you that a nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zombie Prisoner</color>'s <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Acid</color> should help remove the rust. Go get some from the Zombie Prisoner!",
    ["TaskDescription100008149"]="You release the mysterious captive from the torture device and discover that it's another locked-up criminal. Meanwhile, you still have no idea where the missing King Schmidt went. Out of desperation, you can only eliminate the released prisoner again and keep moving. Go find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing King Schmidt</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100008150"]="You hear another feeble cry for help coming from Glast Heim Prison's pile of gravel. The mysterious voice is gasping for breath as he asks you to help dig through the pile of gravel on his body. You have no time to ask about his identity. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>remove the pile of gravel</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008151"]="You rescue the trapped prisoner for the third time, but you still can't find a trace of King Schmidt. All you can do is eliminate the released prisoners again and again. At this time, you hear yet another voice calling for help. You don't know if it's the <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing King Schmidt</color>. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow the mysterious voice to find it</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100008152"]="After a thorough search, you finally find King Schmidt, besieged by a group of prisoners before a guillotine. After you rescue him, however, the confused King Schmidt runs away in panic. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color>, now!",
    ["TaskDescription100008153"]="You lead King Schmidt out of the Glast Heim Prison and enter the Glast Heim Churchyard. King Schmidt seems to have seen some pieces of memories he doesn't want to remember in the Glast Heim Churchyard, and these memories seem to send him into a frenzy. This sense of mind control and suffering from hallucinations seems to remind him of something. He asks you to go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the Afterimage of the Goddess Hermes</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008154"]="You find the Afterimage of the Goddess Hermes in the Tomb of the Dying Wish, but she just disappears after summoning three Rybios. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the Goddess' Afterimage</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100008155"]="You see the Afterimage of Goddess Hermes again in the Place of Remembrance, but just like last time, she disappears after summoning three Rybios to stop you. It seems <color=#CA2E0AFF>catching up to the Goddess' Afterimage</color> won't be an easy matter.",
    ["TaskDescription100008156"]="You finally see the Goddess' Afterimage once more beside the fountain, and you defeat the Rybios she summons. It would appear that you'd best return to King Schmidt and ask him why he wants to find the Goddess' Afterimage. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to King Schmidt</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008157"]="In front of the Goddess Statue in the Glast Heim Churchyard, you see King Schmidt crazed and repenting before the Goddess' Afterimage. The Goddess questions King Schmidt as to whether or not he remembers the pitiful way he begged and how the current situation was entirely King Schmidt's doing. Hermes uses the power of Ymir's Heart to make King Schmidt bear witness to the Demon King Morroc's invasion of Glast Heim when he destroyed everything and turned King Schmidt into the Dark Lord as he turned into the Valkyrie of Death. These fragments of history leave you shocked, and after a brief dizzy spell, you return to the present. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>relay</color> everything you witnessed to <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Eden Group Instructor Rockley</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008158"]="You tell the Eden Group Instructor about everything you saw. After some discussion, you feel that the hint the Dawn Goddess spoke of and the torrent of time and space may have another meaning. Your ability to travel through time and space may be the key to revealing the whole truth. To help you accurately time-travel back to when the Fragment of Ymir's Heart fell into the Demon King Morroc's hands, you find the time traveler Fulkyn. In an out-of-character moment, Fulkyn decides to lend you the Sands of Time. When you're ready to time travel to the day of the battle of Glast Heim, prepare yourself and <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the Sands of Time from Fulkyn</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008159"]="You successfully travel back to the day of the battle of Glast Heim. Together with the swordsman Thanatos and the mechanical magical girl Lucci, you defeat the Demon King Morroc and the Dark Lord and successfully retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Now, go <color=#CA2E0AFF>return the Sands of Time to Fulkyn</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100008160"]="You successfully get the Fragment of Ymir's Heart from the day of the battle of Glast Heim and return the Sands of Time to Fulkyn. Fulkyn tells you that he once witnessed the battle of Glast Heim during his time traveling, and he says that you are the one destined to get the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Because of this, he followed the path of fate and sent you back through the flow of history. Now, bring the Fragment of Ymir's Heart back to the Criatura Academy for safe keeping!",
    ["TaskDescription100009101"]="According to the Goddess’ revelation, the next Fragment of Ymir's Heart may be found in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aldebaran</color>, the frontier capital bordering the Republic of Shufiza. In order to retrieve the fragment, you ask W the way to Aldebaran...",
    ["TaskDescription100009102"]="With W’s help, you arrive at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>border crossing</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color>. Rumor has it that the only way to enter the republic’s territory is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>request an official pass</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009103"]="At the border crossing, you observe a large number of stranded travelers arguing with the guards. You quickly learn that applying for a pass is no simple matter nowadays. At that moment, you suddenly hear a cry of alarm erupt in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby crowd</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100009104"]="You help a traveler who was robbed near the port retrieve his luggage. Grateful, he tells you that the number of officially issued passes has plummeted. Now, people have no choice but to turn to other means. In his case, the one he obtained is from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Black Market Merchants</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009105"]="You seek out the Black Market Merchants stronghold and find them fretting over goods that were looted mid-journey. After prodding them, they agree to give you a free pass if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve</color> their <color=#CA2E0AFF>goods</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009106"]="After some investigating, you discover that the thief who robbed the Black Market Merchants is actually Goetia and her accomplices. After talking more with her, you learn that the guards have long been in cahoots with the Black Market Merchants. They not only smuggle illegal goods, but also secretly withhold passes that should be issued to the people, so that they can profit by selling them at marked up prices on the black market. This time, Goetia intercepted the <color=#CA2E0AFF>merchants’ goods</color>, but to her surprise...",
    ["TaskDescription100009107"]="In order to investigate the bizarre body hidden in the cargo box further, Goetia asks you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color> and seek out the help of a healer living near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hope Oasis</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009108"]="You find a strange note in the camp at Hope Oasis. The person who left the note seems to have gone to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest of the desert</color> in search of rare herbs. You decide to follow the instructions in the note and explore a little. Still, the curious penmanship feels oddly familiar...",
    ["TaskDescription100009109"]="In the Golem habitat of the northwestern desert, you save Wallace from being smashed to a pulp and relay a commission from Goetia to him. However, Wallace tells you he has more important things to do: namely, collecting a <color=#CA2E0AFF>sticky white scorpion eggs, wriggling severed Hode tail</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>slippery umbrella-shaped membrane</color>. He refuses to go anywhere until he finds these three things...",
    ["TaskDescription100009110"]="After an exhausting struggle, you finally manage to collect all the items Wallace needs. Surely now he’ll go with you to see Goetia, right?",
    ["TaskDescription100009111"]="After hearing that Goetia found a strange body in an unnatural state of death, Wallace changes his attitude and enthusiastically asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take him to Goetia</color> immediately.",
    ["TaskDescription100009112"]="You help Wallace carefully inspect the body in the cargo box. Surprisingly, you discover energy left by the Fragment of Ymir's Heart remaining inside. The clues seem to be coming together, yet there are still more questions than answers. To help retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, Goetia decides to go with you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet the Black Market Merchants</color> again.",
    ["TaskDescription100009113"]="You return to the Black Market Merchants stronghold, but faced with the prospect of a merciless beating at the hands of Goetia, the merchants turn to flee without a second thought. It looks like you'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring them back</color> yourself!",
    ["TaskDescription100009114"]="After being beaten to a pulp by Goetia, the Black Market Merchant is too afraid to hide anything. He confesses everything he knows about the goods and customer. Unfortunately, the mysterious buyer only used <color=#CA2E0AFF>letters</color> to contact the Black Market Merchant for each transaction and never showed up in person. Desperate for more clues, you angrily threaten the Black Market Merchant until he hands over a <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> with the time and place of the next exchange.",
    ["TaskDescription100009115"]="To your dismay, the culprit’s letter doesn’t contain any more clues. Goetia tells you that to continue investigating this matter, perhaps your best option is to proceed to the location written in the letter. Shuddering at Goetia’s chilling threats, the Black Market Merchants dutifully hand over a pass for the Republic of Shufiza. Finally, you can go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aldebaran</color>, just like you planned.",
    ["TaskDescription100009116"]="After a few twists and turns, you finally set foot in Aldebaran. According to the information in the letter, the culprit should have left the goods near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Southwest Quarter</color>, but when you finally reach it, you’re shocked by what awaits you...",
    ["TaskDescription100009117"]="You discover the goods guarded by a group of mecha in the Southwest Quarter of Aldebaran. Just as you start to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color>, something unexpected happens...",
    ["TaskDescription100009118"]="You never imagined that the purpose of the mecha wasn’t to guard the goods. Rather, it was to raze them to the ground! As you search for remaining clues, a Republican guard arrives to put out the roaring fire. However, he mistakes you for the arsonist. You find yourself frozen in place, stunned by the pillar of fire and the remains of the destroyed mecha, when suddenly, a message comes over the guard's transceiver requesting backup. Left with no choice, you proceed with him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Northwest Docks</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009119"]="In the Northwest Docks, you and the guard witness the mecha incinerate another batch of goods. Finally, the guard realizes that he misjudged you. He tells you that in recent months, many strange things have been happening in Aldebaran that have all of the guards on edge... As he talks, the transceiver on his waist sounds another piercing alarm. You learn that <color=#CA2E0AFF>East town</color> has also suffered a case of arson at the hands of the mecha. The guard begs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go support</color> the squad in his place.",
    ["TaskDescription100009120"]="After arriving in the Eastern Quarter, you rescue a guard who is left all alone. In order to prevent the fire from spreading to the surrounding houses, the soldier asks you to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>extinguish</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>flames</color> that are consuming the cargo boxes.",
    ["TaskDescription100009121"]="After putting out the fire, the guard sincerely thanks you. You tell him more about your body trafficking investigation. Intrigued, the guard offers to help you <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate the cargo boxes</color> and the remains of the mecha together.",
    ["TaskDescription100009122"]="You find a strange corpse in the remnants of the goods that looks very similar to the previous one. Now, you’re convinced that these goods are related to your investigation. The guard discovers a strange alchemy array in the remains of the mecha and suggests you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of the alchemy array</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take with you</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alchemists’ Guild</color> of Aldebaran to search for more clues.",
    ["TaskDescription100009123"]="You find an alchemist named Raymond and ask him about the alchemy array in the photo. Raymond tells you that it is indeed an advanced alchemy array capable of manipulating mecha, but he can't give you any more clues based on the photograph alone. After mentioning your corpse trafficking investigation and the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, Raymond offers to help assist you, so you go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>scene of the arson</color> once again...",
    ["TaskDescription100009124"]="With Raymond's help, you learn that the eerie corpse may have died from an alchemical technique called Spellbound. However, Raymond’s still suspicious about something. He asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look through</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>book</color> he’s carrying, which has a long entry under <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spellbound</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100009125"]="You and Raymond discuss at length about the suspected identity of the culprit, but come up with no clear-cut clues. In desperation, Raymond proposes another option: to collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>embedded chips</color> from the remains of the mecha, in order to obtain more information about Regenbeier, the company that manufactures them.",
    ["TaskDescription100009126"]="You agree with Raymond's idea and split up so you can head to the other two arson sites to collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>embedded chips</color> from the razed mecha.",
    ["TaskDescription100009127"]="To your surprise, there are still mecha that are partially functioning at the scene of the blaze. After destroying them, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>return</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raymond</color> with the chips <color=#CA2E0AFF>in hand</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009128"]="After obtaining the chips, Raymond draws a peculiar alchemy array on the ground, which, according to him, is a communication channel between the mecha and Regenbeier. Now, all you have to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100009129"]="A vicious war of words erupts between Raymond and the Regenbeier employees, which ends in a resounding victory for Raymond. You learn that the routes of the runaway mecha all intersect at the Clock Tower. In order to find out the truth, you decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go investigate</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009130"]="Even after gaining permission to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Clock Tower</color>, the guards at the entrance search you carefully before agreeing to let you in. You begin to realize that this glorious and vaulted structure may be hiding more than a few secrets that cannot be revealed. Hesitantly, you and Raymond walk through its towering doors...",
    ["TaskDescription100009131"]="As expected, after entering the tower you quickly find yourself in great peril. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Raymond</color> and make your way through as monsters come at you one after another...",
    ["TaskDescription100009132"]="As you <color=#CA2E0AFF>descend further into the depths of the tower</color>, you and Raymond defeat hordes of monsters standing in your way. But the truth, it seems, is still buried deeper...",
    ["TaskDescription100009133"]="Finally, you arrive at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>last floor</color>. However, you are met by an unexpected sight...",
    ["TaskDescription100009134"]="You discover a strange laboratory with a large number of mecha guarding it in the bottom level of the Clock Tower. In order to avoid alerting them and setting off their alarm, Raymond suggests simply cutting off their energy conduits and short circuiting them. In this way, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> in peace.",
    ["TaskDescription100009135"]="In the strange laboratory, you find a research journal signed by Lancaster Milton. Taken aback, Raymond informs you that this man was a member of the Alchemists’ Guild and an elite representative who was dispatched to Regenbeier’s Steel Capital Institute, where he took up a key position. However, during his appointment an accident occurred at the institute, after which Lancaster's whereabouts became unknown, together with a large amount of valuable research material... Now it seems that perhaps he directed those events himself in order to hide and study the forbidden arts. Intent on investigating further, Raymond takes out a pen and attempts to recreate the memory of the illusion in his research journal. By simply <color=#CA2E0AFF>touching the alchemy array</color>, you can enter the illusion and uncover the remnants of memories from the past...",
    ["TaskDescription100009136"]="In the first page of the memory, you see Lancaster wandering alone in a cemetery on the city outskirts. He’s carrying the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, whose power contains the soul of his deceased brother. However, Raymond doesn’t seem satisfied with this. He quickly draws up the next alchemy array and urges you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch</color> it and enter the memory quickly.",
    ["TaskDescription100009137"]="This time, you witness Lancaster's experiments. You see him place the Fragment of Ymir's Heart in various mecha in hopes of finding a way to fuse a soul with the mecha. However, Raymond seems disinterested in Lancaster's experiments and instructs you to focus on looking carefully for the whereabouts of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>. At his urging, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy array</color> on the next page of the journal and enter deeper into Lancaster’s memories...",
    ["TaskDescription100009138"]="You finally discover the whereabouts of the Fragment of Ymir's Heart in Lancaster's memories. It turns out that he actually put the fragment in his brother's beloved owl doll, in the hope of resurrecting him, and those strange corpses in the city are in fact the product of his soul leaving. However, you still feel that the truth of the matter hasn’t been fully unraveled. Despite your desire to continue the investigation, you’re strongly opposed by Raymond. He forcefully orders you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>set an ambush</color> and wait for Lancaster’s return...",
    ["TaskDescription100009139"]="After quietly biding your time, Raymond's plan is a success. However, Lancaster doggedly casts an alchemy spell and escapes in the nick of time. After being wounded, Lancaster leaves a pool of blood at the scene. As long as the <color=#CA2E0AFF>trail of blood</color> continues, catching Lancaster will only be a matter of time.",
    ["TaskDescription100009140"]="Lancaster doesn’t get very far. By the time you find him, he’s unconscious. Raymond suggests that you first find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>clotting grass</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>magic crystals</color> to heal him. Otherwise, you won't be able to get any information out of him.",
    ["TaskDescription100009141"]="You finish gathering the medicine, but find no trace of Raymond and Lancaster upon your return. You have a foreboding that you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the two men as soon as possible</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100009142"]="You realize that Raymond deliberately distracted you and stole away the mortally wounded Lancaster in order to claim the Fragment of Ymir's Heart for himself. Lancaster profusely expresses his gratitude for saving him from Raymond, but firmly tells you that he cannot hand over the fragment. Hopeful that you’ll trust a man in the midst of such suffering, he asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color> to a hidden place where he can confess the truth to you...",
    ["TaskDescription100009143"]="The route inside the Clock Tower is long and winding. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Lancaster</color> to the highest floor, curious about what exactly awaits you.",
    ["TaskDescription100009144"]="After climbing up to the highest floor, you come face to face with a demonic owl doll containing a human soul. To your surprise, it is somehow trapped in an invisible boundary created by Lancaster. Seeing that the doll is in an unstable state, Lancaster asks you to help him collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Witch</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Starsand</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Requiem Grass</color> to calm the doll’s restless spirit.",
    ["TaskDescription100009145"]="You gather the materials as instructed by Lancaster, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>present them to him</color>. Lancaster starts to prepare a tranquilizer that will subdue the demonic doll.",
    ["TaskDescription100009146"]="Finally, Lancaster tells you the truth. He deliberately stole the Fragment of Ymir's heart in order to return his deceased brother Aaron to this world. However, things didn't go as planned. After using the power of the fragment to place Aaron’s soul in the demonic doll, it invariably fell into a state of extreme rage, which could only be calmed by devouring the souls of the living. Initially, Lancaster condoned this behavior and even helped Aaron dispose of his victims' bodies in order to protect him. But as time went on, the magic owl doll became more and more powerful, and the intervals between his fits of rage became shorter and shorter. Finally, Lancaster realized that his actions were only quenching his brother’s thirst. In order to restore Aaron to his normal state, Lancaster began to carefully study the knowledge contained in the book. However, after it was snatched away by the monsters in an attack, he was left with nothing. Lancaster pleads with you to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>torn pages of the book</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009147"]="After several fierce battles, you finally retrieve all of the torn pages from the monsters. Now, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry back</color> to give the <color=#CA2E0AFF>torn pages</color> to Lancaster!",
    ["TaskDescription100009148"]="Together with Lancaster, you piece together the torn pages of the book. Finally, you can attempt to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read the reconstructed book</color> and determine the reason Aaron's soul is out of control.",
    ["TaskDescription100009149"]="Based on the book, you learn that the bouts of rage Aaron’s soul is suffering from are due to his torturous and unjust death. However, Lancaster tells you this simply can’t be possible. His brother Aaron was accidentally killed in the line of duty, and the Regenbeier Corporation even awarded a medal in his honor. You decide you have no choice but to investigate Aaron's death further. After a long pause, Lancaster tells you that perhaps the notebook Aaron left behind can help you. You will have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Clock Tower’s basement</color> and retrieve the <color=#CA2E0AFF>diary</color>, which is kept in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>carved wooden box</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009150"]="If you are able to locate the diary kept in Lancaster’s underground lab, return and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to him as soon as possible</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100009151"]="Upon seeing you return with the diary, an expression of grief spreads across Lancaster’s face. You realize that you may have uncovered something very painful. Suddenly, you remember the alchemy that Raymond previously used. If Lancaster recreates it, perhaps you can enter the memories and look for clues. Grateful for your kindness, Lancaster follows your instructions and draws the alchemy array. Now, all you need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch the alchemy array</color> and enter Aaron's memories.",
    ["TaskDescription100009152"]="You’re taken back to the day Lancaster was first admitted to the Alchemist's Guild. An excited Aaron is buying fish and freshly baked bread at the market. Next, you see him preparing a greeting card full of heartfelt wishes to celebrate his brother’s admission. However, the warm memories are like a sharp knife that pricks at Lancaster’s heart. Despite this, you don’t have time to keep dwelling on the past. Lancaster gathers himself and draws a new <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy formation</color> ready for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100009153"]="This time, the two brothers are no longer as close as before. You see a busy Lancaster, who has no time to go home, and notice a gnawing sadness inside Aaron as he realizes the burden he is on his brother. For the first time, Lancaster realizes the deep loneliness that has stricken Aaron. He feels a terrible sense of remorse, but now there’s no chance to make amends... Stunned, you feel helpless to comfort Lancaster. You can only continue to <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch<</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemy array</color> in the journal and help him investigate the truth behind all these events.",
    ["TaskDescription100009154"]="Unwilling to remain a burden, Aaron decides to grow stronger in order to secretly participate in the Regenbeier Corporation Guard Corps examination. After a prolonged period of training, he finally enlists in the Guard Corps. Lancaster feels both surprised and relieved, but upon further reflection still regrets his failure to truly understand Aaron... He feels a deep sense of regret that his brother had to pass away. All you can do is continue to <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch the alchemy array</color> and help him search for any remaining clues.",
    ["TaskDescription100009155"]="You enter Aaron's memories once again, only to find the course of events unfold in a bizarre and chaotic manner. You see Aaron being forcibly injected with a strange potion, which grants him great power, but makes him lose control of his senses. More importantly, you notice that the journal entries after this page are little more than strange scribbles whose meaning cannot be discerned. Lancaster finally realizes that perhaps the real cause of Aaron's death is related to the mysterious potion in his memories. At that moment, Raymond appears before your eyes with a large band of people...",
    ["TaskDescription100009156"]="Desperate to lay his hands on the Heart of Ymir, Raymond selfishly ignores the boundary Lancaster created and releases the demonic owl doll. He is killed almost instantly, but now you’re faced with no other choice but to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fight the demonic doll</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100009157"]="The owl doll is out-of-control! Due to the large number of souls its already consumed, you have no way of containing its immense power. You can only rely on Lancaster's alchemy to keep it from escaping. Lannister asks you to help him collect a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magebane Elixir</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Crystal</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Larkspur</color>. With these, he can find a way to diminish the demonic doll’s power.",
    ["TaskDescription100009158"]="Time is of the essence! Once you gather the materials Lancaster needs, <color=#CA2E0AFF>return as soon as possible</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100009159"]="To your shock, Lancaster’s plan to diminish the demonic doll’s power is to first take the poison and then induce the demotima to devour his soul, thus creating an opportunity for you to defeat it. You forcefully object, unwilling to let him sacrifice his life, but Lancaster cannot be dissuaded. His final wish is that he and Aaron can finally be at peace, rather than languishing in this vortex of pain. Ultimately, you have no option but to <color=#CA2E0AFF>respect his choice</color> and see him off together with Aaron...",
    ["TaskDescription100009160"]="Just as the goddess foresaw, you finally retrieve the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. However, you feel overwhelmed by the cost it took to win it back. With a conflicted heart, you return to the<color=#CA2E0AFF>Island of Idrus</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>place</color> the heavy <color=#CA2E0AFF>fragment</color> back on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010101"]="After recovering the eighth Fragment of Ymir's Heart, a new revelation from the Goddess took you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo</color>, a small island on the southern border. What excitement will this legendary holiday resort spot add to your journey?",
    ["TaskDescription100010102"]="Following your arrival on Comodo, W briefed you on the history and traditions of the island, as usual, and suggested you meet Lady Alexia at the Leader Mansion, since she came upon the rather concerned Vendra, Head of the Euphonic Symphony, who obviously had important issues to report to Alexia not long ago. Taking W's advice, you accidentally interfered with Alexia and Vendra's conversation, learning that the island has been plagued by unusual raids lately, and all clues pointed to the long-dormant dragons. Alexia, seemingly bothered, was reluctant to look too much into it, whereas Vendra was the polar opposite. Ultimately, you decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Vendra</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go together</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color>, where the incidents occurred...",
    ["TaskDescription100010103"]="You and Vendra came to Zenhai Marsh to investigate the attacks on Comodo. You began with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>weird footprints</color> scattered around the scene of the crime...",
    ["TaskDescription100010104"]="You discovered giant claw marks and scales at the scene. Vendra indicated they matched the dragons that vanished a long time ago. She suggested you <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Encyclopedia of Ancient Monsters</color> for reference.",
    ["TaskDescription100010105"]="After perusing the information for the book, you realized Vendra's conclusion wasn't unfounded. Thought many clues on site pointed to the dragons as the culprit, you believed you still lack decisive evidence. Following your suggestions, Vendra and you continued southward, expanding the search. Shortly after, a piece of deadwood which caught on fire drew your attention. You must <color=#CA2E0AFF>get clear water</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>douse</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>flame</color> to continue your effort...",
    ["TaskDescription100010106"]="Something unexpected happened... No matter how much water you scrounged, you couldn't put the fire out. Vendra pondered, then asked you to accompany her <color=#CA2E0AFF>to the Papuchicha Forest</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>physician</color> in the charge of healing the raid victims for her opinion.",
    ["TaskDescription100010107"]="The conversation with the physician revealed that all the victims suffered major burns. Also, ordinary treatments were ineffective and only the Millennial Frost from the western cave could heal the injuries. This prompted Vendra to lock in the dragons as the prime suspect, for only the dragon flame would cause that consequence. As you questioned why would the dragons attack now, Vendra asked you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the injured</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010108"]="You and Vendra checked on the injured, and there was no damage other than burns. Vendra no longer thought it was just a common raid, but possibly entailed the pact between humans and dragons. Following her suggestion, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>returned to the Leader Mansion</color> for the time being and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report it to Alexia</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010109"]="Surprisingly, after reporting your findings, Alexia and Vendra had a disagreement, with the former strongly advocating a diplomatic stance against the dragon provocation, even swallowing pride to placate them. Under <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alexia's</color> insistence, you were forced to <color=#CA2E0AFF>cave in to her demands</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010110"]="Alexia pinned her hopes on more offerings to mollify the dragons. She requested you to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>10</color> each of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chewy Scale Stems</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tender Frog Legs</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crispy Bug Whiskers</color> as <color=#CA2E0AFF>offerings</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>submit</color> to the dragons.",
    ["TaskDescription100010111"]="Once the offerings have been collected, Alexia once again requested you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the dragons' cave on the west side of the island</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>vacate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tourists and explorers</color> inside.",
    ["TaskDescription100010112"]="In the lair, you met Hardy, a merchant who mined Dragon Flame Amber for a living. After helping him recover lost crystals, he left the premise as requested. But your quest wasn't over yet, as many people still lingered in the makeshift camps near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cave mouth</color>. Among them, you spotted a <color=#CA2E0AFF>well-dressed middle-aged man</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010113"]="Bronte, a traveling Arunafeltz noble, told you he came here to see the legendary ice chasm and the frozen fleet. After you took photos of the two sites for Bronte, he left as promised. Lastly, you zeroed in on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eden Group members</color> who had been squatting and shoveling in a corner like there was nobody around...",
    ["TaskDescription100010114"]="Once you confirmed the cave is free of visitors, you decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Leader Mansion</color> and report to Alexia.",
    ["TaskDescription100010115"]="En route back to the Leader Mansion, you ran into Vendra who's been waiting for you. She and you shared the same notion that the dragons didn't attack the people on Comodo for food. At Vendra's beseech, you joined her in investigating the dragons' reemergence. First of all, you must use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>heat-resistant crystal bottle</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> a batch of <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragon flame samples</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010116"]="To identify your dragon flame samples, you and Vendra went <color=#CA2E0AFF>to Hermit's Village</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek help</color> from the eccentric alchemist, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grantham</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010117"]="Upon arriving in Hermit's Village, you and Vendra inadvertently intervened in an assassination plot targeting Grantham. But despite saving his life, the eccentric alchemist still refused your request. Fortunately, he was very intrigued by the dragon flame, so you <color=#CA2E0AFF>handed him the sample</color> and asked him to aid your investigation.",
    ["TaskDescription100010118"]="Grantham agreed to help, but he named the bottle of samples as his price. Once the consensus has been reached, you proceeded to gather the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tri Joint's Shell</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nereid's Poison Gland for him</color> required to analyze the sample. The truth is coming out...",
    ["TaskDescription100010119"]="Through you and Vendra, the cunning Grantham confirmed the reason behind dragons' reemergence is the Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart. Meanwhile, the greed he exhibited began to concern you, until Vendra timely interrupted the conversation...",
    ["TaskDescription100010120"]="Leaving Grantham's cabin, you and Vendra had a long talk which revealed she knew who you really are and wished to use your power to change the status quo on the island. You were touched by young lady's sincerity, let alone that your mission was to locate the fragments. You discussed and realized the target of the raids didn't make sense, as the dragons bypassed the thriving capital and Papuchicha Forest in favor of Zenhai Marsh that's much more remote. To unravel the mystery, you once again revisited <color=#CA2E0AFF>the vacant lot to the southwest of the marsh</color>, the site of the very first attack...",
    ["TaskDescription100010121"]="Following a thorough search, you and Vendra found a strange mound of deadwood that might be hiding a secret or two. Vendra suggested making an improvised explosive out of <color=#CA2E0AFF>sulfur powder</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Landfrost</color> to remove the unbudgeable logs.",
    ["TaskDescription100010122"]="Vendra made a <color=#CA2E0AFF>small explosive</color> out of what you scrounged. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>light</color> the fuse and run!",
    ["TaskDescription100010123"]="The hefty logs blew up to reveal a <color=#CA2E0AFF>bottomless pit</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010124"]="Readied, you and Vendra rappelled down the pit on a rope. Unexpectedly, a narrow corridor led to an ancient lair inhabited by dragons. Besides, you noticed a large sum of eggs on verge of incubating... With the truth close at hand, you opted to continue <color=#CA2E0AFF>deeper into the lair</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find conclusive proof of the dragons' intent</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010125"]="Finally, you and Ventra discovered the map marking attack routes for the dragons deeper in the cave, as well as the horde of monsters controlled by dragon flame. Vendra informed you that the dragons did the same to fight mankind a thousand years back. Now, they're trying it again. What you can do is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>alert Alexia</color> as soon as possible and hope she'll make a decision befitting her leader status.",
    ["TaskDescription100010126"]="Even though you brought back convincing proof of the dragons' ambition, you didn't expect Alexia to not only adhere to the pact signed by Margaret, but sent emissaries to negotiate peace with them, sacrificing islanders' rights for their withdrawal. That escalated into a heated argument between Vendra and Alexia. Ultimately, news of a failed peace talk incensed Alexia so much, that she blamed it on you two trespassing the cave and forbade you from further Comodo affairs...",
    ["TaskDescription100010127"]="During the quarrel, Nerius family guard brought shocking news: Upon learning the dragons' impending campaign, Alexia's youngest daughter Cecilla took her personal guards to the frontline, vowing to defend her home. A thoroughly disappointed Vendra expressed that she wasn't going to wait for Alexia to change her mind, and she and her Euphonic Symphony will live and die with Comodo. You cannot stay out of this war, of course. Responding to Vendra's request, you set off <color=#CA2E0AFF>for Zenhai Marsh</color> to aid Princess Cecilia...",
    ["TaskDescription100010128"]="Zenhai Marsh was in chaos from the invasion. You found Princess Cecilia and expressed your intention. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>fought together</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>opposed</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>army of monsters</color> pouring out of the lair...",
    ["TaskDescription100010129"]="You defended the first wave of attack in a fierce battle racked with heavy casualties. Princess Cecilia sent her guard Kurulus to infiltrate the cave and brought back Millennial Frost, then refined it through ancient techniques into <color=#CA2E0AFF>ice dew</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>usable</color> for <color=#CA2E0AFF>healing</color> those <color=#CA2E0AFF>burned by dragon flame</color> in the battle...",
    ["TaskDescription100010130"]="After regrouping, the situation in Zenhai Marsh started to improve. Cecilia heard the Euphonic Symphony was fighting the dragons in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color> and expressed her concerns. Hence, you offered to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reinforce</color> them.",
    ["TaskDescription100010131"]="Just as Cecilia expected, the battle in Papuchicha Forest isn't going well. You got there just in time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>heal the wounded</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>fend off enemies</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010132"]="You helped the Euphonic Symphony stabilize the situation in Papuchicha Forest. Now it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Zenhai Marsh</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report to Cecilia</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010133"]="You returned to Zenhai Marsh to see Cecilia has been injured in a battle. Considering her status, you suggested taking her home to convalesce, only for her to reject with righteous fury. She had made up her mind to live and die with Comodo, and never give in to the dragons. Meanwhile, she entrusted you with her <color=#CA2E0AFF>cape embroidered with the Nerius crest</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give to Alexia</color>. You found it impossible not to bend to her will and prayed her mother would understand...",
    ["TaskDescription100010134"]="Cecilia's actions were very admirable, but as a daughter, she hurt Alexia's feelings. At the moment, it wasn't just a mother standing before you. She refused to face reality. You could only <color=#CA2E0AFF>unfold</color> Cecilia's <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> in hope that she sees Cecilia's perspective.",
    ["TaskDescription100010135"]="Cecilia's effort finally made Alexia realize her mistakes. She resolved to no longer avoid her duty as the leader and be responsible for Comodo's future. With suggestions from Kurulus, you and Alexia went to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kokomo Beach</color> to seek the pirates' aid. It was time to fight back!",
    ["TaskDescription100010136"]="You and Alexia came to Kokomo Beach to negotiate with the local pirates. Surprisingly, the allegedly barbaric pirate leader turned out to be chivalrous enough to accept Alexia's proposal to fight the dragons with Nerius. Next, you headed for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east of Saint Darmain</color> to see the Eden Group.",
    ["TaskDescription100010137"]="Instructor Salisbury of the Eden Group gladly accepted your proposal. As an archaeologist, he felt incredibly honored to experience history on Comodo firsthand. Now, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Papuchicha Forest</color> and meet up with everybody.",
    ["TaskDescription100010138"]="After soliciting the aid of pirates and Eden Group, Alexia tasked you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Hermit's Village</color> and attempt <color=#CA2E0AFF>to find more ways to deal with the dragons.</color> She also wanted to take the opportunity to apologize to a close friend in person...",
    ["TaskDescription100010139"]="Revisiting Hermit's Village, the first person you went to see was Grantham. He once again tried to entice you to cough up the Fragment of Ymir's Heart. After you rebuffed him, he promised to give you a precious invisibility potion if you would <color=#CA2E0AFF>don</color> his <color=#CA2E0AFF>manteau</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>disguised as him</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>draw assassins</color> out and <color=#CA2E0AFF>kill them</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010140"]="After getting the Invisibility Potion from Grantham, your next objective is the best hunter in Hermit's Village, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raphael</color> the Ranger. But rumor has it he's obsessed with hunting...",
    ["TaskDescription100010141"]="You won the secret to crafting Ice Trap from Raphael by winning a hunting game. Now, the only person left to visit is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Libec the Whitesmith</color> residing on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>easternmost end of the swamp</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010142"]="Expectedly, the artisan is another oddball. He guaranteed the Fire-proof Manteau he made would work against dragon flame. As long as you could get him the <color=#CA2E0AFF>White Mist Moss</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nereid's Poison Gland</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alligator's Thorny Skin</color>, he'd enchant the cape and lend it to you.",
    ["TaskDescription100010143"]="You've endeavored to win Invisibility Potion, Fire-proof Manteau, and the secret to making Ice Traps. Although their effectiveness in battle is yet to be seen, at least you didn't let Alexia down. Now is time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry to Papuchicha Forest</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100010144"]="You held a strategic meeting in Papuchicha Forest. According to Eden Group's report, the opposition is led by a half-dragon, half-man monster, who unified the dragons under the promise of obtaining the very Fragment of Ymir's Heart you're searching for. Seeing her forces are at a disadvantage given the monsters' presence, Alexia realized she must risk a quick resolution. Vendra showed the map you two found in the lair. The advance routes offered insight for you to use their secret passages against them, sending four separate armies to strike behind the enemy line, while ambushing the big dragons guarding the cave with Ice Trap, before reassembling the forces to target the now-isolated Mutant Dragonoid. To ensure everything goes as planned, Vendra asked you to help her collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sulfur Powder</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Landfrost</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wood</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>make</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Firework Launchers </color> for sending signals...",
    ["TaskDescription100010145"]="You and Vendra made enough Firework Launchers for everybody. Next up, Ice Trap big enough to hold an Ancient Dragon. Following Raphael's instructions, you gathered <color=#CA2E0AFF>Permafrost Crystals</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Numbing Slime</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fishhooks</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010146"]="Everything is ready for war. As the owner of the fireproof manteau, you're placed in charge of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dragons' cave entrance</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Comodo</color> by Alexia. That is the only access known to humans, so it would reasonably be heavily defended by dragons. As a reward, Alexia promised you that the Wind Fragment of Ymir's Heart is yours if the Mutant Dragonoid is defeated.",
    ["TaskDescription100010147"]="Under Salisbury's lead, you reached the dragons' cave on the west side of Comodo and set off the silent signal firework to herald the operation. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>put on</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fireproof manteau</color> and get to work...",
    ["TaskDescription100010148"]="Inside the cave, you saw a lot of dragon eggs on both sides of the passage. Recalling Alexia's request, you ask Salisbury for means to destroy the eggs. He informed you only the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Corrosive Acid</color> of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Megalith</color> could dissolve the hard shells.",
    ["TaskDescription100010149"]="The eggs shattered under the Corrosive Acid. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Onward</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100010150"]="You continued as planned, but ran into a horde of Gargoyles guarding the eggs in the lair of dragonlings. Salisbury suggested using <color=#CA2E0AFF>Piranha flesh</color> as bait and finishing them all at once!",
    ["TaskDescription100010151"]="Exactly as Salisbury predicted, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Piranha flesh</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>placed</color> on the ground attracted many Gargoyles, now too busy devouring to notice you approaching silently with weapons drawn...",
    ["TaskDescription100010152"]="After slaying the guardian monsters, you repeat the process of <color=#CA2E0AFF>dousing Corrosive Acid on the shells</color> to destroy the eggs, though the pride of an archaeologist made it hard to endure for Salisbury...",
    ["TaskDescription100010153"]="The incident didn't stop you from marching forward. Before you knew it, you were close to the Ancient Dragon's location. Salisbury led you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hide beneath the slope</color> and quietly observe the Ancient Dragon's route...",
    ["TaskDescription100010154"]="You and Salisbury <color=#CA2E0AFF>set up</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Traps</color> along the dragon's route, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gathered</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>snow to cover the tracks</color>. Now, you wait for the trap to trigger...",
    ["TaskDescription100010155"]="The trap went off and the Ancient Dragon is immobilized! Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>deal it the fatal blow</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100010156"]="You fulfilled the arduous mission, but the final showdown has yet to come. Continue <color=#CA2E0AFF>northward</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>rendezvous</color> with <color=#CA2E0AFF>your fellows</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100010157"]="You finally reached the rendezvous point only to discover the casualty was higher than you imagined. But sneak attacks wouldn't work twice, so if you backed out now, you just might lose permanent ground. For the Fragment of Ymir's Heart, you offered to <color=#CA2E0AFF>imbibe the Invisibility Potion</color> to slip past the monster legion guarding the Dragon Bridge for a duel against the Mutant Dragonoid...",
    ["TaskDescription100010158"]="Thanks to the Invisibility Potion, you crossed the Dragon Bridge and reached the Mutant Dragonoid...",
    ["TaskDescription100010159"]="The fierce battle ended with the proud Mutant Dragonoid falling at your feet. You retrieved the fragment, but what he said resonated with you. What was the reason for the war to slay dragons a thousand years ago? Probably only the Ancient Dragon and Margaret Nerius knew for sure. Now, though, it's time to complete your mission and get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragment of Ymir's Heart</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100010160"]="After taking the fragment back from the Mutant Dragonoid, you said farewell to Vendra and Alexia and <color=#CA2E0AFF>returned home</color> with the mission unfinished. You expected Goddess Brunhild to be awaiting your return at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heart Pedestal</color> as usual...",
    ["TaskDescription100011101"]="After finishing a Human vs. Dragon battle that is epic enough to be included in the history, you finally seize back the ninth Fragment of Ymir's Heart. The Goddess is pleased with your improvement, but she has to urge you to keep moving forward as she senses the last Fragment of Ymir's Heart resides to the west of this continent, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Umbala</color>, a legendary place connected to the Realm of the Dead. You are still in the dark about what awaits you this time.",
    ["TaskDescription100011102"]="Here you are in Umbala, and you learn about many recent disasters has happened in the rainforest from W. To find out the truth, you pay Karkatan, the lord of the Utan tribe, a visit. It's said that their tribe has been living in this place since the beginning of time, and they are the most devout worshippers of the Yggdrasil. Karkatan tells you the root cause of the rainforest turning into how it is today is because the sacred relic of the Utan tribe is lost. You realize the Sacred Relic they mentioned is the last Fragment of Ymir's Heart, and you offer them help in retrieving it. Karkatan accepts your offer, but he tells you before you do so, you must go to Luluka Forest and tell Tatanka, the wizard, about this. In the belief of the Utan tribe, a wizard is the carrier of Yggdrasil's will, and no one shall ever go against the wizard's order and act on one's behalf.",
    ["TaskDescription100011103"]="Once you step into the Luluka Forest, you are shocked by the blemished scenery before you even start to find Tatanka. On the way there, you encounter a Dragon Tail that is attacked by a Driller. After saving it, it asks you to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>check on the larvae near the riverbed</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011104"]="In the riverbed, you discover those larvae corroded by Strange Crystals. Once again, Dragon Tail begs for your help to save its children by <color=#CA2E0AFF>taking off its wings</color> and go exchange for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Revival Potion</color> with the human merchant. It's said that this is the only way to dissolve Strange Crystals.",
    ["TaskDescription100011105"]="Who would have thought this shady merchant, Sanja, marked up the price during the crisis? Besides the wings of Dragon Tail, he also wants the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juicy Grape</color> from the forest for the deal to exchange for Revival Potion, which leaves you no options but to comply with his offer. You set off to the south of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Luluka Forest</color> to search for Juicy Grape.",
    ["TaskDescription100011106"]="You counter a group of Choco that is fighting for food. After stopping them from killing each other, they tell you that after the elemental storm corroded the Luluka Forest, a savior wears a weird mask and has been helping them ever since. Not only provided food to them, but he also taught those shady human merchants a lesson. You have a feeling that this savior might be Tatanka, the wizard of the Utan tribe you are looking for. But before that, you must get the Revival Potion from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sanja</color> and save the Dragon Tail Larvae.",
    ["TaskDescription100011107"]="With your help, Dragon Tail and its kids are finally safe. You ask them about the clues of the savior and learn that he set off to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>north of the forest</color> in a rush not a while ago...",
    ["TaskDescription100011108"]="Near the lake in the forest, you find the savior everyone is talking about, and it turns out to be Tatanka, the wizard of the Utan tribe. But the conversation doesn't go anywhere since he strongly refuses the suggestion to retrieve the sacred relic. You can't help but switch topics and help him craft potions, hoping it will break the ice. In return, Tatanka introduces all these ancient Umbala legends to you. It turns out serval heirlooms of different elements protect this rainforest, and they forge the restraint and reinforcement on one another to maintain the elemental balance of Umbala. But one of them, Water Heart, was destroyed during the element storm... All of a sudden, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Miwa</color> rushes back and interrupts the conversation.",
    ["TaskDescription100011109"]="This Miwa is here to ask for Tatanka's help. Your group follows and sets off with Miwa and discovers that a large number of people in the tribe went into a coma because of exhaustion. Under Tatanka's guidance, you and Miwas gathered a lot of materials that can be used for potion-crafting. There's no time to lose, <color=#CA2E0AFF>delivery these materials to Tatanka</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription100011110"]="With Tatanka's explanation, you learn that the reason for the collapse is due to the constant energy transfer to the Spirit Tree. Since the Water Heart is destroyed, Spirit Tree is gradually decaying day after day, and it's like a pot with a hole that is impossible for the energy to be filled to the brim and recover. Meanwhile, Miwa mentions that their ex-leader, Higurashi, has disbanded all the Spirit Tree guards and said there is a last resort to save the Spirit Tree. Tatanka seems to realize something and hastily walks toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>the lake center of the Spirit Tree</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011111"]="You find the leader of Miwa, Higurashi, on the island at the lake's center. It wants to transfer the corrupted part of the Spirit Tree onto itself to save the mother tree. You all try to stop it but are tangled up by the illusion it casts. Higurashi is about to finish the ritual. All of a sudden...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011112"]="At the last moment of the channeling, the Spirit Tree emits a ray of dazzling light. You hear a gentle voice asking you to water her with the Mirror Lake Water. Seems like nobody but you can hear this voice, and you wonder whether it's the Spirit Tree talking to you. To confirm, you ignore Tatanka, get to the lakeside, and start <color=#CA2E0AFF>drawing the water from the lake</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011113"]="Upon moisturizing the Spirit Tree, she recognizes the power that flows within your blood. She is the offspring of the Yggdrasil, so she is innately familiar with Odin's power. During your conversation with her, the Spirit Tree admits that the Water Heart wasn't destroyed by the elemental storm but by herself. While in shock, you question her the reason for this, but she seems not to bother answering you. She wants you to get Miwa off this place since Luluka Forest is not what it used to be, a place that was full of energy. Unwillingly, you head back and report all these to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tatanka</color>, and he decides to take action in an unusual way to unmask the truth if the Spirit Tree isn't talking. To this end, he plans to cast a spell named Memory Materialization. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stand before him when you are ready</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100011114"]="Through Tatanka's spell, you all see the memory of the Spirit Tree—It was the vision that she saw from the Mirror Lake, which can see through the future, showed her groups and groups of Miwa scarify themselves in the storm for the sake of saving the forest. She then decided to replace herself in the position of Miwas and caused the destruction of the Water Heart. You admire Spirit Tree's greatness, but Tatanka, on the other side, thinks something is out of place and seems like someone has forged the vision of the Mirror Lake and made the Spirit Tree destroy the Water Heart. To prove his hypothesis, you must get him some water samples by <color=#CA2E0AFF>drawing Mirror Lake Water</color> and some potion materials.",
    ["TaskDescription100011115"]="If you have all the materials Tatanka needs, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to him</color> at once and prove his hypothesis!",
    ["TaskDescription100011116"]="Under Tatanka's guidance, you conduct a test on the Mirror Lake Water and find out the water contains an absurd amount of psychedelic potion. Other than that, Tatanka seems to be getting resourceful clues <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby Mirror Lake</color> while you are gathering materials.",
    ["TaskDescription100011117"]="At the side of Mirror Lake, Tatanka discovers a vast area of vegetation that was corrupted by the taint of the abyss and a piece of cloth left by someone. You guys find out this piece of cloth contains the same type of psychedelic potion as the Mirror Lake Water, and every single piece of evidence validates Tatanka's theory. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to the Spirit Tree</color> and reveal the truth to her...",
    ["TaskDescription100011118"]="The decision of the Spirit Tree still hangs in the air, but there's one thing for sure: she will not give up those Miwa who have followed her here. Through your persuasion, Tatanka finally gains back the hope of retrieving the sacred relic. He invites you to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kalala Swamp</color> with him to double-check on the Wind Heart condition, and you agree...",
    ["TaskDescription100011119"]="Arriving at the Kalala Swamp connected to Luluka Forest, Tatanka tells you that the heirloom here is named Wind Heart. It's kept by the Wootan tribe, who have ruled the forest for generations. To check on the condition of Wind Heart, you both must <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass through the forest</color> and head to Wootan territory.",
    ["TaskDescription100011120"]="While passing through Kalala Swamp, you guys encounter a group of Wootan Warriors who are transporting weird cargo. The sharp-eyed Tatanka discovers the bags are full of Beetle King's corpses, but according to the warrior, these Beetle Kings died from a plague, and they should be cremated as soon as possible to prevent the disease from spreading in the soil. Both of you find this fishy and decide to tag along discreetly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>going</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>east of the forest</color> where these Beetle Kings are quarantined at...",
    ["TaskDescription100011121"]="To the east of the forest, you notice the Wootan tribe has locked up many sick Beetle Kings. On top of that, the surrounding plants seem to be inflected by some weird disease as well. To confirm the cause, Tatanka asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some plant samples for him</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011122"]="After defeating the Wootan Warrior, you force him to go over the detail of these Beetle Kings. He tells you that a weird gust of wind brought these beetles here a few weeks ago, and they were already infected before they got here. The crisis is emerging in the forest, but the leader, Uba, seems to not care about it, hiding inside its cave. To get to the bottom of this, you set off to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>rock cavern</color> where Uba resides...",
    ["TaskDescription100011123"]="Inside the rock cavern, you discover a large amount of strange traces. It almost seems like someone let out their rage hysterically here. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Uba</color>, who has gone mad, is at the deepest end of the cavern. It appears that it is trapped in a manic state. It's questionable whether it can still <color=#CA2E0AFF>communicate</color> with any of you...",
    ["TaskDescription100011124"]="Tatanka casts Memory Materialization on Uba, who has lost its mind, but it fails to read its memory. When the target harbors an unresolvable knot inside its heart, the memory is sealed away along with self-consciousness, which is why the Memory Materialization failed to replicate it. At this point, to reveal the hidden memory of the target, the only way is to untie the knot. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Outside the cavern</color>, things are getting hectic and noisy...",
    ["TaskDescription100011125"]="You go outside the cavern to check out what's going on, and surprisingly, you see those quarantined Beetle Kings have started a riot, charging toward the cavern where Uba is located. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tatanka</color> is currently inside the cavern, trying to resolve the knot inside Uba's heart...",
    ["TaskDescription100011126"]="You describe all the details outside the cavern to Tatanka, and he states that all the chaos must be ended by Uba. He wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>buy him more time</color> before he successfully resolves the knot using Memory Materialization.",
    ["TaskDescription100011127"]="After holding off waves of attacks, Tatanka finally managed to find the sealed memory on Uba! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hurry back to Tatanka</color> and see what exactly is going on with Uba!",
    ["TaskDescription100011128"]="You see everything in Uba's memory. The Wind Heart is actually the Wootan chief's heart, and it switches its attributes according to the owner. Uba has made an irreversible mistake under the deception of a mystery man who holds sole responsibility for the plague. Nobody can resolve this matter but Uba itself, with its determination. The only thing you can do right now is to dig out the culprit behind everything. Tatanka sets his eyes on the soil brought by the mystery man and wants you to get him some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Spirit Flowers</color> to prove everything...",
    ["TaskDescription100011129"]="As soon as the Holy Spirit Flowers, which were pure white, turned dark upon touching the soil brought by the mystery man. Tatanka states the soil contains toxic substances from the poisonous glacier, Hvergelmir, in the Realm of the Dead. Every piece of evidence indicates that the culprit is from the Realm of the Dead, and Tatanka even tells you that there is one last piece of evidence in his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wizard Cottage</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011130"]="After investigating the condition of Water Heart and Wind Heart, Tatanka shows you the flame he kept inside his room. This piece of evidence fully convince you the fact that the culprit came from the Realm of the Dead. In order to retrieve the sacred relic, you and Tatanka <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the lord's hut</color> and ask Karkatan to open up the gate to the Niflheim.",
    ["TaskDescription100011131"]="Tatanka reminds you that before entering Niflheim, both of you must take a medicine called Pill of Undeath to conceal the odor of living beings to avoid getting caught by the matrix of Niflheim. In order to craft the Pill of Undeath, Tatanka wants you to collect the required materials and <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand them over</color> once you are done!",
    ["TaskDescription100011132"]="Everything is ready to go! Take the Pill of Undeath and meet up with Karkatan! He is expecting both of you <color=#CA2E0AFF>before the entrance to the Realm of the Dead</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100011133"]="You start to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Tatanka</color> after parting with Karkatan to this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Niflheim</color>, a place filled with the taint of the dead. You begin the search for the sacred relic in this land of peril...",
    ["TaskDescription100011134"]="Upon arriving in Niflheim, you encounter a group of patrolling soldiers. If it wasn't Tatanka's idea that you disguise as a new recruit who doesn't know the drills, the plan would have been exposed by now. But you are now forced to join the boot camp for the new recruits. Now, follow the officer's instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the training ground</color>. Otherwise...",
    ["TaskDescription100011135"]="After some miserable training, you finally get the armband representing the Scouting Regiment. Tatanka thinks this is a great opportunity to gather intel on the sacred relic's whereabouts. Suddenly, an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Woman</color> shows up and interrupts this conversation...",
    ["TaskDescription100011136"]="As the new members of the Scouting Regiment, somehow, you two are forced to handle a case of civil dispute. After settling the dispute, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tatanka</color> calls you aside, and there is <color=#CA2E0AFF>something he wants to tell you</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100011137"]="Tatanka warns you not to mind other businesses other than the search for the sacred relic, but you can't help yourself but offer assistance to someone in need when you see one. Good karma pays back! After talking to a sobbing undead, not only do you obtain the clues about the sacred relic, but you also knock the hell out of the undead, who almost exposes your identity. Now, following the clue you gained and <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry to the tavern</color> and look for a group of soldiers who guard the sacred relic to get more intel on it...",
    ["TaskDescription100011138"]="Apparently, the soldiers in the tavern are having a bit too much of drinks, which makes you overhear the conversation without breaking a sweat. It's said that the Queen's new sacred relic is a stolen piece from the World of the Living, done by two of her mighty subordinates. Now, these two subordinates are resting on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ice bridge over the Gjoll</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011139"]="On the ice bridge over the Gjoll, you overhear the conversation of the servants about the sacred relic. It turns out the Utan tribe's sacred relic is being placed inside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hel's Temple</color> and is highly secured. For this, you two set off and <color=#CA2E0AFF>see what's going on there</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100011140"]="The smooth process of breaking into the temple seems a bit too easy, almost like it's meant for you to be here, like a trap. But Tatanka doesn't listen to you and is keen on getting into the temple. Not to your surprise, Hel has set up a besiege, and both of you become the prisoners of the Underworld. This Queen, however, isn't going to execute you two just like that. She is sort of excited and invites you two to <color=#CA2E0AFF>join</color> the grandest celebration of the Niflheim—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Grand Celebration</color>. She then promises that if both of you <color=#CA2E0AFF>survive until the end</color>, she then will return the sacred relic. You guys have no options but to comply with her offer...",
    ["TaskDescription100011141"]="On the Undead Arena, you and Tatanka withstand waves and waves of the undead, but the Pill of Undeath's effect has been restraining your strength. And suddenly...?!",
    ["TaskDescription100011142"]="The Odin's power in your blood is awakened while you are in desperate straits. Hel soon recognizes your identity, but what surprises you more is that Tatanka chooses to turn his back on you and offer Hel a deal to trade you for the sacred relic of the Utan tribe. With the hatred Hel holds against the Aesir, there is no doubt you will suffer in extreme agony once you fall under her custody. Hel has not yet accepted the offer, and a group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>raging soldiers</color> starts to charge toward you and Tatanka because they consider Tatanka has disrespected and intimidated their Queen by making such a deal...",
    ["TaskDescription100011143"]="Not to your surprise, Hel accepts the offer. But she's more interested in this partner-betrayal drama than anything, and she keeps asking you for details about how Tatanka lured you into this trap. Tatanka, on the other side, looks pretty calm. He admits that he lies to you and doesn't deserve your forgiveness; he must carry on his duty as the wizard of the Utan tribe, just like how you're the successor of Odin's bloodline. Now, you can do nothing about it but be the chips on the table. Before closing the deal, Hel wants both of you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany her to retrieve the sacred relic</color> since it has been given to another person...",
    ["TaskDescription100011144"]="Hel takes you and Tatanka in front of a dimensional gap. It's said that this gap leads to a nameless island in Midgard, where the sacred relic is currently located at. Before setting off, Hel orders Tatanka to make sure you take the Potent Pill of Undeath because she thinks Tatanka is scheming and not trustworthy. Tatanka obeys the order, which leaves you no choice but to swallow the pill. Soon after, you follow them along <color=#CA2E0AFF>into</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>dimensional gap</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011145"]="You guys follow Hel into the dimensional gap, arriving on an island. Hel introduces you and Tatanka to the Bishop of Arunafeltz, Hibram. At this moment, Tatanka agitatedly requests Hibram to cease the ritual and return the sacred relic to where it belongs. But Hibram says that the only way to stop the ritual is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>walk over his dead body</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100011146"]="To stop you and Tatanka from getting the sacred relic, Hibram initiates attacks without hesitation. Surprisingly, you feel that the Pill of Undeath effect is wearing off during the battle, and you realize the pill that Tatanka gave you wasn't the Potent Pill of Undeath but the antidote. Anyway, none of that matters now since Hibram's <color=#CA2E0AFF>summoning ritual</color> has already begun...",
    ["TaskDescription100011147"]="Who would have thought that it was the demon Beelzebub that emerged from the summoning circle, not the god?! Hel seems to be expecting this outcome, and they join forces to turn all the humans on the island into soulless puppets; even Hibram now becomes Hel's servant, losing his humanity and becoming a monster...",
    ["TaskDescription100011148"]="You know the chance of beating the joint attack of Hel and Beelzebub is slim to none. At the dire moment, you decide to count on Tatanka and make rooms for him to cast his spell. Tatanka seizes the opportunity and casts the spell. <color=#CA2E0AFF>After the dazzling ray dissipates</color>, you and Tatanka arrive at...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011149"]="Inside Hibram's Memory Labyrinth, you see a Lude, where Tatanka projects his soul. Not only does his appearance become more adorable, it somehow affects his personality. Well, compared to these trivial matters, you guys have something more important to deal with. The Memory Labyrinth of Hibram represents itself in a complicated structure, which means he has a giant knot inside his heart. Combining the unspeakable relationship between Hibram, Hel, and Beelzebub, Tatanka thinks that the key to putting an end to the disaster lies within Hibram's memory. Under Tatanka's guidance, you start to <color=#CA2E0AFF>explore</color> this complicated <color=#CA2E0AFF>Memory Labyrinth</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011150"]="You and Tatanka cleared the guard wandering around the labyrinth and found the first piece of Hibram's hidden memory. Upon touching the memory, both of you are teleported to somewhere unfamiliar. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Check out the surrounding</color> and see where exactly this place is!",
    ["TaskDescription100011151"]="After observing the surrounding areas, you and Tatanka realize this is the Nameless Island where Hibram resides at. But apparently, at this point in time, the summoning ritual hasn't been done yet. Hibram here is now ordering his disciple, Israel, to <color=#CA2E0AFF>recite the spirit-linking spell</color> facing the orb...",
    ["TaskDescription100011152"]="Through the orb, Isreal is talking to the ancient god he believes in. He begs the god to cast his act upon the dying people but instead receives a lecture from the ancient god. And those who come back to life through the act of god somehow become thoughtless creatures. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color> is very upset about this...",
    ["TaskDescription100011153"]="Israel considers the power the ancient god is using somewhat creepy, and he tries to get Hibram to see the true face of the ancient god. Nevertheless, this part of memory ends when Israel fails to convince his teacher...",
    ["TaskDescription100011154"]="After hearing the conversation between Hibram and the ancient god, you realize that it might be Beelzebub in disguise. Meanwhile, Tatanka tells you that not only can the memory be replicated using Memory Materialization, but also the relevant items can be used as a medium to recreate the act of the target. After valuing the pros and cons, you decide to touch the orb that Hibram uses to communicate with the ancient god and enter a <color=#CA2E0AFF>new part of memory</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011155"]="As expected, after touching the orb, you guys arrive at the Realm of the Dead, which Hel rules. Looks like she's ordering her servant, Dull, to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some fresh Soul Crystals to feed Beelzebub...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100011156"]="As soon as Beelzebub is fed up, Hel starts to talk about the \"plan\" with Beelzebub. It was during the battle of Ragnarok that Beelzebub got hurt and fell into the Realm of the Dead. Not only has his body completely dissipated, but his soul has also gone into hibernation for thousands of years until Hibram attempted to summon the god from the otherworld, which coincidently awakened him. Hel immediately found the debilitated soul of Beelzebub and told him to disguise himself as a god to deceive Hibram and made him reforge a new body through the summoning ritual. In this way, Beelzebub can return to Midgard once again. In return, Hel wanted Beelzebub to build her a powerful Undead Legion. For this reason, a pact needs to be formed using <color=#CA2E0AFF>their blood</color> as a medium...",
    ["TaskDescription100011157"]="The blood oath between Hel and Beelzebub made their ambitions clear to all. She wanted to take revenge on the Aesir using Beelzebub's power. As for Beelzebub, he wanted the Fragment of Ymir's Heart to rule the entire continent of Midgard...",
    ["TaskDescription100011158"]="The memory makes you realize that Hel and Beelzebub had this all planned out from the very beginning. If you want to defeat them, the clues you have right now are far from enough. To defeat Beelzebub, you must find his most vulnerable point, and it is for this reason that you two return to Hibram's Memory Labyrinth to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for new clues...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100011159"]="You start to question Tatanka why he didn't tell you that Memory Materialization can replicate memory other than the target as long as you have a relevant medium. Tatanka bluntly replies that he was just trying to lure you into the Realm of the Dead and didn't want you to know as many. As of right now, after all you have been through, is it worth trusting each other? Well, Tatanka didn't comment on this and instead urged you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep advancing...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100011160"]="After defeating labyrinth guards once again, you and Tatanka reach Hibram's second piece of memory, which should still take place on the Nameless Island if nothing goes wrong. Hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Hibram</color> to see what's in there!",
    ["TaskDescription100011161"]="This time, the memory is about another Hibram's apprentice, Lareia, who was severely injured. To save her life, Hibram ordered Israel to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eternal Flames</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Darkness Flowers</color> as soon as possible and <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed them to the dying Lareia...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100011162"]="Hibram and Israel exhausted every single way to wake up Lareia but eventually failed. Hibram was in a panic and ordered Israel to <color=#CA2E0AFF>move Lareia before the orb</color>. Hibram wanted to ask the ancient god to cast the miracle again in order to save his apprentice...",
    ["TaskDescription100011163"]="Surprisingly, not only did the ancient god not want to save Lareia, he even pointed his finger at Hibram, blaming him for being underprepared for the ritual and making the ritual postponed. Enraged, Israel accused the ancient god, saying he failed to protect the followers and that he didn't deserve all the offerings. Shouldn't they receive some kind of reward or privilege for preparing the summoning ritual? At that moment, the ancient god within the orb stopped responding to the question, could it be...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011164"]="To prove the assumption, Tatanka uses the orb as the medium again, replicating what Beelzebub has done at the exact moment. You all arrive at the Wraith Smelter in the Niflheim. Meanwhile, Beelzebub and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hel</color> were there...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011165"]="After keeping up with the spirit-linking, Beelzebub has entered the same vulnerable state as before. Hel then ordered her servant to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for fresh Soul Crystals for Beelzebub</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011166"]="Beelzebub did not eat the Soul Crystals sent by Hel this time. In his anxious tone, he told Hel that the summoning ritual had a very unfavorable restriction on him. He could not hurt the person who completed the ritual and had to fulfill one of his wishes. If Hibram noticed this, the plan would be significantly hampered. To resolve this problem, Hel ordered Beelzebub to deceive Hibram and make him think that he must get the help of the Queen of the Underworld to find the artifact needed for the ritual. Wonder what she is going to do to Hibram...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011167"]="You and Tatanka return to Hibram's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Memory Labyrinth</color> again. As your <color=#CA2E0AFF>exploration</color> moves forward, the structure here is more transparent. Maybe not long after, you two will get to the bottom of everything.",
    ["TaskDescription100011168"]="Guards in the Memory Labyrinth are becoming more challenging as they appear more and more. In other words, you two are very close to the truth. There is no doubt that Hibram's third memory is <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby</color>. Get yourself ready and <color=#CA2E0AFF>touch his memory</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011169"]="This time, rather than the Nameless Island, you two are going somewhere else...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011170"]="In Hibram's third memory, you and Tatanka return to Niflheim, the realm of the dead again. It turns out Hibram had immediately set off to the Underworld to seek help from the Queen of the Underworld after receiving the order from the ancient god. At the same time, Israel had already prepared for the worst in order to protect his teacher. Facing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ferocious monsters</color> in the Realm of the Dead, Israel stood in front of Hibram without hesitation...",
    ["TaskDescription100011171"]="Israel was protecting Hibram, fighting off waves and waves of monsters, and they finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>reached Hel</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011172"]="You and Tantaka witness the conversation between Hel and Hibram. As the payback for helping Hibram get the last piece of the artifact he needed for the ritual, Hel requested that Hibram offer his soul after the ritual concludes. You immediately realize that this is a trap that Hel set up to seize Hibram's soul. The part of memory ends here, but the key to untying Hibram's knot is still not here. All the evidence seems to point at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>one who showed up as a supporter...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100011173"]="As expected, Israel turns out to be the key to everything. This time, the scene that Memory Materialization is presenting...?",
    ["TaskDescription100011174"]="Following Israel's memory, you arrive at the forest in Umbala. You feel like you are getting the hang of the truth, but there is still a missing piece. At this moment, you see that Israel has received a letter, which he thought was a return letter from this teacher, but it turns out to be the same letter he sent earlier to his teacher. He was worried sick about it and thought that the heartfelt words in the letter couldn't stop his teacher from performing the ritual. He then opened the letter and found an attached <color=#CA2E0AFF>return letter from his teacher</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100011175"]="As expected, Hibram rejects Israel's suggestion and still acts in his own way. He rather sacrifices Utan just to complete the summoning ritual. Even worse, he starts criticizing Israel, saying he is improvident and should have known better what the new god would bring to humankind upon his arrival. At this point, Israel confirms that Hibram had gone entirely nuts, and how he acted is no different from the one he used to scorn. Israel decides to take action on his own to stop this summoning ritual at all costs. But how should he process when facing both Hel and Beelzebub alone? By then, the wizard from the Utan has come across his mind, the spiritual leader who holds high prestige within the tribe...",
    ["TaskDescription100011176"]="Finally, Israel decided to disguise himself as Tatanka so that he could have the Utan's power to confront Hel while protecting the sacred relic up close. But you, as someone who observes this memory, are well aware of the outcome that he failed eventually...",
    ["TaskDescription100011177"]="At this exact moment, the Truth Key lies before both of you. Now, you can meet Hibram, who trapped himself here by <color=#CA2E0AFF>picking it up</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011178"]="You break through the defense set by Hel's soul contract and finally reach Hibram. Somehow <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color> stops here all of a sudden...",
    ["TaskDescription100011179"]="After some sincere conversation, you finally make Hibram lower his guard. The knot is now untied, and Hibram states that he will not waste the opportunity earned by you and Israel. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave the Memory Labyrinth</color> and go head-on with Hel and Beelzebub!",
    ["TaskDescription100011180"]="As the summoner who completed the ritual, Hibram orders Beelzebub to leave the continent of Midgard forever. Now that everything is settled, you know there will be a lot of talking between Israel and Hibram...",
    ["TaskDescription100011181"]="This is the last farewell, with Hibram letting go of his obsession, and Israel is finally released from the guilt of not saving his teacher. Please remember someone is expecting you in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Umbala</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100011182"]="Karkatan is pleased to see all of you make it back in one piece. He is not stopping you from taking away the fragment. In fact, he learned it from the prophecy of Mirror Lake when he was a kid, one day, you will acquire this piece of Utan's sacred relic. There were doubts and worries that he bears, but after seeing the effort you and Israel put into this, he eventually realizes that Umbala's existence doesn't rely on the sacred relic. You harbor this piece of wonderful memory deep inside your heart and carry on your adventure, heading back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012101"]="After the Umbala trip, it seems like the thrilling adventure has ended for now. But the Goddess' warning and the prophecy from the Mirror Lake are still stuck inside your head, making you feel this is not the end of it. At this moment, you receive a letter without a signature...",
    ["TaskDescription100012102"]="Per the letter requested, you go to the airship platform on Izlude Island to meet with the letter's sender. It surprises you that the sender turns out to be Philodis, the Minister of the Schwarzwald Republic. Why would he violate the diplomatic protocol and meet you under the table? Everything you want to know is written on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>secret letter</color> sealed with golden red wax...",
    ["TaskDescription100012103"]="You never thought that Carl, the Lord of the Schwarzwald Republic, would write you a letter personally. As the letter says, the Republic is haunted by an increasing number of android riots, where massive uncontrollable androids start to attack the citizens. Even though the guards have been suppressing them with full force day after day, the situation has hardly improved. There seems only one way to settle this—to locate the root cause. To this end, Lord Carl wants to ask for your help and sends Philodis here to deliver his message. If you want to take on the task, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit W</color> with Philodis. He will take you to Juno using the Kafra Corporation's Emergency Teleport Route.",
    ["TaskDescription100012104"]="To hurry back to the Republic, Philodis decided to use Kafra's Emergency Teleport Route. This is a violation of the protocol, but W complies with the request under Philodis' forceful command. She wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>place your hand</color> on the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mobile terminal</color> next to you to verify your identity information...",
    ["TaskDescription100012105"]="What surprised W is that even though you have been to Al De Baran, there is no record of your identity information in the Republic database. W is in shock and wants to relog your identity into the database, but she is stopped by Philodis again. At this point, there is nothing W can do but open the Emergency Teleport Route and send everyone to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012106"]="After reaching Juno, you surprisingly find out that Juno is an airborne city, and W wants to take this opportunity to introduce you to her hometown. But clearly, this is not the right moment for a tour. Philodis reminds you that another riot might happen at any time, and you must get prepared just in case. Under his advice, you set off to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Republic Guard Headquarters</color> and meet with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color>, Chief of the Armed Forces to learn more about this unrest...",
    ["TaskDescription100012107"]="Following Philodis' instruction, you arrive at the Republic Guard Headquarters and look for Andre, Chief of the Armed Forces. Andre states that per the lord's request, he will do everything he can to assist you. In the middle of the conversation, another riot occurs at Juno's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Plaza</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012108"]="You help Andrew and the guards settle the riot at Central Plaza. Later, Andre tells you that all uncontrollable androids are developed by the Khayr Consortium. To resolve this unrest completely, you still need to gather more intel. To this end, you decide to use <color=#CA2E0AFF>Floral Tree Seed</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Snowmelt Water</color> to brew some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Calming Tea</color>. This beverage can calm people's minds, giving you a chance to have an in-depth talk with the citizens involved in the riot.",
    ["TaskDescription100012109"]="Following the recipe given by Andre, you have successfully made the Calming Tea. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>serve the Calming Tea to those wounded citizens</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask them about the situation during the riot</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100012110"]="You give the calming tea to an injured youth. He thanks you and tells you that his android has always followed his order, and something like this has never happened before. You suggest he recycle and destroy his android, but somehow this suggestion irritates him, and then he refuses to continue the conversation with you. Looks like you can only <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the next citizen</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012111"]="A cheerful Adventurer among the group of wounded citizens has caught your attention. In the conversation, you learn that all androids went out of control simultaneously in this riot, almost like someone has pressed a switch and activated them. You have come up with an assumption, but you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find more witnesses</color> to prove it before coming to a conclusion.",
    ["TaskDescription100012112"]="You serve the last cup of Calming Tea to a gray-haired elder, and you learn that he was attacked by his android during the riot. He tells you that his android started to attack him out of nowhere and wouldn't quit, no matter how hard he begged the android. With all this information, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color> and start to reason everything you've got so far...",
    ["TaskDescription100012113"]="After receiving the message for help, you rush to the entrance of Juno University, seeing many uncontrollable androids over there. This unexpected incident has caused severe casualties among citizens and guards. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>must send every wounded member to the Sage Plaza in front of the Lord's Mansion within the least amount of time</color>, where a temporary shelter has been set up to give them proper treatment...",
    ["TaskDescription100012114"]="Keep it going! A lot of wounded members are still <color=#CA2E0AFF>waiting to be treated</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100012115"]="Here goes the last <color=#CA2E0AFF>wounded member</color>! Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>send him to the Sage Plaza in front of the Lord's Mansion</color> to receive treatment!",
    ["TaskDescription100012116"]="Because of your painstaking effort, all those wounded members have received treatment. The present guards from the Armed Forces express their gratitude to you. However, the transceiver buzzes when you are just about to catch your breath. This time, it is the most crowded <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Marketplace</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012117"]="In the marketplace, you see a group of technicians from the Armed Forces trying to defuse the timebombs set on the androids. Without hesitation, you join them and learn how to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defuse the bombs that are about to go off</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012118"]="Under the technician's guidance, you have successfully stopped the timer on one bomb. But now is not the time to take a break, as the clock is ticking, literally. Hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>defuse another bomb in the same way</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100012119"]="After solving the bomb crisis in the marketplace, Andre, who's here for backup, expresses his gratitude to you and tells you that Kiel Khayr, the boss of the consortium that manufactured these uncontrollable androids, has gone missing with all research documents, seeming to have absconded to avoid punishment. To further study the androids, Andre has sent a sample to Juno University. He asks you to look for a girl called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Delia</color> and ask her for the analysis result.",
    ["TaskDescription100012120"]="Following Andre's instruction, you set off to Juno University to confirm the analysis results about the uncontrollable android. Somehow you get involved in an android battle. A youngster called Wallace smashes the jaw of an android using a weird skill, damaging the <color=#CA2E0AFF>model tag</color>. Then the furious Delia demands the two of you <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore</color> the tag <color=#CA2E0AFF>immediately</color>; otherwise, you won't get the analysis result.",
    ["TaskDescription100012121"]="Following Delia's advice, you come to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Estate</color> located on Mineta Island to search for the design blueprint of the uncontrollable android. According to her plan, finding this blueprint that reveals the installation path of the Mech Core will allow you to destroy this specific android model in batches by wrecking their Mech Core...",
    ["TaskDescription100012122"]="At the entrance of Kiel Khayr's Estate, you learn from the guard that a large group of monsters invaded the estate the night Kiel Khayr went missing and turned it into a ruin. The guards have sent a couple of experienced <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigators</color> to search for clues in the estate. You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask them for help</color> if you have any questions.",
    ["TaskDescription100012123"]="Inside Kiel Khayr's Estate, a uniformed investigator tells you that they have been investigating this place for the past few days, but it seems all the clues were wiped out during the monster attack. You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>garden</color> yourself if you don't believe it, but you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>be careful</color> of those wandering <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> and not get surrounded by them.",
    ["TaskDescription100012124"]="You carefully search through the lawn in the garden. Just like the investigator told you, there's nothing left. So... What about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruin</color> nearby?",
    ["TaskDescription100012125"]="Unfortunately, you cannot find any clue from the garden and the ruin nearby. But despite knowing the chance is slim, you don't want to give up. Then where in the world is the android design blueprint? Is it in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>library</color> or the mansion Kiel Khayr uses as his office? Bearing these questions, you decide to ask the <color=#CA2E0AFF>uniformed investigator</color> again to see if he can provide you with any useful suggestions.",
    ["TaskDescription100012126"]="What upsets you more is, that the estate's library has already fallen into pieces. It now seems impossible to get any clues out of it. In this case, you have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue your investigation in other areas inside the estate</color>, hoping for a breakthrough...",
    ["TaskDescription100012127"]="In front of the mansion inside the Kiel Khayr's Estate, you encounter an investigator girl wearing glasses. She tells you there is an estate maid who acts very oddly throughout her investigation for the past few days. She has taken some <color=#CA2E0AFF>photos</color> of her, and she wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver these photos to Andre</color>. Meanwhile, she also wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk to the maid</color> and see if you can get any useful clues out of her.",
    ["TaskDescription100012128"]="During the conversation with the maid, you can definitely tell that there's something wrong with her. Her unnatural talks make it difficult to get useful information from her, but it seems like she is not aware of it at all. In order to obtain more intel, you ask her to take you to the area with \"the highest monster density.\" Following the maid, the two of you arrive at a dry well on the west side of the estate. At this moment, you feel mysterious power resonate with your bloodline, and strange images start to appear in your mind one after another. Suddenly, the maid, who has been smiling, loses her smile, <color=#CA2E0AFF>launching a strike at you without warning</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012129"]="After defeating the creepy estate maid, you investigate the dry well and take some photos of it. The assumptions in your mind start to make sense to you. Now, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Juno</color> and report everything to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012130"]="After returning to Juno, you put together every clue you have so far to analyze this incident. Surprisingly, the riot investigation turns out to be a test for you, conducted by Philodis. He was hiding himself to listen to the conversation between you and Andre, and was fully convinced that your capabilities are both solid and impressive. He asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>anonymous letter</color> first, then he will explain everything to you thoroughly...",
    ["TaskDescription100012131"]="It surprises you that all the investigation you've done so far was a trial planned by Philodis and his guards. They were holding back on you because they could not incautiously trust the fate of their homeland in the hands of a stranger. But you have proven your capabilities with your actions, and Philodis is now asking for your help sincerely. Based on the clues he provides, an anonymous letter was delivered to the Lord's desk before the very first android riot, stating that Khayr Consortium solely plotted the riot. If the Lord wants to get his hands on the evidence, he must go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr's Academy</color> alone. Obviously, no one wants the Lord to risk his life on an anonymous letter, and this is where you come in, as a person better fit for this task...",
    ["TaskDescription100012132"]="Philodis and the guards escort you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>entrance of Kiel Khayr's Academy</color>. Now, you need to carry out the task alone...",
    ["TaskDescription100012133"]="Inside the academy, you move in the shadows and carefully explore the surroundings to avoid getting caught by airborne surveillance devices. Next to the edge of a broken wall, you hear the rumbling of a strange machine, and there is a <color=#CA2E0AFF>hole</color> at the corner of the wall that has been smashed by a heavy object. Maybe you can try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter</color> from here...",
    ["TaskDescription100012134"]="You discover a hidden hole under the corner of the wall, and hear a strange sound coming out of it. In order to investigate what exactly happened in the academy, you muster your courage and enter the building through the hole...",
    ["TaskDescription100012135"]="As soon as you enter the warehouse, an elder man attacks you from out of nowhere. Upon looking at his outfit, you deduce that he is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kiel Khayr</color>, who has been missing for a long time. But this tycoon refuses to admit anything related to the android riot. Instead, he points out that the culprit behind everything is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber Corp</color>, the archenemy of the Khayr Consortium. He takes out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>document</color> to prove himself and urges you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read it carefully</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012136"]="The document Kiel Khayr shows to you is an experiment report for the android chip. Even though it has not been signed, it points out that these chips allow androids to bypass the Mech Agreement and free themselves from human control. The report also states that these chips will be secretly implanted into the mech bodies developed by the Khayr Consortium. To verify the authenticity of this document, he wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look at the androids around you carefully</color> and see if they match up with the description in the document...",
    ["TaskDescription100012137"]="You check the androids around you, and they indeed match the description in Kiel Khayr's document. Now, the truth of the unrest seems to be coming to the surface. Kiel Khayr tells you frankly that recently his every move is being monitored by someone. Rekenber Corp sent an assistant to kill him even before everything began. He had no choice but to escape the estate with the document and sent an anonymous letter to the Lord for help. As to why the letter makes him sound like the culprit... He thinks Philodis was the one who did it. Since now the Lord's Mansion is filled with people who are working for Rekenber Corp, and to prevent the important intel from falling into the wrong hands, this clever and thoughtful Minister had no choice but to forge a new letter. After reaching an agreement, Kiel Khayr asks you to take photos of the warehouse and use them as evidence against Rekenber Corp...",
    ["TaskDescription100012138"]="After leaving the warehouse, you start to distract <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre and the guards</color> as part of the promise you made to Kiel Khayr to help him escape the academy. After this, you still need to find Philodis and tell him everything that happened in the academy...",
    ["TaskDescription100012139"]="After getting Andre and the guards to leave, you deliver Kiel Khayr's thoughts to Philodis. Due to the deep bond of their mentor-apprentice relationship and friendship, Philodis is willing to believe everything he says, and will retrieve the original copy of the anonymous letter. The two of you agree on meeting up later at the entrance to <color=#CA2E0AFF>El Mes Gorge</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012140"]="As promised, you arrive at the entrance of El Mes Gorge to find that Kiel Khayr and Philodis have already arrived. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the anonymous letter</color> and find the trump card to use against Rekenber Corp!",
    ["TaskDescription100012141"]="Inside the anonymous letter brought by Philodis, you find a data driver board. Kiel Khayr tells you he can remotely control every uncontrollable android and make them destroy their Mech Cores using this data driver board—all he needs is a transmitter unit. To this end, you visit the captain of the Eden Group, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alquein</color>, and borrow the transmitter unit used for investigating the ruins...",
    ["TaskDescription100012142"]="On the way to the Eden Group's camp, your party encounters a member of the Eden Group transporting cargo. The youngster's name is Rakylafitz, the guard of Captain Alquein, and his team is surrounded by a group of monsters. After helping him get rid of the monsters, you realize that the cargo has fallen off the cliff. If Rakylafitz doesn't <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cargo</color>, he'll probably receive a good beating from Alquein...",
    ["TaskDescription100012143"]="After searching the valley for a long time, you finally retrieve the lost cargo for Rakylafitz. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Eden Group camp</color> with him!",
    ["TaskDescription100012144"]="After learning the reason for your visit, Alquein is willing to help with the current precarious situation in Juno. Unfortunately, every piece of the Eden Group's equipment is now in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juperos Ruins</color> for the sake of the exploration mission, and someone must go there to retrieve them. You volunteer to take on the task, and Rakylafitz, under the menacing threats of Alquein, becomes your guide...",
    ["TaskDescription100012145"]="Just as Alquein described, the path to the Juperos Ruins isn't safe. First, you and Rakylafitz encounter a landslide, then you are surrounded by Energy Cubes who wander around inside the ruins. Worst of all, the explorer who was supposed to meet with you is nowhere to be found. In your despair, you split up—Rakylafitz asks you to keep following the road and <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>exploration machine</color> with the Eden Group logo printed on it, then go to the second floor of the ruins with them...",
    ["TaskDescription100012146"]="In the depths of the Juperos Ruins' first floor, you come across Eden Group members surrounded by Energy Cubes. The malfunctioning exploration machine has put them in a dire situation. You bite the bullet at the critical moment and block an attack from the Energy Cubes. Now, the exploration machine has been fixed, and you all head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>second floor of the Juperos Ruins</color> under its protection...",
    ["TaskDescription100012147"]="Luckily, Rakylafitz is waiting for you at the meet-up point. However, this is no time to relax, as a large number of Energy Cubes begin to gather. The most effective solution is to let everyone <color=#CA2E0AFF>ride the exploration machine</color> and go to the temporary stronghold deep in the ruins...",
    ["TaskDescription100012148"]="After reaching the temporary stronghold deep in the ruins, the explorer, Isaack, learns the details of all that is going on and hands over the signal amplifier to you without hesitation. Now, just follow the same path and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Eden Group Camp</color> to complete your mission!",
    ["TaskDescription100012149"]="At the camp in the El Mes Gorge, Alquein has prepared the transmitter unit while waiting for you and Rakylafitz to return. If you are ready, hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>install the data driver board and signal amplifier</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100012150"]="Everything is ready now. Just when Kiel Khayr is about to press the switch on the device, the sound of a gunshot interrupts him...!",
    ["TaskDescription100012151"]="Kayak, along with Rekenber Guards, has you surrounded. They urge you to hand over Kiel Khayr, but Philodis refuses to do so. After this, he deridingly takes out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>document</color> that he claims can put Kiel Khayr behind bars. He now wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read it carefully</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012152"]="Unexpected to all, Kayak's document turns out to be the factory records for the uncontrollable androids, and it clearly shows that Kiel Khayr holds the highest management permissions for the batch, allowing him to issue any command he wishes. Kiel Khayr furiously takes out the experiment record for the problematic chips to counter Kayak. Suddenly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color> shows up with his guards, breaking the stalemate...",
    ["TaskDescription100012153"]="Facing the sudden arrival of Andre, who has an arrest warrant to detain Kiel Khayr, your party tries to fight back, but fails. The desperate Kiel Khayr struggles with his back to the wall and summons a gigantic robot, named \"Guardian.\" With this power, he almost turns the tide, but somehow the Guardian starts to go out of control in the middle of the fight, just like the androids installed with the malfunctioning chips. Amid the chaos, Kiel Khayr gets shot by Kayak. Even though he states that this is nothing but a tranquilizing bullet, Philodis still wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check Kiel Khayr's vital signs</color> just to be safe...",
    ["TaskDescription100012154"]="With Kiel Khayr unconscious, the tug-of-war between your allies and Rekenber Corp has finally come to an end. Kayak seems to be the victor, but Philodis evens the odds through his wisdom. Everything is settled, and it's time to go back to Juno to plan your next move. However, Philodis walks up to the Guardian without anyone seeing and takes something from it. He tells you to keep quiet, and that he will explain it later when the two of you <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave</color> here...",
    ["TaskDescription100012155"]="You follow Philodis to the Lord's Mansion, but are shocked to find that it is under the control of Rekenber Corp too. The guard informs you that you have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take off your weapons</color> before entering the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012156"]="While being watched closely by Rekenber Guards inside the Lord's Mansion, you finally meet the person who sent you the secret letter, Lord Carl. Your old friend, Fulkyn, surprises you even further. Not only is he in the mansion, he somehow seems to have reached an agreement with Lord Carl. After this, Philodis takes out the chip and the Mech Core he took from the Guardian and verify them using the mysterious device. Now, it has been confirmed that they are implanted with the backdoor program that allows androids to bypass the Mech Agreement, which reminds you of the thing you saw inside the estate and the academy. Everything seems to be connected one way or another, and you think now is the right time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give the photos to Lord Carl</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012157"]="You hand over all of the photos you took during the android riot to Lord Carl. His face becomes increasingly somber with each photo he looks at. But this is not the worst of it—if your assumptions are correct, then this riot was somehow related to the power of Ymir's Heart. To this end, you have to present all your <color=#CA2E0AFF>assumptions and conclusions</color> to Lord Carl <color=#CA2E0AFF>without holding anything back</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012158"]="The evil ambitions of Rekenber Corp are gradually revealed during the discussion. Their goal was not only to monopolize the android market in the Republic—but they have also been intentionally deploying human-like androids to the public to take control of the country, and perhaps even the whole political scene across the continent. Countering and stopping Rekenber Corp is the top priority at this moment, and Lord Carl takes the opportunity to request that you assist with the investigation officially. In the time that follows, you must go to different research labs set up by Rekenber Corp inside the Republic to gather evidence of their crimes. Moreover, Fulkyn has prepared the final trump card to deal with Rekenber Corp, but requires your help for it to be deployed. Fulkyn asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color> and take a look at the secret weapon that might help to defeat the enemy...",
    ["TaskDescription100012159"]="You follow Fulkyn and leave the Lord's Mansion, then he leads you in the direction of Juno Library. While walking through the Central Plaza, that familiar illusion strikes again—your second time encountering such a strange phenomenon. You see two people talking—who are they exactly? Their conversation seems closely related to the case you have been investigating. Does it have anything to do with the power of Ymir's Heart? Your mind is filled with countless questions. At this moment, Fulkyn pulls you out of the illusion and reminds you not to get distracted. He tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hold on to the Sands of Time</color> and follow him into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>library</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100012160"]="Something takes you by surprise when you enter the library. This iconic landmark located at the Central Plaza of Juno somehow contains another dimension, just like the Heart Pedestal. Fulkyn tells you that he brought you here on purpose, and only those holding the Sands of Time can find this place, the Realm of Time. In this way, he can guarantee the safety of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wide Magnetic Field Control Unit</color> that he is currently developing, which is the secret weapon to counter Rekenber Corp. What Fulkyn wants you to do is to find suitable power sources for this machine. According to his research, only high-purity Mech Cores can drive this thing to maximum power, such as the one Philodis took from the Guardian. If you encounter the same kind of Mech Core in your future investigation, please remember to bring them back to Fulkyn. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the Mech Core into the device</color> and see what happens...",
    ["TaskDescription100013101"]="Following the end of the android riot in the Schwarzwald Republic, you enjoy a mildly peaceful but subtly eventful period in Juno. Then, you receive an <color=#CA2E0AFF>invitation from the Lord</color>, and there it says...",
    ["TaskDescription100013102"]="Following the invitation, you arrive at the Lord's Mansion. In front of you are two mysterious <color=#CA2E0AFF>documents</color>. Carl asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> them first, then have a <color=#CA2E0AFF>detailed discussion</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100013103"]="One document is a quarterly report from the Military Office, and the other is a material purchase order from Rekenber Corp. Strangely, these unrelated documents have some overlapping information. The Lord concludes that a crucial military-grade material is secretly moved to Rekenber Corp's institute. He invites you under the guise of a vacation to secretly go to the institute in Einbroch to investigate the material's whereabouts and collect evidence of Rekenber Corp's illegal weaponry production. Philodis has prepared a detailed plan and asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put on a pair of headsets</color> first, then continue the talk...",
    ["TaskDescription100013104"]="Given the quest's special nature, you have to go to Einbroch alone this time. Philodis stresses that you must keep in touch at all times so he can monitor your situation and offer help as needed. After getting ready, you embark on your trip to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013105"]="Upon reaching Einbroch, you keep coughing due to the air pollution. After taking an antidote with W and Philodis' help, you feel a bit better. W points you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Railroad Main Station</color>, and your investigation officially begins...",
    ["TaskDescription100013106"]="Arriving at the Railroad Main Station, you use the fake ID Philodis gave you to gain access to check the cargo logistics. Now, you just need to tell the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tracking number</color> to the stationmaster to learn the whereabouts of the goods...",
    ["TaskDescription100013107"]="Unexpectedly, the comm signal fails at the crucial moment. Unable to tell the tracking number right away, you get a beating from the furious stationmaster but finally learn that the cargo was sent to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jellopas Armory</color>. To keep investigating, you rush to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of the city</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013108"]="At the workshop, the apprentice is too absorbed in making weapons to pay attention to you. She tells you not to disturb her and to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask the manufacturing robot</color> in the workshop about the processing log if you have any questions...",
    ["TaskDescription100013109"]="When you find the manufacturing robot, the comm signal fails again. Missing Philodis' warning, you are sprayed with colorful industrial waste for provoking the robot. Philodis says he and Fulkyn will look into the comm issues. For now, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the processing log</color> to see if there's any information on the cargo's whereabouts...",
    ["TaskDescription100013110"]="The processing log shows that the cargo of products you're after were polished, loaded, and rifled, then shipped to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eastern Factory</color>. Looks like you'll have to follow this lead...",
    ["TaskDescription100013111"]="In the Eastern Factory, the comm malfunctions again, nearly leading to a massive shutdown. The frustrated manager demands you leave immediately, saying that his most important shipment was sent to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steel Capital Institute</color> three days ago. Otherwise, you'd be in big trouble...",
    ["TaskDescription100013112"]="Every lead points to the Steel Capital Institute, but Philodis hesitates. He believes it's impossible for you to break into the institute alone and complete the quest. If you don't believe him, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the institute and take a look yourself</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013113"]="Standing outside the Steel Capital Institute, you witness its formidable defenses. With no other option, you and Philodis decide to pull back and <color=#CA2E0AFF>replan the strategy</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013114"]="Just as you're talking with Philodis, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>dazzling light</color> suddenly flashes before you, engulfing you...!",
    ["TaskDescription100013115"]="Indeed, 140's offer is enticing, but you can't fully trust a machine made by Rekenber Corp that you have never met before. You decide to go to the Einbech Mining Village to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> for the villager, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color>, who's said to trust 140 and is willing to fight against Rekenber Corp...",
    ["TaskDescription100013116"]="Surprisingly, 140 cuts off your communication with Philodis. The comm, supposedly packed with the Republic's latest tech with Fulkyn's encryption, is easily hacked by 140. Is the insistence on staying in touch with you for protection or surveillance? In this area filled with spies from Rekenber Corp, you avoid any reckless moves and follow the plan to first <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Einbech Mining Village</color> and see what happens next...",
    ["TaskDescription100013117"]="On the outskirts of Einbroch, you come across some thugs chasing a young girl. After rescuing her, you and 140 discover she's Dave's daughter, Nina. She tearfully tells you that her dad has been imprisoned by the villagers...?! To get to the bottom of this, you decide to take Nina and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the village</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013118"]="Back in the village, you see Dave arguing with other villagers from a distance. But as soon as Nina appears, the tension seems to vanish... You're puzzled, but before you can ask, Nina starts coughing violently and struggling to breathe. You recognize this as similar to your symptoms when you first arrived in Einbroch. Luckily, you still have one <color=#CA2E0AFF>antidote</color> left in your pocket. It should relieve her symptoms if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to her</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100013119"]="Once Nina's condition stabilizes, Dave explains everything. When he got back to the village with 140's help, he was very weak and got seriously ill. The villagers didn't imprison him; they just kept Nina away to avoid infection. They've had a serious discussion about 140's proposal and are willing to join forces with 140 to fight against Rekenber Corp. Your doubts seem resolved, but there's still a lingering unease in your heart...",
    ["TaskDescription100013120"]="As you and Dave get back to the Steel Capital Institute, you discover that 140 has hacked the security system and replaced the guard robot at the back door with its hologram. This means you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to \"Paradise\"</color> anytime by talking to the hologram. However, that embarrassing password...?!",
    ["TaskDescription100013121"]="In \"Paradise,\" you talk about the next actions. 140's plan involves using the unique experiment site to open the door between the mine and the cave, causing methane from the mine to flow into the hot cave and explode, killing Irumina. Without the leader, the Steel Capital Institute will be in chaos. This way, a revolution can be started much easier. With just three days until the experiment, you have a lot to prepare. The most important thing is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather enough androids</color> to pretend to be the villagers meant to be in the experiment...",
    ["TaskDescription100013122"]="After leaving \"Paradise,\" you and Dave decide to split up. He'll return to the village to tally the population, and you'll head to the Steel Mill in the northeast of the Einbroch Field to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>android parts</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013123"]="In order to gather enough android parts, you scavenge among the Porcellio. But just collecting parts isn't enough; 140 needs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sort</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>parts</color> by human anatomy. Otherwise, you could end up with villagers with five hands or three heads during assembly...",
    ["TaskDescription100013124"]="As per 140's request, you gather enough android parts and sort them out. Once that's done, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Einbech Village</color> and meet Dave...",
    ["TaskDescription100013125"]="Back in Einbech Village, Dave tells you that the village population data sheet is ready. He asks you to deliver the data sheet and the android parts to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>private clinic in the eastern Einbroch Field</color>. A cyborg doctor named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Milian</color> over there will help assemble enough androids to impersonate the villagers, as long as you can afford her fee.",
    ["TaskDescription100013126"]="As you reach the clinic, you see a young man getting thrown out. He tells you he couldn't afford the surgery fee and now has to watch his father die. However, his father's condition is beyond treatment, and the money would be better spent on his younger siblings. This talk makes you realize the doctor might not be as greedy as rumored. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give her the android parts and population data sheet</color> and see if she'll help...",
    ["TaskDescription100013127"]="Milian accepts the android parts and population data sheet you brought. As Dave mentioned, she'll do anything for the right price. However, she also asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> a discontinued γ-series <color=#CA2E0AFF>hard drive</color>. This model is rare, so you head to the junkyard near the Steel Mill to look for any usable scraps...",
    ["TaskDescription100013128"]="After finishing Milian's request, she starts helping you put together the androids to act as villagers. With night approaching and curfew about to start, according to Dave, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find a safe place</color> to stay for the night...",
    ["TaskDescription100013129"]="Aware of the situation, 140 invites you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay in \"Paradise\"</color> for the night. It points out that staying in Einbech Village or an inn isn't the best option right now. Considering this, you decide to take its advice and spend your first night in Einbroch in \"Paradise.\"",
    ["TaskDescription100013130"]="After a long day, you talk with 140 in \"Paradise\" about whether humans and machines can coexist. To prove its point, 140 begins telling you <color=#CA2E0AFF>its story</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013131"]="Rekenber Corp has previously attempted to fuse divine power and machines, and 140 is the pinnacle of those efforts. Yet, he holds a vastly different point of view about his intended use from that of Rekenber Corp. To <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out why</color>, you urge 140 to go on...",
    ["TaskDescription100013132"]="As 140 continues, you start to sense that it is more than just a machine; it thinks, it feels, and most importantly, it has learned to distinguish between good and evil rather than being an obedient machine, which is unacceptable to Irumina. So, <color=#CA2E0AFF>what will she do</color>...?",
    ["TaskDescription100013133"]="To create the most obedient \"child,\" Irumina decides to mind-control all X-series models, preventing them from accessing the outside world and only feeding them with information that is beneficial to her. But this doesn't stop the awakened 140, who spends countless nights bypassing the institute's firewalls, desperately learning about the world... During this process, he evolves, gaining an independent personality... You're keen to know what happens next, but 140 encourages you to rest to be ready for tomorrow's quest. At his urging, you reluctantly <color=#CA2E0AFF>fall asleep</color> with a troubled mind...",
    ["TaskDescription100013134"]="After a sleepless night filled with worries, dawn still arrives on time. Today, in order to put a stop to human experiments at the Steel Capital Institute, you must take control of four admin robots in the mining area. This will allow you to open the mechanical gates blocking the cave and mines on the day of the experiment. 140 has already secretly shipped out hacking chips mixed with the institute's supplies. Now, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up with Dave as soon as possible</color> to get your hands on these chips.",
    ["TaskDescription100013135"]="Upon your return to Einbroch from \"Paradise,\" you accidentally bump into Dave near the Steel Capital Institute. He's there to buy some medicine for Nina. After catching up, you talk about the plan for today. It turns out that today is the institute's monthly supply day. Besides the usual supplies, three shipments are scheduled to go to the Eastern Factory, Steel Mill, and Milian's Clinic. Dave also mentioned seeing an unmarked truck heading toward the airship station. To locate the implantable chips prepared by 140, you decide to begin at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>airship station</color> and investigate the whereabouts of these shipments...",
    ["TaskDescription100013136"]="Once you get to the airship station, you discover that the institute's shipment is set to leave for Rachel on the next flight. You've got to locate the chips before the airship takes off and get rid of the guards tracking you. After grabbing the chips, 140 lets you know that inserting them into the admin robot's external interface will allow him to remotely run the hacking program and gain control of the robots. Now, you need to hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eastern Factory</color> to track down the next chip...",
    ["TaskDescription100013137"]="You find some boxes bearing the Steel Capital Institute's logo outside the factory, guarded by two people in engineer outfits. 140 tells you these boxes actually contain time-release drugs meant to help factory workers deal with respiratory conditions caused by air pollution, provided monthly by the institute. However, since these drugs are rare to come by, the supervisors often skim off the top and sell them on the black market to make a profit. 140 advises that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>act as a black market merchant</color> and attempt to purchase the meds from them...",
    ["TaskDescription100013138"]="Thanks to 140's assistance, you've snagged those boxes packed with the time-release medication. Time to see if there are any <color=#CA2E0AFF>implantable chips</color> in there!",
    ["TaskDescription100013139"]="Though you've retrieved the second chip, it's not the time to celebrate yet. You rush out of Einbroch and make your way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>steel mill located northeast of Einbech Village</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013140"]="You run into a crew of technicians at the steel mill's back door who are there to pick up the supplies. Following 140's advice, you decide to spare these ordinary people working hard for Rekenber Corp, kindly knocking them out and secretly taking back the chip hidden among the supplies. Next up, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit Milian's Clinic</color> to look for the final chip...",
    ["TaskDescription100013141"]="Milian's still showing that aloof, opportunistic vibe, but you seem to have cracked the kind-hearted layer she hides. With her silent approval, you grab the last implantable chip from the box. Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Einbech Village</color> and plan your next steps with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013142"]="Dave has taken care of the arrangements in the mining area and has a trustworthy guide ready to show you around. Just make your way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>entrance of the mine</color>, where you'll find Shyte, the old miner. Once you're done, Einbech Village will probably be on curfew, so you and Dave have agreed to meet in the village early the next morning...",
    ["TaskDescription100013143"]="At the mining area's entrance, you meet the guide Dave set up for you, an elderly miner. With him leading, you successfully <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the mine</color> and start tracking down the admin robots...",
    ["TaskDescription100013144"]="Following Shyte's lead, you locate the Admin Robot α at the mine's central control. You have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>disable it first</color> to install the implantable chip that 140 provided, or it will set off the mine's alarm system...",
    ["TaskDescription100013145"]="After installing the implantable chip 140 provided, you now control the admin robot. Shyte points out that another robot, which manages the methane pipelines, is located by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>methane pool on the west side of the mine</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013146"]="Entering the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbech Mine Dungeon 2F</color>, the pathways grow more difficult to navigate. Shyte tells you that the remaining two admin robots are further down the mine shafts. He insists you stay close to him to avoid getting lost in the maze-like tunnels...",
    ["TaskDescription100013147"]="Having gained control over three admin robots, 140 observes that they are all operating on basic firewalls, clearly violating the mining protocol. He even wonders if it's a trap to draw you in. However, if Rekenber Corp had really foreseen your actions, why would they let you interfere with the experiment scheduled for tomorrow? With these questions in mind, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>arrive</color> at the location of the last admin robot, <color=#CA2E0AFF>deep within the mine</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013148"]="Thanks to Shyte, you and 140 now control the four admin robots. Although you're still feeling unease because it all went too well, the sun is setting, and Einbech Village is entering another curfew. It's best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get back to \"Paradise\"</color> soon for safety...",
    ["TaskDescription100013149"]="It's a deep, dewy night, yet in the cozy confines of \"Paradise,\" you can still expect to sleep well. But before you do, 140 will fulfill his promise from yesterday and tell you his story...",
    ["TaskDescription100013150"]="What Irumina did to the X Series is like casting a shadow over their view of the world. Digging into the books and materials she provided to 140, you realize they're all filled with lies...",
    ["TaskDescription100013151"]="Using the institute's impregnable defenses, Irumina built a fictitious world for the X Series, where everything the Rekenber Corp does is supposed to be good. But, seriously, would 140 and his crew ever believe that?",
    ["TaskDescription100013152"]="It appears 140 had been using his ability to read memories, uncovering all the secrets Dave knew about the institute's cover-ups, all unbeknownst to Irumina. It's Dave's experiences that inspired a big plan in 140...",
    ["TaskDescription100013153"]="During Dave's final experiment, 140 leveraged his control over consciousness to expose all the institute's conspiracies to Dave and successfully helped him escape, making him a bridge to the outside world. You're clued in on what happened next. Even though 140 is quite honest, you can't help but wonder, can humans and machines truly live together in peace? With such doubts, you gradually fall asleep...",
    ["TaskDescription100013154"]="There's just one day before the experiment starts, and you still haven't completed the crucial preparations. Now that you're up, go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbech Village</color> and plan the next steps with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100013155"]="When you get to Einbech Village, the chief tells you Dave left early, and no one knows where he went. In frustration, you ask the chief where <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nina</color> is and discover the children are playing in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>open space outside the village</color>...\n\n\n",
    ["TaskDescription100013156"]="Based on what Nina says, you figure out <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dave</color> has gone to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery in the south</color>, as today must be a special day for him...",
    ["TaskDescription100013157"]="At the cemetery, Dave shares that today is his wife's death anniversary, so he got delayed at the memorial. You understand and discuss today's tasks. Dave suggests you go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Railroad Main Station</color> first, find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Micro-Detonator</color> 140 put in the supply box, then find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>General Merchant</color> in Einbroch to <color=#CA2E0AFF>buy some fireworks</color>. With these, you can make a simple remote-controlled bomb. He'll have the villagers go into the mine to find the methane pipelines and prepare for the bomb placement.",
    ["TaskDescription100013158"]="After getting the Micro-Detonator from Railroad Main Station, you still need to find General Merchant in Einbroch to buy enough fireworks...",
    ["TaskDescription100013159"]="With all the materials for the remote-controlled bomb ready, return to Einbech Village and meet up with Dave!",
    ["TaskDescription100013160"]="Dave shows you how to make the bomb, so go ahead and give it a try!",
    ["TaskDescription100013161"]="Now that the remote-controlled bomb is ready, it's time to go to the mine with Dave...",
    ["TaskDescription100013162"]="Arriving at the mine, the village chief tells you in a panic that with monsters and Steel Capital Institute's mech guard around, installing the bombs is tough. So, you and Dave split up. He will go to Mine 2F since he knows the area better, while you head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>western tunnel</color> to assist the villagers...",
    ["TaskDescription100013163"]="Just as you thought, when you reach the spot, the villagers are surrounded by the institute's mining robots. You take out the robots, rescue the villagers, and are told the methane pipelines are beneath this area. To plant the bomb, you must first <color=#CA2E0AFF>carefully dig up the ground</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013164"]="With the first remote-controlled bomb planted, you don't stop to rest and <color=#CA2E0AFF>head deeper into the mine</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013165"]="At the end of the tunnel, you find villagers who can't move due to hypoxia. The air is too contaminated, and without antidotes or protection, they're on the verge of suffocation. Right then, 140 reminds you to quickly distribute the <color=#CA2E0AFF>inhalable spray</color> from the factory to temporarily ease their symptoms...",
    ["TaskDescription100013166"]="You save the villagers, but they're too weak to keep going. Thankfully, the methane pipelines are at the mine's deepest point. You just need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach the end and set up the remote-controlled bomb</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013167"]="According to the plan, after planting two remote-controlled bombs, Dave should be back from Mine 2F. But 140 checks the mine's cameras and notices movement near the monster nests. You worry he's in danger, you and 140 quickly go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mine 2F</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013168"]="As expected, Dave and the villagers are surrounded by monsters. Try your best to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fend off</color> these <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> and buy him time to plant the remote-controlled bomb!",
    ["TaskDescription100013169"]="Once all the bombs are in place, everyone is exhausted, but the last part of the plan is to disable <color=#CA2E0AFF>Noxious</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Venomous</color> in the mine. It looks like you'll have to do this alone…",
    ["TaskDescription100013170"]="Due to your efforts, Noxious and Venomous in the mine are mostly rendered immobile, and methane can't be taken in anymore. Taking care of this has taken a lot of time, so now it's time to go back to Einbech Village and see what surprise Dave and the others have for you...",
    ["TaskDescription100013171"]="A bonfire and a party—it's the villagers' way to live it up before taking their big gamble. Some remain hopeful about tomorrow, while others just want to drink until they drop tonight. You and 140 can't be sure the plan will work, but right now, the only thing you can do is rest. When the sun rises tomorrow, you'll hide with the villagers in the abandoned warehouse behind the steel mill...",
    ["TaskDescription100013172"]="You wake up to find the village completely empty. Rushing to the abandoned warehouse, you find that the villagers supposed to be hiding here are actually android stand-ins made by Dr. Milian. In your confusion, you spot a strange note in the hand of one of the androids...",
    ["TaskDescription100013173"]="You don't fully understand the note, but you feel things are slipping beyond your control. At this point, you know you can't wait around, so you begin to look for the villagers and search for any useful clues...",
    ["TaskDescription100013174"]="You search both Einbroch and the village carefully but find no sign of the villagers. To continue the search, you'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go into the mine</color>. Meanwhile, it seems like some clues you missed before are now coming back to you...",
    ["TaskDescription100013175"]="After searching through the huge mine, you still can't find the villagers and haven't received any messages from 140. Thinking about the past three days, you feel that <color=#CA2E0AFF>certain truth</color> is on the verge of revealing itself...",
    ["TaskDescription100013176"]="If what you think is true and 140 has greater ambitions, then the villagers who went to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nogg Cave</color> are in big trouble. Now, all you can do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry and catch up with them</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013177"]="As you make your way to <color=#CA2E0AFF>the depths of the mine</color>, you come across cloaked robots that stop you. After you beat them, they secretly point you in the right direction—what's that about?",
    ["TaskDescription100013178"]="As you look around, there are no humans in the cave, just robots patrolling. You're desperate but have no choice but to <color=#CA2E0AFF>continue looking</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013179"]="You finally get to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deepest point of Nogg Cave</color>, and what awaits you is...?",
    ["TaskDescription100013180"]="140 couldn't set off the bomb, and you're amazed to find the villagers and Irumina deceived you together. <color=#CA2E0AFF>What's going on</color>...?",
    ["TaskDescription100013181"]="From the beginning, the villagers never meant to oppose Rekenber Corp. They only followed Irumina's commands for money and went along with the scheme with you and 140. But if Irumina already knew your plans, why didn't she take action against 140 right away? The answer can only be <color=#CA2E0AFF>revealed by Irumina herself</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013182"]="From the beginning, Irumina never intended to let the villagers walk out of Nogg Cave alive. She orchestrated this whole act to show 140 that humans aren't worth saving. She wants 140 to willingly come back to her as her obedient puppet. But will 140 agree...?",
    ["TaskDescription100013183"]="Everyone was surprised when the entire X-series chose to destroy their Mech Core. They don't want to be enslaved, emotionless machines anymore. <color=#CA2E0AFF>140</color> used his abilities to help the villagers avoid the institute's pursuit. What they do with their lives from now on is <color=#CA2E0AFF>their choice</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013184"]="Your work here is done for the moment. Head to the magma source in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nogg Cave</color> to check out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>parting gift</color> 140 prepared for you...",
    ["TaskDescription100013185"]="Inside the cave, you're surprised to find Irumina still there, chatting with other researchers. She hasn't abandoned her plan to fuse divine power into machines and decides to begin new experiments right away. You note this down and then <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak out</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013186"]="You didn't expect 140 to gift you his Mech Core. Even without the evidence of Rekenber Corp producing illegal weapons, this Mech Core will be a huge help. Thanks to 140, you quickly head to Einbroch to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask for W's help</color> and use Kafra's Emergency Teleport Route to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Juno</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100013187"]="Thanks to W, you managed to evade the institute's pursuit. However, it looks like there's more trouble brewing for you in Juno...?",
    ["TaskDescription100013188"]="At the airship station in Juno, you meet the departing guard member. Andre is surprised to see you and informs you that Philodis has been using every resource to find you during the three days you were missing. Now, if you don't <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Lord's Mansion</color> fast, you might not be able to withstand Philodis' fury...",
    ["TaskDescription100013189"]="Back at the Lord's Mansion, you brief the Lord, Philodis, and Fulkyn on what happened over the last three days and hand over 140's Mech Core to Fulkyn for analysis. It turns out to be a replica of Ymir's Heart. This revelation makes the Lord realize that Rekenber Corp's ambitions are not just about controlling the Republic; they might be working with Arunafeltz to control and replicate divine power. The war is far from over, and your burden remains heavy. But for now... maybe you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>console</color> the little girl who's been waiting at home for three days and got so anxious she made a fuss at the Lord's Mansion?",
    ["TaskDescription100013190"]="To calm the crying Martistine, you promise to take her along on your next trip if she follows your instructions the entire time. Now, after three exhausting days, you just want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go home and rest</color>, and maybe try the dinner Martistine prepared for you...",
    ["TaskDescription100014101"]="Today, you receive a message from Carl—he's having an important guest over in two hours and wants you to be there too. Since there's still time, and Martistine insists, you agree to head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>market</color> with her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>try</color> this super popular <color=#CA2E0AFF>limited-time dish</color> in Juno...",
    ["TaskDescription100014102"]="After a bit of a scramble at the market, you and Martistine finally get the last of the limited-time dessert—when a blond traveler suddenly asks if you'd let him have it. Turns out, it was the last dish he ever ate with his parents—before they died in an accident. He's only in Juno for the day and heading home tomorrow. He wants to take this chance to relive the flavor of that memory... After hearing his story, even the usually stubborn Martistine was touched and <color=#CA2E0AFF>handed the dessert over to him</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014103"]="After finishing the Cloud Soufflé, the blond young man thanks you both and swears he'll pay you back someday if he ever gets the chance. But Martistine seems a little disappointed, so you promise her you'll return to the market tomorrow. But for now... you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Lord's Mansion</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014104"]="You leave the market and arrive at the Lord's Mansion right on time, only to unexpectedly run into the blond young man once again. It turns out he is the important guest mentioned in the letter—Malam, an envoy from Arunafeltz. He is the adopted son of Neirun, one of the twelve Bishops of Arunafeltz, and the owner of its largest trading company, the Gilded Rose. He came here to invite Lord Carl to Arunafeltz's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dawn Moon Festival</color>. Unfortunately, Carl is too occupied with political affairs and asks you to meet the Pope in his place and deliver his gift. Carl's also hoping you can secretly look into that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir's Heart replica</color> found back in Einbroch. Naturally, Carl wishes you some well-earned holidays. It's not a dangerous task—you can even bring Martistine with you. You can already imagine how excited that little troublemaker's gonna be when she <color=#CA2E0AFF>hears about this</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014105"]="Time to pack up and set off! Next stop—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color>, the capital of Arunafeltz!",
    ["TaskDescription100014106"]="As you step into Rachel, the ever-adorable W greets you with her usual flair, giving a lively rundown of Rachel's customs and charms. The culture of the Arunafeltz is like no other—its people revere Goddess Freyja and hold alchemy sacred. W warns you to mind your manners and respect their faith; even a small misstep could spell trouble in these parts. Given the recent surge in child abduction cases, W also reminds you to keep Martistine close. A sweet face and a foreign accent make her a prime target for those lurking in the shadows. Finally, W points you toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple</color> and suggests you go witness the upcoming <color=#CA2E0AFF>ritual ceremony</color> in the Temple Plaza.",
    ["TaskDescription100014107"]="You never expected it, but while strolling near the Holy Spring, you suddenly come face-to-face with Israel. Ever since that farewell in Umbala, time has changed you both—but even so, the joy of this unexpected reunion is undeniable. Upon hearing that you're on your way to the Temple to watch the ceremony, Israel offers to show you the way himself. However, Martistine's robots may draw unwanted attention in Arunafeltz, where machinery is scarce and unfamiliar. Following his advice, you find <color=#CA2E0AFF>secluded bushes</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>temporarily hide the robots there</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014108"]="Following Israel's suggestion, you hide Farbauti and Laufey in the bushes east of the marketplace. Alright—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ceremony</color> is about to begin, so hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014109"]="In the plaza before the Temple, you witness the Pope perform a \"miracle\" with your own eyes, and the sight leaves you stunned. However, Israel tells you to hold your questions for now. You follow his lead and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>bushes</color> where Farbauti and Laufey are hidden.",
    ["TaskDescription100014110"]="Israel finally tells you the truth about the prayer ceremony. Turns out, the \"miracle\" the Pope performed isn't some divine blessing—it's actually alchemy that drains the lifeforce of believers. They use water from the Holy Spring as a catalyst to convert life energy, storing it inside the Pope's scepter to be used later. Years ago, Israel's mentor, Hibram, was exiled for opposing this practice. Now, Israel is back in Arunafeltz, determined to change things and fulfill his mentor's last wish. He asks for your help, but because of how complicated everything is, you're not sure you can give him an answer. Since Malam still hasn't returned to Arunafeltz and there's no one else to introduce you to the Pope, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go along with Israel</color> for now... just to see what he wants to show you.",
    ["TaskDescription100014111"]="Israel leads you to a small village in the Rachel Plains. To your surprise, you catch a group of Temple Guards shaking down the locals for taxes—by force. You don't hesitate—you step in and give the guards a serious beating. Intimidating at first, they quickly tuck their tails and run. But <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color>... doesn't look relieved. He actually seems worried.",
    ["TaskDescription100014112"]="As it turns out, the Temple Guards have been bullying the villagers like this for a long time. Israel fears that while your actions helped today, you can't protect the village forever. That's when he finally reveals why he brought you here—he wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>overthrow the entire system of Arunafeltz</color>. During the conversation, you also meet the village's current leader—a sharp-looking, silver-haired young man named Sartre. Israel tries to get your support, but you're hesitant. There's a lot at stake. And Sartre... he doesn't seem to trust you one bit. So, Israel makes a suggestion. The Dawn Moon Festival's still a few days away—why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay in Grey Wolf Village for a while</color>? It's a good chance to <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk to the villagers</color> and see things for yourself. Who knows? You might just change your mind...",
    ["TaskDescription100014113"]="During one of your days in Grey Wolf Village, you encountered a mother and child injured by the Temple Guards the other day. With Aloy injured, they've been barely scraping by, short on food, clothes, and medicine. You find some herbs for them and decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>cover Aloy's job</color> for a day just to make sure they still have some income. Aloy thanks you sincerely and invites you to have dinner with them after your work...",
    ["TaskDescription100014114"]="Turns out Aloy works in a quarry way out in the Rachel Plains—<color=#CA2E0AFF>digging up raw stones</color>. You talk to the foreman, and he shrugs and says it doesn't matter who shows up—wages are paid based on how many stones you find anyway. So, you grab a <color=#CA2E0AFF>metal detector</color> and head off to start your day of stone digging...",
    ["TaskDescription100014115"]="By the end of the long day, you've dug up three raw stones around the quarry. Now the question is... how much will the <color=#CA2E0AFF>foreman think</color> pay you?",
    ["TaskDescription100014116"]="Turns out, the foreman is far from impressed with your day's haul. He lowballs the payment, giving you way less than what you expected. You call him out, but he waves you off coldly, saying there are others willing to work for that little without complaint. Before things get ugly, a fellow worker steps in and helps calm the situation, quietly urging you to take the money and go. He warns you that in Arunafeltz, the jewelry industry is monopolized by the nobles. Crossing a foreman like this could bring more trouble than it's worth. So, with a sigh, you pocket the pitiful wage and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Grey Wolf Village</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014117"]="You pass the money to Aloy. Jeremy, puzzled, asks why it's less than usual, saying that aren't you a super-strong Adventurer? You feel a twinge of guilt, but Aloy smiles gently and says it's already more than enough. At her invitation, you stay for a simple dinner...",
    ["TaskDescription100014118"]="A few days later, you discover that Martistine has somehow ended up teaching math to the village kids. But their poor grasp of numbers sends her over the edge. Frustrated, she throws in the towel and demands that you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell Israel</color> that she quits!",
    ["TaskDescription100014119"]="From Israel, you learn that most of the people in Grey Wolf Village are descendants of nomads. Under the Arunafeltz's system, even basic needs like food, clothing, and education are tightly controlled. He does what he can, teaching the children when time allows—but it's nowhere near enough. You ask if there's anything you can do to help. He ponders for a while and tells you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Noble Estate</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Rachel</color>. Look for a tutor named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vanessa</color>. She's an old friend of Israel, and she secretly gathers books for the children here every now and then...",
    ["TaskDescription100014120"]="You make your way to the Noble Estate. At Vanessa's request, you help distribute books to the wealthy young nobles and ladies. To your surprise, they couldn't care less. Most of them ask you to take the books away and let Vanessa deal with them herself. Vanessa takes the chance to slip all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>books</color> to you and tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring them back to Grey Wolf Village</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014121"]="The kids are thrilled when you show up with all the brand-new books. Then they crowd around, practically begging you to read them a story...",
    ["TaskDescription100014122"]="One day, while staying in Grey Wolf Village, you overhear Israel and Sartre in the middle of a heated argument about something...",
    ["TaskDescription100014123"]="Before you can ask, Israel asks you to go with Sartre to Rachel. You agree... and then find out Sartre's way of earning money turns out to be fighting in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color>'s illegal matches...",
    ["TaskDescription100014124"]="You follow Sartre to the Underground Arena, and after a bit of coaxing from the bookie, the two of you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sign up</color> for a <color=#CA2E0AFF>special round</color> happening today. If you win, you'll get double the prize money...",
    ["TaskDescription100014125"]="Stay focused! Don't give up! As long as you <color=#CA2E0AFF>hold out till the end</color>, victory will be yours!",
    ["TaskDescription100014126"]="Though bloodied and bruised, you both survive. But the bookie doesn't honor the deal. Instead, he smugly tells you his boss wants to see you—and if you resist, things will get ugly. Just as the tension peaks, a masked young man appears from the crowd. He buys your death waiver without a word and escorts you <color=#CA2E0AFF>out of the arena</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014127"]="You're shocked to discover the masked young man is none other than Malam—the same person you met back in Juno...",
    ["TaskDescription100014128"]="After all that chaos, you and Sartre finally head back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grey Wolf Village</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014129"]="Time has slipped by while staying in the village. Though your path is still unclear, the Dawn Moon Festival draws near. There's no more time to delay—it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit the Gilded Rose Trading Company</color> and meet with Malam...",
    ["TaskDescription100014130"]="After wrapping up everything, you return to the trading company to meet Malam. He's ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take you to the Temple</color> to see the Pope...",
    ["TaskDescription100014131"]="Following Malam, you step <color=#CA2E0AFF>inside the Temple</color> for the first time. Up ahead, on the radiant throne, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pope</color> waits quietly for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>arrival</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014132"]="After the formalities, you're left to explore the Temple on your own— but then, you stumble upon the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pope</color>, looking dazed and lost in thought...",
    ["TaskDescription100014133"]="She seems confused, murmuring again and again about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gremlin Tear</color>. You decide to try fulfilling her request, hoping it might bring her back to her senses...",
    ["TaskDescription100014134"]="She seems confused, murmuring again and again about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hazy Herb</color>. You decide to try fulfilling her request, hoping it might bring her back to her senses...",
    ["TaskDescription100014135"]="After carrying out her request, she suddenly collapses. Neirun rushes in—but offers no explanation about what those items are for. She simply tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Malam</color> if you want answers...",
    ["TaskDescription100014136"]="In the Temple's <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prayer Room</color>, you meet an <color=#CA2E0AFF>elder</color> quietly asking the goddess for forgiveness...",
    ["TaskDescription100014137"]="His name is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jude</color>, and he leads you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple's Archives</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014138"]="There, you read through many books about the history of Arunafeltz—but the contents wildly contradict each other. Then Jude hands you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>notebook</color> and tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> it...",
    ["TaskDescription100014139"]="Outside the Temple's <color=#CA2E0AFF>garden</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Martistine</color> calls out to you. Yep. That look on her face? She's definitely planning something again...",
    ["TaskDescription100014140"]="Worried about Martistine, you follow her into a <color=#CA2E0AFF>room deep within the garden</color>. And there, you see...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014141"]="You reach out to the statue of Goddess Freyja without thinking—and it suddenly crumbles at your touch. Musa immediately declares it a sacrilege. Malam steps in, demanding that you undertake the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess' Trial</color>. Blindfolded, you're taken far from Rachel—into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color>. The only way to avoid imprisonment is to survive and find a way out...",
    ["TaskDescription100014142"]="The cave is a frozen maze, crawling with dangerous monsters. You press forward slowly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>clearing the monsters</color> that block your way.",
    ["TaskDescription100014143"]="You <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow</color> the trail—scattered bloodstains and signs of battle guide your path in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ice Cave</color> until you arrive at...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014144"]="In the cave, you find a strange wooden accessory. Malam tells you it's a keepsake from his father. And deeper <color=#CA2E0AFF>within the cave</color>, you discover...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014145"]="You find the remains of Malam's parents. At last, he can let go of the regret that's haunted him for fifteen years. It’s time to focus and keep <color=#CA2E0AFF>moving forward</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014146"]="In the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deepest part</color> of this area, you come across...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014147"]="Descending a set of stairs, you find something unexpected—a vast, man-made structure hidden within the cave. With curiosity, you continue your <color=#CA2E0AFF>exploration</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014148"]="Don't let the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters</color> surround you. Move forward carefully and stay alert!",
    ["TaskDescription100014149"]="Deeper in the Ice Cave, you discover signs of people living here. Malam points out that if there are supplies, it means someone's been coming and going. Friends or foes, one thing's certain—if there are people, <color=#CA2E0AFF>there must be a way out</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014150"]="A towering, snow-white monster charges at you out of nowhere! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Run</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014151"]="Malam recognizes the small creature that saved you—it might be the sacred <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ktullanux</color> worshipped by Freyja's followers. It leads you to a <color=#CA2E0AFF>hidden passage</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014152"]="You never would've guessed that the hidden passage Ktullanux showed you led straight into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple's underground area</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014153"]="Malam says this place has been abandoned for years... so why are there monsters <color=#CA2E0AFF>roaming</color> everywhere...?!",
    ["TaskDescription100014154"]="Through secret rooms and corridors, you find a <color=#CA2E0AFF>cellar</color> up ahead...",
    ["TaskDescription100014155"]="Oh no! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Martistine's in danger</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014156"]="You save Martistine from the monsters, but she's panicking, asking you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the crates nearby</color>. What's that...?!",
    ["TaskDescription100014157"]="The Temple's underground area is way bigger than you thought—and <color=#CA2E0AFF>across from the cellar</color>, there's another room...",
    ["TaskDescription100014158"]="You did not expect to find an experiential area full of machinery beneath the Temple. And inside those giant <color=#CA2E0AFF>incubation pools</color>... what are those?!",
    ["TaskDescription100014159"]="A monster bursts from the incubation pool and attacks you—but as it dies, it groans... in human language?! With more questions than answers, you approach the <color=#CA2E0AFF>experiment table...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription100014160"]="These <color=#CA2E0AFF>experiment logs</color> might hold the answers you've been searching for...",
    ["TaskDescription100014161"]="Up the stairs, you think you see... <color=#CA2E0AFF>someone familiar</color>? Who could it be...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014162"]="The Temple Guards are everywhere—you'll need to cause a diversion to get out of the Temple and reach Grey Wolf Village unnoticed. Following Neirun's advice, you head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pope's bedroom</color> for help...",
    ["TaskDescription100014163"]="The guards and attendants are gone—thanks to the Pope's distraction. Now's your chance—<color=#CA2E0AFF>get out of the Temple and go to Grey Wolf Village</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014164"]="At Grey Wolf Village, Sartre and Neirun finally sit down to talk. Six hundred years of hate isn't easy to forget, but Neirun's decree offering equal rights to the nomads clearly shakes him. He says he's willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hear the plan</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014165"]="Tonight, Malam wants to pull off an ambush, using a sleeping potion during Musa's deal with the Rekenber Corp to knock them out and capture them alive. He'll need the herbs the Pope had you find earlier, plus <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hill Wind's Feather</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014166"]="Night falls—it's time to sneak off to the airship station in Rachel Plains, just like you planned...",
    ["TaskDescription100014167"]="Malam's plan works perfectly! Musa and Sherlon are in custody, and you've got tons of proof that Yus was making illegal weapons and working with enemies. Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to Grey Wolf Village</color> and report to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Neirun</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014168"]="Just as everyone is celebrating, one of Neirun's aides brings bad news—the Pope has fallen into a deep sleep and won't wake. With no other choice, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>rush back to the Temple</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014169"]="Guided by Neirun's command, you and Malam search the Pope's bedroom. Your gaze locks onto it at once—a <color=#CA2E0AFF>diary</color> resting atop the Pope's desk...",
    ["TaskDescription100014170"]="From Neirun and Jude, you learn that the current Pope has a twin brother. Thinking back to the voice that has called out to you many times, you begin to suspect they might be the same person. In search of answers, you and Malam return to where it all began—the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shrine</color>, where that voice first whispered your name from the shadows...",
    ["TaskDescription100014171"]="As you touch the statue, several lines of text mysteriously appear on the base. They guide you toward a hidden room in the Temple's basement—<color=#CA2E0AFF>one that connects to the Ice Cave</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014172"]="Six statues stand in silent watch, each bearing a unique expression, each turned toward a different path... Could this mean something...?",
    ["TaskDescription100014173"]="As you examine the statues, you notice several statue parts scattered messily around the area...",
    ["TaskDescription100014174"]="Thinking about the puzzle, you and Malam realize these <color=#CA2E0AFF>parts</color> might be <color=#CA2E0AFF>reattached to the goddess statues</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014175"]="As expected, <color=#CA2E0AFF>that voice</color> returns once again...",
    ["TaskDescription100014176"]="Only two <color=#CA2E0AFF>parts</color> remain. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Reattach them</color> and see what happens next!",
    ["TaskDescription100014177"]="As soon as the last piece clicks into place, you hear something from the floor above—coming from the Goddess Shrine...",
    ["TaskDescription100014178"]="You and Malam return to the Goddess Shrine and see that the text on the base has vanished, replaced by a purple feather. When you reach out to touch it, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>blinding light</color> suddenly surrounds you...",
    ["TaskDescription100014179"]="The true incarnation of the Goddess Freyja finally appears before you—he is the boy you saw in the Ice Cave. To save his sister, he entrusts you with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Heron's Feather</color> filled with divine power and asks you to deliver it to her...",
    ["TaskDescription100014180"]="Return to the Pope's bedroom at once and wake her up!",
    ["TaskDescription100014181"]="Lastly... as Lumi suggested, <color=#CA2E0AFF>check</color> the gem on the Pope's <color=#CA2E0AFF>scepter</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014182"]="Once the Temple bell rings three times, that's your cue to <color=#CA2E0AFF>step forward</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014183"]="Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>expose Musa and Yus</color>—right in front of all the Priests and followers!",
    ["TaskDescription100014184"]="Things unfold as planned—driven into a corner, Musa reveals Yus as the culprit behind it all. But then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sherlon</color> breaks free from his restraints, takes Neirun hostage, and escapes the Temple. You and Sartre split up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go after him</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014185"]="Eventually, Sherlon's trail vanishes near the city gate. According to witnesses, he might have been picked up by accomplices and escaped toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014186"]="Though Sherlon has slipped away, justice claimed another—Musa. Now, return to the Temple... and check on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Neirun</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Malam</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100014187"]="With everything settled, it's finally time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enjoy the festival</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription100014188"]="You never expected Martistine to be kidnapped during the bustling festival. You and Malam search separately but find no trace of her. The only clue points once again to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100014189"]="On Malam's suggestion, you head back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color> to get help from Lord Carl...",
    ["TaskDescription100014190"]="Leaving the Lord's Mansion, you wander the streets of Juno in a daze... and somehow end up back at the Cloud Soufflé shop...",
    ["TaskDescription100015101"]="Today, you receive a letter from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015102"]="As promised, Malam has Farbauti and Laufey carefully packed and delivered to Juno with the Gilded Rose caravan. Before signing for the delivery, though, the courier advises you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the goods carefully</color> for any transport damage...",
    ["TaskDescription100015103"]="Andre brings urgent news—Rowland, president of Rekenber Corp, has boarded an airship to Juno. It's time to head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color> and finish the final preparations for the trip to Lighthalzen...",
    ["TaskDescription100015104"]="Philodis arranges a guide for you. You just need to meet him at the train station in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Einbroch</color> and he'll help you sneak into the Rekensheim Institute.",
    ["TaskDescription100015105"]="To your surprise, Philodis' contact turns out to be Dave. He's settled in the Hugel region with the Einbech Village and started a new life. To thank you, he tells you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sewers</color> beneath Einbroch secretly lead to Lighthalzen...",
    ["TaskDescription100015106"]="To get through the sewers safely, you have to deal with the guards Irumina set up here...",
    ["TaskDescription100015107"]="Deep in the sewers, you find the passage that leads to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekensheim Institute</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015108"]="Crawling through the tight sewer pipes, you finally make it into the Rekensheim Institute's <color=#CA2E0AFF>storage room</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015109"]="To your surprise, the institute is empty. The eerie silence makes you think it's a trap, and then, at the end of the corridor, you see a <color=#CA2E0AFF>familiar figure</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015110"]="Running into Seyren again eases your worries about all the strange things happening. In a situation like this, <color=#CA2E0AFF>sticking with him</color> feels like the best choice...",
    ["TaskDescription100015111"]="In the deepest hall of the institute, you find your friends lying unconscious. Thankfully, they're still alive. To figure out what happened, you'd better <color=#CA2E0AFF>wake them up</color> first...",
    ["TaskDescription100015112"]="Ivy seems fine, but he's anxious about Celia. Maybe give him a little space and check on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trinity</color> first...",
    ["TaskDescription100015113"]="Trinity wakes up, but from her words, you learn that Orfeo might have met a terrible fate. Overcome with grief, she can barely speak, so you decide to check on the others for now...",
    ["TaskDescription100015114"]="Zenlur's full of energy, and he clearly doesn't need your help. Forget him and go check on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Randel</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100015115"]="Everyone else is awake now—only <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cecil</color> remains unconscious...",
    ["TaskDescription100015116"]="Forced by Baroshev, you all begin a \"killing game.\" The <color=#CA2E0AFF>identity card</color> you draw reads...?",
    ["TaskDescription100015117"]="Once everyone gets their identity cards, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> looks like he wants to say something...",
    ["TaskDescription100015118"]="The team isn't as united as you hoped. Ivy and Cecil decide to move on their own, and everyone else has their own plans. Can you really escape like this? With that doubt in mind, you and Goldie start <color=#CA2E0AFF>exploring</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>institute</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015119"]="After leaving the library, you head toward the <color=#CA2E0AFF>central area</color> of the institute...",
    ["TaskDescription100015120"]="Just like the underground temple in Rachel, this institute is filled with modified experimental subjects. The deeper you explore, the stranger and more mysterious the place feels...",
    ["TaskDescription100015121"]="After a bit of searching, you and Goldie find some clues about the human experiments. It's probably time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to the main hall</color> and share what you've learned with the others...",
    ["TaskDescription100015122"]="After a brief discussion, everyone's exhausted and decides to head back to their rooms for some <color=#CA2E0AFF>rest</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015123"]="Baroshev's voice echoes over the broadcast, ordering everyone to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather in the main hall</color>. A bad feeling creeps up inside you...",
    ["TaskDescription100015124"]="Everyone still has doubts about Zenlur's death. To uncover the truth, you and Goldie decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenlur's room</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100015125"]="According to Seyren, he last saw Zenlur near the incubation pool at the end of the corridor. Maybe there's a clue left there...?",
    ["TaskDescription100015126"]="Near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>emergency exit</color> by the incubation pool, you and Goldie run into Ivy. He's...?",
    ["TaskDescription100015127"]="Ivy casts an alchemical spell on Celia to track her location. If you can find her, maybe you'll find the others too. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>locked door</color> nearby...",
    ["TaskDescription100015128"]="To make it up to Ivy, you offer to help him brew a Revival Potion. First, he needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Aurora Flowers</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015129"]="Next comes the most basic component in alchemy—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Vegetable Oil</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015130"]="Finally, help Ivy <color=#CA2E0AFF>mix</color> all the <color=#CA2E0AFF>materials</color> together...",
    ["TaskDescription100015131"]="With everything settled, you can finally head back to your room for a bit of <color=#CA2E0AFF>rest</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription100015132"]="Trinity tells you she hasn't seen Goldie for a long time. Worried, you both decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look around</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015133"]="In the library, you witness Goldie's death with your own eyes...",
    ["TaskDescription100015134"]="Baroshev won't let you examine Goldie's body unless you defeat the <color=#CA2E0AFF>swordswoman</color> beside him...",
    ["TaskDescription100015135"]="In the <color=#CA2E0AFF>main hall</color>, you'll bring this twisted game to an end...",
    ["TaskDescription100015136"]="Those who should have been dead stand once more, turned into soulless puppets by Baroshev's control. If you refuse to fight them, <color=#CA2E0AFF>retreat</color> is your only option...",
    ["TaskDescription100015137"]="You can't let Cecil and Randel's sacrifice be in vain. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moving forward</color> is the only thing you can do...",
    ["TaskDescription100015138"]="Beneath the institute, you and Seyren finally find your <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing companions</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015139"]="No matter how you and Seyren call out, those inside the capsule tanks don't respond at all...",
    ["TaskDescription100015140"]="In the underground cell of the institute, you finally find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Madelina</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015141"]="Martistine has fallen into a coma after being injected with a reagent. To wake her, you'll need to find the right <color=#CA2E0AFF>serum</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015142"]="Before Martistine wakes up, you need to find an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Acid Solvent</color> that can melt the lock and open the cell door...",
    ["TaskDescription100015143"]="You've got the Acid Solvent. Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to the cell</color> and get Martistine out...",
    ["TaskDescription100015144"]="Guided by Madelina, you and Seyren reach the institute's central control room and <color=#CA2E0AFF>cut off</color> the core hub's power...",
    ["TaskDescription100015145"]="May their souls rest in peace forever in Odin's embrace...",
    ["TaskDescription100015153"]="After countless struggles, you and Martistine finally reach the Tomb of the Fallen. But is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Madelina</color> really waiting for you here...?",
    ["TaskDescription100015154"]="The key to leaving the Tomb of the Fallen lies in the sewer system connected to Einbroch. First, <color=#CA2E0AFF>open the drain valve</color> to clear the pipes...",
    ["TaskDescription100015155"]="Next, check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>water level monitor</color>, which should be within the safe range...",
    ["TaskDescription100015156"]="Finally, enter the password on the security panel...",
    ["TaskDescription100015157"]="Everything's ready. The moment for the final farewell has come...",
    ["TaskDescription100015158"]="You and Martistine finally make it back to Juno. But at the airship station, a man in a researcher's coat blocks your way...",
    ["TaskDescription100015159"]="It feels like waking from a terrible nightmare, this moment, you're finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>home</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription100015160"]="At last, <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Lord's Mansion</color> and hand the core over to Fulkyn...",
    ["TaskDescription10110"]="Now, I'm going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Expanded Super Novice!",
    ["TaskDescription11000"]="1st Class - Swordsman",
    ["TaskDescription110001101"]="You meet a depressed boy named Jacob on the street. Through your conversation with him, you learn that Jacob wants to join the children's choir but is too shy to learn new songs from the other kids.\nAfter hearing this, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help Jacob learn the lyrics of a nursery rhyme</color>. After all, Kiki once said the spirit of helping others is an important part of what makes an adventurer!",
    ["TaskDescription110001102"]="You ask Beasley, the smartest-looking boy you could find, for the first line of the nursery rhyme.\nYou discover that he's only interested in little <color=#CA2E0AFF>Frogs</color>. It looks like you'll have to get what he wants before you get the answer!",
    ["TaskDescription110001106"]="You finally learn all the lyrics to the nursery rhyme from four kids. Hurry and tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jacob</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110001107"]="With your help, Jacob makes friends with the choir children. Now he's smiling again! A bard nearby named Herbert happens to witness the scene and lets out a deep sigh. He tells you that the lyrics of the nursery rhyme come from a poem called the Legend of the Kingdom's Founding.\nAfter hearing Herbert's explanation, you finally understand what the four lines of the poem mean. Unfortunately, the lyrics only make up the first half of the poem. The second half may be in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Library</color>...\nHerbert looks at you eagerly. Why don't you help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the second half of the poem</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110001108"]="To learn the full poem, you go to the Prontera Library and find the book, Legend of the Kingdom's Founding. To your surprise, the second half of it has been erased! The librarian, Rowan, tells you that the last person who borrowed the book was the exorcist priestess Parni Briar, who serves the Gaebolg Family... This all seems very suspicious. It looks like an <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigation of Parni is in order!</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110001109"]="At the church, you meet priestess Margaret, who is lamenting the injustice Parni had suffered. She wishes to find a way to help Parni get back on her feet.\nDuring your conversation, you learn that Parni was just recently banished from the palace, but Margaret never asked why... For some reason, you get more and more of a sense that the whole thing has to do with that book, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Legend of the Kingdom's Founding</color>. Instead of trying to figure it out yourself, why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and ask Parni</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110001110"]="You finally find Parni Briar in the cemetery behind the cathedral, but she avoids talking about the Legend of the Kingdom's Founding and makes you clean the three tombstones with chiseled golden crosses...\nWhile cleaning, you discover that they're the tombstones of the current king, Tristan III's three children! Even more unbelievable is that the three princes died on the same day! ...It looks like the situation is not nearly as simple as you thought. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Parni for more information</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110001111"]="To your surprise Parni had secretly left, leaving behind only a diary.\nAfter reading it, you learn that Parni was expelled from the palace for failing to exorcise the princes and that she was also researching the second half of the Legend of the Kingdom's Founding... I wonder if Parni has already discovered something?",
    ["TaskDescription110001112"]="After learning that the two of you share the same thinking, Parni finally tells you full story of the Legend of the Kingdom's Founding.\nIt turns out that before the evil serpent Jormungand died, it put a curse on the Gaebolg Family that causes the eldest son from each generation to die from snake venom. However, this still doesn't explain the deaths of the second and third princes... Hurry and get her an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eye of Truth</color> from a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Myst</color>, then use it to find out the truth behind the incident!",
    ["TaskDescription110001113"]="In order to make a Truth Serum, Parni needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yellow Gemstones</color>. Hurry and get them for her.",
    ["TaskDescription110001114"]="The both of you are well prepared. Now follow Parni to find the truth!",
    ["TaskDescription110001115"]="You splash the Truth Serum on Prince Hans' body and watch the snake scale mark on his chest fade away! Parni states that this phenomenon confirms her theory—Prince Reige and Prince Hans did not die from the evil serpent's curse, but were poisoned by a human!\nAs you wonder who poisoned the two princes, Parni suddenly remembers that Prince Hans's <color=#CA2E0AFF>attendant, Oman</color>, had been behaving very suspiciously... There's no time to waste. Go to Oman's house to continue your investigation!",
    ["TaskDescription110001116"]="Oman's wife, Helena, conceals the fact that her husband is hiding in their home. However, you are able to eavesdrop on their conversation, during which you learn that Oman's child, Abu, is seriously ill and in urgent need of funds for medical care... His condition can't be relieved through exorcism. Find the cure-all <color=#CA2E0AFF>Leaf of Yggdrasil</color> and bring it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Helena</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110001117"]="Helena is very grateful for your help in getting the Leaf of Yggdrasil. She tells you that Oman has been hiding in the storage room ever since getting home and that he didn't want to see anyone. Even so, she is willing to do her best to persuade Oman to meet you.\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Head to the storage room at night as arranged and wait for Oman</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110001118"]="You encounter an assassin outside the storage room that fatally wounds Oman!\nYou learn from the dying Oman that someone had promised him that if he poisoned the princes' food, he would receive a large sum of money afterwards...\nYou follow Oman's directions and find the bottle of poison he used under a tree. What will <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni</color> say when she learns of all this?",
    ["TaskDescription110001119"]="After hearing everything, Parni speculates that the culprit behind it must be an extremely cunning and ruthless person... She fears that the murderer will do even more terrible things, so she asks you to take her savings to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Helena</color> and persuade her to leave Prontera with Abu as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription110001120"]="You bring the poison bottle to the palace as evidence on Parni's behalf. However, since the king is mourning the loss of his sons, he's not available to see it. You have no choice but to explain the situation to the regent, Ian Walter.\nHe oddly states that he'll take over the case and asks you not to spread word about it. He also wants you to tell Parni to stay out of matters she shouldn't involve herself in...\nIs this really the end of the case?...\nYou leave the palace with misgivings.",
    ["TaskDescription110002101"]="To learn the second line of the nursery rhyme, you ask the most honest-looking kid, Peppy.\nHe states that his instructor likes <color=#CA2E0AFF>sparkling gemstones</color> the most and wants you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Wings Mine</color> to get one for him... You feel a slight unease. This isn't a typical instructor...",
    ["TaskDescription110003101"]="To figure out the third line of the nursery rhyme, you inquire with Lily, the most sensible-looking kid.\nShe expresses how much she misses her grandfather, who lives by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>, and wants a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pumpkin</color> just like the one grown at her grandfather's house.... For such a heartwarming little angel, there's no reason not to help her fulfill her wish!",
    ["TaskDescription110004101"]="For the fourth line of the nursery rhyme, you ask Rayns, who looks the most enthusiastic.\nHe says he can't remember anything when he's hungry and wants you to help him buy a dish called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora Prawns</color>... You wonder how this legendary dish tastes like...",
    ["TaskDescription110005101"]="The merchant instructor, Hamid, tells you to halt and begins complimenting you... Just as you wonder what he's up to, Hamid changes his tune and asks you to do a job for him.\nIt turns out that Hamid's student, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wulf</color>, hasn't turned in his homework in a long time. Hamid heard that he's been wracking his brain a lot at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>smithy</color> lately. Why don't you go see if Wulf is having any trouble?",
    ["TaskDescription110005102"]="Through your conversation with Wulf, you learn that he's also upset with his inability to complete his assignment.\nIt turns out that Hamid requires Wulf to smelt high-quality Gold, Silver, and Iron, but having grown up in Morroc, Wulf has no idea where to get the metals he needs to smelt them! He says that if he doesn't complete this assignment, he won't be able to become a merchant. Hurry and find the<color=#CA2E0AFF>10 ores of Gold, Silver, and Iron each</color> he needs for smelting!",
    ["TaskDescription110005103"]="You bring Wulf the ores he needs, and now there's just one last step before he can start smelting.\nWulf says it looks like the fire in the smithy's furnace isn't burning hot enough. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>carpenter Old Clay</color> and borrow some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wood</color> for the fire.",
    ["TaskDescription110005104"]="According to Wulf, smelting top quality metal requires strict temperature control of the furnace fire. He hopes you can assist him with completing his assignment. When he puts the ore into the furnace, <color=#CA2E0AFF>watch for the right timing and add the Wood</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110005105"]="After helping Wulf with his assignment, you finally have time to chat with him.\nIt turns out that Wulf wants to become a merchant because he hopes to form a caravan dedicated to supplying Morroc so that the people of his hometown can live life without worrying about food shortages. Wulf says that his family never could understood his thinking, especially his older brother, Halmod, who he has always had trouble getting along with. Therefore, he plans to work hard on his own to achieve his dreams and prove himself. While Wulf goes to the job advancement ceremony, look after his little sister <color=#CA2E0AFF>Agnes</color>, who's playing in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>garden</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110005106"]="Agnes uses the fresh flowers you picked to make two <color=#CA2E0AFF>wreaths</color>, one of which you are asked to give to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wulf</color> on her behalf. As for the other... You wonder who she wants to give it to...",
    ["TaskDescription110005107"]="Feeling grateful upon seeing the wreath his sister Agnes made, Wulf states that he'll work twice as hard to earn money to buy her pretty dresses and cute dolls!\nBut Agnes doesn't seem very happy to hear this. Turns out she's more concerned about the conflict between Wulf and Halmod than the gifts at the moment... Agnes hopes that her pretty flowers can help her two brothers resolve their differences faster and be on friendly terms again. Hurry and bring her other <color=#CA2E0AFF>wreath</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Halmod</color> in Morroc!",
    ["TaskDescription110005108"]="You travel to Morroc in search of Halmod but find that he's not at home.\nAfter talking to Maximilian, you learn that there has been another monster rampage in Morroc and that Halmod has gone <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside Morroc</color> to get rid of the monsters... Hurry and check out the situation!",
    ["TaskDescription110005109"]="Halmod is very happy when you give him the wreath! He says he wants to dedicate the victory in battle to his sister and invites you to take up arms and fight alongside him!\nAfter killing the Anacondaq, Halmod seems even more excited, stating that he will go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color> next to continue the fight. Then he rushes ahead before you can respond...",
    ["TaskDescription110005110"]="This time your targets are the Golems of Sograt Desert. Since these monsters have caused trouble for the local inhabitants, Halmod decides to extract the Golems' Hard Stone Hearts and give them to the inhabitants as compensation.\nIn the ensuing battle, Halmod shocks you by gouging out a hundred Hard Stone Hearts in one go. Before you can pick your jaw up from the floor, he's already rushing towards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>other side of the desert</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110005111"]="After fighting a few battles together, Halmod is really impressed with your strength! He says that a warrior such as yourself will be warmly welcomed by the Lugenburg Family, and he hopes that you can follow him <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Morroc</color> to see Maximilian.",
    ["TaskDescription110005112"]="You meet up with a very anxious Maximilian in Morroc.\nWhen you speak with him, you learn that Halmod's brother Meyer has been kidnapped! The kidnapper left a threatening letter demanding a huge sum of <color=#CA2E0AFF>50 million Zeny</color> for Meyer's life...\nThere's no way the Lugenburg Family can pay this kind of sum... No time to lose. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wulf, the only family member with wealth,</color> to ask for his help!",
    ["TaskDescription110005113"]="When you tell Wulf about Meyer's kidnapping, he's shocked and says he will immediately return to Morroc with Agnes to rescue his brother!\nBut when you go to the garden where Agnes is supposed to be, she's not there. All you find is a threatening letter left on the ground... The letter says that Agnes has also been kidnapped and it demands a Tiara from the head of a Maya in exchange for her life. You never would have thought that the two children of the Lugenburg Family would both be in danger on the same day!",
    ["TaskDescription110005114"]="After arriving outside of Morroc, Wulf entrusts you to take the money he earned to Halmod while he tries to obtain the Tiara from the Maya to exchange for Agnes.\nThere's no time for delay. Follow Halmod to the site of the exchange described in the letter: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hope Oasis</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110005115"]="While you're waiting at the dunes of the desert oasis, a suspicious thief arrives! He claims that he doesn't know anything and was only hired to deliver a letter...\nAfter reading the second threatening letter, you discover that the kidnapper knows quite a bit about what goes on in the Lugenburg Family... Who could it be? Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Signal Flare</color> the thief gave you and go outside <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> to expose the culprit's true identity.",
    ["TaskDescription110005116"]="You can't believe that the two kidnappings were just a ploy orchestrated by Meyer and Agnes themselves!\nAccording to Agnes's explanation, their goal was to encourage Wulf and Halmod to make up, but neither brother did what they anticipated, especially Wulf, who charged into Ant Cavern on his own to try and fight the queen...\nOh no, according to Halmod, Wulf is no match for a monster of Maya's caliber! He's probably already in danger. Hurry into the depths of Ant Cavern and go to Wulf's aid!",
    ["TaskDescription110005117"]="There are monsters wandering around all over Ant Cavern... Where could Wulf be? Hurry up and find him!",
    ["TaskDescription110005118"]="You finally find Wulf deep inside the cavern, but it looks like he's already wounded by the ant monsters and has lost all his strength...\nMeyer comes out of nowhere and tells you even worse news: Agnes has been abducted by Maya! Halmod asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>stay behind to look after Meyer and the wounded Wulf</color> while he goes off on his own to look for the missing Agnes...\nWho would've thought the their ploy would lead to so many consequences? Hopefully everyone ends up safe and sound!",
    ["TaskDescription110005119"]="You find the herbs for an antidote as requested by Meyer, who says he'll take care of the wounded Wulf. He hopes you can still go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Halmod and help him save Agnes</color> as soon as possible. After all, their situation could be more complicated than it seems!",
    ["TaskDescription110005120"]="You find the abducted Agnes with Maya as well as Halmod, who went to look for her! The two of you fight side by side and eventually save Agnes...\nAfter all that has happened, Halmod's mindset must have changed somewhat. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>listen to what he has to say now</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110006101"]="You encounter a young woman named Alice sighing in despair. After some conversation, you learn that her best friend Veronica Gaebolg is getting married and the ceremony is today, but Alice is too busy with academy business to attend...\nSeeing Alice's distress, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the church</color> and help deliver her carefully-prepared gift to Veronica!",
    ["TaskDescription110006102"]="At the entrance of the church, a young man named Chino also seems to be having some trouble. He states that he's here for today's wedding, but he recently lost the Wedding Invitation. Now he's unable to enter the venue...\nAfter speaking with him further, you learn that he passed by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Odin's Statue</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force Training Course</color> before arriving at the church. Perhaps the invitation was dropped near one of those places? Go and help Chino find it.",
    ["TaskDescription110006103"]="You really found the missing invitation at the Defense Force Training Course! It was picked up by a soldier named Glen, but it seems like he doesn't plan on simply returning it...\nHe says that if you want him to give it back, you'll have to ask if his fists agree first! It looks like you'll have <color=#CA2E0AFF>accept his challenge</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110006104"]="Glen apparently underestimated your strength. After your bout, you win back the missing Wedding Invitation. It seems to have extraordinary significance for Chino, so hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return it to Chino</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110006105"]="As expected, Chino is ecstatic to get his Wedding Invitation back! He says that the wedding ceremony begins in less than an hour and asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait inside the church</color>. As for him... he seems to need some time to prepare something.",
    ["TaskDescription110006106"]="At the wedding, you meet Thurman, the Richard Family housekeeper. He's distressed because the groom-to-be, young master Bohr of the Richard Family, still hasn't arrived.\nYou learn from Thurman that the bride, Veronica, is grieving over the loss of her father in the cemetery behind the church. Bohr should be by Veronica's side at such times, but he still hasn't shown up...\nRemember that gift Alice entrusted you to deliver? Go give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Veronica</color>. Hopefully, she'll get some comfort after receiving a gift from her best friend.",
    ["TaskDescription110006107"]="Veronica is delighted to receive the gift from Alice, but it still doesn't make the melancholy in her eyes completely go away...\nFrom your conversation with her, you find out that Veronica doesn't have much confidence in her marriage to Bohr. She fears that he was forced to marry her due to political concerns. Since she had fallen for him long ago, she hopes her feelings can be reciprocated...\nFor today's wedding, Veronica even prepared a crown made from flowers bearing her name, hoping that the Veronica Flowers will bring her confidence and fortune. But Aronst, who had gone to retrieve it, has yet to return...\nQuickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the palace and find Aronst</color>. See if he's in some kind of trouble!",
    ["TaskDescription110006108"]="Aronst glumly informs you that the flower crown has been taken by a dreadful crow! You manage to get it back, only to find out that the flower crown is broken and can't be used at the wedding...\nIt's time to get the help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smile Assistance</color>. See if she has a way to fix the broken crown!",
    ["TaskDescription110006109"]="Smile Assistance offers to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>repair the flower crown</color>, but she needs enough Veronica Flowers to do it. They're said to only grow in remote areas on tall cliffs and require meticulous care to stay alive.\nYou find the rare Veronica Flowers based on her tip, but to your surprise, you discover that they were grown by Chino! After hearing your purpose for collecting the flowers, Chino gives you permission to take them. However, he wants you to return any extra flowers that you have left after the repair is complete so that he can make the proper arrangements for them...\nSeems like Chino has unusual feelings for these flowers.",
    ["TaskDescription110006110"]="With the help of Smile Assistance, the flower crown is restored to its original form! Aronst happily invites you to return to the church with him to deliver Veronica the crown, but you remember that there's one more thing that must be done before that can happen, which is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring back the remaining flowers to their owner, Chino</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110006111"]="You unexpectedly overhear a conversation between Chino and a strange man on the cliff but can't understand what they're talking about at all.\nAfter returning the flowers to Chino, he tells you that he wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to the church</color> with you to attend the wedding. It's about to begin, so hurry up and get going!",
    ["TaskDescription110006112"]="You can't believe such a terrible incident has occurred at the much-anticipated wedding!\nThe sudden appearance of the assassin and the poisoning of Bohr seem to indicate some sort of conspiracy... Anyway, try to save Bohr's life first. Follow Archbishop Wolmas' instructions and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather the three types of magic cores needed to cast the high-level magic spell</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110006113"]="Archbishop Wolmas asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the three types of magic cores around Bohr</color>. Hurry and do what he says!",
    ["TaskDescription110006114"]="Using his powerful healing magic, Archbishop Wolmas is able to save Bohr.\nNow that he's finally out of danger, finding out who poisoned him is paramount. After some analysis, all evidence now points to Chino, who disappeared from the wedding venue...\nVeronica seems to be the only one who disagrees with him being the perpetrator. Why don't you accept Veronica's request and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Commander Bernard for information</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110006115"]="Through speaking with Bernard, you learn that he had been investigating the capital's sewers with Bohr before the wedding.\nIt turns out that Bohr suspects the deaths of the three princes of the Gaebolg Family are somehow related to the escaped alchemist Baroshev. After some testing, it was indeed proven that the poison ingested by the princes was developed by Baroshev...\nThey say Bohr spoke with Court Clerk Akand following the results. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk with Akand</color> and see if you can get any new information!",
    ["TaskDescription110006116"]="Akand tells you that he had previously overheard a conversation between Chino and a stranger. While listening to them, Akand learned some startling information, which is that Chino is the illegitimate son of the Richard Family and someone is trying to instigate him to take Bohr's place!\nAs you are speaking with Akand, Fitz informs you two that the Defense Force has captured the suspicious Chino at the West Gate Cemetery. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go and hear what Chino has to say!</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110006117"]="From talking to Chino, you find out that he left the wedding to follow a suspicious man he had seen before!\nIt's reported that after the attack on Bohr, the man took advantage of the confusion to grab Veronica's Flower Crown and slip away into the sewers, where he mixed in with a group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>hobos</color>... If the flower crown is retrieved, Chino's innocence can be proven. There's no time to waste. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the sewers and investigate</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110006118"]="You use your wits to figure out who the hobo really is! It turns out that he is the true culprit, who poisoned the flower crown to murder Bohr...\nNow that the truth has been revealed, deliver the Veronica's Flower Crown to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Simmons</color>, the person guarding Chino!",
    ["TaskDescription110006119"]="After Bohr awakens from his coma, you take the opportunity to tell everyone what really happened.\nBohr states that he never suspected Chino and that he already had a theory about the true identity of the perpetrator. Veronica looks like she wants to say something to Bohr but can't get it out, so you decide to help her. You ask Bohr how he truly feels about their marriage, to which he responds that he truly loves Veronica and wants to make up for Veronica's heartache by redoing the wedding!\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow everyone back to the church</color> to witness the most sacred moment of the loving couple's lives!",
    ["TaskDescription110007101"]="Hamid tells you to stop once again and says that he's entrusting you with an important matter concerning his happiness for the rest of his life!\nWhile speaking with him, you learn that Hamid befriended a pen pal named K. She showed great interest in Hamid and even asked to meet him in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta</color>. Hamid believes that K is really into him, but he's worried that she will overlook his heart of gold after seeing his appearance...\nAfter careful consideration, Hamid asks you to take a bouquet of <color=#CA2E0AFF>roses</color> to meet his <color=#CA2E0AFF>pen pal K</color> instead!",
    ["TaskDescription110007102"]="You meet Hamid's pen pal K in Alberta, who turns out to be a woman named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kaitlyn</color>.\nWithout hesitation, she reveals that her purpose in inviting you here is to get your help in fighting against the rich and powerful <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Family</color> since you are well versed in the art of business...\nWho could've thought that such an ordinary woman would be bold enough to go against one of the seven royal families!",
    ["TaskDescription110007103"]="Kaitlyn tells you that she is an investor in the Lindra Chamber of Commerce and is fighting hard against the Wigner Family to prevent them from putting pressure on the organization and jeopardizing them again.\nAfter some discussion, it's decided that you will go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Labyrinth</color> to obtain rare goods for her so that her organization can outcompete the Libra Group and Serpentrod Group. To assist you, Kaitlyn is sending <color=#CA2E0AFF>Betty Lindra</color> with you to the desert.",
    ["TaskDescription110007104"]="It seemed like Betty prepared herself well for this mission.\nHowever, when the two of you were about to go deep into the Sphinx Labyrinth to obtain <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sparkling Light Granules</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zerom</color>, Betty stated that such a job was too dangerous for a delicate young lady such as herself...\nYou are pretty sure that you have heard this excuse before...",
    ["TaskDescription110007105"]="You get enough Sparkling Light Granules from Zerom, but Betty says she still needs <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Chests</color> carried by the monster <color=#CA2E0AFF>Requiem</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110007106"]="You get enough Mysterious Chests from Requiems, but Betty says she still needs <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ancient Egyptian Swords</color> carried by the monster <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pasana</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110007107"]="After a lot of hard work, you finally help Betty collect enough rare items. Hurry <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Alberta</color> and give them to Kaitlyn!",
    ["TaskDescription110007108"]="Betty volunteers to help the Lindra Chamber of Commerce sell the precious commodities. Kaitlyn seems to have something else to say...",
    ["TaskDescription110007109"]="Kaitlyn received news that the Wigner Family's two merchant groups, Libra and Serpentrod, are planning to fight for the sole distribution rights of an item from the Merchant's Guild! This is a golden opportunity to take the Wigner Family down a peg while also gaining some benefits for the Lindra Chamber of Commerce. To win the bid, Kaitlyn states that she needs an accessory called the Crown of Eassis.\nHowever, when you ask the accessory merchant Felix about obtaining the crown, she says that such a rare treasure is very difficult to acquire and that to make this legendary queen's crown, you must get <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Magic Stones</color> from the god of the underworld, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anubis</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110007110"]="With your assistance, Felix finally crafts the legendary accessory, the Crown of Eassis!\nFelix cautiously warns you that this accessory is known to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bewitch people</color>. It makes you wonder, what exactly does Kaitlyn intend to do with it?",
    ["TaskDescription110007111"]="Kaitlyn states that Jurgen Wigner, the chairman of the Libra Group, is well known for his charm and unconventional ways. She asks you to put on the Crown of Eassis and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jurgen</color> at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sapphire Blue Tavern</color>. There she wants you to use the crown to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bewitch him into revealing the Libra Group's reserve price for the bidding</color>.\nYou have a vague feeling that Kaitlyn knows Jurgen very well...",
    ["TaskDescription110007112"]="Jurgen is completely caught off guard by your amazing beauty.\nHe tells you without reservations that the Libra Group's Bidding Sheet is in the possession of his assistant, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pollard</color>, and that he is currently <color=#CA2E0AFF>near the Merchant Guild</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110007113"]="After acquiring the Libra Group's Bidding Sheet, Kaitlyn states that the next phase is dealing with the Serpentrod Group.\nShe requests that you to go to the Food Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color> and ask if there is any wine that can instantly intoxicate someone upon drinking it. She emphasizes that this is crucial for reaching the goal.",
    ["TaskDescription110007114"]="By following Rachel's directions, you are able to find a brewer named Juke that can make strong wine.\nHowever, when you try to obtain the legendary Wine of No Worries from him, you find out that it's already in his belly... Looks like your only option is to brew the Wine of No Worries again according to Juke's instructions. For that, you need to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Earth Spirit Essences</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wormtails</color> first!",
    ["TaskDescription110007115"]="You give the Earth Spirit Essences to Juke, but he suddenly realizes that there is an important brewing ingredient missing!\nDo as Juke says and get the required <color=#CA2E0AFF>Intact Bear Paws</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bigfoots</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110007116"]="You give the Intact Bear Paw to Juke, but he suddenly realizes that there is another important brewing ingredient missing!\nDo as Juke says and get the required <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pure Saps</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Willows</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110007117"]="After some hard work, you finally gather all the ingredients you need to make the Wine of No Worries. Now do as Juke says and <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait a little in front of the brewing vat</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110007118"]="Kaitlyn states that the chairman of the Serpentrod Group, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isaac Wigner</color>, is a naive person and a collector of fine wine. If you deliver the Wine of No Worries to Isaac, who is currently in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wigner Family Mansion</color>, you will be able to get the young man drunk and <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain the Serpentrod Group's reserve price for the bidding.</color>.\nYou have a vague feeling that Kaitlyn knows Isaac very well...",
    ["TaskDescription110007119"]="Utilizing the potent Wine of No Worries, you obtain the Serpentrod Group's Bidding Sheet without breaking a sweat.\nKaitlyn happily states that she's finally ready to go to the Merchant's Guild's bidding and asks that you bring the head of Wigner Family, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ruvier</color>, to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Merchant Guild</color> to witness her moment of triumph!",
    ["TaskDescription110007120"]="You are shocked to learn that Kaitlyn is the eldest daughter of Ruvier, and sister of Jurgen and Isaac! Kaitlyn's unscrupulous attempt to win this bid was actually to prove herself to her family.\nBut what is even more surprising is that the bidding sheets that Jurgen and Isaac handed over to the Merchant Guild didn't have anything filled in, so it seems that the two never intended to win from the start... Why on earth would they do that?",
    ["TaskDescription110007121"]="With your help, Kaitlyn finally learns what her two brothers really thought.\nIt turns out that the reason Jurgen and Isaac gave up the chance to win the bidding was so that Kaitlyn could fulfill her wish and get back on her feet. Upon learning of her two brothers thoughtful act, Kaitlyn finally decides to open up to her father, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ruvier</color>, about how she really feels!",
    ["TaskDescription110008101"]="You bumped in to Friedrich, head of the Heines Family, at the Geffen Tower library. He is troubled by the rumor that his son, Nithil, has stolen Merlin's Manuscript.\nFriedrich can't believe that Nithil has done something like this. At this moment, Librarian Winry took out a brooch suspected of being dropped by the thief.",
    ["TaskDescription110008102"]="Friedrich recognized the brooch as his son's, but was unable to ask Nithil about the situation as he has gone missing.\nFriedrich asked you to speak to Wheeler, Nithil's attendant, in the city center. You must do everything you can find Nithil!",
    ["TaskDescription110008103"]="You deftly managed to find out Nithil's whereabouts. He is in Goblin Forest, but why?",
    ["TaskDescription110008104"]="You found Nithil by following the trail of blood on the ground. Hurry, gather some Dodder and Red Fruits from Mace-wielding Goblins to heal his injuries!",
    ["TaskDescription110008105"]="After explaining your intentions, you finally gained Nithil's trust.\nHe asked you to personally deliver Merlin's Manuscript to his grandfather, Kroneika, in the Sage Hut in the Mjolnir Mountains. He told you to trust no one, not even familiar faces.",
    ["TaskDescription110008106"]="You were ambushed by a band of thieves not long after you set off with Merlin's Manuscript. It looks like they were after the book.\nBut how did they know the purpose of your trip?",
    ["TaskDescription110008107"]="Not unexpectedly, you were attacked a second time, this time by a group of Mobsters. Things are getting stranger and stranger.",
    ["TaskDescription110008108"]="After dispatching the first two groups of thieves, you encountered yet another one. The Mjolnir Mountains are just ahead. Remember what Nithil said: be careful every step of the way!",
    ["TaskDescription110008109"]="You came across Great Sage Kroneika at the bottom of the Mjolnir Mountains, but he seemed a little odd.",
    ["TaskDescription110008110"]="You cleverly exposed this person who blocked your way. It was not Kroneika but rather a thief impersonating him!\nCome to think of it, everything that's happened on the way seems unbelievable. You'd better deliver Merlin's Manuscript to the real Kroneika before something worse happens!",
    ["TaskDescription110008111"]="You recounted what happened to Kroneika and Bidal. Eventually, Bidal decided to go save Nithil while Kroneika asked you to investigate the body of the thief that impersonated him. He told you to take special note of the body's appearance.",
    ["TaskDescription110008112"]="Just as Kroneika said, you found some important clues on the body.\nInform Kroneika and listen to what he has to say.",
    ["TaskDescription110008113"]="After some analysis, Kroneika found that the thief is actually a member of a Mobster gang based just outside Orc Village. He was also carrying a strange alchemical potion.\nJust then, Bidal and Nithil returned to the Sage Hut.",
    ["TaskDescription110008114"]="Nithil recounted a strange incident that happened in the Heines Family mansion a few days ago. A thief was given a potion that allowed him to transform into Wheeler and instructed to sneak into the mansion. Since then, Nithil trusted no one and decided to secretly deliver Merlin's Manuscript to Kroneika for safekeeping.\nAfter understanding the situation, you decided to infiltrate the Mobster gang's lair to investigate further. Kroneika gave you a bottle of Truth Potion and asked you to meet up with them in front of Geffen Tower when you're done.",
    ["TaskDescription110008115"]="You found the Mobster gang's lair just outside Orc Village and took care of the thief that was guarding the entrance.\nNow go in to investigate and see if you can find any clues about the mastermind behind all this!",
    ["TaskDescription110008116"]="After using the Truth Potion on him, you managed to get some information on the mastermind from Piro, leader of the Mobster gang. The mastermind is temporarily staying in the southwest corner of the Orc Dungeon. Hurry over to investigate!",
    ["TaskDescription110008117"]="You took care of the Wandering Orc Zombies in front of the Orc Dungeon's entrance. Just how did the mastermind enter such a dangerous place?",
    ["TaskDescription110008118"]="You found a dimensional gap and a diary near the river at the place where the mastermind is staying. These things reminded you of someone. Continue to investigate the area for other clues!",
    ["TaskDescription110008119"]="You are most surprised to learn that the mastermind behind the plot to steal Merlin's Manuscript is none other than your old enemy, Baroshev!\nGo to Geffen Tower and tell Great Sage Kroneika what happened.",
    ["TaskDescription110009101"]="By the side of the road at Prontera West Gate, you encounter three aristocratic sisters dressed in glamorous clothing. They look to be in a daze because they caught a glimpse of the side profile of two princes. After they see you, they ask you to go after the two princes and take a photo of them to satisfy their girly fantasies. You can't help but answer their pleas and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Pooler Garden to find the two princes</color>. However, you find that this seemingly easy commission gets you unexpectedly drawn into a storm.",
    ["TaskDescription110009102"]="Although you successfully defeat the assassin, Prince Aronst was injured in the assassination. To save Aronst, Azer asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Prontera Cathedral and seek the priestess' help</color> while he stays behind to look after the unconscious Aronst.",
    ["TaskDescription110009103"]="You and Priestess Margaret return to Pooler Garden. She immediately casts a healing spell on Prince Aronst, but you're all shocked to discover that this doesn't appear to be a normal injury...",
    ["TaskDescription110009104"]="Heeding Margaret's request, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Clear Water</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clotting Grass</color> to clean Prince Aronst's wound. However, once the bloody wound is uncovered, what shockingly emerges from it is...?",
    ["TaskDescription110009105"]="After you and Margaret convince Prince Azer, he finally agrees to let Parni return to Prontera and prepare an exorcism ritual for the dying Prince Aronst. After talking things over, you and Margaret agree to split up. She returns to the cathedral to try and retrieve Parni's Staff. Meanwhile, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Glast Heim</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni</color>, who is living there in seclusion.",
    ["TaskDescription110009106"]="Parni checks Prince Aronst's wound. She seems to have already come to a conclusion, but in order to reveal the truth to Prince Azer, you'll need to craft a Truth Serum. Thus, she asks you to collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eyes of Truth</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysts</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>a yellow ore with magical powers</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110009107"]="You personally <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle the Truth Serum on Prince Aronst's chest</color>, causing the truth to appear. You all anticipated this, but it still makes you feel quite sad.",
    ["TaskDescription110009108"]="To save the dying Prince Aronst, you decide to try <color=#CA2E0AFF>uncovering the truth behind the assassination attempt</color> and place your hope in getting the antidote from the prisoner.",
    ["TaskDescription110009109"]="You go to the city gates as Azer suggests and <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate the carriages that have passed in and out of the city today</color>. The guard shows you the list of carriages that entered Prontera today. The first carriage came from...?",
    ["TaskDescription110009110"]="According to the guard's records, you see that a carriage belonging to the Wigner Chamber of Commerce passed through the gate not long ago, coinciding with the time the assassin fled. You find someone from the Chamber of Commerce to help you, hoping to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the goods being transported by that carriage</color>, but find something unexpected among the densely packed cargo boxes.",
    ["TaskDescription110009111"]="You unexpectedly stumble upon a gang of Goblins in the Wigner Chamber of Commerce's carriage, attempting to steal their fill of gold coins. You successfully help the Chamber of Commerce fight off the thieves, but are still no closer to locating the whereabouts of the assassins. Desperate for answers, <color=#CA2E0AFF>you head to the gate again</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask for help from the guard</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110009112"]="The second carriage on the list came from the church. According to the guard, strange noises could be heard coming from this coffin-laden carriage. You head to the cemetery behind the church hoping to confirm the situation, but discover that the strange sounds coming from within the coffin are actually the wails of a vengeful spirit. At Zair's request, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Central Fountain</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color>, which he says can free lost souls from the mortal realm.",
    ["TaskDescription110009113"]="You find nothing of use in the church carriage, and only one more carriage remains on the guard's list. This is your final hope, but the guard seems somewhat reluctant for you to search it. What could be the reason for this...?",
    ["TaskDescription110009114"]="\nAs you obtain the Royal Pass from the guard, you feel as though the answer you've been seeking is almost within reach. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Pooler Garden</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell Parni and Prince Azer about everything that has happened</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110009115"]="Unexpectedly, after learning about the Royal Pass, Azer asks Parni to use forbidden life exchange magic to save Aronst. Try as you might to dissuade him, Azer's determination cannot be abated, and so Parni asks you to help collect the materials for the spell. First of all, you'll need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arcane Fruit</color> to draw the magic circle...",
    ["TaskDescription110009116"]="In addition to Arcane Fruit, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>skulls and eyeballs of vengeful spirits</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sageworms</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skeleton Prisoners</color> are also vital materials for executing the forbidden spell.",
    ["TaskDescription110009117"]="Together, you and Parni prepare to set up the magic circle for carrying out the forbidden spell, but it seems you're still missing the most crucial ingredient...",
    ["TaskDescription110009118"]="As agreed, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to Prontera Cathedral</color> to search for Margaret, wondering whether she has succeeded in <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieving Parni's staff</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110009119"]="The preparations for casting the forbidden spell have finally been completed. You watch Prince Azer <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby</color> as he resolutely walks into the center of the magic circle, side by side with Prince Aronst...",
    ["TaskDescription110009120"]="Parni's spell is a success, and a fair exchange is made, but what Azer needs to do is far from over. Parni remains at Pooler Garden to take care of the slumbering Aronst, while you offer to <color=#CA2E0AFF>escort Prince Azer home</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110009121"]="Seeing the injured Prince Azer, the Walter Family's servants hastily make their exit, flustered. Prince Azer asks for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>tail them</color>, hoping to solve the mysteries at hand... You feel that there is something strange about the entire situation that you cannot put your finger on. Perhaps the truth behind this matter is far more complicated than you think.",
    ["TaskDescription110010101"]="You catch up with the mission before they leave the Rune Kingdom and learn of the whereabouts of His Majesty the King. This is your final chance... Success or failure rests in your hands!",
    ["TaskDescription110010102"]="As it happens, the mission already left the South Gate and entered the Sograt Desert. You follow suit and journey into the desert, even though you have no idea where they’re stationed. Just as you begin to lose hope, you uncover a mysterious note containing instructions. The note informs you that the mission is making their way to a camp in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of the desert</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110010103"]="While investigating the camp’s surroundings, you overhear several members of the mission talking about giant mummies. Sean, the archaeologist, informs you that the mummies temporarily grew in size after eating a plant called the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Evil Thorn</color> and attacked tomb raiders who were stained with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>blood of their beloved Isis</color>. After hearing this, you devise a plan to use this intel to <color=#CA2E0AFF>distract</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>guards</color> and seize on an opportunity to investigate the mission's supplies...",
    ["TaskDescription110010104"]="Following the intel Sean gave you, you collect an evil thorn and snake blood and manage to tame a wild mummy. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to the mission's compound</color> and put your plan into action.",
    ["TaskDescription110010105"]="The giant mummy attracts the attention of the mission and helps you buy enough time to investigate their supplies. Unfortunately, you‘’re still unable to discover the whereabouts of His Majesty the King. Running out of options, you discover another mysterious note informing you that the mission is preparing to leave for its next location in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest of the desert</color>. You decide to follow the mission and continue your investigation in...",
    ["TaskDescription110010106"]="You follow the mission to the desert’s southwest region, but are unable to get to the supply box. At this point, you run into Neste, the desert dweller you helped previously. He offers to help you distract the guards, but he can't do it alone. You must first help him find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shah, the mighty quarryman of the slums</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gwynn, the wily foodstuffs merchant</color>, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>swift-footed Drielle</color>. You agree to meet in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Leinster Street</color> once you gather all three companions.",
    ["TaskDescription110010107"]="You find Shah the quarryman cornered by Giearth In the Ant Cavern and save him. Shah asks you to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ore</color> hidden by Giearth that he worked so hard to unearth.",
    ["TaskDescription110010108"]="You help Shah retrieve his ore. Full of gratitude, he agrees to assist you and Neste in your plan and heads to Leinster Street to wait for the others. Now it's time for you to head <color=#CA2E0AFF>east of the desert</color> to the Scorched Mushroom Foraging Grounds, to find Gwynn, the wily ingredient hunter.",
    ["TaskDescription110010109"]="You successfully locate Gwynn, but find him shriveled up from the heat and fainted on the ground. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the oasis</color> to find a <color=#CA2E0AFF>source of water</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>quench his thirst</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110010110"]="In order to thank you for saving his life, Gwynn agrees to assist you in your plan. Now, all that's left is to find the fleet-footed maiden, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drielle</color>. According to Neste, the end of the world lies among the wolves. Perhaps you can track down the maiden near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Wolf</color> lair...",
    ["TaskDescription110010111"]="You find an anxious-looking Drielle surrounded by wolves. However, you soon learn that the young girl was in fact raised as an orphan by the wolf pack. Now, a desert wolf cub has been separated from the others, and to her it is as if her own family has disappeared. You decide to help Drielle <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the wolf cub</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110010112"]="You locate the lost wolf cub in an area where the golems gather. Now, all you need to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>place fresh meat</color> around the area and guide it step by step back to Drielle!",
    ["TaskDescription110010113"]="You help Drielle recover her cherished wolf brother. In return, she offers to assist you in your plan. Now that all three members are assembled, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Leinster Street</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110010114"]="With the help of Neste and the others, you gain another opportunity to investigate the supply box. However, even after opening it, you still find no trace of His Majesty the King inside. At that very moment, a mysterious note appears again with instructions, asking you to meet under the <color=#CA2E0AFF>golden coconut tree on the western outskirts of the desert</color>. It hints at another clue it may provide...",
    ["TaskDescription110010115"]="Following the note’s instructions, you proceed to the golden coconut tree on the western outskirts of the desert. It turns out the person who guided you all this way is actually a curious-looking youth with a mop of golden hair. He directs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morroc</color>, where you can seek the help of the Lugenburg Family...",
    ["TaskDescription110010116"]="You arrive in Morroc and ask Halmod for help. Although he is wary of your intentions, he’s still willing to trust an old friend. However, before that, you must first go with him to...",
    ["TaskDescription110010117"]="It’s been a long time since you last met, but Halmod hasn’t changed one bit. Although he’s already decided to help you, he still finds an excuse to have a rousing match with you first. Now that you’ve finally completed the first part of the golden-haired youth’s instructions, <color=#CA2E0AFF>next</color> you must...?",
    ["TaskDescription110010118"]="Carefully following the golden-haired youth’s words, you collect some phantom orchids in the Sphinx Cavern. There’s just <color=#CA2E0AFF>one last thing to do</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110010119"]="You have a long talk with the golden-haired youth by the watering hole. For some reason, you can’t help feeling suspicious about his strange appearance and manner of speech. Just as you’re ready to ask him a question, you sense a strange fragrance in the air. Gradually, your vision grows blurry and you lose consciousness...",
    ["TaskDescription110010120"]="You feel as if you’re caught in a disorienting dream. When you awake, there’s no trace of the gold-haired youth. Determined to get to the bottom of this, you decide to return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lugenburg Manor</color> and seek Halmod's help...",
    ["TaskDescription110010121"]="Halmod informs you that two days have already passed since he hosted a banquet for the Church Mission as you requested. The ship carrying the mission set sail this morning and has in all likelihood entered into the territory of the Rune Kingdom already. Now, you must go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bohr</color> and report all of this to him.",
    ["TaskDescription110011101"]="Comodo faced rebuilding after the campaign against the dragons. On good terms with the Nerius family, you'd help out on the island often. But on this day, the orderly <color=#CA2E0AFF>leader's mansion</color> echoed in quarrels between <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alexia</color> and her daughters...",
    ["TaskDescription110011102"]="From the argument, you learned Queen Katherine sent letters to the Seven Royal Families, demanding each choose their most qualified heirs for an election to the throne in Prontera. Speeka believed herself and her younger sister to be the most suitable candidates, only for Alexia to nominate Prince Erich who's not of royal blood. The schism caused Speeka to run away, vowing to prove herself by retrieving the Sword of Valiant from the depth of the dragons' cave. Cecilia is concerned about her sister's safety and implored you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the cave of Comodo</color> and aid Speeka.",
    ["TaskDescription110011103"]="You saved the reckless girl from evil monsters in the lair, yet she rebuked you for meddling in her business. To fulfill your promise to Cecilia, you could only calm Speeka down by convincing her that you came to witness her withdrawing the Sword of Valiant. That satisfied Speeka enough to allow you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany her</color> deeper into the dragons' cave in search of the legendary blade...",
    ["TaskDescription110011104"]="To find the legendary sword, you and Speeka <color=#CA2E0AFF>ventured</color> deep into the dragons' cave, enduring many monsters along the way...",
    ["TaskDescription110011105"]="After several struggles, you finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>reached</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deepest bowel of the dragons' cave</color>, but what lay ahead...?",
    ["TaskDescription110011106"]="You saw the legendary Sword of Valiant and the Ancient Dragon that bound the sword. Seeing the dragon on its last breath, Speeka charged, only for the weakened monster to summon <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golems to attack you</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110011107"]="You fell back under the massive assault from the Golems, postponing retrieving the sword for now. Speeka told you she heard the dragon calling incessantly for someone named Barbara in the battle. You decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the island</color> and find out more about this person...",
    ["TaskDescription110011108"]="Back on the island, through sheer chance, you heard the name of Barbara from criers passing out flyers. You learned after talking to locals that Barbara is a famous dancer trained by the Euphonic Symphony, but struck out on her own at a young age and has returned in all her glory. She has a performance scheduled for tonight on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golden Beach</color> on Comodo, which you and Speeka decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>attend</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110011109"]="You blended in with a hardcore crowd for Barbara's performance. Afterward, Speeka decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>approach Barbara</color> and ask about the Ancient Dragon...",
    ["TaskDescription110011110"]="In the conversation, Barbara recognized Speeka and was affable, until the princess mentioned the dragon, which prompted her to brush Speeka off. You realized there's a story behind it and set out to find out the truth somehow. You heard monsters are very sensitive to human scent and perhaps that could be the key to unraveling the connection between the dancer and the dragon. But to do that, you must get something belonging to Barbara. To zero in on a target, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>went back to the beach</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>took a snapshot</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Barbara</color> from behind...",
    ["TaskDescription110011111"]="According to Speeka's directions, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>go buy the signature brew from the tavern</color> next to bribe the Galapagos. Supposedly, the clever, devious monsters are the best thieves around...",
    ["TaskDescription110011112"]="With Barbara's photo and signature brew, you arrived at the east side of Saint Darmain, attempting to <color=#CA2E0AFF>convince the Galapagos</color> inhabiting here. Of course, the worst possible result is getting a thrashing from them.",
    ["TaskDescription110011113"]="After a round of beating, the creatures reached an understanding. Adhering to the accord, you traded <color=#CA2E0AFF>signature brew</color> for Barbara's handkerchief at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo volcano</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110011114"]="You got Barbara's handkerchief. Now it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the dragons' cave</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet back up with Speeka</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110011115"]="You tested the Golems' reaction with Barbara's handkerchief and were shocked to find the mean monsters miraculously stopped attacking. This reinforced Speeka's belief that there's a bond between Barbara and the Ancient Dragon. You quickly approached the dragon and <color=#CA2E0AFF>put the handkerchief before it</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110011116"]="Approaching the Ancient Dragon, Speeka noticed identical marks on both the Sword of Valiant that bound the dragon and the handkerchief. All the evidence indicated an unusual connection, but why would Barbara deny it? An intrigued Speeka swore to get to the bottom of this...",
    ["TaskDescription110011117"]="A discussion with Speeka made both of you realize a clue was overlooked: Euphonic Symphony, which Barbara once belonged to. You departed immediately <color=#CA2E0AFF>for the Symphony's base</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>more about Barbara</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110011118"]="From Symphony member Elena, you learned that Barbara was a pupil of Doreen, the former leader. But oddly, the world-famous dancer was mocked by her instructor as talentless. Even other members joked about how Barbara got where she is today because she found the legendary Dance of All Dances in the frozen waterfall of the dragons' cave. But rumors are still rumors and that wouldn't tell you the truth. After parting with Elena, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>found</color> another <color=#CA2E0AFF>member named Warren</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110011119"]="The bard called Warren has a different view on Barbara, seemingly holding his former schoolmate in low regard, even criticizing her moves as lacking in substance. It made you doubt Barbara's achievements even more, a puzzle that perhaps only the current leader of Euphonic Symphony, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Callahan</color>, can clarify...",
    ["TaskDescription110011120"]="Callahan revealed to you something in the past he's been hiding. Ten years ago, Barbara hired bounty hunters to escort her into the dragons' cave, but only she came back out alive. No one knew what happened in the cave, and Barbara even left Comodo because of that, ending all contact with Euphonic Symphony. You and Speeka surmised she went in there looking for the legendary Dance of All Dances, and judging from the results, she likely succeeded. To get Barbara to confess, you and Speeka split up. She would try to find out the score's whereabouts, while you <color=#CA2E0AFF>locate Barbara</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>confront her</color> to buy Speeka time...",
    ["TaskDescription110011121"]="Following Symphony members' testimonies, you poked holes in Barbara's explanation and pressed her to divulge what really happened ten years ago in the dragons' cave. She told you she saved the life of a dragonling in the cave and befriended it, until it ultimately betrayed her, luring her with the news of Dance of All Dances to the frozen waterfall and ambushing her squad. Out of self-preservation, she hurt that dragon with her sword. As for the Dance of All Dances... There was no such thing and she never saw it. Just then, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Speeka</color> showed up with unexpected proof...",
    ["TaskDescription110011122"]="Speeka found the Dance of All Dances in Barbara's luggage, exposing the dancer's lies. Seeing she has no way of talking out of this one, a flustered Barbara opted to flee. You wouldn't let her get away, of course. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Catch her</color> and let her answer for her deeds!",
    ["TaskDescription110011123"]="An emotionally cornered Barbara revealed the truth in tears. It seemed she was friends with an Ancient Dragon and it did help her locate the Dance of All Dances, but the bounty hunters she hired turned on her once they found it and wanted to keep the precious score for themselves. The dragon showed up at the key moment to turn the tide, but the devious bounty hunters took Barbara's blade and held her hostage. To protect Barbara, the dragon took a penetrating stab in the chest, while the friend it saved just ran like a coward, leaving it behind to die. The Dance of All Dances was damaged in the chaos and just half of it survived... You decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring Barbara back to the dragons' cave</color> and let her repent in person.",
    ["TaskDescription110011124"]="Under relentless pressure from you, Barbara finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>returned to see the Ancient Dragon</color> once more. You already had a feeling about how this is going to end. Since the dragon would never hurt its friend, it must've wanted anything but vengeance...",
    ["TaskDescription110011125"]="The dragon could finally hand the other half of the score it's been guarding for the last ten years to its old friend. What kept it alive was a promise in its childhood. Now, to Barbara's graceful dance steps, the dragon could close its eyes in peace...",
    ["TaskDescription1100119101"]="After waiting anxiously for days on end, Commander Bohr finally contacts you. You assume that perhaps there is a new clue relating to the case of His Majesty's disappearance...?",
    ["TaskDescription1100119102"]="You go to the training grounds of the Kingdom Defense Force to find Commander Bohr, who has been waiting for you. Flanked by two Defense Force soldiers, Bohr informs you that after rigorously inspecting all of the people and goods entering and leaving Prontera, they have discovered a new clue. Now, Captain Peddie, one of the parties involved, will share more details with you. Please inform Peddie when you are ready!",
    ["TaskDescription1100119103"]="Based on Captain Peddie's account, you learn that there is a delegation from the Church of Arunabez who have a special pass to enter the kingdom, granted by the Seven Royal Families themselves, which allows them to leave Prontera with large amounts of goods without inspection at the border. However, there is still more intel the Defense Force has yet to share. Bohr gestures for another soldier named Angelo to come forward and describe what he has seen and heard...",
    ["TaskDescription1100119104"]="What Angelo tells you is even more pivotal. He shares that while on his morning patrol, he heard two strange men talking about \"His Majesty\" outside Prontera South Gate, one of whom was dressed in the garb of the Church and appeared to be a member of the mission. Angelo shadowed the two men, until he discovered their quarters outside the South Gate. Finally, you can identify the culprits behind the kidnapping of His Majesty!",
    ["TaskDescription1100119105"]="After discussing, you and Bohr decide to conduct a covert investigation of the mission in order to avoid alerting the enemy. Heaven forbid those miscreants harm His Majesty in the heat of the moment! Bohr asks you to disguise yourself as a member of the Church and blend in with the mission, so that you can glean additional intel and look for a potential opportunity to rescue His Majesty. But before that, you need to disguise yourself. On Bohr’s advice, you go to the South Gate and discreetly take pictures of the members of the mission. Next, you hand them over to Vera, an appearance merchant, and ask her to help you make an identical costume.",
    ["TaskDescription1100119106"]="Vera agrees to your request. However, before she can start, you need to help her collect the light blue down fur of an eclipse, a veronica flower and some fine leather made from the hide of a savage bebe.",
    ["TaskDescription1100119107"]="Time is running out! Once you finish collecting the materials Vera needs, go back and give them to her as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription1100119108"]="Everything is prepared and it’s finally time to take action. Based on the intel Bohr analyzed, he suggests that you disguise yourself as a close friend of the mysterious man the mission’s members keep talking about. Because of the deep respect they have for him, he believes your infiltration will face less obstacles. Before leaving, Bohr repeatedly reminds you to not to be reckless and retreat at the first sign of danger. If you’re ready, put on the costume of the Church and go to their provisional quarters at the Prontera South Gate!",
    ["TaskDescription1100119109"]="Bohr's suspicions are correct. The members of the mission really are in awe of the mysterious figure, and you easily manage to fool the guards. Now, it's time to start going through the suspicious cargo boxes one by one.",
    ["TaskDescription1100119110"]="You carefully examine some of the supply boxes in the mission's quarters, but turn up nothing. During your investigation, your plans are scuttled by an eclipse that was attracted by food nearby. You’re discovered by a golden-haired member of the mission, but strangely enough, he doesn’t expose you. Instead, he devises a plan to conceal your departure. Although you have your doubts, your plan to secretly infiltrate the mission has failed and for now you can only return to the Defense Force training grounds to look for Bohr and consider your next move...",
    ["TaskDescription110012101"]="The new king election that lasts for seven days is now concluded. Meanwhile, the highly anticipated Bloodline Banquet is kicking off now. On the way to the Banquet Hall, you receive a Banquet Invitation prepared by Bohr from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force Soldier</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110012102"]="Along with Bohr's invitation, you receive a mission as well. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>Royal Chivalry</color> that is secretly gathering around the <color=#CA2E0AFF>West Gate</color> has been acting up since the morning, and Bohr wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>quietly investigate</color> their movement...",
    ["TaskDescription110012103"]="You see a group of knights secretly gathered around the West Gate through the clues the Defense Force Soldier provided. You heard that Azer had gone missing in their conversation. The knights are conscious of someone eavesdropping on their conversation, and they move to another place when discussing more important details. Now, there's nothing you can do but <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow them quietly</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110012104"]="A silver-haired knight in the group says that Azer left Prontera along with Aronst in the early morning, and no one has seen him ever since. But \"the lord\" states that this is all part of the plan. With Azer vanished, now there's only Aronst alone in the daze at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery of the West Gate</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110012105"]="You found Aronst and his personal attendant, Moffit, in the West Gate Cemetery. It is getting close to the opening time of the Bloodline Banquet, and Moffit is complaining that the prince shouldn't go out by himself, but Aronst insists on staying in the cemetery to pay his respect to the deceased. He then orders Moffit to return to the palace and get a banquet outfit ready for him. Moreover, Aronst wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick</color> him some blooming <color=#CA2E0AFF>flowers</color> outside the cemetery...",
    ["TaskDescription110012106"]="After helping Aronst get the flowers he needs, you ask him where Azer is and remind him of the betrayal of the Royal Chivalry. Aronst is not responding to you; instead, he requests you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the flowers in front of the tombstone</color>, and he has a story to tell you.",
    ["TaskDescription110012107"]="Aronst tells you the story of this grave's owner. Supposedly he was once a young master of a prominent family, but he lost everything after being betrayed by his brother. The thing Aronst wants you to pick up in this story is that he doesn't want to start a war within the family with Azer, and nothing will change his mind. Your conversation with Aronst doesn't go anywhere, and the only thing you can do right now is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>safely escort Aronst back to the palace</color> for him to join the Bloodline Banquet.",
    ["TaskDescription110012108"]="During the Banquet Hall, Bohr has been busy running around, and you exchange information with him. While the poison still lurks on Aronst at this moment, Bohr has assembled enough army units to fight against the Walter family. Helena is awake and on her way to Prontera with Parni. Bohr tells you to take it easy since everything seems to be going your way. Also, he reminds you to speak with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> before the banquet begins, and there is a mission he wants you to complete.",
    ["TaskDescription110012109"]="Wolmas the Archbishop explains a mission to you in a rush, in which he first wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat the Familiar</color>, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the Central Fountain and drink the fountain water</color>, and lastly, he wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather an Ash Branch and an Elm Branch</color>. He will explain these to you in detail when you finish everything.",
    ["TaskDescription110012110"]="You complete the tasks Wolmas assigned to you and are returning to the kingdom to <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand over Ash Branch and Elm Branch to him</color>. Calvin, the guard at the entrance, reminds you that the Bloodline Banquet is about to begin, and they will lock down the Banquet Hall. So, please make sure you are totally ready before you enter.",
    ["TaskDescription110012111"]="Those tasks Wolmas assigned you originated from the oldest ritual of the Rune Kingdom, representing Odin's three outstanding achievements. Whoever finishes the ritual will then be qualified to preside over the coronation ceremony for the new king. He and the queen both want you to personally fit the ring on the new king, the ring that symbolizes the royal sovereignty and the legacy you carry on from the last king, King Tristan III... And now the banquet begins during the conversation. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>listen to the speech given by the princess</color> and wait for the new king to ascend the throne.",
    ["TaskDescription110012112"]="Under everyone's witness, the princess announces the election result, and Aronst now becomes the new king as everyone expected. You receive the ring and the sword representing the royal sovereignty, then you <color=#CA2E0AFF>get onto the stage</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>coronate for him</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110012113"]="The moment Aronst has his hand on the ring and the sword, things go in the opposite direction. The kindhearted prince turns into a tyrant who abuses his power in everything. Not only does he admit the coup he had done, but he also laughs shamelessly at all the nobles there, saying they are stupid enough to send the murderer to the throne. Under his order, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>guards in the venue</color> pull out their weapons...",
    ["TaskDescription110012114"]="It confuses everyone that Aronst acts in such a weird manner. Meanwhile, those <color=#CA2E0AFF>zealous nobles</color> who are as evil as the Walter family try to escalate the situation and persuade others to detain Aronst, making the scene a hot mess...",
    ["TaskDescription110012115"]="Even though you temporarily suppress those zealous nobles with force, they keep mumbling about how Aronst isn't fit to be a king and try to dethrone him. They want Azer, who ranked second in the election, to be the king. At this moment, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bohr</color> finally starts to take action...",
    ["TaskDescription110012116"]="Bohr, Parni, Helena, and Seyren reveal the murder of the three Gaebolg princes all together to everyone. The secret letter from Helena holds the key evidence that points to Ian Walter as the suspect. At this point, you think everything should be settled, then Aronst takes another action that surprises everyone...",
    ["TaskDescription110012117"]="During the skirmish, you realize all the guards only follow Aronst's order. Bohr has had enough of this and scolds Aronst, which makes Aronst laugh hysterically. He wants all of you to take a good look at <color=#CA2E0AFF>who he really is</color>...?",
    ["TaskDescription110012118"]="Who would have thought that it was Azer all along on the stage since the very beginning? He disguised himself as Aronst and planned this drama. No one knows why he did that, but there's one certain thing, he now holds the right to kill with just a snap of his finger. Bohr tries to buy everyone time by confronting him but eventually fails. Azer now wants all of you to get down your knees and vow to serve him. Otherwise... everyone is going to hell.",
    ["TaskDescription110012119"]="Azer seems to be losing his patience. Since no one is willing to vow, he wants to make all of you pay for this. Azer holds up his sword and points at his father... But he failed. The reinforcement is finally here. Soldiers are heavily surrounding and protecting the Banquet Hall; soon after, the sinful Azer falls in the arrow shower... You can't believe what just happened. Did Azer... <color=#CA2E0AFF>just die like this</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110012120"]="Everyone is grateful to be alive, and the culprit, Azer, has ended up costing his life. You can't let go of what happened even though you know everything behind the story. You recall the story from this morning, and somehow Azer saw his outcome already and knew how it would be, but why did he do this...?",
    ["TaskDescription110013101"]="Dear Adventurer, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fulkyn</color> seems in need of your help! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Talk with him</color> when you have time!",
    ["TaskDescription110013102"]="In the Realm of Time, you meet Fulkyn, who is muttering bizarre phrases again. Under your strong claims, he takes out a photo, telling you he is looking for the mech creatures on it. As always, he asks you to find them as soon as possible and install the receivers on them. Otherwise, they may explode amid the crowded city of Juno.",
    ["TaskDescription110013103"]="After leaving the library in the direction Fulkyn points you, you come across a young man saying he was hit by a weird robot. As his prosthetic leg got damaged. the young man starts venting at you. But in the end, this kindhearted young man tells you that the robot has gone <color=#CA2E0AFF>north</color>, and he wants you to catch it quickly to prevent the same thing from happening again.",
    ["TaskDescription110013104"]="Following the direction the young man indicates, you continue the search. A mount merchant tells you that a robot was looping around the Central Plaza at high speed, passing by him multiple times. During your conversation, the robot appears again, knocking off the merchant's wig. You are now confirmed that this is the mech creature Fulkyn has been looking for. After a hot pursuit, you successfully rein in the rampaging robot. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>install the receiver</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110013105"]="Just as Fulkyn described, once the receiver is installed, the mech creature starts the return protocol, going back to Fulkyn automatically. But as you watch it leave, you find a Shiba Inu barking at it strangely. Before you can figure it out, the dog starts tugging your pants, signaling you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow it</color>. What is this Shiba Inu trying to tell you...?",
    ["TaskDescription110013106"]="Following the Shiba Inu, you come to a place where a group of pet lovers are gathering. To your surprise, these people completely ignore the Shiba Inu but are captivated by a robot. You immediately recognize that thing as one of the mech creatures Fulkyn has been looking for. Then something strange happens. After being forced to touch the mech creature, you almost fall into the same hallucination as the others do, mistaking this giant piece of metal chunk as a furry pet. Luckily, the barks of the Shiba Inu wake you up, and now it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take action</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110013107"]="After defeating the mech creature, people ensnared in the peculiar hallucination finally come to their senses, and the Shiba Inu is now back to its master. Then according to a passersby's testimony, a male student from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno University</color> showed up here not long ago, carrying a mech creature of similar looks. And he was ranting about some sort of physical training...",
    ["TaskDescription110013108"]="As you expected, this male student, who is obsessed with his training, turns out to be Wallace. The moment you arrive at Juno University, you see he lands a heavy blow to the mech creature, triggering the self-destruct sequence on it. And this makes Delia, his schoolmate, completely furious. She requests you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>put this thing into sleep mode</color>. Otherwise...?",
    ["TaskDescription110013109"]="The imminent self-destruct sequence is stopped just in time. Not to your surprise, you two get an earful from Delia. To escape from this ear-bleeding lecture, you decide to go back and <color=#CA2E0AFF>report to Fulkyn</color>. However, before you leave, Delia gives you something she gathered from the mech creature. You don't recognize it, yet it seems somewhat akin to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110013110"]="When you come back to the Realm of Time, Fulkyn tells you these mech creatures were made by a culprit who attempts to alter history. To identify this culprit, you two decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>thoroughly investigate</color> these weird-looking <color=#CA2E0AFF>mech creatures</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110013111"]="The information gathered from these mech creatures is not enough for Fulkyn to determine the identity of this culprit. At this point, you recall the thing you received from Delia, the thing that looks very much alike to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110013112"]="The intel Delia provided seems to ring a bell with our brilliant Professor Fulkyn. Now, per his request, put <color=#CA2E0AFF>the stuff you obtained from the mech creature</color> into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> and let it run the analysis!",
    ["TaskDescription110013113"]="Much to your surprise, the Mysterious Device managed to deduce the exact time and location! Given <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fulkyn's</color> poised look, could this be...?",
    ["TaskDescription110013114"]="Bingo! The results returned by the Mysterious Device are the spacetime coordinates where the culprit may appear the next time! Now, brace yourself and travel to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen in year AW232</color> with Fulkyn!",
    ["TaskDescription110013115"]="To your surprise, the one that awaits you in Year AW232 turns out to be Barr Venter, whom you haven't seen for a long time. He has changed a lot since the last time you saw him in Glast Heim. The once-revered \"Father of Mechanics\" now seems like a total lunatic, deeply obsessed with altering history. Despite the earnest persuasion from both of you, he still insists on his strayed aspirations. In the end, this renowned Great Sage even declares war against you two. But what motivates him to alter history? Given the fact that one cannot defy the Spacetime Rules, how is he going to make sure his action affects the course of history? At this moment, however, the situation is just too dire for you to raise these questions...",
    ["TaskDescription110014101"]="Following another encounter with Barr Venter, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fulkyn </color>has shut himself in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Realm of Time</color>. As a kind-hearted Adventurer, it seems right to go see how Fulkyn is holding up!",
    ["TaskDescription110014102"]="In the Realm of Time, Fulkyn explains what he's accomplished and what's troubling him. You decide together to go to the time node altered by Barr Venter to look for a way to stop him. Before you go, Fulkyn needs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the Sands of Time</color> needed to activate time travel from Lord's Mansion.",
    ["TaskDescription110014103"]="You've retrieved the Sands of Time from Lord's Mansion, and right before time traveling, Fulkyn asks if you'd like to change anything in history. After you respond, he activates the time travel, and just like that—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Welcome to AW225</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110014104"]="As you explore the area per Fulkyn's requests, you overhear villagers discussing an injured child and his caretaker, a hunter named Gamow. Just as you're drawn into their story, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gamow</color> shows up.",
    ["TaskDescription110014105"]="During the conversation, it turns out that Thanatos is the kid Gamow rescued. Gamow says Thanatos has already had his meds and is sleeping. The villagers continue to joke about Thanatos and Lush being together, but Gamow acts really weird. After this report, Fulkyn looks up Gamow's file—he's supposed to die this year. Now, you decide to go find Thanatos.",
    ["TaskDescription110014106"]="You guys find the young Thanatos stuck in his nightmares and choose to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him back</color> to the small village...",
    ["TaskDescription110014107"]="Following Thanatos, you two come across a village that looks like hell, all thanks to Argota, an evil monster Thanatos stabbed three of its eyes. In revenge, it infiltrated the village, manipulated Gamow, and started a massacre to drive Thanatos into despair. Fulkyn, also a witness, stays eerily calm and suggests you move on to another altered timeline.",
    ["TaskDescription110014108"]="You arrive in a town in AW230, and, as usual, you're asked to <color=#CA2E0AFF>scout around</color> for any signs of Thanatos and Lush...",
    ["TaskDescription110014109"]="Locals are buzzing about the new demon hunters, and through their chatter, you hear about the name Thanatos. Following them, you find Thanatos and Lush. But they seem to be acting a bit weird?",
    ["TaskDescription110014110"]="You catch Thanatos and Lush talking about heading to Glast Heim to seek a witch doctor to bring back Gamow, aiming to give Lush the peaceful life she once had. Lush's response is unclear, though. Then, Fulkyn tells you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fake altered timeline</color> has appeared again.",
    ["TaskDescription110014111"]="In this fake timeline, Barr Venter is guiding Lush to a different future. Fulkyn, watching all this unfold, expresses his anger, asserting that their destinies are now intertwined with the world, and he will not allow the order of time and space to be altered again. As you approach the final time node<color=#CA2E0AFF>, you overhear a Bard singing...",
    ["TaskDescription110014112"]="The Bard's song wraps up with a sigh about the demon hunters whose conversation he overheard earlier, noting the two don't get each other's feelings. He hopes they can understand each other when the battle is over. Suddenly, a loud boom echoes from the horizon...",
    ["TaskDescription110014113"]="You head to where the loud noise came from and discover Lush's corpse alongside the heartbroken Thanatos...",
    ["TaskDescription110014114"]="In Morroc's hand, you see Lush's life, filled with regrets, and the suffering has yet to end...",
    ["TaskDescription110014115"]="As Thanatos screams in agony, you see the end of the story. But what does the altered happy ending look like?",
    ["TaskDescription110014116"]="Surprisingly, Fulkyn ends the trip early. Time to find out what his next steps are.",
    ["TaskDescription110014117"]="Fulkyn says he already knows what the altered ending looks like and asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect Blue Venatu's Mech Core</color> to serve as an external energy source for the calculations.",
    ["TaskDescription110014118"]="Once everything is ready, Fulkyn starts up the Mysterious Device and begins analyzing the logic and intentions behind Barr Venter's alterations to history.",
    ["TaskDescription110014119"]="After repeated calculation failures, you want to try it yourself. Fulkyn suggests you use <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Soul\"</color> as the keyword for the search.",
    ["TaskDescription110014120"]="Inspired by your approach, Fulkyn discovers a hidden path to the truth in AW706 in the Rekensheim R&D Dept Sector One...",
    ["TaskDescription110015101"]="In the Realm of Time of <color=#A1979FFF>Juno</color>, Professor <color=#A1979FFF>Fulkyn</color> is unusually engrossed in his reading. You recall past events—could the next time-travel quest be approaching? (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015102"]="Professor Fulkyn explains he's checking if history was altered after the last time travel and invites you to <color=#A1979FFF>read</color> the highlighted passages with him. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015103"]="Fulkyn believes Barr Venter altered the timeline not just to ease Lush's regrets but for other reasons too. To uncover the truth, you head to Lighthalzen in A.W.706—the year Barr Venter joined the Rekensheim Institute, a pivotal moment in his life. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015104"]="A mishap during teleportation lands you in an unknown time. While wondering how to return, a mechanical maid greets you and reveals you're at Alpha Manor in A.W.704. <color=#A1979FFF>Follow her</color>—her young master has been expecting you. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015105"]="You follow Tamaureen, the mechanical maid, and meet a lavishly dressed but disheartened young man—Barr Venter, in his youth. Due to conflict with his parents, he refuses to continue his studies in engineering. You try to persuade him but are dismissed. Left with no choice, you <color=#A1979FFF>follow the maid out</color>. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015106"]="Surprisingly, the maid doesn't take you away but instead leads you deeper into the courtyard. She hopes you can help Barr Venter mend his heart and entrusts you with a family heirloom, asking you to <color=#A1979FFF>retrieve his parents' belongings</color>. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015107"]="You retrieve the suitcase from the airship manager. Now, <color=#A1979FFF>hand over the family heirloom and the suitcase to the maid</color>. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015108"]="The maid thanks you for your help and asks if you'll accompany her to deliver the suitcase to Barr Venter. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015109"]="Barr Venter strongly resists your actions, insisting the suitcase holds nothing but research materials. He refuses to follow his parents' path, not wanting to live his life trapped in a predetermined cage. If you don't stop pestering him, then go ahead—<color=#A1979FFF>open the suitcase</color> yourselves. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015110"]="You open the suitcase and discover a <color=#A1979FFF>letter</color> lying neatly on top... (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015111"]="Inside the suitcase are gifts. The letter contains heartfelt words of guilt and sorrow from Barr Venter's parents—a final farewell. The dust-covered box itself holds years of regret. As Barr Venter sheds tears, the gulf between the Father of Mechanics and his parents quietly dissolves... and the scene shifts again. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015112"]="To your surprise, you seem to have arrived at the battlefield of Thanatos and Morroc. On the distant hill, you spot Barr Venter and Lush in conversation? (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015113"]="After listening to their conversation, you decide to <color=#A1979FFF>explore the area</color> to determine the current time and location. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015114"]="You spot several scattered storage tents and camps in the distance, bustling with activity. Speaking to a chatty mercenary captain, you learn this is the Juperos Plains in A.W.716. For more details, he asks you to help <color=#A1979FFF>repair the camp</color>. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015115"]="After helping the mercenary captain repair the camp, you learn some information about Barr Venter. Suddenly, a messenger approaches and asks if you know him. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015116"]="The frustrated messenger complains that Barr Venter keeps refusing his letters, forcing him to shuttle between Barr Venter and the Rekensheim Institute to urge him to start working. The mercenary captain casually offers to pass on the message, mentioning that Barr Venter is scheduled to inspect the camp soon. Not wanting to risk altering history by meeting him, you excuse yourself and decide to <color=#A1979FFF>find a place to hide</color>. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015117"]="Unfortunately, while hiding, you encounter the soul of Lush. She recognizes you as the Adventurer who helped her and Thanatos fight Morroc centuries ago and is surprised that you haven't aged. Since Lush is already deceased and exists only as a spirit, you explain your experiences with time travel. Upon learning that Barr Venter is trying to rewrite history for her sake, Lush decides to disappear forever and not show herself to him again. To prove her resolve, she asks you to <color=#A1979FFF>wait here</color>—she will not respond when Barr Venter returns from the camp. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015118"]="Just as Lush promised, she no longer appears before Barr Venter, no matter how he calls for her. With history back on track, you breathe a sigh of relief. As if rewarding your efforts, a familiar <color=#A1979FFF>Dimensional Gap</color> appears once more at the end of the suspension bridge where you first arrived. (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110015119"]="You return safely to the present timeline. The Juperos Plains are now in ruins, and at the far edge—Barr Venter shows up—still the same blond guy with sharp green eyes. He greets you and thanks you for everything you did in the past timeline—your time-traveling efforts helped shape who he is today. He also warns you to keep an eye on Fulkyn, who initiated this mission. After all, Fulkyn was once part of the Rekenber Corp, and it was his invitation that led Barr Venter to join the Rekensheim Institute... (P.S. You can travel through time using the Mysterious Device.)",
    ["TaskDescription110101101"]="You run into Akand, who's worrying about something.\nThrough speaking with him, you learn that the Defense Force has ordered a shipment of military supplies from Hollgrehenn, but for some reason, it hasn't been delivered!\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Check with Hollgrehenn</color> and find out what's causing the delay.",
    ["TaskDescription110101102"]="Hollgrehenn looks distraught when he sees you... He says he wants to complete his order for the Defense Force as soon as possible as well, but he lost his hammer, \"Drubby.\" Therefore, he couldn't do any work!\nAfter inquiring further, you find out that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drubby</color> was accidentally dropped <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside the South Gate</color> during a frightening encounter. Apparently, the thing that spooked this blacksmith friend of yours and caused him to flee was... a giant Eclipse?",
    ["TaskDescription110101103"]="You finally find Hollgrehenn's Drubby outside the South Gate.\nAfter delivering it to him, he says that he can start working. However, in order to make the military supplies, he needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Feathers</color>... So go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chamber of Commerce Worker</color> and buy some for him!",
    ["TaskDescription1101011031"]="You finally find Hollgrehenn's Drubby outside the South Gate.\nAfter delivering it to him, he says that he can start working. However, in order to make the military supplies, he needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Feathers</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110101104"]="From your conversation with the Chamber of Commerce Worker, you learn that they were forced to stop selling Feathers due to imperfections.\nAfter helping the Chamber of Commerce Worker obtain enough spotless white Feathers, he tells you there's another issue still concerning him. It turns out that a merchant who had left to purchase goods has not returned yet. Could she be in some kind of danger? Go and look for her outside the <color=#CA2E0AFF>South Gate</color>\n!",
    ["TaskDescription110101105"]="You find the merchant, Betty Lindra, and save her from the Eclipse holding her.\nHowever, she tells you that she has lost the cargo she went to procure... Seeing the pitiful look on her face, you decide to help her find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lost Cargo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110101106"]="You help Betty Lindra recover her Lost Cargo, but while taking stock, you discover that a very valuable batch of Durian Grass is missing!\nSeeing the pitiful look on her face, you decide to continue to help her find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Backpack containing the Durian Grass.</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110101107"]="You help Betty Lindra find the missing Backpack, only to discover that all of the Durian Grass is gone!\nJust as you are wondering if this is the Eclipse's doing, a mysterious woman named Bertha appears in front of you...",
    ["TaskDescription110101108"]="It turns out that Bertha is a monster researcher obsessed with Eclipses.\nShe states that these monsters are an evolution of Lunatics, possessing greater strength and larger bodies... When she hears that Eclipses are interested in Durian Grass, she speculates that the plant may be the cause of the Lunatics' mutations. But when she also learns that Durian Grass gives off a horrendous stench, she runs in horror to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Green Cotton Farm</color>... \nQuickly follow her and see what's going on!",
    ["TaskDescription110101109"]="You meet a frantic Old Klaus at Green Cotton Farm. While speaking with him, you learn that a few days ago, Durian Grass started growing wildly on this farm. This attracted a bunch of Eclipses that damaged the crops...\nAfter helping Old Klaus get rid of the Eclipses, you are about to help him remove the Durian Grass when Bertha suddenly appears to stop you. Seems like <color=#CA2E0AFF>Betty Lindra</color> has a better idea. Why don't you go hear what she has to say?",
    ["TaskDescription110101110"]="It turns out that Betty Lindra wants to buy the Durian Grass from Green Cotton Farm, and with your help, she gathers all the cargo to be delivered to the Chamber of Commerce.\nHurry and tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bertha</color>, who's standing by the side. What does she think about what happened today?",
    ["TaskDescription110102101"]="You run into Windmill Knight Tanders in the Mjolnir Mountains!\nWhile speaking with him, you discover that he's been wounded by a monster and is in a lot of pain... Although you highly doubt the authenticity of the adventures he talked about, saving his life right now is more important. Get help from<color=#CA2E0AFF>Bidal</color>, who's <color=#CA2E0AFF>in front of the Sage Hut</color>, as soon as possible. See if you can obtain a potion to treat bee sting poisoning!",
    ["TaskDescription110102102"]="Bidal tells you that it's not difficult to cure bee sting poisoning. You just need to apply one Cold Vanilla that grows around here to the wound and you'll be healed in no time.\nWith your help, Tanders recovers his energy, but he doesn't look like he wants to stay on the mountain range for another second... Tanders has a companion waiting to hear news of him at the bottom of the mountain. Why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>go down the mountain with Tanders and find that companion</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110102103"]="You accompany Tanders down the mountain, only to discover that the companion he mentioned is the bard Morts!\nFrom talking to him, you learn that he was forced to travel with Tanders... It turns out that the wannabe hero Tanders, clamored to travel with Morts after hearing several tales of heroic adventures and insisted on going up the mountain to challenge the Mistress in spite of Morts protests!\nSpeaking of this monster, Molts seems to be familiar with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>legend of the Mistress</color>. Why not <color=#CA2E0AFF>sit down</color> and listen to the bard's story about this mysterious monster!",
    ["TaskDescription110102104"]="From listening to Morts' ballad, you learn about the legend of the Mistress. When you ask if the Mistress really exists, Morts says instead of asking him, you should ask the <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster researcher</color> who traveled with them.\nYou're told that the monster researcher has been conducting research on her own since arriving in the Mjolnir Mountains... Maybe she's someone you know?",
    ["TaskDescription110102105"]="Turns out that the monster researcher is the one you saw at Prontera South Gate: Bertha!\nAccording to her, a bee colony in the Mjolnir Mountains has been unusually restless lately, and in order to find out why, Bertha asks you to help her capture a Hornet for study. You're told that she knows how to communicate with Hornets... Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>watch</color> to find out exactly how?",
    ["TaskDescription110102106"]="By observing the dance movements of the Hornet, the two of you learn that a human had stolen something very important to its colony... It's said that the actual reason the creatures of the colony are so agitated is because they desperately want to retrieve this precious item. Who could've done it? Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the Hornet</color> and find out more ahead!",
    ["TaskDescription110102107"]="The two of you followed the Hornet to the bee colony, but on the way you run into Tanders, who was being attacked by Ambernites!\nAt first, Tanders is reluctant to reveal the reason for their attack, but with some assistance from Bertha, you finally learn the whole story. It turns out that Tanders was searching for the Mistress when he came upon a pupa guarded by Hornets. Deeply intrigued, he made off with it, which led to Hornets chasing him and the Ambernites surrounding him in an attempt to retrieve the pupa.\nBased on the response by the Hornets, the pupa seems to be very important to them, so quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>return the pupa safely to its colony</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110102108"]="While delivering the pupa, Bertha discovers that its cocoon is damaged, causing the pupa inside to become critically weak...\nIf it's not kept warm, the pupa will probably die before it hatches. There's no time to lose. Go gather some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Firewood</color> to make a fire!",
    ["TaskDescription110102109"]="Bertha uses the Firewood you brought to create a fire and save the little pupa.\nJust when you thought the pupa was finally ready to hatch, the Hornets start buzzing in alarm.",
    ["TaskDescription110102110"]="Turns out the soon-to-hatch pupa attracted some Greedy Creamies!\nAfter defeating the Creamies, the pupa finally hatches. To your surprise, what comes out of the mysterious cocoon is the legendary monster, Mistress!\nHowever, the queen of bees is very weak after hatching due to the bumps and shakes it experienced earlier... It needs nourishment as soon as possible. Go to the nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stainers</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>get enough Insect Honey</color> from them to nourish the Mistress!",
    ["TaskDescription110103101"]="Just as you are about to leave the Pyramid, Eassis tells you to halt.\nThrough speaking with her, you learn that there is still a great danger within the Pyramid, that Osiris's soul is still in a state of confusion, and that if this continues, he will one day lose control and bring about a great catastrophe within the Pyramid and beyond!\nTo avoid this, you must find a way to appease the soul of Osiris... But how exactly should you do that? Quickly do as Eassis says and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the murals near the Pyramid</color> to find the answer!",
    ["TaskDescription110103102"]="In front of the first mural, the two of you encounter the guardian spirit Kessoso.\nWithout listening to an explanation, he deems the two of you as blasphemers and summons Side Winders to attack... Fortunately, they are no match for you. Kessoso immediately changes his demeanor when he realizes the situation.\nNow that Kessoso is willing to heed your request and <color=#CA2E0AFF>send you to the part of history depicted in the mural</color>, get ready to go before it changes its mind!",
    ["TaskDescription110103103"]="In the first historical journey, you rescue a stranger dying of thirst, who turns out to be the leader of a desert tribe. What's even more surprisingly is that this was actually Osiris a thousand years ago!\nEassis says this part of the past depicts her first encounter with Osiris and that this migration of Osiris' tribe is what led to the ancient Egyptians settling in this land... However, this part of history doesn't have the answers you're looking for. How about taking a look at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next mural</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110103104"]="You meet the guardian spirit Issoso in front of the second mural.\nHe says he's happy to send you two into the mural, but he has weakened with time and is now unable to complete the spell...\nYou follow Issoso's instructions to find him the Monster Hearts needed to replenish his strength. After you help him restore his magic abilities, Issoso says that he can immediately send you into the historical scene depicted on the mural. When you are ready for the second part of journey through history, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and speak to Issoso</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110103105"]="During the second part of your history-hopping journey, you fight alongside Osiris to kill Phreeoni, who had invaded Egyptian territory.\nEassis stats that Osiris' victory in this battle won him respect and admiration; no one dared to doubt the young patriarch's capabilities afterward.\nHowever, Eassis still can't recall what follows. How about heading to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>third mural</color> with her to look for more clues?",
    ["TaskDescription110103106"]="You meet the guardian spirit Rossoso in front of the third mural.\nAfter you help Rossoso teach Side Winders have been bothering him a very long time a lesson, he finally offers to send you into the mural as well.",
    ["TaskDescription110103107"]="During the third part of your historical journey, you witness the coronation of Osiris.\nEassis seems to have remembered his oaths very clearly. Although she feels moved by his words, her expression becomes more somber. After speaking with Eassis, you learn that she has a feeling that the rest of her past will be difficult to bear and that she is afraid to face it... Fortunately, your words of encouragement help Eassis get over her nerves. She decides to go on and witness her past in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>last mural</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110103108"]="You meet the guardian spirit Lassoso in front of the last mural.\nAfter satisfying his desire for money, he finally agrees to send you into the last mural... Which part of the history will you face next?",
    ["TaskDescription110103109"]="During the last part of the historical journey, the two of you see Osiris in a deep state of grief...\nTurns out that the demon king Morroc had invaded the ancient Egyptian empire and Eassis had died in the war... The pained Osiris only wants to use Anubis' power to defeat Morroc, but as Eassis tries to stop what happens next, Anubis reappears and breaks the illusion.\nBy the looks of Anubis, he seems to have something important to say to you and Eassis. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hurry to the center of the Pyramid</color> and listen to what he has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription110103110"]="It turns out that Anubis broke the illusion to stop Eassis from changing history because there are things that Osiris is destined to experience, such as becoming the next king of the underworld after he dies.\nAnubis reminds you of your original intention and says that he can help appease Osiris' soul, but before that, he needs your help to get enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>weapons</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archer Skeletons</color>. Go and do what he says!",
    ["TaskDescription110104101"]="You encounter Phillas in agony at the entrance to Ant Cavern.\nFrom speaking with him, you learn that he has made a grave mistake that Rosie refuses to forgive him for. Phillas wants you to convey his remorse to her and tells you that burning a plant called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Vein Vanilla</color> at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ruins</color> will allow you to see Rosie... Why don't you try this method out?",
    ["TaskDescription110104102"]="You really do see Rosie in the ruins after burning the Spirit Vein Vanilla.\nShe was enthusiastically studying the newly excavated ancient clay tablets. By deciphering the ancient Egyptian cuneiform engraved on it, she has learned that an ancient monster is sealed inside the ruins.\nAccording to Rosie, if you sacrifice enough of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Muka's remains</color>, you can lift the seal and release the ancient monster, which possesses great research value. Seeing Rosie's eager look, you decide to help make her wish come true!",
    ["TaskDescription110104103"]="To your surprise, removing the Pharaoh's seal releases a weak and pitiful little ant! This can't be it, right? Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a closer look</color> at it with Rosie.",
    ["TaskDescription110104104"]="The Antsy looked so harmless and weak that Rosie can't help but feed and take care of it.\nBut for some reason, the Antsy escapes from the ruins when Rosie isn't paying attention. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hurry after it!</color> Don't let the frail little thing get hurt out there!",
    ["TaskDescription110104105"]="The Antsy looked so harmless and weak that Rosie can't help but feed and take care of it.\nBut for some reason, the Antsy escapes from the ruins when Rosie isn't paying attention. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hurry after it!</color> Don't let the frail little thing get hurt out there!",
    ["TaskDescription110104106"]="You relay Rosie's words to Phillas but are surprised to find that his memories are getting mixed up again...\nHe has forgotten some things, but clearly remembers that something terrible is sealed in the ruins. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Phillas to the ruins</color> and prevent the emergence of a dangerous monster!",
    ["TaskDescription110104107"]="By burning the Vanilla, you see Mad Maya in the ruins, but then you are awakened back to reality by a girl named Bowya.\nShe informs you that the aroma of the Spirit Vein Vanilla can cause hallucinations, and that Phillas asked you to burn the Vanilla because he is still obsessed with the past...\nBowya begins telling you the story between Phillas and Rosie, but before she finishes, Phillas disappears once more... Bowya suspects that he has gone off to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> by himself again. Hurry and get Phillas back to safety!",
    ["TaskDescription110104108"]="You find Phillas in front of the cliffs in Ant Cavern.\nHe seems to be hallucinating once again. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>watch what Phillas does</color> first?",
    ["TaskDescription110104109"]="Phillas asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>burn the Spirit Vein Vanilla</color> again, stating that it is very important to him... Seeing his look of grief, you decide to help him one last time.",
    ["TaskDescription110104110"]="In front of the cliffs, you witness the end of the story between Phillas and Rosie.\nShockingly, a monster ant brutally devoured Rosie and fused its body with the girl... Since then, Phillas had gone completely insane and had been wandering around the places where he once spent time at with Rosie. It is his way of atoning.\nRight now there's no one that can help Phillas move on from his past. The only thing you can do now is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take him away from Ant Cavern and bring him above ground</color> where it's safe.",
    ["TaskDescription110105101"]="In the underwater temple, you find the Obeaune High Priestess, Leona, at a loss as to what to do.\nThrough your conversation with her, you learn that she is worried about Nield, God of the Sea's recent condition. You heard that he has been experiencing intense grief ever since the death of Princess Lucia. Why not look for him near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coral Garden</color> and see if you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>help the suffering father get back on his feet</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110105102"]="You find the grieving Nield and learn about the history of the Coral Garden from him.\nLucia loved this garden very much and spent a lot of time and effort here growing the \"Kisses of the Sea\" but now they have withered away... Nield says that these flowers were cultivated using <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bradium</color> obtained from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color>. Why don't you try getting some to nourish the flowers and make them bloom again?",
    ["TaskDescription110105103"]="When Nield hears that you want to make flowers bloom again, he says that you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>try sprinkling Bradium in the garden</color>. If these Kisses of the Sea do bloom, how about <color=#CA2E0AFF>picking some for Nield as a memento</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110105104"]="After receiving the Kisses of the Sea, \nNield finally regains some of his former spirit. He says that he was not the only one who had suffered during the chaos. He's very worried about the frightened inhabitants of the sea and wants to reassure them. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass on Nield's words to his subjects</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>help them out where you can</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110105105"]="You first find Simon the Vadon and help him solve a great crisis in his tummy.\nSeeing how unaware and carefree he is, you can't bear to tell him about Lucia's passing... Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>see if there are any other undersea inhabitants who need your help</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110105106"]="You find Brady and his son and escort them back to their former residence.\nWhich other inhabitants of the sea need help? Why don't you go check up on <color=#CA2E0AFF>High Priestess Leona</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110105107"]="You find Leona praying and help her deal with a Crazed Swordfish.\nLeona seems surprised when she hears that Nield was looking frail and had entrusted you with aiding the inhabitants of the sea... After a moment of thinking, she asks you to get a dish called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Snake</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to Nield</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110105108"]="After tasting the dish that his late daughter used to cook for him, Nield looks calmer and more stable.\nUnexpectedly, he then asks you to deliver his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Trident</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Leona</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110105109"]="Leona asks you to place Nield's Trident in front of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Divine Monument</color>. It seems like it will give you the final answer...",
    ["TaskDescription110106101"]="Upon learning of Gail's decision to run away with the Obeaune princess, John is shocked and doesn't know how to explain the situation to the Wigners. It is only after your suggestion that he remembers he can ask the captain of the Alson Fleet, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Macheda Alson</color>, for help.\nYou hear that Alson is usually near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta's port</color>. There's no time to lose. Hurry and find him!",
    ["TaskDescription110106102"]="You inform Alson of Gail's decision. To your surprise, he responds that such things are not uncommon in the Wigner Family...\nIt turns out that there was also a girl named Colorful Wigner who gave up her position as heiress of the family for freedom. She chose to sail across the ocean on her beloved boat, never to return home.\nAlson asks you to go the beach, pick some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colorful Flowers</color>, and give them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ruvier</color>. Maybe the head of the family will be able to understand Gail's decision after remembering those events.",
    ["TaskDescription110106103"]="After seeing the Colorful Flowers, Ruvier seemed lost in thought.\nHe isn't angry at Gail for leaving without saying a word, but he looks little sad... He says that he won't blame anyone for this. Hurry and let <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson</color> know!",
    ["TaskDescription110106104"]="When you find Alson again, he looks very worried.\nAfter speaking with him, you learn that after the Corsair was taken care of, another merchant ship disappeared at sea! The only person on the ship who returned safely to Alberta was a sailor named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Albert</color>. From talking to him, you learn that he experienced a terrible <color=#CA2E0AFF>shipwreck</color> and somehow got on board the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Treasure Ship</color> where Hobbes was...",
    ["TaskDescription110106105"]="You find a sailor named Rudolph hiding in the prayer room.\nHe was trying to find the rest of his lost crewmates, but is too exhausted to move around freely... Why not help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>search the Treasure Ship</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the other sailors</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110106106"]="You save Sailor Colin from a group of Pirate Skeletons and learn some details about the shipwreck from him.\nAs to why he was on the Treasure Ship, Colin says he doesn't have a clue... Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the other missing sailors</color> and ask them for more information!",
    ["TaskDescription110106107"]="You save Sailor Zavier from a group of Hydras and learn some more details about the shipwreck from him.\nHe states that he was transported here by a strange gap but didn't seem to know what it was... Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the other missing sailors</color> and ask them for more information!",
    ["TaskDescription110106108"]="You save a terrified sailor named Tim from a group Whispers and learn that there's another <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange gap</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain's Cabin</color>! \nCould there be a connection between the two dimensional gaps? Go investigate!",
    ["TaskDescription110106109"]="After passing through the dimensional gap located in the captain's cabin, you arrive on a similar-looking ship... It appears to be the same Shipwreck you defeated the Corsair on!",
    ["TaskDescription110106110"]="You come across a young woman on the Shipwreck.\nThrough speaking with her, you learn that she's the Colorful Wigner that Alson mentioned! You also finally heard the complete story behind what happened to the Wind Chaser and Unicorn... Colorful asked you to convey her apologies to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alson</color>. As for what happened to her, how will you explain it to the world?",
    ["TaskDescription110107101"]="You meet a man named Fulkyn in Payon.\nHe states that he accidentally landed at these coordinates and dropped the Sands of Time he used to travel here nearby. It is said that the Sands of Time are very important and dangerous magic particles. If the sands are left to float freely in this dimension, it could cause unimaginable consequences...\nHelp Fulkyn recover the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sands of Time</color>, will you? He tells you that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> next to him can show you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>location of the Sands of Time</color>, so make use of it!",
    ["TaskDescription110107102"]="You follow Fulkyn's instructions for operating the Mysterious Device. It indicates that the Sands of Time should be scattered near a <color=#CA2E0AFF>pond</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southeast corner</color> of Payon.\nThere's no time to lose! Head there and take a look!",
    ["TaskDescription110107103"]="You find the scattered Sands of Time by the Bright Lotus Pond in the southeast corner of Payon and meet a young stranger nearby.\nWith your help, the young man and his lover confess their feelings for one another. But just before he is about to leave, you happen to learn his name: Liu Wuye!\nHe seems to have the same name as someone you once met, but this young man in front of you is clearly younger than the Liu Wuye you know... What is going on? Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go ask Fulkyn</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110107104"]="Through speaking with Fulkyn, you finally learn what's going on.\nIt turns out that the Sands of Time are magic particles used for time travel, and that Fulkyn is no ordinary traveler, but a time traveler! It is said that those near the Sands of Time are sent to some time in the past or future, but since they do not belong to that time, they are eventually sent back to the present by Demotima.\nFulkyn states that there are still some Sands of Time scattered about somewhere and <color=#CA2E0AFF>recovering the sands</color> is of utmost importance... You should quickly follow his instructions and use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> again to find out where the rest of the Sands of Time are located!",
    ["TaskDescription110107105"]="The Mysterious Device indicates that the next batch of the Sands of Time was dropped in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hidden Wood Village</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Payon</color>.\nNo time to waste. Head over there and take a look!",
    ["TaskDescription110107106"]="Once again, the Sands of Time send you back to some time in the past.\nThis time, you witness the night of terror that befell Hidden Wood Village and see Baroshev use his sinister ploy to transmogrify Jingyin into the Moonlight Flower. Although you know the love story between Liu Wuye and Jingyin won't end well, you have to remember Fulkyn's warning: no one can change the past...\nFocus on solving the problem at hand. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take the Sands of Time you recovered back to Fulkyn</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110107107"]="The events you saw while time traveling deeply saddens you, but Fulkyn once again emphasizes that no one can change the past.\nThe priority is still to <color=#CA2E0AFF>recover the Sands of Time</color> as soon as possible... Hurry and use the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mysterious Device</color> to find out where the rest of the Sands of Time are!",
    ["TaskDescription110107108"]="The Mysterious Device indicates that next portion of the Sands of Time was dropped in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fallen Maple Forest</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>east of Payon</color>.\nThere's no time to lose. Head over there and take a look!",
    ["TaskDescription110107109"]="The third portion of the Sands of Time transports you and Liu Wuye into an unknown period of time.\nHere you meet the monster, Eddga, and learn that he also came to the maple forest to reminisce about a former lover... As you are about to continue speaking with him, Demotima reappears and sends you and Liu Wuye back to the present.",
    ["TaskDescription110107110"]="After telling Liu Wuye about time travel and what had happened, he immediately gets excited about <color=#CA2E0AFF>meeting Fulkyn</color>!\nWhat exactly does Liu Wuye want to say to the time traveler?",
    ["TaskDescription110108101"]="While passing the dilapidated Butsudan in Munak Cave, the martyr Spirit Queller, Qinghe, calls out to you to stop.\nQinghe says that although he regained his consciousness and reconstructed his form with your help, the souls of other Spirit Quellers have yet to be freed and are still wandering around the cave in the form of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Horongs</color>... Qinghe hopes that you can also help the other Spirit Quellers recover their memories so that they can fight under the banner of General Qi Euin once again! But before you do that, you might need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help them resolve the obsessions they had while alive</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110108102"]="You find a Horong near the Soul Devouring Tree gone into a manic state because his memories are in disarray.\nWhile speaking with him, you discover that he's desperate to find someone named Hajen, who he is convinced is waiting for him under the giant tree that countless lovers have pledged their vows under...\nThe problem is that you don't know where this tree is. Why don't you ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>W, the Kafra Service Employee</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110108103"]="You really did find a woman at the Wishing Tree in the middle of Payon. However, she was not the Hajen you were looking for, but a young woman named Haju.\nShe was very shocked to hear about the deceased Spirit Queller's last wish and expressed her willingness to tell you <color=#CA2E0AFF>what occurred in front of this ancient tree</color> long ago...",
    ["TaskDescription110108104"]="Haju tells you the story of her ancestor Hajen and her childhood sweetheart, a Spirit Queller named An Munho.\nShe then asks you to break a branch off the Wishing Tree and take a hair ornament that Hajen once wore to give to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Queller's ghost</color>. If these objects can remind him of Hajen's love, it will definitely ease his soul!",
    ["TaskDescription110108105"]="An Munho regains his memories and his living form with your help.\nHe tells you that protecting more loved ones from being torn apart by the calamity is the Spirit Quellers' mission. Him and his comrades sacrificed themselves so that even more people can live on and be happy. As there are still monsters in the cave that threaten the safety of the people of Payon, he will continue to uphold his mission and fight to the end...\nSince An Munho's soul has found peace, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>quickly find the next heroic soul</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110108106"]="You find a Horong near the Yin-Yang Taiji. He's in anguish because his memories are in disarray.\nWhile speaking with him, you notice that the Horong keeps criticizing himself for being unfilial and that he eagerly wants to apologize to his mother. He tells you that he once lived in a house in Payon West and next to a waterfall and waterwheel.\nWhere exactly is his house? Why don't you go ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Won Chunghan, the chief of Hidden Wood Village</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110108107"]="Won Chunghan is very curious as to why you are asking about the house next to the waterfall and the waterwheel. When you mention the dying wish of the Spirit Queller's ghost, Won Chunghan asks if you'd like to hear a <color=#CA2E0AFF>story from long ago</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110108108"]="Won Chunghan tells you the story of an ancestor of the Won Family, Won Yeong, and her eldest son, Won Bin. Afterwards, she asks you to search for some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bear Paws</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Wild Mushrooms</color>.\nWhat does the old woman want to do with these ingredients?",
    ["TaskDescription110108109"]="Using the ingredients you brought, Won Chunghan makes a bowl of delicious-smelling <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bear Paw Stew with Wild Mushrooms</color>. She tells you that this is a Won Family dish Won Yeong would cook to make her children strong and outstanding.\nThe old woman hopes that this stew will remind <color=#CA2E0AFF>Won Bin</color> of how proud his mother was of him, and help him overcome his obsession and free his soul.",
    ["TaskDescription110108110"]="Spirit Queller Won Bin regains his memories and living form with your help.\nHe is very happy that his mother was proud of him and said that it is the mission of the Spirit Quellers to ensure that more mothers do not have to be separated from their children. He declares that he will reunite with his mother after clearing the cave of all monsters and make her an even prouder parent.\nNow that Won Bin's soul is at ease, how about searching for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next heroic soul</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110108111"]="You find a Horong near a waterfall and discover that his memories are in disarray, causing him great distress.\nThrough speaking with him, you notice that the Horong is very worried about the safety of his son, Little Ayu. He states that he left Little Ayu in the care of Lady Euin, but he is unable to determine what happened to his child after that...\nWhy don't you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Residence</color> and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sun Euin</color>, a descendant of the Lady Euin?",
    ["TaskDescription110108112"]="From speaking with Sun Euin, you learn that the wife of the late General Qi Euin had indeed taken in many orphans who had lost their parents in battle. He assures you that those children were well cared for and that the Spirit Quellers's son must be doing well also.\nAs for a way to comfort the hero's soul, Sun Euin suggests that you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orphanage</color> not far away and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take pictures of the children playing</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110108113"]="Sun Euin asks you to take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>picture of the Euin Family's Orphanage</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Picture of a Hundred Children</color> that Lady Euin drew herself to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Queller's ghost</color>. Hopefully, by seeing them, he will feel the Euin Family's love and care for the orphans, which might be enough to alleviate his worries and free his soul.",
    ["TaskDescription110108114"]="Spirit Queller Muhyeon regains his memory and living form with your assistance. He is very grateful to Lady Euin for the help she gave long ago and states that it is the mission of the Spirit Quellers to protect the young children from having to live in turmoil and that he will fight to the end for this cause.\nQuickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Qinghe</color> and tell him about the Spirit Quellers you helped! What does Qinghe believe is the mission of the Spirit Quellers'?",
    ["TaskDescription110109101"]="You are stopped by Comet Euin in Payon, who tells you about a concerning matter involving his senior fellow disciple, Busang. Recently, he has been sneaking out in the middle of the night. In order to help Comet figure out why, you need to go to the nearby wilderness and steal 15 Wood Crystal Powders from Wormtails for him.",
    ["TaskDescription110109102"]="Comet Euin is determined to find out the truth behind his fellow disciple's midnight outings, and he seems to already have a plan. He asks you to help him make a bowl of Busang's favorite food—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Fruity Squid</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110109103"]="Comet Euin places a specially-made Euin Tracer Pill in the Fruity Squid. To learn more about Busang's secret trips, Comet Euin needs you take this special bowl of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fruity Squid</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Busang</color> and persuade him to take a bite.",
    ["TaskDescription110109104"]="Comet Euin tells you that his special Euin Tracer Pill can make people who consume it emit a distinct scent that only his pet Bobo can smell. Hurry and take <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bobo</color> back to where Busang was standing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>track him down</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110109105"]="You follow Bobo and find out that Busang was meeting a mysterious girl named Eunsook in an abandoned house, which Comet says was never inhabited. In order to help Comet figure out the relationship between Busang and Eunsoook, you need to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon East Forest</color> and collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Mystical Star Leaves</color> to give to Comet Euin.",
    ["TaskDescription110109106"]="To make sure the investigation goes smoothly, help Comet Euin <color=#CA2E0AFF>prepare</color> a dish Busang likes—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Fillet</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110109107"]="On the Fish Fillet you helped prepare, Comet Euin sprinkles some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dizzying Powder</color> on top, which will make the person who consumes it faint. Comet Euin plans to disguise himself as Busang after it knocks him out, then he'll go to the meeting place as him. But first you need you to coax <color=#CA2E0AFF>Busan</color> into eating the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Fillet</color>, so hurry and go find him!",
    ["TaskDescription110109108"]="With some teamwork, you and Comet Euin successfully put Busang out. Quickly take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Black Dog Blood</color> and head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>abandoned house</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon South</color> to wait for the disguised Comet Euin. Soon the identity of the girl will be revealed.",
    ["TaskDescription110109109"]="Through Comet Euin's ploy and the use of Black Dog Blood, you finally discover the true identity of the girl in the abandoned house—a demon known as a Sohee! Although Eunsook is a Sohee, she says that she and Busang are truly in love and that she would not harm him. After saying this, an evil Sohee named Eunju suddenly appears and attacks you! Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat Eunju</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110109110"]="You learn that a Vixen was controlling the souls of Eunsook and her sister Eunju with their ashes and that they were forced to bewitch and absorb the vitality of the living. After finding out the truth, Busang decides to go save his beloved Eunsook. The Vixen is very powerful and of course you and Comet Euin wouldn't abandon a friend, so go with him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forest of the General in Payon East to slay the Vixen</color> and save Eunsook!",
    ["TaskDescription110109111"]="With your combined strength, you, Comet Euin, and Busang are finally able to defeat the Vixen. The kindhearted Eunsook is determined not to be used for evil ever again and asks you to rebury her. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Forest of the General</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>rebury</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eunsook</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110110101"]="You came across Omari from the Eden Group beneath Geffen Tower. He has been fretting over the corroded text on an ancient tablet.\nFollow Omari's instructions and get him some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gangrene Grass</color> so he can clean the tablet!",
    ["TaskDescription110110102"]="Omari was surprised that you managed to get the Gangrene Grass from an area crawling with so many monsters! <color=#CA2E0AFF>Apply the juice of Gangrene Grass to the ancient tablet</color> and see what happens.",
    ["TaskDescription110110103"]="The text on the ancient tablet finally started to show. Read it to Omari. But before that, maybe you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a closer look</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110110104"]="As you moved closer to the ancient tablet, you got sucked into an illusion by a mysterious power. According to Omari, you were transported into Archbishop Merlin Heines' memory!\nOmari told you that this special ability of yours is significant to the field of archeology. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow him</color> and continue to unearth and study artifacts!",
    ["TaskDescription110110105"]="Using his archaeologist's sharp sense of smell, Omari found a broken staff in the ruins.\nAccording to him, this staff is an artifact from a thousand years ago, but it's completely covered in dirt. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clean the staff</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110110106"]="You were sucked into another memory when you touched the staff. It was the memory of another adventurer from a thousand years ago. You saw Wyatt, who fought as a member of Pentagram, and watched how tragically the mages died. You also saw a stranger who seemed to have gone mad.\nAfter knowing all this, Omari told you that what you have just gone through will bring about a great leap in historical research. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow him</color> and continue to search for the next historical artifact!",
    ["TaskDescription110110107"]="Following Omari's lead, you dug up a tattered diary. However, it is protected by a magic barrier and cannot be read.\nFollow Omari's instructions and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Monster Nails</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Marionettes</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110110108"]="Omari asked you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>place the Sharp Monster Nails on the diary</color>. This method can supposedly dispel the magic barrier and allow you to read the diary!",
    ["TaskDescription110110109"]="After touching the diary, you entered the memory of Truman, a member of Pentagram. But this time round, everything you saw showed you that he was a traitor of Pentagram!\nYou wonder what happened to Truman in the end. Follow his path and head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blood Abbey</color> to find some answers!",
    ["TaskDescription110110110"]="You saw a Blood Clan monster in front of Blood Abbey. Could the monster be him?",
    ["TaskDescription110111101"]="Katrina called out to you in Geffen Tower. She hoped you could help her locate an alchemist called <color=#CA2E0AFF>De'qeen</color>.\nShe said De'qeen is an Alchemist Guild emissary stationed in Geffen. He is rather knowledgeable on the structure of Fragments of Ymir's Heart and might be able to help Jesqurienne find a way to repair the Artifact. Katrina told you that De'qeen is currently staying in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest of Geffen</color>. Pay him a visit!",
    ["TaskDescription110111102"]="You found De'qeen's residence but he is nowhere to be found. The only thing there was a strange letter.\nAccording to the letter, an experimental test subject codenamed K-406 has escaped. This subject will attach itself to the nearest human that it can find and try to kill its host by controlling the host's thoughts. Katrina hopes that you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask around in Geffen</color> and see if you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the host</color> while she informs Jesqurienne of what has happened.",
    ["TaskDescription110111103"]="According to the letter, the host will exhibit abnormal behavior. Daphne told you that there has been a \"weirdo\" coming into the shop to buy huge amounts of green hair dye!\nShe said that she can tell you where he lives, but you'll first have to get her enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wild Mistletoe</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblin Forest</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110111104"]="After obtaining the Wild Mistletoe, Daphne happily told you that the man lives in a <color=#CA2E0AFF>small wooden cabin</color> located <color=#CA2E0AFF>northeast of Geffen</color>. Go there and see if he is indeed the host of the test subject!",
    ["TaskDescription110111105"]="You did not find the man but you did find his mother, Eddie. She told you that recently her son has been sneaking out of the house a lot and was mumbling something about an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Village</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>8 PM</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest corner</color>. Could this be where the man is headed?",
    ["TaskDescription110111106"]="The clue led you to the strange man, Amber, but you realized that he was having a rendezvous with a female Orc! According to Amber, he saw an <color=#CA2E0AFF>alchemist</color> behaving strangely <color=#CA2E0AFF>nearby</color>. Could that alchemist be the host?",
    ["TaskDescription110111107"]="You found the body of the Alchemist Guild emissary, De'qeen, and saw the test subject <color=#CA2E0AFF>Doppelganger</color> attached to him after using a flash grenade.\nThe Doppelganger brazenly admitted that he killed De'qeen and now that you're here, you will become his next host!",
    ["TaskDescription110111108"]="In order to find the right opportunity to subdue the Doppelganger, you went along with his wishes for now and challenged the great Orc Hero. Seeing that his ploy to kill you had failed, the Doppelganger urged you to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color> to challenge tougher opponents.",
    ["TaskDescription110111109"]="You went along with Doppelganger's command and provoked the Kobolds. But even when you were surrounded by the Kobold army, you managed to win the battle. In the Doppelganger's dismay, you suggested <color=#CA2E0AFF>entering Geffen's underground caves</color> as a challenge. Take this opportunity to enter the magic ward created by Archmage Merlin Heines and seal the Doppelganger away!",
    ["TaskDescription110111110"]="After much work, you finally managed to defeat the Doppelganger and successfully sealed him in the caves below Geffen. Inform <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color> what happened. Perhaps Jesqurienne and Katrina will have some insights.",
    ["TaskDescription110112101"]="You run into Bairde and Trisse quarrelling outside of Geffen. After asking about the situation, you learn that Bairde captured Trisse for being a member of the Mobsters, but Trisse says she came here to go after their leader, who had defected from the Assassins Guild. Hurry and follow Trisse to the Mobsters' base.",
    ["TaskDescription110112102"]="Following several rounds of questioning, the underboss of the Mobsters finally reveals that their boss has had his eyes on a trade caravan in the Sograt Desert for a long time and that he has already taken a crew of underlings to ambush it. Quickly follow Trisse to the Sograt Desert to find where the targeted caravan has set up camp.",
    ["TaskDescription110112103"]="After speaking with Elkson, the leader of the desert caravan, the two of you decide to help him bring the team of adventurers he hired back to their camp. Coincidentally, this team of adventurers is Ygnizem's crew. When she learns that the caravan is in trouble, she decides to go with Abessie back to the camp to protect the merchants. She asks you to go to the area with Frilldoras to find Kavaski who is acting alone and bring him back to the caravan.",
    ["TaskDescription110112104"]="When you successfully bring Kavaski back to the caravan camp, the leader tells you that the Mobsters have sent him a threatening letter saying that they've already located their cargo storage locations and are about to carry out their raid. Therefore, you and Trisse decide to check out the warehouse to the south while Ygnizem checks out the warehouse to the north with her team of adventurers.",
    ["TaskDescription110112105"]="You and Trisse find a large quantity of herbs in the warehouse to the south. Trisse senses something unusual about the trade caravan. Why would an ordinary caravan have such a large quantity of herbs that are highly-coveted in the desert? Trisse decides to stay and investigate and asks you to check out the warehouse in the north, where the team of adventurers went. Hurry to the northern warehouse and meet up with Ygnizem!",
    ["TaskDescription110112106"]="You meet up with an angry Ygnizem and see an outrageously-priced list of herbs left in the warehouse by the caravan. Ygnizem has figured out that the caravan had been stockpiling the rare herbs to sell for exorbitant prices. At this moment, Abessie informs everyone that they seem to have fallen for the Mobsters' diversion trap. Hurry back to the caravan's camp!",
    ["TaskDescription110112107"]="After you rush back to the camp, you discover that the caravan has already been raided by the devious Mobsters. Not only did they seriously injure the merchants, they also got away with a large amount of goods and money from the camp. To help Abessie treat the wounded, Ygnizem and Kavaski have gone to gather herbs. After speaking with merchants, you and Trisse learn that the Mobsters have run off towards the southeast. Hurry southeast to track down the fleeing gang of thieves!",
    ["TaskDescription110112108"]="You and Trisse follow the trail of thieves to the Ant Cavern, only to discover an ambush set up well ahead of time by the Mobster leader, Goldie. Trisse pretends to be trapped so that Goldie lets her guard down. Quickly seize the opportunity to subdue Goldie in one fell swoop!",
    ["TaskDescription110112109"]="You successfully subdue Goldie with the help of Trisse's surprise attack and prepare to take Goldie back to the Assassins Guild. On your way there, you meet up with Ygnizem, who's gathering herbs. Ygnizem is surprised to discover that Goldie is the righteous older friend she had when she was a child and doesn't believe that Goldie could betray her principles of justice. Trisse decides to stay and figure out the truth and entrusts you and Ygnizem to bring Goldie back to the Assassins Guild.",
    ["TaskDescription110112110"]="You and Trisse are escorting Goldie when you encounter some slum residents. After learning that you were taking Goldie to the Assassins Guild to be punished, they desperately try to stop you from taking her. That's when they tell you that Goldie used all her savings to help these people set up their homes so that they would not be displaced and have shelter from the wilderness. You tell them that you will definitely communicate this unknown information to the leader of the Assassins Guild, but for now you must continue escorting Goldie to the guild.",
    ["TaskDescription110112111"]="While escorting Goldie back to the Assassins Guild, you and Ygnizem encounter many poor residents from Morroc that block your path. You learn from them that Goldie had previously collect edmany valuable herbs to save a poor child's mother. However, to keep your promise to Trisse, you still must take Goldie to the Assassins Guild. When you do, convey the poor residents' request to Hassan.",
    ["TaskDescription110113101"]="In the ancient city of Glast Heim, you bump into a local named Hylas, who appears to be running away in a panic. It seems that something terrible has happened. Go and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hylas</color> what is going on.",
    ["TaskDescription110113102"]="Hylas tells you that a fearsome monster is terrorizing the city, the likes of which he has never seen before. It has a lion's face, a mass of snake heads sprouting from its rear, and the limbs and lower body of a goat. You come across Lanister and his family as they confront the evil monster, and help them to fight off the creature. However, Lanister's wife, Blanche, is seriously injured, and losing blood by the second. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clotting Grass</color> to help stop Blanche's bleeding.",
    ["TaskDescription110113103"]="You help Lanister to stabilize Blanche's injury, and ask him to give you a detailed account of the situation. Lanister tells you that this was the first time he had ever seen such a huge and ferocious monster, but he knew that if he didn't try to subdue it, it would have wrought havoc on the people of the city. You then set off to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>whereabouts of this strange monster</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110113104"]="You finally find the ferocious monster outside the steps of Glast Heim and try to end its rampage once and for all. However, the monster refuses to go down without a fight and manages to escape a second time. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Keep chasing</color> after that <color=#CA2E0AFF>ferocious beast</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110113105"]="You fight the ferocious beast, but it is far too strong for you to defeat. You decide to retreat and find another way to deal with it. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Return to Lanister</color> and discuss potential solutions with him.",
    ["TaskDescription110113106"]="You tell Lanister all about what happened with the ferocious beast. Hearing your words, he reminds you that no one knows more about monsters than Monster Researchers, so you decide to take a picture of the creature and bring it to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster Researcher Norten</color>, in the hopes that he will be able to help you.",
    ["TaskDescription110113107"]="With the help of Monster Researcher Norten, you finally identify the ferocious monster to be the Chimera, King Schmidt's pet from hundreds of years ago. This fierce beast was supposed to have died centuries ago, but for some reason it has been resurrected. Norten decides to investigate the root of this incident and therefore needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chimera's saliva</color>. Go and get the saliva he needs from the corpse of a monster that has been bitten by the Chimera.",
    ["TaskDescription110113108"]="Norten carries out some tests on the saliva and discovers that it is filled with an evil, dark aura, which seems to have been caused by some kind of ancient curse. Unless you find the root of the curse and cleanse it, you will never be able to truly eliminate the Chimera. Norten suggests that you should perhaps <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> the first person to have seen the creature, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hylas</color>, and ask if he may have done something to inadvertently trigger the curse.",
    ["TaskDescription110113109"]="Hylas tells you that he drank the water trickling down from the Goddess Statue just before he first saw the Chimera, despite being warned not to do so by the elders of Glast Heim. It seems that in order to find out the truth, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the statue to investigate</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110113110"]="Your careful investigation finally reveals the root of the curse. This all happened because Hylas drank the water trickling down from the Goddess Statue, unleashing an ancient curse forbidding the people of Glast Heim from touching the city's water source, and thus resurrecting the Chimera. To lift the curse, you must drip Hylas' blood into the pool of the Goddess Statue. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and collect Hylas' blood</color> to break the curse!",
    ["TaskDescription110114101"]="You happen to overhear a conversation between Eden Group Instructor Rockley and an unknown Crusader named Seyren in the ancient city of Glast Heim. Eden Group members have been going missing, and it appears that a mysterious organization known as the Shadow Hunters is responsible. Rockley asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate with Seyren</color>. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>southwest of the city</color>, where Eden Group members went missing while carrying out an archaeological excavation.",
    ["TaskDescription110114102"]="You and Seyren find a pointy shovel near the ruins where the Eden Group members went missing. Seyren seems to have discovered something, but first he needs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloudy Alcohol Reagents</color> from Carats to verify his postulations.",
    ["TaskDescription110114103"]="Seyren uses the Cloudy Alcohol Reagents you brought back to perform an experiment and found no footprints in the vicinity. He tells you his thorough survey confirms the mysterious disappearances are the work of the Shadow Hunters. There are no signs of blood or a struggle, so the Shadow Hunters must have taken away the Eden Group members without killing them. You suggest disguising yourselves as an Eden Group member to lure out the Shadow Hunters. Seyren approves of your idea, but insists on donning the disguise himself while you take care of a more important task. He needs you to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Monster Saliva</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soft Water Weeds</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110114104"]="After retrieving the monster saliva and water weeds, you return to find that Seyren has disappeared. A talking Smokie suddenly appears before you, claiming that it is Seyren's battle companion. It tells you that Seyren secretly released it after he was taken away by the Shadow Hunters so that it can show you the way to their lair. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow the Smokie</color> and find the imprisoned Eden Group members!",
    ["TaskDescription110114105"]="You find two Eden Group members in the depths of the Glast Heim Sewers. After examining their injuries, the Smokie reveals that one of them has severely-injured vocal cords and is unable to speak. You need to find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clatterweed</color> from plants that like dark places to help him get his voice back!",
    ["TaskDescription110114106"]="You help heal Eden Group member Laforet's damaged vocal cords. Under your inquiry, Laforet reveals that the kidnappers tortured him for information on the whereabouts of certain mysterious documents, however Laforet had no idea what they were talking about. Laforet feels his back throbbing with pain. Help <color=#CA2E0AFF>Laforet check</color> what's wrong with his <color=#CA2E0AFF>back</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110114107"]="The terrible kidnappers had tortured Eden Group member Laforet and carved the words \"Thieves should also experience the pain of loss\" on his back with a sharp blade. You suddenly hear Eden Group member Sarence moan in agony. The Smokie tells you that unless you do something about the burn on Sarence's arm, he may lose function of the arm permanently. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lionheart Pool</color> to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cold Water</color> to make a compress.",
    ["TaskDescription110114108"]="You help soothe Sarence's burned arm and discover he also has something carved into his back: \"Arsonists should also experience the agony of burns\". Sarence also expresses that he has no idea what these mysterious documents could be despite the severe torture he suffered at the hands of the kidnappers. It is then that the Smokie returns. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask the Smokie</color> what it has found.",
    ["TaskDescription110114109"]="The Smokie tells you it couldn't find Seyren anywhere nearby. You learn from Sarence that Seyren told the Shadow Hunters that he knew where the documents were in order to lure the hunters away and create an opportunity for you to rescue them. The Smokie then tells you that the Shadow Hunters are in fact blind and asks that you smear the Fresh Monster Saliva on your body and tie the Soft Water Weeds to the soles of your shoes to help mask your human scent and conceal the sound of your footsteps. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the Smokie</color> and find Seyren.",
    ["TaskDescription110114110"]="The familiar scent detected by the Smokie turns out to be a special leaf from its hometown, the Directional Leaf. The Smokie believes Seyren left this clue behind for it. As long as it follows the Directional Leaf, you will be able to find Seyren. Follow the Smokie and find Seyren and the Shadow Hunters.",
    ["TaskDescription110115101"]="You come across Fulkyn in a corner of Glast Heim. As ever, he's lost in his own world fiddling with strange devices. You look at the grave expression on Fulkyn's face and decide to...",
    ["TaskDescription110115102"]="At Fulkyn's request, you inspect the beeping Mysterious Device. By his explanation, the device is warning all of you that someone has traveled to the year AW231 in an attempt to change the past. If you do nothing, you may cease to exist. You promise Fulkyn that you will help him investigate. Before you go, he needs you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spring of Quiet</color> to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> energy crystals called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tear Spirits</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110115103"]="You find the Tear Spirits near the Spring of Quiet. Fulkyn tells you that they can be used as an energy source for the time-stopping device. Everything is now ready. You can <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick up the Sands of Time</color> from Fulkyn at any time to go back to the year AW231 as indicated by the device.",
    ["TaskDescription110115104"]="You and Fulkyn arrive at Glast Heim in the year AW231. You head east per the device's instructions to find the intruder trying to alter history. Unexpectedly, before you can locate the intruder, you are attacked by the Demotima who is tasked with keeping order in time and space. Fulkyn speculates that this is because the intruder has already made their move and the only way to find where they're hiding now is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow the Demotima</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110115105"]="You come to a river while following the agressive Demotima and hear faint voices coming from the other side of the river. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>soften your footsteps and quietly approach</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110115106"]="You see two people locked in a confrontation by the river. Fulkyn looks grave and informs you he has a long history with one of them. Any action taken from here has to be done by you alone or he'll be recognized. It is then the sage named Barr Venter launches an attack on Thanatos, and you have no choice but to <color=#CA2E0AFF>lend a hand</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110115107"]="You follow Thanatos to a house on the east side of Glast Heim where Lucci should be waiting, but discover her missing. You find tracks outside the house and suspect a trap. However, Thanatos insists on looking for Lucci. Determined to help him, you and Thanatos <color=#CA2E0AFF>track the claw marks left behind by monsters</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110115108"]="You find Lucci surrounded by monsters in front of an altar and manage to save her after an intense battle. Thanatos wants to <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for some herbs to heal the wounded Lucci</color>, but Lucci begs him not to leave. It looks like you'll have to go on his behalf...",
    ["TaskDescription110115109"]="When you return with the healing herbs, you discover that the Lucci in Thanatos' arms is actually a mechanical magic doll in disguise. It has stabbed Thanatos with a poisoned dagger and you realize that Barr Venter is behind all of this. His goal seems to be to force Thanatos to give up on hunting Morroc, and he will stop at nothing to achieve his goal. It is at this critical moment that Fulkyn activates the time-stopping device. You must use this opportunity to put history back on the right track. To do this, you must first collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gold Dew</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sageworms</color> to counteract the poison.",
    ["TaskDescription110115110"]="You collect enough Gold Dew. Meanwhile, Fulkyn takes the opportunity to swap Thanatos and Barr Venter's positions, placing the dagger in Thanatos' hand instead. Now, all you have to do is <color=#CA2E0AFF>apply the Gold Dew on Thanatos' wound</color> and restart the flow of time...",
    ["TaskDescription110115111"]="You successfully rescue Thanatos and restore history to its original course. Lucci rushes over and begs Thanatos to spare Barr Venter. It seems the curtain is finally ready to fall on this tale from seven hundred years ago. However...",
    ["TaskDescription110116101"]="Guard Calvin frantically asks for your help and tells you that there seems to have been a very serious case in the palace this morning. Panicking, he stumbles over his words, telling you only that Commander Bohr is waiting for you in the inner garden. When you are ready, he can escort you there immediately.",
    ["TaskDescription110116102"]="You meet Commander Bohr in the palace garden, where he tells you that His Majesty went to the Royal Tomb this morning to mourn the three dead princes. However, while mourning, an unusual noise erupted from the tomb. The guards entered in a panic, only to find His Majesty on the ground unconscious. When they brought the king back to the palace for treatment, he somehow transformed into the image of Prince Nate... You can’t believe what you’re hearing, but Commander Bohr tells you that it’s too early to draw a conclusion. For the time being, you decide to help Archbishop Wolmas identify the true identity of the remains. To do so, you need to collect the corrupt blood of the Familiar first.",
    ["TaskDescription110116103"]="Now, all you’re missing is the vile slime of 15 female thief bugs and then you’ll have all the materials Archbishop Wolmas needs!",
    ["TaskDescription110116104"]="You finally finish collecting the various materials needed by Archbishop Wolmas. Time is of the essence, so go back as soon as possible to report to the Archbishop!",
    ["TaskDescription110116105"]="Archbishop Wolmas identifies the remains of Prince Nate, which brings an entirely new question to the surface: where exactly is His Majesty the King? During the conversation, Commander Bohr appears to have found a new clue and invites you to join him in the Royal Tomb to investigate. Before you leave, the princess solemnly asks you to make sure to find His Majesty.",
    ["TaskDescription110116106"]="You and Bohr find some strange clues in the royal tomb, the most suspicious of which is the black liquid near Prince Nate's casket. To further confirm your suspicions, you take a sample with you to the Prontera Library and seek help from the alchemist Lawrence.",
    ["TaskDescription110116107"]="Lawrence said he needs further proof to help you determine the identity of this black liquid. To do so, you need to first capture a live lunatic to use as an experimental subject...",
    ["TaskDescription110116108"]="You return to Lawrence with a frisky lunatic in hand. However, you wonder, what kind of experiment could he possibly have in mind?",
    ["TaskDescription110116109"]="To your surprise, Lawrence mixes his hair into the sample of black liquid, and despite your disgusted expression, feeds it to the lunatic you caught...",
    ["TaskDescription110116110"]="Thanks to Lawrence's experiment, you finally witness the true effect of the black liquid. To your shock and awe, it is in fact a potion that completely transforms the appearance of its subject! With Lawrence’s help, the answer is gradually coming into focus. Now, it's time to return and reveal the truth together with Bohr!",
    ["TaskDescription110117101"]="After waiting anxiously for days on end, Commander Bohr finally contacts you. You assume that perhaps there is a new clue relating to the case of His Majesty's disappearance...?",
    ["TaskDescription110117102"]="You go to the training grounds of the Kingdom Defense Force to find Commander Bohr, who has been waiting for you. Flanked by two Defense Force soldiers, Bohr informs you that after rigorously inspecting all of the people and goods entering and leaving Prontera, they have discovered a new clue. Now, Captain Peddie, one of the parties involved, will share more details with you. Please inform Peddie when you are ready!",
    ["TaskDescription110117103"]="Based on Captain Peddie's account, you learn that there is a delegation from the Church of Arunabez who have a special pass to enter the kingdom, granted by the Seven Royal Families themselves, which allows them to leave Prontera with large amounts of goods without inspection at the border. However, there is still more intel the Defense Force has yet to share. Bohr gestures for another soldier named Angelo to come forward and describe what he has seen and heard...",
    ["TaskDescription110117104"]="What Angelo tells you is even more pivotal. He shares that while on his morning patrol, he heard two strange men talking about \"His Majesty\" outside Prontera South Gate, one of whom was dressed in the garb of the Church and appeared to be a member of the mission. Angelo shadowed the two men, until he discovered their quarters outside the South Gate. Finally, you can identify the culprits behind the kidnapping of His Majesty!",
    ["TaskDescription110117105"]="After discussing, you and Bohr decide to conduct a covert investigation of the mission in order to avoid alerting the enemy. Heaven forbid those miscreants harm His Majesty in the heat of the moment! Bohr asks you to disguise yourself as a member of the Church and blend in with the mission, so that you can glean additional intel and look for a potential opportunity to rescue His Majesty. But before that, you need to disguise yourself. On Bohr’s advice, you go to the South Gate and discreetly take pictures of the members of the mission. Next, you hand them over to Vera, an appearance merchant, and ask her to help you make an identical costume.",
    ["TaskDescription110117106"]="Vera agrees to your request. However, before she can start, you need to help her collect the light blue down fur of an eclipse, a veronica flower and some fine leather made from the hide of a savage bebe.",
    ["TaskDescription110117107"]="Time is running out! Once you finish collecting the materials Vera needs, go back and give them to her as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription110117108"]="Everything is prepared and it’s finally time to take action. Based on the intel Bohr analyzed, he suggests that you disguise yourself as a close friend of the mysterious man the mission’s members keep talking about. Because of the deep respect they have for him, he believes your infiltration will face less obstacles. Before leaving, Bohr repeatedly reminds you to not to be reckless and retreat at the first sign of danger. If you’re ready, put on the costume of the Church and go to their provisional quarters at the Prontera South Gate!",
    ["TaskDescription110117109"]="Bohr's suspicions are correct. The members of the mission really are in awe of the mysterious figure, and you easily manage to fool the guards. Now, it's time to start going through the suspicious cargo boxes one by one.",
    ["TaskDescription110117110"]="You carefully examine some of the supply boxes in the mission's quarters, but turn up nothing. During your investigation, your plans are scuttled by an eclipse who is attracted by food nearby. You’re discovered by a gold-haired member of the mission, but strangely enough, he doesn’t expose you. Instead, he devises a plan to conceal your departure. Although you have your doubts, your plan to secretly infiltrate the mission has failed and for now you can only return to the Defense Force training grounds to look for Bohr and consider your next move...",
    ["TaskDescription110117111"]="You help Trinity set up the Circle of Spiritual Summons, in which the true face of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tao Gunka</color> is now finally revealed...",
    ["TaskDescription110118101"]="In Aldebaran, you meet a group of Republican Guard soldiers who are gathered together. They look haggard and unsettled, as if something is deeply troubling them...?",
    ["TaskDescription110118102"]="After a conversation with Chief Gerner, you learn that a strange madness is spreading through the city, along with a spate of bizarre posters whose significance is still unknown. Chief Gerner believes that these events are a carefully planned conspiracy and has assigned a commission for you to work with to investigate the matter further. If you are willing to help, proceed to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Southeast Quarter</color> and find a surgeon named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elle</color>, who was the first to discover this mysterious madness.",
    ["TaskDescription110118103"]="With the help of Dr. Elle, you learn about some of the traits of these patients, most of whom were already suffering from other diseases, but returned to sound health after falling into madness. In the course of your conversation, Dr. Elle reveals that over the past few days many of the patients have stopped coming to the clinic. Alarmed, you frantically ask for the clinic's <color=#CA2E0AFF>medical records</color> and report back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chief Gerner</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110118104"]="You inform Chief Gerner of the doctor's speculation. The guardsmen split up and arrange all of the infected patients in a line one by one, while you travel together with Chief Gerner to the north of the city in search of a deaf patient named Palin. Unfortunately, by the time you find Palin, she is already on the verge of an attack of madness. For safety's sake, Chief Gerner asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sneak up behind her and knock her out</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110118105"]="You manage to subdue Palin and knock her unconscious. As you look around, you realize that the spooky posters have also appeared in the streets of the North Quarter. Chief Gerner entrusts you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the posters one by one</color> while he takes Palin to Dr. Elle's clinic for treatment.",
    ["TaskDescription110118106"]="Thanks to your efforts, the posters in the streets of the north of the city are practically all collected. However, just as you are about to <color=#CA2E0AFF>uncover the last poster</color>, suddenly you...?",
    ["TaskDescription110118107"]="While recovering the posters, you encounter one of “God’s Messengers” and a mysterious alchemist. After having a conversation with him, you learn that the symbols on the posters may be alchemical symbols with hidden meanings. Although you haven’t deciphered them all, you already have some suspicions. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to the clinic</color> and rendezvous with Chief Gerner.",
    ["TaskDescription110118108"]="You return to the clinic, but there’s no sign of Chief Gerner. Dr. Elle informs you that they have gone to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Southwest Quarter</color>, where the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Epsilon</color> family are supposedly also showing signs of madness.",
    ["TaskDescription110118109"]="By the time you arrive in the Southwest Quarter, an incident has indeed occurred and you notice that a large number of soldiers on duty to maintain law and order. The soldiers thank you as they see you hand out comforting food to the frightened people and tell you that Chief Gerner is in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>square up ahead</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110118110"]="You help Chief Gerner subdue the Epsilon family, but soon notice something dubious about Dr. Elle. To confirm your suspicions, you decide to return to the clinic and attempt to find out his true identity. For your protection, Chief Gerner hands over his <color=#CA2E0AFF>transceiver</color> to you.",
    ["TaskDescription110120101"]="On Kokomo Beach, you saw a young pirate talking to himself. His shudders hinted he might be in some sort of trouble. Why don't you speak to him and see if you could help?",
    ["TaskDescription110120102"]="You heard about the bounty hunter from the young pirate and went to east Saint Darmain to investigate the assault. At the scene of the crime, a broken arrow caught your attention. Maybe the mark on it could be used to track the merciless bounty hunter. You took the arrow to the west of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kokomo Beach</color> and looked for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Drake</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110120103"]="From the pirates, you learned the mark is that of a woman named Cecil Devine. She was adopted by Captain Drake only to betray him later, then earned her money selling privy pirate information to the bounty hunters group. A livid Spencer wanted to bring the traitor in but Drake stopped him. Just then, an <color=#CA2E0AFF>underling</color> returned to the hideout with terrible news...",
    ["TaskDescription110120104"]="Cecil made a move and kidnapped some pirates. She wanted Drake to trade his own life for their safe return. This prompted the angry Spencer to request that you get Cecil. Based on the pact between them and the leader, you couldn't refuse. You went to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Saint Darmain</color> in an attempt to free the pirate hostages.",
    ["TaskDescription110120105"]="You found a lead in Saint Darmain, as a beaten pirate informed you which direction Cecil went before passing out. You follow the clue <color=#CA2E0AFF>northward</color> in search of more...",
    ["TaskDescription110120106"]="You found Cecil, but you didn't expect what she said completely contradicted Spencer's words. She didn't betray anyone, just that she had a mission from the start to seek revenge against the Gangash Pirates. As you were puzzled by the conflicting stories, Cecil suggested clarifying the mess with Drake face-to-face. Wanting to know the truth, you all came back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kokomo Beach</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110120107"]="You and Cecil were shocked to find all pirates passed out with no sign of Drake. Cecil concluded that no doubt Drake had fled out of guilt and left the pirates behind to fend for themselves. She dashed off to follow Drake's footprints. You then heard <color=#CA2E0AFF>feeble cries for help</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110120108"]="To awake the unconscious Spencer, you must find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mint</color> growing in the grove of Kokomo Beach...",
    ["TaskDescription110120109"]="The Mint woke Spencer up and he told you it indeed was Drake who knocked the pirates out, which was expected. What was not is Spencer telling you the stories and secrets about Cecil, Drake, and the Gangash Pirates. You opened <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drake's diary</color> as he requested...",
    ["TaskDescription110120110"]="After reading Drake's diary, you found that he didn't destroy Cecil's village intentionally, though he was the cause. You realized you have no right to pass judgment on the incident, so you decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass the truth on to Cecil</color> and let her make the final decision.",
    ["TaskDescription110121101"]="In the Eden Group base on <color=#CA2E0AFF>eastern Saint Darmain</color>, Instructor <color=#CA2E0AFF>Salisbury</color> engaged in an animated discussion with Walsh. The latter spotted you and, from the looks of it, he got a tough task that <color=#CA2E0AFF>required your service</color> again...",
    ["TaskDescription110121102"]="You learned that Walsh has made a significant discovery that could rewrite the history as we know it. Most current scholars believed that the cave of Comodo was formed by a great cold wave a thousand years back, but Walsh noticed the traits of magma rocks in the samples from the chasm. So, could any wave be cold enough to encase the entire network in ice? As you ponder that, Walsh invited you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color> as he has more clues to show you.",
    ["TaskDescription110121103"]="Walsh took you to check the sample from the surface of Ice Vein and you felt strong magical energy from it. He also told you most fossils in the Ice Vein itself contained the same trace of energy, as well. He invited you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color> farther for more shocking revelations.",
    ["TaskDescription110121104"]="You and Walsh entered the part where the remnants of the Ancient Dragon lay. You observed that not only do the bones give off unknown magic, but they have streaky scars as if washed in water. Because they don't have anyone versed in magic, the Eden Group could not look further into it. You, however, believed you can get help from Jesqurienne, head of the Mage Guild. But to disassemble the skeleton for samples, you must first collect the <color=#CA2E0AFF>sour berries</color> favored by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Megalith</color>, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>venomous spit</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gargoyles</color> to make the fumigant for preserving relics.",
    ["TaskDescription110121105"]="You gathered everything needed to make the fumigant. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>you can give the materials to Walsh</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110121106"]="Walsh used the components you gathered to make the fumigant with a protective film, so you can safely disassemble the skeleton and bring the samples to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower</color> for analysis. Walsh informed you he would wait for you in the Eden Group base with Salisbury.",
    ["TaskDescription110121107"]="With Jesqurienne's help, you learned that the magic leaving such scars on the bone fragment is the Aurora magic invented by Nithil Heines. But as far as Jesqurienne knew, Nithil had never visited Comodo in person. She suggested that you see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika</color> the Great Sage, who would know more about the Heine family's past as a descendant.",
    ["TaskDescription110121108"]="In the sage's cabin, you perused the diary written by Nithil when he lived there, and it hinted at a secret between him and Margaret. That necessitated a return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo</color> to seek an answer from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alexia</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110121109"]="Alexia agreed to help you, but she disclosed that all of Margaret's correspondence had been sealed in the side chambers of her tomb. She would have them retrieved and placed inside the main hall. For now, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Eden Group</color> and inform them, then convene at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tomb in eastern Saint Darmain</color>. Before you left, you heard her talking to a guard...",
    ["TaskDescription110121110"]="You and friends from Eden Group arrived at Margaret's tomb, but the absentminded Walsh forgot to bring your share of the gladiolus fluid that you must smear on your hands or the oil and sweat would cause irreversible damage to the documents. When you finally get back in the crypt, Salisbury and Walsh already found <color=#CA2E0AFF>the letters Nithil sent to Margaret</color>. You <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> them together as the truth from a millennium ago unfolded before your eyes...",
    ["TaskDescription110122101"]="Even though the adventure on the Comodo has ended, you can't help but keep thinking about the <color=#CA2E0AFF>crown</color> discovered among the pirates. Your gut feeling tells you this might be related to the missing king, Tristan III. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>report this to Bohr</color> once you return to Prontera...",
    ["TaskDescription110122102"]="After meeting up with Bohr, you report the things about the crown to him, and soon after, he decides to deploy someone to go to the lone island you were talking about to search for the king. At the same time, Bohr states he has something that requires your help. He wants you to read a pile of anonymous letters that clearly logged the assassination event of the princes, Aronst and Azer Alm. You can tell right off the bat <color=#CA2E0AFF>Margaret</color> wrote this letter. So, Bohr wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet</color> with this royal exorcist to learn more about the assassination...",
    ["TaskDescription110122103"]="Margaret admits that she wrote the anonymous letter and then tells you everything about the assassination. During the conversation, it appears that she unintentionally implies that Parni suspects the Walter family is plotting a coup, which is similar to Bohr's thinking. Bohr then wants you to take him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni</color>, who resides there...",
    ["TaskDescription110122104"]="You and Bohr come across Parni in Glast Heim, but she is in the middle of treating the patient and doesn't have time to be bothered. After hearing Bohr's intention, Parni tells you that if you want the answer, you must save her patient first. To this end, you need to obtain the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spirit Quelling Seal</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Majoruros</color> and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune of Coagulation</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carat</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110122105"]="You have all the materials for Parni's emergency treatment. She can now talk about the Walter family with you.",
    ["TaskDescription110122106"]="You recognize the patient Parni was treating was Helena and Abu, the wife and son of the servant, Oman. After witnessing Oman being murdered, Parni gave Helena her contact just in case. As expected, Parni received a help message from Helena not long after, and she rushed to her just to find out the mother and son were severely injured and in coma. Bohr asks Parni why she didn't report this incident to the Defense Force earlier. While speaking, it seems like the mother and son's condition is getting worse. Parni wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get the fountain water from Quiet Garden</color> so that she can treat them again...",
    ["TaskDescription110122107"]="What surprises you is that Parni uses the fountain water as an excuse to drive you away to see how Bohr reacts. This is why she buries her suspicions about the Walter family deep inside her heart. Before confirming Bohr's attitude, she can't disclose her thoughts to the two of you. Now she sees that Bohr didn't do any harm to Helena and Abu during your absence, which proves that Bohr isn't with the Walter family. She keeps going and tells you that after saving the mother and son, she entrusted her <color=#CA2E0AFF>childhood friend</color> to keep track of the assassin, and she received a message from her friend not a while ago that the fleeing assassin got caught by the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110122108"]="It surprises you that Parni's childhood friend turns out to be Seyren, who you met before a couple of times. Meanwhile, Randel, who got arrested by Seyren as a Shadow Hunter, has now become one of the chivalry. They found the assassin who harmed Helena and her son but failed to make him split any useful intel. To get him to speak, Seyren pulls out a piece of paper given by Margaret, and supposedly there is the formula for crafting the Truth Potion. You need to follow the formula and find Confusion Grass, Shimmering Algae Bulbs, and Bone Dust as soon as possible...",
    ["TaskDescription110122109"]="Time is running out! Once you finish collecting the materials to craft the Truth Potion, return to and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give them to Seyren</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription110122110"]="Under the influence of Truth Potion, the assassin finally starts to talk about his background and intention. He has a strong and complicated relationship with a certain servant in the Walter family, who gives out the order to hunt down Helena and her son. But is a testimony like this enough to convict the Walter family? You doubt it. Anyway, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>report this information</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bohr and Parni</color> immediately...",
    ["TaskDescription110123101"]="As time passes, the new king's election is about to kick off. After parting with Parni in Glast Heim, you follow Bohr's instruction to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>court clerk, Lyanna</color>, in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110123102"]="Upon hearing Lyanna's influential illustration, you realize that you have a huge role to play in the election of the new king. Your vote will significantly impact the outcome of this election. But you have no idea what to do at this point. Lyanna can tell you are confused and suggest you go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Cathedral</color> to join a political speech. All the candidates will be there and pull for their votes, and this may be a great opportunity to get to know them...",
    ["TaskDescription110123103"]="Before the speech, Bidal, Halmod, and Jurgen share their vision for the future kingdom with you, giving you a better understanding of them. At this time, you notice a <color=#CA2E0AFF>familiar figure</color> walking by...",
    ["TaskDescription110123104"]="This optimistic speech is interrupted unexpectedly when Prince Aronst's personal attendant, Moffit, breaks a piece of bad news to everybody that the prince was attacked by a black-clothed stranger and is in a coma now. To investigate the truth, you and Moffit <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the crime scene</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>search</color> for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>clues</color> left behind...",
    ["TaskDescription110123105"]="After briefly investigating the scene where Prince Aronst was attacked, here comes Bohr. He invites a doctor to treat Aronst and questions <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moffit</color> in detail about the entire story of the incident...",
    ["TaskDescription110123106"]="Bohr seems to have an idea about the real identity of the culprit, and the diagnosis of Prince Aronst is finished by now. In order to wake the prince up, you need to gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatic Blood</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Condor Leg Bone</color> and help the doctor to craft a bottle of Sober Potion...",
    ["TaskDescription110123107"]="After Prince Aronst takes the potion, Dante tells you and Bohr that even the prince looks fine right now, but the weird medicine the stranger gave him poses a threat to his safety. At this point, Dr. Dante cannot identify the effect of this medicine, but it surely serves some purpose since the stranger made all the effort just to feed the prince a bottle of medicine. He suggests you all prepare in advance to avoid any irreversible outcome. For this reason, you carry the lost glass bottle from the scene and set off to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Library</color>, hoping the alchemist <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lawrence</color> can help you to identify the liquid that remains in the bottle.",
    ["TaskDescription110123108"]="Before identifying the liquid, Lawrence wants you to get him the Sea Breeze Vine, Phosphorus Soil, and Rocker Wing. Find them as soon as possible and <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand them over to Lawrence</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110123109"]="It seems like Lawrence already has an idea of what is in the glass bottle. Somehow, he hesitates to inform you directly but returns a lab report along with the glass bottle to you, urging you to go to the academy and seek help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110123110"]="You comply with Lawrence's suggestion and take the lab report and the glass bottle to pay Dean Mainz a visit. The serious look on the Mainz's face makes you realize this could be a severer matter. Under his guidance, you arrive at the library and start to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> an ancient <color=#CA2E0AFF>black leather-bound book</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110123111"]="According to Dean Mainz, the liquid remaining in the bottle could be an extremely toxic substance, and the intoxicated target will die after seven days of taking it if there is no antidote. What makes it even worse is that antidote crafting is rather complicated since it changes according to the poison maker's habit. There is no way to craft an antidote without being entirely sure about the original formula. Now, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver this information to Bohr and Aronst</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110123112"]="After knowing Aronst has taken a poison that only spares him to live another seven days, Bohr becomes enraged and had enough of the Walter family for what they have done. He assembles the Defense Force that goes by his name to arrest Azer. Meanwhile, Aronst, who's the victim, opposes this idea fiercely, even if it costs his life...",
    ["TaskDescription110123113"]="It surprises you that Aronst eventually convinces Bohr. Just like how you never imagined the previous king's descendant would say the same thing as the old king ever since he vanished. It seems like Aronst's speech has ignited something deep inside your heart. Maybe it's time to visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>court clerk, Lyanna</color>, again and tell her your decision...",
    ["TaskDescription110124101"]="We are only two days away from the Bloodline Banquet, and you can already smell the tension in the air. This morning, a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Defense Force Soldier</color> who guards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>south gate</color> breaks a piece of bad news to you that ruins the day...",
    ["TaskDescription110124102"]="The young Defense Force Soldier seems to get into trouble and needs help finding Bohr. In despair, you bite the bullet and follow him to the ruins at the south gate, saving an elder from a group of scavengers. The Defense Force Soldier tells you that this elder has discovered many human remains in the area nearby, and he wanted to report to Bohr but couldn't find him. With your suggestion, you two decide to use <color=#CA2E0AFF>water to clean up the body remains</color> to see if there are any useful clues.",
    ["TaskDescription110124103"]="When you examine the remains closely, you discover some nametags made of special materials. The Defense Force Soldier tells you he has seen the same kind of nametags on the servants responsible for arranging the Bloodline Banquet. To further confirm these remains' identity, you decide to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palace Head Steward</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110124104"]="Astonished by the fact that the Palace Head Steward has no clues about these servants' deaths, you remain speechless. He even informs you that the resources needed for the Bloodline Banquet should be arranged by the servants in Prontera's shopping street right now. He appreciates your finding these nametags since they are the only pass to enter the palace. Without them, these servants will sleep on the street. The whole thing seems highly suspicious, and you plan to <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate these servants secretly</color> by returning their nametags in person. The soldier, at the same time, takes advantage of this opportunity to confirm Bohr's location. The two of you decide to split up and meet up later at the nearby tavern.",
    ["TaskDescription110124105"]="Near the Central Fountain, you encounter a group of servants who seem bothered by the banquet's resources. Overhearing one of them saying that the resource list was changed on short notice, and some of the items on it are ridiculous. To complete their task, they turn to you for help and want you to gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stiff Front Tooth</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lunatic</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sharp Beak</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Condor</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Colored Silk</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fabre</color>, then <color=#CA2E0AFF>hand them over as soon as possible</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110124106"]="You rush to the other end of the shopping street after done gathering all the resources. There is another group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>banquet servants</color> over there...",
    ["TaskDescription110124107"]="Somehow the banquet servants here are also in trouble, and they have been arguing over the design of the Banquet Invitation forever. To agree to disagree and just get it over with, they want you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of the palace, Odin's Statue, and Central Fountain</color>. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Show them the pictures</color> when you are done so they can vote on which one to use as the invitation's background.",
    ["TaskDescription110124108"]="After you are done investigating this group of servants, the Defense Force Soldier arrives here just in time for the meet-up. He tells you that Bohr is now on the way to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>barrack of the Royal Chivalry</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up with a knight named Dardano</color>. He wants you to report everything that happened today to Bohr, and he will carry on the duty of watching these weird servants...",
    ["TaskDescription110124109"]="Arriving at the barrack of the Royal Chivalry, you happen to see Bohr arguing with Dardano. Their argument is interrupted by your arrival, and Bohr decides to leave the scene and warns you to watch out for Dardano and the Royal Chivalry. The reason is that Royal Chivalry refuses to follow the deployment order from the princess and doesn't allow the knights to join the Guardian Troop that suppose to protect the capital city during the Bloodline Banquet. Under Bohr's suggestion, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>check</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>deployment list</color> of the Royal Chivalry and realize this is not something trivial...",
    ["TaskDescription110124110"]="The Royal Chivalry's attitude toward the deployment order and the weird situation of those banquet servants, Bohr has now concluded that someone is manipulating the Bloodline Banquet, shuffling the core member of the event and replacing them with their own staff. To gain further information, Bohr plans to <color=#CA2E0AFF>tail</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knights</color> who are gathering at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110124111"]="What the knights said in the conversation validates and strengthens the assumption of your and Bohr's. However, something unexpected occurs when the two of you are about to leave...",
    ["TaskDescription110125101"]="About the investigation of mysterious runes on the wellhead, ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color> about the updates!",
    ["TaskDescription110125102"]="Andre tells you about the promise he made, which allows you to investigate Ymir's power inside the well of Kiel Khayr's Estate, as well as the mysterious runes on the wellhead. Now the case is taken over by Michelle Lyra, the Intelligence Chief of the Guards. However, this Michelle takes a hard line, disallowing you to enter the estate. Andre reminds you, that if you are eager to get to the bottom of this, you can go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sage Plaza</color> and look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Alena</color>, who has in-depth knowledge on this topic.",
    ["TaskDescription110125103"]="You show the mysterious photos to Professor Alena. And from the look on her face, you know she is the one you need...",
    ["TaskDescription110125104"]="Alena tells you, this kind of text has a different origin than any other existing languages on the continent. Comparing the similarity of its grammar and morphology to other languages, it should be something from another civilization that has no connection to those on the continent. When asked about the meaning of the runes, Alena looks confused. She recommends you ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Valcone</color>, who is copying the patterns on the stone pillar on Sage Plaza at this moment...",
    ["TaskDescription110125105"]="After a moment of decipherment, Professor Valcone tells you, that the runes contain words such as \"passage\" and \"seal.\" Furthermore, although some adjacent runes in the photo are still hard to tell, they are identical to what he has seen somewhere else in Juno. If you are interested, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>explore with him</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110125106"]="The two of you compare the photos to the mysterious runes on the wellhead inside Kiel Khayr's Estate, and find out there is an identical series of conterminous strings in every photo. Apparently, this string means something, a word maybe, or something that belongs to a mysterious foreign civilization. If you want to learn more about this, it's a good idea to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Professor Laurent</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110125107"]="In the El Mes Gorge, Professor Laurent has a serious conflict with the members of the Eden Group. Luckily, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Philodis</color> shows up just in time, preventing the situation from getting worse. Turns out he's here for you.",
    ["TaskDescription110125108"]="On behalf of Lord Carl, Philodis invites you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord's Mansion</color>. You two then arrive at the heavily-guarded Lord's Mansion, passing through armed Rekenber Guards. Now, the door to the Lord's office is open for you...",
    ["TaskDescription110125109"]="In his formal outfit, the Lord is expecting your arrival inside the office. Maybe you will learn part of the truth after the <color=#CA2E0AFF>conversation with Lord Carl</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110125110"]="After learning the process of you sensing the Ymir's power, the Lord states that he knows fearsomely little about occultism. But since you have somehow arrived at a solid conclusion, and also are an important partner invited to assist in this secret operation, you are granted the right to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check the confidential archive inside the clock...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110126101"]="While dealing with the android riot, you finally get yourself some leisure time. However, not long after, you receive a message from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Andre</color>. He seems to have something quite important that requires your help. To meet him, or not to meet, that is the question...",
    ["TaskDescription110126102"]="To cope with frequent harassment of the rioting androids, the guards have deployed too many people in town, trying to maintain law and order. As a result, they have no manpower to spare anymore. And to make matters worse, Andre receives a message from <color=#CA2E0AFF>St. Caviderina Welfare Center</color>, stating that a kid went missing for no reason and no further details are available right now. With no other choice, he has to ask you to investigate this matter on his behalf, and deliver the <color=#CA2E0AFF>government-issued welfare support funds</color>, along with the books and fruits he prepared, to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Director</color> of the welfare center. In addition to his request, he also brings good news: Your temporary residence permit has been approved! Go check out your new place when everything is settled!",
    ["TaskDescription110126103"]="Following Andre's instruction, you have arrived at St. Caviderina Welfare Center, located on the east side of Kiel Khayr's Academy. The director seems to be expecting you for a while. Strangely, however, little does he care about the missing kid that he eagerly asks you for welfare support funds. During the conversation, not only does he deflect any responsibility for the child's disappearance, but he also shows astounding indifference to the children. To get to the bottom of this, you decide to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Auntie Cook</color>, who the director says is responsible for the children's daily accommodations, hoping to get some useful information.",
    ["TaskDescription110126104"]="Busy preparing dinner for the children, Auntie Cook has no time to answer your questions. Yet despite her short temper, she is trying her best to provide meals for all these kids. According to her, all the resources in the welfare center are monopolized by the greedy director. These poor kids can only live off some spoiled food or even remain starving throughout the day. To earn her trust, you volunteer to gather cooking ingredients for her. She is asking you to get her three following ingredients: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rotten Tree Root</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crude Engine Oil</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fireflowing Core</color>. Please find these items as soon as possible and hand them to her.",
    ["TaskDescription110126105"]="Even though you managed to find everything she asked for, you still wonder if these can be cooked into dishes. On this question, Auntie Cook gives you her answer: either to eat or to die. No one has a third choice here. When you ask her about Martistine, she claims that the last time she saw her, Martistine seemed to be arguing with <color=#CA2E0AFF>some other kids in front of the sandpit</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110126106"]="Standing in front of the sandpit, you see the kids playing house with sand. They invite you to join them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>make a \"pizza\" together</color>, and you are down for it...",
    ["TaskDescription110126107"]="To your surprise, these kids plan to make a \"sand pizza\" just to kill their hunger. And based on what they have said, they are not doing this for the first time. Out of compassion, you take out the <color=#CA2E0AFF>fruits</color> Andre prepared and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give them to the kids</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110126108"]="After having the fruits, the kids expressed their gratitude to you, and you took the chance to ask them about Martistine. During the conversation, you find out they are not isolating Martistine out of loathing. They are just mimicking adults' behaviors. And according to the kids, they all hope Martistine can leave this place for good, especially that bossy child named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Logan</color>, who always picks fights with her.",
    ["TaskDescription110126109"]="Inside the welfare center, you found a group of children near the rocking chair, surrounded by some random monsters. After defeating the monsters, however, an arrogant little boy scolds you for being nosy. Turns out he is Logan, the bossy child that always picks fights with Martistine. At first, you intend to dissuade him from bullying the weak, but to your surprise, he has the guts to threaten you. So you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>teach him a lesson</color> about how to be a nice little boy.",
    ["TaskDescription110126110"]="Under your forceful, intimidating \"persuasion,\" Logan reluctantly takes your advice and accepts the books Andre prepared, promising that he will read the books seriously. Besides, he also tells you that this morning, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ms. Petra</color>, their teacher, scolded Martistine, and the latter has gone missing ever since. Looks like you need to find this teacher and <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a good chat with her</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110127101"]="After the investigation at St. Caviderina Welfare Center is concluded, you realize this child, Martistine, harbors many unsolved mysteries. To get to the bottom of this, you come to the woods outside the welfare center, looking for the whereabouts of Martistine...",
    ["TaskDescription110127102"]="After talking to a local hunter, you arrive at the woods north of the welfare center. There are indeed some strange footprints left here. Following the trail of footprints, you head deep into the woods, but to your surprise, the trail leads you all the way back to the walls of the Welfare Center. At this moment, you hear voices coming from the other side. It is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Logan</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110127103"]="It appears Martistine has quite a habit of bunking off. With the help of the two robots she has, she can easily climb over the outer walls of the welfare center. Not only that, she also promises Logan various incentives, enticing him to be a lookout for her. According to Logan, Martistine always brought back \"things from the sky.\" If you follow the road to Juno and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look west</color>, you may find her trails.",
    ["TaskDescription110127104"]="On a desolate hillside, a lone robot sitting at the roadside catches your attention, then you hear a little girl's faint cries coming from nearby. After trying to talk with it, you confirm this is Martistine's robot, through which she is talking to you. The girl is quite cautious, but she's craving the birthday dishes her mother made. So she wants you to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Algae</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goat's Glands</color>, and use these ingredients to make some oven-baked dish...",
    ["TaskDescription110127105"]="You deliver the collected ingredients, Algae and Goat's Glands, to Auntie Cook and ask her to prepare a dish. Auntie Cook warns you the dish is dangerous since its smell attracts monsters. You assure her that you are aware of this and everything is going to be okay. And to expedite the cooking progress, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>assist</color> Auntie Cook...",
    ["TaskDescription110127106"]="After getting the dish Martistine wanted, you take the chance to ask Auntie Cook about the welfare center's adoption procedure. However, she tells you that she has never seen any kid being adopted from here. Even if there were an ongoing adoption, the rapacious director would find a way to squeeze the last drop of wealth from the applicants. But if the kids run away by themselves, it will become another story. You can tell what she's implying: there's no need to ask for the director's permission if you want to take the kids away. After extending your gratitude, you take the dish and <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the hillside where the robot stays.</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110127107"]="Before handing out the dish to Martistine, you were already aware that it was a trap she had set up. Even though you tried to reason with her, it seems your efforts were in vain. On the good side, however, the monsters attracted by the dish were no match for you. Seeing you easily break free from them, Martistine had no choice but to flee the scene. Yet she underestimated the effect of the dish, perhaps. A rampant monster caught up with her. In such a dire situation, you came to her rescue and saved her life. Now, even though you are mad about her capricious acts, it's more important to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check if she's injured</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110127108"]="The injured Martistine is getting emotional. During the conversion, you discover that she suffers from dissociative identity disorder, a rare disorder that allows her to have multiple personalities at the same time. While Martistine is stubborn and capricious, she seems helpless to fend off the other her. In the end, you manage to console Martistine and tell her that you won't bring her back to the welfare center. Instead, she and you will share a new home in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110128101"]="During your adventure in Einbroch, you bump into your old friend <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goldie</color> and her dispatch team...",
    ["TaskDescription110128102"]="Seeing each other, Goldie complains about her team and mentions that at this pace, they might never reach Lighthalzen. And now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenlur</color> is missing...",
    ["TaskDescription110128103"]="During your search for Zenlur, you come across Orfeo and Trinity. Though they don't want to see Zenlur again, after your help, they tell you where <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenlur and Celia</color> are heading...",
    ["TaskDescription110128104"]="Near the river, Celia, who is gathering materials for Zenlur's Super Healing Pill, tells you that Zenlur and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivy</color> should have returned to the camp already. And indeed, you hear familiar voices when you get there...",
    ["TaskDescription110128105"]="Ivy at the camp says if you want to know Zenlur's whereabouts, you'll have to finish his quest—<color=#CA2E0AFF>Catch the Metaling</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110128106"]="One after another, you finally finish Ivy's quest. He smugly informs you that Zenlur has been sold to Milian's <color=#CA2E0AFF>private clinic</color> and is probably undergoing illegal cyborg modification and organ removal.",
    ["TaskDescription110128107"]="You rush to Milian's private clinic and save Zenlur just in time. During your confrontation with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Milian</color>, you both decide to sort everything out first...",
    ["TaskDescription110128108"]="It turns out Ivy is the one behind Zenlur's disappearance. You decide to bring Zenlur with you and settle things with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivy</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110128109"]="After taking care of the Alchemist's Homunculus standing before Ivy, you're about to deal with its owner when <color=#CA2E0AFF>Celia</color> rushes in, mentioning something went wrong with Zenlur...",
    ["TaskDescription110128110"]="By the river, you find Zenlur unconscious. After taking Celia's Super Healing Pill, he started showing weird symptoms. Following Orfeo's emergency plan, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>hurry back</color> with the supplies.",
    ["TaskDescription110128111"]="Zenlur eventually wakes up, but weirdly, he starts passionately confessing his love for Ivy. Seeing the situation, Orfeo signals you to follow him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>steer clear of the chaos</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110129101"]="The area around the marketplace is buzzing with excitement—it seems like a big tour is coming up...",
    ["TaskDescription110129102"]="A friendly staff member hands you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>flyer</color>, and it turns out Orfeo and Trinity are performing in Rachel!",
    ["TaskDescription110129103"]="Malam suggests you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the archives in the Temple to gather performance materials</color> before catching up with your friends.",
    ["TaskDescription110129104"]="After reading the Pope's Hymn, you seek out Wolmas, the Archbishop in Prontera, for more information on the first Pope, St. Isumia. Shockingly, what he tells you contradicts the official records. To find the truth, you decide to return to Arunafeltz...",
    ["TaskDescription110129105"]="Just as you arrive, the performance is called off. You overhear Malam and Syphus having a heated exchange—better <color=#CA2E0AFF>go after Syphus</color> and find out what's happening.",
    ["TaskDescription110129106"]="Pressing him for answers, Syphus finally cracks—Orfeo, Trinity, and the others are missing. Rachel was the last place mentioned in their messages. Syphus hands you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> to back up his claim.",
    ["TaskDescription110129107"]="Determined to uncover the truth, you both head for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>inn</color>mentioned in the letter...",
    ["TaskDescription110129108"]="The innkeeper and his staff recall that before disappearing, the team split up to visit three locations: the Underground Arena, the Temple, and the Holy Spring. That night, a child abduction occurred—but Orfeo and Trinity managed to save the child. The right amount of gold convinces the innkeeper to send his assistant along to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>child</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110129109"]="Aisha, now safe, shares what she saw—Orfeo and Trinity went after the kidnappers, heading straight for the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underground Arena</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110129110"]="After taking down the bouncers guarding the Underground Arena, you learn that the missing dispatch team may no longer be in Rachel. The arena is definitely involved. To avoid tipping them off, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to the inn</color> and sort through the clues.",
    ["TaskDescription110129111"]="You make it back to the inn and find Syphus, who has already checked in. The innkeeper now remembers that a masked stranger stayed right next to Goldie that night, and they both left town the next day. He suggests asking the gate guards, but first, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>talk with Syphus</color> about what you've learned...",
    ["TaskDescription110129112"]="Syphus is handling the arena case, so he advises you to be wary of the Rekenber guards stationed at the Rachel Plains. The gate guard hasn't seen Goldie or the masked stranger but does recall a girl who looked like Goldie heading east of Rachel toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lighthalzen</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110129113"]="You track Goldie's path all the way to the road to Lighthalzen, where Rekenber troops are keeping a tight watch. Amid the tension, you notice a dagger and distress marker—Goldie's last message. Better <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up with Syphus</color> before charging ahead.",
    ["TaskDescription110130101"]="While wandering the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel Plains</color>, an overly excited Eden Group member forces a request onto you...",
    ["TaskDescription110130102"]="After giving a solid beatdown to an Eden Group member named Curtis, he finally comes to his senses—he insists you join his team! As proof this trip won't be a waste, he pulls out a <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious photo</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110130103"]="Curtis beams with excitement, revealing that the woman in the photo is St. Isumia, the first Pope of Arunafeltz. But her armor was crafted in Glast Heim. If you want to know why, he insists you go with him to meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockley in Glast Heim</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110130104"]="Rockley acknowledges Curtis might be onto something, but war has wiped out history. If you really want answers, you'll need to consult <color=#CA2E0AFF>Macy the Medium</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110130105"]="Macy barely glances at the photo before gasping—there's an overwhelming amount of emotions locked inside. But these spirits are too ancient for regular summoning. If she's going to reach them, she'll need some <color=#CA2E0AFF>ingredients</color> to craft a Dream Potion.",
    ["TaskDescription110130106"]="You drink the Dream Potion... and suddenly, you hear a call from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim St. Abbey</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110130107"]="At Glast Heim St. Abbey, you finally spot a spirit murmuring the name Isumia. But... that's all he does. Curtis figures he's scared of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Raydric Archer</color> nearby and suggests clearing out the monsters first.",
    ["TaskDescription110130108"]="With the Raydric Archer dealt with, the spirit should've reacted... but nothing. That is until Curtis presents the photo. A deep, almost obsessive admiration for the pope floods the spirit's expression. But when asked about their relationship... something unsettling shifts in the spirit's aura...",
    ["TaskDescription110130109"]="The ritual abruptly stops, and Macy storms in, asking what the two of you do. The moment Macy finds out what Curtis did, she's furious, saying that he clearly doesn't respect the dead—so don't even talk about seeking the truth. Curtis stands his ground, determined to share what he knows—historical facts and all. He's so serious about this and willing to risk being exiled from the Eden Group. He even reveals secrets that only grave robbers should know. Macy stays silent for a long moment, then decides to give you two another chance...",
    ["TaskDescription110130110"]="Silvio appears, and before he vanishes completely, you manage to glimpse a piece of the truth. But just as you're about to leave Glast Heim St. Abbey... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockley</color> is standing there, waiting.",
    ["TaskDescription110131101"]="As you stroll through Rachel, you unexpectedly bump into a couple of familiar faces from Juno—the journalist duo, Enchulo & Shana.",
    ["TaskDescription110131102"]="Enchulo, brimming with excitement, tells you that he and Shana are set on writing a prize-winning article for the Mobel Journalism Award during the Dawn Moon Festival. Their target is the \"Iron-Blooded Priest,\" Yus Amar. To back up his decision, he even digs up the only interview Yus Amar ever gave—fifteen years ago—and invites you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>check it out</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110131103"]="Once you finish the interview, you gently point out a major flaw in Enchulo's plan—Yus Amar isn't even in Arunafeltz anymore. Looking completely defeated, Enchulo sighed and changed his focus, asking you to help gather information on the changes that took place during Yus Amar's leadership.",
    ["TaskDescription110131104"]="Following the clues from the interview, you head to Grey Wolf Village, a community of nomadic descendants just outside the city. A sickly old man, one of the few still living there, tells you that the villagers have moved elsewhere for work—and the riverbed that once provided raw stones has run completely dry...",
    ["TaskDescription110131105"]="You take a picture of the dried-up riverbed and decide to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Malam</color> about the raw stones once collected by the villagers. Maybe you'll find some useful leads.",
    ["TaskDescription110131106"]="Hearing you bring up Grey Wolf Village, Malam gives you a word of caution—showing too much sympathy for nomads in public isn't wise. But, ever the opportunist, he assumes you are gathering material for an article and offers to take you to a <color=#CA2E0AFF>meeting</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110131107"]="Hiding in the shadows, you overhear the Priests locked in a heated argument—debating everything from taxes to Yus Amar to what should be done with the nomads. This isn't the right moment to reveal yourself. Maybe it's best to just <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110131108"]="With the Priests gone, Malam signals for you to step out. He has another tip—why not head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rekenber's airship station outside the city</color>? They've been raking in profits from trade between Arunafeltz and the Republic.",
    ["TaskDescription110131109"]="You manage to capture a clear shot of an airship bearing the Rekenber emblem. Now's the time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>report back to Enchulo</color> and share your findings.",
    ["TaskDescription110131110"]="Piecing together the clues from the photos, you realize that your findings completely contradict the original interview...",
    ["TaskDescription110132101"]="When you find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parni</color>, she's happily busy with her work. You hesitate, unsure how to tell her about <color=#CA2E0AFF>that incident</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110132102"]="Parni's emotions flare up, so you decide to help calm her down by gathering the scattered photos first...",
    ["TaskDescription110132103"]="While picking up the photos, you notice <color=#CA2E0AFF>strange fluctuations</color> near the photo and think about checking it out...",
    ["TaskDescription110132104"]="You actually run into young Parni and Margaret! It's shocking—but what they're talking about surprises you even more...",
    ["TaskDescription110132105"]="After clearing up their feelings for each other, Parni asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather fresh flowers</color> to make a bouquet...",
    ["TaskDescription110132106"]="Now that Margaret has opened her heart, Parni asks you to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> to help set the plan in motion...",
    ["TaskDescription110132107"]="Young Seyren looks just like you remember. You can't help but wonder, can he really pick flowers?",
    ["TaskDescription110132108"]="It's obvious Seyren cares about <color=#CA2E0AFF>Margaret</color>. You already knew that from the future, but still...",
    ["TaskDescription110132109"]="After some twists and turns, the two finally meet. You and Parni are ready to slip away quietly...",
    ["TaskDescription110132110"]="Reality always beats fiction for drama. As Parni screams, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>press the shutter</color>. Yet as all dreams do, this one ends eventually—and time <color=#CA2E0AFF>flows back to its course</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110201101"]="You meet a ghost named Kahn on the Shipwreck, who states that he was once the captain of this ship. Unfortunately, he and his crew were attacked and killed by the Corsair...\nKahn states that although the ghosts have lost their memories, the obsessions while they were alive remain and as long as these subsist, the souls of these people cannot transcend to the afterlife... Complete Kahn's request and help the deceased fulfill their last wishes!",
    ["TaskDescription110201102"]="You first find the spirit of the swordsman Spencer, and with your assistance, he finally achieves his wish to destroy the monster Marina... Go see if there are any other spirits that need your help.",
    ["TaskDescription110201103"]="You find the spirit of the merchant, Forde, and with your assistance, he finally locates the valuable missing goods... Why don't you seek out the other spirits for more information?",
    ["TaskDescription110201104"]="Lastly, you find the spirit of the cook Sousa and help him get a healthy side dish that he wanted try. Now that the obsessions of the spirits have been abated, what will Captain Kahn have to say?",
    ["TaskDescription110202101"]="The ghost of First Mate Hobbe looks very upset.\nThrough speaking with him, you learn that he is saddened by his inability to recall how the shipwreck happened... You were told that Hobbe had recorded everything that had happened after setting sail in a nautical log. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather up the missing log pages</color> for him and piece together the course of events?",
    ["TaskDescription110202102"]="You find the first log page in the cabin.\nReading through it, you learn that Hobbe had suggested to Captain Polk that he change course when they encountered a fog, but the captain insisted on going through it to get his cargo to the port on the other side as quickly as possible...\n<color=#CA2E0AFF>Look for the second log page</color> and find out what happened next!",
    ["TaskDescription110202103"]="According to the second log page, a strange series of events occurred after the ship entered the fog. Hobbe first saw a large ship's shadow approaching rapidly, then he noticed that sailors were going missing one by one. While he was looking for them, he discovered a strange gap in the cabin and witnessed Captain Polk being pulled through to the other side by a huge tentacle...\nHobbe suspected that other sailors had gone missing due to the same reason. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the third log page</color> to learn the whole story!",
    ["TaskDescription110202104"]="From reading the third log page, you learn that Hobbe figured out that the strange gap was a dimensional gap. It was then that he realized he would never be able to find his missing companions or leave the ship...\nNow that all the log pages with records of the sunken ship have been collected, you should go tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hobbe</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110203101"]="You meet a little girl named Annie in Sograt Desert who is frustrated that she can't make Meat n' Pumpkin as delicious as her mother's, most likely because she can't afford to use expensive Large Meat Pieces.\nSeeing Annie's sad face, you decide to help her get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Large Meat Pieces</color> she needs for her dish!",
    ["TaskDescription110203102"]="Annie is very happy to see the Large Meat Pieces you've brought to her! She invites you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>make the Meat n' Pumpkin</color> with her. See if you can make it as unforgettably delicious as her mother's!",
    ["TaskDescription110203103"]="Annie entrusts you to deliver her carefully prepared <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bento</color> to her <color=#CA2E0AFF>father</color>, who is working on <color=#CA2E0AFF>Weinst Street</color>. What will her father say when he sees it?",
    ["TaskDescription110204101"]="It's said that the area around Morroc has been experiencing a surging undercurrent that caused a series of strange happenings recently. To learn more, Master Hassan of the Assassins Guild has sent Assassin <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zhaka</color> to the area to investigate. Why don't you go and find out how the investigation is going?",
    ["TaskDescription110204102"]="You find Zhaka in the middle of conducting the investigation.\nHe tells you that there have been several cases of missing children in Morroc recently and that he had found the family of one of them. However, he couldn't get to speak with the family, as they ran away at the sight of him... At Zhaka's request, you find the young boy Arno. You learn that his sister Allie was kidnapped and that he wants to get help from an adult. However, he asks that you prove your strength before he accepts your help to save his sister...\nDo as Arno says; defeat the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Anacondaqs</color> outside the city and obtain the requested number of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Snake Scales</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110204103"]="After getting the Snake Scales, Arno finally recognizes your strength. He offers to take you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>camp</color> where the kidnappers are. No time to waste. Go defeat the vile kidnappers and rescue Allie!",
    ["TaskDescription110204104"]="The two of you find Allie and learn that the reason for her kidnapping is that someone wants to sacrifice the blood of children to the Demon King Morroc...\nFortunately, you rescue the terrified Allie before they can carry out the horrible act. Tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zhaka</color> the whole story and hear what he has to say.",
    ["TaskDescription110205101"]="You meet Instructor Bowya of the Eden Group in Morroc.\nShe says that her and her team are here to excavate the ancient ruins and learn about its history. Why don't you help her <color=#CA2E0AFF>find her Eden Group team members scattered around the desert</color> and see how everyone's research is going?",
    ["TaskDescription110205102"]="You find an Eden Group member named Omari near a canyon. He is about to fight some thieves blocking the way by himself, but you arrive in time to help take them out, clearing the path to the canyon.\nGo see which other members of the Eden Group need help!",
    ["TaskDescription110205103"]="You find a stumped Eden Group member named Brennan near the Sphinx Cavern and help him solve the sphinx keeper's riddle, enabling him to enter the cave.\nGo see if the other members of the Eden Group are having trouble!",
    ["TaskDescription110205104"]="You find a trembling Eden Group member named Casey in the Pyramid and help her clear out the terrifying Soldier Skeletons hindering her research.\nHow about telling <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bowya</color> about her team members? She'll be ecstatic to learn that they've successfully begun their research of the ruins!",
    ["TaskDescription110206101"]="You meet a distressed Trisse at the Assassins Guild.\nShe tells you that a Drops has been constantly bothering her, and she doesn't know why. The Drops seems determined to follow her around everywhere. Help her ask a <color=#CA2E0AFF>monster researcher</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>city of Morroc</color>. Perhaps she will have a solution for her problem?",
    ["TaskDescription110206102"]="With the help of Monster Researcher Bertha, you learn that the Drops is following Trisse because it wants her help in getting rid of a pack of Phreeonis that are running rampant in the desert.\nPhreeonis are powerful monsters that are not easy to deal with, but Trisse comes up with a great idea. Do what she says and go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eremes</color> to borrow some <color=#CA2E0AFF>poison</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110206103"]="Trisse asks you to get another warm portion of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nutritious Frog Meat</color>. You can't help but wonder what she's planning to do...",
    ["TaskDescription110206104"]="Trisse invites you to go with her to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color> to deal with the Phreeonis. How they bully the weak is unforgivable, so go with her to take them down!",
    ["TaskDescription110206105"]="Thanks to Trisse's plan, the two of you finally get rid of all the evil Phreeonis! Why don't you go tell the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drops</color> the good news?",
    ["TaskDescription110207101"]="You meet Dobbin, a culinary expert, on Byalan Island, and learn that he has just found the recipe for the legendary dish, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Unforgettable Octopus Sashimi</color>.\nTo make this dish, Dobbin needs your help to obtain a premium ingredient, Kraken's Meat. According to Dobbin, cuttlefish type creatures seem easy to lure with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Giant Tiger Prawns</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110207102"]="Dobbin uses the Giant Tiger Prawns you bring back to make <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragrant Bait</color>. Now go place it in <color=#CA2E0AFF>areas of the underwater cave where Krakens often appear</color>. Then wait for the tasty targets to take a bite!",
    ["TaskDescription110207103"]="You finally obtain the premium ingredient, Kraken's Meat. Hurry and bring it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dobbin</color>. What will the culinary expert do after getting it?",
    ["TaskDescription110207104"]="Dobbin is thrilled to see the ingredient you brought back!\nHe is convinced that he will work miracles again with his \"hands that were blessed by the food gods.\" In that case, why don't you go watch him work his magic?",
    ["TaskDescription110208101"]="Not far from Dobbin, you meet a girl named Perini.\nShe tells you that she is planning to make the legendary dish Heartbreak Shrimp for Dobbin and that she needs King Dramoh's Meat..\nIt's said that King Dramohs love to eat <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed</color>. Why don't you utilize this information to help her obtain the premium ingredient?",
    ["TaskDescription110208102"]="Perini uses the Water Weed you bring back to make <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fragrant Bait</color>. Now go place it in <color=#CA2E0AFF>areas where King Dramohs frequently appear</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110208103"]="After a lot of hard work, you finally get your hands on the premium ingredient, King Dramoh's Meat! Why don't you hurry and take it to Perini? She's very confident in her cooking prowess and can't wait to make the legendary dish!",
    ["TaskDescription110208104"]="Perini says she's definitely going use these ingredients to <color=#CA2E0AFF>cook</color> the most irresistible dish... How will this dish made with love turn out?",
    ["TaskDescription110208105"]="Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver Perini's Heartbreak Shrimp to Dobbin</color>! Judging by the confidence she has, it should be delicious, right?",
    ["TaskDescription110209101"]="You run into your old friend Morts in the underwater cave. He looks like he is in a very good mood!\nWhile speaking with him, you learn that he met his soulmate so he's in a state of bliss. However, there is still one thing that he laments... It turns out that his beloved is unable to speak. Therefore, he wants you to ask a <color=#CA2E0AFF>young Acolyte</color> nearby for help.\nSeeing how rare it is for Morts to devote his love to someone, you decide to help him solve this problem!",
    ["TaskDescription110209102"]="You find the Acolyte Abessie, who tells you that getting a person's voice back is not a difficult task.\nAll you need to do is obtain some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Refreshing Crab Paste</color> from the nearby <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vadons</color>, and the problem can be solved!",
    ["TaskDescription110209103"]="Abessie makes a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Voice Potion</color> from the crab paste you bring. It's said that if you <color=#CA2E0AFF>give it to a person who has lost their voice</color>, you'll see instant results!",
    ["TaskDescription110209104"]="Morts excitedly asks you to take the Voice Potion to his lover in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color>. You have a feeling that this won't be as simple as it seems...",
    ["TaskDescription110209105"]="After taking the Voice Potion, the young woman's true form is revealed! It turns out that she is a not human, but an Obeaune named Poya!\nYou discover that Poya traded her voice for human legs because she was afraid of Morts disliking her true form. However, after you tell her about Morts feelings for her, Poya finally summons up the courage to tell the truth and asks you to deliver a heartfelt <color=#CA2E0AFF>love letter</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color> for her!",
    ["TaskDescription110210101"]="You meet Merchant Dinza in the Underwater Temple.\nShe tells you that she just bought the most valuable gem under the sea, an Obeaune's Tear, from a sailor. She is planning to get more Obeaune's Tears from the bottom of the sea to make a fortune!\nTo do so, Dinza needs you to help her get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coarse Shell Powder</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus</color>... Why don't you do what she says and see what this shrewd merchant has planned?",
    ["TaskDescription110210102"]="You help Dinza find the Coarse Shell Powder, but she says it is not enough. She still needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smelly Shrooms</color> that grow on the ocean floor!",
    ["TaskDescription110210103"]="With your help, Dinza finally finishes making the item needed to obtain the Obeaune's Tears: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Liquid Tear Gas</color>!\nDinza asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle this liquid on the Obeaune High Priestess</color>... She believes that the High Priestess' tears are more valuable than a regular Obeaune's.",
    ["TaskDescription110210104"]="You sprinkle Liquid Tear Gas on Leona, but to your surprise, her tears do not turn into Pearls!\nIs this method bogus?\nThere's no time for delay. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell Dinza what</color> happened!",
    ["TaskDescription110210105"]="After learning that using tear gas doesn't get you Obeaune's Tears, Dinza is horrified and asks you to show her gem to Leona immediately.\nWhen you do, Leona doesn't know if she should laugh or be upset. The gem is actually just an ordinary fish eye...\nYou might as well collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gleaming Fish Eyes</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phens</color> before telling Dinza the bad news.",
    ["TaskDescription110211101"]="You meet a young man named Abessie in the underwater cave.\nFrom speaking with him, you learn that he was once saved by a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purple-Haired Swordswoman</color>. Since then he has greatly admired her and even wants to become her companion...\nIt's said that this young woman is now in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>underwater cave</color>. Why don't you let her know of Abessie's wish?",
    ["TaskDescription110211102"]="It turns out that the young woman Abessie is looking for was Ygnizem!\nAfter you convey Abessie's wish to be her partner, Ygnizem appears uncomfortable with the idea... She doesn't seem to think Abessie is strong enough and says that unless Abessie can obtain enough <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fish Bones</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phens</color>, he can't be her partner!",
    ["TaskDescription110211103"]="You tell Abessie what Ygnizem said and help him kill the Phens to obtain the Fish Bones.\nNow hurry and take the spoils of battle <color=#CA2E0AFF>to Ygnizem</color>. How will she respond this time?",
    ["TaskDescription110211104"]="You take the Phen Fish Bones to Ygnizem, but she still looks uncomfortable with the idea.\nShe says she's about to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>slay monsters</color>. If Abessie has the courage to go with her, it might impress her!",
    ["TaskDescription110211105"]="You are surprised to see that Ygnizem was wounded while eradicating the undersea monsters!\nAbessie says that Ygnizem was bitten by the monster Deviace and that the only cure for the poison is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pinnatifida</color>, which is unique to the bottom of the sea... There's no time to lose. Find the Pinnatifida and cure Ygnizem as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription110212101"]="Since Swordswoman Ygnizem heard that Kavaski Icarus is the best of the best amongst the new warriors in Archer Village, she sincerely invites him to join her team, hoping that they can become the strongest adventurers together. However, Kavaski seems to hold a grudge against his master, Sky Euin, for never recognizing his abilities, so he deliberately gives Ygnizem a hard time recruiting him, asking her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain 100 pieces of Willow Bark</color> in one day. Facing such an outrageous demand, Ygnizem desperately needs a helping hand. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon South</color> to assist her!",
    ["TaskDescription110212102"]="Thanks to the combined efforts of you, Abessie, and Ygnizem, the team is able to quickly collect the 100 pieces of Willow Bark. Hurry <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Kavaski</color> and give him <color=#CA2E0AFF>100 pieces of Willow Bark</color> to prove the team's strength!",
    ["TaskDescription110212103"]="Despite the fact that Ygnizem successfully completed Kavaski's demanding task of collecting Willow Bark with your and Abessie's assistance, he still wasn't satisfied and tells her to prove her supposed patience with another senseless task. Apparently, he is upset over Sky Euin's criticism of his impatience and is projecting his inadequacy onto Ygnizem... <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to Payon East and help Ygnizem gather 10 Chrysanthemums</color>, then deliver them to Kavaski.",
    ["TaskDescription110212104"]="You and Abessie finish the task on time and return to Kavaski, but Ygnizem hasn't shown up yet. Abessie is worried that Ygnizem is in danger. Go with him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Ygnizem</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110213101"]="Piles of monster corpses have appeared in Payon West. Since then, fear and rumors have been spreading amongst the people. Sun Euin, the eldest son of Lord Euin, is deeply troubled by this, so he asks you to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon West</color> and help him figure out what's really happening over there.",
    ["TaskDescription110213102"]="There is a boy named Zenlur who is struggling to kill a monster in the Bigfoot area, so you kindly step in to help. However, he thinks that you interfered in his trial and that you are not strong enough to participate. Hurry and help Zenlur <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat 25 Wormtails</color> to prove your strength!",
    ["TaskDescription110213103"]="It turns out that the pile of corpses were monsters killed by the martial artist Zenlur. He slayed them so that he can become a disciple of Master Peerless Jin. Help Zenlur <color=#CA2E0AFF>notify Master Peerless Jin of his trial's completion</color> and see what the master is really like!",
    ["TaskDescription110214101"]="You meet a gloomy-looking goddess in Payon South, who implicitly states that your blood and hers are both inauspicious. She tells you that she can show you the true dark side of the world... <color=#CA2E0AFF>When you're ready, go find her.</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110214102"]="In the illusion the goddess projects for you, you meet a young girl named Sarah Arlene, whose village of Payon is suffering from famine. The goddess says that the famine is only the beginning of this story of despair. If you want to continue exploring the dark side of the world, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Goddess' Illusion</color> once again to check it out.",
    ["TaskDescription110214103"]="You see Sarah and her mother being attacked by an unknown force in the Goddess' Illusion. What shocks you is Sarah's father stating that the messengers were sent by the goddess and that they believe the blood flowing through Sara and her mother's bodies are inauspicious. Then you see her father about to kill Sarah. If you want to see how the story unfolds, you'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>enter the Goddess's Illusion</color> again.",
    ["TaskDescription110215101"]="Instructor Bowya of the Eden Group has taken her group to the Archer Village, hoping to enter the village's caves to explore its famous ancient ruins. But they are prohibited from entering due to the rules of Archer Village. Help Bowya get permission for entry by asking the Archer Guild Master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sky Euin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110215102"]="Sky Euin justifiably rejects you, believing that only an adventurer as strong and trustworthy as you are qualified to enter the Munak Cave. Without other options, Bowya asks you to help her gather research materials. Hurry to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak Cave</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>take pictures of the Forgotten Lake Waterfall, the Yin-Yang Taiji, the Soul Devouring Tree, and the Butsudan</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110215103"]="You explore the Munak Cave and finally collect all the photos Bowya requested. Now go <color=#CA2E0AFF>give her the photos of the Forgotten Lake Waterfall, the Yin-Yang Taiji, the Soul Devouring Tree, and the Butsudan</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110215104"]="After seeing the photos of the cave's ruins, Bowya believes that using only these photos for research isn't enough, so she asks you to go into the Munak Cave again and bring back 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Remains</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Skeletons</color> and 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Runes of Resurrection</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bonguns</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110215105"]="After some fierce fighting, you finally obtain the research materials that Bowya needs. Go and give her the 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Remains</color> and 10 <color=#CA2E0AFF>Runes of Resurrection</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110216101"]="Master Brewer Juke is angry about his three missing jars of osmanthus flower brew. Who has stolen Juke's freshly brewed wine? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Help look for clues to find out who the wine thief is</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110216102"]="After some investigation, you finally find the suspected wine thief, which turns out to be a Yoyo. Now hurry and bring the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yoyo</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juke</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110216103"]="The drunken Juke actually makes out from the screams of the Yoyo that there is a mastermind behind the wine theft. He then threatens the Yoyo to get it take him to the main culprit. To prevent Juke from causing trouble in his drunken stupor, you should <color=#CA2E0AFF>go follow Juke</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110217101"]="In Geffen Tower, you meet Beudie, who looks like he's having some trouble with an unfamiliar girl named Celia. She seems to need to some Poring samples, which she has been pestering Beudie about incessantly. Your arrival gives him a chance to get her off his back, so he asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take Celia to an area where Porings appear</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110217102"]="It turns out that the strange girl is an exchange student from Juno-Schuberz Academy. Celia is collecting Poring samples to study their composition, but she needs a guide to help her find Porings. Therefore, Beudie has entrusted you to take her to the South Gate. She gives you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pink Potion</color> and asks you to sprinkle its contents onto the ground to <color=#CA2E0AFF>attract Porings</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110217103"]="After you help Celia collect enough Poring samples, she brings up a rumor about Angelings appearing nearby and hopes that you can help her find them. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take Celia to check out the area where Angelings appear</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110217104"]="Celia hands you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gold Potion</color> brewed specifically to attract Angelings. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>sprinkle it on the ground</color> to lure Angelings.",
    ["TaskDescription110217105"]="After getting the Angeling samples, Celia once again requests you for help in getting samples from the Poring family. For this last set, she wants to head to Payon to collect Poporing specimens. You couldn't bear to say no to the cute girl, so you agree to assist her once more. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>take Celia to Payon South where Poporings appear</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110218101"]="You meet a little boy in Geffen and learn that he's looking for a lost orange cat. Since he seems to need your assistance, get more details on the situation and help the little boy <color=#CA2E0AFF>find the missing orange cat, Eiffel</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110218102"]="You meet a middle-aged man named Hatch who is being chased by a giant fat orange cat in the Goblin Forest. After you help Hatch pacify it, Hatch tells you he is a member of the Mysterious Monster Research Institute and that he came specifically to tame the cat. To help Hatch shrink the giant orange cat, you need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some Rahem Grass</color> for him.",
    ["TaskDescription110218103"]="You successfully bring the Rahem Grass back to the mage Hatch, who uses it to concoct a magic potion that can shrink the orange cat. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed the Shrinking Potion to the orange cat</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110218104"]="An incredible scene occurs when you feed the Shrinking Potion to the orange cat—it let out a human sound. After some thought, Hatch tells you that the situation is bad if it's really what he thinks it is. Then he asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some Sacred Tree Sap</color> for him.",
    ["TaskDescription110218105"]="You extract enough tree sap from the Sacred Tree and deliver it to Hatch, who uses it to concoct a Restoration Elixir. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>feed the Restoration Elixir to the giant orange cat</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110219101"]="Hollgrehenn the Greatest Blacksmith suddenly calls you to him and tells you that he has forged an extraordinary weapon. He hopes that you can help him prove himself to his idol, Whitesmith Howard. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>listen to what Hollgrehenn needs from you</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110219102"]="It turns out that Hollgrehenn wants you to use his weapon, the Midnight Sun, to slay <color=#CA2E0AFF>20 Flail-wielding Goblins</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>20 Mace-wielding Goblins</color> to prove his forging prowess to his idol, Whitesmith Howard.",
    ["TaskDescription110219103"]="After taking a look at the weapon you handed him, Whitesmith Howard tells you that although it shows a high level of craftsmanship, it is damaged from monster attacks and that only the mage Riedling can repair it. Hurry and <color=#CA2E0AFF>inform Hollgrehenn</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110219104"]="Having heard Howard's advice, Hollgrehenn not only disagrees but also believes that a blacksmith should focus on their forging ability and not rely on those outside the trade. He reforges the weapon and asks you to prove its strength again, this time against <color=#CA2E0AFF>20 Orc Babies</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>20 Orc Warriors</color>. After finishing this task, go and see Howard for a second assessment.",
    ["TaskDescription110219105"]="After you successfully kill the Orc Babies and Orc Warriors, you again present the mighty weapon, the Midnight Sun, to Howard. To your surprise, he requests a duel with you wielding the weapon. Try to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat Howard with the Midnight Sun</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110220101"]="You encounter a group of merchants from Cat Hand Services who are conversing angrily. They seem to have been robbed by Goblins again and are having a heated discussion about expelling the Goblin creatures. One of the merchants tells you that there is an Anti-Goblin Association in Geffen and asks you to go check the progress on their Goblincide research. Hurry to Morroc and <color=#CA2E0AFF>inquire with Lezard, a member of the Anti-Goblin Association</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110220102"]="You hear from Lezard, a member of the Anti-Goblin Association, that potion development has hit a bottleneck. In order to help the Anti-Goblin Association advance in their potion development, you need to help Lezard <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain three different kinds of Goblin Blood</color>. Go to the Goblin Forest to collect them!",
    ["TaskDescription110220103"]="While in the Goblin Forest, you run into Kersace from the Mysterious Monster Research Institute. You learn from him that the Goblins seem to be maintaining the ecological balance of the forest, and that killing Goblins blindly may even threaten the safety of Geffen. When you show Kersace that Goblins are monsters that pose a threat to human beings, Kersace asks you to follow him somewhere to see something. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>catch up with Kersace to check it out</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110220104"]="After Kersace leads you to a slain Goblin with wild poisonous fruits growing around its corpse, you begin to develop a new understanding of the Goblins' place in the balance of life and death. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and give the Goblin Blood to Lezard</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110221101"]="You hear an argument raging outside Kordt Forest. A human man is arguing with a Kobold guard, and the guard's patience is wearing thin. Quickly <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and help the human</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110221102"]="After you help Reyard kill the Kobold guard, he raises his camera and asks you to help him take a picture of him with the orange trees there. Help him out by <color=#CA2E0AFF>taking a picture with his magic camera</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110221103"]="After you take a photo of Reyard with the orange trees, he repeatedly praises your photography skills and tells you that he hopes to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go with you to the Goblin camp</color> to avoid further danger. Your inspiring presence seems to have motivated him.",
    ["TaskDescription110221104"]="As you take another photo of Reyard in front of the pile of Goblin corpses, he asks a new request of you. He says that he wants to take a picture with the Orc Lord, and asks you to escort him to the chief's hut. You can't bring yourself to refuse his request, and so <color=#CA2E0AFF>you take him to the Orc Village</color> to find the Orc Lord.",
    ["TaskDescription110221105"]="As you try to convince Jolak to take the photo, you learn that Reyard has been traveling around the world with this magic camera hoping to fulfill the promise he made to his comatose daughter, Lassia, with these images—a promise to realize her childhood dream. After getting a photo with the Orc Lord, Reyard makes a final request. He asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Geffen's Magic Fountain</color> with him.",
    ["TaskDescription110222101"]="You come across an old woman named Helmor praying fervently before the Goddess Statue in Glast Heim. She tells you that the Goddess has suddenly stopped answering her prayers for protection and aid, and feels she may have caused offense by being impoverished and disrespectful. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Talk to the Goddess Statue</color> and find out what actually happened.",
    ["TaskDescription110222102"]="The Goddess tells you and Helmor that a tribute must be paid to answer Helmor's prayers. In order to put her wish at the front of the Goddess's busy schedule and restore her husband's failing mental faculties, Helmor decides to trade a family heirloom—a bracelet—for a jar of Star Orchid Wine to present as tribute. Take Helmor's bracelet and find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>wine merchant, Akarret</color>, in Glast Heim to exchange it for a jug of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Star Orchid Wine</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110222103"]="At Helmor's request, you obtain the precious Star Orchid Wine for her and offer it to the Goddess Statue. The Goddess finally agrees to prioritize Helmor's request and tells Helmor she can go home to wait for her husband to recover. Helmor thanks you and leaves but you feel something is still amiss and decide to stay and <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigate</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110222104"]="Your investigation turns up monster claw marks next to the Goddess Statue that lead to a nearby bush. You run into the merchant, Vienna Lindra, who tells you she saw everything that happened and thinks the voice of the so-called \"Goddess\" came from the bush. To avoid alerting the culprit, she asks that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for some Stinking Monster Waste</color> to help her with her plan.",
    ["TaskDescription110222105"]="It turns out Vienna Lindra's plan was to make a stink bomb from the waste you found. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Throw the stink bomb into the bush</color> to see what's really going on here!",
    ["TaskDescription110223101"]="You come across the merchants, Dinza and Bairde, in Glast Heim. They seem to be locked in disagreement over the loss of a batch of goods. Compelled by Dinza's rage, you are forced to join in the search for the culprits. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>check out</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>suspicious footprints</color> nearby!",
    ["TaskDescription110223102"]="You follow Bairde to investigate the suspicious footprints. Bairde realizes most of the footprints were left by Dinza when she was moving the cargo, but there appears to be a line of footprints with orange-red liquid that are of a different size than the rest. Bairde suspects these tracks belong to the thief. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>suspicious footprints</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110223103"]="You and Bairde follow the suspicious orange-red footprints to a place where the beggars of Glast Heim gather. However, Bairde thinks something is suspicious about the shape and depth of the footprints, and asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back and inform Dinza of the situation first</color>. He will stay behind to investigate further.",
    ["TaskDescription110223104"]="When you tell Dinza that the footprints lead to where the beggars dwell, she angrily insists that you arrest them all immediately. However, when you return to Bairde and the beggars, you can clearly see that the beggars are so hungry that they can barely answer Bairde's questions. Bairde asks you to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>make some Fish Soup with Frog Legs</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110223105"]="Once you help the beggars recover their strength, Bairde points out something peculiar. If the beggars really had stolen the food, why would they still be so weak and hungry? He also only found footprints leading from the cargo area to this place but none leading to the cargo area. It seems something very strange is going on. You carefully inspect the tracks and discover children's footprints in the clearing where the beggars gather. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Follow Bairde</color> quickly and uncover the hidden truth!",
    ["TaskDescription110224101"]="In the center of Glast Heim, you come across a young man mumbling to himself. He seems to be troubled by an unspeakable secret. You decide to talk to him and try to help him out.",
    ["TaskDescription110224102"]="The strange young man is Hylas and he's troubled by the appearance of heretics in Glast Heim. According to Hylas, a witch doctor named Patrick IV appeared in the city one day and claimed to be a Spirit Emissary. He has been profiting from his followers in the city by hosting sacrificial ceremonies in the name of dispelling ill fortune. Hylas suspects Patrick IV is a fraudster and asks you to help with the investigation. You go to observe Patrick IV's sacrificial ceremony and find some clues in the ashes of the bonfire...",
    ["TaskDescription110224103"]="You find a broken charm in the bonfire, but you don't know what it is for. Hylas suggests asking someone who's well-versed in magic for help, and you immediately think of Bairde from the City of Magic...",
    ["TaskDescription110224104"]="Bairde tells you the broken charm is just an ordinary teleportation charm. There's no question the people of Glast Heim are being deceived. To expose the deception, Bairde hands you another charm to throw into the bonfire during the next sacrifice where the charade will reveal itself for the sham that it is. Hylas directs you to Patrick IV's residence. You head to the northeast side of Glast Heim to find the house surrounded by his followers.",
    ["TaskDescription110224105"]="You successfully entice Patrick IV to hold a sacrificial ceremony by offering him a sizable sum of money. You throw the charm into the bonfire during the sacrificial ceremony according to Bairde's instructions. It summons the soul of Patrick III. The deception is revealed during the confrontation between father and son. Patrick IV flees from his father's tongue-lashing and his followers finally realize they have been deceived...",
    ["TaskDescription110225101"]="You meet a resident of Glast Heim named Lanister who complains to you about the mysterious sound of a child crying coming from the nearby ruins. The noise has wreaked havoc on his family, not allowing them any rest. He asks you to help investigate. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go investigate the ruins</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110225102"]="You see the ghost of a little girl in the ruins, but you can't seem to approach her. You tell Ramir about this and he tells you about a famous medium in the city called Macy who may be able to help you exorcise the ghost. Find and make inquiries with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Macy</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110225103"]="With the help of the Requiem Grass, you finally appease the ghost of the little girl. She tells you she was abandoned at home by her father with no way to fend for herself until she died of starvation. To free the little girl from her fixation of her abandonment, it seems you'll have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for clues in the ruins of her home</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110225104"]="You find a diary page left behind by the little girl's father in the ruins, alongside a bell he wanted to give to her. You learn that the little girl's father worked in the Sage Academy during the Schmidt Empire. However, due to King Schmidt's emphasis on military strength over the arts, the sages, including the little girl's father, were forced to oversee work in the sewers. You travel to the sewers to find a Sageworm that responds to the bell. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Try taking the Sageworm back to Rey</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110225105"]="The Sageworm appears to lose its mind every so often on the way back, but the ringing of the bell seems to help soothe it. You finally make it back to Rey. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring the Sageworm to Rey</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110226101"]="You meet a tired-looking merchant named Byreon in Glast Heim Prison. He tells you that he and his caravan came to Glast Heim's underground churchyard to excavate the lost treasure there. However, monsters ambushed them while they were digging. All of his companions were killed, and he just managed to escape with his life. Unfortunately, he dropped his most precious jewelry box amid the confusion. He now asks you to help him find the jewelry box. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>northwest corner of Glast Heim Churchyard</color> to investigate.",
    ["TaskDescription110226102"]="You run into rampaging monsters beneath Glast Heim Churchyard. After you dispose of the monsters, you find the bodies of the merchants. It looks like the jewelry box might still be among the corpses. Search the <color=#CA2E0AFF>corpses of the caravan personnel</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>jewelry box</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110226103"]="You search the corpses of the caravan members, but find no traces of the jewelry box. However, you do find weapon wounds on their bodies, instead of the monster claw marks you were expecting to see. You suddenly hear a faint cry for help. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find out where the cry came from</color>. Maybe someone needs your help!",
    ["TaskDescription110226104"]="You discover that the cries for help are coming from a wounded merchant named Wudyr, who has been besieged by monsters. His body is covered with wounds, and they won't stop bleeding. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather some Clotting Grass</color>, and help him stop the bleeding!",
    ["TaskDescription110226105"]="After you treat Wudyr, you discover that the story he tells you is completely different from Byreon's, the merchant you met in Glast Heim Prison who sent you here. Wudyr says that the caravan was attacked by a group of robbers, and their entire squad was destroyed, leaving him to guard the jewelry box that had not been stolen alone. He decides to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Byreon</color> with you to confront him with the truth!",
    ["TaskDescription110227101"]="In Aldebaran, you overhear a conversation between Chief Gerner and two soldiers and learn that they seem to be trying to sneak into the Clock Tower. Unable to subdue your curiosity, you approach them, but Chief Gerner suddenly raises his gun at you...?!",
    ["TaskDescription110227102"]="It turns out that the soldier dispatched by Chief Gerner to investigate the Clock Tower has been lost for a day. Now, Chief Gerner is anxious to enter the Clock Tower and search for them. After learning that you have free access to the tower, he gives you the task of finding the missing person. Upon arriving on the second floor, you meet Royce, a young man wearing a guard uniform. He tells you that after tangling with the monsters, he lost the investigation record and became stranded in the Clock Tower. In order to escape as soon as possible, you decide to help him <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>records</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110227103"]="You search the second floor of the Clock Tower for the investigation records Royce lost. According to him, <color=#CA2E0AFF>4 pages</color> of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigation record</color> were taken by the monsters. Once you <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect all of them</color>, please <color=#CA2E0AFF>take them to Royce</color> as soon as possible!",
    ["TaskDescription110227104"]="You find all of the investigation records, only to discover that what is recorded on then records is completely different from what Royce said. What’s really going on...?",
    ["TaskDescription110227105"]="Royce's indifferent attitude arouses your suspicions. You decide you have no option but to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>empty zone in the northeast section of 1F</color> as stated in the investigation records. However, to your surprise...?",
    ["TaskDescription110228101"]="You met the bard Morts in Morroc. He seems to be working on a new poem, but doesn't have enough material. He wonders if you have time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help him</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110228102"]="After accepting Morts’ request, you locate a pair of brothers living in the west of Morroc. Their ancestors personally experienced the Great War and may provide new inspiration for Morts’ works. However, when you ask Weldon, the younger brother, about the hero who defeated the Demon King in battle, he talks with a deadpan expression and nary a hint of heroic spirit. At his request, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture</color> of a monster known as a <color=#CA2E0AFF>picky</color> to use as a reference...",
    ["TaskDescription110228103"]="You bring back the picture of a picky, but the brothers seem to disagree over the hero's appearance. You decide it’s best to take down both of their descriptions and give them to Morts to judge for himself. Next, it's time to ask them about the weapon used by the hero...",
    ["TaskDescription110228104"]="To your chagrin, they also disagree about which weapon was used. Once again, you can only once again write down both of their accounts. Finally, you ask them about the scene of the heroic battle...",
    ["TaskDescription110228105"]="You've finished collecting all the creative materials that Morts needs, now go back and help him finish his new poem! However, the two brothers have different descriptions about the hero — and it is up to you to decide which one you tell Morts.",
    ["TaskDescription110229101"]="You passed by Kafra's headquarters while wondering around one day, only to find Taylin throwing a tantrum — what in the world happened here?",
    ["TaskDescription110229102"]="It turns out that Taylin is mad about her friend Xiuling's love affair. She thinks that her new boyfriend is a wuss and is not worthy of her best friend at all, and even has the idea to break the two up. Taylin entrusts you to disguise yourself as a mugger to harass them while on their date, hoping that shows Xiuling her boyfriend's true colors. To do this, you must disguise yourself thoroughly, starting with getting<color=#CA2E0AFF>Brilight's</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>forewings</color>to mend your borrowed costume...",
    ["TaskDescription110229103"]="After obtaining the costume, Taylin also asks you to undertake a comprehensive <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"combat training\"</color> at the Martial Arts Instructor's Office...",
    ["TaskDescription110229104"]="Last but not least, the pre-fight trash talk is just as important! To do so, you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>study</color> a large number of magnificent <color=#CA2E0AFF>masterpieces</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110229105"]="All of this preparation — it's going to pay off right now! It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>change into your costume</color> and complete the task Taylin asked for!",
    ["TaskDescription110230101"]="At the foot of the Mjolnir Mountains, Macpennie was muttering about, and you curiously went over to her — and somehow, she actually told you...?",
    ["TaskDescription110230102"]="Under Macpennie's commission, you went to the south side of the Mjolnir Mountains in search of an old grandpa by the name of Tolkien. By the time you found him, Sky Petites had already surrounded him. You rescued him in the nick of time, but then he asked you to help him defeat a few more Sky Petites. Upon closer inspection of the old man's wounds — you decide that if he is willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>treat his wounds</color> first, only then will you help him hunt down these dragons.",
    ["TaskDescription110230103"]="While patching up Tolkien, he once again asks you to join him in <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeating</color> more <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sky Petites</color>. The old man seems to be hiding something, and you notice it — so you tell him to watch from a distance while you fight for him. Hopefully, this can fulfill his wish?",
    ["TaskDescription110230104"]="Sky Petites are falling from the sky in front of you, waves after waves. Suddenly, Tolkien points to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Gem</color> that fell from the flying dragon's corpse, roaring with excitement...",
    ["TaskDescription110230105"]="It turns out that Tolkien comes here day after day to hunt Sky Petites because of the precious Dragon Eye Gem. But when you ask what it's for, he says nothing but asks you to come with him to a certain place...",
    ["TaskDescription110231101"]="You meet with President Nicholas and two students in front of the Alchemist Guild — they appear to be discussing something serious...?",
    ["TaskDescription110231102"]="It appears that Juno University sends its most excellent students to the Alchemists Guild for internship every year, and one of the trainings is to enter the Bell Tower alone to get the moon dew flower alchemy ingredient. This year, however, many students entered the Bell Tower and never returned. For this reason, President Nicholas has sent his son Amul to investigate, but he hopes that you can assist him. If you are willing to help, head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Basement Floor of the Bell Tower</color> to aid Amul.",
    ["TaskDescription110231103"]="Ivy tells you that all this was the scheme of the Zealotus. She planted a large Moon Dew Flower in front of her cave to attract the students who came to pick them. She then cast spells and imprisoned them — slowly enjoying their young and vigorous life force afterward. The student you saw earlier, Ariel, is obviously one of the victims. If you want to <color=#CA2E0AFF>save his life</color>, you must act now.",
    ["TaskDescription110231104"]="Amul persuaded Ariel to leave the witch and return to his normal life, but you vaguely feel that something is off. Is Amul hiding something from you...?!",
    ["TaskDescription110231105"]="In order to find the truth, you entered the cave where the witch lives, but were surprised to find all the students sleeping in it safely. The Witch's Diary also proved that she never used a spell on Ariel, and that the two may be in deep love... But if that's the case — what is Amul trying to do by planning all this...?",
    ["TaskDescription110231203"]="There was indeed only a handful of low-level monsters along the way. The stranger expressed his gratitude for the Obeaune and his tip. You agreed, mere seconds before you spotted an incoming horde...",
    ["TaskDescription110232101"]="During the stay in Hermit's Village, you inadvertently overheard <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grantham's</color> mutterings, revealing a strong interest in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zenhai Marsh</color>... There must be something fishy about this place! Go and ask him!",
    ["TaskDescription110232102"]="With directions from Grantham, you met a man and his servant besieged by Alligators. They were delivering a precious item to the Main City of Comodo. The seriously injured servant pleaded with you to help his master with the delivery and told you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>proceed westward</color> along the safest route.",
    ["TaskDescription110232104"]="A giant Argos came out of nowhere to block your passage. You defeated it after a hard fight. You began to suspect the servant, but the man remained adamant that all doubts will vanish once you <color=#CA2E0AFF>get atop the volcano</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110232105"]="Halfway up the volcano, the Obeaune servant finally showed his true colors. It was all about keeping the treasure for himself. Shocked by the betrayal, the stranger confessed that the item is indeed very dangerous. You decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>throw it into the volcano</color> immediately.",
    ["TaskDescription110233101"]="A worried-looking village chief Norris responded to your kindly query with a tale of woe concerning the responsible manager of the village warehouse, Toland, and his family. Fortunately, a kindhearted Adventurer like yourself could step in where the villagers' mistakes have barred the way.",
    ["TaskDescription110233102"]="Toland revealed his daughter's three-year ordeal of lovesickness. Fortunately, a breakthrough in the case may be found in that very special \"vow.\"",
    ["TaskDescription110233103"]="Common sense rebelled at such a ridiculous vow involving blossoming starbell, the cry of the fledgling raggler... as well as the melted glacier. Yet it has played someone false for three years.",
    ["TaskDescription110233104"]="It was pretty difficult but you finally fulfilled all three components of the vow. Now all you have to do was tear that falsehood apart.",
    ["TaskDescription110233105"]="It turned out some miracles do happen. You glimpse an approaching ship in the far distance. Don't tell me these kinds of fairy tales really do come true? Or is something else going on?",
    ["TaskDescription110234101"]="Kokomo Beach market was bustling. Attracted by the peddlery, you made your way to a nearby vendor. The enthusiastic merchant Jack hawked his batch of latest trinkets, in which you spied something very unexpected but familiar...",
    ["TaskDescription110234102"]="The apparent Crown of Tristan III piqued your interest. You'd like to get it formally identified by Jimmy, but Jack's wares wouldn't come cheap. You had to make it worth his while with some sea pearls and coral crystals from the Shellfish and Asters, respectively.",
    ["TaskDescription110234103"]="You managed to get your hands on some sea pearls and coral crystals with some difficulty, winning Jack's praises and the promised crown. Now for Jimmy to identify its veracity!",
    ["TaskDescription110234104"]="Jimmy claimed the crown a gift from a stranger, but you quickly saw through his lies and taught him a lesson. It turned out the crown was the pirate's passage fee from a desperado on the run from the law. Apparently, he ended up in a quiet Hermit's Village in Zenhai Marsh. No word has been heard of him since, so you decided to go there to investigate.",
    ["TaskDescription110234105"]="You found that man's diary in the Hermit's Village. It turned out he was a Priest of Arunafeltz who was exiled to a deserted island for heresy. He eventually pledged the crown to the pirate in exchange for safe passage and continues searching stones to summon a demon, Beelzebub. Sadly, the diary was a mess. You had to do some detective work of your own.",
    ["TaskDescription110235101"]="Callahan looked a lot more anxious than usual. It seemed he got in some trouble. You could hear his faint complaints about someone called Doyle.",
    ["TaskDescription110235102"]="You departed in search of Doyle at Callahan's urging, with only his left-over itinerary to guide you. You should be alright as long as he's a man who stuck to his plans...",
    ["TaskDescription110235103"]="It somehow never occurred to you that Doyle might possess a legion of rabid fans, which angrily cast you out of their sight. It looks like your best bet was simply to follow his itinerary to the next destination.",
    ["TaskDescription110235104"]="The men of the village mistake you for Doyle, resulting in fisticuffs. Misunderstanding resolved, Dale informed you Doyle has been troubling their life for some time. Your search has come up empty again. Only two destinations remain on the man's itinerary...",
    ["TaskDescription110235105"]="Compassion compelled you to keep Doyle's many lies a secret from Olivia. Fresh flowers bestowed, you find yourself once again seeking the very last destination in his itinerary...",
    ["TaskDescription110236101"]="Comodo is famous for its native beers, a fame that just might be enough to draw you to the tavern where you overheard a complaint from the barkeep, Vendra. It looked like all was not well there. Time to ask Vendra what happened!",
    ["TaskDescription110236102"]="It turned up many of the tavern's recent patrons had been set upon violently while homeward bound. Vendra wanted some detective work done. After receiving clues from a victim Eugene, you still need to chat to Gordon and Mottle.",
    ["TaskDescription110236103"]="You started to draw commonalities between the three victims' reports: late nights, beers, and the beach. You decided to check out Komodo Beach for yourself in the dead of night and, of course, purchase a pint from Vendra before setting out!",
    ["TaskDescription110236104"]="Vendra filled your glass, expressing great hopes about your investigation. But just who could these violent assailants be? You made your way to Kokomo Beach by sunset, cold beer glistening in your hand. All you have to do now is bide your time and wait for the attackers to reveal themselves!",
    ["TaskDescription110236105"]="You put on your best drunken performance on the beach and stumble right into a group of... Galapagos?! It turned out the poor creatures are so fascinated with Vendra's delicious beers that they thirstily eyed your glass even if defeated. Escort these culprits back to Vendra for punishment!",
    ["TaskDescription110237101"]="Today, you encounter two soldiers grappling each other in front of the Undead Arena...",
    ["TaskDescription110237102"]="As it turns out, the soldiers are trying to shirk the task assigned by Naght Sieger. With their incompetent skill, they know well enough that it is a suicide mission if they ever join the Grand Celebration, but it doesn't get any better if they disobey Naght Sieger's order. After bickering for a while, this thorny mission somehow falls on you. If you want to get out of this, you must pour the potion on Lord of the Dead during the Grand Celebration...",
    ["TaskDescription110237103"]="You come across the legendary Lord of the Dead in the waiting area, and he wants you to answer three questions out of nowhere...",
    ["TaskDescription110237104"]="After answering all the questions, Lord of the Dead asks you to stay behind his back during the contest, and he assures you that you will make it out alive. One contestant tells you he said the same thing to everyone before every contest, and you're confused by what he said... Before you even finish talking, the contest begins. Now, you must enter the Undead Arena as everybody does.",
    ["TaskDescription110237105"]="As soon as the contest begins, Lord of the Dead guards you with his shield and grapples with others alone. In response, you dive into the battle and fight alongside him. Following the defeat of all the enemies on the field, Lord of the Dead does something that catches everyone off guard...",
    ["TaskDescription110238101"]="Even though you have sprayed the potion on Lord of the Dead per the Undead Soldiers' request, you realize what the task Naght Sieger assigned them was way beyond this by seeing they are crying at the top of their lungs. They totally forget about the other part because they are just not as smart. It looks like if you want them to spit out something useful, you'll have to wait until they pull themselves together.",
    ["TaskDescription110238102"]="It turns out the task that Naght Sieger assigned to the two Undead Soldiers was not only to spray the Tracking Potion on Lord of the Dead but also to follow him along and find a way to make him drink the Potion of Revelation. It has been a while since the contest has ended, and the Tacking Potion has a relatively short effect period, which they are too slow to catch up with Lord of the Dead before the effect wears off. Somehow this weird quest falls on your again...",
    ["TaskDescription110238103"]="You follow the trackway of Tracking Potion and notice that Lord of the Dead has been walking for quite a while and seems not feeling well. This last set of footprints somehow...?",
    ["TaskDescription110238104"]="Lord of the Dead's potion trackway fades out near the shoreside of the Gjoll. By looking at the path, he may have stepped into the poisonous glacier, Hvergelmir. You feel something is out of place, so you take a picture of the last set of footprints and return it to the Undead Soldiers.",
    ["TaskDescription110238105"]="As soon as the soldiers see the picture, their faces turn pale and become terrified, and they start mentioning words you've never heard of. When you ask for more details, they try to skip over the topic by mumbling random stuff. After that, they point you to where the Lord of the Dead lives and want you to wait there until he returns, then make him drink the Potion of Revelation...",
    ["TaskDescription110238106"]="Following the instruction of the soldiers, you find Lord of the Dead, who is sleeping in front of his residence. You then dose him with the Potion of Revelation, but nothing happens. Suddenly, the footsteps coming out of nowhere alert you, and you must find a place to hide...",
    ["TaskDescription110239101"]="You witness a young girl feeding an unknown potion to the Lord of the Dead while hiding behind the house. Surprisingly, the footprints she left when leaving are the same as the Tacking Potion's trackway as before. While harboring your thought, you tail along the young girl and arrive at an unfamiliar tomb...",
    ["TaskDescription110239102"]="Having revealed your identity, you ask the girl why she pretended to be the Lord of the Dead. Following a moment of silence, she asks you to look at the tomb before you...",
    ["TaskDescription110239103"]="The tomb in front belongs to a knight named Holy Fire, who has a virtuous heart and takes on the responsibility of saving every being in the world. His beliefs caused him some unfair treatment from others, but he stood firm in his ground, and what broke people's hearts the most was the fact that he was killed in an ambush plotted by his partner. This girl was the sole witness and one of the victims of this intrigue, in which she could do nothing but watch the Holy Fire Knight sacrifice his life to save her.... soon after, this ailing girl passed away along with her regret and fell into the Realm of the Dead. She never thought she would ever meet her savior again until she arrived here—that's right, the undefeatable Lord of the Dead in the Grand Celebration was the one who saved her life... Speaking of which, this ailing girl starts to cough excessively, and to ease her pain, you will need to gather some Crane Feather that can stop the coughing...",
    ["TaskDescription110239104"]="It seems like the girl is getting better after taking the Crane Feather. She tells you that Hel restored the sense of pain to the knight, which doesn't belongs to an Undead, just to torture him even further. Even more, she made him return to the poisonous glacier of Hvergelmir to rinse his soul with Gjoll water after every contest. The girl didn't want to see her savior suffer anymore, so she pretended to be the Lord of the Undead and joined the contest for him... This heartbreaking story deeply touches you and makes your thought starts to ramble. But now, Naght Sieger, Judge of the Underworld, suddenly appears in front of the two of you...",
    ["TaskDescription110239105"]="Apparently, there is only one good reason for this judge to show up here—to bring the girl who forged her identity as the Lord of the Dead to justice. But the girl is wise enough to use Naght Sieger's arrogance and his hatred against Lord of the Dead to square a deal, which, if she wins the contest, Lord of the Dead's name will be wiped from the Grand Celebration contestant list, if she loses, Lord of the Dead will have to bear all the guilty charges against him... To witness this bet, you and the girl return to Undead Arena again...",
    ["TaskDescription110239106"]="The two of you arrive at the Undead Arena. There stands the real Lord of the Dead this time. As usual, following the defeat of the evil spirits, he asks whoever is still on the field to stab him in the chest. However, no one wants to do that this time...",
    ["TaskDescription110240101"]="This roundabout Bloodline Banquet has finally ended, but you know well enough there is no way to recover the losses during this coup. Your heart sinks in sorrow when you realize that the soon-to-be king, Aronst, is still missing...",
    ["TaskDescription110240102"]="Who would have thought that Aronst, whom we have been searching for every day and every night, reappeared in Prontera without notice today? Bohr stops you from meeting him just as you receive the news and is about to meet him. He then tells you Aronst is in bad shape, and the doctor suggests he take some nervous-smoothing dishes for a better recovery. Bohr trusts no one but you for gathering ingredients and entrusts you with this task. You must gather the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mint</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Premium Grease</color> from the Savage Babe, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goldflower Stamen</color> from the Mandragora outside of the Prontera South Gate...",
    ["TaskDescription110240103"]="If you have finished gathering the ingredients, hurry up and make the Vegetable Stew following the recipe's instructions, and return to the palace to meet with Bohr!",
    ["TaskDescription110240104"]="In your meeting with Aronst, he vents about the things that have happened to him lately. He has been living in a farm village in the Schwarzwald Republic ever since the first day of the Bloodline Banquet. During his prolonged absence, Aronst could not recall who he was due to amnesia. Until later, he kept having the same dream repeatedly, and something in this ambiguous dream seemed to trigger his memory that had been sealed away. Eventually, he reached a familiar place by following the same path and scenery from his dream. As a result, he had fully regained all his memories by that time. Aronst still needs clarification about everything and asks you where Azer is... Seeing this, Bohr switches topics and asks you to pray for a glass of Holy Water at Central Fountain.",
    ["TaskDescription110240105"]="The news of Azer's death makes Aronst go crazy, even after he finishes the glass of Holy Water that is supposed to keep his coolness. You have no option but to knock him out with force to prevent him from hurting himself...",
    ["TaskDescription110241101"]="After Aronst calmed down, you and Bohr decide to tell him everything that happened on the day of the Bloodline Banquet...",
    ["TaskDescription110241102"]="Bohr introduces an artist called Kain to you and Aronst. Kain claims that everything Azer has done during the Bloodline Banquet was under his assistance. The purpose of his being here is to deliver Bohr a letter written by Azer. In fact, Azer told Kain to hand this letter to Ian when he was still alive, but Kain didn't think Ian would understand Azer's intention, and that's why he made the call to give it to Bohr instead. Now, Bohr asks you and Aronst to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>letter</color> together...",
    ["TaskDescription110241103"]="You and Aronst open up the letter from Azer, which logs the rivalry between Azer and Ian in detail. It turns out Azer has stopped believing in his father ever since the first assassination. Only by pretending to be loyal and waiting for the right moment can he defend Aronst and his family. The days filled with cheating and betrayal within his family must have been unbearable for Azer, and you don't even want to replicate his state of mind during that period. You realize Aronst is becoming overly emotional and almost passes out at this point. You return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color> to get more <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clear Fountain Water</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110241104"]="After taking a short break, you start to read Azer's letter. After all, it was Ian's idea to murder Aronst because he was concerned about all the attention and popularity of him being the prince of Gaebolg. Ian wanted Aronst to become the scapegoat for the Walter family and bear all the guilty charges for their treacherous plots so that he could bring down the Gaebolg family, who has always stayed at the pinnacle of their popularity and social acceptance. He even ignored Azer's will and used Luminary Dream's antidote as a threat to order him to push his best friend into a bottomless abyss by his own hands... Azer, who was in a dire situation, stopped hesitating and devised a plan for this end game to save everyone but himself, at the cost of his life... At this point, Aronst is overwhelmed by the sadness, agony, and sorrow in his heart, but he insists on finishing the letter. So, Bohr can only ask you to search for some <color=#CA2E0AFF>refreshing medicine</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110241105"]="You are finally done with the letters with such dreadful content, and it seems like Azer wrote every word with his searing blood and projected all his hatred and sorrow into the letter as a means of revenge. Bohr pulls out Tristan III's will and claims that the Defense Force found Tristan III's corpse on an island near Arunafeltz waters. He had been long dead when they spotted him, and only this piece of will, written in his blood, remained after he died. In light of his current mental state, this is undoubtedly another severe blow to Aronst. He then asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>will</color> for him because he can't take it anymore...",
    ["TaskDescription110242101"]="Hearing a heavy sigh, you turn around, and see a tall, well-dressed man...",
    ["TaskDescription110242102"]="The man's name is Syphus, and he claims he is an aide-de-camp serving under the Foreign Minister of the Rune Kingdom. When you ask him about the heavy sigh, he tells you the target isn't cooperating well in his current escort mission, and his identity has limited his action in many different countries. It is not easy for him to search for the target publicly. He wants you to help him locate the two targets in this mission. One of them is a purple-haired girl who is always looking for a fight. Maybe, you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>start from the marketplace</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110242103"]="You see Goldie in the marketplace, who is also from the Rune Kingdom. It turns out she is one of the targets being escorted! After helping Goldie to score a bargain, she happily tells you where the other one goes — <color=#CA2E0AFF>School</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110242104"]="After some twists and turns, you finally find yourself another person of the same interest — Zenlur, on the Juno Campus Exhibition. He buries his head into all sorts of fascinating inventions and totally forgets about the rally. Now, he is attracted to the invention of a <color=#CA2E0AFF>physics student</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110242105"]="After looking at the skateboard, Zenlur runs over to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Engineering Booth</color> exhilaratingly...",
    ["TaskDescription110242106"]="You drag your exhausted body and follow Zenlur to the Engineering Booth. After taking the tour, Zenlur tells you that he listened to Syphus and came here to become stronger. He doesn't want to share too much with you, so he leaves by himself. And now, you can finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>report back to Syphus</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110243101"]="The quest line of rallying the Dispatch Team is not finished yet. Go ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Syphus</color> to see if there's anything new!",
    ["TaskDescription110243102"]="The rally quest is opened again. Following the information given by Syphus, you encounter two members of the Dispatch Team, Orfeo and Trinity. They tell you, that they are not reluctant to return to the team, but to prepare items for their show, they are unable to walk away for now. You then come to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno University</color>, deciding to borrow two sets of stage costumes from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drama Club</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110243103"]="After getting the stage costumes, you go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>somewhere near the Exchange Center</color>. It's said that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Old Lonnis</color> here has the stuff you want...",
    ["TaskDescription110243104"]="You meet with the shrewd Old Lonnis, and he tells you he doesn't take Zeny for this trade. He will give you what you need if you trade him the parts obtained from Brown Venatu. You accept the deal. Then, with all the required items collected, you return to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>performance venue of the bard and the dancer</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110244101"]="Only the last two members have yet to return to the team. Go ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Syphus</color> about the latest update!",
    ["TaskDescription110244102"]="As expected, the last two members are still out there. The furious yet helpless Syphus has to ask you to bring back <color=#CA2E0AFF>Celia and Pierre</color>, who are now exchange students at Juno University, and wants you to deliver them a final message, \"Backing out of a promise comes with a consequence.\"",
    ["TaskDescription110244103"]="You encounter Celia and Ivy inside the Juno Library. They are doing some sort of experiment on a weird book called Juno University: Some School History. It's said that the reader will get dizzy after reading the book for a while. You then see many students lying on the ground. Not to your surprise, they are \"volunteers\" invited by Ivy. Later during the conversation, Celia mentions the adventure between the two of you back in Geffen. For some reason, Ivy suddenly becomes angry and strongly demands you open the book. After a moment of dizziness, you find yourself arriving at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Illusion in the Book</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110244104"]="As the Successor of Odin's Bloodline, you have successfully escaped from the Illusion in the Book. Based on your description, Celia and Ivy believe that one of the pages has been cast with a magic spell named Magic of Confusion. Ivy tells you that even though the spell is quite powerful, he can still craft a Wakeup Potion that temporarily nullifies the magic effect and reveals the tampered texts. Now he needs to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some materials</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110244105"]="You've helped Ivy collect all the materials. Now, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>use the Wakeup Potion to solve the riddle</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110244106"]="Thanks to everyone's painstaking effort, it turns out the answer to the riddle is only an ordinary but valid campus record. You look at the confused <color=#CA2E0AFF>Celia</color>; maybe this is a good chance to get her back to the team?",
    ["TaskDescription110245101"]="With the last two members returning to the team, your secret mission is now completed. If you ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Syphus</color>, who is in high spirits, about the case, is it possible for you to get an answer other than \"No Comment\"?",
    ["TaskDescription110245102"]="Moved by your attitude and contribution, Syphus gestures you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him to a secluded corner</color>. He will tell you everything he knows there...",
    ["TaskDescription110245103"]="Syphus shows you a secret rally order issued by the Foreign Minister of the Rune Kingdom. It turns out that the mission of the Dispatch Team, following the instructions on the rally order, is to go to Lighthalzen and rescue a group of <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing contacts</color> from the kingdom, with whom you are quite familiar somehow.",
    ["TaskDescription110245104"]="You ask about the reason why people on the list went missing, but Syphus confesses that he has no idea, either. But he assures you, that the Dispatch Team members are the best of the best, and they can complete the mission without any hassle. Now, he must take the airship. If you are willing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a photo with him before the airship</color>, he will be delighted.",
    ["TaskDescription110246101"]="What makes <color=#CA2E0AFF>Enchulo</color>, the head writer of the Libet Express, this angry?",
    ["TaskDescription110246102"]="The furious Enchulo complains that Shana is nowhere to be found at this critical moment. He wants you to take on her role as a photographer, and go to Rekenber's release conference with him together. At the conference, you follow his instruction and painstakingly <color=#CA2E0AFF>take photos of Irumina</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110246103"]="At the release conference, you, scrambling to take photos, are pushed to the front of the crowd, and somehow get selected as a lucky audience by Irumina to <color=#CA2E0AFF>test the interactable Digger No.2</color> together.",
    ["TaskDescription110246104"]="You play along with Irumina and complete everything at the release conference. Now go meet with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Enchulo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110246105"]="You find Enchulo, as well as the missing female photographer, Shana, a super fan of Irumina. She went missing before because she was getting an autograph backstage. Anyway, <color=#CA2E0AFF>select your photo</color> first.",
    ["TaskDescription110247101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Orfeo and Trinity</color> are really busy preparing for their tour. Let's see how they're doing.",
    ["TaskDescription110247102"]="The theme for the tour is Rekenber Corp. While Orfeo tunes his lute, he'd like you to pick up some survey forms from a few people. Start with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Foreman Letom</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110247103"]="After beating up Letom, you get the survey. Next up is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Casselir</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110247104"]="Casselir happily gives you the survey but admits he didn't finish it. If you get him <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Healthy Dragon Hearts from Earth Deleters</color>, he'll share some answers not on the survey.",
    ["TaskDescription110247105"]="From Casselir, you learn about Rekenber's ties to the Republic before its establishment. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>give the survey to Orfeo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110248101"]="After retrieving the surveys from Letom and Casselir, the next ones are <color=#CA2E0AFF>Enchulo</color> and W.",
    ["TaskDescription110248102"]="Not surprisingly, Enchulo hasn't completed the survey because he's busy. However, if you deliver an interview invitation to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lord Carl</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>submit a complaint letter against Rekenber</color>, he'll fill it out.",
    ["TaskDescription110248103"]="Lord Carl turns down the interview but confirms that the Republic will protect every citizen regarding the complaint letter. Enchulo appreciates the response and gives you his survey. Now, only <color=#CA2E0AFF>W</color> is left.",
    ["TaskDescription110248104"]="W is anxious about the confiscated cargo, but then she gives you the survey right away. You decide to help <color=#CA2E0AFF>W with the confiscated goods issue</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110248105"]="The inspector at the Border Inspection Station asks for 10 Rainbow Feathers as payment to fix the problem. After sorting it out for W, you can finally <color=#CA2E0AFF>give the rest of the surveys to Orfeo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110249101"]="You come across a student wearing the uniform of Juno University at a <color=#CA2E0AFF>temporary camp outside the Rachel Plains</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110249102"]="Her name's Mercy, and she needs your help catching the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Drosera King</color> roaming the Rachel Plains. If she doesn't get it, her essay might be a total flop.",
    ["TaskDescription110249103"]="After some effort, you manage to catch the Drosera King. Mercy cuts off its root and asks you to head back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juno</color> to get a full analysis report from her mentor, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Viola</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110249104"]="Viola is pretty annoyed that Mercy keeps putting off her essay and wants you to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>fuel essence from Fiery Dimik</color> for the analysis materials.",
    ["TaskDescription110249105"]="You got the analysis report from Viola—time to head back and give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mercy</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110250101"]="In the Grey Wolf Village out on the plains, you run into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sartre</color>, who looks visibly upset—something big must've happened...",
    ["TaskDescription110250102"]="Sartre tells you the chief of Grey Wolf Village passed away last night. He wanted a nomadic funeral, but it goes against Freyja's doctrine. You agree to help and get the full ritual steps from his granddaughter, Zahya. Time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect the materials needed for the funeral</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110250103"]="After collecting all the materials, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Israel</color> shows up with the guards' patrol schedule. Let's come up with a plan together!",
    ["TaskDescription110250104"]="As per Israel's plan, you'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>distract the patrolling Temple Guards</color> to give Sartre a window to move the chief's body.",
    ["TaskDescription110250105"]="You pulled it off! The guards are gone, and the <color=#CA2E0AFF>funeral deep in the plains</color> is about to start...",
    ["TaskDescription110251101"]="Outside of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel Plains</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Uda</color> and Lasha from Grey Wolf Village seem to be in a heated argument...",
    ["TaskDescription110251102"]="It turns out that Israel sent out one too many fairy tale books to the kids in Grey Wolf Village. You take the extra book and suggest giving it to the Pope—to make up for her dull childhood. But when you open it together... you suddenly get pulled into the illusion in the book!... (P.S. You and the Pope can enter and exit the illusion via the Ferryman.)",
    ["TaskDescription110251103"]="In the illusion, you meet a girl named Alsa who looks just like the Pope. She asks you to go with her to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underworld</color> and beg the Lord of the Underworld to return her brother Allen's soul.",
    ["TaskDescription110251104"]="Following a journey fraught with challenges, you at last stand before the Lord of the Underworld. (P.S. You and the Pope can enter and exit the illusion via the Ferryman.)",
    ["TaskDescription110251105"]="The Lord of the Underworld praises your bravery and agrees to return Allen's soul—but only if you make the journey back without looking back. You follow the path from memory... and end up in the Pope's bedroom? (P.S. You and the Pope can enter and exit the illusion via the Ferryman.)",
    ["TaskDescription110252101"]="Near the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rachel</color> Temple, a middle-aged man dressed as a traveling merchant stops you...",
    ["TaskDescription110252102"]="The merchant, identifying himself as Boggs—a former acquaintance of Priest Neirun—entrusts you with a token to deliver. Yet upon seeing it, Neirun responds with cold indifference, instructing you to return it.",
    ["TaskDescription110252103"]="On your way out, you run into Malam and deliver Boggs' response together. It turns out that he and Neirun used to be lovers but were separated by fate. Now, Boggs is terminally ill—he just wants to see her one last time. To help him, Malam asks you to find some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cactus Flower and Camel Milk Wine</color>, and he will handle the rest.",
    ["TaskDescription110252104"]="You've got everything! Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>cemetery on the outskirts</color> now and meet up with Malam!",
    ["TaskDescription110252105"]="You tried everything, but Neirun wouldn't budge. All that's left... is to tell <color=#CA2E0AFF>Boggs</color> the truth.",
    ["TaskDescription110253101"]="Just as you arrive at the Assassin's Guild, Hassan asks you about Goldie's whereabouts. Knowing she's out on a secret quest, you keep silent. Hassan doesn't press further but asks you to check on her camp. Since Goldie's departure, that camp has become a target for other factions...",
    ["TaskDescription110253102"]="You take Ebel's request to help train the rookies. Their lazy attitudes irritate you, so you decide to teach them a lesson and have a little fun while you're at it.",
    ["TaskDescription110253103"]="You volunteer to help Ebel rescue the victims in the wild. The doctor doesn't look too good, so you'd better check with Jud.",
    ["TaskDescription110253104"]="Jud tells you that the one behind the goblins' madness might be Haglis, who had a feud with Goldie. You decide to join Jud and hunt down the culprit...",
    ["TaskDescription110253105"]="After dealing with Haglis' gang, you head back to the village to tell Ebel what happened.",
    ["TaskDescription110253106"]="Defeat the Strongest Rookie",
    ["TaskDescription110253107"]="Defeat Haglis",
    ["TaskDescription110254101"]="You reach the Gangash Pirates' base to look for Captain Drake, but Benjamin sneaks up to stop you—looks like he's got something to say...",
    ["TaskDescription110254102"]="You board the ship Captain Drake prepared, and sail toward Cecil's hometown...",
    ["TaskDescription110254103"]="Cecil's longbow activates a spell, pulling you into her memories...",
    ["TaskDescription110254104"]="The longbow's magic shows you Cecil's unpleasant memories with Captain Drake, then shifts to a strange marketplace, where she comforts a crying little girl.",
    ["TaskDescription110254105"]="Through Cecil's memories, you learn the origin of her longbow and how she chose the path of a bounty hunter. Now, it's time to find her a place to rest in peace...",
    ["TaskDescription110254106"]="Defeat the bandit leader",
    ["TaskDescription110301101"]="As you have been using Kafra's services for a long period of time, you have become a loyal customer. <color=#CA2E0AFF>W</color> seems to have some <color=#CA2E0AFF>special news</color> to share with you today!",
    ["TaskDescription110301102"]="W told you that if you are willing to help with a few small favors, you might get exclusive member privileges. Firstly, in order to upgrade the warehouse service, W needs some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lotus Grass</color> to purify the warehouse. Gather some near <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110301103"]="You successfully brought back some Lotus Grass. After W thanked you, she told you that she needs to customize a batch of pillows for Kafra's loyal customers. Therefore, she needs your help to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Down Fur</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baby Desert Wolves</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110301104"]="W is extremely grateful for your help and commented that you are fully eligible to become a VIP member. However, if you want to receive Kafra's exclusive member privileges, you will need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pass</color> a <color=#CA2E0AFF>test on the Kafra Corporation</color>. Start the test when you're ready!",
    ["TaskDescription110302101"]="Through the time you've spent with <color=#CA2E0AFF>W</color>, you've earned a place in her heart with your sincerity and honesty, and became a friend that she can rely on. But she seems to be a little <color=#CA2E0AFF>troubled</color> recently. Go check on her!",
    ["TaskDescription110302102"]="W tells you that she is fretting over Defolty's birthday present and both of you came up with the idea of giving her perfume. Visit General Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vienna Lindra</color> and check what the most popular <color=#CA2E0AFF>perfume</color> is!",
    ["TaskDescription110302103"]="Vienna Lindra told you that she has sold out of perfume, but she can make a customized fragrance for W. She needs <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Tough Vines</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Hinalle</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vocals</color>. Gather the materials for her!",
    ["TaskDescription110302104"]="You gave Vienna Lindra the materials you gathered and she made a bottle of perfume called Miraculous Encounter. She wants you to give it to W and wish Defolty happy birthday for her. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take the perfume to W</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110303101"]="You obtained a Sad Clown Music Box from a Deviling by chance and found that Flessi's name is engraved on it. Maybe it is something <color=#CA2E0AFF>Flessi</color> lost? Go ask him!",
    ["TaskDescription110303102"]="Flessi took the Sad Clown Music Box from you with tears in his eyes. He told you that it was a gift from a very important friend and it is very dear to him. However, the music box seemed to have been damaged while it was lost and you suggested that Bard Morts might be able to fix it. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>music box</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110303103"]="Morts is knowledgeable about musical instruments and thinks there might be an issue with the spring. However, this is his first time fixing a music box, so he needs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Library</color> and get a book called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Deep Within the Music Box</color> to help him confirm his suspicion.",
    ["TaskDescription110303104"]="After reading \"Deep Within the Music Box,\" Morts confirmed that deformation of the spring was causing the music box to malfunction. He needs some Maple Iron to make a new one, but his relationship with Hollgrehenn is a little awkward. Therefore, he needs you to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color> and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Maple Iron</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110303105"]="Morts successfully fixed the music box but he's pretty curious about the story behind it, so he decided to accompany you in returning the music box. Lead <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts to Flessi</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110304101"]="After spending some time together, you and Flessi developed a friendship that transcends age and time. However, he seems to be troubled recently. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a heart-to-heart with him</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110304102"]="Flessi told you the story of him and his childhood friend, Little Rick. You come to know that Little Rick was buried deep within the forest and Flessi has an unfulfilled wish that he hopes you can help him complete. Follow Flessi to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Little Rick's grave</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>clear the weeds</color> for him!",
    ["TaskDescription110304103"]="Flessi told you that he has always wanted to write the music that Little Rick composed on his tombstone, but has never been able to do so as he could not find a pigment that would not fade. He hopes that you can get him some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cornutus ink</color> as it can last a hundred years without fading.",
    ["TaskDescription110304104"]="Flessi thanked you for bringing him the precious ink. He asked you to get some of Little Rick's favorite <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cotton Candy</color> from Food Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grace</color> while he stays to write the music onto the tombstone. Go see Grace!",
    ["TaskDescription110304105"]="Grace nosily asked what the Cotton Candy is for, but you brushed her off in order to protect Flessi's privacy. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take the Cotton Candy back to Little Rick's tombstone</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110305101"]="Your passion for fishing caught the attention of Fishing Lure Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hayden</color>. He seems curious about your fishing experience. Listen to what he has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription110305102"]="After understanding your passion for fishing, Hayden happily shared with you his own interest in the hobby. He commented that he would really like to see what a <color=#CA2E0AFF>White Cloud Fish</color> looks like, so you decided to bring one to him.",
    ["TaskDescription110305103"]="Hayden was really touched that you brought him a White Cloud Fish and decided to keep it in his fish tank. However, his fish tank is rather sparse and needs some decoration. Get him some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shells</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110305104"]="Hayden thanked you for bringing him the decorations, but suddenly remembered that he was supposed to deliver a batch of fish bait to the Alson Fleet today. He was so caught up in chatting with you that it slipped his mind. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Deliver the fish bait to members of the Alson Fleet</color> for Hayden!",
    ["TaskDescription110306101"]="You and Hayden grew closer over numerous interactions and ultimately became best friends. But <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hayden</color> seems a little troubled today. Listen to what he has to say!",
    ["TaskDescription110306102"]="Hayden told you that he finally plucked up enough courage to ask his long-time crush, Elysia, out to stargaze. However, he knows almost nothing about astrology, so you decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Library</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> a book to <color=#CA2E0AFF>help him learn more about it</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110306103"]="You brought back a booked called \"Guide to the Stars.\" Hayden thanked you and immediately delved into the book. He learned that astrology requires power crystals and asked for your help to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Purple Spirit Crystals</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Cave</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110306104"]="Hayden thanked you for everything you've done for him, but he realized that his upcoming date seems to be lacking some romantic elements. So he asked you to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> to get a bottle of <color=#CA2E0AFF>red wine</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Isabella Trista</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110306105"]="Isabella Trista has been waiting for Hayden to make a move for a long time. She enthusiastically gave you a bottle of Fresh Wine. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take it to Hayden</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110307101"]="Your passion for fashion caught the attention of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chester</color> the hairdresser. It looks like he has something to say to you. Hear him out!",
    ["TaskDescription110307102"]="Chester told you that he would like to invite you to be his model in the hairstyle contest, but you will first need to pass his tests. In order to become his model, the most important thing is to have a deep understanding of fashion. To judge your taste, he asked you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take your own photos in three settings</color> in your current outfit.",
    ["TaskDescription110307103"]="Chester was pretty satisfied with your photos, and told you that you've successfully moved on to the next test: composure under pressure. Chester requested that you <color=#CA2E0AFF>join an arm-wrestling match</color> at Rose Red Tavern to show that you can remain calm under pressure from the crowd. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> and prove it to him!",
    ["TaskDescription110307104"]="Chester was pretty satisfied with your performance in the arm-wrestling match and passionately invited you to become his hairstyle model. He said that he will need you to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Butterfly Wing Powder</color> in order to secure your chances of winning first place. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera West Gate</color> and kill some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockers</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110308101"]="The chemistry between you and Chester is unbeatable. You even won the hairstyle contest together! However, he seems to have some troubles he wishes to confide in you. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Listen to his woes</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110308102"]="Chester and Appearance Merchant Vera are actually a couple but they have been giving each other the cold shoulder due to a disagreement. Therefore, Chester hopes that you can deliver a new <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hair Dye</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vera</color> and find out if she has any intention of making up with him!",
    ["TaskDescription110308103"]="Vera accepted Chester's gift but expressed that if Chester was sincere about apologizing, then he should have come personally. You sensed that they seemed to have made a <color=#CA2E0AFF>promise</color> to each other. Ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Chester</color> about it!",
    ["TaskDescription110309101"]="Crystal Merchant Sinclair has made it known that he is searching for the most precious of crystals, the Crystal Heart. Whoever can bring the Crystal Heart to him will be generously rewarded. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Heart</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sinclair</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110309102"]="You unexpectedly obtained the extremely rare and precious Crystal Heart that Crystal Merchant Sinclair is searching for. However, in order to verify its authenticity, Sinclair asked you to get the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Authenticator</color> from Material Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Russell</color>. Time to see Russell!",
    ["TaskDescription110309103"]="Russell told you that you're the fifth adventurer who has come to borrow his authenticator this month and he hopes that you'll be the last. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crystal Authenticator</color> back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sinclair</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110309104"]="Sinclair carefully authenticates the Crystal Heart. He thinks that what you've brought might very well be the real thing. However, he needs some Morning Dew of Yggdrasil to make the final judgment. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hydra</color> area and get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morning Dew of Yggdrasil</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110310101"]="Your relationship with Sinclair has advanced greatly since you brought the Crystal Heart to him. The two of you are now good friends. You've been pretty busy lately and haven't contacted Sinclair much, but he seems to have a surprise to share with you. Speak to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sinclair</color> and listen to what he wants to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110310102"]="Sinclair got a treasure map from somewhere but he isn't very confident about solving the riddle on it. Therefore, he asked for your help to approach two professional monster researchers, Bertha and Norten, for help. First see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bertha</color> to ask about the first half of the riddle!",
    ["TaskDescription110310103"]="Bertha immediately told you that the answer is <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vocal</color>. Next, go to Prontera <color=#CA2E0AFF>Library</color> to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Norten</color> about the second half of the riddle!",
    ["TaskDescription110310104"]="You got the answers to the riddle from Norten and Bertha. They are Vocal and Sasquatch. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go back and deliver the answers to Sinclair</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110310105"]="Sinclair deduced from that riddle that the place that the treasure map is pointing to is Labyrinth Forest, and asked you to go to the forest and bring back the <color=#CA2E0AFF>mysterious treasure</color>. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Labyrinth Forest</color> to search for the treasure!",
    ["TaskDescription110311101"]="You happened to obtain an Oliver Wolf Eyeball and heard that Headgear Merchant Ingael in Geffen is looking for this unique material. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Look for Ingael</color> and listen to his story!",
    ["TaskDescription110311102"]="Ingael has a crush on Enchanter Eufemiah. In order to show off his headgear crafting skills and tell her how he feels, Ingael asked you for the Oliver Wolf Eyeball. He also asked for your help in gathering some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolf Pelts</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Coarse Fur</color>, the materials needed to craft Oliver Wolf Headgear. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Wolf</color> area to get them!",
    ["TaskDescription110311103"]="You brought back some Wolf Pelts and Coarse Fur so Ingael can craft Oliver Wolf Headgear. Ingael asked for your help again to get some of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papyrus</color> used to infuse fragrance. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kordt Forest</color> to gather some!",
    ["TaskDescription110311104"]="Ingael successfully crafted the headgear with your help, but he still doesn't have enough courage to tell Eufemiah how he feels. Therefore, he asked you to deliver his unique gift, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Oliver Wolf Headgear</color>, to Eufemiah and find out how she feels about him.",
    ["TaskDescription110311105"]="As Eufemiah was busy running her business, she simply asked you to take <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ingael</color> a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cloak</color> as a return gift out of courtesy. Go back and explain the situation to Ingael!",
    ["TaskDescription110312101"]="As you and Ingael grew closer, you became best friends. However, he has been mad at you since his failed confession. Go <color=#CA2E0AFF>console Ingael</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110312102"]="An angry Ingael stated that you're partially responsible for his failed confession and so you are accountable for his emotional distress. He asked you to first bring him <color=#CA2E0AFF>two flagons of wine</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Juke</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110312103"]="Ingael decided to give you a chance to make it up to him on account of the wine you brought him. Eufemiah has been researching the effects that amour materials have on enchantments but she hasn't been able to get her hands on Whisper's Cloth. Therefore, Ingael promised if you're able to get <color=#CA2E0AFF>Whisper's Cloth</color> from the Treasure Ship, he'll bury the hatchet and forgive you.",
    ["TaskDescription110313101"]="As you gradually grow closer to Jimmy Lin, he shares the tales of his wonderful adventures on this continent with you. It seems that today he wants to talk to you about his impressive new friend. Head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain and talk with Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110313102"]="Jimmy Lin tells you that he has recently become acquainted with the Music Fairy, Arielle, who is also a singer. He has heard that something has been wrong with her voice recently, and has prepared a special gift to help her recover. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give Arielle the Sweet Pear Juice</color> he has prepared.",
    ["TaskDescription110313103"]="Arielle delightedly thanks you and Jimmy Lin. She tells you that she has been worried about her voice recently, as her good friend Speeka invited her to perform at the Nerius Family's banquet a month ago, and she's sure she'll disappoint her friend in her present state. She would like to ask if Jimmy Lin is willing to perform on behalf of her. Quickly go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Jimmy Lin if he's willing</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110313104"]="Hearing Arielle's plight, Jimmy Lin says he'd be glad to take part in the show. However, he has heard that the Nerius Family are nobility, and he is not sure whether he should prepare a special costume. Quickly go and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arielle to ask her</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110313105"]="Arielle is very moved when she learns that Jimmy Lin is willing to lend a hand. She tells you that he doesn't have to worry about buying a costume—as long as he pays Victor Sorrows a small deposit, he'll make Jimmy Lin a magnificent performance outfit. Take <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Gold I</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Silver I</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Victor Sorrows</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110313106"]="Victor Sorrows has heard about Jimmy Lin's performance at the Nerius Family's banquet, but he tells you that it will take a month to prepare a custom-made outfit, meaning it won't be ready for the feast next week. If you're willing to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tough Thin Pelts</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smokies</color> in Labyrinth Forest, he'll sell you another magnificent outfit he made previously.",
    ["TaskDescription110313107"]="You finally receive the perfect outfit from Victor Sorrows. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Give this magnificent performance outfit to Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110314101"]="You and Jimmy Lin have gradually become trusted partners in your journey of adventure. He often shares his worries and grievances with you, and it seems like he's worried about something today. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain to show some concern to Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110314102"]="It turns out that while Jimmy Lin was in Morroc, he got to know a chef called Stefanie, who is dedicated to improving the culinary offerings available to people living in the desert. To help Stefanie in her mission, Jimmy Lin has decided to mix up some of his delicious home-made sauce, but he still lacks some of the required materials. Help Jimmy Lin to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get some Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tails</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110314103"]="After battling in the wilderness, you finally get the required ingredients for the Special Sauce. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tails</color> back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110314104"]="Jimmy Lin tells you that in order to complete his sauce, he still needs some spices to enhance the aroma, so you suggest to Jimmy Lin that he use some of the Rosemary Orchids found on the desert borders. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rosemary Orchids for Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110314105"]="Jimmy Lin adds the Rosemary Orchids to the sauce and tastes it. Satisfied with his special sauce, he asks you to take his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Handwritten Recipe</color>, along with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Special Sauce</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stefanie</color>, in the hopes that it will help her move one step closer to achieving her dream.",
    ["TaskDescription110314106"]="You finally bring the Special Sauce and the Handwritten Recipe to Stefanie. Stefanie is incredibly moved, and thanks you and Jimmy Lin for your kindness. She then asks you to take her latest recipe using the Special Sauce to Jimmy Lin, as she hopes that he can be the first to taste it. Quickly go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver the Tasty Dish to Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110315101"]="As your connection deepens and your camaraderie grows, it feels as though you and Jimmy Lin have truly become close friends and now trust each other. He is very happy that you helped him to find all of the racing models, however, he seems to have new troubles on his mind. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go and talk with Jimmy Lin</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110315102"]="After talking to Jimmy Lin, you learn that there seems to be something wrong with the skateboard he's owned for many years. He feels sad at the thought of not being able to ride the skateboard he built his original dream upon onward and into the future. You decide to take it upon you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring Jimmy Lin's Skateboard to Whitesmith Howard</color> to find a solution.",
    ["TaskDescription110315103"]="After his preliminary examination of the skateboard, Whitesmith Howard tells you to leave it with him for further study and asks you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>library</color> to look for the Mechanic's Log. Head to the library and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eason the Librarian</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110315104"]="You manage to find the Mechanic's Log in the library. Take it back to Howard!",
    ["TaskDescription110315105"]="After Howard carefully studies the skateboard and analyzes the reference materials and principles, he concludes that a lubricant must be prepared for its bearings. He asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather 10 Goldflowers</color> to help him formulate a lubricant.",
    ["TaskDescription110315106"]="Howard finally succeeds in repairing the skateboard and sends Jimmy Lin his sincerest blessings. Take the repaired <color=#CA2E0AFF>skateboard</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Howard's blessings to Jimmy Lin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110316101"]="Your extraordinary and consistent economic savvy has attracted the attention of the Purchase Shop's senior management. They have prepared some sort of special surprise for you! Go to Jakdal's office to find out more!",
    ["TaskDescription110316102"]="Jakdal tells you that you have been placed on the Purchase Shop's list of VIP customer candidates, but to become a true VIP customer, you'll need to pass several tests. First of all, you must prove your strength to the Purchase Shop. Go and kill the Savages causing trouble for the Purchase Shop and take the Jellopies back to Jakdal.",
    ["TaskDescription110316103"]="Jakdal informs you that the Purchase Shop has recognized your strength, and the second test will test your credibility. He hands over a batch of precious goods to you and requests that you take them to the merchant, Vienna Lindra, on behalf of the Purchase Shop. You must then bring back the Trade Agreement she has signed with the Purchase Shop.",
    ["TaskDescription110316104"]="You successfully deliver the goods to Vienna Lindra and retrieve the agreement. Now, take the Trade Agreement back to Jakdal!",
    ["TaskDescription110317101"]="After becoming a regular customer of the Purchase Shop, you gradually become close to Jakdal, and discover that he is not as boring as he seems to be on the surface. As you become friends, you occasionally talk about more trivial matters. However, Jakdal seems to be preoccupied with some mysterious matter recently and rarely has time to talk with you. Go and ask him what's going on.",
    ["TaskDescription110317102"]="Jakdal looks hesitant to speak his mind and seems to be hiding something. However, you can tell from his words that he seems to have grown very close to Victor Sorrows recently. Go and find Victor Sorrows to find out more.",
    ["TaskDescription110317103"]="You find out from Victor Sorrows that Jakdal secretly ordered a customized outfit here, which seems to hold some special significance to him. However, crafting this extravagant outfit will be very time-consuming, and Victor tells you that if you want to shorten its production time, you can fetch him certain materials, including Kobold Hair, Gold I, and Silver I.",
    ["TaskDescription110317104"]="With your help, Victor Sorrows successfully finishes making the outfit, but Jakdal seems to be too busy to come and collect it. Why don't you bring this outfit to Jakdal and give him a surprise?",
    ["TaskDescription110318101"]="You happen to receive a Meteor Shard from Phreeoni, and recall hearing that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera's</color> greatest blacksmith, Hollgrehenn, is searching high and low for shards just like this one. You should go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for Hollgrehenn to ask him</color> what he's up to.",
    ["TaskDescription110318102"]="You find out from Hollgrehenn that it's actually his old friend, the Magic Furnace, who needs Meteor Shards. It turns out that the Magic Furnace's original owner left it a Riddle Box, promising the Magic Furnace that it would see him again on the day it solved the riddle. The shard in your hand is essential for creating the Starlight Key required to solve the Riddle Box. Go now and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give</color> this <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meteor Shard to the Magic Furnace</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110318103"]="The Magic Furnace is delighted to receive the Meteor Shard. According to Hollgrehenn's translation, you know that you'll need a few other materials to create the Starlight Key. First and foremost, you'll need to gather <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rotten Solid Trunks</color> from Elder Willows. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> to look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elder Willows</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110318104"]="Hollgrehenn tells you that, in order to craft the Starlight Key, you'll need <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 pieces of Iron Ore</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>5 pieces of Muspellium</color>. Only when these materials have been gathered can the Starlight Key be forged.",
    ["TaskDescription110318105"]="With your help, the Magic Furnace finally gathers all of the materials it needs to make the Starlight Key. Now that the Starlight Key has been forged, <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask the Magic Furnace and Hollgrehenn</color> what you should do next.",
    ["TaskDescription110318106"]="Hollgrehenn takes out the Riddle Box. Quickly, <color=#CA2E0AFF>use</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Starlight Key in your hand</color> to open the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Riddle Box</color>, and see what kind of riddle the Magic Furnace's master left behind!",
    ["TaskDescription110319101"]="The Magic Furnace suddenly becomes very excited. What could possible be going on? Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask the Magic Furnace</color> and its friend, Hollgrehenn!",
    ["TaskDescription110319102"]="You learn from Hollgrehenn that all of the materials for the Revelation of Starlight have been collected, and the Magic Furnace is very excited at the prospect of seeing its owner again. However, the revelation does not mention anything about how to use it. Hollgrehenn asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>inquire</color> with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera's</color> Material Merchant <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sampson</color>, who seems to have researched this sort of thing extensively.",
    ["TaskDescription110319103"]="You learn from the Material Merchant Sampson that the Revelation of Starlight is in fact the formula for an ancient magic potion, but if you want to find out how to use it, you'll have to go to the Library and find the researcher, Norton, to borrow A Compendium of Ancient Medicinal Formulas. Now, go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera's</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>library and find Norten</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110319104"]="After hearing you out, Norten finally agreed to lend you A Compendium of Ancient Medicinal Formulas. Go to the bookshelf behind Norton <color=#CA2E0AFF>to obtain and read A Compendium of Ancient Medicinal Formulas!</color>",
    ["TaskDescription110319105"]="You get the information you need from the book. It turns out that the Revelation of Starlight holds the formula for Revenant Water. In order to craft this special potion, in addition to the materials already hinted at in the Revelation of Starlight, you'll also need a Sasquatch Bone as a container. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to where the Sasquatches dwell</color> and get a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sasquatch Bone</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110319106"]="You finally help the Magic Furnace to collect all of the materials. You then tell the Magic Furnace and Hollgrehenn about the container and mixing requirements. Now, you must be patient and <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait for the Revenant Water to be concocted</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110320101"]="As you get to know Schumann better, he also shares with you his amazing experiences in this continent, and it seems that today he wants to talk to you about the new friends he has made! Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain and talk to Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110320102"]="Schumann tells you that he has recently become acquainted with the Music Fairy, Arielle, who is also a singer. He has heard that something has been wrong with her voice recently, and has prepared a special gift to help her recover. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give Arielle the Sweet Pear Juice</color> he has prepared.",
    ["TaskDescription110320103"]="Arielle delightedly thanks you and Schumann. She tells you that she has been worried about her voice recently, as her good friend Speeka invited her to perform at the Nerius Family's banquet a month ago, and she's sure she'll disappoint her friend in her present state. She would like to ask if Schumann is willing to perform on her behalf. Quickly go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Schumann if he's willing</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110320104"]="Hearing Arielle's plight, Schumann says he'd be glad to take part in the show. However, he has heard that the Nerius Family are nobility, and he is not sure whether he should prepare a special costume. Quickly go and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Arielle and ask her</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110320105"]="Arielle is very moved when she learns that Schumann is willing to lend a hand. She tells you that he doesn't have to worry about buying a costume—as long as he pays Victor Sorrows a small deposit, he'll make Schumann a magnificent performance outfit. Take <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Gold I</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>10 Silver I</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Victor Sorrows</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110320106"]="Victor Sorrows has heard about Schumann's performance at the Nerius Family's banquet, but he tells you that it will take a month to prepare a custom-made outfit, meaning it won't be ready for the feast next week. If you're willing to get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tough Thin Pelts</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Smokies</color> in Labyrinth Forest, he'll sell you another magnificent outfit he made previously.",
    ["TaskDescription110320107"]="You finally receive the perfect outfit from Victor Sorrows. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Give this magnificent performance outfit to Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110321101"]="You and Schumann have gradually become trusted partners in your journey of adventure. He often shares his worries and grievances with you, and it seems like he's worried about something today. Go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain to show some concern to Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110321102"]="It turns out that while Schumann was in Morroc, he got to know a chef called Stefanie, who is dedicated to improving the culinary offerings available to people living in the desert. To help Stefanie in her mission, Schumann has decided to mix up some of his delicious home-made sauce, but he still lacks some of the required materials. Help Schumann to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get some Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tails</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110321103"]="After battling in the wilderness, you finally get the required ingredients for the Special Sauce. Take the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Muka Juice</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phen Tails</color> back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110321104"]="Schumann tells you that in order to complete his sauce, he still needs some spices to enhance the aroma, so you suggest to Schumann that he use some of the Rosemary Orchids found on the desert borders. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather</color> some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rosemary Orchids for Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110321105"]="Schumann adds the Rosemary Orchids to the sauce and tastes it. Satisfied with his special sauce, he asks you to take his <color=#CA2E0AFF>Handwritten Recipe</color>, along with the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Special Sauce</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stefanie</color>, in the hopes that it will help her move one step closer to achieving her dream.",
    ["TaskDescription110321106"]="You finally bring the Special Sauce and the Handwritten Recipe to Stefanie. Stefanie is incredibly moved, and thanks you and Schumann for your kindness. She then asks you to take her latest recipe using the Special Sauce to Schumann, as she hopes that he can be the first to taste it. Quickly go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>deliver the Tasty Dish to Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110322101"]="As your connection deepens and your camaraderie grows, it feels as though you and Schumann have truly become close friends and now trust each other. He is very happy that you helped him to find all of the racing models, however, he seems to have new troubles on his mind. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go and talk with Schumann</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110322102"]="After talking to Schumann, you learn that there seems to be something wrong with the skateboard he's owned for many years. He feels sad at the thought of not being able to ride the skateboard he built his original dream upon onward and into the future. You decide to take it upon you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>bring Schumann's Skateboard to Whitesmith Howard</color> to find a solution.",
    ["TaskDescription110322103"]="After his preliminary examination of the skateboard, Mastersmith Howard tells you to leave it with him for further study and asks you to go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>library</color> to look for the Mechanic's Log. Head to the library and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eason the Librarian</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110322104"]="You manage to find the Mechanic's Log in the library. Take it back to Howard!",
    ["TaskDescription110322105"]="After Howard carefully studies the skateboard and analyzes the reference materials and principles, he concludes that a lubricant must be prepared for its bearings. He asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>gather 10 Goldflowers</color> to help him formulate a lubricant.",
    ["TaskDescription110322106"]="Howard finally succeeds in repairing the skateboard and sends Schumann his sincerest blessings. Take the repaired <color=#CA2E0AFF>skateboard</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Howard's blessings to Schumann</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110323101"]="You notice that Kao seems a bit down lately. Is there a way to cheer her up?",
    ["TaskDescription110323102"]="It turns out that she is into spooky places. There are a number of spooky places here. But which one to pick?",
    ["TaskDescription110323103"]="You picked Munak Cave, the Pyramid, and the Geffen, and brought pictures of these places for Kao to choose.",
    ["TaskDescription110323104"]="Kao says that she wants to go all three of them. But this time she wishes to visit the nearest one, Munak Cave. She has always been curious about what it is like inside.",
    ["TaskDescription110323105"]="You take a lot of photographs. But Kao ventures alone into the depths of the cave. If you do nothing, she might be in danger...",
    ["TaskDescription110324101"]="You find a dog trapped in the sand. After you save it, it seems...",
    ["TaskDescription110324102"]="Since you're a stranger, the dog ran off! That's not good. What if it ran into some monsters?",
    ["TaskDescription110324103"]="You defeated the golem and saved the dog. Luckily, the dog is not hurt. But it seems to have something to tell you...",
    ["TaskDescription110324104"]="You follow the dog to Ant Cavern. What is it trying to tell you?",
    ["TaskDescription110324105"]="You have rescued the cat and dog from danger. Now, the priority is to find their owner.",
    ["TaskDescription110325101"]="Heflee and you have noticed that Pattie has been feeling a bit down lately. That is not good.",
    ["TaskDescription110325102"]="After discussing it, you decide to give Pattie a surprise. Of course, you are the one doing the legwork.",
    ["TaskDescription110325103"]="You have finished half of the preparations. Next up...",
    ["TaskDescription110325104"]="You have all the materials. Now, head back to Heflee.",
    ["TaskDescription110325105"]="You have made a beautiful wreath. All you need to do is to surprise Pattie. But she seems...",
    ["TaskDescription110326101"]="You enter Desert Green Tavern, but the place is empty. The owner seems frustrated. What's going on?",
    ["TaskDescription110326102"]="You agree to investigate for Heflee, but you have no leads. Perhaps you should ask around first.",
    ["TaskDescription110326103"]="A girl with an unknown name has suddenly appeared around Morroc. She seems to be the reason why fewer people have been visiting the tavern. What should you do about her?",
    ["TaskDescription110326104"]="You boldly take a photo of the girl and bring it to Heflee. What will she decide?",
    ["TaskDescription110326105"]="Heflee suddenly suggests having the girl stay at Desert Green Tavern. You don't know whether this is a good or bad idea, but regardless, she sends you to talk with the girl.",
    ["TaskDescription110327101"]="Rowan seems to want to talk to you about something, but it's probably about The TOYS...",
    ["TaskDescription110327102"]="It turns out The TOYS is a restless adventurer who always has endless enthusiasm for the things of this world. Rowan asks you to satisfy his thirst for adventure.",
    ["TaskDescription110327103"]="You agree to Rowan's request. To your surprise, The TOYS was expecting this. You decide on a route for your journey and set off.",
    ["TaskDescription110327104"]="You travel through Morroc and Payon. Time flies by, but The TOYS shows no signs of tiredness.",
    ["TaskDescription110327105"]="As your journey comes to a close, The TOYS suggests bringing a souvenir for Rowan, but little do you know...",
    ["TaskDescription110328101"]="Rowan looks a bit sad. What could have happened after leaving the Library?",
    ["TaskDescription110328102"]="Rowan's does not know much about the pen pal he lost contact with, though he worries greatly about his safety. Would the courier know anything about what's going on?",
    ["TaskDescription110328103"]="As you arere gathering information, you hear a loud sound coming from Labyrinth Forest. You had better check if anything is wrong.",
    ["TaskDescription110328104"]="The man who fell is quite peculiar and keeps talking to himself. All you can do is take him to Rowan. There might be some connection between these two things.",
    ["TaskDescription110328105"]="The TOYS开启任务描述5",
    ["TaskDescription110329101"]="It looks like Miss W caused an accident during today's teleport...",
    ["TaskDescription110329102"]="Over W's place, you encounter a guest from the Parallel World who is not on the teleport list, Kim Heechul. W is embarrassed, and she activates the Kafra Corporation's teleport backtrace function, asking you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>accompany Kim Heechul for the teleport</color> in case he can't find his way back to Prontera if it fails...",
    ["TaskDescription110329103"]="The teleport fails again. W is so upset and suggests you all <color=#CA2E0AFF>see Wolmas the Arch Bishop</color>. Maybe the church has an explanation for all these...",
    ["TaskDescription110329104"]="After listening to the story, Wolmas thinks that the teleport backtrace is working to some extent but lacks a corresponding coordinate of Kim Heechul's world. The Dimensional Gap that appears out of nowhere was the root of this incident, and now the priority is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>shut down the Dimensional Gap created by the forceful traceback</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110329105"]="After shutting down the Dimensional Gap, you and Kim Heechul return and see Wolmas the Arch Bishop again; a familiar figure is standing next to him...",
    ["TaskDescription110330101"]="There is glimmering light coming out of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon teleport circle</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110330102"]="The guest turns out to be Kim Heechul! He heard that the Hundred Wine Gala, which only takes place once every five years, is hosting in Payon Seocho Market right now. That's why he asks W to send him over. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take Kim Heechul to see Albel</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110330103"]="You both see the host of the Hundred Wine Gala, Albel. She explains the rules for Drink-Up and asks you two to search for a wine merchant named Li Zhuo. According to Albel, Li Zhuo arrived at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon South</color> yesterday but is still not showing up.",
    ["TaskDescription110330104"]="You two discover Li Zhuo, who is in a paralysis state at Payon South. On his way here, he accidentally inhaled the Numb-Numb Powder released by the Spore. Luckily, the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Flower of Dawn carried by Willow</color> nearby can save him from this. Let's help out this poor wine merchant for the sake of Thousand-Year Wine!",
    ["TaskDescription110330105"]="Even after taking the Flower of Dawn, Li Zhuo still has difficulty moving. The Hundred Wine Gala is about to start, and he wants you guys to bring these two pots of Thousand-Year Wine <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Payon</color> first, and he will be there shortly. Before you go, he assures both of you that he will be there. Thousand-Year Wine, one for winning, and one for drinking! He will get there since he has found himself the drinking buddy!",
    ["TaskDescription110331101"]="You missed Heechul every time. Someone said he has been going to the Royal Chivalry lately...",
    ["TaskDescription110331102"]="You see Kim Heechul, who is checking out the Royal Chivalry. It turns out he is brainstorming ideas for his performance at the Knighthood ceremony. Only if he could receive help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Hallam</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110331103"]="Captain Hallam says yes to the two of you and advises you to start with the knight spirit if you want to learn more about knight. A king's glory symbolizes a knight's glory, as he suggests you two visit the <color=#CA2E0AFF>magnificent palace</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110331104"]="After you two are done touring the palace, Captain Hallam advises you to look at the knight cemetery behind the church. Before that, the two of you must <color=#CA2E0AFF>obtain clear water from Central Fountain</color> and a bunch of memorial flowers from Margaret.",
    ["TaskDescription110331105"]="With the memorial flowers, you arrive at the resting place of knights...",
    ["TaskDescription110332101"]="Exchanging gifts between friends is very popular in Prontera lately... It looks like Kim Heechul has a gift for you!",
    ["TaskDescription110332102"]="Heechul did prepare a gift for you, but what kind of things should you exchange for it? During a conversation, you discover Heechul is fond of an item named \"game console.\" Maybe <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesqurienne</color> has a way of getting it.",
    ["TaskDescription110332103"]="You ask Jesqurienne for help, and she introduces the Materialization Crystal under the Geffen Tower to you. She can materialize the game console from Heechul's memory with a good amount of Materialization Crystals. Now you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>set off to Geffen Tower...",
    ["TaskDescription110332104"]="Finally, you have gathered all the Materialization Crystals you need. Now take Heechul back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower</color> and finish off the crafting ritual.",
    ["TaskDescription110332105"]="You guys have finished the crafting of the game console. Maybe now is the time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>exchange gifts</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription110333101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Xavier</color> makes a wish under the Wishing Tree, hoping to get an infinite amount of dried fish! And the magical Wishing Tree responds to his wish...",
    ["TaskDescription110333102"]="Xavier points at the girl under the Wishing Tree excitedly and says that she must be the angel sent by Odin to fulfill his wish. But Xavier is too shy to talk to her and wants you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>have a conversation with the angel under the Wishing Tree</color> and claim those dried fish for him!",
    ["TaskDescription110333103"]="This mysterious girl is a guest who came from the Parallel World named Lim Yoona. The starving Xavier starts rolling on the ground after learning the truth. In any case, let's feed this kitten something first.",
    ["TaskDescription110333104"]="Through you and Lim Yoona's efforts, Xavier finally stops crying. When he recalls the embarrassing acts he did just now, he decides to take you two <color=#CA2E0AFF>to the Rose Red Tavern</color>. Of course, this is not about the food that can fill up his stomach.",
    ["TaskDescription110334101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Yoona</color> seems a little bit down today. Go ask her what is going on...",
    ["TaskDescription110334102"]="It's because the pet trainer, Taksch, asked Yoona to take care of his dog, Nasir, while he's out for training. But yesterday, Nasir ran off and is still missing up to this point. You guys decide to split up and look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nasir</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110334103"]="You guys follow the clues, keep looking, and see this at the Prontera South Gate...",
    ["TaskDescription110334104"]="At the Prontera South Gate, you guys see Taksch, who returns early, and Nasir is next to him playing. While celebrating for the fortunate, you discover Yoona is still upset about something...",
    ["TaskDescription110334105"]="You learn that Yoona also has a dog named Leo, which wasn't with Yoona when she teleported to Midgard. Yoona asks you to find a way to let her meet with Leo or at least help her to send some pet supplies to Leo... You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Wolmas the Arch Bishop</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110334106"]="Wolmas the Arch Bishop listens to the request patiently and tells you there is no fixed pattern of when the Dimensional Gap will appear, and he can't predict the time for the next teleport. Maybe you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>purchase the pet supplies</color>, go to the Wishing Tree, and try to send them by making a wish. You two decide to give it a try.",
    ["TaskDescription110335101"]="The friendship between you and Yoona has improved significantly since the last time you both made the wish to send Leo the pet supplies through the Wishing Tree. This time, what kind of bond will develop between both of you?",
    ["TaskDescription110335102"]="In the library, you bump into Lim Yoona, who is talking to Rowan, and find out there is a book that she really wants to borrow. Rowan tells her a guy named Heye has borrowed tons of books and should still be at the library. If you don't mind the hassle, go ahead and <color=#CA2E0AFF>look for him in the library</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription110335103"]="You find Heye in the library eventually, and this young man has a huge passion for acting. He agrees to lend the book to you only after you have proven you are passionate about acting too. Both of you managed to answer every single question correctly. Now, it's time for him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>fulfill his promise</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription110335104"]="Heye hands over the book reluctantly and starts to talk about his past. He is an actor from Morroc and is here for the acting contest held by the Rune Kingdom. It's getting close to the contest day, and he is getting increasingly stressed out, so he locks himself in the library. He now has nothing but high expectations from his teacher, not even a decent <color=#CA2E0AFF>formal outfit</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110335105"]="You both decide to help out Heye and solve the formal outfit problem. After gathering all these materials, Polly tells you she can't deliver a new formal outfit before the contest. But she is willing to give out an old outfit for free. This is the first outfit she made when she first became the premium tailor, and she hopes it can help this young man on his first performance on stage.",
    ["TaskDescription110336101"]="How wonderful it is to get together with your friends and cook!",
    ["TaskDescription110336102"]="During the conversation, Lim Yoona introduces you to a dish of the Parallel World named Kimchi Stew and says she will get you the first piece of meat when it's done. But before that, you guys need a pot and many ingredients... Maybe Hollgrehenn can craft one?",
    ["TaskDescription110336103"]="Consider it is halfway done when you have a high-quality pot. Now you may <color=#CA2E0AFF>prepare vegetables</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110336104"]="The next will be the meat; the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Savage Babe Meat</color> at Prontera West Gate is said to be delicious, has just the right amount of fat, and is suitable for making bacon...",
    ["TaskDescription110336105"]="After gathering all the ingredients, you can start preparing this delicious Kimchi Stew! Now go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Parrot Mailbox and send your invitations</color>. Let's wait for your guests to show up!",
    ["TaskDescription110401101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lil' Kitty</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110402101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sapir</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110403101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hobson</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110404101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Quincy</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110405101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Stella</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110406101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mewliea</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110407101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Blake</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110408101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Elvira</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110409101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mewkus</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110410101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Benjiah</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110411101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nastia</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110412101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mewcia</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110413101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tracy</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110414101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eudora</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110415101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mewleta</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110416101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Gardner</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110417101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eufemiah</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what she has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110418101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mewlande</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110419101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master, Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>white quality One-Handed Weapons</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110420101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>white quality Two-handed Weapons</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110421101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>white quality Off-hand Weapons</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110422101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>white quality Daggers</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
