    ["TaskDescription110440101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Daggers</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110441101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Armor</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110442101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Cloaks</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110443101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Shoes</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110444101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Accessories</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110445101"]="With your help the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Magic Furnace</color> has obtained a new power, and once again is in the hands of its master Swick. It seems it can help you increase the refining success rate or reduce the consumption of refining materials of <color=#CA2E0AFF>purple or orange quality Talismans</color>. However, it seems you'll first need to help the furnace collect some materials to exert this new power.",
    ["TaskDescription110446101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kayden</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110447101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Beth</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110448101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meoffel</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110449101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Klein</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110450101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Welch</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110451101"]="Your relationship with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mistley</color> grows deeper with every encounter you share. You have finally become trusted friends! Go and find out what he has to tell you!",
    ["TaskDescription110501101"]="You've finally completed your vow ceremony and found your soulmate, but before the big day, there are many things you still need to take care of...",
    ["TaskDescription110501102"]="Archbishop Wolmas explains the wedding process to you. Before the wedding, you'll also need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>customize your wedding outfit</color> and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>someone suitable to be your witness</color>. On the advice of Archbishop Wolmas, you head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>west of Prontera</color> to find the famed legendary outfit designer.",
    ["TaskDescription110501103"]="You ask Mewt to make a custom outfit for you, but he turns you down. Something seems to be bothering him, but he is unable to explain it to you. As you converse, you learn that Mewt's grandson, Jimmy, went out to play earlier, but he hasn't returned yet. You offer to help, for which Mewt is very grateful. He tells you that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jimmy</color> should be playing with his friends in the field <color=#CA2E0AFF>outside Prontera West Gate</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110501104"]="You find a group of children in the field outside Prontera West Gate, but you don't see Jimmy. You ask around and find out that Jimmy had an argument with his friends while playing earlier, and stormed off in a bad mood. It's getting late. You have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Jimmy</color> as soon as possible.",
    ["TaskDescription110501105"]="You find Jimmy lost in the Ghastly Cemetery. He reveals that this is where his grandmother was buried. After he lost his irreplaceable soulmate, his grandfather became a shadow of his former self. Hoping to bring some joy into his life, Jimmy begs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture for him</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription110501106"]="You finally bring Jimmy back to Mewt. Jimmy now has a lot he needs to discuss with his grandfather...",
    ["TaskDescription110501107"]="With your help, it seems that Mewt is finally ready for a new beginning. To express his thanks, he offers to make your wedding outfits. As long as you help him to collect the materials, he promises that he'll make the most gorgeous outfits you've ever seen in the whole of Prontera.",
    ["TaskDescription110501108"]="You finally have your wedding outfits... Now, the only thing apart from the vow ceremony and the wedding is...?",
    ["TaskDescription110502101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you and your partner, and you send them an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and give a wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription110503101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you, and you send him an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription110504101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you, and you send him an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription110505101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you, and you send him an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription110506101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you, and you send him an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription110507101"]="At the suggestion of Archbishop Wolmas, you choose a witness who can clearly see the feelings between you, and you send him an invitation to preside over the vow ceremony and wedding speech...",
    ["TaskDescription11100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Knight!",
    ["TaskDescription111002201"]="Follow the academy recruiter's directions and take a tour of Izlude Island!",
    ["TaskDescription11110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription11200"]="2nd Class - Crusader",
    ["TaskDescription11210"]="A long-awaited peace had returned to Prontera. Busy laughter reigned in the city streets as a major public works program under the royal family worked to clean up all traces of the troubles. Yet I have been summoned by the Great Sage. He seems to be planning something.",
    ["TaskDescription117014101"]="I'll return to the Mjolnir Mountains and show Master Sage Kroneika the results of my training!",
    ["TaskDescription117016301"]="I gave the issue of whether to pursue the life of a Monk much thought after leaving Payon. Now I would like to submit my answer to Master <color=#CA2E0AFF>Peerless Jin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117501301"]="To better protect my companions, it's time to seek new power from advancement!",
    ["TaskDescription117501302"]="Your travels have taught you all basic combat techniques appropriate to a professional Swordsman. But you'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> your master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color>, to hone these skills further!",
    ["TaskDescription117502301"]="Knight... Hmm, sounds like a title filled with honor and glory. Let's go learn more.",
    ["TaskDescription117502302"]="Make the Pecopeco happy?... It won't hurt to go ask.",
    ["TaskDescription117502303"]="The pumpkin pie for the Pecopeco is finished. I hope it's okay...",
    ["TaskDescription117503301"]="So you wish to become a Crusader, do you? In that case, I believe a <color=#CA2E0AFF>visit</color> to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Crusader Captain</color> currently stationed in Prontera to be in order!",
    ["TaskDescription117503302"]="You convinced the Crusader Captain of your enthusiasm after a heart-felt discussion, yet he would seek to qualify you further with little test before approving a Class Advancement. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the Mjolnir Mountains</color> and accept what he has fashioned for you!",
    ["TaskDescription117503303"]="The Crusader Captain wished to test your resolve with an arduous task: <color=#CA2E0AFF>moving supplies to the Sage Hut at the top of the mountain</color>. A sure test of your limits, but remember—risk and reward often go hand-in-hand! So, what do you choose?",
    ["TaskDescription117504301"]="I've become adept at manipulating the elements. Where can I go to learn new magic?",
    ["TaskDescription117505301"]="A Wizard? Manipulating the elements to destroy the enemy... Sounds awesome! Let's find out more!",
    ["TaskDescription117505302"]="I've run into a slight complication while trying to obtain the Mana Crystals...",
    ["TaskDescription117505303"]="Only having fragments of the crystal... I wonder what Iskren will do with the fragments?",
    ["TaskDescription117506101"]="Master Charles has advised me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek Great Sage Kroneika's help</color>. I will depart for the Mjolnir Mountains immediately to learn everything I need to know to become a Sage.",
    ["TaskDescription117506102"]="After proving my determination to Great Sage Kroneika, he wanted me to develop my own knowledge system from the magic I have learned and complete an essay. I can go to the Prontera Library to seek the help of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Norten and Lawrence</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117506103"]="Norten recommended many different literatures to me. Anyway, I better start by <color=#CA2E0AFF>reading books</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117506104"]="While I was reading books, the scholar Lawrence gave me completely different advice than Norten... In the end, I decided to <color=#CA2E0AFF>write the essay</color> the way I wanted to.",
    ["TaskDescription117507301"]="The Holy Light has become a part of my soul. How do I make use of its power?",
    ["TaskDescription117507302"]="I have reached the very end of the path of the Acolyte. It's time to return to Criatura Academy and <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Master Alice</color> for help...",
    ["TaskDescription117508301"]="Healing teammates with Holy Light... I'd really like that! Go to the archbishop to learn more about being a Priest!",
    ["TaskDescription117508302"]="As a Priest, exorcising the spirits of the dead is also a necessary duty.",
    ["TaskDescription117508303"]="The ghosts aren't all evil... If I can help fulfill their wishes, that would be better than destroying them, right?",
    ["TaskDescription117509301"]="Master Alice has advised me to <color=#CA2E0AFF>consult Master Peerless Jin</color> for my Monk Class Advancement, whom I can find in Payon.",
    ["TaskDescription117509302"]="It appeared that Peerless Jin of Payon had long awaited my arrival. We will prepare the special Purification Elixir for my Class Advancement once I prove my dedication to the Way of the Monk. But first of all, I need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect some Beast Blood</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117510301"]="Arrows are my best companions, but they're not enough...",
    ["TaskDescription117511301"]="Hunters. I heard they're loners with bows, arrows and falcons as their companions. Let's find out more about them.",
    ["TaskDescription117511302"]="The mission of the Payon archer... General, so this place involves such an important mission?",
    ["TaskDescription117511303"]="So the Hunters have this kind of past... Protecting the world. Isn't that what an adventurer aspiring to be a hero is supposed to do?",
    ["TaskDescription117514301"]="Continue hiding in the darkness or look for another way? Go inquire for more information...",
    ["TaskDescription117515301"]="Moving in the shadows... That seems really cool! But is the Assassin job really like this? Go ask to learn more!",
    ["TaskDescription117515302"]="What exactly is this request? Is it a trial or...?",
    ["TaskDescription117515303"]="Adhering to your sense of justice and never going astray... This is the essence of an Assassin.",
    ["TaskDescription117516301"]="I should head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Green Tavern</color> right now and deliver master the recommendation letter from Moxie.",
    ["TaskDescription117516302"]="You hand over the recommendation letter to Rogge, a leader of Rogues. He agrees to let you join them on one condition: you'll need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>teach McGille, a black market merchant, a lesson</color> as your token of allegiance.",
    ["TaskDescription117516303"]="The black market merchant McGille learned his lesson. Now, listen to Rogge the Great's <color=#CA2E0AFF>conversation with McGille</color>. After all, this new boss said he would handle the rest.",
    ["TaskDescription117516304"]="In the conversation, it is clear that Rogge the Great and McGille harbor deep-seated resentments for each other, and they both have powerful ones behind their backs. Lamy, who got beaten up last night, finally ignited this drama. In order to inform the agent that the business has been handled, Rogge the Great sends you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>port on Izlude Island</color> after questioning McGille.",
    ["TaskDescription117517301"]="Hmm, what if I could make money more efficiently? Why not ask him about it?",
    ["TaskDescription117518301"]="Being a Blacksmith that's always surrounded by the clanging of metal... Seems like they would have strong bodies... Can I become like them too?",
    ["TaskDescription117518302"]="Kick boxing... with Skel Pirates? The Blacksmith Instructor is a real interesting guy.",
    ["TaskDescription117519301"]="I should <color=#CA2E0AFF>head to Al De Baran</color> right now and learn from Nicolas how to become an Alchemist.",
    ["TaskDescription117519302"]="After some conversation, Nicolas told me that if I managed to make an Alchemy Potion, I would be qualified to become an Alchemist. Now, I need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Mjolnir Dead Pit 1F</color> to gather the required materials.",
    ["TaskDescription117519303"]="I successfully acquired the first two materials, and Nicolas told me that the last one, which is Hardened Soul, required the Soul Fixer from Ivy. He asked Ivy to meet me at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Dead Pit 1F</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117519304"]="With the Hardened Soul in hand, I can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Al De Baran</color> and begin making the Alchemy Potion under Nicolas' guidance!",
    ["TaskDescription117520301"]="Recently, there seems to be a lot of unrest in the Rune Kingdom...",
    ["TaskDescription117520302"]="All the Mana Crystal mines are in danger of having their seals broken.",
    ["TaskDescription117520303"]="When Mjolnir Mine is facing trouble, and the area of Morroc is also unsafe.",
    ["TaskDescription117520304"]="The real culprit has been revealed. Baphomet's ambitions must be thwarted!",
    ["TaskDescription117521301"]="It appears that something new has happened at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> — the infamous place where many stories are buried. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rockley</color> is waiting anxiously for your help...",
    ["TaskDescription117521302"]="Rockley tells you all about the latest oddities. It is said that several adventurers who went to the Glast Heim Churchyard to investigate are now missing, and the cause of this could be due to the mysterious <color=#CA2E0AFF>Horong</color>. After accepting this mission, you rushed immediately to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Churchyard</color>, and started your <color=#CA2E0AFF>investigation</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117521303"]="Upon arriving at the Glast Heim Churchyard, you encounter the so-called Horong that is rumored to make people disappear. As soon as you get close, your surroundings immediately change! You heard an <color=#CA2E0AFF>ethereal female voice</color>, and she appeared to be trying to guide you to do something...",
    ["TaskDescription117521304"]="You worshipped the Weeping Goddess Statue under the guidance of that mysterious voice. She has now given you <color=#CA2E0AFF>new instructions</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117521305"]="You defeated the monsters near the Garden of Sorrows as guided by that mysterious voice — now she appears to be calling your name yet again...",
    ["TaskDescription117521306"]="After completing the three trials, the mysterious voice finally unveils its true self. She claims to be a Valkyrie named Shikoti, and entrusts you with a slab engraved with strange characters. Upon picking up the slate, your surroundings change again...",
    ["TaskDescription117521307"]="Upon returning to the Glast Heim, Rockley couldn't believe that you were at the Glast Heim Churchyard for so long, and that seven days had already passed. You explain all the details to Rockley — he suggests that you take the Stone Slab and visit Wolmas the Archbishop, as he might know something more about these strange characters. Rockley also mentioned the characters being something about divine power and wisdom...",
    ["TaskDescription117522301"]="When your job level reaches 70, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>. He will help you prepare for your Job Advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117522302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117522303"]="Yadrew appreciates your efforts and progress, and wants you to follow him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ant Cavern</color> in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sograt Desert</color>. Over there is where you will learn to be a great <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rune Knight</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117522304"]="You follow Yadrew to the entrance of the Ant Cavern, and now you face your biggest challenge. You must rely on your own strength to <color=#CA2E0AFF>defeat</color> every single <color=#CA2E0AFF>Monster</color> that stands in your way, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach</color> the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Abyssal Maw</color> in the deepest part of the cave...",
    ["TaskDescription117522305"]="It is said that every Rune Knight must have a dragon of their own, which is why Yadrew had you go get your own Dragon Egg. With your new companion, you can now go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117523301"]="When your job level reaches 70, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>. He will help you prepare for your Job Advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117523302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moxie</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117523303"]="Moxie appreciates your efforts and progress, and wants you to follow her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Dead Pit</color>. Over there is where you will learn to be a great <color=#CA2E0AFF>Guillotine Cross</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117523304"]="You follow Moxie to the Mjolnir Dead Pit. She asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the contents in the treasure chests</color> in the cave <color=#CA2E0AFF>without alarming Giearth</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117523305"]="The treasure chests of Moxie's request have finally all been explored! Now head to the 1st floor, find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lift</color> as soon as possible, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>give Moxie</color> the treasure's contents!",
    ["TaskDescription117523306"]="You've worked effortlessly to complete Moxie's trial, but she is evilly trying to make things more difficult for you. It seems that if you don't complete her request, you won't get what you want...",
    ["TaskDescription117523307"]="You've finally passed Moxie's trial, obtaining a recipe that can enhance the potency of the poison, and have also exercised your ability to hide your breath. Now you can return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117524301"]="When your job level reaches <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>, he will help you prepare for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117524302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hamid</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117524303"]="In order to not to let you disturb him from making money, Hamid has decided to help you complete your job advancement preparations as soon as possible. Under his lead, you both <color=#CA2E0AFF>set foot towards Glast Heim St. Abbey</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117524304"]="Hamid tells you that the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mechanical Magic Core</color> is essential if you wish to become a true Mechanic. Hamid, as lazy as always, hopes that you can be <color=#CA2E0AFF>self-sufficient</color>, and get this crucial item from <color=#CA2E0AFF>ancient Mech Monsters</color>by yourself...",
    ["TaskDescription117524305"]="After defeating a large number of Mech Monsters, you have finally obtained your own Mechanical Magic Core. Now you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117525301"]="When your job level reaches <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>, he will help you prepare for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117525302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117525303"]="Alice appreciates your efforts and progress, and wants you to follow her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>. Over there is where you will learn to be a great <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archbishop</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117525304"]="You followed Alice to Glast Heim, but whilst on the journey, an accident happened — causing the tome in Alice's hands to be damaged. In order to help Alice repair it, you must retrieve the scattered <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ancient Tome Fragments</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Carat</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Majoruros</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117525305"]="You helped Alice finish repairing the tome, and she thanks you. She also tells you that someone is waiting for you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Palace Square of Glast Heim</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117525306"]="Under Alice's instructions, you open the unnamed tome — and begin to <color=#CA2E0AFF>tell</color> that one very familiar <color=#CA2E0AFF>story</color> of yours...",
    ["TaskDescription117525307"]="With all the things Alice has given you, you now feel the entire weight of responsibility on your shoulders. You should <color=#CA2E0AFF>go back to Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117526301"]="When your job level reaches <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>, he will help you prepare for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117526302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117526303"]="Charles appreciates your efforts and progress, and wants you to follow him to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen</color>. Over there is where you will learn to be a great <color=#CA2E0AFF>Warlock</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117526304"]="You followed Charles' instruction to fill the element vessel. During this process, you can feel your ability to control the elements improving. Maybe it's time you should go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Tower's 2nd underground floor</color> to meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color> again...",
    ["TaskDescription117526305"]="Charles and the elders of the Pentagram have helped you with all their might. In this trial, you found that your understanding of the elements has deepened. Now you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117527301"]="When your job level reaches <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>, please visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>, he will help you prepare for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117527302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Melbrun</color>, and receive guidance for your job advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117527303"]="Melbrun appreciates your efforts and progress, and wants you to follow him to Munak Cave in the Payon. Over there is where you will learn to be a great Ranger...",
    ["TaskDescription117527304"]="You must complete Payon's most traditional sacrificial rituals in order to obtain the token to become a ranger. At Melbrun's request, you began to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Munak's eyeball</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bongun's finger</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sohee's hair</color> in order to use as tributes to comfort the spirits of the heroic souls who have passed away.",
    ["TaskDescription117527305"]="After collecting all the tributes, you arrived at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>altar of the idol</color> in the depths of the Munak Cave. To your surprise, there was another old friend waiting for you here besides Melbrun...",
    ["TaskDescription117527306"]="The Almighty Qi Euin has approved of your arrows and will. It's time to place the <color=#CA2E0AFF>tributes on the altar</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117527307"]="Upon successfully completing Payon's most traditional sacrificial ritual, you have now obtained a whistle that can command the Wolf, and is also a token you must have to become a ranger. Now you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> for your <color=#CA2E0AFF>Job Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117528301"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117528302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you returned to Criatura Academy in search of your previous Class Master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice</color> to receive guidance for your Class Advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117528303"]="Alice appreciated your progress and asked you to follow her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> to unlock a <color=#CA2E0AFF>fuller understanding of the Shura</color> class...",
    ["TaskDescription117528304"]="Master Jin explained the perils of the Shura in front of the Incense Pavilion: \"Power often comes at a cost to emotion and compassion.\" Peerless Jin would like you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray once again at the Earth Guardian Statue</color> for peace of mind and heart.",
    ["TaskDescription117528305"]="I received a strange Holy Bead while praying in front of the Earth Guardian Statue. I need to <color=#CA2E0AFF>prove my strength to Master Jin</color> to learn more about the Holy Bead.",
    ["TaskDescription117528306"]="The monster blood was enough to prove my strength. So Master Jin explained some of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>hidden histories of Payon in front of the quiet Incense Pavilion</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117528307"]="I'll take the evidence of Earth Guardian Shura's approval <color=#CA2E0AFF>back to Prontera</color> now that the mystery has been unveiled and to attend my Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117529301"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level <color=#CA2E0AFF>70</color>. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117529302"]="You heeded Archbishop Wolmas' advice and returned to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to seek the guidance of your former Class Master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color>, for further Class Advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117529303"]="Yadrew informed that the man you must see for a Class Advancement to a Royal Guard goes by the name of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>. You should also <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect</color> <color=#CA2E0AFF>Holy Water</color> from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera's Central Fountain</color> before you depart as \"it will come in handy for the trials.\"",
    ["TaskDescription117529304"]="You finally made your way to the path leading to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>, Holy Water in tow, as you excitedly prepare to meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seyren</color> who, as Yadrew instructed, can provide Class Advancement. You also wonder whether the mysterious Seyren, who you have not met for some time, is expecting you?",
    ["TaskDescription117529305"]="You managed to purify the wandering Spirit of the Nameless Knight with Seyren's help, thus completing the Class Advancement trial. It is time for you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return now to Prontera</color> and take part in your own <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117530301"]="Arrows are my best companions, but they're not enough...",
    ["TaskDescription117531101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117531102"]="You heeded Archbishop Wolmas' advice and returned to Criatura Academy to seek the guidance of your former Class Master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color>, for further Class Advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117531103"]="Charles appreciated your progress and asked you to follow him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color> for a Third Class journey...",
    ["TaskDescription117531104"]="Master Sage Kroneika has opened up a Magic Circle in the Mjolnir Mountains to commune with Elemental Spirits. All you need to do to prove your worthiness as an Elemental Envoy is to step into the Circle and gain Elemental Spirits' trust!",
    ["TaskDescription117531105"]="You somehow found yourself in possession of a Contract titled \"Ode of the Elemental Envoy\" after stepping inside the Circle. Master Sage Kroneika explained you must follow the directions of the poems to a specific destination to continue.",
    ["TaskDescription117531106"]="I will <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> after signing a Contract with an Elemental Spirit and gaining the Master Sage Kroneika's approval to complete my Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117532301"]="Master Melbrun told me to seek help from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Callahan</color>. I must go to Papuchicha Forest at once and learn everything about Bard/Dancer.",
    ["TaskDescription117532302"]="After proving my determination to Mr. Callahan, he taught me the first lesson—auditory perception. First, I must go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kokomo Beach</color> and collect the sound of sea breeze assembling and dispersing.",
    ["TaskDescription117532303"]="After taking a little girl to a concert, she gave me a conch with the echos of sea breeze. As for the sound of a forest growing, she suggested I ask Toland in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117532304"]="Toland gave me a seed of a banyan tree and asked me to deliver a costume to someone in the Comodo lighthouse, where Lindsey took that outfit and instructed me to check the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Comodo volcano</color> for the sound of fire passing through the ground.",
    ["TaskDescription117533301"]="I've been training throughout Midgards after leaving Comodo. Now it's time <color=#CA2E0AFF>to show Mr. Callahan the results</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription117534301"]="I've been training throughout Midgards after leaving Comodo. Now it's time <color=#CA2E0AFF>to show Mr. Callahan the results</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription117535301"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at class level 70. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117535302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to Criatura Academy in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Melbrun</color>, to receive guidance for your class advancement...",
    ["TaskDescription117535303"]="Melbrun appreciated your progress and asked you to follow him to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color> for a Third Class journey...",
    ["TaskDescription117535304"]="In Papuchicha Forest, Callahan wants you to show your perception of human emotions. He asks you to decide the outcome of his bet with Vendra on the emotional tone of the Final Work, and it falls to you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>retrieve the manuscript</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117535305"]="You came to the Kokomo Beach and retrieved the manuscript from the Obeaune. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>give the manuscript to Callahan</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription117535306"]="After the truth comes out, I will <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> with Master Callahan's approval to complete my Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117537301"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job Lv.70. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117537302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to Criatura Academy in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moxie</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117537303"]="Moxie appreciates your efforts and progress and wants you to follow her to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Desert Green Tavern</color> to acquire strength from a powerful monster for your own use...",
    ["TaskDescription117537304"]="In Desert Green Tavern, Moxie asks for an extremely flattering Ode from Caslisse the Bard and suggests you meet her later that day at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pyramid 1F</color>. By then, she might be able to answer some of your questions.",
    ["TaskDescription117537305"]="After all, the monster you're trying to summon and acquire the power from is named the Betrayer of Light. The Ode turns out to be one of the offerings needed to be present in the ritual. After a few battles, you are now in possession of all the offerings. Now, it's the moment of truth to <color=#CA2E0AFF>face the Betrayer of Light</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription117537306"]="After defeating the projection of the Betrayer of Light, you're now <color=#CA2E0AFF>returning to Prontera</color> with the mighty Shadow Power needed to complete your Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117538301"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job Lv.70. He will help you prepare for a Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117538302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you return to Criatura Academy in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hamid</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription117538303"]="Hamid talks about how the Genetic plays their role in the field of Life Transmutation. He suggests you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Al De Baran</color> and learn from Nicolas how to become a Genetic.",
    ["TaskDescription117538304"]="In Al De Baran, Nicolas tells you the first step of becoming a Genetic is to use yourself as a sample to complete the Life Transmutation. You can find replacements from humanoid monsters. Once you collect all the materials, the last step is to return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Al De Baran</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117538305"]="Under the witness of Nicolas, you completed the Life Transmutation. But the product was a bit off from what you had in mind. Was it missing some of the materials? You decided to find out by <color=#CA2E0AFF>asking Nicolas</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117539101"]="I've been on the path of Super Novice for too long. Where can I find a new starting point?",
    ["TaskDescription117540101"]="Mainz advised me <color=#CA2E0AFF>to seek Master Tanders' guidance</color>. I must go to Mjolnir Mountains at once and learn everything I need to know about Expanded Super Novice.",
    ["TaskDescription117540102"]="In Mjolnir Mountains, you met the nagging Tanders and his assistant, Sansha. From their rather profound conversation, you made out \"<color=#CA2E0AFF>Go into the Labyrinth Forest</color> and get a certain object.\" So what can the forest be concealing?",
    ["TaskDescription117540103"]="The first challenge was the cunning Vries. He demanded that you pick the correct portal out of four that would yield the right passage. You got the answer with a simple but effective means, and the bruised Vries informed you <color=#CA2E0AFF>the next challenge is ahead...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription117540104"]="Following Vries' directions, you encountered a distrait Zealotus in the second challenge, who was apparently waiting for a man named Anthony. Following the guidance of the witch's ring, you saw a frail man deep in the forest...",
    ["TaskDescription117540105"]="It turned out the stranger was the Anthony that the witch had been pining for. Alas, they were forced to part after the reunion. With the witch's blessing, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>surged into the next challenge</color>, only to see Tanders blocking your path...",
    ["TaskDescription117541301"]="Now, I'm going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Expanded Super Novice!",
    ["TaskDescription117542301"]="Visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117542302"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you decide to go to Morroc and<color=#CA2E0AFF>seek out Tanders the Tutor</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117542303"]="Tanders lauded your progress and wanted you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow him</color> and get started on a third class...",
    ["TaskDescription117542304"]="In the mouth of the cave, Tanders related the threat behind the Job Advancement Ceremony. He suggested that you ponder carefully before deciding to enter the <color=#CA2E0AFF>extremely dangerous Sphinx Cavern</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117542305"]="You defeated the many monsters in the cavern to finally reach the sacrificial altar, only to realize the Sacrificial Ritual has already begun.",
    ["TaskDescription117542306"]="After taking the oath, you will <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> with the Subconscious Divinity's approval and complete your own Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117543101"]="I've journeyed as a Gunslinger for a long time. Where might I discover a fresh beginning?",
    ["TaskDescription117544101"]="Mainz suggested I <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek Instructor Miller's guidance</color>. I need to get to Glast Heim promptly and learn all the required knowledge about the Rebellion class.",
    ["TaskDescription117544102"]="In Glast Heim St. Abbey, Instructor Miller spoke of a 700-year-old assassination attempt on King Schmidt by Gunslingers. Now, it's your turn to <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow in Instructor Miller's steps</color> and embark on the brave journey of the Gunslinger from 700 years ago.",
    ["TaskDescription117544103"]="As you hear about the Night of Gunfire, you tag along with Instructor Miller to the Glast Heim Sewer. Before you step into Glast Heim Prison, he asks you to grab some Soulsoothing Grass for the prison's lost souls, then you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep going</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117544104"]="The Soulsoothing Grass slowly burns down. In the flickering firelight, you spot <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color> not too far off.",
    ["TaskDescription117544105"]="Instructor Miller points out that the finale of this assassination story is just ahead to be witnessed, marking your next journey as a Rebellion. You stare at the structure before you, known to younger generations as the Glast Heim Churchyard.",
    ["TaskDescription117546101"]="Visit Wolmas the Archbishop at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117546102"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you decide to go to Glast Heim Churchyard and seek out Instructor Miller...",
    ["TaskDescription117546103"]="You encounter Instructor Miller at the Glast Heim Churchyard. He tells you that the Dimensional Gap ahead is the testing ground for Predators. You're set to journey back to the Night of Gunfire, more than 700 years ago, and witness the story's conclusion. As your mentor, he fervently wishes you could make it back alive.",
    ["TaskDescription117546104"]="Amidst the corpses in Glast Heim Churchyard, you spot a goddess-like Graveyard Phantom. She gifts you the power to become a Predator, and asks you to remember her face so that you can shoot a bullet into her heart once you become a Predator.",
    ["TaskDescription117546105"]="After taking the vow, you will return to Prontera with Instructor Miller's approval and complete your own Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117547101"]="I've been on the path of Ninja for too long. Where can I find a new starting point?",
    ["TaskDescription117548101"]="Mainz suggested I <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek help from Akahyo</color>. I need to get to Munak Cave 1F in Payon immediately and learn all the required knowledge about the Kagerou/Oboro class.",
    ["TaskDescription117548102"]="You are now at Munak Cave 1F, where you and two Ninjas named Souzo and Ohka are waiting for the Class Advancement Trial to begin. At the start, Ohka pitches this bold idea of working as a team, saying that she and Souzo can guarantee your victory in the trial. In return, she wants you to escort them to the Universe Stone Formation after <color=#CA2E0AFF>reaching the Forgotten Lake Waterfall</color>. It turns out that the place behind it is what drives them to join this trial.",
    ["TaskDescription117548103"]="Thanks to Ohka and Souzo, you finally make it to Forgotten Lake, waiting to meet up with them.",
    ["TaskDescription117548104"]="Beneath the Forgotten Lake Waterfall, Ohka and Souzo are there expecting you, hoping you'll keep your word and help them to <color=#CA2E0AFF>reach the Universe Stone Formation</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117548105"]="You've just wrapped up a battle and made your way to the Universe Stone Formation, ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet up with Ohka and Souzo</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117549101"]="Now, you are going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Kagerou/Oboro!",
    ["TaskDescription117550101"]="Visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117550102"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you decide to go to Munak Cave 1F and<color=#CA2E0AFF>seek out Akahyo</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117550103"]="Inside the Munak Cave, Akahyo clues you in that the Universe Stone Formation leads to the Land of Trials. According to the rules, only the last survivor gets to advance to the third class. The Land of Trials is teeming with spooky Horong, and here are your opponents standing before you — <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ohka and Souzo</color>, as well as a talking Horong. What?",
    ["TaskDescription117550104"]="In your conversation with Ohka, you find out that both the Skeleton you cut down during the second-class advancement and these Horong wandering everywhere are all Ninjas who died in trials or death matches. The Horong, now speaking to Ohka, had a deep history with Akahyo and was taken out by him during a third-class advancement. Ohka pitched to team up with you during the second-class advancement to probe for Akahyo's weak spot for a better shot in their next battle. Just as you're about to dig deeper, Akahyo shows up. Now, it's your turn for the trial.",
    ["TaskDescription117550105"]="Under Akahyo's supervision, you nailed the trail. But why? Why does winning come with the cost of somebody's life? Why these obsolete ancient rules? Can't we just switch classes in a more gentle way? You decide to get to the bottom of this by <color=#CA2E0AFF>asking Akahyo</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription117550106"]="Akahyo casually brushes off your questions, saying you're not ready to handle the truth. If you really want to do something, then you should aim beyond the third class. But heads up, Akahyo won't be your mentor by then but your opponent.",
    ["TaskDescription117553101"]="I've been on the path of Taekwon for too long. Where can I find a new starting point?",
    ["TaskDescription117554101"]="Mainz suggested I <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek Instructor Phoenix's guidance</color>. I need to get to Sograt Desert promptly and learn all the required knowledge about the Star Gladiator class.",
    ["TaskDescription117554102"]="In Morroc, with Phoenix watching, you affirm your martial arts training intention and begin your first lesson: defeat <color=#CA2E0AFF>Golem</color> while weighted down.",
    ["TaskDescription117554103"]="After finishing the training of \"Slow,\" Phoenix removes the rocks from your. Time to kill Anacondaq with the power of \"Speed\"!",
    ["TaskDescription117555101"]="Now, you are going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Star Gladiator!",
    ["TaskDescription117556101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Visit Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Job Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription117556102"]="Under Wolmas the Archbishop's advice, you decide to go to Goblin Forest and<color=#CA2E0AFF>seek out Phoenix...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription117556103"]="Meeting Phoenix as planned, and after ensuring your intention remains unchanged, the Class Advancement Trial begins. You need to beat the weakest creature around Geffen, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goblins</color>, and learn the power of \"Defense\" from them.",
    ["TaskDescription117556104"]="After defeating these Goblins, you will learn the power of \"Attack\" from the battle of survival with an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Orc Hero</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription117556105"]="Having defeated the Orc Hero, before making the advancement, go and listen to the teachings of your instructor, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Phoenix</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription117556106"]="You're now ready to <color=#CA2E0AFF>head back to Prontera</color> for the Job Advancement Ceremony that Wolmas the Archbishop has set up for you.",
    ["TaskDescription117557101"]="Dean Mainz has sent you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> to find the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Soul Linker</color> mentor. Let's get moving!",
    ["TaskDescription117557102"]="Your mentor, Moonstrider, says the animals around <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> have gone wild. Eliminate the ones posing a threat!",
    ["TaskDescription117557103"]="You've taken down the Snake and Bigfoot, but something still feels off...",
    ["TaskDescription117558101"]="Now, you are going to the Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Soul Linker!",
    ["TaskDescription117559101"]="Visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> at Job level 70. He will help you prepare for a Job Advancement Ceremony.\n\n",
    ["TaskDescription117559102"]="Wolmas the Archbishop asked you to find your class mentor, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moonstrider</color>. Head out now!",
    ["TaskDescription117559103"]="The moment you meet, Moonstrider points to the forest, where your trial is going to take place. What's waiting for you inside.....",
    ["TaskDescription12000"]="1st Class - Mage",
    ["TaskDescription120001101"]="At the Central Fountain of Prontera, you meet the kingdom's famous bard, Morts, who invites you to listen to the story of Tristan Gaebolg, an ancestor of the seven royal families.\nIt is said that Tristan was very arrogant at one point during his youth. With his exceptional looks and talents, he thought very little of others. He even ridiculed the goddess of dawn when she professed her love for him. Tears of humiliation flowed from her eyes, creating the current Central Fountain of Prontera...\nWhen Morts gets to this point of the story, he expresses a desire to taste the tears of the goddess for himself. Help retrieve some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fountain Water</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Central Fountain</color> for him to drink!",
    ["TaskDescription120001102"]="After drinking the fountain water, Morts continued the story.\nFollowing the ridicule she received from the person she loved, the goddess of dawn refused to appear before humanity. Her light disappeared from the world, never to be seen again. This began a long, endless night and gave devious monsters the opportunity to launch surprise attacks on humanity, causing a great panic.... Tristan's humiliation of the goddess was blamed for bringing about the calamity, but the young man did not recognize his error until a dancer who had lost a loved one during this endless night appeared before him.\nThe dancer told Tristan that if his pride was merely based on his looks and talents, he might as well not have any. At that moment, Tristan realized that he'd been failing everyone all along and decided to make up for his mistake by using a mirror made out of Jellopy.\nJust as you are eager to hear what Tristan was going to do with the mirror, Morts suddenly stated that he also wants to get <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pure Jellopy</color> and recreate Tristan's mirror. If you want him finish the story, you'll have to satisfy his request!",
    ["TaskDescription120002101"]="You meet the bard Morts again in the Mjolnir Mountains, and this time he tells you a story of desire.\nLegend has it that an ancestor of the Heines Family, Nithil Heine, was an innocent youth. During one of his travels, he journeyed into the Labyrinth Forest and became trapped by spatial magic. At a critical moment, a graceful witch named Vivienne appeared in front of Nithil, who was soon overcome by her beauty. When she gave him a magic potion, he drank it without caution, which caused him to lose his memory...\nIt is said that the magic potion was made from boiling the seeds of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragoras</color>. Does it really have this magical effect? Quickly get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mandragora Seeds</color> for Morts to study!",
    ["TaskDescription120002102"]="Having lost his memory, Nithil thought Vivienne was his partner and decided to stay with her in the forest forever.\nHowever, after not hearing from the missing Nithir for a long period of time, Merlin followed his beloved apprentice's trail to the entrance of the Labyrinth Forest and deduced that Nithil's disappearance had something to do with the witch Vivienne.\nWhen Merlin found the two of them, he came up with the idea of using the witch's competitiveness to help Nithil regain his memories. After he casted a spell on Nithil, Nithil suddenly chose to leave the forest, no matter how much the pregnant Vivienne begged him not to...\nWhat kind of spell could have caused such a transformation in Nithil? Why don't you go to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen Library</color> and learn about the effects of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Spell of Metis</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription120002103"]="After some research, you learn that the spell Merlin casted reversed the effect of Vivienne's potion. Therefore, although he regained his memories before he entered the forest, he forgot the time he spent with Vivienne.\nBut Vivienne did not know about any of this. She only saw a heartless betrayer, so she turned her resentment into a curse to put on Nithil, which made it so that if he turned to look back on his way out of the forest, the pain of separation would strike both Nithil and Merlin.\nNithil was cautious and didn't let his guard down until he crossed the suspension bridge in the Labyrinth Forest. It was at that moment that he heard his mentor's screams from behind him, causing him to turn around. It was then he witnessed his mentor Merlin turn into a giant tree...\nMorts stops his story there and expresses his desire to see what this tree looks like. Hurry and follow his instructions. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go to the top of the hill and take a picture of the giant tree,</color> then bring it back and show it him!",
    ["TaskDescription120003101"]="You meet the bard Morts on Izlude Island, who states that he has just composed a poem about the story of Izlude Island and invites you to be the first to listen to it.\nLegend has it that before Ragnarok, many races coexisted in Midgard, but not every person had goodwill towards the humans. One such was person was a giant named Izlude.\nRelying on his formidable physique, Izlude often wandered the outskirts of human villages, threatening people to hand over food they worked so laboriously to grow. Most would acquiesce silently, except for a young man named Ewan Richard.\nOne day while Ewan was tilling his wheat, Izlude came once again to plunder his crops. This time the young man vowed to be patient no longer. He devised a plan and decided to fight back using his brains!\nAt this point in the story, Morts expresses his surprise that the giant liked eating healthy food such as <color=#CA2E0AFF>Island Wheat</color>… Hurry and bring him some to study!",
    ["TaskDescription120003102"]="The next spring Ewan worked much harder than before, cultivating more land and harvesting more crops. But Ewan kept only a small portion of the grain for himself and offered the rest to Izlude. Ewan requested that the giant never come to a human village in person again to ask for anything. As long as the giant called out for what he wanted from the cave he lived in, Ewan would directly bring him anything.\nOh, what a wonderful life Izlude lived. Each day he grew plumper as well as lazier as Ewan continually fed him... As for what happens after that, Morts says he'll let you know when you bring him a piece of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meat n' Pumpkin</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription120003103"]="One day, Izlude finally got so fat that he couldn't even crawl out of his cave. He could only lie at the bottom of the cave and let Ewan deliver food directly into his mouth, which was exactly what Ewan wanted.\nEwan returned to the village and told the villagers the time had come to grab their knives and axes and follow him take revenge.\nWhile Izlude was asleep, Ewan moved forward and cut off a piece of the giant's flesh with his knife. Upon seeing this, the villagers swarmed forward with their weapons. By the time Izude realized his predicament, he was too weak to resist due to the lack of exercise over a long period.\nAccording to Morts, the taste of giant meat seems very similar to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rocker Leg Meat</color> of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vocals</color>... You don't know if that's true or not. Go get some and let him have a bite!",
    ["TaskDescription120004101"]="You meet the bard Morts in the West Gate Cemetery, where, according to him, a forgotten nobleman of the seven royal families is buried. He happily begins telling you the story of the man's past.\nIt is said that many years ago, the Walter Family had a pair of twins who were identical in appearance but very different in talent and disposition. The older brother, Ian, was sharp and eloquent but had very little skill with a sword, while the younger brother, Ivan, was a great swordsman but was inarticulate and reticent.\nSince no one could tell their appearance apart and Ivan didn't want his older brother Ian to feel disappointed in himself, he often took on sword duels pretending to be Ian. This caused news of a pair of talented twin swordsmen in the Walter Family to reach the ears of the king, who decided to hold a great tournament on the day the brothers came of age.\nWhen Morts gets to this point of the story, he expresses a great interest in knowing what the venue where the tournament took place long ago looked like. Why don't you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture</color> of the venue, which is the<color=#CA2E0AFF>square in front of the palace</color> and show it to him?",
    ["TaskDescription120004102"]="On the day of the tournament, Ivan competed in Ian's place as usual. But after all the opponents were defeated, leaving only the two brothers for the final match, their father, who was the head of the Walter Family, told them that the winner of the tournament would be his successor.\nThe news both surprised and angered Ian, who had always believed that the future head of the family would be none other than himself, but now he was forced to surrender everything because his brother had the fortune of being gifted in swordsmanship.\nFor the first time in his life, Ian felt jealous of his brother Ivan, and an evil thought formed in his mind.\nBefore Morts could finish his story, his tummy begins growling. Hurry and bring him some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Steamed Egg n' Fish</color> to fill his stomach.",
    ["TaskDescription120004103"]="On the day of the final match, everyone expected to see a spectacular duel, but Ivan found that he had lost the strength to even draw his sword, let alone fight.\nAt that moment, Ian stepped forward and revealed the \"truth\" that he had been hiding for years, that it was actually Ian himself who had been the better swordsman of the two brothers all along and that he had been helping his brother hide his weakness by pretending to be Ivan and accepting duels.\nMorts stops there and expresses that it must be very painful to be misunderstood. He then requests that you pick up some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Flowers</color> to be used later from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pooler Gardens</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription120004104"]="After hearing Ian's words, Ivan finally realized his older brother's plot... Receiving complete scorn from the crowd, he gave up and left the Walter Family on his own.\nFrom then on Ivan wandered around the continent, abandoning his family name and the person he once was, until Ivan met Morts' mentor at the end of his life. That was when he told the truth about his past and asked the bard to bury him in the West Gate Cemetery.\nWith his story finished, Morts asks you pay your respects by placing the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Fresh Flowers</color> you just gathered at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ivan's gravestone</color>. Hopefully this will bring him a little solace.",
    ["TaskDescription120005101"]="You meet the bard Morts in the city of Morroc, who tells you that his mentor's manuscripts contain a story about the ancestors of the Lugenburg Family and after hearing it, you may understand why this family is known to have \"lava flowing in their veins.\"\nIt is said that Alex Lugenburg was once a slave in the desert. He was abused by slavers and even bullied by other slaves due to his young age and frailty. Unable to resist, Alex could only suffer in silence until one day the slavers told him that rare Red Crystals had been found in an underground cave and that whoever dug up a hundred could exchange them for their freedom.\nWhen Morts gets to this point of the story, he expresses a great desire to see what the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Red Crystals</color> that the slavers wanted so much actually look like. Why don't you go find some and show him?",
    ["TaskDescription120005102"]="Alex saw what the slaver said to be his only chance to gain freedom, and so he endured excruciating pain, digging up the entire one hundred Red Crystals with his bare hands. But just as he was full of hope and about to take them to the slavers, he was attacked by the other slaves... Not only did they rob him of the crystals he painstakingly collected, but they also pushed him into Golden Lava to keep the young man from exposing their theft.\nMorts stops the story there and tells you that he's very curious about the Golden Lava that engulfed one of the members of the seven royal families. Hurry and satisfy his curiosity by <color=#CA2E0AFF>taking a picture of the Golden Lava</color> and showing it to him!",
    ["TaskDescription120005103"]="Oh how horrible it was for Alex when he was thrown into the molten rock. The scorching lava melted his flesh and dissolved his bones... But just as he was about to die, he seemed to hear a mocking sigh. It turned out that it came from the god of fire Loki, who happened to witness Alex's plight. Out of \"compassion,\" Loki decided to give him a chance to escape death.\nLoki told Alex that if he was willing to swallow the lava in front of him, his body would heal and gain as much power as he could swallow. The fear of dying made Alex realize how terrible it was to be weak, so without saying a word, he swallowed all the lava he could.\nAs a result, Loki's promise came to fruition. Alex become a mighty giant, but he could no longer feel inner peace. No matter how little something displeased him, it could stoke the flames of anger in Alex's heart... It turned out that Loki didn't tell Alex that such a rebirth came with a price: the more power the young man gained, the more of his sanity would be lost.\nMorts stops at this point in the story and says that he has trouble dealing with dry mouth caused by the desert climate. Quickly get some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cactus Dew</color> from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mukas</color> outside the city for him to drink!",
    ["TaskDescription120006101"]="You meet the bard Morts in the port city of Alberta. When he learns that you haven't heard the story of the ancestor of the Wigner Family, he begins singing a song, taking you back into the past.\nThe story goes that Ricky Wigner was a fisherman making a living in Alberta, which during his time was a small seaside village. Although he had humble beginnings, he was ambitious and possessed a shrewd mind that could always maximize profits from the opportunities that came his way.\nWhile going out fishing one day, Ricky happened to catch a legendary monster, an Obeaune. He was filled with joy and felt that fate had finally given him a miracle.\nAt this point of the story, Morts laments that he has never seen the beautiful monster... How about you <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of an Obeaune</color> and show it to Morts?",
    ["TaskDescription120006102"]="The poor captured Obeaune was so innocent. She begged Ricky not to harm her and offered to give him a crystal-clear Pearl in exchange for her freedom. Ricky realized the value of the rare gem, but had already fallen for the Obeaune's beauty. Therefore, he devised a way to get both the treasure and the Obeaune.\nHe brought the Obeaune home and said that one Pearl was not enough, but if she met his three demands, he would set her free. The Obeaune had no choice but to agree to his conditions; however, she stated that no one was allowed to be around when she forms the Pearl. Since Ricky did not care how the gems come to be, he agreed to the mermaid's request.\nHis first demand was for her to provide him ten Pearls, which he sold to merchants. With the money he earned, he built a port and established a maritime caravan. But Ricky's ambitions did not stop there. He made a second demand of the Obeaune, asking for one hundred Pearls this time because he needed more funds to build a city.\nMorty stops there and tells you that the port in front of him is the one that Ricky funded and built and that recently, ships sailing from it have been getting attacked by <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vadons</color>. Hurry and teach those aggressive monsters a lesson!",
    ["TaskDescription120006103"]="Not long after, the Age of Gods arrived and Midgard was plunged into chaos. The legendary hero, Tristan Gaebolg summoned mighty adventurers to join him in eradicating the monsters plaguing the continent. The shrewd Ricky, on the other hand, once again detected a business opportunity.\nRicky made a third demand of the Obeaune, which was to deliver one thousand Pearls. He used all the profit from the sales of the gems to support Tristan and join his campaigns across the continent. Just as he predicted, the next time he returned to his hometown, he became one of the members of the seven royal families due to his contributions in founding the kingdom. But when he was about to share the happy news with the Obeaune at his home, he found that she had become increasingly emaciated due to her prolonged separation from her place of origin, the sea.\nThe Obeaune again pleaded for Ricky to set her free but was rebuffed with various excuses. This time the Obeaune could not hold back and began shedding tears in front of Ricky. As the tears dripped to the ground, they turned into blood-red Pearls.\nMorts stops at this point of the story and tells you that he also wants to collect some <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pearls</color>. Why don't you get some from the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Obeaunes</color> to satisfy his wish?",
    ["TaskDescription120007101"]="You meet the bard Morts in Sograt Desert, who tells you that he was part of the music band, Beautiful Bells, and begins telling you a story about the band's founder, Margaret Nerius.\nThe story took place during an extremely turbulent time, when the most powerful ancient Egyptian empire in the desert had fallen. This barren land became a paradise for monsters, and its human inhabitants lost their faith. They were defenseless against calamities, natural and man-made. The most brutal of all the monsters was the demon king Morroc, who not only slaughtered humans indiscriminately but also tortured them for his own amusement. There were priests who bent their knees and worshiped Morroc. They held a grand celebration for him every year, where beautiful handpicked girls were made to dance in gorgeous gowns. Little did the girls know, they were performing sacrificial dances. Once the dances were over, Morroc would eat every last one of them.\nMargaret, our protagonist in this story, was just a nameless orphan in the desert with no memory of her parents or when they left her. She was fortunate enough to survive and overcome adversity with intelligence and perseverance. Unfortunately for her, she was taken in by Morroc's priests... That day the fate of the young girl was decided...\nMorts stops at this point of the story and tells you that his long journey has left him starving. Quickly prepare him a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Water Weed Salad</color> to satisfy his appetite!",
    ["TaskDescription120007102"]="The priests named the young girl Margaret, which means noble princess, and gave her and her dance partners a luxurious life, filled with fine dining and clothing. The priests taught the girls how to carry themselves and dance, which they practiced daily. They were told that they would be the dancers of the grand celebration when they reached eighteen years old and that anyone who danced for Morroc would be blessed with supreme happiness... However, the priest did not tell them that were actually going to become Morroc's dish and that they were being groomed for the sole purpose of making them more enticing and delicious.\nOur protagonist, Margaret, soon grew up to be the most beautiful girl in the desert. She had a beautiful figure, graceful dance moves, and no excitement toward obtaining \"supreme happiness.\" She merely wished to repay the priests for their nurture and care with a great performance. But the day after Margaret was chosen as a dancer, the goddess Valkyrie appeared in her dreams and told her the true purpose of the celebration. She then advised Margaret to travel to the source of Hope Oasis to find a way to save herself.\nMorts stops at this point of the story and expresses curiosity as to what the oasis the legendary dancer visited looks like. How about you go <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a picture of Hope Oasis</color> and show it to him?",
    ["TaskDescription120007103"]="On the day of the celebration, Margaret put on her most gorgeous dress and danced with utmost elegance, waiting for what the goddess had indicated was going to happen. As expected, after the ritual dance ended, Demon King Morroc appeared and watched with great pleasure as the dancers screamed and fled in horror. However, among them was a calm and composed young woman. Morroc curiously asked our protagonist why she was not afraid, and Margaret replied that she had already guessed her fate, that she was proud to offer herself to the demon, and that she had come up with three suggestions that would make Morroc even happier.\nThe first suggestion was that the demon king should eat her first, for she was clearly the fairest of the maidens, and finest food should be enjoyed first. The second suggestion was for Morroc to swallow her and the other young women in one bite, which would keep their bodies intact and allow them to continue dancing for the demon in the underworld as well. The third suggestion was for Morroc to first eat a small, round fruit that was tart and sweet and would whet the demon king's appetite before consuming the girls.\nBefore going any further, Morts states that he too would like to taste the fruit, which is said to be called <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sweet and Sour Berry</color>... Hurry and satisfy the bard's wish!",
    ["TaskDescription12100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Wizard!",
    ["TaskDescription12110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription12200"]="2nd Class - Sage",
    ["TaskDescription12210"]="A long-awaited peace had returned to Prontera. Busy laughter reigned in the city streets as a major public works program under the royal family worked to clean up all traces of the troubles. Yet I have been summoned by the Great Sage. He seems to be planning something.",
    ["TaskDescription13000"]="1st Class - Acolyte",
    ["TaskDescription13100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Priest!",
    ["TaskDescription13110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription13200"]="2nd Class - Monk",
    ["TaskDescription13210"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription13220"]="3rd Class - Champion",
    ["TaskDescription14000"]="1st Class - Archer",
    ["TaskDescription14100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Hunter!",
    ["TaskDescription14110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription14200"]="I'll return to Prontera and showcase the results of my training in the battle trials!",
    ["TaskDescription15000"]="1st Class - Thief",
    ["TaskDescription15100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Assassin!",
    ["TaskDescription15110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription16000"]="1st Class - Merchant",
    ["TaskDescription16100"]="I've decided to choose you. The Blacksmith!",
    ["TaskDescription16110"]="Finally, peace was restored to Prontera. The people were smiling and laughing again, and the city was systematically repaired under the leadership of the royal family. It looks as if there was never a disaster. Now the the Great Sage, who seems to be planning something, is calling me over.",
    ["TaskDescription16200"]="I'll <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Prontera</color> and showcase the results of my training in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>battle trials</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription17001"]="Dean Mainz advises further lessons to guide your career. If you aspire to become a cool Gunslinger, find Instructor Miller outside the academy!",
    ["TaskDescription17100"]="Now, I'm going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for the Rebellion!",
    ["TaskDescription18000"]="At the end of the trial, you have chosen your own path to becoming stronger! Go and tell Dean Mainz about your decision.",
    ["TaskDescription18001"]="Dean Mainz advises further lessons to guide your career. If you aspire to become a Ninja, find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Akahyo on the Izlude Island</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription18002"]="After you complete your first job course, Kiki asks you to go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> to meet Dean Mainz. You wonder what he'll say when he sees how much you've grown.",
    ["TaskDescription18100"]="Now, you are going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Kagerou!",
    ["TaskDescription18200"]="Now, you are going to Prontera Cathedral to take the Class Advancement Trial for Oboro!",
    ["TaskDescription19000"]="At the end of the trial, you have chosen your own path to becoming stronger! Go and tell Dean Mainz about your decision.",
    ["TaskDescription19001"]="Dean Mainz advises further lessons to guide your career. If you aspire to become a Taekwon, <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Instructor Phoenix on Izlude Island</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription19002"]="After you complete your first job course, Kiki asks you to go back to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Temple of Dawn</color> to meet Dean Mainz. You wonder what he'll say when he sees how much you've grown.",
    ["TaskDescription2"]="Test mission board quest description placeholder text.",
    ["TaskDescription20001"]="Green Cotton Farm is infested with Fabres! Please help us get rid of them!",
    ["TaskDescription20002"]="Naughty Lunatics are greatly interfering with the caravan's progress. Please drive them away!",
    ["TaskDescription20003"]="The noise the Rockers make are keeping people awake! Please quiet them down!",
    ["TaskDescription20004"]="Condors have taken over a large area outside South Gate. They need to be shown who owns the place!",
    ["TaskDescription20005"]="The Kingdom Defense Force needs people to deal with these disgusting things!",
    ["TaskDescription20006"]="The desert heat plus the annoying buzzing... Please get rid of the Chonchons!",
    ["TaskDescription20007"]="The Academy urgently needs Mandragora Juice to teach cooking and will buy as much as you have!",
    ["TaskDescription20008"]="What is it that allows Willows to move? Aren't you curious about what's hidden inside these wooden beings? How about helping us do some research?",
    ["TaskDescription20009"]="Anyone collecting Savage Bebe Bristles? We're in urgent need of them! We'd appreciate any help!",
    ["TaskDescription20010"]="Is there any adventurer traveling between Izlude Island and Prontera South Gate who can help deliver a package?",
    ["TaskDescription20011"]="Please be a bridge of communication for my daughter and I. Help me deliver my letter to her.",
    ["TaskDescription20012"]="Please help a young girl fulfill her wish of collaborating with her idol!",
    ["TaskDescription20013"]="As I'm old and weak, I would like an adventurer to help me sweep a grave.",
    ["TaskDescription20014"]="Pretty girls and beautiful flowers are a match made in heaven, so please surround me with flowers and cheers.",
    ["TaskDescription20015"]="There's a request from the chivalry for cargo transport. Please report to Tanders at the West Gate Windmill.",
    ["TaskDescription20101"]="The Kingdom Defense Force needs people to deal with these disgusting things!",
    ["TaskDescription20102"]="Blood-sucking bats have been planning something targeting humans. Let's deal with this before something bad happens!",
    ["TaskDescription20103"]="The war between Female and Male Thief Bugs is in full swing. Take this opportunity to exterminate them and solve the Thief Bug problem!",
    ["TaskDescription20104"]="Even more so than the hidden bats eyeing your neck, these harmless demon Planktons need to be eliminated.",
    ["TaskDescription20105"]="Nobody dares provoke those relentless Hornets. Please help maintain peace on Mjolnir Mountains!",
    ["TaskDescription20106"]="Nobody dares provoke those relentless Hornets. Please help maintain peace on Mjolnir Mountains!",
    ["TaskDescription20107"]="The Academy urgently needs Mandragora Juice to teach cooking and will buy as much as you have!",
    ["TaskDescription20108"]="Anyone collecting Savage Bebe Bristles? We're in urgent need of them! We'd appreciate any help!",
    ["TaskDescription20109"]="Besides Lunatic Fur, there's nothing more beautiful in this world than the pelts of Desert Wolves, Baby Desert Pelts to be specific, which I'll buy in bulk!",
    ["TaskDescription20110"]="If you don't mind shattering a young girl's fantasy and making her come to terms with reality, please come see me.",
    ["TaskDescription20111"]="If what is written in this book is true, the world will soon come to an end!",
    ["TaskDescription20112"]="We have a report of vital importance and urge a diligent adventurer to undertake this request.",
    ["TaskDescription20113"]="The first step to becoming a fishing master begins with bait collecting!",
    ["TaskDescription20114"]="A poor Pecopeco has gone missing and must be very scared. Please find and bring it back!",
    ["TaskDescription20115"]="Can an adventurer that is an expert at vine-climbing and Crow shooing come listen to our request?",
    ["TaskDescription20201"]="Blood-sucking bats have been planning something targeting humans. Let's deal with this before something bad happens!",
    ["TaskDescription20202"]="The war between Female and Male Thief Bugs is in full swing. Take this opportunity to exterminate them and solve the Thief Bug problem!",
    ["TaskDescription20203"]="The war between Female and Male Thief Bugs is in full swing. Take this opportunity to exterminate them and solve the Thief Bug problem!",
    ["TaskDescription20204"]="The increasingly red glow of the Drainliars is an ominous sign. Please help us deal with the situation!",
    ["TaskDescription20205"]="Even moreso than the hidden bats eyeing your neck, these harmless demon Planktons need to be eliminated.",
    ["TaskDescription20206"]="Nobody dares provoke those relentless Hornets. Please help maintain peace on Mjolnir Mountains!",
    ["TaskDescription20207"]="The church is researching the applications of Mushroom Venom and wishes to receive assistance from adventurers!",
    ["TaskDescription20208"]="Creamy's Honey is the perfect treat! Please deliver it to us for processing. It can't be directly consumed!",
    ["TaskDescription20209"]="Cocos collecting too many Acorns will lead to the end of the world! I'm not kidding! Don't let them succeed!",
    ["TaskDescription20210"]="We're looking for adventurers to help transport supplies to the worksite of an archaeological team.",
    ["TaskDescription20211"]="The recipes of Rose Red Tavern and Desert Green Tavern's will be shared from now on. Adventurers who assist with recipe delivery will be the first to taste the dishes!",
    ["TaskDescription20212"]="Kafra is in need of adventurers heading to Morroc for the delivery of a document.",
    ["TaskDescription20213"]="Until the carrier pigeons adapt to their new landing site, please help us communicate!",
    ["TaskDescription20214"]="I treat each piece of work like my own child! I wonder if my Road Sign in the desert is doing well. It's been concerning me quite a lot.",
    ["TaskDescription20215"]="The Desert Green Tavern is in dire need of workers. Please come lend a hand!",
    ["TaskDescription20301"]="Seeking specialists to get rid of monster flies! We need real professionals! These Dustinesses are much stronger than the average Chonchon!",
    ["TaskDescription20302"]="You want us to enjoy the music of those Vocals? Don't be ridiculous! Please come quickly and help us!",
    ["TaskDescription20303"]="Those who also think Stainers are pests, please contact me! Otherwise, don't bother me!",
    ["TaskDescription20304"]="An overpopulation of Horns will lead to a great loss of vegetation! For the sake of the forest's ecology, please help cull their numbers!",
    ["TaskDescription20305"]="The Roda Frogs inhabiting the Shipwreck have become increasingly violent due to the influence of dark forces. It's very worrisome.",
    ["TaskDescription20306"]="A highly venomous creature, suspected to be a hybrid between a Marina and a Plankton, appeared on the Shipwreck. Come help me study them!",
    ["TaskDescription20307"]="Creamy's Honey is the perfect treat! Please deliver it to us for processing. It can't be directly consumed!",
    ["TaskDescription20308"]="Cocos collecting too many Acorns will lead to the end of the world! I'm not kidding! Don't let them succeed!",
    ["TaskDescription20309"]="Collecting leaves from the head of Smokies! Will take in bulk in any amount! Don't ask what for!",
    ["TaskDescription20310"]="This once peaceful and stoic heart of mine has suddenly been stirred by a very beautiful woman... Can anyone help me?",
    ["TaskDescription20311"]="I don't pay for slackers. Please help bring this guy back.",
    ["TaskDescription20312"]="The Alson Fleet has sent a letter with an assignment. Details are to be discussed in person.",
    ["TaskDescription20313"]="This is an outrage! A black crow has been appearing out of nowhere, stealing jewelry and flying off! Please, somebody help us deal with this issue!",
    ["TaskDescription20314"]="I need some reliable adventurers to help me harvest Bamboo without eating them!",
    ["TaskDescription20315"]="Daisy Cloth is both gorgeous and fragrant, but it's missing one last material!",
    ["TaskDescription20316"]="Pascal has a wish that must be fulfilled, no matter what the cost!",
    ["TaskDescription20401"]="There's no monster that can match the mischief that Yoyos cause! Please, someone do something about them!",
    ["TaskDescription20402"]="The cause of the recent geological disaster at Mjolnir Dead Pit has been identified. Please come quickly to get rid of those darn Martins!",
    ["TaskDescription20403"]="The Radiance of Odin shines over the land. The souls of the miners cannot be left seething with bitterness. The church requests your aid.",
    ["TaskDescription20404"]="These Pirate Skeletons were a menace when they were alive. Now they're guarding ill-gotten lands in death. Eliminate them once and for all!",
    ["TaskDescription20405"]="Seeking specialists to get rid of monster flies! We need real professionals! These Dustinesses are much stronger than the average Chonchon!",
    ["TaskDescription20406"]="You want us to enjoy the music of those Vocals? Don't be ridiculous! Please come quickly and help us!",
    ["TaskDescription20407"]="A dish made from Hydra Tentacles is the best offering for the God of the Sea, so please help us!",
    ["TaskDescription20408"]="Those darn Skel Pirates! Please eradicate them and bring me proof of their demise!",
    ["TaskDescription20409"]="Those darn Skel Pirates! Please eradicate them and bring me proof of their demise!",
    ["TaskDescription20501"]="Argos are horrible, disgusting creatures that shouldn't exist, so please get rid of as many as you can!",
    ["TaskDescription20502"]="Legend has it that some Mantises have bladed arms that can rival actual swords. Please help us verify this statement!",
    ["TaskDescription20503"]="Rampaging Savages have injured multiple adventurers! Is there anyone that can deal with them?",
    ["TaskDescription20504"]="Mukas seek warriors who can face their deadly spikes. Please show them humanity's strength!",
    ["TaskDescription20505"]="Wild Pecopecos can be more vicious than you can imagine! Please protect our caravans from Pecopecos!",
    ["TaskDescription20506"]="Heavy metal music is beautiful? No, no, no, at least not in the desert. Please get rid of the noise!",
    ["TaskDescription20507"]="Why would there be Sasquatches in Labyrinth Forest?! Please bring me their fur as proof!",
    ["TaskDescription20508"]="The church is researching the applications of Snake Venom and wish to receive assistance from adventurers!",
    ["TaskDescription20509"]="If you knew that tasting the ultimate dessert would kill you, would you still try it? Please bring me Scorpion Venom. I've already made my choice!",
    ["TaskDescription20601"]="The Andres in Ant Cavern are up to something bad, so go intimidate them before they make their move!",
    ["TaskDescription20602"]="Pieres are frontline soldiers and the foundation of their colony's development. Eliminating them can effectively stifle their colony's growth!",
    ["TaskDescription20603"]="Golems blocking the roads in the desert are creating serious problems. Please kindly \"remind\" them to make way!",
    ["TaskDescription20604"]="The ferocious Wolves of the desert have a deep-seated hatred for humans, so beware!",
    ["TaskDescription20605"]="The undead Soldier Skeletons still faithfully carry out their duty as guards. Defeat them to discover the Egyptian empire's past!",
    ["TaskDescription20606"]="Nine Tails represent good luck. But the Matyrs in the Pyramid are causing alarm among the people... Please take care of them before anything bad happens!",
    ["TaskDescription20607"]="The church is researching the applications of Snake Venom and wish to receive assistance from adventurers!",
    ["TaskDescription20608"]="If you knew that tasting the ultimate dessert would kill you, would you still try it? Please bring me Scorpion Venom. I've already made my choice!",
    ["TaskDescription20609"]="What exactly does a Magnolia taste like? Does anyone want to try some? If you're interested, please come work with me!",
    ["TaskDescription20701"]="Deniros are the main fighting force of the colony. Defeating them means winning the battle!",
    ["TaskDescription20702"]="Vitatas are the fighting elite of the colony. We have to get through them before facing Maya!",
    ["TaskDescription20703"]="(Various swears) Argiopes don't deserve to live in this world!",
    ["TaskDescription20704"]="Alberta has had many cases of jellyfish poisoning lately. Please go to the source of the poisoning and cull the Marina population!",
    ["TaskDescription20705"]="If we don't do something about these Phens, the bottom of every ship in the sea will have holes pierced through them.",
    ["TaskDescription20706"]="Darn ancient Egyptian barbarians! I can't believe they turned a cute dog into this Mummy! And they named it Verit!",
    ["TaskDescription20707"]="Mummy bandages have endured thousands of years of history. Help us collect some for our research on the ancient Egyptian empire!",
    ["TaskDescription20708"]="Humph! Only we know how delicious those vicious Vadons are! Interested? Then come see us!",
    ["TaskDescription20709"]="It is said that you can prove the sturdiness of a weapon by chopping through a Cornutus Shell. Please help me collect some!",
    ["TaskDescription20801"]="The Mage Guild seeks those who have experience fighting Marduks, the ancient Egyptian warlocks! Will provide excellent pay!",
    ["TaskDescription20802"]="To rescue adventurers who have been attacked by Side Winders, the church is seeking assistance in gathering more information about the snakes' ecology!",
    ["TaskDescription20803"]="Almighty Odin, please allow the Zeroms who have been abandoned in the Sphinx Cavern to transcend.",
    ["TaskDescription20804"]="Don't let the beauty of Isis deceive you, unless you want to end up as her meal!",
    ["TaskDescription20805"]="Don't be seduced by the Obeaunes' beauty. You have to prove your strength to them first before you are accepted under the sea!",
    ["TaskDescription20806"]="If we don't do something about these Phens, the bottom of every ship in the sea will have holes pierced through them.",
    ["TaskDescription20807"]="Fish Fins from legendary deep-sea fish are extraordinary. They must be delicious—I mean beautiful! Please help me get some!",
    ["TaskDescription20808"]="Minorous's Warhammer was created using ancient Egyptian forging techniques. I'd love to see how it compares to my work!",
    ["TaskDescription20809"]="Artificial Ink can't compare to the naturally-produced Ink of Marses? I don't believe it! Not until I see it with my own eyes!",
    ["TaskDescription20901"]="Almighty Odin, please allow the Requiems who have been abandoned in the Sphinx Cavern to transcend.",
    ["TaskDescription20902"]="Most of the tomb robbers who sneaked into the Pyramid were corrupted and became Pasanas. They're already dead, so there's no need to show mercy.",
    ["TaskDescription20903"]="Secret mission! Secret mission! Brave warriors who can defeat Wolves, please come to Payon and make contact with.... uh, Mystery Man #1!",
    ["TaskDescription20904"]="Snake... a scary green Snake, a vicious green Snake. Meow!",
    ["TaskDescription20905"]="Arclouzes have severely hampered the excavation of the ruins. The Eden Group is looking for a strong, brave warrior that doesn't suffer from trypophobia.",
    ["TaskDescription20906"]="That Skeleton warrior can no longer be called a warrior!",
    ["TaskDescription20907"]="(The text is written so messily that you can't tell what it says.)",
    ["TaskDescription20908"]="(The text is written so messily that you can't tell what it says.)",
    ["TaskDescription20909"]="Is there anyone who can obtain something of value from Anubis? Note: This task has absolutely no commercial purpose!",
    ["TaskDescription21000"]="There's too many Porings gathering outside the South Gate. Go get rid of them!",
    ["TaskDescription21001"]="While Marcs are usually gentle creatures, once you enter their undersea territory...",
    ["TaskDescription21002"]="Buying live Deviaces for high prices! Please come work with us!",
    ["TaskDescription21003"]="I finally know... Those Elder Willows don't have big feet for nothing!",
    ["TaskDescription21004"]="How strange. Why can't Munaks just walk normally?",
    ["TaskDescription21005"]="How strange. Dokebies can't feel emotions?",
    ["TaskDescription21006"]="There's a rumor about \"that\" blueprint again! It may be hidden with the next Greatest General...",
    ["TaskDescription21007"]="Let those Bongun creatures do their thing.",
    ["TaskDescription21008"]="It's said that the long-haired Sohees represent women's fashion during the old days of Payon.",
    ["TaskDescription21009"]="Looking for an adult who can defeat Eggyras! URGENT!!",
    ["TaskDescription21010"]="Is the legend of the Nine Tail true or not?",
    ["TaskDescription21011"]="There's been a Rocker infestation at the West Gate Garden! If things get any worse, the garden will be wiped out! Hurry and exterminate those Rockers!",
    ["TaskDescription21012"]="The Culinary Association has a famous roast suckling pig dish that is receiving world-wide attention. They say the ingredients are obtained right here at West Gate. Help me steal some ingredients!",
    ["TaskDescription21101"]="Not all monsters are evil, like those Horongs...",
    ["TaskDescription21102"]="Will those Goblins that swing chains every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["TaskDescription21103"]="Make all those Giant Whispers that appear in dreams go straight to the netherworld!",
    ["TaskDescription21104"]="Will those Goblins that swing maces every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["TaskDescription21105"]="Will those Kobolds that swing maces every day also have perfect biceps just like me?",
    ["TaskDescription21106"]="Huh... The pumpkin on top of Jakks. Is it their head or headgear?",
    ["TaskDescription21107"]="Those Skeleton Generals deserve better weapons... But of course, no one will forge them!",
    ["TaskDescription21108"]="Stealing from the pockets of the Wigner Chamber of Commerce? Those Goblins must have lost their minds.",
    ["TaskDescription21109"]="Sometimes Orc Warriors can set fashion trends.",
    ["TaskDescription21201"]="Legend has it that Ground Petites are descendants of an ancient race of Dragons. Any warriors brave enough to challenge them?",
    ["TaskDescription21202"]="Urgent! Traces of Baphomets have been found in the Labyrinth Forest! Please quickly help to exterminate them!",
    ["TaskDescription21203"]="Which monster shall I use to test the strength of my armor? Oh, how about going with Ghouls this year?",
    ["TaskDescription21204"]="Hee hee, does anyone want to join the Goblin Club?",
    ["TaskDescription21205"]="Only a truly powerful weapon can penetrate the incredibly tough skin as well as bones of an Orc!",
    ["TaskDescription21206"]="If you want to be a \"real\" Marionette, you have to have both form and spirit!",
    ["TaskDescription21207"]="Recruiting some humans that can tolerate the smell of canines, meow!",
    ["TaskDescription21208"]="Those vile, irredeemable Goblins... I've had enough of them!",
    ["TaskDescription21209"]="Who knew that the Orc Zombies possessed something of use?",
    ["TaskDescription21210"]="If there's no support for the theory, then all conjectures about the Sky Petites are just fantasy.",
    ["TaskDescription21301"]="Accuracy in archery has nothing to do with size, so don't underestimate these sharp little guys.",
    ["TaskDescription21302"]="No circus has a clown as evil as this. Come outside Glast Heim and \"play\" with Carat.",
    ["TaskDescription21303"]="I heard that the Kobolds outside the city are fighting again. This is bad. What if this affects the citizens coming to and from the city?",
    ["TaskDescription21304"]="They were the sharpest swords of this city, but now they turn their blades against what they once guarded.",
    ["TaskDescription21305"]="A lady deserves to be treated with gentlemanly manners, but what about... orc ladies?",
    ["TaskDescription21306"]="\"Whoa! Hey, those little Deviruchi stole my and Arlene's candy!\"—Pearson",
    ["TaskDescription21307"]="No one could have imagined this! The sauce is actually a perfect substitute for black pepper! This time it's going to make a fortune!",
    ["TaskDescription21308"]="Their armor and weapons embody the essence of ancient craftsmanship! If only we could get a set of samples...",
    ["TaskDescription21309"]="I wonder if it reminds you of the fear of leaping from a flying airship...",
    ["TaskDescription21310"]="Kobolds are monsters that live in packs, so don't expect them to fight you alone.",
    ["TaskDescription21311"]="Ooh... the mesmerizing muscles as well as a beautiful skin tone, like fresh grass...",
    ["TaskDescription21312"]="The beast that prowls the labyrinth and the prey it pursues will never be able to leave this place.",
    ["TaskDescription21313"]="Night falls. The moon and the stars begin to dance. The children go to sleep, and darkness follows like a shadow.",
    ["TaskDescription21314"]="\"Oh my God! The monsters are holding books! Could it be that they possess intelligence?!\"—Monster Researcher",
    ["TaskDescription21315"]="It is said that orcs possess first-rate skills in crafting bows and arrows. If only we could get some from them...",
    ["TaskDescription21316"]="Cat Hand Services sent a request! Kobolds have been attacking with a new type of weapon! Please provide assistance immediately!",
    ["TaskDescription21317"]="If you want to enter the lower levels of Geffen Tower, you have to pass the trials of these guardians first.",
    ["TaskDescription21318"]="I can always hear it, the wailing from deep underground... No... Make them stop...",
    ["TaskDescription21319"]="It's not just wind that whistles by their chests, but also a looming, menacing threat.",
    ["TaskDescription21320"]="Please! I want to see what Rybios' faces look like under their hoods, no matter what! Huh? You too?",
    ["TaskDescription21321"]="Ignore the Stings that invite you to dance, or you'll be the next one who needs to be saved.",
    ["TaskDescription21322"]="Only when you have looked directly into the eyes of the undead can you understand what the gaze of the abyss is.",
    ["TaskDescription21323"]="Even in death, their souls cannot be freed. Please, let the undead rest in peace.",
    ["TaskDescription21401"]="Don't you think the infestation is getting worse lately? If this continues, we will be driven away in turn!",
    ["TaskDescription21402"]="Our neighborhood is infested with rats and our food has all been ruined by them!",
    ["TaskDescription21403"]="Recently, spooky songs can always be heard at night. We should expel the witches and protect the children!",
    ["TaskDescription21404"]="Those eerie Abysmal Knights are always roaming around and I can always hear the cold hoofbeats…",
    ["TaskDescription21405"]="Affected by the distorted magic, items in the Clock Tower seem to be alive.",
    ["TaskDescription21406"]="The deceased soldiers seem to be reluctant to leave… they keep doing what they did in the last moments of their lives.",
    ["TaskDescription21407"]="Oh! Punks are everywhere, there's not even a place to stand anymore!",
    ["TaskDescription21408"]="It seems that because of the attraction to each other, a large number of Jokers gathered. Solve them before they become troublesome.",
    ["TaskDescription21409"]="Recently, the habitat of Penomena has been expanding towards the coast, and it is urgent to slow down their reproduction.",
    ["TaskDescription21410"]="The corrupted clerics are still faithful to their duties, although they no longer serve the light…",
    ["TaskDescription21411"]="Do not gaze at the shadowy mirrors, they do not reflect the faces of the living.",
    ["TaskDescription21412"]="The nobles who were buried with advanced armor seem to awake. That’s a problem.",
    ["TaskDescription21413"]="The wild souls eventually became the undead. It is really saddening…",
    ["TaskDescription21414"]="The older the clock, the more powerful the demonic spirit that resides on it.",
    ["TaskDescription21415"]="So many witches… Where the hell did they come from?! There are too many to deal with!",
    ["TaskDescription21416"]="I don't know what mechanism we triggered, but the structure in the Clock Tower moved on its own!",
    ["TaskDescription21417"]="After being transformed, the warriors seem to have become irrational monsters with just power. That's barbaric.",
    ["TaskDescription21418"]="Please bring the letter from Vienna to Miss Clarice in Kafra. Return here to claim your reward when you’re done.",
    ["TaskDescription21419"]="I am Rupert, please help me with the new batch of weapons.",
    ["TaskDescription21420"]="Those who received the quest, please come to the store to deliver meals for the guards!",
    ["TaskDescription21501"]="One of the most practical steps any Adventurer can take to improve their sleep is keep that infuriating Raggler's beak shut!",
    ["TaskDescription21502"]="Adventurers who crossed the marshland report Tri Joint colonies seem to run much more rampant...",
    ["TaskDescription21503"]="We don't believe in fairy tales. We have a fiduciary duty to stop any Thara Frog seeking to transform itself into a prince from setting foot in any lady's room!",
    ["TaskDescription21504"]="The President of the Comodo Cares for Foodies Society prays to you: If only there could be just Shellfish which never catches people's fingers living on the beach.",
    ["TaskDescription21505"]="The great once yearly migration of the sea otters has begun! We have been forced to take drastic measures against traffic disruptions...",
    ["TaskDescription21506"]="Megalodons forever crave the taste of warm flesh. As such, we make them slices of cold-chilled death.",
    ["TaskDescription21507"]="Nereids love humid environments. You would never wish to meet them in the marsh...",
    ["TaskDescription21508"]="Stem Worms have cast their furious eyes on our village, please help us retake our homes!",
    ["TaskDescription21509"]="Tide goes in and goes out. No one knows how many Asters are hiding along the shoal.",
    ["TaskDescription21510"]="We are trying to investigate Megalith's core can make nothing of it...",
    ["TaskDescription21511"]="Some uncontrollable Seals are wreaking havoc. Send 'em back!",
    ["TaskDescription21512"]="Alligators are vicious by nature, so don't trust their tears when they are \"near death.\"",
    ["TaskDescription21513"]="These Galapagos are juveniles but have become beer connoisseurs. Bad guys!",
    ["TaskDescription21514"]="When a mass of Pests gather, they have their eyes everywhere.",
    ["TaskDescription21515"]="We have every reason to believe the existence of the Anolian serves as a counterevidence to reproductive isolation.",
    ["TaskDescription21516"]="Rules of gentlemen don't apply to mobsters.",
    ["TaskDescription21517"]="Salutations to the first brave soul who eats Crab. Bravo, Bravo!",
    ["TaskDescription21518"]="Not enough arrows? Let Gargoyles shoot at you with their all, and then it's time to get what you want!",
    ["TaskDescription21519"]="What does the most beautiful Merman look like? Well, think about how to survive first before trying to find out the answer...",
    ["TaskDescription21520"]="The photographer's son discovers a closeup of the patterns on a Stalactic Golem among his late father's bloody possessions.",
    ["TaskDescription21521"]="Does Ronald remember we had an agreement to go adventuring tomorrow or not? Darn it!",
    ["TaskDescription21522"]="This is Uncle Benson. Please ask Yvette about her crafting progress for me.",
    ["TaskDescription21523"]="What's the most lucrative business in the Comodo market these days? I'd appreciate a few pointers from Jaffit.",
    ["TaskDescription21524"]="Follow in their footsteps, and you can also become a hero in the future.",
    ["TaskDescription21601"]="The curse turns this young lady's hair into venomous snakes. She now can't even tell whether she's a human or a snake herself...",
    ["TaskDescription21602"]="The Bloody Murderer seeks blood from all species, especially their own kind...",
    ["TaskDescription21603"]="Make sure you bring the special bug spray from Umbala before entering the forest.",
    ["TaskDescription21604"]="Someone says it's the soul that makes the skull burns, but the composition of the burning substance still remains unclear up to this point.",
    ["TaskDescription21605"]="The frames are made out of bones and beast tendons. Wootan Shooters may be the most primitive snipers in Midgard.",
    ["TaskDescription21606"]="The starving Hell Poodle decides to go foraging after its master implements a weight-loss plan on it...",
    ["TaskDescription21607"]="They have impenetrable rotten skin and thin oily hair.",
    ["TaskDescription21608"]="Wootan Fighters never surrender. Please give them a clean and honorable death.",
    ["TaskDescription21609"]="Use chocolate to lure those Choco here and kick their butts with the boots!",
    ["TaskDescription21610"]="Don't ever look back if you hear some uncanny frolic sounds from kids.",
    ["TaskDescription21611"]="They are the dead of ecstasy and the incarnation of slaughter.",
    ["TaskDescription21612"]="Dullahan's been searching for a substitute for his head...",
    ["TaskDescription21613"]="A true warrior is brave enough to discipline the awfully spoiled princess Parasite.",
    ["TaskDescription21614"]="One thing is guaranteed: no fairy on the moon but the witch.",
    ["TaskDescription21615"]="Banshee has countless pursuers, but she has yet to find her true love up to this day.",
    ["TaskDescription21616"]="It's said that a storm will happen in Umbala whenever a dragonfly in Luluka Forest flaps its wings.",
    ["TaskDescription21617"]="I doubt anyone can resist the primitive seduction and turn down Dryad, who is dangerous yet bewitching.",
    ["TaskDescription21618"]="Residences living next to the Stone Shooter look blessed and happy.",
    ["TaskDescription21619"]="Catch these hole-punching little things if you don't want your house to collapse.",
    ["TaskDescription21620"]="The creator of Wooden Golem has been long dead. Let's put an end to their meaningless roaming...",
    ["TaskDescription21621"]="I wonder how the day has been going for La Grada. After all, it is quite exhausting to act like a fair lady.",
    ["TaskDescription21622"]="This is a mission from Rowena. Please make an appointment in advance for other matters.",
    ["TaskDescription21623"]="Say hi for me to Kunara, and remind her that the deal we made is still valid.",
    ["TaskDescription21624"]="I wonder why Danielova stops doing morning exercises with me. I want to know why.",
    ["TaskDescription21625"]="I hear that Antares has got bitten by the flowers in Luluka Forest. Please send my regard.",
    ["TaskDescription21701"]="In the eye of the storm, it opens greenish eyes.",
    ["TaskDescription21702"]="Why is the haze still lingering around? Go ask Demon Pungus about it!",
    ["TaskDescription21703"]="We've discovered a brand-new Poring breed! It's just a bit too cold when holding it...",
    ["TaskDescription21704"]="The scent emanating from Menblatt's fingertips is a mixture of toxicity and sweetness.",
    ["TaskDescription21705"]="Born in light, longs for darkness.",
    ["TaskDescription21706"]="Their bodies are covered with rust, the marking of time.",
    ["TaskDescription21707"]="The low bushes are no good for an ambush, except for Rafflesia.",
    ["TaskDescription21708"]="The occurrence of a sandstorm is closely related to Sleeper's migration.",
    ["TaskDescription21709"]="We've discovered a new Pecopeco breed! Can they be tamed?",
    ["TaskDescription21710"]="Storms baptize them. Storms serve them.",
    ["TaskDescription21711"]="After receiving the blessing from Baphomet, they finally stopped being scapegoats.",
    ["TaskDescription21712"]="Painted with the color of the sky. Buried beneath the ruin.",
    ["TaskDescription21713"]="Even the warmest orange color can't warm up the icy-cold iron body.",
    ["TaskDescription21714"]="Every component of Sundering Dimik can be launched.",
    ["TaskDescription21715"]="Alarm! Alarm! We are under air strike!",
    ["TaskDescription21716"]="It's best to battle Fiery Dimik on a rainy day.",
    ["TaskDescription21717"]="Grass doesn't grow in ruins, but Green Venatu does.",
    ["TaskDescription21718"]="You will get insanely rich if you can get the coolant from a Frost Dimik!",
    ["TaskDescription21719"]="Kill the intruder, or get killed by the intruder.",
    ["TaskDescription21720"]="No kills. Only rests. The apocalypse is boring to death!",
    ["TaskDescription21721"]="I want to know the meaning of life...",
    ["TaskDescription21722"]="Please deliver a message for me to Vanessa: Let's talk face-to-face.",
    ["TaskDescription21723"]="Please deliver a message for me to Kasen: Let's talk face-to-face.",
    ["TaskDescription21724"]="Please bring back the thing I lost at the Border Inspection Station.",
    ["TaskDescription21725"]="Urgently hiring an assistant photographer. For interested parties, a face-to-face interview is available at any time.",
    ["TaskDescription21726"]="Please restore a very important photo for me! Please!",
    ["TaskDescription21801"]="This construction site isn't a cafe. Get these Metalings out of here!",
    ["TaskDescription21802"]="Their iron armor saved them from countless disasters since ancient times until we pulled out the bug spray.",
    ["TaskDescription21803"]="No smoking for underage Mole, even underground!",
    ["TaskDescription21804"]="These aren't your typical squishable insects; they are an Adventurer's nightmare.",
    ["TaskDescription21805"]="Ferus got a genetic makeover from some serious radiation, rocking scales in rainbow colors now.",
    ["TaskDescription21806"]="We want to see natural rainbows, not a brunch of Sky Deleter flying in the sky!",
    ["TaskDescription21807"]="Einbroch's pollution is getting worse; help us take down these Noxious.",
    ["TaskDescription21808"]="Einbroch's pollution is getting worse; help us take down these Venomous.",
    ["TaskDescription21809"]="Not everyone wearing a safety helmet in the mines is a miner; it could be a Pitman.",
    ["TaskDescription21810"]="The obsidian on the work table springs to life, launching a ruthless assault on the craftsman.",
    ["TaskDescription21811"]="Mineral sent us a warning letter, claiming it would steal the most beautiful diamond in the mine...",
    ["TaskDescription21812"]="Help! These waste stoves are gonna blow up!",
    ["TaskDescription21813"]="Something's off with my teddy bear... It's, it's looking at me!",
    ["TaskDescription21814"]="There is always only one truth! The arsonist is — Blazzer!",
    ["TaskDescription21815"]="Hate those Explosions; their bites itch and burn like crazy!",
    ["TaskDescription21816"]="To make way for trade in the desert, we've got to get rid of Gig's nest.",
    ["TaskDescription21817"]="Catch these Diabolic fooling around! It's not Halloween yet!",
    ["TaskDescription21818"]="Surrounded by flames, are these Grizzlies medium-rare or well-done?",
    ["TaskDescription21819"]="Its path leaves nothing but scorched earth.",
    ["TaskDescription21820"]="Nightmare Terror leads its victims through six layers of sweet dreams, then on the seventh...",
    ["TaskDescription21821"]="Please collect some sewage samples from Einbech Village for me.",
    ["TaskDescription21822"]="Please deliver a message to Dr. Milian outside Einbech Village for me.",
    ["TaskDescription21823"]="Please make a trip to Einbech Village for me. Details in person.",
    ["TaskDescription21901"]="Their immunity means nothing to humans—they hold no value to us.",
    ["TaskDescription21902"]="Fear of the day: What does a Drosera feast on?",
    ["TaskDescription21903"]="Hold onto your wallet—something's lurking above!",
    ["TaskDescription21904"]="Dogs are loyal friends... weasels? Not so much.",
    ["TaskDescription21905"]="How can a being formed from pure water possess human feelings?",
    ["TaskDescription21906"]="Rumor has it Phylla likes Aquarians, so they get a free pass.",
    ["TaskDescription21907"]="If you spot a Siroma in the snow, double-check that you're not lost.",
    ["TaskDescription21908"]="The Iceicle can pierce a skull, especially when gravity does its job.",
    ["TaskDescription21909"]="If you spot a Snowier in the snow, double-check that you can outrun your friends.",
    ["TaskDescription21910"]="Heartless and brutal—that's how Ice Titan has been since forever.",
    ["TaskDescription21911"]="An Ice Wolf's howl can set off an avalanche—and they never come alone.",
    ["TaskDescription21912"]="Evil can exist without cause—just ask the Beholder.",
    ["TaskDescription21913"]="Why call them Gremlin when they're so massive in size?",
    ["TaskDescription21914"]="Cold... so cold... the Gazeti would give anything to touch a flame.",
    ["TaskDescription21915"]="Once the mask fuses to flesh, taking it off is... messy.",
    ["TaskDescription21916"]="Where are you? Ah, there you are.",
    ["TaskDescription21917"]="The blood has dried and hardened. Even if washed clean, the soul won't return.",
    ["TaskDescription21918"]="A normal bite stings. Hodremlin's bite? Lethal.",
    ["TaskDescription21919"]="With a dagger in one hand and a curved blade in the other—Echio fights with precision.",
    ["TaskDescription21920"]="With a dagger in one hand and a mace in the other—Agav loves the splatter.",
    ["TaskDescription21921"]="Please deliver this season's designer catalog to our client.",
    ["TaskDescription21922"]="Nothing fresh this time? Come on!",
    ["TaskDescription21923"]="I need someone to run an errand outside the city...",
    ["TaskDescription22001"]="She never found her answer in life, only the bowstring wept because of her trembling.",
    ["TaskDescription22002"]="So much left undone, so much left unsaid... will she ever see her loved ones again?",
    ["TaskDescription22003"]="Through faith and doubt, she wandered until all paths dissolved into the haze of memory.",
    ["TaskDescription22004"]="Maybe crossing life and death is the final test for an assassin...",
    ["TaskDescription22005"]="Just like before—patrolling, training, fighting to protect the people!",
    ["TaskDescription22006"]="She's a famous scholar, a tireless student, always thinking, always learning...",
    ["TaskDescription22007"]="They say only the stars' favorite child can perform the most beautiful dance in the world.",
    ["TaskDescription22008"]="His students still remember him saying over and over—stop war with war!",
    ["TaskDescription22009"]="Having created life himself, he knows how precious it truly is.",
    ["TaskDescription22010"]="Go back in time—wander under the sun, drink beneath the stars... good old days...",
    ["TaskDescription22011"]="Please take a picture of the lab for me.",
    ["TaskDescription22012"]="Please... save my essay...",
    ["TaskDescription22013"]="Please help me find my sister!",
    ["TaskDescription25001"]="True soulmates never back down from a battle! These <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hunter Flies</color> don't stand a chance against you!",
    ["TaskDescription25002"]="True soulmates never back down from a battle! These <color=#CA2E0AFF>Whispers</color> don't stand a chance against you!",
