    ["TaskDescription50000201"]="I've finally become a member of Criatura Academy! Seeing the library shelves brimming with records of adventures makes my heart race with excitement! Soon my own stories will be inscribed here as well!",
    ["TaskDescription50001201"]="After gaining enough renown in the Rune Kingdom, you finally gained the attention of the Central Exchange Center!\nJakdal, one of their employees, wants you to work with them and says that the Central Exchange Center has the best rules and regulations in place to provide a fair and safe trading environment for all of the kingdom's subjects. If you're interested in Jakdal's proposal, why don't you first read the <color=#CA2E0AFF>\"Exchange Center Rules and Regulations\"</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription50002201"]="Taming pets and fighting alongside them... Sounds good!",
    ["TaskDescription50003201"]="The life of an adventurer includes a variety of interesting experiences besides combat, such as peacefully fishing on a shore.",
    ["TaskDescription50003202"]="If you're not interested in fishing, gardening may be more up your alley.",
    ["TaskDescription50003203"]="Sweat from swinging a pickaxe will reap shiny ore.",
    ["TaskDescription50003204"]="Smelting is wonderful. By getting better materials, you'll be able to keep improving yourself!",
    ["TaskDescription50004201"]="You heard that Lil' Kitty of Prontera can add unique magic properties to equipment! Sounds very interesting!",
    ["TaskDescription50005201"]="It is said that in addition to upgrading, there is another process to make equipment stronger called refinement! I should be qualified to try it now!",
    ["TaskDescription50006201"]="You follow Kiki's directions and check out the Mission Board on Izlude Island. There you discover something awful...",
    ["TaskDescription50006202"]="You get Upgrading Metal from the carpenter Old Clay. The ability to upgrade your equipment with it sounds amazing!",
    ["TaskDescription50006203"]="There's not enough Upgrading Metal! You have no choice but to help complete the request!",
    ["TaskDescription50006204"]="Okay, you can continue to upgrade it, but it feels like it's not enough...",
    ["TaskDescription50009201"]="The Criatura Academy New Student Headgear?! I don't think something that good will be easily obtained...",
    ["TaskDescription50009202"]="Crafting my own headgear... What an awesome experience!",
    ["TaskDescription50009203"]="This headgear looks sooo cute on you! Take a selfie to commemorate this moment!",
    ["TaskDescription50010201"]="You follow Kiki's directions and check out the Mission Board on Izlude Island. There you discover something awful...",
    ["TaskDescription50010202"]="Turns out the Mission Board is badly damaged! You find the carpenter of Izlude Island, Old Clay, to repair it, but he is... well, old.",
    ["TaskDescription50010203"]="Although the Mission Board has been repaired, the guard's mood hasn't seemed to get any better...",
    ["TaskDescription50011101"]="You heard that there is a magician in Geffen asking around about you. They seem to need your help for something important. Go to Geffen City to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find</color> a magician named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lysons</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50011102"]="You met Lysons of the Mage Guild in Geffen, who told you that Urd, the goddess of the past and one of the three Norns, is known to have hidden a shard containing the remnants of her divine consciousness in a place nobody knows. But actually, Archmage Merlin sealed different shards of divine consciousness into several Crystal Balls after founding Pentagram. However, the method of opening these Crystal Balls has always remained a mystery. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go with Lysons</color> and check out the situation.",
    ["TaskDescription50011201"]="To defeat more powerful enemies, not only must I become stronger, but my weapons must also be improved!",
    ["TaskDescription50011202"]="Hollgrehenn... I thought he was a slacker before. Who knew he was that good?",
    ["TaskDescription50012201"]="Now that the adventure has begun, you need to buy some good equipment first!",
    ["TaskDescription50013201"]="What kind of adventurer do you aspire to be in Midgard? A lone wolf? Do you want to be part of a family? Or would you like to be a leader of a party? The Adventurers Guild will help recommend the best path forward for you based on your preferences.",
    ["TaskDescription50014201"]="Although shots haven't been fired in the conflict between the Chambers of Commerce, the faint smell of gunpowder is in the air.",
    ["TaskDescription50015201"]="What kind of tablet is this? It seems to be faintly glowing? Go take a look...",
    ["TaskDescription50016201"]="Hollgrehenn's Magic Furnace possesses fantastic power. But it's useless when broken. If you want to see what it can do, help fix it!",
    ["TaskDescription50016202"]="It's fixed! Seeing the magic furnace puffing and smoking makes you feel like it can create something amazing!",
    ["TaskDescription50017201"]="I heard that Odin's protection can make our adventure go more smoothly. Is this true?",
    ["TaskDescription50018201"]="Having learned Falconry Mastery, of course you got to get a falcon companion! Go rent a falcon!",
    ["TaskDescription50019201"]="Having advanced to your 2nd class, of course you got to get a class mount! Go obtain your new mount!",
    ["TaskDescription50020201"]="Speaking of merchants, you can't be without your own cart! Go rent your own cart!",
    ["TaskDescription50021201"]="You receive a secret letter from the Rekenber Institute.\nFrom reading the contents, you learn that the institute is requesting assistance from adventurers far and wide for reasons that cannot be disclosed to the public.\nThe end of the letter states that those interested can go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dr. Emanuel</color>, who is temporarily stationed with the research team there. Why don't you heard over there and find out what's going on?",
    ["TaskDescription50021202"]="From talking to Emanuel, you learn that an epidemic is ravaging the continent! In order to produce more vaccines, the Rekenber Institute needs assistance from a large number of adventurers to obtain the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Cell Solutions</color> they need from specific monsters.\nThe only way to survive this crisis is to work together. There's no time to lose, so get moving!",
    ["TaskDescription50021203"]="Emanuel asks you to give the precious Cell Solution to his assistant, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Jesse</color>, and states that your help may still be needed in the future.\nHe tells you that the virus may continue to mutate and that he'll keep you updated with the details in the Virus Specimen Handbook.",
    ["TaskDescription50022201"]="You see Lyanna, the kingdom's court clerk, who seems to be calling for you to come over and assist her...\nHurry and see what kind of help she needs!",
    ["TaskDescription50023201"]="You won the Kingdom Quiz's grand prize! With your extraordinary luck, you seem to have become the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Child of Fortune</color>! Which is... What is it exactly? Go talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lyanna</color> to learn more!",
    ["TaskDescription50023202"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color> decides to give you a riddle, the answer to which nobody knows to this day, and you decide to test your abilities as the Child of Fortune.",
    ["TaskDescription50023203"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Hollgrehenn</color> seems to be looking for the Child of Fortune. Does he need some kind of help? You decide to go and ask him about it.",
    ["TaskDescription50024201"]="Kafra Corporation provides high-quality and reliable <color=#CA2E0AFF>warehouse</color> services. Speak to W in Prontera to find out more!",
    ["TaskDescription50025201"]="Morts, one of Midgard's most popular bards, seems to have come up against a challenge recently—a mysterious visitor is stealing his limelight. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color> if he needs help!",
    ["TaskDescription50025202"]="From a distance, you see a mysterious man in Rose Red Tavern surrounded by a crowd, and learn from Morts that the mysterious man is actually quite a talented musician. To help Morts regain his popularity, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>approach the mysterious man for more information</color>. Now, go ask him who he really is!",
    ["TaskDescription50025203"]="You learn from the mysterious man that he is an artist who came to this world by accident when a dimensional gap opened. He is willing to speak with Morts any time he wants. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go and tell Morts the good news</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50025204"]="After learning the identity of the mysterious man, Morts immediately decides to challenge him to a musical battle. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Morts</color> as he begins this fateful duel!",
    ["TaskDescription50025205"]="In the duel between Morts and the mysterious man, they seem to establish a tacit connection, putting on a wonderful performance for the audience of Rose Red Tavern. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>share opinions with the mysterious man and Morts</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50025206"]="You've finally become good friends with the mysterious man and learned that his name is Jimmy Lin. Jimmy Lin tells you that the skateboard he's held dear for many years has disappeared. You hear that the merchant Vienna Lindra has a strange item on sale at the moment. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Vienna Lindra's shop</color> to find out <color=#CA2E0AFF>about the skateboard</color> on Jimmy Lin's behalf.",
    ["TaskDescription50025207"]="After a bit of investigation, you find the skateboard and another mysterious object at Vienna Lindra's shop. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take them back to Jimmy Lin!</color>",
    ["TaskDescription50026201"]="You suddenly receive a secret letter from the Kingdom Defense Force, mentioning that they have encountered certain undisclosed difficulties and are requesting the assistance of the most powerful adventurers. The letter says that if you're willing to help the Kingdom, you should head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> to find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Staff Officer Hershey</color> for more information on the situation. Go and find Hershey and see what has happened.",
    ["TaskDescription50026202"]="You learn from Staff Officer Hershey that the Kingdom Defense Force is preparing for a battle against the monsters from the dimensional rift. To ensure victory in battle, he needs your help to collect some additional war preparation resources. After checking the Kingdom's War Preparation Resource Manual, you discover that the resource they're in most dire need of is Sharpening Stones. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>collect 1 Sharpening Stone and give it to Hershey</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50026203"]="With the Sharpening Stone you collected in hand, you seek out Staff Officer Hershey. After carefully examining it, he confirms that it is indeed a war preparation resource required by the Kingdom Defense Force, and asks you to take it to Freida, Captain of the Second Regiment's Assault Squad. If demand for new war preparation resources arise in the future, he will update them in the Kingdom's War Preparation Resource Manual, and you can check the details with Hershey at any time. Now, go and find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Captain Freida</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50027201"]="You've been adventuring in Midgard for some time now, and you hear that Ophelia, the Valkyrie, has been looking for an adventurer with extraordinary strength. It seems she has some instructions she wishes to convey. Why don't you <color=#CA2E0AFF>go and speak with Ophelia</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription50027202"]="You learn from Ophelia that, before Ragnarok, the three Norns in charge of fate foresaw the impending disaster. To make sure that seeds of hope remained in the world after Ragnarok, they warned the gods, and so the gods placed fragments of their consciousness into vessels called Shadow Equipment. When Shadow Equipment is awakened, it can call upon the power of the gods to temporarily summon divine weapons. To guide adventurers and organizations possessing the power to change the world after Ragnarok, and lead the world into the light, the Goddess of the Present, Verthandi, preserved her consciousness in this way on the continent of Midgard. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Head to your Guild territory</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>pray beneath the statue of Verthandi</color>, and listen to the Goddess of Fate's guidance.",
    ["TaskDescription50028201"]="In the blink of an eye, you have established yourself as an adventurer of Midgard, and have met many like-minded companions. On this particular day, as you wander around Prontera, you are suddenly grabbed by a frantic girl...",
    ["TaskDescription50028202"]="After a brief dispute, the strange girl forces you to stand before Archbishop Wolmas. She seems to have mistaken you for someone else. What is the meaning of this farce?",
    ["TaskDescription50029201"]="As the Lantern Festival arrives, the amusement park outside of Prontera South Gate seems to have changed slightly. You encounter a girl from a foreign country there with two cute bunnies. She invites you to join her in celebrating this year's Lantern Festival. However, it seems there's more to this invitation than meets the eye...",
    ["TaskDescription50029202"]="You beat Moon in the riddle challenge, and she marvels at your profound knowledge. However, the festival has just begun, and there are more games waiting to be challenged. If you're ready, hurry up and <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep pace with Moon</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription50029203"]="After successfully completing the rocking chair trial, Moon commends you on your excellent performance, but she also reminds you that the game is far from over. Spurred on by Moon's insistence, you <color=#CA2E0AFF>set out for the next challenge</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription50029204"]="The mystery of the carousel poses no threat of bamboozling you. Now, Moon asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>take a ride on the Mini Train with your most important friend</color>. This is the festival blessing she has bestowed upon you. She hopes you can create unforgettable memories with the one you cherish most. So, who do you hold in your heart...?",
    ["TaskDescription50032201"]="You already have your own Shadow Equipment, please visit Hollgrehenn to learn how to develop Shadow Weapon materials",
    ["TaskDescription50033201"]="On the west side of Izlude Island, you encountered two ghosts arguing. They were dressed in ancient clothes that clearly don't belong to your time. Curiosity prompted you to sneak up closer to the two. What they were discussing came as something of a surprise.",
    ["TaskDescription50033202"]="You accepted a mission from Lowell and Eleanor to help them purify the tainted Fragments of Ymir's Heart together. It's also your duty as the successor to Odin's bloodline. When you're ready, set out immediately and <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Eleanor to the Heart Pedestal</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription50034201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50035201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50036201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50037201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50038201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50039201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50040201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50041201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50042201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50043201"]="If you obtain an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ymir Crystal</color> in the process of purifying Ymir's Heart, remember to give it to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eleanor</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50044201"]="You received a letter from the Eden Group requesting help. From it, you learned that the Eden Group seems to be having a little trouble with their research in Glast Heim, and are asking for your assistance. If you are willing, <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Glast Heim</color> to get more details from Eden Group member <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sarence</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription50044202"]="You followed the instructions of the letter and arrived in Glast Heim to find Sarence. He told you that the Eden Group recently discovered an epic poem written in an unknown script, and to decipher these ancient texts, they need a significant number of text samples. For this reason, Sarence asked for your help in finding more samples with ancient texts to help them advance their deciphering work. The details have already been recorded in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Archaeological Notes</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50044203"]="Sarence requested that you deliver the <color=#CA2E0AFF>text samples</color> to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Laforet</color>, who is solely responsible for the deciphering work. They say that a rather large sample base is needed to complete the deciphering, so there's no time to waste and you should start as soon as possible.",
    ["TaskDescription50045201"]="Morts, one of Midgard's most popular bards, seems to have come up against a challenge recently—a mysterious visitor is stealing his limelight. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> and ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Morts</color> if he needs help!",
    ["TaskDescription50045202"]="From a distance, you see a mysterious man in Rose Red Tavern surrounded by a crowd, and learn from Morts that the mysterious man is actually quite a talented musician. To help Morts regain his popularity, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>approach the mysterious man for more information</color>. Now, go ask him who he really is!",
    ["TaskDescription50045203"]="You learn from the mysterious man that he is an artist who came to this world by accident when a dimensional gap opened. He is willing to speak with Morts any time he wants. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go and tell Morts the good news</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50045204"]="After learning the identity of the mysterious man, Morts immediately decides to challenge him to a musical battle. Now, <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Morts</color> as he begins this fateful duel!",
    ["TaskDescription50045205"]="In the duel between Morts and the mysterious man, they seem to establish a tacit connection, putting on a wonderful performance for the audience of Rose Red Tavern. Go and <color=#CA2E0AFF>share opinions with the mysterious man and Morts</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50045206"]="You've finally become good friends with the mysterious man and learned that his name is Schumann. Schumann tells you that the skateboard he's held dear for many years has disappeared. You hear that the merchant Vienna Lindra has a strange item on sale at the moment. You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Vienna Lindra's shop</color> to find out <color=#CA2E0AFF>about the skateboard</color> on Schumann's behalf.",
    ["TaskDescription50045207"]="After a bit of investigation, you find the skateboard and another mysterious object at Vienna Lindra's shop. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Take them back to Schumann!</color>",
    ["TaskDescription50046101"]="Some strange visitors have come to the kingdom. Go and ask them what business they have here.",
    ["TaskDescription50047101"]="In this special day, you meet the strange girl who is waving warmly at you in Prontera…",
    ["TaskDescription50047102"]="The strange girl is called Mirabelle, and she claims to be the emissary of the White Valentine's Day event. It’s said that players who complete her quests in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Amusement Park</color> will be rewarded!",
    ["TaskDescription50048101"]="You have heard that a great celebration is being prepared in the Morroc Desert, and it seems to be related to water. Being curious, you decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Heflee for information</color>…",
    ["TaskDescription50048102"]="Heflee introduces you to the upcoming Songkran event. You are having a nice chat when she suddenly realizes that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the venue for the Water Gun Battle</color> has not yet been decided, and the busy Heflee asks for your help…",
    ["TaskDescription50050101"]="Everything you have experienced since coming to Criatura Academy has been so new and strange to you, and you wonder to yourself, with so many possibilities before you—what is the best way to go about setting a starting point for yourself? You should probably go to Criatura Academy and ask Kiki, the new student adviser, for help!",
    ["TaskDescription50050102"]="Kiki enthusiastically introduces the academy's Master system to you, and recommends that you apply for a Master of your own to learn from. If you're interested, go and talk to Dean Mainz!",
    ["TaskDescription50051101"]="Without even realizing it, you have grown from a clueless newcomer to an independent expert Adventurer, and now, your time at Criatura Academy has added a new accomplishment to your long list of feats. One day, you hear that Dean Mainz is recruiting new Masters for the academy. Perhaps it's time to return to Criatura Academy...",
    ["TaskDescription50051102"]="Dean Mainz acknowledges your achievements and encourages you to become a Master. However, if you want to obtain the official title of a Criatura Academy Master, you must pass the Masters' Examination. Talk to Dean Mainz to begin the first test!",
    ["TaskDescription50051103"]="You pass the first test without too much trouble, and now, the second test is a series of questions. Dean Mainz advises you to listen to your inner voice. If you feel prepared, talk to Dean Mainz to start the second test, while his words of confidence are still fresh in your mind!",
    ["TaskDescription50051104"]="You have completed both of the tests, and you feel as though you have gained a lot from this experience. Now, all you need to do is take an oath before the Heart Pedestal, and you'll officially become a Master of Criatura Academy. Hurry up and follow Dean Mainz!",
    ["TaskDescription50052101"]="When you walk past the central fountain, you find Morts standing aside with his lute, and he looks in a slump. What's going on?",
    ["TaskDescription50052102"]="It turns out Morts was assigned the task by the princess to send out the invitations for the ROX 1st Anniversary Music Festival. Somehow Lunatic rolls in and take all of them away! It will definitely make a dent in Morts' perfect impression if the princess finds out this has happened. This is a big deal, hurry up to Prontera South Gate and search for Lunatics to seize back the invitations!",
    ["TaskDescription50052103"]="You hand over those invitations to Morts, but he seems to be allergic to the down fur of the Lunatic and is unable to carry on the task. There are still some invitees on the list yet to receive invitations. Anyway, you decide to take over from here since you're such a bleeding heart.",
    ["TaskDescription50052104"]="You finish sending out the invitations after running around Prontera. Just when you try to catch your breath, Miss Vienna Lindra reminds you that Morts, who's nearby, must be worrying about the music festival. Report to Morts now!",
    ["TaskDescription50053101"]="While resting at Rose Red Tavern, you overhear a heated discussion between Rowan and The TOYS about a song or something. Your curiosity drives you to get closer to find out more.",
    ["TaskDescription50053102"]="It turns out that The TOYS is searching for inspiration for a new song and wants everyone's approval. At Rowan's request, you and The TOYS embark on a kingdom-wide tour. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Meet him at the entrance of Rose Red Tavern</color> to depart.",
    ["TaskDescription50053103"]="Just as you enthusiastically put the river lantern into the water, Xavier appears suddenly to stop you and recommends the newest way of praying with Drift Bottles to you. After you try it out, Xavier keeps his promise and agrees to take you to his secret base to search for inspiration. Follow him for now!",
    ["TaskDescription50053104"]="Xavier's secret base is actually some Poring ruins! In the ruins, Xavier tells you that this place was once a wall that was used to repel monster attacks until the Evil Serpent Jormungand was slayed. Inspired by this place, The TOYS tells you he will immediately return to Rose Red Tavern to start creating, and agrees to meet you there.",
    ["TaskDescription50053105"]="At Rose Red Tavern, you complete the performance of the first melody. The TOYS excitedly tells you about his plan. He wants to get inspiration from the customs of each major city, as he believes he can create an excellent piece if he can integrate all these different styles. You agree to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet at the entrance of Rose Red Tavern</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to Izlude Island together</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053106"]="As soon as you get off the ship, you encounter Old Clay at the port, looking very worried. It turns out that he is worried about a batch of unwaxed wood. After you help him solve his problem, to express his gratitude, the craftsman decides to show you his lifetime's greatest work. You gladly <color=#CA2E0AFF>follow Old Clay</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053107"]="The greatest work of Old Clay's lifetime is Criatura Academy. As the designer of the academy, Old Clay has replaced the original building materials many times. He is now worried that his connection with the building will be lost after a hundred years as future generations take over the maintenance of the building. You spend some time to help him get his head around his concerns. After the tour, The TOYS has managed to find some inspiration and needs to return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color> to continue creating.",
    ["TaskDescription50053108"]="You listen to The TOYS's new song at Rose Red Tavern. After that, you decide to go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alberta</color> to prepare for another inspirational encounter.",
    ["TaskDescription50053109"]="You encounter Pascal, who is on vacation in Alberta, and he \"enthusiastically\" invites you to try a local specialty: baked seabird eggs. After the meal, he motions for you to follow him. He seems to be walking towards the <color=#CA2E0AFF>port</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053110"]="Following close behind Pascal, you experience the unique tranquility and bustle of the port city of Alberta. Inspired by this experience, The TOYS decides to immediately <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Rose Red Tavern</color> to continue creating. Pascal recommends a ship operated by the Alson Fleet to him.",
    ["TaskDescription50053111"]="You listen to The TOYS's new creation at Rose Red Tavern. He praises your dancing and agrees to meet you at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>entrance of Rose Red Tavern</color> to go on another trip together.",
    ["TaskDescription50053112"]="Heflee of Desert Green Tavern listens to the stories of your adventures after arriving at Morroc and hopes you can give some exotic gifts to her friend, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Pattie</color>. In exchange, she will tell you everything about Morroc. For now, enjoy the culture of the desert with Heflee!",
    ["TaskDescription50053113"]="In the oasis next to Sphinx Cavern, Heflee tells you various legends and stories of Morroc, which inspire The TOYS. You agree to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet at Rose Red Tavern</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053114"]="You hear many different melodies at Rose Red Tavern. After the performance, you and The TOYS once again <color=#CA2E0AFF>leave Rose Red Tavern for Geffen</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053115"]="You wake up Winry from her coma. She seems to have been given a terrible fright by the underground monsters. After you take a photo of the situation underground and give it to Master Jesqurienne, she gives you a beam of light shaped by magic to <color=#CA2E0AFF>give you a tour of Geffen Tower</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053116"]="The magical beam of light gives you a full tour of Geffen Tower. After encountering the magic of the parallel world for the first time, The TOYS was surprised that he gained more inspiration and wanted to use the teleporter to <color=#CA2E0AFF>return to Rose Red Tavern</color> to continue creating.",
    ["TaskDescription50053117"]="You complete the performance in Rose Red Tavern but are still reluctant to leave Geffen. You travel to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>, and The TOYS seems to be looking forward to finding traces of the gods here.",
    ["TaskDescription50053118"]="Helmor, whose prayers have been interrupted many times by a clanging sound, asks you to convey her distress to Brock Sledgehammer. However, Brock Sledgehammer thinks that Helmor's prayers are useless. He refuses to disclose more information and only tells you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>ask Helmor</color> about it.",
    ["TaskDescription50053119"]="From the conversation with Helmor, you learn that her partner, Joelso, has been bedridden for many years. The pious Helmor has prayed many times to the Goddess, but received no response. She is lost in her pain and cannot help you. The TOYS becomes silent for a moment before agreeing to <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet you at Rose Red Tavern</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50053120"]="After finishing the performance in the tavern, The TOYS says that Helmor's misfortune has evoked some emotions in him and inspired him. After you <color=#CA2E0AFF>meet at Rose Red Tavern</color>, you decide that <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color>, a place reputed to be a truly pure land, will be the last stop on your journey.",
    ["TaskDescription50053121"]="At Payon, you encounter a reclusive expert called Peerless Jin. He wants to share his destiny in meeting you with a new visitor to Payon, hoping you will form ties with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kao</color>. You complete his test. After you return to Peerless Jin's residence, he tells you a piece of Payon's history that is hard to verify the truth of, but when he gets to the turning point, he slips away to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Seocho Market</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription50053122"]="Peerless Jin finishes telling his story at Seocho Market. He wants you to stop worrying about Helmor's tragedy and to welcome your destiny with calmness. The TOYS is inspired by this and agrees to meet you at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Rose Red Tavern</color>, as that place is both the start and the end of his journey.",
    ["TaskDescription50054101"]="You heard that there is a magician in Geffen asking around about you. They seem to need your help for something important. Go to Geffen City to find a magician named Lysons.",
    ["TaskDescription50054102"]="It turns out that Lysons has been searching for a group of adventurers who saved the world from crisis mentioned by a prophecy and has finally made contact with you. What you must do next is work to recreate the prophecy and find a way to train a hero to save the world.",
    ["TaskDescription50054103"]="The second step is finding another person mentioned by the oracle—one who wields a key that unlocks sealed events. A variety of signs all point to the librarian Winry. You find that the history books stored here can be transformed into a gateway to the past through a ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription50054104"]="You've solved the issue of access, yet the battlefield ancient warriors once fought on cannot be faced by one person alone. The prophecy mentioned that the heroes relied on an artifact called the \"locator\". It is at this point that you find the crystal ball in the Library beginning to glow.",
    ["TaskDescription50054105"]="So far, Lysons and Winry have completed the remaining arrangements for the rest of the prophecy. Now, both people and items are all prepared. With this gate to a realm of epic illusion, it will not be long now before the training of heroes capable of saving the world begins.",
    ["TaskDescription50055101"]="You meet a sneaky stranger in the halls of Criatura Academy. The person looks like he wants to talk to Dean Mainz rather desperately but does not dare come forward. As a kind-hearted Adventurer, will you <color=#CA2E0AFF>help</color> him?",
    ["TaskDescription50055102"]="It turns out the stranger is named Travers, and he is the professor of the new Class Conversion course in Criatura Academy. He asks you to go to the library to pick up the file to report for duty, and you run into <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> by coincidence in the library...",
    ["TaskDescription50055103"]="Dean Mainz shows you Travers' file. It's nothing short of a template for a problem student. But why is he calling himself Professor Travers? You decide to <color=#CA2E0AFF>seek answers from Dean Mainz</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50055104"]="Finally, you await Travers in the library. Now <color=#CA2E0AFF>go ahead</color> and ask your questions!",
    ["TaskDescription50056101"]="The enchanters of Al De Baran have announced their latest enchantment conversion technique to the public. Go to the “Alchemy Capital” now and find out more from Zachary~",
    ["TaskDescription50057101"]="Passing by the smithy in Prontera, you hear the call of Hollgrehenn. It appears he has a new discovery to share with you...",
    ["TaskDescription50058101"]="A stranger named Kusari approaches you on the bustling streets of Prontera. From the looks of it, they are in dire need of help...",
    ["TaskDescription50061101"]="The guest from the Parallel World seems to have something to tell you. Go look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Eren Jaeger</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription50062101"]="The guest from the Parallel World seems to have something to tell you. Go look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Armin Arlert</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription50063101"]="The guest from the Parallel World seems to have something to tell you. Go look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mikasa Ackerman</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription50064101"]="While clearing up the battlefield at the Prontera South Gate, you meet a stranger named <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zeke Jaeger</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription50065101"]="The guest from the Parallel World seems to have something to tell you. Go look for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Levi</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription50066101"]="There is a stranger named Lingjun Chu mumbling to himself on the busy street of Prontera. Looks like he desperately needs help...",
    ["TaskDescription50069101"]="In the mid-summer, when you are just about to wrap up the adventure in the Morroc Desert and go on a vacation in Prontera. Heflee stops you...",
    ["TaskDescription50069102"]="Heflee introduces the summer event that is currently being prepared for you and asks for your help...",
    ["TaskDescription50070101"]="You are venturing everywhere on the continent of Midgard, and you hear the summon of Brunhild all of a sudden...",
    ["TaskDescription50071101"]="Midgard isn't as peaceful as it seems, and new crises are emerging from places we aren't aware of...",
    ["TaskDescription50072101"]="There are sounds vaguely coming out of the void.",
    ["TaskDescription50073101"]="Monsters are coming out of the void.",
    ["TaskDescription50076101"]="A scream pierced the sky above the silent Geffen Tower...",
    ["TaskDescription50076102"]="The screamer's name is Andre. Out of curiosity about the work of his classmate, Diorus, he sneaked into Diorus' dormitory and was turned into a girl by the residual magic energy. She asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>repair the broken protective clothing with the Dragon Scale</color> and collect the escaped magic energy.",
    ["TaskDescription50076103"]="After the restoration is completed, you put on protective clothing and enter the Geffen Dungeon 1F with a collection device to <color=#CA2E0AFF>search for the escaped magic energy</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50076104"]="You have finally collected the escaped magic energy. To \"thank\" you, Andre has generously prepared a <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera Meeting</color> for you and Diorus.",
    ["TaskDescription50077101"]="As Christmas is just around the corner, the workload in the Toy Factory has increased significantly. Garm seizes the chance and invades the Toy Factory, bewitching the denizens who reside in the factory. The managers ask Adventurers to help expel those invaders and sober up the bewitched denizens.",
    ["TaskDescription50078101"]="When you get to the factory, you realize the worker are not in their right mind. Since Christmas day is getting close, the managers want you to be the supervisor on the production chain and expel those Garm Babies that are bewitching the Cookie workers. Most importantly, make the workers sober up as soon as possible! They're all counting on you so the denizens can receive their latest toys this Christmas!",
    ["TaskDescription50079101"]="When you get to the factory, you realize the worker are not in their right mind. Since Christmas day is getting close, the managers want you to be the supervisor on the production chain and expel those Garm Babies that are bewitching the Christmas Cookie workers. Most importantly, make the workers sober up as soon as possible! They're all counting on you so the denizens can receive their latest toys this Christmas!",
    ["TaskDescription50080101"]="It appears that the latest batch of toys does not meet the standard. Turns out the Gram Babies are what caused it. You now need to clear the inferior products and deal with those Garm Babies and their power. That's no way to let the denizens receive these inferior products!",
    ["TaskDescription50081101"]="The toy productions are done by the workers with all their hard work. Somehow, the toys start moving on their own! Gram Babies are invading once again! For the sake of getting the toys to the denizens in time, please expel them one more time!",
    ["TaskDescription50083101"]="Here comes the most popular event among the Lutie! Snow Festival! These passionate Gingerbread Men have sent the Icing Gingerbread to Midgard as a holiday ambassador to provide the teleport service for all kind-hearted Adventurers!",
    ["TaskDescription50087101"]="A new, epic war has started. Talk to Lysons and set off, revealing your destiny...",
    ["TaskDescription50088101"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Beneath Odin's Statue in Prontera</color>, a woman with fiery red hair and crimson pupils is whispering...",
    ["TaskDescription50088102"]="Encountering the incarnation of Sol, the Sun Goddess, beneath Odin's Statue, you discover that numerous Fire Boulders from the sun chariot have descended upon Midgard, with even traces of these blocks <color=#CA2E0AFF>near Prontera</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription50089101"]="After a thousand times of socketing, splitting, and dismantling, Brock Sledgehammer finally acquires this secret technique—Star Card Upgrade!",
    ["TaskDescription50091101"]="Despite being set apart by the Wonderland, the bond remains strong! Who will come through the Dimensional Gap this time? Hurry back to Prontera and reveal the answer now!",
    ["TaskDescription50093101"]="The abnormal weather of Midgard still persists, and Sol, the Goddess of the Sun, has also disappeared. You decide to go to the Heart Pedestal to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brunhild the Goddess...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription50093102"]="Under the Heart Pedestal, you see Sol talking to Brunhild. She refuses to believe that Ragnarok has come and that Mani, the God of the Moon, has fallen into a deep slumber. So she decides to head to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Underwater Temple</color> and see for herself.",
    ["TaskDescription50093103"]="Sol can sense the residual aura of Mani, the God of the Moon, at the Underwater Temple. When you try to console her, she tells you that you can <color=#CA2E0AFF>pick a \"Luna\"</color> for her if you really want to do something for her.",
    ["TaskDescription50094101"]="You sensed the goddess's beckoning once more. Please <color=#CA2E0AFF>make your way to the Heart Pedestal...</color>",
    ["TaskDescription50094102"]="Upon reaching the Heart Pedestal, Brunhild unveils the story of Sol's past to you. She explains that as the scattered Fire Boulders are being steadily gathered, \"Sol\" is becoming more and more feeble. At this point, Brunhild is unable to discern Sol's whereabouts. Amid this uncertainty, she implores you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>find Sol</color>, wishing to say a last goodbye to her trusted friend.",
    ["TaskDescription50094103"]="In the Mjolnir Mountains, you encounter a weakened Sol. She reveals that her memory slowly returns as the Fire Boulders are retrieved, signaling a decrease in the continent's fanaticism. Just then, Brunhild makes her appearance...",
    ["TaskDescription50095101"]="Tony Chir, the Head of the Free Arena, has sent an invitation to you. Seems like he has a new challenge for you.",
    ["TaskDescription50096101"]="You received a request from a merchant named Ronald, asking you to find a fishing expert and promising you <color=#CA2E0AFF>generous compensation</color> once the job is done.",
    ["TaskDescription50096102"]="You stumbled upon Xavier, who was nearly starved to death. You gave him a Carp. In return, Xavier wrote down the <color=#CA2E0AFF>recommendation letter Ronald was asking for</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50096103"]="You handed over Xavier's letter to Ronald. Ronald kept his promise and gifted you a <color=#CA2E0AFF>luxurious estate</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50097101"]="You've felt the summon from Brunhild, and it seems like it's about <color=#CA2E0AFF>heroes from the Parallel World</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription50098101"]="Go to Prontera Central Plaza. Take a photo with Watchdog Man Statue and check in.",
    ["TaskDescription50099101"]="Ronald introduced you to the mine butler, Lehner. You now need to learn the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knowledge and skills of how to manage the mine</color> from Lehner.",
    ["TaskDescription50099102"]="Ronald introduced you to the pond butler, Peierls. You now need to learn the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knowledge and skills of how to manage the pond</color> from Peierls.",
    ["TaskDescription50099103"]="Ronald introduced you to the farmland butler, Skylie. You now need to learn the <color=#CA2E0AFF>knowledge and skills of how to manage the farmland</color> from Skylie.",
    ["TaskDescription50099104"]="Lehner was telling you that there's a <color=#CA2E0AFF>precious ore vein</color> hidden in the mine. But you need to be all ready for any surprises if you're going to dig it up.",
    ["TaskDescription50099105"]="After using the teleport item Ronald gave you, you arrived at your home for the very first time. You saw Ronald was expecting you already.",
    ["TaskDescription50099106"]="Ronald introduced you to the mine butler, Lehner. You now need to learn certain knowledge about your new home from him.",
    ["TaskDescription50099107"]="Ronald introduced you to the pond butler, Peierls. You now need to learn certain knowledge about your new home from him.",
    ["TaskDescription50099108"]="Ronald introduced you to the farmland butler, Skylie. You now need to learn certain knowledge about your new home from her.",
    ["TaskDescription50099109"]="After a crash course with Skylie, you're now ready to construct a home of a higher level.",
    ["TaskDescription50099110"]="After a crash course with Lehner, you're now ready to construct a home of a higher level.",
    ["TaskDescription50099111"]="After a crash course with Peierls, you're now ready to construct a home of a higher level.",
    ["TaskDescription50099112"]="After a crash course with Skylie, you're now ready to construct a home of a higher level.",
    ["TaskDescription50101101"]="After running your home for a while, Butler Ronald swings by to introduce you to a seasoned craftsman.",
    ["TaskDescription50101102"]="Rony shows you the new addition to your home and tells you he can craft some furniture for you if you have enough materials.",
    ["TaskDescription50101103"]="After looking at your home, Rony tells you he can craft some furniture for you if you have enough materials.",
    ["TaskDescription50112101"]="Capture the Splendorous Moment of Ken-Oh, Behold the Legend of the Conqueror",
    ["TaskDescription50113101"]="You received a secret letter from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>, summoning you to meet him in Prontera...",
    ["TaskDescription50114101"]="Raoh's legion is moving towards Midgard. Quickly, answer <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brunhild</color>'s call and defend Midgard together!",
    ["TaskDescription50114102"]="As the goddess foretold, an arrow has shattered the peace of Prontera. Commander <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bernard</color> of the Kingdom Defense Force needs your help...",
    ["TaskDescription50114103"]="After getting the challenge letter from Raoh's vanguard, Bernard mentions he must head back to the palace to plan it out. Now, your job is to <color=#CA2E0AFF>get in touch with Kenshiro</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription50115101"]="You run into Kenshiro and Yuria training in the wild. After fending off the vanguard's assault, they're still on high alert, seemingly waiting for someone...",
    ["TaskDescription50115102"]="After some talking, Raoh shows up, full of ambition, claiming the Ken-Oh legion has joined the fray, and he'll win the battle. As he leaves, some <color=#CA2E0AFF>monsters under control</color> jump at you from the shadows.",
    ["TaskDescription50116101"]="After defeating Raoh's monster vanguards, you see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yuria</color> and Rei near the church cemetery...",
    ["TaskDescription50116102"]="Follow Yuria's advice and offer a prayer for the fallen soldiers, then go find Kenshiro!",
    ["TaskDescription50117101"]="With Kenshiro's help, you have put an end to Raoh's ambitions. Now, it's time to go to Izlude Island and report to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brunhild</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription50117102"]="Brunhild praises your heroic efforts and mentions the Dimensional Gap will soon reopen, with <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kenshiro</color> and the others returning to their world. As the host on this side of the world, let's hear out our guests' final wishes!",
    ["TaskDescription50117103"]="Upon returning to Prontera, you ask Kenshiro if he has any unfilled goals here. Kenshiro responds that his goal can only be accomplished in the Otherworld, where he came from. However, he wants you to bring <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yuria</color> a pot of flowers to make up for her regrets in the past.",
    ["TaskDescription50118101"]="Glast Heim has been swarming with Defense Force Soldiers lately. Let's find out what's happening!",
    ["TaskDescription50118102"]="You chat with a Defense Force Soldier, and he recognizes you as the legendary Adventurer. He mentions something similar to a Dimensional Gap that appears here, so they've been ordered to keep an eye on it and prevent anyone from getting close. You'll need to head back to Prontera to talk to Bohr if you want to investigate. As you're about to leave, you hear Fulkyn's voice.",
    ["TaskDescription50119101"]="The time has come to meet Fulkyn. Go to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Geffen</color> now!",
    ["TaskDescription50120101"]="According to Fulkyn, the next Dimensional Gap is at Prontera West Gate...",
    ["TaskDescription50121101"]="Head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color> and wait for Fulkyn!",
    ["TaskDescription50121102"]="Your conversation with Fulkyn is suddenly interrupted by Hornet. After the battle, Fulkyn asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>keep up with him</color> and track down the Hornet colony.",
    ["TaskDescription50122101"]="Fulkyn's probably recovered by now. Let's go to the Sograt Desert and keep exploring.",
    ["TaskDescription50123101"]="The meeting time with Fulkyn has come again. Go to Payon West to meet him.",
    ["TaskDescription50124101"]="Time to reveal the secrets. Head to Payon and listen out to Fulkyn's analysis.",
    ["TaskDescription50126101"]="An unseen terror is quietly descending upon Midgard. Quickly, answer Brunhild's call and defend Midgard together!",
    ["TaskDescription50126102"]="Following the goddess' instructions, you find Subaru Natsuki in Prontera. Upon hearing about the looming danger, Subaru Natsuki asks you to help fend off the evil.",
    ["TaskDescription50128101"]="The Geffen scholar <color=#CA2E0AFF>Lysons</color> wants to show you what he's discovered about the Trial Illusion. Go find him now!",
    ["TaskDescription50129101"]="Looks like the maid from another world has her own worries. Hurry over and see if you can lend a hand!",
    ["TaskDescription50129102"]="So, Rem is looking for a poetry collection to fill her spare time. Go find W for clues on where to find the Bard, Morts.",
    ["TaskDescription50129103"]="Based on W's info, you head to the Rose Red Tavern to rescue an utterly wasted Morts...",
    ["TaskDescription50129104"]="Upon hearing your request, Morts suggests trading the poetry collection for some Rose Red Wine. Go ask the boss, Isabella, at the front desk for help!",
    ["TaskDescription50129105"]="After handing Isabella enough Lunatic Meat, you finally get the Rose Red Wine. Time to trade it for the poetry collection!",
    ["TaskDescription50130101"]="Your new friend Emilia seems to be in trouble. It's only right to help a friend—head over and see what you can do!",
    ["TaskDescription50130102"]="Turns out, Emilia's trying to borrow a magic book from the Geffen Library, but the rules say she needs a qualified guarantor.",
    ["TaskDescription50130103"]="After hearing your request, Archmage Jesqurienne quickly writes a guarantor letter for you. Now, take it to Winry!",
    ["TaskDescription50130104"]="Now, go to the Geffen Library and exchange the guarantor letter for the magic book!",
    ["TaskDescription50130105"]="After receiving the guarantor letter from Jesqurienne, Winry gives you \"Beginner's Magic Guide\" for Emilia. Now, bring it to her!",
    ["TaskDescription50131101"]="It's been a while since you saw your fishing mentor, Xavier. Time to pay him a visit!",
    ["TaskDescription50131102"]="From Xavier's description, you can guess the stranger is Subaru Natsuki from another world. Go ask why he's watching Xavier fish all the time!",
    ["TaskDescription50131103"]="Turns out Subaru Natsuki is after Xavier's sea bream. He needs your help to buy it. Time to get moving!",
    ["TaskDescription50131104"]="After finding out Xavier's fish are all reserved for someone else, you catch a sea bream yourself. Go give it to Subaru Natsuki!",
    ["TaskDescription50132101"]="The serpent that brings new year blessings to the people of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> is about to awaken! However, a horde of evil monsters has its eyes set on its power. Adventurers, step up and become the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Serpent Guardian</color> while collecting fortune for the new year!",
    ["TaskDescription50134101"]="A stranger named Uma approaches you on the bustling streets of Prontera. She seems to need help...",
    ["TaskDescription50135101"]="You have heard that a great celebration is being prepared in the Morroc Desert, which seems related to water. Being curious, you decide to ask Heflee for information…",
    ["TaskDescription50135102"]="Heflee introduces you to the upcoming <color=#CA2E0AFF>Street Party</color> event. You are having a nice chat when she suddenly realizes that <color=#CA2E0AFF>the Water Gun Battle</color> venue has not yet been decided, and the busy Heflee asks for your help...",
    ["TaskDescription50136101"]="A fierce call echoes through your bloodline... Perhaps the time has come to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Brunhild</color>?",
    ["TaskDescription50137101"]="Snap a photo with Taichi and Agumon at Prontera's Central Fountain!\nThough the adventure ends at some point, a smile frozen in time transforms a fleeting encounter into eternity.\n\"The gate to the Digital World is open—DigiDestined—let's go!\"",
    ["TaskDescription50138101"]="You feel the goddess calling—what kind of adventure awaits this time? Let's go!",
    ["TaskDescription600001101"]="You meet a valiant-looking young man named Radish Warrior on a cliff overlooking the sea. He happily welcomes you and says he too had stumbled upon the place by accident.\nRadish Warrior tells you that every time he stands by the cliff and watches the sea, he gets an endless flow of thoughts... Like the adventurers of this continent, he has a dream of his own, which is to become a hero and create a paradise for the countless people with love and warmth in their hearts!\nBut when you ask Radish Warrior if his dream has come true, he responds with a question, asking if you would like to be a great hero who defends this paradise and maintains peace. Once you've made up your mind, <color=#CA2E0AFF>give Radish Warrior your answer</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription600001102"]="Inspired by Radish Warrior's enthusiasm, you quickly respond with a resounding yes!\nRadish Warrior applauds your decision and asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>slay 678 Porings</color> to prove your growth.",
    ["TaskDescription600001103"]="You managed to kill 678 Porings, but when asked about the reason for this number, Radish Warrior gives you a solemn look.\nHe tells you that he too had a tough time on his way to becoming a hero, but he never gave in and kept fighting for no more or less than exactly 678 days.<color=#CA2E0AFF>Then Radish Warrior suddenly remembers that he has a </color>few more important aspirations\nto fulfill. Why don't see what else he needs help with?",
    ["TaskDescription600001104"]="You follow Radish Warrior's instructions and bring back 99 pieces of Iron and 1 Clover for him, but he appears melancholy when you ask what these items are supposed to signify.\nSeeing his dispirited look, you wonder if he still has unresolved matters on his mind.",
    ["TaskDescription600001105"]="You follow Radish Warrior's instructions and bring back 1 Witherless Rose for him, only to learn that the rose symbolizes his undying love for his sweetheart.\nRemember the question you asked in the beginning about dreams? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Go listen to Radish Warrior's answer now</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription600002101"]="Radish Warrior still stands at the cliff edge overlooking the sea. Do you still remember he once told you that he would show up every year on June 6 and December 27 and asked you to complete his quest on the same day?",
    ["TaskDescription600002102"]="Once again, you have brought a Witherless Rose for Radish Warrior, who looks both surprised and delighted.\nQuickly do as Radish Warrior says and <color=#CA2E0AFF>offer the rose before the sacrificial stone under the maple tree behind him</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription600003101"]="You meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Master Fisherman Xavier</color> at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Prontera South Gate</color>, and he seems to have a mysterious magical gadget in his hand. What is it? Hurry and go ask him!",
    ["TaskDescription600003102"]="Xavier gives you the magic bait that he made. No time to waste.<color=#CA2E0AFF>Use the magic bait</color> at the nearby pond and try to make a fish print!",
    ["TaskDescription600005101"]="It is said that there are more pet masters who fail to tame a pet than those who succeed...",
    ["TaskDescription891001101"]="Skyfire... The Haze... Omens of the end of days.",
    ["TaskDescription891401101"]="Defeat the ferocious beast.",
    ["TaskDescription900001101"]="The Rune Slab holding the power of class advancement is shining again. Head over to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color> in Prontera, and hear what he has to say.",
    ["TaskDescription900001102"]="Wolmas the Archbishop recommends visiting <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color> to ask <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shikoti</color> for the key to becoming a fourth-class Adventurer.",
    ["TaskDescription900001103"]="You finally meet Goddess Shikoti and show her your righteous heart, but the trial isn't over yet...",
    ["TaskDescription900001104"]="Goddess Shikoti recounts the story of Glast Heim Chivalry and asks you to defeat the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Bloody Knight plaguing the city</color>. Now, Collect the Breath of Knights, a token to summon the Knight Spirit who once protected Glast Heim and earn his recognition.",
    ["TaskDescription900001105"]="Before you stand the Knight Spirit who protected Glast Heim, he asks you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>restore the gleam of their ancient gear</color>. Yet, beware the Abysmal Knight who lurk nearby.",
    ["TaskDescription900001106"]="With the quest fulfilled, you earn the knights' blessing. Bring the word of this success back to Goddess Shikoti.",
    ["TaskDescription900002101"]="Having met the criteria for advancement, you receive a message from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Wolmas the Archbishop</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900002102"]="An unknown anomaly has overtaken the Rune Slab of class advancement, and Wolmas advises seeking answers from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shikoti</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription900011101"]="Now that your Job Level has reached <color=#CA2E0AFF>60</color>, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>revisit Glast Heim</color> and receive guidance from <color=#CA2E0AFF>Goddess Shikoti</color> for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900011102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900011103"]="Impressed by your advancement, Yadrew sends you on a solitary journey to Comodo Cave to retrieve a drop of ancient dragon blood.",
    ["TaskDescription900011104"]="Deep in Comodo Cave, you see the presence of a dragon. To claim the dragon blood, you must face and triumph over this fierce battle...",
    ["TaskDescription900011105"]="Now you can go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900012101"]="Now that your Job Level has reached <color=#CA2E0AFF>60</color>, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>revisit Glast Heim</color> and receive guidance from Goddess <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shikoti</color> for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900012102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900012103"]="Alice praises your progress and advises you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>go to the Prontera Cathedral</color>, where listening to the concerns of the citizens will guide you in becoming a Cardinal.",
    ["TaskDescription900012104"]="Now you can go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900013101"]="Now that your Job Level has reached <color=#CA2E0AFF>60</color>, it's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>revisit Glast Heim</color> and receive guidance from Goddess <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shikoti</color> for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900013102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900013103"]="The stern Charles pulls forth a scroll of forbidden spells, informing you that by mastering it, you will ascend as an Arch Mage...",
    ["TaskDescription900013104"]="Now you can go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900014102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hamid</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900014103"]="Hamid explains that to ascend as a Meister, you need a stronger Mechanical Core, and he directs you to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Clock Tower B2</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900015102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moxie</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900015103"]="Moxie reveals the essence of Shadow Cross, directing you to the Labyrinth Forest to cleanse the den of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Baphomet Jr.</color> and retrieve the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Shadow Heart</color> from their king as a mark of your trial's success.",
    ["TaskDescription900016102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Melbrun</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900016103"]="Melbrun hands you a packet of Spirit-Summoning Incense and advises you to head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Ghastly Graveyard</color> to test if your arrows, honed through trials, now possess the power to pierce the unseen. This is what defines a genuine Wind Hawk.",
    ["TaskDescription900017102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Yadrew</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900017103"]="Becoming an Imperial Guard means your sword will no longer be for you. If you're truly ready, visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hallam</color>, the Captain of the Royal Chivalry, and he'll guide you through your Class Advancement Ceremony.",
    ["TaskDescription900017104"]="The knights are waiting for you in the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Grand Banquet Hall</color>. Get your weapon, step up, and show them you're determined!",
    ["TaskDescription900018102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Charles</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900018103"]="Under Charles's advice, you arrive at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mjolnir Mountains</color> to seek help from the Great Sage <color=#CA2E0AFF>Kroneika</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900018104"]="\"The <color=#CA2E0AFF>creator</color> builds. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>protector</color> protects. The <color=#CA2E0AFF>destroyer</color> never bows.\" You will have to figure out the rest yourself.",
    ["TaskDescription900018105"]="White for creation, purple for protection, and black for destruction. <color=#CA2E0AFF>Burn the charm</color> in front of the corresponding snake head to <color=#CA2E0AFF>awaken Serpens</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900019102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Moxie</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900019103"]="Moxie guides you to the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Realm of the Dead</color> in <color=#CA2E0AFF>Umbala</color> to find out what this mysterious \"Death Experience\" is all about...",
    ["TaskDescription900019104"]="You learned that in order to sign a contract with Hel, you need an <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Contract</color>. Moxie didn't say anything and just kicked you in. Now you're waking up all disoriented... Well, first things first, go find the Necromancer <color=#CA2E0AFF>Zorser</color> to ask.",
    ["TaskDescription900019105"]="Zorser receives the offering and gives you the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Undead Contract</color>. Before signing, make sure to <color=#CA2E0AFF>read it thoroughly</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>think it over</color>.",
    ["TaskDescription900019106"]="Here comes the final step: <color=#CA2E0AFF>Throw the Undead Contract</color> into the Wraith Forge. What will happen next?",
    ["TaskDescription900020102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> in search of your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Melbrun</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900020103"]="Melbrun still hasn't gotten over the fact that you didn't become a Wind Hawk, but whatever—that's your choice. Ignoring his look of disdain, you set off cheerfully toward <color=#CA2E0AFF>Papuchicha Forest</color>, where <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vendra</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Callahan</color> are expecting you...",
    ["TaskDescription900020104"]="Ever since becoming an Adventurer, you've been part of everyone else's stories. But this time, you're the protagonist in your own story. Take a moment to reflect—if you ever feel lost, revisit the places that left the strongest impressions on you, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>relive your journey</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription900020105"]="It's time to head back to the camp of Euphonic Symphony and give <color=#CA2E0AFF>Vendra</color> and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Callahan</color> your final answer!",
    ["TaskDescription900022102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Hamid</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900022103"]="Following Hamid's instructions, you arrive at <color=#CA2E0AFF>Al De Baran</color> to see <color=#CA2E0AFF>Nicolas</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900022104"]="Nicolas tells you that in order to advance as a Biolo, you'll need an Evolution Potion. He wants you to collect <color=#CA2E0AFF>Twilight Creeper</color>, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Entwined Root</color>, and <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dew of Spirit Tree</color>. With that, you set off for <color=#CA2E0AFF>Umbala</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900022105"]="After gathering everything for the Evolution Potion, you deliver the materials to Nicolas. Now, you just have to <color=#CA2E0AFF>wait patiently</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900023102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit your previous class master, <color=#CA2E0AFF>Alice</color>, and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900023103"]="Even though you haven't seen Alice in a long time, she's still the gentle mentor you remember. As soon as she heard about the Rune Slab, she set everything up for you. Now, just head to the southern area of <color=#CA2E0AFF>Payon</color> and meet Master Peerless Jin at the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Incense Pavilion</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900023104"]="Master Peerless Jin hands you a tome. Following its cryptic poem, you set out toward the Munak Cave, searching for a Broken Butsudan...",
    ["TaskDescription900025102"]="The goddess has illuminated your path. It's time to <color=#CA2E0AFF>advance your class</color>! Everyone's cheering for your progress!",
    ["TaskDescription900025103"]="What? <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tanders</color> is <color=#CA2E0AFF>missing</color>? Sure, Sansha's acting a bit weird, but finding him safe comes first!",
    ["TaskDescription900025104"]="You and Sansha spotted strange footprints near the cave—one probably belonged to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Tanders</color> and the other to an <color=#CA2E0AFF>unknown figure</color>. Better stay sharp as you head into the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Sphinx Cavern</color>!",
    ["TaskDescription900026102"]="The goddess is calling—you're finally getting that class advancement trial! Go talk to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> and see what he has to say.",
    ["TaskDescription900026103"]="Instead of answering your question, Akahyo kicks you straight into the Forgotten Lake...",
    ["TaskDescription900026104"]="Akahyo finally reveals the truth and challenges you—but the <color=#CA2E0AFF>ninja puppets</color> he summons are Ohka and Souzo, who have already died...",
    ["TaskDescription900028101"]="Now that your Job Level has reached 60, it's time to revisit Glast Heim and receive guidance from Goddess Shikoti for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900028102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900028103"]="Encouraged by Dean Mainz's praise, it's time to head out and meet <color=#CA2E0AFF>Mentor Phoenix</color> for your fourth class advancement trial.",
    ["TaskDescription900028104"]="Phoenix usually waits at the meeting spot... but this time, he's late? Wonder what secret trial he's preparing. Well, let's <color=#CA2E0AFF>go</color> anyway!",
    ["TaskDescription900028105"]="You beat those Medusas and mastered the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Way of Strength</color>! Phoenix is proud of you! But no time to relax; the <color=#CA2E0AFF>next trial</color> is about to begin!",
    ["TaskDescription900028106"]="After the Way of Strength trial, Phoenix takes you to Kordt Forest... Oh, for Odin's sake, did he just make a weird friend...?",
    ["TaskDescription900028107"]="Now you can go back to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Glast Heim Chivalry</color> and join the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Class Advancement Ceremony</color>...",
    ["TaskDescription900029102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to <color=#CA2E0AFF>Criatura Academy</color> to visit <color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900029103"]="<color=#CA2E0AFF>Dean Mainz</color> tells you to go find <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color>. He's got a new trial for you—something weird is going on beneath Glast Heim...",
    ["TaskDescription900029104"]="The body of the <color=#CA2E0AFF>Missing Adventurer</color> was found in the underground of Glast Heim. You mention the <color=#CA2E0AFF>girl</color> from your third class advancement trial, but <color=#CA2E0AFF>Instructor Miller</color> chuckles. The trial is far from over.",
    ["TaskDescription900029105"]="You've fulfilled the promise that's lasted seven hundred years. But... is it really over?",
    ["TaskDescription900030101"]="Now that your Job Level has reached 60, it's time to revisit Glast Heim and receive guidance from Goddess Shikoti for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900030102"]="Under Goddess Shikoti's advice, you return to Criatura Academy to visit Dean Mainz and receive guidance for your class advancement.",
    ["TaskDescription900030103"]="Moonstrider's formation was affected by some strange power and turned into a death trap. You've decided to use it to lure out whoever's behind this...",
    ["TaskDescription900030104"]="The truth is revealed—the tragedy of the Soul Linker lineage unfolds before your eyes...",
    ["TaskDescription_01"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Wicked) in the Prontera Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_02"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Wicked) in the Morroc Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_03"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Wicked) in the Payon Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_04"]="Successfully clearing all Disasters (Wicked).",
    ["TaskDescription_05"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Tiger) in the Prontera Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_06"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Tiger) in the Morroc Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_07"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Tiger) in the Payon Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_08"]="Successfully clearing all Disasters (Tiger).",
    ["TaskDescription_09"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Demon) in the Prontera Region.",
    ["TaskDescription_10"]="Successfully clearing the Disasters (Demon) in the Morroc Region.",
