    ["TeamBattleMode04"]="Poring Blitz",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc01"]="Capture the flag and bring it to your base",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc02"]="Occupy the resource point to secure resources",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc03"]="Defeat your opponent",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc04"]="Grab the Little Poring",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc05"]="Obtained points by activating mechanical devices.",
    ["TeamBattleModeDesc06"]="Capture the base to win.",
    ["TeamBattleNPCNameBlue"]="Blue Party's Drop-Off Point",
    ["TeamBattleNPCNameRed"]="Red Party's Drop-Off Point",
    ["TeamBattlePeopleNum01"]="Your party size doesn't meet the requirement",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule01"]="1. Capture the flag located at the middle of the scene.\n2. Successfully delivering the captured flag to your party's flag drop-off point counts as one flag submission.\n3. Your party's flag drop-off point is located in the opponent's base.\n4. The first party to submit the flag 3 times wins the match.",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule02"]="1. There are three resource points in the scene.\n2. Occupy resource points to continuously obtain resources.\n3. Occupied resource points can still be seized and reclaimed by other parties.\n4. The party that first collects a specified amount of resources wins the match.",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule03"]="1. When members of the opponent party are defeated, our party scores points.\n2. The party that first reaches the target score wins the match.",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule04"]="1. The Mastering will randomly summon little Porings in the scene.\n2. Get close to little Porings to pick them up.\n3. When defeated, you will drop all Porings that have been picked up.\n4. Collecting a certain number of little Porings for a certain period to win the match.",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule05"]="1. Multiple mechanical devices are scattered across the area, and a few will activate every so often for Adventurers to compete over.\n2. You can earn points by capturing devices or taking down enemies. When the battle ends, the side with more points wins. If it's a tie, the side with the higher total damage dealt wins.",
    ["TeamBattlePlayRule06"]="1. There's one base in the area. If only your faction is in the area, your capture progress goes up. First to fill the progress bar wins. If both sides are on it, the one with more damage dealt wins.\n2. Powerful battle fruits randomly spawn around the map—they might just turn the tide!",
    ["TeamBattleProtectStars"]="The Star Protection Card is activated; no stars will be lost this time .",
    ["TeamBattleRank01"]="The Warlord tier is required. The leaderboard only shows the Top 200 Warlords.",
