    ["WonderWorldTips010"]="Exchange Deadline:\n%s",
    ["WonderWorldTips011"]="Purchase Shuna's Aid Gift Pack?\n(If the price exceeds the final price at the end of the event, the difference will be returned as the equivalent amount of Diamonds at the end of the event)",
    ["WonderWorldTips012"]="You've completed Wonderland Adventure a total of <size=28><color=#F97897>%s</color></size> times.",
    ["WonderWorldTips013"]="Number of players server-wide who have completed Wonderland <size=30><color=#FFB44FFF>%s</color></size> times",
    ["WonderWorldTips014"]="Complete %s round(s).",
    ["WonderWorldTips015"]="Use at least one dice to advance!",
    ["WonderWorldTips016"]="Dear Wonderland Traveller, %s players have already claimed the Shuna’s Otherworld Rally Pack, and the Rally Level has already reached Lv.%s! Come bargain together! Shuna is also hurriedly replenishing her goods!",
    ["WonderWorldTips017"]="You cannot perform this action when you are in Wonderland.",
    ["WonderWorldTips018"]="You cannot auto-path in this Wonderland! You need to explore it for yourself!",
    ["WonderWorldTips019"]="The minimum number you can choose in current form: %s",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_001"]="Total Invasion",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_002"]="Settlement Time: Daily at %s",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_003"]="Leaderboard rewards are shared upward. If the Adventurers' results are the same, they receive the same rank and the same rewards, and subsequent rankings are pushed back accordingly.",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_004"]="Leaderboard rewards will be sent via mail",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_005"]="Total Invasion in progress",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_006"]="Gameplay Description:\n1. During the event, the daily boss appears on all servers at 12:00 and 20:00, and stays for only 3 minutes. Heroes can use the MVP menu to auto-path and get there early to prepare for battles.\n2. The boss is the same on all servers with no affixes, no level scaling, and unlimited HP.\n3. Adventurers who participate in the battle receive participation rewards and a chance for rare drops. Drop rules follow the MVP system, but these do not count toward normal MVP drop limits.\n4. Damage dealt by all participating Adventurers across all servers will be recorded on the daily leaderboard (up to 5,000 entries). When in a party, the party's total damage is counted as each member's personal damage. The highest damage from multiple attempts is taken. Identical damage results in the same ranks, with subsequent ranks moving down accordingly.\n5. Leaderboard rewards will be distributed via in-game mail at 23:00 each day, and the leaderboard resets at 05:00 the following morning.",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_007"]="Today has ended.",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_008"]="A shroud of darkness engulfs Midgard! Wicked beings hunger for this world, stealing the shapes of its monsters and scattering their phantoms across the realm. Only by uniting the strength of every Adventurer can these evils be purged. Therefore, let battle become the trial of courage, and let the glorious rankings immortalize the valor of every hero who rises against the shadow!",
    ["WorldBossActivityTips_009"]="%s",
    ["WorldKVM_JobSwitchTip01"]="No changes to party members or load-outs are allowed after 20 seconds.",
    ["WorldKVM_JobSwitchTip02"]="The match is about to begin—no changes to party members or load-outs are allowed.",
    ["WorldKVM_TeamTip01"]="The party name cannot be blank.",
    ["WorldKVM_TeamTip02"]="The party declaration cannot be blank.",
    ["WorldKVM_TeamTip03"]="The party name contains invalid characters. Please edit and try again.",
    ["WorldKVM_TeamTip04"]="The party declaration contains invalid characters. Please edit and try again.",
    ["WorldKvmCreatTeam_001"]="Party name should be within 4-14 characters",
    ["WorldKvmCreatTeam_002"]="Please support us~",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_001"]="No. %s",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_002"]="Didn't Participate",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_003"]="Qualifying Round Champion",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_004"]="Qualifying Round 1st Runner-up",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_005"]="Qualifying Semi-finals",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_006"]="Qualifying Quarterfinals",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_007"]="Elimination Round Champion",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_008"]="Elimination Round 1st Runner-up",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_009"]="Elimination Round Semi-finals",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_010"]="Elimination Group Champion",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_011"]="Elimination Group 1st Runner-up",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_012"]="Elimination Group Semi-finals",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_013"]="Elimination Group Quarterfinals",
    ["WorldKvmInfo_014"]="Eliminated at Qualifying Round",
    ["WorldKvmSameJobBuffName"]="<size=20>Party Buff</size>\n<size=16>Activates when the number of identical classes in the deployed party is <color=#ff6d6d>≤%s</color>.</size>\n<size=16>Gains the following buffs upon activation:</size>\n%s",
    ["WorldKvmSameJobTips"]="Gains extra buffs in WOC when the number of identical classes in the deployed party is ≤2.",
    ["WorldLevel"]="1. Base Level reaches <color=#FFDA3EFF>35</color> and at least <color=#FFDA3EFFF>3</color> levels below the World Level.\n2. EXP gained from Wilderness AFK will be boosted; others, such as main quests, side quests, and daily quests, stay the same.\n3. When the Base Level is <color=#FFDA3EFF>3</color> levels below the World Level, every level below the World Level increases the EXP multiplier by 20%, and the level multiplier is capped at <color=#FFDA3EFF>500%</color>.\n4. When the Base Level is higher than the World Level, every level above the World Level reduces the EXP multiplier by 10%, down to a minimum of <color=#FFDA3EFF>10%</color> for the Base Level and <color=#FFDA3EFF>30%</color> for the Job Level.\n5. Stop gaining the EXP when the character's Base Level reaches max.\n6. When the World Level is below <color=#FFDA3EFF>150</color>, the first <color=#FFDA3EFF>2,000</color> Odin's Blessings and Stamina you consume each day will grant extra bonuses.",
    ["WorldLevel_1"]="1. Character Base Level lower than the world level by <color=#FFDA3EFFF>30</color> will activate the bonus.\n2. When there are bonus members with remaining reward attempts in the team, every time a bonus member uses 1 instance reward, the non-bonus members will receive a gift pack.\n3. When there are bonus members with remaining reward attempts in the team, every time a bonus member uses 1 MVP/MINI time, the non-bonus members will receive a gift pack.\n4. When there are bonus members in the team, every time a bonus member uses 500 Odin's Blessings and all team members are on the same map, the non-bonus members will receive a gift pack.\n5. Bonus players and world level differences will enhance the different Odin's Blessings EXP multipliers.\nLv.1-49: 10x\nLv.50-69: 9x\nLv.70-89: 8x\nLv.90-99: 7x\nLv.100-160: 6x\n6. Maximum daily limit for obtaining A Travel Companion Pack: 10",
    ["WorldShopAIDesc_001"]="Remains %s",
    ["WorldShopAIDesc_002"]="Owned: %s",
    ["WorldShopAIDesc_003"]="Purchase Limit: %s",
    ["WorldTaskAreaTips1"]="You've entered the <color=#ec8a5a>%s</color> event area.",
    ["WorldTaskAreaTips2"]="You've left the <color=#ec8a5a>%s</color> event area.",
    ["WorldTaskCompleteTips1"]="You've completed the world event %s. Rewards will be sent via mail. Please check.",
    ["WorldTaskCompleteTips2"]="You've completed the world event %s. No more rewards will be given today. Please come back tomorrow!",
    ["WorldTaskDescription1"]="The Reindeer Parcel Center is short-staffed! Piles of Christmas Gifts need to be delivered ASAP! Yet, no one has found out the weird stuff attached to the gifts...\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, obtain the Christmas Gift (weight: 5,000) from Gingerbread Reindeer in Lutie and submit it to Gingerbread Deliveryman to progress the quest.\n2. For each delivery, up to 5 Christmas Gifts can be obtained from Gingerbread Reindeer. Upon submission, all Christmas Gifts will be turned in.\n3. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 8) for every 5 Christmas Gifts submitted. There's an extra chance of getting Warg Breath x1 every time you submit them.\n4. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription2"]="It was Cookie Bandit and Myst Case Bandit who stole the celebration fireworks. However... are they really the masterminds behind everything...\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, there is a chance to get Lost Firework x1 and Warg Breath x1 after defeating Cookie Bandit and Myst Case Bandit in Toy Factory. Submit the Lost Firework to Christmas Cookie Foreman to progress the quest.\n2. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 8) for every 5 Lost Fireworks submitted. Upon submission, all Lost Fireworks will be turned in.\n3. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription3"]="The retrieved celebration fireworks soar up into the sky. Meanwhile, there's been a sighting of a scary wolf at night...\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, set off the Firework Box in Lutie to progress the quest.\n2. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 6) for every 3 Firework Boxes set off. There's an extra chance of getting Warg Breath x1 every time you set them off.\n3. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription4"]="Peace in Lutie is slowly taking a hit, and yep, our reliable Cruiser is having some pretty wild nightmares about a giant frost wolf...\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, defeat Nightmare Cruiser in Toy Factory to progress the quest.\n2. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 8) for every 5 Nightmare Cruisers defeated. There's an extra chance of getting Warg Breath x1 every time you defeat them.\n3. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription5"]="He wakes up after snapping back to reality, speaking out a familiar name—Garm. It's battle time, no doubt. The Gingerbread Factory Manager leads everyone to this quiet church area, where this legendary Witch Evelyn, the owner of Lutie, left some sort of energy to deal with invasions...\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, obtain Energy Fragment x1/x3/x5 by gathering Energy Crystals within the Lutie - Church area. Submit the Energy Fragments to the Gingerbread Factory Manager to progress the quest.\n2. There's an extra chance of getting Warg Breath x1 during each gathering. Upon submission, all Energy Fragments will be turned in.\n3. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 6) for every 3 Energy Fragments submitted.\n4. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription6"]="The magic on the Energy Crystal somehow brings back Witch Evelyn from her seal. Even though she can't go toe-to-toe with Garm, she can sniff him out by tracking down the Warg scent.\nGameplay:\n1. During the event, submit Warg Breath to Evelyn, the witch in Toy Factory, to progress the quest.\n2. There's a chance to obtain Warg Breaths in previous event ①-⑤, or by defeating monsters in Toy Factory (Cookie, Christmas Cookie, Myst Case, and Cruiser) and by defeating Garm Baby from the event ⑥. It remains valid for the day it's obtained and expires at 05:00 the next day.\n3. Receive Holly Leaf x1 (daily limit: 10) for every 5 Warg Breaths submitted. Upon submission, all Warg Breaths will be turned in.\n4. Event rewards will be sent via mail when the event is completed.",
    ["WorldTaskDescription7"]="Out in the frozen wilds, <color=#FFBC8BFF>Gingerbread Prophet</color> has opened the <color=#FFBC8BFF>Challenge Garm</color> arena...",
    ["WorldTaskName1"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Surprise Delivery</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName2"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Eve of Celebration</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName3"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Celebration Commencement</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName4"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Nightmare Cruiser</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName5"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Energy Armament</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName6"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Warg Tracking</color>",
    ["WorldTaskName7"]="<color=#FF8487FF>Challenge Garm</color>",
    ["WorldTaskRule"]="Event Description:\n1. Event Time: December 19, 2024, 05:00 to January 2, 2025, 05:00. Christmas Splendor Exchange and Sale Deadline: January 4, 2025, 05:00.\n2. Each event can only be joined once per day.\n3. Rewards will be sent via mail after the event ends. Please stay online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't get any mail if offline for over 30 days.\n4. Quest completion counts are updated after the reward mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule1"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, obtain the quest item - Christmas Gift (weight: 5,000) from the NPC - Gingerbread Reindeer and submit it to the NPC - Gingerbread Deliveryman to progress the quest.\n 2. For each delivery, up to 5 Christmas Gifts can be obtained from the NPC - Gingerbread Reindeer. Upon submission, all Christmas Gifts will be turned in.\n 3. There's a 10% chance of getting the extra item - Warg Breath x1 every time you submit, no matter how many Christmas Gifts you're turning in.\n\n About Rewards:\n Deliver 1-10 Gifts: Holly Leaf x1\n Deliver 11-59 Gifts: Holly Leaf x3\n Deliver 60-149 Gifts: Holly Leaf x5\n Deliver 150+ Gifts: Holly Leaf x8\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule2"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, there's a 12.5% chance of getting the quest item - Lost Firework x1 after defeating the special event monsters - Cookie Bandit and Myst Case Bandit in Toy Factory. Submit the Lost Firework to the NPC - Christmas Cookie Foreman to progress the quest.\n 2. There's a 10% chance of getting the extra item - Warg Breath x1 whenever you defeat an event monster. Upon submission, all Lost Fireworks will be turned in.\n\n About Rewards:\n Submit 1-5 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x1\n Submit 6-29 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x3\n Submit 30-99 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x5\n Submit 100+ Fireworks: Holly Leaf x8\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule3"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, set off the Firework Box in Lutie to progress the quest.\n 2. There's a 10% chance of getting the extra item - Warg Breath x1 every time you set off the fireworks, no matter what kind of fireworks effects you trigger.\n\n About Rewards:\n Set off 1-5 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x1\n Set off 6-29 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x2\n Set off 30-59 Fireworks: Holly Leaf x3\n Set off 60+ Fireworks: Holly Leaf x6\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule4"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, defeat the special event monster - Nightmare Cruiser in Toy Factory to progress the quest.\n 2. There's a 10% chance of getting the extra item - Warg Breath x1 whenever you defeat an event monster.\n\n About Rewards:\n Defeat 1-5 Nightmare Cruisers: Holly Leaf x1\n Defeat 6-29 Nightmare Cruisers: Holly Leaf x3\n Defeat 30-99 Nightmare Cruisers: Holly Leaf x5\n Defeat 100+ Nightmare Cruisers: Holly Leaf x8\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule5"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, obtain the quest item - Energy Fragments by gathering the Energy Crystals within the Lutie - Church area. Submit the Energy Fragments to the NPC - Gingerbread Factory Manager to progress the quest.\n 2. When gathering the Energy Crystals, there's a 70%/25%/5% chance of getting the quest item - Energy Fragment x1/x3/x5, as well as a 7% chance of getting the extra item - Warg Breath x1.\n 3. Upon submission, all Energy Fragments will be turned in.\n\n About Rewards:\n Submit 1-10 Energy Fragments: Holly Leaf x1\n Submit 11-49 Energy Fragments: Holly Leaf x2\n Submit 50-129 Energy Fragments: Holly Leaf x3\n Submit 130+ Energy Fragments: Holly Leaf x6\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskRule6"]="Gameplay:\n 1. During the event, submit the extra item - Warg Breath to the NPC - Witch Evelyn to progress the quest.\n 2. Upon submission, all Warg Breaths will be turned in.\n\n About Rewards:\n Submit 1-5 Warg Breaths: Holly Leaf x1\n Submit 6-19 Warg Breaths: Holly Leaf x3\n Submit 20-49 Warg Breaths: Holly Leaf x5\n Submit 50+ Warg Breaths: Holly Leaf x10\n\n Note:\n 1. While the world event is going on, you will only be rewarded for the same event after your first participation and progress contribution, and you can claim the reward only once per day. If you participate in the event again, you won't be able to claim the reward again, but your personal contribution still counts toward the world progress.\n 2. When the event is over, please wait for the thank-you mail or reward mail based on whether you participated more than once. Please remain online. If you go offline before receiving the mail, it will be sent to you the next time you log in. However, you won't be getting any mail if you are offline for more than 30 days.\n 3. For other parts of the gameplay, the count for completing relevant world events will be effective and recorded after the mail is sent.",
    ["WorldTaskStep1"]="Obtain <color=#ffe788>Christmas Gifts</color> from the <color=#ffe788>Gingerbread Reindeer</color>, and submit them to the <color=#ffe788>Gingerbread Deliveryman</color>",
    ["WorldTaskStep2"]="Obtain <color=#ffe788>Lost Fireworks</color> from the special event monsters - <color=#ffe788>Cookie Bandit</color> and <color=#ffe788>Myst Case Bandit</color>, and submit them to the <color=#ffe788>Christmas Cookie Foreman</color>",
    ["WorldTaskStep3"]="Set off the <color=#ffe788>Celebration Firework Box</color> at the center of Lutie",
    ["WorldTaskStep4"]="Defeat <color=#ffe788>Nightmare Cruiser</color>",
    ["WorldTaskStep5"]="Gather <color=#ffe788>Energy Fragments</color> and submit them to the <color=#ffe788>Gingerbread Factory Manager</color>",
    ["WorldTaskStep6"]="Submit <color=#ffe788>Warg Breaths</color> to <color=#ffe788>Evelyn</color>",
    ["WorldTaskStep7"]="Party up and defeat <color=#ec8a5a>Garm</color> in Lutie",
    ["WorldTaskStepFinish"]="Max Personal Contribution",
    ["WorldTaskStepTotalProcess"]="Total Current Progress: %s%%",
