    ["homesteadFarmPet_effect1"]="When a pet is deployed to the Farmland, it will automatically water the crops when they need it (requires an extra bit of time for pets to water).",
    ["homesteadFarm_UseItem"]="Spend %s items to replenish %s Farmland Fertility?",
    ["homesteadFarm_help"]="About Home Farmland:\n1. To sow seeds, Adventurers can go next to the lots fit for sowing and tap <color=#3acfef>Sow</color> to select their desired seeds.\n2. Seeds that have a higher level than the Adventurer's <color=#3acfef>Gardening Level</color> cannot be sowed.\n3. After sowing, crops will grow automatically in the Farmland. The growing of crops has 5 phases: <color=#3acfef>Seed, Sprout, Seedling, Bloom, and Fruit</color>. Each phase has a distinct status indicator in the Farmland, showing the time required to enter the next phase.\n4. All crops, while under the <color=#3acfef>Seedling phase</color>, require watering 1 time to progress to the Bloom phase. Otherwise, the crop will remain in the Seedling phase.\n5. When a <color=#3acfef>pet</color> is deployed to the Farmland, it will take care of the Farmland automatically, watering the crops when they need it.\n6. When the crops reach the <color=#3acfef>Fruit phase</color>, they can be harvested, yielding crops corresponding to the seeds.\n7. <color=#3acfef>Skylie</color> will monitor the soil's fertility. Fertile soil yields more produce upon harvest. Each seed in Life yields a minimum of 15 crops and a maximum of 30 crops. Each seed in Home Materials yields a minimum of 2 crops and a maximum of 5 crops. \n8. Submit <color=#3acfef>Estate Fertilizer</color> to <color=#3acfef>Skylie</color> to increase the Fertility of your Farmland.\n9. When harvesting, <color=#3acfef>each crop lot</color> needs at least <color=#3acfef>2 points</color> of Fertility. Without enough Fertility, you won't receive any bonus yields.",
    ["homesteadFarm_lab_gardenLevel"]="Requires Gardening Lv.%s",
    ["homesteadFarm_plot_text"]="Lot Quantity: %s",
    ["homesteadFarm_unlock"]="Requires Gardening Lv.%s",
    ["homesteadFarm_vitality"]="Stamina Cost: %s",
    ["homesteadFishPet_effect1"]="When a pet is deployed to the Pond, it will feed the fingerlings every %s hours. The feeding effect only lasts %s minutes.",
    ["homesteadFish_capacity_text"]="Pond Capacity: %s",
    ["homesteadFish_help"]="About Home Pond: \n 1. When the character is next to the Pond, tap <color=#3acfef>Release Fingerlings</color> to select your desired fish.\n 2. <color=#3acfef>Fingerlings that have a higher level than the Adventurer's Fishing Level cannot be released</color>.\n 3. After fingerlings are released into the Pond, they will grow gradually. Adventurers can speed up their growth by feeding them <color=#3acfef>Growth Bait</color>.\n 4. <color=#3acfef>Peierls</color> will monitor the growth of the fish group. Once the fish hit the <color=#3acfef>minimum harvestable growth</color>, they can be netted, granting corresponding fish catches.\n 5. When the fish group reaches the <color=#3acfef>minimum harvestable growth</color>, the fish will continue to grow until they hit the <color=#3acfef>maximum growth</color>. By then, netting them will yield the maximum amount of fish catch. Each batch of fingerlings can yield a minimum of 10 and a maximum of 25 fish.\n 6. When a <color=#3acfef>pet</color> is deployed to the Pond, it will take care of the fish group automatically, feeding the fish periodically to accelerate their growth.\n 7. The feeding effect of the Pond <color=#3acfef>cannot be stacked</color>. And it's impossible to feed the fish group repeatedly during the feeding period.",
    ["homesteadFish_lab_fishingLevel"]="Requires Fishing Lv.%s",
    ["homesteadFish_unlock"]="Requires Fishing Lv.%s",
    ["homesteadFish_vitality"]="Stamina Cost: %s",
    ["homesteadForge_help"]="Home Craftsman Explanation:\n1. Craftsman Rony is here to help you <color=#3acfef>craft furniture</color>. Just bring him the right materials for what you want, and he will get started.\n2. Certain pieces of furniture are really complicated. Apart from basic materials, you will need to give Rony the <color=#3acfef>blueprint</color> to craft those.\n3. It takes a while to craft the furniture. Drop by Rony's <color=#3acfef>when it's done</color> to <color=#3acfef>pick up</color> your furniture.\n4. During the crafting, <color=#3acfef>Time Candles</color> can be used to speed up the process.\n5. Every time a piece of furniture is completed, 500 Home EXP will be granted.\n6. Upgrading the Craftsman's Cottage and its tools allows Rony to craft more advanced furniture.",
    ["homesteadForge_itemEnough"]="Reached the max usage limit",
    ["homesteadForge_noItem"]="Select how many items to use",
    ["homesteadForge_spendtime"]="Crafting Time: %s",
    ["homesteadForge_tip_speedup"]="Consume <color=#3acfef>%s</color> items to reduce the production time by <color=#3acfef>%s</color> seconds.",
