    ["robot_mount_tips05"]="Unable to cast skill. Get the required mount or equipment first.",
    ["roxicRule_01"]="<size=18><color=#ff8c00>◆ROXIC Overview◆</color></size>\n① The ROXIC is a player-verse-player contest for Adventurers from around the world, entry to which is by sign-ups and is open to everyone. Please refer to the official website for detailed information and qualifications.\n② The matches are party-based. Eligible Adventurers can form a party of 8 for 6v6 battles, with 2 members as reserve members, and can freely switch up the participating members for each battle.\n③ The competition consists of two sessions: Qualifier and Apex Showdown. The Qualifier features multiple rounds among every participating party, accumulating points based on the match outcomes. At the end of the Qualifier, the top-ranked parties in each channel will be qualified for the Apex Showdown. The Apex Showdown uses dedicated servers and clients, ensuring everyone starts with the same initial character date. Parties will battle against each other using strategic formation and development tactics to claim the ROXIC Championship title.\n<size=18><color=#ff8c00>◆Qualifier◆</color></size>\n<color=#ff6347>▼Qualifying Party Formation</color>\n① All participating Adventurers can form parties with a maximum of 8 members, including the option for cross-server party formation.\n② There's a time limit for forming parties. For more details, please refer to the event page.\n③ At the end of the party formation phase, parties with less than 6 members will be automatically disbanded. Please pay attention to your party's member count.\n<color=#ff6347>▼Contest Rules</color>\n① For the first round, all teams are randomly matched for 1 battle. For upcoming rounds, matchups are determined by the previous round's rankings, with the top-ranked party facing the second, and so on. Parties without a match receive a bye and automatically win the match.\n② The match format is BO3. If the parties are tied in the number of wins, the winner is decided based on the number of survivors and total damage dealt at the end of the match.\n③ Each party can select up to 6 members to participate in each battle, with up to 2 members serving as reserves.\n④ There are 2 matches daily. Please pay attention to the battle times listed in the schedule (local time 21:00 and 22:00). In each match, the winning party earns 1 Qualifying Point, while the defeated party earns no points.\n<color=#ff6347>▼Ranking Rules</color>\n① Parties with higher points are ranked higher.\n② When points are the same, rankings are decided by adding up the points of each party's opponent in every round, with the party having higher total points ranked higher.\n③ If the points are still the same, parties are ranked based on the sum of their own points in each round, with the party having a higher total points ranked higher.\n<color=#ff6347>▼Advancing to Apex Showdown</color>\nUpon the completion of all Qualifier matches, the party will advance based on the Qualifying Point Ranking and the quotas in different regions, as specified below:\n--HMT Regions: Top 11 parties from the Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan regions\n--SEA Region: Top 11 parties from Southeast Asia\n--KR Region: Top 10 parties from Korea\nA total of 32 parties will participate in the final ROXIC Apex Showdown.\n<size=18><color=#ff8c00>◆Apex Showdown◆</color></size>\n<color=#ff6347>▼Pre-battle Preparation</color>\n① The Apex Showdown will be conducted on a dedicated client and server. Parties that have qualified will be provided with a unique contest client by the official team. Adventurers must log in to the contest server once to activate their eligibility.\n② All Adventurers in advancing parties will carry over their Qualifier data such as initial class, gender (changing genders and classes is allowed during the contest), and party. However, the rest of the data will be the same as that of other participants, including Base Level, Job Level, items, etc.\n③ After logging into the contest server, Adventurers will receive an equal number of <color=#da70d6>ROXIC Apex Coins</color>, which can be used to cultivate their characters quickly.\n④ In the contest server version, the base level limit is 130, and the stat and damage calculations are slightly different from the local versions of players. You can use the Training Course and Free Arena to verify the development results before the game.\n<color=#ff6347>▼ROXIC Cultivation</color>\n① ROXIC Store: There are exclusive stores available in the ROXIC, including Equipment Store, Card Store, and Sundries Store. All items are exclusively provided for the ROXIC and can be purchased with <color=#da70d6>ROXIC Apex Coins</color>. There might be slight differences in items between the contest server and Adventurers' local server. Please refer to the contest server for the final result.\n② Equipment Upgrade: Adventurers can visit the ROXIC-exclusive envoy to upgrade their equipment. All upgrades are guaranteed to be successful. Weapons can be upgraded up to Lv.260, armor to Lv.130, and accessories to Lv.65. Resetting will return all consumed materials.\n③ Equipment Refinement: Adventurers can visit the ROXIC-exclusive envoy to refine their equipment. All refinements are guaranteed to be successful and can be refined up to Lv.15. Resetting will return all consumed materials.\n④ Enchanting Enchantment: Adventurers can visit the ROXIC-exclusive envoy to enchant their equipment. Adventurers can freely select their preferred regions and stats, with a maximum enchantment level of 15. Resetting will return all consumed materials. The currently available enchantment regions are shown below: <color=#da70d6>Prontera, Izlude, Alberta, Geffen, Morroc, Payon, Glast Heim, and Comodo.</color>\n⑤ Shadow Equipment: Shadow Equipment comes fully unlocked with maxed-out levels according to the Adventurer class. Skills can be adjusted by visiting the ROXIC-exclusive envoy.\n<color=#ff6347>▼Contest Rules</color>\n① All participating parties will draw lots on the official website to initialize their matchups. The entire contest will be conducted in a BO5 single-elimination format, with the first party winning 3 out of the 5 games advancing to the next round, while the defeated party is eliminated.\n② Each time a party successfully advances to the next round, they will receive a specified number of <color=#da70d6>ROXIC Apex Coins</color>, which can be used for character cultivation and to boost their battle strength.\n③The contest is scheduled at 22:00 (UTC+9) every contest day, which is 22:00 local time in the KR region, 21:00 local time in the HMT Regions, and 20:00 local time in the SEA Region. Please plan your time accordingly.\n<size=18><color=#ff8c00>◆Contest Rewards</color></size>\nAdvancing to Apex Showdown: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive avatar frame, chat frame, side bar, tail</color>\nApex Showdown Top 16: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive outfit</color>\nApex Showdown Top 8: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive headgear</color>\nApex Showdown Top 4: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive kill effect</color>\nApex Showdown Top 2: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive wake effect, teleport effect</color>\nApex Showdown Champion: <color=#ffa500>Contest-exclusive backpack, tail, aura effect</color>\n<size=18><color=#ff8c00>◆Special Note◆</color></size>\n① Publishing inappropriate comments in the game is prohibited. Any personal attacks against participating members or other players will result in warnings or mutes once verified. In severe cases, this could lead to a losing match.\n② Please ensure all character cultivations and resources are ready before the contest begins. Complaints about the match schedule due to inadequate preparation will be rejected.\n ",
    ["roxicRule_02"]="◆ Create Party\n ① All players who qualify for the ROXIC can create parties.\n ② During the Qualifier, parties can only use the system's default avatars. Custom avatars can be used during the ROXIC Apex Showdown.\n ③ A party can include a maximum of 8 players.",
    ["roxicRule_03"]="◆ Request List\n ① Each party can receive up to 20 applications at the same time. Once the limit is exceeded, additional applications will be blocked until the existing ones on the request list are processed.\n ② When the party exceeds its member capacity, it's not possible to accept the request until there's an available spot within the party.",
