    ["ui_Jobber036"]="I want to purchase",
    ["ui_Jobber037"]="I want to sell",
    ["ui_Jobber038"]="History",
    ["ui_Jobber039"]="Rare Equipment",
    ["ui_Jobber040"]="Clothes",
    ["ui_Jobber041"]="Shoes",
    ["ui_Jobber042"]="Cloak",
    ["ui_Jobber043"]="Main-hand Weapon",
    ["ui_Jobber044"]="Off-hand Weapon",
    ["ui_Jobber045"]="Two-handed Weapon",
    ["ui_Jobber046"]="Cloak",
    ["ui_Jobber047"]="Costume",
    ["ui_Jobber048"]="Cards",
    ["ui_Jobber049"]="Card Fragment",
    ["ui_Jobber050"]="Rare Appraisal",
    ["ui_Jobber051"]="Equipment",
    ["ui_Jobber052"]="Please select the items you want to sell.",
    ["ui_Jobber053"]="Please tap the tag on the left to select and purchase item.",
    ["ui_Jobber054"]="Exceeded",
    ["ui_Jobber055"]="Diamonds",
    ["ui_Jobber056"]="Exchange Center",
    ["ui_Jobber057"]="Items purchased with Crystals can be obtained from the transaction history.\nUp to 5,000 Diamonds can be purchased daily and the monthly purchase limit is 30,000 Diamonds.",
    ["ui_Jobber058"]="Purchasing Rules:",
    ["ui_Jobber059"]="The system will automatically display items which can be sold on the shelf list.\nPlayers can adjust the selling price by increasing or decreasing the price provided by the system when listing.\nSuccessfully listed items have a selling time. When the selling time is over, the item will be deemed expired and returned.\nAfter selling an item successfully, the Crystals gained from sale can be claimed. The system will deduct a certain amount of trading tax.",
    ["ui_Jobber060"]="Selling Rules:",
    ["ui_Jobber061"]="The player's participation in auctions is divided into three phases: Public Bidding, Blind Bidding and Bidding Wars.\nWhen participating in the bidding, each bid must raise the price by at least 100. There is no upper limit.\nWhen participating in the auction, Diamonds equal to the bidding price will be deducted and kept in the Bid Storage.\nThe Diamonds can be viewed and withdrawn from the Bid Storage and will also be returned via mail after the auction ends.",
    ["ui_Jobber062"]="Purchasing Rules:",
    ["ui_Jobber063"]="The sale of rare equipment, headgear, and cards is conducted with Diamonds as the currency of trade. If the item to be sold belongs to this category,\nthe system will automatically switch to Auction mode.\nThe Adventurer can enter the selling price they want while listing, but it cannot be less than the standard minimum bid.\nIf no Adventurer has made a bid on the item 6 hours after its entering the auction phase, it will be deemed unsold and returned to the seller.\nAfter selling an item successfully, the gains can be claimed from the transaction history. The Diamonds obtained will be converted into Crystals of equal value.\nThe Diamond Exchange Center is closed from 01:00 - 07:00 (UTC+7) daily. The countdown for orders during this period will be extended to resume after the Diamond Exchange Center reopens.",
    ["ui_Jobber064"]="Selling Rules:",
    ["ui_Jobber065"]="Trade Successful",
    ["ui_Jobber066"]="Auction Item",
    ["ui_Jobber067"]="List Item",
    ["ui_Jobber068"]="Auction Process:",
    ["ui_Jobber069"]="Normal",
    ["ui_Jobber070"]="Rare Items",
    ["ui_Jobber071"]="Selling:",
    ["ui_Jobber072"]="Enter item",
    ["ui_Jobber073"]="Unclaimed",
    ["ui_Jobber074"]="Talisman",
    ["ui_Jobber075"]="Selling",
    ["ui_Jobber076"]="Pet-related",
    ["ui_Jobber077"]="Pet Cage",
    ["ui_Jobber078"]="Water Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber079"]="Fire Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber080"]="Wind Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber081"]="Earth Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber082"]="Poison Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber083"]="Holy Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber084"]="Shadow Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber085"]="Ghost Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber086"]="Undead Pets",
    ["ui_Jobber087"]="Pet Skill Item",
    ["ui_Jobber088"]="Low Tax Mechanic:",
    ["ui_Jobber089"]="Players have a default low tax quota of 500,000 Crystals. Kafra's VIP card can increase this quota.\nIf the weekly transaction amount for sales < low tax quota, the trading tax will be relatively lower.\nIf the weekly total sales > low tax quota, different ratios of trading tax will be deducted according to the tax bracket that week's total transaction\n is in.\nWeekly total sales is cleared every Monday at 5:00 AM and the calculation for next week's total transactions begins.",
    ["ui_Jobber090"]="Pet Advance Item",
    ["ui_Jobber091"]="Pet Book",
    ["ui_Jobber092"]="Bidding Wars",
    ["ui_Jobber093"]="Popular Items",
    ["ui_Jobber094"]="Trading Volume",
    ["ui_Jobber095"]="Rise",
    ["ui_Jobber096"]="Fall",
    ["ui_Jobber097"]="Weekly Total Sales:",
    ["ui_Jobber098"]="Low Tax Quota:",
    ["ui_Jobber099"]="Tiered Tax Rate:",
    ["ui_Jobber100"]="Total Transaction Bracket",
    ["ui_Jobber101"]="Spectator",
    ["ui_Jobber102"]="Auction",
    ["ui_Jobber103"]="Waiting to Sell",
    ["ui_Jobber104"]="Bid Storage",
    ["ui_Jobber105"]="Public Bidding:",
    ["ui_Jobber106"]="In the first phase of bidding, players can select items to bid for.\nOnly players who have participated in the auction during the public period can enter to the Blind Bidding phase.\nPublic bidding lasts for 5 hours 30 minutes.",
    ["ui_Jobber107"]="Blind Bidding:",
    ["ui_Jobber108"]="After Public Bidding ends, Blind Bidding begins.\nIn this phase, players can only see their own bidding price and not those of other players'.\nPlayer's bid should be at least 100 higher than their own previous bid.\nBlind Bidding has a price cap. The auction items in Blind Bidding have a bidding cap.\nThe highest price a player can bid is 1.5 times the highest bid during the Public Bidding phase.\nIf, by the end of the Blind Bidding phase, there is only one highest bidder, then this player will obtain the item.\nBlind Bidding lasts for 30 minutes.",
    ["ui_Jobber109"]="Bidding Wars:",
    ["ui_Jobber110"]="If, by the end of the Blind Bidding phase, there are several highest bidders, then Bidding Wars phase will begin after 60 seconds.\nBidding Wars is on a new bidding screen and the auction process will be livestreamed to the whole sever.\nA Bidding Wars tab will appear on the Exchange Center screen. Players can enter an ongoing Bidding War from this tab.\nIn the Bidding Wars phase, players have a total of 5 chances to bid. Each bid resets the ending countdown.\nWhen the countdown ends, the highest bidder gets the item.\nSpectators can increase the Popularity of players by sending gifts. If the bidder they support wins, then they will get a betting reward.\n⁣Note: Gifts can only be given by players whose Kafra's VIP cards are activated.",
    ["ui_Jobber111"]="Blind Bidding",
    ["ui_Jobber112"]="(Auction)",
    ["ui_Jobber113"]="(Trade)",
    ["ui_Jobber114"]="Pre-order Mechanic:",
    ["ui_Jobber115"]="If the pre-order feature is available for an item, when the Purchase Shop is out of stock, pre-order options will appear.\nReservations of Purchase Shop items can be made via the pre-order feature. When the items in question relist, pre-orders are prioritized to be fulfilled first.\nOnly one pre-order can be made for each item. Pre-orders for different items are mutually independent.\nPre-orders last 48 hours and cannot be canceled by the player once issued.\nIf the current highest bidding price for an item exceeds the pre-order price, the pre-order will be closed.\nAfter a pre-order is fulfilled or closed, the remaining amount will be returned to the player via mail.\nCompleted transactions can be claimed from the transaction history. The remaining amount will only be settled when the entire pre-order closes.",
    ["ui_Jobber116"]="Diamond Trading Tax:",
    ["ui_Jobber117"]="The Diamond trading tax will be collected in tiers based on the final strike price.\nThe tax rate for each bracket is different. Please see the following table for more details (Unit: Diamond).",
    ["ui_Jobber118"]="Tax Policy Table:",
    ["ui_Jobber119"]="Lower Limit of Tax Bracket",
