    ["ui_Personalized_010"]="Tap to enter your personalized signature",
    ["ui_Personalized_011"]="No gifts received yet!\nMake more friends to receive more gifts!",
    ["ui_Personalized_012"]="No unlocked styles currently.",
    ["ui_Personalized_013"]="Limited Time Event",
    ["ui_Personalized_014"]="Limited Time",
    ["ui_PetActivity_001"]="Pet Event",
    ["ui_PetActivity_002"]="Sold Out",
    ["ui_PetAdventure_001"]="Material Swap",
    ["ui_PetAdventure_002"]="Reward",
    ["ui_PetCage_001"]="Caging Pets",
    ["ui_PetCage_002"]="Consume one Pet Cage to sell captured pets in the Exchange Center",
    ["ui_PetCage_003"]="Caged pets retain current level, skills, stats and talents",
    ["ui_PetCage_004"]="Pets will retain Satiety and Favor when caged",
    ["ui_PetCage_005"]="Put in cage",
    ["ui_PetCage_006"]="Insufficient Pet Cages. Purchase more and use?",
    ["ui_PetCage_007"]="Can only cage pets with stats >225 (Superior pets)",
    ["ui_PetCage_008"]="Can only cage pets once",
    ["ui_PetHelp_001"]="Pet Tips",
    ["ui_PetHelp_002"]="Knowledge",
    ["ui_PetHelp_003"]="Basic Cultivation",
    ["ui_PetHelp_004"]="Advanced Cultivation",
    ["ui_PetHelp_005"]="Pet Rarity:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_006"]="1. Rarity Types: White, Purple, Gold (including Gold SP)",
    ["ui_PetHelp_007"]="Pet Medal:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_008"]="1. Pet Medals are ranked: B<A<S.\n2. Pet Medals can boost your pet's stats; the higher the medal level, the stronger the boost.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_009"]="Pet Stats:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_010"]="1. Pet Stats automatically convert into the pet's attributes.\n2. Pet Stats = Base + Medals",
    ["ui_PetHelp_011"]="Pet Talent:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_012"]="1. These are the skills that come with every pet.\n2. Gold SP pets have multiple talents while pets of other rarities only have one.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_013"]="Pet Skills:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_014"]="1. A pet's skill pool depends on its attribute type (Gold SP pets have dual attributes).\n2. Items used for awakening or refining pet skills are available via Life Skills or the Exchange Center.\n3. Pets can have up to 4 skills, unlocked as their star level increases.\n4. Check the details in the [Skill] page.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_015"]="Pet Taming:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_016"]="1. Taming a pet consumes the pet's [Favorite Items], which can be purchased in the Prontera Pet Store.\n2. Equipping a [Pet Slingshot] and [Pet Taming] skills are required.\nEach slingshot allows you to inflict 30% True DMG (After attacking 3 times, pet taming becomes easier).\n3. Only monsters labeled as [Tamable] in the Encyclopedia can be tamed.\n4. To tame a monster, your character must be a higher level than the monster.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_017"]="Pet Favor:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_018"]="1. Pet Favor = Pet Level.\n2. Increasing Pet Favor boosts the pet's attribute.\n3. Pet Favor can be increased by interacting with the pet and giving gifts.\n4. Long-press [Pat] or other interaction items to use them quickly.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_019"]="Pet Deployment:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_020"]="1. 1. Pets must be on the Deployment List before being deployed onto the battlefield. You can only deploy 1 pet at a time.\n2. The pet will consume Stamina continuously while deployed. When Stamina reaches 0, they will be automatically called back.\n3. Pet consumes 1 Stamina per 60 seconds.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_021"]="Pet Stamina:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_022"]="1. When a pet's Stamina reaches 0, it will be unable to deploy.\n2. You can replenish a pet's Stamina by feeding it or purchasing it in the Prontera Pet Store.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_023"]="Pet Release:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_024"]="1. After a pet is released, a proportion of consumed training materials will be returned to your Backpack.\n2. If there is only one pet remaining in the Pet Backpack, you won't be able to release it.\n3. The number of returned materials varies based on the rarity of the pet being released.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_025"]="Pet Transfer:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_026"]="1. Transferring is available for pets with the same name but different medals.\n2. After transferring, the selected pets will switch their [medals] with each other (the inheritance ratio will be based on the current pet refining progress).",
    ["ui_PetHelp_027"]="Pet Advanced Transfer:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_028"]="1. Pet Advanced Transfer requires a [Pet Advanced Transfer Voucher], which can be obtained through in-game events.\n2. Advanced Transfer requires pets of the same rarity (Gold and Gold SP are considered the same rarity).\n3. For more details, check the [Advanced Transfer] page.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_029"]="Pet Awakening:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_030"]="1. When awakening conditions are met, the pet gets extra base attributes.\n2. Check the [Awakening] page for conditions and rewards.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_031"]="Pet Refining:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_032"]="1. Adventurers can redistribute a pet's stats by refining it.\n2. Refining a pet will not change the total stats of the pet.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_033"]="Pet Advancement (Star Upgrade):",
    ["ui_PetHelp_034"]="1. Advancing a pet will increase its stats, thereby enhancing its attributes.\n2. The stats must reach a certain value before a pet's Rank can be increased.",
    ["ui_PetHelp_035"]="Pet Evolution:",
    ["ui_PetHelp_036"]="1. To be evolved, a pet must reach a certain Rank and Favor level with the required evolution materials. The success rate of pet evolution is guaranteed 100%.\n2. A pet's evolution materials include both items and costumes (from MVP/MINIs, Exchange Center, gift packs).\n3. Upon successful evolution, the pet's rarity increases by one level.\n4. There's a chance to change the Pet Medal's level during evolution (shown on the interface).",
    ["ui_PetHelp_037"]="Pet Base Stats",
