    ["ui_Pve_025"]="Reward Chance Consumption Multiplier",
    ["ui_QuestFinishInfo"]="Use %s <color=#CA2E0AFF>%s</color> to complete mission immediately?",
    ["ui_RE0_Dungeon_tips125"]="1. Each day, a quest of Guests from Another World will be refreshed. You can only pick one NPC to complete their missions.\n2. Completing missions for different NPCs grants you the corresponding Favor item.\n3. Giving the right gift to an NPC increases their Favor.\n4. Build up Favor to unlock great rewards.\n5. Defeating wilderness monsters while consuming Odin's Blessings gives you a chance to get Favor items.",
    ["ui_ROXIC_001"]="Qualifying Party Formation",
    ["ui_ROXIC_002"]="Qualifying Battle",
    ["ui_ROXIC_003"]="My Party",
    ["ui_ROXIC_004"]="Party Formation Plaza",
    ["ui_ROXIC_005"]="Match List",
    ["ui_ROXIC_006"]="Qualifying Points",
    ["ui_ROXIC_007"]="Fair Play Championship awaits your challenge",
    ["ui_ROXIC_008"]="Enter Party ID",
    ["ui_ROXIC_009"]="Party Leader",
    ["ui_ROXIC_010"]="Select Party Symbol",
    ["ui_ROXIC_011"]="To be joined",
    ["ui_ROXIC_012"]="Not Started",
    ["ui_ROXIC_013"]="In Progress",
    ["ui_ROXIC_014"]="Ended",
    ["ui_ROXIC_015"]="TBD",
    ["ui_ROXIC_016"]="TIPS: Tap below to view the details of each round",
    ["ui_ROXIC_017"]="Apex Battle",
    ["ui_ROXIC_018"]="Advancing Party",
    ["ui_ROXIC_019"]="Parties with less than 6 members at the end of the party formation phase will be disbanded automatically.",
    ["ui_ROXIC_020"]="You can send recruitment messages to the ROXIC channel",
    ["ui_ROXIC_021"]="Party name should not exceed 7 characters",
    ["ui_ROXIC_022"]="Bye Round",
    ["ui_ROXIC_023"]="Currently not in a party",
    ["ui_ROXIC_024"]="Go to Battle",
    ["ui_ROXIC_025"]="100% Refinement Success Rate",
    ["ui_ROXIC_026"]="100% Upgrade Success Rate",
    ["ui_ROXIC_027"]="ROXIC Apex Showdown",
    ["ui_ROXIC_028"]="Please select your equipment",
    ["ui_ROXIC_029"]="Please select your enchantment region",
    ["ui_ROXIC_030"]="Level Boosted",
    ["ui_ROXIC_031"]="Participate in Betting",
    ["ui_ROXIC_032"]="Betting Quests",
    ["ui_ROXIC_033"]="Register & Party Up",
    ["ui_ROXIC_034"]="Participating Character Cultivation",
    ["ui_ROXIC_035"]="Qualifier",
    ["ui_ROXIC_036"]="Elimination Match",
    ["ui_ROXIC_037"]="After registering successfully, you will immediately receive the above registration rewards. Please check your mailbox.",
    ["ui_ROXIC_038"]="① During the event, parties compete against each other through matchmaking at specific times. Points will be awarded or deducted depending on the result.\n② Participate in the competition by logging in to the <color=#ece275>Contest Server</color> during matchmaking times. Each match's outcome is determined by a single round.\n③ Ranked matches support Form Party or Full Party modes. Please pick the mode that fits your party size.\n④ When there are ≥6 members in the party from the same challenge party, the party leader can start Matchmaking to match up with parties of similar strength.\n⑤ Earn extra matchmaking rewards by completing a certain number of matches every day. Rewards will be distributed by mail at 05:00 the next day.",
    ["ui_ROXIC_039"]="Daily at 21:00–22:00",
    ["ui_ROXIC_040"]="Matchmaking Time:",
    ["ui_ROXIC_041"]="Matchmaking Rules:",
    ["ui_ROXIC_042"]="Betting",
    ["ui_ROXIC_043"]="Party Details",
    ["ui_ROXIC_044"]="<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Championship Overview◆</color></size>\n① The ROX Fair Play Championship is a competition open to everyone, where all Adventurers compete against each other from the same starting points.\n② The matches are party-based. All registered Adventurers can form a party of 8 for 6v6 battles, with 2 remaining members as reserve members, and can freely switch up the participating members for each battle based on the strategy.\n③ The competition consists of two sessions: Qualifier and Elimination Match. In the Qualifier, all parties will compete over several days, accumulating points based on the match outcomes. At the end of the Qualifier, the <color=#ece275>top 32</color> parties will advance to the Elimination Match. The first round of the Elimination Match will have random matchmaking, with participants advancing and eliminating based on the results. The final remaining party will be the grand champion of the event.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Register & Party Up◆</color></size>\n<color=#b98ff7>▼Registration</color>\n① Any Adventurer with a Base Level of 45 and above can join, but each account is limited to one character.\n② Registering costs a certain number of diamonds, and successful registration grants you generous registration rewards right away.\n<color=#b98ff7>▼Party Formation</color>\n① All participating Adventurers can form parties with a maximum of 8 members from the same sub server only.\n② There's a time limit for forming parties. For more details, please refer to the event page.\n③ At the end of the party formation phase, parties with less than 6 members will be automatically disbanded. Please pay attention to your party's member count.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Character Cultivation◆</color></size>\nOnce the party formation time is over, Adventurers who successfully form a party will be given a character with identical stats. The character will retain the registered gender (changeable on the Contest Server) and party, with all other data completely matching other participants, including the class (starting as a Rune Knight but changeable on the Contest Server), base level, job level, items, etc. Exclusive Championship Coins can be used on the Contest Server to freely develop and transform your character. The following attributes can be changed:\n① Championship Store: There are exclusive stores available in the championship, including the Equipment Store, Card Store, and Sundries Store. All items are exclusively provided for the ROX Fair Play Championship and can be purchased with <color=#ece275>Exclusive Championship Coins</color>.\n② Equipment Upgrade: Adventurers can visit the championship-exclusive envoy to upgrade their equipment. All upgrades are guaranteed to be successful. Weapons can be upgraded up to Lv.240, armor to Lv.120, and accessories to Lv.60. Resetting will return all consumed materials.\n③ Equipment Refinement: Adventurers can visit the championship-exclusive envoy to refine their equipment. All refinements are guaranteed to be successful and can be refined up to Lv.10. Resetting will return all consumed materials.\n④ Equipment Enchantment: Adventurers can visit the championship-exclusive envoy to enchant their equipment. Adventurers can freely select their preferred regions and stats, with a maximum enchantment level of 10. Resetting will return all consumed materials. The currently available enchantment regions are shown below:<color=#ece275>Prontera, Alberta, Geffen, Morroc, Payon, and Glast Heim.</color>\n⑤ Shadow Equipment: Shadow Equipment comes fully unlocked with maxed-out levels according to the Adventurer class. Skills can be adjusted by visiting the ROXIC-exclusive envoy.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Qualifier◆</color></size>\n<color=#b98ff7>▼Contest Rules</color>\n① During the event, parties compete against each other through matchmaking at specific times. Points will be awarded or deducted depending on the result.\n② Participate in the competition by logging in to the <color=#ece275>Contest Server</color> during matchmaking times. Each match's outcome is determined by a single round.\n③ Ranked matches support Form Party or Full Party modes. Please pick the mode that fits your party size.\n④ When there are ≥6 members in the party from the same challenge party, the party leader can start Matchmaking to match up with parties of similar strength.\n⑤ Earn extra matchmaking rewards by completing a certain number of matches every day. Rewards will be distributed by mail at 05:00 the next day.\n<color=#b98ff7>▼Points Rules</color>\n① Each party starts with 1,000 points. At the end of a match, points are calculated based on the match outcome and point difference.\n② Parties gain an extra 50 points after 3 consecutive wins. No points will be deducted for 3 consecutive losses.\n③ Parties will lose 300 points if they abandon a match after entering.\n<color=#b98ff7>▼Advancing to Elimination Match</color>\n① All teams are ranked by their points. At the end of the Qualifier, the <color=#ece275>top 32</color> parties will advance to the Elimination Match.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Elimination Match◆</color></size>\n① All advancing parties will be paired randomly to initialize their matchups. The entire contest will be conducted in a single-elimination format, with the winning party advancing while the defeated party is eliminated.\n② Matches before the Quarterfinals will follow a BO5 format while matches after the Quarterfinals will follow a BO7 format.\n③ Each time a party successfully advances to the next round, they will receive a specified number of <color=#ece275>Exclusive Championship Coins</color>, which can be used for character cultivation and to boost their battle strength.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Others◆</color></size>\n① During the event, defeating monsters while consuming Odin's Blessings earns you <color=#ece275>Betting Tickets</color>, with a daily cap of 390 tickets that resets at 05:00.\n② <color=#ece275>Betting Tickets</color> will be removed at the end of the event. Please use them in time.\n\n\n<size=18><color=#7adeff>◆Special Note◆</color></size>\n① Publishing inappropriate comments in the game is prohibited. Any personal attacks against participating members or other players will result in warnings or mutes once verified. In severe cases, this could lead to a losing match.\n② Please ensure all character cultivations and resources are ready before the contest begins. Complaints about the match schedule due to inadequate preparation by your party will be rejected.",
