    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_001"]="Couple in Pairs",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_002"]="Paper Crane Love",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_003"]="Every day, the Pure White Emissary will be waiting for all adventurers at the entrance of Prontera Cathedral.\nAfter accepting the quest, team up with your beloved one and go to the Amusement Park!\nComplete the quest and you will receive a Time of Love Gift Box and a White Paper Crane!",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_004"]="Cupid has prepared a <size=28>50%</size> off wedding coupon for you, which can only be claimed and used during the event!",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_005"]="During the event, adventurers can not only get the Time of Love Gift Box by completing quests, but also can purchase it in the Friends Gifting!\nIf you give the Time of Love Gift Box to your beloved one, you will not only get a Favor increase, but will also receive\nspecial food like Golden Jar Cookies or Silver Jar Cookies.",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_006"]="If Adventurers holding different Fortune Cookies gather together and perform the ‘Heart Emote’ action, <color=#D39FEFFF>Cupid, the God of Love</color>, will bestow upon you his blessings, and you’ll encounter White Paper Cranes as drops. If you’re lucky, you might even see some <color=#FD97B6FF>Pink Paper Cranes</color>!",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_007"]="Couples will encounter Pink Paper Cranes as drops if they perform the ‘Heart Emote’ action together, which can be exchanged for rare rewards.",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_008"]="White Valentine's Day Event",
    ["ui_WhiteValentineDayActivity_009"]="Exclusive",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_001"]="invites you to join",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_002"]="Refill",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_003"]="Toast",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_004"]="Drunk",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_005"]="Give Up",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_006"]="Ingredients",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_007"]="Finish making the Prepped Dishes can receive rewards from the Boss Lady.",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_008"]="Hand over Ingredients",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_009"]="Sync Dishes",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_010"]="No history currently",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_011"]="No Booze-up Invites",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_012"]="No Booze-up party requests",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_013"]="No Booze-up requests",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_014"]="Daily",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_015"]="Booze-up Invite",
    ["ui_WineCelebration_016"]="Join Request",
    ["ui_WorldKvmInvitedInfo_1"]="Invite to Party",
    ["ui_WorldKvmInvitedInfo_2"]="%s has invited you to join their War of the Chosen Party %s",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_1"]="Tournament Guide",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_10"]="Ranked Match",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_11"]="Teams that successfully pass the voting round will compete against each other according to the ranking order of votes. Matching Conditions: No. 1 vs. No. 8, No. 2 vs. No. 7, No. 3 vs. No. 6, No. 4 vs. No. 5.\nThe battle is conducted in 5 vs 5 mode. When the match starts, go to the designated NPC to teleport to the match field. The Team Leader will choose a maximum of 5 people to compete, with a maximum of 3 people as reserves. Each battle consists of 3 rounds. The first team to win 2 rounds will immediately advance to the next phase, the losing team will be eliminated. If the two sides are tied, the winner will be determined based on the battle data of the deciding round, and the one with the higher data will win. The priority is determined as follows: Number of Survivors > Total Damage > Total Kills > Total Healing.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_12"]="Elimination Match",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_13"]="Each sub-server’s Qualifying Match Champion Team qualifies for the Elimination Match. Other additional spaces will be filled by teams based on their server opening times. Please refer to the event page for the number of available spots.\nMatching Conditions: All knock-out teams are randomly divided into 8 divisions, and match-ups are randomly assigned. The winner from each group will enter the grand championship round.\nBattle format is the same as the qualifying match. In order to participate, at the beginning of the battle you need to log in to the designated sub-server within a specified time, 3 hours before the start of the game, player equipment and other data will be automatically synchronized to the game server. Please note that before that time, in order to avoid abnormal characters in the game, you should adjust your own character match ups. Players who have not entered the game server within the time limit will not be able to join this round.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_14"]="Result betting",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_15"]="During the qualifying and elimination matches, players can make predictions for the upcoming matches. The predictions will require Crystals.\nA failed prediction will result in the loss of all crystals consumed. A successful prediction will result in the return of all crystals cost and the gain of all crystals from the failed players in proportion to the crystals spent after deducting the 10% administration fee. Rewards need to be claimed manually in the \"My Prediction\" page, and the earnings generated on the same day can only be claimed at 05:00 on the next day.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_16"]="Contest Rewards",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_17"]="Qualifying Match Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_18"]="Qualifying Match Participation Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_19"]="Qualifying Match Champion Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_2"]="Prepare to start",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_20"]="Elimination Match Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_21"]="Elimination Match Champion Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_22"]="Grand Champion Reward",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_23"]="Server Spot",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_24"]="The number of spot in the Elimination Round defers based on the launch time of each server. For example, if a server only has 1 spot, then the Qualifying Round Champion will advance to the Elimination Round. If there are 2 spots, both the Qualifying Round Champion and 1st Runner-up can advance to the Elimination Round, etc. Please find the spot details below:",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_25"]="Server Name",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_26"]="Number of Spot",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_27"]="Qualifying Match Flow",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_28"]="Tap the avatar to go to <color=#f65050>Sigrdrifa</color> and enter battle.\nPlease note that players will only be able to enter <color=#f65050>5 minutes</color> after the tournament has started. Players will be considered to have surrendered if they do not enter the arena within the specified time.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_29"]="Elimination Match Flow",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_3"]="Participation rules",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_30"]="<color=#f65050>3 hours</color> before the tournament starts, character data will be synced to the tournament server. Until that time, players need to select \"Contest Server\" and select the specified character to enter the tournament.\nThe contestants are expected to be able to enter the tournament server faster to check the contestant's character data. Please contact us as soon as possible if there is a problem.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_31"]="How to join",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_4"]="Adventurers with Base level ≥45 can participate.\nProcess: Preparation Phase → Voting Phase → Qualifying Match → Elimination Match → Hall of Glory",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_5"]="Form a team",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_6"]="Only Adventurers who obtained the [Party Creation Voucher] during War Preparation can create teams, all other Adventurers that meet the requirements can join teams that have been created. After the team is created, you have 5 days to recruit team members. Each team can accommodate a maximum of 8 players. When a team reaches 5 players and all the players are ready to register, the team leader can either submit the registration manually or it will automatically submit after the time is over. The team will fail to register if there are less than 5 players.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_7"]="Vote for promotion",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_8"]="All Adventurers can cast votes for the teams they like and receive rewards for voting. The top 8 teams in each server will get a place in the Qualifying Match.\nThere are four types of votes. Voting ticket Lv.1 can be obtained in the War Preparation event and cannot be traded. Adventurers who owned a VIP card or obtained a VIP card during the War Preparation event will receive a certain number of Lv.2 to Lv.4 votes. A vote can be traded at the Exchange Center. Voting Tickets will be withdrawn after the event ends, please use them on time.",
    ["ui_WorldKvmRule_9"]="Tournament match",
