    ["worldKVM2_rule_001"]="Step 1 - Form a Party",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_002"]="Use Crystals to form a party or join other parties to participate in the Ranked Match.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_003"]="Step 2 - Ranked Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_004"]="Participate in the Ranked Match within a limited time to earn points, and the top 64 parties on the server with the most points will be qualified to participate in the Elimination Match.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_005"]="Step 3 - Regional Elimination Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_006"]="Qualifying parties in the region will be put into groups for the Elimination Match to determine the winner of each group.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_008"]="Step 4 - Final 8 Double-Elimination Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_009"]="The matches of the Final 8 will be held in the format of double-elimination. Parties with one losing match will enter the Losers' Bracket for another chance to seize the championship.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_01"]="Contest Process",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_011"]="Step 5 - Display of Honor",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_012"]="Announce information on the Champion Team members and the list of MVP players of each index.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_014"]="Party Creation and Registration Phase",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_015"]="Event and Condition: Base Lv. ≥ 45",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_016"]="The Party formation stage can be done through using Crystals. Other qualified Adventurers can join the created party to participate in the event.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_017"]="After a Party is created, 3 days are given to recruit teammates. Each party can have a maximum of 8 members. Once the party has at least 5 players and all the players are ready to register, the party leader can manually submit the registration. Alternatively, the system can automatically confirm the registration after the end of the registration time. If the number of party members is less than 5, the Party will fail to be registered.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_018"]="Ranked Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019"]="Parties with higher points will receive fewer points when they win the game, and parties with lower points will have fewer points deducted from them when they lose.\nIn contrast, parties with higher points will have more points deducted from them when they lose the game, and parties with fewer points will receive more points when they win.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019A"]="Points Bonus",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019B"]="Victory",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019C"]="Additional Bonus for winning 3 in a row",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019D"]="Additional decrease for losing 3 in a row",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019E"]="Dynamic Change",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019F"]="+10 pts",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019G"]="No points deducted",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019H"]="Count is reset after",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019I"]="Count is reset after",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019J"]="Points decrease",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019K"]="Failed the competition",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019L"]="Leave match after matchmaking and entering the map.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019M"]="Dynamic Change",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_019N"]="-100 pts",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_02"]="Rules",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020"]="After the end of the event, rewards are issued according to the ranking. For detailed rewards content, please refer to Contest Rewards.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020A"]="Tier",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020B"]="Point Ranges",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020C"]="Iron",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020D"]="0-1,299",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020E"]="Bronze",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020F"]="1,300-1,599",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020G"]="Silver",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020H"]="1,600-1,999",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020I"]="Gold",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020J"]="≥2,000",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020K"]="King",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_020L"]="≥600",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_021"]="After the event, the top 64 Parties on the server with the most points will be qualified to participate in the Elimination Match.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_022"]="Contest Battles",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_023"]="● Ranked Match Rules\n1. During the event, Parties compete against each other through matchmaking in the specified time frame, and points will be awarded or deducted depending on victory or defeat.\n2. The match requires Parties to log into the corresponding competition server during the opening hours for participation.\n3. The Ranked Match supports Party or Team mode. Please choose the appropriate mode according to the number of participants.\n4. The Party Leader can start matchmaking only when there are ≥ 5 members, and they all belong to the same Chosen Party.\n",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_024"]="● Elimination Match Spots\n1. The top 64 parties in Ranked Matches across all servers will advance into the Elimination Match.\n\n● Bracket Rules\n1. Group Bracket Rules: All parties in the Elimination Match are randomly assigned to 8 groups for random pairing. The winners of these groups will compete against each other in the finals to determine the champion of the season.\n2. The match follows the same rules as a Ranked Match. To participate in the match, parties must log into the corresponding server by the end of the preparation period. Otherwise, it's considered forfeiting the game.\n\n● Competition Format\n1. For the matches in groups 1 to 8, a BO3 format is adopted, with victory going to the party that first achieves 2 wins.\n2. In the Final 8, a BO5 format is adopted, with each party having a double-elimination chance. The first party that achieves 3 wins will advance to the next round, and the losing party will enter the defeated bracket.\n3. Parties in the defeated bracket will compete against each other in a BO5 format. Winners advance to the next round within the defeated bracket, while losing parties are eliminated immediately.\n\n● Merging Character Data\n1. Before the match, participants can synchronize their character data from the current server to the Contest Server through WOC Emissary, Sigrdrifa, up to 2 times each day.\n2. The data cannot be synchronized 75 minutes before or during the competition, and the participating Adventurers can get prepared 45 minutes before the competition by logging into the Contest Server.\n3. Changes on the Contest Server will not affect the normal server, except for Diamond consumptions. Be careful to avoid spending Diamonds on the Contest Server; Participants are responsible for any Diamond expenditure caused by their actions.\n4. Certain Cooking Materials cannot be used on the Contest Server.\n5. Participants who have concerns about their character data should reach out to customer service immediately.\n\n● Match Rules\n1. Every match (including Ranked Match and Elimination Match) lasts 5 minutes per round. Two rounds of small pillars and 1 round of the central pillar will activate during this time. Parties earn points by defeating enemies or opening pillars, with victory going to the party with the highest points.\n2. Each kill awards 15 points, opening a small pillar awards 100 points, and opening a central pillar awards 200 points.\n3. About Small Pillar: Three out of eight locations will be randomly activated for 60 seconds. Pillars not opened in time will return to inactive status. Only 1 Adventurer can open a pillar at a time, taking 5 seconds.\n4. About Central Pillar: The central pillar will be activated in the final round and remain active until the battle ends. Only 1 Adventurer can open a pillar at a time, taking 5 seconds.\n5. Both sides start in their own safe zones, which grant invincibility, disable attacks, and provide continuous healing. These effects are removed in the last 30 seconds. Staying in the safe zone for more than 20 seconds disables its effects. Leaving the safe zone grants a 3-second invincibility and speed boost (cannot benefit from the safe zone effects again for the next 6 seconds). After dying, both sides will automatically respawn with full HP in the safe zone after 10 seconds. Enemy Adventurers entering your safe zone will suffer heavy MSPD reduction and continuous damage.\n6. Deploying ≤2 units of the same class grants all party members the Divine Might effect for the entire battle.\nIf the target's current HP is higher than 300M (including shields), 15 stacks of special marks will be applied when dealing damage to them. Each subsequent hit consumes 1 stack of the mark, dealing one additional True DMG equal to (target's Max HP - 300M)/15. Triggers once every 0.2 seconds. If the damage interval is too long, the number of stacks consumed per hit increases over time, consuming 1 extra stack every 0.2 seconds, up to 5 stacks per hit. (Marks applied by each party member are calculated separately, and all marks disappear if not triggered for 5 seconds or when out of combat.)\nNote: The damage cannot be reduced or shared by any skill effects.\n7. Class switching is only allowed during the selection phase, with a limit of 10 switches per character in a single match.\n8. A surrender feature has been added for each round. After 3 minutes, anyone can start a surrender vote (60-second cooldown). If 4 or more party members agree within 30 seconds, the party surrenders. Surrendering is not allowed within the last 40 seconds of the battle.\n\n● Special Match Combat Rules\n1. Increase Final DMG and its minimum threshold (36%) for all Adventurers and extend the Final Penetration cap (1,250%).\nClarification (example given with P.DMG, same applies to M.DMG):\nAttacker's P.PEN fixed conversion percentage + Attacker's Final P.PEN percentage - Defender's P.DEF fixed conversion percentage - Defender's Final P.DEF percentage ≤ 1,250%\n2. Weaken the effectiveness of HP recovery (75%) and Lifesteal (75%) effect for 5 seconds.\n3. Opening a pillar temporarily disables the Endure and Debuff Immunity effect while greatly reducing the Debuff Resistance by 1,000%.\n4. Extend the cooldown of Acolyte's Resurrection skill to 10 seconds and remove the vulnerable effect after the resurrection.\n5. All equipment refresh effects now have a 3-second internal cooldown.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_025"]="● Outcome Betting\n1. During the Elimination Match, players can spend Chosen's Medals betting on the upcoming results.\n- Losing the bet will take away all your bet capitals.\nWinning the bet will return the amount you bet plus a share of the losing bettors. The share proportion will be the total winnings of the winning bettors divided by the individual betting amount.\n2. In the event of a rematch or shutdown, the match organizer is entitled to close all related bets of the current match and return the bet capitals.\n3. The betting function will be closed when the match is complete. Prize claiming and betting for the next round become available on the following day at 12:00.\n\n● Match Dispute\n1. If there are any flaws or special circumstances in a single match or the entire event (War of the Chosen) that have been verified, the organizer reserves the right to adjust the match schedule or restart the match.\n- By restarting the match, all disputes over the affected match will be considered invalid, and all bet capitals in the affected match will be refunded.\n- By adjusting the match schedules, there will not be any change to the participating Parties, match rules, and the matches that have already finished. Please refer to the official announcements for the schedule adjustments.\n2. If participants conduct the match through unauthorized means, the organizer has the right to disqualify the Party and cancel the affected match. All bet capitals and rewards in the affected match will be refunded.\n3. For Parties manipulating the match, which severely affects the match outcome, the organizer reserves the right to impose penalties.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_028"]="Ranked Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_029"]="After the event, rewards will be issued based on the points.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_03"]="Contest Rewards",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_030"]="Sub-server Champion",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_031"]="Ranked in 1st place on the server by total points at the end of the ranked matchmaking. (The frame bundle reward, including Avatar Frame, Chat Frame, and Side Bar, cannot be obtained repeatedly.)",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_032"]="Cross-server Elimination Match",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_033"]="Participants will obtain corresponding rewards every time they advance to the next stage. (The frame bundle reward, including Avatar Frame, Chat Frame, and Side Bar, cannot be obtained repeatedly.)",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_034"]="Season MVP",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_035"]="The MVP of each Class is selected at the end of the event.",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_036"]="Points: %s",
    ["worldKVM2_rule_037"]="● Event Time: Daily at 21:30-22:30 (UTC+7)\n● During the event, Parties compete against each other through matchmaking, and Points will be awarded or deducted according to victory or defeat.\n● Party Formation Rules:\n1. The Ranked Match supports Party or Team mode. Please choose the appropriate mode according to the number of participants.\n2. The Party Leader can start matchmaking only when there are ≥ 5 members, and they all belong to the <color=#ff646f>same Chosen Party</color>.\n3. The match needs to take place on a dedicated Contest Server.",
